Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: GEN 1:19
Text: And the evening and the morning were the fourth day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffa20dea-901d-428b-b640-214be9c22459>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: GEN 1:20
Text: And God said, Let the waters bring forth abundantly the moving creature that hath life, and fowl that may fly above the earth in the open firmament of heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/1/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:350e7264-cdd1-4b8d-a57a-ed463d51997d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: GEN 1:21
Text: And God created great whales, and every living creature that moveth, which the waters brought forth abundantly, after their kind, and every winged fowl after his kind: and God saw that it was good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/1/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1172c3b9-a2b8-4706-b0cb-308079eef760>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: GEN 1:22
Text: And God blessed them, saying, Be fruitful, and multiply, and fill the waters in the seas, and let fowl multiply in the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/1/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd085582-fb2a-4749-9403-40a79bd8aefc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: GEN 1:23
Text: And the evening and the morning were the fifth day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/1/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a2a9802-70ec-4aa9-a7ba-4c7e22b6242b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: GEN 1:24
Text: And God said, Let the earth bring forth the living creature after his kind, cattle, and creeping thing, and beast of the earth after his kind: and it was so.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/1/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97746115-112e-4262-aed9-85b1b8bc284c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: GEN 1:25
Text: And God made the beast of the earth after his kind, and cattle after their kind, and every thing that creepeth upon the earth after his kind: and God saw that it was good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/1/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd696bbc-ea21-4a0c-a3b1-7525067e136f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 278

Reference: GEN 1:26
Text: And God said, Let us make man in our image, after our likeness: and let them have dominion over the fish of the sea, and over the fowl of the air, and over the cattle, and over all the earth, and over every creeping thing that creepeth upon the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/1/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba0dc49a-ebe5-4e94-b79a-5661a03d78c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: GEN 1:27
Text: So God created man in his own image, in the image of God created he him; male and female created he them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/1/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7ff1aff-f95e-47e5-8abc-d1342c1f6ead>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: GEN 1:28
Text: And God blessed them, and God said unto them, Be fruitful, and multiply, and replenish the earth, and subdue it: and have dominion over the fish of the sea, and over the fowl of the air, and over every living thing that moveth upon the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/1/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a724dce9-2ac6-4f24-94ee-0d6e0d8c00da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: GEN 1:29
Text: And God said, Behold, I have given you every herb bearing seed, which is upon the face of all the earth, and every tree, in the which is the fruit of a tree yielding seed; to you it shall be for meat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/1/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6b9a030-668d-4862-a423-9d2e5f83848e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: GEN 1:30
Text: And to every beast of the earth, and to every fowl of the air, and to every thing that creepeth upon the earth, wherein there is life, I have given every green herb for meat: and it was so.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/1/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d594e118-7a69-42b3-88e4-5caf57748dfa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: GEN 1:31
Text: And God saw every thing that he had made, and, behold, it was very good. And the evening and the morning were the sixth day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d0f513f-bfdb-4572-aa4b-3218ae058371>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: GEN 2:1
Text: Thus the heavens and the earth were finished, and all the host of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91043963-1830-4e2c-9dd2-076054205e78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: GEN 2:2
Text: And on the seventh day God ended his work which he had made; and he rested on the seventh day from all his work which he had made.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94a53c58-d018-4181-be45-8bfe735baa2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: GEN 2:3
Text: And God blessed the seventh day, and sanctified it: because that in it he had rested from all his work which God created and made.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7090ce93-8787-4bc6-ae5e-076daa728303>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: GEN 2:4
Text: These are the generations of the heavens and of the earth when they were created, in the day that the LORD God made the earth and the heavens,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:593a0b59-2aa6-4795-ab94-fc3d45b47083>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: GEN 2:5
Text: And every plant of the field before it was in the earth, and every herb of the field before it grew: for the LORD God had not caused it to rain upon the earth, and there was not a man to till the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52ff9e61-9b56-4a96-b3e3-30bc2fde7642>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: GEN 2:6
Text: But there went up a mist from the earth, and watered the whole face of the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cee08db0-fae5-4de9-859d-6201bffc9b24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: GEN 2:7
Text: And the LORD God formed man of the dust of the ground, and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life; and man became a living soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f0991fe-7acf-4f18-8ae9-1f94b236141c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: GEN 2:8
Text: And the LORD God planted a garden eastward in Eden; and there he put the man whom he had formed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1be0c9b1-e8ea-46d2-b504-a37b61549825>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: GEN 2:9
Text: And out of the ground made the LORD God to grow every tree that is pleasant to the sight, and good for food; the tree of life also in the midst of the garden, and the tree of knowledge of good and evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d3134ae-9b0c-460d-98d0-7e790f3c5d7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: GEN 2:10
Text: And a river went out of Eden to water the garden; and from thence it was parted, and became into four heads.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f852f0ca-8796-47ee-994d-8a42c3167e80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: GEN 2:11
Text: The name of the first is Pison: that is it which compasseth the whole land of Havilah, where there is gold;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f77dfdc2-d7af-450c-9058-5da49927080f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: GEN 2:12
Text: And the gold of that land is good: there is bdellium and the onyx stone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36c9baac-085b-4603-9343-fe068ef52f83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: GEN 2:13
Text: And the name of the second river is Gihon: the same is it that compasseth the whole land of Ethiopia.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:add3cae0-d615-4db5-815b-002188c400f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: GEN 2:14
Text: And the name of the third river is Hiddekel: that is it which goeth toward the east of Assyria. And the fourth river is Euphrates.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a5e79ff-0b83-4da5-9312-71f400931e63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: GEN 2:15
Text: And the LORD God took the man, and put him into the garden of Eden to dress it and to keep it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0839d13-9381-4acf-ae40-4f7d0b195e83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: GEN 2:16
Text: And the LORD God commanded the man, saying, Of every tree of the garden thou mayest freely eat:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e03c24f5-8dab-406c-815a-3703f3a93d70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: GEN 2:17
Text: But of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil, thou shalt not eat of it: for in the day that thou eatest thereof thou shalt surely die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0c09a3e-e400-4983-9e3a-4089470b0fa1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: GEN 2:18
Text: And the LORD God said, It is not good that the man should be alone; I will make him an help meet for him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e2b04ba-e19b-423e-aa28-640460cb923c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: GEN 2:19
Text: And out of the ground the LORD God formed every beast of the field, and every fowl of the air; and brought them unto Adam to see what he would call them: and whatsoever Adam called every living creature, that was the name thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62d82813-a8bc-4f9d-926a-c0e7cb820208>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: GEN 2:20
Text: And Adam gave names to all cattle, and to the fowl of the air, and to every beast of the field; but for Adam there was not found an help meet for him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0a05126-fc1b-48cb-887c-7c0340d0c4fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: GEN 2:21
Text: And the LORD God caused a deep sleep to fall upon Adam, and he slept: and he took one of his ribs, and closed up the flesh instead thereof;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b72612a-1ba4-49e6-b374-73c36bb7ccf5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: GEN 2:22
Text: And the rib, which the LORD God had taken from man, made he a woman, and brought her unto the man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5dbfb7ae-a3f5-43b1-bcc2-29a39b07ad4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: GEN 2:23
Text: And Adam said, This is now bone of my bones, and flesh of my flesh: she shall be called Woman, because she was taken out of Man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25f21e2a-034d-41a7-9003-89bf59f37f11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: GEN 2:24
Text: Therefore shall a man leave his father and his mother, and shall cleave unto his wife: and they shall be one flesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/2/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aad433c1-2e0a-4b7a-b07c-030f11c39232>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: GEN 2:25
Text: And they were both naked, the man and his wife, and were not ashamed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f806cc0-4230-4700-bfd5-4d7aff43c7c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: GEN 3:1
Text: Now the serpent was more subtil than any beast of the field which the LORD God had made. And he said unto the woman, Yea, hath God said, Ye shall not eat of every tree of the garden?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12517e8a-252e-4995-b7fa-318cfb26a299>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: GEN 3:2
Text: And the woman said unto the serpent, We may eat of the fruit of the trees of the garden:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbc17a87-229b-43ad-a58c-6b129bf56b94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: GEN 3:3
Text: But of the fruit of the tree which is in the midst of the garden, God hath said, Ye shall not eat of it, neither shall ye touch it, lest ye die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f2f7521-763a-4f8c-936a-b9b9576f7a06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: GEN 3:4
Text: And the serpent said unto the woman, Ye shall not surely die:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6796306a-b356-4ab3-97f7-b79949250852>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: GEN 3:5
Text: For God doth know that in the day ye eat thereof, then your eyes shall be opened, and ye shall be as gods, knowing good and evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef2d37f5-4d68-4f11-ba77-d08048d71993>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: GEN 3:6
Text: And when the woman saw that the tree was good for food, and that it was pleasant to the eyes, and a tree to be desired to make one wise, she took of the fruit thereof, and did eat, and gave also unto her husband with her; and he did eat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:877f3240-75c4-457d-b741-6f4c0b85beed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: GEN 3:7
Text: And the eyes of them both were opened, and they knew that they were naked; and they sewed fig leaves together, and made themselves aprons.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d54291c-57f5-4262-8a6a-e1a30cded6e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: GEN 3:8
Text: And they heard the voice of the LORD God walking in the garden in the cool of the day: and Adam and his wife hid themselves from the presence of the LORD God amongst the trees of the garden.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b2954b2-d8ae-43f7-b076-d854a120d132>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: GEN 3:9
Text: And the LORD God called unto Adam, and said unto him, Where art thou?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f216747b-2528-4aa2-a5f2-0b5c0ae0139a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: GEN 3:10
Text: And he said, I heard thy voice in the garden, and I was afraid, because I was naked; and I hid myself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:007ab9e0-cecb-4d3c-a0c2-f73347d19c0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: GEN 3:11
Text: And he said, Who told thee that thou wast naked? Hast thou eaten of the tree, whereof I commanded thee that thou shouldest not eat?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8a2f647-a90f-479b-abd9-23aa05326992>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: GEN 3:12
Text: And the man said, The woman whom thou gavest to be with me, she gave me of the tree, and I did eat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd50f4ed-c069-4b90-8973-c8324c535a83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: GEN 3:13
Text: And the LORD God said unto the woman, What is this that thou hast done? And the woman said, The serpent beguiled me, and I did eat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e50c50dd-887c-4c3a-9350-bb038ac8648a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: GEN 3:14
Text: And the LORD God said unto the serpent, Because thou hast done this, thou art cursed above all cattle, and above every beast of the field; upon thy belly shalt thou go, and dust shalt thou eat all the days of thy life:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2620a092-846c-4e18-b3fb-b50e610b1945>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: GEN 3:15
Text: And I will put enmity between thee and the woman, and between thy seed and her seed; it shall bruise thy head, and thou shalt bruise his heel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8f0791b-b7a7-4f9d-a38d-54fb7ee94e9f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: GEN 3:16
Text: Unto the woman he said, I will greatly multiply thy sorrow and thy conception; in sorrow thou shalt bring forth children; and thy desire shall be to thy husband, and he shall rule over thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c64200f-1e8d-410b-9a11-406f7a3e173a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 286

Reference: GEN 3:17
Text: And unto Adam he said, Because thou hast hearkened unto the voice of thy wife, and hast eaten of the tree, of which I commanded thee, saying, Thou shalt not eat of it: cursed is the ground for thy sake; in sorrow shalt thou eat of it all the days of thy life;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:978c00fa-64be-4fbb-8add-e6f4eb6225d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: GEN 3:18
Text: Thorns also and thistles shall it bring forth to thee; and thou shalt eat the herb of the field;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25e97a06-cf85-46a8-baac-36924cfdcc1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: GEN 3:19
Text: In the sweat of thy face shalt thou eat bread, till thou return unto the ground; for out of it wast thou taken: for dust thou art, and unto dust shalt thou return.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:989df0a2-9e5d-47e4-9f4b-e1b536751969>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: GEN 3:20
Text: And Adam called his wife’s name Eve; because she was the mother of all living.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b847e52-0b39-4833-a7fa-76b5d92564a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: GEN 3:21
Text: Unto Adam also and to his wife did the LORD God make coats of skins, and clothed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:500bf658-71b4-4127-ab03-324292bb01fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: GEN 3:22
Text: And the LORD God said, Behold, the man is become as one of us, to know good and evil: and now, lest he put forth his hand, and take also of the tree of life, and eat, and live for ever:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10e55d82-5f18-4608-9f25-afd423aa8bb2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: GEN 3:23
Text: Therefore the LORD God sent him forth from the garden of Eden, to till the ground from whence he was taken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/3/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:085dbc4d-9036-45c1-b766-19b90b7932da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: GEN 3:24
Text: So he drove out the man; and he placed at the east of the garden of Eden Cherubims, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to keep the way of the tree of life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1733aefe-872f-46f9-9e8d-ea9251542a85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: GEN 4:1
Text: And Adam knew Eve his wife; and she conceived, and bare Cain, and said, I have gotten a man from the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8021ae18-9dc1-4314-b37d-d88ac0729f1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: GEN 4:2
Text: And she again bare his brother Abel. And Abel was a keeper of sheep, but Cain was a tiller of the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56fb2b1a-0ca4-4b8f-9fdd-8f8c46012369>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: GEN 4:3
Text: And in process of time it came to pass, that Cain brought of the fruit of the ground an offering unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e93e3e7-4817-427d-9e13-bb589ec4ee22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: GEN 4:4
Text: And Abel, he also brought of the firstlings of his flock and of the fat thereof. And the LORD had respect unto Abel and to his offering:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b312f3a5-fe1b-470c-9ba9-41afbe114bf8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: GEN 4:5
Text: But unto Cain and to his offering he had not respect. And Cain was very wroth, and his countenance fell.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac98b87f-dc79-4da2-9260-28a3847f3c8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: GEN 4:6
Text: And the LORD said unto Cain, Why art thou wroth? and why is thy countenance fallen?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5076b877-690f-4b98-8df7-e9ad4c7f76b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: GEN 4:7
Text: If thou doest well, shalt thou not be accepted? and if thou doest not well, sin lieth at the door. And unto thee shall be his desire, and thou shalt rule over him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1139c411-f80f-4957-8567-df5fb7c02eab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: GEN 4:8
Text: And Cain talked with Abel his brother: and it came to pass, when they were in the field, that Cain rose up against Abel his brother, and slew him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bb3fb64-34f1-4384-b311-98cc2b17e7f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: GEN 4:9
Text: And the LORD said unto Cain, Where is Abel thy brother? And he said, I know not: Am I my brother’s keeper?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92adedcf-9438-476e-8d88-b9bb055be04b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: GEN 4:10
Text: And he said, What hast thou done? the voice of thy brother’s blood crieth unto me from the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0cb71caa-ff76-4295-ac79-55d553255a7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: GEN 4:11
Text: And now art thou cursed from the earth, which hath opened her mouth to receive thy brother’s blood from thy hand;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c787bdcb-c40a-418f-8bb7-1a223dea05f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: GEN 4:12
Text: When thou tillest the ground, it shall not henceforth yield unto thee her strength; a fugitive and a vagabond shalt thou be in the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f75a768-6134-47c8-8ca8-944e06402b1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: GEN 4:13
Text: And Cain said unto the LORD, My punishment is greater than I can bear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afa2f84d-489f-44f7-aaa4-3b3c9a1d2f73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: GEN 4:14
Text: Behold, thou hast driven me out this day from the face of the earth; and from thy face shall I be hid; and I shall be a fugitive and a vagabond in the earth; and it shall come to pass, that every one that findeth me shall slay me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66e3fcdf-1101-4e71-8298-16cc3a347eda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: GEN 4:15
Text: And the LORD said unto him, Therefore whosoever slayeth Cain, vengeance shall be taken on him sevenfold. And the LORD set a mark upon Cain, lest any finding him should kill him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8a80f10-d47f-4599-9eff-335e4f1dc494>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: GEN 4:16
Text: And Cain went out from the presence of the LORD, and dwelt in the land of Nod, on the east of Eden.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35fa000d-707f-42b6-b3eb-e202e2678edd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: GEN 4:17
Text: And Cain knew his wife; and she conceived, and bare Enoch: and he builded a city, and called the name of the city, after the name of his son, Enoch.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:110ed619-48f0-4000-a32f-4c583e3c2a1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: GEN 4:18
Text: And unto Enoch was born Irad: and Irad begat Mehujael: and Mehujael begat Methusael: and Methusael begat Lamech.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17cc5254-92f4-4c93-84ee-bc7503d7c51c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: GEN 4:19
Text: And Lamech took unto him two wives: the name of the one was Adah, and the name of the other Zillah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77c80508-7642-4582-a653-091b82302880>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: GEN 4:20
Text: And Adah bare Jabal: he was the father of such as dwell in tents, and of such as have cattle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96c0f5d2-4c4b-4b8a-950b-a2813cd547b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: GEN 4:21
Text: And his brother’s name was Jubal: he was the father of all such as handle the harp and organ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b38a00f6-acfe-4ad8-8f4a-cc9a12766487>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: GEN 4:22
Text: And Zillah, she also bare Tubalcain, an instructer of every artificer in brass and iron: and the sister of Tubalcain was Naamah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3657b0d9-b694-4c72-8cd2-7f4b14ff7cd1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: GEN 4:23
Text: And Lamech said unto his wives, Adah and Zillah, Hear my voice; ye wives of Lamech, hearken unto my speech: for I have slain a man to my wounding, and a young man to my hurt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76b9cd34-926f-452e-89b5-ab4e585f4955>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: GEN 4:24
Text: If Cain shall be avenged sevenfold, truly Lamech seventy and sevenfold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f51b718-e26d-4b32-bfe1-255195a9d639>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: GEN 4:25
Text: And Adam knew his wife again; and she bare a son, and called his name Seth: For God, said she, hath appointed me another seed instead of Abel, whom Cain slew.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/4/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5aeb1e9-df11-4d8a-a614-d610934549de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: GEN 4:26
Text: And to Seth, to him also there was born a son; and he called his name Enos: then began men to call upon the name of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
