Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: GEN 5:28
Text: And Lamech lived an hundred eighty and two years, and begat a son:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/5/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e80991a6-b7c6-4d42-8b1b-cddf7443432b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: GEN 5:29
Text: And he called his name Noah, saying, This same shall comfort us concerning our work and toil of our hands, because of the ground which the LORD hath cursed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/5/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5470ee3d-f915-4c63-9c1c-8d31361f6a07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: GEN 5:30
Text: And Lamech lived after he begat Noah five hundred ninety and five years, and begat sons and daughters:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/5/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93e77d9b-13f5-4f65-8df0-db95e51bef1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: GEN 5:31
Text: And all the days of Lamech were seven hundred seventy and seven years: and he died.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/5/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f17c41f-096c-4802-95be-3c39d80c1294>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: GEN 5:32
Text: And Noah was five hundred years old: and Noah begat Shem, Ham, and Japheth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26d59460-6de5-4729-a083-e59317cbd0b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: GEN 6:1
Text: And it came to pass, when men began to multiply on the face of the earth, and daughters were born unto them,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e34952d-def5-47dc-829e-e7987f2aedfd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: GEN 6:2
Text: That the sons of God saw the daughters of men that they were fair; and they took them wives of all which they chose.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e7b36dc-62dd-47c3-bf87-90cc45e53c00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: GEN 6:3
Text: And the LORD said, My spirit shall not always strive with man, for that he also is flesh: yet his days shall be an hundred and twenty years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5a0efdb-dc39-486e-9f7e-ab8a3569e226>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: GEN 6:4
Text: There were giants in the earth in those days; and also after that, when the sons of God came in unto the daughters of men, and they bare children to them, the same became mighty men which were of old, men of renown.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6b8f989-471d-4d4e-9a9e-404af3fe1ac0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: GEN 6:5
Text: And God saw that the wickedness of man was great in the earth, and that every imagination of the thoughts of his heart was only evil continually.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79257eb4-b3de-4b54-bf59-ea2adb80138a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: GEN 6:6
Text: And it repented the LORD that he had made man on the earth, and it grieved him at his heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0301ab0e-8f07-4109-85ce-f24b6b6731e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: GEN 6:7
Text: And the LORD said, I will destroy man whom I have created from the face of the earth; both man, and beast, and the creeping thing, and the fowls of the air; for it repenteth me that I have made them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df857428-acd3-4f72-95e8-a4f0f1604379>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 71

Reference: GEN 6:8
Text: But Noah found grace in the eyes of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29e6432d-fe1c-4e30-8c7b-a99c9bc78583>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: GEN 6:9
Text: These are the generations of Noah: Noah was a just man and perfect in his generations, and Noah walked with God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:276e7fbe-0f8e-4790-9ae4-277204ae4631>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: GEN 6:10
Text: And Noah begat three sons, Shem, Ham, and Japheth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a665cbc-2601-460e-934b-e9ab3327dcf5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: GEN 6:11
Text: The earth also was corrupt before God, and the earth was filled with violence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f298aa54-03f3-4195-b05d-beb390328e74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: GEN 6:12
Text: And God looked upon the earth, and, behold, it was corrupt; for all flesh had corrupted his way upon the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c980de78-a6d0-44cd-9509-281ec649df64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: GEN 6:13
Text: And God said unto Noah, The end of all flesh is come before me; for the earth is filled with violence through them; and, behold, I will destroy them with the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/6/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b53149a1-d76e-42a4-9653-1c1327eecbc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: GEN 6:14
Text: Make thee an ark of gopher wood; rooms shalt thou make in the ark, and shalt pitch it within and without with pitch.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/6/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d49b6389-7ab4-4b5a-9b64-15b0abb1cefb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: GEN 6:15
Text: And this is the fashion which thou shalt make it of: The length of the ark shall be three hundred cubits, the breadth of it fifty cubits, and the height of it thirty cubits.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/6/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:699fd380-19b1-410d-83e3-5e55853e283d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: GEN 6:16
Text: A window shalt thou make to the ark, and in a cubit shalt thou finish it above; and the door of the ark shalt thou set in the side thereof; with lower, second, and third stories shalt thou make it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/6/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3654506a-c021-4261-a127-b88193847a20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: GEN 6:17
Text: And, behold, I, even I, do bring a flood of waters upon the earth, to destroy all flesh, wherein is the breath of life, from under heaven; and every thing that is in the earth shall die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/6/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ef92c6c-b02b-4cfe-b894-fe2e994b2e59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: GEN 6:18
Text: But with thee will I establish my covenant; and thou shalt come into the ark, thou, and thy sons, and thy wife, and thy sons’ wives with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/6/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31ece817-f3ea-499d-8fa5-68667b882cbe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: GEN 6:19
Text: And of every living thing of all flesh, two of every sort shalt thou bring into the ark, to keep them alive with thee; they shall be male and female.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/6/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:759e6f90-6852-4196-9227-bf953ffdb222>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: GEN 6:20
Text: Of fowls after their kind, and of cattle after their kind, of every creeping thing of the earth after his kind, two of every sort shall come unto thee, to keep them alive.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/6/21
