Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: GEN 6:21
Text: And take thou unto thee of all food that is eaten, and thou shalt gather it to thee; and it shall be for food for thee, and for them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/6/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5eec5c72-60b0-42fc-b039-bd99fd8176a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: GEN 6:22
Text: Thus did Noah; according to all that God commanded him, so did he.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99bf4350-80bf-40b6-a234-d6a0e5de6f66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: GEN 7:1
Text: And the LORD said unto Noah, Come thou and all thy house into the ark; for thee have I seen righteous before me in this generation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abb96318-1b8d-45e0-a36d-bc9abbf7a652>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: GEN 7:2
Text: Of every clean beast thou shalt take to thee by sevens, the male and his female: and of beasts that are not clean by two, the male and his female.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dddcae98-3aa2-45dd-8723-8e0c8de783d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: GEN 7:3
Text: Of fowls also of the air by sevens, the male and the female; to keep seed alive upon the face of all the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edf6c39c-b366-43ec-bcf5-60a19b1288ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: GEN 7:4
Text: For yet seven days, and I will cause it to rain upon the earth forty days and forty nights; and every living substance that I have made will I destroy from off the face of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b98f1d45-a951-4a45-8f8c-4588fa8d7ee1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: GEN 7:5
Text: And Noah did according unto all that the LORD commanded him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c811beb-dfd3-44c5-afc0-071ff271e281>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: GEN 7:6
Text: And Noah was six hundred years old when the flood of waters was upon the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ab7ef63-cb09-4330-be3b-cb24938f5fab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: GEN 7:7
Text: And Noah went in, and his sons, and his wife, and his sons’ wives with him, into the ark, because of the waters of the flood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84b19ee8-7a26-4528-bdd4-6a1c78bb2eee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: GEN 7:8
Text: Of clean beasts, and of beasts that are not clean, and of fowls, and of every thing that creepeth upon the earth,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef185b8c-98c2-4bdb-9b0a-f68848a6f3bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: GEN 7:9
Text: There went in two and two unto Noah into the ark, the male and the female, as God had commanded Noah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d71191a0-38c0-42b7-8634-1dbc59e66633>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: GEN 7:10
Text: And it came to pass after seven days, that the waters of the flood were upon the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab3662d2-cb0b-4fd1-9717-77fc647d6e5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: GEN 7:11
Text: In the six hundredth year of Noah’s life, in the second month, the seventeenth day of the month, the same day were all the fountains of the great deep broken up, and the windows of heaven were opened.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec0371b2-a768-40c9-8af9-15fb490ad793>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: GEN 7:12
Text: And the rain was upon the earth forty days and forty nights.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e247e3cb-a852-4d92-966e-7c049adaff4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: GEN 7:13
Text: In the selfsame day entered Noah, and Shem, and Ham, and Japheth, the sons of Noah, and Noah’s wife, and the three wives of his sons with them, into the ark;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6173be1-2259-4ce3-ba30-502b12f9528c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: GEN 7:14
Text: They, and every beast after his kind, and all the cattle after their kind, and every creeping thing that creepeth upon the earth after his kind, and every fowl after his kind, every bird of every sort.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6dcb0110-82a8-4211-9c39-b758ff02fe2d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: GEN 7:15
Text: And they went in unto Noah into the ark, two and two of all flesh, wherein is the breath of life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bad46d6-0d11-411e-8c0a-320b1535fc2b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: GEN 7:16
Text: And they that went in, went in male and female of all flesh, as God had commanded him: and the LORD shut him in.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac59e051-8724-47a6-aef9-4bc7f12040fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: GEN 7:17
Text: And the flood was forty days upon the earth; and the waters increased, and bare up the ark, and it was lift up above the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80050ff1-1ff0-4b18-9e5a-e00c9be28ff6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: GEN 7:18
Text: And the waters prevailed, and were increased greatly upon the earth; and the ark went upon the face of the waters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6216fdf-cc4a-4af2-8017-9ed76ed03273>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: GEN 7:19
Text: And the waters prevailed exceedingly upon the earth; and all the high hills, that were under the whole heaven, were covered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d515374-452d-4141-967e-99d175a18dd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: GEN 7:20
Text: Fifteen cubits upward did the waters prevail; and the mountains were covered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:097c5037-021d-49f1-9c46-17de16f34939>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: GEN 7:21
Text: And all flesh died that moved upon the earth, both of fowl, and of cattle, and of beast, and of every creeping thing that creepeth upon the earth, and every man:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ca0c3e3-1229-4470-8a95-33de097fa345>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: GEN 7:22
Text: All in whose nostrils was the breath of life, of all that was in the dry land, died.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:643c2862-54e8-47ca-b581-80854ec00052>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 291

Reference: GEN 7:23
Text: And every living substance was destroyed which was upon the face of the ground, both man, and cattle, and the creeping things, and the fowl of the heaven; and they were destroyed from the earth: and Noah only remained alive, and they that were with him in the ark.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/7/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfeb7810-0c9d-4596-9088-23c532713d92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: GEN 7:24
Text: And the waters prevailed upon the earth an hundred and fifty days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/8/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5dbeb365-0280-49bd-9cef-58ba5ca8a9b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: GEN 8:1
Text: And God remembered Noah, and every living thing, and all the cattle that was with him in the ark: and God made a wind to pass over the earth, and the waters asswaged;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/8/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99e38e4a-1986-4c71-b57b-2212c1d81ee9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: GEN 8:2
Text: The fountains also of the deep and the windows of heaven were stopped, and the rain from heaven was restrained;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/8/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d91e0f98-df99-492d-a3fb-a4f98909c15b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: GEN 8:3
Text: And the waters returned from off the earth continually: and after the end of the hundred and fifty days the waters were abated.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/8/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ce32fed-d01b-4b14-9276-cebcba323d0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: GEN 8:4
Text: And the ark rested in the seventh month, on the seventeenth day of the month, upon the mountains of Ararat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/8/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:657a4d62-a624-43b3-944a-0dfdaa4942e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: GEN 8:5
Text: And the waters decreased continually until the tenth month: in the tenth month, on the first day of the month, were the tops of the mountains seen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/8/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15207f9b-e968-4120-a00c-a5f278e1e642>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: GEN 8:6
Text: And it came to pass at the end of forty days, that Noah opened the window of the ark which he had made:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/8/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f545e3b7-3b98-4007-ad34-aeb177e5484e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: GEN 8:7
Text: And he sent forth a raven, which went forth to and fro, until the waters were dried up from off the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/8/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d3effcd-3336-4d4b-b759-e8dbfd19b9a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: GEN 8:8
Text: Also he sent forth a dove from him, to see if the waters were abated from off the face of the ground;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/8/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:988b4b3c-7f7a-4685-8542-2c0f6be525f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: GEN 8:9
Text: But the dove found no rest for the sole of her foot, and she returned unto him into the ark, for the waters were on the face of the whole earth: then he put forth his hand, and took her, and pulled her in unto him into the ark.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/8/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e78a6c2d-6f70-486d-bf69-030a7b972a7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: GEN 8:10
Text: And he stayed yet other seven days; and again he sent forth the dove out of the ark;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/8/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a1305b1-dea8-4f11-9b1a-b933267eab41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: GEN 8:11
Text: And the dove came in to him in the evening; and, lo, in her mouth was an olive leaf pluckt off: so Noah knew that the waters were abated from off the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/8/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f810b9f1-2d6e-45ad-9e6d-fa19d7c2d0e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: GEN 8:12
Text: And he stayed yet other seven days; and sent forth the dove; which returned not again unto him any more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/8/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1153c831-3cfe-497f-a627-3877e229cfb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: GEN 8:13
Text: And it came to pass in the six hundredth and first year, in the first month, the first day of the month, the waters were dried up from off the earth: and Noah removed the covering of the ark, and looked, and, behold, the face of the ground was dry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/8/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e323d7c-3b5f-4a22-b80a-59baf9cf81d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: GEN 8:14
Text: And in the second month, on the seven and twentieth day of the month, was the earth dried.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/8/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:145619dc-a558-4334-8b26-37a7cd2a18e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 59

Reference: GEN 8:15
Text: And God spake unto Noah, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/8/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8e502e0-a125-442d-b5da-0f20daa398a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: GEN 8:16
Text: Go forth of the ark, thou, and thy wife, and thy sons, and thy sons’ wives with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/8/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0274f978-cb14-4604-af07-4539393a14f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 278

Reference: GEN 8:17
Text: Bring forth with thee every living thing that is with thee, of all flesh, both of fowl, and of cattle, and of every creeping thing that creepeth upon the earth; that they may breed abundantly in the earth, and be fruitful, and multiply upon the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/8/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:329689d1-7b5d-4254-a739-02346f030dcf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: GEN 8:18
Text: And Noah went forth, and his sons, and his wife, and his sons’ wives with him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/8/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b213afa5-1a1f-4e61-baa5-7301537f1feb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: GEN 8:19
Text: Every beast, every creeping thing, and every fowl, and whatsoever creepeth upon the earth, after their kinds, went forth out of the ark.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/8/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8fdd1ba6-8a4e-4146-b48f-29c4c9acdbbc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: GEN 8:20
Text: And Noah builded an altar unto the LORD; and took of every clean beast, and of every clean fowl, and offered burnt offerings on the altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/8/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1bba75d3-a381-4fbd-a6dc-96863f0bbcc5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 289

Reference: GEN 8:21
Text: And the LORD smelled a sweet savour; and the LORD said in his heart, I will not again curse the ground any more for man’s sake; for the imagination of man’s heart is evil from his youth; neither will I again smite any more every thing living, as I have done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/8/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84d5baee-6a6e-4128-a433-7719eea64f0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: GEN 8:22
Text: While the earth remaineth, seedtime and harvest, and cold and heat, and summer and winter, and day and night shall not cease.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/9/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c847230-22f9-4fe3-9d1f-7a28ce38a7b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: GEN 9:1
Text: And God blessed Noah and his sons, and said unto them, Be fruitful, and multiply, and replenish the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/9/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4562a570-3881-40f8-86e8-de190980bdc5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: GEN 9:2
Text: And the fear of you and the dread of you shall be upon every beast of the earth, and upon every fowl of the air, upon all that moveth upon the earth, and upon all the fishes of the sea; into your hand are they delivered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/9/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbe9fe9b-d609-463a-bc8d-84c88a209d51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: GEN 9:3
Text: Every moving thing that liveth shall be meat for you; even as the green herb have I given you all things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/9/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6a2c118-de84-4572-a05a-12b820d714c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: GEN 9:4
Text: But flesh with the life thereof, which is the blood thereof, shall ye not eat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/9/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7772048f-41a8-4981-9add-232695ca1760>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: GEN 9:5
Text: And surely your blood of your lives will I require; at the hand of every beast will I require it, and at the hand of man; at the hand of every man’s brother will I require the life of man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/9/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d7e88fa-edb3-4035-bc27-c2cc35f7c838>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: GEN 9:6
Text: Whoso sheddeth man’s blood, by man shall his blood be shed: for in the image of God made he man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/9/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6aa25197-4339-473f-a957-f0f561e8b240>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: GEN 9:7
Text: And you, be ye fruitful, and multiply; bring forth abundantly in the earth, and multiply therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/9/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:903bbca3-e385-4e49-8f4c-6ddd7c2eb95b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: GEN 9:8
Text: And God spake unto Noah, and to his sons with him, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/9/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa4897e6-ffc8-4b24-92d9-55b96f72dba3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: GEN 9:9
Text: And I, behold, I establish my covenant with you, and with your seed after you;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/9/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8eb7a485-8859-4112-8491-09c5d00a3610>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: GEN 9:10
Text: And with every living creature that is with you, of the fowl, of the cattle, and of every beast of the earth with you; from all that go out of the ark, to every beast of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/9/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6772db1f-721c-4b60-b289-79d79266402c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: GEN 9:11
Text: And I will establish my covenant with you, neither shall all flesh be cut off any more by the waters of a flood; neither shall there any more be a flood to destroy the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/9/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22ddaa2b-333f-4c3c-9743-01c6b25a17a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: GEN 9:12
Text: And God said, This is the token of the covenant which I make between me and you and every living creature that is with you, for perpetual generations:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/9/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7003296f-6979-411b-ae76-f4ec1203a5f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: GEN 9:13
Text: I do set my bow in the cloud, and it shall be for a token of a covenant between me and the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/9/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5672bc3b-11c1-4456-b9e7-364afc0f8fe9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: GEN 9:14
Text: And it shall come to pass, when I bring a cloud over the earth, that the bow shall be seen in the cloud:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/9/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58517dc6-dfbe-49b2-9b78-c17c41f0b3ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: GEN 9:15
Text: And I will remember my covenant, which is between me and you and every living creature of all flesh; and the waters shall no more become a flood to destroy all flesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/9/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ddb40c6-3f84-4f0a-916b-7b6bf8511af9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: GEN 9:16
Text: And the bow shall be in the cloud; and I will look upon it, that I may remember the everlasting covenant between God and every living creature of all flesh that is upon the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/9/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c113db8-9b6e-4357-bb98-9b78c47d1436>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: GEN 9:17
Text: And God said unto Noah, This is the token of the covenant, which I have established between me and all flesh that is upon the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/9/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e999ca9a-46ed-4484-ac0e-eebca0d544a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

