Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: GEN 10:30
Text: And their dwelling was from Mesha, as thou goest unto Sephar a mount of the east.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/10/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f04719d-689d-42da-957a-d1ab3e58278d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: GEN 10:31
Text: These are the sons of Shem, after their families, after their tongues, in their lands, after their nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/10/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e37ed2a6-4a6c-4d83-ac7d-a9848f13401a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: GEN 10:32
Text: These are the families of the sons of Noah, after their generations, in their nations: and by these were the nations divided in the earth after the flood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c738367-ea3f-4e4e-ad22-baa6cbdfd801>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: GEN 11:1
Text: And the whole earth was of one language, and of one speech.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef736769-724d-4576-a8ff-ff2fa3184f57>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: GEN 11:2
Text: And it came to pass, as they journeyed from the east, that they found a plain in the land of Shinar; and they dwelt there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f02ffba-793d-45c3-aa89-2a17f2c68eff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: GEN 11:3
Text: And they said one to another, Go to, let us make brick, and burn them thoroughly. And they had brick for stone, and slime had they for morter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e055a273-2a9c-46b6-abee-7e0049c011e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: GEN 11:4
Text: And they said, Go to, let us build us a city and a tower, whose top may reach unto heaven; and let us make us a name, lest we be scattered abroad upon the face of the whole earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b880049-d8be-44bb-8326-5196c29eec42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: GEN 11:5
Text: And the LORD came down to see the city and the tower, which the children of men builded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:218fed24-5393-4567-b797-f7016c1fae93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: GEN 11:6
Text: And the LORD said, Behold, the people is one, and they have all one language; and this they begin to do: and now nothing will be restrained from them, which they have imagined to do.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e084c28-0518-478e-b41e-3ed2773144a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: GEN 11:7
Text: Go to, let us go down, and there confound their language, that they may not understand one another’s speech.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bed0a3dc-471a-4d43-b674-9672a6a4cf55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: GEN 11:8
Text: So the LORD scattered them abroad from thence upon the face of all the earth: and they left off to build the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33590a1b-74a7-4c11-9793-260adfab3371>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: GEN 11:9
Text: Therefore is the name of it called Babel; because the LORD did there confound the language of all the earth: and from thence did the LORD scatter them abroad upon the face of all the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48452f3f-64f4-4e6f-8573-76934f4767e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: GEN 11:10
Text: These are the generations of Shem: Shem was an hundred years old, and begat Arphaxad two years after the flood:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4550e401-0f54-44e8-861b-ead9337010a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: GEN 11:11
Text: And Shem lived after he begat Arphaxad five hundred years, and begat sons and daughters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90534f6a-ce73-46cf-b5a5-1500bbb75432>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: GEN 11:12
Text: And Arphaxad lived five and thirty years, and begat Salah:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef4ca74d-9806-41fc-8845-4a95f057f546>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: GEN 11:13
Text: And Arphaxad lived after he begat Salah four hundred and three years, and begat sons and daughters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6c7a077-bb28-476e-ae88-ce830d669d86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: GEN 11:14
Text: And Salah lived thirty years, and begat Eber:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63949e73-8355-45b4-bacf-bb6bcdcbdce3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: GEN 11:15
Text: And Salah lived after he begat Eber four hundred and three years, and begat sons and daughters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c790b2b4-80d5-42fc-a9de-e9d6e5447fa3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: GEN 11:16
Text: And Eber lived four and thirty years, and begat Peleg:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d43ccd87-58ce-4993-91d1-9011ab71c583>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: GEN 11:17
Text: And Eber lived after he begat Peleg four hundred and thirty years, and begat sons and daughters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5aa2673-dddf-4d10-bd67-f747e756535b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 72

Reference: GEN 11:18
Text: And Peleg lived thirty years, and begat Reu:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f604867-eb77-4741-80b9-525d26378ee6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: GEN 11:19
Text: And Peleg lived after he begat Reu two hundred and nine years, and begat sons and daughters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f935629-7f02-489e-b30c-a1657cea74be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: GEN 11:20
Text: And Reu lived two and thirty years, and begat Serug:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6aad768-4158-4b29-8aa8-3002cfbb97c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: GEN 11:21
Text: And Reu lived after he begat Serug two hundred and seven years, and begat sons and daughters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5c1f76a-d601-4489-a98c-2fbf352f40d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: GEN 11:22
Text: And Serug lived thirty years, and begat Nahor:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7151020-87a8-484e-bb38-006353fe3b9f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: GEN 11:23
Text: And Serug lived after he begat Nahor two hundred years, and begat sons and daughters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68a74317-03ff-4267-a29d-e60570c91669>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: GEN 11:24
Text: And Nahor lived nine and twenty years, and begat Terah:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00eff8e8-7eb0-4722-b0e0-9010e4686deb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: GEN 11:25
Text: And Nahor lived after he begat Terah an hundred and nineteen years, and begat sons and daughters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8730b3b5-481f-45a1-921d-c6a8a76ac4e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: GEN 11:26
Text: And Terah lived seventy years, and begat Abram, Nahor, and Haran.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bedb2a4-92cb-43d2-bf6e-93aca42d469b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: GEN 11:27
Text: Now these are the generations of Terah: Terah begat Abram, Nahor, and Haran; and Haran begat Lot.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f37574fe-2460-4baf-b538-e4e98011c5d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: GEN 11:28
Text: And Haran died before his father Terah in the land of his nativity, in Ur of the Chaldees.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6344749b-a048-4914-b2ba-64222d0abc0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: GEN 11:29
Text: And Abram and Nahor took them wives: the name of Abram’s wife was Sarai; and the name of Nahor’s wife, Milcah, the daughter of Haran, the father of Milcah, and the father of Iscah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19d078f2-c737-4216-b6bb-646ef2c0942a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 67

Reference: GEN 11:30
Text: But Sarai was barren; she had no child.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e16e0fe3-f7b2-4dad-9462-fc0c0f37b863>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 283

Reference: GEN 11:31
Text: And Terah took Abram his son, and Lot the son of Haran his son’s son, and Sarai his daughter in law, his son Abram’s wife; and they went forth with them from Ur of the Chaldees, to go into the land of Canaan; and they came unto Haran, and dwelt there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/11/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29ef0910-11db-4711-992e-82a156a9b61b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: GEN 11:32
Text: And the days of Terah were two hundred and five years: and Terah died in Haran.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/12/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edb99e8e-5fac-447e-a05a-ebfd86715be3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: GEN 12:1
Text: Now the LORD had said unto Abram, Get thee out of thy country, and from thy kindred, and from thy father’s house, unto a land that I will shew thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/12/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1fe314a-54c4-4d93-b390-64aa9fd16068>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: GEN 12:2
Text: And I will make of thee a great nation, and I will bless thee, and make thy name great; and thou shalt be a blessing:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/12/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29c5b368-15a0-4f3c-afc6-d7cd75758d64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: GEN 12:3
Text: And I will bless them that bless thee, and curse him that curseth thee: and in thee shall all families of the earth be blessed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/12/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bce7a410-a4b9-47c8-82da-2ed0793a97e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: GEN 12:4
Text: So Abram departed, as the LORD had spoken unto him; and Lot went with him: and Abram was seventy and five years old when he departed out of Haran.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/12/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0476ccdf-07b4-4423-988d-167950480056>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: GEN 12:5
Text: And Abram took Sarai his wife, and Lot his brother’s son, and all their substance that they had gathered, and the souls that they had gotten in Haran; and they went forth to go into the land of Canaan; and into the land of Canaan they came.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/12/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:207f28a4-1759-4506-880f-ded53699ae67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: GEN 12:6
Text: And Abram passed through the land unto the place of Sichem, unto the plain of Moreh. And the Canaanite was then in the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/12/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2690123-dad2-4835-a6d8-f830c6df076e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: GEN 12:7
Text: And the LORD appeared unto Abram, and said, Unto thy seed will I give this land: and there builded he an altar unto the LORD, who appeared unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/12/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f0c7045-1c68-4eb9-897e-ada1c7e6d6b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: GEN 12:8
Text: And he removed from thence unto a mountain on the east of Bethel, and pitched his tent, having Bethel on the west, and Hai on the east: and there he builded an altar unto the LORD, and called upon the name of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/12/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b6a7d8b-aba5-4556-abe6-081a059ad464>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: GEN 12:9
Text: And Abram journeyed, going on still toward the south.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/12/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fb060dd-1446-4acf-9e1e-72128f789c98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: GEN 12:10
Text: And there was a famine in the land: and Abram went down into Egypt to sojourn there; for the famine was grievous in the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/12/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1baff864-3fc5-4f1b-9908-5367c2f409fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: GEN 12:11
Text: And it came to pass, when he was come near to enter into Egypt, that he said unto Sarai his wife, Behold now, I know that thou art a fair woman to look upon:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/12/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b394531-367d-439b-a03a-6c0c77eff77d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: GEN 12:12
Text: Therefore it shall come to pass, when the Egyptians shall see thee, that they shall say, This is his wife: and they will kill me, but they will save thee alive.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/12/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3545173-a1ed-4df4-86b9-0586031e3f7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: GEN 12:13
Text: Say, I pray thee, thou art my sister: that it may be well with me for thy sake; and my soul shall live because of thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/12/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba35218d-c6ce-4896-bd95-c53a1efd035d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: GEN 12:14
Text: And it came to pass, that, when Abram was come into Egypt, the Egyptians beheld the woman that she was very fair.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/12/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79fc919c-327f-411e-aaf9-a613935af6db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: GEN 12:15
Text: The princes also of Pharaoh saw her, and commended her before Pharaoh: and the woman was taken into Pharaoh’s house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/12/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d6fd392-0daf-4f94-baa5-e3e3a3ac99d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: GEN 12:16
Text: And he entreated Abram well for her sake: and he had sheep, and oxen, and he asses, and menservants, and maidservants, and she asses, and camels.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/12/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b904c59e-057a-4dd7-afc8-3648117983c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: GEN 12:17
Text: And the LORD plagued Pharaoh and his house with great plagues because of Sarai Abram’s wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/12/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66fc7c0d-7941-4d2b-8c79-9cc5897dd527>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: GEN 12:18
Text: And Pharaoh called Abram and said, What is this that thou hast done unto me? why didst thou not tell me that she was thy wife?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/12/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52484e84-1a43-4b93-a234-9d22761708a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: GEN 12:19
Text: Why saidst thou, She is my sister? so I might have taken her to me to wife: now therefore behold thy wife, take her, and go thy way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/12/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7393937-b2e3-408f-bc74-168fe553ae7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: GEN 12:20
Text: And Pharaoh commanded his men concerning him: and they sent him away, and his wife, and all that he had.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/13/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a06a930-866d-4c06-9593-c4208329c676>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: GEN 13:1
Text: And Abram went up out of Egypt, he, and his wife, and all that he had, and Lot with him, into the south.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/13/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8b18f25-b2e0-406e-be1c-9bd833afcae8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: GEN 13:2
Text: And Abram was very rich in cattle, in silver, and in gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/13/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0f2895a-ced9-4943-9bae-f9025d1e4158>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: GEN 13:3
Text: And he went on his journeys from the south even to Bethel, unto the place where his tent had been at the beginning, between Bethel and Hai;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/13/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6c31369-7881-4b76-a0e6-9162e865fa4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: GEN 13:4
Text: Unto the place of the altar, which he had made there at the first: and there Abram called on the name of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/13/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5077af80-71d3-47f2-b51c-fee836463cdb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: GEN 13:5
Text: And Lot also, which went with Abram, had flocks, and herds, and tents.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/13/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d995f090-d4ca-4af1-8023-b988cc3d2488>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: GEN 13:6
Text: And the land was not able to bear them, that they might dwell together: for their substance was great, so that they could not dwell together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/13/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b245293-b92b-48a5-b017-f3f517ee33cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: GEN 13:7
Text: And there was a strife between the herdmen of Abram’s cattle and the herdmen of Lot’s cattle: and the Canaanite and the Perizzite dwelled then in the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/13/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:240616db-b225-478f-9730-914e1a72d3f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: GEN 13:8
Text: And Abram said unto Lot, Let there be no strife, I pray thee, between me and thee, and between my herdmen and thy herdmen; for we be brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/13/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7acf96d0-3979-4816-a597-bc1260e66335>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: GEN 13:9
Text: Is not the whole land before thee? separate thyself, I pray thee, from me: if thou wilt take the left hand, then I will go to the right; or if thou depart to the right hand, then I will go to the left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/13/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18f45df5-3a73-4099-b1c1-bb87a1884694>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: GEN 13:10
Text: And Lot lifted up his eyes, and beheld all the plain of Jordan, that it was well watered every where, before the LORD destroyed Sodom and Gomorrah, even as the garden of the LORD, like the land of Egypt, as thou comest unto Zoar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/13/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e54a0d68-ecc9-48c4-bb17-b86645caba02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: GEN 13:11
Text: Then Lot chose him all the plain of Jordan; and Lot journeyed east: and they separated themselves the one from the other.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/13/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae335d45-5d56-442b-9d6c-091f8c5a8ae9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: GEN 13:12
Text: Abram dwelled in the land of Canaan, and Lot dwelled in the cities of the plain, and pitched his tent toward Sodom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/13/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d58b3a70-297f-42db-bb79-51d724a38fed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: GEN 13:13
Text: But the men of Sodom were wicked and sinners before the LORD exceedingly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/13/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:549b2cd5-a6fb-481f-8587-561315928195>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: GEN 13:14
Text: And the LORD said unto Abram, after that Lot was separated from him, Lift up now thine eyes, and look from the place where thou art northward, and southward, and eastward, and westward:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/13/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:febbb8f4-6ec0-4e32-a2ca-3db77b19a3d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: GEN 13:15
Text: For all the land which thou seest, to thee will I give it, and to thy seed for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/13/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8bef5483-465d-4162-baff-0b4a86036f1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: GEN 13:16
Text: And I will make thy seed as the dust of the earth: so that if a man can number the dust of the earth, then shall thy seed also be numbered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/13/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebe040f8-aa86-48aa-935e-44f5ca3dfe8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: GEN 13:17
Text: Arise, walk through the land in the length of it and in the breadth of it; for I will give it unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/13/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94ae9674-e329-41dc-8996-2646b2a371e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: GEN 13:18
Text: Then Abram removed his tent, and came and dwelt in the plain of Mamre, which is in Hebron, and built there an altar unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3dd0342-7e8a-42e7-9a18-9dfc27f7447e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: GEN 14:1
Text: And it came to pass in the days of Amraphel king of Shinar, Arioch king of Ellasar, Chedorlaomer king of Elam, and Tidal king of nations;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00dd7671-e647-43f3-8d09-3a9bb3ac4df1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: GEN 14:2
Text: That these made war with Bera king of Sodom, and with Birsha king of Gomorrah, Shinab king of Admah, and Shemeber king of Zeboiim, and the king of Bela, which is Zoar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fe6e857-aeda-494a-a173-18f8a1b85dfc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: GEN 14:3
Text: All these were joined together in the vale of Siddim, which is the salt sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7a0864a-4210-4730-9479-a34d60beae5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: GEN 14:4
Text: Twelve years they served Chedorlaomer, and in the thirteenth year they rebelled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52cb2dfb-0759-4e31-9cf9-929be568a622>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: GEN 14:5
Text: And in the fourteenth year came Chedorlaomer, and the kings that were with him, and smote the Rephaims in Ashteroth Karnaim, and the Zuzims in Ham, and the Emins in Shaveh Kiriathaim,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:829048ae-ed84-494f-a083-09e9e8a35814>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: GEN 14:6
Text: And the Horites in their mount Seir, unto Elparan, which is by the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6fc314f7-03c1-4f75-a81f-e46331652cad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: GEN 14:7
Text: And they returned, and came to Enmishpat, which is Kadesh, and smote all the country of the Amalekites, and also the Amorites, that dwelt in Hazezontamar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbb15ce9-067d-4a2f-bcb3-ff241fbf4901>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: GEN 14:8
Text: And there went out the king of Sodom, and the king of Gomorrah, and the king of Admah, and the king of Zeboiim, and the king of Bela (the same is Zoar;) and they joined battle with them in the vale of Siddim;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10b5bc57-ac0b-4afb-8442-84477fc80e49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: GEN 14:9
Text: With Chedorlaomer the king of Elam, and with Tidal king of nations, and Amraphel king of Shinar, and Arioch king of Ellasar; four kings with five.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfebfd9d-cacd-4706-b727-f7893c71c5a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: GEN 14:10
Text: And the vale of Siddim was full of slimepits; and the kings of Sodom and Gomorrah fled, and fell there; and they that remained fled to the mountain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86e82cf4-62d9-4342-9915-e6b15d874fa2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: GEN 14:11
Text: And they took all the goods of Sodom and Gomorrah, and all their victuals, and went their way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:502fbc9a-a783-4be5-9b91-197770b8aa37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: GEN 14:12
Text: And they took Lot, Abram’s brother’s son, who dwelt in Sodom, and his goods, and departed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d972593-4a12-4a03-9c01-a053be02668e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: GEN 14:13
Text: And there came one that had escaped, and told Abram the Hebrew; for he dwelt in the plain of Mamre the Amorite, brother of Eshcol, and brother of Aner: and these were confederate with Abram.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a68ef811-ed3d-42ac-a76a-5088668a0ede>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: GEN 14:14
Text: And when Abram heard that his brother was taken captive, he armed his trained servants, born in his own house, three hundred and eighteen, and pursued them unto Dan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb3f2f33-57b8-4936-a2b0-05704108b8d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: GEN 14:15
Text: And he divided himself against them, he and his servants, by night, and smote them, and pursued them unto Hobah, which is on the left hand of Damascus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09dfe05a-6f92-48f8-bc9e-e580cf490b36>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: GEN 14:16
Text: And he brought back all the goods, and also brought again his brother Lot, and his goods, and the women also, and the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e582629a-bc7b-4354-b91a-59ca3575496d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: GEN 14:17
Text: And the king of Sodom went out to meet him after his return from the slaughter of Chedorlaomer, and of the kings that were with him, at the valley of Shaveh, which is the king’s dale.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52826b5b-f016-4901-b751-6571124be54a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: GEN 14:18
Text: And Melchizedek king of Salem brought forth bread and wine: and he was the priest of the most high God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1096fb4f-6ae8-48cb-85c4-f8457c9cbd8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: GEN 14:19
Text: And he blessed him, and said, Blessed be Abram of the most high God, possessor of heaven and earth:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98fd4cb3-ed1b-4df8-b865-c74257550ced>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: GEN 14:20
Text: And blessed be the most high God, which hath delivered thine enemies into thy hand. And he gave him tithes of all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d010f0f4-dbc9-4e52-ac05-abde05687ef0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: GEN 14:21
Text: And the king of Sodom said unto Abram, Give me the persons, and take the goods to thyself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f49ccd7e-f708-4511-906a-2f46fc536924>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: GEN 14:22
Text: And Abram said to the king of Sodom, I have lift up mine hand unto the LORD, the most high God, the possessor of heaven and earth,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9a0be35-b582-4d2f-96c6-e5f28f787865>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: GEN 14:23
Text: That I will not take from a thread even to a shoelatchet, and that I will not take any thing that is thine, lest thou shouldest say, I have made Abram rich:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/14/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33fe362c-f64e-4bd9-a747-e5cb614cd19f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: GEN 14:24
Text: Save only that which the young men have eaten, and the portion of the men which went with me, Aner, Eshcol, and Mamre; let them take their portion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/15/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91b34d24-f3eb-4970-98be-7e63839ea03c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: GEN 15:1
Text: After these things the word of the LORD came unto Abram in a vision, saying, Fear not, Abram: I am thy shield, and thy exceeding great reward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/15/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:320dfff0-5044-4ed2-9e27-6807777fe309>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: GEN 15:2
Text: And Abram said, LORD God, what wilt thou give me, seeing I go childless, and the steward of my house is this Eliezer of Damascus?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/15/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b368a74-724c-45a7-97a2-d4396a506db6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: GEN 15:3
Text: And Abram said, Behold, to me thou hast given no seed: and, lo, one born in my house is mine heir.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/15/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55db8de7-4eaa-4eac-a0f7-fa0203f08e8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: GEN 15:4
Text: And, behold, the word of the LORD came unto him, saying, This shall not be thine heir; but he that shall come forth out of thine own bowels shall be thine heir.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/15/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b100c1e3-d43f-4512-b223-8e78ef1ea870>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: GEN 15:5
Text: And he brought him forth abroad, and said, Look now toward heaven, and tell the stars, if thou be able to number them: and he said unto him, So shall thy seed be.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/15/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:587c8571-8263-4779-8e59-f636235a0e5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: GEN 15:6
Text: And he believed in the LORD; and he counted it to him for righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/15/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a97e476-6d36-4f2d-b8be-8ca62cf40a53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: GEN 15:7
Text: And he said unto him, I am the LORD that brought thee out of Ur of the Chaldees, to give thee this land to inherit it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/15/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c876a4da-46ed-4eda-9d00-783344a48190>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: GEN 15:8
Text: And he said, LORD God, whereby shall I know that I shall inherit it?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/15/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5f3df19-b458-48c9-9e37-67f7ac8dbdd4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: GEN 15:9
Text: And he said unto him, Take me an heifer of three years old, and a she goat of three years old, and a ram of three years old, and a turtledove, and a young pigeon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/15/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33ba405e-d730-4702-b0db-033d1d8aff08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: GEN 15:10
Text: And he took unto him all these, and divided them in the midst, and laid each piece one against another: but the birds divided he not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/15/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:475e440c-ebab-4091-8f37-b0a28190e84a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: GEN 15:11
Text: And when the fowls came down upon the carcases, Abram drove them away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/15/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52f6c3fb-18f7-4ad9-8be5-5b6ec354f6a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: GEN 15:12
Text: And when the sun was going down, a deep sleep fell upon Abram; and, lo, an horror of great darkness fell upon him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/15/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9adf9fbf-f2db-4d23-8eea-6e60647e886b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: GEN 15:13
Text: And he said unto Abram, Know of a surety that thy seed shall be a stranger in a land that is not theirs, and shall serve them; and they shall afflict them four hundred years;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/15/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db8e8d38-07e0-4d81-901d-15ab5949d9ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: GEN 15:14
Text: And also that nation, whom they shall serve, will I judge: and afterward shall they come out with great substance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/15/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddbb52a4-7f39-415c-b40b-e9da7dae709e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: GEN 15:15
Text: And thou shalt go to thy fathers in peace; thou shalt be buried in a good old age.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/15/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d60a7e9-f903-4fc6-9cba-2c186fc86c32>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: GEN 15:16
Text: But in the fourth generation they shall come hither again: for the iniquity of the Amorites is not yet full.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/15/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e74afd7-b183-4852-8d7a-5b1cb8fb65c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: GEN 15:17
Text: And it came to pass, that, when the sun went down, and it was dark, behold a smoking furnace, and a burning lamp that passed between those pieces.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/15/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94d5f572-8e27-4926-a6ed-796f5e0c962e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: GEN 15:18
Text: In the same day the LORD made a covenant with Abram, saying, Unto thy seed have I given this land, from the river of Egypt unto the great river, the river Euphrates:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/15/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9edc404-249d-4afa-ae08-349238ec0606>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: GEN 15:19
Text: The Kenites, and the Kenizzites, and the Kadmonites,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/15/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63874240-6925-4d1b-859c-2c5e5d937233>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: GEN 15:20
Text: And the Hittites, and the Perizzites, and the Rephaims,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/15/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b24eff59-231b-4acc-a79c-ef0c8bab3f2b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: GEN 15:21
Text: And the Amorites, and the Canaanites, and the Girgashites, and the Jebusites.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/16/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9871206-4509-49b5-9f47-bac69b801f62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: GEN 16:1
Text: Now Sarai Abram’s wife bare him no children: and she had an handmaid, an Egyptian, whose name was Hagar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/16/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92af1828-00ec-487f-9d87-a8fc8107bc9e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: GEN 16:2
Text: And Sarai said unto Abram, Behold now, the LORD hath restrained me from bearing: I pray thee, go in unto my maid; it may be that I may obtain children by her. And Abram hearkened to the voice of Sarai.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/16/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:027661c6-9943-4b11-b525-af6124f2fa26>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: GEN 16:3
Text: And Sarai Abram’s wife took Hagar her maid the Egyptian, after Abram had dwelt ten years in the land of Canaan, and gave her to her husband Abram to be his wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/16/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7047c6e1-779a-40bc-8d38-4c92fee4bbe9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: GEN 16:4
Text: And he went in unto Hagar, and she conceived: and when she saw that she had conceived, her mistress was despised in her eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/16/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13685616-eb93-431e-9d82-4ab8cf631427>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: GEN 16:5
Text: And Sarai said unto Abram, My wrong be upon thee: I have given my maid into thy bosom; and when she saw that she had conceived, I was despised in her eyes: the LORD judge between me and thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/16/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef645577-e9a6-424c-a7cd-0d33f02969f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: GEN 16:6
Text: But Abram said unto Sarai, Behold, thy maid is in thine hand; do to her as it pleaseth thee. And when Sarai dealt hardly with her, she fled from her face.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/16/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae0b681c-9f20-47c4-b33a-8b2e6dd17550>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: GEN 16:7
Text: And the angel of the LORD found her by a fountain of water in the wilderness, by the fountain in the way to Shur.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/16/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64d2a856-a6bb-41e8-bb0b-25738c0b1aed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: GEN 16:8
Text: And he said, Hagar, Sarai’s maid, whence camest thou? and whither wilt thou go? And she said, I flee from the face of my mistress Sarai.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/16/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3827ee0f-4291-401a-84b4-d9b81a74ce47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: GEN 16:9
Text: And the angel of the LORD said unto her, Return to thy mistress, and submit thyself under her hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/16/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae0e7d3a-40b9-4055-8a7b-fd524484a0fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: GEN 16:10
Text: And the angel of the LORD said unto her, I will multiply thy seed exceedingly, that it shall not be numbered for multitude.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/16/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5db8c234-8535-430e-a079-6acae4a17749>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: GEN 16:11
Text: And the angel of the LORD said unto her, Behold, thou art with child and shalt bear a son, and shalt call his name Ishmael; because the LORD hath heard thy affliction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/16/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:641827bd-9ea9-4a53-a06a-2266a2fcde27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: GEN 16:12
Text: And he will be a wild man; his hand will be against every man, and every man’s hand against him; and he shall dwell in the presence of all his brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/16/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0b0cab9-7eaf-4735-a434-221b7bb04f67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: GEN 16:13
Text: And she called the name of the LORD that spake unto her, Thou God seest me: for she said, Have I also here looked after him that seeth me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/16/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d654fe0a-dab0-4662-8bfc-a3895737707a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: GEN 16:14
Text: Wherefore the well was called Beerlahairoi; behold, it is between Kadesh and Bered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/16/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:416693a1-eedc-4350-b944-e01634e484c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: GEN 16:15
Text: And Hagar bare Abram a son: and Abram called his son’s name, which Hagar bare, Ishmael.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/16/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f96bb46-c602-4f98-a3a4-6ae2c12a78b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: GEN 16:16
Text: And Abram was fourscore and six years old, when Hagar bare Ishmael to Abram.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f379a3c3-415b-447f-acda-807b6c9571fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: GEN 17:1
Text: And when Abram was ninety years old and nine, the LORD appeared to Abram, and said unto him, I am the Almighty God; walk before me, and be thou perfect.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d88bba5-ae06-48d0-8f4c-52ba6389561a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: GEN 17:2
Text: And I will make my covenant between me and thee, and will multiply thee exceedingly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c396c3b4-2a25-46d1-919c-11265b4f948f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: GEN 17:3
Text: And Abram fell on his face: and God talked with him, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c3f0ed2-e813-494b-ab89-59cfb80a51dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: GEN 17:4
Text: As for me, behold, my covenant is with thee, and thou shalt be a father of many nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:503b4f13-464f-487a-bf31-e50381b29483>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: GEN 17:5
Text: Neither shall thy name any more be called Abram, but thy name shall be Abraham; for a father of many nations have I made thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:460e6ef8-4451-4605-865e-71fba08e9e19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: GEN 17:6
Text: And I will make thee exceeding fruitful, and I will make nations of thee, and kings shall come out of thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4a41fce-df9e-4255-89d4-fd6cc292c61a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: GEN 17:7
Text: And I will establish my covenant between me and thee and thy seed after thee in their generations for an everlasting covenant, to be a God unto thee, and to thy seed after thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8e055fc-8e59-49bc-9eb5-f6443476aba3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: GEN 17:8
Text: And I will give unto thee, and to thy seed after thee, the land wherein thou art a stranger, all the land of Canaan, for an everlasting possession; and I will be their God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abdb913e-c231-43e6-934a-ceabe00fb1b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: GEN 17:9
Text: And God said unto Abraham, Thou shalt keep my covenant therefore, thou, and thy seed after thee in their generations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95bd9a2b-1404-4dad-ab84-057b80d135ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: GEN 17:10
Text: This is my covenant, which ye shall keep, between me and you and thy seed after thee; Every man child among you shall be circumcised.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e4d71e6-ec4c-4bb4-8325-60818acf471a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: GEN 17:11
Text: And ye shall circumcise the flesh of your foreskin; and it shall be a token of the covenant betwixt me and you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:325ac9ce-f472-4367-9968-096e66199001>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: GEN 17:12
Text: And he that is eight days old shall be circumcised among you, every man child in your generations, he that is born in the house, or bought with money of any stranger, which is not of thy seed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:951d13a6-3636-49cc-ac78-568a30f033d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: GEN 17:13
Text: He that is born in thy house, and he that is bought with thy money, must needs be circumcised: and my covenant shall be in your flesh for an everlasting covenant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6461b61b-ce30-44c1-babd-7d2f92e74019>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: GEN 17:14
Text: And the uncircumcised man child whose flesh of his foreskin is not circumcised, that soul shall be cut off from his people; he hath broken my covenant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ccee8e3c-387e-4603-af14-20c1437ad01b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: GEN 17:15
Text: And God said unto Abraham, As for Sarai thy wife, thou shalt not call her name Sarai, but Sarah shall her name be.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c49360ed-76fc-4099-96a0-516cbacb8105>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: GEN 17:16
Text: And I will bless her, and give thee a son also of her: yea, I will bless her, and she shall be a mother of nations; kings of people shall be of her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c65913e-939d-4b4a-b086-8776e330699a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: GEN 17:17
Text: Then Abraham fell upon his face, and laughed, and said in his heart, Shall a child be born unto him that is an hundred years old? and shall Sarah, that is ninety years old, bear?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37aa20fa-00fc-44f2-b1cb-b7a6eaebb5f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: GEN 17:18
Text: And Abraham said unto God, O that Ishmael might live before thee!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b68401f-3f8d-4d9e-a805-619fcd5f0fe6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: GEN 17:19
Text: And God said, Sarah thy wife shall bear thee a son indeed; and thou shalt call his name Isaac: and I will establish my covenant with him for an everlasting covenant, and with his seed after him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e868193-adf7-491f-8a5f-349c410d8066>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: GEN 17:20
Text: And as for Ishmael, I have heard thee: Behold, I have blessed him, and will make him fruitful, and will multiply him exceedingly; twelve princes shall he beget, and I will make him a great nation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0e5470a-6667-4bb7-810e-5b6e0106b182>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: GEN 17:21
Text: But my covenant will I establish with Isaac, which Sarah shall bear unto thee at this set time in the next year.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d14a6c0-d557-4b8d-9993-a2ab7a076b21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: GEN 17:22
Text: And he left off talking with him, and God went up from Abraham.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f55a3fe2-119f-4dae-8028-238ac6febaaf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 277

Reference: GEN 17:23
Text: And Abraham took Ishmael his son, and all that were born in his house, and all that were bought with his money, every male among the men of Abraham’s house; and circumcised the flesh of their foreskin in the selfsame day, as God had said unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47192ebf-d96e-4a6c-ae89-289eb60f3fd4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: GEN 17:24
Text: And Abraham was ninety years old and nine, when he was circumcised in the flesh of his foreskin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7906cfa1-e1b6-4aba-b54d-2a191eefc2ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: GEN 17:25
Text: And Ishmael his son was thirteen years old, when he was circumcised in the flesh of his foreskin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37490422-f4a3-46a1-ab8b-f2ea00e90b2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: GEN 17:26
Text: In the selfsame day was Abraham circumcised, and Ishmael his son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/17/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f40d4bc5-999f-46c8-9af2-8493a22ab4a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: GEN 17:27
Text: And all the men of his house, born in the house, and bought with money of the stranger, were circumcised with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa5d6bfd-6360-4388-b5e3-c627f533eb1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: GEN 18:1
Text: And the LORD appeared unto him in the plains of Mamre: and he sat in the tent door in the heat of the day;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2bbd2dc-3ed6-4575-9f9a-3ad702a8f23d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: GEN 18:2
Text: And he lift up his eyes and looked, and, lo, three men stood by him: and when he saw them, he ran to meet them from the tent door, and bowed himself toward the ground,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93640799-f892-4fdd-872c-6d7382725479>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: GEN 18:3
Text: And said, My LORD, if now I have found favour in thy sight, pass not away, I pray thee, from thy servant:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36a7b7c0-94d4-4379-b563-bdb36ff5b1a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: GEN 18:4
Text: Let a little water, I pray you, be fetched, and wash your feet, and rest yourselves under the tree:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4790d0c4-b928-4c50-861e-ee67c46de79b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: GEN 18:5
Text: And I will fetch a morsel of bread, and comfort ye your hearts; after that ye shall pass on: for therefore are ye come to your servant. And they said, So do, as thou hast said.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2a1d4f6-bdef-4fa2-937f-8fb08571693a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: GEN 18:6
Text: And Abraham hastened into the tent unto Sarah, and said, Make ready quickly three measures of fine meal, knead it, and make cakes upon the hearth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c3deff4-c525-4220-bed8-5ce941cf8c06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: GEN 18:7
Text: And Abraham ran unto the herd, and fetcht a calf tender and good, and gave it unto a young man; and he hasted to dress it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2786633-6220-42cc-8aad-dd2818587ab3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: GEN 18:8
Text: And he took butter, and milk, and the calf which he had dressed, and set it before them; and he stood by them under the tree, and they did eat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9296a334-dccc-46fb-acc0-a6010403429d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: GEN 18:9
Text: And they said unto him, Where is Sarah thy wife? And he said, Behold, in the tent.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6277fd30-a9e3-42db-8788-8109eb4ece12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: GEN 18:10
Text: And he said, I will certainly return unto thee according to the time of life; and, lo, Sarah thy wife shall have a son. And Sarah heard it in the tent door, which was behind him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d37c5465-5555-43eb-ac0f-e7cec32a1ec2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: GEN 18:11
Text: Now Abraham and Sarah were old and well stricken in age; and it ceased to be with Sarah after the manner of women.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b710f8ef-c089-4425-8bc9-e70bf08e6521>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: GEN 18:12
Text: Therefore Sarah laughed within herself, saying, After I am waxed old shall I have pleasure, my lord being old also?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fcf45103-526a-4729-a38f-3b36f7384e3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: GEN 18:13
Text: And the LORD said unto Abraham, Wherefore did Sarah laugh, saying, Shall I of a surety bear a child, which am old?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4969c56d-4614-419a-9263-384011730425>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: GEN 18:14
Text: Is any thing too hard for the LORD? At the time appointed I will return unto thee, according to the time of life, and Sarah shall have a son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ee63ef3-8cbd-4cee-8632-d2061f6411ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: GEN 18:15
Text: Then Sarah denied, saying, I laughed not; for she was afraid. And he said, Nay; but thou didst laugh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48239854-ae2b-4ce9-84a6-d4524b04a7ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: GEN 18:16
Text: And the men rose up from thence, and looked toward Sodom: and Abraham went with them to bring them on the way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06454d3f-c0f1-41d2-a890-6c5f997a51b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: GEN 18:17
Text: And the LORD said, Shall I hide from Abraham that thing which I do;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5927c612-96b1-4c3c-8e0a-7162f9670b0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: GEN 18:18
Text: Seeing that Abraham shall surely become a great and mighty nation, and all the nations of the earth shall be blessed in him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:644cb244-87fd-4bdd-90b9-24bce5bbc14a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: GEN 18:19
Text: For I know him, that he will command his children and his household after him, and they shall keep the way of the LORD, to do justice and judgment; that the LORD may bring upon Abraham that which he hath spoken of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:505d61c0-ad41-4697-b8e7-95983e32de17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: GEN 18:20
Text: And the LORD said, Because the cry of Sodom and Gomorrah is great, and because their sin is very grievous;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c62310bb-6101-4cdd-adb5-b31376b30167>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: GEN 18:21
Text: I will go down now, and see whether they have done altogether according to the cry of it, which is come unto me; and if not, I will know.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1a03428-4fa8-4165-8787-a6386166edf2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: GEN 18:22
Text: And the men turned their faces from thence, and went toward Sodom: but Abraham stood yet before the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ec177ef-bdb2-4470-94e9-91a547cf67f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: GEN 18:23
Text: And Abraham drew near, and said, Wilt thou also destroy the righteous with the wicked?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8686f7e2-3e20-4ed1-bd75-2b3d3aa135aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: GEN 18:24
Text: Peradventure there be fifty righteous within the city: wilt thou also destroy and not spare the place for the fifty righteous that are therein?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b2581b2-6ed0-4897-b60d-ee33ea455b7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: GEN 18:25
Text: That be far from thee to do after this manner, to slay the righteous with the wicked: and that the righteous should be as the wicked, that be far from thee: Shall not the Judge of all the earth do right?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fd65245-e7b0-4b01-a267-c8720b06d4b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: GEN 18:26
Text: And the LORD said, If I find in Sodom fifty righteous within the city, then I will spare all the place for their sakes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5463401-58c9-4e0d-9c11-09ce010c0b99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: GEN 18:27
Text: And Abraham answered and said, Behold now, I have taken upon me to speak unto the LORD, which am but dust and ashes:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80a29e63-6e5f-4979-8334-9f0bcf682d44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: GEN 18:28
Text: Peradventure there shall lack five of the fifty righteous: wilt thou destroy all the city for lack of five? And he said, If I find there forty and five, I will not destroy it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6731dc40-2a0b-4c7f-81d2-4a788a9ad22c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: GEN 18:29
Text: And he spake unto him yet again, and said, Peradventure there shall be forty found there. And he said, I will not do it for forty’s sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d81ee13-4783-45d3-bbe6-83392941679d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: GEN 18:30
Text: And he said unto him, Oh let not the LORD be angry, and I will speak: Peradventure there shall thirty be found there. And he said, I will not do it, if I find thirty there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d36c6479-3e38-4021-a552-7c5d4cb7d7bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: GEN 18:31
Text: And he said, Behold now, I have taken upon me to speak unto the LORD: Peradventure there shall be twenty found there. And he said, I will not destroy it for twenty’s sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:924e11f5-f70d-40dc-b109-8b214b2a9c48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: GEN 18:32
Text: And he said, Oh let not the LORD be angry, and I will speak yet but this once: Peradventure ten shall be found there. And he said, I will not destroy it for ten’s sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/18/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54545a79-66cc-4c28-b42d-081a33c9aab9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: GEN 18:33
Text: And the LORD went his way, as soon as he had left communing with Abraham: and Abraham returned unto his place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2dd1a053-d363-4ad1-985c-9f6014f3f4b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: GEN 19:1
Text: And there came two angels to Sodom at even; and Lot sat in the gate of Sodom: and Lot seeing them rose up to meet them; and he bowed himself with his face toward the ground;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01364c09-c98b-4113-8c9d-2e60349be622>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: GEN 19:2
Text: And he said, Behold now, my lords, turn in, I pray you, into your servant’s house, and tarry all night, and wash your feet, and ye shall rise up early, and go on your ways. And they said, Nay; but we will abide in the street all night.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1877e446-7f14-43fd-bc9a-3c45928e0fc3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: GEN 19:3
Text: And he pressed upon them greatly; and they turned in unto him, and entered into his house; and he made them a feast, and did bake unleavened bread, and they did eat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3186c14-7913-4109-8786-0c78ccd60ad4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: GEN 19:4
Text: But before they lay down, the men of the city, even the men of Sodom, compassed the house round, both old and young, all the people from every quarter:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75c67b95-44e0-4e33-ac4f-21c616d3153d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: GEN 19:5
Text: And they called unto Lot, and said unto him, Where are the men which came in to thee this night? bring them out unto us, that we may know them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51a37123-9991-48a7-ab02-b12eba0d391b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: GEN 19:6
Text: And Lot went out at the door unto them, and shut the door after him,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87bf07af-1aa1-454e-88a5-b21b4049e3bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: GEN 19:7
Text: And said, I pray you, brethren, do not so wickedly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9bab059-bed7-49e5-8962-6a05b1674e44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: GEN 19:8
Text: Behold now, I have two daughters which have not known man; let me, I pray you, bring them out unto you, and do ye to them as is good in your eyes: only unto these men do nothing; for therefore came they under the shadow of my roof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b202143-4cfc-40f0-beee-fa988e614c7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: GEN 19:9
Text: And they said, Stand back. And they said again, This one fellow came in to sojourn, and he will needs be a judge: now will we deal worse with thee, than with them. And they pressed sore upon the man, even Lot, and came near to break the door.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3dfe6493-b3ff-44d3-957e-6f6b33a955d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: GEN 19:10
Text: But the men put forth their hand, and pulled Lot into the house to them, and shut to the door.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b22a8be1-c79b-478f-b82a-4d4e9d72c56b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: GEN 19:11
Text: And they smote the men that were at the door of the house with blindness, both small and great: so that they wearied themselves to find the door.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:072231dc-000d-4687-a51d-4074a8bce486>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: GEN 19:12
Text: And the men said unto Lot, Hast thou here any besides? son in law, and thy sons, and thy daughters, and whatsoever thou hast in the city, bring them out of this place:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10fc9ee5-fa3a-4659-8b38-d444deab0177>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: GEN 19:13
Text: For we will destroy this place, because the cry of them is waxen great before the face of the LORD; and the LORD hath sent us to destroy it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c19903ca-9b86-47ba-8a68-f264147d1e58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: GEN 19:14
Text: And Lot went out, and spake unto his sons in law, which married his daughters, and said, Up, get you out of this place; for the LORD will destroy this city. But he seemed as one that mocked unto his sons in law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9a53b75-552d-4779-9a5e-0d53d2ba43d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: GEN 19:15
Text: And when the morning arose, then the angels hastened Lot, saying, Arise, take thy wife, and thy two daughters, which are here; lest thou be consumed in the iniquity of the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75bbdfee-0689-47be-a344-95efc729c51e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: GEN 19:16
Text: And while he lingered, the men laid hold upon his hand, and upon the hand of his wife, and upon the hand of his two daughters; the LORD being merciful unto him: and they brought him forth, and set him without the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e4f70d5-9bab-4fbb-bab3-150438bdff8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: GEN 19:17
Text: And it came to pass, when they had brought them forth abroad, that he said, Escape for thy life; look not behind thee, neither stay thou in all the plain; escape to the mountain, lest thou be consumed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8e20422-9b23-4081-9878-43908ed72b95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 72

Reference: GEN 19:18
Text: And Lot said unto them, Oh, not so, my LORD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:869c59fe-f7d2-4dcd-a834-cb5a8b0f93c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: GEN 19:19
Text: Behold now, thy servant hath found grace in thy sight, and thou hast magnified thy mercy, which thou hast shewed unto me in saving my life; and I cannot escape to the mountain, lest some evil take me, and I die:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88339cde-a401-4b83-a5f2-b6d45868fb1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: GEN 19:20
Text: Behold now, this city is near to flee unto, and it is a little one: Oh, let me escape thither, (is it not a little one?) and my soul shall live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8111f76d-b073-4352-bbf6-c34a76a795bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: GEN 19:21
Text: And he said unto him, See, I have accepted thee concerning this thing also, that I will not overthrow this city, for the which thou hast spoken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bef9d817-e7c5-4f1e-a866-10c1e38b5167>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: GEN 19:22
Text: Haste thee, escape thither; for I cannot do anything till thou be come thither. Therefore the name of the city was called Zoar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83ae2fc3-808a-4bec-b2c1-5fc09e1a96dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: GEN 19:23
Text: The sun was risen upon the earth when Lot entered into Zoar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f989582-a239-4cc6-a1b1-c280109aa407>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: GEN 19:24
Text: Then the LORD rained upon Sodom and upon Gomorrah brimstone and fire from the LORD out of heaven;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48e507e1-1f8e-4ac7-9d0b-e4baf90aafc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: GEN 19:25
Text: And he overthrew those cities, and all the plain, and all the inhabitants of the cities, and that which grew upon the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8438001f-dba6-4ad7-88a1-6f030caa97a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: GEN 19:26
Text: But his wife looked back from behind him, and she became a pillar of salt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7059c203-d922-4f4b-9055-5444204fce2b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: GEN 19:27
Text: And Abraham gat up early in the morning to the place where he stood before the LORD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:003a3732-f27e-414d-a57e-0d03cc5bfcd3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: GEN 19:28
Text: And he looked toward Sodom and Gomorrah, and toward all the land of the plain, and beheld, and, lo, the smoke of the country went up as the smoke of a furnace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b853f348-f372-4c8f-8a62-cf64138cb97c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: GEN 19:29
Text: And it came to pass, when God destroyed the cities of the plain, that God remembered Abraham, and sent Lot out of the midst of the overthrow, when he overthrew the cities in the which Lot dwelt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a4221ca-108b-4b50-89e3-1bf9172d454a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: GEN 19:30
Text: And Lot went up out of Zoar, and dwelt in the mountain, and his two daughters with him; for he feared to dwell in Zoar: and he dwelt in a cave, he and his two daughters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e5ba5c3-55b2-4b01-8342-19949235e3dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: GEN 19:31
Text: And the firstborn said unto the younger, Our father is old, and there is not a man in the earth to come in unto us after the manner of all the earth:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8431a196-eb34-44b6-a1ba-12677da6a14c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: GEN 19:32
Text: Come, let us make our father drink wine, and we will lie with him, that we may preserve seed of our father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be4c376d-3536-4154-802f-3eed5ded960b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: GEN 19:33
Text: And they made their father drink wine that night: and the firstborn went in, and lay with her father; and he perceived not when she lay down, nor when she arose.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61f590a0-201d-414a-a830-0d8f386cc9cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: GEN 19:34
Text: And it came to pass on the morrow, that the firstborn said unto the younger, Behold, I lay yesternight with my father: let us make him drink wine this night also; and go thou in, and lie with him, that we may preserve seed of our father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef3fb70a-bce4-4b9a-8e02-5c348437ca44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: GEN 19:35
Text: And they made their father drink wine that night also: and the younger arose, and lay with him; and he perceived not when she lay down, nor when she arose.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2c6938e-9b5d-49af-b779-32502e0bf253>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: GEN 19:36
Text: Thus were both the daughters of Lot with child by their father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:add94a49-34ff-4aad-8645-aba6ca873e7a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: GEN 19:37
Text: And the first born bare a son, and called his name Moab: the same is the father of the Moabites unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/19/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:561e7df4-806a-479c-94b6-af0ae213f263>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: GEN 19:38
Text: And the younger, she also bare a son, and called his name Benammi: the same is the father of the children of Ammon unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/20/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5716c762-e86c-4028-93f3-7988c30c8be1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: GEN 20:1
Text: And Abraham journeyed from thence toward the south country, and dwelled between Kadesh and Shur, and sojourned in Gerar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/20/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:020ed490-fae3-4732-9a1b-c4c17de02632>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: GEN 20:2
Text: And Abraham said of Sarah his wife, She is my sister: and Abimelech king of Gerar sent, and took Sarah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/20/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4db88014-acce-4377-8872-73ae4ae57669>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: GEN 20:3
Text: But God came to Abimelech in a dream by night, and said to him, Behold, thou art but a dead man, for the woman which thou hast taken; for she is a man’s wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/20/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b681afac-a483-419d-a114-dee1dc73d167>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: GEN 20:4
Text: But Abimelech had not come near her: and he said, LORD, wilt thou slay also a righteous nation?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/20/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8da7e97c-d684-4f98-8dfc-c2b3876ea057>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: GEN 20:5
Text: Said he not unto me, She is my sister? and she, even she herself said, He is my brother: in the integrity of my heart and innocency of my hands have I done this.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/20/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a44135b-e0c6-485e-b889-a8d089e2cb5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: GEN 20:6
Text: And God said unto him in a dream, Yea, I know that thou didst this in the integrity of thy heart; for I also withheld thee from sinning against me: therefore suffered I thee not to touch her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/20/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3499c4f-4f4d-4631-ae12-755b9c258911>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: GEN 20:7
Text: Now therefore restore the man his wife; for he is a prophet, and he shall pray for thee, and thou shalt live: and if thou restore her not, know thou that thou shalt surely die, thou, and all that are thine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/20/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6abbfa76-9e7a-430e-8406-6798c0a430bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: GEN 20:8
Text: Therefore Abimelech rose early in the morning, and called all his servants, and told all these things in their ears: and the men were sore afraid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/20/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0581d08b-47f3-4828-9906-41099069af85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: GEN 20:9
Text: Then Abimelech called Abraham, and said unto him, What hast thou done unto us? and what have I offended thee, that thou hast brought on me and on my kingdom a great sin? thou hast done deeds unto me that ought not to be done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/20/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ba6cbdc-7407-4dbc-89ef-3be080edf925>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: GEN 20:10
Text: And Abimelech said unto Abraham, What sawest thou, that thou hast done this thing?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/20/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21d7da77-fa3a-445e-a1c5-783c72a357f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: GEN 20:11
Text: And Abraham said, Because I thought, Surely the fear of God is not in this place; and they will slay me for my wife’s sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/20/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddf651ea-0dae-47b8-a7e6-f7dc3c7810df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: GEN 20:12
Text: And yet indeed she is my sister; she is the daughter of my father, but not the daughter of my mother; and she became my wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/20/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1feb9755-fa19-4965-99c8-22ea24564e27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: GEN 20:13
Text: And it came to pass, when God caused me to wander from my father’s house, that I said unto her, This is thy kindness which thou shalt shew unto me; at every place whither we shall come, say of me, He is my brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/20/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8681dab-cc19-4680-88b7-d0455f782d97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: GEN 20:14
Text: And Abimelech took sheep, and oxen, and menservants, and womenservants, and gave them unto Abraham, and restored him Sarah his wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/20/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10e22485-b76d-4038-9787-71a477a7073f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: GEN 20:15
Text: And Abimelech said, Behold, my land is before thee: dwell where it pleaseth thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/20/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21a6b4f2-c3aa-403c-a644-9c7a4ddd3d2f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: GEN 20:16
Text: And unto Sarah he said, Behold, I have given thy brother a thousand pieces of silver: behold, he is to thee a covering of the eyes, unto all that are with thee, and with all other: thus she was reproved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/20/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a278e51-e373-4b76-9fb4-43a1ffc6e1de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: GEN 20:17
Text: So Abraham prayed unto God: and God healed Abimelech, and his wife, and his maidservants; and they bare children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/20/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f856e656-a7ae-4737-907c-9393a428f995>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: GEN 20:18
Text: For the LORD had fast closed up all the wombs of the house of Abimelech, because of Sarah Abraham’s wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39226326-3a8c-4bf4-b634-fe57012d337d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: GEN 21:1
Text: And the LORD visited Sarah as he had said, and the LORD did unto Sarah as he had spoken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab05ef26-7280-417d-bb63-06ccd2246cd5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: GEN 21:2
Text: For Sarah conceived, and bare Abraham a son in his old age, at the set time of which God had spoken to him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c7d2e0c-05b6-4f50-95fe-79907a5a9e5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: GEN 21:3
Text: And Abraham called the name of his son that was born unto him, whom Sarah bare to him, Isaac.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d6c8428-291c-4784-9330-65d124f634a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: GEN 21:4
Text: And Abraham circumcised his son Isaac being eight days old, as God had commanded him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c0ae6ca-9bda-4830-a741-60a45248479f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: GEN 21:5
Text: And Abraham was an hundred years old, when his son Isaac was born unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d653844-6e7b-4f82-bc45-326c7c56c8c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: GEN 21:6
Text: And Sarah said, God hath made me to laugh, so that all that hear will laugh with me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87068c4f-be15-42d4-95b3-f724944f07f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: GEN 21:7
Text: And she said, Who would have said unto Abraham, that Sarah should have given children suck? for I have born him a son in his old age.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc6736c3-9fdd-4260-be84-93509407e731>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: GEN 21:8
Text: And the child grew, and was weaned: and Abraham made a great feast the same day that Isaac was weaned.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e5442df-5f8f-4d67-81c5-491d4a70c7ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: GEN 21:9
Text: And Sarah saw the son of Hagar the Egyptian, which she had born unto Abraham, mocking.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9bd07f1e-9734-4deb-87e4-383d54fbed76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: GEN 21:10
Text: Wherefore she said unto Abraham, Cast out this bondwoman and her son: for the son of this bondwoman shall not be heir with my son, even with Isaac.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66b59b03-ea7a-4c55-85e4-34bcd9a01616>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: GEN 21:11
Text: And the thing was very grievous in Abraham’s sight because of his son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7aa9e849-5b7a-437e-b853-ee8adcc18464>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: GEN 21:12
Text: And God said unto Abraham, Let it not be grievous in thy sight because of the lad, and because of thy bondwoman; in all that Sarah hath said unto thee, hearken unto her voice; for in Isaac shall thy seed be called.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3506160-3964-45ed-8b82-fdbd71cb67ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: GEN 21:13
Text: And also of the son of the bondwoman will I make a nation, because he is thy seed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04fae4bf-943a-446f-8b7d-82df86799bf5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: GEN 21:14
Text: And Abraham rose up early in the morning, and took bread, and a bottle of water, and gave it unto Hagar, putting it on her shoulder, and the child, and sent her away: and she departed, and wandered in the wilderness of Beersheba.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a755d074-f2de-4793-986b-129998b356cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: GEN 21:15
Text: And the water was spent in the bottle, and she cast the child under one of the shrubs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:540ad3fa-16ba-453b-b9eb-94a72241ffd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: GEN 21:16
Text: And she went, and sat her down over against him a good way off, as it were a bow shot: for she said, Let me not see the death of the child. And she sat over against him, and lift up her voice, and wept.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44b170ef-2610-47ae-85d3-d3474003d54d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: GEN 21:17
Text: And God heard the voice of the lad; and the angel of God called to Hagar out of heaven, and said unto her, What aileth thee, Hagar? fear not; for God hath heard the voice of the lad where he is.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04f9dd22-a20f-4f6c-93c1-acbf0b29f5e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: GEN 21:18
Text: Arise, lift up the lad, and hold him in thine hand; for I will make him a great nation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8a27e47-a430-4a1b-94b0-b4d2f5a89b19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: GEN 21:19
Text: And God opened her eyes, and she saw a well of water; and she went, and filled the bottle with water, and gave the lad drink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73ba218c-79ce-4c08-9b7c-85f2c8f520aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: GEN 21:20
Text: And God was with the lad; and he grew, and dwelt in the wilderness, and became an archer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:188f6998-000a-4a5e-80d4-3d4480416d54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: GEN 21:21
Text: And he dwelt in the wilderness of Paran: and his mother took him a wife out of the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0980d0a-dee5-40e8-b8e2-ec1fd9a084a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: GEN 21:22
Text: And it came to pass at that time, that Abimelech and Phichol the chief captain of his host spake unto Abraham, saying, God is with thee in all that thou doest:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5beb9631-227b-4696-bcd4-ae3ef70b44d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: GEN 21:23
Text: Now therefore swear unto me here by God that thou wilt not deal falsely with me, nor with my son, nor with my son’s son: but according to the kindness that I have done unto thee, thou shalt do unto me, and to the land wherein thou hast sojourned.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0a141fc-0efa-4053-bf63-518d9a458caa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 59

Reference: GEN 21:24
Text: And Abraham said, I will swear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b09259af-0005-4ee3-b0ff-2a4c3c7025dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: GEN 21:25
Text: And Abraham reproved Abimelech because of a well of water, which Abimelech’s servants had violently taken away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7da78221-0b54-4efb-8007-fd080503f62a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: GEN 21:26
Text: And Abimelech said, I wot not who hath done this thing; neither didst thou tell me, neither yet heard I of it, but to day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78848888-610f-4e63-8e45-52d8af9fccf4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: GEN 21:27
Text: And Abraham took sheep and oxen, and gave them unto Abimelech; and both of them made a covenant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f460b8a-1f50-46a2-a15d-c8aa9f56fc5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: GEN 21:28
Text: And Abraham set seven ewe lambs of the flock by themselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77df6c4c-d598-47e7-a6c9-252409f1db55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: GEN 21:29
Text: And Abimelech said unto Abraham, What mean these seven ewe lambs which thou hast set by themselves?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cce2bc7-dc3d-4274-bf2e-d65bef919f41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: GEN 21:30
Text: And he said, For these seven ewe lambs shalt thou take of my hand, that they may be a witness unto me, that I have digged this well.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99bc7912-3055-4ca8-a3d0-74bd7bbd0f95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: GEN 21:31
Text: Wherefore he called that place Beersheba; because there they sware both of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77fcb893-61cd-4bac-b0bc-58d42dae7ea7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: GEN 21:32
Text: Thus they made a covenant at Beersheba: then Abimelech rose up, and Phichol the chief captain of his host, and they returned into the land of the Philistines.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3cbfcf9-dd31-498d-a09b-8e2698cc00a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: GEN 21:33
Text: And Abraham planted a grove in Beersheba, and called there on the name of the LORD, the everlasting God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/21/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24aa76ec-a821-4f23-88b9-2f5eab35158c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: GEN 21:34
Text: And Abraham sojourned in the Philistines’ land many days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:727db39a-7a62-44e9-9cb8-76c623a97450>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: GEN 22:1
Text: And it came to pass after these things, that God did tempt Abraham, and said unto him, Abraham: and he said, Behold, here I am.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b4e03e4-bb24-4ca4-9a58-6cf53cb26e8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: GEN 22:2
Text: And he said, Take now thy son, thine only son Isaac, whom thou lovest, and get thee into the land of Moriah; and offer him there for a burnt offering upon one of the mountains which I will tell thee of.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9bed796-0cc8-499c-9602-e721d74e8622>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: GEN 22:3
Text: And Abraham rose up early in the morning, and saddled his ass, and took two of his young men with him, and Isaac his son, and clave the wood for the burnt offering, and rose up, and went unto the place of which God had told him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38233376-a4fc-4e65-bdcd-1e84d88d1b7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: GEN 22:4
Text: Then on the third day Abraham lifted up his eyes, and saw the place afar off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97c4895f-b638-4b99-96a9-4f9a516808ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: GEN 22:5
Text: And Abraham said unto his young men, Abide ye here with the ass; and I and the lad will go yonder and worship, and come again to you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6746c69-561e-46ec-a2dc-6dd1c11e6bfb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: GEN 22:6
Text: And Abraham took the wood of the burnt offering, and laid it upon Isaac his son; and he took the fire in his hand, and a knife; and they went both of them together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2099c32a-716b-4234-a8d5-805963ed8b07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: GEN 22:7
Text: And Isaac spake unto Abraham his father, and said, My father: and he said, Here am I, my son. And he said, Behold the fire and the wood: but where is the lamb for a burnt offering?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29ff264c-fb7a-42a5-a3f7-5fe42b9525e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: GEN 22:8
Text: And Abraham said, My son, God will provide himself a lamb for a burnt offering: so they went both of them together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea1f0fa3-f304-440d-ab3c-d01d75b6ea3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: GEN 22:9
Text: And they came to the place which God had told him of; and Abraham built an altar there, and laid the wood in order, and bound Isaac his son, and laid him on the altar upon the wood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c40f589-fd21-4d24-b0f3-cf64ff88742d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: GEN 22:10
Text: And Abraham stretched forth his hand, and took the knife to slay his son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cabd0354-f3b3-43a1-9f5f-00a7196dd6d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: GEN 22:11
Text: And the angel of the LORD called unto him out of heaven, and said, Abraham, Abraham: and he said, Here am I.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f48c01b8-6798-4d57-90bf-0ea26f7c61b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: GEN 22:12
Text: And he said, Lay not thine hand upon the lad, neither do thou any thing unto him: for now I know that thou fearest God, seeing thou hast not withheld thy son, thine only son from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fff36496-be5e-4063-8cbc-938e8ddc6c4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: GEN 22:13
Text: And Abraham lifted up his eyes, and looked, and behold behind him a ram caught in a thicket by his horns: and Abraham went and took the ram, and offered him up for a burnt offering in the stead of his son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f14a5945-3fde-4a12-ac28-bda420babc1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: GEN 22:14
Text: And Abraham called the name of that place Jehovahjireh: as it is said to this day, In the mount of the LORD it shall be seen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3020b59-3c84-491f-9937-a7f0634a48d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: GEN 22:15
Text: And the angel of the LORD called unto Abraham out of heaven the second time,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bdf78455-9fa7-481a-8bd3-ccadafdadd52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: GEN 22:16
Text: And said, By myself have I sworn, saith the LORD, for because thou hast done this thing, and hast not withheld thy son, thine only son:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e67dbd38-e69c-4fe7-ac5a-de33241546e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: GEN 22:17
Text: That in blessing I will bless thee, and in multiplying I will multiply thy seed as the stars of the heaven, and as the sand which is upon the sea shore; and thy seed shall possess the gate of his enemies;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89d7f4ce-488a-46a5-a7cb-2c24af97f366>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: GEN 22:18
Text: And in thy seed shall all the nations of the earth be blessed; because thou hast obeyed my voice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0e86f38-9da2-423d-83f0-6a4c8499fd88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: GEN 22:19
Text: So Abraham returned unto his young men, and they rose up and went together to Beersheba; and Abraham dwelt at Beersheba.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ce4e313-63c9-4707-b5ec-42c3d37a948a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: GEN 22:20
Text: And it came to pass after these things, that it was told Abraham, saying, Behold, Milcah, she hath also born children unto thy brother Nahor;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c05dee3-0cec-40d2-9ad7-75a3d7655e55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: GEN 22:21
Text: Huz his firstborn, and Buz his brother, and Kemuel the father of Aram,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89e3ce75-877c-459b-9587-76293382e8ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: GEN 22:22
Text: And Chesed, and Hazo, and Pildash, and Jidlaph, and Bethuel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c65dde76-572a-4df7-9872-f6a0d71ec80f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: GEN 22:23
Text: And Bethuel begat Rebekah: these eight Milcah did bear to Nahor, Abraham’s brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/22/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:755e7371-8758-41bc-803c-7aa674a9aaed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: GEN 22:24
Text: And his concubine, whose name was Reumah, she bare also Tebah, and Gaham, and Thahash, and Maachah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/23/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2344d5e-527f-41dc-bd6b-b5e6415b74b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: GEN 23:1
Text: And Sarah was an hundred and seven and twenty years old: these were the years of the life of Sarah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/23/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52bd4f45-44c7-465b-babc-10b0f31e73fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: GEN 23:2
Text: And Sarah died in Kirjatharba; the same is Hebron in the land of Canaan: and Abraham came to mourn for Sarah, and to weep for her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/23/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d102bfe-80e3-44aa-b9a7-c4fb60386bc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: GEN 23:3
Text: And Abraham stood up from before his dead, and spake unto the sons of Heth, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/23/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ccad7914-a286-4ece-8fba-20540e174d21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: GEN 23:4
Text: I am a stranger and a sojourner with you: give me a possession of a buryingplace with you, that I may bury my dead out of my sight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/23/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff46e224-6d77-4a19-ab12-3a29d3e6a6f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: GEN 23:5
Text: And the children of Heth answered Abraham, saying unto him,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/23/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3facdc0-0835-4abb-8633-b54eb65c5579>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: GEN 23:6
Text: Hear us, my lord: thou art a mighty prince among us: in the choice of our sepulchres bury thy dead; none of us shall withhold from thee his sepulchre, but that thou mayest bury thy dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/23/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79292af2-0ba3-4095-b2ec-52751678a2b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: GEN 23:7
Text: And Abraham stood up, and bowed himself to the people of the land, even to the children of Heth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/23/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7f56c2e-6d77-406a-9492-5c179f5da4df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: GEN 23:8
Text: And he communed with them, saying, If it be your mind that I should bury my dead out of my sight; hear me, and intreat for me to Ephron the son of Zohar,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/23/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db3ae11f-69e2-4e4d-a4b4-6b52bfa3b063>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: GEN 23:9
Text: That he may give me the cave of Machpelah, which he hath, which is in the end of his field; for as much money as it is worth he shall give it me for a possession of a buryingplace amongst you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/23/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19ccb65b-0443-49b6-b77b-5f3387b0e9fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: GEN 23:10
Text: And Ephron dwelt among the children of Heth: and Ephron the Hittite answered Abraham in the audience of the children of Heth, even of all that went in at the gate of his city, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/23/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34a8fa0f-a406-4c4e-819e-fc5f3e5658e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: GEN 23:11
Text: Nay, my lord, hear me: the field give I thee, and the cave that is therein, I give it thee; in the presence of the sons of my people give I it thee: bury thy dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/23/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1f6cd28-42d7-454a-aa43-89c9942eed25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: GEN 23:12
Text: And Abraham bowed down himself before the people of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/23/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b92bdcca-8cc4-4fff-835c-3e6ae76bbd94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: GEN 23:13
Text: And he spake unto Ephron in the audience of the people of the land, saying, But if thou wilt give it, I pray thee, hear me: I will give thee money for the field; take it of me, and I will bury my dead there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/23/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b3ebc2f-26af-4028-864f-ea8ef7e85796>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: GEN 23:14
Text: And Ephron answered Abraham, saying unto him,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/23/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b39fe6d6-a192-4924-8cbe-0cbebf122604>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: GEN 23:15
Text: My lord, hearken unto me: the land is worth four hundred shekels of silver; what is that betwixt me and thee? bury therefore thy dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/23/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:726d367a-ac86-447a-80dc-ac8397cb8033>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: GEN 23:16
Text: And Abraham hearkened unto Ephron; and Abraham weighed to Ephron the silver, which he had named in the audience of the sons of Heth, four hundred shekels of silver, current money with the merchant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/23/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3bee8953-7033-4d76-bf99-47d4775e2fe9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: GEN 23:17
Text: And the field of Ephron which was in Machpelah, which was before Mamre, the field, and the cave which was therein, and all the trees that were in the field, that were in all the borders round about, were made sure


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/23/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7de352c-dfa3-4924-83ea-5b4e42897dd8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: GEN 23:18
Text: Unto Abraham for a possession in the presence of the children of Heth, before all that went in at the gate of his city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/23/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db25cf4e-7786-4a3a-8986-ca9b79f7b1a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: GEN 23:19
Text: And after this, Abraham buried Sarah his wife in the cave of the field of Machpelah before Mamre: the same is Hebron in the land of Canaan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/23/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fa53111-b5b7-40c1-bd09-3dcb1206d1af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: GEN 23:20
Text: And the field, and the cave that is therein, were made sure unto Abraham for a possession of a buryingplace by the sons of Heth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cb9c477-0961-42b5-a2ee-50cccac2b79d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: GEN 24:1
Text: And Abraham was old, and well stricken in age: and the LORD had blessed Abraham in all things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a343325-36cc-44ab-9234-65f5bc90b041>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: GEN 24:2
Text: And Abraham said unto his eldest servant of his house, that ruled over all that he had, Put, I pray thee, thy hand under my thigh:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d7f1ef5-db2c-4b32-acb8-c68c6524f6a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: GEN 24:3
Text: And I will make thee swear by the LORD, the God of heaven, and the God of the earth, that thou shalt not take a wife unto my son of the daughters of the Canaanites, among whom I dwell:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a43853c8-2e86-4c7d-87ba-f72f4d633ce2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: GEN 24:4
Text: But thou shalt go unto my country, and to my kindred, and take a wife unto my son Isaac.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af137504-a037-4f21-b8b1-09c6509e6f5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: GEN 24:5
Text: And the servant said unto him, Peradventure the woman will not be willing to follow me unto this land: must I needs bring thy son again unto the land from whence thou camest?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84f096e8-6dcf-4c8e-8b1d-1417f02e23b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: GEN 24:6
Text: And Abraham said unto him, Beware thou that thou bring not my son thither again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d500273c-bbde-46d4-b510-826cf9abd3c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 306

Reference: GEN 24:7
Text: The LORD God of heaven, which took me from my father’s house, and from the land of my kindred, and which spake unto me, and that sware unto me, saying, Unto thy seed will I give this land; he shall send his angel before thee, and thou shalt take a wife unto my son from thence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18999cb8-c2c9-40e6-8ae6-f47f90f5e716>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: GEN 24:8
Text: And if the woman will not be willing to follow thee, then thou shalt be clear from this my oath: only bring not my son thither again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a3abf9d-9c67-496b-8f9f-5848c5138b07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: GEN 24:9
Text: And the servant put his hand under the thigh of Abraham his master, and sware to him concerning that matter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ba934d5-db33-4fc2-ab4a-94ec997115b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: GEN 24:10
Text: And the servant took ten camels of the camels of his master, and departed; for all the goods of his master were in his hand: and he arose, and went to Mesopotamia, unto the city of Nahor.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8190aa5-f1e2-494a-852d-b375f4a986bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: GEN 24:11
Text: And he made his camels to kneel down without the city by a well of water at the time of the evening, even the time that women go out to draw water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14010eab-b037-433d-ac5a-80b14af46716>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: GEN 24:12
Text: And he said O LORD God of my master Abraham, I pray thee, send me good speed this day, and shew kindness unto my master Abraham.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7242a851-aa4c-405a-b43a-0390d5610c2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: GEN 24:13
Text: Behold, I stand here by the well of water; and the daughters of the men of the city come out to draw water:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd15f6ca-7b55-456a-99bf-dfcdbb090a41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 347

Reference: GEN 24:14
Text: And let it come to pass, that the damsel to whom I shall say, Let down thy pitcher, I pray thee, that I may drink; and she shall say, Drink, and I will give thy camels drink also: let the same be she that thou hast appointed for thy servant Isaac; and thereby shall I know that thou hast shewed kindness unto my master.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:572c6e2c-08a9-45fc-887d-9649e48426a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: GEN 24:15
Text: And it came to pass, before he had done speaking, that, behold, Rebekah came out, who was born to Bethuel, son of Milcah, the wife of Nahor, Abraham’s brother, with her pitcher upon her shoulder.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:877b3e46-6e33-4d6d-9123-4a8481fe8f87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: GEN 24:16
Text: And the damsel was very fair to look upon, a virgin, neither had any man known her: and she went down to the well, and filled her pitcher, and came up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:957ac39c-1ce2-44ae-8a43-f1a7943595e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: GEN 24:17
Text: And the servant ran to meet her, and said, Let me, I pray thee, drink a little water of thy pitcher.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1d2bf87-4946-4d79-946c-fdce9e50dccf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: GEN 24:18
Text: And she said, Drink, my lord: and she hasted, and let down her pitcher upon her hand, and gave him drink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7698e48c-faa9-42b5-b91e-6c1b79f6137e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: GEN 24:19
Text: And when she had done giving him drink, she said, I will draw water for thy camels also, until they have done drinking.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18b666d4-cf8d-4d4a-9c9c-d8794eb5ba65>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: GEN 24:20
Text: And she hasted, and emptied her pitcher into the trough, and ran again unto the well to draw water, and drew for all his camels.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4dff48c-ce9b-40c4-911c-d828253f2834>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: GEN 24:21
Text: And the man wondering at her held his peace, to wit whether the LORD had made his journey prosperous or not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36a6c7d3-adf5-41c8-a6a3-183413328931>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: GEN 24:22
Text: And it came to pass, as the camels had done drinking, that the man took a golden earring of half a shekel weight, and two bracelets for her hands of ten shekels weight of gold;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5dc93d83-3950-4879-97d2-cf504cd5697b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: GEN 24:23
Text: And said, Whose daughter art thou? tell me, I pray thee: is there room in thy father’s house for us to lodge in?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f392dd8-c2bd-49d9-8208-ed774039adc9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: GEN 24:24
Text: And she said unto him, I am the daughter of Bethuel the son of Milcah, which she bare unto Nahor.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a4cc6ad-f313-4b79-9464-b97219576b7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: GEN 24:25
Text: She said moreover unto him, We have both straw and provender enough, and room to lodge in.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb664fc6-3307-44f3-bd4c-f1ce39aa450b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: GEN 24:26
Text: And the man bowed down his head, and worshipped the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07a25ecf-a590-4aea-b4ee-67ac1f02aaa5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: GEN 24:27
Text: And he said, Blessed be the LORD God of my master Abraham, who hath not left destitute my master of his mercy and his truth: I being in the way, the LORD led me to the house of my master’s brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cbe0f35-e37e-46bf-89f7-5e57ef71436f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: GEN 24:28
Text: And the damsel ran, and told them of her mother’s house these things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:349e5c4d-c965-49dd-9f20-16792796f77f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: GEN 24:29
Text: And Rebekah had a brother, and his name was Laban: and Laban ran out unto the man, unto the well.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d4883a1-fb1c-45a7-adc4-2861bef77236>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: GEN 24:30
Text: And it came to pass, when he saw the earring and bracelets upon his sister’s hands, and when he heard the words of Rebekah his sister, saying, Thus spake the man unto me; that he came unto the man; and, behold, he stood by the camels at the well.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51b67a09-5eca-45ff-a73d-b3c0b9bd9b2d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: GEN 24:31
Text: And he said, Come in, thou blessed of the LORD; wherefore standest thou without? for I have prepared the house, and room for the camels.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0055480a-4cbd-4b1f-892e-b53f71b5c0a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: GEN 24:32
Text: And the man came into the house: and he ungirded his camels, and gave straw and provender for the camels, and water to wash his feet, and the men’s feet that were with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fad6f840-0814-46ae-ad29-2bdd05f2c08f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: GEN 24:33
Text: And there was set meat before him to eat: but he said, I will not eat, until I have told mine errand. And he said, Speak on.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5987b2f1-404e-40cc-90a4-fb9749046f91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 66

Reference: GEN 24:34
Text: And he said, I am Abraham’s servant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:656435c7-bd3b-4b1d-8ceb-b4524ff1da8e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: GEN 24:35
Text: And the LORD hath blessed my master greatly; and he is become great: and he hath given him flocks, and herds, and silver, and gold, and menservants, and maidservants, and camels, and asses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af85a2fa-d3e1-4cf9-8a9b-9c9f05d7070f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: GEN 24:36
Text: And Sarah my master’s wife bare a son to my master when she was old: and unto him hath he given all that he hath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:620ab8ba-c322-4680-b9fb-ef2d917388c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: GEN 24:37
Text: And my master made me swear, saying, Thou shalt not take a wife to my son of the daughters of the Canaanites, in whose land I dwell:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:756f473e-cf5b-4579-a76d-71b15005e9c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: GEN 24:38
Text: But thou shalt go unto my father’s house, and to my kindred, and take a wife unto my son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24f14e64-3a7f-4655-8ea6-0fe6b78998e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: GEN 24:39
Text: And I said unto my master, Peradventure the woman will not follow me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f24c0d33-3d0e-4542-9cfd-1d4489c82a01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: GEN 24:40
Text: And he said unto me, The LORD, before whom I walk, will send his angel with thee, and prosper thy way; and thou shalt take a wife for my son of my kindred, and of my father’s house:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fff16e41-9a1c-46d4-a4e7-020a53e0305c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: GEN 24:41
Text: Then shalt thou be clear from this my oath, when thou comest to my kindred; and if they give not thee one, thou shalt be clear from my oath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ba3cb7f-2a06-416b-8f58-260fca6b2fdf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: GEN 24:42
Text: And I came this day unto the well, and said, O LORD God of my master Abraham, if now thou do prosper my way which I go:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f829ae7-3898-46bd-80ad-390813fcf297>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: GEN 24:43
Text: Behold, I stand by the well of water; and it shall come to pass, that when the virgin cometh forth to draw water, and I say to her, Give me, I pray thee, a little water of thy pitcher to drink;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:161730de-283b-42bb-a0fd-dce9edf35898>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: GEN 24:44
Text: And she say to me, Both drink thou, and I will also draw for thy camels: let the same be the woman whom the LORD hath appointed out for my master’s son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e65507d4-e833-488d-9aef-35e7afb31d70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: GEN 24:45
Text: And before I had done speaking in mine heart, behold, Rebekah came forth with her pitcher on her shoulder; and she went down unto the well, and drew water: and I said unto her, Let me drink, I pray thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:626839b8-5fe8-4f1b-8edf-6f67862c5a60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: GEN 24:46
Text: And she made haste, and let down her pitcher from her shoulder, and said, Drink, and I will give thy camels drink also: so I drank, and she made the camels drink also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23d621a4-da42-4fd4-a5e1-344ea5c881f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: GEN 24:47
Text: And I asked her, and said, Whose daughter art thou? And she said, the daughter of Bethuel, Nahor’s son, whom Milcah bare unto him: and I put the earring upon her face, and the bracelets upon her hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fcdeff28-f43f-4b21-a15d-ec9f6c8e3e0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: GEN 24:48
Text: And I bowed down my head, and worshipped the LORD, and blessed the LORD God of my master Abraham, which had led me in the right way to take my master’s brother’s daughter unto his son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dcdce372-019d-4614-b278-2c4cad999064>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: GEN 24:49
Text: And now if ye will deal kindly and truly with my master, tell me: and if not, tell me; that I may turn to the right hand, or to the left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c071e427-dab4-4cc9-b52f-06b4c1b0e5a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: GEN 24:50
Text: Then Laban and Bethuel answered and said, The thing proceedeth from the LORD: we cannot speak unto thee bad or good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10c1304c-d33e-43ee-ade4-cafe456fb6fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: GEN 24:51
Text: Behold, Rebekah is before thee, take her, and go, and let her be thy master’s son’s wife, as the LORD hath spoken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dff78a7d-fa48-4f42-95e8-33e2afce35bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: GEN 24:52
Text: And it came to pass, that, when Abraham’s servant heard their words, he worshipped the LORD, bowing himself to the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6735c1fa-c888-4fbe-8ea4-6aed16b3273f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: GEN 24:53
Text: And the servant brought forth jewels of silver, and jewels of gold, and raiment, and gave them to Rebekah: he gave also to her brother and to her mother precious things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d45ef58-0e06-4847-9150-8ab5827a8afc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: GEN 24:54
Text: And they did eat and drink, he and the men that were with him, and tarried all night; and they rose up in the morning, and he said, Send me away unto my master.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/55
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:436ec5a2-28af-4611-8e4a-00ebc9ec1375>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: GEN 24:55
Text: And her brother and her mother said, Let the damsel abide with us a few days, at the least ten; after that she shall go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/56
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04e79679-1f04-46e8-a9f3-cae3dcd35efe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: GEN 24:56
Text: And he said unto them, Hinder me not, seeing the LORD hath prospered my way; send me away that I may go to my master.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/57
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e048cad4-41e3-41f0-a761-5e98a466fb74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: GEN 24:57
Text: And they said, We will call the damsel, and enquire at her mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/58
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7c7d64e-8314-4c54-a826-c56c0ce3b6fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: GEN 24:58
Text: And they called Rebekah, and said unto her, Wilt thou go with this man? And she said, I will go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/59
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8afb2a1f-8877-4d82-a7fa-c09621fba5cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: GEN 24:59
Text: And they sent away Rebekah their sister, and her nurse, and Abraham’s servant, and his men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/60
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60d29351-b2c2-4039-804a-5c87d848c31b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: GEN 24:60
Text: And they blessed Rebekah, and said unto her, Thou art our sister, be thou the mother of thousands of millions, and let thy seed possess the gate of those which hate them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/61
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6210c8a8-2296-4c2e-acc4-70fa803ca463>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: GEN 24:61
Text: And Rebekah arose, and her damsels, and they rode upon the camels, and followed the man: and the servant took Rebekah, and went his way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/62
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bb3453e-ee8a-4b5d-9e2f-39def529d453>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: GEN 24:62
Text: And Isaac came from the way of the well Lahairoi; for he dwelt in the south country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/63
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a1ad21b-df2e-4e54-809e-b4edf7a0790c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: GEN 24:63
Text: And Isaac went out to meditate in the field at the eventide: and he lifted up his eyes, and saw, and, behold, the camels were coming.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/64
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b8e9322-dfbb-48a2-bf39-b1ae0ddf1827>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: GEN 24:64
Text: And Rebekah lifted up her eyes, and when she saw Isaac, she lighted off the camel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/65
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79658f69-af7e-45e9-820e-f7b217c2f7c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: GEN 24:65
Text: For she had said unto the servant, What man is this that walketh in the field to meet us? And the servant had said, It is my master: therefore she took a vail, and covered herself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/66
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4771fe8-3efc-4645-90ba-ec1901ac5692>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: GEN 24:66
Text: And the servant told Isaac all things that he had done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/24/67
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8106d985-a631-4c18-a70b-ee7312e9441e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: GEN 24:67
Text: And Isaac brought her into his mother Sarah’s tent, and took Rebekah, and she became his wife; and he loved her: and Isaac was comforted after his mother’s death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10e5281e-f564-4a64-bbc2-87c3836981ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: GEN 25:1
Text: Then again Abraham took a wife, and her name was Keturah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c883d7b7-4174-42f9-b4c4-6867447b3de2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: GEN 25:2
Text: And she bare him Zimran, and Jokshan, and Medan, and Midian, and Ishbak, and Shuah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b6b9f59-98e4-4635-bc72-751c4c365925>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: GEN 25:3
Text: And Jokshan begat Sheba, and Dedan. And the sons of Dedan were Asshurim, and Letushim, and Leummim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69f73cc6-b95c-4405-9a94-d36ba0f41c6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: GEN 25:4
Text: And the sons of Midian; Ephah, and Epher, and Hanoch, and Abidah, and Eldaah. All these were the children of Keturah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e6f53d8-a2ad-44c8-90da-a0c6180ee48b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 71

Reference: GEN 25:5
Text: And Abraham gave all that he had unto Isaac.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00d01e05-8025-4ab1-8ba1-9988b342333c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: GEN 25:6
Text: But unto the sons of the concubines, which Abraham had, Abraham gave gifts, and sent them away from Isaac his son, while he yet lived, eastward, unto the east country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b37d36f4-95e8-4aed-86f1-a25f5675a04c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: GEN 25:7
Text: And these are the days of the years of Abraham’s life which he lived, an hundred threescore and fifteen years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4fa8b4a-cc78-44ec-9ae9-c1c8c2547adb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: GEN 25:8
Text: Then Abraham gave up the ghost, and died in a good old age, an old man, and full of years; and was gathered to his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5132a46d-c74f-463e-8722-c4763f0a1a91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: GEN 25:9
Text: And his sons Isaac and Ishmael buried him in the cave of Machpelah, in the field of Ephron the son of Zohar the Hittite, which is before Mamre;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2566087-e74c-4b86-b8a8-e794d33ae4f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: GEN 25:10
Text: The field which Abraham purchased of the sons of Heth: there was Abraham buried, and Sarah his wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06581a4a-237a-4cd0-9e51-0bd4a12c7ade>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: GEN 25:11
Text: And it came to pass after the death of Abraham, that God blessed his son Isaac; and Isaac dwelt by the well Lahairoi.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04a43186-d1e8-4dfd-bcc0-1e5b96c6264f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: GEN 25:12
Text: Now these are the generations of Ishmael, Abraham’s son, whom Hagar the Egyptian, Sarah’s handmaid, bare unto Abraham:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8422aca0-7bf2-41a2-804b-073155e69c6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: GEN 25:13
Text: And these are the names of the sons of Ishmael, by their names, according to their generations: the firstborn of Ishmael, Nebajoth; and Kedar, and Adbeel, and Mibsam,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa9f6501-ef73-4d40-9fa5-1c977c58c920>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 61

Reference: GEN 25:14
Text: And Mishma, and Dumah, and Massa,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51d13e58-218c-4329-8c2c-4311b7211860>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: GEN 25:15
Text: Hadar, and Tema, Jetur, Naphish, and Kedemah:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac271e9b-f6fd-45cc-ac89-28d2e5c97287>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: GEN 25:16
Text: These are the sons of Ishmael, and these are their names, by their towns, and by their castles; twelve princes according to their nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7766e66f-559f-40e4-a576-4e2384840254>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: GEN 25:17
Text: And these are the years of the life of Ishmael, an hundred and thirty and seven years: and he gave up the ghost and died; and was gathered unto his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e73f665-784d-4732-a0a5-d2edb6e5e6ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: GEN 25:18
Text: And they dwelt from Havilah unto Shur, that is before Egypt, as thou goest toward Assyria: and he died in the presence of all his brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a106f064-d549-47b0-aa4f-648ee11a1b32>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: GEN 25:19
Text: And these are the generations of Isaac, Abraham’s son: Abraham begat Isaac:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:430203f0-8e8d-4bf8-9a5a-972b4d0c958a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: GEN 25:20
Text: And Isaac was forty years old when he took Rebekah to wife, the daughter of Bethuel the Syrian of Padanaram, the sister to Laban the Syrian.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ed5d797-8ac8-415c-b0f2-4b6141a47f60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: GEN 25:21
Text: And Isaac intreated the LORD for his wife, because she was barren: and the LORD was intreated of him, and Rebekah his wife conceived.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa97213c-f9cc-4727-a381-1f8366cb3df6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: GEN 25:22
Text: And the children struggled together within her; and she said, If it be so, why am I thus? And she went to enquire of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00d9bab8-aa4f-4ffb-ac75-2dd2da595078>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: GEN 25:23
Text: And the LORD said unto her, Two nations are in thy womb, and two manner of people shall be separated from thy bowels; and the one people shall be stronger than the other people; and the elder shall serve the younger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73a7660d-b67e-44e5-987a-c6de52f7d249>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: GEN 25:24
Text: And when her days to be delivered were fulfilled, behold, there were twins in her womb.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ff19bcf-39c0-4263-b2f6-93070cc0a040>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: GEN 25:25
Text: And the first came out red, all over like an hairy garment; and they called his name Esau.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f8c09fd-64bb-4f19-bf0b-a1474fa486cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: GEN 25:26
Text: And after that came his brother out, and his hand took hold on Esau’s heel; and his name was called Jacob: and Isaac was threescore years old when she bare them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96597d86-0521-4749-b2b4-fc6cb782fb66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: GEN 25:27
Text: And the boys grew: and Esau was a cunning hunter, a man of the field; and Jacob was a plain man, dwelling in tents.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef494f00-e81d-4f87-bb49-37a68dcfcdb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: GEN 25:28
Text: And Isaac loved Esau, because he did eat of his venison: but Rebekah loved Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:188298be-84d7-43c6-9cf5-77fe48535770>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: GEN 25:29
Text: And Jacob sod pottage: and Esau came from the field, and he was faint:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d01abc5-80ff-41ce-b39f-727525d39515>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: GEN 25:30
Text: And Esau said to Jacob, Feed me, I pray thee, with that same red pottage; for I am faint: therefore was his name called Edom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d695e9f8-9050-4dfa-bd2e-c0383e372c90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: GEN 25:31
Text: And Jacob said, Sell me this day thy birthright.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90dc469d-e082-4c4e-9887-1619312748c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: GEN 25:32
Text: And Esau said, Behold, I am at the point to die: and what profit shall this birthright do to me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a8ab0e6-a709-4e8e-b358-0c1bc0290a22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: GEN 25:33
Text: And Jacob said, Swear to me this day; and he sware unto him: and he sold his birthright unto Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/25/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef1a04b8-bff2-4e5e-b2f7-040309451438>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: GEN 25:34
Text: Then Jacob gave Esau bread and pottage of lentiles; and he did eat and drink, and rose up, and went his way: thus Esau despised his birthright.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a92feb17-f34b-4883-99ca-10052e0ff002>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: GEN 26:1
Text: And there was a famine in the land, beside the first famine that was in the days of Abraham. And Isaac went unto Abimelech king of the Philistines unto Gerar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:229f6af6-e3d1-4858-8693-cdc436339530>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: GEN 26:2
Text: And the LORD appeared unto him, and said, Go not down into Egypt; dwell in the land which I shall tell thee of:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6d9ee44-642e-465e-9c5d-fd4a6f883998>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: GEN 26:3
Text: Sojourn in this land, and I will be with thee, and will bless thee; for unto thee, and unto thy seed, I will give all these countries, and I will perform the oath which I sware unto Abraham thy father;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19dd7f09-8683-4eac-aa91-c8f3664551a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: GEN 26:4
Text: And I will make thy seed to multiply as the stars of heaven, and will give unto thy seed all these countries; and in thy seed shall all the nations of the earth be blessed;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50c6d2b5-aff0-4308-9d19-0ad5b76f877d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: GEN 26:5
Text: Because that Abraham obeyed my voice, and kept my charge, my commandments, my statutes, and my laws.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0463c5a6-d7bc-4a9e-b43e-d331033c4eab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 52

Reference: GEN 26:6
Text: And Isaac dwelt in Gerar:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abc83306-42a2-43ae-89fc-0de9cd04beb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: GEN 26:7
Text: And the men of the place asked him of his wife; and he said, She is my sister: for he feared to say, She is my wife; lest, said he, the men of the place should kill me for Rebekah; because she was fair to look upon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75131551-37ad-4d4a-8796-7671ee5c72a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: GEN 26:8
Text: And it came to pass, when he had been there a long time, that Abimelech king of the Philistines looked out at a window, and saw, and, behold, Isaac was sporting with Rebekah his wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3035875-b9e8-4540-85df-3fe5193c8fdf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: GEN 26:9
Text: And Abimelech called Isaac, and said, Behold, of a surety she is thy wife; and how saidst thou, She is my sister? And Isaac said unto him, Because I said, Lest I die for her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a6025b5-d034-467d-9937-9d7a19938ce8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: GEN 26:10
Text: And Abimelech said, What is this thou hast done unto us? one of the people might lightly have lien with thy wife, and thou shouldest have brought guiltiness upon us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b23157d-c9f4-4b08-beb9-336ffedd1b8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: GEN 26:11
Text: And Abimelech charged all his people, saying, He that toucheth this man or his wife shall surely be put to death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21564426-625b-494f-a7aa-0e9deb31c93c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: GEN 26:12
Text: Then Isaac sowed in that land, and received in the same year an hundredfold: and the LORD blessed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc78c5d4-c408-4e45-9b04-2e230181fbbe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: GEN 26:13
Text: And the man waxed great, and went forward, and grew until he became very great:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c45fe83d-f55c-40c1-888f-98d4ea30c5c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: GEN 26:14
Text: For he had possession of flocks, and possession of herds, and great store of servants: and the Philistines envied him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d8c8b35-96c1-4f60-9abd-e18ffcd8c56f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: GEN 26:15
Text: For all the wells which his father’s servants had digged in the days of Abraham his father, the Philistines had stopped them, and filled them with earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32a6329d-f38e-41d9-878a-1dd744bc4764>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: GEN 26:16
Text: And Abimelech said unto Isaac, Go from us; for thou art much mightier than we.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ccb948ad-99c0-4795-910d-a29b59126813>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: GEN 26:17
Text: And Isaac departed thence, and pitched his tent in the valley of Gerar, and dwelt there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9ca589b-dc62-4fcf-85f1-2378129ada85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: GEN 26:18
Text: And Isaac digged again the wells of water, which they had digged in the days of Abraham his father; for the Philistines had stopped them after the death of Abraham: and he called their names after the names by which his father had called them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c498a3b8-2741-45bd-8145-b77d9d08d18e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: GEN 26:19
Text: And Isaac’s servants digged in the valley, and found there a well of springing water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc68b4ed-9e80-4f23-a2b8-7d2a8e72e573>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: GEN 26:20
Text: And the herdmen of Gerar did strive with Isaac’s herdmen, saying, The water is ours: and he called the name of the well Esek; because they strove with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d75b26c-76a6-4104-b8e3-35650c27645a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: GEN 26:21
Text: And they digged another well, and strove for that also: and he called the name of it Sitnah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8784db8-f7d9-4774-8204-52d39f22a4fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: GEN 26:22
Text: And he removed from thence, and digged another well; and for that they strove not: and he called the name of it Rehoboth; and he said, For now the LORD hath made room for us, and we shall be fruitful in the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4ce179f-c990-4a39-88b6-e594554d7662>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 68

Reference: GEN 26:23
Text: And he went up from thence to Beersheba.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e21ff517-36f7-4781-86a8-a424981ee31d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: GEN 26:24
Text: And the LORD appeared unto him the same night, and said, I am the God of Abraham thy father: fear not, for I am with thee, and will bless thee, and multiply thy seed for my servant Abraham’s sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:790545b1-31fc-4a75-a365-49f7225fedb6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: GEN 26:25
Text: And he builded an altar there, and called upon the name of the LORD, and pitched his tent there: and there Isaac’s servants digged a well.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5aaa7e3-15f9-480e-bdbf-97a1e8a42bd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: GEN 26:26
Text: Then Abimelech went to him from Gerar, and Ahuzzath one of his friends, and Phichol the chief captain of his army.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a71093b-9a4f-429a-ad7f-0c9bfb9f4476>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: GEN 26:27
Text: And Isaac said unto them, Wherefore come ye to me, seeing ye hate me, and have sent me away from you?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:452cbacb-bfef-418b-b9b3-7918652c29eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: GEN 26:28
Text: And they said, We saw certainly that the LORD was with thee: and we said, Let there be now an oath betwixt us, even betwixt us and thee, and let us make a covenant with thee;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1755c9e1-05aa-4d39-9c0e-11cd64190125>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: GEN 26:29
Text: That thou wilt do us no hurt, as we have not touched thee, and as we have done unto thee nothing but good, and have sent thee away in peace: thou art now the blessed of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55b55edb-92cc-42f3-994a-60814ae9ad1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: GEN 26:30
Text: And he made them a feast, and they did eat and drink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6dc9cba-8997-424b-b8ff-1c67c061b19a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: GEN 26:31
Text: And they rose up betimes in the morning, and sware one to another: and Isaac sent them away, and they departed from him in peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d759a9fb-48ce-45b0-9272-9185fa6aba78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: GEN 26:32
Text: And it came to pass the same day, that Isaac’s servants came, and told him concerning the well which they had digged, and said unto him, We have found water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e780fae4-5426-4db9-b7ed-fcff4b90eeb7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: GEN 26:33
Text: And he called it Shebah: therefore the name of the city is Beersheba unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c52b84f-bd25-42a4-bddc-9c9f9690fb8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: GEN 26:34
Text: And Esau was forty years old when he took to wife Judith the daughter of Beeri the Hittite, and Bashemath the daughter of Elon the Hittite:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/26/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52271e33-5585-48b8-8f23-2d74245546a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: GEN 26:35
Text: Which were a grief of mind unto Isaac and to Rebekah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7d2ed3e-4530-4894-9b33-598b529b2efc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: GEN 27:1
Text: And it came to pass, that when Isaac was old, and his eyes were dim, so that he could not see, he called Esau his eldest son, and said unto him, My son: and he said unto him, Behold, here am I.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c53667bf-80ed-4fea-b5a6-e788da67cd3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: GEN 27:2
Text: And he said, Behold now, I am old, I know not the day of my death:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b830fe6a-1135-4c68-be92-213061fc6011>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: GEN 27:3
Text: Now therefore take, I pray thee, thy weapons, thy quiver and thy bow, and go out to the field, and take me some venison;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:387ac24a-40e6-45c4-9f39-79240b750495>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: GEN 27:4
Text: And make me savoury meat, such as I love, and bring it to me, that I may eat; that my soul may bless thee before I die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebd392ae-1716-4ece-b6c5-8822e0014f9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: GEN 27:5
Text: And Rebekah heard when Isaac spake to Esau his son. And Esau went to the field to hunt for venison, and to bring it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7f82e13-4195-4054-97aa-20d380b971c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: GEN 27:6
Text: And Rebekah spake unto Jacob her son, saying, Behold, I heard thy father speak unto Esau thy brother, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17ac5b5c-0680-4d88-85ec-6938c61b8bc9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: GEN 27:7
Text: Bring me venison, and make me savoury meat, that I may eat, and bless thee before the LORD before my death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb07895a-b9c5-4171-8c6b-9d450f47b3ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: GEN 27:8
Text: Now therefore, my son, obey my voice according to that which I command thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d1efa53-0cb9-42ae-a768-ab8afbced1d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: GEN 27:9
Text: Go now to the flock, and fetch me from thence two good kids of the goats; and I will make them savoury meat for thy father, such as he loveth:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:220bf259-6dbb-4258-91c5-73c7cab1f222>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: GEN 27:10
Text: And thou shalt bring it to thy father, that he may eat, and that he may bless thee before his death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3d0d072-d1f6-43b9-8d27-f5f2162f6c0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: GEN 27:11
Text: And Jacob said to Rebekah his mother, Behold, Esau my brother is a hairy man, and I am a smooth man:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b43f6b2-4682-4b7a-8264-1fd064aca351>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: GEN 27:12
Text: My father peradventure will feel me, and I shall seem to him as a deceiver; and I shall bring a curse upon me, and not a blessing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23f9f303-7c8e-4b75-bf46-c311a783800b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: GEN 27:13
Text: And his mother said unto him, Upon me be thy curse, my son: only obey my voice, and go fetch me them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbc30e9f-5ca6-4bb3-8b5b-788dc76f4474>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: GEN 27:14
Text: And he went, and fetched, and brought them to his mother: and his mother made savoury meat, such as his father loved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e8bf919-1f6c-4c69-89f1-9995f0116b1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: GEN 27:15
Text: And Rebekah took goodly raiment of her eldest son Esau, which were with her in the house, and put them upon Jacob her younger son:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09c54ea6-9ddf-491d-b432-2832127ec4c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: GEN 27:16
Text: And she put the skins of the kids of the goats upon his hands, and upon the smooth of his neck:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1002eabc-69ed-4c62-93ba-e4787de49e58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: GEN 27:17
Text: And she gave the savoury meat and the bread, which she had prepared, into the hand of her son Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80917aa6-976d-489f-9053-ca45050dba35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: GEN 27:18
Text: And he came unto his father, and said, My father: and he said, Here am I; who art thou, my son?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4e204a2-9b4d-471c-ad92-826d4a145a3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: GEN 27:19
Text: And Jacob said unto his father, I am Esau thy first born; I have done according as thou badest me: arise, I pray thee, sit and eat of my venison, that thy soul may bless me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e746865e-d264-4f4b-a669-07413fd530c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: GEN 27:20
Text: And Isaac said unto his son, How is it that thou hast found it so quickly, my son? And he said, Because the LORD thy God brought it to me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27cc5d44-d65c-44ec-a984-9829c087b861>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: GEN 27:21
Text: And Isaac said unto Jacob, Come near, I pray thee, that I may feel thee, my son, whether thou be my very son Esau or not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45166a2e-be21-4684-abc0-1f43d61c161c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: GEN 27:22
Text: And Jacob went near unto Isaac his father; and he felt him, and said, The voice is Jacob’s voice, but the hands are the hands of Esau.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39686002-2f4d-49dd-9e49-4ff07cca8007>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: GEN 27:23
Text: And he discerned him not, because his hands were hairy, as his brother Esau’s hands: so he blessed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fea9922-362b-4521-af37-6518c2299cfc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: GEN 27:24
Text: And he said, Art thou my very son Esau? And he said, I am.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac4d4fd0-84da-485c-94a8-69354a9bbb1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: GEN 27:25
Text: And he said, Bring it near to me, and I will eat of my son’s venison, that my soul may bless thee. And he brought it near to him, and he did eat: and he brought him wine and he drank.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d869d93-a3c9-4b3b-85b8-363ab651b2ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: GEN 27:26
Text: And his father Isaac said unto him, Come near now, and kiss me, my son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f44aa00a-7534-48f2-a554-de4324b9a3e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: GEN 27:27
Text: And he came near, and kissed him: and he smelled the smell of his raiment, and blessed him, and said, See, the smell of my son is as the smell of a field which the LORD hath blessed:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3a23a91-daee-4ac8-91a7-993ec7f30b25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: GEN 27:28
Text: Therefore God give thee of the dew of heaven, and the fatness of the earth, and plenty of corn and wine:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d9f13ab-4d1e-4be4-b634-9d32a5a0b1f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: GEN 27:29
Text: Let people serve thee, and nations bow down to thee: be lord over thy brethren, and let thy mother’s sons bow down to thee: cursed be every one that curseth thee, and blessed be he that blesseth thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f27f119-5e6b-43c9-8b37-17ef25a448d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: GEN 27:30
Text: And it came to pass, as soon as Isaac had made an end of blessing Jacob, and Jacob was yet scarce gone out from the presence of Isaac his father, that Esau his brother came in from his hunting.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:900425e1-dff2-4abc-8f40-f12a041b9d7a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: GEN 27:31
Text: And he also had made savoury meat, and brought it unto his father, and said unto his father, Let my father arise, and eat of his son’s venison, that thy soul may bless me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a98c2d8d-b33a-4ba3-9522-d5daba9f5dff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: GEN 27:32
Text: And Isaac his father said unto him, Who art thou? And he said, I am thy son, thy firstborn Esau.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad71433d-53e9-4a29-a3d9-480502490ee2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: GEN 27:33
Text: And Isaac trembled very exceedingly, and said, Who? where is he that hath taken venison, and brought it me, and I have eaten of all before thou camest, and have blessed him? yea, and he shall be blessed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1db685dd-88cb-4eb9-b5d0-bfc373788361>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: GEN 27:34
Text: And when Esau heard the words of his father, he cried with a great and exceeding bitter cry, and said unto his father, Bless me, even me also, O my father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:039f7d7b-d4d0-4730-afb3-1a2af00ed7db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: GEN 27:35
Text: And he said, Thy brother came with subtilty, and hath taken away thy blessing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27dd613c-deb6-4734-bfe4-0ec6bdb2498b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: GEN 27:36
Text: And he said, Is not he rightly named Jacob? for he hath supplanted me these two times: he took away my birthright; and, behold, now he hath taken away my blessing. And he said, Hast thou not reserved a blessing for me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c595aa85-e8b6-4f38-a1af-4dd043ff8213>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: GEN 27:37
Text: And Isaac answered and said unto Esau, Behold, I have made him thy lord, and all his brethren have I given to him for servants; and with corn and wine have I sustained him: and what shall I do now unto thee, my son?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51528354-0a9a-469f-8b4f-7a5a819b9c87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: GEN 27:38
Text: And Esau said unto his father, Hast thou but one blessing, my father? bless me, even me also, O my father. And Esau lifted up his voice, and wept.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30ab6c76-f4af-41c6-bc7f-59d80a156d4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: GEN 27:39
Text: And Isaac his father answered and said unto him, Behold, thy dwelling shall be the fatness of the earth, and of the dew of heaven from above;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6b47a7f-afa4-436a-8f7e-3b85a03e989b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: GEN 27:40
Text: And by thy sword shalt thou live, and shalt serve thy brother; and it shall come to pass when thou shalt have the dominion, that thou shalt break his yoke from off thy neck.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2166b688-2ec8-451f-8f34-e9cc73a9ec89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: GEN 27:41
Text: And Esau hated Jacob because of the blessing wherewith his father blessed him: and Esau said in his heart, The days of mourning for my father are at hand; then will I slay my brother Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9988ac26-e840-4cd0-af8f-d9e4e2142753>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: GEN 27:42
Text: And these words of Esau her elder son were told to Rebekah: and she sent and called Jacob her younger son, and said unto him, Behold, thy brother Esau, as touching thee, doth comfort himself, purposing to kill thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba2d3985-f6ba-4851-a7c9-d38120df1f33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: GEN 27:43
Text: Now therefore, my son, obey my voice; arise, flee thou to Laban my brother to Haran;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09c21d0b-908e-43ac-b196-1f765eba95b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: GEN 27:44
Text: And tarry with him a few days, until thy brother’s fury turn away;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93cb3f0d-e636-48b4-8f56-6a65732de420>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: GEN 27:45
Text: Until thy brother’s anger turn away from thee, and he forget that which thou hast done to him: then I will send, and fetch thee from thence: why should I be deprived also of you both in one day?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/27/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:212ace59-8201-4d2e-94e8-b7f12f669815>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: GEN 27:46
Text: And Rebekah said to Isaac, I am weary of my life because of the daughters of Heth: if Jacob take a wife of the daughters of Heth, such as these which are of the daughters of the land, what good shall my life do me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/28/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6544e6d2-c272-4bb8-8fe0-9072a205114b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: GEN 28:1
Text: And Isaac called Jacob, and blessed him, and charged him, and said unto him, Thou shalt not take a wife of the daughters of Canaan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/28/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc9e9c2b-6eda-4fc0-8f8b-c016ff4ccbf1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: GEN 28:2
Text: Arise, go to Padanaram, to the house of Bethuel thy mother’s father; and take thee a wife from thence of the daughters of Laban thy mother’s brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/28/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3af7c18a-3c97-4aaa-a973-e22b86801d4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: GEN 28:3
Text: And God Almighty bless thee, and make thee fruitful, and multiply thee, that thou mayest be a multitude of people;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/28/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39e68d58-d4a6-4bb3-bdea-0a8c10e8f9c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: GEN 28:4
Text: And give thee the blessing of Abraham, to thee, and to thy seed with thee; that thou mayest inherit the land wherein thou art a stranger, which God gave unto Abraham.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/28/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb5a1a4f-2cff-44a2-a31e-d7c63be1ab22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: GEN 28:5
Text: And Isaac sent away Jacob: and he went to Padanaram unto Laban, son of Bethuel the Syrian, the brother of Rebekah, Jacob’s and Esau’s mother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/28/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45e86a66-55eb-4c46-be39-2fe220fa43db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: GEN 28:6
Text: When Esau saw that Isaac had blessed Jacob, and sent him away to Padanaram, to take him a wife from thence; and that as he blessed him he gave him a charge, saying, Thou shalt not take a wife of the daughters of Canaan;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/28/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf92e21b-d0a0-465d-937c-c67e02ce5c57>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: GEN 28:7
Text: And that Jacob obeyed his father and his mother, and was gone to Padanaram;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/28/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9518a984-8385-4cf5-be6a-2d6fd26229f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: GEN 28:8
Text: And Esau seeing that the daughters of Canaan pleased not Isaac his father;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/28/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54441cef-99dc-4dbf-ab40-8664c997d56a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: GEN 28:9
Text: Then went Esau unto Ishmael, and took unto the wives which he had Mahalath the daughter of Ishmael Abraham’s son, the sister of Nebajoth, to be his wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/28/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac9f7716-2171-408a-aa38-91e1773dd5f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: GEN 28:10
Text: And Jacob went out from Beersheba, and went toward Haran.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/28/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3fdd3fa-8936-44d6-bcb4-20cee27af164>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: GEN 28:11
Text: And he lighted upon a certain place, and tarried there all night, because the sun was set; and he took of the stones of that place, and put them for his pillows, and lay down in that place to sleep.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/28/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c11d3421-ed86-4396-8cfd-c293b6214993>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: GEN 28:12
Text: And he dreamed, and behold a ladder set up on the earth, and the top of it reached to heaven: and behold the angels of God ascending and descending on it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/28/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:415cf9bc-bb3a-43ab-b65b-7aa645b6bd6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: GEN 28:13
Text: And, behold, the LORD stood above it, and said, I am the LORD God of Abraham thy father, and the God of Isaac: the land whereon thou liest, to thee will I give it, and to thy seed;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/28/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd7a1c2d-f267-4291-b585-b3984b927828>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: GEN 28:14
Text: And thy seed shall be as the dust of the earth, and thou shalt spread abroad to the west, and to the east, and to the north, and to the south: and in thee and in thy seed shall all the families of the earth be blessed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/28/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c5f3ca7-518a-441f-a415-08515c50fbd5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: GEN 28:15
Text: And, behold, I am with thee, and will keep thee in all places whither thou goest, and will bring thee again into this land; for I will not leave thee, until I have done that which I have spoken to thee of.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/28/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0272f3f7-1428-4435-9c8b-07a0c96b9b58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: GEN 28:16
Text: And Jacob awaked out of his sleep, and he said, Surely the LORD is in this place; and I knew it not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/28/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1fa2777-ee70-47c0-ab3c-5a3cec5ad813>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: GEN 28:17
Text: And he was afraid, and said, How dreadful is this place! this is none other but the house of God, and this is the gate of heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/28/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1e67e96-cb8c-42ba-8c01-b7787349f2b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: GEN 28:18
Text: And Jacob rose up early in the morning, and took the stone that he had put for his pillows, and set it up for a pillar, and poured oil upon the top of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/28/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1199910-69c0-47e5-b479-f4b658079717>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: GEN 28:19
Text: And he called the name of that place Bethel: but the name of that city was called Luz at the first.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/28/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:963e8e13-59a9-4f1d-a005-459bd4c64dd3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: GEN 28:20
Text: And Jacob vowed a vow, saying, If God will be with me, and will keep me in this way that I go, and will give me bread to eat, and raiment to put on,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/28/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07cc9686-d0d5-486f-8799-f7622663c52d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: GEN 28:21
Text: So that I come again to my father’s house in peace; then shall the LORD be my God:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/28/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3110e87-d479-466e-814b-3c1a885da2e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: GEN 28:22
Text: And this stone, which I have set for a pillar, shall be God’s house: and of all that thou shalt give me I will surely give the tenth unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:607222c6-7d7f-44f5-9e9d-bd72315273f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: GEN 29:1
Text: Then Jacob went on his journey, and came into the land of the people of the east.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7de1c565-833c-45ec-8175-d1442c583629>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: GEN 29:2
Text: And he looked, and behold a well in the field, and, lo, there were three flocks of sheep lying by it; for out of that well they watered the flocks: and a great stone was upon the well’s mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ddce25d-938e-4cd1-b76c-9a4692c7f316>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: GEN 29:3
Text: And thither were all the flocks gathered: and they rolled the stone from the well’s mouth, and watered the sheep, and put the stone again upon the well’s mouth in his place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f154450-fd82-4747-b07b-2247394b7477>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: GEN 29:4
Text: And Jacob said unto them, My brethren, whence be ye? And they said, Of Haran are we.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11bbfbab-8160-432e-859a-59448ab8f003>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: GEN 29:5
Text: And he said unto them, Know ye Laban the son of Nahor? And they said, We know him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0f93c1a-04bc-40b5-87dd-8c67a0f67c35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: GEN 29:6
Text: And he said unto them, Is he well? And they said, He is well: and, behold, Rachel his daughter cometh with the sheep.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84064782-c8e5-4a92-9807-117df3026614>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: GEN 29:7
Text: And he said, Lo, it is yet high day, neither is it time that the cattle should be gathered together: water ye the sheep, and go and feed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f21d7236-c9b3-414a-be3a-4170f53c6841>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: GEN 29:8
Text: And they said, We cannot, until all the flocks be gathered together, and till they roll the stone from the well’s mouth; then we water the sheep.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb04a7de-81fc-4a89-9220-9acd26499e47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: GEN 29:9
Text: And while he yet spake with them, Rachel came with her father’s sheep; for she kept them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98a1ee51-a52f-4cd6-bd39-925dc1d5677f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 286

Reference: GEN 29:10
Text: And it came to pass, when Jacob saw Rachel the daughter of Laban his mother’s brother, and the sheep of Laban his mother’s brother, that Jacob went near, and rolled the stone from the well’s mouth, and watered the flock of Laban his mother’s brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc03aeab-cee4-42d3-babc-4f513b53f047>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: GEN 29:11
Text: And Jacob kissed Rachel, and lifted up his voice, and wept.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31423183-cb80-4d93-8172-34a5bb69c444>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: GEN 29:12
Text: And Jacob told Rachel that he was her father’s brother, and that he was Rebekah’s son: and she ran and told her father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36156c06-472e-41d7-a730-3087003861f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: GEN 29:13
Text: And it came to pass, when Laban heard the tidings of Jacob his sister’s son, that he ran to meet him, and embraced him, and kissed him, and brought him to his house. And he told Laban all these things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96b5ea36-f41c-4c55-a977-3ea969b67944>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: GEN 29:14
Text: And Laban said to him, Surely thou art my bone and my flesh. And he abode with him the space of a month.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be08ab68-84df-4c36-b1a1-79493344fd1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: GEN 29:15
Text: And Laban said unto Jacob, Because thou art my brother, shouldest thou therefore serve me for nought? tell me, what shall thy wages be?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:879083aa-72a9-451e-8ca0-081e9ae3c478>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: GEN 29:16
Text: And Laban had two daughters: the name of the elder was Leah, and the name of the younger was Rachel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f170b83-febd-4a92-b719-d3011696ece6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: GEN 29:17
Text: Leah was tender eyed; but Rachel was beautiful and well favoured.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97d5497e-dfac-46b8-9f80-30ccf4e144b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: GEN 29:18
Text: And Jacob loved Rachel; and said, I will serve thee seven years for Rachel thy younger daughter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb89b96f-4c7e-488e-893f-da5fafcc4d74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: GEN 29:19
Text: And Laban said, It is better that I give her to thee, than that I should give her to another man: abide with me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92c5948f-7448-4ac2-8c05-2b2afc4efdb8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: GEN 29:20
Text: And Jacob served seven years for Rachel; and they seemed unto him but a few days, for the love he had to her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49f499a8-f005-44d8-b090-f929e1be0cf9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: GEN 29:21
Text: And Jacob said unto Laban, Give me my wife, for my days are fulfilled, that I may go in unto her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebbd6df9-ca62-40e2-b62a-dda238fe440a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: GEN 29:22
Text: And Laban gathered together all the men of the place, and made a feast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b125c54b-60f5-46be-a6a3-c225f53e9c7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: GEN 29:23
Text: And it came to pass in the evening, that he took Leah his daughter, and brought her to him; and he went in unto her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4aef920e-58c8-48fb-8bd5-d38c542a9340>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: GEN 29:24
Text: And Laban gave unto his daughter Leah Zilpah his maid for an handmaid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8311e352-a368-4704-8810-8c86158997ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: GEN 29:25
Text: And it came to pass, that in the morning, behold, it was Leah: and he said to Laban, What is this thou hast done unto me? did not I serve with thee for Rachel? wherefore then hast thou beguiled me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aeddb6da-e9c6-4686-b669-7daf0d9f7712>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: GEN 29:26
Text: And Laban said, It must not be so done in our country, to give the younger before the firstborn.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b087cd5-827a-4a0a-8f54-dc17844ff81e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: GEN 29:27
Text: Fulfil her week, and we will give thee this also for the service which thou shalt serve with me yet seven other years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:692853e7-c3d7-40a4-a015-0e7ad086e9a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: GEN 29:28
Text: And Jacob did so, and fulfilled her week: and he gave him Rachel his daughter to wife also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b77a8f62-ab6c-4d07-9b29-37877d832e70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: GEN 29:29
Text: And Laban gave to Rachel his daughter Bilhah his handmaid to be her maid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b54e2e0a-a707-4e8b-905a-e0954fc4fc63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: GEN 29:30
Text: And he went in also unto Rachel, and he loved also Rachel more than Leah, and served with him yet seven other years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:293d06c2-a452-4079-af3b-b636c23e4b65>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: GEN 29:31
Text: And when the LORD saw that Leah was hated, he opened her womb: but Rachel was barren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62a44688-ad52-4290-8037-f6f0246d6c96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: GEN 29:32
Text: And Leah conceived, and bare a son, and she called his name Reuben: for she said, Surely the LORD hath looked upon my affliction; now therefore my husband will love me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3855b02-d664-42d1-8879-0b275626d01f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: GEN 29:33
Text: And she conceived again, and bare a son; and said, Because the LORD hath heard I was hated, he hath therefore given me this son also: and she called his name Simeon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6a60185-117c-4534-9fdf-8988305f69cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: GEN 29:34
Text: And she conceived again, and bare a son; and said, Now this time will my husband be joined unto me, because I have born him three sons: therefore was his name called Levi.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/29/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f38c7490-ec71-4363-a7be-a86d16a2f900>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: GEN 29:35
Text: And she conceived again, and bare a son: and she said, Now will I praise the LORD: therefore she called his name Judah; and left bearing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db5cf5f6-4bf7-49a7-8b9c-48569cb0dce5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: GEN 30:1
Text: And when Rachel saw that she bare Jacob no children, Rachel envied her sister; and said unto Jacob, Give me children, or else I die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0444bf64-d70b-4703-beac-4018758cdec1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: GEN 30:2
Text: And Jacob’s anger was kindled against Rachel: and he said, Am I in God’s stead, who hath withheld from thee the fruit of the womb?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:447ee0f9-95a0-4f53-8c15-ce73c6026d0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: GEN 30:3
Text: And she said, Behold my maid Bilhah, go in unto her; and she shall bear upon my knees, that I may also have children by her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26156365-6b6f-474a-8d2c-36e593cc4b2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: GEN 30:4
Text: And she gave him Bilhah her handmaid to wife: and Jacob went in unto her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60ada674-3081-44f8-be48-db365935a106>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 70

Reference: GEN 30:5
Text: And Bilhah conceived, and bare Jacob a son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a72c872-8987-44ee-9375-d66c70003506>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: GEN 30:6
Text: And Rachel said, God hath judged me, and hath also heard my voice, and hath given me a son: therefore called she his name Dan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0cf5ec96-1a9b-4867-a8f4-dc9b7a97d564>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: GEN 30:7
Text: And Bilhah Rachel’s maid conceived again, and bare Jacob a second son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d1df96c-59d2-48d0-8c0e-94b6ff081599>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: GEN 30:8
Text: And Rachel said, With great wrestlings have I wrestled with my sister, and I have prevailed: and she called his name Naphtali.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d903576c-8c80-4e05-ae27-932510176e07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: GEN 30:9
Text: When Leah saw that she had left bearing, she took Zilpah her maid, and gave her Jacob to wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:148c5f83-54c4-4858-abba-c0e473bf6b7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 70

Reference: GEN 30:10
Text: And Zilpah Leah’s maid bare Jacob a son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c0a763f-6bf3-48eb-9b2a-2e2d80f37aa3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: GEN 30:11
Text: And Leah said, A troop cometh: and she called his name Gad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:422a90ce-abda-4cfe-8608-a45196aecff0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: GEN 30:12
Text: And Zilpah Leah’s maid bare Jacob a second son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2aa0c1af-1669-41b4-be85-c0a8e6e12c8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: GEN 30:13
Text: And Leah said, Happy am I, for the daughters will call me blessed: and she called his name Asher.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:479d0860-cf96-475d-887d-68301fac78b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: GEN 30:14
Text: And Reuben went in the days of wheat harvest, and found mandrakes in the field, and brought them unto his mother Leah. Then Rachel said to Leah, Give me, I pray thee, of thy son’s mandrakes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b69943a-0a2b-4198-bb08-679495d99c0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: GEN 30:15
Text: And she said unto her, Is it a small matter that thou hast taken my husband? and wouldest thou take away my son’s mandrakes also? And Rachel said, Therefore he shall lie with thee to night for thy son’s mandrakes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fee2eddb-b6d2-4a8b-850b-c6a98868138c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: GEN 30:16
Text: And Jacob came out of the field in the evening, and Leah went out to meet him, and said, Thou must come in unto me; for surely I have hired thee with my son’s mandrakes. And he lay with her that night.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d7d0b30-76a2-46c6-8789-61e4795526e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: GEN 30:17
Text: And God hearkened unto Leah, and she conceived, and bare Jacob the fifth son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c895d6a9-ded3-45d0-86a5-c813fd948874>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: GEN 30:18
Text: And Leah said, God hath given me my hire, because I have given my maiden to my husband: and she called his name Issachar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bce7deb3-ebea-42c5-bd21-ca3dfb22d159>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: GEN 30:19
Text: And Leah conceived again, and bare Jacob the sixth son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee4d454d-010c-4e3f-a41c-818cb6f92a12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: GEN 30:20
Text: And Leah said, God hath endued me with a good dowry; now will my husband dwell with me, because I have born him six sons: and she called his name Zebulun.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c294e3e7-c02b-45cb-b17a-8cfafb4597ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: GEN 30:21
Text: And afterwards she bare a daughter, and called her name Dinah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64439ba0-f60e-4190-ab95-c4d6e4efb403>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: GEN 30:22
Text: And God remembered Rachel, and God hearkened to her, and opened her womb.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1970ab5-29d6-4de3-ad60-a74f747935a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: GEN 30:23
Text: And she conceived, and bare a son; and said, God hath taken away my reproach:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:222619d8-7287-4721-8ee1-a147ceb4e937>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: GEN 30:24
Text: And she called his name Joseph; and said, The LORD shall add to me another son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81e8c6dd-7e6e-4669-9582-c93cf12a1183>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: GEN 30:25
Text: And it came to pass, when Rachel had born Joseph, that Jacob said unto Laban, Send me away, that I may go unto mine own place, and to my country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70c676cd-82cb-44e5-994e-7603af5d404e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: GEN 30:26
Text: Give me my wives and my children, for whom I have served thee, and let me go: for thou knowest my service which I have done thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db6a6034-c168-4fbe-9827-4231d4140e7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: GEN 30:27
Text: And Laban said unto him, I pray thee, if I have found favour in thine eyes, tarry: for I have learned by experience that the LORD hath blessed me for thy sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b53d8b66-4154-4a58-a3f8-e513c071c726>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: GEN 30:28
Text: And he said, Appoint me thy wages, and I will give it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3246383d-85b5-4e16-a48c-d94c983473fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: GEN 30:29
Text: And he said unto him, Thou knowest how I have served thee, and how thy cattle was with me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e607b6c-d2a0-45f1-89b5-01324b65b793>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: GEN 30:30
Text: For it was little which thou hadst before I came, and it is now increased unto a multitude; and the LORD hath blessed thee since my coming: and now when shall I provide for mine own house also?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81352a39-eeba-4be9-8436-19ed0633ea2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: GEN 30:31
Text: And he said, What shall I give thee? And Jacob said, Thou shalt not give me any thing: if thou wilt do this thing for me, I will again feed and keep thy flock.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3fd3d6c9-ce89-461e-9f3c-dde501a6614e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: GEN 30:32
Text: I will pass through all thy flock to day, removing from thence all the speckled and spotted cattle, and all the brown cattle among the sheep, and the spotted and speckled among the goats: and of such shall be my hire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ce3b2ef-c02c-4865-9634-b44c427e7119>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: GEN 30:33
Text: So shall my righteousness answer for me in time to come, when it shall come for my hire before thy face: every one that is not speckled and spotted among the goats, and brown among the sheep, that shall be counted stolen with me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:070be13a-813d-464d-bd3f-8a37923e509e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: GEN 30:34
Text: And Laban said, Behold, I would it might be according to thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71fa2349-1d72-499f-a213-db37b101b402>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: GEN 30:35
Text: And he removed that day the he goats that were ringstraked and spotted, and all the she goats that were speckled and spotted, and every one that had some white in it, and all the brown among the sheep, and gave them into the hand of his sons.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:565f86db-024f-412c-8fe3-4feb000b6c85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: GEN 30:36
Text: And he set three days’ journey betwixt himself and Jacob: and Jacob fed the rest of Laban’s flocks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f862323d-aab9-49c9-96d9-638dbd6362d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: GEN 30:37
Text: And Jacob took him rods of green poplar, and of the hazel and chestnut tree; and pilled white strakes in them, and made the white appear which was in the rods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7d7813d-92bc-4a60-9eeb-ca45630548ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: GEN 30:38
Text: And he set the rods which he had pilled before the flocks in the gutters in the watering troughs when the flocks came to drink, that they should conceive when they came to drink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9530a3b9-2d8f-4a95-b2d3-981c66ac8237>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: GEN 30:39
Text: And the flocks conceived before the rods, and brought forth cattle ringstraked, speckled, and spotted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a272e8b-64ca-485c-8340-0eee3794cdd9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: GEN 30:40
Text: And Jacob did separate the lambs, and set the faces of the flocks toward the ringstraked, and all the brown in the flock of Laban; and he put his own flocks by themselves, and put them not unto Laban’s cattle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86993ee2-f777-4a8b-b01a-ae6cea230362>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: GEN 30:41
Text: And it came to pass, whensoever the stronger cattle did conceive, that Jacob laid the rods before the eyes of the cattle in the gutters, that they might conceive among the rods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f576edb-8ff0-4e5f-9948-7302bf840314>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: GEN 30:42
Text: But when the cattle were feeble, he put them not in: so the feebler were Laban’s, and the stronger Jacob’s.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/30/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ff1fb73-84f5-4e18-a4aa-44b40a36ce89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: GEN 30:43
Text: And the man increased exceedingly, and had much cattle, and maidservants, and menservants, and camels, and asses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25e69786-5b18-4c08-945f-e4c468e8a27e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: GEN 31:1
Text: And he heard the words of Laban’s sons, saying, Jacob hath taken away all that was our father’s; and of that which was our father’s hath he gotten all this glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a47967d6-01bf-4451-9600-f852835b51b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: GEN 31:2
Text: And Jacob beheld the countenance of Laban, and, behold, it was not toward him as before.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ea78ced-5fe5-4a85-9afd-3f9919030f85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: GEN 31:3
Text: And the LORD said unto Jacob, Return unto the land of thy fathers, and to thy kindred; and I will be with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05294b0c-c109-4b51-b45f-ff8b44cbbd18>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: GEN 31:4
Text: And Jacob sent and called Rachel and Leah to the field unto his flock,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2a88fcd-d65d-433a-ac8c-fd4464b7f1a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: GEN 31:5
Text: And said unto them, I see your father’s countenance, that it is not toward me as before; but the God of my father hath been with me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d5756b8-da50-422a-9975-6eee474b3a2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: GEN 31:6
Text: And ye know that with all my power I have served your father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff9c5200-abb2-445c-9b2b-ee39dec897d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: GEN 31:7
Text: And your father hath deceived me, and changed my wages ten times; but God suffered him not to hurt me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05871306-7176-4546-bc21-4a0dda1871f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: GEN 31:8
Text: If he said thus, The speckled shall be thy wages; then all the cattle bare speckled: and if he said thus, The ringstraked shall be thy hire; then bare all the cattle ringstraked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b576ea2-886e-451f-b08d-102f97464fa3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: GEN 31:9
Text: Thus God hath taken away the cattle of your father, and given them to me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92f15c92-c278-4945-9bdb-9fb353485d7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: GEN 31:10
Text: And it came to pass at the time that the cattle conceived, that I lifted up mine eyes, and saw in a dream, and, behold, the rams which leaped upon the cattle were ringstraked, speckled, and grisled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:250466a7-c6a2-4c2e-98bf-46e19663260d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: GEN 31:11
Text: And the angel of God spake unto me in a dream, saying, Jacob: And I said, Here am I.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:504d61c8-f4b9-43d1-a34d-42c2e8844c0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: GEN 31:12
Text: And he said, Lift up now thine eyes, and see, all the rams which leap upon the cattle are ringstraked, speckled, and grisled: for I have seen all that Laban doeth unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a807a654-84c6-4578-a0b6-60a9f450559c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: GEN 31:13
Text: I am the God of Bethel, where thou anointedst the pillar, and where thou vowedst a vow unto me: now arise, get thee out from this land, and return unto the land of thy kindred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce51ae2c-5002-4e4f-a0bc-e958a39c59dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: GEN 31:14
Text: And Rachel and Leah answered and said unto him, Is there yet any portion or inheritance for us in our father’s house?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c05d34f-a4e1-4f5d-a049-ce6f42f191df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: GEN 31:15
Text: Are we not counted of him strangers? for he hath sold us, and hath quite devoured also our money.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10bcf822-476a-446e-aecf-aad23ad03abd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: GEN 31:16
Text: For all the riches which God hath taken from our father, that is ours, and our children’s: now then, whatsoever God hath said unto thee, do.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b5b231b-985a-4639-86e4-12602a4a8291>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: GEN 31:17
Text: Then Jacob rose up, and set his sons and his wives upon camels;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31893217-021d-4bbb-bd94-a30077235a7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: GEN 31:18
Text: And he carried away all his cattle, and all his goods which he had gotten, the cattle of his getting, which he had gotten in Padanaram, for to go to Isaac his father in the land of Canaan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2eb7d433-df80-480a-83e6-1116d762f049>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: GEN 31:19
Text: And Laban went to shear his sheep: and Rachel had stolen the images that were her father’s.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1929e09-3f44-4d00-bd51-556ce89ade08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: GEN 31:20
Text: And Jacob stole away unawares to Laban the Syrian, in that he told him not that he fled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a618378a-472b-4eea-ac7a-c099a93a05a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: GEN 31:21
Text: So he fled with all that he had; and he rose up, and passed over the river, and set his face toward the mount Gilead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acac054b-fdd2-4ec9-a56d-d06d32ac190f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: GEN 31:22
Text: And it was told Laban on the third day that Jacob was fled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f77e7db9-c516-419c-9014-688c6a70b92c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: GEN 31:23
Text: And he took his brethren with him, and pursued after him seven days’ journey; and they overtook him in the mount Gilead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d350cf8-ec0c-4604-baa2-9f094b2bfd47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: GEN 31:24
Text: And God came to Laban the Syrian in a dream by night, and said unto him, Take heed that thou speak not to Jacob either good or bad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd227cff-faa8-4a24-8d76-e615a112c9cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: GEN 31:25
Text: Then Laban overtook Jacob. Now Jacob had pitched his tent in the mount: and Laban with his brethren pitched in the mount of Gilead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5cfabdcd-4442-4c4e-ab0b-e233fb56a2b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: GEN 31:26
Text: And Laban said to Jacob, What hast thou done, that thou hast stolen away unawares to me, and carried away my daughters, as captives taken with the sword?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55f1bedb-a1fb-48f4-9ed2-e309d47d29be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: GEN 31:27
Text: Wherefore didst thou flee away secretly, and steal away from me; and didst not tell me, that I might have sent thee away with mirth, and with songs, with tabret, and with harp?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:323af3bf-028d-4543-a63d-3e70deb2aca7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: GEN 31:28
Text: And hast not suffered me to kiss my sons and my daughters? thou hast now done foolishly in so doing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c406126e-991a-4543-823f-70d2ad23e6f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: GEN 31:29
Text: It is in the power of my hand to do you hurt: but the God of your father spake unto me yesternight, saying, Take thou heed that thou speak not to Jacob either good or bad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18caea37-6302-46b4-8d39-675cce092957>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: GEN 31:30
Text: And now, though thou wouldest needs be gone, because thou sore longedst after thy father’s house, yet wherefore hast thou stolen my gods?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9062a4e6-8907-42a8-8cde-b969b0a39600>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: GEN 31:31
Text: And Jacob answered and said to Laban, Because I was afraid: for I said, Peradventure thou wouldest take by force thy daughters from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5346cee2-0fae-495e-849f-cb0a14fa2255>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: GEN 31:32
Text: With whomsoever thou findest thy gods, let him not live: before our brethren discern thou what is thine with me, and take it to thee. For Jacob knew not that Rachel had stolen them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c04b92f-1bb7-4187-8dba-532684cbb54e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: GEN 31:33
Text: And Laban went into Jacob’s tent, and into Leah’s tent, and into the two maidservants’ tents; but he found them not. Then went he out of Leah’s tent, and entered into Rachel’s tent.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73dc9300-e22b-4c0a-80b6-e8a730bb5e1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: GEN 31:34
Text: Now Rachel had taken the images, and put them in the camel’s furniture, and sat upon them. And Laban searched all the tent, but found them not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bdd8f31-0dc7-4266-b16c-9923c3ee8e57>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: GEN 31:35
Text: And she said to her father, Let it not displease my lord that I cannot rise up before thee; for the custom of women is upon me. And he searched but found not the images.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:088fb760-fdca-40a9-9006-185236476689>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: GEN 31:36
Text: And Jacob was wroth, and chode with Laban: and Jacob answered and said to Laban, What is my trespass? what is my sin, that thou hast so hotly pursued after me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5195a53-2809-4704-9369-d3da0fa09c16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: GEN 31:37
Text: Whereas thou hast searched all my stuff, what hast thou found of all thy household stuff? set it here before my brethren and thy brethren, that they may judge betwixt us both.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:041f5eef-3bff-4b4e-a8e3-06d40aa57cb8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: GEN 31:38
Text: This twenty years have I been with thee; thy ewes and thy she goats have not cast their young, and the rams of thy flock have I not eaten.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9010dd82-5c5a-4e0f-bb22-3e109251ac9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: GEN 31:39
Text: That which was torn of beasts I brought not unto thee; I bare the loss of it; of my hand didst thou require it, whether stolen by day, or stolen by night.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e59bde47-6757-4c12-ba9a-90ccfae2d02d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: GEN 31:40
Text: Thus I was; in the day the drought consumed me, and the frost by night; and my sleep departed from mine eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d62e286d-ff44-48c1-a52c-c483ff4bd22c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: GEN 31:41
Text: Thus have I been twenty years in thy house; I served thee fourteen years for thy two daughters, and six years for thy cattle: and thou hast changed my wages ten times.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df75f272-d3b2-447e-8851-82d26f98ebe5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: GEN 31:42
Text: Except the God of my father, the God of Abraham, and the fear of Isaac, had been with me, surely thou hadst sent me away now empty. God hath seen mine affliction and the labour of my hands, and rebuked thee yesternight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b3fe741-027b-4339-a942-d4b9388d9e71>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 299

Reference: GEN 31:43
Text: And Laban answered and said unto Jacob, These daughters are my daughters, and these children are my children, and these cattle are my cattle, and all that thou seest is mine: and what can I do this day unto these my daughters, or unto their children which they have born?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c05e5d8-7917-4341-b6ec-e29f2ff15e52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: GEN 31:44
Text: Now therefore come thou, let us make a covenant, I and thou; and let it be for a witness between me and thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1b8935b-9706-4a4f-ac34-1d4845013778>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: GEN 31:45
Text: And Jacob took a stone, and set it up for a pillar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:394a5fa5-17c3-455c-97d6-bb16deeec92c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: GEN 31:46
Text: And Jacob said unto his brethren, Gather stones; and they took stones, and made an heap: and they did eat there upon the heap.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:593d21cd-ddc9-4f94-9481-6d90e8f21f8e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: GEN 31:47
Text: And Laban called it Jegarsahadutha: but Jacob called it Galeed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8841df81-4864-4283-b33a-db123c0f7604>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: GEN 31:48
Text: And Laban said, This heap is a witness between me and thee this day. Therefore was the name of it called Galeed;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dec8320b-629c-4733-90fa-b61d2af8dc00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: GEN 31:49
Text: And Mizpah; for he said, The LORD watch between me and thee, when we are absent one from another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6760e5a9-4213-4f97-a80d-04fd5d3014fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: GEN 31:50
Text: If thou shalt afflict my daughters, or if thou shalt take other wives beside my daughters, no man is with us; see, God is witness betwixt me and thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cda922d7-22c4-4204-899d-bb2b9fd972e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: GEN 31:51
Text: And Laban said to Jacob, Behold this heap, and behold this pillar, which I have cast betwixt me and thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7565f21a-13cc-456b-9766-99b0d9b07add>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: GEN 31:52
Text: This heap be witness, and this pillar be witness, that I will not pass over this heap to thee, and that thou shalt not pass over this heap and this pillar unto me, for harm.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afd546c1-bc88-463d-ac68-aeba687f0d3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: GEN 31:53
Text: The God of Abraham, and the God of Nahor, the God of their father, judge betwixt us. And Jacob sware by the fear of his father Isaac.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d67a5e1-b0d2-4fc3-a356-537dc7f7bb80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: GEN 31:54
Text: Then Jacob offered sacrifice upon the mount, and called his brethren to eat bread: and they did eat bread, and tarried all night in the mount.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/31/55
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a4a0d8f-19c3-4760-8991-5a71a9b3cecd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: GEN 31:55
Text: And early in the morning Laban rose up, and kissed his sons and his daughters, and blessed them: and Laban departed, and returned unto his place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b25292f4-1971-498e-9a03-06cb07449a40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: GEN 32:1
Text: And Jacob went on his way, and the angels of God met him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9645de5-10b3-4ffb-95af-1ef038eea4ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: GEN 32:2
Text: And when Jacob saw them, he said, This is God’s host: and he called the name of that place Mahanaim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:964c067b-8870-4aa5-b0e1-9e63e3082977>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: GEN 32:3
Text: And Jacob sent messengers before him to Esau his brother unto the land of Seir, the country of Edom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fceaa302-dfb5-4522-aa76-547901b372f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: GEN 32:4
Text: And he commanded them, saying, Thus shall ye speak unto my lord Esau; Thy servant Jacob saith thus, I have sojourned with Laban, and stayed there until now:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb0ccf96-7fa9-4dbe-940d-2a93e7bf0d20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: GEN 32:5
Text: And I have oxen, and asses, flocks, and menservants, and womenservants: and I have sent to tell my lord, that I may find grace in thy sight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c594cb3-a0be-40d5-a478-50ee5543f95a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: GEN 32:6
Text: And the messengers returned to Jacob, saying, We came to thy brother Esau, and also he cometh to meet thee, and four hundred men with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1a1a8d0-7b6d-43e6-ab8d-079d01fe0117>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: GEN 32:7
Text: Then Jacob was greatly afraid and distressed: and he divided the people that was with him, and the flocks, and herds, and the camels, into two bands;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9336c95b-4429-4c79-bca0-8854534dffe3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: GEN 32:8
Text: And said, If Esau come to the one company, and smite it, then the other company which is left shall escape.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c28c2d0-1765-4cd1-9e6b-085d3f0685e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: GEN 32:9
Text: And Jacob said, O God of my father Abraham, and God of my father Isaac, the LORD which saidst unto me, Return unto thy country, and to thy kindred, and I will deal well with thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5fade1b-a318-4e36-9702-30161a3c3fd1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: GEN 32:10
Text: I am not worthy of the least of all the mercies, and of all the truth, which thou hast shewed unto thy servant; for with my staff I passed over this Jordan; and now I am become two bands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7c681b9-3089-4f98-8d49-3f3533672875>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: GEN 32:11
Text: Deliver me, I pray thee, from the hand of my brother, from the hand of Esau: for I fear him, lest he will come and smite me, and the mother with the children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0aa36a70-23bd-42a8-b0fe-45abe75bdd7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: GEN 32:12
Text: And thou saidst, I will surely do thee good, and make thy seed as the sand of the sea, which cannot be numbered for multitude.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:380fae29-56da-41c7-9c2b-37c2cda1873b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: GEN 32:13
Text: And he lodged there that same night; and took of that which came to his hand a present for Esau his brother;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46acce2f-fcfd-4cdc-a6e0-2ed51947a6e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: GEN 32:14
Text: Two hundred she goats, and twenty he goats, two hundred ewes, and twenty rams,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f1f3b27-b418-4d7f-93d5-66045b6cacae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: GEN 32:15
Text: Thirty milch camels with their colts, forty kine, and ten bulls, twenty she asses, and ten foals.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff8e1beb-4e83-467c-8f72-78d85f39d76b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: GEN 32:16
Text: And he delivered them into the hand of his servants, every drove by themselves; and said unto his servants, Pass over before me, and put a space betwixt drove and drove.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfd2a96f-ac90-43a2-9731-beac0aef937b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: GEN 32:17
Text: And he commanded the foremost, saying, When Esau my brother meeteth thee, and asketh thee, saying, Whose art thou? and whither goest thou? and whose are these before thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee367789-c4e4-4b9e-8e9d-9574cf73e9e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: GEN 32:18
Text: Then thou shalt say, They be thy servant Jacob’s; it is a present sent unto my lord Esau: and, behold, also he is behind us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:faeab446-57bd-4c4a-afa1-f7e6659fa2fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: GEN 32:19
Text: And so commanded he the second, and the third, and all that followed the droves, saying, On this manner shall ye speak unto Esau, when ye find him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d1903d9-def9-43a7-bc06-9ffd3d7e4619>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: GEN 32:20
Text: And say ye moreover, Behold, thy servant Jacob is behind us. For he said, I will appease him with the present that goeth before me, and afterward I will see his face; peradventure he will accept of me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e89e17b8-3fd0-4bd8-8404-801ebd1ba5e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: GEN 32:21
Text: So went the present over before him: and himself lodged that night in the company.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:826fd306-7058-4fe1-b801-23e03dd46f7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: GEN 32:22
Text: And he rose up that night, and took his two wives, and his two womenservants, and his eleven sons, and passed over the ford Jabbok.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbfef1a6-94a3-4f61-b861-e23f46b0c2a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: GEN 32:23
Text: And he took them, and sent them over the brook, and sent over that he had.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:031cc959-9ce5-4386-9ef2-95317a9afbc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: GEN 32:24
Text: And Jacob was left alone; and there wrestled a man with him until the breaking of the day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2de1e669-85e8-48f1-9679-bd4f1b1caa6d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: GEN 32:25
Text: And when he saw that he prevailed not against him, he touched the hollow of his thigh; and the hollow of Jacob’s thigh was out of joint, as he wrestled with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35470736-b06c-4a4a-9dfc-6193f9db26e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: GEN 32:26
Text: And he said, Let me go, for the day breaketh. And he said, I will not let thee go, except thou bless me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:190e03df-b9e4-4c75-ba37-d7e65db2f392>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: GEN 32:27
Text: And he said unto him, What is thy name? And he said, Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4280bc96-e882-4b1c-8fb7-50cded46774b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: GEN 32:28
Text: And he said, Thy name shall be called no more Jacob, but Israel: for as a prince hast thou power with God and with men, and hast prevailed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e49e5b4c-3e81-4558-88bd-e8e191955fda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: GEN 32:29
Text: And Jacob asked him, and said, Tell me, I pray thee, thy name. And he said, Wherefore is it that thou dost ask after my name? And he blessed him there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed590239-cc6f-4b79-80df-ac92d7669bec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: GEN 32:30
Text: And Jacob called the name of the place Peniel: for I have seen God face to face, and my life is preserved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e25782f-c925-4ba0-b3f4-3fce692cd5f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: GEN 32:31
Text: And as he passed over Penuel the sun rose upon him, and he halted upon his thigh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/32/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:304545d6-263f-4016-99a3-086f1db100f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: GEN 32:32
Text: Therefore the children of Israel eat not of the sinew which shrank, which is upon the hollow of the thigh, unto this day: because he touched the hollow of Jacob’s thigh in the sinew that shrank.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/33/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00ca13c5-84c1-4937-bea2-df966119bd98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: GEN 33:1
Text: And Jacob lifted up his eyes, and looked, and, behold, Esau came, and with him four hundred men. And he divided the children unto Leah, and unto Rachel, and unto the two handmaids.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/33/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93e11d14-34c4-4708-aeb6-828829acf0d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: GEN 33:2
Text: And he put the handmaids and their children foremost, and Leah and her children after, and Rachel and Joseph hindermost.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/33/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1c16956-38a7-4306-9272-9e80aaeb2787>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: GEN 33:3
Text: And he passed over before them, and bowed himself to the ground seven times, until he came near to his brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/33/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e851057-4723-4f6f-b163-b1967c55c810>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: GEN 33:4
Text: And Esau ran to meet him, and embraced him, and fell on his neck, and kissed him: and they wept.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/33/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:815b89cc-752a-4844-9cef-11c4d76e89de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: GEN 33:5
Text: And he lifted up his eyes, and saw the women and the children; and said, Who are those with thee? And he said, The children which God hath graciously given thy servant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/33/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0277f70a-18d6-4e24-854a-27ef87e4f8ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: GEN 33:6
Text: Then the handmaidens came near, they and their children, and they bowed themselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/33/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d2340dd-34d7-43b9-a962-9495bccc5d44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: GEN 33:7
Text: And Leah also with her children came near, and bowed themselves: and after came Joseph near and Rachel, and they bowed themselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/33/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5589c78-a0ff-478e-9ed7-34d337628a94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: GEN 33:8
Text: And he said, What meanest thou by all this drove which I met? And he said, These are to find grace in the sight of my lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/33/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4b11a0e-06be-44b4-9767-aacb3ffaf617>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: GEN 33:9
Text: And Esau said, I have enough, my brother; keep that thou hast unto thyself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/33/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eab16be8-0551-42c4-b46f-c54fdabca8ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: GEN 33:10
Text: And Jacob said, Nay, I pray thee, if now I have found grace in thy sight, then receive my present at my hand: for therefore I have seen thy face, as though I had seen the face of God, and thou wast pleased with me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/33/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2349817e-0eec-4883-a49d-eed66def0346>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: GEN 33:11
Text: Take, I pray thee, my blessing that is brought to thee; because God hath dealt graciously with me, and because I have enough. And he urged him, and he took it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/33/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:198452b3-6712-4d85-b386-0b15fd797d74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: GEN 33:12
Text: And he said, Let us take our journey, and let us go, and I will go before thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/33/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09940cc1-468e-4eb6-baca-ba93fadae5ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: GEN 33:13
Text: And he said unto him, My lord knoweth that the children are tender, and the flocks and herds with young are with me: and if men should overdrive them one day, all the flock will die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/33/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52f51297-935c-4462-9a77-ee5b8fca8e3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: GEN 33:14
Text: Let my lord, I pray thee, pass over before his servant: and I will lead on softly, according as the cattle that goeth before me and the children be able to endure, until I come unto my lord unto Seir.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/33/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cafc8d19-cd61-4b7e-a947-aaa890990612>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: GEN 33:15
Text: And Esau said, Let me now leave with thee some of the folk that are with me. And he said, What needeth it? let me find grace in the sight of my lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/33/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76b9c920-425e-4f25-a908-e0727f9b055f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: GEN 33:16
Text: So Esau returned that day on his way unto Seir.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/33/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b82ec1f-5e65-4175-90d0-c9cbc00f10cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: GEN 33:17
Text: And Jacob journeyed to Succoth, and built him an house, and made booths for his cattle: therefore the name of the place is called Succoth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/33/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82c80a27-7465-4f9c-9e0e-97387e870ddc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: GEN 33:18
Text: And Jacob came to Shalem, a city of Shechem, which is in the land of Canaan, when he came from Padanaram; and pitched his tent before the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/33/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c30c5dbd-c39b-48a8-85e4-c09e07514797>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: GEN 33:19
Text: And he bought a parcel of a field, where he had spread his tent, at the hand of the children of Hamor, Shechem’s father, for an hundred pieces of money.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/33/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c029a19-f107-4512-ab1c-553b2ef31822>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: GEN 33:20
Text: And he erected there an altar, and called it EleloheIsrael.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53c88ffc-0b48-4305-b688-fbcaace788d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: GEN 34:1
Text: And Dinah the daughter of Leah, which she bare unto Jacob, went out to see the daughters of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04528f18-e512-4a25-b5d2-4eb70568e36a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: GEN 34:2
Text: And when Shechem the son of Hamor the Hivite, prince of the country, saw her, he took her, and lay with her, and defiled her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f869ab61-924e-42fb-b053-3918eb421584>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: GEN 34:3
Text: And his soul clave unto Dinah the daughter of Jacob, and he loved the damsel, and spake kindly unto the damsel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af9dbe12-a047-49f1-897e-6f6d6fae8b52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: GEN 34:4
Text: And Shechem spake unto his father Hamor, saying, Get me this damsel to wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cf26d66-12da-4ed7-9581-e1e97885d9c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: GEN 34:5
Text: And Jacob heard that he had defiled Dinah his daughter: now his sons were with his cattle in the field: and Jacob held his peace until they were come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b0915db-5b6e-45dd-9e44-4cf58694b721>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: GEN 34:6
Text: And Hamor the father of Shechem went out unto Jacob to commune with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6409a1fd-d66f-4410-ba93-8f3d73b00bfd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: GEN 34:7
Text: And the sons of Jacob came out of the field when they heard it: and the men were grieved, and they were very wroth, because he had wrought folly in Israel in lying with Jacob’s daughter: which thing ought not to be done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbd2f521-ea03-4cc5-bf98-c87f00552e06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: GEN 34:8
Text: And Hamor communed with them, saying, The soul of my son Shechem longeth for your daughter: I pray you give her him to wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c8f2031-a0e2-4f9d-a264-c9a4e068d3be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: GEN 34:9
Text: And make ye marriages with us, and give your daughters unto us, and take our daughters unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89c42469-cc3a-4c1b-8b69-25d105d8409e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: GEN 34:10
Text: And ye shall dwell with us: and the land shall be before you; dwell and trade ye therein, and get you possessions therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31850e32-c829-4c86-8cb6-43b973494ad4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: GEN 34:11
Text: And Shechem said unto her father and unto her brethren, Let me find grace in your eyes, and what ye shall say unto me I will give.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dea42032-7e99-4746-a1c6-1f3b771dc491>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: GEN 34:12
Text: Ask me never so much dowry and gift, and I will give according as ye shall say unto me: but give me the damsel to wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8dd3c0d1-4a0d-4043-811c-bd69e0159864>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: GEN 34:13
Text: And the sons of Jacob answered Shechem and Hamor his father deceitfully, and said, because he had defiled Dinah their sister:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:143af2d8-6f2e-4849-a252-e11d2cdb35b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: GEN 34:14
Text: And they said unto them, We cannot do this thing, to give our sister to one that is uncircumcised; for that were a reproach unto us:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d43c008-cb83-4066-b88f-db73e2ce0b16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: GEN 34:15
Text: But in this will we consent unto you: If ye will be as we be, that every male of you be circumcised;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25dd8262-f282-4c7d-b367-2be11bc1078b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: GEN 34:16
Text: Then will we give our daughters unto you, and we will take your daughters to us, and we will dwell with you, and we will become one people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58f65599-79b9-4698-bc16-72a20defef73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: GEN 34:17
Text: But if ye will not hearken unto us, to be circumcised; then will we take our daughter, and we will be gone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ba8c097-52a2-4f5e-8ce8-ab4f7d40b620>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: GEN 34:18
Text: And their words pleased Hamor, and Shechem Hamor’s son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a802b54c-b3b2-4a5b-9540-ee6490e63794>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: GEN 34:19
Text: And the young man deferred not to do the thing, because he had delight in Jacob’s daughter: and he was more honourable than all the house of his father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f47febe2-c1f3-4275-a077-fe3d43936971>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: GEN 34:20
Text: And Hamor and Shechem his son came unto the gate of their city, and communed with the men of their city, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4efd996-830b-40d0-b09b-90e06a72eeea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: GEN 34:21
Text: These men are peaceable with us; therefore let them dwell in the land, and trade therein; for the land, behold, it is large enough for them; let us take their daughters to us for wives, and let us give them our daughters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6201f5d5-595a-4fdc-bcd9-8787dd54ba91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: GEN 34:22
Text: Only herein will the men consent unto us for to dwell with us, to be one people, if every male among us be circumcised, as they are circumcised.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d08847fb-bf29-4702-8496-e0a9d759abc3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: GEN 34:23
Text: Shall not their cattle and their substance and every beast of theirs be ours? only let us consent unto them, and they will dwell with us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f22608e-b4d2-455a-9aa4-d886e6305088>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: GEN 34:24
Text: And unto Hamor and unto Shechem his son hearkened all that went out of the gate of his city; and every male was circumcised, all that went out of the gate of his city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d2c95b4-ab0d-4a41-a82b-cc80098992d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: GEN 34:25
Text: And it came to pass on the third day, when they were sore, that two of the sons of Jacob, Simeon and Levi, Dinah’s brethren, took each man his sword, and came upon the city boldly, and slew all the males.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48a10953-50f5-4746-ad75-eb7b6dde73df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: GEN 34:26
Text: And they slew Hamor and Shechem his son with the edge of the sword, and took Dinah out of Shechem’s house, and went out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:636587cb-8674-4b4d-ad23-a710f0535fc9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: GEN 34:27
Text: The sons of Jacob came upon the slain, and spoiled the city, because they had defiled their sister.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6b07ea4-9d60-4d85-b3ad-204b2266b8e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: GEN 34:28
Text: They took their sheep, and their oxen, and their asses, and that which was in the city, and that which was in the field,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e43617a2-fab5-4a77-8c97-99121784e3d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: GEN 34:29
Text: And all their wealth, and all their little ones, and their wives took they captive, and spoiled even all that was in the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2788c90b-73f1-40ae-80f0-56371f74a2c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 310

Reference: GEN 34:30
Text: And Jacob said to Simeon and Levi, Ye have troubled me to make me to stink among the inhabitants of the land, among the Canaanites and the Perizzites: and I being few in number, they shall gather themselves together against me, and slay me; and I shall be destroyed, I and my house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/34/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7fb3d22-9fcb-4d22-8322-2b3549077d82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: GEN 34:31
Text: And they said, Should he deal with our sister as with an harlot?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:878a0ac5-95dc-46ea-956c-23bb699c2fe5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: GEN 35:1
Text: And God said unto Jacob, Arise, go up to Bethel, and dwell there: and make there an altar unto God, that appeared unto thee when thou fleddest from the face of Esau thy brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d492f1d-7cfd-432d-8d44-1c1c2b2dcc5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: GEN 35:2
Text: Then Jacob said unto his household, and to all that were with him, Put away the strange gods that are among you, and be clean, and change your garments:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55feff00-5d74-4967-8de5-c8f3a0d911a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: GEN 35:3
Text: And let us arise, and go up to Bethel; and I will make there an altar unto God, who answered me in the day of my distress, and was with me in the way which I went.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec651049-e56f-4c3d-9ec5-6b8fdcd4918c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: GEN 35:4
Text: And they gave unto Jacob all the strange gods which were in their hand, and all their earrings which were in their ears; and Jacob hid them under the oak which was by Shechem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e78847a-b667-468b-acd0-c458060598a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: GEN 35:5
Text: And they journeyed: and the terror of God was upon the cities that were round about them, and they did not pursue after the sons of Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13a58c1a-4743-48ff-9798-afac7eced11b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: GEN 35:6
Text: So Jacob came to Luz, which is in the land of Canaan, that is, Bethel, he and all the people that were with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb8e5239-4f10-45bd-8369-1f9a11118002>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: GEN 35:7
Text: And he built there an altar, and called the place Elbethel: because there God appeared unto him, when he fled from the face of his brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9145f10d-037c-483d-8369-8504061c0d78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: GEN 35:8
Text: But Deborah Rebekah’s nurse died, and she was buried beneath Bethel under an oak: and the name of it was called Allonbachuth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21443898-ab3f-4d9f-ad72-da6f8ddaeb74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: GEN 35:9
Text: And God appeared unto Jacob again, when he came out of Padanaram, and blessed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:372f107f-5f1a-4e3a-970b-a48625bf7197>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: GEN 35:10
Text: And God said unto him, Thy name is Jacob: thy name shall not be called any more Jacob, but Israel shall be thy name: and he called his name Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85474735-bddb-42e5-8ded-9623ea40fedd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: GEN 35:11
Text: And God said unto him, I am God Almighty: be fruitful and multiply; a nation and a company of nations shall be of thee, and kings shall come out of thy loins;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:702a8742-e978-497c-845b-dabaf1540855>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: GEN 35:12
Text: And the land which I gave Abraham and Isaac, to thee I will give it, and to thy seed after thee will I give the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e302983-aaa5-4dc5-98dd-f4e9b98a55bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: GEN 35:13
Text: And God went up from him in the place where he talked with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1d56eeb-74eb-4dc7-8721-b85aebab684f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: GEN 35:14
Text: And Jacob set up a pillar in the place where he talked with him, even a pillar of stone: and he poured a drink offering thereon, and he poured oil thereon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7225e509-b7e0-48f2-8d26-1f0ccfc391c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: GEN 35:15
Text: And Jacob called the name of the place where God spake with him, Bethel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b00d331a-6a15-46ea-bc2a-6e9f6e43662b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: GEN 35:16
Text: And they journeyed from Bethel; and there was but a little way to come to Ephrath: and Rachel travailed, and she had hard labour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f49bb94f-69e8-4596-9ac6-60a4f48c5845>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: GEN 35:17
Text: And it came to pass, when she was in hard labour, that the midwife said unto her, Fear not; thou shalt have this son also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa6cdfd1-d72d-455b-b096-c1a615f15a48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: GEN 35:18
Text: And it came to pass, as her soul was in departing, (for she died) that she called his name Benoni: but his father called him Benjamin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59434b15-0903-441b-bd78-c2ffd625172e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: GEN 35:19
Text: And Rachel died, and was buried in the way to Ephrath, which is Bethlehem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c30cc94-a345-4651-bdab-6a203f99c69e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: GEN 35:20
Text: And Jacob set a pillar upon her grave: that is the pillar of Rachel’s grave unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a353fce-328d-4a60-aded-9c84bd9fa4d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: GEN 35:21
Text: And Israel journeyed, and spread his tent beyond the tower of Edar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77fbf31e-a14d-4f67-87de-ffacbebf92ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: GEN 35:22
Text: And it came to pass, when Israel dwelt in that land, that Reuben went and lay with Bilhah his father’s concubine: and Israel heard it. Now the sons of Jacob were twelve:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9229b6e-4e94-40df-9c71-82cf29247c51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: GEN 35:23
Text: The sons of Leah; Reuben, Jacob’s firstborn, and Simeon, and Levi, and Judah, and Issachar, and Zebulun:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d85fe371-9f0e-4921-8590-4a85673c5963>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 69

Reference: GEN 35:24
Text: The sons of Rachel; Joseph, and Benjamin:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21225b16-63ce-4053-8c7b-fb46787e33d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: GEN 35:25
Text: And the sons of Bilhah, Rachel’s handmaid; Dan, and Naphtali:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a218b18-54e6-41b5-b440-facb6d1d2786>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: GEN 35:26
Text: And the sons of Zilpah, Leah’s handmaid: Gad, and Asher: these are the sons of Jacob, which were born to him in Padanaram.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94ebdba5-05ae-4ff3-9e4b-2a43fe81a9b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: GEN 35:27
Text: And Jacob came unto Isaac his father unto Mamre, unto the city of Arbah, which is Hebron, where Abraham and Isaac sojourned.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:457d31bc-fff4-4807-8553-74f7dcbd1791>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: GEN 35:28
Text: And the days of Isaac were an hundred and fourscore years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/35/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e509610c-7565-4773-9f56-56d2755f9b41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: GEN 35:29
Text: And Isaac gave up the ghost, and died, and was gathered unto his people, being old and full of days: and his sons Esau and Jacob buried him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/36/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:facf5d14-9ab1-4a47-803e-c062e6f134e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: GEN 36:1
Text: Now these are the generations of Esau, who is Edom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/36/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31bb6457-3f41-4232-913a-9b63dafb25dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: GEN 36:2
Text: Esau took his wives of the daughters of Canaan; Adah the daughter of Elon the Hittite, and Aholibamah the daughter of Anah the daughter of Zibeon the Hivite;


