Reference: GEN 37:1
Text: And Jacob dwelt in the land wherein his father was a stranger, in the land of Canaan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d385ef97-f4ef-4e22-ab9e-0a0903556adb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: GEN 37:2
Text: These are the generations of Jacob. Joseph, being seventeen years old, was feeding the flock with his brethren; and the lad was with the sons of Bilhah, and with the sons of Zilpah, his father’s wives: and Joseph brought unto his father their evil report.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2feba5b8-e106-4bad-a489-94914128075b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: GEN 37:3
Text: Now Israel loved Joseph more than all his children, because he was the son of his old age: and he made him a coat of many colours.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:177c2f23-3b96-4a43-a396-97a26ea1994d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: GEN 37:4
Text: And when his brethren saw that their father loved him more than all his brethren, they hated him, and could not speak peaceably unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eea2313c-cb06-46ac-ab4f-3da2d6b28e57>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: GEN 37:5
Text: And Joseph dreamed a dream, and he told it his brethren: and they hated him yet the more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f491c3e2-a0c0-4753-ad4e-690f7cfb5a1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: GEN 37:6
Text: And he said unto them, Hear, I pray you, this dream which I have dreamed:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83388985-12f3-4781-b251-7cf8b15c5110>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: GEN 37:7
Text: For, behold, we were binding sheaves in the field, and, lo, my sheaf arose, and also stood upright; and, behold, your sheaves stood round about, and made obeisance to my sheaf.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d32ea58-817e-410a-b181-b8512f2340fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: GEN 37:8
Text: And his brethren said to him, Shalt thou indeed reign over us? or shalt thou indeed have dominion over us? And they hated him yet the more for his dreams, and for his words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a46c276e-bf51-4317-a3ef-a6cd73200fd2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: GEN 37:9
Text: And he dreamed yet another dream, and told it his brethren, and said, Behold, I have dreamed a dream more; and, behold, the sun and the moon and the eleven stars made obeisance to me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7b5de6b-e0ce-44a3-9110-da8489b1923a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: GEN 37:10
Text: And he told it to his father, and to his brethren: and his father rebuked him, and said unto him, What is this dream that thou hast dreamed? Shall I and thy mother and thy brethren indeed come to bow down ourselves to thee to the earth?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ae38544-bb5e-45d0-b938-66ff29424668>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: GEN 37:11
Text: And his brethren envied him; but his father observed the saying.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a153761b-aa0e-437b-9cb5-0fa1dc4e6d99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: GEN 37:12
Text: And his brethren went to feed their father’s flock in Shechem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:243d59c5-6637-4999-937f-ffb675cbd798>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: GEN 37:13
Text: And Israel said unto Joseph, Do not thy brethren feed the flock in Shechem? come, and I will send thee unto them. And he said to him, Here am I.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3d25043-d086-4b6c-9924-76249a224965>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: GEN 37:14
Text: And he said to him, Go, I pray thee, see whether it be well with thy brethren, and well with the flocks; and bring me word again. So he sent him out of the vale of Hebron, and he came to Shechem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77923625-2b02-483f-966d-ec6550fe74a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: GEN 37:15
Text: And a certain man found him, and, behold, he was wandering in the field: and the man asked him, saying, What seekest thou?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5349b7c4-dc4f-453c-b28e-db282658bcc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: GEN 37:16
Text: And he said, I seek my brethren: tell me, I pray thee, where they feed their flocks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d63ef1bb-59c9-4b15-9ede-a7eae7fc7dbb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: GEN 37:17
Text: And the man said, They are departed hence; for I heard them say, Let us go to Dothan. And Joseph went after his brethren, and found them in Dothan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82ee41e2-94c9-44ff-aae1-afea4e1efdf9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: GEN 37:18
Text: And when they saw him afar off, even before he came near unto them, they conspired against him to slay him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d98a508-072e-4a95-bb12-444b03babb48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: GEN 37:19
Text: And they said one to another, Behold, this dreamer cometh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:526e0b7f-37a7-444a-8e06-e0f861c34409>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: GEN 37:20
Text: Come now therefore, and let us slay him, and cast him into some pit, and we will say, Some evil beast hath devoured him: and we shall see what will become of his dreams.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:177b7f33-14c2-4301-bcd7-e76062dab549>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: GEN 37:21
Text: And Reuben heard it, and he delivered him out of their hands; and said, Let us not kill him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7ffa0bd-cc19-4b6e-bcc8-3eff4163fa84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: GEN 37:22
Text: And Reuben said unto them, Shed no blood, but cast him into this pit that is in the wilderness, and lay no hand upon him; that he might rid him out of their hands, to deliver him to his father again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5ddf6be-8835-4ca0-ac08-e525076bf13f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: GEN 37:23
Text: And it came to pass, when Joseph was come unto his brethren, that they stript Joseph out of his coat, his coat of many colours that was on him;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b45c3b1-6da8-4866-8e1c-2950ec4c4b45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: GEN 37:24
Text: And they took him, and cast him into a pit: and the pit was empty, there was no water in it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac822376-e2aa-4635-b0c9-73c3ede26d30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: GEN 37:25
Text: And they sat down to eat bread: and they lifted up their eyes and looked, and, behold, a company of Ishmeelites came from Gilead with their camels bearing spicery and balm and myrrh, going to carry it down to Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9113923-f63f-4334-8c47-5e8cd1eaa98b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: GEN 37:26
Text: And Judah said unto his brethren, What profit is it if we slay our brother, and conceal his blood?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db359ca2-4c18-452d-8a58-23fcce27f951>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: GEN 37:27
Text: Come, and let us sell him to the Ishmeelites, and let not our hand be upon him; for he is our brother and our flesh. And his brethren were content.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e907dd49-26bb-4e25-a2ec-59a3fda09806>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: GEN 37:28
Text: Then there passed by Midianites merchantmen; and they drew and lifted up Joseph out of the pit, and sold Joseph to the Ishmeelites for twenty pieces of silver: and they brought Joseph into Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de078a4a-874a-4bd5-90e4-88a43d6b5f66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: GEN 37:29
Text: And Reuben returned unto the pit; and, behold, Joseph was not in the pit; and he rent his clothes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77c4ccd8-8481-418b-806c-b95e7c2c695e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: GEN 37:30
Text: And he returned unto his brethren, and said, The child is not; and I, whither shall I go?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc47f2cd-757f-4522-9e79-d04af70ef5c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: GEN 37:31
Text: And they took Joseph’s coat, and killed a kid of the goats, and dipped the coat in the blood;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:342cacf6-cc93-4820-ac12-345f0de7a4a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: GEN 37:32
Text: And they sent the coat of many colours, and they brought it to their father; and said, This have we found: know now whether it be thy son’s coat or no.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98edf685-becb-4d13-9ff2-c2dd02071878>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: GEN 37:33
Text: And he knew it, and said, It is my son’s coat; an evil beast hath devoured him; Joseph is without doubt rent in pieces.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d4f6b0f-3660-4726-acb1-a7b5abf48649>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: GEN 37:34
Text: And Jacob rent his clothes, and put sackcloth upon his loins, and mourned for his son many days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97b96bc5-f05d-4e56-a0f3-b9baf24e2056>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: GEN 37:35
Text: And all his sons and all his daughters rose up to comfort him; but he refused to be comforted; and he said, For I will go down into the grave unto my son mourning. Thus his father wept for him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/37/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4603467-4ad6-43c3-b525-af32f7ab0559>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: GEN 37:36
Text: And the Midianites sold him into Egypt unto Potiphar, an officer of Pharaoh’s, and captain of the guard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d1a1a8f-544b-4fed-a5f6-affaaeb11b79>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: GEN 38:1
Text: And it came to pass at that time, that Judah went down from his brethren, and turned in to a certain Adullamite, whose name was Hirah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1da26ab7-eba4-49e8-8261-cb5688aa3382>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: GEN 38:2
Text: And Judah saw there a daughter of a certain Canaanite, whose name was Shuah; and he took her, and went in unto her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:575fb9e6-cc8c-457f-bb66-0d06c7e5cb05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: GEN 38:3
Text: And she conceived, and bare a son; and he called his name Er.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e7c4c28-fcc6-4024-8f32-556c0872dc3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: GEN 38:4
Text: And she conceived again, and bare a son; and she called his name Onan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ea03e61-33b7-4424-8c58-971f703b21f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: GEN 38:5
Text: And she yet again conceived, and bare a son; and called his name Shelah: and he was at Chezib, when she bare him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3563054-50e0-4c3d-b8bf-c0cec67bc3e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: GEN 38:6
Text: And Judah took a wife for Er his firstborn, whose name was Tamar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc0bfb0c-17c6-4a10-9085-78258317a6a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: GEN 38:7
Text: And Er, Judah’s firstborn, was wicked in the sight of the LORD; and the LORD slew him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b49e3d1-5c9f-4b29-9c00-54b1b5259ab1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: GEN 38:8
Text: And Judah said unto Onan, Go in unto thy brother’s wife, and marry her, and raise up seed to thy brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aad3d089-c3a9-4388-b16b-fba91742be79>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: GEN 38:9
Text: And Onan knew that the seed should not be his; and it came to pass, when he went in unto his brother’s wife, that he spilled it on the ground, lest that he should give seed to his brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa82b23c-012b-478b-8547-7198990b27f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: GEN 38:10
Text: And the thing which he did displeased the LORD: wherefore he slew him also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9cd06f4-ddbe-4443-989f-d48eef284019>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: GEN 38:11
Text: Then said Judah to Tamar his daughter in law, Remain a widow at thy father’s house, till Shelah my son be grown: for he said, Lest peradventure he die also, as his brethren did. And Tamar went and dwelt in her father’s house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfcb4869-5202-4260-bcbc-9c048a163ec6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: GEN 38:12
Text: And in process of time the daughter of Shuah Judah’s wife died; and Judah was comforted, and went up unto his sheepshearers to Timnath, he and his friend Hirah the Adullamite.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3fef4ab8-37f3-4e8b-a35f-4c4adbded7c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: GEN 38:13
Text: And it was told Tamar, saying, Behold thy father in law goeth up to Timnath to shear his sheep.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec6096b0-45c9-4e87-b3fc-8f3b35d72a80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: GEN 38:14
Text: And she put her widow’s garments off from her, and covered her with a vail, and wrapped herself, and sat in an open place, which is by the way to Timnath; for she saw that Shelah was grown, and she was not given unto him to wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e8bf34d-3d70-400f-9144-03e4e330c60e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: GEN 38:15
Text: When Judah saw her, he thought her to be an harlot; because she had covered her face.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f902dd1b-9c11-4e8b-9bb6-8f2293979ffd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: GEN 38:16
Text: And he turned unto her by the way, and said, Go to, I pray thee, let me come in unto thee; (for he knew not that she was his daughter in law.) And she said, What wilt thou give me, that thou mayest come in unto me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82df8602-9b45-457c-ae19-54d01983db6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: GEN 38:17
Text: And he said, I will send thee a kid from the flock. And she said, Wilt thou give me a pledge, till thou send it?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94789a5a-2a93-4e90-8738-9eb6214b998f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: GEN 38:18
Text: And he said, What pledge shall I give thee? And she said, Thy signet, and thy bracelets, and thy staff that is in thine hand. And he gave it her, and came in unto her, and she conceived by him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8c8406d-81ae-48b4-adf0-4fc9f5345d46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: GEN 38:19
Text: And she arose, and went away, and laid by her vail from her, and put on the garments of her widowhood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8663db3a-fa79-4584-99de-80c4718d1d12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: GEN 38:20
Text: And Judah sent the kid by the hand of his friend the Adullamite, to receive his pledge from the woman’s hand: but he found her not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2acdde20-bd8a-4537-a136-558333ad3adb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: GEN 38:21
Text: Then he asked the men of that place, saying, Where is the harlot, that was openly by the way side? And they said, There was no harlot in this place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a19171dd-560e-4b89-a7d0-5fe2c5de03b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: GEN 38:22
Text: And he returned to Judah, and said, I cannot find her; and also the men of the place said, that there was no harlot in this place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b35e6034-ea81-44e2-92ab-18b62e81d61c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: GEN 38:23
Text: And Judah said, Let her take it to her, lest we be shamed: behold, I sent this kid, and thou hast not found her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc3666d5-fd01-4abc-87e1-ee77eb9705b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: GEN 38:24
Text: And it came to pass about three months after, that it was told Judah, saying, Tamar thy daughter in law hath played the harlot; and also, behold, she is with child by whoredom. And Judah said, Bring her forth, and let her be burnt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0d11276-6026-4940-a776-e1b2c429a3ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: GEN 38:25
Text: When she was brought forth, she sent to her father in law, saying, By the man, whose these are, am I with child: and she said, Discern, I pray thee, whose are these, the signet, and bracelets, and staff.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ace9507-b8ab-465b-86c9-e5d472b80c02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: GEN 38:26
Text: And Judah acknowledged them, and said, She hath been more righteous than I; because that I gave her not to Shelah my son. And he knew her again no more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33f5e4f7-e5da-4266-91d9-efe6cdb738c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: GEN 38:27
Text: And it came to pass in the time of her travail, that, behold, twins were in her womb.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9830abfe-6be1-4270-9e65-11e78e01015d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: GEN 38:28
Text: And it came to pass, when she travailed, that the one put out his hand: and the midwife took and bound upon his hand a scarlet thread, saying, This came out first.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4162d9bc-1aa7-40dd-9134-b33313feef31>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: GEN 38:29
Text: And it came to pass, as he drew back his hand, that, behold, his brother came out: and she said, How hast thou broken forth? this breach be upon thee: therefore his name was called Pharez.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/38/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10c2d7a8-f44a-4529-93ec-1704752dc8d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: GEN 38:30
Text: And afterward came out his brother, that had the scarlet thread upon his hand: and his name was called Zarah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/39/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:293c3f8a-69e3-48ce-be91-b7537a248d25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: GEN 39:1
Text: And Joseph was brought down to Egypt; and Potiphar, an officer of Pharaoh, captain of the guard, an Egyptian, bought him of the hands of the Ishmeelites, which had brought him down thither.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/39/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d5425ee-6080-45b3-af66-ae9796c16d37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: GEN 39:2
Text: And the LORD was with Joseph, and he was a prosperous man; and he was in the house of his master the Egyptian.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/39/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c80f5c3d-1564-4d4e-b39e-6a089a4c4375>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: GEN 39:3
Text: And his master saw that the LORD was with him, and that the LORD made all that he did to prosper in his hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/39/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:212f1abf-7a60-4792-b9f5-2ffae1dbf3b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: GEN 39:4
Text: And Joseph found grace in his sight, and he served him: and he made him overseer over his house, and all that he had he put into his hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/39/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2c52223-d27e-462b-88d5-c6d6da72cdb0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 282

Reference: GEN 39:5
Text: And it came to pass from the time that he had made him overseer in his house, and over all that he had, that the LORD blessed the Egyptian’s house for Joseph’s sake; and the blessing of the LORD was upon all that he had in the house, and in the field.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/39/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bbfa3269-fc53-47ff-8796-8bfa81c785c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: GEN 39:6
Text: And he left all that he had in Joseph’s hand; and he knew not ought he had, save the bread which he did eat. And Joseph was a goodly person, and well favoured.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/39/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bfdb5bc6-e3a9-4067-a5dc-fc2c38590ce6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: GEN 39:7
Text: And it came to pass after these things, that his master’s wife cast her eyes upon Joseph; and she said, Lie with me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/39/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bfa43956-b0c5-4ca0-9986-df2b25fffd4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: GEN 39:8
Text: But he refused, and said unto his master’s wife, Behold, my master wotteth not what is with me in the house, and he hath committed all that he hath to my hand;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/39/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79e3d164-9431-4e52-b0aa-e1fddfff5bf6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: GEN 39:9
Text: There is none greater in this house than I; neither hath he kept back any thing from me but thee, because thou art his wife: how then can I do this great wickedness, and sin against God?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/39/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34c3aef9-2d8c-4110-b569-edb4ba0157e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: GEN 39:10
Text: And it came to pass, as she spake to Joseph day by day, that he hearkened not unto her, to lie by her, or to be with her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/39/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:796e7a69-fbec-454d-abda-9f7ebe63b720>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: GEN 39:11
Text: And it came to pass about this time, that Joseph went into the house to do his business; and there was none of the men of the house there within.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/39/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22038319-6503-4bac-baac-888c271d617b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: GEN 39:12
Text: And she caught him by his garment, saying, Lie with me: and he left his garment in her hand, and fled, and got him out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/39/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ee20dfa-ef0a-4a91-ba5b-6a6e8e38cf85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: GEN 39:13
Text: And it came to pass, when she saw that he had left his garment in her hand, and was fled forth,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/39/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edb8eda9-37ec-4310-9f83-5455850d14e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: GEN 39:14
Text: That she called unto the men of her house, and spake unto them, saying, See, he hath brought in an Hebrew unto us to mock us; he came in unto me to lie with me, and I cried with a loud voice:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/39/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d94d8cc9-7260-49c7-8997-8ce822cea880>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: GEN 39:15
Text: And it came to pass, when he heard that I lifted up my voice and cried, that he left his garment with me, and fled, and got him out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/39/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cdb8a648-0c45-43c0-86e3-0e994339b37f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: GEN 39:16
Text: And she laid up his garment by her, until his lord came home.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/39/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b601af12-c820-4052-9c6a-3b571e9138e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: GEN 39:17
Text: And she spake unto him according to these words, saying, The Hebrew servant, which thou hast brought unto us, came in unto me to mock me:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/39/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21ee43d6-ec51-4c7b-a00a-6dc7398f14cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: GEN 39:18
Text: And it came to pass, as I lifted up my voice and cried, that he left his garment with me, and fled out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/39/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bfbd1689-9674-4934-812b-d83272b60eeb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: GEN 39:19
Text: And it came to pass, when his master heard the words of his wife, which she spake unto him, saying, After this manner did thy servant to me; that his wrath was kindled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/39/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a57dee8-cbdc-4082-b53e-a9e19d294fdd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: GEN 39:20
Text: And Joseph’s master took him, and put him into the prison, a place where the king’s prisoners were bound: and he was there in the prison.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/39/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df7e991f-7347-4d79-a725-4c9d2f9a40db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: GEN 39:21
Text: But the LORD was with Joseph, and shewed him mercy, and gave him favour in the sight of the keeper of the prison.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/39/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1f37912-a296-4072-8307-0cbaaa02b864>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: GEN 39:22
Text: And the keeper of the prison committed to Joseph’s hand all the prisoners that were in the prison; and whatsoever they did there, he was the doer of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/39/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81f67133-bfb0-41f2-81a9-0394713b18a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: GEN 39:23
Text: The keeper of the prison looked not to any thing that was under his hand; because the LORD was with him, and that which he did, the LORD made it to prosper.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/40/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49f7c0bc-edd1-460a-850a-5fc101c136f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: GEN 40:1
Text: And it came to pass after these things, that the butler of the king of Egypt and his baker had offended their lord the king of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/40/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b52e42f-8ae3-4650-9b9f-fb055d6ca8bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: GEN 40:2
Text: And Pharaoh was wroth against two of his officers, against the chief of the butlers, and against the chief of the bakers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/40/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:564619f2-2cd6-4bf6-90b7-784e3a61f37b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: GEN 40:3
Text: And he put them in ward in the house of the captain of the guard, into the prison, the place where Joseph was bound.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/40/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc05cd91-dbe2-4e78-a0eb-60cb822ae62a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: GEN 40:4
Text: And the captain of the guard charged Joseph with them, and he served them: and they continued a season in ward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/40/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f1137af-8687-404e-9dd0-5f2f2c2d6f53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: GEN 40:5
Text: And they dreamed a dream both of them, each man his dream in one night, each man according to the interpretation of his dream, the butler and the baker of the king of Egypt, which were bound in the prison.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/40/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8356ebb4-58cd-469a-ab1b-4f4c6ab51432>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: GEN 40:6
Text: And Joseph came in unto them in the morning, and looked upon them, and, behold, they were sad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/40/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1da1423-83b5-4a98-b60c-f27a7eb6794b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: GEN 40:7
Text: And he asked Pharaoh’s officers that were with him in the ward of his lord’s house, saying, Wherefore look ye so sadly to day?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/40/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c01dc437-0545-444e-b200-11cf1cc30ea2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: GEN 40:8
Text: And they said unto him, We have dreamed a dream, and there is no interpreter of it. And Joseph said unto them, Do not interpretations belong to God? tell me them, I pray you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/40/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eca6cfe8-5dfa-4b06-abc5-f56f7654fead>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: GEN 40:9
Text: And the chief butler told his dream to Joseph, and said to him, In my dream, behold, a vine was before me;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/40/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75c98dca-ed81-4568-b4c7-e2949a39c2c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: GEN 40:10
Text: And in the vine were three branches: and it was as though it budded, and her blossoms shot forth; and the clusters thereof brought forth ripe grapes:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/40/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11669ad1-8f2e-4d86-b49e-f36995b930d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: GEN 40:11
Text: And Pharaoh’s cup was in my hand: and I took the grapes, and pressed them into Pharaoh’s cup, and I gave the cup into Pharaoh’s hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/40/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7007e6f1-3c4c-43a1-af80-aed300b37f64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: GEN 40:12
Text: And Joseph said unto him, This is the interpretation of it: The three branches are three days:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/40/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6a51e90-ed38-425f-960d-c66246e59bc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: GEN 40:13
Text: Yet within three days shall Pharaoh lift up thine head, and restore thee unto thy place: and thou shalt deliver Pharaoh’s cup into his hand, after the former manner when thou wast his butler.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/40/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34c78901-697c-4e12-a2b7-2b650510bda5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: GEN 40:14
Text: But think on me when it shall be well with thee, and shew kindness, I pray thee, unto me, and make mention of me unto Pharaoh, and bring me out of this house:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/40/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8b480ba-ec2f-499a-b782-1cf4127f7c55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: GEN 40:15
Text: For indeed I was stolen away out of the land of the Hebrews: and here also have I done nothing that they should put me into the dungeon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/40/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e72d1087-c95b-4575-a338-32a43dce1e7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: GEN 40:16
Text: When the chief baker saw that the interpretation was good, he said unto Joseph, I also was in my dream, and, behold, I had three white baskets on my head:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/40/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:968bfc05-5040-44d3-816a-fa472af8bb2f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: GEN 40:17
Text: And in the uppermost basket there was of all manner of bakemeats for Pharaoh; and the birds did eat them out of the basket upon my head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/40/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a35ba33-bb86-41c3-af02-9fdcc3e1d25e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: GEN 40:18
Text: And Joseph answered and said, This is the interpretation thereof: The three baskets are three days:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/40/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fdcf800a-6672-4248-b1c3-a74956ae10c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: GEN 40:19
Text: Yet within three days shall Pharaoh lift up thy head from off thee, and shall hang thee on a tree; and the birds shall eat thy flesh from off thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/40/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5725b76b-7890-42e6-a096-16aebb5e7b28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: GEN 40:20
Text: And it came to pass the third day, which was Pharaoh’s birthday, that he made a feast unto all his servants: and he lifted up the head of the chief butler and of the chief baker among his servants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/40/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f206585e-42e8-49c1-948b-ee65f1cb5754>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: GEN 40:21
Text: And he restored the chief butler unto his butlership again; and he gave the cup into Pharaoh’s hand:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/40/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad0f0fe5-a5f8-470f-9ee1-03b8531e640e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: GEN 40:22
Text: But he hanged the chief baker: as Joseph had interpreted to them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/40/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86b89f5b-9c88-4763-8425-99d7aac08dc3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: GEN 40:23
Text: Yet did not the chief butler remember Joseph, but forgat him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:944c6118-a49d-4ab3-ac0f-2205b7847d76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: GEN 41:1
Text: And it came to pass at the end of two full years, that Pharaoh dreamed: and, behold, he stood by the river.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3ec2000-c67d-46fc-8a37-9ea8357ffd4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: GEN 41:2
Text: And, behold, there came up out of the river seven well favoured kine and fatfleshed; and they fed in a meadow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7180c604-4a16-4f01-bdb2-d472b94aea62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: GEN 41:3
Text: And, behold, seven other kine came up after them out of the river, ill favoured and leanfleshed; and stood by the other kine upon the brink of the river.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc050b14-97eb-4ed3-8a13-c444c39aa2f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: GEN 41:4
Text: And the ill favoured and leanfleshed kine did eat up the seven well favoured and fat kine. So Pharaoh awoke.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50d88ffe-f05e-4a5c-ba93-ad40ea2b3cd3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: GEN 41:5
Text: And he slept and dreamed the second time: and, behold, seven ears of corn came up upon one stalk, rank and good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d77cab7-f34a-4500-9da1-8e9241092608>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: GEN 41:6
Text: And, behold, seven thin ears and blasted with the east wind sprung up after them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6735e10b-e88e-42bd-b44f-1af37e52de4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: GEN 41:7
Text: And the seven thin ears devoured the seven rank and full ears. And Pharaoh awoke, and, behold, it was a dream.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7364b92-5cd2-4d1f-b1e6-93b84ca9c96e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: GEN 41:8
Text: And it came to pass in the morning that his spirit was troubled; and he sent and called for all the magicians of Egypt, and all the wise men thereof: and Pharaoh told them his dream; but there was none that could interpret them unto Pharaoh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b9849e3-e601-4afa-941f-7d1e6c882478>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: GEN 41:9
Text: Then spake the chief butler unto Pharaoh, saying, I do remember my faults this day:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4efd17a-2261-48ee-9d3d-dc63fa18cffa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: GEN 41:10
Text: Pharaoh was wroth with his servants, and put me in ward in the captain of the guard’s house, both me and the chief baker:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:874d322f-91dc-4cbb-bd74-af81f72559c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: GEN 41:11
Text: And we dreamed a dream in one night, I and he; we dreamed each man according to the interpretation of his dream.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3bd02de-7e13-4649-90e0-adf2a3baa812>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: GEN 41:12
Text: And there was there with us a young man, an Hebrew, servant to the captain of the guard; and we told him, and he interpreted to us our dreams; to each man according to his dream he did interpret.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6064577d-71a9-4cd1-8119-0ca5093806d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: GEN 41:13
Text: And it came to pass, as he interpreted to us, so it was; me he restored unto mine office, and him he hanged.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:115cf1d7-0bb1-4be7-b8a3-02216f11c5b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: GEN 41:14
Text: Then Pharaoh sent and called Joseph, and they brought him hastily out of the dungeon: and he shaved himself, and changed his raiment, and came in unto Pharaoh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3248c4ea-f83b-44e0-bde2-966cff7960c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: GEN 41:15
Text: And Pharaoh said unto Joseph, I have dreamed a dream, and there is none that can interpret it: and I have heard say of thee, that thou canst understand a dream to interpret it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6dd774a1-09e0-4113-be68-b95d75575a67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: GEN 41:16
Text: And Joseph answered Pharaoh, saying, It is not in me: God shall give Pharaoh an answer of peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a92afba-e10c-45ae-90b3-ce8b18950e45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: GEN 41:17
Text: And Pharaoh said unto Joseph, In my dream, behold, I stood upon the bank of the river:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d2c8b90-cefc-44f0-94c7-d31ea11de3db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: GEN 41:18
Text: And, behold, there came up out of the river seven kine, fatfleshed and well favoured; and they fed in a meadow:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eda53479-813a-404c-9fa6-d70ba8dbf571>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: GEN 41:19
Text: And, behold, seven other kine came up after them, poor and very ill favoured and leanfleshed, such as I never saw in all the land of Egypt for badness:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7e8c2e1-62cd-4151-a1e5-755c763fb5de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: GEN 41:20
Text: And the lean and the ill favoured kine did eat up the first seven fat kine:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32deb8fc-9bc6-4624-bcd9-e877018ddac1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: GEN 41:21
Text: And when they had eaten them up, it could not be known that they had eaten them; but they were still ill favoured, as at the beginning. So I awoke.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88163f2c-f5a5-4829-9d77-48ef0c60a57e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: GEN 41:22
Text: And I saw in my dream, and, behold, seven ears came up in one stalk, full and good:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8ac3454-851e-4ee7-aed8-8c516d39a9f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: GEN 41:23
Text: And, behold, seven ears, withered, thin, and blasted with the east wind, sprung up after them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:319c0116-11ae-4d2e-8704-747993be8d51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: GEN 41:24
Text: And the thin ears devoured the seven good ears: and I told this unto the magicians; but there was none that could declare it to me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:843e6a6c-2579-4cc7-92f8-b2f5180f2382>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: GEN 41:25
Text: And Joseph said unto Pharaoh, The dream of Pharaoh is one: God hath shewed Pharaoh what he is about to do.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d3cfdf3-63d8-4e98-9856-60edee51c378>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: GEN 41:26
Text: The seven good kine are seven years; and the seven good ears are seven years: the dream is one.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ef31edf-3fff-43c9-bfb3-bcb6a35426a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: GEN 41:27
Text: And the seven thin and ill favoured kine that came up after them are seven years; and the seven empty ears blasted with the east wind shall be seven years of famine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5ec54ef-31c9-4431-a0d3-22b6ac3604cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: GEN 41:28
Text: This is the thing which I have spoken unto Pharaoh: What God is about to do he sheweth unto Pharaoh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4289980b-4cf9-4004-ac85-02269e69b7e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: GEN 41:29
Text: Behold, there come seven years of great plenty throughout all the land of Egypt:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2acb682-92fa-45ee-9aa0-cdc898d5b221>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: GEN 41:30
Text: And there shall arise after them seven years of famine; and all the plenty shall be forgotten in the land of Egypt; and the famine shall consume the land;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce6d08c5-36ad-4292-820c-2966d89639b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: GEN 41:31
Text: And the plenty shall not be known in the land by reason of that famine following; for it shall be very grievous.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b3395c1-1f70-4ff7-a6b6-3b29b412665a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: GEN 41:32
Text: And for that the dream was doubled unto Pharaoh twice; it is because the thing is established by God, and God will shortly bring it to pass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b887c119-3fb5-4d75-bc36-c01e04ffa42a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: GEN 41:33
Text: Now therefore let Pharaoh look out a man discreet and wise, and set him over the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c38d5c8d-123e-44c8-9f2b-41f59255e408>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: GEN 41:34
Text: Let Pharaoh do this, and let him appoint officers over the land, and take up the fifth part of the land of Egypt in the seven plenteous years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4704653-795d-40cc-9a41-a794d8338fe5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: GEN 41:35
Text: And let them gather all the food of those good years that come, and lay up corn under the hand of Pharaoh, and let them keep food in the cities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e6c4ace-725d-44c9-97ed-4435f329b4a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: GEN 41:36
Text: And that food shall be for store to the land against the seven years of famine, which shall be in the land of Egypt; that the land perish not through the famine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:089b65a9-4cf2-4ffc-be1c-c8ba1e667961>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: GEN 41:37
Text: And the thing was good in the eyes of Pharaoh, and in the eyes of all his servants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec27073c-bd0d-4c7f-b8ba-dafd3a308900>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: GEN 41:38
Text: And Pharaoh said unto his servants, Can we find such a one as this is, a man in whom the Spirit of God is?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d925152-8d2f-4848-9108-2584d994293f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: GEN 41:39
Text: And Pharaoh said unto Joseph, Forasmuch as God hath shewed thee all this, there is none so discreet and wise as thou art:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f5c7d6b-b9f9-4963-8048-3ffbe849ce06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: GEN 41:40
Text: Thou shalt be over my house, and according unto thy word shall all my people be ruled: only in the throne will I be greater than thou.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f94590e4-f7cc-4702-bb73-7ee7020564f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: GEN 41:41
Text: And Pharaoh said unto Joseph, See, I have set thee over all the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e935656-dad8-4337-bdbe-e6ab8b178bd8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: GEN 41:42
Text: And Pharaoh took off his ring from his hand, and put it upon Joseph’s hand, and arrayed him in vestures of fine linen, and put a gold chain about his neck;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:adefe431-c369-47a9-8dab-7177447acb81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: GEN 41:43
Text: And he made him to ride in the second chariot which he had; and they cried before him, Bow the knee: and he made him ruler over all the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6dd80306-871e-418a-9006-7d9e054ba819>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: GEN 41:44
Text: And Pharaoh said unto Joseph, I am Pharaoh, and without thee shall no man lift up his hand or foot in all the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e03b7e8-8576-4230-ae07-02cf33dc099d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: GEN 41:45
Text: And Pharaoh called Joseph’s name Zaphnathpaaneah; and he gave him to wife Asenath the daughter of Potipherah priest of On. And Joseph went out over all the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66dbf46e-b725-48d5-9821-2174fa7fb49c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: GEN 41:46
Text: And Joseph was thirty years old when he stood before Pharaoh king of Egypt. And Joseph went out from the presence of Pharaoh, and went throughout all the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:369bd114-2e64-4500-ade4-b5fd0d437b93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: GEN 41:47
Text: And in the seven plenteous years the earth brought forth by handfuls.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c21e6470-df4f-4581-b14b-43031301e97b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: GEN 41:48
Text: And he gathered up all the food of the seven years, which were in the land of Egypt, and laid up the food in the cities: the food of the field, which was round about every city, laid he up in the same.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9490cd79-870f-4417-a909-0c39132ce4c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: GEN 41:49
Text: And Joseph gathered corn as the sand of the sea, very much, until he left numbering; for it was without number.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7cb441c0-4ac3-4773-b443-0f1f8403f006>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: GEN 41:50
Text: And unto Joseph were born two sons before the years of famine came, which Asenath the daughter of Potipherah priest of On bare unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b719d953-8a0f-4e69-ba5f-17b2ea0d2635>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: GEN 41:51
Text: And Joseph called the name of the firstborn Manasseh: For God, said he, hath made me forget all my toil, and all my father’s house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d8b54b5-2382-41ed-b777-6a855ade5f74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: GEN 41:52
Text: And the name of the second called he Ephraim: For God hath caused me to be fruitful in the land of my affliction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf5780a1-0d6b-465f-a754-3137538c002c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: GEN 41:53
Text: And the seven years of plenteousness, that was in the land of Egypt, were ended.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3f8269e-c227-454f-900d-cbfed3eda2e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: GEN 41:54
Text: And the seven years of dearth began to come, according as Joseph had said: and the dearth was in all lands; but in all the land of Egypt there was bread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/55
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55972371-0b36-4b66-90cb-8f16f0a45777>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: GEN 41:55
Text: And when all the land of Egypt was famished, the people cried to Pharaoh for bread: and Pharaoh said unto all the Egyptians, Go unto Joseph; what he saith to you, do.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/56
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5350319-5c2c-4ebc-83ec-49d1cc133e0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: GEN 41:56
Text: And the famine was over all the face of the earth: and Joseph opened all the storehouses, and sold unto the Egyptians; and the famine waxed sore in the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/41/57
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb001431-ee6b-4e43-98cd-9b0c4c5b1f54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: GEN 41:57
Text: And all countries came into Egypt to Joseph for to buy corn; because that the famine was so sore in all lands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ffcc0f1-73de-4151-a1a9-a6273f027e0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: GEN 42:1
Text: Now when Jacob saw that there was corn in Egypt, Jacob said unto his sons, Why do ye look one upon another?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88bf6d8e-3286-40ed-8e14-e6ea958f781b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: GEN 42:2
Text: And he said, Behold, I have heard that there is corn in Egypt: get you down thither, and buy for us from thence; that we may live, and not die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aac6fadc-ad56-4087-b5bc-62ba48f9be3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: GEN 42:3
Text: And Joseph’s ten brethren went down to buy corn in Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05f677f2-d191-4ebf-8ea8-f09de4e6398a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: GEN 42:4
Text: But Benjamin, Joseph’s brother, Jacob sent not with his brethren; for he said, Lest peradventure mischief befall him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6192d93-da95-4e13-8a65-ed95e72c46bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: GEN 42:5
Text: And the sons of Israel came to buy corn among those that came: for the famine was in the land of Canaan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a6618e0-b5ff-4db7-b8d4-59329bc688d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: GEN 42:6
Text: And Joseph was the governor over the land, and he it was that sold to all the people of the land: and Joseph’s brethren came, and bowed down themselves before him with their faces to the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e41e0b9f-15fc-4810-b1f1-274c132a3c0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: GEN 42:7
Text: And Joseph saw his brethren, and he knew them, but made himself strange unto them, and spake roughly unto them; and he said unto them, Whence come ye? And they said, From the land of Canaan to buy food.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ac742ec-5266-479c-8756-ff8df1387094>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: GEN 42:8
Text: And Joseph knew his brethren, but they knew not him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe0f844f-7847-4e25-96aa-95a77e3527d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: GEN 42:9
Text: And Joseph remembered the dreams which he dreamed of them, and said unto them, Ye are spies; to see the nakedness of the land ye are come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:008be64e-d2a5-4302-ab22-44ec47a727b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: GEN 42:10
Text: And they said unto him, Nay, my lord, but to buy food are thy servants come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8eca6f99-7b8e-4f2d-b4d8-60662afe0e8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: GEN 42:11
Text: We are all one man’s sons; we are true men, thy servants are no spies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a681600f-3182-4495-8958-5bcda5cc4071>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: GEN 42:12
Text: And he said unto them, Nay, but to see the nakedness of the land ye are come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4e9d0b1-24e9-4467-9800-123ea78cbd5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: GEN 42:13
Text: And they said, Thy servants are twelve brethren, the sons of one man in the land of Canaan; and, behold, the youngest is this day with our father, and one is not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5eb843c-b6c5-4d69-81bc-155e959ff289>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: GEN 42:14
Text: And Joseph said unto them, That is it that I spake unto you, saying, Ye are spies:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11d8c882-e281-40af-9204-8b3bef89d089>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: GEN 42:15
Text: Hereby ye shall be proved: By the life of Pharaoh ye shall not go forth hence, except your youngest brother come hither.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e9d81b2-137c-4cea-9a38-a9486ee612fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: GEN 42:16
Text: Send one of you, and let him fetch your brother, and ye shall be kept in prison, that your words may be proved, whether there be any truth in you: or else by the life of Pharaoh surely ye are spies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4209c8ba-66e3-44e3-b333-78d5a4008927>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: GEN 42:17
Text: And he put them all together into ward three days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83bb52ba-ac6b-45d0-bddb-1fbea9e8f8e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: GEN 42:18
Text: And Joseph said unto them the third day, This do, and live; for I fear God:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2d3ce42-8109-4cbd-ac1d-75b23c2eea59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: GEN 42:19
Text: If ye be true men, let one of your brethren be bound in the house of your prison: go ye, carry corn for the famine of your houses:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d05afa30-457b-46c6-8246-79e1b988e2c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: GEN 42:20
Text: But bring your youngest brother unto me; so shall your words be verified, and ye shall not die. And they did so.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9008c953-9449-4821-9e13-99c39c5dcc81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: GEN 42:21
Text: And they said one to another, We are verily guilty concerning our brother, in that we saw the anguish of his soul, when he besought us, and we would not hear; therefore is this distress come upon us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3345526d-d789-4c27-98f3-d66025466bb9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: GEN 42:22
Text: And Reuben answered them, saying, Spake I not unto you, saying, Do not sin against the child; and ye would not hear? therefore, behold, also his blood is required.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65e02687-b1f1-4c0e-a047-2dc61eff1735>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: GEN 42:23
Text: And they knew not that Joseph understood them; for he spake unto them by an interpreter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7dbced0c-600d-420d-bad2-f489efbcb811>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: GEN 42:24
Text: And he turned himself about from them, and wept; and returned to them again, and communed with them, and took from them Simeon, and bound him before their eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac608ddc-a325-45a5-8f7a-ab9eac6d4ebf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: GEN 42:25
Text: Then Joseph commanded to fill their sacks with corn, and to restore every man’s money into his sack, and to give them provision for the way: and thus did he unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ad63ae2-5446-41d8-8545-79eafb23febe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: GEN 42:26
Text: And they laded their asses with the corn, and departed thence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a8ac4bd-ddbd-4fd6-93e8-2e4f9e41ef31>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: GEN 42:27
Text: And as one of them opened his sack to give his ass provender in the inn, he espied his money; for, behold, it was in his sack’s mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23ca019f-4996-4b6f-bae7-a3aa83368c9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: GEN 42:28
Text: And he said unto his brethren, My money is restored; and, lo, it is even in my sack: and their heart failed them, and they were afraid, saying one to another, What is this that God hath done unto us?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df913a87-fdc4-4b0d-a679-8f987a5d2ecd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: GEN 42:29
Text: And they came unto Jacob their father unto the land of Canaan, and told him all that befell unto them; saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5cb4de50-39ab-4eed-98e4-063e1f90a28e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: GEN 42:30
Text: The man, who is the lord of the land, spake roughly to us, and took us for spies of the country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7df1e4ba-0754-44c3-83cf-6b96f8287745>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: GEN 42:31
Text: And we said unto him, We are true men; we are no spies:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24d82f81-6a3e-4af9-a49e-f225509f6d96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: GEN 42:32
Text: We be twelve brethren, sons of our father; one is not, and the youngest is this day with our father in the land of Canaan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60cfa8fb-6ac5-4139-a514-121887e3a65a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: GEN 42:33
Text: And the man, the lord of the country, said unto us, Hereby shall I know that ye are true men; leave one of your brethren here with me, and take food for the famine of your households, and be gone:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a7c1a02-b40f-45cb-92c6-add512c81479>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: GEN 42:34
Text: And bring your youngest brother unto me: then shall I know that ye are no spies, but that ye are true men: so will I deliver you your brother, and ye shall traffick in the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d98445f-633f-43fa-9b53-f7fa7e0d2047>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: GEN 42:35
Text: And it came to pass as they emptied their sacks, that, behold, every man’s bundle of money was in his sack: and when both they and their father saw the bundles of money, they were afraid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04b27a9a-83d9-47e4-95ea-8a0f1da4c1b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: GEN 42:36
Text: And Jacob their father said unto them, Me have ye bereaved of my children: Joseph is not, and Simeon is not, and ye will take Benjamin away: all these things are against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a1b718d-36be-4a1d-963b-e1d3f35d646d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: GEN 42:37
Text: And Reuben spake unto his father, saying, Slay my two sons, if I bring him not to thee: deliver him into my hand, and I will bring him to thee again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/42/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49ea30fd-0bb1-4707-b600-4803108e9ebe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: GEN 42:38
Text: And he said, My son shall not go down with you; for his brother is dead, and he is left alone: if mischief befall him by the way in the which ye go, then shall ye bring down my gray hairs with sorrow to the grave.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23a6260c-5871-42b6-a5b5-6dc37acec42c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 63

Reference: GEN 43:1
Text: And the famine was sore in the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7925e06-b2eb-466a-8f2b-8f9968516b25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: GEN 43:2
Text: And it came to pass, when they had eaten up the corn which they had brought out of Egypt, their father said unto them, Go again, buy us a little food.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6266557e-e43c-47ed-82a5-515a9c9addec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: GEN 43:3
Text: And Judah spake unto him, saying, The man did solemnly protest unto us, saying, Ye shall not see my face, except your brother be with you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f42da0d7-fbbf-446b-8c81-f569d7e05335>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: GEN 43:4
Text: If thou wilt send our brother with us, we will go down and buy thee food:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9e102fe-e1e9-4ce5-9715-d8fe53aee947>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: GEN 43:5
Text: But if thou wilt not send him, we will not go down: for the man said unto us, Ye shall not see my face, except your brother be with you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c97719a3-b5a6-4fb3-9d68-40418650fb60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: GEN 43:6
Text: And Israel said, Wherefore dealt ye so ill with me, as to tell the man whether ye had yet a brother?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cec98372-4c03-4fd3-aa54-1e1a911ed576>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 283

Reference: GEN 43:7
Text: And they said, The man asked us straitly of our state, and of our kindred, saying, Is your father yet alive? have ye another brother? and we told him according to the tenor of these words: could we certainly know that he would say, Bring your brother down?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0202af9a-1294-41db-bd31-b645df498bda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: GEN 43:8
Text: And Judah said unto Israel his father, Send the lad with me, and we will arise and go; that we may live, and not die, both we, and thou, and also our little ones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f69a0e5-f96c-45ff-94c3-0c6780c9cb6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: GEN 43:9
Text: I will be surety for him; of my hand shalt thou require him: if I bring him not unto thee, and set him before thee, then let me bear the blame for ever:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03d7524c-62de-4fbf-ae68-fe0a0e39db2b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: GEN 43:10
Text: For except we had lingered, surely now we had returned this second time.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8de2d075-e273-4cdd-809f-fcd842759882>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: GEN 43:11
Text: And their father Israel said unto them, If it must be so now, do this; take of the best fruits in the land in your vessels, and carry down the man a present, a little balm, and a little honey, spices, and myrrh, nuts, and almonds:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d339a8ea-ce01-4ebf-ab89-206a183f4824>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: GEN 43:12
Text: And take double money in your hand; and the money that was brought again in the mouth of your sacks, carry it again in your hand; peradventure it was an oversight:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:020f3347-7233-4877-83f3-171016e03d91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: GEN 43:13
Text: Take also your brother, and arise, go again unto the man:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed690d4e-06d3-43ac-aa99-32384796551b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: GEN 43:14
Text: And God Almighty give you mercy before the man, that he may send away your other brother, and Benjamin. If I be bereaved of my children, I am bereaved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:363f49ca-a760-42c4-9fe8-5c8c942d9f88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: GEN 43:15
Text: And the men took that present, and they took double money in their hand and Benjamin; and rose up, and went down to Egypt, and stood before Joseph.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d49d34bb-2719-4fb7-8916-7ace5e596306>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: GEN 43:16
Text: And when Joseph saw Benjamin with them, he said to the ruler of his house, Bring these men home, and slay, and make ready; for these men shall dine with me at noon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:285f985b-b4fa-447e-9a94-9bb1464c79ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: GEN 43:17
Text: And the man did as Joseph bade; and the man brought the men into Joseph’s house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bcd8c9d9-ae70-4e71-8699-fd0c7b87f60d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 301

Reference: GEN 43:18
Text: And the men were afraid, because they were brought into Joseph’s house; and they said, Because of the money that was returned in our sacks at the first time are we brought in; that he may seek occasion against us, and fall upon us, and take us for bondmen, and our asses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3bd4ec33-0d5c-4cf3-994f-235322109f1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: GEN 43:19
Text: And they came near to the steward of Joseph’s house, and they communed with him at the door of the house,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3320044c-c3d8-4936-aac7-85339469645d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: GEN 43:20
Text: And said, O sir, we came indeed down at the first time to buy food:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afd861c3-1128-435a-8c1d-b2794caa5109>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: GEN 43:21
Text: And it came to pass, when we came to the inn, that we opened our sacks, and, behold, every man’s money was in the mouth of his sack, our money in full weight: and we have brought it again in our hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89e420ae-06a0-4594-bce5-097e49cddf19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: GEN 43:22
Text: And other money have we brought down in our hands to buy food: we cannot tell who put our money in our sacks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36bedac8-ced8-420f-b224-92ce0bcb289d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: GEN 43:23
Text: And he said, Peace be to you, fear not: your God, and the God of your father, hath given you treasure in your sacks: I had your money. And he brought Simeon out unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0be9549-bc8b-41fe-b311-c95617fb29ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: GEN 43:24
Text: And the man brought the men into Joseph’s house, and gave them water, and they washed their feet; and he gave their asses provender.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0327ff15-c145-462f-8d9e-336951304675>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: GEN 43:25
Text: And they made ready the present against Joseph came at noon: for they heard that they should eat bread there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47632530-ffd4-4481-81d1-74cabdb8559e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: GEN 43:26
Text: And when Joseph came home, they brought him the present which was in their hand into the house, and bowed themselves to him to the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17db9cd0-1aaa-47bb-9b5d-d0bd8632e4b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: GEN 43:27
Text: And he asked them of their welfare, and said, Is your father well, the old man of whom ye spake? Is he yet alive?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6409dc9d-450d-4029-9f87-41314ba0eb0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: GEN 43:28
Text: And they answered, Thy servant our father is in good health, he is yet alive. And they bowed down their heads, and made obeisance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d0088f7-ddef-4a2d-8514-f1751df3956b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: GEN 43:29
Text: And he lifted up his eyes, and saw his brother Benjamin, his mother’s son, and said, Is this your younger brother, of whom ye spake unto me? And he said, God be gracious unto thee, my son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:623fbe75-6c3d-4350-8ccd-9fdf01bbf2d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: GEN 43:30
Text: And Joseph made haste; for his bowels did yearn upon his brother: and he sought where to weep; and he entered into his chamber, and wept there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f26d288e-6fef-4e16-8740-a4ec79f17d0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: GEN 43:31
Text: And he washed his face, and went out, and refrained himself, and said, Set on bread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a8036ea-82b9-4a23-a397-f1f75a69cfb2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: GEN 43:32
Text: And they set on for him by himself, and for them by themselves, and for the Egyptians, which did eat with him, by themselves: because the Egyptians might not eat bread with the Hebrews; for that is an abomination unto the Egyptians.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c26da619-9dff-4fc8-9491-23f44acb2589>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: GEN 43:33
Text: And they sat before him, the firstborn according to his birthright, and the youngest according to his youth: and the men marvelled one at another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/43/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c64e491-67e8-487e-9430-9c39adf7c164>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: GEN 43:34
Text: And he took and sent messes unto them from before him: but Benjamin’s mess was five times so much as any of theirs. And they drank, and were merry with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef2c4b98-931b-4246-84be-f2c0d6373721>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: GEN 44:1
Text: And he commanded the steward of his house, saying, Fill the men’s sacks with food, as much as they can carry, and put every man’s money in his sack’s mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08cf07be-ebba-4b4e-bb26-183b3c35d16c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: GEN 44:2
Text: And put my cup, the silver cup, in the sack’s mouth of the youngest, and his corn money. And he did according to the word that Joseph had spoken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ea06578-daa4-47b1-ba0f-573c769b363a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: GEN 44:3
Text: As soon as the morning was light, the men were sent away, they and their asses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ef17a74-224f-4bea-9232-1c952a8e9a1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: GEN 44:4
Text: And when they were gone out of the city, and not yet far off, Joseph said unto his steward, Up, follow after the men; and when thou dost overtake them, say unto them, Wherefore have ye rewarded evil for good?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bc05d86-4076-4796-a5f8-d903b487622d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: GEN 44:5
Text: Is not this it in which my lord drinketh, and whereby indeed he divineth? ye have done evil in so doing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fccb5793-3319-4567-bfba-fd0b2334397b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: GEN 44:6
Text: And he overtook them, and he spake unto them these same words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a62fbd1e-67a4-4bfb-9140-37322c084ccb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: GEN 44:7
Text: And they said unto him, Wherefore saith my lord these words? God forbid that thy servants should do according to this thing:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f50f6910-fb18-4664-8e07-256c462a4026>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: GEN 44:8
Text: Behold, the money, which we found in our sacks’ mouths, we brought again unto thee out of the land of Canaan: how then should we steal out of thy lord’s house silver or gold?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4d71d61-9643-44ba-8b42-c426d1588a44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: GEN 44:9
Text: With whomsoever of thy servants it be found, both let him die, and we also will be my lord’s bondmen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7498fac2-288a-48f2-8bfb-903d972343ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: GEN 44:10
Text: And he said, Now also let it be according unto your words: he with whom it is found shall be my servant; and ye shall be blameless.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55369ffb-4c54-45b5-8a3d-dad584082ff7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: GEN 44:11
Text: Then they speedily took down every man his sack to the ground, and opened every man his sack.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca20d679-2d9b-434c-b94f-d3af1efe86c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: GEN 44:12
Text: And he searched, and began at the eldest, and left at the youngest: and the cup was found in Benjamin’s sack.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35b3773d-24f5-4862-b4bf-45880b1bd15c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: GEN 44:13
Text: Then they rent their clothes, and laded every man his ass, and returned to the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4acf0db-963c-4ead-9a12-d211f641f356>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: GEN 44:14
Text: And Judah and his brethren came to Joseph’s house; for he was yet there: and they fell before him on the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1830ac3f-13dc-478d-9de3-1dabae2c0cca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: GEN 44:15
Text: And Joseph said unto them, What deed is this that ye have done? wot ye not that such a man as I can certainly divine?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98745d5c-50bd-4276-a75a-51ed1b2a1626>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: GEN 44:16
Text: And Judah said, What shall we say unto my lord? what shall we speak? or how shall we clear ourselves? God hath found out the iniquity of thy servants: behold, we are my lord’s servants, both we, and he also with whom the cup is found.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df9f5a5c-7408-4a02-bac5-cee9612efc3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: GEN 44:17
Text: And he said, God forbid that I should do so: but the man in whose hand the cup is found, he shall be my servant; and as for you, get you up in peace unto your father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97951a58-aa26-4100-bdba-6209bbf650bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: GEN 44:18
Text: Then Judah came near unto him, and said, Oh my lord, let thy servant, I pray thee, speak a word in my lord’s ears, and let not thine anger burn against thy servant: for thou art even as Pharaoh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc812c80-1a14-4f5e-9e61-4311f1100aee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: GEN 44:19
Text: My lord asked his servants, saying, Have ye a father, or a brother?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97a39d13-b5a7-4680-a2e5-64d5d226576d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: GEN 44:20
Text: And we said unto my lord, We have a father, an old man, and a child of his old age, a little one; and his brother is dead, and he alone is left of his mother, and his father loveth him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80a5403b-400f-4513-aec2-ed520f66b50e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: GEN 44:21
Text: And thou saidst unto thy servants, Bring him down unto me, that I may set mine eyes upon him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f48e61ea-8f89-4c9a-b868-254ae7c63a4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: GEN 44:22
Text: And we said unto my lord, The lad cannot leave his father: for if he should leave his father, his father would die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d650ed88-17e1-4e43-9228-5bb11accd088>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: GEN 44:23
Text: And thou saidst unto thy servants, Except your youngest brother come down with you, ye shall see my face no more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aee10879-a81c-43e9-9fb8-8054f169de09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: GEN 44:24
Text: And it came to pass when we came up unto thy servant my father, we told him the words of my lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b8dc5bf-2609-4948-a881-fd73d34a2944>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: GEN 44:25
Text: And our father said, Go again, and buy us a little food.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:780e7246-133e-4c8d-a219-a32c6d548e0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: GEN 44:26
Text: And we said, We cannot go down: if our youngest brother be with us, then will we go down: for we may not see the man’s face, except our youngest brother be with us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:739224d1-ff60-4010-a865-b19fafb33b37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: GEN 44:27
Text: And thy servant my father said unto us, Ye know that my wife bare me two sons:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:248a8fe8-cd9f-4676-9d17-3c8fb11adced>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: GEN 44:28
Text: And the one went out from me, and I said, Surely he is torn in pieces; and I saw him not since:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c35a71ce-c7c7-4cda-8d95-d986601d0200>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: GEN 44:29
Text: And if ye take this also from me, and mischief befall him, ye shall bring down my gray hairs with sorrow to the grave.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30d9b516-d659-4291-b330-6ffa44b59aa3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: GEN 44:30
Text: Now therefore when I come to thy servant my father, and the lad be not with us; seeing that his life is bound up in the lad’s life;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:735cdcfd-b6ca-4857-8710-b85e197d57d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: GEN 44:31
Text: It shall come to pass, when he seeth that the lad is not with us, that he will die: and thy servants shall bring down the gray hairs of thy servant our father with sorrow to the grave.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb4d77b7-4afa-4056-8cda-7236205159e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: GEN 44:32
Text: For thy servant became surety for the lad unto my father, saying, If I bring him not unto thee, then I shall bear the blame to my father for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79efe236-b348-4306-99da-7dc8fcdd0b04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: GEN 44:33
Text: Now therefore, I pray thee, let thy servant abide instead of the lad a bondman to my lord; and let the lad go up with his brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/44/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:147eab0d-dead-4cda-9d73-64807dd6b76b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: GEN 44:34
Text: For how shall I go up to my father, and the lad be not with me? lest peradventure I see the evil that shall come on my father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb7613b0-35d5-4056-a422-616579107cdb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: GEN 45:1
Text: Then Joseph could not refrain himself before all them that stood by him; and he cried, Cause every man to go out from me. And there stood no man with him, while Joseph made himself known unto his brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8ab4bca-5a09-494d-8df3-75f5c9b61341>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: GEN 45:2
Text: And he wept aloud: and the Egyptians and the house of Pharaoh heard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6af61d49-7c23-46e9-ac0f-8364e8207873>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: GEN 45:3
Text: And Joseph said unto his brethren, I am Joseph; doth my father yet live? And his brethren could not answer him; for they were troubled at his presence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9680057d-07c1-4f02-9d4e-7e9995d87c15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: GEN 45:4
Text: And Joseph said unto his brethren, Come near to me, I pray you. And they came near. And he said, I am Joseph your brother, whom ye sold into Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70e387e5-715a-4135-8d3e-a899bac9da3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: GEN 45:5
Text: Now therefore be not grieved, nor angry with yourselves, that ye sold me hither: for God did send me before you to preserve life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3196918d-5db4-41b3-8be6-4ead27c5fa21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: GEN 45:6
Text: For these two years hath the famine been in the land: and yet there are five years, in the which there shall neither be earing nor harvest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3aa05bc6-24ca-4481-ab7d-3714017e7305>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: GEN 45:7
Text: And God sent me before you to preserve you a posterity in the earth, and to save your lives by a great deliverance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b7b57a1-87e5-4d4e-b7aa-7873045a74eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: GEN 45:8
Text: So now it was not you that sent me hither, but God: and he hath made me a father to Pharaoh, and lord of all his house, and a ruler throughout all the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cc632b3-26e0-4b71-baa9-88b8ff11b2d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: GEN 45:9
Text: Haste ye, and go up to my father, and say unto him, Thus saith thy son Joseph, God hath made me lord of all Egypt: come down unto me, tarry not:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b461687e-e478-4b67-b88a-4c56a2d4f764>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: GEN 45:10
Text: And thou shalt dwell in the land of Goshen, and thou shalt be near unto me, thou, and thy children, and thy children’s children, and thy flocks, and thy herds, and all that thou hast:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3318e626-ff3b-4d2f-b421-4c843ce6bcd0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: GEN 45:11
Text: And there will I nourish thee; for yet there are five years of famine; lest thou, and thy household, and all that thou hast, come to poverty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ad7006d-d582-4df7-8738-feef5d5d266a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: GEN 45:12
Text: And, behold, your eyes see, and the eyes of my brother Benjamin, that it is my mouth that speaketh unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a7d6cae-8377-4148-a1d5-5fade735e9b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: GEN 45:13
Text: And ye shall tell my father of all my glory in Egypt, and of all that ye have seen; and ye shall haste and bring down my father hither.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c83b7385-6cef-4d39-b5b7-3e9a679c71dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: GEN 45:14
Text: And he fell upon his brother Benjamin’s neck, and wept; and Benjamin wept upon his neck.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99ded7d4-c5f9-4520-a125-deebf755716f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: GEN 45:15
Text: Moreover he kissed all his brethren, and wept upon them: and after that his brethren talked with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d1fdbcb-3af0-48e1-8e75-21b0ec6646ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: GEN 45:16
Text: And the fame thereof was heard in Pharaoh’s house, saying, Joseph’s brethren are come: and it pleased Pharaoh well, and his servants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb0d8fad-e728-44d7-8d17-e33eefb3aa4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: GEN 45:17
Text: And Pharaoh said unto Joseph, Say unto thy brethren, This do ye; lade your beasts, and go, get you unto the land of Canaan;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb748883-321d-4ccb-96f7-0331a20c7a38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: GEN 45:18
Text: And take your father and your households, and come unto me: and I will give you the good of the land of Egypt, and ye shall eat the fat of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ac867da-3037-4ae4-ba1e-e2558c0d540b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: GEN 45:19
Text: Now thou art commanded, this do ye; take you wagons out of the land of Egypt for your little ones, and for your wives, and bring your father, and come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6bb7f7e-b62b-45d2-b09d-bf1b501fec95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: GEN 45:20
Text: Also regard not your stuff; for the good of all the land of Egypt is yours.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b643a9ac-7908-46bb-b0bd-ab79db248647>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: GEN 45:21
Text: And the children of Israel did so: and Joseph gave them wagons, according to the commandment of Pharaoh, and gave them provision for the way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:367a933d-5c70-4d45-bbcc-83b961d14dae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: GEN 45:22
Text: To all of them he gave each man changes of raiment; but to Benjamin he gave three hundred pieces of silver, and five changes of raiment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a0bfd15-03fc-4298-a70b-5930a7b8f247>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: GEN 45:23
Text: And to his father he sent after this manner; ten asses laden with the good things of Egypt, and ten she asses laden with corn and bread and meat for his father by the way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ab29770-56fe-460b-9f53-741935a7539a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: GEN 45:24
Text: So he sent his brethren away, and they departed: and he said unto them, See that ye fall not out by the way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:efb4264d-3e8c-4bbf-8159-65362f4374bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: GEN 45:25
Text: And they went up out of Egypt, and came into the land of Canaan unto Jacob their father,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca3846f5-7068-468b-80be-15b9907affbe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: GEN 45:26
Text: And told him, saying, Joseph is yet alive, and he is governor over all the land of Egypt. And Jacob’s heart fainted, for he believed them not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f75a608-9267-447c-beab-6deb739a5947>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: GEN 45:27
Text: And they told him all the words of Joseph, which he had said unto them: and when he saw the wagons which Joseph had sent to carry him, the spirit of Jacob their father revived:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/45/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3654951-3275-4eca-8176-e41689f42c25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: GEN 45:28
Text: And Israel said, It is enough; Joseph my son is yet alive: I will go and see him before I die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d040f403-4bab-4c0a-8f27-ec0fa597f548>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: GEN 46:1
Text: And Israel took his journey with all that he had, and came to Beersheba, and offered sacrifices unto the God of his father Isaac.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e161993d-1751-49e8-a581-eece693bd5da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: GEN 46:2
Text: And God spake unto Israel in the visions of the night, and said, Jacob, Jacob. And he said, Here am I.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a708f1ef-cf03-41cf-8702-cfdea8a2e3e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: GEN 46:3
Text: And he said, I am God, the God of thy father: fear not to go down into Egypt; for I will there make of thee a great nation:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5cc0cf4-67d1-4b70-88b9-db7bab353445>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: GEN 46:4
Text: I will go down with thee into Egypt; and I will also surely bring thee up again: and Joseph shall put his hand upon thine eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c590d77-728c-439c-ad47-de63b3303095>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: GEN 46:5
Text: And Jacob rose up from Beersheba: and the sons of Israel carried Jacob their father, and their little ones, and their wives, in the wagons which Pharaoh had sent to carry him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58eabd44-a2f0-4704-a1e0-c34d89c9e263>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: GEN 46:6
Text: And they took their cattle, and their goods, which they had gotten in the land of Canaan, and came into Egypt, Jacob, and all his seed with him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0aadb80-3296-435c-881d-7d4089df5ab6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: GEN 46:7
Text: His sons, and his sons’ sons with him, his daughters, and his sons’ daughters, and all his seed brought he with him into Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e3bf5cc-fa05-461a-9836-2f16bcc0ca7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: GEN 46:8
Text: And these are the names of the children of Israel, which came into Egypt, Jacob and his sons: Reuben, Jacob’s firstborn.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d675b6d-b546-44d7-805c-4aa963d26e3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: GEN 46:9
Text: And the sons of Reuben; Hanoch, and Phallu, and Hezron, and Carmi.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9fe4dfe-c1c7-4ecb-a156-5b95647b5f84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: GEN 46:10
Text: And the sons of Simeon; Jemuel, and Jamin, and Ohad, and Jachin, and Zohar, and Shaul the son of a Canaanitish woman.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d798518-e86b-4378-8236-82b448a4381a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: GEN 46:11
Text: And the sons of Levi; Gershon, Kohath, and Merari.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee9c003d-6bac-4ab3-82c9-417677832e62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: GEN 46:12
Text: And the sons of Judah; Er, and Onan, and Shelah, and Pharez, and Zarah: but Er and Onan died in the land of Canaan. And the sons of Pharez were Hezron and Hamul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e409bb8-99a3-432d-9382-8c737645fb2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: GEN 46:13
Text: And the sons of Issachar; Tola, and Phuvah, and Job, and Shimron.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:932832dd-7b32-48d0-91e1-c028e2112c82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: GEN 46:14
Text: And the sons of Zebulun; Sered, and Elon, and Jahleel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15a3a7df-9acf-48d3-81c7-f1eaa60d8810>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: GEN 46:15
Text: These be the sons of Leah, which she bare unto Jacob in Padanaram, with his daughter Dinah: all the souls of his sons and his daughters were thirty and three.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19550653-c251-40c8-aace-c5a96accfd83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: GEN 46:16
Text: And the sons of Gad; Ziphion, and Haggi, Shuni, and Ezbon, Eri, and Arodi, and Areli.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05d0981f-43df-4792-81f8-116e2d5f1bd5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: GEN 46:17
Text: And the sons of Asher; Jimnah, and Ishuah, and Isui, and Beriah, and Serah their sister: and the sons of Beriah; Heber, and Malchiel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb75ac76-dfbc-4916-96bb-64342b76ac59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: GEN 46:18
Text: These are the sons of Zilpah, whom Laban gave to Leah his daughter, and these she bare unto Jacob, even sixteen souls.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3e06008-90fa-47ff-b8d6-88de3161e664>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: GEN 46:19
Text: The sons of Rachel Jacob’s wife; Joseph, and Benjamin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d928e789-400e-4146-b614-59cb6ee863c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: GEN 46:20
Text: And unto Joseph in the land of Egypt were born Manasseh and Ephraim, which Asenath the daughter of Potipherah priest of On bare unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2cfd6c2c-8b82-4dd0-9508-e623215933e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: GEN 46:21
Text: And the sons of Benjamin were Belah, and Becher, and Ashbel, Gera, and Naaman, Ehi, and Rosh, Muppim, and Huppim, and Ard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f095e0e-c4a4-49be-a40a-edd5b6c78189>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: GEN 46:22
Text: These are the sons of Rachel, which were born to Jacob: all the souls were fourteen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8be8590-8d4a-4a31-955f-9d1fa10a329a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 56

Reference: GEN 46:23
Text: And the sons of Dan; Hushim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d4b943c-e854-4b34-8d7c-173cec2f3661>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: GEN 46:24
Text: And the sons of Naphtali; Jahzeel, and Guni, and Jezer, and Shillem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9af5e27a-75b3-42d9-bab1-23e45321b2a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: GEN 46:25
Text: These are the sons of Bilhah, which Laban gave unto Rachel his daughter, and she bare these unto Jacob: all the souls were seven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83c2f277-6d9f-4006-8ba1-b1fdbe9b2a5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: GEN 46:26
Text: All the souls that came with Jacob into Egypt, which came out of his loins, besides Jacob’s sons’ wives, all the souls were threescore and six;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d0112c0-7f0a-438e-b284-26c79061ae8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: GEN 46:27
Text: And the sons of Joseph, which were born him in Egypt, were two souls: all the souls of the house of Jacob, which came into Egypt, were threescore and ten.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40b5ee72-2ff0-4793-afc0-fb07cf007bdc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: GEN 46:28
Text: And he sent Judah before him unto Joseph, to direct his face unto Goshen; and they came into the land of Goshen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2a5db46-99f2-4ede-b275-3d7642176f83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: GEN 46:29
Text: And Joseph made ready his chariot, and went up to meet Israel his father, to Goshen, and presented himself unto him; and he fell on his neck, and wept on his neck a good while.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec16061c-16ad-4b22-a10e-b5025208c329>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: GEN 46:30
Text: And Israel said unto Joseph, Now let me die, since I have seen thy face, because thou art yet alive.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d5e3da1-d850-486f-97d6-e8f86920ad74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: GEN 46:31
Text: And Joseph said unto his brethren, and unto his father’s house, I will go up, and shew Pharaoh, and say unto him, My brethren, and my father’s house, which were in the land of Canaan, are come unto me;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ed87343-b268-4a4d-82e8-d3854411b2d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: GEN 46:32
Text: And the men are shepherds, for their trade hath been to feed cattle; and they have brought their flocks, and their herds, and all that they have.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90be01c6-879c-46e9-99dd-5c6570ad3779>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: GEN 46:33
Text: And it shall come to pass, when Pharaoh shall call you, and shall say, What is your occupation?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/46/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56adc76b-0323-4fda-b982-7ca5b861990b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: GEN 46:34
Text: That ye shall say, Thy servants’ trade hath been about cattle from our youth even until now, both we, and also our fathers: that ye may dwell in the land of Goshen; for every shepherd is an abomination unto the Egyptians.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7197eb5c-649c-40a2-a8bb-9ce439596daf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: GEN 47:1
Text: Then Joseph came and told Pharaoh, and said, My father and my brethren, and their flocks, and their herds, and all that they have, are come out of the land of Canaan; and, behold, they are in the land of Goshen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0744a67-6027-4f96-997d-9470d3a76d96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: GEN 47:2
Text: And he took some of his brethren, even five men, and presented them unto Pharaoh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:834367ce-ada7-4072-b76f-e064395cd7d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: GEN 47:3
Text: And Pharaoh said unto his brethren, What is your occupation? And they said unto Pharaoh, Thy servants are shepherds, both we, and also our fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45085e8f-aa27-4f0a-9338-8b3a3f8ad81b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: GEN 47:4
Text: They said morever unto Pharaoh, For to sojourn in the land are we come; for thy servants have no pasture for their flocks; for the famine is sore in the land of Canaan: now therefore, we pray thee, let thy servants dwell in the land of Goshen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1420c23-d820-4828-98a0-e26d6fcd9692>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: GEN 47:5
Text: And Pharaoh spake unto Joseph, saying, Thy father and thy brethren are come unto thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99f78d0e-3078-48f7-a926-39c8fdc12ea0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: GEN 47:6
Text: The land of Egypt is before thee; in the best of the land make thy father and brethren to dwell; in the land of Goshen let them dwell: and if thou knowest any men of activity among them, then make them rulers over my cattle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c0ea2a2-ae1d-472c-9fbf-d1f844097b17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: GEN 47:7
Text: And Joseph brought in Jacob his father, and set him before Pharaoh: and Jacob blessed Pharaoh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4252110-ec3b-446b-a9c6-cd28c95adf39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: GEN 47:8
Text: And Pharaoh said unto Jacob, How old art thou?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7048ffd4-f339-4579-8576-986027cc547c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 292

Reference: GEN 47:9
Text: And Jacob said unto Pharaoh, The days of the years of my pilgrimage are an hundred and thirty years: few and evil have the days of the years of my life been, and have not attained unto the days of the years of the life of my fathers in the days of their pilgrimage.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1b451d5-8190-4689-b7c8-859c79517271>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: GEN 47:10
Text: And Jacob blessed Pharaoh, and went out from before Pharaoh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff6ce72e-eb86-4083-a77b-5fef3c78e37f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: GEN 47:11
Text: And Joseph placed his father and his brethren, and gave them a possession in the land of Egypt, in the best of the land, in the land of Rameses, as Pharaoh had commanded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:784888e2-b6d9-4e4c-8861-11df840c1dd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: GEN 47:12
Text: And Joseph nourished his father, and his brethren, and all his father’s household, with bread, according to their families.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b65a8e9-add7-4ba5-b63b-45642b88115e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: GEN 47:13
Text: And there was no bread in all the land; for the famine was very sore, so that the land of Egypt and all the land of Canaan fainted by reason of the famine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:764ad90a-832f-4c8b-962b-76f8210177fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: GEN 47:14
Text: And Joseph gathered up all the money that was found in the land of Egypt, and in the land of Canaan, for the corn which they bought: and Joseph brought the money into Pharaoh’s house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd0cc2bc-5263-4889-b415-eedbb1cf498b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: GEN 47:15
Text: And when money failed in the land of Egypt, and in the land of Canaan, all the Egyptians came unto Joseph, and said, Give us bread: for why should we die in thy presence? for the money faileth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c55e3d7-9a18-4737-8d3a-6598f21ca35a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: GEN 47:16
Text: And Joseph said, Give your cattle; and I will give you for your cattle, if money fail.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c40e7d2-636d-4db0-9f50-faddb22b6b33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: GEN 47:17
Text: And they brought their cattle unto Joseph: and Joseph gave them bread in exchange for horses, and for the flocks, and for the cattle of the herds, and for the asses: and he fed them with bread for all their cattle for that year.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4607e572-4ea5-40c1-8004-311a85bcad77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 290

Reference: GEN 47:18
Text: When that year was ended, they came unto him the second year, and said unto him, We will not hide it from my lord, how that our money is spent; my lord also hath our herds of cattle; there is not ought left in the sight of my lord, but our bodies, and our lands:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2948fb15-cd5a-416f-a725-6875397f275c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: GEN 47:19
Text: Wherefore shall we die before thine eyes, both we and our land? buy us and our land for bread, and we and our land will be servants unto Pharaoh: and give us seed, that we may live, and not die, that the land be not desolate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb4358be-55d8-4099-9ecf-442c2de152a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: GEN 47:20
Text: And Joseph bought all the land of Egypt for Pharaoh; for the Egyptians sold every man his field, because the famine prevailed over them: so the land became Pharaoh’s.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30154da3-894a-439e-8ff1-55e2560e7163>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: GEN 47:21
Text: And as for the people, he removed them to cities from one end of the borders of Egypt even to the other end thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39725079-3823-4754-89c0-2ce00ed5724d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: GEN 47:22
Text: Only the land of the priests bought he not; for the priests had a portion assigned them of Pharaoh, and did eat their portion which Pharaoh gave them: wherefore they sold not their lands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff5d1b4d-02d1-4e75-b876-79a36aa9ad1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: GEN 47:23
Text: Then Joseph said unto the people, Behold, I have bought you this day and your land for Pharaoh: lo, here is seed for you, and ye shall sow the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e81b9077-4a7e-4ea0-b3d5-74872e26ba0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 262

Reference: GEN 47:24
Text: And it shall come to pass in the increase, that ye shall give the fifth part unto Pharaoh, and four parts shall be your own, for seed of the field, and for your food, and for them of your households, and for food for your little ones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc4215f7-dcc1-4d51-9f52-d7ce0712750d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: GEN 47:25
Text: And they said, Thou hast saved our lives: let us find grace in the sight of my lord, and we will be Pharaoh’s servants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98d51104-ec64-4dff-ac46-75b407fa2eef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: GEN 47:26
Text: And Joseph made it a law over the land of Egypt unto this day, that Pharaoh should have the fifth part, except the land of the priests only, which became not Pharaoh’s.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4786f06-2f4c-4d36-a165-4b0e9ad3d0e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: GEN 47:27
Text: And Israel dwelt in the land of Egypt, in the country of Goshen; and they had possessions therein, and grew, and multiplied exceedingly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e6cf182-f7e4-4275-8a4e-8ced0312268b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: GEN 47:28
Text: And Jacob lived in the land of Egypt seventeen years: so the whole age of Jacob was an hundred forty and seven years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85dfea59-49f1-4ed5-87c9-45fea173be97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: GEN 47:29
Text: And the time drew nigh that Israel must die: and he called his son Joseph, and said unto him, If now I have found grace in thy sight, put, I pray thee, thy hand under my thigh, and deal kindly and truly with me; bury me not, I pray thee, in Egypt:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:808bf77e-157e-41f8-924d-5385e0b96968>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: GEN 47:30
Text: But I will lie with my fathers, and thou shalt carry me out of Egypt, and bury me in their buryingplace. And he said, I will do as thou hast said.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/47/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa0d513e-9fbd-4a0e-97bf-7612c6bdf069>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: GEN 47:31
Text: And he said, Swear unto me. And he sware unto him. And Israel bowed himself upon the bed’s head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/48/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1313735a-c784-4a83-bc35-f4c2844a0b20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: GEN 48:1
Text: And it came to pass after these things, that one told Joseph, Behold, thy father is sick: and he took with him his two sons, Manasseh and Ephraim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/48/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:637402f2-570c-49a4-90f3-55bd1fcb2f65>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: GEN 48:2
Text: And one told Jacob, and said, Behold, thy son Joseph cometh unto thee: and Israel strengthened himself, and sat upon the bed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/48/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9dbbda7c-55a5-4ce8-bee4-4b66e75c9331>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: GEN 48:3
Text: And Jacob said unto Joseph, God Almighty appeared unto me at Luz in the land of Canaan, and blessed me,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/48/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f91826e-3ab0-4641-8961-cb1c8d6de2c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: GEN 48:4
Text: And said unto me, Behold, I will make thee fruitful, and multiply thee, and I will make of thee a multitude of people; and will give this land to thy seed after thee for an everlasting possession.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/48/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1f7abd9-6f22-4f73-bb4a-f0786a7d3518>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: GEN 48:5
Text: And now thy two sons, Ephraim and Manasseh, which were born unto thee in the land of Egypt before I came unto thee into Egypt, are mine; as Reuben and Simeon, they shall be mine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/48/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fa562c0-0e52-4da8-bd86-448a418f0d0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: GEN 48:6
Text: And thy issue, which thou begettest after them, shall be thine, and shall be called after the name of their brethren in their inheritance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/48/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31ec857d-ca5e-4518-94da-64b3464c8f27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: GEN 48:7
Text: And as for me, when I came from Padan, Rachel died by me in the land of Canaan in the way, when yet there was but a little way to come unto Ephrath: and I buried her there in the way of Ephrath; the same is Bethlehem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/48/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56c28ec5-fbba-47b5-b7cb-28bca3c031b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: GEN 48:8
Text: And Israel beheld Joseph’s sons, and said, Who are these?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/48/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07014ee3-935b-4dd1-9f31-873cde8db659>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: GEN 48:9
Text: And Joseph said unto his father, They are my sons, whom God hath given me in this place. And he said, Bring them, I pray thee, unto me, and I will bless them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/48/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ee35697-7b80-45e6-a678-0cf10ed9ec25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: GEN 48:10
Text: Now the eyes of Israel were dim for age, so that he could not see. And he brought them near unto him; and he kissed them, and embraced them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/48/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54a8b415-813c-4af0-bf45-cae087713ddf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: GEN 48:11
Text: And Israel said unto Joseph, I had not thought to see thy face: and, lo, God hath shewed me also thy seed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/48/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70d213bc-6fb7-42e5-866b-9a02dad1811d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: GEN 48:12
Text: And Joseph brought them out from between his knees, and he bowed himself with his face to the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/48/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10480243-e016-4274-a7ec-ad1f8ff70a94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: GEN 48:13
Text: And Joseph took them both, Ephraim in his right hand toward Israel’s left hand, and Manasseh in his left hand toward Israel’s right hand, and brought them near unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/48/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec4be8cf-d95a-4c71-9519-171c66fc287e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: GEN 48:14
Text: And Israel stretched out his right hand, and laid it upon Ephraim’s head, who was the younger, and his left hand upon Manasseh’s head, guiding his hands wittingly; for Manasseh was the firstborn.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/48/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a209508b-9648-43dc-852c-a2405652c2a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: GEN 48:15
Text: And he blessed Joseph, and said, God, before whom my fathers Abraham and Isaac did walk, the God which fed me all my life long unto this day,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/48/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0fa6abea-ecc2-4f94-9b91-c30e15abaeb1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: GEN 48:16
Text: The Angel which redeemed me from all evil, bless the lads; and let my name be named on them, and the name of my fathers Abraham and Isaac; and let them grow into a multitude in the midst of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/48/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3518f8cd-ff24-4037-bf37-d6a2fb37c6e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: GEN 48:17
Text: And when Joseph saw that his father laid his right hand upon the head of Ephraim, it displeased him: and he held up his father’s hand, to remove it from Ephraim’s head unto Manasseh’s head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/48/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25f9f18b-d703-45ff-9740-690d7d13c0ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: GEN 48:18
Text: And Joseph said unto his father, Not so, my father: for this is the firstborn; put thy right hand upon his head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/48/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20feaec7-e862-4eca-85c3-8a7dedc55b44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: GEN 48:19
Text: And his father refused, and said, I know it, my son, I know it: he also shall become a people, and he also shall be great: but truly his younger brother shall be greater than he, and his seed shall become a multitude of nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/48/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15dd2211-7182-44ca-906a-adedea717c79>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: GEN 48:20
Text: And he blessed them that day, saying, In thee shall Israel bless, saying, God make thee as Ephraim and as Manasseh: and he set Ephraim before Manasseh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/48/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d26af14-2802-43dc-b112-b8653c8a5a7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: GEN 48:21
Text: And Israel said unto Joseph, Behold, I die: but God shall be with you, and bring you again unto the land of your fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/48/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18fb8103-e6a1-43f8-b461-87f9f5ced400>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: GEN 48:22
Text: Moreover I have given to thee one portion above thy brethren, which I took out of the hand of the Amorite with my sword and with my bow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aed99fd7-16fc-46e6-b475-80ea0577d15b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: GEN 49:1
Text: And Jacob called unto his sons, and said, Gather yourselves together, that I may tell you that which shall befall you in the last days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e733e2d2-a7ad-4220-9cfe-c48d78d533ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: GEN 49:2
Text: Gather yourselves together, and hear, ye sons of Jacob; and hearken unto Israel your father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24103485-c5e7-4038-901c-a51b6433c313>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: GEN 49:3
Text: Reuben, thou art my firstborn, my might, and the beginning of my strength, the excellency of dignity, and the excellency of power:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff5f40d4-8650-4d2f-ba82-1b726726c358>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: GEN 49:4
Text: Unstable as water, thou shalt not excel; because thou wentest up to thy father’s bed; then defiledst thou it: he went up to my couch.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dcd42b98-696c-4ac0-ae35-7b6feb5203e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: GEN 49:5
Text: Simeon and Levi are brethren; instruments of cruelty are in their habitations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a6957ee-27b4-4472-aa70-1c8a170844c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: GEN 49:6
Text: O my soul, come not thou into their secret; unto their assembly, mine honour, be not thou united: for in their anger they slew a man, and in their selfwill they digged down a wall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c52237d4-8f8e-44b0-8094-f9af3b0ed258>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: GEN 49:7
Text: Cursed be their anger, for it was fierce; and their wrath, for it was cruel: I will divide them in Jacob, and scatter them in Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a390e1ce-1660-4810-b5c3-cbc35f00ce9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: GEN 49:8
Text: Judah, thou art he whom thy brethren shall praise: thy hand shall be in the neck of thine enemies; thy father’s children shall bow down before thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a07a514-fac2-43e3-b8bf-a9b7be234010>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: GEN 49:9
Text: Judah is a lion’s whelp: from the prey, my son, thou art gone up: he stooped down, he couched as a lion, and as an old lion; who shall rouse him up?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f83acf5b-3b91-4e9c-a96c-1168e0c618fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: GEN 49:10
Text: The sceptre shall not depart from Judah, nor a lawgiver from between his feet, until Shiloh come; and unto him shall the gathering of the people be.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70f558e9-9db7-449e-acb5-4974c98088ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: GEN 49:11
Text: Binding his foal unto the vine, and his ass’s colt unto the choice vine; he washed his garments in wine, and his clothes in the blood of grapes:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ae98b44-b2b3-408d-acd9-d7b302fad314>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: GEN 49:12
Text: His eyes shall be red with wine, and his teeth white with milk.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:766c62f6-506d-4df3-9753-80d1020abb13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: GEN 49:13
Text: Zebulun shall dwell at the haven of the sea; and he shall be for an haven of ships; and his border shall be unto Zidon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2814d69-7399-49aa-b3da-c465f88756f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: GEN 49:14
Text: Issachar is a strong ass couching down between two burdens:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:368576cb-826c-4081-9d8d-ca71034aa454>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: GEN 49:15
Text: And he saw that rest was good, and the land that it was pleasant; and bowed his shoulder to bear, and became a servant unto tribute.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3196e1d3-c84d-47b9-ba81-07afdfaeba5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: GEN 49:16
Text: Dan shall judge his people, as one of the tribes of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3dd1c645-885f-4819-969e-75f20d118479>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: GEN 49:17
Text: Dan shall be a serpent by the way, an adder in the path, that biteth the horse heels, so that his rider shall fall backward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:465d8ab9-3f2d-4221-ab7c-41c4d1140330>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 68

Reference: GEN 49:18
Text: I have waited for thy salvation, O LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10e16202-73ea-4c04-8ba8-4dc38901cc59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: GEN 49:19
Text: Gad, a troop shall overcome him: but he shall overcome at the last.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d33903d-3536-417f-bbe2-265ddbb7db7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: GEN 49:20
Text: Out of Asher his bread shall be fat, and he shall yield royal dainties.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edf4725e-f30d-4c0d-8720-8fb6f19fcc4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: GEN 49:21
Text: Naphtali is a hind let loose: he giveth goodly words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20761504-09f1-4156-abb7-4c5b7f552575>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: GEN 49:22
Text: Joseph is a fruitful bough, even a fruitful bough by a well; whose branches run over the wall:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47488a20-3925-41ed-89f4-3e862168c8e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: GEN 49:23
Text: The archers have sorely grieved him, and shot at him, and hated him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46a15a54-ad86-4e57-ae78-fa44531ef00d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: GEN 49:24
Text: But his bow abode in strength, and the arms of his hands were made strong by the hands of the mighty God of Jacob; (from thence is the shepherd, the stone of Israel:)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69c63040-8b58-4d43-b5a8-cf693e9f63e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: GEN 49:25
Text: Even by the God of thy father, who shall help thee; and by the Almighty, who shall bless thee with blessings of heaven above, blessings of the deep that lieth under, blessings of the breasts, and of the womb:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d12ce0a-8dc1-47a2-b3dc-797bb8424296>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 266

Reference: GEN 49:26
Text: The blessings of thy father have prevailed above the blessings of my progenitors unto the utmost bound of the everlasting hills: they shall be on the head of Joseph, and on the crown of the head of him that was separate from his brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0207aef-1cea-47fc-9e24-99be264b0ffa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: GEN 49:27
Text: Benjamin shall ravin as a wolf: in the morning he shall devour the prey, and at night he shall divide the spoil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5408c85f-54cf-45f0-9c08-a28bb4a9e3d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: GEN 49:28
Text: All these are the twelve tribes of Israel: and this is it that their father spake unto them, and blessed them; every one according to his blessing he blessed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ccedd8f-d4fa-47f7-bd7d-eabbdd32b864>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: GEN 49:29
Text: And he charged them, and said unto them, I am to be gathered unto my people: bury me with my fathers in the cave that is in the field of Ephron the Hittite,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46e4e408-ae79-4dfa-957a-d4286e4576a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: GEN 49:30
Text: In the cave that is in the field of Machpelah, which is before Mamre, in the land of Canaan, which Abraham bought with the field of Ephron the Hittite for a possession of a buryingplace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:436b681b-1209-40d7-a6b3-03f34d0e1c76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: GEN 49:31
Text: There they buried Abraham and Sarah his wife; there they buried Isaac and Rebekah his wife; and there I buried Leah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8b1eae8-8167-4cde-a864-d36407e3d504>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: GEN 49:32
Text: The purchase of the field and of the cave that is therein was from the children of Heth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/49/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97a1852a-1141-49f6-8476-ecd03cbb74f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: GEN 49:33
Text: And when Jacob had made an end of commanding his sons, he gathered up his feet into the bed, and yielded up the ghost, and was gathered unto his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df05a05e-9832-4c75-8367-a1fd6a0454f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: GEN 50:1
Text: And Joseph fell upon his father’s face, and wept upon him, and kissed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ecf042e-ed51-4f81-88e6-34b255591674>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: GEN 50:2
Text: And Joseph commanded his servants the physicians to embalm his father: and the physicians embalmed Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cec27486-f092-468b-9dfd-b6ed9c72afc8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: GEN 50:3
Text: And forty days were fulfilled for him; for so are fulfilled the days of those which are embalmed: and the Egyptians mourned for him threescore and ten days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d08a34f8-8f70-409c-b670-0b6878b967ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: GEN 50:4
Text: And when the days of his mourning were past, Joseph spake unto the house of Pharaoh, saying, If now I have found grace in your eyes, speak, I pray you, in the ears of Pharaoh, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fbaea52-52a1-4491-a825-11d6754be4c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: GEN 50:5
Text: My father made me swear, saying, Lo, I die: in my grave which I have digged for me in the land of Canaan, there shalt thou bury me. Now therefore let me go up, I pray thee, and bury my father, and I will come again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8382ced-6bb0-49d1-a43c-40c7485c09be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: GEN 50:6
Text: And Pharaoh said, Go up, and bury thy father, according as he made thee swear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26dd410c-7b41-48b2-8cd5-0f7ccfdd1fba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: GEN 50:7
Text: And Joseph went up to bury his father: and with him went up all the servants of Pharaoh, the elders of his house, and all the elders of the land of Egypt,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b075c020-eae7-4bb6-a868-191df0d464e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: GEN 50:8
Text: And all the house of Joseph, and his brethren, and his father’s house: only their little ones, and their flocks, and their herds, they left in the land of Goshen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ed7eaf3-3bc2-4878-9c77-24d3285d3fc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: GEN 50:9
Text: And there went up with him both chariots and horsemen: and it was a very great company.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33c89c15-08d1-49bd-adce-815a6e2de002>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: GEN 50:10
Text: And they came to the threshingfloor of Atad, which is beyond Jordan, and there they mourned with a great and very sore lamentation: and he made a mourning for his father seven days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f43d5d7-5589-449e-9392-a15b4910271c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: GEN 50:11
Text: And when the inhabitants of the land, the Canaanites, saw the mourning in the floor of Atad, they said, This is a grievous mourning to the Egyptians: wherefore the name of it was called Abelmizraim, which is beyond Jordan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55b6b0aa-185a-4f00-b91b-40aef6a36978>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: GEN 50:12
Text: And his sons did unto him according as he commanded them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b2e90ee-681c-49a3-8ace-7b628218f134>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: GEN 50:13
Text: For his sons carried him into the land of Canaan, and buried him in the cave of the field of Machpelah, which Abraham bought with the field for a possession of a buryingplace of Ephron the Hittite, before Mamre.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:434042bd-4b63-4b11-bf46-531187f8de11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: GEN 50:14
Text: And Joseph returned into Egypt, he, and his brethren, and all that went up with him to bury his father, after he had buried his father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4b9ed73-382d-44a2-9890-16fecfb92fcd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: GEN 50:15
Text: And when Joseph’s brethren saw that their father was dead, they said, Joseph will peradventure hate us, and will certainly requite us all the evil which we did unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de81aa55-b729-4315-a94f-cc73bf21bc2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: GEN 50:16
Text: And they sent a messenger unto Joseph, saying, Thy father did command before he died, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7fe5439-d9cd-43c3-839d-5e1869a3593a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: GEN 50:17
Text: So shall ye say unto Joseph, Forgive, I pray thee now, the trespass of thy brethren, and their sin; for they did unto thee evil: and now, we pray thee, forgive the trespass of the servants of the God of thy father. And Joseph wept when they spake unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a10ab41-bb97-4db4-8dcd-b029f072bb3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: GEN 50:18
Text: And his brethren also went and fell down before his face; and they said, Behold, we be thy servants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef635b15-9d40-4de7-b0cd-aa751f5f152f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: GEN 50:19
Text: And Joseph said unto them, Fear not: for am I in the place of God?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22e6a3f2-c11d-4ec3-9e18-8ecfe4cc5a2f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: GEN 50:20
Text: But as for you, ye thought evil against me; but God meant it unto good, to bring to pass, as it is this day, to save much people alive.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef596f6d-f09a-40cd-9107-dfb4cdac70f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: GEN 50:21
Text: Now therefore fear ye not: I will nourish you, and your little ones. And he comforted them, and spake kindly unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06a185bf-cf78-444c-8808-5892b4f41649>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: GEN 50:22
Text: And Joseph dwelt in Egypt, he, and his father’s house: and Joseph lived an hundred and ten years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7da8ca98-646f-43fb-a34b-a40d657e7cc8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: GEN 50:23
Text: And Joseph saw Ephraim’s children of the third generation: the children also of Machir the son of Manasseh were brought up upon Joseph’s knees.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cedef2b0-e3f1-4cf0-9193-1133fd07073e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: GEN 50:24
Text: And Joseph said unto his brethren, I die: and God will surely visit you, and bring you out of this land unto the land which he sware to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4058f319-ac41-42ea-9faf-c762615c5d17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: GEN 50:25
Text: And Joseph took an oath of the children of Israel, saying, God will surely visit you, and ye shall carry up my bones from hence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/GEN/50/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60d70618-bb01-4113-abee-cc776eff866f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: GEN 50:26
Text: So Joseph died, being an hundred and ten years old: and they embalmed him, and he was put in a coffin in Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:632e3c4e-fb21-44cd-9cde-7a0ce3021e44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: EXO 1:1
Text: Now these are the names of the children of Israel, which came into Egypt; every man and his household came with Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:957b29fb-3303-4165-ad58-5a543b8a37fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 58

Reference: EXO 1:2
Text: Reuben, Simeon, Levi, and Judah,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43a55775-f245-4daa-b342-7c3912900156>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 58

Reference: EXO 1:3
Text: Issachar, Zebulun, and Benjamin,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e2a90f6-e8b0-44c7-a75c-d8a2d6a6f6f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 60

Reference: EXO 1:4
Text: Dan, and Naphtali, Gad, and Asher.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:535f9bd7-9523-4048-bf3f-4780c658f608>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: EXO 1:5
Text: And all the souls that came out of the loins of Jacob were seventy souls: for Joseph was in Egypt already.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a27d4328-15f9-48d6-93bb-1f8de4a078a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: EXO 1:6
Text: And Joseph died, and all his brethren, and all that generation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:827b59fd-c681-49f4-9212-bc213851f02d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: EXO 1:7
Text: And the children of Israel were fruitful, and increased abundantly, and multiplied, and waxed exceeding mighty; and the land was filled with them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b88f889-1c23-4fe6-931a-78502b285d14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: EXO 1:8
Text: Now there arose up a new king over Egypt, which knew not Joseph.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da3f982a-4d01-4ad3-9988-fdc365ef46a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: EXO 1:9
Text: And he said unto his people, Behold, the people of the children of Israel are more and mightier than we:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3d48f41-e77e-453b-b93c-5b31513a4413>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: EXO 1:10
Text: Come on, let us deal wisely with them; lest they multiply, and it come to pass, that, when there falleth out any war, they join also unto our enemies, and fight against us, and so get them up out of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0afeecb3-87d2-4071-b1e0-b6610c56e33d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: EXO 1:11
Text: Therefore they did set over them taskmasters to afflict them with their burdens. And they built for Pharaoh treasure cities, Pithom and Raamses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7088ec77-c710-4ef4-8047-daff5106fafd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: EXO 1:12
Text: But the more they afflicted them, the more they multiplied and grew. And they were grieved because of the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53a12527-b115-48c4-b354-1db6da430132>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: EXO 1:13
Text: And the Egyptians made the children of Israel to serve with rigour:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb13abce-5433-4977-be1a-d2f958e2205a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: EXO 1:14
Text: And they made their lives bitter with hard bondage, in morter, and in brick, and in all manner of service in the field: all their service, wherein they made them serve, was with rigour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cace8453-985f-4b82-bc29-754edd558a78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: EXO 1:15
Text: And the king of Egypt spake to the Hebrew midwives, of which the name of the one was Shiphrah, and the name of the other Puah:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b71db2d3-4d92-4dd6-ae32-c7a788772ae1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: EXO 1:16
Text: And he said, When ye do the office of a midwife to the Hebrew women, and see them upon the stools; if it be a son, then ye shall kill him: but if it be a daughter, then she shall live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6020592-0df2-4d4b-80f5-6cf2e377d840>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: EXO 1:17
Text: But the midwives feared God, and did not as the king of Egypt commanded them, but saved the men children alive.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81b6857e-b086-45c5-b471-f1a92028843d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: EXO 1:18
Text: And the king of Egypt called for the midwives, and said unto them, Why have ye done this thing, and have saved the men children alive?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3059110-7cb4-4576-9d6a-9e8d04411086>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: EXO 1:19
Text: And the midwives said unto Pharaoh, Because the Hebrew women are not as the Egyptian women; for they are lively, and are delivered ere the midwives come in unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ddf6c5b-9dd5-4a1a-8dc0-d3418abf52ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: EXO 1:20
Text: Therefore God dealt well with the midwives: and the people multiplied, and waxed very mighty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/1/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35b616ae-113c-4f27-a4bd-fa3ac4e23087>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: EXO 1:21
Text: And it came to pass, because the midwives feared God, that he made them houses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/1/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:406faef2-85b9-40f7-8416-2b3ebbd8340c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: EXO 1:22
Text: And Pharaoh charged all his people, saying, Every son that is born ye shall cast into the river, and every daughter ye shall save alive.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e5e290b-0e61-47fb-809b-0748eac76551>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: EXO 2:1
Text: And there went a man of the house of Levi, and took to wife a daughter of Levi.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cbf0310-3d41-4df1-b376-6bbcf197ea68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: EXO 2:2
Text: And the woman conceived, and bare a son: and when she saw him that he was a goodly child, she hid him three months.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:821b0d7e-91f4-47aa-b9a2-d19b715d1168>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: EXO 2:3
Text: And when she could not longer hide him, she took for him an ark of bulrushes, and daubed it with slime and with pitch, and put the child therein; and she laid it in the flags by the river’s brink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f4a1911-5e60-4b5c-b488-79a73f3862a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: EXO 2:4
Text: And his sister stood afar off, to wit what would be done to him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cdbb17ac-cd41-4b14-a38c-524350bc1eff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: EXO 2:5
Text: And the daughter of Pharaoh came down to wash herself at the river; and her maidens walked along by the river’s side; and when she saw the ark among the flags, she sent her maid to fetch it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5dd5a066-7b2c-47d4-bafd-7e04816ff007>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: EXO 2:6
Text: And when she had opened it, she saw the child: and, behold, the babe wept. And she had compassion on him, and said, This is one of the Hebrews’ children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:649ea46e-b3a7-45ef-8f02-177c3de90b5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: EXO 2:7
Text: Then said his sister to Pharaoh’s daughter, Shall I go and call to thee a nurse of the Hebrew women, that she may nurse the child for thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e8c217d-85c1-45b8-ae76-6c8b5e705995>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: EXO 2:8
Text: And Pharaoh’s daughter said to her, Go. And the maid went and called the child’s mother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a6a8233-b728-4e8a-816d-481de46765c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: EXO 2:9
Text: And Pharaoh’s daughter said unto her, Take this child away, and nurse it for me, and I will give thee thy wages. And the woman took the child, and nursed it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17aa7fbd-9cb0-4fbe-a484-eb9b6ffe7a4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: EXO 2:10
Text: And the child grew, and she brought him unto Pharaoh’s daughter, and he became her son. And she called his name Moses: and she said, Because I drew him out of the water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa7795ba-1341-47d1-b03c-79d61fb9073b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: EXO 2:11
Text: And it came to pass in those days, when Moses was grown, that he went out unto his brethren, and looked on their burdens: and he spied an Egyptian smiting an Hebrew, one of his brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a417d86-6346-49f1-b65a-2dd640feb047>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: EXO 2:12
Text: And he looked this way and that way, and when he saw that there was no man, he slew the Egyptian, and hid him in the sand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8112d698-0908-439c-97ae-ca080d75dc2d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: EXO 2:13
Text: And when he went out the second day, behold, two men of the Hebrews strove together: and he said to him that did the wrong, Wherefore smitest thou thy fellow?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f42af67-d1fb-4ee2-baa9-8b33a621127f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: EXO 2:14
Text: And he said, Who made thee a prince and a judge over us? intendest thou to kill me, as thou killedst the Egyptian? And Moses feared, and said, Surely this thing is known.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f6afb0a-9d59-407a-b249-7d6e7b4a8609>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: EXO 2:15
Text: Now when Pharaoh heard this thing, he sought to slay Moses. But Moses fled from the face of Pharaoh, and dwelt in the land of Midian: and he sat down by a well.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e06d50c-896c-4ac1-96ba-15508d81224c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EXO 2:16
Text: Now the priest of Midian had seven daughters: and they came and drew water, and filled the troughs to water their father’s flock.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67f6e0f3-9497-491f-b76f-f782e1a27edc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: EXO 2:17
Text: And the shepherds came and drove them away: but Moses stood up and helped them, and watered their flock.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf122636-ac2a-4051-ae05-f7be35b26a55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: EXO 2:18
Text: And when they came to Reuel their father, he said, How is it that ye are come so soon to day?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e349e14-09ca-4112-9417-3a09ff00b807>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EXO 2:19
Text: And they said, An Egyptian delivered us out of the hand of the shepherds, and also drew water enough for us, and watered the flock.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54cc107c-3afe-4510-b90e-c2638ae51da4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: EXO 2:20
Text: And he said unto his daughters, And where is he? why is it that ye have left the man? call him, that he may eat bread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:145b00f9-ccda-42d6-bdd7-1ee65b84b162>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: EXO 2:21
Text: And Moses was content to dwell with the man: and he gave Moses Zipporah his daughter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0eb50c49-cd6e-456b-96e7-3dd6a5cec3ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: EXO 2:22
Text: And she bare him a son, and he called his name Gershom: for he said, I have been a stranger in a strange land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7bbbf16c-e037-49f7-9b23-19488b5e73d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: EXO 2:23
Text: And it came to pass in process of time, that the king of Egypt died: and the children of Israel sighed by reason of the bondage, and they cried, and their cry came up unto God by reason of the bondage.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad4cc9af-2644-4006-b91d-77bc4c91a652>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: EXO 2:24
Text: And God heard their groaning, and God remembered his covenant with Abraham, with Isaac, and with Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/2/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41109d03-d22b-4714-a48a-8ebbc33641dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: EXO 2:25
Text: And God looked upon the children of Israel, and God had respect unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73571337-a85e-432a-ba0f-d35933775dba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: EXO 3:1
Text: Now Moses kept the flock of Jethro his father in law, the priest of Midian: and he led the flock to the backside of the desert, and came to the mountain of God, even to Horeb.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2851955-a62a-431a-9d7b-da63b939d45a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: EXO 3:2
Text: And the angel of the LORD appeared unto him in a flame of fire out of the midst of a bush: and he looked, and, behold, the bush burned with fire, and the bush was not consumed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2ecaa8b-1a4d-4237-bb68-8944c6eb312e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: EXO 3:3
Text: And Moses said, I will now turn aside, and see this great sight, why the bush is not burnt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d48832b-b280-4ffe-9332-92266992e444>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: EXO 3:4
Text: And when the LORD saw that he turned aside to see, God called unto him out of the midst of the bush, and said, Moses, Moses. And he said, Here am I.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9609f002-74f0-486a-8262-3cc6e768db80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: EXO 3:5
Text: And he said, Draw not nigh hither: put off thy shoes from off thy feet, for the place whereon thou standest is holy ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00e8f289-5b21-4bae-8569-6be7ad487576>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: EXO 3:6
Text: Moreover he said, I am the God of thy father, the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob. And Moses hid his face; for he was afraid to look upon God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15e15a25-a895-4281-9bb1-eeded084b829>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: EXO 3:7
Text: And the LORD said, I have surely seen the affliction of my people which are in Egypt, and have heard their cry by reason of their taskmasters; for I know their sorrows;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:013ac2e3-a1b9-49f3-af86-67b036666272>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 329

Reference: EXO 3:8
Text: And I am come down to deliver them out of the hand of the Egyptians, and to bring them up out of that land unto a good land and a large, unto a land flowing with milk and honey; unto the place of the Canaanites, and the Hittites, and the Amorites, and the Perizzites, and the Hivites, and the Jebusites.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62e3a6c5-83f3-467b-9a7e-4b8ab9068cd3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: EXO 3:9
Text: Now therefore, behold, the cry of the children of Israel is come unto me: and I have also seen the oppression wherewith the Egyptians oppress them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f57aa57-422d-43af-b89e-08abd22bebd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EXO 3:10
Text: Come now therefore, and I will send thee unto Pharaoh, that thou mayest bring forth my people the children of Israel out of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b24ff548-3807-4eb4-9396-32f0180042c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: EXO 3:11
Text: And Moses said unto God, Who am I, that I should go unto Pharaoh, and that I should bring forth the children of Israel out of Egypt?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c60fcf97-0b9f-4dd3-9e98-00faf2bb48df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: EXO 3:12
Text: And he said, Certainly I will be with thee; and this shall be a token unto thee, that I have sent thee: When thou hast brought forth the people out of Egypt, ye shall serve God upon this mountain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfb62e65-4c50-411c-ae16-feab0ddd6c9f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: EXO 3:13
Text: And Moses said unto God, Behold, when I come unto the children of Israel, and shall say unto them, The God of your fathers hath sent me unto you; and they shall say to me, What is his name? what shall I say unto them?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:adea5615-819c-40df-9770-ab18d3838bae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EXO 3:14
Text: And God said unto Moses, I AM THAT I AM: and he said, Thus shalt thou say unto the children of Israel, I AM hath sent me unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af16ab09-bc0e-42d1-88c3-3b3f62c90cf4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 294

Reference: EXO 3:15
Text: And God said moreover unto Moses, Thus shalt thou say unto the children of Israel, the LORD God of your fathers, the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob, hath sent me unto you: this is my name for ever, and this is my memorial unto all generations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:684b5d04-3d53-4f75-b9b7-0f16feb4ba6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: EXO 3:16
Text: Go, and gather the elders of Israel together, and say unto them, The LORD God of your fathers, the God of Abraham, of Isaac, and of Jacob, appeared unto me, saying, I have surely visited you, and seen that which is done to you in Egypt:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a8aa788-8426-4b24-b0a4-880b18d62bd4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: EXO 3:17
Text: And I have said, I will bring you up out of the affliction of Egypt unto the land of the Canaanites, and the Hittites, and the Amorites, and the Perizzites, and the Hivites, and the Jebusites, unto a land flowing with milk and honey.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:441000fc-a961-4e14-8b03-5c89dc8145c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 334

Reference: EXO 3:18
Text: And they shall hearken to thy voice: and thou shalt come, thou and the elders of Israel, unto the king of Egypt, and ye shall say unto him, The LORD God of the Hebrews hath met with us: and now let us go, we beseech thee, three days’ journey into the wilderness, that we may sacrifice to the LORD our God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93230807-e247-4440-a80c-fbcf5a7b56a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: EXO 3:19
Text: And I am sure that the king of Egypt will not let you go, no, not by a mighty hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/3/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b279c582-0e0f-48ac-b57c-d86f5277a866>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: EXO 3:20
Text: And I will stretch out my hand, and smite Egypt with all my wonders which I will do in the midst thereof: and after that he will let you go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/3/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc7858a1-b127-4e6e-8961-b814c247875a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EXO 3:21
Text: And I will give this people favour in the sight of the Egyptians: and it shall come to pass, that, when ye go, ye shall not go empty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/3/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebaf69e8-4ebf-4a6f-80bd-a5fe7d237477>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 262

Reference: EXO 3:22
Text: But every woman shall borrow of her neighbour, and of her that sojourneth in her house, jewels of silver, and jewels of gold, and raiment: and ye shall put them upon your sons, and upon your daughters; and ye shall spoil the Egyptians.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ace860fb-7061-4bb0-ac2e-85e151c8d70c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: EXO 4:1
Text: And Moses answered and said, But, behold, they will not believe me, nor hearken unto my voice: for they will say, The LORD hath not appeared unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a9919d0-516c-4b95-b2e9-119ac601182b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: EXO 4:2
Text: And the LORD said unto him, What is that in thine hand? And he said, A rod.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:234b38c7-9e75-43b4-92e6-1c219e160949>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: EXO 4:3
Text: And he said, Cast it on the ground. And he cast it on the ground, and it became a serpent; and Moses fled from before it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08a7e140-37c8-47ff-b836-788ae504ad8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: EXO 4:4
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Put forth thine hand, and take it by the tail. And he put forth his hand, and caught it, and it became a rod in his hand:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38e6e973-0099-4e3b-8a69-90f82419425d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: EXO 4:5
Text: That they may believe that the LORD God of their fathers, the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob, hath appeared unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa325a1e-b0f3-4ddd-9b1f-ac0dec343f83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: EXO 4:6
Text: And the LORD said furthermore unto him, Put now thine hand into thy bosom. And he put his hand into his bosom: and when he took it out, behold, his hand was leprous as snow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:086e2ec5-b3a8-4764-96a2-5acad395fcc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: EXO 4:7
Text: And he said, Put thine hand into thy bosom again. And he put his hand into his bosom again; and plucked it out of his bosom, and, behold, it was turned again as his other flesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ac22e0a-bac9-43f9-8056-8384c31253ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: EXO 4:8
Text: And it shall come to pass, if they will not believe thee, neither hearken to the voice of the first sign, that they will believe the voice of the latter sign.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb88247a-29d3-4548-a50e-495bfe7c8b74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 297

Reference: EXO 4:9
Text: And it shall come to pass, if they will not believe also these two signs, neither hearken unto thy voice, that thou shalt take of the water of the river, and pour it upon the dry land: and the water which thou takest out of the river shall become blood upon the dry land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83928929-d4f8-49ca-a43f-1972c28d3f13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: EXO 4:10
Text: And Moses said unto the LORD, O my LORD, I am not eloquent, neither heretofore, nor since thou hast spoken unto thy servant: but I am slow of speech, and of a slow tongue.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15289b20-3e91-40b0-a8b5-09b3f745c885>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: EXO 4:11
Text: And the LORD said unto him, Who hath made man’s mouth? or who maketh the dumb, or deaf, or the seeing, or the blind? have not I the LORD?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26f14053-bd99-4b22-a76b-a5614ce6ed3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: EXO 4:12
Text: Now therefore go, and I will be with thy mouth, and teach thee what thou shalt say.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a4b6ce7-703f-4074-85d9-a10bf17af785>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: EXO 4:13
Text: And he said, O my LORD, send, I pray thee, by the hand of him whom thou wilt send.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bda514f7-d091-49f6-93d5-03379a1b7e06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 262

Reference: EXO 4:14
Text: And the anger of the LORD was kindled against Moses, and he said, Is not Aaron the Levite thy brother? I know that he can speak well. And also, behold, he cometh forth to meet thee: and when he seeth thee, he will be glad in his heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6553732-de6c-463e-9514-6de7bb9a4529>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: EXO 4:15
Text: And thou shalt speak unto him, and put words in his mouth: and I will be with thy mouth, and with his mouth, and will teach you what ye shall do.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f285bfa5-ffb4-4551-ab36-a5384b9a0008>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: EXO 4:16
Text: And he shall be thy spokesman unto the people: and he shall be, even he shall be to thee instead of a mouth, and thou shalt be to him instead of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04340e37-423d-4456-9935-470d3854e69d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: EXO 4:17
Text: And thou shalt take this rod in thine hand, wherewith thou shalt do signs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57d3cbe2-9c32-48b4-b71b-b78121e4638d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: EXO 4:18
Text: And Moses went and returned to Jethro his father in law, and said unto him, Let me go, I pray thee, and return unto my brethren which are in Egypt, and see whether they be yet alive. And Jethro said to Moses, Go in peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7933dcd-184b-4aa1-a084-d87a57a9bea0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: EXO 4:19
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses in Midian, Go, return into Egypt: for all the men are dead which sought thy life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d16a85e9-9d55-4c8a-acf8-e1035c536806>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: EXO 4:20
Text: And Moses took his wife and his sons, and set them upon an ass, and he returned to the land of Egypt: and Moses took the rod of God in his hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f7fdcf4-4bc4-4258-9edb-d95f1fb45930>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: EXO 4:21
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, When thou goest to return into Egypt, see that thou do all those wonders before Pharaoh, which I have put in thine hand: but I will harden his heart, that he shall not let the people go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d67ac8a1-7394-4ec2-8411-043f0ea61efe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: EXO 4:22
Text: And thou shalt say unto Pharaoh, Thus saith the LORD, Israel is my son, even my firstborn:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9f971af-d473-4cb1-898f-d24801aad0a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: EXO 4:23
Text: And I say unto thee, Let my son go, that he may serve me: and if thou refuse to let him go, behold, I will slay thy son, even thy firstborn.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7135b08-f6fc-4b21-bc7d-92d9507fd422>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: EXO 4:24
Text: And it came to pass by the way in the inn, that the LORD met him, and sought to kill him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c6821a1-f177-450f-9171-d97b3ae2444f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: EXO 4:25
Text: Then Zipporah took a sharp stone, and cut off the foreskin of her son, and cast it at his feet, and said, Surely a bloody husband art thou to me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7bfea82c-9c82-4231-97c1-890b3803db2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: EXO 4:26
Text: So he let him go: then she said, A bloody husband thou art, because of the circumcision.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e588788e-1c68-42df-b3f2-719fd7bd4b67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: EXO 4:27
Text: And the LORD said to Aaron, Go into the wilderness to meet Moses. And he went, and met him in the mount of God, and kissed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8de9da39-f27e-4495-966f-4a3a383c98c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: EXO 4:28
Text: And Moses told Aaron all the words of the LORD who had sent him, and all the signs which he had commanded him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce1568f7-0f65-4500-b121-4fd3b16b83d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: EXO 4:29
Text: And Moses and Aaron went and gathered together all the elders of the children of Israel:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9864ffd7-4076-453c-a876-6517fbc2ecbd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: EXO 4:30
Text: And Aaron spake all the words which the LORD had spoken unto Moses, and did the signs in the sight of the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/4/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf592061-e76c-4951-91d2-86334d8a521d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: EXO 4:31
Text: And the people believed: and when they heard that the LORD had visited the children of Israel, and that he had looked upon their affliction, then they bowed their heads and worshipped.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59a61184-2a4d-4e30-a835-286af46d59b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: EXO 5:1
Text: And afterward Moses and Aaron went in, and told Pharaoh, Thus saith the LORD God of Israel, Let my people go, that they may hold a feast unto me in the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a409800-c165-4900-9576-3bdd9a47f469>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EXO 5:2
Text: And Pharaoh said, Who is the LORD, that I should obey his voice to let Israel go? I know not the LORD, neither will I let Israel go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aff52ef9-9155-47e9-93b2-5a25cc4bac5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: EXO 5:3
Text: And they said, The God of the Hebrews hath met with us: let us go, we pray thee, three days’ journey into the desert, and sacrifice unto the LORD our God; lest he fall upon us with pestilence, or with the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80ff2a14-c7c9-4991-9c45-31a9f171b1ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EXO 5:4
Text: And the king of Egypt said unto them, Wherefore do ye, Moses and Aaron, let the people from their works? get you unto your burdens.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d8dd804-ace9-4c2d-bd5e-6ac8e40e5f41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: EXO 5:5
Text: And Pharaoh said, Behold, the people of the land now are many, and ye make them rest from their burdens.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f283a96-3221-45b7-97b4-dee5d96466e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: EXO 5:6
Text: And Pharaoh commanded the same day the taskmasters of the people, and their officers, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3528859b-74ff-4cc2-9455-552e852e41ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: EXO 5:7
Text: Ye shall no more give the people straw to make brick, as heretofore: let them go and gather straw for themselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14d32ea4-940f-488e-938c-27fb7c321762>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: EXO 5:8
Text: And the tale of the bricks, which they did make heretofore, ye shall lay upon them; ye shall not diminish ought thereof: for they be idle; therefore they cry, saying, Let us go and sacrifice to our God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c7502e1-9829-42d2-a096-c82c1dcfd3b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: EXO 5:9
Text: Let there more work be laid upon the men, that they may labour therein; and let them not regard vain words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:daad0aa6-1b69-47dd-8a23-fcb47ee84981>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: EXO 5:10
Text: And the taskmasters of the people went out, and their officers, and they spake to the people, saying, Thus saith Pharaoh, I will not give you straw.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74f3bc47-87a8-4e2c-8782-d4ab5ddde47f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: EXO 5:11
Text: Go ye, get you straw where ye can find it: yet not ought of your work shall be diminished.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23974a1e-ed84-43ab-916c-048122337d4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: EXO 5:12
Text: So the people were scattered abroad throughout all the land of Egypt to gather stubble instead of straw.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ce25776-b835-459b-aa15-b3cbb013cd3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: EXO 5:13
Text: And the taskmasters hasted them, saying, Fulfil your works, your daily tasks, as when there was straw.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fccfe351-1cb1-407d-a922-75c8b7685bd3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: EXO 5:14
Text: And the officers of the children of Israel, which Pharaoh’s taskmasters had set over them, were beaten, and demanded, Wherefore have ye not fulfilled your task in making brick both yesterday and to day, as heretofore?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8bc7c740-6cc2-4758-8375-b9000695f07e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: EXO 5:15
Text: Then the officers of the children of Israel came and cried unto Pharaoh, saying, Wherefore dealest thou thus with thy servants?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:187c7d5b-e661-4d32-8794-11e9d5c45c2d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: EXO 5:16
Text: There is no straw given unto thy servants, and they say to us, Make brick: and, behold, thy servants are beaten; but the fault is in thine own people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/5/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9c67e57-f37c-40a4-abb8-1964cc360c14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: EXO 5:17
Text: But he said, Ye are idle, ye are idle: therefore ye say, Let us go and do sacrifice to the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/5/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11bc7c0c-715f-47a0-a0d4-fb93734de6d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: EXO 5:18
Text: Go therefore now, and work; for there shall no straw be given you, yet shall ye deliver the tale of bricks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/5/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8bf72290-3ca2-44a9-b135-f47b889933d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: EXO 5:19
Text: And the officers of the children of Israel did see that they were in evil case, after it was said, Ye shall not minish ought from your bricks of your daily task.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/5/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4e62f78-ced9-47b7-ab4c-237b59b5e1fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: EXO 5:20
Text: And they met Moses and Aaron, who stood in the way, as they came forth from Pharaoh:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/5/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c06be86-a024-4ac6-bd17-1b7538dcf909>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: EXO 5:21
Text: And they said unto them, The LORD look upon you, and judge; because ye have made our savour to be abhorred in the eyes of Pharaoh, and in the eyes of his servants, to put a sword in their hand to slay us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/5/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be491f56-4201-4f8c-8af0-80a594cf74be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: EXO 5:22
Text: And Moses returned unto the LORD, and said, LORD, wherefore hast thou so evil entreated this people? why is it that thou hast sent me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/5/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0438a444-1c58-4f97-a605-b3be8eb0021c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EXO 5:23
Text: For since I came to Pharaoh to speak in thy name, he hath done evil to this people; neither hast thou delivered thy people at all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7637ecc0-ffb5-4444-88fd-f02f1bfe7b9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: EXO 6:1
Text: Then the LORD said unto Moses, Now shalt thou see what I will do to Pharaoh: for with a strong hand shall he let them go, and with a strong hand shall he drive them out of his land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ab5d5dc-edec-4d81-b29c-02d203ef808d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: EXO 6:2
Text: And God spake unto Moses, and said unto him, I am the LORD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc986267-f912-4ade-b283-952dc5ae0b5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: EXO 6:3
Text: And I appeared unto Abraham, unto Isaac, and unto Jacob, by the name of God Almighty, but by my name JEHOVAH was I not known to them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a6b0ad0-8dd9-427a-b901-9eb8aece68ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: EXO 6:4
Text: And I have also established my covenant with them, to give them the land of Canaan, the land of their pilgrimage, wherein they were strangers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33387be3-a7f7-4618-8ee3-bdd903097c69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EXO 6:5
Text: And I have also heard the groaning of the children of Israel, whom the Egyptians keep in bondage; and I have remembered my covenant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
