Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: EXO 6:30
Text: And Moses said before the LORD, Behold, I am of uncircumcised lips, and how shall Pharaoh hearken unto me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:642758e4-4fc4-4aed-8ffc-968a3923f6ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: EXO 7:1
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, See, I have made thee a god to Pharaoh: and Aaron thy brother shall be thy prophet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:577f96b2-2427-4c6a-9a60-e6cae1685045>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: EXO 7:2
Text: Thou shalt speak all that I command thee: and Aaron thy brother shall speak unto Pharaoh, that he send the children of Israel out of his land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab4467e2-c9fe-469a-a684-995a29cc0632>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: EXO 7:3
Text: And I will harden Pharaoh’s heart, and multiply my signs and my wonders in the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6564065c-2bdf-4647-8e3f-ea605e7a845d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: EXO 7:4
Text: But Pharaoh shall not hearken unto you, that I may lay my hand upon Egypt, and bring forth mine armies, and my people the children of Israel, out of the land of Egypt by great judgments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e24441d-30e9-42e5-af12-c2204d662c48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: EXO 7:5
Text: And the Egyptians shall know that I am the LORD, when I stretch forth mine hand upon Egypt, and bring out the children of Israel from among them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49596dde-d8df-4375-b94a-de1247e36b17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: EXO 7:6
Text: And Moses and Aaron did as the LORD commanded them, so did they.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f0774c9-3755-441e-ab53-1b24ca81f7c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: EXO 7:7
Text: And Moses was fourscore years old, and Aaron fourscore and three years old, when they spake unto Pharaoh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6faef4f-72ba-412e-9db9-76048e21cff7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: EXO 7:8
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses and unto Aaron, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:482d0963-4d6d-417c-a959-35fb6704db8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: EXO 7:9
Text: When Pharaoh shall speak unto you, saying, Shew a miracle for you: then thou shalt say unto Aaron, Take thy rod, and cast it before Pharaoh, and it shall become a serpent.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:573349fc-fcea-4f95-abab-d3928c284d46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: EXO 7:10
Text: And Moses and Aaron went in unto Pharaoh, and they did so as the LORD had commanded: and Aaron cast down his rod before Pharaoh, and before his servants, and it became a serpent.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21378e30-f38b-483d-b1bf-86dd38b8a354>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: EXO 7:11
Text: Then Pharaoh also called the wise men and the sorcerers: now the magicians of Egypt, they also did in like manner with their enchantments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:529f82ea-c3fb-43ae-b822-b813451d5b4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: EXO 7:12
Text: For they cast down every man his rod, and they became serpents: but Aaron’s rod swallowed up their rods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e52a418-47cd-466a-8f85-029fd52102f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: EXO 7:13
Text: And he hardened Pharaoh’s heart, that he hearkened not unto them; as the LORD had said.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64361756-4284-4f37-ad66-0a0811458545>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: EXO 7:14
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Pharaoh’s heart is hardened, he refuseth to let the people go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d875e844-0b23-4e09-b9d5-00864a2d0b90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: EXO 7:15
Text: Get thee unto Pharaoh in the morning; lo, he goeth out unto the water; and thou shalt stand by the river’s brink against he come; and the rod which was turned to a serpent shalt thou take in thine hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f2389ba-bbdb-4597-b703-bb3170b3ebac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: EXO 7:16
Text: And thou shalt say unto him, The LORD God of the Hebrews hath sent me unto thee, saying, Let my people go, that they may serve me in the wilderness: and, behold, hitherto thou wouldest not hear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03f546f3-2bab-40f9-9920-a1b1afcddce4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: EXO 7:17
Text: Thus saith the LORD, In this thou shalt know that I am the LORD: behold, I will smite with the rod that is in mine hand upon the waters which are in the river, and they shall be turned to blood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a7c1195-206c-45bd-bc65-2a0ab069f361>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: EXO 7:18
Text: And the fish that is in the river shall die, and the river shall stink; and the Egyptians shall lothe to drink of the water of the river.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76334cc8-535e-47b6-a143-6eb0c72283c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 376

Reference: EXO 7:19
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, Say unto Aaron, Take thy rod, and stretch out thine hand upon the waters of Egypt, upon their streams, upon their rivers, and upon their ponds, and upon all their pools of water, that they may become blood; and that there may be blood throughout all the land of Egypt, both in vessels of wood, and in vessels of stone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7cd67ff-05ed-4389-bd5b-60b97a4ebc4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: EXO 7:20
Text: And Moses and Aaron did so, as the LORD commanded; and he lifted up the rod, and smote the waters that were in the river, in the sight of Pharaoh, and in the sight of his servants; and all the waters that were in the river were turned to blood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34ce5091-2b3e-40e6-baf1-97bad8dad0a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: EXO 7:21
Text: And the fish that was in the river died; and the river stank, and the Egyptians could not drink of the water of the river; and there was blood throughout all the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:320e8f23-a92d-48ad-899a-26e9c611ea05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: EXO 7:22
Text: And the magicians of Egypt did so with their enchantments: and Pharaoh’s heart was hardened, neither did he hearken unto them; as the LORD had said.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31533ec2-fa62-42b9-8c52-03491eff5c87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: EXO 7:23
Text: And Pharaoh turned and went into his house, neither did he set his heart to this also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd455c98-7a85-4d48-8afc-7255cea3d3da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: EXO 7:24
Text: And all the Egyptians digged round about the river for water to drink; for they could not drink of the water of the river.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/7/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3350a497-3277-4cab-9f38-769a3fda2a6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: EXO 7:25
Text: And seven days were fulfilled, after that the LORD had smitten the river.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:410bc5e3-e63a-4a67-b99e-aa9674bbf299>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: EXO 8:1
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, Go unto Pharaoh, and say unto him, Thus saith the LORD, Let my people go, that they may serve me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22159bb3-1ef5-4d6f-a471-7270d9045836>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: EXO 8:2
Text: And if thou refuse to let them go, behold, I will smite all thy borders with frogs:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47291430-b89c-45f1-a618-32e5f9021ce5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: EXO 8:3
Text: And the river shall bring forth frogs abundantly, which shall go up and come into thine house, and into thy bedchamber, and upon thy bed, and into the house of thy servants, and upon thy people, and into thine ovens, and into thy kneadingtroughs:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2e667e5-6016-4dcf-b5e0-29d6d62d3613>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: EXO 8:4
Text: And the frogs shall come up both on thee, and upon thy people, and upon all thy servants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d55ce3b5-6cd5-4006-82b9-2bca0426a8cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: EXO 8:5
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, Say unto Aaron, Stretch forth thine hand with thy rod over the streams, over the rivers, and over the ponds, and cause frogs to come up upon the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0309ca8f-8fb1-4048-b314-232d38fb76df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: EXO 8:6
Text: And Aaron stretched out his hand over the waters of Egypt; and the frogs came up, and covered the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3f86dfb-4068-47b7-84cc-feeff76f5c4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: EXO 8:7
Text: And the magicians did so with their enchantments, and brought up frogs upon the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bbd19e7e-b3ad-4580-bd14-5046f8959d47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: EXO 8:8
Text: Then Pharaoh called for Moses and Aaron, and said, Intreat the LORD, that he may take away the frogs from me, and from my people; and I will let the people go, that they may do sacrifice unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:976294aa-4e5b-42cb-bc42-5dbc02d8f599>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: EXO 8:9
Text: And Moses said unto Pharaoh, Glory over me: when shall I intreat for thee, and for thy servants, and for thy people, to destroy the frogs from thee and thy houses, that they may remain in the river only?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:130ea0d9-d575-4e18-b11b-e8c27c478c19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: EXO 8:10
Text: And he said, To morrow. And he said, Be it according to thy word: that thou mayest know that there is none like unto the LORD our God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef327ce6-577a-488d-bb1b-ce049959e475>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: EXO 8:11
Text: And the frogs shall depart from thee, and from thy houses, and from thy servants, and from thy people; they shall remain in the river only.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29ad9397-6a18-412c-af2b-227c71c5ec00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EXO 8:12
Text: And Moses and Aaron went out from Pharaoh: and Moses cried unto the LORD because of the frogs which he had brought against Pharaoh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c2de760-9e9d-47cb-af62-50fc35a15fbb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EXO 8:13
Text: And the LORD did according to the word of Moses; and the frogs died out of the houses, out of the villages, and out of the fields.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84cf6506-85ff-4580-acfd-5947b3d3698a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: EXO 8:14
Text: And they gathered them together upon heaps: and the land stank.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11ef3bc9-5d0f-4c1e-ba6f-daeaefcfe865>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: EXO 8:15
Text: But when Pharaoh saw that there was respite, he hardened his heart, and hearkened not unto them; as the LORD had said.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5fb1c49b-3b2c-47de-8914-821e68782601>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: EXO 8:16
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Say unto Aaron, Stretch out thy rod, and smite the dust of the land, that it may become lice throughout all the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a344241d-a1e7-42ba-81ee-0df565ec0358>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: EXO 8:17
Text: And they did so; for Aaron stretched out his hand with his rod, and smote the dust of the earth, and it became lice in man, and in beast; all the dust of the land became lice throughout all the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce7bad81-329e-4acd-87ab-ba28ce8e539c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: EXO 8:18
Text: And the magicians did so with their enchantments to bring forth lice, but they could not: so there were lice upon man, and upon beast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb1ddd9c-b0b0-4542-80cf-1075da327084>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: EXO 8:19
Text: Then the magicians said unto Pharaoh, This is the finger of God: and Pharaoh’s heart was hardened, and he hearkened not unto them; as the LORD had said.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15cd6ad8-3817-4a29-af29-0fbf97c24eb1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: EXO 8:20
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Rise up early in the morning, and stand before Pharaoh; lo, he cometh forth to the water; and say unto him, Thus saith the LORD, Let my people go, that they may serve me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e45baeb-7389-4469-8f08-cc10508460eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 283

Reference: EXO 8:21
Text: Else, if thou wilt not let my people go, behold, I will send swarms of flies upon thee, and upon thy servants, and upon thy people, and into thy houses: and the houses of the Egyptians shall be full of swarms of flies, and also the ground whereon they are.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5cfda50-6ca6-44a5-b1d3-96293772fade>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: EXO 8:22
Text: And I will sever in that day the land of Goshen, in which my people dwell, that no swarms of flies shall be there; to the end thou mayest know that I am the LORD in the midst of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a110397-2b03-44a2-9823-8f7ba838d632>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: EXO 8:23
Text: And I will put a division between my people and thy people: to morrow shall this sign be.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30fae85c-2327-4b1a-b7ef-00564baed4d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: EXO 8:24
Text: And the LORD did so; and there came a grievous swarm of flies into the house of Pharaoh, and into his servants’ houses, and into all the land of Egypt: the land was corrupted by reason of the swarm of flies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e81d5bdd-9100-4289-8561-83ae575cc28d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: EXO 8:25
Text: And Pharaoh called for Moses and for Aaron, and said, Go ye, sacrifice to your God in the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a6ffa13-ec57-4b27-95b3-845af738e10b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: EXO 8:26
Text: And Moses said, It is not meet so to do; for we shall sacrifice the abomination of the Egyptians to the LORD our God: lo, shall we sacrifice the abomination of the Egyptians before their eyes, and will they not stone us?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43e7999b-0a1b-4a5f-80b8-dfd29652811f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: EXO 8:27
Text: We will go three days’ journey into the wilderness, and sacrifice to the LORD our God, as he shall command us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:508502c7-ea66-4214-81fb-cd4ffa2fe00b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: EXO 8:28
Text: And Pharaoh said, I will let you go, that ye may sacrifice to the LORD your God in the wilderness; only ye shall not go very far away: intreat for me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a855ee6e-a2d9-4198-b2f1-384aed3014bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 300

Reference: EXO 8:29
Text: And Moses said, Behold, I go out from thee, and I will intreat the LORD that the swarms of flies may depart from Pharaoh, from his servants, and from his people, to morrow: but let not Pharaoh deal deceitfully any more in not letting the people go to sacrifice to the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42f54ec7-4a7a-437f-8c20-a51e529eb46f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: EXO 8:30
Text: And Moses went out from Pharaoh, and intreated the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:368ba13c-6ccf-4b8b-9689-724478f5bfcc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: EXO 8:31
Text: And the LORD did according to the word of Moses; and he removed the swarms of flies from Pharaoh, from his servants, and from his people; there remained not one.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/8/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9c9beca-c18d-4c87-8649-ec74f3feee62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: EXO 8:32
Text: And Pharaoh hardened his heart at this time also, neither would he let the people go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f4fd7be-5694-4916-8f84-e005f436ffeb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: EXO 9:1
Text: Then the LORD said unto Moses, Go in unto Pharaoh, and tell him, Thus saith the LORD God of the Hebrews, Let my people go, that they may serve me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3482254-4c8c-4220-84a2-305a387f7164>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: EXO 9:2
Text: For if thou refuse to let them go, and wilt hold them still,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c6c29d9-aeac-4197-98c9-9217677ce38a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: EXO 9:3
Text: Behold, the hand of the LORD is upon thy cattle which is in the field, upon the horses, upon the asses, upon the camels, upon the oxen, and upon the sheep: there shall be a very grievous murrain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63869b4c-bcb3-4a39-8b3f-544723bb7a79>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: EXO 9:4
Text: And the LORD shall sever between the cattle of Israel and the cattle of Egypt: and there shall nothing die of all that is the children’s of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ba2c6b3-812f-4ccf-a8c3-8c31eb5d6be6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: EXO 9:5
Text: And the LORD appointed a set time, saying, To morrow the LORD shall do this thing in the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f74f2f8b-8d38-4464-94cf-072db0134f2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EXO 9:6
Text: And the LORD did that thing on the morrow, and all the cattle of Egypt died: but of the cattle of the children of Israel died not one.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da2cd55c-e9cb-43c7-9c3a-e3379c34109a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: EXO 9:7
Text: And Pharaoh sent, and, behold, there was not one of the cattle of the Israelites dead. And the heart of Pharaoh was hardened, and he did not let the people go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14567fca-8acc-4435-9898-ed8cd4fd3352>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: EXO 9:8
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses and unto Aaron, Take to you handfuls of ashes of the furnace, and let Moses sprinkle it toward the heaven in the sight of Pharaoh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e03973c3-e317-4887-b2cf-9892a06eccc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: EXO 9:9
Text: And it shall become small dust in all the land of Egypt, and shall be a boil breaking forth with blains upon man, and upon beast, throughout all the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1a012eb-f41e-40a0-b58c-287610c2918b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: EXO 9:10
Text: And they took ashes of the furnace, and stood before Pharaoh; and Moses sprinkled it up toward heaven; and it became a boil breaking forth with blains upon man, and upon beast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5cbb3b4-eae8-4888-b659-2a9384df193b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EXO 9:11
Text: And the magicians could not stand before Moses because of the boils; for the boil was upon the magicians, and upon all the Egyptians.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b64dc7b-a22b-47ec-a04c-d6effa9ff018>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: EXO 9:12
Text: And the LORD hardened the heart of Pharaoh, and he hearkened not unto them; as the LORD had spoken unto Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bb4a19d-1bbd-45b4-8c6e-19d2721bfdbc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: EXO 9:13
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Rise up early in the morning, and stand before Pharaoh, and say unto him, Thus saith the LORD God of the Hebrews, Let my people go, that they may serve me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51bbcb13-c581-40f4-8c4f-9ed161e8aff2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: EXO 9:14
Text: For I will at this time send all my plagues upon thine heart, and upon thy servants, and upon thy people; that thou mayest know that there is none like me in all the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4ec6425-eab1-4430-bb91-5b3f7e3fedcc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EXO 9:15
Text: For now I will stretch out my hand, that I may smite thee and thy people with pestilence; and thou shalt be cut off from the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b9048fa-9fe0-47e8-a0b3-302f9e7cfc5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: EXO 9:16
Text: And in very deed for this cause have I raised thee up, for to shew in thee my power; and that my name may be declared throughout all the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c26b76fd-6e59-4916-bd60-545731b77faf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: EXO 9:17
Text: As yet exaltest thou thyself against my people, that thou wilt not let them go?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27df82bb-94e0-4a96-9e78-273d12840973>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: EXO 9:18
Text: Behold, to morrow about this time I will cause it to rain a very grievous hail, such as hath not been in Egypt since the foundation thereof even until now.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81a29b9b-6058-4f19-a57b-edd2daae9b11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: EXO 9:19
Text: Send therefore now, and gather thy cattle, and all that thou hast in the field; for upon every man and beast which shall be found in the field, and shall not be brought home, the hail shall come down upon them, and they shall die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1535a21-7939-40d3-b34a-6a94ade96a0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: EXO 9:20
Text: He that feared the word of the LORD among the servants of Pharaoh made his servants and his cattle flee into the houses:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:baabe663-c539-4e22-946e-ddb421421656>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: EXO 9:21
Text: And he that regarded not the word of the LORD left his servants and his cattle in the field.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3909758-891f-412c-92a4-20c9b99c3d27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: EXO 9:22
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Stretch forth thine hand toward heaven, that there may be hail in all the land of Egypt, upon man, and upon beast, and upon every herb of the field, throughout the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63906c65-8377-4a80-848b-6f50fd9c9760>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: EXO 9:23
Text: And Moses stretched forth his rod toward heaven: and the LORD sent thunder and hail, and the fire ran along upon the ground; and the LORD rained hail upon the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5644b3bd-19fe-4baa-9b18-46cee2770bcd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: EXO 9:24
Text: So there was hail, and fire mingled with the hail, very grievous, such as there was none like it in all the land of Egypt since it became a nation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4a668f3-db25-4672-baa8-105b3c1cd2d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: EXO 9:25
Text: And the hail smote throughout all the land of Egypt all that was in the field, both man and beast; and the hail smote every herb of the field, and brake every tree of the field.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cddeeee0-764c-4694-a4d1-865d52b01ea9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: EXO 9:26
Text: Only in the land of Goshen, where the children of Israel were, was there no hail.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66cf8e22-80b9-436f-b6b1-5cdb1273f2ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: EXO 9:27
Text: And Pharaoh sent, and called for Moses and Aaron, and said unto them, I have sinned this time: the LORD is righteous, and I and my people are wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b14c637b-b8d8-496f-9493-da2dc4b4a3c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: EXO 9:28
Text: Intreat the LORD (for it is enough) that there be no more mighty thunderings and hail; and I will let you go, and ye shall stay no longer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:398e5f96-d1ce-4ba2-b5f0-14f8ecb54b3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: EXO 9:29
Text: And Moses said unto him, As soon as I am gone out of the city, I will spread abroad my hands unto the LORD; and the thunder shall cease, neither shall there be any more hail; that thou mayest know how that the earth is the LORD’s.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5064fc9f-7eb8-477a-9560-93539d635774>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: EXO 9:30
Text: But as for thee and thy servants, I know that ye will not yet fear the LORD God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6eeb713-a76e-4f68-9a60-4a7cc08325d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: EXO 9:31
Text: And the flax and the barley was smitten: for the barley was in the ear, and the flax was bolled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38c83144-5168-431a-8714-5e38b8380203>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: EXO 9:32
Text: But the wheat and the rie were not smitten: for they were not grown up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:304b6971-03c8-4a80-a0e4-814d19fc7d87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: EXO 9:33
Text: And Moses went out of the city from Pharaoh, and spread abroad his hands unto the LORD: and the thunders and hail ceased, and the rain was not poured upon the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f06f8b6-d764-4eca-86b7-179f959ef0c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: EXO 9:34
Text: And when Pharaoh saw that the rain and the hail and the thunders were ceased, he sinned yet more, and hardened his heart, he and his servants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/9/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7eb811c-9ce2-48bd-8355-78e3a051d484>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: EXO 9:35
Text: And the heart of Pharaoh was hardened, neither would he let the children of Israel go; as the LORD had spoken by Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d58987b-b890-49be-8469-49b2e5216c9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: EXO 10:1
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Go in unto Pharaoh: for I have hardened his heart, and the heart of his servants, that I might shew these my signs before him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bda75654-306a-4235-a71b-dbbecfb0cd13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: EXO 10:2
Text: And that thou mayest tell in the ears of thy son, and of thy son’s son, what things I have wrought in Egypt, and my signs which I have done among them; that ye may know how that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9e7fffa-61cb-4a9b-8505-93d5f204af8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: EXO 10:3
Text: And Moses and Aaron came in unto Pharaoh, and said unto him, Thus saith the LORD God of the Hebrews, How long wilt thou refuse to humble thyself before me? let my people go, that they may serve me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39050c6c-e5c7-40ff-8d70-3c243b63c0d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: EXO 10:4
Text: Else, if thou refuse to let my people go, behold, to morrow will I bring the locusts into thy coast:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b22e4092-df4d-4bc4-af4d-6a08351a5446>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 274

Reference: EXO 10:5
Text: And they shall cover the face of the earth, that one cannot be able to see the earth: and they shall eat the residue of that which is escaped, which remaineth unto you from the hail, and shall eat every tree which groweth for you out of the field:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:646d4c41-9796-4c77-ab26-359eb99d6ca1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 305

Reference: EXO 10:6
Text: And they shall fill thy houses, and the houses of all thy servants, and the houses of all the Egyptians; which neither thy fathers, nor thy fathers’ fathers have seen, since the day that they were upon the earth unto this day. And he turned himself, and went out from Pharaoh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c0ece85-e8a0-4dea-9367-7f19b0220e71>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: EXO 10:7
Text: And Pharaoh’s servants said unto him, How long shall this man be a snare unto us? let the men go, that they may serve the LORD their God: knowest thou not yet that Egypt is destroyed?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f3da224-9a18-4a7e-939a-387a52a821cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: EXO 10:8
Text: And Moses and Aaron were brought again unto Pharaoh: and he said unto them, Go, serve the LORD your God: but who are they that shall go?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bfff5665-73f6-4646-ae74-29d62562bf4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: EXO 10:9
Text: And Moses said, We will go with our young and with our old, with our sons and with our daughters, with our flocks and with our herds will we go; for we must hold a feast unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58b64465-7810-4a73-a681-ee1df235c3d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: EXO 10:10
Text: And he said unto them, Let the LORD be so with you, as I will let you go, and your little ones: look to it; for evil is before you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b97308e6-97b7-4431-9e07-c0ae102f5efa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: EXO 10:11
Text: Not so: go now ye that are men, and serve the LORD; for that ye did desire. And they were driven out from Pharaoh’s presence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbdf811e-700c-47f4-a513-f67a332898ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: EXO 10:12
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Stretch out thine hand over the land of Egypt for the locusts, that they may come up upon the land of Egypt, and eat every herb of the land, even all that the hail hath left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2499737e-ab27-4958-ab0b-5afccca9b7eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: EXO 10:13
Text: And Moses stretched forth his rod over the land of Egypt, and the LORD brought an east wind upon the land all that day, and all that night; and when it was morning, the east wind brought the locusts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c691cb4c-42e0-4d07-9111-f471617ded0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: EXO 10:14
Text: And the locust went up over all the land of Egypt, and rested in all the coasts of Egypt: very grievous were they; before them there were no such locusts as they, neither after them shall be such.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb04fcb2-9d08-4752-adbe-4bcd7140b42f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 315

Reference: EXO 10:15
Text: For they covered the face of the whole earth, so that the land was darkened; and they did eat every herb of the land, and all the fruit of the trees which the hail had left: and there remained not any green thing in the trees, or in the herbs of the field, through all the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfda859c-0184-4373-8a2e-c16eb1dff93e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: EXO 10:16
Text: Then Pharaoh called for Moses and Aaron in haste; and he said, I have sinned against the LORD your God, and against you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f17c10ef-64ad-40cc-9da4-c04a28a7058f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: EXO 10:17
Text: Now therefore forgive, I pray thee, my sin only this once, and intreat the LORD your God, that he may take away from me this death only.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a038ee28-e7ff-4ac4-b404-17a19970617b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: EXO 10:18
Text: And he went out from Pharaoh, and intreated the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32aab2d6-93f5-49e9-bf30-646c16df608f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: EXO 10:19
Text: And the LORD turned a mighty strong west wind, which took away the locusts, and cast them into the Red sea; there remained not one locust in all the coasts of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0d2fce0-3033-4594-8646-ea9f59950a59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: EXO 10:20
Text: But the LORD hardened Pharaoh’s heart, so that he would not let the children of Israel go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ebf9cd7-ccc0-4883-9734-59981e5960d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: EXO 10:21
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Stretch out thine hand toward heaven, that there may be darkness over the land of Egypt, even darkness which may be felt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:105385a4-6cfa-4ded-85d2-bd7a80de0310>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: EXO 10:22
Text: And Moses stretched forth his hand toward heaven; and there was a thick darkness in all the land of Egypt three days:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd182174-adae-4021-a297-1c051fadf02a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: EXO 10:23
Text: They saw not one another, neither rose any from his place for three days: but all the children of Israel had light in their dwellings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b13ec56-520e-4dd0-abea-68d03e21a9ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: EXO 10:24
Text: And Pharaoh called unto Moses, and said, Go ye, serve the LORD; only let your flocks and your herds be stayed: let your little ones also go with you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33352b55-ac04-4779-ad50-6a85e22df804>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: EXO 10:25
Text: And Moses said, Thou must give us also sacrifices and burnt offerings, that we may sacrifice unto the LORD our God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a77af73d-1f40-4215-bea2-f9834c0c3419>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: EXO 10:26
Text: Our cattle also shall go with us; there shall not an hoof be left behind; for thereof must we take to serve the LORD our God; and we know not with what we must serve the LORD, until we come thither.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29df244a-bc44-4853-a338-92410fc18e9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: EXO 10:27
Text: But the LORD hardened Pharaoh’s heart, and he would not let them go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce094012-34df-40b8-881f-cce2aefae21f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: EXO 10:28
Text: And Pharaoh said unto him, Get thee from me, take heed to thyself, see my face no more; for in that day thou seest my face thou shalt die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/10/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f00da7bc-9cb9-4ebf-ae01-721ff3849161>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: EXO 10:29
Text: And Moses said, Thou hast spoken well, I will see thy face again no more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/11/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49dd0759-d2d4-4e9e-b586-9a219546dd64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: EXO 11:1
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Yet will I bring one plague more upon Pharaoh, and upon Egypt; afterwards he will let you go hence: when he shall let you go, he shall surely thrust you out hence altogether.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/11/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2ac5ed1-336c-4d1e-b6ac-91e23f89aad9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: EXO 11:2
Text: Speak now in the ears of the people, and let every man borrow of his neighbour, and every woman of her neighbour, jewels of silver and jewels of gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/11/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd8134ee-3e90-47e4-831f-08221fbff4aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: EXO 11:3
Text: And the LORD gave the people favour in the sight of the Egyptians. Moreover the man Moses was very great in the land of Egypt, in the sight of Pharaoh’s servants, and in the sight of the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/11/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17c4ec00-1fb3-4628-871d-91b0dcd14234>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: EXO 11:4
Text: And Moses said, Thus saith the LORD, About midnight will I go out into the midst of Egypt:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/11/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52026a6f-a6e9-405b-a19b-45fff7ec9655>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: EXO 11:5
Text: And all the firstborn in the land of Egypt shall die, from the first born of Pharaoh that sitteth upon his throne, even unto the firstborn of the maidservant that is behind the mill; and all the firstborn of beasts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/11/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57404822-9bba-4d7b-9b73-f50053702324>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: EXO 11:6
Text: And there shall be a great cry throughout all the land of Egypt, such as there was none like it, nor shall be like it any more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/11/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:094896d7-224c-42ea-8dee-3b70aec7f348>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: EXO 11:7
Text: But against any of the children of Israel shall not a dog move his tongue, against man or beast: that ye may know how that the LORD doth put a difference between the Egyptians and Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/11/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c01a247-afa4-4ccf-9448-eb3332efd6d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: EXO 11:8
Text: And all these thy servants shall come down unto me, and bow down themselves unto me, saying, Get thee out, and all the people that follow thee: and after that I will go out. And he went out from Pharaoh in a great anger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/11/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d85299c-b0b2-49c4-9ef0-a6f008374a08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: EXO 11:9
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Pharaoh shall not hearken unto you; that my wonders may be multiplied in the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/11/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c86cf66-e361-44c7-8a7a-5b56bf606d64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: EXO 11:10
Text: And Moses and Aaron did all these wonders before Pharaoh: and the LORD hardened Pharaoh’s heart, so that he would not let the children of Israel go out of his land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:966ca3b6-b95a-4918-9dab-d95df363fe1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: EXO 12:1
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses and Aaron in the land of Egypt saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4de39c39-e2d6-4e25-ac26-220c357c62db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: EXO 12:2
Text: This month shall be unto you the beginning of months: it shall be the first month of the year to you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40a4904e-ef3d-4ee5-807b-4e6b96a2c43a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: EXO 12:3
Text: Speak ye unto all the congregation of Israel, saying, In the tenth day of this month they shall take to them every man a lamb, according to the house of their fathers, a lamb for an house:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a191a51a-d09b-4d28-8d87-7b356a6dd14f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: EXO 12:4
Text: And if the household be too little for the lamb, let him and his neighbour next unto his house take it according to the number of the souls; every man according to his eating shall make your count for the lamb.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57d7eb49-c0fb-4a14-8911-52a143467f04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: EXO 12:5
Text: Your lamb shall be without blemish, a male of the first year: ye shall take it out from the sheep, or from the goats:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c44c4ea3-8665-4671-843f-6715bf59a031>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: EXO 12:6
Text: And ye shall keep it up until the fourteenth day of the same month: and the whole assembly of the congregation of Israel shall kill it in the evening.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:224f5abe-5231-433d-877f-013095d5244e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: EXO 12:7
Text: And they shall take of the blood, and strike it on the two side posts and on the upper door post of the houses, wherein they shall eat it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1b21e86-a317-47af-af52-a42edd2bdd6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: EXO 12:8
Text: And they shall eat the flesh in that night, roast with fire, and unleavened bread; and with bitter herbs they shall eat it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43689ef4-68c8-4615-867f-c29698a41527>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: EXO 12:9
Text: Eat not of it raw, nor sodden at all with water, but roast with fire; his head with his legs, and with the purtenance thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bc09d23-2e9b-47dc-ba33-5e47c16d5ba1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EXO 12:10
Text: And ye shall let nothing of it remain until the morning; and that which remaineth of it until the morning ye shall burn with fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:504a0dbf-3f40-4779-85d2-5340a9144c10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: EXO 12:11
Text: And thus shall ye eat it; with your loins girded, your shoes on your feet, and your staff in your hand; and ye shall eat it in haste: it is the LORD’s passover.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:669ec868-4175-4672-ac55-1445f32cbc6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: EXO 12:12
Text: For I will pass through the land of Egypt this night, and will smite all the firstborn in the land of Egypt, both man and beast; and against all the gods of Egypt I will execute judgment: I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e9dff45-2bde-47f0-b5e3-45b5d36e8475>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: EXO 12:13
Text: And the blood shall be to you for a token upon the houses where ye are: and when I see the blood, I will pass over you, and the plague shall not be upon you to destroy you, when I smite the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c258f7ce-adc8-45c6-9553-d27da592b06c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: EXO 12:14
Text: And this day shall be unto you for a memorial; and ye shall keep it a feast to the LORD throughout your generations; ye shall keep it a feast by an ordinance for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1da2e4e4-fbd9-42b2-8678-1a68dbe048fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: EXO 12:15
Text: Seven days shall ye eat unleavened bread; even the first day ye shall put away leaven out of your houses: for whosoever eateth leavened bread from the first day until the seventh day, that soul shall be cut off from Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:827bffd4-edb2-43e6-945f-2b6cc402f36f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: EXO 12:16
Text: And in the first day there shall be an holy convocation, and in the seventh day there shall be an holy convocation to you; no manner of work shall be done in them, save that which every man must eat, that only may be done of you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e96108d-2775-4a47-9d29-6dc6cc62e1d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: EXO 12:17
Text: And ye shall observe the feast of unleavened bread; for in this selfsame day have I brought your armies out of the land of Egypt: therefore shall ye observe this day in your generations by an ordinance for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2e77830-2e3c-4858-a410-3afa9d667099>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: EXO 12:18
Text: In the first month, on the fourteenth day of the month at even, ye shall eat unleavened bread, until the one and twentieth day of the month at even.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acba1688-7b9a-46b2-b0e3-15b79d8b5c65>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: EXO 12:19
Text: Seven days shall there be no leaven found in your houses: for whosoever eateth that which is leavened, even that soul shall be cut off from the congregation of Israel, whether he be a stranger, or born in the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bd2c118-bf23-4e21-a544-5f4d156200d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: EXO 12:20
Text: Ye shall eat nothing leavened; in all your habitations shall ye eat unleavened bread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d860484a-6bb4-40e3-9657-8551687abfce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: EXO 12:21
Text: Then Moses called for all the elders of Israel, and said unto them, Draw out and take you a lamb according to your families, and kill the passover.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d855ddda-9880-4e26-a22e-94d9ff2d49c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: EXO 12:22
Text: And ye shall take a bunch of hyssop, and dip it in the blood that is in the bason, and strike the lintel and the two side posts with the blood that is in the bason; and none of you shall go out at the door of his house until the morning.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2179c661-068c-4f6b-8afb-6001e1f3a42b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: EXO 12:23
Text: For the LORD will pass through to smite the Egyptians; and when he seeth the blood upon the lintel, and on the two side posts, the LORD will pass over the door, and will not suffer the destroyer to come in unto your houses to smite you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c29f3a67-4a80-48dc-be0c-d1b47be8bc14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: EXO 12:24
Text: And ye shall observe this thing for an ordinance to thee and to thy sons for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff5ac387-e4d6-44ff-b9bb-1f2887dc58bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: EXO 12:25
Text: And it shall come to pass, when ye be come to the land which the LORD will give you, according as he hath promised, that ye shall keep this service.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7cb7554-f96a-4605-aae3-4cc0ae88c5b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: EXO 12:26
Text: And it shall come to pass, when your children shall say unto you, What mean ye by this service?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0995e4ce-7e61-488d-bd93-1865d870c6fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: EXO 12:27
Text: That ye shall say, It is the sacrifice of the LORD’s passover, who passed over the houses of the children of Israel in Egypt, when he smote the Egyptians, and delivered our houses. And the people bowed the head and worshipped.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d81fc6a8-58ac-475f-87d8-9b43ac66ec4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: EXO 12:28
Text: And the children of Israel went away, and did as the LORD had commanded Moses and Aaron, so did they.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:174d5d01-0658-42ab-91a1-c9c55fa011bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: EXO 12:29
Text: And it came to pass, that at midnight the LORD smote all the firstborn in the land of Egypt, from the firstborn of Pharaoh that sat on his throne unto the firstborn of the captive that was in the dungeon; and all the firstborn of cattle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72742010-c6c4-47c6-b127-0a8757e60a02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: EXO 12:30
Text: And Pharaoh rose up in the night, he, and all his servants, and all the Egyptians; and there was a great cry in Egypt; for there was not a house where there was not one dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59ec297f-ecad-40cd-b821-c4128e747c85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: EXO 12:31
Text: And he called for Moses and Aaron by night, and said, Rise up, and get you forth from among my people, both ye and the children of Israel; and go, serve the LORD, as ye have said.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f42677c6-288c-407c-93d2-2cee7a8a1c68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: EXO 12:32
Text: Also take your flocks and your herds, as ye have said, and be gone; and bless me also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8016517-5d28-4de7-a2d1-3a067e3c0659>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: EXO 12:33
Text: And the Egyptians were urgent upon the people, that they might send them out of the land in haste; for they said, We be all dead men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e1c30d5-d5e3-4e4d-83d0-80a9d78e2c6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: EXO 12:34
Text: And the people took their dough before it was leavened, their kneadingtroughs being bound up in their clothes upon their shoulders.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e02fc39c-2f6f-4a38-9341-1737acdb9b51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: EXO 12:35
Text: And the children of Israel did according to the word of Moses; and they borrowed of the Egyptians jewels of silver, and jewels of gold, and raiment:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ab00314-e940-401f-aea7-8941ec8f5bc5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: EXO 12:36
Text: And the LORD gave the people favour in the sight of the Egyptians, so that they lent unto them such things as they required. And they spoiled the Egyptians.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f32271db-b37a-4c24-ab5a-e2434c981fe2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: EXO 12:37
Text: And the children of Israel journeyed from Rameses to Succoth, about six hundred thousand on foot that were men, beside children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8d69125-b6cc-471b-8b2b-b11179b42dd2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: EXO 12:38
Text: And a mixed multitude went up also with them; and flocks, and herds, even very much cattle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7911a22f-c856-4a97-8110-4ba3eaf20bdf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: EXO 12:39
Text: And they baked unleavened cakes of the dough which they brought forth out of Egypt, for it was not leavened; because they were thrust out of Egypt, and could not tarry, neither had they prepared for themselves any victual.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11885bd0-7af9-46a5-b1d8-4897889631b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: EXO 12:40
Text: Now the sojourning of the children of Israel, who dwelt in Egypt, was four hundred and thirty years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac4a60e5-e544-4ab1-8a61-202d556aebe9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: EXO 12:41
Text: And it came to pass at the end of the four hundred and thirty years, even the selfsame day it came to pass, that all the hosts of the LORD went out from the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d00fc30f-194f-4406-b28e-6d2c7f80acb0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: EXO 12:42
Text: It is a night to be much observed unto the LORD for bringing them out from the land of Egypt: this is that night of the LORD to be observed of all the children of Israel in their generations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74bf1866-25d9-45d9-aa2d-942f829f4a11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: EXO 12:43
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses and Aaron, This is the ordinance of the passover: There shall no stranger eat thereof:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f94e450c-872a-4429-af94-c0b149c63d68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: EXO 12:44
Text: But every man’s servant that is bought for money, when thou hast circumcised him, then shall he eat thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:698819f2-f1fa-42d9-987d-f82cf708b4f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: EXO 12:45
Text: A foreigner and an hired servant shall not eat thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
