Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: EXO 12:46
Text: In one house shall it be eaten; thou shalt not carry forth ought of the flesh abroad out of the house; neither shall ye break a bone thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e93586f-adad-4732-af63-2300137ae22b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: EXO 12:47
Text: All the congregation of Israel shall keep it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f996f270-6ace-4149-a428-dfaf845b1887>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 282

Reference: EXO 12:48
Text: And when a stranger shall sojourn with thee, and will keep the passover to the LORD, let all his males be circumcised, and then let him come near and keep it; and he shall be as one that is born in the land: for no uncircumcised person shall eat thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13e60ec5-ba93-4d6a-be68-95b3b6c5caeb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: EXO 12:49
Text: One law shall be to him that is homeborn, and unto the stranger that sojourneth among you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:243cc694-0740-4944-bfe8-e6aec1fe9a20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: EXO 12:50
Text: Thus did all the children of Israel; as the LORD commanded Moses and Aaron, so did they.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/12/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57667df4-6c19-4c8e-8d2a-56bc52ceaa8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: EXO 12:51
Text: And it came to pass the selfsame day, that the LORD did bring the children of Israel out of the land of Egypt by their armies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/13/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1637f11-8687-4265-8269-a6f9dfc9383b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 65

Reference: EXO 13:1
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/13/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2dea914d-114b-46ad-818a-918cb04df209>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EXO 13:2
Text: Sanctify unto me all the firstborn, whatsoever openeth the womb among the children of Israel, both of man and of beast: it is mine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/13/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e582aaf4-5ae2-4d34-9051-301036dfcb7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: EXO 13:3
Text: And Moses said unto the people, Remember this day, in which ye came out from Egypt, out of the house of bondage; for by strength of hand the LORD brought you out from this place: there shall no leavened bread be eaten.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/13/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e904a23e-1845-48fd-849c-e81658792362>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 66

Reference: EXO 13:4
Text: This day came ye out in the month Abib.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/13/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23f00056-b573-4943-aa48-70008d8a1511>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 309

Reference: EXO 13:5
Text: And it shall be when the LORD shall bring thee into the land of the Canaanites, and the Hittites, and the Amorites, and the Hivites, and the Jebusites, which he sware unto thy fathers to give thee, a land flowing with milk and honey, that thou shalt keep this service in this month.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/13/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab39237d-31d4-42a4-90ed-cbbe1f7a3608>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: EXO 13:6
Text: Seven days thou shalt eat unleavened bread, and in the seventh day shall be a feast to the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/13/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3afb356a-8e3a-4960-b203-c9865d64cb72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: EXO 13:7
Text: Unleavened bread shall be eaten seven days; and there shall no leavened bread be seen with thee, neither shall there be leaven seen with thee in all thy quarters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/13/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82d81215-b00f-4d90-8bc4-7df3f53472f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: EXO 13:8
Text: And thou shalt shew thy son in that day, saying, This is done because of that which the LORD did unto me when I came forth out of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/13/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c9f43de-f186-4a83-92a8-a410341b6254>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: EXO 13:9
Text: And it shall be for a sign unto thee upon thine hand, and for a memorial between thine eyes, that the LORD’s law may be in thy mouth: for with a strong hand hath the LORD brought thee out of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/13/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:318cd550-9a33-4032-aeb6-dd3197109a0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: EXO 13:10
Text: Thou shalt therefore keep this ordinance in his season from year to year.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/13/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a6ab9a2-d5fd-45a7-abd1-7a4e0744255d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: EXO 13:11
Text: And it shall be when the LORD shall bring thee into the land of the Canaanites, as he sware unto thee and to thy fathers, and shall give it thee,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/13/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a3f01b2-da10-44d2-8564-62f562041219>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: EXO 13:12
Text: That thou shalt set apart unto the LORD all that openeth the matrix, and every firstling that cometh of a beast which thou hast; the males shall be the LORD’s.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/13/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5279646d-48db-4e71-8d41-2fad1fe1544c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: EXO 13:13
Text: And every firstling of an ass thou shalt redeem with a lamb; and if thou wilt not redeem it, then thou shalt break his neck: and all the firstborn of man among thy children shalt thou redeem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/13/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:393e19a5-b905-4ffb-97ce-2df180bf37f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: EXO 13:14
Text: And it shall be when thy son asketh thee in time to come, saying, What is this? that thou shalt say unto him, By strength of hand the LORD brought us out from Egypt, from the house of bondage:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/13/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6acc03e5-c64d-4e2c-9f23-e972783c3b6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 322

Reference: EXO 13:15
Text: And it came to pass, when Pharaoh would hardly let us go, that the LORD slew all the firstborn in the land of Egypt, both the firstborn of man, and the firstborn of beast: therefore I sacrifice to the LORD all that openeth the matrix, being males; but all the firstborn of my children I redeem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/13/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c1a1d4f-059a-4818-8bf0-56615bcd61eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: EXO 13:16
Text: And it shall be for a token upon thine hand, and for frontlets between thine eyes: for by strength of hand the LORD brought us forth out of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/13/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:195e5e76-9dd8-4595-bc61-7455d09e6d92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 273

Reference: EXO 13:17
Text: And it came to pass, when Pharaoh had let the people go, that God led them not through the way of the land of the Philistines, although that was near; for God said, Lest peradventure the people repent when they see war, and they return to Egypt:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/13/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67f84ed2-3af8-4dc6-ade6-40929f921c95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: EXO 13:18
Text: But God led the people about, through the way of the wilderness of the Red sea: and the children of Israel went up harnessed out of the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/13/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a078c65-982e-4a31-a0cc-054dddd09659>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: EXO 13:19
Text: And Moses took the bones of Joseph with him: for he had straitly sworn the children of Israel, saying, God will surely visit you; and ye shall carry up my bones away hence with you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/13/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4a81edd-26b1-4579-8793-e2af62d64335>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: EXO 13:20
Text: And they took their journey from Succoth, and encamped in Etham, in the edge of the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/13/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfadd952-6b06-4daa-8fb0-3a5a8ec21a97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: EXO 13:21
Text: And the LORD went before them by day in a pillar of a cloud, to lead them the way; and by night in a pillar of fire, to give them light; to go by day and night:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/13/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b2d9989-f869-440d-8786-ce48dca5ff4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: EXO 13:22
Text: He took not away the pillar of the cloud by day, nor the pillar of fire by night, from before the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb62d5b1-81c5-43e9-b746-2ad3b7f69278>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 65

Reference: EXO 14:1
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83f28e86-a9e3-4158-a2c5-5b7a2a054f62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: EXO 14:2
Text: Speak unto the children of Israel, that they turn and encamp before Pihahiroth, between Migdol and the sea, over against Baalzephon: before it shall ye encamp by the sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45a0d162-6213-4ff7-81b9-7e0a9654cce6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: EXO 14:3
Text: For Pharaoh will say of the children of Israel, They are entangled in the land, the wilderness hath shut them in.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14c3d264-c8f2-4ce9-9254-0e39704ee677>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: EXO 14:4
Text: And I will harden Pharaoh’s heart, that he shall follow after them; and I will be honoured upon Pharaoh, and upon all his host; that the Egyptians may know that I am the LORD. And they did so.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebc2e17e-e663-47c5-b112-a7323c24947e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: EXO 14:5
Text: And it was told the king of Egypt that the people fled: and the heart of Pharaoh and of his servants was turned against the people, and they said, Why have we done this, that we have let Israel go from serving us?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e744328f-53ae-4ca3-b8d9-68adfc264c25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: EXO 14:6
Text: And he made ready his chariot, and took his people with him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a42a2a19-6adb-459e-bdd2-f41a20de1a4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: EXO 14:7
Text: And he took six hundred chosen chariots, and all the chariots of Egypt, and captains over every one of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9add04f-6651-42f4-9fe0-8422f5b255a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: EXO 14:8
Text: And the LORD hardened the heart of Pharaoh king of Egypt, and he pursued after the children of Israel: and the children of Israel went out with an high hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b14032e-c7f4-4367-861d-aab1f4524078>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: EXO 14:9
Text: But the Egyptians pursued after them, all the horses and chariots of Pharaoh, and his horsemen, and his army, and overtook them encamping by the sea, beside Pihahiroth, before Baalzephon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b15a1f2b-32e8-4fd8-a78a-8744461a04e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: EXO 14:10
Text: And when Pharaoh drew nigh, the children of Israel lifted up their eyes, and, behold, the Egyptians marched after them; and they were sore afraid: and the children of Israel cried out unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb3e4f16-fcc4-4d27-a9f4-0e0eda407d5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: EXO 14:11
Text: And they said unto Moses, Because there were no graves in Egypt, hast thou taken us away to die in the wilderness? wherefore hast thou dealt thus with us, to carry us forth out of Egypt?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b62433b-3a51-4cd5-8b9e-1a8fb8e14fb7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: EXO 14:12
Text: Is not this the word that we did tell thee in Egypt, saying, Let us alone, that we may serve the Egyptians? For it had been better for us to serve the Egyptians, than that we should die in the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:168caa40-2232-4d16-9440-e415a288c5d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: EXO 14:13
Text: And Moses said unto the people, Fear ye not, stand still, and see the salvation of the LORD, which he will shew to you to day: for the Egyptians whom ye have seen to day, ye shall see them again no more for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6fb5c5bb-d56d-4651-82a0-c158b2a05603>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: EXO 14:14
Text: The LORD shall fight for you, and ye shall hold your peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6551cb5a-b4ee-46ea-b03a-a8f12a9acc64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: EXO 14:15
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Wherefore criest thou unto me? speak unto the children of Israel, that they go forward:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:822b69b0-e23b-4b6f-9d64-4f37cf4df22f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: EXO 14:16
Text: But lift thou up thy rod, and stretch out thine hand over the sea, and divide it: and the children of Israel shall go on dry ground through the midst of the sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1c32f7b-2fff-4d62-9005-e01505cfb640>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: EXO 14:17
Text: And I, behold, I will harden the hearts of the Egyptians, and they shall follow them: and I will get me honour upon Pharaoh, and upon all his host, upon his chariots, and upon his horsemen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82b23eff-28cf-419e-93c0-96380f9f962b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: EXO 14:18
Text: And the Egyptians shall know that I am the LORD, when I have gotten me honour upon Pharaoh, upon his chariots, and upon his horsemen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a39ca53-78b1-45d0-8e64-4332c4262e7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: EXO 14:19
Text: And the angel of God, which went before the camp of Israel, removed and went behind them; and the pillar of the cloud went from before their face, and stood behind them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee31844a-04f0-40ac-bdd7-601cafe4f554>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: EXO 14:20
Text: And it came between the camp of the Egyptians and the camp of Israel; and it was a cloud and darkness to them, but it gave light by night to these: so that the one came not near the other all the night.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76e4fd81-03f2-4ad7-a75f-36e43a9a1def>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: EXO 14:21
Text: And Moses stretched out his hand over the sea; and the LORD caused the sea to go back by a strong east wind all that night, and made the sea dry land, and the waters were divided.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f339a1b4-bd4b-44da-9c52-254f1a5733b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: EXO 14:22
Text: And the children of Israel went into the midst of the sea upon the dry ground: and the waters were a wall unto them on their right hand, and on their left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a04128a2-f117-475e-a537-ca421375052f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: EXO 14:23
Text: And the Egyptians pursued, and went in after them to the midst of the sea, even all Pharaoh’s horses, his chariots, and his horsemen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2db14bf1-d3b3-4e22-8161-5169450bec1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: EXO 14:24
Text: And it came to pass, that in the morning watch the LORD looked unto the host of the Egyptians through the pillar of fire and of the cloud, and troubled the host of the Egyptians,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b1cdfe5-c56b-45cd-960e-c1e1262bcd54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: EXO 14:25
Text: And took off their chariot wheels, that they drave them heavily: so that the Egyptians said, Let us flee from the face of Israel; for the LORD fighteth for them against the Egyptians.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e48baea9-7f03-46a7-ae11-888407e18e7a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: EXO 14:26
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Stretch out thine hand over the sea, that the waters may come again upon the Egyptians, upon their chariots, and upon their horsemen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:002c7608-63fc-4ba7-8a41-f99d71ba3217>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: EXO 14:27
Text: And Moses stretched forth his hand over the sea, and the sea returned to his strength when the morning appeared; and the Egyptians fled against it; and the LORD overthrew the Egyptians in the midst of the sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:085574ca-588b-4b89-895f-0b90702fb394>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: EXO 14:28
Text: And the waters returned, and covered the chariots, and the horsemen, and all the host of Pharaoh that came into the sea after them; there remained not so much as one of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a86b0ad-6a1a-44c0-a8c0-a87e7fecea5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: EXO 14:29
Text: But the children of Israel walked upon dry land in the midst of the sea; and the waters were a wall unto them on their right hand, and on their left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5efdfb65-f923-43d8-8cbc-dd14c01ca00b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: EXO 14:30
Text: Thus the LORD saved Israel that day out of the hand of the Egyptians; and Israel saw the Egyptians dead upon the sea shore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/14/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:634537e4-2890-481b-91f3-bd66898ec4a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: EXO 14:31
Text: And Israel saw that great work which the LORD did upon the Egyptians: and the people feared the LORD, and believed the LORD, and his servant Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4dec1dc-19cb-4b69-871a-5d9eaf1ef3c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: EXO 15:1
Text: Then sang Moses and the children of Israel this song unto the LORD, and spake, saying, I will sing unto the LORD, for he hath triumphed gloriously: the horse and his rider hath he thrown into the sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bbbd569b-b527-4d2d-80a5-34f9a23c8660>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: EXO 15:2
Text: The LORD is my strength and song, and he is become my salvation: he is my God, and I will prepare him an habitation; my father’s God, and I will exalt him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0cd94c4d-f350-47ef-9e7f-35c361f9d4b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: EXO 15:3
Text: The LORD is a man of war: the LORD is his name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edd822a1-62a1-4193-876e-b7d91f6f2d53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: EXO 15:4
Text: Pharaoh’s chariots and his host hath he cast into the sea: his chosen captains also are drowned in the Red sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77543ee7-3573-4ee3-a95f-776001d9898e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: EXO 15:5
Text: The depths have covered them: they sank into the bottom as a stone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39173325-552d-4dcf-bdbd-a440bc6d3de9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: EXO 15:6
Text: Thy right hand, O LORD, is become glorious in power: thy right hand, O LORD, hath dashed in pieces the enemy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14c16fdc-1829-4b41-b216-ab64dbb6aba0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: EXO 15:7
Text: And in the greatness of thine excellency thou hast overthrown them that rose up against thee: thou sentest forth thy wrath, which consumed them as stubble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d9822b1-753e-49f0-babf-ee9e8869ab6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: EXO 15:8
Text: And with the blast of thy nostrils the waters were gathered together, the floods stood upright as an heap, and the depths were congealed in the heart of the sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a34c2db-be31-4c3f-8e1c-84d22d15fafc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: EXO 15:9
Text: The enemy said, I will pursue, I will overtake, I will divide the spoil; my lust shall be satisfied upon them; I will draw my sword, my hand shall destroy them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:410c7030-3cd0-46e5-b5e1-ed75bc1be7db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: EXO 15:10
Text: Thou didst blow with thy wind, the sea covered them: they sank as lead in the mighty waters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9a2cf0c-2e1a-4f43-b8b0-1ddabdcfbdad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: EXO 15:11
Text: Who is like unto thee, O LORD, among the gods? who is like thee, glorious in holiness, fearful in praises, doing wonders?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ec4edc3-9c17-4766-ae80-f3fa7a7e9096>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: EXO 15:12
Text: Thou stretchedst out thy right hand, the earth swallowed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b923bf36-580f-47b9-97ce-34fc54babc7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: EXO 15:13
Text: Thou in thy mercy hast led forth the people which thou hast redeemed: thou hast guided them in thy strength unto thy holy habitation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:445e2503-71a0-494a-89e2-2f3fa1a2336e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: EXO 15:14
Text: The people shall hear, and be afraid: sorrow shall take hold on the inhabitants of Palestina.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4821f2b2-e00a-4265-b84c-6edf9d27966b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: EXO 15:15
Text: Then the dukes of Edom shall be amazed; the mighty men of Moab, trembling shall take hold upon them; all the inhabitants of Canaan shall melt away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ebf0eb1-c872-48af-9c87-0215bca028a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: EXO 15:16
Text: Fear and dread shall fall upon them; by the greatness of thine arm they shall be as still as a stone; till thy people pass over, O LORD, till the people pass over, which thou hast purchased.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8de03100-190f-47cc-9b6c-b878c55f4ac0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: EXO 15:17
Text: Thou shalt bring them in, and plant them in the mountain of thine inheritance, in the place, O LORD, which thou hast made for thee to dwell in, in the Sanctuary, O LORD, which thy hands have established.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f267292-affa-4df7-9a9e-d10ca801e8a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 67

Reference: EXO 15:18
Text: The LORD shall reign for ever and ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13aeadef-bb48-4457-9bb0-b43372cb81cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: EXO 15:19
Text: For the horse of Pharaoh went in with his chariots and with his horsemen into the sea, and the LORD brought again the waters of the sea upon them; but the children of Israel went on dry land in the midst of the sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ab8f11a-4042-410f-be50-268738274893>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: EXO 15:20
Text: And Miriam the prophetess, the sister of Aaron, took a timbrel in her hand; and all the women went out after her with timbrels and with dances.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e27899ad-373f-4f35-84ea-625906894eb9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: EXO 15:21
Text: And Miriam answered them, Sing ye to the LORD, for he hath triumphed gloriously; the horse and his rider hath he thrown into the sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c9b0be9-6c0b-4133-ab84-1d3e0f79c3b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: EXO 15:22
Text: So Moses brought Israel from the Red sea, and they went out into the wilderness of Shur; and they went three days in the wilderness, and found no water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:539af7c3-429c-485d-b720-d5d471589e15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: EXO 15:23
Text: And when they came to Marah, they could not drink of the waters of Marah, for they were bitter: therefore the name of it was called Marah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bcb0eb37-1f4d-41d8-aba3-e7358c47d35d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: EXO 15:24
Text: And the people murmured against Moses, saying, What shall we drink?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd6cb6df-9abb-4d0d-b93e-c3d46b19a6e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: EXO 15:25
Text: And he cried unto the LORD; and the LORD shewed him a tree, which when he had cast into the waters, the waters were made sweet: there he made for them a statute and an ordinance, and there he proved them,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4442d2a2-8319-4191-af9e-e6d427a5be06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 338

Reference: EXO 15:26
Text: And said, If thou wilt diligently hearken to the voice of the LORD thy God, and wilt do that which is right in his sight, and wilt give ear to his commandments, and keep all his statutes, I will put none of these diseases upon thee, which I have brought upon the Egyptians: for I am the LORD that healeth thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/15/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e40a37c-25aa-4b94-bffe-a7f8f89d6fc5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EXO 15:27
Text: And they came to Elim, where were twelve wells of water, and threescore and ten palm trees: and they encamped there by the waters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fed30088-4b5e-462f-bda4-033041424d30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: EXO 16:1
Text: And they took their journey from Elim, and all the congregation of the children of Israel came unto the wilderness of Sin, which is between Elim and Sinai, on the fifteenth day of the second month after their departing out of the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84e36d73-fbbf-4b41-b556-72bce6c8bc42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: EXO 16:2
Text: And the whole congregation of the children of Israel murmured against Moses and Aaron in the wilderness:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2b6dc9a-cba6-423c-859a-e95cbc1d8350>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 302

Reference: EXO 16:3
Text: And the children of Israel said unto them, Would to God we had died by the hand of the LORD in the land of Egypt, when we sat by the flesh pots, and when we did eat bread to the full; for ye have brought us forth into this wilderness, to kill this whole assembly with hunger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:110aa542-e336-48a9-9c08-692878581425>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: EXO 16:4
Text: Then said the LORD unto Moses, Behold, I will rain bread from heaven for you; and the people shall go out and gather a certain rate every day, that I may prove them, whether they will walk in my law, or no.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1712e186-6c91-4c65-93df-7f210285edbc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: EXO 16:5
Text: And it shall come to pass, that on the sixth day they shall prepare that which they bring in; and it shall be twice as much as they gather daily.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7609ab8f-e0be-443b-9566-7bbe4680d4a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: EXO 16:6
Text: And Moses and Aaron said unto all the children of Israel, At even, then ye shall know that the LORD hath brought you out from the land of Egypt:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7e01519-e7cb-478d-bdbf-89a08e0152fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: EXO 16:7
Text: And in the morning, then ye shall see the glory of the LORD; for that he heareth your murmurings against the LORD: and what are we, that ye murmur against us?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f7db080-5757-4da3-89a5-359f7140bb03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 299

Reference: EXO 16:8
Text: And Moses said, This shall be, when the LORD shall give you in the evening flesh to eat, and in the morning bread to the full; for that the LORD heareth your murmurings which ye murmur against him: and what are we? your murmurings are not against us, but against the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7eccbbef-8826-4506-8e44-f7d12f929902>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: EXO 16:9
Text: And Moses spake unto Aaron, Say unto all the congregation of the children of Israel, Come near before the LORD: for he hath heard your murmurings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52fbc3b3-6ad2-4e52-8b3a-fb40313ef5e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: EXO 16:10
Text: And it came to pass, as Aaron spake unto the whole congregation of the children of Israel, that they looked toward the wilderness, and, behold, the glory of the LORD appeared in the cloud.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e04273f-a280-4a09-8102-cdabc8c3b11b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 66

Reference: EXO 16:11
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:020d19d3-713d-4a3b-a89e-6c9cbfb3c1c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: EXO 16:12
Text: I have heard the murmurings of the children of Israel: speak unto them, saying, At even ye shall eat flesh, and in the morning ye shall be filled with bread; and ye shall know that I am the LORD your God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f6c2d44-02fe-4aa7-b870-04c27cdec643>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: EXO 16:13
Text: And it came to pass, that at even the quails came up, and covered the camp: and in the morning the dew lay round about the host.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38d9070e-240c-4a6f-aa35-d6cd202ea0b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: EXO 16:14
Text: And when the dew that lay was gone up, behold, upon the face of the wilderness there lay a small round thing, as small as the hoar frost on the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b07dd00-70c2-43bb-aac1-be796b684cfe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: EXO 16:15
Text: And when the children of Israel saw it, they said one to another, It is manna: for they wist not what it was. And Moses said unto them, This is the bread which the LORD hath given you to eat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25fefeca-c325-4ddc-9782-1a8fa919bd2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: EXO 16:16
Text: This is the thing which the LORD hath commanded, Gather of it every man according to his eating, an omer for every man, according to the number of your persons; take ye every man for them which are in his tents.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca840bcb-2900-46c0-8a04-4fdd8b971e82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: EXO 16:17
Text: And the children of Israel did so, and gathered, some more, some less.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b070c319-f79c-4523-9497-cc998c670d1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: EXO 16:18
Text: And when they did mete it with an omer, he that gathered much had nothing over, and he that gathered little had no lack; they gathered every man according to his eating.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7908708f-b7c7-41d7-a4a8-a6509e75e8c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: EXO 16:19
Text: And Moses said, Let no man leave of it till the morning.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5cff1c31-cdd6-4a4d-bde6-8fdec7625a8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: EXO 16:20
Text: Notwithstanding they hearkened not unto Moses; but some of them left of it until the morning, and it bred worms, and stank: and Moses was wroth with them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:885638d3-8469-4d25-8992-46adc6072234>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: EXO 16:21
Text: And they gathered it every morning, every man according to his eating: and when the sun waxed hot, it melted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b9bd0d7-00c1-4da1-8ae9-f01ba725f059>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: EXO 16:22
Text: And it came to pass, that on the sixth day they gathered twice as much bread, two omers for one man: and all the rulers of the congregation came and told Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49bf6b7c-540c-4cfb-809d-439ca0d0adfd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 290

Reference: EXO 16:23
Text: And he said unto them, This is that which the LORD hath said, To morrow is the rest of the holy sabbath unto the LORD: bake that which ye will bake to day, and seethe that ye will seethe; and that which remaineth over lay up for you to be kept until the morning.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cdc5bad5-30b7-4d8e-bbc0-e06696d03b3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: EXO 16:24
Text: And they laid it up till the morning, as Moses bade: and it did not stink, neither was there any worm therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8fb27354-8b0d-48eb-9612-cf7f3ff8df67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: EXO 16:25
Text: And Moses said, Eat that to day; for to day is a sabbath unto the LORD: to day ye shall not find it in the field.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13748041-3391-4357-a834-a3c6413d9537>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: EXO 16:26
Text: Six days ye shall gather it; but on the seventh day, which is the sabbath, in it there shall be none.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bcec9075-514b-4839-9b79-57cc707915fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: EXO 16:27
Text: And it came to pass, that there went out some of the people on the seventh day for to gather, and they found none.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d9e9b87-8292-4e4d-a1b3-2e9c6ace3ff7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: EXO 16:28
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, How long refuse ye to keep my commandments and my laws?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ebad837-31cd-4292-bf08-dfba6d7d08fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: EXO 16:29
Text: See, for that the LORD hath given you the sabbath, therefore he giveth you on the sixth day the bread of two days; abide ye every man in his place, let no man go out of his place on the seventh day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d9a2093-7a28-47e6-b27f-100fd8f3d929>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 68

Reference: EXO 16:30
Text: So the people rested on the seventh day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b3d077f-b165-4b6b-87a4-2edbbd4a76e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: EXO 16:31
Text: And the house of Israel called the name thereof Manna: and it was like coriander seed, white; and the taste of it was like wafers made with honey.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6efd2107-3f7d-4905-9301-022f5f38ec64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: EXO 16:32
Text: And Moses said, This is the thing which the LORD commandeth, Fill an omer of it to be kept for your generations; that they may see the bread wherewith I have fed you in the wilderness, when I brought you forth from the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:768a0486-6e04-4222-b9b5-a1d4ce2ff2ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: EXO 16:33
Text: And Moses said unto Aaron, Take a pot, and put an omer full of manna therein, and lay it up before the LORD, to be kept for your generations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0738762b-d213-4e3f-a12c-12d9b7d1c1e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: EXO 16:34
Text: As the LORD commanded Moses, so Aaron laid it up before the Testimony, to be kept.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33bfa87f-0db4-4597-9ef8-30a5c9722780>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: EXO 16:35
Text: And the children of Israel did eat manna forty years, until they came to a land inhabited; they did eat manna, until they came unto the borders of the land of Canaan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/16/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e39d9a2-0d78-4c18-ba09-fc78910c656c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 70

Reference: EXO 16:36
Text: Now an omer is the tenth part of an ephah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/17/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b459231-9c22-4ac8-ac67-735115abadd0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: EXO 17:1
Text: And all the congregation of the children of Israel journeyed from the wilderness of Sin, after their journeys, according to the commandment of the LORD, and pitched in Rephidim: and there was no water for the people to drink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/17/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2913ce64-f7be-4a3c-8de7-9b06862b7757>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: EXO 17:2
Text: Wherefore the people did chide with Moses, and said, Give us water that we may drink. And Moses said unto them, Why chide ye with me? wherefore do ye tempt the LORD?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/17/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48f41f81-c8d9-4009-accb-95b4b6944641>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: EXO 17:3
Text: And the people thirsted there for water; and the people murmured against Moses, and said, Wherefore is this that thou hast brought us up out of Egypt, to kill us and our children and our cattle with thirst?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/17/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56ca5cb9-d71c-4ab9-bdd3-82c8b0ece072>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: EXO 17:4
Text: And Moses cried unto the LORD, saying, What shall I do unto this people? they be almost ready to stone me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/17/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ebd556e-e5f8-4ca9-86e3-f83d5be3a129>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: EXO 17:5
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Go on before the people, and take with thee of the elders of Israel; and thy rod, wherewith thou smotest the river, take in thine hand, and go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/17/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ad0429d-49b8-4837-9723-ac08ff31de51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: EXO 17:6
Text: Behold, I will stand before thee there upon the rock in Horeb; and thou shalt smite the rock, and there shall come water out of it, that the people may drink. And Moses did so in the sight of the elders of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/17/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8fe6d2ad-fb02-4880-8359-35fb66045e08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: EXO 17:7
Text: And he called the name of the place Massah, and Meribah, because of the chiding of the children of Israel, and because they tempted the LORD, saying, Is the LORD among us, or not?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/17/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55b3a60f-4edd-4971-b2c2-8ca4602543c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: EXO 17:8
Text: Then came Amalek, and fought with Israel in Rephidim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/17/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71c8d4f3-c262-4566-9bba-a7db29c694cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: EXO 17:9
Text: And Moses said unto Joshua, Choose us out men, and go out, fight with Amalek: to morrow I will stand on the top of the hill with the rod of God in mine hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/17/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee1c342d-9900-4aeb-b74f-5159bc1ce81b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: EXO 17:10
Text: So Joshua did as Moses had said to him, and fought with Amalek: and Moses, Aaron, and Hur went up to the top of the hill.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/17/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fcf3a47f-da94-4ad4-ac2f-b134984ee3b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: EXO 17:11
Text: And it came to pass, when Moses held up his hand, that Israel prevailed: and when he let down his hand, Amalek prevailed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/17/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae8c5d60-bfc4-4ed1-9887-84b990cef49e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 279

Reference: EXO 17:12
Text: But Moses’ hands were heavy; and they took a stone, and put it under him, and he sat thereon; and Aaron and Hur stayed up his hands, the one on the one side, and the other on the other side; and his hands were steady until the going down of the sun.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/17/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ce2c799-63c6-4bb1-a92d-8481f93586c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: EXO 17:13
Text: And Joshua discomfited Amalek and his people with the edge of the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/17/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43a34fdc-e3d8-494a-ad87-664a09f2415e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: EXO 17:14
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Write this for a memorial in a book, and rehearse it in the ears of Joshua: for I will utterly put out the remembrance of Amalek from under heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/17/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20e4d2db-cc7e-4753-a0b6-934febf2c2d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: EXO 17:15
Text: And Moses built an altar, and called the name of it Jehovahnissi:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/17/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad61a169-ffb4-4aee-aaf4-d92d794dcc4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: EXO 17:16
Text: For he said, Because the LORD hath sworn that the LORD will have war with Amalek from generation to generation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:619fed07-4b43-4a69-bb4e-836f674e7d2f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: EXO 18:1
Text: When Jethro, the priest of Midian, Moses’ father in law, heard of all that God had done for Moses, and for Israel his people, and that the LORD had brought Israel out of Egypt;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70dcad33-161d-4248-a4cb-2a1d72d5a89b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: EXO 18:2
Text: Then Jethro, Moses’ father in law, took Zipporah, Moses’ wife, after he had sent her back,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be2e386a-e8e4-4b38-83c4-5ae252a4de7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: EXO 18:3
Text: And her two sons; of which the name of the one was Gershom; for he said, I have been an alien in a strange land:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8b19d83-5e3f-4d32-bbe2-9768a3577b5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: EXO 18:4
Text: And the name of the other was Eliezer; for the God of my father, said he, was mine help, and delivered me from the sword of Pharaoh:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f9d1fb1-9d3d-4f29-910e-bf49a2a98ff4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: EXO 18:5
Text: And Jethro, Moses’ father in law, came with his sons and his wife unto Moses into the wilderness, where he encamped at the mount of God:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60b81dbb-8cf6-42bb-a9b6-6373a012d3fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: EXO 18:6
Text: And he said unto Moses, I thy father in law Jethro am come unto thee, and thy wife, and her two sons with her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8e26402-46d9-4b67-979f-1bb64c20f2af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: EXO 18:7
Text: And Moses went out to meet his father in law, and did obeisance, and kissed him; and they asked each other of their welfare; and they came into the tent.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09472f91-cfe6-48c9-a461-c2d0e05a4d64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: EXO 18:8
Text: And Moses told his father in law all that the LORD had done unto Pharaoh and to the Egyptians for Israel’s sake, and all the travail that had come upon them by the way, and how the LORD delivered them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:416c3f79-60f5-4286-8cd3-67bbed6bb807>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EXO 18:9
Text: And Jethro rejoiced for all the goodness which the LORD had done to Israel, whom he had delivered out of the hand of the Egyptians.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0955f16-9143-4d46-a1ef-5d71275ac27b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: EXO 18:10
Text: And Jethro said, Blessed be the LORD, who hath delivered you out of the hand of the Egyptians, and out of the hand of Pharaoh, who hath delivered the people from under the hand of the Egyptians.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2429c356-abfa-4068-a30a-690336a4c3a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: EXO 18:11
Text: Now I know that the LORD is greater than all gods: for in the thing wherein they dealt proudly he was above them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:755e00fd-ba59-467f-8ecf-83f5ee829f75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: EXO 18:12
Text: And Jethro, Moses’ father in law, took a burnt offering and sacrifices for God: and Aaron came, and all the elders of Israel, to eat bread with Moses’ father in law before God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18f5d6cd-6353-4d1a-bbf1-b21de5b3e5cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: EXO 18:13
Text: And it came to pass on the morrow, that Moses sat to judge the people: and the people stood by Moses from the morning unto the evening.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec486b79-2090-453d-ac97-bd816be22edf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: EXO 18:14
Text: And when Moses’ father in law saw all that he did to the people, he said, What is this thing that thou doest to the people? why sittest thou thyself alone, and all the people stand by thee from morning unto even?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d59b198f-fe2d-44b8-bab4-e36a41e14b9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: EXO 18:15
Text: And Moses said unto his father in law, Because the people come unto me to enquire of God:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17f65324-fd42-4b23-88f6-8dfd2679eb20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: EXO 18:16
Text: When they have a matter, they come unto me; and I judge between one and another, and I do make them know the statutes of God, and his laws.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f07a9491-d407-44ed-afc4-ba3d7543dc6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: EXO 18:17
Text: And Moses’ father in law said unto him, The thing that thou doest is not good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:875ad2e6-5d65-46cf-bd29-04a4ebdf5b01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: EXO 18:18
Text: Thou wilt surely wear away, both thou, and this people that is with thee: for this thing is too heavy for thee; thou art not able to perform it thyself alone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c37a240c-6a62-43f0-9e63-941042e1cf51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: EXO 18:19
Text: Hearken now unto my voice, I will give thee counsel, and God shall be with thee: Be thou for the people to God-ward, that thou mayest bring the causes unto God:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aac3a44b-e274-4c17-9e2d-263e4c435b36>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EXO 18:20
Text: And thou shalt teach them ordinances and laws, and shalt shew them the way wherein they must walk, and the work that they must do.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7006d10-37a0-41ef-8830-473004493289>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: EXO 18:21
Text: Moreover thou shalt provide out of all the people able men, such as fear God, men of truth, hating covetousness; and place such over them, to be rulers of thousands, and rulers of hundreds, rulers of fifties, and rulers of tens:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:358c52c7-d5f8-40b5-ba53-424d5f2df763>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: EXO 18:22
Text: And let them judge the people at all seasons: and it shall be, that every great matter they shall bring unto thee, but every small matter they shall judge: so shall it be easier for thyself, and they shall bear the burden with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc6cc66a-ad44-4a84-bb87-8856f89bf3c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: EXO 18:23
Text: If thou shalt do this thing, and God command thee so, then thou shalt be able to endure, and all this people shall also go to their place in peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:153f4368-d5e5-46d8-92af-1f994fb1ade0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: EXO 18:24
Text: So Moses hearkened to the voice of his father in law, and did all that he had said.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12a592be-c822-47fd-98e1-21b188319c20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: EXO 18:25
Text: And Moses chose able men out of all Israel, and made them heads over the people, rulers of thousands, rulers of hundreds, rulers of fifties, and rulers of tens.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:607fc875-05f5-4223-9964-6d2096fb197d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EXO 18:26
Text: And they judged the people at all seasons: the hard causes they brought unto Moses, but every small matter they judged themselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/18/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51e71394-cf8e-4fd1-8be0-bdb4908279e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: EXO 18:27
Text: And Moses let his father in law depart; and he went his way into his own land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13797abc-d6d5-496d-9aea-a3643dcba9e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: EXO 19:1
Text: In the third month, when the children of Israel were gone forth out of the land of Egypt, the same day came they into the wilderness of Sinai.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48dc7221-e252-432a-b0b1-05068f1a2562>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: EXO 19:2
Text: For they were departed from Rephidim, and were come to the desert of Sinai, and had pitched in the wilderness; and there Israel camped before the mount.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d05f3406-e436-4236-b3eb-6da7151d18e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: EXO 19:3
Text: And Moses went up unto God, and the LORD called unto him out of the mountain, saying, Thus shalt thou say to the house of Jacob, and tell the children of Israel;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c45517e-697c-4e1d-b142-b3f2b13b1e7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: EXO 19:4
Text: Ye have seen what I did unto the Egyptians, and how I bare you on eagles’ wings, and brought you unto myself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac6c1c1d-6c45-4545-a665-cbfaee42a8d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: EXO 19:5
Text: Now therefore, if ye will obey my voice indeed, and keep my covenant, then ye shall be a peculiar treasure unto me above all people: for all the earth is mine:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d58994d5-8777-49c3-9f79-829d1e19cc07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: EXO 19:6
Text: And ye shall be unto me a kingdom of priests, and an holy nation. These are the words which thou shalt speak unto the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5a62f21-2bc9-4730-999c-47df9fea3e09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: EXO 19:7
Text: And Moses came and called for the elders of the people, and laid before their faces all these words which the LORD commanded him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5dde3672-01d2-4f68-a510-8792bbabd801>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: EXO 19:8
Text: And all the people answered together, and said, All that the LORD hath spoken we will do. And Moses returned the words of the people unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91f701c9-8713-4a12-8a22-d3eac0f90662>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: EXO 19:9
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Lo, I come unto thee in a thick cloud, that the people may hear when I speak with thee, and believe thee for ever. And Moses told the words of the people unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f17308e6-5c54-477f-bc68-ea91c494d0f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: EXO 19:10
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Go unto the people, and sanctify them to day and to morrow, and let them wash their clothes,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b48dc6d4-78b4-401e-924c-da379bc16812>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: EXO 19:11
Text: And be ready against the third day: for the third day the LORD will come down in the sight of all the people upon mount Sinai.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f3a8a17-11b3-4962-930a-9c4f33384d5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: EXO 19:12
Text: And thou shalt set bounds unto the people round about, saying, Take heed to yourselves, that ye go not up into the mount, or touch the border of it: whosoever toucheth the mount shall be surely put to death:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07d33d0a-5fe0-4374-98c6-c22ba92b019e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: EXO 19:13
Text: There shall not an hand touch it, but he shall surely be stoned, or shot through; whether it be beast or man, it shall not live: when the trumpet soundeth long, they shall come up to the mount.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d947894f-5402-441e-b160-c4716fec3284>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: EXO 19:14
Text: And Moses went down from the mount unto the people, and sanctified the people; and they washed their clothes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad14ee2c-08b6-477a-abc8-d7b5726222af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: EXO 19:15
Text: And he said unto the people, Be ready against the third day: come not at your wives.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c502d25a-e52e-4478-9095-da0020950b29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: EXO 19:16
Text: And it came to pass on the third day in the morning, that there were thunders and lightnings, and a thick cloud upon the mount, and the voice of the trumpet exceeding loud; so that all the people that was in the camp trembled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35b7474e-58c1-4bb2-b00e-243eca32593a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: EXO 19:17
Text: And Moses brought forth the people out of the camp to meet with God; and they stood at the nether part of the mount.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4679d9f-31a8-46cb-b242-73d44165d5ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: EXO 19:18
Text: And mount Sinai was altogether on a smoke, because the LORD descended upon it in fire: and the smoke thereof ascended as the smoke of a furnace, and the whole mount quaked greatly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d833d91d-c3e7-4836-9487-50276e38a460>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: EXO 19:19
Text: And when the voice of the trumpet sounded long, and waxed louder and louder, Moses spake, and God answered him by a voice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91ef5835-b100-45dc-ab3b-67418c90785a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: EXO 19:20
Text: And the LORD came down upon mount Sinai, on the top of the mount: and the LORD called Moses up to the top of the mount; and Moses went up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83dbdd81-d710-457c-9197-061d7a546c44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EXO 19:21
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Go down, charge the people, lest they break through unto the LORD to gaze, and many of them perish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9be4828-a7fa-4e5f-80f0-9bbddbb78847>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: EXO 19:22
Text: And let the priests also, which come near to the LORD, sanctify themselves, lest the LORD break forth upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50d59056-c841-4550-adec-49c0c1eb0da8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: EXO 19:23
Text: And Moses said unto the LORD, The people cannot come up to mount Sinai: for thou chargedst us, saying, Set bounds about the mount, and sanctify it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d993f4b7-45e9-4249-b799-03803f389fb6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: EXO 19:24
Text: And the LORD said unto him, Away, get thee down, and thou shalt come up, thou, and Aaron with thee: but let not the priests and the people break through to come up unto the LORD, lest he break forth upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/19/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a77c28a5-8399-4785-92a1-0b8ecdbd74cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: EXO 19:25
Text: So Moses went down unto the people, and spake unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f7034b5-797f-4085-a30e-90cf762edcbf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 65

Reference: EXO 20:1
Text: And God spake all these words, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ae16d0e-df2b-4eda-b0aa-28b7250ec7b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: EXO 20:2
Text: I am the LORD thy God, which have brought thee out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of bondage.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:141a3c10-3b19-4fb5-8749-8f0cb7bdf94f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 67

Reference: EXO 20:3
Text: Thou shalt have no other gods before me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0808111b-3c35-432c-b7f8-47d94a7dd125>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: EXO 20:4
Text: Thou shalt not make unto thee any graven image, or any likeness of any thing that is in heaven above, or that is in the earth beneath, or that is in the water under the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e8f60df-4087-4549-b34a-96b8bf63e224>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: EXO 20:5
Text: Thou shalt not bow down thyself to them, nor serve them: for I the LORD thy God am a jealous God, visiting the iniquity of the fathers upon the children unto the third and fourth generation of them that hate me;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f90a74c-b241-48be-912b-0994870c83e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: EXO 20:6
Text: And shewing mercy unto thousands of them that love me, and keep my commandments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d49e0e7f-0124-4c90-82c8-10757855f215>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: EXO 20:7
Text: Thou shalt not take the name of the LORD thy God in vain; for the LORD will not hold him guiltless that taketh his name in vain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8cf60510-f4ff-4dee-8145-a4bb35c2f56d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 69

Reference: EXO 20:8
Text: Remember the sabbath day, to keep it holy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6c54842-c23d-4b75-91fb-fdb0c89651f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: EXO 20:9
Text: Six days shalt thou labour, and do all thy work:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fd2c795-ff70-4233-920b-4e80f216e986>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: EXO 20:10
Text: But the seventh day is the sabbath of the LORD thy God: in it thou shalt not do any work, thou, nor thy son, nor thy daughter, thy manservant, nor thy maidservant, nor thy cattle, nor thy stranger that is within thy gates:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4279164d-ac37-4585-989d-7c194574a32c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: EXO 20:11
Text: For in six days the LORD made heaven and earth, the sea, and all that in them is, and rested the seventh day: wherefore the LORD blessed the sabbath day, and hallowed it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff3934e0-94ff-4327-9783-ea9191737bb7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: EXO 20:12
Text: Honour thy father and thy mother: that thy days may be long upon the land which the LORD thy God giveth thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
