WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9fa8c64-006a-4233-a685-3c45cbb5b92f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 59

Reference: EXO 20:14
Text: Thou shalt not commit adultery.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d06b7c1-bfcb-46e6-b8fb-224abbf4c322>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 49

Reference: EXO 20:15
Text: Thou shalt not steal.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db18e3b7-4837-4be8-88ba-d1f0901f48ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: EXO 20:16
Text: Thou shalt not bear false witness against thy neighbour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7af0426e-a387-43f5-ae61-52cd616da7f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: EXO 20:17
Text: Thou shalt not covet thy neighbour’s house, thou shalt not covet thy neighbour’s wife, nor his manservant, nor his maidservant, nor his ox, nor his ass, nor any thing that is thy neighbour’s.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd2cc68f-1071-4f5f-9ab2-99b1032c08e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: EXO 20:18
Text: And all the people saw the thunderings, and the lightnings, and the noise of the trumpet, and the mountain smoking: and when the people saw it, they removed, and stood afar off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f66b12e-acb7-4c39-8700-b1fc49743dab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: EXO 20:19
Text: And they said unto Moses, Speak thou with us, and we will hear: but let not God speak with us, lest we die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95a052df-f6a6-4548-8a5c-b97624f6b7da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EXO 20:20
Text: And Moses said unto the people, Fear not: for God is come to prove you, and that his fear may be before your faces, that ye sin not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85f01a9b-209d-4c87-84ab-01ec647088ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: EXO 20:21
Text: And the people stood afar off, and Moses drew near unto the thick darkness where God was.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2e8c13e-8910-4c08-b7ac-922f871be09e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EXO 20:22
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Thus thou shalt say unto the children of Israel, Ye have seen that I have talked with you from heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf626915-329b-463f-b455-e1c8a5995c58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: EXO 20:23
Text: Ye shall not make with me gods of silver, neither shall ye make unto you gods of gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf2a8664-63ad-4b27-a960-c521f7a3c1f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: EXO 20:24
Text: An altar of earth thou shalt make unto me, and shalt sacrifice thereon thy burnt offerings, and thy peace offerings, thy sheep, and thine oxen: in all places where I record my name I will come unto thee, and I will bless thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3481b073-430d-45fc-be76-84fea7ef3755>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: EXO 20:25
Text: And if thou wilt make me an altar of stone, thou shalt not build it of hewn stone: for if thou lift up thy tool upon it, thou hast polluted it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/20/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c592e9c1-bb28-4c0a-baac-33e6030fdad9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: EXO 20:26
Text: Neither shalt thou go up by steps unto mine altar, that thy nakedness be not discovered thereon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:610b0a8c-5598-4081-bfb7-7c339d4b1222>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: EXO 21:1
Text: Now these are the judgments which thou shalt set before them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c699e39-7b6c-481f-b3f6-c9ab699845c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: EXO 21:2
Text: If thou buy an Hebrew servant, six years he shall serve: and in the seventh he shall go out free for nothing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7d43cda-135f-4f42-b2fe-fc050e71ce92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: EXO 21:3
Text: If he came in by himself, he shall go out by himself: if he were married, then his wife shall go out with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04767f7b-a5e1-4533-91fc-57a5d0602b8e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: EXO 21:4
Text: If his master have given him a wife, and she have born him sons or daughters; the wife and her children shall be her master’s, and he shall go out by himself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e537629-9143-4db1-b272-57e562557324>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: EXO 21:5
Text: And if the servant shall plainly say, I love my master, my wife, and my children; I will not go out free:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30cb4142-abe3-4d16-a3cc-47292b94c053>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: EXO 21:6
Text: Then his master shall bring him unto the judges; he shall also bring him to the door, or unto the door post; and his master shall bore his ear through with an aul; and he shall serve him for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cbdc118-5514-4953-8f2a-e5b3c9aff376>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: EXO 21:7
Text: And if a man sell his daughter to be a maidservant, she shall not go out as the menservants do.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c0a5613-5b17-4a02-9b60-e9bd8cdb8eeb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: EXO 21:8
Text: If she please not her master, who hath betrothed her to himself, then shall he let her be redeemed: to sell her unto a strange nation he shall have no power, seeing he hath dealt deceitfully with her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:686e82a4-12c1-40f3-abc7-984926c5d352>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: EXO 21:9
Text: And if he have betrothed her unto his son, he shall deal with her after the manner of daughters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66c227a9-67af-47d5-9d9d-4b47ee831da5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: EXO 21:10
Text: If he take him another wife; her food, her raiment, and her duty of marriage, shall he not diminish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:883fe653-e23d-4502-9404-dfa856d9881c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: EXO 21:11
Text: And if he do not these three unto her, then shall she go out free without money.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38ae9c36-6b08-4440-b7f8-d9e5ce5cff40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: EXO 21:12
Text: He that smiteth a man, so that he die, shall be surely put to death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6403350e-cbad-4a9a-85cb-915286086675>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: EXO 21:13
Text: And if a man lie not in wait, but God deliver him into his hand; then I will appoint thee a place whither he shall flee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e07e7da-6c3f-46f3-9b57-53eb725b08b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EXO 21:14
Text: But if a man come presumptuously upon his neighbour, to slay him with guile; thou shalt take him from mine altar, that he may die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f736aec-3a20-4173-9a23-22413e1c5b87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: EXO 21:15
Text: And he that smiteth his father, or his mother, shall be surely put to death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c04716f-47fe-441b-92e3-e0c2f4c41343>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: EXO 21:16
Text: And he that stealeth a man, and selleth him, or if he be found in his hand, he shall surely be put to death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ab79c9a-8454-44f2-a649-245affcec31c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: EXO 21:17
Text: And he that curseth his father, or his mother, shall surely be put to death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8d4e7d1-6985-4e12-a812-263a0e9014be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: EXO 21:18
Text: And if men strive together, and one smite another with a stone, or with his fist, and he die not, but keepeth his bed:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a31ec18-a180-4ef2-b5b5-8b6addb0778b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: EXO 21:19
Text: If he rise again, and walk abroad upon his staff, then shall he that smote him be quit: only he shall pay for the loss of his time, and shall cause him to be thoroughly healed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6104294-8f3e-4dcf-b833-d26309c6b9c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: EXO 21:20
Text: And if a man smite his servant, or his maid, with a rod, and he die under his hand; he shall be surely punished.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8cc2fe5-cc32-46dd-904d-8137d176a71d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: EXO 21:21
Text: Notwithstanding, if he continue a day or two, he shall not be punished: for he is his money.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5d4c948-1715-42da-9df9-06321df224b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: EXO 21:22
Text: If men strive, and hurt a woman with child, so that her fruit depart from her, and yet no mischief follow: he shall be surely punished, according as the woman’s husband will lay upon him; and he shall pay as the judges determine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fe81cf4-5ce4-4f06-8e81-de55d32c3c30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: EXO 21:23
Text: And if any mischief follow, then thou shalt give life for life,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:613394ad-b00a-4265-9d32-8fe9ba670432>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: EXO 21:24
Text: Eye for eye, tooth for tooth, hand for hand, foot for foot,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:254d477f-6b14-44e8-a0dd-e8778187c3a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: EXO 21:25
Text: Burning for burning, wound for wound, stripe for stripe.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31bd7511-e22a-4ef1-bc88-fa4018673119>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EXO 21:26
Text: And if a man smite the eye of his servant, or the eye of his maid, that it perish; he shall let him go free for his eye’s sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8907226b-5a33-444f-83da-8f5598ab7a40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: EXO 21:27
Text: And if he smite out his manservant’s tooth, or his maidservant’s tooth; he shall let him go free for his tooth’s sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cde4c7c8-6002-45ed-99f1-f5d3cbfec336>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: EXO 21:28
Text: If an ox gore a man or a woman, that they die: then the ox shall be surely stoned, and his flesh shall not be eaten; but the owner of the ox shall be quit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6500fcb9-6ac5-44a0-805f-cf4198b0bff7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: EXO 21:29
Text: But if the ox were wont to push with his horn in time past, and it hath been testified to his owner, and he hath not kept him in, but that he hath killed a man or a woman; the ox shall be stoned, and his owner also shall be put to death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a8805ec-ff14-45eb-afb2-2beb3900cd5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: EXO 21:30
Text: If there be laid on him a sum of money, then he shall give for the ransom of his life whatsoever is laid upon him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b3d6701-4750-4f97-b4db-ec465659fec5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: EXO 21:31
Text: Whether he have gored a son, or have gored a daughter, according to this judgment shall it be done unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:940833bf-74b1-4aec-a072-7b28b821f4f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: EXO 21:32
Text: If the ox shall push a manservant or a maidservant; he shall give unto their master thirty shekels of silver, and the ox shall be stoned.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1dbd60c2-bba8-4396-a7f5-a49981016469>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: EXO 21:33
Text: And if a man shall open a pit, or if a man shall dig a pit, and not cover it, and an ox or an ass fall therein;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a93a1fa9-d98f-4ca3-8b7d-0d6989e2d742>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: EXO 21:34
Text: The owner of the pit shall make it good, and give money unto the owner of them; and the dead beast shall be his.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e19d2ac8-1c38-4728-a5c8-7751de790f3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: EXO 21:35
Text: And if one man’s ox hurt another’s, that he die; then they shall sell the live ox, and divide the money of it; and the dead ox also they shall divide.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/21/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd2cd2d4-c3ea-4e7d-acf5-0a6eaa10dcd9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: EXO 21:36
Text: Or if it be known that the ox hath used to push in time past, and his owner hath not kept him in; he shall surely pay ox for ox; and the dead shall be his own.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9240f21f-e7cd-482c-abcc-49afd9404f99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EXO 22:1
Text: If a man shall steal an ox, or a sheep, and kill it, or sell it; he shall restore five oxen for an ox, and four sheep for a sheep.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:397aa53d-960b-423c-b7ad-0b105f6333e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: EXO 22:2
Text: If a thief be found breaking up, and be smitten that he die, there shall no blood be shed for him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90a3716e-736b-482e-93b9-cc7335121cf3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: EXO 22:3
Text: If the sun be risen upon him, there shall be blood shed for him; for he should make full restitution; if he have nothing, then he shall be sold for his theft.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a633c170-d612-44c8-983b-f7415ad46082>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: EXO 22:4
Text: If the theft be certainly found in his hand alive, whether it be ox, or ass, or sheep; he shall restore double.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc1a3b8a-fb6e-486e-80e3-238d35fde9ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: EXO 22:5
Text: If a man shall cause a field or vineyard to be eaten, and shall put in his beast, and shall feed in another man’s field; of the best of his own field, and of the best of his own vineyard, shall he make restitution.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:665d0afc-9a44-4135-82b8-4124508241c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: EXO 22:6
Text: If fire break out, and catch in thorns, so that the stacks of corn, or the standing corn, or the field, be consumed therewith; he that kindled the fire shall surely make restitution.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48a57d5b-5f01-4d2a-8e55-20ebad507b44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: EXO 22:7
Text: If a man shall deliver unto his neighbour money or stuff to keep, and it be stolen out of the man’s house; if the thief be found, let him pay double.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edb7dedb-b81f-4367-ba08-f9674fd92717>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: EXO 22:8
Text: If the thief be not found, then the master of the house shall be brought unto the judges, to see whether he have put his hand unto his neighbour’s goods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19737ebd-8133-46ed-94da-2458c809b2d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 309

Reference: EXO 22:9
Text: For all manner of trespass, whether it be for ox, for ass, for sheep, for raiment, or for any manner of lost thing which another challengeth to be his, the cause of both parties shall come before the judges; and whom the judges shall condemn, he shall pay double unto his neighbour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:954fea28-4ab3-4d8b-ae9e-1291f612c980>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: EXO 22:10
Text: If a man deliver unto his neighbour an ass, or an ox, or a sheep, or any beast, to keep; and it die, or be hurt, or driven away, no man seeing it:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9902179-bd69-4749-8ec6-1749a12e66b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: EXO 22:11
Text: Then shall an oath of the LORD be between them both, that he hath not put his hand unto his neighbour’s goods; and the owner of it shall accept thereof, and he shall not make it good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f30bf9a2-afb3-4eba-9532-266685954307>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: EXO 22:12
Text: And if it be stolen from him, he shall make restitution unto the owner thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60d6bb3a-ff39-49ea-8a8f-441f24c21892>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: EXO 22:13
Text: If it be torn in pieces, then let him bring it for witness, and he shall not make good that which was torn.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6ddbd04-a095-440b-8659-6c8d0871c398>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: EXO 22:14
Text: And if a man borrow ought of his neighbour, and it be hurt, or die, the owner thereof being not with it, he shall surely make it good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db46e36d-f307-4e5a-8212-4ceb10bc70b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: EXO 22:15
Text: But if the owner thereof be with it, he shall not make it good: if it be an hired thing, it came for his hire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5d65f79-e950-4457-aa42-67e974a4d832>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: EXO 22:16
Text: And if a man entice a maid that is not betrothed, and lie with her, he shall surely endow her to be his wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7576592-337b-4a96-a3d5-6f9dcb20f78a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: EXO 22:17
Text: If her father utterly refuse to give her unto him, he shall pay money according to the dowry of virgins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30edfccd-525a-48cf-bb90-b46fae71a404>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 66

Reference: EXO 22:18
Text: Thou shalt not suffer a witch to live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d65d3ac-3d40-466a-9cb6-20246e821f99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: EXO 22:19
Text: Whosoever lieth with a beast shall surely be put to death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ea896d9-5a92-4bad-89fa-312f3cc46528>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: EXO 22:20
Text: He that sacrificeth unto any god, save unto the LORD only, he shall be utterly destroyed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd22f53d-180c-4eab-b0f9-aaa0a0a19be1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: EXO 22:21
Text: Thou shalt neither vex a stranger, nor oppress him: for ye were strangers in the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:feb6d016-38d1-49cb-9756-1a9a87525f52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: EXO 22:22
Text: Ye shall not afflict any widow, or fatherless child.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dec987d1-280f-40d9-884f-ea08b2009a9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: EXO 22:23
Text: If thou afflict them in any wise, and they cry at all unto me, I will surely hear their cry;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:261ba3a6-4f59-40ab-a9bf-5089bade9608>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: EXO 22:24
Text: And my wrath shall wax hot, and I will kill you with the sword; and your wives shall be widows, and your children fatherless.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97c29946-c06b-4b51-836b-f323b17a0368>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: EXO 22:25
Text: If thou lend money to any of my people that is poor by thee, thou shalt not be to him as an usurer, neither shalt thou lay upon him usury.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:204c744c-46ff-45c5-a695-978a7875404b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: EXO 22:26
Text: If thou at all take thy neighbour’s raiment to pledge, thou shalt deliver it unto him by that the sun goeth down:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9adc374-6d10-49ae-b58d-d80abe5a184e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: EXO 22:27
Text: For that is his covering only, it is his raiment for his skin: wherein shall he sleep? and it shall come to pass, when he crieth unto me, that I will hear; for I am gracious.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e24e9a6-6a8f-476c-886a-36577a865527>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: EXO 22:28
Text: Thou shalt not revile the gods, nor curse the ruler of thy people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c79fc90-c83d-40d4-b0a8-c51b726a62c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EXO 22:29
Text: Thou shalt not delay to offer the first of thy ripe fruits, and of thy liquors: the firstborn of thy sons shalt thou give unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec0ff2fd-9d44-4afa-b075-528f48b89216>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: EXO 22:30
Text: Likewise shalt thou do with thine oxen, and with thy sheep: seven days it shall be with his dam; on the eighth day thou shalt give it me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/22/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24b4f08e-c628-4cbd-afd9-e784d025d215>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: EXO 22:31
Text: And ye shall be holy men unto me: neither shall ye eat any flesh that is torn of beasts in the field; ye shall cast it to the dogs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05b049b9-ca8d-4a33-9a0d-41bce7316062>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: EXO 23:1
Text: Thou shalt not raise a false report: put not thine hand with the wicked to be an unrighteous witness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b810c09-e21d-488c-9b32-e4413a4d6251>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: EXO 23:2
Text: Thou shalt not follow a multitude to do evil; neither shalt thou speak in a cause to decline after many to wrest judgment:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fd68f60-ff08-47b7-a26c-d790472e798e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: EXO 23:3
Text: Neither shalt thou countenance a poor man in his cause.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a35588ba-2342-4b6d-8569-31b3b98c0002>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: EXO 23:4
Text: If thou meet thine enemy’s ox or his ass going astray, thou shalt surely bring it back to him again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8c6d339-d3b4-4e85-ad84-6d8911fbc603>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: EXO 23:5
Text: If thou see the ass of him that hateth thee lying under his burden, and wouldest forbear to help him, thou shalt surely help with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07c41200-f588-4b07-a9e2-4c9efa98998b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: EXO 23:6
Text: Thou shalt not wrest the judgment of thy poor in his cause.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:106aaa06-37bf-4aef-be46-4e2fa189cc3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: EXO 23:7
Text: Keep thee far from a false matter; and the innocent and righteous slay thou not: for I will not justify the wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:692848e6-0849-424c-97fd-e3cc3d0c97b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: EXO 23:8
Text: And thou shalt take no gift: for the gift blindeth the wise, and perverteth the words of the righteous.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ebbbd08-f109-4ad4-a979-457aa835f516>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: EXO 23:9
Text: Also thou shalt not oppress a stranger: for ye know the heart of a stranger, seeing ye were strangers in the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e9b77a4-c813-4a87-8501-05cc25753af2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: EXO 23:10
Text: And six years thou shalt sow thy land, and shalt gather in the fruits thereof:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6417e734-72e6-4b2f-a446-a968f136c98d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: EXO 23:11
Text: But the seventh year thou shalt let it rest and lie still; that the poor of thy people may eat: and what they leave the beasts of the field shall eat. In like manner thou shalt deal with thy vineyard, and with thy oliveyard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b24683df-aeae-41f4-9dc7-51f4e2a80221>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: EXO 23:12
Text: Six days thou shalt do thy work, and on the seventh day thou shalt rest: that thine ox and thine ass may rest, and the son of thy handmaid, and the stranger, may be refreshed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f047c66-7349-475f-928d-4d6892a4966f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: EXO 23:13
Text: And in all things that I have said unto you be circumspect: and make no mention of the name of other gods, neither let it be heard out of thy mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1f73d42-da34-497a-94fc-444da7603e48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: EXO 23:14
Text: Three times thou shalt keep a feast unto me in the year.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea1fd7c1-8d3d-4c8e-8390-4f51ee0018e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: EXO 23:15
Text: Thou shalt keep the feast of unleavened bread: (thou shalt eat unleavened bread seven days, as I commanded thee, in the time appointed of the month Abib; for in it thou camest out from Egypt: and none shall appear before me empty:)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0426ba6-41d1-4831-957b-c39b1a094072>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: EXO 23:16
Text: And the feast of harvest, the firstfruits of thy labours, which thou hast sown in the field: and the feast of ingathering, which is in the end of the year, when thou hast gathered in thy labours out of the field.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5497d6de-bd2f-40db-aa57-e25982ab57d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: EXO 23:17
Text: Three times in the year all thy males shall appear before the LORD God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55efb3f9-5580-46af-9b7f-156fe14f00b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: EXO 23:18
Text: Thou shalt not offer the blood of my sacrifice with leavened bread; neither shall the fat of my sacrifice remain until the morning.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26935d28-9cd2-49ed-8fa1-b61e4f722056>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: EXO 23:19
Text: The first of the firstfruits of thy land thou shalt bring into the house of the LORD thy God. Thou shalt not seethe a kid in his mother’s milk.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e57c6c5a-ed9e-4eea-a198-f7174e004c0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: EXO 23:20
Text: Behold, I send an Angel before thee, to keep thee in the way, and to bring thee into the place which I have prepared.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3713519-d11e-489f-90d1-7c4d79475801>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: EXO 23:21
Text: Beware of him, and obey his voice, provoke him not; for he will not pardon your transgressions: for my name is in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db91d953-5113-4074-9296-9b4332c997c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: EXO 23:22
Text: But if thou shalt indeed obey his voice, and do all that I speak; then I will be an enemy unto thine enemies, and an adversary unto thine adversaries.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51f438b6-2797-4a03-8dac-f1e73dcdbce3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: EXO 23:23
Text: For mine Angel shall go before thee, and bring thee in unto the Amorites, and the Hittites, and the Perizzites, and the Canaanites, the Hivites, and the Jebusites: and I will cut them off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a79deaf4-71b2-4c09-be7b-c161d25387c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: EXO 23:24
Text: Thou shalt not bow down to their gods, nor serve them, nor do after their works: but thou shalt utterly overthrow them, and quite break down their images.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb8e79f5-9682-486d-8a73-d9dd9d71caa5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: EXO 23:25
Text: And ye shall serve the LORD your God, and he shall bless thy bread, and thy water; and I will take sickness away from the midst of thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acc4b5f2-5f00-4114-9138-43e9ab30f180>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: EXO 23:26
Text: There shall nothing cast their young, nor be barren, in thy land: the number of thy days I will fulfil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:072142d2-acf4-4a25-b8e2-b132e95307d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: EXO 23:27
Text: I will send my fear before thee, and will destroy all the people to whom thou shalt come, and I will make all thine enemies turn their backs unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1dd57247-6e59-4cf9-9be4-4b9292c1ad90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: EXO 23:28
Text: And I will send hornets before thee, which shall drive out the Hivite, the Canaanite, and the Hittite, from before thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a49e0af-799e-46ca-86b3-03e9e4c685cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: EXO 23:29
Text: I will not drive them out from before thee in one year; lest the land become desolate, and the beast of the field multiply against thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f83d64c7-d174-4823-9a03-f55b5a0510d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: EXO 23:30
Text: By little and little I will drive them out from before thee, until thou be increased, and inherit the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8eaced8d-d078-4a32-9747-0198d7c80587>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: EXO 23:31
Text: And I will set thy bounds from the Red sea even unto the sea of the Philistines, and from the desert unto the river: for I will deliver the inhabitants of the land into your hand; and thou shalt drive them out before thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:918d7336-8485-47ea-b37e-e0e485a18002>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: EXO 23:32
Text: Thou shalt make no covenant with them, nor with their gods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/23/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3faffed9-3c81-478e-b10a-1bfa59f6646b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: EXO 23:33
Text: They shall not dwell in thy land, lest they make thee sin against me: for if thou serve their gods, it will surely be a snare unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/24/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d3434b3-e1e6-4880-9dc0-b9f1cca20895>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: EXO 24:1
Text: And he said unto Moses, Come up unto the LORD, thou, and Aaron, Nadab, and Abihu, and seventy of the elders of Israel; and worship ye afar off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/24/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20a49236-6679-41e4-a2e0-748ed63018d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: EXO 24:2
Text: And Moses alone shall come near the LORD: but they shall not come nigh; neither shall the people go up with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/24/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60c41102-bb8d-493e-94ed-a6fbaf08061b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: EXO 24:3
Text: And Moses came and told the people all the words of the LORD, and all the judgments: and all the people answered with one voice, and said, All the words which the LORD hath said will we do.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/24/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd2912d0-7225-4790-bc2b-b9ae9bf1c38e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: EXO 24:4
Text: And Moses wrote all the words of the LORD, and rose up early in the morning, and builded an altar under the hill, and twelve pillars, according to the twelve tribes of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/24/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed6d8bb4-a336-46a9-b360-dd9b5359017d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EXO 24:5
Text: And he sent young men of the children of Israel, which offered burnt offerings, and sacrificed peace offerings of oxen unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/24/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1872215-7146-400d-a86a-7171560a77b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: EXO 24:6
Text: And Moses took half of the blood, and put it in basons; and half of the blood he sprinkled on the altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/24/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e38337a0-bba3-4b07-b43c-bbac3c8e8057>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: EXO 24:7
Text: And he took the book of the covenant, and read in the audience of the people: and they said, All that the LORD hath said will we do, and be obedient.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/24/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0976552d-b130-4efe-a5f3-eb1060929f45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: EXO 24:8
Text: And Moses took the blood, and sprinkled it on the people, and said, Behold the blood of the covenant, which the LORD hath made with you concerning all these words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/24/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:847a9ad4-fa36-4979-8872-49bbc359a1cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: EXO 24:9
Text: Then went up Moses, and Aaron, Nadab, and Abihu, and seventy of the elders of Israel:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/24/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0fedcc26-5468-4d45-87b4-7f75ab7473be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: EXO 24:10
Text: And they saw the God of Israel: and there was under his feet as it were a paved work of a sapphire stone, and as it were the body of heaven in his clearness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/24/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75801c7a-a287-470c-a8c6-db4747d763ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: EXO 24:11
Text: And upon the nobles of the children of Israel he laid not his hand: also they saw God, and did eat and drink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/24/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53711fa4-8414-446b-8961-202eb4f13762>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: EXO 24:12
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Come up to me into the mount, and be there: and I will give thee tables of stone, and a law, and commandments which I have written; that thou mayest teach them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/24/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c7c7746-9b6d-41d1-a1c0-764f45aa03e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: EXO 24:13
Text: And Moses rose up, and his minister Joshua: and Moses went up into the mount of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/24/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:991773ec-78e6-41e0-ae7b-ed3423f1e057>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: EXO 24:14
Text: And he said unto the elders, Tarry ye here for us, until we come again unto you: and, behold, Aaron and Hur are with you: if any man have any matters to do, let him come unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/24/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4aa411d-5b50-4b97-9b61-fab61895503f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: EXO 24:15
Text: And Moses went up into the mount, and a cloud covered the mount.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/24/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f72967e-e4e1-4fea-bdbf-3b9914706d5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: EXO 24:16
Text: And the glory of the LORD abode upon mount Sinai, and the cloud covered it six days: and the seventh day he called unto Moses out of the midst of the cloud.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/24/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7525fdd-fc5c-4042-8128-5aa06a229269>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: EXO 24:17
Text: And the sight of the glory of the LORD was like devouring fire on the top of the mount in the eyes of the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/24/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d37c21f-f74a-464b-9a2c-423d6b862c10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EXO 24:18
Text: And Moses went into the midst of the cloud, and gat him up into the mount: and Moses was in the mount forty days and forty nights.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9a8e5c5-a8fe-4c29-b99b-186bc410fe37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 65

Reference: EXO 25:1
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63771944-9b3e-4f80-a9f2-697f96ab163a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: EXO 25:2
Text: Speak unto the children of Israel, that they bring me an offering: of every man that giveth it willingly with his heart ye shall take my offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05bbd986-ae2f-4bc3-9830-fd6e3deaf00b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: EXO 25:3
Text: And this is the offering which ye shall take of them; gold, and silver, and brass,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41221a34-cfee-45dc-8162-edefd3823633>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: EXO 25:4
Text: And blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine linen, and goats’ hair,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83217651-dd4b-4c8c-b9da-6634238e3317>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: EXO 25:5
Text: And rams’ skins dyed red, and badgers’ skins, and shittim wood,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2dc88002-35cc-4ed5-a3a1-65859e6d2b08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: EXO 25:6
Text: Oil for the light, spices for anointing oil, and for sweet incense,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5906b24-c025-4c8b-85a5-9685af2f0a9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: EXO 25:7
Text: Onyx stones, and stones to be set in the ephod, and in the breastplate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76398c18-dc89-4b22-ac35-b4445a21c2d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: EXO 25:8
Text: And let them make me a sanctuary; that I may dwell among them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb942e7a-9ff5-4da2-b609-cbc7a1350075>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: EXO 25:9
Text: According to all that I shew thee, after the pattern of the tabernacle, and the pattern of all the instruments thereof, even so shall ye make it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fb994e7-008e-4e17-b1be-4785a1ffa7ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: EXO 25:10
Text: And they shall make an ark of shittim wood: two cubits and a half shall be the length thereof, and a cubit and a half the breadth thereof, and a cubit and a half the height thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3eea774-5033-46e9-8407-034dfb0f934f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: EXO 25:11
Text: And thou shalt overlay it with pure gold, within and without shalt thou overlay it, and shalt make upon it a crown of gold round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44a32709-62bb-433c-a9ad-474254008629>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: EXO 25:12
Text: And thou shalt cast four rings of gold for it, and put them in the four corners thereof; and two rings shall be in the one side of it, and two rings in the other side of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:556d99ca-82c1-4128-9ac6-26defcffe338>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: EXO 25:13
Text: And thou shalt make staves of shittim wood, and overlay them with gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c825e5d1-8026-44ef-aba6-d5b0f0644234>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: EXO 25:14
Text: And thou shalt put the staves into the rings by the sides of the ark, that the ark may be borne with them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bdff5d4c-173c-4227-8958-ac3561bb6685>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: EXO 25:15
Text: The staves shall be in the rings of the ark: they shall not be taken from it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7bababb5-9fb5-449e-9956-009e18e27df8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: EXO 25:16
Text: And thou shalt put into the ark the testimony which I shall give thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ecd3560-1a18-4426-97ab-82f91216c340>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: EXO 25:17
Text: And thou shalt make a mercy seat of pure gold: two cubits and a half shall be the length thereof, and a cubit and a half the breadth thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c75e0da7-45e4-4a02-81c3-63559c76a6e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: EXO 25:18
Text: And thou shalt make two cherubims of gold, of beaten work shalt thou make them, in the two ends of the mercy seat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:724f4e00-9cb1-4d7e-85a6-5bf7c6b6b933>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: EXO 25:19
Text: And make one cherub on the one end, and the other cherub on the other end: even of the mercy seat shall ye make the cherubims on the two ends thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75fc04e8-c270-431e-8daf-d4b23c419d21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: EXO 25:20
Text: And the cherubims shall stretch forth their wings on high, covering the mercy seat with their wings, and their faces shall look one to another; toward the mercy seat shall the faces of the cherubims be.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3372730-cb64-4099-b00f-dd72bc9ed77d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: EXO 25:21
Text: And thou shalt put the mercy seat above upon the ark; and in the ark thou shalt put the testimony that I shall give thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb0b8cc5-5f43-44b4-ad5b-541fff58b261>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: EXO 25:22
Text: And there I will meet with thee, and I will commune with thee from above the mercy seat, from between the two cherubims which are upon the ark of the testimony, of all things which I will give thee in commandment unto the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9389fee0-e3f9-44aa-b69e-0c36730ecf89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: EXO 25:23
Text: Thou shalt also make a table of shittim wood: two cubits shall be the length thereof, and a cubit the breadth thereof, and a cubit and a half the height thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97abb193-f6d5-4181-a510-6267fd37661b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: EXO 25:24
Text: And thou shalt overlay it with pure gold, and make thereto a crown of gold round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44df1d07-59c0-4867-9c05-fb9e6181c3fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: EXO 25:25
Text: And thou shalt make unto it a border of an hand breadth round about, and thou shalt make a golden crown to the border thereof round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:feb099eb-38cc-4ddd-969b-5c6fad6b5b20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: EXO 25:26
Text: And thou shalt make for it four rings of gold, and put the rings in the four corners that are on the four feet thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26bc3a7d-b312-44e0-9bab-1b27e8a2e28a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: EXO 25:27
Text: Over against the border shall the rings be for places of the staves to bear the table.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:411d35fa-e441-435b-8547-50c01b686b52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: EXO 25:28
Text: And thou shalt make the staves of shittim wood, and overlay them with gold, that the table may be borne with them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e7c2faf-a24e-4634-bff7-953537d40f08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: EXO 25:29
Text: And thou shalt make the dishes thereof, and spoons thereof, and covers thereof, and bowls thereof, to cover withal: of pure gold shalt thou make them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b600cd2-e7bb-4274-a21c-0980a6b1ea37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: EXO 25:30
Text: And thou shalt set upon the table shewbread before me alway.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:864dadc3-ef5c-4efa-bc9f-02e3948d1db5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: EXO 25:31
Text: And thou shalt make a candlestick of pure gold: of beaten work shall the candlestick be made: his shaft, and his branches, his bowls, his knops, and his flowers, shall be of the same.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4860763d-590d-4e03-b9d0-031179f923db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: EXO 25:32
Text: And six branches shall come out of the sides of it; three branches of the candlestick out of the one side, and three branches of the candlestick out of the other side:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d433a59f-6cd5-454b-a02a-ff6f19f04462>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: EXO 25:33
Text: Three bowls made like unto almonds, with a knop and a flower in one branch; and three bowls made like almonds in the other branch, with a knop and a flower: so in the six branches that come out of the candlestick.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2d1f5d1-2df0-40a5-a4b1-83bd4ffe8a32>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: EXO 25:34
Text: And in the candlesticks shall be four bowls made like unto almonds, with their knops and their flowers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d68d244-f7b5-4bd6-a32c-9e2cdf29ca62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: EXO 25:35
Text: And there shall be a knop under two branches of the same, and a knop under two branches of the same, and a knop under two branches of the same, according to the six branches that proceed out of the candlestick.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9aeea85-2775-4291-8d40-b5175c7b98df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: EXO 25:36
Text: Their knops and their branches shall be of the same: all it shall be one beaten work of pure gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e0f3577-d944-41e8-bb16-a864a65fb2f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: EXO 25:37
Text: And thou shalt make the seven lamps thereof: and they shall light the lamps thereof, that they may give light over against it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf52c6bf-9f47-44f3-ac22-aa00e36c1940>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: EXO 25:38
Text: And the tongs thereof, and the snuffdishes thereof, shall be of pure gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0145a820-0186-4c2d-b491-7cfba298a878>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: EXO 25:39
Text: Of a talent of pure gold shall he make it, with all these vessels.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/25/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:277459c2-2122-4e49-9feb-50c8a56bb366>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: EXO 25:40
Text: And look that thou make them after their pattern, which was shewed thee in the mount.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3bd44e7f-4e48-45db-86c0-930edf7f526c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: EXO 26:1
Text: Moreover thou shalt make the tabernacle with ten curtains of fine twined linen, and blue, and purple, and scarlet: with cherubims of cunning work shalt thou make them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:696f83c1-910c-4bd6-993f-08bd48cf01f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: EXO 26:2
Text: The length of one curtain shall be eight and twenty cubits, and the breadth of one curtain four cubits: and every one of the curtains shall have one measure.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e411200-532f-496a-a645-3a82dd7e2b21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: EXO 26:3
Text: The five curtains shall be coupled together one to another; and other five curtains shall be coupled one to another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0850c10-bcdb-4817-a4de-77d1483c0ee4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: EXO 26:4
Text: And thou shalt make loops of blue upon the edge of the one curtain from the selvedge in the coupling; and likewise shalt thou make in the uttermost edge of another curtain, in the coupling of the second.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58459e93-0992-4909-9650-ca7fdac9f17a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: EXO 26:5
Text: Fifty loops shalt thou make in the one curtain, and fifty loops shalt thou make in the edge of the curtain that is in the coupling of the second; that the loops may take hold one of another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ec3590c-be82-4018-b659-eb760245a685>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: EXO 26:6
Text: And thou shalt make fifty taches of gold, and couple the curtains together with the taches: and it shall be one tabernacle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71190372-80fa-40b1-9619-a02129dd1113>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: EXO 26:7
Text: And thou shalt make curtains of goats’ hair to be a covering upon the tabernacle: eleven curtains shalt thou make.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7dc3eb5-e997-4e8b-b376-d4df2e780f69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: EXO 26:8
Text: The length of one curtain shall be thirty cubits, and the breadth of one curtain four cubits: and the eleven curtains shall be all of one measure.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e876b11-69e3-4468-b04a-0b28fa451e43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: EXO 26:9
Text: And thou shalt couple five curtains by themselves, and six curtains by themselves, and shalt double the sixth curtain in the forefront of the tabernacle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ecc6a626-cbc9-4fdd-9871-5c54b03ab136>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: EXO 26:10
Text: And thou shalt make fifty loops on the edge of the one curtain that is outmost in the coupling, and fifty loops in the edge of the curtain which coupleth the second.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c2dfeb1-e027-471c-bcd1-70358128526d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: EXO 26:11
Text: And thou shalt make fifty taches of brass, and put the taches into the loops, and couple the tent together, that it may be one.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33597eaf-170c-4831-a4bb-9b1f5cb94a6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: EXO 26:12
Text: And the remnant that remaineth of the curtains of the tent, the half curtain that remaineth, shall hang over the backside of the tabernacle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c363bcb1-9e0a-49be-9f8d-eee81186db16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: EXO 26:13
Text: And a cubit on the one side, and a cubit on the other side of that which remaineth in the length of the curtains of the tent, it shall hang over the sides of the tabernacle on this side and on that side, to cover it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a5922af-b23b-4a54-a2a0-a056e50c2454>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: EXO 26:14
Text: And thou shalt make a covering for the tent of rams’ skins dyed red, and a covering above of badgers’ skins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf84c05c-156c-4a94-93dd-685532227046>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: EXO 26:15
Text: And thou shalt make boards for the tabernacle of shittim wood standing up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1c83c15-c4bd-4a28-945b-243b0e95df54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: EXO 26:16
Text: Ten cubits shall be the length of a board, and a cubit and a half shall be the breadth of one board.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3efb2c5-d5b4-4a12-85b7-788c29773f3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EXO 26:17
Text: Two tenons shall there be in one board, set in order one against another: thus shalt thou make for all the boards of the tabernacle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1303aabc-ab11-4a38-8f98-7896b39aaf08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: EXO 26:18
Text: And thou shalt make the boards for the tabernacle, twenty boards on the south side southward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12341acc-5d0c-4112-84bd-0ff68e43f03f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: EXO 26:19
Text: And thou shalt make forty sockets of silver under the twenty boards; two sockets under one board for his two tenons, and two sockets under another board for his two tenons.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad6eb42e-c9ed-4461-8fbf-9896fdd4f46d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: EXO 26:20
Text: And for the second side of the tabernacle on the north side there shall be twenty boards:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9298dc6f-49ed-4c07-a150-715c9c4c94ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: EXO 26:21
Text: And their forty sockets of silver; two sockets under one board, and two sockets under another board.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9049eb74-5863-4cef-b6dd-ce7b815362b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: EXO 26:22
Text: And for the sides of the tabernacle westward thou shalt make six boards.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2de13b7-6032-4eca-9ce0-dbe0e8f94c6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: EXO 26:23
Text: And two boards shalt thou make for the corners of the tabernacle in the two sides.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bea6461b-7ead-4b57-bd19-7c2f29ab1b53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: EXO 26:24
Text: And they shall be coupled together beneath, and they shall be coupled together above the head of it unto one ring: thus shall it be for them both; they shall be for the two corners.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:678282b1-f22b-4e82-8ed5-aa01f7bc1f27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: EXO 26:25
Text: And they shall be eight boards, and their sockets of silver, sixteen sockets; two sockets under one board, and two sockets under another board.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8fb0077-ff9c-4333-9a21-30e66d0c4818>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: EXO 26:26
Text: And thou shalt make bars of shittim wood; five for the boards of the one side of the tabernacle,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f9cc22a-fe70-4e6c-9bf9-00b5475062d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: EXO 26:27
Text: And five bars for the boards of the other side of the tabernacle, and five bars for the boards of the side of the tabernacle, for the two sides westward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c907944f-bf60-4417-9e38-813ecfd7f5ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: EXO 26:28
Text: And the middle bar in the midst of the boards shall reach from end to end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3268484e-c66e-425c-ad66-ddb60ff161a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: EXO 26:29
Text: And thou shalt overlay the boards with gold, and make their rings of gold for places for the bars: and thou shalt overlay the bars with gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf59d006-4137-45a2-8c7b-2667d08642d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: EXO 26:30
Text: And thou shalt rear up the tabernacle according to the fashion thereof which was shewed thee in the mount.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e34f7d12-92f9-4474-96c3-df07e2bd99ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EXO 26:31
Text: And thou shalt make a vail of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen of cunning work: with cherubims shall it be made:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b60e9ae-cb8f-4589-bcb0-87635afd69c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: EXO 26:32
Text: And thou shalt hang it upon four pillars of shittim wood overlaid with gold: their hooks shall be of gold, upon the four sockets of silver.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22deeb5d-4936-4f36-a9eb-8fcb9a1b71f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: EXO 26:33
Text: And thou shalt hang up the vail under the taches, that thou mayest bring in thither within the vail the ark of the testimony: and the vail shall divide unto you between the holy place and the most holy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2d10278-f474-4518-91b8-8fd48c65c4f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: EXO 26:34
Text: And thou shalt put the mercy seat upon the ark of the testimony in the most holy place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9bccd441-8852-438e-93aa-a6659078a519>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: EXO 26:35
Text: And thou shalt set the table without the vail, and the candlestick over against the table on the side of the tabernacle toward the south: and thou shalt put the table on the north side.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/26/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
