Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: EXO 31:2
Text: See, I have called by name Bezaleel the son of Uri, the son of Hur, of the tribe of Judah:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/31/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08e16950-907c-4b61-9146-1ba79355172f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EXO 31:3
Text: And I have filled him with the spirit of God, in wisdom, and in understanding, and in knowledge, and in all manner of workmanship,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/31/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0430ebb-be3f-4cb1-af2e-6576d6709f19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: EXO 31:4
Text: To devise cunning works, to work in gold, and in silver, and in brass,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/31/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a36643e6-a6a5-4016-a49a-4130fc3ea9d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: EXO 31:5
Text: And in cutting of stones, to set them, and in carving of timber, to work in all manner of workmanship.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/31/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97347654-aec0-4380-8c50-4dd8bcdae5af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: EXO 31:6
Text: And I, behold, I have given with him Aholiab, the son of Ahisamach, of the tribe of Dan: and in the hearts of all that are wise hearted I have put wisdom, that they may make all that I have commanded thee;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/31/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5dc1761f-3437-4ffe-adb7-44470203952a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: EXO 31:7
Text: The tabernacle of the congregation, and the ark of the testimony, and the mercy seat that is thereupon, and all the furniture of the tabernacle,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/31/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b844094e-d5d0-4678-8fab-583987f09220>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: EXO 31:8
Text: And the table and his furniture, and the pure candlestick with all his furniture, and the altar of incense,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/31/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5881dbc1-4a92-48e1-8d7a-0b99699bcbca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: EXO 31:9
Text: And the altar of burnt offering with all his furniture, and the laver and his foot,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/31/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1d5cb59-8e07-4e88-a156-0f4d8d00f5f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: EXO 31:10
Text: And the cloths of service, and the holy garments for Aaron the priest, and the garments of his sons, to minister in the priest’s office,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/31/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:711986e6-008e-4930-8157-4c61c0817826>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: EXO 31:11
Text: And the anointing oil, and sweet incense for the holy place: according to all that I have commanded thee shall they do.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/31/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bde5948-22da-493e-9754-65ada71a2ef1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 66

Reference: EXO 31:12
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/31/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec6648b3-90d2-4fd5-a9e6-6bd01ba6c2a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: EXO 31:13
Text: Speak thou also unto the children of Israel, saying, Verily my sabbaths ye shall keep: for it is a sign between me and you throughout your generations; that ye may know that I am the LORD that doth sanctify you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/31/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e41a406-501e-4fc8-8908-c63fa8a43284>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: EXO 31:14
Text: Ye shall keep the sabbath therefore; for it is holy unto you: every one that defileth it shall surely be put to death: for whosoever doeth any work therein, that soul shall be cut off from among his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/31/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc9f488c-0395-4ade-b8e0-c4892152ea8e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: EXO 31:15
Text: Six days may work be done; but in the seventh is the sabbath of rest, holy to the LORD: whosoever doeth any work in the sabbath day, he shall surely be put to death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/31/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5c4b2ef-9478-418b-950a-17d4cf6ef9d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: EXO 31:16
Text: Wherefore the children of Israel shall keep the sabbath, to observe the sabbath throughout their generations, for a perpetual covenant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/31/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f687d1f-0479-4f01-895c-1c2355d3c4f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: EXO 31:17
Text: It is a sign between me and the children of Israel for ever: for in six days the LORD made heaven and earth, and on the seventh day he rested, and was refreshed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/31/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81f66137-fb31-4ba8-9a27-8cba5c80258f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: EXO 31:18
Text: And he gave unto Moses, when he had made an end of communing with him upon mount Sinai, two tables of testimony, tables of stone, written with the finger of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e350bc9-cf71-4adc-8cc0-af5c85f9c468>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 325

Reference: EXO 32:1
Text: And when the people saw that Moses delayed to come down out of the mount, the people gathered themselves together unto Aaron, and said unto him, Up, make us gods, which shall go before us; for as for this Moses, the man that brought us up out of the land of Egypt, we wot not what is become of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b345c4e6-84bf-48af-8ece-cd19a88ce859>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: EXO 32:2
Text: And Aaron said unto them, Break off the golden earrings, which are in the ears of your wives, of your sons, and of your daughters, and bring them unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b8c0382-15b9-49a0-84d1-f47bfe0d4a97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: EXO 32:3
Text: And all the people brake off the golden earrings which were in their ears, and brought them unto Aaron.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85c08d20-577c-4876-8b4b-554021191a00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: EXO 32:4
Text: And he received them at their hand, and fashioned it with a graving tool, after he had made it a molten calf: and they said, These be thy gods, O Israel, which brought thee up out of the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:913e9dbb-3938-4730-883e-62b0073a14fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: EXO 32:5
Text: And when Aaron saw it, he built an altar before it; and Aaron made proclamation, and said, To morrow is a feast to the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3396b5ab-275f-4914-b256-0313d1453bfa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: EXO 32:6
Text: And they rose up early on the morrow, and offered burnt offerings, and brought peace offerings; and the people sat down to eat and to drink, and rose up to play.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e04ac36-face-45ae-b486-22761a6f7ead>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: EXO 32:7
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Go, get thee down; for thy people, which thou broughtest out of the land of Egypt, have corrupted themselves:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ff86bc5-a0c0-4e26-972c-95451df848f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 278

Reference: EXO 32:8
Text: They have turned aside quickly out of the way which I commanded them: they have made them a molten calf, and have worshipped it, and have sacrificed thereunto, and said, These be thy gods, O Israel, which have brought thee up out of the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4c52fb6-33c1-4bf9-905a-51c9f2574db3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: EXO 32:9
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, I have seen this people, and, behold, it is a stiffnecked people:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7629ef7b-a499-4b9d-b30d-91dd6dc24e0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: EXO 32:10
Text: Now therefore let me alone, that my wrath may wax hot against them, and that I may consume them: and I will make of thee a great nation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:726d80f4-375a-4aa3-a326-9f5ecdf4f492>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: EXO 32:11
Text: And Moses besought the LORD his God, and said, LORD, why doth thy wrath wax hot against thy people, which thou hast brought forth out of the land of Egypt with great power, and with a mighty hand?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a7e2b8e-54ff-4ae8-a6a7-315edc83b18f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: EXO 32:12
Text: Wherefore should the Egyptians speak, and say, For mischief did he bring them out, to slay them in the mountains, and to consume them from the face of the earth? Turn from thy fierce wrath, and repent of this evil against thy people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c3acb3f-6633-47c8-8c60-ab1154f951e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 294

Reference: EXO 32:13
Text: Remember Abraham, Isaac, and Israel, thy servants, to whom thou swarest by thine own self, and saidst unto them, I will multiply your seed as the stars of heaven, and all this land that I have spoken of will I give unto your seed, and they shall inherit it for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abcacd11-5058-480e-80a2-b5984773aaae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: EXO 32:14
Text: And the LORD repented of the evil which he thought to do unto his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9b8b377-9001-476f-b549-8754672f45cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: EXO 32:15
Text: And Moses turned, and went down from the mount, and the two tables of the testimony were in his hand: the tables were written on both their sides; on the one side and on the other were they written.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d65522a0-79d1-49d0-ac75-052fd25c1455>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: EXO 32:16
Text: And the tables were the work of God, and the writing was the writing of God, graven upon the tables.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e6c428f-2bec-465b-89b4-2edf3bbaf674>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: EXO 32:17
Text: And when Joshua heard the noise of the people as they shouted, he said unto Moses, There is a noise of war in the camp.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39197d28-21ef-4094-8456-23e4f8a00040>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: EXO 32:18
Text: And he said, It is not the voice of them that shout for mastery, neither is it the voice of them that cry for being overcome: but the noise of them that sing do I hear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5af47aff-9813-4a2c-9d4c-ffe08101c99d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: EXO 32:19
Text: And it came to pass, as soon as he came nigh unto the camp, that he saw the calf, and the dancing: and Moses’ anger waxed hot, and he cast the tables out of his hands, and brake them beneath the mount.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac2c7a42-c8fe-4ada-8744-0dc4238c8a6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: EXO 32:20
Text: And he took the calf which they had made, and burnt it in the fire, and ground it to powder, and strawed it upon the water, and made the children of Israel drink of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55118c60-553a-429b-9a52-34f30818be73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: EXO 32:21
Text: And Moses said unto Aaron, What did this people unto thee, that thou hast brought so great a sin upon them?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c3c1bd0-d03b-4aac-a80d-78ff53629566>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: EXO 32:22
Text: And Aaron said, Let not the anger of my lord wax hot: thou knowest the people, that they are set on mischief.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0deca711-7a54-431d-8127-77b0b0c62204>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: EXO 32:23
Text: For they said unto me, Make us gods, which shall go before us: for as for this Moses, the man that brought us up out of the land of Egypt, we wot not what is become of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59a45181-a94d-431b-a635-1ef43623ecc5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: EXO 32:24
Text: And I said unto them, Whosoever hath any gold, let them break it off. So they gave it me: then I cast it into the fire, and there came out this calf.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08ed6aab-aa67-4a47-837b-087676da7f0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: EXO 32:25
Text: And when Moses saw that the people were naked; (for Aaron had made them naked unto their shame among their enemies:)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eaeb7305-f48a-4bf6-95df-80b88c9e26db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: EXO 32:26
Text: Then Moses stood in the gate of the camp, and said, Who is on the LORD’s side? let him come unto me. And all the sons of Levi gathered themselves together unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89fcfacc-c46e-4d45-9f7d-22bba1cda4cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: EXO 32:27
Text: And he said unto them, Thus saith the LORD God of Israel, Put every man his sword by his side, and go in and out from gate to gate throughout the camp, and slay every man his brother, and every man his companion, and every man his neighbour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9fea92b-8b44-4880-be73-846ceb5c079b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: EXO 32:28
Text: And the children of Levi did according to the word of Moses: and there fell of the people that day about three thousand men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbd47b97-9645-4fd9-bdf0-3830f00c5a7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: EXO 32:29
Text: For Moses had said, Consecrate yourselves today to the LORD, even every man upon his son, and upon his brother; that he may bestow upon you a blessing this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:805d1b47-6138-4bba-a4af-267a291f37a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: EXO 32:30
Text: And it came to pass on the morrow, that Moses said unto the people, Ye have sinned a great sin: and now I will go up unto the LORD; peradventure I shall make an atonement for your sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ffa2d2c-9910-4293-98b8-0a09d4307bbc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: EXO 32:31
Text: And Moses returned unto the LORD, and said, Oh, this people have sinned a great sin, and have made them gods of gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19a406e0-2802-4c32-9689-17663b3e1f0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: EXO 32:32
Text: Yet now, if thou wilt forgive their sin--; and if not, blot me, I pray thee, out of thy book which thou hast written.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60146839-3829-469f-8cb4-87b03c1fb8d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: EXO 32:33
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Whosoever hath sinned against me, him will I blot out of my book.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad26ac78-2fe8-4ed7-a533-fcc762e6cad8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: EXO 32:34
Text: Therefore now go, lead the people unto the place of which I have spoken unto thee: behold, mine Angel shall go before thee: nevertheless in the day when I visit I will visit their sin upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/32/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2c2bbe1-bbe0-4e5f-9c57-2a8cee0b4da8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: EXO 32:35
Text: And the LORD plagued the people, because they made the calf, which Aaron made.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/33/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0567b0cd-d2ec-440c-8abe-13b4d7440ccb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: EXO 33:1
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Depart, and go up hence, thou and the people which thou hast brought up out of the land of Egypt, unto the land which I sware unto Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob, saying, Unto thy seed will I give it:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/33/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3413617-f114-464a-9793-29311d2a4c3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: EXO 33:2
Text: And I will send an angel before thee; and I will drive out the Canaanite, the Amorite, and the Hittite, and the Perizzite, the Hivite, and the Jebusite:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/33/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b144f06-a0a8-4420-91fb-2c0748d16617>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: EXO 33:3
Text: Unto a land flowing with milk and honey: for I will not go up in the midst of thee; for thou art a stiffnecked people: lest I consume thee in the way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/33/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:658a16f0-82a0-4b11-951f-20c34a9317d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: EXO 33:4
Text: And when the people heard these evil tidings, they mourned: and no man did put on him his ornaments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/33/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5146b65-0183-4973-aa8b-1f2cd26283c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: EXO 33:5
Text: For the LORD had said unto Moses, Say unto the children of Israel, Ye are a stiffnecked people: I will come up into the midst of thee in a moment, and consume thee: therefore now put off thy ornaments from thee, that I may know what to do unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/33/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5adb088b-441d-486a-a1da-13306f24bfbb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: EXO 33:6
Text: And the children of Israel stripped themselves of their ornaments by the mount Horeb.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/33/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4996adf-49c1-4b8f-8ea4-665866dfd97e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 300

Reference: EXO 33:7
Text: And Moses took the tabernacle, and pitched it without the camp, afar off from the camp, and called it the Tabernacle of the congregation. And it came to pass, that every one which sought the LORD went out unto the tabernacle of the congregation, which was without the camp.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/33/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8e63840-4b23-4228-9478-9e3e6489fc47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: EXO 33:8
Text: And it came to pass, when Moses went out unto the tabernacle, that all the people rose up, and stood every man at his tent door, and looked after Moses, until he was gone into the tabernacle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/33/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4b321ec-508e-43ca-8e84-6cad18ba6c27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: EXO 33:9
Text: And it came to pass, as Moses entered into the tabernacle, the cloudy pillar descended, and stood at the door of the tabernacle, and the Lord talked with Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/33/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a1d14dd-4d52-455b-9074-40a1fb33509f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: EXO 33:10
Text: And all the people saw the cloudy pillar stand at the tabernacle door: and all the people rose up and worshipped, every man in his tent door.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/33/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf17b13d-e20c-4d37-b0f4-63c36bd1c30a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: EXO 33:11
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses face to face, as a man speaketh unto his friend. And he turned again into the camp: but his servant Joshua, the son of Nun, a young man, departed not out of the tabernacle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/33/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60ce2aec-5897-457c-b310-64632f8bc276>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: EXO 33:12
Text: And Moses said unto the LORD, See, thou sayest unto me, Bring up this people: and thou hast not let me know whom thou wilt send with me. Yet thou hast said, I know thee by name, and thou hast also found grace in my sight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/33/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50c661e2-b994-43aa-976b-64cf4c978777>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: EXO 33:13
Text: Now therefore, I pray thee, if I have found grace in thy sight, shew me now thy way, that I may know thee, that I may find grace in thy sight: and consider that this nation is thy people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/33/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e5ef64b-30cd-4d5d-8f0f-5fcf6783b5ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: EXO 33:14
Text: And he said, My presence shall go with thee, and I will give thee rest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/33/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:412ceca8-01d9-4a5a-aee6-823e0ec64a50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: EXO 33:15
Text: And he said unto him, If thy presence go not with me, carry us not up hence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/33/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:842a999d-223c-497b-8f48-0be56f55bc2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: EXO 33:16
Text: For wherein shall it be known here that I and thy people have found grace in thy sight? is it not in that thou goest with us? so shall we be separated, I and thy people, from all the people that are upon the face of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/33/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e943b6b-a7c5-4101-8f36-a480e0ec2ca0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: EXO 33:17
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, I will do this thing also that thou hast spoken: for thou hast found grace in my sight, and I know thee by name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/33/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07314ed1-1386-4a3c-a76b-a62350f4af1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: EXO 33:18
Text: And he said, I beseech thee, shew me thy glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/33/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71190ed9-c536-4a0d-9d32-a57ce432124b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: EXO 33:19
Text: And he said, I will make all my goodness pass before thee, and I will proclaim the name of the LORD before thee; and will be gracious to whom I will be gracious, and will shew mercy on whom I will shew mercy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/33/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab448509-24e5-4a9e-ab07-4075f08eba91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: EXO 33:20
Text: And he said, Thou canst not see my face: for there shall no man see me, and live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/33/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9044f49f-790b-4e38-b434-cb1a277f7c54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: EXO 33:21
Text: And the LORD said, Behold, there is a place by me, and thou shalt stand upon a rock:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/33/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10457ec8-37b8-41bc-bbf7-162efedb678a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: EXO 33:22
Text: And it shall come to pass, while my glory passeth by, that I will put thee in a clift of the rock, and will cover thee with my hand while I pass by:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/33/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5245b675-d446-4e61-85da-d535d190166e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: EXO 33:23
Text: And I will take away mine hand, and thou shalt see my back parts: but my face shall not be seen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db727ea0-3fb4-47ea-869a-57d4ef912b88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: EXO 34:1
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Hew thee two tables of stone like unto the first: and I will write upon these tables the words that were in the first tables, which thou brakest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a78ac292-4712-4c1d-8107-1d1933f1ce77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EXO 34:2
Text: And be ready in the morning, and come up in the morning unto mount Sinai, and present thyself there to me in the top of the mount.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87a64c8c-3495-4980-9d36-ea65a1a59430>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: EXO 34:3
Text: And no man shall come up with thee, neither let any man be seen throughout all the mount; neither let the flocks nor herds feed before that mount.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1911f05-0f6e-42db-8d50-fac6a36bda01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: EXO 34:4
Text: And he hewed two tables of stone like unto the first; and Moses rose up early in the morning, and went up unto mount Sinai, as the LORD had commanded him, and took in his hand the two tables of stone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34a22123-ef25-4818-918c-efb57a2b6480>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: EXO 34:5
Text: And the LORD descended in the cloud, and stood with him there, and proclaimed the name of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44359d90-3325-4fd4-aa1f-ced9c270935f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: EXO 34:6
Text: And the LORD passed by before him, and proclaimed, The LORD, The LORD God, merciful and gracious, longsuffering, and abundant in goodness and truth,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:064ab8a0-13c6-42b3-abb0-c6d91db68ebc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 282

Reference: EXO 34:7
Text: Keeping mercy for thousands, forgiving iniquity and transgression and sin, and that will by no means clear the guilty; visiting the iniquity of the fathers upon the children, and upon the children’s children, unto the third and to the fourth generation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3c9300b-5184-49cd-baa1-ba221f246543>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: EXO 34:8
Text: And Moses made haste, and bowed his head toward the earth, and worshipped.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9245b81-f6b1-48d1-804a-040aa56cb133>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: EXO 34:9
Text: And he said, If now I have found grace in thy sight, O LORD, let my LORD, I pray thee, go among us; for it is a stiffnecked people; and pardon our iniquity and our sin, and take us for thine inheritance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a33bad7a-caf5-4f0c-b443-028e36eae767>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 297

Reference: EXO 34:10
Text: And he said, Behold, I make a covenant: before all thy people I will do marvels, such as have not been done in all the earth, nor in any nation: and all the people among which thou art shall see the work of the LORD: for it is a terrible thing that I will do with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93f17b39-622a-4c7d-a1d2-2f2e933aaa75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: EXO 34:11
Text: Observe thou that which I command thee this day: behold, I drive out before thee the Amorite, and the Canaanite, and the Hittite, and the Perizzite, and the Hivite, and the Jebusite.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d519ab0c-9932-49c6-bba4-126dd9c042f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: EXO 34:12
Text: Take heed to thyself, lest thou make a covenant with the inhabitants of the land whither thou goest, lest it be for a snare in the midst of thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:043712bb-342b-42b4-9759-b54a383cab12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: EXO 34:13
Text: But ye shall destroy their altars, break their images, and cut down their groves:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b1734ba-fba3-4fea-92c6-e9b6ae8aaa75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: EXO 34:14
Text: For thou shalt worship no other god: for the LORD, whose name is Jealous, is a jealous God:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5134b1b0-fba4-4a07-a232-3b94acd538f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: EXO 34:15
Text: Lest thou make a covenant with the inhabitants of the land, and they go a whoring after their gods, and do sacrifice unto their gods, and one call thee, and thou eat of his sacrifice;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d52e5e4-599c-4d18-be0c-cbfa80fcf586>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: EXO 34:16
Text: And thou take of their daughters unto thy sons, and their daughters go a whoring after their gods, and make thy sons go a whoring after their gods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef8488dd-2979-4734-9127-adf5b4813efb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 64

Reference: EXO 34:17
Text: Thou shalt make thee no molten gods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fcbdfaf3-f3e8-4940-a962-d07da3e9367c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: EXO 34:18
Text: The feast of unleavened bread shalt thou keep. Seven days thou shalt eat unleavened bread, as I commanded thee, in the time of the month Abib: for in the month Abib thou camest out from Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dad73998-f706-4580-b363-df22922a17b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: EXO 34:19
Text: All that openeth the matrix is mine; and every firstling among thy cattle, whether ox or sheep, that is male.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f63a45c-96fa-4825-ad97-9bae001ac796>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: EXO 34:20
Text: But the firstling of an ass thou shalt redeem with a lamb: and if thou redeem him not, then shalt thou break his neck. All the firstborn of thy sons thou shalt redeem. And none shall appear before me empty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31fc6a76-38e2-44b4-af65-f72794249811>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: EXO 34:21
Text: Six days thou shalt work, but on the seventh day thou shalt rest: in earing time and in harvest thou shalt rest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa5dfd65-cb4c-4bc9-8604-a3d52ab96248>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EXO 34:22
Text: And thou shalt observe the feast of weeks, of the firstfruits of wheat harvest, and the feast of ingathering at the year’s end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d23fa88-97e5-4972-9b0f-9ff8b15570d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: EXO 34:23
Text: Thrice in the year shall all your menchildren appear before the LORD God, the God of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00ce5a29-3282-4018-b4d1-502c109df218>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: EXO 34:24
Text: For I will cast out the nations before thee, and enlarge thy borders: neither shall any man desire thy land, when thou shalt go up to appear before the LORD thy God thrice in the year.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8165f4b-20aa-4087-bdf4-d5d81ce2e2d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: EXO 34:25
Text: Thou shalt not offer the blood of my sacrifice with leaven; neither shall the sacrifice of the feast of the passover be left unto the morning.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/34/26
