Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: EXO 40:22
Text: And he put the table in the tent of the congregation, upon the side of the tabernacle northward, without the vail.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/40/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee998f4a-6dd7-4684-898b-e39ffc5c6b48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: EXO 40:23
Text: And he set the bread in order upon it before the LORD; as the LORD had commanded Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/40/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d681ed82-ad17-4645-a20b-cc525f2e74c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: EXO 40:24
Text: And he put the candlestick in the tent of the congregation, over against the table, on the side of the tabernacle southward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/40/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:326a2fcc-29f4-4b3e-8c84-817e293b4f16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: EXO 40:25
Text: And he lighted the lamps before the LORD; as the LORD commanded Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/40/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7685f73b-77cd-4c5d-8a5e-54d6be50e2a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: EXO 40:26
Text: And he put the golden altar in the tent of the congregation before the vail:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/40/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ab1984c-65f2-4130-8f18-f130fc7a805e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: EXO 40:27
Text: And he burnt sweet incense thereon; as the LORD commanded Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/40/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2eb15085-ac11-40b6-a1af-c8111ee02b2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: EXO 40:28
Text: And he set up the hanging at the door of the tabernacle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/40/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acea1ffe-7fcd-42bf-89cb-23f03c511ec7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: EXO 40:29
Text: And he put the altar of burnt offering by the door of the tabernacle of the tent of the congregation, and offered upon it the burnt offering and the meat offering; as the LORD commanded Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/40/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ac9c58d-e11f-41cf-a5d2-bb0d55929a1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: EXO 40:30
Text: And he set the laver between the tent of the congregation and the altar, and put water there, to wash withal.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/40/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8867563-f7d7-41d5-b8f6-057ae7e78b75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: EXO 40:31
Text: And Moses and Aaron and his sons washed their hands and their feet thereat:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/40/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec100a0c-2868-44e3-a33d-15687b192f29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: EXO 40:32
Text: When they went into the tent of the congregation, and when they came near unto the altar, they washed; as the LORD commanded Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/40/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4762e294-fc73-412a-98a8-5b09848afffa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: EXO 40:33
Text: And he reared up the court round about the tabernacle and the altar, and set up the hanging of the court gate. So Moses finished the work.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/40/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e5acd31-f6dc-4721-bca0-6b84630737cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: EXO 40:34
Text: Then a cloud covered the tent of the congregation, and the glory of the LORD filled the tabernacle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/40/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e11d00e4-aaa1-4786-82fd-03d0b53fc2ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: EXO 40:35
Text: And Moses was not able to enter into the tent of the congregation, because the cloud abode thereon, and the glory of the LORD filled the tabernacle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/40/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d55939ba-f10f-4ea0-9e71-6ce359b1076e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: EXO 40:36
Text: And when the cloud was taken up from over the tabernacle, the children of Israel went onward in all their journeys:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/40/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0a44204-922a-48be-bc3c-ebf473eef971>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: EXO 40:37
Text: But if the cloud were not taken up, then they journeyed not till the day that it was taken up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EXO/40/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9fa546e-a3fd-4cab-9ed0-4b9e13a71ad9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: EXO 40:38
Text: For the cloud of the LORD was upon the tabernacle by day, and fire was on it by night, in the sight of all the house of Israel, throughout all their journeys.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc6e8ccb-d62d-4153-a6a1-5ea44ea8f617>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: LEV 1:1
Text: And the LORD called unto Moses, and spake unto him out of the tabernacle of the congregation, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9059f37a-e289-44a1-9e15-e9356c4d2527>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: LEV 1:2
Text: Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, If any man of you bring an offering unto the LORD, ye shall bring your offering of the cattle, even of the herd, and of the flock.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68944546-9c9a-4972-993a-4480d1970e72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: LEV 1:3
Text: If his offering be a burnt sacrifice of the herd, let him offer a male without blemish: he shall offer it of his own voluntary will at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation before the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:803e3ba2-4207-4474-a168-37f8530a05ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: LEV 1:4
Text: And he shall put his hand upon the head of the burnt offering; and it shall be accepted for him to make atonement for him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3694e613-3b88-4b3e-9fd1-33a13a720d10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: LEV 1:5
Text: And he shall kill the bullock before the LORD: and the priests, Aaron’s sons, shall bring the blood, and sprinkle the blood round about upon the altar that is by the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b13326f-1796-4571-92d1-87705c5e7dd8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: LEV 1:6
Text: And he shall flay the burnt offering, and cut it into his pieces.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc2f02e3-37f1-4687-80d0-9494f40f2934>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: LEV 1:7
Text: And the sons of Aaron the priest shall put fire upon the altar, and lay the wood in order upon the fire:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01beca8d-80f5-4ee0-99c8-7859f4684ffa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: LEV 1:8
Text: And the priests, Aaron’s sons, shall lay the parts, the head, and the fat, in order upon the wood that is on the fire which is upon the altar:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac0b110c-efae-4fc5-b322-321c13e2bf84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: LEV 1:9
Text: But his inwards and his legs shall he wash in water: and the priest shall burn all on the altar, to be a burnt sacrifice, an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57499250-d2f1-4d1d-adf7-e9a4814997a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: LEV 1:10
Text: And if his offering be of the flocks, namely, of the sheep, or of the goats, for a burnt sacrifice; he shall bring it a male without blemish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:deec9c5d-9d39-41d4-baa4-52a4f28499fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: LEV 1:11
Text: And he shall kill it on the side of the altar northward before the LORD: and the priests, Aaron’s sons, shall sprinkle his blood round about upon the altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1282b7e-6074-48a9-b4d3-b5bdf4512f27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: LEV 1:12
Text: And he shall cut it into his pieces, with his head and his fat: and the priest shall lay them in order on the wood that is on the fire which is upon the altar:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3446f4d7-1d01-4ee9-8d29-59112ce7a17a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: LEV 1:13
Text: But he shall wash the inwards and the legs with water: and the priest shall bring it all, and burn it upon the altar: it is a burnt sacrifice, an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c801802-888c-452a-a5e5-485e686f4c7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: LEV 1:14
Text: And if the burnt sacrifice for his offering to the LORD be of fowls, then he shall bring his offering of turtledoves, or of young pigeons.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acd7d8bd-92e0-4271-b5b0-665a6659ea13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: LEV 1:15
Text: And the priest shall bring it unto the altar, and wring off his head, and burn it on the altar; and the blood thereof shall be wrung out at the side of the altar:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12265b29-f047-48d2-a8c8-a9d32ad4b051>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: LEV 1:16
Text: And he shall pluck away his crop with his feathers, and cast it beside the altar on the east part, by the place of the ashes:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b9a691e-2191-4d89-a42b-f76fd447fe44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: LEV 1:17
Text: And he shall cleave it with the wings thereof, but shall not divide it asunder: and the priest shall burn it upon the altar, upon the wood that is upon the fire: it is a burnt sacrifice, an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70a94c23-7eba-461e-8714-f0888addc12f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: LEV 2:1
Text: And when any will offer a meat offering unto the LORD, his offering shall be of fine flour; and he shall pour oil upon it, and put frankincense thereon:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2fa7476-1888-4f38-b43d-41af7501b987>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 324

Reference: LEV 2:2
Text: And he shall bring it to Aaron’s sons the priests: and he shall take thereout his handful of the flour thereof, and of the oil thereof, with all the frankincense thereof; and the priest shall burn the memorial of it upon the altar, to be an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53b43dbd-fb80-47f4-bd9b-52e59edd2411>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: LEV 2:3
Text: And the remnant of the meat offering shall be Aaron’s and his sons’: it is a thing most holy of the offerings of the LORD made by fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:865a7aca-2ce3-48c7-bebf-6a2cabd86e9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: LEV 2:4
Text: And if thou bring an oblation of a meat offering baken in the oven, it shall be unleavened cakes of fine flour mingled with oil, or unleavened wafers anointed with oil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:292841da-1b7a-405e-996f-5c0c6767d46d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: LEV 2:5
Text: And if thy oblation be a meat offering baken in a pan, it shall be of fine flour unleavened, mingled with oil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bce62c80-c72b-4de0-b630-ca381253b167>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: LEV 2:6
Text: Thou shalt part it in pieces, and pour oil thereon: it is a meat offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cbfce59-25ca-4899-8a43-fda872e3668f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: LEV 2:7
Text: And if thy oblation be a meat offering baken in the fryingpan, it shall be made of fine flour with oil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffdd03c6-fc9a-4391-9e28-391a5389dd83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: LEV 2:8
Text: And thou shalt bring the meat offering that is made of these things unto the LORD: and when it is presented unto the priest, he shall bring it unto the altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:957fb986-c7ab-4ec6-9509-59a45f5a654f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: LEV 2:9
Text: And the priest shall take from the meat offering a memorial thereof, and shall burn it upon the altar: it is an offering made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a026fef2-5544-470e-94a6-06152c68c127>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: LEV 2:10
Text: And that which is left of the meat offering shall be Aaron’s and his sons’: it is a thing most holy of the offerings of the LORD made by fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7476731e-9beb-4945-99f1-427ae7671b45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: LEV 2:11
Text: No meat offering, which ye shall bring unto the LORD, shall be made with leaven: for ye shall burn no leaven, nor any honey, in any offering of the LORD made by fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f554b455-87d7-4084-8196-698243477fc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: LEV 2:12
Text: As for the oblation of the firstfruits, ye shall offer them unto the LORD: but they shall not be burnt on the altar for a sweet savour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0006615-386f-4f97-9ae9-2f9e36db48fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: LEV 2:13
Text: And every oblation of thy meat offering shalt thou season with salt; neither shalt thou suffer the salt of the covenant of thy God to be lacking from thy meat offering: with all thine offerings thou shalt offer salt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5fdca33-ea5a-4b87-af14-b2c4927b05f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: LEV 2:14
Text: And if thou offer a meat offering of thy firstfruits unto the LORD, thou shalt offer for the meat offering of thy firstfruits green ears of corn dried by the fire, even corn beaten out of full ears.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e0a2d03-1197-4be4-bf2d-ac7c82144c68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: LEV 2:15
Text: And thou shalt put oil upon it, and lay frankincense thereon: it is a meat offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7025b230-cb9b-4430-b96b-7bcc2a273d1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: LEV 2:16
Text: And the priest shall burn the memorial of it, part of the beaten corn thereof, and part of the oil thereof, with all the frankincense thereof: it is an offering made by fire unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21436a45-bfcc-4870-bc80-f40b631f4a17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: LEV 3:1
Text: And if his oblation be a sacrifice of peace offering, if he offer it of the herd; whether it be a male or female, he shall offer it without blemish before the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
