WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/4/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:189c2377-1bd2-41fb-a874-ecf794a86379>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 357

Reference: LEV 4:35
Text: And he shall take away all the fat thereof, as the fat of the lamb is taken away from the sacrifice of the peace offerings; and the priest shall burn them upon the altar, according to the offerings made by fire unto the LORD: and the priest shall make an atonement for his sin that he hath committed, and it shall be forgiven him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e031ead-0828-4fab-a462-576719bd8cc5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: LEV 5:1
Text: And if a soul sin, and hear the voice of swearing, and is a witness, whether he hath seen or known of it; if he do not utter it, then he shall bear his iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f209d089-e22b-43d4-b3c7-3b766787704d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: LEV 5:2
Text: Or if a soul touch any unclean thing, whether it be a carcase of an unclean beast, or a carcase of unclean cattle, or the carcase of unclean creeping things, and if it be hidden from him; he also shall be unclean, and guilty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28b8c3ca-ea56-4b92-a278-2c740484b3dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: LEV 5:3
Text: Or if he touch the uncleanness of man, whatsoever uncleanness it be that a man shall be defiled withal, and it be hid from him; when he knoweth of it, then he shall be guilty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1ad1bdb-c2b9-4dba-98bd-df74d6abdd86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: LEV 5:4
Text: Or if a soul swear, pronouncing with his lips to do evil, or to do good, whatsoever it be that a man shall pronounce with an oath, and it be hid from him; when he knoweth of it, then he shall be guilty in one of these.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e48de0ca-1614-46ec-a5ca-d19ae4a611c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: LEV 5:5
Text: And it shall be, when he shall be guilty in one of these things, that he shall confess that he hath sinned in that thing:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7381f242-6998-413b-b0b5-13d0a9a34894>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: LEV 5:6
Text: And he shall bring his trespass offering unto the LORD for his sin which he hath sinned, a female from the flock, a lamb or a kid of the goats, for a sin offering; and the priest shall make an atonement for him concerning his sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd44ff11-0792-477d-9db3-e2d3943f6cc9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: LEV 5:7
Text: And if he be not able to bring a lamb, then he shall bring for his trespass, which he hath committed, two turtledoves, or two young pigeons, unto the LORD; one for a sin offering, and the other for a burnt offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a4c609c-95f1-442d-b683-103524fa5347>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: LEV 5:8
Text: And he shall bring them unto the priest, who shall offer that which is for the sin offering first, and wring off his head from his neck, but shall not divide it asunder:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7371fc01-d709-495b-8fc6-b9df35cff129>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: LEV 5:9
Text: And he shall sprinkle of the blood of the sin offering upon the side of the altar; and the rest of the blood shall be wrung out at the bottom of the altar: it is a sin offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:097bbbe8-05b9-4e4a-9a0f-8deee26da16b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: LEV 5:10
Text: And he shall offer the second for a burnt offering, according to the manner: and the priest shall make an atonement for him for his sin which he hath sinned, and it shall be forgiven him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a6d239d-5b3d-471f-badb-7ed19bf75327>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 308

Reference: LEV 5:11
Text: But if he be not able to bring two turtledoves, or two young pigeons, then he that sinned shall bring for his offering the tenth part of an ephah of fine flour for a sin offering; he shall put no oil upon it, neither shall he put any frankincense thereon: for it is a sin offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4a710a1-2879-4c0b-a97b-186b1c3488ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: LEV 5:12
Text: Then shall he bring it to the priest, and the priest shall take his handful of it, even a memorial thereof, and burn it on the altar, according to the offerings made by fire unto the LORD: it is a sin offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed004dd9-0bac-4281-b8fd-8fe9bbdd9541>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: LEV 5:13
Text: And the priest shall make an atonement for him as touching his sin that he hath sinned in one of these, and it shall be forgiven him: and the remnant shall be the priest’s, as a meat offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b25c378-acdb-48d2-9ce9-696845fb5b0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 65

Reference: LEV 5:14
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e52f5a6e-8b8c-49ec-9d06-162e1a88037d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 308

Reference: LEV 5:15
Text: If a soul commit a trespass, and sin through ignorance, in the holy things of the LORD; then he shall bring for his trespass unto the LORD a ram without blemish out of the flocks, with thy estimation by shekels of silver, after the shekel of the sanctuary, for a trespass offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b9165f5-d38e-43da-8911-1ef146eccacd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: LEV 5:16
Text: And he shall make amends for the harm that he hath done in the holy thing, and shall add the fifth part thereto, and give it unto the priest: and the priest shall make an atonement for him with the ram of the trespass offering, and it shall be forgiven him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/5/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a164c3d-85a6-4fbd-8c28-8a65be3dec45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: LEV 5:17
Text: And if a soul sin, and commit any of these things which are forbidden to be done by the commandments of the LORD; though he wist it not, yet is he guilty, and shall bear his iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/5/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11183b73-5541-412e-88a6-7872309890be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: LEV 5:18
Text: And he shall bring a ram without blemish out of the flock, with thy estimation, for a trespass offering, unto the priest: and the priest shall make an atonement for him concerning his ignorance wherein he erred and wist it not, and it shall be forgiven him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/5/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef0e9ba5-3009-4224-8cb1-4cf033b3b3c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: LEV 5:19
Text: It is a trespass offering: he hath certainly trespassed against the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2cef1292-ded7-4e75-a30c-613b23554c87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 64

Reference: LEV 6:1
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:262be880-ad4c-4475-91fa-8565d7ab3e4f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: LEV 6:2
Text: If a soul sin, and commit a trespass against the LORD, and lie unto his neighbour in that which was delivered him to keep, or in fellowship, or in a thing taken away by violence, or hath deceived his neighbour;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba38b557-f088-4cb4-a66f-c9b54d6cfb85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: LEV 6:3
Text: Or have found that which was lost, and lieth concerning it, and sweareth falsely; in any of all these that a man doeth, sinning therein:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbfa77b3-5536-4fc8-9d18-004ebe6f74ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: LEV 6:4
Text: Then it shall be, because he hath sinned, and is guilty, that he shall restore that which he took violently away, or the thing which he hath deceitfully gotten, or that which was delivered him to keep, or the lost thing which he found,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b52f142a-86a8-4650-a938-06e0494b48f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: LEV 6:5
Text: Or all that about which he hath sworn falsely; he shall even restore it in the principal, and shall add the fifth part more thereto, and give it unto him to whom it appertaineth, in the day of his trespass offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f720d49b-befb-43a9-8622-b8532e9cdbb6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: LEV 6:6
Text: And he shall bring his trespass offering unto the LORD, a ram without blemish out of the flock, with thy estimation, for a trespass offering, unto the priest:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bab2fe29-d347-4d82-a9f3-a400d3ea19f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: LEV 6:7
Text: And the priest shall make an atonement for him before the LORD: and it shall be forgiven him for any thing of all that he hath done in trespassing therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:138b3791-c874-4c5c-8d89-4c20266cb846>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 64

Reference: LEV 6:8
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57e90e87-3821-4c8a-a084-ff480e673059>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: LEV 6:9
Text: Command Aaron and his sons, saying, This is the law of the burnt offering: It is the burnt offering, because of the burning upon the altar all night unto the morning, and the fire of the altar shall be burning in it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd20034d-cd09-42ae-b7f0-cccb84cef7ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: LEV 6:10
Text: And the priest shall put on his linen garment, and his linen breeches shall he put upon his flesh, and take up the ashes which the fire hath consumed with the burnt offering on the altar, and he shall put them beside the altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:627853da-523c-40dd-b1dc-43b4a4efa4ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: LEV 6:11
Text: And he shall put off his garments, and put on other garments, and carry forth the ashes without the camp unto a clean place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56185eb0-2043-47b3-bf39-785c438ff968>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: LEV 6:12
Text: And the fire upon the altar shall be burning in it; it shall not be put out: and the priest shall burn wood on it every morning, and lay the burnt offering in order upon it; and he shall burn thereon the fat of the peace offerings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d3a9540-34ee-423c-82f7-7ed32e45ee44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: LEV 6:13
Text: The fire shall ever be burning upon the altar; it shall never go out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0dad7a76-5ba3-4b49-b589-f460aa12b165>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: LEV 6:14
Text: And this is the law of the meat offering: the sons of Aaron shall offer it before the LORD, before the altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4d8b290-0739-49c0-b1a5-f7617e90a0ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 273

Reference: LEV 6:15
Text: And he shall take of it his handful, of the flour of the meat offering, and of the oil thereof, and all the frankincense which is upon the meat offering, and shall burn it upon the altar for a sweet savour, even the memorial of it, unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a01bf51-eccf-4772-862b-10d6ad2119bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: LEV 6:16
Text: And the remainder thereof shall Aaron and his sons eat: with unleavened bread shall it be eaten in the holy place; in the court of the tabernacle of the congregation they shall eat it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7b9a36b-1c55-4403-ba56-d99dfe0e2a54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: LEV 6:17
Text: It shall not be baken with leaven. I have given it unto them for their portion of my offerings made by fire; it is most holy, as is the sin offering, and as the trespass offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc1fb248-428b-4d88-a116-6a55b41ffcef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: LEV 6:18
Text: All the males among the children of Aaron shall eat of it. It shall be a statute for ever in your generations concerning the offerings of the LORD made by fire: every one that toucheth them shall be holy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c6f52e3-1198-4252-8fdd-f4912e543036>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 65

Reference: LEV 6:19
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3efdfea1-3d2d-4bc0-9301-b65c4372882f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: LEV 6:20
Text: This is the offering of Aaron and of his sons, which they shall offer unto the LORD in the day when he is anointed; the tenth part of an ephah of fine flour for a meat offering perpetual, half of it in the morning, and half thereof at night.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57c8c5b3-b439-47af-ad43-3fc3664be127>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: LEV 6:21
Text: In a pan it shall be made with oil; and when it is baken, thou shalt bring it in: and the baken pieces of the meat offering shalt thou offer for a sweet savour unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c6ba2ac-afa5-4855-bf0e-6c431215789c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: LEV 6:22
Text: And the priest of his sons that is anointed in his stead shall offer it: it is a statute for ever unto the LORD; it shall be wholly burnt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4efb7c92-ff19-45b8-bf89-ffdbf9dd6490>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: LEV 6:23
Text: For every meat offering for the priest shall be wholly burnt: it shall not be eaten.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dcb1888a-d256-4388-a351-bb2e293269c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 65

Reference: LEV 6:24
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6aed8255-d6c3-487c-8b54-fb97c176304a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: LEV 6:25
Text: Speak unto Aaron and to his sons, saying, This is the law of the sin offering: In the place where the burnt offering is killed shall the sin offering be killed before the LORD: it is most holy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2d0e7e8-e2b0-4d44-a070-745ba152b538>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: LEV 6:26
Text: The priest that offereth it for sin shall eat it: in the holy place shall it be eaten, in the court of the tabernacle of the congregation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9868d5d-529a-4ecd-8e90-add5bb66ec47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: LEV 6:27
Text: Whatsoever shall touch the flesh thereof shall be holy: and when there is sprinkled of the blood thereof upon any garment, thou shalt wash that whereon it was sprinkled in the holy place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4966b50-cb50-472c-9380-233804356b42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: LEV 6:28
Text: But the earthen vessel wherein it is sodden shall be broken: and if it be sodden in a brasen pot, it shall be both scoured, and rinsed in water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e02ebb60-1737-48b8-9d4b-86e2758551b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: LEV 6:29
Text: All the males among the priests shall eat thereof: it is most holy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/6/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:148411b8-792b-4463-a13c-dbeb4781dc99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: LEV 6:30
Text: And no sin offering, whereof any of the blood is brought into the tabernacle of the congregation to reconcile withal in the holy place, shall be eaten: it shall be burnt in the fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6fb73fe-3785-44fe-a629-4b427e1bcd33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: LEV 7:1
Text: Likewise this is the law of the trespass offering: it is most holy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27303d23-746e-4c53-bbdb-4eeeff93159c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: LEV 7:2
Text: In the place where they kill the burnt offering shall they kill the trespass offering: and the blood thereof shall he sprinkle round about upon the altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a613e577-50b1-4432-ae75-fedcd27dfe0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: LEV 7:3
Text: And he shall offer of it all the fat thereof; the rump, and the fat that covereth the inwards,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd16b5e9-2554-49a7-887f-c6b12fb9c3dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: LEV 7:4
Text: And the two kidneys, and the fat that is on them, which is by the flanks, and the caul that is above the liver, with the kidneys, it shall he take away:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abea28e7-a67f-4dcc-85fb-9cf0b05eb95a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: LEV 7:5
Text: And the priest shall burn them upon the altar for an offering made by fire unto the LORD: it is a trespass offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57e6b418-3e7f-4f1e-ab77-947fa11618f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: LEV 7:6
Text: Every male among the priests shall eat thereof: it shall be eaten in the holy place: it is most holy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6a2ce1c-5d8d-4df1-a162-528fb6d860be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: LEV 7:7
Text: As the sin offering is, so is the trespass offering: there is one law for them: the priest that maketh atonement therewith shall have it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e85b7df0-ebc2-4f56-8a28-ed7318669e2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: LEV 7:8
Text: And the priest that offereth any man’s burnt offering, even the priest shall have to himself the skin of the burnt offering which he hath offered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79796a91-4987-4058-830c-cc16cab601cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: LEV 7:9
Text: And all the meat offering that is baken in the oven, and all that is dressed in the fryingpan, and in the pan, shall be the priest’s that offereth it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:291d1b08-a7fd-4bf1-9b07-8f413eb36b5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: LEV 7:10
Text: And every meat offering, mingled with oil, and dry, shall all the sons of Aaron have, one as much as another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4609b7d7-0e66-48bf-b1fa-3fb52cc65c33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: LEV 7:11
Text: And this is the law of the sacrifice of peace offerings, which he shall offer unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b1bc4a8-308c-41e0-bbcb-136f71f2a601>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: LEV 7:12
Text: If he offer it for a thanksgiving, then he shall offer with the sacrifice of thanksgiving unleavened cakes mingled with oil, and unleavened wafers anointed with oil, and cakes mingled with oil, of fine flour, fried.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5ad6acb-fbea-4c67-a164-b8ca254665b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: LEV 7:13
Text: Besides the cakes, he shall offer for his offering leavened bread with the sacrifice of thanksgiving of his peace offerings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c99b6094-f450-4a0c-a7b7-91e17b413e4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: LEV 7:14
Text: And of it he shall offer one out of the whole oblation for an heave offering unto the LORD, and it shall be the priest’s that sprinkleth the blood of the peace offerings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9698aaf-2dd8-4b22-a595-be18f4ca22a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: LEV 7:15
Text: And the flesh of the sacrifice of his peace offerings for thanksgiving shall be eaten the same day that it is offered; he shall not leave any of it until the morning.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78f0a830-209d-44ec-9c8d-d4875d98bdcd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: LEV 7:16
Text: But if the sacrifice of his offering be a vow, or a voluntary offering, it shall be eaten the same day that he offereth his sacrifice: and on the morrow also the remainder of it shall be eaten:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fc20203-d7e2-4c0a-9741-09e22418fb03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: LEV 7:17
Text: But the remainder of the flesh of the sacrifice on the third day shall be burnt with fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2d77a90-d33c-44b2-b178-79d9ae2280b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 289

Reference: LEV 7:18
Text: And if any of the flesh of the sacrifice of his peace offerings be eaten at all on the third day, it shall not be accepted, neither shall it be imputed unto him that offereth it: it shall be an abomination, and the soul that eateth of it shall bear his iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:889dbad3-75a3-44c8-91a6-34c67957ee13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: LEV 7:19
Text: And the flesh that toucheth any unclean thing shall not be eaten; it shall be burnt with fire: and as for the flesh, all that be clean shall eat thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:028cf39c-ca47-4998-ace0-a9fcd8e21b16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: LEV 7:20
Text: But the soul that eateth of the flesh of the sacrifice of peace offerings, that pertain unto the LORD, having his uncleanness upon him, even that soul shall be cut off from his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1b26199-d7d2-4f3d-8f77-eb62c4861182>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 298

Reference: LEV 7:21
Text: Moreover the soul that shall touch any unclean thing, as the uncleanness of man, or any unclean beast, or any abominable unclean thing, and eat of the flesh of the sacrifice of peace offerings, which pertain unto the LORD, even that soul shall be cut off from his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f98f8211-43f4-41ea-95b2-b8a6904dcefb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 65

Reference: LEV 7:22
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9369147d-c841-48b3-8296-e7e7e083e726>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: LEV 7:23
Text: Speak unto the children of Israel, saying, Ye shall eat no manner of fat, of ox, or of sheep, or of goat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:053d37df-a5b6-487d-a430-f7f674c0d37f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: LEV 7:24
Text: And the fat of the beast that dieth of itself, and the fat of that which is torn with beasts, may be used in any other use: but ye shall in no wise eat of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7576f53e-673a-47b1-8885-c80bef0a9302>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: LEV 7:25
Text: For whosoever eateth the fat of the beast, of which men offer an offering made by fire unto the LORD, even the soul that eateth it shall be cut off from his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51a0c9ba-f35a-4fc9-9751-61a27410fd10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: LEV 7:26
Text: Moreover ye shall eat no manner of blood, whether it be of fowl or of beast, in any of your dwellings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab780486-1f1d-49ae-8569-1fcd98ca6e03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: LEV 7:27
Text: Whatsoever soul it be that eateth any manner of blood, even that soul shall be cut off from his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc733c84-3a16-4fb4-bda3-bfa8f99358a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 65

Reference: LEV 7:28
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12117996-c5fd-45fc-bd4d-57f1235167df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: LEV 7:29
Text: Speak unto the children of Israel, saying, He that offereth the sacrifice of his peace offerings unto the LORD shall bring his oblation unto the LORD of the sacrifice of his peace offerings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd831b2a-3ba3-4932-871d-8adb819fffc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: LEV 7:30
Text: His own hands shall bring the offerings of the LORD made by fire, the fat with the breast, it shall he bring, that the breast may be waved for a wave offering before the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3e0fded-b935-4638-8848-6cdcb2775dfd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: LEV 7:31
Text: And the priest shall burn the fat upon the altar: but the breast shall be Aaron’s and his sons’.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46e2d156-d264-4d64-acc4-56a77ec8e6fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: LEV 7:32
Text: And the right shoulder shall ye give unto the priest for an heave offering of the sacrifices of your peace offerings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b30cd90d-ddcd-4fa7-93e9-7164f0fad9a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: LEV 7:33
Text: He among the sons of Aaron, that offereth the blood of the peace offerings, and the fat, shall have the right shoulder for his part.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb54d21b-ccc4-4ce8-bcf6-1c2151f8e7e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: LEV 7:34
Text: For the wave breast and the heave shoulder have I taken of the children of Israel from off the sacrifices of their peace offerings, and have given them unto Aaron the priest and unto his sons by a statute for ever from among the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47097f00-d1e5-44de-9586-ec858c45861f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: LEV 7:35
Text: This is the portion of the anointing of Aaron, and of the anointing of his sons, out of the offerings of the LORD made by fire, in the day when he presented them to minister unto the LORD in the priest’s office;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c900215-d083-4cb5-af7a-e06dc0214c93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: LEV 7:36
Text: Which the LORD commanded to be given them of the children of Israel, in the day that he anointed them, by a statute for ever throughout their generations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c2f1c46-b96d-434f-bc79-e9f1c83a0336>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: LEV 7:37
Text: This is the law of the burnt offering, of the meat offering, and of the sin offering, and of the trespass offering, and of the consecrations, and of the sacrifice of the peace offerings;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/7/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:070f16dc-b5db-40bd-b448-00d26e8ff4cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: LEV 7:38
Text: Which the LORD commanded Moses in mount Sinai, in the day that he commanded the children of Israel to offer their oblations unto the LORD, in the wilderness of Sinai.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ea8651f-895c-46e4-8335-87531f43d56a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 64

Reference: LEV 8:1
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3407deda-7adc-4a27-a6fa-2bd7836d6675>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: LEV 8:2
Text: Take Aaron and his sons with him, and the garments, and the anointing oil, and a bullock for the sin offering, and two rams, and a basket of unleavened bread;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:841b911c-ab45-42eb-afd9-df2b2600ab19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: LEV 8:3
Text: And gather thou all the congregation together unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47631538-c6c6-48f2-8d1f-6256fe79a8a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: LEV 8:4
Text: And Moses did as the LORD commanded him; and the assembly was gathered together unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe5ec695-bf49-4f47-83f4-ee57225d9997>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: LEV 8:5
Text: And Moses said unto the congregation, This is the thing which the LORD commanded to be done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db3d851f-1cef-4104-bfe6-c44f6a6d276d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: LEV 8:6
Text: And Moses brought Aaron and his sons, and washed them with water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c0231c3-e843-432e-8a0a-3352215d8477>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: LEV 8:7
Text: And he put upon him the coat, and girded him with the girdle, and clothed him with the robe, and put the ephod upon him, and he girded him with the curious girdle of the ephod, and bound it unto him therewith.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39c5febc-0325-4600-a593-f575ddbda539>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: LEV 8:8
Text: And he put the breastplate upon him: also he put in the breastplate the Urim and the Thummim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da5d2518-956a-4371-b588-2954100317a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: LEV 8:9
Text: And he put the mitre upon his head; also upon the mitre, even upon his forefront, did he put the golden plate, the holy crown; as the LORD commanded Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9688b376-362d-4a14-bb53-2ffdf269c5bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: LEV 8:10
Text: And Moses took the anointing oil, and anointed the tabernacle and all that was therein, and sanctified them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59fef5c5-2d8f-4dca-8230-d39238d630dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: LEV 8:11
Text: And he sprinkled thereof upon the altar seven times, and anointed the altar and all his vessels, both the laver and his foot, to sanctify them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bf7d09b-2540-450d-9ce7-89c6155188a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: LEV 8:12
Text: And he poured of the anointing oil upon Aaron’s head, and anointed him, to sanctify him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53bd878f-b876-4773-a8cc-8ae3ec08f98d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: LEV 8:13
Text: And Moses brought Aaron’s sons, and put coats upon them, and girded them with girdles, and put bonnets upon them; as the LORD commanded Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52ffc8fb-adc1-43cd-94fc-c1c02f5d1a82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: LEV 8:14
Text: And he brought the bullock for the sin offering: and Aaron and his sons laid their hands upon the head of the bullock for the sin offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5e4174c-151c-4fb0-a0f9-11e0cc53cd6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: LEV 8:15
Text: And he slew it; and Moses took the blood, and put it upon the horns of the altar round about with his finger, and purified the altar, and poured the blood at the bottom of the altar, and sanctified it, to make reconciliation upon it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42088dba-5c75-4d46-97b0-70c4e0e50c61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: LEV 8:16
Text: And he took all the fat that was upon the inwards, and the caul above the liver, and the two kidneys, and their fat, and Moses burned it upon the altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59169912-1cac-4077-9341-f0de31b5f610>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: LEV 8:17
Text: But the bullock, and his hide, his flesh, and his dung, he burnt with fire without the camp; as the LORD commanded Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e7f5a81-e551-404f-a4c7-0da156e9bb68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: LEV 8:18
Text: And he brought the ram for the burnt offering: and Aaron and his sons laid their hands upon the head of the ram.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4ef6c63-97ba-41b7-917f-850a46fa3f59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: LEV 8:19
Text: And he killed it; and Moses sprinkled the blood upon the altar round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:682a645d-99c5-4d8b-b26f-2ceca712165f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: LEV 8:20
Text: And he cut the ram into pieces; and Moses burnt the head, and the pieces, and the fat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e2fc66f-ccb6-41b3-8521-1b61090fb869>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: LEV 8:21
Text: And he washed the inwards and the legs in water; and Moses burnt the whole ram upon the altar: it was a burnt sacrifice for a sweet savour, and an offering made by fire unto the LORD; as the LORD commanded Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43d73492-1835-45c3-acde-54f975a27708>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: LEV 8:22
Text: And he brought the other ram, the ram of consecration: and Aaron and his sons laid their hands upon the head of the ram.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b5b3fd7-0e21-4bf9-b9c0-3eaf0ffc1f75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: LEV 8:23
Text: And he slew it; and Moses took of the blood of it, and put it upon the tip of Aaron’s right ear, and upon the thumb of his right hand, and upon the great toe of his right foot.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c833fcdf-26c9-451e-b7bc-831c2a447968>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 262

Reference: LEV 8:24
Text: And he brought Aaron’s sons, and Moses put of the blood upon the tip of their right ear, and upon the thumbs of their right hands, and upon the great toes of their right feet: and Moses sprinkled the blood upon the altar round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LEV/8/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
