Content-Length: 238

Reference: NUM 1:40
Text: Of the children of Asher, by their generations, after their families, by the house of their fathers, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/1/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a5b9e5c-9756-4a41-80ce-f09c6c79ed53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: NUM 1:41
Text: Those that were numbered of them, even of the tribe of Asher, were forty and one thousand and five hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/1/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d10cc285-ef05-4266-8c99-68307934aafc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: NUM 1:42
Text: Of the children of Naphtali, throughout their generations, after their families, by the house of their fathers, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/1/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea738c23-96d2-413f-9333-1be98827c173>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: NUM 1:43
Text: Those that were numbered of them, even of the tribe of Naphtali, were fifty and three thousand and four hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/1/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ad1af39-ac65-4224-b051-5c1ae2d39897>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: NUM 1:44
Text: These are those that were numbered, which Moses and Aaron numbered, and the princes of Israel, being twelve men: each one was for the house of his fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/1/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67d79019-e68e-41ae-946e-d8362fc2e027>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: NUM 1:45
Text: So were all those that were numbered of the children of Israel, by the house of their fathers, from twenty years old and upward, all that were able to go forth to war in Israel;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/1/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a165fd6-c9a5-4934-96c6-9d23154cb86d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: NUM 1:46
Text: Even all they that were numbered were six hundred thousand and three thousand and five hundred and fifty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/1/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0006fc63-dea5-4c51-9f2b-27776bfe7fb9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: NUM 1:47
Text: But the Levites after the tribe of their fathers were not numbered among them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/1/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:940dfca7-5cfc-46c4-b3a8-140b59e19ed3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 70

Reference: NUM 1:48
Text: For the LORD had spoken unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/1/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75c9dcaf-fdf9-4bf2-aee7-f85f0212e2fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: NUM 1:49
Text: Only thou shalt not number the tribe of Levi, neither take the sum of them among the children of Israel:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/1/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c7f6aac-a079-44a7-b9f2-12ab427a5e25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 307

Reference: NUM 1:50
Text: But thou shalt appoint the Levites over the tabernacle of testimony, and over all the vessels thereof, and over all things that belong to it: they shall bear the tabernacle, and all the vessels thereof; and they shall minister unto it, and shall encamp round about the tabernacle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/1/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b04d0150-e9d5-4d8e-b6f2-9092ec918ff9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: NUM 1:51
Text: And when the tabernacle setteth forward, the Levites shall take it down: and when the tabernacle is to be pitched, the Levites shall set it up: and the stranger that cometh nigh shall be put to death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/1/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:befaacef-b6aa-4b78-8cae-745271debd0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: NUM 1:52
Text: And the children of Israel shall pitch their tents, every man by his own camp, and every man by his own standard, throughout their hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/1/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:090ffb54-4a3b-46d7-a32f-c17e1dc40585>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: NUM 1:53
Text: But the Levites shall pitch round about the tabernacle of testimony, that there be no wrath upon the congregation of the children of Israel: and the Levites shall keep the charge of the tabernacle of testimony.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/1/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0279b94f-635f-4867-a5e3-9789ba33b437>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: NUM 1:54
Text: And the children of Israel did according to all that the LORD commanded Moses, so did they.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb624f67-81e4-44a8-9a3a-0f0c28a29b84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: NUM 2:1
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses and unto Aaron, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc9405b1-09e5-47e3-b432-5074fc485280>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: NUM 2:2
Text: Every man of the children of Israel shall pitch by his own standard, with the ensign of their father’s house: far off about the tabernacle of the congregation shall they pitch.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7100aeab-c5ad-4bd9-982e-1a8429b337d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: NUM 2:3
Text: And on the east side toward the rising of the sun shall they of the standard of the camp of Judah pitch throughout their armies: and Nahshon the son of Amminadab shall be captain of the children of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7952be03-48d5-4dfd-a8dd-925a73446ca9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: NUM 2:4
Text: And his host, and those that were numbered of them, were threescore and fourteen thousand and six hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef5e3e0f-0356-4108-a432-ebc8b4203f13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: NUM 2:5
Text: And those that do pitch next unto him shall be the tribe of Issachar: and Nethaneel the son of Zuar shall be captain of the children of Issachar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58023f92-6662-4362-a2e8-fd1432e723c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: NUM 2:6
Text: And his host, and those that were numbered thereof, were fifty and four thousand and four hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a183bee-f303-48cd-b9e9-a88df8553fd1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: NUM 2:7
Text: Then the tribe of Zebulun: and Eliab the son of Helon shall be captain of the children of Zebulun.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df502ac6-5431-446e-94da-22bcd2920e61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: NUM 2:8
Text: And his host, and those that were numbered thereof, were fifty and seven thousand and four hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cdbf31bc-ecbc-4ba4-b2bd-0fdc9c0ab446>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: NUM 2:9
Text: All that were numbered in the camp of Judah were an hundred thousand and fourscore thousand and six thousand and four hundred, throughout their armies. These shall first set forth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1850daeb-c456-4aeb-ad6a-8bf9f25c7f67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: NUM 2:10
Text: On the south side shall be the standard of the camp of Reuben according to their armies: and the captain of the children of Reuben shall be Elizur the son of Shedeur.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2b13bb2-f120-46b4-b1a5-be0067d70a64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: NUM 2:11
Text: And his host, and those that were numbered thereof, were forty and six thousand and five hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fdaffaa0-0d68-455c-9940-ad5759dc9fd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: NUM 2:12
Text: And those which pitch by him shall be the tribe of Simeon: and the captain of the children of Simeon shall be Shelumiel the son of Zurishaddai.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ab3c18a-ff6b-400d-91e4-ace057149986>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: NUM 2:13
Text: And his host, and those that were numbered of them, were fifty and nine thousand and three hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8e54cfd-9e7e-4f37-a531-9c8956630b22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: NUM 2:14
Text: Then the tribe of Gad: and the captain of the sons of Gad shall be Eliasaph the son of Reuel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26d842cc-b903-4e28-94cf-0440f226e144>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: NUM 2:15
Text: And his host, and those that were numbered of them, were forty and five thousand and six hundred and fifty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3309cf06-7981-4cfb-8d59-5feb99083547>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: NUM 2:16
Text: All that were numbered in the camp of Reuben were an hundred thousand and fifty and one thousand and four hundred and fifty, throughout their armies. And they shall set forth in the second rank.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e101b874-160b-4a7e-9b3b-805bbad0bc6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: NUM 2:17
Text: Then the tabernacle of the congregation shall set forward with the camp of the Levites in the midst of the camp: as they encamp, so shall they set forward, every man in his place by their standards.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2853278e-3183-4dc1-a397-aacbd99a7bd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: NUM 2:18
Text: On the west side shall be the standard of the camp of Ephraim according to their armies: and the captain of the sons of Ephraim shall be Elishama the son of Ammihud.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67c8f6ed-af46-45a5-a655-77089ce961de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: NUM 2:19
Text: And his host, and those that were numbered of them, were forty thousand and five hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f88edc49-4572-47ba-8758-00f8260af459>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: NUM 2:20
Text: And by him shall be the tribe of Manasseh: and the captain of the children of Manasseh shall be Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b6cae9e-a6b1-47a5-95a1-1ee6e938122e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: NUM 2:21
Text: And his host, and those that were numbered of them, were thirty and two thousand and two hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69b7967c-2f28-4b42-b46e-999346145046>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: NUM 2:22
Text: Then the tribe of Benjamin: and the captain of the sons of Benjamin shall be Abidan the son of Gideoni.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37064108-b99b-4db3-807d-651a1583dd4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: NUM 2:23
Text: And his host, and those that were numbered of them, were thirty and five thousand and four hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80db69de-22da-46e8-932d-bb7b523310a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: NUM 2:24
Text: All that were numbered of the camp of Ephraim were an hundred thousand and eight thousand and an hundred, throughout their armies. And they shall go forward in the third rank.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3476127-1bdc-4f46-bc8f-26312c2eeffd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: NUM 2:25
Text: The standard of the camp of Dan shall be on the north side by their armies: and the captain of the children of Dan shall be Ahiezer the son of Ammishaddai.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c84b978-9d75-4ae4-858c-921e3fe726b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: NUM 2:26
Text: And his host, and those that were numbered of them, were threescore and two thousand and seven hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0dabc82b-24b4-418a-b97b-a5c393b892ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: NUM 2:27
Text: And those that encamp by him shall be the tribe of Asher: and the captain of the children of Asher shall be Pagiel the son of Ocran.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27e51cb3-db34-489a-9ded-364a7bcf6fb7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: NUM 2:28
Text: And his host, and those that were numbered of them, were forty and one thousand and five hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f78ea408-f2e4-47b7-95d6-d654578b7457>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: NUM 2:29
Text: Then the tribe of Naphtali: and the captain of the children of Naphtali shall be Ahira the son of Enan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e53a40fb-835c-4c84-b4ce-8460ec759e28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: NUM 2:30
Text: And his host, and those that were numbered of them, were fifty and three thousand and four hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4dbaed43-1254-4cbb-8c69-c4dd92bdd892>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: NUM 2:31
Text: All they that were numbered in the camp of Dan were an hundred thousand and fifty and seven thousand and six hundred. They shall go hindmost with their standards.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1e9816b-7f73-4313-ae5a-76ef50a41e14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: NUM 2:32
Text: These are those which were numbered of the children of Israel by the house of their fathers: all those that were numbered of the camps throughout their hosts were six hundred thousand and three thousand and five hundred and fifty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1adfa787-21c0-4ec6-bbce-628e39f7a88c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: NUM 2:33
Text: But the Levites were not numbered among the children of Israel; as the LORD commanded Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/2/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d6929fe-7516-43eb-b723-2e321b1d2b02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: NUM 2:34
Text: And the children of Israel did according to all that the LORD commanded Moses: so they pitched by their standards, and so they set forward, every one after their families, according to the house of their fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3acf3fdb-f13e-4278-a6fc-4a728636055f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: NUM 3:1
Text: These also are the generations of Aaron and Moses in the day that the LORD spake with Moses in mount Sinai.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6e8366d-0323-49ee-9854-af33fadbe5a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: NUM 3:2
Text: And these are the names of the sons of Aaron; Nadab the firstborn, and Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c95264fe-67b7-43f1-973f-b04091c44fb7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: NUM 3:3
Text: These are the names of the sons of Aaron, the priests which were anointed, whom he consecrated to minister in the priest’s office.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:490893c7-7fab-40f7-ac45-dd883e36f752>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: NUM 3:4
Text: And Nadab and Abihu died before the LORD, when they offered strange fire before the LORD, in the wilderness of Sinai, and they had no children: and Eleazar and Ithamar ministered in the priest’s office in the sight of Aaron their father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
