Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 64

Reference: NUM 3:5
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:134ea448-86c8-4744-8507-1f1151596adb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: NUM 3:6
Text: Bring the tribe of Levi near, and present them before Aaron the priest, that they may minister unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b60eca5-ea02-40f4-b45b-88ae391828e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: NUM 3:7
Text: And they shall keep his charge, and the charge of the whole congregation before the tabernacle of the congregation, to do the service of the tabernacle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2490a52a-e3c7-44bc-8754-b515c09ff51d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: NUM 3:8
Text: And they shall keep all the instruments of the tabernacle of the congregation, and the charge of the children of Israel, to do the service of the tabernacle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b256a8f0-896e-469f-8b5b-5abd58308677>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: NUM 3:9
Text: And thou shalt give the Levites unto Aaron and to his sons: they are wholly given unto him out of the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c044dddf-a2a3-4879-a67e-48a01779a8ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: NUM 3:10
Text: And thou shalt appoint Aaron and his sons, and they shall wait on their priest’s office: and the stranger that cometh nigh shall be put to death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f955f30-646b-4270-92b5-81ee126daa84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 65

Reference: NUM 3:11
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56841e02-69db-4c61-9b54-07252ec85f52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: NUM 3:12
Text: And I, behold, I have taken the Levites from among the children of Israel instead of all the firstborn that openeth the matrix among the children of Israel: therefore the Levites shall be mine;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5b20ef1-0013-476c-a698-c8d2cd167cf8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: NUM 3:13
Text: Because all the firstborn are mine; for on the day that I smote all the firstborn in the land of Egypt I hallowed unto me all the firstborn in Israel, both man and beast: mine shall they be: I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2cd8baa9-d509-4533-ab26-692ae5b88487>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: NUM 3:14
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses in the wilderness of Sinai, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cf572dc-fda9-47c9-a033-47b518cee81b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: NUM 3:15
Text: Number the children of Levi after the house of their fathers, by their families: every male from a month old and upward shalt thou number them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:768dab68-cb62-4863-b9e7-669e2201170c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: NUM 3:16
Text: And Moses numbered them according to the word of the LORD, as he was commanded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82296630-671a-4aeb-a628-df8d0eaff78c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: NUM 3:17
Text: And these were the sons of Levi by their names; Gershon, and Kohath, and Merari.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:439c1277-269f-4c16-9a98-a150a9808d4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: NUM 3:18
Text: And these are the names of the sons of Gershon by their families; Libni, and Shimei.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b7c43b2-02e5-4656-9b40-b8ec02eec514>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: NUM 3:19
Text: And the sons of Kohath by their families; Amram, and Izehar, Hebron, and Uzziel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3c21f9e-5d19-4b54-b3f3-df5df10dcccd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: NUM 3:20
Text: And the sons of Merari by their families; Mahli, and Mushi. These are the families of the Levites according to the house of their fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b602585-2609-4efb-add8-821ad81b0c81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: NUM 3:21
Text: Of Gershon was the family of the Libnites, and the family of the Shimites: these are the families of the Gershonites.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ebc8f47-efa7-4402-a705-871ec3bd3286>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: NUM 3:22
Text: Those that were numbered of them, according to the number of all the males, from a month old and upward, even those that were numbered of them were seven thousand and five hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba1d2936-e042-4d05-96da-8af94c1c3ee2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: NUM 3:23
Text: The families of the Gershonites shall pitch behind the tabernacle westward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa49b669-40ba-40bf-ba61-df56b93ec7e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: NUM 3:24
Text: And the chief of the house of the father of the Gershonites shall be Eliasaph the son of Lael.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38c5c1bc-2163-488a-88b9-e40cb04112ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: NUM 3:25
Text: And the charge of the sons of Gershon in the tabernacle of the congregation shall be the tabernacle, and the tent, the covering thereof, and the hanging for the door of the tabernacle of the congregation,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ddecd6a-8c4c-4149-a0b2-92b129f83c81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: NUM 3:26
Text: And the hangings of the court, and the curtain for the door of the court, which is by the tabernacle, and by the altar round about, and the cords of it for all the service thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3cbf3f2-a2e3-48e5-9105-1ddbdf75c1a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: NUM 3:27
Text: And of Kohath was the family of the Amramites, and the family of the Izeharites, and the family of the Hebronites, and the family of the Uzzielites: these are the families of the Kohathites.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9846029-ab74-4505-9faa-8846bad9fad3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: NUM 3:28
Text: In the number of all the males, from a month old and upward, were eight thousand and six hundred, keeping the charge of the sanctuary.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad939a70-2895-4c36-8808-d4ee822c93b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: NUM 3:29
Text: The families of the sons of Kohath shall pitch on the side of the tabernacle southward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f33dd582-08fb-4b2f-9ff7-2f2abe808c3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: NUM 3:30
Text: And the chief of the house of the father of the families of the Kohathites shall be Elizaphan the son of Uzziel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d86fbf3d-93a2-4482-90f0-520cf162d403>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: NUM 3:31
Text: And their charge shall be the ark, and the table, and the candlestick, and the altars, and the vessels of the sanctuary wherewith they minister, and the hanging, and all the service thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:763f7e8e-cede-4520-a98a-be545f3cc0ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: NUM 3:32
Text: And Eleazar the son of Aaron the priest shall be chief over the chief of the Levites, and have the oversight of them that keep the charge of the sanctuary.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66c1c56c-7c30-43e8-b598-9cad4f85edad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: NUM 3:33
Text: Of Merari was the family of the Mahlites, and the family of the Mushites: these are the families of Merari.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70e8fe8a-f7a8-4b2f-9b38-cc234c6469f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: NUM 3:34
Text: And those that were numbered of them, according to the number of all the males, from a month old and upward, were six thousand and two hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68215c15-4be2-4e87-b249-c2c6b5a58a54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: NUM 3:35
Text: And the chief of the house of the father of the families of Merari was Zuriel the son of Abihail: these shall pitch on the side of the tabernacle northward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:508bc9b8-89f5-426e-ba88-0a676b57c974>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: NUM 3:36
Text: And under the custody and charge of the sons of Merari shall be the boards of the tabernacle, and the bars thereof, and the pillars thereof, and the sockets thereof, and all the vessels thereof, and all that serveth thereto,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:307d1787-0b43-47d6-bfdb-1bcf73e207ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: NUM 3:37
Text: And the pillars of the court round about, and their sockets, and their pins, and their cords.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a1cab92-8aee-49cf-a47c-d37fea12e02e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 319

Reference: NUM 3:38
Text: But those that encamp before the tabernacle toward the east, even before the tabernacle of the congregation eastward, shall be Moses, and Aaron and his sons, keeping the charge of the sanctuary for the charge of the children of Israel; and the stranger that cometh nigh shall be put to death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bcb923c9-7287-40c9-8bba-f25def480cd4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: NUM 3:39
Text: All that were numbered of the Levites, which Moses and Aaron numbered at the commandment of the LORD, throughout their families, all the males from a month old and upward, were twenty and two thousand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a51b72bb-f96e-4bf3-be13-94d044974ecc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: NUM 3:40
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Number all the firstborn of the males of the children of Israel from a month old and upward, and take the number of their names.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27e59f17-a154-4715-9e75-0d2a24f55232>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: NUM 3:41
Text: And thou shalt take the Levites for me (I am the LORD) instead of all the firstborn among the children of Israel; and the cattle of the Levites instead of all the firstlings among the cattle of the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f69b429c-050a-406d-9936-b1657bd94fa1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: NUM 3:42
Text: And Moses numbered, as the LORD commanded him, all the firstborn among the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33abba7b-1661-4a0c-a298-3c166729adba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: NUM 3:43
Text: And all the firstborn males by the number of names, from a month old and upward, of those that were numbered of them, were twenty and two thousand two hundred and threescore and thirteen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01bdf00c-c369-4b77-83c5-e019da80d26b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 65

Reference: NUM 3:44
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c8380ea-7821-4451-b176-ce3daa92d465>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: NUM 3:45
Text: Take the Levites instead of all the firstborn among the children of Israel, and the cattle of the Levites instead of their cattle; and the Levites shall be mine: I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ce80522-3b40-48a7-a959-f3e5ba74fc06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: NUM 3:46
Text: And for those that are to be redeemed of the two hundred and threescore and thirteen of the firstborn of the children of Israel, which are more than the Levites;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c809999-2811-4883-b9b1-cb5a9d8952ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: NUM 3:47
Text: Thou shalt even take five shekels apiece by the poll, after the shekel of the sanctuary shalt thou take them: (the shekel is twenty gerahs:)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f15593d2-fe3a-4ac2-abd6-98954a6ae558>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: NUM 3:48
Text: And thou shalt give the money, wherewith the odd number of them is to be redeemed, unto Aaron and to his sons.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f216e98-cbfb-4a3c-8c32-33222cbac42b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: NUM 3:49
Text: And Moses took the redemption money of them that were over and above them that were redeemed by the Levites:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a8cfb61-a184-41a5-96b8-b0f53e2cc4e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: NUM 3:50
Text: Of the firstborn of the children of Israel took he the money; a thousand three hundred and threescore and five shekels, after the shekel of the sanctuary:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/3/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6fc67795-6f4b-4748-b429-cda008831951>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: NUM 3:51
Text: And Moses gave the money of them that were redeemed unto Aaron and to his sons, according to the word of the LORD, as the LORD commanded Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0994d3de-20b8-4e43-b56e-8a33971f9319>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: NUM 4:1
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses and unto Aaron, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5a068c9-61ef-46da-b3ae-ce9f8ec8149b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: NUM 4:2
Text: Take the sum of the sons of Kohath from among the sons of Levi, after their families, by the house of their fathers,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ace261e9-0b4e-4b8d-8748-cbafd7395ad2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: NUM 4:3
Text: From thirty years old and upward even until fifty years old, all that enter into the host, to do the work in the tabernacle of the congregation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aac8fd49-8cb6-4a3f-bb4a-a4a93f721b95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: NUM 4:4
Text: This shall be the service of the sons of Kohath in the tabernacle of the congregation, about the most holy things:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46f1ab26-ac79-49f4-9d23-fc9994a6c621>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: NUM 4:5
Text: And when the camp setteth forward, Aaron shall come, and his sons, and they shall take down the covering vail, and cover the ark of testimony with it:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:977a40de-7e00-4f6c-89a0-1af35bcf7334>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: NUM 4:6
Text: And shall put thereon the covering of badgers’ skins, and shall spread over it a cloth wholly of blue, and shall put in the staves thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4398b4f-88c9-4029-9ddc-7af153e45702>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: NUM 4:7
Text: And upon the table of shewbread they shall spread a cloth of blue, and put thereon the dishes, and the spoons, and the bowls, and covers to cover withal: and the continual bread shall be thereon:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34854196-455f-45aa-9ef6-2d8416efbecc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: NUM 4:8
Text: And they shall spread upon them a cloth of scarlet, and cover the same with a covering of badgers’ skins, and shall put in the staves thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2803bdf2-a04f-49e0-83e5-e917db837a38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: NUM 4:9
Text: And they shall take a cloth of blue, and cover the candlestick of the light, and his lamps, and his tongs, and his snuffdishes, and all the oil vessels thereof, wherewith they minister unto it:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60690505-03d6-4b2c-b039-2815fc411628>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: NUM 4:10
Text: And they shall put it and all the vessels thereof within a covering of badgers’ skins, and shall put it upon a bar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f3042ad-0337-4a53-9032-0d7c846cab0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: NUM 4:11
Text: And upon the golden altar they shall spread a cloth of blue, and cover it with a covering of badgers’ skins, and shall put to the staves thereof:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7750c6d3-691c-4dc3-8ee9-ae682b4fe482>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: NUM 4:12
Text: And they shall take all the instruments of ministry, wherewith they minister in the sanctuary, and put them in a cloth of blue, and cover them with a covering of badgers’ skins, and shall put them on a bar:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9309abb6-08fc-4008-8f47-1a33100db7f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: NUM 4:13
Text: And they shall take away the ashes from the altar, and spread a purple cloth thereon:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ddcbc3e-7c7e-4753-b46c-8a7e8fec13c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 300

Reference: NUM 4:14
Text: And they shall put upon it all the vessels thereof, wherewith they minister about it, even the censers, the fleshhooks, and the shovels, and the basons, all the vessels of the altar; and they shall spread upon it a covering of badgers’ skins, and put to the staves of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1465e183-1046-497e-8aad-2239cab5f57d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 366

Reference: NUM 4:15
Text: And when Aaron and his sons have made an end of covering the sanctuary, and all the vessels of the sanctuary, as the camp is to set forward; after that, the sons of Kohath shall come to bear it: but they shall not touch any holy thing, lest they die. These things are the burden of the sons of Kohath in the tabernacle of the congregation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ca3b252-7a9b-4fc7-b455-4d142854c273>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 307

Reference: NUM 4:16
Text: And to the office of Eleazar the son of Aaron the priest pertaineth the oil for the light, and the sweet incense, and the daily meat offering, and the anointing oil, and the oversight of all the tabernacle, and of all that therein is, in the sanctuary, and in the vessels thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03781146-17a8-4573-8802-a30ff4058220>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: NUM 4:17
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses and unto Aaron saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b24b213-b8a8-455d-a883-7967894ecb9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: NUM 4:18
Text: Cut ye not off the tribe of the families of the Kohathites from among the Levites:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f75f6f5-3e7b-4cb0-8fb4-8c95498139fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: NUM 4:19
Text: But thus do unto them, that they may live, and not die, when they approach unto the most holy things: Aaron and his sons shall go in, and appoint them every one to his service and to his burden:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3be0cc94-2a3c-4231-91e6-df8a165efd16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: NUM 4:20
Text: But they shall not go in to see when the holy things are covered, lest they die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8041cd36-1713-41b2-9f2c-184050c4fae1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 65

Reference: NUM 4:21
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e27835a7-d427-4a98-a5ed-e2a1d1a672e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: NUM 4:22
Text: Take also the sum of the sons of Gershon, throughout the houses of their fathers, by their families;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ba9c5f7-b5a0-410a-88ed-faf487b93625>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: NUM 4:23
Text: From thirty years old and upward until fifty years old shalt thou number them; all that enter in to perform the service, to do the work in the tabernacle of the congregation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f17b9ef-6a72-492e-af7b-633744cb67d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: NUM 4:24
Text: This is the service of the families of the Gershonites, to serve, and for burdens:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cb868e4-0dd6-4ad6-b85c-ec9e77bc39e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: NUM 4:25
Text: And they shall bear the curtains of the tabernacle, and the tabernacle of the congregation, his covering, and the covering of the badgers’ skins that is above upon it, and the hanging for the door of the tabernacle of the congregation,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7227e333-016b-4d3e-88f3-a0d9d3ee1d4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 280

Reference: NUM 4:26
Text: And the hangings of the court, and the hanging for the door of the gate of the court, which is by the tabernacle and by the altar round about, and their cords, and all the instruments of their service, and all that is made for them: so shall they serve.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0c40e84-e36b-4007-bae6-69ba2379369d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: NUM 4:27
Text: At the appointment of Aaron and his sons shall be all the service of the sons of the Gershonites, in all their burdens, and in all their service: and ye shall appoint unto them in charge all their burdens.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d259467-e647-432a-ae90-32488198693b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: NUM 4:28
Text: This is the service of the families of the sons of Gershon in the tabernacle of the congregation: and their charge shall be under the hand of Ithamar the son of Aaron the priest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e21c90d8-0017-463e-88f6-af2661f2eab4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: NUM 4:29
Text: As for the sons of Merari, thou shalt number them after their families, by the house of their fathers;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ebffe5c-2be3-4a3c-aa61-aa8c13ec7fbe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: NUM 4:30
Text: From thirty years old and upward even unto fifty years old shalt thou number them, every one that entereth into the service, to do the work of the tabernacle of the congregation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e2eb2cc-51fd-4a44-84e8-ea1eee02c4ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: NUM 4:31
Text: And this is the charge of their burden, according to all their service in the tabernacle of the congregation; the boards of the tabernacle, and the bars thereof, and the pillars thereof, and sockets thereof,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cfad8bc-8d28-45d7-a6c4-4f9d959b481d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: NUM 4:32
Text: And the pillars of the court round about, and their sockets, and their pins, and their cords, with all their instruments, and with all their service: and by name ye shall reckon the instruments of the charge of their burden.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38699d28-46ef-4636-8a49-c43f2209f938>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: NUM 4:33
Text: This is the service of the families of the sons of Merari, according to all their service, in the tabernacle of the congregation, under the hand of Ithamar the son of Aaron the priest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f437f231-9546-41e9-bde3-7a204580e33b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: NUM 4:34
Text: And Moses and Aaron and the chief of the congregation numbered the sons of the Kohathites after their families, and after the house of their fathers,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a28d16c-90eb-4fe9-b169-723c92cfd256>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: NUM 4:35
Text: From thirty years old and upward even unto fifty years old, every one that entereth into the service, for the work in the tabernacle of the congregation:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b249f1d-213b-40b0-8bfd-4b84e07b472a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: NUM 4:36
Text: And those that were numbered of them by their families were two thousand seven hundred and fifty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32f9bd7a-165b-4737-a750-2af57937f09c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: NUM 4:37
Text: These were they that were numbered of the families of the Kohathites, all that might do service in the tabernacle of the congregation, which Moses and Aaron did number according to the commandment of the LORD by the hand of Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9473d6e6-eab0-4c4f-9aa2-6be09f58ad3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: NUM 4:38
Text: And those that were numbered of the sons of Gershon, throughout their families, and by the house of their fathers,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b586fa56-0591-4e55-9fc1-7cba717a318b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: NUM 4:39
Text: From thirty years old and upward even unto fifty years old, every one that entereth into the service, for the work in the tabernacle of the congregation,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4821ba90-c788-4b36-8a89-c2986962b1a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: NUM 4:40
Text: Even those that were numbered of them, throughout their families, by the house of their fathers, were two thousand and six hundred and thirty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ff4cce8-188e-4f4d-a6d0-3670e228d578>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: NUM 4:41
Text: These are they that were numbered of the families of the sons of Gershon, of all that might do service in the tabernacle of the congregation, whom Moses and Aaron did number according to the commandment of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b647e00-66eb-49f5-a21a-660524741c91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: NUM 4:42
Text: And those that were numbered of the families of the sons of Merari, throughout their families, by the house of their fathers,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc8dc9ed-fc37-47e7-87c5-3f2c0c21d895>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: NUM 4:43
Text: From thirty years old and upward even unto fifty years old, every one that entereth into the service, for the work in the tabernacle of the congregation,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5880fa1-acec-4a6d-866e-11fd78d8ce16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: NUM 4:44
Text: Even those that were numbered of them after their families, were three thousand and two hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e99f2843-4c04-4e9c-ae7a-b8ec619a5036>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: NUM 4:45
Text: These be those that were numbered of the families of the sons of Merari, whom Moses and Aaron numbered according to the word of the LORD by the hand of Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:902f67ec-8610-4ac6-b3e2-ab597c0601b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: NUM 4:46
Text: All those that were numbered of the Levites, whom Moses and Aaron and the chief of Israel numbered, after their families, and after the house of their fathers,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09a79a2c-62ae-4b27-933a-e87ab7185e06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: NUM 4:47
Text: From thirty years old and upward even unto fifty years old, every one that came to do the service of the ministry, and the service of the burden in the tabernacle of the congregation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7aa5ddd8-ef4c-46c9-9b18-18002ed51618>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: NUM 4:48
Text: Even those that were numbered of them, were eight thousand and five hundred and fourscore,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/4/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3c349b5-d956-4830-8bda-58afb0b11a49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: NUM 4:49
Text: According to the commandment of the LORD they were numbered by the hand of Moses, every one according to his service, and according to his burden: thus were they numbered of him, as the LORD commanded Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6870ee99-c94d-45e5-a1fe-29a0408b1e0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 64

Reference: NUM 5:1
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79052e73-bed6-4c06-a1d0-3533f945c975>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: NUM 5:2
Text: Command the children of Israel, that they put out of the camp every leper, and every one that hath an issue, and whosoever is defiled by the dead:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32437548-2c91-4f82-963f-ea31f3e44579>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: NUM 5:3
Text: Both male and female shall ye put out, without the camp shall ye put them; that they defile not their camps, in the midst whereof I dwell.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6360f97-df1a-4f1f-ac19-43df015c2742>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: NUM 5:4
Text: And the children of Israel did so, and put them out without the camp: as the LORD spake unto Moses, so did the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa14f9b6-f714-4079-9046-791fb871158d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 64

Reference: NUM 5:5
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dac3caf0-b980-4706-8a10-60ec4c3013a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: NUM 5:6
Text: Speak unto the children of Israel, When a man or woman shall commit any sin that men commit, to do a trespass against the LORD, and that person be guilty;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12101d32-fae9-440d-8ab3-87fa18ae603c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: NUM 5:7
Text: Then they shall confess their sin which they have done: and he shall recompense his trespass with the principal thereof, and add unto it the fifth part thereof, and give it unto him against whom he hath trespassed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bfda5d6-37c7-42b1-9429-fb5d94e21d18>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: NUM 5:8
Text: But if the man have no kinsman to recompense the trespass unto, let the trespass be recompensed unto the LORD, even to the priest; beside the ram of the atonement, whereby an atonement shall be made for him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0c1f9c8-b9fb-4ba6-8a8a-77da47e2a54c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: NUM 5:9
Text: And every offering of all the holy things of the children of Israel, which they bring unto the priest, shall be his.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05010903-3cc9-47c6-8c9f-ea86ab560d05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: NUM 5:10
Text: And every man’s hallowed things shall be his: whatsoever any man giveth the priest, it shall be his.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35769921-1388-4abd-b733-abb5dd82cc62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 65

Reference: NUM 5:11
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00f93230-e8ba-43d1-b68e-8d4eb960de2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: NUM 5:12
Text: Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, If any man’s wife go aside, and commit a trespass against him,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f1667a4-b7e5-4e54-b974-d55a8b8095c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: NUM 5:13
Text: And a man lie with her carnally, and it be hid from the eyes of her husband, and be kept close, and she be defiled, and there be no witness against her, neither she be taken with the manner;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb5a8729-72a7-4698-9d79-a990dc6a4426>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: NUM 5:14
Text: And the spirit of jealousy come upon him, and he be jealous of his wife, and she be defiled: or if the spirit of jealousy come upon him, and he be jealous of his wife, and she be not defiled:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7268e5b-1369-4adc-86bb-1e637cfdc363>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 315

Reference: NUM 5:15
Text: Then shall the man bring his wife unto the priest, and he shall bring her offering for her, the tenth part of an ephah of barley meal; he shall pour no oil upon it, nor put frankincense thereon; for it is an offering of jealousy, an offering of memorial, bringing iniquity to remembrance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3133f11b-6f55-431d-9869-fa0ed55b0db1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: NUM 5:16
Text: And the priest shall bring her near, and set her before the LORD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99902ba6-08d9-4bff-98ae-8b95afb8b57a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: NUM 5:17
Text: And the priest shall take holy water in an earthen vessel; and of the dust that is in the floor of the tabernacle the priest shall take, and put it into the water:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9da0756e-a9eb-4928-bd2a-b232e7e05f5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: NUM 5:18
Text: And the priest shall set the woman before the LORD, and uncover the woman’s head, and put the offering of memorial in her hands, which is the jealousy offering: and the priest shall have in his hand the bitter water that causeth the curse:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7ce799a-1986-4a49-b5a5-8fdcdd6977a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: NUM 5:19
Text: And the priest shall charge her by an oath, and say unto the woman, If no man have lain with thee, and if thou hast not gone aside to uncleanness with another instead of thy husband, be thou free from this bitter water that causeth the curse:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50544104-c6d8-4d8c-9a67-32a183f08f05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: NUM 5:20
Text: But if thou hast gone aside to another instead of thy husband, and if thou be defiled, and some man have lain with thee beside thine husband:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03080983-9a25-4d7d-be35-5f4ee8ec3f2f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: NUM 5:21
Text: Then the priest shall charge the woman with an oath of cursing, and the priest shall say unto the woman, The LORD make thee a curse and an oath among thy people, when the LORD doth make thy thigh to rot, and thy belly to swell;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e8139c7-03be-44e7-9fcb-ef5a0334835e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: NUM 5:22
Text: And this water that causeth the curse shall go into thy bowels, to make thy belly to swell, and thy thigh to rot: And the woman shall say, Amen, amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a990819d-78ec-4141-bc4b-1e683fd3cd24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: NUM 5:23
Text: And the priest shall write these curses in a book, and he shall blot them out with the bitter water:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:787b2591-13cb-403f-899d-0e0de06fb178>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: NUM 5:24
Text: And he shall cause the woman to drink the bitter water that causeth the curse: and the water that causeth the curse shall enter into her, and become bitter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e51cc5c-2304-4860-b377-a42a3e4cbc7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: NUM 5:25
Text: Then the priest shall take the jealousy offering out of the woman’s hand, and shall wave the offering before the LORD, and offer it upon the altar:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d71154e-917c-4a18-b60e-c4a4ec3ef7ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: NUM 5:26
Text: And the priest shall take an handful of the offering, even the memorial thereof, and burn it upon the altar, and afterward shall cause the woman to drink the water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c75a58b-3faa-43ed-b9c2-be374bce53d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 349

Reference: NUM 5:27
Text: And when he hath made her to drink the water, then it shall come to pass, that, if she be defiled, and have done trespass against her husband, that the water that causeth the curse shall enter into her, and become bitter, and her belly shall swell, and her thigh shall rot: and the woman shall be a curse among her people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd022e32-e108-48bb-9f38-bc98912a80cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: NUM 5:28
Text: And if the woman be not defiled, but be clean; then she shall be free, and shall conceive seed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13ea7cd6-fe4c-4dd9-b870-980760de9bb7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: NUM 5:29
Text: This is the law of jealousies, when a wife goeth aside to another instead of her husband, and is defiled;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e62267ee-2101-4869-b4fc-b8a9b84bac1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: NUM 5:30
Text: Or when the spirit of jealousy cometh upon him, and he be jealous over his wife, and shall set the woman before the LORD, and the priest shall execute upon her all this law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/5/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:808e9461-1b2d-4f54-b7dc-82f47372b68a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: NUM 5:31
Text: Then shall the man be guiltless from iniquity, and this woman shall bear her iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acd1fbc7-bb05-4b39-a122-2b17ef0adf9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 64

Reference: NUM 6:1
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0402518b-893e-4f14-a286-09fbc1482151>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: NUM 6:2
Text: Speak unto the children of Israel, and say unto them, When either man or woman shall separate themselves to vow a vow of a Nazarite, to separate themselves unto the LORD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d933248-1508-4fe5-ba32-e1d78c84b325>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: NUM 6:3
Text: He shall separate himself from wine and strong drink, and shall drink no vinegar of wine, or vinegar of strong drink, neither shall he drink any liquor of grapes, nor eat moist grapes, or dried.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9244a3de-2672-470d-8526-dbda390a119a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: NUM 6:4
Text: All the days of his separation shall he eat nothing that is made of the vine tree, from the kernels even to the husk.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f021a9a-51dd-467c-9f89-8c91ede018e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: NUM 6:5
Text: All the days of the vow of his separation there shall no razor come upon his head: until the days be fulfilled, in the which he separateth himself unto the LORD, he shall be holy, and shall let the locks of the hair of his head grow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52c21fad-a5aa-4d52-bec6-e69af778f839>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: NUM 6:6
Text: All the days that he separateth himself unto the LORD he shall come at no dead body.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:462b2ef4-5e55-42aa-9d02-c8754a0ce5a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: NUM 6:7
Text: He shall not make himself unclean for his father, or for his mother, for his brother, or for his sister, when they die: because the consecration of his God is upon his head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:986f7504-0971-4d6f-bbce-4b66781f3645>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: NUM 6:8
Text: All the days of his separation he is holy unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df77936e-529b-469e-bbec-73ebaba894af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: NUM 6:9
Text: And if any man die very suddenly by him, and he hath defiled the head of his consecration; then he shall shave his head in the day of his cleansing, on the seventh day shall he shave it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35ac5e40-bdfb-44e6-bfac-11ba3dfa07e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: NUM 6:10
Text: And on the eighth day he shall bring two turtles, or two young pigeons, to the priest, to the door of the tabernacle of the congregation:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5123afe1-fcc4-4227-a05f-6f43b46e8192>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: NUM 6:11
Text: And the priest shall offer the one for a sin offering, and the other for a burnt offering, and make an atonement for him, for that he sinned by the dead, and shall hallow his head that same day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4025b00c-53ef-4da7-8b38-d3c4f5b78632>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: NUM 6:12
Text: And he shall consecrate unto the LORD the days of his separation, and shall bring a lamb of the first year for a trespass offering: but the days that were before shall be lost, because his separation was defiled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06799e37-0ddb-48ef-8283-586cdd6c3e97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: NUM 6:13
Text: And this is the law of the Nazarite, when the days of his separation are fulfilled: he shall be brought unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d52787e-1d24-4e2d-ae12-ed61bac3882e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: NUM 6:14
Text: And he shall offer his offering unto the LORD, one he lamb of the first year without blemish for a burnt offering, and one ewe lamb of the first year without blemish for a sin offering, and one ram without blemish for peace offerings,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66dbb37c-033d-4729-925d-c8e1396aab01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: NUM 6:15
Text: And a basket of unleavened bread, cakes of fine flour mingled with oil, and wafers of unleavened bread anointed with oil, and their meat offering, and their drink offerings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d359039b-522a-492d-b815-00c1d3ee15b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: NUM 6:16
Text: And the priest shall bring them before the LORD, and shall offer his sin offering, and his burnt offering:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0677f8d6-ae28-4efd-bade-da0c2ca461dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: NUM 6:17
Text: And he shall offer the ram for a sacrifice of peace offerings unto the LORD, with the basket of unleavened bread: the priest shall offer also his meat offering, and his drink offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:215979da-53a7-4e72-8abe-2cfe6404be22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: NUM 6:18
Text: And the Nazarite shall shave the head of his separation at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, and shall take the hair of the head of his separation, and put it in the fire which is under the sacrifice of the peace offerings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07b8d881-ff65-41ac-bd3e-5d11c1122802>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: NUM 6:19
Text: And the priest shall take the sodden shoulder of the ram, and one unleavened cake out of the basket, and one unleavened wafer, and shall put them upon the hands of the Nazarite, after the hair of his separation is shaven:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0c124b5-f452-4b41-ae68-9e1f88f19e42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: NUM 6:20
Text: And the priest shall wave them for a wave offering before the LORD: this is holy for the priest, with the wave breast and heave shoulder: and after that the Nazarite may drink wine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a13956fc-b6a4-4dfd-8ae1-bb19954d5321>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: NUM 6:21
Text: This is the law of the Nazarite who hath vowed, and of his offering unto the LORD for his separation, beside that that his hand shall get: according to the vow which he vowed, so he must do after the law of his separation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81ecebf8-6073-4c65-a1a6-b7f601d1fb77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 65

Reference: NUM 6:22
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a547e8df-6cb1-4fdd-9a83-48b13e75b02b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: NUM 6:23
Text: Speak unto Aaron and unto his sons, saying, On this wise ye shall bless the children of Israel, saying unto them,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e8159fd-8cc1-4d02-a5b1-12482407a9a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 62

Reference: NUM 6:24
Text: The LORD bless thee, and keep thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70a8d9eb-842a-4cdc-896a-314d5915fb23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: NUM 6:25
Text: The LORD make his face shine upon thee, and be gracious unto thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a48e347a-e18f-4271-b4fc-626c47f556d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: NUM 6:26
Text: The LORD lift up his countenance upon thee, and give thee peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/6/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4aee36e-b577-4e3a-835a-9e7de5090be0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: NUM 6:27
Text: And they shall put my name upon the children of Israel, and I will bless them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/7/1
