Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: NUM 29:35
Text: On the eighth day ye shall have a solemn assembly: ye shall do no servile work therein:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/29/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1d065d7-aebe-41bb-bf5d-08c4f254f16f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: NUM 29:36
Text: But ye shall offer a burnt offering, a sacrifice made by fire, of a sweet savour unto the LORD: one bullock, one ram, seven lambs of the first year without blemish:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/29/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c6c4471-ee78-4208-8306-5c036834bd5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: NUM 29:37
Text: Their meat offering and their drink offerings for the bullock, for the ram, and for the lambs, shall be according to their number, after the manner:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/29/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc86f45a-08b6-484f-b65b-c7a86a6346cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: NUM 29:38
Text: And one goat for a sin offering; beside the continual burnt offering, and his meat offering, and his drink offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/29/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70e7d5b3-74e0-495c-a9f4-2f601905f955>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: NUM 29:39
Text: These things ye shall do unto the LORD in your set feasts, beside your vows, and your freewill offerings, for your burnt offerings, and for your meat offerings, and for your drink offerings, and for your peace offerings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/29/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06c39ca4-014d-48f4-aa11-e3471610f315>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: NUM 29:40
Text: And Moses told the children of Israel according to all that the LORD commanded Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/30/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ea013e5-0218-40ed-8b4f-6a7563647b82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: NUM 30:1
Text: And Moses spake unto the heads of the tribes concerning the children of Israel, saying, This is the thing which the LORD hath commanded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/30/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10d5a495-c474-4791-9a45-07e53b7cacbf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: NUM 30:2
Text: If a man vow a vow unto the LORD, or swear an oath to bind his soul with a bond; he shall not break his word, he shall do according to all that proceedeth out of his mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/30/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15854de7-27b2-45c6-b30a-2e98f14d4486>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: NUM 30:3
Text: If a woman also vow a vow unto the LORD, and bind herself by a bond, being in her father’s house in her youth;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/30/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfc2fd65-2a8f-4375-bf0d-9285bcc7e3ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: NUM 30:4
Text: And her father hear her vow, and her bond wherewith she hath bound her soul, and her father shall hold his peace at her; then all her vows shall stand, and every bond wherewith she hath bound her soul shall stand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/30/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30eab8f8-cdcc-4886-aa87-a3a39269663c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: NUM 30:5
Text: But if her father disallow her in the day that he heareth; not any of her vows, or of her bonds wherewith she hath bound her soul, shall stand: and the LORD shall forgive her, because her father disallowed her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/30/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d3a2468-1a9f-491c-b7da-fc37c286677b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: NUM 30:6
Text: And if she had at all an husband, when she vowed, or uttered ought out of her lips, wherewith she bound her soul;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/30/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d500431-0953-42a8-a30e-d94ca328bd2f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: NUM 30:7
Text: And her husband heard it, and held his peace at her in the day that he heard it: then her vows shall stand, and her bonds wherewith she bound her soul shall stand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/30/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44410e41-ebcb-4466-8187-43c35b61d2ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: NUM 30:8
Text: But if her husband disallowed her on the day that he heard it; then he shall make her vow which she vowed, and that which she uttered with her lips, wherewith she bound her soul, of none effect: and the LORD shall forgive her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/30/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed52840b-4ac5-4cdf-b38d-392a100cb162>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: NUM 30:9
Text: But every vow of a widow, and of her that is divorced, wherewith they have bound their souls, shall stand against her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/30/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5fa052cf-5af4-4560-99f4-0ce6a47af130>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: NUM 30:10
Text: And if she vowed in her husband’s house, or bound her soul by a bond with an oath;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/30/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d01d7a51-ef8f-4307-a65e-abfa1f4f5440>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: NUM 30:11
Text: And her husband heard it, and held his peace at her, and disallowed her not: then all her vows shall stand, and every bond wherewith she bound her soul shall stand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/30/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:302f3bc7-6ac9-408e-99e9-a1d5a8c79148>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 281

Reference: NUM 30:12
Text: But if her husband hath utterly made them void on the day he heard them; then whatsoever proceeded out of her lips concerning her vows, or concerning the bond of her soul, shall not stand: her husband hath made them void; and the LORD shall forgive her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/30/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ebc77c3-045e-42e1-a293-91c31439a043>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: NUM 30:13
Text: Every vow, and every binding oath to afflict the soul, her husband may establish it, or her husband may make it void.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/30/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9a21f1b-3cf7-4196-96a3-68d097b59ef5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: NUM 30:14
Text: But if her husband altogether hold his peace at her from day to day; then he establisheth all her vows, or all her bonds, which are upon her: he confirmeth them, because he held his peace at her in the day that he heard them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/30/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2ac554c-9c40-4a97-a777-86da17fdfecb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: NUM 30:15
Text: But if he shall any ways make them void after that he hath heard them; then he shall bear her iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/30/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:287d9d45-0fff-4954-96f2-5939be5b312b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: NUM 30:16
Text: These are the statutes, which the LORD commanded Moses, between a man and his wife, between the father and his daughter, being yet in her youth in her father’s house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:736bf6b4-b521-4829-bb5d-9fa11544375c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 65

Reference: NUM 31:1
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:296d5f63-0d20-4c80-9d5e-149cff823617>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: NUM 31:2
Text: Avenge the children of Israel of the Midianites: afterward shalt thou be gathered unto thy people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0f72274-aeb3-4693-8051-4965a0508e48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: NUM 31:3
Text: And Moses spake unto the people, saying, Arm some of yourselves unto the war, and let them go against the Midianites, and avenge the LORD of Midian.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:100f962e-2fe5-4f18-b938-f0119ccef372>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: NUM 31:4
Text: Of every tribe a thousand, throughout all the tribes of Israel, shall ye send to the war.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37740b27-103a-4d11-b7b6-271cd7f21423>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: NUM 31:5
Text: So there were delivered out of the thousands of Israel, a thousand of every tribe, twelve thousand armed for war.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43f4c636-a914-444b-b804-8c025cb651ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: NUM 31:6
Text: And Moses sent them to the war, a thousand of every tribe, them and Phinehas the son of Eleazar the priest, to the war, with the holy instruments, and the trumpets to blow in his hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15855312-5601-4e64-9000-c5433dc9ec28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: NUM 31:7
Text: And they warred against the Midianites, as the LORD commanded Moses; and they slew all the males.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:891f287f-fab0-4862-82e1-9dd374f718c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: NUM 31:8
Text: And they slew the kings of Midian, beside the rest of them that were slain; namely, Evi, and Rekem, and Zur, and Hur, and Reba, five kings of Midian: Balaam also the son of Beor they slew with the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:730857f3-5479-4d21-a6d9-d3c642918af3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: NUM 31:9
Text: And the children of Israel took all the women of Midian captives, and their little ones, and took the spoil of all their cattle, and all their flocks, and all their goods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74a8adff-3ecb-4070-9fe7-388bf7c217f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: NUM 31:10
Text: And they burnt all their cities wherein they dwelt, and all their goodly castles, with fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1473804-99c3-41aa-a150-35d3beaa16c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: NUM 31:11
Text: And they took all the spoil, and all the prey, both of men and of beasts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:037b1e7d-6be5-45ee-987e-2354dcf45a8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: NUM 31:12
Text: And they brought the captives, and the prey, and the spoil, unto Moses, and Eleazar the priest, and unto the congregation of the children of Israel, unto the camp at the plains of Moab, which are by Jordan near Jericho.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b154167-c11f-4a50-aafb-b606cc186c1e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: NUM 31:13
Text: And Moses, and Eleazar the priest, and all the princes of the congregation, went forth to meet them without the camp.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfea15a9-7f74-4b57-947d-0bb3729b034f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: NUM 31:14
Text: And Moses was wroth with the officers of the host, with the captains over thousands, and captains over hundreds, which came from the battle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7260fd5-5262-4675-917f-acd7726a466e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: NUM 31:15
Text: And Moses said unto them, Have ye saved all the women alive?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94f6c227-3e3c-4d80-af7b-161b9b434b88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: NUM 31:16
Text: Behold, these caused the children of Israel, through the counsel of Balaam, to commit trespass against the LORD in the matter of Peor, and there was a plague among the congregation of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64ec12f5-0028-4f35-8154-bc9742129b70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: NUM 31:17
Text: Now therefore kill every male among the little ones, and kill every woman that hath known man by lying with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f09c2b01-919f-4f68-8e30-7f773be6fe8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: NUM 31:18
Text: But all the women children, that have not known a man by lying with him, keep alive for yourselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07e0d3db-a8bb-4302-a0f3-0119d7a829b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: NUM 31:19
Text: And do ye abide without the camp seven days: whosoever hath killed any person, and whosoever hath touched any slain, purify both yourselves and your captives on the third day, and on the seventh day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd34146f-2f87-4708-8b3f-9f0d8de80e8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: NUM 31:20
Text: And purify all your raiment, and all that is made of skins, and all work of goats’ hair, and all things made of wood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9d61382-d456-4c32-9c06-4ecb80824467>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: NUM 31:21
Text: And Eleazar the priest said unto the men of war which went to the battle, This is the ordinance of the law which the LORD commanded Moses;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79570267-19ae-43c1-b4fb-481d3566bd51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: NUM 31:22
Text: Only the gold, and the silver, the brass, the iron, the tin, and the lead,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:145e3924-af72-411e-8b54-82c8327112cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: NUM 31:23
Text: Every thing that may abide the fire, ye shall make it go through the fire, and it shall be clean: nevertheless it shall be purified with the water of separation: and all that abideth not the fire ye shall make go through the water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bfe968d5-de7f-4dbd-b79d-abadfc332cea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: NUM 31:24
Text: And ye shall wash your clothes on the seventh day, and ye shall be clean, and afterward ye shall come into the camp.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67b94df4-360c-4ffc-a5ff-7604d6a63dc2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 66

Reference: NUM 31:25
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2763cd5-a7b5-46c0-bed4-1924d32fe79d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: NUM 31:26
Text: Take the sum of the prey that was taken, both of man and of beast, thou, and Eleazar the priest, and the chief fathers of the congregation:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13c9378f-1c77-40ac-94df-dc56a235e06d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: NUM 31:27
Text: And divide the prey into two parts; between them that took the war upon them, who went out to battle, and between all the congregation:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e49d9095-e5cd-478c-a14b-2d4f436f6d4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: NUM 31:28
Text: And levy a tribute unto the Lord of the men of war which went out to battle: one soul of five hundred, both of the persons, and of the beeves, and of the asses, and of the sheep:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c315648-e30b-4081-9b98-c95e8199a18f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: NUM 31:29
Text: Take it of their half, and give it unto Eleazar the priest, for an heave offering of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66cdaff4-6575-4567-95a2-e4b25b0a108b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 279

Reference: NUM 31:30
Text: And of the children of Israel’s half, thou shalt take one portion of fifty, of the persons, of the beeves, of the asses, and of the flocks, of all manner of beasts, and give them unto the Levites, which keep the charge of the tabernacle of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c51d7b77-cabb-43f0-9026-34fa85c82d8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: NUM 31:31
Text: And Moses and Eleazar the priest did as the LORD commanded Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a14ab68-2f1a-405f-bc04-08102e607b9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: NUM 31:32
Text: And the booty, being the rest of the prey which the men of war had caught, was six hundred thousand and seventy thousand and five thousand sheep,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b85cb518-6c21-4533-ab9d-b5f742c29a05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 70

Reference: NUM 31:33
Text: And threescore and twelve thousand beeves,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24615cc5-1795-44bf-8ff4-3a6d8d34808e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 66

Reference: NUM 31:34
Text: And threescore and one thousand asses,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2b43c14-bbc3-4b7d-b628-4c50d93bd616>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: NUM 31:35
Text: And thirty and two thousand persons in all, of women that had not known man by lying with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d4db68b-43eb-479f-b071-704aca802cf3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: NUM 31:36
Text: And the half, which was the portion of them that went out to war, was in number three hundred thousand and seven and thirty thousand and five hundred sheep:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0404683-7e3f-4a5e-a44d-973e421d0ecf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: NUM 31:37
Text: And the LORD’s tribute of the sheep was six hundred and threescore and fifteen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1ba7c31-a21e-434c-876d-b768f2116a68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: NUM 31:38
Text: And the beeves were thirty and six thousand; of which the LORD’s tribute was threescore and twelve.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94880032-5c0c-46b0-9c7d-8b22aa9a32c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: NUM 31:39
Text: And the asses were thirty thousand and five hundred; of which the LORD’s tribute was threescore and one.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0026f2b-65f9-4109-b3d5-f3995f6e47da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: NUM 31:40
Text: And the persons were sixteen thousand; of which the LORD’s tribute was thirty and two persons.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cadc764-d9e7-44fd-9935-d43df74d4d72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: NUM 31:41
Text: And Moses gave the tribute, which was the LORD’s heave offering, unto Eleazar the priest, as the LORD commanded Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95611c34-5fe5-4b45-b7d4-2ed743b9872d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: NUM 31:42
Text: And of the children of Israel’s half, which Moses divided from the men that warred,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ade50917-def5-4ddf-9eb6-589b68ad7197>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: NUM 31:43
Text: (Now the half that pertained unto the congregation was three hundred thousand and thirty thousand and seven thousand and five hundred sheep,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72e7dd7e-56fd-4244-bf87-ffd0b07f34d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 63

Reference: NUM 31:44
Text: And thirty and six thousand beeves,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89366221-38d0-4edb-ad6b-290dad1d0d6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 71

Reference: NUM 31:45
Text: And thirty thousand asses and five hundred,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54448b72-34e2-47ed-aa4e-b75616bba2bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 58

Reference: NUM 31:46
Text: And sixteen thousand persons;)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa3cc7c6-c89d-43aa-bed8-e0f0614d1780>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: NUM 31:47
Text: Even of the children of Israel’s half, Moses took one portion of fifty, both of man and of beast, and gave them unto the Levites, which kept the charge of the tabernacle of the LORD; as the LORD commanded Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87705fd8-9f62-4da8-9eb7-d1e38d65ac79>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: NUM 31:48
Text: And the officers which were over thousands of the host, the captains of thousands, and captains of hundreds, came near unto Moses:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa952bd4-510e-4779-b0a9-c717cc86bc85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: NUM 31:49
Text: And they said unto Moses, Thy servants have taken the sum of the men of war which are under our charge, and there lacketh not one man of us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:629853de-8a96-46c7-9735-1e96a20cd375>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: NUM 31:50
Text: We have therefore brought an oblation for the LORD, what every man hath gotten, of jewels of gold, chains, and bracelets, rings, earrings, and tablets, to make an atonement for our souls before the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1766911f-d947-4ac9-933e-c5412455c781>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: NUM 31:51
Text: And Moses and Eleazar the priest took the gold of them, even all wrought jewels.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab673ac7-d2a5-4a16-96ba-bf4f83a59dc0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: NUM 31:52
Text: And all the gold of the offering that they offered up to the LORD, of the captains of thousands, and of the captains of hundreds, was sixteen thousand seven hundred and fifty shekels.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ed3e5f2-8166-4bc9-a65d-b04e56acc555>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: NUM 31:53
Text: (For the men of war had taken spoil, every man for himself.)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/31/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ed9f59c-7f49-40e7-b7b9-c1863159f082>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: NUM 31:54
Text: And Moses and Eleazar the priest took the gold of the captains of thousands and of hundreds, and brought it into the tabernacle of the congregation, for a memorial for the children of Israel before the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99c16733-155d-4b00-88e6-5d68632ba721>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: NUM 32:1
Text: Now the children of Reuben and the children of Gad had a very great multitude of cattle: and when they saw the land of Jazer, and the land of Gilead, that, behold, the place was a place for cattle;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8330676c-ebff-4e86-acda-2c0c2d692237>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: NUM 32:2
Text: The children of Gad and the children of Reuben came and spake unto Moses, and to Eleazar the priest, and unto the princes of the congregation, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d15a5cf3-eb66-4eb0-9fb6-af7b121a513b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: NUM 32:3
Text: Ataroth, and Dibon, and Jazer, and Nimrah, and Heshbon, and Elealeh, and Shebam, and Nebo, and Beon,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d25ec320-5944-4047-a727-9a15b0871aea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: NUM 32:4
Text: Even the country which the LORD smote before the congregation of Israel, is a land for cattle, and thy servants have cattle:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99d3c5b5-4a6e-40e4-9fa8-683fee3d6ef2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: NUM 32:5
Text: Wherefore, said they, if we have found grace in thy sight, let this land be given unto thy servants for a possession, and bring us not over Jordan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c589c0d-5b0a-4d5a-8307-31683f7770bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: NUM 32:6
Text: And Moses said unto the children of Gad and to the children of Reuben, Shall your brethren go to war, and shall ye sit here?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0907996-29ca-4be5-9607-7b2de384ccf1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: NUM 32:7
Text: And wherefore discourage ye the heart of the children of Israel from going over into the land which the LORD hath given them?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90684cd0-ab53-44bd-a053-7ba1705da4e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: NUM 32:8
Text: Thus did your fathers, when I sent them from Kadeshbarnea to see the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5aed60a-520f-48c7-ad5d-1515f78ba5bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: NUM 32:9
Text: For when they went up unto the valley of Eshcol, and saw the land, they discouraged the heart of the children of Israel, that they should not go into the land which the LORD had given them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb7f28d1-51af-4306-8fef-026620792802>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: NUM 32:10
Text: And the LORD’s anger was kindled the same time, and he sware, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:197da803-c42d-48ff-8bc9-2d5309df922d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: NUM 32:11
Text: Surely none of the men that came up out of Egypt, from twenty years old and upward, shall see the land which I sware unto Abraham, unto Isaac, and unto Jacob; because they have not wholly followed me:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16f2571f-4ddb-4500-9826-8ea058f2539f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: NUM 32:12
Text: Save Caleb the son of Jephunneh the Kenezite, and Joshua the son of Nun: for they have wholly followed the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d5a8532-569d-4d9c-9856-2585d785450d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: NUM 32:13
Text: And the LORD’s anger was kindled against Israel, and he made them wander in the wilderness forty years, until all the generation, that had done evil in the sight of the LORD, was consumed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab6acfaf-a3a1-4692-ba6c-f0ad027b185e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: NUM 32:14
Text: And, behold, ye are risen up in your fathers’ stead, an increase of sinful men, to augment yet the fierce anger of the LORD toward Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c188cfa7-73b7-4e4c-9fff-5a64890c68d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: NUM 32:15
Text: For if ye turn away from after him, he will yet again leave them in the wilderness; and ye shall destroy all this people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5d3669a-bfbb-4dee-80b1-9e2b446aa26a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: NUM 32:16
Text: And they came near unto him, and said, We will build sheepfolds here for our cattle, and cities for our little ones:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce244add-db8d-4197-9b51-833f4b7c6fb2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: NUM 32:17
Text: But we ourselves will go ready armed before the children of Israel, until we have brought them unto their place: and our little ones shall dwell in the fenced cities because of the inhabitants of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd75e648-390a-41f5-b5e8-52ea6fc499f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: NUM 32:18
Text: We will not return unto our houses, until the children of Israel have inherited every man his inheritance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0a64383-0255-47ae-80a3-05ef8409cc2b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: NUM 32:19
Text: For we will not inherit with them on yonder side Jordan, or forward; because our inheritance is fallen to us on this side Jordan eastward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:753c5862-8152-4624-88dc-78ee671f3cef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: NUM 32:20
Text: And Moses said unto them, If ye will do this thing, if ye will go armed before the LORD to war,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ff41a6d-b201-4cd5-9a6f-ceb9e3713d52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: NUM 32:21
Text: And will go all of you armed over Jordan before the LORD, until he hath driven out his enemies from before him,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5fc4738-f846-452e-945b-463bd909347d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: NUM 32:22
Text: And the land be subdued before the LORD: then afterward ye shall return, and be guiltless before the LORD, and before Israel; and this land shall be your possession before the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af8a0a5f-a379-451a-9e09-86bbe3e6e89b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: NUM 32:23
Text: But if ye will not do so, behold, ye have sinned against the LORD: and be sure your sin will find you out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe52e652-9f77-4cf9-8c66-9fd870c29b5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: NUM 32:24
Text: Build you cities for your little ones, and folds for your sheep; and do that which hath proceeded out of your mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6de8b93a-d55c-4f04-910f-c40db51766ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: NUM 32:25
Text: And the children of Gad and the children of Reuben spake unto Moses, saying, Thy servants will do as my lord commandeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d3be7ab-7d3e-4182-bf1d-ab07bce5f21a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: NUM 32:26
Text: Our little ones, our wives, our flocks, and all our cattle, shall be there in the cities of Gilead:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:284757a6-e8d9-4b76-ae1c-d3b9cb678c24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: NUM 32:27
Text: But thy servants will pass over, every man armed for war, before the LORD to battle, as my lord saith.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6c12944-62ee-4e01-9371-1453f332047d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: NUM 32:28
Text: So concerning them Moses commanded Eleazar the priest, and Joshua the son of Nun, and the chief fathers of the tribes of the children of Israel:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0e76fe1-7b20-4023-80aa-602a99c91a0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 282

Reference: NUM 32:29
Text: And Moses said unto them, If the children of Gad and the children of Reuben will pass with you over Jordan, every man armed to battle, before the LORD, and the land shall be subdued before you; then ye shall give them the land of Gilead for a possession:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12178cdd-6108-4958-a9af-0a374936bb46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: NUM 32:30
Text: But if they will not pass over with you armed, they shall have possessions among you in the land of Canaan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb23404d-68d3-4e37-be05-11566bb9c667>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: NUM 32:31
Text: And the children of Gad and the children of Reuben answered, saying, As the LORD hath said unto thy servants, so will we do.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c3f2181-210b-454e-a4e7-30fe62d7979b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: NUM 32:32
Text: We will pass over armed before the LORD into the land of Canaan, that the possession of our inheritance on this side Jordan may be ours.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e75319cc-3eaa-45fc-8269-3cc2bf7c8408>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 342

Reference: NUM 32:33
Text: And Moses gave unto them, even to the children of Gad, and to the children of Reuben, and unto half the tribe of Manasseh the son of Joseph, the kingdom of Sihon king of the Amorites, and the kingdom of Og king of Bashan, the land, with the cities thereof in the coasts, even the cities of the country round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d45fa0d3-e528-4e17-ac9b-c67e20b44ce7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: NUM 32:34
Text: And the children of Gad built Dibon, and Ataroth, and Aroer,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97552af4-6860-4b54-8d87-5cf87072ba9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: NUM 32:35
Text: And Atroth, Shophan, and Jaazer, and Jogbehah,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9548548-f5c6-4850-b9b5-8f6ad24207e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: NUM 32:36
Text: And Bethnimrah, and Bethharan, fenced cities: and folds for sheep.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97ac4754-dfd3-4a3a-b626-2b76dae6fa82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: NUM 32:37
Text: And the children of Reuben built Heshbon, and Elealeh, and Kirjathaim,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a7f4f39-53cc-4ca2-86f0-61d8f75b6d81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: NUM 32:38
Text: And Nebo, and Baalmeon, (their names being changed,) and Shibmah: and gave other names unto the cities which they builded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0dbf2a7-a815-435b-a100-e8a78cf79ab8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: NUM 32:39
Text: And the children of Machir the son of Manasseh went to Gilead, and took it, and dispossessed the Amorite which was in it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6f8eff3-4d7a-4dad-b6d1-f573b92f100e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: NUM 32:40
Text: And Moses gave Gilead unto Machir the son of Manasseh; and he dwelt therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6943586e-1633-4693-9508-fdb9b84d8c82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: NUM 32:41
Text: And Jair the son of Manasseh went and took the small towns thereof, and called them Havothjair.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/32/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6cd1e5c5-75b5-47b6-a193-07d1551264b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: NUM 32:42
Text: And Nobah went and took Kenath, and the villages thereof, and called it Nobah, after his own name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:980ae891-5dd4-4613-b916-b48ec08ca7ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: NUM 33:1
Text: These are the journeys of the children of Israel, which went forth out of the land of Egypt with their armies under the hand of Moses and Aaron.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e70e7d6e-b639-4271-90e9-3496894051ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: NUM 33:2
Text: And Moses wrote their goings out according to their journeys by the commandment of the LORD: and these are their journeys according to their goings out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6eddc1b7-f1e8-4d57-bc93-d5cafcb14d11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: NUM 33:3
Text: And they departed from Rameses in the first month, on the fifteenth day of the first month; on the morrow after the passover the children of Israel went out with an high hand in the sight of all the Egyptians.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:468b4224-3048-4888-94f6-4a49067b9990>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: NUM 33:4
Text: For the Egyptians buried all their firstborn, which the LORD had smitten among them: upon their gods also the LORD executed judgments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41baf725-a7aa-403b-a694-51372a819fed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: NUM 33:5
Text: And the children of Israel removed from Rameses, and pitched in Succoth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f0911ca-9c5f-41f6-8125-bdc97f44af3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: NUM 33:6
Text: And they departed from Succoth, and pitched in Etham, which is in the edge of the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c9efdff-c522-4b70-ad01-f8f6d8d2bbd9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: NUM 33:7
Text: And they removed from Etham, and turned again unto Pihahiroth, which is before Baalzephon: and they pitched before Migdol.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d67edc0-a356-4e4c-8342-55ff9697ef19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: NUM 33:8
Text: And they departed from before Pihahiroth, and passed through the midst of the sea into the wilderness, and went three days’ journey in the wilderness of Etham, and pitched in Marah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f53c68d-1a44-4f9a-b804-730a3f870ec8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: NUM 33:9
Text: And they removed from Marah, and came unto Elim: and in Elim were twelve fountains of water, and threescore and ten palm trees; and they pitched there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db38077e-a791-4d1f-b926-e0a834d5062e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: NUM 33:10
Text: And they removed from Elim, and encamped by the Red sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a1c4a00-6751-4167-b944-5eefe8b4f7cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: NUM 33:11
Text: And they removed from the Red sea, and encamped in the wilderness of Sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54ff16c6-f868-41af-a52d-92b80ee623be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: NUM 33:12
Text: And they took their journey out of the wilderness of Sin, and encamped in Dophkah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5324451-0417-404e-81c4-963c80983b5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: NUM 33:13
Text: And they departed from Dophkah, and encamped in Alush.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b292c462-64df-4953-8d0a-da38ee6ce741>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: NUM 33:14
Text: And they removed from Alush, and encamped at Rephidim, where was no water for the people to drink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:267680f8-c2a2-4bad-8562-f47b4ef417e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: NUM 33:15
Text: And they departed from Rephidim, and pitched in the wilderness of Sinai.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13e08c24-91f2-47fc-9bd6-25856751d713>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: NUM 33:16
Text: And they removed from the desert of Sinai, and pitched at Kibrothhattaavah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06290378-7607-4a78-a6f3-8658acfdc5a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: NUM 33:17
Text: And they departed from Kibrothhattaavah, and encamped at Hazeroth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bae91197-7576-4307-b2dc-3e38e207a772>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: NUM 33:18
Text: And they departed from Hazeroth, and pitched in Rithmah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:542e3fac-2293-441a-b3b3-080279566d3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: NUM 33:19
Text: And they departed from Rithmah, and pitched at Rimmonparez.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae195bd5-3a6c-4c3a-ba7a-3e2feb18f2fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: NUM 33:20
Text: And they departed from Rimmonparez, and pitched in Libnah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2fe619a-2b56-44fc-9fe1-dd76d7909f36>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: NUM 33:21
Text: And they removed from Libnah, and pitched at Rissah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16aeb893-72b1-4cae-b85d-8ddd82107aa0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: NUM 33:22
Text: And they journeyed from Rissah, and pitched in Kehelathah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98c5b1e0-e845-4dec-9da0-751c1b366f2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: NUM 33:23
Text: And they went from Kehelathah, and pitched in mount Shapher.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NUM/33/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
