Content-Length: 184

Reference: DEU 27:12
Text: These shall stand upon mount Gerizim to bless the people, when ye are come over Jordan; Simeon, and Levi, and Judah, and Issachar, and Joseph, and Benjamin:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/27/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3245074-2b44-4b91-8fb7-676119c4c9c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: DEU 27:13
Text: And these shall stand upon mount Ebal to curse; Reuben, Gad, and Asher, and Zebulun, Dan, and Naphtali.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/27/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe101a56-9808-416f-a6db-6386a0d60633>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: DEU 27:14
Text: And the Levites shall speak, and say unto all the men of Israel with a loud voice,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/27/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e1d3b2c-b418-4715-9f66-c3f2f9cfe8c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: DEU 27:15
Text: Cursed be the man that maketh any graven or molten image, an abomination unto the LORD, the work of the hands of the craftsman, and putteth it in a secret place. And all the people shall answer and say, Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/27/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:012a18b3-dadb-43b0-950a-38c19ff8bf6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: DEU 27:16
Text: Cursed be he that setteth light by his father or his mother. And all the people shall say, Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/27/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5988931-cad3-41e7-87fe-8dbc1b30bd89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: DEU 27:17
Text: Cursed be he that removeth his neighbour’s landmark. And all the people shall say, Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/27/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:762d6c9d-f10b-4c4e-b175-e87831bae6f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: DEU 27:18
Text: Cursed be he that maketh the blind to wander out of the way. And all the people shall say, Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/27/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b57df8a-727d-4393-9485-03c367caa20e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: DEU 27:19
Text: Cursed be he that perverteth the judgment of the stranger, fatherless, and widow. And all the people shall say, Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/27/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37c9a8d9-a5f5-4ce7-ac59-69247ad997d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: DEU 27:20
Text: Cursed be he that lieth with his father’s wife; because he uncovereth his father’s skirt. And all the people shall say, Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/27/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc503bb0-4a75-4fe0-95de-0a0d31f51280>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: DEU 27:21
Text: Cursed be he that lieth with any manner of beast. And all the people shall say, Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/27/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0b76a3f-bb28-461f-8d1b-32389d68dda0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: DEU 27:22
Text: Cursed be he that lieth with his sister, the daughter of his father, or the daughter of his mother. And all the people shall say, Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/27/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a0e37da-70f7-42b5-8196-bd1fbf3231c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: DEU 27:23
Text: Cursed be he that lieth with his mother in law. And all the people shall say, Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/27/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13d18a57-bda1-490d-a808-63de181f1201>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: DEU 27:24
Text: Cursed be he that smiteth his neighbour secretly. And all the people shall say, Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/27/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a826a005-eb68-4d1c-b478-606c963c0fc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: DEU 27:25
Text: Cursed be he that taketh reward to slay an innocent person. And all the people shall say, Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/27/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36ef76ab-1b10-4d85-98b3-1a683482bd87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: DEU 27:26
Text: Cursed be he that confirmeth not all the words of this law to do them. And all the people shall say, Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ec8358e-af23-4115-96b5-88463d056300>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: DEU 28:1
Text: And it shall come to pass, if thou shalt hearken diligently unto the voice of the LORD thy God, to observe and to do all his commandments which I command thee this day, that the LORD thy God will set thee on high above all nations of the earth:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa8fc6b3-125c-4e9c-b8a2-1bf9ac853d12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: DEU 28:2
Text: And all these blessings shall come on thee, and overtake thee, if thou shalt hearken unto the voice of the LORD thy God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dba503ba-c991-40f8-b7d0-ec838b39ead7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: DEU 28:3
Text: Blessed shalt thou be in the city, and blessed shalt thou be in the field.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df70606a-6920-4d17-a7a0-2b1fc934eba0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: DEU 28:4
Text: Blessed shall be the fruit of thy body, and the fruit of thy ground, and the fruit of thy cattle, the increase of thy kine, and the flocks of thy sheep.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee01d621-a736-457b-a149-fcfd2a382ca5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 69

Reference: DEU 28:5
Text: Blessed shall be thy basket and thy store.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d33458c-c811-44ab-8b22-3af9b5bc371f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: DEU 28:6
Text: Blessed shalt thou be when thou comest in, and blessed shalt thou be when thou goest out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:adff5013-8250-44f6-aab1-cc2837e5b010>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: DEU 28:7
Text: The LORD shall cause thine enemies that rise up against thee to be smitten before thy face: they shall come out against thee one way, and flee before thee seven ways.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6949b20f-485f-4adf-8ed9-b3c10285b179>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: DEU 28:8
Text: The LORD shall command the blessing upon thee in thy storehouses, and in all that thou settest thine hand unto; and he shall bless thee in the land which the LORD thy God giveth thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fca40b50-de43-418e-b3bc-799ce161a0ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: DEU 28:9
Text: The LORD shall establish thee an holy people unto himself, as he hath sworn unto thee, if thou shalt keep the commandments of the LORD thy God, and walk in his ways.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b4da4d3-f01e-4762-ab01-09edfc3a4b12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: DEU 28:10
Text: And all people of the earth shall see that thou art called by the name of the LORD; and they shall be afraid of thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef1e53f6-767e-4721-85e9-6b6c7456643d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: DEU 28:11
Text: And the LORD shall make thee plenteous in goods, in the fruit of thy body, and in the fruit of thy cattle, and in the fruit of thy ground, in the land which the LORD sware unto thy fathers to give thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3374681f-f060-4c8c-9f95-19f5223c5c4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: DEU 28:12
Text: The LORD shall open unto thee his good treasure, the heaven to give the rain unto thy land in his season, and to bless all the work of thine hand: and thou shalt lend unto many nations, and thou shalt not borrow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57d1cf1c-2044-4620-a127-d7ae65b74396>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: DEU 28:13
Text: And the LORD shall make thee the head, and not the tail; and thou shalt be above only, and thou shalt not be beneath; if that thou hearken unto the commandments of the LORD thy God, which I command thee this day, to observe and to do them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7a96e7e-25e0-491f-860f-db3a2b186463>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: DEU 28:14
Text: And thou shalt not go aside from any of the words which I command thee this day, to the right hand, or to the left, to go after other gods to serve them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac58be70-0c20-4886-afae-1d74f0ba91ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: DEU 28:15
Text: But it shall come to pass, if thou wilt not hearken unto the voice of the LORD thy God, to observe to do all his commandments and his statutes which I command thee this day; that all these curses shall come upon thee, and overtake thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:153c78e5-ec65-4d04-958d-8b8ad45266d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: DEU 28:16
Text: Cursed shalt thou be in the city, and cursed shalt thou be in the field.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4383006f-fee6-4d9f-9543-98258ee3c0b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 69

Reference: DEU 28:17
Text: Cursed shall be thy basket and thy store.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bfb44d99-f392-4c28-a7cb-e8dc13b1a288>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: DEU 28:18
Text: Cursed shall be the fruit of thy body, and the fruit of thy land, the increase of thy kine, and the flocks of thy sheep.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80abd5b9-d0af-4cf0-a198-cc71f8c40173>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: DEU 28:19
Text: Cursed shalt thou be when thou comest in, and cursed shalt thou be when thou goest out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a00430e5-4f0b-4928-a0ab-fd6c947db6c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: DEU 28:20
Text: The LORD shall send upon thee cursing, vexation, and rebuke, in all that thou settest thine hand unto for to do, until thou be destroyed, and until thou perish quickly; because of the wickedness of thy doings, whereby thou hast forsaken me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16629ead-8896-492c-bc20-94ffd9728ec0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: DEU 28:21
Text: The LORD shall make the pestilence cleave unto thee, until he have consumed thee from off the land, whither thou goest to possess it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fdc0e27a-68eb-4d1f-bda8-4057882d2fed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: DEU 28:22
Text: The LORD shall smite thee with a consumption, and with a fever, and with an inflammation, and with an extreme burning, and with the sword, and with blasting, and with mildew; and they shall pursue thee until thou perish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab2a7330-e357-498e-8426-555cf3b91f3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: DEU 28:23
Text: And thy heaven that is over thy head shall be brass, and the earth that is under thee shall be iron.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c76ba2b0-2cc0-4172-823d-2e033f6aac09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: DEU 28:24
Text: The LORD shall make the rain of thy land powder and dust: from heaven shall it come down upon thee, until thou be destroyed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:810cfe42-e32a-4e86-a4ad-65a1bbd48076>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: DEU 28:25
Text: The LORD shall cause thee to be smitten before thine enemies: thou shalt go out one way against them, and flee seven ways before them: and shalt be removed into all the kingdoms of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6cd12429-e1ca-4724-8997-6163fbdcb614>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: DEU 28:26
Text: And thy carcase shall be meat unto all fowls of the air, and unto the beasts of the earth, and no man shall fray them away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a32274ed-8266-4c81-a6a6-859ec0944a6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: DEU 28:27
Text: The LORD will smite thee with the botch of Egypt, and with the emerods, and with the scab, and with the itch, whereof thou canst not be healed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80502c47-8892-4e83-9869-7f5643ff9dc7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: DEU 28:28
Text: The LORD shall smite thee with madness, and blindness, and astonishment of heart:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d556e79-f63f-4caa-808a-29ae6e38ff09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: DEU 28:29
Text: And thou shalt grope at noonday, as the blind gropeth in darkness, and thou shalt not prosper in thy ways: and thou shalt be only oppressed and spoiled evermore, and no man shall save thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54044aef-4dcd-4681-9ba5-d0bde1e3e87c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: DEU 28:30
Text: Thou shalt betroth a wife, and another man shall lie with her: thou shalt build an house, and thou shalt not dwell therein: thou shalt plant a vineyard, and shalt not gather the grapes thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bf61b7d-ee5e-457d-85c7-fb21afd42e61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 285

Reference: DEU 28:31
Text: Thine ox shall be slain before thine eyes, and thou shalt not eat thereof: thine ass shall be violently taken away from before thy face, and shall not be restored to thee: thy sheep shall be given unto thine enemies, and thou shalt have none to rescue them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cdea0e85-c964-4783-a47f-672987ab98bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: DEU 28:32
Text: Thy sons and thy daughters shall be given unto another people, and thine eyes shall look, and fail with longing for them all the day long; and there shall be no might in thine hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44441886-d556-42fa-8336-9340abc2eddc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: DEU 28:33
Text: The fruit of thy land, and all thy labours, shall a nation which thou knowest not eat up; and thou shalt be only oppressed and crushed alway:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34eca308-4b8d-42ab-944e-fa2643452768>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: DEU 28:34
Text: So that thou shalt be mad for the sight of thine eyes which thou shalt see.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf3370b3-01e5-4ab7-8473-5b1a6c67093a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: DEU 28:35
Text: The LORD shall smite thee in the knees, and in the legs, with a sore botch that cannot be healed, from the sole of thy foot unto the top of thy head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3e26c76-2b80-4b1d-91c2-6543d29bcd88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: DEU 28:36
Text: The LORD shall bring thee, and thy king which thou shalt set over thee, unto a nation which neither thou nor thy fathers have known; and there shalt thou serve other gods, wood and stone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b23e727-a97e-48fe-aa16-b93c9b456d4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: DEU 28:37
Text: And thou shalt become an astonishment, a proverb, and a byword, among all nations whither the LORD shall lead thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3f29ff0-9d25-44ae-8ac6-db14d5b21eab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: DEU 28:38
Text: Thou shalt carry much seed out into the field, and shalt gather but little in; for the locust shall consume it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbb5bee3-ca67-4ab4-96c5-819c810abfcf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: DEU 28:39
Text: Thou shalt plant vineyards, and dress them, but shalt neither drink of the wine, nor gather the grapes; for the worms shall eat them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbe13860-cbf6-4150-99aa-5862963550fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: DEU 28:40
Text: Thou shalt have olive trees throughout all thy coasts, but thou shalt not anoint thyself with the oil; for thine olive shall cast his fruit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:815b035d-c273-4775-80bc-c7d64982cf07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: DEU 28:41
Text: Thou shalt beget sons and daughters, but thou shalt not enjoy them; for they shall go into captivity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8009f9d-82c6-4750-b6fa-bd69dad39a95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: DEU 28:42
Text: All thy trees and fruit of thy land shall the locust consume.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0956c8cb-5384-4a27-975c-3331b9c1abda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: DEU 28:43
Text: The stranger that is within thee shall get up above thee very high; and thou shalt come down very low.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3a9a1cc-fed5-46a6-afb1-4335812f95b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: DEU 28:44
Text: He shall lend to thee, and thou shalt not lend to him: he shall be the head, and thou shalt be the tail.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7802c2e-4d77-4457-912d-680070baf0f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 273

Reference: DEU 28:45
Text: Moreover all these curses shall come upon thee, and shall pursue thee, and overtake thee, till thou be destroyed; because thou hearkenedst not unto the voice of the LORD thy God, to keep his commandments and his statutes which he commanded thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0d92fe7-5340-4114-aac0-70e46c042a1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: DEU 28:46
Text: And they shall be upon thee for a sign and for a wonder, and upon thy seed for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:793c9753-3ca3-4a0c-b6ff-71e735ceaeae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: DEU 28:47
Text: Because thou servedst not the LORD thy God with joyfulness, and with gladness of heart, for the abundance of all things;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:798d92f8-c316-4d67-80a7-4f0d9a9b31a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: DEU 28:48
Text: Therefore shalt thou serve thine enemies which the LORD shall send against thee, in hunger, and in thirst, and in nakedness, and in want of all things: and he shall put a yoke of iron upon thy neck, until he have destroyed thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10ca8414-931a-474d-8370-2a8740429e34>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: DEU 28:49
Text: The LORD shall bring a nation against thee from far, from the end of the earth, as swift as the eagle flieth; a nation whose tongue thou shalt not understand;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b57a635-3847-452a-80b7-a7098b43dd49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: DEU 28:50
Text: A nation of fierce countenance, which shall not regard the person of the old, nor shew favour to the young:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a8f3924-bcd9-4a65-8b0a-e2bda25dd4db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: DEU 28:51
Text: And he shall eat the fruit of thy cattle, and the fruit of thy land, until thou be destroyed: which also shall not leave thee either corn, wine, or oil, or the increase of thy kine, or flocks of thy sheep, until he have destroyed thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ae9d867-ea2d-4488-a859-97bae11cdd7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: DEU 28:52
Text: And he shall besiege thee in all thy gates, until thy high and fenced walls come down, wherein thou trustedst, throughout all thy land: and he shall besiege thee in all thy gates throughout all thy land, which the LORD thy God hath given thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:773d6595-f44c-48ec-8338-4575662e6d37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: DEU 28:53
Text: And thou shalt eat the fruit of thine own body, the flesh of thy sons and of thy daughters, which the LORD thy God hath given thee, in the siege, and in the straitness, wherewith thine enemies shall distress thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d028ec27-8afa-47b6-84a4-5dc57d32ba15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: DEU 28:54
Text: So that the man that is tender among you, and very delicate, his eye shall be evil toward his brother, and toward the wife of his bosom, and toward the remnant of his children which he shall leave:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/55
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c217ab3d-d878-4cfb-9413-e8ef074547dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: DEU 28:55
Text: So that he will not give to any of them of the flesh of his children whom he shall eat: because he hath nothing left him in the siege, and in the straitness, wherewith thine enemies shall distress thee in all thy gates.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/56
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08fe06d6-69b5-4d67-8caa-0edfd92f0d6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: DEU 28:56
Text: The tender and delicate woman among you, which would not adventure to set the sole of her foot upon the ground for delicateness and tenderness, her eye shall be evil toward the husband of her bosom, and toward her son, and toward her daughter,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/57
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:758a8626-d71e-4dce-abcf-93b37eb17b04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 277

Reference: DEU 28:57
Text: And toward her young one that cometh out from between her feet, and toward her children which she shall bear: for she shall eat them for want of all things secretly in the siege and straitness, wherewith thine enemy shall distress thee in thy gates.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/58
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e50b452a-c9bd-4317-81b5-9e10cc99976a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: DEU 28:58
Text: If thou wilt not observe to do all the words of this law that are written in this book, that thou mayest fear this glorious and fearful name, THE LORD THY GOD;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/59
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0109c9aa-5b53-4a0b-aaf7-bfad97e8b92f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: DEU 28:59
Text: Then the LORD will make thy plagues wonderful, and the plagues of thy seed, even great plagues, and of long continuance, and sore sicknesses, and of long continuance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/60
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29db6f91-a9e5-4c65-a01f-f802f386266d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: DEU 28:60
Text: Moreover he will bring upon thee all the diseases of Egypt, which thou wast afraid of; and they shall cleave unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/61
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78e5d413-f464-4d6e-ba27-8d4752d0b6f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: DEU 28:61
Text: Also every sickness, and every plague, which is not written in the book of this law, them will the LORD bring upon thee, until thou be destroyed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/62
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5663f7b3-c7da-4347-a857-e1d1d907ed96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: DEU 28:62
Text: And ye shall be left few in number, whereas ye were as the stars of heaven for multitude; because thou wouldest not obey the voice of the LORD thy God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/63
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f54895fc-2d3a-4e50-a41b-b966c8c9d9f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 280

Reference: DEU 28:63
Text: And it shall come to pass, that as the LORD rejoiced over you to do you good, and to multiply you; so the LORD will rejoice over you to destroy you, and to bring you to nought; and ye shall be plucked from off the land whither thou goest to possess it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/64
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:492b3d04-5fdc-4f9b-ad44-92a54b0641f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: DEU 28:64
Text: And the LORD shall scatter thee among all people, from the one end of the earth even unto the other; and there thou shalt serve other gods, which neither thou nor thy fathers have known, even wood and stone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/65
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:460bef7b-cd6f-40de-bf22-997d71378bff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: DEU 28:65
Text: And among these nations shalt thou find no ease, neither shall the sole of thy foot have rest: but the LORD shall give thee there a trembling heart, and failing of eyes, and sorrow of mind:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/66
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:425acbcf-3173-4dd6-b8ed-5fb21c5a533d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: DEU 28:66
Text: And thy life shall hang in doubt before thee; and thou shalt fear day and night, and shalt have none assurance of thy life:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/67
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac037cf4-a757-4186-9518-7952d9441b0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: DEU 28:67
Text: In the morning thou shalt say, Would God it were even! and at even thou shalt say, Would God it were morning! for the fear of thine heart wherewith thou shalt fear, and for the sight of thine eyes which thou shalt see.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/28/68
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae972d85-398b-4ae1-beb6-37a1a7861e6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: DEU 28:68
Text: And the LORD shall bring thee into Egypt again with ships, by the way whereof I spake unto thee, Thou shalt see it no more again: and there ye shall be sold unto your enemies for bondmen and bondwomen, and no man shall buy you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7ea8882-9ff6-49c2-b336-bccb95cd6c3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: DEU 29:1
Text: These are the words of the covenant, which the LORD commanded Moses to make with the children of Israel in the land of Moab, beside the covenant which he made with them in Horeb.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f9a9fbe-2ff3-41c3-a077-b11bfb776454>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: DEU 29:2
Text: And Moses called unto all Israel, and said unto them, Ye have seen all that the LORD did before your eyes in the land of Egypt unto Pharaoh, and unto all his servants, and unto all his land;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e7389a0-bba8-4154-a381-4c4950b2a70f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: DEU 29:3
Text: The great temptations which thine eyes have seen, the signs, and those great miracles:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f08a44a2-d3b2-4f63-82a9-6bc5920f40a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: DEU 29:4
Text: Yet the LORD hath not given you an heart to perceive, and eyes to see, and ears to hear, unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c53afb3-a090-4983-853e-131dcbbc4644>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: DEU 29:5
Text: And I have led you forty years in the wilderness: your clothes are not waxen old upon you, and thy shoe is not waxen old upon thy foot.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:104dc443-8872-46ca-b610-2466a5c54752>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: DEU 29:6
Text: Ye have not eaten bread, neither have ye drunk wine or strong drink: that ye might know that I am the LORD your God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f18bd5e1-2959-4a97-bc7c-9cc1beafea52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: DEU 29:7
Text: And when ye came unto this place, Sihon the king of Heshbon, and Og the king of Bashan, came out against us unto battle, and we smote them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:787ee7a2-dcae-46eb-aa89-b82fb96e953b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: DEU 29:8
Text: And we took their land, and gave it for an inheritance unto the Reubenites, and to the Gadites, and to the half tribe of Manasseh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f03eb5e4-7a1c-4545-90a7-5a90a3da8356>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: DEU 29:9
Text: Keep therefore the words of this covenant, and do them, that ye may prosper in all that ye do.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c441f51-1c97-4da0-818e-ee9b60021461>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: DEU 29:10
Text: Ye stand this day all of you before the LORD your God; your captains of your tribes, your elders, and your officers, with all the men of Israel,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05d5f8f0-ce3a-4d6d-9594-ef157d171379>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: DEU 29:11
Text: Your little ones, your wives, and thy stranger that is in thy camp, from the hewer of thy wood unto the drawer of thy water:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3fbcd5e-4d6e-4a67-a319-f229230a27fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: DEU 29:12
Text: That thou shouldest enter into covenant with the LORD thy God, and into his oath, which the LORD thy God maketh with thee this day:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:724b528e-7f39-484e-96e9-79372ee63bbf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: DEU 29:13
Text: That he may establish thee to day for a people unto himself, and that he may be unto thee a God, as he hath said unto thee, and as he hath sworn unto thy fathers, to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f52fafc-e780-47d1-b652-46fb43a80443>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: DEU 29:14
Text: Neither with you only do I make this covenant and this oath;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e1768f8-4975-449f-9c2c-e4465e8aad32>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: DEU 29:15
Text: But with him that standeth here with us this day before the LORD our God, and also with him that is not here with us this day:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34bbedb2-2721-4788-be16-58fe88211e1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: DEU 29:16
Text: (For ye know how we have dwelt in the land of Egypt; and how we came through the nations which ye passed by;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:833241ba-1444-4e20-bb28-30c2c3d27c5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: DEU 29:17
Text: And ye have seen their abominations, and their idols, wood and stone, silver and gold, which were among them:)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:361a8de1-fcc9-4f9b-9053-a895309bcdd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: DEU 29:18
Text: Lest there should be among you man, or woman, or family, or tribe, whose heart turneth away this day from the LORD our God, to go and serve the gods of these nations; lest there should be among you a root that beareth gall and wormwood;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee2b103a-2da5-47c8-b83c-a4bc5cb9e300>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: DEU 29:19
Text: And it come to pass, when he heareth the words of this curse, that he bless himself in his heart, saying, I shall have peace, though I walk in the imagination of mine heart, to add drunkenness to thirst:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39e3f130-3e7a-44bd-86cb-fb4edc6fd335>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: DEU 29:20
Text: The LORD will not spare him, but then the anger of the LORD and his jealousy shall smoke against that man, and all the curses that are written in this book shall lie upon him, and the LORD shall blot out his name from under heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee232882-7c7b-4013-b866-4e78ad91f194>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: DEU 29:21
Text: And the LORD shall separate him unto evil out of all the tribes of Israel, according to all the curses of the covenant that are written in this book of the law:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc6c1464-5b69-4b51-91fe-35e2eee464be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: DEU 29:22
Text: So that the generation to come of your children that shall rise up after you, and the stranger that shall come from a far land, shall say, when they see the plagues of that land, and the sicknesses which the LORD hath laid upon it;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec96dae8-c32b-4dac-b718-15976b0e329d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 280

Reference: DEU 29:23
Text: And that the whole land thereof is brimstone, and salt, and burning, that it is not sown, nor beareth, nor any grass groweth therein, like the overthrow of Sodom, and Gomorrah, Admah, and Zeboim, which the LORD overthrew in his anger, and in his wrath:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dba214d7-ccc9-456c-be86-3c7159b3d2da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: DEU 29:24
Text: Even all nations shall say, Wherefore hath the LORD done thus unto this land? what meaneth the heat of this great anger?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:caac90d2-619e-417f-a1a5-f0347af8aee8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: DEU 29:25
Text: Then men shall say, Because they have forsaken the covenant of the LORD God of their fathers, which he made with them when he brought them forth out of the land of Egypt:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a879f708-e18b-4a25-9615-1d52f8f6c55a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: DEU 29:26
Text: For they went and served other gods, and worshipped them, gods whom they knew not, and whom he had not given unto them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e624e7a-acaf-4a31-8bc7-61fa4a884263>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: DEU 29:27
Text: And the anger of the LORD was kindled against this land, to bring upon it all the curses that are written in this book:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09681b6c-2468-4564-94d9-e5445144c946>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: DEU 29:28
Text: And the LORD rooted them out of their land in anger, and in wrath, and in great indignation, and cast them into another land, as it is this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/29/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ebc5885-df71-49e4-9881-77f3d1e204d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: DEU 29:29
Text: The secret things belong unto the LORD our God: but those things which are revealed belong unto us and to our children for ever, that we may do all the words of this law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/30/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9f944d1-0f88-43e5-bcbb-2201ec1dea61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: DEU 30:1
Text: And it shall come to pass, when all these things are come upon thee, the blessing and the curse, which I have set before thee, and thou shalt call them to mind among all the nations, whither the LORD thy God hath driven thee,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/30/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f3d28a5-a08c-40fe-aabd-a3eaf3ac4421>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: DEU 30:2
Text: And shalt return unto the LORD thy God, and shalt obey his voice according to all that I command thee this day, thou and thy children, with all thine heart, and with all thy soul;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/30/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b349cad7-2291-4c77-a81a-2f8a220bb013>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: DEU 30:3
Text: That then the LORD thy God will turn thy captivity, and have compassion upon thee, and will return and gather thee from all the nations, whither the LORD thy God hath scattered thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/30/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76ff9ade-7c4f-4f19-a384-eea4c7ada858>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: DEU 30:4
Text: If any of thine be driven out unto the outmost parts of heaven, from thence will the LORD thy God gather thee, and from thence will he fetch thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/30/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0dd09bcb-a261-426a-a45f-d9141183dc64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: DEU 30:5
Text: And the LORD thy God will bring thee into the land which thy fathers possessed, and thou shalt possess it; and he will do thee good, and multiply thee above thy fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/30/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b4269ac-9d5b-4088-b114-4837bde8ed18>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: DEU 30:6
Text: And the LORD thy God will circumcise thine heart, and the heart of thy seed, to love the LORD thy God with all thine heart, and with all thy soul, that thou mayest live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/30/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fda988fc-b481-4086-bb3a-98da300150ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: DEU 30:7
Text: And the LORD thy God will put all these curses upon thine enemies, and on them that hate thee, which persecuted thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/30/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8006f231-7e2a-4756-a9b8-9b3500ad5d89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: DEU 30:8
Text: And thou shalt return and obey the voice of the LORD, and do all his commandments which I command thee this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/30/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09c5f3d7-9b03-4a16-8cf0-cf930c1fb7ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: DEU 30:9
Text: And the LORD thy God will make thee plenteous in every work of thine hand, in the fruit of thy body, and in the fruit of thy cattle, and in the fruit of thy land, for good: for the LORD will again rejoice over thee for good, as he rejoiced over thy fathers:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/30/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b651a60-b21e-4b4b-b987-b3a07ee77074>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: DEU 30:10
Text: If thou shalt hearken unto the voice of the LORD thy God, to keep his commandments and his statutes which are written in this book of the law, and if thou turn unto the LORD thy God with all thine heart, and with all thy soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/30/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98618bd4-e2cc-4693-b4a9-495bceae39f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: DEU 30:11
Text: For this commandment which I command thee this day, it is not hidden from thee, neither is it far off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/30/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4486766-3fc6-456e-801c-e904b191fc8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: DEU 30:12
Text: It is not in heaven, that thou shouldest say, Who shall go up for us to heaven, and bring it unto us, that we may hear it, and do it?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/30/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18728712-b679-4e91-a7cc-efc7592e1f97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: DEU 30:13
Text: Neither is it beyond the sea, that thou shouldest say, Who shall go over the sea for us, and bring it unto us, that we may hear it, and do it?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/30/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40e18fda-e77a-4eb0-b153-1b172eb77384>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: DEU 30:14
Text: But the word is very nigh unto thee, in thy mouth, and in thy heart, that thou mayest do it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/30/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad84f962-12c8-4351-b4c6-60b4f45303f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: DEU 30:15
Text: See, I have set before thee this day life and good, and death and evil;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/30/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ea2f597-4247-4d7a-a738-840ec7415cfb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 291

Reference: DEU 30:16
Text: In that I command thee this day to love the LORD thy God, to walk in his ways, and to keep his commandments and his statutes and his judgments, that thou mayest live and multiply: and the LORD thy God shall bless thee in the land whither thou goest to possess it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/30/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:daafb13c-2fc2-4d01-8bbf-5e676da38895>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: DEU 30:17
Text: But if thine heart turn away, so that thou wilt not hear, but shalt be drawn away, and worship other gods, and serve them;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/30/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f407eb10-ceb5-4f4a-b75e-10dc4d8a004e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: DEU 30:18
Text: I denounce unto you this day, that ye shall surely perish, and that ye shall not prolong your days upon the land, whither thou passest over Jordan to go to possess it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/30/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bf038c7-5cc5-40a4-81bc-35380390165a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: DEU 30:19
Text: I call heaven and earth to record this day against you, that I have set before you life and death, blessing and cursing: therefore choose life, that both thou and thy seed may live:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/30/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51e5ed4d-e77d-4dfa-ac0d-419dbd9c8186>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 314

Reference: DEU 30:20
Text: That thou mayest love the LORD thy God, and that thou mayest obey his voice, and that thou mayest cleave unto him: for he is thy life, and the length of thy days: that thou mayest dwell in the land which the LORD sware unto thy fathers, to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob, to give them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71a5b78a-6136-46c5-8d2b-fab0806f16a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: DEU 31:1
Text: And Moses went and spake these words unto all Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d23d9534-1f43-4416-bff6-02076f21bbd4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: DEU 31:2
Text: And he said unto them, I am an hundred and twenty years old this day; I can no more go out and come in: also the LORD hath said unto me, Thou shalt not go over this Jordan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d9b4ea4-0a6a-4955-84d5-0585920bfa43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: DEU 31:3
Text: The LORD thy God, he will go over before thee, and he will destroy these nations from before thee, and thou shalt possess them: and Joshua, he shall go over before thee, as the LORD hath said.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99fba798-440e-4864-a170-9f4596c0b35c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: DEU 31:4
Text: And the LORD shall do unto them as he did to Sihon and to Og, kings of the Amorites, and unto the land of them, whom he destroyed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c63cae9d-6bab-41f7-9351-c387ec893cd1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: DEU 31:5
Text: And the LORD shall give them up before your face, that ye may do unto them according unto all the commandments which I have commanded you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4423f2f-781e-4a03-8db9-eb2e57b8c441>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: DEU 31:6
Text: Be strong and of a good courage, fear not, nor be afraid of them: for the LORD thy God, he it is that doth go with thee; he will not fail thee, nor forsake thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:219aca61-c81f-4481-be28-ee355ae9a9ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 283

Reference: DEU 31:7
Text: And Moses called unto Joshua, and said unto him in the sight of all Israel, Be strong and of a good courage: for thou must go with this people unto the land which the LORD hath sworn unto their fathers to give them; and thou shalt cause them to inherit it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6760ef81-3de4-4974-a747-fc5778346e97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: DEU 31:8
Text: And the LORD, he it is that doth go before thee; he will be with thee, he will not fail thee, neither forsake thee: fear not, neither be dismayed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53600d8f-4220-4ce7-a9c0-f2bc50746fcd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: DEU 31:9
Text: And Moses wrote this law, and delivered it unto the priests the sons of Levi, which bare the ark of the covenant of the LORD, and unto all the elders of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee3044fd-a014-4289-9d59-4e716d4248e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: DEU 31:10
Text: And Moses commanded them, saying, At the end of every seven years, in the solemnity of the year of release, in the feast of tabernacles,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6c8f949-589d-44cb-92c8-7e9a807fd7ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: DEU 31:11
Text: When all Israel is come to appear before the LORD thy God in the place which he shall choose, thou shalt read this law before all Israel in their hearing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1e07557-7a84-4a78-b81d-e68ff1fb5459>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: DEU 31:12
Text: Gather the people together, men and women, and children, and thy stranger that is within thy gates, that they may hear, and that they may learn, and fear the LORD your God, and observe to do all the words of this law:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:240d154f-f658-45fd-b4e0-4480e0bbc16c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: DEU 31:13
Text: And that their children, which have not known any thing, may hear, and learn to fear the LORD your God, as long as ye live in the land whither ye go over Jordan to possess it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bde9e14b-5d02-4d02-b7d1-a4acb242eec1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 299

Reference: DEU 31:14
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Behold, thy days approach that thou must die: call Joshua, and present yourselves in the tabernacle of the congregation, that I may give him a charge. And Moses and Joshua went, and presented themselves in the tabernacle of the congregation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f12ffbc9-1634-4159-9534-a576aa112691>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: DEU 31:15
Text: And the LORD appeared in the tabernacle in a pillar of a cloud: and the pillar of the cloud stood over the door of the tabernacle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9071e04e-0809-453b-8c26-a752f77d86a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 298

Reference: DEU 31:16
Text: And the LORD said unto Moses, Behold, thou shalt sleep with thy fathers; and this people will rise up, and go a whoring after the gods of the strangers of the land, whither they go to be among them, and will forsake me, and break my covenant which I have made with them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5544635-60ba-470a-9ea1-bb7a3b9d3989>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 321

Reference: DEU 31:17
Text: Then my anger shall be kindled against them in that day, and I will forsake them, and I will hide my face from them, and they shall be devoured, and many evils and troubles shall befall them; so that they will say in that day, Are not these evils come upon us, because our God is not among us?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad11da7c-afb4-468e-87c6-a2bc7cbcff50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: DEU 31:18
Text: And I will surely hide my face in that day for all the evils which they shall have wrought, in that they are turned unto other gods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35d1d3f5-e303-48c7-b608-1c11fc290e44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: DEU 31:19
Text: Now therefore write ye this song for you, and teach it the children of Israel: put it in their mouths, that this song may be a witness for me against the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb07c84c-82fc-4d78-9d21-1b99f50cda74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 300

Reference: DEU 31:20
Text: For when I shall have brought them into the land which I sware unto their fathers, that floweth with milk and honey; and they shall have eaten and filled themselves, and waxen fat; then will they turn unto other gods, and serve them, and provoke me, and break my covenant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89d0a7bd-bf94-485d-8025-d4679995a440>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 337

Reference: DEU 31:21
Text: And it shall come to pass, when many evils and troubles are befallen them, that this song shall testify against them as a witness; for it shall not be forgotten out of the mouths of their seed: for I know their imagination which they go about, even now, before I have brought them into the land which I sware.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b83f4531-92b1-4b74-b27f-c40e09719d8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: DEU 31:22
Text: Moses therefore wrote this song the same day, and taught it the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66b724f3-cd4b-4b55-aede-215d80b20721>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: DEU 31:23
Text: And he gave Joshua the son of Nun a charge, and said, Be strong and of a good courage: for thou shalt bring the children of Israel into the land which I sware unto them: and I will be with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9ad3094-2d8a-44f9-8df1-0381c24b1feb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: DEU 31:24
Text: And it came to pass, when Moses had made an end of writing the words of this law in a book, until they were finished,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2231b3e1-6584-4cdd-ba59-dd0fdcc6ed0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: DEU 31:25
Text: That Moses commanded the Levites, which bare the ark of the covenant of the LORD, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a177094-a0bd-41db-bd47-a68d0fead9df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: DEU 31:26
Text: Take this book of the law, and put it in the side of the ark of the covenant of the LORD your God, that it may be there for a witness against thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a506286-e34d-4c85-91f7-4cf4846ab4b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: DEU 31:27
Text: For I know thy rebellion, and thy stiff neck: behold, while I am yet alive with you this day, ye have been rebellious against the LORD; and how much more after my death?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc544d98-4ee1-49d9-8eb7-c1fbb7a58460>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: DEU 31:28
Text: Gather unto me all the elders of your tribes, and your officers, that I may speak these words in their ears, and call heaven and earth to record against them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:854df134-af8f-4d11-b46d-2e9992cb279b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 301

Reference: DEU 31:29
Text: For I know that after my death ye will utterly corrupt yourselves, and turn aside from the way which I have commanded you; and evil will befall you in the latter days; because ye will do evil in the sight of the LORD, to provoke him to anger through the work of your hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/31/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5157c4fc-f159-4c4a-9498-e76123f717dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: DEU 31:30
Text: And Moses spake in the ears of all the congregation of Israel the words of this song, until they were ended.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:408179c5-572e-4211-b796-22ea9fe6a202>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: DEU 32:1
Text: Give ear, O ye heavens, and I will speak; and hear, O earth, the words of my mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0140f96-0f99-4ce3-a46a-bf5ecde303c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: DEU 32:2
Text: My doctrine shall drop as the rain, my speech shall distil as the dew, as the small rain upon the tender herb, and as the showers upon the grass:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dee5d116-8abb-4b7a-805b-9abcd5976312>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: DEU 32:3
Text: Because I will publish the name of the LORD: ascribe ye greatness unto our God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb2deb4c-124e-42c3-b937-a60792c2ff54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: DEU 32:4
Text: He is the Rock, his work is perfect: for all his ways are judgment: a God of truth and without iniquity, just and right is he.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9e5f27b-cad6-4fa2-bda4-8ddfc6db020b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: DEU 32:5
Text: They have corrupted themselves, their spot is not the spot of his children: they are a perverse and crooked generation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81b61398-a6cd-45f9-bb2e-e64ce0511594>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: DEU 32:6
Text: Do ye thus requite the LORD, O foolish people and unwise? is not he thy father that hath bought thee? hath he not made thee, and established thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0251777b-7295-443f-ba7f-aa903bea8d52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: DEU 32:7
Text: Remember the days of old, consider the years of many generations: ask thy father, and he will shew thee; thy elders, and they will tell thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a08bf2be-eb35-4110-8d13-ef928bbc386d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: DEU 32:8
Text: When the Most High divided to the nations their inheritance, when he separated the sons of Adam, he set the bounds of the people according to the number of the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50d5af8e-bb9b-4231-bdf3-58b3a2ad0bbc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: DEU 32:9
Text: For the LORD’s portion is his people; Jacob is the lot of his inheritance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc17013e-3cb0-44dc-a6e8-b6bd6b79d0b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: DEU 32:10
Text: He found him in a desert land, and in the waste howling wilderness; he led him about, he instructed him, he kept him as the apple of his eye.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e53ebcd2-6222-470c-a4b0-cba7224a0137>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: DEU 32:11
Text: As an eagle stirreth up her nest, fluttereth over her young, spreadeth abroad her wings, taketh them, beareth them on her wings:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9750222-5cb0-4c8b-a55d-c3bdcd931908>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: DEU 32:12
Text: So the LORD alone did lead him, and there was no strange god with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d251ae8-270b-4dda-b67f-070109c781ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: DEU 32:13
Text: He made him ride on the high places of the earth, that he might eat the increase of the fields; and he made him to suck honey out of the rock, and oil out of the flinty rock;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a4cafa3-cb55-43b4-a75d-339f6c67bdb1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: DEU 32:14
Text: Butter of kine, and milk of sheep, with fat of lambs, and rams of the breed of Bashan, and goats, with the fat of kidneys of wheat; and thou didst drink the pure blood of the grape.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a21d32d1-2990-4c89-919b-53fe1f3be690>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: DEU 32:15
Text: But Jeshurun waxed fat, and kicked: thou art waxen fat, thou art grown thick, thou art covered with fatness; then he forsook God which made him, and lightly esteemed the Rock of his salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3049f302-d029-44bb-9b61-005643b62e7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: DEU 32:16
Text: They provoked him to jealousy with strange gods, with abominations provoked they him to anger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:148eae47-09f0-413f-ad9f-cd9ba21f2068>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: DEU 32:17
Text: They sacrificed unto devils, not to God; to gods whom they knew not, to new gods that came newly up, whom your fathers feared not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f22dcac7-6bf8-4174-89be-e54112c8526f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: DEU 32:18
Text: Of the Rock that begat thee thou art unmindful, and hast forgotten God that formed thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6093df24-bff5-4751-bf65-e4306b60245f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: DEU 32:19
Text: And when the LORD saw it, he abhorred them, because of the provoking of his sons, and of his daughters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17b4baee-22ea-45f3-b995-3d6636466477>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: DEU 32:20
Text: And he said, I will hide my face from them, I will see what their end shall be: for they are a very froward generation, children in whom is no faith.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63a0ea15-7674-4216-aa53-4b7711f84d5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: DEU 32:21
Text: They have moved me to jealousy with that which is not God; they have provoked me to anger with their vanities: and I will move them to jealousy with those which are not a people; I will provoke them to anger with a foolish nation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b470c57d-f3b9-4024-bb29-f63eb655544a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: DEU 32:22
Text: For a fire is kindled in mine anger, and shall burn unto the lowest hell, and shall consume the earth with her increase, and set on fire the foundations of the mountains.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85c34fe1-6c6d-42e4-bbf1-61efba5ba4a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: DEU 32:23
Text: I will heap mischiefs upon them; I will spend mine arrows upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eae052a0-ca2e-45f0-8a18-1e3fe6e5dd46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: DEU 32:24
Text: They shall be burnt with hunger, and devoured with burning heat, and with bitter destruction: I will also send the teeth of beasts upon them, with the poison of serpents of the dust.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e89816c8-80ab-41f5-8ca1-cfd8f673897b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: DEU 32:25
Text: The sword without, and terror within, shall destroy both the young man and the virgin, the suckling also with the man of gray hairs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e9cd3ce-144c-49a8-a669-95f13c736a30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: DEU 32:26
Text: I said, I would scatter them into corners, I would make the remembrance of them to cease from among men:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d06b1376-8ed6-44c3-9058-c91452b6193a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: DEU 32:27
Text: Were it not that I feared the wrath of the enemy, lest their adversaries should behave themselves strangely, and lest they should say, Our hand is high, and the LORD hath not done all this.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9f2511e-f9d3-423f-9544-2911f8ab8673>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: DEU 32:28
Text: For they are a nation void of counsel, neither is there any understanding in them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1c8558d-8ff6-44e5-9115-d85d86d16b95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: DEU 32:29
Text: O that they were wise, that they understood this, that they would consider their latter end!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8d51ed2-3fda-44e6-9078-4791533dc903>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: DEU 32:30
Text: How should one chase a thousand, and two put ten thousand to flight, except their Rock had sold them, and the LORD had shut them up?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:365c9ba5-9c1a-4bd6-97b1-d0bcf9687c67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: DEU 32:31
Text: For their rock is not as our Rock, even our enemies themselves being judges.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e445c78d-0125-485e-9d55-aac16c9ac4dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: DEU 32:32
Text: For their vine is of the vine of Sodom, and of the fields of Gomorrah: their grapes are grapes of gall, their clusters are bitter:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3af81e22-77b5-439a-bb39-815ac071ce69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: DEU 32:33
Text: Their wine is the poison of dragons, and the cruel venom of asps.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d5e3b7c-2a5a-4b4e-b78c-67a0108bab1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: DEU 32:34
Text: Is not this laid up in store with me, and sealed up among my treasures?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ead0f36-a651-4960-852e-7426b98da6b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: DEU 32:35
Text: To me belongeth vengeance and recompence; their foot shall slide in due time: for the day of their calamity is at hand, and the things that shall come upon them make haste.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22bbfe67-7f9b-400e-af75-f7626ff7a836>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: DEU 32:36
Text: For the LORD shall judge his people, and repent himself for his servants, when he seeth that their power is gone, and there is none shut up, or left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aefc385f-11de-4554-af02-4c043a195b0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: DEU 32:37
Text: And he shall say, Where are their gods, their rock in whom they trusted,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0cfd7910-17b6-4df3-a3a2-aff18181a42b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: DEU 32:38
Text: Which did eat the fat of their sacrifices, and drank the wine of their drink offerings? let them rise up and help you, and be your protection.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee8f78dc-5bf8-4338-89dc-75bbc0954eb2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: DEU 32:39
Text: See now that I, even I, am he, and there is no god with me: I kill, and I make alive; I wound, and I heal: neither is there any that can deliver out of my hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86c7fc3a-ca64-414c-951c-2b371e96b009>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: DEU 32:40
Text: For I lift up my hand to heaven, and say, I live for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c669178-f8eb-41c8-9a94-08e0a3fc6f32>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: DEU 32:41
Text: If I whet my glittering sword, and mine hand take hold on judgment; I will render vengeance to mine enemies, and will reward them that hate me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74ce1e2c-3a6d-4493-9a2d-f205ba539d15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: DEU 32:42
Text: I will make mine arrows drunk with blood, and my sword shall devour flesh; and that with the blood of the slain and of the captives, from the beginning of revenges upon the enemy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b7b0731-3e9b-4d89-8cf4-4fd032ec998f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: DEU 32:43
Text: Rejoice, O ye nations, with his people: for he will avenge the blood of his servants, and will render vengeance to his adversaries, and will be merciful unto his land, and to his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2ea7eaf-03ab-4a99-8119-d8430164cc45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: DEU 32:44
Text: And Moses came and spake all the words of this song in the ears of the people, he, and Hoshea the son of Nun.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2becf00-622e-446e-ae48-3fc71b598eee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: DEU 32:45
Text: And Moses made an end of speaking all these words to all Israel:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b25c083c-365f-41d3-809d-2d0c758e490d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: DEU 32:46
Text: And he said unto them, Set your hearts unto all the words which I testify among you this day, which ye shall command your children to observe to do, all the words of this law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f1d4ec3-a695-4df8-b146-9187b465f82a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: DEU 32:47
Text: For it is not a vain thing for you; because it is your life: and through this thing ye shall prolong your days in the land, whither ye go over Jordan to possess it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b26d3705-a4bf-4ae9-9b9e-0edf3baf93a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: DEU 32:48
Text: And the LORD spake unto Moses that selfsame day, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7229e32-b5ee-49cf-b175-b23ad5ab3d53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: DEU 32:49
Text: Get thee up into this mountain Abarim, unto mount Nebo, which is in the land of Moab, that is over against Jericho; and behold the land of Canaan, which I give unto the children of Israel for a possession:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6054be30-d32a-420e-9a9c-b0708dc53d4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: DEU 32:50
Text: And die in the mount whither thou goest up, and be gathered unto thy people; as Aaron thy brother died in mount Hor, and was gathered unto his people:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:764b873c-9745-496a-b637-6cf5b4fd81ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: DEU 32:51
Text: Because ye trespassed against me among the children of Israel at the waters of MeribahKadesh, in the wilderness of Zin; because ye sanctified me not in the midst of the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/32/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3517727b-5b1c-4653-bc8e-fa978ffcd994>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: DEU 32:52
Text: Yet thou shalt see the land before thee; but thou shalt not go thither unto the land which I give the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3bc6072-2516-4218-b5e2-e71d1f057e7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: DEU 33:1
Text: And this is the blessing, wherewith Moses the man of God blessed the children of Israel before his death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ff898e3-fa33-42d2-9963-e041bf94a743>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: DEU 33:2
Text: And he said, The LORD came from Sinai, and rose up from Seir unto them; he shined forth from mount Paran, and he came with ten thousands of saints: from his right hand went a fiery law for them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46a029e6-4932-4d29-b5c5-5ccbc65f3710>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: DEU 33:3
Text: Yea, he loved the people; all his saints are in thy hand: and they sat down at thy feet; every one shall receive of thy words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6249e2f9-4c4d-4da9-a955-ba86f89a0f84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: DEU 33:4
Text: Moses commanded us a law, even the inheritance of the congregation of Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1dc93897-341a-4be7-8699-ba178a6ee3df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: DEU 33:5
Text: And he was king in Jeshurun, when the heads of the people and the tribes of Israel were gathered together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29e0b89a-d3dd-40f0-9c08-846872cb5fc2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: DEU 33:6
Text: Let Reuben live, and not die; and let not his men be few.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85b5ae43-9bc1-4d82-9679-cd7880fcd51e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: DEU 33:7
Text: And this is the blessing of Judah: and he said, Hear, LORD, the voice of Judah, and bring him unto his people: let his hands be sufficient for him; and be thou an help to him from his enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76e757c4-eb55-4ba5-bbd5-8a6d6dba87ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: DEU 33:8
Text: And of Levi he said, Let thy Thummim and thy Urim be with thy holy one, whom thou didst prove at Massah, and with whom thou didst strive at the waters of Meribah;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a45c75ab-a5d0-406f-9d11-27e0eee54aaa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: DEU 33:9
Text: Who said unto his father and to his mother, I have not seen him; neither did he acknowledge his brethren, nor knew his own children: for they have observed thy word, and kept thy covenant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6d0887d-6157-4379-8933-a9ac42046579>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: DEU 33:10
Text: They shall teach Jacob thy judgments, and Israel thy law: they shall put incense before thee, and whole burnt sacrifice upon thine altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d817a587-ca61-4011-9f28-43aa65031552>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: DEU 33:11
Text: Bless, LORD, his substance, and accept the work of his hands; smite through the loins of them that rise against him, and of them that hate him, that they rise not again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56bb37f1-ae00-42aa-9358-ae7210bd630e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: DEU 33:12
Text: And of Benjamin he said, The beloved of the LORD shall dwell in safety by him; and the Lord shall cover him all the day long, and he shall dwell between his shoulders.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec90ce77-c3cf-46bd-92e9-1974942a121c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: DEU 33:13
Text: And of Joseph he said, Blessed of the LORD be his land, for the precious things of heaven, for the dew, and for the deep that coucheth beneath,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec69f6a7-1157-490f-8ab9-29ce94a3c93f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: DEU 33:14
Text: And for the precious fruits brought forth by the sun, and for the precious things put forth by the moon,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82d71006-c9ff-4e13-8a00-b37b7692131e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: DEU 33:15
Text: And for the chief things of the ancient mountains, and for the precious things of the lasting hills,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86ed55ba-5e8f-40a5-a8d3-b699b54eff75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: DEU 33:16
Text: And for the precious things of the earth and fulness thereof, and for the good will of him that dwelt in the bush: let the blessing come upon the head of Joseph, and upon the top of the head of him that was separated from his brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fcba3e3-85b9-4106-9f47-7ce7ee360007>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 274

Reference: DEU 33:17
Text: His glory is like the firstling of his bullock, and his horns are like the horns of unicorns: with them he shall push the people together to the ends of the earth: and they are the ten thousands of Ephraim, and they are the thousands of Manasseh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59b0e5bc-c45a-41bb-b85d-eb7aeed11a1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: DEU 33:18
Text: And of Zebulun he said, Rejoice, Zebulun, in thy going out; and, Issachar, in thy tents.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52fa61c9-af8d-4942-bd98-1b0a59a71941>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: DEU 33:19
Text: They shall call the people unto the mountain; there they shall offer sacrifices of righteousness: for they shall suck of the abundance of the seas, and of treasures hid in the sand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb1605f0-93ae-4ad8-bcdd-f62b1ea16277>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: DEU 33:20
Text: And of Gad he said, Blessed be he that enlargeth Gad: he dwelleth as a lion, and teareth the arm with the crown of the head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6faeea3-4aba-4328-83eb-e3b392f1340b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: DEU 33:21
Text: And he provided the first part for himself, because there, in a portion of the lawgiver, was he seated; and he came with the heads of the people, he executed the justice of the LORD, and his judgments with Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b905202f-71da-475d-b2c0-ff6d656b87cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: DEU 33:22
Text: And of Dan he said, Dan is a lion’s whelp: he shall leap from Bashan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa75643d-4190-4458-85fb-2e0d68ce415d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: DEU 33:23
Text: And of Naphtali he said, O Naphtali, satisfied with favour, and full with the blessing of the LORD: possess thou the west and the south.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04ce7832-0030-4024-aeec-449c774fa6de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: DEU 33:24
Text: And of Asher he said, Let Asher be blessed with children; let him be acceptable to his brethren, and let him dip his foot in oil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebda0ecf-598e-49f9-b73d-d5948b8e3720>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: DEU 33:25
Text: Thy shoes shall be iron and brass; and as thy days, so shall thy strength be.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f059673d-1e82-4f5a-a5b0-32f428c5d2b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: DEU 33:26
Text: There is none like unto the God of Jeshurun, who rideth upon the heaven in thy help, and in his excellency on the sky.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20dc0b8d-9bdb-4134-8255-1aa9c4a2f5e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: DEU 33:27
Text: The eternal God is thy refuge, and underneath are the everlasting arms: and he shall thrust out the enemy from before thee; and shall say, Destroy them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ddd06a2-0e4e-4254-8cc1-b042fa4d3af9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: DEU 33:28
Text: Israel then shall dwell in safety alone: the fountain of Jacob shall be upon a land of corn and wine; also his heavens shall drop down dew.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/33/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
