Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: DEU 34:5
Text: So Moses the servant of the LORD died there in the land of Moab, according to the word of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/34/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:097580ce-3798-446e-9798-47dc032b4654>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: DEU 34:6
Text: And he buried him in a valley in the land of Moab, over against Bethpeor: but no man knoweth of his sepulchre unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/34/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f121e14e-77e9-4ffc-a792-e6c8b36380e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: DEU 34:7
Text: And Moses was an hundred and twenty years old when he died: his eye was not dim, nor his natural force abated.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/34/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93d15ffb-dada-43a8-b1ba-1f29c139d899>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: DEU 34:8
Text: And the children of Israel wept for Moses in the plains of Moab thirty days: so the days of weeping and mourning for Moses were ended.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/34/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1811ea21-2268-4df8-8541-525ee53e24be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: DEU 34:9
Text: And Joshua the son of Nun was full of the spirit of wisdom; for Moses had laid his hands upon him: and the children of Israel hearkened unto him, and did as the LORD commanded Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/34/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4ff0ce4-ef40-484a-8f45-cc6a8b4de0d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: DEU 34:10
Text: And there arose not a prophet since in Israel like unto Moses, whom the LORD knew face to face,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/34/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a6f5824-02ae-4a54-ad22-625d684bcbd8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: DEU 34:11
Text: In all the signs and the wonders, which the LORD sent him to do in the land of Egypt to Pharaoh, and to all his servants, and to all his land,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DEU/34/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a44ba42c-2a0f-4568-ad78-2c2ae8a340fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: DEU 34:12
Text: And in all that mighty hand, and in all the great terror which Moses shewed in the sight of all Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8caac589-307f-486b-8ce2-e030d95a5002>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: JOS 1:1
Text: Now after the death of Moses the servant of the LORD it came to pass, that the LORD spake unto Joshua the son of Nun, Moses’ minister, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0aeb916e-e8f1-4b9a-b15b-fa26c49a98b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: JOS 1:2
Text: Moses my servant is dead; now therefore arise, go over this Jordan, thou, and all this people, unto the land which I do give to them, even to the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0c6ca0e-a3cf-4087-978a-2279157b4bba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: JOS 1:3
Text: Every place that the sole of your foot shall tread upon, that have I given unto you, as I said unto Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc643c3e-0050-4cac-8d1a-e84f43e2d81e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: JOS 1:4
Text: From the wilderness and this Lebanon even unto the great river, the river Euphrates, all the land of the Hittites, and unto the great sea toward the going down of the sun, shall be your coast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5af64de3-24fa-403e-9697-7d0ab5246b07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: JOS 1:5
Text: There shall not any man be able to stand before thee all the days of thy life: as I was with Moses, so I will be with thee: I will not fail thee, nor forsake thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e54d0ccd-d84d-45ef-b0b5-8d806415df75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: JOS 1:6
Text: Be strong and of a good courage: for unto this people shalt thou divide for an inheritance the land, which I sware unto their fathers to give them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eea92cb4-acdc-41ac-8d10-2cbdc0843b77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: JOS 1:7
Text: Only be thou strong and very courageous, that thou mayest observe to do according to all the law, which Moses my servant commanded thee: turn not from it to the right hand or to the left, that thou mayest prosper whithersoever thou goest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9db27897-d99c-4cec-8918-92afb019be3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 285

Reference: JOS 1:8
Text: This book of the law shall not depart out of thy mouth; but thou shalt meditate therein day and night, that thou mayest observe to do according to all that is written therein: for then thou shalt make thy way prosperous, and then thou shalt have good success.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c386e1c-185d-421f-abb6-47b7fa189a73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: JOS 1:9
Text: Have not I commanded thee? Be strong and of a good courage; be not afraid, neither be thou dismayed: for the LORD thy God is with thee whithersoever thou goest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0dcf224e-7901-466d-82ec-9fca9e6a70b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: JOS 1:10
Text: Then Joshua commanded the officers of the people, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30c59f84-d2db-44d3-a28a-2ec1c9bc865a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: JOS 1:11
Text: Pass through the host, and command the people, saying, Prepare you victuals; for within three days ye shall pass over this Jordan, to go in to possess the land, which the LORD your God giveth you to possess it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9277cc57-f952-4d62-b37a-7f481f73c1fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: JOS 1:12
Text: And to the Reubenites, and to the Gadites, and to half the tribe of Manasseh, spake Joshua, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c24b822-0501-4916-b4ad-a5efe639b36e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: JOS 1:13
Text: Remember the word which Moses the servant of the LORD commanded you, saying, The LORD your God hath given you rest, and hath given you this land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f048a9b-323b-4af7-9622-86aa850d4e3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: JOS 1:14
Text: Your wives, your little ones, and your cattle, shall remain in the land which Moses gave you on this side Jordan; but ye shall pass before your brethren armed, all the mighty men of valour, and help them;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a67a2776-9adc-4dcb-af31-aefb3ed04b6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 322

Reference: JOS 1:15
Text: Until the LORD have given your brethren rest, as he hath given you, and they also have possessed the land which the LORD your God giveth them: then ye shall return unto the land of your possession, and enjoy it, which Moses the LORD’s servant gave you on this side Jordan toward the sunrising.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66c170dd-0fe4-4f21-b12e-6e99ea4cd9a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: JOS 1:16
Text: And they answered Joshua, saying, All that thou commandest us we will do, and whithersoever thou sendest us, we will go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d7a48ae-1cd0-4098-a8e4-a4d9e2aeb454>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: JOS 1:17
Text: According as we hearkened unto Moses in all things, so will we hearken unto thee: only the LORD thy God be with thee, as he was with Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc03756d-01e0-48a5-b23f-246887189b04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: JOS 1:18
Text: Whosoever he be that doth rebel against thy commandment, and will not hearken unto thy words in all that thou commandest him, he shall be put to death: only be strong and of a good courage.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11eed48b-fbb8-445f-abe2-42db850f2587>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: JOS 2:1
Text: And Joshua the son of Nun sent out of Shittim two men to spy secretly, saying, Go view the land, even Jericho. And they went, and came into an harlot’s house, named Rahab, and lodged there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c7c983a-f964-48ce-827d-b09bf372d211>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: JOS 2:2
Text: And it was told the king of Jericho, saying, Behold, there came men in hither to night of the children of Israel to search out the country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58fa86f0-d5cc-4867-9022-c096992cc7be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: JOS 2:3
Text: And the king of Jericho sent unto Rahab, saying, Bring forth the men that are come to thee, which are entered into thine house: for they be come to search out all the country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8b01eb1-4614-4066-84f5-7c424fb658dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: JOS 2:4
Text: And the woman took the two men, and hid them, and said thus, There came men unto me, but I wist not whence they were:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22abb31a-e541-4707-9457-91ec0a5f43be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: JOS 2:5
Text: And it came to pass about the time of shutting of the gate, when it was dark, that the men went out: whither the men went I wot not: pursue after them quickly; for ye shall overtake them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de198583-f393-4835-9c88-554c0603bdf2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: JOS 2:6
Text: But she had brought them up to the roof of the house, and hid them with the stalks of flax, which she had laid in order upon the roof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0587ed9b-98fe-4c99-baa1-6b436d946989>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: JOS 2:7
Text: And the men pursued after them the way to Jordan unto the fords: and as soon as they which pursued after them were gone out, they shut the gate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f2eeb58-1244-4483-811d-c1a8e9b5d655>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: JOS 2:8
Text: And before they were laid down, she came up unto them upon the roof;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a120c68-8839-46e3-ad56-ee11e79d9469>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: JOS 2:9
Text: And she said unto the men, I know that the LORD hath given you the land, and that your terror is fallen upon us, and that all the inhabitants of the land faint because of you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:232b6c29-0e61-4623-80e2-b62538b92d8e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: JOS 2:10
Text: For we have heard how the LORD dried up the water of the Red sea for you, when ye came out of Egypt; and what ye did unto the two kings of the Amorites, that were on the other side Jordan, Sihon and Og, whom ye utterly destroyed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12bb0e0e-36ce-4348-8d23-9539fe4df3f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: JOS 2:11
Text: And as soon as we had heard these things, our hearts did melt, neither did there remain any more courage in any man, because of you: for the LORD your God, he is God in heaven above, and in earth beneath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b7c22c5-8a40-4094-b569-cd23c4d59197>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: JOS 2:12
Text: Now therefore, I pray you, swear unto me by the LORD, since I have shewed you kindness, that ye will also shew kindness unto my father’s house, and give me a true token:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cdf36cbb-cb68-4b3c-8b1c-556d5d408cf7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: JOS 2:13
Text: And that ye will save alive my father, and my mother, and my brethren, and my sisters, and all that they have, and deliver our lives from death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72a490e9-7c0e-4a6f-b03a-1f2e503f8e60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: JOS 2:14
Text: And the men answered her, Our life for yours, if ye utter not this our business. And it shall be, when the LORD hath given us the land, that we will deal kindly and truly with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb1ce559-3937-4dbf-8931-3dbade1b6c59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: JOS 2:15
Text: Then she let them down by a cord through the window: for her house was upon the town wall, and she dwelt upon the wall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4eb4d9ed-3f00-4f39-bd43-aa2bab429d0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: JOS 2:16
Text: And she said unto them, Get you to the mountain, lest the pursuers meet you; and hide yourselves there three days, until the pursuers be returned: and afterward may ye go your way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7cbbbd2c-7ea3-46e0-9350-3762842a8742>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: JOS 2:17
Text: And the men said unto her, We will be blameless of this thine oath which thou hast made us swear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7546b65-02f6-466e-9a6d-c48024c49b98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: JOS 2:18
Text: Behold, when we come into the land, thou shalt bind this line of scarlet thread in the window which thou didst let us down by: and thou shalt bring thy father, and thy mother, and thy brethren, and all thy father’s household, home unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f333d85f-1afc-4389-b832-301aa0ffc2b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 278

Reference: JOS 2:19
Text: And it shall be, that whosoever shall go out of the doors of thy house into the street, his blood shall be upon his head, and we will be guiltless: and whosoever shall be with thee in the house, his blood shall be on our head, if any hand be upon him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eacc3896-a206-4662-b7e4-4183fbc8c4b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: JOS 2:20
Text: And if thou utter this our business, then we will be quit of thine oath which thou hast made us to swear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf923c79-77ae-4e0c-a2cc-07e1ac583de5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: JOS 2:21
Text: And she said, According unto your words, so be it. And she sent them away, and they departed: and she bound the scarlet line in the window.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af19a2a9-e79f-4f07-882d-8efdf4472835>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: JOS 2:22
Text: And they went, and came unto the mountain, and abode there three days, until the pursuers were returned: and the pursuers sought them throughout all the way, but found them not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18a1a9d0-2be0-4c02-baf9-376c89d186b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: JOS 2:23
Text: So the two men returned, and descended from the mountain, and passed over, and came to Joshua the son of Nun, and told him all things that befell them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/2/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b44d1395-d74e-4ac4-9b25-1ad156fae546>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: JOS 2:24
Text: And they said unto Joshua, Truly the LORD hath delivered into our hands all the land; for even all the inhabitants of the country do faint because of us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f7caef1-f1c7-40ec-ad58-d7d66b41fe2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: JOS 3:1
Text: And Joshua rose early in the morning; and they removed from Shittim, and came to Jordan, he and all the children of Israel, and lodged there before they passed over.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75feaabe-7c30-45e1-bcbc-8373cfb18124>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: JOS 3:2
Text: And it came to pass after three days, that the officers went through the host;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9875daf7-5e45-43e4-91a8-52673b6d2e24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: JOS 3:3
Text: And they commanded the people, saying, When ye see the ark of the covenant of the LORD your God, and the priests the Levites bearing it, then ye shall remove from your place, and go after it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7cc6d77d-ca84-48f6-b403-c739d152cb20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: JOS 3:4
Text: Yet there shall be a space between you and it, about two thousand cubits by measure: come not near unto it, that ye may know the way by which ye must go: for ye have not passed this way heretofore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd6b8e40-fcea-4d33-869f-2b57cda802dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: JOS 3:5
Text: And Joshua said unto the people, Sanctify yourselves: for to morrow the LORD will do wonders among you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffa5c9be-a724-4f5f-b547-54d89c3e4a46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: JOS 3:6
Text: And Joshua spake unto the priests, saying, Take up the ark of the covenant, and pass over before the people. And they took up the ark of the covenant, and went before the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7baedb10-6fff-4ca7-8553-0847038cc1c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: JOS 3:7
Text: And the LORD said unto Joshua, This day will I begin to magnify thee in the sight of all Israel, that they may know that, as I was with Moses, so I will be with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0371340d-d833-4a11-82ab-5f0cb8ab2526>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: JOS 3:8
Text: And thou shalt command the priests that bear the ark of the covenant, saying, When ye are come to the brink of the water of Jordan, ye shall stand still in Jordan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c50ff3c-6808-4b51-a558-598228788045>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: JOS 3:9
Text: And Joshua said unto the children of Israel, Come hither, and hear the words of the LORD your God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78726512-56c1-465b-a95b-68b52ca02314>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 283

Reference: JOS 3:10
Text: And Joshua said, Hereby ye shall know that the living God is among you, and that he will without fail drive out from before you the Canaanites, and the Hittites, and the Hivites, and the Perizzites, and the Girgashites, and the Amorites, and the Jebusites.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63ef53c7-0c78-4c0e-91f3-112cb2e9355b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: JOS 3:11
Text: Behold, the ark of the covenant of the LORD of all the earth passeth over before you into Jordan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc436385-8eb3-464d-a61c-1d8a7d97a2c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: JOS 3:12
Text: Now therefore take you twelve men out of the tribes of Israel, out of every tribe a man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4619f0a6-371e-42e2-bacf-6ae94534e988>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 316

Reference: JOS 3:13
Text: And it shall come to pass, as soon as the soles of the feet of the priests that bear the ark of the LORD, the LORD of all the earth, shall rest in the waters of Jordan, that the waters of Jordan shall be cut off from the waters that come down from above; and they shall stand upon an heap.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2867db64-e95f-4321-82e8-f35664c8c791>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: JOS 3:14
Text: And it came to pass, when the people removed from their tents, to pass over Jordan, and the priests bearing the ark of the covenant before the people;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ad8c538-d88a-4b58-9e76-0b5dd21b959c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: JOS 3:15
Text: And as they that bare the ark were come unto Jordan, and the feet of the priests that bare the ark were dipped in the brim of the water, (for Jordan overfloweth all his banks all the time of harvest,)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc64dc62-22e5-47ed-8e51-66ec619ddb40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 302

Reference: JOS 3:16
Text: That the waters which came down from above stood and rose up upon an heap very far from the city Adam, that is beside Zaretan: and those that came down toward the sea of the plain, even the salt sea, failed, and were cut off: and the people passed over right against Jericho.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc39243d-93f1-4828-9434-2f6eccb9e6fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: JOS 3:17
Text: And the priests that bare the ark of the covenant of the LORD stood firm on dry ground in the midst of Jordan, and all the Israelites passed over on dry ground, until all the people were passed clean over Jordan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d404da25-f11b-4d28-992b-d3d34d68dbc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: JOS 4:1
Text: And it came to pass, when all the people were clean passed over Jordan, that the LORD spake unto Joshua, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6f13308-d41f-44ba-bbd9-2d69b399b831>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: JOS 4:2
Text: Take you twelve men out of the people, out of every tribe a man,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc1392ae-0dbe-4b5a-a831-ec62af21f964>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: JOS 4:3
Text: And command ye them, saying, Take you hence out of the midst of Jordan, out of the place where the priests’ feet stood firm, twelve stones, and ye shall carry them over with you, and leave them in the lodging place, where ye shall lodge this night.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bec56d40-1afe-4a7e-8d6c-22eee53e8950>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: JOS 4:4
Text: Then Joshua called the twelve men, whom he had prepared of the children of Israel, out of every tribe a man:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af32e6d7-28d2-4c5e-8491-117c88b3f1b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: JOS 4:5
Text: And Joshua said unto them, Pass over before the ark of the LORD your God into the midst of Jordan, and take you up every man of you a stone upon his shoulder, according unto the number of the tribes of the children of Israel:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96da818d-0bd8-49dc-aaeb-b269dee34029>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: JOS 4:6
Text: That this may be a sign among you, that when your children ask their fathers in time to come, saying, What mean ye by these stones?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f403623-3b6d-4961-b013-34f5a1ad5f19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 277

Reference: JOS 4:7
Text: Then ye shall answer them, That the waters of Jordan were cut off before the ark of the covenant of the LORD; when it passed over Jordan, the waters of Jordan were cut off: and these stones shall be for a memorial unto the children of Israel for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f1d1153-c3a2-448f-84cd-1d626a6c2205>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 322

Reference: JOS 4:8
Text: And the children of Israel did so as Joshua commanded, and took up twelve stones out of the midst of Jordan, as the LORD spake unto Joshua, according to the number of the tribes of the children of Israel, and carried them over with them unto the place where they lodged, and laid them down there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b4b175c-28e0-4cf3-a552-5c9ed44c2b31>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: JOS 4:9
Text: And Joshua set up twelve stones in the midst of Jordan, in the place where the feet of the priests which bare the ark of the covenant stood: and they are there unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e28b35e-c8a1-416e-9133-542b5c8932c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: JOS 4:10
Text: For the priests which bare the ark stood in the midst of Jordan, until everything was finished that the LORD commanded Joshua to speak unto the people, according to all that Moses commanded Joshua: and the people hasted and passed over.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56bde358-d23d-4fbd-a6a7-d71d3f3aaf93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: JOS 4:11
Text: And it came to pass, when all the people were clean passed over, that the ark of the LORD passed over, and the priests, in the presence of the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9e2b5f2-4d10-43c6-b7b7-31fff74d8352>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: JOS 4:12
Text: And the children of Reuben, and the children of Gad, and half the tribe of Manasseh, passed over armed before the children of Israel, as Moses spake unto them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d815388-e743-4bfe-8e97-863907a1ccc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: JOS 4:13
Text: About forty thousand prepared for war passed over before the LORD unto battle, to the plains of Jericho.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69e5f303-661a-4c89-af7b-d21a9a51bfac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: JOS 4:14
Text: On that day the LORD magnified Joshua in the sight of all Israel; and they feared him, as they feared Moses, all the days of his life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a673512-2f39-4332-94e3-37743002a87b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 66

Reference: JOS 4:15
Text: And the LORD spake unto Joshua, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:642b3bdc-9aac-41cb-afc8-0ac7a3abde2d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: JOS 4:16
Text: Command the priests that bear the ark of the testimony, that they come up out of Jordan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0cc419f2-b5ba-4f1c-999f-7efb37a77453>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: JOS 4:17
Text: Joshua therefore commanded the priests, saying, Come ye up out of Jordan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:707c1a12-9211-4bb1-a62e-0de596e851c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 326

Reference: JOS 4:18
Text: And it came to pass, when the priests that bare the ark of the covenant of the LORD were come up out of the midst of Jordan, and the soles of the priests’ feet were lifted up unto the dry land, that the waters of Jordan returned unto their place, and flowed over all his banks, as they did before.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ec51d40-e6a9-4709-bd74-a35a98adf919>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: JOS 4:19
Text: And the people came up out of Jordan on the tenth day of the first month, and encamped in Gilgal, in the east border of Jericho.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39fcdfbd-8b72-4bce-9786-789d97f52317>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: JOS 4:20
Text: And those twelve stones, which they took out of Jordan, did Joshua pitch in Gilgal.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab846535-cc32-4267-aacf-bfab2329f9cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: JOS 4:21
Text: And he spake unto the children of Israel, saying, When your children shall ask their fathers in time to come, saying, What mean these stones?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:721affa8-e80f-4aee-ae73-4a336c547a15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: JOS 4:22
Text: Then ye shall let your children know, saying, Israel came over this Jordan on dry land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f00f29a-c210-4538-baf9-7147767ec534>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: JOS 4:23
Text: For the LORD your God dried up the waters of Jordan from before you, until ye were passed over, as the LORD your God did to the Red sea, which he dried up from before us, until we were gone over:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/4/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4025d2ce-51d8-48db-af37-126219548866>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: JOS 4:24
Text: That all the people of the earth might know the hand of the LORD, that it is mighty: that ye might fear the LORD your God for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b5aec0e-23fd-4f58-8e65-930d309046b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 405

Reference: JOS 5:1
Text: And it came to pass, when all the kings of the Amorites, which were on the side of Jordan westward, and all the kings of the Canaanites, which were by the sea, heard that the LORD had dried up the waters of Jordan from before the children of Israel, until we were passed over, that their heart melted, neither was there spirit in them any more, because of the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fcf769bc-6a50-4a8a-b0e9-d8c6510346f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: JOS 5:2
Text: At that time the LORD said unto Joshua, Make thee sharp knives, and circumcise again the children of Israel the second time.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff5b01f4-73a0-4f4d-a24c-5f90dcdb887d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: JOS 5:3
Text: And Joshua made him sharp knives, and circumcised the children of Israel at the hill of the foreskins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc407845-d0b1-48d9-85ff-6d0d7cc6eeb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: JOS 5:4
Text: And this is the cause why Joshua did circumcise: All the people that came out of Egypt, that were males, even all the men of war, died in the wilderness by the way, after they came out of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:945c1605-2b46-4c57-a1f0-b6c0c1e86d20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: JOS 5:5
Text: Now all the people that came out were circumcised: but all the people that were born in the wilderness by the way as they came forth out of Egypt, them they had not circumcised.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e1dabb5-4b2d-4a34-b9fa-94b534042a84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 386

Reference: JOS 5:6
Text: For the children of Israel walked forty years in the wilderness, till all the people that were men of war, which came out of Egypt, were consumed, because they obeyed not the voice of the LORD: unto whom the LORD sware that he would not shew them the land, which the LORD sware unto their fathers that he would give us, a land that floweth with milk and honey.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:620b9abd-d438-468b-84f3-fbf7502bb670>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: JOS 5:7
Text: And their children, whom he raised up in their stead, them Joshua circumcised: for they were uncircumcised, because they had not circumcised them by the way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f0f2d15-4efc-4dd5-926d-ac1a459f91b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: JOS 5:8
Text: And it came to pass, when they had done circumcising all the people, that they abode in their places in the camp, till they were whole.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f66cc726-f6f3-48d7-a838-d6166c8c7ed3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: JOS 5:9
Text: And the LORD said unto Joshua, This day have I rolled away the reproach of Egypt from off you. Wherefore the name of the place is called Gilgal unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b607470-46b6-410f-9f61-bb0d855bc954>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: JOS 5:10
Text: And the children of Israel encamped in Gilgal, and kept the passover on the fourteenth day of the month at even in the plains of Jericho.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:493d64e1-a83a-4dc9-86f8-849638b6ffae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: JOS 5:11
Text: And they did eat of the old corn of the land on the morrow after the passover, unleavened cakes, and parched corn in the selfsame day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5918e809-5447-486f-849c-526ef8a9e42f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: JOS 5:12
Text: And the manna ceased on the morrow after they had eaten of the old corn of the land; neither had the children of Israel manna any more; but they did eat of the fruit of the land of Canaan that year.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e058e1c-6c81-4835-8ab1-d536a0a9e1ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 282

Reference: JOS 5:13
Text: And it came to pass, when Joshua was by Jericho, that he lifted up his eyes and looked, and, behold, there stood a man over against him with his sword drawn in his hand: and Joshua went unto him, and said unto him, Art thou for us, or for our adversaries?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3474c81b-0896-4810-b52f-2e98f2862a91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: JOS 5:14
Text: And he said, Nay; but as captain of the host of the LORD am I now come. And Joshua fell on his face to the earth, and did worship, and said unto him, What saith my Lord unto his servant?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51428e07-90b3-4180-9136-75bc3adfe279>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: JOS 5:15
Text: And the captain of the LORD’s host said unto Joshua, Loose thy shoe from off thy foot; for the place whereon thou standest is holy. And Joshua did so.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:055406f3-0e85-48cd-8a52-019732b76897>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: JOS 6:1
Text: Now Jericho was straitly shut up because of the children of Israel: none went out, and none came in.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:675b64f3-fbd2-4b53-8c32-31b49ebfb615>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: JOS 6:2
Text: And the LORD said unto Joshua, See, I have given into thine hand Jericho, and the king thereof, and the mighty men of valour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0846db21-0687-49aa-a714-e268e20c4087>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: JOS 6:3
Text: And ye shall compass the city, all ye men of war, and go round about the city once. Thus shalt thou do six days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94c8c36d-0ee6-422e-bb6f-dc0afbe9ddf5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: JOS 6:4
Text: And seven priests shall bear before the ark seven trumpets of rams’ horns: and the seventh day ye shall compass the city seven times, and the priests shall blow with the trumpets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d9ddf27-b62c-4354-8dc1-4accea1a02ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 307

Reference: JOS 6:5
Text: And it shall come to pass, that when they make a long blast with the ram’s horn, and when ye hear the sound of the trumpet, all the people shall shout with a great shout; and the wall of the city shall fall down flat, and the people shall ascend up every man straight before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:599c38eb-c187-4c7d-a366-1d881f452471>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: JOS 6:6
Text: And Joshua the son of Nun called the priests, and said unto them, Take up the ark of the covenant, and let seven priests bear seven trumpets of rams’ horns before the ark of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab5dd005-5047-4991-a489-5e788ffa7d44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: JOS 6:7
Text: And he said unto the people, Pass on, and compass the city, and let him that is armed pass on before the ark of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9de5bd1d-cecd-4f2e-a775-09c5448d3d6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: JOS 6:8
Text: And it came to pass, when Joshua had spoken unto the people, that the seven priests bearing the seven trumpets of rams’ horns passed on before the LORD, and blew with the trumpets: and the ark of the covenant of the LORD followed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4d3387c-6d0b-4863-8d33-0d7702bdb920>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: JOS 6:9
Text: And the armed men went before the priests that blew with the trumpets, and the rereward came after the ark, the priests going on, and blowing with the trumpets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80f67ca5-92cf-458c-abf0-cd5998bae503>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: JOS 6:10
Text: And Joshua had commanded the people, saying, Ye shall not shout, nor make any noise with your voice, neither shall any word proceed out of your mouth, until the day I bid you shout; then shall ye shout.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2104eb71-8fcc-434b-b0c5-7e023f486d12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: JOS 6:11
Text: So the ark of the LORD compassed the city, going about it once: and they came into the camp, and lodged in the camp.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf292940-2344-4e3f-8d46-a2688438e63d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: JOS 6:12
Text: And Joshua rose early in the morning, and the priests took up the ark of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f07f551-bd33-4163-ac8f-dd22172b84b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 298

Reference: JOS 6:13
Text: And seven priests bearing seven trumpets of rams’ horns before the ark of the LORD went on continually, and blew with the trumpets: and the armed men went before them; but the rereward came after the ark of the LORD, the priests going on, and blowing with the trumpets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3d83e24-41c1-4dde-8dfc-dbef05580c48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: JOS 6:14
Text: And the second day they compassed the city once, and returned into the camp: so they did six days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be13a435-b4e5-4d3a-85f7-c7cf00891f84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: JOS 6:15
Text: And it came to pass on the seventh day, that they rose early about the dawning of the day, and compassed the city after the same manner seven times: only on that day they compassed the city seven times.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7117ea0-456d-4317-9e43-3dca0d6d90ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JOS 6:16
Text: And it came to pass at the seventh time, when the priests blew with the trumpets, Joshua said unto the people, Shout; for the LORD hath given you the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46522a14-50e5-47a6-93cc-cadfa5dd9c9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: JOS 6:17
Text: And the city shall be accursed, even it, and all that are therein, to the LORD: only Rahab the harlot shall live, she and all that are with her in the house, because she hid the messengers that we sent.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9350f0cd-1cf7-4fc9-a322-4a1b03e03cad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: JOS 6:18
Text: And ye, in any wise keep yourselves from the accursed thing, lest ye make yourselves accursed, when ye take of the accursed thing, and make the camp of Israel a curse, and trouble it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5335a4fa-91a4-4ed6-85ea-b4df7e351661>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: JOS 6:19
Text: But all the silver, and gold, and vessels of brass and iron, are consecrated unto the LORD: they shall come into the treasury of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c90bc16-6d2a-45bb-ac56-6a162453899c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 328

Reference: JOS 6:20
Text: So the people shouted when the priests blew with the trumpets: and it came to pass, when the people heard the sound of the trumpet, and the people shouted with a great shout, that the wall fell down flat, so that the people went up into the city, every man straight before him, and they took the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5c3ecb4-c04a-4f3b-b85a-669e8956c81c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: JOS 6:21
Text: And they utterly destroyed all that was in the city, both man and woman, young and old, and ox, and sheep, and ass, with the edge of the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d90847f8-714d-49cb-9bd4-058758ef4967>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: JOS 6:22
Text: But Joshua had said unto the two men that had spied out the country, Go into the harlot’s house, and bring out thence the woman, and all that she hath, as ye sware unto her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d51b2e0a-d240-4c46-8ba7-4ee5da43d5a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: JOS 6:23
Text: And the young men that were spies went in, and brought out Rahab, and her father, and her mother, and her brethren, and all that she had; and they brought out all her kindred, and left them without the camp of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c64c9e91-88da-48e0-a617-b64fdff8cee8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: JOS 6:24
Text: And they burnt the city with fire, and all that was therein: only the silver, and the gold, and the vessels of brass and of iron, they put into the treasury of the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:868592f3-54a9-481c-8aba-1964e342295b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: JOS 6:25
Text: And Joshua saved Rahab the harlot alive, and her father’s household, and all that she had; and she dwelleth in Israel even unto this day; because she hid the messengers, which Joshua sent to spy out Jericho.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb390e11-69c2-4b60-a813-75b638bdfa3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: JOS 6:26
Text: And Joshua adjured them at that time, saying, Cursed be the man before the LORD, that riseth up and buildeth this city Jericho: he shall lay the foundation thereof in his firstborn, and in his youngest son shall he set up the gates of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/6/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd9d66e9-3430-44ea-a264-7b9ff6493cde>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: JOS 6:27
Text: So the LORD was with Joshua; and his fame was noised throughout all the country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10065a9a-f440-4124-8915-40b707883512>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 282

Reference: JOS 7:1
Text: But the children of Israel committed a trespass in the accursed thing: for Achan, the son of Carmi, the son of Zabdi, the son of Zerah, of the tribe of Judah, took of the accursed thing: and the anger of the LORD was kindled against the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb894314-42ab-48b4-aa5c-3c8e59d0a814>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: JOS 7:2
Text: And Joshua sent men from Jericho to Ai, which is beside Bethaven, on the east of Bethel, and spake unto them, saying, Go up and view the country. And the men went up and viewed Ai.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:488fd973-141f-4a89-b84c-bfb0c798ae5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: JOS 7:3
Text: And they returned to Joshua, and said unto him, Let not all the people go up; but let about two or three thousand men go up and smite Ai; and make not all the people to labour thither; for they are but few.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5290042-66a8-42c2-91dd-e283a0652638>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: JOS 7:4
Text: So there went up thither of the people about three thousand men: and they fled before the men of Ai.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71bf7281-3fcb-480d-a98f-7d5d1e31d187>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: JOS 7:5
Text: And the men of Ai smote of them about thirty and six men: for they chased them from before the gate even unto Shebarim, and smote them in the going down: wherefore the hearts of the people melted, and became as water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3dbf11bc-589b-4f72-8b6b-782e3aef9a72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: JOS 7:6
Text: And Joshua rent his clothes, and fell to the earth upon his face before the ark of the LORD until the eventide, he and the elders of Israel, and put dust upon their heads.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54f56023-e5d1-4ae5-90b2-d572f02c3e77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: JOS 7:7
Text: And Joshua said, Alas, O LORD God, wherefore hast thou at all brought this people over Jordan, to deliver us into the hand of the Amorites, to destroy us? would to God we had been content, and dwelt on the other side Jordan!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5a4ad59-9403-4d30-aaac-68beccbe54b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: JOS 7:8
Text: O LORD, what shall I say, when Israel turneth their backs before their enemies!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:587d046b-c709-47e2-92a5-1ecc663c0eea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: JOS 7:9
Text: For the Canaanites and all the inhabitants of the land shall hear of it, and shall environ us round, and cut off our name from the earth: and what wilt thou do unto thy great name?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b309053a-6256-4a9d-b0d8-1f4dd599a65d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: JOS 7:10
Text: And the LORD said unto Joshua, Get thee up; wherefore liest thou thus upon thy face?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4fca191-1e0d-45d1-9630-6e82f8296d3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: JOS 7:11
Text: Israel hath sinned, and they have also transgressed my covenant which I commanded them: for they have even taken of the accursed thing, and have also stolen, and dissembled also, and they have put it even among their own stuff.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8c070e9-d059-4b38-9f29-f559a952d954>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: JOS 7:12
Text: Therefore the children of Israel could not stand before their enemies, but turned their backs before their enemies, because they were accursed: neither will I be with you any more, except ye destroy the accursed from among you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2010fae7-8167-4ab0-8735-94a7d2f47581>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 294

Reference: JOS 7:13
Text: Up, sanctify the people, and say, Sanctify yourselves against to morrow: for thus saith the LORD God of Israel, There is an accursed thing in the midst of thee, O Israel: thou canst not stand before thine enemies, until ye take away the accursed thing from among you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fccb6d5-95ab-49fe-80a3-d848cbfba24c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 331

Reference: JOS 7:14
Text: In the morning therefore ye shall be brought according to your tribes: and it shall be, that the tribe which the LORD taketh shall come according to the families thereof; and the family which the LORD shall take shall come by households; and the household which the LORD shall take shall come man by man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8f8a71b-3f6b-4ed6-a31f-968f36887381>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: JOS 7:15
Text: And it shall be, that he that is taken with the accursed thing shall be burnt with fire, he and all that he hath: because he hath transgressed the covenant of the LORD, and because he hath wrought folly in Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7eb63592-a84c-4415-a732-d428a854d9f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: JOS 7:16
Text: So Joshua rose up early in the morning, and brought Israel by their tribes; and the tribe of Judah was taken:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d03bf9c4-3130-4b61-9039-15f12ad1fd37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: JOS 7:17
Text: And he brought the family of Judah; and he took the family of the Zarhites: and he brought the family of the Zarhites man by man; and Zabdi was taken:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed3e959e-6791-4778-ab76-333045a27099>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: JOS 7:18
Text: And he brought his household man by man; and Achan, the son of Carmi, the son of Zabdi, the son of Zerah, of the tribe of Judah, was taken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e920c8b5-8ac4-44ac-862b-eec35a571588>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: JOS 7:19
Text: And Joshua said unto Achan, My son, give, I pray thee, glory to the LORD God of Israel, and make confession unto him; and tell me now what thou hast done; hide it not from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12fb9e55-fc6e-477c-99f6-be2c7fc199d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: JOS 7:20
Text: And Achan answered Joshua, and said, Indeed I have sinned against the LORD God of Israel, and thus and thus have I done:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4ff4650-5a83-4c39-88c0-201e99ce6dc3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 288

Reference: JOS 7:21
Text: When I saw among the spoils a goodly Babylonish garment, and two hundred shekels of silver, and a wedge of gold of fifty shekels weight, then I coveted them, and took them; and, behold, they are hid in the earth in the midst of my tent, and the silver under it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a102ff29-10dc-4a58-84b6-902a365fc790>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: JOS 7:22
Text: So Joshua sent messengers, and they ran unto the tent; and, behold, it was hid in his tent, and the silver under it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38099a3a-8f31-44ff-8726-562321b9c1d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: JOS 7:23
Text: And they took them out of the midst of the tent, and brought them unto Joshua, and unto all the children of Israel, and laid them out before the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66a9991e-f99c-43f1-bafe-dfe14ce44d97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 308

Reference: JOS 7:24
Text: And Joshua, and all Israel with him, took Achan the son of Zerah, and the silver, and the garment, and the wedge of gold, and his sons, and his daughters, and his oxen, and his asses, and his sheep, and his tent, and all that he had: and they brought them unto the valley of Achor.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:787a3738-34c7-4be8-9fbf-7de4190fe077>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: JOS 7:25
Text: And Joshua said, Why hast thou troubled us? the LORD shall trouble thee this day. And all Israel stoned him with stones, and burned them with fire, after they had stoned them with stones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/7/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b09a1bbb-29b3-4d4b-a17d-fa85ca952314>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: JOS 7:26
Text: And they raised over him a great heap of stones unto this day. So the LORD turned from the fierceness of his anger. Wherefore the name of that place was called, The valley of Achor, unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0823862c-f7cc-4eb9-9247-b96bb3c2b4f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: JOS 8:1
Text: And the LORD said unto Joshua, Fear not, neither be thou dismayed: take all the people of war with thee, and arise, go up to Ai: see, I have given into thy hand the king of Ai, and his people, and his city, and his land:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5bf2faf-f943-4562-bed0-824a0da99e74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: JOS 8:2
Text: And thou shalt do to Ai and her king as thou didst unto Jericho and her king: only the spoil thereof, and the cattle thereof, shall ye take for a prey unto yourselves: lay thee an ambush for the city behind it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de0d7e55-56e1-4f0f-9ead-e0eaa1ad7d28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: JOS 8:3
Text: So Joshua arose, and all the people of war, to go up against Ai: and Joshua chose out thirty thousand mighty men of valour, and sent them away by night.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:526d859b-6007-409f-8dcd-22a7fee0c295>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: JOS 8:4
Text: And he commanded them, saying, Behold, ye shall lie in wait against the city, even behind the city: go not very far from the city, but be ye all ready:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1e29e93-1512-4c73-90cf-d2776f25ca85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: JOS 8:5
Text: And I, and all the people that are with me, will approach unto the city: and it shall come to pass, when they come out against us, as at the first, that we will flee before them,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ce6afa2-8650-46a3-9a85-e47fca92ce3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: JOS 8:6
Text: (For they will come out after us) till we have drawn them from the city; for they will say, They flee before us, as at the first: therefore we will flee before them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:951c8ea2-c3d7-4250-9b92-5a36ab55b545>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: JOS 8:7
Text: Then ye shall rise up from the ambush, and seize upon the city: for the LORD your God will deliver it into your hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba7c5ce5-da78-4c79-a7ec-0225dd02df79>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: JOS 8:8
Text: And it shall be, when ye have taken the city, that ye shall set the city on fire: according to the commandment of the LORD shall ye do. See, I have commanded you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c46636c-890f-4d66-b8e3-24382e300ee2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: JOS 8:9
Text: Joshua therefore sent them forth: and they went to lie in ambush, and abode between Bethel and Ai, on the west side of Ai: but Joshua lodged that night among the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4255ca16-0aff-4bdb-a541-55b5e7ead4be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: JOS 8:10
Text: And Joshua rose up early in the morning, and numbered the people, and went up, he and the elders of Israel, before the people to Ai.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbff06ca-46f9-4c47-bd24-e00dd2f7403f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: JOS 8:11
Text: And all the people, even the people of war that were with him, went up, and drew nigh, and came before the city, and pitched on the north side of Ai: now there was a valley between them and Ai.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f62b44b3-e4cb-42f4-9256-0c64571a300e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: JOS 8:12
Text: And he took about five thousand men, and set them to lie in ambush between Bethel and Ai, on the west side of the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c1a710d-e270-4ccc-ac2b-975e775dc322>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: JOS 8:13
Text: And when they had set the people, even all the host that was on the north of the city, and their liers in wait on the west of the city, Joshua went that night into the midst of the valley.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:041529f9-6520-451a-acf8-64ca9adb29b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 309

Reference: JOS 8:14
Text: And it came to pass, when the king of Ai saw it, that they hasted and rose up early, and the men of the city went out against Israel to battle, he and all his people, at a time appointed, before the plain; but he wist not that there were liers in ambush against him behind the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e919ce0-86a0-484d-92d8-c757ab144318>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: JOS 8:15
Text: And Joshua and all Israel made as if they were beaten before them, and fled by the way of the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f27656f4-0c2e-4690-8948-fa10aaadaf02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: JOS 8:16
Text: And all the people that were in Ai were called together to pursue after them: and they pursued after Joshua, and were drawn away from the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3357f7e-3f90-4c22-8b18-210675badfaa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: JOS 8:17
Text: And there was not a man left in Ai or Bethel, that went not out after Israel: and they left the city open, and pursued after Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41106dee-0c51-4dd1-b2b6-b9582ba31291>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: JOS 8:18
Text: And the LORD said unto Joshua, Stretch out the spear that is in thy hand toward Ai; for I will give it into thine hand. And Joshua stretched out the spear that he had in his hand toward the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c279e07b-63c8-4e5a-a39c-dc37bec174a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: JOS 8:19
Text: And the ambush arose quickly out of their place, and they ran as soon as he had stretched out his hand: and they entered into the city, and took it, and hasted and set the city on fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d088b36d-908c-42a9-a910-2dd7982fefc2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: JOS 8:20
Text: And when the men of Ai looked behind them, they saw, and, behold, the smoke of the city ascended up to heaven, and they had no power to flee this way or that way: and the people that fled to the wilderness turned back upon the pursuers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7ab0565-c9bf-4832-a685-bb957ca31ce1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: JOS 8:21
Text: And when Joshua and all Israel saw that the ambush had taken the city, and that the smoke of the city ascended, then they turned again, and slew the men of Ai.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e62f8ea7-10c9-46ae-8a7b-d6a509c78e0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: JOS 8:22
Text: And the other issued out of the city against them; so they were in the midst of Israel, some on this side, and some on that side: and they smote them, so that they let none of them remain or escape.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8212642c-6b1a-4fe8-8727-8534125cb67f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: JOS 8:23
Text: And the king of Ai they took alive, and brought him to Joshua.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d09912e8-0329-4801-9a2e-4ef970468cfb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 335

Reference: JOS 8:24
Text: And it came to pass, when Israel had made an end of slaying all the inhabitants of Ai in the field, in the wilderness wherein they chased them, and when they were all fallen on the edge of the sword, until they were consumed, that all the Israelites returned unto Ai, and smote it with the edge of the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0cabc43b-9393-4075-a79d-c35f174c8253>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: JOS 8:25
Text: And so it was, that all that fell that day, both of men and women, were twelve thousand, even all the men of Ai.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acd13382-acf6-426f-a243-03a7f19f488d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: JOS 8:26
Text: For Joshua drew not his hand back, wherewith he stretched out the spear, until he had utterly destroyed all the inhabitants of Ai.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ceaec1a-c032-48c1-b8dd-4e94960bd0c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: JOS 8:27
Text: Only the cattle and the spoil of that city Israel took for a prey unto themselves, according unto the word of the LORD which he commanded Joshua.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1752da8-d935-4bb7-a0ae-38d0338a7f86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: JOS 8:28
Text: And Joshua burnt Ai, and made it an heap for ever, even a desolation unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4c4cda9-9126-44cb-bb7e-54c2074e3ae5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 310

Reference: JOS 8:29
Text: And the king of Ai he hanged on a tree until eventide: and as soon as the sun was down, Joshua commanded that they should take his carcase down from the tree, and cast it at the entering of the gate of the city, and raise thereon a great heap of stones, that remaineth unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2948db14-9c69-4b63-91ab-faf2d8236483>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: JOS 8:30
Text: Then Joshua built an altar unto the LORD God of Israel in mount Ebal,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f40093ef-ab5b-40bd-aee4-51a85d77adbb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 298

Reference: JOS 8:31
Text: As Moses the servant of the LORD commanded the children of Israel, as it is written in the book of the law of Moses, an altar of whole stones, over which no man hath lift up any iron: and they offered thereon burnt offerings unto the LORD, and sacrificed peace offerings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e6c2e16-8949-48bd-adaa-3fa3dc2e45d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: JOS 8:32
Text: And he wrote there upon the stones a copy of the law of Moses, which he wrote in the presence of the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/8/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
