Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 297

Reference: JOS 9:1
Text: And it came to pass, when all the kings which were on this side Jordan, in the hills, and in the valleys, and in all the coasts of the great sea over against Lebanon, the Hittite, and the Amorite, the Canaanite, the Perizzite, the Hivite, and the Jebusite, heard thereof;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de77d282-5c71-4855-a9b7-6c4ee3a847a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: JOS 9:2
Text: That they gathered themselves together, to fight with Joshua and with Israel, with one accord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02cc4b28-34a7-4186-9da0-45518a292c16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: JOS 9:3
Text: And when the inhabitants of Gibeon heard what Joshua had done unto Jericho and to Ai,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf34c2a0-f219-4d8d-882d-e4fd6c1ca89a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JOS 9:4
Text: They did work wilily, and went and made as if they had been ambassadors, and took old sacks upon their asses, and wine bottles, old, and rent, and bound up;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:215b9f90-8153-4916-afd4-aae9946661a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: JOS 9:5
Text: And old shoes and clouted upon their feet, and old garments upon them; and all the bread of their provision was dry and mouldy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34687568-d0bc-4efb-a5c3-bb76fbda8a84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: JOS 9:6
Text: And they went to Joshua unto the camp at Gilgal, and said unto him, and to the men of Israel, We be come from a far country: now therefore make ye a league with us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60f6c18b-f260-4d7c-9b99-887fe7037897>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: JOS 9:7
Text: And the men of Israel said unto the Hivites, Peradventure ye dwell among us; and how shall we make a league with you?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d69d9bc-034c-4806-8be0-9b4c9105873c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: JOS 9:8
Text: And they said unto Joshua, We are thy servants. And Joshua said unto them, Who are ye? and from whence come ye?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e3cc0bd-0cfb-438c-b982-f85741c57223>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: JOS 9:9
Text: And they said unto him, From a very far country thy servants are come because of the name of the LORD thy God: for we have heard the fame of him, and all that he did in Egypt,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3340b140-5d18-4cc9-8e60-9610fe67d1bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: JOS 9:10
Text: And all that he did to the two kings of the Amorites, that were beyond Jordan, to Sihon king of Heshbon, and to Og king of Bashan, which was at Ashtaroth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66282830-89e7-483a-af82-a66f1b7484b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: JOS 9:11
Text: Wherefore our elders and all the inhabitants of our country spake to us, saying, Take victuals with you for the journey, and go to meet them, and say unto them, We are your servants: therefore now make ye a league with us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:413be271-b8ae-47cc-9e66-8ef62eae7864>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: JOS 9:12
Text: This our bread we took hot for our provision out of our houses on the day we came forth to go unto you; but now, behold, it is dry, and it is mouldy:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5df2993c-8ef0-4e66-9422-c443b630e1ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: JOS 9:13
Text: And these bottles of wine, which we filled, were new; and, behold, they be rent: and these our garments and our shoes are become old by reason of the very long journey.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e789c51-ff7e-4c7a-9e0a-f95014dcf538>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: JOS 9:14
Text: And the men took of their victuals, and asked not counsel at the mouth of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39139e0f-95f9-4414-8d56-a902609c2c8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: JOS 9:15
Text: And Joshua made peace with them, and made a league with them, to let them live: and the princes of the congregation sware unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10b77d9d-1448-4b1c-96d0-108e3d52a860>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: JOS 9:16
Text: And it came to pass at the end of three days after they had made a league with them, that they heard that they were their neighbours, and that they dwelt among them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96bed0c6-e45a-4cda-a311-bac6ff3d3b7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: JOS 9:17
Text: And the children of Israel journeyed, and came unto their cities on the third day. Now their cities were Gibeon, and Chephirah, and Beeroth, and Kirjathjearim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa5160da-98cc-423f-9075-1c0e94c4b0af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: JOS 9:18
Text: And the children of Israel smote them not, because the princes of the congregation had sworn unto them by the LORD God of Israel. And all the congregation murmured against the princes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8802f8c9-fba9-45db-8507-90e5dc2332d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: JOS 9:19
Text: But all the princes said unto all the congregation, We have sworn unto them by the LORD God of Israel: now therefore we may not touch them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92332703-6e96-4192-a81d-12057706ba37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: JOS 9:20
Text: This we will do to them; we will even let them live, lest wrath be upon us, because of the oath which we sware unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:037e5521-105a-4b0a-97d2-d7c17197bf3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: JOS 9:21
Text: And the princes said unto them, Let them live; but let them be hewers of wood and drawers of water unto all the congregation; as the princes had promised them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f34a8849-3bba-45c1-baa4-b08217adc7b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: JOS 9:22
Text: And Joshua called for them, and he spake unto them, saying, Wherefore have ye beguiled us, saying, We are very far from you; when ye dwell among us?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc51f1f0-8155-47bc-a317-6283b0932b81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: JOS 9:23
Text: Now therefore ye are cursed, and there shall none of you be freed from being bondmen, and hewers of wood and drawers of water for the house of my God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9d96113-a219-425b-a523-05a5aef7966c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 335

Reference: JOS 9:24
Text: And they answered Joshua, and said, Because it was certainly told thy servants, how that the LORD thy God commanded his servant Moses to give you all the land, and to destroy all the inhabitants of the land from before you, therefore we were sore afraid of our lives because of you, and have done this thing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fcdd581-ad0b-4674-bfd3-262adffdb3db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: JOS 9:25
Text: And now, behold, we are in thine hand: as it seemeth good and right unto thee to do unto us, do.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15713830-1b5e-436c-acbe-8a672b5c4277>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: JOS 9:26
Text: And so did he unto them, and delivered them out of the hand of the children of Israel, that they slew them not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/9/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52a3b9b0-3739-42f6-b03b-05e858d1d5af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: JOS 9:27
Text: And Joshua made them that day hewers of wood and drawers of water for the congregation, and for the altar of the LORD, even unto this day, in the place which he should choose.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee7177fc-5079-4ada-9af9-57bc11fe566d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 304

Reference: JOS 10:1
Text: Now it came to pass, when Adonizedec king of Jerusalem had heard how Joshua had taken Ai, and had utterly destroyed it; as he had done to Jericho and her king, so he had done to Ai and her king; and how the inhabitants of Gibeon had made peace with Israel, and were among them;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:898d9e5b-e0d9-410c-934a-dc3c6fa860bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: JOS 10:2
Text: That they feared greatly, because Gibeon was a great city, as one of the royal cities, and because it was greater than Ai, and all the men thereof were mighty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2286a8db-ac41-4455-8ab5-1d3c469d4a5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: JOS 10:3
Text: Wherefore Adonizedec king of Jerusalem, sent unto Hoham king of Hebron, and unto Piram king of Jarmuth, and unto Japhia king of Lachish, and unto Debir king of Eglon, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c3a40f5-aa0f-4eaf-a223-b27e775c9da7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: JOS 10:4
Text: Come up unto me, and help me, that we may smite Gibeon: for it hath made peace with Joshua and with the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4f353cb-e5c3-4ea6-812a-58ad29c0ab86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 294

Reference: JOS 10:5
Text: Therefore the five kings of the Amorites, the king of Jerusalem, the king of Hebron, the king of Jarmuth, the king of Lachish, the king of Eglon, gathered themselves together, and went up, they and all their hosts, and encamped before Gibeon, and made war against it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78dc1ede-24ec-4cf7-9156-96336e7dd527>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 279

Reference: JOS 10:6
Text: And the men of Gibeon sent unto Joshua to the camp to Gilgal, saying, Slack not thy hand from thy servants; come up to us quickly, and save us, and help us: for all the kings of the Amorites that dwell in the mountains are gathered together against us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b83a86bd-6554-4577-a7a7-b5c0a16d3baa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: JOS 10:7
Text: So Joshua ascended from Gilgal, he, and all the people of war with him, and all the mighty men of valour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30035a89-bd77-411b-87ec-78e529eb62b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: JOS 10:8
Text: And the LORD said unto Joshua, Fear them not: for I have delivered them into thine hand; there shall not a man of them stand before thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02c014e9-289b-4b89-8394-74c974d698d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: JOS 10:9
Text: Joshua therefore came unto them suddenly, and went up from Gilgal all night.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1970abbf-6c9e-4368-b415-02973e5ed9e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: JOS 10:10
Text: And the LORD discomfited them before Israel, and slew them with a great slaughter at Gibeon, and chased them along the way that goeth up to Bethhoron, and smote them to Azekah, and unto Makkedah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:159bf9b1-4589-4874-a0b1-fbab2bb87a63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 310

Reference: JOS 10:11
Text: And it came to pass, as they fled from before Israel, and were in the going down to Bethhoron, that the LORD cast down great stones from heaven upon them unto Azekah, and they died: they were more which died with hailstones than they whom the children of Israel slew with the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c5bdc8a-e56a-420c-8d03-a0adc7622b76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: JOS 10:12
Text: Then spake Joshua to the LORD in the day when the LORD delivered up the Amorites before the children of Israel, and he said in the sight of Israel, Sun, stand thou still upon Gibeon; and thou, Moon, in the valley of Ajalon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4dc19800-80f0-4fb9-84c8-66ad96303082>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: JOS 10:13
Text: And the sun stood still, and the moon stayed, until the people had avenged themselves upon their enemies. Is not this written in the book of Jasher? So the sun stood still in the midst of heaven, and hasted not to go down about a whole day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67ea4e4c-2518-4c5a-9512-30e63ade75ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: JOS 10:14
Text: And there was no day like that before it or after it, that the LORD hearkened unto the voice of a man: for the LORD fought for Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9fe1e27-5461-4d8f-839b-381d530ae180>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: JOS 10:15
Text: And Joshua returned, and all Israel with him, unto the camp to Gilgal.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2e5b4b1-8d27-404a-b2c1-1fdf906a80cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: JOS 10:16
Text: But these five kings fled, and hid themselves in a cave at Makkedah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:038d811f-6e5b-4cd1-902d-286438183f07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: JOS 10:17
Text: And it was told Joshua, saying, The five kings are found hid in a cave at Makkedah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8bba62ac-9de7-447f-ace3-cb6f1953bede>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: JOS 10:18
Text: And Joshua said, Roll great stones upon the mouth of the cave, and set men by it for to keep them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6acc0992-8963-44e7-89be-b80dec261820>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: JOS 10:19
Text: And stay ye not, but pursue after your enemies, and smite the hindmost of them; suffer them not to enter into their cities: for the LORD your God hath delivered them into your hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29bddd33-6b3a-4133-b869-f3f13ed00e00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: JOS 10:20
Text: And it came to pass, when Joshua and the children of Israel had made an end of slaying them with a very great slaughter, till they were consumed, that the rest which remained of them entered into fenced cities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e540020-eaea-4015-881f-852ba4380f91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: JOS 10:21
Text: And all the people returned to the camp to Joshua at Makkedah in peace: none moved his tongue against any of the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc2490af-6acd-4c28-8196-b87eeded2ad1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: JOS 10:22
Text: Then said Joshua, Open the mouth of the cave, and bring out those five kings unto me out of the cave.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:601947a9-1ee1-4271-8c94-99f6b046936c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: JOS 10:23
Text: And they did so, and brought forth those five kings unto him out of the cave, the king of Jerusalem, the king of Hebron, the king of Jarmuth, the king of Lachish, and the king of Eglon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a51f95ae-bdd0-4801-aece-3c63fe27fb88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 326

Reference: JOS 10:24
Text: And it came to pass, when they brought out those kings unto Joshua, that Joshua called for all the men of Israel, and said unto the captains of the men of war which went with him, Come near, put your feet upon the necks of these kings. And they came near, and put their feet upon the necks of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e88ad0c-1435-4bbc-b20f-9277fed1db6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JOS 10:25
Text: And Joshua said unto them, Fear not, nor be dismayed, be strong and of good courage: for thus shall the LORD do to all your enemies against whom ye fight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0851b5d3-8666-4029-b762-c54b9d2146df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: JOS 10:26
Text: And afterward Joshua smote them, and slew them, and hanged them on five trees: and they were hanging upon the trees until the evening.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f645dbf-511a-453c-8450-358c7e8cb385>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 285

Reference: JOS 10:27
Text: And it came to pass at the time of the going down of the sun, that Joshua commanded, and they took them down off the trees, and cast them into the cave wherein they had been hid, and laid great stones in the cave’s mouth, which remain until this very day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df7cc681-d858-4014-b635-3c17b58df882>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 280

Reference: JOS 10:28
Text: And that day Joshua took Makkedah, and smote it with the edge of the sword, and the king thereof he utterly destroyed, them, and all the souls that were therein; he let none remain: and he did to the king of Makkedah as he did unto the king of Jericho.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77feac87-ff6f-4a5f-b3d6-dd2e75b788c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: JOS 10:29
Text: Then Joshua passed from Makkedah, and all Israel with him, unto Libnah, and fought against Libnah:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93cf080d-499e-4d77-9298-78db995dfe7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 279

Reference: JOS 10:30
Text: And the LORD delivered it also, and the king thereof, into the hand of Israel; and he smote it with the edge of the sword, and all the souls that were therein; he let none remain in it; but did unto the king thereof as he did unto the king of Jericho.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfd466b9-a076-4c27-8560-151b4372d256>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: JOS 10:31
Text: And Joshua passed from Libnah, and all Israel with him, unto Lachish, and encamped against it, and fought against it:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6efc24e7-e8f6-4b97-befd-9311a690b357>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: JOS 10:32
Text: And the LORD delivered Lachish into the hand of Israel, which took it on the second day, and smote it with the edge of the sword, and all the souls that were therein, according to all that he had done to Libnah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:856eaef8-6e92-4d63-84b4-1d4f91bdb40d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: JOS 10:33
Text: Then Horam king of Gezer came up to help Lachish; and Joshua smote him and his people, until he had left him none remaining.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43b2536d-d748-4e63-8edf-1e10e37eb971>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: JOS 10:34
Text: And from Lachish Joshua passed unto Eglon, and all Israel with him; and they encamped against it, and fought against it:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6433d2e4-ac0f-496c-b990-e9eca6a731a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: JOS 10:35
Text: And they took it on that day, and smote it with the edge of the sword, and all the souls that were therein he utterly destroyed that day, according to all that he had done to Lachish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:286d0508-df0b-456a-89ae-2dad59ddd646>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: JOS 10:36
Text: And Joshua went up from Eglon, and all Israel with him, unto Hebron; and they fought against it:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:504bd488-8dc8-43d4-b4ac-f169a363097c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 304

Reference: JOS 10:37
Text: And they took it, and smote it with the edge of the sword, and the king thereof, and all the cities thereof, and all the souls that were therein; he left none remaining, according to all that he had done to Eglon; but destroyed it utterly, and all the souls that were therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:604a8e75-70d5-4ac6-8efe-ee021670dc5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: JOS 10:38
Text: And Joshua returned, and all Israel with him, to Debir; and fought against it:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca45bd47-2e89-4b51-99bc-debcf43d9f55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 339

Reference: JOS 10:39
Text: And he took it, and the king thereof, and all the cities thereof; and they smote them with the edge of the sword, and utterly destroyed all the souls that were therein; he left none remaining: as he had done to Hebron, so he did to Debir, and to the king thereof; as he had done also to Libnah, and to her king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ecd7ab1-e2a8-4e95-ba25-84c8bf8c99c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: JOS 10:40
Text: So Joshua smote all the country of the hills, and of the south, and of the vale, and of the springs, and all their kings: he left none remaining, but utterly destroyed all that breathed, as the LORD God of Israel commanded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97be0b35-6511-4a77-8e05-bfeab71e4e75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: JOS 10:41
Text: And Joshua smote them from Kadeshbarnea even unto Gaza, and all the country of Goshen, even unto Gibeon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03309497-e687-4c46-a0df-099684e98a6d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: JOS 10:42
Text: And all these kings and their land did Joshua take at one time, because the LORD God of Israel fought for Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/10/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71b699db-edcb-45dd-ac48-847c216b4427>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: JOS 10:43
Text: And Joshua returned, and all Israel with him, unto the camp to Gilgal.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/11/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a33ed87-1f35-4296-8588-e788015da2ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: JOS 11:1
Text: And it came to pass, when Jabin king of Hazor had heard those things, that he sent to Jobab king of Madon, and to the king of Shimron, and to the king of Achshaph,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/11/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b9b6ee5-3d1b-4c96-982f-fbe5ce81b5dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: JOS 11:2
Text: And to the kings that were on the north of the mountains, and of the plains south of Chinneroth, and in the valley, and in the borders of Dor on the west,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/11/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42195730-2073-4779-8fac-68dc661e7d59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: JOS 11:3
Text: And to the Canaanite on the east and on the west, and to the Amorite, and the Hittite, and the Perizzite, and the Jebusite in the mountains, and to the Hivite under Hermon in the land of Mizpeh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/11/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd633dcb-1656-407b-95fc-7dbde9c9b93b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: JOS 11:4
Text: And they went out, they and all their hosts with them, much people, even as the sand that is upon the sea shore in multitude, with horses and chariots very many.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/11/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d7cdc41-70f2-4efd-806a-515724f3a04d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: JOS 11:5
Text: And when all these kings were met together, they came and pitched together at the waters of Merom, to fight against Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/11/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:912164f6-0a0e-4320-a2f8-339ef26222ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: JOS 11:6
Text: And the LORD said unto Joshua, Be not afraid because of them: for to morrow about this time will I deliver them up all slain before Israel: thou shalt hough their horses, and burn their chariots with fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/11/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d05020a4-3400-4e1c-a8b9-19ae5720c037>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: JOS 11:7
Text: So Joshua came, and all the people of war with him, against them by the waters of Merom suddenly; and they fell upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/11/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52cebf84-2fbc-4219-93b6-1e3a22210ff7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: JOS 11:8
Text: And the LORD delivered them into the hand of Israel, who smote them, and chased them unto great Zidon, and unto Misrephothmaim, and unto the valley of Mizpeh eastward; and they smote them, until they left them none remaining.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/11/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7234f59-d7c7-4a40-afa9-2617cd0cb254>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: JOS 11:9
Text: And Joshua did unto them as the LORD bade him: he houghed their horses, and burnt their chariots with fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/11/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a6bd8a8-63c2-41db-ac95-516773b4c006>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: JOS 11:10
Text: And Joshua at that time turned back, and took Hazor, and smote the king thereof with the sword: for Hazor beforetime was the head of all those kingdoms.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/11/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:670ab988-5bef-476d-97ec-5f8de8b3e69b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: JOS 11:11
Text: And they smote all the souls that were therein with the edge of the sword, utterly destroying them: there was not any left to breathe: and he burnt Hazor with fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/11/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ed3d167-dd4b-4018-89e0-9314522d39d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: JOS 11:12
Text: And all the cities of those kings, and all the kings of them, did Joshua take, and smote them with the edge of the sword, and he utterly destroyed them, as Moses the servant of the LORD commanded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/11/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38463253-df7e-4366-aeef-f53c2901ff92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: JOS 11:13
Text: But as for the cities that stood still in their strength, Israel burned none of them, save Hazor only; that did Joshua burn.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/11/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7cfc915e-cf88-47fb-aa6c-385b28bc8ca1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: JOS 11:14
Text: And all the spoil of these cities, and the cattle, the children of Israel took for a prey unto themselves; but every man they smote with the edge of the sword, until they had destroyed them, neither left they any to breathe.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/11/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bff60209-9f9d-4259-8535-a2a68ee5e0e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: JOS 11:15
Text: As the LORD commanded Moses his servant, so did Moses command Joshua, and so did Joshua; he left nothing undone of all that the LORD commanded Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/11/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2eddbc66-2c45-4150-8f26-d8ea3ec9b846>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: JOS 11:16
Text: So Joshua took all that land, the hills, and all the south country, and all the land of Goshen, and the valley, and the plain, and the mountain of Israel, and the valley of the same;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/11/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ab9d68c-31aa-4e56-a0b3-20f32d1a2888>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: JOS 11:17
Text: Even from the mount Halak, that goeth up to Seir, even unto Baalgad in the valley of Lebanon under mount Hermon: and all their kings he took, and smote them, and slew them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/11/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f04fe11e-b33d-4d7e-95dc-4eceb9a8e5ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: JOS 11:18
Text: Joshua made war a long time with all those kings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/11/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1c8045e-ff44-492d-8261-2aed9af848ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: JOS 11:19
Text: There was not a city that made peace with the children of Israel, save the Hivites the inhabitants of Gibeon: all other they took in battle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/11/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5732218-f7ed-43f7-a2a8-b6826e337cf5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: JOS 11:20
Text: For it was of the LORD to harden their hearts, that they should come against Israel in battle, that he might destroy them utterly, and that they might have no favour, but that he might destroy them, as the LORD commanded Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/11/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f64f150-70a6-453e-8e4b-6b4e9f483db5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: JOS 11:21
Text: And at that time came Joshua, and cut off the Anakims from the mountains, from Hebron, from Debir, from Anab, and from all the mountains of Judah, and from all the mountains of Israel: Joshua destroyed them utterly with their cities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/11/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34690c1b-a624-4810-8754-d9264542b040>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: JOS 11:22
Text: There was none of the Anakims left in the land of the children of Israel: only in Gaza, in Gath, and in Ashdod, there remained.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/11/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50fc5410-c888-4afc-a679-8a0ee017a5b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: JOS 11:23
Text: So Joshua took the whole land, according to all that the LORD said unto Moses; and Joshua gave it for an inheritance unto Israel according to their divisions by their tribes. And the land rested from war.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/12/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a43de917-fe50-46dd-8ada-cfc926e7291c>
Content-Type: text/plain
