WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/13/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd10a863-4b1d-456c-bebd-cd7b7b230924>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: JOS 13:29
Text: And Moses gave inheritance unto the half tribe of Manasseh: and this was the possession of the half tribe of the children of Manasseh by their families.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/13/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:831786fc-7b9e-4918-ae92-f525d74054f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: JOS 13:30
Text: And their coast was from Mahanaim, all Bashan, all the kingdom of Og king of Bashan, and all the towns of Jair, which are in Bashan, threescore cities:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/13/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a4cfc4f-703a-4252-8f73-14ffafad1dbf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: JOS 13:31
Text: And half Gilead, and Ashtaroth, and Edrei, cities of the kingdom of Og in Bashan, were pertaining unto the children of Machir the son of Manasseh, even to the one half of the children of Machir by their families.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/13/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a11d12e-1fa5-454b-9e48-ccb48a8e4f9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: JOS 13:32
Text: These are the countries which Moses did distribute for inheritance in the plains of Moab, on the other side Jordan, by Jericho, eastward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/13/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:477e4bfc-93a6-400b-be23-dc64d69680ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: JOS 13:33
Text: But unto the tribe of Levi Moses gave not any inheritance: the LORD God of Israel was their inheritance, as he said unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/14/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6e10f9f-a281-43be-bc6b-d900ff01f574>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: JOS 14:1
Text: And these are the countries which the children of Israel inherited in the land of Canaan, which Eleazar the priest, and Joshua the son of Nun, and the heads of the fathers of the tribes of the children of Israel, distributed for inheritance to them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/14/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e20928e1-313a-4353-bc27-5869975ff7d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: JOS 14:2
Text: By lot was their inheritance, as the LORD commanded by the hand of Moses, for the nine tribes, and for the half tribe.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/14/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03e4574c-789a-4ed7-a9f2-876de7bab80d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: JOS 14:3
Text: For Moses had given the inheritance of two tribes and an half tribe on the other side Jordan: but unto the Levites he gave none inheritance among them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/14/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:999692b9-a2e7-48cb-b330-1ba635afa8bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: JOS 14:4
Text: For the children of Joseph were two tribes, Manasseh and Ephraim: therefore they gave no part unto the Levites in the land, save cities to dwell in, with their suburbs for their cattle and for their substance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/14/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f21acf4-b8e9-4d87-82ff-f85fd5bade99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: JOS 14:5
Text: As the LORD commanded Moses, so the children of Israel did, and they divided the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/14/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c4a0b71-8244-4df1-ae9f-f679d196ab0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: JOS 14:6
Text: Then the children of Judah came unto Joshua in Gilgal: and Caleb the son of Jephunneh the Kenezite said unto him, Thou knowest the thing that the LORD said unto Moses the man of God concerning me and thee in Kadeshbarnea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/14/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b006323-267c-4967-aa2e-bbfe2d9d41a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JOS 14:7
Text: Forty years old was I when Moses the servant of the LORD sent me from Kadeshbarnea to espy out the land; and I brought him word again as it was in mine heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/14/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af833bea-ed2b-43a8-9675-23172afe46d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: JOS 14:8
Text: Nevertheless my brethren that went up with me made the heart of the people melt: but I wholly followed the LORD my God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/14/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82a71142-97ea-4a85-b50f-af8b5087eb3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: JOS 14:9
Text: And Moses sware on that day, saying, Surely the land whereon thy feet have trodden shall be thine inheritance, and thy children’s for ever, because thou hast wholly followed the LORD my God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/14/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c03569fe-d75f-45a1-83ab-40f6e578c275>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: JOS 14:10
Text: And now, behold, the LORD hath kept me alive, as he said, these forty and five years, even since the LORD spake this word unto Moses, while the children of Israel wandered in the wilderness: and now, lo, I am this day fourscore and five years old.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/14/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfee7735-d0f1-4283-bf01-4349536933be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: JOS 14:11
Text: As yet I am as strong this day as I was in the day that Moses sent me: as my strength was then, even so is my strength now, for war, both to go out, and to come in.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/14/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9e4e89c-c26c-43d0-8ed7-01967812f93d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 294

Reference: JOS 14:12
Text: Now therefore give me this mountain, whereof the LORD spake in that day; for thou heardest in that day how the Anakims were there, and that the cities were great and fenced: if so be the LORD will be with me, then I shall be able to drive them out, as the LORD said.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/14/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7bf67d9f-e84b-4362-b238-6657817fcf3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: JOS 14:13
Text: And Joshua blessed him, and gave unto Caleb the son of Jephunneh Hebron for an inheritance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/14/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e2991af-fac1-462a-89d5-7f68bf053974>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: JOS 14:14
Text: Hebron therefore became the inheritance of Caleb the son of Jephunneh the Kenezite unto this day, because that he wholly followed the LORD God of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/14/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46167604-68ce-477f-92a5-5dc5de8083f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: JOS 14:15
Text: And the name of Hebron before was Kirjatharba; which Arba was a great man among the Anakims. And the land had rest from war.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/15/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71e432c1-eced-495f-a230-cda17ffdeaa5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: JOS 15:1
Text: This then was the lot of the tribe of the children of Judah by their families; even to the border of Edom the wilderness of Zin southward was the uttermost part of the south coast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/15/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
