Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: JOS 16:10
Text: And they drave not out the Canaanites that dwelt in Gezer: but the Canaanites dwell among the Ephraimites unto this day, and serve under tribute.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/17/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76d17e3a-c27d-47bc-8207-6eff13c43804>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: JOS 17:1
Text: There was also a lot for the tribe of Manasseh; for he was the firstborn of Joseph; to wit, for Machir the firstborn of Manasseh, the father of Gilead: because he was a man of war, therefore he had Gilead and Bashan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/17/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd4354cc-fc61-45ed-a134-a1fe44a3cc45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 375

Reference: JOS 17:2
Text: There was also a lot for the rest of the children of Manasseh by their families; for the children of Abiezer, and for the children of Helek, and for the children of Asriel, and for the children of Shechem, and for the children of Hepher, and for the children of Shemida: these were the male children of Manasseh the son of Joseph by their families.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/17/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ed77553-ba0f-4eab-96d3-a4583a0eacb9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: JOS 17:3
Text: But Zelophehad, the son of Hepher, the son of Gilead, the son of Machir, the son of Manasseh, had no sons, but daughters: and these are the names of his daughters, Mahlah, and Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/17/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c8a62a1-5662-43a4-bf49-6b65dfe8aba1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 324

Reference: JOS 17:4
Text: And they came near before Eleazar the priest, and before Joshua the son of Nun, and before the princes, saying, The LORD commanded Moses to give us an inheritance among our brethren. Therefore according to the commandment of the LORD he gave them an inheritance among the brethren of their father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/17/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:282bc0de-14f6-4b9f-9360-4ba6f187aaa0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: JOS 17:5
Text: And there fell ten portions to Manasseh, beside the land of Gilead and Bashan, which were on the other side Jordan;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/17/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:123254fa-b29c-44d1-bdff-f8619b5eae3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: JOS 17:6
Text: Because the daughters of Manasseh had an inheritance among his sons: and the rest of Manasseh’s sons had the land of Gilead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/17/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ace9d63e-98e5-4aad-8427-7e02a271c3ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: JOS 17:7
Text: And the coast of Manasseh was from Asher to Michmethah, that lieth before Shechem; and the border went along on the right hand unto the inhabitants of Entappuah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/17/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8173c141-18cc-45f1-ad67-87a0f4fd6700>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: JOS 17:8
Text: Now Manasseh had the land of Tappuah: but Tappuah on the border of Manasseh belonged to the children of Ephraim;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/17/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7cf33e28-4474-44c4-a932-cf92f77604fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: JOS 17:9
Text: And the coast descended unto the river Kanah, southward of the river: these cities of Ephraim are among the cities of Manasseh: the coast of Manasseh also was on the north side of the river, and the outgoings of it were at the sea:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/17/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:550ea812-4540-4351-9f09-45bdeb79fb84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: JOS 17:10
Text: Southward it was Ephraim’s, and northward it was Manasseh’s, and the sea is his border; and they met together in Asher on the north, and in Issachar on the east.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/17/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4c8fb84-f4f5-48e3-aa98-c0b40500f037>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 320

Reference: JOS 17:11
Text: And Manasseh had in Issachar and in Asher Bethshean and her towns, and Ibleam and her towns, and the inhabitants of Dor and her towns, and the inhabitants of Endor and her towns, and the inhabitants of Taanach and her towns, and the inhabitants of Megiddo and her towns, even three countries.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/17/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f35ea1a-0eed-4f7e-be7f-39c7ea2ebbb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: JOS 17:12
Text: Yet the children of Manasseh could not drive out the inhabitants of those cities; but the Canaanites would dwell in that land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/17/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71c9bafc-30ea-4999-9938-fbbdc3fd794e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: JOS 17:13
Text: Yet it came to pass, when the children of Israel were waxen strong, that they put the Canaanites to tribute, but did not utterly drive them out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/17/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3410b55-2bc7-4c98-9d03-221a87608b75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: JOS 17:14
Text: And the children of Joseph spake unto Joshua, saying, Why hast thou given me but one lot and one portion to inherit, seeing I am a great people, forasmuch as the LORD hath blessed me hitherto?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/17/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a418f5c2-b964-4b52-8240-4481a5d00aeb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: JOS 17:15
Text: And Joshua answered them, If thou be a great people, then get thee up to the wood country, and cut down for thyself there in the land of the Perizzites and of the giants, if mount Ephraim be too narrow for thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/17/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49df4b00-2a81-4595-8176-7a18163bd957>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: JOS 17:16
Text: And the children of Joseph said, The hill is not enough for us: and all the Canaanites that dwell in the land of the valley have chariots of iron, both they who are of Bethshean and her towns, and they who are of the valley of Jezreel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/17/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c98c25f8-37d0-4824-8900-426d5d7469e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: JOS 17:17
Text: And Joshua spake unto the house of Joseph, even to Ephraim and to Manasseh, saying, Thou art a great people, and hast great power: thou shalt not have one lot only:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/17/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb58c060-150d-499b-801e-d05d7b767f92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: JOS 17:18
Text: But the mountain shall be thine; for it is a wood, and thou shalt cut it down: and the outgoings of it shall be thine: for thou shalt drive out the Canaanites, though they have iron chariots, and though they be strong.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/18/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24fa8cd5-8225-4eb4-bd40-1adbda60d797>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: JOS 18:1
Text: And the whole congregation of the children of Israel assembled together at Shiloh, and set up the tabernacle of the congregation there. And the land was subdued before them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/18/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e86fcab-1016-460b-80e6-f9ef8e4c1895>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: JOS 18:2
Text: And there remained among the children of Israel seven tribes, which had not yet received their inheritance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/18/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73a1c121-73ea-4692-8849-5fdddfde694d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: JOS 18:3
Text: And Joshua said unto the children of Israel, How long are ye slack to go to possess the land, which the LORD God of your fathers hath given you?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/18/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b154bd80-996c-4a71-87de-77441f4c54d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: JOS 18:4
Text: Give out from among you three men for each tribe: and I will send them, and they shall rise, and go through the land, and describe it according to the inheritance of them; and they shall come again to me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/18/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5fd4f23f-b369-41d5-9482-bff72911a2c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JOS 18:5
Text: And they shall divide it into seven parts: Judah shall abide in their coast on the south, and the house of Joseph shall abide in their coasts on the north.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/18/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a7cf806-9785-468b-a585-851523c92600>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: JOS 18:6
Text: Ye shall therefore describe the land into seven parts, and bring the description hither to me, that I may cast lots for you here before the LORD our God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/18/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d00c115f-a927-433f-b50b-45bb6e4d3456>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 278

Reference: JOS 18:7
Text: But the Levites have no part among you; for the priesthood of the LORD is their inheritance: and Gad, and Reuben, and half the tribe of Manasseh, have received their inheritance beyond Jordan on the east, which Moses the servant of the LORD gave them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/18/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0deafaa-8846-4e5a-89db-b455d45d97f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: JOS 18:8
Text: And the men arose, and went away: and Joshua charged them that went to describe the land, saying, Go and walk through the land, and describe it, and come again to me, that I may here cast lots for you before the LORD in Shiloh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/18/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df14dd2e-77df-4727-942d-e005b3af0a98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: JOS 18:9
Text: And the men went and passed through the land, and described it by cities into seven parts in a book, and came again to Joshua to the host at Shiloh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/18/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
