Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 335

Reference: JOS 19:51
Text: These are the inheritances, which Eleazar the priest, and Joshua the son of Nun, and the heads of the fathers of the tribes of the children of Israel, divided for an inheritance by lot in Shiloh before the LORD, at the door of the tabernacle of the congregation. So they made an end of dividing the country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/20/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7aabd681-16c7-4737-b962-d3dcd96c356e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 67

Reference: JOS 20:1
Text: The LORD also spake unto Joshua, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/20/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81d12f73-6bd0-49a2-956c-d77fddd19f12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: JOS 20:2
Text: Speak to the children of Israel, saying, Appoint out for you cities of refuge, whereof I spake unto you by the hand of Moses:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/20/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a95c79e8-ac30-4c2e-8be2-48f8902d4bf0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: JOS 20:3
Text: That the slayer that killeth any person unawares and unwittingly may flee thither: and they shall be your refuge from the avenger of blood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/20/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8830ec93-5860-498f-a265-1e58e9fbe509>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 296

Reference: JOS 20:4
Text: And when he that doth flee unto one of those cities shall stand at the entering of the gate of the city, and shall declare his cause in the ears of the elders of that city, they shall take him into the city unto them, and give him a place, that he may dwell among them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/20/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1ff71a6-5a92-47a2-b2e2-de43ef4b7daa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: JOS 20:5
Text: And if the avenger of blood pursue after him, then they shall not deliver the slayer up into his hand; because he smote his neighbour unwittingly, and hated him not beforetime.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/20/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21664a51-2f3d-4454-ac0f-aff8eda4513b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 297

Reference: JOS 20:6
Text: And he shall dwell in that city, until he stand before the congregation for judgment, and until the death of the high priest that shall be in those days: then shall the slayer return, and come unto his own city, and unto his own house, unto the city from whence he fled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/20/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59130eb1-c34e-4f05-952c-2c13cb570837>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: JOS 20:7
Text: And they appointed Kedesh in Galilee in mount Naphtali, and Shechem in mount Ephraim, and Kirjatharba, which is Hebron, in the mountain of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/20/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72cf7767-df85-45db-a340-9b7250730ade>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: JOS 20:8
Text: And on the other side Jordan by Jericho eastward, they assigned Bezer in the wilderness upon the plain out of the tribe of Reuben, and Ramoth in Gilead out of the tribe of Gad, and Golan in Bashan out of the tribe of Manasseh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/20/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:790544ee-06ac-4527-85cf-b48d481edb75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 294

Reference: JOS 20:9
Text: These were the cities appointed for all the children of Israel, and for the stranger that sojourneth among them, that whosoever killeth any person at unawares might flee thither, and not die by the hand of the avenger of blood, until he stood before the congregation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/21/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3707064b-7218-465a-9be1-e8003334d255>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: JOS 21:1
Text: Then came near the heads of the fathers of the Levites unto Eleazar the priest, and unto Joshua the son of Nun, and unto the heads of the fathers of the tribes of the children of Israel;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/21/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d3b2377-ff81-42e3-9a9d-249675466b27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: JOS 21:2
Text: And they spake unto them at Shiloh in the land of Canaan, saying, The LORD commanded by the hand of Moses to give us cities to dwell in, with the suburbs thereof for our cattle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/21/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
