Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: JOS 22:1
Text: Then Joshua called the Reubenites, and the Gadites, and the half tribe of Manasseh,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:989ba0d8-eb88-4d70-9d4a-6b7bb53d2607>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: JOS 22:2
Text: And said unto them, Ye have kept all that Moses the servant of the LORD commanded you, and have obeyed my voice in all that I commanded you:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7cae273d-1fcb-4152-96ed-a199d0fbcd37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: JOS 22:3
Text: Ye have not left your brethren these many days unto this day, but have kept the charge of the commandment of the LORD your God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55f58c53-1cd4-44ed-9605-6d16f23a6eaf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: JOS 22:4
Text: And now the LORD your God hath given rest unto your brethren, as he promised them: therefore now return ye, and get you unto your tents, and unto the land of your possession, which Moses the servant of the LORD gave you on the other side Jordan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e246139-e835-4d15-88a7-6eab0c1a06d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 304

Reference: JOS 22:5
Text: But take diligent heed to do the commandment and the law, which Moses the servant of the LORD charged you, to love the LORD your God, and to walk in all his ways, and to keep his commandments, and to cleave unto him, and to serve him with all your heart and with all your soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b56296f-d408-4c7e-84e1-ee37993d98de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: JOS 22:6
Text: So Joshua blessed them, and sent them away: and they went unto their tents.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae0b1498-f8c3-4cf0-9a22-e71e5bf1b8d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 280

Reference: JOS 22:7
Text: Now to the one half of the tribe of Manasseh Moses had given possession in Bashan: but unto the other half thereof gave Joshua among their brethren on this side Jordan westward. And when Joshua sent them away also unto their tents, then he blessed them,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e6cdd9b-d8a7-46a6-8d69-212aefad4166>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 266

Reference: JOS 22:8
Text: And he spake unto them, saying, Return with much riches unto your tents, and with very much cattle, with silver, and with gold, and with brass, and with iron, and with very much raiment: divide the spoil of your enemies with your brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f883323-2d08-4746-9deb-2b9667cd3b75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 358

Reference: JOS 22:9
Text: And the children of Reuben and the children of Gad and the half tribe of Manasseh returned, and departed from the children of Israel out of Shiloh, which is in the land of Canaan, to go unto the country of Gilead, to the land of their possession, whereof they were possessed, according to the word of the LORD by the hand of Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9dc7924-81ce-4d8c-8878-1eec8ef5cbac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: JOS 22:10
Text: And when they came unto the borders of Jordan, that are in the land of Canaan, the children of Reuben and the children of Gad and the half tribe of Manasseh built there an altar by Jordan, a great altar to see to.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94bb2641-e2cc-48bc-99b7-d265ecd76898>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: JOS 22:11
Text: And the children of Israel heard say, Behold, the children of Reuben and the children of Gad and the half tribe of Manasseh have built an altar over against the land of Canaan, in the borders of Jordan, at the passage of the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2663bed-9e19-41f3-8150-a293989cbc0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: JOS 22:12
Text: And when the children of Israel heard of it, the whole congregation of the children of Israel gathered themselves together at Shiloh, to go up to war against them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd1ce0ad-6e76-4610-96a3-acf16f4815e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: JOS 22:13
Text: And the children of Israel sent unto the children of Reuben, and to the children of Gad, and to the half tribe of Manasseh, into the land of Gilead, Phinehas the son of Eleazar the priest,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8658f144-6438-4d95-9533-68cd31d3f994>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: JOS 22:14
Text: And with him ten princes, of each chief house a prince throughout all the tribes of Israel; and each one was an head of the house of their fathers among the thousands of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d040a380-da1d-4a5c-8040-819cd2b61f80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: JOS 22:15
Text: And they came unto the children of Reuben, and to the children of Gad, and to the half tribe of Manasseh, unto the land of Gilead, and they spake with them, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8d3fb3c-8d80-4cb6-b850-5290c6fcf7e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 278

Reference: JOS 22:16
Text: Thus saith the whole congregation of the LORD, What trespass is this that ye have committed against the God of Israel, to turn away this day from following the LORD, in that ye have builded you an altar, that ye might rebel this day against the LORD?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:742169f5-5d05-4ff6-ba1a-c145259cf5e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: JOS 22:17
Text: Is the iniquity of Peor too little for us, from which we are not cleansed until this day, although there was a plague in the congregation of the LORD,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a6f585e-7baa-4e57-a873-957bfce3e474>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: JOS 22:18
Text: But that ye must turn away this day from following the LORD? and it will be, seeing ye rebel to day against the LORD, that to morrow he will be wroth with the whole congregation of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b163cbfc-803c-45cd-a8b4-ee59ef8b3d27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 339

Reference: JOS 22:19
Text: Notwithstanding, if the land of your possession be unclean, then pass ye over unto the land of the possession of the LORD, wherein the LORD’s tabernacle dwelleth, and take possession among us: but rebel not against the LORD, nor rebel against us, in building you an altar beside the altar of the LORD our God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edd0f186-fe96-4d95-b5c7-9002d26b8c3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: JOS 22:20
Text: Did not Achan the son of Zerah commit a trespass in the accursed thing, and wrath fell on all the congregation of Israel? and that man perished not alone in his iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4dd281a6-2117-4857-8497-b5e862c46871>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: JOS 22:21
Text: Then the children of Reuben and the children of Gad and the half tribe of Manasseh answered, and said unto the heads of the thousands of Israel,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:849d0753-1c15-406d-a309-bad9fae909d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: JOS 22:22
Text: The LORD God of gods, the LORD God of gods, he knoweth, and Israel he shall know; if it be in rebellion, or if in transgression against the LORD, (save us not this day,)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59681544-a3ec-4e15-96ca-d7ff95d8f179>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: JOS 22:23
Text: That we have built us an altar to turn from following the LORD, or if to offer thereon burnt offering or meat offering, or if to offer peace offerings thereon, let the LORD himself require it;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1631758-30cf-47c9-9870-d2d1edfcb861>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: JOS 22:24
Text: And if we have not rather done it for fear of this thing, saying, In time to come your children might speak unto our children, saying, What have ye to do with the LORD God of Israel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8fb78751-cc80-455f-a48b-835fc9628b7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: JOS 22:25
Text: For the LORD hath made Jordan a border between us and you, ye children of Reuben and children of Gad; ye have no part in the LORD: so shall your children make our children cease from fearing the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0dd60c51-e09e-4734-87d7-cc708389afb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: JOS 22:26
Text: Therefore we said, Let us now prepare to build us an altar, not for burnt offering, nor for sacrifice:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee820289-98b0-414d-97aa-4ef54ec1765f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 333

Reference: JOS 22:27
Text: But that it may be a witness between us, and you, and our generations after us, that we might do the service of the LORD before him with our burnt offerings, and with our sacrifices, and with our peace offerings; that your children may not say to our children in time to come, Ye have no part in the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4eaa81e7-8212-4795-90ce-94fd2dcff4b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 310

Reference: JOS 22:28
Text: Therefore said we, that it shall be, when they should so say to us or to our generations in time to come, that we may say again, Behold the pattern of the altar of the LORD, which our fathers made, not for burnt offerings, nor for sacrifices; but it is a witness between us and you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a96c3d09-0351-461b-a05e-50c793f12906>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 266

Reference: JOS 22:29
Text: God forbid that we should rebel against the LORD, and turn this day from following the LORD, to build an altar for burnt offerings, for meat offerings, or for sacrifices, beside the altar of the LORD our God that is before his tabernacle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95bc1ee8-2d82-46f4-9a68-ac6aff8efecb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: JOS 22:30
Text: And when Phinehas the priest, and the princes of the congregation and heads of the thousands of Israel which were with him, heard the words that the children of Reuben and the children of Gad and the children of Manasseh spake, it pleased them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7b65687-dc5e-49a8-9c7e-bee7377094d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 349

Reference: JOS 22:31
Text: And Phinehas the son of Eleazar the priest said unto the children of Reuben, and to the children of Gad, and to the children of Manasseh, This day we perceive that the LORD is among us, because ye have not committed this trespass against the LORD: now ye have delivered the children of Israel out of the hand of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42961dad-d535-47e1-99d6-043379bf5f0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: JOS 22:32
Text: And Phinehas the son of Eleazar the priest, and the princes, returned from the children of Reuben, and from the children of Gad, out of the land of Gilead, unto the land of Canaan, to the children of Israel, and brought them word again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7054f202-7d5c-40a5-bb0c-f3743945e602>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: JOS 22:33
Text: And the thing pleased the children of Israel; and the children of Israel blessed God, and did not intend to go up against them in battle, to destroy the land wherein the children of Reuben and Gad dwelt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/22/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f34e725f-cf7c-4656-8d9f-e0235312cfcd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: JOS 22:34
Text: And the children of Reuben and the children of Gad called the altar Ed: for it shall be a witness between us that the LORD is God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/23/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47342f41-4e09-4630-8b35-22b70307429c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: JOS 23:1
Text: And it came to pass a long time after that the LORD had given rest unto Israel from all their enemies round about, that Joshua waxed old and stricken in age.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/23/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:852b28bc-a869-41ca-98df-d69fac60fd8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: JOS 23:2
Text: And Joshua called for all Israel, and for their elders, and for their heads, and for their judges, and for their officers, and said unto them, I am old and stricken in age:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/23/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3bd2e91a-89d4-4392-929f-1e80a872eb9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: JOS 23:3
Text: And ye have seen all that the LORD your God hath done unto all these nations because of you; for the LORD your God is he that hath fought for you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/23/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bda2f35-88a4-4457-9dfe-e23bc8a956d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: JOS 23:4
Text: Behold, I have divided unto you by lot these nations that remain, to be an inheritance for your tribes, from Jordan, with all the nations that I have cut off, even unto the great sea westward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/23/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:652c58fb-dea3-4b81-8bcc-41b4442c8342>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: JOS 23:5
Text: And the LORD your God, he shall expel them from before you, and drive them from out of your sight; and ye shall possess their land, as the LORD your God hath promised unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/23/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a87ab47b-c7d6-4eb0-8d77-941e325ed1e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: JOS 23:6
Text: Be ye therefore very courageous to keep and to do all that is written in the book of the law of Moses, that ye turn not aside therefrom to the right hand or to the left;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/23/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c58232d-ac37-466a-b0f3-eb37f9601c1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: JOS 23:7
Text: That ye come not among these nations, these that remain among you; neither make mention of the name of their gods, nor cause to swear by them, neither serve them, nor bow yourselves unto them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/23/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7737c3c3-2324-4520-99da-538d24214406>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: JOS 23:8
Text: But cleave unto the LORD your God, as ye have done unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/23/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f897a5a-1149-492f-87d5-6865fc5b236c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: JOS 23:9
Text: For the LORD hath driven out from before you great nations and strong: but as for you, no man hath been able to stand before you unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/23/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99d0c274-409a-48a9-b6b2-4b43f8d6dc8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: JOS 23:10
Text: One man of you shall chase a thousand: for the LORD your God, he it is that fighteth for you, as he hath promised you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/23/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d197e3cd-02b0-4a97-838e-951a8f6fb8a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: JOS 23:11
Text: Take good heed therefore unto yourselves, that ye love the LORD your God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/23/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4975263-5b3e-4454-8905-aaa18e8b92f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: JOS 23:12
Text: Else if ye do in any wise go back, and cleave unto the remnant of these nations, even these that remain among you, and shall make marriages with them, and go in unto them, and they to you:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/23/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e047c1cb-e04d-46fb-9fe0-cbd49f78774d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 310

Reference: JOS 23:13
Text: Know for a certainty that the LORD your God will no more drive out any of these nations from before you; but they shall be snares and traps unto you, and scourges in your sides, and thorns in your eyes, until ye perish from off this good land which the LORD your God hath given you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/23/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf7de4ea-f07e-46df-bfa9-4985093105e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 310

Reference: JOS 23:14
Text: And, behold, this day I am going the way of all the earth: and ye know in all your hearts and in all your souls, that not one thing hath failed of all the good things which the LORD your God spake concerning you; all are come to pass unto you, and not one thing hath failed thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/23/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d4880dc-fb5f-44db-8eeb-a230265fb028>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 283

Reference: JOS 23:15
Text: Therefore it shall come to pass, that as all good things are come upon you, which the LORD your God promised you; so shall the LORD bring upon you all evil things, until he have destroyed you from off this good land which the LORD your God hath given you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/23/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbfcbf4c-3971-4cd2-b955-b2eb7abd22fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 317

Reference: JOS 23:16
Text: When ye have transgressed the covenant of the LORD your God, which he commanded you, and have gone and served other gods, and bowed yourselves to them; then shall the anger of the LORD be kindled against you, and ye shall perish quickly from off the good land which he hath given unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5352dc9-bffa-43e6-97de-467ae8dbae9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: JOS 24:1
Text: And Joshua gathered all the tribes of Israel to Shechem, and called for the elders of Israel, and for their heads, and for their judges, and for their officers; and they presented themselves before God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2f9ae42-af28-482d-a7e8-e1fe4029ff42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: JOS 24:2
Text: And Joshua said unto all the people, Thus saith the LORD God of Israel, Your fathers dwelt on the other side of the flood in old time, even Terah, the father of Abraham, and the father of Nachor: and they served other gods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16d90eee-601d-4203-9d6f-b8c2e2b8e6b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: JOS 24:3
Text: And I took your father Abraham from the other side of the flood, and led him throughout all the land of Canaan, and multiplied his seed, and gave him Isaac.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb368f25-2662-4bd5-91c6-211084763b38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: JOS 24:4
Text: And I gave unto Isaac Jacob and Esau: and I gave unto Esau mount Seir, to possess it; but Jacob and his children went down into Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3794fc7-9225-4fef-97d4-658d4191299f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: JOS 24:5
Text: I sent Moses also and Aaron, and I plagued Egypt, according to that which I did among them: and afterward I brought you out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c4c6561-9790-4f22-930a-89abd68ad2a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: JOS 24:6
Text: And I brought your fathers out of Egypt: and ye came unto the sea; and the Egyptians pursued after your fathers with chariots and horsemen unto the Red sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a8f749c-9ada-4044-b759-3e1a2b43327c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: JOS 24:7
Text: And when they cried unto the LORD, he put darkness between you and the Egyptians, and brought the sea upon them, and covered them; and your eyes have seen what I have done in Egypt: and ye dwelt in the wilderness a long season.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:331a2968-ac3d-4a3d-9879-5a34bc6f7cad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: JOS 24:8
Text: And I brought you into the land of the Amorites, which dwelt on the other side Jordan; and they fought with you: and I gave them into your hand, that ye might possess their land; and I destroyed them from before you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3dfa53f-4fda-402e-8e30-a303e0a02cd2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: JOS 24:9
Text: Then Balak the son of Zippor, king of Moab, arose and warred against Israel, and sent and called Balaam the son of Beor to curse you:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01802933-93c1-4338-a7e3-b2f3ae623382>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: JOS 24:10
Text: But I would not hearken unto Balaam; therefore he blessed you still: so I delivered you out of his hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c861053-67ca-4511-96be-295935f16325>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 281

Reference: JOS 24:11
Text: And you went over Jordan, and came unto Jericho: and the men of Jericho fought against you, the Amorites, and the Perizzites, and the Canaanites, and the Hittites, and the Girgashites, the Hivites, and the Jebusites; and I delivered them into your hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d49ba43-862f-4c1c-afa0-e0e9dbe2c36a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: JOS 24:12
Text: And I sent the hornet before you, which drave them out from before you, even the two kings of the Amorites; but not with thy sword, nor with thy bow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37d3e437-f08e-4c47-8bc4-639e13e85bb9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: JOS 24:13
Text: And I have given you a land for which ye did not labour, and cities which ye built not, and ye dwell in them; of the vineyards and oliveyards which ye planted not do ye eat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:792fa17f-4619-4d12-a77b-df4542dd6ad6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: JOS 24:14
Text: Now therefore fear the LORD, and serve him in sincerity and in truth: and put away the gods which your fathers served on the other side of the flood, and in Egypt; and serve ye the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05787ddd-bb5e-4530-9f1d-9526b3a5908a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 305

Reference: JOS 24:15
Text: And if it seem evil unto you to serve the LORD, choose you this day whom ye will serve; whether the gods which your fathers served that were on the other side of the flood, or the gods of the Amorites, in whose land ye dwell: but as for me and my house, we will serve the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1915d82-7eca-4e49-8822-6bed62924f63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: JOS 24:16
Text: And the people answered and said, God forbid that we should forsake the LORD, to serve other gods;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5be3455-b4e2-4985-9c5f-5379ba37da92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 290

Reference: JOS 24:17
Text: For the LORD our God, he it is that brought us up and our fathers out of the land of Egypt, from the house of bondage, and which did those great signs in our sight, and preserved us in all the way wherein we went, and among all the people through whom we passed:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3116637d-26c3-4f45-a55f-8f80a0d7d6b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JOS 24:18
Text: And the LORD drave out from before us all the people, even the Amorites which dwelt in the land: therefore will we also serve the LORD; for he is our God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e8e6ef7-3ac2-42c7-9472-72574f659283>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JOS 24:19
Text: And Joshua said unto the people, Ye cannot serve the LORD: for he is an holy God; he is a jealous God; he will not forgive your transgressions nor your sins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bd85807-32e7-474c-9e3b-bde54283ac21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: JOS 24:20
Text: If ye forsake the LORD, and serve strange gods, then he will turn and do you hurt, and consume you, after that he hath done you good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78b24c66-a27c-4cc6-b7ec-57e8c85a5e0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: JOS 24:21
Text: And the people said unto Joshua, Nay; but we will serve the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1be00b04-ea4a-4a1b-a258-dbbab9da535f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: JOS 24:22
Text: And Joshua said unto the people, Ye are witnesses against yourselves that ye have chosen you the LORD, to serve him. And they said, We are witnesses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61104085-113b-4a15-9843-0cfde65f6a47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: JOS 24:23
Text: Now therefore put away, said he, the strange gods which are among you, and incline your heart unto the LORD God of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7269c60-d7fd-4e98-ad3e-68cb44c6c421>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: JOS 24:24
Text: And the people said unto Joshua, The LORD our God will we serve, and his voice will we obey.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eeb8e024-7d34-4bff-a01b-8135873d2fa1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: JOS 24:25
Text: So Joshua made a covenant with the people that day, and set them a statute and an ordinance in Shechem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f88d3bd4-3980-4f18-b0e5-37ef6249688e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: JOS 24:26
Text: And Joshua wrote these words in the book of the law of God, and took a great stone, and set it up there under an oak, that was by the sanctuary of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc2610f1-d9ba-47c6-8a20-55e4d87f38d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: JOS 24:27
Text: And Joshua said unto all the people, Behold, this stone shall be a witness unto us; for it hath heard all the words of the LORD which he spake unto us: it shall be therefore a witness unto you, lest ye deny your God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd1f5d96-55ad-4ed3-a6aa-485a2557bff7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: JOS 24:28
Text: So Joshua let the people depart, every man unto his inheritance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9779f8df-b25e-431c-872d-6e0d503c84e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: JOS 24:29
Text: And it came to pass after these things, that Joshua the son of Nun, the servant of the LORD, died, being an hundred and ten years old.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e061d682-c91b-46f6-8ae2-ad366dbad6b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: JOS 24:30
Text: And they buried him in the border of his inheritance in Timnathserah, which is in mount Ephraim, on the north side of the hill of Gaash.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14a260f2-822a-477e-968c-fcd7bc7cff69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: JOS 24:31
Text: And Israel served the LORD all the days of Joshua, and all the days of the elders that overlived Joshua, and which had known all the works of the LORD, that he had done for Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6f637d5-e3e3-429b-80de-7c2154a4efba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 304

Reference: JOS 24:32
Text: And the bones of Joseph, which the children of Israel brought up out of Egypt, buried they in Shechem, in a parcel of ground which Jacob bought of the sons of Hamor the father of Shechem for an hundred pieces of silver: and it became the inheritance of the children of Joseph.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOS/24/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f750f244-bb1e-49f6-9f0a-68d2b4cddc75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: JOS 24:33
Text: And Eleazar the son of Aaron died; and they buried him in a hill that pertained to Phinehas his son, which was given him in mount Ephraim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0491c734-3015-449f-93f8-89dde60305ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: JDG 1:1
Text: Now after the death of Joshua it came to pass, that the children of Israel asked the LORD, saying, Who shall go up for us against the Canaanites first, to fight against them?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:340e17fa-e9e8-4050-b33e-b394470bd32a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: JDG 1:2
Text: And the LORD said, Judah shall go up: behold, I have delivered the land into his hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5199aef-83d3-44b7-bdd8-00d935142f49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: JDG 1:3
Text: And Judah said unto Simeon his brother, Come up with me into my lot, that we may fight against the Canaanites; and I likewise will go with thee into thy lot. So Simeon went with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:844f3b45-c116-4e97-8a34-e43ac1ed06ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: JDG 1:4
Text: And Judah went up; and the LORD delivered the Canaanites and the Perizzites into their hand: and they slew of them in Bezek ten thousand men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72b4622a-5ee5-4523-aa1e-df47a996b968>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: JDG 1:5
Text: And they found Adonibezek in Bezek: and they fought against him, and they slew the Canaanites and the Perizzites.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3d3e1bb-bebc-4d1c-829d-9639c4878e8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: JDG 1:6
Text: But Adonibezek fled; and they pursued after him, and caught him, and cut off his thumbs and his great toes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc6006ed-eb95-4c70-b623-564da61e0005>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: JDG 1:7
Text: And Adonibezek said, Threescore and ten kings, having their thumbs and their great toes cut off, gathered their meat under my table: as I have done, so God hath requited me. And they brought him to Jerusalem, and there he died.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77e47b54-fa2d-4bdd-ae33-a9cee754b0d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: JDG 1:8
Text: Now the children of Judah had fought against Jerusalem, and had taken it, and smitten it with the edge of the sword, and set the city on fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9e11376-1b91-4c94-8463-34ef1e8e3127>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: JDG 1:9
Text: And afterward the children of Judah went down to fight against the Canaanites, that dwelt in the mountain, and in the south, and in the valley.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce7f3fe9-ad96-4ea3-b4aa-fa228386e2a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JDG 1:10
Text: And Judah went against the Canaanites that dwelt in Hebron: (now the name of Hebron before was Kirjatharba:) and they slew Sheshai, and Ahiman, and Talmai.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6cb7525e-89eb-4474-81a7-ed73c07a9539>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: JDG 1:11
Text: And from thence he went against the inhabitants of Debir: and the name of Debir before was Kirjathsepher:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71c1f6d2-6a51-4f50-91a8-37cacf2e0e55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: JDG 1:12
Text: And Caleb said, He that smiteth Kirjathsepher, and taketh it, to him will I give Achsah my daughter to wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b704219-23b5-4d08-b5dc-50815ccbf0fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: JDG 1:13
Text: And Othniel the son of Kenaz, Caleb’s younger brother, took it: and he gave him Achsah his daughter to wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7bada2a-1212-48f8-b680-1b44e13495ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: JDG 1:14
Text: And it came to pass, when she came to him, that she moved him to ask of her father a field: and she lighted from off her ass; and Caleb said unto her, What wilt thou?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da640aab-abfe-4857-9f47-40398feadc63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: JDG 1:15
Text: And she said unto him, Give me a blessing: for thou hast given me a south land; give me also springs of water. And Caleb gave her the upper springs and the nether springs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05d836be-6a8e-4c99-b5b1-ec6cb14ac1e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: JDG 1:16
Text: And the children of the Kenite, Moses’ father in law, went up out of the city of palm trees with the children of Judah into the wilderness of Judah, which lieth in the south of Arad; and they went and dwelt among the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c01a2c6-5053-4990-821f-49c64ddf0cc3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: JDG 1:17
Text: And Judah went with Simeon his brother, and they slew the Canaanites that inhabited Zephath, and utterly destroyed it. And the name of the city was called Hormah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d645f542-9a61-48e1-9fff-5a683feec7e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: JDG 1:18
Text: Also Judah took Gaza with the coast thereof, and Askelon with the coast thereof, and Ekron with the coast thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b30e574-e014-483a-92ee-6e1a1ed03b04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: JDG 1:19
Text: And the LORD was with Judah; and he drave out the inhabitants of the mountain; but could not drive out the inhabitants of the valley, because they had chariots of iron.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b7e1280-d61f-45ff-bbdf-a66e9a454412>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: JDG 1:20
Text: And they gave Hebron unto Caleb, as Moses said: and he expelled thence the three sons of Anak.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a95072e0-9abe-4ef7-b8b2-141936a983ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: JDG 1:21
Text: And the children of Benjamin did not drive out the Jebusites that inhabited Jerusalem; but the Jebusites dwell with the children of Benjamin in Jerusalem unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66c57005-d7a2-4870-9630-50363670b822>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: JDG 1:22
Text: And the house of Joseph, they also went up against Bethel: and the LORD was with them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a93d1376-89da-4026-bc5a-ead1b34a810f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: JDG 1:23
Text: And the house of Joseph sent to descry Bethel. (Now the name of the city before was Luz.)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04ee06a9-152e-407a-a81c-191bb62d6b24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JDG 1:24
Text: And the spies saw a man come forth out of the city, and they said unto him, Shew us, we pray thee, the entrance into the city, and we will shew thee mercy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c8eff6f-8db2-428f-b109-af5b02eced63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: JDG 1:25
Text: And when he shewed them the entrance into the city, they smote the city with the edge of the sword; but they let go the man and all his family.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4319239d-b303-424b-9069-de58d625884e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: JDG 1:26
Text: And the man went into the land of the Hittites, and built a city, and called the name thereof Luz: which is the name thereof unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f87a8ed-6433-4b93-9beb-e757cba2fdb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 306

Reference: JDG 1:27
Text: Neither did Manasseh drive out the inhabitants of Bethshean and her towns, nor Taanach and her towns, nor the inhabitants of Dor and her towns, nor the inhabitants of Ibleam and her towns, nor the inhabitants of Megiddo and her towns: but the Canaanites would dwell in that land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:253dc7de-b86a-4f9d-9eeb-9a1e7b954524>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: JDG 1:28
Text: And it came to pass, when Israel was strong, that they put the Canaanites to tribute, and did not utterly drive them out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1a08eab-90df-4625-b3f5-549ac9d9ad37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: JDG 1:29
Text: Neither did Ephraim drive out the Canaanites that dwelt in Gezer; but the Canaanites dwelt in Gezer among them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd8f4241-4efd-446f-9e59-124508432959>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: JDG 1:30
Text: Neither did Zebulun drive out the inhabitants of Kitron, nor the inhabitants of Nahalol; but the Canaanites dwelt among them, and became tributaries.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac311b82-ffc3-4bc3-ae01-93792c690fc8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JDG 1:31
Text: Neither did Asher drive out the inhabitants of Accho, nor the inhabitants of Zidon, nor of Ahlab, nor of Achzib, nor of Helbah, nor of Aphik, nor of Rehob:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6df09135-5d03-4e59-af45-039c95abf7b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: JDG 1:32
Text: But the Asherites dwelt among the Canaanites, the inhabitants of the land: for they did not drive them out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c98e4b31-8f1e-4fa4-bda7-1b7faea704e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 278

Reference: JDG 1:33
Text: Neither did Naphtali drive out the inhabitants of Bethshemesh, nor the inhabitants of Bethanath; but he dwelt among the Canaanites, the inhabitants of the land: nevertheless the inhabitants of Bethshemesh and of Bethanath became tributaries unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c8d63e6-4491-40a3-b1a9-ff87b16a746c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: JDG 1:34
Text: And the Amorites forced the children of Dan into the mountain: for they would not suffer them to come down to the valley:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aed3e2b0-b8aa-4ac4-9a78-c75fc6994f94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: JDG 1:35
Text: But the Amorites would dwell in mount Heres in Aijalon, and in Shaalbim: yet the hand of the house of Joseph prevailed, so that they became tributaries.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/1/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52b95785-3e43-4578-90fa-265d96d88c72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: JDG 1:36
Text: And the coast of the Amorites was from the going up to Akrabbim, from the rock, and upward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:709b3c4b-2ea8-4a8f-82d8-fd25be2458d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: JDG 2:1
Text: And an angel of the LORD came up from Gilgal to Bochim, and said, I made you to go up out of Egypt, and have brought you unto the land which I sware unto your fathers; and I said, I will never break my covenant with you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27490990-ad67-451a-903b-e0ee38edda23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: JDG 2:2
Text: And ye shall make no league with the inhabitants of this land; ye shall throw down their altars: but ye have not obeyed my voice: why have ye done this?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b37a5fd0-959d-455a-a7d1-034b0051d0fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: JDG 2:3
Text: Wherefore I also said, I will not drive them out from before you; but they shall be as thorns in your sides, and their gods shall be a snare unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d9b27dd-8767-4b6d-8db1-00317f52a5ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: JDG 2:4
Text: And it came to pass, when the angel of the LORD spake these words unto all the children of Israel, that the people lifted up their voice, and wept.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e78acce2-fbe2-467f-8e07-cd8b230ad2b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: JDG 2:5
Text: And they called the name of that place Bochim: and they sacrificed there unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6198185-2dd0-4331-8bc2-1ec24e168c2d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: JDG 2:6
Text: And when Joshua had let the people go, the children of Israel went every man unto his inheritance to possess the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:612795f1-94c4-4ca4-8227-7d5862ccf9c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: JDG 2:7
Text: And the people served the LORD all the days of Joshua, and all the days of the elders that outlived Joshua, who had seen all the great works of the LORD, that he did for Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:095ca42f-0794-4719-b589-55a7d187e163>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: JDG 2:8
Text: And Joshua the son of Nun, the servant of the LORD, died, being an hundred and ten years old.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a312db14-6260-44ff-81a3-4d4efdeb074c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: JDG 2:9
Text: And they buried him in the border of his inheritance in Timnathheres, in the mount of Ephraim, on the north side of the hill Gaash.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:068f3e7b-7d82-4d6d-bf3c-dc7ce72c2ed1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: JDG 2:10
Text: And also all that generation were gathered unto their fathers: and there arose another generation after them, which knew not the LORD, nor yet the works which he had done for Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b452ae9d-6160-4aa1-aa2b-fe54b9647820>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: JDG 2:11
Text: And the children of Israel did evil in the sight of the LORD, and served Baalim:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e87abc3e-0a7d-4807-a47a-927e7dc02c1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 262

Reference: JDG 2:12
Text: And they forsook the LORD God of their fathers, which brought them out of the land of Egypt, and followed other gods, of the gods of the people that were round about them, and bowed themselves unto them, and provoked the LORD to anger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a37a6094-37f7-4513-8992-8fc4a9947d77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: JDG 2:13
Text: And they forsook the LORD, and served Baal and Ashtaroth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1782a43b-44fa-4a24-a0bf-0edfada707ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: JDG 2:14
Text: And the anger of the LORD was hot against Israel, and he delivered them into the hands of spoilers that spoiled them, and he sold them into the hands of their enemies round about, so that they could not any longer stand before their enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edc08fbb-c07f-4849-9d2c-42d0a726bc82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: JDG 2:15
Text: Whithersoever they went out, the hand of the LORD was against them for evil, as the LORD had said, and as the LORD had sworn unto them: and they were greatly distressed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53b3fbcd-6c7b-4543-8bae-7363aca0c0cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: JDG 2:16
Text: Nevertheless the LORD raised up judges, which delivered them out of the hand of those that spoiled them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ac4cc91-d0fb-44b2-abd8-b7b13f8783b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: JDG 2:17
Text: And yet they would not hearken unto their judges, but they went a whoring after other gods, and bowed themselves unto them: they turned quickly out of the way which their fathers walked in, obeying the commandments of the LORD; but they did not so.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e9de4d0-f870-4cbc-9836-e3d4eb7ffa3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 286

Reference: JDG 2:18
Text: And when the LORD raised them up judges, then the LORD was with the judge, and delivered them out of the hand of their enemies all the days of the judge: for it repented the LORD because of their groanings by reason of them that oppressed them and vexed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:728b7e29-c9d9-41ca-8c3b-f4af99ecd5b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: JDG 2:19
Text: And it came to pass, when the judge was dead, that they returned, and corrupted themselves more than their fathers, in following other gods to serve them, and to bow down unto them; they ceased not from their own doings, nor from their stubborn way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d85f6f0-ddb8-4e35-9666-6516c2e5d3fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: JDG 2:20
Text: And the anger of the LORD was hot against Israel; and he said, Because that this people hath transgressed my covenant which I commanded their fathers, and have not hearkened unto my voice;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f809d4cb-dcb8-4d0a-90fe-352adc7e0aec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: JDG 2:21
Text: I also will not henceforth drive out any from before them of the nations which Joshua left when he died:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa8d243d-fc5c-4a15-872f-cb19f134b039>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: JDG 2:22
Text: That through them I may prove Israel, whether they will keep the way of the LORD to walk therein, as their fathers did keep it, or not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/2/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:602f25fe-e4da-4381-8199-c0297cdd3e8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: JDG 2:23
Text: Therefore the LORD left those nations, without driving them out hastily; neither delivered he them into the hand of Joshua.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e3ed60b-35ab-4353-9621-f8917c310b5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: JDG 3:1
Text: Now these are the nations which the LORD left, to prove Israel by them, even as many of Israel as had not known all the wars of Canaan;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a9a86a9-a04b-4bfe-9784-865063feaad9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: JDG 3:2
Text: Only that the generations of the children of Israel might know, to teach them war, at the least such as before knew nothing thereof;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bfd4869-6b31-4272-bb99-dbd53fed0581>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: JDG 3:3
Text: Namely, five lords of the Philistines, and all the Canaanites, and the Sidonians, and the Hivites that dwelt in mount Lebanon, from mount Baalhermon unto the entering in of Hamath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f0543aa-a9fc-419f-bcb4-6977ffe88b84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: JDG 3:4
Text: And they were to prove Israel by them, to know whether they would hearken unto the commandments of the LORD, which he commanded their fathers by the hand of Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ff4e03b-de06-495a-9aed-47c9d9ba552d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: JDG 3:5
Text: And the children of Israel dwelt among the Canaanites, Hittites, and Amorites, and Perizzites, and Hivites, and Jebusites:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f0a134f-1741-4269-80d8-2a91ecc88529>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: JDG 3:6
Text: And they took their daughters to be their wives, and gave their daughters to their sons, and served their gods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f953fae6-4a82-492a-9879-04a7c48c6ccc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: JDG 3:7
Text: And the children of Israel did evil in the sight of the LORD, and forgat the LORD their God, and served Baalim and the groves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8134b24a-16c7-4e8f-bc60-aa1e24863090>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: JDG 3:8
Text: Therefore the anger of the LORD was hot against Israel, and he sold them into the hand of Chushanrishathaim king of Mesopotamia: and the children of Israel served Chushanrishathaim eight years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2544ee34-e8ab-424c-a45c-64939a6c3c93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: JDG 3:9
Text: And when the children of Israel cried unto the LORD, the LORD raised up a deliverer to the children of Israel, who delivered them, even Othniel the son of Kenaz, Caleb’s younger brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1ce66b5-220e-4cd4-97e8-a63279429c19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: JDG 3:10
Text: And the Spirit of the LORD came upon him, and he judged Israel, and went out to war: and the LORD delivered Chushanrishathaim king of Mesopotamia into his hand; and his hand prevailed against Chushanrishathaim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a224af7-0222-4fb0-b906-881b43e809fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: JDG 3:11
Text: And the land had rest forty years. And Othniel the son of Kenaz died.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:450aea64-639d-4c71-addf-76c52177c144>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: JDG 3:12
Text: And the children of Israel did evil again in the sight of the LORD: and the LORD strengthened Eglon the king of Moab against Israel, because they had done evil in the sight of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00e0a27e-ec28-4b26-8ebb-743df51b0acb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: JDG 3:13
Text: And he gathered unto him the children of Ammon and Amalek, and went and smote Israel, and possessed the city of palm trees.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65c41f47-6a18-4b6e-9bb9-4d7d79150fcb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: JDG 3:14
Text: So the children of Israel served Eglon the king of Moab eighteen years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c926553e-fc88-40f1-b4bb-fa8d6bc9831d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: JDG 3:15
Text: But when the children of Israel cried unto the LORD, the LORD raised them up a deliverer, Ehud the son of Gera, a Benjamite, a man lefthanded: and by him the children of Israel sent a present unto Eglon the king of Moab.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9442e788-355f-4729-9f55-b991217e836d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: JDG 3:16
Text: But Ehud made him a dagger which had two edges, of a cubit length; and he did gird it under his raiment upon his right thigh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:495e29ab-bacb-4aca-85a6-3fe8b5fda4d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: JDG 3:17
Text: And he brought the present unto Eglon king of Moab: and Eglon was a very fat man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60676963-7819-4fa0-b350-c3f186b8c5e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: JDG 3:18
Text: And when he had made an end to offer the present, he sent away the people that bare the present.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1913607a-da7e-4d0f-91d9-576cdbc1b809>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: JDG 3:19
Text: But he himself turned again from the quarries that were by Gilgal, and said, I have a secret errand unto thee, O king: who said, Keep silence. And all that stood by him went out from him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fd72701-8c0a-4217-a487-ce07f9f53ead>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: JDG 3:20
Text: And Ehud came unto him; and he was sitting in a summer parlour, which he had for himself alone. And Ehud said, I have a message from God unto thee. And he arose out of his seat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e53b709e-bc84-4047-bb9f-e06d0c92cb27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: JDG 3:21
Text: And Ehud put forth his left hand, and took the dagger from his right thigh, and thrust it into his belly:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21fd7cbe-83e1-4359-9a9a-0444f900f425>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JDG 3:22
Text: And the haft also went in after the blade; and the fat closed upon the blade, so that he could not draw the dagger out of his belly; and the dirt came out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f14e3f0-f676-4eac-9269-0d5ecf7f298c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: JDG 3:23
Text: Then Ehud went forth through the porch, and shut the doors of the parlour upon him, and locked them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a39fb4c-865b-4eda-8858-73cf51002b5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: JDG 3:24
Text: When he was gone out, his servants came; and when they saw that, behold, the doors of the parlour were locked, they said, Surely he covereth his feet in his summer chamber.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d557283-5e69-48e4-8314-37235659f5b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: JDG 3:25
Text: And they tarried till they were ashamed: and, behold, he opened not the doors of the parlour; therefore they took a key, and opened them: and, behold, their lord was fallen down dead on the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b4315a7-f31a-4acb-9dbf-c4141f8de9bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: JDG 3:26
Text: And Ehud escaped while they tarried, and passed beyond the quarries, and escaped unto Seirath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59f74da4-4d55-4daa-bbb5-d1cc83f49b29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: JDG 3:27
Text: And it came to pass, when he was come, that he blew a trumpet in the mountain of Ephraim, and the children of Israel went down with him from the mount, and he before them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4d1719e-f04d-42d4-8d90-b85d64d03f2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: JDG 3:28
Text: And he said unto them, Follow after me: for the LORD hath delivered your enemies the Moabites into your hand. And they went down after him, and took the fords of Jordan toward Moab, and suffered not a man to pass over.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd7ddc07-8add-4524-bbb9-cf6d9ca245d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: JDG 3:29
Text: And they slew of Moab at that time about ten thousand men, all lusty, and all men of valour; and there escaped not a man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64c24d57-719d-41df-a625-34c424847514>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: JDG 3:30
Text: So Moab was subdued that day under the hand of Israel. And the land had rest fourscore years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/3/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad12c5d3-4908-49a9-ac37-564462453e3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: JDG 3:31
Text: And after him was Shamgar the son of Anath, which slew of the Philistines six hundred men with an ox goad: and he also delivered Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f245ecb2-ce81-40b8-99ca-a41571644465>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: JDG 4:1
Text: And the children of Israel again did evil in the sight of the LORD, when Ehud was dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1141f7d3-b8eb-43d2-b409-08964afbf439>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: JDG 4:2
Text: And the LORD sold them into the hand of Jabin king of Canaan, that reigned in Hazor; the captain of whose host was Sisera, which dwelt in Harosheth of the Gentiles.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86acc636-8a30-47c7-8153-8435ede29927>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: JDG 4:3
Text: And the children of Israel cried unto the LORD: for he had nine hundred chariots of iron; and twenty years he mightily oppressed the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9cb39a1-edbf-44dd-9912-da7da246c891>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: JDG 4:4
Text: And Deborah, a prophetess, the wife of Lapidoth, she judged Israel at that time.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c476381-f485-46d8-96ff-f4de303e7bea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: JDG 4:5
Text: And she dwelt under the palm tree of Deborah between Ramah and Bethel in mount Ephraim: and the children of Israel came up to her for judgment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5681ab1b-426e-4c41-abb0-7c9a3ae6d341>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 295

Reference: JDG 4:6
Text: And she sent and called Barak the son of Abinoam out of Kedeshnaphtali, and said unto him, Hath not the LORD God of Israel commanded, saying, Go and draw toward mount Tabor, and take with thee ten thousand men of the children of Naphtali and of the children of Zebulun?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5ac57e7-7d22-44d4-ae30-2b0dc5abe4b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: JDG 4:7
Text: And I will draw unto thee to the river Kishon Sisera, the captain of Jabin’s army, with his chariots and his multitude; and I will deliver him into thine hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e55c6f81-57e3-48ad-b79f-35141d08a1b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: JDG 4:8
Text: And Barak said unto her, If thou wilt go with me, then I will go: but if thou wilt not go with me, then I will not go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ea33ddc-a5a8-47b3-9e50-320d61935ea7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: JDG 4:9
Text: And she said, I will surely go with thee: notwithstanding the journey that thou takest shall not be for thine honour; for the LORD shall sell Sisera into the hand of a woman. And Deborah arose, and went with Barak to Kedesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7cc55162-c5b1-42ac-b7ad-2022552a7dbd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: JDG 4:10
Text: And Barak called Zebulun and Naphtali to Kedesh; and he went up with ten thousand men at his feet: and Deborah went up with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24fef81a-5097-4a8a-a43f-c017722a0aa5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: JDG 4:11
Text: Now Heber the Kenite, which was of the children of Hobab the father in law of Moses, had severed himself from the Kenites, and pitched his tent unto the plain of Zaanaim, which is by Kedesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3b760ba-3056-4a1c-a76d-f44cf1eb7a93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: JDG 4:12
Text: And they shewed Sisera that Barak the son of Abinoam was gone up to mount Tabor.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c24897c3-98d1-4530-bd92-a86f11d25449>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: JDG 4:13
Text: And Sisera gathered together all his chariots, even nine hundred chariots of iron, and all the people that were with him, from Harosheth of the Gentiles unto the river of Kishon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74a59864-fc59-49f9-b445-7471776b6911>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: JDG 4:14
Text: And Deborah said unto Barak, Up; for this is the day in which the LORD hath delivered Sisera into thine hand: is not the LORD gone out before thee? So Barak went down from mount Tabor, and ten thousand men after him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:342c3276-551e-45e7-bb74-23a7c9d7ef65>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: JDG 4:15
Text: And the LORD discomfited Sisera, and all his chariots, and all his host, with the edge of the sword before Barak; so that Sisera lighted down off his chariot, and fled away on his feet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aff69e72-17a7-4764-977c-9381722a031f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: JDG 4:16
Text: But Barak pursued after the chariots, and after the host, unto Harosheth of the Gentiles: and all the host of Sisera fell upon the edge of the sword; and there was not a man left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ccd688b6-5c98-4731-89e0-9b19a402f113>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: JDG 4:17
Text: Howbeit Sisera fled away on his feet to the tent of Jael the wife of Heber the Kenite: for there was peace between Jabin the king of Hazor and the house of Heber the Kenite.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33b55d25-b677-45c9-95ff-ca988c7482a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: JDG 4:18
Text: And Jael went out to meet Sisera, and said unto him, Turn in, my lord, turn in to me; fear not. And when he had turned in unto her into the tent, she covered him with a mantle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf9179b4-2e7c-44ad-b4c6-a7ecb608b862>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: JDG 4:19
Text: And he said unto her, Give me, I pray thee, a little water to drink; for I am thirsty. And she opened a bottle of milk, and gave him drink, and covered him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c44ba94-20ac-4a69-b9a8-6bdb9bf1278d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: JDG 4:20
Text: Again he said unto her, Stand in the door of the tent, and it shall be, when any man doth come and enquire of thee, and say, Is there any man here? that thou shalt say, No.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0af24c8d-67d2-4c3e-8b39-5029f6f80cd0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: JDG 4:21
Text: Then Jael Heber’s wife took a nail of the tent, and took an hammer in her hand, and went softly unto him, and smote the nail into his temples, and fastened it into the ground: for he was fast asleep and weary. So he died.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73849b65-7f70-4219-a1fd-1b94bdf4ad0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: JDG 4:22
Text: And, behold, as Barak pursued Sisera, Jael came out to meet him, and said unto him, Come, and I will shew thee the man whom thou seekest. And when he came into her tent, behold, Sisera lay dead, and the nail was in his temples.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:baa50e45-dbb7-4326-8725-fb3e304ed57a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: JDG 4:23
Text: So God subdued on that day Jabin the king of Canaan before the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/4/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b33a3d5d-79da-42c7-9f46-9cef0712e35c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: JDG 4:24
Text: And the hand of the children of Israel prospered, and prevailed against Jabin the king of Canaan, until they had destroyed Jabin king of Canaan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d4bd076-9e6f-4fdf-9f96-96af32b0e73c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: JDG 5:1
Text: Then sang Deborah and Barak the son of Abinoam on that day, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68ae68ae-b83a-434a-a63c-d34702af19d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: JDG 5:2
Text: Praise ye the LORD for the avenging of Israel, when the people willingly offered themselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b7202c5-199f-45e3-9e2b-0170f867fcbe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: JDG 5:3
Text: Hear, O ye kings; give ear, O ye princes; I, even I, will sing unto the LORD; I will sing praise to the LORD God of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7cc634f-5df7-421b-9b4d-bb31ebd4cb1e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: JDG 5:4
Text: LORD, when thou wentest out of Seir, when thou marchedst out of the field of Edom, the earth trembled, and the heavens dropped, the clouds also dropped water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9629cf7-5ea3-4790-9b0a-43bfe764837f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: JDG 5:5
Text: The mountains melted from before the LORD, even that Sinai from before the LORD God of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab8d6141-a1e7-4418-9e22-bf61b301b9c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: JDG 5:6
Text: In the days of Shamgar the son of Anath, in the days of Jael, the highways were unoccupied, and the travellers walked through byways.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d50d930-96a2-42a9-b32a-c5a1c977caa0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: JDG 5:7
Text: The inhabitants of the villages ceased, they ceased in Israel, until that I Deborah arose, that I arose a mother in Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32caf995-2ef5-4bd2-ac29-1bbc4a261538>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: JDG 5:8
Text: They chose new gods; then was war in the gates: was there a shield or spear seen among forty thousand in Israel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06cb4b0c-85b3-418e-9dae-e18527da031b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: JDG 5:9
Text: My heart is toward the governors of Israel, that offered themselves willingly among the people. Bless ye the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bbb2b6eb-5f30-4d2c-b959-2ca7b7a033e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: JDG 5:10
Text: Speak, ye that ride on white asses, ye that sit in judgment, and walk by the way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4b02360-317c-4e69-ad9e-6d2a5ac95e84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 296

Reference: JDG 5:11
Text: They that are delivered from the noise of archers in the places of drawing water, there shall they rehearse the righteous acts of the LORD, even the righteous acts toward the inhabitants of his villages in Israel: then shall the people of the LORD go down to the gates.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8e17cb0-3775-49f9-8829-0f80e81f1d94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: JDG 5:12
Text: Awake, awake, Deborah: awake, awake, utter a song: arise, Barak, and lead thy captivity captive, thou son of Abinoam.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6f88614-0366-4d2f-ab6c-6e2031670940>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: JDG 5:13
Text: Then he made him that remaineth have dominion over the nobles among the people: the LORD made me have dominion over the mighty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e4a419c-6a0a-4a0b-8211-9c9b6f7a5ec8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: JDG 5:14
Text: Out of Ephraim was there a root of them against Amalek; after thee, Benjamin, among thy people; out of Machir came down governors, and out of Zebulun they that handle the pen of the writer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89d5a1bb-4001-40bd-aae6-c3990b0d9798>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: JDG 5:15
Text: And the princes of Issachar were with Deborah; even Issachar, and also Barak: he was sent on foot into the valley. For the divisions of Reuben there were great thoughts of heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b50636f4-e0f7-497c-908c-62fe9469d61b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: JDG 5:16
Text: Why abodest thou among the sheepfolds, to hear the bleatings of the flocks? For the divisions of Reuben there were great searchings of heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33984705-00b2-41b8-8a43-4d972228dd45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: JDG 5:17
Text: Gilead abode beyond Jordan: and why did Dan remain in ships? Asher continued on the sea shore, and abode in his breaches.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ddeec2c-54b0-4b72-8f7d-5f7fa6a8da1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: JDG 5:18
Text: Zebulun and Naphtali were a people that jeoparded their lives unto the death in the high places of the field.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0d71217-9a27-4124-8c72-ab31a48f2f87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: JDG 5:19
Text: The kings came and fought, then fought the kings of Canaan in Taanach by the waters of Megiddo; they took no gain of money.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c95f2afb-1d66-469e-8ce8-8678abba85e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: JDG 5:20
Text: They fought from heaven; the stars in their courses fought against Sisera.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e443ae2-f7b6-4844-8450-669f346804ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: JDG 5:21
Text: The river of Kishon swept them away, that ancient river, the river Kishon. O my soul, thou hast trodden down strength.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5cdbde67-cda1-49d0-b55a-3dccdf123b5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: JDG 5:22
Text: Then were the horsehoofs broken by the means of the pransings, the pransings of their mighty ones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f94ea9e3-aabb-4d6a-8c09-1ae2f3640943>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: JDG 5:23
Text: Curse ye Meroz, said the angel of the LORD, curse ye bitterly the inhabitants thereof; because they came not to the help of the LORD, to the help of the LORD against the mighty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b2568d0-1e5d-4320-b497-607c25680b89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: JDG 5:24
Text: Blessed above women shall Jael the wife of Heber the Kenite be, blessed shall she be above women in the tent.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c9521eb-cff5-4622-9e21-e14d1cf3c702>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: JDG 5:25
Text: He asked water, and she gave him milk; she brought forth butter in a lordly dish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6f63bea-ff1d-4aa7-aaf6-c34f2d23f971>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: JDG 5:26
Text: She put her hand to the nail, and her right hand to the workmen’s hammer; and with the hammer she smote Sisera, she smote off his head, when she had pierced and stricken through his temples.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:280a046a-81f9-4719-a8e9-4676d25c437b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: JDG 5:27
Text: At her feet he bowed, he fell, he lay down: at her feet he bowed, he fell: where he bowed, there he fell down dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b10e2299-4f7b-441d-9597-0e21f4230e51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: JDG 5:28
Text: The mother of Sisera looked out at a window, and cried through the lattice, Why is his chariot so long in coming? why tarry the wheels of his chariots?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3055801b-d2d1-4743-acf9-d6f6f5de2a08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: JDG 5:29
Text: Her wise ladies answered her, yea, she returned answer to herself,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fbfee51-e190-4bd7-9bd8-17fadf8cf411>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 279

Reference: JDG 5:30
Text: Have they not sped? have they not divided the prey; to every man a damsel or two; to Sisera a prey of divers colours, a prey of divers colours of needlework, of divers colours of needlework on both sides, meet for the necks of them that take the spoil?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/5/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5363ae8-d690-4537-a145-c09d8a9d34e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: JDG 5:31
Text: So let all thine enemies perish, O LORD: but let them that love him be as the sun when he goeth forth in his might. And the land had rest forty years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20d25631-35ce-4603-8470-3e03aebbde6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: JDG 6:1
Text: And the children of Israel did evil in the sight of the LORD: and the LORD delivered them into the hand of Midian seven years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1c3c5e9-9931-4b16-acca-102fc4d11b35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: JDG 6:2
Text: And the hand of Midian prevailed against Israel: and because of the Midianites the children of Israel made them the dens which are in the mountains, and caves, and strong holds.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a014cef7-35cc-4787-902d-6a649eba6a06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: JDG 6:3
Text: And so it was, when Israel had sown, that the Midianites came up, and the Amalekites, and the children of the east, even they came up against them;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a98636a9-df4f-4201-9cfe-2bca58afb180>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: JDG 6:4
Text: And they encamped against them, and destroyed the increase of the earth, till thou come unto Gaza, and left no sustenance for Israel, neither sheep, nor ox, nor ass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1dac0bb-708a-4e07-9029-19b56886fbde>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: JDG 6:5
Text: For they came up with their cattle and their tents, and they came as grasshoppers for multitude; for both they and their camels were without number: and they entered into the land to destroy it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:058c28f0-62ee-4296-9451-c8a493e1c8f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: JDG 6:6
Text: And Israel was greatly impoverished because of the Midianites; and the children of Israel cried unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:534943c4-83b8-4a0d-8e35-f9bfd5b87982>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: JDG 6:7
Text: And it came to pass, when the children of Israel cried unto the LORD because of the Midianites,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2a25bab-b493-4a77-8936-293f2da049a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: JDG 6:8
Text: That the LORD sent a prophet unto the children of Israel, which said unto them, Thus saith the LORD God of Israel, I brought you up from Egypt, and brought you forth out of the house of bondage;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:130a5e08-7d8c-40a1-9f2c-d011f2720017>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: JDG 6:9
Text: And I delivered you out of the hand of the Egyptians, and out of the hand of all that oppressed you, and drave them out from before you, and gave you their land;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4533c3e-a579-45b7-8801-ac758b311a00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: JDG 6:10
Text: And I said unto you, I am the LORD your God; fear not the gods of the Amorites, in whose land ye dwell: but ye have not obeyed my voice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f62a2996-2ff3-4fae-b3d8-1951812c7a82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: JDG 6:11
Text: And there came an angel of the LORD, and sat under an oak which was in Ophrah, that pertained unto Joash the Abiezrite: and his son Gideon threshed wheat by the winepress, to hide it from the Midianites.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc9bd109-f8c1-4cb3-b7c1-0fd2ce65d077>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: JDG 6:12
Text: And the angel of the LORD appeared unto him, and said unto him, The LORD is with thee, thou mighty man of valour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55a0c297-efa0-4ab9-a472-7f886fc7f109>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 317

Reference: JDG 6:13
Text: And Gideon said unto him, Oh my Lord, if the LORD be with us, why then is all this befallen us? and where be all his miracles which our fathers told us of, saying, Did not the LORD bring us up from Egypt? but now the LORD hath forsaken us, and delivered us into the hands of the Midianites.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7cfb0f6-90e5-488d-8fdc-43e8d2903c4f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: JDG 6:14
Text: And the LORD looked upon him, and said, Go in this thy might, and thou shalt save Israel from the hand of the Midianites: have not I sent thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a915cec8-88d2-4914-a95a-d46904261a1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: JDG 6:15
Text: And he said unto him, Oh my Lord, wherewith shall I save Israel? behold, my family is poor in Manasseh, and I am the least in my father’s house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0bc6152-d1df-4031-9c96-df8ca41e539d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: JDG 6:16
Text: And the LORD said unto him, Surely I will be with thee, and thou shalt smite the Midianites as one man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b05b8fac-2930-419d-b43c-6abc1f7128cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: JDG 6:17
Text: And he said unto him, If now I have found grace in thy sight, then shew me a sign that thou talkest with me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d920dde-3300-4b91-a7f0-86b4e97957b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JDG 6:18
Text: Depart not hence, I pray thee, until I come unto thee, and bring forth my present, and set it before thee. And he said, I will tarry until thou come again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:760dec8f-c7d8-4484-8bd3-304a977b874b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: JDG 6:19
Text: And Gideon went in, and made ready a kid, and unleavened cakes of an ephah of flour: the flesh he put in a basket, and he put the broth in a pot, and brought it out unto him under the oak, and presented it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd305b5c-bd13-4b5f-ad64-3b5a90dc0c22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: JDG 6:20
Text: And the angel of God said unto him, Take the flesh and the unleavened cakes, and lay them upon this rock, and pour out the broth. And he did so.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a296c067-8dc7-4af8-86b4-2e4e006ec8df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 297

Reference: JDG 6:21
Text: Then the angel of the LORD put forth the end of the staff that was in his hand, and touched the flesh and the unleavened cakes; and there rose up fire out of the rock, and consumed the flesh and the unleavened cakes. Then the angel of the LORD departed out of his sight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:052edc74-3ac8-4058-8e4d-c758b8cbea57>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: JDG 6:22
Text: And when Gideon perceived that he was an angel of the LORD, Gideon said, Alas, O LORD God! for because I have seen an angel of the LORD face to face.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ec27604-f3d9-436a-87f4-7a6e101dfebf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: JDG 6:23
Text: And the LORD said unto him, Peace be unto thee; fear not: thou shalt not die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:267a0032-0af8-4f0b-93ab-f52a6f1c374e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: JDG 6:24
Text: Then Gideon built an altar there unto the LORD, and called it Jehovahshalom: unto this day it is yet in Ophrah of the Abiezrites.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09fcad24-810e-483c-8879-570d395b4379>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: JDG 6:25
Text: And it came to pass the same night, that the LORD said unto him, Take thy father’s young bullock, even the second bullock of seven years old, and throw down the altar of Baal that thy father hath, and cut down the grove that is by it:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae4b0dd9-a23c-4ac0-a517-81c0b5eb17d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: JDG 6:26
Text: And build an altar unto the LORD thy God upon the top of this rock, in the ordered place, and take the second bullock, and offer a burnt sacrifice with the wood of the grove which thou shalt cut down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c787ef9d-a579-465f-b347-dabc0ca8ff42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: JDG 6:27
Text: Then Gideon took ten men of his servants, and did as the LORD had said unto him: and so it was, because he feared his father’s household, and the men of the city, that he could not do it by day, that he did it by night.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2dc8cb08-cb37-4757-b114-3aa7cda8a1bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: JDG 6:28
Text: And when the men of the city arose early in the morning, behold, the altar of Baal was cast down, and the grove was cut down that was by it, and the second bullock was offered upon the altar that was built.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a783670b-82e2-4dec-b935-2a9dd61c2f1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: JDG 6:29
Text: And they said one to another, Who hath done this thing? And when they enquired and asked, they said, Gideon the son of Joash hath done this thing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d482bf68-9b98-42d7-bd59-1ea4c8472e8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: JDG 6:30
Text: Then the men of the city said unto Joash, Bring out thy son, that he may die: because he hath cast down the altar of Baal, and because he hath cut down the grove that was by it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e246811-7cb7-4b9f-9a72-1d47d9b1bb43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: JDG 6:31
Text: And Joash said unto all that stood against him, Will ye plead for Baal? will ye save him? he that will plead for him, let him be put to death whilst it is yet morning: if he be a god, let him plead for himself, because one hath cast down his altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82afda22-c2cd-46b9-802c-2091499d254a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: JDG 6:32
Text: Therefore on that day he called him Jerubbaal, saying, Let Baal plead against him, because he hath thrown down his altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb0cff34-ae84-43a0-aea0-f1f4ad2861b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: JDG 6:33
Text: Then all the Midianites and the Amalekites and the children of the east were gathered together, and went over, and pitched in the valley of Jezreel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:864f9bc9-a03e-437a-8228-5ac16dc077f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: JDG 6:34
Text: But the Spirit of the LORD came upon Gideon, and he blew a trumpet; and Abiezer was gathered after him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:debd8e7e-8cdf-4f68-8f8a-f81b97e994a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: JDG 6:35
Text: And he sent messengers throughout all Manasseh; who also was gathered after him: and he sent messengers unto Asher, and unto Zebulun, and unto Naphtali; and they came up to meet them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da35d7a5-a7ce-48f8-a701-661bb00e67a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: JDG 6:36
Text: And Gideon said unto God, If thou wilt save Israel by mine hand, as thou hast said,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5962028-cc31-4b5b-863b-e58ec2e717e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: JDG 6:37
Text: Behold, I will put a fleece of wool in the floor; and if the dew be on the fleece only, and it be dry upon all the earth beside, then shall I know that thou wilt save Israel by mine hand, as thou hast said.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3f81a93-d595-49c9-a441-8f18247e4a96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: JDG 6:38
Text: And it was so: for he rose up early on the morrow, and thrust the fleece together, and wringed the dew out of the fleece, a bowl full of water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0530416-7dd8-4772-98b5-3e051ee14b3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: JDG 6:39
Text: And Gideon said unto God, Let not thine anger be hot against me, and I will speak but this once: let me prove, I pray thee, but this once with the fleece; let it now be dry only upon the fleece, and upon all the ground let there be dew.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/6/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cafad23e-ab2f-4f8f-9867-62a2b2c39140>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: JDG 6:40
Text: And God did so that night: for it was dry upon the fleece only, and there was dew on all the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75f6e3bd-1ad6-4879-96ed-b5109ce345db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: JDG 7:1
Text: Then Jerubbaal, who is Gideon, and all the people that were with him, rose up early, and pitched beside the well of Harod: so that the host of the Midianites were on the north side of them, by the hill of Moreh, in the valley.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6a03bea-6449-4b09-8ebd-c0ece0c490b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: JDG 7:2
Text: And the LORD said unto Gideon, The people that are with thee are too many for me to give the Midianites into their hands, lest Israel vaunt themselves against me, saying, Mine own hand hath saved me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2298f389-fd7f-4be0-bf1d-bfe054ae94a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: JDG 7:3
Text: Now therefore go to, proclaim in the ears of the people, saying, Whosoever is fearful and afraid, let him return and depart early from mount Gilead. And there returned of the people twenty and two thousand; and there remained ten thousand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9539c1d7-2faf-4a6c-9702-05b953dc44b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 341

Reference: JDG 7:4
Text: And the LORD said unto Gideon, The people are yet too many; bring them down unto the water, and I will try them for thee there: and it shall be, that of whom I say unto thee, This shall go with thee, the same shall go with thee; and of whomsoever I say unto thee, This shall not go with thee, the same shall not go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7a884aa-0154-4fe5-b619-3bd1debe06fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: JDG 7:5
Text: So he brought down the people unto the water: and the LORD said unto Gideon, Every one that lappeth of the water with his tongue, as a dog lappeth, him shalt thou set by himself; likewise every one that boweth down upon his knees to drink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:118f56dd-3dd5-44b8-813f-bba80b87dbc0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: JDG 7:6
Text: And the number of them that lapped, putting their hand to their mouth, were three hundred men: but all the rest of the people bowed down upon their knees to drink water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f697a6e0-1e67-4ece-bdfc-862a3e21b67d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: JDG 7:7
Text: And the LORD said unto Gideon, By the three hundred men that lapped will I save you, and deliver the Midianites into thine hand: and let all the other people go every man unto his place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:676a6b78-bc69-4936-9aab-b4f427e2114b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: JDG 7:8
Text: So the people took victuals in their hand, and their trumpets: and he sent all the rest of Israel every man unto his tent, and retained those three hundred men: and the host of Midian was beneath him in the valley.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca8253c9-3ce7-4920-b870-c50e462462d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: JDG 7:9
Text: And it came to pass the same night, that the LORD said unto him, Arise, get thee down unto the host; for I have delivered it into thine hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6254e3eb-1d37-4288-bff1-df3c48321412>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: JDG 7:10
Text: But if thou fear to go down, go thou with Phurah thy servant down to the host:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6fd4880e-e253-481e-8ffc-3adcce49b9d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: JDG 7:11
Text: And thou shalt hear what they say; and afterward shall thine hands be strengthened to go down unto the host. Then went he down with Phurah his servant unto the outside of the armed men that were in the host.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b405fb65-b818-491c-bb76-547343d815b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: JDG 7:12
Text: And the Midianites and the Amalekites and all the children of the east lay along in the valley like grasshoppers for multitude; and their camels were without number, as the sand by the sea side for multitude.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d079bab-06ae-41eb-91ed-0b82458139b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 306

Reference: JDG 7:13
Text: And when Gideon was come, behold, there was a man that told a dream unto his fellow, and said, Behold, I dreamed a dream, and, lo, a cake of barley bread tumbled into the host of Midian, and came unto a tent, and smote it that it fell, and overturned it, that the tent lay along.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:349c2f12-d70f-463c-8aee-fa3865ae1d9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: JDG 7:14
Text: And his fellow answered and said, This is nothing else save the sword of Gideon the son of Joash, a man of Israel: for into his hand hath God delivered Midian, and all the host.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ecb9539c-6346-4937-99b0-04faf377d019>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: JDG 7:15
Text: And it was so, when Gideon heard the telling of the dream, and the interpretation thereof, that he worshipped, and returned into the host of Israel, and said, Arise; for the LORD hath delivered into your hand the host of Midian.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5103b069-8b98-4455-8b1e-c1c1ff5c56f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: JDG 7:16
Text: And he divided the three hundred men into three companies, and he put a trumpet in every man’s hand, with empty pitchers, and lamps within the pitchers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb188a96-a797-42e1-8054-9e08c23188ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: JDG 7:17
Text: And he said unto them, Look on me, and do likewise: and, behold, when I come to the outside of the camp, it shall be that, as I do, so shall ye do.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e82edca2-9cb2-4c9f-ab17-85dd115ace9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: JDG 7:18
Text: When I blow with a trumpet, I and all that are with me, then blow ye the trumpets also on every side of all the camp, and say, The sword of the LORD, and of Gideon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1818742c-4551-47e1-b7a1-4df1879a4668>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: JDG 7:19
Text: So Gideon, and the hundred men that were with him, came unto the outside of the camp in the beginning of the middle watch; and they had but newly set the watch: and they blew the trumpets, and brake the pitchers that were in their hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f29e592-4963-4612-8b26-6f49beabefa3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: JDG 7:20
Text: And the three companies blew the trumpets, and brake the pitchers, and held the lamps in their left hands, and the trumpets in their right hands to blow withal: and they cried, The sword of the LORD, and of Gideon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac3fbedc-0fef-4f2a-8e87-197b601085a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: JDG 7:21
Text: And they stood every man in his place round about the camp; and all the host ran, and cried, and fled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed16e02d-0cd6-4ebd-94c5-7a78c0deeb04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: JDG 7:22
Text: And the three hundred blew the trumpets, and the LORD set every man’s sword against his fellow, even throughout all the host: and the host fled to Bethshittah in Zererath, and to the border of Abelmeholah, unto Tabbath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9dbb1a76-7c93-4b2b-bf16-98de41e14f29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: JDG 7:23
Text: And the men of Israel gathered themselves together out of Naphtali, and out of Asher, and out of all Manasseh, and pursued after the Midianites.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ef25f49-02ad-4e83-a47f-d0e3e4e7e773>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 289

Reference: JDG 7:24
Text: And Gideon sent messengers throughout all mount Ephraim, saying, come down against the Midianites, and take before them the waters unto Bethbarah and Jordan. Then all the men of Ephraim gathered themselves together, and took the waters unto Bethbarah and Jordan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/7/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc34fcee-fdc8-430f-9b8c-2412c00e2b06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: JDG 7:25
Text: And they took two princes of the Midianites, Oreb and Zeeb; and they slew Oreb upon the rock Oreb, and Zeeb they slew at the winepress of Zeeb, and pursued Midian, and brought the heads of Oreb and Zeeb to Gideon on the other side Jordan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddee9a47-7105-4172-a904-90f8e1d2b0b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: JDG 8:1
Text: And the men of Ephraim said unto him, Why hast thou served us thus, that thou calledst us not, when thou wentest to fight with the Midianites? And they did chide with him sharply.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5518731a-6ebf-495b-84f7-52b4c232e688>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: JDG 8:2
Text: And he said unto them, What have I done now in comparison of you? Is not the gleaning of the grapes of Ephraim better than the vintage of Abiezer?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5246c581-311c-4c09-aaf1-eb6741d38325>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: JDG 8:3
Text: God hath delivered into your hands the princes of Midian, Oreb and Zeeb: and what was I able to do in comparison of you? Then their anger was abated toward him, when he had said that.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:744a5edd-eaaa-4e5a-b8cc-a851a77ae9f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: JDG 8:4
Text: And Gideon came to Jordan, and passed over, he, and the three hundred men that were with him, faint, yet pursuing them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2edc5df3-8799-4fa8-bb02-622446912919>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: JDG 8:5
Text: And he said unto the men of Succoth, Give, I pray you, loaves of bread unto the people that follow me; for they be faint, and I am pursuing after Zebah and Zalmunna, kings of Midian.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9451e73b-39bf-49ec-abde-8b751805f61b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: JDG 8:6
Text: And the princes of Succoth said, Are the hands of Zebah and Zalmunna now in thine hand, that we should give bread unto thine army?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c92e8f8-9067-46e2-9ab0-801fe3015acd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: JDG 8:7
Text: And Gideon said, Therefore when the LORD hath delivered Zebah and Zalmunna into mine hand, then I will tear your flesh with the thorns of the wilderness and with briers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc69ddd2-a975-4111-846c-5b2feb3713ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: JDG 8:8
Text: And he went up thence to Penuel, and spake unto them likewise: and the men of Penuel answered him as the men of Succoth had answered him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8becb7ff-58d9-4342-869a-24de898262a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: JDG 8:9
Text: And he spake also unto the men of Penuel, saying, When I come again in peace, I will break down this tower.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1471fa56-f346-4162-ab7c-3822b9def0be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: JDG 8:10
Text: Now Zebah and Zalmunna were in Karkor, and their hosts with them, about fifteen thousand men, all that were left of all the hosts of the children of the east: for there fell an hundred and twenty thousand men that drew sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73497010-8d8a-4575-94e6-732cdb956eab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: JDG 8:11
Text: And Gideon went up by the way of them that dwelt in tents on the east of Nobah and Jogbehah, and smote the host; for the host was secure.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed32c930-f33a-438d-904c-3a46202c0f84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: JDG 8:12
Text: And when Zebah and Zalmunna fled, he pursued after them, and took the two kings of Midian, Zebah and Zalmunna, and discomfited all the host.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bbc2d5a5-256b-4689-be20-71174daffa91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: JDG 8:13
Text: And Gideon the son of Joash returned from battle before the sun was up,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7b4d1fa-270c-445f-93c5-b0d3a3623be1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: JDG 8:14
Text: And caught a young man of the men of Succoth, and enquired of him: and he described unto him the princes of Succoth, and the elders thereof, even threescore and seventeen men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:100696dc-ba9d-4fbf-b7e1-c191db4c7461>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: JDG 8:15
Text: And he came unto the men of Succoth, and said, Behold Zebah and Zalmunna, with whom ye did upbraid me, saying, Are the hands of Zebah and Zalmunna now in thine hand, that we should give bread unto thy men that are weary?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07dcfd91-16ba-459a-a1be-bb97605fbe73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: JDG 8:16
Text: And he took the elders of the city, and thorns of the wilderness and briers, and with them he taught the men of Succoth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d4f4423-136c-4c8d-8776-39569f794a7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: JDG 8:17
Text: And he beat down the tower of Penuel, and slew the men of the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26b8ebd5-87b5-4808-bc62-70f97c6259da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: JDG 8:18
Text: Then said he unto Zebah and Zalmunna, What manner of men were they whom ye slew at Tabor? And they answered, As thou art, so were they; each one resembled the children of a king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b2a29f2-dd8c-4120-950c-18b10f7defc7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: JDG 8:19
Text: And he said, They were my brethren, even the sons of my mother: as the LORD liveth, if ye had saved them alive, I would not slay you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:feb19215-aae9-4593-801e-36cef91dd52f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: JDG 8:20
Text: And he said unto Jether his firstborn, Up, and slay them. But the youth drew not his sword: for he feared, because he was yet a youth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3e137c1-0b8a-4fc6-a4f3-0ac11eca324a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: JDG 8:21
Text: Then Zebah and Zalmunna said, Rise thou, and fall upon us: for as the man is, so is his strength. And Gideon arose, and slew Zebah and Zalmunna, and took away the ornaments that were on their camels’ necks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e40758f-7d91-488a-8aa0-883d48baa229>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: JDG 8:22
Text: Then the men of Israel said unto Gideon, Rule thou over us, both thou, and thy son, and thy son’s son also: for thou hast delivered us from the hand of Midian.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff8e3542-89ea-4e98-b5fa-9b37d316f48d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: JDG 8:23
Text: And Gideon said unto them, I will not rule over you, neither shall my son rule over you: the LORD shall rule over you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4cef093-2258-49c7-9bd1-0c4acfb15255>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: JDG 8:24
Text: And Gideon said unto them, I would desire a request of you, that ye would give me every man the earrings of his prey. (For they had golden earrings, because they were Ishmaelites.)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55194cd7-6315-4009-a8a2-bed5dc5f29d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: JDG 8:25
Text: And they answered, We will willingly give them. And they spread a garment, and did cast therein every man the earrings of his prey.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76a733d1-acec-45a8-81fb-a1046aab4386>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: JDG 8:26
Text: And the weight of the golden earrings that he requested was a thousand and seven hundred shekels of gold; beside ornaments, and collars, and purple raiment that was on the kings of Midian, and beside the chains that were about their camels’ necks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:459a1dec-97d6-4e6d-a17e-58bcaf6b7ebb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: JDG 8:27
Text: And Gideon made an ephod thereof, and put it in his city, even in Ophrah: and all Israel went thither a whoring after it: which thing became a snare unto Gideon, and to his house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f813a581-0d9a-4f46-ae2c-323d14fc1d8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: JDG 8:28
Text: Thus was Midian subdued before the children of Israel, so that they lifted up their heads no more. And the country was in quietness forty years in the days of Gideon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eed5e965-ef21-49b3-9b1e-ba43633cacd9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: JDG 8:29
Text: And Jerubbaal the son of Joash went and dwelt in his own house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25d4b7c0-a6b3-4583-84ac-55c36f04427e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: JDG 8:30
Text: And Gideon had threescore and ten sons of his body begotten: for he had many wives.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf79f2a1-a07f-43e9-96c2-1b9a2d330aab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: JDG 8:31
Text: And his concubine that was in Shechem, she also bare him a son, whose name he called Abimelech.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9db7210-e223-4751-bcb7-d245f0f68521>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: JDG 8:32
Text: And Gideon the son of Joash died in a good old age, and was buried in the sepulchre of Joash his father, in Ophrah of the Abiezrites.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7551d30e-fdac-4569-adde-26b8b9517728>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: JDG 8:33
Text: And it came to pass, as soon as Gideon was dead, that the children of Israel turned again, and went a whoring after Baalim, and made Baalberith their god.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a717b585-0e47-4e14-9eca-ed480cb101f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: JDG 8:34
Text: And the children of Israel remembered not the LORD their God, who had delivered them out of the hands of all their enemies on every side:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/8/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8505fc0f-3962-4908-9f9a-aa31d722a949>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: JDG 8:35
Text: Neither shewed they kindness to the house of Jerubbaal, namely, Gideon, according to all the goodness which he had shewed unto Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa2b2772-e0de-4030-afc9-f190210ab53f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: JDG 9:1
Text: And Abimelech the son of Jerubbaal went to Shechem unto his mother’s brethren, and communed with them, and with all the family of the house of his mother’s father, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ce2cfda-b9cb-4f27-9166-d2c4a55655e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 281

Reference: JDG 9:2
Text: Speak, I pray you, in the ears of all the men of Shechem, Whether is better for you, either that all the sons of Jerubbaal, which are threescore and ten persons, reign over you, or that one reign over you? remember also that I am your bone and your flesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0706450-21c4-4c5b-9831-a1abe766fb50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: JDG 9:3
Text: And his mother’s brethren spake of him in the ears of all the men of Shechem all these words: and their hearts inclined to follow Abimelech; for they said, He is our brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46e078d1-fe4b-483f-924a-fe13e3094609>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: JDG 9:4
Text: And they gave him threescore and ten pieces of silver out of the house of Baalberith, wherewith Abimelech hired vain and light persons, which followed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32c1775a-1a71-494a-bffe-6b2f6ca42aa9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: JDG 9:5
Text: And he went unto his father’s house at Ophrah, and slew his brethren the sons of Jerubbaal, being threescore and ten persons, upon one stone: notwithstanding yet Jotham the youngest son of Jerubbaal was left; for he hid himself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:447c1c8c-1719-4194-9773-981571257006>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JDG 9:6
Text: And all the men of Shechem gathered together, and all the house of Millo, and went, and made Abimelech king, by the plain of the pillar that was in Shechem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17292df3-e72a-4898-a894-6d7d9391f189>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: JDG 9:7
Text: And when they told it to Jotham, he went and stood in the top of mount Gerizim, and lifted up his voice, and cried, and said unto them, Hearken unto me, ye men of Shechem, that God may hearken unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:353ee7be-2341-4ce8-9334-5b8b7acbe3a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: JDG 9:8
Text: The trees went forth on a time to anoint a king over them; and they said unto the olive tree, Reign thou over us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44058fdd-7c6d-4d33-8756-6c795946785e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: JDG 9:9
Text: But the olive tree said unto them, Should I leave my fatness, wherewith by me they honour God and man, and go to be promoted over the trees?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42ef36d1-3c56-425e-b777-d1ef8627cbab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: JDG 9:10
Text: And the trees said to the fig tree, Come thou, and reign over us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d97cbdd-8b2a-4f09-bead-38af064f3a7a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: JDG 9:11
Text: But the fig tree said unto them, Should I forsake my sweetness, and my good fruit, and go to be promoted over the trees?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f824818-0a09-4a1c-a499-5d2b1ebca8a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: JDG 9:12
Text: Then said the trees unto the vine, Come thou, and reign over us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7496e076-9010-4e08-9a13-5a64abe3ddf2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: JDG 9:13
Text: And the vine said unto them, Should I leave my wine, which cheereth God and man, and go to be promoted over the trees?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47063167-890f-47cc-805b-7dcd4c8a97ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: JDG 9:14
Text: Then said all the trees unto the bramble, Come thou, and reign over us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89764b8c-727d-4688-b04d-eaca6ab46cf7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: JDG 9:15
Text: And the bramble said unto the trees, If in truth ye anoint me king over you, then come and put your trust in my shadow: and if not, let fire come out of the bramble, and devour the cedars of Lebanon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:023e76b3-52f5-4ad6-8829-6c87dd76b6a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: JDG 9:16
Text: Now therefore, if ye have done truly and sincerely, in that ye have made Abimelech king, and if ye have dealt well with Jerubbaal and his house, and have done unto him according to the deserving of his hands;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d139d0f2-acdc-43ef-a490-44657b4843b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: JDG 9:17
Text: (For my father fought for you, and adventured his life far, and delivered you out of the hand of Midian:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3bd99c6c-64a1-4d5e-80b1-c126c2890397>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: JDG 9:18
Text: And ye are risen up against my father’s house this day, and have slain his sons, threescore and ten persons, upon one stone, and have made Abimelech, the son of his maidservant, king over the men of Shechem, because he is your brother;)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41f32a29-afe1-4970-b1ec-bd465eee8eee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: JDG 9:19
Text: If ye then have dealt truly and sincerely with Jerubbaal and with his house this day, then rejoice ye in Abimelech, and let him also rejoice in you:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5ce50d4-5dfd-4304-a507-766da500d2d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: JDG 9:20
Text: But if not, let fire come out from Abimelech, and devour the men of Shechem, and the house of Millo; and let fire come out from the men of Shechem, and from the house of Millo, and devour Abimelech.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:614a1f18-1e6f-4698-beb4-35f16c7972bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: JDG 9:21
Text: And Jotham ran away, and fled, and went to Beer, and dwelt there, for fear of Abimelech his brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8959da20-7013-439c-8096-5738a6d98e3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: JDG 9:22
Text: When Abimelech had reigned three years over Israel,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8ea0013-1811-498c-8ac1-78254c0919f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: JDG 9:23
Text: Then God sent an evil spirit between Abimelech and the men of Shechem; and the men of Shechem dealt treacherously with Abimelech:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de842435-3284-449c-ba95-8fd56268e6ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: JDG 9:24
Text: That the cruelty done to the threescore and ten sons of Jerubbaal might come, and their blood be laid upon Abimelech their brother, which slew them; and upon the men of Shechem, which aided him in the killing of his brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e064339-5b39-45ba-a30f-0c6f31d099f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JDG 9:25
Text: And the men of Shechem set liers in wait for him in the top of the mountains, and they robbed all that came along that way by them: and it was told Abimelech.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d359160-0fd6-4316-b31b-81e77b129553>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: JDG 9:26
Text: And Gaal the son of Ebed came with his brethren, and went over to Shechem: and the men of Shechem put their confidence in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:304d8161-b561-4cd4-94d6-13dda6ffc03d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: JDG 9:27
Text: And they went out into the fields, and gathered their vineyards, and trode the grapes, and made merry, and went into the house of their god, and did eat and drink, and cursed Abimelech.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e96e8d5-3008-4f04-b2b3-d28f1a99ed80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: JDG 9:28
Text: And Gaal the son of Ebed said, Who is Abimelech, and who is Shechem, that we should serve him? is not he the son of Jerubbaal? and Zebul his officer? serve the men of Hamor the father of Shechem: for why should we serve him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30c7331e-769c-4498-a6a4-c19395e4e722>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: JDG 9:29
Text: And would to God this people were under my hand! then would I remove Abimelech. And he said to Abimelech, Increase thine army, and come out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b4c1700-ab83-4c6d-b33c-ce6d529bd65c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: JDG 9:30
Text: And when Zebul the ruler of the city heard the words of Gaal the son of Ebed, his anger was kindled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d9b690d-6ea8-47bc-beda-2eb13a884c52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: JDG 9:31
Text: And he sent messengers unto Abimelech privily, saying, Behold, Gaal the son of Ebed and his brethren be come to Shechem; and, behold, they fortify the city against thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1aecf94-86f3-47e6-a56e-5eb00cc0ed9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: JDG 9:32
Text: Now therefore up by night, thou and the people that is with thee, and lie in wait in the field:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1994b48e-519c-4fb9-949c-08bb465059c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: JDG 9:33
Text: And it shall be, that in the morning, as soon as the sun is up, thou shalt rise early, and set upon the city: and, behold, when he and the people that is with him come out against thee, then mayest thou do to them as thou shalt find occasion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d056f05-14c7-4e78-892d-4e258bc8f654>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: JDG 9:34
Text: And Abimelech rose up, and all the people that were with him, by night, and they laid wait against Shechem in four companies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8ae3787-f03f-4d1f-ab1e-080fe1372cba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: JDG 9:35
Text: And Gaal the son of Ebed went out, and stood in the entering of the gate of the city: and Abimelech rose up, and the people that were with him, from lying in wait.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:887740c6-069a-4330-b5a6-4695ab4e5d7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: JDG 9:36
Text: And when Gaal saw the people, he said to Zebul, Behold, there come people down from the top of the mountains. And Zebul said unto him, Thou seest the shadow of the mountains as if they were men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed96fc85-a43c-4bb9-990c-5b087089ea38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: JDG 9:37
Text: And Gaal spake again, and said, See there come people down by the middle of the land, and another company come along by the plain of Meonenim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:173de420-c71b-46d5-8932-4b5a2ae816cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: JDG 9:38
Text: Then said Zebul unto him, Where is now thy mouth, wherewith thou saidst, Who is Abimelech, that we should serve him? is not this the people that thou hast despised? go out, I pray now, and fight with them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6773dd2f-cfe7-4ace-9571-02ac57e80346>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: JDG 9:39
Text: And Gaal went out before the men of Shechem, and fought with Abimelech.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3c37b1f-68e9-4da4-b386-8aa677f6cd6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: JDG 9:40
Text: And Abimelech chased him, and he fled before him, and many were overthrown and wounded, even unto the entering of the gate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35847986-47b0-4e7f-93b7-ad145b0ef7dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: JDG 9:41
Text: And Abimelech dwelt at Arumah: and Zebul thrust out Gaal and his brethren, that they should not dwell in Shechem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ecef5830-ec35-4311-a51b-d8c1ff303894>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: JDG 9:42
Text: And it came to pass on the morrow, that the people went out into the field; and they told Abimelech.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82422364-5cf4-46a5-ab74-837aab2ef875>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: JDG 9:43
Text: And he took the people, and divided them into three companies, and laid wait in the field, and looked, and, behold, the people were come forth out of the city; and he rose up against them, and smote them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1684cd22-52d5-4eaf-9fa6-f47585abe017>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: JDG 9:44
Text: And Abimelech, and the company that was with him, rushed forward, and stood in the entering of the gate of the city: and the two other companies ran upon all the people that were in the fields, and slew them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9058c132-7ae7-4c67-a133-a3c186952459>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: JDG 9:45
Text: And Abimelech fought against the city all that day; and he took the city, and slew the people that was therein, and beat down the city, and sowed it with salt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:954b0e3b-3ddf-4c61-b73b-a6e29c034997>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: JDG 9:46
Text: And when all the men of the tower of Shechem heard that, they entered into an hold of the house of the god Berith.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4136525-e8c6-44d3-9e3e-6afc69550af6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: JDG 9:47
Text: And it was told Abimelech, that all the men of the tower of Shechem were gathered together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0324dc3d-9684-45e4-bc10-290d462ecfdf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 333

Reference: JDG 9:48
Text: And Abimelech gat him up to mount Zalmon, he and all the people that were with him; and Abimelech took an axe in his hand, and cut down a bough from the trees, and took it, and laid it on his shoulder, and said unto the people that were with him, What ye have seen me do, make haste, and do as I have done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de57613d-4b19-43db-a746-0fb13bd8ef69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: JDG 9:49
Text: And all the people likewise cut down every man his bough, and followed Abimelech, and put them to the hold, and set the hold on fire upon them; so that all the men of the tower of Shechem died also, about a thousand men and women.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0ef0768-7d39-4653-bc1e-9649c37892a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: JDG 9:50
Text: Then went Abimelech to Thebez, and encamped against Thebez, and took it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb3302e8-3cdf-47e2-9b0c-a7fbf245b131>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: JDG 9:51
Text: But there was a strong tower within the city, and thither fled all the men and women, and all they of the city, and shut it to them, and gat them up to the top of the tower.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd781054-1676-4c1b-99cc-da8254b08828>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: JDG 9:52
Text: And Abimelech came unto the tower, and fought against it, and went hard unto the door of the tower to burn it with fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67e8d731-7be9-4833-b2bd-46e8d1e1f87c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: JDG 9:53
Text: And a certain woman cast a piece of a millstone upon Abimelech’s head, and all to brake his skull.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3feed99-2b83-469a-bec4-a27aef625720>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: JDG 9:54
Text: Then he called hastily unto the young man his armourbearer, and said unto him, Draw thy sword, and slay me, that men say not of me, A women slew him. And his young man thrust him through, and he died.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/55
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37a93cde-2074-4b5d-a3eb-2a98c2160b2b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: JDG 9:55
Text: And when the men of Israel saw that Abimelech was dead, they departed every man unto his place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/56
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:249f80cd-66ce-4b79-bbc4-cd43ca8cd48d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: JDG 9:56
Text: Thus God rendered the wickedness of Abimelech, which he did unto his father, in slaying his seventy brethren:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/9/57
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:930bfd37-0c02-4db4-bfd9-5c7bcd7c3caf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: JDG 9:57
Text: And all the evil of the men of Shechem did God render upon their heads: and upon them came the curse of Jotham the son of Jerubbaal.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/10/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:609d1d68-8142-4f40-b84e-573f021aa5f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: JDG 10:1
Text: And after Abimelech there arose to defend Israel Tola the son of Puah, the son of Dodo, a man of Issachar; and he dwelt in Shamir in mount Ephraim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/10/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26c932f3-4837-453d-8395-aa823f148a3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: JDG 10:2
Text: And he judged Israel twenty and three years, and died, and was buried in Shamir.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/10/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6960736c-64b6-479b-b98a-a41a04676637>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: JDG 10:3
Text: And after him arose Jair, a Gileadite, and judged Israel twenty and two years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/10/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47951244-d867-4001-83c6-b7a8f3acd5e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: JDG 10:4
Text: And he had thirty sons that rode on thirty ass colts, and they had thirty cities, which are called Havothjair unto this day, which are in the land of Gilead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/10/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47d2b9db-3cb2-4726-9f47-20473326f0f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 66

Reference: JDG 10:5
Text: And Jair died, and was buried in Camon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/10/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9ede560-0541-4aef-a06f-fbf52a8cf0ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 310

Reference: JDG 10:6
Text: And the children of Israel did evil again in the sight of the LORD, and served Baalim, and Ashtaroth, and the gods of Syria, and the gods of Zidon, and the gods of Moab, and the gods of the children of Ammon, and the gods of the Philistines, and forsook the LORD, and served not him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/10/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3bd8c6e8-5295-4d0d-b47c-d256fa9ce2d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: JDG 10:7
Text: And the anger of the LORD was hot against Israel, and he sold them into the hands of the Philistines, and into the hands of the children of Ammon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/10/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b104839-5437-4ecb-90f6-053ff76519e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: JDG 10:8
Text: And that year they vexed and oppressed the children of Israel: eighteen years, all the children of Israel that were on the other side Jordan in the land of the Amorites, which is in Gilead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/10/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:721ac498-0293-4a63-9886-ef395b4586d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: JDG 10:9
Text: Moreover the children of Ammon passed over Jordan to fight also against Judah, and against Benjamin, and against the house of Ephraim; so that Israel was sore distressed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/10/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75c52e0b-1276-475b-997d-9dcad188a5ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: JDG 10:10
Text: And the children of Israel cried unto the LORD, saying, We have sinned against thee, both because we have forsaken our God, and also served Baalim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/10/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6df6789c-4be4-4c0c-95b4-8c89d4972da6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: JDG 10:11
Text: And the LORD said unto the children of Israel, Did not I deliver you from the Egyptians, and from the Amorites, from the children of Ammon, and from the Philistines?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/10/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4cc319bb-a57d-4029-965d-b756a24f3b64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: JDG 10:12
Text: The Zidonians also, and the Amalekites, and the Maonites, did oppress you; and ye cried to me, and I delivered you out of their hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/10/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c21dc44e-591e-4372-af96-57b15ddf7686>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: JDG 10:13
Text: Yet ye have forsaken me, and served other gods: wherefore I will deliver you no more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/10/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b79c5143-a905-46b6-bf3f-9aaa0af7e904>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: JDG 10:14
Text: Go and cry unto the gods which ye have chosen; let them deliver you in the time of your tribulation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/10/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ab504a5-e624-48a6-a1f7-d3206b10811e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JDG 10:15
Text: And the children of Israel said unto the LORD, We have sinned: do thou unto us whatsoever seemeth good unto thee; deliver us only, we pray thee, this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/10/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6cbe8f31-4bb7-4d41-81f4-428304b31808>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: JDG 10:16
Text: And they put away the strange gods from among them, and served the LORD: and his soul was grieved for the misery of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/10/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ceb5e35c-f318-4855-b26f-41a7fbab73e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: JDG 10:17
Text: Then the children of Ammon were gathered together, and encamped in Gilead. And the children of Israel assembled themselves together, and encamped in Mizpeh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/10/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0212bbe-3eb6-4cd1-ba32-15fcac6b0417>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: JDG 10:18
Text: And the people and princes of Gilead said one to another, What man is he that will begin to fight against the children of Ammon? he shall be head over all the inhabitants of Gilead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1b33c3e-fdee-41b9-9f1d-647200bdc70e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: JDG 11:1
Text: Now Jephthah the Gileadite was a mighty man of valour, and he was the son of an harlot: and Gilead begat Jephthah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6656615-dfee-4623-9ac8-3dea7f70485f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: JDG 11:2
Text: And Gilead’s wife bare him sons; and his wife’s sons grew up, and they thrust out Jephthah, and said unto him, Thou shalt not inherit in our father’s house; for thou art the son of a strange woman.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e00aa642-0531-42e3-89bf-0b7e92863abd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: JDG 11:3
Text: Then Jephthah fled from his brethren, and dwelt in the land of Tob: and there were gathered vain men to Jephthah, and went out with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:358d1e16-3738-4e7c-866d-946751447410>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: JDG 11:4
Text: And it came to pass in process of time, that the children of Ammon made war against Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90b8f19e-3785-4ff3-9409-55d032dd91c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: JDG 11:5
Text: And it was so, that when the children of Ammon made war against Israel, the elders of Gilead went to fetch Jephthah out of the land of Tob:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e20c8280-d7b8-4c5f-8cac-9d38df146bff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: JDG 11:6
Text: And they said unto Jephthah, Come, and be our captain, that we may fight with the children of Ammon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc4e1290-309f-4c57-adb1-83e81449501a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: JDG 11:7
Text: And Jephthah said unto the elders of Gilead, Did not ye hate me, and expel me out of my father’s house? and why are ye come unto me now when ye are in distress?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4ba8b6d-b5c8-414a-a5c5-a1a80bc29147>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: JDG 11:8
Text: And the elders of Gilead said unto Jephthah, Therefore we turn again to thee now, that thou mayest go with us, and fight against the children of Ammon, and be our head over all the inhabitants of Gilead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a28578c-d176-47c1-92a9-acb99142b27f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: JDG 11:9
Text: And Jephthah said unto the elders of Gilead, If ye bring me home again to fight against the children of Ammon, and the LORD deliver them before me, shall I be your head?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64ab272e-b9eb-4656-a4d4-bd62d98b6b2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: JDG 11:10
Text: And the elders of Gilead said unto Jephthah, The LORD be witness between us, if we do not so according to thy words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5136f20-d8ad-4bb1-b3f1-ce492dfb93d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: JDG 11:11
Text: Then Jephthah went with the elders of Gilead, and the people made him head and captain over them: and Jephthah uttered all his words before the LORD in Mizpeh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3bb7e03f-6b33-43a4-a41b-0d40f9045bcc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JDG 11:12
Text: And Jephthah sent messengers unto the king of the children of Ammon, saying, What hast thou to do with me, that thou art come against me to fight in my land?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6fa72891-6163-4dbc-98fb-8d4bd25bd87b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: JDG 11:13
Text: And the king of the children of Ammon answered unto the messengers of Jephthah, Because Israel took away my land, when they came up out of Egypt, from Arnon even unto Jabbok, and unto Jordan: now therefore restore those lands again peaceably.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:028c2b9e-d3c1-41a8-a244-186c34600443>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: JDG 11:14
Text: And Jephthah sent messengers again unto the king of the children of Ammon:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d59f0070-36a6-4529-8c9c-7fd89d8458f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: JDG 11:15
Text: And said unto him, Thus saith Jephthah, Israel took not away the land of Moab, nor the land of the children of Ammon:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64344285-34e9-4bd0-bffe-2450fffbabe7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: JDG 11:16
Text: But when Israel came up from Egypt, and walked through the wilderness unto the Red sea, and came to Kadesh;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93d07f0c-fd37-4cc6-9a57-21b07263cf3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: JDG 11:17
Text: Then Israel sent messengers unto the king of Edom, saying, Let me, I pray thee, pass through thy land: but the king of Edom would not hearken thereto. And in like manner they sent unto the king of Moab: but he would not consent: and Israel abode in Kadesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa04ab4a-555e-444b-a45a-b98a51572e52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 287

Reference: JDG 11:18
Text: Then they went along through the wilderness, and compassed the land of Edom, and the land of Moab, and came by the east side of the land of Moab, and pitched on the other side of Arnon, but came not within the border of Moab: for Arnon was the border of Moab.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6047ad8c-ec81-4009-aee3-cb89555c13be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: JDG 11:19
Text: And Israel sent messengers unto Sihon king of the Amorites, the king of Heshbon; and Israel said unto him, Let us pass, we pray thee, through thy land into my place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23e9e7df-7f84-4356-9c5e-f21353d97712>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: JDG 11:20
Text: But Sihon trusted not Israel to pass through his coast: but Sihon gathered all his people together, and pitched in Jahaz, and fought against Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b7f097c-6a1e-4ec7-8d2f-4f417aee3aaf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: JDG 11:21
Text: And the LORD God of Israel delivered Sihon and all his people into the hand of Israel, and they smote them: so Israel possessed all the land of the Amorites, the inhabitants of that country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de29c8fa-6e7c-4c12-9fa1-21c7bc84624e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: JDG 11:22
Text: And they possessed all the coasts of the Amorites, from Arnon even unto Jabbok, and from the wilderness even unto Jordan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a57d8c4-a744-4f30-81a0-d5334e171967>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: JDG 11:23
Text: So now the LORD God of Israel hath dispossessed the Amorites from before his people Israel, and shouldest thou possess it?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bcd6162d-6c7a-4d02-b93b-f8b300312a82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JDG 11:24
Text: Wilt not thou possess that which Chemosh thy god giveth thee to possess? So whomsoever the LORD our God shall drive out from before us, them will we possess.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:014e4eb8-654c-4b85-959b-3e20c062f5f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: JDG 11:25
Text: And now art thou any thing better than Balak the son of Zippor, king of Moab? did he ever strive against Israel, or did he ever fight against them,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08ed092a-fad9-43b4-8491-acb0410738db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: JDG 11:26
Text: While Israel dwelt in Heshbon and her towns, and in Aroer and her towns, and in all the cities that be along by the coasts of Arnon, three hundred years? why therefore did ye not recover them within that time?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0c6876d-61f8-44e4-ac35-5eb8775bd94c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: JDG 11:27
Text: Wherefore I have not sinned against thee, but thou doest me wrong to war against me: the LORD the Judge be judge this day between the children of Israel and the children of Ammon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24d990d8-1535-464e-b1f9-37c523ca5086>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: JDG 11:28
Text: Howbeit the king of the children of Ammon hearkened not unto the words of Jephthah which he sent him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75e49cd9-56cf-4881-8e4f-0b419317e92e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: JDG 11:29
Text: Then the Spirit of the LORD came upon Jephthah, and he passed over Gilead, and Manasseh, and passed over Mizpeh of Gilead, and from Mizpeh of Gilead he passed over unto the children of Ammon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fd27fac-94d6-407f-8039-c98d09db83f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: JDG 11:30
Text: And Jephthah vowed a vow unto the LORD, and said, If thou shalt without fail deliver the children of Ammon into mine hands,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:925930f3-7b11-494e-a136-3e67799b7348>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: JDG 11:31
Text: Then it shall be, that whatsoever cometh forth of the doors of my house to meet me, when I return in peace from the children of Ammon, shall surely be the LORD’s, and I will offer it up for a burnt offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b8fb993-d383-4abd-918d-72fbedc9fc10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: JDG 11:32
Text: So Jephthah passed over unto the children of Ammon to fight against them; and the LORD delivered them into his hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57cb43bf-c06f-4542-8f53-20bedd24d0af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: JDG 11:33
Text: And he smote them from Aroer, even till thou come to Minnith, even twenty cities, and unto the plain of the vineyards, with a very great slaughter. Thus the children of Ammon were subdued before the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37424d00-f874-418c-9c14-3ece14a32092>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: JDG 11:34
Text: And Jephthah came to Mizpeh unto his house, and, behold, his daughter came out to meet him with timbrels and with dances: and she was his only child; beside her he had neither son nor daughter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3deb404f-a2b8-46e2-b091-5ffaf4f56af9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: JDG 11:35
Text: And it came to pass, when he saw her, that he rent his clothes, and said, Alas, my daughter! thou hast brought me very low, and thou art one of them that trouble me: for I have opened my mouth unto the LORD, and I cannot go back.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02b8f939-6d65-4446-bdfe-15f727cba167>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 273

Reference: JDG 11:36
Text: And she said unto him, My father, if thou hast opened thy mouth unto the LORD, do to me according to that which hath proceeded out of thy mouth; forasmuch as the LORD hath taken vengeance for thee of thine enemies, even of the children of Ammon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afa7b0b8-13f9-44b1-b7e8-d611ca58d719>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: JDG 11:37
Text: And she said unto her father, Let this thing be done for me: let me alone two months, that I may go up and down upon the mountains, and bewail my virginity, I and my fellows.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:822c9dd3-5081-4751-8c99-7aa42414ad2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: JDG 11:38
Text: And he said, Go. And he sent her away for two months: and she went with her companions, and bewailed her virginity upon the mountains.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3bb8ddee-bdae-4883-8d10-f8ae2439163b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: JDG 11:39
Text: And it came to pass at the end of two months, that she returned unto her father, who did with her according to his vow which he had vowed: and she knew no man. And it was a custom in Israel,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/11/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac6ef9f8-3633-44a0-a928-d5a4718dd9e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: JDG 11:40
Text: That the daughters of Israel went yearly to lament the daughter of Jephthah the Gileadite four days in a year.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/12/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05d461cb-8046-439c-8cf8-179fed779fc2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 277

Reference: JDG 12:1
Text: And the men of Ephraim gathered themselves together, and went northward, and said unto Jephthah, Wherefore passedst thou over to fight against the children of Ammon, and didst not call us to go with thee? we will burn thine house upon thee with fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/12/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b719eab-5847-4429-b358-131b9eb33f51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: JDG 12:2
Text: And Jephthah said unto them, I and my people were at great strife with the children of Ammon; and when I called you, ye delivered me not out of their hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/12/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea50b391-c0fe-4112-8021-b795672b895b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: JDG 12:3
Text: And when I saw that ye delivered me not, I put my life in my hands, and passed over against the children of Ammon, and the LORD delivered them into my hand: wherefore then are ye come up unto me this day, to fight against me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/12/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49afa679-cf0a-49fb-9a83-85cad819e638>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: JDG 12:4
Text: Then Jephthah gathered together all the men of Gilead, and fought with Ephraim: and the men of Gilead smote Ephraim, because they said, Ye Gileadites are fugitives of Ephraim among the Ephraimites, and among the Manassites.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/12/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93bef0d6-9850-4fbb-9e54-23e93c03414b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: JDG 12:5
Text: And the Gileadites took the passages of Jordan before the Ephraimites: and it was so, that when those Ephraimites which were escaped said, Let me go over; that the men of Gilead said unto him, Art thou an Ephraimite? If he said, Nay;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/12/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e6d1ecc-4242-487d-93c2-ae55a14359d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: JDG 12:6
Text: Then said they unto him, Say now Shibboleth: and he said Sibboleth: for he could not frame to pronounce it right. Then they took him, and slew him at the passages of Jordan: and there fell at that time of the Ephraimites forty and two thousand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/12/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c37abb6e-7928-4816-b71b-6521ba6948d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: JDG 12:7
Text: And Jephthah judged Israel six years. Then died Jephthah the Gileadite, and was buried in one of the cities of Gilead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/12/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd0df369-4301-4698-a8bc-2a6103fe156f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: JDG 12:8
Text: And after him Ibzan of Bethlehem judged Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/12/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b177823-c6ba-484e-9eee-4ac365946bc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JDG 12:9
Text: And he had thirty sons, and thirty daughters, whom he sent abroad, and took in thirty daughters from abroad for his sons. And he judged Israel seven years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/12/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c11fb67-92e5-4122-b810-a2b5913c11ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: JDG 12:10
Text: Then died Ibzan, and was buried at Bethlehem.


