Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: JDG 13:2
Text: And there was a certain man of Zorah, of the family of the Danites, whose name was Manoah; and his wife was barren, and bare not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/13/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e499a5aa-a559-478b-abe3-d21f06283930>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: JDG 13:3
Text: And the angel of the LORD appeared unto the woman, and said unto her, Behold now, thou art barren, and bearest not: but thou shalt conceive, and bear a son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/13/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2421b538-efbe-4eff-bf53-70f03137bf9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: JDG 13:4
Text: Now therefore beware, I pray thee, and drink not wine nor strong drink, and eat not any unclean thing:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/13/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4e2fb8d-6230-44df-8949-849bc0ed6626>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: JDG 13:5
Text: For, lo, thou shalt conceive, and bear a son; and no razor shall come on his head: for the child shall be a Nazarite unto God from the womb: and he shall begin to deliver Israel out of the hand of the Philistines.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/13/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3d12ab5-2382-4d94-ac44-bcc1f1c2fea7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: JDG 13:6
Text: Then the woman came and told her husband, saying, A man of God came unto me, and his countenance was like the countenance of an angel of God, very terrible: but I asked him not whence he was, neither told he me his name:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/13/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:524e090e-5dcf-4899-b511-48a41d6c50f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: JDG 13:7
Text: But he said unto me, Behold, thou shalt conceive, and bear a son; and now drink no wine nor strong drink, neither eat any unclean thing: for the child shall be a Nazarite to God from the womb to the day of his death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/13/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0763c189-eded-4899-bb27-d1762d2c4eda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: JDG 13:8
Text: Then Manoah intreated the LORD, and said, O my Lord, let the man of God which thou didst send come again unto us, and teach us what we shall do unto the child that shall be born.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/13/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e6a16da-597d-41f9-8c38-987e473a7ee4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: JDG 13:9
Text: And God hearkened to the voice of Manoah; and the angel of God came again unto the woman as she sat in the field: but Manoah her husband was not with her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/13/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e211803-92ad-45e2-9f98-50566d802743>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: JDG 13:10
Text: And the woman made haste, and ran, and shewed her husband, and said unto him, Behold, the man hath appeared unto me, that came unto me the other day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/13/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ece82e95-a494-4ed1-b85a-c829cc64b4f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: JDG 13:11
Text: And Manoah arose, and went after his wife, and came to the man, and said unto him, Art thou the man that spakest unto the woman? And he said, I am.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/13/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6122da45-a79f-4396-8747-18dddc941b3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: JDG 13:12
Text: And Manoah said, Now let thy words come to pass. How shall we order the child, and how shall we do unto him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/13/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86a7a6e5-8a0b-46a4-a600-e5b30e1955a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: JDG 13:13
Text: And the angel of the LORD said unto Manoah, Of all that I said unto the woman let her beware.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/13/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01a59dd2-6ad7-4fe7-b21c-02a76caa0c2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: JDG 13:14
Text: She may not eat of any thing that cometh of the vine, neither let her drink wine or strong drink, nor eat any unclean thing: all that I commanded her let her observe.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/13/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84e7128a-d3ba-4456-9519-5563e8b43a58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: JDG 13:15
Text: And Manoah said unto the angel of the LORD, I pray thee, let us detain thee, until we shall have made ready a kid for thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/13/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f13fc533-4409-4c24-b999-909a92024a97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: JDG 13:16
Text: And the angel of the LORD said unto Manoah, Though thou detain me, I will not eat of thy bread: and if thou wilt offer a burnt offering, thou must offer it unto the LORD. For Manoah knew not that he was an angel of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/13/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5ad90dd-b5c0-4932-b8e7-0130bc58432b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: JDG 13:17
Text: And Manoah said unto the angel of the LORD, What is thy name, that when thy sayings come to pass we may do thee honour?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/13/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:602c7f8d-e0a2-406f-9103-2be42e73c586>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: JDG 13:18
Text: And the angel of the LORD said unto him, Why askest thou thus after my name, seeing it is secret?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/13/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e04dee7d-6119-4cf2-bc9b-c441de56ab56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: JDG 13:19
Text: So Manoah took a kid with a meat offering, and offered it upon a rock unto the LORD: and the angel did wonderously; and Manoah and his wife looked on.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/13/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e55f8f94-b829-4d82-a8af-aa3f75048af1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: JDG 13:20
Text: For it came to pass, when the flame went up toward heaven from off the altar, that the angel of the LORD ascended in the flame of the altar. And Manoah and his wife looked on it, and fell on their faces to the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/13/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aea1c799-2dd3-48a2-aa00-959a82a7da49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: JDG 13:21
Text: But the angel of the LORD did no more appear to Manoah and to his wife. Then Manoah knew that he was an angel of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/13/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3122f0af-3a71-4149-aff7-2455bf2b13b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: JDG 13:22
Text: And Manoah said unto his wife, We shall surely die, because we have seen God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/13/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31be5cdf-9c5c-404f-9dcf-654d3f8876bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 281

Reference: JDG 13:23
Text: But his wife said unto him, If the LORD were pleased to kill us, he would not have received a burnt offering and a meat offering at our hands, neither would he have shewed us all these things, nor would as at this time have told us such things as these.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/13/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e387e36a-0ada-4b5f-8c0b-45ce29c2bedf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: JDG 13:24
Text: And the woman bare a son, and called his name Samson: and the child grew, and the LORD blessed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/13/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59ea0645-ff18-49ca-9b4b-1cc7dd4360ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: JDG 13:25
Text: And the Spirit of the LORD began to move him at times in the camp of Dan between Zorah and Eshtaol.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/14/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba740bf4-f4a9-4360-b200-8c9d81e71c0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: JDG 14:1
Text: And Samson went down to Timnath, and saw a woman in Timnath of the daughters of the Philistines.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/14/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd6cb671-ed66-4ad3-8d4a-8a489854812d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: JDG 14:2
Text: And he came up, and told his father and his mother, and said, I have seen a woman in Timnath of the daughters of the Philistines: now therefore get her for me to wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/14/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd92bea6-ce41-46ad-b8b6-d0645e63deb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 296

Reference: JDG 14:3
Text: Then his father and his mother said unto him, Is there never a woman among the daughters of thy brethren, or among all my people, that thou goest to take a wife of the uncircumcised Philistines? And Samson said unto his father, Get her for me; for she pleaseth me well.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/14/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21dc3f19-f8d7-4917-8aa2-c5ad8e76b088>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: JDG 14:4
Text: But his father and his mother knew not that it was of the LORD, that he sought an occasion against the Philistines: for at that time the Philistines had dominion over Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/14/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af0944e6-a0fb-41cf-a67b-de2319c6d1fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: JDG 14:5
Text: Then went Samson down, and his father and his mother, to Timnath, and came to the vineyards of Timnath: and, behold, a young lion roared against him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/14/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6de6771a-d74d-4f7b-b130-ae2dc9817a63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: JDG 14:6
Text: And the Spirit of the LORD came mightily upon him, and he rent him as he would have rent a kid, and he had nothing in his hand: but he told not his father or his mother what he had done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/14/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffe8b57a-9588-407e-8379-5d1b7a9f7991>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: JDG 14:7
Text: And he went down, and talked with the woman; and she pleased Samson well.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/14/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:024411c9-9e11-4d2a-91db-687d6f83efed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: JDG 14:8
Text: And after a time he returned to take her, and he turned aside to see the carcase of the lion: and, behold, there was a swarm of bees and honey in the carcase of the lion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/14/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24f7bf17-7e0c-4a07-a1a2-4724a223205c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: JDG 14:9
Text: And he took thereof in his hands, and went on eating, and came to his father and mother, and he gave them, and they did eat: but he told not them that he had taken the honey out of the carcase of the lion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/14/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d40306a-45b0-4a4c-8ab0-6bbb537d95be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: JDG 14:10
Text: So his father went down unto the woman: and Samson made there a feast; for so used the young men to do.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/14/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84dba763-b8b4-4f45-921e-bddb1dd13d66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: JDG 14:11
Text: And it came to pass, when they saw him, that they brought thirty companions to be with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/14/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e966851-b89a-498f-81b5-c6914eacbf67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: JDG 14:12
Text: And Samson said unto them, I will now put forth a riddle unto you: if ye can certainly declare it me within the seven days of the feast, and find it out, then I will give you thirty sheets and thirty change of garments:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/14/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:147d7eb9-38d2-4cf3-b2cd-7445db9b6f6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: JDG 14:13
Text: But if ye cannot declare it me, then shall ye give me thirty sheets and thirty change of garments. And they said unto him, Put forth thy riddle, that we may hear it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/14/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f98cade8-5f89-4bd9-8177-8a83460f2e72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: JDG 14:14
Text: And he said unto them, Out of the eater came forth meat, and out of the strong came forth sweetness. And they could not in three days expound the riddle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/14/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8552250-fc54-4327-b39e-311d350b413c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: JDG 14:15
Text: And it came to pass on the seventh day, that they said unto Samson’s wife, Entice thy husband, that he may declare unto us the riddle, lest we burn thee and thy father’s house with fire: have ye called us to take that we have? is it not so?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/14/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:952e398b-a47f-42b6-8f80-493bf6a96be0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 302

Reference: JDG 14:16
Text: And Samson’s wife wept before him, and said, Thou dost but hate me, and lovest me not: thou hast put forth a riddle unto the children of my people, and hast not told it me. And he said unto her, Behold, I have not told it my father nor my mother, and shall I tell it thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/14/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f72406c-edb2-4021-b0dc-6f7944ef68e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: JDG 14:17
Text: And she wept before him the seven days, while their feast lasted: and it came to pass on the seventh day, that he told her, because she lay sore upon him: and she told the riddle to the children of her people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/14/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d5cf4f5-8418-4fa9-a5b8-b89229630d42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: JDG 14:18
Text: And the men of the city said unto him on the seventh day before the sun went down, What is sweeter than honey? And what is stronger than a lion? and he said unto them, If ye had not plowed with my heifer, ye had not found out my riddle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/14/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1758ebb-5390-4baf-b183-d4217a55e036>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 283

Reference: JDG 14:19
Text: And the Spirit of the LORD came upon him, and he went down to Ashkelon, and slew thirty men of them, and took their spoil, and gave change of garments unto them which expounded the riddle. And his anger was kindled, and he went up to his father’s house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JDG/14/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
