Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: 2SA 24:6
Text: Then they came to Gilead, and to the land of Tahtimhodshi; and they came to Danjaan, and about to Zidon,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2SA/24/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c718d204-2c1c-491d-aecb-bf22e7954f8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: 2SA 24:7
Text: And came to the strong hold of Tyre, and to all the cities of the Hivites, and of the Canaanites: and they went out to the south of Judah, even to Beersheba.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2SA/24/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03477eea-fc41-4d0b-93a5-337532e711db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: 2SA 24:8
Text: So when they had gone through all the land, they came to Jerusalem at the end of nine months and twenty days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2SA/24/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5209d5f1-1be8-42f7-b942-72d0fdadcb8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: 2SA 24:9
Text: And Joab gave up the sum of the number of the people unto the king: and there were in Israel eight hundred thousand valiant men that drew the sword; and the men of Judah were five hundred thousand men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2SA/24/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:efd18f74-2758-4b01-a963-cc0b33c8ac6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 273

Reference: 2SA 24:10
Text: And David’s heart smote him after that he had numbered the people. And David said unto the LORD, I have sinned greatly in that I have done: and now, I beseech thee, O LORD, take away the iniquity of thy servant; for I have done very foolishly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2SA/24/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7258710-44ba-41e4-a6f2-8bdcaae7bbc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 2SA 24:11
Text: For when David was up in the morning, the word of the LORD came unto the prophet Gad, David’s seer, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2SA/24/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:345c22e2-989a-4353-b1df-2ae7ec44920d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: 2SA 24:12
Text: Go and say unto David, Thus saith the LORD, I offer thee three things; choose thee one of them, that I may do it unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2SA/24/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00468db1-ab31-4f85-bc27-447539e4f261>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 338

Reference: 2SA 24:13
Text: So Gad came to David, and told him, and said unto him, Shall seven years of famine come unto thee in thy land? or wilt thou flee three months before thine enemies, while they pursue thee? or that there be three days’ pestilence in thy land? now advise, and see what answer I shall return to him that sent me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2SA/24/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1bc5de5-2a11-43b2-99a8-1cbf938e343a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 2SA 24:14
Text: And David said unto Gad, I am in a great strait: let us fall now into the hand of the LORD; for his mercies are great: and let me not fall into the hand of man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2SA/24/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0298390b-98bb-4cd5-b482-e036ec231b21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: 2SA 24:15
Text: So the LORD sent a pestilence upon Israel from the morning even to the time appointed: and there died of the people from Dan even to Beersheba seventy thousand men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2SA/24/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c7e1e4e-8426-4745-ae07-d3a40e69144b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 295

Reference: 2SA 24:16
Text: And when the angel stretched out his hand upon Jerusalem to destroy it, the LORD repented him of the evil, and said to the angel that destroyed the people, It is enough: stay now thine hand. And the angel of the LORD was by the threshingplace of Araunah the Jebusite.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2SA/24/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b11d4e7f-201f-46ea-936a-d03311f5d514>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: 2SA 24:17
Text: And David spake unto the LORD when he saw the angel that smote the people, and said, Lo, I have sinned, and I have done wickedly: but these sheep, what have they done? let thine hand, I pray thee, be against me, and against my father’s house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2SA/24/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66722907-ebcd-4b3c-96ca-c3f5995ad0b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 2SA 24:18
Text: And Gad came that day to David, and said unto him, Go up, rear an altar unto the LORD in the threshingfloor of Araunah the Jebusite.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2SA/24/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db98593f-4e6b-4904-b7c9-adba1f3bfedb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: 2SA 24:19
Text: And David, according to the saying of Gad, went up as the LORD commanded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2SA/24/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea06d13b-48c7-40b3-8ce7-75f14db313c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 2SA 24:20
Text: And Araunah looked, and saw the king and his servants coming on toward him: and Araunah went out, and bowed himself before the king on his face upon the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2SA/24/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64335d73-5fac-4f8a-baac-9906b741113a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: 2SA 24:21
Text: And Araunah said, Wherefore is my lord the king come to his servant? And David said, To buy the threshingfloor of thee, to build an altar unto the LORD, that the plague may be stayed from the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2SA/24/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6045ffa5-8ed5-470a-838d-a8a67929c772>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: 2SA 24:22
Text: And Araunah said unto David, Let my lord the king take and offer up what seemeth good unto him: behold, here be oxen for burnt sacrifice, and threshing instruments and other instruments of the oxen for wood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2SA/24/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f242087c-820c-4f3c-85e2-5a20fa66e520>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: 2SA 24:23
Text: All these things did Araunah, as a king, give unto the king. And Araunah said unto the king, The LORD thy God accept thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2SA/24/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36dab0f1-af5e-463d-8bfb-8538afd6358b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 280

Reference: 2SA 24:24
Text: And the king said unto Araunah, Nay; but I will surely buy it of thee at a price: neither will I offer burnt offerings unto the LORD my God of that which doth cost me nothing. So David bought the threshingfloor and the oxen for fifty shekels of silver.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2SA/24/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45390887-daf8-4dd8-bc09-baa2484a21c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: 2SA 24:25
Text: And David built there an altar unto the LORD, and offered burnt offerings and peace offerings. So the LORD was intreated for the land, and the plague was stayed from Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
