Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: 1KI 1:1
Text: Now king David was old and stricken in years; and they covered him with clothes, but he gat no heat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46ec2ee6-edb3-469d-8adf-7925ab1f2103>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: 1KI 1:2
Text: Wherefore his servants said unto him, Let there be sought for my lord the king a young virgin: and let her stand before the king, and let her cherish him, and let her lie in thy bosom, that my lord the king may get heat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6140ccbc-5fa4-41f1-8518-3abcbac04ec4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: 1KI 1:3
Text: So they sought for a fair damsel throughout all the coasts of Israel, and found Abishag a Shunammite, and brought her to the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d24e8de0-259c-4e95-bab4-2335ed4b3020>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: 1KI 1:4
Text: And the damsel was very fair, and cherished the king, and ministered to him: but the king knew her not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc1859aa-ff2b-4b3a-8302-b0fba2c4a85f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 1KI 1:5
Text: Then Adonijah the son of Haggith exalted himself, saying, I will be king: and he prepared him chariots and horsemen, and fifty men to run before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e463c7ab-e981-4035-a7e0-a6fc6e5fbf8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: 1KI 1:6
Text: And his father had not displeased him at any time in saying, Why hast thou done so? and he also was a very goodly man; and his mother bare him after Absalom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81e7f451-5ba2-4164-9a9a-5bb274ecacd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: 1KI 1:7
Text: And he conferred with Joab the son of Zeruiah, and with Abiathar the priest: and they following Adonijah helped him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:516c6a7b-f424-4fe5-ba65-c48457c22e8e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: 1KI 1:8
Text: But Zadok the priest, and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and Nathan the prophet, and Shimei, and Rei, and the mighty men which belonged to David, were not with Adonijah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f28c884-55ff-4447-96bb-d0fa66e6d473>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: 1KI 1:9
Text: And Adonijah slew sheep and oxen and fat cattle by the stone of Zoheleth, which is by Enrogel, and called all his brethren the king’s sons, and all the men of Judah the king’s servants:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de3b50aa-0d79-44c7-a77d-9bea80aabf15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 1KI 1:10
Text: But Nathan the prophet, and Benaiah, and the mighty men, and Solomon his brother, he called not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8daabdb2-4922-47a9-8529-85dc843e215c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: 1KI 1:11
Text: Wherefore Nathan spake unto Bathsheba the mother of Solomon, saying, Hast thou not heard that Adonijah the son of Haggith doth reign, and David our lord knoweth it not?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4adbde2d-3c96-47d8-90bb-7a55e89f1600>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 1KI 1:12
Text: Now therefore come, let me, I pray thee, give thee counsel, that thou mayest save thine own life, and the life of thy son Solomon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f4b61e7-ea0f-45fa-9a07-881664570f30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: 1KI 1:13
Text: Go and get thee in unto king David, and say unto him, Didst not thou, my lord, O king, swear unto thine handmaid, saying, Assuredly Solomon thy son shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne? why then doth Adonijah reign?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46ff1038-888f-45de-b470-44fe1e8c4f1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: 1KI 1:14
Text: Behold, while thou yet talkest there with the king, I also will come in after thee, and confirm thy words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f381d888-4575-49e9-868e-83e7c053df80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 1KI 1:15
Text: And Bathsheba went in unto the king into the chamber: and the king was very old; and Abishag the Shunammite ministered unto the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc72b486-f16e-4976-b489-384f0086773c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: 1KI 1:16
Text: And Bathsheba bowed, and did obeisance unto the king. And the king said, What wouldest thou?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9eb8b17-a8e4-478b-a8c3-36cf53032ea3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: 1KI 1:17
Text: And she said unto him, My lord, thou swarest by the LORD thy God unto thine handmaid, saying, Assuredly Solomon thy son shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a0a544d-e744-48fb-88a8-3186b94465ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: 1KI 1:18
Text: And now, behold, Adonijah reigneth; and now, my lord the king, thou knowest it not:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9499469-51fc-4ea0-9eb5-3b5dc7598f4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: 1KI 1:19
Text: And he hath slain oxen and fat cattle and sheep in abundance, and hath called all the sons of the king, and Abiathar the priest, and Joab the captain of the host: but Solomon thy servant hath he not called.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4453398-03ec-4394-9070-0b331f91b7a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: 1KI 1:20
Text: And thou, my lord, O king, the eyes of all Israel are upon thee, that thou shouldest tell them who shall sit on the throne of my lord the king after him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f743d34-a5e7-4b8e-b42a-bef73a975a48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: 1KI 1:21
Text: Otherwise it shall come to pass, when my lord the king shall sleep with his fathers, that I and my son Solomon shall be counted offenders.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64094a9d-a753-45b5-a0eb-c713e2fef875>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: 1KI 1:22
Text: And, lo, while she yet talked with the king, Nathan the prophet also came in.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7e9f881-7fa2-4378-9270-718f22d54a90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 1KI 1:23
Text: And they told the king, saying, Behold Nathan the prophet. And when he was come in before the king, he bowed himself before the king with his face to the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d004246-eb50-4626-ae38-0834244f0fad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 1KI 1:24
Text: And Nathan said, My lord, O king, hast thou said, Adonijah shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b721e08a-9565-41d2-ad75-e14208935f1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 286

Reference: 1KI 1:25
Text: For he is gone down this day, and hath slain oxen and fat cattle and sheep in abundance, and hath called all the king’s sons, and the captains of the host, and Abiathar the priest; and, behold, they eat and drink before him, and say, God save king Adonijah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bae574c8-5b80-45a9-bb00-58e282a20420>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 1KI 1:26
Text: But me, even me thy servant, and Zadok the priest, and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and thy servant Solomon, hath he not called.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9839c5b-7fe1-472a-90a7-8319fede65bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: 1KI 1:27
Text: Is this thing done by my lord the king, and thou hast not shewed it unto thy servant, who should sit on the throne of my lord the king after him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5f5efad-6548-4f57-b4c3-c5979b788397>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 1KI 1:28
Text: Then king David answered and said, Call me Bathsheba. And she came into the king’s presence, and stood before the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cff1e92f-af68-4ce3-bc83-f5b77b1858a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: 1KI 1:29
Text: And the king sware, and said, As the LORD liveth, that hath redeemed my soul out of all distress,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d31ec379-2dbc-49da-ae04-48f9dc7e2a12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: 1KI 1:30
Text: Even as I sware unto thee by the LORD God of Israel, saying, Assuredly Solomon thy son shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne in my stead; even so will I certainly do this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90e357fd-911b-4841-b843-fd7d8b9f433b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: 1KI 1:31
Text: Then Bathsheba bowed with her face to the earth, and did reverence to the king, and said, Let my lord king David live for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53fc879a-2bff-48e3-8ff9-ce7bf0d4fb6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 1KI 1:32
Text: And king David said, Call me Zadok the priest, and Nathan the prophet, and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada. And they came before the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a47ed17-e931-474a-b435-13e34f98e8ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 1KI 1:33
Text: The king also said unto them, Take with you the servants of your lord, and cause Solomon my son to ride upon mine own mule, and bring him down to Gihon:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:868b746e-20f2-4aa3-b42b-df23ea59189b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: 1KI 1:34
Text: And let Zadok the priest and Nathan the prophet anoint him there king over Israel: and blow ye with the trumpet, and say, God save king Solomon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a494127-1cea-4f70-856e-b0832ee7e2ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: 1KI 1:35
Text: Then ye shall come up after him, that he may come and sit upon my throne; for he shall be king in my stead: and I have appointed him to be ruler over Israel and over Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7f78139-fc67-4755-a6f7-a4e9287c9e8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: 1KI 1:36
Text: And Benaiah the son of Jehoiada answered the king, and said, Amen: the LORD God of my lord the king say so too.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8010801a-7637-4dac-9a96-60521d614d54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: 1KI 1:37
Text: As the LORD hath been with my lord the king, even so be he with Solomon, and make his throne greater than the throne of my lord king David.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:948a560b-588a-4f48-9d04-9af577db4961>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: 1KI 1:38
Text: So Zadok the priest, and Nathan the prophet, and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and the Cherethites, and the Pelethites, went down, and caused Solomon to ride upon king David’s mule, and brought him to Gihon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71d82aea-77af-458f-ad9f-405a5eb84dd5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 1KI 1:39
Text: And Zadok the priest took an horn of oil out of the tabernacle, and anointed Solomon. And they blew the trumpet; and all the people said, God save king Solomon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e912fab-f62a-4971-971c-b5a1a876b75c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 1KI 1:40
Text: And all the people came up after him, and the people piped with pipes, and rejoiced with great joy, so that the earth rent with the sound of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:763d0020-738a-4d05-881b-d9c07312dced>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: 1KI 1:41
Text: And Adonijah and all the guests that were with him heard it as they had made an end of eating. And when Joab heard the sound of the trumpet, he said, Wherefore is this noise of the city being in an uproar?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c9ea979-20e0-42ea-95d1-45957cf0b168>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: 1KI 1:42
Text: And while he yet spake, behold, Jonathan the son of Abiathar the priest came; and Adonijah said unto him, Come in; for thou art a valiant man, and bringest good tidings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a62b21f-b0e4-4c7a-86da-73348e170771>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 1KI 1:43
Text: And Jonathan answered and said to Adonijah, Verily our lord king David hath made Solomon king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9766e519-9da2-4f5b-8667-2ec89ffe2ff6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: 1KI 1:44
Text: And the king hath sent with him Zadok the priest, and Nathan the prophet, and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and the Cherethites, and the Pelethites, and they have caused him to ride upon the king’s mule:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac8ad370-a59c-4de1-8eec-a2f076041c52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: 1KI 1:45
Text: And Zadok the priest and Nathan the prophet have anointed him king in Gihon: and they are come up from thence rejoicing, so that the city rang again. This is the noise that ye have heard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77173690-ddea-417b-b88d-7e698a1f9271>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: 1KI 1:46
Text: And also Solomon sitteth on the throne of the kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe4df03d-fab0-4e08-ad70-1cf15d10b431>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: 1KI 1:47
Text: And moreover the king’s servants came to bless our lord king David, saying, God make the name of Solomon better than thy name, and make his throne greater than thy throne. And the king bowed himself upon the bed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e662197f-7697-4d6c-85e3-301dda838217>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 1KI 1:48
Text: And also thus said the king, Blessed be the LORD God of Israel, which hath given one to sit on my throne this day, mine eyes even seeing it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fadf3a9e-c1a5-45e2-a8ad-9e0db072527c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 1KI 1:49
Text: And all the guests that were with Adonijah were afraid, and rose up, and went every man his way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bfa95ff-9c3e-4573-b964-87f327be41b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: 1KI 1:50
Text: And Adonijah feared because of Solomon, and arose, and went, and caught hold on the horns of the altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f48909b3-5823-47fc-bfa5-7d35f814b735>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: 1KI 1:51
Text: And it was told Solomon, saying, Behold, Adonijah feareth king Solomon: for, lo, he hath caught hold on the horns of the altar, saying, Let king Solomon swear unto me today that he will not slay his servant with the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:677bd5d5-b50d-4807-bdd5-9ebe880f92d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 1KI 1:52
Text: And Solomon said, If he will shew himself a worthy man, there shall not an hair of him fall to the earth: but if wickedness shall be found in him, he shall die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/1/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d4b7d4c-1cf3-4749-9a41-18ca07acb14a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: 1KI 1:53
Text: So king Solomon sent, and they brought him down from the altar. And he came and bowed himself to king Solomon: and Solomon said unto him, Go to thine house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:373108be-2394-440c-983a-1d24fc866d92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: 1KI 2:1
Text: Now the days of David drew nigh that he should die; and he charged Solomon his son, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9ffe7d1-6f85-42a0-928a-91835d9ed792>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: 1KI 2:2
Text: I go the way of all the earth: be thou strong therefore, and shew thyself a man;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c569d4c3-ee4f-4474-9508-7075d6697472>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 298

Reference: 1KI 2:3
Text: And keep the charge of the LORD thy God, to walk in his ways, to keep his statutes, and his commandments, and his judgments, and his testimonies, as it is written in the law of Moses, that thou mayest prosper in all that thou doest, and whithersoever thou turnest thyself:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f59eb57-f2b3-48be-9a97-da97ddbb921d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 279

Reference: 1KI 2:4
Text: That the LORD may continue his word which he spake concerning me, saying, If thy children take heed to their way, to walk before me in truth with all their heart and with all their soul, there shall not fail thee (said he) a man on the throne of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db008241-cfb7-482b-8dbe-37c68855c6af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 370

Reference: 1KI 2:5
Text: Moreover thou knowest also what Joab the son of Zeruiah did to me, and what he did to the two captains of the hosts of Israel, unto Abner the son of Ner, and unto Amasa the son of Jether, whom he slew, and shed the blood of war in peace, and put the blood of war upon his girdle that was about his loins, and in his shoes that were on his feet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d0b0570-b1f7-4cc4-bfd1-9066ae9fd62a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: 1KI 2:6
Text: Do therefore according to thy wisdom, and let not his hoar head go down to the grave in peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2184082e-6ab1-4606-88b6-8a1d08d754c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 1KI 2:7
Text: But shew kindness unto the sons of Barzillai the Gileadite, and let them be of those that eat at thy table: for so they came to me when I fled because of Absalom thy brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89e5564b-9445-43f1-829a-2943f683a1bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 304

Reference: 1KI 2:8
Text: And, behold, thou hast with thee Shimei the son of Gera, a Benjamite of Bahurim, which cursed me with a grievous curse in the day when I went to Mahanaim: but he came down to meet me at Jordan, and I sware to him by the LORD, saying, I will not put thee to death with the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a87fc9f-c65d-47d4-8f2b-6466c7d2e87e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: 1KI 2:9
Text: Now therefore hold him not guiltless: for thou art a wise man, and knowest what thou oughtest to do unto him; but his hoar head bring thou down to the grave with blood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f72fb63-bc19-4d0b-8361-7f8fba7c728c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: 1KI 2:10
Text: So David slept with his fathers, and was buried in the city of David.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f48a068a-0962-435a-a604-cd1a963eebe7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: 1KI 2:11
Text: And the days that David reigned over Israel were forty years: seven years reigned he in Hebron, and thirty and three years reigned he in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f989c1a-1b40-4619-b402-e4518583d3e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 1KI 2:12
Text: Then sat Solomon upon the throne of David his father; and his kingdom was established greatly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7919706-607f-4e2a-a5f7-c5826bd610c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 1KI 2:13
Text: And Adonijah the son of Haggith came to Bathsheba the mother of Solomon. And she said, Comest thou peaceably? And he said, Peaceably.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7cfc8466-333d-4a94-b7bf-e065d94dc231>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: 1KI 2:14
Text: He said moreover, I have somewhat to say unto thee. And she said, Say on.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3a5fd55-4373-4718-84f1-44a15c021ec0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: 1KI 2:15
Text: And he said, Thou knowest that the kingdom was mine, and that all Israel set their faces on me, that I should reign: howbeit the kingdom is turned about, and is become my brother’s: for it was his from the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b860616d-f720-473f-a15d-53e5f5eca30e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: 1KI 2:16
Text: And now I ask one petition of thee, deny me not. And she said unto him, Say on.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7728d7ae-e839-4fe1-b06c-f2646a05c708>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 1KI 2:17
Text: And he said, Speak, I pray thee, unto Solomon the king, (for he will not say thee nay,) that he give me Abishag the Shunammite to wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0482c0b0-0f0f-4be9-b885-e7543bdaea8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: 1KI 2:18
Text: And Bathsheba said, Well; I will speak for thee unto the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56be925e-e7c2-4216-aaec-d52eaf68bd86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: 1KI 2:19
Text: Bathsheba therefore went unto king Solomon, to speak unto him for Adonijah. And the king rose up to meet her, and bowed himself unto her, and sat down on his throne, and caused a seat to be set for the king’s mother; and she sat on his right hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b4b2bd3-e286-45ea-9172-880bd1a37945>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: 1KI 2:20
Text: Then she said, I desire one small petition of thee; I pray thee, say me not nay. And the king said unto her, Ask on, my mother: for I will not say thee nay.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd077b2c-9db4-42ca-b088-236c8bb8ca89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: 1KI 2:21
Text: And she said, Let Abishag the Shunammite be given to Adonijah thy brother to wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec055b4d-7938-490e-87af-acce1b8a8a65>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 273

Reference: 1KI 2:22
Text: And king Solomon answered and said unto his mother, And why dost thou ask Abishag the Shunammite for Adonijah? ask for him the kingdom also; for he is mine elder brother; even for him, and for Abiathar the priest, and for Joab the son of Zeruiah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:892debdb-81a3-4dc6-81cb-232131524ae0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: 1KI 2:23
Text: Then king Solomon sware by the LORD, saying, God do so to me, and more also, if Adonijah have not spoken this word against his own life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2f7cd75-e6a6-4438-958d-349d2fd14b78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: 1KI 2:24
Text: Now therefore, as the LORD liveth, which hath established me, and set me on the throne of David my father, and who hath made me an house, as he promised, Adonijah shall be put to death this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86bf236c-8eb7-42b3-b251-bdfcb70ff605>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 1KI 2:25
Text: And king Solomon sent by the hand of Benaiah the son of Jehoiada; and he fell upon him that he died.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e0b0e19-e074-4dfd-9b88-6b49cc016895>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 337

Reference: 1KI 2:26
Text: And unto Abiathar the priest said the king, Get thee to Anathoth, unto thine own fields; for thou art worthy of death: but I will not at this time put thee to death, because thou barest the ark of the LORD God before David my father, and because thou hast been afflicted in all wherein my father was afflicted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2206595b-458b-4c60-ba0a-91927ad7a474>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 1KI 2:27
Text: So Solomon thrust out Abiathar from being priest unto the LORD; that he might fulfil the word of the LORD, which he spake concerning the house of Eli in Shiloh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68145b2d-d009-45bc-b974-2b0fde31fa01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: 1KI 2:28
Text: Then tidings came to Joab: for Joab had turned after Adonijah, though he turned not after Absalom. And Joab fled unto the tabernacle of the LORD, and caught hold on the horns of the altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51c8d52f-46f5-4d38-b75c-8949bc08db91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: 1KI 2:29
Text: And it was told king Solomon that Joab was fled unto the tabernacle of the LORD; and, behold, he is by the altar. Then Solomon sent Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, saying, Go, fall upon him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9859bf26-317f-42e4-9f61-9e79b71619d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: 1KI 2:30
Text: And Benaiah came to the tabernacle of the LORD, and said unto him, Thus saith the king, Come forth. And he said, Nay; but I will die here. And Benaiah brought the king word again, saying, Thus said Joab, and thus he answered me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4791407-df1c-4595-bd7f-7e08dd350af6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: 1KI 2:31
Text: And the king said unto him, Do as he hath said, and fall upon him, and bury him; that thou mayest take away the innocent blood, which Joab shed, from me, and from the house of my father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a853e280-081c-496e-878e-2d47e7d53e05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 325

Reference: 1KI 2:32
Text: And the LORD shall return his blood upon his own head, who fell upon two men more righteous and better than he, and slew them with the sword, my father David not knowing thereof, to wit, Abner the son of Ner, captain of the host of Israel, and Amasa the son of Jether, captain of the host of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3580a64e-e9d8-4d50-a1a1-b99b0a365488>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: 1KI 2:33
Text: Their blood shall therefore return upon the head of Joab, and upon the head of his seed for ever: but upon David, and upon his seed, and upon his house, and upon his throne, shall there be peace for ever from the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0689460e-37df-4e74-9363-4c3dc84358dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 1KI 2:34
Text: So Benaiah the son of Jehoiada went up, and fell upon him, and slew him: and he was buried in his own house in the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ca21489-b6b1-41f1-b2ec-8297846ee741>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 1KI 2:35
Text: And the king put Benaiah the son of Jehoiada in his room over the host: and Zadok the priest did the king put in the room of Abiathar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8eff434-aec6-4d13-a1dd-743d4d736d9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: 1KI 2:36
Text: And the king sent and called for Shimei, and said unto him, Build thee an house in Jerusalem, and dwell there, and go not forth thence any whither.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eff035fe-d35a-428e-8648-782be5f07547>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: 1KI 2:37
Text: For it shall be, that on the day thou goest out, and passest over the brook Kidron, thou shalt know for certain that thou shalt surely die: thy blood shall be upon thine own head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4792643-1fd7-4d5e-8219-114eeae380d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 1KI 2:38
Text: And Shimei said unto the king, The saying is good: as my lord the king hath said, so will thy servant do. And Shimei dwelt in Jerusalem many days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67926df5-c1f6-412c-ae69-1429010b4771>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: 1KI 2:39
Text: And it came to pass at the end of three years, that two of the servants of Shimei ran away unto Achish son of Maachah king of Gath. And they told Shimei, saying, Behold, thy servants be in Gath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da88194d-d417-479e-aca4-522a43f3122e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 1KI 2:40
Text: And Shimei arose, and saddled his ass, and went to Gath to Achish to seek his servants: and Shimei went, and brought his servants from Gath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ac4fcac-8ba2-47c1-8600-f3b749a82944>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: 1KI 2:41
Text: And it was told Solomon that Shimei had gone from Jerusalem to Gath, and was come again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92ef5072-834b-4a9e-8df3-fedc8c53b551>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 329

Reference: 1KI 2:42
Text: And the king sent and called for Shimei, and said unto him, Did I not make thee to swear by the LORD, and protested unto thee, saying, Know for a certain, on the day thou goest out, and walkest abroad any whither, that thou shalt surely die? and thou saidst unto me, The word that I have heard is good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da33110e-68a5-4ff9-90bf-853646d0747f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 1KI 2:43
Text: Why then hast thou not kept the oath of the LORD, and the commandment that I have charged thee with?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c408137-3e52-4969-96a2-8f1afbd6767e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: 1KI 2:44
Text: The king said moreover to Shimei, Thou knowest all the wickedness which thine heart is privy to, that thou didst to David my father: therefore the LORD shall return thy wickedness upon thine own head;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e2c0ad3-ae77-41d4-90a3-95867cc08389>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 1KI 2:45
Text: And king Solomon shall be blessed, and the throne of David shall be established before the LORD for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/2/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fd26bf8-489b-449b-9481-2ee8806cb050>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: 1KI 2:46
Text: So the king commanded Benaiah the son of Jehoiada; which went out, and fell upon him, that he died. And the kingdom was established in the hand of Solomon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56af630b-3346-4a2c-b3e3-f20a85dec8da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: 1KI 3:1
Text: And Solomon made affinity with Pharaoh king of Egypt, and took Pharaoh’s daughter, and brought her into the city of David, until he had made an end of building his own house, and the house of the LORD, and the wall of Jerusalem round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7555699-9d54-4dbd-9ad1-033d1f4c747e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: 1KI 3:2
Text: Only the people sacrificed in high places, because there was no house built unto the name of the LORD, until those days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4ec9005-397b-4038-9cd9-47beb7fe4f2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: 1KI 3:3
Text: And Solomon loved the LORD, walking in the statutes of David his father: only he sacrificed and burnt incense in high places.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13ff804b-9198-4295-86bc-11d08715d272>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 1KI 3:4
Text: And the king went to Gibeon to sacrifice there; for that was the great high place: a thousand burnt offerings did Solomon offer upon that altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f947aa2a-482f-4415-9ce4-3a6a2d995ada>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 1KI 3:5
Text: In Gibeon the LORD appeared to Solomon in a dream by night: and God said, Ask what I shall give thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23064a68-7e37-44d6-a697-b9dc6f6bffe3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 332

Reference: 1KI 3:6
Text: And Solomon said, Thou hast shewed unto thy servant David my father great mercy, according as he walked before thee in truth, and in righteousness, and in uprightness of heart with thee; and thou hast kept for him this great kindness, that thou hast given him a son to sit on his throne, as it is this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04c5e60b-7cd9-44af-83e5-a278f5a6f44f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 1KI 3:7
Text: And now, O LORD my God, thou hast made thy servant king instead of David my father: and I am but a little child: I know not how to go out or come in.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba6ffd42-2e26-4483-8646-d1c699231cbc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 1KI 3:8
Text: And thy servant is in the midst of thy people which thou hast chosen, a great people, that cannot be numbered nor counted for multitude.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7391e31-c028-483e-8368-debced646c58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: 1KI 3:9
Text: Give therefore thy servant an understanding heart to judge thy people, that I may discern between good and bad: for who is able to judge this thy so great a people?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa60656f-4514-47fb-81e2-ce8f82f5c214>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: 1KI 3:10
Text: And the speech pleased the LORD, that Solomon had asked this thing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7320ca4-c59d-4d70-9514-83e0e5f1a573>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: 1KI 3:11
Text: And God said unto him, Because thou hast asked this thing, and hast not asked for thyself long life; neither hast asked riches for thyself, nor hast asked the life of thine enemies; but hast asked for thyself understanding to discern judgment;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aafe0c59-2b68-481c-a842-a1f125110b58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: 1KI 3:12
Text: Behold, I have done according to thy words: lo, I have given thee a wise and an understanding heart; so that there was none like thee before thee, neither after thee shall any arise like unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1b51a79-b905-44ab-9b71-06e9a05a384e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: 1KI 3:13
Text: And I have also given thee that which thou hast not asked, both riches, and honour: so that there shall not be any among the kings like unto thee all thy days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5ab418a-e805-4d84-8a4b-fbda938bfab5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 1KI 3:14
Text: And if thou wilt walk in my ways, to keep my statutes and my commandments, as thy father David did walk, then I will lengthen thy days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6139b050-f0c3-47f5-bfd5-2d4753f2fc34>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: 1KI 3:15
Text: And Solomon awoke; and, behold, it was a dream. And he came to Jerusalem, and stood before the ark of the covenant of the LORD, and offered up burnt offerings, and offered peace offerings, and made a feast to all his servants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58a3bac6-f3f2-470c-bfbe-b800c2c38cde>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: 1KI 3:16
Text: Then came there two women, that were harlots, unto the king, and stood before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4bc62e6-b3e0-46d5-8f6c-909fe4f0bf53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: 1KI 3:17
Text: And the one woman said, O my lord, I and this woman dwell in one house; and I was delivered of a child with her in the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:388168c9-9e60-4dee-8bd3-aa53258855c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: 1KI 3:18
Text: And it came to pass the third day after that I was delivered, that this woman was delivered also: and we were together; there was no stranger with us in the house, save we two in the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb42d4af-978e-4f1f-9e6a-703f6aee6c81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: 1KI 3:19
Text: And this woman’s child died in the night; because she overlaid it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e0d1fdf-8cd0-4151-81c3-ed92c5426666>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: 1KI 3:20
Text: And she arose at midnight, and took my son from beside me, while thine handmaid slept, and laid it in her bosom, and laid her dead child in my bosom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fd9c63b-702e-44a1-b2b9-72d8380afddc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: 1KI 3:21
Text: And when I rose in the morning to give my child suck, behold, it was dead: but when I had considered it in the morning, behold, it was not my son, which I did bear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9756f241-7250-4ea1-be8e-42b7c28d7e24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: 1KI 3:22
Text: And the other woman said, Nay; but the living is my son, and the dead is thy son. And this said, No; but the dead is thy son, and the living is my son. Thus they spake before the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f35cac98-d1b9-414a-8501-6b623626a7fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: 1KI 3:23
Text: Then said the king, The one saith, This is my son that liveth, and thy son is the dead: and the other saith, Nay; but thy son is the dead, and my son is the living.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:185be31a-2bca-4c96-9071-a40bf5b72fb2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: 1KI 3:24
Text: And the king said, Bring me a sword. And they brought a sword before the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c676e738-55e4-47b3-8be1-def03cb48d67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: 1KI 3:25
Text: And the king said, Divide the living child in two, and give half to the one, and half to the other.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c8c81a9-a959-46a7-9f58-5f98c4ffe6f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: 1KI 3:26
Text: Then spake the woman whose the living child was unto the king, for her bowels yearned upon her son, and she said, O my lord, give her the living child, and in no wise slay it. But the other said, Let it be neither mine nor thine, but divide it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5c5dd2a-e00d-4120-8abd-f4b956c98f0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 1KI 3:27
Text: Then the king answered and said, Give her the living child, and in no wise slay it: she is the mother thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/3/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8dd39d0-9209-4b19-86e2-b63434c0f289>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: 1KI 3:28
Text: And all Israel heard of the judgment which the king had judged; and they feared the king: for they saw that the wisdom of God was in him, to do judgment.


