Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 1KI 4:22
Text: And Solomon’s provision for one day was thirty measures of fine flour, and threescore measures of meal,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/4/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11a63191-07f8-47e0-997b-214fb2dfa243>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 1KI 4:23
Text: Ten fat oxen, and twenty oxen out of the pastures, and an hundred sheep, beside harts, and roebucks, and fallowdeer, and fatted fowl.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/4/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01f46911-fab9-4a60-8a82-22d78aa264eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: 1KI 4:24
Text: For he had dominion over all the region on this side the river, from Tiphsah even to Azzah, over all the kings on this side the river: and he had peace on all sides round about him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/4/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87b2f063-7878-4adf-af90-413025f81aba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: 1KI 4:25
Text: And Judah and Israel dwelt safely, every man under his vine and under his fig tree, from Dan even to Beersheba, all the days of Solomon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/4/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58377383-d98b-47e8-8509-292acb8e796b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: 1KI 4:26
Text: And Solomon had forty thousand stalls of horses for his chariots, and twelve thousand horsemen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/4/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2dc2c14-f3e9-43f8-b845-62387fa0fd62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: 1KI 4:27
Text: And those officers provided victual for king Solomon, and for all that came unto king Solomon’s table, every man in his month: they lacked nothing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/4/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c35bb274-6e33-4ee7-9968-eeb7bded815f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 1KI 4:28
Text: Barley also and straw for the horses and dromedaries brought they unto the place where the officers were, every man according to his charge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/4/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a610dc8-2e1b-4047-9c68-f29a088e35de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 1KI 4:29
Text: And God gave Solomon wisdom and understanding exceeding much, and largeness of heart, even as the sand that is on the sea shore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/4/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea7aaba9-ec81-4f92-a94b-3c0e8ca4a92d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: 1KI 4:30
Text: And Solomon’s wisdom excelled the wisdom of all the children of the east country, and all the wisdom of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/4/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a6a2b52-d7cc-4d1c-9e5f-eee648ba6461>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: 1KI 4:31
Text: For he was wiser than all men; than Ethan the Ezrahite, and Heman, and Chalcol, and Darda, the sons of Mahol: and his fame was in all nations round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/4/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46f70301-cad3-43e5-bb31-7ac00cfa8da1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: 1KI 4:32
Text: And he spake three thousand proverbs: and his songs were a thousand and five.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/4/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79a6a8ae-6265-47f1-a6d3-ebab0b8c7c7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: 1KI 4:33
Text: And he spake of trees, from the cedar tree that is in Lebanon even unto the hyssop that springeth out of the wall: he spake also of beasts, and of fowl, and of creeping things, and of fishes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/4/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5fac057-770e-4e88-a826-4d969c63c1dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: 1KI 4:34
Text: And there came of all people to hear the wisdom of Solomon, from all kings of the earth, which had heard of his wisdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5faa20a2-8ae1-4a54-8f2c-d2ec0e4c5bfe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: 1KI 5:1
Text: And Hiram king of Tyre sent his servants unto Solomon; for he had heard that they had anointed him king in the room of his father: for Hiram was ever a lover of David.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f7b75e5-a0b4-4c82-b6af-153fe781d279>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 60

Reference: 1KI 5:2
Text: And Solomon sent to Hiram, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa2403e7-73d7-4971-ad8b-623f0ed04fba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: 1KI 5:3
Text: Thou knowest how that David my father could not build an house unto the name of the LORD his God for the wars which were about him on every side, until the LORD put them under the soles of his feet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc1adbcc-87d8-44ab-9c15-3c15292e0877>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: 1KI 5:4
Text: But now the LORD my God hath given me rest on every side, so that there is neither adversary nor evil occurrent.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:530d3688-6b6f-4e3d-a9ed-0f230a89d1e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: 1KI 5:5
Text: And, behold, I purpose to build an house unto the name of the LORD my God, as the LORD spake unto David my father, saying, Thy son, whom I will set upon thy throne in thy room, he shall build an house unto my name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5d87953-6a3c-41ac-892b-9beb0fff51cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 333

Reference: 1KI 5:6
Text: Now therefore command thou that they hew me cedar trees out of Lebanon; and my servants shall be with thy servants: and unto thee will I give hire for thy servants according to all that thou shalt appoint: for thou knowest that there is not among us any that can skill to hew timber like unto the Sidonians.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16329b17-8f70-4d0c-82fe-47aeb4b57c13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: 1KI 5:7
Text: And it came to pass, when Hiram heard the words of Solomon, that he rejoiced greatly, and said, Blessed be the LORD this day, which hath given unto David a wise son over this great people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bb48b87-6947-40e2-9fa1-12c12b2c66c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: 1KI 5:8
Text: And Hiram sent to Solomon, saying, I have considered the things which thou sentest to me for: and I will do all thy desire concerning timber of cedar, and concerning timber of fir.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94501fff-4575-40f8-a21d-87527d758f0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 312

Reference: 1KI 5:9
Text: My servants shall bring them down from Lebanon unto the sea: and I will convey them by sea in floats unto the place that thou shalt appoint me, and will cause them to be discharged there, and thou shalt receive them: and thou shalt accomplish my desire, in giving food for my household.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90b284a3-f31d-4b8f-923d-d9a224fbdd49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: 1KI 5:10
Text: So Hiram gave Solomon cedar trees and fir trees according to all his desire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ade5db70-bfb8-4497-920c-bb185dfda1d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: 1KI 5:11
Text: And Solomon gave Hiram twenty thousand measures of wheat for food to his household, and twenty measures of pure oil: thus gave Solomon to Hiram year by year.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07266d27-5d2e-4b7a-b46e-91bc1a75f0d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: 1KI 5:12
Text: And the LORD gave Solomon wisdom, as he promised him: and there was peace between Hiram and Solomon; and they two made a league together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f19f22ff-3b29-4c4e-9f61-8359ea711486>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: 1KI 5:13
Text: And king Solomon raised a levy out of all Israel; and the levy was thirty thousand men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3e2b2cc-918a-4415-aa9c-6e56dd58c5d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: 1KI 5:14
Text: And he sent them to Lebanon, ten thousand a month by courses: a month they were in Lebanon, and two months at home: and Adoniram was over the levy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c38c38ce-fd62-4272-8852-42ab3d5fea76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 1KI 5:15
Text: And Solomon had threescore and ten thousand that bare burdens, and fourscore thousand hewers in the mountains;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e98dbc05-c4e6-4bed-95b6-714fcf64b816>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: 1KI 5:16
Text: Beside the chief of Solomon’s officers which were over the work, three thousand and three hundred, which ruled over the people that wrought in the work.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/5/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3425f870-75d0-49f7-af4c-88ee5522e82a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: 1KI 5:17
Text: And the king commanded, and they brought great stones, costly stones, and hewed stones, to lay the foundation of the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/5/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac3cd37c-0572-422c-8278-29f6ae487e5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: 1KI 5:18
Text: And Solomon’s builders and Hiram’s builders did hew them, and the stonesquarers: so they prepared timber and stones to build the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:842663d5-6d04-4a44-a8ec-b7abfc599af0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 293

Reference: 1KI 6:1
Text: And it came to pass in the four hundred and eightieth year after the children of Israel were come out of the land of Egypt, in the fourth year of Solomon’s reign over Israel, in the month Zif, which is the second month, that he began to build the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58f64b76-d01c-4c9d-9350-95dcdf1d63e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: 1KI 6:2
Text: And the house which king Solomon built for the LORD, the length thereof was threescore cubits, and the breadth thereof twenty cubits, and the height thereof thirty cubits.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f1487d6-b95e-4013-927d-15103c817b7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: 1KI 6:3
Text: And the porch before the temple of the house, twenty cubits was the length thereof, according to the breadth of the house; and ten cubits was the breadth thereof before the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a8a61cf-c063-412f-9ea5-015d0403c5e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: 1KI 6:4
Text: And for the house he made windows of narrow lights.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b085d4f-29ed-4599-8407-91b208166f37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: 1KI 6:5
Text: And against the wall of the house he built chambers round about, against the walls of the house round about, both of the temple and of the oracle: and he made chambers round about:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2da35158-970b-45af-89e1-4a991b31e6da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: 1KI 6:6
Text: The nethermost chamber was five cubits broad, and the middle was six cubits broad, and the third was seven cubits broad: for without in the wall of the house he made narrowed rests round about, that the beams should not be fastened in the walls of the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60b6dce7-a65c-470c-9c36-5ff26a6dc5c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: 1KI 6:7
Text: And the house, when it was in building, was built of stone made ready before it was brought thither: so that there was neither hammer nor axe nor any tool of iron heard in the house, while it was in building.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f941510-36fc-4a17-ba08-cc37c01e3d9e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: 1KI 6:8
Text: The door for the middle chamber was in the right side of the house: and they went up with winding stairs into the middle chamber, and out of the middle into the third.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e64a75ad-77d9-413b-b267-2a6f8d114d41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: 1KI 6:9
Text: So he built the house, and finished it; and covered the house with beams and boards of cedar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d2e22b6-003f-467e-9814-d853419fa392>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 1KI 6:10
Text: And then he built chambers against all the house, five cubits high: and they rested on the house with timber of cedar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee2d5c8d-9f12-4c54-8b38-8f5b751e1375>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: 1KI 6:11
Text: And the word of the LORD came to Solomon, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83bca51e-d73e-41d0-b3f8-6e2b0d64308a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: 1KI 6:12
Text: Concerning this house which thou art in building, if thou wilt walk in my statutes, and execute my judgments, and keep all my commandments to walk in them; then will I perform my word with thee, which I spake unto David thy father:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be80d588-0fd0-43d4-a5d5-7e731584163d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: 1KI 6:13
Text: And I will dwell among the children of Israel, and will not forsake my people Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5d68d9b-2bea-4e69-a547-50671958f663>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 71

Reference: 1KI 6:14
Text: So Solomon built the house, and finished it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffdb47ce-ed9b-497b-9ea2-457927e772fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: 1KI 6:15
Text: And he built the walls of the house within with boards of cedar, both the floor of the house, and the walls of the ceiling: and he covered them on the inside with wood, and covered the floor of the house with planks of fir.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03acf84c-75f7-4c41-88f9-945412005061>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: 1KI 6:16
Text: And he built twenty cubits on the sides of the house, both the floor and the walls with boards of cedar: he even built them for it within, even for the oracle, even for the most holy place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:811eec0a-d7f7-4d90-bb8f-ffd87b9b2526>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: 1KI 6:17
Text: And the house, that is, the temple before it, was forty cubits long.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67e20d7e-3f8b-4d2f-a1ab-ee9338a115ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 1KI 6:18
Text: And the cedar of the house within was carved with knops and open flowers: all was cedar; there was no stone seen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eaea8640-8380-46a5-a324-0c94b9b872f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: 1KI 6:19
Text: And the oracle he prepared in the house within, to set there the ark of the covenant of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc533909-2298-4cb3-86e4-00cc5e39cdb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: 1KI 6:20
Text: And the oracle in the forepart was twenty cubits in length, and twenty cubits in breadth, and twenty cubits in the height thereof: and he overlaid it with pure gold; and so covered the altar which was of cedar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36a69b92-b023-4977-bca3-c0b091a115ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: 1KI 6:21
Text: So Solomon overlaid the house within with pure gold: and he made a partition by the chains of gold before the oracle; and he overlaid it with gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:943f33ca-3b78-4e45-b314-a1ecee861fbf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 1KI 6:22
Text: And the whole house he overlaid with gold, until he had finished all the house: also the whole altar that was by the oracle he overlaid with gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5650955a-6c93-4522-86cc-bbdd344902ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: 1KI 6:23
Text: And within the oracle he made two cherubims of olive tree, each ten cubits high.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfd46bcc-3bcd-44e2-8de8-6245a48689d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: 1KI 6:24
Text: And five cubits was the one wing of the cherub, and five cubits the other wing of the cherub: from the uttermost part of the one wing unto the uttermost part of the other were ten cubits.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4dcb5190-9253-4cb4-95b8-f5b8e69d2a31>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: 1KI 6:25
Text: And the other cherub was ten cubits: both the cherubims were of one measure and one size.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c42941d1-a6f9-41f5-9f12-63086132bdaf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: 1KI 6:26
Text: The height of the one cherub was ten cubits, and so was it of the other cherub.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1d1cf72-7f56-42ae-9c26-751780b10b5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 298

Reference: 1KI 6:27
Text: And he set the cherubims within the inner house: and they stretched forth the wings of the cherubims, so that the wing of the one touched the one wall, and the wing of the other cherub touched the other wall; and their wings touched one another in the midst of the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a4436fe-7e68-45d7-ba83-e4251757fd7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 67

Reference: 1KI 6:28
Text: And he overlaid the cherubims with gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9854ce3-7117-497c-ac13-e0aafe35a10d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: 1KI 6:29
Text: And he carved all the walls of the house round about with carved figures of cherubims and palm trees and open flowers, within and without.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df3f0421-2dd9-47e6-ae19-213558fcaa30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: 1KI 6:30
Text: And the floors of the house he overlaid with gold, within and without.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29e3c594-0f0b-4518-a862-68218359f737>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 1KI 6:31
Text: And for the entering of the oracle he made doors of olive tree: the lintel and side posts were a fifth part of the wall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:340e7e14-be5c-4fda-8018-333ccd7444ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: 1KI 6:32
Text: The two doors also were of olive tree; and he carved upon them carvings of cherubims and palm trees and open flowers, and overlaid them with gold, and spread gold upon the cherubims, and upon the palm trees.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ece93bf-e8f8-4845-aa2c-3e931134daa1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: 1KI 6:33
Text: So also made he for the door of the temple posts of olive tree, a fourth part of the wall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c9fd3bd-a5dd-4eed-9d3c-2cfc826e43d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 1KI 6:34
Text: And the two doors were of fir tree: the two leaves of the one door were folding, and the two leaves of the other door were folding.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfd6a539-5f3b-4ab7-84bb-3ffab694663e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 1KI 6:35
Text: And he carved thereon cherubims and palm trees and open flowers: and covered them with gold fitted upon the carved work.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:623a6c20-bd6d-436e-8166-88c5721f0243>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: 1KI 6:36
Text: And he built the inner court with three rows of hewed stone, and a row of cedar beams.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d16dff63-5399-4769-a75d-9dd5e8e6d399>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: 1KI 6:37
Text: In the fourth year was the foundation of the house of the LORD laid, in the month Zif:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/6/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37deae4b-ee58-4070-948c-a0fd1d03fdf8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: 1KI 6:38
Text: And in the eleventh year, in the month Bul, which is the eighth month, was the house finished throughout all the parts thereof, and according to all the fashion of it. So was he seven years in building it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:238917f2-96db-4a2c-8900-3cde3c3bfe10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: 1KI 7:1
Text: But Solomon was building his own house thirteen years, and he finished all his house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72770d6e-7e03-4e46-b6f0-8881fbaa5475>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: 1KI 7:2
Text: He built also the house of the forest of Lebanon; the length thereof was an hundred cubits, and the breadth thereof fifty cubits, and the height thereof thirty cubits, upon four rows of cedar pillars, with cedar beams upon the pillars.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e78832a-9d36-4828-a841-1c49babc432b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 1KI 7:3
Text: And it was covered with cedar above upon the beams, that lay on forty five pillars, fifteen in a row.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69b472b2-72f3-4ebd-ab2d-2f371697f54d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: 1KI 7:4
Text: And there were windows in three rows, and light was against light in three ranks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a51dc02-fce9-4993-ad13-ac81595a04e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 1KI 7:5
Text: And all the doors and posts were square, with the windows: and light was against light in three ranks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:666a1ea2-ddc3-41cd-ac89-bf149e404c04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: 1KI 7:6
Text: And he made a porch of pillars; the length thereof was fifty cubits, and the breadth thereof thirty cubits: and the porch was before them: and the other pillars and the thick beam were before them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93d3591c-9f09-4000-95a6-46c9e2a3117a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: 1KI 7:7
Text: Then he made a porch for the throne where he might judge, even the porch of judgment: and it was covered with cedar from one side of the floor to the other.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a097c8d5-a6af-4b2c-93b3-50de8568dfab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: 1KI 7:8
Text: And his house where he dwelt had another court within the porch, which was of the like work. Solomon made also an house for Pharaoh’s daughter, whom he had taken to wife, like unto this porch.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05472bd2-89a0-4431-be7c-f2d9d67e4ff7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: 1KI 7:9
Text: All these were of costly stones, according to the measures of hewed stones, sawed with saws, within and without, even from the foundation unto the coping, and so on the outside toward the great court.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87cae038-28e2-42d4-9cc2-935c18d9a20b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: 1KI 7:10
Text: And the foundation was of costly stones, even great stones, stones of ten cubits, and stones of eight cubits.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7590625-39f9-466c-ba47-6895564f3455>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: 1KI 7:11
Text: And above were costly stones, after the measures of hewed stones, and cedars.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a09efdc-0fec-4f01-9b74-760be03ee3dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: 1KI 7:12
Text: And the great court round about was with three rows of hewed stones, and a row of cedar beams, both for the inner court of the house of the LORD, and for the porch of the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:053c6c40-b1bb-49da-8959-ea638096edcf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: 1KI 7:13
Text: And king Solomon sent and fetched Hiram out of Tyre.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80c33895-11c8-4e7a-b478-456999f7ddb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 273

Reference: 1KI 7:14
Text: He was a widow’s son of the tribe of Naphtali, and his father was a man of Tyre, a worker in brass: and he was filled with wisdom, and understanding, and cunning to work all works in brass. And he came to king Solomon, and wrought all his work.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16f536ca-b883-43e2-9535-e6633009d61b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: 1KI 7:15
Text: For he cast two pillars of brass, of eighteen cubits high apiece: and a line of twelve cubits did compass either of them about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43cce73a-7bcf-4cab-8803-2ce4640814f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: 1KI 7:16
Text: And he made two chapiters of molten brass, to set upon the tops of the pillars: the height of the one chapiter was five cubits, and the height of the other chapiter was five cubits:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e710f89-6f28-4bf0-8b6c-65561138fdd8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: 1KI 7:17
Text: And nets of checker work, and wreaths of chain work, for the chapiters which were upon the top of the pillars; seven for the one chapiter, and seven for the other chapiter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f80cdc6-ee62-45b0-9aac-60cb6952099c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: 1KI 7:18
Text: And he made the pillars, and two rows round about upon the one network, to cover the chapiters that were upon the top, with pomegranates: and so did he for the other chapiter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ade414c-5f69-4618-8679-d6bc6656b2b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 1KI 7:19
Text: And the chapiters that were upon the top of the pillars were of lily work in the porch, four cubits.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7847a36-5c8d-49ad-b628-db157ed0053f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: 1KI 7:20
Text: And the chapiters upon the two pillars had pomegranates also above, over against the belly which was by the network: and the pomegranates were two hundred in rows round about upon the other chapiter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e4fb9c7-e471-4902-ab61-b7a5d9ed857c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: 1KI 7:21
Text: And he set up the pillars in the porch of the temple: and he set up the right pillar, and called the name thereof Jachin: and he set up the left pillar, and called the name thereof Boaz.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f41b070-078d-4608-8ff1-b9035f9446cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: 1KI 7:22
Text: And upon the top of the pillars was lily work: so was the work of the pillars finished.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89ffa563-2abc-493a-8e55-615b240fbc3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: 1KI 7:23
Text: And he made a molten sea, ten cubits from the one brim to the other: it was round all about, and his height was five cubits: and a line of thirty cubits did compass it round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4cc2e4a-5c05-4817-b435-9497317984f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: 1KI 7:24
Text: And under the brim of it round about there were knops compassing it, ten in a cubit, compassing the sea round about: the knops were cast in two rows, when it was cast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb34ff6d-1606-48f6-93d1-9bb424d8fbf7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: 1KI 7:25
Text: It stood upon twelve oxen, three looking toward the north, and three looking toward the west, and three looking toward the south, and three looking toward the east: and the sea was set above upon them, and all their hinder parts were inward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:430fb3f5-2303-437e-a084-79d40649e33c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: 1KI 7:26
Text: And it was an hand breadth thick, and the brim thereof was wrought like the brim of a cup, with flowers of lilies: it contained two thousand baths.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31bc4bf1-3b60-4007-a585-e47104206bad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 1KI 7:27
Text: And he made ten bases of brass; four cubits was the length of one base, and four cubits the breadth thereof, and three cubits the height of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec130c0e-98a6-483f-bc53-ef120844301f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: 1KI 7:28
Text: And the work of the bases was on this manner: they had borders, and the borders were between the ledges:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf3c0cc4-7bba-4fba-af50-7854f687aaa8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: 1KI 7:29
Text: And on the borders that were between the ledges were lions, oxen, and cherubims: and upon the ledges there was a base above: and beneath the lions and oxen were certain additions made of thin work.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce33958e-9dc9-4685-a6ea-52ec0793ddf2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: 1KI 7:30
Text: And every base had four brasen wheels, and plates of brass: and the four corners thereof had undersetters: under the laver were undersetters molten, at the side of every addition.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be55f951-d3a2-4b40-aedb-8aab987c257b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: 1KI 7:31
Text: And the mouth of it within the chapiter and above was a cubit: but the mouth thereof was round after the work of the base, a cubit and an half: and also upon the mouth of it were gravings with their borders, foursquare, not round.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec9675f7-8ba0-438d-9c7f-d6648de42d13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 1KI 7:32
Text: And under the borders were four wheels; and the axletrees of the wheels were joined to the base: and the height of a wheel was a cubit and half a cubit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bd964dd-fd70-4c79-898e-411d82c41c76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 1KI 7:33
Text: And the work of the wheels was like the work of a chariot wheel: their axletrees, and their naves, and their felloes, and their spokes, were all molten.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3679e8b4-e280-48f7-966f-59ac2489d14f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: 1KI 7:34
Text: And there were four undersetters to the four corners of one base: and the undersetters were of the very base itself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ecf69d6-260f-422e-a0c9-4ef6bc7db221>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: 1KI 7:35
Text: And in the top of the base was there a round compass of half a cubit high: and on the top of the base the ledges thereof and the borders thereof were of the same.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92cfc221-b85b-4492-9376-2a201afefa92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: 1KI 7:36
Text: For on the plates of the ledges thereof, and on the borders thereof, he graved cherubims, lions, and palm trees, according to the proportion of every one, and additions round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da7bb5cd-801e-4ca6-afc7-ea43a5a1b29c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 1KI 7:37
Text: After this manner he made the ten bases: all of them had one casting, one measure, and one size.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:270d293f-92c5-483d-a75d-62ad1a5bfede>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 1KI 7:38
Text: Then made he ten lavers of brass: one laver contained forty baths: and every laver was four cubits: and upon every one of the ten bases one laver.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c164ed79-7347-4918-ab91-8b123e4e8fcd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: 1KI 7:39
Text: And he put five bases on the right side of the house, and five on the left side of the house: and he set the sea on the right side of the house eastward over against the south.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd3ca371-2be9-400a-82ff-6e165e47dad2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: 1KI 7:40
Text: And Hiram made the lavers, and the shovels, and the basons. So Hiram made an end of doing all the work that he made king Solomon for the house of the LORD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f188ef9d-fe7a-494b-b4ef-51f87d7df75e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: 1KI 7:41
Text: The two pillars, and the two bowls of the chapiters that were on the top of the two pillars; and the two networks, to cover the two bowls of the chapiters which were upon the top of the pillars;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55b8292a-e336-4ed9-b501-00fc4d3d072f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: 1KI 7:42
Text: And four hundred pomegranates for the two networks, even two rows of pomegranates for one network, to cover the two bowls of the chapiters that were upon the pillars;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3960345e-52c9-4506-9022-b0338e3ec59b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: 1KI 7:43
Text: And the ten bases, and ten lavers on the bases;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd8e4baa-6cd1-4194-b72d-1dc1292a06d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 70

Reference: 1KI 7:44
Text: And one sea, and twelve oxen under the sea;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9dcd9100-af7f-4414-b2d9-6bc9a8ecac56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: 1KI 7:45
Text: And the pots, and the shovels, and the basons: and all these vessels, which Hiram made to king Solomon for the house of the LORD, were of bright brass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
