Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 1KI 7:46
Text: In the plain of Jordan did the king cast them, in the clay ground between Succoth and Zarthan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cad70380-fa24-4144-8cc7-be82a4bfb242>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: 1KI 7:47
Text: And Solomon left all the vessels unweighed, because they were exceeding many: neither was the weight of the brass found out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:760f8486-c30f-49ba-b473-96a52243733b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 1KI 7:48
Text: And Solomon made all the vessels that pertained unto the house of the LORD: the altar of gold, and the table of gold, whereupon the shewbread was,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec11fe5b-47b2-4b70-9ef5-f5fb726119cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: 1KI 7:49
Text: And the candlesticks of pure gold, five on the right side, and five on the left, before the oracle, with the flowers, and the lamps, and the tongs of gold,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07869af9-fa50-464d-bc59-6f52c4bbe1da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: 1KI 7:50
Text: And the bowls, and the snuffers, and the basons, and the spoons, and the censers of pure gold; and the hinges of gold, both for the doors of the inner house, the most holy place, and for the doors of the house, to wit, of the temple.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/7/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e85342c0-f589-4b46-8a10-ac16e1fb3ce0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 279

Reference: 1KI 7:51
Text: So was ended all the work that king Solomon made for the house of the LORD. And Solomon brought in the things which David his father had dedicated; even the silver, and the gold, and the vessels, did he put among the treasures of the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48259e48-9070-476e-873a-ae827273956c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 289

Reference: 1KI 8:1
Text: Then Solomon assembled the elders of Israel, and all the heads of the tribes, the chief of the fathers of the children of Israel, unto king Solomon in Jerusalem, that they might bring up the ark of the covenant of the LORD out of the city of David, which is Zion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30ae0af3-a2ab-4466-9094-6daf98f2acde>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 1KI 8:2
Text: And all the men of Israel assembled themselves unto king Solomon at the feast in the month Ethanim, which is the seventh month.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e422fc09-87f7-4561-8b47-d5aa8f0c9b72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: 1KI 8:3
Text: And all the elders of Israel came, and the priests took up the ark.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5c5de07-6f75-4469-8a59-9c9e6319da46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: 1KI 8:4
Text: And they brought up the ark of the LORD, and the tabernacle of the congregation, and all the holy vessels that were in the tabernacle, even those did the priests and the Levites bring up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37aae9c9-ffee-42a6-9931-d8ee1962892e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: 1KI 8:5
Text: And king Solomon, and all the congregation of Israel, that were assembled unto him, were with him before the ark, sacrificing sheep and oxen, that could not be told nor numbered for multitude.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e83ea2e9-2d59-4643-8708-a652e37af1f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: 1KI 8:6
Text: And the priests brought in the ark of the covenant of the LORD unto his place, into the oracle of the house, to the most holy place, even under the wings of the cherubims.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e2cc59e-53fe-4223-9e1e-8377ae2203d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: 1KI 8:7
Text: For the cherubims spread forth their two wings over the place of the ark, and the cherubims covered the ark and the staves thereof above.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:131be31a-fe90-4a2a-b810-d454cf38c700>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 1KI 8:8
Text: And they drew out the staves, that the ends of the staves were seen out in the holy place before the oracle, and they were not seen without: and there they are unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22b37b51-be28-41b2-9e02-cd86dc8b5182>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: 1KI 8:9
Text: There was nothing in the ark save the two tables of stone, which Moses put there at Horeb, when the LORD made a covenant with the children of Israel, when they came out of the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33916966-841f-4d4e-8e4c-6271849be0a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: 1KI 8:10
Text: And it came to pass, when the priests were come out of the holy place, that the cloud filled the house of the LORD,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a85278d-b034-4f71-be66-1bed182bcf7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: 1KI 8:11
Text: So that the priests could not stand to minister because of the cloud: for the glory of the LORD had filled the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c8ba961-474a-4565-a7ce-3403e8e15a86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: 1KI 8:12
Text: Then spake Solomon, The LORD said that he would dwell in the thick darkness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6dbf5d86-ed56-4c5b-8eda-447a710dccdf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: 1KI 8:13
Text: I have surely built thee an house to dwell in, a settled place for thee to abide in for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8312bb61-c37a-4b10-b4c3-70cd03bfec01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: 1KI 8:14
Text: And the king turned his face about, and blessed all the congregation of Israel: (and all the congregation of Israel stood;)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fc29d61-4bd6-4e14-b710-59094a90abe4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: 1KI 8:15
Text: And he said, Blessed be the LORD God of Israel, which spake with his mouth unto David my father, and hath with his hand fulfilled it, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5059822d-1513-4e17-be90-781a24e1ca90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: 1KI 8:16
Text: Since the day that I brought forth my people Israel out of Egypt, I chose no city out of all the tribes of Israel to build an house, that my name might be therein; but I chose David to be over my people Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8773ed9f-d48c-4763-ac89-4beb820c9d45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 1KI 8:17
Text: And it was in the heart of David my father to build an house for the name of the LORD God of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3aaff527-7587-4291-a001-3dd74168df2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: 1KI 8:18
Text: And the LORD said unto David my father, Whereas it was in thine heart to build an house unto my name, thou didst well that it was in thine heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88bf2fe1-c5e1-4fad-98fa-c0a56b7f8170>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 1KI 8:19
Text: Nevertheless thou shalt not build the house; but thy son that shall come forth out of thy loins, he shall build the house unto my name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d42ff1ff-8e4a-4ca6-bc21-4d7ea510db44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: 1KI 8:20
Text: And the LORD hath performed his word that he spake, and I am risen up in the room of David my father, and sit on the throne of Israel, as the LORD promised, and have built an house for the name of the LORD God of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:054e7dcb-56d7-497d-97d3-49a4dd268352>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: 1KI 8:21
Text: And I have set there a place for the ark, wherein is the covenant of the LORD, which he made with our fathers, when he brought them out of the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2664a520-3414-473a-adc6-bfbc4c20ffa6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: 1KI 8:22
Text: And Solomon stood before the altar of the LORD in the presence of all the congregation of Israel, and spread forth his hands toward heaven:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75b89d6d-bdd8-4610-acc3-6981041a6fce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: 1KI 8:23
Text: And he said, LORD God of Israel, there is no God like thee, in heaven above, or on earth beneath, who keepest covenant and mercy with thy servants that walk before thee with all their heart:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:040214c0-fdb8-4b30-885e-7f88f2e2767d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: 1KI 8:24
Text: Who hast kept with thy servant David my father that thou promisedst him: thou spakest also with thy mouth, and hast fulfilled it with thine hand, as it is this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68f3041c-5d1f-4ca2-84bf-81b878a1c8ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 310

Reference: 1KI 8:25
Text: Therefore now, LORD God of Israel, keep with thy servant David my father that thou promisedst him, saying, There shall not fail thee a man in my sight to sit on the throne of Israel; so that thy children take heed to their way, that they walk before me as thou hast walked before me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0259ef8-11ed-47dc-a60d-9de93652d122>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 1KI 8:26
Text: And now, O God of Israel, let thy word, I pray thee, be verified, which thou spakest unto thy servant David my father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f99cd4a6-f052-4376-a93f-aec4cbe68149>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: 1KI 8:27
Text: But will God indeed dwell on the earth? behold, the heaven and heaven of heavens cannot contain thee; how much less this house that I have builded?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dedda80f-7532-486e-9428-985841693019>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: 1KI 8:28
Text: Yet have thou respect unto the prayer of thy servant, and to his supplication, O LORD my God, to hearken unto the cry and to the prayer, which thy servant prayeth before thee to day:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:247b5b4f-779e-4ea1-a0cb-de730a8dab6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: 1KI 8:29
Text: That thine eyes may be open toward this house night and day, even toward the place of which thou hast said, My name shall be there: that thou mayest hearken unto the prayer which thy servant shall make toward this place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58be16c9-a961-43a3-965d-f55990140aa4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: 1KI 8:30
Text: And hearken thou to the supplication of thy servant, and of thy people Israel, when they shall pray toward this place: and hear thou in heaven thy dwelling place: and when thou hearest, forgive.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b68ad7a-9380-43a5-bc16-14470d7979f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 1KI 8:31
Text: If any man trespass against his neighbour, and an oath be laid upon him to cause him to swear, and the oath come before thine altar in this house:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e288923-b37b-47a3-ae56-27812dd4eb95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: 1KI 8:32
Text: Then hear thou in heaven, and do, and judge thy servants, condemning the wicked, to bring his way upon his head; and justifying the righteous, to give him according to his righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96eefd6f-c7f2-4ca0-9437-9d51036e8e38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: 1KI 8:33
Text: When thy people Israel be smitten down before the enemy, because they have sinned against thee, and shall turn again to thee, and confess thy name, and pray, and make supplication unto thee in this house:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fce18794-e192-4fcc-b099-a080f73a3b6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 1KI 8:34
Text: Then hear thou in heaven, and forgive the sin of thy people Israel, and bring them again unto the land which thou gavest unto their fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8ed2f59-b6de-4a2a-8995-854a08ef79fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: 1KI 8:35
Text: When heaven is shut up, and there is no rain, because they have sinned against thee; if they pray toward this place, and confess thy name, and turn from their sin, when thou afflictest them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf6a202e-f1fa-4ca4-8795-06f1ee47043a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: 1KI 8:36
Text: Then hear thou in heaven, and forgive the sin of thy servants, and of thy people Israel, that thou teach them the good way wherein they should walk, and give rain upon thy land, which thou hast given to thy people for an inheritance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33e6190b-27ae-4e9a-9c03-060e1e5858fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: 1KI 8:37
Text: If there be in the land famine, if there be pestilence, blasting, mildew, locust, or if there be caterpiller; if their enemy besiege them in the land of their cities; whatsoever plague, whatsoever sickness there be;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76ca57e8-9eb6-426e-980b-29a41e2774c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: 1KI 8:38
Text: What prayer and supplication soever be made by any man, or by all thy people Israel, which shall know every man the plague of his own heart, and spread forth his hands toward this house:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2e850ec-d12f-4159-bb29-9cdf9edbe0bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: 1KI 8:39
Text: Then hear thou in heaven thy dwelling place, and forgive, and do, and give to every man according to his ways, whose heart thou knowest; (for thou, even thou only, knowest the hearts of all the children of men;)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4efc8b99-fadd-41c0-a56a-143fe6c04c3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: 1KI 8:40
Text: That they may fear thee all the days that they live in the land which thou gavest unto our fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9241c372-20e4-4ddd-9fbf-90dbac0b5c93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 1KI 8:41
Text: Moreover concerning a stranger, that is not of thy people Israel, but cometh out of a far country for thy name’s sake;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:840f9bb7-613e-43aa-813c-c731f330422f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: 1KI 8:42
Text: (For they shall hear of thy great name, and of thy strong hand, and of thy stretched out arm;) when he shall come and pray toward this house;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b587aa5e-81d6-434d-86dc-e81f64126ea0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 301

Reference: 1KI 8:43
Text: Hear thou in heaven thy dwelling place, and do according to all that the stranger calleth to thee for: that all people of the earth may know thy name, to fear thee, as do thy people Israel; and that they may know that this house, which I have builded, is called by thy name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8be29594-0038-48a7-b7b8-0fb27e24e26c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: 1KI 8:44
Text: If thy people go out to battle against their enemy, whithersoever thou shalt send them, and shall pray unto the LORD toward the city which thou hast chosen, and toward the house that I have built for thy name:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e7dba4f-6456-43c1-9902-bcbb52958d84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: 1KI 8:45
Text: Then hear thou in heaven their prayer and their supplication, and maintain their cause.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b7f17c8-e287-4af1-b3ac-7d020afa5e2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: 1KI 8:46
Text: If they sin against thee, (for there is no man that sinneth not,) and thou be angry with them, and deliver them to the enemy, so that they carry them away captives unto the land of the enemy, far or near;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b03243a-e72b-4b9f-9442-74a4d6258379>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 283

Reference: 1KI 8:47
Text: Yet if they shall bethink themselves in the land whither they were carried captives, and repent, and make supplication unto thee in the land of them that carried them captives, saying, We have sinned, and have done perversely, we have committed wickedness;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80b666ba-cfe7-41f0-8c42-9c7c823c03d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 312

Reference: 1KI 8:48
Text: And so return unto thee with all their heart, and with all their soul, in the land of their enemies, which led them away captive, and pray unto thee toward their land, which thou gavest unto their fathers, the city which thou hast chosen, and the house which I have built for thy name:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4aa4ef3a-c6e6-4cee-9b01-ab4f8c9e1155>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: 1KI 8:49
Text: Then hear thou their prayer and their supplication in heaven thy dwelling place, and maintain their cause,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4cc8cb3f-a053-49f8-a6f7-22e9fc3a4085>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: 1KI 8:50
Text: And forgive thy people that have sinned against thee, and all their transgressions wherein they have transgressed against thee, and give them compassion before them who carried them captive, that they may have compassion on them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d589f549-d523-4a32-8337-5213c273ff26>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: 1KI 8:51
Text: For they be thy people, and thine inheritance, which thou broughtest forth out of Egypt, from the midst of the furnace of iron:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78ed5855-c6a9-4895-a35e-9b49de3741b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: 1KI 8:52
Text: That thine eyes may be open unto the supplication of thy servant, and unto the supplication of thy people Israel, to hearken unto them in all that they call for unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6df32a20-6604-4d4f-b00d-9d9cc3e49c70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: 1KI 8:53
Text: For thou didst separate them from among all the people of the earth, to be thine inheritance, as thou spakest by the hand of Moses thy servant, when thou broughtest our fathers out of Egypt, O LORD God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e92cdd54-cc9f-4b58-a33d-82212fa188d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: 1KI 8:54
Text: And it was so, that when Solomon had made an end of praying all this prayer and supplication unto the LORD, he arose from before the altar of the LORD, from kneeling on his knees with his hands spread up to heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/55
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b564874-6596-4563-88a4-466e58b03271>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: 1KI 8:55
Text: And he stood, and blessed all the congregation of Israel with a loud voice, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/56
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2eecf5b0-36ce-45da-9e43-93a25571c5bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: 1KI 8:56
Text: Blessed be the LORD, that hath given rest unto his people Israel, according to all that he promised: there hath not failed one word of all his good promise, which he promised by the hand of Moses his servant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/57
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b31f1e42-55ee-4e44-80af-25a01b652d7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 1KI 8:57
Text: The LORD our God be with us, as he was with our fathers: let him not leave us, nor forsake us:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/58
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f87f816-367d-4c4f-99c3-0a0917a0c63c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: 1KI 8:58
Text: That he may incline our hearts unto him, to walk in all his ways, and to keep his commandments, and his statutes, and his judgments, which he commanded our fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/59
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce03ae76-8a4f-4908-bb30-0633309a2c5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: 1KI 8:59
Text: And let these my words, wherewith I have made supplication before the LORD, be nigh unto the LORD our God day and night, that he maintain the cause of his servant, and the cause of his people Israel at all times, as the matter shall require:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/60
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70921a62-590e-4dd6-87c2-085c0b1e5e23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: 1KI 8:60
Text: That all the people of the earth may know that the LORD is God, and that there is none else.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/61
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed96c6fe-e882-4126-ab24-f090f0fe3d28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: 1KI 8:61
Text: Let your heart therefore be perfect with the LORD our God, to walk in his statutes, and to keep his commandments, as at this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/62
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d2b14f9-5747-49da-aa95-c912a311b924>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: 1KI 8:62
Text: And the king, and all Israel with him, offered sacrifice before the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/63
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70d2b4d4-63d5-4e8f-a6da-285d3d5075ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: 1KI 8:63
Text: And Solomon offered a sacrifice of peace offerings, which he offered unto the LORD, two and twenty thousand oxen, and an hundred and twenty thousand sheep. So the king and all the children of Israel dedicated the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/64
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac5fe070-9640-423c-8882-b4053b39788f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 369

Reference: 1KI 8:64
Text: The same day did the king hallow the middle of the court that was before the house of the LORD: for there he offered burnt offerings, and meat offerings, and the fat of the peace offerings: because the brasen altar that was before the LORD was too little to receive the burnt offerings, and meat offerings, and the fat of the peace offerings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/65
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06b3cbac-d6c7-4b0d-ada1-783d3e28952f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: 1KI 8:65
Text: And at that time Solomon held a feast, and all Israel with him, a great congregation, from the entering in of Hamath unto the river of Egypt, before the LORD our God, seven days and seven days, even fourteen days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/8/66
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:831e0d46-a55d-4dbd-bf47-f4ebd167ab1e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: 1KI 8:66
Text: On the eighth day he sent the people away: and they blessed the king, and went unto their tents joyful and glad of heart for all the goodness that the LORD had done for David his servant, and for Israel his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41746980-fde4-4d1a-b728-47fc2561fa49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: 1KI 9:1
Text: And it came to pass, when Solomon had finished the building of the house of the LORD, and the king’s house, and all Solomon’s desire which he was pleased to do,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59eb0b88-e214-4342-a3dc-1223042e72d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: 1KI 9:2
Text: That the LORD appeared to Solomon the second time, as he had appeared unto him at Gibeon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e98ac3ca-440b-4267-81d5-cf5a5e3cf168>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: 1KI 9:3
Text: And the LORD said unto him, I have heard thy prayer and thy supplication, that thou hast made before me: I have hallowed this house, which thou hast built, to put my name there for ever; and mine eyes and mine heart shall be there perpetually.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18e61d43-d269-4f15-9203-7d8338199389>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: 1KI 9:4
Text: And if thou wilt walk before me, as David thy father walked, in integrity of heart, and in uprightness, to do according to all that I have commanded thee, and wilt keep my statutes and my judgments:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c14033b-43ad-45ae-b489-af1336e4e303>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: 1KI 9:5
Text: Then I will establish the throne of thy kingdom upon Israel for ever, as I promised to David thy father, saying, There shall not fail thee a man upon the throne of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22623877-b0a7-4833-89ac-4563d6054cbd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: 1KI 9:6
Text: But if ye shall at all turn from following me, ye or your children, and will not keep my commandments and my statutes which I have set before you, but go and serve other gods, and worship them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:380aa001-8630-4f6e-bdb8-2e29a82701c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: 1KI 9:7
Text: Then will I cut off Israel out of the land which I have given them; and this house, which I have hallowed for my name, will I cast out of my sight; and Israel shall be a proverb and a byword among all people:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5153aea-19d0-43b9-a045-1340000e9bf2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: 1KI 9:8
Text: And at this house, which is high, every one that passeth by it shall be astonished, and shall hiss; and they shall say, Why hath the LORD done thus unto this land, and to this house?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bf8ba3e-92db-46b3-b618-c5eb3cde1fcd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: 1KI 9:9
Text: And they shall answer, Because they forsook the LORD their God, who brought forth their fathers out of the land of Egypt, and have taken hold upon other gods, and have worshipped them, and served them: therefore hath the LORD brought upon them all this evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:417bb6b1-186c-401f-9777-70042e59f16b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 1KI 9:10
Text: And it came to pass at the end of twenty years, when Solomon had built the two houses, the house of the LORD, and the king’s house,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a538ffda-8197-432e-a1f0-1999e9ef0aa6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: 1KI 9:11
Text: (Now Hiram the king of Tyre had furnished Solomon with cedar trees and fir trees, and with gold, according to all his desire,) that then king Solomon gave Hiram twenty cities in the land of Galilee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0af6c7d8-e5f9-41ab-8485-8c92255b5715>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 1KI 9:12
Text: And Hiram came out from Tyre to see the cities which Solomon had given him; and they pleased him not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c585fe95-491e-4930-8147-6d20bcd7a056>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: 1KI 9:13
Text: And he said, What cities are these which thou hast given me, my brother? And he called them the land of Cabul unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18fcdb64-6d36-41b8-a271-e5bc69b2fd82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: 1KI 9:14
Text: And Hiram sent to the king sixscore talents of gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74704db4-1aa6-4847-9640-6d85e6f8f6d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: 1KI 9:15
Text: And this is the reason of the levy which king Solomon raised; for to build the house of the LORD, and his own house, and Millo, and the wall of Jerusalem, and Hazor, and Megiddo, and Gezer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f14428f7-a36d-425b-ae03-54d5c429f464>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: 1KI 9:16
Text: For Pharaoh king of Egypt had gone up, and taken Gezer, and burnt it with fire, and slain the Canaanites that dwelt in the city, and given it for a present unto his daughter, Solomon’s wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5370e64a-a7ea-4fb1-8668-f7ba09616413>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: 1KI 9:17
Text: And Solomon built Gezer, and Bethhoron the nether,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5fec184-4033-47e6-aed2-f5f638b671b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: 1KI 9:18
Text: And Baalath, and Tadmor in the wilderness, in the land,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3e4b254-8ccd-44c6-b910-aff03ddc5ca2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: 1KI 9:19
Text: And all the cities of store that Solomon had, and cities for his chariots, and cities for his horsemen, and that which Solomon desired to build in Jerusalem, and in Lebanon, and in all the land of his dominion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aab18b4b-5220-40f0-86d0-8b576edace15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: 1KI 9:20
Text: And all the people that were left of the Amorites, Hittites, Perizzites, Hivites, and Jebusites, which were not of the children of Israel,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e695517-3cde-4933-ac55-7643fedf1e1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: 1KI 9:21
Text: Their children that were left after them in the land, whom the children of Israel also were not able utterly to destroy, upon those did Solomon levy a tribute of bondservice unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:246c37db-ec17-41a8-ac7c-06fd57b1764e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: 1KI 9:22
Text: But of the children of Israel did Solomon make no bondmen: but they were men of war, and his servants, and his princes, and his captains, and rulers of his chariots, and his horsemen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb24bd33-412b-4a18-85d0-0e254f3358e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: 1KI 9:23
Text: These were the chief of the officers that were over Solomon’s work, five hundred and fifty, which bare rule over the people that wrought in the work.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f799c0cf-8868-479a-8b94-58678ce1349a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 1KI 9:24
Text: But Pharaoh’s daughter came up out of the city of David unto her house which Solomon had built for her: then did he build Millo.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f7a06dd-07a9-4332-a085-9713765caa11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: 1KI 9:25
Text: And three times in a year did Solomon offer burnt offerings and peace offerings upon the altar which he built unto the LORD, and he burnt incense upon the altar that was before the LORD. So he finished the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06161df8-5edd-4d29-b69c-bcceaa6e7f22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: 1KI 9:26
Text: And king Solomon made a navy of ships in Eziongeber, which is beside Eloth, on the shore of the Red sea, in the land of Edom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19301e6a-76ad-4865-9484-6002cc1957f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: 1KI 9:27
Text: And Hiram sent in the navy his servants, shipmen that had knowledge of the sea, with the servants of Solomon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/9/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66060ff9-5c4c-4a7a-8fcb-df7591447b73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 1KI 9:28
Text: And they came to Ophir, and fetched from thence gold, four hundred and twenty talents, and brought it to king Solomon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce3cb605-6236-43f9-8589-583e64706bd0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: 1KI 10:1
Text: And when the queen of Sheba heard of the fame of Solomon concerning the name of the LORD, she came to prove him with hard questions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76dc1cdd-2b13-4838-a879-348088d21fa0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: 1KI 10:2
Text: And she came to Jerusalem with a very great train, with camels that bare spices, and very much gold, and precious stones: and when she was come to Solomon, she communed with him of all that was in her heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a89d9bd-572a-4838-a73f-ffa91cf9119f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 1KI 10:3
Text: And Solomon told her all her questions: there was not any thing hid from the king, which he told her not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b1c3824-e9f8-4f5e-a75f-c457cc51ae95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: 1KI 10:4
Text: And when the queen of Sheba had seen all Solomon’s wisdom, and the house that he had built,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a77b4161-fded-4c27-a0f7-81c7cf1aa060>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: 1KI 10:5
Text: And the meat of his table, and the sitting of his servants, and the attendance of his ministers, and their apparel, and his cupbearers, and his ascent by which he went up unto the house of the LORD; there was no more spirit in her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:745967bd-a704-400c-81a6-7075d12cc1d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: 1KI 10:6
Text: And she said to the king, It was a true report that I heard in mine own land of thy acts and of thy wisdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:543e4d9d-0cfc-4677-b4b5-a81bb8197517>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 1KI 10:7
Text: Howbeit I believed not the words, until I came, and mine eyes had seen it: and, behold, the half was not told me: thy wisdom and prosperity exceedeth the fame which I heard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a8472d8-587f-4955-bf59-82d38800db33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: 1KI 10:8
Text: Happy are thy men, happy are these thy servants, which stand continually before thee, and that hear thy wisdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4eb7c49f-2bbc-42e8-b11b-d69c909a9fdd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: 1KI 10:9
Text: Blessed be the LORD thy God, which delighted in thee, to set thee on the throne of Israel: because the LORD loved Israel for ever, therefore made he thee king, to do judgment and justice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe9ee5a7-ab51-413e-978e-906b90870e43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: 1KI 10:10
Text: And she gave the king an hundred and twenty talents of gold, and of spices very great store, and precious stones: there came no more such abundance of spices as these which the queen of Sheba gave to king Solomon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:834b5879-b397-4bde-98a4-5fb0f891ab49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 1KI 10:11
Text: And the navy also of Hiram, that brought gold from Ophir, brought in from Ophir great plenty of almug trees, and precious stones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1410b5e8-7924-4d44-ad39-df09772a7227>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: 1KI 10:12
Text: And the king made of the almug trees pillars for the house of the LORD, and for the king’s house, harps also and psalteries for singers: there came no such almug trees, nor were seen unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:818040f9-dace-47bd-86be-59d4b7905d5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: 1KI 10:13
Text: And king Solomon gave unto the queen of Sheba all her desire, whatsoever she asked, beside that which Solomon gave her of his royal bounty. So she turned and went to her own country, she and her servants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d87a9b5-53e9-481f-8ccb-cc2e3e5a19f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 1KI 10:14
Text: Now the weight of gold that came to Solomon in one year was six hundred threescore and six talents of gold,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:198bf8ff-fe64-4b93-b48d-47f4d36895bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 1KI 10:15
Text: Beside that he had of the merchantmen, and of the traffick of the spice merchants, and of all the kings of Arabia, and of the governors of the country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0dbae98-b2cf-4662-9459-b40aacd28ebd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: 1KI 10:16
Text: And king Solomon made two hundred targets of beaten gold: six hundred shekels of gold went to one target.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f31741fd-a7b0-4f3b-bdb0-dc36b76dbc9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: 1KI 10:17
Text: And he made three hundred shields of beaten gold; three pound of gold went to one shield: and the king put them in the house of the forest of Lebanon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f5f9abb-4868-4914-ba98-d3e2cb134a81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: 1KI 10:18
Text: Moreover the king made a great throne of ivory, and overlaid it with the best gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c5f1296-8cf5-4831-9b8f-169677a71f5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: 1KI 10:19
Text: The throne had six steps, and the top of the throne was round behind: and there were stays on either side on the place of the seat, and two lions stood beside the stays.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee2570f2-adfa-47ae-9d6f-afae6ed6cb29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 1KI 10:20
Text: And twelve lions stood there on the one side and on the other upon the six steps: there was not the like made in any kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84609f4e-0571-4560-a7fe-0a81dd252977>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: 1KI 10:21
Text: And all king Solomon’s drinking vessels were of gold, and all the vessels of the house of the forest of Lebanon were of pure gold; none were of silver: it was nothing accounted of in the days of Solomon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:493c2ce8-4b04-4d95-9b97-e4294d092e4f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: 1KI 10:22
Text: For the king had at sea a navy of Tharshish with the navy of Hiram: once in three years came the navy of Tharshish, bringing gold, and silver, ivory, and apes, and peacocks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3595baa2-9517-434b-b332-f984ef048950>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: 1KI 10:23
Text: So king Solomon exceeded all the kings of the earth for riches and for wisdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da266359-51ef-4458-9f10-681fb6bb1894>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: 1KI 10:24
Text: And all the earth sought to Solomon, to hear his wisdom, which God had put in his heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1aab12d7-ce63-45b5-8814-d16b11385d65>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 1KI 10:25
Text: And they brought every man his present, vessels of silver, and vessels of gold, and garments, and armour, and spices, horses, and mules, a rate year by year.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e35723c-3472-47f8-8114-37ee750911ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: 1KI 10:26
Text: And Solomon gathered together chariots and horsemen: and he had a thousand and four hundred chariots, and twelve thousand horsemen, whom he bestowed in the cities for chariots, and with the king at Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e523a30-a26d-4abb-b9c0-06812994e831>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: 1KI 10:27
Text: And the king made silver to be in Jerusalem as stones, and cedars made he to be as the sycomore trees that are in the vale, for abundance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5889cfb4-fddc-4c42-9a56-e4d870ac1c10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 1KI 10:28
Text: And Solomon had horses brought out of Egypt, and linen yarn: the king’s merchants received the linen yarn at a price.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/10/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:590706fe-8d91-4b49-a6f0-fd16abcb83ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: 1KI 10:29
Text: And a chariot came up and went out of Egypt for six hundred shekels of silver, and an horse for an hundred and fifty: and so for all the kings of the Hittites, and for the kings of Syria, did they bring them out by their means.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c647bad-f553-4386-bc54-4ada93e509ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 1KI 11:1
Text: But king Solomon loved many strange women, together with the daughter of Pharaoh, women of the Moabites, Ammonites, Edomites, Zidonians, and Hittites:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffc44ff1-667d-494e-9949-794f99a7ec57>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: 1KI 11:2
Text: Of the nations concerning which the LORD said unto the children of Israel, Ye shall not go in to them, neither shall they come in unto you: for surely they will turn away your heart after their gods: Solomon clave unto these in love.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3e1fc9a-fe84-4fec-addb-4b7e7df4a4ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 1KI 11:3
Text: And he had seven hundred wives, princesses, and three hundred concubines: and his wives turned away his heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4494e33-7051-4d54-9fdd-2540da5281d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: 1KI 11:4
Text: For it came to pass, when Solomon was old, that his wives turned away his heart after other gods: and his heart was not perfect with the LORD his God, as was the heart of David his father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb6a679c-d9d4-4395-a470-d28c758dda25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 1KI 11:5
Text: For Solomon went after Ashtoreth the goddess of the Zidonians, and after Milcom the abomination of the Ammonites.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d81f24e9-a0df-4881-8760-315a6c87d1fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: 1KI 11:6
Text: And Solomon did evil in the sight of the LORD, and went not fully after the LORD, as did David his father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b446ff7-0616-4182-92b2-39be4e8db3ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: 1KI 11:7
Text: Then did Solomon build an high place for Chemosh, the abomination of Moab, in the hill that is before Jerusalem, and for Molech, the abomination of the children of Ammon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c0c3c93-31e0-4fe6-afce-f75f4bdef888>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: 1KI 11:8
Text: And likewise did he for all his strange wives, which burnt incense and sacrificed unto their gods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b27ae7b2-d5a4-4603-a5cc-d7e8fd976077>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: 1KI 11:9
Text: And the LORD was angry with Solomon, because his heart was turned from the LORD God of Israel, which had appeared unto him twice,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b41542f5-06e9-4d3d-9329-abcca1618a79>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: 1KI 11:10
Text: And had commanded him concerning this thing, that he should not go after other gods: but he kept not that which the LORD commanded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bfb5fb0-2d6e-4886-9aa7-93d29c6773df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: 1KI 11:11
Text: Wherefore the LORD said unto Solomon, Forasmuch as this is done of thee, and thou hast not kept my covenant and my statutes, which I have commanded thee, I will surely rend the kingdom from thee, and will give it to thy servant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a49f0dba-62e6-46fc-989c-7f3f6560af35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: 1KI 11:12
Text: Notwithstanding in thy days I will not do it for David thy father’s sake: but I will rend it out of the hand of thy son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f37cdcb1-6438-4c7b-8997-1d3627e2cf79>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 1KI 11:13
Text: Howbeit I will not rend away all the kingdom; but will give one tribe to thy son for David my servant’s sake, and for Jerusalem’s sake which I have chosen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c4e51e9-a16a-405c-963f-af84e467dc16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: 1KI 11:14
Text: And the LORD stirred up an adversary unto Solomon, Hadad the Edomite: he was of the king’s seed in Edom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95fa3a0d-69b5-468e-97fa-682bfc90a5f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 1KI 11:15
Text: For it came to pass, when David was in Edom, and Joab the captain of the host was gone up to bury the slain, after he had smitten every male in Edom;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb53c860-8eab-461e-884e-bece1d598607>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: 1KI 11:16
Text: (For six months did Joab remain there with all Israel, until he had cut off every male in Edom:)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7c26251-d7e5-4004-8fdd-170df5a23d70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 1KI 11:17
Text: That Hadad fled, he and certain Edomites of his father’s servants with him, to go into Egypt; Hadad being yet a little child.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b207df8a-be0e-4e6d-b7bb-b5ed1c3bf6bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: 1KI 11:18
Text: And they arose out of Midian, and came to Paran: and they took men with them out of Paran, and they came to Egypt, unto Pharaoh king of Egypt; which gave him an house, and appointed him victuals, and gave him land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c83138ca-ae18-4903-99a8-9f6281176870>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: 1KI 11:19
Text: And Hadad found great favour in the sight of Pharaoh, so that he gave him to wife the sister of his own wife, the sister of Tahpenes the queen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e370dc9e-e8d5-4f7a-a5e1-91fc18370aba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: 1KI 11:20
Text: And the sister of Tahpenes bare him Genubath his son, whom Tahpenes weaned in Pharaoh’s house: and Genubath was in Pharaoh’s household among the sons of Pharaoh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f15d03c3-fc21-498a-a5e6-86635dee00a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: 1KI 11:21
Text: And when Hadad heard in Egypt that David slept with his fathers, and that Joab the captain of the host was dead, Hadad said to Pharaoh, Let me depart, that I may go to mine own country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac2fa731-cb86-481d-bc45-007bafeb369d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: 1KI 11:22
Text: Then Pharaoh said unto him, But what hast thou lacked with me, that, behold, thou seekest to go to thine own country? And he answered, Nothing: howbeit let me go in any wise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ed12179-f10c-4678-ac5d-17b25a09ac5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 1KI 11:23
Text: And God stirred him up another adversary, Rezon the son of Eliadah, which fled from his lord Hadadezer king of Zobah:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8bde5bc-9035-4ab2-b3a7-e31baaeaaccf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: 1KI 11:24
Text: And he gathered men unto him, and became captain over a band, when David slew them of Zobah: and they went to Damascus, and dwelt therein, and reigned in Damascus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02ab6939-0790-44ae-9f20-fa0b24591a61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 1KI 11:25
Text: And he was an adversary to Israel all the days of Solomon, beside the mischief that Hadad did: and he abhorred Israel, and reigned over Syria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4e7c46a-0b4a-4a66-9df5-b13b197b2b7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: 1KI 11:26
Text: And Jeroboam the son of Nebat, an Ephrathite of Zereda, Solomon’s servant, whose mother’s name was Zeruah, a widow woman, even he lifted up his hand against the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19bcc923-1f5e-4007-822b-e3a24591da52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 1KI 11:27
Text: And this was the cause that he lifted up his hand against the king: Solomon built Millo, and repaired the breaches of the city of David his father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b897b823-7713-47fb-93a2-4427a65e298e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: 1KI 11:28
Text: And the man Jeroboam was a mighty man of valour: and Solomon seeing the young man that he was industrious, he made him ruler over all the charge of the house of Joseph.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02431247-8864-49d1-b42a-4fd1022017f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: 1KI 11:29
Text: And it came to pass at that time when Jeroboam went out of Jerusalem, that the prophet Ahijah the Shilonite found him in the way; and he had clad himself with a new garment; and they two were alone in the field:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:843bc241-1e6d-4805-8734-590dc5a953a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: 1KI 11:30
Text: And Ahijah caught the new garment that was on him, and rent it in twelve pieces:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7fc8977-52ec-49c4-bde4-ac14a7ee713a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: 1KI 11:31
Text: And he said to Jeroboam, Take thee ten pieces: for thus saith the LORD, the God of Israel, Behold, I will rend the kingdom out of the hand of Solomon, and will give ten tribes to thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65b509e6-0e27-464b-91b2-bcae4745e380>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: 1KI 11:32
Text: (But he shall have one tribe for my servant David’s sake, and for Jerusalem’s sake, the city which I have chosen out of all the tribes of Israel:)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61e00a61-5e71-47a9-8436-f76545a4fb97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 340

Reference: 1KI 11:33
Text: Because that they have forsaken me, and have worshipped Ashtoreth the goddess of the Zidonians, Chemosh the god of the Moabites, and Milcom the god of the children of Ammon, and have not walked in my ways, to do that which is right in mine eyes, and to keep my statutes and my judgments, as did David his father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc273c35-a1b8-4a96-8cfb-08089c149c19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: 1KI 11:34
Text: Howbeit I will not take the whole kingdom out of his hand: but I will make him prince all the days of his life for David my servant’s sake, whom I chose, because he kept my commandments and my statutes:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3dfa8432-43a3-4bd6-8e87-0e655bd526b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: 1KI 11:35
Text: But I will take the kingdom out of his son’s hand, and will give it unto thee, even ten tribes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2e6699d-083d-46d1-b950-de4ac93aa515>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: 1KI 11:36
Text: And unto his son will I give one tribe, that David my servant may have a light alway before me in Jerusalem, the city which I have chosen me to put my name there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07cf5cf7-2125-419a-8d11-1c0bd6a92379>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: 1KI 11:37
Text: And I will take thee, and thou shalt reign according to all that thy soul desireth, and shalt be king over Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
