Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 330

Reference: 1KI 11:38
Text: And it shall be, if thou wilt hearken unto all that I command thee, and wilt walk in my ways, and do that is right in my sight, to keep my statutes and my commandments, as David my servant did; that I will be with thee, and build thee a sure house, as I built for David, and will give Israel unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e5b5a2e-ea68-49a6-8023-854422e1be05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: 1KI 11:39
Text: And I will for this afflict the seed of David, but not for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99ea8d3c-9262-4bda-bbe1-255d091a7432>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: 1KI 11:40
Text: Solomon sought therefore to kill Jeroboam. And Jeroboam arose, and fled into Egypt, unto Shishak king of Egypt, and was in Egypt until the death of Solomon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11fbe922-a735-44a4-9426-f701c9abe277>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 1KI 11:41
Text: And the rest of the acts of Solomon, and all that he did, and his wisdom, are they not written in the book of the acts of Solomon?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83bad47f-50ed-4b33-b708-d7a2b9fee56e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: 1KI 11:42
Text: And the time that Solomon reigned in Jerusalem over all Israel was forty years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/11/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbb07018-bae7-43a1-9ec7-efbf1ab8c0c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: 1KI 11:43
Text: And Solomon slept with his fathers, and was buried in the city of David his father: and Rehoboam his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a41257d-b21a-4f87-a790-9d6e508fec0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: 1KI 12:1
Text: And Rehoboam went to Shechem: for all Israel were come to Shechem to make him king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f52a823-aee4-4fd5-87dd-76119c6d65cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: 1KI 12:2
Text: And it came to pass, when Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who was yet in Egypt, heard of it, (for he was fled from the presence of king Solomon, and Jeroboam dwelt in Egypt;)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:636cd49b-22f9-426a-a414-9a81036d0615>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: 1KI 12:3
Text: That they sent and called him. And Jeroboam and all the congregation of Israel came, and spake unto Rehoboam, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f30c9df8-faf1-4bad-b7f4-5a7411eb46e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: 1KI 12:4
Text: Thy father made our yoke grievous: now therefore make thou the grievous service of thy father, and his heavy yoke which he put upon us, lighter, and we will serve thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfe986c6-197b-4433-88ad-178acf81615a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: 1KI 12:5
Text: And he said unto them, Depart yet for three days, then come again to me. And the people departed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f5dcce4-bd30-44e4-9307-a7396fe9e475>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 1KI 12:6
Text: And king Rehoboam consulted with the old men, that stood before Solomon his father while he yet lived, and said, How do ye advise that I may answer this people?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea485202-853e-4d7d-a866-b47586eaf6e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: 1KI 12:7
Text: And they spake unto him, saying, If thou wilt be a servant unto this people this day, and wilt serve them, and answer them, and speak good words to them, then they will be thy servants for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:565879c1-6b33-4397-9a16-4b3d91f4d6b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 1KI 12:8
Text: But he forsook the counsel of the old men, which they had given him, and consulted with the young men that were grown up with him, and which stood before him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3f72b7b-b552-4a37-b6ea-5277bd28eb99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: 1KI 12:9
Text: And he said unto them, What counsel give ye that we may answer this people, who have spoken to me, saying, Make the yoke which thy father did put upon us lighter?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0acc436c-8aec-41eb-a03c-36ce57717a5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 323

Reference: 1KI 12:10
Text: And the young men that were grown up with him spake unto him, saying, Thus shalt thou speak unto this people that spake unto thee, saying, Thy father made our yoke heavy, but make thou it lighter unto us; thus shalt thou say unto them, My little finger shall be thicker than my father’s loins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7153dcc-da1d-47ba-a456-e865f7a66332>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: 1KI 12:11
Text: And now whereas my father did lade you with a heavy yoke, I will add to your yoke: my father hath chastised you with whips, but I will chastise you with scorpions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04984303-0fcf-4a12-aeb4-2bbdb6782f8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 1KI 12:12
Text: So Jeroboam and all the people came to Rehoboam the third day, as the king had appointed, saying, Come to me again the third day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35157b8c-514c-4212-a012-c8c936fac563>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: 1KI 12:13
Text: And the king answered the people roughly, and forsook the old men’s counsel that they gave him;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:993e8416-8199-4c8d-bcff-01d0082c03c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: 1KI 12:14
Text: And spake to them after the counsel of the young men, saying, My father made your yoke heavy, and I will add to your yoke: my father also chastised you with whips, but I will chastise you with scorpions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:634b06db-84c2-4b27-8497-1099ad046494>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: 1KI 12:15
Text: Wherefore the king hearkened not unto the people; for the cause was from the LORD, that he might perform his saying, which the LORD spake by Ahijah the Shilonite unto Jeroboam the son of Nebat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbc3dbe5-f83b-4175-a4e6-51576dbcbf8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 304

Reference: 1KI 12:16
Text: So when all Israel saw that the king hearkened not unto them, the people answered the king, saying, What portion have we in David? neither have we inheritance in the son of Jesse: to your tents, O Israel: now see to thine own house, David. So Israel departed unto their tents.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8978bc84-9743-45f6-9b1d-0a71ddc5c76f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: 1KI 12:17
Text: But as for the children of Israel which dwelt in the cities of Judah, Rehoboam reigned over them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d647358-1d00-43ba-9142-355a49d15a22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: 1KI 12:18
Text: Then king Rehoboam sent Adoram, who was over the tribute; and all Israel stoned him with stones, that he died. Therefore king Rehoboam made speed to get him up to his chariot, to flee to Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7d4d715-0704-4713-9dd9-e14314294580>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: 1KI 12:19
Text: So Israel rebelled against the house of David unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae286229-a4fc-4f9c-83db-3aa7b18f69e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 266

Reference: 1KI 12:20
Text: And it came to pass, when all Israel heard that Jeroboam was come again, that they sent and called him unto the congregation, and made him king over all Israel: there was none that followed the house of David, but the tribe of Judah only.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc2cddea-fcbc-4a10-a480-d998670f432e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 297

Reference: 1KI 12:21
Text: And when Rehoboam was come to Jerusalem, he assembled all the house of Judah, with the tribe of Benjamin, an hundred and fourscore thousand chosen men, which were warriors, to fight against the house of Israel, to bring the kingdom again to Rehoboam the son of Solomon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74485f86-c184-428f-b297-3f4cbbfce64a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: 1KI 12:22
Text: But the word of God came unto Shemaiah the man of God, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:865fb74d-70bd-46b9-a873-b81b4a69175c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: 1KI 12:23
Text: Speak unto Rehoboam, the son of Solomon, king of Judah, and unto all the house of Judah and Benjamin, and to the remnant of the people, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55214b05-62b6-4bc2-afd1-128a7ac2e453>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 291

Reference: 1KI 12:24
Text: Thus saith the LORD, Ye shall not go up, nor fight against your brethren the children of Israel: return every man to his house; for this thing is from me. They hearkened therefore to the word of the LORD, and returned to depart, according to the word of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d703a2ba-89dd-4439-bb57-ff88a2734954>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: 1KI 12:25
Text: Then Jeroboam built Shechem in mount Ephraim, and dwelt therein; and went out from thence, and built Penuel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c5d0622-4af9-4a03-98e7-5b7c4c6c84dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: 1KI 12:26
Text: And Jeroboam said in his heart, Now shall the kingdom return to the house of David:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab8e2e1c-8165-4bfc-b77b-4581fee9eb16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: 1KI 12:27
Text: If this people go up to do sacrifice in the house of the LORD at Jerusalem, then shall the heart of this people turn again unto their lord, even unto Rehoboam king of Judah, and they shall kill me, and go again to Rehoboam king of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8207afd4-27ea-4fb0-beca-7c197570041e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: 1KI 12:28
Text: Whereupon the king took counsel, and made two calves of gold, and said unto them, It is too much for you to go up to Jerusalem: behold thy gods, O Israel, which brought thee up out of the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9022dbdd-2493-4b41-8b5a-8622048577cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: 1KI 12:29
Text: And he set the one in Bethel, and the other put he in Dan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c9c089c-500f-4752-8eaf-f75ecd38a5f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: 1KI 12:30
Text: And this thing became a sin: for the people went to worship before the one, even unto Dan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09da1d32-9d5d-4b57-9821-3bdbcbf98d7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: 1KI 12:31
Text: And he made an house of high places, and made priests of the lowest of the people, which were not of the sons of Levi.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fad1bf1-f058-4e39-b09c-fe21d0f0535f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 323

Reference: 1KI 12:32
Text: And Jeroboam ordained a feast in the eighth month, on the fifteenth day of the month, like unto the feast that is in Judah, and he offered upon the altar. So did he in Bethel, sacrificing unto the calves that he had made: and he placed in Bethel the priests of the high places which he had made.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/12/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d688c060-3ff7-49a5-88c1-7514ca7d4437>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 280

Reference: 1KI 12:33
Text: So he offered upon the altar which he had made in Bethel the fifteenth day of the eighth month, even in the month which he had devised of his own heart; and ordained a feast unto the children of Israel: and he offered upon the altar, and burnt incense.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1870cf12-ceb1-4b10-ab37-ae97c19efcb8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 1KI 13:1
Text: And, behold, there came a man of God out of Judah by the word of the LORD unto Bethel: and Jeroboam stood by the altar to burn incense.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:041b189b-b8f4-4e67-9827-fe0c836dbedc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 333

Reference: 1KI 13:2
Text: And he cried against the altar in the word of the LORD, and said, O altar, altar, thus saith the LORD; Behold, a child shall be born unto the house of David, Josiah by name; and upon thee shall he offer the priests of the high places that burn incense upon thee, and men’s bones shall be burnt upon thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eba60f88-c8ca-4e97-8ebb-25a0000d6eed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: 1KI 13:3
Text: And he gave a sign the same day, saying, This is the sign which the LORD hath spoken; Behold, the altar shall be rent, and the ashes that are upon it shall be poured out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:414d240e-6c7d-446a-b34f-8b362aae9559>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 317

Reference: 1KI 13:4
Text: And it came to pass, when king Jeroboam heard the saying of the man of God, which had cried against the altar in Bethel, that he put forth his hand from the altar, saying, Lay hold on him. And his hand, which he put forth against him, dried up, so that he could not pull it in again to him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5f6d1cd-7789-4f0b-a1a2-5987482956e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 1KI 13:5
Text: The altar also was rent, and the ashes poured out from the altar, according to the sign which the man of God had given by the word of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cd82622-edf7-407c-9263-1979b191f1b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 289

Reference: 1KI 13:6
Text: And the king answered and said unto the man of God, Intreat now the face of the LORD thy God, and pray for me, that my hand may be restored me again. And the man of God besought the LORD, and the king’s hand was restored him again, and became as it was before.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92a95a48-7706-4130-8dbb-02a9361e5b53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: 1KI 13:7
Text: And the king said unto the man of God, Come home with me, and refresh thyself, and I will give thee a reward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb619f61-bea7-4ce0-b79f-c9fe2ee57d8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 1KI 13:8
Text: And the man of God said unto the king, If thou wilt give me half thine house, I will not go in with thee, neither will I eat bread nor drink water in this place:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:051a9559-9e62-426d-86ef-eea2c190b033>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: 1KI 13:9
Text: For so was it charged me by the word of the LORD, saying, Eat no bread, nor drink water, nor turn again by the same way that thou camest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e8f3559-893a-4ae6-ad2e-3e7167bb1096>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: 1KI 13:10
Text: So he went another way, and returned not by the way that he came to Bethel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74e4325a-1725-42cf-a51c-a3e20dbdbc06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: 1KI 13:11
Text: Now there dwelt an old prophet in Bethel; and his sons came and told him all the works that the man of God had done that day in Bethel: the words which he had spoken unto the king, them they told also to their father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b72f0752-008d-49d9-9192-e56dae9ef5f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 1KI 13:12
Text: And their father said unto them, What way went he? For his sons had seen what way the man of God went, which came from Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58c82751-a874-4d03-a276-b5e69ecfb5a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 1KI 13:13
Text: And he said unto his sons, Saddle me the ass. So they saddled him the ass: and he rode thereon,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bf3bc8f-4e94-4c18-96f0-51121927646e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: 1KI 13:14
Text: And went after the man of God, and found him sitting under an oak: and he said unto him, Art thou the man of God that camest from Judah? And he said, I am.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20d19e16-312d-44b8-8990-02a72cd46655>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: 1KI 13:15
Text: Then he said unto him, Come home with me, and eat bread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7d9f1a1-83b7-4dec-b520-d03e4666ea1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 1KI 13:16
Text: And he said, I may not return with thee, nor go in with thee: neither will I eat bread nor drink water with thee in this place:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f611d52-d12b-4f03-945c-15fe59bd3c66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: 1KI 13:17
Text: For it was said to me by the word of the LORD, Thou shalt eat no bread nor drink water there, nor turn again to go by the way that thou camest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10d43b86-ea8e-4f9f-95d2-8780831cb2c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: 1KI 13:18
Text: He said unto him, I am a prophet also as thou art; and an angel spake unto me by the word of the LORD, saying, Bring him back with thee into thine house, that he may eat bread and drink water. But he lied unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:977ddcad-3089-4ba1-b587-1b03b6036c53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: 1KI 13:19
Text: So he went back with him, and did eat bread in his house, and drank water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eed54a3b-7d9e-4c16-a497-84b6c5216a3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 1KI 13:20
Text: And it came to pass, as they sat at the table, that the word of the LORD came unto the prophet that brought him back:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4a37b7d-8394-4b90-9d06-20abdcac0ab0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: 1KI 13:21
Text: And he cried unto the man of God that came from Judah, saying, Thus saith the LORD, Forasmuch as thou hast disobeyed the mouth of the LORD, and hast not kept the commandment which the LORD thy God commanded thee,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa8782f2-eb48-4a4f-9b49-a4c5b05d5a80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: 1KI 13:22
Text: But camest back, and hast eaten bread and drunk water in the place, of the which the Lord did say to thee, Eat no bread, and drink no water; thy carcase shall not come unto the sepulchre of thy fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7e59003-4b51-482c-a514-7aca0eb5c8f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: 1KI 13:23
Text: And it came to pass, after he had eaten bread, and after he had drunk, that he saddled for him the ass, to wit, for the prophet whom he had brought back.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f01dc1cc-9eb8-453c-acae-eaad06eb0556>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 1KI 13:24
Text: And when he was gone, a lion met him by the way, and slew him: and his carcase was cast in the way, and the ass stood by it, the lion also stood by the carcase.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b515bfe1-66ef-4d2c-bff9-ebf605b1784e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: 1KI 13:25
Text: And, behold, men passed by, and saw the carcase cast in the way, and the lion standing by the carcase: and they came and told it in the city where the old prophet dwelt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:900caec6-09fa-44c0-8cd6-99db33112335>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 325

Reference: 1KI 13:26
Text: And when the prophet that brought him back from the way heard thereof, he said, It is the man of God, who was disobedient unto the word of the LORD: therefore the LORD hath delivered him unto the lion, which hath torn him, and slain him, according to the word of the LORD, which he spake unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9b486e8-5827-4349-bd12-628650a20dfe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: 1KI 13:27
Text: And he spake to his sons, saying, Saddle me the ass. And they saddled him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b58a16ec-87e4-4382-b85b-b1ea0a8dce40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: 1KI 13:28
Text: And he went and found his carcase cast in the way, and the ass and the lion standing by the carcase: the lion had not eaten the carcase, nor torn the ass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8aaa666c-9dde-4a4c-a870-9ff986ef0f2f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: 1KI 13:29
Text: And the prophet took up the carcase of the man of God, and laid it upon the ass, and brought it back: and the old prophet came to the city, to mourn and to bury him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99096c45-ab32-4114-a4bd-31ad1d093bdf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: 1KI 13:30
Text: And he laid his carcase in his own grave; and they mourned over him, saying, Alas, my brother!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30e4a430-f081-48c9-afaa-a0f2cf0850dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: 1KI 13:31
Text: And it came to pass, after he had buried him, that he spake to his sons, saying, When I am dead, then bury me in the sepulchre wherein the man of God is buried; lay my bones beside his bones:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c85dd7e4-3481-47c2-8772-4a900ff5d133>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: 1KI 13:32
Text: For the saying which he cried by the word of the LORD against the altar in Bethel, and against all the houses of the high places which are in the cities of Samaria, shall surely come to pass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06772ff0-31ed-402d-bc66-911b9222f316>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: 1KI 13:33
Text: After this thing Jeroboam returned not from his evil way, but made again of the lowest of the people priests of the high places: whosoever would, he consecrated him, and he became one of the priests of the high places.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/13/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78406543-95fc-4759-bc17-b04b1e9d84f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: 1KI 13:34
Text: And this thing became sin unto the house of Jeroboam, even to cut it off, and to destroy it from off the face of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed20ff4c-3ea6-427c-9c2f-c29a2e5bc58b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: 1KI 14:1
Text: At that time Abijah the son of Jeroboam fell sick.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52989a5d-f8fe-4c69-87ba-edfa6deef200>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: 1KI 14:2
Text: And Jeroboam said to his wife, Arise, I pray thee, and disguise thyself, that thou be not known to be the wife of Jeroboam; and get thee to Shiloh: behold, there is Ahijah the prophet, which told me that I should be king over this people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79691c38-efd3-413f-b081-d8cc01ea90ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 1KI 14:3
Text: And take with thee ten loaves, and cracknels, and a cruse of honey, and go to him: he shall tell thee what shall become of the child.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:421b4364-9de6-4613-b2d4-b90140b7535d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: 1KI 14:4
Text: And Jeroboam’s wife did so, and arose, and went to Shiloh, and came to the house of Ahijah. But Ahijah could not see; for his eyes were set by reason of his age.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09a01068-b91f-4889-b8ab-e0123413718e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: 1KI 14:5
Text: And the LORD said unto Ahijah, Behold, the wife of Jeroboam cometh to ask a thing of thee for her son; for he is sick: thus and thus shalt thou say unto her: for it shall be, when she cometh in, that she shall feign herself to be another woman.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fac72975-f1f5-4014-a22c-0f4bd005086b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: 1KI 14:6
Text: And it was so, when Ahijah heard the sound of her feet, as she came in at the door, that he said, Come in, thou wife of Jeroboam; why feignest thou thyself to be another? for I am sent to thee with heavy tidings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91a7d0bf-f1b8-41ff-b17f-4e871ce1d966>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 1KI 14:7
Text: Go, tell Jeroboam, Thus saith the LORD God of Israel, Forasmuch as I exalted thee from among the people, and made thee prince over my people Israel,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a9bfddc-ffb6-4e26-b6ca-e4a179e7fc0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: 1KI 14:8
Text: And rent the kingdom away from the house of David, and gave it thee: and yet thou hast not been as my servant David, who kept my commandments, and who followed me with all his heart, to do that only which was right in mine eyes;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45c125a2-d9f7-4e64-826f-1b9e41af8e7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 1KI 14:9
Text: But hast done evil above all that were before thee: for thou hast gone and made thee other gods, and molten images, to provoke me to anger, and hast cast me behind thy back:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1d44729-e5a4-41ae-93ea-b10ae1bf9785>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 307

Reference: 1KI 14:10
Text: Therefore, behold, I will bring evil upon the house of Jeroboam, and will cut off from Jeroboam him that pisseth against the wall, and him that is shut up and left in Israel, and will take away the remnant of the house of Jeroboam, as a man taketh away dung, till it be all gone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1973914d-10a0-4e46-ac96-f02f66a9f69a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 1KI 14:11
Text: Him that dieth of Jeroboam in the city shall the dogs eat; and him that dieth in the field shall the fowls of the air eat: for the LORD hath spoken it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:421a5e8d-0e0d-42fd-acf9-ea144163b8a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: 1KI 14:12
Text: Arise thou therefore, get thee to thine own house: and when thy feet enter into the city, the child shall die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3064cf57-30f9-4571-bb44-d81f217f30c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: 1KI 14:13
Text: And all Israel shall mourn for him, and bury him: for he only of Jeroboam shall come to the grave, because in him there is found some good thing toward the LORD God of Israel in the house of Jeroboam.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74e8f045-5460-4d26-a453-f5ab2786aa25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: 1KI 14:14
Text: Moreover the LORD shall raise him up a king over Israel, who shall cut off the house of Jeroboam that day: but what? even now.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96a657b0-226a-4e3b-a263-2a9d18506dfd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: 1KI 14:15
Text: For the LORD shall smite Israel, as a reed is shaken in the water, and he shall root up Israel out of this good land, which he gave to their fathers, and shall scatter them beyond the river, because they have made their groves, provoking the LORD to anger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e440bec3-6892-481f-b785-6c777f696ccd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: 1KI 14:16
Text: And he shall give Israel up because of the sins of Jeroboam, who did sin, and who made Israel to sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c600e8b4-051b-42be-9c0a-93550b01c09b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: 1KI 14:17
Text: And Jeroboam’s wife arose, and departed, and came to Tirzah: and when she came to the threshold of the door, the child died;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4d2dd20-12d2-4843-b025-f68a4b7e66cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 1KI 14:18
Text: And they buried him; and all Israel mourned for him, according to the word of the LORD, which he spake by the hand of his servant Ahijah the prophet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46905bf2-cfd7-43b8-9613-e2d54140a014>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 1KI 14:19
Text: And the rest of the acts of Jeroboam, how he warred, and how he reigned, behold, they are written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad0f12e6-1c45-4757-a24f-b85c13bd3c72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 1KI 14:20
Text: And the days which Jeroboam reigned were two and twenty years: and he slept with his fathers, and Nadab his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0084e918-d4a8-4a88-a34e-bf7e64e7d35f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 324

Reference: 1KI 14:21
Text: And Rehoboam the son of Solomon reigned in Judah. Rehoboam was forty and one years old when he began to reign, and he reigned seventeen years in Jerusalem, the city which the LORD did choose out of all the tribes of Israel, to put his name there. And his mother’s name was Naamah an Ammonitess.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51ea1c5c-7f93-48a5-b1c3-697c7e75cc52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 1KI 14:22
Text: And Judah did evil in the sight of the LORD, and they provoked him to jealousy with their sins which they had committed, above all that their fathers had done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3cad2b0-69a8-4903-976e-362b80449f16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 1KI 14:23
Text: For they also built them high places, and images, and groves, on every high hill, and under every green tree.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddecd747-b2fa-4000-bff9-3480005d2f83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 1KI 14:24
Text: And there were also sodomites in the land: and they did according to all the abominations of the nations which the LORD cast out before the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0337670-3905-4248-9f6a-60cfdefc9abb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 1KI 14:25
Text: And it came to pass in the fifth year of king Rehoboam, that Shishak king of Egypt came up against Jerusalem:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a6ff079-b14d-405c-8388-4d446e79dae6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: 1KI 14:26
Text: And he took away the treasures of the house of the LORD, and the treasures of the king’s house; he even took away all: and he took away all the shields of gold which Solomon had made.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91591fb5-5449-4455-aae7-47effdccd811>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 1KI 14:27
Text: And king Rehoboam made in their stead brasen shields, and committed them unto the hands of the chief of the guard, which kept the door of the king’s house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a97371ab-e5af-46b5-b08e-0ba570791cdf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 1KI 14:28
Text: And it was so, when the king went into the house of the LORD, that the guard bare them, and brought them back into the guard chamber.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6f5b96c-4ee3-4710-96b4-fcf51a2f2bfb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 1KI 14:29
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Rehoboam, and all that he did, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3aa8ad1-21c5-4d62-84fa-aad64b88b74a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: 1KI 14:30
Text: And there was war between Rehoboam and Jeroboam all their days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/14/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09f4105b-44df-4119-b816-c61d2362b89f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: 1KI 14:31
Text: And Rehoboam slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in the city of David. And his mother’s name was Naamah an Ammonitess. And Abijam his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65daa866-403a-4072-a33e-37c8f92a6ee2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: 1KI 15:1
Text: Now in the eighteenth year of king Jeroboam the son of Nebat reigned Abijam over Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29cab5c8-0863-4432-9874-babf82ff0354>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 1KI 15:2
Text: Three years reigned he in Jerusalem. and his mother’s name was Maachah, the daughter of Abishalom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31394d3d-9635-4f62-a65e-0db7e592b024>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 1KI 15:3
Text: And he walked in all the sins of his father, which he had done before him: and his heart was not perfect with the LORD his God, as the heart of David his father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:765276cf-858c-4c1f-8819-d2bd5cbc1c25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: 1KI 15:4
Text: Nevertheless for David’s sake did the LORD his God give him a lamp in Jerusalem, to set up his son after him, and to establish Jerusalem:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7edca437-6698-4beb-aebe-591df5b74e9f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: 1KI 15:5
Text: Because David did that which was right in the eyes of the LORD, and turned not aside from any thing that he commanded him all the days of his life, save only in the matter of Uriah the Hittite.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80278716-4b10-4951-a758-c50c613ea7b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: 1KI 15:6
Text: And there was war between Rehoboam and Jeroboam all the days of his life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1eabbea-91e8-4624-b637-a3c312b91c89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: 1KI 15:7
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Abijam, and all that he did, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah? And there was war between Abijam and Jeroboam.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3455f056-415a-4571-96e1-c4793b9bc253>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 1KI 15:8
Text: And Abijam slept with his fathers; and they buried him in the city of David: and Asa his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28b1c0e0-80db-44d8-899f-e73e01ba387a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: 1KI 15:9
Text: And in the twentieth year of Jeroboam king of Israel reigned Asa over Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0edb5843-a1a0-4288-aa73-af1d454b3dfe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 1KI 15:10
Text: And forty and one years reigned he in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Maachah, the daughter of Abishalom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7252a13-804e-4c10-9982-bb151e9590d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: 1KI 15:11
Text: And Asa did that which was right in the eyes of the LORD, as did David his father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e63fe436-6693-4566-9601-396de05928b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 1KI 15:12
Text: And he took away the sodomites out of the land, and removed all the idols that his fathers had made.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45fb2ba1-ff7a-42e7-9a13-54cb0c81f893>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: 1KI 15:13
Text: And also Maachah his mother, even her he removed from being queen, because she had made an idol in a grove; and Asa destroyed her idol, and burnt it by the brook Kidron.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3c7532a-e4a6-439b-947b-c94a48673c56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 1KI 15:14
Text: But the high places were not removed: nevertheless Asa’s heart was perfect with the LORD all his days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4579dc50-7cd9-4cc3-8b73-e73b4a573d3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: 1KI 15:15
Text: And he brought in the things which his father had dedicated, and the things which himself had dedicated, into the house of the LORD, silver, and gold, and vessels.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae992b9d-e327-4b47-b7c3-e66f07be6cba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: 1KI 15:16
Text: And there was war between Asa and Baasha king of Israel all their days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4823101-eddb-493f-8dbc-8f7c5db169bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: 1KI 15:17
Text: And Baasha king of Israel went up against Judah, and built Ramah, that he might not suffer any to go out or come in to Asa king of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1d80bfb-f67b-4320-a3a6-ed2d1ad0ad09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 341

Reference: 1KI 15:18
Text: Then Asa took all the silver and the gold that were left in the treasures of the house of the LORD, and the treasures of the king’s house, and delivered them into the hand of his servants: and king Asa sent them to Benhadad, the son of Tabrimon, the son of Hezion, king of Syria, that dwelt at Damascus, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c8241c5-ed06-4dab-8e52-0de38b024407>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: 1KI 15:19
Text: There is a league between me and thee, and between my father and thy father: behold, I have sent unto thee a present of silver and gold; come and break thy league with Baasha king of Israel, that he may depart from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bbe2f8b8-936b-4da6-b709-cd8bb3ad111e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: 1KI 15:20
Text: So Benhadad hearkened unto king Asa, and sent the captains of the hosts which he had against the cities of Israel, and smote Ijon, and Dan, and Abelbethmaachah, and all Cinneroth, with all the land of Naphtali.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:639fdaf2-d9c2-44a2-9dcc-19dcce9fa61a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 1KI 15:21
Text: And it came to pass, when Baasha heard thereof, that he left off building of Ramah, and dwelt in Tirzah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3c2f24a-9147-4e7d-8a1a-c0f2b8e3bbd9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: 1KI 15:22
Text: Then king Asa made a proclamation throughout all Judah; none was exempted: and they took away the stones of Ramah, and the timber thereof, wherewith Baasha had builded; and king Asa built with them Geba of Benjamin, and Mizpah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:344bce01-64e2-4c9f-b5cd-cd9b4b804194>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 274

Reference: 1KI 15:23
Text: The rest of all the acts of Asa, and all his might, and all that he did, and the cities which he built, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah? Nevertheless in the time of his old age he was diseased in his feet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17ce4574-bb84-46b3-860a-bc8507904990>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 1KI 15:24
Text: And Asa slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in the city of David his father: and Jehoshaphat his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88d522b7-65a7-4fbd-99f2-277965d93051>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 1KI 15:25
Text: And Nadab the son of Jeroboam began to reign over Israel in the second year of Asa king of Judah, and reigned over Israel two years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aba02e4c-422e-423c-9c3b-23689a314908>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: 1KI 15:26
Text: And he did evil in the sight of the LORD, and walked in the way of his father, and in his sin wherewith he made Israel to sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:684965ac-539b-48e6-a831-3520c6167eea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: 1KI 15:27
Text: And Baasha the son of Ahijah, of the house of Issachar, conspired against him; and Baasha smote him at Gibbethon, which belonged to the Philistines; for Nadab and all Israel laid siege to Gibbethon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:428361c0-6408-430d-8156-512d57df7dd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: 1KI 15:28
Text: Even in the third year of Asa king of Judah did Baasha slay him, and reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dad6314a-7555-43e0-b689-f9009d3307bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: 1KI 15:29
Text: And it came to pass, when he reigned, that he smote all the house of Jeroboam; he left not to Jeroboam any that breathed, until he had destroyed him, according unto the saying of the LORD, which he spake by his servant Ahijah the Shilonite:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a87ab82-a776-4f71-ab13-7789b4ba18da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: 1KI 15:30
Text: Because of the sins of Jeroboam which he sinned, and which he made Israel sin, by his provocation wherewith he provoked the LORD God of Israel to anger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbb1cf95-91f6-43c3-91cd-6e09bc79a4d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 1KI 15:31
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Nadab, and all that he did, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8406ed6-9529-4d1f-85bd-e1a95949e787>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: 1KI 15:32
Text: And there was war between Asa and Baasha king of Israel all their days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cb9108c-fad6-43d0-8357-d4c3a656fb41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: 1KI 15:33
Text: In the third year of Asa king of Judah began Baasha the son of Ahijah to reign over all Israel in Tirzah, twenty and four years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/15/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ecf47036-7c08-473a-9711-0a17c74a1870>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: 1KI 15:34
Text: And he did evil in the sight of the LORD, and walked in the way of Jeroboam, and in his sin wherewith he made Israel to sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d365521c-30a3-4a1c-827b-5152bfef3d19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: 1KI 16:1
Text: Then the word of the LORD came to Jehu the son of Hanani against Baasha, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:752c2a57-f8a1-47ac-9441-fef5821945ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: 1KI 16:2
Text: Forasmuch as I exalted thee out of the dust, and made thee prince over my people Israel; and thou hast walked in the way of Jeroboam, and hast made my people Israel to sin, to provoke me to anger with their sins;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a791d154-db96-42bd-ab79-1d17257a4291>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 1KI 16:3
Text: Behold, I will take away the posterity of Baasha, and the posterity of his house; and will make thy house like the house of Jeroboam the son of Nebat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06f2e7b2-ea18-46ca-bbe8-fba5dc16b7be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 1KI 16:4
Text: Him that dieth of Baasha in the city shall the dogs eat; and him that dieth of his in the fields shall the fowls of the air eat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:174ad986-3074-4a9f-a384-4d14fa6c8b0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: 1KI 16:5
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Baasha, and what he did, and his might, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7c88df7-a8bc-4e0a-bc5c-e4338a467a23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: 1KI 16:6
Text: So Baasha slept with his fathers, and was buried in Tirzah: and Elah his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f223875-ab97-43c6-8770-19a24da23fe9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 328

Reference: 1KI 16:7
Text: And also by the hand of the prophet Jehu the son of Hanani came the word of the LORD against Baasha, and against his house, even for all the evil that he did in the sight of the LORD, in provoking him to anger with the work of his hands, in being like the house of Jeroboam; and because he killed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d70328f-0958-4bfa-81ae-9f8b3c3e01e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 1KI 16:8
Text: In the twenty and sixth year of Asa king of Judah began Elah the son of Baasha to reign over Israel in Tirzah, two years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c3ebedf-fc91-490c-818f-4ac0918213c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: 1KI 16:9
Text: And his servant Zimri, captain of half his chariots, conspired against him, as he was in Tirzah, drinking himself drunk in the house of Arza steward of his house in Tirzah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5dc9201-8d99-4f18-8b63-e69116ef49eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 1KI 16:10
Text: And Zimri went in and smote him, and killed him, in the twenty and seventh year of Asa king of Judah, and reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:036873f4-b619-4081-bf60-a8603c2046ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: 1KI 16:11
Text: And it came to pass, when he began to reign, as soon as he sat on his throne, that he slew all the house of Baasha: he left him not one that pisseth against a wall, neither of his kinsfolks, nor of his friends.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac036d71-5244-4e1a-bebd-0b15eb852e06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 1KI 16:12
Text: Thus did Zimri destroy all the house of Baasha, according to the word of the LORD, which he spake against Baasha by Jehu the prophet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1e8e597-0711-4faf-aeb1-639dea1ca7d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: 1KI 16:13
Text: For all the sins of Baasha, and the sins of Elah his son, by which they sinned, and by which they made Israel to sin, in provoking the LORD God of Israel to anger with their vanities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f4fccac-f00a-4f0c-b2bd-912ab5ec1c54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 1KI 16:14
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Elah, and all that he did, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1e5f1bc-dcda-49ea-9743-df8e615ac90a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 1KI 16:15
Text: In the twenty and seventh year of Asa king of Judah did Zimri reign seven days in Tirzah. And the people were encamped against Gibbethon, which belonged to the Philistines.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1021c99a-5b55-41de-9c26-932fa5d067f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: 1KI 16:16
Text: And the people that were encamped heard say, Zimri hath conspired, and hath also slain the king: wherefore all Israel made Omri, the captain of the host, king over Israel that day in the camp.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b7a5e84-8f6a-4d27-8dd4-0829a19fd411>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: 1KI 16:17
Text: And Omri went up from Gibbethon, and all Israel with him, and they besieged Tirzah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7c47d11-d827-4f87-80f5-2f8b0d840b43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: 1KI 16:18
Text: And it came to pass, when Zimri saw that the city was taken, that he went into the palace of the king’s house, and burnt the king’s house over him with fire, and died.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34cf9314-71cf-44f4-82b1-9548552a04e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: 1KI 16:19
Text: For his sins which he sinned in doing evil in the sight of the LORD, in walking in the way of Jeroboam, and in his sin which he did, to make Israel to sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0937047f-fe66-4a78-a76f-909e8649f216>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 1KI 16:20
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Zimri, and his treason that he wrought, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df05fe57-64f1-4f2c-b829-6a046781acdd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 1KI 16:21
Text: Then were the people of Israel divided into two parts: half of the people followed Tibni the son of Ginath, to make him king; and half followed Omri.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5968e46-c2b5-4878-9611-94ea6b56f760>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 1KI 16:22
Text: But the people that followed Omri prevailed against the people that followed Tibni the son of Ginath: so Tibni died, and Omri reigned.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3430617e-beb2-40f8-9a6e-adab1c4b91ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: 1KI 16:23
Text: In the thirty and first year of Asa king of Judah began Omri to reign over Israel, twelve years: six years reigned he in Tirzah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fa114b1-a20d-4136-9200-5fd6ecb97721>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: 1KI 16:24
Text: And he bought the hill Samaria of Shemer for two talents of silver, and built on the hill, and called the name of the city which he built, after the name of Shemer, owner of the hill, Samaria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4cb42b13-a0fb-4623-96e8-3418050e1c53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: 1KI 16:25
Text: But Omri wrought evil in the eyes of the LORD, and did worse than all that were before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec2970ab-ba30-43a1-85e7-f5b89693e00e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: 1KI 16:26
Text: For he walked in all the way of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, and in his sin wherewith he made Israel to sin, to provoke the LORD God of Israel to anger with their vanities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a33774b6-0c03-40cd-b224-1d18af483487>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 1KI 16:27
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Omri which he did, and his might that he shewed, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36751f6c-5689-490e-871f-5d7267f06fa0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: 1KI 16:28
Text: So Omri slept with his fathers, and was buried in Samaria: and Ahab his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:164de546-fd6b-488c-b3f4-9725484d0af1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: 1KI 16:29
Text: And in the thirty and eighth year of Asa king of Judah began Ahab the son of Omri to reign over Israel: and Ahab the son of Omri reigned over Israel in Samaria twenty and two years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa8e62c2-fc1b-4de2-a8c2-d8dd596e04df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: 1KI 16:30
Text: And Ahab the son of Omri did evil in the sight of the LORD above all that were before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f6eeed0-5a64-46e1-b165-8f8c68f8f003>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: 1KI 16:31
Text: And it came to pass, as if it had been a light thing for him to walk in the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, that he took to wife Jezebel the daughter of Ethbaal king of the Zidonians, and went and served Baal, and worshipped him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd9164b9-55fc-402f-83b9-585eb4b0220f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: 1KI 16:32
Text: And he reared up an altar for Baal in the house of Baal, which he had built in Samaria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3ecaa9c-eb8b-454c-9618-b888234118f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 1KI 16:33
Text: And Ahab made a grove; and Ahab did more to provoke the LORD God of Israel to anger than all the kings of Israel that were before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/16/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83cf8bb4-b614-4dca-9dd1-0bcdabcc8953>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: 1KI 16:34
Text: In his days did Hiel the Bethelite build Jericho: he laid the foundation thereof in Abiram his firstborn, and set up the gates thereof in his youngest son Segub, according to the word of the LORD, which he spake by Joshua the son of Nun.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07f182d2-6abc-4165-a43c-f827b28005bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: 1KI 17:1
Text: And Elijah the Tishbite, who was of the inhabitants of Gilead, said unto Ahab, As the LORD God of Israel liveth, before whom I stand, there shall not be dew nor rain these years, but according to my word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d30b30b1-bafc-49b0-aae6-9fa72287a736>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: 1KI 17:2
Text: And the word of the LORD came unto him, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be5507e8-3495-4bf4-b743-22e10cf17995>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 1KI 17:3
Text: Get thee hence, and turn thee eastward, and hide thyself by the brook Cherith, that is before Jordan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:502b7d85-c5b0-4d11-a41e-011d0a0f600a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: 1KI 17:4
Text: And it shall be, that thou shalt drink of the brook; and I have commanded the ravens to feed thee there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e25b380-a42c-466e-aeec-fcf6666c147f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: 1KI 17:5
Text: So he went and did according unto the word of the LORD: for he went and dwelt by the brook Cherith, that is before Jordan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba5e33cd-5992-43a3-8e72-93ef31e728d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 1KI 17:6
Text: And the ravens brought him bread and flesh in the morning, and bread and flesh in the evening; and he drank of the brook.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c32a52d-8649-4e0d-90ae-bfbf30388ad6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: 1KI 17:7
Text: And it came to pass after a while, that the brook dried up, because there had been no rain in the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a0efcfb-80bc-4bab-ae58-24a6db81e35b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: 1KI 17:8
Text: And the word of the LORD came unto him, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2effae3-0699-40fa-823f-b28cf2cf4b7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 1KI 17:9
Text: Arise, get thee to Zarephath, which belongeth to Zidon, and dwell there: behold, I have commanded a widow woman there to sustain thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c308be31-2dc9-4db6-adf2-cfc7fcfc3330>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: 1KI 17:10
Text: So he arose and went to Zarephath. And when he came to the gate of the city, behold, the widow woman was there gathering of sticks: and he called to her, and said, Fetch me, I pray thee, a little water in a vessel, that I may drink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a56bb88-58eb-41e5-9907-683991461ff8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 1KI 17:11
Text: And as she was going to fetch it, he called to her, and said, Bring me, I pray thee, a morsel of bread in thine hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de4704e2-3381-4389-8731-191dd8571f3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: 1KI 17:12
Text: And she said, As the LORD thy God liveth, I have not a cake, but an handful of meal in a barrel, and a little oil in a cruse: and, behold, I am gathering two sticks, that I may go in and dress it for me and my son, that we may eat it, and die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20aced5e-1527-414c-b65f-3b52e9a81fbb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: 1KI 17:13
Text: And Elijah said unto her, Fear not; go and do as thou hast said: but make me thereof a little cake first, and bring it unto me, and after make for thee and for thy son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8592743-9334-4dac-9741-4a8244b30a2b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: 1KI 17:14
Text: For thus saith the LORD God of Israel, The barrel of meal shall not waste, neither shall the cruse of oil fail, until the day that the LORD sendeth rain upon the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c949d3ee-880d-4800-90e3-f6b6df8496fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: 1KI 17:15
Text: And she went and did according to the saying of Elijah: and she, and he, and her house, did eat many days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9652e64-ae76-4569-b92f-a4c9b821601d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 1KI 17:16
Text: And the barrel of meal wasted not, neither did the cruse of oil fail, according to the word of the LORD, which he spake by Elijah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5f76718-c6fc-4d29-bf1f-f93fa8e8af23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 1KI 17:17
Text: And it came to pass after these things, that the son of the woman, the mistress of the house, fell sick; and his sickness was so sore, that there was no breath left in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c7c1506-73b2-47fc-9ba5-930d7036e8fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: 1KI 17:18
Text: And she said unto Elijah, What have I to do with thee, O thou man of God? art thou come unto me to call my sin to remembrance, and to slay my son?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5e70285-859b-4cb0-b98a-cdcb00958487>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 1KI 17:19
Text: And he said unto her, Give me thy son. And he took him out of her bosom, and carried him up into a loft, where he abode, and laid him upon his own bed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b230b854-4e8d-42ac-9081-9f39376764e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: 1KI 17:20
Text: And he cried unto the LORD, and said, O LORD my God, hast thou also brought evil upon the widow with whom I sojourn, by slaying her son?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:122c35b5-e5f7-430f-b93f-ad796410f245>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 1KI 17:21
Text: And he stretched himself upon the child three times, and cried unto the LORD, and said, O LORD my God, I pray thee, let this child’s soul come into him again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfc3198a-a4b1-4ef8-b138-1ffd64383a91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: 1KI 17:22
Text: And the LORD heard the voice of Elijah; and the soul of the child came into him again, and he revived.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20f660b5-3977-4dee-8ccc-61d941e5a46e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: 1KI 17:23
Text: And Elijah took the child, and brought him down out of the chamber into the house, and delivered him unto his mother: and Elijah said, See, thy son liveth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/17/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:625ede38-2226-4931-aca7-7903be6d763f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 1KI 17:24
Text: And the woman said to Elijah, Now by this I know that thou art a man of God, and that the word of the LORD in thy mouth is truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da961f7b-54c7-4527-8934-fd01ecd52f8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: 1KI 18:1
Text: And it came to pass after many days, that the word of the LORD came to Elijah in the third year, saying, Go, shew thyself unto Ahab; and I will send rain upon the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ebc7f35-6286-4b57-8076-606584d270cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: 1KI 18:2
Text: And Elijah went to shew himself unto Ahab. And there was a sore famine in Samaria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55b2e225-8dc0-43f1-8bbc-08c1cbe1a32d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: 1KI 18:3
Text: And Ahab called Obadiah, which was the governor of his house. (Now Obadiah feared the LORD greatly:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b36945d-ecc4-49f8-9930-335cd1a73573>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: 1KI 18:4
Text: For it was so, when Jezebel cut off the prophets of the LORD, that Obadiah took an hundred prophets, and hid them by fifty in a cave, and fed them with bread and water.)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f24ecf6-3cee-4bae-bb65-1996ce4cd45c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: 1KI 18:5
Text: And Ahab said unto Obadiah, Go into the land, unto all fountains of water, and unto all brooks: peradventure we may find grass to save the horses and mules alive, that we lose not all the beasts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b623cc8e-a4a7-420f-b958-4ede688c1c25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 1KI 18:6
Text: So they divided the land between them to pass throughout it: Ahab went one way by himself, and Obadiah went another way by himself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad6f9631-be3c-4138-9461-37040f8c3141>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 1KI 18:7
Text: And as Obadiah was in the way, behold, Elijah met him: and he knew him, and fell on his face, and said, Art thou that my lord Elijah?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a3a5db6-7505-4c45-890f-4ff23c9e8b05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: 1KI 18:8
Text: And he answered him, I am: go, tell thy lord, Behold, Elijah is here.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f6eb58a-6ff7-45f8-b4fe-50d4df63f46a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: 1KI 18:9
Text: And he said, What have I sinned, that thou wouldest deliver thy servant into the hand of Ahab, to slay me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c03c378-a524-43b5-b057-9bf3146804bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: 1KI 18:10
Text: As the LORD thy God liveth, there is no nation or kingdom, whither my lord hath not sent to seek thee: and when they said, He is not there; he took an oath of the kingdom and nation, that they found thee not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59f06100-1239-4159-a358-f9191b0973fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: 1KI 18:11
Text: And now thou sayest, Go, tell thy lord, Behold, Elijah is here.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb1e3b55-747b-4e8b-9220-0056e7eba990>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: 1KI 18:12
Text: And it shall come to pass, as soon as I am gone from thee, that the Spirit of the LORD shall carry thee whither I know not; and so when I come and tell Ahab, and he cannot find thee, he shall slay me: but I thy servant fear the LORD from my youth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62c7280c-698a-418f-809d-bdecb997538c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: 1KI 18:13
Text: Was it not told my lord what I did when Jezebel slew the prophets of the LORD, how I hid an hundred men of the LORD’s prophets by fifty in a cave, and fed them with bread and water?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b6c4a61-a058-4006-9136-1c5da1695f90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: 1KI 18:14
Text: And now thou sayest, Go, tell thy lord, Behold, Elijah is here: and he shall slay me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d0b6af6-f1b7-42d5-9eda-cb8e5c787bb2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 1KI 18:15
Text: And Elijah said, As the LORD of hosts liveth, before whom I stand, I will surely shew myself unto him to day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddbacdd3-8ff2-4077-b774-cfe7ceae8c4f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: 1KI 18:16
Text: So Obadiah went to meet Ahab, and told him: and Ahab went to meet Elijah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c63836ea-86fb-4eb3-882f-ec7fb221adf0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: 1KI 18:17
Text: And it came to pass, when Ahab saw Elijah, that Ahab said unto him, Art thou he that troubleth Israel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5df99b7e-a55a-4fe1-8c91-76ea59b01f62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: 1KI 18:18
Text: And he answered, I have not troubled Israel; but thou, and thy father’s house, in that ye have forsaken the commandments of the LORD, and thou hast followed Baalim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7dcde485-377d-4000-b0c3-48d953ed83d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: 1KI 18:19
Text: Now therefore send, and gather to me all Israel unto mount Carmel, and the prophets of Baal four hundred and fifty, and the prophets of the groves four hundred, which eat at Jezebel’s table.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18de9f40-4605-4b2c-bbae-668b692e3e13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 1KI 18:20
Text: So Ahab sent unto all the children of Israel, and gathered the prophets together unto mount Carmel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:109bb93c-bcd3-4a28-948f-53911449044f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: 1KI 18:21
Text: And Elijah came unto all the people, and said, How long halt ye between two opinions? if the LORD be God, follow him: but if Baal, then follow him. And the people answered him not a word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8dd1d6de-b1eb-4755-a776-c3571ef41979>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 1KI 18:22
Text: Then said Elijah unto the people, I, even I only, remain a prophet of the LORD; but Baal’s prophets are four hundred and fifty men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e516b6f7-7750-4bb5-84f9-017480a79aa4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: 1KI 18:23
Text: Let them therefore give us two bullocks; and let them choose one bullock for themselves, and cut it in pieces, and lay it on wood, and put no fire under: and I will dress the other bullock, and lay it on wood, and put no fire under:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f81f0da-8264-4667-b634-19605e955eb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: 1KI 18:24
Text: And call ye on the name of your gods, and I will call on the name of the LORD: and the God that answereth by fire, let him be God. And all the people answered and said, It is well spoken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2415c5a-7f68-4745-a517-40418fb1e47b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: 1KI 18:25
Text: And Elijah said unto the prophets of Baal, Choose you one bullock for yourselves, and dress it first; for ye are many; and call on the name of your gods, but put no fire under.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c2dda52-2ed0-4018-9639-fd279383c99b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: 1KI 18:26
Text: And they took the bullock which was given them, and they dressed it, and called on the name of Baal from morning even until noon, saying, O Baal, hear us. But there was no voice, nor any that answered. And they leaped upon the altar which was made.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8803b4a-81a8-46a4-b401-ad696e18ffa1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: 1KI 18:27
Text: And it came to pass at noon, that Elijah mocked them, and said, Cry aloud: for he is a god; either he is talking, or he is pursuing, or he is in a journey, or peradventure he sleepeth, and must be awaked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:528c021c-0b87-40e7-9050-206db7096912>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: 1KI 18:28
Text: And they cried aloud, and cut themselves after their manner with knives and lancets, till the blood gushed out upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d83fda89-e55e-44a1-b3e7-2890ba00c970>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: 1KI 18:29
Text: And it came to pass, when midday was past, and they prophesied until the time of the offering of the evening sacrifice, that there was neither voice, nor any to answer, nor any that regarded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4f27469-5785-439d-8cc2-1f308495b9fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: 1KI 18:30
Text: And Elijah said unto all the people, Come near unto me. And all the people came near unto him. And he repaired the altar of the LORD that was broken down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f9124a6-8e7e-4a15-a9ea-304182deeadb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: 1KI 18:31
Text: And Elijah took twelve stones, according to the number of the tribes of the sons of Jacob, unto whom the word of the LORD came, saying, Israel shall be thy name:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6319997d-8b72-465d-8d7f-b7b1d682ed6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: 1KI 18:32
Text: And with the stones he built an altar in the name of the LORD: and he made a trench about the altar, as great as would contain two measures of seed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:059a2dbc-f6e7-4675-bd6b-f7d10eb751f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: 1KI 18:33
Text: And he put the wood in order, and cut the bullock in pieces, and laid him on the wood, and said, Fill four barrels with water, and pour it on the burnt sacrifice, and on the wood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3aa018f9-09e9-487d-9af2-4eb488559303>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: 1KI 18:34
Text: And he said, Do it the second time. And they did it the second time. And he said, Do it the third time. And they did it the third time.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad73815a-8eaf-4a87-9986-d13c4b4e8bb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: 1KI 18:35
Text: And the water ran round about the altar; and he filled the trench also with water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:751a2598-9738-4e55-b8fc-de0aa09108f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 321

Reference: 1KI 18:36
Text: And it came to pass at the time of the offering of the evening sacrifice, that Elijah the prophet came near, and said, LORD God of Abraham, Isaac, and of Israel, let it be known this day that thou art God in Israel, and that I am thy servant, and that I have done all these things at thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9afef3e-0a18-4375-aabf-d3f00f92b314>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 1KI 18:37
Text: Hear me, O LORD, hear me, that this people may know that thou art the LORD God, and that thou hast turned their heart back again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f74b7d3-176b-4d59-bf7f-91aae9e8d07c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 1KI 18:38
Text: Then the fire of the LORD fell, and consumed the burnt sacrifice, and the wood, and the stones, and the dust, and licked up the water that was in the trench.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a98d690-1cf3-4576-9ef1-b51ec0a3211b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: 1KI 18:39
Text: And when all the people saw it, they fell on their faces: and they said, The LORD, he is the God; the LORD, he is the God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6ba5865-9e0a-463d-be75-451b6efc3037>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 1KI 18:40
Text: And Elijah said unto them, Take the prophets of Baal; let not one of them escape. And they took them: and Elijah brought them down to the brook Kishon, and slew them there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0b79f12-3809-4bfb-9c7a-34284caca3e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: 1KI 18:41
Text: And Elijah said unto Ahab, Get thee up, eat and drink; for there is a sound of abundance of rain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae1df66e-d689-4306-b2fd-ccf9341bfa62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: 1KI 18:42
Text: So Ahab went up to eat and to drink. And Elijah went up to the top of Carmel; and he cast himself down upon the earth, and put his face between his knees,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cccd351e-ed05-4f2a-b759-02e8cffc057c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 1KI 18:43
Text: And said to his servant, Go up now, look toward the sea. And he went up, and looked, and said, There is nothing. And he said, Go again seven times.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c85eb858-3acd-4032-889b-3d4a7274409d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: 1KI 18:44
Text: And it came to pass at the seventh time, that he said, Behold, there ariseth a little cloud out of the sea, like a man’s hand. And he said, Go up, say unto Ahab, Prepare thy chariot, and get thee down that the rain stop thee not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10560534-f6bc-45e7-b31c-89bac7fed22f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: 1KI 18:45
Text: And it came to pass in the mean while, that the heaven was black with clouds and wind, and there was a great rain. And Ahab rode, and went to Jezreel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/18/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cec17c70-3471-4ee0-b68b-8249af63a454>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: 1KI 18:46
Text: And the hand of the LORD was on Elijah; and he girded up his loins, and ran before Ahab to the entrance of Jezreel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/19/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8136714-19d4-4f55-b14f-b7ca84920cde>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 1KI 19:1
Text: And Ahab told Jezebel all that Elijah had done, and withal how he had slain all the prophets with the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/19/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:886114e8-f76e-424e-baa8-126ae4f14802>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: 1KI 19:2
Text: Then Jezebel sent a messenger unto Elijah, saying, So let the gods do to me, and more also, if I make not thy life as the life of one of them by to morrow about this time.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/19/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ea91f15-d616-4c54-afb3-b191873c7d74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 1KI 19:3
Text: And when he saw that, he arose, and went for his life, and came to Beersheba, which belongeth to Judah, and left his servant there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/19/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:423bb0bf-b49d-43ee-88ea-bfc4b073ab94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: 1KI 19:4
Text: But he himself went a day’s journey into the wilderness, and came and sat down under a juniper tree: and he requested for himself that he might die; and said, It is enough; now, O LORD, take away my life; for I am not better than my fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/19/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1bed129-2a93-4517-982a-8d2b820510ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 1KI 19:5
Text: And as he lay and slept under a juniper tree, behold, then an angel touched him, and said unto him, Arise and eat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/19/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:125a4362-7f2d-4384-aa02-acc0b84ffe5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: 1KI 19:6
Text: And he looked, and, behold, there was a cake baken on the coals, and a cruse of water at his head. And he did eat and drink, and laid him down again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/19/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26adc357-3319-4676-9f5a-05ff98f86632>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: 1KI 19:7
Text: And the angel of the LORD came again the second time, and touched him, and said, Arise and eat; because the journey is too great for thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/19/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13646460-12ad-45bd-a2d6-c1027697a8a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 1KI 19:8
Text: And he arose, and did eat and drink, and went in the strength of that meat forty days and forty nights unto Horeb the mount of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/19/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c24437f9-feee-4ddd-bf2b-5d698b123e0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: 1KI 19:9
Text: And he came thither unto a cave, and lodged there; and, behold, the word of the LORD came to him, and he said unto him, What doest thou here, Elijah?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/19/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47a49481-896d-4f16-8bf9-7897ad15598a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 281

Reference: 1KI 19:10
Text: And he said, I have been very jealous for the LORD God of hosts: for the children of Israel have forsaken thy covenant, thrown down thine altars, and slain thy prophets with the sword; and I, even I only, am left; and they seek my life, to take it away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/19/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84feb011-8d5b-4c3d-8f55-ea4344987569>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 328

Reference: 1KI 19:11
Text: And he said, Go forth, and stand upon the mount before the LORD. And, behold, the LORD passed by, and a great and strong wind rent the mountains, and brake in pieces the rocks before the LORD; but the LORD was not in the wind: and after the wind an earthquake; but the LORD was not in the earthquake:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/19/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:275f4cab-3bb0-495c-9a64-b521423f2dee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: 1KI 19:12
Text: And after the earthquake a fire; but the LORD was not in the fire: and after the fire a still small voice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/19/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5afe590f-9571-4be5-aa95-e562f2c27bc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: 1KI 19:13
Text: And it was so, when Elijah heard it, that he wrapped his face in his mantle, and went out, and stood in the entering in of the cave. And, behold, there came a voice unto him, and said, What doest thou here, Elijah?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/19/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80194a35-33ca-4f34-bd63-999c598aefca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 285

Reference: 1KI 19:14
Text: And he said, I have been very jealous for the LORD God of hosts: because the children of Israel have forsaken thy covenant, thrown down thine altars, and slain thy prophets with the sword; and I, even I only, am left; and they seek my life, to take it away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/19/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47d0bab1-2d07-4a66-8e19-51703268d436>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 1KI 19:15
Text: And the LORD said unto him, Go, return on thy way to the wilderness of Damascus: and when thou comest, anoint Hazael to be king over Syria:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/19/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff500a23-5c2f-4993-b10c-04fafa170b67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: 1KI 19:16
Text: And Jehu the son of Nimshi shalt thou anoint to be king over Israel: and Elisha the son of Shaphat of Abelmeholah shalt thou anoint to be prophet in thy room.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/19/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82ad77ec-5d82-404a-a9ac-55b571d7107e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: 1KI 19:17
Text: And it shall come to pass, that him that escapeth the sword of Hazael shall Jehu slay: and him that escapeth from the sword of Jehu shall Elisha slay.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/19/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7df4b44b-e515-47b8-946c-ba97c6a04052>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 1KI 19:18
Text: Yet I have left me seven thousand in Israel, all the knees which have not bowed unto Baal, and every mouth which hath not kissed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/19/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aaa86ef2-b84e-40a5-a2da-80de28241427>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: 1KI 19:19
Text: So he departed thence, and found Elisha the son of Shaphat, who was plowing with twelve yoke of oxen before him, and he with the twelfth: and Elijah passed by him, and cast his mantle upon him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/19/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:792091b3-ba17-4841-b2e6-99a690989443>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: 1KI 19:20
Text: And he left the oxen, and ran after Elijah, and said, Let me, I pray thee, kiss my father and my mother, and then I will follow thee. And he said unto him, Go back again: for what have I done to thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/19/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08d67092-1311-4344-9e09-e0f2f04138bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 262

Reference: 1KI 19:21
Text: And he returned back from him, and took a yoke of oxen, and slew them, and boiled their flesh with the instruments of the oxen, and gave unto the people, and they did eat. Then he arose, and went after Elijah, and ministered unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c30df2a-0bf4-4bbd-ba8d-3e6490df780d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: 1KI 20:1
Text: And Benhadad the king of Syria gathered all his host together: and there were thirty and two kings with him, and horses, and chariots; and he went up and besieged Samaria, and warred against it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64f9ae52-0b47-4d7b-9042-68ddd98c51a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 1KI 20:2
Text: And he sent messengers to Ahab king of Israel into the city, and said unto him, Thus saith Benhadad,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5824500-1a43-40df-ad0f-70d8625c7e14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: 1KI 20:3
Text: Thy silver and thy gold is mine; thy wives also and thy children, even the goodliest, are mine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1608b9f1-1e6e-46b9-8799-0ffd76abc010>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: 1KI 20:4
Text: And the king of Israel answered and said, My lord, O king, according to thy saying, I am thine, and all that I have.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1de05e29-2c76-4dc9-a5cf-647a1fd0c766>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: 1KI 20:5
Text: And the messengers came again, and said, Thus speaketh Benhadad, saying, Although I have sent unto thee, saying, Thou shalt deliver me thy silver, and thy gold, and thy wives, and thy children;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fd5d0d0-fa56-4442-a2db-5506681ed6cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: 1KI 20:6
Text: Yet I will send my servants unto thee to morrow about this time, and they shall search thine house, and the houses of thy servants; and it shall be, that whatsoever is pleasant in thine eyes, they shall put it in their hand, and take it away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4edf199f-9894-4691-b582-acc2ed046b6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: 1KI 20:7
Text: Then the king of Israel called all the elders of the land, and said, Mark, I pray you, and see how this man seeketh mischief: for he sent unto me for my wives, and for my children, and for my silver, and for my gold; and I denied him not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85e2e4cd-a2b1-4e91-b1e1-55c2b228534e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: 1KI 20:8
Text: And all the elders and all the people said unto him, Hearken not unto him, nor consent.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:832dd72d-84fe-4e34-8218-6356a7b805b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: 1KI 20:9
Text: Wherefore he said unto the messengers of Benhadad, Tell my lord the king, All that thou didst send for to thy servant at the first I will do: but this thing I may not do. And the messengers departed, and brought him word again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0cf8281f-c21b-4898-a6d6-d790fdcc810a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: 1KI 20:10
Text: And Benhadad sent unto him, and said, The gods do so unto me, and more also, if the dust of Samaria shall suffice for handfuls for all the people that follow me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ec9226f-9be1-483b-bce9-8833254af61c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 1KI 20:11
Text: And the king of Israel answered and said, Tell him, Let not him that girdeth on his harness boast himself as he that putteth it off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c7d59cc-22d1-49ef-b7f1-734a009ac3fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: 1KI 20:12
Text: And it came to pass, when Benhadad heard this message, as he was drinking, he and the kings in the pavilions, that he said unto his servants, Set yourselves in array. And they set themselves in array against the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9507a34-4e66-4332-bc75-45cd1a635aee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: 1KI 20:13
Text: And, behold, there came a prophet unto Ahab king of Israel, saying, Thus saith the LORD, Hast thou seen all this great multitude? behold, I will deliver it into thine hand this day; and thou shalt know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2483fbe-743c-402a-81db-7df42ad6f69a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: 1KI 20:14
Text: And Ahab said, By whom? And he said, Thus saith the LORD, Even by the young men of the princes of the provinces. Then he said, Who shall order the battle? And he answered, Thou.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79e64229-1e6f-41ef-bd86-f327e520637b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: 1KI 20:15
Text: Then he numbered the young men of the princes of the provinces, and they were two hundred and thirty two: and after them he numbered all the people, even all the children of Israel, being seven thousand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6e3ef5a-c22d-4478-8d5e-b2679afbfdb9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: 1KI 20:16
Text: And they went out at noon. But Benhadad was drinking himself drunk in the pavilions, he and the kings, the thirty and two kings that helped him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06872803-fd9f-442b-8ead-061dced4fc89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: 1KI 20:17
Text: And the young men of the princes of the provinces went out first; and Benhadad sent out, and they told him, saying, There are men come out of Samaria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3716eb55-940d-4163-97ab-074545c1f9b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 1KI 20:18
Text: And he said, Whether they be come out for peace, take them alive; or whether they be come out for war, take them alive.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4b7fec2-7fa3-437b-883c-833086b63b34>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: 1KI 20:19
Text: So these young men of the princes of the provinces came out of the city, and the army which followed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ccbb9f5-cea7-4c66-8e12-baa1149ea24b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 1KI 20:20
Text: And they slew every one his man: and the Syrians fled; and Israel pursued them: and Benhadad the king of Syria escaped on an horse with the horsemen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddb8bdbd-4d34-4d61-8629-064c59dc0b7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 1KI 20:21
Text: And the king of Israel went out, and smote the horses and chariots, and slew the Syrians with a great slaughter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eba97379-df95-430a-9fa0-513233aa7cfb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: 1KI 20:22
Text: And the prophet came to the king of Israel, and said unto him, Go, strengthen thyself, and mark, and see what thou doest: for at the return of the year the king of Syria will come up against thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6fc4186-4904-41f3-8e83-8e94b7ae2663>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: 1KI 20:23
Text: And the servants of the king of Syria said unto him, Their gods are gods of the hills; therefore they were stronger than we; but let us fight against them in the plain, and surely we shall be stronger than they.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5200376a-6ad7-4d73-95f1-12e8dbc40fba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 1KI 20:24
Text: And do this thing, Take the kings away, every man out of his place, and put captains in their rooms:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb198994-c0c1-4380-875d-03850df95f05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: 1KI 20:25
Text: And number thee an army, like the army that thou hast lost, horse for horse, and chariot for chariot: and we will fight against them in the plain, and surely we shall be stronger than they. And he hearkened unto their voice, and did so.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6cff64e3-d08d-4d17-87f2-54c8506b41a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 1KI 20:26
Text: And it came to pass at the return of the year, that Benhadad numbered the Syrians, and went up to Aphek, to fight against Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e14311d-7c2e-489f-979a-9249b90f486d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: 1KI 20:27
Text: And the children of Israel were numbered, and were all present, and went against them: and the children of Israel pitched before them like two little flocks of kids; but the Syrians filled the country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c5f7e86-37d5-4302-a548-4865ca2136ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 322

Reference: 1KI 20:28
Text: And there came a man of God, and spake unto the king of Israel, and said, Thus saith the LORD, Because the Syrians have said, The LORD is God of the hills, but he is not God of the valleys, therefore will I deliver all this great multitude into thine hand, and ye shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2dacc9d8-62b4-43de-9f08-ceb075a86db5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: 1KI 20:29
Text: And they pitched one over against the other seven days. And so it was, that in the seventh day the battle was joined: and the children of Israel slew of the Syrians an hundred thousand footmen in one day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa2962a9-913a-46a9-8116-2d57584b200a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: 1KI 20:30
Text: But the rest fled to Aphek, into the city; and there a wall fell upon twenty and seven thousand of the men that were left. And Benhadad fled, and came into the city, into an inner chamber.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68ef8009-46d0-451f-abf0-e4ca0e6cc8b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 288

Reference: 1KI 20:31
Text: And his servants said unto him, Behold now, we have heard that the kings of the house of Israel are merciful kings: let us, I pray thee, put sackcloth on our loins, and ropes upon our heads, and go out to the king of Israel: peradventure he will save thy life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8dbb5fab-fc61-4361-b15a-714789594093>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: 1KI 20:32
Text: So they girded sackcloth on their loins, and put ropes on their heads, and came to the king of Israel, and said, Thy servant Benhadad saith, I pray thee, let me live. And he said, Is he yet alive? he is my brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a58f867-b978-4989-98e7-4dc54677c7b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: 1KI 20:33
Text: Now the men did diligently observe whether any thing would come from him, and did hastily catch it: and they said, Thy brother Benhadad. Then he said, Go ye, bring him. Then Benhadad came forth to him; and he caused him to come up into the chariot.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64824c62-0279-4f7a-a752-4d6d4d948973>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 310

Reference: 1KI 20:34
Text: And Benhadad said unto him, The cities, which my father took from thy father, I will restore; and thou shalt make streets for thee in Damascus, as my father made in Samaria. Then said Ahab, I will send thee away with this covenant. So he made a covenant with him, and sent him away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:271cbea6-155c-4f17-8029-832c367b6636>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 1KI 20:35
Text: And a certain man of the sons of the prophets said unto his neighbour in the word of the LORD, Smite me, I pray thee. And the man refused to smite him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b4752bd-2ecf-4838-a8e4-7222ede7e125>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: 1KI 20:36
Text: Then said he unto him, Because thou hast not obeyed the voice of the LORD, behold, as soon as thou art departed from me, a lion shall slay thee. And as soon as he was departed from him, a lion found him, and slew him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:438acdca-1318-4398-a107-c8a2bea598d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 1KI 20:37
Text: Then he found another man, and said, Smite me, I pray thee. And the man smote him, so that in smiting he wounded him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23d58e99-6ead-4482-85c7-d89e075c7551>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: 1KI 20:38
Text: So the prophet departed, and waited for the king by the way, and disguised himself with ashes upon his face.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3119748f-4f55-4419-b538-3848a53af904>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 338

Reference: 1KI 20:39
Text: And as the king passed by, he cried unto the king: and he said, Thy servant went out into the midst of the battle; and, behold, a man turned aside, and brought a man unto me, and said, Keep this man: if by any means he be missing, then shall thy life be for his life, or else thou shalt pay a talent of silver.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4335d0e-0227-4f7d-b461-99bcc1359815>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 1KI 20:40
Text: And as thy servant was busy here and there, he was gone. And the king of Israel said unto him, So shall thy judgment be; thyself hast decided it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1bbe23f8-b6ca-4bd5-b2ae-a697e35ade6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 1KI 20:41
Text: And he hasted, and took the ashes away from his face; and the king of Israel discerned him that he was of the prophets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6b52851-64eb-40dc-bd51-fc95cc4019b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: 1KI 20:42
Text: And he said unto him, Thus saith the LORD, Because thou hast let go out of thy hand a man whom I appointed to utter destruction, therefore thy life shall go for his life, and thy people for his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/20/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f79761dc-fc07-4347-918a-8d16d081fd0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: 1KI 20:43
Text: And the king of Israel went to his house heavy and displeased, and came to Samaria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2c59483-5f2a-43fa-bab7-c27705e0067d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 1KI 21:1
Text: And it came to pass after these things, that Naboth the Jezreelite had a vineyard, which was in Jezreel, hard by the palace of Ahab king of Samaria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ac53090-34a1-4f0c-976d-bd7f65c13348>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 287

Reference: 1KI 21:2
Text: And Ahab spake unto Naboth, saying, Give me thy vineyard, that I may have it for a garden of herbs, because it is near unto my house: and I will give thee for it a better vineyard than it; or, if it seem good to thee, I will give thee the worth of it in money.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c84c58e-3f58-4c4c-80fd-1d1a77b6f3a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: 1KI 21:3
Text: And Naboth said to Ahab, The LORD forbid it me, that I should give the inheritance of my fathers unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14dd254c-9362-41d1-b47f-5a97f802b2fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 297

Reference: 1KI 21:4
Text: And Ahab came into his house heavy and displeased because of the word which Naboth the Jezreelite had spoken to him: for he had said, I will not give thee the inheritance of my fathers. And he laid him down upon his bed, and turned away his face, and would eat no bread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:650566fb-c50b-4e26-9f01-3741c8cb89e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 1KI 21:5
Text: But Jezebel his wife came to him, and said unto him, Why is thy spirit so sad, that thou eatest no bread?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8dcb0384-ab76-43cf-b13d-e1afc7d5efc7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: 1KI 21:6
Text: And he said unto her, Because I spake unto Naboth the Jezreelite, and said unto him, Give me thy vineyard for money; or else, if it please thee, I will give thee another vineyard for it: and he answered, I will not give thee my vineyard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d4012d3-b9b8-434d-acfd-075f17722fea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: 1KI 21:7
Text: And Jezebel his wife said unto him, Dost thou now govern the kingdom of Israel? arise, and eat bread, and let thine heart be merry: I will give thee the vineyard of Naboth the Jezreelite.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:433e539e-5b2c-446e-b9d2-be792d4a9ab9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: 1KI 21:8
Text: So she wrote letters in Ahab’s name, and sealed them with his seal, and sent the letters unto the elders and to the nobles that were in his city, dwelling with Naboth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4431af05-dd8d-423b-995c-99775d3b90f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: 1KI 21:9
Text: And she wrote in the letters, saying, Proclaim a fast, and set Naboth on high among the people:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e6bac99-7488-426e-b8b3-f62a07782239>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: 1KI 21:10
Text: And set two men, sons of Belial, before him, to bear witness against him, saying, Thou didst blaspheme God and the king. And then carry him out, and stone him, that he may die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6eef003-32c4-4103-83f8-251d86cb768e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: 1KI 21:11
Text: And the men of his city, even the elders and the nobles who were the inhabitants in his city, did as Jezebel had sent unto them, and as it was written in the letters which she had sent unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d634fea8-d40a-4470-ba32-2a26948cb3ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: 1KI 21:12
Text: They proclaimed a fast, and set Naboth on high among the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f3a3a42-c7ef-4041-acee-4ac4c0529988>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 325

Reference: 1KI 21:13
Text: And there came in two men, children of Belial, and sat before him: and the men of Belial witnessed against him, even against Naboth, in the presence of the people, saying, Naboth did blaspheme God and the king. Then they carried him forth out of the city, and stoned him with stones, that he died.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d364e027-b165-4a9d-b2bd-be83199c461e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: 1KI 21:14
Text: Then they sent to Jezebel, saying, Naboth is stoned, and is dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e036af51-5ac7-43a3-8d12-8780a6ba9582>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 273

Reference: 1KI 21:15
Text: And it came to pass, when Jezebel heard that Naboth was stoned, and was dead, that Jezebel said to Ahab, Arise, take possession of the vineyard of Naboth the Jezreelite, which he refused to give thee for money: for Naboth is not alive, but dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f6fd9d0-b131-4e2b-9383-b341074b8e93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: 1KI 21:16
Text: And it came to pass, when Ahab heard that Naboth was dead, that Ahab rose up to go down to the vineyard of Naboth the Jezreelite, to take possession of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87c7736b-9be4-4ee9-83e0-9ddf7b983fe1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: 1KI 21:17
Text: And the word of the LORD came to Elijah the Tishbite, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63f604fd-5dd9-4a80-8524-6c330aaf5517>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: 1KI 21:18
Text: Arise, go down to meet Ahab king of Israel, which is in Samaria: behold, he is in the vineyard of Naboth, whither he is gone down to possess it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff16287d-756f-4fcd-bdde-688e5fe9a933>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 282

Reference: 1KI 21:19
Text: And thou shalt speak unto him, saying, Thus saith the LORD, Hast thou killed, and also taken possession? And thou shalt speak unto him, saying, Thus saith the LORD, In the place where dogs licked the blood of Naboth shall dogs lick thy blood, even thine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4c60c27-6597-4624-88b1-86adafb2cb34>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: 1KI 21:20
Text: And Ahab said to Elijah, Hast thou found me, O mine enemy? And he answered, I have found thee: because thou hast sold thyself to work evil in the sight of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d74ceac7-204a-47db-a5f1-f32d04722834>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: 1KI 21:21
Text: Behold, I will bring evil upon thee, and will take away thy posterity, and will cut off from Ahab him that pisseth against the wall, and him that is shut up and left in Israel,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e7848c5-e2e8-4093-8f6d-56a6a68160ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: 1KI 21:22
Text: And will make thine house like the house of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, and like the house of Baasha the son of Ahijah, for the provocation wherewith thou hast provoked me to anger, and made Israel to sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c3c11fe-61c9-4dc4-8641-b8e6bec187e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: 1KI 21:23
Text: And of Jezebel also spake the LORD, saying, The dogs shall eat Jezebel by the wall of Jezreel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af4a6492-67da-4d96-a606-8e049827b213>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: 1KI 21:24
Text: Him that dieth of Ahab in the city the dogs shall eat; and him that dieth in the field shall the fowls of the air eat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b204ad42-8647-498c-9212-f70f437bab51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: 1KI 21:25
Text: But there was none like unto Ahab, which did sell himself to work wickedness in the sight of the LORD, whom Jezebel his wife stirred up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffc3a0bf-c072-456b-91f6-5126597efa40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 1KI 21:26
Text: And he did very abominably in following idols, according to all things as did the Amorites, whom the LORD cast out before the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b58d8831-0dec-46f9-8eed-1c6a5878a0e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 1KI 21:27
Text: And it came to pass, when Ahab heard those words, that he rent his clothes, and put sackcloth upon his flesh, and fasted, and lay in sackcloth, and went softly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca4bc900-605a-40e0-9b56-6351c2ef32c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: 1KI 21:28
Text: And the word of the LORD came to Elijah the Tishbite, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/21/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f96545f-14d2-4383-b141-521ab6b35bcd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: 1KI 21:29
Text: Seest thou how Ahab humbleth himself before me? because he humbleth himself before me, I will not bring the evil in his days: but in his son’s days will I bring the evil upon his house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99ae933e-b9ef-43dd-9ddb-4a42d36a6173>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: 1KI 22:1
Text: And they continued three years without war between Syria and Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2869f818-6d9e-4cf7-ac34-fe741077801b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: 1KI 22:2
Text: And it came to pass in the third year, that Jehoshaphat the king of Judah came down to the king of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db7b74d1-9088-471e-835c-29da78964b45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: 1KI 22:3
Text: And the king of Israel said unto his servants, Know ye that Ramoth in Gilead is ours, and we be still, and take it not out of the hand of the king of Syria?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:258bb632-6526-44b0-9e7f-2c0fb774b577>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: 1KI 22:4
Text: And he said unto Jehoshaphat, Wilt thou go with me to battle to Ramothgilead? And Jehoshaphat said to the king of Israel, I am as thou art, my people as thy people, my horses as thy horses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0aceedfe-5071-4a07-b6dc-f8cb682540fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: 1KI 22:5
Text: And Jehoshaphat said unto the king of Israel, Enquire, I pray thee, at the word of the LORD to day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eaad984e-5e79-4a4e-be21-5381ae7dbc47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: 1KI 22:6
Text: Then the king of Israel gathered the prophets together, about four hundred men, and said unto them, Shall I go against Ramothgilead to battle, or shall I forbear? And they said, Go up; for the LORD shall deliver it into the hand of the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e284ecd-5547-4b6c-8286-3414237685a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 1KI 22:7
Text: And Jehoshaphat said, Is there not here a prophet of the LORD besides, that we might enquire of him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:336b27c8-59cf-47cf-b83e-b3e5c2901975>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 274

Reference: 1KI 22:8
Text: And the king of Israel said unto Jehoshaphat, There is yet one man, Micaiah the son of Imlah, by whom we may enquire of the LORD: but I hate him; for he doth not prophesy good concerning me, but evil. And Jehoshaphat said, Let not the king say so.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d558a3a3-27e0-4ea1-8434-b47fdb4614e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: 1KI 22:9
Text: Then the king of Israel called an officer, and said, Hasten hither Micaiah the son of Imlah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d0d39b5-27ac-481a-b549-c796db87dee3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: 1KI 22:10
Text: And the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat the king of Judah sat each on his throne, having put on their robes, in a void place in the entrance of the gate of Samaria; and all the prophets prophesied before them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:357bc79e-9d20-4e5e-9cd0-b06eacb973c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: 1KI 22:11
Text: And Zedekiah the son of Chenaanah made him horns of iron: and he said, Thus saith the LORD, With these shalt thou push the Syrians, until thou have consumed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:154a7e2d-d9a3-49d2-a888-fcc9e86ce722>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 1KI 22:12
Text: And all the prophets prophesied so, saying, Go up to Ramothgilead, and prosper: for the LORD shall deliver it into the king’s hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fee3bb33-5f2a-4e8a-b571-ceb366a8676e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: 1KI 22:13
Text: And the messenger that was gone to call Micaiah spake unto him, saying, Behold now, the words of the prophets declare good unto the king with one mouth: let thy word, I pray thee, be like the word of one of them, and speak that which is good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e679ae23-5a12-4b40-9454-1406be99379d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: 1KI 22:14
Text: And Micaiah said, As the LORD liveth, what the LORD saith unto me, that will I speak.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:610dc410-7af9-413b-b9fa-97106d34e354>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: 1KI 22:15
Text: So he came to the king. And the king said unto him, Micaiah, shall we go against Ramothgilead to battle, or shall we forbear? And he answered him, Go, and prosper: for the LORD shall deliver it into the hand of the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2dd7c5e-cd2c-4cdf-8dc3-0f2280a2929c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: 1KI 22:16
Text: And the king said unto him, How many times shall I adjure thee that thou tell me nothing but that which is true in the name of the LORD?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f95e203f-530f-4a6a-b544-ae2d9b512f65>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: 1KI 22:17
Text: And he said, I saw all Israel scattered upon the hills, as sheep that have not a shepherd: and the LORD said, These have no master: let them return every man to his house in peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:099822f8-7470-4c2e-85e7-aee38550a1df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: 1KI 22:18
Text: And the king of Israel said unto Jehoshaphat, Did I not tell thee that he would prophesy no good concerning me, but evil?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d51bc3d-e423-4701-a3a3-520c40c69632>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: 1KI 22:19
Text: And he said, Hear thou therefore the word of the LORD: I saw the LORD sitting on his throne, and all the host of heaven standing by him on his right hand and on his left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba65d16b-b90f-466a-8369-8b3ba2618901>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 1KI 22:20
Text: And the LORD said, Who shall persuade Ahab, that he may go up and fall at Ramothgilead? And one said on this manner, and another said on that manner.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:564c75fd-c536-40d5-a0cd-fc85751093cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: 1KI 22:21
Text: And there came forth a spirit, and stood before the LORD, and said, I will persuade him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08e67bec-c324-4064-b2fa-e2cef8aae7ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: 1KI 22:22
Text: And the LORD said unto him, Wherewith? And he said, I will go forth, and I will be a lying spirit in the mouth of all his prophets. And he said, Thou shalt persuade him, and prevail also: go forth, and do so.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fbab5bd-b32d-4b60-8944-ad053d93ec27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 1KI 22:23
Text: Now therefore, behold, the LORD hath put a lying spirit in the mouth of all these thy prophets, and the LORD hath spoken evil concerning thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:401b922e-acbc-44b9-b4fe-f3c5f9f65c5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: 1KI 22:24
Text: But Zedekiah the son of Chenaanah went near, and smote Micaiah on the cheek, and said, Which way went the Spirit of the LORD from me to speak unto thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e344b00e-9143-414c-8eb2-78d0ec8d5230>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: 1KI 22:25
Text: And Micaiah said, Behold, thou shalt see in that day, when thou shalt go into an inner chamber to hide thyself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ff8c5ee-5263-4f95-80d5-8efdf1bed335>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: 1KI 22:26
Text: And the king of Israel said, Take Micaiah, and carry him back unto Amon the governor of the city, and to Joash the king’s son;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da68a72d-8357-4176-8d69-02b169d40fbb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 1KI 22:27
Text: And say, Thus saith the king, Put this fellow in the prison, and feed him with bread of affliction and with water of affliction, until I come in peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7cad76c4-5b7b-45d4-9466-d02dc0d35d11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: 1KI 22:28
Text: And Micaiah said, If thou return at all in peace, the LORD hath not spoken by me. And he said, Hearken, O people, every one of you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:345e1746-8d36-45ee-8097-4ce67104a325>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: 1KI 22:29
Text: So the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat the king of Judah went up to Ramothgilead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a20118e8-0a09-4624-85b1-6211c65e138f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: 1KI 22:30
Text: And the king of Israel said unto Jehoshaphat, I will disguise myself, and enter into the battle; but put thou on thy robes. And the king of Israel disguised himself, and went into the battle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b52e9fd3-1f69-4b63-8cca-f52f850ed1af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: 1KI 22:31
Text: But the king of Syria commanded his thirty and two captains that had rule over his chariots, saying, Fight neither with small nor great, save only with the king of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24bfe2a6-88b6-4580-ad40-6b07f3a49ec5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: 1KI 22:32
Text: And it came to pass, when the captains of the chariots saw Jehoshaphat, that they said, Surely it is the king of Israel. And they turned aside to fight against him: and Jehoshaphat cried out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73f205b8-2663-43ca-9336-4960c20ba993>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: 1KI 22:33
Text: And it came to pass, when the captains of the chariots perceived that it was not the king of Israel, that they turned back from pursuing him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:710cfa76-0747-45a8-9585-fa83e5938842>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: 1KI 22:34
Text: And a certain man drew a bow at a venture, and smote the king of Israel between the joints of the harness: wherefore he said unto the driver of his chariot, Turn thine hand, and carry me out of the host; for I am wounded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:658f332f-8373-469e-a330-5219c966c8a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: 1KI 22:35
Text: And the battle increased that day: and the king was stayed up in his chariot against the Syrians, and died at even: and the blood ran out of the wound into the midst of the chariot.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd391bf3-55a0-40a9-bd2a-215f57d0b98b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 1KI 22:36
Text: And there went a proclamation throughout the host about the going down of the sun, saying, Every man to his city, and every man to his own country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a08be33d-cc6d-4361-b5fb-c690e45ff722>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: 1KI 22:37
Text: So the king died, and was brought to Samaria; and they buried the king in Samaria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac1ab57b-48f8-4008-ada5-542445f9ce8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: 1KI 22:38
Text: And one washed the chariot in the pool of Samaria; and the dogs licked up his blood; and they washed his armour; according unto the word of the LORD which he spake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2db1b60c-478c-4495-8dca-3464af37437e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: 1KI 22:39
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Ahab, and all that he did, and the ivory house which he made, and all the cities that he built, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5e3e797-fce1-45c0-9b31-63046812b8f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: 1KI 22:40
Text: So Ahab slept with his fathers; and Ahaziah his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8986c93e-070b-415a-a55b-f23f3dd1a91f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 1KI 22:41
Text: And Jehoshaphat the son of Asa began to reign over Judah in the fourth year of Ahab king of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18bb3daf-af99-405c-82da-9c82100c108b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: 1KI 22:42
Text: Jehoshaphat was thirty and five years old when he began to reign; and he reigned twenty and five years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Azubah the daughter of Shilhi.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0d895e9-549d-4d2b-b3e8-dd2b25c51e63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: 1KI 22:43
Text: And he walked in all the ways of Asa his father; he turned not aside from it, doing that which was right in the eyes of the LORD: nevertheless the high places were not taken away; for the people offered and burnt incense yet in the high places.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f9d942d-ba7f-4a2b-8281-1c9a1d46c328>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: 1KI 22:44
Text: And Jehoshaphat made peace with the king of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8c1ec54-3081-4f78-82a2-a1270bbed1cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: 1KI 22:45
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Jehoshaphat, and his might that he shewed, and how he warred, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:465456fa-4f1b-485e-9226-eac923a2f04e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 1KI 22:46
Text: And the remnant of the sodomites, which remained in the days of his father Asa, he took out of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23399bc6-932f-44bf-90aa-eac764b0a778>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: 1KI 22:47
Text: There was then no king in Edom: a deputy was king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c04c9ed3-6993-4cc5-9b5e-4e73bb6c53fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 1KI 22:48
Text: Jehoshaphat made ships of Tharshish to go to Ophir for gold: but they went not; for the ships were broken at Eziongeber.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18c348c9-6351-4d79-90e3-f825af355865>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 1KI 22:49
Text: Then said Ahaziah the son of Ahab unto Jehoshaphat, Let my servants go with thy servants in the ships. But Jehoshaphat would not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fad0342d-cdcb-49ab-bcd3-0084092e6a0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: 1KI 22:50
Text: And Jehoshaphat slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in the city of David his father: and Jehoram his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96ab1156-cb1e-445a-b631-5a3e4696aa1e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 1KI 22:51
Text: Ahaziah the son of Ahab began to reign over Israel in Samaria the seventeenth year of Jehoshaphat king of Judah, and reigned two years over Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02b27b59-6ea9-443d-9b40-768fbb87ac17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: 1KI 22:52
Text: And he did evil in the sight of the LORD, and walked in the way of his father, and in the way of his mother, and in the way of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who made Israel to sin:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1KI/22/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32b6a9c1-2cc9-42cf-b71e-0b1c9d33fdfa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: 1KI 22:53
Text: For he served Baal, and worshipped him, and provoked to anger the LORD God of Israel, according to all that his father had done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82a07f89-dc62-4572-970f-62539822a001>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: 2KI 1:1
Text: Then Moab rebelled against Israel after the death of Ahab.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ceab8224-11cd-4394-b2af-57b4f2d34b0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: 2KI 1:2
Text: And Ahaziah fell down through a lattice in his upper chamber that was in Samaria, and was sick: and he sent messengers, and said unto them, Go, enquire of Baalzebub the god of Ekron whether I shall recover of this disease.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c51834a-39f8-450d-994a-2a41e5209779>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: 2KI 1:3
Text: But the angel of the LORD said to Elijah the Tishbite, Arise, go up to meet the messengers of the king of Samaria, and say unto them, Is it not because there is not a God in Israel, that ye go to enquire of Baalzebub the god of Ekron?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:596a09f4-71f6-466e-a2aa-e7b5bd0988a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: 2KI 1:4
Text: Now therefore thus saith the LORD, Thou shalt not come down from that bed on which thou art gone up, but shalt surely die. And Elijah departed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89241974-b94d-44fe-af4e-ac9d37b08538>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: 2KI 1:5
Text: And when the messengers turned back unto him, he said unto them, Why are ye now turned back?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:374ea616-82b1-4a89-aefb-37eb8d7bc87a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 388

Reference: 2KI 1:6
Text: And they said unto him, There came a man up to meet us, and said unto us, Go, turn again unto the king that sent you, and say unto him, Thus saith the LORD, Is it not because there is not a God in Israel, that thou sendest to enquire of Baalzebub the god of Ekron? therefore thou shalt not come down from that bed on which thou art gone up, but shalt surely die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:262d9aa4-f226-4ab0-ab60-ea2831bb7a39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 2KI 1:7
Text: And he said unto them, What manner of man was he which came up to meet you, and told you these words?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ed6c92c-9df6-4dce-b654-68484fb27777>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 2KI 1:8
Text: And they answered him, He was an hairy man, and girt with a girdle of leather about his loins. And he said, It is Elijah the Tishbite.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:444fdead-eba5-4d64-8db8-a3eaf46dc645>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: 2KI 1:9
Text: Then the king sent unto him a captain of fifty with his fifty. And he went up to him: and, behold, he sat on the top of an hill. And he spake unto him, Thou man of God, the king hath said, Come down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf4280ca-3fe5-44d1-9778-bc1557521a25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: 2KI 1:10
Text: And Elijah answered and said to the captain of fifty, If I be a man of God, then let fire come down from heaven, and consume thee and thy fifty. And there came down fire from heaven, and consumed him and his fifty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9282d2c7-23e7-4151-a2c1-42e980af966a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 2KI 1:11
Text: Again also he sent unto him another captain of fifty with his fifty. And he answered and said unto him, O man of God, thus hath the king said, Come down quickly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4767571-8680-46cf-b296-bd5b5326055a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: 2KI 1:12
Text: And Elijah answered and said unto them, If I be a man of God, let fire come down from heaven, and consume thee and thy fifty. And the fire of God came down from heaven, and consumed him and his fifty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2be6c06-90fe-4b9c-88a3-d6c643169aa6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 320

Reference: 2KI 1:13
Text: And he sent again a captain of the third fifty with his fifty. And the third captain of fifty went up, and came and fell on his knees before Elijah, and besought him, and said unto him, O man of God, I pray thee, let my life, and the life of these fifty thy servants, be precious in thy sight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:796082cc-356c-4b2e-bc21-0cbff9de212d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: 2KI 1:14
Text: Behold, there came fire down from heaven, and burnt up the two captains of the former fifties with their fifties: therefore let my life now be precious in thy sight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e57ee97a-2128-4fe4-8b33-34c068153b1e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 2KI 1:15
Text: And the angel of the LORD said unto Elijah, Go down with him: be not afraid of him. And he arose, and went down with him unto the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a33a159-029b-4cd6-94a7-7b6828660dcd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 315

Reference: 2KI 1:16
Text: And he said unto him, Thus saith the LORD, Forasmuch as thou hast sent messengers to enquire of Baalzebub the god of Ekron, is it not because there is no God in Israel to enquire of his word? therefore thou shalt not come down off that bed on which thou art gone up, but shalt surely die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd99204c-e5da-4c28-87a9-01d45583d77b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: 2KI 1:17
Text: So he died according to the word of the LORD which Elijah had spoken. And Jehoram reigned in his stead in the second year of Jehoram the son of Jehoshaphat king of Judah; because he had no son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:609e485b-9a20-45a6-93d9-d5eb9837cf6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: 2KI 1:18
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Ahaziah which he did, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb61cce2-bfdd-4605-80a0-6ce008ec7f08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: 2KI 2:1
Text: And it came to pass, when the LORD would take up Elijah into heaven by a whirlwind, that Elijah went with Elisha from Gilgal.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c68f6de-64a8-48cd-a96d-e0650cab90ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: 2KI 2:2
Text: And Elijah said unto Elisha, Tarry here, I pray thee; for the LORD hath sent me to Bethel. And Elisha said unto him, As the LORD liveth, and as thy soul liveth, I will not leave thee. So they went down to Bethel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69fc7a7f-48d6-4aad-bb3a-08e413397cf3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: 2KI 2:3
Text: And the sons of the prophets that were at Bethel came forth to Elisha, and said unto him, Knowest thou that the LORD will take away thy master from thy head to day? And he said, Yea, I know it; hold ye your peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9eb33f75-2245-4d2f-9745-0c0d68f909ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: 2KI 2:4
Text: And Elijah said unto him, Elisha, tarry here, I pray thee; for the LORD hath sent me to Jericho. And he said, As the LORD liveth, and as thy soul liveth, I will not leave thee. So they came to Jericho.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30c1685a-029e-4bda-b35a-a6520b74a093>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: 2KI 2:5
Text: And the sons of the prophets that were at Jericho came to Elisha, and said unto him, Knowest thou that the LORD will take away thy master from thy head to day? And he answered, Yea, I know it; hold ye your peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fc49809-b23b-4523-866b-ad71b52943a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: 2KI 2:6
Text: And Elijah said unto him, Tarry, I pray thee, here; for the LORD hath sent me to Jordan. And he said, As the LORD liveth, and as thy soul liveth, I will not leave thee. And they two went on.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0b0d190-7d5e-46d5-8787-112a6f4eff26>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: 2KI 2:7
Text: And fifty men of the sons of the prophets went, and stood to view afar off: and they two stood by Jordan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1a96233-a225-4425-aec5-1e1f867b1aad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: 2KI 2:8
Text: And Elijah took his mantle, and wrapped it together, and smote the waters, and they were divided hither and thither, so that they two went over on dry ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e901c5d8-1dd7-4d3b-ba83-67a4c245929f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: 2KI 2:9
Text: And it came to pass, when they were gone over, that Elijah said unto Elisha, Ask what I shall do for thee, before I be taken away from thee. And Elisha said, I pray thee, let a double portion of thy spirit be upon me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24831e57-d2db-427f-853f-8510f41c193e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: 2KI 2:10
Text: And he said, Thou hast asked a hard thing: nevertheless, if thou see me when I am taken from thee, it shall be so unto thee; but if not, it shall not be so.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d47bac4c-b7ec-48db-ba35-0504368adb1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: 2KI 2:11
Text: And it came to pass, as they still went on, and talked, that, behold, there appeared a chariot of fire, and horses of fire, and parted them both asunder; and Elijah went up by a whirlwind into heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6451826-4080-4e70-ae92-7e876a553b2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: 2KI 2:12
Text: And Elisha saw it, and he cried, My father, my father, the chariot of Israel, and the horsemen thereof. And he saw him no more: and he took hold of his own clothes, and rent them in two pieces.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfe1a3c0-50a2-4d65-a039-a0c98a1571c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: 2KI 2:13
Text: He took up also the mantle of Elijah that fell from him, and went back, and stood by the bank of Jordan;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa0b1e7e-c171-491c-98f5-7a1c50297189>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: 2KI 2:14
Text: And he took the mantle of Elijah that fell from him, and smote the waters, and said, Where is the LORD God of Elijah? and when he also had smitten the waters, they parted hither and thither: and Elisha went over.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:beacd270-1eda-4f55-b9e0-17386a70b0fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: 2KI 2:15
Text: And when the sons of the prophets which were to view at Jericho saw him, they said, The spirit of Elijah doth rest on Elisha. And they came to meet him, and bowed themselves to the ground before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df71f7bd-a98f-48a3-9082-3efc774da2b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 301

Reference: 2KI 2:16
Text: And they said unto him, Behold now, there be with thy servants fifty strong men; let them go, we pray thee, and seek thy master: lest peradventure the Spirit of the LORD hath taken him up, and cast him upon some mountain, or into some valley. And he said, Ye shall not send.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce6f29be-2123-4db7-ab8a-9e94a4180ba2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: 2KI 2:17
Text: And when they urged him till he was ashamed, he said, Send. They sent therefore fifty men; and they sought three days, but found him not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:284f7ee4-c0af-4ac6-b614-dc45953f3de2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: 2KI 2:18
Text: And when they came again to him, (for he tarried at Jericho,) he said unto them, Did I not say unto you, Go not?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:736e816d-4496-4513-9683-f2bcb9092df4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: 2KI 2:19
Text: And the men of the city said unto Elisha, Behold, I pray thee, the situation of this city is pleasant, as my lord seeth: but the water is naught, and the ground barren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93c3a97e-0f9c-4eab-8bdc-24c524d6fbe7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: 2KI 2:20
Text: And he said, Bring me a new cruse, and put salt therein. And they brought it to him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d26547f3-f658-42c7-a479-303ffb9d1fd3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: 2KI 2:21
Text: And he went forth unto the spring of the waters, and cast the salt in there, and said, Thus saith the LORD, I have healed these waters; there shall not be from thence any more death or barren land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1289497e-adfc-4c40-a9fa-635b43165395>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: 2KI 2:22
Text: So the waters were healed unto this day, according to the saying of Elisha which he spake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bad0e16-c200-4716-b0fe-94e6e2c8a67c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: 2KI 2:23
Text: And he went up from thence unto Bethel: and as he was going up by the way, there came forth little children out of the city, and mocked him, and said unto him, Go up, thou bald head; go up, thou bald head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e546f67-e38c-4758-9bf2-44770d46fe47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 2KI 2:24
Text: And he turned back, and looked on them, and cursed them in the name of the LORD. And there came forth two she bears out of the wood, and tare forty and two children of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/2/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:888670c7-c8be-48c9-b801-1d28b731f7ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: 2KI 2:25
Text: And he went from thence to mount Carmel, and from thence he returned to Samaria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd5fb458-399e-4f7d-8df5-c20358ac9ad3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 2KI 3:1
Text: Now Jehoram the son of Ahab began to reign over Israel in Samaria the eighteenth year of Jehoshaphat king of Judah, and reigned twelve years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0145c2b1-6915-447f-8f40-72896298b342>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 2KI 3:2
Text: And he wrought evil in the sight of the LORD; but not like his father, and like his mother: for he put away the image of Baal that his father had made.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:221f87c0-ae05-45d1-949f-26ae66d72adc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: 2KI 3:3
Text: Nevertheless he cleaved unto the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, which made Israel to sin; he departed not therefrom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1610e385-3ef6-4d50-a55f-fea7dcd80e1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: 2KI 3:4
Text: And Mesha king of Moab was a sheepmaster, and rendered unto the king of Israel an hundred thousand lambs, and an hundred thousand rams, with the wool.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:130c4ff6-85bc-48e2-8343-18ade851349a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: 2KI 3:5
Text: But it came to pass, when Ahab was dead, that the king of Moab rebelled against the king of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7a898fe-6495-4233-a1f8-e71565d28f67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: 2KI 3:6
Text: And king Jehoram went out of Samaria the same time, and numbered all Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64141bc9-08ab-4978-a812-ed687e024223>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: 2KI 3:7
Text: And he went and sent to Jehoshaphat the king of Judah, saying, The king of Moab hath rebelled against me: wilt thou go with me against Moab to battle? And he said, I will go up: I am as thou art, my people as thy people, and my horses as thy horses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61cfa3da-1397-41a9-8b0e-5448fe6f178f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 2KI 3:8
Text: And he said, Which way shall we go up? And he answered, The way through the wilderness of Edom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:927d6434-dc74-4453-93fa-a49c7de38294>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: 2KI 3:9
Text: So the king of Israel went, and the king of Judah, and the king of Edom: and they fetched a compass of seven days’ journey: and there was no water for the host, and for the cattle that followed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6d451a4-68a2-4e45-87b8-19f09293e817>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: 2KI 3:10
Text: And the king of Israel said, Alas! that the LORD hath called these three kings together, to deliver them into the hand of Moab!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e40cc361-163d-4faf-ba4b-781d30a9ff48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: 2KI 3:11
Text: But Jehoshaphat said, Is there not here a prophet of the LORD, that we may enquire of the LORD by him? And one of the king of Israel’s servants answered and said, Here is Elisha the son of Shaphat, which poured water on the hands of Elijah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b0b4b2f-63ba-4380-a4c6-ec2a4bdb214c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: 2KI 3:12
Text: And Jehoshaphat said, The word of the LORD is with him. So the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat and the king of Edom went down to him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0be9a39-86da-4e89-a4a8-3a242314babd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 306

Reference: 2KI 3:13
Text: And Elisha said unto the king of Israel, What have I to do with thee? get thee to the prophets of thy father, and to the prophets of thy mother. And the king of Israel said unto him, Nay: for the LORD hath called these three kings together, to deliver them into the hand of Moab.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b60aa94d-94f6-4629-a760-5e1c88081ebd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: 2KI 3:14
Text: And Elisha said, As the LORD of hosts liveth, before whom I stand, surely, were it not that I regard the presence of Jehoshaphat the king of Judah, I would not look toward thee, nor see thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a8dedc3-23ca-484c-aa1f-8502ef43a101>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: 2KI 3:15
Text: But now bring me a minstrel. And it came to pass, when the minstrel played, that the hand of the LORD came upon him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a94c4f1b-3bc5-4e91-a7b0-f8aaa2a0ed2d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: 2KI 3:16
Text: And he said, Thus saith the LORD, Make this valley full of ditches.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c24dcf5d-5eee-417b-a8fd-a371617e0b41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: 2KI 3:17
Text: For thus saith the LORD, Ye shall not see wind, neither shall ye see rain; yet that valley shall be filled with water, that ye may drink, both ye, and your cattle, and your beasts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:add7a973-72a9-4ac7-99d2-b1067c81e555>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 2KI 3:18
Text: And this is but a light thing in the sight of the LORD: he will deliver the Moabites also into your hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6073f0cc-27a3-44f3-8b48-a7b2f6da2fee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: 2KI 3:19
Text: And ye shall smite every fenced city, and every choice city, and shall fell every good tree, and stop all wells of water, and mar every good piece of land with stones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5aa7e9f-1c2f-4a95-a68d-a9f8db18332a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 2KI 3:20
Text: And it came to pass in the morning, when the meat offering was offered, that, behold, there came water by the way of Edom, and the country was filled with water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dcc24a35-4f34-4ecb-89ad-0d7773489bab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: 2KI 3:21
Text: And when all the Moabites heard that the kings were come up to fight against them, they gathered all that were able to put on armour, and upward, and stood in the border.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e44840b3-f2e0-433d-933d-5f5044c66bb2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: 2KI 3:22
Text: And they rose up early in the morning, and the sun shone upon the water, and the Moabites saw the water on the other side as red as blood:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02c46fb3-1f24-43ec-b76f-2bfd546901a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: 2KI 3:23
Text: And they said, This is blood: the kings are surely slain, and they have smitten one another: now therefore, Moab, to the spoil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33f9399e-d008-4ec6-aabd-cbae36bed008>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: 2KI 3:24
Text: And when they came to the camp of Israel, the Israelites rose up and smote the Moabites, so that they fled before them: but they went forward smiting the Moabites, even in their country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df57fb9c-7315-4bce-95f4-5aa57be56ec2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 302

Reference: 2KI 3:25
Text: And they beat down the cities, and on every good piece of land cast every man his stone, and filled it; and they stopped all the wells of water, and felled all the good trees: only in Kirharaseth left they the stones thereof; howbeit the slingers went about it, and smote it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b52460d2-734b-43f5-977e-2c1b4edb0aff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: 2KI 3:26
Text: And when the king of Moab saw that the battle was too sore for him, he took with him seven hundred men that drew swords, to break through even unto the king of Edom: but they could not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/3/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a070669a-7387-4070-a307-6e8db1816f2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: 2KI 3:27
Text: Then he took his eldest son that should have reigned in his stead, and offered him for a burnt offering upon the wall. And there was great indignation against Israel: and they departed from him, and returned to their own land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e47a5c58-f182-4fad-8f31-dd5cce473b4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 273

Reference: 2KI 4:1
Text: Now there cried a certain woman of the wives of the sons of the prophets unto Elisha, saying, Thy servant my husband is dead; and thou knowest that thy servant did fear the LORD: and the creditor is come to take unto him my two sons to be bondmen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bfab4a13-44a8-41f5-9497-2c314b78ff1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: 2KI 4:2
Text: And Elisha said unto her, What shall I do for thee? tell me, what hast thou in the house? And she said, Thine handmaid hath not any thing in the house, save a pot of oil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49e9e9e4-8683-44b7-9782-5fa76b920efc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: 2KI 4:3
Text: Then he said, Go, borrow thee vessels abroad of all thy neighbours, even empty vessels; borrow not a few.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8911429a-0dac-4448-96ca-6201710feacb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: 2KI 4:4
Text: And when thou art come in, thou shalt shut the door upon thee and upon thy sons, and shalt pour out into all those vessels, and thou shalt set aside that which is full.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f170666b-ca45-4102-8c1f-997f451c5d38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 2KI 4:5
Text: So she went from him, and shut the door upon her and upon her sons, who brought the vessels to her; and she poured out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c71466f-35cf-4700-a6e9-8e0974ccf425>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: 2KI 4:6
Text: And it came to pass, when the vessels were full, that she said unto her son, Bring me yet a vessel. And he said unto her, There is not a vessel more. And the oil stayed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a489a78-66c6-4503-ab1a-d111ace32fca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 2KI 4:7
Text: Then she came and told the man of God. And he said, Go, sell the oil, and pay thy debt, and live thou and thy children of the rest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a970c6f-b4c1-41e1-8e83-c23a77be7ff2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: 2KI 4:8
Text: And it fell on a day, that Elisha passed to Shunem, where was a great woman; and she constrained him to eat bread. And so it was, that as oft as he passed by, he turned in thither to eat bread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2710923-762e-4c50-bbfe-670f92e1727f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 2KI 4:9
Text: And she said unto her husband, Behold now, I perceive that this is an holy man of God, which passeth by us continually.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:419d01a7-4535-473f-9241-20a132e83c03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: 2KI 4:10
Text: Let us make a little chamber, I pray thee, on the wall; and let us set for him there a bed, and a table, and a stool, and a candlestick: and it shall be, when he cometh to us, that he shall turn in thither.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:837334c7-7126-41e5-ac24-cccd4ec4cc38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: 2KI 4:11
Text: And it fell on a day, that he came thither, and he turned into the chamber, and lay there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f07005e-44ed-42da-9b8e-1326c45a73d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: 2KI 4:12
Text: And he said to Gehazi his servant, Call this Shunammite. And when he had called her, she stood before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac78083c-d3a2-4667-a1b4-2adf4f5d1444>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 274

Reference: 2KI 4:13
Text: And he said unto him, Say now unto her, Behold, thou hast been careful for us with all this care; what is to be done for thee? wouldest thou be spoken for to the king, or to the captain of the host? And she answered, I dwell among mine own people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a39555f7-f6eb-402c-88b2-9ea9666ba09d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: 2KI 4:14
Text: And he said, What then is to be done for her? And Gehazi answered, Verily she hath no child, and her husband is old.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8dac90d6-bfa9-480f-ab4b-60ff69a512d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: 2KI 4:15
Text: And he said, Call her. And when he had called her, she stood in the door.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1dd24a7-a5c7-4586-aebe-94f5915bb684>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: 2KI 4:16
Text: And he said, About this season, according to the time of life, thou shalt embrace a son. And she said, Nay, my lord, thou man of God, do not lie unto thine handmaid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d4a6b38-d370-4b83-9bc3-344c0ec21207>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: 2KI 4:17
Text: And the woman conceived, and bare a son at that season that Elisha had said unto her, according to the time of life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff5b1189-3f2e-4c93-8151-2bd473bef19e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 2KI 4:18
Text: And when the child was grown, it fell on a day, that he went out to his father to the reapers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2eb05b6-aebb-4963-aca5-b37d1bcf423a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: 2KI 4:19
Text: And he said unto his father, My head, my head. And he said to a lad, Carry him to his mother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91045c5f-c248-495f-91f9-92bf5e87f272>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: 2KI 4:20
Text: And when he had taken him, and brought him to his mother, he sat on her knees till noon, and then died.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3da3ccd8-0920-488b-aeee-fae21b457f5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 2KI 4:21
Text: And she went up, and laid him on the bed of the man of God, and shut the door upon him, and went out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9125ee7b-43fd-4437-aadd-3fed49987a35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 2KI 4:22
Text: And she called unto her husband, and said, Send me, I pray thee, one of the young men, and one of the asses, that I may run to the man of God, and come again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9cbd9986-f7eb-4720-b478-ee41db70452a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: 2KI 4:23
Text: And he said, Wherefore wilt thou go to him to day? it is neither new moon, nor sabbath. And she said, It shall be well.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba66af5f-2b5b-4b43-9586-90bdcea4c9a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 2KI 4:24
Text: Then she saddled an ass, and said to her servant, Drive, and go forward; slack not thy riding for me, except I bid thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53f3e9ae-9aaa-47c8-a9e8-5c8ef1c9bdc8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: 2KI 4:25
Text: So she went and came unto the man of God to mount Carmel. And it came to pass, when the man of God saw her afar off, that he said to Gehazi his servant, Behold, yonder is that Shunammite:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ca79445-f2e8-4f5f-8cfc-68d103e372ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 2KI 4:26
Text: Run now, I pray thee, to meet her, and say unto her, Is it well with thee? is it well with thy husband? is it well with the child? And she answered, It is well:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35fec65a-b740-469d-870e-230947e396ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 274

Reference: 2KI 4:27
Text: And when she came to the man of God to the hill, she caught him by the feet: but Gehazi came near to thrust her away. And the man of God said, Let her alone; for her soul is vexed within her: and the LORD hath hid it from me, and hath not told me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fcf9a653-3918-46f3-85ff-24b805850c9e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: 2KI 4:28
Text: Then she said, Did I desire a son of my lord? did I not say, Do not deceive me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cedded8-4866-47cd-bffd-9c524a7ce93a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: 2KI 4:29
Text: Then he said to Gehazi, Gird up thy loins, and take my staff in thine hand, and go thy way: if thou meet any man, salute him not; and if any salute thee, answer him not again: and lay my staff upon the face of the child.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64466915-c66e-4e0c-99c0-375c2d0c0876>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: 2KI 4:30
Text: And the mother of the child said, As the LORD liveth, and as thy soul liveth, I will not leave thee. And he arose, and followed her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e13a6a6-b529-4209-9189-1bd6468bef78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: 2KI 4:31
Text: And Gehazi passed on before them, and laid the staff upon the face of the child; but there was neither voice, nor hearing. Wherefore he went again to meet him, and told him, saying, The child is not awaked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:544ea6ee-7d39-4f22-8b77-8fd71f2ab027>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: 2KI 4:32
Text: And when Elisha was come into the house, behold, the child was dead, and laid upon his bed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d37eb87d-9431-42e1-8682-ad53547a31d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: 2KI 4:33
Text: He went in therefore, and shut the door upon them twain, and prayed unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2642fafe-2ef4-4e35-a88d-a365077a8516>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: 2KI 4:34
Text: And he went up, and lay upon the child, and put his mouth upon his mouth, and his eyes upon his eyes, and his hands upon his hands: and stretched himself upon the child; and the flesh of the child waxed warm.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f35434bb-9160-4e5a-938e-531ea54a4395>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: 2KI 4:35
Text: Then he returned, and walked in the house to and fro; and went up, and stretched himself upon him: and the child sneezed seven times, and the child opened his eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31079e40-dbed-4274-9ef7-4346569f3988>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: 2KI 4:36
Text: And he called Gehazi, and said, Call this Shunammite. So he called her. And when she was come in unto him, he said, Take up thy son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1bd717f0-fcb2-4742-8c65-36ffc5e54db2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: 2KI 4:37
Text: Then she went in, and fell at his feet, and bowed herself to the ground, and took up her son, and went out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed77ddfc-4c1d-4094-8e92-71a29f85c483>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: 2KI 4:38
Text: And Elisha came again to Gilgal: and there was a dearth in the land; and the sons of the prophets were sitting before him: and he said unto his servant, Set on the great pot, and seethe pottage for the sons of the prophets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c737a5b-89d5-422c-99c9-e874259e415b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: 2KI 4:39
Text: And one went out into the field to gather herbs, and found a wild vine, and gathered thereof wild gourds his lap full, and came and shred them into the pot of pottage: for they knew them not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b8d369b-b6a7-4be6-89fd-36a329114e12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: 2KI 4:40
Text: So they poured out for the men to eat. And it came to pass, as they were eating of the pottage, that they cried out, and said, O thou man of God, there is death in the pot. And they could not eat thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:171c1663-b65a-4f2b-ada4-8bba737aac3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: 2KI 4:41
Text: But he said, Then bring meal. And he cast it into the pot; and he said, Pour out for the people, that they may eat. And there was no harm in the pot.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a19edd10-7086-4423-86ac-4dca6ab70f5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: 2KI 4:42
Text: And there came a man from Baalshalisha, and brought the man of God bread of the firstfruits, twenty loaves of barley, and full ears of corn in the husk thereof. And he said, Give unto the people, that they may eat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:615b297d-8f0e-4969-823f-8730b586e0a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: 2KI 4:43
Text: And his servitor said, What, should I set this before an hundred men? He said again, Give the people, that they may eat: for thus saith the LORD, They shall eat, and shall leave thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/4/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b891dc2-587f-425b-9591-8ae2c41147ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 2KI 4:44
Text: So he set it before them, and they did eat, and left thereof, according to the word of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1dfe49a7-f6f3-455c-9426-a908d8ee07df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: 2KI 5:1
Text: Now Naaman, captain of the host of the king of Syria, was a great man with his master, and honourable, because by him the LORD had given deliverance unto Syria: he was also a mighty man in valour, but he was a leper.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f77a2009-87d6-4ee7-bed4-d38c5430a7ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 2KI 5:2
Text: And the Syrians had gone out by companies, and had brought away captive out of the land of Israel a little maid; and she waited on Naaman’s wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edc2bc60-342f-4070-8bd0-db79a7c62ef4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 2KI 5:3
Text: And she said unto her mistress, Would God my lord were with the prophet that is in Samaria! for he would recover him of his leprosy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed916035-e11d-4b06-801d-320d227b27bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 2KI 5:4
Text: And one went in, and told his lord, saying, Thus and thus said the maid that is of the land of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ec2fc93-5f3d-495b-ab6f-f361e7b3f1f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: 2KI 5:5
Text: And the king of Syria said, Go to, go, and I will send a letter unto the king of Israel. And he departed, and took with him ten talents of silver, and six thousand pieces of gold, and ten changes of raiment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2108cba8-d696-406e-bffd-83c742454fe2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: 2KI 5:6
Text: And he brought the letter to the king of Israel, saying, Now when this letter is come unto thee, behold, I have therewith sent Naaman my servant to thee, that thou mayest recover him of his leprosy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02e39283-92e5-4aa9-bddf-d7d2eadef537>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 306

Reference: 2KI 5:7
Text: And it came to pass, when the king of Israel had read the letter, that he rent his clothes, and said, Am I God, to kill and to make alive, that this man doth send unto me to recover a man of his leprosy? wherefore consider, I pray you, and see how he seeketh a quarrel against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e2ea6d2-2669-4650-9de5-c6544f5344bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: 2KI 5:8
Text: And it was so, when Elisha the man of God had heard that the king of Israel had rent his clothes, that he sent to the king, saying, Wherefore hast thou rent thy clothes? let him come now to me, and he shall know that there is a prophet in Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c80645b-d8d0-48ba-bea3-e76286af8a38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: 2KI 5:9
Text: So Naaman came with his horses and with his chariot, and stood at the door of the house of Elisha.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55f18411-a3cf-449c-a644-b9835880733e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: 2KI 5:10
Text: And Elisha sent a messenger unto him, saying, Go and wash in Jordan seven times, and thy flesh shall come again to thee, and thou shalt be clean.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fe2377f-652e-42c0-90cc-8ffe3c4c0427>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: 2KI 5:11
Text: But Naaman was wroth, and went away, and said, Behold, I thought, He will surely come out to me, and stand, and call on the name of the LORD his God, and strike his hand over the place, and recover the leper.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a2411e4-c0a7-42d0-8b5c-90b5b9419302>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 2KI 5:12
Text: Are not Abana and Pharpar, rivers of Damascus, better than all the waters of Israel? may I not wash in them, and be clean? So he turned and went away in a rage.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8b6c8c8-9d78-4290-8f34-7a94a294e0b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: 2KI 5:13
Text: And his servants came near, and spake unto him, and said, My father, if the prophet had bid thee do some great thing, wouldest thou not have done it? how much rather then, when he saith to thee, Wash, and be clean?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09aac9fa-07b8-4a9e-86d7-3b844437db0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: 2KI 5:14
Text: Then went he down, and dipped himself seven times in Jordan, according to the saying of the man of God: and his flesh came again like unto the flesh of a little child, and he was clean.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:423783d4-fcc6-4a73-b494-5da7edecac82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: 2KI 5:15
Text: And he returned to the man of God, he and all his company, and came, and stood before him: and he said, Behold, now I know that there is no God in all the earth, but in Israel: now therefore, I pray thee, take a blessing of thy servant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e489c3ad-835e-4f9a-acf0-47be12519a23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: 2KI 5:16
Text: But he said, As the LORD liveth, before whom I stand, I will receive none. And he urged him to take it; but he refused.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:799a42c7-146b-4aea-823e-cd3ef34750c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: 2KI 5:17
Text: And Naaman said, Shall there not then, I pray thee, be given to thy servant two mules’ burden of earth? for thy servant will henceforth offer neither burnt offering nor sacrifice unto other gods, but unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:030a1236-0e5e-462c-a8e9-354ab4911b9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 296

Reference: 2KI 5:18
Text: In this thing the LORD pardon thy servant, that when my master goeth into the house of Rimmon to worship there, and he leaneth on my hand, and I bow myself in the house of Rimmon: when I bow down myself in the house of Rimmon, the LORD pardon thy servant in this thing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bba08836-d378-44d5-884b-f298e343d169>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: 2KI 5:19
Text: And he said unto him, Go in peace. So he departed from him a little way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1b32902-6e62-44a0-9656-12a1dfac1411>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: 2KI 5:20
Text: But Gehazi, the servant of Elisha the man of God, said, Behold, my master hath spared Naaman this Syrian, in not receiving at his hands that which he brought: but, as the LORD liveth, I will run after him, and take somewhat of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c333a06-d1fd-48b4-9ce2-c83d076fea26>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: 2KI 5:21
Text: So Gehazi followed after Naaman. And when Naaman saw him running after him, he lighted down from the chariot to meet him, and said, Is all well?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d42ab55-c9b5-4d3f-9282-de7754e7641f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: 2KI 5:22
Text: And he said, All is well. My master hath sent me, saying, Behold, even now there be come to me from mount Ephraim two young men of the sons of the prophets: give them, I pray thee, a talent of silver, and two changes of garments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13899ce1-4783-4936-aef3-7c9fc364cd99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: 2KI 5:23
Text: And Naaman said, Be content, take two talents. And he urged him, and bound two talents of silver in two bags, with two changes of garments, and laid them upon two of his servants; and they bare them before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c3dbd86-d755-4575-b1e1-c977036702f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 2KI 5:24
Text: And when he came to the tower, he took them from their hand, and bestowed them in the house: and he let the men go, and they departed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fd2afb7-51a2-4b04-9066-3a5b25f8cb34>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 2KI 5:25
Text: But he went in, and stood before his master. And Elisha said unto him, Whence comest thou, Gehazi? And he said, Thy servant went no whither.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88de5fc4-29d1-4b3a-9de3-8a965c643330>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 279

Reference: 2KI 5:26
Text: And he said unto him, Went not mine heart with thee, when the man turned again from his chariot to meet thee? Is it a time to receive money, and to receive garments, and oliveyards, and vineyards, and sheep, and oxen, and menservants, and maidservants?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/5/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28c3cdf6-7f91-4cf3-9de9-ee473c81e938>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 2KI 5:27
Text: The leprosy therefore of Naaman shall cleave unto thee, and unto thy seed for ever. And he went out from his presence a leper as white as snow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25d13a40-4af9-45cc-9119-5812d12cc703>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 2KI 6:1
Text: And the sons of the prophets said unto Elisha, Behold now, the place where we dwell with thee is too strait for us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:027f67d5-38fa-46c9-aa20-39618ac5a94d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 2KI 6:2
Text: Let us go, we pray thee, unto Jordan, and take thence every man a beam, and let us make us a place there, where we may dwell. And he answered, Go ye.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9751c44-6bc7-46b4-a1bf-d76ae45353a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: 2KI 6:3
Text: And one said, Be content, I pray thee, and go with thy servants. And he answered, I will go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d59e50d1-6772-4517-aa44-72086c69b46d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: 2KI 6:4
Text: So he went with them. And when they came to Jordan, they cut down wood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e97885f-9297-4299-a9bb-a42bf5dad3eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: 2KI 6:5
Text: But as one was felling a beam, the axe head fell into the water: and he cried, and said, Alas, master! for it was borrowed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c65ac18-f237-4ece-b8c8-4cf4bf62b14d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: 2KI 6:6
Text: And the man of God said, Where fell it? And he shewed him the place. And he cut down a stick, and cast it in thither; and the iron did swim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de078b9f-508a-4789-9b2e-1562dfe71361>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: 2KI 6:7
Text: Therefore said he, Take it up to thee. And he put out his hand, and took it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f349443-f298-4b0f-9880-401da8523494>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 2KI 6:8
Text: Then the king of Syria warred against Israel, and took counsel with his servants, saying, In such and such a place shall be my camp.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:307610ee-a530-41e0-b011-c8ef1aa1d137>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 2KI 6:9
Text: And the man of God sent unto the king of Israel, saying, Beware that thou pass not such a place; for thither the Syrians are come down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0d02b7e-a1c9-4b79-b440-8664e8e503e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 2KI 6:10
Text: And the king of Israel sent to the place which the man of God told him and warned him of, and saved himself there, not once nor twice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e54674d-7c7e-4a4a-9d8d-29eb394dd849>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: 2KI 6:11
Text: Therefore the heart of the king of Syria was sore troubled for this thing; and he called his servants, and said unto them, Will ye not shew me which of us is for the king of Israel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8f070fc-ec09-4a95-97b5-56abb15e4b72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: 2KI 6:12
Text: And one of his servants said, None, my lord, O king: but Elisha, the prophet that is in Israel, telleth the king of Israel the words that thou speakest in thy bedchamber.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:528b67b6-3e7c-4ff7-8e5a-2e9c192533ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 2KI 6:13
Text: And he said, Go and spy where he is, that I may send and fetch him. And it was told him, saying, Behold, he is in Dothan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:868d80a1-50a2-4cb2-96fb-575c898da3f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: 2KI 6:14
Text: Therefore sent he thither horses, and chariots, and a great host: and they came by night, and compassed the city about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:906381cc-2d84-4290-a1c7-de2c0e2c536e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: 2KI 6:15
Text: And when the servant of the man of God was risen early, and gone forth, behold, an host compassed the city both with horses and chariots. And his servant said unto him, Alas, my master! how shall we do?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19c1e516-d883-4663-96c4-59795e546d0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: 2KI 6:16
Text: And he answered, Fear not: for they that be with us are more than they that be with them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:954415d3-c74a-4614-b1f5-6d54a327c496>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: 2KI 6:17
Text: And Elisha prayed, and said, LORD, I pray thee, open his eyes, that he may see. And the LORD opened the eyes of the young man; and he saw: and, behold, the mountain was full of horses and chariots of fire round about Elisha.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fcff1fb5-ceb4-4f12-9b7a-0254d98356f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: 2KI 6:18
Text: And when they came down to him, Elisha prayed unto the LORD, and said, Smite this people, I pray thee, with blindness. And he smote them with blindness according to the word of Elisha.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d26c9ed-bfa2-4628-b009-b6379709987a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 2KI 6:19
Text: And Elisha said unto them, This is not the way, neither is this the city: follow me, and I will bring you to the man whom ye seek. But he led them to Samaria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:579a5d1f-e293-4659-816c-17833fa8981b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: 2KI 6:20
Text: And it came to pass, when they were come into Samaria, that Elisha said, LORD, open the eyes of these men, that they may see. And the LORD opened their eyes, and they saw; and, behold, they were in the midst of Samaria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f27c7e33-3bc1-43fe-9ab1-e5f2114f02e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: 2KI 6:21
Text: And the king of Israel said unto Elisha, when he saw them, My father, shall I smite them? shall I smite them?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4431975-96a1-48c1-8f7a-57bb82f5f937>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: 2KI 6:22
Text: And he answered, Thou shalt not smite them: wouldest thou smite those whom thou hast taken captive with thy sword and with thy bow? set bread and water before them, that they may eat and drink, and go to their master.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:585e0afe-a302-4479-afbe-8fd6cc30f44f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: 2KI 6:23
Text: And he prepared great provision for them: and when they had eaten and drunk, he sent them away, and they went to their master. So the bands of Syria came no more into the land of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2946be5-c028-4baf-a89a-08983163b79d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: 2KI 6:24
Text: And it came to pass after this, that Benhadad king of Syria gathered all his host, and went up, and besieged Samaria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c17d0c8-703f-4f01-a98b-1a69f0be79fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: 2KI 6:25
Text: And there was a great famine in Samaria: and, behold, they besieged it, until an ass’s head was sold for fourscore pieces of silver, and the fourth part of a cab of dove’s dung for five pieces of silver.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc9a8c09-292c-4387-9085-aaff6934abee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: 2KI 6:26
Text: And as the king of Israel was passing by upon the wall, there cried a woman unto him, saying, Help, my lord, O king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:206396e9-785e-4808-983b-4a13d96e3a9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: 2KI 6:27
Text: And he said, If the LORD do not help thee, whence shall I help thee? out of the barnfloor, or out of the winepress?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce1bb815-83c6-4bec-8e5e-8eaff152e534>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: 2KI 6:28
Text: And the king said unto her, What aileth thee? And she answered, This woman said unto me, Give thy son, that we may eat him to day, and we will eat my son to morrow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11d6af8b-4405-4afb-89f7-e8c999f6cf56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 2KI 6:29
Text: So we boiled my son, and did eat him: and I said unto her on the next day, Give thy son, that we may eat him: and she hath hid her son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3419057-b081-4c10-906b-72e6bdce8647>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: 2KI 6:30
Text: And it came to pass, when the king heard the words of the woman, that he rent his clothes; and he passed by upon the wall, and the people looked, and, behold, he had sackcloth within upon his flesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1bb7ef4-9ba9-4ffb-a77e-2b22b2ffa1a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 2KI 6:31
Text: Then he said, God do so and more also to me, if the head of Elisha the son of Shaphat shall stand on him this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:113e3eba-0209-40d3-83b5-47c07326c711>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 382

Reference: 2KI 6:32
Text: But Elisha sat in his house, and the elders sat with him; and the king sent a man from before him: but ere the messenger came to him, he said to the elders, See ye how this son of a murderer hath sent to take away mine head? look, when the messenger cometh, shut the door, and hold him fast at the door: is not the sound of his master’s feet behind him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/6/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b946d7de-640c-4bd0-9809-986199397dc3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: 2KI 6:33
Text: And while he yet talked with them, behold, the messenger came down unto him: and he said, Behold, this evil is of the LORD; what should I wait for the LORD any longer?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a29d531f-29e3-4c96-920c-33e6c9711c2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: 2KI 7:1
Text: Then Elisha said, Hear ye the word of the LORD; Thus saith the LORD, To morrow about this time shall a measure of fine flour be sold for a shekel, and two measures of barley for a shekel, in the gate of Samaria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b9db294-286c-4c86-a2fb-9885aff30b30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: 2KI 7:2
Text: Then a lord on whose hand the king leaned answered the man of God, and said, Behold, if the LORD would make windows in heaven, might this thing be? And he said, Behold, thou shalt see it with thine eyes, but shalt not eat thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9058f8b2-7ca6-4437-b1a6-7ffbf5d2c952>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: 2KI 7:3
Text: And there were four leprous men at the entering in of the gate: and they said one to another, Why sit we here until we die?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2814e093-faee-4d80-be43-b35353d964f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 303

Reference: 2KI 7:4
Text: If we say, We will enter into the city, then the famine is in the city, and we shall die there: and if we sit still here, we die also. Now therefore come, and let us fall unto the host of the Syrians: if they save us alive, we shall live; and if they kill us, we shall but die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:915d1a6f-3629-478e-99b3-967172bfd470>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: 2KI 7:5
Text: And they rose up in the twilight, to go unto the camp of the Syrians: and when they were come to the uttermost part of the camp of Syria, behold, there was no man there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92e298fc-7efa-4160-8e5d-3443004b4ce2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 306

Reference: 2KI 7:6
Text: For the LORD had made the host of the Syrians to hear a noise of chariots, and a noise of horses, even the noise of a great host: and they said one to another, Lo, the king of Israel hath hired against us the kings of the Hittites, and the kings of the Egyptians, to come upon us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c17aa9e-2d4a-4806-a8f7-cdd06ca2d4b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 2KI 7:7
Text: Wherefore they arose and fled in the twilight, and left their tents, and their horses, and their asses, even the camp as it was, and fled for their life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c355ad6b-a632-4b42-95a4-d632714d4af1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 299

Reference: 2KI 7:8
Text: And when these lepers came to the uttermost part of the camp, they went into one tent, and did eat and drink, and carried thence silver, and gold, and raiment, and went and hid it; and came again, and entered into another tent, and carried thence also, and went and hid it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d41b87f7-b13a-47f4-b234-9e378d3ef621>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: 2KI 7:9
Text: Then they said one to another, We do not well: this day is a day of good tidings, and we hold our peace: if we tarry till the morning light, some mischief will come upon us: now therefore come, that we may go and tell the king’s household.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27297313-ff50-4836-969a-0da4136d38ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: 2KI 7:10
Text: So they came and called unto the porter of the city: and they told them, saying, We came to the camp of the Syrians, and, behold, there was no man there, neither voice of man, but horses tied, and asses tied, and the tents as they were.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91190319-b33d-41c3-bfe5-5ee72ada9ed5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: 2KI 7:11
Text: And he called the porters; and they told it to the king’s house within.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:318e17ab-c54a-430b-b3f8-fbe98b56eea1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 333

Reference: 2KI 7:12
Text: And the king arose in the night, and said unto his servants, I will now shew you what the Syrians have done to us. They know that we be hungry; therefore are they gone out of the camp to hide themselves in the field, saying, When they come out of the city, we shall catch them alive, and get into the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e3150f9-15cb-4338-88da-1c81ad9ebd3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 340

Reference: 2KI 7:13
Text: And one of his servants answered and said, Let some take, I pray thee, five of the horses that remain, which are left in the city, (behold, they are as all the multitude of Israel that are left in it: behold, I say, they are even as all the multitude of the Israelites that are consumed:) and let us send and see.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/7/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32105571-695b-44ae-bf14-2bce2fec0f39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 2KI 7:14
Text: They took therefore two chariot horses; and the king sent after the host of the Syrians, saying, Go and see.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/7/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85c6b074-f781-4eb2-881b-7adbcf880d46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: 2KI 7:15
Text: And they went after them unto Jordan: and, lo, all the way was full of garments and vessels, which the Syrians had cast away in their haste. And the messengers returned, and told the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/7/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be1ea9b2-8ed3-4a8c-88ec-a115441ad22e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: 2KI 7:16
Text: And the people went out, and spoiled the tents of the Syrians. So a measure of fine flour was sold for a shekel, and two measures of barley for a shekel, according to the word of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/7/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7908622a-0e1a-4487-bc4d-925a0b830dce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: 2KI 7:17
Text: And the king appointed the lord on whose hand he leaned to have the charge of the gate: and the people trode upon him in the gate, and he died, as the man of God had said, who spake when the king came down to him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/7/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d2a9ad4-8984-481c-9f51-dca0fa0a8a5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: 2KI 7:18
Text: And it came to pass as the man of God had spoken to the king, saying, Two measures of barley for a shekel, and a measure of fine flour for a shekel, shall be to morrow about this time in the gate of Samaria:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/7/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c2d8c88-0827-4cd2-938c-89ad7599ec12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: 2KI 7:19
Text: And that lord answered the man of God, and said, Now, behold, if the LORD should make windows in heaven, might such a thing be? And he said, Behold, thou shalt see it with thine eyes, but shalt not eat thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/7/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5edd7933-76a0-4f9c-80bf-1bb8808a462e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: 2KI 7:20
Text: And so it fell out unto him: for the people trode upon him in the gate, and he died.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fdc95f1-846d-4ce3-a4ec-a72a47f08bdf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: 2KI 8:1
Text: Then spake Elisha unto the woman, whose son he had restored to life, saying, Arise, and go thou and thine household, and sojourn wheresoever thou canst sojourn: for the LORD hath called for a famine; and it shall also come upon the land seven years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bcd1adf4-fb76-4274-a074-82dbcc5744fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: 2KI 8:2
Text: And the woman arose, and did after the saying of the man of God: and she went with her household, and sojourned in the land of the Philistines seven years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1434af28-592d-4e91-9b10-bd43d76839a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: 2KI 8:3
Text: And it came to pass at the seven years’ end, that the woman returned out of the land of the Philistines: and she went forth to cry unto the king for her house and for her land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65f0bfee-8b8b-40c7-bd50-1abf8dcf07f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 2KI 8:4
Text: And the king talked with Gehazi the servant of the man of God, saying, Tell me, I pray thee, all the great things that Elisha hath done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57ee332d-2056-4b9d-ba06-52c0f19ecdd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 328

Reference: 2KI 8:5
Text: And it came to pass, as he was telling the king how he had restored a dead body to life, that, behold, the woman, whose son he had restored to life, cried to the king for her house and for her land. And Gehazi said, My lord, O king, this is the woman, and this is her son, whom Elisha restored to life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3d8975c-cd48-4041-90ba-fc0436167203>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: 2KI 8:6
Text: And when the king asked the woman, she told him. So the king appointed unto her a certain officer, saying, Restore all that was hers, and all the fruits of the field since the day that she left the land, even until now.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34a8e3f5-cf3b-45a6-bb60-9b9c1ce6a883>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 2KI 8:7
Text: And Elisha came to Damascus; and Benhadad the king of Syria was sick; and it was told him, saying, The man of God is come hither.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0063daac-a909-4e66-b6b1-982591c2002a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 2KI 8:8
Text: And the king said unto Hazael, Take a present in thine hand, and go, meet the man of God, and enquire of the LORD by him, saying, Shall I recover of this disease?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9379493b-402a-4ed0-8108-fa5974aeb9de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 279

Reference: 2KI 8:9
Text: So Hazael went to meet him, and took a present with him, even of every good thing of Damascus, forty camels’ burden, and came and stood before him, and said, Thy son Benhadad king of Syria hath sent me to thee, saying, Shall I recover of this disease?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d618f65-158e-4485-8f04-70e4ce6acaa3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: 2KI 8:10
Text: And Elisha said unto him, Go, say unto him, Thou mayest certainly recover: howbeit the LORD hath shewed me that he shall surely die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba5af723-93a9-42d7-a653-613ca26ca7ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: 2KI 8:11
Text: And he settled his countenance stedfastly, until he was ashamed: and the man of God wept.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c7b835f-7d5c-4177-92a2-fa75ae530d24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 310

Reference: 2KI 8:12
Text: And Hazael said, Why weepeth my lord? And he answered, Because I know the evil that thou wilt do unto the children of Israel: their strong holds wilt thou set on fire, and their young men wilt thou slay with the sword, and wilt dash their children, and rip up their women with child.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:daac5b02-ebc8-4968-a683-b2a2eaff52b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: 2KI 8:13
Text: And Hazael said, But what, is thy servant a dog, that he should do this great thing? And Elisha answered, The LORD hath shewed me that thou shalt be king over Syria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f971514a-c0d1-443e-816a-27b1125f99a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 2KI 8:14
Text: So he departed from Elisha, and came to his master; who said to him, What said Elisha to thee? And he answered, He told me that thou shouldest surely recover.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fdc3b7ad-2c92-4e54-8afb-14bba3735fa3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: 2KI 8:15
Text: And it came to pass on the morrow, that he took a thick cloth, and dipped it in water, and spread it on his face, so that he died: and Hazael reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e65ee006-3101-497b-bad1-dbbcb0f9ba54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 2KI 8:16
Text: And in the fifth year of Joram the son of Ahab king of Israel, Jehoshaphat being then king of Judah, Jehoram the son of Jehoshaphat king of Judah began to reign.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbdbc6ba-8422-4edc-bcb9-e0794591439f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 2KI 8:17
Text: Thirty and two years old was he when he began to reign; and he reigned eight years in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec215d46-be3f-4375-9533-8f8fe6f23c60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: 2KI 8:18
Text: And he walked in the way of the kings of Israel, as did the house of Ahab: for the daughter of Ahab was his wife: and he did evil in the sight of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3092764a-9cb2-4241-a769-d8102d9fbc17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 2KI 8:19
Text: Yet the LORD would not destroy Judah for David his servant’s sake, as he promised him to give him alway a light, and to his children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5970ca1-becd-4e52-b5c8-61a9b4b991eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: 2KI 8:20
Text: In his days Edom revolted from under the hand of Judah, and made a king over themselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3ed394c-27ff-415c-b703-72bb9fd15cd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: 2KI 8:21
Text: So Joram went over to Zair, and all the chariots with him: and he rose by night, and smote the Edomites which compassed him about, and the captains of the chariots: and the people fled into their tents.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6d01c02-4d78-495d-8fa7-d214cf87e612>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 2KI 8:22
Text: Yet Edom revolted from under the hand of Judah unto this day. Then Libnah revolted at the same time.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b7b0a76-2b54-4bcc-9c6e-4708ec351b15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: 2KI 8:23
Text: And the rest of the acts of Joram, and all that he did, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8681f78-aaa2-4052-a8ac-10d9ac60de01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: 2KI 8:24
Text: And Joram slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in the city of David: and Ahaziah his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05e1dc12-0d6e-4185-a3b9-05ebe89a4bd9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 2KI 8:25
Text: In the twelfth year of Joram the son of Ahab king of Israel did Ahaziah the son of Jehoram king of Judah begin to reign.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c3af86d-042a-429f-b2e5-14d86cd23ffb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 2KI 8:26
Text: Two and twenty years old was Ahaziah when he began to reign; and he reigned one year in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Athaliah, the daughter of Omri king of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:878b6317-3e06-494b-8ad5-3c69c9f0900c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: 2KI 8:27
Text: And he walked in the way of the house of Ahab, and did evil in the sight of the LORD, as did the house of Ahab: for he was the son in law of the house of Ahab.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5443d1fc-9e3d-4948-8a81-5ab5f90456ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 2KI 8:28
Text: And he went with Joram the son of Ahab to the war against Hazael king of Syria in Ramothgilead; and the Syrians wounded Joram.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/8/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47df13fe-641f-4311-867c-75230093c373>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 293

Reference: 2KI 8:29
Text: And king Joram went back to be healed in Jezreel of the wounds which the Syrians had given him at Ramah, when he fought against Hazael king of Syria. And Ahaziah the son of Jehoram king of Judah went down to see Joram the son of Ahab in Jezreel, because he was sick.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7b806c6-7c43-4538-807b-c032e6a40ac4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: 2KI 9:1
Text: And Elisha the prophet called one of the children of the prophets, and said unto him, Gird up thy loins, and take this box of oil in thine hand, and go to Ramothgilead:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eefbc8c9-b7b9-4e6f-b2db-9ef75193ded9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: 2KI 9:2
Text: And when thou comest thither, look out there Jehu the son of Jehoshaphat the son of Nimshi, and go in, and make him arise up from among his brethren, and carry him to an inner chamber;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:364a1959-c479-4395-894c-825fdf54300e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: 2KI 9:3
Text: Then take the box of oil, and pour it on his head, and say, Thus saith the LORD, I have anointed thee king over Israel. Then open the door, and flee, and tarry not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa6b1e89-7fdf-4903-94e6-8406b83ebe20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: 2KI 9:4
Text: So the young man, even the young man the prophet, went to Ramothgilead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba843937-cf19-47cf-a2ee-b78c0983a4d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: 2KI 9:5
Text: And when he came, behold, the captains of the host were sitting; and he said, I have an errand to thee, O captain. And Jehu said, Unto which of all us? And he said, To thee, O captain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c823e1de-95d2-44e7-b4e1-63b0d240382b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: 2KI 9:6
Text: And he arose, and went into the house; and he poured the oil on his head, and said unto him, Thus saith the LORD God of Israel, I have anointed thee king over the people of the LORD, even over Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0dfb019-520c-437f-bb5d-1b68479e552d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: 2KI 9:7
Text: And thou shalt smite the house of Ahab thy master, that I may avenge the blood of my servants the prophets, and the blood of all the servants of the LORD, at the hand of Jezebel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f68fa2e8-2cbf-48e4-92ab-cec879d7fe72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 2KI 9:8
Text: For the whole house of Ahab shall perish: and I will cut off from Ahab him that pisseth against the wall, and him that is shut up and left in Israel:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:455bcf59-c91b-4e4d-ad56-8704db22cc69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: 2KI 9:9
Text: And I will make the house of Ahab like the house of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, and like the house of Baasha the son of Ahijah:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:362fd482-6db4-4e2a-a8a5-18a15569ffe7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 2KI 9:10
Text: And the dogs shall eat Jezebel in the portion of Jezreel, and there shall be none to bury her. And he opened the door, and fled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7785fc78-f4ce-4224-bdbe-95384e43516a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: 2KI 9:11
Text: Then Jehu came forth to the servants of his lord: and one said unto him, Is all well? wherefore came this mad fellow to thee? And he said unto them, Ye know the man, and his communication.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb4f769a-d758-4024-8eb6-90bfbb3cad7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: 2KI 9:12
Text: And they said, It is false; tell us now. And he said, Thus and thus spake he to me, saying, Thus saith the LORD, I have anointed thee king over Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86bbd103-35aa-472b-bdaf-853a2b13bf82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: 2KI 9:13
Text: Then they hasted, and took every man his garment, and put it under him on the top of the stairs, and blew with trumpets, saying, Jehu is king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5ddfcb2-3eab-4fed-96ea-9746be2e959b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: 2KI 9:14
Text: So Jehu the son of Jehoshaphat the son of Nimshi conspired against Joram. (Now Joram had kept Ramothgilead, he and all Israel, because of Hazael king of Syria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b5dd0e7-defe-469a-a037-7d1b25deb824>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 283

Reference: 2KI 9:15
Text: But king Joram was returned to be healed in Jezreel of the wounds which the Syrians had given him, when he fought with Hazael king of Syria.) And Jehu said, If it be your minds, then let none go forth nor escape out of the city to go to tell it in Jezreel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef296da9-551b-4b49-9245-b7f7fd43cc0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: 2KI 9:16
Text: So Jehu rode in a chariot, and went to Jezreel; for Joram lay there. And Ahaziah king of Judah was come down to see Joram.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52ec6afa-e047-4821-b864-43f7aff8ccf9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: 2KI 9:17
Text: And there stood a watchman on the tower in Jezreel, and he spied the company of Jehu as he came, and said, I see a company. And Joram said, Take an horseman, and send to meet them, and let him say, Is it peace?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebe69b0f-fbb0-4c6f-b43b-49a695d75561>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: 2KI 9:18
Text: So there went one on horseback to meet him, and said, Thus saith the king, Is it peace? And Jehu said, What hast thou to do with peace? turn thee behind me. And the watchman told, saying, The messenger came to them, but he cometh not again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4d77b0a-4650-4cf7-921b-8a308a5194eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: 2KI 9:19
Text: Then he sent out a second on horseback, which came to them, and said, Thus saith the king, Is it peace? And Jehu answered, What hast thou to do with peace? turn thee behind me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:037fb8a6-d7bc-476f-ae06-087455cdb0d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: 2KI 9:20
Text: And the watchman told, saying, He came even unto them, and cometh not again: and the driving is like the driving of Jehu the son of Nimshi; for he driveth furiously.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71712ed7-8e1e-496e-af33-d389816b0acb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: 2KI 9:21
Text: And Joram said, Make ready. And his chariot was made ready. And Joram king of Israel and Ahaziah king of Judah went out, each in his chariot, and they went out against Jehu, and met him in the portion of Naboth the Jezreelite.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46920ccf-9c1c-48f9-96f7-ca7aee7dee35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: 2KI 9:22
Text: And it came to pass, when Joram saw Jehu, that he said, Is it peace, Jehu? And he answered, What peace, so long as the whoredoms of thy mother Jezebel and her witchcrafts are so many?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9097d4bc-9e96-47e7-840f-467a6795fad0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: 2KI 9:23
Text: And Joram turned his hands, and fled, and said to Ahaziah, There is treachery, O Ahaziah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d87e37e5-487b-4a2d-ba7f-42df08cb24ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: 2KI 9:24
Text: And Jehu drew a bow with his full strength, and smote Jehoram between his arms, and the arrow went out at his heart, and he sunk down in his chariot.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04505b67-ba13-41b2-b4b4-2b4dbb784b38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: 2KI 9:25
Text: Then said Jehu to Bidkar his captain, Take up, and cast him in the portion of the field of Naboth the Jezreelite: for remember how that, when I and thou rode together after Ahab his father, the LORD laid this burden upon him;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9409ed77-872b-43e0-b633-4312730db058>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: 2KI 9:26
Text: Surely I have seen yesterday the blood of Naboth, and the blood of his sons, saith the LORD; and I will requite thee in this plat, saith the LORD. Now therefore take and cast him into the plat of ground, according to the word of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f783b030-9991-4320-a9e9-edf8de74f56a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 281

Reference: 2KI 9:27
Text: But when Ahaziah the king of Judah saw this, he fled by the way of the garden house. And Jehu followed after him, and said, Smite him also in the chariot. And they did so at the going up to Gur, which is by Ibleam. And he fled to Megiddo, and died there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cbf12d1-d31f-4c79-aec7-216b28e93842>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 2KI 9:28
Text: And his servants carried him in a chariot to Jerusalem, and buried him in his sepulchre with his fathers in the city of David.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aff7accd-79aa-4dde-a924-0c4f89196c49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: 2KI 9:29
Text: And in the eleventh year of Joram the son of Ahab began Ahaziah to reign over Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9a56981-cf1c-44fd-b553-ec70e744f3a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: 2KI 9:30
Text: And when Jehu was come to Jezreel, Jezebel heard of it; and she painted her face, and tired her head, and looked out at a window.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9173e9f-817d-4f28-8213-7398876ffee1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: 2KI 9:31
Text: And as Jehu entered in at the gate, she said, Had Zimri peace, who slew his master?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:715a3112-b361-4b48-b74f-8f67873a0997>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: 2KI 9:32
Text: And he lifted up his face to the window, and said, Who is on my side? who? And there looked out to him two or three eunuchs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:004c235b-ed27-4b8d-9aa8-e0fd5d6574c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: 2KI 9:33
Text: And he said, Throw her down. So they threw her down: and some of her blood was sprinkled on the wall, and on the horses: and he trode her under foot.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:490876e8-314c-4fb1-8232-e72399ea08bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 2KI 9:34
Text: And when he was come in, he did eat and drink, and said, Go, see now this cursed woman, and bury her: for she is a king’s daughter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5738a819-3620-4974-a4e3-91c5309a839c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 2KI 9:35
Text: And they went to bury her: but they found no more of her than the skull, and the feet, and the palms of her hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ab41869-555f-4799-bc5d-66127aa69017>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: 2KI 9:36
Text: Wherefore they came again, and told him. And he said, This is the word of the LORD, which he spake by his servant Elijah the Tishbite, saying, In the portion of Jezreel shall dogs eat the flesh of Jezebel:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/9/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b085da90-547c-42f6-b5be-52d6c970f410>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: 2KI 9:37
Text: And the carcase of Jezebel shall be as dung upon the face of the field in the portion of Jezreel; so that they shall not say, This is Jezebel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:526ef76b-0cdc-4e3e-93b6-38b29cd485bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: 2KI 10:1
Text: And Ahab had seventy sons in Samaria. And Jehu wrote letters, and sent to Samaria, unto the rulers of Jezreel, to the elders, and to them that brought up Ahab’s children, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d87af601-6ee1-4d4a-bd8a-470be60f4833>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: 2KI 10:2
Text: Now as soon as this letter cometh to you, seeing your master’s sons are with you, and there are with you chariots and horses, a fenced city also, and armour;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf379581-538e-4b2a-af54-4ea372d8fd89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 2KI 10:3
Text: Look even out the best and meetest of your master’s sons, and set him on his father’s throne, and fight for your master’s house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa5ac539-2196-4aea-b79a-4d1a6e853808>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 2KI 10:4
Text: But they were exceedingly afraid, and said, Behold, two kings stood not before him: how then shall we stand?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3b3e459-2e7a-4fc5-b8f8-26ea53f522d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 295

Reference: 2KI 10:5
Text: And he that was over the house, and he that was over the city, the elders also, and the bringers up of the children, sent to Jehu, saying, We are thy servants, and will do all that thou shalt bid us; we will not make any king: do thou that which is good in thine eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec6547e8-cead-4188-8ce0-3b37aa56989c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 342

Reference: 2KI 10:6
Text: Then he wrote a letter the second time to them, saying, If ye be mine, and if ye will hearken unto my voice, take ye the heads of the men your master’s sons, and come to me to Jezreel by to morrow this time. Now the king’s sons, being seventy persons, were with the great men of the city, which brought them up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48eea30d-57b6-495c-8113-3f06eb876176>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: 2KI 10:7
Text: And it came to pass, when the letter came to them, that they took the king’s sons, and slew seventy persons, and put their heads in baskets, and sent him them to Jezreel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f023cabd-f5dd-4863-8ef4-f6129c0494de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: 2KI 10:8
Text: And there came a messenger, and told him, saying, They have brought the heads of the king’s sons. And he said, Lay ye them in two heaps at the entering in of the gate until the morning.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:733bd419-a4e0-465d-9f9b-a512bfce3fca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: 2KI 10:9
Text: And it came to pass in the morning, that he went out, and stood, and said to all the people, Ye be righteous: behold, I conspired against my master, and slew him: but who slew all these?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbe1714d-3fb9-4aca-8c03-4c82af2cbb2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: 2KI 10:10
Text: Know now that there shall fall unto the earth nothing of the word of the LORD, which the LORD spake concerning the house of Ahab: for the LORD hath done that which he spake by his servant Elijah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5da681b9-5a8b-41be-a913-d36a3294186c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: 2KI 10:11
Text: So Jehu slew all that remained of the house of Ahab in Jezreel, and all his great men, and his kinsfolks, and his priests, until he left him none remaining.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:920a35f7-c3f1-4f28-97af-444a6df770eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 2KI 10:12
Text: And he arose and departed, and came to Samaria. And as he was at the shearing house in the way,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3f41f16-2ac6-4552-a4b7-91df645402b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: 2KI 10:13
Text: Jehu met with the brethren of Ahaziah king of Judah, and said, Who are ye? And they answered, We are the brethren of Ahaziah; and we go down to salute the children of the king and the children of the queen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:075905fa-b6a4-4342-bddf-c34666196d9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: 2KI 10:14
Text: And he said, Take them alive. And they took them alive, and slew them at the pit of the shearing house, even two and forty men; neither left he any of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a0b189b-6443-49e4-8be9-a704743039cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 343

Reference: 2KI 10:15
Text: And when he was departed thence, he lighted on Jehonadab the son of Rechab coming to meet him: and he saluted him, and said to him, Is thine heart right, as my heart is with thy heart? And Jehonadab answered, It is. If it be, give me thine hand. And he gave him his hand; and he took him up to him into the chariot.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bebee8bc-b715-4cc2-99f0-bfc78ce0c850>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: 2KI 10:16
Text: And he said, Come with me, and see my zeal for the LORD. So they made him ride in his chariot.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e42af757-a2ee-4810-9cc0-018999167d98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: 2KI 10:17
Text: And when he came to Samaria, he slew all that remained unto Ahab in Samaria, till he had destroyed him, according to the saying of the LORD, which he spake to Elijah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d2e2b8d-da5d-4721-92e4-5b0ec5d8c7e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 2KI 10:18
Text: And Jehu gathered all the people together, and said unto them, Ahab served Baal a little; but Jehu shall serve him much.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c7f9b0c-7cc4-484b-910c-de0fea2f535b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 321

Reference: 2KI 10:19
Text: Now therefore call unto me all the prophets of Baal, all his servants, and all his priests; let none be wanting: for I have a great sacrifice to do to Baal; whosoever shall be wanting, he shall not live. But Jehu did it in subtilty, to the intent that he might destroy the worshippers of Baal.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8cebe3e7-a5ce-4d5f-aebf-13833331212e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: 2KI 10:20
Text: And Jehu said, Proclaim a solemn assembly for Baal. And they proclaimed it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27a0fafc-2261-4b6a-8fe9-70bef3d9cfe5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: 2KI 10:21
Text: And Jehu sent through all Israel: and all the worshippers of Baal came, so that there was not a man left that came not. And they came into the house of Baal; and the house of Baal was full from one end to another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13333221-9d3a-47a8-a6df-50f730f35c22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: 2KI 10:22
Text: And he said unto him that was over the vestry, Bring forth vestments for all the worshippers of Baal. And he brought them forth vestments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:367337cd-32bd-461a-981f-b9c7b9d9c5a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: 2KI 10:23
Text: And Jehu went, and Jehonadab the son of Rechab, into the house of Baal, and said unto the worshippers of Baal, Search, and look that there be here with you none of the servants of the LORD, but the worshippers of Baal only.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fda994ac-9442-4ec0-a5d2-35e9f8bf6893>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: 2KI 10:24
Text: And when they went in to offer sacrifices and burnt offerings, Jehu appointed fourscore men without, and said, If any of the men whom I have brought into your hands escape, he that letteth him go, his life shall be for the life of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5be7638b-29e4-43ac-8581-fb3416900763>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 339

Reference: 2KI 10:25
Text: And it came to pass, as soon as he had made an end of offering the burnt offering, that Jehu said to the guard and to the captains, Go in, and slay them; let none come forth. And they smote them with the edge of the sword; and the guard and the captains cast them out, and went to the city of the house of Baal.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2384321-65eb-48de-b4f1-902e55971664>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: 2KI 10:26
Text: And they brought forth the images out of the house of Baal, and burned them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:898faa61-6f1d-49a9-ba5d-42d246be76a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: 2KI 10:27
Text: And they brake down the image of Baal, and brake down the house of Baal, and made it a draught house unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7964fe7-9f0f-4aab-8f93-814999a5afdb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 67

Reference: 2KI 10:28
Text: Thus Jehu destroyed Baal out of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b15d946f-50e5-456b-9ecc-2b13f8530c20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: 2KI 10:29
Text: Howbeit from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who made Israel to sin, Jehu departed not from after them, to wit, the golden calves that were in Bethel, and that were in Dan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f93e55b7-a278-421e-bc9e-6bd3f08359f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 282

Reference: 2KI 10:30
Text: And the LORD said unto Jehu, Because thou hast done well in executing that which is right in mine eyes, and hast done unto the house of Ahab according to all that was in mine heart, thy children of the fourth generation shall sit on the throne of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86603b25-b2ad-4ed7-8d7e-d473566d7066>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 2KI 10:31
Text: But Jehu took no heed to walk in the law of the LORD God of Israel with all his heart: for he departed not from the sins of Jeroboam, which made Israel to sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e03cd98-e787-40bf-8606-fd6463a610c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 2KI 10:32
Text: In those days the LORD began to cut Israel short: and Hazael smote them in all the coasts of Israel;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1848a397-4037-4327-b1bb-b3d54052c41e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: 2KI 10:33
Text: From Jordan eastward, all the land of Gilead, the Gadites, and the Reubenites, and the Manassites, from Aroer, which is by the river Arnon, even Gilead and Bashan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8531d88-3435-4526-8095-f49e0cb5435e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: 2KI 10:34
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Jehu, and all that he did, and all his might, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41dfbf14-cb5c-4c00-bbf4-4a9ee99188fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 2KI 10:35
Text: And Jehu slept with his fathers: and they buried him in Samaria. And Jehoahaz his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/10/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:014dd139-402a-41df-a453-f60d469409aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: 2KI 10:36
Text: And the time that Jehu reigned over Israel in Samaria was twenty and eight years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/11/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f19b13a0-923b-410d-8a08-28266e53e668>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 2KI 11:1
Text: And when Athaliah the mother of Ahaziah saw that her son was dead, she arose and destroyed all the seed royal.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/11/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a0e3b38-0fb0-44d4-9235-3fe1fdc357b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 281

Reference: 2KI 11:2
Text: But Jehosheba, the daughter of king Joram, sister of Ahaziah, took Joash the son of Ahaziah, and stole him from among the king’s sons which were slain; and they hid him, even him and his nurse, in the bedchamber from Athaliah, so that he was not slain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/11/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5158d7de-c32b-4244-a6db-aa4d0a181408>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: 2KI 11:3
Text: And he was with her hid in the house of the LORD six years. And Athaliah did reign over the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/11/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93384f74-507b-4d93-b504-5e2acf6738a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 300

Reference: 2KI 11:4
Text: And the seventh year Jehoiada sent and fetched the rulers over hundreds, with the captains and the guard, and brought them to him into the house of the LORD, and made a covenant with them, and took an oath of them in the house of the LORD, and shewed them the king’s son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/11/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7586e79-2488-4b0a-be67-9d4b329c7848>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 2KI 11:5
Text: And he commanded them, saying, This is the thing that ye shall do; A third part of you that enter in on the sabbath shall even be keepers of the watch of the king’s house;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/11/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f0cf53a-5190-4a79-a8ef-75e24038dc3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 2KI 11:6
Text: And a third part shall be at the gate of Sur; and a third part at the gate behind the guard: so shall ye keep the watch of the house, that it be not broken down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/11/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b738ff8-5f03-4cb2-8e77-d5a201baadf4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 2KI 11:7
Text: And two parts of all you that go forth on the sabbath, even they shall keep the watch of the house of the LORD about the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/11/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e380524b-e00f-427d-a619-380b28769128>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: 2KI 11:8
Text: And ye shall compass the king round about, every man with his weapons in his hand: and he that cometh within the ranges, let him be slain: and be ye with the king as he goeth out and as he cometh in.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/11/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7733d6a-988a-4c07-b8db-f67d6539d8f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: 2KI 11:9
Text: And the captains over the hundreds did according to all things that Jehoiada the priest commanded: and they took every man his men that were to come in on the sabbath, with them that should go out on the sabbath, and came to Jehoiada the priest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/11/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4229553-6756-43c1-9def-7e6c37c38b2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 2KI 11:10
Text: And to the captains over hundreds did the priest give king David’s spears and shields, that were in the temple of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/11/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c0d15b1-7cc5-4b11-9460-5aa69db7b385>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: 2KI 11:11
Text: And the guard stood, every man with his weapons in his hand, round about the king, from the right corner of the temple to the left corner of the temple, along by the altar and the temple.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/11/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec98deca-eb99-49d5-a54e-3daff7476fd1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: 2KI 11:12
Text: And he brought forth the king’s son, and put the crown upon him, and gave him the testimony; and they made him king, and anointed him; and they clapped their hands, and said, God save the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/11/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c6f9c95-0c4f-4ecf-bfad-ede21109a6f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 2KI 11:13
Text: And when Athaliah heard the noise of the guard and of the people, she came to the people into the temple of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/11/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:beb2b7ba-f2f1-462f-89a8-74f302bb6923>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: 2KI 11:14
Text: And when she looked, behold, the king stood by a pillar, as the manner was, and the princes and the trumpeters by the king, and all the people of the land rejoiced, and blew with trumpets: and Athaliah rent her clothes, and cried, Treason, Treason.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/11/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40a4bbc6-6ff6-4694-90cb-b1638883e37a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 292

Reference: 2KI 11:15
Text: But Jehoiada the priest commanded the captains of the hundreds, the officers of the host, and said unto them, Have her forth without the ranges: and him that followeth her kill with the sword. For the priest had said, Let her not be slain in the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/11/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54570133-5d13-4d70-9432-a5d986e0a6c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 2KI 11:16
Text: And they laid hands on her; and she went by the way by the which the horses came into the king’s house: and there was she slain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/11/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8bdece2c-5c3e-4ad1-8f70-cc495b3bc606>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: 2KI 11:17
Text: And Jehoiada made a covenant between the LORD and the king and the people, that they should be the LORD’s people; between the king also and the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/11/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f47c14d3-dfa9-4488-8575-2658b4bbc2c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 281

Reference: 2KI 11:18
Text: And all the people of the land went into the house of Baal, and brake it down; his altars and his images brake they in pieces thoroughly, and slew Mattan the priest of Baal before the altars. And the priest appointed officers over the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/11/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7bf195ce-6e47-4921-baf8-268d4e2d0bde>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 296

Reference: 2KI 11:19
Text: And he took the rulers over hundreds, and the captains, and the guard, and all the people of the land; and they brought down the king from the house of the LORD, and came by the way of the gate of the guard to the king’s house. And he sat on the throne of the kings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/11/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3465b0f-d01a-4d39-aaa7-f1d2401c93bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 2KI 11:20
Text: And all the people of the land rejoiced, and the city was in quiet: and they slew Athaliah with the sword beside the king’s house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/11/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47ff11ee-61a1-4fa2-ac05-efa83627b767>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: 2KI 11:21
Text: Seven years old was Jehoash when he began to reign.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/12/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a636db4-153d-41f9-948e-4c7d5452f2d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: 2KI 12:1
Text: In the seventh year of Jehu Jehoash began to reign; and forty years reigned he in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Zibiah of Beersheba.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/12/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a16e228a-a1d5-4c6c-aae4-8387d621d36f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 2KI 12:2
Text: And Jehoash did that which was right in the sight of the LORD all his days wherein Jehoiada the priest instructed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/12/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2d6ee20-d72f-4e9d-a421-58d5cbae06b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: 2KI 12:3
Text: But the high places were not taken away: the people still sacrificed and burnt incense in the high places.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/12/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a235d3d-96e4-49c7-ad1b-297ece417de2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 321

Reference: 2KI 12:4
Text: And Jehoash said to the priests, All the money of the dedicated things that is brought into the house of the LORD, even the money of every one that passeth the account, the money that every man is set at, and all the money that cometh into any man’s heart to bring into the house of the LORD,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/12/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a2b799e-035e-43d9-bf42-208fe2edb12f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: 2KI 12:5
Text: Let the priests take it to them, every man of his acquaintance: and let them repair the breaches of the house, wheresoever any breach shall be found.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/12/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad4625de-45de-41f1-ba6a-73bb722e78b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: 2KI 12:6
Text: But it was so, that in the three and twentieth year of king Jehoash the priests had not repaired the breaches of the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/12/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a1c37e4-c5bb-4ae4-b323-da3941d2db14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: 2KI 12:7
Text: Then king Jehoash called for Jehoiada the priest, and the other priests, and said unto them, Why repair ye not the breaches of the house? now therefore receive no more money of your acquaintance, but deliver it for the breaches of the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/12/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72825d11-b13b-42ea-ba26-fc7b085d7738>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 2KI 12:8
Text: And the priests consented to receive no more money of the people, neither to repair the breaches of the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/12/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0746a220-dc4f-4480-996e-30ca86eed231>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 294

Reference: 2KI 12:9
Text: But Jehoiada the priest took a chest, and bored a hole in the lid of it, and set it beside the altar, on the right side as one cometh into the house of the LORD: and the priests that kept the door put therein all the money that was brought into the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/12/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09f504fb-c19f-4a75-9d18-97793abc675e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: 2KI 12:10
Text: And it was so, when they saw that there was much money in the chest, that the king’s scribe and the high priest came up, and they put up in bags, and told the money that was found in the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/12/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:521ba78a-9344-4c72-b2fa-4055ba83575f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: 2KI 12:11
Text: And they gave the money, being told, into the hands of them that did the work, that had the oversight of the house of the LORD: and they laid it out to the carpenters and builders, that wrought upon the house of the LORD,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/12/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c6b02e2-8cce-44e8-a451-8245e991d3bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: 2KI 12:12
Text: And to masons, and hewers of stone, and to buy timber and hewed stone to repair the breaches of the house of the LORD, and for all that was laid out for the house to repair it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/12/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62189efc-8305-4892-b069-37a1d933e607>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: 2KI 12:13
Text: Howbeit there were not made for the house of the LORD bowls of silver, snuffers, basons, trumpets, any vessels of gold, or vessels of silver, of the money that was brought into the house of the LORD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/12/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49013095-556a-4019-a432-926657ff5c6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: 2KI 12:14
Text: But they gave that to the workmen, and repaired therewith the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/12/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4669bc19-8751-40e4-9613-7b5bf8249cc9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: 2KI 12:15
Text: Moreover they reckoned not with the men, into whose hand they delivered the money to be bestowed on workmen: for they dealt faithfully.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/12/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:166436e8-7bf2-4884-b312-ff966137e956>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 2KI 12:16
Text: The trespass money and sin money was not brought into the house of the LORD: it was the priests’.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/12/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4210f4d8-b1bc-45c9-99ad-a1d203a38391>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 2KI 12:17
Text: Then Hazael king of Syria went up, and fought against Gath, and took it: and Hazael set his face to go up to Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/12/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a908cbb6-e184-4489-ac86-3250ec59fe2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 371

Reference: 2KI 12:18
Text: And Jehoash king of Judah took all the hallowed things that Jehoshaphat, and Jehoram, and Ahaziah, his fathers, kings of Judah, had dedicated, and his own hallowed things, and all the gold that was found in the treasures of the house of the LORD, and in the king’s house, and sent it to Hazael king of Syria: and he went away from Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/12/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8099fdf3-ce2d-42df-8aa1-51f9a7ce3d8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 2KI 12:19
Text: And the rest of the acts of Joash, and all that he did, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/12/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:183d7fdc-d347-4c3d-848d-933808add787>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: 2KI 12:20
Text: And his servants arose, and made a conspiracy, and slew Joash in the house of Millo, which goeth down to Silla.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/12/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7823c045-3d47-4733-9d25-e876734a4392>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: 2KI 12:21
Text: For Jozachar the son of Shimeath, and Jehozabad the son of Shomer, his servants, smote him, and he died; and they buried him with his fathers in the city of David: and Amaziah his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13405848-f213-4141-8fe2-cd2fe982e4cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: 2KI 13:1
Text: In the three and twentieth year of Joash the son of Ahaziah king of Judah Jehoahaz the son of Jehu began to reign over Israel in Samaria, and reigned seventeen years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba8e2de8-7f2e-463c-ae95-0bfed8c03a48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 2KI 13:2
Text: And he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD, and followed the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, which made Israel to sin; he departed not therefrom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b11cb9bc-01cf-4bd7-9132-50e17d92beb7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: 2KI 13:3
Text: And the anger of the LORD was kindled against Israel, and he delivered them into the hand of Hazael king of Syria, and into the hand of Benhadad the son of Hazael, all their days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca009da5-231b-446f-9e43-75c4472f994d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 2KI 13:4
Text: And Jehoahaz besought the LORD, and the LORD hearkened unto him: for he saw the oppression of Israel, because the king of Syria oppressed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12ddbc8c-77fa-4bc7-8af6-a2877ab20a74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 2KI 13:5
Text: (And the LORD gave Israel a saviour, so that they went out from under the hand of the Syrians: and the children of Israel dwelt in their tents, as beforetime.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da6da725-eca9-4914-9438-c8b7c7bfef35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 2KI 13:6
Text: Nevertheless they departed not from the sins of the house of Jeroboam, who made Israel sin, but walked therein: and there remained the grove also in Samaria.)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eed807df-e317-4d95-b50b-fe4cba6f428e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: 2KI 13:7
Text: Neither did he leave of the people to Jehoahaz but fifty horsemen, and ten chariots, and ten thousand footmen; for the king of Syria had destroyed them, and had made them like the dust by threshing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9797ec2f-1496-4e00-8bae-cd3c80809552>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 2KI 13:8
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Jehoahaz, and all that he did, and his might, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59860faa-07a1-49d6-bfc3-425062287efc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 2KI 13:9
Text: And Jehoahaz slept with his fathers; and they buried him in Samaria: and Joash his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0102a630-9e5e-4944-9d09-d44a112128c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 2KI 13:10
Text: In the thirty and seventh year of Joash king of Judah began Jehoash the son of Jehoahaz to reign over Israel in Samaria, and reigned sixteen years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53c4c61c-729a-4b14-9c9a-f048bd8035f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: 2KI 13:11
Text: And he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD; he departed not from all the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who made Israel sin: but he walked therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:143b02d1-ae45-4e71-b0c4-329892ac0e99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: 2KI 13:12
Text: And the rest of the acts of Joash, and all that he did, and his might wherewith he fought against Amaziah king of Judah, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76a30846-6e8e-4409-9f7d-5f59f2e0784a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 2KI 13:13
Text: And Joash slept with his fathers; and Jeroboam sat upon his throne: and Joash was buried in Samaria with the kings of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:babf1d67-ae5d-41f1-aa6c-4f803101dbd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: 2KI 13:14
Text: Now Elisha was fallen sick of his sickness whereof he died. And Joash the king of Israel came down unto him, and wept over his face, and said, O my father, my father, the chariot of Israel, and the horsemen thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0747c6a8-cb9b-490f-a41b-70396170dc46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: 2KI 13:15
Text: And Elisha said unto him, Take bow and arrows. And he took unto him bow and arrows.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16ae8285-1b0a-4f85-9c2a-22340ee0e0b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 2KI 13:16
Text: And he said to the king of Israel, Put thine hand upon the bow. And he put his hand upon it: and Elisha put his hands upon the king’s hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acd867b8-dbcc-4a08-95be-453fe59ec062>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 288

Reference: 2KI 13:17
Text: And he said, Open the window eastward. And he opened it. Then Elisha said, Shoot. And he shot. And he said, The arrow of the LORD’s deliverance, and the arrow of deliverance from Syria: for thou shalt smite the Syrians in Aphek, till thou have consumed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33264976-a82b-440e-ace8-34acf0b706dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: 2KI 13:18
Text: And he said, Take the arrows. And he took them. And he said unto the king of Israel, Smite upon the ground. And he smote thrice, and stayed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ecb551f7-5b81-43fb-98fe-bfabe8c3a9dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: 2KI 13:19
Text: And the man of God was wroth with him, and said, Thou shouldest have smitten five or six times; then hadst thou smitten Syria till thou hadst consumed it: whereas now thou shalt smite Syria but thrice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00e7d739-92f3-45be-b8f0-361d38b4e252>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: 2KI 13:20
Text: And Elisha died, and they buried him. And the bands of the Moabites invaded the land at the coming in of the year.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42fb982c-719b-4b88-8b77-57ffa0b4d148>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: 2KI 13:21
Text: And it came to pass, as they were burying a man, that, behold, they spied a band of men; and they cast the man into the sepulchre of Elisha: and when the man was let down, and touched the bones of Elisha, he revived, and stood up on his feet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49408707-d5a1-4eb5-8c7e-73b86990d53e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: 2KI 13:22
Text: But Hazael king of Syria oppressed Israel all the days of Jehoahaz.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f602dd95-0e83-46f3-96f5-7fe9474473b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: 2KI 13:23
Text: And the LORD was gracious unto them, and had compassion on them, and had respect unto them, because of his covenant with Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, and would not destroy them, neither cast he them from his presence as yet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ecda812-e5c0-4d2a-b286-c29bc0ff8b4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: 2KI 13:24
Text: So Hazael king of Syria died; and Benhadad his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/13/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ebec05e-1e1e-4543-85c3-d39f46a617ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 262

Reference: 2KI 13:25
Text: And Jehoash the son of Jehoahaz took again out of the hand of Benhadad the son of Hazael the cities, which he had taken out of the hand of Jehoahaz his father by war. Three times did Joash beat him, and recovered the cities of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9430f1d3-10c3-4024-a7fd-406671e486bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: 2KI 14:1
Text: In the second year of Joash son of Jehoahaz king of Israel reigned Amaziah the son of Joash king of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a94b686-2e97-4221-9339-5be17e9bb9e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: 2KI 14:2
Text: He was twenty and five years old when he began to reign, and reigned twenty and nine years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Jehoaddan of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d19e207b-fb38-4218-9cf1-4d98776c455c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: 2KI 14:3
Text: And he did that which was right in the sight of the LORD, yet not like David his father: he did according to all things as Joash his father did.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:436b07f9-ba52-48bb-add0-bbab8f8adb2b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 2KI 14:4
Text: Howbeit the high places were not taken away: as yet the people did sacrifice and burnt incense on the high places.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e085c275-16ad-4fd1-8150-b86575fb521f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 2KI 14:5
Text: And it came to pass, as soon as the kingdom was confirmed in his hand, that he slew his servants which had slain the king his father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bcda535-9fc1-4a32-835e-90607394b495>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 338

Reference: 2KI 14:6
Text: But the children of the murderers he slew not: according unto that which is written in the book of the law of Moses, wherein the LORD commanded, saying, The fathers shall not be put to death for the children, nor the children be put to death for the fathers; but every man shall be put to death for his own sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f81004f1-2867-494b-8c6b-e9eb83841ada>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: 2KI 14:7
Text: He slew of Edom in the valley of salt ten thousand, and took Selah by war, and called the name of it Joktheel unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11329c45-640c-4820-a7c0-9311e7cd7dcf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 2KI 14:8
Text: Then Amaziah sent messengers to Jehoash, the son of Jehoahaz son of Jehu, king of Israel, saying, Come, let us look one another in the face.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff491d0e-ec5a-4880-b4b8-e15903b89845>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 294

Reference: 2KI 14:9
Text: And Jehoash the king of Israel sent to Amaziah king of Judah, saying, The thistle that was in Lebanon sent to the cedar that was in Lebanon, saying, Give thy daughter to my son to wife: and there passed by a wild beast that was in Lebanon, and trode down the thistle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b946854d-c2dd-4180-ab02-3f3cd54df993>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: 2KI 14:10
Text: Thou hast indeed smitten Edom, and thine heart hath lifted thee up: glory of this, and tarry at home: for why shouldest thou meddle to thy hurt, that thou shouldest fall, even thou, and Judah with thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff947df4-ba85-4aaf-8698-a381eec69be9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: 2KI 14:11
Text: But Amaziah would not hear. Therefore Jehoash king of Israel went up; and he and Amaziah king of Judah looked one another in the face at Bethshemesh, which belongeth to Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8fb9966-8e95-410b-a1d2-4c7ef65e271c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: 2KI 14:12
Text: And Judah was put to the worse before Israel; and they fled every man to their tents.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6190d0f1-8e98-4537-96fc-b513cdea37d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: 2KI 14:13
Text: And Jehoash king of Israel took Amaziah king of Judah, the son of Jehoash the son of Ahaziah, at Bethshemesh, and came to Jerusalem, and brake down the wall of Jerusalem from the gate of Ephraim unto the corner gate, four hundred cubits.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:986dddc0-57df-46e0-ae16-71104a0dad3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: 2KI 14:14
Text: And he took all the gold and silver, and all the vessels that were found in the house of the LORD, and in the treasures of the king’s house, and hostages, and returned to Samaria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:421520e7-54f3-410f-b75d-b1294ed77292>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: 2KI 14:15
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Jehoash which he did, and his might, and how he fought with Amaziah king of Judah, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32876f17-323a-485a-9666-4b288a153af1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 2KI 14:16
Text: And Jehoash slept with his fathers, and was buried in Samaria with the kings of Israel; and Jeroboam his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:186a8a35-def4-4a1b-b9f5-943632f1598b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: 2KI 14:17
Text: And Amaziah the son of Joash king of Judah lived after the death of Jehoash son of Jehoahaz king of Israel fifteen years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7eb2c146-b736-43fb-94df-bcfb3ed83e0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: 2KI 14:18
Text: And the rest of the acts of Amaziah, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9b42531-83ef-4b6b-a8b0-58d86e8ef16a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 2KI 14:19
Text: Now they made a conspiracy against him in Jerusalem: and he fled to Lachish; but they sent after him to Lachish, and slew him there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc8dc567-ba56-45f9-a51a-404ac4c18dc0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: 2KI 14:20
Text: And they brought him on horses: and he was buried at Jerusalem with his fathers in the city of David.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bcf536ce-6125-4d78-8fec-6fdab4cee427>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 2KI 14:21
Text: And all the people of Judah took Azariah, which was sixteen years old, and made him king instead of his father Amaziah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6359af0-94cd-43f4-8ed4-29d4c9706bef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: 2KI 14:22
Text: He built Elath, and restored it to Judah, after that the king slept with his fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6aa6eff-87fb-4203-9699-6eb7ab860de3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: 2KI 14:23
Text: In the fifteenth year of Amaziah the son of Joash king of Judah Jeroboam the son of Joash king of Israel began to reign in Samaria, and reigned forty and one years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03e1c06c-4849-47b8-8162-38479d1ea223>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: 2KI 14:24
Text: And he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD: he departed not from all the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who made Israel to sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1461bed-9718-4952-ba36-cd6ff11fdf52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: 2KI 14:25
Text: He restored the coast of Israel from the entering of Hamath unto the sea of the plain, according to the word of the LORD God of Israel, which he spake by the hand of his servant Jonah, the son of Amittai, the prophet, which was of Gathhepher.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04e7f668-7ba6-4ded-ba20-1241942e492f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 2KI 14:26
Text: For the LORD saw the affliction of Israel, that it was very bitter: for there was not any shut up, nor any left, nor any helper for Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3411cee6-8b84-4fe8-b563-46f166d808f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 2KI 14:27
Text: And the LORD said not that he would blot out the name of Israel from under heaven: but he saved them by the hand of Jeroboam the son of Joash.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5293c93-23f4-4d53-a3fb-aff50a9f844f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: 2KI 14:28
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Jeroboam, and all that he did, and his might, how he warred, and how he recovered Damascus, and Hamath, which belonged to Judah, for Israel, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/14/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0dbb2b0-d288-4512-a65f-03abc2044d7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: 2KI 14:29
Text: And Jeroboam slept with his fathers, even with the kings of Israel; and Zachariah his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bdd1e32-ab0b-498c-8e67-6b8a32c620ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 2KI 15:1
Text: In the twenty and seventh year of Jeroboam king of Israel began Azariah son of Amaziah king of Judah to reign.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d18bc27a-da25-4a03-9b18-032c8074e074>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: 2KI 15:2
Text: Sixteen years old was he when he began to reign, and he reigned two and fifty years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Jecholiah of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08d9a45f-3d49-4291-8b61-faffce4aea23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 2KI 15:3
Text: And he did that which was right in the sight of the LORD, according to all that his father Amaziah had done;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e7a2e8d-c9f1-4beb-b759-aaf03ffaeea7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: 2KI 15:4
Text: Save that the high places were not removed: the people sacrificed and burnt incense still on the high places.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f3c6030-074c-4beb-8329-ba163da930b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: 2KI 15:5
Text: And the LORD smote the king, so that he was a leper unto the day of his death, and dwelt in a several house. And Jotham the king’s son was over the house, judging the people of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb942c64-2856-4d75-9f10-6476871ebfa5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 2KI 15:6
Text: And the rest of the acts of Azariah, and all that he did, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:726fe90e-0f6d-4b77-96be-cc9128fcea87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 2KI 15:7
Text: So Azariah slept with his fathers; and they buried him with his fathers in the city of David: and Jotham his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce395de9-66a9-421b-b0c7-579a9a8e8f2d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: 2KI 15:8
Text: In the thirty and eighth year of Azariah king of Judah did Zachariah the son of Jeroboam reign over Israel in Samaria six months.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b00ff132-d670-4725-852c-5a53a3528457>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: 2KI 15:9
Text: And he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD, as his fathers had done: he departed not from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who made Israel to sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:571e39cc-52cc-438f-902a-5e592db924ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 2KI 15:10
Text: And Shallum the son of Jabesh conspired against him, and smote him before the people, and slew him, and reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:933c6c53-d89e-4caa-82e4-798797a496be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 2KI 15:11
Text: And the rest of the acts of Zachariah, behold, they are written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d14a3219-25a5-4b53-a16d-f0f1d9efe8fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: 2KI 15:12
Text: This was the word of the LORD which he spake unto Jehu, saying, Thy sons shall sit on the throne of Israel unto the fourth generation. And so it came to pass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3494db54-f757-4b64-82c4-c21471227fe9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: 2KI 15:13
Text: Shallum the son of Jabesh began to reign in the nine and thirtieth year of Uzziah king of Judah; and he reigned a full month in Samaria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:919aa01c-0b2e-4f8b-b1bf-b7bcb20c11cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 2KI 15:14
Text: For Menahem the son of Gadi went up from Tirzah, and came to Samaria, and smote Shallum the son of Jabesh in Samaria, and slew him, and reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ac51de3-5495-4336-bb1c-b27d26610169>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 2KI 15:15
Text: And the rest of the acts of Shallum, and his conspiracy which he made, behold, they are written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ccef3a56-43a3-432d-9158-002ea95f881a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: 2KI 15:16
Text: Then Menahem smote Tiphsah, and all that were therein, and the coasts thereof from Tirzah: because they opened not to him, therefore he smote it; and all the women therein that were with child he ripped up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26183b9c-1876-4793-8827-1afcee6adf1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: 2KI 15:17
Text: In the nine and thirtieth year of Azariah king of Judah began Menahem the son of Gadi to reign over Israel, and reigned ten years in Samaria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fff510f4-9856-4910-a887-61ad9481e3ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: 2KI 15:18
Text: And he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD: he departed not all his days from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who made Israel to sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f36d734-c67d-4991-81d2-b9d97fbb215c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: 2KI 15:19
Text: And Pul the king of Assyria came against the land: and Menahem gave Pul a thousand talents of silver, that his hand might be with him to confirm the kingdom in his hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:147b7fd6-1294-4e27-85b0-b6c300bc9a65>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: 2KI 15:20
Text: And Menahem exacted the money of Israel, even of all the mighty men of wealth, of each man fifty shekels of silver, to give to the king of Assyria. So the king of Assyria turned back, and stayed not there in the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb9d9ab7-3dcf-46bb-a3b9-a5ff00329b00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 2KI 15:21
Text: And the rest of the acts of Menahem, and all that he did, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b74d0cc0-3f87-484e-847a-d5b872988ff8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: 2KI 15:22
Text: And Menahem slept with his fathers; and Pekahiah his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5856c2fd-089a-418f-8b79-a1ea775f8f88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: 2KI 15:23
Text: In the fiftieth year of Azariah king of Judah Pekahiah the son of Menahem began to reign over Israel in Samaria, and reigned two years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:731858a4-efb7-4f80-923e-84f3e9c4f039>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: 2KI 15:24
Text: And he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD: he departed not from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who made Israel to sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d757768c-4f60-4e7a-aac5-35b60efa9c8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: 2KI 15:25
Text: But Pekah the son of Remaliah, a captain of his, conspired against him, and smote him in Samaria, in the palace of the king’s house, with Argob and Arieh, and with him fifty men of the Gileadites: and he killed him, and reigned in his room.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7949648a-ec4e-4b9a-a8b1-4c487e6812f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: 2KI 15:26
Text: And the rest of the acts of Pekahiah, and all that he did, behold, they are written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:403f8827-8fa4-4012-9812-b8b5b0aae117>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: 2KI 15:27
Text: In the two and fiftieth year of Azariah king of Judah Pekah the son of Remaliah began to reign over Israel in Samaria, and reigned twenty years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d854a3ba-e0ab-4773-ad09-247881c60d5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: 2KI 15:28
Text: And he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD: he departed not from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who made Israel to sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2965c77f-9ed1-492c-b99d-c0d545b8063a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: 2KI 15:29
Text: In the days of Pekah king of Israel came Tiglathpileser king of Assyria, and took Ijon, and Abelbethmaachah, and Janoah, and Kedesh, and Hazor, and Gilead, and Galilee, all the land of Naphtali, and carried them captive to Assyria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d46907b-f79d-4a7f-b5a2-8279d96f6cde>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: 2KI 15:30
Text: And Hoshea the son of Elah made a conspiracy against Pekah the son of Remaliah, and smote him, and slew him, and reigned in his stead, in the twentieth year of Jotham the son of Uzziah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb9806ba-f622-410f-846d-d4c50f99be57>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 2KI 15:31
Text: And the rest of the acts of Pekah, and all that he did, behold, they are written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c49533ed-e0a9-4191-83b3-558cb6f62df3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 2KI 15:32
Text: In the second year of Pekah the son of Remaliah king of Israel began Jotham the son of Uzziah king of Judah to reign.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa259121-8990-4105-932c-6768a7977203>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 2KI 15:33
Text: Five and twenty years old was he when he began to reign, and he reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Jerusha, the daughter of Zadok.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be3a8f75-d5ed-479e-b5c4-45afee31fbe7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: 2KI 15:34
Text: And he did that which was right in the sight of the LORD: he did according to all that his father Uzziah had done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc200989-2388-4951-8897-7aae813781cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 2KI 15:35
Text: Howbeit the high places were not removed: the people sacrificed and burned incense still in the high places. He built the higher gate of the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09eb1ee6-bdd1-4386-8834-074a95a8598b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 2KI 15:36
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Jotham, and all that he did, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fef2ef66-0d3c-404e-ba7d-31d051b611e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: 2KI 15:37
Text: In those days the LORD began to send against Judah Rezin the king of Syria, and Pekah the son of Remaliah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/15/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:535ea943-b96a-4ebc-a7fb-8e65bf9ee36a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: 2KI 15:38
Text: And Jotham slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in the city of David his father: and Ahaz his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/16/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f133c1fe-89ea-4f71-bab2-2f38c925c6be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 2KI 16:1
Text: In the seventeenth year of Pekah the son of Remaliah Ahaz the son of Jotham king of Judah began to reign.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/16/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb0e1d3e-5fd8-4ccb-849e-53f9aac01079>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: 2KI 16:2
Text: Twenty years old was Ahaz when he began to reign, and reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem, and did not that which was right in the sight of the LORD his God, like David his father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/16/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bcb20a0-2575-4fe0-8de5-64a4a8737a85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: 2KI 16:3
Text: But he walked in the way of the kings of Israel, yea, and made his son to pass through the fire, according to the abominations of the heathen, whom the LORD cast out from before the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/16/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6f539c0-ed64-44b4-97c9-592dc45df2c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 2KI 16:4
Text: And he sacrificed and burnt incense in the high places, and on the hills, and under every green tree.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/16/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3f94985-9784-403e-9c73-4fce73739144>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 2KI 16:5
Text: Then Rezin king of Syria and Pekah son of Remaliah king of Israel came up to Jerusalem to war: and they besieged Ahaz, but could not overcome him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/16/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df3c4f66-5741-40c8-a04b-4361402829e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: 2KI 16:6
Text: At that time Rezin king of Syria recovered Elath to Syria, and drave the Jews from Elath: and the Syrians came to Elath, and dwelt there unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/16/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:415b34b0-fd25-4a72-b302-e9d8635babbf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: 2KI 16:7
Text: So Ahaz sent messengers to Tiglathpileser king of Assyria, saying, I am thy servant and thy son: come up, and save me out of the hand of the king of Syria, and out of the hand of the king of Israel, which rise up against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/16/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:205c66ca-7e74-4f4e-8e5d-0ba6e3cf0d8e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: 2KI 16:8
Text: And Ahaz took the silver and gold that was found in the house of the LORD, and in the treasures of the king’s house, and sent it for a present to the king of Assyria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/16/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2fbb866-f46d-4cc3-9a79-a7e234cd448f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: 2KI 16:9
Text: And the king of Assyria hearkened unto him: for the king of Assyria went up against Damascus, and took it, and carried the people of it captive to Kir, and slew Rezin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/16/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b219c7a1-41a8-4afd-b065-b81bbbe4bf4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: 2KI 16:10
Text: And king Ahaz went to Damascus to meet Tiglathpileser king of Assyria, and saw an altar that was at Damascus: and king Ahaz sent to Urijah the priest the fashion of the altar, and the pattern of it, according to all the workmanship thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/16/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef5426f8-5115-4ccf-83b8-4e6bac5b7d97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 2KI 16:11
Text: And Urijah the priest built an altar according to all that king Ahaz had sent from Damascus: so Urijah the priest made it against king Ahaz came from Damascus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/16/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a597e812-ffa6-460f-894b-de09b9b9a742>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: 2KI 16:12
Text: And when the king was come from Damascus, the king saw the altar: and the king approached to the altar, and offered thereon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/16/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66ffa99c-1f4d-4cce-970e-9bfead1a3833>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 2KI 16:13
Text: And he burnt his burnt offering and his meat offering, and poured his drink offering, and sprinkled the blood of his peace offerings, upon the altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/16/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb328660-639a-41a9-83df-4ee7fa6403d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: 2KI 16:14
Text: And he brought also the brasen altar, which was before the LORD, from the forefront of the house, from between the altar and the house of the LORD, and put it on the north side of the altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/16/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2aff105-4104-4196-88a5-33dd6a74e048>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 473

Reference: 2KI 16:15
Text: And king Ahaz commanded Urijah the priest, saying, Upon the great altar burn the morning burnt offering, and the evening meat offering, and the king’s burnt sacrifice, and his meat offering, with the burnt offering of all the people of the land, and their meat offering, and their drink offerings; and sprinkle upon it all the blood of the burnt offering, and all the blood of the sacrifice: and the brasen altar shall be for me to enquire by.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/16/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c87dd4c-f1dd-4248-a4e2-012037962ea6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: 2KI 16:16
Text: Thus did Urijah the priest, according to all that king Ahaz commanded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/16/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbe6521f-2519-495f-954d-49657381359f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: 2KI 16:17
Text: And king Ahaz cut off the borders of the bases, and removed the laver from off them; and took down the sea from off the brasen oxen that were under it, and put it upon the pavement of stones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/16/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12493aff-a42c-461b-8bed-93bde72dd3e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: 2KI 16:18
Text: And the covert for the sabbath that they had built in the house, and the king’s entry without, turned he from the house of the LORD for the king of Assyria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/16/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:442c2108-3d82-4bbf-8db2-9ec78f142a6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 2KI 16:19
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Ahaz which he did, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/16/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c19284d5-23fa-4a7f-9e5a-27f95ed239af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 2KI 16:20
Text: And Ahaz slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in the city of David: and Hezekiah his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00e56719-551e-4371-9c6b-be5f25c713ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 2KI 17:1
Text: In the twelfth year of Ahaz king of Judah began Hoshea the son of Elah to reign in Samaria over Israel nine years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d40fee7-5ce9-425b-97b1-246b35f80696>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: 2KI 17:2
Text: And he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD, but not as the kings of Israel that were before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac3d68be-0b7f-4835-844c-417595de9bd3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: 2KI 17:3
Text: Against him came up Shalmaneser king of Assyria; and Hoshea became his servant, and gave him presents.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52c68ce9-87fe-4c89-8d74-3ce831906b89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: 2KI 17:4
Text: And the king of Assyria found conspiracy in Hoshea: for he had sent messengers to So king of Egypt, and brought no present to the king of Assyria, as he had done year by year: therefore the king of Assyria shut him up, and bound him in prison.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4383295f-6e4b-4b51-82e7-f863551fb31d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 2KI 17:5
Text: Then the king of Assyria came up throughout all the land, and went up to Samaria, and besieged it three years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:147906fb-1f92-4050-b36d-5f97c0a59c5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: 2KI 17:6
Text: In the ninth year of Hoshea the king of Assyria took Samaria, and carried Israel away into Assyria, and placed them in Halah and in Habor by the river of Gozan, and in the cities of the Medes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e4f6f81-e225-4919-8ae9-6fe734b8adb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: 2KI 17:7
Text: For so it was, that the children of Israel had sinned against the LORD their God, which had brought them up out of the land of Egypt, from under the hand of Pharaoh king of Egypt, and had feared other gods,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a76636e2-b68d-4612-b882-b83679081fa8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 2KI 17:8
Text: And walked in the statutes of the heathen, whom the LORD cast out from before the children of Israel, and of the kings of Israel, which they had made.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f270b0d-7081-4afb-a1fc-51191c14c00d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: 2KI 17:9
Text: And the children of Israel did secretly those things that were not right against the LORD their God, and they built them high places in all their cities, from the tower of the watchmen to the fenced city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95317dc4-58ef-44d4-bc59-76760ad7a1bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: 2KI 17:10
Text: And they set them up images and groves in every high hill, and under every green tree:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01737b37-fd58-4c87-92d6-1a7ddf08021a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: 2KI 17:11
Text: And there they burnt incense in all the high places, as did the heathen whom the LORD carried away before them; and wrought wicked things to provoke the LORD to anger:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17325f10-a070-42ba-998b-dfa3beb03455>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: 2KI 17:12
Text: For they served idols, whereof the LORD had said unto them, Ye shall not do this thing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10998304-fcc7-4b78-971f-5341e465f410>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 317

Reference: 2KI 17:13
Text: Yet the LORD testified against Israel, and against Judah, by all the prophets, and by all the seers, saying, Turn ye from your evil ways, and keep my commandments and my statutes, according to all the law which I commanded your fathers, and which I sent to you by my servants the prophets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9551e957-cb1b-4119-9081-277d99d6fce4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: 2KI 17:14
Text: Notwithstanding they would not hear, but hardened their necks, like to the neck of their fathers, that did not believe in the LORD their God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:317dce3f-7a92-4fe8-9bee-65869898a1bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 338

Reference: 2KI 17:15
Text: And they rejected his statutes, and his covenant that he made with their fathers, and his testimonies which he testified against them; and they followed vanity, and became vain, and went after the heathen that were round about them, concerning whom the LORD had charged them, that they should not do like them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43721e14-46a8-401d-8184-90ac017c708d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: 2KI 17:16
Text: And they left all the commandments of the LORD their God, and made them molten images, even two calves, and made a grove, and worshipped all the host of heaven, and served Baal.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c646ef11-38e3-4375-96d2-a8dc1a6e461d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: 2KI 17:17
Text: And they caused their sons and their daughters to pass through the fire, and used divination and enchantments, and sold themselves to do evil in the sight of the LORD, to provoke him to anger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f208c8b8-cb8d-4519-83fe-bb328c0442f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 2KI 17:18
Text: Therefore the LORD was very angry with Israel, and removed them out of his sight: there was none left but the tribe of Judah only.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae1eacdb-8739-419e-8896-dd5fc64aca3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 2KI 17:19
Text: Also Judah kept not the commandments of the LORD their God, but walked in the statutes of Israel which they made.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2cf6ebe6-52bc-48c4-a99f-b49ebb356b59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: 2KI 17:20
Text: And the LORD rejected all the seed of Israel, and afflicted them, and delivered them into the hand of spoilers, until he had cast them out of his sight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9f7176f-4f35-436b-8f2a-7ed9b0b01ba7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: 2KI 17:21
Text: For he rent Israel from the house of David; and they made Jeroboam the son of Nebat king: and Jeroboam drave Israel from following the LORD, and made them sin a great sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6372192-f1c6-4313-91ab-874a2a3f0da9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 2KI 17:22
Text: For the children of Israel walked in all the sins of Jeroboam which he did; they departed not from them;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32b1df46-7ad4-4859-a0a1-55ebf16a46e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: 2KI 17:23
Text: Until the LORD removed Israel out of his sight, as he had said by all his servants the prophets. So was Israel carried away out of their own land to Assyria unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8beb588-052a-442a-a125-5f5d2090c69d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 283

Reference: 2KI 17:24
Text: And the king of Assyria brought men from Babylon, and from Cuthah, and from Ava, and from Hamath, and from Sepharvaim, and placed them in the cities of Samaria instead of the children of Israel: and they possessed Samaria, and dwelt in the cities thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:028c35f4-3f31-4c3f-9f77-a56055276c27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: 2KI 17:25
Text: And so it was at the beginning of their dwelling there, that they feared not the LORD: therefore the LORD sent lions among them, which slew some of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:159b613a-a1d2-4c0a-95b3-54246da7a9d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 325

Reference: 2KI 17:26
Text: Wherefore they spake to the king of Assyria, saying, The nations which thou hast removed, and placed in the cities of Samaria, know not the manner of the God of the land: therefore he hath sent lions among them, and, behold, they slay them, because they know not the manner of the God of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96933a1b-45a3-4049-b8b5-e8f94d310538>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: 2KI 17:27
Text: Then the king of Assyria commanded, saying, Carry thither one of the priests whom ye brought from thence; and let them go and dwell there, and let him teach them the manner of the God of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f7847c8-baaf-49cf-a081-8d395e33e732>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: 2KI 17:28
Text: Then one of the priests whom they had carried away from Samaria came and dwelt in Bethel, and taught them how they should fear the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b11b43d-c496-410a-95d3-83b56be5ca4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: 2KI 17:29
Text: Howbeit every nation made gods of their own, and put them in the houses of the high places which the Samaritans had made, every nation in their cities wherein they dwelt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe093bcb-d5b5-4678-84a8-d275b1911774>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: 2KI 17:30
Text: And the men of Babylon made Succothbenoth, and the men of Cuth made Nergal, and the men of Hamath made Ashima,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ae87923-f847-41da-a5b0-be574c133820>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 2KI 17:31
Text: And the Avites made Nibhaz and Tartak, and the Sepharvites burnt their children in fire to Adrammelech and Anammelech, the gods of Sepharvaim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac2b2f6d-a287-4fed-94a6-ad4329eba6ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 2KI 17:32
Text: So they feared the LORD, and made unto themselves of the lowest of them priests of the high places, which sacrificed for them in the houses of the high places.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32a34ec9-c8a7-4502-9110-e6c0f754d037>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: 2KI 17:33
Text: They feared the LORD, and served their own gods, after the manner of the nations whom they carried away from thence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a193a283-5e43-420a-bf74-880eabe55881>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: 2KI 17:34
Text: Unto this day they do after the former manners: they fear not the LORD, neither do they after their statutes, or after their ordinances, or after the law and commandment which the LORD commanded the children of Jacob, whom he named Israel;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57853443-6309-443e-a865-09da5fb3fbe9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: 2KI 17:35
Text: With whom the LORD had made a covenant, and charged them, saying, Ye shall not fear other gods, nor bow yourselves to them, nor serve them, nor sacrifice to them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5fe3e08a-03ab-4415-b05e-020eae2df6a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: 2KI 17:36
Text: But the LORD, who brought you up out of the land of Egypt with great power and a stretched out arm, him shall ye fear, and him shall ye worship, and to him shall ye do sacrifice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a50e2a2-c40b-4f57-806d-2d7bc5d9d030>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: 2KI 17:37
Text: And the statutes, and the ordinances, and the law, and the commandment, which he wrote for you, ye shall observe to do for evermore; and ye shall not fear other gods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:158fe942-025a-4ffd-a8bc-be8a42c49c36>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: 2KI 17:38
Text: And the covenant that I have made with you ye shall not forget; neither shall ye fear other gods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fa6b57f-b5f6-4d4a-a04d-06a7026b8ebd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: 2KI 17:39
Text: But the LORD your God ye shall fear; and he shall deliver you out of the hand of all your enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19998576-29b5-4bb8-a31b-7deadc2f38ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: 2KI 17:40
Text: Howbeit they did not hearken, but they did after their former manner.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/17/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd5840bf-9db9-4bd8-8c55-8286ae928222>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: 2KI 17:41
Text: So these nations feared the LORD, and served their graven images, both their children, and their children’s children: as did their fathers, so do they unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:deea5776-c64b-4082-ad50-58afd94976f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 2KI 18:1
Text: Now it came to pass in the third year of Hoshea son of Elah king of Israel, that Hezekiah the son of Ahaz king of Judah began to reign.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a016b20-5f73-4cb1-af89-e3a0140e5932>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: 2KI 18:2
Text: Twenty and five years old was he when he began to reign; and he reigned twenty and nine years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name also was Abi, the daughter of Zachariah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28ace058-3a58-4d7e-b373-9d4d28752b61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 2KI 18:3
Text: And he did that which was right in the sight of the LORD, according to all that David his father did.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e58df6ae-fd32-4394-9241-73e020dc4e84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: 2KI 18:4
Text: He removed the high places, and brake the images, and cut down the groves, and brake in pieces the brasen serpent that Moses had made: for unto those days the children of Israel did burn incense to it: and he called it Nehushtan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e73193ff-9a59-4551-980b-0956ffae4500>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 2KI 18:5
Text: He trusted in the LORD God of Israel; so that after him was none like him among all the kings of Judah, nor any that were before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29289221-0f7b-432e-bb10-09848386ba25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 2KI 18:6
Text: For he clave to the LORD, and departed not from following him, but kept his commandments, which the LORD commanded Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa38ef64-d301-4712-81e6-8df078900a41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: 2KI 18:7
Text: And the LORD was with him; and he prospered whithersoever he went forth: and he rebelled against the king of Assyria, and served him not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31c741cf-5373-44b3-a2cf-5fbc0e722b6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: 2KI 18:8
Text: He smote the Philistines, even unto Gaza, and the borders thereof, from the tower of the watchmen to the fenced city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c873e8d-8ecf-461d-91ca-61018055bb76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: 2KI 18:9
Text: And it came to pass in the fourth year of king Hezekiah, which was the seventh year of Hoshea son of Elah king of Israel, that Shalmaneser king of Assyria came up against Samaria, and besieged it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82fd7bcf-b199-4bb8-abb9-733f2cdff7c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: 2KI 18:10
Text: And at the end of three years they took it: even in the sixth year of Hezekiah, that is in the ninth year of Hoshea king of Israel, Samaria was taken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd96c106-b1bd-4970-957f-41089cfc4ef4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 2KI 18:11
Text: And the king of Assyria did carry away Israel unto Assyria, and put them in Halah and in Habor by the river of Gozan, and in the cities of the Medes:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7803ca8a-d1c6-4862-91e1-a02fc0d88e5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: 2KI 18:12
Text: Because they obeyed not the voice of the LORD their God, but transgressed his covenant, and all that Moses the servant of the LORD commanded, and would not hear them, nor do them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28e649ff-b6a7-4cd7-8d60-1507f4748818>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: 2KI 18:13
Text: Now in the fourteenth year of king Hezekiah did Sennacherib king of Assyria come up against all the fenced cities of Judah, and took them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfee2d0a-1291-41fb-b699-51cd1422cfe7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 300

Reference: 2KI 18:14
Text: And Hezekiah king of Judah sent to the king of Assyria to Lachish, saying, I have offended; return from me: that which thou puttest on me will I bear. And the king of Assyria appointed unto Hezekiah king of Judah three hundred talents of silver and thirty talents of gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc07d170-04be-4973-ad9b-4223704d5d3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: 2KI 18:15
Text: And Hezekiah gave him all the silver that was found in the house of the LORD, and in the treasures of the king’s house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:843758d6-4ee9-4e05-b264-7f42b6aac124>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: 2KI 18:16
Text: At that time did Hezekiah cut off the gold from the doors of the temple of the LORD, and from the pillars which Hezekiah king of Judah had overlaid, and gave it to the king of Assyria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:378ce1d7-3ec3-4c49-b848-c941592d4d34>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 328

Reference: 2KI 18:17
Text: And the king of Assyria sent Tartan and Rabsaris and Rabshakeh from Lachish to king Hezekiah with a great host against Jerusalem. And they went up and came to Jerusalem. And when they were come up, they came and stood by the conduit of the upper pool, which is in the highway of the fuller’s field.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:216df027-e4a6-4993-91d5-99a588ceadc7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: 2KI 18:18
Text: And when they had called to the king, there came out to them Eliakim the son of Hilkiah, which was over the household, and Shebna the scribe, and Joah the son of Asaph the recorder.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e5358ba-3103-4d7f-bd96-bcfb90ebd098>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: 2KI 18:19
Text: And Rabshakeh said unto them, Speak ye now to Hezekiah, Thus saith the great king, the king of Assyria, What confidence is this wherein thou trustest?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aec5162e-e024-4ee4-8a33-6a66f9eac4a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 2KI 18:20
Text: Thou sayest, (but they are but vain words,) I have counsel and strength for the war. Now on whom dost thou trust, that thou rebellest against me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6081515b-9f04-4644-9d21-5b74ac75040b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: 2KI 18:21
Text: Now, behold, thou trustest upon the staff of this bruised reed, even upon Egypt, on which if a man lean, it will go into his hand, and pierce it: so is Pharaoh king of Egypt unto all that trust on him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18539e99-720d-41b8-a3f3-48f48bb8a55d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: 2KI 18:22
Text: But if ye say unto me, We trust in the LORD our God: is not that he, whose high places and whose altars Hezekiah hath taken away, and hath said to Judah and Jerusalem, Ye shall worship before this altar in Jerusalem?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35f3636f-c4bd-421b-ac82-24293a2d84e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: 2KI 18:23
Text: Now therefore, I pray thee, give pledges to my lord the king of Assyria, and I will deliver thee two thousand horses, if thou be able on thy part to set riders upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78ef2276-e1f5-409e-9d7c-92d3558cb53d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: 2KI 18:24
Text: How then wilt thou turn away the face of one captain of the least of my master’s servants, and put thy trust on Egypt for chariots and for horsemen?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36bae409-e0fb-49d8-a211-3cf21987d9b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 2KI 18:25
Text: Am I now come up without the LORD against this place to destroy it? The LORD said to me, Go up against this land, and destroy it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a6c33b6-f058-4ede-b680-27e74111e9b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 278

Reference: 2KI 18:26
Text: Then said Eliakim the son of Hilkiah, and Shebna, and Joah, unto Rabshakeh, Speak, I pray thee, to thy servants in the Syrian language; for we understand it: and talk not with us in the Jews’ language in the ears of the people that are on the wall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fab121f2-9f2c-4ded-805a-f3024175305a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: 2KI 18:27
Text: But Rabshakeh said unto them, Hath my master sent me to thy master, and to thee, to speak these words? hath he not sent me to the men which sit on the wall, that they may eat their own dung, and drink their own piss with you?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ffb1455-62f2-41b5-8b23-3c908a36317e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: 2KI 18:28
Text: Then Rabshakeh stood and cried with a loud voice in the Jews’ language, and spake, saying, Hear the word of the great king, the king of Assyria:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1857a0dc-0722-4c06-b10e-7bfffccf5304>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 2KI 18:29
Text: Thus saith the king, Let not Hezekiah deceive you: for he shall not be able to deliver you out of his hand:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf015f53-60ec-49e2-be3d-e002835e70bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: 2KI 18:30
Text: Neither let Hezekiah make you trust in the LORD, saying, The LORD will surely deliver us, and this city shall not be delivered into the hand of the king of Assyria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9de60001-bba4-447c-8a21-aeb7e10dc0c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: 2KI 18:31
Text: Hearken not to Hezekiah: for thus saith the king of Assyria, Make an agreement with me by a present, and come out to me, and then eat ye every man of his own vine, and every one of his fig tree, and drink ye every one the waters of his cistern:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35c95c17-f73f-42d1-b1ec-2b6e94c0fb81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 298

Reference: 2KI 18:32
Text: Until I come and take you away to a land like your own land, a land of corn and wine, a land of bread and vineyards, a land of oil olive and of honey, that ye may live, and not die: and hearken not unto Hezekiah, when he persuadeth you, saying, The LORD will deliver us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5d12e89-451f-422f-aae2-ffe458964cf3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: 2KI 18:33
Text: Hath any of the gods of the nations delivered at all his land out of the hand of the king of Assyria?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9648501a-c3be-4128-9cbc-6481835aea1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 2KI 18:34
Text: Where are the gods of Hamath, and of Arpad? where are the gods of Sepharvaim, Hena, and Ivah? have they delivered Samaria out of mine hand?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50187376-bd75-4032-afec-9b6ff120d702>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: 2KI 18:35
Text: Who are they among all the gods of the countries, that have delivered their country out of mine hand, that the LORD should deliver Jerusalem out of mine hand?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:512eaab1-0506-47d3-9b3a-e8cec91a53dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 2KI 18:36
Text: But the people held their peace, and answered him not a word: for the king’s commandment was, saying, Answer him not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/18/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:677becf5-eef2-4db9-8a1a-e5e56dfaad78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: 2KI 18:37
Text: Then came Eliakim the son of Hilkiah, which was over the household, and Shebna the scribe, and Joah the son of Asaph the recorder, to Hezekiah with their clothes rent, and told him the words of Rabshakeh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4478659-3e62-414b-a1dc-6902b5e57cd8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 2KI 19:1
Text: And it came to pass, when king Hezekiah heard it, that he rent his clothes, and covered himself with sackcloth, and went into the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43a57df7-9596-4eb3-b096-6dbf1824c390>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: 2KI 19:2
Text: And he sent Eliakim, which was over the household, and Shebna the scribe, and the elders of the priests, covered with sackcloth, to Isaiah the prophet the son of Amoz.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac461841-0533-4daf-85e7-7c48e4955ec1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: 2KI 19:3
Text: And they said unto him, Thus saith Hezekiah, This day is a day of trouble, and of rebuke, and blasphemy; for the children are come to the birth, and there is not strength to bring forth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2482fa2-119b-4528-9e37-e2b79e56ff5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 287

Reference: 2KI 19:4
Text: It may be the LORD thy God will hear all the words of Rabshakeh, whom the king of Assyria his master hath sent to reproach the living God; and will reprove the words which the LORD thy God hath heard: wherefore lift up thy prayer for the remnant that are left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c6f25ee-b1c7-4571-9e6f-e4c1166505f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: 2KI 19:5
Text: So the servants of king Hezekiah came to Isaiah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ab097da-31a0-4699-97a0-af928aded855>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: 2KI 19:6
Text: And Isaiah said unto them, Thus shall ye say to your master, Thus saith the LORD, Be not afraid of the words which thou hast heard, with which the servants of the king of Assyria have blasphemed me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7b65b76-5f0b-4503-9259-f56a7945a570>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 2KI 19:7
Text: Behold, I will send a blast upon him, and he shall hear a rumour, and shall return to his own land; and I will cause him to fall by the sword in his own land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:484ed3d0-49f9-403f-82f9-ab21f4e6f9d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 2KI 19:8
Text: So Rabshakeh returned, and found the king of Assyria warring against Libnah: for he had heard that he was departed from Lachish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82724493-dd98-4ae7-9bba-1da79d221edc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: 2KI 19:9
Text: And when he heard say of Tirhakah king of Ethiopia, Behold, he is come out to fight against thee: he sent messengers again unto Hezekiah, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:496e42d3-88d5-4a97-b29e-b855f97597f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: 2KI 19:10
Text: Thus shall ye speak to Hezekiah king of Judah, saying, Let not thy God in whom thou trustest deceive thee, saying, Jerusalem shall not be delivered into the hand of the king of Assyria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e05b75b-f6e2-46d6-87da-3b7869f7bf3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 2KI 19:11
Text: Behold, thou hast heard what the kings of Assyria have done to all lands, by destroying them utterly: and shalt thou be delivered?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6e1ac37-d4fe-4644-99e7-1573aff17c08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: 2KI 19:12
Text: Have the gods of the nations delivered them which my fathers have destroyed; as Gozan, and Haran, and Rezeph, and the children of Eden which were in Thelasar?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad3194d9-1504-4eb4-9a1c-7a2f6aac6a7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: 2KI 19:13
Text: Where is the king of Hamath, and the king of Arpad, and the king of the city of Sepharvaim, of Hena, and Ivah?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:770e5d50-01ca-4b73-8fdf-8dd65d6a1f13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: 2KI 19:14
Text: And Hezekiah received the letter of the hand of the messengers, and read it: and Hezekiah went up into the house of the LORD, and spread it before the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46a22d2a-b911-4256-a1a3-12969e124b26>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: 2KI 19:15
Text: And Hezekiah prayed before the LORD, and said, O LORD God of Israel, which dwellest between the cherubims, thou art the God, even thou alone, of all the kingdoms of the earth; thou hast made heaven and earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd55dc58-b910-49de-aad1-052648f2251d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 2KI 19:16
Text: LORD, bow down thine ear, and hear: open, LORD, thine eyes, and see: and hear the words of Sennacherib, which hath sent him to reproach the living God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b0e17b9-0e4d-42c8-a65f-b1d7ebd53134>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: 2KI 19:17
Text: Of a truth, LORD, the kings of Assyria have destroyed the nations and their lands,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a8ac60d-7c46-419a-8734-895de0abcd97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 2KI 19:18
Text: And have cast their gods into the fire: for they were no gods, but the work of men’s hands, wood and stone: therefore they have destroyed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5cd50e34-4bc2-4fe5-b1b4-4a433b06318b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: 2KI 19:19
Text: Now therefore, O LORD our God, I beseech thee, save thou us out of his hand, that all the kingdoms of the earth may know that thou art the LORD God, even thou only.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d09e2c0c-3423-409d-8d63-1d347cbcac57>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 2KI 19:20
Text: Then Isaiah the son of Amoz sent to Hezekiah, saying, Thus saith the LORD God of Israel, That which thou hast prayed to me against Sennacherib king of Assyria I have heard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54153c36-5ce4-4445-8acb-aa80bb1f49a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: 2KI 19:21
Text: This is the word that the LORD hath spoken concerning him; The virgin the daughter of Zion hath despised thee, and laughed thee to scorn; the daughter of Jerusalem hath shaken her head at thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66332f2f-97e5-47cb-b966-827721bd46b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: 2KI 19:22
Text: Whom hast thou reproached and blasphemed? and against whom hast thou exalted thy voice, and lifted up thine eyes on high? even against the Holy One of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad0270da-5963-400f-b0e1-cd65a84bec36>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 363

Reference: 2KI 19:23
Text: By thy messengers thou hast reproached the LORD, and hast said, With the multitude of my chariots I am come up to the height of the mountains, to the sides of Lebanon, and will cut down the tall cedar trees thereof, and the choice fir trees thereof: and I will enter into the lodgings of his borders, and into the forest of his Carmel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01cf2db2-8327-4fb4-9ddc-934813369562>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 2KI 19:24
Text: I have digged and drunk strange waters, and with the sole of my feet have I dried up all the rivers of besieged places.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1bd94e08-c614-4e0d-975e-4691d5aaa8af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: 2KI 19:25
Text: Hast thou not heard long ago how I have done it, and of ancient times that I have formed it? now have I brought it to pass, that thou shouldest be to lay waste fenced cities into ruinous heaps.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:066c11d8-e4f8-46a5-a755-89c567ae4734>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: 2KI 19:26
Text: Therefore their inhabitants were of small power, they were dismayed and confounded; they were as the grass of the field, and as the green herb, as the grass on the house tops, and as corn blasted before it be grown up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86d88e09-87fa-4ada-96ef-6d1d2b34647a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: 2KI 19:27
Text: But I know thy abode, and thy going out, and thy coming in, and thy rage against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb364744-5933-47e8-8b2c-2cbe66a76940>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: 2KI 19:28
Text: Because thy rage against me and thy tumult is come up into mine ears, therefore I will put my hook in thy nose, and my bridle in thy lips, and I will turn thee back by the way by which thou camest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a5d4534-3caf-4c30-9432-00992e4ad598>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: 2KI 19:29
Text: And this shall be a sign unto thee, Ye shall eat this year such things as grow of themselves, and in the second year that which springeth of the same; and in the third year sow ye, and reap, and plant vineyards, and eat the fruits thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3aa43122-252f-41c5-a151-fe26bb684dea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 2KI 19:30
Text: And the remnant that is escaped of the house of Judah shall yet again take root downward, and bear fruit upward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:569b9e4f-a606-47ce-b23f-8ff18c9671f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: 2KI 19:31
Text: For out of Jerusalem shall go forth a remnant, and they that escape out of mount Zion: the zeal of the LORD of hosts shall do this.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f786cdc-e557-42f1-b477-e5f56af69f4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: 2KI 19:32
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD concerning the king of Assyria, He shall not come into this city, nor shoot an arrow there, nor come before it with shield, nor cast a bank against it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e089f9f-99c2-482f-b87e-2b788f91f2d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 2KI 19:33
Text: By the way that he came, by the same shall he return, and shall not come into this city, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf82ff34-8168-4c70-8e59-e5c4f05a94fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: 2KI 19:34
Text: For I will defend this city, to save it, for mine own sake, and for my servant David’s sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:529174de-9e6c-4ed5-a71d-cab74c9cc530>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: 2KI 19:35
Text: And it came to pass that night, that the angel of the LORD went out, and smote in the camp of the Assyrians an hundred fourscore and five thousand: and when they arose early in the morning, behold, they were all dead corpses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0c0636a-4429-4c22-b8a8-5808fe800b97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: 2KI 19:36
Text: So Sennacherib king of Assyria departed, and went and returned, and dwelt at Nineveh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/19/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09a2db30-ae11-49bf-a298-7137f8be1bdb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: 2KI 19:37
Text: And it came to pass, as he was worshipping in the house of Nisroch his god, that Adrammelech and Sharezer his sons smote him with the sword: and they escaped into the land of Armenia. And Esarhaddon his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/20/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5dbc840f-c727-4c13-8a8a-438f766bcc7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: 2KI 20:1
Text: In those days was Hezekiah sick unto death. And the prophet Isaiah the son of Amoz came to him, and said unto him, Thus saith the LORD, Set thine house in order; for thou shalt die, and not live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/20/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b586c294-411c-4663-8bf2-a9e6a8749638>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: 2KI 20:2
Text: Then he turned his face to the wall, and prayed unto the LORD, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/20/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd1ba052-e3c4-4a4d-a535-be6ca52321f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: 2KI 20:3
Text: I beseech thee, O LORD, remember now how I have walked before thee in truth and with a perfect heart, and have done that which is good in thy sight. And Hezekiah wept sore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/20/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ccf16ce5-149b-4cae-80de-12dac40090a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: 2KI 20:4
Text: And it came to pass, afore Isaiah was gone out into the middle court, that the word of the LORD came to him, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/20/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08e0e31f-4aa5-4d0c-a853-a9b309a33555>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: 2KI 20:5
Text: Turn again, and tell Hezekiah the captain of my people, Thus saith the LORD, the God of David thy father, I have heard thy prayer, I have seen thy tears: behold, I will heal thee: on the third day thou shalt go up unto the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/20/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da1e9968-a75b-4213-b796-2f48310464bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: 2KI 20:6
Text: And I will add unto thy days fifteen years; and I will deliver thee and this city out of the hand of the king of Assyria; and I will defend this city for mine own sake, and for my servant David’s sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/20/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de3885ff-54b8-4bc0-bdeb-1b476e56884e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 2KI 20:7
Text: And Isaiah said, Take a lump of figs. And they took and laid it on the boil, and he recovered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/20/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cef0e8d4-79af-4f6a-8999-6a0af4e141ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 2KI 20:8
Text: And Hezekiah said unto Isaiah, What shall be the sign that the LORD will heal me, and that I shall go up into the house of the LORD the third day?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/20/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c49b21b-ae5b-498a-b46a-0b0aee3d8362>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 2KI 20:9
Text: And Isaiah said, This sign shalt thou have of the LORD, that the LORD will do the thing that he hath spoken: shall the shadow go forward ten degrees, or go back ten degrees?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/20/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc77417f-6751-4465-9f99-66468406b6fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 2KI 20:10
Text: And Hezekiah answered, It is a light thing for the shadow to go down ten degrees: nay, but let the shadow return backward ten degrees.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/20/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2b23d15-7333-4dab-b587-91d7debb3cea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: 2KI 20:11
Text: And Isaiah the prophet cried unto the LORD: and he brought the shadow ten degrees backward, by which it had gone down in the dial of Ahaz.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/20/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:407dc95b-a112-4bdb-a85a-45a2251cc5e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: 2KI 20:12
Text: At that time Berodachbaladan, the son of Baladan, king of Babylon, sent letters and a present unto Hezekiah: for he had heard that Hezekiah had been sick.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/20/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d68b7fbb-54b2-48d6-8d4e-ee6810aee64d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 346

Reference: 2KI 20:13
Text: And Hezekiah hearkened unto them, and shewed them all the house of his precious things, the silver, and the gold, and the spices, and the precious ointment, and all the house of his armour, and all that was found in his treasures: there was nothing in his house, nor in all his dominion, that Hezekiah shewed them not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/20/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87c57d78-a024-4054-9e98-9eb29f8d374f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: 2KI 20:14
Text: Then came Isaiah the prophet unto king Hezekiah, and said unto him, What said these men? and from whence came they unto thee? And Hezekiah said, They are come from a far country, even from Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/20/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7514d12-9efa-40d9-864a-10fdb35621c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: 2KI 20:15
Text: And he said, What have they seen in thine house? And Hezekiah answered, All the things that are in mine house have they seen: there is nothing among my treasures that I have not shewed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/20/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d9d4839-0e06-49dc-81a1-63a452e5b08f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: 2KI 20:16
Text: And Isaiah said unto Hezekiah, Hear the word of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/20/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:828ffd1c-c1c4-4e63-a258-fee9e615430e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: 2KI 20:17
Text: Behold, the days come, that all that is in thine house, and that which thy fathers have laid up in store unto this day, shall be carried into Babylon: nothing shall be left, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/20/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc428eb4-7d1f-4712-ba14-f66bac76823a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: 2KI 20:18
Text: And of thy sons that shall issue from thee, which thou shalt beget, shall they take away; and they shall be eunuchs in the palace of the king of Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/20/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b73cc75-f460-42d0-bf01-d89d1d55fbea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 2KI 20:19
Text: Then said Hezekiah unto Isaiah, Good is the word of the LORD which thou hast spoken. And he said, Is it not good, if peace and truth be in my days?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/20/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89d56d69-07a5-44eb-8b3f-05abc1343997>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: 2KI 20:20
Text: And the rest of the acts of Hezekiah, and all his might, and how he made a pool, and a conduit, and brought water into the city, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/20/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2faf33e4-473e-4976-98be-1dcf97a6f962>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: 2KI 20:21
Text: And Hezekiah slept with his fathers: and Manasseh his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93771e23-b60d-436f-aa1a-48630b9981d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: 2KI 21:1
Text: Manasseh was twelve years old when he began to reign, and reigned fifty and five years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Hephzibah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da83857c-53e4-47b5-805d-9e0c0c3b871f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: 2KI 21:2
Text: And he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD, after the abominations of the heathen, whom the LORD cast out before the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3f49967-4045-4b29-9533-59a9e03523a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: 2KI 21:3
Text: For he built up again the high places which Hezekiah his father had destroyed; and he reared up altars for Baal, and made a grove, as did Ahab king of Israel; and worshipped all the host of heaven, and served them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24157933-0d46-462a-9a27-02f60f3fbf83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: 2KI 21:4
Text: And he built altars in the house of the LORD, of which the LORD said, In Jerusalem will I put my name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58925029-6631-4dbb-8a75-e9ee5d868093>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: 2KI 21:5
Text: And he built altars for all the host of heaven in the two courts of the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac082fb7-23d0-4c7f-907c-890680035df7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: 2KI 21:6
Text: And he made his son pass through the fire, and observed times, and used enchantments, and dealt with familiar spirits and wizards: he wrought much wickedness in the sight of the LORD, to provoke him to anger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:864911a4-7d63-4c99-b6bd-ff1e48e22106>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: 2KI 21:7
Text: And he set a graven image of the grove that he had made in the house, of which the LORD said to David, and to Solomon his son, In this house, and in Jerusalem, which I have chosen out of all tribes of Israel, will I put my name for ever:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ed750df-8494-4363-a938-83ddd4f1b2f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: 2KI 21:8
Text: Neither will I make the feet of Israel move any more out of the land which I gave their fathers; only if they will observe to do according to all that I have commanded them, and according to all the law that my servant Moses commanded them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e72b1c95-c857-4ac1-b469-40c83d316544>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: 2KI 21:9
Text: But they hearkened not: and Manasseh seduced them to do more evil than did the nations whom the LORD destroyed before the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1db6fc4-f482-48eb-b59d-13024d0ca373>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: 2KI 21:10
Text: And the LORD spake by his servants the prophets, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2aea1691-a203-4ebe-be60-7fce3d6cbe96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: 2KI 21:11
Text: Because Manasseh king of Judah hath done these abominations, and hath done wickedly above all that the Amorites did, which were before him, and hath made Judah also to sin with his idols:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bd9cc80-abac-441b-be5b-f82e4493b9a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 2KI 21:12
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD God of Israel, Behold, I am bringing such evil upon Jerusalem and Judah, that whosoever heareth of it, both his ears shall tingle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7be2d6d-cd7c-4068-b68b-abe741343e63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: 2KI 21:13
Text: And I will stretch over Jerusalem the line of Samaria, and the plummet of the house of Ahab: and I will wipe Jerusalem as a man wipeth a dish, wiping it, and turning it upside down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87f9efef-e1f9-4a9d-9146-c53e90b35f96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: 2KI 21:14
Text: And I will forsake the remnant of mine inheritance, and deliver them into the hand of their enemies; and they shall become a prey and a spoil to all their enemies;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3bef893-cbf3-4ba6-95e2-f24c9636a730>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 2KI 21:15
Text: Because they have done that which was evil in my sight, and have provoked me to anger, since the day their fathers came forth out of Egypt, even unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4921fbae-789f-441c-a260-0739cc53b0f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: 2KI 21:16
Text: Moreover Manasseh shed innocent blood very much, till he had filled Jerusalem from one end to another; beside his sin wherewith he made Judah to sin, in doing that which was evil in the sight of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89c4bc83-a485-49c7-84a9-a6119739ffa0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 2KI 21:17
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Manasseh, and all that he did, and his sin that he sinned, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d539d91e-8845-4deb-89be-5bf419a0cf86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 2KI 21:18
Text: And Manasseh slept with his fathers, and was buried in the garden of his own house, in the garden of Uzza: and Amon his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f089ec6c-2b1f-41a7-8eb8-d93c6d2dd802>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: 2KI 21:19
Text: Amon was twenty and two years old when he began to reign, and he reigned two years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Meshullemeth, the daughter of Haruz of Jotbah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c423f47-c472-4857-910d-879f4c7d9e87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: 2KI 21:20
Text: And he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD, as his father Manasseh did.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8eb9b793-c8e4-45b5-8cf6-4e875c974b39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: 2KI 21:21
Text: And he walked in all the way that his father walked in, and served the idols that his father served, and worshipped them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7378add-9c51-465d-9cf2-bc1b8c150880>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: 2KI 21:22
Text: And he forsook the LORD God of his fathers, and walked not in the way of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d036591d-23dd-4aab-85f5-5fcf45435dd3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: 2KI 21:23
Text: And the servants of Amon conspired against him, and slew the king in his own house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5025031d-13ee-470e-af3f-aa5946e2f346>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: 2KI 21:24
Text: And the people of the land slew all them that had conspired against king Amon; and the people of the land made Josiah his son king in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ade25b8-fbfe-437f-9cee-75a099b7022d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 2KI 21:25
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Amon which he did, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/21/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f34595a-62d1-4ab1-b2a1-a3ec0397b8a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: 2KI 21:26
Text: And he was buried in his sepulchre in the garden of Uzza: and Josiah his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/22/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d14d537-fe3f-4c75-9ddc-dbbe2f5ad437>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: 2KI 22:1
Text: Josiah was eight years old when he began to reign, and he reigned thirty and one years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Jedidah, the daughter of Adaiah of Boscath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/22/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3625216f-b726-45d4-bbe3-02b1d66ca31f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: 2KI 22:2
Text: And he did that which was right in the sight of the LORD, and walked in all the way of David his father, and turned not aside to the right hand or to the left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/22/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fcc43f3f-44dd-4412-8beb-1ed021e3b271>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 2KI 22:3
Text: And it came to pass in the eighteenth year of king Josiah, that the king sent Shaphan the son of Azaliah, the son of Meshullam, the scribe, to the house of the LORD, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/22/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:701b9727-ea39-4bda-8ba9-f97b45862041>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: 2KI 22:4
Text: Go up to Hilkiah the high priest, that he may sum the silver which is brought into the house of the LORD, which the keepers of the door have gathered of the people:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/22/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a67d9885-1b88-4fd7-989b-d5eff823c722>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: 2KI 22:5
Text: And let them deliver it into the hand of the doers of the work, that have the oversight of the house of the LORD: and let them give it to the doers of the work which is in the house of the LORD, to repair the breaches of the house,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/22/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3ff3d9d-da35-420b-87e2-d56c4b4d4fc7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 2KI 22:6
Text: Unto carpenters, and builders, and masons, and to buy timber and hewn stone to repair the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/22/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:574eb36c-9173-4e35-869f-6d68c5544fee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: 2KI 22:7
Text: Howbeit there was no reckoning made with them of the money that was delivered into their hand, because they dealt faithfully.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/22/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:289f9655-6c40-47e9-a869-255c2191951a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: 2KI 22:8
Text: And Hilkiah the high priest said unto Shaphan the scribe, I have found the book of the law in the house of the LORD. And Hilkiah gave the book to Shaphan, and he read it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/22/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d23cafa2-dba2-466b-b871-1c9c02d77446>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 288

Reference: 2KI 22:9
Text: And Shaphan the scribe came to the king, and brought the king word again, and said, Thy servants have gathered the money that was found in the house, and have delivered it into the hand of them that do the work, that have the oversight of the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/22/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dba24ddc-9bfe-4f16-85f1-687d8ab63d54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 2KI 22:10
Text: And Shaphan the scribe shewed the king, saying, Hilkiah the priest hath delivered me a book. And Shaphan read it before the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/22/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b848b3c-476c-4b51-ab07-5feb7c622508>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 2KI 22:11
Text: And it came to pass, when the king had heard the words of the book of the law, that he rent his clothes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/22/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e5fc980-4bdb-46b6-a0d5-c914c06d659e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: 2KI 22:12
Text: And the king commanded Hilkiah the priest, and Ahikam the son of Shaphan, and Achbor the son of Michaiah, and Shaphan the scribe, and Asahiah a servant of the king’s, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/22/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cdc7bca9-c75f-4d92-8b06-68188e58efa7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 343

Reference: 2KI 22:13
Text: Go ye, enquire of the LORD for me, and for the people, and for all Judah, concerning the words of this book that is found: for great is the wrath of the LORD that is kindled against us, because our fathers have not hearkened unto the words of this book, to do according unto all that which is written concerning us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/22/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af1c4063-2186-4b66-979b-d4318a256717>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 288

Reference: 2KI 22:14
Text: So Hilkiah the priest, and Ahikam, and Achbor, and Shaphan, and Asahiah, went unto Huldah the prophetess, the wife of Shallum the son of Tikvah, the son of Harhas, keeper of the wardrobe; (now she dwelt in Jerusalem in the college;) and they communed with her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/22/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5362900-f410-47ae-b2ea-b7d6ece58908>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: 2KI 22:15
Text: And she said unto them, Thus saith the LORD God of Israel, Tell the man that sent you to me,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/22/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f25fc5b-5b1b-401b-aa94-d778a11036a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: 2KI 22:16
Text: Thus saith the LORD, Behold, I will bring evil upon this place, and upon the inhabitants thereof, even all the words of the book which the king of Judah hath read:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/22/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb00f2a4-9273-469f-8d99-5199b260c0cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: 2KI 22:17
Text: Because they have forsaken me, and have burned incense unto other gods, that they might provoke me to anger with all the works of their hands; therefore my wrath shall be kindled against this place, and shall not be quenched.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/22/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b88eabd8-4d04-439c-b6fb-159052997114>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: 2KI 22:18
Text: But to the king of Judah which sent you to enquire of the LORD, thus shall ye say to him, Thus saith the LORD God of Israel, As touching the words which thou hast heard;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/22/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3249bf26-1f71-45c6-b49a-61a08140e53e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 332

Reference: 2KI 22:19
Text: Because thine heart was tender, and thou hast humbled thyself before the LORD, when thou heardest what I spake against this place, and against the inhabitants thereof, that they should become a desolation and a curse, and hast rent thy clothes, and wept before me; I also have heard thee, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/22/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d24e2210-abc6-41cc-9a30-0d2ba4783504>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: 2KI 22:20
Text: Behold therefore, I will gather thee unto thy fathers, and thou shalt be gathered into thy grave in peace; and thine eyes shall not see all the evil which I will bring upon this place. And they brought the king word again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61183a5a-c726-47b2-b99d-ec05081302a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: 2KI 23:1
Text: And the king sent, and they gathered unto him all the elders of Judah and of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:027b3d3d-ba5e-4356-afe4-760f52c5c01c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 334

Reference: 2KI 23:2
Text: And the king went up into the house of the LORD, and all the men of Judah and all the inhabitants of Jerusalem with him, and the priests, and the prophets, and all the people, both small and great: and he read in their ears all the words of the book of the covenant which was found in the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffccf902-13ba-45f3-9680-551afea7da66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 338

Reference: 2KI 23:3
Text: And the king stood by a pillar, and made a covenant before the LORD, to walk after the LORD, and to keep his commandments and his testimonies and his statutes with all their heart and all their soul, to perform the words of this covenant that were written in this book. And all the people stood to the covenant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a17f308-064f-42f1-8beb-5d362e0308e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 382

Reference: 2KI 23:4
Text: And the king commanded Hilkiah the high priest, and the priests of the second order, and the keepers of the door, to bring forth out of the temple of the LORD all the vessels that were made for Baal, and for the grove, and for all the host of heaven: and he burned them without Jerusalem in the fields of Kidron, and carried the ashes of them unto Bethel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b33246a-77c9-4b1f-bc74-aa69d01278be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 324

Reference: 2KI 23:5
Text: And he put down the idolatrous priests, whom the kings of Judah had ordained to burn incense in the high places in the cities of Judah, and in the places round about Jerusalem; them also that burned incense unto Baal, to the sun, and to the moon, and to the planets, and to all the host of heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a07a3c71-7173-431a-a3b4-9d48eaf57d0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: 2KI 23:6
Text: And he brought out the grove from the house of the LORD, without Jerusalem, unto the brook Kidron, and burned it at the brook Kidron, and stamped it small to powder, and cast the powder thereof upon the graves of the children of the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d6778c6-9d1e-4bf6-bcfc-b429d12c747e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: 2KI 23:7
Text: And he brake down the houses of the sodomites, that were by the house of the LORD, where the women wove hangings for the grove.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b4c656b-13b6-4ceb-8190-2b20924ea960>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 355

Reference: 2KI 23:8
Text: And he brought all the priests out of the cities of Judah, and defiled the high places where the priests had burned incense, from Geba to Beersheba, and brake down the high places of the gates that were in the entering in of the gate of Joshua the governor of the city, which were on a man’s left hand at the gate of the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d32f6932-7854-4a8d-8097-c2c690344239>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: 2KI 23:9
Text: Nevertheless the priests of the high places came not up to the altar of the LORD in Jerusalem, but they did eat of the unleavened bread among their brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a30c41b7-030e-4ab0-b57e-35f6197bef02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: 2KI 23:10
Text: And he defiled Topheth, which is in the valley of the children of Hinnom, that no man might make his son or his daughter to pass through the fire to Molech.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f373941-d6b0-44c0-8dfe-06d6af47bdfa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 266

Reference: 2KI 23:11
Text: And he took away the horses that the kings of Judah had given to the sun, at the entering in of the house of the LORD, by the chamber of Nathanmelech the chamberlain, which was in the suburbs, and burned the chariots of the sun with fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4374023-0e5d-45f5-8980-4a8ba2118ad2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 317

Reference: 2KI 23:12
Text: And the altars that were on the top of the upper chamber of Ahaz, which the kings of Judah had made, and the altars which Manasseh had made in the two courts of the house of the LORD, did the king beat down, and brake them down from thence, and cast the dust of them into the brook Kidron.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6ad09e1-cbb6-42a1-bf98-44483b63a8d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 352

Reference: 2KI 23:13
Text: And the high places that were before Jerusalem, which were on the right hand of the mount of corruption, which Solomon the king of Israel had builded for Ashtoreth the abomination of the Zidonians, and for Chemosh the abomination of the Moabites, and for Milcom the abomination of the children of Ammon, did the king defile.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08bb6239-fd0b-498b-81f6-4e75c6ae088b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: 2KI 23:14
Text: And he brake in pieces the images, and cut down the groves, and filled their places with the bones of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67bdeb6a-bb33-4577-84d4-a6b817686ade>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 283

Reference: 2KI 23:15
Text: Moreover the altar that was at Bethel, and the high place which Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who made Israel to sin, had made, both that altar and the high place he brake down, and burned the high place, and stamped it small to powder, and burned the grove.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3fdc4fce-7c13-434b-8411-38c93fe8a074>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 307

Reference: 2KI 23:16
Text: And as Josiah turned himself, he spied the sepulchres that were there in the mount, and sent, and took the bones out of the sepulchres, and burned them upon the altar, and polluted it, according to the word of the LORD which the man of God proclaimed, who proclaimed these words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1909b2e3-69b9-4644-b068-fc6269dcdda6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: 2KI 23:17
Text: Then he said, What title is that that I see? And the men of the city told him, It is the sepulchre of the man of God, which came from Judah, and proclaimed these things that thou hast done against the altar of Bethel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d699e1ab-7b5f-43ef-9c44-ce20a06497e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 2KI 23:18
Text: And he said, Let him alone; let no man move his bones. So they let his bones alone, with the bones of the prophet that came out of Samaria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1428d68-0432-467a-8ed1-2d12dbe21420>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: 2KI 23:19
Text: And all the houses also of the high places that were in the cities of Samaria, which the kings of Israel had made to provoke the Lord to anger, Josiah took away, and did to them according to all the acts that he had done in Bethel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:997e9114-ce2b-4730-86cc-9a48efcaa26f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 2KI 23:20
Text: And he slew all the priests of the high places that were there upon the altars, and burned men’s bones upon them, and returned to Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3940ed1c-4b65-4622-a447-a8047f321ebc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: 2KI 23:21
Text: And the king commanded all the people, saying, Keep the passover unto the LORD your God, as it is written in the book of this covenant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92ee4027-661f-4ff0-a4bb-e11f69297cac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: 2KI 23:22
Text: Surely there was not holden such a passover from the days of the judges that judged Israel, nor in all the days of the kings of Israel, nor of the kings of Judah;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8047b17c-6ac1-4c0f-b44e-d13d37ba6078>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: 2KI 23:23
Text: But in the eighteenth year of king Josiah, wherein this passover was holden to the LORD in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:536e6676-babd-420b-8fbf-7e4682d43191>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 350

Reference: 2KI 23:24
Text: Moreover the workers with familiar spirits, and the wizards, and the images, and the idols, and all the abominations that were spied in the land of Judah and in Jerusalem, did Josiah put away, that he might perform the words of the law which were written in the book that Hilkiah the priest found in the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57e17e23-86df-4cee-975e-bcc62d9608d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: 2KI 23:25
Text: And like unto him was there no king before him, that turned to the LORD with all his heart, and with all his soul, and with all his might, according to all the law of Moses; neither after him arose there any like him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd1fb43f-112e-4d65-937a-b7b17c4209c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: 2KI 23:26
Text: Notwithstanding the LORD turned not from the fierceness of his great wrath, wherewith his anger was kindled against Judah, because of all the provocations that Manasseh had provoked him withal.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fea7164a-d954-4eeb-a1d1-31e4c1133a2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: 2KI 23:27
Text: And the LORD said, I will remove Judah also out of my sight, as I have removed Israel, and will cast off this city Jerusalem which I have chosen, and the house of which I said, My name shall be there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10eaf125-bdaa-46c7-b60b-840f95ed7905>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 2KI 23:28
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Josiah, and all that he did, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef646e23-1f7a-4df5-8aa7-813aca19d1e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: 2KI 23:29
Text: In his days Pharaohnechoh king of Egypt went up against the king of Assyria to the river Euphrates: and king Josiah went against him; and he slew him at Megiddo, when he had seen him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3aa97e07-e54b-4a50-acca-c5bfe9c1c2f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: 2KI 23:30
Text: And his servants carried him in a chariot dead from Megiddo, and brought him to Jerusalem, and buried him in his own sepulchre. And the people of the land took Jehoahaz the son of Josiah, and anointed him, and made him king in his father’s stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8dff12a7-1fae-4458-939b-863d49c2f2d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: 2KI 23:31
Text: Jehoahaz was twenty and three years old when he began to reign; and he reigned three months in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Hamutal, the daughter of Jeremiah of Libnah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2eef90d3-0a8f-40e7-a1c4-817e3df7670f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 2KI 23:32
Text: And he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD, according to all that his fathers had done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb692d77-cd5b-43f1-885e-743330a99140>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: 2KI 23:33
Text: And Pharaohnechoh put him in bands at Riblah in the land of Hamath, that he might not reign in Jerusalem; and put the land to a tribute of an hundred talents of silver, and a talent of gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2d7a880-a815-4f9b-b3ad-fc6b47bba03e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: 2KI 23:34
Text: And Pharaohnechoh made Eliakim the son of Josiah king in the room of Josiah his father, and turned his name to Jehoiakim, and took Jehoahaz away: and he came to Egypt, and died there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:432202c3-00e4-47c5-bddf-3bdaacd3b94e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 296

Reference: 2KI 23:35
Text: And Jehoiakim gave the silver and the gold to Pharaoh; but he taxed the land to give the money according to the commandment of Pharaoh: he exacted the silver and the gold of the people of the land, of every one according to his taxation, to give it unto Pharaohnechoh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:857a9bee-b06d-4d14-9099-08629d7be659>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: 2KI 23:36
Text: Jehoiakim was twenty and five years old when he began to reign; and he reigned eleven years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Zebudah, the daughter of Pedaiah of Rumah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/23/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc1cdcf5-bf36-471c-af33-7b00bef095fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 2KI 23:37
Text: And he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD, according to all that his fathers had done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/24/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc1bc63f-17ad-4a6d-bd1b-94668a700dab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: 2KI 24:1
Text: In his days Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came up, and Jehoiakim became his servant three years: then he turned and rebelled against him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/24/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2edc3ee7-dd47-428c-a4f3-d25299c36e24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 291

Reference: 2KI 24:2
Text: And the LORD sent against him bands of the Chaldees, and bands of the Syrians, and bands of the Moabites, and bands of the children of Ammon, and sent them against Judah to destroy it, according to the word of the LORD, which he spake by his servants the prophets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/24/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebdfae06-eb85-44cd-83a7-2a7bc77a3d71>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 2KI 24:3
Text: Surely at the commandment of the LORD came this upon Judah, to remove them out of his sight, for the sins of Manasseh, according to all that he did;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/24/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6766abe2-ec59-44b8-a74a-a6c1711aa117>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: 2KI 24:4
Text: And also for the innocent blood that he shed: for he filled Jerusalem with innocent blood; which the LORD would not pardon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/24/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc1fcb83-ef78-4ec8-b72b-a89b2755915e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 2KI 24:5
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Jehoiakim, and all that he did, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/24/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3614e7f-4078-4d9a-81b3-25e92d65e3e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: 2KI 24:6
Text: So Jehoiakim slept with his fathers: and Jehoiachin his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/24/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb947251-f91d-4ca6-864b-1f0457bffbc8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: 2KI 24:7
Text: And the king of Egypt came not again any more out of his land: for the king of Babylon had taken from the river of Egypt unto the river Euphrates all that pertained to the king of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/24/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c346be5c-8a80-4663-aa54-b716e1429d20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: 2KI 24:8
Text: Jehoiachin was eighteen years old when he began to reign, and he reigned in Jerusalem three months. And his mother’s name was Nehushta, the daughter of Elnathan of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/24/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8882b973-dbec-4b5b-9fdd-23a033f7efb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: 2KI 24:9
Text: And he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD, according to all that his father had done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/24/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e500dc98-3ba9-4e11-b5f0-a6964b2fe3f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 2KI 24:10
Text: At that time the servants of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came up against Jerusalem, and the city was besieged.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/24/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d08645e3-9a28-44cb-bd3a-3b8f8bf2a030>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: 2KI 24:11
Text: And Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came against the city, and his servants did besiege it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/24/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e728d278-fe96-4ede-a502-964fce2bb82f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: 2KI 24:12
Text: And Jehoiachin the king of Judah went out to the king of Babylon, he, and his mother, and his servants, and his princes, and his officers: and the king of Babylon took him in the eighth year of his reign.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/24/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5f02b17-0721-48e9-805f-1f3a9ebd1388>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: 2KI 24:13
Text: And he carried out thence all the treasures of the house of the LORD, and the treasures of the king’s house, and cut in pieces all the vessels of gold which Solomon king of Israel had made in the temple of the LORD, as the LORD had said.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/24/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47b952e1-9bae-41a2-b39b-27a93e2fd827>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: 2KI 24:14
Text: And he carried away all Jerusalem, and all the princes, and all the mighty men of valour, even ten thousand captives, and all the craftsmen and smiths: none remained, save the poorest sort of the people of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/24/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31c5bfb4-d190-4a2a-9535-e244cd36ff69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: 2KI 24:15
Text: And he carried away Jehoiachin to Babylon, and the king’s mother, and the king’s wives, and his officers, and the mighty of the land, those carried he into captivity from Jerusalem to Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/24/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:851bd57e-a761-441c-97c1-9a3e4c2f35d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: 2KI 24:16
Text: And all the men of might, even seven thousand, and craftsmen and smiths a thousand, all that were strong and apt for war, even them the king of Babylon brought captive to Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/24/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73942371-efc1-4701-b9f7-96729880665a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: 2KI 24:17
Text: And the king of Babylon made Mattaniah his father’s brother king in his stead, and changed his name to Zedekiah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/24/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3d4e7df-9cd5-4748-b660-a7154b0b3c19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: 2KI 24:18
Text: Zedekiah was twenty and one years old when he began to reign, and he reigned eleven years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Hamutal, the daughter of Jeremiah of Libnah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/24/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a822520-ce35-442a-b9b2-1a2a580c69c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: 2KI 24:19
Text: And he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD, according to all that Jehoiakim had done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/24/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21b08ee2-2d89-48ba-99ca-de81e223ee0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: 2KI 24:20
Text: For through the anger of the LORD it came to pass in Jerusalem and Judah, until he had cast them out from his presence, that Zedekiah rebelled against the king of Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00028bfd-e9d0-4bc4-b0e6-8a07b06fd13a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 281

Reference: 2KI 25:1
Text: And it came to pass in the ninth year of his reign, in the tenth month, in the tenth day of the month, that Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came, he, and all his host, against Jerusalem, and pitched against it; and they built forts against it round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1cbcdf6-32dc-4a54-a0ef-5a984ef1307e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: 2KI 25:2
Text: And the city was besieged unto the eleventh year of king Zedekiah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4b34671-76e6-4702-a86f-a955103d0ecd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: 2KI 25:3
Text: And on the ninth day of the fourth month the famine prevailed in the city, and there was no bread for the people of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba7c54b6-37f6-49b0-8bd3-a07461d7cea8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: 2KI 25:4
Text: And the city was broken up, and all the men of war fled by night by the way of the gate between two walls, which is by the king’s garden: (now the Chaldees were against the city round about:) and the king went the way toward the plain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ad2559a-71a9-4622-aac7-86cbb0b88620>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: 2KI 25:5
Text: And the army of the Chaldees pursued after the king, and overtook him in the plains of Jericho: and all his army were scattered from him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0937ff6-872c-42f4-8ff1-ee7cde37d014>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 2KI 25:6
Text: So they took the king, and brought him up to the king of Babylon to Riblah; and they gave judgment upon him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4f6e66c-8607-4661-8e50-0af983bae2d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 2KI 25:7
Text: And they slew the sons of Zedekiah before his eyes, and put out the eyes of Zedekiah, and bound him with fetters of brass, and carried him to Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37666d8e-ad32-4a7d-afb5-b071beb74804>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: 2KI 25:8
Text: And in the fifth month, on the seventh day of the month, which is the nineteenth year of king Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, came Nebuzaradan, captain of the guard, a servant of the king of Babylon, unto Jerusalem:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8837da3-6bf4-4a17-b3cc-fe70ef3dc214>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: 2KI 25:9
Text: And he burnt the house of the LORD, and the king’s house, and all the houses of Jerusalem, and every great man’s house burnt he with fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea763237-4744-4c94-a77c-a015f274dcb8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: 2KI 25:10
Text: And all the army of the Chaldees, that were with the captain of the guard, brake down the walls of Jerusalem round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cdf37f4e-c7c6-46aa-a7d8-7bd57f69ab08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: 2KI 25:11
Text: Now the rest of the people that were left in the city, and the fugitives that fell away to the king of Babylon, with the remnant of the multitude, did Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard carry away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d03dd8d5-185c-4fe8-9f42-92713e92a277>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: 2KI 25:12
Text: But the captain of the guard left of the poor of the land to be vinedressers and husbandmen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4602e275-461b-4a48-a67d-c2a6165ba4cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: 2KI 25:13
Text: And the pillars of brass that were in the house of the LORD, and the bases, and the brasen sea that was in the house of the LORD, did the Chaldees break in pieces, and carried the brass of them to Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0106299-4c8d-4ea9-ba62-1a9645115f3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: 2KI 25:14
Text: And the pots, and the shovels, and the snuffers, and the spoons, and all the vessels of brass wherewith they ministered, took they away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de63f9d2-f8d4-4679-b44d-c49c4e5c4858>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: 2KI 25:15
Text: And the firepans, and the bowls, and such things as were of gold, in gold, and of silver, in silver, the captain of the guard took away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b79309e4-62cc-4231-8ebd-fccfd0900c33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: 2KI 25:16
Text: The two pillars, one sea, and the bases which Solomon had made for the house of the LORD; the brass of all these vessels was without weight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:100df4e0-9ae2-4741-bf41-d504589e6845>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 305

Reference: 2KI 25:17
Text: The height of the one pillar was eighteen cubits, and the chapiter upon it was brass: and the height of the chapiter three cubits; and the wreathen work, and pomegranates upon the chapiter round about, all of brass: and like unto these had the second pillar with wreathen work.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28dd09d7-f319-479e-9dfe-dbbf8d9ce974>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 2KI 25:18
Text: And the captain of the guard took Seraiah the chief priest, and Zephaniah the second priest, and the three keepers of the door:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec164e58-0126-4772-8cd8-28a1237cb7b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 338

Reference: 2KI 25:19
Text: And out of the city he took an officer that was set over the men of war, and five men of them that were in the king’s presence, which were found in the city, and the principal scribe of the host, which mustered the people of the land, and threescore men of the people of the land that were found in the city:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6facfac-6275-463e-af9d-7674b9c65d30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 2KI 25:20
Text: And Nebuzaradan captain of the guard took these, and brought them to the king of Babylon to Riblah:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74be3fff-4df1-4489-9d17-f5e53ddb21a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 2KI 25:21
Text: And the king of Babylon smote them, and slew them at Riblah in the land of Hamath. So Judah was carried away out of their land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a904980a-520f-4331-82d0-a45caac69a4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: 2KI 25:22
Text: And as for the people that remained in the land of Judah, whom Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon had left, even over them he made Gedaliah the son of Ahikam, the son of Shaphan, ruler.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28e17251-a229-4468-abd8-61dfb2cfe274>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 358

Reference: 2KI 25:23
Text: And when all the captains of the armies, they and their men, heard that the king of Babylon had made Gedaliah governor, there came to Gedaliah to Mizpah, even Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, and Johanan the son of Careah, and Seraiah the son of Tanhumeth the Netophathite, and Jaazaniah the son of a Maachathite, they and their men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b80a1b6-1b18-497a-8ce7-c4762cdb5a83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: 2KI 25:24
Text: And Gedaliah sware to them, and to their men, and said unto them, Fear not to be the servants of the Chaldees: dwell in the land, and serve the king of Babylon; and it shall be well with you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63b537fd-4826-4f80-a853-0fd0430672f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 266

Reference: 2KI 25:25
Text: But it came to pass in the seventh month, that Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, the son of Elishama, of the seed royal, came, and ten men with him, and smote Gedaliah, that he died, and the Jews and the Chaldees that were with him at Mizpah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31f1108d-d22d-4c73-a005-bc4f00fcf589>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: 2KI 25:26
Text: And all the people, both small and great, and the captains of the armies, arose, and came to Egypt: for they were afraid of the Chaldees.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb58c1c5-858a-4eff-a9d1-679162b4c3aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 325

Reference: 2KI 25:27
Text: And it came to pass in the seven and thirtieth year of the captivity of Jehoiachin king of Judah, in the twelfth month, on the seven and twentieth day of the month, that Evilmerodach king of Babylon in the year that he began to reign did lift up the head of Jehoiachin king of Judah out of prison;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9220a74-e770-46db-90dc-f238c30cf91b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 2KI 25:28
Text: And he spake kindly to him, and set his throne above the throne of the kings that were with him in Babylon;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0bfd142-15a9-4c68-b8ee-ecc9a9b6fcde>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: 2KI 25:29
Text: And changed his prison garments: and he did eat bread continually before him all the days of his life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2KI/25/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d87b444a-cd32-43af-b5ac-aaf7ed2ea8f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 2KI 25:30
Text: And his allowance was a continual allowance given him of the king, a daily rate for every day, all the days of his life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
