Text: And the porters were, Shallum, and Akkub, and Talmon, and Ahiman, and their brethren: Shallum was the chief;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0cb302f0-d975-4a09-8c52-0d20dc0211dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 1CH 9:18
Text: Who hitherto waited in the king’s gate eastward: they were porters in the companies of the children of Levi.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad1bf778-f696-40d1-b40d-c61cc62b109f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 309

Reference: 1CH 9:19
Text: And Shallum the son of Kore, the son of Ebiasaph, the son of Korah, and his brethren, of the house of his father, the Korahites, were over the work of the service, keepers of the gates of the tabernacle: and their fathers, being over the host of the LORD, were keepers of the entry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6166ddac-817f-4d79-a45a-0991c777d705>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 1CH 9:20
Text: And Phinehas the son of Eleazar was the ruler over them in time past, and the LORD was with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3591cf05-1e32-4bf9-af0c-b595562c64f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: 1CH 9:21
Text: And Zechariah the son of Meshelemiah was porter of the door of the tabernacle of the congregation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89ccd160-52cb-45d1-af6e-36ff2317895f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: 1CH 9:22
Text: All these which were chosen to be porters in the gates were two hundred and twelve. These were reckoned by their genealogy in their villages, whom David and Samuel the seer did ordain in their set office.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:772b9518-ae32-49a3-b771-29d03db92ad4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 1CH 9:23
Text: So they and their children had the oversight of the gates of the house of the LORD, namely, the house of the tabernacle, by wards.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30c4ba8d-cd8b-4ece-b742-89948fadff29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: 1CH 9:24
Text: In four quarters were the porters, toward the east, west, north, and south.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc53956f-2b9f-4788-af1c-2fb42cc3498d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 1CH 9:25
Text: And their brethren, which were in their villages, were to come after seven days from time to time with them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc8da616-de47-4e0e-b745-c4735f6ace97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 1CH 9:26
Text: For these Levites, the four chief porters, were in their set office, and were over the chambers and treasuries of the house of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87aa0922-7c0e-46f4-9a22-47990b05368a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: 1CH 9:27
Text: And they lodged round about the house of God, because the charge was upon them, and the opening thereof every morning pertained to them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af5a87b0-d1d5-4376-b3c6-22cbfd60d71d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 1CH 9:28
Text: And certain of them had the charge of the ministering vessels, that they should bring them in and out by tale.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49524eb9-bb97-497f-a5de-ed498b444d1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: 1CH 9:29
Text: Some of them also were appointed to oversee the vessels, and all the instruments of the sanctuary, and the fine flour, and the wine, and the oil, and the frankincense, and the spices.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37cb6b1a-0ffe-434b-8861-ebcb7cf65544>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: 1CH 9:30
Text: And some of the sons of the priests made the ointment of the spices.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:547e02ea-d190-4894-adb1-389bd378a9b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: 1CH 9:31
Text: And Mattithiah, one of the Levites, who was the firstborn of Shallum the Korahite, had the set office over the things that were made in the pans.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33a4b3b3-ebaf-4161-b1d3-3b50c14f766b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 1CH 9:32
Text: And other of their brethren, of the sons of the Kohathites, were over the shewbread, to prepare it every sabbath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bdb26b9-e274-4b11-9ffb-5ca09aa6a04a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: 1CH 9:33
Text: And these are the singers, chief of the fathers of the Levites, who remaining in the chambers were free: for they were employed in that work day and night.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00a9c836-05e7-42a7-ba09-51c72b70cf7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 1CH 9:34
Text: These chief fathers of the Levites were chief throughout their generations; these dwelt at Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1981f0c5-4c69-410f-89fa-dc2ddc01c8f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: 1CH 9:35
Text: And in Gibeon dwelt the father of Gibeon, Jehiel, whose wife’s name was Maachah:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48328d86-3426-4477-8091-64745237cc1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: 1CH 9:36
Text: And his firstborn son Abdon, then Zur, and Kish, and Baal, and Ner, and Nadab.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:446ac7eb-5bbc-463a-b1f8-225d1f0b5df5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: 1CH 9:37
Text: And Gedor, and Ahio, and Zechariah, and Mikloth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58199b54-8049-4ceb-b6ec-7079902a0460>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: 1CH 9:38
Text: And Mikloth begat Shimeam. And they also dwelt with their brethren at Jerusalem, over against their brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca95c326-572b-4883-b4be-eb72b1359836>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 1CH 9:39
Text: And Ner begat Kish; and Kish begat Saul; and Saul begat Jonathan, and Malchishua, and Abinadab, and Eshbaal.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:adcf1676-793a-467c-b1a8-8efa6f9dbf4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: 1CH 9:40
Text: And the son of Jonathan was Meribbaal: and Meribbaal begat Micah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:872eda2a-73fc-4a6f-bac2-82b607e31158>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: 1CH 9:41
Text: And the sons of Micah were, Pithon, and Melech, and Tahrea, and Ahaz.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01638ee2-d960-4af5-b5cc-9bbdc55bbf92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: 1CH 9:42
Text: And Ahaz begat Jarah; and Jarah begat Alemeth, and Azmaveth, and Zimri; and Zimri begat Moza;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:373b099e-9287-4800-8d99-d7fe36b19837>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: 1CH 9:43
Text: And Moza begat Binea; and Rephaiah his son, Eleasah his son, Azel his son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/9/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:332b4d96-ef2a-487a-8afa-b5b614a948fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 1CH 9:44
Text: And Azel had six sons, whose names are these, Azrikam, Bocheru, and Ishmael, and Sheariah, and Obadiah, and Hanan: these were the sons of Azel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/10/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fc64207-e7c3-4194-831e-74ff924bc98f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 1CH 10:1
Text: Now the Philistines fought against Israel; and the men of Israel fled from before the Philistines, and fell down slain in mount Gilboa.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/10/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38e6ddcc-64bf-4df9-923a-ff7f1449fad5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 1CH 10:2
Text: And the Philistines followed hard after Saul, and after his sons; and the Philistines slew Jonathan, and Abinadab, and Malchishua, the sons of Saul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/10/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5820f5c0-33cd-40e4-99ba-28b3419d05ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: 1CH 10:3
Text: And the battle went sore against Saul, and the archers hit him, and he was wounded of the archers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/10/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c6aa953-2028-4ae5-b0e7-434abbd4203d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: 1CH 10:4
Text: Then said Saul to his armourbearer, Draw thy sword, and thrust me through therewith; lest these uncircumcised come and abuse me. But his armourbearer would not; for he was sore afraid. So Saul took a sword, and fell upon it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/10/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4428e1bd-a20a-418a-a9ff-881014493a98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: 1CH 10:5
Text: And when his armourbearer saw that Saul was dead, he fell likewise on the sword, and died.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/10/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce6d8eca-de1d-4607-83e5-2135f747cae1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: 1CH 10:6
Text: So Saul died, and his three sons, and all his house died together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/10/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ece280f6-cd50-46d3-96af-34e067f294c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: 1CH 10:7
Text: And when all the men of Israel that were in the valley saw that they fled, and that Saul and his sons were dead, then they forsook their cities, and fled: and the Philistines came and dwelt in them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/10/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9eaeef95-ba90-4679-9e88-249a8bce026d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: 1CH 10:8
Text: And it came to pass on the morrow, when the Philistines came to strip the slain, that they found Saul and his sons fallen in mount Gilboa.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/10/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb57528b-f06e-4e23-9bef-f28730912d42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: 1CH 10:9
Text: And when they had stripped him, they took his head, and his armour, and sent into the land of the Philistines round about, to carry tidings unto their idols, and to the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/10/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7890c17-0de8-4279-8fc0-5bc237161a1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: 1CH 10:10
Text: And they put his armour in the house of their gods, and fastened his head in the temple of Dagon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/10/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a955053-ad59-440c-bc7b-80905f905de0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: 1CH 10:11
Text: And when all Jabeshgilead heard all that the Philistines had done to Saul,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/10/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9f2e84a-63e2-43b9-a949-99d6d8436c8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: 1CH 10:12
Text: They arose, all the valiant men, and took away the body of Saul, and the bodies of his sons, and brought them to Jabesh, and buried their bones under the oak in Jabesh, and fasted seven days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/10/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7c72063-5d20-4160-b271-8f52f09eac38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: 1CH 10:13
Text: So Saul died for his transgression which he committed against the LORD, even against the word of the LORD, which he kept not, and also for asking counsel of one that had a familiar spirit, to enquire of it;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/10/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d749ed74-6dab-42c0-827e-8ad570810d75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 1CH 10:14
Text: And enquired not of the LORD: therefore he slew him, and turned the kingdom unto David the son of Jesse.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a6c58c9-6cf0-44e1-a4c5-1e1f06eb4e9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: 1CH 11:1
Text: Then all Israel gathered themselves to David unto Hebron, saying, Behold, we are thy bone and thy flesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d492a70a-aa2e-4ff2-81d9-2f6eccb4a025>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: 1CH 11:2
Text: And moreover in time past, even when Saul was king, thou wast he that leddest out and broughtest in Israel: and the LORD thy God said unto thee, Thou shalt feed my people Israel, and thou shalt be ruler over my people Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a75d3846-51ea-43ee-95b4-39e0a1db37c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: 1CH 11:3
Text: Therefore came all the elders of Israel to the king to Hebron; and David made a covenant with them in Hebron before the LORD; and they anointed David king over Israel, according to the word of the LORD by Samuel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fae7bda9-96d3-4bf1-be8b-45f3f6620e60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 1CH 11:4
Text: And David and all Israel went to Jerusalem, which is Jebus; where the Jebusites were, the inhabitants of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae50403a-d5dd-45ff-beee-6b04fdc63ab2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 1CH 11:5
Text: And the inhabitants of Jebus said to David, Thou shalt not come hither. Nevertheless David took the castle of Zion, which is the city of David.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a313699-2104-4440-8c4c-de9beb185b69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: 1CH 11:6
Text: And David said, Whosoever smiteth the Jebusites first shall be chief and captain. So Joab the son of Zeruiah went first up, and was chief.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e4ab644-bb06-4a53-99dc-be5604ecece6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: 1CH 11:7
Text: And David dwelt in the castle; therefore they called it the city of David.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12e74444-8b96-4078-93aa-9e5323cfeabe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: 1CH 11:8
Text: And he built the city round about, even from Millo round about: and Joab repaired the rest of the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7507095-7326-44da-979b-8bdd1ab6b9e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: 1CH 11:9
Text: So David waxed greater and greater: for the LORD of hosts was with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:415d2fa0-f05e-44d2-8f0a-2707b7ec45a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: 1CH 11:10
Text: These also are the chief of the mighty men whom David had, who strengthened themselves with him in his kingdom, and with all Israel, to make him king, according to the word of the LORD concerning Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0f599d3-7998-49c5-8245-b0a39c7faef0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: 1CH 11:11
Text: And this is the number of the mighty men whom David had; Jashobeam, an Hachmonite, the chief of the captains: he lifted up his spear against three hundred slain by him at one time.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed112eea-9266-4a2b-a8e5-ed9d187fb7dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: 1CH 11:12
Text: And after him was Eleazar the son of Dodo, the Ahohite, who was one of the three mighties.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2606a404-a996-420a-a899-14e3f2157258>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: 1CH 11:13
Text: He was with David at Pasdammim, and there the Philistines were gathered together to battle, where was a parcel of ground full of barley; and the people fled from before the Philistines.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:300ea0ce-31c3-4944-a056-38f982e9014c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: 1CH 11:14
Text: And they set themselves in the midst of that parcel, and delivered it, and slew the Philistines; and the LORD saved them by a great deliverance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e134edf7-fe3e-4be0-b2e3-09958448586e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 1CH 11:15
Text: Now three of the thirty captains went down to the rock to David, into the cave of Adullam; and the host of the Philistines encamped in the valley of Rephaim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ff2d742-27dd-489d-b67d-d8cad09cff88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: 1CH 11:16
Text: And David was then in the hold, and the Philistines’ garrison was then at Bethlehem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ec38051-7b09-4569-bd73-4e0835fcc740>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 1CH 11:17
Text: And David longed, and said, Oh that one would give me drink of the water of the well of Bethlehem, that is at the gate!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fee02538-d697-4c33-bf42-574bad8ad38a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: 1CH 11:18
Text: And the three brake through the host of the Philistines, and drew water out of the well of Bethlehem, that was by the gate, and took it, and brought it to David: but David would not drink of it, but poured it out to the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b620baa4-f758-4c83-8b03-27e25a1931ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 290

Reference: 1CH 11:19
Text: And said, My God forbid it me, that I should do this thing: shall I drink the blood of these men that have put their lives in jeopardy? for with the jeopardy of their lives they brought it. Therefore he would not drink it. These things did these three mightiest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c4b6161-bbdd-4bad-a4bd-7b7b748abcdf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: 1CH 11:20
Text: And Abishai the brother of Joab, he was chief of the three: for lifting up his spear against three hundred, he slew them, and had a name among the three.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b9061bb-e91b-4ee4-a67a-579c116b359f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 1CH 11:21
Text: Of the three, he was more honourable than the two; for he was their captain: howbeit he attained not to the first three.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff45a286-bcb4-4c70-b7f5-1e1110c6a849>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: 1CH 11:22
Text: Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, the son of a valiant man of Kabzeel, who had done many acts; he slew two lionlike men of Moab: also he went down and slew a lion in a pit in a snowy day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a10c226-99e8-457f-97cd-3eba0433b029>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 282

Reference: 1CH 11:23
Text: And he slew an Egyptian, a man of great stature, five cubits high; and in the Egyptian’s hand was a spear like a weaver’s beam; and he went down to him with a staff, and plucked the spear out of the Egyptian’s hand, and slew him with his own spear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/11/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
