Reference: 1CH 12:16
Text: And there came of the children of Benjamin and Judah to the hold unto David.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56c5f9fe-0fae-4272-a9ea-7d08ec95f997>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 312

Reference: 1CH 12:17
Text: And David went out to meet them, and answered and said unto them, If ye be come peaceably unto me to help me, mine heart shall be knit unto you: but if ye be come to betray me to mine enemies, seeing there is no wrong in mine hands, the God of our fathers look thereon, and rebuke it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:248600a0-0280-4301-ae01-91f3a654d9ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 308

Reference: 1CH 12:18
Text: Then the spirit came upon Amasai, who was chief of the captains, and he said, Thine are we, David, and on thy side, thou son of Jesse: peace, peace be unto thee, and peace be to thine helpers; for thy God helpeth thee. Then David received them, and made them captains of the band.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0fab1d6-b508-49d1-aea4-c52ef6a3fae7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 287

Reference: 1CH 12:19
Text: And there fell some of Manasseh to David, when he came with the Philistines against Saul to battle: but they helped them not: for the lords of the Philistines upon advisement sent him away, saying, He will fall to his master Saul to the jeopardy of our heads.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb003ab2-9fad-436e-b744-49403d2b89ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: 1CH 12:20
Text: As he went to Ziklag, there fell to him of Manasseh, Adnah, and Jozabad, and Jediael, and Michael, and Jozabad, and Elihu, and Zilthai, captains of the thousands that were of Manasseh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15a54c4c-139a-4896-90eb-e157ce314939>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: 1CH 12:21
Text: And they helped David against the band of the rovers: for they were all mighty men of valour, and were captains in the host.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a03e9fa3-e479-409a-bd34-a3b31137b4b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 1CH 12:22
Text: For at that time day by day there came to David to help him, until it was a great host, like the host of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c98f177-205d-4e52-b120-0f38f42ab820>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 1CH 12:23
Text: And these are the numbers of the bands that were ready armed to the war, and came to David to Hebron, to turn the kingdom of Saul to him, according to the word of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:937fc895-59f3-4175-b429-89d5dcc38843>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 1CH 12:24
Text: The children of Judah that bare shield and spear were six thousand and eight hundred, ready armed to the war.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c68fac3f-5da9-46f5-becf-92a5d1eebc6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: 1CH 12:25
Text: Of the children of Simeon, mighty men of valour for the war, seven thousand and one hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7374c6a1-f1eb-4cad-bec6-ffa3b88c4e5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: 1CH 12:26
Text: Of the children of Levi four thousand and six hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c39167f-da37-444b-8c75-a02efcf46a8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: 1CH 12:27
Text: And Jehoiada was the leader of the Aaronites, and with him were three thousand and seven hundred;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9789883c-274b-4465-8af8-5aa8d6b3a2ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 1CH 12:28
Text: And Zadok, a young man mighty of valour, and of his father’s house twenty and two captains.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cae0804d-0326-4a28-bbea-dbbdb664838c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: 1CH 12:29
Text: And of the children of Benjamin, the kindred of Saul, three thousand: for hitherto the greatest part of them had kept the ward of the house of Saul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6b43650-6cbb-4170-b3db-72ad8ac1b91e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 1CH 12:30
Text: And of the children of Ephraim twenty thousand and eight hundred, mighty men of valour, famous throughout the house of their fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ffb8ec4-d42d-4662-8137-7486099e02b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: 1CH 12:31
Text: And of the half tribe of Manasseh eighteen thousand, which were expressed by name, to come and make David king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b2a5bf4-fcbd-463d-9d0b-0ac77f589f3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: 1CH 12:32
Text: And of the children of Issachar, which were men that had understanding of the times, to know what Israel ought to do; the heads of them were two hundred; and all their brethren were at their commandment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9341514-578c-49c3-828a-99a3cbe53491>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: 1CH 12:33
Text: Of Zebulun, such as went forth to battle, expert in war, with all instruments of war, fifty thousand, which could keep rank: they were not of double heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cba02425-87d2-4fa4-8516-9c5b27acf978>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 1CH 12:34
Text: And of Naphtali a thousand captains, and with them with shield and spear thirty and seven thousand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dededc34-692e-450f-a57a-65298d7dd93b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: 1CH 12:35
Text: And of the Danites expert in war twenty and eight thousand and six hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57f4bb53-a386-4024-aa5e-74be53ff7ff1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: 1CH 12:36
Text: And of Asher, such as went forth to battle, expert in war, forty thousand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9bd67e0-72b4-4098-820f-9498f29d0261>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: 1CH 12:37
Text: And on the other side of Jordan, of the Reubenites, and the Gadites, and of the half tribe of Manasseh, with all manner of instruments of war for the battle, an hundred and twenty thousand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b85e24ad-1213-4785-bbd3-5ed92bd6110e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: 1CH 12:38
Text: All these men of war, that could keep rank, came with a perfect heart to Hebron, to make David king over all Israel: and all the rest also of Israel were of one heart to make David king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32ac999e-53f4-4492-ba33-86f7ea4e3c74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: 1CH 12:39
Text: And there they were with David three days, eating and drinking: for their brethren had prepared for them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/12/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:703e5848-648b-4af6-86cf-b798b62a4aac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 308

Reference: 1CH 12:40
Text: Moreover they that were nigh them, even unto Issachar and Zebulun and Naphtali, brought bread on asses, and on camels, and on mules, and on oxen, and meat, meal, cakes of figs, and bunches of raisins, and wine, and oil, and oxen, and sheep abundantly: for there was joy in Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/13/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f6a2ba5-4b16-4c2a-8d17-303b3f1cf174>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: 1CH 13:1
Text: And David consulted with the captains of thousands and hundreds, and with every leader.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/13/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b0e39a5-ea68-453c-a45b-9146d3b15d66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 357

Reference: 1CH 13:2
Text: And David said unto all the congregation of Israel, If it seem good unto you, and that it be of the LORD our God, let us send abroad unto our brethren every where, that are left in all the land of Israel, and with them also to the priests and Levites which are in their cities and suburbs, that they may gather themselves unto us:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/13/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9aeb1ae-741b-4339-a2af-94d8005d5937>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: 1CH 13:3
Text: And let us bring again the ark of our God to us: for we enquired not at it in the days of Saul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/13/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6091698f-2699-4f52-a425-eea950b4f239>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: 1CH 13:4
Text: And all the congregation said that they would do so: for the thing was right in the eyes of all the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/13/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:503841ed-9126-4770-a1e3-1d713d90ec4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: 1CH 13:5
Text: So David gathered all Israel together, from Shihor of Egypt even unto the entering of Hemath, to bring the ark of God from Kirjathjearim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/13/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67c65de5-ffe6-41da-8833-bc00e0ff9e46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: 1CH 13:6
Text: And David went up, and all Israel, to Baalah, that is, to Kirjathjearim, which belonged to Judah, to bring up thence the ark of God the LORD, that dwelleth between the cherubims, whose name is called on it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/13/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78b4bdf7-93ba-4744-8405-a67259162c24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: 1CH 13:7
Text: And they carried the ark of God in a new cart out of the house of Abinadab: and Uzza and Ahio drave the cart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/13/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e384deb-73f4-4767-a7c7-c0bc2299a405>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: 1CH 13:8
Text: And David and all Israel played before God with all their might, and with singing, and with harps, and with psalteries, and with timbrels, and with cymbals, and with trumpets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/13/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac23591f-8924-4bb2-9d62-2d5b4a07d0f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: 1CH 13:9
Text: And when they came unto the threshingfloor of Chidon, Uzza put forth his hand to hold the ark; for the oxen stumbled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/13/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b201966-afc3-426d-a7ad-d0ab86b5d6cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: 1CH 13:10
Text: And the anger of the LORD was kindled against Uzza, and he smote him, because he put his hand to the ark: and there he died before God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/13/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9512a0b6-390f-47e7-be15-4c0965542077>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 1CH 13:11
Text: And David was displeased, because the LORD had made a breach upon Uzza: wherefore that place is called Perezuzza to this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/13/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7eb70dc-c2d8-4ad5-9d3a-38e3021d0458>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: 1CH 13:12
Text: And David was afraid of God that day, saying, How shall I bring the ark of God home to me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/13/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dcc76811-64b2-43dc-b2d4-166d3b27b734>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 1CH 13:13
Text: So David brought not the ark home to himself to the city of David, but carried it aside into the house of Obededom the Gittite.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/13/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57d554b8-ed86-4e13-a1c7-c4e0f4308d69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 1CH 13:14
Text: And the ark of God remained with the family of Obededom in his house three months. And the LORD blessed the house of Obededom, and all that he had.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/14/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:344ab60a-15ab-48e3-a715-51590dc028c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 1CH 14:1
Text: Now Hiram king of Tyre sent messengers to David, and timber of cedars, with masons and carpenters, to build him an house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/14/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a5759c0-f8f8-49ec-a14b-3bf0689b0798>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: 1CH 14:2
Text: And David perceived that the LORD had confirmed him king over Israel, for his kingdom was lifted up on high, because of his people Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/14/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94d4df34-0a9b-4b14-99e0-2e2cc71bafba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: 1CH 14:3
Text: And David took more wives at Jerusalem: and David begat more sons and daughters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/14/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31b85459-44e9-4cce-89f9-6c422b724b1e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 1CH 14:4
Text: Now these are the names of his children which he had in Jerusalem; Shammua, and Shobab, Nathan, and Solomon,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/14/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db0e9e94-1f43-47c5-9637-c92ef3415673>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 63

Reference: 1CH 14:5
Text: And Ibhar, and Elishua, and Elpalet,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/14/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2f80d11-c293-481a-9ba0-ccd023646e8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 61

Reference: 1CH 14:6
Text: And Nogah, and Nepheg, and Japhia,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/14/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd8af69c-be04-4036-8176-343b8435bb56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 69

Reference: 1CH 14:7
Text: And Elishama, and Beeliada, and Eliphalet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/14/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8a6913c-c0ab-48e3-8448-7a693d564734>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: 1CH 14:8
Text: And when the Philistines heard that David was anointed king over all Israel, all the Philistines went up to seek David. And David heard of it, and went out against them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/14/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38724e4d-9afb-4ed6-b6e1-8d0abf58ea9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: 1CH 14:9
Text: And the Philistines came and spread themselves in the valley of Rephaim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/14/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:667ac2cd-a69e-40d7-bd1b-5456baa3a1c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: 1CH 14:10
Text: And David enquired of God, saying, Shall I go up against the Philistines? And wilt thou deliver them into mine hand? And the LORD said unto him, Go up; for I will deliver them into thine hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/14/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0dd8834e-4b4c-4e19-9ecb-22be765b8565>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: 1CH 14:11
Text: So they came up to Baalperazim; and David smote them there. Then David said, God hath broken in upon mine enemies by mine hand like the breaking forth of waters: therefore they called the name of that place Baalperazim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/14/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38d9b197-d69f-4288-b9ee-2c3b8ebbe494>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: 1CH 14:12
Text: And when they had left their gods there, David gave a commandment, and they were burned with fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/14/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89cbacf9-1997-47b3-86c0-4e4497a7d192>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: 1CH 14:13
Text: And the Philistines yet again spread themselves abroad in the valley.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/14/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d831be6-680a-4105-a203-4b3cb1bcc6a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: 1CH 14:14
Text: Therefore David enquired again of God; and God said unto him, Go not up after them; turn away from them, and come upon them over against the mulberry trees.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/14/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:017022e8-48e3-4c34-af3b-7f3f336b6164>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: 1CH 14:15
Text: And it shall be, when thou shalt hear a sound of going in the tops of the mulberry trees, that then thou shalt go out to battle: for God is gone forth before thee to smite the host of the Philistines.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/14/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3ece451-0a98-4453-ac4b-207bfca3f843>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: 1CH 14:16
Text: David therefore did as God commanded him: and they smote the host of the Philistines from Gibeon even to Gazer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/14/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:796fd208-7273-4add-bde8-4e741f17c8ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: 1CH 14:17
Text: And the fame of David went out into all lands; and the LORD brought the fear of him upon all nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:addfd81c-73b0-4eb8-bc8d-66ca6124d339>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: 1CH 15:1
Text: And David made him houses in the city of David, and prepared a place for the ark of God, and pitched for it a tent.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7415c655-877c-44aa-89a9-1fc66aed0518>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 1CH 15:2
Text: Then David said, None ought to carry the ark of God but the Levites: for them hath the LORD chosen to carry the ark of God, and to minister unto him for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f97cf4fe-917c-4eac-9826-60588ce64380>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 1CH 15:3
Text: And David gathered all Israel together to Jerusalem, to bring up the ark of the LORD unto his place, which he had prepared for it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f609e961-4b21-41c5-b0fc-7a63c335f0a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: 1CH 15:4
Text: And David assembled the children of Aaron, and the Levites:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:876b42a2-9bfa-4ddd-8fbb-4868bf32cc1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: 1CH 15:5
Text: Of the sons of Kohath; Uriel the chief, and his brethren an hundred and twenty:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3fb2bc0-8090-44c7-a986-95be62181788>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: 1CH 15:6
Text: Of the sons of Merari; Asaiah the chief, and his brethren two hundred and twenty:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3baa61c0-abfa-4461-be82-4028ee64579a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: 1CH 15:7
Text: Of the sons of Gershom; Joel the chief and his brethren an hundred and thirty:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26621c6f-e9f0-421b-950e-643140ccdc4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: 1CH 15:8
Text: Of the sons of Elizaphan; Shemaiah the chief, and his brethren two hundred:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7132b89f-75f8-4011-9ea9-dfb7eb33c198>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: 1CH 15:9
Text: Of the sons of Hebron; Eliel the chief, and his brethren fourscore:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7076916e-bc82-447d-a521-281d927dfd6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: 1CH 15:10
Text: Of the sons of Uzziel; Amminadab the chief, and his brethren an hundred and twelve.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9dd53b2d-848e-48ec-b1fe-a045f6c03bc2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: 1CH 15:11
Text: And David called for Zadok and Abiathar the priests, and for the Levites, for Uriel, Asaiah, and Joel, Shemaiah, and Eliel, and Amminadab,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ff1ac7d-3258-499a-a3f1-02185700b0f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: 1CH 15:12
Text: And said unto them, Ye are the chief of the fathers of the Levites: sanctify yourselves, both ye and your brethren, that ye may bring up the ark of the LORD God of Israel unto the place that I have prepared for it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63cf16fe-5584-450d-ad85-eccef8f5506f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 1CH 15:13
Text: For because ye did it not at the first, the LORD our God made a breach upon us, for that we sought him not after the due order.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee34f8e3-066e-4d6d-ae0a-6522f477385d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 1CH 15:14
Text: So the priests and the Levites sanctified themselves to bring up the ark of the LORD God of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4cb8d14f-47a2-4236-9c79-100da5af617e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 1CH 15:15
Text: And the children of the Levites bare the ark of God upon their shoulders with the staves thereon, as Moses commanded according to the word of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:328ddb23-e1a2-4f3d-89ed-382a9871c3e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: 1CH 15:16
Text: And David spake to the chief of the Levites to appoint their brethren to be the singers with instruments of musick, psalteries and harps and cymbals, sounding, by lifting up the voice with joy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:104767f0-cafc-4d5e-9168-838676de5c63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: 1CH 15:17
Text: So the Levites appointed Heman the son of Joel; and of his brethren, Asaph the son of Berechiah; and of the sons of Merari their brethren, Ethan the son of Kushaiah;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48a002a6-5077-4d55-8934-8d927359fba0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: 1CH 15:18
Text: And with them their brethren of the second degree, Zechariah, Ben, and Jaaziel, and Shemiramoth, and Jehiel, and Unni, Eliab, and Benaiah, and Maaseiah, and Mattithiah, and Elipheleh, and Mikneiah, and Obededom, and Jeiel, the porters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb19094f-b626-4e0a-91c4-989975b80561>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: 1CH 15:19
Text: So the singers, Heman, Asaph, and Ethan, were appointed to sound with cymbals of brass;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:382463d3-bb4f-4561-86c7-b58ad95e9aca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 1CH 15:20
Text: And Zechariah, and Aziel, and Shemiramoth, and Jehiel, and Unni, and Eliab, and Maaseiah, and Benaiah, with psalteries on Alamoth;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:221950fb-4bba-4e93-94cf-178c8d26c249>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 1CH 15:21
Text: And Mattithiah, and Elipheleh, and Mikneiah, and Obededom, and Jeiel, and Azaziah, with harps on the Sheminith to excel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5449e745-bcf7-47a8-8fe9-e756f7db8a59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 1CH 15:22
Text: And Chenaniah, chief of the Levites, was for song: he instructed about the song, because he was skilful.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc6f02fb-74f0-4fb3-91a5-9959b3b6ba3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: 1CH 15:23
Text: And Berechiah and Elkanah were doorkeepers for the ark.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7a929a0-9699-4054-85ee-5e57f12afb34>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: 1CH 15:24
Text: And Shebaniah, and Jehoshaphat, and Nethaneel, and Amasai, and Zechariah, and Benaiah, and Eliezer, the priests, did blow with the trumpets before the ark of God: and Obededom and Jehiah were doorkeepers for the ark.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d80c6af-abc1-42fb-b47f-f1162bfd860c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 1CH 15:25
Text: So David, and the elders of Israel, and the captains over thousands, went to bring up the ark of the covenant of the LORD out of the house of Obededom with joy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1319e8e-3b55-4a52-b567-83ecc981eb9f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: 1CH 15:26
Text: And it came to pass, when God helped the Levites that bare the ark of the covenant of the LORD, that they offered seven bullocks and seven rams.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e66d5df8-14e8-4a07-ae9c-70376da7ff11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: 1CH 15:27
Text: And David was clothed with a robe of fine linen, and all the Levites that bare the ark, and the singers, and Chenaniah the master of the song with the singers: David also had upon him an ephod of linen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e51d325a-78a8-4a93-85c3-607a86cffe9e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: 1CH 15:28
Text: Thus all Israel brought up the ark of the covenant of the LORD with shouting, and with sound of the cornet, and with trumpets, and with cymbals, making a noise with psalteries and harps.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/15/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c711120b-d979-4f33-aa38-e4a20e32740a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: 1CH 15:29
Text: And it came to pass, as the ark of the covenant of the LORD came to the city of David, that Michal, the daughter of Saul looking out at a window saw king David dancing and playing: and she despised him in her heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e29597a-0bad-40f3-85a4-5d140079efcf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: 1CH 16:1
Text: So they brought the ark of God, and set it in the midst of the tent that David had pitched for it: and they offered burnt sacrifices and peace offerings before God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d627157-ad26-487c-b8e2-077d89f758a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 1CH 16:2
Text: And when David had made an end of offering the burnt offerings and the peace offerings, he blessed the people in the name of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa026b54-1c8b-49df-88e2-591ecc565907>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 1CH 16:3
Text: And he dealt to every one of Israel, both man and woman, to every one a loaf of bread, and a good piece of flesh, and a flagon of wine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5cc1e99-a113-4890-95cb-ead99652f070>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: 1CH 16:4
Text: And he appointed certain of the Levites to minister before the ark of the LORD, and to record, and to thank and praise the LORD God of Israel:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b18a5ae2-b2b6-4f09-ac5f-ef99542df961>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: 1CH 16:5
Text: Asaph the chief, and next to him Zechariah, Jeiel, and Shemiramoth, and Jehiel, and Mattithiah, and Eliab, and Benaiah, and Obededom: and Jeiel with psalteries and with harps; but Asaph made a sound with cymbals;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73c5c2e1-05cd-48a8-a9a6-2d0c6b5edbba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: 1CH 16:6
Text: Benaiah also and Jahaziel the priests with trumpets continually before the ark of the covenant of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c061c094-7a99-4faf-b641-165563fa0573>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 1CH 16:7
Text: Then on that day David delivered first this psalm to thank the LORD into the hand of Asaph and his brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56d38865-6dc3-40d4-ad68-458950349e13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: 1CH 16:8
Text: Give thanks unto the LORD, call upon his name, make known his deeds among the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e44c761d-91f4-40cf-a01a-dde6b67234f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: 1CH 16:9
Text: Sing unto him, sing psalms unto him, talk ye of all his wondrous works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:528fac16-5b1e-4487-83a8-832361db1679>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: 1CH 16:10
Text: Glory ye in his holy name: let the heart of them rejoice that seek the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d821b5a-e6ee-497b-8886-32c6fb3d50ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: 1CH 16:11
Text: Seek the LORD and his strength, seek his face continually.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e01cf480-06e4-420b-be5c-b04be3958b09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 1CH 16:12
Text: Remember his marvellous works that he hath done, his wonders, and the judgments of his mouth;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe56367b-a5cb-4a75-bbac-ca9c3a70cd73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: 1CH 16:13
Text: O ye seed of Israel his servant, ye children of Jacob, his chosen ones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb076870-e01f-406d-b195-ed61257dc4a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: 1CH 16:14
Text: He is the LORD our God; his judgments are in all the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b996d24f-14d7-468c-9994-2e0d19220172>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: 1CH 16:15
Text: Be ye mindful always of his covenant; the word which he commanded to a thousand generations;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d6c56e7-cfa9-4387-b5a0-0825000a6013>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: 1CH 16:16
Text: Even of the covenant which he made with Abraham, and of his oath unto Isaac;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99152980-d9c8-4530-8151-3a5e02150a22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: 1CH 16:17
Text: And hath confirmed the same to Jacob for a law, and to Israel for an everlasting covenant,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8fbe4b07-5f04-47dd-abd8-ecf16743f5c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: 1CH 16:18
Text: Saying, Unto thee will I give the land of Canaan, the lot of your inheritance;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:937278a0-8f4e-462a-abbe-0447963a9865>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: 1CH 16:19
Text: When ye were but few, even a few, and strangers in it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f3f92b8-8475-47ef-98c0-f9acd3db918e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: 1CH 16:20
Text: And when they went from nation to nation, and from one kingdom to another people;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2a10b29-8d34-4d59-bbe3-f764165c425f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: 1CH 16:21
Text: He suffered no man to do them wrong: yea, he reproved kings for their sakes,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:589205ad-d975-49ac-965a-283b8963c424>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: 1CH 16:22
Text: Saying, Touch not mine anointed, and do my prophets no harm.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95c7cebe-e0f6-4381-933d-a9f80ffb4c0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: 1CH 16:23
Text: Sing unto the LORD, all the earth; shew forth from day to day his salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34a05c44-b431-4ef9-8213-95cf977912d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: 1CH 16:24
Text: Declare his glory among the heathen; his marvellous works among all nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ad72fa0-7595-4a52-b3f0-52675ef6aa82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: 1CH 16:25
Text: For great is the LORD, and greatly to be praised: he also is to be feared above all gods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4926e956-b456-435f-9119-9ebdb99ad756>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: 1CH 16:26
Text: For all the gods of the people are idols: but the LORD made the heavens.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8fc9406e-988d-4c4a-9483-398a321e7e76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: 1CH 16:27
Text: Glory and honour are in his presence; strength and gladness are in his place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e119f263-8a6f-4a70-bc0d-8c83bb96e46e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: 1CH 16:28
Text: Give unto the LORD, ye kindreds of the people, give unto the LORD glory and strength.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5d369b4-b4c8-4ab4-a52d-27779852038b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: 1CH 16:29
Text: Give unto the LORD the glory due unto his name: bring an offering, and come before him: worship the LORD in the beauty of holiness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2846c0d-4dec-45f1-8b72-0aa4b17414b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: 1CH 16:30
Text: Fear before him, all the earth: the world also shall be stable, that it be not moved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8917a236-783e-40a4-8b5f-13cb6dab4857>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: 1CH 16:31
Text: Let the heavens be glad, and let the earth rejoice: and let men say among the nations, The LORD reigneth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:456af6d6-31ef-4654-a2f4-5394d15deae6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: 1CH 16:32
Text: Let the sea roar, and the fulness thereof: let the fields rejoice, and all that is therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b79d21af-941c-4537-9f0e-4f8d6b57d0ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: 1CH 16:33
Text: Then shall the trees of the wood sing out at the presence of the LORD, because he cometh to judge the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f27ca1a-8e4c-463b-91dc-39e96c115ab2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: 1CH 16:34
Text: O give thanks unto the LORD; for he is good; for his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4145fb18-5c85-4e82-947c-e0871c3c69dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: 1CH 16:35
Text: And say ye, Save us, O God of our salvation, and gather us together, and deliver us from the heathen, that we may give thanks to thy holy name, and glory in thy praise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89c5872c-4057-4f90-90e6-91208c327782>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: 1CH 16:36
Text: Blessed be the LORD God of Israel for ever and ever. And all the people said, Amen, and praised the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bc5701b-4228-4d90-9f50-d14eeec172a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: 1CH 16:37
Text: So he left there before the ark of the covenant of the LORD Asaph and his brethren, to minister before the ark continually, as every day’s work required:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27cb3121-6557-4770-b7ca-813c28d711e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: 1CH 16:38
Text: And Obededom with their brethren, threescore and eight; Obededom also the son of Jeduthun and Hosah to be porters:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ab35698-da7f-4604-822a-e85d6b645073>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: 1CH 16:39
Text: And Zadok the priest, and his brethren the priests, before the tabernacle of the LORD in the high place that was at Gibeon,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f373978b-9515-4e29-b90e-d18ba77001b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: 1CH 16:40
Text: To offer burnt offerings unto the LORD upon the altar of the burnt offering continually morning and evening, and to do according to all that is written in the law of the LORD, which he commanded Israel;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f1fc38b-b36d-4045-8c0f-da06d218b97e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 1CH 16:41
Text: And with them Heman and Jeduthun, and the rest that were chosen, who were expressed by name, to give thanks to the LORD, because his mercy endureth for ever;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b1360e5-0a12-45af-a917-b42fa48a5615>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: 1CH 16:42
Text: And with them Heman and Jeduthun with trumpets and cymbals for those that should make a sound, and with musical instruments of God. And the sons of Jeduthun were porters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/16/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3591ed5c-2560-49d7-b9c2-01d4206d6dac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: 1CH 16:43
Text: And all the people departed every man to his house: and David returned to bless his house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:200d26ab-5a33-4b19-8743-cde35f005ae4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: 1CH 17:1
Text: Now it came to pass, as David sat in his house, that David said to Nathan the prophet, Lo, I dwell in an house of cedars, but the ark of the covenant of the LORD remaineth under curtains.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17bfa79d-847f-4edf-a3c9-d9b0ff8c2cd4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: 1CH 17:2
Text: Then Nathan said unto David, Do all that is in thine heart; for God is with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb02b17f-8cf3-4a33-a448-610643970629>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: 1CH 17:3
Text: And it came to pass the same night, that the word of God came to Nathan, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55a43b0d-de65-4567-ad78-c4efd261e341>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 1CH 17:4
Text: Go and tell David my servant, Thus saith the LORD, Thou shalt not build me an house to dwell in:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30b0d4c7-382c-4520-bcc9-3920f8cac7ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: 1CH 17:5
Text: For I have not dwelt in an house since the day that I brought up Israel unto this day; but have gone from tent to tent, and from one tabernacle to another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32b5e486-875e-4991-9d1a-95cbd2bec7f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: 1CH 17:6
Text: Wheresoever I have walked with all Israel, spake I a word to any of the judges of Israel, whom I commanded to feed my people, saying, Why have ye not built me an house of cedars?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a2f8371-7f85-4b9d-aaa8-99a6df08eea4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: 1CH 17:7
Text: Now therefore thus shalt thou say unto my servant David, Thus saith the LORD of hosts, I took thee from the sheepcote, even from following the sheep, that thou shouldest be ruler over my people Israel:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed5faa0a-7d60-4258-81b9-ec8bd029d5b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: 1CH 17:8
Text: And I have been with thee whithersoever thou hast walked, and have cut off all thine enemies from before thee, and have made thee a name like the name of the great men that are in the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c85e1cc1-f866-482f-a112-a3b71ae4f766>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: 1CH 17:9
Text: Also I will ordain a place for my people Israel, and will plant them, and they shall dwell in their place, and shall be moved no more; neither shall the children of wickedness waste them any more, as at the beginning,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bdfccbf6-acab-40d8-9104-48fb67c9c485>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: 1CH 17:10
Text: And since the time that I commanded judges to be over my people Israel. Moreover I will subdue all thine enemies. Furthermore I tell thee that the LORD will build thee an house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40be1981-44f3-4e5f-800e-f06779b06981>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: 1CH 17:11
Text: And it shall come to pass, when thy days be expired that thou must go to be with thy fathers, that I will raise up thy seed after thee, which shall be of thy sons; and I will establish his kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa7d2044-3b39-4417-b64f-67df65e0fd60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: 1CH 17:12
Text: He shall build me an house, and I will stablish his throne for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07a4b3ee-68d0-4b38-8db4-ac7299d14acd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 1CH 17:13
Text: I will be his father, and he shall be my son: and I will not take my mercy away from him, as I took it from him that was before thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e6306c6-62c7-4bc4-b3fb-bc6e60d86efe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 1CH 17:14
Text: But I will settle him in mine house and in my kingdom for ever: and his throne shall be established for evermore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:691f34d5-7a51-4290-8c73-f91ee7dadce6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 1CH 17:15
Text: According to all these words, and according to all this vision, so did Nathan speak unto David.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c48fd06b-340a-46df-869b-fa76afd835a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: 1CH 17:16
Text: And David the king came and sat before the LORD, and said, Who am I, O LORD God, and what is mine house, that thou hast brought me hitherto?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0143181d-bb1c-4afb-8216-a1806fdfd54a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: 1CH 17:17
Text: And yet this was a small thing in thine eyes, O God; for thou hast also spoken of thy servant’s house for a great while to come, and hast regarded me according to the estate of a man of high degree, O LORD God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5cde2ce7-eb72-430b-85db-31ba28e7d6fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: 1CH 17:18
Text: What can David speak more to thee for the honour of thy servant? for thou knowest thy servant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e20cec25-7482-4c11-8023-36cd54511deb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 1CH 17:19
Text: O LORD, for thy servant’s sake, and according to thine own heart, hast thou done all this greatness, in making known all these great things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d937156-50e4-4a49-9a7e-4265f82a8043>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: 1CH 17:20
Text: O LORD, there is none like thee, neither is there any God beside thee, according to all that we have heard with our ears.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6ec28e0-fab9-45a6-be58-56963fee84bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: 1CH 17:21
Text: And what one nation in the earth is like thy people Israel, whom God went to redeem to be his own people, to make thee a name of greatness and terribleness, by driving out nations from before thy people whom thou hast redeemed out of Egypt?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f89eeba3-2c97-486c-bc43-aebc467200e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 1CH 17:22
Text: For thy people Israel didst thou make thine own people for ever; and thou, LORD, becamest their God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b020367-ee8d-440e-a669-6bf22ec8964e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: 1CH 17:23
Text: Therefore now, LORD, let the thing that thou hast spoken concerning thy servant and concerning his house be established for ever, and do as thou hast said.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2288df6-bbf8-4612-ac59-25b2757ff71a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: 1CH 17:24
Text: Let it even be established, that thy name may be magnified for ever, saying, The LORD of hosts is the God of Israel, even a God to Israel: and let the house of David thy servant be established before thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1adc533e-20ce-455a-befc-ef6423b3a9b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: 1CH 17:25
Text: For thou, O my God, hast told thy servant that thou wilt build him an house: therefore thy servant hath found in his heart to pray before thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50d762b2-e1d3-41d8-a985-c66d44199e15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: 1CH 17:26
Text: And now, LORD, thou art God, and hast promised this goodness unto thy servant:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/17/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7f273e0-6793-4cad-b72f-bf7b17c0f78f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: 1CH 17:27
Text: Now therefore let it please thee to bless the house of thy servant, that it may be before thee for ever: for thou blessest, O LORD, and it shall be blessed for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/18/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd216481-5a99-43a2-9110-08d857ff8cef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: 1CH 18:1
Text: Now after this it came to pass, that David smote the Philistines, and subdued them, and took Gath and her towns out of the hand of the Philistines.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/18/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5779cdef-696d-4bf7-b884-566a4584677f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: 1CH 18:2
Text: And he smote Moab; and the Moabites became David’s servants, and brought gifts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/18/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec8a3498-e7aa-4579-92ca-c139446d4a40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: 1CH 18:3
Text: And David smote Hadarezer king of Zobah unto Hamath, as he went to stablish his dominion by the river Euphrates.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/18/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ca76a97-8f2c-4d3a-9693-200f508cf9bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: 1CH 18:4
Text: And David took from him a thousand chariots, and seven thousand horsemen, and twenty thousand footmen: David also houghed all the chariot horses, but reserved of them an hundred chariots.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/18/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70c50dd7-77aa-4520-b6bd-4ee2b2920d71>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: 1CH 18:5
Text: And when the Syrians of Damascus came to help Hadarezer king of Zobah, David slew of the Syrians two and twenty thousand men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/18/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:920dafd9-c923-4f94-8146-dd887b10c295>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: 1CH 18:6
Text: Then David put garrisons in Syriadamascus; and the Syrians became David’s servants, and brought gifts. Thus the LORD preserved David whithersoever he went.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/18/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b28cc1b-9c0b-4106-ab65-99dc79c09fb5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 1CH 18:7
Text: And David took the shields of gold that were on the servants of Hadarezer, and brought them to Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/18/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd442084-968e-42bf-8b67-c74a66fda65f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: 1CH 18:8
Text: Likewise from Tibhath, and from Chun, cities of Hadarezer, brought David very much brass, wherewith Solomon made the brasen sea, and the pillars, and the vessels of brass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/18/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8078e217-136d-4d9c-8a83-b9518ffc3186>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 1CH 18:9
Text: Now when Tou king of Hamath heard how David had smitten all the host of Hadarezer king of Zobah;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/18/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e2c0277-f528-489b-a55d-fee8c6998336>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: 1CH 18:10
Text: He sent Hadoram his son to king David, to enquire of his welfare, and to congratulate him, because he had fought against Hadarezer, and smitten him; (for Hadarezer had war with Tou;) and with him all manner of vessels of gold and silver and brass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/18/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d247e21d-1e77-4a67-b0d1-2a053ed1dbb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: 1CH 18:11
Text: Them also king David dedicated unto the LORD, with the silver and the gold that he brought from all these nations; from Edom, and from Moab, and from the children of Ammon, and from the Philistines, and from Amalek.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/18/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e0e7e52-2c54-4cf1-ba32-79eb13a31004>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: 1CH 18:12
Text: Moreover Abishai the son of Zeruiah slew of the Edomites in the valley of salt eighteen thousand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/18/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fad595ae-e501-41f4-8a64-f3f59f44f055>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 1CH 18:13
Text: And he put garrisons in Edom; and all the Edomites became David’s servants. Thus the LORD preserved David whithersoever he went.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/18/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af686455-ee5d-471b-9a05-a47829bbf2d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: 1CH 18:14
Text: So David reigned over all Israel, and executed judgment and justice among all his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/18/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5477f98-9757-40aa-844b-977b684fd8d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: 1CH 18:15
Text: And Joab the son of Zeruiah was over the host; and Jehoshaphat the son of Ahilud, recorder.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/18/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8f5180a-7532-4bd5-9b54-a0f44bc9862a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: 1CH 18:16
Text: And Zadok the son of Ahitub, and Abimelech the son of Abiathar, were the priests; and Shavsha was scribe;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/18/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37d91582-9f99-4cf5-a116-74b3125dcc31>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 1CH 18:17
Text: And Benaiah the son of Jehoiada was over the Cherethites and the Pelethites; and the sons of David were chief about the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/19/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d23b178-6cc6-408d-9a02-26ea7355cd75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: 1CH 19:1
Text: Now it came to pass after this, that Nahash the king of the children of Ammon died, and his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/19/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db1ed058-418e-4762-a9af-560c41cb5312>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 294

Reference: 1CH 19:2
Text: And David said, I will shew kindness unto Hanun the son of Nahash, because his father shewed kindness to me. And David sent messengers to comfort him concerning his father. So the servants of David came into the land of the children of Ammon to Hanun, to comfort him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/19/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24a7b34c-6c87-4fa9-b7a1-c804fc1abdfc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: 1CH 19:3
Text: But the princes of the children of Ammon said to Hanun, Thinkest thou that David doth honour thy father, that he hath sent comforters unto thee? are not his servants come unto thee for to search, and to overthrow, and to spy out the land?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/19/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af701edb-7416-4df0-9a1f-5b7f52244fcc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: 1CH 19:4
Text: Wherefore Hanun took David’s servants, and shaved them, and cut off their garments in the midst hard by their buttocks, and sent them away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/19/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d441ee92-9741-41e7-baf4-ca538f04147d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: 1CH 19:5
Text: Then there went certain, and told David how the men were served. And he sent to meet them: for the men were greatly ashamed. And the king said, Tarry at Jericho until your beards be grown, and then return.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/19/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a29b3af-bf1e-41b4-9878-189a7a4969c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: 1CH 19:6
Text: And when the children of Ammon saw that they had made themselves odious to David, Hanun and the children of Ammon sent a thousand talents of silver to hire them chariots and horsemen out of Mesopotamia, and out of Syriamaachah, and out of Zobah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/19/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4abb1ee-8a50-4ae9-9f25-6741f3cb90e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: 1CH 19:7
Text: So they hired thirty and two thousand chariots, and the king of Maachah and his people; who came and pitched before Medeba. And the children of Ammon gathered themselves together from their cities, and came to battle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/19/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cddeb38-f609-4158-a9c1-5ca532de8ce4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: 1CH 19:8
Text: And when David heard of it, he sent Joab, and all the host of the mighty men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/19/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b268f274-524a-40c8-b831-8d7cdb6cba9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: 1CH 19:9
Text: And the children of Ammon came out, and put the battle in array before the gate of the city: and the kings that were come were by themselves in the field.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/19/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e23383be-81bf-4928-9c33-79ecfd38811f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 1CH 19:10
Text: Now when Joab saw that the battle was set against him before and behind, he chose out of all the choice of Israel, and put them in array against the Syrians.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/19/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1de65252-0684-48e4-aae9-faa77d784ecc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: 1CH 19:11
Text: And the rest of the people he delivered unto the hand of Abishai his brother, and they set themselves in array against the children of Ammon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/19/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfedf9ae-91c5-49bd-a31f-3a91a4432ff5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: 1CH 19:12
Text: And he said, If the Syrians be too strong for me, then thou shalt help me: but if the children of Ammon be too strong for thee, then I will help thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/19/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e69b687b-3a69-43e7-b814-c0fba0c51fc5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 1CH 19:13
Text: Be of good courage, and let us behave ourselves valiantly for our people, and for the cities of our God: and let the LORD do that which is good in his sight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/19/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b261b8b-61b2-4e96-aece-8a0336ca3a16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 1CH 19:14
Text: So Joab and the people that were with him drew nigh before the Syrians unto the battle; and they fled before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/19/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9debe959-b3d7-4ae0-8368-c15139fdab73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: 1CH 19:15
Text: And when the children of Ammon saw that the Syrians were fled, they likewise fled before Abishai his brother, and entered into the city. Then Joab came to Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/19/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a4cac6b-c017-4a3b-8152-3d256bfb89f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: 1CH 19:16
Text: And when the Syrians saw that they were put to the worse before Israel, they sent messengers, and drew forth the Syrians that were beyond the river: and Shophach the captain of the host of Hadarezer went before them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/19/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7daf264b-74d8-488c-9ba4-cfb0a7dcd9ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: 1CH 19:17
Text: And it was told David; and he gathered all Israel, and passed over Jordan, and came upon them, and set the battle in array against them. So when David had put the battle in array against the Syrians, they fought with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/19/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e220d0a-44a8-4aa1-85c1-dd7d4cc6fcd0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: 1CH 19:18
Text: But the Syrians fled before Israel; and David slew of the Syrians seven thousand men which fought in chariots, and forty thousand footmen, and killed Shophach the captain of the host.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/19/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed572f38-bff0-416b-91cd-ea21729deeb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: 1CH 19:19
Text: And when the servants of Hadarezer saw that they were put to the worse before Israel, they made peace with David, and became his servants: neither would the Syrians help the children of Ammon any more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/20/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:609025bc-df7b-49dd-9b93-e51a6ce294d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 311

Reference: 1CH 20:1
Text: And it came to pass, that after the year was expired, at the time that kings go out to battle, Joab led forth the power of the army, and wasted the country of the children of Ammon, and came and besieged Rabbah. But David tarried at Jerusalem. And Joab smote Rabbah, and destroyed it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/20/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd04d2b8-a25a-4041-98c0-d56aeb112c4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: 1CH 20:2
Text: And David took the crown of their king from off his head, and found it to weigh a talent of gold, and there were precious stones in it; and it was set upon David’s head: and he brought also exceeding much spoil out of the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/20/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d625a7ea-79d1-490c-a3aa-b3bceb99621c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: 1CH 20:3
Text: And he brought out the people that were in it, and cut them with saws, and with harrows of iron, and with axes. Even so dealt David with all the cities of the children of Ammon. And David and all the people returned to Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/20/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21d060cb-ac69-47d4-8f18-b41c4f2039c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: 1CH 20:4
Text: And it came to pass after this, that there arose war at Gezer with the Philistines; at which time Sibbechai the Hushathite slew Sippai, that was of the children of the giant: and they were subdued.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/20/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:337cd41c-bea3-4e75-892c-d0ee3551f162>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: 1CH 20:5
Text: And there was war again with the Philistines; and Elhanan the son of Jair slew Lahmi the brother of Goliath the Gittite, whose spear staff was like a weaver’s beam.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/20/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9bfacd02-a39c-4a77-ac84-e91a82eced0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: 1CH 20:6
Text: And yet again there was war at Gath, where was a man of great stature, whose fingers and toes were four and twenty, six on each hand, and six on each foot and he also was the son of the giant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/20/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee9b3e63-b7d7-47ef-b38c-4851d79b46c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: 1CH 20:7
Text: But when he defied Israel, Jonathan the son of Shimea David’s brother slew him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/20/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:840a45ff-d675-4bf0-8162-603b5c827ae5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 1CH 20:8
Text: These were born unto the giant in Gath; and they fell by the hand of David, and by the hand of his servants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:545c0d4d-3fb8-45d0-b271-08ccb8b94efa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: 1CH 21:1
Text: And Satan stood up against Israel, and provoked David to number Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00fb5684-f419-46cf-9566-95139af7c715>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: 1CH 21:2
Text: And David said to Joab and to the rulers of the people, Go, number Israel from Beersheba even to Dan; and bring the number of them to me, that I may know it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea3732b6-b3bd-449f-90cc-d0d111c3f8ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 262

Reference: 1CH 21:3
Text: And Joab answered, The LORD make his people an hundred times so many more as they be: but, my lord the king, are they not all my lord’s servants? why then doth my lord require this thing? why will he be a cause of trespass to Israel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2fcc73f-74be-45a1-932e-62c6080ebb35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 1CH 21:4
Text: Nevertheless the king’s word prevailed against Joab. Wherefore Joab departed, and went throughout all Israel, and came to Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c8f5ae2-1c36-416f-a488-513ad580544a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: 1CH 21:5
Text: And Joab gave the sum of the number of the people unto David. And all they of Israel were a thousand thousand and an hundred thousand men that drew sword: and Judah was four hundred threescore and ten thousand men that drew sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ffa7f37-c330-4718-87a6-60191eb354e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 1CH 21:6
Text: But Levi and Benjamin counted he not among them: for the king’s word was abominable to Joab.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aad0fd79-1be8-4f08-b288-6a0607d33ff3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: 1CH 21:7
Text: And God was displeased with this thing; therefore he smote Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:efe1bfd1-9952-46d6-ab1f-9c240db9f9fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 1CH 21:8
Text: And David said unto God, I have sinned greatly, because I have done this thing: but now, I beseech thee, do away the iniquity of thy servant; for I have done very foolishly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0d9550c-4346-4ec7-bc2c-1b95a0e96f31>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: 1CH 21:9
Text: And the LORD spake unto Gad, David’s seer, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a33e2b9d-fe96-4bfa-add7-97acb5e96d14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 1CH 21:10
Text: Go and tell David, saying, Thus saith the LORD, I offer thee three things: choose thee one of them, that I may do it unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eeb9c073-8820-4cd5-a941-a25a38702646>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: 1CH 21:11
Text: So Gad came to David, and said unto him, Thus saith the LORD, Choose thee


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc8be041-558f-4f0f-a3a6-54b90fc31ef9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 391

Reference: 1CH 21:12
Text: Either three years’ famine; or three months to be destroyed before thy foes, while that the sword of thine enemies overtaketh thee; or else three days the sword of the LORD, even the pestilence, in the land, and the angel of the LORD destroying throughout all the coasts of Israel. Now therefore advise thyself what word I shall bring again to him that sent me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d7c0822-2626-4126-8850-797616587de8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: 1CH 21:13
Text: And David said unto Gad, I am in a great strait: let me fall now into the hand of the LORD; for very great are his mercies: but let me not fall into the hand of man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97420810-fee8-47ea-82d4-7782127e2c1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: 1CH 21:14
Text: So the LORD sent pestilence upon Israel: and there fell of Israel seventy thousand men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a550fb5-bd3b-4e83-a62c-53354dccaeff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 305

Reference: 1CH 21:15
Text: And God sent an angel unto Jerusalem to destroy it: and as he was destroying, the LORD beheld, and he repented him of the evil, and said to the angel that destroyed, It is enough, stay now thine hand. And the angel of the LORD stood by the threshingfloor of Ornan the Jebusite.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86b9b5f3-de0a-4079-a687-cc2a37a8e0ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 281

Reference: 1CH 21:16
Text: And David lifted up his eyes, and saw the angel of the LORD stand between the earth and the heaven, having a drawn sword in his hand stretched out over Jerusalem. Then David and the elders of Israel, who were clothed in sackcloth, fell upon their faces.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:026dd2c3-830c-4e1c-b0de-b56ba5a3783a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 337

Reference: 1CH 21:17
Text: And David said unto God, Is it not I that commanded the people to be numbered? even I it is that have sinned and done evil indeed; but as for these sheep, what have they done? let thine hand, I pray thee, O LORD my God, be on me, and on my father’s house; but not on thy people, that they should be plagued.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b55fb39-515e-4515-a0bf-5ff279a3f002>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: 1CH 21:18
Text: Then the angel of the LORD commanded Gad to say to David, that David should go up, and set up an altar unto the LORD in the threshingfloor of Ornan the Jebusite.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6399df77-2a58-4e5b-a0c1-4967fd19b600>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: 1CH 21:19
Text: And David went up at the saying of Gad, which he spake in the name of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d4ad87f-d9d5-4b6d-b8e0-51f5239945f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: 1CH 21:20
Text: And Ornan turned back, and saw the angel; and his four sons with him hid themselves. Now Ornan was threshing wheat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2f32848-5fc6-4362-a641-60d6a7782f9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 1CH 21:21
Text: And as David came to Ornan, Ornan looked and saw David, and went out of the threshingfloor, and bowed himself to David with his face to the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0697df21-3770-4be0-849c-97039291e82b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: 1CH 21:22
Text: Then David said to Ornan, Grant me the place of this threshingfloor, that I may build an altar therein unto the LORD: thou shalt grant it me for the full price: that the plague may be stayed from the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:957fcb81-5a3d-46a0-bf24-33d8f5c029c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 274

Reference: 1CH 21:23
Text: And Ornan said unto David, Take it to thee, and let my lord the king do that which is good in his eyes: lo, I give thee the oxen also for burnt offerings, and the threshing instruments for wood, and the wheat for the meat offering; I give it all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09fa9258-b2e6-48aa-95f7-e22385f029ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: 1CH 21:24
Text: And king David said to Ornan, Nay; but I will verily buy it for the full price: for I will not take that which is thine for the LORD, nor offer burnt offerings without cost.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1f5d2f6-d2b8-44fe-bfbf-d7c4dbac18b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: 1CH 21:25
Text: So David gave to Ornan for the place six hundred shekels of gold by weight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7e43474-8709-4431-bd92-a19478fbe438>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: 1CH 21:26
Text: And David built there an altar unto the LORD, and offered burnt offerings and peace offerings, and called upon the LORD; and he answered him from heaven by fire upon the altar of burnt offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c3ff391-d5c6-449b-9193-f52c59acf6ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: 1CH 21:27
Text: And the LORD commanded the angel; and he put up his sword again into the sheath thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b230c858-39b5-4ffa-911e-5075b43970f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 1CH 21:28
Text: At that time when David saw that the LORD had answered him in the threshingfloor of Ornan the Jebusite, then he sacrificed there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a09be2f0-30f0-4797-84c2-adbc2901a6ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: 1CH 21:29
Text: For the tabernacle of the LORD, which Moses made in the wilderness, and the altar of the burnt offering, were at that season in the high place at Gibeon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/21/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28c981e6-ae82-461a-a5d6-6b48869d3449>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: 1CH 21:30
Text: But David could not go before it to enquire of God: for he was afraid because of the sword of the angel of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/22/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd7a318e-1827-4e21-b244-3a290364f103>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: 1CH 22:1
Text: Then David said, This is the house of the LORD God, and this is the altar of the burnt offering for Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/22/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51bd109f-3e7c-4590-9f90-2b844350852a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 1CH 22:2
Text: And David commanded to gather together the strangers that were in the land of Israel; and he set masons to hew wrought stones to build the house of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/22/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca368b36-eb21-42d9-9d07-7079a52c5360>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: 1CH 22:3
Text: And David prepared iron in abundance for the nails for the doors of the gates, and for the joinings; and brass in abundance without weight;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/22/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5389ecae-37e3-4692-babc-b30a065eea23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: 1CH 22:4
Text: Also cedar trees in abundance: for the Zidonians and they of Tyre brought much cedar wood to David.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/22/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5e56459-0a5b-4206-a611-8810b0331a74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 297

Reference: 1CH 22:5
Text: And David said, Solomon my son is young and tender, and the house that is to be builded for the LORD must be exceeding magnifical, of fame and of glory throughout all countries: I will therefore now make preparation for it. So David prepared abundantly before his death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/22/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e455f17-744c-4ce5-a91e-3ae8d4aac70c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: 1CH 22:6
Text: Then he called for Solomon his son, and charged him to build an house for the LORD God of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/22/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1a9b0f9-3d4f-409f-9986-a8d2d3411fa4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: 1CH 22:7
Text: And David said to Solomon, My son, as for me, it was in my mind to build an house unto the name of the LORD my God:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/22/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b948c2f-89f7-4c62-9583-1dfd959edb6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: 1CH 22:8
Text: But the word of the LORD came to me, saying, Thou hast shed blood abundantly, and hast made great wars: thou shalt not build an house unto my name, because thou hast shed much blood upon the earth in my sight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/22/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3b960d6-2f29-481e-a343-bcea4e4717db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: 1CH 22:9
Text: Behold, a son shall be born to thee, who shall be a man of rest; and I will give him rest from all his enemies round about: for his name shall be Solomon, and I will give peace and quietness unto Israel in his days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/22/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5b3d45d-bcaa-439a-a74c-8e30bba905ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: 1CH 22:10
Text: He shall build an house for my name; and he shall be my son, and I will be his father; and I will establish the throne of his kingdom over Israel for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/22/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f6a584c-d1a6-418a-a4c8-3473fc856359>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 1CH 22:11
Text: Now, my son, the LORD be with thee; and prosper thou, and build the house of the LORD thy God, as he hath said of thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/22/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90467b2b-8b5c-4574-889f-f82095649d77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: 1CH 22:12
Text: Only the LORD give thee wisdom and understanding, and give thee charge concerning Israel, that thou mayest keep the law of the LORD thy God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/22/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6525ec79-8151-41ef-91e6-29cbcf6a6bb6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: 1CH 22:13
Text: Then shalt thou prosper, if thou takest heed to fulfil the statutes and judgments which the LORD charged Moses with concerning Israel: be strong, and of good courage; dread not, nor be dismayed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/22/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:146890a0-6086-49b5-bd96-472ef18cff7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 306

Reference: 1CH 22:14
Text: Now, behold, in my trouble I have prepared for the house of the LORD an hundred thousand talents of gold, and a thousand thousand talents of silver; and of brass and iron without weight; for it is in abundance: timber also and stone have I prepared; and thou mayest add thereto.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/22/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63f0b20b-4372-445e-a3e0-f9c5ca0ecdd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: 1CH 22:15
Text: Moreover there are workmen with thee in abundance, hewers and workers of stone and timber, and all manner of cunning men for every manner of work.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/22/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f11e3e7e-de15-4d15-8bd9-b7ddaf789066>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: 1CH 22:16
Text: Of the gold, the silver, and the brass, and the iron, there is no number. Arise therefore, and be doing, and the LORD be with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/22/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e08f4e31-4335-4918-87d7-ea6d3ea59074>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: 1CH 22:17
Text: David also commanded all the princes of Israel to help Solomon his son, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/22/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11372ad3-8535-48a5-9c5a-985934b410ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: 1CH 22:18
Text: Is not the LORD your God with you? and hath he not given you rest on every side? for he hath given the inhabitants of the land into mine hand; and the land is subdued before the LORD, and before his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/22/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d07f1cc-ea41-4810-9416-a9108d68906b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 283

Reference: 1CH 22:19
Text: Now set your heart and your soul to seek the LORD your God; arise therefore, and build ye the sanctuary of the LORD God, to bring the ark of the covenant of the LORD, and the holy vessels of God, into the house that is to be built to the name of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/23/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d01a0a25-634e-4405-b5c1-64f6695507cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: 1CH 23:1
Text: So when David was old and full of days, he made Solomon his son king over Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/23/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74836af1-8720-4d69-a199-8fbd3e163ecf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: 1CH 23:2
Text: And he gathered together all the princes of Israel, with the priests and the Levites.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/23/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5b7b486-213f-4650-be08-e69e3da657aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 1CH 23:3
Text: Now the Levites were numbered from the age of thirty years and upward: and their number by their polls, man by man, was thirty and eight thousand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/23/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbd04b6b-1d95-4793-9306-42e939374b00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: 1CH 23:4
Text: Of which, twenty and four thousand were to set forward the work of the house of the LORD; and six thousand were officers and judges:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/23/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b013500e-e8db-48e8-ae07-ee82669ecd1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: 1CH 23:5
Text: Moreover four thousand were porters; and four thousand praised the LORD with the instruments which I made, said David, to praise therewith.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/23/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58343ed0-3828-4a9c-8169-007a275bb4e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 1CH 23:6
Text: And David divided them into courses among the sons of Levi, namely, Gershon, Kohath, and Merari.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
