Content-Length: 286

Reference: 1CH 28:2
Text: Then David the king stood up upon his feet, and said, Hear me, my brethren, and my people: As for me, I had in mine heart to build an house of rest for the ark of the covenant of the LORD, and for the footstool of our God, and had made ready for the building:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/28/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7beeb25-88a6-4870-88bf-27291d2e8248>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: 1CH 28:3
Text: But God said unto me, Thou shalt not build an house for my name, because thou hast been a man of war, and hast shed blood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/28/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fe815ef-f86d-4a71-9480-2497e3065e48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 303

Reference: 1CH 28:4
Text: Howbeit the LORD God of Israel chose me before all the house of my father to be king over Israel for ever: for he hath chosen Judah to be the ruler; and of the house of Judah, the house of my father; and among the sons of my father he liked me to make me king over all Israel:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/28/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abaa097f-7284-4c6a-8c49-23243328ac4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 1CH 28:5
Text: And of all my sons, (for the LORD hath given me many sons,) he hath chosen Solomon my son to sit upon the throne of the kingdom of the LORD over Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/28/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0cf6c20-0ea9-44ea-bb36-a12c502cf616>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: 1CH 28:6
Text: And he said unto me, Solomon thy son, he shall build my house and my courts: for I have chosen him to be my son, and I will be his father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/28/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0550ace6-9c03-460c-9be6-443281139478>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 1CH 28:7
Text: Moreover I will establish his kingdom for ever, if he be constant to do my commandments and my judgments, as at this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/28/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95648895-ae37-4ba4-8753-92085903e8c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 296

Reference: 1CH 28:8
Text: Now therefore in the sight of all Israel the congregation of the LORD, and in the audience of our God, keep and seek for all the commandments of the LORD your God: that ye may possess this good land, and leave it for an inheritance for your children after you for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/28/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fe9b97a-6cf1-48ab-9bf7-23d1a01bef90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 337

Reference: 1CH 28:9
Text: And thou, Solomon my son, know thou the God of thy father, and serve him with a perfect heart and with a willing mind: for the LORD searcheth all hearts, and understandeth all the imaginations of the thoughts: if thou seek him, he will be found of thee; but if thou forsake him, he will cast thee off for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/28/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f40df2e4-609d-4c12-bca7-0b9f3520198f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: 1CH 28:10
Text: Take heed now; for the LORD hath chosen thee to build an house for the sanctuary: be strong, and do it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/28/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8091d9fa-b7f0-44f2-b909-df10444ad077>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: 1CH 28:11
Text: Then David gave to Solomon his son the pattern of the porch, and of the houses thereof, and of the treasuries thereof, and of the upper chambers thereof, and of the inner parlours thereof, and of the place of the mercy seat,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/28/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ebc3920-394d-4337-8877-687e07e75b1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: 1CH 28:12
Text: And the pattern of all that he had by the spirit, of the courts of the house of the LORD, and of all the chambers round about, of the treasuries of the house of God, and of the treasuries of the dedicated things:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/28/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89547c53-d0cd-4705-a585-afff1a2e5a9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: 1CH 28:13
Text: Also for the courses of the priests and the Levites, and for all the work of the service of the house of the LORD, and for all the vessels of service in the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/28/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afdf60e2-3921-4702-b0ec-47bfbdaca7fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: 1CH 28:14
Text: He gave of gold by weight for things of gold, for all instruments of all manner of service; silver also for all instruments of silver by weight, for all instruments of every kind of service:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/28/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27c581d0-0992-4383-bb55-12fc7c589ece>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 309

Reference: 1CH 28:15
Text: Even the weight for the candlesticks of gold, and for their lamps of gold, by weight for every candlestick, and for the lamps thereof: and for the candlesticks of silver by weight, both for the candlestick, and also for the lamps thereof, according to the use of every candlestick.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/28/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c66a4339-6687-40c4-8fe0-e7a9dc374ec0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: 1CH 28:16
Text: And by weight he gave gold for the tables of shewbread, for every table; and likewise silver for the tables of silver:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/28/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52dd166a-c12c-4ce8-9367-a0ace41c5e8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: 1CH 28:17
Text: Also pure gold for the fleshhooks, and the bowls, and the cups: and for the golden basons he gave gold by weight for every bason; and likewise silver by weight for every bason of silver:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/28/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f5c186e-05ae-4360-9fde-240e0cd1d0bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: 1CH 28:18
Text: And for the altar of incense refined gold by weight; and gold for the pattern of the chariot of the cherubims, that spread out their wings, and covered the ark of the covenant of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/28/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9da82c9-5b75-41d4-aa4f-0267abb96fec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 1CH 28:19
Text: All this, said David, the LORD made me understand in writing by his hand upon me, even all the works of this pattern.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/28/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b6ee44a-f1fd-49ec-9a07-f13794640754>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 302

Reference: 1CH 28:20
Text: And David said to Solomon his son, Be strong and of good courage, and do it: fear not, nor be dismayed: for the LORD God, even my God, will be with thee; he will not fail thee, nor forsake thee, until thou hast finished all the work for the service of the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/28/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed959104-d9cd-4bfc-8984-33ea31beeb68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 338

Reference: 1CH 28:21
Text: And, behold, the courses of the priests and the Levites, even they shall be with thee for all the service of the house of God: and there shall be with thee for all manner of workmanship every willing skilful man, for any manner of service: also the princes and all the people will be wholly at thy commandment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95f4199a-bc67-4f7c-bf88-fa219c118f94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: 1CH 29:1
Text: Furthermore David the king said unto all the congregation, Solomon my son, whom alone God hath chosen, is yet young and tender, and the work is great: for the palace is not for man, but for the LORD God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5daabfd5-b68e-4fea-9d13-e418cc3ebd95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 402

Reference: 1CH 29:2
Text: Now I have prepared with all my might for the house of my God the gold for things to be made of gold, and the silver for things of silver, and the brass for things of brass, the iron for things of iron, and wood for things of wood; onyx stones, and stones to be set, glistering stones, and of divers colours, and all manner of precious stones, and marble stones in abundance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e1eb2d2-ab1c-4996-af0e-e19855a402b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: 1CH 29:3
Text: Moreover, because I have set my affection to the house of my God, I have of mine own proper good, of gold and silver, which I have given to the house of my God, over and above all that I have prepared for the holy house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10fcbdcb-3eae-4798-865a-3a2db82f737f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: 1CH 29:4
Text: Even three thousand talents of gold, of the gold of Ophir, and seven thousand talents of refined silver, to overlay the walls of the houses withal:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:671c2be3-93ee-4d4e-829a-1c9c0c5c6f1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: 1CH 29:5
Text: The gold for things of gold, and the silver for things of silver, and for all manner of work to be made by the hands of artificers. And who then is willing to consecrate his service this day unto the LORD?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb75921a-75f9-4487-89d2-84b101285441>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: 1CH 29:6
Text: Then the chief of the fathers and princes of the tribes of Israel and the captains of thousands and of hundreds, with the rulers of the king’s work, offered willingly,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6818efe-c454-478f-a29a-7386046e6f54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: 1CH 29:7
Text: And gave for the service of the house of God of gold five thousand talents and ten thousand drams, and of silver ten thousand talents, and of brass eighteen thousand talents, and one hundred thousand talents of iron.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12a09b10-682e-4881-8e10-11e4cf2be769>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 1CH 29:8
Text: And they with whom precious stones were found gave them to the treasure of the house of the LORD, by the hand of Jehiel the Gershonite.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8dd92734-59e1-4b84-bebc-a649f0b05e72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: 1CH 29:9
Text: Then the people rejoiced, for that they offered willingly, because with perfect heart they offered willingly to the LORD: and David the king also rejoiced with great joy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9c0528b-4b16-4420-b743-21f6c09bff61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: 1CH 29:10
Text: Wherefore David blessed the LORD before all the congregation: and David said, Blessed be thou, LORD God of Israel our father, for ever and ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:566d0909-15a8-4225-b283-deffbb8c9fe4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: 1CH 29:11
Text: Thine, O LORD is the greatness, and the power, and the glory, and the victory, and the majesty: for all that is in the heaven and in the earth is thine; thine is the kingdom, O LORD, and thou art exalted as head above all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69f10be3-8089-4b26-9707-d056dbdbcafe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 1CH 29:12
Text: Both riches and honour come of thee, and thou reignest over all; and in thine hand is power and might; and in thine hand it is to make great, and to give strength unto all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:220d6db9-ebfb-4609-95fc-09fc9cbf7834>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: 1CH 29:13
Text: Now therefore, our God, we thank thee, and praise thy glorious name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f595887-1e3d-4aaf-be01-31948d62ced8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: 1CH 29:14
Text: But who am I, and what is my people, that we should be able to offer so willingly after this sort? for all things come of thee, and of thine own have we given thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbf9b1e2-65cd-4dd3-a28f-fef6e2e8e3c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: 1CH 29:15
Text: For we are strangers before thee, and sojourners, as were all our fathers: our days on the earth are as a shadow, and there is none abiding.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9455e7cd-6cef-4d76-88b5-ab14be4fbf44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 1CH 29:16
Text: O LORD our God, all this store that we have prepared to build thee an house for thine holy name cometh of thine hand, and is all thine own.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b194c64a-3b41-414d-882e-2f178ec10e61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 292

Reference: 1CH 29:17
Text: I know also, my God, that thou triest the heart, and hast pleasure in uprightness. As for me, in the uprightness of mine heart I have willingly offered all these things: and now have I seen with joy thy people, which are present here, to offer willingly unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8955ac11-890d-421f-81bf-d261bc7a7bc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: 1CH 29:18
Text: O LORD God of Abraham, Isaac, and of Israel, our fathers, keep this for ever in the imagination of the thoughts of the heart of thy people, and prepare their heart unto thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:399b2785-8b6d-472e-8e2b-1632da5fb636>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: 1CH 29:19
Text: And give unto Solomon my son a perfect heart, to keep thy commandments, thy testimonies, and thy statutes, and to do all these things, and to build the palace, for the which I have made provision.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a49562bc-8fff-4664-8a76-ff94b0e4c476>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: 1CH 29:20
Text: And David said to all the congregation, Now bless the LORD your God. And all the congregation blessed the LORD God of their fathers, and bowed down their heads, and worshipped the LORD, and the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d00cec4-2bae-4a4b-bd4b-4a18236c7d09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 283

Reference: 1CH 29:21
Text: And they sacrificed sacrifices unto the LORD, and offered burnt offerings unto the LORD, on the morrow after that day, even a thousand bullocks, a thousand rams, and a thousand lambs, with their drink offerings, and sacrifices in abundance for all Israel:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c889787d-7ad8-477d-a69d-5ebb94dd220c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: 1CH 29:22
Text: And did eat and drink before the LORD on that day with great gladness. And they made Solomon the son of David king the second time, and anointed him unto the LORD to be the chief governor, and Zadok to be priest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a9ba1f4-dc31-49ab-a0ac-a44869ffd9d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: 1CH 29:23
Text: Then Solomon sat on the throne of the LORD as king instead of David his father, and prospered; and all Israel obeyed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fa65e9b-4f68-4fa0-af39-ae94c302f963>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 1CH 29:24
Text: And all the princes, and the mighty men, and all the sons likewise of king David, submitted themselves unto Solomon the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f22f7fe8-d83a-4d1b-99be-0034ad91ae7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: 1CH 29:25
Text: And the LORD magnified Solomon exceedingly in the sight of all Israel, and bestowed upon him such royal majesty as had not been on any king before him in Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41a39ae7-ba98-4e04-b5ea-4e661195ab83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: 1CH 29:26
Text: Thus David the son of Jesse reigned over all Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a36328d9-a985-4f61-b962-1caa4d74ebb2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: 1CH 29:27
Text: And the time that he reigned over Israel was forty years; seven years reigned he in Hebron, and thirty and three years reigned he in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e92b77eb-0c08-4da4-b898-2111b613d260>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: 1CH 29:28
Text: And he died in a good old age, full of days, riches, and honour: and Solomon his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9ad4ec0-19ec-464e-990b-110f4a7f47ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: 1CH 29:29
Text: Now the acts of David the king, first and last, behold, they are written in the book of Samuel the seer, and in the book of Nathan the prophet, and in the book of Gad the seer,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1CH/29/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
