Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 2CH 1:1
Text: And Solomon the son of David was strengthened in his kingdom, and the LORD his God was with him, and magnified him exceedingly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd219162-3736-47c0-9952-310836540cbd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: 2CH 1:2
Text: Then Solomon spake unto all Israel, to the captains of thousands and of hundreds, and to the judges, and to every governor in all Israel, the chief of the fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3187c233-7755-468a-a03a-b600fc371ffe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: 2CH 1:3
Text: So Solomon, and all the congregation with him, went to the high place that was at Gibeon; for there was the tabernacle of the congregation of God, which Moses the servant of the LORD had made in the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2bd17d8-f59e-483e-826c-998e794e6234>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 2CH 1:4
Text: But the ark of God had David brought up from Kirjathjearim to the place which David had prepared for it: for he had pitched a tent for it at Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58d9015f-e3b7-45b3-8819-efb058b1bd8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: 2CH 1:5
Text: Moreover the brasen altar, that Bezaleel the son of Uri, the son of Hur, had made, he put before the tabernacle of the LORD: and Solomon and the congregation sought unto it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50e21269-0cd9-4f5f-8772-8fe27ee26ca2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 2CH 1:6
Text: And Solomon went up thither to the brasen altar before the LORD, which was at the tabernacle of the congregation, and offered a thousand burnt offerings upon it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f464d1b8-035f-4b5a-8f33-3ec2353deece>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: 2CH 1:7
Text: In that night did God appear unto Solomon, and said unto him, Ask what I shall give thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afa3cb44-0eb2-467e-8263-bea7b7cb77fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: 2CH 1:8
Text: And Solomon said unto God, Thou hast shewed great mercy unto David my father, and hast made me to reign in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8bc51a2-eeca-4193-bcd6-0dd15d875cfd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 2CH 1:9
Text: Now, O LORD God, let thy promise unto David my father be established: for thou hast made me king over a people like the dust of the earth in multitude.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02d1eb20-a6c4-443a-acdb-c4cfc761b062>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: 2CH 1:10
Text: Give me now wisdom and knowledge, that I may go out and come in before this people: for who can judge this thy people, that is so great?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2150d888-c84a-4e86-b139-b8ed271f61ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 316

Reference: 2CH 1:11
Text: And God said to Solomon, Because this was in thine heart, and thou hast not asked riches, wealth, or honour, nor the life of thine enemies, neither yet hast asked long life; but hast asked wisdom and knowledge for thyself, that thou mayest judge my people, over whom I have made thee king:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b844a3d3-6786-4bf3-8ac9-269c16585434>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: 2CH 1:12
Text: Wisdom and knowledge is granted unto thee; and I will give thee riches, and wealth, and honour, such as none of the kings have had that have been before thee, neither shall there any after thee have the like.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3069efb-a4ef-4f26-8fdf-c5a990f8e1e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 2CH 1:13
Text: Then Solomon came from his journey to the high place that was at Gibeon to Jerusalem, from before the tabernacle of the congregation, and reigned over Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc82d9d9-d187-4316-9196-4bdaee467e08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: 2CH 1:14
Text: And Solomon gathered chariots and horsemen: and he had a thousand and four hundred chariots, and twelve thousand horsemen, which he placed in the chariot cities, and with the king at Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27c34350-24ff-4ef6-a7ce-aa3c2f5260b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 2CH 1:15
Text: And the king made silver and gold at Jerusalem as plenteous as stones, and cedar trees made he as the sycomore trees that are in the vale for abundance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f87f5b39-76ff-4d86-b054-b01faaf1bc28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: 2CH 1:16
Text: And Solomon had horses brought out of Egypt, and linen yarn: the king’s merchants received the linen yarn at a price.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ff7d6e4-6433-4bc8-9342-39dc4a693553>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: 2CH 1:17
Text: And they fetched up, and brought forth out of Egypt a chariot for six hundred shekels of silver, and an horse for an hundred and fifty: and so brought they out horses for all the kings of the Hittites, and for the kings of Syria, by their means.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6aadf7f5-fa35-4725-8775-c57f5c8d5ddc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: 2CH 2:1
Text: And Solomon determined to build an house for the name of the LORD, and an house for his kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d741b7d5-4066-4a76-8aa1-7b309b707b48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: 2CH 2:2
Text: And Solomon told out threescore and ten thousand men to bear burdens, and fourscore thousand to hew in the mountain, and three thousand and six hundred to oversee them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fa1db5b-5931-4076-a710-b8613d803d3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: 2CH 2:3
Text: And Solomon sent to Huram the king of Tyre, saying, As thou didst deal with David my father, and didst send him cedars to build him an house to dwell therein, even so deal with me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3aceea0f-2ca4-46bf-aedf-a277689899b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 351

Reference: 2CH 2:4
Text: Behold, I build an house to the name of the LORD my God, to dedicate it to him, and to burn before him sweet incense, and for the continual shewbread, and for the burnt offerings morning and evening, on the sabbaths, and on the new moons, and on the solemn feasts of the LORD our God. This is an ordinance for ever to Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80cacb9e-e4bf-40a5-a5c0-f902bc08dd1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: 2CH 2:5
Text: And the house which I build is great: for great is our God above all gods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da373c5f-66dc-49b3-a70a-ddcec72efe0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: 2CH 2:6
Text: But who is able to build him an house, seeing the heaven and heaven of heavens cannot contain him? who am I then, that I should build him an house, save only to burn sacrifice before him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60e34720-3454-410c-8c9c-af53d35ee2dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 285

Reference: 2CH 2:7
Text: Send me now therefore a man cunning to work in gold, and in silver, and in brass, and in iron, and in purple, and crimson, and blue, and that can skill to grave with the cunning men that are with me in Judah and in Jerusalem, whom David my father did provide.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4eb361c2-bc1f-441b-b894-92c6206b4382>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: 2CH 2:8
Text: Send me also cedar trees, fir trees, and algum trees, out of Lebanon: for I know that thy servants can skill to cut timber in Lebanon; and, behold, my servants shall be with thy servants,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a76005df-1c9e-47a7-b82b-c88dc2ad907d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: 2CH 2:9
Text: Even to prepare me timber in abundance: for the house which I am about to build shall be wonderful great.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9cd2c31f-bb2a-491c-b1ff-22c56f5bc9a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: 2CH 2:10
Text: And, behold, I will give to thy servants, the hewers that cut timber, twenty thousand measures of beaten wheat, and twenty thousand measures of barley, and twenty thousand baths of wine, and twenty thousand baths of oil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8dae5a5c-8a4c-426a-afdc-4613a180c154>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 2CH 2:11
Text: Then Huram the king of Tyre answered in writing, which he sent to Solomon, Because the LORD hath loved his people, he hath made thee king over them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5b1410d-4cfa-4d41-ba13-06b0ff644b64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: 2CH 2:12
Text: Huram said moreover, Blessed be the LORD God of Israel, that made heaven and earth, who hath given to David the king a wise son, endued with prudence and understanding, that might build an house for the LORD, and an house for his kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5be8e1f9-5691-43bb-ae19-14662f8d3d68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: 2CH 2:13
Text: And now I have sent a cunning man, endued with understanding, of Huram my father’s,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe952b84-0b52-44b7-8638-f97b9fede548>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 412

Reference: 2CH 2:14
Text: The son of a woman of the daughters of Dan, and his father was a man of Tyre, skilful to work in gold, and in silver, in brass, in iron, in stone, and in timber, in purple, in blue, and in fine linen, and in crimson; also to grave any manner of graving, and to find out every device which shall be put to him, with thy cunning men, and with the cunning men of my lord David thy father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5480e711-121e-4262-a739-f6201bad1e25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: 2CH 2:15
Text: Now therefore the wheat, and the barley, the oil, and the wine, which my lord hath spoken of, let him send unto his servants:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc3268de-b33c-4ba4-85cd-4b64e388893f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 2CH 2:16
Text: And we will cut wood out of Lebanon, as much as thou shalt need: and we will bring it to thee in floats by sea to Joppa; and thou shalt carry it up to Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5563433b-1929-4bb3-92e5-8c7c8baf278b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: 2CH 2:17
Text: And Solomon numbered all the strangers that were in the land of Israel, after the numbering wherewith David his father had numbered them; and they were found an hundred and fifty thousand and three thousand and six hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:041b095b-4b48-453d-b35b-418723ebac00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: 2CH 2:18
Text: And he set threescore and ten thousand of them to be bearers of burdens, and fourscore thousand to be hewers in the mountain, and three thousand and six hundred overseers to set the people a work.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1321dd5-ec9c-4977-888a-2bc74df50cea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: 2CH 3:1
Text: Then Solomon began to build the house of the LORD at Jerusalem in mount Moriah, where the Lord appeared unto David his father, in the place that David had prepared in the threshingfloor of Ornan the Jebusite.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9deb8162-4b11-4195-8331-44700cc437e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: 2CH 3:2
Text: And he began to build in the second day of the second month, in the fourth year of his reign.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b969c19-2f3c-4533-a50f-93dfe84d8d16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: 2CH 3:3
Text: Now these are the things wherein Solomon was instructed for the building of the house of God. The length by cubits after the first measure was threescore cubits, and the breadth twenty cubits.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7e04c53-c30f-43da-94d2-89c0d7a57702>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: 2CH 3:4
Text: And the porch that was in the front of the house, the length of it was according to the breadth of the house, twenty cubits, and the height was an hundred and twenty: and he overlaid it within with pure gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea591c3e-a504-49a8-83aa-f17d87194bbe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 2CH 3:5
Text: And the greater house he cieled with fir tree, which he overlaid with fine gold, and set thereon palm trees and chains.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:086f869e-0fea-48d2-9057-2a0f98dc0597>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: 2CH 3:6
Text: And he garnished the house with precious stones for beauty: and the gold was gold of Parvaim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:385dbd8b-ed01-4688-be36-e8720a0be171>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 2CH 3:7
Text: He overlaid also the house, the beams, the posts, and the walls thereof, and the doors thereof, with gold; and graved cherubims on the walls.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78c96764-1fec-455a-8031-afc9f444ffea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: 2CH 3:8
Text: And he made the most holy house, the length whereof was according to the breadth of the house, twenty cubits, and the breadth thereof twenty cubits: and he overlaid it with fine gold, amounting to six hundred talents.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61609d73-4732-4e59-9bdc-a76297316d92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: 2CH 3:9
Text: And the weight of the nails was fifty shekels of gold. And he overlaid the upper chambers with gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8310f157-3ff5-4e02-90c7-7340534a3bb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: 2CH 3:10
Text: And in the most holy house he made two cherubims of image work, and overlaid them with gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79249316-d723-43b2-be8e-6f18724b7021>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: 2CH 3:11
Text: And the wings of the cherubims were twenty cubits long: one wing of the one cherub was five cubits, reaching to the wall of the house: and the other wing was likewise five cubits, reaching to the wing of the other cherub.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41bf9fcc-8d5a-4e6e-be12-1011b96bce8e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: 2CH 3:12
Text: And one wing of the other cherub was five cubits, reaching to the wall of the house: and the other wing was five cubits also, joining to the wing of the other cherub.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2dded90c-7523-4889-89b8-f7fe69e4b9f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 2CH 3:13
Text: The wings of these cherubims spread themselves forth twenty cubits: and they stood on their feet, and their faces were inward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
