Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 2CH 3:14
Text: And he made the vail of blue, and purple, and crimson, and fine linen, and wrought cherubims thereon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2df40d7e-b49e-42ef-84c4-a5e5c37a77fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 2CH 3:15
Text: Also he made before the house two pillars of thirty and five cubits high, and the chapiter that was on the top of each of them was five cubits.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b25fffe-8272-4dd5-b76f-5329c5885c77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: 2CH 3:16
Text: And he made chains, as in the oracle, and put them on the heads of the pillars; and made an hundred pomegranates, and put them on the chains.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65584e47-064e-48ed-a817-b139cd55def5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: 2CH 3:17
Text: And he reared up the pillars before the temple, one on the right hand, and the other on the left; and called the name of that on the right hand Jachin, and the name of that on the left Boaz.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1351ae95-e634-48c9-9ef4-204b45b6a064>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: 2CH 4:1
Text: Moreover he made an altar of brass, twenty cubits the length thereof, and twenty cubits the breadth thereof, and ten cubits the height thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bcac9d91-3507-4089-a06f-fd70196ecce9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: 2CH 4:2
Text: Also he made a molten sea of ten cubits from brim to brim, round in compass, and five cubits the height thereof; and a line of thirty cubits did compass it round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58c1d0c8-2171-4605-9baf-fc0b91006759>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: 2CH 4:3
Text: And under it was the similitude of oxen, which did compass it round about: ten in a cubit, compassing the sea round about. Two rows of oxen were cast, when it was cast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f482d0b7-6937-48ad-93e4-118fcb02b36e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: 2CH 4:4
Text: It stood upon twelve oxen, three looking toward the north, and three looking toward the west, and three looking toward the south, and three looking toward the east: and the sea was set above upon them, and all their hinder parts were inward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bbca96ef-699d-42b2-bd6b-a32366f0e0ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: 2CH 4:5
Text: And the thickness of it was an handbreadth, and the brim of it like the work of the brim of a cup, with flowers of lilies; and it received and held three thousand baths.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48592da8-092a-49c1-a4db-a65611028adb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: 2CH 4:6
Text: He made also ten lavers, and put five on the right hand, and five on the left, to wash in them: such things as they offered for the burnt offering they washed in them; but the sea was for the priests to wash in.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48cfe978-f8be-4619-95da-3e023f3d3f6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 2CH 4:7
Text: And he made ten candlesticks of gold according to their form, and set them in the temple, five on the right hand, and five on the left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40c5130e-a50b-4e54-98c2-3fd81e0821e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: 2CH 4:8
Text: He made also ten tables, and placed them in the temple, five on the right side, and five on the left. And he made an hundred basons of gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5aed71d6-dcda-4497-82a9-c18841b9bd76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 2CH 4:9
Text: Furthermore he made the court of the priests, and the great court, and doors for the court, and overlaid the doors of them with brass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88932bf6-7294-45f1-a925-d2d91900b09a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: 2CH 4:10
Text: And he set the sea on the right side of the east end, over against the south.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06f7efe9-f3d1-4940-a689-4b24c6e1b0a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: 2CH 4:11
Text: And Huram made the pots, and the shovels, and the basons. And Huram finished the work that he was to make for king Solomon for the house of God;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
