Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 61

Reference: 2CH 4:15
Text: One sea, and twelve oxen under it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09a22d69-91df-49fb-9c15-5e00720453ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: 2CH 4:16
Text: The pots also, and the shovels, and the fleshhooks, and all their instruments, did Huram his father make to king Solomon for the house of the LORD of bright brass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4a0cff8-d422-4f9c-b62d-9edcdc3de738>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: 2CH 4:17
Text: In the plain of Jordan did the king cast them, in the clay ground between Succoth and Zeredathah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/4/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5e493c5-7d05-4a30-a27a-2de0555f5531>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: 2CH 4:18
Text: Thus Solomon made all these vessels in great abundance: for the weight of the brass could not be found out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/4/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bc96e79-179c-402e-9593-55d92bacfd46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 2CH 4:19
Text: And Solomon made all the vessels that were for the house of God, the golden altar also, and the tables whereon the shewbread was set;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/4/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
