Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: 2CH 4:20
Text: Moreover the candlesticks with their lamps, that they should burn after the manner before the oracle, of pure gold;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/4/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:396d172f-583b-42fb-af17-4dd42bfbfcdb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: 2CH 4:21
Text: And the flowers, and the lamps, and the tongs, made he of gold, and that perfect gold;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/4/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:674d1e46-d926-4784-9500-faa5cf1bb470>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: 2CH 4:22
Text: And the snuffers, and the basons, and the spoons, and the censers, of pure gold: and the entry of the house, the inner doors thereof for the most holy place, and the doors of the house of the temple, were of gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae42d58a-1500-48dd-ab72-f80ed5589efc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 279

Reference: 2CH 5:1
Text: Thus all the work that Solomon made for the house of the LORD was finished: and Solomon brought in all the things that David his father had dedicated; and the silver, and the gold, and all the instruments, put he among the treasures of the house of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85f8fccc-f71c-43c4-89c5-ad4fba1009ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: 2CH 5:2
Text: Then Solomon assembled the elders of Israel, and all the heads of the tribes, the chief of the fathers of the children of Israel, unto Jerusalem, to bring up the ark of the covenant of the LORD out of the city of David, which is Zion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec613151-deb5-4af7-8921-56b5fa7860b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 2CH 5:3
Text: Wherefore all the men of Israel assembled themselves unto the king in the feast which was in the seventh month.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e221122f-c7eb-4425-97dd-b94a2ed6a269>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: 2CH 5:4
Text: And all the elders of Israel came; and the Levites took up the ark.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bf7be05-8e59-4173-bc9a-d5737fa20e25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: 2CH 5:5
Text: And they brought up the ark, and the tabernacle of the congregation, and all the holy vessels that were in the tabernacle, these did the priests and the Levites bring up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:923fc293-841f-4332-be59-47263c8f314e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: 2CH 5:6
Text: Also king Solomon, and all the congregation of Israel that were assembled unto him before the ark, sacrificed sheep and oxen, which could not be told nor numbered for multitude.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe8ef5b1-c1dc-4652-a0a6-5ce90059b442>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: 2CH 5:7
Text: And the priests brought in the ark of the covenant of the LORD unto his place, to the oracle of the house, into the most holy place, even under the wings of the cherubims:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea5f1d55-1d5a-43ab-ac6a-b48e48b2245a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: 2CH 5:8
Text: For the cherubims spread forth their wings over the place of the ark, and the cherubims covered the ark and the staves thereof above.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da68db61-63e6-4285-963c-6576b32d7587>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: 2CH 5:9
Text: And they drew out the staves of the ark, that the ends of the staves were seen from the ark before the oracle; but they were not seen without. And there it is unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3538656c-d8e5-4995-aa17-989cb13349af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: 2CH 5:10
Text: There was nothing in the ark save the two tables which Moses put therein at Horeb, when the LORD made a covenant with the children of Israel, when they came out of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a115c9be-9b05-4c0b-abae-664b94631be5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: 2CH 5:11
Text: And it came to pass, when the priests were come out of the holy place: (for all the priests that were present were sanctified, and did not then wait by course:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:126d76ac-0e87-4487-9a3e-cb9da930c9b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 324

Reference: 2CH 5:12
Text: Also the Levites which were the singers, all of them of Asaph, of Heman, of Jeduthun, with their sons and their brethren, being arrayed in white linen, having cymbals and psalteries and harps, stood at the east end of the altar, and with them an hundred and twenty priests sounding with trumpets:)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c6d4498-caa0-44ae-9ecf-fbed5f59f9e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 401

Reference: 2CH 5:13
Text: It came even to pass, as the trumpeters and singers were as one, to make one sound to be heard in praising and thanking the LORD; and when they lifted up their voice with the trumpets and cymbals and instruments of musick, and praised the LORD, saying, For he is good; for his mercy endureth for ever: that then the house was filled with a cloud, even the house of the LORD;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5809722a-76c8-4927-9ccf-35499a193e41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 2CH 5:14
Text: So that the priests could not stand to minister by reason of the cloud: for the glory of the LORD had filled the house of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:105ab5a6-264e-4da7-b8b5-70ef899a4afa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: 2CH 6:1
Text: Then said Solomon, The LORD hath said that he would dwell in the thick darkness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78180fa7-211b-41f5-a809-6671008c8707>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: 2CH 6:2
Text: But I have built an house of habitation for thee, and a place for thy dwelling for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85982428-13e2-44f2-9332-4c34e68de167>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: 2CH 6:3
Text: And the king turned his face, and blessed the whole congregation of Israel: and all the congregation of Israel stood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2510a98d-6557-40fd-8aba-82e7686f2464>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 2CH 6:4
Text: And he said, Blessed be the LORD God of Israel, who hath with his hands fulfilled that which he spake with his mouth to my father David, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fdc5204-4bab-4c75-b9d1-2712f025f837>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: 2CH 6:5
Text: Since the day that I brought forth my people out of the land of Egypt I chose no city among all the tribes of Israel to build an house in, that my name might be there; neither chose I any man to be a ruler over my people Israel:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d67d06de-0bb4-44f7-ac6c-80afabb9b6eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: 2CH 6:6
Text: But I have chosen Jerusalem, that my name might be there; and have chosen David to be over my people Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:414da626-31a0-45c8-8a21-bcef53cfb4f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: 2CH 6:7
Text: Now it was in the heart of David my father to build an house for the name of the LORD God of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97f180c7-92f6-4543-853c-da7236565085>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: 2CH 6:8
Text: But the LORD said to David my father, Forasmuch as it was in thine heart to build an house for my name, thou didst well in that it was in thine heart:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a639a268-a71c-42a0-9a20-d4eabbacf012>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: 2CH 6:9
Text: Notwithstanding thou shalt not build the house; but thy son which shall come forth out of thy loins, he shall build the house for my name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87f0917b-9ed7-4d42-b880-a6c44ef0b9ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: 2CH 6:10
Text: The LORD therefore hath performed his word that he hath spoken: for I am risen up in the room of David my father, and am set on the throne of Israel, as the LORD promised, and have built the house for the name of the LORD God of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:faa640f1-5201-4cb8-928e-d08fead2fa50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 2CH 6:11
Text: And in it have I put the ark, wherein is the covenant of the LORD, that he made with the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54e9a808-dee5-4ab0-87aa-2c86ddd52fa5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 2CH 6:12
Text: And he stood before the altar of the LORD in the presence of all the congregation of Israel, and spread forth his hands:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8cad760d-eaa6-45c7-bfab-6615f5d4c164>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 309

Reference: 2CH 6:13
Text: For Solomon had made a brasen scaffold of five cubits long, and five cubits broad, and three cubits high, and had set it in the midst of the court: and upon it he stood, and kneeled down upon his knees before all the congregation of Israel, and spread forth his hands toward heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3b318fc-6401-4b51-b1e3-a07121bdb24b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: 2CH 6:14
Text: And said, O LORD God of Israel, there is no God like thee in the heaven, nor in the earth; which keepest covenant, and shewest mercy unto thy servants, that walk before thee with all their hearts:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af6e4cfc-5940-4685-a3a8-0148bd76d573>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: 2CH 6:15
Text: Thou which hast kept with thy servant David my father that which thou hast promised him; and spakest with thy mouth, and hast fulfilled it with thine hand, as it is this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74ce8e62-c949-45c2-96bd-5e0ad0511720>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 320

Reference: 2CH 6:16
Text: Now therefore, O LORD God of Israel, keep with thy servant David my father that which thou hast promised him, saying, There shall not fail thee a man in my sight to sit upon the throne of Israel; yet so that thy children take heed to their way to walk in my law, as thou hast walked before me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:139f2211-6d2c-47d4-9424-b5aeae1d4199>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: 2CH 6:17
Text: Now then, O LORD God of Israel, let thy word be verified, which thou hast spoken unto thy servant David.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f09df1f-9fe4-4a2b-a156-3a3e075e3826>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 2CH 6:18
Text: But will God in very deed dwell with men on the earth? behold, heaven and the heaven of heavens cannot contain thee; how much less this house which I have built!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d19651d2-d464-44f8-9b89-23ef7342b5e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: 2CH 6:19
Text: Have respect therefore to the prayer of thy servant, and to his supplication, O LORD my God, to hearken unto the cry and the prayer which thy servant prayeth before thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19415e91-8472-4663-bf8d-26c1f1f694d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: 2CH 6:20
Text: That thine eyes may be open upon this house day and night, upon the place whereof thou hast said that thou wouldest put thy name there; to hearken unto the prayer which thy servant prayeth toward this place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bf5753c-ec6d-4225-b21d-6804bc5fb844>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: 2CH 6:21
Text: Hearken therefore unto the supplications of thy servant, and of thy people Israel, which they shall make toward this place: hear thou from thy dwelling place, even from heaven; and when thou hearest, forgive.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:668f3021-9cb4-4d01-b889-9eea1a0de9c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 2CH 6:22
Text: If a man sin against his neighbour, and an oath be laid upon him to make him swear, and the oath come before thine altar in this house;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5e03002-fccb-4a47-8647-81a320bd1252>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: 2CH 6:23
Text: Then hear thou from heaven, and do, and judge thy servants, by requiting the wicked, by recompensing his way upon his own head; and by justifying the righteous, by giving him according to his righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ac2e0f8-138e-4244-b4c3-2b2fff2c30a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: 2CH 6:24
Text: And if thy people Israel be put to the worse before the enemy, because they have sinned against thee; and shall return and confess thy name, and pray and make supplication before thee in this house;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a894d3b-5506-461f-900c-3c69f970a736>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: 2CH 6:25
Text: Then hear thou from the heavens, and forgive the sin of thy people Israel, and bring them again unto the land which thou gavest to them and to their fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b60397a6-303a-4511-a1a7-a9d3d6cab2ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: 2CH 6:26
Text: When the heaven is shut up, and there is no rain, because they have sinned against thee; yet if they pray toward this place, and confess thy name, and turn from their sin, when thou dost afflict them;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31a23557-97ca-48dd-9419-3390b6365122>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: 2CH 6:27
Text: Then hear thou from heaven, and forgive the sin of thy servants, and of thy people Israel, when thou hast taught them the good way, wherein they should walk; and send rain upon thy land, which thou hast given unto thy people for an inheritance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7114f26d-4169-4e22-bdb4-f753e8c10e74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: 2CH 6:28
Text: If there be dearth in the land, if there be pestilence, if there be blasting, or mildew, locusts, or caterpillers; if their enemies besiege them in the cities of their land; whatsoever sore or whatsoever sickness there be:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9e022f7-c5e1-4e8e-81f0-ac980cb7a628>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: 2CH 6:29
Text: Then what prayer or what supplication soever shall be made of any man, or of all thy people Israel, when every one shall know his own sore and his own grief, and shall spread forth his hands in this house:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acb62efa-ff58-45c2-b516-fba03dca49d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: 2CH 6:30
Text: Then hear thou from heaven thy dwelling place, and forgive, and render unto every man according unto all his ways, whose heart thou knowest; (for thou only knowest the hearts of the children of men:)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef6ccc44-e5fc-4624-beca-16cf30088646>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 2CH 6:31
Text: That they may fear thee, to walk in thy ways, so long as they live in the land which thou gavest unto our fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6386134a-f41a-4c46-84d1-97d490abbf54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: 2CH 6:32
Text: Moreover concerning the stranger, which is not of thy people Israel, but is come from a far country for thy great name’s sake, and thy mighty hand, and thy stretched out arm; if they come and pray in this house;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4e16e06-a30f-47d0-ae28-75a227170d35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 313

Reference: 2CH 6:33
Text: Then hear thou from the heavens, even from thy dwelling place, and do according to all that the stranger calleth to thee for; that all people of the earth may know thy name, and fear thee, as doth thy people Israel, and may know that this house which I have built is called by thy name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca537554-a7eb-4016-898a-2b93237624dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: 2CH 6:34
Text: If thy people go out to war against their enemies by the way that thou shalt send them, and they pray unto thee toward this city which thou hast chosen, and the house which I have built for thy name;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5475908-bc74-4ebd-8079-08fe444351f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 2CH 6:35
Text: Then hear thou from the heavens their prayer and their supplication, and maintain their cause.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e02b37e1-ef8e-4d04-8b3e-1fd804f65e45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: 2CH 6:36
Text: If they sin against thee, (for there is no man which sinneth not,) and thou be angry with them, and deliver them over before their enemies, and they carry them away captives unto a land far off or near;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dac4b375-d2c8-4124-a177-c2affb594ae8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: 2CH 6:37
Text: Yet if they bethink themselves in the land whither they are carried captive, and turn and pray unto thee in the land of their captivity, saying, We have sinned, we have done amiss, and have dealt wickedly;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb2e0be0-c84f-40a3-b557-89baf49944e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 331

Reference: 2CH 6:38
Text: If they return to thee with all their heart and with all their soul in the land of their captivity, whither they have carried them captives, and pray toward their land, which thou gavest unto their fathers, and toward the city which thou hast chosen, and toward the house which I have built for thy name:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3afe6f3-b491-4e61-ae87-7b6f9aecb49d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: 2CH 6:39
Text: Then hear thou from the heavens, even from thy dwelling place, their prayer and their supplications, and maintain their cause, and forgive thy people which have sinned against thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e875728f-edbc-4b88-81af-20245f77181a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 2CH 6:40
Text: Now, my God, let, I beseech thee, thine eyes be open, and let thine ears be attent unto the prayer that is made in this place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6eac3145-a982-4892-b888-aca9142d4610>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: 2CH 6:41
Text: Now therefore arise, O LORD God, into thy resting place, thou, and the ark of thy strength: let thy priests, O LORD God, be clothed with salvation, and let thy saints rejoice in goodness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/6/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21c744ac-3404-4b39-8e92-3e62ece393f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 2CH 6:42
Text: O LORD God, turn not away the face of thine anointed: remember the mercies of David thy servant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae0110bd-c10f-4a98-82a4-88742fa70d83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: 2CH 7:1
Text: Now when Solomon had made an end of praying, the fire came down from heaven, and consumed the burnt offering and the sacrifices; and the glory of the LORD filled the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8b5e032-1c5a-4931-bc51-e35bb68d98c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: 2CH 7:2
Text: And the priests could not enter into the house of the LORD, because the glory of the LORD had filled the LORD’s house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a612fec-ab81-4eac-82e9-0ef90a94c38f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 298

Reference: 2CH 7:3
Text: And when all the children of Israel saw how the fire came down, and the glory of the LORD upon the house, they bowed themselves with their faces to the ground upon the pavement, and worshipped, and praised the LORD, saying, For he is good; for his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2262456f-de27-4a2f-9ac4-5c054c04f4c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: 2CH 7:4
Text: Then the king and all the people offered sacrifices before the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7505adc0-a37a-44fe-afb3-eac8920251c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: 2CH 7:5
Text: And king Solomon offered a sacrifice of twenty and two thousand oxen, and an hundred and twenty thousand sheep: so the king and all the people dedicated the house of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a80c9c0b-05e7-4df2-bff6-f3c2375435f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 316

Reference: 2CH 7:6
Text: And the priests waited on their offices: the Levites also with instruments of musick of the LORD, which David the king had made to praise the LORD, because his mercy endureth for ever, when David praised by their ministry; and the priests sounded trumpets before them, and all Israel stood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0040b5b0-b794-4bea-8b4d-8fc701910002>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 318

Reference: 2CH 7:7
Text: Moreover Solomon hallowed the middle of the court that was before the house of the LORD: for there he offered burnt offerings, and the fat of the peace offerings, because the brasen altar which Solomon had made was not able to receive the burnt offerings, and the meat offerings, and the fat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c068ee0-94ef-4804-a277-cacb04d4c91a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: 2CH 7:8
Text: Also at the same time Solomon kept the feast seven days, and all Israel with him, a very great congregation, from the entering in of Hamath unto the river of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ea5f2c7-fcd4-49fa-b7f1-6903ef0bc228>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: 2CH 7:9
Text: And in the eighth day they made a solemn assembly: for they kept the dedication of the altar seven days, and the feast seven days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e17ae0a-fcfc-49d4-bf9a-55fb87d37bd4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: 2CH 7:10
Text: And on the three and twentieth day of the seventh month he sent the people away into their tents, glad and merry in heart for the goodness that the LORD had shewed unto David, and to Solomon, and to Israel his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2c40553-6e4d-47cb-b5ee-639d1c186285>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: 2CH 7:11
Text: Thus Solomon finished the house of the LORD, and the king’s house: and all that came into Solomon’s heart to make in the house of the LORD, and in his own house, he prosperously effected.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40cf9374-386c-4039-ab3b-03e1cfcf6e6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 2CH 7:12
Text: And the LORD appeared to Solomon by night, and said unto him, I have heard thy prayer, and have chosen this place to myself for an house of sacrifice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a2fb9d4-7079-4cf2-985b-6b2bff4a4922>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 2CH 7:13
Text: If I shut up heaven that there be no rain, or if I command the locusts to devour the land, or if I send pestilence among my people;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/7/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34ffc7c0-fd25-46db-bf7c-422892dcabf8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: 2CH 7:14
Text: If my people, which are called by my name, shall humble themselves, and pray, and seek my face, and turn from their wicked ways; then will I hear from heaven, and will forgive their sin, and will heal their land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/7/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe2e3c3e-36a0-4059-a346-3e7cad446115>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: 2CH 7:15
Text: Now mine eyes shall be open, and mine ears attent unto the prayer that is made in this place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/7/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ef94368-2061-4f9d-89d2-d51175b1659f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: 2CH 7:16
Text: For now have I chosen and sanctified this house, that my name may be there for ever: and mine eyes and mine heart shall be there perpetually.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/7/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aca6a150-1348-4532-873b-459c330207f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 2CH 7:17
Text: And as for thee, if thou wilt walk before me, as David thy father walked, and do according to all that I have commanded thee, and shalt observe my statutes and my judgments;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/7/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:232da49b-c187-4457-90e8-ca39d53c5530>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: 2CH 7:18
Text: Then will I stablish the throne of thy kingdom, according as I have covenanted with David thy father, saying, There shall not fail thee a man to be ruler in Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/7/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3ff53fa-64a0-4079-814c-c137bf484c6d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: 2CH 7:19
Text: But if ye turn away, and forsake my statutes and my commandments, which I have set before you, and shall go and serve other gods, and worship them;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/7/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32b0efcd-7fd3-4c2d-aff7-7274703a8b96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: 2CH 7:20
Text: Then will I pluck them up by the roots out of my land which I have given them; and this house, which I have sanctified for my name, will I cast out of my sight, and will make it to be a proverb and a byword among all nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/7/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d6b075f-5edf-4a44-aa56-19758636b873>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: 2CH 7:21
Text: And this house, which is high, shall be an astonishment to every one that passeth by it; so that he shall say, Why hath the LORD done thus unto this land, and unto this house?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/7/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:273b9500-7ef8-461d-8c45-b7dffea3433c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 273

Reference: 2CH 7:22
Text: And it shall be answered, Because they forsook the LORD God of their fathers, which brought them forth out of the land of Egypt, and laid hold on other gods, and worshipped them, and served them: therefore hath he brought all this evil upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/8/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:763da8d6-b763-44ef-9a6b-5614fe3f4119>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 2CH 8:1
Text: And it came to pass at the end of twenty years, wherein Solomon had built the house of the LORD, and his own house,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/8/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86326c0e-8017-41da-9e99-6a066250b896>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 2CH 8:2
Text: That the cities which Huram had restored to Solomon, Solomon built them, and caused the children of Israel to dwell there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/8/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9da8e558-bf47-4493-b302-23779b6a854a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: 2CH 8:3
Text: And Solomon went to Hamathzobah, and prevailed against it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/8/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7970712a-bac2-4dea-aa99-83c0bbc1a429>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: 2CH 8:4
Text: And he built Tadmor in the wilderness, and all the store cities, which he built in Hamath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/8/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae7eb6d9-c069-4099-b478-a92ecfec0d70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: 2CH 8:5
Text: Also he built Bethhoron the upper, and Bethhoron the nether, fenced cities, with walls, gates, and bars;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/8/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e47f276-bf05-42ae-acf7-a73d8f874bb9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: 2CH 8:6
Text: And Baalath, and all the store cities that Solomon had, and all the chariot cities, and the cities of the horsemen, and all that Solomon desired to build in Jerusalem, and in Lebanon, and throughout all the land of his dominion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/8/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29280dc2-8ae5-4f2d-b03b-0d1c5c985525>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 2CH 8:7
Text: As for all the people that were left of the Hittites, and the Amorites, and the Perizzites, and the Hivites, and the Jebusites, which were not of Israel,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/8/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51db65a4-fa76-4d37-b6a3-e8436ac5fdf9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: 2CH 8:8
Text: But of their children, who were left after them in the land, whom the children of Israel consumed not, them did Solomon make to pay tribute until this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/8/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35b07d5a-0c55-444c-a5a9-e9b75e6dd7fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: 2CH 8:9
Text: But of the children of Israel did Solomon make no servants for his work; but they were men of war, and chief of his captains, and captains of his chariots and horsemen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/8/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfb874cd-81d3-4849-81cf-eceb2d83c885>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 2CH 8:10
Text: And these were the chief of king Solomon’s officers, even two hundred and fifty, that bare rule over the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/8/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91921348-f71e-4ad9-ba42-5086360dee41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 285

Reference: 2CH 8:11
Text: And Solomon brought up the daughter of Pharaoh out of the city of David unto the house that he had built for her: for he said, My wife shall not dwell in the house of David king of Israel, because the places are holy, whereunto the ark of the LORD hath come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/8/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec335dba-7179-463e-b855-85f73b014174>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 2CH 8:12
Text: Then Solomon offered burnt offerings unto the LORD on the altar of the LORD, which he had built before the porch,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/8/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b32c9938-8b5f-48e9-8339-f182c538cc0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 300

Reference: 2CH 8:13
Text: Even after a certain rate every day, offering according to the commandment of Moses, on the sabbaths, and on the new moons, and on the solemn feasts, three times in the year, even in the feast of unleavened bread, and in the feast of weeks, and in the feast of tabernacles.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/8/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:311631f4-458a-446b-a4b0-f38c3e3b249c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 337

Reference: 2CH 8:14
Text: And he appointed, according to the order of David his father, the courses of the priests to their service, and the Levites to their charges, to praise and minister before the priests, as the duty of every day required: the porters also by their courses at every gate: for so had David the man of God commanded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/8/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bff5172c-3fd0-4fa1-8aa1-3eec842bf94a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 2CH 8:15
Text: And they departed not from the commandment of the king unto the priests and Levites concerning any matter, or concerning the treasures.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/8/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56fcda47-f94c-4a7e-9a45-8b43dcd571e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: 2CH 8:16
Text: Now all the work of Solomon was prepared unto the day of the foundation of the house of the LORD, and until it was finished. So the house of the LORD was perfected.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/8/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9d82f89-750f-42cd-8d33-2b2815dccf5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: 2CH 8:17
Text: Then went Solomon to Eziongeber, and to Eloth, at the sea side in the land of Edom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/8/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b75e503a-f24d-484b-a9a7-502e782f0476>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: 2CH 8:18
Text: And Huram sent him by the hands of his servants ships, and servants that had knowledge of the sea; and they went with the servants of Solomon to Ophir, and took thence four hundred and fifty talents of gold, and brought them to king Solomon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8cb540c-5698-40dc-a6b8-50a46bdae524>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 329

Reference: 2CH 9:1
Text: And when the queen of Sheba heard of the fame of Solomon, she came to prove Solomon with hard questions at Jerusalem, with a very great company, and camels that bare spices, and gold in abundance, and precious stones: and when she was come to Solomon, she communed with him of all that was in her heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:720352e0-51b0-4022-95bf-bb789bed807a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 2CH 9:2
Text: And Solomon told her all her questions: and there was nothing hid from Solomon which he told her not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dadec15f-f7eb-4044-b01c-6208cbd17a7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: 2CH 9:3
Text: And when the queen of Sheba had seen the wisdom of Solomon, and the house that he had built,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2d01874-ec75-47c0-bebb-7b160965f6a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 277

Reference: 2CH 9:4
Text: And the meat of his table, and the sitting of his servants, and the attendance of his ministers, and their apparel; his cupbearers also, and their apparel; and his ascent by which he went up into the house of the LORD; there was no more spirit in her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd091feb-5a8c-4c65-86de-033b562b5021>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 2CH 9:5
Text: And she said to the king, It was a true report which I heard in mine own land of thine acts, and of thy wisdom:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d063e204-e0cd-4a19-b17f-902aab5de727>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: 2CH 9:6
Text: Howbeit I believed not their words, until I came, and mine eyes had seen it: and, behold, the one half of the greatness of thy wisdom was not told me: for thou exceedest the fame that I heard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:604352fb-a75c-4d5e-ba17-8885aa7a50d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: 2CH 9:7
Text: Happy are thy men, and happy are these thy servants, which stand continually before thee, and hear thy wisdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:228cd174-97b9-485a-9b62-29aeed1cb6a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: 2CH 9:8
Text: Blessed be the LORD thy God, which delighted in thee to set thee on his throne, to be king for the LORD thy God: because thy God loved Israel, to establish them for ever, therefore made he thee king over them, to do judgment and justice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8dd8f117-8873-43db-8fc5-bc9d8523b691>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: 2CH 9:9
Text: And she gave the king an hundred and twenty talents of gold, and of spices great abundance, and precious stones: neither was there any such spice as the queen of Sheba gave king Solomon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92133d94-9fc9-403f-b5f3-67f1dc1e9679>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: 2CH 9:10
Text: And the servants also of Huram, and the servants of Solomon, which brought gold from Ophir, brought algum trees and precious stones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e832377-6e26-4e9a-a070-85c4721b4079>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: 2CH 9:11
Text: And the king made of the algum trees terraces to the house of the LORD, and to the king’s palace, and harps and psalteries for singers: and there were none such seen before in the land of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c33afbe5-1ccf-4bfd-8e17-85fdcf13c6b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: 2CH 9:12
Text: And king Solomon gave to the queen of Sheba all her desire, whatsoever she asked, beside that which she had brought unto the king. So she turned, and went away to her own land, she and her servants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7abfd7eb-85a3-4085-ac78-3336db267680>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: 2CH 9:13
Text: Now the weight of gold that came to Solomon in one year was six hundred and threescore and six talents of gold;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4bab61b-5ac5-47a6-ae85-5e9521e0fe59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: 2CH 9:14
Text: Beside that which chapmen and merchants brought. And all the kings of Arabia and governors of the country brought gold and silver to Solomon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9cf028f-bd15-4ba4-9a54-9d74ff5c2030>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: 2CH 9:15
Text: And king Solomon made two hundred targets of beaten gold: six hundred shekels of beaten gold went to one target.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a3867b9-50fc-4330-9b63-f55f2ed4cb30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 2CH 9:16
Text: And three hundred shields made he of beaten gold: three hundred shekels of gold went to one shield. And the king put them in the house of the forest of Lebanon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38b26fc5-c1ea-49f1-b8ab-8c4300a1e04b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: 2CH 9:17
Text: Moreover the king made a great throne of ivory, and overlaid it with pure gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a93e150-c635-437b-9104-fef4195f30f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: 2CH 9:18
Text: And there were six steps to the throne, with a footstool of gold, which were fastened to the throne, and stays on each side of the sitting place, and two lions standing by the stays:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d1cdc5f-04bb-4ed7-9d57-6dd414ee34d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: 2CH 9:19
Text: And twelve lions stood there on the one side and on the other upon the six steps. There was not the like made in any kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6984322e-02a4-449a-999b-b0fe8aa28ffe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: 2CH 9:20
Text: And all the drinking vessels of king Solomon were of gold, and all the vessels of the house of the forest of Lebanon were of pure gold: none were of silver; it was not any thing accounted of in the days of Solomon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95ed5579-1c9d-44eb-9474-e01b54da951b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: 2CH 9:21
Text: For the king’s ships went to Tarshish with the servants of Huram: every three years once came the ships of Tarshish bringing gold, and silver, ivory, and apes, and peacocks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c838e98-b83c-460e-9499-e488c6c39396>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: 2CH 9:22
Text: And king Solomon passed all the kings of the earth in riches and wisdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b19b0305-d764-44d5-bd1a-2808e5bfe2a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 2CH 9:23
Text: And all the kings of the earth sought the presence of Solomon, to hear his wisdom, that God had put in his heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f19a901e-3b92-4f36-9dc5-862723f875a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: 2CH 9:24
Text: And they brought every man his present, vessels of silver, and vessels of gold, and raiment, harness, and spices, horses, and mules, a rate year by year.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe8539f6-9957-4e06-98b0-99e67170f1b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: 2CH 9:25
Text: And Solomon had four thousand stalls for horses and chariots, and twelve thousand horsemen; whom he bestowed in the chariot cities, and with the king at Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbb72889-3920-41bd-adf0-2d89d56355b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: 2CH 9:26
Text: And he reigned over all the kings from the river even unto the land of the Philistines, and to the border of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de7cabde-11a1-41ec-bedd-62d438818d91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 2CH 9:27
Text: And the king made silver in Jerusalem as stones, and cedar trees made he as the sycomore trees that are in the low plains in abundance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e5b5751-5b89-4e6a-9989-51fc71ba3465>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: 2CH 9:28
Text: And they brought unto Solomon horses out of Egypt, and out of all lands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74956415-4edd-491f-8f5f-822d84a103e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: 2CH 9:29
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Solomon, first and last, are they not written in the book of Nathan the prophet, and in the prophecy of Ahijah the Shilonite, and in the visions of Iddo the seer against Jeroboam the son of Nebat?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff2e7dc1-f87d-4b0d-b8fc-5060b08a378f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: 2CH 9:30
Text: And Solomon reigned in Jerusalem over all Israel forty years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/9/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81d92c89-c777-45d3-8434-edb6d99b0d77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: 2CH 9:31
Text: And Solomon slept with his fathers, and he was buried in the city of David his father: and Rehoboam his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/10/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2c1b83f-be2b-4d65-a39a-d73d3504d667>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: 2CH 10:1
Text: And Rehoboam went to Shechem: for to Shechem were all Israel come to make him king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/10/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8aca2d0-0415-4914-b395-c3a15c4a4a0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: 2CH 10:2
Text: And it came to pass, when Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who was in Egypt, whither he fled from the presence of Solomon the king, heard it, that Jeroboam returned out of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/10/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93ef76a5-2264-4e97-a842-47190e50a229>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: 2CH 10:3
Text: And they sent and called him. So Jeroboam and all Israel came and spake to Rehoboam, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/10/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c99bc38c-ab97-43ce-9903-821c24d71d9e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: 2CH 10:4
Text: Thy father made our yoke grievous: now therefore ease thou somewhat the grievous servitude of thy father, and his heavy yoke that he put upon us, and we will serve thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/10/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30d9a727-fba3-4f23-af41-7ed0c0ce875a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: 2CH 10:5
Text: And he said unto them, Come again unto me after three days. And the people departed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/10/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a942e26-50e0-4864-bf17-34300daae6d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 2CH 10:6
Text: And king Rehoboam took counsel with the old men that had stood before Solomon his father while he yet lived, saying, What counsel give ye me to return answer to this people?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/10/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d022c6f7-3df4-4433-a94e-077a44410706>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: 2CH 10:7
Text: And they spake unto him, saying, If thou be kind to this people, and please them, and speak good words to them, they will be thy servants for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/10/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e270237b-a204-437e-b513-ff38ec58dd6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: 2CH 10:8
Text: But he forsook the counsel which the old men gave him, and took counsel with the young men that were brought up with him, that stood before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/10/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:687706d3-65ff-4c6d-b41a-3cecf15a1fc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 2CH 10:9
Text: And he said unto them, What advice give ye that we may return answer to this people, which have spoken to me, saying, Ease somewhat the yoke that thy father did put upon us?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/10/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f48b3a46-17b8-427b-8509-8394889e5ab4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 328

Reference: 2CH 10:10
Text: And the young men that were brought up with him spake unto him, saying, Thus shalt thou answer the people that spake unto thee, saying, Thy father made our yoke heavy, but make thou it somewhat lighter for us; thus shalt thou say unto them, My little finger shall be thicker than my father’s loins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/10/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bd3e85a-c6ab-4e23-ae27-407420ded558>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: 2CH 10:11
Text: For whereas my father put a heavy yoke upon you, I will put more to your yoke: my father chastised you with whips, but I will chastise you with scorpions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/10/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26bdab9c-f953-4ee9-97a8-4a8f7ff41e88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: 2CH 10:12
Text: So Jeroboam and all the people came to Rehoboam on the third day, as the king bade, saying, Come again to me on the third day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/10/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94fcf7f1-faa4-4b37-956f-195f94dbe6ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: 2CH 10:13
Text: And the king answered them roughly; and king Rehoboam forsook the counsel of the old men,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/10/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a33f632-d148-4c06-8d38-b414861822d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: 2CH 10:14
Text: And answered them after the advice of the young men, saying, My father made your yoke heavy, but I will add thereto: my father chastised you with whips, but I will chastise you with scorpions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/10/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3e7610d-496b-43a5-93a6-1db46d941577>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: 2CH 10:15
Text: So the king hearkened not unto the people: for the cause was of God, that the LORD might perform his word, which he spake by the hand of Ahijah the Shilonite to Jeroboam the son of Nebat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/10/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81f15448-a061-4bb9-8793-e4a62003be3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 323

Reference: 2CH 10:16
Text: And when all Israel saw that the king would not hearken unto them, the people answered the king, saying, What portion have we in David? and we have none inheritance in the son of Jesse: every man to your tents, O Israel: and now, David, see to thine own house. So all Israel went to their tents.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/10/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce7decfb-c04b-4f9d-8994-bf02f6fb192e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: 2CH 10:17
Text: But as for the children of Israel that dwelt in the cities of Judah, Rehoboam reigned over them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/10/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d33b0490-b3d6-4bd4-a1a7-10e9a9d60283>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: 2CH 10:18
Text: Then king Rehoboam sent Hadoram that was over the tribute; and the children of Israel stoned him with stones, that he died. But king Rehoboam made speed to get him up to his chariot, to flee to Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/10/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25f1d13e-8664-49dd-9208-9881f88e6a99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: 2CH 10:19
Text: And Israel rebelled against the house of David unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/11/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e03cc540-e039-4e0a-aa78-20933863a3b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: 2CH 11:1
Text: And when Rehoboam was come to Jerusalem, he gathered of the house of Judah and Benjamin an hundred and fourscore thousand chosen men, which were warriors, to fight against Israel, that he might bring the kingdom again to Rehoboam.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/11/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
