Content-Length: 281

Reference: 2CH 12:5
Text: Then came Shemaiah the prophet to Rehoboam, and to the princes of Judah, that were gathered together to Jerusalem because of Shishak, and said unto them, Thus saith the LORD, Ye have forsaken me, and therefore have I also left you in the hand of Shishak.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/12/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1472d18-d31d-41ab-a6c9-009245b6cd35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: 2CH 12:6
Text: Whereupon the princes of Israel and the king humbled themselves; and they said, The LORD is righteous.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/12/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:215c2b01-7643-4fa0-816e-22d81adede01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 306

Reference: 2CH 12:7
Text: And when the LORD saw that they humbled themselves, the word of the LORD came to Shemaiah, saying, They have humbled themselves; therefore I will not destroy them, but I will grant them some deliverance; and my wrath shall not be poured out upon Jerusalem by the hand of Shishak.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/12/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6f6c76c-26c3-4f77-86bc-9326fe988989>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 2CH 12:8
Text: Nevertheless they shall be his servants; that they may know my service, and the service of the kingdoms of the countries.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/12/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a4d946a-28c8-4f0a-81f8-c9458eec848f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: 2CH 12:9
Text: So Shishak king of Egypt came up against Jerusalem, and took away the treasures of the house of the LORD, and the treasures of the king’s house; he took all: he carried away also the shields of gold which Solomon had made.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/12/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b40c8363-38eb-4d67-b4c7-c333a75484dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: 2CH 12:10
Text: Instead of which king Rehoboam made shields of brass, and committed them to the hands of the chief of the guard, that kept the entrance of the king’s house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/12/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93f00fa1-801b-4e93-adc8-cd21aae9a558>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 2CH 12:11
Text: And when the king entered into the house of the LORD, the guard came and fetched them, and brought them again into the guard chamber.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/12/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1316146-f67c-4356-8a49-9415ccad62ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 2CH 12:12
Text: And when he humbled himself, the wrath of the LORD turned from him, that he would not destroy him altogether: and also in Judah things went well.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/12/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fe82aac-4682-4dba-b956-86bf9e08a028>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 343

Reference: 2CH 12:13
Text: So king Rehoboam strengthened himself in Jerusalem, and reigned: for Rehoboam was one and forty years old when he began to reign, and he reigned seventeen years in Jerusalem, the city which the LORD had chosen out of all the tribes of Israel, to put his name there. And his mother’s name was Naamah an Ammonitess.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/12/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4c9ee47-c384-4999-bbb5-256e08bb7457>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: 2CH 12:14
Text: And he did evil, because he prepared not his heart to seek the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/12/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:774e0fa4-4c13-41e6-a28f-941eeb9a4312>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: 2CH 12:15
Text: Now the acts of Rehoboam, first and last, are they not written in the book of Shemaiah the prophet, and of Iddo the seer concerning genealogies? And there were wars between Rehoboam and Jeroboam continually.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/12/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb77c63a-8840-4d5f-bf8c-3fc366ea3a75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: 2CH 12:16
Text: And Rehoboam slept with his fathers, and was buried in the city of David: and Abijah his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/13/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:757ba21d-e548-45bd-afaf-6625744cb42a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: 2CH 13:1
Text: Now in the eighteenth year of king Jeroboam began Abijah to reign over Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/13/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e305021-3cc5-42a0-8c4b-710c2ddfae28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: 2CH 13:2
Text: He reigned three years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name also was Michaiah the daughter of Uriel of Gibeah. And there was war between Abijah and Jeroboam.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/13/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01062147-529d-43b7-8af6-83160c3f6fbd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: 2CH 13:3
Text: And Abijah set the battle in array with an army of valiant men of war, even four hundred thousand chosen men: Jeroboam also set the battle in array against him with eight hundred thousand chosen men, being mighty men of valour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/13/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:528c90dc-14ba-4cfc-98a9-34b0eb8cb2ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: 2CH 13:4
Text: And Abijah stood up upon mount Zemaraim, which is in mount Ephraim, and said, Hear me, thou Jeroboam, and all Israel;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/13/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e4e3715-df94-489b-a6e2-d138a88a1e81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: 2CH 13:5
Text: Ought ye not to know that the LORD God of Israel gave the kingdom over Israel to David for ever, even to him and to his sons by a covenant of salt?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/13/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe75b2ef-e507-4a32-b5ec-a0f58dc62ca9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 2CH 13:6
Text: Yet Jeroboam the son of Nebat, the servant of Solomon the son of David, is risen up, and hath rebelled against his lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/13/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65fe6a09-de76-4cb4-a605-94f746edda41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: 2CH 13:7
Text: And there are gathered unto him vain men, the children of Belial, and have strengthened themselves against Rehoboam the son of Solomon, when Rehoboam was young and tenderhearted, and could not withstand them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/13/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f6c704a-e59a-41e8-8274-7f6e874f861a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: 2CH 13:8
Text: And now ye think to withstand the kingdom of the LORD in the hand of the sons of David; and ye be a great multitude, and there are with you golden calves, which Jeroboam made you for gods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/13/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c6735ce-6ef3-4471-af99-bbcc0b5251f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 317

Reference: 2CH 13:9
Text: Have ye not cast out the priests of the LORD, the sons of Aaron, and the Levites, and have made you priests after the manner of the nations of other lands? so that whosoever cometh to consecrate himself with a young bullock and seven rams, the same may be a priest of them that are no gods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/13/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7296a558-c942-4119-9614-c69bcf735243>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: 2CH 13:10
Text: But as for us, the LORD is our God, and we have not forsaken him; and the priests, which minister unto the LORD, are the sons of Aaron, and the Levites wait upon their business:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/13/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ac56c2f-afe4-4c37-a183-a8e6efe9073a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 326

Reference: 2CH 13:11
Text: And they burn unto the LORD every morning and every evening burnt sacrifices and sweet incense: the shewbread also set they in order upon the pure table; and the candlestick of gold with the lamps thereof, to burn every evening: for we keep the charge of the LORD our God; but ye have forsaken him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/13/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e84983a8-9045-484f-b12c-2d9d02da433d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: 2CH 13:12
Text: And, behold, God himself is with us for our captain, and his priests with sounding trumpets to cry alarm against you. O children of Israel, fight ye not against the LORD God of your fathers; for ye shall not prosper.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/13/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef24a4ce-9183-4a25-a5c6-e0eb521a1b62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: 2CH 13:13
Text: But Jeroboam caused an ambushment to come about behind them: so they were before Judah, and the ambushment was behind them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/13/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa891362-4720-4579-aed5-291d04fad219>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 2CH 13:14
Text: And when Judah looked back, behold, the battle was before and behind: and they cried unto the LORD, and the priests sounded with the trumpets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/13/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9eb69ab3-d305-40e7-9d3a-9936405100e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 2CH 13:15
Text: Then the men of Judah gave a shout: and as the men of Judah shouted, it came to pass, that God smote Jeroboam and all Israel before Abijah and Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/13/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57b01f5f-71fe-4f2d-b1cf-0e61dc94a78b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: 2CH 13:16
Text: And the children of Israel fled before Judah: and God delivered them into their hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/13/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37f6d6ab-00c5-4da1-8782-dae9268c63a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: 2CH 13:17
Text: And Abijah and his people slew them with a great slaughter: so there fell down slain of Israel five hundred thousand chosen men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/13/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4cd20d4-04c6-4a1e-b9dd-5306c0d4f900>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: 2CH 13:18
Text: Thus the children of Israel were brought under at that time, and the children of Judah prevailed, because they relied upon the LORD God of their fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/13/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93e44663-a9b2-4aff-850d-3f8290129d08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: 2CH 13:19
Text: And Abijah pursued after Jeroboam, and took cities from him, Bethel with the towns thereof, and Jeshanah with the towns thereof, and Ephraim with the towns thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/13/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc0bc5f6-ff6d-4356-acae-ee2a67ac6b6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 2CH 13:20
Text: Neither did Jeroboam recover strength again in the days of Abijah: and the LORD struck him, and he died.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/13/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a80652d1-9bec-4901-8e8c-62c81eaad9dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: 2CH 13:21
Text: But Abijah waxed mighty, and married fourteen wives, and begat twenty and two sons, and sixteen daughters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/13/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba22dd72-c715-4616-a605-45cf87b1ca66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 2CH 13:22
Text: And the rest of the acts of Abijah, and his ways, and his sayings, are written in the story of the prophet Iddo.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/14/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d32b82c-9667-4343-b6f4-d3974c7d28b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: 2CH 14:1
Text: So Abijah slept with his fathers, and they buried him in the city of David: and Asa his son reigned in his stead. In his days the land was quiet ten years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/14/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8b8f1e7-41dc-4669-9777-160015db360f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: 2CH 14:2
Text: And Asa did that which was good and right in the eyes of the LORD his God:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/14/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:694617f4-50f1-41b8-8116-9ca89b038ca8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 2CH 14:3
Text: For he took away the altars of the strange gods, and the high places, and brake down the images, and cut down the groves:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/14/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89046647-26ea-4bfc-bc66-da4397219ec4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: 2CH 14:4
Text: And commanded Judah to seek the LORD God of their fathers, and to do the law and the commandment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/14/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5697e3e9-daf2-4523-b3d2-368949a067d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 2CH 14:5
Text: Also he took away out of all the cities of Judah the high places and the images: and the kingdom was quiet before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/14/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2696d9d5-e10b-4b73-8c17-363d60208c1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 2CH 14:6
Text: And he built fenced cities in Judah: for the land had rest, and he had no war in those years; because the LORD had given him rest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/14/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97ad000d-6447-4ce5-8491-a128533f5975>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 303

Reference: 2CH 14:7
Text: Therefore he said unto Judah, Let us build these cities, and make about them walls, and towers, gates, and bars, while the land is yet before us; because we have sought the LORD our God, we have sought him, and he hath given us rest on every side. So they built and prospered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/14/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54b4b665-c747-4efc-ad48-1a29c8dca729>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: 2CH 14:8
Text: And Asa had an army of men that bare targets and spears, out of Judah three hundred thousand; and out of Benjamin, that bare shields and drew bows, two hundred and fourscore thousand: all these were mighty men of valour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/14/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72510338-423c-4083-a5ad-3f36f588aed9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 2CH 14:9
Text: And there came out against them Zerah the Ethiopian with an host of a thousand thousand, and three hundred chariots; and came unto Mareshah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/14/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06b4a620-eba0-4972-b53c-191cceff45fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: 2CH 14:10
Text: Then Asa went out against him, and they set the battle in array in the valley of Zephathah at Mareshah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/14/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a2ce58f-bafd-44ff-9e3b-012ef3ce1645>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 316

Reference: 2CH 14:11
Text: And Asa cried unto the LORD his God, and said, LORD, it is nothing with thee to help, whether with many, or with them that have no power: help us, O LORD our God; for we rest on thee, and in thy name we go against this multitude. O LORD, thou art our God; let no man prevail against thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/14/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a569c764-3a04-44d0-ab2b-d6a281b23f30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: 2CH 14:12
Text: So the LORD smote the Ethiopians before Asa, and before Judah; and the Ethiopians fled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/14/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43a3ec83-a764-4822-8dd3-2c319d537787>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: 2CH 14:13
Text: And Asa and the people that were with him pursued them unto Gerar: and the Ethiopians were overthrown, that they could not recover themselves; for they were destroyed before the LORD, and before his host; and they carried away very much spoil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/14/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:735edea2-f82d-482a-a452-10912fdec2be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: 2CH 14:14
Text: And they smote all the cities round about Gerar; for the fear of the LORD came upon them: and they spoiled all the cities; for there was exceeding much spoil in them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/14/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f4e4b74-5506-4861-a5f1-590a6ed3b05c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: 2CH 14:15
Text: They smote also the tents of cattle, and carried away sheep and camels in abundance, and returned to Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/15/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ac09ead-314e-495f-9b21-076c46589e37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: 2CH 15:1
Text: And the Spirit of God came upon Azariah the son of Oded:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/15/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4dd123ef-473d-40d9-be5d-8a47ff71cdce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: 2CH 15:2
Text: And he went out to meet Asa, and said unto him, Hear ye me, Asa, and all Judah and Benjamin; The LORD is with you, while ye be with him; and if ye seek him, he will be found of you; but if ye forsake him, he will forsake you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/15/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:def91b87-5ee0-4961-84c9-1dca0ac4b4d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 2CH 15:3
Text: Now for a long season Israel hath been without the true God, and without a teaching priest, and without law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/15/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8807d93c-3df6-4890-9f9c-c012180b9ae0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: 2CH 15:4
Text: But when they in their trouble did turn unto the LORD God of Israel, and sought him, he was found of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/15/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a34c8e8b-bcf3-4d0d-8dda-ab338fed610a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 2CH 15:5
Text: And in those times there was no peace to him that went out, nor to him that came in, but great vexations were upon all the inhabitants of the countries.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/15/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b12da684-afad-419f-acc3-8d19710e61b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 2CH 15:6
Text: And nation was destroyed of nation, and city of city: for God did vex them with all adversity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/15/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d230153e-25e6-4432-aba7-adf79565c101>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: 2CH 15:7
Text: Be ye strong therefore, and let not your hands be weak: for your work shall be rewarded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/15/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f9d0884-0a24-4130-b079-92d7f870044c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 325

Reference: 2CH 15:8
Text: And when Asa heard these words, and the prophecy of Oded the prophet, he took courage, and put away the abominable idols out of all the land of Judah and Benjamin, and out of the cities which he had taken from mount Ephraim, and renewed the altar of the LORD, that was before the porch of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/15/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1617033-7f9a-46bf-98ca-1e1fb1ff71f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: 2CH 15:9
Text: And he gathered all Judah and Benjamin, and the strangers with them out of Ephraim and Manasseh, and out of Simeon: for they fell to him out of Israel in abundance, when they saw that the LORD his God was with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/15/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63b04e05-a6b5-401d-8be3-55291a6aa106>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 2CH 15:10
Text: So they gathered themselves together at Jerusalem in the third month, in the fifteenth year of the reign of Asa.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/15/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e091b1b-a32f-43b0-9dcc-95f629618d3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 2CH 15:11
Text: And they offered unto the LORD the same time, of the spoil which they had brought, seven hundred oxen and seven thousand sheep.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/15/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a199c719-41c2-48ce-b689-eaf9361cff15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: 2CH 15:12
Text: And they entered into a covenant to seek the LORD God of their fathers with all their heart and with all their soul;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/15/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b677352c-b690-4bfb-978c-f08ee2543ce7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: 2CH 15:13
Text: That whosoever would not seek the LORD God of Israel should be put to death, whether small or great, whether man or woman.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/15/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c43a3c14-692e-4581-8da9-d7b8196e3259>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: 2CH 15:14
Text: And they sware unto the LORD with a loud voice, and with shouting, and with trumpets, and with cornets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/15/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b31eaea-f572-44df-8ee4-b6cd8d36838c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: 2CH 15:15
Text: And all Judah rejoiced at the oath: for they had sworn with all their heart, and sought him with their whole desire; and he was found of them: and the LORD gave them rest round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/15/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c88c034-2ff6-41a7-942b-7035c3da9437>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: 2CH 15:16
Text: And also concerning Maachah the mother of Asa the king, he removed her from being queen, because she had made an idol in a grove: and Asa cut down her idol, and stamped it, and burnt it at the brook Kidron.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/15/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:061beabf-f917-4bb4-82a5-d7f852415a55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: 2CH 15:17
Text: But the high places were not taken away out of Israel: nevertheless the heart of Asa was perfect all his days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/15/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1750c8d6-6348-4bb0-a254-c28a2f5d9990>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: 2CH 15:18
Text: And he brought into the house of God the things that his father had dedicated, and that he himself had dedicated, silver, and gold, and vessels.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/15/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7e2c455-44a4-4ac9-b13c-fa926f199356>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: 2CH 15:19
Text: And there was no more war unto the five and thirtieth year of the reign of Asa.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/16/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbc3d950-1c82-40a7-8504-8f3d4d36a5fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: 2CH 16:1
Text: In the six and thirtieth year of the reign of Asa Baasha king of Israel came up against Judah, and built Ramah, to the intent that he might let none go out or come in to Asa king of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/16/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:629bb4dd-5b2d-443c-8519-df578b753af8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: 2CH 16:2
Text: Then Asa brought out silver and gold out of the treasures of the house of the LORD and of the king’s house, and sent to Benhadad king of Syria, that dwelt at Damascus, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/16/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d07b56b0-f03f-41d1-a525-2ecd953bf49c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: 2CH 16:3
Text: There is a league between me and thee, as there was between my father and thy father: behold, I have sent thee silver and gold; go, break thy league with Baasha king of Israel, that he may depart from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/16/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0bad60a-511c-42e8-964f-b9c7bc5cb3ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: 2CH 16:4
Text: And Benhadad hearkened unto king Asa, and sent the captains of his armies against the cities of Israel; and they smote Ijon, and Dan, and Abelmaim, and all the store cities of Naphtali.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/16/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:753ba50b-1c4a-4c6d-97db-338540044434>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: 2CH 16:5
Text: And it came to pass, when Baasha heard it, that he left off building of Ramah, and let his work cease.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/16/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50e026d5-cdee-4a79-81d6-6c05acae89b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: 2CH 16:6
Text: Then Asa the king took all Judah; and they carried away the stones of Ramah, and the timber thereof, wherewith Baasha was building; and he built therewith Geba and Mizpah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/16/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e4bd9ce-27a1-4e57-9512-2b912b93b33b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: 2CH 16:7
Text: And at that time Hanani the seer came to Asa king of Judah, and said unto him, Because thou hast relied on the king of Syria, and not relied on the LORD thy God, therefore is the host of the king of Syria escaped out of thine hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/16/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3268c4ad-a2c4-4218-b647-4d378fdd388e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: 2CH 16:8
Text: Were not the Ethiopians and the Lubims a huge host, with very many chariots and horsemen? yet, because thou didst rely on the LORD, he delivered them into thine hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/16/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebc4c137-3734-447b-907e-8b666bf8cf9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: 2CH 16:9
Text: For the eyes of the LORD run to and fro throughout the whole earth, to shew himself strong in the behalf of them whose heart is perfect toward him. Herein thou hast done foolishly: therefore from henceforth thou shalt have wars.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/16/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e40cde14-d9be-4c37-9ff4-9a30abe77886>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: 2CH 16:10
Text: Then Asa was wroth with the seer, and put him in a prison house; for he was in a rage with him because of this thing. And Asa oppressed some of the people the same time.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/16/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2795a667-d89e-4e12-a7d4-7ef70891441e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 2CH 16:11
Text: And, behold, the acts of Asa, first and last, lo, they are written in the book of the kings of Judah and Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/16/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0f706f5-1035-4620-9e1e-03bfb13daf99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: 2CH 16:12
Text: And Asa in the thirty and ninth year of his reign was diseased in his feet, until his disease was exceeding great: yet in his disease he sought not to the LORD, but to the physicians.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/16/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4738dcf5-dbed-4367-aae8-588dccc1b23e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: 2CH 16:13
Text: And Asa slept with his fathers, and died in the one and fortieth year of his reign.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/16/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d567e3de-f144-4464-a0a9-d32825b6311c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 289

Reference: 2CH 16:14
Text: And they buried him in his own sepulchres, which he had made for himself in the city of David, and laid him in the bed which was filled with sweet odours and divers kinds of spices prepared by the apothecaries’ art: and they made a very great burning for him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/17/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e469a751-f009-41ce-a391-b368e9bbddcf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: 2CH 17:1
Text: And Jehoshaphat his son reigned in his stead, and strengthened himself against Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/17/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98d50dda-09fa-4138-bfe3-8b0414317904>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: 2CH 17:2
Text: And he placed forces in all the fenced cities of Judah, and set garrisons in the land of Judah, and in the cities of Ephraim, which Asa his father had taken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/17/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76359a7c-af6b-4558-88c7-f1db8aa89c16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: 2CH 17:3
Text: And the LORD was with Jehoshaphat, because he walked in the first ways of his father David, and sought not unto Baalim;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/17/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:adf0838b-b2f0-4181-b2bc-c0a2c48ca922>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: 2CH 17:4
Text: But sought to the Lord God of his father, and walked in his commandments, and not after the doings of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/17/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80467a83-3b48-4c10-a8bb-be1b9c318644>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: 2CH 17:5
Text: Therefore the LORD stablished the kingdom in his hand; and all Judah brought to Jehoshaphat presents; and he had riches and honour in abundance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/17/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dac57f22-7ea8-4422-afbd-4e5ee540cc2b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: 2CH 17:6
Text: And his heart was lifted up in the ways of the LORD: moreover he took away the high places and groves out of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/17/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00fe011e-19da-4005-bd7c-e83c7bd15fcb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: 2CH 17:7
Text: Also in the third year of his reign he sent to his princes, even to Benhail, and to Obadiah, and to Zechariah, and to Nethaneel, and to Michaiah, to teach in the cities of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/17/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eaaaad16-5800-4206-9f76-76be65aee073>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: 2CH 17:8
Text: And with them he sent Levites, even Shemaiah, and Nethaniah, and Zebadiah, and Asahel, and Shemiramoth, and Jehonathan, and Adonijah, and Tobijah, and Tobadonijah, Levites; and with them Elishama and Jehoram, priests.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/17/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a09abacb-dee9-4601-9cc9-27a2fabe7e78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 2CH 17:9
Text: And they taught in Judah, and had the book of the law of the LORD with them, and went about throughout all the cities of Judah, and taught the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/17/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d22549a2-83ee-4468-bccb-ffa8499366c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 2CH 17:10
Text: And the fear of the LORD fell upon all the kingdoms of the lands that were round about Judah, so that they made no war against Jehoshaphat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/17/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:409f9350-1b83-4f4d-bb82-a7220c928a7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: 2CH 17:11
Text: Also some of the Philistines brought Jehoshaphat presents, and tribute silver; and the Arabians brought him flocks, seven thousand and seven hundred rams, and seven thousand and seven hundred he goats.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/17/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e211565-a175-4acb-b9c8-d17f85ed3ae4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: 2CH 17:12
Text: And Jehoshaphat waxed great exceedingly; and he built in Judah castles, and cities of store.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/17/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60cc7dcf-93d8-42b4-945b-de85c449b8e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 2CH 17:13
Text: And he had much business in the cities of Judah: and the men of war, mighty men of valour, were in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/17/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f4fc339-1ccd-4eab-a5da-82b5e6fcc3f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: 2CH 17:14
Text: And these are the numbers of them according to the house of their fathers: Of Judah, the captains of thousands; Adnah the chief, and with him mighty men of valour three hundred thousand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/17/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:062b5f8a-82ab-4498-b6bf-8c207194c997>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: 2CH 17:15
Text: And next to him was Jehohanan the captain, and with him two hundred and fourscore thousand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/17/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:665f6723-8649-46db-8613-8a004f8238d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: 2CH 17:16
Text: And next him was Amasiah the son of Zichri, who willingly offered himself unto the LORD; and with him two hundred thousand mighty men of valour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/17/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11e7a537-d49f-4eae-a307-9aa6cda3f45d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 2CH 17:17
Text: And of Benjamin; Eliada a mighty man of valour, and with him armed men with bow and shield two hundred thousand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/17/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:742dc31b-1c9d-4b58-818f-f42e531fdb33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: 2CH 17:18
Text: And next him was Jehozabad, and with him an hundred and fourscore thousand ready prepared for the war.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/17/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a92fd635-8aa6-4bfd-aaa1-1db9eebbaedb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 2CH 17:19
Text: These waited on the king, beside those whom the king put in the fenced cities throughout all Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:038c4b10-df7d-4330-8921-4fcfd8629d99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: 2CH 18:1
Text: Now Jehoshaphat had riches and honour in abundance, and joined affinity with Ahab.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9df9a104-2386-4c07-96f7-ab93e7434535>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: 2CH 18:2
Text: And after certain years he went down to Ahab to Samaria. And Ahab killed sheep and oxen for him in abundance, and for the people that he had with him, and persuaded him to go up with him to Ramothgilead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:793375d3-c1df-4126-94c6-ae74ed1f8282>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: 2CH 18:3
Text: And Ahab king of Israel said unto Jehoshaphat king of Judah, Wilt thou go with me to Ramothgilead? And he answered him, I am as thou art, and my people as thy people; and we will be with thee in the war.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34a56130-53ea-44bd-84a4-594b01553bb2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: 2CH 18:4
Text: And Jehoshaphat said unto the king of Israel, Enquire, I pray thee, at the word of the LORD to day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:503bbd44-5e72-4f14-ba09-107bcc191b18>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: 2CH 18:5
Text: Therefore the king of Israel gathered together of prophets four hundred men, and said unto them, Shall we go to Ramothgilead to battle, or shall I forbear? And they said, Go up; for God will deliver it into the king’s hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6d1afcc-ef17-4f47-863c-b6e1477262e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 2CH 18:6
Text: But Jehoshaphat said, Is there not here a prophet of the LORD besides, that we might enquire of him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4b37b91-6d93-4a54-90ac-74d4aa300f4f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 285

Reference: 2CH 18:7
Text: And the king of Israel said unto Jehoshaphat, There is yet one man, by whom we may enquire of the LORD: but I hate him; for he never prophesied good unto me, but always evil: the same is Micaiah the son of Imla. And Jehoshaphat said, Let not the king say so.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2738b049-8dbf-4451-a137-6de6511b4283>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: 2CH 18:8
Text: And the king of Israel called for one of his officers, and said, Fetch quickly Micaiah the son of Imla.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d0facc5-5943-41c1-baa7-d2a00266b70d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: 2CH 18:9
Text: And the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat king of Judah sat either of them on his throne, clothed in their robes, and they sat in a void place at the entering in of the gate of Samaria; and all the prophets prophesied before them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7cd6574-06f5-4b23-bbe7-91a047f0e47c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 2CH 18:10
Text: And Zedekiah the son of Chenaanah had made him horns of iron, and said, Thus saith the LORD, With these thou shalt push Syria until they be consumed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfa28250-fcf8-4b07-82b3-002d68ba056b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: 2CH 18:11
Text: And all the prophets prophesied so, saying, Go up to Ramothgilead, and prosper: for the LORD shall deliver it into the hand of the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39d6b13d-6aba-4b40-b000-a433e0d84f64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: 2CH 18:12
Text: And the messenger that went to call Micaiah spake to him, saying, Behold, the words of the prophets declare good to the king with one assent; let thy word therefore, I pray thee, be like one of theirs, and speak thou good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36328feb-ced6-4f52-ba45-17c76aa26387>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: 2CH 18:13
Text: And Micaiah said, As the LORD liveth, even what my God saith, that will I speak.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f663ee1e-18db-4ab4-b3ec-073353b9f87a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: 2CH 18:14
Text: And when he was come to the king, the king said unto him, Micaiah, shall we go to Ramothgilead to battle, or shall I forbear? And he said, Go ye up, and prosper, and they shall be delivered into your hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:181c7115-9f98-4b5a-b33d-474936afd4f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 2CH 18:15
Text: And the king said to him, How many times shall I adjure thee that thou say nothing but the truth to me in the name of the LORD?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c756efc0-d9fa-4471-83c2-2f2ae3efef57>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: 2CH 18:16
Text: Then he said, I did see all Israel scattered upon the mountains, as sheep that have no shepherd: and the LORD said, These have no master; let them return therefore every man to his house in peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61d8bc48-b37b-4d02-bdc7-7c81e03e89de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: 2CH 18:17
Text: And the king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat, Did I not tell thee that he would not prophesy good unto me, but evil?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70a095a5-f2bc-4a38-a7f4-6eec36e4715d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: 2CH 18:18
Text: Again he said, Therefore hear the word of the LORD; I saw the LORD sitting upon his throne, and all the host of heaven standing on his right hand and on his left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5fc86999-ab4c-4eb5-8f9b-f10df568b7f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: 2CH 18:19
Text: And the LORD said, Who shall entice Ahab king of Israel, that he may go up and fall at Ramothgilead? And one spake saying after this manner, and another saying after that manner.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ba7d09d-fea1-4240-afc9-e994315ff404>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: 2CH 18:20
Text: Then there came out a spirit, and stood before the LORD, and said, I will entice him. And the LORD said unto him, Wherewith?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9bce6c9e-0817-4ec0-aaee-984163e45d4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: 2CH 18:21
Text: And he said, I will go out, and be a lying spirit in the mouth of all his prophets. And the Lord said, Thou shalt entice him, and thou shalt also prevail: go out, and do even so.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40613ef5-f471-4236-99d5-b3859cfaa9f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: 2CH 18:22
Text: Now therefore, behold, the LORD hath put a lying spirit in the mouth of these thy prophets, and the LORD hath spoken evil against thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a74c44e-44c9-43c5-80dc-8ceeb8685335>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: 2CH 18:23
Text: Then Zedekiah the son of Chenaanah came near, and smote Micaiah upon the cheek, and said, Which way went the Spirit of the LORD from me to speak unto thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07226907-bef2-4efb-8439-be20ed5104d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: 2CH 18:24
Text: And Micaiah said, Behold, thou shalt see on that day when thou shalt go into an inner chamber to hide thyself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd86c31f-2484-42ae-ae4a-a8e047a98264>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 2CH 18:25
Text: Then the king of Israel said, Take ye Micaiah, and carry him back to Amon the governor of the city, and to Joash the king’s son;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9811fc51-4d73-49cb-978b-629bd36f482c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: 2CH 18:26
Text: And say, Thus saith the king, Put this fellow in the prison, and feed him with bread of affliction and with water of affliction, until I return in peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d37ed705-1f52-46c2-bd1b-ba411e0a7f0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: 2CH 18:27
Text: And Micaiah said, If thou certainly return in peace, then hath not the LORD spoken by me. And he said, Hearken, all ye people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19976356-d595-4fbd-b5ae-9bebae24b4b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: 2CH 18:28
Text: So the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat the king of Judah went up to Ramothgilead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edc9ae0f-5e72-4cdd-93d6-e3c38e66563c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: 2CH 18:29
Text: And the king of Israel said unto Jehoshaphat, I will disguise myself, and I will go to the battle; but put thou on thy robes. So the king of Israel disguised himself; and they went to the battle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b0bc2ec-b850-4d6c-bf4b-20450b4cd767>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: 2CH 18:30
Text: Now the king of Syria had commanded the captains of the chariots that were with him, saying, Fight ye not with small or great, save only with the king of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20ccee31-f2d1-47c2-97f0-1710434de4e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 277

Reference: 2CH 18:31
Text: And it came to pass, when the captains of the chariots saw Jehoshaphat, that they said, It is the king of Israel. Therefore they compassed about him to fight: but Jehoshaphat cried out, and the LORD helped him; and God moved them to depart from him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:443ec2c0-7b26-4a45-9201-2c78018fe1ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: 2CH 18:32
Text: For it came to pass, that, when the captains of the chariots perceived that it was not the king of Israel, they turned back again from pursuing him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e99cf3a7-e50e-4e9a-b610-8e2cb83ff354>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: 2CH 18:33
Text: And a certain man drew a bow at a venture, and smote the king of Israel between the joints of the harness: therefore he said to his chariot man, Turn thine hand, that thou mayest carry me out of the host; for I am wounded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/18/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c03b8e0-48de-42a5-b0c1-7a4d317b7dc5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: 2CH 18:34
Text: And the battle increased that day: howbeit the king of Israel stayed himself up in his chariot against the Syrians until the even: and about the time of the sun going down he died.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/19/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d24690d-fd9c-4f05-a9f6-bfadd0fced06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: 2CH 19:1
Text: And Jehoshaphat the king of Judah returned to his house in peace to Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/19/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:119a477c-8c16-4224-9f65-b1f5ee11987e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: 2CH 19:2
Text: And Jehu the son of Hanani the seer went out to meet him, and said to king Jehoshaphat, Shouldest thou help the ungodly, and love them that hate the LORD? therefore is wrath upon thee from before the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/19/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5438f41-ad79-4efe-a1d4-5fb541f2b3c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: 2CH 19:3
Text: Nevertheless there are good things found in thee, in that thou hast taken away the groves out of the land, and hast prepared thine heart to seek God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/19/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3565e702-a512-4573-b704-1586d17489ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: 2CH 19:4
Text: And Jehoshaphat dwelt at Jerusalem: and he went out again through the people from Beersheba to mount Ephraim, and brought them back unto the LORD God of their fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/19/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb98a454-bffe-49af-8edf-7794901f6ad2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: 2CH 19:5
Text: And he set judges in the land throughout all the fenced cities of Judah, city by city,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/19/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a105a75a-78b1-46aa-82f7-842dc13a3f61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: 2CH 19:6
Text: And said to the judges, Take heed what ye do: for ye judge not for man, but for the LORD, who is with you in the judgment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/19/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e47b2211-4812-4ca2-9604-3909bd644b65>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: 2CH 19:7
Text: Wherefore now let the fear of the LORD be upon you; take heed and do it: for there is no iniquity with the LORD our God, nor respect of persons, nor taking of gifts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/19/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7f57de6-0ff9-4ac7-a231-1ecbc2f59f6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: 2CH 19:8
Text: Moreover in Jerusalem did Jehoshaphat set of the Levites, and of the priests, and of the chief of the fathers of Israel, for the judgment of the LORD, and for controversies, when they returned to Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/19/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68ecf657-6bdd-491d-b1c1-4436e87f7b3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 2CH 19:9
Text: And he charged them, saying, Thus shall ye do in the fear of the LORD, faithfully, and with a perfect heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/19/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20197d0a-50fe-4ac9-92dc-dfa8a59c02ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 342

Reference: 2CH 19:10
Text: And what cause soever shall come to you of your brethren that dwell in your cities, between blood and blood, between law and commandment, statutes and judgments, ye shall even warn them that they trespass not against the LORD, and so wrath come upon you, and upon your brethren: this do, and ye shall not trespass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/19/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:250c9222-a4e3-478f-a259-d2117b3d897a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 304

Reference: 2CH 19:11
Text: And, behold, Amariah the chief priest is over you in all matters of the LORD; and Zebadiah the son of Ishmael, the ruler of the house of Judah, for all the king’s matters: also the Levites shall be officers before you. Deal courageously, and the LORD shall be with the good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da48bdfa-61a8-4fe1-89e5-f1334a6567f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: 2CH 20:1
Text: It came to pass after this also, that the children of Moab, and the children of Ammon, and with them other beside the Ammonites, came against Jehoshaphat to battle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09cf9875-1e8a-4c81-a3f5-8c4f47aa3d0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: 2CH 20:2
Text: Then there came some that told Jehoshaphat, saying, There cometh a great multitude against thee from beyond the sea on this side Syria; and, behold, they be in Hazazontamar, which is Engedi.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2aa9a3bf-f79f-4a6d-8384-0b47cffd2cd4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 2CH 20:3
Text: And Jehoshaphat feared, and set himself to seek the LORD, and proclaimed a fast throughout all Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69fc1087-388e-4061-b0be-6587cb70bbea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 2CH 20:4
Text: And Judah gathered themselves together, to ask help of the LORD: even out of all the cities of Judah they came to seek the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33d688ee-5cee-431e-aec1-9f2b7fdbd396>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 2CH 20:5
Text: And Jehoshaphat stood in the congregation of Judah and Jerusalem, in the house of the LORD, before the new court,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04fa687c-45a4-4856-b867-6c73c8c66e1e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: 2CH 20:6
Text: And said, O LORD God of our fathers, art not thou God in heaven? and rulest not thou over all the kingdoms of the heathen? and in thine hand is there not power and might, so that none is able to withstand thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bcf59d7b-5563-4b1d-86d6-7b1ff3abcabf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: 2CH 20:7
Text: Art not thou our God, who didst drive out the inhabitants of this land before thy people Israel, and gavest it to the seed of Abraham thy friend for ever?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99926e86-a927-4126-8895-1ea587561718>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: 2CH 20:8
Text: And they dwelt therein, and have built thee a sanctuary therein for thy name, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51b9dceb-4219-4358-940b-615ce336216a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: 2CH 20:9
Text: If, when evil cometh upon us, as the sword, judgment, or pestilence, or famine, we stand before this house, and in thy presence, (for thy name is in this house,) and cry unto thee in our affliction, then thou wilt hear and help.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abab807d-9423-479d-bed6-36ee85272332>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: 2CH 20:10
Text: And now, behold, the children of Ammon and Moab and mount Seir, whom thou wouldest not let Israel invade, when they came out of the land of Egypt, but they turned from them, and destroyed them not;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9493946b-5fd7-4155-9bb7-5f44e1285b74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 2CH 20:11
Text: Behold, I say, how they reward us, to come to cast us out of thy possession, which thou hast given us to inherit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e337317e-1801-4be7-b05e-338a7e74705d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: 2CH 20:12
Text: O our God, wilt thou not judge them? for we have no might against this great company that cometh against us; neither know we what to do: but our eyes are upon thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c09f6b0a-ed0b-4856-a00d-d9c534a7e1e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 2CH 20:13
Text: And all Judah stood before the LORD, with their little ones, their wives, and their children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dce5ae2b-8f94-4607-9f62-4d5c7759e96b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: 2CH 20:14
Text: Then upon Jahaziel the son of Zechariah, the son of Benaiah, the son of Jeiel, the son of Mattaniah, a Levite of the sons of Asaph, came the Spirit of the LORD in the midst of the congregation;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f97c7e4c-d6b3-41df-abc9-52ccc4607ed9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: 2CH 20:15
Text: And he said, Hearken ye, all Judah, and ye inhabitants of Jerusalem, and thou king Jehoshaphat, Thus saith the LORD unto you, Be not afraid nor dismayed by reason of this great multitude; for the battle is not yours, but God’s.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:638b0761-135d-40c6-a573-dc7d426573a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 2CH 20:16
Text: To morrow go ye down against them: behold, they come up by the cliff of Ziz; and ye shall find them at the end of the brook, before the wilderness of Jeruel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a51a801-9aac-4a0c-bd60-cedced845e4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: 2CH 20:17
Text: Ye shall not need to fight in this battle: set yourselves, stand ye still, and see the salvation of the LORD with you, O Judah and Jerusalem: fear not, nor be dismayed; to morrow go out against them: for the LORD will be with you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef175d60-68e9-43f4-b2a7-5b88e0067e07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: 2CH 20:18
Text: And Jehoshaphat bowed his head with his face to the ground: and all Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem fell before the LORD, worshipping the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dda8b011-2c49-41aa-9c03-7e844355992b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 2CH 20:19
Text: And the Levites, of the children of the Kohathites, and of the children of the Korhites, stood up to praise the LORD God of Israel with a loud voice on high.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c320a690-4761-4712-8f4d-a0d1220e99a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 312

Reference: 2CH 20:20
Text: And they rose early in the morning, and went forth into the wilderness of Tekoa: and as they went forth, Jehoshaphat stood and said, Hear me, O Judah, and ye inhabitants of Jerusalem; Believe in the LORD your God, so shall ye be established; believe his prophets, so shall ye prosper.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70252fc0-9b8f-4902-837c-13dd94ea5962>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: 2CH 20:21
Text: And when he had consulted with the people, he appointed singers unto the LORD, and that should praise the beauty of holiness, as they went out before the army, and to say, Praise the LORD; for his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc370e5c-e2bb-44f1-a27c-3d5a6e5b101a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: 2CH 20:22
Text: And when they began to sing and to praise, the LORD set ambushments against the children of Ammon, Moab, and mount Seir, which were come against Judah; and they were smitten.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3f6d87a-4af1-485b-acdf-8e9cb3eba29d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: 2CH 20:23
Text: For the children of Ammon and Moab stood up against the inhabitants of mount Seir, utterly to slay and destroy them: and when they had made an end of the inhabitants of Seir, every one helped to destroy another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c682359-cf76-4f51-8f6d-122075b5456d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: 2CH 20:24
Text: And when Judah came toward the watch tower in the wilderness, they looked unto the multitude, and, behold, they were dead bodies fallen to the earth, and none escaped.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92366897-68db-4272-bd34-cbd0e19fd769>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 331

Reference: 2CH 20:25
Text: And when Jehoshaphat and his people came to take away the spoil of them, they found among them in abundance both riches with the dead bodies, and precious jewels, which they stripped off for themselves, more than they could carry away: and they were three days in gathering of the spoil, it was so much.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ff6880c-bf67-4c64-a41f-bdc79387d8c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: 2CH 20:26
Text: And on the fourth day they assembled themselves in the valley of Berachah; for there they blessed the LORD: therefore the name of the same place was called, The valley of Berachah, unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ee27a27-7af1-4199-a4ce-ad225d8fa637>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: 2CH 20:27
Text: Then they returned, every man of Judah and Jerusalem, and Jehoshaphat in the forefront of them, to go again to Jerusalem with joy; for the LORD had made them to rejoice over their enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70ce7e30-e030-4594-ac3e-245f2cd5f328>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 2CH 20:28
Text: And they came to Jerusalem with psalteries and harps and trumpets unto the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a33502f7-ed66-4bfb-aa5f-f0a4f86866c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: 2CH 20:29
Text: And the fear of God was on all the kingdoms of those countries, when they had heard that the LORD fought against the enemies of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eccfbe46-cdcd-48f8-bbb8-b4ed2d45444f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: 2CH 20:30
Text: So the realm of Jehoshaphat was quiet: for his God gave him rest round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d81c9fa7-4cfd-4e3f-9584-6042b2ea9327>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: 2CH 20:31
Text: And Jehoshaphat reigned over Judah: he was thirty and five years old when he began to reign, and he reigned twenty and five years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Azubah the daughter of Shilhi.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b19b773a-d4f2-4b1e-a332-5c922fbfc7e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: 2CH 20:32
Text: And he walked in the way of Asa his father, and departed not from it, doing that which was right in the sight of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73ab606e-9283-4b49-87cf-39fb954a1184>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 2CH 20:33
Text: Howbeit the high places were not taken away: for as yet the people had not prepared their hearts unto the God of their fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f26a66c-3e5c-46f5-875e-cf8e42724f21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: 2CH 20:34
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Jehoshaphat, first and last, behold, they are written in the book of Jehu the son of Hanani, who is mentioned in the book of the kings of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4601db6-b9f7-4e58-948d-a1bf12eef586>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 2CH 20:35
Text: And after this did Jehoshaphat king of Judah join himself with Ahaziah king of Israel, who did very wickedly:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4e768e5-72bd-41e5-b0ec-d7cc015e050f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: 2CH 20:36
Text: And he joined himself with him to make ships to go to Tarshish: and they made the ships in Eziongaber.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/20/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dde4ff81-f322-4fef-9662-e46dd4217f38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: 2CH 20:37
Text: Then Eliezer the son of Dodavah of Mareshah prophesied against Jehoshaphat, saying, Because thou hast joined thyself with Ahaziah, the LORD hath broken thy works. And the ships were broken, that they were not able to go to Tarshish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/21/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5fc153b-4858-4834-85e5-b7afb6bcf23e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 2CH 21:1
Text: Now Jehoshaphat slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in the city of David. And Jehoram his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/21/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cab7fe68-22cf-41be-a1a1-0b7071b481bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: 2CH 21:2
Text: And he had brethren the sons of Jehoshaphat, Azariah, and Jehiel, and Zechariah, and Azariah, and Michael, and Shephatiah: all these were the sons of Jehoshaphat king of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/21/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:914347af-7591-4ba8-b4aa-88010bb007ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: 2CH 21:3
Text: And their father gave them great gifts of silver, and of gold, and of precious things, with fenced cities in Judah: but the kingdom gave he to Jehoram; because he was the firstborn.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/21/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:807ada50-9f8f-4cc6-9f87-6dffb3d0b166>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: 2CH 21:4
Text: Now when Jehoram was risen up to the kingdom of his father, he strengthened himself, and slew all his brethren with the sword, and divers also of the princes of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/21/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e5040ed-a43d-4928-8ac1-888388284494>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 2CH 21:5
Text: Jehoram was thirty and two years old when he began to reign, and he reigned eight years in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/21/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ac2b3b0-e7be-4deb-9224-fd2dc8ac7b1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: 2CH 21:6
Text: And he walked in the way of the kings of Israel, like as did the house of Ahab: for he had the daughter of Ahab to wife: and he wrought that which was evil in the eyes of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/21/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87ffbe3e-2bb2-4507-8a1d-3027e213958b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: 2CH 21:7
Text: Howbeit the LORD would not destroy the house of David, because of the covenant that he had made with David, and as he promised to give a light to him and to his sons for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/21/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae91c2d6-95e2-47d0-ab81-52dc4313e6ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: 2CH 21:8
Text: In his days the Edomites revolted from under the dominion of Judah, and made themselves a king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/21/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21f51a0c-d814-4a21-a768-9044161494e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: 2CH 21:9
Text: Then Jehoram went forth with his princes, and all his chariots with him: and he rose up by night, and smote the Edomites which compassed him in, and the captains of the chariots.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/21/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7a105e8-1f87-4795-80d8-80070839b470>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: 2CH 21:10
Text: So the Edomites revolted from under the hand of Judah unto this day. The same time also did Libnah revolt from under his hand; because he had forsaken the LORD God of his fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/21/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e86c5cdc-3767-4f55-a7bc-b49ddf359b86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: 2CH 21:11
Text: Moreover he made high places in the mountains of Judah and caused the inhabitants of Jerusalem to commit fornication, and compelled Judah thereto.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/21/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5742348-3f07-4bdf-b61b-a71f9643a5f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: 2CH 21:12
Text: And there came a writing to him from Elijah the prophet, saying, Thus saith the LORD God of David thy father, Because thou hast not walked in the ways of Jehoshaphat thy father, nor in the ways of Asa king of Judah,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/21/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c891dde1-b100-4714-9b1b-647d79eee376>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 282

Reference: 2CH 21:13
Text: But hast walked in the way of the kings of Israel, and hast made Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem to go a whoring, like to the whoredoms of the house of Ahab, and also hast slain thy brethren of thy father’s house, which were better than thyself:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/21/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:841ae3b8-6fe1-4a6d-9967-75a0675af215>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: 2CH 21:14
Text: Behold, with a great plague will the LORD smite thy people, and thy children, and thy wives, and all thy goods:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/21/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:056a4063-e328-4cc2-9382-a90499b1ee90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: 2CH 21:15
Text: And thou shalt have great sickness by disease of thy bowels, until thy bowels fall out by reason of the sickness day by day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/21/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:deac6848-e679-4286-a086-0c236c475323>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 2CH 21:16
Text: Moreover the LORD stirred up against Jehoram the spirit of the Philistines, and of the Arabians, that were near the Ethiopians:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/21/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac636963-e282-4417-a8ee-252ac31bf5ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: 2CH 21:17
Text: And they came up into Judah, and brake into it, and carried away all the substance that was found in the king’s house, and his sons also, and his wives; so that there was never a son left him, save Jehoahaz, the youngest of his sons.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/21/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ec7a710-60b5-4ba3-8f72-389eda826c90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: 2CH 21:18
Text: And after all this the LORD smote him in his bowels with an incurable disease.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/21/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5cc74234-fe7f-4947-9b0f-6c49a405d3b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: 2CH 21:19
Text: And it came to pass, that in process of time, after the end of two years, his bowels fell out by reason of his sickness: so he died of sore diseases. And his people made no burning for him, like the burning of his fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/21/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:403a4285-6284-439f-8b1a-c872b91f9945>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: 2CH 21:20
Text: Thirty and two years old was he when he began to reign, and he reigned in Jerusalem eight years, and departed without being desired. Howbeit they buried him in the city of David, but not in the sepulchres of the kings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/22/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbac3c1f-2064-40b7-83c8-9758d4b94849>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: 2CH 22:1
Text: And the inhabitants of Jerusalem made Ahaziah his youngest son king in his stead: for the band of men that came with the Arabians to the camp had slain all the eldest. So Ahaziah the son of Jehoram king of Judah reigned.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/22/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26ef7842-6e2a-4342-885d-aafbb4c03a5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: 2CH 22:2
Text: Forty and two years old was Ahaziah when he began to reign, and he reigned one year in Jerusalem. His mother’s name also was Athaliah the daughter of Omri.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/22/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69c6609e-e64f-4881-83fb-51db546a1450>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: 2CH 22:3
Text: He also walked in the ways of the house of Ahab: for his mother was his counsellor to do wickedly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/22/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f377cdf2-7a80-4768-b74e-c8df685fae94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 2CH 22:4
Text: Wherefore he did evil in the sight of the LORD like the house of Ahab: for they were his counsellors after the death of his father to his destruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/22/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2519567e-f4da-4436-9c05-1a7108b74f17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: 2CH 22:5
Text: He walked also after their counsel, and went with Jehoram the son of Ahab king of Israel to war against Hazael king of Syria at Ramothgilead: and the Syrians smote Joram.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/22/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a3cd869-f74f-4ac6-86e7-f2331b5c519f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 280

Reference: 2CH 22:6
Text: And he returned to be healed in Jezreel because of the wounds which were given him at Ramah, when he fought with Hazael king of Syria. And Azariah the son of Jehoram king of Judah went down to see Jehoram the son of Ahab at Jezreel, because he was sick.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/22/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64b04144-745a-4cef-8a39-4b445f85050f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: 2CH 22:7
Text: And the destruction of Ahaziah was of God by coming to Joram: for when he was come, he went out with Jehoram against Jehu the son of Nimshi, whom the LORD had anointed to cut off the house of Ahab.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/22/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:725f5582-17c1-4ecd-82c1-b1161f666ee9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: 2CH 22:8
Text: And it came to pass, that, when Jehu was executing judgment upon the house of Ahab, and found the princes of Judah, and the sons of the brethren of Ahaziah, that ministered to Ahaziah, he slew them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/22/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d5e8c23-4967-4d5d-ab57-ee4f8779e75a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 324

Reference: 2CH 22:9
Text: And he sought Ahaziah: and they caught him, (for he was hid in Samaria,) and brought him to Jehu: and when they had slain him, they buried him: Because, said they, he is the son of Jehoshaphat, who sought the LORD with all his heart. So the house of Ahaziah had no power to keep still the kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/22/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60af70a9-b851-4236-be51-03f6610b16e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 2CH 22:10
Text: But when Athaliah the mother of Ahaziah saw that her son was dead, she arose and destroyed all the seed royal of the house of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/22/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b066172e-2b94-4596-8198-1d3fb4c600f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 371

Reference: 2CH 22:11
Text: But Jehoshabeath, the daughter of the king, took Joash the son of Ahaziah, and stole him from among the king’s sons that were slain, and put him and his nurse in a bedchamber. So Jehoshabeath, the daughter of king Jehoram, the wife of Jehoiada the priest, (for she was the sister of Ahaziah,) hid him from Athaliah, so that she slew him not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/22/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1bb767a-7f4b-4c42-93e5-b75716f29268>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: 2CH 22:12
Text: And he was with them hid in the house of God six years: and Athaliah reigned over the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/23/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aff1da44-21ca-48a2-beea-11d5b749d72c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 297

Reference: 2CH 23:1
Text: And in the seventh year Jehoiada strengthened himself, and took the captains of hundreds, Azariah the son of Jeroham, and Ishmael the son of Jehohanan, and Azariah the son of Obed, and Maaseiah the son of Adaiah, and Elishaphat the son of Zichri, into covenant with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/23/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90f11c95-b547-4616-8eb1-8812b6fc34e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: 2CH 23:2
Text: And they went about in Judah, and gathered the Levites out of all the cities of Judah, and the chief of the fathers of Israel, and they came to Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/23/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3e74a17-fef8-4efc-a575-55b1d832819a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: 2CH 23:3
Text: And all the congregation made a covenant with the king in the house of God. And he said unto them, Behold, the king’s son shall reign, as the LORD hath said of the sons of David.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/23/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:800bd6d0-97ca-4039-b68a-49c9b1ac98e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 2CH 23:4
Text: This is the thing that ye shall do; A third part of you entering on the sabbath, of the priests and of the Levites, shall be porters of the doors;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/23/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c43af781-45f9-4785-9df3-e803787824ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: 2CH 23:5
Text: And a third part shall be at the king’s house; and a third part at the gate of the foundation: and all the people shall be in the courts of the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/23/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3d62363-a63e-404b-aab7-1c28bc043cab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: 2CH 23:6
Text: But let none come into the house of the LORD, save the priests, and they that minister of the Levites; they shall go in, for they are holy: but all the people shall keep the watch of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/23/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf363a34-15a6-4c4b-973a-848fb152a632>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: 2CH 23:7
Text: And the Levites shall compass the king round about, every man with his weapons in his hand; and whosoever else cometh into the house, he shall be put to death: but be ye with the king when he cometh in, and when he goeth out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/23/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd1bee87-c1f5-4e01-b148-988c4ffa12a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: 2CH 23:8
Text: So the Levites and all Judah did according to all things that Jehoiada the priest had commanded, and took every man his men that were to come in on the sabbath, with them that were to go out on the sabbath: for Jehoiada the priest dismissed not the courses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/23/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93106244-21b7-434e-abc6-f5439e18d113>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: 2CH 23:9
Text: Moreover Jehoiada the priest delivered to the captains of hundreds spears, and bucklers, and shields, that had been king David’s, which were in the house of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/23/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e150ac9-727e-45b7-9aaa-9420240df404>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: 2CH 23:10
Text: And he set all the people, every man having his weapon in his hand, from the right side of the temple to the left side of the temple, along by the altar and the temple, by the king round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/23/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da37a491-705e-4287-a139-86254352b865>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: 2CH 23:11
Text: Then they brought out the king’s son, and put upon him the crown, and gave him the testimony, and made him king. And Jehoiada and his sons anointed him, and said, God save the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/23/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad6e58af-78dd-4ca8-98a8-fe92a79641d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 2CH 23:12
Text: Now when Athaliah heard the noise of the people running and praising the king, she came to the people into the house of the LORD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/23/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a15efe57-b754-44bc-9c5e-02154166d9ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 359

Reference: 2CH 23:13
Text: And she looked, and, behold, the king stood at his pillar at the entering in, and the princes and the trumpets by the king: and all the people of the land rejoiced, and sounded with trumpets, also the singers with instruments of musick, and such as taught to sing praise. Then Athaliah rent her clothes, and said, Treason, Treason.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/23/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abdfeb96-f375-4f64-9cb3-e88bc93ff501>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 286

Reference: 2CH 23:14
Text: Then Jehoiada the priest brought out the captains of hundreds that were set over the host, and said unto them, Have her forth of the ranges: and whoso followeth her, let him be slain with the sword. For the priest said, Slay her not in the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/23/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:839dec7d-ee42-4f3b-a8fb-ae04ef0141c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: 2CH 23:15
Text: So they laid hands on her; and when she was come to the entering of the horse gate by the king’s house, they slew her there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/23/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:310a4092-8aed-43f5-a7ad-53fa1fd0bea6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 2CH 23:16
Text: And Jehoiada made a covenant between him, and between all the people, and between the king, that they should be the LORD’s people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/23/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e7bf9cc-2c31-48eb-95eb-2684c7c1de5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: 2CH 23:17
Text: Then all the people went to the house of Baal, and brake it down, and brake his altars and his images in pieces, and slew Mattan the priest of Baal before the altars.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/23/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2c7c9f1-0095-41d7-98c8-349895184b9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 323

Reference: 2CH 23:18
Text: Also Jehoiada appointed the offices of the house of the LORD by the hand of the priests the Levites, whom David had distributed in the house of the LORD, to offer the burnt offerings of the LORD, as it is written in the law of Moses, with rejoicing and with singing, as it was ordained by David.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/23/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d382906-1dc9-4cc4-a051-968b0a6d39c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 2CH 23:19
Text: And he set the porters at the gates of the house of the LORD, that none which was unclean in any thing should enter in.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/23/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b266a853-a010-4315-9f13-7da48efa5e7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 310

Reference: 2CH 23:20
Text: And he took the captains of hundreds, and the nobles, and the governors of the people, and all the people of the land, and brought down the king from the house of the LORD: and they came through the high gate into the king’s house, and set the king upon the throne of the kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/23/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7de7fba5-8c54-41ae-b6f0-a66f00dbbcee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: 2CH 23:21
Text: And all the people of the land rejoiced: and the city was quiet, after that they had slain Athaliah with the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aed66293-6d82-4597-a228-5a92e0a7de4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 2CH 24:1
Text: Joash was seven years old when he began to reign, and he reigned forty years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name also was Zibiah of Beersheba.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e01cac09-3721-4c06-8f0f-61573b21c8fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 2CH 24:2
Text: And Joash did that which was right in the sight of the LORD all the days of Jehoiada the priest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db4dc089-dadc-451a-a0d2-c39721691339>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: 2CH 24:3
Text: And Jehoiada took for him two wives; and he begat sons and daughters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19bddda9-bccd-4c46-9fba-26c8edbfc81f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: 2CH 24:4
Text: And it came to pass after this, that Joash was minded to repair the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:598e0824-0291-43d4-ba8c-438971d981b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 285

Reference: 2CH 24:5
Text: And he gathered together the priests and the Levites, and said to them, Go out unto the cities of Judah, and gather of all Israel money to repair the house of your God from year to year, and see that ye hasten the matter. Howbeit the Levites hastened it not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:187c7fad-0a54-4ab5-9f23-d97f8f0d745b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 322

Reference: 2CH 24:6
Text: And the king called for Jehoiada the chief, and said unto him, Why hast thou not required of the Levites to bring in out of Judah and out of Jerusalem the collection, according to the commandment of Moses the servant of the LORD, and of the congregation of Israel, for the tabernacle of witness?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e046beb-a471-4c30-8084-0d866b39fd0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: 2CH 24:7
Text: For the sons of Athaliah, that wicked woman, had broken up the house of God; and also all the dedicated things of the house of the LORD did they bestow upon Baalim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9001d0da-842d-4fe9-8d7a-6e0e1cf3a810>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: 2CH 24:8
Text: And at the king’s commandment they made a chest, and set it without at the gate of the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af940d4b-7880-4299-aa26-eb3ed689dde5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: 2CH 24:9
Text: And they made a proclamation through Judah and Jerusalem, to bring in to the LORD the collection that Moses the servant of God laid upon Israel in the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc5a19d9-ee3b-4d16-bafa-6bf4d5b6de21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 2CH 24:10
Text: And all the princes and all the people rejoiced, and brought in, and cast into the chest, until they had made an end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd6462f0-3ef3-4f6c-8d4d-2fb2632f5d7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 373

Reference: 2CH 24:11
Text: Now it came to pass, that at what time the chest was brought unto the king’s office by the hand of the Levites, and when they saw that there was much money, the king’s scribe and the high priest’s officer came and emptied the chest, and took it, and carried it to his place again. Thus they did day by day, and gathered money in abundance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2cf3b45-6b25-4c33-84db-6de0fd571207>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 262

Reference: 2CH 24:12
Text: And the king and Jehoiada gave it to such as did the work of the service of the house of the LORD, and hired masons and carpenters to repair the house of the LORD, and also such as wrought iron and brass to mend the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f2d4b4c-6673-4495-9f64-0dfb95ebaf50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: 2CH 24:13
Text: So the workmen wrought, and the work was perfected by them, and they set the house of God in his state, and strengthened it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70fdef54-bcfe-4ad9-96c4-da016c6cb173>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 363

Reference: 2CH 24:14
Text: And when they had finished it, they brought the rest of the money before the king and Jehoiada, whereof were made vessels for the house of the LORD, even vessels to minister, and to offer withal, and spoons, and vessels of gold and silver. And they offered burnt offerings in the house of the LORD continually all the days of Jehoiada.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:578ec330-4a05-4432-8573-3e6e6bfb1b05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: 2CH 24:15
Text: But Jehoiada waxed old, and was full of days when he died; an hundred and thirty years old was he when he died.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c8bede8-8981-4a01-9a14-a3a8a782275c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 2CH 24:16
Text: And they buried him in the city of David among the kings, because he had done good in Israel, both toward God, and toward his house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61e50b51-7837-4730-affb-b8870679d852>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 2CH 24:17
Text: Now after the death of Jehoiada came the princes of Judah, and made obeisance to the king. Then the king hearkened unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ab93129-f850-4ce1-bab6-5729f5eab490>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 2CH 24:18
Text: And they left the house of the LORD God of their fathers, and served groves and idols: and wrath came upon Judah and Jerusalem for this their trespass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8fd0c10-4e76-44ca-95cf-4b635e66c087>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: 2CH 24:19
Text: Yet he sent prophets to them, to bring them again unto the LORD; and they testified against them: but they would not give ear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ccf19895-7a60-4b25-8ae4-5337267992c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 301

Reference: 2CH 24:20
Text: And the Spirit of God came upon Zechariah the son of Jehoiada the priest, which stood above the people, and said unto them, Thus saith God, Why transgress ye the commandments of the LORD, that ye cannot prosper? because ye have forsaken the LORD, he hath also forsaken you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2761d60d-ddf5-42b0-874f-8399f18313ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: 2CH 24:21
Text: And they conspired against him, and stoned him with stones at the commandment of the king in the court of the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:542ecfce-51ac-48d4-869d-b568273a90e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: 2CH 24:22
Text: Thus Joash the king remembered not the kindness which Jehoiada his father had done to him, but slew his son. And when he died, he said, The LORD look upon it, and require it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:512b0f6f-54fb-4861-9085-984d0803d9ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 278

Reference: 2CH 24:23
Text: And it came to pass at the end of the year, that the host of Syria came up against him: and they came to Judah and Jerusalem, and destroyed all the princes of the people from among the people, and sent all the spoil of them unto the king of Damascus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3c8061f-21ee-40a9-949f-33572c10443a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: 2CH 24:24
Text: For the army of the Syrians came with a small company of men, and the LORD delivered a very great host into their hand, because they had forsaken the LORD God of their fathers. So they executed judgment against Joash.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:527f88f5-dc37-477c-bec7-9f8097a528b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 329

Reference: 2CH 24:25
Text: And when they were departed from him, (for they left him in great diseases,) his own servants conspired against him for the blood of the sons of Jehoiada the priest, and slew him on his bed, and he died: and they buried him in the city of David, but they buried him not in the sepulchres of the kings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ad15d93-b73e-466f-8925-1cc45440097f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 2CH 24:26
Text: And these are they that conspired against him; Zabad the son of Shimeath an Ammonitess, and Jehozabad the son of Shimrith a Moabitess.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/24/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24ffb367-7be1-4a6d-af0e-d87ee39bd354>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: 2CH 24:27
Text: Now concerning his sons, and the greatness of the burdens laid upon him, and the repairing of the house of God, behold, they are written in the story of the book of the kings. And Amaziah his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d327f5a-0b5a-4169-88e7-eac4c6fec294>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: 2CH 25:1
Text: Amaziah was twenty and five years old when he began to reign, and he reigned twenty and nine years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Jehoaddan of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ad79461-53f4-4945-9179-ebb19226e019>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: 2CH 25:2
Text: And he did that which was right in the sight of the LORD, but not with a perfect heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78fe0bc6-0d54-4029-9db2-77cb8f8db476>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: 2CH 25:3
Text: Now it came to pass, when the kingdom was established to him, that he slew his servants that had killed the king his father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00ed3678-cf9b-408d-908d-d5a36280985b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 283

Reference: 2CH 25:4
Text: But he slew not their children, but did as it is written in the law in the book of Moses, where the LORD commanded, saying, The fathers shall not die for the children, neither shall the children die for the fathers, but every man shall die for his own sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c71405a-0b8b-4f68-9154-880fe75504ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 377

Reference: 2CH 25:5
Text: Moreover Amaziah gathered Judah together, and made them captains over thousands, and captains over hundreds, according to the houses of their fathers, throughout all Judah and Benjamin: and he numbered them from twenty years old and above, and found them three hundred thousand choice men, able to go forth to war, that could handle spear and shield.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2441922-41c4-4e61-8bb4-6941f93084ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: 2CH 25:6
Text: He hired also an hundred thousand mighty men of valour out of Israel for an hundred talents of silver.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96aeb81e-5e59-4470-9dee-1f10a998e7e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: 2CH 25:7
Text: But there came a man of God to him, saying, O king, let not the army of Israel go with thee; for the LORD is not with Israel, to wit, with all the children of Ephraim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:757e9558-f2c7-49fb-a5d2-cb7160aeb626>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: 2CH 25:8
Text: But if thou wilt go, do it; be strong for the battle: God shall make thee fall before the enemy: for God hath power to help, and to cast down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc815eb8-d56c-4c44-a9f0-50a478884bad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: 2CH 25:9
Text: And Amaziah said to the man of God, But what shall we do for the hundred talents which I have given to the army of Israel? And the man of God answered, The LORD is able to give thee much more than this.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:270e7c42-24ec-47fe-bedf-7ee535cc0307>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: 2CH 25:10
Text: Then Amaziah separated them, to wit, the army that was come to him out of Ephraim, to go home again: wherefore their anger was greatly kindled against Judah, and they returned home in great anger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a2ffc40-d9c6-44d8-ab91-c306ee85269c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 2CH 25:11
Text: And Amaziah strengthened himself, and led forth his people, and went to the valley of salt, and smote of the children of Seir ten thousand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b76643e1-ca9f-4198-a9b3-17cb38c71250>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: 2CH 25:12
Text: And other ten thousand left alive did the children of Judah carry away captive, and brought them unto the top of the rock, and cast them down from the top of the rock, that they all were broken in pieces.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0501e378-e1a7-4de4-937d-0511c0c0cf6d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: 2CH 25:13
Text: But the soldiers of the army which Amaziah sent back, that they should not go with him to battle, fell upon the cities of Judah, from Samaria even unto Bethhoron, and smote three thousand of them, and took much spoil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:febf516a-38d5-44b0-85eb-ab409480191f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: 2CH 25:14
Text: Now it came to pass, after that Amaziah was come from the slaughter of the Edomites, that he brought the gods of the children of Seir, and set them up to be his gods, and bowed down himself before them, and burned incense unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a85ac80-9f6a-4ca4-bf92-ba5096ae518a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: 2CH 25:15
Text: Wherefore the anger of the LORD was kindled against Amaziah, and he sent unto him a prophet, which said unto him, Why hast thou sought after the gods of the people, which could not deliver their own people out of thine hand?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a145b9eb-ba16-45cc-8c51-b478a33fc64b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 333

Reference: 2CH 25:16
Text: And it came to pass, as he talked with him, that the king said unto him, Art thou made of the king’s counsel? forbear; why shouldest thou be smitten? Then the prophet forbare, and said, I know that God hath determined to destroy thee, because thou hast done this, and hast not hearkened unto my counsel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c948e4e3-d8f6-43b4-a709-25f8c593296d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: 2CH 25:17
Text: Then Amaziah king of Judah took advice, and sent to Joash, the son of Jehoahaz, the son of Jehu, king of Israel, saying, Come, let us see one another in the face.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9bc8d46e-4e54-492e-92a9-cdcc3831f688>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 289

Reference: 2CH 25:18
Text: And Joash king of Israel sent to Amaziah king of Judah, saying, The thistle that was in Lebanon sent to the cedar that was in Lebanon, saying, Give thy daughter to my son to wife: and there passed by a wild beast that was in Lebanon, and trode down the thistle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:235942c2-3c90-49e9-8f04-88a49fbd9b62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: 2CH 25:19
Text: Thou sayest, Lo, thou hast smitten the Edomites; and thine heart lifteth thee up to boast: abide now at home; why shouldest thou meddle to thine hurt, that thou shouldest fall, even thou, and Judah with thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6795e217-6712-45ab-957f-26fb3d979394>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: 2CH 25:20
Text: But Amaziah would not hear; for it came of God, that he might deliver them into the hand of their enemies, because they sought after the gods of Edom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6acf4399-9b77-4f08-8920-02438732fd7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 2CH 25:21
Text: So Joash the king of Israel went up; and they saw one another in the face, both he and Amaziah king of Judah, at Bethshemesh, which belongeth to Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3611ee10-b17f-4df1-9751-03a463ca4552>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: 2CH 25:22
Text: And Judah was put to the worse before Israel, and they fled every man to his tent.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40666afc-684e-42b3-bd6b-20ac46ddc19b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: 2CH 25:23
Text: And Joash the king of Israel took Amaziah king of Judah, the son of Joash, the son of Jehoahaz, at Bethshemesh, and brought him to Jerusalem, and brake down the wall of Jerusalem from the gate of Ephraim to the corner gate, four hundred cubits.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6120cb07-3873-4ff1-bee8-fc8dc6cca2cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: 2CH 25:24
Text: And he took all the gold and the silver, and all the vessels that were found in the house of God with Obededom, and the treasures of the king’s house, the hostages also, and returned to Samaria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0faba70-9280-42ce-846c-6cae7188c6ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 2CH 25:25
Text: And Amaziah the son of Joash king of Judah lived after the death of Joash son of Jehoahaz king of Israel fifteen years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77ffb244-2e60-47db-8dfd-cfd6afaf0a0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 2CH 25:26
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Amaziah, first and last, behold, are they not written in the book of the kings of Judah and Israel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1cb0953-71df-464d-a3b3-4ebe94346f0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: 2CH 25:27
Text: Now after the time that Amaziah did turn away from following the LORD they made a conspiracy against him in Jerusalem; and he fled to Lachish: but they sent to Lachish after him, and slew him there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/25/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac34af90-add3-4c54-935f-e51aadf7e19d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: 2CH 25:28
Text: And they brought him upon horses, and buried him with his fathers in the city of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/26/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a92c6666-0bca-442d-855c-c590e5e3d79c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 2CH 26:1
Text: Then all the people of Judah took Uzziah, who was sixteen years old, and made him king in the room of his father Amaziah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/26/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca8f84f9-7a2c-4810-9fb1-656c3b2f1b96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: 2CH 26:2
Text: He built Eloth, and restored it to Judah, after that the king slept with his fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/26/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a13e14e8-4199-4ca7-b620-5d5a62199993>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: 2CH 26:3
Text: Sixteen years old was Uzziah when he began to reign, and he reigned fifty and two years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name also was Jecoliah of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/26/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb544bd3-1134-4b90-a7d0-c630248556c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: 2CH 26:4
Text: And he did that which was right in the sight of the LORD, according to all that his father Amaziah did.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/26/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c565d602-88e6-483e-82f1-a8a50efb2e3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 2CH 26:5
Text: And he sought God in the days of Zechariah, who had understanding in the visions of God: and as long as he sought the LORD, God made him to prosper.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/26/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0cad8db-c3e7-4446-9b03-965bfe8c3cea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: 2CH 26:6
Text: And he went forth and warred against the Philistines, and brake down the wall of Gath, and the wall of Jabneh, and the wall of Ashdod, and built cities about Ashdod, and among the Philistines.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/26/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ded8ecb8-976f-4956-9e2d-9f7e6bc79270>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: 2CH 26:7
Text: And God helped him against the Philistines, and against the Arabians that dwelt in Gurbaal, and the Mehunims.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/26/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:825924d8-08b9-4c42-b072-4206b1cbcb62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: 2CH 26:8
Text: And the Ammonites gave gifts to Uzziah: and his name spread abroad even to the entering in of Egypt; for he strengthened himself exceedingly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/26/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59672203-89a0-4f40-acaa-37db69a25164>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: 2CH 26:9
Text: Moreover Uzziah built towers in Jerusalem at the corner gate, and at the valley gate, and at the turning of the wall, and fortified them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/26/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5a05d78-268c-47aa-8f2d-797d9b7ec4f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: 2CH 26:10
Text: Also he built towers in the desert, and digged many wells: for he had much cattle, both in the low country, and in the plains: husbandmen also, and vine dressers in the mountains, and in Carmel: for he loved husbandry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/26/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5235f15-ca31-4bc9-b647-facc0add8e4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: 2CH 26:11
Text: Moreover Uzziah had an host of fighting men, that went out to war by bands, according to the number of their account by the hand of Jeiel the scribe and Maaseiah the ruler, under the hand of Hananiah, one of the king’s captains.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/26/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6676925e-9cfc-419f-b135-f28eb5c07f63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 2CH 26:12
Text: The whole number of the chief of the fathers of the mighty men of valour were two thousand and six hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/26/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0f0be6b-1d20-4856-aa7c-7f4ee220db68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: 2CH 26:13
Text: And under their hand was an army, three hundred thousand and seven thousand and five hundred, that made war with mighty power, to help the king against the enemy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/26/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:978f405e-b930-4413-8b90-0f13d1a0e40b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 2CH 26:14
Text: And Uzziah prepared for them throughout all the host shields, and spears, and helmets, and habergeons, and bows, and slings to cast stones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/26/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ed704dd-676e-400f-b775-cd0a43bb03d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: 2CH 26:15
Text: And he made in Jerusalem engines, invented by cunning men, to be on the towers and upon the bulwarks, to shoot arrows and great stones withal. And his name spread far abroad; for he was marvellously helped, till he was strong.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/26/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acb0dbf4-26a3-475f-aad9-d05b8b1eeeb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: 2CH 26:16
Text: But when he was strong, his heart was lifted up to his destruction: for he transgressed against the LORD his God, and went into the temple of the LORD to burn incense upon the altar of incense.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/26/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e82c65c-e55f-4894-9ec3-2f2316ee571f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: 2CH 26:17
Text: And Azariah the priest went in after him, and with him fourscore priests of the LORD, that were valiant men:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/26/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbf44f8b-847a-4f89-bbae-8828e7e0b6c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 335

Reference: 2CH 26:18
Text: And they withstood Uzziah the king, and said unto him, It appertaineth not unto thee, Uzziah, to burn incense unto the LORD, but to the priests the sons of Aaron, that are consecrated to burn incense: go out of the sanctuary; for thou hast trespassed; neither shall it be for thine honour from the LORD God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/26/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f75e81d6-48aa-43df-835b-0090358a9e41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: 2CH 26:19
Text: Then Uzziah was wroth, and had a censer in his hand to burn incense: and while he was wroth with the priests, the leprosy even rose up in his forehead before the priests in the house of the LORD, from beside the incense altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/26/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9999c40e-6c6d-4eaa-a481-7da8005cd08f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: 2CH 26:20
Text: And Azariah the chief priest, and all the priests, looked upon him, and, behold, he was leprous in his forehead, and they thrust him out from thence; yea, himself hasted also to go out, because the LORD had smitten him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/26/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f9e4600-cd65-45d7-85e5-54c0b941bd5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: 2CH 26:21
Text: And Uzziah the king was a leper unto the day of his death, and dwelt in a several house, being a leper; for he was cut off from the house of the LORD: and Jotham his son was over the king’s house, judging the people of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/26/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11776756-25b3-4d2c-bdde-b8169fb01acb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 2CH 26:22
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Uzziah, first and last, did Isaiah the prophet, the son of Amoz, write.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/26/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0110d05e-e00f-4ee5-9a6b-c1a579a8512e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: 2CH 26:23
Text: So Uzziah slept with his fathers, and they buried him with his fathers in the field of the burial which belonged to the kings; for they said, He is a leper: and Jotham his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/27/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba13ae11-8528-4680-b65b-f5e47300236b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: 2CH 27:1
Text: Jotham was twenty and five years old when he began to reign, and he reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem. His mother’s name also was Jerushah, the daughter of Zadok.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/27/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54855a9f-8c5a-4b3b-ae6b-2af8f52aee9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: 2CH 27:2
Text: And he did that which was right in the sight of the LORD, according to all that his father Uzziah did: howbeit he entered not into the temple of the LORD. And the people did yet corruptly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/27/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36a1c8e5-bd2a-4293-ac1c-fc7a2026fa54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: 2CH 27:3
Text: He built the high gate of the house of the LORD, and on the wall of Ophel he built much.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/27/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee8be9be-ff57-4fb8-9c02-38f7e64d04a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: 2CH 27:4
Text: Moreover he built cities in the mountains of Judah, and in the forests he built castles and towers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/27/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42289801-0474-4e46-8e0b-7e6344eb44ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 329

Reference: 2CH 27:5
Text: He fought also with the king of the Ammonites, and prevailed against them. And the children of Ammon gave him the same year an hundred talents of silver, and ten thousand measures of wheat, and ten thousand of barley. So much did the children of Ammon pay unto him, both the second year, and the third.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/27/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15800252-f7da-41ac-9877-455484453cfc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: 2CH 27:6
Text: So Jotham became mighty, because he prepared his ways before the LORD his God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/27/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34098ccc-99c1-4b18-bb30-d6d8c7be98ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 2CH 27:7
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Jotham, and all his wars, and his ways, lo, they are written in the book of the kings of Israel and Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/27/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6217d205-8614-4b56-801a-65ffe784838a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 2CH 27:8
Text: He was five and twenty years old when he began to reign, and reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/27/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:231ef5c2-584d-4b7a-b7dc-176230dafe0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: 2CH 27:9
Text: And Jotham slept with his fathers, and they buried him in the city of David: and Ahaz his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5172e63b-89ba-4572-ac43-c3fa361864d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: 2CH 28:1
Text: Ahaz was twenty years old when he began to reign, and he reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem: but he did not that which was right in the sight of the LORD, like David his father:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7629d9bb-d793-41d5-91b4-1481ed2e0364>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: 2CH 28:2
Text: For he walked in the ways of the kings of Israel, and made also molten images for Baalim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d3386c8-96a7-4146-b89d-4ee2c471e05b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: 2CH 28:3
Text: Moreover he burnt incense in the valley of the son of Hinnom, and burnt his children in the fire, after the abominations of the heathen whom the LORD had cast out before the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f07c8af2-12ac-4524-9883-f0e123ec05cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: 2CH 28:4
Text: He sacrificed also and burnt incense in the high places, and on the hills, and under every green tree.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e546aca4-8ff9-463c-97e4-a95ae5aaddf5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 307

Reference: 2CH 28:5
Text: Wherefore the LORD his God delivered him into the hand of the king of Syria; and they smote him, and carried away a great multitude of them captives, and brought them to Damascus. And he was also delivered into the hand of the king of Israel, who smote him with a great slaughter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c3cd25a-5d15-4a3d-a6b8-a1f6492b3a4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: 2CH 28:6
Text: For Pekah the son of Remaliah slew in Judah an hundred and twenty thousand in one day, which were all valiant men; because they had forsaken the LORD God of their fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b64b3cf-3d19-44a5-8b01-f1565db851e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 2CH 28:7
Text: And Zichri, a mighty man of Ephraim, slew Maaseiah the king’s son, and Azrikam the governor of the house, and Elkanah that was next to the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eac12bf6-936a-49e7-87e3-53ff13ab6800>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: 2CH 28:8
Text: And the children of Israel carried away captive of their brethren two hundred thousand, women, sons, and daughters, and took also away much spoil from them, and brought the spoil to Samaria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:082970ef-ad8d-4cd7-8e2a-9d0185eab9fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 327

Reference: 2CH 28:9
Text: But a prophet of the LORD was there, whose name was Oded: and he went out before the host that came to Samaria, and said unto them, Behold, because the LORD God of your fathers was wroth with Judah, he hath delivered them into your hand, and ye have slain them in a rage that reacheth up unto heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2201ca28-559f-4113-a8ff-ce0008e65550>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: 2CH 28:10
Text: And now ye purpose to keep under the children of Judah and Jerusalem for bondmen and bondwomen unto you: but are there not with you, even with you, sins against the LORD your God?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a8b2640-bf86-4635-b339-a5a5b87ea68d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: 2CH 28:11
Text: Now hear me therefore, and deliver the captives again, which ye have taken captive of your brethren: for the fierce wrath of the LORD is upon you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:764969a7-a462-46f3-a9ea-c764d6cca2a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: 2CH 28:12
Text: Then certain of the heads of the children of Ephraim, Azariah the son of Johanan, Berechiah the son of Meshillemoth, and Jehizkiah the son of Shallum, and Amasa the son of Hadlai, stood up against them that came from the war,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9234d0f-3bee-4551-8088-0f3713f4a3c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: 2CH 28:13
Text: And said unto them, Ye shall not bring in the captives hither: for whereas we have offended against the LORD already, ye intend to add more to our sins and to our trespass: for our trespass is great, and there is fierce wrath against Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50ee4983-277d-401a-865d-128511acc89a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 2CH 28:14
Text: So the armed men left the captives and the spoil before the princes and all the congregation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e9bb796-bb2b-4005-9ea2-0a53e1789827>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 396

Reference: 2CH 28:15
Text: And the men which were expressed by name rose up, and took the captives, and with the spoil clothed all that were naked among them, and arrayed them, and shod them, and gave them to eat and to drink, and anointed them, and carried all the feeble of them upon asses, and brought them to Jericho, the city of palm trees, to their brethren: then they returned to Samaria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6752c342-b6ea-45c6-92db-d0915879b27d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: 2CH 28:16
Text: At that time did king Ahaz send unto the kings of Assyria to help him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68296ff1-502b-45ab-8035-52557b278c08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: 2CH 28:17
Text: For again the Edomites had come and smitten Judah, and carried away captives.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fc7d88f-b600-4a90-a298-eeccc829017b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 306

Reference: 2CH 28:18
Text: The Philistines also had invaded the cities of the low country, and of the south of Judah, and had taken Bethshemesh, and Ajalon, and Gederoth, and Shocho with the villages thereof, and Timnah with the villages thereof, Gimzo also and the villages thereof: and they dwelt there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2948cf0f-b58d-44e7-a1bd-334b73ce8967>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 2CH 28:19
Text: For the LORD brought Judah low because of Ahaz king of Israel; for he made Judah naked, and transgressed sore against the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f37ede65-5fc7-46d6-bb56-5d44a38e14e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: 2CH 28:20
Text: And Tilgathpilneser king of Assyria came unto him, and distressed him, but strengthened him not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3961dd6f-e088-471e-8093-9d65797093e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: 2CH 28:21
Text: For Ahaz took away a portion out of the house of the LORD, and out of the house of the king, and of the princes, and gave it unto the king of Assyria: but he helped him not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8e65c0d-2ba2-403d-8591-e883033c556b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: 2CH 28:22
Text: And in the time of his distress did he trespass yet more against the LORD: this is that king Ahaz.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e7075b1-dda2-43fd-bc48-b7f08cc8eba4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: 2CH 28:23
Text: For he sacrificed unto the gods of Damascus, which smote him: and he said, Because the gods of the kings of Syria help them, therefore will I sacrifice to them, that they may help me. But they were the ruin of him, and of all Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c8b7a22-45b8-43a5-9a3a-661738f3ecab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: 2CH 28:24
Text: And Ahaz gathered together the vessels of the house of God, and cut in pieces the vessels of the house of God, and shut up the doors of the house of the LORD, and he made him altars in every corner of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bce9b64-ef71-4818-adb6-5ba515fd450b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: 2CH 28:25
Text: And in every several city of Judah he made high places to burn incense unto other gods, and provoked to anger the LORD God of his fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea1c8af4-ca8e-41d8-a2c6-4510213e0e5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 2CH 28:26
Text: Now the rest of his acts and of all his ways, first and last, behold, they are written in the book of the kings of Judah and Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/28/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72918201-d871-4609-8dcc-446d40730ea5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: 2CH 28:27
Text: And Ahaz slept with his fathers, and they buried him in the city, even in Jerusalem: but they brought him not into the sepulchres of the kings of Israel: and Hezekiah his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6cc294e-a896-4cce-9f0e-486989902020>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: 2CH 29:1
Text: Hezekiah began to reign when he was five and twenty years old, and he reigned nine and twenty years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Abijah, the daughter of Zechariah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fe7ad89-7a2d-4d83-bae9-71adf5be8b0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: 2CH 29:2
Text: And he did that which was right in the sight of the LORD, according to all that David his father had done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86c2e051-b2f1-42cc-985c-d090a20e903a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: 2CH 29:3
Text: He in the first year of his reign, in the first month, opened the doors of the house of the LORD, and repaired them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70af18a3-c0ec-4987-9273-a5e5ccfef385>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: 2CH 29:4
Text: And he brought in the priests and the Levites, and gathered them together into the east street,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8cb60346-fba7-4ad6-ac44-1907c32e52dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: 2CH 29:5
Text: And said unto them, Hear me, ye Levites, sanctify now yourselves, and sanctify the house of the LORD God of your fathers, and carry forth the filthiness out of the holy place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4a4fbe1-8e3a-44e7-838d-8306b516caf9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: 2CH 29:6
Text: For our fathers have trespassed, and done that which was evil in the eyes of the LORD our God, and have forsaken him, and have turned away their faces from the habitation of the LORD, and turned their backs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fffdc9e4-60ad-4a33-a261-a9950643a5c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: 2CH 29:7
Text: Also they have shut up the doors of the porch, and put out the lamps, and have not burned incense nor offered burnt offerings in the holy place unto the God of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:787ff776-4346-4c34-b29d-83b0f9dbd848>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: 2CH 29:8
Text: Wherefore the wrath of the LORD was upon Judah and Jerusalem, and he hath delivered them to trouble, to astonishment, and to hissing, as ye see with your eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b784326e-1f50-4d56-ada2-8a2ac1e08a09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 2CH 29:9
Text: For, lo, our fathers have fallen by the sword, and our sons and our daughters and our wives are in captivity for this.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08a1b8e8-5ad2-4f7f-8ec6-0e3ef86faf15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: 2CH 29:10
Text: Now it is in mine heart to make a covenant with the LORD God of Israel, that his fierce wrath may turn away from us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca565f1f-7ea1-48c1-bfff-9c56bc555292>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: 2CH 29:11
Text: My sons, be not now negligent: for the LORD hath chosen you to stand before him, to serve him, and that ye should minister unto him, and burn incense.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd14db18-dbf6-4f20-9aea-ef01283f9ee6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 294

Reference: 2CH 29:12
Text: Then the Levites arose, Mahath the son of Amasai, and Joel the son of Azariah, of the sons of the Kohathites: and of the sons of Merari, Kish the son of Abdi, and Azariah the son of Jehalelel: and of the Gershonites; Joah the son of Zimmah, and Eden the son of Joah:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d4b776d-06e0-441a-a7a2-690efbbe77e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 2CH 29:13
Text: And of the sons of Elizaphan; Shimri, and Jeiel: and of the sons of Asaph; Zechariah, and Mattaniah:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:608e9530-2e1c-42c3-bb97-833740d8a6ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: 2CH 29:14
Text: And of the sons of Heman; Jehiel, and Shimei: and of the sons of Jeduthun; Shemaiah, and Uzziel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cd72bc0-d7b0-451d-8686-7177a9bb7371>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 2CH 29:15
Text: And they gathered their brethren, and sanctified themselves, and came, according to the commandment of the king, by the words of the LORD, to cleanse the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90054a91-15ae-4e8b-8510-517dd9fab888>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 299

Reference: 2CH 29:16
Text: And the priests went into the inner part of the house of the LORD, to cleanse it, and brought out all the uncleanness that they found in the temple of the LORD into the court of the house of the LORD. And the Levites took it, to carry it out abroad into the brook Kidron.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff356f76-5c35-48a3-a439-78b1a1007811>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 280

Reference: 2CH 29:17
Text: Now they began on the first day of the first month to sanctify, and on the eighth day of the month came they to the porch of the LORD: so they sanctified the house of the LORD in eight days; and in the sixteenth day of the first month they made an end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae6e372b-740a-4850-b1de-86b10d634942>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: 2CH 29:18
Text: Then they went in to Hezekiah the king, and said, We have cleansed all the house of the LORD, and the altar of burnt offering, with all the vessels thereof, and the shewbread table, with all the vessels thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36d28893-6c04-40fb-87ca-bc1209947e3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: 2CH 29:19
Text: Moreover all the vessels, which king Ahaz in his reign did cast away in his transgression, have we prepared and sanctified, and, behold, they are before the altar of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:950f8ed3-ce1e-4c83-8f2e-6b0ae55df837>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 2CH 29:20
Text: Then Hezekiah the king rose early, and gathered the rulers of the city, and went up to the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0d6abb3-4fee-4462-8399-450612348d64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 274

Reference: 2CH 29:21
Text: And they brought seven bullocks, and seven rams, and seven lambs, and seven he goats, for a sin offering for the kingdom, and for the sanctuary, and for Judah. And he commanded the priests the sons of Aaron to offer them on the altar of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79fffbd9-33d8-435f-a813-66acd73fff80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 278

Reference: 2CH 29:22
Text: So they killed the bullocks, and the priests received the blood, and sprinkled it on the altar: likewise, when they had killed the rams, they sprinkled the blood upon the altar: they killed also the lambs, and they sprinkled the blood upon the altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67f58825-caf9-450e-8419-680260882774>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: 2CH 29:23
Text: And they brought forth the he goats for the sin offering before the king and the congregation; and they laid their hands upon them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9571bc6-7ca7-42c4-995a-bc6b5c4a1de4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: 2CH 29:24
Text: And the priests killed them, and they made reconciliation with their blood upon the altar, to make an atonement for all Israel: for the king commanded that the burnt offering and the sin offering should be made for all Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a673351-9f4a-4ff0-8a2f-4bba6302cbd5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: 2CH 29:25
Text: And he set the Levites in the house of the LORD with cymbals, with psalteries, and with harps, according to the commandment of David, and of Gad the king’s seer, and Nathan the prophet: for so was the commandment of the LORD by his prophets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f18a23b-4eeb-49ba-ba9a-3d63a662812d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: 2CH 29:26
Text: And the Levites stood with the instruments of David, and the priests with the trumpets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0cec93dd-315c-470b-af4f-c7e38e15da6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: 2CH 29:27
Text: And Hezekiah commanded to offer the burnt offering upon the altar. And when the burnt offering began, the song of the LORD began also with the trumpets, and with the instruments ordained by David king of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8c1376f-1be4-4d7d-bc21-36fae69e09ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: 2CH 29:28
Text: And all the congregation worshipped, and the singers sang, and the trumpeters sounded: and all this continued until the burnt offering was finished.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1491d808-448a-4b73-8db5-394cbc368467>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 2CH 29:29
Text: And when they had made an end of offering, the king and all that were present with him bowed themselves, and worshipped.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b75d72c-ca16-4875-88a8-384d67330954>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: 2CH 29:30
Text: Moreover Hezekiah the king and the princes commanded the Levites to sing praise unto the LORD with the words of David, and of Asaph the seer. And they sang praises with gladness, and they bowed their heads and worshipped.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5eb57dd-34b8-4074-9a5c-8e49ca3e7bdd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 306

Reference: 2CH 29:31
Text: Then Hezekiah answered and said, Now ye have consecrated yourselves unto the LORD, come near and bring sacrifices and thank offerings into the house of the LORD. And the congregation brought in sacrifices and thank offerings; and as many as were of a free heart burnt offerings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f80e72a-d6da-4e49-8580-1fce89776e6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: 2CH 29:32
Text: And the number of the burnt offerings, which the congregation brought, was threescore and ten bullocks, an hundred rams, and two hundred lambs: all these were for a burnt offering to the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91c11ab3-6b1f-40b7-bd15-66257d43ef1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: 2CH 29:33
Text: And the consecrated things were six hundred oxen and three thousand sheep.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97b2b38c-5605-40f8-8db4-cd431778a1db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 326

Reference: 2CH 29:34
Text: But the priests were too few, so that they could not flay all the burnt offerings: wherefore their brethren the Levites did help them, till the work was ended, and until the other priests had sanctified themselves: for the Levites were more upright in heart to sanctify themselves than the priests.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b38b2c7-0cce-40b4-9e8b-49f2c8f2e6e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: 2CH 29:35
Text: And also the burnt offerings were in abundance, with the fat of the peace offerings, and the drink offerings for every burnt offering. So the service of the house of the LORD was set in order.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/29/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c0bee64-d10f-438e-a1f1-3a62c1156336>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 2CH 29:36
Text: And Hezekiah rejoiced, and all the people, that God had prepared the people: for the thing was done suddenly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:959167af-a4e8-4e60-976c-29eb7474e51b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: 2CH 30:1
Text: And Hezekiah sent to all Israel and Judah, and wrote letters also to Ephraim and Manasseh, that they should come to the house of the LORD at Jerusalem, to keep the passover unto the LORD God of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7777d96f-dd1c-4af1-a520-d4f1ee813b6d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: 2CH 30:2
Text: For the king had taken counsel, and his princes, and all the congregation in Jerusalem, to keep the passover in the second month.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:088644b7-6ad5-4c9d-af82-dd0353083f64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: 2CH 30:3
Text: For they could not keep it at that time, because the priests had not sanctified themselves sufficiently, neither had the people gathered themselves together to Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac33e506-6dc6-4c74-9712-9c9ef6a80a64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: 2CH 30:4
Text: And the thing pleased the king and all the congregation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a149fd84-3328-4da2-a5f3-4e85a6c8ce7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: 2CH 30:5
Text: So they established a decree to make proclamation throughout all Israel, from Beersheba even to Dan, that they should come to keep the passover unto the LORD God of Israel at Jerusalem: for they had not done it of a long time in such sort as it was written.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b09d0a5-3ac8-4629-bc9a-f3d27de5c7a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 361

Reference: 2CH 30:6
Text: So the posts went with the letters from the king and his princes throughout all Israel and Judah, and according to the commandment of the king, saying, Ye children of Israel, turn again unto the LORD God of Abraham, Isaac, and Israel, and he will return to the remnant of you, that are escaped out of the hand of the kings of Assyria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f71e83e2-29c7-4967-9765-c32f41192c80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: 2CH 30:7
Text: And be not ye like your fathers, and like your brethren, which trespassed against the LORD God of their fathers, who therefore gave them up to desolation, as ye see.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a6631dc-411f-4be9-bfd0-742230be79ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 262

Reference: 2CH 30:8
Text: Now be ye not stiffnecked, as your fathers were, but yield yourselves unto the LORD, and enter into his sanctuary, which he hath sanctified for ever: and serve the LORD your God, that the fierceness of his wrath may turn away from you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0958717d-ecf2-4a56-aa3f-52b721d85fa8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 311

Reference: 2CH 30:9
Text: For if ye turn again unto the LORD, your brethren and your children shall find compassion before them that lead them captive, so that they shall come again into this land: for the LORD your God is gracious and merciful, and will not turn away his face from you, if ye return unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:097c38ae-84d1-468e-bd0a-06f928454c7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 2CH 30:10
Text: So the posts passed from city to city through the country of Ephraim and Manasseh even unto Zebulun: but they laughed them to scorn, and mocked them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f57cad7-a02f-473b-b9f9-8e2c0c30b4e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 2CH 30:11
Text: Nevertheless divers of Asher and Manasseh and of Zebulun humbled themselves, and came to Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64ce7e80-dbe4-4a75-b287-863daab84a67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: 2CH 30:12
Text: Also in Judah the hand of God was to give them one heart to do the commandment of the king and of the princes, by the word of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b0787a7-6eba-4120-a1bd-37a82a7afab4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 2CH 30:13
Text: And there assembled at Jerusalem much people to keep the feast of unleavened bread in the second month, a very great congregation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:615689b1-5f48-4295-87b5-49a4288129e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 2CH 30:14
Text: And they arose and took away the altars that were in Jerusalem, and all the altars for incense took they away, and cast them into the brook Kidron.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fbc7e19-dccc-4a85-ab35-d25f7712b6ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: 2CH 30:15
Text: Then they killed the passover on the fourteenth day of the second month: and the priests and the Levites were ashamed, and sanctified themselves, and brought in the burnt offerings into the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40c220ac-c178-4a64-8c43-ee9af53393c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: 2CH 30:16
Text: And they stood in their place after their manner, according to the law of Moses the man of God: the priests sprinkled the blood, which they received of the hand of the Levites.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f80de14-101a-40de-9fc4-a31d5f22e0f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: 2CH 30:17
Text: For there were many in the congregation that were not sanctified: therefore the Levites had the charge of the killing of the passovers for every one that was not clean, to sanctify them unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90bfecba-eccf-4755-ac85-9ed3194a3ffd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: 2CH 30:18
Text: For a multitude of the people, even many of Ephraim, and Manasseh, Issachar, and Zebulun, had not cleansed themselves, yet did they eat the passover otherwise than it was written. But Hezekiah prayed for them, saying, The good LORD pardon every one


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cab56be-373b-4ff4-9d65-d266b5dccb53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: 2CH 30:19
Text: That prepareth his heart to seek God, the LORD God of his fathers, though he be not cleansed according to the purification of the sanctuary.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef7f6db7-ecb3-4fc1-aa54-2104fe6a2bc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: 2CH 30:20
Text: And the LORD hearkened to Hezekiah, and healed the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4ad101c-aea2-449d-91f1-cfda57309d00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: 2CH 30:21
Text: And the children of Israel that were present at Jerusalem kept the feast of unleavened bread seven days with great gladness: and the Levites and the priests praised the LORD day by day, singing with loud instruments unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d57133c1-f769-4bf1-97b1-5317c847fac0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: 2CH 30:22
Text: And Hezekiah spake comfortably unto all the Levites that taught the good knowledge of the LORD: and they did eat throughout the feast seven days, offering peace offerings, and making confession to the LORD God of their fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8585e342-61ea-4da8-8d84-9d316e003aa9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 2CH 30:23
Text: And the whole assembly took counsel to keep other seven days: and they kept other seven days with gladness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e5eaa38-49d0-4193-9b87-3123bf1a0d69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: 2CH 30:24
Text: For Hezekiah king of Judah did give to the congregation a thousand bullocks and seven thousand sheep; and the princes gave to the congregation a thousand bullocks and ten thousand sheep: and a great number of priests sanctified themselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e2eb6ae-8fe0-430d-a48a-1c627ae89b3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: 2CH 30:25
Text: And all the congregation of Judah, with the priests and the Levites, and all the congregation that came out of Israel, and the strangers that came out of the land of Israel, and that dwelt in Judah, rejoiced.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:512b4c28-291a-406b-9a39-73474a713268>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: 2CH 30:26
Text: So there was great joy in Jerusalem: for since the time of Solomon the son of David king of Israel there was not the like in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/30/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8169756-b566-4a5e-aa98-a759dab89bc2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: 2CH 30:27
Text: Then the priests the Levites arose and blessed the people: and their voice was heard, and their prayer came up to his holy dwelling place, even unto heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/31/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ced901c-78e1-4919-911c-efa96997ec1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 421

Reference: 2CH 31:1
Text: Now when all this was finished, all Israel that were present went out to the cities of Judah, and brake the images in pieces, and cut down the groves, and threw down the high places and the altars out of all Judah and Benjamin, in Ephraim also and Manasseh, until they had utterly destroyed them all. Then all the children of Israel returned, every man to his possession, into their own cities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/31/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c6bf3d2-0b33-4351-8ce0-a8af14a27b82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 304

Reference: 2CH 31:2
Text: And Hezekiah appointed the courses of the priests and the Levites after their courses, every man according to his service, the priests and Levites for burnt offerings and for peace offerings, to minister, and to give thanks, and to praise in the gates of the tents of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/31/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60924e24-d238-4c20-904f-df2ccba6a30c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 290

Reference: 2CH 31:3
Text: He appointed also the king’s portion of his substance for the burnt offerings, to wit, for the morning and evening burnt offerings, and the burnt offerings for the sabbaths, and for the new moons, and for the set feasts, as it is written in the law of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/31/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15d28836-3151-4e8d-b5a5-fc6738f389f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: 2CH 31:4
Text: Moreover he commanded the people that dwelt in Jerusalem to give the portion of the priests and the Levites, that they might be encouraged in the law of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/31/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03cd47d5-f59c-4c74-a1f2-878036c9cb03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: 2CH 31:5
Text: And as soon as the commandment came abroad, the children of Israel brought in abundance the firstfruits of corn, wine, and oil, and honey, and of all the increase of the field; and the tithe of all things brought they in abundantly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/31/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1bdc93db-e4bf-4aa9-8498-a2268f11359a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: 2CH 31:6
Text: And concerning the children of Israel and Judah, that dwelt in the cities of Judah, they also brought in the tithe of oxen and sheep, and the tithe of holy things which were consecrated unto the LORD their God, and laid them by heaps.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/31/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79a0a755-ee8c-4949-b9aa-63e53480bb3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 2CH 31:7
Text: In the third month they began to lay the foundation of the heaps, and finished them in the seventh month.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/31/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43ff8161-8fe6-465b-9a08-ba570619feee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: 2CH 31:8
Text: And when Hezekiah and the princes came and saw the heaps, they blessed the LORD, and his people Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/31/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20565b4d-b838-4715-bbae-d0d8de595527>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: 2CH 31:9
Text: Then Hezekiah questioned with the priests and the Levites concerning the heaps.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/31/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06bbe42c-235e-4fbf-a725-1be440893aec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 307

Reference: 2CH 31:10
Text: And Azariah the chief priest of the house of Zadok answered him, and said, Since the people began to bring the offerings into the house of the LORD, we have had enough to eat, and have left plenty: for the LORD hath blessed his people; and that which is left is this great store.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/31/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eaf988c6-a023-4c20-9450-51a025fd1936>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 2CH 31:11
Text: Then Hezekiah commanded to prepare chambers in the house of the LORD; and they prepared them,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/31/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f52cdeca-c606-4cf7-8e8d-82bb896f9e84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 2CH 31:12
Text: And brought in the offerings and the tithes and the dedicated things faithfully: over which Cononiah the Levite was ruler, and Shimei his brother was the next.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/31/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2753aa0-030b-4d7f-8c56-35a03170f7d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 304

Reference: 2CH 31:13
Text: And Jehiel, and Azaziah, and Nahath, and Asahel, and Jerimoth, and Jozabad, and Eliel, and Ismachiah, and Mahath, and Benaiah, were overseers under the hand of Cononiah and Shimei his brother, at the commandment of Hezekiah the king, and Azariah the ruler of the house of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/31/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4acc976-928d-4788-8d19-74bae7ac1f0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 2CH 31:14
Text: And Kore the son of Imnah the Levite, the porter toward the east, was over the freewill offerings of God, to distribute the oblations of the LORD, and the most holy things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/31/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:808ce053-0ef6-41a2-b162-db8af485244d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: 2CH 31:15
Text: And next him were Eden, and Miniamin, and Jeshua, and Shemaiah, Amariah, and Shecaniah, in the cities of the priests, in their set office, to give to their brethren by courses, as well to the great as to the small:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/31/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c26b9c9-12c5-4d34-8859-c5c1bf79b184>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: 2CH 31:16
Text: Beside their genealogy of males, from three years old and upward, even unto every one that entereth into the house of the LORD, his daily portion for their service in their charges according to their courses;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/31/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab2ec5cd-4405-44d8-bf01-ef8f8cc3d6f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: 2CH 31:17
Text: Both to the genealogy of the priests by the house of their fathers, and the Levites from twenty years old and upward, in their charges by their courses;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/31/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:060a280a-6a02-4ccb-81a9-ccf6b6c53024>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: 2CH 31:18
Text: And to the genealogy of all their little ones, their wives, and their sons, and their daughters, through all the congregation: for in their set office they sanctified themselves in holiness:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/31/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7fa64ee-bef9-4889-90c1-4940e033df85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 300

Reference: 2CH 31:19
Text: Also of the sons of Aaron the priests, which were in the fields of the suburbs of their cities, in every several city, the men that were expressed by name, to give portions to all the males among the priests, and to all that were reckoned by genealogies among the Levites.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/31/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fec0996a-e0de-4850-9c4b-5af18012ebdf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 2CH 31:20
Text: And thus did Hezekiah throughout all Judah, and wrought that which was good and right and truth before the LORD his God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/31/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11e0ec8f-12f3-4b99-8308-aecf7b833e8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: 2CH 31:21
Text: And in every work that he began in the service of the house of God, and in the law, and in the commandments, to seek his God, he did it with all his heart, and prospered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e975a715-3f6d-40d1-836a-0dbecac6ebe3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: 2CH 32:1
Text: After these things, and the establishment thereof, Sennacherib king of Assyria came, and entered into Judah, and encamped against the fenced cities, and thought to win them for himself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d0e45f8-864b-4aae-b4c5-0764ee49973a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 2CH 32:2
Text: And when Hezekiah saw that Sennacherib was come, and that he was purposed to fight against Jerusalem,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2aa0d6ab-a910-405a-9513-71fcaa34fdb0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: 2CH 32:3
Text: He took counsel with his princes and his mighty men to stop the waters of the fountains which were without the city: and they did help him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f68b82b3-d0d3-46d7-bec9-168c2f4824db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: 2CH 32:4
Text: So there was gathered much people together, who stopped all the fountains, and the brook that ran through the midst of the land, saying, Why should the kings of Assyria come, and find much water?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8194d0ad-ede9-4e31-ab95-347e3fbf18d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: 2CH 32:5
Text: Also he strengthened himself, and built up all the wall that was broken, and raised it up to the towers, and another wall without, and repaired Millo in the city of David, and made darts and shields in abundance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96c39d25-1a63-4b8f-bc5b-3e65388b5d24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: 2CH 32:6
Text: And he set captains of war over the people, and gathered them together to him in the street of the gate of the city, and spake comfortably to them, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1f2b1c5-1e97-455c-bc4c-599f76386b10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: 2CH 32:7
Text: Be strong and courageous, be not afraid nor dismayed for the king of Assyria, nor for all the multitude that is with him: for there be more with us than with him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58d73552-a75a-4f5b-9642-d9e92b7724d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 2CH 32:8
Text: With him is an arm of flesh; but with us is the LORD our God to help us, and to fight our battles. And the people rested themselves upon the words of Hezekiah king of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aff8cc5e-b014-4df6-be73-5c654615da2d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: 2CH 32:9
Text: After this did Sennacherib king of Assyria send his servants to Jerusalem, (but he himself laid siege against Lachish, and all his power with him,) unto Hezekiah king of Judah, and unto all Judah that were at Jerusalem, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98323f53-596b-4182-8ae4-17b2f288b9b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: 2CH 32:10
Text: Thus saith Sennacherib king of Assyria, Whereon do ye trust, that ye abide in the siege in Jerusalem?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8fcd1ba-9981-4195-aec0-3da89bc1a620>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: 2CH 32:11
Text: Doth not Hezekiah persuade you to give over yourselves to die by famine and by thirst, saying, The LORD our God shall deliver us out of the hand of the king of Assyria?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c06d8f8-4af1-4d0b-b7ad-4044e83a736c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: 2CH 32:12
Text: Hath not the same Hezekiah taken away his high places and his altars, and commanded Judah and Jerusalem, saying, Ye shall worship before one altar, and burn incense upon it?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2e8e6ca-2d8f-45ae-b569-9301111b494a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: 2CH 32:13
Text: Know ye not what I and my fathers have done unto all the people of other lands? were the gods of the nations of those lands any ways able to deliver their lands out of mine hand?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:618b2efa-039e-4fc5-8320-285799631139>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: 2CH 32:14
Text: Who was there among all the gods of those nations that my fathers utterly destroyed, that could deliver his people out of mine hand, that your God should be able to deliver you out of mine hand?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bffbea4e-5afc-40d4-9fa7-8f7159ffc207>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 308

Reference: 2CH 32:15
Text: Now therefore let not Hezekiah deceive you, nor persuade you on this manner, neither yet believe him: for no god of any nation or kingdom was able to deliver his people out of mine hand, and out of the hand of my fathers: how much less shall your God deliver you out of mine hand?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd7799ee-5b0b-4489-8ba7-885d301c5df1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: 2CH 32:16
Text: And his servants spake yet more against the LORD God, and against his servant Hezekiah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f0081b3-c2af-4ccd-89a0-9fb2c3fd6009>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 280

Reference: 2CH 32:17
Text: He wrote also letters to rail on the LORD God of Israel, and to speak against him, saying, As the gods of the nations of other lands have not delivered their people out of mine hand, so shall not the God of Hezekiah deliver his people out of mine hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6c640ec-27ed-4047-a064-8d0c3b14246e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: 2CH 32:18
Text: Then they cried with a loud voice in the Jews’ speech unto the people of Jerusalem that were on the wall, to affright them, and to trouble them; that they might take the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e996fa8-a22b-4fdb-a2f3-7410add5e15a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 2CH 32:19
Text: And they spake against the God of Jerusalem, as against the gods of the people of the earth, which were the work of the hands of man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4012edef-6cb2-4c30-9dde-bd9f0848d94b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: 2CH 32:20
Text: And for this cause Hezekiah the king, and the prophet Isaiah the son of Amoz, prayed and cried to heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:377a93c9-4894-4471-b55f-1d2b0e7d357a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 333

Reference: 2CH 32:21
Text: And the LORD sent an angel, which cut off all the mighty men of valour, and the leaders and captains in the camp of the king of Assyria. So he returned with shame of face to his own land. And when he was come into the house of his god, they that came forth of his own bowels slew him there with the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eaf338d4-fc7c-4d6c-bdde-9911e9f4a8a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: 2CH 32:22
Text: Thus the LORD saved Hezekiah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem from the hand of Sennacherib the king of Assyria, and from the hand of all other, and guided them on every side.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41138e09-5f62-4d04-b680-8280378efc34>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: 2CH 32:23
Text: And many brought gifts unto the LORD to Jerusalem, and presents to Hezekiah king of Judah: so that he was magnified in the sight of all nations from thenceforth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7f3ed93-7e96-467e-9520-ef306fbcdf26>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: 2CH 32:24
Text: In those days Hezekiah was sick to the death, and prayed unto the LORD: and he spake unto him, and he gave him a sign.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78629670-b920-4dcc-8324-3adfe71e20ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: 2CH 32:25
Text: But Hezekiah rendered not again according to the benefit done unto him; for his heart was lifted up: therefore there was wrath upon him, and upon Judah and Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2054afd5-8122-4891-b213-e4371bb0f6eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: 2CH 32:26
Text: Notwithstanding Hezekiah humbled himself for the pride of his heart, both he and the inhabitants of Jerusalem, so that the wrath of the LORD came not upon them in the days of Hezekiah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a51f44e-9a92-4e66-8da9-23641d8a9352>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: 2CH 32:27
Text: And Hezekiah had exceeding much riches and honour: and he made himself treasuries for silver, and for gold, and for precious stones, and for spices, and for shields, and for all manner of pleasant jewels;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3630276a-0b36-4923-a128-c981cfebdbaf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 2CH 32:28
Text: Storehouses also for the increase of corn, and wine, and oil; and stalls for all manner of beasts, and cotes for flocks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a01ec42-8d5d-40e1-b1a7-0963a43390ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 2CH 32:29
Text: Moreover he provided him cities, and possessions of flocks and herds in abundance: for God had given him substance very much.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fa436a3-7e67-43b0-8f46-3cb9e9f10efb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 2CH 32:30
Text: This same Hezekiah also stopped the upper watercourse of Gihon, and brought it straight down to the west side of the city of David. And Hezekiah prospered in all his works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a3239b3-fd42-40a4-ac7f-9488f4b52324>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: 2CH 32:31
Text: Howbeit in the business of the ambassadors of the princes of Babylon, who sent unto him to enquire of the wonder that was done in the land, God left him, to try him, that he might know all that was in his heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:058e0f22-dca5-42a5-8437-901e91e6df2b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: 2CH 32:32
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Hezekiah, and his goodness, behold, they are written in the vision of Isaiah the prophet, the son of Amoz, and in the book of the kings of Judah and Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/32/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b1b084c-8ade-448b-b5f5-a071c5b277b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: 2CH 32:33
Text: And Hezekiah slept with his fathers, and they buried him in the chiefest of the sepulchres of the sons of David: and all Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem did him honour at his death. And Manasseh his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d826b44-6c15-48d5-977f-9663a56326d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: 2CH 33:1
Text: Manasseh was twelve years old when he began to reign, and he reigned fifty and five years in Jerusalem:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96217f3a-5514-42ea-81bf-9514459b9149>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: 2CH 33:2
Text: But did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD, like unto the abominations of the heathen, whom the LORD had cast out before the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce8234e5-b0d1-43db-be53-7b5e0ccd4e15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: 2CH 33:3
Text: For he built again the high places which Hezekiah his father had broken down, and he reared up altars for Baalim, and made groves, and worshipped all the host of heaven, and served them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fc13ed9-5501-4fa4-b8be-8959a35bd9e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 2CH 33:4
Text: Also he built altars in the house of the LORD, whereof the LORD had said, In Jerusalem shall my name be for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b75e3a72-2ebc-4527-b9de-04c1e463bfe2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: 2CH 33:5
Text: And he built altars for all the host of heaven in the two courts of the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b90771e-cc8c-4cbb-b9c4-1d607f5557a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 306

Reference: 2CH 33:6
Text: And he caused his children to pass through the fire in the valley of the son of Hinnom: also he observed times, and used enchantments, and used witchcraft, and dealt with a familiar spirit, and with wizards: he wrought much evil in the sight of the LORD, to provoke him to anger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46423f53-7274-4cf2-bb3f-55b24b0db74b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: 2CH 33:7
Text: And he set a carved image, the idol which he had made, in the house of God, of which God had said to David and to Solomon his son, In this house, and in Jerusalem, which I have chosen before all the tribes of Israel, will I put my name for ever:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4918346f-8ef8-4135-b825-2620fd3cae79>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 289

Reference: 2CH 33:8
Text: Neither will I any more remove the foot of Israel from out of the land which I have appointed for your fathers; so that they will take heed to do all that I have commanded them, according to the whole law and the statutes and the ordinances by the hand of Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c7a3021-dab5-426b-8fdf-ca4e1c68fefc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: 2CH 33:9
Text: So Manasseh made Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem to err, and to do worse than the heathen, whom the LORD had destroyed before the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f244f2b1-535c-4fc5-8615-9513a830e5d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: 2CH 33:10
Text: And the LORD spake to Manasseh, and to his people: but they would not hearken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d636341-9994-494a-8060-a509b77e1dbe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: 2CH 33:11
Text: Wherefore the LORD brought upon them the captains of the host of the king of Assyria, which took Manasseh among the thorns, and bound him with fetters, and carried him to Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63e7c4ba-d012-44c8-80f4-1fbf200fe6cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 2CH 33:12
Text: And when he was in affliction, he besought the LORD his God, and humbled himself greatly before the God of his fathers,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73b30b07-e3f9-4624-8727-4527b382eda5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: 2CH 33:13
Text: And prayed unto him: and he was intreated of him, and heard his supplication, and brought him again to Jerusalem into his kingdom. Then Manasseh knew that the LORD he was God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4389d355-79e6-45b9-8cb1-0a8fd7eb442e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 293

Reference: 2CH 33:14
Text: Now after this he built a wall without the city of David, on the west side of Gihon, in the valley, even to the entering in at the fish gate, and compassed about Ophel, and raised it up a very great height, and put captains of war in all the fenced cities of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1310a311-0ac6-4dc9-8b2f-9648dcb938bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: 2CH 33:15
Text: And he took away the strange gods, and the idol out of the house of the LORD, and all the altars that he had built in the mount of the house of the LORD, and in Jerusalem, and cast them out of the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0149cb1a-6af8-4af9-bd95-b2833cc2694a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 2CH 33:16
Text: And he repaired the altar of the LORD, and sacrificed thereon peace offerings and thank offerings, and commanded Judah to serve the LORD God of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef72a5e3-07df-4ac6-9cb5-315773a97eec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: 2CH 33:17
Text: Nevertheless the people did sacrifice still in the high places, yet unto the LORD their God only.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae7d68cb-613b-4641-a0a6-2da662db080e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: 2CH 33:18
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Manasseh, and his prayer unto his God, and the words of the seers that spake to him in the name of the LORD God of Israel, behold, they are written in the book of the kings of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55184e68-af9f-4626-90fa-8c54120b6975>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: 2CH 33:19
Text: His prayer also, and how God was intreated of him, and all his sins, and his trespass, and the places wherein he built high places, and set up groves and graven images, before he was humbled: behold, they are written among the sayings of the seers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5eebefc-f7ca-4240-9fb3-94103f1335c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 2CH 33:20
Text: So Manasseh slept with his fathers, and they buried him in his own house: and Amon his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7bce603-c57d-45f8-97f3-e7722f833c5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 2CH 33:21
Text: Amon was two and twenty years old when he began to reign, and reigned two years in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:027eda07-1a16-4fc3-9d53-ffe2c5f832f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: 2CH 33:22
Text: But he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD, as did Manasseh his father: for Amon sacrificed unto all the carved images which Manasseh his father had made, and served them;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e78f278-ce0b-4e74-b888-0b6188aa4fac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 2CH 33:23
Text: And humbled not himself before the LORD, as Manasseh his father had humbled himself; but Amon trespassed more and more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eeaf535b-1113-41f9-81df-a26cd44b2d1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: 2CH 33:24
Text: And his servants conspired against him, and slew him in his own house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/33/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c875278f-3a9d-4383-9d72-aee870ad6778>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: 2CH 33:25
Text: But the people of the land slew all them that had conspired against king Amon; and the people of the land made Josiah his son king in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43d5d6d4-768c-49d1-90c1-896bfaf82891>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 2CH 34:1
Text: Josiah was eight years old when he began to reign, and he reigned in Jerusalem one and thirty years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c45b42cd-6f6f-4ad1-9c7d-736a4add4436>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 2CH 34:2
Text: And he did that which was right in the sight of the LORD, and walked in the ways of David his father, and declined neither to the right hand, nor to the left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:789b8154-b63d-431e-bbda-0be15bcf1b13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 285

Reference: 2CH 34:3
Text: For in the eighth year of his reign, while he was yet young, he began to seek after the God of David his father: and in the twelfth year he began to purge Judah and Jerusalem from the high places, and the groves, and the carved images, and the molten images.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f11f404c-87af-4b5c-8eac-4094fa1ab397>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 318

Reference: 2CH 34:4
Text: And they brake down the altars of Baalim in his presence; and the images, that were on high above them, he cut down; and the groves, and the carved images, and the molten images, he brake in pieces, and made dust of them, and strowed it upon the graves of them that had sacrificed unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2ee8f4e-d3bb-42d5-a10f-5519ea77a54a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: 2CH 34:5
Text: And he burnt the bones of the priests upon their altars, and cleansed Judah and Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17a60be1-cd6c-4999-8b4b-a51f699aae76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 2CH 34:6
Text: And so did he in the cities of Manasseh, and Ephraim, and Simeon, even unto Naphtali, with their mattocks round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc2e400b-99b6-406e-abbb-95bc39561f44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: 2CH 34:7
Text: And when he had broken down the altars and the groves, and had beaten the graven images into powder, and cut down all the idols throughout all the land of Israel, he returned to Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ba91b1f-3296-423e-b1fb-dbac638bd0bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: 2CH 34:8
Text: Now in the eighteenth year of his reign, when he had purged the land, and the house, he sent Shaphan the son of Azaliah, and Maaseiah the governor of the city, and Joah the son of Joahaz the recorder, to repair the house of the LORD his God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52492bad-36e7-4497-bb6e-2a70d3323ce4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 323

Reference: 2CH 34:9
Text: And when they came to Hilkiah the high priest, they delivered the money that was brought into the house of God, which the Levites that kept the doors had gathered of the hand of Manasseh and Ephraim, and of all the remnant of Israel, and of all Judah and Benjamin; and they returned to Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9408b98-bfd5-434b-bf61-596b7e32b911>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: 2CH 34:10
Text: And they put it in the hand of the workmen that had the oversight of the house of the LORD, and they gave it to the workmen that wrought in the house of the LORD, to repair and amend the house:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5db72632-b77f-498f-85b2-71a15e7673e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: 2CH 34:11
Text: Even to the artificers and builders gave they it, to buy hewn stone, and timber for couplings, and to floor the houses which the kings of Judah had destroyed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc9ddd47-abb7-478e-a62b-526ac40e0a95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 303

Reference: 2CH 34:12
Text: And the men did the work faithfully: and the overseers of them were Jahath and Obadiah, the Levites, of the sons of Merari; and Zechariah and Meshullam, of the sons of the Kohathites, to set it forward; and other of the Levites, all that could skill of instruments of musick.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88bcf076-183e-480a-a6e8-960f9721562f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: 2CH 34:13
Text: Also they were over the bearers of burdens, and were overseers of all that wrought the work in any manner of service: and of the Levites there were scribes, and officers, and porters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a4d52f7-d984-4d5c-b721-070ffe35aed2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 2CH 34:14
Text: And when they brought out the money that was brought into the house of the LORD, Hilkiah the priest found a book of the law of the LORD given by Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b08e8c23-fb3d-4520-a038-942f9a130d64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: 2CH 34:15
Text: And Hilkiah answered and said to Shaphan the scribe, I have found the book of the law in the house of the LORD. And Hilkiah delivered the book to Shaphan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c66d9fb1-adcb-4642-9179-87d52c30cddc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 2CH 34:16
Text: And Shaphan carried the book to the king, and brought the king word back again, saying, All that was committed to thy servants, they do it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:503e7001-580a-4d52-8673-68a978ebd6ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: 2CH 34:17
Text: And they have gathered together the money that was found in the house of the LORD, and have delivered it into the hand of the overseers, and to the hand of the workmen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6191f35-f1ee-4351-9ea1-14dcc3295096>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: 2CH 34:18
Text: Then Shaphan the scribe told the king, saying, Hilkiah the priest hath given me a book. And Shaphan read it before the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f714a65-1ae3-4233-a37d-416f2eb6fdf2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: 2CH 34:19
Text: And it came to pass, when the king had heard the words of the law, that he rent his clothes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a32e2feb-c65b-489a-805b-cb962d3ad2fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 2CH 34:20
Text: And the king commanded Hilkiah, and Ahikam the son of Shaphan, and Abdon the son of Micah, and Shaphan the scribe, and Asaiah a servant of the king’s, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46e4957e-2f0a-4253-91c8-32a81c3e2a89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 323

Reference: 2CH 34:21
Text: Go, enquire of the LORD for me, and for them that are left in Israel and in Judah, concerning the words of the book that is found: for great is the wrath of the LORD that is poured out upon us, because our fathers have not kept the word of the LORD, to do after all that is written in this book.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4301e6b-04a9-4b50-82a3-661ea74079ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: 2CH 34:22
Text: And Hilkiah, and they that the king had appointed, went to Huldah the prophetess, the wife of Shallum the son of Tikvath, the son of Hasrah, keeper of the wardrobe; (now she dwelt in Jerusalem in the college:) and they spake to her to that effect.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:deba96a4-71ea-453b-9957-859d92497a98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: 2CH 34:23
Text: And she answered them, Thus saith the LORD God of Israel, Tell ye the man that sent you to me,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c080f53-1355-4696-8fc3-0930af4cb998>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: 2CH 34:24
Text: Thus saith the LORD, Behold, I will bring evil upon this place, and upon the inhabitants thereof, even all the curses that are written in the book which they have read before the king of Judah:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d011ac38-87a3-4434-b92d-ca2e681f3dc9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: 2CH 34:25
Text: Because they have forsaken me, and have burned incense unto other gods, that they might provoke me to anger with all the works of their hands; therefore my wrath shall be poured out upon this place, and shall not be quenched.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:112815ee-dc65-4a4b-84ca-8f498eda0211>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: 2CH 34:26
Text: And as for the king of Judah, who sent you to enquire of the LORD, so shall ye say unto him, Thus saith the LORD God of Israel concerning the words which thou hast heard;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6fbeadf2-30b5-4615-b950-4b8b023d9dd4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 313

Reference: 2CH 34:27
Text: Because thine heart was tender, and thou didst humble thyself before God, when thou heardest his words against this place, and against the inhabitants thereof, and humbledst thyself before me, and didst rend thy clothes, and weep before me; I have even heard thee also, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ddbe1f0-a2a6-47ea-b381-3abc26c473ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: 2CH 34:28
Text: Behold, I will gather thee to thy fathers, and thou shalt be gathered to thy grave in peace, neither shall thine eyes see all the evil that I will bring upon this place, and upon the inhabitants of the same. So they brought the king word again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a024a0c-fe99-411e-84b9-de0544cc6fe9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: 2CH 34:29
Text: Then the king sent and gathered together all the elders of Judah and Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93ad0e98-8bc9-4b2a-bd22-19d4e9a394f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 316

Reference: 2CH 34:30
Text: And the king went up into the house of the LORD, and all the men of Judah, and the inhabitants of Jerusalem, and the priests, and the Levites, and all the people, great and small: and he read in their ears all the words of the book of the covenant that was found in the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ffb702d-1446-4bde-9aab-749190c660f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 302

Reference: 2CH 34:31
Text: And the king stood in his place, and made a covenant before the LORD, to walk after the LORD, and to keep his commandments, and his testimonies, and his statutes, with all his heart, and with all his soul, to perform the words of the covenant which are written in this book.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6fd6c247-b264-419d-823f-b561361133dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: 2CH 34:32
Text: And he caused all that were present in Jerusalem and Benjamin to stand to it. And the inhabitants of Jerusalem did according to the covenant of God, the God of their fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/34/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03c3262f-9237-4e80-b18e-c42cfc9761e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 307

Reference: 2CH 34:33
Text: And Josiah took away all the abominations out of all the countries that pertained to the children of Israel, and made all that were present in Israel to serve, even to serve the LORD their God. And all his days they departed not from following the LORD, the God of their fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e30510b-8322-4e6e-9c32-81950d084242>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 2CH 35:1
Text: Moreover Josiah kept a passover unto the LORD in Jerusalem: and they killed the passover on the fourteenth day of the first month.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9355e68-2a03-4765-be65-565309c6bd21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 2CH 35:2
Text: And he set the priests in their charges, and encouraged them to the service of the house of the LORD,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96e782bf-b720-45ce-8e60-994f691e030a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 292

Reference: 2CH 35:3
Text: And said unto the Levites that taught all Israel, which were holy unto the LORD, Put the holy ark in the house which Solomon the son of David king of Israel did build; it shall not be a burden upon your shoulders: serve now the LORD your God, and his people Israel,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2deeefc3-4a73-4342-9a02-48efe8476a53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: 2CH 35:4
Text: And prepare yourselves by the houses of your fathers, after your courses, according to the writing of David king of Israel, and according to the writing of Solomon his son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74cfaf8f-485e-43db-82cb-4bd1e8502078>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: 2CH 35:5
Text: And stand in the holy place according to the divisions of the families of the fathers of your brethren the people, and after the division of the families of the Levites.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b24e9b9f-2f52-4412-b75d-d1ba5ff71cbd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 2CH 35:6
Text: So kill the passover, and sanctify yourselves, and prepare your brethren, that they may do according to the word of the LORD by the hand of Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:483129d4-ec57-4654-9509-131a0d64af7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: 2CH 35:7
Text: And Josiah gave to the people, of the flock, lambs and kids, all for the passover offerings, for all that were present, to the number of thirty thousand, and three thousand bullocks: these were of the king’s substance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:010104f6-e60b-4289-87ee-52a45a4a85b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 287

Reference: 2CH 35:8
Text: And his princes gave willingly unto the people, to the priests, and to the Levites: Hilkiah and Zechariah and Jehiel, rulers of the house of God, gave unto the priests for the passover offerings two thousand and six hundred small cattle and three hundred oxen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:996c8f27-0236-4419-8803-e4a8394205a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: 2CH 35:9
Text: Conaniah also, and Shemaiah and Nethaneel, his brethren, and Hashabiah and Jeiel and Jozabad, chief of the Levites, gave unto the Levites for passover offerings five thousand small cattle, and five hundred oxen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14f486ba-7ea7-463f-8b91-704257987872>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 2CH 35:10
Text: So the service was prepared, and the priests stood in their place, and the Levites in their courses, according to the king’s commandment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a230116-89b1-4235-820c-a8da1c26a249>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 2CH 35:11
Text: And they killed the passover, and the priests sprinkled the blood from their hands, and the Levites flayed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23090346-1a87-4b24-a96a-54a4970fc922>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: 2CH 35:12
Text: And they removed the burnt offerings, that they might give according to the divisions of the families of the people, to offer unto the LORD, as it is written in the book of Moses. And so did they with the oxen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b369596b-e107-47e7-aa20-d1410956cd23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: 2CH 35:13
Text: And they roasted the passover with fire according to the ordinance: but the other holy offerings sod they in pots, and in caldrons, and in pans, and divided them speedily among all the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4021b87-757f-42a4-8884-bd2815f32bd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 286

Reference: 2CH 35:14
Text: And afterward they made ready for themselves, and for the priests: because the priests the sons of Aaron were busied in offering of burnt offerings and the fat until night; therefore the Levites prepared for themselves, and for the priests the sons of Aaron.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9236451-a789-47d3-986e-455734829569>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 305

Reference: 2CH 35:15
Text: And the singers the sons of Asaph were in their place, according to the commandment of David, and Asaph, and Heman, and Jeduthun the king’s seer; and the porters waited at every gate; they might not depart from their service; for their brethren the Levites prepared for them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ab74a1b-1807-4eb2-b6cf-e2c982c7e02a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: 2CH 35:16
Text: So all the service of the LORD was prepared the same day, to keep the passover, and to offer burnt offerings upon the altar of the LORD, according to the commandment of king Josiah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1931b642-5e20-4cd0-a0a7-975d8f409f74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: 2CH 35:17
Text: And the children of Israel that were present kept the passover at that time, and the feast of unleavened bread seven days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4b39dea-1fff-4475-b1d4-8b490cef7240>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 303

Reference: 2CH 35:18
Text: And there was no passover like to that kept in Israel from the days of Samuel the prophet; neither did all the kings of Israel keep such a passover as Josiah kept, and the priests, and the Levites, and all Judah and Israel that were present, and the inhabitants of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8dcebe0a-847c-4487-91a4-a1009b958a3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: 2CH 35:19
Text: In the eighteenth year of the reign of Josiah was this passover kept.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64fd2406-210f-4f43-bb4d-061f108a00b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: 2CH 35:20
Text: After all this, when Josiah had prepared the temple, Necho king of Egypt came up to fight against Charchemish by Euphrates: and Josiah went out against him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f534f437-d26d-46db-ae59-cbe9e68edd36>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 309

Reference: 2CH 35:21
Text: But he sent ambassadors to him, saying, What have I to do with thee, thou king of Judah? I come not against thee this day, but against the house wherewith I have war: for God commanded me to make haste: forbear thee from meddling with God, who is with me, that he destroy thee not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78c369d7-b7eb-44d5-a169-60f42e8e5e62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: 2CH 35:22
Text: Nevertheless Josiah would not turn his face from him, but disguised himself, that he might fight with him, and hearkened not unto the words of Necho from the mouth of God, and came to fight in the valley of Megiddo.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11aa8613-e7a0-4eec-b91d-89f1055ebaa5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: 2CH 35:23
Text: And the archers shot at king Josiah; and the king said to his servants, Have me away; for I am sore wounded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d74eeba4-6bca-4e02-b73e-31c0ade94a86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 279

Reference: 2CH 35:24
Text: His servants therefore took him out of that chariot, and put him in the second chariot that he had; and they brought him to Jerusalem, and he died, and was buried in one of the sepulchres of his fathers. And all Judah and Jerusalem mourned for Josiah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a678d21-37de-4568-ab00-e6fbe1a1b54f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: 2CH 35:25
Text: And Jeremiah lamented for Josiah: and all the singing men and the singing women spake of Josiah in their lamentations to this day, and made them an ordinance in Israel: and, behold, they are written in the lamentations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:739245d6-512e-40ae-b042-54a3b4c2e4c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 2CH 35:26
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Josiah, and his goodness, according to that which was written in the law of the LORD,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/35/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa1de3ee-5e3b-4e3e-8367-15ce292f3698>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: 2CH 35:27
Text: And his deeds, first and last, behold, they are written in the book of the kings of Israel and Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/36/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20d4eacd-c58f-4e25-9aa2-c551abecc27c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: 2CH 36:1
Text: Then the people of the land took Jehoahaz the son of Josiah, and made him king in his father’s stead in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/36/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d1d63bb-3796-4616-8b10-aa9125138b36>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 2CH 36:2
Text: Jehoahaz was twenty and three years old when he began to reign, and he reigned three months in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/36/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8367b691-56e4-412f-ba95-c9ea694ff8a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: 2CH 36:3
Text: And the king of Egypt put him down at Jerusalem, and condemned the land in an hundred talents of silver and a talent of gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/36/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0fa5dda-1593-4793-a271-3c9c3fb7a336>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: 2CH 36:4
Text: And the king of Egypt made Eliakim his brother king over Judah and Jerusalem, and turned his name to Jehoiakim. And Necho took Jehoahaz his brother, and carried him to Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/36/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7075e68-0b18-4dd5-ba5c-b7d83719b5f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: 2CH 36:5
Text: Jehoiakim was twenty and five years old when he began to reign, and he reigned eleven years in Jerusalem: and he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD his God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/36/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36497dd0-2e13-44d3-9446-b29c5c7354af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: 2CH 36:6
Text: Against him came up Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, and bound him in fetters, to carry him to Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/36/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd88f0dc-22dc-4f8b-8d0b-0101c2a7cb77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 2CH 36:7
Text: Nebuchadnezzar also carried of the vessels of the house of the LORD to Babylon, and put them in his temple at Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/36/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a759741e-40fc-449a-8edd-0fe1e1af84f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: 2CH 36:8
Text: Now the rest of the acts of Jehoiakim, and his abominations which he did, and that which was found in him, behold, they are written in the book of the kings of Israel and Judah: and Jehoiachin his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/36/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ae08fc7-0a25-48d6-864b-ffd5787df607>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: 2CH 36:9
Text: Jehoiachin was eight years old when he began to reign, and he reigned three months and ten days in Jerusalem: and he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/36/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec2ffc5a-1cc5-4295-8978-cd2d0813eab4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: 2CH 36:10
Text: And when the year was expired, king Nebuchadnezzar sent, and brought him to Babylon, with the goodly vessels of the house of the LORD, and made Zedekiah his brother king over Judah and Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/36/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ade57720-a85b-4565-8d75-819765cab01d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 2CH 36:11
Text: Zedekiah was one and twenty years old when he began to reign, and reigned eleven years in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/36/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a12373ee-f75f-4e7e-bfc8-622db55f13c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: 2CH 36:12
Text: And he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD his God, and humbled not himself before Jeremiah the prophet speaking from the mouth of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/36/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33ffb979-3421-49e1-a684-9046343dfee3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 2CH 36:13
Text: And he also rebelled against king Nebuchadnezzar, who had made him swear by God: but he stiffened his neck, and hardened his heart from turning unto the LORD God of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/36/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06338340-ae38-418e-9774-24650ffb4ef7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: 2CH 36:14
Text: Moreover all the chief of the priests, and the people, transgressed very much after all the abominations of the heathen; and polluted the house of the LORD which he had hallowed in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/36/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1345f59b-6477-4f93-b5f8-1af5b3c69c9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: 2CH 36:15
Text: And the LORD God of their fathers sent to them by his messengers, rising up betimes, and sending; because he had compassion on his people, and on his dwelling place:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/36/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b953055-8414-45f7-af68-4c105326f87f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: 2CH 36:16
Text: But they mocked the messengers of God, and despised his words, and misused his prophets, until the wrath of the LORD arose against his people, till there was no remedy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/36/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9f0213a-74f5-46e7-a0af-00f0e6de2bf9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: 2CH 36:17
Text: Therefore he brought upon them the king of the Chaldees, who slew their young men with the sword in the house of their sanctuary, and had no compassion upon young man or maiden, old man, or him that stooped for age: he gave them all into his hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/36/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5a36536-18ba-4b25-bfba-fa5b0ac73dd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: 2CH 36:18
Text: And all the vessels of the house of God, great and small, and the treasures of the house of the LORD, and the treasures of the king, and of his princes; all these he brought to Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/36/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db919fd7-1964-420f-8636-e5fc6229119e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: 2CH 36:19
Text: And they burnt the house of God, and brake down the wall of Jerusalem, and burnt all the palaces thereof with fire, and destroyed all the goodly vessels thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/36/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d981178-7ee5-45a0-9c97-2bb4041546df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: 2CH 36:20
Text: And them that had escaped from the sword carried he away to Babylon; where they were servants to him and his sons until the reign of the kingdom of Persia:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/36/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:665134cd-0f1f-4203-b0a6-bd2a2171765c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: 2CH 36:21
Text: To fulfil the word of the LORD by the mouth of Jeremiah, until the land had enjoyed her sabbaths: for as long as she lay desolate she kept sabbath, to fulfil threescore and ten years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/36/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf0a8c6b-e3a9-4c05-8190-dee08f1dcd68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 303

Reference: 2CH 36:22
Text: Now in the first year of Cyrus king of Persia, that the word of the LORD spoken by the mouth of Jeremiah might be accomplished, the LORD stirred up the spirit of Cyrus king of Persia, that he made a proclamation throughout all his kingdom, and put it also in writing, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2CH/36/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1df8f06d-8227-4c5a-afd0-4d9198d10d95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 297

Reference: 2CH 36:23
Text: Thus saith Cyrus king of Persia, All the kingdoms of the earth hath the LORD God of heaven given me; and he hath charged me to build him an house in Jerusalem, which is in Judah. Who is there among you of all his people? The LORD his God be with him, and let him go up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29b3ee77-8554-437f-b437-1b3da2137f0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 291

Reference: EZR 1:1
Text: Now in the first year of Cyrus king of Persia, that the word of the LORD by the mouth of Jeremiah might be fulfilled, the LORD stirred up the spirit of Cyrus king of Persia, that he made a proclamation throughout all his kingdom, and put it also in writing, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8259a933-6eb4-42c7-8266-a1ad5f48fe48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: EZR 1:2
Text: Thus saith Cyrus king of Persia, The LORD God of heaven hath given me all the kingdoms of the earth; and he hath charged me to build him an house at Jerusalem, which is in Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1535aef-b169-4eea-98d2-070885b40272>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: EZR 1:3
Text: Who is there among you of all his people? his God be with him, and let him go up to Jerusalem, which is in Judah, and build the house of the LORD God of Israel, (he is the God,) which is in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46ec96f4-cf7e-466b-9d79-a82a3e3b5676>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: EZR 1:4
Text: And whosoever remaineth in any place where he sojourneth, let the men of his place help him with silver, and with gold, and with goods, and with beasts, beside the freewill offering for the house of God that is in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:936b8484-c5d3-4e74-b150-93527f4ee620>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: EZR 1:5
Text: Then rose up the chief of the fathers of Judah and Benjamin, and the priests, and the Levites, with all them whose spirit God had raised, to go up to build the house of the LORD which is in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfaf740e-ab60-41dd-baa3-31290e5c809c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: EZR 1:6
Text: And all they that were about them strengthened their hands with vessels of silver, with gold, with goods, and with beasts, and with precious things, beside all that was willingly offered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51879da2-cc56-4205-9a59-8af436a7674d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: EZR 1:7
Text: Also Cyrus the king brought forth the vessels of the house of the LORD, which Nebuchadnezzar had brought forth out of Jerusalem, and had put them in the house of his gods;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fdd9f481-d00f-41b0-accb-d69717c7edbc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: EZR 1:8
Text: Even those did Cyrus king of Persia bring forth by the hand of Mithredath the treasurer, and numbered them unto Sheshbazzar, the prince of Judah.


