Content-Length: 93

Reference: EZR 4:18
Text: The letter which ye sent unto us hath been plainly read before me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/4/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f969de7-f4ea-4da8-839d-df5615d0c292>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: EZR 4:19
Text: And I commanded, and search hath been made, and it is found that this city of old time hath made insurrection against kings, and that rebellion and sedition have been made therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/4/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d8eede6-02b4-477c-adb5-7d8f2e2ffedb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: EZR 4:20
Text: There have been mighty kings also over Jerusalem, which have ruled over all countries beyond the river; and toll, tribute, and custom, was paid unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/4/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c6703e5-cfe9-4ab3-ac05-6607db90eb2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: EZR 4:21
Text: Give ye now commandment to cause these men to cease, and that this city be not builded, until another commandment shall be given from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/4/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d0c9f1b-2c5d-4f98-b2d5-96e1318bfdb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: EZR 4:22
Text: Take heed now that ye fail not to do this: why should damage grow to the hurt of the kings?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/4/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0aa8c211-9954-44b6-aaec-f1e25b331109>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: EZR 4:23
Text: Now when the copy of king Artaxerxes’ letter was read before Rehum, and Shimshai the scribe, and their companions, they went up in haste to Jerusalem unto the Jews, and made them to cease by force and power.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/4/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ded955a8-8a6f-4b11-b29f-10687b248c1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: EZR 4:24
Text: Then ceased the work of the house of God which is at Jerusalem. So it ceased unto the second year of the reign of Darius king of Persia.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:458876c9-015c-4c45-b8a6-f42faefcd467>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: EZR 5:1
Text: Then the prophets, Haggai the prophet, and Zechariah the son of Iddo, prophesied unto the Jews that were in Judah and Jerusalem in the name of the God of Israel, even unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a5416e7-bfaa-4b70-8644-0dcf1d2f69bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: EZR 5:2
Text: Then rose up Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, and Jeshua the son of Jozadak, and began to build the house of God which is at Jerusalem: and with them were the prophets of God helping them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54fe8c3e-af41-4c0c-8610-aea2fabdff12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: EZR 5:3
Text: At the same time came to them Tatnai, governor on this side the river, and Shetharboznai and their companions, and said thus unto them, Who hath commanded you to build this house, and to make up this wall?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03d4bb31-1c1d-4ba1-9b5b-05eb2fb0b4fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: EZR 5:4
Text: Then said we unto them after this manner, What are the names of the men that make this building?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b4eaf9d-b8e3-49b8-ac24-80df4ae3dd58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: EZR 5:5
Text: But the eye of their God was upon the elders of the Jews, that they could not cause them to cease, till the matter came to Darius: and then they returned answer by letter concerning this matter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a935160f-5c07-48d4-a5e4-d757770413cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: EZR 5:6
Text: The copy of the letter that Tatnai, governor on this side the river, and Shetharboznai and his companions the Apharsachites, which were on this side the river, sent unto Darius the king:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a4724b4-2198-4d3b-9c7e-48e2aa0566d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: EZR 5:7
Text: They sent a letter unto him, wherein was written thus; Unto Darius the king, all peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:090de5fe-34da-4df9-b339-f1ff90963e21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: EZR 5:8
Text: Be it known unto the king, that we went into the province of Judea, to the house of the great God, which is builded with great stones, and timber is laid in the walls, and this work goeth fast on, and prospereth in their hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b584c931-0b12-4b68-8320-ea01ed65d09a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: EZR 5:9
Text: Then asked we those elders, and said unto them thus, Who commanded you to build this house, and to make up these walls?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88969b50-d597-47e4-93c9-302da91c351e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: EZR 5:10
Text: We asked their names also, to certify thee, that we might write the names of the men that were the chief of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d681b6f-bc95-458e-b597-46870a839d64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: EZR 5:11
Text: And thus they returned us answer, saying, We are the servants of the God of heaven and earth, and build the house that was builded these many years ago, which a great king of Israel builded and set up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:930439fd-acb9-48a1-ae90-6190e6385f7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: EZR 5:12
Text: But after that our fathers had provoked the God of heaven unto wrath, he gave them into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon, the Chaldean, who destroyed this house, and carried the people away into Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d51d5d05-dd79-4da9-821b-71b7d961e3ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: EZR 5:13
Text: But in the first year of Cyrus the king of Babylon the same king Cyrus made a decree to build this house of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f01f822-0006-4cbe-b75c-5be8dbfed79c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 348

Reference: EZR 5:14
Text: And the vessels also of gold and silver of the house of God, which Nebuchadnezzar took out of the temple that was in Jerusalem, and brought them into the temple of Babylon, those did Cyrus the king take out of the temple of Babylon, and they were delivered unto one, whose name was Sheshbazzar, whom he had made governor;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:feb7f4ce-0ed2-4d9f-ba78-8a28acbc2130>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: EZR 5:15
Text: And said unto him, Take these vessels, go, carry them into the temple that is in Jerusalem, and let the house of God be builded in his place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb270ac5-6d5e-481e-b39e-932b669b2858>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: EZR 5:16
Text: Then came the same Sheshbazzar, and laid the foundation of the house of God which is in Jerusalem: and since that time even until now hath it been in building, and yet it is not finished.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/5/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35c01aa3-7a84-48ae-bacc-5a8a5aefe1b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 319

Reference: EZR 5:17
Text: Now therefore, if it seem good to the king, let there be search made in the king’s treasure house, which is there at Babylon, whether it be so, that a decree was made of Cyrus the king to build this house of God at Jerusalem, and let the king send his pleasure to us concerning this matter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60c7c8db-1e45-428f-b5f9-b9f877f35cd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: EZR 6:1
Text: Then Darius the king made a decree, and search was made in the house of the rolls, where the treasures were laid up in Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44dd2932-9747-4aaf-8653-5b63da4b7d43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EZR 6:2
Text: And there was found at Achmetha, in the palace that is in the province of the Medes, a roll, and therein was a record thus written:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18c16043-244e-4bc4-bf6f-e67fee1e5e23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 339

Reference: EZR 6:3
Text: In the first year of Cyrus the king the same Cyrus the king made a decree concerning the house of God at Jerusalem, Let the house be builded, the place where they offered sacrifices, and let the foundations thereof be strongly laid; the height thereof threescore cubits, and the breadth thereof threescore cubits;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bf1247d-ee95-4110-bb8f-c6fa24df4a9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: EZR 6:4
Text: With three rows of great stones, and a row of new timber: and let the expenses be given out of the king’s house:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a026a02-04f2-4105-85e3-0b05680cb620>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 318

Reference: EZR 6:5
Text: And also let the golden and silver vessels of the house of God, which Nebuchadnezzar took forth out of the temple which is at Jerusalem, and brought unto Babylon, be restored, and brought again unto the temple which is at Jerusalem, every one to his place, and place them in the house of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59ce750b-b9ae-47dd-9f6a-0ad16e2f5b05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: EZR 6:6
Text: Now therefore, Tatnai, governor beyond the river, Shetharboznai, and your companions the Apharsachites, which are beyond the river, be ye far from thence:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:adc1f803-8a13-451c-ba69-90e8f1ea98eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EZR 6:7
Text: Let the work of this house of God alone; let the governor of the Jews and the elders of the Jews build this house of God in his place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4163669-a0d9-458c-a945-b93b726f2dbd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: EZR 6:8
Text: Moreover I make a decree what ye shall do to the elders of these Jews for the building of this house of God: that of the king’s goods, even of the tribute beyond the river, forthwith expenses be given unto these men, that they be not hindered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afbe0c4f-25e8-435a-a11b-27126d74fc8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 289

Reference: EZR 6:9
Text: And that which they have need of, both young bullocks, and rams, and lambs, for the burnt offerings of the God of heaven, wheat, salt, wine, and oil, according to the appointment of the priests which are at Jerusalem, let it be given them day by day without fail:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb38528b-7635-4a43-8db9-a04572d9fe5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: EZR 6:10
Text: That they may offer sacrifices of sweet savours unto the God of heaven, and pray for the life of the king, and of his sons.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04f13ee0-4c8e-49ef-9bbe-4d7f0d6a24a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: EZR 6:11
Text: Also I have made a decree, that whosoever shall alter this word, let timber be pulled down from his house, and being set up, let him be hanged thereon; and let his house be made a dunghill for this.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:592cbc61-d141-4a34-ad1f-c717dd7341fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: EZR 6:12
Text: And the God that hath caused his name to dwell there destroy all kings and people, that shall put to their hand to alter and to destroy this house of God which is at Jerusalem. I Darius have made a decree; let it be done with speed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f17c23f-d42e-4d14-807a-f8703bcfe209>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: EZR 6:13
Text: Then Tatnai, governor on this side the river, Shetharboznai, and their companions, according to that which Darius the king had sent, so they did speedily.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/6/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8550b93-27a9-4717-b952-b5a2aef0c3f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 330

Reference: EZR 6:14
Text: And the elders of the Jews builded, and they prospered through the prophesying of Haggai the prophet and Zechariah the son of Iddo. And they builded, and finished it, according to the commandment of the God of Israel, and according to the commandment of Cyrus, and Darius, and Artaxerxes king of Persia.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/6/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32ba916c-b65c-4ac9-b945-4cd907f8576c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: EZR 6:15
Text: And this house was finished on the third day of the month Adar, which was in the sixth year of the reign of Darius the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/6/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f4b2bd4-cae8-412b-ad03-e9d114f65510>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: EZR 6:16
Text: And the children of Israel, the priests, and the Levites, and the rest of the children of the captivity, kept the dedication of this house of God with joy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/6/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb9ed079-a594-4687-8ca0-4c6e4b5d7318>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: EZR 6:17
Text: And offered at the dedication of this house of God an hundred bullocks, two hundred rams, four hundred lambs; and for a sin offering for all Israel, twelve he goats, according to the number of the tribes of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/6/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55e71d83-a523-41cf-89d7-9bedf3c84db5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: EZR 6:18
Text: And they set the priests in their divisions, and the Levites in their courses, for the service of God, which is at Jerusalem; as it is written in the book of Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/6/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35d260d5-c942-46d4-a49f-589af33c5720>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: EZR 6:19
Text: And the children of the captivity kept the passover upon the fourteenth day of the first month.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/6/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd4f9181-8c4f-46f8-8260-e50b2fa30a6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: EZR 6:20
Text: For the priests and the Levites were purified together, all of them were pure, and killed the passover for all the children of the captivity, and for their brethren the priests, and for themselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZR/6/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
