Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: NEH 13:1
Text: On that day they read in the book of Moses in the audience of the people; and therein was found written, that the Ammonite and the Moabite should not come into the congregation of God for ever;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e64ae8a3-ede7-43f1-8a1a-8b74d04068fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: NEH 13:2
Text: Because they met not the children of Israel with bread and with water, but hired Balaam against them, that he should curse them: howbeit our God turned the curse into a blessing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a489540-9f23-43dd-bb18-bf1c57894ccb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: NEH 13:3
Text: Now it came to pass, when they had heard the law, that they separated from Israel all the mixed multitude.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d50c94af-5c7b-46ae-ba78-5dd2d32926e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: NEH 13:4
Text: And before this, Eliashib the priest, having the oversight of the chamber of the house of our God, was allied unto Tobiah:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
