WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:014780b6-914d-4a9f-a2b4-87c9165ed049>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: NEH 13:6
Text: But in all this time was not I at Jerusalem: for in the two and thirtieth year of Artaxerxes king of Babylon came I unto the king, and after certain days obtained I leave of the king:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:136f21ee-fd63-4466-886f-992ad56ab063>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: NEH 13:7
Text: And I came to Jerusalem, and understood of the evil that Eliashib did for Tobiah, in preparing him a chamber in the courts of the house of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59a6c49c-82a6-4296-aa88-3c0fbcd12f28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: NEH 13:8
Text: And it grieved me sore: therefore I cast forth all the household stuff to Tobiah out of the chamber.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a338f83-b7b7-4dc3-ae3c-96299aea689b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: NEH 13:9
Text: Then I commanded, and they cleansed the chambers: and thither brought I again the vessels of the house of God, with the meat offering and the frankincense.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f511674-4124-4337-915c-768f0907a354>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: NEH 13:10
Text: And I perceived that the portions of the Levites had not been given them: for the Levites and the singers, that did the work, were fled every one to his field.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c901ab6-130f-463a-b4de-06fdf6671708>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: NEH 13:11
Text: Then contended I with the rulers, and said, Why is the house of God forsaken? And I gathered them together, and set them in their place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4cda55c0-856e-428a-af6e-ce6dadba6a6d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: NEH 13:12
Text: Then brought all Judah the tithe of the corn and the new wine and the oil unto the treasuries.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:060f939d-b772-4e09-beef-c09c452b4f20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 299

Reference: NEH 13:13
Text: And I made treasurers over the treasuries, Shelemiah the priest, and Zadok the scribe, and of the Levites, Pedaiah: and next to them was Hanan the son of Zaccur, the son of Mattaniah: for they were counted faithful, and their office was to distribute unto their brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a5d902e-4276-4610-b249-32a8b53cdabb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: NEH 13:14
Text: Remember me, O my God, concerning this, and wipe not out my good deeds that I have done for the house of my God, and for the offices thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8dc4649d-edb5-4f32-bc3e-42731ab94c22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 323

Reference: NEH 13:15
Text: In those days saw I in Judah some treading wine presses on the sabbath, and bringing in sheaves, and lading asses; as also wine, grapes, and figs, and all manner of burdens, which they brought into Jerusalem on the sabbath day: and I testified against them in the day wherein they sold victuals.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6d772a9-c26d-44b3-bb14-2ccf3e16a1ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: NEH 13:16
Text: There dwelt men of Tyre also therein, which brought fish, and all manner of ware, and sold on the sabbath unto the children of Judah, and in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fc8ff66-7475-4074-b026-09bc1ebf01d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: NEH 13:17
Text: Then I contended with the nobles of Judah, and said unto them, What evil thing is this that ye do, and profane the sabbath day?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d47e433-bba7-4585-930a-a3baddfd68ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: NEH 13:18
Text: Did not your fathers thus, and did not our God bring all this evil upon us, and upon this city? yet ye bring more wrath upon Israel by profaning the sabbath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3560a8c6-0dcd-4e5e-b535-d84bb8376f46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 334

Reference: NEH 13:19
Text: And it came to pass, that when the gates of Jerusalem began to be dark before the sabbath, I commanded that the gates should be shut, and charged that they should not be opened till after the sabbath: and some of my servants set I at the gates, that there should no burden be brought in on the sabbath day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c10ecb72-9b77-4db3-b527-c79dd2347d5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: NEH 13:20
Text: So the merchants and sellers of all kind of ware lodged without Jerusalem once or twice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86623532-615c-442e-ac54-f28a72f45069>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: NEH 13:21
Text: Then I testified against them, and said unto them, Why lodge ye about the wall? if ye do so again, I will lay hands on you. From that time forth came they no more on the sabbath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57f2006f-ab1d-4dfa-8b2a-c0ecce4327ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 266

Reference: NEH 13:22
Text: And I commanded the Levites that they should cleanse themselves, and that they should come and keep the gates, to sanctify the sabbath day. Remember me, O my God, concerning this also, and spare me according to the greatness of thy mercy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79646879-a337-4192-84e7-a0c73ae8f70f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: NEH 13:23
Text: In those days also saw I Jews that had married wives of Ashdod, of Ammon, and of Moab:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3de4c39-2ef5-4e96-a478-c69a9b202678>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: NEH 13:24
Text: And their children spake half in the speech of Ashdod, and could not speak in the Jews’ language, but according to the language of each people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4313b23a-a6ac-4fd5-a805-31d13af32411>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: NEH 13:25
Text: And I contended with them, and cursed them, and smote certain of them, and plucked off their hair, and made them swear by God, saying, Ye shall not give your daughters unto their sons, nor take their daughters unto your sons, or for yourselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ee44dbc-7288-4016-a964-7dba7c069dd5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: NEH 13:26
Text: Did not Solomon king of Israel sin by these things? yet among many nations was there no king like him, who was beloved of his God, and God made him king over all Israel: nevertheless even him did outlandish women cause to sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:620e6243-4132-44c2-a2ac-0a7fd9f0640e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: NEH 13:27
Text: Shall we then hearken unto you to do all this great evil, to transgress against our God in marrying strange wives?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5fbec089-4f3f-458b-8608-46712a192c3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: NEH 13:28
Text: And one of the sons of Joiada, the son of Eliashib the high priest, was son in law to Sanballat the Horonite: therefore I chased him from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79ec47db-4a22-4e53-bb06-38a96e588027>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: NEH 13:29
Text: Remember them, O my God, because they have defiled the priesthood, and the covenant of the priesthood, and of the Levites.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8f52b16-0da6-48f2-b81b-d15fcc674893>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: NEH 13:30
Text: Thus cleansed I them from all strangers, and appointed the wards of the priests and the Levites, every one in his business;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NEH/13/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8005bba8-155d-4193-be5d-b54aa4cee2c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: NEH 13:31
Text: And for the wood offering, at times appointed, and for the firstfruits. Remember me, O my God, for good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd0216e9-f3f2-4171-9452-db60fde90819>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: EST 1:1
Text: Now it came to pass in the days of Ahasuerus, (this is Ahasuerus which reigned, from India even unto Ethiopia, over an hundred and seven and twenty provinces:)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:183a8654-5764-4fa7-b14c-8e4e26188643>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: EST 1:2
Text: That in those days, when the king Ahasuerus sat on the throne of his kingdom, which was in Shushan the palace,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:068ed12f-48b3-41d8-b254-c90bb1f44a31>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: EST 1:3
Text: In the third year of his reign, he made a feast unto all his princes and his servants; the power of Persia and Media, the nobles and princes of the provinces, being before him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6e8110c-098f-4323-aa9b-3482bc59590a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: EST 1:4
Text: When he shewed the riches of his glorious kingdom and the honour of his excellent majesty many days, even an hundred and fourscore days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b1488dd-dbb3-4e7f-b471-634ad0122803>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: EST 1:5
Text: And when these days were expired, the king made a feast unto all the people that were present in Shushan the palace, both unto great and small, seven days, in the court of the garden of the king’s palace;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e881625-a6fa-4847-bc02-65bc3c6c13a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: EST 1:6
Text: Where were white, green, and blue, hangings, fastened with cords of fine linen and purple to silver rings and pillars of marble: the beds were of gold and silver, upon a pavement of red, and blue, and white, and black, marble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e827836-f074-4132-adf2-8f6c91ae8ed8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: EST 1:7
Text: And they gave them drink in vessels of gold, (the vessels being diverse one from another,) and royal wine in abundance, according to the state of the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc8c479c-2a27-41ac-a132-e949f50fe10e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: EST 1:8
Text: And the drinking was according to the law; none did compel: for so the king had appointed to all the officers of his house, that they should do according to every man’s pleasure.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aee8df92-0d9c-4777-9ecf-d70a6796af98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: EST 1:9
Text: Also Vashti the queen made a feast for the women in the royal house which belonged to king Ahasuerus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92e725a1-da1a-484d-85eb-ccf16b57de90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: EST 1:10
Text: On the seventh day, when the heart of the king was merry with wine, he commanded Mehuman, Biztha, Harbona, Bigtha, and Abagtha, Zethar, and Carcas, the seven chamberlains that served in the presence of Ahasuerus the king,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06e3d3a6-59be-4a50-a221-249209037c7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: EST 1:11
Text: To bring Vashti the queen before the king with the crown royal, to shew the people and the princes her beauty: for she was fair to look on.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ed14f21-8fc7-482d-8c40-ef3e4cdfebcd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: EST 1:12
Text: But the queen Vashti refused to come at the king’s commandment by his chamberlains: therefore was the king very wroth, and his anger burned in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc477529-ceb5-4991-ab9f-4f518ace6662>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: EST 1:13
Text: Then the king said to the wise men, which knew the times, (for so was the king’s manner toward all that knew law and judgment:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aaa8932b-8a8b-4948-8284-18ac5620d042>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: EST 1:14
Text: And the next unto him was Carshena, Shethar, Admatha, Tarshish, Meres, Marsena, and Memucan, the seven princes of Persia and Media, which saw the king’s face, and which sat the first in the kingdom;)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c604e23d-f180-42f5-ae7c-3f1fc58dba28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: EST 1:15
Text: What shall we do unto the queen Vashti according to law, because she hath not performed the commandment of the king Ahasuerus by the chamberlains?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27f9710b-fffd-4d05-be5c-dbbf8a16f903>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: EST 1:16
Text: And Memucan answered before the king and the princes, Vashti the queen hath not done wrong to the king only, but also to all the princes, and to all the people that are in all the provinces of the king Ahasuerus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe414c42-ac68-4b7e-9cfd-4dac6054931f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: EST 1:17
Text: For this deed of the queen shall come abroad unto all women, so that they shall despise their husbands in their eyes, when it shall be reported, The king Ahasuerus commanded Vashti the queen to be brought in before him, but she came not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b02ef9c0-f95a-4e34-a5a1-2c2d957eeab1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: EST 1:18
Text: Likewise shall the ladies of Persia and Media say this day unto all the king’s princes, which have heard of the deed of the queen. Thus shall there arise too much contempt and wrath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ee07c72-d067-4e05-9a79-3f1f1d545ccc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 309

Reference: EST 1:19
Text: If it please the king, let there go a royal commandment from him, and let it be written among the laws of the Persians and the Medes, that it be not altered, That Vashti come no more before king Ahasuerus; and let the king give her royal estate unto another that is better than she.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aafc71a7-ee98-4aa3-9e34-522697290fbd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: EST 1:20
Text: And when the king’s decree which he shall make shall be published throughout all his empire, (for it is great,) all the wives shall give to their husbands honour, both to great and small.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/1/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:594e5874-7712-4eeb-9a70-0deaf59db5d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: EST 1:21
Text: And the saying pleased the king and the princes; and the king did according to the word of Memucan:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/1/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b8025e1-8f28-45e2-986f-8b6a72224052>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 300

Reference: EST 1:22
Text: For he sent letters into all the king’s provinces, into every province according to the writing thereof, and to every people after their language, that every man should bear rule in his own house, and that it should be published according to the language of every people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91504436-da0e-4510-bc4d-db9329a1cfc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: EST 2:1
Text: After these things, when the wrath of king Ahasuerus was appeased, he remembered Vashti, and what she had done, and what was decreed against her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e92ad7d5-b891-46fe-838d-7faad3faaeb7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: EST 2:2
Text: Then said the king’s servants that ministered unto him, Let there be fair young virgins sought for the king:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67825c19-992b-4067-bf9a-12b28bbe1aa1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 330

Reference: EST 2:3
Text: And let the king appoint officers in all the provinces of his kingdom, that they may gather together all the fair young virgins unto Shushan the palace, to the house of the women, unto the custody of Hege the king’s chamberlain, keeper of the women; and let their things for purification be given them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6d69d29-817d-435b-850a-422409d7f666>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: EST 2:4
Text: And let the maiden which pleaseth the king be queen instead of Vashti. And the thing pleased the king; and he did so.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec84f2e7-5079-4d7e-a314-081a57a53169>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: EST 2:5
Text: Now in Shushan the palace there was a certain Jew, whose name was Mordecai, the son of Jair, the son of Shimei, the son of Kish, a Benjamite;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf111c63-9408-4463-8ff0-14afd68c44da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: EST 2:6
Text: Who had been carried away from Jerusalem with the captivity which had been carried away with Jeconiah king of Judah, whom Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon had carried away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31eda756-b189-4853-8531-3e0bcad69333>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: EST 2:7
Text: And he brought up Hadassah, that is, Esther, his uncle’s daughter: for she had neither father nor mother, and the maid was fair and beautiful; whom Mordecai, when her father and mother were dead, took for his own daughter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5737937d-63cd-4335-a023-eeb75d66791d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 296

Reference: EST 2:8
Text: So it came to pass, when the king’s commandment and his decree was heard, and when many maidens were gathered together unto Shushan the palace, to the custody of Hegai, that Esther was brought also unto the king’s house, to the custody of Hegai, keeper of the women.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b75701b-5b43-4f2e-9d68-2410b352f3e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 339

Reference: EST 2:9
Text: And the maiden pleased him, and she obtained kindness of him; and he speedily gave her her things for purification, with such things as belonged to her, and seven maidens, which were meet to be given her, out of the king’s house: and he preferred her and her maids unto the best place of the house of the women.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7fa81dc-05ff-471d-be65-53aecbef4df1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: EST 2:10
Text: Esther had not shewed her people nor her kindred: for Mordecai had charged her that she should not shew it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e0dd371-f51a-4e7f-b2d5-de9bcc1186fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: EST 2:11
Text: And Mordecai walked every day before the court of the women’s house, to know how Esther did, and what should become of her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4bb2bba-dc23-4215-9ce6-c3e33b7b704a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 355

Reference: EST 2:12
Text: Now when every maid’s turn was come to go in to king Ahasuerus, after that she had been twelve months, according to the manner of the women, (for so were the days of their purifications accomplished, to wit, six months with oil of myrrh, and six months with sweet odours, and with other things for the purifying of the women;)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0208f9ab-597b-4ddc-8952-54cbf7652b74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: EST 2:13
Text: Then thus came every maiden unto the king; whatsoever she desired was given her to go with her out of the house of the women unto the king’s house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d944f5a3-9cd9-435d-9b5d-4a52c905dcf0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 303

Reference: EST 2:14
Text: In the evening she went, and on the morrow she returned into the second house of the women, to the custody of Shaashgaz, the king’s chamberlain, which kept the concubines: she came in unto the king no more, except the king delighted in her, and that she were called by name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41236f1a-9916-46c4-9e11-ebe664feeb3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 343

Reference: EST 2:15
Text: Now when the turn of Esther, the daughter of Abihail the uncle of Mordecai, who had taken her for his daughter, was come to go in unto the king, she required nothing but what Hegai the king’s chamberlain, the keeper of the women, appointed. And Esther obtained favour in the sight of all them that looked upon her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ecd19856-b001-4d62-a723-4a17b5362fa9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: EST 2:16
Text: So Esther was taken unto king Ahasuerus into his house royal in the tenth month, which is the month Tebeth, in the seventh year of his reign.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cdca1514-d6d5-4634-ab9c-3cb4f1c7abb8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: EST 2:17
Text: And the king loved Esther above all the women, and she obtained grace and favour in his sight more than all the virgins; so that he set the royal crown upon her head, and made her queen instead of Vashti.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1eef6d81-8c94-4a89-8db7-c7e425fbc416>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: EST 2:18
Text: Then the king made a great feast unto all his princes and his servants, even Esther’s feast; and he made a release to the provinces, and gave gifts, according to the state of the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5104d793-a1dc-4d20-a947-5aa911a5d18e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: EST 2:19
Text: And when the virgins were gathered together the second time, then Mordecai sat in the king’s gate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84907a11-56ae-4dae-b81b-e773f1f008be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: EST 2:20
Text: Esther had not yet shewed her kindred nor her people; as Mordecai had charged her: for Esther did the commandment of Mordecai, like as when she was brought up with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf238f37-26de-43cb-b3ba-0d474921bbb1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: EST 2:21
Text: In those days, while Mordecai sat in the king’s gate, two of the king’s chamberlains, Bigthan and Teresh, of those which kept the door, were wroth, and sought to lay hands on the king Ahasuerus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4904c414-a2ac-422f-9387-abf9332e210e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EST 2:22
Text: And the thing was known to Mordecai, who told it unto Esther the queen; and Esther certified the king thereof in Mordecai’s name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/2/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c92487a-5d9e-43f8-bedc-44792711fdb6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: EST 2:23
Text: And when inquisition was made of the matter, it was found out; therefore they were both hanged on a tree: and it was written in the book of the chronicles before the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd5341b3-b3a8-4eff-8c87-2d1f849f55f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: EST 3:1
Text: After these things did king Ahasuerus promote Haman the son of Hammedatha the Agagite, and advanced him, and set his seat above all the princes that were with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:998a1c5c-db58-4e67-95d0-9ee5237ca74e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: EST 3:2
Text: And all the king’s servants, that were in the king’s gate, bowed, and reverenced Haman: for the king had so commanded concerning him. But Mordecai bowed not, nor did him reverence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acc4c598-3c34-4f41-b2f1-93253cb904d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: EST 3:3
Text: Then the king’s servants, which were in the king’s gate, said unto Mordecai, Why transgressest thou the king’s commandment?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f115c01f-1c0e-4c35-a307-213385515e76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: EST 3:4
Text: Now it came to pass, when they spake daily unto him, and he hearkened not unto them, that they told Haman, to see whether Mordecai’s matters would stand: for he had told them that he was a Jew.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e814406b-365c-4d16-ba94-a33cd6587936>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: EST 3:5
Text: And when Haman saw that Mordecai bowed not, nor did him reverence, then was Haman full of wrath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e311ffd1-09c2-40ce-9bd6-f3ed74018079>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: EST 3:6
Text: And he thought scorn to lay hands on Mordecai alone; for they had shewed him the people of Mordecai: wherefore Haman sought to destroy all the Jews that were throughout the whole kingdom of Ahasuerus, even the people of Mordecai.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:042c66bf-5359-4ae7-9513-11c9b20ea18d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: EST 3:7
Text: In the first month, that is, the month Nisan, in the twelfth year of king Ahasuerus, they cast Pur, that is, the lot, before Haman from day to day, and from month to month, to the twelfth month, that is, the month Adar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17f7b028-2bff-4b81-aaba-21e162809d9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 313

Reference: EST 3:8
Text: And Haman said unto king Ahasuerus, There is a certain people scattered abroad and dispersed among the people in all the provinces of thy kingdom; and their laws are diverse from all people; neither keep they the king’s laws: therefore it is not for the king’s profit to suffer them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f35d56d9-732f-4900-80f4-d19cecc118a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: EST 3:9
Text: If it please the king, let it be written that they may be destroyed: and I will pay ten thousand talents of silver to the hands of those that have the charge of the business, to bring it into the king’s treasuries.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c9fc8f0-fbe9-4277-b4b9-7b931a54c53a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: EST 3:10
Text: And the king took his ring from his hand, and gave it unto Haman the son of Hammedatha the Agagite, the Jews’ enemy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24db084a-d75e-40dc-9801-d6cd65b7ba76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: EST 3:11
Text: And the king said unto Haman, The silver is given to thee, the people also, to do with them as it seemeth good to thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47d01189-299d-4f82-9340-f0d3cc624ad4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 462

Reference: EST 3:12
Text: Then were the king’s scribes called on the thirteenth day of the first month, and there was written according to all that Haman had commanded unto the king’s lieutenants, and to the governors that were over every province, and to the rulers of every people of every province according to the writing thereof, and to every people after their language; in the name of king Ahasuerus was it written, and sealed with the king’s ring.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19ba079b-1b17-45ba-84ab-dc23a6009944>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 326

Reference: EST 3:13
Text: And the letters were sent by posts into all the king’s provinces, to destroy, to kill, and to cause to perish, all Jews, both young and old, little children and women, in one day, even upon the thirteenth day of the twelfth month, which is the month Adar, and to take the spoil of them for a prey.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a857b4d-ecf6-4763-835c-7962758058b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: EST 3:14
Text: The copy of the writing for a commandment to be given in every province was published unto all people, that they should be ready against that day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79810dc4-179a-4e88-8f02-b9cd754d897d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: EST 3:15
Text: The posts went out, being hastened by the king’s commandment, and the decree was given in Shushan the palace. And the king and Haman sat down to drink; but the city Shushan was perplexed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a293f193-1618-454f-867e-57079478ccff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: EST 4:1
Text: When Mordecai perceived all that was done, Mordecai rent his clothes, and put on sackcloth with ashes, and went out into the midst of the city, and cried with a loud and a bitter cry;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:748e41d7-f10f-41c4-bcee-20e62bd6fae9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: EST 4:2
Text: And came even before the king’s gate: for none might enter into the king’s gate clothed with sackcloth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e8a8921-d798-4a81-a41f-10f68f72dabd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: EST 4:3
Text: And in every province, whithersoever the king’s commandment and his decree came, there was great mourning among the Jews, and fasting, and weeping, and wailing; and many lay in sackcloth and ashes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c31ac0af-a3b8-4739-89da-cdbe9a7ee164>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: EST 4:4
Text: So Esther’s maids and her chamberlains came and told it her. Then was the queen exceedingly grieved; and she sent raiment to clothe Mordecai, and to take away his sackcloth from him: but he received it not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ed35b40-23c7-4a71-acef-02278b506460>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: EST 4:5
Text: Then called Esther for Hatach, one of the king’s chamberlains, whom he had appointed to attend upon her, and gave him a commandment to Mordecai, to know what it was, and why it was.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07d5327e-6eb0-42f5-b540-386617e07161>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: EST 4:6
Text: So Hatach went forth to Mordecai unto the street of the city, which was before the king’s gate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3365c769-0940-4c9b-9d17-51811e50d229>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: EST 4:7
Text: And Mordecai told him of all that had happened unto him, and of the sum of the money that Haman had promised to pay to the king’s treasuries for the Jews, to destroy them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b9f8cbd-b6cb-46ee-8d80-2cc5f20e8ee4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 308

Reference: EST 4:8
Text: Also he gave him the copy of the writing of the decree that was given at Shushan to destroy them, to shew it unto Esther, and to declare it unto her, and to charge her that she should go in unto the king, to make supplication unto him, and to make request before him for her people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af2c51c4-0554-454f-ab07-645595fca9a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: EST 4:9
Text: And Hatach came and told Esther the words of Mordecai.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8391c599-8368-457e-b892-e49701f87e17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: EST 4:10
Text: Again Esther spake unto Hatach, and gave him commandment unto Mordecai;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9edeb3b4-a8a9-443a-8f6e-54cef416de4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 406

Reference: EST 4:11
Text: All the king’s servants, and the people of the king’s provinces, do know, that whosoever, whether man or woman, shall come unto the king into the inner court, who is not called, there is one law of his to put him to death, except such to whom the king shall hold out the golden sceptre, that he may live: but I have not been called to come in unto the king these thirty days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6eede0a1-1336-46dd-b549-590bb9e3394e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 70

Reference: EST 4:12
Text: And they told to Mordecai Esther’s words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8480f1c-0dde-4d87-bb3c-1d4b01cb81d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: EST 4:13
Text: Then Mordecai commanded to answer Esther, Think not with thyself that thou shalt escape in the king’s house, more than all the Jews.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96640941-25e4-4be8-8050-60a233914592>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 296

Reference: EST 4:14
Text: For if thou altogether holdest thy peace at this time, then shall there enlargement and deliverance arise to the Jews from another place; but thou and thy father’s house shall be destroyed: and who knoweth whether thou art come to the kingdom for such a time as this?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf034413-05d3-4f4b-9eab-7e10c1ad929b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: EST 4:15
Text: Then Esther bade them return Mordecai this answer,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2de16407-6430-42bd-baea-428aa12390cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 299

Reference: EST 4:16
Text: Go, gather together all the Jews that are present in Shushan, and fast ye for me, and neither eat nor drink three days, night or day: I also and my maidens will fast likewise; and so will I go in unto the king, which is not according to the law: and if I perish, I perish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ead7dd04-53bb-441a-ac9e-56b3198f2fdc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: EST 4:17
Text: So Mordecai went his way, and did according to all that Esther had commanded him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:473204af-69c9-47f9-a8fc-fb7967719872>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 281

Reference: EST 5:1
Text: Now it came to pass on the third day, that Esther put on her royal apparel, and stood in the inner court of the king’s house, over against the king’s house: and the king sat upon his royal throne in the royal house, over against the gate of the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e616b00d-5b30-44b1-aefa-55e4561995e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: EST 5:2
Text: And it was so, when the king saw Esther the queen standing in the court, that she obtained favour in his sight: and the king held out to Esther the golden sceptre that was in his hand. So Esther drew near, and touched the top of the sceptre.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:391369ce-009a-4cce-be96-d1aecf8bb754>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: EST 5:3
Text: Then said the king unto her, What wilt thou, queen Esther? and what is thy request? it shall be even given thee to the half of the kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d25e4c1a-2989-453a-8a82-fd8930de3479>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: EST 5:4
Text: And Esther answered, If it seem good unto the king, let the king and Haman come this day unto the banquet that I have prepared for him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05de8e15-e234-4af0-8b61-3cc6d320dfb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: EST 5:5
Text: Then the king said, Cause Haman to make haste, that he may do as Esther hath said. So the king and Haman came to the banquet that Esther had prepared.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c31485ba-3e82-4665-8b10-43f943cc57fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: EST 5:6
Text: And the king said unto Esther at the banquet of wine, What is thy petition? and it shall be granted thee: and what is thy request? even to the half of the kingdom it shall be performed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a2d49f0-f82c-45f6-9105-f2543a7d862a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: EST 5:7
Text: Then answered Esther, and said, My petition and my request is;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c512b25-18af-4031-99dc-12fd80b6994f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: EST 5:8
Text: If I have found favour in the sight of the king, and if it please the king to grant my petition, and to perform my request, let the king and Haman come to the banquet that I shall prepare for them, and I will do to morrow as the king hath said.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68dfeef2-ab09-4b77-a434-24fb005c728d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: EST 5:9
Text: Then went Haman forth that day joyful and with a glad heart: but when Haman saw Mordecai in the king’s gate, that he stood not up, nor moved for him, he was full of indignation against Mordecai.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c8de031-6da9-4491-8775-30930d2c9fc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: EST 5:10
Text: Nevertheless Haman refrained himself: and when he came home, he sent and called for his friends, and Zeresh his wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9540bc80-f158-4c82-bd67-850e807d6722>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: EST 5:11
Text: And Haman told them of the glory of his riches, and the multitude of his children, and all the things wherein the king had promoted him, and how he had advanced him above the princes and servants of the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9426172-1a5f-4cc5-9634-7e973d8c5038>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: EST 5:12
Text: Haman said moreover, Yea, Esther the queen did let no man come in with the king unto the banquet that she had prepared but myself; and to morrow am I invited unto her also with the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40d29043-468a-493e-9357-6be80812221a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: EST 5:13
Text: Yet all this availeth me nothing, so long as I see Mordecai the Jew sitting at the king’s gate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4079fa41-df14-4ad0-b2f7-712b1a11033f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 325

Reference: EST 5:14
Text: Then said Zeresh his wife and all his friends unto him, Let a gallows be made of fifty cubits high, and to morrow speak thou unto the king that Mordecai may be hanged thereon: then go thou in merrily with the king unto the banquet. And the thing pleased Haman; and he caused the gallows to be made.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d8dc564-7331-4823-b9d1-b2c36ab3e995>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: EST 6:1
Text: On that night could not the king sleep, and he commanded to bring the book of records of the chronicles; and they were read before the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:957c5c32-1e85-4605-b8e6-14ed4000831d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: EST 6:2
Text: And it was found written, that Mordecai had told of Bigthana and Teresh, two of the king’s chamberlains, the keepers of the door, who sought to lay hand on the king Ahasuerus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6befc63-2f07-4dbc-8449-c0aa9079dda6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: EST 6:3
Text: And the king said, What honour and dignity hath been done to Mordecai for this? Then said the king’s servants that ministered unto him, There is nothing done for him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4e55fb2-fdac-4c2f-bfc4-1b63a5f2f9d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: EST 6:4
Text: And the king said, Who is in the court? Now Haman was come into the outward court of the king’s house, to speak unto the king to hang Mordecai on the gallows that he had prepared for him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c566408-4cb8-412b-9651-6271de60a882>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: EST 6:5
Text: And the king’s servants said unto him, Behold, Haman standeth in the court. And the king said, Let him come in.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74dd0c26-03bc-4b75-ab4a-d0320fd1748b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: EST 6:6
Text: So Haman came in. And the king said unto him, What shall be done unto the man whom the king delighteth to honour? Now Haman thought in his heart, To whom would the king delight to do honour more than to myself?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de36d2fc-8602-4453-bd95-b73ddf3c3ed3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: EST 6:7
Text: And Haman answered the king, For the man whom the king delighteth to honour,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c2192fd-8b29-4825-9031-5ae30e3eaf74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: EST 6:8
Text: Let the royal apparel be brought which the king useth to wear, and the horse that the king rideth upon, and the crown royal which is set upon his head:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:073efc26-7dda-4f5b-888c-ee8e04a3109c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 348

Reference: EST 6:9
Text: And let this apparel and horse be delivered to the hand of one of the king’s most noble princes, that they may array the man withal whom the king delighteth to honour, and bring him on horseback through the street of the city, and proclaim before him, Thus shall it be done to the man whom the king delighteth to honour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61adce76-6f28-4102-a8da-e298967dcb75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: EST 6:10
Text: Then the king said to Haman, Make haste, and take the apparel and the horse, as thou hast said, and do even so to Mordecai the Jew, that sitteth at the king’s gate: let nothing fail of all that thou hast spoken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:809ffb69-8abc-47d2-8f25-1ac7456d659f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: EST 6:11
Text: Then took Haman the apparel and the horse, and arrayed Mordecai, and brought him on horseback through the street of the city, and proclaimed before him, Thus shall it be done unto the man whom the king delighteth to honour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46cf46e0-6960-481e-bc9c-a33798be1e90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: EST 6:12
Text: And Mordecai came again to the king’s gate. But Haman hasted to his house mourning, and having his head covered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1150b35d-fc19-4042-8057-655986ef5e46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 312

Reference: EST 6:13
Text: And Haman told Zeresh his wife and all his friends every thing that had befallen him. Then said his wise men and Zeresh his wife unto him, If Mordecai be of the seed of the Jews, before whom thou hast begun to fall, thou shalt not prevail against him, but shalt surely fall before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/6/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9990a706-0868-4de8-8b08-cbf04733802b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: EST 6:14
Text: And while they were yet talking with him, came the king’s chamberlains, and hasted to bring Haman unto the banquet that Esther had prepared.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:383945a9-8ffb-48c3-bc96-a7fd87f5761f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: EST 7:1
Text: So the king and Haman came to banquet with Esther the queen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29a83b1e-5374-4766-a818-35a33539622e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: EST 7:2
Text: And the king said again unto Esther on the second day at the banquet of wine, What is thy petition, queen Esther? and it shall be granted thee: and what is thy request? and it shall be performed, even to the half of the kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84754323-4b4a-402f-b576-cf3f38310601>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: EST 7:3
Text: Then Esther the queen answered and said, If I have found favour in thy sight, O king, and if it please the king, let my life be given me at my petition, and my people at my request:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bea2794e-89da-4ef9-bde0-0f8d5bb46f70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: EST 7:4
Text: For we are sold, I and my people, to be destroyed, to be slain, and to perish. But if we had been sold for bondmen and bondwomen, I had held my tongue, although the enemy could not countervail the king’s damage.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e71adc4a-b7e4-4404-adc6-7b846a666276>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EST 7:5
Text: Then the king Ahasuerus answered and said unto Esther the queen, Who is he, and where is he, that durst presume in his heart to do so?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:639e9430-b6fd-44c3-a13c-becf26667c88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: EST 7:6
Text: And Esther said, The adversary and enemy is this wicked Haman. Then Haman was afraid before the king and the queen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b7479fc-7274-4238-9b09-2b09bb8d46c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: EST 7:7
Text: And the king arising from the banquet of wine in his wrath went into the palace garden: and Haman stood up to make request for his life to Esther the queen; for he saw that there was evil determined against him by the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80a8e7ad-1af6-4f4c-9215-06c2cc97c8d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 312

Reference: EST 7:8
Text: Then the king returned out of the palace garden into the place of the banquet of wine; and Haman was fallen upon the bed whereon Esther was. Then said the king, Will he force the queen also before me in the house? As the word went out of the king’s mouth, they covered Haman’s face.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98aeb0b2-7daa-48dc-8591-e12e50b3499c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: EST 7:9
Text: And Harbonah, one of the chamberlains, said before the king, Behold also, the gallows fifty cubits high, which Haman had made for Mordecai, who had spoken good for the king, standeth in the house of Haman. Then the king said, Hang him thereon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1c87eb0-2a69-4611-9600-932af70f58b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: EST 7:10
Text: So they hanged Haman on the gallows that he had prepared for Mordecai. Then was the king’s wrath pacified.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/8/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8749192d-7839-46f9-8317-fad5b60cad35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: EST 8:1
Text: On that day did the king Ahasuerus give the house of Haman the Jews’ enemy unto Esther the queen. And Mordecai came before the king; for Esther had told what he was unto her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/8/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06d7ff1c-0999-4a2c-81ae-49cc05833aba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: EST 8:2
Text: And the king took off his ring, which he had taken from Haman, and gave it unto Mordecai. And Esther set Mordecai over the house of Haman.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/8/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a9296e9-4bc8-4785-aadf-21eb0710951f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: EST 8:3
Text: And Esther spake yet again before the king, and fell down at his feet, and besought him with tears to put away the mischief of Haman the Agagite, and his device that he had devised against the Jews.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/8/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60895362-3faa-498b-8c7f-04d5c53cbb03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: EST 8:4
Text: Then the king held out the golden sceptre toward Esther. So Esther arose, and stood before the king,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/8/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:329c609b-8acd-4544-b311-294f4ca6838f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 335

Reference: EST 8:5
Text: And said, If it please the king, and if I have favour in his sight, and the thing seem right before the king, and I be pleasing in his eyes, let it be written to reverse the letters devised by Haman the son of Hammedatha the Agagite, which he wrote to destroy the Jews which are in all the king’s provinces:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/8/6
