WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38b42149-14ca-4540-8832-986afeffbcee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: EST 8:6
Text: For how can I endure to see the evil that shall come unto my people? or how can I endure to see the destruction of my kindred?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/8/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8ff5a06-7b2e-4626-9500-8262c5c2d659>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: EST 8:7
Text: Then the king Ahasuerus said unto Esther the queen and to Mordecai the Jew, Behold, I have given Esther the house of Haman, and him they have hanged upon the gallows, because he laid his hand upon the Jews.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/8/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1db08767-921f-4d05-b229-9720e9bfe285>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: EST 8:8
Text: Write ye also for the Jews, as it liketh you, in the king’s name, and seal it with the king’s ring: for the writing which is written in the king’s name, and sealed with the king’s ring, may no man reverse.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/8/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4442c464-334d-41ef-a151-fb8126e395c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 556

Reference: EST 8:9
Text: Then were the king’s scribes called at that time in the third month, that is, the month Sivan, on the three and twentieth day thereof; and it was written according to all that Mordecai commanded unto the Jews, and to the lieutenants, and the deputies and rulers of the provinces which are from India unto Ethiopia, an hundred twenty and seven provinces, unto every province according to the writing thereof, and unto every people after their language, and to the Jews according to their writing, and according to their language.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/8/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b1882db-e16c-4c2a-8537-3dcf124fc3e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: EST 8:10
Text: And he wrote in the king Ahasuerus’ name, and sealed it with the king’s ring, and sent letters by posts on horseback, and riders on mules, camels, and young dromedaries:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/8/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffb0c294-1064-463e-ade6-47c14c7a9268>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 325

Reference: EST 8:11
Text: Wherein the king granted the Jews which were in every city to gather themselves together, and to stand for their life, to destroy, to slay and to cause to perish, all the power of the people and province that would assault them, both little ones and women, and to take the spoil of them for a prey,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/8/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b0b5bad-df84-435b-a7c8-1132a690eac6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EST 8:12
Text: Upon one day in all the provinces of king Ahasuerus, namely, upon the thirteenth day of the twelfth month, which is the month Adar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/8/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b28a0e05-3587-4f9c-9430-6160e57062fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: EST 8:13
Text: The copy of the writing for a commandment to be given in every province was published unto all people, and that the Jews should be ready against that day to avenge themselves on their enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/8/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7df4e4a-1da6-425f-9d29-e589b1f4a0ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: EST 8:14
Text: So the posts that rode upon mules and camels went out, being hastened and pressed on by the king’s commandment. And the decree was given at Shushan the palace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/8/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c87bc02e-6727-4d42-a76d-bf632a7c9031>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: EST 8:15
Text: And Mordecai went out from the presence of the king in royal apparel of blue and white, and with a great crown of gold, and with a garment of fine linen and purple: and the city of Shushan rejoiced and was glad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/8/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1e66985-3e72-41df-a96d-efaa59be5e97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: EST 8:16
Text: The Jews had light, and gladness, and joy, and honour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/8/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9532d497-2c1a-44cf-b46b-d757467dc6c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: EST 8:17
Text: And in every province, and in every city, whithersoever the king’s commandment and his decree came, the Jews had joy and gladness, a feast and a good day. And many of the people of the land became Jews; for the fear of the Jews fell upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ace9ec64-bdb6-4cb3-bd46-a790c3d142ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 351

Reference: EST 9:1
Text: Now in the twelfth month, that is, the month Adar, on the thirteenth day of the same, when the king’s commandment and his decree drew near to be put in execution, in the day that the enemies of the Jews hoped to have power over them, (though it was turned to the contrary, that the Jews had rule over them that hated them;)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:076edccb-72b5-422f-9935-54caa58c4615>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: EST 9:2
Text: The Jews gathered themselves together in their cities throughout all the provinces of the king Ahasuerus, to lay hand on such as sought their hurt: and no man could withstand them; for the fear of them fell upon all people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abbdd0f9-d5a2-48ea-9434-07e78d305f48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: EST 9:3
Text: And all the rulers of the provinces, and the lieutenants, and the deputies, and officers of the king, helped the Jews; because the fear of Mordecai fell upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc6885e9-6866-43d6-9496-bf7444d32322>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: EST 9:4
Text: For Mordecai was great in the king’s house, and his fame went out throughout all the provinces: for this man Mordecai waxed greater and greater.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96076d8d-c4d4-413c-8660-fb60e1521a23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: EST 9:5
Text: Thus the Jews smote all their enemies with the stroke of the sword, and slaughter, and destruction, and did what they would unto those that hated them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60add6cc-7c3b-466c-800d-8c36f3eb9fbf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: EST 9:6
Text: And in Shushan the palace the Jews slew and destroyed five hundred men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
