Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: EST 9:10
Text: The ten sons of Haman the son of Hammedatha, the enemy of the Jews, slew they; but on the spoil laid they not their hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5dd300d1-72b0-4910-acb7-7f8db172637d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: EST 9:11
Text: On that day the number of those that were slain in Shushan the palace was brought before the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc46145e-5646-4903-9796-e3cd88ddbd69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 337

Reference: EST 9:12
Text: And the king said unto Esther the queen, The Jews have slain and destroyed five hundred men in Shushan the palace, and the ten sons of Haman; what have they done in the rest of the king’s provinces? now what is thy petition? and it shall be granted thee: or what is thy request further? and it shall be done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6679863-137e-4827-b53e-976e5335b611>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: EST 9:13
Text: Then said Esther, If it please the king, let it be granted to the Jews which are in Shushan to do to morrow also according unto this day’s decree, and let Haman’s ten sons be hanged upon the gallows.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf7fac83-2650-4cbf-884d-dbd474d54404>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: EST 9:14
Text: And the king commanded it so to be done: and the decree was given at Shushan; and they hanged Haman’s ten sons.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:784ceeea-8b90-4a67-989b-ff46dd25f896>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: EST 9:15
Text: For the Jews that were in Shushan gathered themselves together on the fourteenth day also of the month Adar, and slew three hundred men at Shushan; but on the prey they laid not their hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f9c910e-6cd8-483b-a8d3-3db73a31261a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: EST 9:16
Text: But the other Jews that were in the king’s provinces gathered themselves together, and stood for their lives, and had rest from their enemies, and slew of their foes seventy and five thousand, but they laid not their hands on the prey,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6db2ea7-6812-4bd6-912e-51be673d0f2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: EST 9:17
Text: On the thirteenth day of the month Adar; and on the fourteenth day of the same rested they, and made it a day of feasting and gladness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46bd9196-ab80-4ac1-a98e-15b4e6188ba5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: EST 9:18
Text: But the Jews that were at Shushan assembled together on the thirteenth day thereof, and on the fourteenth thereof; and on the fifteenth day of the same they rested, and made it a day of feasting and gladness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5154233a-2766-4efb-9157-aa052a22d7cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: EST 9:19
Text: Therefore the Jews of the villages, that dwelt in the unwalled towns, made the fourteenth day of the month Adar a day of gladness and feasting, and a good day, and of sending portions one to another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42faceaf-d6fc-41a3-805a-67564801cd6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: EST 9:20
Text: And Mordecai wrote these things, and sent letters unto all the Jews that were in all the provinces of the king Ahasuerus, both nigh and far,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1811852c-919b-45f6-82f7-2926617ccecb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EST 9:21
Text: To stablish this among them, that they should keep the fourteenth day of the month Adar, and the fifteenth day of the same, yearly,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4804ace3-ca8c-410e-99e5-fbc6a19cd0b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 294

Reference: EST 9:22
Text: As the days wherein the Jews rested from their enemies, and the month which was turned unto them from sorrow to joy, and from mourning into a good day: that they should make them days of feasting and joy, and of sending portions one to another, and gifts to the poor.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19d8820f-fb5b-4f9b-bf81-36f7ed961038>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: EST 9:23
Text: And the Jews undertook to do as they had begun, and as Mordecai had written unto them;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d0c72f5-201c-4a8d-8a3b-2cb064aab8c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: EST 9:24
Text: Because Haman the son of Hammedatha, the Agagite, the enemy of all the Jews, had devised against the Jews to destroy them, and had cast Pur, that is, the lot, to consume them, and to destroy them;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90d133a7-703f-4565-adce-accc5fb5a63c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: EST 9:25
Text: But when Esther came before the king, he commanded by letters that his wicked device, which he devised against the Jews, should return upon his own head, and that he and his sons should be hanged on the gallows.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8971656e-5c50-4f40-889a-1cbd6f20fe8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: EST 9:26
Text: Wherefore they called these days Purim after the name of Pur. Therefore for all the words of this letter, and of that which they had seen concerning this matter, and which had come unto them,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce0d8c6b-832a-497c-8a63-8fb10d3253a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: EST 9:27
Text: The Jews ordained, and took upon them, and upon their seed, and upon all such as joined themselves unto them, so as it should not fail, that they would keep these two days according to their writing, and according to their appointed time every year;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db08e204-ca6c-400a-b65f-b18438527ac7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 266

Reference: EST 9:28
Text: And that these days should be remembered and kept throughout every generation, every family, every province, and every city; and that these days of Purim should not fail from among the Jews, nor the memorial of them perish from their seed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d387702e-5d52-4d21-b8ed-f86c3aca1e85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: EST 9:29
Text: Then Esther the queen, the daughter of Abihail, and Mordecai the Jew, wrote with all authority, to confirm this second letter of Purim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7567bcef-ea78-4d77-aeaa-e2f63c6812e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: EST 9:30
Text: And he sent the letters unto all the Jews, to the hundred twenty and seven provinces of the kingdom of Ahasuerus, with words of peace and truth,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6843f73-d443-4e43-989b-d27ef208fd38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: EST 9:31
Text: To confirm these days of Purim in their times appointed, according as Mordecai the Jew and Esther the queen had enjoined them, and as they had decreed for themselves and for their seed, the matters of the fastings and their cry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/9/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1d880df-3ca9-452d-bce5-fabcb237c80c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: EST 9:32
Text: And the decree of Esther confirmed these matters of Purim; and it was written in the book.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EST/10/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
