Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: JOB 39:1
Text: Knowest thou the time when the wild goats of the rock bring forth? or canst thou mark when the hinds do calve?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06bd2a74-57be-47cd-9918-e0ce9e93245a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: JOB 39:2
Text: Canst thou number the months that they fulfil? or knowest thou the time when they bring forth?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14396fe0-ca1d-4df3-b188-133846b3ca8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: JOB 39:3
Text: They bow themselves, they bring forth their young ones, they cast out their sorrows.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:505c1e09-9487-4282-b827-bd983b080458>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: JOB 39:4
Text: Their young ones are in good liking, they grow up with corn; they go forth, and return not unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c6624e5-8106-4fce-a9f4-3b0a184558fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: JOB 39:5
Text: Who hath sent out the wild ass free? or who hath loosed the bands of the wild ass?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a423dff-f593-4be8-84f6-d07ea5ffac97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: JOB 39:6
Text: Whose house I have made the wilderness, and the barren land his dwellings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9affb3e3-d454-4d3d-9e4b-cabccc738df2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: JOB 39:7
Text: He scorneth the multitude of the city, neither regardeth he the crying of the driver.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63a99c87-616d-443f-b21e-99fc51afbde1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: JOB 39:8
Text: The range of the mountains is his pasture, and he searcheth after every green thing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8acf079-01f7-475e-b28a-07807447987e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: JOB 39:9
Text: Will the unicorn be willing to serve thee, or abide by thy crib?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80efbb02-c61c-4557-b703-5b6ee0913fc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: JOB 39:10
Text: Canst thou bind the unicorn with his band in the furrow? or will he harrow the valleys after thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d47ed69e-f2c7-4c12-a7c3-a542e179c222>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: JOB 39:11
Text: Wilt thou trust him, because his strength is great? or wilt thou leave thy labour to him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21140946-5fa7-4311-8d23-f036777367a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: JOB 39:12
Text: Wilt thou believe him, that he will bring home thy seed, and gather it into thy barn?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8875b7a-801b-4739-b603-42c47ff78846>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: JOB 39:13
Text: Gavest thou the goodly wings unto the peacocks? or wings and feathers unto the ostrich?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70074ebb-568b-4d47-a33f-ff54056bec0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: JOB 39:14
Text: Which leaveth her eggs in the earth, and warmeth them in dust,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b45ecb1e-678c-4c1f-87fc-f7493b97cd75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: JOB 39:15
Text: And forgetteth that the foot may crush them, or that the wild beast may break them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2deadfc-1220-4214-adc7-7a5d5c4493b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: JOB 39:16
Text: She is hardened against her young ones, as though they were not hers: her labour is in vain without fear;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b411564-3d07-441e-8504-416356738592>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: JOB 39:17
Text: Because God hath deprived her of wisdom, neither hath he imparted to her understanding.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42ec8fa8-7d91-4bca-a026-d9ae5173ff51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: JOB 39:18
Text: What time she lifteth up herself on high, she scorneth the horse and his rider.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06c13a0f-b4d2-4e41-afaf-8c352896fbac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: JOB 39:19
Text: Hast thou given the horse strength? hast thou clothed his neck with thunder?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc0dc3ed-6f4f-42d5-b519-29160a4013e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: JOB 39:20
Text: Canst thou make him afraid as a grasshopper? the glory of his nostrils is terrible.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ae34f09-64ba-4fa3-b75e-c8d0d445c7f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: JOB 39:21
Text: He paweth in the valley, and rejoiceth in his strength: he goeth on to meet the armed men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c75fecaf-fb9b-41cc-9a41-77e7985c7109>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: JOB 39:22
Text: He mocketh at fear, and is not affrighted; neither turneth he back from the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cb41750-6fcb-4709-bd64-6b7d2734646b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: JOB 39:23
Text: The quiver rattleth against him, the glittering spear and the shield.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a331ca35-9205-4028-8f4a-88a6948a7d65>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: JOB 39:24
Text: He swalloweth the ground with fierceness and rage: neither believeth he that it is the sound of the trumpet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38bb1812-9f44-4715-b26f-12d6bff52239>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: JOB 39:25
Text: He saith among the trumpets, Ha, ha; and he smelleth the battle afar off, the thunder of the captains, and the shouting.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7aa4023b-3ca1-4c63-8346-ac3301f750c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: JOB 39:26
Text: Doth the hawk fly by thy wisdom, and stretch her wings toward the south?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42f74701-ba2e-494c-92c1-5354ce148108>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: JOB 39:27
Text: Doth the eagle mount up at thy command, and make her nest on high?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5666e362-2ff7-4d09-b532-c91eb4a031bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: JOB 39:28
Text: She dwelleth and abideth on the rock, upon the crag of the rock, and the strong place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30c4db27-e1dc-4f8b-a0c3-8313c885c28b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: JOB 39:29
Text: From thence she seeketh the prey, and her eyes behold afar off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/39/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22b140a5-b576-4cd9-adc9-7b57a8335f48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: JOB 39:30
Text: Her young ones also suck up blood: and where the slain are, there is she.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/40/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
