WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f7933b3-4c8b-4f2f-97bd-38485950245f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: JOB 40:2
Text: Shall he that contendeth with the Almighty instruct him? he that reproveth God, let him answer it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/40/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a06cab5a-2e4b-4965-99a4-123a5adee1f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 64

Reference: JOB 40:3
Text: Then Job answered the LORD, and said,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/40/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a11edca-8d99-4aa4-8d7f-5e104afbae5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: JOB 40:4
Text: Behold, I am vile; what shall I answer thee? I will lay mine hand upon my mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/40/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5fe1c9c4-d765-432d-bb08-9e73b5720c1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: JOB 40:5
Text: Once have I spoken; but I will not answer: yea, twice; but I will proceed no further.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/40/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cac39b3c-ec3d-4fab-9bb1-1af752fb8892>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: JOB 40:6
Text: Then answered the LORD unto Job out of the whirlwind, and said,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/40/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff72ad64-4eee-4022-85fd-337118dbd5d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: JOB 40:7
Text: Gird up thy loins now like a man: I will demand of thee, and declare thou unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/40/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:879b69cb-25b3-440b-b25e-8b4445185445>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: JOB 40:8
Text: Wilt thou also disannul my judgment? wilt thou condemn me, that thou mayest be righteous?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/40/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:178324c2-d1d6-49ba-a6a3-77f37fcef80e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: JOB 40:9
Text: Hast thou an arm like God? or canst thou thunder with a voice like him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/40/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1c7ae25-0056-4dc0-a9cd-ad7c87591262>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: JOB 40:10
Text: Deck thyself now with majesty and excellency; and array thyself with glory and beauty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/40/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a1c36b1-bfc8-4f14-bae6-c2629491fa39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: JOB 40:11
Text: Cast abroad the rage of thy wrath: and behold every one that is proud, and abase him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/40/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7fe1656-c6c7-47f1-a8e5-2c996223db7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: JOB 40:12
Text: Look on every one that is proud, and bring him low; and tread down the wicked in their place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/40/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96901a22-8457-4ed1-a006-c535d97ad525>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: JOB 40:13
Text: Hide them in the dust together; and bind their faces in secret.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/40/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9acd2d8a-77e9-4b3f-9274-d512ec229152>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: JOB 40:14
Text: Then will I also confess unto thee that thine own right hand can save thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/40/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bda26ddb-f8f6-4e96-8804-14771b169e56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: JOB 40:15
Text: Behold now behemoth, which I made with thee; he eateth grass as an ox.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/40/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:177b4146-6401-46cf-b546-fe42c68c8fa1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: JOB 40:16
Text: Lo now, his strength is in his loins, and his force is in the navel of his belly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/40/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67ce71c7-0917-4b6c-a325-5c870bd9208d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: JOB 40:17
Text: He moveth his tail like a cedar: the sinews of his stones are wrapped together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/40/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50e8ad38-b415-4c57-a8a0-e71cab774282>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: JOB 40:18
Text: His bones are as strong pieces of brass; his bones are like bars of iron.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/40/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae4180c8-35a3-4da9-95a4-1a027a340bdd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: JOB 40:19
Text: He is the chief of the ways of God: he that made him can make his sword to approach unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/40/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bea3e71-be0c-41dc-9a54-453d831e5c9e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: JOB 40:20
Text: Surely the mountains bring him forth food, where all the beasts of the field play.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/40/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec16f98d-8f93-454a-986c-28b2fcc1f106>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: JOB 40:21
Text: He lieth under the shady trees, in the covert of the reed, and fens.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/40/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78b57ce2-5315-428a-ac2c-8b1937c194bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: JOB 40:22
Text: The shady trees cover him with their shadow; the willows of the brook compass him about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/40/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1be52cc0-600f-4412-b51d-f2c0fe692bac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: JOB 40:23
Text: Behold, he drinketh up a river, and hasteth not: he trusteth that he can draw up Jordan into his mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/40/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fc81e42-f34a-48ed-9f83-c6c020f1f8ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: JOB 40:24
Text: He taketh it with his eyes: his nose pierceth through snares.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72d015cb-4e35-48f1-9218-32ffc8a5737f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: JOB 41:1
Text: Canst thou draw out leviathan with an hook? or his tongue with a cord which thou lettest down?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20240c60-a3f2-4e47-bee0-dee39e4f0da9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: JOB 41:2
Text: Canst thou put an hook into his nose? or bore his jaw through with a thorn?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66083fad-ac42-44fb-849d-9d19fac7f196>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: JOB 41:3
Text: Will he make many supplications unto thee? will he speak soft words unto thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bcc33d52-acc3-426e-b737-7cd8d98852ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: JOB 41:4
Text: Will he make a covenant with thee? wilt thou take him for a servant for ever?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8fc451d0-6cfc-4bc8-9168-0a77c3addddc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: JOB 41:5
Text: Wilt thou play with him as with a bird? or wilt thou bind him for thy maidens?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03e7162b-6ea3-4cdd-bb05-0106ba7f5027>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: JOB 41:6
Text: Shall the companions make a banquet of him? shall they part him among the merchants?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:034cf33c-bb91-466b-81b0-c7a11535d5eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: JOB 41:7
Text: Canst thou fill his skin with barbed irons? or his head with fish spears?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b4401c9-a168-40bd-bddb-3cea188ab301>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: JOB 41:8
Text: Lay thine hand upon him, remember the battle, do no more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd35dffd-023d-4d86-a380-9de72eeed8fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: JOB 41:9
Text: Behold, the hope of him is in vain: shall not one be cast down even at the sight of him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7300fa79-90f1-44ca-854a-324a34e4881e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: JOB 41:10
Text: None is so fierce that dare stir him up: who then is able to stand before me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbdbb0ba-2c2f-4c37-a128-1ea681b7a8d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: JOB 41:11
Text: Who hath prevented me, that I should repay him? whatsoever is under the whole heaven is mine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9691f113-776b-438d-b26c-61038dd79e3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: JOB 41:12
Text: I will not conceal his parts, nor his power, nor his comely proportion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e7e2f1a-ee7d-4aa1-ace0-6d11e479fc1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: JOB 41:13
Text: Who can discover the face of his garment? or who can come to him with his double bridle?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d2c960e-0528-4d51-9ca6-cf4a04538fda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: JOB 41:14
Text: Who can open the doors of his face? his teeth are terrible round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d320229-7247-4e01-9177-c28c603a4572>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: JOB 41:15
Text: His scales are his pride, shut up together as with a close seal.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebbcd84d-fe30-4cb6-b601-a3a628894222>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: JOB 41:16
Text: One is so near to another, that no air can come between them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5fe1436-63a3-41b9-8ac7-9ae008a9bd09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: JOB 41:17
Text: They are joined one to another, they stick together, that they cannot be sundered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec0bd1e8-1061-47f2-bae4-c84671e36eda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: JOB 41:18
Text: By his neesings a light doth shine, and his eyes are like the eyelids of the morning.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:044cee6f-a481-46df-ae22-dbba2ff6063b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: JOB 41:19
Text: Out of his mouth go burning lamps, and sparks of fire leap out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:503036fc-670f-4dbb-a10c-3669a46b1924>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: JOB 41:20
Text: Out of his nostrils goeth smoke, as out of a seething pot or caldron.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36fa5076-4fd5-43ec-b372-9cab747d8fcd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: JOB 41:21
Text: His breath kindleth coals, and a flame goeth out of his mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e77effaa-2238-43bf-9658-9a6504449d7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: JOB 41:22
Text: In his neck remaineth strength, and sorrow is turned into joy before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff67a71f-7f59-4a48-b0a0-04dfdff715a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: JOB 41:23
Text: The flakes of his flesh are joined together: they are firm in themselves; they cannot be moved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bab1aae-56f7-49d7-9c46-1070a25403e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: JOB 41:24
Text: His heart is as firm as a stone; yea, as hard as a piece of the nether millstone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ca299ad-ce21-4802-a90d-2af5b7c03557>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: JOB 41:25
Text: When he raiseth up himself, the mighty are afraid: by reason of breakings they purify themselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:251f915d-c70f-4817-9f47-ad33a758ddf4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: JOB 41:26
Text: The sword of him that layeth at him cannot hold: the spear, the dart, nor the habergeon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9f581b6-cb12-4316-b6e3-9046dcd5ce47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: JOB 41:27
Text: He esteemeth iron as straw, and brass as rotten wood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b15b872-ab3a-46b8-9592-9ff7b97c8fe8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: JOB 41:28
Text: The arrow cannot make him flee: slingstones are turned with him into stubble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb5685fd-5915-46be-8615-6450e7f68c61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: JOB 41:29
Text: Darts are counted as stubble: he laugheth at the shaking of a spear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61d017b7-cee5-424a-9756-4f80c72c426e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: JOB 41:30
Text: Sharp stones are under him: he spreadeth sharp pointed things upon the mire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1684ffc-f0c1-4bbb-a718-c6f57ee39ed8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: JOB 41:31
Text: He maketh the deep to boil like a pot: he maketh the sea like a pot of ointment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cae396a1-b113-4ca2-a84a-39e76e2abb40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: JOB 41:32
Text: He maketh a path to shine after him; one would think the deep to be hoary.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f84d747-6a14-4646-ae82-f27515ad2a59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: JOB 41:33
Text: Upon earth there is not his like, who is made without fear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/41/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:228e5e77-3f8a-4d10-bca2-2999c44405cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: JOB 41:34
Text: He beholdeth all high things: he is a king over all the children of pride.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/42/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17b6c4dd-c3eb-43d8-a109-f381f53df3f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 64

Reference: JOB 42:1
Text: Then Job answered the LORD, and said,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/42/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1c17452-f1eb-4c40-902e-c33e3762849d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: JOB 42:2
Text: I know that thou canst do every thing, and that no thought can be withholden from thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/42/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3aa0211b-a3c1-4bbb-bb70-f6cd2f3e32ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: JOB 42:3
Text: Who is he that hideth counsel without knowledge? therefore have I uttered that I understood not; things too wonderful for me, which I knew not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/42/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0aec11c6-eece-47cd-b77c-24a68c2f365b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: JOB 42:4
Text: Hear, I beseech thee, and I will speak: I will demand of thee, and declare thou unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/42/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22586716-3eae-4633-8f59-9247194e8cbf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: JOB 42:5
Text: I have heard of thee by the hearing of the ear: but now mine eye seeth thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/42/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4429640-3d75-4e28-940a-a04c92177bf7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: JOB 42:6
Text: Wherefore I abhor myself, and repent in dust and ashes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/42/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79240e91-f672-4a82-a61d-17731452512f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 274

Reference: JOB 42:7
Text: And it was so, that after the LORD had spoken these words unto Job, the LORD said to Eliphaz the Temanite, My wrath is kindled against thee, and against thy two friends: for ye have not spoken of me the thing that is right, as my servant Job hath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/42/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae1c321e-43c1-4a8e-a779-dbccadc49283>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 338

Reference: JOB 42:8
Text: Therefore take unto you now seven bullocks and seven rams, and go to my servant Job, and offer up for yourselves a burnt offering; and my servant Job shall pray for you: for him will I accept: lest I deal with you after your folly, in that ye have not spoken of me the thing which is right, like my servant Job.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/42/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83885368-9044-413a-a711-37abfdd3fdcb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: JOB 42:9
Text: So Eliphaz the Temanite and Bildad the Shuhite and Zophar the Naamathite went, and did according as the LORD commanded them: the LORD also accepted Job.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/42/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0cc6950f-820d-427a-9464-0a9c545c690a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: JOB 42:10
Text: And the LORD turned the captivity of Job, when he prayed for his friends: also the LORD gave Job twice as much as he had before.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/42/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3991cea9-6d01-431d-8a89-a0164594ee77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 358

Reference: JOB 42:11
Text: Then came there unto him all his brethren, and all his sisters, and all they that had been of his acquaintance before, and did eat bread with him in his house: and they bemoaned him, and comforted him over all the evil that the LORD had brought upon him: every man also gave him a piece of money, and every one an earring of gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/42/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a45f8ac4-c655-4614-85b5-7b25de819e1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: JOB 42:12
Text: So the LORD blessed the latter end of Job more than his beginning: for he had fourteen thousand sheep, and six thousand camels, and a thousand yoke of oxen, and a thousand she asses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/42/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f313700-38ec-458c-b840-0e8385d7d41d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 71

Reference: JOB 42:13
Text: He had also seven sons and three daughters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/42/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44f4d187-8508-46d3-9e48-83b80a44739a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: JOB 42:14
Text: And he called the name of the first, Jemima; and the name of the second, Kezia; and the name of the third, Kerenhappuch.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/42/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fbcc0d9-0d4d-4482-a93b-660b5a33df91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: JOB 42:15
Text: And in all the land were no women found so fair as the daughters of Job: and their father gave them inheritance among their brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/42/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0b9acf4-ffa4-4c2e-aaac-8ca597f03a3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: JOB 42:16
Text: After this lived Job an hundred and forty years, and saw his sons, and his sons’ sons, even four generations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOB/42/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97c5c2a5-4cc6-4039-b1e5-ff381fe49cab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 68

Reference: JOB 42:17
Text: So Job died, being old and full of days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:185ba702-cd90-47f9-9f09-64a2e424904b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: PSA 1:1
Text: Blessed is the man that walketh not in the counsel of the ungodly, nor standeth in the way of sinners, nor sitteth in the seat of the scornful.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a31a9312-4cf8-4566-889c-35b850892b95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 1:2
Text: But his delight is in the law of the LORD; and in his law doth he meditate day and night.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71049cf7-455b-480c-858c-9b39cd7c26e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: PSA 1:3
Text: And he shall be like a tree planted by the rivers of water, that bringeth forth his fruit in his season; his leaf also shall not wither; and whatsoever he doeth shall prosper.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ffb72b1-6741-4eee-b6b1-b4d329c43872>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 1:4
Text: The ungodly are not so: but are like the chaff which the wind driveth away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8b9bc79-c285-4101-852f-a16aab420e48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 1:5
Text: Therefore the ungodly shall not stand in the judgment, nor sinners in the congregation of the righteous.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8bd37899-f6ad-42ac-acf0-f912ce9c3ad8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 1:6
Text: For the LORD knoweth the way of the righteous: but the way of the ungodly shall perish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9edb3774-8f28-4b06-832b-12467bef4929>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PSA 2:1
Text: Why do the heathen rage, and the people imagine a vain thing?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21c07509-a458-481a-ab1b-74b8bc0d5195>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: PSA 2:2
Text: The kings of the earth set themselves, and the rulers take counsel together, against the LORD, and against his anointed, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7951bf01-3c4d-4197-aabc-e27ef1e7b90e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 2:3
Text: Let us break their bands asunder, and cast away their cords from us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef1832d2-1cb6-456b-b170-3fcd4f1c2ed2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 2:4
Text: He that sitteth in the heavens shall laugh: the LORD shall have them in derision.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b6509ee-c382-45dd-972f-38db8622e17c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 2:5
Text: Then shall he speak unto them in his wrath, and vex them in his sore displeasure.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:639e7695-1fa0-45c0-bfc4-7c839a823a86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: PSA 2:6
Text: Yet have I set my king upon my holy hill of Zion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00cdd772-bdc1-4da7-a5d2-a5c854bda7fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 2:7
Text: I will declare the decree: the LORD hath said unto me, Thou art my Son; this day have I begotten thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69ec3c3c-a9cf-4a5b-801d-aeca84e75b2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: PSA 2:8
Text: Ask of me, and I shall give thee the heathen for thine inheritance, and the uttermost parts of the earth for thy possession.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e3c9968-8025-4524-a78d-e56b32bd3b93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 2:9
Text: Thou shalt break them with a rod of iron; thou shalt dash them in pieces like a potter’s vessel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a7cb8f5-1767-4a7b-b42d-7dfcc3cabdb8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 2:10
Text: Be wise now therefore, O ye kings: be instructed, ye judges of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6faf3f00-af9f-4a3d-b763-4a1b59acdd38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: PSA 2:11
Text: Serve the LORD with fear, and rejoice with trembling.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de2ffbf9-a987-4a9e-a680-f2c1bb574c88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: PSA 2:12
Text: Kiss the Son, lest he be angry, and ye perish from the way, when his wrath is kindled but a little. Blessed are all they that put their trust in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33990130-eade-4d71-9284-3bd4e3e76211>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 3:1
Text: Lord, how are they increased that trouble me! many are they that rise up against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5134c00a-3a18-49b4-aea8-7c81672e49ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 3:2
Text: Many there be which say of my soul, There is no help for him in God. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b671bb2-153e-4c1f-b526-bcd00b180410>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 3:3
Text: But thou, O LORD, art a shield for me; my glory, and the lifter up of mine head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbed5821-858c-4632-8df9-b62257c9de07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 3:4
Text: I cried unto the LORD with my voice, and he heard me out of his holy hill. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c792919-42a6-4da7-89a5-432918dbcab3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 3:5
Text: I laid me down and slept; I awaked; for the LORD sustained me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0644627f-5b26-4743-9616-89b3fc9884ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 3:6
Text: I will not be afraid of ten thousands of people, that have set themselves against me round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff146826-28c1-4c14-b9f1-92395d199b76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: PSA 3:7
Text: Arise, O LORD; save me, O my God: for thou hast smitten all mine enemies upon the cheek bone; thou hast broken the teeth of the ungodly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb36ed00-0198-495c-8404-e06dda375c62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 3:8
Text: Salvation belongeth unto the LORD: thy blessing is upon thy people. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0db56dc9-2d33-4bf9-9995-be869bae88b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: PSA 4:1
Text: Hear me when I call, O God of my righteousness: thou hast enlarged me when I was in distress; have mercy upon me, and hear my prayer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02a70abc-409e-4715-bcd8-9586fc64f359>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: PSA 4:2
Text: O ye sons of men, how long will ye turn my glory into shame? how long will ye love vanity, and seek after leasing? Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40e71243-9238-42a6-9c84-89711ac4025f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PSA 4:3
Text: But know that the LORD hath set apart him that is godly for himself: the LORD will hear when I call unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3461e119-7475-4210-bfbb-dce0b6e74886>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 4:4
Text: Stand in awe, and sin not: commune with your own heart upon your bed, and be still. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7dc7294d-2a81-46a0-8335-4577f4c4b8e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 4:5
Text: Offer the sacrifices of righteousness, and put your trust in the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3f67df7-f5d7-4a76-b266-d8e64b0a6067>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: PSA 4:6
Text: There be many that say, Who will shew us any good? LORD, lift thou up the light of thy countenance upon us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fafb16ba-0225-4530-aa8b-74c98e508958>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 4:7
Text: Thou hast put gladness in my heart, more than in the time that their corn and their wine increased.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:815a5192-5346-4f60-abad-9889f48b6ab2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 4:8
Text: I will both lay me down in peace, and sleep: for thou, LORD, only makest me dwell in safety.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9caae495-077f-4207-b340-ef7f4298b41b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: PSA 5:1
Text: Give ear to my words, O LORD, consider my meditation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:651aa8e6-7b55-449c-a05e-6de5e31d56f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 5:2
Text: Hearken unto the voice of my cry, my King, and my God: for unto thee will I pray.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce5889de-607c-4c70-b39f-ac51ad4d7f93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: PSA 5:3
Text: My voice shalt thou hear in the morning, O LORD; in the morning will I direct my prayer unto thee, and will look up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85e2bc3e-9f11-407e-b54d-68b384d874f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 5:4
Text: For thou art not a God that hath pleasure in wickedness: neither shall evil dwell with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8646742a-6096-4a0a-9ec2-064903462537>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 5:5
Text: The foolish shall not stand in thy sight: thou hatest all workers of iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58176a1a-5e78-402f-bd4a-c42c7a4736f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 5:6
Text: Thou shalt destroy them that speak leasing: the LORD will abhor the bloody and deceitful man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3dec927c-1d8e-4c67-9ac1-72c0b78ab515>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: PSA 5:7
Text: But as for me, I will come into thy house in the multitude of thy mercy: and in thy fear will I worship toward thy holy temple.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65c981bb-e950-45ce-8a8e-48c10a8b4177>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 5:8
Text: Lead me, O LORD, in thy righteousness because of mine enemies; make thy way straight before my face.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d11e50c5-89cb-4a08-a06d-652663c65412>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: PSA 5:9
Text: For there is no faithfulness in their mouth; their inward part is very wickedness; their throat is an open sepulchre; they flatter with their tongue.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1e89683-101f-42a6-9483-3d693df05279>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: PSA 5:10
Text: Destroy thou them, O God; let them fall by their own counsels; cast them out in the multitude of their transgressions; for they have rebelled against thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61d6b427-8a26-43cc-833d-d7b3f4cea741>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: PSA 5:11
Text: But let all those that put their trust in thee rejoice: let them ever shout for joy, because thou defendest them: let them also that love thy name be joyful in thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30aa25e2-3754-4696-8701-73767d069ff3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 5:12
Text: For thou, LORD, wilt bless the righteous; with favour wilt thou compass him as with a shield.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09e91fd7-647a-4b8b-b08f-631157b8118a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 6:1
Text: O LORD, rebuke me not in thine anger, neither chasten me in thy hot displeasure.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:259be6e9-07b8-420f-86c5-bfd60a784eff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 6:2
Text: Have mercy upon me, O LORD; for I am weak: O LORD, heal me; for my bones are vexed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1079f368-a984-49d5-9a4a-fd3a8d4c53e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: PSA 6:3
Text: My soul is also sore vexed: but thou, O LORD, how long?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6d5b288-fcc8-45c9-b96d-eb9692a9fac9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 6:4
Text: Return, O LORD, deliver my soul: oh save me for thy mercies’ sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a9cb45a-054e-4c18-bafd-9311f559cc28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 6:5
Text: For in death there is no remembrance of thee: in the grave who shall give thee thanks?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebf483f2-2133-4875-a34b-e141556bb44d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 6:6
Text: I am weary with my groaning; all the night make I my bed to swim; I water my couch with my tears.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2e44c22-6d06-47fe-ba2f-c60bbb8b89fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 6:7
Text: Mine eye is consumed because of grief; it waxeth old because of all mine enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6820d116-0fa4-4b80-8a9f-988a33ccce02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 6:8
Text: Depart from me, all ye workers of iniquity; for the LORD hath heard the voice of my weeping.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87a4cf8c-6d61-4a6f-86d3-3393be2548b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 6:9
Text: The LORD hath heard my supplication; the LORD will receive my prayer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:477317ba-5c37-4b80-b182-d0553acebc08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 6:10
Text: Let all mine enemies be ashamed and sore vexed: let them return and be ashamed suddenly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fff2c103-030e-47f6-b837-080d31529683>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 7:1
Text: O LORD my God, in thee do I put my trust: save me from all them that persecute me, and deliver me:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acf6a478-281f-447b-b6a9-fedfbb76b14b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 7:2
Text: Lest he tear my soul like a lion, rending it in pieces, while there is none to deliver.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc18d1ba-7f18-4c8f-87a7-a68a3803d1ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 7:3
Text: O LORD my God, If I have done this; if there be iniquity in my hands;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d50442c2-4308-40ea-8dda-17ab60a99917>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: PSA 7:4
Text: If I have rewarded evil unto him that was at peace with me; (yea, I have delivered him that without cause is mine enemy:)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:566d6b78-dbd3-4c38-99b1-6743a807e641>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: PSA 7:5
Text: Let the enemy persecute my soul, and take it; yea, let him tread down my life upon the earth, and lay mine honour in the dust. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c1d47e4-afd4-4bb8-a36b-55c2137d59c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: PSA 7:6
Text: Arise, O LORD, in thine anger, lift up thyself because of the rage of mine enemies: and awake for me to the judgment that thou hast commanded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74abede3-5123-4f00-adae-40042e4f5b92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 7:7
Text: So shall the congregation of the people compass thee about: for their sakes therefore return thou on high.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d109631b-81b5-4375-af05-9b4660569616>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: PSA 7:8
Text: The LORD shall judge the people: judge me, O LORD, according to my righteousness, and according to mine integrity that is in me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd011e7e-9d2c-4bdf-8a71-9e099bfefadf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: PSA 7:9
Text: Oh let the wickedness of the wicked come to an end; but establish the just: for the righteous God trieth the hearts and reins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2880055-5b71-4364-84dd-ce92f99a54d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: PSA 7:10
Text: My defence is of God, which saveth the upright in heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23bf5434-644b-4571-b698-89c869a4f10a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 7:11
Text: God judgeth the righteous, and God is angry with the wicked every day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:625810ed-5b0c-490e-af2b-3a8fdec838f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 7:12
Text: If he turn not, he will whet his sword; he hath bent his bow, and made it ready.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f119103e-2bf4-4060-8eed-38a032f4117f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 7:13
Text: He hath also prepared for him the instruments of death; he ordaineth his arrows against the persecutors.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/7/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:511bbd09-9920-42a5-b637-e38a0c65b23a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 7:14
Text: Behold, he travaileth with iniquity, and hath conceived mischief, and brought forth falsehood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/7/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97086f99-4c1a-4c0a-a1a6-3a10f722f01d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 7:15
Text: He made a pit, and digged it, and is fallen into the ditch which he made.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/7/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1f817b0-2122-48a6-bc56-f047cd31443c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 7:16
Text: His mischief shall return upon his own head, and his violent dealing shall come down upon his own pate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/7/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0a17023-3278-40b6-be22-60fea922aa9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: PSA 7:17
Text: I will praise the LORD according to his righteousness: and will sing praise to the name of the LORD most high.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/8/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc341efe-0c1e-4b83-b6a5-fe895190ef44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PSA 8:1
Text: O LORD, our Lord, how excellent is thy name in all the earth! who hast set thy glory above the heavens.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/8/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96caaee0-35ec-4167-b91f-bc334ab7c107>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: PSA 8:2
Text: Out of the mouth of babes and sucklings hast thou ordained strength because of thine enemies, that thou mightest still the enemy and the avenger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/8/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d60dda21-e9f8-4c12-bccf-c5fa3803fc30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PSA 8:3
Text: When I consider thy heavens, the work of thy fingers, the moon and the stars, which thou hast ordained;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/8/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebc23eec-248c-422a-99b1-c4d89d024d67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 8:4
Text: What is man, that thou art mindful of him? and the son of man, that thou visitest him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/8/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f5ef376-6884-404e-9836-21750ce2e76d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 8:5
Text: For thou hast made him a little lower than the angels, and hast crowned him with glory and honour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/8/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae7ff343-6a97-40b8-aa9d-23b2d6a1ef64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 8:6
Text: Thou madest him to have dominion over the works of thy hands; thou hast put all things under his feet:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/8/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61b901ff-bd2c-4a51-9587-0fa5575c24e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: PSA 8:7
Text: All sheep and oxen, yea, and the beasts of the field;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/8/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f501f200-075d-47ef-9630-aadfbe968599>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 8:8
Text: The fowl of the air, and the fish of the sea, and whatsoever passeth through the paths of the seas.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/8/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e6fa684-a3f6-4920-9144-272a765b16c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PSA 8:9
Text: O LORD our Lord, how excellent is thy name in all the earth!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/9/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5521daf1-4687-4742-8111-666daeb36e66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 9:1
Text: I will praise thee, O LORD, with my whole heart; I will shew forth all thy marvellous works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/9/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a80a3d0-da7c-44f4-9630-da7cfef55b1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 9:2
Text: I will be glad and rejoice in thee: I will sing praise to thy name, O thou most High.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/9/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b0f117e-5a44-4329-ae60-7478191903d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 9:3
Text: When mine enemies are turned back, they shall fall and perish at thy presence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/9/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65dcb2f8-a4f9-431e-9404-25ed581b8156>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 9:4
Text: For thou hast maintained my right and my cause; thou satest in the throne judging right.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/9/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0432201e-72b3-4499-bdf8-9401017028b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PSA 9:5
Text: Thou hast rebuked the heathen, thou hast destroyed the wicked, thou hast put out their name for ever and ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/9/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:614ebf32-a9f5-41e8-ad22-4efa11605514>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: PSA 9:6
Text: O thou enemy, destructions are come to a perpetual end: and thou hast destroyed cities; their memorial is perished with them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/9/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76ddcd09-f4b0-4394-80b3-5e51c2cbb6c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 9:7
Text: But the LORD shall endure for ever: he hath prepared his throne for judgment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/9/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f82a3f95-8811-43b7-96aa-24c78ca94dda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PSA 9:8
Text: And he shall judge the world in righteousness, he shall minister judgment to the people in uprightness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/9/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d9ad673-0e29-458a-8ba5-aaef7f16a5b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 9:9
Text: The LORD also will be a refuge for the oppressed, a refuge in times of trouble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/9/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8cf540ab-1efc-4141-996e-7f4b80d58e59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: PSA 9:10
Text: And they that know thy name will put their trust in thee: for thou, LORD, hast not forsaken them that seek thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/9/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80ed725f-d318-42b7-ae45-ebc7e35bd75f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 9:11
Text: Sing praises to the LORD, which dwelleth in Zion: declare among the people his doings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/9/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e45d1258-9366-412b-8f9c-7242b0b5f036>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 9:12
Text: When he maketh inquisition for blood, he remembereth them: he forgetteth not the cry of the humble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/9/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87db3433-ad2a-44e7-8525-2de4c712ad35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: PSA 9:13
Text: Have mercy upon me, O LORD; consider my trouble which I suffer of them that hate me, thou that liftest me up from the gates of death:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/9/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c75eee1-befd-4d45-9f44-d58ff5542b8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PSA 9:14
Text: That I may shew forth all thy praise in the gates of the daughter of Zion: I will rejoice in thy salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/9/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68b18cb2-dea4-4186-b65d-b54431eb0b20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 9:15
Text: The heathen are sunk down in the pit that they made: in the net which they hid is their own foot taken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/9/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:143bbdc2-2b27-4e85-a0fd-b4676e7f7ef0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: PSA 9:16
Text: The LORD is known by the judgment which he executeth: the wicked is snared in the work of his own hands. Higgaion. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/9/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d110e9f-8f50-44bb-97e0-f84ee2672413>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 9:17
Text: The wicked shall be turned into hell, and all the nations that forget God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/9/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b45c3506-b96f-4e52-bfaa-7203d1e1c51a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 9:18
Text: For the needy shall not alway be forgotten: the expectation of the poor shall not perish for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/9/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba6379f0-8b34-4ddf-8876-580c80dab1c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 9:19
Text: Arise, O LORD; let not man prevail: let the heathen be judged in thy sight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/9/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00ea77dd-7f74-4e76-ba66-677bbeb724ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 9:20
Text: Put them in fear, O LORD: that the nations may know themselves to be but men. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/10/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a532f08-558a-42f8-b9ac-6bf434a41d12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 10:1
Text: Why standest thou afar off, O LORD? why hidest thou thyself in times of trouble?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/10/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fed1bfd-c2fb-4eb5-9879-54824fe8e64a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: PSA 10:2
Text: The wicked in his pride doth persecute the poor: let them be taken in the devices that they have imagined.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/10/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c2b956c-5306-46bf-b12b-1bf7759cb004>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PSA 10:3
Text: For the wicked boasteth of his heart’s desire, and blesseth the covetous, whom the LORD abhorreth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/10/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21e10533-9b7c-4605-98a3-c891c033b206>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: PSA 10:4
Text: The wicked, through the pride of his countenance, will not seek after God: God is not in all his thoughts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/10/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3f64846-ef16-4072-b7dc-78bb7afda80a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: PSA 10:5
Text: His ways are always grievous; thy judgments are far above out of his sight: as for all his enemies, he puffeth at them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/10/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eed7ee1f-9ea1-4255-bfcc-127040432dbd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 10:6
Text: He hath said in his heart, I shall not be moved: for I shall never be in adversity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/10/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cac5f70e-e99a-41c7-a5cc-3175410679c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 10:7
Text: His mouth is full of cursing and deceit and fraud: under his tongue is mischief and vanity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/10/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3508e36d-4647-4580-8471-591bc3bfef72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: PSA 10:8
Text: He sitteth in the lurking places of the villages: in the secret places doth he murder the innocent: his eyes are privily set against the poor.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/10/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d34d60c-0bd7-4888-8f5e-413e17bfea00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: PSA 10:9
Text: He lieth in wait secretly as a lion in his den: he lieth in wait to catch the poor: he doth catch the poor, when he draweth him into his net.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/10/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc5f75ff-8baf-4279-ae06-d3c0d9a458c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 10:10
Text: He croucheth, and humbleth himself, that the poor may fall by his strong ones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/10/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e045a79-7188-4f39-9536-59e211d3053c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 10:11
Text: He hath said in his heart, God hath forgotten: he hideth his face; he will never see it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/10/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46fa6287-50fd-40ba-8d07-bc9712252498>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PSA 10:12
Text: Arise, O LORD; O God, lift up thine hand: forget not the humble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/10/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0e71cbd-ab17-4e3e-b44c-e4477a1c742f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 10:13
Text: Wherefore doth the wicked contemn God? he hath said in his heart, Thou wilt not require it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/10/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f3e7e26-d555-40dd-a91d-3c71e3d953a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: PSA 10:14
Text: Thou hast seen it; for thou beholdest mischief and spite, to requite it with thy hand: the poor committeth himself unto thee; thou art the helper of the fatherless.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/10/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1dc7bf97-d35c-40f4-8b3e-342a9fabce4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 10:15
Text: Break thou the arm of the wicked and the evil man: seek out his wickedness till thou find none.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/10/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eda0f482-a8e6-49b9-ae34-a4d5c1c9ec81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 10:16
Text: The LORD is King for ever and ever: the heathen are perished out of his land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/10/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:476e25f7-aadd-446a-94b4-fa3743402dc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: PSA 10:17
Text: LORD, thou hast heard the desire of the humble: thou wilt prepare their heart, thou wilt cause thine ear to hear:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/10/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9953d0f-1cff-444c-a754-041aa5f36493>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 10:18
Text: To judge the fatherless and the oppressed, that the man of the earth may no more oppress.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/11/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb3d4a93-aded-4cba-a7d1-dfd969dc8543>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 11:1
Text: In the LORD put I my trust: how say ye to my soul, Flee as a bird to your mountain?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/11/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:238fa4c5-0ecb-4496-8c8c-b6b76d4025df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: PSA 11:2
Text: For, lo, the wicked bend their bow, they make ready their arrow upon the string, that they may privily shoot at the upright in heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/11/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e915ad8-d13c-4daf-a592-46f2adad7019>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PSA 11:3
Text: If the foundations be destroyed, what can the righteous do?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/11/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc7ece85-49df-4e23-811c-1c7c62c732e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: PSA 11:4
Text: The LORD is in his holy temple, the LORD’s throne is in heaven: his eyes behold, his eyelids try, the children of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/11/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5247a674-12cd-49a7-8ebb-8d0ce86259ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 11:5
Text: The LORD trieth the righteous: but the wicked and him that loveth violence his soul hateth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/11/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c647b629-d1cc-4e20-bb53-6b274061085a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: PSA 11:6
Text: Upon the wicked he shall rain snares, fire and brimstone, and an horrible tempest: this shall be the portion of their cup.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/11/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3348bac-4807-472c-a8c0-c26a57186166>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 11:7
Text: For the righteous LORD loveth righteousness; his countenance doth behold the upright.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/12/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4b78151-c934-459a-b8d9-7725857ce0b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 12:1
Text: Help, LORD; for the godly man ceaseth; for the faithful fail from among the children of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/12/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c056677-c112-4a96-9829-c79cc782ec20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PSA 12:2
Text: They speak vanity every one with his neighbour: with flattering lips and with a double heart do they speak.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/12/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edeec380-06f3-4b6a-82dc-ace1deb80acc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 12:3
Text: The LORD shall cut off all flattering lips, and the tongue that speaketh proud things:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/12/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7cf26467-3984-4a1e-bf0a-3811bbd7893f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 12:4
Text: Who have said, With our tongue will we prevail; our lips are our own: who is lord over us?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/12/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f0ea7fa-7398-45ab-9652-1f0642871ca6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: PSA 12:5
Text: For the oppression of the poor, for the sighing of the needy, now will I arise, saith the LORD; I will set him in safety from him that puffeth at him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/12/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e4a528b-2b6a-4dc3-9cc1-18b4a83fdb95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 12:6
Text: The words of the LORD are pure words: as silver tried in a furnace of earth, purified seven times.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/12/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:328c226f-765d-424b-b692-6d5749644500>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 12:7
Text: Thou shalt keep them, O LORD, thou shalt preserve them from this generation for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/12/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44e0f86e-058d-4260-8c64-5866c1ca0b24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 12:8
Text: The wicked walk on every side, when the vilest men are exalted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/13/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be05fcb5-af94-4001-8d7e-fb4b684e2e1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 13:1
Text: How long wilt thou forget me, O LORD? for ever? how long wilt thou hide thy face from me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/13/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:adc3d151-fdf5-40ca-9654-8b6345307710>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: PSA 13:2
Text: How long shall I take counsel in my soul, having sorrow in my heart daily? how long shall mine enemy be exalted over me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/13/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:364b414e-5df1-4dea-a0c6-bcc436edac66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 13:3
Text: Consider and hear me, O LORD my God: lighten mine eyes, lest I sleep the sleep of death;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/13/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de956e85-6ce1-4ced-b05c-dada7df5af50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 13:4
Text: Lest mine enemy say, I have prevailed against him; and those that trouble me rejoice when I am moved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/13/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3626fe78-c4ba-4b16-9fa4-9df1cfe7fbb8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 13:5
Text: But I have trusted in thy mercy; my heart shall rejoice in thy salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/13/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:670437a4-ecd1-4701-840a-02b9f6847ca7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 13:6
Text: I will sing unto the LORD, because he hath dealt bountifully with me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/14/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:081e2c14-7183-4746-be44-a5f04570ca7a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: PSA 14:1
Text: The fool hath said in his heart, There is no God. They are corrupt, they have done abominable works, there is none that doeth good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/14/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d432cf07-371f-4e53-b3c2-b149ff0e7e24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: PSA 14:2
Text: The LORD looked down from heaven upon the children of men, to see if there were any that did understand, and seek God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/14/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b4c5990-3646-4e8f-a345-5b450f50c94f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 14:3
Text: They are all gone aside, they are all together become filthy: there is none that doeth good, no, not one.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/14/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9766955d-a51c-45f8-a04b-be551ea648a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: PSA 14:4
Text: Have all the workers of iniquity no knowledge? who eat up my people as they eat bread, and call not upon the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/14/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9698277f-d0b5-4d8a-94bb-04911e2f727f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 14:5
Text: There were they in great fear: for God is in the generation of the righteous.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/14/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30642981-9c77-4ee1-8392-d9947056b936>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 14:6
Text: Ye have shamed the counsel of the poor, because the LORD is his refuge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/14/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:160eb3d3-606d-44e8-9b32-e34454fe697d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: PSA 14:7
Text: Oh that the salvation of Israel were come out of Zion! when the LORD bringeth back the captivity of his people, Jacob shall rejoice, and Israel shall be glad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/15/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6258095f-0c0f-4758-8e13-e4f69edf6d42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 15:1
Text: Lord, who shall abide in thy tabernacle? who shall dwell in thy holy hill?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/15/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b03dfbc-7de5-4269-aeaa-25b85500d771>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 15:2
Text: He that walketh uprightly, and worketh righteousness, and speaketh the truth in his heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/15/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4d5facb-e3c2-42f1-b138-ddbda39e7e8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: PSA 15:3
Text: He that backbiteth not with his tongue, nor doeth evil to his neighbour, nor taketh up a reproach against his neighbour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/15/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca4e11c4-b89e-4b26-998a-c0cee5ecc0bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: PSA 15:4
Text: In whose eyes a vile person is contemned; but he honoureth them that fear the LORD. He that sweareth to his own hurt, and changeth not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/15/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00d99c6c-9762-479a-b3d2-a83cee9f3971>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: PSA 15:5
Text: He that putteth not out his money to usury, nor taketh reward against the innocent. He that doeth these things shall never be moved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/16/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e4f633e-b0e5-4615-8947-d8b6b7dc59c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: PSA 16:1
Text: Preserve me, O God: for in thee do I put my trust.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/16/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64ddd353-7d26-4c0b-bd64-4829ce21be95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 16:2
Text: O my soul, thou hast said unto the LORD, Thou art my Lord: my goodness extendeth not to thee;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/16/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f50d1ee3-d4de-43e6-b5ae-65bb45b47d89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 16:3
Text: But to the saints that are in the earth, and to the excellent, in whom is all my delight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/16/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0daf1bd2-424e-4187-9dc5-b0192fd6d5ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: PSA 16:4
Text: Their sorrows shall be multiplied that hasten after another god: their drink offerings of blood will I not offer, nor take up their names into my lips.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/16/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0977885d-e9c0-4f8e-b0ef-d1ba35c98ef9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 16:5
Text: The LORD is the portion of mine inheritance and of my cup: thou maintainest my lot.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/16/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be89784d-e2f1-4a4b-889d-190efff5b274>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 16:6
Text: The lines are fallen unto me in pleasant places; yea, I have a goodly heritage.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/16/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c064874e-50ec-4664-b08d-1593332ca4bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 16:7
Text: I will bless the LORD, who hath given me counsel: my reins also instruct me in the night seasons.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/16/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:684393af-c288-42f7-9cf1-1af888905327>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 16:8
Text: I have set the LORD always before me: because he is at my right hand, I shall not be moved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/16/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2dd0b52-c215-4944-ab74-cdea49a281cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 16:9
Text: Therefore my heart is glad, and my glory rejoiceth: my flesh also shall rest in hope.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/16/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b1fd58c-39ef-40ef-9346-db52afeb0dfa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PSA 16:10
Text: For thou wilt not leave my soul in hell; neither wilt thou suffer thine Holy One to see corruption.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/16/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86566411-4ea4-49fa-801e-126c9068de02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: PSA 16:11
Text: Thou wilt shew me the path of life: in thy presence is fulness of joy; at thy right hand there are pleasures for evermore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/17/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:178d9ef9-0b30-4651-9997-542d14da594e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 17:1
Text: Hear the right, O LORD, attend unto my cry, give ear unto my prayer, that goeth not out of feigned lips.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/17/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f687113b-9dc3-45c9-99b6-8e4ed25ed97a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 17:2
Text: Let my sentence come forth from thy presence; let thine eyes behold the things that are equal.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/17/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:394d9529-8c1b-43b7-8382-2e96e5184ddd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: PSA 17:3
Text: Thou hast proved mine heart; thou hast visited me in the night; thou hast tried me, and shalt find nothing; I am purposed that my mouth shall not transgress.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/17/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2f8a60c-19ba-4a49-be86-1faffa1d84a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PSA 17:4
Text: Concerning the works of men, by the word of thy lips I have kept me from the paths of the destroyer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/17/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07c61f95-8074-41f9-b58f-256dc87ba306>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PSA 17:5
Text: Hold up my goings in thy paths, that my footsteps slip not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/17/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:283b7958-1de2-4903-8109-d26243903611>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 17:6
Text: I have called upon thee, for thou wilt hear me, O God: incline thine ear unto me, and hear my speech.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/17/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79781fb7-5c35-4f61-b410-6124f339587f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: PSA 17:7
Text: Shew thy marvellous lovingkindness, O thou that savest by thy right hand them which put their trust in thee from those that rise up against them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/17/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34c7b408-592d-4adc-ac85-0f7191a1925a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 17:8
Text: Keep me as the apple of the eye, hide me under the shadow of thy wings,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/17/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e970337f-20a2-47e1-8f87-6e75a49acca2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 17:9
Text: From the wicked that oppress me, from my deadly enemies, who compass me about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/17/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3499633f-2beb-40ef-b5a0-1609c62e6f9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 17:10
Text: They are inclosed in their own fat: with their mouth they speak proudly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/17/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1d89a80-8ac3-4fc0-8781-78b025a8d461>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 17:11
Text: They have now compassed us in our steps: they have set their eyes bowing down to the earth;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/17/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f482761f-d729-45cf-a81a-ad4702769de7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 17:12
Text: Like as a lion that is greedy of his prey, and as it were a young lion lurking in secret places.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/17/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d65fb52-e955-4010-a782-b31412f20e33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 17:13
Text: Arise, O LORD, disappoint him, cast him down: deliver my soul from the wicked, which is thy sword:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/17/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4363413e-0376-43d5-b39a-edc721fbc1ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: PSA 17:14
Text: From men which are thy hand, O LORD, from men of the world, which have their portion in this life, and whose belly thou fillest with thy hid treasure: they are full of children, and leave the rest of their substance to their babes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/17/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12bfb939-ba3b-4597-8628-d96cab3d8e5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PSA 17:15
Text: As for me, I will behold thy face in righteousness: I shall be satisfied, when I awake, with thy likeness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afb719b3-882b-407a-ac85-a488cc1cf891>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 65

Reference: PSA 18:1
Text: I will love thee, O LORD, my strength.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ce4cbbc-6b33-4559-a889-8af1fb19bcd0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: PSA 18:2
Text: The LORD is my rock, and my fortress, and my deliverer; my God, my strength, in whom I will trust; my buckler, and the horn of my salvation, and my high tower.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da5a7733-5f5b-4f6c-a608-f2f94b96715f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 18:3
Text: I will call upon the LORD, who is worthy to be praised: so shall I be saved from mine enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea5efd58-b865-4aec-8636-cf0b39446c42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 18:4
Text: The sorrows of death compassed me, and the floods of ungodly men made me afraid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:add0216d-8dab-4445-ab31-baa21e2343a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 18:5
Text: The sorrows of hell compassed me about: the snares of death prevented me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8f0c237-f3ef-46f3-be68-73c711fae817>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: PSA 18:6
Text: In my distress I called upon the LORD, and cried unto my God: he heard my voice out of his temple, and my cry came before him, even into his ears.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b8bdd34-0620-42f1-afd2-91e5db67e57f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: PSA 18:7
Text: Then the earth shook and trembled; the foundations also of the hills moved and were shaken, because he was wroth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8f87e9e-b5d1-40d2-bd33-7675c57f6ae0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 18:8
Text: There went up a smoke out of his nostrils, and fire out of his mouth devoured: coals were kindled by it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3963638-c37e-4ae7-9e4d-53a7546164de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 18:9
Text: He bowed the heavens also, and came down: and darkness was under his feet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c84858de-bd97-4888-8657-90b31f4297b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 18:10
Text: And he rode upon a cherub, and did fly: yea, he did fly upon the wings of the wind.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3369988-8a4e-4a7a-9376-cf016ed96874>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: PSA 18:11
Text: He made darkness his secret place; his pavilion round about him were dark waters and thick clouds of the skies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02563055-16b0-4454-83fb-947d92ad5dd1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 18:12
Text: At the brightness that was before him his thick clouds passed, hail stones and coals of fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e26bf1d5-399d-47b1-8ceb-a19cf64145b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 18:13
Text: The LORD also thundered in the heavens, and the Highest gave his voice; hail stones and coals of fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ec329b3-09e4-456c-bfc0-d9a6a0ef4148>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 18:14
Text: Yea, he sent out his arrows, and scattered them; and he shot out lightnings, and discomfited them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cef6522c-5f7a-457d-a783-dafa220572a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: PSA 18:15
Text: Then the channels of waters were seen, and the foundations of the world were discovered at thy rebuke, O LORD, at the blast of the breath of thy nostrils.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd143f71-6ee2-4f9a-ab18-7d97959cd6cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 18:16
Text: He sent from above, he took me, he drew me out of many waters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:577dc86d-5c7e-4eae-bbcc-70d83e479cdb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 18:17
Text: He delivered me from my strong enemy, and from them which hated me: for they were too strong for me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f2ce050-da57-440a-bc87-f6cffcb596ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 18:18
Text: They prevented me in the day of my calamity: but the LORD was my stay.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5122073-4174-483d-a99a-17741f293a46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 18:19
Text: He brought me forth also into a large place; he delivered me, because he delighted in me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d73a794-d252-402c-9f97-57c5255a3503>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: PSA 18:20
Text: The LORD rewarded me according to my righteousness; according to the cleanness of my hands hath he recompensed me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d093ca0b-2bbd-456d-9408-86db5d155fdb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 18:21
Text: For I have kept the ways of the LORD, and have not wickedly departed from my God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28c8941a-2f1d-43a9-8b60-f4ddec2711ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 18:22
Text: For all his judgments were before me, and I did not put away his statutes from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0567be14-e48f-433b-8258-3822d224e12b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 18:23
Text: I was also upright before him, and I kept myself from mine iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a02e239f-9871-40b9-9386-b8c7b95340ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: PSA 18:24
Text: Therefore hath the LORD recompensed me according to my righteousness, according to the cleanness of my hands in his eyesight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4d78bc9-2998-4245-82ca-267ccca6a6dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 18:25
Text: With the merciful thou wilt shew thyself merciful; with an upright man thou wilt shew thyself upright;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0df55011-8a81-4249-b001-7f5d372b0401>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 18:26
Text: With the pure thou wilt shew thyself pure; and with the froward thou wilt shew thyself froward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53b4733d-c717-42d4-99e3-a4f53f71a315>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 18:27
Text: For thou wilt save the afflicted people; but wilt bring down high looks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c605f44-25f8-4c0f-9080-b010a6d192bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 18:28
Text: For thou wilt light my candle: the LORD my God will enlighten my darkness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26e795f4-cc48-4030-b25b-37c7f9869997>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 18:29
Text: For by thee I have run through a troop; and by my God have I leaped over a wall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4e42806-cc12-4ba0-894d-dce29844924a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PSA 18:30
Text: As for God, his way is perfect: the word of the LORD is tried: he is a buckler to all those that trust in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61b1ea6c-2600-4204-93bb-083d3e93f174>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 18:31
Text: For who is God save the LORD? or who is a rock save our God?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3bdffc7-0abc-4d2c-bab8-7f2ca6cacb53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 18:32
Text: It is God that girdeth me with strength, and maketh my way perfect.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:446095dc-9fa0-409d-ac52-26a7c1c3995c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 18:33
Text: He maketh my feet like hinds’ feet, and setteth me upon my high places.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ec60a11-5ebe-4785-832f-841fccf05be7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 18:34
Text: He teacheth my hands to war, so that a bow of steel is broken by mine arms.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:926a6706-7bb8-4d9c-87cd-65bfcc6bd81b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: PSA 18:35
Text: Thou hast also given me the shield of thy salvation: and thy right hand hath holden me up, and thy gentleness hath made me great.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4dbc49d-8c43-4ed2-a417-85d83a078c73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PSA 18:36
Text: Thou hast enlarged my steps under me, that my feet did not slip.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60e428e7-7fca-440d-8f5f-b6b3d7a5b29f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 18:37
Text: I have pursued mine enemies, and overtaken them: neither did I turn again till they were consumed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbab4d4f-57c8-48b6-935b-6ce5220ee25f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 18:38
Text: I have wounded them that they were not able to rise: they are fallen under my feet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9dc2a899-c740-49fe-b8a3-016c3745f176>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: PSA 18:39
Text: For thou hast girded me with strength unto the battle: thou hast subdued under me those that rose up against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1e60c74-f7af-4b66-a99e-cfcfb0b7aedb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 18:40
Text: Thou hast also given me the necks of mine enemies; that I might destroy them that hate me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99157693-3097-42c8-986b-4d1ebeb14bd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 18:41
Text: They cried, but there was none to save them: even unto the LORD, but he answered them not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8eecafe-9111-426d-9a1e-d40d344d66a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 18:42
Text: Then did I beat them small as the dust before the wind: I did cast them out as the dirt in the streets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:683bc5d9-c68c-4551-991a-9d74d5b667e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: PSA 18:43
Text: Thou hast delivered me from the strivings of the people; and thou hast made me the head of the heathen: a people whom I have not known shall serve me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e636608-052d-4be5-a698-eff1161f3c0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 18:44
Text: As soon as they hear of me, they shall obey me: the strangers shall submit themselves unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d16b5de6-85d3-4033-82d8-1e34ba476b6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 18:45
Text: The strangers shall fade away, and be afraid out of their close places.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d221e7bd-9bbe-4a77-93ed-6ac3c4d6e43c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 18:46
Text: The LORD liveth; and blessed be my rock; and let the God of my salvation be exalted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:690bb456-eece-4c57-bbac-275f08ee1724>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 18:47
Text: It is God that avengeth me, and subdueth the people under me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57d7ee02-33f5-404f-a129-663aa70c40b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: PSA 18:48
Text: He delivereth me from mine enemies: yea, thou liftest me up above those that rise up against me: thou hast delivered me from the violent man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b67daeb6-a43b-4df8-8b39-14d08d2993dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 18:49
Text: Therefore will I give thanks unto thee, O LORD, among the heathen, and sing praises unto thy name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/18/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8bbf9001-3b7c-42cd-a289-4859b085f770>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: PSA 18:50
Text: Great deliverance giveth he to his king; and sheweth mercy to his anointed, to David, and to his seed for evermore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/19/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d22982fc-cacd-443d-854c-f49ffc10105c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 19:1
Text: The heavens declare the glory of God; and the firmament sheweth his handywork.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/19/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a7917a9-09b4-408a-bc08-9982b7b4b83c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 19:2
Text: Day unto day uttereth speech, and night unto night sheweth knowledge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/19/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9bd72887-3bff-4d95-9311-97da08c1cf7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 19:3
Text: There is no speech nor language, where their voice is not heard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/19/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36569c58-f1a4-48c3-950e-dae211debbed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: PSA 19:4
Text: Their line is gone out through all the earth, and their words to the end of the world. In them hath he set a tabernacle for the sun,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/19/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57968f61-98e9-4212-9624-9a7fd97bd2f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 19:5
Text: Which is as a bridegroom coming out of his chamber, and rejoiceth as a strong man to run a race.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/19/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d3eb6ef-b675-42d5-aad4-ad89660df495>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: PSA 19:6
Text: His going forth is from the end of the heaven, and his circuit unto the ends of it: and there is nothing hid from the heat thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/19/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71f61527-31fd-4162-8c97-6986154e8f46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PSA 19:7
Text: The law of the LORD is perfect, converting the soul: the testimony of the LORD is sure, making wise the simple.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/19/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10cde4f1-4f9e-4111-af0c-f2555b89f197>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: PSA 19:8
Text: The statutes of the LORD are right, rejoicing the heart: the commandment of the LORD is pure, enlightening the eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/19/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31179725-7f2c-4858-a7eb-a4fe1b7c8c89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: PSA 19:9
Text: The fear of the LORD is clean, enduring for ever: the judgments of the LORD are true and righteous altogether.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/19/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa142892-a5a8-49c1-b889-1fefc2d85b88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PSA 19:10
Text: More to be desired are they than gold, yea, than much fine gold: sweeter also than honey and the honeycomb.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/19/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2914fc08-fa84-48e4-aa4b-de03e3eb0b69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 19:11
Text: Moreover by them is thy servant warned: and in keeping of them there is great reward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/19/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:712b8379-2888-4448-acab-d63f48829d86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 19:12
Text: Who can understand his errors? cleanse thou me from secret faults.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/19/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef7cdb2f-bee1-44f7-822f-db45613a1114>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: PSA 19:13
Text: Keep back thy servant also from presumptuous sins; let them not have dominion over me: then shall I be upright, and I shall be innocent from the great transgression.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/19/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29f795b4-eeef-494b-bcb5-7fab6baf4ce6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: PSA 19:14
Text: Let the words of my mouth, and the meditation of my heart, be acceptable in thy sight, O LORD, my strength, and my redeemer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/20/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a6dcc55-b900-49de-b8fa-587e50a886ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 20:1
Text: The LORD hear thee in the day of trouble; the name of the God of Jacob defend thee;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/20/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8863d56e-4b5d-4c4a-acd3-00f56864b2e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 20:2
Text: Send thee help from the sanctuary, and strengthen thee out of Zion;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/20/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d9aa128-0fc8-49fe-a3c9-a13daa77fedc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 20:3
Text: Remember all thy offerings, and accept thy burnt sacrifice; Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/20/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9ef9332-175b-47d7-8b10-45845ee2d059>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 20:4
Text: Grant thee according to thine own heart, and fulfil all thy counsel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/20/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e7e1ef3-e4ff-4ba5-9a5b-1e6142a3716a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: PSA 20:5
Text: We will rejoice in thy salvation, and in the name of our God we will set up our banners: the LORD fulfil all thy petitions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/20/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7e0a847-0d41-4aad-b5a2-5a5b8887fe41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: PSA 20:6
Text: Now know I that the LORD saveth his anointed; he will hear him from his holy heaven with the saving strength of his right hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/20/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43a9e891-5f18-4c9a-93b9-a63c50918a28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 20:7
Text: Some trust in chariots, and some in horses: but we will remember the name of the LORD our God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/20/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75f73b7d-e429-46ff-820b-699b66c37eb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 20:8
Text: They are brought down and fallen: but we are risen, and stand upright.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/20/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01ad3bf6-749e-42c4-8387-f29e27d83027>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: PSA 20:9
Text: Save, LORD: let the king hear us when we call.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/21/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5dc6617-3d17-41a1-847d-c370cd280914>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 21:1
Text: The king shall joy in thy strength, O LORD; and in thy salvation how greatly shall he rejoice!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/21/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa9e10c6-f690-46ab-a1f6-321ce41b0e18>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 21:2
Text: Thou hast given him his heart’s desire, and hast not withholden the request of his lips. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/21/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0143fd5f-1395-4b60-99df-dc13184174ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PSA 21:3
Text: For thou preventest him with the blessings of goodness: thou settest a crown of pure gold on his head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/21/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c44e938-a66a-40af-954e-1139dd7b26ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 21:4
Text: He asked life of thee, and thou gavest it him, even length of days for ever and ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/21/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:359d3ff4-6dac-48db-9ccd-069d7a1c9188>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 21:5
Text: His glory is great in thy salvation: honour and majesty hast thou laid upon him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/21/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2589d1a0-28b6-4258-aaeb-5c874f41c5b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 21:6
Text: For thou hast made him most blessed for ever: thou hast made him exceeding glad with thy countenance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/21/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0cbf5727-9704-433b-9f59-2932458999e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 21:7
Text: For the king trusteth in the LORD, and through the mercy of the most High he shall not be moved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/21/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b555146d-e8c9-4a23-91df-4ca6eaf54a2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 21:8
Text: Thine hand shall find out all thine enemies: thy right hand shall find out those that hate thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/21/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b9a8e66-fdaf-4725-aa4d-d0df9138a3d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: PSA 21:9
Text: Thou shalt make them as a fiery oven in the time of thine anger: the LORD shall swallow them up in his wrath, and the fire shall devour them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/21/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71b8f28e-0763-4e8b-9423-e6f9df06c666>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 21:10
Text: Their fruit shalt thou destroy from the earth, and their seed from among the children of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/21/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5633b63-d220-44e9-b5c4-f102a1acfb0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PSA 21:11
Text: For they intended evil against thee: they imagined a mischievous device, which they are not able to perform.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/21/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67915dfd-c3ed-4ca7-a114-8b1015e89d97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: PSA 21:12
Text: Therefore shalt thou make them turn their back, when thou shalt make ready thine arrows upon thy strings against the face of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/21/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9dc1bbf2-6a4e-495a-8509-3724d3032c84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 21:13
Text: Be thou exalted, LORD, in thine own strength: so will we sing and praise thy power.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3746ebd-e68d-412a-b59e-40360af98c2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: PSA 22:1
Text: My God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me? why art thou so far from helping me, and from the words of my roaring?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a9c6770-befa-4882-9c98-e876285efc95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 22:2
Text: O my God, I cry in the day time, but thou hearest not; and in the night season, and am not silent.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12bfb6ed-334b-49c5-a870-ff76075fc76c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 22:3
Text: But thou art holy, O thou that inhabitest the praises of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e284c37-939b-45fc-ac73-49c445fb185d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 22:4
Text: Our fathers trusted in thee: they trusted, and thou didst deliver them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a28ab90f-b2d9-4b35-98d3-4f1da299abf3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 22:5
Text: They cried unto thee, and were delivered: they trusted in thee, and were not confounded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8c0f2fe-f822-4cab-a8e1-077fffd684fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 22:6
Text: But I am a worm, and no man; a reproach of men, and despised of the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ff88c61-50ee-4df4-a2ae-9ada0cc63e47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 22:7
Text: All they that see me laugh me to scorn: they shoot out the lip, they shake the head, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4f196bb-f022-4bf8-aa43-e574042da2c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 22:8
Text: He trusted on the LORD that he would deliver him: let him deliver him, seeing he delighted in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:062f0718-caf2-45ed-a210-c2345fb96e67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PSA 22:9
Text: But thou art he that took me out of the womb: thou didst make me hope when I was upon my mother’s breasts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e50936f-f144-49f3-b598-e2246170da45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 22:10
Text: I was cast upon thee from the womb: thou art my God from my mother’s belly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:177baa74-15d5-4806-b557-b1ed939b0a97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 22:11
Text: Be not far from me; for trouble is near; for there is none to help.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65e77614-29a6-4a83-aafe-7b9be9247dff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 22:12
Text: Many bulls have compassed me: strong bulls of Bashan have beset me round.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e91a4c83-f4dd-4a87-8132-52ecc8d7b5b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 22:13
Text: They gaped upon me with their mouths, as a ravening and a roaring lion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77ebc68b-9056-4ebb-b948-9376bd29847b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: PSA 22:14
Text: I am poured out like water, and all my bones are out of joint: my heart is like wax; it is melted in the midst of my bowels.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4613bc6b-5fb3-4985-8037-7c2fc9ac973c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: PSA 22:15
Text: My strength is dried up like a potsherd; and my tongue cleaveth to my jaws; and thou hast brought me into the dust of death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b0b1886-c102-4481-af28-f7af1906ec97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PSA 22:16
Text: For dogs have compassed me: the assembly of the wicked have inclosed me: they pierced my hands and my feet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55053cab-c43e-4f11-8cf6-8bb60f5621ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: PSA 22:17
Text: I may tell all my bones: they look and stare upon me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2afd3e1b-4d5e-4c45-85a4-9b62be09cfdd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PSA 22:18
Text: They part my garments among them, and cast lots upon my vesture.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f37a1900-d616-42de-b2d4-d8e31a3255ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 22:19
Text: But be not thou far from me, O LORD: O my strength, haste thee to help me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc72cfd4-dfa9-4015-8991-e3e5bf94cf61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 22:20
Text: Deliver my soul from the sword; my darling from the power of the dog.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b717beb-7a95-4361-8b4e-e4c4621409c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 22:21
Text: Save me from the lion’s mouth: for thou hast heard me from the horns of the unicorns.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:511943b1-d525-475e-9ff1-08a0e59129e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 22:22
Text: I will declare thy name unto my brethren: in the midst of the congregation will I praise thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bdc04ccf-e75d-4172-9c95-360494bb8b81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: PSA 22:23
Text: Ye that fear the LORD, praise him; all ye the seed of Jacob, glorify him; and fear him, all ye the seed of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f21c1932-fc30-48a8-9392-4bc05896efd2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: PSA 22:24
Text: For he hath not despised nor abhorred the affliction of the afflicted; neither hath he hid his face from him; but when he cried unto him, he heard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1a4ee33-41d6-44af-82fc-54364f7d07c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PSA 22:25
Text: My praise shall be of thee in the great congregation: I will pay my vows before them that fear him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff8328b7-55a9-4b78-8cfe-91391beacded>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PSA 22:26
Text: The meek shall eat and be satisfied: they shall praise the LORD that seek him: your heart shall live for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36610a06-4cfd-4186-9331-b24feb3d69df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: PSA 22:27
Text: All the ends of the world shall remember and turn unto the LORD: and all the kindreds of the nations shall worship before thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f769f240-8311-4c49-ae40-5576a339f08b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 22:28
Text: For the kingdom is the LORD’s: and he is the governor among the nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:232152a9-8586-4aaf-9302-50734c0ee3a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: PSA 22:29
Text: All they that be fat upon earth shall eat and worship: all they that go down to the dust shall bow before him: and none can keep alive his own soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf1be9ce-d723-44bf-8919-3892c43ff4d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 22:30
Text: A seed shall serve him; it shall be accounted to the Lord for a generation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/22/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fce1925e-2d12-4946-a1c7-43a5eeabf4dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PSA 22:31
Text: They shall come, and shall declare his righteousness unto a people that shall be born, that he hath done this.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/23/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35a5fba8-332b-4b6b-b04a-ba22642316bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 69

Reference: PSA 23:1
Text: The LORD is my shepherd; I shall not want.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/23/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2777eac-47ee-4d64-a7bd-ec34b417a867>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 23:2
Text: He maketh me to lie down in green pastures: he leadeth me beside the still waters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/23/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5d791c6-87cf-4901-9e0f-ddb8f997f940>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 23:3
Text: He restoreth my soul: he leadeth me in the paths of righteousness for his name’s sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/23/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ea647ca-ebc4-4b07-99dd-672ca638e282>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: PSA 23:4
Text: Yea, though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, I will fear no evil: for thou art with me; thy rod and thy staff they comfort me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/23/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa6a5c84-a9f3-4d3c-b5a3-890e975c9529>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: PSA 23:5
Text: Thou preparest a table before me in the presence of mine enemies: thou anointest my head with oil; my cup runneth over.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/23/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4cf181b-935b-4552-aa5d-bfdee20c47d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: PSA 23:6
Text: Surely goodness and mercy shall follow me all the days of my life: and I will dwell in the house of the LORD for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/24/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24a47f85-aff8-40f3-b9ca-f82120453838>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 24:1
Text: The earth is the LORD’s, and the fulness thereof; the world, and they that dwell therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/24/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:288a1a2d-b55f-4afc-8552-0557e93d708c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 24:2
Text: For he hath founded it upon the seas, and established it upon the floods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/24/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ded48ab1-7038-4a1c-b061-6c0726e24f54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 24:3
Text: Who shall ascend into the hill of the LORD? or who shall stand in his holy place?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/24/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6db25372-7c74-4aef-95e3-dbb68115d729>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PSA 24:4
Text: He that hath clean hands, and a pure heart; who hath not lifted up his soul unto vanity, nor sworn deceitfully.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/24/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51561cda-3e5f-481e-8ad5-c6dd8a7b118d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 24:5
Text: He shall receive the blessing from the LORD, and righteousness from the God of his salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/24/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32a13d34-de89-42f4-bd81-aa5e39aa85d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 24:6
Text: This is the generation of them that seek him, that seek thy face, O Jacob. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/24/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e492a61-0aa0-412d-82ae-253963dff4c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PSA 24:7
Text: Lift up your heads, O ye gates; and be ye lift up, ye everlasting doors; and the King of glory shall come in.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/24/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d13c4ed2-e0c9-4c98-be2b-28b3ca755d61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 24:8
Text: Who is this King of glory? The LORD strong and mighty, the LORD mighty in battle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/24/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ea8c1f2-c9d3-4448-95a9-4d7886b81c53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PSA 24:9
Text: Lift up your heads, O ye gates; even lift them up, ye everlasting doors; and the King of glory shall come in.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/24/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca0ebfb3-032c-45ba-9358-6399ec8b96bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 24:10
Text: Who is this King of glory? The LORD of hosts, he is the King of glory. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/25/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9afee94-f525-45a4-88c5-6d88d28f81c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 67

Reference: PSA 25:1
Text: Unto thee, O LORD, do I lift up my soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/25/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:937f4e9c-aece-4074-9c38-21ad4b48e01e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 25:2
Text: O my God, I trust in thee: let me not be ashamed, let not mine enemies triumph over me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/25/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be11b506-b3b7-4980-a2f0-e96cd0fa148e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 25:3
Text: Yea, let none that wait on thee be ashamed: let them be ashamed which transgress without cause.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/25/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6047525b-06a5-4e90-b33e-e7e5f6fda010>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 72

Reference: PSA 25:4
Text: Shew me thy ways, O LORD; teach me thy paths.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/25/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a39f6f7c-ef58-4649-a6c7-c526ac888102>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 25:5
Text: Lead me in thy truth, and teach me: for thou art the God of my salvation; on thee do I wait all the day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/25/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c65231a7-8468-43d8-913b-2dae6f856e75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 25:6
Text: Remember, O LORD, thy tender mercies and thy lovingkindnesses; for they have been ever of old.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/25/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8bfe4b06-af90-4d8f-8653-262174042e7a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: PSA 25:7
Text: Remember not the sins of my youth, nor my transgressions: according to thy mercy remember thou me for thy goodness’ sake, O LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/25/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68073dfb-d792-48c8-9481-fc1476c3c8da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 25:8
Text: Good and upright is the LORD: therefore will he teach sinners in the way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/25/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eed13b70-37bd-4d79-9242-a132f3bd0fb1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 25:9
Text: The meek will he guide in judgment: and the meek will he teach his way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/25/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9446566d-d5d9-4056-9705-d0580782ea12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 25:10
Text: All the paths of the LORD are mercy and truth unto such as keep his covenant and his testimonies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/25/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57354527-fbd1-4dcf-93be-917483356a5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 25:11
Text: For thy name’s sake, O LORD, pardon mine iniquity; for it is great.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/25/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:666410eb-e358-465a-b429-96cb2367d6d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 25:12
Text: What man is he that feareth the LORD? him shall he teach in the way that he shall choose.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/25/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ba6ce0d-717a-4881-80f6-31f13aef1460>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 25:13
Text: His soul shall dwell at ease; and his seed shall inherit the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/25/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49150fa0-49b0-453d-9b4b-9b8129024cd5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 25:14
Text: The secret of the LORD is with them that fear him; and he will shew them his covenant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/25/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4884b2c5-d7c4-48ce-9446-90ad7df6b763>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 25:15
Text: Mine eyes are ever toward the LORD; for he shall pluck my feet out of the net.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/25/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00dd9280-a3c4-4013-81fd-e417c17961a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 25:16
Text: Turn thee unto me, and have mercy upon me; for I am desolate and afflicted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/25/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fee004dc-87d1-4c14-a42f-3627664a9ef1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 25:17
Text: The troubles of my heart are enlarged: O bring thou me out of my distresses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/25/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7dcbdfdd-e04e-43f4-a0dc-1fa83d3e0750>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 25:18
Text: Look upon mine affliction and my pain; and forgive all my sins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/25/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a41fb83-a6a1-44cd-abc3-92f6423510b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 25:19
Text: Consider mine enemies; for they are many; and they hate me with cruel hatred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/25/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd468ca4-f6b8-4f81-8455-bb96e6d62858>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 25:20
Text: O keep my soul, and deliver me: let me not be ashamed; for I put my trust in thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/25/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c27eecb-8375-4774-ac9f-a38a7e2a8252>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 25:21
Text: Let integrity and uprightness preserve me; for I wait on thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/25/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1173ada7-6fe6-4da4-b18e-69c443774e87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: PSA 25:22
Text: Redeem Israel, O God, out of all his troubles.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/26/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abe01b09-df34-403f-b581-2918d6ad9fc7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: PSA 26:1
Text: Judge me, O LORD; for I have walked in mine integrity: I have trusted also in the LORD; therefore I shall not slide.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/26/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e64a3b72-5036-40e3-98b4-3c38d5a72471>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PSA 26:2
Text: Examine me, O LORD, and prove me; try my reins and my heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/26/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:295dc845-aa58-467e-8866-ba3a1d848dc3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 26:3
Text: For thy lovingkindness is before mine eyes: and I have walked in thy truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/26/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b82bed5-7b0c-4c5f-834c-b1b02e1d3318>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 26:4
Text: I have not sat with vain persons, neither will I go in with dissemblers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/26/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:869de091-3711-443d-ab74-c16c9c50bbbb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 26:5
Text: I have hated the congregation of evil doers; and will not sit with the wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/26/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8ff8b8c-a0ed-48ba-89d9-b34488ba7602>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 26:6
Text: I will wash mine hands in innocency: so will I compass thine altar, O LORD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/26/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d668e38f-b1d0-46be-8fc9-a933c12c83bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 26:7
Text: That I may publish with the voice of thanksgiving, and tell of all thy wondrous works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/26/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ab2faad-fee6-425c-a438-ca950214c127>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 26:8
Text: LORD, I have loved the habitation of thy house, and the place where thine honour dwelleth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/26/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:030375db-7302-49af-be4f-746eece81cd4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 26:9
Text: Gather not my soul with sinners, nor my life with bloody men:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/26/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b87b4a3-9a11-408f-b9f7-5e950e9bb714>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 26:10
Text: In whose hands is mischief, and their right hand is full of bribes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/26/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e8ca6d4-53c5-49aa-8811-b5af136eb34e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 26:11
Text: But as for me, I will walk in mine integrity: redeem me, and be merciful unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/26/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9428b479-49d4-4ae3-9d49-b815ddd83701>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 26:12
Text: My foot standeth in an even place: in the congregations will I bless the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/27/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ab08bcb-bd7a-4ee8-94dc-42456dffe5b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: PSA 27:1
Text: The LORD is my light and my salvation; whom shall I fear? the LORD is the strength of my life; of whom shall I be afraid?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/27/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f0e4e68-0004-4953-a1e6-24d5b7546185>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 27:2
Text: When the wicked, even mine enemies and my foes, came upon me to eat up my flesh, they stumbled and fell.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/27/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2fb25af-08a9-4b1f-b544-3fee981fdd5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: PSA 27:3
Text: Though an host should encamp against me, my heart shall not fear: though war should rise against me, in this will I be confident.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/27/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee53716a-551a-49b9-b15f-b6a3435f6cd9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: PSA 27:4
Text: One thing have I desired of the LORD, that will I seek after; that I may dwell in the house of the LORD all the days of my life, to behold the beauty of the LORD, and to enquire in his temple.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/27/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:358a86ae-3c5c-462b-b17d-dbd9ef4f6221>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: PSA 27:5
Text: For in the time of trouble he shall hide me in his pavilion: in the secret of his tabernacle shall he hide me; he shall set me up upon a rock.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/27/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:113bd95e-1e7c-47ec-8547-c6ec15812aec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: PSA 27:6
Text: And now shall mine head be lifted up above mine enemies round about me: therefore will I offer in his tabernacle sacrifices of joy; I will sing, yea, I will sing praises unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/27/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:464aadec-d598-4340-9bc9-33aacf0318a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 27:7
Text: Hear, O LORD, when I cry with my voice: have mercy also upon me, and answer me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/27/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42205176-1902-46c7-a728-3ab08fbd7513>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 27:8
Text: When thou saidst, Seek ye my face; my heart said unto thee, Thy face, LORD, will I seek.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/27/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c231bde9-fe42-4311-82fd-ee210ee8317d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: PSA 27:9
Text: Hide not thy face far from me; put not thy servant away in anger: thou hast been my help; leave me not, neither forsake me, O God of my salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/27/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e304e020-b8c5-49b1-ae93-eb71e351ad03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 27:10
Text: When my father and my mother forsake me, then the LORD will take me up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/27/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31c3bc23-e5ef-4ebf-8e39-8170b36e58fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 27:11
Text: Teach me thy way, O LORD, and lead me in a plain path, because of mine enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/27/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:530e2d54-8fac-4513-8a79-8630bce77964>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: PSA 27:12
Text: Deliver me not over unto the will of mine enemies: for false witnesses are risen up against me, and such as breathe out cruelty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/27/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e2b47f0-440f-4080-8b21-8541e26487b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 27:13
Text: I had fainted, unless I had believed to see the goodness of the LORD in the land of the living.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/27/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df51ebd8-b9c8-4bd5-8837-567c6f67c1e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 27:14
Text: Wait on the LORD: be of good courage, and he shall strengthen thine heart: wait, I say, on the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/28/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68ddc0f7-16d6-465a-90ff-d178fc3a294f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: PSA 28:1
Text: Unto thee will I cry, O LORD my rock; be not silent to me: lest, if thou be silent to me, I become like them that go down into the pit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/28/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b116dd6-a9f3-42d3-abad-e4241750e412>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 28:2
Text: Hear the voice of my supplications, when I cry unto thee, when I lift up my hands toward thy holy oracle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/28/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:146a9648-ea33-4f9d-b80c-43fe7661c3db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: PSA 28:3
Text: Draw me not away with the wicked, and with the workers of iniquity, which speak peace to their neighbours, but mischief is in their hearts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/28/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f078756-2ac4-457c-b43c-c2fac441cfe3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: PSA 28:4
Text: Give them according to their deeds, and according to the wickedness of their endeavours: give them after the work of their hands; render to them their desert.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/28/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9f040bf-b5d0-43d5-b0df-a39a7347663e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: PSA 28:5
Text: Because they regard not the works of the LORD, nor the operation of his hands, he shall destroy them, and not build them up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/28/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7eba61aa-d866-4157-99cb-62b1bff8ec84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 28:6
Text: Blessed be the LORD, because he hath heard the voice of my supplications.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/28/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef48dba8-1c21-4630-8c47-d21334a19430>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: PSA 28:7
Text: The LORD is my strength and my shield; my heart trusted in him, and I am helped: therefore my heart greatly rejoiceth; and with my song will I praise him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/28/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40b89bf5-1603-4def-809e-0a55a7cfc1b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 28:8
Text: The LORD is their strength, and he is the saving strength of his anointed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/28/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62c34b3d-0bb6-437a-8172-e87791362a5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 28:9
Text: Save thy people, and bless thine inheritance: feed them also, and lift them up for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/29/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:818f0185-b358-439b-a5b4-584f77383850>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 29:1
Text: Give unto the LORD, O ye mighty, give unto the LORD glory and strength.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/29/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4c331ac-4fd2-48f0-9a1c-7b74d77c11ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 29:2
Text: Give unto the LORD the glory due unto his name; worship the LORD in the beauty of holiness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/29/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65a245a4-a2dd-496a-959b-ab7731e65bad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PSA 29:3
Text: The voice of the LORD is upon the waters: the God of glory thundereth: the LORD is upon many waters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/29/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54cb9943-e1d7-48a7-a393-d3637342cf95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 29:4
Text: The voice of the LORD is powerful; the voice of the LORD is full of majesty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/29/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be981fc4-96b5-46d5-957e-617668c53148>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 29:5
Text: The voice of the LORD breaketh the cedars; yea, the LORD breaketh the cedars of Lebanon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/29/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:beaa13ec-3cec-4879-8467-2dbb7cf0d9ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 29:6
Text: He maketh them also to skip like a calf; Lebanon and Sirion like a young unicorn.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/29/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d974adcc-cdba-494c-9c0a-1f8235f81514>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: PSA 29:7
Text: The voice of the LORD divideth the flames of fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/29/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d682eec-6a50-47a6-8558-c07e8b123581>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 29:8
Text: The voice of the LORD shaketh the wilderness; the LORD shaketh the wilderness of Kadesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/29/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3dbc72b0-9feb-41c7-968a-aa742a6737f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: PSA 29:9
Text: The voice of the LORD maketh the hinds to calve, and discovereth the forests: and in his temple doth every one speak of his glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/29/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08e89284-15e3-4338-b304-e9c3fe69fb53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 29:10
Text: The LORD sitteth upon the flood; yea, the LORD sitteth King for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/29/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26f8954e-c9e3-45f0-ba7d-fa921c11984d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 29:11
Text: The LORD will give strength unto his people; the LORD will bless his people with peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/30/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cafa3443-8230-4a5b-bba8-27b3174d4b19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PSA 30:1
Text: I will extol thee, O LORD; for thou hast lifted me up, and hast not made my foes to rejoice over me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/30/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ae57d9b-c413-4ab0-99b3-93d3ea7eae2b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: PSA 30:2
Text: O LORD my God, I cried unto thee, and thou hast healed me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/30/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21eb47a2-8e4f-4ea6-b51f-c4de65f62ae5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: PSA 30:3
Text: O LORD, thou hast brought up my soul from the grave: thou hast kept me alive, that I should not go down to the pit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/30/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:239c6d4f-3086-4c62-a7d2-2b9ad5af4b81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 30:4
Text: Sing unto the LORD, O ye saints of his, and give thanks at the remembrance of his holiness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/30/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b93d2c4-e939-408e-8ba2-0634ce3ab6bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: PSA 30:5
Text: For his anger endureth but a moment; in his favour is life: weeping may endure for a night, but joy cometh in the morning.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/30/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1a6e319-6f44-4506-b074-e4f562bcf99a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: PSA 30:6
Text: And in my prosperity I said, I shall never be moved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/30/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7f1c8bc-896a-4b0a-b666-d96f12a408b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PSA 30:7
Text: LORD, by thy favour thou hast made my mountain to stand strong: thou didst hide thy face, and I was troubled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/30/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce47fdd3-afd5-404e-8d52-a0695ed0275f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 30:8
Text: I cried to thee, O LORD; and unto the LORD I made supplication.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/30/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1db51d2f-a7bc-499a-afb1-6819bfd3d852>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: PSA 30:9
Text: What profit is there in my blood, when I go down to the pit? Shall the dust praise thee? shall it declare thy truth?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/30/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8065c7a6-f131-4509-8a05-844f4bee0259>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 30:10
Text: Hear, O LORD, and have mercy upon me: LORD, be thou my helper.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/30/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8f51f16-45fd-4eee-ba97-06693ba95ea6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PSA 30:11
Text: Thou hast turned for me my mourning into dancing: thou hast put off my sackcloth, and girded me with gladness;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/30/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e6e4c96-ad12-405a-a4d9-e90b5dbfd7c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: PSA 30:12
Text: To the end that my glory may sing praise to thee, and not be silent. O LORD my God, I will give thanks unto thee for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd1e8990-825f-4e52-aa3b-fcfaf73ea92f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 31:1
Text: In thee, O LORD, do I put my trust; let me never be ashamed: deliver me in thy righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9880271-ab3e-45f9-9285-1950ee1ca0de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: PSA 31:2
Text: Bow down thine ear to me; deliver me speedily: be thou my strong rock, for an house of defence to save me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8f7bbfe-98d7-4241-bb41-676da4bb4ea2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 31:3
Text: For thou art my rock and my fortress; therefore for thy name’s sake lead me, and guide me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4b7459b-a3f0-4056-ae53-3e21e4c0e5da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 31:4
Text: Pull me out of the net that they have laid privily for me: for thou art my strength.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9bc0865-1118-4abc-b300-22a88d2a76a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 31:5
Text: Into thine hand I commit my spirit: thou hast redeemed me, O LORD God of truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c07b0e1-6cae-4f3f-8d01-67f642973478>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 31:6
Text: I have hated them that regard lying vanities: but I trust in the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da6b77bd-fa4d-444a-868e-e22d3b54d06f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: PSA 31:7
Text: I will be glad and rejoice in thy mercy: for thou hast considered my trouble; thou hast known my soul in adversities;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7db08ebf-688f-4758-9173-df98fd8c978e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 31:8
Text: And hast not shut me up into the hand of the enemy: thou hast set my feet in a large room.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05c418f8-e183-42a1-95ee-220b8c6d4323>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PSA 31:9
Text: Have mercy upon me, O LORD, for I am in trouble: mine eye is consumed with grief, yea, my soul and my belly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04f79ea8-1705-427f-b24b-8486749c1c53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: PSA 31:10
Text: For my life is spent with grief, and my years with sighing: my strength faileth because of mine iniquity, and my bones are consumed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9996fab7-eb5c-405f-a540-add1da13b534>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: PSA 31:11
Text: I was a reproach among all mine enemies, but especially among my neighbours, and a fear to mine acquaintance: they that did see me without fled from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef535576-66c6-475b-80c4-43a1001367bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 31:12
Text: I am forgotten as a dead man out of mind: I am like a broken vessel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0283f212-97a9-4794-a578-121095940248>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: PSA 31:13
Text: For I have heard the slander of many: fear was on every side: while they took counsel together against me, they devised to take away my life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35dda6a5-a0cd-494b-b7d5-da8d1336c656>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: PSA 31:14
Text: But I trusted in thee, O LORD: I said, Thou art my God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abb73ff9-6ec2-49dc-a0bc-3d25425c3506>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 31:15
Text: My times are in thy hand: deliver me from the hand of mine enemies, and from them that persecute me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f3d91bc-518d-4a77-bacb-6073697a8a49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 31:16
Text: Make thy face to shine upon thy servant: save me for thy mercies’ sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:943f0dd6-0464-481f-bf7f-762f56acb9c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: PSA 31:17
Text: Let me not be ashamed, O LORD; for I have called upon thee: let the wicked be ashamed, and let them be silent in the grave.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d9969de-4251-49e5-954a-b4e1ba26708a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: PSA 31:18
Text: Let the lying lips be put to silence; which speak grievous things proudly and contemptuously against the righteous.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54e32eed-33af-4f33-8363-aca99b67052d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: PSA 31:19
Text: Oh how great is thy goodness, which thou hast laid up for them that fear thee; which thou hast wrought for them that trust in thee before the sons of men!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0c87993-09e2-4275-95be-2ddc661a5699>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: PSA 31:20
Text: Thou shalt hide them in the secret of thy presence from the pride of man: thou shalt keep them secretly in a pavilion from the strife of tongues.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69c72eb1-110d-4d06-83b1-486dfe4e0acc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 31:21
Text: Blessed be the LORD: for he hath shewed me his marvellous kindness in a strong city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:102b4227-241d-46a1-8c71-19dee25fc5b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: PSA 31:22
Text: For I said in my haste, I am cut off from before thine eyes: nevertheless thou heardest the voice of my supplications when I cried unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6a20df8-b1b7-4f45-8007-f81ce5cd26fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: PSA 31:23
Text: O love the LORD, all ye his saints: for the LORD preserveth the faithful, and plentifully rewardeth the proud doer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/31/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0650e0e4-a48d-4cfe-822f-73728a6ed856>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 31:24
Text: Be of good courage, and he shall strengthen your heart, all ye that hope in the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/32/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e5508f8-129e-454c-a123-00df59fa19a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 32:1
Text: Blessed is he whose transgression is forgiven, whose sin is covered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/32/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d0e2ab1-cfd8-469e-835d-5da3e286c587>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 32:2
Text: Blessed is the man unto whom the LORD imputeth not iniquity, and in whose spirit there is no guile.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/32/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e32de5c5-39b8-40b4-8989-8c28a16a511e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 32:3
Text: When I kept silence, my bones waxed old through my roaring all the day long.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/32/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4b2545c-00c9-438a-9b9f-6ae63fe9d2e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PSA 32:4
Text: For day and night thy hand was heavy upon me: my moisture is turned into the drought of summer. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/32/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d6ccd9f-7d08-47dd-b61a-946c7067bce0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: PSA 32:5
Text: I acknowledge my sin unto thee, and mine iniquity have I not hid. I said, I will confess my transgressions unto the LORD; and thou forgavest the iniquity of my sin. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/32/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cfa3950-da56-415b-8b56-055abc601f6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: PSA 32:6
Text: For this shall every one that is godly pray unto thee in a time when thou mayest be found: surely in the floods of great waters they shall not come nigh unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/32/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1589a279-116e-4591-abd7-0db9c55bf3d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: PSA 32:7
Text: Thou art my hiding place; thou shalt preserve me from trouble; thou shalt compass me about with songs of deliverance. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/32/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9873d2c-8485-47f0-be12-6437d033220e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PSA 32:8
Text: I will instruct thee and teach thee in the way which thou shalt go: I will guide thee with mine eye.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/32/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:045902ed-0d3c-4f20-a2b9-57d658ae2e88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: PSA 32:9
Text: Be ye not as the horse, or as the mule, which have no understanding: whose mouth must be held in with bit and bridle, lest they come near unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/32/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b29a5a2-2897-452e-b689-e24f712b77a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PSA 32:10
Text: Many sorrows shall be to the wicked: but he that trusteth in the LORD, mercy shall compass him about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/32/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12f5c415-8c97-4a6b-9369-6eec7e1c80b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 32:11
Text: Be glad in the LORD, and rejoice, ye righteous: and shout for joy, all ye that are upright in heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/33/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e2d8ce8-6c36-446c-adce-7b64e87a4117>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 33:1
Text: Rejoice in the LORD, O ye righteous: for praise is comely for the upright.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/33/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4c0cd43-98d6-452f-8a25-4b0606786a1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 33:2
Text: Praise the LORD with harp: sing unto him with the psaltery and an instrument of ten strings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/33/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ce764d5-ccfd-4048-94ad-173628456e77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PSA 33:3
Text: Sing unto him a new song; play skilfully with a loud noise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/33/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:060423b7-6dce-4118-839f-f041f42e2268>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 33:4
Text: For the word of the LORD is right; and all his works are done in truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/33/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80532f8e-d62c-484c-8541-862c7cafef6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 33:5
Text: He loveth righteousness and judgment: the earth is full of the goodness of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/33/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85faeb03-07ee-453c-893e-c3fc8221d397>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 33:6
Text: By the word of the LORD were the heavens made; and all the host of them by the breath of his mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/33/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e874a4f-93eb-4faa-bdc1-081e855652e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 33:7
Text: He gathereth the waters of the sea together as an heap: he layeth up the depth in storehouses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/33/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fbba81b-01fb-4fbb-b88a-a83933037de4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 33:8
Text: Let all the earth fear the LORD: let all the inhabitants of the world stand in awe of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/33/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f410161-c821-4e06-92b6-43c7fdcbee1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 33:9
Text: For he spake, and it was done; he commanded, and it stood fast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/33/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f12b69ea-a675-4b4c-bc39-c8f94b21ef25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PSA 33:10
Text: The LORD bringeth the counsel of the heathen to nought: he maketh the devices of the people of none effect.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/33/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:729c8b3f-65a8-46b9-9917-ec9ab0fb7336>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 33:11
Text: The counsel of the LORD standeth for ever, the thoughts of his heart to all generations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/33/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:849dd5b6-5547-445b-907d-1f8d5ed8ca36>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 33:12
Text: Blessed is the nation whose God is the LORD; and the people whom he hath chosen for his own inheritance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/33/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8bb63f5-09cf-4dcb-b203-28bb23854be9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 33:13
Text: The LORD looketh from heaven; he beholdeth all the sons of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/33/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54ea90dc-22ce-497c-91f3-538c81c1c240>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 33:14
Text: From the place of his habitation he looketh upon all the inhabitants of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/33/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3734592f-8a0a-4fec-941e-915c037f6ffb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 33:15
Text: He fashioneth their hearts alike; he considereth all their works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/33/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ff80ec9-1059-46f1-9061-14a0095f80e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PSA 33:16
Text: There is no king saved by the multitude of an host: a mighty man is not delivered by much strength.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/33/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43baa033-a58e-4dd8-87a3-0a76b66a2ead>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 33:17
Text: An horse is a vain thing for safety: neither shall he deliver any by his great strength.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/33/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bef1bf9-ea48-4ccb-91b2-747d63b40288>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 33:18
Text: Behold, the eye of the LORD is upon them that fear him, upon them that hope in his mercy;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/33/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae9e42ef-0fd2-476e-a069-517d6d51a5ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 33:19
Text: To deliver their soul from death, and to keep them alive in famine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/33/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f543096-37af-4e67-a44a-27707be78e99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 33:20
Text: Our soul waiteth for the LORD: he is our help and our shield.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/33/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d56110c-c0b8-4528-ba97-d7cfe55665ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 33:21
Text: For our heart shall rejoice in him, because we have trusted in his holy name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/33/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2ec67e3-ae3a-4e9d-9f20-a3b4a76bdb69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PSA 33:22
Text: Let thy mercy, O LORD, be upon us, according as we hope in thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/34/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc5e407a-038a-414e-ad94-c2865592c787>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 34:1
Text: I will bless the LORD at all times: his praise shall continually be in my mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/34/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d508a32b-bade-4c61-917d-9edd65dfd9e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 34:2
Text: My soul shall make her boast in the LORD: the humble shall hear thereof, and be glad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/34/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d49add1-5046-4b77-bd66-53d1ae4a36b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 34:3
Text: O magnify the LORD with me, and let us exalt his name together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/34/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a8353bf-ae45-4380-9e7d-5c7cb8472067>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 34:4
Text: I sought the LORD, and he heard me, and delivered me from all my fears.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/34/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4653db00-00b5-47ef-b377-c704304fe6ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 34:5
Text: They looked unto him, and were lightened: and their faces were not ashamed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/34/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a2e1f43-24e9-46b7-9be0-997ec8d72c37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 34:6
Text: This poor man cried, and the LORD heard him, and saved him out of all his troubles.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/34/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0bfd516-9f79-4460-a3ea-6c078beef910>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 34:7
Text: The angel of the LORD encampeth round about them that fear him, and delivereth them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/34/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2c37eae-ee1c-4b8f-802e-6503ff0738af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 34:8
Text: O taste and see that the LORD is good: blessed is the man that trusteth in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/34/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb7b4e5e-c2c7-453a-ba92-f654f955ea38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 34:9
Text: O fear the LORD, ye his saints: for there is no want to them that fear him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/34/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49567d9a-2731-4c0f-8ead-45a2f0fadb59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 34:10
Text: The young lions do lack, and suffer hunger: but they that seek the LORD shall not want any good thing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/34/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:663910a2-fee4-4b40-95ce-26f275d2f304>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 34:11
Text: Come, ye children, hearken unto me: I will teach you the fear of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/34/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e685f03-c6e3-4e2b-9dcf-f13aa52b721d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 34:12
Text: What man is he that desireth life, and loveth many days, that he may see good?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/34/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42d77519-b9ef-4c0b-b63f-ac63e43488d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 34:13
Text: Keep thy tongue from evil, and thy lips from speaking guile.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/34/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28d10750-faf7-497f-a143-36c61d68e7d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: PSA 34:14
Text: Depart from evil, and do good; seek peace, and pursue it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/34/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bc2acdf-d367-4b78-b43c-a9db27b0dfd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 34:15
Text: The eyes of the LORD are upon the righteous, and his ears are open unto their cry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/34/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61edd3ce-c99e-4665-aa92-28149fc44688>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PSA 34:16
Text: The face of the LORD is against them that do evil, to cut off the remembrance of them from the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/34/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6a83322-ef49-4c43-87e3-723959bf52d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 34:17
Text: The righteous cry, and the LORD heareth, and delivereth them out of all their troubles.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/34/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72675019-eac6-42cd-8d96-b960b4a0dff3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 34:18
Text: The LORD is nigh unto them that are of a broken heart; and saveth such as be of a contrite spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/34/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3271cd3f-a0b8-4ff4-9e76-a4b684e54edb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 34:19
Text: Many are the afflictions of the righteous: but the LORD delivereth him out of them all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/34/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e90383b6-c267-499d-825d-cdd48093480a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: PSA 34:20
Text: He keepeth all his bones: not one of them is broken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/34/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ba393ce-ded6-49d9-a187-aeb1ed647de4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 34:21
Text: Evil shall slay the wicked: and they that hate the righteous shall be desolate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/34/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9cafbe1-fbcd-4972-bdc2-53d2332c5469>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 34:22
Text: The LORD redeemeth the soul of his servants: and none of them that trust in him shall be desolate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38d20214-37cf-4293-9379-c65366c66a0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 35:1
Text: Plead my cause, O LORD, with them that strive with me: fight against them that fight against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:960ff201-21ea-4d5d-8af6-c49e9af6d5ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PSA 35:2
Text: Take hold of shield and buckler, and stand up for mine help.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2546ba53-6aac-4c1b-82ef-27719197fcb9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PSA 35:3
Text: Draw out also the spear, and stop the way against them that persecute me: say unto my soul, I am thy salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76c901c0-2b42-4bc2-8929-5e3027df11d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: PSA 35:4
Text: Let them be confounded and put to shame that seek after my soul: let them be turned back and brought to confusion that devise my hurt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:452ba9fc-99f1-4b88-bb7a-5f476390c8d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 35:5
Text: Let them be as chaff before the wind: and let the angel of the LORD chase them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:073a825a-095f-4c10-a55e-3a72715be72b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 35:6
Text: Let their way be dark and slippery: and let the angel of the LORD persecute them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c3bcc8f-e448-4523-8c76-297f309c0a68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PSA 35:7
Text: For without cause have they hid for me their net in a pit, which without cause they have digged for my soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a15ecdf-9e2c-4d90-8280-2d87716b3bfb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: PSA 35:8
Text: Let destruction come upon him at unawares; and let his net that he hath hid catch himself: into that very destruction let him fall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f9ae671-01e0-41e0-9701-2c5508421a3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 35:9
Text: And my soul shall be joyful in the LORD: it shall rejoice in his salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0f79a0e-4bee-47a6-8ccb-f6c316682b95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: PSA 35:10
Text: All my bones shall say, LORD, who is like unto thee, which deliverest the poor from him that is too strong for him, yea, the poor and the needy from him that spoileth him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbed36d1-a721-4c1c-8de9-83207ff975c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 35:11
Text: False witnesses did rise up; they laid to my charge things that I knew not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8c69e6a-1cf9-465b-bd35-6c2f7be83ba8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PSA 35:12
Text: They rewarded me evil for good to the spoiling of my soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b830cf70-bb43-40e9-9e00-df86d8564abb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: PSA 35:13
Text: But as for me, when they were sick, my clothing was sackcloth: I humbled my soul with fasting; and my prayer returned into mine own bosom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61159578-b115-4f25-a5a1-5a4eb2b21fe7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: PSA 35:14
Text: I behaved myself as though he had been my friend or brother: I bowed down heavily, as one that mourneth for his mother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a72c40b-b8ec-45ac-9315-d59f37839cce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: PSA 35:15
Text: But in mine adversity they rejoiced, and gathered themselves together: yea, the abjects gathered themselves together against me, and I knew it not; they did tear me, and ceased not:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba027f85-938c-4f32-8745-92566d80dcd9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 35:16
Text: With hypocritical mockers in feasts, they gnashed upon me with their teeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9cec81ac-d686-4e9c-a946-88b4005dfebf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 35:17
Text: Lord, how long wilt thou look on? rescue my soul from their destructions, my darling from the lions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b35b5081-524b-4978-b71c-f01415d13b33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 35:18
Text: I will give thee thanks in the great congregation: I will praise thee among much people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ad8c9f0-0901-4d01-b27b-54eb28705f22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: PSA 35:19
Text: Let not them that are mine enemies wrongfully rejoice over me: neither let them wink with the eye that hate me without a cause.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fcf4d84-bfa6-439a-b223-b26a574b1366>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 35:20
Text: For they speak not peace: but they devise deceitful matters against them that are quiet in the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c668da1b-dbf8-4991-a0e6-5f44e0ac3840>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 35:21
Text: Yea, they opened their mouth wide against me, and said, Aha, aha, our eye hath seen it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c59b6442-fc59-4269-95b9-fdf38f51bbef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 35:22
Text: This thou hast seen, O LORD: keep not silence: O Lord, be not far from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bbdc477d-2634-409e-a5a8-1aadd5820152>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 35:23
Text: Stir up thyself, and awake to my judgment, even unto my cause, my God and my Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3924766-e044-4bc7-a08b-a849dc46c8cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 35:24
Text: Judge me, O LORD my God, according to thy righteousness; and let them not rejoice over me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13d3178c-716f-4c55-b74a-7622974b80cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 35:25
Text: Let them not say in their hearts, Ah, so would we have it: let them not say, We have swallowed him up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18a25f2d-ae03-4ed9-a78b-8e9d74c07923>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: PSA 35:26
Text: Let them be ashamed and brought to confusion together that rejoice at mine hurt: let them be clothed with shame and dishonour that magnify themselves against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:041222d6-cf9e-47c6-b871-f9cdb8463c73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: PSA 35:27
Text: Let them shout for joy, and be glad, that favour my righteous cause: yea, let them say continually, Let the LORD be magnified, which hath pleasure in the prosperity of his servant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/35/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9de64975-6f72-4cac-bcdc-6c4f6e5b092b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 35:28
Text: And my tongue shall speak of thy righteousness and of thy praise all the day long.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/36/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46d18d60-32bd-483a-a419-c992ac28caeb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PSA 36:1
Text: The transgression of the wicked saith within my heart, that there is no fear of God before his eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/36/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:774c1d3c-c7cb-40d8-8914-f2aeafd95fa4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 36:2
Text: For he flattereth himself in his own eyes, until his iniquity be found to be hateful.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/36/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7047fcb9-6c56-41ac-9b55-99916ad0c9ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 36:3
Text: The words of his mouth are iniquity and deceit: he hath left off to be wise, and to do good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/36/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fba4723d-cdb4-4dd4-8a1c-67ef10a99c21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 36:4
Text: He deviseth mischief upon his bed; he setteth himself in a way that is not good; he abhorreth not evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/36/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c920d9b2-04a5-4daf-a59a-39643eba636d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 36:5
Text: Thy mercy, O LORD, is in the heavens; and thy faithfulness reacheth unto the clouds.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/36/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93c74697-f228-4d3c-8c05-754601d6151b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: PSA 36:6
Text: Thy righteousness is like the great mountains; thy judgments are a great deep: O LORD, thou preservest man and beast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/36/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28d40724-142b-4d36-b955-69eb8fa6358d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: PSA 36:7
Text: How excellent is thy lovingkindness, O God! therefore the children of men put their trust under the shadow of thy wings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/36/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c67ec93-a0d9-4ea3-9fbc-5f0106e3cbfb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: PSA 36:8
Text: They shall be abundantly satisfied with the fatness of thy house; and thou shalt make them drink of the river of thy pleasures.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/36/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f15a788-7b88-47c7-9390-2ff554862138>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 36:9
Text: For with thee is the fountain of life: in thy light shall we see light.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/36/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:329e267f-4b56-4fe0-b620-176ece01e690>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 36:10
Text: O continue thy lovingkindness unto them that know thee; and thy righteousness to the upright in heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/36/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c886f742-b789-46ca-8c8f-2b73c1ada8ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 36:11
Text: Let not the foot of pride come against me, and let not the hand of the wicked remove me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/36/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d283bd0-ea5e-4ec2-a110-43683f3a73ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 36:12
Text: There are the workers of iniquity fallen: they are cast down, and shall not be able to rise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da27d248-8e89-46c2-a107-6111eeb2d4ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 37:1
Text: Fret not thyself because of evildoers, neither be thou envious against the workers of iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b6ad581-7e6c-4b55-aa09-307937123cd2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 37:2
Text: For they shall soon be cut down like the grass, and wither as the green herb.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea9e3b50-8bb9-4574-bf8a-f58cdc9c6b4f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 37:3
Text: Trust in the LORD, and do good; so shalt thou dwell in the land, and verily thou shalt be fed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c140931d-735b-4e56-a29c-e09e0ddc6d23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 37:4
Text: Delight thyself also in the LORD: and he shall give thee the desires of thine heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66d9ad4e-5281-4a1c-980a-ceb232841870>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 37:5
Text: Commit thy way unto the LORD; trust also in him; and he shall bring it to pass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5dfd2b1-5f5c-4457-8d92-b26450ee08b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 37:6
Text: And he shall bring forth thy righteousness as the light, and thy judgment as the noonday.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1bf264b4-ed86-4e07-8757-5f2a19b6f21c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: PSA 37:7
Text: Rest in the LORD, and wait patiently for him: fret not thyself because of him who prospereth in his way, because of the man who bringeth wicked devices to pass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d80e8987-6c82-425d-bd75-95c796ae59ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 37:8
Text: Cease from anger, and forsake wrath: fret not thyself in any wise to do evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17d7209f-2081-4f8c-be0e-9fe7eb424427>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 37:9
Text: For evildoers shall be cut off: but those that wait upon the LORD, they shall inherit the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31dbb5f1-7065-4294-952a-d9376af2a426>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: PSA 37:10
Text: For yet a little while, and the wicked shall not be: yea, thou shalt diligently consider his place, and it shall not be.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b903653f-4496-41b6-846e-be174c23c297>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 37:11
Text: But the meek shall inherit the earth; and shall delight themselves in the abundance of peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c1b4c45-ec22-46ab-a481-ac93823b041b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 37:12
Text: The wicked plotteth against the just, and gnasheth upon him with his teeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b704af4a-d0de-4041-a084-e4921bfbf0a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 37:13
Text: The LORD shall laugh at him: for he seeth that his day is coming.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9a24b44-a3da-4972-baf5-0fc084b00987>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: PSA 37:14
Text: The wicked have drawn out the sword, and have bent their bow, to cast down the poor and needy, and to slay such as be of upright conversation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91d988c6-91bb-497f-aa88-aafbc0751782>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 37:15
Text: Their sword shall enter into their own heart, and their bows shall be broken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b7a6a82-3998-4fda-985e-6398fd5301f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 37:16
Text: A little that a righteous man hath is better than the riches of many wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7485a5d-f578-4a75-a0ba-5bf0aaa4b640>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 37:17
Text: For the arms of the wicked shall be broken: but the LORD upholdeth the righteous.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fa91bc8-638b-440a-878c-ad6479b820a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 37:18
Text: The LORD knoweth the days of the upright: and their inheritance shall be for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8fa7d58-b643-4410-ab0c-32ffd43f4efe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 37:19
Text: They shall not be ashamed in the evil time: and in the days of famine they shall be satisfied.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:587f2321-5322-4202-9286-9a34bea79592>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: PSA 37:20
Text: But the wicked shall perish, and the enemies of the LORD shall be as the fat of lambs: they shall consume; into smoke shall they consume away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6f1875e-4a13-4d57-a50c-7386245bb9e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 37:21
Text: The wicked borroweth, and payeth not again: but the righteous sheweth mercy, and giveth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80b2db9f-95ad-40c8-bcdf-3cd82fef273e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 37:22
Text: For such as be blessed of him shall inherit the earth; and they that be cursed of him shall be cut off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42aa5aa2-da15-4a50-b032-8bef6e669612>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 37:23
Text: The steps of a good man are ordered by the LORD: and he delighteth in his way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a4c792a-b9c2-4460-a5f3-cb1248fff22e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 37:24
Text: Though he fall, he shall not be utterly cast down: for the LORD upholdeth him with his hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d1d0f3b-2ec3-4ee2-93cb-5e531596e0bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PSA 37:25
Text: I have been young, and now am old; yet have I not seen the righteous forsaken, nor his seed begging bread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eefdeb6d-43e3-4b54-909e-88aee79ce201>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PSA 37:26
Text: He is ever merciful, and lendeth; and his seed is blessed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23516d1e-4578-4328-a570-5224eb7da154>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: PSA 37:27
Text: Depart from evil, and do good; and dwell for evermore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59337555-8826-42b1-b7cb-1559e675d848>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: PSA 37:28
Text: For the LORD loveth judgment, and forsaketh not his saints; they are preserved for ever: but the seed of the wicked shall be cut off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48a68533-a50c-4350-9cbe-3883652c8c63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 37:29
Text: The righteous shall inherit the land, and dwell therein for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a02fcfa5-58a8-4d61-bd54-e1002888434f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 37:30
Text: The mouth of the righteous speaketh wisdom, and his tongue talketh of judgment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08525d2e-c18b-46ad-9dbc-25fc71989d39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 37:31
Text: The law of his God is in his heart; none of his steps shall slide.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f783b4e-c845-48ce-b3c5-d0d95388775a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PSA 37:32
Text: The wicked watcheth the righteous, and seeketh to slay him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:218902be-17e8-4fb9-bbf2-0050c18fbca9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 37:33
Text: The LORD will not leave him in his hand, nor condemn him when he is judged.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dba3fe35-e9bd-4175-8305-4feadcac3b19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: PSA 37:34
Text: Wait on the LORD, and keep his way, and he shall exalt thee to inherit the land: when the wicked are cut off, thou shalt see it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4338ea97-6fd1-45c9-865f-2412f39c75ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 37:35
Text: I have seen the wicked in great power, and spreading himself like a green bay tree.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:122aa8e4-535e-47ac-ac7d-6cb50c03ea6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 37:36
Text: Yet he passed away, and, lo, he was not: yea, I sought him, but he could not be found.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70c6ae04-524f-4b9d-a2f6-bbaf9cef4648>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 37:37
Text: Mark the perfect man, and behold the upright: for the end of that man is peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5748d7a4-260e-42f1-9d23-efb9d46e076e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 37:38
Text: But the transgressors shall be destroyed together: the end of the wicked shall be cut off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bd04d41-40ae-450c-a315-6fe46103edca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 37:39
Text: But the salvation of the righteous is of the LORD: he is their strength in the time of trouble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/37/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d95458e-81fc-41d4-9648-dfbc3a5f87c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: PSA 37:40
Text: And the LORD shall help them, and deliver them: he shall deliver them from the wicked, and save them, because they trust in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/38/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0b11e5b-82b1-4bf4-90dc-fbeb179be0e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 38:1
Text: O lord, rebuke me not in thy wrath: neither chasten me in thy hot displeasure.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/38/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c9df860-0451-4244-ba29-2df424866777>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PSA 38:2
Text: For thine arrows stick fast in me, and thy hand presseth me sore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/38/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b474027e-6a26-4397-acab-eaa1560b6555>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: PSA 38:3
Text: There is no soundness in my flesh because of thine anger; neither is there any rest in my bones because of my sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/38/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5467ad2f-ecf8-4cee-b90d-2e476db58f37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 38:4
Text: For mine iniquities are gone over mine head: as an heavy burden they are too heavy for me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/38/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfd9013b-b2dc-4eb4-973b-35393b45c46e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: PSA 38:5
Text: My wounds stink and are corrupt because of my foolishness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/38/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05d0feb0-a99d-47c1-ae51-612727290378>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 38:6
Text: I am troubled; I am bowed down greatly; I go mourning all the day long.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/38/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9125180e-8b3c-4fcd-b3cf-87260cb85adc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 38:7
Text: For my loins are filled with a loathsome disease: and there is no soundness in my flesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/38/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c51b67b1-8b7f-4bd6-90c9-802b2dd75277>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 38:8
Text: I am feeble and sore broken: I have roared by reason of the disquietness of my heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/38/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3128648-76f0-42bb-9ccb-06fcb4712faa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 38:9
Text: Lord, all my desire is before thee; and my groaning is not hid from thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/38/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed4ceb15-b678-4bf6-ac49-4ba5df6ac4f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 38:10
Text: My heart panteth, my strength faileth me: as for the light of mine eyes, it also is gone from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/38/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:929d566e-d56b-4c2d-b28d-01a5ef8bdbe7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 38:11
Text: My lovers and my friends stand aloof from my sore; and my kinsmen stand afar off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/38/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eeff5775-c395-449a-a258-7614a6938082>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: PSA 38:12
Text: They also that seek after my life lay snares for me: and they that seek my hurt speak mischievous things, and imagine deceits all the day long.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/38/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53a9171e-2757-4db8-83f1-94195cde84e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 38:13
Text: But I, as a deaf man, heard not; and I was as a dumb man that openeth not his mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/38/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:879fe318-d3da-4db8-b64f-ca3884137f23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 38:14
Text: Thus I was as a man that heareth not, and in whose mouth are no reproofs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/38/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a4eecfc-30c5-401b-b1cf-544f447d6ca7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 38:15
Text: For in thee, O LORD, do I hope: thou wilt hear, O Lord my God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/38/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eeba5d20-ea10-478e-9e90-7812f026858f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: PSA 38:16
Text: For I said, Hear me, lest otherwise they should rejoice over me: when my foot slippeth, they magnify themselves against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/38/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4894797-8c68-441b-a6b9-6063a1aa1b00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 38:17
Text: For I am ready to halt, and my sorrow is continually before me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/38/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58d2c99c-a228-4c41-8c64-53a4202a0524>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 38:18
Text: For I will declare mine iniquity; I will be sorry for my sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/38/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e32e2a9-09c6-45e6-b417-fcb7d19fe2ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 38:19
Text: But mine enemies are lively, and they are strong: and they that hate me wrongfully are multiplied.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/38/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b628074-c4fd-49d0-acc0-4d401d754df6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 38:20
Text: They also that render evil for good are mine adversaries; because I follow the thing that good is.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/38/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a2562c3-742d-4a7f-b0bc-e642093df73a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: PSA 38:21
Text: Forsake me not, O LORD: O my God, be not far from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/38/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60df90ad-daad-4deb-bf3b-6c8e6fa7b37c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 71

Reference: PSA 38:22
Text: Make haste to help me, O Lord my salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/39/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8787727-7482-4c9b-b486-ab4168a119ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: PSA 39:1
Text: I said, I will take heed to my ways, that I sin not with my tongue: I will keep my mouth with a bridle, while the wicked is before me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/39/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e974035-6a10-4a3d-9bed-e507bb3eec7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 39:2
Text: I was dumb with silence, I held my peace, even from good; and my sorrow was stirred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/39/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23f07e28-14a4-49b3-a418-4a56d8ef5656>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 39:3
Text: My heart was hot within me, while I was musing the fire burned: then spake I with my tongue,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/39/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34084fa2-a832-4aa9-a1d8-ac7328245305>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 39:4
Text: LORD, make me to know mine end, and the measure of my days, what it is: that I may know how frail I am.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/39/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ea9240e-e0f3-4311-b06c-64a4cf273472>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: PSA 39:5
Text: Behold, thou hast made my days as an handbreadth; and mine age is as nothing before thee: verily every man at his best state is altogether vanity. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/39/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea3edace-60e1-494e-94ba-d3e058db064a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: PSA 39:6
Text: Surely every man walketh in a vain shew: surely they are disquieted in vain: he heapeth up riches, and knoweth not who shall gather them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/39/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21ffa458-4065-4b23-b02f-b05f9a20d942>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: PSA 39:7
Text: And now, Lord, what wait I for? my hope is in thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/39/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76bce7fd-a6f0-4bb1-9dec-46ce43b9002c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 39:8
Text: Deliver me from all my transgressions: make me not the reproach of the foolish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/39/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:775da3e5-6f44-4c60-b9d6-f170fd097389>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PSA 39:9
Text: I was dumb, I opened not my mouth; because thou didst it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/39/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:760e790c-088d-4010-a107-c9d06fcfd548>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 39:10
Text: Remove thy stroke away from me: I am consumed by the blow of thine hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/39/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf5eab84-4365-4174-a494-2899d6ea0376>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: PSA 39:11
Text: When thou with rebukes dost correct man for iniquity, thou makest his beauty to consume away like a moth: surely every man is vanity. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/39/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f025820-c14e-4e28-8fff-4b77587982ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: PSA 39:12
Text: Hear my prayer, O LORD, and give ear unto my cry; hold not thy peace at my tears: for I am a stranger with thee, and a sojourner, as all my fathers were.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/39/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a336b587-087f-458b-8de3-7729966f1d14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 39:13
Text: O spare me, that I may recover strength, before I go hence, and be no more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/40/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bf0ce8b-3af1-493e-b366-ad0c8dae06a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 40:1
Text: I waited patiently for the LORD; and he inclined unto me, and heard my cry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/40/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85a0ef1e-2e08-4474-bef9-9f71226468d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: PSA 40:2
Text: He brought me up also out of an horrible pit, out of the miry clay, and set my feet upon a rock, and established my goings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/40/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f10ad5b-6096-4657-b45b-fd2e080e1cac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: PSA 40:3
Text: And he hath put a new song in my mouth, even praise unto our God: many shall see it, and fear, and shall trust in the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/40/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e184341-b7b8-4128-8393-ffbf6e08791c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: PSA 40:4
Text: Blessed is that man that maketh the LORD his trust, and respecteth not the proud, nor such as turn aside to lies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/40/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9613e0c5-bcb9-48e5-8bf9-3914832a36d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: PSA 40:5
Text: Many, O LORD my God, are thy wonderful works which thou hast done, and thy thoughts which are to us-ward: they cannot be reckoned up in order unto thee: if I would declare and speak of them, they are more than can be numbered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/40/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51d16560-78c7-4bec-866f-9a27fb67d647>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: PSA 40:6
Text: Sacrifice and offering thou didst not desire; mine ears hast thou opened: burnt offering and sin offering hast thou not required.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/40/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eca96d74-10db-473c-9f40-0ea89626f2af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 40:7
Text: Then said I, Lo, I come: in the volume of the book it is written of me,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/40/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8dd2736e-e946-4b0b-9c4f-7f7692fa806e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 40:8
Text: I delight to do thy will, O my God: yea, thy law is within my heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/40/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b68374c-a36d-4107-8aae-aaa92412af09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: PSA 40:9
Text: I have preached righteousness in the great congregation: lo, I have not refrained my lips, O LORD, thou knowest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/40/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:376470fe-0ee8-4bde-8522-d593bba37c9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: PSA 40:10
Text: I have not hid thy righteousness within my heart; I have declared thy faithfulness and thy salvation: I have not concealed thy lovingkindness and thy truth from the great congregation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/40/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ac0fa47-67fb-40c8-8d67-105aaf2fd7e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: PSA 40:11
Text: Withhold not thou thy tender mercies from me, O LORD: let thy lovingkindness and thy truth continually preserve me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/40/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd8b3e6c-2ec3-47b0-bd82-83631222ca43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: PSA 40:12
Text: For innumerable evils have compassed me about: mine iniquities have taken hold upon me, so that I am not able to look up; they are more than the hairs of mine head: therefore my heart faileth me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/40/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65542f3e-ad4f-428d-9010-516dbe2cee75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 40:13
Text: Be pleased, O LORD, to deliver me: O LORD, make haste to help me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/40/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81b38201-83d4-4a5f-b47e-573256844be2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: PSA 40:14
Text: Let them be ashamed and confounded together that seek after my soul to destroy it; let them be driven backward and put to shame that wish me evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/40/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb2c07b6-e832-470f-b546-96e80b0c7633>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 40:15
Text: Let them be desolate for a reward of their shame that say unto me, Aha, aha.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/40/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c59d7b3-7934-488d-98d0-ab877d31660d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: PSA 40:16
Text: Let all those that seek thee rejoice and be glad in thee: let such as love thy salvation say continually, The LORD be magnified.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/40/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:928ba99c-b0af-4520-8dd0-e924ff2e1757>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: PSA 40:17
Text: But I am poor and needy; yet the Lord thinketh upon me: thou art my help and my deliverer; make no tarrying, O my God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/41/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30ae7db1-0cf2-4d53-b34c-a26c32d92b28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 41:1
Text: Blessed is he that considereth the poor: the LORD will deliver him in time of trouble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/41/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb63cd9a-c0f4-4638-87e8-ff97c2d7e0b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: PSA 41:2
Text: The LORD will preserve him, and keep him alive; and he shall be blessed upon the earth: and thou wilt not deliver him unto the will of his enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/41/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79f97561-b5fd-4237-863d-5052acc69a1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 41:3
Text: The LORD will strengthen him upon the bed of languishing: thou wilt make all his bed in his sickness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/41/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49d3659e-db57-4fe0-85d5-fb225610b1f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 41:4
Text: I said, LORD, be merciful unto me: heal my soul; for I have sinned against thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/41/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c3dcaff-655a-4ce3-b301-bc4c6044c895>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 41:5
Text: Mine enemies speak evil of me, When shall he die, and his name perish?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/41/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79b47319-2141-4e7a-9bb5-681293ce4003>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: PSA 41:6
Text: And if he come to see me, he speaketh vanity: his heart gathereth iniquity to itself; when he goeth abroad, he telleth it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/41/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:effd5efa-c33c-42e4-8a05-726e8136980d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 41:7
Text: All that hate me whisper together against me: against me do they devise my hurt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/41/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d190d521-3eaa-49d3-a07e-d8a9b0a08164>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 41:8
Text: An evil disease, say they, cleaveth fast unto him: and now that he lieth he shall rise up no more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/41/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26cdeb5c-1af6-4efe-b4c1-19347df0d397>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: PSA 41:9
Text: Yea, mine own familiar friend, in whom I trusted, which did eat of my bread, hath lifted up his heel against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/41/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0825ea93-5955-4b5f-a2d3-1212e80d4ae3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 41:10
Text: But thou, O LORD, be merciful unto me, and raise me up, that I may requite them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/41/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5de6703-0c52-40a4-a725-368ebd988faf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 41:11
Text: By this I know that thou favourest me, because mine enemy doth not triumph over me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/41/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9ae7b01-5d5a-463e-9b93-a27bc7a5b6c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 41:12
Text: And as for me, thou upholdest me in mine integrity, and settest me before thy face for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/41/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:706db7ed-a52c-4706-896b-e0eee95e6296>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 41:13
Text: Blessed be the LORD God of Israel from everlasting, and to everlasting. Amen, and Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/42/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f944868-33fa-4f33-8c18-2887b86cbf93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 42:1
Text: As the hart panteth after the water brooks, so panteth my soul after thee, O God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/42/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b103c8a-91a0-49c0-badc-a4ef1c4d5b18>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 42:2
Text: My soul thirsteth for God, for the living God: when shall I come and appear before God?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/42/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88a434b2-6166-4acb-b114-54d9b4c79e9e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 42:3
Text: My tears have been my meat day and night, while they continually say unto me, Where is thy God?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/42/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:125cd4ae-a151-44b5-94c6-02b99509b1f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: PSA 42:4
Text: When I remember these things, I pour out my soul in me: for I had gone with the multitude, I went with them to the house of God, with the voice of joy and praise, with a multitude that kept holyday.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/42/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22c693c5-2d1f-48be-9f4f-eb079ad6ec75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: PSA 42:5
Text: Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and why art thou disquieted in me? hope thou in God: for I shall yet praise him for the help of his countenance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/42/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19517f13-cce0-43c9-9b0b-ea271d604be7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: PSA 42:6
Text: O my God, my soul is cast down within me: therefore will I remember thee from the land of Jordan, and of the Hermonites, from the hill Mizar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/42/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6553184a-2941-4f2e-9a45-841d178baa7a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 42:7
Text: Deep calleth unto deep at the noise of thy waterspouts: all thy waves and thy billows are gone over me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/42/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa7163ab-1401-4bd0-8eae-a7c1ff8eea07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: PSA 42:8
Text: Yet the LORD will command his lovingkindness in the day time, and in the night his song shall be with me, and my prayer unto the God of my life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/42/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:665de311-f475-47ae-84b7-e2edcaa8e758>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: PSA 42:9
Text: I will say unto God my rock, Why hast thou forgotten me? why go I mourning because of the oppression of the enemy?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/42/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d93829b-8645-491d-a575-4009bd28586d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 42:10
Text: As with a sword in my bones, mine enemies reproach me; while they say daily unto me, Where is thy God?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/42/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d994f52e-9768-44c8-96a4-e296cacb7531>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: PSA 42:11
Text: Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and why art thou disquieted within me? hope thou in God: for I shall yet praise him, who is the health of my countenance, and my God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/43/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29b33f7e-535e-4172-80cb-293d74f643b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: PSA 43:1
Text: Judge me, O God, and plead my cause against an ungodly nation: O deliver me from the deceitful and unjust man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/43/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb71f103-1491-4303-b748-5132b82f8052>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: PSA 43:2
Text: For thou art the God of my strength: why dost thou cast me off? why go I mourning because of the oppression of the enemy?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/43/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eab6fa76-927e-4f60-976b-2152c2c34930>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: PSA 43:3
Text: O send out thy light and thy truth: let them lead me; let them bring me unto thy holy hill, and to thy tabernacles.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/43/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7bb1b33d-25d2-4f58-8c72-5f88656cac3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: PSA 43:4
Text: Then will I go unto the altar of God, unto God my exceeding joy: yea, upon the harp will I praise thee, O God my God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/43/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad440b07-6032-447e-91a4-ccec5b803e0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: PSA 43:5
Text: Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and why art thou disquieted within me? hope in God: for I shall yet praise him, who is the health of my countenance, and my God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c905f2d9-16a9-4f66-9747-e071b225ee77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: PSA 44:1
Text: We have heard with our ears, O God, our fathers have told us, what work thou didst in their days, in the times of old.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:707d55f2-8919-4c4d-b2ae-953813eb8361>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: PSA 44:2
Text: How thou didst drive out the heathen with thy hand, and plantedst them; how thou didst afflict the people, and cast them out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:696af252-db36-4ed1-8373-40da96165ae3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: PSA 44:3
Text: For they got not the land in possession by their own sword, neither did their own arm save them: but thy right hand, and thine arm, and the light of thy countenance, because thou hadst a favour unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07e889e2-a8bf-4a23-933f-81573583b445>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: PSA 44:4
Text: Thou art my King, O God: command deliverances for Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82f9ba7f-e774-488f-944b-14a0ca760813>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: PSA 44:5
Text: Through thee will we push down our enemies: through thy name will we tread them under that rise up against us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47343697-f88a-4b2a-9b3f-dc5c35830804>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 44:6
Text: For I will not trust in my bow, neither shall my sword save me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10e5b108-0a60-4b4b-9fb1-fbb9b582b467>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 44:7
Text: But thou hast saved us from our enemies, and hast put them to shame that hated us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aba1e7cf-a354-411f-aa1b-8bbf846ae6e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 44:8
Text: In God we boast all the day long, and praise thy name for ever. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38b85b29-38f8-40a8-a69a-ff556c462994>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 44:9
Text: But thou hast cast off, and put us to shame; and goest not forth with our armies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14b15b15-22bd-4045-91c4-25462a6213c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 44:10
Text: Thou makest us to turn back from the enemy: and they which hate us spoil for themselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f47f5add-74a5-4c75-b419-d1a7a3672cbc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 44:11
Text: Thou hast given us like sheep appointed for meat; and hast scattered us among the heathen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3691fcf4-29dd-40ca-af79-35e7b02afa8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 44:12
Text: Thou sellest thy people for nought, and dost not increase thy wealth by their price.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ccc30ea0-8574-43ee-ada3-582bcfdce8d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 44:13
Text: Thou makest us a reproach to our neighbours, a scorn and a derision to them that are round about us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47a1e2f1-b303-4be2-bcd8-d114d2ac22e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 44:14
Text: Thou makest us a byword among the heathen, a shaking of the head among the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:565ee1ec-ea3e-44d2-b10d-aeb6fc65cac0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 44:15
Text: My confusion is continually before me, and the shame of my face hath covered me,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee7eb8ee-2b40-428d-b38f-e507842de463>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 44:16
Text: For the voice of him that reproacheth and blasphemeth; by reason of the enemy and avenger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85f7dee6-d265-40f6-b7be-c4072f18c289>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 44:17
Text: All this is come upon us; yet have we not forgotten thee, neither have we dealt falsely in thy covenant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5df1afc5-9942-40b0-9665-3dba5782e0b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 44:18
Text: Our heart is not turned back, neither have our steps declined from thy way;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70c1479c-84d6-4e28-870f-e1e4d40e5658>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 44:19
Text: Though thou hast sore broken us in the place of dragons, and covered us with the shadow of death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5810244-c336-461b-a9b2-7505f5770621>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 44:20
Text: If we have forgotten the name of our God, or stretched out our hands to a strange god;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd0adf9b-ea35-4e0c-807b-3f203f28dd40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 44:21
Text: Shall not God search this out? for he knoweth the secrets of the heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ac157ba-5283-4b13-bac9-81dfde956410>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 44:22
Text: Yea, for thy sake are we killed all the day long; we are counted as sheep for the slaughter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3a5686c-f131-4831-b9a6-54854584e090>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 44:23
Text: Awake, why sleepest thou, O Lord? arise, cast us not off for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1dc81938-b855-4062-af09-8a27d5c9f37b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 44:24
Text: Wherefore hidest thou thy face, and forgettest our affliction and our oppression?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7038289d-bba1-444a-8292-fab76da0f028>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 44:25
Text: For our soul is bowed down to the dust: our belly cleaveth unto the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/44/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74715501-ebe5-4358-942a-a90cf5fc88b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PSA 44:26
Text: Arise for our help, and redeem us for thy mercies’ sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/45/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85dab5c0-af53-4480-b308-6bd37deb3221>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: PSA 45:1
Text: My heart is inditing a good matter: I speak of the things which I have made touching the king: my tongue is the pen of a ready writer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/45/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ccb7a756-24b0-4755-8c76-cc1f648f6ec2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: PSA 45:2
Text: Thou art fairer than the children of men: grace is poured into thy lips: therefore God hath blessed thee for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/45/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:796f4b97-37a7-43ab-841b-5d1c32654c50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 45:3
Text: Gird thy sword upon thy thigh, O most mighty, with thy glory and thy majesty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/45/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87e7b924-32bd-4536-8c49-d6e175fd12c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: PSA 45:4
Text: And in thy majesty ride prosperously because of truth and meekness and righteousness; and thy right hand shall teach thee terrible things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/45/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5ba6683-1ef6-4251-bf35-e4e83a78c789>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 45:5
Text: Thine arrows are sharp in the heart of the king’s enemies; whereby the people fall under thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/45/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:439660eb-8000-43ed-899d-450683a1613c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 45:6
Text: Thy throne, O God, is for ever and ever: the sceptre of thy kingdom is a right sceptre.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/45/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff32a350-992e-4235-9c4d-497e9a223c1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: PSA 45:7
Text: Thou lovest righteousness, and hatest wickedness: therefore God, thy God, hath anointed thee with the oil of gladness above thy fellows.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/45/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ef88c40-4114-4348-b066-2fdd2beabd90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: PSA 45:8
Text: All thy garments smell of myrrh, and aloes, and cassia, out of the ivory palaces, whereby they have made thee glad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/45/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fcdf62f5-9a85-409d-b67c-22119ee07574>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PSA 45:9
Text: Kings’ daughters were among thy honourable women: upon thy right hand did stand the queen in gold of Ophir.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/45/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24c7eda4-77e4-4559-9525-3a2f0c920dfc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: PSA 45:10
Text: Hearken, O daughter, and consider, and incline thine ear; forget also thine own people, and thy father’s house;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/45/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:935971bd-4b08-434d-a0f6-ff2bc375eb94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 45:11
Text: So shall the king greatly desire thy beauty: for he is thy Lord; and worship thou him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/45/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae40da6a-c6d1-45ab-8663-0146488bdccb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: PSA 45:12
Text: And the daughter of Tyre shall be there with a gift; even the rich among the people shall intreat thy favour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/45/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:641e3ae7-d8ed-46be-9414-32db1d03b84a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 45:13
Text: The king’s daughter is all glorious within: her clothing is of wrought gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/45/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2533a6e6-82f6-46de-9b91-e91e61dc7852>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: PSA 45:14
Text: She shall be brought unto the king in raiment of needlework: the virgins her companions that follow her shall be brought unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/45/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d71c5b0-0d15-47f5-a834-4b4f004a3c1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 45:15
Text: With gladness and rejoicing shall they be brought: they shall enter into the king’s palace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/45/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab8347e3-7640-4806-97c3-bb14532393ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 45:16
Text: Instead of thy fathers shall be thy children, whom thou mayest make princes in all the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/45/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f13db69d-51f6-46a5-b6e1-be663dedf70f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: PSA 45:17
Text: I will make thy name to be remembered in all generations: therefore shall the people praise thee for ever and ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/46/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29672b59-497f-45b3-bf11-5c2f92d856fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 46:1
Text: God is our refuge and strength, a very present help in trouble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/46/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:594928e7-7193-4642-a49c-84ee089dffd8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: PSA 46:2
Text: Therefore will not we fear, though the earth be removed, and though the mountains be carried into the midst of the sea;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/46/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b045fba-5cd9-46cc-aa6b-aef1244ae3f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PSA 46:3
Text: Though the waters thereof roar and be troubled, though the mountains shake with the swelling thereof. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/46/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:335a78d8-7de3-478e-9b95-8e67d9224b4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: PSA 46:4
Text: There is a river, the streams whereof shall make glad the city of God, the holy place of the tabernacles of the most High.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/46/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:089673d3-e75f-4b57-9181-4a9049df29fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 46:5
Text: God is in the midst of her; she shall not be moved: God shall help her, and that right early.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/46/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43bd94e0-4a0d-4254-b5ee-7b2bb8c34f92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 46:6
Text: The heathen raged, the kingdoms were moved: he uttered his voice, the earth melted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/46/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6803f35d-3cad-43e3-acb9-86dfbc345015>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 46:7
Text: The LORD of hosts is with us; the God of Jacob is our refuge. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/46/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c1475b9-d2b1-4cf9-9ad4-a0fd54c58abb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 46:8
Text: Come, behold the works of the LORD, what desolations he hath made in the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/46/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b347caf6-afc9-4e78-8c1e-30e01ae6fd95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: PSA 46:9
Text: He maketh wars to cease unto the end of the earth; he breaketh the bow, and cutteth the spear in sunder; he burneth the chariot in the fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/46/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:542f07a9-e761-49ed-9f49-0716d71ba1b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 46:10
Text: Be still, and know that I am God: I will be exalted among the heathen, I will be exalted in the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/46/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5425fecc-fae7-4a03-b5f0-26b4f94aa12b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 46:11
Text: The LORD of hosts is with us; the God of Jacob is our refuge. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/47/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5253f83-fc6d-4121-8811-cdc77409f3cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 47:1
Text: O clap your hands, all ye people; shout unto God with the voice of triumph.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/47/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fdf576d-f0f4-4676-9638-85cbfc22154e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 47:2
Text: For the LORD most high is terrible; he is a great King over all the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/47/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b61d89e-3c63-47bb-b712-da11cb675406>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 47:3
Text: He shall subdue the people under us, and the nations under our feet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/47/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e9eb2c1-9a60-43b3-81d5-250ba9d4a4e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 47:4
Text: He shall choose our inheritance for us, the excellency of Jacob whom he loved. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/47/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5e3feb4-5328-4e88-aac0-7d9e2c4610c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 47:5
Text: God is gone up with a shout, the LORD with the sound of a trumpet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/47/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55328ec4-fd59-4843-959e-7f58a5b584af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 47:6
Text: Sing praises to God, sing praises: sing praises unto our King, sing praises.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/47/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33c931e2-71c4-45b4-be92-569e4324cc30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 47:7
Text: For God is the King of all the earth: sing ye praises with understanding.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/47/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d20c9bd-70ab-4cc3-b502-80d445a7b2a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 47:8
Text: God reigneth over the heathen: God sitteth upon the throne of his holiness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/47/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e94ece06-7590-4281-bb84-f67a90fee62a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: PSA 47:9
Text: The princes of the people are gathered together, even the people of the God of Abraham: for the shields of the earth belong unto God: he is greatly exalted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/48/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95437878-2670-40e0-bd61-da5bcdf2bdb7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 48:1
Text: Great is the LORD, and greatly to be praised in the city of our God, in the mountain of his holiness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/48/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1d5d1e9-fbc1-4b59-95db-7aa8f20567c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: PSA 48:2
Text: Beautiful for situation, the joy of the whole earth, is mount Zion, on the sides of the north, the city of the great King.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/48/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42501b63-75e2-4c58-86ec-b30ec9761936>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 68

Reference: PSA 48:3
Text: God is known in her palaces for a refuge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/48/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:196306c9-5fdb-414b-8e6d-767a2a1ce304>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PSA 48:4
Text: For, lo, the kings were assembled, they passed by together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/48/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffe08e7e-5be5-4a72-b235-9db7f6d45fc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 48:5
Text: They saw it, and so they marvelled; they were troubled, and hasted away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/48/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea82eb5b-8382-484e-8b4b-5fcc7ccdef00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 48:6
Text: Fear took hold upon them there, and pain, as of a woman in travail.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/48/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0471c99-5eae-4953-ab7f-caa156c029aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: PSA 48:7
Text: Thou breakest the ships of Tarshish with an east wind.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/48/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2249870-3309-40b8-bc2f-69d4c1ee74ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: PSA 48:8
Text: As we have heard, so have we seen in the city of the LORD of hosts, in the city of our God: God will establish it for ever. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/48/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0c5aef2-be30-42a9-9526-7a837c60e4f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 48:9
Text: We have thought of thy lovingkindness, O God, in the midst of thy temple.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/48/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be06a392-d35d-4eb5-8482-351115730af0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: PSA 48:10
Text: According to thy name, O God, so is thy praise unto the ends of the earth: thy right hand is full of righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/48/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eeeda484-63c7-42af-8257-53f293314bec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 48:11
Text: Let mount Zion rejoice, let the daughters of Judah be glad, because of thy judgments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/48/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9de4d56c-d792-4f5c-a5f4-6532c18044a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 48:12
Text: Walk about Zion, and go round about her: tell the towers thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/48/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2889e372-a563-40e9-a463-489dd837337b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 48:13
Text: Mark ye well her bulwarks, consider her palaces; that ye may tell it to the generation following.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/48/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da944b8c-8ca9-4b39-a2e5-c133c8a1be80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 48:14
Text: For this God is our God for ever and ever: he will be our guide even unto death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/49/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f1ddbd9-62a8-44ce-9962-69034606ad55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 49:1
Text: Hear this, all ye people; give ear, all ye inhabitants of the world:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/49/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf3379b9-2958-4c76-ab09-e9ab7add29db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 70

Reference: PSA 49:2
Text: Both low and high, rich and poor, together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/49/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3caefe0-aca3-45a7-9403-6770fe0c3f4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 49:3
Text: My mouth shall speak of wisdom; and the meditation of my heart shall be of understanding.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/49/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aca49c58-61b7-4f92-b343-8cc751084a61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 49:4
Text: I will incline mine ear to a parable: I will open my dark saying upon the harp.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/49/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd4dc7b3-32d0-4a38-9b66-8d6e88fdcb16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 49:5
Text: Wherefore should I fear in the days of evil, when the iniquity of my heels shall compass me about?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/49/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1cf25f8-31b8-4e52-beec-661b975c1d74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 49:6
Text: They that trust in their wealth, and boast themselves in the multitude of their riches;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/49/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1962b0ae-741f-47ca-8d6e-f583ef10e291>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 49:7
Text: None of them can by any means redeem his brother, nor give to God a ransom for him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/49/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b00d5445-cc8b-4224-9dc7-8933a1a85a97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 49:8
Text: (For the redemption of their soul is precious, and it ceaseth for ever:)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/49/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ec70dfb-ab14-45b8-8242-0feb1e61d3f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PSA 49:9
Text: That he should still live for ever, and not see corruption.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/49/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b1139ac-d47b-4df0-9b51-7d39ef3fb1d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: PSA 49:10
Text: For he seeth that wise men die, likewise the fool and the brutish person perish, and leave their wealth to others.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/49/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1abb853-5a8a-4446-8a94-601da76b1660>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: PSA 49:11
Text: Their inward thought is, that their houses shall continue for ever, and their dwelling places to all generations; they call their lands after their own names.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/49/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4bd59f7-0ae4-4b0a-81f9-8dd0a3d6e9e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 49:12
Text: Nevertheless man being in honour abideth not: he is like the beasts that perish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/49/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:061c3a56-3399-44ed-a4ac-1159e8552949>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 49:13
Text: This their way is their folly: yet their posterity approve their sayings. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/49/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9388364d-26fd-4d1c-844c-d860e31e304f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: PSA 49:14
Text: Like sheep they are laid in the grave; death shall feed on them; and the upright shall have dominion over them in the morning; and their beauty shall consume in the grave from their dwelling.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/49/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:868f6631-d611-4cd9-a7ea-c9ed7718b0fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 49:15
Text: But God will redeem my soul from the power of the grave: for he shall receive me. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/49/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8942a0b0-6242-4f75-9be5-ef3f1c442fcd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 49:16
Text: Be not thou afraid when one is made rich, when the glory of his house is increased;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/49/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ed4d5f4-e8d7-465d-be08-8f90e02c1f56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 49:17
Text: For when he dieth he shall carry nothing away: his glory shall not descend after him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/49/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4b185d9-c814-4ab3-8a68-d4866bcdd59e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PSA 49:18
Text: Though while he lived he blessed his soul: and men will praise thee, when thou doest well to thyself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/49/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:745613fa-cba1-4197-8ef6-8b44c886841a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 49:19
Text: He shall go to the generation of his fathers; they shall never see light.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/49/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9c68236-06d0-484c-b4c9-2cf4d1b00972>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 49:20
Text: Man that is in honour, and understandeth not, is like the beasts that perish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/50/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50bc2f25-110a-4066-8f98-f3ed188bdfe3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: PSA 50:1
Text: The mighty God, even the LORD, hath spoken, and called the earth from the rising of the sun unto the going down thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/50/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1895c32-73da-4f8c-a0ee-09f74bfc132c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: PSA 50:2
Text: Out of Zion, the perfection of beauty, God hath shined.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/50/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6132caa5-af8e-408b-8d22-bc818992d419>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: PSA 50:3
Text: Our God shall come, and shall not keep silence: a fire shall devour before him, and it shall be very tempestuous round about him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/50/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07c931ff-665d-43d9-b299-19c363b514bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 50:4
Text: He shall call to the heavens from above, and to the earth, that he may judge his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/50/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71c5f7d3-8b5c-481b-b155-d6ff268e0969>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 50:5
Text: Gather my saints together unto me; those that have made a covenant with me by sacrifice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/50/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b7f75a1-233f-45f0-a688-721b1b079f9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 50:6
Text: And the heavens shall declare his righteousness: for God is judge himself. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/50/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82180ee9-6ed9-41f4-a549-f7fc6cee1d6d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 50:7
Text: Hear, O my people, and I will speak; O Israel, and I will testify against thee: I am God, even thy God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/50/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e92341b1-d493-458f-ad37-e9a0eebd21a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PSA 50:8
Text: I will not reprove thee for thy sacrifices or thy burnt offerings, to have been continually before me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/50/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2fc3be9-3234-4f20-9ba3-0b8dce124f52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 50:9
Text: I will take no bullock out of thy house, nor he goats out of thy folds.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/50/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:085be98c-7ecf-4cbd-bbcd-24bb13f444ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 50:10
Text: For every beast of the forest is mine, and the cattle upon a thousand hills.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/50/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db9bcba1-a79f-4ed1-a243-fe587e5d743c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 50:11
Text: I know all the fowls of the mountains: and the wild beasts of the field are mine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/50/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a872ecc5-7ab7-482b-bfe0-f1c21db34930>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 50:12
Text: If I were hungry, I would not tell thee: for the world is mine, and the fulness thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/50/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82b23c27-d5e4-451a-ad31-8a52d1dffa93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PSA 50:13
Text: Will I eat the flesh of bulls, or drink the blood of goats?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/50/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73d1424a-77f5-48f2-aebb-a7f3e3370356>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 50:14
Text: Offer unto God thanksgiving; and pay thy vows unto the most High:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/50/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73ad6b04-41fc-4380-8f6b-d3b514ce2677>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 50:15
Text: And call upon me in the day of trouble: I will deliver thee, and thou shalt glorify me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/50/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d1e5ec7-a4d5-42f1-a8cb-cc3794cfb6f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: PSA 50:16
Text: But unto the wicked God saith, What hast thou to do to declare my statutes, or that thou shouldest take my covenant in thy mouth?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/50/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1693b77e-ed17-4e0e-a1dd-bf0687bfa26c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 50:17
Text: Seeing thou hatest instruction, and casteth my words behind thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/50/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2dabb35-5a34-4627-bd29-c8e6d08be97f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 50:18
Text: When thou sawest a thief, then thou consentedst with him, and hast been partaker with adulterers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/50/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:073a4540-cd5e-4627-a218-587483ce2283>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 50:19
Text: Thou givest thy mouth to evil, and thy tongue frameth deceit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/50/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13dbe615-2ea1-4538-a6aa-a73a176e7615>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 50:20
Text: Thou sittest and speakest against thy brother; thou slanderest thine own mother’s son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/50/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0a4675f-1b84-4394-aa5d-d48b1a04a884>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: PSA 50:21
Text: These things hast thou done, and I kept silence; thou thoughtest that I was altogether such an one as thyself: but I will reprove thee, and set them in order before thine eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/50/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0d61027-ccc3-4f62-8fdd-ad0ad99d6ec0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 50:22
Text: Now consider this, ye that forget God, lest I tear you in pieces, and there be none to deliver.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/50/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aee2b952-fdb9-4403-ab14-40e816f66f1e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: PSA 50:23
Text: Whoso offereth praise glorifieth me: and to him that ordereth his conversation aright will I shew the salvation of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/51/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c65806a-a6a1-4625-9892-672a51c97417>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: PSA 51:1
Text: Have mercy upon me, O God, according to thy lovingkindness: according unto the multitude of thy tender mercies blot out my transgressions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/51/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:394d5dec-480a-40f7-a11a-fa3ea20c8329>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PSA 51:2
Text: Wash me throughly from mine iniquity, and cleanse me from my sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/51/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ad11e26-7a77-46cd-b28a-531fc40cfc97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 51:3
Text: For I acknowledge my transgressions: and my sin is ever before me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/51/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76e16352-5e09-42c1-8be7-3a444759a64d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: PSA 51:4
Text: Against thee, thee only, have I sinned, and done this evil in thy sight: that thou mightest be justified when thou speakest, and be clear when thou judgest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/51/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3a04c6a-4282-451a-bcbf-7727257de0de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 51:5
Text: Behold, I was shapen in iniquity; and in sin did my mother conceive me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/51/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63593160-dfbc-4ac8-996d-02ad98c258a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: PSA 51:6
Text: Behold, thou desirest truth in the inward parts: and in the hidden part thou shalt make me to know wisdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/51/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1410a671-6163-4942-9932-321201d1e4cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 51:7
Text: Purge me with hyssop, and I shall be clean: wash me, and I shall be whiter than snow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/51/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bb93ccc-4460-4c50-85dc-fecf1311ff24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 51:8
Text: Make me to hear joy and gladness; that the bones which thou hast broken may rejoice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/51/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c6b30ed-f780-48f1-a71a-8a59372630a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 51:9
Text: Hide thy face from my sins, and blot out all mine iniquities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/51/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b682887-b595-44d8-a1fe-1fc223ff6d98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 51:10
Text: Create in me a clean heart, O God; and renew a right spirit within me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/51/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7f86f72-b3f5-4076-8091-a606bf4ddf94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 51:11
Text: Cast me not away from thy presence; and take not thy holy spirit from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/51/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a16df7c8-d432-4527-9bb2-986b37df3df9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 51:12
Text: Restore unto me the joy of thy salvation; and uphold me with thy free spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/51/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac5690ac-726f-435b-ae9d-7749db301ace>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 51:13
Text: Then will I teach transgressors thy ways; and sinners shall be converted unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/51/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81c78bd3-058e-4c70-b1c3-f6714f2fb0a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: PSA 51:14
Text: Deliver me from bloodguiltiness, O God, thou God of my salvation: and my tongue shall sing aloud of thy righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/51/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:563b29b6-9d7f-4c43-a47a-11f258a181e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 51:15
Text: O Lord, open thou my lips; and my mouth shall shew forth thy praise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/51/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c33769a1-66ed-42fe-a441-2ee76a23f2db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 51:16
Text: For thou desirest not sacrifice; else would I give it: thou delightest not in burnt offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/51/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:450c7a86-1c9c-44dd-bf7e-9fb8a6a3c1bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 51:17
Text: The sacrifices of God are a broken spirit: a broken and a contrite heart, O God, thou wilt not despise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/51/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc532b66-f4bb-4578-aa95-b0665fb85165>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 51:18
Text: Do good in thy good pleasure unto Zion: build thou the walls of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/51/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fae10bd5-3cca-4fb0-b959-90c2dda38671>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: PSA 51:19
Text: Then shalt thou be pleased with the sacrifices of righteousness, with burnt offering and whole burnt offering: then shall they offer bullocks upon thine altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/52/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89b00571-c257-4ee4-af53-bada8d3ee794>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 52:1
Text: Why boastest thou thyself in mischief, O mighty man? the goodness of God endureth continually.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/52/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60a64e39-8931-4721-8fcd-df9b22016732>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 52:2
Text: The tongue deviseth mischiefs; like a sharp razor, working deceitfully.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/52/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6017bbc3-3663-443c-bd68-d2d67c54e34a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 52:3
Text: Thou lovest evil more than good; and lying rather than to speak righteousness. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/52/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17b11a61-a18d-4bf5-a85e-eac246bf0ebb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PSA 52:4
Text: Thou lovest all devouring words, O thou deceitful tongue.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/52/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:307bbb84-8753-4fde-8f0f-c278499f5b83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: PSA 52:5
Text: God shall likewise destroy thee for ever, he shall take thee away, and pluck thee out of thy dwelling place, and root thee out of the land of the living. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/52/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef6a31d8-731d-46c4-81e3-053934483ea8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 52:6
Text: The righteous also shall see, and fear, and shall laugh at him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/52/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08da016f-876e-405d-87e6-57f61ea52b85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: PSA 52:7
Text: Lo, this is the man that made not God his strength; but trusted in the abundance of his riches, and strengthened himself in his wickedness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/52/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a355965-76eb-4dff-a601-72cf996988b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PSA 52:8
Text: But I am like a green olive tree in the house of God: I trust in the mercy of God for ever and ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/52/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2055a3bd-71a3-4bb8-b6d8-12c94d7b39f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: PSA 52:9
Text: I will praise thee for ever, because thou hast done it: and I will wait on thy name; for it is good before thy saints.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/53/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2172542f-6edc-4685-a6ff-d29bcc358a52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: PSA 53:1
Text: The fool hath said in his heart, There is no God. Corrupt are they, and have done abominable iniquity: there is none that doeth good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/53/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c95f6cf0-f922-4bfd-9c16-6afa43f4c88c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: PSA 53:2
Text: God looked down from heaven upon the children of men, to see if there were any that did understand, that did seek God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/53/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f3783c1-b48f-4dd3-a02b-f5ec4458b60c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: PSA 53:3
Text: Every one of them is gone back: they are altogether become filthy; there is none that doeth good, no, not one.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/53/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69916202-888b-41c0-978e-e2979515f2cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: PSA 53:4
Text: Have the workers of iniquity no knowledge? who eat up my people as they eat bread: they have not called upon God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/53/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a03bf949-ad4a-4e22-b16c-ef68fe900e43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: PSA 53:5
Text: There were they in great fear, where no fear was: for God hath scattered the bones of him that encampeth against thee: thou hast put them to shame, because God hath despised them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/53/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eab14bbd-d8f0-4f41-9cae-3dd591e3f7b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: PSA 53:6
Text: Oh that the salvation of Israel were come out of Zion! When God bringeth back the captivity of his people, Jacob shall rejoice, and Israel shall be glad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/54/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1fadf7c-e6db-4c9c-979f-a7964a8535fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: PSA 54:1
Text: Save me, O God, by thy name, and judge me by thy strength.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/54/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c61c7f3-9ac7-43f9-b4b6-a2210b5da5ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PSA 54:2
Text: Hear my prayer, O God; give ear to the words of my mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/54/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fea229d-95d8-4492-a90d-2add5875a452>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: PSA 54:3
Text: For strangers are risen up against me, and oppressors seek after my soul: they have not set God before them. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/54/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e723c30-1d2c-4cb4-93b4-afa3585e4455>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 54:4
Text: Behold, God is mine helper: the Lord is with them that uphold my soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/54/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7285691d-17d2-48c3-8f32-fa12ea5de16a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 54:5
Text: He shall reward evil unto mine enemies: cut them off in thy truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/54/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10949004-6baf-4910-a272-eed0f861d2b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 54:6
Text: I will freely sacrifice unto thee: I will praise thy name, O LORD; for it is good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/54/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be78feac-3750-47ae-be1c-500846f8a952>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 54:7
Text: For he hath delivered me out of all trouble: and mine eye hath seen his desire upon mine enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/55/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee84aa36-fae7-4f9d-9154-655ba6764c3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 55:1
Text: Give ear to my prayer, O God; and hide not thyself from my supplication.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/55/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:792075dd-4982-447b-8552-ce4b473d4033>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 55:2
Text: Attend unto me, and hear me: I mourn in my complaint, and make a noise;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/55/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac7de11c-0b1b-45c6-b0bd-04b60a202eb1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: PSA 55:3
Text: Because of the voice of the enemy, because of the oppression of the wicked: for they cast iniquity upon me, and in wrath they hate me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/55/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:355d4400-594a-41d8-aef2-4e3743be53b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 55:4
Text: My heart is sore pained within me: and the terrors of death are fallen upon me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/55/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7786533d-bb57-431f-8a3c-c19a0f4f4312>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 55:5
Text: Fearfulness and trembling are come upon me, and horror hath overwhelmed me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/55/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24ccb8ee-79a1-4523-80e5-a1cd605d9626>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 55:6
Text: And I said, Oh that I had wings like a dove! for then would I fly away, and be at rest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/55/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddbc3e0e-dd6e-4e98-9a3a-3287b3b75fd2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 55:7
Text: Lo, then would I wander far off, and remain in the wilderness. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/55/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b959206-26e7-4076-9121-a44ea11cecf0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: PSA 55:8
Text: I would hasten my escape from the windy storm and tempest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/55/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bd5f457-91b1-44c9-b968-11b5af0ee249>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 55:9
Text: Destroy, O Lord, and divide their tongues: for I have seen violence and strife in the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/55/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d090261-7649-4740-94c2-bc16fd4ca750>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 55:10
Text: Day and night they go about it upon the walls thereof: mischief also and sorrow are in the midst of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/55/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:924d29b3-1f7f-4eca-accd-23f604dae0ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 55:11
Text: Wickedness is in the midst thereof: deceit and guile depart not from her streets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/55/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11014ae0-4710-4200-887d-2f822dc18d80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: PSA 55:12
Text: For it was not an enemy that reproached me; then I could have borne it: neither was it he that hated me that did magnify himself against me; then I would have hid myself from him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/55/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd89056f-b32d-45ac-9612-06286270c949>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 55:13
Text: But it was thou, a man mine equal, my guide, and mine acquaintance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/55/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f25e159f-812c-4879-b287-d1d9468b7581>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 55:14
Text: We took sweet counsel together, and walked unto the house of God in company.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/55/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7a2d135-fa92-491e-9030-dbe7547834e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: PSA 55:15
Text: Let death seize upon them, and let them go down quick into hell: for wickedness is in their dwellings, and among them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/55/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36810e15-ba2f-4542-8d9b-1b1e1e6cbf9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 55:16
Text: As for me, I will call upon God; and the LORD shall save me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/55/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:feaf7f86-cda0-4f7b-b764-11c1c27da7a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 55:17
Text: Evening, and morning, and at noon, will I pray, and cry aloud: and he shall hear my voice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/55/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe84f7b9-266d-4483-a71f-b9afbe4828c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 55:18
Text: He hath delivered my soul in peace from the battle that was against me: for there were many with me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/55/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:769bf798-f3c2-4db9-9584-216dc5cbead1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: PSA 55:19
Text: God shall hear, and afflict them, even he that abideth of old. Selah. Because they have no changes, therefore they fear not God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/55/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62fe636e-da29-4381-a7e3-e0d7cbcdc87f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 55:20
Text: He hath put forth his hands against such as be at peace with him: he hath broken his covenant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/55/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c83aa8f3-74b6-4454-ac19-d9f36f1804a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: PSA 55:21
Text: The words of his mouth were smoother than butter, but war was in his heart: his words were softer than oil, yet were they drawn swords.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/55/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4403723c-40d0-4ffa-a06f-0b19f88577f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PSA 55:22
Text: Cast thy burden upon the LORD, and he shall sustain thee: he shall never suffer the righteous to be moved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/55/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b5d475a-26a9-47fb-8b98-d6aa3cb65f89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: PSA 55:23
Text: But thou, O God, shalt bring them down into the pit of destruction: bloody and deceitful men shall not live out half their days; but I will trust in thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/56/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5dd227af-2f9d-4c9b-84f0-7afc5d5d10f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 56:1
Text: Be merciful unto me, O God: for man would swallow me up; he fighting daily oppresseth me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/56/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1334f39f-036f-497c-bdcf-1fcad8844d95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 56:2
Text: Mine enemies would daily swallow me up: for they be many that fight against me, O thou most High.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/56/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:379948db-75b6-4b24-b233-cf873ebe0776>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 71

Reference: PSA 56:3
Text: What time I am afraid, I will trust in thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/56/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6290105-5a56-4f33-aabe-96e9030c8a82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 56:4
Text: In God I will praise his word, in God I have put my trust; I will not fear what flesh can do unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/56/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9e13b44-cad1-4e3c-b5b5-de8ab3047686>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 56:5
Text: Every day they wrest my words: all their thoughts are against me for evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/56/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2271f115-7a0f-4783-bd3b-98756f6cdd9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PSA 56:6
Text: They gather themselves together, they hide themselves, they mark my steps, when they wait for my soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/56/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bb66b48-4754-4093-a651-115242638516>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 56:7
Text: Shall they escape by iniquity? in thine anger cast down the people, O God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/56/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7d1f161-7e7c-41a3-85f5-67937a6b0862>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 56:8
Text: Thou tellest my wanderings: put thou my tears into thy bottle: are they not in thy book?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/56/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50b86130-1ec9-41e7-a7ca-b9393229d28a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 56:9
Text: When I cry unto thee, then shall mine enemies turn back: this I know; for God is for me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/56/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc7607cf-8183-4fdc-90d8-0468f609abff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 56:10
Text: In God will I praise his word: in the LORD will I praise his word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/56/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3351aa60-abcb-4e6b-9293-d0df7ea7e5b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 56:11
Text: In God have I put my trust: I will not be afraid what man can do unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/56/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f739490-754f-40e3-90e3-9d7558d96f05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 56:12
Text: Thy vows are upon me, O God: I will render praises unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/56/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd398614-3d4a-4b2f-bfc8-40716ea54721>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: PSA 56:13
Text: For thou hast delivered my soul from death: wilt not thou deliver my feet from falling, that I may walk before God in the light of the living?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/57/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3fac68b-63e0-411a-9a68-76b29a6b3f54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: PSA 57:1
Text: Be merciful unto me, O God, be merciful unto me: for my soul trusteth in thee: yea, in the shadow of thy wings will I make my refuge, until these calamities be overpast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/57/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be63596c-7bf1-487a-a60e-1ca34900771c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 57:2
Text: I will cry unto God most high; unto God that performeth all things for me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/57/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d09b201-27ae-45a7-ac8e-e668ea1b0781>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: PSA 57:3
Text: He shall send from heaven, and save me from the reproach of him that would swallow me up. Selah. God shall send forth his mercy and his truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/57/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a02a4da-085c-4d0e-b15e-ff3709ba0993>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: PSA 57:4
Text: My soul is among lions: and I lie even among them that are set on fire, even the sons of men, whose teeth are spears and arrows, and their tongue a sharp sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/57/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aae24d1a-15fc-4f56-8ffd-d3c72e79c8a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 57:5
Text: Be thou exalted, O God, above the heavens; let thy glory be above all the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/57/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f4a7fd9-7954-44f9-ba82-949b64cdc428>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: PSA 57:6
Text: They have prepared a net for my steps; my soul is bowed down: they have digged a pit before me, into the midst whereof they are fallen themselves. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/57/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f968f0f6-37e4-4ba1-9672-be2703577079>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 57:7
Text: My heart is fixed, O God, my heart is fixed: I will sing and give praise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/57/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92c8dea1-2d4f-4984-9107-6ea0169f251f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 57:8
Text: Awake up, my glory; awake, psaltery and harp: I myself will awake early.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/57/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6b7c160-7b60-4391-8440-ee2bd536360a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 57:9
Text: I will praise thee, O Lord, among the people: I will sing unto thee among the nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/57/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d198b16-8da6-4237-afee-dfcc070eca68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 57:10
Text: For thy mercy is great unto the heavens, and thy truth unto the clouds.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/57/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:345909f4-8550-4f3a-8cfb-e34c4ce95097>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 57:11
Text: Be thou exalted, O God, above the heavens: let thy glory be above all the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/58/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7695fb18-7e81-4218-b009-a95a52e63e77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 58:1
Text: Do ye indeed speak righteousness, O congregation? do ye judge uprightly, O ye sons of men?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/58/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd147435-fcd6-4d9a-ae7a-dc25714c3044>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 58:2
Text: Yea, in heart ye work wickedness; ye weigh the violence of your hands in the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/58/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da1e0188-1bc3-4d5e-a5dd-ca557cf07059>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 58:3
Text: The wicked are estranged from the womb: they go astray as soon as they be born, speaking lies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/58/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e73ef7b-6b28-4bb0-8f8d-6f4a90e68d49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 58:4
Text: Their poison is like the poison of a serpent: they are like the deaf adder that stoppeth her ear;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/58/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8253135d-0132-4ffb-a672-82aa20681f8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 58:5
Text: Which will not hearken to the voice of charmers, charming never so wisely.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/58/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41c4dd75-c12d-4628-8fe6-13b3583b4717>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 58:6
Text: Break their teeth, O God, in their mouth: break out the great teeth of the young lions, O LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/58/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc4469e7-4026-4ee2-9538-5a2675d1804c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: PSA 58:7
Text: Let them melt away as waters which run continually: when he bendeth his bow to shoot his arrows, let them be as cut in pieces.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/58/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddfe8471-3097-4f61-95ad-af1cd0e9664d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: PSA 58:8
Text: As a snail which melteth, let every one of them pass away: like the untimely birth of a woman, that they may not see the sun.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/58/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6dae2985-b84e-4770-8642-02104d898e70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: PSA 58:9
Text: Before your pots can feel the thorns, he shall take them away as with a whirlwind, both living, and in his wrath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/58/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aed934a2-9d67-48df-b62a-5ba953bbc811>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PSA 58:10
Text: The righteous shall rejoice when he seeth the vengeance: he shall wash his feet in the blood of the wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/58/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78c142dd-35e0-4557-bff3-36d8169eafef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: PSA 58:11
Text: So that a man shall say, Verily there is a reward for the righteous: verily he is a God that judgeth in the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/59/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a76da293-0368-400d-8204-bdcec842b622>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 59:1
Text: Deliver me from mine enemies, O my God: defend me from them that rise up against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/59/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:844b1b7b-c6d4-434c-ad3a-c03888c62cfb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 59:2
Text: Deliver me from the workers of iniquity, and save me from bloody men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/59/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1af2d47b-7900-4ece-8550-54f172aa315d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: PSA 59:3
Text: For, lo, they lie in wait for my soul: the mighty are gathered against me; not for my transgression, nor for my sin, O LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/59/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:844ee83a-b079-45ff-826c-522b1f992ad8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 59:4
Text: They run and prepare themselves without my fault: awake to help me, and behold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/59/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83c01c1e-c880-4d5c-9827-bf2786c61123>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: PSA 59:5
Text: Thou therefore, O LORD God of hosts, the God of Israel, awake to visit all the heathen: be not merciful to any wicked transgressors. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/59/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e58ae805-87c8-44eb-89ac-1d048b3194aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 59:6
Text: They return at evening: they make a noise like a dog, and go round about the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/59/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3fbf260-488d-4ca0-90af-6601c537f358>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 59:7
Text: Behold, they belch out with their mouth: swords are in their lips: for who, say they, doth hear?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/59/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e920b6e-c990-4ff3-a810-a48a02212f96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 59:8
Text: But thou, O LORD, shalt laugh at them; thou shalt have all the heathen in derision.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/59/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ace2420c-e484-4ed9-a199-4d30c395e949>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 59:9
Text: Because of his strength will I wait upon thee: for God is my defence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/59/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8870df65-e96d-4f1a-9dfb-ffde8137e896>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 59:10
Text: The God of my mercy shall prevent me: God shall let me see my desire upon mine enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/59/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84732a78-d0e9-435a-8d22-071b226ba37b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 59:11
Text: Slay them not, lest my people forget: scatter them by thy power; and bring them down, O Lord our shield.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/59/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fb34dd5-dcec-4321-9c5d-f4bf627a5690>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: PSA 59:12
Text: For the sin of their mouth and the words of their lips let them even be taken in their pride: and for cursing and lying which they speak.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/59/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:efaceba3-0b03-4beb-b87c-56a94cfa1366>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: PSA 59:13
Text: Consume them in wrath, consume them, that they may not be: and let them know that God ruleth in Jacob unto the ends of the earth. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/59/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a96206b-b56f-4050-b368-d04ef89bbf7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 59:14
Text: And at evening let them return; and let them make a noise like a dog, and go round about the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/59/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:387cc07c-7113-4450-a413-61e95baca248>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 59:15
Text: Let them wander up and down for meat, and grudge if they be not satisfied.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/59/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a242eb5f-fa31-42e6-bbf3-a76fc2145175>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: PSA 59:16
Text: But I will sing of thy power; yea, I will sing aloud of thy mercy in the morning: for thou hast been my defence and refuge in the day of my trouble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/59/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab95af6a-4c5f-4adb-b6b2-13526e40acff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 59:17
Text: Unto thee, O my strength, will I sing: for God is my defence, and the God of my mercy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/60/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:311e50dc-f42c-4324-a74f-82caba517edd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PSA 60:1
Text: O God, thou hast cast us off, thou hast scattered us, thou hast been displeased; O turn thyself to us again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/60/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bd4e2be-e57c-45ed-86af-b8b86944d63b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PSA 60:2
Text: Thou hast made the earth to tremble; thou hast broken it: heal the breaches thereof; for it shaketh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/60/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e058dce-fe36-434e-976f-7dcc2b5ba038>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 60:3
Text: Thou hast shewed thy people hard things: thou hast made us to drink the wine of astonishment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/60/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a283f455-7555-4b5f-8356-6b4d8ca3a3b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PSA 60:4
Text: Thou hast given a banner to them that fear thee, that it may be displayed because of the truth. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/60/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b1e5042-d953-4d0d-88e1-180fe06df301>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 60:5
Text: That thy beloved may be delivered; save with thy right hand, and hear me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/60/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20c0a411-f926-4631-870e-620a240cda1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PSA 60:6
Text: God hath spoken in his holiness; I will rejoice, I will divide Shechem, and mete out the valley of Succoth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/60/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a06a72d1-77f3-4601-b071-68af928770bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PSA 60:7
Text: Gilead is mine, and Manasseh is mine; Ephraim also is the strength of mine head; Judah is my lawgiver;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/60/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64aaf57e-cdf7-42e2-96f9-73bc5392cabc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 60:8
Text: Moab is my washpot; over Edom will I cast out my shoe: Philistia, triumph thou because of me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/60/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fda419d3-b125-413b-8ef6-96a198c9b187>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 60:9
Text: Who will bring me into the strong city? who will lead me into Edom?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/60/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de0c8b75-91ad-43e1-bb7c-ecc36e7a4cc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 60:10
Text: Wilt not thou, O God, which hadst cast us off? and thou, O God, which didst not go out with our armies?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/60/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:476a930f-d20b-482e-95fc-ef6e8374edf8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: PSA 60:11
Text: Give us help from trouble: for vain is the help of man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/60/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6c60698-0954-431c-b35d-546901cbc8f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 60:12
Text: Through God we shall do valiantly: for he it is that shall tread down our enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/61/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e9ea5c4-b899-490e-8aec-b87f8154a88e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 69

Reference: PSA 61:1
Text: Hear my cry, O God; attend unto my prayer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/61/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3db886f9-dc2d-4706-86b5-d744b7d9771e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: PSA 61:2
Text: From the end of the earth will I cry unto thee, when my heart is overwhelmed: lead me to the rock that is higher than I.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/61/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68fb6eb5-a908-4f9b-8f66-bb948ee64dcc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 61:3
Text: For thou hast been a shelter for me, and a strong tower from the enemy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/61/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:271cf698-7bfa-4be9-898d-865a7cafa75c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 61:4
Text: I will abide in thy tabernacle for ever: I will trust in the covert of thy wings. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/61/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4eeb2e2f-2c65-4fd3-80eb-979cf787d47a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 61:5
Text: For thou, O God, hast heard my vows: thou hast given me the heritage of those that fear thy name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/61/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31372e01-39bc-4d76-92ea-93ce92dfe26c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 61:6
Text: Thou wilt prolong the king’s life: and his years as many generations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/61/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b1994ef-10b4-4167-a0ba-c8081d2b6a1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 61:7
Text: He shall abide before God for ever: O prepare mercy and truth, which may preserve him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/61/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67b0ba03-0f4b-4553-9a56-90224e22a6df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 61:8
Text: So will I sing praise unto thy name for ever, that I may daily perform my vows.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/62/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:651adcad-e95d-4f3d-8441-54433c897e55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 62:1
Text: Truly my soul waiteth upon God: from him cometh my salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/62/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be8b6e5a-4765-46ba-ac58-f453a6021413>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 62:2
Text: He only is my rock and my salvation; he is my defence; I shall not be greatly moved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/62/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e61bbbe8-e5c3-472d-8e71-a521e0d2336c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: PSA 62:3
Text: How long will ye imagine mischief against a man? ye shall be slain all of you: as a bowing wall shall ye be, and as a tottering fence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/62/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6f93f83-ff0b-4b2f-8acf-70a4f117591b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: PSA 62:4
Text: They only consult to cast him down from his excellency: they delight in lies: they bless with their mouth, but they curse inwardly. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/62/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f34801b-bfb2-4b8b-ad3e-8b49278c612b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PSA 62:5
Text: My soul, wait thou only upon God; for my expectation is from him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/62/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18cac0cc-284c-4af8-a6ea-4005172d53be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 62:6
Text: He only is my rock and my salvation: he is my defence; I shall not be moved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/62/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84ce7ce7-886d-48b5-a297-00ef0e322ae1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 62:7
Text: In God is my salvation and my glory: the rock of my strength, and my refuge, is in God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/62/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6267079b-c613-4142-b4fa-360cc67755f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PSA 62:8
Text: Trust in him at all times; ye people, pour out your heart before him: God is a refuge for us. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/62/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ebd2340-0ead-428f-b7db-797b4ac14e99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: PSA 62:9
Text: Surely men of low degree are vanity, and men of high degree are a lie: to be laid in the balance, they are altogether lighter than vanity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/62/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:794fb6d3-541f-49dd-945f-7cf0a3d67676>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PSA 62:10
Text: Trust not in oppression, and become not vain in robbery: if riches increase, set not your heart upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/62/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de99c1f7-bb6f-44db-9ced-64192540139a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 62:11
Text: God hath spoken once; twice have I heard this; that power belongeth unto God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/62/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb33557b-a92a-4f8c-b6d6-c17c8226b05f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 62:12
Text: Also unto thee, O Lord, belongeth mercy: for thou renderest to every man according to his work.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/63/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06828abe-1772-4fa9-923e-d09021959543>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: PSA 63:1
Text: O God, thou art my God; early will I seek thee: my soul thirsteth for thee, my flesh longeth for thee in a dry and thirsty land, where no water is;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/63/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:980131a4-574a-498a-ab86-4a94e9a3415e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 63:2
Text: To see thy power and thy glory, so as I have seen thee in the sanctuary.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/63/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:559b80a8-e3eb-4dab-a55f-7a06a9b21430>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 63:3
Text: Because thy lovingkindness is better than life, my lips shall praise thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/63/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e70eb0e7-bb5f-42de-96e0-388216993d3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 63:4
Text: Thus will I bless thee while I live: I will lift up my hands in thy name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/63/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbda658a-e7c8-4563-a0a0-e7e26021c4e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 63:5
Text: My soul shall be satisfied as with marrow and fatness; and my mouth shall praise thee with joyful lips:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/63/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c818f6b-de97-473e-a9fa-bd770d4c882e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 63:6
Text: When I remember thee upon my bed, and meditate on thee in the night watches.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/63/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5185fd95-d608-4f55-b452-5246760bd541>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 63:7
Text: Because thou hast been my help, therefore in the shadow of thy wings will I rejoice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/63/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a852412-c981-4605-ab0c-8a9e9b39cd3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 63:8
Text: My soul followeth hard after thee: thy right hand upholdeth me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/63/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51081bc4-ca5b-421f-8e10-7cb9cae48bfb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 63:9
Text: But those that seek my soul, to destroy it, shall go into the lower parts of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/63/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c9e4ac0-f448-427a-8eb5-8c1ffe87b06a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PSA 63:10
Text: They shall fall by the sword: they shall be a portion for foxes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/63/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9cb68a4-9787-44bb-a97a-f028d2ed5d66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: PSA 63:11
Text: But the king shall rejoice in God; every one that sweareth by him shall glory: but the mouth of them that speak lies shall be stopped.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/64/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3d57aae-8951-4146-8fce-f26b71786ddc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 64:1
Text: Hear my voice, O God, in my prayer: preserve my life from fear of the enemy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/64/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9187842d-2760-4851-890c-f40bc2d765ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 64:2
Text: Hide me from the secret counsel of the wicked; from the insurrection of the workers of iniquity:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/64/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a03b6bc-f6dd-497a-868f-d8da9d3121ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 64:3
Text: Who whet their tongue like a sword, and bend their bows to shoot their arrows, even bitter words:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/64/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb981d00-f950-4cb8-a48c-2878a94fdb5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 64:4
Text: That they may shoot in secret at the perfect: suddenly do they shoot at him, and fear not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/64/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fb78cbb-0a55-4560-a98a-0b119b8f1904>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: PSA 64:5
Text: They encourage themselves in an evil matter: they commune of laying snares privily; they say, Who shall see them?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/64/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5844121a-b772-4621-be4c-29b154a2b153>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: PSA 64:6
Text: They search out iniquities; they accomplish a diligent search: both the inward thought of every one of them, and the heart, is deep.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/64/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a753a4ed-d77a-408c-a1a2-2847d3c44544>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 64:7
Text: But God shall shoot at them with an arrow; suddenly shall they be wounded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/64/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e856bde4-48e1-439c-811b-a2e99ae921e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 64:8
Text: So they shall make their own tongue to fall upon themselves: all that see them shall flee away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/64/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb66387f-a514-4bf6-8304-b17646dea2a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 64:9
Text: And all men shall fear, and shall declare the work of God; for they shall wisely consider of his doing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/64/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6e5abdf-4919-492a-947a-2860bcb2f6a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PSA 64:10
Text: The righteous shall be glad in the LORD, and shall trust in him; and all the upright in heart shall glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/65/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:617d3bb5-7819-4237-a128-609aa9ca5c30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 65:1
Text: Praise waiteth for thee, O God, in Sion: and unto thee shall the vow be performed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/65/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17e0c7bb-a23c-4e69-93dc-68764dca3a71>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PSA 65:2
Text: O thou that hearest prayer, unto thee shall all flesh come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/65/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a815d25b-644b-4239-a77c-e2aa546423ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 65:3
Text: Iniquities prevail against me: as for our transgressions, thou shalt purge them away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/65/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f025691e-ecdf-4bfb-be90-165abd30ec97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: PSA 65:4
Text: Blessed is the man whom thou choosest, and causest to approach unto thee, that he may dwell in thy courts: we shall be satisfied with the goodness of thy house, even of thy holy temple.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/65/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be5a4f7a-20e3-4bd7-b441-43ca41a5f81a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: PSA 65:5
Text: By terrible things in righteousness wilt thou answer us, O God of our salvation; who art the confidence of all the ends of the earth, and of them that are afar off upon the sea:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/65/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:172a6a71-39bc-4dda-bb2e-6a80cb73a76f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 65:6
Text: Which by his strength setteth fast the mountains; being girded with power:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/65/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d525faa3-c7c4-42a9-8140-585bfcffcd14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 65:7
Text: Which stilleth the noise of the seas, the noise of their waves, and the tumult of the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/65/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc726bd8-4716-4c2a-8cdc-75f4af400c18>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: PSA 65:8
Text: They also that dwell in the uttermost parts are afraid at thy tokens: thou makest the outgoings of the morning and evening to rejoice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/65/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bfc57e5d-8a87-498c-a027-69d1cb9cbd04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: PSA 65:9
Text: Thou visitest the earth, and waterest it: thou greatly enrichest it with the river of God, which is full of water: thou preparest them corn, when thou hast so provided for it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/65/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9342a679-7130-4dcf-b387-f4e5df816a44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: PSA 65:10
Text: Thou waterest the ridges thereof abundantly: thou settlest the furrows thereof: thou makest it soft with showers: thou blessest the springing thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/65/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2093293b-16e6-4b56-8a50-b35be5e1af66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 65:11
Text: Thou crownest the year with thy goodness; and thy paths drop fatness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/65/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34eef043-0999-4a99-86ee-8bab4275ad9e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 65:12
Text: They drop upon the pastures of the wilderness: and the little hills rejoice on every side.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/65/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:928aa5db-17d7-4c08-bf2d-ea667d4acf6d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: PSA 65:13
Text: The pastures are clothed with flocks; the valleys also are covered over with corn; they shout for joy, they also sing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/66/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d1e6841-10f7-4907-86e0-bd16e319b158>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 70

Reference: PSA 66:1
Text: Make a joyful noise unto God, all ye lands:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/66/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbe8cc26-6bb3-403e-a377-994ccf9fe006>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PSA 66:2
Text: Sing forth the honour of his name: make his praise glorious.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/66/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ecde15b-b6d3-4151-9974-a2fb8c651c69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: PSA 66:3
Text: Say unto God, How terrible art thou in thy works! through the greatness of thy power shall thine enemies submit themselves unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/66/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60be6f1a-688f-44c8-8aea-159a6e14b483>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 66:4
Text: All the earth shall worship thee, and shall sing unto thee; they shall sing to thy name. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/66/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61a81376-f336-44c3-9e67-f9dd273b14b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 66:5
Text: Come and see the works of God: he is terrible in his doing toward the children of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/66/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e411297-4f54-48e7-b9be-59e759c53417>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 66:6
Text: He turned the sea into dry land: they went through the flood on foot: there did we rejoice in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/66/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6c10898-94d5-4aa6-874a-387936fdae8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PSA 66:7
Text: He ruleth by his power for ever; his eyes behold the nations: let not the rebellious exalt themselves. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/66/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e52fa24d-7f09-4037-bbf6-462c7887c1df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 66:8
Text: O bless our God, ye people, and make the voice of his praise to be heard:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/66/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86fd6952-f375-4bd0-bd1b-8caa5b67281a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 66:9
Text: Which holdeth our soul in life, and suffereth not our feet to be moved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/66/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:766d35a8-63a1-4a1a-8492-6eabe484c58f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 66:10
Text: For thou, O God, hast proved us: thou hast tried us, as silver is tried.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/66/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2448e35-7f4b-4914-9522-10ac2367aaec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 66:11
Text: Thou broughtest us into the net; thou laidst affliction upon our loins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/66/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f827fec-0e17-4bbc-abce-e008e31d6392>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: PSA 66:12
Text: Thou hast caused men to ride over our heads; we went through fire and through water: but thou broughtest us out into a wealthy place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/66/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8e89a9f-3394-44e0-ba3e-3bc0abdc360f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 66:13
Text: I will go into thy house with burnt offerings: I will pay thee my vows,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/66/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37979d7a-4805-4868-8c62-53071a5178f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 66:14
Text: Which my lips have uttered, and my mouth hath spoken, when I was in trouble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/66/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c94f3e6-7350-4b0f-8c73-4386c5e2c668>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: PSA 66:15
Text: I will offer unto thee burnt sacrifices of fatlings, with the incense of rams; I will offer bullocks with goats. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/66/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6b2808a-f830-4ead-a6f5-23db3506497e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 66:16
Text: Come and hear, all ye that fear God, and I will declare what he hath done for my soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/66/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8050432-9f85-4b25-b17e-8091b88cbb09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 66:17
Text: I cried unto him with my mouth, and he was extolled with my tongue.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/66/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ffd770a-1d5f-440e-8171-65fd9dc0fb37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 66:18
Text: If I regard iniquity in my heart, the Lord will not hear me:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/66/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8537e3c1-ab05-41c1-9fd0-7e02c6028911>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 66:19
Text: But verily God hath heard me; he hath attended to the voice of my prayer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/66/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3e290de-b791-45a4-a9d8-a493afed89b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 66:20
Text: Blessed be God, which hath not turned away my prayer, nor his mercy from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/67/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:339ce13b-3539-40ae-a78c-145d77ade07f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 67:1
Text: God be merciful unto us, and bless us; and cause his face to shine upon us; Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/67/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0fbb143f-f02a-4d6b-979c-27abd587945a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 67:2
Text: That thy way may be known upon earth, thy saving health among all nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/67/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26190e31-9ee0-404c-9a25-ceeb54face1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 67:3
Text: Let the people praise thee, O God; let all the people praise thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/67/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66c8a856-8402-4a92-894b-705013c7c924>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: PSA 67:4
Text: O let the nations be glad and sing for joy: for thou shalt judge the people righteously, and govern the nations upon earth. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/67/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a789dbe8-0a83-4907-a1a7-97791e3987cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 67:5
Text: Let the people praise thee, O God; let all the people praise thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/67/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7a8f38d-480b-415c-a403-9edef1760b31>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 67:6
Text: Then shall the earth yield her increase; and God, even our own God, shall bless us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/67/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb533954-a24f-4716-9d6b-b1ee685e919b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PSA 67:7
Text: God shall bless us; and all the ends of the earth shall fear him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1ef10d0-59af-4e8c-9943-2ba0236fbb9e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 68:1
Text: Let God arise, let his enemies be scattered: let them also that hate him flee before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acde4aea-64b0-4444-88a6-8483d92c28a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: PSA 68:2
Text: As smoke is driven away, so drive them away: as wax melteth before the fire, so let the wicked perish at the presence of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a1bb1f9-dfdb-4f61-9ccc-ed5d87a0a29a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 68:3
Text: But let the righteous be glad; let them rejoice before God: yea, let them exceedingly rejoice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad8ab6d5-74d9-4d94-84c6-96b4a1d0e5c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: PSA 68:4
Text: Sing unto God, sing praises to his name: extol him that rideth upon the heavens by his name JAH, and rejoice before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6db74fb0-58a2-457d-bd6f-73077ebc3fa8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 68:5
Text: A father of the fatherless, and a judge of the widows, is God in his holy habitation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:543abce6-248d-486a-b678-819cba1a89b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: PSA 68:6
Text: God setteth the solitary in families: he bringeth out those which are bound with chains: but the rebellious dwell in a dry land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97cb1c65-3809-4be2-bdea-1472e104c71b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PSA 68:7
Text: O God, when thou wentest forth before thy people, when thou didst march through the wilderness; Selah:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbc5e7ad-9c8b-48e6-afb4-b09f350f2a71>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: PSA 68:8
Text: The earth shook, the heavens also dropped at the presence of God: even Sinai itself was moved at the presence of God, the God of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2e37b3f-f1ca-42c8-aa1c-2eae2f03ed65>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: PSA 68:9
Text: Thou, O God, didst send a plentiful rain, whereby thou didst confirm thine inheritance, when it was weary.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4502fec5-4e18-433b-a532-25a207b3e024>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 68:10
Text: Thy congregation hath dwelt therein: thou, O God, hast prepared of thy goodness for the poor.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aed6c718-60f8-4cdb-8d45-a659f11ba2ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 68:11
Text: The Lord gave the word: great was the company of those that published it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4628c1e6-7488-42e3-945b-db9f9fde2b38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 68:12
Text: Kings of armies did flee apace: and she that tarried at home divided the spoil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26fef109-4fc3-475f-b410-9f01a6c18701>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: PSA 68:13
Text: Though ye have lien among the pots, yet shall ye be as the wings of a dove covered with silver, and her feathers with yellow gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5722701-e912-4b99-9b1a-c11e1373d93b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 68:14
Text: When the Almighty scattered kings in it, it was white as snow in Salmon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f75149ff-7bfd-4f7f-8e8b-85fca343a721>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 68:15
Text: The hill of God is as the hill of Bashan; an high hill as the hill of Bashan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2569e3f8-6d63-4209-9fde-19d81b421585>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: PSA 68:16
Text: Why leap ye, ye high hills? this is the hill which God desireth to dwell in; yea, the LORD will dwell in it for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fec80fbf-ccf0-4f9f-bf0b-2402939e79dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: PSA 68:17
Text: The chariots of God are twenty thousand, even thousands of angels: the Lord is among them, as in Sinai, in the holy place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be0f3e67-fb4b-4797-a24f-340f0904a6b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: PSA 68:18
Text: Thou hast ascended on high, thou hast led captivity captive: thou hast received gifts for men; yea, for the rebellious also, that the LORD God might dwell among them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d79ee75f-2af2-4fd7-98b0-8dddb9f73b31>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 68:19
Text: Blessed be the Lord, who daily loadeth us with benefits, even the God of our salvation. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a3284dd-aa10-470d-85cf-726a11b8759b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 68:20
Text: He that is our God is the God of salvation; and unto GOD the Lord belong the issues from death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d29e1d7f-e03f-448b-bb94-0cc5d86cca96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: PSA 68:21
Text: But God shall wound the head of his enemies, and the hairy scalp of such an one as goeth on still in his trespasses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a16e2ab3-ad90-460f-8a8e-3950d99df3cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 68:22
Text: The Lord said, I will bring again from Bashan, I will bring my people again from the depths of the sea:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48af9f59-5e39-41e6-b1b8-132d55238cfa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 68:23
Text: That thy foot may be dipped in the blood of thine enemies, and the tongue of thy dogs in the same.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b0853d7-72b1-41cb-82ea-2bef5ab4fa3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 68:24
Text: They have seen thy goings, O God; even the goings of my God, my King, in the sanctuary.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6703f8e-d1f0-4dbe-9ca9-1e9d5d8c271e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: PSA 68:25
Text: The singers went before, the players on instruments followed after; among them were the damsels playing with timbrels.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d47e51a8-2673-4e25-a03a-3dbe624ba6c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 68:26
Text: Bless ye God in the congregations, even the Lord, from the fountain of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f442996-ccec-4b0a-b8ad-355eabcd15fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: PSA 68:27
Text: There is little Benjamin with their ruler, the princes of Judah and their council, the princes of Zebulun, and the princes of Naphtali.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2202908-8b4f-4b65-9752-fd7130799e77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 68:28
Text: Thy God hath commanded thy strength: strengthen, O God, that which thou hast wrought for us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22950d17-e7de-41c5-9b50-9f2357289812>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 68:29
Text: Because of thy temple at Jerusalem shall kings bring presents unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b710913e-75dc-4aa8-9e42-0fca01651a55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: PSA 68:30
Text: Rebuke the company of spearmen, the multitude of the bulls, with the calves of the people, till every one submit himself with pieces of silver: scatter thou the people that delight in war.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e3edbed-e5e4-4809-8693-bde83d8d9f8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 68:31
Text: Princes shall come out of Egypt; Ethiopia shall soon stretch out her hands unto God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c86e1397-c261-47f5-8aed-e240cf5133d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 68:32
Text: Sing unto God, ye kingdoms of the earth; O sing praises unto the Lord; Selah:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57e470f2-654e-4ca0-8adb-db6c45d3ba43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: PSA 68:33
Text: To him that rideth upon the heavens of heavens, which were of old; lo, he doth send out his voice, and that a mighty voice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40a3fd4f-49ae-4011-a432-9a253c680069>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 68:34
Text: Ascribe ye strength unto God: his excellency is over Israel, and his strength is in the clouds.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/68/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ba47df9-fdeb-4046-a302-b313cc842d93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: PSA 68:35
Text: O God, thou art terrible out of thy holy places: the God of Israel is he that giveth strength and power unto his people. Blessed be God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2e04b75-87c2-4e22-82fa-05abc8c5f6e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: PSA 69:1
Text: Save me, O God; for the waters are come in unto my soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fcf5ca8b-7b1f-487f-b19f-d47b37c07985>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: PSA 69:2
Text: I sink in deep mire, where there is no standing: I am come into deep waters, where the floods overflow me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3928672a-1f9d-41b0-ad41-51c7cedd03f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 69:3
Text: I am weary of my crying: my throat is dried: mine eyes fail while I wait for my God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d3098fd-7a74-4648-a13e-e4fca53c49c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: PSA 69:4
Text: They that hate me without a cause are more than the hairs of mine head: they that would destroy me, being mine enemies wrongfully, are mighty: then I restored that which I took not away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76500531-17ad-4536-b1ff-75fcff22f858>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 69:5
Text: O God, thou knowest my foolishness; and my sins are not hid from thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cabb3fc4-111e-4f92-a4f5-62b33aeb2cc7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: PSA 69:6
Text: Let not them that wait on thee, O Lord GOD of hosts, be ashamed for my sake: let not those that seek thee be confounded for my sake, O God of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bea3bd9c-b4ed-4c47-a40e-fa94b85710d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 69:7
Text: Because for thy sake I have borne reproach; shame hath covered my face.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a2dca45-3b92-4aa8-a85f-5e679ac51c55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 69:8
Text: I am become a stranger unto my brethren, and an alien unto my mother’s children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5779b1c-2556-4209-9ca7-289b90ccad40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: PSA 69:9
Text: For the zeal of thine house hath eaten me up; and the reproaches of them that reproached thee are fallen upon me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a44d68dd-825e-4988-9d1c-328d2530bace>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 69:10
Text: When I wept, and chastened my soul with fasting, that was to my reproach.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:efb19e9b-c8ab-4a0e-bf99-a03027c34052>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 69:11
Text: I made sackcloth also my garment; and I became a proverb to them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6deb7b6-c4ae-4b69-8169-0c8d87001b94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 69:12
Text: They that sit in the gate speak against me; and I was the song of the drunkards.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddec98a8-2167-48ce-a9c5-dab62657ca11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: PSA 69:13
Text: But as for me, my prayer is unto thee, O LORD, in an acceptable time: O God, in the multitude of thy mercy hear me, in the truth of thy salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8af84fbf-8fda-4b1b-816f-f82c2756dbff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: PSA 69:14
Text: Deliver me out of the mire, and let me not sink: let me be delivered from them that hate me, and out of the deep waters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc6073d9-d0ef-4f15-b8ee-049b2b82a8cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: PSA 69:15
Text: Let not the waterflood overflow me, neither let the deep swallow me up, and let not the pit shut her mouth upon me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43bdc2e2-86cd-47e5-9532-4551152688a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: PSA 69:16
Text: Hear me, O LORD; for thy lovingkindness is good: turn unto me according to the multitude of thy tender mercies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd539aa1-1623-4150-835b-a53fb1fbd1f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 69:17
Text: And hide not thy face from thy servant; for I am in trouble: hear me speedily.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cdee7292-6e9f-4aaf-84ae-17cdae213796>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 69:18
Text: Draw nigh unto my soul, and redeem it: deliver me because of mine enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a1c0150-34dd-4c5d-95f2-d1c8ff61596a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 69:19
Text: Thou hast known my reproach, and my shame, and my dishonour: mine adversaries are all before thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a32b6f53-d186-4f42-8104-bd023975acd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: PSA 69:20
Text: Reproach hath broken my heart; and I am full of heaviness: and I looked for some to take pity, but there was none; and for comforters, but I found none.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9dd641a-a99d-4878-b655-54ac619a41d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 69:21
Text: They gave me also gall for my meat; and in my thirst they gave me vinegar to drink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19273d7b-84f9-44d4-a4cc-aa05b2b007f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: PSA 69:22
Text: Let their table become a snare before them: and that which should have been for their welfare, let it become a trap.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28295197-fde7-4edc-ae82-137b8afa31ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 69:23
Text: Let their eyes be darkened, that they see not; and make their loins continually to shake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec14bb6b-4af4-4aee-b2a2-3eb140e11dd5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 69:24
Text: Pour out thine indignation upon them, and let thy wrathful anger take hold of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94fbcdd0-b9d0-4c7b-8dc3-4983a3e6711e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 69:25
Text: Let their habitation be desolate; and let none dwell in their tents.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebe5a385-e151-498f-ac5f-72b7a89afa08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PSA 69:26
Text: For they persecute him whom thou hast smitten; and they talk to the grief of those whom thou hast wounded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9eec677-5cb3-45ae-babc-f390b4c19a28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 69:27
Text: Add iniquity unto their iniquity: and let them not come into thy righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:217a7734-f0e1-475f-8458-71442d9ea0e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 69:28
Text: Let them be blotted out of the book of the living, and not be written with the righteous.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e99b5390-8155-418e-9c50-8731a3afc711>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 69:29
Text: But I am poor and sorrowful: let thy salvation, O God, set me up on high.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a1741b5-dac8-4058-8f4c-26994dfe7aa0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 69:30
Text: I will praise the name of God with a song, and will magnify him with thanksgiving.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8dff8414-0f9f-4176-8286-2eafdb910c9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 69:31
Text: This also shall please the LORD better than an ox or bullock that hath horns and hoofs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4edee8e4-1569-4ea0-a5a9-f4b198152a3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 69:32
Text: The humble shall see this, and be glad: and your heart shall live that seek God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3255e5a-b17c-49eb-b7da-0e0e64ae0467>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 69:33
Text: For the LORD heareth the poor, and despiseth not his prisoners.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d5cf3d9-0ed4-4b7b-b2d8-aea6cdb5b246>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 69:34
Text: Let the heaven and earth praise him, the seas, and every thing that moveth therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5caeb6b9-e1b2-46fb-b54c-8f9ab5af1f1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: PSA 69:35
Text: For God will save Zion, and will build the cities of Judah: that they may dwell there, and have it in possession.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/69/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:235e0b54-638d-4528-b18c-85111747ea9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 69:36
Text: The seed also of his servants shall inherit it: and they that love his name shall dwell therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/70/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fc609ee-e193-46a7-9a5d-215f9f978b69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 70:1
Text: Make haste, O God, to deliver me; make haste to help me, O Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/70/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:257c23a0-ac58-45f5-9a72-8dff8e54c5b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: PSA 70:2
Text: Let them be ashamed and confounded that seek after my soul: let them be turned backward, and put to confusion, that desire my hurt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/70/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33946f2d-dcbe-43c6-bdd2-9d05445856ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 70:3
Text: Let them be turned back for a reward of their shame that say, Aha, aha.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/70/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d28168b9-db74-4a7c-beda-e669f0b2a5f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: PSA 70:4
Text: Let all those that seek thee rejoice and be glad in thee: and let such as love thy salvation say continually, Let God be magnified.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/70/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24ce2bbf-8259-4bb1-a605-1ed29b18876d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: PSA 70:5
Text: But I am poor and needy: make haste unto me, O God: thou art my help and my deliverer; O LORD, make no tarrying.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46f1755f-37b2-4d80-b270-09aa0f57d7f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 71:1
Text: In thee, O LORD, do I put my trust: let me never be put to confusion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b53fdf6-8507-47f6-bf7c-f9fac040ce53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 71:2
Text: Deliver me in thy righteousness, and cause me to escape: incline thine ear unto me, and save me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb0fc2f0-da4a-44dd-8c8b-6ff28eb1a3e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: PSA 71:3
Text: Be thou my strong habitation, whereunto I may continually resort: thou hast given commandment to save me; for thou art my rock and my fortress.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34d9e1f3-0f9b-4442-981b-7d661d48058e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PSA 71:4
Text: Deliver me, O my God, out of the hand of the wicked, out of the hand of the unrighteous and cruel man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a385cfc3-e9d5-4a56-98c6-d257d3455b6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 71:5
Text: For thou art my hope, O Lord GOD: thou art my trust from my youth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31d13d2d-857b-4db9-a8fe-a18baf4dfcc7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: PSA 71:6
Text: By thee have I been holden up from the womb: thou art he that took me out of my mother’s bowels: my praise shall be continually of thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e670899e-b9f8-4775-9fdc-1726695d599c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: PSA 71:7
Text: I am as a wonder unto many; but thou art my strong refuge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b82181a-a9ff-40b4-aaaa-6a5f2896ac77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 71:8
Text: Let my mouth be filled with thy praise and with thy honour all the day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7258758-00ca-4021-ba4c-06fb21fe30f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 71:9
Text: Cast me not off in the time of old age; forsake me not when my strength faileth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3407a5f4-5abe-47d5-80de-ea51bf3f6d6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 71:10
Text: For mine enemies speak against me; and they that lay wait for my soul take counsel together,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b130b5b-adbf-4471-b6e7-6d37260c9b52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 71:11
Text: Saying, God hath forsaken him: persecute and take him; for there is none to deliver him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99783285-9401-4124-bee4-be6fe5cc1109>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 71:12
Text: O God, be not far from me: O my God, make haste for my help.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e77704f-faaa-4a01-b061-40cb8fc1120f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: PSA 71:13
Text: Let them be confounded and consumed that are adversaries to my soul; let them be covered with reproach and dishonour that seek my hurt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6e8c54e-cc74-48c1-af1f-f933172ea8fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 71:14
Text: But I will hope continually, and will yet praise thee more and more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2e7cd87-3314-4591-9f4c-6e843ca0808a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PSA 71:15
Text: My mouth shall shew forth thy righteousness and thy salvation all the day; for I know not the numbers thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df126df9-0304-49e8-b306-6b446e1a6808>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 71:16
Text: I will go in the strength of the Lord GOD: I will make mention of thy righteousness, even of thine only.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03fe5ab2-6637-48c5-8f13-a0a112222ef1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 71:17
Text: O God, thou hast taught me from my youth: and hitherto have I declared thy wondrous works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55e4ec2f-f5a0-4aee-8a26-318a4976567e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: PSA 71:18
Text: Now also when I am old and greyheaded, O God, forsake me not; until I have shewed thy strength unto this generation, and thy power to every one that is to come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:543b48bd-0014-48ea-846e-30e0cec37d56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 71:19
Text: Thy righteousness also, O God, is very high, who hast done great things: O God, who is like unto thee!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec3add88-ad39-4083-9dd9-4f35433f029b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: PSA 71:20
Text: Thou, which hast shewed me great and sore troubles, shalt quicken me again, and shalt bring me up again from the depths of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7db62ce7-65b1-468c-b29b-75457c558663>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 71:21
Text: Thou shalt increase my greatness, and comfort me on every side.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30858dda-1986-435e-b849-abe1886d1bc2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: PSA 71:22
Text: I will also praise thee with the psaltery, even thy truth, O my God: unto thee will I sing with the harp, O thou Holy One of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c0ca570-4a5d-4eb5-b34b-1a7686ae7719>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 71:23
Text: My lips shall greatly rejoice when I sing unto thee; and my soul, which thou hast redeemed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/71/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:516dc5cc-52cb-4928-8318-b4428614d702>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: PSA 71:24
Text: My tongue also shall talk of thy righteousness all the day long: for they are confounded, for they are brought unto shame, that seek my hurt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/72/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50a5102b-a601-4e63-8d17-7366aea3c1cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 72:1
Text: Give the king thy judgments, O God, and thy righteousness unto the king’s son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/72/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:989a9efd-a22f-4b39-9cde-9e5497c39e4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 72:2
Text: He shall judge thy people with righteousness, and thy poor with judgment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/72/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:256f971e-bb41-4aa4-9abd-6153032e1c22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 72:3
Text: The mountains shall bring peace to the people, and the little hills, by righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/72/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3669c552-2e28-4409-babd-e69d281a43d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: PSA 72:4
Text: He shall judge the poor of the people, he shall save the children of the needy, and shall break in pieces the oppressor.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/72/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c10f02e5-19cc-4bdd-a744-d2da9ff82054>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 72:5
Text: They shall fear thee as long as the sun and moon endure, throughout all generations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/72/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fee0e908-0b8c-4bee-a24e-1313a31a3615>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 72:6
Text: He shall come down like rain upon the mown grass: as showers that water the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/72/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b632041-a033-4218-9420-513393692105>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 72:7
Text: In his days shall the righteous flourish; and abundance of peace so long as the moon endureth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/72/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9c9bf66-67aa-41e6-a930-5e2a579777ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 72:8
Text: He shall have dominion also from sea to sea, and from the river unto the ends of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/72/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89142640-a85d-4a70-9f20-a8aed99ee344>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 72:9
Text: They that dwell in the wilderness shall bow before him; and his enemies shall lick the dust.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/72/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7bab1b58-ce61-4b90-bf72-04c3ad009119>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PSA 72:10
Text: The kings of Tarshish and of the isles shall bring presents: the kings of Sheba and Seba shall offer gifts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/72/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bc34cee-4b3a-4b44-af04-49a7eb47f263>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 72:11
Text: Yea, all kings shall fall down before him: all nations shall serve him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/72/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bfc889e9-b1cf-46ee-8f03-fcd58c056591>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 72:12
Text: For he shall deliver the needy when he crieth; the poor also, and him that hath no helper.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/72/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b77ccf6-5b1b-4d17-9ceb-d23d36791059>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 72:13
Text: He shall spare the poor and needy, and shall save the souls of the needy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/72/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b49d62c-4941-4271-8c04-954c1f2e069b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 72:14
Text: He shall redeem their soul from deceit and violence: and precious shall their blood be in his sight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/72/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef55bd21-13ab-4848-b20b-f524c0fbd467>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: PSA 72:15
Text: And he shall live, and to him shall be given of the gold of Sheba: prayer also shall be made for him continually; and daily shall he be praised.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/72/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0e5f510-f241-4d7b-9393-83d99879966f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: PSA 72:16
Text: There shall be an handful of corn in the earth upon the top of the mountains; the fruit thereof shall shake like Lebanon: and they of the city shall flourish like grass of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/72/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:feb4d44a-fca9-472a-9577-32c5286ca65c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: PSA 72:17
Text: His name shall endure for ever: his name shall be continued as long as the sun: and men shall be blessed in him: all nations shall call him blessed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/72/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39717042-8da1-4e04-8b48-246fab493465>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 72:18
Text: Blessed be the LORD God, the God of Israel, who only doeth wondrous things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/72/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d8fdf25-ceff-428b-b2de-ff3c7419a517>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PSA 72:19
Text: And blessed be his glorious name for ever: and let the whole earth be filled with his glory; Amen, and Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/72/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4276c417-439b-4541-939f-7539adc0c180>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: PSA 72:20
Text: The prayers of David the son of Jesse are ended.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f0ecc8f-3089-4783-9e37-858038ee4d01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 73:1
Text: Truly God is good to Israel, even to such as are of a clean heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d9d8023-e8a1-4932-be9e-b5de31935f44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 73:2
Text: But as for me, my feet were almost gone; my steps had well nigh slipped.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:429d20c1-138a-4dae-a10b-582bc0885ffd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 73:3
Text: For I was envious at the foolish, when I saw the prosperity of the wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd4ca13e-0309-4501-90f3-08d16ccc362b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 73:4
Text: For there are no bands in their death: but their strength is firm.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0cb4b8fe-e3f4-4685-b54f-522652b717e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 73:5
Text: They are not in trouble as other men; neither are they plagued like other men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1f693ee-fbbb-4668-b46a-15ae90ebc80e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 73:6
Text: Therefore pride compasseth them about as a chain; violence covereth them as a garment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e9169cb-55de-412e-a0fc-9e669fb76894>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 73:7
Text: Their eyes stand out with fatness: they have more than heart could wish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ecfcd028-f8a6-4554-a708-fb7470983442>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 73:8
Text: They are corrupt, and speak wickedly concerning oppression: they speak loftily.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66ece35b-6353-4738-b001-b0cbd665ae52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 73:9
Text: They set their mouth against the heavens, and their tongue walketh through the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4c91c51-50ac-42ea-a38f-94de30f01dba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 73:10
Text: Therefore his people return hither: and waters of a full cup are wrung out to them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e018540a-d83f-49bb-98cf-de67df405bd0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 73:11
Text: And they say, How doth God know? and is there knowledge in the most High?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:954b5fea-abf2-4813-b44b-cfad315e985a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 73:12
Text: Behold, these are the ungodly, who prosper in the world; they increase in riches.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3bc55105-1543-4809-bc7e-0634078283d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 73:13
Text: Verily I have cleansed my heart in vain, and washed my hands in innocency.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f350747e-91e0-4820-858b-23995e1c5271>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 73:14
Text: For all the day long have I been plagued, and chastened every morning.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f14a5836-442e-4073-bb4f-8c7770eb6e72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 73:15
Text: If I say, I will speak thus; behold, I should offend against the generation of thy children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f6b88bf-2f10-4c03-ba47-6b8188337dd3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: PSA 73:16
Text: When I thought to know this, it was too painful for me;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:faf27846-5893-4ac1-b2c7-31752b29a179>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 73:17
Text: Until I went into the sanctuary of God; then understood I their end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8c7a6bf-0be1-4b00-9a5d-368ebe6d914d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 73:18
Text: Surely thou didst set them in slippery places: thou castedst them down into destruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4cf2e350-0ac2-4fbd-985e-1ddfc0d12a49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 73:19
Text: How are they brought into desolation, as in a moment! they are utterly consumed with terrors.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d7146de-d159-4100-8a4b-ac06adfb288b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 73:20
Text: As a dream when one awaketh; so, O Lord, when thou awakest, thou shalt despise their image.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:408c857e-0ff5-43aa-b521-234e34caf330>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: PSA 73:21
Text: Thus my heart was grieved, and I was pricked in my reins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39fd9e15-9826-4da0-94c9-d2ac310d93b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 73:22
Text: So foolish was I, and ignorant: I was as a beast before thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a8d90fd-acda-4519-92e2-dfc5519b9c0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 73:23
Text: Nevertheless I am continually with thee: thou hast holden me by my right hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87a404d8-da0f-4721-9189-4ac205d7a763>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 73:24
Text: Thou shalt guide me with thy counsel, and afterward receive me to glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c26c8bc-ebd5-48a3-9e0a-3c0b4d1412f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 73:25
Text: Whom have I in heaven but thee? and there is none upon earth that I desire beside thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5fb41ba4-d0d9-4aa9-9e82-e5debe7d6545>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 73:26
Text: My flesh and my heart faileth: but God is the strength of my heart, and my portion for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e55212fc-f0c1-417a-aece-305072b51569>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PSA 73:27
Text: For, lo, they that are far from thee shall perish: thou hast destroyed all them that go a whoring from thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/73/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:219691df-ec42-4f45-adf6-ec5ddf79b028>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: PSA 73:28
Text: But it is good for me to draw near to God: I have put my trust in the Lord GOD, that I may declare all thy works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/74/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1a8e50e-47f1-4774-a339-ab810121bd9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 74:1
Text: O God, why hast thou cast us off for ever? why doth thine anger smoke against the sheep of thy pasture?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/74/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bef7aaa1-2b84-42b2-a606-1120d761f3f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: PSA 74:2
Text: Remember thy congregation, which thou hast purchased of old; the rod of thine inheritance, which thou hast redeemed; this mount Zion, wherein thou hast dwelt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/74/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee6f405d-8e2f-4743-b9d6-f782a207dd65>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PSA 74:3
Text: Lift up thy feet unto the perpetual desolations; even all that the enemy hath done wickedly in the sanctuary.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/74/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe7c435a-8b51-43ce-94b8-ae3c6c91006a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 74:4
Text: Thine enemies roar in the midst of thy congregations; they set up their ensigns for signs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/74/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:634c9fdd-59ee-4e2f-ae2e-0ddd7bcbaf68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 74:5
Text: A man was famous according as he had lifted up axes upon the thick trees.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/74/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b9e8603-f117-4e74-9a6d-21b24e6a5967>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 74:6
Text: But now they break down the carved work thereof at once with axes and hammers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/74/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d57e29c9-d87c-487e-ac9f-f457cf2780d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: PSA 74:7
Text: They have cast fire into thy sanctuary, they have defiled by casting down the dwelling place of thy name to the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/74/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:122c6b01-7b56-4426-816e-c4f099e4b0d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: PSA 74:8
Text: They said in their hearts, Let us destroy them together: they have burned up all the synagogues of God in the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/74/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a519b0e8-0078-4447-ae14-ebe1d5b1936f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 74:9
Text: We see not our signs: there is no more any prophet: neither is there among us any that knoweth how long.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/74/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37688875-62ce-406b-bbdd-de1f94ca67e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 74:10
Text: O God, how long shall the adversary reproach? shall the enemy blaspheme thy name for ever?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/74/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:484a6de8-0944-418a-8f83-b5c46b0fa546>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 74:11
Text: Why withdrawest thou thy hand, even thy right hand? pluck it out of thy bosom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/74/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69ae2396-324d-4a89-9460-3a9d9a3b27f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 74:12
Text: For God is my King of old, working salvation in the midst of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/74/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08ec423e-fe93-416b-9533-ff20e006508d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 74:13
Text: Thou didst divide the sea by thy strength: thou brakest the heads of the dragons in the waters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/74/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9d12e96-e7b2-4a74-a4b6-f734b071eeff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: PSA 74:14
Text: Thou brakest the heads of leviathan in pieces, and gavest him to be meat to the people inhabiting the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/74/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb76567d-6bf5-4f35-89dc-cae891eb851a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 74:15
Text: Thou didst cleave the fountain and the flood: thou driedst up mighty rivers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/74/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9239f910-34d6-4ec0-8f54-37a24ff6f6d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 74:16
Text: The day is thine, the night also is thine: thou hast prepared the light and the sun.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/74/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb7c6a02-14aa-4706-8884-7d2f192cab22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 74:17
Text: Thou hast set all the borders of the earth: thou hast made summer and winter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/74/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48dc60fd-5318-43b9-8d76-d40a072052fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PSA 74:18
Text: Remember this, that the enemy hath reproached, O LORD, and that the foolish people have blasphemed thy name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/74/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5831802b-0e92-41f8-842d-fdebbc85b33b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: PSA 74:19
Text: O deliver not the soul of thy turtledove unto the multitude of the wicked: forget not the congregation of thy poor for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/74/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d44703a-7774-4613-986b-e52c05610b27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 74:20
Text: Have respect unto the covenant: for the dark places of the earth are full of the habitations of cruelty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/74/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e59d7df2-1dc5-4a9b-8a35-9d163df8b136>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 74:21
Text: O let not the oppressed return ashamed: let the poor and needy praise thy name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/74/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d8a630f-ad87-47ed-832e-1f8e24572ea1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 74:22
Text: Arise, O God, plead thine own cause: remember how the foolish man reproacheth thee daily.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/74/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:822a8375-0369-4126-a4de-140580caad10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PSA 74:23
Text: Forget not the voice of thine enemies: the tumult of those that rise up against thee increaseth continually.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/75/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ec869d9-4f89-4ff2-a20b-c704fa30a88d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: PSA 75:1
Text: Unto thee, O God, do we give thanks, unto thee do we give thanks: for that thy name is near thy wondrous works declare.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/75/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d34b423-38b6-4fa4-a725-5ff20ed6ef5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 75:2
Text: When I shall receive the congregation I will judge uprightly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/75/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3b19025-3dd6-4e45-950b-24bcc59644b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 75:3
Text: The earth and all the inhabitants thereof are dissolved: I bear up the pillars of it. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/75/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d5411a4-7415-40a8-ba77-3280bf62e4c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 75:4
Text: I said unto the fools, Deal not foolishly: and to the wicked, Lift not up the horn:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/75/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a9afaad-7507-4167-aa7a-6f1c4ddcec4f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PSA 75:5
Text: Lift not up your horn on high: speak not with a stiff neck.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/75/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abf3b5e9-659f-4446-b180-9867dc3d961d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 75:6
Text: For promotion cometh neither from the east, nor from the west, nor from the south.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/75/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eed3f118-9268-4aa8-ad2b-d7978328957f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 75:7
Text: But God is the judge: he putteth down one, and setteth up another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/75/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:524cab0d-2e53-4af4-a8e7-9df994116f5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: PSA 75:8
Text: For in the hand of the LORD there is a cup, and the wine is red; it is full of mixture; and he poureth out of the same: but the dregs thereof, all the wicked of the earth shall wring them out, and drink them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/75/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00697a7b-6c26-4664-918a-e87da94cf8bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 75:9
Text: But I will declare for ever; I will sing praises to the God of Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/75/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54a6c1c0-e128-40f8-9f91-2a8bb08603e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 75:10
Text: All the horns of the wicked also will I cut off; but the horns of the righteous shall be exalted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/76/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f19f3bf-1ca7-4d1b-ac1c-03e2932b9710>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: PSA 76:1
Text: In Judah is God known: his name is great in Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/76/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:399934e6-4d9e-4024-bac5-950246828091>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 76:2
Text: In Salem also is his tabernacle, and his dwelling place in Zion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/76/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6c46157-cc6f-43b7-aeb8-7867d2c20928>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 76:3
Text: There brake he the arrows of the bow, the shield, and the sword, and the battle. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/76/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c59ccde-75b6-482c-b63b-e93d1c105d3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 76:4
Text: Thou art more glorious and excellent than the mountains of prey.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/76/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2481c3a-2610-4bca-9875-e99675e99f91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PSA 76:5
Text: The stouthearted are spoiled, they have slept their sleep: and none of the men of might have found their hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/76/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a970de2d-3507-442e-aaaa-75bb0408d7f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 76:6
Text: At thy rebuke, O God of Jacob, both the chariot and horse are cast into a dead sleep.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/76/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bfd30bf5-6a9a-43b6-a91b-9611f1ab013c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 76:7
Text: Thou, even thou, art to be feared: and who may stand in thy sight when once thou art angry?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/76/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37698d50-3230-4b0f-ac42-2e2e0a268dee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 76:8
Text: Thou didst cause judgment to be heard from heaven; the earth feared, and was still,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/76/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b68bf90-c2fb-44b3-bdda-f49b8db56df1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 76:9
Text: When God arose to judgment, to save all the meek of the earth. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/76/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb3dbee8-03c9-4a03-8857-755f338d2584>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 76:10
Text: Surely the wrath of man shall praise thee: the remainder of wrath shalt thou restrain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/76/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5c6cc06-a631-4096-9ba8-b8f4c82ef606>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: PSA 76:11
Text: Vow, and pay unto the LORD your God: let all that be round about him bring presents unto him that ought to be feared.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/76/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edf87cc0-ed49-4e7e-ac81-efa300eccfbe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 76:12
Text: He shall cut off the spirit of princes: he is terrible to the kings of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/77/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9e5f907-51e9-478d-996a-25423f0b4ef1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 77:1
Text: I cried unto God with my voice, even unto God with my voice; and he gave ear unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/77/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ceda5e6d-64d9-4f1e-adb7-a053ab647382>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: PSA 77:2
Text: In the day of my trouble I sought the Lord: my sore ran in the night, and ceased not: my soul refused to be comforted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/77/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7eb75b2c-0228-4776-932f-c1a8e571ea01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 77:3
Text: I remembered God, and was troubled: I complained, and my spirit was overwhelmed. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/77/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20f401a6-432d-40d8-be74-da649f2421d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 77:4
Text: Thou holdest mine eyes waking: I am so troubled that I cannot speak.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/77/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5abe5da-b5fd-4972-95cf-f6e9ac1d16f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 77:5
Text: I have considered the days of old, the years of ancient times.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/77/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1473356c-615c-45fb-b6c7-2052fbeb0d82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: PSA 77:6
Text: I call to remembrance my song in the night: I commune with mine own heart: and my spirit made diligent search.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/77/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8dfb3869-fc75-430e-9956-cefebb6463d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 77:7
Text: Will the Lord cast off for ever? and will he be favourable no more?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/77/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9e53f00-1931-4272-8b5b-31ebe1935b5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 77:8
Text: Is his mercy clean gone for ever? doth his promise fail for evermore?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/77/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24016ef8-31e8-4b2a-8b0a-99f3268a54c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 77:9
Text: Hath God forgotten to be gracious? hath he in anger shut up his tender mercies? Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/77/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5369d5db-fcac-4e94-8dcc-13bb0ac3ea0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PSA 77:10
Text: And I said, This is my infirmity: but I will remember the years of the right hand of the most High.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/77/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b730ea2b-e3fc-4296-8f5c-7db8f3b52a0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 77:11
Text: I will remember the works of the LORD: surely I will remember thy wonders of old.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/77/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7a79794-3105-49c9-8603-4962bc8f1446>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 77:12
Text: I will meditate also of all thy work, and talk of thy doings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/77/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce77398a-0c6b-4200-bbf9-03982e945d9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 77:13
Text: Thy way, O God, is in the sanctuary: who is so great a God as our God?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/77/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:928cca43-b9b3-4742-b2d1-eaff8b1b0ab4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 77:14
Text: Thou art the God that doest wonders: thou hast declared thy strength among the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/77/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70dbc018-65fb-4a32-8fb5-f72409ad425b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 77:15
Text: Thou hast with thine arm redeemed thy people, the sons of Jacob and Joseph. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/77/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28d3ea2c-5a2d-41ce-800a-41dbf1f71ca5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 77:16
Text: The waters saw thee, O God, the waters saw thee; they were afraid: the depths also were troubled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/77/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af4fe8c4-edc6-4fb6-b4fb-549a819dbef2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 77:17
Text: The clouds poured out water: the skies sent out a sound: thine arrows also went abroad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/77/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:664dcfa0-7683-4766-8d42-7fc7963e9c46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: PSA 77:18
Text: The voice of thy thunder was in the heaven: the lightnings lightened the world: the earth trembled and shook.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/77/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be89a235-e2e5-4a1b-ac38-5a61f0dc8171>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 77:19
Text: Thy way is in the sea, and thy path in the great waters, and thy footsteps are not known.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/77/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:faa0ef6e-1f30-4b14-9d8d-8c3752f87a5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 77:20
Text: Thou leddest thy people like a flock by the hand of Moses and Aaron.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59dcd5a8-f1d8-44c5-8fec-1ce524fe0768>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 78:1
Text: Give ear, O my people, to my law: incline your ears to the words of my mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:580c9c8c-cd29-42b0-86b8-0eaa4340efde>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 78:2
Text: I will open my mouth in a parable: I will utter dark sayings of old:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95c24a0d-fe17-4c32-85a1-07f70598a985>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PSA 78:3
Text: Which we have heard and known, and our fathers have told us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf8464a7-34cc-4d77-b7a9-8943a158bcd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: PSA 78:4
Text: We will not hide them from their children, shewing to the generation to come the praises of the LORD, and his strength, and his wonderful works that he hath done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e27d495-daf9-4147-acbb-dadcbd4bba78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: PSA 78:5
Text: For he established a testimony in Jacob, and appointed a law in Israel, which he commanded our fathers, that they should make them known to their children:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e94a3471-30ef-452f-a6cc-0e11961e9522>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: PSA 78:6
Text: That the generation to come might know them, even the children which should be born; who should arise and declare them to their children:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62dd9a51-41c5-4364-ba99-e8ca4f035f1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 78:7
Text: That they might set their hope in God, and not forget the works of God, but keep his commandments:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c2d8b58-1fd6-442c-833f-4dd271a2fb1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: PSA 78:8
Text: And might not be as their fathers, a stubborn and rebellious generation; a generation that set not their heart aright, and whose spirit was not stedfast with God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e14581ce-08dc-440d-8090-8c638132b7aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 78:9
Text: The children of Ephraim, being armed, and carrying bows, turned back in the day of battle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ffdb243-2388-4320-9f4c-4f48cef058f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 78:10
Text: They kept not the covenant of God, and refused to walk in his law;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:704e377c-f594-4dbf-8668-b4407ed9a058>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 78:11
Text: And forgat his works, and his wonders that he had shewed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c3ccd6d-e626-4216-9af4-a635e6d094c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PSA 78:12
Text: Marvellous things did he in the sight of their fathers, in the land of Egypt, in the field of Zoan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e6a1d8d-2f25-43bf-84db-5310e661474c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 78:13
Text: He divided the sea, and caused them to pass through; and he made the waters to stand as an heap.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e301461-0651-4cc3-a6e1-da889e274928>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 78:14
Text: In the daytime also he led them with a cloud, and all the night with a light of fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07087d29-72d5-4deb-a69d-6828398d6b6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 78:15
Text: He clave the rocks in the wilderness, and gave them drink as out of the great depths.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ca977e5-bd1e-486e-949a-b422cc1c2c9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 78:16
Text: He brought streams also out of the rock, and caused waters to run down like rivers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5cf83625-c51c-4e86-a36d-fb2c1d0098ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 78:17
Text: And they sinned yet more against him by provoking the most High in the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8175f66-9750-46b7-b025-02578e712fc5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 78:18
Text: And they tempted God in their heart by asking meat for their lust.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:404591bf-3032-4a98-865f-36e074ca7e16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 78:19
Text: Yea, they spake against God; they said, Can God furnish a table in the wilderness?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73d2d460-91a9-46c6-8da6-75f5e5704569>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: PSA 78:20
Text: Behold, he smote the rock, that the waters gushed out, and the streams overflowed; can he give bread also? can he provide flesh for his people?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91a85428-5172-4dc4-9a5b-ddfd0867d980>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: PSA 78:21
Text: Therefore the LORD heard this, and was wroth: so a fire was kindled against Jacob, and anger also came up against Israel;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:201ba5e8-d4c8-4cc8-a3aa-4e8e3c664049>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 78:22
Text: Because they believed not in God, and trusted not in his salvation:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0b785ba-6d85-4c10-9b77-027922e80aa5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 78:23
Text: Though he had commanded the clouds from above, and opened the doors of heaven,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8486b604-28d8-444f-a13a-b2257d3a175b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 78:24
Text: And had rained down manna upon them to eat, and had given them of the corn of heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bc50e40-a1fc-4707-a8da-58a56a2953ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PSA 78:25
Text: Man did eat angels’ food: he sent them meat to the full.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9f28d0d-3f3e-45be-af66-4f19fab2d8f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 78:26
Text: He caused an east wind to blow in the heaven: and by his power he brought in the south wind.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ff0ded0-45c3-42aa-bda4-0a33f73b80b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 78:27
Text: He rained flesh also upon them as dust, and feathered fowls like as the sand of the sea:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2122415-37b4-4b16-b61b-6db1ef75df4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 78:28
Text: And he let it fall in the midst of their camp, round about their habitations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bc6019f-0f33-4ce1-ba40-80b145f8e0f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 78:29
Text: So they did eat, and were well filled: for he gave them their own desire;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b33fc0a-487c-427f-8f30-ad6a386255fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 78:30
Text: They were not estranged from their lust. But while their meat was yet in their mouths,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67d4adb7-2863-4bfc-8564-9ea9408b72e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 78:31
Text: The wrath of God came upon them, and slew the fattest of them, and smote down the chosen men of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0683f4fb-a064-458e-a330-b85c2a070dab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 78:32
Text: For all this they sinned still, and believed not for his wondrous works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e64dcdf8-2ef0-4a3b-86fd-6c59e160c472>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 78:33
Text: Therefore their days did he consume in vanity, and their years in trouble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc263b46-6738-45ec-9985-ca55f95d40e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 78:34
Text: When he slew them, then they sought him: and they returned and enquired early after God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8cb48189-89ba-4e79-a853-f1ab6d22339d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 78:35
Text: And they remembered that God was their rock, and the high God their redeemer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2ab0e0a-c2d3-497a-a1bd-3a114d154019>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 78:36
Text: Nevertheless they did flatter him with their mouth, and they lied unto him with their tongues.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f09b6584-322b-428b-abef-ed7a51bb9a30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 78:37
Text: For their heart was not right with him, neither were they stedfast in his covenant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6ba7b5c-ac20-4e6b-8cba-705b610c6fe0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: PSA 78:38
Text: But he, being full of compassion, forgave their iniquity, and destroyed them not: yea, many a time turned he his anger away, and did not stir up all his wrath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b216675-6d54-4905-ae16-c4c48e9a6c54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 78:39
Text: For he remembered that they were but flesh; a wind that passeth away, and cometh not again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1803d86c-d8e9-4959-8ff8-5f0dadcfcca7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 78:40
Text: How oft did they provoke him in the wilderness, and grieve him in the desert!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:477a6f31-bfc3-4df8-b0f9-dc962e9f20a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 78:41
Text: Yea, they turned back and tempted God, and limited the Holy One of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5163b968-2458-432e-ac0b-0221a98a97d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 78:42
Text: They remembered not his hand, nor the day when he delivered them from the enemy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fac6af0-6fdc-47dc-b0c0-98cb4f5eda37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 78:43
Text: How he had wrought his signs in Egypt, and his wonders in the field of Zoan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c9b1675-1fae-4cdf-b8ab-c76c602dce59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 78:44
Text: And had turned their rivers into blood; and their floods, that they could not drink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e32fd7c-6da1-4995-ab8a-2b6471bdbe33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 78:45
Text: He sent divers sorts of flies among them, which devoured them; and frogs, which destroyed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd73e0b4-ca8f-4895-a4c2-fcfdde51416f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 78:46
Text: He gave also their increase unto the caterpiller, and their labour unto the locust.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a13d8b43-42a0-4f36-963d-6b83789d008d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 78:47
Text: He destroyed their vines with hail, and their sycomore trees with frost.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa6769af-a923-448a-b3d1-0f4a38bb4689>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 78:48
Text: He gave up their cattle also to the hail, and their flocks to hot thunderbolts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e526792a-2ef2-4c3f-85dd-7cb70d5bf2d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: PSA 78:49
Text: He cast upon them the fierceness of his anger, wrath, and indignation, and trouble, by sending evil angels among them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05a5b4ad-f1e4-4b97-a191-28cdc14268f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PSA 78:50
Text: He made a way to his anger; he spared not their soul from death, but gave their life over to the pestilence;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f94793da-327d-42bc-b0cb-447743470e57>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 78:51
Text: And smote all the firstborn in Egypt; the chief of their strength in the tabernacles of Ham:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:170e6f97-a348-47c0-9d95-9116f242147f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 78:52
Text: But made his own people to go forth like sheep, and guided them in the wilderness like a flock.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c9367dc-d05e-4c10-a5e9-1c8a31283993>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 78:53
Text: And he led them on safely, so that they feared not: but the sea overwhelmed their enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da6f0762-66ba-4611-8a5f-ed2395dae014>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PSA 78:54
Text: And he brought them to the border of his sanctuary, even to this mountain, which his right hand had purchased.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/55
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e118152-8502-470c-adc9-d15204340dbc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: PSA 78:55
Text: He cast out the heathen also before them, and divided them an inheritance by line, and made the tribes of Israel to dwell in their tents.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/56
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f15a115c-d490-4e54-b6fa-ef5414d20330>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 78:56
Text: Yet they tempted and provoked the most high God, and kept not his testimonies:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/57
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad30d371-7bea-4c51-9620-445650763c69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 78:57
Text: But turned back, and dealt unfaithfully like their fathers: they were turned aside like a deceitful bow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/58
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19907723-558a-4d24-b82d-27fce62a849e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PSA 78:58
Text: For they provoked him to anger with their high places, and moved him to jealousy with their graven images.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/59
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20606e54-50a4-41bb-bc94-c8d84e990c56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 78:59
Text: When God heard this, he was wroth, and greatly abhorred Israel:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/60
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42294630-2b5f-4b37-aaa3-18a3add4158c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 78:60
Text: So that he forsook the tabernacle of Shiloh, the tent which he placed among men;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/61
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2acb7612-ccc8-4d58-951b-b8dc6cd0e26b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 78:61
Text: And delivered his strength into captivity, and his glory into the enemy’s hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/62
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:321c490f-6f4f-4c22-94fb-b2cf63007a8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 78:62
Text: He gave his people over also unto the sword; and was wroth with his inheritance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/63
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3aaabe80-8f82-4bd8-94c3-d6fb0f49373e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 78:63
Text: The fire consumed their young men; and their maidens were not given to marriage.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/64
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3d09904-3d7b-413a-9966-6d37be66af4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 78:64
Text: Their priests fell by the sword; and their widows made no lamentation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/65
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:151d3543-fe6b-45df-878d-1cedfbf79735>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 78:65
Text: Then the LORD awaked as one out of sleep, and like a mighty man that shouteth by reason of wine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/66
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f68bdb5-2257-4186-8850-cb6feb7d7648>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 78:66
Text: And he smote his enemies in the hinder parts: he put them to a perpetual reproach.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/67
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:823b4f68-a668-489c-96f0-595b7873c22e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 78:67
Text: Moreover he refused the tabernacle of Joseph, and chose not the tribe of Ephraim:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/68
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:141f74d2-7688-467a-83b3-fe363a715290>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 78:68
Text: But chose the tribe of Judah, the mount Zion which he loved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/69
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9720d81f-9e32-4a20-b4cd-681360c5aee4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 78:69
Text: And he built his sanctuary like high palaces, like the earth which he hath established for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/70
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe060103-501d-413a-add9-5572e4e8ce7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 78:70
Text: He chose David also his servant, and took him from the sheepfolds:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/71
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:303eb86b-5b20-4142-8ec3-c9e53ba16805>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: PSA 78:71
Text: From following the ewes great with young he brought him to feed Jacob his people, and Israel his inheritance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/78/72
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8bacbeea-007f-474d-b107-fc5063ff8c33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 78:72
Text: So he fed them according to the integrity of his heart; and guided them by the skilfulness of his hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/79/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73fd9efb-56df-4a73-a077-1de46a493f4f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: PSA 79:1
Text: O God, the heathen are come into thine inheritance; thy holy temple have they defiled; they have laid Jerusalem on heaps.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/79/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91085c87-91e3-41bc-9d4a-49325f4992e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: PSA 79:2
Text: The dead bodies of thy servants have they given to be meat unto the fowls of the heaven, the flesh of thy saints unto the beasts of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/79/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16eda17c-732f-4324-a5e2-d7ac92c57d3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 79:3
Text: Their blood have they shed like water round about Jerusalem; and there was none to bury them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/79/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1e57743-e14c-436c-b50c-e4694f31c7e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 79:4
Text: We are become a reproach to our neighbours, a scorn and derision to them that are round about us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/79/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b1d1b42-cd38-488b-8cb9-fcb07d6f0767>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 79:5
Text: How long, LORD? wilt thou be angry for ever? shall thy jealousy burn like fire?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/79/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e30d9415-9828-48be-a62f-ded8a68ed607>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: PSA 79:6
Text: Pour out thy wrath upon the heathen that have not known thee, and upon the kingdoms that have not called upon thy name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/79/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78ba33bd-a77f-4590-ac20-ac59e378b253>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 79:7
Text: For they have devoured Jacob, and laid waste his dwelling place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/79/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34306606-394f-4643-bbbc-66aa443ba466>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: PSA 79:8
Text: O remember not against us former iniquities: let thy tender mercies speedily prevent us: for we are brought very low.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/79/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5c814ff-e204-49db-832a-4f9a8566f2e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: PSA 79:9
Text: Help us, O God of our salvation, for the glory of thy name: and deliver us, and purge away our sins, for thy name’s sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/79/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d609f21b-aeb1-4b17-b3b2-8b7d5c483708>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: PSA 79:10
Text: Wherefore should the heathen say, Where is their God? let him be known among the heathen in our sight by the revenging of the blood of thy servants which is shed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/79/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cacf39d-c1fa-4558-addd-0a088c26d152>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: PSA 79:11
Text: Let the sighing of the prisoner come before thee; according to the greatness of thy power preserve thou those that are appointed to die;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/79/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0f30862-0900-431f-8e5e-04f9fd6d72bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: PSA 79:12
Text: And render unto our neighbours sevenfold into their bosom their reproach, wherewith they have reproached thee, O Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/79/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72d432d5-bff9-49cd-aa73-e2ce41720758>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: PSA 79:13
Text: So we thy people and sheep of thy pasture will give thee thanks for ever: we will shew forth thy praise to all generations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/80/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2efaea4-ecc6-45c6-a09e-0cc1ac1beae3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: PSA 80:1
Text: Give ear, O Shepherd of Israel, thou that leadest Joseph like a flock; thou that dwellest between the cherubims, shine forth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/80/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:976826c9-d0be-46b0-89eb-9dc0b28221bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 80:2
Text: Before Ephraim and Benjamin and Manasseh stir up thy strength, and come and save us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/80/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8a59db8-0e16-4642-8536-a32dee1872ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 80:3
Text: Turn us again, O God, and cause thy face to shine; and we shall be saved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/80/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52d2b599-5c11-4bdd-87c2-8b191413fa0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 80:4
Text: O LORD God of hosts, how long wilt thou be angry against the prayer of thy people?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/80/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28580788-6191-4e9b-b842-9b65de691c24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 80:5
Text: Thou feedest them with the bread of tears; and givest them tears to drink in great measure.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/80/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f91660b-4e1e-447e-b0e5-b5d233e33b8e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 80:6
Text: Thou makest us a strife unto our neighbours: and our enemies laugh among themselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/80/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5807f3f-f153-4004-9495-ed0cbd7ae5a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 80:7
Text: Turn us again, O God of hosts, and cause thy face to shine; and we shall be saved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/80/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46a08cbf-2f08-45c9-91a9-be9a9a85195a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 80:8
Text: Thou hast brought a vine out of Egypt: thou hast cast out the heathen, and planted it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/80/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c4f0786-e446-4845-a2f8-5868284c4e3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 80:9
Text: Thou preparedst room before it, and didst cause it to take deep root, and it filled the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/80/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cca2ead9-c28c-470a-93c3-77b00a9151ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 80:10
Text: The hills were covered with the shadow of it, and the boughs thereof were like the goodly cedars.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/80/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5b30b2b-acea-4d9c-96e3-08bc0970597d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 80:11
Text: She sent out her boughs unto the sea, and her branches unto the river.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/80/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f18777ee-2552-410f-ab94-3f4084f1d282>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 80:12
Text: Why hast thou then broken down her hedges, so that all they which pass by the way do pluck her?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/80/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:839d6a1d-c263-46a3-8115-209230696a7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 80:13
Text: The boar out of the wood doth waste it, and the wild beast of the field doth devour it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/80/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:221c1779-66e3-4050-bb63-b326677135f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 80:14
Text: Return, we beseech thee, O God of hosts: look down from heaven, and behold, and visit this vine;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/80/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a27e8750-30ea-41f2-b36a-b5535c5a231f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 80:15
Text: And the vineyard which thy right hand hath planted, and the branch that thou madest strong for thyself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/80/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8c93af0-32a5-4676-87eb-2ae61c93f69b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 80:16
Text: It is burned with fire, it is cut down: they perish at the rebuke of thy countenance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/80/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9108d87-46ad-4dfb-9967-6113cdd6cb65>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 80:17
Text: Let thy hand be upon the man of thy right hand, upon the son of man whom thou madest strong for thyself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/80/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:684f1e24-d990-49aa-94b0-2f07ba5f7003>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 80:18
Text: So will not we go back from thee: quicken us, and we will call upon thy name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/80/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b883950f-495b-41ad-980c-9d1b6aefc39a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 80:19
Text: Turn us again, O LORD God of hosts, cause thy face to shine; and we shall be saved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/81/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53937521-f1c6-48ef-96fc-60fc12d7cc0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 81:1
Text: Sing aloud unto God our strength: make a joyful noise unto the God of Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/81/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b7aace9-7152-4d37-8ac7-3ca67421732c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 81:2
Text: Take a psalm, and bring hither the timbrel, the pleasant harp with the psaltery.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/81/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ccf21131-0afd-4023-bcc3-434fbc777528>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 81:3
Text: Blow up the trumpet in the new moon, in the time appointed, on our solemn feast day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/81/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a147d8d0-ac25-4472-9653-bb1204a0035c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PSA 81:4
Text: For this was a statute for Israel, and a law of the God of Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/81/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8348dab-ede5-442c-aa2d-b3f8c467c8b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: PSA 81:5
Text: This he ordained in Joseph for a testimony, when he went out through the land of Egypt: where I heard a language that I understood not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/81/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1af9c702-b5f7-498c-97bc-744fbbc53680>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 81:6
Text: I removed his shoulder from the burden: his hands were delivered from the pots.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/81/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95869de1-99f7-4ad7-8dcf-a80712195fc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: PSA 81:7
Text: Thou calledst in trouble, and I delivered thee; I answered thee in the secret place of thunder: I proved thee at the waters of Meribah. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/81/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd8c0e00-0e66-4290-a94a-dd482b168445>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 81:8
Text: Hear, O my people, and I will testify unto thee: O Israel, if thou wilt hearken unto me;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/81/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:238934ed-2d09-4811-835d-4848c6e550c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 81:9
Text: There shall no strange god be in thee; neither shalt thou worship any strange god.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/81/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:954541af-24eb-4a28-a2af-4be70f4896d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PSA 81:10
Text: I am the LORD thy God, which brought thee out of the land of Egypt: open thy mouth wide, and I will fill it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/81/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:836c1393-1096-4789-85eb-921d13efade8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 81:11
Text: But my people would not hearken to my voice; and Israel would none of me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/81/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e87f7cfa-e9f8-4c82-9fe0-5c7af935b603>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 81:12
Text: So I gave them up unto their own hearts’ lust: and they walked in their own counsels.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/81/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:854576d4-a0db-4f22-b824-30f60211c504>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 81:13
Text: Oh that my people had hearkened unto me, and Israel had walked in my ways!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/81/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1c44d59-77e1-4559-a478-ba96320bb4de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 81:14
Text: I should soon have subdued their enemies, and turned my hand against their adversaries.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/81/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c6c7b15-f7a2-4295-9163-392dc808ce95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PSA 81:15
Text: The haters of the LORD should have submitted themselves unto him: but their time should have endured for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/81/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cdf3c9f9-e31c-4fc8-b862-3868c6651848>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: PSA 81:16
Text: He should have fed them also with the finest of the wheat: and with honey out of the rock should I have satisfied thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/82/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95420e04-857f-4432-8ef4-ef21c21a4417>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 82:1
Text: God standeth in the congregation of the mighty; he judgeth among the gods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/82/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1655ef3c-7b88-4fe8-b1a5-2c719056614e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 82:2
Text: How long will ye judge unjustly, and accept the persons of the wicked? Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/82/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:518e2ede-9574-4ec1-90fd-d1fa0d8804d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 82:3
Text: Defend the poor and fatherless: do justice to the afflicted and needy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/82/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea5c1315-aac0-4ea6-a9a0-4df565487e43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 82:4
Text: Deliver the poor and needy: rid them out of the hand of the wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/82/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7bdd457-87b0-442c-95fd-1ef55ee3f8c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: PSA 82:5
Text: They know not, neither will they understand; they walk on in darkness: all the foundations of the earth are out of course.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/82/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbab2f2c-d0ca-4c6d-82a6-34c976a43549>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 82:6
Text: I have said, Ye are gods; and all of you are children of the most High.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/82/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93f4b139-31e0-416c-aa54-ab51ef705798>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PSA 82:7
Text: But ye shall die like men, and fall like one of the princes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/82/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:223103f6-b3aa-47b9-a7fc-78a5ac9ac788>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 82:8
Text: Arise, O God, judge the earth: for thou shalt inherit all nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/83/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:950684ba-6ba2-4cf3-a36f-5fd68e234889>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 83:1
Text: Keep not thou silence, O God: hold not thy peace, and be not still, O God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/83/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f1b368b-f22d-4fcc-8139-418a90bfabfa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 83:2
Text: For, lo, thine enemies make a tumult: and they that hate thee have lifted up the head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/83/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88f2ea5e-9c57-49c1-80de-f1972548fdce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 83:3
Text: They have taken crafty counsel against thy people, and consulted against thy hidden ones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/83/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0a21e33-9bda-41a4-bfea-90452219f748>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: PSA 83:4
Text: They have said, Come, and let us cut them off from being a nation; that the name of Israel may be no more in remembrance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/83/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c70c6ce-b543-4803-a3bc-fb7b580c574f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 83:5
Text: For they have consulted together with one consent: they are confederate against thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/83/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f18c120-204a-4be7-9f8a-82bfcfaf1b36>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 83:6
Text: The tabernacles of Edom, and the Ishmaelites; of Moab, and the Hagarenes;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/83/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37eb3655-7295-4950-a824-b33b2da2fecb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 83:7
Text: Gebal, and Ammon, and Amalek; the Philistines with the inhabitants of Tyre;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/83/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0645b54-836c-45f9-bc06-01f1fabef615>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 83:8
Text: Assur also is joined with them: they have holpen the children of Lot. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/83/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fae1b572-d2b3-41b4-ba1b-94e8ca490390>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 83:9
Text: Do unto them as unto the Midianites; as to Sisera, as to Jabin, at the brook of Kison:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/83/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e5a91a5-ef83-455e-bf43-dae7b4d10a8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PSA 83:10
Text: Which perished at Endor: they became as dung for the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/83/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:baed704c-8e9a-4716-8a61-13e8d1b1903c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 83:11
Text: Make their nobles like Oreb, and like Zeeb: yea, all their princes as Zebah, and as Zalmunna:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/83/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63e96816-90b9-47a0-84d8-3d97dd77ae6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 83:12
Text: Who said, Let us take to ourselves the houses of God in possession.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/83/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4876fb5b-314c-47dd-97d6-dd890cf61897>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 83:13
Text: O my God, make them like a wheel; as the stubble before the wind.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/83/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50ba9b11-8f07-42e7-8087-f5ef52ea63fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 83:14
Text: As the fire burneth a wood, and as the flame setteth the mountains on fire;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/83/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ca1a105-779d-49a7-be34-f2778c39e649>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 83:15
Text: So persecute them with thy tempest, and make them afraid with thy storm.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/83/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86447cda-36bc-411e-a35b-a911f641b4cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 83:16
Text: Fill their faces with shame; that they may seek thy name, O LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/83/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4885f075-91ad-482a-9a44-aad83442c1d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 83:17
Text: Let them be confounded and troubled for ever; yea, let them be put to shame, and perish:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/83/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7610e9c1-41f0-4e32-bb67-545f80243f11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 83:18
Text: That men may know that thou, whose name alone is JEHOVAH, art the most high over all the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/84/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56b3ad72-5e2c-4929-a651-2a5b9bd56302>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: PSA 84:1
Text: How amiable are thy tabernacles, O LORD of hosts!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/84/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba24e4d7-eded-4fec-a53e-486b1e052cf4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: PSA 84:2
Text: My soul longeth, yea, even fainteth for the courts of the LORD: my heart and my flesh crieth out for the living God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/84/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5de10e08-4bdf-4dff-afc6-76d43a65bd06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: PSA 84:3
Text: Yea, the sparrow hath found an house, and the swallow a nest for herself, where she may lay her young, even thine altars, O LORD of hosts, my King, and my God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/84/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89c7e477-5f6d-40c7-8458-bbcdbbf7cd8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 84:4
Text: Blessed are they that dwell in thy house: they will be still praising thee. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/84/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16b2a9fc-a67d-40a2-bc70-f8d7e6dbd82c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 84:5
Text: Blessed is the man whose strength is in thee; in whose heart are the ways of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/84/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18fe1819-490f-4a6a-bf5f-8009b66821b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 84:6
Text: Who passing through the valley of Baca make it a well; the rain also filleth the pools.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/84/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38bc59fa-b620-49a5-bb43-e6e94191ed11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 84:7
Text: They go from strength to strength, every one of them in Zion appeareth before God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/84/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7ca43d8-6aeb-4d65-b00b-5eca006041b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 84:8
Text: O LORD God of hosts, hear my prayer: give ear, O God of Jacob. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/84/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b5f6c37-0257-456f-9bcc-3249b267978e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 84:9
Text: Behold, O God our shield, and look upon the face of thine anointed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/84/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e247b06-6d99-4f66-89a4-5a30dc8e03c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: PSA 84:10
Text: For a day in thy courts is better than a thousand. I had rather be a doorkeeper in the house of my God, than to dwell in the tents of wickedness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/84/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c84c0829-1c41-4851-9129-a25c6518c76c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: PSA 84:11
Text: For the LORD God is a sun and shield: the LORD will give grace and glory: no good thing will he withhold from them that walk uprightly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/84/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea106c40-2d12-4fc6-addf-fb918a673368>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PSA 84:12
Text: O LORD of hosts, blessed is the man that trusteth in thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/85/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72f2b5d7-46dc-4dfb-8046-b66322e4043f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 85:1
Text: Lord, thou hast been favourable unto thy land: thou hast brought back the captivity of Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/85/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:419af8c9-027c-4333-8321-65c160b935e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 85:2
Text: Thou hast forgiven the iniquity of thy people, thou hast covered all their sin. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/85/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad48d3d4-1350-4d9d-96ae-fe91c3c7c59b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 85:3
Text: Thou hast taken away all thy wrath: thou hast turned thyself from the fierceness of thine anger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/85/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bae28dd-875c-4cb4-b05d-dad8c35f8c22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 85:4
Text: Turn us, O God of our salvation, and cause thine anger toward us to cease.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/85/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:621e23ce-38c6-4c23-be9a-61c03dd43380>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 85:5
Text: Wilt thou be angry with us for ever? wilt thou draw out thine anger to all generations?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/85/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e314b10e-fdab-4026-b97d-4acf1cb73ec2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 85:6
Text: Wilt thou not revive us again: that thy people may rejoice in thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/85/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b1d3b22-218f-44b1-9291-00a9b78c3cfe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: PSA 85:7
Text: Shew us thy mercy, O LORD, and grant us thy salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/85/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:378e3298-003e-4b39-93e1-df10e5b04303>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: PSA 85:8
Text: I will hear what God the LORD will speak: for he will speak peace unto his people, and to his saints: but let them not turn again to folly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/85/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d05e969c-f770-4cd0-b3c7-cb58d4b0e459>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 85:9
Text: Surely his salvation is nigh them that fear him; that glory may dwell in our land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/85/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a4bee97-ff6a-4c6e-865b-5d5d52f3ed60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 85:10
Text: Mercy and truth are met together; righteousness and peace have kissed each other.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/85/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e110b7df-c71e-44f5-bcc6-288caeeb7908>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 85:11
Text: Truth shall spring out of the earth; and righteousness shall look down from heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/85/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29245e14-4552-476b-b676-99a9a67f436f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 85:12
Text: Yea, the LORD shall give that which is good; and our land shall yield her increase.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/85/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fede0708-d436-4a82-9f32-5eca4a194120>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 85:13
Text: Righteousness shall go before him; and shall set us in the way of his steps.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/86/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7af9bc6d-3dc2-459c-9a87-9b27dc66c139>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 86:1
Text: Bow down thine ear, O LORD, hear me: for I am poor and needy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/86/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2278c0b1-3164-49a4-bc4d-6e89536982b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 86:2
Text: Preserve my soul; for I am holy: O thou my God, save thy servant that trusteth in thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/86/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:550f8817-3477-44c4-90fa-525be87d6904>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: PSA 86:3
Text: Be merciful unto me, O Lord: for I cry unto thee daily.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/86/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39132dec-d733-4c4f-9044-85415b6ab67a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 86:4
Text: Rejoice the soul of thy servant: for unto thee, O Lord, do I lift up my soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/86/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81375599-d2d1-4d99-908d-6f0d8d28a2e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 86:5
Text: For thou, Lord, art good, and ready to forgive; and plenteous in mercy unto all them that call upon thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/86/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bdb40214-1a58-4d16-aa7e-c79c91d9c51c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 86:6
Text: Give ear, O LORD, unto my prayer; and attend to the voice of my supplications.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/86/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d37439b-5db5-4e49-b15b-51536e60f752>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 86:7
Text: In the day of my trouble I will call upon thee: for thou wilt answer me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/86/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88b33eaf-4bb1-44a6-87c1-c521668cc917>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 86:8
Text: Among the gods there is none like unto thee, O Lord; neither are there any works like unto thy works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/86/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82360fc0-a44e-4c9b-b141-041d9496324e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 86:9
Text: All nations whom thou hast made shall come and worship before thee, O Lord; and shall glorify thy name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/86/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05a39dfe-2495-4758-aa62-48e26c7135e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 86:10
Text: For thou art great, and doest wondrous things: thou art God alone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/86/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3202384f-c762-4397-b34b-17d1d56f50eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 86:11
Text: Teach me thy way, O LORD; I will walk in thy truth: unite my heart to fear thy name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/86/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:765c2c7c-72bf-4b4c-9e58-f24418b33979>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 86:12
Text: I will praise thee, O Lord my God, with all my heart: and I will glorify thy name for evermore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/86/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57803d5a-151b-4b49-b469-e32527c908d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 86:13
Text: For great is thy mercy toward me: and thou hast delivered my soul from the lowest hell.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/86/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:485920b8-0b6a-4983-8bcb-14a914239e28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: PSA 86:14
Text: O God, the proud are risen against me, and the assemblies of violent men have sought after my soul; and have not set thee before them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/86/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2d19436-f035-47de-9509-18a8f339e920>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PSA 86:15
Text: But thou, O Lord, art a God full of compassion, and gracious, longsuffering, and plenteous in mercy and truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/86/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ce70445-85c2-4bb8-9256-a5738c0deaf5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: PSA 86:16
Text: O turn unto me, and have mercy upon me; give thy strength unto thy servant, and save the son of thine handmaid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/86/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:342881b5-5676-4845-a867-ccb507bf8176>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: PSA 86:17
Text: Shew me a token for good; that they which hate me may see it, and be ashamed: because thou, LORD, hast holpen me, and comforted me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/87/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9ee4f8d-187c-4f17-85d3-500d237ae131>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 67

Reference: PSA 87:1
Text: His foundation is in the holy mountains.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/87/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1aac4d37-4829-4534-8dfa-e9be5ca214d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 87:2
Text: The LORD loveth the gates of Zion more than all the dwellings of Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/87/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4a2e64f-5d8b-4aa4-b53f-19160c967ac3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PSA 87:3
Text: Glorious things are spoken of thee, O city of God. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/87/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7328ed36-60aa-4dee-a467-c335dea45997>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: PSA 87:4
Text: I will make mention of Rahab and Babylon to them that know me: behold Philistia, and Tyre, with Ethiopia; this man was born there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/87/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6183048c-cbc4-4b28-974c-2f046034e958>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PSA 87:5
Text: And of Zion it shall be said, This and that man was born in her: and the highest himself shall establish her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/87/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04b64f39-e1f0-4e52-a7cf-530ceb4a27f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 87:6
Text: The LORD shall count, when he writeth up the people, that this man was born there. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/87/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2086982-ade0-479d-93d2-1e11d754f783>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 87:7
Text: As well the singers as the players on instruments shall be there: all my springs are in thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/88/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bb1e4f7-ef95-4456-ad8b-aa0465312f02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 88:1
Text: O lord God of my salvation, I have cried day and night before thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/88/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ae4df06-1618-46e2-bd5e-b325c9c0116a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 88:2
Text: Let my prayer come before thee: incline thine ear unto my cry;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/88/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:633d1463-6342-4839-8b99-921a06ec1403>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 88:3
Text: For my soul is full of troubles: and my life draweth nigh unto the grave.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/88/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc448d29-d9d0-4ad5-8365-0d28f5e821f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 88:4
Text: I am counted with them that go down into the pit: I am as a man that hath no strength:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/88/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9699889d-68f8-4999-90cf-7817b3133e8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: PSA 88:5
Text: Free among the dead, like the slain that lie in the grave, whom thou rememberest no more: and they are cut off from thy hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/88/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c807c5a4-d8db-4261-9db6-68e2154cc5d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 88:6
Text: Thou hast laid me in the lowest pit, in darkness, in the deeps.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/88/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d062305-e50d-4d8b-ba61-11976a7b54f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 88:7
Text: Thy wrath lieth hard upon me, and thou hast afflicted me with all thy waves. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/88/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f4cccb3-3b3d-42c5-9b99-6b13d35e0695>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: PSA 88:8
Text: Thou hast put away mine acquaintance far from me; thou hast made me an abomination unto them: I am shut up, and I cannot come forth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/88/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfee019b-f7e4-4617-8d70-0119822c237e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: PSA 88:9
Text: Mine eye mourneth by reason of affliction: LORD, I have called daily upon thee, I have stretched out my hands unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/88/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a980857-dee9-4372-85ec-37e9f4473112>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 88:10
Text: Wilt thou shew wonders to the dead? shall the dead arise and praise thee? Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/88/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e643974-ceb2-4fb9-bb0b-dcf810f64f1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 88:11
Text: Shall thy lovingkindness be declared in the grave? or thy faithfulness in destruction?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/88/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74056b04-c5cc-43e7-bd52-11c15e0b209d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 88:12
Text: Shall thy wonders be known in the dark? and thy righteousness in the land of forgetfulness?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/88/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:630d532a-5c5c-4ea8-81d9-07a9c322c0e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 88:13
Text: But unto thee have I cried, O LORD; and in the morning shall my prayer prevent thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/88/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aecb94ba-96ec-46f7-ba69-c2cef1198327>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 88:14
Text: LORD, why castest thou off my soul? why hidest thou thy face from me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/88/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed9fc833-97f6-47f7-9584-39be1b1793af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 88:15
Text: I am afflicted and ready to die from my youth up: while I suffer thy terrors I am distracted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/88/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b54bcac-abb7-47d0-a008-3d4ff179b7bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 88:16
Text: Thy fierce wrath goeth over me; thy terrors have cut me off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/88/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edc23ab2-afb6-45d9-8471-d5240eaec3d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 88:17
Text: They came round about me daily like water; they compassed me about together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/88/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e583ea0-e85f-4dc2-b928-9d203ce3c9fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 88:18
Text: Lover and friend hast thou put far from me, and mine acquaintance into darkness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5cbed8c-781f-44ec-b299-5e95f4780c96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: PSA 89:1
Text: I will sing of the mercies of the LORD for ever: with my mouth will I make known thy faithfulness to all generations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3d2db72-f787-4f81-8360-ef21f45593a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PSA 89:2
Text: For I have said, Mercy shall be built up for ever: thy faithfulness shalt thou establish in the very heavens.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78773597-0a94-4fdf-98b5-a21cd10084c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 89:3
Text: I have made a covenant with my chosen, I have sworn unto David my servant,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bbb82b79-2f0d-4f3a-8874-ba85bdb9b064>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 89:4
Text: Thy seed will I establish for ever, and build up thy throne to all generations. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:805e042c-5db1-41fd-9ad6-4f2e9419863a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: PSA 89:5
Text: And the heavens shall praise thy wonders, O LORD: thy faithfulness also in the congregation of the saints.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cb6ccdf-a5ac-4732-8494-00975c7688a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: PSA 89:6
Text: For who in the heaven can be compared unto the LORD? who among the sons of the mighty can be likened unto the LORD?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8618dfc1-d1d3-4757-b49e-be0e3e31300e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: PSA 89:7
Text: God is greatly to be feared in the assembly of the saints, and to be had in reverence of all them that are about him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:988727f8-fd00-4cc3-bec8-b560c4267516>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 89:8
Text: O LORD God of hosts, who is a strong LORD like unto thee? or to thy faithfulness round about thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52e5d9ea-520e-46e1-8396-059fffdb6623>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 89:9
Text: Thou rulest the raging of the sea: when the waves thereof arise, thou stillest them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea6bf432-5d6b-4462-8508-33a7b26d3cc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PSA 89:10
Text: Thou hast broken Rahab in pieces, as one that is slain; thou hast scattered thine enemies with thy strong arm.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a57c85a-067f-43b6-ba0c-d48ef7ab1b52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: PSA 89:11
Text: The heavens are thine, the earth also is thine: as for the world and the fulness thereof, thou hast founded them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a93a8c2-619b-4bed-beb0-917f8687d387>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 89:12
Text: The north and the south thou hast created them: Tabor and Hermon shall rejoice in thy name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86da3cc7-2729-4864-a0fb-ac0c212b8fd4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 89:13
Text: Thou hast a mighty arm: strong is thy hand, and high is thy right hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:658b6211-07ab-41f0-99d5-fcb383941e53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 89:14
Text: Justice and judgment are the habitation of thy throne: mercy and truth shall go before thy face.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69f06ed5-d1ed-4bec-b869-f3bdd4ff8425>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PSA 89:15
Text: Blessed is the people that know the joyful sound: they shall walk, O LORD, in the light of thy countenance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed5f9d76-8014-4bb7-a07e-3022ea29ccfc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 89:16
Text: In thy name shall they rejoice all the day: and in thy righteousness shall they be exalted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:741169be-5439-48e9-aacb-82d7f5471900>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 89:17
Text: For thou art the glory of their strength: and in thy favour our horn shall be exalted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46bb5db9-0e5c-4a91-b3f2-034c6c0a2073>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 89:18
Text: For the LORD is our defence; and the Holy One of Israel is our king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f26be4c-4f6c-4b37-bcf0-73c97f6ad937>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: PSA 89:19
Text: Then thou spakest in vision to thy holy one, and saidst, I have laid help upon one that is mighty; I have exalted one chosen out of the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:552e0b9e-94db-4b93-aa9b-31f0534c51a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 89:20
Text: I have found David my servant; with my holy oil have I anointed him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea732f6f-13b8-46ce-8f20-07ce17b77271>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 89:21
Text: With whom my hand shall be established: mine arm also shall strengthen him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e147129c-8a20-4d0e-9186-439565e51afc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 89:22
Text: The enemy shall not exact upon him; nor the son of wickedness afflict him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:636f6191-48c0-4f0c-b211-d699567b6f0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 89:23
Text: And I will beat down his foes before his face, and plague them that hate him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb10258a-b6cf-423e-8459-02013e2ea9c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 89:24
Text: But my faithfulness and my mercy shall be with him: and in my name shall his horn be exalted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9538abb-cd0b-4006-8548-f426ac84df71>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 89:25
Text: I will set his hand also in the sea, and his right hand in the rivers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8c13fff-22c8-4b72-891f-db8137815f01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 89:26
Text: He shall cry unto me, Thou art my father, my God, and the rock of my salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2973310b-a4fb-416c-975f-685a465b8d10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 89:27
Text: Also I will make him my firstborn, higher than the kings of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11fc32be-2fe4-4ae8-8529-7c287269cfa3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 89:28
Text: My mercy will I keep for him for evermore, and my covenant shall stand fast with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b42c82d-302d-4df7-8c0c-7eae1c12b212>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 89:29
Text: His seed also will I make to endure for ever, and his throne as the days of heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0df05ff5-f28c-4a63-b6ca-002adf4b14dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 89:30
Text: If his children forsake my law, and walk not in my judgments;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b98bd906-0ee0-43a7-b7e7-f0f40af9362d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PSA 89:31
Text: If they break my statutes, and keep not my commandments;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c3876a8-e8d0-4ebd-9c07-7804a39ba485>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 89:32
Text: Then will I visit their transgression with the rod, and their iniquity with stripes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5159155-a5ee-4340-bd37-160cf34c4164>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 89:33
Text: Nevertheless my lovingkindness will I not utterly take from him, nor suffer my faithfulness to fail.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:684ad5da-f6cc-4ac0-ac0e-5c5691492152>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 89:34
Text: My covenant will I not break, nor alter the thing that is gone out of my lips.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9766b8f-6608-4d13-a19b-61adc518fbd2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PSA 89:35
Text: Once have I sworn by my holiness that I will not lie unto David.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ce554bd-66a6-453f-9a7f-6da6ff7b7837>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 89:36
Text: His seed shall endure for ever, and his throne as the sun before me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:754a6d20-7ed7-4f87-ba16-e319ca9dea3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 89:37
Text: It shall be established for ever as the moon, and as a faithful witness in heaven. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8a28480-e904-4be5-8259-1bd020a28f2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 89:38
Text: But thou hast cast off and abhorred, thou hast been wroth with thine anointed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60507538-a1a0-4581-b8c4-80677c7154f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PSA 89:39
Text: Thou hast made void the covenant of thy servant: thou hast profaned his crown by casting it to the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e107ac97-869e-42b8-a1e3-7313e59833c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 89:40
Text: Thou hast broken down all his hedges; thou hast brought his strong holds to ruin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:654b9779-59e7-4853-afa9-75b633b4c1d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 89:41
Text: All that pass by the way spoil him: he is a reproach to his neighbours.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e14783b6-3868-498b-8559-1f6428e23cb2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 89:42
Text: Thou hast set up the right hand of his adversaries; thou hast made all his enemies to rejoice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f137f597-0acd-4aad-809a-95b3c9fd8971>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 89:43
Text: Thou hast also turned the edge of his sword, and hast not made him to stand in the battle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a831ce1-890d-46be-a26e-d798a51ab518>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 89:44
Text: Thou hast made his glory to cease, and cast his throne down to the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70e23d05-07d9-4409-a8a3-12be31ab932e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 89:45
Text: The days of his youth hast thou shortened: thou hast covered him with shame. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:241cba76-a440-4e33-b2a0-505972d69ac2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 89:46
Text: How long, LORD? wilt thou hide thyself for ever? shall thy wrath burn like fire?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b562113-041d-4df6-aa8b-7fe074f87ca3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 89:47
Text: Remember how short my time is: wherefore hast thou made all men in vain?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a81a715-d1aa-4ba8-be78-8cd7223d3ea4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: PSA 89:48
Text: What man is he that liveth, and shall not see death? shall he deliver his soul from the hand of the grave? Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3665e42-aaa2-4fca-8bee-9c5580b5aa34>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 89:49
Text: Lord, where are thy former lovingkindnesses, which thou swarest unto David in thy truth?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31ad4e46-3c0b-42dd-9696-dc3c66fc704c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PSA 89:50
Text: Remember, Lord, the reproach of thy servants; how I do bear in my bosom the reproach of all the mighty people;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7efffb5a-060d-4149-80df-558725f49faf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: PSA 89:51
Text: Wherewith thine enemies have reproached, O LORD; wherewith they have reproached the footsteps of thine anointed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/89/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:631415da-1a5c-4e84-8458-9f30c6856e51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: PSA 89:52
Text: Blessed be the LORD for evermore. Amen, and Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/90/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d59604c2-a23c-4ba1-8409-1ef64ce07ee9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PSA 90:1
Text: Lord, thou hast been our dwelling place in all generations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/90/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7d2b020-8c9d-49ff-85fe-b5fcf18f3cf0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: PSA 90:2
Text: Before the mountains were brought forth, or ever thou hadst formed the earth and the world, even from everlasting to everlasting, thou art God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/90/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:deaef89f-6c9c-4aa0-9d92-233224d91a52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 90:3
Text: Thou turnest man to destruction; and sayest, Return, ye children of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/90/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b0f2eb6-aba1-40e1-9f90-395f349dc16a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PSA 90:4
Text: For a thousand years in thy sight are but as yesterday when it is past, and as a watch in the night.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/90/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:334db8fc-1930-452f-9c58-2c2da100bc04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: PSA 90:5
Text: Thou carriest them away as with a flood; they are as a sleep: in the morning they are like grass which groweth up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/90/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:005a527e-b979-4a11-a374-3d099bf3551f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 90:6
Text: In the morning it flourisheth, and groweth up; in the evening it is cut down, and withereth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/90/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b2501a2-7491-41eb-8554-2c615c2baeaf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 90:7
Text: For we are consumed by thine anger, and by thy wrath are we troubled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/90/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc1b9324-e493-4e04-a691-c693ab32c5e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 90:8
Text: Thou hast set our iniquities before thee, our secret sins in the light of thy countenance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/90/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23ea8d28-552e-46c7-8bc5-b390b43563a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 90:9
Text: For all our days are passed away in thy wrath: we spend our years as a tale that is told.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/90/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aaf47fbf-0e43-4a3e-b756-c501814d3580>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: PSA 90:10
Text: The days of our years are threescore years and ten; and if by reason of strength they be fourscore years, yet is their strength labour and sorrow; for it is soon cut off, and we fly away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/90/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91ed3ca1-c7b7-4261-8daf-2ebb69d7d5fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 90:11
Text: Who knoweth the power of thine anger? even according to thy fear, so is thy wrath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/90/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:018e9d3e-43b2-41c0-a519-edab126107e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 90:12
Text: So teach us to number our days, that we may apply our hearts unto wisdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/90/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:351577d9-ca6f-4eea-b0aa-8b6fc4101efa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 90:13
Text: Return, O LORD, how long? and let it repent thee concerning thy servants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/90/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d00fdf7-0933-4414-ad7c-f55c6e54a557>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 90:14
Text: O satisfy us early with thy mercy; that we may rejoice and be glad all our days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/90/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86ba8051-31a5-4d7e-ba76-32063998c6a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PSA 90:15
Text: Make us glad according to the days wherein thou hast afflicted us, and the years wherein we have seen evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/90/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4d31203-e99b-4f97-9d70-4da433f779ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 90:16
Text: Let thy work appear unto thy servants, and thy glory unto their children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/90/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca1ca12c-5db9-4244-a39a-90f00bb72c02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: PSA 90:17
Text: And let the beauty of the LORD our God be upon us: and establish thou the work of our hands upon us; yea, the work of our hands establish thou it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/91/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae6c0500-7f9d-4d8c-aa2b-e7ba1c6f806d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 91:1
Text: He that dwelleth in the secret place of the most High shall abide under the shadow of the Almighty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/91/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b7ae480-378d-46b3-9987-fcb7b4071b3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 91:2
Text: I will say of the LORD, He is my refuge and my fortress: my God; in him will I trust.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/91/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65b1f5af-5d4a-4cbe-a1d4-77c5407ecabd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 91:3
Text: Surely he shall deliver thee from the snare of the fowler, and from the noisome pestilence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/91/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e730a4f-d62e-42cb-9e74-d8f2eaa5da32>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: PSA 91:4
Text: He shall cover thee with his feathers, and under his wings shalt thou trust: his truth shall be thy shield and buckler.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/91/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f49b4757-b872-4520-8bc9-83fdd6980480>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 91:5
Text: Thou shalt not be afraid for the terror by night; nor for the arrow that flieth by day;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/91/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4384d0b3-4850-4f8d-ab5c-a46f43d5d720>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 91:6
Text: Nor for the pestilence that walketh in darkness; nor for the destruction that wasteth at noonday.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/91/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45e7e803-8135-4f45-912d-45114cefd582>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 91:7
Text: A thousand shall fall at thy side, and ten thousand at thy right hand; but it shall not come nigh thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/91/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:730b91c2-872c-4980-92ed-4078da46cdea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 91:8
Text: Only with thine eyes shalt thou behold and see the reward of the wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/91/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ba80465-63dc-4f77-a966-89ae874ec3e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 91:9
Text: Because thou hast made the LORD, which is my refuge, even the most High, thy habitation;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/91/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e40a0d9-7145-4443-bcab-71b7421b4859>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 91:10
Text: There shall no evil befall thee, neither shall any plague come nigh thy dwelling.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/91/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bce732c1-75a6-4a5e-846e-b97dcb9b2c72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 91:11
Text: For he shall give his angels charge over thee, to keep thee in all thy ways.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/91/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6948729a-eaab-498e-9c06-cd02292e7f3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 91:12
Text: They shall bear thee up in their hands, lest thou dash thy foot against a stone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/91/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97eefefa-0531-4344-88b3-55b6933b4ca0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 91:13
Text: Thou shalt tread upon the lion and adder: the young lion and the dragon shalt thou trample under feet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/91/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14764e7e-3c2b-4a66-bf89-8ca82665d42c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: PSA 91:14
Text: Because he hath set his love upon me, therefore will I deliver him: I will set him on high, because he hath known my name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/91/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfd7a751-b100-41c8-8751-abc59595e46a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: PSA 91:15
Text: He shall call upon me, and I will answer him: I will be with him in trouble; I will deliver him, and honour him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/91/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bcbacf1-9852-4e1a-bc88-394c92eb3f4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 91:16
Text: With long life will I satisfy him, and shew him my salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/92/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da68e788-a6fd-41b3-a5f1-394ab102177c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 92:1
Text: It is a good thing to give thanks unto the Lord, and to sing praises unto thy name, O most High:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/92/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ae8d733-3e57-4c27-a603-8187e4f4dc85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 92:2
Text: To shew forth thy lovingkindness in the morning, and thy faithfulness every night,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/92/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6efa78fb-af00-4bfd-b937-af2b4c26fefd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 92:3
Text: Upon an instrument of ten strings, and upon the psaltery; upon the harp with a solemn sound.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/92/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff02fcb8-4407-4b80-92be-dc11156ed9fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 92:4
Text: For thou, LORD, hast made me glad through thy work: I will triumph in the works of thy hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/92/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:789a19f6-0406-470a-ad9c-aac56a88f66b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 92:5
Text: O LORD, how great are thy works! and thy thoughts are very deep.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/92/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3667bd5d-1e9b-4511-b8a5-211cbe8b51af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 92:6
Text: A brutish man knoweth not; neither doth a fool understand this.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/92/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c9d435b-429d-487a-a9b1-179165219f33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: PSA 92:7
Text: When the wicked spring as the grass, and when all the workers of iniquity do flourish; it is that they shall be destroyed for ever:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/92/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af33cada-9975-40b3-a184-42cf8805f02f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 70

Reference: PSA 92:8
Text: But thou, LORD, art most high for evermore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/92/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07e5ef7b-e458-4ca1-bea3-dc7a2f71f079>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: PSA 92:9
Text: For, lo, thine enemies, O LORD, for, lo, thine enemies shall perish; all the workers of iniquity shall be scattered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/92/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88feb077-8e6f-4d5a-bd57-1e4efa9a7a56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 92:10
Text: But my horn shalt thou exalt like the horn of an unicorn: I shall be anointed with fresh oil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/92/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0afe3bb-28f6-473a-a91c-37869778eb3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: PSA 92:11
Text: Mine eye also shall see my desire on mine enemies, and mine ears shall hear my desire of the wicked that rise up against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/92/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2ee1ccb-8004-46ce-a984-77eb32465a19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 92:12
Text: The righteous shall flourish like the palm tree: he shall grow like a cedar in Lebanon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/92/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:979a70a8-7bf3-4c58-8398-82ba547a4975>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 92:13
Text: Those that be planted in the house of the LORD shall flourish in the courts of our God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/92/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e211332-548f-41b5-afe4-139c88df3d1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 92:14
Text: They shall still bring forth fruit in old age; they shall be fat and flourishing;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/92/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:124e067f-2cdf-4f8b-9210-655826da62f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 92:15
Text: To shew that the LORD is upright: he is my rock, and there is no unrighteousness in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/93/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95677881-c8d8-4560-ae17-ae230750a6e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: PSA 93:1
Text: The LORD reigneth, he is clothed with majesty; the LORD is clothed with strength, wherewith he hath girded himself: the world also is stablished, that it cannot be moved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/93/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22de24e3-983d-4119-9884-68c12dfb50b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PSA 93:2
Text: Thy throne is established of old: thou art from everlasting.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/93/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e06b69c-47ac-46ec-846e-50ec3379214f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 93:3
Text: The floods have lifted up, O LORD, the floods have lifted up their voice; the floods lift up their waves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/93/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80802c5e-af4e-46da-a6b5-c9a5f36ead4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 93:4
Text: The LORD on high is mightier than the noise of many waters, yea, than the mighty waves of the sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/93/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ceb15d2d-8fb4-4430-a8a9-a576af100515>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 93:5
Text: Thy testimonies are very sure: holiness becometh thine house, O LORD, for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/94/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e31f036b-5c35-4464-9767-49f6823c9e42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 94:1
Text: O Lord God, to whom vengeance belongeth; O God, to whom vengeance belongeth, shew thyself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/94/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a190bb2-2097-418a-9320-e7127509af15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 94:2
Text: Lift up thyself, thou judge of the earth: render a reward to the proud.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/94/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f0a8e0d-f07d-4351-bfbd-f1e64d73ab93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 94:3
Text: LORD, how long shall the wicked, how long shall the wicked triumph?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/94/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:035737bf-05f6-44c8-9fc1-4a3b31806ad7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 94:4
Text: How long shall they utter and speak hard things? and all the workers of iniquity boast themselves?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/94/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:004c533a-4b74-4347-bb2a-baab7e8a883f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 94:5
Text: They break in pieces thy people, O LORD, and afflict thine heritage.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/94/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23184658-4619-4094-b6e5-7b5f0f7de4ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 94:6
Text: They slay the widow and the stranger, and murder the fatherless.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/94/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d770cd11-5bde-4f05-9761-a4631e52d1ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 94:7
Text: Yet they say, The LORD shall not see, neither shall the God of Jacob regard it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/94/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29d4bf5d-e3ee-4f8b-a0ae-54acdcc9fdb8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 94:8
Text: Understand, ye brutish among the people: and ye fools, when will ye be wise?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/94/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:929c5495-86ec-4b6c-aa9d-280afe3e1248>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 94:9
Text: He that planted the ear, shall he not hear? he that formed the eye, shall he not see?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/94/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:438ca989-c19f-4204-9c83-6f0455bed65a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 94:10
Text: He that chastiseth the heathen, shall not he correct? he that teacheth man knowledge, shall not he know?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/94/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d649b99b-b1ab-4959-986f-19d0d7b603a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PSA 94:11
Text: The LORD knoweth the thoughts of man, that they are vanity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/94/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef2f42cc-2ed6-4e90-8d9a-6aed34cc3545>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 94:12
Text: Blessed is the man whom thou chastenest, O LORD, and teachest him out of thy law;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/94/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44f9e4ee-2060-431e-9585-5b96b3b3f551>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 94:13
Text: That thou mayest give him rest from the days of adversity, until the pit be digged for the wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/94/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0fd04e33-bcd2-455c-9e63-f9f98b91326d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 94:14
Text: For the LORD will not cast off his people, neither will he forsake his inheritance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/94/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:efaf7d27-9b01-43fe-864c-8885a5d13477>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 94:15
Text: But judgment shall return unto righteousness: and all the upright in heart shall follow it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/94/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6dbb8681-8eef-4886-8017-b0ce09fdc9ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PSA 94:16
Text: Who will rise up for me against the evildoers? or who will stand up for me against the workers of iniquity?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/94/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49708774-b492-4722-8c14-381fe17b5a78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 94:17
Text: Unless the LORD had been my help, my soul had almost dwelt in silence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/94/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2320c22-44e2-4a9c-8c12-3d1f584de28a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 94:18
Text: When I said, My foot slippeth; thy mercy, O LORD, held me up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/94/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:493e4fcc-0ca3-4383-948c-bae8d2ebc7a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 94:19
Text: In the multitude of my thoughts within me thy comforts delight my soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/94/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f802a9e-1a9f-444c-8d41-a5cab6056794>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 94:20
Text: Shall the throne of iniquity have fellowship with thee, which frameth mischief by a law?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/94/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fcfce933-b88b-4511-9788-51ff3766bacc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 94:21
Text: They gather themselves together against the soul of the righteous, and condemn the innocent blood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/94/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ccef5e84-2929-4099-b57a-c9cfa9767647>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PSA 94:22
Text: But the LORD is my defence; and my God is the rock of my refuge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/94/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ad5c005-5f24-4766-94b5-d28944704c81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: PSA 94:23
Text: And he shall bring upon them their own iniquity, and shall cut them off in their own wickedness; yea, the LORD our God shall cut them off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/95/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bab5951e-f643-4bcc-89ae-e67c3faf1c5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 95:1
Text: O come, let us sing unto the LORD: let us make a joyful noise to the rock of our salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/95/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b662bc59-25f4-44b4-a16c-ad34c8232b2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 95:2
Text: Let us come before his presence with thanksgiving, and make a joyful noise unto him with psalms.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/95/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc75d9c6-85c8-4963-ba30-25aa5279bb2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 95:3
Text: For the LORD is a great God, and a great King above all gods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/95/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:230ba1e0-bc3c-47e2-b2a1-d9f7b8c9a43e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 95:4
Text: In his hand are the deep places of the earth: the strength of the hills is his also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/95/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fe3b9a3-cbad-42c6-a500-836fc0edd707>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 95:5
Text: The sea is his, and he made it: and his hands formed the dry land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/95/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:209f8ec8-fe2d-4f58-a88e-9fc4933d2019>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 95:6
Text: O come, let us worship and bow down: let us kneel before the LORD our maker.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/95/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a31e749a-cab2-4cd4-8fc5-75a6af549586>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: PSA 95:7
Text: For he is our God; and we are the people of his pasture, and the sheep of his hand. To day if ye will hear his voice,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/95/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32d91376-e4f4-420b-9e34-55fb562f5edd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 95:8
Text: Harden not your heart, as in the provocation, and as in the day of temptation in the wilderness:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/95/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c536805b-9d55-4a57-9196-203ca689c16e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PSA 95:9
Text: When your fathers tempted me, proved me, and saw my work.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/95/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08d4e194-28e8-40fd-a5cd-954e89ca00e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: PSA 95:10
Text: Forty years long was I grieved with this generation, and said, It is a people that do err in their heart, and they have not known my ways:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/95/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:578270d8-c36b-40e3-be7e-d2f4ccd1eede>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 95:11
Text: Unto whom I sware in my wrath that they should not enter into my rest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/96/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7bbcf884-c05d-4031-ba7c-bc6bb2dfc771>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 96:1
Text: O sing unto the LORD a new song: sing unto the LORD, all the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/96/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bcf60206-9316-4418-8b12-1452a0586650>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 96:2
Text: Sing unto the LORD, bless his name; shew forth his salvation from day to day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/96/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24c32107-8597-420e-bc67-b76d5ab498fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 96:3
Text: Declare his glory among the heathen, his wonders among all people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/96/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a1d6a2e-261d-4a78-9386-2582f1ce154d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 96:4
Text: For the LORD is great, and greatly to be praised: he is to be feared above all gods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/96/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a494c3a-a43a-43f4-b0db-e77ed34cbeda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 96:5
Text: For all the gods of the nations are idols: but the LORD made the heavens.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/96/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4e3f492-72d9-4116-a9de-8ee2df766668>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 96:6
Text: Honour and majesty are before him: strength and beauty are in his sanctuary.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/96/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a32de253-7f32-4b4f-b0ee-5d98b94e9700>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 96:7
Text: Give unto the LORD, O ye kindreds of the people, give unto the LORD glory and strength.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/96/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25d05d2b-ca14-4071-87a2-5c16109f4e7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 96:8
Text: Give unto the LORD the glory due unto his name: bring an offering, and come into his courts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/96/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8ce8788-89e9-432e-b1c1-c519601e2806>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 96:9
Text: O worship the LORD in the beauty of holiness: fear before him, all the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/96/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:efe30a72-6307-44ea-85b1-448f4f911625>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: PSA 96:10
Text: Say among the heathen that the LORD reigneth: the world also shall be established that it shall not be moved: he shall judge the people righteously.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/96/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f38ca490-9af1-4a32-a85f-c560cf0062e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 96:11
Text: Let the heavens rejoice, and let the earth be glad; let the sea roar, and the fulness thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/96/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7bcb7d4-1b2c-4b83-a522-afb7308bf62a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 96:12
Text: Let the field be joyful, and all that is therein: then shall all the trees of the wood rejoice


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/96/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53349558-bff1-46bb-b4e8-29b689d3a5d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: PSA 96:13
Text: Before the LORD: for he cometh, for he cometh to judge the earth: he shall judge the world with righteousness, and the people with his truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/97/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a0f2bbe-f5b7-4a9d-a4c4-f297b6146017>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 97:1
Text: The LORD reigneth; let the earth rejoice; let the multitude of isles be glad thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/97/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bbfda24-0394-4c2f-860b-022db6f25643>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 97:2
Text: Clouds and darkness are round about him: righteousness and judgment are the habitation of his throne.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/97/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3404340-7dbb-4e09-bb2c-ecae45e802d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 97:3
Text: A fire goeth before him, and burneth up his enemies round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/97/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f5289d7-8e4d-4e3e-9747-a6d610f577ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 97:4
Text: His lightnings enlightened the world: the earth saw, and trembled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/97/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1788d3ad-1b47-4c1c-90f4-64a488be6ea6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PSA 97:5
Text: The hills melted like wax at the presence of the LORD, at the presence of the Lord of the whole earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/97/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c058ada-e0fa-4158-af93-4ebeddfaa628>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 97:6
Text: The heavens declare his righteousness, and all the people see his glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/97/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9cdb791d-8109-4388-ba78-bac427f4ce4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: PSA 97:7
Text: Confounded be all they that serve graven images, that boast themselves of idols: worship him, all ye gods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/97/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:606d3ac7-9247-47cf-afbd-4afeafc98092>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 97:8
Text: Zion heard, and was glad; and the daughters of Judah rejoiced because of thy judgments, O LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/97/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b34e351-6ae2-4982-82a7-35b4a86982a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 97:9
Text: For thou, LORD, art high above all the earth: thou art exalted far above all gods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/97/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55273b3d-de9a-4f64-b3df-7e9fceb016ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: PSA 97:10
Text: Ye that love the LORD, hate evil: he preserveth the souls of his saints; he delivereth them out of the hand of the wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/97/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c0df3a8-32fc-4145-9bf2-798854cfed4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 97:11
Text: Light is sown for the righteous, and gladness for the upright in heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/97/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51792913-816b-4080-b3fd-c9049d5f9f55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 97:12
Text: Rejoice in the LORD, ye righteous; and give thanks at the remembrance of his holiness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/98/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5b005d4-c9de-4c60-a2b1-4d37703c531d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: PSA 98:1
Text: O sing unto the LORD a new song; for he hath done marvellous things: his right hand, and his holy arm, hath gotten him the victory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/98/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3908dca-ea27-46c5-b7df-080f00bbaebe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PSA 98:2
Text: The LORD hath made known his salvation: his righteousness hath he openly shewed in the sight of the heathen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/98/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d43defa-e905-4361-9145-07c4c2b00d46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: PSA 98:3
Text: He hath remembered his mercy and his truth toward the house of Israel: all the ends of the earth have seen the salvation of our God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/98/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae5fef96-ee4d-40ef-897a-dd3ecf3239f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 98:4
Text: Make a joyful noise unto the LORD, all the earth: make a loud noise, and rejoice, and sing praise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/98/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af5766a3-5bd7-4694-a97a-82e9a9623153>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 98:5
Text: Sing unto the LORD with the harp; with the harp, and the voice of a psalm.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/98/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ff81cec-afd7-452e-ac01-df96548c349e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 98:6
Text: With trumpets and sound of cornet make a joyful noise before the LORD, the King.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/98/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e72a7a5-d3bd-45d6-b5df-675dc6a18a0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 98:7
Text: Let the sea roar, and the fulness thereof; the world, and they that dwell therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/98/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4955e112-9f07-4149-a6b0-fce931d12473>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PSA 98:8
Text: Let the floods clap their hands: let the hills be joyful together


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/98/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:262de7cd-cb89-40a2-afb3-3d8f21ad53ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: PSA 98:9
Text: Before the LORD; for he cometh to judge the earth: with righteousness shall he judge the world, and the people with equity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/99/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c6bf793-5024-49c6-bfc6-85688f378a51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PSA 99:1
Text: The LORD reigneth; let the people tremble: he sitteth between the cherubims; let the earth be moved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/99/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21bf8428-9c8d-4c12-8e52-8bdcb6f3f224>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 99:2
Text: The LORD is great in Zion; and he is high above all the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/99/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aea52efd-4a37-4a34-a916-e739a5c21bac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PSA 99:3
Text: Let them praise thy great and terrible name; for it is holy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/99/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e44fcf7c-6f19-4009-ad28-8acdc23d3943>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: PSA 99:4
Text: The king’s strength also loveth judgment; thou dost establish equity, thou executest judgment and righteousness in Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/99/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93eae3c5-8c25-4aed-b0a6-794579199274>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 99:5
Text: Exalt ye the LORD our God, and worship at his footstool; for he is holy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/99/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3e1e0b5-f12a-458c-a574-8f807284c747>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: PSA 99:6
Text: Moses and Aaron among his priests, and Samuel among them that call upon his name; they called upon the LORD, and he answered them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/99/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd5b0131-d94c-4313-9a1c-c569e94a1288>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 99:7
Text: He spake unto them in the cloudy pillar: they kept his testimonies, and the ordinance that he gave them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/99/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ba0787c-45b7-4557-abc2-704a67d3ab8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: PSA 99:8
Text: Thou answeredst them, O LORD our God: thou wast a God that forgavest them, though thou tookest vengeance of their inventions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/99/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e112dbaa-28c7-4795-85b3-8f0b30b418d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 99:9
Text: Exalt the LORD our God, and worship at his holy hill; for the LORD our God is holy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/100/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60fb352d-b3e0-4253-8a72-6469cf088f89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: PSA 100:1
Text: Make a joyful noise unto the LORD, all ye lands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/100/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fdddb346-957f-4ecc-9da8-3af2337b2e43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 100:2
Text: Serve the LORD with gladness: come before his presence with singing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/100/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d29a036-3eb1-47aa-85fc-c7c11ad2be63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: PSA 100:3
Text: Know ye that the LORD he is God: it is he that hath made us, and not we ourselves; we are his people, and the sheep of his pasture.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/100/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea0df926-eac5-4809-acb4-6dedd0f58b3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: PSA 100:4
Text: Enter into his gates with thanksgiving, and into his courts with praise: be thankful unto him, and bless his name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/100/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16fccc20-b2d5-4fa8-a7c6-c15080d1a0f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 100:5
Text: For the LORD is good; his mercy is everlasting; and his truth endureth to all generations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/101/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6495c8d5-92d4-478a-8b20-bae2a0ac6753>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 101:1
Text: I will sing of mercy and judgment: unto thee, O LORD, will I sing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/101/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:368eae77-c728-4714-abdf-1ae156009cfd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: PSA 101:2
Text: I will behave myself wisely in a perfect way. O when wilt thou come unto me? I will walk within my house with a perfect heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/101/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9f3fc22-9d4d-4f67-8dba-a02cd34f58e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: PSA 101:3
Text: I will set no wicked thing before mine eyes: I hate the work of them that turn aside; it shall not cleave to me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/101/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d038293-8e7b-4d3d-9947-a1a16b814201>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 101:4
Text: A froward heart shall depart from me: I will not know a wicked person.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/101/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1a1e867-c62d-4cfc-923b-b116098253f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: PSA 101:5
Text: Whoso privily slandereth his neighbour, him will I cut off: him that hath an high look and a proud heart will not I suffer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/101/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed72cca9-e63e-4375-800c-4f1ecd753087>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: PSA 101:6
Text: Mine eyes shall be upon the faithful of the land, that they may dwell with me: he that walketh in a perfect way, he shall serve me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/101/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b326e9b-9150-4b98-9d12-384582ea25ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: PSA 101:7
Text: He that worketh deceit shall not dwell within my house: he that telleth lies shall not tarry in my sight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/101/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70b743fa-8eb0-4fab-a946-bf3b05065d54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: PSA 101:8
Text: I will early destroy all the wicked of the land; that I may cut off all wicked doers from the city of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88c741f2-9807-4f56-9d42-7b92dec9e2ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: PSA 102:1
Text: Hear my prayer, O LORD, and let my cry come unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5efa9207-c4f7-41c8-a2be-1e56d9248d3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: PSA 102:2
Text: Hide not thy face from me in the day when I am in trouble; incline thine ear unto me: in the day when I call answer me speedily.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b18e1eb-3c04-4266-a692-c5932c5880ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 102:3
Text: For my days are consumed like smoke, and my bones are burned as an hearth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a5159a2-4e9e-41c7-afac-ef6c9a673852>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 102:4
Text: My heart is smitten, and withered like grass; so that I forget to eat my bread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:758f92b6-d758-4ad8-bd77-fa8886ead0e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 102:5
Text: By reason of the voice of my groaning my bones cleave to my skin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b8b7ab4-7971-43b7-b867-b20349ca7317>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 102:6
Text: I am like a pelican of the wilderness: I am like an owl of the desert.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72ba7b05-05f3-43c9-80bf-3bcb63c5390f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: PSA 102:7
Text: I watch, and am as a sparrow alone upon the house top.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac54ae94-4681-4569-8c55-c601f3d21212>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 102:8
Text: Mine enemies reproach me all the day; and they that are mad against me are sworn against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57b6b5fa-d1ed-4978-ac98-d30e66274aa2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 102:9
Text: For I have eaten ashes like bread, and mingled my drink with weeping.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6da2017c-bed4-4c90-927c-a38e2a528b54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 102:10
Text: Because of thine indignation and thy wrath: for thou hast lifted me up, and cast me down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97bae341-627c-4cb8-bd44-a59077b1a97a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 102:11
Text: My days are like a shadow that declineth; and I am withered like grass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c12ebf06-3f98-4801-becf-da15eab34d3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 102:12
Text: But thou, O LORD, shall endure for ever; and thy remembrance unto all generations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe395830-f0e6-48af-bfdc-671b8ab3f738>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 102:13
Text: Thou shalt arise, and have mercy upon Zion: for the time to favour her, yea, the set time, is come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e0bc861-6346-42b8-b126-11922e6f57bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 102:14
Text: For thy servants take pleasure in her stones, and favour the dust thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a815ec64-9cd0-4bcb-99e1-b1a6533d0b13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 102:15
Text: So the heathen shall fear the name of the LORD, and all the kings of the earth thy glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54d700ab-7090-4faa-a4e8-d1efc910829e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 102:16
Text: When the LORD shall build up Zion, he shall appear in his glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83a23139-d621-4d8f-ae03-4f6824f2d266>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 102:17
Text: He will regard the prayer of the destitute, and not despise their prayer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c35b19b7-3a8a-4735-b229-bb9d3fbcacea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: PSA 102:18
Text: This shall be written for the generation to come: and the people which shall be created shall praise the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3df1bb87-3a9d-412c-a5b8-c2dfdf4e1182>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PSA 102:19
Text: For he hath looked down from the height of his sanctuary; from heaven did the LORD behold the earth;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ec6b9be-4ad0-4ace-90a1-ad69f37ddb59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 102:20
Text: To hear the groaning of the prisoner; to loose those that are appointed to death;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f40b2ee9-d012-46a3-ac6e-e87dded03ee3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 102:21
Text: To declare the name of the LORD in Zion, and his praise in Jerusalem;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6efefd33-c9f7-4ef5-ade1-292fe367e15a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 102:22
Text: When the people are gathered together, and the kingdoms, to serve the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c74f6de3-d0e8-4a53-9afd-ae4cb0db1e97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PSA 102:23
Text: He weakened my strength in the way; he shortened my days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd128af2-2001-4029-bb44-29e16289dc01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 102:24
Text: I said, O my God, take me not away in the midst of my days: thy years are throughout all generations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac8b9a1c-0b8d-4622-b446-008a2aaa1dd2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 102:25
Text: Of old hast thou laid the foundation of the earth: and the heavens are the work of thy hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70b0fda1-cdb5-4dee-a7f7-1ba80aeef35f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: PSA 102:26
Text: They shall perish, but thou shalt endure: yea, all of them shall wax old like a garment; as a vesture shalt thou change them, and they shall be changed:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5946261-8da7-435b-98d3-c546911666e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PSA 102:27
Text: But thou art the same, and thy years shall have no end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/102/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20692241-a859-44da-a1a0-90a6f2c72978>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 102:28
Text: The children of thy servants shall continue, and their seed shall be established before thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/103/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20c767d1-9339-499d-8545-32800ae9d276>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 103:1
Text: Bless the LORD, O my soul: and all that is within me, bless his holy name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/103/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e98dd0a-9001-43dc-8f39-66c43b2f8886>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PSA 103:2
Text: Bless the LORD, O my soul, and forget not all his benefits:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/103/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38ea56cd-8cb2-45b7-b8dd-acb78f64757e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 103:3
Text: Who forgiveth all thine iniquities; who healeth all thy diseases;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/103/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e34866e4-7fe1-42cf-8cfc-ad3f5b9bd019>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 103:4
Text: Who redeemeth thy life from destruction; who crowneth thee with lovingkindness and tender mercies;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/103/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed9ebcf8-5b62-458c-ac21-4624b8876c7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 103:5
Text: Who satisfieth thy mouth with good things; so that thy youth is renewed like the eagle’s.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/103/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f8582d0-9be7-4f62-81c4-8a99f6cb760c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 103:6
Text: The LORD executeth righteousness and judgment for all that are oppressed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/103/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edab1ee5-25e0-4c43-81b0-e60088fc983b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 103:7
Text: He made known his ways unto Moses, his acts unto the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/103/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f1eb628-8190-4ad9-b147-012d587ce475>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 103:8
Text: The LORD is merciful and gracious, slow to anger, and plenteous in mercy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/103/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b86e833d-3a88-4ae0-955f-0e08eec53de4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 103:9
Text: He will not always chide: neither will he keep his anger for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/103/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01cfefbd-5aa9-41b5-995d-91b6b36aca0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 103:10
Text: He hath not dealt with us after our sins; nor rewarded us according to our iniquities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/103/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80dcc5b7-8255-4c56-a98f-3c4071174b57>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 103:11
Text: For as the heaven is high above the earth, so great is his mercy toward them that fear him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/103/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11fae66b-48d4-4a1f-b5fc-9f68dad08065>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 103:12
Text: As far as the east is from the west, so far hath he removed our transgressions from us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/103/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:638deb6f-3f31-4206-9f1c-08ea9a352dff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 103:13
Text: Like as a father pitieth his children, so the LORD pitieth them that fear him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/103/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4754328-69ac-4b2c-941d-dd6494f44c2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PSA 103:14
Text: For he knoweth our frame; he remembereth that we are dust.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/103/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03bb48ae-3dd3-4499-9daf-75edd42bc68e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 103:15
Text: As for man, his days are as grass: as a flower of the field, so he flourisheth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/103/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55183e4c-8004-43bd-87b7-c8513a843a8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 103:16
Text: For the wind passeth over it, and it is gone; and the place thereof shall know it no more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/103/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51b02f1c-56ea-4c78-848f-ea97bd2a2403>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: PSA 103:17
Text: But the mercy of the LORD is from everlasting to everlasting upon them that fear him, and his righteousness unto children’s children;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/103/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18092833-eb6f-44f6-afb8-9663f6a5e42e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 103:18
Text: To such as keep his covenant, and to those that remember his commandments to do them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/103/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce20afcd-7078-4008-9856-d3c5a2cc5373>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 103:19
Text: The LORD hath prepared his throne in the heavens; and his kingdom ruleth over all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/103/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc1a8079-9180-40a3-9100-db53a64d68e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: PSA 103:20
Text: Bless the LORD, ye his angels, that excel in strength, that do his commandments, hearkening unto the voice of his word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/103/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5366d269-c5bf-4cb3-876e-8f3d17b18275>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 103:21
Text: Bless ye the LORD, all ye his hosts; ye ministers of his, that do his pleasure.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/103/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec4b18c9-1712-4b2c-951f-e31245a4142c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 103:22
Text: Bless the LORD, all his works in all places of his dominion: bless the LORD, O my soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5561fec-e49b-4202-8a82-dc81c1066ba0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 104:1
Text: Bless the LORD, O my soul. O LORD my God, thou art very great; thou art clothed with honour and majesty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:410b5ae7-da62-4cc0-864d-d06ea4130af6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 104:2
Text: Who coverest thyself with light as with a garment: who stretchest out the heavens like a curtain:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f939fd6-e9e8-43b2-a0fa-51e69c2e2567>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: PSA 104:3
Text: Who layeth the beams of his chambers in the waters: who maketh the clouds his chariot: who walketh upon the wings of the wind:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cc9d618-0a4e-4e0e-9328-2e7b370cb117>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 104:4
Text: Who maketh his angels spirits; his ministers a flaming fire:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93ddc84a-54a0-4a94-b9dd-e64e678cf5da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 104:5
Text: Who laid the foundations of the earth, that it should not be removed for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b307668-2cf5-487f-a245-4154dbe289f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 104:6
Text: Thou coveredst it with the deep as with a garment: the waters stood above the mountains.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb7ad284-216c-451f-a017-ce58aaf4aa28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 104:7
Text: At thy rebuke they fled; at the voice of thy thunder they hasted away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8711f3f-5f40-49cd-b29f-a83f12385227>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: PSA 104:8
Text: They go up by the mountains; they go down by the valleys unto the place which thou hast founded for them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afbb6332-9f06-4e1f-ab0a-7e5f54ec3000>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 104:9
Text: Thou hast set a bound that they may not pass over; that they turn not again to cover the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bf259ea-b8bd-47be-914a-1a74517d1950>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 104:10
Text: He sendeth the springs into the valleys, which run among the hills.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb0d1866-43e0-4c2c-9457-bd416981727d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 104:11
Text: They give drink to every beast of the field: the wild asses quench their thirst.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ee1fb02-31fb-4ee7-907c-dbeac95a9cc7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 104:12
Text: By them shall the fowls of the heaven have their habitation, which sing among the branches.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8621786c-eadd-4b88-9d50-4a16cbbb933f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 104:13
Text: He watereth the hills from his chambers: the earth is satisfied with the fruit of thy works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88996009-1996-498d-9c5e-91372cd5fb0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: PSA 104:14
Text: He causeth the grass to grow for the cattle, and herb for the service of man: that he may bring forth food out of the earth;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f19b696c-053b-4695-953f-60112e83e48b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: PSA 104:15
Text: And wine that maketh glad the heart of man, and oil to make his face to shine, and bread which strengtheneth man’s heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f5e964d-3fd1-4b36-b5fc-ead6e1e8d74f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 104:16
Text: The trees of the LORD are full of sap; the cedars of Lebanon, which he hath planted;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44482a30-0faa-462c-814f-395f6b8ab60e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 104:17
Text: Where the birds make their nests: as for the stork, the fir trees are her house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4f52612-b346-43fc-83de-c2d5cd0a550b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 104:18
Text: The high hills are a refuge for the wild goats; and the rocks for the conies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5aa11a4-d4fa-4835-88c3-26642e44fca4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 104:19
Text: He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:830c8a41-06c5-409d-a077-7ccd34da9968>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 104:20
Text: Thou makest darkness, and it is night: wherein all the beasts of the forest do creep forth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ec9ea30-65dc-4042-819a-87cee5774bb6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 104:21
Text: The young lions roar after their prey, and seek their meat from God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b81015ca-d320-4b8d-ad4a-54eff7f2fdd9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 104:22
Text: The sun ariseth, they gather themselves together, and lay them down in their dens.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4fc80fe-1b80-4962-a512-c54545e1ef05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 104:23
Text: Man goeth forth unto his work and to his labour until the evening.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea25eea4-e402-478c-bc62-4c84c399de01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 104:24
Text: O LORD, how manifold are thy works! in wisdom hast thou made them all: the earth is full of thy riches.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13265441-4e09-4ac5-b3ec-2bc8933a3415>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PSA 104:25
Text: So is this great and wide sea, wherein are things creeping innumerable, both small and great beasts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6158da0-b072-40a3-8a36-2ee6243686cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 104:26
Text: There go the ships: there is that leviathan, whom thou hast made to play therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9fe9539-44e2-41c8-83ff-1936daf9e3c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 104:27
Text: These wait all upon thee; that thou mayest give them their meat in due season.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2070037-ab01-4afa-b7d6-63f8a6ff4e59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 104:28
Text: That thou givest them they gather: thou openest thine hand, they are filled with good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1529948-b4bf-4d34-9549-fbda02506570>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PSA 104:29
Text: Thou hidest thy face, they are troubled: thou takest away their breath, they die, and return to their dust.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62a847f7-3b52-4bb7-b1a7-4b27f1710094>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 104:30
Text: Thou sendest forth thy spirit, they are created: and thou renewest the face of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13417b0b-6b2b-42ee-aff0-8296c398a288>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 104:31
Text: The glory of the LORD shall endure for ever: the LORD shall rejoice in his works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f3bf08a-1dd9-47f5-b740-7016bf0afca1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 104:32
Text: He looketh on the earth, and it trembleth: he toucheth the hills, and they smoke.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:247db36e-36dd-4e4a-885f-8d3fdbc6aa98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 104:33
Text: I will sing unto the LORD as long as I live: I will sing praise to my God while I have my being.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6927a4b-7cfc-4f32-a93c-d852dbb3b53c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 104:34
Text: My meditation of him shall be sweet: I will be glad in the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/104/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9bb288e-c59d-4298-bf69-30c0b76f2dfb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: PSA 104:35
Text: Let the sinners be consumed out of the earth, and let the wicked be no more. Bless thou the LORD, O my soul. Praise ye the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6414e4e1-af6c-4d89-8b6c-17bb69d58301>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 105:1
Text: O give thanks unto the LORD; call upon his name: make known his deeds among the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22371096-944b-4b85-ae9d-16973ed532ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 105:2
Text: Sing unto him, sing psalms unto him: talk ye of all his wondrous works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d2ecf88-48a2-463c-bc8a-78b855cbb46b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 105:3
Text: Glory ye in his holy name: let the heart of them rejoice that seek the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:169ee437-906e-4178-9a9e-8559af36e87d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PSA 105:4
Text: Seek the LORD, and his strength: seek his face evermore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:618cbca8-b428-4e21-800f-b5ee0be6b92a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 105:5
Text: Remember his marvellous works that he hath done; his wonders, and the judgments of his mouth;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8123ce43-ae09-4985-9659-46bea836370d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 105:6
Text: O ye seed of Abraham his servant, ye children of Jacob his chosen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ade680ad-0c83-47d7-8cbc-675536bcf48a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PSA 105:7
Text: He is the LORD our God: his judgments are in all the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a64d33fa-ce47-405a-9e06-409e5b9b47d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 105:8
Text: He hath remembered his covenant for ever, the word which he commanded to a thousand generations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19aebe82-1ac9-4fb9-a601-705386ffe383>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 105:9
Text: Which covenant he made with Abraham, and his oath unto Isaac;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cabcb351-aa32-4b12-8033-69a95829d03b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 105:10
Text: And confirmed the same unto Jacob for a law, and to Israel for an everlasting covenant:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a09cbe7-ca75-4498-ac8b-fd08b12c66b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 105:11
Text: Saying, Unto thee will I give the land of Canaan, the lot of your inheritance:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6d30d5b-b8ef-4fa4-96de-fd634f707d91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 105:12
Text: When they were but a few men in number; yea, very few, and strangers in it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45a0d982-ee75-427e-80b0-b92e5f18ba72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 105:13
Text: When they went from one nation to another, from one kingdom to another people;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0305a15b-76c7-4b2b-92af-2f949e925055>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 105:14
Text: He suffered no man to do them wrong: yea, he reproved kings for their sakes;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:969bef16-f5a6-4698-b0a3-91096b31014b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 105:15
Text: Saying, Touch not mine anointed, and do my prophets no harm.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac2f18ab-e35c-4e30-a9fc-1ec92577e824>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 105:16
Text: Moreover he called for a famine upon the land: he brake the whole staff of bread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:908453b0-37e5-4ee0-ada5-06bfd6e3befb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 105:17
Text: He sent a man before them, even Joseph, who was sold for a servant:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f91e9274-bab6-4d4d-a88b-7457b38d6a66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PSA 105:18
Text: Whose feet they hurt with fetters: he was laid in iron:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bff1dc0-436b-4e9e-b3a2-41527214495a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 105:19
Text: Until the time that his word came: the word of the LORD tried him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7a84e75-d126-462e-894b-0540851486fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 105:20
Text: The king sent and loosed him; even the ruler of the people, and let him go free.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd8fedfd-4b7d-4114-9c4b-8715132b076c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 105:21
Text: He made him lord of his house, and ruler of all his substance:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1853a536-b521-48de-bcd1-4e21573cd855>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 105:22
Text: To bind his princes at his pleasure; and teach his senators wisdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77593716-c29a-460b-8672-c9636f417c3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 105:23
Text: Israel also came into Egypt; and Jacob sojourned in the land of Ham.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8b5dc12-d670-47d8-ab4c-da4d38e52eff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 105:24
Text: And he increased his people greatly; and made them stronger than their enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c9efc22-47cb-4b39-b937-b479dcddb9c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 105:25
Text: He turned their heart to hate his people, to deal subtilly with his servants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f285075-73f8-4f64-b53c-15bd23356cdf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: PSA 105:26
Text: He sent Moses his servant; and Aaron whom he had chosen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5fb6739e-03b1-4445-a51b-1e09d546e61c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 105:27
Text: They shewed his signs among them, and wonders in the land of Ham.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70b13530-461d-47f5-acb0-ce09a7095e96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 105:28
Text: He sent darkness, and made it dark; and they rebelled not against his word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef445101-2624-45e7-b1a7-12e96e59a9a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PSA 105:29
Text: He turned their waters into blood, and slew their fish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1545672-08ad-4d2b-859a-7e6b7ace9daf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 105:30
Text: Their land brought forth frogs in abundance, in the chambers of their kings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80fff859-ac53-4d12-b6c9-6e6813127f06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 105:31
Text: He spake, and there came divers sorts of flies, and lice in all their coasts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a89807b6-6110-4c10-b95d-7c2e19d6e550>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 105:32
Text: He gave them hail for rain, and flaming fire in their land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69822002-b0d6-47b6-91b5-151ebe1b74c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 105:33
Text: He smote their vines also and their fig trees; and brake the trees of their coasts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:387aa897-e588-4a12-a15b-283400d428da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 105:34
Text: He spake, and the locusts came, and caterpillers, and that without number,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d34611e2-92fc-46d7-9001-f2e70f145f29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 105:35
Text: And did eat up all the herbs in their land, and devoured the fruit of their ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2c3a547-6a15-4847-80ef-d8cfd6992a98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 105:36
Text: He smote also all the firstborn in their land, the chief of all their strength.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11e22db1-bd72-4b8d-9999-e769c5a2d6a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: PSA 105:37
Text: He brought them forth also with silver and gold: and there was not one feeble person among their tribes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e130bf9b-9cde-4d12-ac90-ca7cd11f6b3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 105:38
Text: Egypt was glad when they departed: for the fear of them fell upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23627f9a-14a4-48b3-b778-f027ab4232a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 105:39
Text: He spread a cloud for a covering; and fire to give light in the night.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91ca62d2-a300-4d9c-8278-0a8cb2acf7ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 105:40
Text: The people asked, and he brought quails, and satisfied them with the bread of heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cf55ed9-4260-4350-a180-79f07582bf02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 105:41
Text: He opened the rock, and the waters gushed out; they ran in the dry places like a river.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ee3192a-78d3-4107-800e-f01c506509f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 105:42
Text: For he remembered his holy promise, and Abraham his servant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddf97b2f-c061-4430-8477-a8f68d4947de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 105:43
Text: And he brought forth his people with joy, and his chosen with gladness:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d57791a0-9e8d-4072-a56a-3d5e6ab03114>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 105:44
Text: And gave them the lands of the heathen: and they inherited the labour of the people;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/105/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0b62ae3-e11c-4c69-8edb-ff5eac062a61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 105:45
Text: That they might observe his statutes, and keep his laws. Praise ye the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f4da8e9-e921-48e1-be1d-05bbacb895ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 106:1
Text: Praise ye the LORD. O give thanks unto the LORD; for he is good: for his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2165545b-63ad-4250-a8b0-5f9bb7cd77bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 106:2
Text: Who can utter the mighty acts of the LORD? who can shew forth all his praise?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:939e6292-4416-4f4e-9ae7-3cd316212d1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 106:3
Text: Blessed are they that keep judgment, and he that doeth righteousness at all times.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62f78a5c-c670-40c1-9bb0-360d7e54e714>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 106:4
Text: Remember me, O LORD, with the favour that thou bearest unto thy people: O visit me with thy salvation;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bbfed88d-8e6c-457a-a63b-1b1a7e416264>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: PSA 106:5
Text: That I may see the good of thy chosen, that I may rejoice in the gladness of thy nation, that I may glory with thine inheritance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0adba2b-5c24-40ed-9c0e-24c2e858ec0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 106:6
Text: We have sinned with our fathers, we have committed iniquity, we have done wickedly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5d40001-d993-43a0-8252-1a4c53807c34>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: PSA 106:7
Text: Our fathers understood not thy wonders in Egypt; they remembered not the multitude of thy mercies; but provoked him at the sea, even at the Red sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4d0e7c5-885a-4123-9019-e542347578ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 106:8
Text: Nevertheless he saved them for his name’s sake, that he might make his mighty power to be known.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62bc833d-a412-41da-b960-26e2e092c7fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: PSA 106:9
Text: He rebuked the Red sea also, and it was dried up: so he led them through the depths, as through the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3665fca3-67cd-4dd1-8f0b-e618a5e11b1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 106:10
Text: And he saved them from the hand of him that hated them, and redeemed them from the hand of the enemy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8b5cc56-2a88-4df9-b3b1-43cb3d796fd0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 106:11
Text: And the waters covered their enemies: there was not one of them left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04ad48c9-62d4-4148-bf6b-e12fe177bece>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: PSA 106:12
Text: Then believed they his words; they sang his praise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74eebbc6-5787-4972-a280-5547f0507128>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 106:13
Text: They soon forgat his works; they waited not for his counsel:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43c2264d-836c-45ec-abb9-1e3fe99b5188>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 106:14
Text: But lusted exceedingly in the wilderness, and tempted God in the desert.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fee0e324-9bb7-4fd0-9466-20897b38a59a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 106:15
Text: And he gave them their request; but sent leanness into their soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e26d4575-a0f0-470b-ab9a-25a2847b8ac0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 106:16
Text: They envied Moses also in the camp, and Aaron the saint of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:288fb795-bb1b-479d-a292-a367405fcce2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 106:17
Text: The earth opened and swallowed up Dathan and covered the company of Abiram.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0660a5a0-63e1-47b8-9a3a-eec3162f8ddd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 106:18
Text: And a fire was kindled in their company; the flame burned up the wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7ab8fbd-72fa-4686-a426-1048de15500a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 106:19
Text: They made a calf in Horeb, and worshipped the molten image.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d7864fa-8601-47ce-8971-4a5f1f0cbb0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 106:20
Text: Thus they changed their glory into the similitude of an ox that eateth grass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5156b3c6-93ac-4188-a9fe-605609c37bd1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 106:21
Text: They forgat God their saviour, which had done great things in Egypt;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d94a914-648d-4e8d-b7a8-cf071b0ec6cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 106:22
Text: Wondrous works in the land of Ham, and terrible things by the Red sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8305119e-b1d3-46f7-91bd-6176d5881cd0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: PSA 106:23
Text: Therefore he said that he would destroy them, had not Moses his chosen stood before him in the breach, to turn away his wrath, lest he should destroy them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ae842bc-aff7-4a19-b099-08e901bba023>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 106:24
Text: Yea, they despised the pleasant land, they believed not his word:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9aff2f08-f388-495c-a7be-df5614d13bcc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 106:25
Text: But murmured in their tents, and hearkened not unto the voice of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1bff206-dcf6-47a2-ae5f-1fdbd8a6ac89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 106:26
Text: Therefore he lifted up his hand against them, to overthrow them in the wilderness:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55020998-9a6e-4745-846a-caab469700e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 106:27
Text: To overthrow their seed also among the nations, and to scatter them in the lands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e49b2c7-4ef0-4291-b1dc-df16f288f662>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 106:28
Text: They joined themselves also unto Baalpeor, and ate the sacrifices of the dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:910dbcd6-c164-4679-bf08-1a91f23dbbfb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 106:29
Text: Thus they provoked him to anger with their inventions: and the plague brake in upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2f79d78-0d8d-4bcc-8816-977a68a79ffb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 106:30
Text: Then stood up Phinehas, and executed judgment: and so the plague was stayed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f698d6ca-9f15-4989-8d8d-b362588ed088>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 106:31
Text: And that was counted unto him for righteousness unto all generations for evermore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b6ec5d0-3c18-41e5-ac46-b503675d7bb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 106:32
Text: They angered him also at the waters of strife, so that it went ill with Moses for their sakes:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:574cd8a6-e666-4c8d-81c9-93906180de4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 106:33
Text: Because they provoked his spirit, so that he spake unadvisedly with his lips.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42c7ffac-885b-417a-924c-af608102adb1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 106:34
Text: They did not destroy the nations, concerning whom the LORD commanded them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4def67da-bb88-4fde-8d68-f2f1bf7d839d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 106:35
Text: But were mingled among the heathen, and learned their works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a87e3b5-d095-48db-9168-4be34c1415a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PSA 106:36
Text: And they served their idols: which were a snare unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff1aec01-a88b-4618-a201-3fc6a915b256>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 106:37
Text: Yea, they sacrificed their sons and their daughters unto devils,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf8ddacc-b892-4a5d-b72b-5a689870fd98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: PSA 106:38
Text: And shed innocent blood, even the blood of their sons and of their daughters, whom they sacrificed unto the idols of Canaan: and the land was polluted with blood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bdeac85c-23d4-41dc-8f15-c2fbc98d361f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 106:39
Text: Thus were they defiled with their own works, and went a whoring with their own inventions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:100dee58-66e2-40c2-872e-c283a2c6d829>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: PSA 106:40
Text: Therefore was the wrath of the LORD kindled against his people, insomuch that he abhorred his own inheritance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ca66893-5c8a-4e18-b45a-0f555c31860e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 106:41
Text: And he gave them into the hand of the heathen; and they that hated them ruled over them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ff5f6e9-1f18-4de5-b855-ec08b8c3d683>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 106:42
Text: Their enemies also oppressed them, and they were brought into subjection under their hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:330e07fe-a0f5-407d-b4ca-bdbec1341eef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: PSA 106:43
Text: Many times did he deliver them; but they provoked him with their counsel, and were brought low for their iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b322525-7781-45f0-8a50-efacaec126fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 106:44
Text: Nevertheless he regarded their affliction, when he heard their cry:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:048855d4-0783-4836-bb4e-773851c308b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 106:45
Text: And he remembered for them his covenant, and repented according to the multitude of his mercies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a5f1c7d-0329-444c-a9ac-b682f729f25a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 106:46
Text: He made them also to be pitied of all those that carried them captives.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6926dcb7-8fac-45af-83aa-d1c1e1607bd5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: PSA 106:47
Text: Save us, O LORD our God, and gather us from among the heathen, to give thanks unto thy holy name, and to triumph in thy praise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/106/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09210959-e5a4-4525-b8a9-b5c637928d50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: PSA 106:48
Text: Blessed be the LORD God of Israel from everlasting to everlasting: and let all the people say, Amen. Praise ye the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89ddf1ae-cde7-4b9d-bd8f-8db20376fa65>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 107:1
Text: O give thanks unto the LORD, for he is good: for his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fc450e5-65a6-4ba1-8bd0-1da12c7f3460>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 107:2
Text: Let the redeemed of the LORD say so, whom he hath redeemed from the hand of the enemy;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:656eef2f-3926-4cc6-8fc8-20796306ea5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: PSA 107:3
Text: And gathered them out of the lands, from the east, and from the west, from the north, and from the south.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87964141-1d81-4ef5-a873-2c512ae8eae2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 107:4
Text: They wandered in the wilderness in a solitary way; they found no city to dwell in.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0f6bdcf-d155-43ca-b70c-7cc99577067a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: PSA 107:5
Text: Hungry and thirsty, their soul fainted in them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df38ed10-c2e3-4e1e-86c5-1f6f550561a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 107:6
Text: Then they cried unto the LORD in their trouble, and he delivered them out of their distresses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74df587c-ac7f-443a-8c6d-f703eaf8b48c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 107:7
Text: And he led them forth by the right way, that they might go to a city of habitation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:babb7508-4e59-4f65-a4b2-9e00b535c9d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 107:8
Text: Oh that men would praise the LORD for his goodness, and for his wonderful works to the children of men!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df8179a3-3858-4b28-b45a-509ce81605e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 107:9
Text: For he satisfieth the longing soul, and filleth the hungry soul with goodness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afce3b79-a0a9-4d05-bfb1-9ac107406b55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 107:10
Text: Such as sit in darkness and in the shadow of death, being bound in affliction and iron;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:102af9af-5e21-4b7a-b6c7-c215d1e9e69e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 107:11
Text: Because they rebelled against the words of God, and contemned the counsel of the most High:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c945077e-4da5-498b-bd6e-6b673e9f86ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 107:12
Text: Therefore he brought down their heart with labour; they fell down, and there was none to help.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2bdd3a7-6b5f-41d3-97ac-649e2020407c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 107:13
Text: Then they cried unto the LORD in their trouble, and he saved them out of their distresses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6185f1e7-b8e6-44c1-913c-b5d03cf41e95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 107:14
Text: He brought them out of darkness and the shadow of death, and brake their bands in sunder.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8be78f3-6a73-48b4-954a-5d15f982ccf9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 107:15
Text: Oh that men would praise the LORD for his goodness, and for his wonderful works to the children of men!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e32514b3-ff15-4af2-8b43-63bdcc9cb5a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 107:16
Text: For he hath broken the gates of brass, and cut the bars of iron in sunder.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:437f813f-2fc1-43f1-85fd-6c6b83101e85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 107:17
Text: Fools because of their transgression, and because of their iniquities, are afflicted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e929b28-0e8c-4385-8ee6-ae499dbfa50a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 107:18
Text: Their soul abhorreth all manner of meat; and they draw near unto the gates of death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba0d2866-a0cf-4fab-a47c-dc28db5f7469>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 107:19
Text: Then they cry unto the LORD in their trouble, and he saveth them out of their distresses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b519e29c-d4a3-460e-9edc-99836bb8b343>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 107:20
Text: He sent his word, and healed them, and delivered them from their destructions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fc9e8d0-ab58-426f-a7fe-c166199cde66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 107:21
Text: Oh that men would praise the LORD for his goodness, and for his wonderful works to the children of men!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc79038d-5dac-4738-96f0-c15d18fac8d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 107:22
Text: And let them sacrifice the sacrifices of thanksgiving, and declare his works with rejoicing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10669c7b-10b2-4c1c-95d2-9a12bd77a917>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 107:23
Text: They that go down to the sea in ships, that do business in great waters;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d8d601f-c51d-4f2f-b019-df7d1cb7712a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 107:24
Text: These see the works of the LORD, and his wonders in the deep.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:322e7f01-db69-4e39-91e2-9e293174cacb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 107:25
Text: For he commandeth, and raiseth the stormy wind, which lifteth up the waves thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8012f2cc-34b4-4777-966a-1e712af6b4bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 107:26
Text: They mount up to the heaven, they go down again to the depths: their soul is melted because of trouble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d26e2d6b-0553-46e1-bdf5-0cdfde1a1e42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 107:27
Text: They reel to and fro, and stagger like a drunken man, and are at their wit’s end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c5c6421-990f-4015-9074-c7456080710a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 107:28
Text: Then they cry unto the LORD in their trouble, and he bringeth them out of their distresses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:000cca66-faa7-40f6-97e7-9b40d97d96ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 107:29
Text: He maketh the storm a calm, so that the waves thereof are still.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:141dffd5-f84e-4d1c-b7a2-8a5ca88a3a16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 107:30
Text: Then are they glad because they be quiet; so he bringeth them unto their desired haven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db4287b2-6d42-4a14-bb86-c4557aca8272>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 107:31
Text: Oh that men would praise the LORD for his goodness, and for his wonderful works to the children of men!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ce9c730-ce27-409a-84e9-47d4714fab6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: PSA 107:32
Text: Let them exalt him also in the congregation of the people, and praise him in the assembly of the elders.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9073cf91-80bf-4f2f-8b9e-5bbd44687f93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 107:33
Text: He turneth rivers into a wilderness, and the watersprings into dry ground;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:228c50a4-1929-47f7-8dad-1791c8c24cd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 107:34
Text: A fruitful land into barrenness, for the wickedness of them that dwell therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ecd49c7f-b4f5-4cd7-a3b5-54386cc208d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 107:35
Text: He turneth the wilderness into a standing water, and dry ground into watersprings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c149f79-ff67-4206-8b2f-23bd4c0fc5cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 107:36
Text: And there he maketh the hungry to dwell, that they may prepare a city for habitation;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2563aee-3f51-40bc-ab4f-d997aa7fb13e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 107:37
Text: And sow the fields, and plant vineyards, which may yield fruits of increase.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cab09b80-c062-42b8-806f-ce6008c763e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 107:38
Text: He blesseth them also, so that they are multiplied greatly; and suffereth not their cattle to decrease.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f66da80-6c72-4aa8-82f8-13439eefd312>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 107:39
Text: Again, they are minished and brought low through oppression, affliction, and sorrow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c579f9c7-1151-4e1f-a799-53f9f0f526e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 107:40
Text: He poureth contempt upon princes, and causeth them to wander in the wilderness, where there is no way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17fe19a5-728b-440a-9bae-b9daa8dfff10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 107:41
Text: Yet setteth he the poor on high from affliction, and maketh him families like a flock.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:611ce7b7-c475-404c-98cc-6f24d277666b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 107:42
Text: The righteous shall see it, and rejoice: and all iniquity shall stop her mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/107/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4e90668-89f8-4cae-93c9-57675846c0a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: PSA 107:43
Text: Whoso is wise, and will observe these things, even they shall understand the lovingkindness of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/108/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0816273c-a78c-46b9-8c20-7adfe100a379>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 108:1
Text: O god, my heart is fixed; I will sing and give praise, even with my glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/108/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a0de36b-74ae-4a29-ad03-0068096a2b82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: PSA 108:2
Text: Awake, psaltery and harp: I myself will awake early.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/108/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a64d1d3f-d41e-49b8-b586-e08f0a60dbe1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 108:3
Text: I will praise thee, O LORD, among the people: and I will sing praises unto thee among the nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/108/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e4bb0d9-f641-414c-b99f-2cdfe9c559bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 108:4
Text: For thy mercy is great above the heavens: and thy truth reacheth unto the clouds.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/108/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5314f429-4de2-4c30-82ff-74ef2226016c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 108:5
Text: Be thou exalted, O God, above the heavens: and thy glory above all the earth;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/108/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:434ba69a-0d14-4abd-a251-99e640ca74d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 108:6
Text: That thy beloved may be delivered: save with thy right hand, and answer me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/108/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea5425c1-9f95-4616-bfa9-f705fbd80f00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PSA 108:7
Text: God hath spoken in his holiness; I will rejoice, I will divide Shechem, and mete out the valley of Succoth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/108/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6f37894-85ee-42e9-b186-91cc64fc072b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 108:8
Text: Gilead is mine; Manasseh is mine; Ephraim also is the strength of mine head; Judah is my lawgiver;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/108/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:759c484e-86e2-4350-bb95-4a6f1fc6114d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 108:9
Text: Moab is my washpot; over Edom will I cast out my shoe; over Philistia will I triumph.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/108/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:182624ad-0da6-4e9e-bae7-efbb50a720d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 108:10
Text: Who will bring me into the strong city? who will lead me into Edom?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/108/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:662feb8e-d167-412a-98ce-813ffa017603>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 108:11
Text: Wilt not thou, O God, who hast cast us off? and wilt not thou, O God, go forth with our hosts?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/108/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76a5666d-f65d-4f96-9675-cf1532839a98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PSA 108:12
Text: Give us help from trouble: for vain is the help of man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/108/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33519507-9b5a-46fa-9e31-1e31916e7f53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 108:13
Text: Through God we shall do valiantly: for he it is that shall tread down our enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:330cea03-3a8a-4638-a023-83910ad06d91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 67

Reference: PSA 109:1
Text: Hold not thy peace, O God of my praise;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:548c7c80-59ea-4f43-a7e1-ee74cb72613b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: PSA 109:2
Text: For the mouth of the wicked and the mouth of the deceitful are opened against me: they have spoken against me with a lying tongue.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f895642-e4c4-4d4f-86ab-776aca7c91cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 109:3
Text: They compassed me about also with words of hatred; and fought against me without a cause.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86541006-6a70-4fad-9549-8d92c947ba4f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 109:4
Text: For my love they are my adversaries: but I give myself unto prayer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68d0186f-4356-40f2-886e-c9adce7f9760>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PSA 109:5
Text: And they have rewarded me evil for good, and hatred for my love.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e059dc93-e37a-4107-a299-c6d08636be29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 109:6
Text: Set thou a wicked man over him: and let Satan stand at his right hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbb97c69-f013-4ac6-bfda-19cf795d4168>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 109:7
Text: When he shall be judged, let him be condemned: and let his prayer become sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e42d8d12-2910-4f60-8025-2e1956fdf0f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: PSA 109:8
Text: Let his days be few; and let another take his office.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42dc4fd6-ef00-46fa-abbb-db916ef3d398>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: PSA 109:9
Text: Let his children be fatherless, and his wife a widow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4426a7c-5b86-4d1b-98ef-7ecfd496539c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: PSA 109:10
Text: Let his children be continually vagabonds, and beg: let them seek their bread also out of their desolate places.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b2a933b-a820-497a-a661-406cbd3b604b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 109:11
Text: Let the extortioner catch all that he hath; and let the strangers spoil his labour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee8a35c2-8122-4fe5-8fe7-5b4e43b9f0e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 109:12
Text: Let there be none to extend mercy unto him: neither let there be any to favour his fatherless children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7cbe02c0-2175-4375-bfd7-68d6708b0a86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 109:13
Text: Let his posterity be cut off; and in the generation following let their name be blotted out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3cf538b-f1ab-4cc8-a457-98adef951724>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: PSA 109:14
Text: Let the iniquity of his fathers be remembered with the LORD; and let not the sin of his mother be blotted out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95f50d31-2256-40b2-b346-639b81682a9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 109:15
Text: Let them be before the LORD continually, that he may cut off the memory of them from the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1315f0f-1edd-4c8b-a905-9e45db6cd2ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: PSA 109:16
Text: Because that he remembered not to shew mercy, but persecuted the poor and needy man, that he might even slay the broken in heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2b3f945-f965-4cb4-8ec8-a6db4c755d41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PSA 109:17
Text: As he loved cursing, so let it come unto him: as he delighted not in blessing, so let it be far from him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b6986e2-21f8-45c6-a178-1b0371f77f7a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: PSA 109:18
Text: As he clothed himself with cursing like as with his garment, so let it come into his bowels like water, and like oil into his bones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14cec06d-6be4-4e01-b38a-074faf7b75d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PSA 109:19
Text: Let it be unto him as the garment which covereth him, and for a girdle wherewith he is girded continually.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f68f6156-353f-476f-ad2d-3431059ce9e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 109:20
Text: Let this be the reward of mine adversaries from the LORD, and of them that speak evil against my soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:076a3ff5-6e02-40c5-abae-34d82d24f5c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 109:21
Text: But do thou for me, O GOD the Lord, for thy name’s sake: because thy mercy is good, deliver thou me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70447b51-fd29-4efe-96ad-ac05a589b69d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 109:22
Text: For I am poor and needy, and my heart is wounded within me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b48be5a-08f5-4cc5-9c94-8c40e7a35d56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 109:23
Text: I am gone like the shadow when it declineth: I am tossed up and down as the locust.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f83de60-1dcb-40d7-ba17-d618eef71de7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 109:24
Text: My knees are weak through fasting; and my flesh faileth of fatness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06e67de0-0df1-4673-90ab-d5e8282803ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 109:25
Text: I became also a reproach unto them: when they looked upon me they shaked their heads.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9bbe20de-2a47-43bf-ab26-01c7d9176b70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PSA 109:26
Text: Help me, O LORD my God: O save me according to thy mercy:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0444dcb1-a1eb-4d7e-b4fd-b006fc53acac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 109:27
Text: That they may know that this is thy hand; that thou, LORD, hast done it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2af09f01-9d1a-4529-aff7-f9a111d4b40e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PSA 109:28
Text: Let them curse, but bless thou: when they arise, let them be ashamed; but let thy servant rejoice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:417a712e-e2c7-42db-b9cd-21dee78c7a3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: PSA 109:29
Text: Let mine adversaries be clothed with shame, and let them cover themselves with their own confusion, as with a mantle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4eaf0b78-a9e0-4779-b64c-789815fd27ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 109:30
Text: I will greatly praise the LORD with my mouth; yea, I will praise him among the multitude.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/109/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7bb510e7-f8a2-4d1e-8de9-d54cd9b164d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 109:31
Text: For he shall stand at the right hand of the poor, to save him from those that condemn his soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/110/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b976103d-b3bd-40b4-af65-0ff1d9e66da4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 110:1
Text: The LORD said unto my Lord, Sit thou at my right hand, until I make thine enemies thy footstool.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/110/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:036649dc-b858-4ec7-95bf-5c6960042867>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 110:2
Text: The LORD shall send the rod of thy strength out of Zion: rule thou in the midst of thine enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/110/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3801f427-afd8-4223-a827-e2d119d9abff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: PSA 110:3
Text: Thy people shall be willing in the day of thy power, in the beauties of holiness from the womb of the morning: thou hast the dew of thy youth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/110/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c479c47-e7ba-418b-803c-22dde03fe5de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 110:4
Text: The LORD hath sworn, and will not repent, Thou art a priest for ever after the order of Melchizedek.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/110/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd62ae1b-9a2c-42b6-92e2-47744622ccda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 110:5
Text: The Lord at thy right hand shall strike through kings in the day of his wrath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/110/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a5784a8-3efb-42d0-b781-6e25df00f274>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: PSA 110:6
Text: He shall judge among the heathen, he shall fill the places with the dead bodies; he shall wound the heads over many countries.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/110/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44ee789e-e6f6-43a9-9775-6970277381d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 110:7
Text: He shall drink of the brook in the way: therefore shall he lift up the head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/111/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9324815f-0527-4c83-befc-cd11b2113f51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: PSA 111:1
Text: Praise ye the LORD. I will praise the LORD with my whole heart, in the assembly of the upright, and in the congregation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/111/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf23f514-a192-4670-b1cd-ba0b906ae261>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 111:2
Text: The works of the LORD are great, sought out of all them that have pleasure therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/111/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07bb500d-a76b-4af8-80c4-9bee47cef310>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 111:3
Text: His work is honourable and glorious: and his righteousness endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/111/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1331837-78db-40aa-a831-2e04a554f531>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 111:4
Text: He hath made his wonderful works to be remembered: the LORD is gracious and full of compassion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/111/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28a24002-4e03-40b3-a8b4-266d78588824>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 111:5
Text: He hath given meat unto them that fear him: he will ever be mindful of his covenant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/111/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:667282fa-4190-4089-a288-c621d6cd1b87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 111:6
Text: He hath shewed his people the power of his works, that he may give them the heritage of the heathen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/111/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36039170-28dd-46fd-82df-744158a6e3e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 111:7
Text: The works of his hands are verity and judgment; all his commandments are sure.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/111/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b66551eb-7d24-4ffb-a11d-1507b44f96d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 111:8
Text: They stand fast for ever and ever, and are done in truth and uprightness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/111/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d8d0d21-8242-40e9-a72e-bb401d3688c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PSA 111:9
Text: He sent redemption unto his people: he hath commanded his covenant for ever: holy and reverend is his name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/111/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a875a7e-a20f-485a-a48e-44163782cb63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: PSA 111:10
Text: The fear of the LORD is the beginning of wisdom: a good understanding have all they that do his commandments: his praise endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/112/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5c3b963-80c9-422d-bc24-5094f4a2dd5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PSA 112:1
Text: Praise ye the LORD. Blessed is the man that feareth the LORD, that delighteth greatly in his commandments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/112/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f186363f-69be-46bb-a94a-a0e9737b446c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 112:2
Text: His seed shall be mighty upon earth: the generation of the upright shall be blessed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/112/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0dc796f1-932f-40a9-b008-afc94c9ad12e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 112:3
Text: Wealth and riches shall be in his house: and his righteousness endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/112/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88f49991-2cd1-4f16-8682-f267c02099ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PSA 112:4
Text: Unto the upright there ariseth light in the darkness: he is gracious, and full of compassion, and righteous.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/112/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:317520c1-7722-4877-82ca-03dc62731867>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 112:5
Text: A good man sheweth favour, and lendeth: he will guide his affairs with discretion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/112/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b31fa32-4bc9-40a3-8802-5991c569b6c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 112:6
Text: Surely he shall not be moved for ever: the righteous shall be in everlasting remembrance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/112/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6faa0c4d-9ec0-4d1a-a335-6502c3e5b504>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 112:7
Text: He shall not be afraid of evil tidings: his heart is fixed, trusting in the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/112/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad82267c-ca5f-47fc-94b6-2439f6317f6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 112:8
Text: His heart is established, he shall not be afraid, until he see his desire upon his enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/112/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:527d6d64-99c3-4125-b34e-7866f15506ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: PSA 112:9
Text: He hath dispersed, he hath given to the poor; his righteousness endureth for ever; his horn shall be exalted with honour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/112/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89add6fb-a6ae-4da9-9388-2c77b2422e74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: PSA 112:10
Text: The wicked shall see it, and be grieved; he shall gnash with his teeth, and melt away: the desire of the wicked shall perish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/113/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c8bfd61-b7cf-496e-b7e1-62e848fe5921>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 113:1
Text: Praise ye the LORD. Praise, O ye servants of the LORD, praise the name of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/113/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ef119ba-1e35-4955-82a2-8a0a7f4c2435>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 113:2
Text: Blessed be the name of the LORD from this time forth and for evermore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/113/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07eca929-7ba7-4a63-ac92-21236e8542d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 113:3
Text: From the rising of the sun unto the going down of the same the LORD’s name is to be praised.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/113/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:987ae2de-c920-43a9-a6af-afe82c9677e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 113:4
Text: The LORD is high above all nations, and his glory above the heavens.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/113/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9375eff3-69a1-4a1b-87a5-0cde2dccbec9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PSA 113:5
Text: Who is like unto the LORD our God, who dwelleth on high,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/113/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73069432-9945-4146-ab36-268677c5f84e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 113:6
Text: Who humbleth himself to behold the things that are in heaven, and in the earth!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/113/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78858727-baff-4544-af96-1d46a2a8747e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 113:7
Text: He raiseth up the poor out of the dust, and lifteth the needy out of the dunghill;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/113/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1446940b-449f-4b2f-8826-e5a2cedad7ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 113:8
Text: That he may set him with princes, even with the princes of his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/113/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d07c174-7eec-41cc-b256-daf36ccf41cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 113:9
Text: He maketh the barren woman to keep house, and to be a joyful mother of children. Praise ye the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/114/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c23235cc-359d-42c8-841d-dff849fd155e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 114:1
Text: When Israel went out of Egypt, the house of Jacob from a people of strange language;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/114/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63fdb326-0919-4362-9a1b-c46b54f4279d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: PSA 114:2
Text: Judah was his sanctuary, and Israel his dominion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/114/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d80e50c-d435-45ad-ba93-2490c21e6155>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: PSA 114:3
Text: The sea saw it, and fled: Jordan was driven back.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/114/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d5837cb-4260-446b-a190-9680d43a348d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 114:4
Text: The mountains skipped like rams, and the little hills like lambs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/114/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9bce782d-16cc-4485-a778-2bece84869c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 114:5
Text: What ailed thee, O thou sea, that thou fleddest? thou Jordan, that thou wast driven back?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/114/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a8abe9d-21fc-47d6-9031-5627adf1d04d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 114:6
Text: Ye mountains, that ye skipped like rams; and ye little hills, like lambs?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/114/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2bfadb2-60c7-4ec0-98af-8c45f81a5b2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 114:7
Text: Tremble, thou earth, at the presence of the Lord, at the presence of the God of Jacob;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/114/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd3ae25a-0fa1-4ec9-841d-d59814964cf8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 114:8
Text: Which turned the rock into a standing water, the flint into a fountain of waters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/115/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6fc1c13-7f12-4af7-a323-453dc7611d1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PSA 115:1
Text: Not unto us, O LORD, not unto us, but unto thy name give glory, for thy mercy, and for thy truth’s sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/115/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c922cd8-f73a-4334-8983-9efafc7e230f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: PSA 115:2
Text: Wherefore should the heathen say, Where is now their God?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/115/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d11d66f0-f28e-4b3d-8de4-34962c87b69d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 115:3
Text: But our God is in the heavens: he hath done whatsoever he hath pleased.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/115/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:436f21a8-78c8-42e4-92f9-5e5368c76293>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PSA 115:4
Text: Their idols are silver and gold, the work of men’s hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/115/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eccf804e-8ba2-47f2-9baa-376a9d905b1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 115:5
Text: They have mouths, but they speak not: eyes have they, but they see not:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/115/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba481d34-4545-4844-b0dc-cf3262a8cfab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 115:6
Text: They have ears, but they hear not: noses have they, but they smell not:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/115/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:910e4743-369d-45aa-91bd-37ec9df404f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: PSA 115:7
Text: They have hands, but they handle not: feet have they, but they walk not: neither speak they through their throat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/115/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:329d8113-c1b3-47c4-9a5e-97ad18388e9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 115:8
Text: They that make them are like unto them; so is every one that trusteth in them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/115/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be4248c5-2ae2-4ad9-96c2-6a5eae02dce6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 115:9
Text: O Israel, trust thou in the LORD: he is their help and their shield.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/115/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5aee20aa-b790-4124-a007-e5d48a2fa92a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 115:10
Text: O house of Aaron, trust in the LORD: he is their help and their shield.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/115/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87f5d010-1c2d-4f53-91d7-8de4047892e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 115:11
Text: Ye that fear the LORD, trust in the LORD: he is their help and their shield.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/115/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8065c83e-4edf-4518-8bcf-e86b03612fc8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: PSA 115:12
Text: The LORD hath been mindful of us: he will bless us; he will bless the house of Israel; he will bless the house of Aaron.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/115/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50aac77e-17df-4e4c-b362-28f92ddc595f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 115:13
Text: He will bless them that fear the LORD, both small and great.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/115/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2e56a84-2f33-4118-96bf-51de2b7d74bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 115:14
Text: The LORD shall increase you more and more, you and your children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/115/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9561f6c-2bea-42c8-8628-f7ca843481a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PSA 115:15
Text: Ye are blessed of the LORD which made heaven and earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/115/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2348204-0c0e-4a11-b738-adc0c5599a2b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 115:16
Text: The heaven, even the heavens, are the LORD’s: but the earth hath he given to the children of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/115/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbd2aa81-93f4-46df-a064-e9a78df25e9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 115:17
Text: The dead praise not the LORD, neither any that go down into silence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/115/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:053db92c-9694-4430-9877-d043e5d49127>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 115:18
Text: But we will bless the LORD from this time forth and for evermore. Praise the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/116/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ecd32583-a7b7-4db3-9bb7-0af12d293997>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 116:1
Text: I love the LORD, because he hath heard my voice and my supplications.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/116/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97ad151f-4c8a-43f5-ae2b-2e6eaf02cb95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 116:2
Text: Because he hath inclined his ear unto me, therefore will I call upon him as long as I live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/116/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d350227-f38c-4188-82dc-5f08fccb0393>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 116:3
Text: The sorrows of death compassed me, and the pains of hell gat hold upon me: I found trouble and sorrow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/116/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b992e2b-3d2e-41a7-aca9-0d364d9faa6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 116:4
Text: Then called I upon the name of the LORD; O LORD, I beseech thee, deliver my soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/116/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3eaeddf8-d0bd-4aff-b251-6ec619a31e73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 116:5
Text: Gracious is the LORD, and righteous; yea, our God is merciful.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/116/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69312041-2386-4887-bf0c-0d9862c3f11f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 116:6
Text: The LORD preserveth the simple: I was brought low, and he helped me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/116/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef57f724-0387-4b8c-989d-80497cb1e80f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 116:7
Text: Return unto thy rest, O my soul; for the LORD hath dealt bountifully with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/116/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:167e8e5d-c0ed-422d-bf9d-3053c2f45e69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 116:8
Text: For thou hast delivered my soul from death, mine eyes from tears, and my feet from falling.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/116/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82e4d62a-4fde-4193-bdac-42a87402e570>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: PSA 116:9
Text: I will walk before the LORD in the land of the living.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/116/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f28d08b-05ce-4084-91ca-5a01f32a1325>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 116:10
Text: I believed, therefore have I spoken: I was greatly afflicted:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/116/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:377c7646-052b-4d14-84e5-20f79a56fdc8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 67

Reference: PSA 116:11
Text: I said in my haste, All men are liars.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/116/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dcc91f14-4b72-4b2c-b643-74ea052f16ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 116:12
Text: What shall I render unto the LORD for all his benefits toward me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/116/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a6cade2-4760-4f02-b824-8293cfeb4f39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 116:13
Text: I will take the cup of salvation, and call upon the name of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/116/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4575b8e4-2960-4128-91e7-392d0016d4c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 116:14
Text: I will pay my vows unto the LORD now in the presence of all his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/116/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa129cf2-e2ce-430a-9952-66aa619b32e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 116:15
Text: Precious in the sight of the LORD is the death of his saints.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/116/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6041626-bd63-4579-b7bc-093622e8908d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PSA 116:16
Text: O LORD, truly I am thy servant; I am thy servant, and the son of thine handmaid: thou hast loosed my bonds.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/116/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f48819c-67ac-4990-9f34-dbe132ef2534>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 116:17
Text: I will offer to thee the sacrifice of thanksgiving, and will call upon the name of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/116/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8bfa946-ee4f-4b08-afae-0d3e3bd65b9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 116:18
Text: I will pay my vows unto the LORD now in the presence of all his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/116/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ceac476f-e1fc-4f81-ba20-ab453a95c99d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 116:19
Text: In the courts of the LORD’s house, in the midst of thee, O Jerusalem. Praise ye the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/117/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba5b71f8-e930-4aaa-b88c-3b70cab8969b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 117:1
Text: O praise the LORD, all ye nations: praise him, all ye people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/117/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71ad7c7f-78f4-4f6f-a659-971c9a70963c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PSA 117:2
Text: For his merciful kindness is great toward us: and the truth of the LORD endureth for ever. Praise ye the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d7918f8-60bf-4d21-92aa-4548f13f2a58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 118:1
Text: O give thanks unto the LORD; for he is good: because his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b9d635f-4939-4e35-8209-d73dfead5621>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: PSA 118:2
Text: Let Israel now say, that his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a9a304e-5865-4b3b-ac1f-debdf5ae1f33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 118:3
Text: Let the house of Aaron now say, that his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73241ae7-2d85-4217-b8ac-2ffac2b3e31b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 118:4
Text: Let them now that fear the LORD say, that his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bb81894-2940-40b4-ae02-150d9bb92908>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 118:5
Text: I called upon the LORD in distress: the LORD answered me, and set me in a large place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:017c0200-71d0-4f43-abaf-544e8b096ee8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 118:6
Text: The LORD is on my side; I will not fear: what can man do unto me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9374e528-2fc3-4fb4-9571-df85b03095c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 118:7
Text: The LORD taketh my part with them that help me: therefore shall I see my desire upon them that hate me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea5cb84d-1c9d-4c36-a0b0-be4063c1eea1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PSA 118:8
Text: It is better to trust in the LORD than to put confidence in man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a984d09b-8c36-437c-a97b-f96070289abe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 118:9
Text: It is better to trust in the LORD than to put confidence in princes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe08aa10-7861-4fd7-a211-13ce934e74c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 118:10
Text: All nations compassed me about: but in the name of the LORD will I destroy them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75952cb1-2043-42e4-8bdb-7328a6e924b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 118:11
Text: They compassed me about; yea, they compassed me about: but in the name of the LORD I will destroy them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7cccc42-a1c8-4374-ac17-9882c8c8272d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: PSA 118:12
Text: They compassed me about like bees: they are quenched as the fire of thorns: for in the name of the LORD I will destroy them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9646cea-666a-412d-8dac-bd9521e232f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 118:13
Text: Thou hast thrust sore at me that I might fall: but the LORD helped me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5911c4c-e5ab-4df5-9300-efe986f46566>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 118:14
Text: The LORD is my strength and song, and is become my salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fae419bf-d1c3-40de-a234-395effc44695>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: PSA 118:15
Text: The voice of rejoicing and salvation is in the tabernacles of the righteous: the right hand of the LORD doeth valiantly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10ac71da-442a-4a27-990f-384a0f71e7bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 118:16
Text: The right hand of the LORD is exalted: the right hand of the LORD doeth valiantly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a4f7ebe-29b6-4707-a160-36c6256ea06d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 118:17
Text: I shall not die, but live, and declare the works of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81a99719-ed66-4ad9-b5ef-2898b1e8adcf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 118:18
Text: The LORD hath chastened me sore: but he hath not given me over unto death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7479dadc-1ed5-4f44-aabb-dfbc6fcea25a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 118:19
Text: Open to me the gates of righteousness: I will go into them, and I will praise the LORD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba154f34-b7ad-4bdc-b49d-74eb4cd04c78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 118:20
Text: This gate of the LORD, into which the righteous shall enter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:555286f9-3344-4d09-a3d8-2262ffff1b1e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 118:21
Text: I will praise thee: for thou hast heard me, and art become my salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fce7978e-76f6-4ce4-a36c-bbfdf2493dc5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 118:22
Text: The stone which the builders refused is become the head stone of the corner.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6560de6b-d157-4cf4-9609-c4915863e683>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PSA 118:23
Text: This is the LORD’s doing; it is marvellous in our eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a370a7b5-d184-4f8a-8783-f8cd1798f804>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 118:24
Text: This is the day which the LORD hath made; we will rejoice and be glad in it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:404d2b2e-382e-4091-9051-1504f42b41fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 118:25
Text: Save now, I beseech thee, O LORD: O LORD, I beseech thee, send now prosperity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:439790d2-566e-45ab-8755-837dc29d4a4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PSA 118:26
Text: Blessed be he that cometh in the name of the LORD: we have blessed you out of the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:207f5254-c7dd-48df-9999-51958f12b7c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PSA 118:27
Text: God is the LORD, which hath shewed us light: bind the sacrifice with cords, even unto the horns of the altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8cb0c1ac-e613-41f5-b04a-3a25d54246e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 118:28
Text: Thou art my God, and I will praise thee: thou art my God, I will exalt thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/118/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e330e21-ab93-430e-84d7-52bf81f07b01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 118:29
Text: O give thanks unto the LORD; for he is good: for his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63eca4d4-cc19-4b40-abe4-d0a492a27038>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 119:1
Text: Blessed are the undefiled in the way, who walk in the law of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08c10481-bd19-43b6-863e-7e54d683fd9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 119:2
Text: Blessed are they that keep his testimonies, and that seek him with the whole heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:556bb729-a8a1-4e9c-be94-90613b74be09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: PSA 119:3
Text: They also do no iniquity: they walk in his ways.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ececfa04-a1f3-42fd-9842-1766f57c0295>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: PSA 119:4
Text: Thou hast commanded us to keep thy precepts diligently.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddc58a93-5b8c-4221-aa57-e46575b22b41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: PSA 119:5
Text: O that my ways were directed to keep thy statutes!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d54b602-4ae2-4093-8270-e447806fae34>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 119:6
Text: Then shall I not be ashamed, when I have respect unto all thy commandments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78a94744-53d4-46f4-b884-e7c6503ab85e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 119:7
Text: I will praise thee with uprightness of heart, when I shall have learned thy righteous judgments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b7867f8-7d99-415f-97e5-c62e75eaabd8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: PSA 119:8
Text: I will keep thy statutes: O forsake me not utterly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4aefeba4-f9a9-4eee-bf7b-33e62f15d5fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 119:9
Text: Wherewithal shall a young man cleanse his way? by taking heed thereto according to thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfc4b218-bf6d-4a91-8d05-aef58d3da1b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 119:10
Text: With my whole heart have I sought thee: O let me not wander from thy commandments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7e5c35b-0fe0-45fa-bf14-eed5a6e002be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 119:11
Text: Thy word have I hid in mine heart, that I might not sin against thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41862194-bc15-4650-ae20-c589eb32f464>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: PSA 119:12
Text: Blessed art thou, O LORD: teach me thy statutes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4125a2f7-6997-4e11-bc86-babb3dab21ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 119:13
Text: With my lips have I declared all the judgments of thy mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa576812-9bf0-488a-ac89-f67145c2a6ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 119:14
Text: I have rejoiced in the way of thy testimonies, as much as in all riches.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2785bc54-0499-4b25-8dae-70f93f5df510>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 119:15
Text: I will meditate in thy precepts, and have respect unto thy ways.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b621e57-1a6a-4444-ac87-256771290309>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 119:16
Text: I will delight myself in thy statutes: I will not forget thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0631fa1-ceff-45af-bdbc-1563fd509083>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 119:17
Text: Deal bountifully with thy servant, that I may live, and keep thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:715e1ae0-2313-4a0e-8d5e-d17a6a5a0384>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 119:18
Text: Open thou mine eyes, that I may behold wondrous things out of thy law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0641f7c3-0d55-42f8-941c-dda945e4b1f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 119:19
Text: I am a stranger in the earth: hide not thy commandments from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b6b8d3a-16e2-4737-bc3b-7bf2f46fd55d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 119:20
Text: My soul breaketh for the longing that it hath unto thy judgments at all times.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a23b7a0-8047-4834-beae-808dca2a71d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 119:21
Text: Thou hast rebuked the proud that are cursed, which do err from thy commandments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b63a9055-bc8b-4673-8b4e-76f62fc508ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 119:22
Text: Remove from me reproach and contempt; for I have kept thy testimonies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa962d07-00c2-4b3f-8e76-00d8b7ea1726>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 119:23
Text: Princes also did sit and speak against me: but thy servant did meditate in thy statutes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76cc72ca-e66c-4259-8482-bf7c6ea5f3b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PSA 119:24
Text: Thy testimonies also are my delight and my counsellors.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f0c940a-554c-4fe0-a62d-512a9435f1f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 119:25
Text: My soul cleaveth unto the dust: quicken thou me according to thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b6e0d07-f33b-4978-a516-4a41200ba059>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 119:26
Text: I have declared my ways, and thou heardest me: teach me thy statutes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:749d38ac-396c-4949-9897-1f586d74f519>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 119:27
Text: Make me to understand the way of thy precepts: so shall I talk of thy wondrous works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2bae530-4a74-4c16-9181-c7253583cbe8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 119:28
Text: My soul melteth for heaviness: strengthen thou me according unto thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22987205-3176-4660-a159-95c8f3785d68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 119:29
Text: Remove from me the way of lying: and grant me thy law graciously.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a801b26-bacf-4a44-9d15-4e0cca21c8ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 119:30
Text: I have chosen the way of truth: thy judgments have I laid before me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5cd54e3-5c59-49e4-87a0-2154d0e69a0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PSA 119:31
Text: I have stuck unto thy testimonies: O LORD, put me not to shame.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cdfe66a9-0dd5-4116-a557-36bcc7aae5f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 119:32
Text: I will run the way of thy commandments, when thou shalt enlarge my heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8b43eee-7f87-4463-b096-ba6687072022>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 119:33
Text: Teach me, O LORD, the way of thy statutes; and I shall keep it unto the end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25acf643-c2ba-47c8-9303-fc54d52b04e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 119:34
Text: Give me understanding, and I shall keep thy law; yea, I shall observe it with my whole heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ba4dec5-8b06-4a6d-b084-4ae2ce1eed06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 119:35
Text: Make me to go in the path of thy commandments; for therein do I delight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a6e7d18-69b0-4207-b697-4c631c642934>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PSA 119:36
Text: Incline my heart unto thy testimonies, and not to covetousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1318ba9-86d1-4121-a7f6-98c8825c06c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 119:37
Text: Turn away mine eyes from beholding vanity; and quicken thou me in thy way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ccfdcd5c-d026-450f-8783-2170a2fee9dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PSA 119:38
Text: Stablish thy word unto thy servant, who is devoted to thy fear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:357f969c-96b6-4d33-8892-8c1b1ecce3cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PSA 119:39
Text: Turn away my reproach which I fear: for thy judgments are good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1e96abd-b170-4818-8851-a8b175fbfc63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 119:40
Text: Behold, I have longed after thy precepts: quicken me in thy righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a9b8d1c-38cd-4e02-bc92-1d87098ef4a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 119:41
Text: Let thy mercies come also unto me, O LORD, even thy salvation, according to thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37e3e5c6-69ef-4bde-9732-5010035be202>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 119:42
Text: So shall I have wherewith to answer him that reproacheth me: for I trust in thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce16a3d8-06af-429d-a18d-a8794ebc2c17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 119:43
Text: And take not the word of truth utterly out of my mouth; for I have hoped in thy judgments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58070dcb-a3b5-420a-8067-5ee25415a850>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: PSA 119:44
Text: So shall I keep thy law continually for ever and ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4041eff1-43a2-4b0c-a2c9-0b5e4d71b511>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: PSA 119:45
Text: And I will walk at liberty: for I seek thy precepts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c45d125b-76d6-4474-991e-8550e3de0b62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 119:46
Text: I will speak of thy testimonies also before kings, and will not be ashamed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edbfede6-1563-4403-a29b-fae70e64e1d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 119:47
Text: And I will delight myself in thy commandments, which I have loved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:910387b4-6744-4280-af91-b8ac1f122a0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: PSA 119:48
Text: My hands also will I lift up unto thy commandments, which I have loved; and I will meditate in thy statutes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71c0a155-5845-4379-abe8-54f982f7959f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 119:49
Text: Remember the word unto thy servant, upon which thou hast caused me to hope.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f307dc3b-915b-45e8-be14-048dee763e37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 119:50
Text: This is my comfort in my affliction: for thy word hath quickened me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:785e3025-c89a-4ed7-a2f4-5aa7bfaaf432>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 119:51
Text: The proud have had me greatly in derision: yet have I not declined from thy law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3624c074-1d89-46fa-a55f-42e646a8f69d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 119:52
Text: I remembered thy judgments of old, O LORD; and have comforted myself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1f89184-694f-43a1-a589-2111ba1f61cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 119:53
Text: Horror hath taken hold upon me because of the wicked that forsake thy law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49f7bdbf-57d2-4cef-aeeb-372b1d2e9b6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 119:54
Text: Thy statutes have been my songs in the house of my pilgrimage.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/55
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7052848c-6413-4f23-acbc-2a39d5989acf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 119:55
Text: I have remembered thy name, O LORD, in the night, and have kept thy law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/56
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92170595-5cba-4ed8-9081-032ee7a7249c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 69

Reference: PSA 119:56
Text: This I had, because I kept thy precepts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/57
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64c877db-7637-472e-92db-8eb83a1589d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 119:57
Text: Thou art my portion, O LORD: I have said that I would keep thy words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/58
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d6138a6-0b50-416c-a0fa-e6d6d11414a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 119:58
Text: I intreated thy favour with my whole heart: be merciful unto me according to thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/59
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:343bd4c5-8814-4053-a2a1-072f0ea6a3aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 119:59
Text: I thought on my ways, and turned my feet unto thy testimonies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/60
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28331bdd-b971-4f75-aeb4-9a596ee33292>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PSA 119:60
Text: I made haste, and delayed not to keep thy commandments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/61
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4eb3d544-f9f4-4f11-9957-37ab24acfefe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 119:61
Text: The bands of the wicked have robbed me: but I have not forgotten thy law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/62
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e58eabb-295d-4899-af70-75768f0ef4dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 119:62
Text: At midnight I will rise to give thanks unto thee because of thy righteous judgments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/63
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0831cd2b-0bf6-486a-9f6a-cf0d8559466c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 119:63
Text: I am a companion of all them that fear thee, and of them that keep thy precepts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/64
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02d64e77-a107-43c3-b48d-e3970231b5ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PSA 119:64
Text: The earth, O LORD, is full of thy mercy: teach me thy statutes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/65
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e418d80b-a94d-426a-8ae2-fc8fadf778b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 119:65
Text: Thou hast dealt well with thy servant, O LORD, according unto thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/66
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47b71fe8-053c-4dd4-9ca3-2d821d3a6021>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 119:66
Text: Teach me good judgment and knowledge: for I have believed thy commandments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/67
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b57dcf65-e8af-40c3-8c26-1e90a217f1b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 119:67
Text: Before I was afflicted I went astray: but now have I kept thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/68
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de817947-1db6-4905-a82c-7c76d64cc09f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: PSA 119:68
Text: Thou art good, and doest good; teach me thy statutes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/69
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc01b688-0a99-4666-a98b-780a4d45f4ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 119:69
Text: The proud have forged a lie against me: but I will keep thy precepts with my whole heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/70
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77251439-9df9-4667-8798-e10ee2e52846>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PSA 119:70
Text: Their heart is as fat as grease; but I delight in thy law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/71
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:110ca707-5eb4-42c1-8f2f-db9fbffcd9d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 119:71
Text: It is good for me that I have been afflicted; that I might learn thy statutes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/72
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:224a314e-dad0-416e-861d-b96cc92be646>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 119:72
Text: The law of thy mouth is better unto me than thousands of gold and silver.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/73
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf604112-6796-4c8d-a0ed-6d7da72c8f39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PSA 119:73
Text: Thy hands have made me and fashioned me: give me understanding, that I may learn thy commandments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/74
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:effffe99-eddf-499d-97b4-7f6f7eca4246>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 119:74
Text: They that fear thee will be glad when they see me; because I have hoped in thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/75
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a16268e6-f2db-49a1-a276-9d9e2df290ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 119:75
Text: I know, O LORD, that thy judgments are right, and that thou in faithfulness hast afflicted me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/76
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ba11e16-ab0b-44b9-a0bb-1bc70acf9aab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PSA 119:76
Text: Let, I pray thee, thy merciful kindness be for my comfort, according to thy word unto thy servant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/77
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78e028d7-20c2-404e-9dd0-0269018ffdd3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 119:77
Text: Let thy tender mercies come unto me, that I may live: for thy law is my delight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/78
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cd838ee-ad04-4966-8156-a1b68f951cd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: PSA 119:78
Text: Let the proud be ashamed; for they dealt perversely with me without a cause: but I will meditate in thy precepts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/79
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2cad4c9-e2a8-4809-9a72-f8065c99b996>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 119:79
Text: Let those that fear thee turn unto me, and those that have known thy testimonies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/80
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c2718eb-a747-4102-88da-084d26b9e9ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 119:80
Text: Let my heart be sound in thy statutes; that I be not ashamed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/81
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:210fcaa6-c2e4-4f3e-8cca-df9c1dfeaddf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 119:81
Text: My soul fainteth for thy salvation: but I hope in thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/82
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c29c27c2-f475-448e-ae91-066ea2daf429>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PSA 119:82
Text: Mine eyes fail for thy word, saying, When wilt thou comfort me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/83
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f67f8b77-d262-427e-a726-7c52b170824a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 119:83
Text: For I am become like a bottle in the smoke; yet do I not forget thy statutes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/84
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82c0cfae-fd06-4870-acb8-f8969e6f2c46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 119:84
Text: How many are the days of thy servant? when wilt thou execute judgment on them that persecute me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/85
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0633c859-dcf4-4f79-89cb-863d0e6f285d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PSA 119:85
Text: The proud have digged pits for me, which are not after thy law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/86
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c244e6cf-c7ab-4335-8ab0-505a1a630edd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 119:86
Text: All thy commandments are faithful: they persecute me wrongfully; help thou me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/87
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d743244-9978-41bd-9bb8-b3805bfca794>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 119:87
Text: They had almost consumed me upon earth; but I forsook not thy precepts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/88
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00560948-16d4-46b5-9814-7e08ceb5ca00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 119:88
Text: Quicken me after thy lovingkindness; so shall I keep the testimony of thy mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/89
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c243051-8a4a-4358-8c0c-2e63053529ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: PSA 119:89
Text: For ever, O LORD, thy word is settled in heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/90
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ba88fba-dd9f-4bea-9206-2bbc5a6420cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 119:90
Text: Thy faithfulness is unto all generations: thou hast established the earth, and it abideth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/91
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:826b9ca6-3362-46e8-b17a-94c0b05f97b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 119:91
Text: They continue this day according to thine ordinances: for all are thy servants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/92
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e163955-2c22-49de-b721-e9d2fb67efab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 119:92
Text: Unless thy law had been my delights, I should then have perished in mine affliction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/93
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd6150cb-ceb1-49a4-827d-3e37e50e191c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 119:93
Text: I will never forget thy precepts: for with them thou hast quickened me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/94
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5bdeef0-66e9-4233-87b3-46d0b871ef46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: PSA 119:94
Text: I am thine, save me: for I have sought thy precepts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/95
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20f7fa25-25ce-4793-8b76-d6e3b5524dd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 119:95
Text: The wicked have waited for me to destroy me: but I will consider thy testimonies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/96
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f00113de-968d-460f-b503-83c83ebd883e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 119:96
Text: I have seen an end of all perfection: but thy commandment is exceeding broad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/97
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f2e00cd-bcc5-4717-bad6-57fca828674b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: PSA 119:97
Text: O how I love thy law! it is my meditation all the day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/98
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bd9ea6a-8ec5-4587-9705-fe057379189a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 119:98
Text: Thou through thy commandments hast made me wiser than mine enemies: for they are ever with me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/99
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfb6a136-d332-48ce-98e4-bfdf077ceb78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 119:99
Text: I have more understanding than all my teachers: for thy testimonies are my meditation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/100
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bcd32f56-5b35-45a3-93d8-9071bf47adca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 119:100
Text: I understand more than the ancients, because I keep thy precepts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/101
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84607220-9ecd-4818-8ac0-057b52376ffe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 119:101
Text: I have refrained my feet from every evil way, that I might keep thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/102
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:751781fa-be65-46ed-b92e-70f2b751eec1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 119:102
Text: I have not departed from thy judgments: for thou hast taught me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/103
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5d21003-23f4-467d-b341-f845a8624995>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 119:103
Text: How sweet are thy words unto my taste! yea, sweeter than honey to my mouth!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/104
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7aceea68-2d3b-4c06-9aad-efcc71afcde2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 119:104
Text: Through thy precepts I get understanding: therefore I hate every false way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/105
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a97606c3-98d1-47f7-83b5-2f032d503a0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 119:105
Text: Thy word is a lamp unto my feet, and a light unto my path.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/106
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:858d363e-59c3-4f46-a8ed-92581ac80c0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 119:106
Text: I have sworn, and I will perform it, that I will keep thy righteous judgments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/107
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93855795-ae93-49c0-a9f6-8e94ce1db449>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 119:107
Text: I am afflicted very much: quicken me, O LORD, according unto thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/108
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06fc3506-e3da-4ccb-b88c-e688436101fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PSA 119:108
Text: Accept, I beseech thee, the freewill offerings of my mouth, O LORD, and teach me thy judgments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/109
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd294192-9abb-4019-9cec-b0da4dd0b4ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 119:109
Text: My soul is continually in my hand: yet do I not forget thy law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/110
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cebd6e01-7a2f-4f42-ac94-09061798cc8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 119:110
Text: The wicked have laid a snare for me: yet I erred not from thy precepts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/111
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d98ce502-aac4-4545-8560-69a71eb99a75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 119:111
Text: Thy testimonies have I taken as an heritage for ever: for they are the rejoicing of my heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/112
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10b37701-f99d-4b40-b57f-46605bf91c2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 119:112
Text: I have inclined mine heart to perform thy statutes alway, even unto the end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/113
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ce911ee-3c5b-4a30-b888-dcf13670e3de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: PSA 119:113
Text: I hate vain thoughts: but thy law do I love.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/114
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4a7a1b3-3349-48be-bd93-6f4dcaa7bf5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 119:114
Text: Thou art my hiding place and my shield: I hope in thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/115
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a3f331b-3052-42c7-857f-18910182c26d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 119:115
Text: Depart from me, ye evildoers: for I will keep the commandments of my God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/116
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05677ccd-65e0-4750-9070-5d72cbe15535>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 119:116
Text: Uphold me according unto thy word, that I may live: and let me not be ashamed of my hope.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/117
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12839ec8-2690-4638-bd9c-32374dcf364f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 119:117
Text: Hold thou me up, and I shall be safe: and I will have respect unto thy statutes continually.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/118
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df1c8ec5-848b-44d7-a004-a746cdb34a0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 119:118
Text: Thou hast trodden down all them that err from thy statutes: for their deceit is falsehood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/119
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:423e1081-bb58-4f6d-9623-ee58e1e93e87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 119:119
Text: Thou puttest away all the wicked of the earth like dross: therefore I love thy testimonies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/120
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eac29332-1d43-4207-a729-9340d20b3ea6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 119:120
Text: My flesh trembleth for fear of thee; and I am afraid of thy judgments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/121
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12a58916-0236-417e-9a28-af1a64124069>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 119:121
Text: I have done judgment and justice: leave me not to mine oppressors.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/122
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7df923a-c213-4b74-a501-c4cd296030d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 119:122
Text: Be surety for thy servant for good: let not the proud oppress me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/123
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd2c9b92-f9c8-4a8c-9197-1bb9d1bcc475>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 119:123
Text: Mine eyes fail for thy salvation, and for the word of thy righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/124
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc5f24a0-4d6d-447b-a127-c291f41190d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 119:124
Text: Deal with thy servant according unto thy mercy, and teach me thy statutes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/125
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cef719a-f1a1-4cfb-a44a-83b4b759c1d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 119:125
Text: I am thy servant; give me understanding, that I may know thy testimonies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/126
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ce69e0c-ce32-4b61-bb0a-b167da9acc18>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 119:126
Text: It is time for thee, LORD, to work: for they have made void thy law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/127
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb0160f7-33a5-4298-8241-9df2e5b49a42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 119:127
Text: Therefore I love thy commandments above gold; yea, above fine gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/128
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be478c1e-a207-4b98-bf9c-9ee3a8f3fa2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 119:128
Text: Therefore I esteem all thy precepts concerning all things to be right; and I hate every false way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/129
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5ba489b-a4b5-49be-97a5-4fb6a04e2414>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 119:129
Text: Thy testimonies are wonderful: therefore doth my soul keep them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/130
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b03c62a-0858-4e81-8977-9d98cba17f04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 119:130
Text: The entrance of thy words giveth light; it giveth understanding unto the simple.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/131
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b7a8906-882b-4f70-bb9e-3ca75a65f969>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 119:131
Text: I opened my mouth, and panted: for I longed for thy commandments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/132
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfc19d25-f617-4c19-b80b-b382bc5060ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 119:132
Text: Look thou upon me, and be merciful unto me, as thou usest to do unto those that love thy name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/133
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c075a90-5082-4709-8a47-36699bc55a24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 119:133
Text: Order my steps in thy word: and let not any iniquity have dominion over me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/134
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1590c3c2-915d-47f1-bd61-46b693e11af1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 119:134
Text: Deliver me from the oppression of man: so will I keep thy precepts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/135
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb784191-82d8-4dc9-890f-3ab2f8808afa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 119:135
Text: Make thy face to shine upon thy servant; and teach me thy statutes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/136
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a6c7dec-6935-4629-b70f-79ca6355f1a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 119:136
Text: Rivers of waters run down mine eyes, because they keep not thy law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/137
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d81049c-de3b-4253-a4b6-9c0252c0b56f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 119:137
Text: Righteous art thou, O LORD, and upright are thy judgments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/138
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13843e13-546d-4ccf-a919-a47ce65f155c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 119:138
Text: Thy testimonies that thou hast commanded are righteous and very faithful.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/139
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:249342ba-6683-450c-8d59-6fa93377dc5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 119:139
Text: My zeal hath consumed me, because mine enemies have forgotten thy words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/140
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:924cab33-bcef-49c0-bea0-7d9a0efa6b99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: PSA 119:140
Text: Thy word is very pure: therefore thy servant loveth it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/141
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bbd2becb-32b3-47e5-b2b7-3e2012060b96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 119:141
Text: I am small and despised: yet do not I forget thy precepts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/142
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2f2927e-922c-4182-a22d-b50eed1c6c3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 119:142
Text: Thy righteousness is an everlasting righteousness, and thy law is the truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/143
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49742cc8-4d7b-438e-8b65-db73c8cddab7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 119:143
Text: Trouble and anguish have taken hold on me: yet thy commandments are my delights.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/144
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:526394e2-cf6a-4dff-bff0-a8891a1eeaa6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 119:144
Text: The righteousness of thy testimonies is everlasting: give me understanding, and I shall live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/145
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51aea769-b29c-4bb8-b89a-3f39912cdf04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 119:145
Text: I cried with my whole heart; hear me, O LORD: I will keep thy statutes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/146
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:827684bb-b992-4267-9ef6-d1206cedc3d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 119:146
Text: I cried unto thee; save me, and I shall keep thy testimonies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/147
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7cfa3904-1f3f-403a-80e8-4ee2bc33cbea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 119:147
Text: I prevented the dawning of the morning, and cried: I hoped in thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/148
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9f4c748-a441-4968-a596-17f4187e8113>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 119:148
Text: Mine eyes prevent the night watches, that I might meditate in thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/149
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:adef0d76-e00e-43b3-8456-dcda97112df7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 119:149
Text: Hear my voice according unto thy lovingkindness: O LORD, quicken me according to thy judgment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/150
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e188eba8-4634-4de8-a93b-677f7bdefc81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 119:150
Text: They draw nigh that follow after mischief: they are far from thy law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/151
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dce5ce8e-fc22-4242-9d0c-8345df94e18c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 119:151
Text: Thou art near, O LORD; and all thy commandments are truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/152
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8b10a8e-168e-457f-b04e-671fa48a7aee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 119:152
Text: Concerning thy testimonies, I have known of old that thou hast founded them for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/153
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2dd4bb5a-db91-46f8-8af8-69e97fecf384>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 119:153
Text: Consider mine affliction, and deliver me: for I do not forget thy law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/154
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d9cce5c-9116-4b08-bbbd-002bf74cf280>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 119:154
Text: Plead my cause, and deliver me: quicken me according to thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/155
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4145e66f-4ef2-4e0d-9ab7-f65e4d7b8f4f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 119:155
Text: Salvation is far from the wicked: for they seek not thy statutes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/156
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6451b4e3-7f81-4896-866b-a76a46bdc020>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 119:156
Text: Great are thy tender mercies, O LORD: quicken me according to thy judgments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/157
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f2f6825-9303-4f68-be1e-2b9b3c2ae76b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 119:157
Text: Many are my persecutors and mine enemies; yet do I not decline from thy testimonies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/158
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:699544bf-c9a3-46a8-9c88-9e34579d6603>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 119:158
Text: I beheld the transgressors, and was grieved; because they kept not thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/159
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92f0c477-58fe-4a35-a6d7-4c67be071e21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 119:159
Text: Consider how I love thy precepts: quicken me, O LORD, according to thy lovingkindness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/160
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:412a0cce-2571-43de-ba2d-7ddcaebbbdce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 119:160
Text: Thy word is true from the beginning: and every one of thy righteous judgments endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/161
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99b4bcf2-8eac-4655-a27e-a0562b8d7683>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 119:161
Text: Princes have persecuted me without a cause: but my heart standeth in awe of thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/162
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:471e3727-6677-49c6-a03d-6ffc8236932a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: PSA 119:162
Text: I rejoice at thy word, as one that findeth great spoil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/163
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a105904-f713-4544-8098-ac4871099ee6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: PSA 119:163
Text: I hate and abhor lying: but thy law do I love.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/164
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:295dd15d-c611-4f26-a940-ced7a08c44f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 119:164
Text: Seven times a day do I praise thee because of thy righteous judgments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/165
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39db3fea-1331-4073-b9a7-b6f0ab6e06a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 119:165
Text: Great peace have they which love thy law: and nothing shall offend them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/166
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e30126cc-4da3-425c-9722-6a3d7df53dae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 119:166
Text: LORD, I have hoped for thy salvation, and done thy commandments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/167
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c70e00e-5ec9-44ac-8145-54b99bc00384>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 119:167
Text: My soul hath kept thy testimonies; and I love them exceedingly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/168
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74b3083c-4486-4b01-9dbf-bbad3126893f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 119:168
Text: I have kept thy precepts and thy testimonies: for all my ways are before thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/169
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c22792f-3163-4192-9b6c-6a272ad6289a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 119:169
Text: Let my cry come near before thee, O LORD: give me understanding according to thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/170
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10376ee5-7326-45e5-b697-f39ed94e4428>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 119:170
Text: Let my supplication come before thee: deliver me according to thy word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/171
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b3731ec-d935-45fd-9782-ccf37ce9f047>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 119:171
Text: My lips shall utter praise, when thou hast taught me thy statutes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/172
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c7efe89-640e-4a26-89e6-a0774f0faf1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 119:172
Text: My tongue shall speak of thy word: for all thy commandments are righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/173
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc160ce7-3c71-4e57-baa4-ed5b262e4c07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: PSA 119:173
Text: Let thine hand help me; for I have chosen thy precepts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/174
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a422525d-f8f8-4273-97df-8422537a50c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 119:174
Text: I have longed for thy salvation, O LORD; and thy law is my delight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/175
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f75beba4-d1c0-43f6-a20a-edfbdef77695>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 119:175
Text: Let my soul live, and it shall praise thee; and let thy judgments help me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/119/176
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36fe3704-a2b3-45b3-b9e6-092c269e99d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 119:176
Text: I have gone astray like a lost sheep; seek thy servant; for I do not forget thy commandments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/120/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad2cb1ad-0c0d-470b-a50e-7ff7f54dcec3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: PSA 120:1
Text: In my distress I cried unto the LORD, and he heard me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/120/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12045ce0-071e-4339-a43e-cb31efe1286b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 120:2
Text: Deliver my soul, O LORD, from lying lips, and from a deceitful tongue.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/120/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40a7438a-b074-4090-926e-1f3bd7b4a1bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 120:3
Text: What shall be given unto thee? or what shall be done unto thee, thou false tongue?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/120/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c43bbd2-bd01-4a2e-97f5-0619acd45790>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: PSA 120:4
Text: Sharp arrows of the mighty, with coals of juniper.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/120/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5b15293-f25a-4817-a044-f31adb272ea3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 120:5
Text: Woe is me, that I sojourn in Mesech, that I dwell in the tents of Kedar!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/120/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bc55b8f-31b6-4852-8c70-c92761ea57be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: PSA 120:6
Text: My soul hath long dwelt with him that hateth peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/120/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d4fa15a-00e3-4a14-b823-2757b71237b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: PSA 120:7
Text: I am for peace: but when I speak, they are for war.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/121/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b2c0b28-6a35-43d4-9bce-c26b02e507ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 121:1
Text: I will lift up mine eyes unto the hills, from whence cometh my help.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/121/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d279a42-8412-408c-a06b-e6d10a0259af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PSA 121:2
Text: My help cometh from the LORD, which made heaven and earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/121/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50f343e5-ff71-4f40-970f-3d8bbb0bf33c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 121:3
Text: He will not suffer thy foot to be moved: he that keepeth thee will not slumber.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/121/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3df8eba8-5e1a-44e6-ab57-3f9fea53d7d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 121:4
Text: Behold, he that keepeth Israel shall neither slumber nor sleep.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/121/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab74993c-8870-45a7-9396-3ee10e356c2d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 121:5
Text: The LORD is thy keeper: the LORD is thy shade upon thy right hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/121/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1315d3da-8b58-45bd-89e7-9f81c5bef09c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PSA 121:6
Text: The sun shall not smite thee by day, nor the moon by night.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/121/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:539916a9-77a0-4df7-a2c2-b20faaed76d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 121:7
Text: The LORD shall preserve thee from all evil: he shall preserve thy soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/121/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9415c569-18bf-49f5-a09c-6cae819f38d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 121:8
Text: The LORD shall preserve thy going out and thy coming in from this time forth, and even for evermore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/122/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3946280-562b-47a5-ac7d-18a3ad480a14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 122:1
Text: I was glad when they said unto me, Let us go into the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/122/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8219b786-bd02-4544-8925-3e9319d8530c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: PSA 122:2
Text: Our feet shall stand within thy gates, O Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/122/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1209121-386a-4399-a7d2-edc9c30f6eb2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PSA 122:3
Text: Jerusalem is builded as a city that is compact together:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/122/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2d2ca5e-39f0-4fdb-b65e-66ebef43d432>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: PSA 122:4
Text: Whither the tribes go up, the tribes of the LORD, unto the testimony of Israel, to give thanks unto the name of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/122/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:405e1902-7220-4899-9523-406cbec617eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 122:5
Text: For there are set thrones of judgment, the thrones of the house of David.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/122/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c808de4f-fc1c-492f-afc2-50e106598e02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 122:6
Text: Pray for the peace of Jerusalem: they shall prosper that love thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/122/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ad68908-c594-4b36-b726-6093e4a7c634>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 122:7
Text: Peace be within thy walls, and prosperity within thy palaces.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/122/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:961f63a5-14f5-4406-ade0-9329fd2aeb51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 122:8
Text: For my brethren and companions’ sakes, I will now say, Peace be within thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/122/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:691cecba-7331-49c4-bc98-4de6dea57a70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 122:9
Text: Because of the house of the LORD our God I will seek thy good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/123/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:711230a4-1a2f-49ce-abad-488b03decdd2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 123:1
Text: Unto thee lift I up mine eyes, O thou that dwellest in the heavens.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/123/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c69fe0bb-c98a-47b7-bbf5-e1ff435280e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: PSA 123:2
Text: Behold, as the eyes of servants look unto the hand of their masters, and as the eyes of a maiden unto the hand of her mistress; so our eyes wait upon the LORD our God, until that he have mercy upon us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/123/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de2260b9-8526-48fa-909e-cf7b23decd4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 123:3
Text: Have mercy upon us, O LORD, have mercy upon us: for we are exceedingly filled with contempt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/123/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d87e23f5-29c4-40c6-977c-0d3f8c3cd9b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: PSA 123:4
Text: Our soul is exceedingly filled with the scorning of those that are at ease, and with the contempt of the proud.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/124/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:390e0365-74e9-453a-84ed-733671681a5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 124:1
Text: If it had not been the LORD who was on our side, now may Israel say;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/124/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65ddb622-8850-4bea-b9f1-018c7ae02fa9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 124:2
Text: If it had not been the LORD who was on our side, when men rose up against us:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/124/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6ccfa0e-962a-4413-8b01-f25aef0a78ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 124:3
Text: Then they had swallowed us up quick, when their wrath was kindled against us:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/124/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47dc60c0-4c7d-4485-8d58-bbac8ca4dd49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 124:4
Text: Then the waters had overwhelmed us, the stream had gone over our soul:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/124/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ea26770-62bd-4e2b-b6c8-402793225942>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: PSA 124:5
Text: Then the proud waters had gone over our soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/124/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09b21bc7-2e4c-4b51-b079-2ccd07043dcb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 124:6
Text: Blessed be the LORD, who hath not given us as a prey to their teeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/124/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:672c1324-b36d-4876-aa31-69fee6bd5557>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 124:7
Text: Our soul is escaped as a bird out of the snare of the fowlers: the snare is broken, and we are escaped.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/124/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91581b3e-be23-4b9a-993b-9ab3dbfdbb21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 124:8
Text: Our help is in the name of the LORD, who made heaven and earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/125/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b4bbcdf-ad7b-477f-87b4-349be3b23f69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 125:1
Text: They that trust in the LORD shall be as mount Zion, which cannot be removed, but abideth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/125/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c047b58-6294-430b-b9cc-2426c8c25ee1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: PSA 125:2
Text: As the mountains are round about Jerusalem, so the LORD is round about his people from henceforth even for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/125/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:427dde31-d48a-4357-a2b5-89fd62e47091>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: PSA 125:3
Text: For the rod of the wicked shall not rest upon the lot of the righteous; lest the righteous put forth their hands unto iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/125/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ed37cc8-a501-402f-9d49-5bb69b90036f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 125:4
Text: Do good, O LORD, unto those that be good, and to them that are upright in their hearts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/125/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78826ba9-028a-4fd7-8776-300d6fb8b28e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: PSA 125:5
Text: As for such as turn aside unto their crooked ways, the LORD shall lead them forth with the workers of iniquity: but peace shall be upon Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/126/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5516d27-281a-42c4-82b1-c6f4f28540eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 126:1
Text: When the LORD turned again the captivity of Zion, we were like them that dream.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/126/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2d02313-63fa-4179-88b7-1a2684909e8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: PSA 126:2
Text: Then was our mouth filled with laughter, and our tongue with singing: then said they among the heathen, The LORD hath done great things for them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/126/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:416d9a59-ded2-4fda-a489-7da6f388ab77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 126:3
Text: The LORD hath done great things for us; whereof we are glad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/126/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea214269-159b-4327-bcc0-6b2093f14fef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 126:4
Text: Turn again our captivity, O LORD, as the streams in the south.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/126/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11ee521f-7442-43ee-8f9f-63d86c7cf488>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 69

Reference: PSA 126:5
Text: They that sow in tears shall reap in joy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/126/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00be621d-699c-4cb2-b05e-a902d48f99a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: PSA 126:6
Text: He that goeth forth and weepeth, bearing precious seed, shall doubtless come again with rejoicing, bringing his sheaves with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/127/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8157577-df64-4689-8d1b-eec1a7385872>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: PSA 127:1
Text: Except the LORD build the house, they labour in vain that build it: except the LORD keep the city, the watchman waketh but in vain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/127/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08b94fab-1d1f-40c6-9c26-e48c188a0448>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: PSA 127:2
Text: It is vain for you to rise up early, to sit up late, to eat the bread of sorrows: for so he giveth his beloved sleep.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/127/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89f12d03-74d5-4465-9fae-914e91113112>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 127:3
Text: Lo, children are an heritage of the LORD: and the fruit of the womb is his reward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/127/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f36f5c69-7797-4f6b-a251-f4e6afa13a03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 127:4
Text: As arrows are in the hand of a mighty man; so are children of the youth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/127/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ac838e4-2129-406a-8bb8-e5cfc9e8c03b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: PSA 127:5
Text: Happy is the man that hath his quiver full of them: they shall not be ashamed, but they shall speak with the enemies in the gate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/128/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e76e7a4-8bfd-469f-bd21-77b81aaf1087>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 128:1
Text: Blessed is every one that feareth the LORD; that walketh in his ways.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/128/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e79d564-3fa1-492a-9ca5-138608561a56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 128:2
Text: For thou shalt eat the labour of thine hands: happy shalt thou be, and it shall be well with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/128/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72cd680b-5a7e-401c-8c88-c9cea01868e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: PSA 128:3
Text: Thy wife shall be as a fruitful vine by the sides of thine house: thy children like olive plants round about thy table.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/128/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3fbd3903-dd85-4980-8bd7-144192bb2319>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 128:4
Text: Behold, that thus shall the man be blessed that feareth the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/128/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c1979c2-7bbb-47b1-a570-d1ee87263a35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: PSA 128:5
Text: The LORD shall bless thee out of Zion: and thou shalt see the good of Jerusalem all the days of thy life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/128/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6baede72-f906-4d11-b2d5-b60a374db61a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 128:6
Text: Yea, thou shalt see thy children’s children, and peace upon Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/129/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ed907d8-c3e5-4e23-8737-c296c3931dc2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 129:1
Text: Many a time have they afflicted me from my youth, may Israel now say:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/129/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf1ce557-e747-4b7f-95eb-97f007be6564>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 129:2
Text: Many a time have they afflicted me from my youth: yet they have not prevailed against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/129/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11defba4-c6da-4c48-88f9-b35ff856f9ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PSA 129:3
Text: The plowers plowed upon my back: they made long their furrows.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/129/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ac9ed08-ff2d-4130-8efd-b0c12f9bcf39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 129:4
Text: The LORD is righteous: he hath cut asunder the cords of the wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/129/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e82a068-3d85-4182-856f-39241461319f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PSA 129:5
Text: Let them all be confounded and turned back that hate Zion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/129/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:001125b1-3568-4808-96c7-643751e1b0de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 129:6
Text: Let them be as the grass upon the housetops, which withereth afore it groweth up:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/129/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83e6e32f-48a0-4e00-94c1-9524f0c13281>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 129:7
Text: Wherewith the mower filleth not his hand; nor he that bindeth sheaves his bosom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/129/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46bffce7-2b20-4d53-98d8-0964e4339654>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PSA 129:8
Text: Neither do they which go by say, The blessing of the LORD be upon you: we bless you in the name of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/130/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a56dc543-79ca-4265-a493-fe1b65a2b71f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: PSA 130:1
Text: Out of the depths have I cried unto thee, O LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/130/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4490a607-9b9d-42f1-962d-106a7d14428c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 130:2
Text: Lord, hear my voice: let thine ears be attentive to the voice of my supplications.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/130/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:073fd6a5-d1e4-493e-8368-87ca214c5120>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 130:3
Text: If thou, LORD, shouldest mark iniquities, O Lord, who shall stand?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/130/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:246f1ad1-9595-43bb-9d4f-5109e20a09cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 130:4
Text: But there is forgiveness with thee, that thou mayest be feared.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/130/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8cf3a701-df29-4184-8934-d8427f74baeb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 130:5
Text: I wait for the LORD, my soul doth wait, and in his word do I hope.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/130/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f240f00d-c2e0-449a-9bbb-f635dbe2b6b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: PSA 130:6
Text: My soul waiteth for the Lord more than they that watch for the morning: I say, more than they that watch for the morning.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/130/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55c40e24-0d94-4dea-8dd4-4755b1a9b197>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 130:7
Text: Let Israel hope in the LORD: for with the LORD there is mercy, and with him is plenteous redemption.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/130/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99bf1f6d-2541-4b80-ad78-1c3edceb4633>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: PSA 130:8
Text: And he shall redeem Israel from all his iniquities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/131/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b52566b7-6154-4207-a73b-8adb7b0a3a6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: PSA 131:1
Text: Lord, my heart is not haughty, nor mine eyes lofty: neither do I exercise myself in great matters, or in things too high for me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/131/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d200e8f1-b163-409c-b64f-be0424aa0658>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: PSA 131:2
Text: Surely I have behaved and quieted myself, as a child that is weaned of his mother: my soul is even as a weaned child.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/131/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a060dfc-b8f6-49ac-9c1d-ae7f01dd2ae3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: PSA 131:3
Text: Let Israel hope in the LORD from henceforth and for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/132/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5ea6906-1bf0-443c-ae0b-ec43bf28313c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: PSA 132:1
Text: Lord, remember David, and all his afflictions:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/132/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:684bdd67-3052-4a09-b39c-cfe259db0768>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 132:2
Text: How he sware unto the LORD, and vowed unto the mighty God of Jacob;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/132/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50219be4-867d-480e-b761-257d100fb816>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 132:3
Text: Surely I will not come into the tabernacle of my house, nor go up into my bed;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/132/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67abbd2f-ddd9-43b2-86d7-479fa78d6c28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 132:4
Text: I will not give sleep to mine eyes, or slumber to mine eyelids,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/132/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c1f0a92-8ddf-4ec4-aada-343d11912115>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 132:5
Text: Until I find out a place for the LORD, an habitation for the mighty God of Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/132/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75449cd0-5798-4727-a4aa-9a91d18d1bb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 132:6
Text: Lo, we heard of it at Ephratah: we found it in the fields of the wood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/132/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d60e48be-6ca5-4ff6-84f6-bfb40deba8c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 132:7
Text: We will go into his tabernacles: we will worship at his footstool.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/132/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36fba814-a739-445b-8035-1dd33c4b0c11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PSA 132:8
Text: Arise, O LORD, into thy rest; thou, and the ark of thy strength.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/132/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5cb1279c-fe4c-4873-b0d9-ef05e93c0781>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 132:9
Text: Let thy priests be clothed with righteousness; and let thy saints shout for joy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/132/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b11b8b38-6874-4f24-be81-a20da47b8d1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 132:10
Text: For thy servant David’s sake turn not away the face of thine anointed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/132/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:881bd9e4-c212-4226-821b-3a2400c13c3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: PSA 132:11
Text: The LORD hath sworn in truth unto David; he will not turn from it; Of the fruit of thy body will I set upon thy throne.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/132/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c0df955-444b-4c1c-8ecd-6d1cdb2ab8c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: PSA 132:12
Text: If thy children will keep my covenant and my testimony that I shall teach them, their children shall also sit upon thy throne for evermore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/132/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:798f7dd7-5561-413c-b306-a978cdf3ffb5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 132:13
Text: For the LORD hath chosen Zion; he hath desired it for his habitation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/132/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79990a48-c7e4-46b1-b4af-9bb9abc9c28b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 132:14
Text: This is my rest for ever: here will I dwell; for I have desired it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/132/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a45d09d4-96a8-4e51-a4e3-1e9f684a2a61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 132:15
Text: I will abundantly bless her provision: I will satisfy her poor with bread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/132/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6e37d79-0c99-407f-ac2b-8629b90ac4fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 132:16
Text: I will also clothe her priests with salvation: and her saints shall shout aloud for joy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/132/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:839f1652-1ae9-4804-819f-4bf98fbb53b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 132:17
Text: There will I make the horn of David to bud: I have ordained a lamp for mine anointed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/132/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c69065c-253d-4228-979b-f603fa9481c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 132:18
Text: His enemies will I clothe with shame: but upon himself shall his crown flourish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/133/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd91198c-46cc-4058-8c5e-87e91e259e58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 133:1
Text: Behold, how good and how pleasant it is for brethren to dwell together in unity!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/133/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46bb724e-f396-44eb-9b72-81b6edf129e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: PSA 133:2
Text: It is like the precious ointment upon the head, that ran down upon the beard, even Aaron’s beard: that went down to the skirts of his garments;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/133/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b706bc8-1d7e-49e8-bc36-70d669b9b963>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: PSA 133:3
Text: As the dew of Hermon, and as the dew that descended upon the mountains of Zion: for there the LORD commanded the blessing, even life for evermore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/134/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e8e6044-9d83-46e8-bef6-585a1ee76695>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 134:1
Text: Behold, bless ye the LORD, all ye servants of the LORD, which by night stand in the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/134/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c0d5874-971e-4dc9-b340-1704276d0d59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PSA 134:2
Text: Lift up your hands in the sanctuary, and bless the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/134/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10a3ca95-c44c-44cf-a656-64e7bfedbf08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PSA 134:3
Text: The LORD that made heaven and earth bless thee out of Zion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/135/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f26dfd8d-f58e-4021-a922-51a7432475a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 135:1
Text: Praise ye the LORD. Praise ye the name of the LORD; praise him, O ye servants of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/135/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb330dc7-c187-4fd4-b539-7390f03fbc89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 135:2
Text: Ye that stand in the house of the LORD, in the courts of the house of our God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/135/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6be5970c-80b5-444b-9c37-fcf614bb9c4f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 135:3
Text: Praise the LORD; for the LORD is good: sing praises unto his name; for it is pleasant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/135/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffb21f3f-3b60-4303-aa7f-c61ec51e1771>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 135:4
Text: For the LORD hath chosen Jacob unto himself, and Israel for his peculiar treasure.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/135/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b7c3341-c742-4ab2-b84d-a3b7cbfe0c80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 135:5
Text: For I know that the LORD is great, and that our Lord is above all gods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/135/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51ff499f-9fac-4e2e-b6c3-678d187adbe0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PSA 135:6
Text: Whatsoever the LORD pleased, that did he in heaven, and in earth, in the seas, and all deep places.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/135/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fe89cba-9d39-4378-8425-3ae3b70197a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: PSA 135:7
Text: He causeth the vapours to ascend from the ends of the earth; he maketh lightnings for the rain; he bringeth the wind out of his treasuries.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/135/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a06c97a-1676-40a8-a3bb-68274078273e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PSA 135:8
Text: Who smote the firstborn of Egypt, both of man and beast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/135/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1291dd5-4699-43b2-8b2d-e9ca49465c58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PSA 135:9
Text: Who sent tokens and wonders into the midst of thee, O Egypt, upon Pharaoh, and upon all his servants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/135/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d9d5338-01f6-4c81-b61f-5a6eebbf623c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: PSA 135:10
Text: Who smote great nations, and slew mighty kings;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/135/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffb558cb-0da0-4924-9b72-25ffe499dabf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 135:11
Text: Sihon king of the Amorites, and Og king of Bashan, and all the kingdoms of Canaan:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/135/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26ba65ce-04f5-4b9f-b72d-96583468df86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 135:12
Text: And gave their land for an heritage, an heritage unto Israel his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/135/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c22f5258-89e2-4e56-b84c-eb28216e799f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 135:13
Text: Thy name, O LORD, endureth for ever; and thy memorial, O LORD, throughout all generations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/135/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8bf9442a-1a5a-4b97-aad0-01ec81118447>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 135:14
Text: For the LORD will judge his people, and he will repent himself concerning his servants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/135/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:702da4c7-8b70-484d-997d-7c6313376e2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 135:15
Text: The idols of the heathen are silver and gold, the work of men’s hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/135/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cdef7e2e-0f0f-475a-8625-2aa97f0eeb9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 135:16
Text: They have mouths, but they speak not; eyes have they, but they see not;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/135/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:846b5670-43e9-4996-b699-8ac0fdd6d37c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 135:17
Text: They have ears, but they hear not; neither is there any breath in their mouths.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/135/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad1cf9fc-3319-40fa-bf15-69d2cd082bdb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 135:18
Text: They that make them are like unto them: so is every one that trusteth in them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/135/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b618253-3909-44c4-ac91-6ac2cd9a8cc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 135:19
Text: Bless the LORD, O house of Israel: bless the LORD, O house of Aaron:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/135/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dab82060-6607-494c-9ca1-a8ba6d028434>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 135:20
Text: Bless the LORD, O house of Levi: ye that fear the LORD, bless the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/135/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f40011bf-cc3f-4528-8100-a9f33b7fe2cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 135:21
Text: Blessed be the LORD out of Zion, which dwelleth at Jerusalem. Praise ye the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3eb3cc13-eb5a-48fd-8a19-2a9899893a27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 136:1
Text: O give thanks unto the LORD; for he is good: for his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7ff58c9-d40a-4197-820c-a115088cf849>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 136:2
Text: O give thanks unto the God of gods: for his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7fd8856-5a05-438f-b3ab-5170c6914b5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 136:3
Text: O give thanks to the Lord of lords: for his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4679bb8e-9c75-4c26-872f-936b1015803e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 136:4
Text: To him who alone doeth great wonders: for his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b01e034c-8f74-44ce-940f-99d2681df697>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 136:5
Text: To him that by wisdom made the heavens: for his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2700f834-7562-4896-8d70-fa8a17e01ad2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 136:6
Text: To him that stretched out the earth above the waters: for his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c06b9ff8-025d-4844-826e-f1ef61b36e0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 136:7
Text: To him that made great lights: for his mercy endureth for ever:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9af26f7f-c6c5-4733-80c5-c6adb0a37e17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PSA 136:8
Text: The sun to rule by day: for his mercy endureth for ever:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:983221ac-5105-45e9-b256-b181ddf0434d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 136:9
Text: The moon and stars to rule by night: for his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac7be45d-18c0-4a79-9309-aa88a3ac775c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 136:10
Text: To him that smote Egypt in their firstborn: for his mercy endureth for ever:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:766eb9ef-d4a3-4abc-8cda-a3be18f9c2ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PSA 136:11
Text: And brought out Israel from among them: for his mercy endureth for ever:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ccb788e1-d653-4501-90b4-8c208697f499>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 136:12
Text: With a strong hand, and with a stretched out arm: for his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a50ad37b-47c6-4efd-855e-6c83060e06c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 136:13
Text: To him which divided the Red sea into parts: for his mercy endureth for ever:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d0bbae8-da0e-4845-9e27-7431342b7d25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 136:14
Text: And made Israel to pass through the midst of it: for his mercy endureth for ever:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3c355b4-ed21-4497-93dc-48a9a7ec7a85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 136:15
Text: But overthrew Pharaoh and his host in the Red sea: for his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9839d98-8210-481a-a29f-37d7dce2f45d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 136:16
Text: To him which led his people through the wilderness: for his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2aed55d1-76b0-4459-92b6-af6cd7f3ffff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PSA 136:17
Text: To him which smote great kings: for his mercy endureth for ever:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82a21a83-da03-4135-b2da-ae6041cd4ab9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PSA 136:18
Text: And slew famous kings: for his mercy endureth for ever:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a39d4aab-13d6-4245-aeb6-f16d21402a10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PSA 136:19
Text: Sihon king of the Amorites: for his mercy endureth for ever:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9249d88-e206-49bf-884e-442542302755>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 136:20
Text: And Og the king of Bashan: for his mercy endureth for ever:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80ac9ef5-5893-4bba-acbb-fa7ccd3da06d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 136:21
Text: And gave their land for an heritage: for his mercy endureth for ever:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61361fa4-f59b-4611-9e80-e0233117f01c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 136:22
Text: Even an heritage unto Israel his servant: for his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:774c62ba-0cfa-40b5-be0f-d83685d9c6a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 136:23
Text: Who remembered us in our low estate: for his mercy endureth for ever:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a1c926a-5480-45e5-a7d6-49e7088858c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 136:24
Text: And hath redeemed us from our enemies: for his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45f11379-ab1f-4ff3-8587-a963a3a2d3e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 136:25
Text: Who giveth food to all flesh: for his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/136/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd277521-7c4e-41e6-9f1b-9f70853d6733>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 136:26
Text: O give thanks unto the God of heaven: for his mercy endureth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/137/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf8f2110-5199-488e-a2ae-3fd0e5e44aa6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 137:1
Text: By the rivers of Babylon, there we sat down, yea, we wept, when we remembered Zion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/137/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b7bf231-6a6b-4c89-828e-0e8efe412062>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PSA 137:2
Text: We hanged our harps upon the willows in the midst thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/137/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69d9d042-1d57-4f8f-bb86-7e122faff688>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: PSA 137:3
Text: For there they that carried us away captive required of us a song; and they that wasted us required of us mirth, saying, Sing us one of the songs of Zion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/137/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e3d5b14-440a-4d9e-8d9a-36dfd6f0b7a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: PSA 137:4
Text: How shall we sing the LORD’s song in a strange land?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/137/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c63cde3-5f4b-421b-bd82-132995d2ad2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PSA 137:5
Text: If I forget thee, O Jerusalem, let my right hand forget her cunning.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/137/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31d60e1d-4eed-4cda-a191-f89c56a33f28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: PSA 137:6
Text: If I do not remember thee, let my tongue cleave to the roof of my mouth; if I prefer not Jerusalem above my chief joy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/137/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebefe30a-df7d-45be-8b96-1b30a15b1b7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: PSA 137:7
Text: Remember, O LORD, the children of Edom in the day of Jerusalem; who said, Rase it, rase it, even to the foundation thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/137/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7314bff8-5f82-43ae-affb-8d66b25775f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PSA 137:8
Text: O daughter of Babylon, who art to be destroyed; happy shall he be, that rewardeth thee as thou hast served us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/137/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd417efb-8568-45b0-b7b6-f5c7dc3db124>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 137:9
Text: Happy shall he be, that taketh and dasheth thy little ones against the stones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/138/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5cb07fbf-9913-4937-b1c6-8bf175eb3092>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 138:1
Text: I will praise thee with my whole heart: before the gods will I sing praise unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/138/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2480ed4e-e3e9-4eab-9496-7c5eff452551>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: PSA 138:2
Text: I will worship toward thy holy temple, and praise thy name for thy lovingkindness and for thy truth: for thou hast magnified thy word above all thy name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/138/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f01b2c0-7682-4b3a-a5c9-b19df2b70299>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 138:3
Text: In the day when I cried thou answeredst me, and strengthenedst me with strength in my soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/138/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7aede079-ae74-4e80-8ff2-a8919e486bd0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 138:4
Text: All the kings of the earth shall praise thee, O LORD, when they hear the words of thy mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/138/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9fb566c-0d6c-413d-bff4-49057eaa4900>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 138:5
Text: Yea, they shall sing in the ways of the LORD: for great is the glory of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/138/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:981d9d74-aa84-4981-a119-cef7243a96d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 138:6
Text: Though the LORD be high, yet hath he respect unto the lowly: but the proud he knoweth afar off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/138/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3222aa07-86d5-4792-bac8-6785db2f24e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: PSA 138:7
Text: Though I walk in the midst of trouble, thou wilt revive me: thou shalt stretch forth thine hand against the wrath of mine enemies, and thy right hand shall save me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/138/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb2ac270-544c-4cf1-a163-8e5725a770c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: PSA 138:8
Text: The LORD will perfect that which concerneth me: thy mercy, O LORD, endureth for ever: forsake not the works of thine own hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52e2df2c-0be5-4db2-970b-cffd9bee3cc9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 72

Reference: PSA 139:1
Text: O lord, thou hast searched me, and known me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f5579d0-404b-4de5-80b1-bf51b58f0594>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 139:2
Text: Thou knowest my downsitting and mine uprising, thou understandest my thought afar off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc0b89a4-0d75-4f54-9b9d-311594908354>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 139:3
Text: Thou compassest my path and my lying down, and art acquainted with all my ways.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:051b29e6-35df-4e36-90c8-a7ef2e86f0ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 139:4
Text: For there is not a word in my tongue, but, lo, O LORD, thou knowest it altogether.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84546a16-aa1c-4f05-bae5-5191fd2495c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 139:5
Text: Thou hast beset me behind and before, and laid thine hand upon me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0e97307-a932-407d-afbb-6a9f9ad1922c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 139:6
Text: Such knowledge is too wonderful for me; it is high, I cannot attain unto it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cee4c37a-7d1d-4e8a-a191-84a1faca95ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 139:7
Text: Whither shall I go from thy spirit? or whither shall I flee from thy presence?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8118bf1-c12e-4a76-9dfe-66ff3f54f1da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 139:8
Text: If I ascend up into heaven, thou art there: if I make my bed in hell, behold, thou art there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a89ac381-3d19-4096-993c-c8aae49e6088>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 139:9
Text: If I take the wings of the morning, and dwell in the uttermost parts of the sea;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93e47ef1-e285-4c09-a8e0-bb31e98336f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 139:10
Text: Even there shall thy hand lead me, and thy right hand shall hold me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:414d5b52-756a-4ad0-92d6-97798ab66b2b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PSA 139:11
Text: If I say, Surely the darkness shall cover me; even the night shall be light about me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5aadb68-7129-4ede-9f5d-9d7dbea5610b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: PSA 139:12
Text: Yea, the darkness hideth not from thee; but the night shineth as the day: the darkness and the light are both alike to thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0a15284-7d64-4cb1-b22e-c23d196c870f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 139:13
Text: For thou hast possessed my reins: thou hast covered me in my mother’s womb.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eac1292b-c02a-4c74-82f7-05ad701ed705>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: PSA 139:14
Text: I will praise thee; for I am fearfully and wonderfully made: marvellous are thy works; and that my soul knoweth right well.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fae88b2-f70d-4cc8-85ca-a0e270086500>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: PSA 139:15
Text: My substance was not hid from thee, when I was made in secret, and curiously wrought in the lowest parts of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9c8c617-830d-4e76-924c-969771c33be6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: PSA 139:16
Text: Thine eyes did see my substance, yet being unperfect; and in thy book all my members were written, which in continuance were fashioned, when as yet there was none of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6c370e9-c579-4639-b598-a39cdb8e4d71>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 139:17
Text: How precious also are thy thoughts unto me, O God! how great is the sum of them!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b370adf-cc4c-4ba4-80cf-b84411123602>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PSA 139:18
Text: If I should count them, they are more in number than the sand: when I awake, I am still with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27884d02-7f85-4c8c-b51e-54e596ac7e84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 139:19
Text: Surely thou wilt slay the wicked, O God: depart from me therefore, ye bloody men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22c1d5a7-1b56-46bc-9a62-637017c2d1d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 139:20
Text: For they speak against thee wickedly, and thine enemies take thy name in vain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:023614f3-c6ee-43f1-a630-1e92d1988662>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 139:21
Text: Do not I hate them, O LORD, that hate thee? and am not I grieved with those that rise up against thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe189cf5-8e24-406e-8c1e-35ea7e4a2e75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 139:22
Text: I hate them with perfect hatred: I count them mine enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ecea394c-d1c1-4af3-8c60-b562743ad00b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 139:23
Text: Search me, O God, and know my heart: try me, and know my thoughts:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/139/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:662bc358-c881-463b-af8b-23663f00c373>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 139:24
Text: And see if there be any wicked way in me, and lead me in the way everlasting.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/140/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:455c07d1-e0b2-434d-bf5e-e907d9c491d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PSA 140:1
Text: Deliver me, O LORD, from the evil man: preserve me from the violent man;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/140/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4817716f-b2c3-42ae-9d3f-fb800862c2b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 140:2
Text: Which imagine mischiefs in their heart; continually are they gathered together for war.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/140/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:caa6c960-7579-4b79-897c-0c178f4cfad3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 140:3
Text: They have sharpened their tongues like a serpent; adders’ poison is under their lips. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/140/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0e3a05c-7034-47d1-bdce-bd039b0f60c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: PSA 140:4
Text: Keep me, O LORD, from the hands of the wicked; preserve me from the violent man; who have purposed to overthrow my goings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/140/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d26a2851-5d96-4a2a-b173-e8fa1b95f916>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: PSA 140:5
Text: The proud have hid a snare for me, and cords; they have spread a net by the wayside; they have set gins for me. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/140/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:630bea86-2e26-4e74-afec-4325c8150efa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 140:6
Text: I said unto the LORD, Thou art my God: hear the voice of my supplications, O LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/140/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6fc400a-adc1-403e-ab28-cf9fd88914ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 140:7
Text: O GOD the Lord, the strength of my salvation, thou hast covered my head in the day of battle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/140/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b25c8c4f-e43e-4ab5-b81c-aad5c4358d23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: PSA 140:8
Text: Grant not, O LORD, the desires of the wicked: further not his wicked device; lest they exalt themselves. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/140/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8edf2b12-d56b-42cd-a20e-d1397ea4b51b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 140:9
Text: As for the head of those that compass me about, let the mischief of their own lips cover them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/140/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:523a6efe-9bf3-49fa-9b90-80c119bf156b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: PSA 140:10
Text: Let burning coals fall upon them: let them be cast into the fire; into deep pits, that they rise not up again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/140/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0771bb0-0e9a-4fdf-9d51-356d2bee8ed4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 140:11
Text: Let not an evil speaker be established in the earth: evil shall hunt the violent man to overthrow him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/140/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:100eac65-d0cc-40d1-8c15-80faa21d2699>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 140:12
Text: I know that the LORD will maintain the cause of the afflicted, and the right of the poor.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/140/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:905bf5e9-88fd-4734-b8c5-674a58b2a550>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 140:13
Text: Surely the righteous shall give thanks unto thy name: the upright shall dwell in thy presence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/141/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbe73be9-1386-4cdb-9522-08d257b25f73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 141:1
Text: Lord, I cry unto thee: make haste unto me; give ear unto my voice, when I cry unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/141/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfd15c2e-2fea-4a14-ad80-fc2a50645dfa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PSA 141:2
Text: Let my prayer be set forth before thee as incense; and the lifting up of my hands as the evening sacrifice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/141/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4c45b32-fd6b-426a-95fe-f3a50b2e8144>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 141:3
Text: Set a watch, O LORD, before my mouth; keep the door of my lips.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/141/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d286259-b4d4-4525-a898-461673dbab9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: PSA 141:4
Text: Incline not my heart to any evil thing, to practise wicked works with men that work iniquity: and let me not eat of their dainties.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/141/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b2e8b73-c58c-492d-b8e2-975111ba515a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: PSA 141:5
Text: Let the righteous smite me; it shall be a kindness: and let him reprove me; it shall be an excellent oil, which shall not break my head: for yet my prayer also shall be in their calamities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/141/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b110a78-3b26-4ca2-be72-802708d404c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 141:6
Text: When their judges are overthrown in stony places, they shall hear my words; for they are sweet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/141/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abbab53a-4123-4f35-a012-a06fd021ea99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PSA 141:7
Text: Our bones are scattered at the grave’s mouth, as when one cutteth and cleaveth wood upon the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/141/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c122e219-c57e-46f3-9c69-522e0873f65f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PSA 141:8
Text: But mine eyes are unto thee, O GOD the Lord: in thee is my trust; leave not my soul destitute.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/141/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30189418-20c4-4aa2-ad05-2912d86a7780>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 141:9
Text: Keep me from the snares which they have laid for me, and the gins of the workers of iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/141/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8333c40-4811-4334-8dc0-af8d066a7dfa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 141:10
Text: Let the wicked fall into their own nets, whilst that I withal escape.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/142/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b14b3cf4-c6c2-4729-86e2-eb23ace95ff0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 142:1
Text: I cried unto the LORD with my voice; with my voice unto the LORD did I make my supplication.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/142/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:672a3c28-6af2-4f93-a1ab-b9a541ddd2e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 142:2
Text: I poured out my complaint before him; I shewed before him my trouble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/142/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b3e68c5-2a56-4d3e-b361-667e16638a6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: PSA 142:3
Text: When my spirit was overwhelmed within me, then thou knewest my path. In the way wherein I walked have they privily laid a snare for me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/142/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31b7c59d-29de-4287-8e4a-7d317b98ce23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: PSA 142:4
Text: I looked on my right hand, and beheld, but there was no man that would know me: refuge failed me; no man cared for my soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/142/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef6e57b1-1ecf-4c01-90dc-8363216147db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 142:5
Text: I cried unto thee, O LORD: I said, Thou art my refuge and my portion in the land of the living.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/142/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08592a70-e5dc-4f3b-999c-0fa7a4da064d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PSA 142:6
Text: Attend unto my cry; for I am brought very low: deliver me from my persecutors; for they are stronger than I.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/142/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12c98a0e-9f70-40d3-9676-a854aaae0c01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: PSA 142:7
Text: Bring my soul out of prison, that I may praise thy name: the righteous shall compass me about; for thou shalt deal bountifully with me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/143/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d290f58-2004-4bfe-b647-6bdacd193787>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PSA 143:1
Text: Hear my prayer, O LORD, give ear to my supplications: in thy faithfulness answer me, and in thy righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/143/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fac128a3-7744-479c-b301-4752ece8b97d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 143:2
Text: And enter not into judgment with thy servant: for in thy sight shall no man living be justified.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/143/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a42273c3-b843-4173-b2f8-6bee659892bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: PSA 143:3
Text: For the enemy hath persecuted my soul; he hath smitten my life down to the ground; he hath made me to dwell in darkness, as those that have been long dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/143/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4180fbd3-b2ae-4c7d-b2c7-628e23db4f4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 143:4
Text: Therefore is my spirit overwhelmed within me; my heart within me is desolate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/143/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f50d8114-0a5f-4aee-a676-3c24bad7dd2d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 143:5
Text: I remember the days of old; I meditate on all thy works; I muse on the work of thy hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/143/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa4b4001-6517-4e62-9454-766c45502379>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 143:6
Text: I stretch forth my hands unto thee: my soul thirsteth after thee, as a thirsty land. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/143/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2440d05f-9eef-4e24-9edc-2cbc56e1d353>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: PSA 143:7
Text: Hear me speedily, O LORD: my spirit faileth: hide not thy face from me, lest I be like unto them that go down into the pit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/143/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a55a9c6b-c525-4da4-bcd0-006389ecfe46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: PSA 143:8
Text: Cause me to hear thy lovingkindness in the morning; for in thee do I trust: cause me to know the way wherein I should walk; for I lift up my soul unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/143/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a5cf4a7-9677-4550-8fdb-66ca3985b3a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 143:9
Text: Deliver me, O LORD, from mine enemies: I flee unto thee to hide me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/143/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4962e15-7abe-4958-9a9a-5d6bdbd2166f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 143:10
Text: Teach me to do thy will; for thou art my God: thy spirit is good; lead me into the land of uprightness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/143/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5af5bdc-52a1-4b3c-a6c4-7e0da0eaece3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PSA 143:11
Text: Quicken me, O LORD, for thy name’s sake: for thy righteousness’ sake bring my soul out of trouble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/143/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6159f684-ac02-4238-9afa-4c20ba3fd8be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PSA 143:12
Text: And of thy mercy cut off mine enemies, and destroy all them that afflict my soul: for I am thy servant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/144/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3b7f6a0-9ed7-4463-9cad-e731327866c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PSA 144:1
Text: Blessed be the LORD my strength, which teacheth my hands to war, and my fingers to fight:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/144/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9807a26a-cc24-4a0c-8cc9-36f33ffc3196>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: PSA 144:2
Text: My goodness, and my fortress; my high tower, and my deliverer; my shield, and he in whom I trust; who subdueth my people under me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/144/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a907b0f5-bdc5-46f8-a5b7-c136e820c76e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: PSA 144:3
Text: LORD, what is man, that thou takest knowledge of him! or the son of man, that thou makest account of him!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/144/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df08a335-446d-4f5c-b870-a8ef576cb091>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 144:4
Text: Man is like to vanity: his days are as a shadow that passeth away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/144/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a462775-c83c-41c3-83c6-6caa72e74be4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PSA 144:5
Text: Bow thy heavens, O LORD, and come down: touch the mountains, and they shall smoke.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/144/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d938b7b7-5dd3-4fc5-beb9-307a7638483f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 144:6
Text: Cast forth lightning, and scatter them: shoot out thine arrows, and destroy them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/144/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:278740d5-0072-4da5-aa96-96255756de7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PSA 144:7
Text: Send thine hand from above; rid me, and deliver me out of great waters, from the hand of strange children;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/144/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:034e73af-9601-4926-b402-d6f698c8b6f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 144:8
Text: Whose mouth speaketh vanity, and their right hand is a right hand of falsehood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/144/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea67fcdc-032d-44a3-8ce9-0d128e2fd428>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: PSA 144:9
Text: I will sing a new song unto thee, O God: upon a psaltery and an instrument of ten strings will I sing praises unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/144/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:602efa1e-5560-46ad-90ff-56d6f6427f12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PSA 144:10
Text: It is he that giveth salvation unto kings: who delivereth David his servant from the hurtful sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/144/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba85d6bd-27a1-4810-84c0-cd37cf898e5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: PSA 144:11
Text: Rid me, and deliver me from the hand of strange children, whose mouth speaketh vanity, and their right hand is a right hand of falsehood:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/144/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b53bd2e6-4ff0-4829-8a65-76f7458f9b1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: PSA 144:12
Text: That our sons may be as plants grown up in their youth; that our daughters may be as corner stones, polished after the similitude of a palace:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/144/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa21416d-9621-46c6-a987-e7ca3fa540fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: PSA 144:13
Text: That our garners may be full, affording all manner of store: that our sheep may bring forth thousands and ten thousands in our streets:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/144/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45804ed6-6372-4ff0-9289-6b95d4d47af9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: PSA 144:14
Text: That our oxen may be strong to labour; that there be no breaking in, nor going out; that there be no complaining in our streets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/144/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af3277c4-da83-4127-9513-78d6d5457fa7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 144:15
Text: Happy is that people, that is in such a case: yea, happy is that people, whose God is the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/145/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3197d99-796e-4962-9965-774fdb76afe8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 145:1
Text: I will extol thee, my God, O king; and I will bless thy name for ever and ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/145/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7268e952-beb7-4e03-9e28-fe6634c5a34e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 145:2
Text: Every day will I bless thee; and I will praise thy name for ever and ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/145/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a37db3e5-3da7-4b10-8397-c4eea1775f61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 145:3
Text: Great is the LORD, and greatly to be praised; and his greatness is unsearchable.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/145/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a927fb31-3f39-4f03-b6bf-24034d91ab9e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PSA 145:4
Text: One generation shall praise thy works to another, and shall declare thy mighty acts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/145/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4db37e04-4320-448d-8a3e-e11952228a81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 145:5
Text: I will speak of the glorious honour of thy majesty, and of thy wondrous works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/145/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3495434c-ec57-47bd-a962-4a3bc92462b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 145:6
Text: And men shall speak of the might of thy terrible acts: and I will declare thy greatness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/145/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52b012a1-5283-48fa-bec4-52675883e325>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 145:7
Text: They shall abundantly utter the memory of thy great goodness, and shall sing of thy righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/145/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4192d41-cf03-45f7-b568-f024beadc82a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 145:8
Text: The LORD is gracious, and full of compassion; slow to anger, and of great mercy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/145/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc34ddff-50ed-4246-89fe-a1de58ae7caf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 145:9
Text: The LORD is good to all: and his tender mercies are over all his works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/145/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6e67a7e-68e4-42b3-a38e-d89dc0c8f285>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 145:10
Text: All thy works shall praise thee, O LORD; and thy saints shall bless thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/145/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f03fd662-dbda-4970-a7ac-6c8e1369c542>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 145:11
Text: They shall speak of the glory of thy kingdom, and talk of thy power;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/145/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:636285cb-9016-4fd6-a2e8-d0426e8e9f0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 145:12
Text: To make known to the sons of men his mighty acts, and the glorious majesty of his kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/145/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f491ab6f-0395-4785-b7e3-0ddb253bcde4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 145:13
Text: Thy kingdom is an everlasting kingdom, and thy dominion endureth throughout all generations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/145/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac385a7c-c8f4-4d78-931d-39b611cfc7b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 145:14
Text: The LORD upholdeth all that fall, and raiseth up all those that be bowed down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/145/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67909470-e07f-4005-ab0d-b52193ba70ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 145:15
Text: The eyes of all wait upon thee; and thou givest them their meat in due season.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/145/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cde6e88d-5d4a-47f5-8e8e-e2ff5bc0ea7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 145:16
Text: Thou openest thine hand, and satisfiest the desire of every living thing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/145/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef1a4003-6503-42e3-925b-cf7e664efa1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 145:17
Text: The LORD is righteous in all his ways, and holy in all his works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/145/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21f29cf0-3101-4c29-bc6c-61d434691e48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 145:18
Text: The LORD is nigh unto all them that call upon him, to all that call upon him in truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/145/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0d279e5-e718-49a4-a25a-8b622377db36>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PSA 145:19
Text: He will fulfil the desire of them that fear him: he also will hear their cry, and will save them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/145/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7e79bcf-53ab-488e-9b05-0f01cc9fb6c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 145:20
Text: The LORD preserveth all them that love him: but all the wicked will he destroy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/145/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58f4cbc1-5e93-49cb-9ca7-5b8bd261e0c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PSA 145:21
Text: My mouth shall speak the praise of the LORD: and let all flesh bless his holy name for ever and ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/146/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37ee086d-4e52-4a01-9432-44e4a7828df1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: PSA 146:1
Text: Praise ye the LORD. Praise the LORD, O my soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/146/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d03a817-f89f-4c20-96c6-e621d1a428e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PSA 146:2
Text: While I live will I praise the LORD: I will sing praises unto my God while I have any being.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/146/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6df980a4-fcfb-4b8c-99e6-118a5958a84e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 146:3
Text: Put not your trust in princes, nor in the son of man, in whom there is no help.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/146/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d94a9dcb-6c2d-4aa7-a696-5f1430346cfe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PSA 146:4
Text: His breath goeth forth, he returneth to his earth; in that very day his thoughts perish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/146/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:488182a5-ce91-45b1-a5b4-e89d1abcd87f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 146:5
Text: Happy is he that hath the God of Jacob for his help, whose hope is in the LORD his God:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/146/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10d11b70-60e3-415c-a60a-65c8151c614e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 146:6
Text: Which made heaven, and earth, the sea, and all that therein is: which keepeth truth for ever:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/146/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f3faf82-864f-4477-8d29-eb7b5d7bab8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PSA 146:7
Text: Which executeth judgment for the oppressed: which giveth food to the hungry. The LORD looseth the prisoners:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/146/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cec1882b-acf0-4d20-9808-0c3d37a8cfe9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: PSA 146:8
Text: The LORD openeth the eyes of the blind: the LORD raiseth them that are bowed down: the LORD loveth the righteous:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/146/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c818ea0-6322-4307-8dd9-7aef3c372e67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: PSA 146:9
Text: The LORD preserveth the strangers; he relieveth the fatherless and widow: but the way of the wicked he turneth upside down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/146/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b6e2812-282a-4a83-8455-5fc23bd11671>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 146:10
Text: The LORD shall reign for ever, even thy God, O Zion, unto all generations. Praise ye the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/147/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44d92682-d7a9-4cb7-9c85-8682a4363166>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PSA 147:1
Text: Praise ye the LORD: for it is good to sing praises unto our God; for it is pleasant; and praise is comely.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/147/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3833bb8e-2cdb-469f-b9ca-7ad56ded1e16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 147:2
Text: The LORD doth build up Jerusalem: he gathereth together the outcasts of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/147/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30e0b75a-ec41-4dfa-abbd-71f6a0898df3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 147:3
Text: He healeth the broken in heart, and bindeth up their wounds.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/147/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0664d0a4-f652-4da9-be16-5bf473d4b51f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 147:4
Text: He telleth the number of the stars; he calleth them all by their names.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/147/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05c64977-6682-4f44-b351-7630fb07b1f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 147:5
Text: Great is our Lord, and of great power: his understanding is infinite.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/147/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5ca72d6-5757-428f-98f5-b96d0bd8e060>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 147:6
Text: The LORD lifteth up the meek: he casteth the wicked down to the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/147/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c12daf1-35ab-47a6-9b94-9ab27a0e8e89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PSA 147:7
Text: Sing unto the LORD with thanksgiving; sing praise upon the harp unto our God:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/147/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d78c627-373a-4cc3-8049-5f7e5ae99a3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: PSA 147:8
Text: Who covereth the heaven with clouds, who prepareth rain for the earth, who maketh grass to grow upon the mountains.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/147/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c91372ba-9ab2-460d-aba3-8c11c4cb96c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 147:9
Text: He giveth to the beast his food, and to the young ravens which cry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/147/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2002ebfb-68ae-42b4-b832-8166be724d67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 147:10
Text: He delighteth not in the strength of the horse: he taketh not pleasure in the legs of a man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/147/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92592e12-af0c-48ad-82d6-9b423a40786e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PSA 147:11
Text: The LORD taketh pleasure in them that fear him, in those that hope in his mercy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/147/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0c52a56-0dfd-4000-8f23-384685b06c95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: PSA 147:12
Text: Praise the LORD, O Jerusalem; praise thy God, O Zion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/147/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a846d85-2030-46b5-a0c5-2a89f92adbc0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 147:13
Text: For he hath strengthened the bars of thy gates; he hath blessed thy children within thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/147/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:725f99ce-7a18-460a-8888-c6d00d9213dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PSA 147:14
Text: He maketh peace in thy borders, and filleth thee with the finest of the wheat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/147/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b33553d-c80a-45ad-9c9a-926cbcb6b5a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 147:15
Text: He sendeth forth his commandment upon earth: his word runneth very swiftly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/147/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8516e845-5773-4d7a-8e18-16c800359e0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PSA 147:16
Text: He giveth snow like wool: he scattereth the hoarfrost like ashes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/147/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6228cb0-eecc-440e-bb30-5bb89cbb1e50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PSA 147:17
Text: He casteth forth his ice like morsels: who can stand before his cold?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/147/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:908f66fd-82ef-425f-8596-01ad32467f9e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PSA 147:18
Text: He sendeth out his word, and melteth them: he causeth his wind to blow, and the waters flow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/147/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:653d7532-a656-40a7-8ba5-27187b0bd3e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 147:19
Text: He sheweth his word unto Jacob, his statutes and his judgments unto Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/147/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d4e035b-653f-4620-b55e-a45147546995>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PSA 147:20
Text: He hath not dealt so with any nation: and as for his judgments, they have not known them. Praise ye the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/148/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8150fb84-61d6-4726-9c53-4846550156b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 148:1
Text: Praise ye the LORD. Praise ye the LORD from the heavens: praise him in the heights.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/148/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae834b54-6992-430d-b665-bfb45e8eaf6d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PSA 148:2
Text: Praise ye him, all his angels: praise ye him, all his hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/148/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:593e5f12-c3f3-4b7f-bd91-a923b1ee5a8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PSA 148:3
Text: Praise ye him, sun and moon: praise him, all ye stars of light.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/148/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14aac177-c485-4735-80e0-c6f9597d0d64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PSA 148:4
Text: Praise him, ye heavens of heavens, and ye waters that be above the heavens.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/148/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfd6c065-a462-401d-bda9-ed52861c5e4f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PSA 148:5
Text: Let them praise the name of the LORD: for he commanded, and they were created.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/148/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37023f19-37c7-4dac-8d3f-e3e198457914>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PSA 148:6
Text: He hath also stablished them for ever and ever: he hath made a decree which shall not pass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/148/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17484020-c984-46c6-bd52-c984c52bc406>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PSA 148:7
Text: Praise the LORD from the earth, ye dragons, and all deeps:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/148/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09aba96c-4987-489d-9091-9b0b191c618c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PSA 148:8
Text: Fire, and hail; snow, and vapours; stormy wind fulfilling his word:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/148/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82872c9c-d3ad-42c4-bfab-ec1683e76efc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: PSA 148:9
Text: Mountains, and all hills; fruitful trees, and all cedars:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/148/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4b3c47f-992a-496a-b0f7-e74cf4544145>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PSA 148:10
Text: Beasts, and all cattle; creeping things, and flying fowl:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/148/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c87c4d3a-28ca-4e7a-a877-24c8021b4c1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PSA 148:11
Text: Kings of the earth, and all people; princes, and all judges of the earth:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/148/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d9c1589-24ac-422f-8baf-f8da1001d45d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: PSA 148:12
Text: Both young men, and maidens; old men, and children:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/148/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8bb1db8-f80d-4f02-92f6-9f6d2ff48a47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: PSA 148:13
Text: Let them praise the name of the LORD: for his name alone is excellent; his glory is above the earth and heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/148/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:750ddda5-6075-45d2-8000-d20963a4308c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: PSA 148:14
Text: He also exalteth the horn of his people, the praise of all his saints; even of the children of Israel, a people near unto him. Praise ye the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/149/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf3963b0-2582-401f-ba1d-9d64c833ab36>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 149:1
Text: Praise ye the LORD. Sing unto the LORD a new song, and his praise in the congregation of saints.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/149/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:639ddc4f-c7e4-4263-96d9-448242d22c85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 149:2
Text: Let Israel rejoice in him that made him: let the children of Zion be joyful in their King.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/149/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5de84a81-3e5e-4ba6-b831-dc79e7bfc3ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PSA 149:3
Text: Let them praise his name in the dance: let them sing praises unto him with the timbrel and harp.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/149/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7eecbaae-5150-4ead-9885-683f0d40dba6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PSA 149:4
Text: For the LORD taketh pleasure in his people: he will beautify the meek with salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/149/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9b5624d-d73f-4913-bf08-856dacb6ca8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 149:5
Text: Let the saints be joyful in glory: let them sing aloud upon their beds.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/149/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63d092fc-a067-4117-b854-7827897b2cc7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PSA 149:6
Text: Let the high praises of God be in their mouth, and a two-edged sword in their hand;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/149/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80ec6166-9d77-41a2-81ba-dd772c2c4e0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 149:7
Text: To execute vengeance upon the heathen, and punishments upon the people;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/149/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7095f0de-44b7-4a4c-bb92-10f1debb59b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PSA 149:8
Text: To bind their kings with chains, and their nobles with fetters of iron;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/149/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92843dac-27c2-4f6e-a8d9-b7271a9924f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PSA 149:9
Text: To execute upon them the judgment written: this honour have all his saints. Praise ye the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/150/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:386da75f-cb70-4a83-ad1a-e5cc40901110>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PSA 150:1
Text: Praise ye the LORD. Praise God in his sanctuary: praise him in the firmament of his power.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/150/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3acca68f-ea28-43b9-90b0-24888c55e369>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 150:2
Text: Praise him for his mighty acts: praise him according to his excellent greatness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/150/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fda834d-21c3-400d-a97d-fd6ca462746e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PSA 150:3
Text: Praise him with the sound of the trumpet: praise him with the psaltery and harp.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/150/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:262dcde0-bccf-49d9-8c80-1c39d60cca2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PSA 150:4
Text: Praise him with the timbrel and dance: praise him with stringed instruments and organs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/150/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b960a593-d981-434d-8491-a5a60e06a8e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PSA 150:5
Text: Praise him upon the loud cymbals: praise him upon the high sounding cymbals.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PSA/150/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cd4775b-5a36-4f18-bc4e-2b8f9a747806>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PSA 150:6
Text: Let every thing that hath breath praise the LORD. Praise ye the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8da95a40-55b5-4162-b44d-150dbd1fbd58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: PRO 1:1
Text: The proverbs of Solomon the son of David, king of Israel;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8315db0b-dce1-498c-a066-ddf62dd89d6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PRO 1:2
Text: To know wisdom and instruction; to perceive the words of understanding;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5985b790-59b5-4750-979c-e92c9b35380a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PRO 1:3
Text: To receive the instruction of wisdom, justice, and judgment, and equity;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d72e460c-71c0-4e21-9806-be14ad0572fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PRO 1:4
Text: To give subtilty to the simple, to the young man knowledge and discretion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90232557-d6a2-48cb-8d97-8349883c3e00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PRO 1:5
Text: A wise man will hear, and will increase learning; and a man of understanding shall attain unto wise counsels:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91960c3f-bc3f-42a3-b181-64011601f631>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PRO 1:6
Text: To understand a proverb, and the interpretation; the words of the wise, and their dark sayings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06c3d658-4e59-4788-a306-150bbe5cc68c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PRO 1:7
Text: The fear of the LORD is the beginning of knowledge: but fools despise wisdom and instruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d273f6ca-b9c7-4361-b475-fe95de534124>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PRO 1:8
Text: My son, hear the instruction of thy father, and forsake not the law of thy mother:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff104686-d470-422f-bcd1-cce88d8d6e75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 1:9
Text: For they shall be an ornament of grace unto thy head, and chains about thy neck.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8fbfb75b-b29b-4017-9df9-b7314071a5e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: PRO 1:10
Text: My son, if sinners entice thee, consent thou not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95503cb6-135b-49f2-ad99-b78fb9f1ee80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PRO 1:11
Text: If they say, Come with us, let us lay wait for blood, let us lurk privily for the innocent without cause:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7290f4c8-0263-4816-bada-d797e1e94581>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 1:12
Text: Let us swallow them up alive as the grave; and whole, as those that go down into the pit:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3766e61b-d59c-44eb-8029-94c03969667e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PRO 1:13
Text: We shall find all precious substance, we shall fill our houses with spoil:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9322e65d-56d4-49d1-9108-18e87155deb5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: PRO 1:14
Text: Cast in thy lot among us; let us all have one purse:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75c29cf5-9316-4e66-89c9-20d2020917ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 1:15
Text: My son, walk not thou in the way with them; refrain thy foot from their path:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff1db24c-7634-4477-bcd1-ea8b00b200f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PRO 1:16
Text: For their feet run to evil, and make haste to shed blood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d84d0c51-0845-47af-a2d3-12fa43cecd9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: PRO 1:17
Text: Surely in vain the net is spread in the sight of any bird.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee2d814f-d02c-49ab-bdf5-efc5689ca75f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 1:18
Text: And they lay wait for their own blood; they lurk privily for their own lives.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3dda313a-1d0b-4d85-a936-29c079c575a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PRO 1:19
Text: So are the ways of every one that is greedy of gain; which taketh away the life of the owners thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7529684c-75ae-4dae-9d8e-1a4b4feb8271>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PRO 1:20
Text: Wisdom crieth without; she uttereth her voice in the streets:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68edecd6-fbfd-43e2-9c8a-66c49b20f5d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: PRO 1:21
Text: She crieth in the chief place of concourse, in the openings of the gates: in the city she uttereth her words, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:626f0e7c-8a9a-43c9-a7e0-446d671b441f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: PRO 1:22
Text: How long, ye simple ones, will ye love simplicity? and the scorners delight in their scorning, and fools hate knowledge?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2daffc38-97ed-4bae-8362-9010d98d6de5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PRO 1:23
Text: Turn you at my reproof: behold, I will pour out my spirit unto you, I will make known my words unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fbedbcb-61f0-4c5c-8ffb-d1669df28406>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 1:24
Text: Because I have called, and ye refused; I have stretched out my hand, and no man regarded;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47877092-f870-499e-a348-be84eeebb5a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PRO 1:25
Text: But ye have set at nought all my counsel, and would none of my reproof:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67debc55-2bb4-4392-9ca5-9d550f2bafba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PRO 1:26
Text: I also will laugh at your calamity; I will mock when your fear cometh;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4bfda0c-5ed5-4701-8b09-77d89ee1489a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: PRO 1:27
Text: When your fear cometh as desolation, and your destruction cometh as a whirlwind; when distress and anguish cometh upon you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e82a8acb-ffb5-4fb0-a93f-a2d78d83d1ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: PRO 1:28
Text: Then shall they call upon me, but I will not answer; they shall seek me early, but they shall not find me:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:803d1d5e-f6e8-454b-93af-f6190453287d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PRO 1:29
Text: For that they hated knowledge, and did not choose the fear of the LORD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a81233da-5f1c-4faa-a385-6640fd8aa101>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PRO 1:30
Text: They would none of my counsel: they despised all my reproof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3f24134-691d-46cd-81d7-d9fd1590230f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PRO 1:31
Text: Therefore shall they eat of the fruit of their own way, and be filled with their own devices.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de801504-5cd1-472e-895e-b34f884f099b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PRO 1:32
Text: For the turning away of the simple shall slay them, and the prosperity of fools shall destroy them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/1/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3dcf7f6-35be-4f42-8c66-5070b65dc902>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PRO 1:33
Text: But whoso hearkeneth unto me shall dwell safely, and shall be quiet from fear of evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:663004ce-5ca1-4353-9987-29bff0dffa6d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PRO 2:1
Text: My son, if thou wilt receive my words, and hide my commandments with thee;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b755b88-40ca-450d-a709-1d62f3062ae0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PRO 2:2
Text: So that thou incline thine ear unto wisdom, and apply thine heart to understanding;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d3ce00e-1465-4df4-98b3-a01c30448685>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 2:3
Text: Yea, if thou criest after knowledge, and liftest up thy voice for understanding;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0343f883-878b-4c09-97f5-ccf7fba705cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PRO 2:4
Text: If thou seekest her as silver, and searchest for her as for hid treasures;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38809c85-9152-482b-9114-3cab17dd0ae2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 2:5
Text: Then shalt thou understand the fear of the LORD, and find the knowledge of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94568861-22aa-4588-8f6d-9986a02c4102>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 2:6
Text: For the LORD giveth wisdom: out of his mouth cometh knowledge and understanding.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5337b425-b58c-4fb7-9510-f11e4a24c6f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 2:7
Text: He layeth up sound wisdom for the righteous: he is a buckler to them that walk uprightly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fef5d5d0-83aa-47e5-bf88-5c6eb565b41e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PRO 2:8
Text: He keepeth the paths of judgment, and preserveth the way of his saints.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:828c4497-5e05-41f8-b917-a190d664c7ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 2:9
Text: Then shalt thou understand righteousness, and judgment, and equity; yea, every good path.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:709c7cab-33b3-4775-8ca4-27304bd5bcd4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 2:10
Text: When wisdom entereth into thine heart, and knowledge is pleasant unto thy soul;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39dd117c-39f6-4e35-bc93-bfdd8cb6e518>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PRO 2:11
Text: Discretion shall preserve thee, understanding shall keep thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04eb4bda-1901-4ade-8345-6b3b1a95efac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 2:12
Text: To deliver thee from the way of the evil man, from the man that speaketh froward things;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3a11f5e-2180-4acb-a202-2c0ca7981ebf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PRO 2:13
Text: Who leave the paths of uprightness, to walk in the ways of darkness;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc6a8764-e9cd-4289-9466-4686316ad27e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PRO 2:14
Text: Who rejoice to do evil, and delight in the frowardness of the wicked;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0dc345df-01f0-440a-8c92-93f803bc360f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: PRO 2:15
Text: Whose ways are crooked, and they froward in their paths:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9c00526-51a7-4d73-b9ee-9c63ec71b173>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PRO 2:16
Text: To deliver thee from the strange woman, even from the stranger which flattereth with her words;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1a0ea14-1200-4434-9022-f6da18edfba7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 2:17
Text: Which forsaketh the guide of her youth, and forgetteth the covenant of her God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c1d4fdb-2aa9-4bb9-a3d7-95a5767921ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PRO 2:18
Text: For her house inclineth unto death, and her paths unto the dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a2504a2-9fd5-422e-a70f-7d7e31337604>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 2:19
Text: None that go unto her return again, neither take they hold of the paths of life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc24f1aa-13d9-4b09-88b5-7e749e20dd38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PRO 2:20
Text: That thou mayest walk in the way of good men, and keep the paths of the righteous.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0ae9d97-eb8b-4b91-b13e-3533a391367d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PRO 2:21
Text: For the upright shall dwell in the land, and the perfect shall remain in it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78cf54f6-0e7e-4579-84b5-19fce8dcd202>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 2:22
Text: But the wicked shall be cut off from the earth, and the transgressors shall be rooted out of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1acf60b0-c50b-4edc-a3e9-20122c3c3bd2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PRO 3:1
Text: My son, forget not my law; but let thine heart keep my commandments:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7d7542b-a79b-48ba-91cc-871859fadc90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PRO 3:2
Text: For length of days, and long life, and peace, shall they add to thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f2d8b18-d701-4e9c-898c-c008540418ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PRO 3:3
Text: Let not mercy and truth forsake thee: bind them about thy neck; write them upon the table of thine heart:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d82c6a29-73ac-41b8-abaf-ab9e0d2e34aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PRO 3:4
Text: So shalt thou find favour and good understanding in the sight of God and man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:871fce05-88d1-47ab-9b5b-a50ce28bde80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PRO 3:5
Text: Trust in the LORD with all thine heart; and lean not unto thine own understanding.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:013f273a-89bf-4011-9105-815873ffc2c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PRO 3:6
Text: In all thy ways acknowledge him, and he shall direct thy paths.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17a28fa8-fae6-4ea9-8f08-98a465d72e77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PRO 3:7
Text: Be not wise in thine own eyes: fear the LORD, and depart from evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5750df82-77c8-49bb-9ef9-377a948a8970>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: PRO 3:8
Text: It shall be health to thy navel, and marrow to thy bones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66528fc0-072a-4006-9af1-37d68e612b25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PRO 3:9
Text: Honour the LORD with thy substance, and with the firstfruits of all thine increase:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df85bea4-3443-4f6b-958a-023b2b476406>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 3:10
Text: So shall thy barns be filled with plenty, and thy presses shall burst out with new wine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5890879-1016-4cc3-9a19-dbfbd0ffb257>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PRO 3:11
Text: My son, despise not the chastening of the LORD; neither be weary of his correction:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ed351c5-1dd4-4c3b-81a8-425b2d79dad9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 3:12
Text: For whom the LORD loveth he correcteth; even as a father the son in whom he delighteth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ae99c2c-4eff-49e0-9b63-6965f1f816f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 3:13
Text: Happy is the man that findeth wisdom, and the man that getteth understanding.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9bec0738-9195-41f7-b6f4-8966582d8805>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PRO 3:14
Text: For the merchandise of it is better than the merchandise of silver, and the gain thereof than fine gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:221118c1-6b48-44b7-83e8-c4219befe549>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PRO 3:15
Text: She is more precious than rubies: and all the things thou canst desire are not to be compared unto her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06402993-fafb-4dea-a7c8-64216c33eb34>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PRO 3:16
Text: Length of days is in her right hand; and in her left hand riches and honour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2dc11972-70b8-4587-b9e1-941c06b409e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PRO 3:17
Text: Her ways are ways of pleasantness, and all her paths are peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3454be4-333c-48f8-ac0f-98e73ab39f77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 3:18
Text: She is a tree of life to them that lay hold upon her: and happy is every one that retaineth her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d8518f8-4806-48d9-ae17-e800fdae1528>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PRO 3:19
Text: The LORD by wisdom hath founded the earth; by understanding hath he established the heavens.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4dff62f6-f576-4a61-a41d-ef7f9b6d2fc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PRO 3:20
Text: By his knowledge the depths are broken up, and the clouds drop down the dew.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:251b5f2b-bb4a-41cc-8b6e-d93bfc7f8e0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 3:21
Text: My son, let not them depart from thine eyes: keep sound wisdom and discretion:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d94ffb44-2404-4ed6-b69d-8948d9e85dfa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PRO 3:22
Text: So shall they be life unto thy soul, and grace to thy neck.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32ed94f8-f59e-4e79-a863-8eef5ac47a7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PRO 3:23
Text: Then shalt thou walk in thy way safely, and thy foot shall not stumble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20e15f06-0523-4472-a12c-576b3eb830b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PRO 3:24
Text: When thou liest down, thou shalt not be afraid: yea, thou shalt lie down, and thy sleep shall be sweet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe69e8a4-064e-4dee-83a8-b3122caac0c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PRO 3:25
Text: Be not afraid of sudden fear, neither of the desolation of the wicked, when it cometh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:037aa821-7f45-4b58-b218-21fed9ede50d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 3:26
Text: For the LORD shall be thy confidence, and shall keep thy foot from being taken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bef1e7ba-f1fa-445d-b4e5-10f3c6f26ca5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PRO 3:27
Text: Withhold not good from them to whom it is due, when it is in the power of thine hand to do it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40adbaa3-08e2-472e-b401-3006ead4de3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PRO 3:28
Text: Say not unto thy neighbour, Go, and come again, and to morrow I will give; when thou hast it by thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c6d8e4e-ed30-472b-a794-323c52e21ad8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PRO 3:29
Text: Devise not evil against thy neighbour, seeing he dwelleth securely by thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e06414f5-d1e8-4e99-80d6-6222f304f7f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PRO 3:30
Text: Strive not with a man without cause, if he have done thee no harm.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c0b24e1-80c6-4cdc-af28-dbc03c60be43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PRO 3:31
Text: Envy thou not the oppressor, and choose none of his ways.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:005217bf-9e0d-448c-a3f7-05f40537d0af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PRO 3:32
Text: For the froward is abomination to the LORD: but his secret is with the righteous.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca77bb4e-dce6-4de1-b47f-a141b5590f92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 3:33
Text: The curse of the LORD is in the house of the wicked: but he blesseth the habitation of the just.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1fb89c3-d4c0-43e8-ba80-b774c7bde089>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PRO 3:34
Text: Surely he scorneth the scorners: but he giveth grace unto the lowly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/3/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbdf5ad9-6a2e-4976-8412-88717c46c4ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PRO 3:35
Text: The wise shall inherit glory: but shame shall be the promotion of fools.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b617d53-9f59-4bd2-b7bc-56c812635875>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 4:1
Text: Hear, ye children, the instruction of a father, and attend to know understanding.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0c535f4-0fd3-4331-aa67-5079fc01d15b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: PRO 4:2
Text: For I give you good doctrine, forsake ye not my law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:581a3432-0be4-48d7-80ba-e3cc8078d061>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 4:3
Text: For I was my father’s son, tender and only beloved in the sight of my mother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af0eccc6-e8fb-4d06-a7a9-f098ee029151>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PRO 4:4
Text: He taught me also, and said unto me, Let thine heart retain my words: keep my commandments, and live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da1263cc-be8b-42cc-bf48-2a631affbca4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 4:5
Text: Get wisdom, get understanding: forget it not; neither decline from the words of my mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b11a410-ecd9-45aa-acff-51705461c6a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 4:6
Text: Forsake her not, and she shall preserve thee: love her, and she shall keep thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:907491c5-c9e7-4d36-b252-c318d3a54fa0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PRO 4:7
Text: Wisdom is the principal thing; therefore get wisdom: and with all thy getting get understanding.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f443c28c-9413-4f2f-bcfe-c4c9918d7e0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PRO 4:8
Text: Exalt her, and she shall promote thee: she shall bring thee to honour, when thou dost embrace her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5ea9c79-b387-45d8-b7c0-78373c1da460>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PRO 4:9
Text: She shall give to thine head an ornament of grace: a crown of glory shall she deliver to thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4997b4f-f03c-4e4b-9d4e-a7d120494c3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 4:10
Text: Hear, O my son, and receive my sayings; and the years of thy life shall be many.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4962d73-9e26-4eb4-b771-f7d418040cb7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PRO 4:11
Text: I have taught thee in the way of wisdom; I have led thee in right paths.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:540cc3eb-3adb-4300-a177-feffb56278a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PRO 4:12
Text: When thou goest, thy steps shall not be straitened; and when thou runnest, thou shalt not stumble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d85426f-1520-4557-871d-e2061c6fbb8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 4:13
Text: Take fast hold of instruction; let her not go: keep her; for she is thy life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ad86dfe-cc79-4332-ab71-5b68da965a94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PRO 4:14
Text: Enter not into the path of the wicked, and go not in the way of evil men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79817eb0-43c4-424d-9fd2-696ddc239850>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: PRO 4:15
Text: Avoid it, pass not by it, turn from it, and pass away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44675878-cd37-42ca-8951-c9ec63abb2de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: PRO 4:16
Text: For they sleep not, except they have done mischief; and their sleep is taken away, unless they cause some to fall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e1b5827-0ed8-4882-9b50-29c41aae229e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PRO 4:17
Text: For they eat the bread of wickedness, and drink the wine of violence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e50701e-9e22-444a-b768-9b3dbf9380ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PRO 4:18
Text: But the path of the just is as the shining light, that shineth more and more unto the perfect day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:593aa726-5790-4ac5-b378-baf8125c16db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PRO 4:19
Text: The way of the wicked is as darkness: they know not at what they stumble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef7b729d-f41c-4976-bf81-bd9a187d2523>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PRO 4:20
Text: My son, attend to my words; incline thine ear unto my sayings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6c13f68-6b38-48d3-85ed-ad41760b33ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PRO 4:21
Text: Let them not depart from thine eyes; keep them in the midst of thine heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:681418cf-e055-4a4e-b211-121a8c5d1612>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PRO 4:22
Text: For they are life unto those that find them, and health to all their flesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a87496b-dac7-4a44-bb34-2d8f0faf904e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PRO 4:23
Text: Keep thy heart with all diligence; for out of it are the issues of life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25c0a090-e80b-4a18-8bee-3a06c10b682f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PRO 4:24
Text: Put away from thee a froward mouth, and perverse lips put far from thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9807eaf-3017-4be5-9f79-5eb48addbea1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 4:25
Text: Let thine eyes look right on, and let thine eyelids look straight before thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06881305-8bc5-4269-9c0b-d8a903931a58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PRO 4:26
Text: Ponder the path of thy feet, and let all thy ways be established.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/4/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:525c5a54-3f75-4463-b412-08638e37b64b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PRO 4:27
Text: Turn not to the right hand nor to the left: remove thy foot from evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dec74013-77ca-4f62-9fe9-c5798b524adb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PRO 5:1
Text: My son, attend unto my wisdom, and bow thine ear to my understanding:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee7859c6-9cb9-45d6-892c-0658354280ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PRO 5:2
Text: That thou mayest regard discretion, and that thy lips may keep knowledge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47a6f250-d8e5-43f6-b9c9-a4c220f1d9a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 5:3
Text: For the lips of a strange woman drop as an honeycomb, and her mouth is smoother than oil:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13fd9aed-8e74-40b3-aefd-0442744b2b66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PRO 5:4
Text: But her end is bitter as wormwood, sharp as a two-edged sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4298a08-6da5-4c8a-933a-b4e84c89a6dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: PRO 5:5
Text: Her feet go down to death; her steps take hold on hell.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da009046-aa97-4e78-bc75-966daf86c7a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PRO 5:6
Text: Lest thou shouldest ponder the path of life, her ways are moveable, that thou canst not know them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe98c7ca-2f63-4213-9108-1f04bc83ca50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 5:7
Text: Hear me now therefore, O ye children, and depart not from the words of my mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b473dac-b54b-483b-84e7-9ddc86261a1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PRO 5:8
Text: Remove thy way far from her, and come not nigh the door of her house:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76aa421d-1c6f-4621-b699-7aa774f7addf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PRO 5:9
Text: Lest thou give thine honour unto others, and thy years unto the cruel:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d409157-e30e-42c8-bd84-81396a79aaf7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 5:10
Text: Lest strangers be filled with thy wealth; and thy labours be in the house of a stranger;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78816f13-ca53-4201-bfe9-0a390d3b812e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PRO 5:11
Text: And thou mourn at the last, when thy flesh and thy body are consumed,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75b4c85f-f546-40d9-99e0-307771273128>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PRO 5:12
Text: And say, How have I hated instruction, and my heart despised reproof;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98d4da28-f0b3-45f5-9c40-978ca86f7333>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PRO 5:13
Text: And have not obeyed the voice of my teachers, nor inclined mine ear to them that instructed me!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25a17936-a728-44ad-9314-c5c386ea608c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PRO 5:14
Text: I was almost in all evil in the midst of the congregation and assembly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4e46dd6-7cae-49c4-baa5-a80d6ac81061>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 5:15
Text: Drink waters out of thine own cistern, and running waters out of thine own well.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b3b403c-8fb5-4c47-8970-f24a65ff0d3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PRO 5:16
Text: Let thy fountains be dispersed abroad, and rivers of waters in the streets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/5/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b302057-3f1f-4bf1-974c-7cfdb509593b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PRO 5:17
Text: Let them be only thine own, and not strangers’ with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/5/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34fe8d64-799b-425f-b12b-73b2965be241>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PRO 5:18
Text: Let thy fountain be blessed: and rejoice with the wife of thy youth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/5/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc96992c-1b7f-4aeb-93ea-0daa47fc951d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: PRO 5:19
Text: Let her be as the loving hind and pleasant roe; let her breasts satisfy thee at all times; and be thou ravished always with her love.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/5/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:319f0c59-2c97-4a33-9029-d4a739ea2e5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PRO 5:20
Text: And why wilt thou, my son, be ravished with a strange woman, and embrace the bosom of a stranger?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/5/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:972cc014-24c5-46bc-8c02-48ed709a6e84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 5:21
Text: For the ways of man are before the eyes of the LORD, and he pondereth all his goings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/5/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d040c07b-46e5-42b5-a9a6-e7acdb58d9e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PRO 5:22
Text: His own iniquities shall take the wicked himself, and he shall be holden with the cords of his sins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/5/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0623e6d3-e987-4e46-9260-763acb7f6e7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 5:23
Text: He shall die without instruction; and in the greatness of his folly he shall go astray.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:047aa086-6178-4907-9a22-eded9164fe03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 6:1
Text: My son, if thou be surety for thy friend, if thou hast stricken thy hand with a stranger,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d46bd05-2277-4e6a-b174-ce7d7600a037>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 6:2
Text: Thou art snared with the words of thy mouth, thou art taken with the words of thy mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53a9ae1b-1037-4e88-9334-ef697b35a1b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: PRO 6:3
Text: Do this now, my son, and deliver thyself, when thou art come into the hand of thy friend; go, humble thyself, and make sure thy friend.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9654bde-cbd8-4f33-a9aa-b9436daf2e83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: PRO 6:4
Text: Give not sleep to thine eyes, nor slumber to thine eyelids.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:caf2fc5f-612e-446e-ac76-87de6f6ee2bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PRO 6:5
Text: Deliver thyself as a roe from the hand of the hunter, and as a bird from the hand of the fowler.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a74b3b6-5fc8-4d65-a794-9fadc6edf787>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PRO 6:6
Text: Go to the ant, thou sluggard; consider her ways, and be wise:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9923f7e-b536-4ebe-9c38-483e9374f2ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 68

Reference: PRO 6:7
Text: Which having no guide, overseer, or ruler,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:821ac742-5a4b-4743-ac5e-52daad7ea28c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PRO 6:8
Text: Provideth her meat in the summer, and gathereth her food in the harvest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fd3c3dd-24ce-4a89-94a2-9f2dc29fe3fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PRO 6:9
Text: How long wilt thou sleep, O sluggard? when wilt thou arise out of thy sleep?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2975dfe-3704-4a95-8819-17458f953b25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 6:10
Text: Yet a little sleep, a little slumber, a little folding of the hands to sleep:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c92efe1-b3d1-47aa-aad0-8d82825df183>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 6:11
Text: So shall thy poverty come as one that travelleth, and thy want as an armed man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ed6097c-dc40-4a25-a655-de83492dee7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PRO 6:12
Text: A naughty person, a wicked man, walketh with a froward mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b1bed31-72c3-40c7-8395-983655995f81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PRO 6:13
Text: He winketh with his eyes, he speaketh with his feet, he teacheth with his fingers;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbc5a528-1291-477c-b4ba-b43b7d07894f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PRO 6:14
Text: Frowardness is in his heart, he deviseth mischief continually; he soweth discord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bab0771-7634-4c95-a9d7-4dcc0dd660d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 6:15
Text: Therefore shall his calamity come suddenly; suddenly shall he be broken without remedy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0936c14a-589e-435d-96ad-7ddab4088f45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PRO 6:16
Text: These six things doth the LORD hate: yea, seven are an abomination unto him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bdcd2db7-df2e-4e81-b1af-0811499356d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PRO 6:17
Text: A proud look, a lying tongue, and hands that shed innocent blood,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41fdf894-9593-4211-8b22-68dda9357355>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PRO 6:18
Text: An heart that deviseth wicked imaginations, feet that be swift in running to mischief,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1537bb78-3040-4364-b12b-61f961342cd3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 6:19
Text: A false witness that speaketh lies, and he that soweth discord among brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f00eb037-794e-42b2-886c-8f7df612f6f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 6:20
Text: My son, keep thy father’s commandment, and forsake not the law of thy mother:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b5f7283-555e-471e-9bda-0d7c70a3d923>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PRO 6:21
Text: Bind them continually upon thine heart, and tie them about thy neck.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1e06221-a0f2-4636-9484-32e38f0d7fce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: PRO 6:22
Text: When thou goest, it shall lead thee; when thou sleepest, it shall keep thee; and when thou awakest, it shall talk with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37416d84-8f6b-4ea5-b39d-52c4390d1131>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PRO 6:23
Text: For the commandment is a lamp; and the law is light; and reproofs of instruction are the way of life:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0144fa6-ffd7-4b4a-88e3-e8b4972fcdac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 6:24
Text: To keep thee from the evil woman, from the flattery of the tongue of a strange woman.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cdf05293-f14f-4949-adc0-d41d1ae440d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 6:25
Text: Lust not after her beauty in thine heart; neither let her take thee with her eyelids.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9c1276d-19f3-4deb-9b50-3aef93f0c89d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: PRO 6:26
Text: For by means of a whorish woman a man is brought to a piece of bread: and the adultress will hunt for the precious life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7642ad8-c5dc-4030-9949-63272d8d5278>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PRO 6:27
Text: Can a man take fire in his bosom, and his clothes not be burned?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:273a9dd0-5be0-48ac-8229-56be58a0f294>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: PRO 6:28
Text: Can one go upon hot coals, and his feet not be burned?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0360c36-df6d-4074-b492-fae497492313>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PRO 6:29
Text: So he that goeth in to his neighbour’s wife; whosoever toucheth her shall not be innocent.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f695157-1900-4f9d-9b67-9243394e660b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 6:30
Text: Men do not despise a thief, if he steal to satisfy his soul when he is hungry;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3515d972-55fd-4fb0-962d-743ea2ff9434>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PRO 6:31
Text: But if he be found, he shall restore sevenfold; he shall give all the substance of his house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:faf11035-b475-4e70-8b51-643eb3c6408b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PRO 6:32
Text: But whoso committeth adultery with a woman lacketh understanding: he that doeth it destroyeth his own soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae814c20-3b05-4fb2-a412-cefc5c62ed1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 6:33
Text: A wound and dishonour shall he get; and his reproach shall not be wiped away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:addf3452-e1c4-4674-9868-c39afc42c77f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 6:34
Text: For jealousy is the rage of a man: therefore he will not spare in the day of vengeance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/6/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab44cd3e-467f-4d6a-b90a-6ad07a46168c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PRO 6:35
Text: He will not regard any ransom; neither will he rest content, though thou givest many gifts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c317d9e-6336-4fc3-b277-cef525322c97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PRO 7:1
Text: My son, keep my words, and lay up my commandments with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d0281a6-9c3f-4914-9de3-78291a565b81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PRO 7:2
Text: Keep my commandments, and live; and my law as the apple of thine eye.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7829ee4-4acd-4f14-88fd-ca934357d38a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PRO 7:3
Text: Bind them upon thy fingers, write them upon the table of thine heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0347b946-dac2-4478-be26-1a9e162c8591>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PRO 7:4
Text: Say unto wisdom, Thou art my sister; and call understanding thy kinswoman:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a68361db-595a-4c3e-b9a7-54abb846a7e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PRO 7:5
Text: That they may keep thee from the strange woman, from the stranger which flattereth with her words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c45b108-7740-4ab9-a028-64e5a3550ed7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: PRO 7:6
Text: For at the window of my house I looked through my casement,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8dd31715-ff3c-4c2f-9398-3fcf6c1fdb84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PRO 7:7
Text: And beheld among the simple ones, I discerned among the youths, a young man void of understanding,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63ed1f16-be5e-4344-9959-098ba9684696>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PRO 7:8
Text: Passing through the street near her corner; and he went the way to her house,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d43e177-d1cd-43ce-836b-7bd6199fb2e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PRO 7:9
Text: In the twilight, in the evening, in the black and dark night:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ab75210-7c5f-4beb-90a1-9501111fdec7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 7:10
Text: And, behold, there met him a woman with the attire of an harlot, and subtil of heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:089eeda5-57dc-4d48-adbe-8bd55c8eb1d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PRO 7:11
Text: (She is loud and stubborn; her feet abide not in her house:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:542d1735-7192-4c45-8747-4adb45e86e9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PRO 7:12
Text: Now is she without, now in the streets, and lieth in wait at every corner.)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a76bb3e6-8e3a-47ed-addd-5cf37b00b1b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PRO 7:13
Text: So she caught him, and kissed him, and with an impudent face said unto him,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6ffd58a-7ebf-41c0-b997-a64e6ed5d5de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PRO 7:14
Text: I have peace offerings with me; this day have I payed my vows.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6012617e-d607-4e78-81f6-b3dfee1eaf9f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 7:15
Text: Therefore came I forth to meet thee, diligently to seek thy face, and I have found thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:407398ab-4586-4889-b866-7697f12f80ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PRO 7:16
Text: I have decked my bed with coverings of tapestry, with carved works, with fine linen of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d675814-fe7a-4624-b923-6697d9324581>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: PRO 7:17
Text: I have perfumed my bed with myrrh, aloes, and cinnamon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e85063d3-0dfd-4eb2-a10a-0947c03f3374>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 7:18
Text: Come, let us take our fill of love until the morning: let us solace ourselves with loves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37147335-03c6-4e54-93a1-e69594722131>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: PRO 7:19
Text: For the goodman is not at home, he is gone a long journey:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:056130d6-0143-43a8-b940-0433b3117d39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 7:20
Text: He hath taken a bag of money with him, and will come home at the day appointed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e558199b-7d02-4017-9c51-93b4e90ffae6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PRO 7:21
Text: With her much fair speech she caused him to yield, with the flattering of her lips she forced him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84a50a26-60c3-4406-ac0c-3507df27534c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: PRO 7:22
Text: He goeth after her straightway, as an ox goeth to the slaughter, or as a fool to the correction of the stocks;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c328c4b-7a83-40ea-8e07-c013e0cf2ae6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: PRO 7:23
Text: Till a dart strike through his liver; as a bird hasteth to the snare, and knoweth not that it is for his life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b573d245-95a6-4124-a847-50d05b669c62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PRO 7:24
Text: Hearken unto me now therefore, O ye children, and attend to the words of my mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62812dce-3653-4078-b692-3ab982601bff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PRO 7:25
Text: Let not thine heart decline to her ways, go not astray in her paths.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:282db0ef-d365-4be7-9544-32c37aa29ffb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PRO 7:26
Text: For she hath cast down many wounded: yea, many strong men have been slain by her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/7/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1847e20-50c5-4b3f-b1dd-79ef805eb379>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PRO 7:27
Text: Her house is the way to hell, going down to the chambers of death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13c858b0-a7ea-4ed5-b592-204d0e1b52ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: PRO 8:1
Text: Doth not wisdom cry? and understanding put forth her voice?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b43370d-8063-472d-a280-bcdeaebf1bfa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 8:2
Text: She standeth in the top of high places, by the way in the places of the paths.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be560739-4c7f-4b93-ae1d-4c9965a5424d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 8:3
Text: She crieth at the gates, at the entry of the city, at the coming in at the doors.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:feee9fdd-40c6-480f-8174-f5f59f87c84d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PRO 8:4
Text: Unto you, O men, I call; and my voice is to the sons of man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fccf8040-9980-4cea-ac9e-a4944db9ca2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 8:5
Text: O ye simple, understand wisdom: and, ye fools, be ye of an understanding heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:959c4391-91d2-4953-aa1b-d2733d250389>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PRO 8:6
Text: Hear; for I will speak of excellent things; and the opening of my lips shall be right things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0cfa84ab-41d2-41a7-9fd1-e966654b93d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PRO 8:7
Text: For my mouth shall speak truth; and wickedness is an abomination to my lips.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1b62ffd-0123-45ca-a0c7-6209eba5da5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PRO 8:8
Text: All the words of my mouth are in righteousness; there is nothing froward or perverse in them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9621a0cb-95b7-49a9-b3d8-131dce1ee1d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PRO 8:9
Text: They are all plain to him that understandeth, and right to them that find knowledge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac0798ef-9fb6-4886-b484-1c9fad1cfd5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 8:10
Text: Receive my instruction, and not silver; and knowledge rather than choice gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae88d97b-9c33-44a4-8e69-c2300df7782e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PRO 8:11
Text: For wisdom is better than rubies; and all the things that may be desired are not to be compared to it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ba6b2c4-c7c7-4ac8-98ab-18cc852ef34e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PRO 8:12
Text: I wisdom dwell with prudence, and find out knowledge of witty inventions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6d17e64-da83-420a-b3fd-bb73f32036a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PRO 8:13
Text: The fear of the LORD is to hate evil: pride, and arrogancy, and the evil way, and the froward mouth, do I hate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6817b37d-a9c5-4a42-8c31-f3023efa5eb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PRO 8:14
Text: Counsel is mine, and sound wisdom: I am understanding; I have strength.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c9f2d58-f8b7-495c-91a2-658af3691b6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: PRO 8:15
Text: By me kings reign, and princes decree justice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6aca51cf-342d-4287-94d3-f5893f7be6d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PRO 8:16
Text: By me princes rule, and nobles, even all the judges of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f3503c7-f59d-4eb0-9c65-a2ace59d9252>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PRO 8:17
Text: I love them that love me; and those that seek me early shall find me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:728606ef-925c-4545-8979-59c4158df9f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PRO 8:18
Text: Riches and honour are with me; yea, durable riches and righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8fdd860-7dcf-4d11-b197-4e9ec647e6b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 8:19
Text: My fruit is better than gold, yea, than fine gold; and my revenue than choice silver.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bd685be-d3ea-4152-91a1-007f2c7a7c14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PRO 8:20
Text: I lead in the way of righteousness, in the midst of the paths of judgment:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3fa958ab-d578-438e-a9d7-1b7b09bd0114>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PRO 8:21
Text: That I may cause those that love me to inherit substance; and I will fill their treasures.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e233fda-83e5-406b-8a77-1f915539cae5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PRO 8:22
Text: The LORD possessed me in the beginning of his way, before his works of old.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6a315ab-2408-4e5c-93ab-c3697fddb222>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PRO 8:23
Text: I was set up from everlasting, from the beginning, or ever the earth was.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1ec10ad-b76a-4528-8e4a-2ec3781586ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PRO 8:24
Text: When there were no depths, I was brought forth; when there were no fountains abounding with water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc5ab9a1-158a-4cee-8b16-bd74a8a03b99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PRO 8:25
Text: Before the mountains were settled, before the hills was I brought forth:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a031d024-1f1a-463b-8acb-54bdc47720a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PRO 8:26
Text: While as yet he had not made the earth, nor the fields, nor the highest part of the dust of the world.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d7ab5ce-b168-4d0e-90bf-a8360fd38004>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PRO 8:27
Text: When he prepared the heavens, I was there: when he set a compass upon the face of the depth:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dab64864-068e-4d06-bc26-7f190370ad4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 8:28
Text: When he established the clouds above: when he strengthened the fountains of the deep:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a94d94b2-3f8d-4f88-98af-f59a53727818>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: PRO 8:29
Text: When he gave to the sea his decree, that the waters should not pass his commandment: when he appointed the foundations of the earth:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:992c8f19-30ae-4b56-847f-567678594be8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PRO 8:30
Text: Then I was by him, as one brought up with him: and I was daily his delight, rejoicing always before him;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b8724ac-d270-4c45-bc56-f25a962c7dfc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 8:31
Text: Rejoicing in the habitable part of his earth; and my delights were with the sons of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d55de1ae-d53a-4761-8af7-2e41a0bea85a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 8:32
Text: Now therefore hearken unto me, O ye children: for blessed are they that keep my ways.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74dc4bb8-e545-4471-a0ff-69f15159262f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: PRO 8:33
Text: Hear instruction, and be wise, and refuse it not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c47ceba4-34ee-4715-8088-5ece10ad4cdc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PRO 8:34
Text: Blessed is the man that heareth me, watching daily at my gates, waiting at the posts of my doors.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2341149b-d8da-4f4b-bdf0-360f3c4dd892>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PRO 8:35
Text: For whoso findeth me findeth life, and shall obtain favour of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/8/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5673f912-613d-40c4-9f48-e1a4b0e1cffc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 8:36
Text: But he that sinneth against me wrongeth his own soul: all they that hate me love death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/9/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f71abdfe-6889-4bf3-ac93-586a4ac41a0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PRO 9:1
Text: Wisdom hath builded her house, she hath hewn out her seven pillars:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/9/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6db2591f-5309-4890-a003-1c441911eaa6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 9:2
Text: She hath killed her beasts; she hath mingled her wine; she hath also furnished her table.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/9/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cfa7813-c0b8-44fd-b57c-0333c6910c31>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 9:3
Text: She hath sent forth her maidens: she crieth upon the highest places of the city,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/9/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b65d092-94eb-40fa-97a9-22333a22ecdb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 9:4
Text: Whoso is simple, let him turn in hither: as for him that wanteth understanding, she saith to him,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/9/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:376e12c7-2771-44a5-8c70-049633594a65>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PRO 9:5
Text: Come, eat of my bread, and drink of the wine which I have mingled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/9/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a259625-7723-4e69-8e5d-550c06035702>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PRO 9:6
Text: Forsake the foolish, and live; and go in the way of understanding.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/9/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3188fa8c-2908-4bba-9cca-74009e2f147e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: PRO 9:7
Text: He that reproveth a scorner getteth to himself shame: and he that rebuketh a wicked man getteth himself a blot.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/9/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9cf3641-c897-4a81-b4a2-ab15bdcd0da8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PRO 9:8
Text: Reprove not a scorner, lest he hate thee: rebuke a wise man, and he will love thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/9/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:398bec60-bb9c-489a-9861-445aadb7e892>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PRO 9:9
Text: Give instruction to a wise man, and he will be yet wiser: teach a just man, and he will increase in learning.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/9/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d78e3b86-6ad1-4f4b-80a2-063269361f7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 9:10
Text: The fear of the LORD is the beginning of wisdom: and the knowledge of the holy is understanding.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/9/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02cdc1cc-dee1-44f5-8168-b9a16104ccfd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 9:11
Text: For by me thy days shall be multiplied, and the years of thy life shall be increased.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/9/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4065ca77-b11f-4900-a6d4-8378e70bf17b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 9:12
Text: If thou be wise, thou shalt be wise for thyself: but if thou scornest, thou alone shalt bear it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/9/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31d21b61-40a4-424d-8ef2-0718c19b093c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PRO 9:13
Text: A foolish woman is clamorous: she is simple, and knoweth nothing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/9/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:798825a4-64f0-4241-aa09-14d3530832be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PRO 9:14
Text: For she sitteth at the door of her house, on a seat in the high places of the city,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/9/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:333637ff-82e3-46c0-811f-a53425b0068e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: PRO 9:15
Text: To call passengers who go right on their ways:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/9/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31a946b1-17dd-4513-964f-d51e58e57890>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PRO 9:16
Text: Whoso is simple, let him turn in hither: and as for him that wanteth understanding, she saith to him,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/9/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb44eb25-35f7-492e-8f12-0d75166d8cf0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PRO 9:17
Text: Stolen waters are sweet, and bread eaten in secret is pleasant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/9/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:509d9f24-172b-476a-a5b3-ebb2ad607886>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PRO 9:18
Text: But he knoweth not that the dead are there; and that her guests are in the depths of hell.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c65b016-a20f-4fd0-8fc7-108e5fcbbd56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PRO 10:1
Text: The proverbs of Solomon. A wise son maketh a glad father: but a foolish son is the heaviness of his mother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:768f3c0e-4911-4782-99f3-be178c85f139>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 10:2
Text: Treasures of wickedness profit nothing: but righteousness delivereth from death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7e8c5e7-ce5f-460a-a97f-4c095630fc65>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: PRO 10:3
Text: The LORD will not suffer the soul of the righteous to famish: but he casteth away the substance of the wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4b11f40-71fa-4eca-9719-19fae4a79bea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PRO 10:4
Text: He becometh poor that dealeth with a slack hand: but the hand of the diligent maketh rich.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57d18610-6758-4405-a826-f042379ea180>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PRO 10:5
Text: He that gathereth in summer is a wise son: but he that sleepeth in harvest is a son that causeth shame.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cff10373-d18e-4ffd-bda4-7396018f091d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 10:6
Text: Blessings are upon the head of the just: but violence covereth the mouth of the wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9060c46-f393-4475-b372-23750d74f8d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PRO 10:7
Text: The memory of the just is blessed: but the name of the wicked shall rot.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:124b5594-8d55-49e3-bef1-06ac4fa5164c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PRO 10:8
Text: The wise in heart will receive commandments: but a prating fool shall fall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85195430-a8f7-4664-9a15-889fb2df4bb7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 10:9
Text: He that walketh uprightly walketh surely: but he that perverteth his ways shall be known.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8e1137c-d9e7-4281-b005-c54a95c3bc50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PRO 10:10
Text: He that winketh with the eye causeth sorrow: but a prating fool shall fall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2397e3d9-5a5d-44fe-9d42-4e6ce3339cf8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PRO 10:11
Text: The mouth of a righteous man is a well of life: but violence covereth the mouth of the wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d20a99e9-d9d5-44f0-b6ec-8bb9e82ac634>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: PRO 10:12
Text: Hatred stirreth up strifes: but love covereth all sins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26da4821-c5a8-4d5a-9f99-5f8a1fc226ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: PRO 10:13
Text: In the lips of him that hath understanding wisdom is found: but a rod is for the back of him that is void of understanding.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d5d505f-0011-4a44-9a46-dabcde3e5290>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 10:14
Text: Wise men lay up knowledge: but the mouth of the foolish is near destruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8563816f-566c-4ad9-a830-ddb0e2345f2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PRO 10:15
Text: The rich man’s wealth is his strong city: the destruction of the poor is their poverty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10828025-1af0-4efc-80d4-a19665cd3f6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 10:16
Text: The labour of the righteous tendeth to life: the fruit of the wicked to sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:353241ce-d546-4d76-9be3-331cd8ba4913>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 10:17
Text: He is in the way of life that keepeth instruction: but he that refuseth reproof erreth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee4b2b0f-cb65-4308-a2bf-50b497837f6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PRO 10:18
Text: He that hideth hatred with lying lips, and he that uttereth a slander, is a fool.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9c0027a-72c2-4163-8422-a6ffe98ecb05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PRO 10:19
Text: In the multitude of words there wanteth not sin: but he that refraineth his lips is wise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b76079f4-6f47-4703-a005-edd07d482c59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 10:20
Text: The tongue of the just is as choice silver: the heart of the wicked is little worth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e2896d0-9bf0-47cf-b3e2-ee9163309f92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PRO 10:21
Text: The lips of the righteous feed many: but fools die for want of wisdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d9c40ad-cf6c-4568-bbdd-5997da6b7630>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PRO 10:22
Text: The blessing of the LORD, it maketh rich, and he addeth no sorrow with it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6cf3acd-ebe8-4310-898d-f0d97d00334a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PRO 10:23
Text: It is as sport to a fool to do mischief: but a man of understanding hath wisdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e59c637f-7d38-43b6-8d3c-77b938d2290d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PRO 10:24
Text: The fear of the wicked, it shall come upon him: but the desire of the righteous shall be granted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:926119de-2ba6-4292-abf2-6df7d679ee32>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PRO 10:25
Text: As the whirlwind passeth, so is the wicked no more: but the righteous is an everlasting foundation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71b6ab86-0b68-4ddc-98c1-9015f2a722c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PRO 10:26
Text: As vinegar to the teeth, and as smoke to the eyes, so is the sluggard to them that send him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d88e461-6995-4cd6-a2ae-8f2c5d8bc190>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PRO 10:27
Text: The fear of the LORD prolongeth days: but the years of the wicked shall be shortened.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9b90834-9af1-4ff8-aba0-fcebb2cbaa1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PRO 10:28
Text: The hope of the righteous shall be gladness: but the expectation of the wicked shall perish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46f92d02-e244-4f27-bc97-d8e058fa6929>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PRO 10:29
Text: The way of the LORD is strength to the upright: but destruction shall be to the workers of iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7998ecb0-3391-4372-bc4a-b1bce731f8b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PRO 10:30
Text: The righteous shall never be removed: but the wicked shall not inhabit the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c891457-fb2e-4108-85d4-db7c5e8f41f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PRO 10:31
Text: The mouth of the just bringeth forth wisdom: but the froward tongue shall be cut out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/10/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89d12d57-1322-44c0-a56e-af075adbb037>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PRO 10:32
Text: The lips of the righteous know what is acceptable: but the mouth of the wicked speaketh frowardness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f361e205-2334-4b8c-9b7d-536207a933a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 11:1
Text: A false balance is abomination to the LORD: but a just weight is his delight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:765da434-97bf-4b2c-a47a-dd0f4f457f39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PRO 11:2
Text: When pride cometh, then cometh shame: but with the lowly is wisdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e62d9e86-c145-4ca2-94ea-9bb852235034>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PRO 11:3
Text: The integrity of the upright shall guide them: but the perverseness of transgressors shall destroy them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:984b0906-bb3d-46bd-9946-25597f3bcb06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 11:4
Text: Riches profit not in the day of wrath: but righteousness delivereth from death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bf995f5-6aad-4b3e-8660-85fae0e84f2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PRO 11:5
Text: The righteousness of the perfect shall direct his way: but the wicked shall fall by his own wickedness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f43a53ee-b873-48ef-88e5-cb2772986de6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PRO 11:6
Text: The righteousness of the upright shall deliver them: but transgressors shall be taken in their own naughtiness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3dfdb8a3-4f33-4293-88cd-be3aa142c838>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PRO 11:7
Text: When a wicked man dieth, his expectation shall perish: and the hope of unjust men perisheth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec78f621-fd3d-400c-818d-aaed0067a7e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 11:8
Text: The righteous is delivered out of trouble, and the wicked cometh in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18d00d21-585d-448f-a1fc-2ccb768949af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PRO 11:9
Text: An hypocrite with his mouth destroyeth his neighbour: but through knowledge shall the just be delivered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:175b2e57-6481-4258-9d77-7a2408bcc9f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: PRO 11:10
Text: When it goeth well with the righteous, the city rejoiceth: and when the wicked perish, there is shouting.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17d47d3e-0580-4c92-b800-3b37b1e65bee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PRO 11:11
Text: By the blessing of the upright the city is exalted: but it is overthrown by the mouth of the wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33259437-312f-4bcb-8cef-e90191cfb4f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PRO 11:12
Text: He that is void of wisdom despiseth his neighbour: but a man of understanding holdeth his peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee422c10-e4aa-47cc-983b-10da76dc2734>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PRO 11:13
Text: A talebearer revealeth secrets: but he that is of a faithful spirit concealeth the matter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a4963da-aee3-4e89-ac08-84d718d378f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PRO 11:14
Text: Where no counsel is, the people fall: but in the multitude of counsellors there is safety.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ae75f14-a1e6-4296-8aaa-52feca330ac8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PRO 11:15
Text: He that is surety for a stranger shall smart for it: and he that hateth suretiship is sure.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2803d1f3-b079-478e-aaf8-94e16c65ae17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PRO 11:16
Text: A gracious woman retaineth honour: and strong men retain riches.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28292025-8b74-4150-90cd-102f5570bbe7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PRO 11:17
Text: The merciful man doeth good to his own soul: but he that is cruel troubleth his own flesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8610b010-6d45-4b6e-bbb4-013c9aa14ba2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PRO 11:18
Text: The wicked worketh a deceitful work: but to him that soweth righteousness shall be a sure reward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ea6fbc2-83ec-42b6-8ccb-affaf0ef9346>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 11:19
Text: As righteousness tendeth to life: so he that pursueth evil pursueth it to his own death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:596f06cd-fc12-4a3d-86d4-2da1025935b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: PRO 11:20
Text: They that are of a froward heart are abomination to the LORD: but such as are upright in their way are his delight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8878c54-0544-4066-94d3-bf839ccecf77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: PRO 11:21
Text: Though hand join in hand, the wicked shall not be unpunished: but the seed of the righteous shall be delivered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bd422b4-1824-48e0-9e2e-865f485dd0dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 11:22
Text: As a jewel of gold in a swine’s snout, so is a fair woman which is without discretion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a5c05a2-4d07-40cb-a92d-b6fff09d0a65>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PRO 11:23
Text: The desire of the righteous is only good: but the expectation of the wicked is wrath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0962307-521d-4ee7-bf0e-6057a35c41e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: PRO 11:24
Text: There is that scattereth, and yet increaseth; and there is that withholdeth more than is meet, but it tendeth to poverty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6074e8c-e155-42e5-b171-72933270b0b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 11:25
Text: The liberal soul shall be made fat: and he that watereth shall be watered also himself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c972e80-e685-4c4c-8f3a-226e97acc33a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: PRO 11:26
Text: He that withholdeth corn, the people shall curse him: but blessing shall be upon the head of him that selleth it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0b4c8b3-d6ae-4380-9ee7-f54df600d79a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PRO 11:27
Text: He that diligently seeketh good procureth favour: but he that seeketh mischief, it shall come unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28b8f167-1d04-45a6-9d21-5efd84fa52b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 11:28
Text: He that trusteth in his riches shall fall; but the righteous shall flourish as a branch.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d30eb41-9cef-45a9-a3dd-8b32e9581729>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PRO 11:29
Text: He that troubleth his own house shall inherit the wind: and the fool shall be servant to the wise of heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6fb65cab-6f23-4c71-903e-c6fd1b0a7857>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PRO 11:30
Text: The fruit of the righteous is a tree of life; and he that winneth souls is wise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/11/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97eee0b9-3374-4a3f-9e42-334a5bd695d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PRO 11:31
Text: Behold, the righteous shall be recompensed in the earth: much more the wicked and the sinner.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c0c4d7d-7c11-4485-92ae-883f1f9e82f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PRO 12:1
Text: Whoso loveth instruction loveth knowledge: but he that hateth reproof is brutish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd6a374d-396a-4c72-9582-828a710c2612>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 12:2
Text: A good man obtaineth favour of the LORD: but a man of wicked devices will he condemn.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c462b2d-6f9e-4890-8e1c-eb54686f9d05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PRO 12:3
Text: A man shall not be established by wickedness: but the root of the righteous shall not be moved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89bb135c-7cad-4838-bdcd-47675f406505>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PRO 12:4
Text: A virtuous woman is a crown to her husband: but she that maketh ashamed is as rottenness in his bones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e867db08-2310-41c7-903c-b44feded846c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PRO 12:5
Text: The thoughts of the righteous are right: but the counsels of the wicked are deceit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ffb107a-297c-4079-92cb-8c07b8bbdd78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PRO 12:6
Text: The words of the wicked are to lie in wait for blood: but the mouth of the upright shall deliver them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d352dceb-7c35-47d3-8a0b-72fe624c4173>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PRO 12:7
Text: The wicked are overthrown, and are not: but the house of the righteous shall stand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa60a3d1-56bf-4436-b768-1582446c2953>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PRO 12:8
Text: A man shall be commended according to his wisdom: but he that is of a perverse heart shall be despised.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c584b22-d71a-4999-bd53-88b7f1f5930b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PRO 12:9
Text: He that is despised, and hath a servant, is better than he that honoureth himself, and lacketh bread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d3801e1-e220-4bcd-a367-fab8cb3c5f98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PRO 12:10
Text: A righteous man regardeth the life of his beast: but the tender mercies of the wicked are cruel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:509e4361-ce12-476e-aff8-ca1eb7c83c53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: PRO 12:11
Text: He that tilleth his land shall be satisfied with bread: but he that followeth vain persons is void of understanding.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e746610-1db8-483a-91e3-78c4d1fa41ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 12:12
Text: The wicked desireth the net of evil men: but the root of the righteous yieldeth fruit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02802cc9-8dbd-4d01-9a8d-af789b369d4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PRO 12:13
Text: The wicked is snared by the transgression of his lips: but the just shall come out of trouble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48024009-ef31-4e65-948b-bdfd4a8d55ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: PRO 12:14
Text: A man shall be satisfied with good by the fruit of his mouth: and the recompence of a man’s hands shall be rendered unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f41cab40-6830-480a-b025-94f90f7279d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 12:15
Text: The way of a fool is right in his own eyes: but he that hearkeneth unto counsel is wise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb295251-872d-4a0b-a3ed-eac4f8f53b10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PRO 12:16
Text: A fool’s wrath is presently known: but a prudent man covereth shame.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99abe380-3d1e-4a91-9c45-ef9862a78a55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 12:17
Text: He that speaketh truth sheweth forth righteousness: but a false witness deceit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f58849d5-9c99-4766-8396-f8427864255b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PRO 12:18
Text: There is that speaketh like the piercings of a sword: but the tongue of the wise is health.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6acc7279-b532-46bb-9ca9-f2878ac22ea5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 12:19
Text: The lip of truth shall be established for ever: but a lying tongue is but for a moment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9156c14-0cc5-4637-93dd-0c648e5f5faa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PRO 12:20
Text: Deceit is in the heart of them that imagine evil: but to the counsellors of peace is joy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01fb512d-34f4-44df-a6f1-e281642e7e91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PRO 12:21
Text: There shall no evil happen to the just: but the wicked shall be filled with mischief.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31b6aff7-ba27-4518-8809-4e768f9c78ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PRO 12:22
Text: Lying lips are abomination to the LORD: but they that deal truly are his delight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d3a8739-a725-4b59-a279-967ac143caeb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PRO 12:23
Text: A prudent man concealeth knowledge: but the heart of fools proclaimeth foolishness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9131ba4-08ff-40b9-88ac-6ae8ba6c40eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PRO 12:24
Text: The hand of the diligent shall bear rule: but the slothful shall be under tribute.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5583c5c7-236e-49d0-a61a-0415b9f36bc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 12:25
Text: Heaviness in the heart of man maketh it stoop: but a good word maketh it glad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:704ee614-728f-476a-8181-9e494e718f9e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PRO 12:26
Text: The righteous is more excellent than his neighbour: but the way of the wicked seduceth them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fec18f3f-6e61-4351-a2ce-b8b9e6c107b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: PRO 12:27
Text: The slothful man roasteth not that which he took in hunting: but the substance of a diligent man is precious.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/12/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8899b750-4cc0-4c23-80d8-0edcd0c5611a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PRO 12:28
Text: In the way of righteousness is life: and in the pathway thereof there is no death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a9feeb6-bc6e-4e2a-a523-034b65688197>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 13:1
Text: A wise son heareth his father’s instruction: but a scorner heareth not rebuke.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0055daf-9216-48c5-b0d0-f1fcfe8a8416>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PRO 13:2
Text: A man shall eat good by the fruit of his mouth: but the soul of the transgressors shall eat violence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:567fc46c-da18-4871-b1d0-1444ed46dc9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PRO 13:3
Text: He that keepeth his mouth keepeth his life: but he that openeth wide his lips shall have destruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afb686b8-fb85-4286-aefa-d98391797650>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PRO 13:4
Text: The soul of the sluggard desireth, and hath nothing: but the soul of the diligent shall be made fat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16565b6c-91ae-48d0-8fdf-9ef386b90c34>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PRO 13:5
Text: A righteous man hateth lying: but a wicked man is loathsome, and cometh to shame.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf1043fc-01db-41d8-9002-a27cf4cc1f1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PRO 13:6
Text: Righteousness keepeth him that is upright in the way: but wickedness overthroweth the sinner.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7af21920-60a3-46e7-a96e-46c0eac80850>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: PRO 13:7
Text: There is that maketh himself rich, yet hath nothing: there is that maketh himself poor, yet hath great riches.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73cc3dc6-42a8-4605-a70e-cb4a4eaa06ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 13:8
Text: The ransom of a man’s life are his riches: but the poor heareth not rebuke.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e02090d-552e-4d8d-a07a-0ad0c9b40439>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PRO 13:9
Text: The light of the righteous rejoiceth: but the lamp of the wicked shall be put out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bf31203-2469-40c8-b7b4-39d6912ebedd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PRO 13:10
Text: Only by pride cometh contention: but with the well advised is wisdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0208be6-6410-483c-81c8-cb378476bfa2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PRO 13:11
Text: Wealth gotten by vanity shall be diminished: but he that gathereth by labour shall increase.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9eaac3e-a858-478d-8773-6ddf48895110>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 13:12
Text: Hope deferred maketh the heart sick: but when the desire cometh, it is a tree of life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ca9c2d4-e13d-44cc-879f-f113d1c5dfdd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PRO 13:13
Text: Whoso despiseth the word shall be destroyed: but he that feareth the commandment shall be rewarded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:128a77f0-dce6-4426-a9e8-1325ccb40227>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 13:14
Text: The law of the wise is a fountain of life, to depart from the snares of death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d1c218e-0277-4a35-8a18-6782d8aa69a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PRO 13:15
Text: Good understanding giveth favour: but the way of transgressors is hard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dab3ba5d-84ea-40d4-95a7-4839a9628fe4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PRO 13:16
Text: Every prudent man dealeth with knowledge: but a fool layeth open his folly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b72219d-1d8c-48e6-967a-fe8b071296ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 13:17
Text: A wicked messenger falleth into mischief: but a faithful ambassador is health.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01537512-fb93-496a-bd3b-d71720cce6f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: PRO 13:18
Text: Poverty and shame shall be to him that refuseth instruction: but he that regardeth reproof shall be honoured.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86c029e1-df6a-472c-ade9-8ab73d27d0fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PRO 13:19
Text: The desire accomplished is sweet to the soul: but it is abomination to fools to depart from evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ecaca3a9-c98a-4e2f-b257-aee19d8d900a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PRO 13:20
Text: He that walketh with wise men shall be wise: but a companion of fools shall be destroyed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:305279f6-0222-44d5-857b-08d8c47782a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PRO 13:21
Text: Evil pursueth sinners: but to the righteous good shall be repayed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ce97967-9843-4ec5-b987-7af8794424cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: PRO 13:22
Text: A good man leaveth an inheritance to his children’s children: and the wealth of the sinner is laid up for the just.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6df8844a-10e4-4fa1-904d-9bcb08a6c92d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PRO 13:23
Text: Much food is in the tillage of the poor: but there is that is destroyed for want of judgment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6233237d-f90c-4204-a237-afbc95c3852b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 13:24
Text: He that spareth his rod hateth his son: but he that loveth him chasteneth him betimes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/13/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11820fac-6955-4f4a-946b-de3c2c768c2d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PRO 13:25
Text: The righteous eateth to the satisfying of his soul: but the belly of the wicked shall want.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39ad6665-5944-4a7c-b9ad-5bc368f6d8d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 14:1
Text: Every wise woman buildeth her house: but the foolish plucketh it down with her hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b296b1f8-4278-4f57-a4ea-637f527cacce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PRO 14:2
Text: He that walketh in his uprightness feareth the LORD: but he that is perverse in his ways despiseth him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6da93acf-f93c-4976-aad0-937d18fbab2f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PRO 14:3
Text: In the mouth of the foolish is a rod of pride: but the lips of the wise shall preserve them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04d492bf-5f02-48f7-b96b-be6381170613>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 14:4
Text: Where no oxen are, the crib is clean: but much increase is by the strength of the ox.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cae94390-2b32-477d-8d64-ad8de909b56e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PRO 14:5
Text: A faithful witness will not lie: but a false witness will utter lies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7f9c060-6499-483d-b6fc-f51e280e2e0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 14:6
Text: A scorner seeketh wisdom, and findeth it not: but knowledge is easy unto him that understandeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62082a1c-a4f1-4bb1-98c1-09ea62968ee1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PRO 14:7
Text: Go from the presence of a foolish man, when thou perceivest not in him the lips of knowledge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9515843-5c73-47c1-a85d-fdcfc5fecb9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 14:8
Text: The wisdom of the prudent is to understand his way: but the folly of fools is deceit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:779987a3-89d2-45ca-949a-e8c38f0cb342>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PRO 14:9
Text: Fools make a mock at sin: but among the righteous there is favour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8583fcf1-6f99-4fc9-a87a-6463822cac44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 14:10
Text: The heart knoweth his own bitterness; and a stranger doth not intermeddle with his joy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea21101c-ef97-418a-97c2-0c3114c2c0be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PRO 14:11
Text: The house of the wicked shall be overthrown: but the tabernacle of the upright shall flourish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84f4b26c-74a8-48b0-886f-be614f213796>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PRO 14:12
Text: There is a way which seemeth right unto a man, but the end thereof are the ways of death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:184a44fa-8da3-45b1-a843-400cf90b106c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PRO 14:13
Text: Even in laughter the heart is sorrowful; and the end of that mirth is heaviness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0dad940e-ba1e-42ef-bb03-8ecfc893f110>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PRO 14:14
Text: The backslider in heart shall be filled with his own ways: and a good man shall be satisfied from himself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f002845-94c5-44c4-8aff-0f4e486acadb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 14:15
Text: The simple believeth every word: but the prudent man looketh well to his going.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d01454b1-c785-4a2a-90ae-e2848bc8e789>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PRO 14:16
Text: A wise man feareth, and departeth from evil: but the fool rageth, and is confident.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aec10c92-1f9a-4a95-95f8-42e36b8f2237>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 14:17
Text: He that is soon angry dealeth foolishly: and a man of wicked devices is hated.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df458920-4cdc-480a-9bca-fdc5690203a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PRO 14:18
Text: The simple inherit folly: but the prudent are crowned with knowledge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24bf27d2-2186-438b-b2fb-7f16e2dd6d46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PRO 14:19
Text: The evil bow before the good; and the wicked at the gates of the righteous.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35786760-9d55-48c0-8760-5ee094084e56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 14:20
Text: The poor is hated even of his own neighbour: but the rich hath many friends.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:918674ca-abcd-460b-b8d2-ab5429fe83c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PRO 14:21
Text: He that despiseth his neighbour sinneth: but he that hath mercy on the poor, happy is he.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6b0a769-e4dc-47d0-93b8-e86173db7c62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 14:22
Text: Do they not err that devise evil? but mercy and truth shall be to them that devise good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fced4f9-0161-46d0-8900-7afa9c30db78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 14:23
Text: In all labour there is profit: but the talk of the lips tendeth only to penury.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30d9f5af-c393-41e9-8f7e-7ec27942cb06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 14:24
Text: The crown of the wise is their riches: but the foolishness of fools is folly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e604daf6-ec74-4554-a0fa-6934faa08242>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PRO 14:25
Text: A true witness delivereth souls: but a deceitful witness speaketh lies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:451b611c-3dd2-4c1a-b718-43ebc38cc7ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PRO 14:26
Text: In the fear of the LORD is strong confidence: and his children shall have a place of refuge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7169c67a-d58c-4892-9db0-e177bf9d2aee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 14:27
Text: The fear of the LORD is a fountain of life, to depart from the snares of death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af34c6fd-1997-4c8e-9e71-73aa25e66dde>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PRO 14:28
Text: In the multitude of people is the king’s honour: but in the want of people is the destruction of the prince.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c6952b8-d2b4-430e-8ab6-87575d3a7cab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PRO 14:29
Text: He that is slow to wrath is of great understanding: but he that is hasty of spirit exalteth folly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:861b937a-3fa8-4027-aaee-123677b03f95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 14:30
Text: A sound heart is the life of the flesh: but envy the rottenness of the bones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c9c575a-05c0-4c2c-a9fa-3abb0aff22a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PRO 14:31
Text: He that oppresseth the poor reproacheth his Maker: but he that honoureth him hath mercy on the poor.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a5952d7-85e6-4cce-bc23-23c54b7159dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 14:32
Text: The wicked is driven away in his wickedness: but the righteous hath hope in his death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d27f300b-69b9-42b2-a72c-b0a0cac210e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: PRO 14:33
Text: Wisdom resteth in the heart of him that hath understanding: but that which is in the midst of fools is made known.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f071dc9b-5c6c-4078-b14e-5fae06dc0f1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PRO 14:34
Text: Righteousness exalteth a nation: but sin is a reproach to any people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/14/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:011eb4f4-bb1b-4431-ac6d-f0df26c7d06f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PRO 14:35
Text: The king’s favour is toward a wise servant: but his wrath is against him that causeth shame.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aeacc2bc-e07f-45da-a9a0-1dff8fd2225b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PRO 15:1
Text: A soft answer turneth away wrath: but grievous words stir up anger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3812d532-c2ec-43bb-b9b7-ec65bcbc50e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PRO 15:2
Text: The tongue of the wise useth knowledge aright: but the mouth of fools poureth out foolishness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf52d931-3b17-485f-93e3-204a4c6f63ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PRO 15:3
Text: The eyes of the LORD are in every place, beholding the evil and the good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53043f2d-f705-4503-9ea9-fc6268253d8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 15:4
Text: A wholesome tongue is a tree of life: but perverseness therein is a breach in the spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1bd5d2f8-c7a2-4603-b364-a720e752d262>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PRO 15:5
Text: A fool despiseth his father’s instruction: but he that regardeth reproof is prudent.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f24c16b8-527f-4268-9fb1-8e3563f1d611>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PRO 15:6
Text: In the house of the righteous is much treasure: but in the revenues of the wicked is trouble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3d5d120-b168-414c-8264-afe82c1cc165>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PRO 15:7
Text: The lips of the wise disperse knowledge: but the heart of the foolish doeth not so.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11903079-3985-4b9a-b7aa-321731d1a4af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PRO 15:8
Text: The sacrifice of the wicked is an abomination to the LORD: but the prayer of the upright is his delight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1dcbe811-0a14-4a5f-a8c0-45f83fa234f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PRO 15:9
Text: The way of the wicked is an abomination unto the LORD: but he loveth him that followeth after righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ced443f-58eb-4db2-a949-7acb7942edf5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PRO 15:10
Text: Correction is grievous unto him that forsaketh the way: and he that hateth reproof shall die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b7b1ee5-0b0a-4605-aa14-9a32643df89a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 15:11
Text: Hell and destruction are before the LORD: how much more then the hearts of the children of men?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0497422f-764c-4773-b61a-fe76b6583508>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 15:12
Text: A scorner loveth not one that reproveth him: neither will he go unto the wise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:630e99a0-5610-4d0a-a6dd-07fc2feb9da8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PRO 15:13
Text: A merry heart maketh a cheerful countenance: but by sorrow of the heart the spirit is broken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09d97e08-21be-4e8c-bd89-0f9ea93ceea3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PRO 15:14
Text: The heart of him that hath understanding seeketh knowledge: but the mouth of fools feedeth on foolishness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d55d3a1-fc4c-4716-82d2-46f9e73e7d95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 15:15
Text: All the days of the afflicted are evil: but he that is of a merry heart hath a continual feast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fcdb8d0-3a96-4f0b-aacb-8a079b6eb542>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PRO 15:16
Text: Better is little with the fear of the LORD than great treasure and trouble therewith.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12b38389-c788-4bf2-8bed-0090594fb0b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PRO 15:17
Text: Better is a dinner of herbs where love is, than a stalled ox and hatred therewith.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81e55adb-a30a-4b45-9918-bf3e73b06430>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PRO 15:18
Text: A wrathful man stirreth up strife: but he that is slow to anger appeaseth strife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c0c003c-adcf-4f79-9230-9a1ebe398a5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PRO 15:19
Text: The way of the slothful man is as an hedge of thorns: but the way of the righteous is made plain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f21e6c8-0c0d-471f-916e-61161c2dfa58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PRO 15:20
Text: A wise son maketh a glad father: but a foolish man despiseth his mother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:199437e0-a4bf-493a-afeb-1764e7e6ebb6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PRO 15:21
Text: Folly is joy to him that is destitute of wisdom: but a man of understanding walketh uprightly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:172debcc-f4ec-4032-a684-312bbe403171>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PRO 15:22
Text: Without counsel purposes are disappointed: but in the multitude of counsellors they are established.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1013f1c8-348b-4f0d-80af-e975b00e9bba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PRO 15:23
Text: A man hath joy by the answer of his mouth: and a word spoken in due season, how good is it!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73d4ee94-0a50-41ad-804c-48e94f72ea43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PRO 15:24
Text: The way of life is above to the wise, that he may depart from hell beneath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2cddcb43-d693-433f-83a7-6194ff4e4c36>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PRO 15:25
Text: The LORD will destroy the house of the proud: but he will establish the border of the widow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17f289d6-2b88-4493-9ef7-4b6ac700709e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PRO 15:26
Text: The thoughts of the wicked are an abomination to the LORD: but the words of the pure are pleasant words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a7311f0-1ee1-4ec0-a5dd-46dcffdb6b52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 15:27
Text: He that is greedy of gain troubleth his own house; but he that hateth gifts shall live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0e9ddbf-7b96-4f09-9cfe-c2e4863716b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PRO 15:28
Text: The heart of the righteous studieth to answer: but the mouth of the wicked poureth out evil things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ecab4ef4-ef48-46e5-8202-1fa01025bd82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 15:29
Text: The LORD is far from the wicked: but he heareth the prayer of the righteous.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac5b1851-08f5-41f6-a2a6-22bb9d7f43b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PRO 15:30
Text: The light of the eyes rejoiceth the heart: and a good report maketh the bones fat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5727475-3f11-465c-be47-ced15d99c5c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PRO 15:31
Text: The ear that heareth the reproof of life abideth among the wise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3bc32b7e-5a14-4aab-a6ac-c5308befb257>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PRO 15:32
Text: He that refuseth instruction despiseth his own soul: but he that heareth reproof getteth understanding.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/15/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbceceff-af9d-499d-9e40-8f51390160d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PRO 15:33
Text: The fear of the LORD is the instruction of wisdom; and before honour is humility.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91d8588d-3772-4959-b7fa-df5e85212f3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 16:1
Text: The preparations of the heart in man, and the answer of the tongue, is from the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c96c683f-13f1-4206-bccb-1efdfb64bdc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PRO 16:2
Text: All the ways of a man are clean in his own eyes; but the LORD weigheth the spirits.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6702d529-b0a8-41b4-bbc6-f25338f463f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PRO 16:3
Text: Commit thy works unto the LORD, and thy thoughts shall be established.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e79d4af0-7b5b-4ce5-90e4-6e00a288dd5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PRO 16:4
Text: The LORD hath made all things for himself: yea, even the wicked for the day of evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41d02137-4308-4193-80d9-19e5e2bc39bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: PRO 16:5
Text: Every one that is proud in heart is an abomination to the LORD: though hand join in hand, he shall not be unpunished.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:291e7502-d0a4-4abd-aa35-8e2feeb63a38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 16:6
Text: By mercy and truth iniquity is purged: and by the fear of the LORD men depart from evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c3a3d96-d5ae-41c3-a4c5-1364222e0c2b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 16:7
Text: When a man’s ways please the LORD, he maketh even his enemies to be at peace with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:008bb024-00da-4a35-904f-1b62d61239f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PRO 16:8
Text: Better is a little with righteousness than great revenues without right.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:372f92d2-51a9-4015-af3d-de7f425b066b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PRO 16:9
Text: A man’s heart deviseth his way: but the LORD directeth his steps.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f3a2b19-bc05-40d7-9aca-64a3e74b20c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 16:10
Text: A divine sentence is in the lips of the king: his mouth transgresseth not in judgment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3fca354-3248-4883-93e1-ac866ed1cff4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 16:11
Text: A just weight and balance are the LORD’s: all the weights of the bag are his work.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12879eb8-a3a0-49fd-a053-263456ed0912>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PRO 16:12
Text: It is an abomination to kings to commit wickedness: for the throne is established by righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b10e276-dc23-4b32-8706-62f6208e52d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 16:13
Text: Righteous lips are the delight of kings; and they love him that speaketh right.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef150980-ca88-4cfd-82b5-74bdb0c72912>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 16:14
Text: The wrath of a king is as messengers of death: but a wise man will pacify it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a5750af-a2ba-465a-9a83-52b8172a4a0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PRO 16:15
Text: In the light of the king’s countenance is life; and his favour is as a cloud of the latter rain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47a65cd2-b751-4ef6-99c9-425daf683d67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PRO 16:16
Text: How much better is it to get wisdom than gold! and to get understanding rather to be chosen than silver!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2888921d-ee72-4f0f-a670-b171b5f65c3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 16:17
Text: The highway of the upright is to depart from evil: he that keepeth his way preserveth his soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa26ea46-634d-4ba2-9b4e-f9a5ce21a691>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PRO 16:18
Text: Pride goeth before destruction, and an haughty spirit before a fall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf9e65e5-8f18-4539-aa84-9fd98deb6a81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 16:19
Text: Better it is to be of an humble spirit with the lowly, than to divide the spoil with the proud.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e08437c9-e576-4035-a9ba-5c33bf9a8586>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PRO 16:20
Text: He that handleth a matter wisely shall find good: and whoso trusteth in the LORD, happy is he.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2f2dc36-3adf-4c5b-834b-4e75f0bb9504>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PRO 16:21
Text: The wise in heart shall be called prudent: and the sweetness of the lips increaseth learning.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf15a6ef-10e7-4045-a431-4c01328529fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PRO 16:22
Text: Understanding is a wellspring of life unto him that hath it: but the instruction of fools is folly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c2add6d-d274-4095-85b7-80018374679c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PRO 16:23
Text: The heart of the wise teacheth his mouth, and addeth learning to his lips.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ca6dadc-1fee-47ce-b10a-5cbe5c4dab09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 16:24
Text: Pleasant words are as an honeycomb, sweet to the soul, and health to the bones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38f34a33-d5b6-4050-a0df-34bb2aa8f1ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 16:25
Text: There is a way that seemeth right unto a man, but the end thereof are the ways of death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98a9e485-ec64-43db-bcc1-de4bd7712790>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PRO 16:26
Text: He that laboureth laboureth for himself; for his mouth craveth it of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac43abf0-eee7-48fb-a905-d118d657ab29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PRO 16:27
Text: An ungodly man diggeth up evil: and in his lips there is as a burning fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16102d1b-99d4-4d98-8269-d70ed4573709>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PRO 16:28
Text: A froward man soweth strife: and a whisperer separateth chief friends.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb730c55-0bb7-41aa-831c-1587bf220286>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 16:29
Text: A violent man enticeth his neighbour, and leadeth him into the way that is not good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4e1d5d5-c7a1-405b-894c-9d1794d4e64f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 16:30
Text: He shutteth his eyes to devise froward things: moving his lips he bringeth evil to pass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19be8e8f-178d-491e-ab96-9f54acaaa129>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 16:31
Text: The hoary head is a crown of glory, if it be found in the way of righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4356658-5fdf-4d62-bd29-b56909b0131e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: PRO 16:32
Text: He that is slow to anger is better than the mighty; and he that ruleth his spirit than he that taketh a city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/16/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a7e7962-f489-43d2-a476-c33dacbd9c7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 16:33
Text: The lot is cast into the lap; but the whole disposing thereof is of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4cb8ff6a-b702-4219-becc-01ee3beaa0dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PRO 17:1
Text: Better is a dry morsel, and quietness therewith, than an house full of sacrifices with strife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8bedfb89-ae91-4cb3-9af1-97cfd40c3fee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: PRO 17:2
Text: A wise servant shall have rule over a son that causeth shame, and shall have part of the inheritance among the brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d64b3fa4-56af-4320-b141-bca15aaf4058>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 17:3
Text: The fining pot is for silver, and the furnace for gold: but the LORD trieth the hearts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a0a6b06-dd3a-4c57-b854-da39ea19e9e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PRO 17:4
Text: A wicked doer giveth heed to false lips; and a liar giveth ear to a naughty tongue.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6df8a54e-ee32-432e-a8ab-76263c0e1c0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PRO 17:5
Text: Whoso mocketh the poor reproacheth his Maker: and he that is glad at calamities shall not be unpunished.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c478cb86-ab25-40cf-86e8-603c3a317868>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PRO 17:6
Text: Children’s children are the crown of old men; and the glory of children are their fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd434cea-a0e2-495e-a710-01f0b5fec8f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PRO 17:7
Text: Excellent speech becometh not a fool: much less do lying lips a prince.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22c5cc90-35bb-44d8-be60-3e2343cda1b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PRO 17:8
Text: A gift is as a precious stone in the eyes of him that hath it: whithersoever it turneth, it prospereth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe96fa31-8f85-48cf-b51d-16477c9cbaec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PRO 17:9
Text: He that covereth a transgression seeketh love; but he that repeateth a matter separateth very friends.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87aeb6b2-ff8c-4d4a-9b4a-b1e9c8483b96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 17:10
Text: A reproof entereth more into a wise man than an hundred stripes into a fool.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb55a7be-2688-4a3f-a999-7e4bfb571582>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PRO 17:11
Text: An evil man seeketh only rebellion: therefore a cruel messenger shall be sent against him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5970a51-5422-472d-aa72-61d074142ef4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 17:12
Text: Let a bear robbed of her whelps meet a man, rather than a fool in his folly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa370aee-5006-49f1-bc1a-220112246d9f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PRO 17:13
Text: Whoso rewardeth evil for good, evil shall not depart from his house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15c215fb-38f4-4063-980b-acf3f1594466>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: PRO 17:14
Text: The beginning of strife is as when one letteth out water: therefore leave off contention, before it be meddled with.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1af507b2-6620-41a6-b2af-100b1a5ebbff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PRO 17:15
Text: He that justifieth the wicked, and he that condemneth the just, even they both are abomination to the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2af6e181-852c-40d7-81bb-3f6606728a76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PRO 17:16
Text: Wherefore is there a price in the hand of a fool to get wisdom, seeing he hath no heart to it?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69e23f1a-e75f-4db7-a15b-36be22da4f39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PRO 17:17
Text: A friend loveth at all times, and a brother is born for adversity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c57b7e6-36db-4771-ba6e-a0e8abf32faa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PRO 17:18
Text: A man void of understanding striketh hands, and becometh surety in the presence of his friend.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0dc479bb-2124-49cd-88da-df579424336e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PRO 17:19
Text: He loveth transgression that loveth strife: and he that exalteth his gate seeketh destruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f16f6068-9bb1-4f7a-9006-8934ed696301>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PRO 17:20
Text: He that hath a froward heart findeth no good: and he that hath a perverse tongue falleth into mischief.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7d21a25-7441-497b-9f20-79520855df37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 17:21
Text: He that begetteth a fool doeth it to his sorrow: and the father of a fool hath no joy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:888ff02c-40fe-46e4-aa6a-53c5c6b2db50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 17:22
Text: A merry heart doeth good like a medicine: but a broken spirit drieth the bones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23a1d3f6-8556-402a-b2f6-3b6281b6fb36>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 17:23
Text: A wicked man taketh a gift out of the bosom to pervert the ways of judgment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:beeaa747-5000-42c9-a8c7-04320a5addb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PRO 17:24
Text: Wisdom is before him that hath understanding; but the eyes of a fool are in the ends of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ec3cf8e-9d34-465e-b234-6571cab3b7f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 17:25
Text: A foolish son is a grief to his father, and bitterness to her that bare him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:703f7a9c-bedb-4c2b-9400-6778b82b9b19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PRO 17:26
Text: Also to punish the just is not good, nor to strike princes for equity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bfb22b32-240f-4dbc-9103-0aee99d1c8a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 17:27
Text: He that hath knowledge spareth his words: and a man of understanding is of an excellent spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/17/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3bfaf0ff-75f7-4141-91bf-d77fc3a2fe40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: PRO 17:28
Text: Even a fool, when he holdeth his peace, is counted wise: and he that shutteth his lips is esteemed a man of understanding.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e908717-a138-4282-bc8a-a625f2e42026>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PRO 18:1
Text: Through desire a man, having separated himself, seeketh and intermeddleth with all wisdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:820da356-ba05-48ec-9884-f8b39e853bc5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 18:2
Text: A fool hath no delight in understanding, but that his heart may discover itself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:468cc84d-d71c-447a-8bc3-03c3d44a2a0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 18:3
Text: When the wicked cometh, then cometh also contempt, and with ignominy reproach.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a10e4da-84a4-4c15-a937-727fcbdf1c9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PRO 18:4
Text: The words of a man’s mouth are as deep waters, and the wellspring of wisdom as a flowing brook.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b73152ad-d427-4bc4-ac6d-a412d972c396>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PRO 18:5
Text: It is not good to accept the person of the wicked, to overthrow the righteous in judgment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f6c1b2c-b67e-446a-bce0-e91a08d32115>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PRO 18:6
Text: A fool’s lips enter into contention, and his mouth calleth for strokes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2861f609-b9eb-4840-8463-abe624c07f66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PRO 18:7
Text: A fool’s mouth is his destruction, and his lips are the snare of his soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e69e2e4-6b11-47b4-b02c-624339769a61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 18:8
Text: The words of a talebearer are as wounds, and they go down into the innermost parts of the belly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b09c257-f819-47e0-8b0a-cf94c2185e46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 18:9
Text: He also that is slothful in his work is brother to him that is a great waster.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24918212-8a15-4f1e-b3d8-c2b982a4ae16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PRO 18:10
Text: The name of the LORD is a strong tower: the righteous runneth into it, and is safe.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:223e24e9-ae5c-43b9-a379-45099660f397>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PRO 18:11
Text: The rich man’s wealth is his strong city, and as an high wall in his own conceit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5d804ff-8ef7-491f-afb9-b3008548bf1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 18:12
Text: Before destruction the heart of man is haughty, and before honour is humility.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4106cbb-6771-48d0-ba29-7f234bd484a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PRO 18:13
Text: He that answereth a matter before he heareth it, it is folly and shame unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5e20bea-8f8a-45c4-87ab-72859e3be298>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PRO 18:14
Text: The spirit of a man will sustain his infirmity; but a wounded spirit who can bear?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47d3c27c-a5c5-4dae-96b3-8ac3020654f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 18:15
Text: The heart of the prudent getteth knowledge; and the ear of the wise seeketh knowledge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6356e81-582d-4ac1-9c4f-ba59fcddefa0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PRO 18:16
Text: A man’s gift maketh room for him, and bringeth him before great men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17b3fb5d-1089-4b0d-bf27-bafac650d3a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PRO 18:17
Text: He that is first in his own cause seemeth just; but his neighbour cometh and searcheth him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4103ee3d-14fb-40b9-8f81-f3e63f03ab16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PRO 18:18
Text: The lot causeth contentions to cease, and parteth between the mighty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ced000a8-a034-4d72-a60e-1652ed807cfc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: PRO 18:19
Text: A brother offended is harder to be won than a strong city: and their contentions are like the bars of a castle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35889c19-328d-41f4-a61f-286d78bc433f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: PRO 18:20
Text: A man’s belly shall be satisfied with the fruit of his mouth; and with the increase of his lips shall he be filled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8eb7897a-1acf-40a7-96c3-8bf5855b11ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PRO 18:21
Text: Death and life are in the power of the tongue: and they that love it shall eat the fruit thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d14b0fa9-af4a-4d3c-a133-336eeb86a1b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 18:22
Text: Whoso findeth a wife findeth a good thing, and obtaineth favour of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18039b77-df7f-4dae-9b8c-24849c10c6b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PRO 18:23
Text: The poor useth intreaties; but the rich answereth roughly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/18/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e3e648a-ec51-4d5c-8a5d-fe3e47d5d634>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PRO 18:24
Text: A man that hath friends must shew himself friendly: and there is a friend that sticketh closer than a brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e004bbaa-b77e-42a1-8b83-f0de1fc3fc4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PRO 19:1
Text: Better is the poor that walketh in his integrity, than he that is perverse in his lips, and is a fool.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:956442e9-9e1a-427f-8258-222332789e47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PRO 19:2
Text: Also, that the soul be without knowledge, it is not good; and he that hasteth with his feet sinneth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60ba569f-df62-47f1-ae50-a7a2dd18fb31>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PRO 19:3
Text: The foolishness of man perverteth his way: and his heart fretteth against the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd77e949-2875-4575-9543-b55d5543f3d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PRO 19:4
Text: Wealth maketh many friends; but the poor is separated from his neighbour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3482ed70-57af-400e-8dbd-2816119e825c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PRO 19:5
Text: A false witness shall not be unpunished, and he that speaketh lies shall not escape.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbcc713a-bb6f-443b-8875-f277a1ef63f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PRO 19:6
Text: Many will intreat the favour of the prince: and every man is a friend to him that giveth gifts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77aaee39-a0e8-48d4-8db6-304bbadaeea0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: PRO 19:7
Text: All the brethren of the poor do hate him: how much more do his friends go far from him? he pursueth them with words, yet they are wanting to him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9276e6df-9b1e-4399-9067-1cd0a57b323b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PRO 19:8
Text: He that getteth wisdom loveth his own soul: he that keepeth understanding shall find good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b35a05c-0567-4be1-8ee1-ffac96e00742>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 19:9
Text: A false witness shall not be unpunished, and he that speaketh lies shall perish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca66dbd3-5071-4d38-b090-66e6b32b7640>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 19:10
Text: Delight is not seemly for a fool; much less for a servant to have rule over princes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9a73c6e-a01e-4817-8989-1eed7a684ece>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PRO 19:11
Text: The discretion of a man deferreth his anger; and it is his glory to pass over a transgression.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7e03bea-a6f6-49bc-8b88-e417f5668e6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 19:12
Text: The king’s wrath is as the roaring of a lion; but his favour is as dew upon the grass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:122233e2-7817-4681-ab5f-ddd789f376c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PRO 19:13
Text: A foolish son is the calamity of his father: and the contentions of a wife are a continual dropping.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7639320f-52f3-4a81-9767-33b871ac3bc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PRO 19:14
Text: House and riches are the inheritance of fathers: and a prudent wife is from the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:543fdc91-f8df-4220-af98-026ee3237684>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 19:15
Text: Slothfulness casteth into a deep sleep; and an idle soul shall suffer hunger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eebe8cfc-01e2-4a08-9d64-4f2cf61de79e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 19:16
Text: He that keepeth the commandment keepeth his own soul; but he that despiseth his ways shall die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:087f2b9f-5b87-4385-864a-ef4e04ad526a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PRO 19:17
Text: He that hath pity upon the poor lendeth unto the LORD; and that which he hath given will he pay him again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0585b372-08a4-49ea-9d1d-ef195ba3bcfb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 19:18
Text: Chasten thy son while there is hope, and let not thy soul spare for his crying.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b5af3a6-560e-45c8-bafb-d0d1465e0603>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PRO 19:19
Text: A man of great wrath shall suffer punishment: for if thou deliver him, yet thou must do it again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6822f076-2e57-4177-a5ac-25358c18fb66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PRO 19:20
Text: Hear counsel, and receive instruction, that thou mayest be wise in thy latter end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83ecc424-da2f-488e-b8bd-e502cf98b99c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PRO 19:21
Text: There are many devices in a man’s heart; nevertheless the counsel of the LORD, that shall stand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11cd9fc0-51f0-4e50-957c-a567e84ece59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PRO 19:22
Text: The desire of a man is his kindness: and a poor man is better than a liar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:025930c0-b5a5-45a8-bf1a-a3da9e530434>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: PRO 19:23
Text: The fear of the LORD tendeth to life: and he that hath it shall abide satisfied; he shall not be visited with evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72543e3c-9a8e-434c-91b7-044386aed2bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PRO 19:24
Text: A slothful man hideth his hand in his bosom, and will not so much as bring it to his mouth again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ae92030-2fec-4050-8169-b53d8c8fd56b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: PRO 19:25
Text: Smite a scorner, and the simple will beware: and reprove one that hath understanding, and he will understand knowledge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca0e2815-c538-45ff-80a7-6b422c68271c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PRO 19:26
Text: He that wasteth his father, and chaseth away his mother, is a son that causeth shame, and bringeth reproach.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee845bcf-913f-4b34-8f73-80c3fa1e0eca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 19:27
Text: Cease, my son, to hear the instruction that causeth to err from the words of knowledge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca7c807d-1f3b-4c4e-b440-a88b56fda5e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PRO 19:28
Text: An ungodly witness scorneth judgment: and the mouth of the wicked devoureth iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/19/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:845870e9-48a6-480a-a298-dd3e170713ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PRO 19:29
Text: Judgments are prepared for scorners, and stripes for the back of fools.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00b12050-2d0d-4594-a6f5-adf1e64f8334>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 20:1
Text: Wine is a mocker, strong drink is raging: and whosoever is deceived thereby is not wise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c10761c-0a87-4fab-a7bd-7212df630d35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: PRO 20:2
Text: The fear of a king is as the roaring of a lion: whoso provoketh him to anger sinneth against his own soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c33e122a-5987-46f1-a789-028b68065949>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 20:3
Text: It is an honour for a man to cease from strife: but every fool will be meddling.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:226c4bc5-dfd0-44e9-8f86-fddc239f2ea7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PRO 20:4
Text: The sluggard will not plow by reason of the cold; therefore shall he beg in harvest, and have nothing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1a3c433-f818-4bd9-adbd-e86d2907b266>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PRO 20:5
Text: Counsel in the heart of man is like deep water; but a man of understanding will draw it out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f17bd780-8d22-480c-931c-caff190c7a05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PRO 20:6
Text: Most men will proclaim every one his own goodness: but a faithful man who can find?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:794cbbed-27d2-4579-96db-e03d4dda57c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PRO 20:7
Text: The just man walketh in his integrity: his children are blessed after him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6fdd3f95-0219-4374-952f-ecb00de5fc79>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 20:8
Text: A king that sitteth in the throne of judgment scattereth away all evil with his eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5af18d11-e911-4f83-9f49-56e7a41bd130>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PRO 20:9
Text: Who can say, I have made my heart clean, I am pure from my sin?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f12f6a6f-8c35-4a94-8781-4973224e8895>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 20:10
Text: Divers weights, and divers measures, both of them are alike abomination to the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e550cab-d6d3-4b01-a66d-f012e92ccc72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 20:11
Text: Even a child is known by his doings, whether his work be pure, and whether it be right.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cba20688-b541-40d0-8bbd-f0fc9ac7601a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PRO 20:12
Text: The hearing ear, and the seeing eye, the LORD hath made even both of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc2fef55-0d0b-4a18-bbab-ff06a60789bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PRO 20:13
Text: Love not sleep, lest thou come to poverty; open thine eyes, and thou shalt be satisfied with bread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c216c62-d740-47a3-bcf2-7a426ff3e4ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PRO 20:14
Text: It is naught, it is naught, saith the buyer: but when he is gone his way, then he boasteth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72cadd52-af10-42d5-86d2-1d5fc430395a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PRO 20:15
Text: There is gold, and a multitude of rubies: but the lips of knowledge are a precious jewel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c60bb802-fac0-478d-be55-b82e635e5d51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PRO 20:16
Text: Take his garment that is surety for a stranger: and take a pledge of him for a strange woman.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7199aaf2-38f6-4072-a499-28f78dee9d2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 20:17
Text: Bread of deceit is sweet to a man; but afterwards his mouth shall be filled with gravel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bc5c2b4-e392-4910-89bc-192bc489fe25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PRO 20:18
Text: Every purpose is established by counsel: and with good advice make war.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bd16879-6e89-476a-8e25-ab301c4740c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: PRO 20:19
Text: He that goeth about as a talebearer revealeth secrets: therefore meddle not with him that flattereth with his lips.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93c90782-37ba-43a8-a7fd-8e1a277cb0c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 20:20
Text: Whoso curseth his father or his mother, his lamp shall be put out in obscure darkness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30c2adcb-cb21-4a5c-adc6-890946f9288a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PRO 20:21
Text: An inheritance may be gotten hastily at the beginning; but the end thereof shall not be blessed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2867797e-e22b-42e3-9f8e-ecdd5619f2e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PRO 20:22
Text: Say not thou, I will recompense evil; but wait on the LORD, and he shall save thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b20ba322-66ae-4169-9821-00717078bb22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PRO 20:23
Text: Divers weights are an abomination unto the LORD; and a false balance is not good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7959f684-2ebc-4e28-8d83-7df3617c5c6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PRO 20:24
Text: Man’s goings are of the LORD; how can a man then understand his own way?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8cf88dac-5d4f-457b-b74c-2c42880e00ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PRO 20:25
Text: It is a snare to the man who devoureth that which is holy, and after vows to make enquiry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:062548d9-9d67-46ab-8fab-31e29b40927e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PRO 20:26
Text: A wise king scattereth the wicked, and bringeth the wheel over them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9271a4f-2cb2-4707-85d6-dba92606f77d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PRO 20:27
Text: The spirit of man is the candle of the LORD, searching all the inward parts of the belly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f2eb145-e670-48a8-b1d6-24df8bb794ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PRO 20:28
Text: Mercy and truth preserve the king: and his throne is upholden by mercy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8cf8904b-2092-44e4-818a-bf9f95c31841>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PRO 20:29
Text: The glory of young men is their strength: and the beauty of old men is the grey head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/20/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99602c0e-bbf0-41fd-9b1e-095baf2bae59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PRO 20:30
Text: The blueness of a wound cleanseth away evil: so do stripes the inward parts of the belly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19f85710-a55e-41bd-8b1b-f175ea88a57a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PRO 21:1
Text: The king’s heart is in the hand of the LORD, as the rivers of water: he turneth it whithersoever he will.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3ca0085-0895-4c48-8e08-d06daba68777>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 21:2
Text: Every way of a man is right in his own eyes: but the LORD pondereth the hearts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:316ba998-26c3-4b3e-90f1-b78b564fa92c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PRO 21:3
Text: To do justice and judgment is more acceptable to the LORD than sacrifice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4df1394-b152-4c18-ace7-e5d0a55dd3f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PRO 21:4
Text: An high look, and a proud heart, and the plowing of the wicked, is sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a44f04b1-a625-48d9-a3ca-16f8e7912e6d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PRO 21:5
Text: The thoughts of the diligent tend only to plenteousness; but of every one that is hasty only to want.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f7ca29b-2d99-439a-8350-d5167cb320c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PRO 21:6
Text: The getting of treasures by a lying tongue is a vanity tossed to and fro of them that seek death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49d463b4-55c1-4347-805c-d0e7c539d0b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PRO 21:7
Text: The robbery of the wicked shall destroy them; because they refuse to do judgment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:776a4b9a-54e2-444a-a415-16e33dcd01ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 21:8
Text: The way of man is froward and strange: but as for the pure, his work is right.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bbbb10fb-6e03-4dd0-bdf8-6e93ae48df12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PRO 21:9
Text: It is better to dwell in a corner of the housetop, than with a brawling woman in a wide house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8d62fb9-2519-4338-bf6b-83c346f465f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PRO 21:10
Text: The soul of the wicked desireth evil: his neighbour findeth no favour in his eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0516f03-4bbe-429d-8cfe-23ef64b024df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: PRO 21:11
Text: When the scorner is punished, the simple is made wise: and when the wise is instructed, he receiveth knowledge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19c80a6e-a4bc-4033-9068-74e08c24feaf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: PRO 21:12
Text: The righteous man wisely considereth the house of the wicked: but God overthroweth the wicked for their wickedness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c39f9b73-6fcc-4d07-87b9-c668d6f9de4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PRO 21:13
Text: Whoso stoppeth his ears at the cry of the poor, he also shall cry himself, but shall not be heard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1719867b-b6a7-4925-8543-a536ea463043>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PRO 21:14
Text: A gift in secret pacifieth anger: and a reward in the bosom strong wrath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:264259ed-13c3-47ac-a983-b34dce7199fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PRO 21:15
Text: It is joy to the just to do judgment: but destruction shall be to the workers of iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7cec4d7a-7136-45f8-b8f2-9c86f122e3b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PRO 21:16
Text: The man that wandereth out of the way of understanding shall remain in the congregation of the dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8ea9a15-18d0-4f04-8b92-c5cb216766fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PRO 21:17
Text: He that loveth pleasure shall be a poor man: he that loveth wine and oil shall not be rich.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:baf427e2-3859-465f-92c3-5c9b946dddbf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PRO 21:18
Text: The wicked shall be a ransom for the righteous, and the transgressor for the upright.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03573397-eed5-4586-b987-64b9127b2cd1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 21:19
Text: It is better to dwell in the wilderness, than with a contentious and an angry woman.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9395e4e4-52f1-4f1d-a935-dd15399a0ed3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PRO 21:20
Text: There is treasure to be desired and oil in the dwelling of the wise; but a foolish man spendeth it up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a6a6de9-3512-4778-8c35-cee97553682e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 21:21
Text: He that followeth after righteousness and mercy findeth life, righteousness, and honour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce560771-5299-41ca-be08-04d8cb4c2503>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PRO 21:22
Text: A wise man scaleth the city of the mighty, and casteth down the strength of the confidence thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa26e8e0-e78c-49e7-9cf3-5aee0cda1f7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PRO 21:23
Text: Whoso keepeth his mouth and his tongue keepeth his soul from troubles.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83242ce0-5308-4bc2-be5a-a55710763619>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PRO 21:24
Text: Proud and haughty scorner is his name, who dealeth in proud wrath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:608ce280-2215-4647-9fa2-410d6385998e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PRO 21:25
Text: The desire of the slothful killeth him; for his hands refuse to labour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4701c517-2b61-4c05-b1e4-1fbfa5175de4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PRO 21:26
Text: He coveteth greedily all the day long: but the righteous giveth and spareth not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc7f5ebd-d494-4fcb-aa90-7f09357a2595>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PRO 21:27
Text: The sacrifice of the wicked is abomination: how much more, when he bringeth it with a wicked mind?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bce10edb-43a5-4caa-9538-577ef507d567>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PRO 21:28
Text: A false witness shall perish: but the man that heareth speaketh constantly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:345c8fe4-2c89-4760-afd5-d5add0c629e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 21:29
Text: A wicked man hardeneth his face: but as for the upright, he directeth his way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:affe7bb8-51cf-4c69-abe4-cc167cd44417>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PRO 21:30
Text: There is no wisdom nor understanding nor counsel against the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/21/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:605274af-8bd2-4981-b66e-686eedf60a47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PRO 21:31
Text: The horse is prepared against the day of battle: but safety is of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef1b86d9-c6c8-42de-a1c4-45a4033b7caf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PRO 22:1
Text: A good name is rather to be chosen than great riches, and loving favour rather than silver and gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b78db05-3346-49b0-9fb2-e9ef6ead7b11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PRO 22:2
Text: The rich and poor meet together: the LORD is the maker of them all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1a9198a-f7c5-41f8-97e8-79b864b523fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PRO 22:3
Text: A prudent man foreseeth the evil, and hideth himself: but the simple pass on, and are punished.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:010ea9a3-5eb0-4dd4-8dcf-2f55fc9bab57>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PRO 22:4
Text: By humility and the fear of the LORD are riches, and honour, and life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e109e49c-a139-4fc1-97e6-fb6d32d5514e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PRO 22:5
Text: Thorns and snares are in the way of the froward: he that doth keep his soul shall be far from them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9caa18b2-b1f0-4304-97e8-54090c1d6dae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 22:6
Text: Train up a child in the way he should go: and when he is old, he will not depart from it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:572dc7cc-c741-4fbe-b0a6-0fe48c9718d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PRO 22:7
Text: The rich ruleth over the poor, and the borrower is servant to the lender.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51d873b5-56b4-4232-927e-e7221383d3d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 22:8
Text: He that soweth iniquity shall reap vanity: and the rod of his anger shall fail.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4424552-b63e-47cb-9617-4d6d4c4089d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PRO 22:9
Text: He that hath a bountiful eye shall be blessed; for he giveth of his bread to the poor.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0d497e8-410b-4d0e-acab-ffc0baa1e62b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 22:10
Text: Cast out the scorner, and contention shall go out; yea, strife and reproach shall cease.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbc9e1e0-82f8-4954-b74f-bd300530098e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PRO 22:11
Text: He that loveth pureness of heart, for the grace of his lips the king shall be his friend.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:173e8698-d369-4ecf-b649-8c053ce25208>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PRO 22:12
Text: The eyes of the LORD preserve knowledge, and he overthroweth the words of the transgressor.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:540a87db-3ca4-4802-9600-130cffba33ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PRO 22:13
Text: The slothful man saith, There is a lion without, I shall be slain in the streets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c2e4bcc-c798-4034-8dcf-c3f0134a7fe2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PRO 22:14
Text: The mouth of strange women is a deep pit: he that is abhorred of the LORD shall fall therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf6ed148-5801-4991-a6ea-6ad2c254656a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PRO 22:15
Text: Foolishness is bound in the heart of a child; but the rod of correction shall drive it far from him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63f79844-5cac-41cc-b236-6f2c5ee4c259>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PRO 22:16
Text: He that oppresseth the poor to increase his riches, and he that giveth to the rich, shall surely come to want.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25ad5841-7d45-433f-a76d-fec5fd5877cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PRO 22:17
Text: Bow down thine ear, and hear the words of the wise, and apply thine heart unto my knowledge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52b688ee-adf0-4124-97c6-a67bb129c295>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PRO 22:18
Text: For it is a pleasant thing if thou keep them within thee; they shall withal be fitted in thy lips.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23597d91-dfa0-4b7d-90e3-9a20928a8088>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 22:19
Text: That thy trust may be in the LORD, I have made known to thee this day, even to thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:efdfe818-8fdd-43fd-9645-75eb63b039fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PRO 22:20
Text: Have not I written to thee excellent things in counsels and knowledge,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59c398c7-b15d-4458-a389-3aaa0914adc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: PRO 22:21
Text: That I might make thee know the certainty of the words of truth; that thou mightest answer the words of truth to them that send unto thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09b3d009-c469-4179-9482-83af1b386ed1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PRO 22:22
Text: Rob not the poor, because he is poor: neither oppress the afflicted in the gate:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:106bf098-d9e6-415f-a5ef-cd6926780d98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PRO 22:23
Text: For the LORD will plead their cause, and spoil the soul of those that spoiled them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19126c64-2864-4fd5-bb55-68f59f6c6ad0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 22:24
Text: Make no friendship with an angry man; and with a furious man thou shalt not go:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f505d78-57df-4e62-89d0-bb079362fb08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: PRO 22:25
Text: Lest thou learn his ways, and get a snare to thy soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89afc198-287b-467a-a210-9c912b0dade1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PRO 22:26
Text: Be not thou one of them that strike hands, or of them that are sureties for debts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:463bb320-a7ec-4986-ac0b-a99f01b011b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 22:27
Text: If thou hast nothing to pay, why should he take away thy bed from under thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e337080-5a2f-4b33-9b33-9d3fc1ad06bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PRO 22:28
Text: Remove not the ancient landmark, which thy fathers have set.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/22/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7b7362d-68b5-41c4-92e0-2c57d021c9fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PRO 22:29
Text: Seest thou a man diligent in his business? he shall stand before kings; he shall not stand before mean men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c1cb8a2-bbba-48f9-bfa7-965681579034>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 23:1
Text: When thou sittest to eat with a ruler, consider diligently what is before thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9574f2f1-3595-4b38-802a-72c57cb726d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PRO 23:2
Text: And put a knife to thy throat, if thou be a man given to appetite.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21d76ee1-a9d7-44ff-9c6e-6dc2c1a55fa8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PRO 23:3
Text: Be not desirous of his dainties: for they are deceitful meat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4568f25-e41f-4bea-93dd-4aa7c95f52c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: PRO 23:4
Text: Labour not to be rich: cease from thine own wisdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55f07255-b90f-4560-9b7f-10887dc58a7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: PRO 23:5
Text: Wilt thou set thine eyes upon that which is not? for riches certainly make themselves wings; they fly away as an eagle toward heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd054d23-1163-4ee5-b97f-0560a2483658>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PRO 23:6
Text: Eat thou not the bread of him that hath an evil eye, neither desire thou his dainty meats:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8182955-f905-4b5f-b9f3-35f8641eb7d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PRO 23:7
Text: For as he thinketh in his heart, so is he: Eat and drink, saith he to thee; but his heart is not with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24d5e999-36d1-4d40-96d4-c55749ee5104>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 23:8
Text: The morsel which thou hast eaten shalt thou vomit up, and lose thy sweet words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24df2527-0d8f-4a1b-9da5-4de207cb08da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 23:9
Text: Speak not in the ears of a fool: for he will despise the wisdom of thy words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1999ee22-3d11-498e-9985-b786364e52bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 23:10
Text: Remove not the old landmark; and enter not into the fields of the fatherless:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8f16124-bc2d-477f-8538-0614a353ae98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PRO 23:11
Text: For their redeemer is mighty; he shall plead their cause with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5694fa5-1e96-4d61-a925-836de000765a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 23:12
Text: Apply thine heart unto instruction, and thine ears to the words of knowledge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc414444-837a-4f15-bedc-20c59af1ec6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 23:13
Text: Withhold not correction from the child: for if thou beatest him with the rod, he shall not die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99a6c568-12fb-4d06-8b43-182ce4ff66e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PRO 23:14
Text: Thou shalt beat him with the rod, and shalt deliver his soul from hell.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52bb5d58-a5ba-418c-9109-6a5cad627b14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PRO 23:15
Text: My son, if thine heart be wise, my heart shall rejoice, even mine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf86df75-b8df-42e6-ab88-8a697a90ef63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PRO 23:16
Text: Yea, my reins shall rejoice, when thy lips speak right things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:089974f8-361a-4cab-b0d0-ea3366688e38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 23:17
Text: Let not thine heart envy sinners: but be thou in the fear of the LORD all the day long.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39f243d5-8ae3-43b2-ad3a-54033e15e86f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PRO 23:18
Text: For surely there is an end; and thine expectation shall not be cut off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7ab5f47-f024-460e-8920-ba6ee790b4f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PRO 23:19
Text: Hear thou, my son, and be wise, and guide thine heart in the way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f13dbfd-ccc7-4556-b35c-849702d0d1b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PRO 23:20
Text: Be not among winebibbers; among riotous eaters of flesh:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9c5b8ac-24d5-431c-915d-8a04e9515f67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PRO 23:21
Text: For the drunkard and the glutton shall come to poverty: and drowsiness shall clothe a man with rags.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8d5de59-6bba-4b6d-9dfc-5ffe580212c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 23:22
Text: Hearken unto thy father that begat thee, and despise not thy mother when she is old.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb5f93c5-f7b5-4500-8b6c-d0efea9e7df7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PRO 23:23
Text: Buy the truth, and sell it not; also wisdom, and instruction, and understanding.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a815464-1dc6-40a3-9768-2257b8c5ff16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PRO 23:24
Text: The father of the righteous shall greatly rejoice: and he that begetteth a wise child shall have joy of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:867b6e63-58c9-45ba-91c7-d684443060e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 23:25
Text: Thy father and thy mother shall be glad, and she that bare thee shall rejoice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6ba093c-3cd6-4364-acc7-3e4ddc0ad0dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PRO 23:26
Text: My son, give me thine heart, and let thine eyes observe my ways.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5c3fb49-5d17-4948-be87-3eb90e39ae15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PRO 23:27
Text: For a whore is a deep ditch; and a strange woman is a narrow pit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3bcd801-49ce-4aa9-b7e3-d7dbe5937553>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PRO 23:28
Text: She also lieth in wait as for a prey, and increaseth the transgressors among men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a8993d7-0922-4c38-8984-75aefb0615c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: PRO 23:29
Text: Who hath woe? who hath sorrow? who hath contentions? who hath babbling? who hath wounds without cause? who hath redness of eyes?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:daf3ca77-00db-49d8-9f73-5168225494e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PRO 23:30
Text: They that tarry long at the wine; they that go to seek mixed wine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac558044-af1f-4ea7-bc0c-4aa91d2a140f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: PRO 23:31
Text: Look not thou upon the wine when it is red, when it giveth his colour in the cup, when it moveth itself aright.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b7a95ec-513c-45fa-96c3-081770e0d734>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PRO 23:32
Text: At the last it biteth like a serpent, and stingeth like an adder.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:692fb551-d04c-4fc0-a44d-050dff3b287b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PRO 23:33
Text: Thine eyes shall behold strange women, and thine heart shall utter perverse things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5944bd31-8d21-4363-a606-6d3362f67585>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: PRO 23:34
Text: Yea, thou shalt be as he that lieth down in the midst of the sea, or as he that lieth upon the top of a mast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/23/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:741a0fdd-b73f-425c-ad32-52a6945826d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: PRO 23:35
Text: They have stricken me, shalt thou say, and I was not sick; they have beaten me, and I felt it not: when shall I awake? I will seek it yet again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b6b6a1e-0c35-4752-bf24-5630d66d6b8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PRO 24:1
Text: Be not thou envious against evil men, neither desire to be with them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb1c7bab-c2e9-4b06-8a86-ae23b8d46868>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PRO 24:2
Text: For their heart studieth destruction, and their lips talk of mischief.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc911b99-7580-47b8-853b-eeafe244018f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PRO 24:3
Text: Through wisdom is an house builded; and by understanding it is established:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:825ac5cb-795f-4359-80fe-b53424f354b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PRO 24:4
Text: And by knowledge shall the chambers be filled with all precious and pleasant riches.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f86d5d3-4e38-4945-869b-2bbbf68bc8ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PRO 24:5
Text: A wise man is strong; yea, a man of knowledge increaseth strength.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3f36bdc-bdd9-49ed-a310-e189fdd57f62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PRO 24:6
Text: For by wise counsel thou shalt make thy war: and in multitude of counsellors there is safety.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df5b0f55-1e31-48c6-9b00-8b0f4ea0c9aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PRO 24:7
Text: Wisdom is too high for a fool: he openeth not his mouth in the gate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:980083ea-19ca-49d4-8d79-cb1c8780d9f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PRO 24:8
Text: He that deviseth to do evil shall be called a mischievous person.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7756c597-969b-4a4f-b6a5-b73db121217e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PRO 24:9
Text: The thought of foolishness is sin: and the scorner is an abomination to men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f0b4513-3125-481c-bf17-2eed83219fc9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PRO 24:10
Text: If thou faint in the day of adversity, thy strength is small.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c20a9119-fb3e-47f8-aa5c-39bbe0b458c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PRO 24:11
Text: If thou forbear to deliver them that are drawn unto death, and those that are ready to be slain;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:584bc8ff-b57c-4a45-8221-89d18b8dd97d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: PRO 24:12
Text: If thou sayest, Behold, we knew it not; doth not he that pondereth the heart consider it? and he that keepeth thy soul, doth not he know it? and shall not he render to every man according to his works?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb4d561a-9a2b-421c-8b76-9904bf7e113f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PRO 24:13
Text: My son, eat thou honey, because it is good; and the honeycomb, which is sweet to thy taste:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e4ae865-828a-43c6-bafc-3483631c390b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: PRO 24:14
Text: So shall the knowledge of wisdom be unto thy soul: when thou hast found it, then there shall be a reward, and thy expectation shall not be cut off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d42295f-11b8-4e6b-9e29-b6e909889372>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 24:15
Text: Lay not wait, O wicked man, against the dwelling of the righteous; spoil not his resting place:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe580508-c5c2-44d5-b715-a91896e8d45c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PRO 24:16
Text: For a just man falleth seven times, and riseth up again: but the wicked shall fall into mischief.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:610a5c4b-4dd8-4ccd-bc2a-6e8154aeded1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 24:17
Text: Rejoice not when thine enemy falleth, and let not thine heart be glad when he stumbleth:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17713605-abae-4e87-bddd-a4d5a035285f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PRO 24:18
Text: Lest the LORD see it, and it displease him, and he turn away his wrath from him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:133b7ea8-c873-4b70-b267-f18ef9149cab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 24:19
Text: Fret not thyself because of evil men, neither be thou envious at the wicked:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:910a89e6-8eeb-40f3-a107-f462a7b0023c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 24:20
Text: For there shall be no reward to the evil man; the candle of the wicked shall be put out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40ed709c-adb3-4426-ab50-9fdafdd98d89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PRO 24:21
Text: My son, fear thou the LORD and the king: and meddle not with them that are given to change:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0db4ad4b-aba1-4a6c-be8f-0893e4448598>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 24:22
Text: For their calamity shall rise suddenly; and who knoweth the ruin of them both?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b60c241-49e9-42d5-9f1e-177fede0469b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PRO 24:23
Text: These things also belong to the wise. It is not good to have respect of persons in judgment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13987be7-cf51-4aa4-a5a1-609700ecee3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PRO 24:24
Text: He that saith unto the wicked, Thou are righteous; him shall the people curse, nations shall abhor him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e32f25fe-fc79-4b92-8bf0-37f21bef0c4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 24:25
Text: But to them that rebuke him shall be delight, and a good blessing shall come upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f163f951-d697-405b-ac69-f6d978f3ddfe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: PRO 24:26
Text: Every man shall kiss his lips that giveth a right answer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5078e499-b04a-4a23-8ef3-3e6deec9135d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PRO 24:27
Text: Prepare thy work without, and make it fit for thyself in the field; and afterwards build thine house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9538b352-9044-4e85-be2f-f599cd8edcd0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 24:28
Text: Be not a witness against thy neighbour without cause; and deceive not with thy lips.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db92f963-de05-4c53-85e6-a90a1b02e25d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PRO 24:29
Text: Say not, I will do so to him as he hath done to me: I will render to the man according to his work.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1bbe831-182e-4518-a9bb-91d0961ecb03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PRO 24:30
Text: I went by the field of the slothful, and by the vineyard of the man void of understanding;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:892ef44b-5101-46d5-a319-7867f7c3aa5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: PRO 24:31
Text: And, lo, it was all grown over with thorns, and nettles had covered the face thereof, and the stone wall thereof was broken down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56b5383a-4cb5-4acc-9726-a855f33fe108>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 24:32
Text: Then I saw, and considered it well: I looked upon it, and received instruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d721546-3b63-49ad-ae0e-e6c419da14ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 24:33
Text: Yet a little sleep, a little slumber, a little folding of the hands to sleep:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/24/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b149b741-6cc7-4f3e-864e-62bd7c2713e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 24:34
Text: So shall thy poverty come as one that travelleth; and thy want as an armed man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f4f995a-779b-4bde-b0e9-a8e7ed77c891>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 25:1
Text: These are also proverbs of Solomon, which the men of Hezekiah king of Judah copied out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8eb89246-3708-45ec-bda3-af6d63ee062e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PRO 25:2
Text: It is the glory of God to conceal a thing: but the honour of kings is to search out a matter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07f72634-b624-49e1-9cf2-45eef991966a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 25:3
Text: The heaven for height, and the earth for depth, and the heart of kings is unsearchable.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14736de0-c038-43d6-8ca4-c07b4a37e6c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 25:4
Text: Take away the dross from the silver, and there shall come forth a vessel for the finer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:925fefbd-9641-48d6-bfe5-3c3133575886>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 25:5
Text: Take away the wicked from before the king, and his throne shall be established in righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64b54063-3cae-4ebd-8de4-5cf3f094ae75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PRO 25:6
Text: Put not forth thyself in the presence of the king, and stand not in the place of great men:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bad8b90-912f-4b21-a974-97e857669801>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: PRO 25:7
Text: For better it is that it be said unto thee, Come up hither; than that thou shouldest be put lower in the presence of the prince whom thine eyes have seen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77286d0f-3a5d-475d-a288-2d4b8b2d2ba6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: PRO 25:8
Text: Go not forth hastily to strive, lest thou know not what to do in the end thereof, when thy neighbour hath put thee to shame.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4f9e24b-cd90-4621-a461-c9a93b6f79e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PRO 25:9
Text: Debate thy cause with thy neighbour himself; and discover not a secret to another:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:225e3664-2959-40bb-b035-1090c4fcf68c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PRO 25:10
Text: Lest he that heareth it put thee to shame, and thine infamy turn not away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6450c079-6e99-4f9e-aaea-c974a0a9c723>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PRO 25:11
Text: A word fitly spoken is like apples of gold in pictures of silver.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92d2a745-7fca-46ae-84a2-e4f1b54fa85f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PRO 25:12
Text: As an earring of gold, and an ornament of fine gold, so is a wise reprover upon an obedient ear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:401d1336-cd10-4174-a54f-46759cc62aa2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: PRO 25:13
Text: As the cold of snow in the time of harvest, so is a faithful messenger to them that send him: for he refresheth the soul of his masters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6f00d24-a4d2-4c48-b8fd-8932ba36013a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 25:14
Text: Whoso boasteth himself of a false gift is like clouds and wind without rain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ea33cd6-de79-4980-8b39-bf260f4e18ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 25:15
Text: By long forbearing is a prince persuaded, and a soft tongue breaketh the bone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e656458-eb95-41a4-a1f3-f3acb8abb976>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PRO 25:16
Text: Hast thou found honey? eat so much as is sufficient for thee, lest thou be filled therewith, and vomit it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3886d7e4-dff0-45d7-8751-70882ded77b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PRO 25:17
Text: Withdraw thy foot from thy neighbour’s house; lest he be weary of thee, and so hate thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8a78d09-38da-4d10-aa58-90eee59ce00b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PRO 25:18
Text: A man that beareth false witness against his neighbour is a maul, and a sword, and a sharp arrow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f6dc924-319e-43d3-8874-7ea0adbbaadb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PRO 25:19
Text: Confidence in an unfaithful man in time of trouble is like a broken tooth, and a foot out of joint.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a24deac-9bbf-480e-8c2c-41626c278e8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: PRO 25:20
Text: As he that taketh away a garment in cold weather, and as vinegar upon nitre, so is he that singeth songs to an heavy heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76d53737-1ef5-4025-88a8-9b526bd34012>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 25:21
Text: If thine enemy be hungry, give him bread to eat; and if he be thirsty, give him water to drink:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38b6d63d-1c57-4866-af62-bd2b5401c5f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PRO 25:22
Text: For thou shalt heap coals of fire upon his head, and the LORD shall reward thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b255970-ccf3-4097-a3f7-65647b722ca2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PRO 25:23
Text: The north wind driveth away rain: so doth an angry countenance a backbiting tongue.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c06e599-1d0c-4e5e-87d5-31739ea28b8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PRO 25:24
Text: It is better to dwell in the corner of the housetop, than with a brawling woman and in a wide house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37db48ce-e0a5-4338-8c65-3fcb3ca220fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PRO 25:25
Text: As cold waters to a thirsty soul, so is good news from a far country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e252afe7-ed17-402c-ba37-8329e16a5d68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 25:26
Text: A righteous man falling down before the wicked is as a troubled fountain, and a corrupt spring.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98b00a9e-d3e4-4371-bbe5-5db5e62010ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 25:27
Text: It is not good to eat much honey: so for men to search their own glory is not glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/25/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2be01e5-dea7-4ef4-b4fe-0ba0c62d0c2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 25:28
Text: He that hath no rule over his own spirit is like a city that is broken down, and without walls.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7e3e655-b011-4909-85d0-b17525b726a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 26:1
Text: As snow in summer, and as rain in harvest, so honour is not seemly for a fool.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee70f895-0887-48b2-a5bd-ee92cc6985f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PRO 26:2
Text: As the bird by wandering, as the swallow by flying, so the curse causeless shall not come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06aee560-2595-4ac6-912b-a5184259a52a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PRO 26:3
Text: A whip for the horse, a bridle for the ass, and a rod for the fool’s back.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6fdce0da-6046-4970-95a0-3a26961fab4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PRO 26:4
Text: Answer not a fool according to his folly, lest thou also be like unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87024ea7-7d29-4256-ad88-c87d124ed75a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PRO 26:5
Text: Answer a fool according to his folly, lest he be wise in his own conceit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e6c9844-c950-4e69-9e55-8211f4b7be0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PRO 26:6
Text: He that sendeth a message by the hand of a fool cutteth off the feet, and drinketh damage.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:559fe80a-8af0-42be-bab6-346ab1e1bf29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PRO 26:7
Text: The legs of the lame are not equal: so is a parable in the mouth of fools.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:059241a6-75d6-4a72-b501-2d1128920b09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 26:8
Text: As he that bindeth a stone in a sling, so is he that giveth honour to a fool.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b7009ad-a754-4ca6-8a2f-5f363e339663>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 26:9
Text: As a thorn goeth up into the hand of a drunkard, so is a parable in the mouths of fools.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1b741a5-44df-4d7f-9638-1abb8742d795>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PRO 26:10
Text: The great God that formed all things both rewardeth the fool, and rewardeth transgressors.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ebbeded-dc02-4b4f-bee0-3e2120fbbb38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PRO 26:11
Text: As a dog returneth to his vomit, so a fool returneth to his folly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26355d0a-bb57-47b8-ade8-a41eb8da8891>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PRO 26:12
Text: Seest thou a man wise in his own conceit? there is more hope of a fool than of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6a68274-d1eb-4a5e-abf3-b8f1019cb199>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 26:13
Text: The slothful man saith, There is a lion in the way; a lion is in the streets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98e5f09d-684e-4eee-bfc7-6b4003397f94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PRO 26:14
Text: As the door turneth upon his hinges, so doth the slothful upon his bed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f10bc271-004f-4362-9389-7e07b540e3d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PRO 26:15
Text: The slothful hideth his hand in his bosom; it grieveth him to bring it again to his mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c6ab5bc-919a-4a5e-8001-953be12b6cd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PRO 26:16
Text: The sluggard is wiser in his own conceit than seven men that can render a reason.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e7b4a79-201a-49b6-9cb1-99fd0572e909>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: PRO 26:17
Text: He that passeth by, and meddleth with strife belonging not to him, is like one that taketh a dog by the ears.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a818740-aff7-491c-8609-263025678794>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: PRO 26:18
Text: As a mad man who casteth firebrands, arrows, and death,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e29e4238-da3f-46de-b583-5b7fa8893323>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PRO 26:19
Text: So is the man that deceiveth his neighbour, and saith, Am not I in sport?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2d50d5a-4cf1-4722-83b8-fdfb0e66dd18>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PRO 26:20
Text: Where no wood is, there the fire goeth out: so where there is no talebearer, the strife ceaseth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:308fa4bb-8890-42e9-9e18-8fe4158b81e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PRO 26:21
Text: As coals are to burning coals, and wood to fire; so is a contentious man to kindle strife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74a35bad-8a7e-4dcb-8621-757e1be31e7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PRO 26:22
Text: The words of a talebearer are as wounds, and they go down into the innermost parts of the belly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f21f1b4-ecf3-4565-a0cf-a90d1be30558>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 26:23
Text: Burning lips and a wicked heart are like a potsherd covered with silver dross.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b9f7906-7cf4-473b-afa7-04ad01376d1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PRO 26:24
Text: He that hateth dissembleth with his lips, and layeth up deceit within him;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b69bddf0-60bb-481a-b2a7-77dfeff66302>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 26:25
Text: When he speaketh fair, believe him not: for there are seven abominations in his heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cb133ce-6fce-48f1-9a2f-1883b4cbb251>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PRO 26:26
Text: Whose hatred is covered by deceit, his wickedness shall be shewed before the whole congregation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe25fe48-0499-43b0-91bd-3cbe0c2b72c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PRO 26:27
Text: Whoso diggeth a pit shall fall therein: and he that rolleth a stone, it will return upon him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/26/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7bcc9b05-90e2-4862-ac4e-c6d4ec92bb4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PRO 26:28
Text: A lying tongue hateth those that are afflicted by it; and a flattering mouth worketh ruin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e29e245-0aa3-4c81-87f5-a272bd8e9f33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 27:1
Text: Boast not thyself of to morrow; for thou knowest not what a day may bring forth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3eb7802e-484b-463c-ad77-972d2350705c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 27:2
Text: Let another man praise thee, and not thine own mouth; a stranger, and not thine own lips.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9aded874-9187-417f-b65d-561b73f40ac2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 27:3
Text: A stone is heavy, and the sand weighty; but a fool’s wrath is heavier than them both.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb9c9348-c023-490c-9c83-b37a8ddb5642>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 27:4
Text: Wrath is cruel, and anger is outrageous; but who is able to stand before envy?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c49cf9e7-ea9c-41b9-8db5-5c031cbc5558>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 66

Reference: PRO 27:5
Text: Open rebuke is better than secret love.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d812fe99-b5cd-4591-95f1-17c39fe25912>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 27:6
Text: Faithful are the wounds of a friend; but the kisses of an enemy are deceitful.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbd94769-6da8-4738-a4fd-7de09ba2e92b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 27:7
Text: The full soul loatheth an honeycomb; but to the hungry soul every bitter thing is sweet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a3c4e3f-9799-4441-adcf-3b94f4e1c404>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PRO 27:8
Text: As a bird that wandereth from her nest, so is a man that wandereth from his place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84884d2e-4327-4bd6-8a55-6e2adc80b66e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PRO 27:9
Text: Ointment and perfume rejoice the heart: so doth the sweetness of a man’s friend by hearty counsel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9192f5f7-0aed-40f0-be1e-d375ecd826a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: PRO 27:10
Text: Thine own friend, and thy father’s friend, forsake not; neither go into thy brother’s house in the day of thy calamity: for better is a neighbour that is near than a brother far off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64e8f1ea-d9b7-4251-8e6e-071c9489b1d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PRO 27:11
Text: My son, be wise, and make my heart glad, that I may answer him that reproacheth me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23ba24fd-f16f-4b5f-8e60-f2ce50e7c726>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 27:12
Text: A prudent man foreseeth the evil, and hideth himself; but the simple pass on, and are punished.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f09f7135-4b23-4acf-b8b2-7cbc147b8b34>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PRO 27:13
Text: Take his garment that is surety for a stranger, and take a pledge of him for a strange woman.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c90f828-7f2d-4676-bfa4-21e30fd6f08c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: PRO 27:14
Text: He that blesseth his friend with a loud voice, rising early in the morning, it shall be counted a curse to him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e90589a6-cc5e-4f91-a758-0ee48157313d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PRO 27:15
Text: A continual dropping in a very rainy day and a contentious woman are alike.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c01c8aa2-1523-4e2e-982e-01ed98380de6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PRO 27:16
Text: Whosoever hideth her hideth the wind, and the ointment of his right hand, which bewrayeth itself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fc38eed-fcd1-4292-b257-13c75a1bbe6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PRO 27:17
Text: Iron sharpeneth iron; so a man sharpeneth the countenance of his friend.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4678eca9-3816-40b2-ad39-ea1ca9021e77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PRO 27:18
Text: Whoso keepeth the fig tree shall eat the fruit thereof: so he that waiteth on his master shall be honoured.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bbc15763-0a43-47a7-a9db-eb5bda20732b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PRO 27:19
Text: As in water face answereth to face, so the heart of man to man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c752c5ad-6fb8-4548-9382-baedcfed4af8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 27:20
Text: Hell and destruction are never full; so the eyes of man are never satisfied.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ccae2d81-33f0-4ab3-916c-21689f544f75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PRO 27:21
Text: As the fining pot for silver, and the furnace for gold; so is a man to his praise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfa2004f-84c6-4baa-a2a8-47413210e1e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: PRO 27:22
Text: Though thou shouldest bray a fool in a mortar among wheat with a pestle, yet will not his foolishness depart from him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa0b9487-2cc2-46e0-9645-012390d44a62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 27:23
Text: Be thou diligent to know the state of thy flocks, and look well to thy herds.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6810208-e0b2-4189-bdb0-e980c65d23af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PRO 27:24
Text: For riches are not for ever: and doth the crown endure to every generation?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c20b97e8-b6c4-4160-91f5-44a01ec6ada0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PRO 27:25
Text: The hay appeareth, and the tender grass sheweth itself, and herbs of the mountains are gathered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be3c81e3-ca73-45d6-9b69-f986f4965e84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PRO 27:26
Text: The lambs are for thy clothing, and the goats are the price of the field.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/27/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:191c47c6-6dca-48b6-9006-35fb9441d6fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: PRO 27:27
Text: And thou shalt have goats’ milk enough for thy food, for the food of thy household, and for the maintenance for thy maidens.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4659985f-e855-40e5-ba05-19e33b93c801>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PRO 28:1
Text: The wicked flee when no man pursueth: but the righteous are bold as a lion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8ad80a6-06b8-4c3d-8cc4-3f0deb2fcb71>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: PRO 28:2
Text: For the transgression of a land many are the princes thereof: but by a man of understanding and knowledge the state thereof shall be prolonged.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:385145ba-9694-4034-a048-706f2fa01334>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PRO 28:3
Text: A poor man that oppresseth the poor is like a sweeping rain which leaveth no food.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddd8d862-a743-48eb-a874-bfd8df11c4aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 28:4
Text: They that forsake the law praise the wicked: but such as keep the law contend with them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71259657-0ed8-4850-bee3-2160b9981593>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PRO 28:5
Text: Evil men understand not judgment: but they that seek the LORD understand all things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6655bc5-68ad-48ca-ba51-677b320d7e21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PRO 28:6
Text: Better is the poor that walketh in his uprightness, than he that is perverse in his ways, though he be rich.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb3b86dc-6f49-43d0-8bee-8e55fd32b746>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PRO 28:7
Text: Whoso keepeth the law is a wise son: but he that is a companion of riotous men shameth his father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2301deb-4995-483a-808d-cdda13a32ea5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: PRO 28:8
Text: He that by usury and unjust gain increaseth his substance, he shall gather it for him that will pity the poor.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0f4d581-9ce0-4812-af92-2629165679da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 28:9
Text: He that turneth away his ear from hearing the law, even his prayer shall be abomination.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97230b81-7a16-4bb6-bf0c-40b399b2be4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: PRO 28:10
Text: Whoso causeth the righteous to go astray in an evil way, he shall fall himself into his own pit: but the upright shall have good things in possession.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:320877c9-d66f-4586-9dc9-024a79d0fc9f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PRO 28:11
Text: The rich man is wise in his own conceit; but the poor that hath understanding searcheth him out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fdec83bb-2e05-46f1-a8b8-c8dcbef6fc68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 28:12
Text: When righteous men do rejoice, there is great glory: but when the wicked rise, a man is hidden.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1b7e691-7461-45ba-b28d-859d1078cbbe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PRO 28:13
Text: He that covereth his sins shall not prosper: but whoso confesseth and forsaketh them shall have mercy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62bfa934-5905-470c-8bb4-c7246df664aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PRO 28:14
Text: Happy is the man that feareth alway: but he that hardeneth his heart shall fall into mischief.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b87b361-4e9e-409b-97b7-d3b63693fd82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PRO 28:15
Text: As a roaring lion, and a ranging bear; so is a wicked ruler over the poor people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5da54e21-01da-4b3c-b5af-393c3d962ed5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: PRO 28:16
Text: The prince that wanteth understanding is also a great oppressor: but he that hateth covetousness shall prolong his days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13fd830d-3dd7-40eb-bd70-0c6546408423>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PRO 28:17
Text: A man that doeth violence to the blood of any person shall flee to the pit; let no man stay him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a73cdb24-7fa0-4f2c-8ac4-5a214cd429ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 28:18
Text: Whoso walketh uprightly shall be saved: but he that is perverse in his ways shall fall at once.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05999708-60fe-42bc-b7c7-666d3c226044>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: PRO 28:19
Text: He that tilleth his land shall have plenty of bread: but he that followeth after vain persons shall have poverty enough.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f791340f-ef80-4be8-a264-93bcdeafd44c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PRO 28:20
Text: A faithful man shall abound with blessings: but he that maketh haste to be rich shall not be innocent.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:060000ae-e1a5-441f-9aa8-22f542e3e62e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PRO 28:21
Text: To have respect of persons is not good: for for a piece of bread that man will transgress.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7aac79ce-232e-4b9e-a5df-eb19c07df56a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PRO 28:22
Text: He that hasteth to be rich hath an evil eye, and considereth not that poverty shall come upon him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7df5caff-39fb-4818-8711-c81c6ab12bc0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PRO 28:23
Text: He that rebuketh a man afterwards shall find more favour than he that flattereth with the tongue.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1c58713-155e-42d4-97a8-1cd4adb0b670>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: PRO 28:24
Text: Whoso robbeth his father or his mother, and saith, It is no transgression; the same is the companion of a destroyer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e34a45f-d8e0-4bac-8747-218222eed0d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PRO 28:25
Text: He that is of a proud heart stirreth up strife: but he that putteth his trust in the LORD shall be made fat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:644b6d69-2862-4f70-a522-2b743676f8e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PRO 28:26
Text: He that trusteth in his own heart is a fool: but whoso walketh wisely, he shall be delivered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d66a6e07-9e0d-4c55-a94d-7bc2015a9f0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PRO 28:27
Text: He that giveth unto the poor shall not lack: but he that hideth his eyes shall have many a curse.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/28/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04de3eb3-bb97-460f-bde7-1bed3d224449>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 28:28
Text: When the wicked rise, men hide themselves: but when they perish, the righteous increase.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97b417ba-48ec-48d4-a098-52517975f17f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PRO 29:1
Text: He, that being often reproved hardeneth his neck, shall suddenly be destroyed, and that without remedy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3a84bd3-18d3-4a6f-83a5-43a7999e5719>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PRO 29:2
Text: When the righteous are in authority, the people rejoice: but when the wicked beareth rule, the people mourn.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d754bdc2-f523-4239-8ad7-3c3a21c79052>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: PRO 29:3
Text: Whoso loveth wisdom rejoiceth his father: but he that keepeth company with harlots spendeth his substance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f05e9cc-f5af-4cfb-a148-941b883fd866>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 29:4
Text: The king by judgment establisheth the land: but he that receiveth gifts overthroweth it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77f1b296-3837-4e06-977c-05040b217feb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PRO 29:5
Text: A man that flattereth his neighbour spreadeth a net for his feet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bedc96e-b676-46bb-a491-4c2c9cbcac3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PRO 29:6
Text: In the transgression of an evil man there is a snare: but the righteous doth sing and rejoice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1424d3eb-54d6-41f4-b9b8-37a7f92523c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 29:7
Text: The righteous considereth the cause of the poor: but the wicked regardeth not to know it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:086cea70-2297-4a44-9377-26a47ab54370>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PRO 29:8
Text: Scornful men bring a city into a snare: but wise men turn away wrath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:164ee351-2b29-474a-9549-dfc1403ca35b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 29:9
Text: If a wise man contendeth with a foolish man, whether he rage or laugh, there is no rest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51425e6f-4ecd-44fe-86eb-d966fd8c7bd1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PRO 29:10
Text: The bloodthirsty hate the upright: but the just seek his soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db56a2ab-866f-4fd7-95ac-adec3bb9818a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PRO 29:11
Text: A fool uttereth all his mind: but a wise man keepeth it in till afterwards.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8479a25-3068-4d17-929d-7b9e65d0a644>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PRO 29:12
Text: If a ruler hearken to lies, all his servants are wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6b5432c-ddc5-4ca1-af93-c71ca30b8c93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PRO 29:13
Text: The poor and the deceitful man meet together: the LORD lighteneth both their eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46349c4e-7162-4aa6-a1c6-0f86e00a3d01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 29:14
Text: The king that faithfully judgeth the poor, his throne shall be established for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1dab619c-44e7-4bea-9d3f-92f8810afb43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PRO 29:15
Text: The rod and reproof give wisdom: but a child left to himself bringeth his mother to shame.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71f2ca47-72dc-4c66-8a84-b8c0abd7bd3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PRO 29:16
Text: When the wicked are multiplied, transgression increaseth: but the righteous shall see their fall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfd62231-d730-4e0f-96e0-979efc706149>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PRO 29:17
Text: Correct thy son, and he shall give thee rest; yea, he shall give delight unto thy soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa6b6ad3-a956-45f8-bd42-16934dac700f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 29:18
Text: Where there is no vision, the people perish: but he that keepeth the law, happy is he.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b181e43-d755-4519-a729-ec985d0d7287>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 29:19
Text: A servant will not be corrected by words: for though he understand he will not answer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6bd078f-1f62-4f9f-b6ec-5894b9da4652>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 29:20
Text: Seest thou a man that is hasty in his words? there is more hope of a fool than of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6dd45b73-3668-4536-b48e-e1a6d36d3c9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PRO 29:21
Text: He that delicately bringeth up his servant from a child shall have him become his son at the length.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a2e9b17-3e7e-4668-88a3-71ca625babb2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 29:22
Text: An angry man stirreth up strife, and a furious man aboundeth in transgression.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41ba6049-03b9-4b61-976d-0679a668bd00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PRO 29:23
Text: A man’s pride shall bring him low: but honour shall uphold the humble in spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9931f534-8a91-4a4d-85e0-bd1db7a58256>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PRO 29:24
Text: Whoso is partner with a thief hateth his own soul: he heareth cursing, and bewrayeth it not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:846b6e43-abf7-4cee-9353-847bff0be343>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 29:25
Text: The fear of man bringeth a snare: but whoso putteth his trust in the LORD shall be safe.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1627361-0134-4047-8d78-558b6bd0deae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PRO 29:26
Text: Many seek the ruler’s favour; but every man’s judgment cometh from the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/29/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88fc5b43-caf1-4896-ab35-4b37454b77ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: PRO 29:27
Text: An unjust man is an abomination to the just: and he that is upright in the way is abomination to the wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7bfa418c-d35d-490f-87bf-9353eb4c7c94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PRO 30:1
Text: The words of Agur the son of Jakeh, even the prophecy: the man spake unto Ithiel, even unto Ithiel and Ucal,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:439a037b-7612-48eb-8b59-3b9b4cfef8f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PRO 30:2
Text: Surely I am more brutish than any man, and have not the understanding of a man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d280b06-d8c2-4d4c-ba90-2e8f33a06178>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PRO 30:3
Text: I neither learned wisdom, nor have the knowledge of the holy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3a20dd0-1ea3-4b40-9b16-0ce7b91a0b41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: PRO 30:4
Text: Who hath ascended up into heaven, or descended? who hath gathered the wind in his fists? who hath bound the waters in a garment? who hath established all the ends of the earth? what is his name, and what is his son’s name, if thou canst tell?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6a5f8f9-4339-4cb7-9ee1-3023869942df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 30:5
Text: Every word of God is pure: he is a shield unto them that put their trust in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03b93265-08d9-4f1d-a412-ea4da87f51bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: PRO 30:6
Text: Add thou not unto his words, lest he reprove thee, and thou be found a liar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0dc6c03a-d83d-4cc3-869a-913b0ca2abf9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PRO 30:7
Text: Two things have I required of thee; deny me them not before I die:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be9d0ac0-6c03-469e-9f49-0b47c3745fed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PRO 30:8
Text: Remove far from me vanity and lies: give me neither poverty nor riches; feed me with food convenient for me:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59e09fd9-e29c-4319-b316-64bc0c860f87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: PRO 30:9
Text: Lest I be full, and deny thee, and say, Who is the LORD? or lest I be poor, and steal, and take the name of my God in vain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f39fa9a-d115-48a6-a643-e0698c31b7f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PRO 30:10
Text: Accuse not a servant unto his master, lest he curse thee, and thou be found guilty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3287022c-93ad-49b3-b16b-69eebb9ffd4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PRO 30:11
Text: There is a generation that curseth their father, and doth not bless their mother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d283288-0ce2-45d2-89be-ac7fdf34b9c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: PRO 30:12
Text: There is a generation that are pure in their own eyes, and yet is not washed from their filthiness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f0e602c-700e-47e9-a197-45f05bbb9ff6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PRO 30:13
Text: There is a generation, O how lofty are their eyes! and their eyelids are lifted up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ed47dc2-3983-4868-8982-b06a8e57a05f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: PRO 30:14
Text: There is a generation, whose teeth are as swords, and their jaw teeth as knives, to devour the poor from off the earth, and the needy from among men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2cc3460e-a931-4d6c-a385-ad4812cdb9a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: PRO 30:15
Text: The horseleach hath two daughters, crying, Give, give. There are three things that are never satisfied, yea, four things say not, It is enough:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a9a9a07-f6b3-40e1-8d1a-06c3b4e11521>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: PRO 30:16
Text: The grave; and the barren womb; the earth that is not filled with water; and the fire that saith not, It is enough.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0889957f-b688-412b-8690-daa9c708ef24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: PRO 30:17
Text: The eye that mocketh at his father, and despiseth to obey his mother, the ravens of the valley shall pick it out, and the young eagles shall eat it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a2c8863-de2c-4184-b088-4c288d21907c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PRO 30:18
Text: There be three things which are too wonderful for me, yea, four which I know not:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c92ae03-e867-41c3-beca-b6fbe6f6a53e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: PRO 30:19
Text: The way of an eagle in the air; the way of a serpent upon a rock; the way of a ship in the midst of the sea; and the way of a man with a maid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8199a398-4ebf-4800-8107-09f347aa6653>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: PRO 30:20
Text: Such is the way of an adulterous woman; she eateth, and wipeth her mouth, and saith, I have done no wickedness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1068bc7f-0f51-4e41-a855-4802f93d7c52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 30:21
Text: For three things the earth is disquieted, and for four which it cannot bear:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5214274-fb09-47dc-ad30-7aac56fab62b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: PRO 30:22
Text: For a servant when he reigneth; and a fool when he is filled with meat;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b39b330c-9b55-42e4-9f81-33b8db3e998b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PRO 30:23
Text: For an odious woman when she is married; and an handmaid that is heir to her mistress.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52797676-5cea-4b6d-8497-d5efc72dab45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PRO 30:24
Text: There be four things which are little upon the earth, but they are exceeding wise:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fc26629-abaa-4194-ab36-dd0ee19daf5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 30:25
Text: The ants are a people not strong, yet they prepare their meat in the summer;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3aaeeac4-f72c-4838-b557-bfa2a284db85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PRO 30:26
Text: The conies are but a feeble folk, yet make they their houses in the rocks;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20a3f714-27ab-4fdb-a9cb-ccc84b2a1825>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PRO 30:27
Text: The locusts have no king, yet go they forth all of them by bands;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c91e5f38-1f91-4377-9516-8b585a1eab7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: PRO 30:28
Text: The spider taketh hold with her hands, and is in kings’ palaces.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa34246f-97dd-4372-ae0d-746243e93409>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: PRO 30:29
Text: There be three things which go well, yea, four are comely in going:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6839143a-8d76-409e-94e6-50b8e9b316bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PRO 30:30
Text: A lion which is strongest among beasts, and turneth not away for any;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4db89ccd-0b21-4f8e-b386-fc13451a6bed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 30:31
Text: A greyhound; an he goat also; and a king, against whom there is no rising up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e9d402c-4161-4a5b-a372-561e0181ccee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: PRO 30:32
Text: If thou hast done foolishly in lifting up thyself, or if thou hast thought evil, lay thine hand upon thy mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/30/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15ad6aa3-3aa1-4cb2-84ca-f6204c7760d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: PRO 30:33
Text: Surely the churning of milk bringeth forth butter, and the wringing of the nose bringeth forth blood: so the forcing of wrath bringeth forth strife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f14d95f-f85e-459f-9513-bb2874047fd2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PRO 31:1
Text: The words of king Lemuel, the prophecy that his mother taught him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:403e8006-6bf6-4e48-ac79-5d71b05c4943>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PRO 31:2
Text: What, my son? and what, the son of my womb? and what, the son of my vows?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0494a429-95e8-40d7-8877-4401a0ae5fec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PRO 31:3
Text: Give not thy strength unto women, nor thy ways to that which destroyeth kings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a51e0e7-01bd-4673-bc31-6e5f8da68cb9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PRO 31:4
Text: It is not for kings, O Lemuel, it is not for kings to drink wine; nor for princes strong drink:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbfde217-8eba-420f-8ac6-d6fc08af3be3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PRO 31:5
Text: Lest they drink, and forget the law, and pervert the judgment of any of the afflicted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24d8938b-a2c9-45a6-a49a-858b08f1fa72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: PRO 31:6
Text: Give strong drink unto him that is ready to perish, and wine unto those that be of heavy hearts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7939c676-ffca-4f12-b23c-74057f9ef99a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PRO 31:7
Text: Let him drink, and forget his poverty, and remember his misery no more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c9ee5b5-3745-4aec-a261-7fc04a0217ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 31:8
Text: Open thy mouth for the dumb in the cause of all such as are appointed to destruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b12a399d-5852-4e43-beda-de5548a8107d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 31:9
Text: Open thy mouth, judge righteously, and plead the cause of the poor and needy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:734c7dfc-3605-40f8-b9f4-ed4417a5871e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PRO 31:10
Text: Who can find a virtuous woman? for her price is far above rubies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:076aa427-f54f-4188-a9af-ad6e9564c7a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PRO 31:11
Text: The heart of her husband doth safely trust in her, so that he shall have no need of spoil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b290c3d-1e9d-408a-af60-0866dd6dbd82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PRO 31:12
Text: She will do him good and not evil all the days of her life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e85c4dbd-732b-469e-9107-bceb4810765b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PRO 31:13
Text: She seeketh wool, and flax, and worketh willingly with her hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48faeafd-d864-488d-8099-8590fde8540c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PRO 31:14
Text: She is like the merchants’ ships; she bringeth her food from afar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79f1fb31-fd41-4819-8c98-95da70578f19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PRO 31:15
Text: She riseth also while it is yet night, and giveth meat to her household, and a portion to her maidens.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f170124c-287a-4140-843d-1b73b57538e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PRO 31:16
Text: She considereth a field, and buyeth it: with the fruit of her hands she planteth a vineyard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0205aa9-8360-4299-a6ef-f6f4b3406290>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PRO 31:17
Text: She girdeth her loins with strength, and strengtheneth her arms.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0e12f1d-a6d5-4be6-8e02-d616be061761>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PRO 31:18
Text: She perceiveth that her merchandise is good: her candle goeth not out by night.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24d563d1-7414-4dba-8c4b-57867e98b589>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PRO 31:19
Text: She layeth her hands to the spindle, and her hands hold the distaff.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de7eccf1-d260-469b-b9b1-327a688fcea7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PRO 31:20
Text: She stretcheth out her hand to the poor; yea, she reacheth forth her hands to the needy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2ef4b3b-a315-4b41-a563-11bb8db47ee0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PRO 31:21
Text: She is not afraid of the snow for her household: for all her household are clothed with scarlet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc7cbcbb-c780-4644-af52-afb1ab60d906>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PRO 31:22
Text: She maketh herself coverings of tapestry; her clothing is silk and purple.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2054ae43-5557-4afb-b88b-cc251c87d23e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PRO 31:23
Text: Her husband is known in the gates, when he sitteth among the elders of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:225f71d0-badd-47c1-8bd6-5cbc769ee7c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PRO 31:24
Text: She maketh fine linen, and selleth it; and delivereth girdles unto the merchant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:272e1ba9-3677-4f98-a9c7-0e9dd3675e73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 31:25
Text: Strength and honour are her clothing; and she shall rejoice in time to come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5aad961e-89d1-42b4-9b65-b979b7e082ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PRO 31:26
Text: She openeth her mouth with wisdom; and in her tongue is the law of kindness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b7fa5f2-431e-4254-b3db-f147edd786ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: PRO 31:27
Text: She looketh well to the ways of her household, and eateth not the bread of idleness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd3f62c7-cbaa-4c47-9d60-b9fd9df48781>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PRO 31:28
Text: Her children arise up, and call her blessed; her husband also, and he praiseth her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8972225-484e-44c4-9833-c4a7dbc35907>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PRO 31:29
Text: Many daughters have done virtuously, but thou excellest them all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6efa5c55-4b3a-4d46-9d4c-88afffa8ba6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: PRO 31:30
Text: Favour is deceitful, and beauty is vain: but a woman that feareth the LORD, she shall be praised.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PRO/31/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d736343-f426-4c81-93e1-451ddc5c36a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PRO 31:31
Text: Give her of the fruit of her hands; and let her own works praise her in the gates.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d3df2c5-4b6c-4242-ab50-e5e3eb0cdc9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: ECC 1:1
Text: The words of the Preacher, the son of David, king in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ec07bda-bd01-4c39-86af-f914c37ded54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: ECC 1:2
Text: Vanity of vanities, saith the Preacher, vanity of vanities; all is vanity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abf61951-3066-4729-a036-2211e0480ca2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: ECC 1:3
Text: What profit hath a man of all his labour which he taketh under the sun?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0d8902e-6813-48e9-8da5-073ac32962c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: ECC 1:4
Text: One generation passeth away, and another generation cometh: but the earth abideth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f7a86c8-8fda-4573-8d7b-8ce4fecc5a62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: ECC 1:5
Text: The sun also ariseth, and the sun goeth down, and hasteth to his place where he arose.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a145642-fc42-4428-9108-ee2329c674d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: ECC 1:6
Text: The wind goeth toward the south, and turneth about unto the north; it whirleth about continually, and the wind returneth again according to his circuits.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e65af18-ed00-404c-9b3d-7a552cd028ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: ECC 1:7
Text: All the rivers run into the sea; yet the sea is not full; unto the place from whence the rivers come, thither they return again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81a8e077-250d-43a5-a3f1-eee1b1e69ef2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: ECC 1:8
Text: All things are full of labour; man cannot utter it: the eye is not satisfied with seeing, nor the ear filled with hearing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66aba2d9-2b0c-4535-b789-fa610989cf33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: ECC 1:9
Text: The thing that hath been, it is that which shall be; and that which is done is that which shall be done: and there is no new thing under the sun.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0cdef5b-53d0-47f6-b46b-1ca2b8a2a956>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: ECC 1:10
Text: Is there any thing whereof it may be said, See, this is new? it hath been already of old time, which was before us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:074ffe4a-a171-44ca-970b-7a5dd38a4353>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: ECC 1:11
Text: There is no remembrance of former things; neither shall there be any remembrance of things that are to come with those that shall come after.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3689ae9b-a44b-4c0d-b5eb-80b73d69bc2d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: ECC 1:12
Text: I the Preacher was king over Israel in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2007bba-6bd9-4ec2-a5e2-049d308481f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: ECC 1:13
Text: And I gave my heart to seek and search out by wisdom concerning all things that are done under heaven: this sore travail hath God given to the sons of man to be exercised therewith.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfb81758-a42f-4e0a-add4-aecd80035900>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: ECC 1:14
Text: I have seen all the works that are done under the sun; and, behold, all is vanity and vexation of spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9bccf58-591c-4827-b5e6-1f144e8c49a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: ECC 1:15
Text: That which is crooked cannot be made straight: and that which is wanting cannot be numbered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e06f80be-54bf-410f-865c-8d58c4f0f707>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: ECC 1:16
Text: I communed with mine own heart, saying, Lo, I am come to great estate, and have gotten more wisdom than all they that have been before me in Jerusalem: yea, my heart had great experience of wisdom and knowledge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34475b8c-c391-4af9-a123-97a5073c24a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: ECC 1:17
Text: And I gave my heart to know wisdom, and to know madness and folly: I perceived that this also is vexation of spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0387a9b9-15f7-455c-9ccf-98054574f593>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: ECC 1:18
Text: For in much wisdom is much grief: and he that increaseth knowledge increaseth sorrow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77fb850c-5c07-4a97-9095-cf524f0a6917>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: ECC 2:1
Text: I said in mine heart, Go to now, I will prove thee with mirth, therefore enjoy pleasure: and, behold, this also is vanity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fbc35be-32bf-40db-b40f-8bb98be7ed9e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: ECC 2:2
Text: I said of laughter, It is mad: and of mirth, What doeth it?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed4c01ca-5160-4739-a91f-7d154236a391>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: ECC 2:3
Text: I sought in mine heart to give myself unto wine, yet acquainting mine heart with wisdom; and to lay hold on folly, till I might see what was that good for the sons of men, which they should do under the heaven all the days of their life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f68af653-2b94-45c5-b3ba-83d32f7aaeb8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: ECC 2:4
Text: I made me great works; I builded me houses; I planted me vineyards:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a432bf7-a7f2-4923-9ce0-e4429c35d348>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: ECC 2:5
Text: I made me gardens and orchards, and I planted trees in them of all kind of fruits:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85b74c88-b2ce-4a0b-af02-cd48d6d45617>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: ECC 2:6
Text: I made me pools of water, to water therewith the wood that bringeth forth trees:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d8cfaa2-b1f7-4273-a675-1f9dfeafb97b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: ECC 2:7
Text: I got me servants and maidens, and had servants born in my house; also I had great possessions of great and small cattle above all that were in Jerusalem before me:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7ae927c-ae68-4f7a-a647-d100d971e47d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: ECC 2:8
Text: I gathered me also silver and gold, and the peculiar treasure of kings and of the provinces: I gat me men singers and women singers, and the delights of the sons of men, as musical instruments, and that of all sorts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3228a69-6be9-4433-b0b9-1a1b686b0bea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: ECC 2:9
Text: So I was great, and increased more than all that were before me in Jerusalem: also my wisdom remained with me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f114ba8-e315-4cf2-a405-1311eaeccc6d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: ECC 2:10
Text: And whatsoever mine eyes desired I kept not from them, I withheld not my heart from any joy; for my heart rejoiced in all my labour: and this was my portion of all my labour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c56ad5d-9d50-49c6-9661-8986819a785a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: ECC 2:11
Text: Then I looked on all the works that my hands had wrought, and on the labour that I had laboured to do: and, behold, all was vanity and vexation of spirit, and there was no profit under the sun.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76bcf8c9-9fb3-48f3-bcdb-866a16d16166>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: ECC 2:12
Text: And I turned myself to behold wisdom, and madness, and folly: for what can the man do that cometh after the king? even that which hath been already done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e43d43b-7963-4d8f-b9f1-bac6115507bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: ECC 2:13
Text: Then I saw that wisdom excelleth folly, as far as light excelleth darkness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6a6c63d-f7b4-406d-ad11-968bf873c324>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: ECC 2:14
Text: The wise man’s eyes are in his head; but the fool walketh in darkness: and I myself perceived also that one event happeneth to them all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fd6721a-3eee-4034-9502-3a16945f670d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: ECC 2:15
Text: Then said I in my heart, As it happeneth to the fool, so it happeneth even to me; and why was I then more wise? Then I said in my heart, that this also is vanity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2cb28025-d853-41ca-817f-a9fb552d0d3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: ECC 2:16
Text: For there is no remembrance of the wise more than of the fool for ever; seeing that which now is in the days to come shall all be forgotten. And how dieth the wise man? as the fool.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0cf43ad-1916-42c1-b8a3-5940be844b96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: ECC 2:17
Text: Therefore I hated life; because the work that is wrought under the sun is grievous unto me: for all is vanity and vexation of spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2449fbe1-d81f-4257-a854-aa2f71e03c33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: ECC 2:18
Text: Yea, I hated all my labour which I had taken under the sun: because I should leave it unto the man that shall be after me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1eee6d72-bb45-4272-a139-0fb7e8cf4130>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: ECC 2:19
Text: And who knoweth whether he shall be a wise man or a fool? yet shall he have rule over all my labour wherein I have laboured, and wherein I have shewed myself wise under the sun. This is also vanity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2079815a-437c-424f-bc1d-600cfe6b75eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: ECC 2:20
Text: Therefore I went about to cause my heart to despair of all the labour which I took under the sun.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f510a9ba-6dd8-4691-be16-2f9325f865a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: ECC 2:21
Text: For there is a man whose labour is in wisdom, and in knowledge, and in equity; yet to a man that hath not laboured therein shall he leave it for his portion. This also is vanity and a great evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81c8ac33-55c7-4e22-b892-da68dac2ba27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: ECC 2:22
Text: For what hath man of all his labour, and of the vexation of his heart, wherein he hath laboured under the sun?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:402a52ce-0da3-4252-a7b2-ddffea71404a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: ECC 2:23
Text: For all his days are sorrows, and his travail grief; yea, his heart taketh not rest in the night. This is also vanity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7601e20-459f-4f89-86bd-45de8b1865cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: ECC 2:24
Text: There is nothing better for a man, than that he should eat and drink, and that he should make his soul enjoy good in his labour. This also I saw, that it was from the hand of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35dba0f0-45c6-461d-9939-2aa6246b0c4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: ECC 2:25
Text: For who can eat, or who else can hasten hereunto, more than I?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/2/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f845309b-3c83-4733-b38f-ba0c01516967>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: ECC 2:26
Text: For God giveth to a man that is good in his sight wisdom, and knowledge, and joy: but to the sinner he giveth travail, to gather and to heap up, that he may give to him that is good before God. This also is vanity and vexation of spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5adab458-ae17-4ef4-86b8-d3a893e65918>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: ECC 3:1
Text: To every thing there is a season, and a time to every purpose under the heaven:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8831663-ca99-45f1-a93f-4785e641d5d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: ECC 3:2
Text: A time to be born, and a time to die; a time to plant, and a time to pluck up that which is planted;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1e514b5-fbc3-496a-95e5-b00890d4c305>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: ECC 3:3
Text: A time to kill, and a time to heal; a time to break down, and a time to build up;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7f6a898-651d-4730-8326-a84ead09c4d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: ECC 3:4
Text: A time to weep, and a time to laugh; a time to mourn, and a time to dance;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1bb0ba3f-bcab-47e6-8b0b-3ab81bc80638>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: ECC 3:5
Text: A time to cast away stones, and a time to gather stones together; a time to embrace, and a time to refrain from embracing;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b2df826-f5b3-4836-94ee-55bc02bfaec2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: ECC 3:6
Text: A time to get, and a time to lose; a time to keep, and a time to cast away;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6febf5df-263e-44d2-82b6-3d3e9fc9863c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: ECC 3:7
Text: A time to rend, and a time to sew; a time to keep silence, and a time to speak;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5af595c7-6b46-412d-bcc3-6ec2a4be6fd1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: ECC 3:8
Text: A time to love, and a time to hate; a time of war, and a time of peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e07663f2-67d9-4a26-9e5b-f81215e978c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: ECC 3:9
Text: What profit hath he that worketh in that wherein he laboureth?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:962ea6e4-acfc-4bf9-b004-155e9e2ef51e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: ECC 3:10
Text: I have seen the travail, which God hath given to the sons of men to be exercised in it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41259012-3baa-4a7b-8251-39f07490513c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: ECC 3:11
Text: He hath made every thing beautiful in his time: also he hath set the world in their heart, so that no man can find out the work that God maketh from the beginning to the end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0cddc066-07d6-4e05-a4ce-cff39e0e7311>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: ECC 3:12
Text: I know that there is no good in them, but for a man to rejoice, and to do good in his life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34772650-6b4d-44cc-8ae6-1cc99b22dfc9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: ECC 3:13
Text: And also that every man should eat and drink, and enjoy the good of all his labour, it is the gift of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d568b1fb-49e0-465e-8bdd-7650edff03ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: ECC 3:14
Text: I know that, whatsoever God doeth, it shall be for ever: nothing can be put to it, nor any thing taken from it: and God doeth it, that men should fear before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1631a570-88fe-41ef-aee8-6e38d5240648>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: ECC 3:15
Text: That which hath been is now; and that which is to be hath already been; and God requireth that which is past.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:465dc293-99f2-44a4-b35c-73826b4a539a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: ECC 3:16
Text: And moreover I saw under the sun the place of judgment, that wickedness was there; and the place of righteousness, that iniquity was there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4abb374-9f1b-4d41-adf6-621ba7b99599>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: ECC 3:17
Text: I said in mine heart, God shall judge the righteous and the wicked: for there is a time there for every purpose and for every work.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e44a6692-fd9b-41ed-8866-34b39470ca73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: ECC 3:18
Text: I said in mine heart concerning the estate of the sons of men, that God might manifest them, and that they might see that they themselves are beasts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e83db55-85d6-4fff-a61e-8307d8ede142>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: ECC 3:19
Text: For that which befalleth the sons of men befalleth beasts; even one thing befalleth them: as the one dieth, so dieth the other; yea, they have all one breath; so that a man hath no preeminence above a beast: for all is vanity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/3/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ffdf71a-552e-40bb-a8fa-126a4e50810a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: ECC 3:20
Text: All go unto one place; all are of the dust, and all turn to dust again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/3/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10113b10-e37e-4363-a9a3-0a5fe6084abb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: ECC 3:21
Text: Who knoweth the spirit of man that goeth upward, and the spirit of the beast that goeth downward to the earth?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/3/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48628813-8b25-49e2-9a9c-d57f362576fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: ECC 3:22
Text: Wherefore I perceive that there is nothing better, than that a man should rejoice in his own works; for that is his portion: for who shall bring him to see what shall be after him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed51eafa-f438-4222-a847-56947cf609f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: ECC 4:1
Text: So I returned, and considered all the oppressions that are done under the sun: and behold the tears of such as were oppressed, and they had no comforter; and on the side of their oppressors there was power; but they had no comforter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f75f2e00-02a3-4b3a-a280-4ca45e8adea5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: ECC 4:2
Text: Wherefore I praised the dead which are already dead more than the living which are yet alive.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34d0cc9b-2123-4e35-9c29-cd2c72aff995>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: ECC 4:3
Text: Yea, better is he than both they, which hath not yet been, who hath not seen the evil work that is done under the sun.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f3087e5-b3a1-4007-b47a-9fb6b5393bec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: ECC 4:4
Text: Again, I considered all travail, and every right work, that for this a man is envied of his neighbour. This is also vanity and vexation of spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:efb490f3-643a-4a82-b2a8-c187dd04043d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: ECC 4:5
Text: The fool foldeth his hands together, and eateth his own flesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:912dd506-90a7-4cee-bde9-e84b7c1040fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: ECC 4:6
Text: Better is an handful with quietness, than both the hands full with travail and vexation of spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:958e0444-3cdb-4d53-bf62-a475f6b82a7a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: ECC 4:7
Text: Then I returned, and I saw vanity under the sun.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3092300d-c053-43f8-912b-9cbe2861ba39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 310

Reference: ECC 4:8
Text: There is one alone, and there is not a second; yea, he hath neither child nor brother: yet is there no end of all his labour; neither is his eye satisfied with riches; neither saith he, For whom do I labour, and bereave my soul of good? This is also vanity, yea, it is a sore travail.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c9d7494-53d6-4090-96ba-7e0652143d10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: ECC 4:9
Text: Two are better than one; because they have a good reward for their labour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffbe00fe-224c-4f15-a028-cfd8611463b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: ECC 4:10
Text: For if they fall, the one will lift up his fellow: but woe to him that is alone when he falleth; for he hath not another to help him up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27397f97-8dfa-427f-bdff-e942d2f198c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: ECC 4:11
Text: Again, if two lie together, then they have heat: but how can one be warm alone?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acce9104-0584-4c7b-bc2e-16fe4fc32b54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: ECC 4:12
Text: And if one prevail against him, two shall withstand him; and a threefold cord is not quickly broken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65aafbd4-7d73-44e3-a6d2-3410c7534cf4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: ECC 4:13
Text: Better is a poor and a wise child than an old and foolish king, who will no more be admonished.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f786762-99c7-44aa-a16f-8078fc1c07ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: ECC 4:14
Text: For out of prison he cometh to reign; whereas also he that is born in his kingdom becometh poor.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28075a82-b0c1-4a3a-9c22-4519e537cfde>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: ECC 4:15
Text: I considered all the living which walk under the sun, with the second child that shall stand up in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97ce4a28-1b0e-4518-bbff-70dfec5cac78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: ECC 4:16
Text: There is no end of all the people, even of all that have been before them: they also that come after shall not rejoice in him. Surely this also is vanity and vexation of spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c6addbf-31bb-4275-bb3e-ec0e80b648e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: ECC 5:1
Text: Keep thy foot when thou goest to the house of God, and be more ready to hear, than to give the sacrifice of fools: for they consider not that they do evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e152c62-01dd-470e-85e7-252f92c0bed3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: ECC 5:2
Text: Be not rash with thy mouth, and let not thine heart be hasty to utter any thing before God: for God is in heaven, and thou upon earth: therefore let thy words be few.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82cd5ea5-2aaf-4585-bd47-8afd2c54ee20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: ECC 5:3
Text: For a dream cometh through the multitude of business; and a fool’s voice is known by multitude of words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4dd4f8a6-c15b-4cff-8779-69601087eec7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: ECC 5:4
Text: When thou vowest a vow unto God, defer not to pay it; for he hath no pleasure in fools: pay that which thou hast vowed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:826d6a65-8566-4b66-8c3c-8e835f166624>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: ECC 5:5
Text: Better is it that thou shouldest not vow, than that thou shouldest vow and not pay.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:605b716a-b359-4d76-b545-af5018987c58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: ECC 5:6
Text: Suffer not thy mouth to cause thy flesh to sin; neither say thou before the angel, that it was an error: wherefore should God be angry at thy voice, and destroy the work of thine hands?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b38919a-6f21-4999-aa95-bdffea274533>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: ECC 5:7
Text: For in the multitude of dreams and many words there are also divers vanities: but fear thou God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49449c38-183e-4cd1-87dd-cad8e6834901>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: ECC 5:8
Text: If thou seest the oppression of the poor, and violent perverting of judgment and justice in a province, marvel not at the matter: for he that is higher than the highest regardeth; and there be higher than they.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5fbc981c-453d-42fd-8f1b-c198eca05531>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: ECC 5:9
Text: Moreover the profit of the earth is for all: the king himself is served by the field.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99172f7f-a47e-4240-aac1-22e0f5a9b802>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: ECC 5:10
Text: He that loveth silver shall not be satisfied with silver; nor he that loveth abundance with increase: this is also vanity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96f57bb6-4bea-465f-b749-19e97e1f9310>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: ECC 5:11
Text: When goods increase, they are increased that eat them: and what good is there to the owners thereof, saving the beholding of them with their eyes?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56bb9320-4ba1-4c79-9e97-f6142677caf5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: ECC 5:12
Text: The sleep of a labouring man is sweet, whether he eat little or much: but the abundance of the rich will not suffer him to sleep.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f266bce3-23fd-428d-9cf7-67b655f5e184>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: ECC 5:13
Text: There is a sore evil which I have seen under the sun, namely, riches kept for the owners thereof to their hurt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bfcac6e-7863-4177-8a63-14f2a766ba6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: ECC 5:14
Text: But those riches perish by evil travail: and he begetteth a son, and there is nothing in his hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33c89e2a-ccfa-43a8-8fae-1adbca65b410>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: ECC 5:15
Text: As he came forth of his mother’s womb, naked shall he return to go as he came, and shall take nothing of his labour, which he may carry away in his hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8af1f5f-85b1-477e-835c-7f664f41be07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: ECC 5:16
Text: And this also is a sore evil, that in all points as he came, so shall he go: and what profit hath he that hath laboured for the wind?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/5/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfc20762-6415-45d3-ae46-1fdc640e0992>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: ECC 5:17
Text: All his days also he eateth in darkness, and he hath much sorrow and wrath with his sickness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/5/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abc3e0f1-0110-4b4f-966c-5f68fc3f5a82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: ECC 5:18
Text: Behold that which I have seen: it is good and comely for one to eat and to drink, and to enjoy the good of all his labour that he taketh under the sun all the days of his life, which God giveth him: for it is his portion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/5/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89b4edd4-e132-4bf5-bc7d-fbda218fc277>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: ECC 5:19
Text: Every man also to whom God hath given riches and wealth, and hath given him power to eat thereof, and to take his portion, and to rejoice in his labour; this is the gift of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/5/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c01106e-719f-4bf4-8f14-c90e2b3d0774>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: ECC 5:20
Text: For he shall not much remember the days of his life; because God answereth him in the joy of his heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db58da4e-5979-4966-a56b-6ac3002aa6e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: ECC 6:1
Text: There is an evil which I have seen under the sun, and it is common among men:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3eece558-5217-4036-b609-3d38acee1d33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: ECC 6:2
Text: A man to whom God hath given riches, wealth, and honour, so that he wanteth nothing for his soul of all that he desireth, yet God giveth him not power to eat thereof, but a stranger eateth it: this is vanity, and it is an evil disease.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45bb79fd-d279-46d8-a680-946c18582c88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: ECC 6:3
Text: If a man beget an hundred children, and live many years, so that the days of his years be many, and his soul be not filled with good, and also that he have no burial; I say, that an untimely birth is better than he.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bbdb654-f05b-49c8-9155-193c7ab6f848>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: ECC 6:4
Text: For he cometh in with vanity, and departeth in darkness, and his name shall be covered with darkness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:941f9f67-fc32-4daa-85ed-574d020322bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: ECC 6:5
Text: Moreover he hath not seen the sun, nor known any thing: this hath more rest than the other.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5337774-0a90-48bb-8ba9-bd4b6fc8c0ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: ECC 6:6
Text: Yea, though he live a thousand years twice told, yet hath he seen no good: do not all go to one place?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1760e4c2-4331-4023-bf77-2d11636822ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: ECC 6:7
Text: All the labour of man is for his mouth, and yet the appetite is not filled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:795d149e-60cb-4516-b8a0-076764e5efb9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: ECC 6:8
Text: For what hath the wise more than the fool? what hath the poor, that knoweth to walk before the living?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed17bedb-5f9a-40c4-a5af-7e0f1934f35c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: ECC 6:9
Text: Better is the sight of the eyes than the wandering of the desire: this is also vanity and vexation of spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:475bb433-8061-4b31-8f00-be5969fe2a9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: ECC 6:10
Text: That which hath been is named already, and it is known that it is man: neither may he contend with him that is mightier than he.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ed8d1a5-aff4-40b6-b8f8-934d77b47516>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: ECC 6:11
Text: Seeing there be many things that increase vanity, what is man the better?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:305e1a1e-d974-4523-b201-e09a5904dadf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: ECC 6:12
Text: For who knoweth what is good for man in this life, all the days of his vain life which he spendeth as a shadow? for who can tell a man what shall be after him under the sun?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee5d424c-edfe-4342-b5c5-a4ba847a04be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: ECC 7:1
Text: A good name is better than precious ointment; and the day of death than the day of one’s birth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73cabc7d-9959-45b9-b70b-ff1ddc21cf19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: ECC 7:2
Text: It is better to go to the house of mourning, than to go to the house of feasting: for that is the end of all men; and the living will lay it to his heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1c3300c-312c-4387-8f9d-decf8ddc8d85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: ECC 7:3
Text: Sorrow is better than laughter: for by the sadness of the countenance the heart is made better.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1d8e604-1329-4de1-b76a-c25ebe8d514a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: ECC 7:4
Text: The heart of the wise is in the house of mourning; but the heart of fools is in the house of mirth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38241b83-9f12-485c-ae2d-9a307cb9a651>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: ECC 7:5
Text: It is better to hear the rebuke of the wise, than for a man to hear the song of fools.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e00c8bc-6214-4ab9-a209-026a69d22229>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: ECC 7:6
Text: For as the crackling of thorns under a pot, so is the laughter of the fool: this also is vanity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81fcf845-d290-443e-b875-e12cad043eb1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: ECC 7:7
Text: Surely oppression maketh a wise man mad; and a gift destroyeth the heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06ab78f5-b7bb-464d-9c2b-03c742553da5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: ECC 7:8
Text: Better is the end of a thing than the beginning thereof: and the patient in spirit is better than the proud in spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3777666c-f3b8-4913-941c-50a99709ff85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: ECC 7:9
Text: Be not hasty in thy spirit to be angry: for anger resteth in the bosom of fools.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb20b9f7-c1d5-440e-8133-656724f33360>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: ECC 7:10
Text: Say not thou, What is the cause that the former days were better than these? for thou dost not enquire wisely concerning this.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a05aa74-7a9d-4b1f-8c49-475269870acd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: ECC 7:11
Text: Wisdom is good with an inheritance: and by it there is profit to them that see the sun.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bdbbfa1-a6b1-4c3f-ae69-aac38c13b6ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: ECC 7:12
Text: For wisdom is a defence, and money is a defence: but the excellency of knowledge is, that wisdom giveth life to them that have it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3fac7b6b-514b-4900-9a8b-465ffe077803>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: ECC 7:13
Text: Consider the work of God: for who can make that straight, which he hath made crooked?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb774da5-66b9-4bd9-931c-d3488f81df35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: ECC 7:14
Text: In the day of prosperity be joyful, but in the day of adversity consider: God also hath set the one over against the other, to the end that man should find nothing after him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1d63129-19dc-40d3-81b8-6e24eeb9edee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: ECC 7:15
Text: All things have I seen in the days of my vanity: there is a just man that perisheth in his righteousness, and there is a wicked man that prolongeth his life in his wickedness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28adeba9-42ce-4b35-8bf5-3a592e0527bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: ECC 7:16
Text: Be not righteous over much; neither make thyself over wise: why shouldest thou destroy thyself?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac1e0e30-5b56-4709-b5dc-6158c649b825>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: ECC 7:17
Text: Be not over much wicked, neither be thou foolish: why shouldest thou die before thy time?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19bdaada-10b9-4588-8f98-5fcc18210c7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: ECC 7:18
Text: It is good that thou shouldest take hold of this; yea, also from this withdraw not thine hand: for he that feareth God shall come forth of them all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f36f949-90b3-4cc5-b97f-c4b738a22443>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: ECC 7:19
Text: Wisdom strengtheneth the wise more than ten mighty men which are in the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:188f2a35-7dd6-4272-8de5-803a4c454adc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: ECC 7:20
Text: For there is not a just man upon earth, that doeth good, and sinneth not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cba1a6dd-7681-4ba2-bb31-62371845c615>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: ECC 7:21
Text: Also take no heed unto all words that are spoken; lest thou hear thy servant curse thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:131dceb9-6a4a-408b-b2a0-ac4cb8871456>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: ECC 7:22
Text: For oftentimes also thine own heart knoweth that thou thyself likewise hast cursed others.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e30177f-32a5-4907-88a8-7a3668e6bf51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: ECC 7:23
Text: All this have I proved by wisdom: I said, I will be wise; but it was far from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67c702a8-bb7a-47f4-b9e1-d3b6ce3e9d85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: ECC 7:24
Text: That which is far off, and exceeding deep, who can find it out?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f19d78a3-114b-407e-81cd-b6a8c2238580>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: ECC 7:25
Text: I applied mine heart to know, and to search, and to seek out wisdom, and the reason of things, and to know the wickedness of folly, even of foolishness and madness:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fec5a003-b823-4f87-9f55-13d46b869527>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: ECC 7:26
Text: And I find more bitter than death the woman, whose heart is snares and nets, and her hands as bands: whoso pleaseth God shall escape from her; but the sinner shall be taken by her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0fc4c9d-a719-4781-a14d-b4d10e35616d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: ECC 7:27
Text: Behold, this have I found, saith the preacher, counting one by one, to find out the account:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6da8b1ea-7569-4db1-b94d-982d078882fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: ECC 7:28
Text: Which yet my soul seeketh, but I find not: one man among a thousand have I found; but a woman among all those have I not found.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/7/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:627bdd07-7016-43a2-8d56-5f639fdcb9fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: ECC 7:29
Text: Lo, this only have I found, that God hath made man upright; but they have sought out many inventions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/8/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2be0b34-0901-4b73-8910-1b858a2de241>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: ECC 8:1
Text: Who is as the wise man? and who knoweth the interpretation of a thing? a man’s wisdom maketh his face to shine, and the boldness of his face shall be changed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/8/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3d6ee9b-d221-4a8c-9490-d3c5225d038e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: ECC 8:2
Text: I counsel thee to keep the king’s commandment, and that in regard of the oath of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/8/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92f05e9f-cd8d-4c6c-b886-761507b5dcdd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: ECC 8:3
Text: Be not hasty to go out of his sight: stand not in an evil thing; for he doeth whatsoever pleaseth him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/8/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eeb90f9e-c9ee-4fba-9c57-98cf602b8073>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: ECC 8:4
Text: Where the word of a king is, there is power: and who may say unto him, What doest thou?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/8/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f65c7b41-0117-43e2-abc6-0db40f0f450d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: ECC 8:5
Text: Whoso keepeth the commandment shall feel no evil thing: and a wise man’s heart discerneth both time and judgment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/8/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76f73249-6c01-420c-9050-43073a9ed329>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: ECC 8:6
Text: Because to every purpose there is time and judgment, therefore the misery of man is great upon him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/8/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7830ca11-c217-4dbf-b4d7-c8cfbac0d58b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: ECC 8:7
Text: For he knoweth not that which shall be: for who can tell him when it shall be?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/8/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b9b3cd5-3deb-44b8-bd95-0250c6331266>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: ECC 8:8
Text: There is no man that hath power over the spirit to retain the spirit; neither hath he power in the day of death: and there is no discharge in that war; neither shall wickedness deliver those that are given to it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/8/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01ef5de6-ff6a-400a-80a2-c9f11a930235>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: ECC 8:9
Text: All this have I seen, and applied my heart unto every work that is done under the sun: there is a time wherein one man ruleth over another to his own hurt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/8/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf6bb0cc-0aea-40d9-8504-99ac7de8b074>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: ECC 8:10
Text: And so I saw the wicked buried, who had come and gone from the place of the holy, and they were forgotten in the city where they had so done: this is also vanity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/8/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:337e7658-5710-4366-aa3d-0ef3a200a9f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: ECC 8:11
Text: Because sentence against an evil work is not executed speedily, therefore the heart of the sons of men is fully set in them to do evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/8/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:919d620f-29da-4730-a0da-477001b1b17e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: ECC 8:12
Text: Though a sinner do evil an hundred times, and his days be prolonged, yet surely I know that it shall be well with them that fear God, which fear before him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/8/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c52a7936-57bf-41ca-b990-45d9ba1dfa42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: ECC 8:13
Text: But it shall not be well with the wicked, neither shall he prolong his days, which are as a shadow; because he feareth not before God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/8/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03a79cd4-8609-4d4a-95b4-7c86d22feb23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 280

Reference: ECC 8:14
Text: There is a vanity which is done upon the earth; that there be just men, unto whom it happeneth according to the work of the wicked; again, there be wicked men, to whom it happeneth according to the work of the righteous: I said that this also is vanity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/8/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96b3f8f8-3797-4f81-806e-39f1eb6e290e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: ECC 8:15
Text: Then I commended mirth, because a man hath no better thing under the sun, than to eat, and to drink, and to be merry: for that shall abide with him of his labour the days of his life, which God giveth him under the sun.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/8/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e923c64e-1d3a-40a1-a2da-fc1acce954a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: ECC 8:16
Text: When I applied mine heart to know wisdom, and to see the business that is done upon the earth: (for also there is that neither day nor night seeth sleep with his eyes:)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/8/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ca33180-4a97-41a7-8bcf-ea85a0d86679>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 281

Reference: ECC 8:17
Text: Then I beheld all the work of God, that a man cannot find out the work that is done under the sun: because though a man labour to seek it out, yet he shall not find it; yea farther; though a wise man think to know it, yet shall he not be able to find it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/9/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:924d556f-fdd2-46bb-acac-04104ae29041>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: ECC 9:1
Text: For all this I considered in my heart even to declare all this, that the righteous, and the wise, and their works, are in the hand of God: no man knoweth either love or hatred by all that is before them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/9/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6461fb6-80ed-4180-8b6c-8bb90d88730d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 303

Reference: ECC 9:2
Text: All things come alike to all: there is one event to the righteous, and to the wicked; to the good and to the clean, and to the unclean; to him that sacrificeth, and to him that sacrificeth not: as is the good, so is the sinner; and he that sweareth, as he that feareth an oath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/9/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a6d0e28-818b-4675-bea3-07971d6e4853>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: ECC 9:3
Text: This is an evil among all things that are done under the sun, that there is one event unto all: yea, also the heart of the sons of men is full of evil, and madness is in their heart while they live, and after that they go to the dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/9/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61cc20ba-41b9-4a65-bff6-b4cd0a8ede52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: ECC 9:4
Text: For to him that is joined to all the living there is hope: for a living dog is better than a dead lion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/9/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4db1ee2-803f-4820-966a-f3f176671005>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: ECC 9:5
Text: For the living know that they shall die: but the dead know not any thing, neither have they any more a reward; for the memory of them is forgotten.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/9/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3594401-f67c-48ce-a8fd-5225b21b479d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: ECC 9:6
Text: Also their love, and their hatred, and their envy, is now perished; neither have they any more a portion for ever in any thing that is done under the sun.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/9/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abb4e4dc-b176-4e25-82ed-7cb3b2986852>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: ECC 9:7
Text: Go thy way, eat thy bread with joy, and drink thy wine with a merry heart; for God now accepteth thy works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/9/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7aa10003-1d51-4bdc-94a1-15264a3016c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: ECC 9:8
Text: Let thy garments be always white; and let thy head lack no ointment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/9/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4253e87-7309-42dd-8de2-24610a810285>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: ECC 9:9
Text: Live joyfully with the wife whom thou lovest all the days of the life of thy vanity, which he hath given thee under the sun, all the days of thy vanity: for that is thy portion in this life, and in thy labour which thou takest under the sun.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/9/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02f8a37c-3a6b-4add-adbe-df8fd3b454f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: ECC 9:10
Text: Whatsoever thy hand findeth to do, do it with thy might; for there is no work, nor device, nor knowledge, nor wisdom, in the grave, whither thou goest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/9/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0722803-98fa-4989-9377-262e3c5c0616>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: ECC 9:11
Text: I returned, and saw under the sun, that the race is not to the swift, nor the battle to the strong, neither yet bread to the wise, nor yet riches to men of understanding, nor yet favour to men of skill; but time and chance happeneth to them all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/9/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:038c2b48-838c-484c-9786-e52af983efc9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: ECC 9:12
Text: For man also knoweth not his time: as the fishes that are taken in an evil net, and as the birds that are caught in the snare; so are the sons of men snared in an evil time, when it falleth suddenly upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/9/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e80c0dc2-2b49-43f4-9e7e-38014d24ca01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: ECC 9:13
Text: This wisdom have I seen also under the sun, and it seemed great unto me:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/9/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45ce23bf-69b5-4365-b8ed-b857fcdf1ef9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: ECC 9:14
Text: There was a little city, and few men within it; and there came a great king against it, and besieged it, and built great bulwarks against it:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/9/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f7cc18d-fb5f-458b-9548-1938d525a8ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: ECC 9:15
Text: Now there was found in it a poor wise man, and he by his wisdom delivered the city; yet no man remembered that same poor man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/9/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:884cfd88-bd7d-4abc-afdb-80a0d435ba41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: ECC 9:16
Text: Then said I, Wisdom is better than strength: nevertheless the poor man’s wisdom is despised, and his words are not heard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/9/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa424d5c-699e-4e62-97e8-bf5e5c1a121b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: ECC 9:17
Text: The words of wise men are heard in quiet more than the cry of him that ruleth among fools.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/9/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ce95bd0-2939-4142-aa23-b4606d0f4e0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: ECC 9:18
Text: Wisdom is better than weapons of war: but one sinner destroyeth much good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/10/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d939e558-be01-432f-9d07-b48e1bce24ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: ECC 10:1
Text: Dead flies cause the ointment of the apothecary to send forth a stinking savour: so doth a little folly him that is in reputation for wisdom and honour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/10/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f90d5bb3-03cb-47da-9dea-27ac18236608>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: ECC 10:2
Text: A wise man’s heart is at his right hand; but a fool’s heart at his left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/10/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a6929db-3380-4a95-b593-fad3b6e49bee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: ECC 10:3
Text: Yea also, when he that is a fool walketh by the way, his wisdom faileth him, and he saith to every one that he is a fool.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/10/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21f0318d-96a8-489d-b3cc-eeffff6dc6a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: ECC 10:4
Text: If the spirit of the ruler rise up against thee, leave not thy place; for yielding pacifieth great offences.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/10/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ab3d2af-e597-4b42-b939-7f0501ab4500>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: ECC 10:5
Text: There is an evil which I have seen under the sun, as an error which proceedeth from the ruler:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/10/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32ea1c07-92da-43ea-95e5-ea0edc850b54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: ECC 10:6
Text: Folly is set in great dignity, and the rich sit in low place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/10/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae75b4ae-eb7d-4ea1-82ea-5773ff1977dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: ECC 10:7
Text: I have seen servants upon horses, and princes walking as servants upon the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/10/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0896e86-53a7-4cf7-b8ab-ed38e69d1389>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: ECC 10:8
Text: He that diggeth a pit shall fall into it; and whoso breaketh an hedge, a serpent shall bite him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/10/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3b7be90-a638-450f-9bb7-064b292d0a58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: ECC 10:9
Text: Whoso removeth stones shall be hurt therewith; and he that cleaveth wood shall be endangered thereby.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/10/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd2f97e1-137d-4597-ba8f-6c080ff008e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: ECC 10:10
Text: If the iron be blunt, and he do not whet the edge, then must he put to more strength: but wisdom is profitable to direct.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/10/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c244a42-f4ba-4801-9fb1-91bfc63b19fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: ECC 10:11
Text: Surely the serpent will bite without enchantment; and a babbler is no better.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/10/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c31abd4-b725-4265-b541-368bc0cfc714>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: ECC 10:12
Text: The words of a wise man’s mouth are gracious; but the lips of a fool will swallow up himself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/10/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfe2771e-10ed-490e-a985-adfa45aba7c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: ECC 10:13
Text: The beginning of the words of his mouth is foolishness: and the end of his talk is mischievous madness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/10/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4010bcd-88dc-44d8-a6fc-0281eaed9282>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: ECC 10:14
Text: A fool also is full of words: a man cannot tell what shall be; and what shall be after him, who can tell him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/10/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21cdcfb7-b6ed-472c-8b82-fb56f802fe96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: ECC 10:15
Text: The labour of the foolish wearieth every one of them, because he knoweth not how to go to the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/10/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ea986ee-bfe4-4f56-95f2-fa2d12dac9d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: ECC 10:16
Text: Woe to thee, O land, when thy king is a child, and thy princes eat in the morning!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/10/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:013ec366-3f88-4be1-a660-2c031d2294e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: ECC 10:17
Text: Blessed art thou, O land, when thy king is the son of nobles, and thy princes eat in due season, for strength, and not for drunkenness!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/10/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da15deeb-2a74-4559-a625-7fa1da0df87c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: ECC 10:18
Text: By much slothfulness the building decayeth; and through idleness of the hands the house droppeth through.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/10/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d69bf1d7-0f13-42fa-ab4e-425eb3679888>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: ECC 10:19
Text: A feast is made for laughter, and wine maketh merry: but money answereth all things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/10/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8457136d-9cf2-4e04-956f-7b05ba01e685>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: ECC 10:20
Text: Curse not the king, no not in thy thought; and curse not the rich in thy bedchamber: for a bird of the air shall carry the voice, and that which hath wings shall tell the matter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/11/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2b7e3d2-1c3e-4afb-aa74-d2a10e2d66ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: ECC 11:1
Text: Cast thy bread upon the waters: for thou shalt find it after many days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/11/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:103d9708-8ee5-4683-8067-f50b28903039>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: ECC 11:2
Text: Give a portion to seven, and also to eight; for thou knowest not what evil shall be upon the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/11/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fab75b9a-aba7-4094-946f-cd3bb2d8f87d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: ECC 11:3
Text: If the clouds be full of rain, they empty themselves upon the earth: and if the tree fall toward the south, or toward the north, in the place where the tree falleth, there it shall be.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/11/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9dd8f52c-7a19-453c-b197-d57b4c4a2280>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: ECC 11:4
Text: He that observeth the wind shall not sow; and he that regardeth the clouds shall not reap.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/11/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa7bc073-e7fd-4bfb-85b0-58a686420b9f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: ECC 11:5
Text: As thou knowest not what is the way of the spirit, nor how the bones do grow in the womb of her that is with child: even so thou knowest not the works of God who maketh all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/11/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:961d2772-5d5b-43a1-9376-40bf6ff4023e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: ECC 11:6
Text: In the morning sow thy seed, and in the evening withhold not thine hand: for thou knowest not whether shall prosper, either this or that, or whether they both shall be alike good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/11/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce51062b-78a8-41f0-bf15-a903ab0758d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: ECC 11:7
Text: Truly the light is sweet, and a pleasant thing it is for the eyes to behold the sun:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/11/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f512c582-0229-4b9f-a83d-a68246c70747>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: ECC 11:8
Text: But if a man live many years, and rejoice in them all; yet let him remember the days of darkness; for they shall be many. All that cometh is vanity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/11/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dcdfb12d-3358-4bc6-b927-79dc84486e84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 262

Reference: ECC 11:9
Text: Rejoice, O young man, in thy youth; and let thy heart cheer thee in the days of thy youth, and walk in the ways of thine heart, and in the sight of thine eyes: but know thou, that for all these things God will bring thee into judgment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/11/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bb16dba-3485-40f4-9786-5d44730b9d5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: ECC 11:10
Text: Therefore remove sorrow from thy heart, and put away evil from thy flesh: for childhood and youth are vanity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/12/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:932700f4-b20f-4cf4-b9fa-d571ef7d865d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: ECC 12:1
Text: Remember now thy Creator in the days of thy youth, while the evil days come not, nor the years draw nigh, when thou shalt say, I have no pleasure in them;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/12/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc201b7a-4371-4f45-975e-6d67ad892d83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: ECC 12:2
Text: While the sun, or the light, or the moon, or the stars, be not darkened, nor the clouds return after the rain:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/12/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5912a059-13e9-496b-a843-149b07c4b1be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: ECC 12:3
Text: In the day when the keepers of the house shall tremble, and the strong men shall bow themselves, and the grinders cease because they are few, and those that look out of the windows be darkened,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/12/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:574479fb-a04a-4914-8fc9-822c50b5080c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: ECC 12:4
Text: And the doors shall be shut in the streets, when the sound of the grinding is low, and he shall rise up at the voice of the bird, and all the daughters of musick shall be brought low;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/12/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:389ae84a-987e-4e5d-b202-c09542869f46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: ECC 12:5
Text: Also when they shall be afraid of that which is high, and fears shall be in the way, and the almond tree shall flourish, and the grasshopper shall be a burden, and desire shall fail: because man goeth to his long home, and the mourners go about the streets:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/12/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bdfe98b8-78d4-4c78-9149-706b180b98bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: ECC 12:6
Text: Or ever the silver cord be loosed, or the golden bowl be broken, or the pitcher be broken at the fountain, or the wheel broken at the cistern.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/12/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dec96d1d-e87c-4044-bbc3-baf150537189>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: ECC 12:7
Text: Then shall the dust return to the earth as it was: and the spirit shall return unto God who gave it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/12/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:812d9755-865f-427f-848a-7c8dbffc2e7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: ECC 12:8
Text: Vanity of vanities, saith the preacher; all is vanity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/12/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fa367e9-9428-4396-89a1-d363309f7077>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: ECC 12:9
Text: And moreover, because the preacher was wise, he still taught the people knowledge; yea, he gave good heed, and sought out, and set in order many proverbs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/12/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c44e8755-315f-4cc7-a473-c48d3918b012>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: ECC 12:10
Text: The preacher sought to find out acceptable words: and that which was written was upright, even words of truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/12/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d589d53-48e6-403b-826e-3892d7671ad8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: ECC 12:11
Text: The words of the wise are as goads, and as nails fastened by the masters of assemblies, which are given from one shepherd.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/12/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57a4af4c-9c33-4cca-8bd4-90f7e6e86dab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: ECC 12:12
Text: And further, by these, my son, be admonished: of making many books there is no end; and much study is a weariness of the flesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/12/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98fe9e2f-a3fa-4287-9465-52cba0163878>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: ECC 12:13
Text: Let us hear the conclusion of the whole matter: Fear God, and keep his commandments: for this is the whole duty of man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ECC/12/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba96de8d-3549-4e04-b894-e9bf2818f679>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: ECC 12:14
Text: For God shall bring every work into judgment, with every secret thing, whether it be good, or whether it be evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0e66ad7-ae01-4497-92e3-8e0393d3350b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 66

Reference: SNG 1:1
Text: The song of songs, which is Solomon’s.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9954bda-3aa0-4d75-b688-b9958480c9fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: SNG 1:2
Text: Let him kiss me with the kisses of his mouth: for thy love is better than wine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8e0634b-3342-4989-b8ab-07267e13679f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: SNG 1:3
Text: Because of the savour of thy good ointments thy name is as ointment poured forth, therefore do the virgins love thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03ac32b4-60c6-454f-8719-fdc069c6a16c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: SNG 1:4
Text: Draw me, we will run after thee: the king hath brought me into his chambers: we will be glad and rejoice in thee, we will remember thy love more than wine: the upright love thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a31e487-fea8-4192-834e-36558f246f98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: SNG 1:5
Text: I am black, but comely, O ye daughters of Jerusalem, as the tents of Kedar, as the curtains of Solomon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0748d29-4131-4ef3-9321-5046401b583c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: SNG 1:6
Text: Look not upon me, because I am black, because the sun hath looked upon me: my mother’s children were angry with me; they made me the keeper of the vineyards; but mine own vineyard have I not kept.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c94fcbc1-5b88-4f01-8b3d-f93461c44f6d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: SNG 1:7
Text: Tell me, O thou whom my soul loveth, where thou feedest, where thou makest thy flock to rest at noon: for why should I be as one that turneth aside by the flocks of thy companions?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92a73962-b39c-464e-826a-19b31164992a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: SNG 1:8
Text: If thou know not, O thou fairest among women, go thy way forth by the footsteps of the flock, and feed thy kids beside the shepherds’ tents.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:228d6128-a0c1-439d-939b-50215b659c9f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: SNG 1:9
Text: I have compared thee, O my love, to a company of horses in Pharaoh’s chariots.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a313061-a673-4fa6-bcbe-5535a121983c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: SNG 1:10
Text: Thy cheeks are comely with rows of jewels, thy neck with chains of gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa7cd3f2-7b89-41f4-add8-cf457efbb40b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: SNG 1:11
Text: We will make thee borders of gold with studs of silver.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f25d5f7c-e7f9-412d-b38c-bc6e0f3a9993>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: SNG 1:12
Text: While the king sitteth at his table, my spikenard sendeth forth the smell thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00213919-374f-45dd-be7d-6ec5d3fa2cd4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: SNG 1:13
Text: A bundle of myrrh is my well-beloved unto me; he shall lie all night betwixt my breasts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b01071b6-e3da-4b2a-b01d-27eea4addcf5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: SNG 1:14
Text: My beloved is unto me as a cluster of camphire in the vineyards of Engedi.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7072913a-9a57-4e6d-9f8f-8748d0a42b34>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: SNG 1:15
Text: Behold, thou art fair, my love; behold, thou art fair; thou hast doves’ eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3dda8785-c66a-4e39-b1ec-30e21cfadaee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: SNG 1:16
Text: Behold, thou art fair, my beloved, yea, pleasant: also our bed is green.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a7ada6a-2b6c-40a9-8c21-afaa8d36af09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: SNG 1:17
Text: The beams of our house are cedar, and our rafters of fir.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e91f847-9095-432f-8cef-aaf1c0068dbc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: SNG 2:1
Text: I am the rose of Sharon, and the lily of the valleys.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2761090b-e7c1-4a51-a8d2-990e4ecb6d23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: SNG 2:2
Text: As the lily among thorns, so is my love among the daughters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfbefa93-fb26-42e7-a8d1-d945eca54ebd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: SNG 2:3
Text: As the apple tree among the trees of the wood, so is my beloved among the sons. I sat down under his shadow with great delight, and his fruit was sweet to my taste.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d39d7bee-1e8b-4f90-a221-2783f9ca7b22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: SNG 2:4
Text: He brought me to the banqueting house, and his banner over me was love.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:626e1b61-486a-464c-b2b7-8e8b0b9b1892>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: SNG 2:5
Text: Stay me with flagons, comfort me with apples: for I am sick of love.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63304fc7-c6a3-4dc7-bee0-e455f29743bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: SNG 2:6
Text: His left hand is under my head, and his right hand doth embrace me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6577c21c-6af9-421b-b683-2a882257b959>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: SNG 2:7
Text: I charge you, O ye daughters of Jerusalem, by the roes, and by the hinds of the field, that ye stir not up, nor awake my love, till he please.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e284d88a-559b-4336-870b-843351b52b5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: SNG 2:8
Text: The voice of my beloved! behold, he cometh leaping upon the mountains, skipping upon the hills.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e55e3990-5e1f-456e-921e-a4411419ab84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: SNG 2:9
Text: My beloved is like a roe or a young hart: behold, he standeth behind our wall, he looketh forth at the windows, shewing himself through the lattice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f8e0a9b-be7e-4817-96cb-7ee32af548ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: SNG 2:10
Text: My beloved spake, and said unto me, Rise up, my love, my fair one, and come away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a1abca6-72f2-4c0c-96ac-f9905b7462b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: SNG 2:11
Text: For, lo, the winter is past, the rain is over and gone;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c22b05d1-1969-491c-a908-1511a77c6fdb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: SNG 2:12
Text: The flowers appear on the earth; the time of the singing of birds is come, and the voice of the turtle is heard in our land;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7ec8164-877c-4929-b2e1-ddf3adb8db67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: SNG 2:13
Text: The fig tree putteth forth her green figs, and the vines with the tender grape give a good smell. Arise, my love, my fair one, and come away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6e94056-4af1-4892-9ec6-035688709448>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: SNG 2:14
Text: O my dove, that art in the clefts of the rock, in the secret places of the stairs, let me see thy countenance, let me hear thy voice; for sweet is thy voice, and thy countenance is comely.


WARC/1.0
