Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: SNG 3:1
Text: By night on my bed I sought him whom my soul loveth: I sought him, but I found him not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63bad0ff-0ac7-4907-bbb6-055120ef1540>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: SNG 3:2
Text: I will rise now, and go about the city in the streets, and in the broad ways I will seek him whom my soul loveth: I sought him, but I found him not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92019944-8bbf-4072-aeab-dba59062f33d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: SNG 3:3
Text: The watchmen that go about the city found me: to whom I said, Saw ye him whom my soul loveth?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:788dc1ee-8704-4253-a67d-8d9e6dece657>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: SNG 3:4
Text: It was but a little that I passed from them, but I found him whom my soul loveth: I held him, and would not let him go, until I had brought him into my mother’s house, and into the chamber of her that conceived me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2655eed2-2e67-43ac-82d7-6f674cb1392e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: SNG 3:5
Text: I charge you, O ye daughters of Jerusalem, by the roes, and by the hinds of the field, that ye stir not up, nor awake my love, till he please.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81f545a6-7650-42b5-9f35-74547d282a5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: SNG 3:6
Text: Who is this that cometh out of the wilderness like pillars of smoke, perfumed with myrrh and frankincense, with all powders of the merchant?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:763c9643-debc-4a7a-85c7-6e04d0562b23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: SNG 3:7
Text: Behold his bed, which is Solomon’s; threescore valiant men are about it, of the valiant of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfacaa5c-b18f-4626-81b5-7c78c78e9203>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: SNG 3:8
Text: They all hold swords, being expert in war: every man hath his sword upon his thigh because of fear in the night.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82cf922f-95c8-4486-8aa2-28225ca47bae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: SNG 3:9
Text: King Solomon made himself a chariot of the wood of Lebanon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a84e466-a15f-4885-8669-54404b702448>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: SNG 3:10
Text: He made the pillars thereof of silver, the bottom thereof of gold, the covering of it of purple, the midst thereof being paved with love, for the daughters of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0fd75adf-825d-49e3-ab8a-9d1ef91b2877>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: SNG 3:11
Text: Go forth, O ye daughters of Zion, and behold king Solomon with the crown wherewith his mother crowned him in the day of his espousals, and in the day of the gladness of his heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa725294-8c08-4e94-992a-e2454aa3176d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: SNG 4:1
Text: Behold, thou art fair, my love; behold, thou art fair; thou hast doves’ eyes within thy locks: thy hair is as a flock of goats, that appear from mount Gilead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf4ae03e-9a5c-40fb-b351-4c32bf73e259>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: SNG 4:2
Text: Thy teeth are like a flock of sheep that are even shorn, which came up from the washing; whereof every one bear twins, and none is barren among them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f35b4d0b-7b82-4d2e-b290-2d40b0e3d7ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: SNG 4:3
Text: Thy lips are like a thread of scarlet, and thy speech is comely: thy temples are like a piece of a pomegranate within thy locks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60b54b71-332b-45f7-bcd3-07e04e324146>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: SNG 4:4
Text: Thy neck is like the tower of David builded for an armoury, whereon there hang a thousand bucklers, all shields of mighty men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9863f0a2-43de-4a23-a6fd-10e4c0dae647>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: SNG 4:5
Text: Thy two breasts are like two young roes that are twins, which feed among the lilies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c75618a5-a667-44bd-b7af-78f750041642>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: SNG 4:6
Text: Until the day break, and the shadows flee away, I will get me to the mountain of myrrh, and to the hill of frankincense.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ef6f4ba-6e6e-4d98-9066-43341bf85824>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: SNG 4:7
Text: Thou art all fair, my love; there is no spot in thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de9056dc-add5-453b-88f7-a6b4f5ea431e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: SNG 4:8
Text: Come with me from Lebanon, my spouse, with me from Lebanon: look from the top of Amana, from the top of Shenir and Hermon, from the lions’ dens, from the mountains of the leopards.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8b77484-3a18-4122-bb32-34ae07d4a684>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: SNG 4:9
Text: Thou hast ravished my heart, my sister, my spouse; thou hast ravished my heart with one of thine eyes, with one chain of thy neck.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51e5f02e-8ec6-47f6-8c3b-da6ecbd32aa9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: SNG 4:10
Text: How fair is thy love, my sister, my spouse! how much better is thy love than wine! and the smell of thine ointments than all spices!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac8d7fe1-89f1-41a9-aca0-f015e53f4c26>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: SNG 4:11
Text: Thy lips, O my spouse, drop as the honeycomb: honey and milk are under thy tongue; and the smell of thy garments is like the smell of Lebanon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca1872e1-d887-41f7-b155-d0c32683bbc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: SNG 4:12
Text: A garden inclosed is my sister, my spouse; a spring shut up, a fountain sealed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39e95a6c-5808-40b4-aa66-437103eb80dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: SNG 4:13
Text: Thy plants are an orchard of pomegranates, with pleasant fruits; camphire, with spikenard,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ceba2002-1cfe-41f8-8c4b-a4e4c520d2f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: SNG 4:14
Text: Spikenard and saffron; calamus and cinnamon, with all trees of frankincense; myrrh and aloes, with all the chief spices:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d201487e-af46-4d12-9a85-dd127bf66b51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: SNG 4:15
Text: A fountain of gardens, a well of living waters, and streams from Lebanon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce728c63-4acb-4566-8091-e5f810ca3880>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: SNG 4:16
Text: Awake, O north wind; and come, thou south; blow upon my garden, that the spices thereof may flow out. Let my beloved come into his garden, and eat his pleasant fruits.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce3e0552-7aa2-4198-85b7-b5ff93dbd482>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: SNG 5:1
Text: I am come into my garden, my sister, my spouse: I have gathered my myrrh with my spice; I have eaten my honeycomb with my honey; I have drunk my wine with my milk: eat, O friends; drink, yea, drink abundantly, O beloved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d2e5a8f-f497-4bcb-a101-d7f16398b9d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: SNG 5:2
Text: I sleep, but my heart waketh: it is the voice of my beloved that knocketh, saying, Open to me, my sister, my love, my dove, my undefiled: for my head is filled with dew, and my locks with the drops of the night.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d50b37b-697e-4034-93d0-b29eb237db16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: SNG 5:3
Text: I have put off my coat; how shall I put it on? I have washed my feet; how shall I defile them?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25be833e-5686-402e-b9c4-25276d4748be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: SNG 5:4
Text: My beloved put in his hand by the hole of the door, and my bowels were moved for him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1dbd4cb-6db5-4cd0-9996-17ce01207b89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: SNG 5:5
Text: I rose up to open to my beloved; and my hands dropped with myrrh, and my fingers with sweet smelling myrrh, upon the handles of the lock.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbd067cd-03b6-47e1-9d1d-c9fd01e9f420>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: SNG 5:6
Text: I opened to my beloved; but my beloved had withdrawn himself, and was gone: my soul failed when he spake: I sought him, but I could not find him; I called him, but he gave me no answer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57f2c5b1-a3af-4269-85a3-2f5280b5bdd9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: SNG 5:7
Text: The watchmen that went about the city found me, they smote me, they wounded me; the keepers of the walls took away my veil from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9735372-6d6a-4c8c-b71b-59cb499dd62c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: SNG 5:8
Text: I charge you, O daughters of Jerusalem, if ye find my beloved, that ye tell him, that I am sick of love.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:471f2ca1-d70e-4f98-8acf-a294f14c127f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: SNG 5:9
Text: What is thy beloved more than another beloved, O thou fairest among women? what is thy beloved more than another beloved, that thou dost so charge us?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cebe7f71-35a0-4553-a7b5-393840b7f834>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: SNG 5:10
Text: My beloved is white and ruddy, the chiefest among ten thousand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee25ca10-c621-413b-9ba8-3f1300bd7c5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: SNG 5:11
Text: His head is as the most fine gold, his locks are bushy, and black as a raven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc92ac25-343f-4720-b143-4c3965344c1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: SNG 5:12
Text: His eyes are as the eyes of doves by the rivers of waters, washed with milk, and fitly set.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e16ca922-6edf-417c-ba1f-a5f8c58a136f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: SNG 5:13
Text: His cheeks are as a bed of spices, as sweet flowers: his lips like lilies, dropping sweet smelling myrrh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b763665-c2d1-4f4a-b526-71a4e9356545>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: SNG 5:14
Text: His hands are as gold rings set with the beryl: his belly is as bright ivory overlaid with sapphires.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1dca95dc-7009-4116-b0df-d7d340205ea5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: SNG 5:15
Text: His legs are as pillars of marble, set upon sockets of fine gold: his countenance is as Lebanon, excellent as the cedars.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d0abee0-1ec4-480f-8993-fcb0d3236e12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: SNG 5:16
Text: His mouth is most sweet: yea, he is altogether lovely. This is my beloved, and this is my friend, O daughters of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f0655f9-e48c-4fc6-bae1-e36928d2a91b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: SNG 6:1
Text: Whither is thy beloved gone, O thou fairest among women? whither is thy beloved turned aside? that we may seek him with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74a25e2b-d4a7-4ba6-aa3a-530ad2dc6db9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: SNG 6:2
Text: My beloved is gone down into his garden, to the beds of spices, to feed in the gardens, and to gather lilies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3769ea89-81f3-4283-9c4e-e2b08c24f1d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: SNG 6:3
Text: I am my beloved’s, and my beloved is mine: he feedeth among the lilies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f6e91a2-bde9-4f4e-bec6-ca5e3638be30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: SNG 6:4
Text: Thou art beautiful, O my love, as Tirzah, comely as Jerusalem, terrible as an army with banners.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0826f8a5-d541-4cc9-bc62-f4e65c835db4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: SNG 6:5
Text: Turn away thine eyes from me, for they have overcome me: thy hair is as a flock of goats that appear from Gilead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/6/6
