Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: SNG 6:6
Text: Thy teeth are as a flock of sheep which go up from the washing, whereof every one beareth twins, and there is not one barren among them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46ad75b6-028d-485d-8bec-fbf94a9a7dd2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: SNG 6:7
Text: As a piece of a pomegranate are thy temples within thy locks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc5a388b-6f3c-40ef-ab2a-e3d0dc828704>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: SNG 6:8
Text: There are threescore queens, and fourscore concubines, and virgins without number.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c9ff142-811f-4f09-b44e-6a128e1a8be0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: SNG 6:9
Text: My dove, my undefiled is but one; she is the only one of her mother, she is the choice one of her that bare her. The daughters saw her, and blessed her; yea, the queens and the concubines, and they praised her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8368db2f-edfb-421d-a2a6-5cfbe9d1065b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: SNG 6:10
Text: Who is she that looketh forth as the morning, fair as the moon, clear as the sun, and terrible as an army with banners?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df0b8269-ed2e-40e7-bdce-6f416755515f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: SNG 6:11
Text: I went down into the garden of nuts to see the fruits of the valley, and to see whether the vine flourished and the pomegranates budded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:546ff2cc-36d1-4aaa-bbd7-82f98d1c9638>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: SNG 6:12
Text: Or ever I was aware, my soul made me like the chariots of Amminadib.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c52607b9-cb22-4e47-87f2-71601735de71>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: SNG 6:13
Text: Return, return, O Shulamite; return, return, that we may look upon thee. What will ye see in the Shulamite? As it were the company of two armies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:215ce6c4-4e5f-4a1f-b270-5f6d00f6d9d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: SNG 7:1
Text: How beautiful are thy feet with shoes, O prince’s daughter! the joints of thy thighs are like jewels, the work of the hands of a cunning workman.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ae3a265-f8ae-4d04-8dea-5f8901685d36>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: SNG 7:2
Text: Thy navel is like a round goblet, which wanteth not liquor: thy belly is like an heap of wheat set about with lilies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fe22201-75fb-4fdd-9706-8e64283a7c24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: SNG 7:3
Text: Thy two breasts are like two young roes that are twins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebe23681-7b7f-4c87-b0bb-e19cb0bbcf6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: SNG 7:4
Text: Thy neck is as a tower of ivory; thine eyes like the fishpools in Heshbon, by the gate of Bathrabbim: thy nose is as the tower of Lebanon which looketh toward Damascus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a93c59f9-7653-4d96-ae2a-bb231765e5bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: SNG 7:5
Text: Thine head upon thee is like Carmel, and the hair of thine head like purple; the king is held in the galleries.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e37ee5ff-c2e8-44eb-bc67-28590b12b112>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: SNG 7:6
Text: How fair and how pleasant art thou, O love, for delights!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32454017-7d57-4527-8394-f0a9ced73c98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: SNG 7:7
Text: This thy stature is like to a palm tree, and thy breasts to clusters of grapes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2154ced8-43b7-4391-a9d5-46dde366fa98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: SNG 7:8
Text: I said, I will go up to the palm tree, I will take hold of the boughs thereof: now also thy breasts shall be as clusters of the vine, and the smell of thy nose like apples;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31e621df-f09b-406e-9911-22e3e5b56182>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: SNG 7:9
Text: And the roof of thy mouth like the best wine for my beloved, that goeth down sweetly, causing the lips of those that are asleep to speak.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e84532fc-cab5-4ff9-a5d3-d075ac8953ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: SNG 7:10
Text: I am my beloved’s, and his desire is toward me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:520d0a40-e41c-45e7-a67e-7122cd3e35dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: SNG 7:11
Text: Come, my beloved, let us go forth into the field; let us lodge in the villages.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:208a7d50-b0c3-4a97-8c3f-b5bbc5258f17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: SNG 7:12
Text: Let us get up early to the vineyards; let us see if the vine flourish, whether the tender grape appear, and the pomegranates bud forth: there will I give thee my loves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:002492ad-65b9-420c-a7bb-b31eb0866746>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: SNG 7:13
Text: The mandrakes give a smell, and at our gates are all manner of pleasant fruits, new and old, which I have laid up for thee, O my beloved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/8/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44748a75-3b79-4161-9d60-279d6af7b3a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: SNG 8:1
Text: O that thou wert as my brother, that sucked the breasts of my mother! when I should find thee without, I would kiss thee; yea, I should not be despised.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/8/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dccdb45d-c4dd-409d-9965-e19b9ded196b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: SNG 8:2
Text: I would lead thee, and bring thee into my mother’s house, who would instruct me: I would cause thee to drink of spiced wine of the juice of my pomegranate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/8/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51a2298a-02cf-43e6-bad6-23ffd9bc17f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: SNG 8:3
Text: His left hand should be under my head, and his right hand should embrace me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/8/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2819adc-c5af-4e1e-bbc6-df2b112e66ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: SNG 8:4
Text: I charge you, O daughters of Jerusalem, that ye stir not up, nor awake my love, until he please.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/8/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8cebbd36-f9a6-41dd-b822-7eb90197bf18>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: SNG 8:5
Text: Who is this that cometh up from the wilderness, leaning upon her beloved? I raised thee up under the apple tree: there thy mother brought thee forth: there she brought thee forth that bare thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/8/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b644251-4430-4549-ba89-4dfb003c68eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: SNG 8:6
Text: Set me as a seal upon thine heart, as a seal upon thine arm: for love is strong as death; jealousy is cruel as the grave: the coals thereof are coals of fire, which hath a most vehement flame.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/8/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c5cc6af-373b-4a8a-9621-7503b37ce998>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: SNG 8:7
Text: Many waters cannot quench love, neither can the floods drown it: if a man would give all the substance of his house for love, it would utterly be contemned.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/8/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06ce8b61-ae0f-4c1f-86dc-879e0ecd1b7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: SNG 8:8
Text: We have a little sister, and she hath no breasts: what shall we do for our sister in the day when she shall be spoken for?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/8/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:994f3545-d7b8-4023-bc95-339b3e5c0bfb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: SNG 8:9
Text: If she be a wall, we will build upon her a palace of silver: and if she be a door, we will inclose her with boards of cedar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/8/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32202729-3f65-4579-a79f-2e9bc27ca28a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: SNG 8:10
Text: I am a wall, and my breasts like towers: then was I in his eyes as one that found favour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/8/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:354cbf82-2e17-43d7-ad99-c6e57f902868>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: SNG 8:11
Text: Solomon had a vineyard at Baalhamon; he let out the vineyard unto keepers; every one for the fruit thereof was to bring a thousand pieces of silver.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/8/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3518921-90e5-4f67-94df-f67cfb065611>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: SNG 8:12
Text: My vineyard, which is mine, is before me: thou, O Solomon, must have a thousand, and those that keep the fruit thereof two hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/8/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f75e079-6472-4110-adf1-38fcf528dcdd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: SNG 8:13
Text: Thou that dwellest in the gardens, the companions hearken to thy voice: cause me to hear it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/SNG/8/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f4ad168-ac4c-4486-9d0b-c1354f845f55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: SNG 8:14
Text: Make haste, my beloved, and be thou like to a roe or to a young hart upon the mountains of spices.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb9ac006-6dc3-418f-944f-2b537d37410d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: ISA 1:1
Text: The vision of Isaiah the son of Amoz, which he saw concerning Judah and Jerusalem in the days of Uzziah, Jotham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah, kings of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4347cee2-fd2a-4af8-a7b9-50d9d1ce0b7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: ISA 1:2
Text: Hear, O heavens, and give ear, O earth: for the LORD hath spoken, I have nourished and brought up children, and they have rebelled against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:286db892-1e17-4d5c-bbfd-8f6d3decfa43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: ISA 1:3
Text: The ox knoweth his owner, and the ass his master’s crib: but Israel doth not know, my people doth not consider.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85e6c009-0821-4a7f-99b5-f3c913c84b97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: ISA 1:4
Text: Ah sinful nation, a people laden with iniquity, a seed of evildoers, children that are corrupters: they have forsaken the LORD, they have provoked the Holy One of Israel unto anger, they are gone away backward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b029705-28bd-4ac0-b01e-1095934cd835>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: ISA 1:5
Text: Why should ye be stricken any more? ye will revolt more and more: the whole head is sick, and the whole heart faint.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb7f129a-fd1e-4693-9b58-4c9000681c02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: ISA 1:6
Text: From the sole of the foot even unto the head there is no soundness in it; but wounds, and bruises, and putrifying sores: they have not been closed, neither bound up, neither mollified with ointment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:968a4d0c-1064-4136-b188-ccb5cbc2a505>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: ISA 1:7
Text: Your country is desolate, your cities are burned with fire: your land, strangers devour it in your presence, and it is desolate, as overthrown by strangers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c7f9c6a-e511-49f2-ad59-d858b50bc5f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: ISA 1:8
Text: And the daughter of Zion is left as a cottage in a vineyard, as a lodge in a garden of cucumbers, as a besieged city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:549d3864-96a9-4647-b131-b46f03ba86ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: ISA 1:9
Text: Except the LORD of hosts had left unto us a very small remnant, we should have been as Sodom, and we should have been like unto Gomorrah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3513857c-e16a-4948-92d2-a0be3e3083fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: ISA 1:10
Text: Hear the word of the LORD, ye rulers of Sodom; give ear unto the law of our God, ye people of Gomorrah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf64e17d-49ff-494b-826f-71833ca94e19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: ISA 1:11
Text: To what purpose is the multitude of your sacrifices unto me? saith the LORD: I am full of the burnt offerings of rams, and the fat of fed beasts; and I delight not in the blood of bullocks, or of lambs, or of he goats.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2dfd06cb-56e5-41a3-aedb-38a6074f90fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: ISA 1:12
Text: When ye come to appear before me, who hath required this at your hand, to tread my courts?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56040895-585a-4713-80cc-78d8a13e8f83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: ISA 1:13
Text: Bring no more vain oblations; incense is an abomination unto me; the new moons and sabbaths, the calling of assemblies, I cannot away with; it is iniquity, even the solemn meeting.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3510fcc1-2612-428b-ac27-4e196265cf81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: ISA 1:14
Text: Your new moons and your appointed feasts my soul hateth: they are a trouble unto me; I am weary to bear them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:427fa628-2b91-45ac-88d0-78dac2c99eea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: ISA 1:15
Text: And when ye spread forth your hands, I will hide mine eyes from you: yea, when ye make many prayers, I will not hear: your hands are full of blood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6fc21785-0b46-4238-b7f8-57ee52efe5ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: ISA 1:16
Text: Wash you, make you clean; put away the evil of your doings from before mine eyes; cease to do evil;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc089d9e-c89a-4879-9914-ab03d21086d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: ISA 1:17
Text: Learn to do well; seek judgment, relieve the oppressed, judge the fatherless, plead for the widow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b406502f-c2ef-45f2-b096-0d869e82b4bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: ISA 1:18
Text: Come now, and let us reason together, saith the LORD: though your sins be as scarlet, they shall be as white as snow; though they be red like crimson, they shall be as wool.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:006cb87c-b681-4e36-b79c-380f287f6d2b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: ISA 1:19
Text: If ye be willing and obedient, ye shall eat the good of the land:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f914043-36a4-45c7-8275-08f915994871>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: ISA 1:20
Text: But if ye refuse and rebel, ye shall be devoured with the sword: for the mouth of the LORD hath spoken it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39c24909-7a2b-4721-8042-1675d2475f60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: ISA 1:21
Text: How is the faithful city become an harlot! it was full of judgment; righteousness lodged in it; but now murderers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0e9c356-ed67-4ddd-b542-2dfa32522694>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: ISA 1:22
Text: Thy silver is become dross, thy wine mixed with water:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa6732a1-4f17-4d5c-a7f6-2ded1ae18622>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: ISA 1:23
Text: Thy princes are rebellious, and companions of thieves: every one loveth gifts, and followeth after rewards: they judge not the fatherless, neither doth the cause of the widow come unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa38bb6f-8140-4407-925c-0d5a7689edd9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: ISA 1:24
Text: Therefore saith the LORD, the LORD of hosts, the mighty One of Israel, Ah, I will ease me of mine adversaries, and avenge me of mine enemies:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f0d4d24-db39-4cee-ba75-78f1f233a663>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: ISA 1:25
Text: And I will turn my hand upon thee, and purely purge away thy dross, and take away all thy tin:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:062eaf50-367c-4a44-bee7-75f8e8215abb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: ISA 1:26
Text: And I will restore thy judges as at the first, and thy counsellors as at the beginning: afterward thou shalt be called, The city of righteousness, the faithful city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7fec7e6-badf-4c79-a307-38e432b4d25f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: ISA 1:27
Text: Zion shall be redeemed with judgment, and her converts with righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8eee3a91-177a-415a-a17b-0410c963af0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: ISA 1:28
Text: And the destruction of the transgressors and of the sinners shall be together, and they that forsake the LORD shall be consumed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22e6ba1d-c093-4957-b88f-39495eef4fae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: ISA 1:29
Text: For they shall be ashamed of the oaks which ye have desired, and ye shall be confounded for the gardens that ye have chosen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2349f302-f1b7-467a-b138-91179127a4c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: ISA 1:30
Text: For ye shall be as an oak whose leaf fadeth, and as a garden that hath no water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/1/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7700f19-1c3c-4f1a-8ba6-747f7eaf15b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: ISA 1:31
Text: And the strong shall be as tow, and the maker of it as a spark, and they shall both burn together, and none shall quench them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4c88438-ceb1-4b23-bf1c-e0854f53c499>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: ISA 2:1
Text: The word that Isaiah the son of Amoz saw concerning Judah and Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4ca069b-9ea5-4bb9-87cd-4344c72a2138>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: ISA 2:2
Text: And it shall come to pass in the last days, that the mountain of the LORD’s house shall be established in the top of the mountains, and shall be exalted above the hills; and all nations shall flow unto it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3737ff1-b84f-4dcd-88a6-785e93adbd1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 294

Reference: ISA 2:3
Text: And many people shall go and say, Come ye, and let us go up to the mountain of the LORD, to the house of the God of Jacob; and he will teach us of his ways, and we will walk in his paths: for out of Zion shall go forth the law, and the word of the LORD from Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60c377db-3e05-49fb-81ef-7391027befca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: ISA 2:4
Text: And he shall judge among the nations, and shall rebuke many people: and they shall beat their swords into plowshares, and their spears into pruninghooks: nation shall not lift up sword against nation, neither shall they learn war any more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf8643b8-a6ea-4d9a-9b56-bec1ddaba1a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: ISA 2:5
Text: O house of Jacob, come ye, and let us walk in the light of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:385a785c-5f12-45be-8c7f-94591d9445dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: ISA 2:6
Text: Therefore thou hast forsaken thy people the house of Jacob, because they be replenished from the east, and are soothsayers like the Philistines, and they please themselves in the children of strangers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c88f81b6-3cf4-476a-ae43-1ec22807e1a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: ISA 2:7
Text: Their land also is full of silver and gold, neither is there any end of their treasures; their land is also full of horses, neither is there any end of their chariots:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:befb50b7-daa5-4df5-b222-93faae8d8869>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: ISA 2:8
Text: Their land also is full of idols; they worship the work of their own hands, that which their own fingers have made:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8abdc800-c47d-4355-84ec-7dcd69b85d9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: ISA 2:9
Text: And the mean man boweth down, and the great man humbleth himself: therefore forgive them not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ef683e5-9a34-4bcc-8b31-642690dde7f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: ISA 2:10
Text: Enter into the rock, and hide thee in the dust, for fear of the LORD, and for the glory of his majesty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0677b78-d8c3-47ff-bdb1-5d8e2beb364c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: ISA 2:11
Text: The lofty looks of man shall be humbled, and the haughtiness of men shall be bowed down, and the LORD alone shall be exalted in that day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86c8f892-fe70-4ad5-b068-d5db3ae84296>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: ISA 2:12
Text: For the day of the LORD of hosts shall be upon every one that is proud and lofty, and upon every one that is lifted up; and he shall be brought low:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9942578a-9042-4bab-8aa3-df1cc805c45b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: ISA 2:13
Text: And upon all the cedars of Lebanon, that are high and lifted up, and upon all the oaks of Bashan,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:637561a3-d96f-4581-8280-2924e0241cbc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: ISA 2:14
Text: And upon all the high mountains, and upon all the hills that are lifted up,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f77c3211-ca9e-43bf-b0c9-8c79cd15d14c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: ISA 2:15
Text: And upon every high tower, and upon every fenced wall,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf1d05e6-d3c5-4599-9dab-06830a35fdab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: ISA 2:16
Text: And upon all the ships of Tarshish, and upon all pleasant pictures.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c47b8eed-7fe6-4f31-9500-23ee63f531d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: ISA 2:17
Text: And the loftiness of man shall be bowed down, and the haughtiness of men shall be made low: and the LORD alone shall be exalted in that day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d79a8d9-b137-45f4-ae31-6611e0d3380d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 66

Reference: ISA 2:18
Text: And the idols he shall utterly abolish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:708e4d41-53ba-4579-bfdc-a21cfbb5caa9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: ISA 2:19
Text: And they shall go into the holes of the rocks, and into the caves of the earth, for fear of the LORD, and for the glory of his majesty, when he ariseth to shake terribly the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:216f731a-75ce-4190-bc26-b955752850e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: ISA 2:20
Text: In that day a man shall cast his idols of silver, and his idols of gold, which they made each one for himself to worship, to the moles and to the bats;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e89d27c-b6ba-4ceb-9568-f5e66946690c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: ISA 2:21
Text: To go into the clefts of the rocks, and into the tops of the ragged rocks, for fear of the LORD, and for the glory of his majesty, when he ariseth to shake terribly the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3344e14-7ccc-43a6-8e7a-f790c3ad3163>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: ISA 2:22
Text: Cease ye from man, whose breath is in his nostrils: for wherein is he to be accounted of?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0efbc9d3-0429-440c-8308-205c1fa1df11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: ISA 3:1
Text: For, behold, the Lord, the LORD of hosts, doth take away from Jerusalem and from Judah the stay and the staff, the whole stay of bread, and the whole stay of water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f15cfa6-cabf-4693-bc41-bb94ea0d3e43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: ISA 3:2
Text: The mighty man, and the man of war, the judge, and the prophet, and the prudent, and the ancient,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:225752bb-0886-4c96-bad9-9e6e3ee4d551>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: ISA 3:3
Text: The captain of fifty, and the honourable man, and the counsellor, and the cunning artificer, and the eloquent orator.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52111fa9-9f9d-42b5-95f8-bf86d9fc17ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: ISA 3:4
Text: And I will give children to be their princes, and babes shall rule over them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe74b988-518f-4620-9797-43613a0e2b92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: ISA 3:5
Text: And the people shall be oppressed, every one by another, and every one by his neighbour: the child shall behave himself proudly against the ancient, and the base against the honourable.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a02794f0-d6af-41f3-9169-19fa4d734a03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: ISA 3:6
Text: When a man shall take hold of his brother of the house of his father, saying, Thou hast clothing, be thou our ruler, and let this ruin be under thy hand:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10f9af11-dfaa-45d5-bdf9-d0036db32fbe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: ISA 3:7
Text: In that day shall he swear, saying, I will not be an healer; for in my house is neither bread nor clothing: make me not a ruler of the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36097032-5899-4f2e-aeff-8dcdefffccf9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: ISA 3:8
Text: For Jerusalem is ruined, and Judah is fallen: because their tongue and their doings are against the LORD, to provoke the eyes of his glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9222ae91-faac-4156-b521-870b406b2439>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: ISA 3:9
Text: The shew of their countenance doth witness against them; and they declare their sin as Sodom, they hide it not. Woe unto their soul! for they have rewarded evil unto themselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b6eb2b8-1d22-4a8d-bd6e-766ea08ffdd1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: ISA 3:10
Text: Say ye to the righteous, that it shall be well with him: for they shall eat the fruit of their doings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54506e74-8454-4a5e-904d-d300852d3c12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: ISA 3:11
Text: Woe unto the wicked! it shall be ill with him: for the reward of his hands shall be given him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e98bbce1-dadf-4adb-b3e4-3274b02c9181>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: ISA 3:12
Text: As for my people, children are their oppressors, and women rule over them. O my people, they which lead thee cause thee to err, and destroy the way of thy paths.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f30ebbc-fd78-4a67-a2a4-e66046213be3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: ISA 3:13
Text: The LORD standeth up to plead, and standeth to judge the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e8736cf-961a-4912-a564-5c45dd073d76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: ISA 3:14
Text: The LORD will enter into judgment with the ancients of his people, and the princes thereof: for ye have eaten up the vineyard; the spoil of the poor is in your houses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75a94a64-bae6-49b0-a27a-c724cc002d2d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: ISA 3:15
Text: What mean ye that ye beat my people to pieces, and grind the faces of the poor? saith the Lord GOD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14942a1f-087e-4069-81c1-4947c0ad6ecc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: ISA 3:16
Text: Moreover the LORD saith, Because the daughters of Zion are haughty, and walk with stretched forth necks and wanton eyes, walking and mincing as they go, and making a tinkling with their feet:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/3/17
