Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 54

Reference: ISA 3:21
Text: The rings, and nose jewels,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/3/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f8fb98d-dc05-4c5b-adc7-efc9778aa577>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: ISA 3:22
Text: The changeable suits of apparel, and the mantles, and the wimples, and the crisping pins,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/3/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ede9b5bd-d6f8-4652-9dfa-5dc5cd23c270>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: ISA 3:23
Text: The glasses, and the fine linen, and the hoods, and the vails.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/3/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50aa687d-ee49-4c2b-924b-b91c13fd53ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: ISA 3:24
Text: And it shall come to pass, that instead of sweet smell there shall be stink; and instead of a girdle a rent; and instead of well set hair baldness; and instead of a stomacher a girding of sackcloth; and burning instead of beauty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/3/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:093ab169-9045-4540-b014-36cf9837198d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: ISA 3:25
Text: Thy men shall fall by the sword, and thy mighty in the war.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/3/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8265a1ed-9234-4193-8875-624ddb44b7b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: ISA 3:26
Text: And her gates shall lament and mourn; and she being desolate shall sit upon the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11626af8-2177-4ed3-92d3-59e6e4a99d03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: ISA 4:1
Text: And in that day seven women shall take hold of one man, saying, We will eat our own bread, and wear our own apparel: only let us be called by thy name, to take away our reproach.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b10904cd-2165-4d8b-8626-1684e0f6b0e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: ISA 4:2
Text: In that day shall the branch of the LORD be beautiful and glorious, and the fruit of the earth shall be excellent and comely for them that are escaped of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c1669bd-33d4-4618-abe7-04dd4b55b461>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: ISA 4:3
Text: And it shall come to pass, that he that is left in Zion, and he that remaineth in Jerusalem, shall be called holy, even every one that is written among the living in Jerusalem:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:adeac4b5-0cc6-4237-94b9-d17a6039cce8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: ISA 4:4
Text: When the Lord shall have washed away the filth of the daughters of Zion, and shall have purged the blood of Jerusalem from the midst thereof by the spirit of judgment, and by the spirit of burning.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7287919b-3a6d-41ee-b52c-fab95e88119d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: ISA 4:5
Text: And the LORD will create upon every dwelling place of mount Zion, and upon her assemblies, a cloud and smoke by day, and the shining of a flaming fire by night: for upon all the glory shall be a defence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2ed6c8b-8569-4cfc-9fd9-005863e7ef39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: ISA 4:6
Text: And there shall be a tabernacle for a shadow in the day time from the heat, and for a place of refuge, and for a covert from storm and from rain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9630e866-66bf-4c94-80a9-e5cd99fc00dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: ISA 5:1
Text: Now will I sing to my wellbeloved a song of my beloved touching his vineyard. My wellbeloved hath a vineyard in a very fruitful hill:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afb549dd-0993-4133-b145-b9b48f9df0c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: ISA 5:2
Text: And he fenced it, and gathered out the stones thereof, and planted it with the choicest vine, and built a tower in the midst of it, and also made a winepress therein: and he looked that it should bring forth grapes, and it brought forth wild grapes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1cd8ea6-ef66-41b4-952f-b33353f5eb95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: ISA 5:3
Text: And now, O inhabitants of Jerusalem, and men of Judah, judge, I pray you, betwixt me and my vineyard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1cc1185-ea77-4f02-b9ea-24daed0cf181>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: ISA 5:4
Text: What could have been done more to my vineyard, that I have not done in it? wherefore, when I looked that it should bring forth grapes, brought it forth wild grapes?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd67f493-3b84-47af-9b9e-f9d195f497f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: ISA 5:5
Text: And now go to; I will tell you what I will do to my vineyard: I will take away the hedge thereof, and it shall be eaten up; and break down the wall thereof, and it shall be trodden down:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0359efa-ac0c-49e9-b23a-b2fd2cc067a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: ISA 5:6
Text: And I will lay it waste: it shall not be pruned, nor digged; but there shall come up briers and thorns: I will also command the clouds that they rain no rain upon it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8660e51c-a69d-4f0c-9711-9e6fadcb2079>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: ISA 5:7
Text: For the vineyard of the LORD of hosts is the house of Israel, and the men of Judah his pleasant plant: and he looked for judgment, but behold oppression; for righteousness, but behold a cry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8785c67b-4488-44b3-afb1-3fab76c77f5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: ISA 5:8
Text: Woe unto them that join house to house, that lay field to field, till there be no place, that they may be placed alone in the midst of the earth!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ff3a3ae-a42c-41d4-a22e-d6e0eea9f5d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: ISA 5:9
Text: In mine ears said the LORD of hosts, Of a truth many houses shall be desolate, even great and fair, without inhabitant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f7dd63f-8711-4f8b-afa7-7410026b4055>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: ISA 5:10
Text: Yea, ten acres of vineyard shall yield one bath, and the seed of an homer shall yield an ephah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbc78685-8b42-4508-9a43-03d8af80cf10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: ISA 5:11
Text: Woe unto them that rise up early in the morning, that they may follow strong drink; that continue until night, till wine inflame them!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57b4a053-5d46-446d-8787-11f1a34e3206>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: ISA 5:12
Text: And the harp, and the viol, the tabret, and pipe, and wine, are in their feasts: but they regard not the work of the LORD, neither consider the operation of his hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6eaa20a2-cc7d-4c2f-a9b5-6a520fb10609>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: ISA 5:13
Text: Therefore my people are gone into captivity, because they have no knowledge: and their honourable men are famished, and their multitude dried up with thirst.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a60e26bb-b95e-49f0-8312-bf6ae1804fe9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: ISA 5:14
Text: Therefore hell hath enlarged herself, and opened her mouth without measure: and their glory, and their multitude, and their pomp, and he that rejoiceth, shall descend into it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3aaa2b1-180b-43b9-b345-d403cc1bd86b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: ISA 5:15
Text: And the mean man shall be brought down, and the mighty man shall be humbled, and the eyes of the lofty shall be humbled:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4091e485-3db6-420f-b41d-4e6c8eba1afc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: ISA 5:16
Text: But the LORD of hosts shall be exalted in judgment, and God that is holy shall be sanctified in righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97cb31d0-e955-472c-9302-50c99ade7f98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: ISA 5:17
Text: Then shall the lambs feed after their manner, and the waste places of the fat ones shall strangers eat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c5b4aae-6c00-4b21-aa15-5a06b529e3b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: ISA 5:18
Text: Woe unto them that draw iniquity with cords of vanity, and sin as it were with a cart rope:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e55da85c-862a-4460-a728-f53d2de82f42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: ISA 5:19
Text: That say, Let him make speed, and hasten his work, that we may see it: and let the counsel of the Holy One of Israel draw nigh and come, that we may know it!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25afe08e-0280-4855-8dbe-1798bb007601>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: ISA 5:20
Text: Woe unto them that call evil good, and good evil; that put darkness for light, and light for darkness; that put bitter for sweet, and sweet for bitter!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c279257c-db7f-43a1-a732-8bd9bbce1edd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: ISA 5:21
Text: Woe unto them that are wise in their own eyes, and prudent in their own sight!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3436ef99-40a0-4381-aaee-95d1725850d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: ISA 5:22
Text: Woe unto them that are mighty to drink wine, and men of strength to mingle strong drink:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ef376c4-9a1a-4512-9876-4f5de1c4336f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: ISA 5:23
Text: Which justify the wicked for reward, and take away the righteousness of the righteous from him!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13382ba5-93e1-4274-b273-c5b7f677c545>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 290

Reference: ISA 5:24
Text: Therefore as the fire devoureth the stubble, and the flame consumeth the chaff, so their root shall be as rottenness, and their blossom shall go up as dust: because they have cast away the law of the LORD of hosts, and despised the word of the Holy One of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:900af76a-b2a6-41d1-a380-56c067a10e0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 328

Reference: ISA 5:25
Text: Therefore is the anger of the LORD kindled against his people, and he hath stretched forth his hand against them, and hath smitten them: and the hills did tremble, and their carcases were torn in the midst of the streets. For all this his anger is not turned away, but his hand is stretched out still.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de9cb64b-f1f6-40d4-93eb-e70ddb14ab32>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: ISA 5:26
Text: And he will lift up an ensign to the nations from far, and will hiss unto them from the end of the earth: and, behold, they shall come with speed swiftly:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2898ed47-2a4a-49a0-8ad7-fb1b6a513e51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: ISA 5:27
Text: None shall be weary nor stumble among them; none shall slumber nor sleep; neither shall the girdle of their loins be loosed, nor the latchet of their shoes be broken:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cbb83a9-e111-4a56-8777-3422eea7b3f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: ISA 5:28
Text: Whose arrows are sharp, and all their bows bent, their horses’ hoofs shall be counted like flint, and their wheels like a whirlwind:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78ac697e-0306-4f97-b397-7da3daa26232>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: ISA 5:29
Text: Their roaring shall be like a lion, they shall roar like young lions: yea, they shall roar, and lay hold of the prey, and shall carry it away safe, and none shall deliver it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/5/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:867623fd-fb97-467a-a019-97e61e484b7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: ISA 5:30
Text: And in that day they shall roar against them like the roaring of the sea: and if one look unto the land, behold darkness and sorrow, and the light is darkened in the heavens thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08f4bd8f-dbb1-4d0e-9d79-83e530abb66a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: ISA 6:1
Text: In the year that king Uzziah died I saw also the LORD sitting upon a throne, high and lifted up, and his train filled the temple.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75859fae-aaa5-4a74-ae5a-605a0001d883>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: ISA 6:2
Text: Above it stood the seraphims: each one had six wings; with twain he covered his face, and with twain he covered his feet, and with twain he did fly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4d3efbe-5582-4d31-a71f-4d3a3ab4c0c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: ISA 6:3
Text: And one cried unto another, and said, Holy, holy, holy, is the LORD of hosts: the whole earth is full of his glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d9e48fe-3a6f-490c-94bf-b0810274f45a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: ISA 6:4
Text: And the posts of the door moved at the voice of him that cried, and the house was filled with smoke.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c54262b-cbc1-4f0a-8171-e5c069c6ec83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: ISA 6:5
Text: Then said I, Woe is me! for I am undone; because I am a man of unclean lips, and I dwell in the midst of a people of unclean lips: for mine eyes have seen the King, the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3985d63d-25de-4851-93c9-b8dec27ccfa4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: ISA 6:6
Text: Then flew one of the seraphims unto me, having a live coal in his hand, which he had taken with the tongs from off the altar:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74cc5c84-4981-409d-a098-3fbbbb4d10b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: ISA 6:7
Text: And he laid it upon my mouth, and said, Lo, this hath touched thy lips; and thine iniquity is taken away, and thy sin purged.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e38fa0e3-d60f-4f55-b034-5389d511fc23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: ISA 6:8
Text: Also I heard the voice of the Lord, saying, Whom shall I send, and who will go for us? Then said I, Here am I; send me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47cce507-36aa-4a60-88dd-2b68407526c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: ISA 6:9
Text: And he said, Go, and tell this people, Hear ye indeed, but understand not; and see ye indeed, but perceive not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58e16820-12ce-4f26-845b-fb3895a48795>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: ISA 6:10
Text: Make the heart of this people fat, and make their ears heavy, and shut their eyes; lest they see with their eyes, and hear with their ears, and understand with their heart, and convert, and be healed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53a82ac2-0c64-4c63-9cb0-d64559b41ad6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: ISA 6:11
Text: Then said I, Lord, how long? And he answered, Until the cities be wasted without inhabitant, and the houses without man, and the land be utterly desolate,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29784f54-34e5-4624-b8ef-f9c29126a29c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: ISA 6:12
Text: And the LORD have removed men far away, and there be a great forsaking in the midst of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e3b885a-e6fd-4635-9e25-ee41f7e9e3f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: ISA 6:13
Text: But yet in it shall be a tenth, and it shall return, and shall be eaten: as a teil tree, and as an oak, whose substance is in them, when they cast their leaves: so the holy seed shall be the substance thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9372192f-f8e4-457a-98cd-04ec3b28433d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 273

Reference: ISA 7:1
Text: And it came to pass in the days of Ahaz the son of Jotham, the son of Uzziah, king of Judah, that Rezin the king of Syria, and Pekah the son of Remaliah, king of Israel, went up toward Jerusalem to war against it, but could not prevail against it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc627295-c536-4011-9062-2349d85bd202>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: ISA 7:2
Text: And it was told the house of David, saying, Syria is confederate with Ephraim. And his heart was moved, and the heart of his people, as the trees of the wood are moved with the wind.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c17b5054-6488-43b9-a76b-a822bb1e3dfe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: ISA 7:3
Text: Then said the LORD unto Isaiah, Go forth now to meet Ahaz, thou, and Shearjashub thy son, at the end of the conduit of the upper pool in the highway of the fuller’s field;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:097a7132-ee46-4075-b1ca-6102411a17f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: ISA 7:4
Text: And say unto him, Take heed, and be quiet; fear not, neither be fainthearted for the two tails of these smoking firebrands, for the fierce anger of Rezin with Syria, and of the son of Remaliah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b23ac806-a836-4331-8643-8e8edb36d191>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: ISA 7:5
Text: Because Syria, Ephraim, and the son of Remaliah, have taken evil counsel against thee, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3542abb9-d7d7-48e6-9068-2573f6ab8986>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: ISA 7:6
Text: Let us go up against Judah, and vex it, and let us make a breach therein for us, and set a king in the midst of it, even the son of Tabeal:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d12d641-d26d-4d39-9bf0-70d487f99210>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: ISA 7:7
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD, It shall not stand, neither shall it come to pass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4894c6d6-260d-4da2-9c21-417a32469aef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: ISA 7:8
Text: For the head of Syria is Damascus, and the head of Damascus is Rezin; and within threescore and five years shall Ephraim be broken, that it be not a people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ca76d55-ea27-488b-ab06-9a1c2cd763de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: ISA 7:9
Text: And the head of Ephraim is Samaria, and the head of Samaria is Remaliah’s son. If ye will not believe, surely ye shall not be established.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ec9bff6-9d71-458c-a804-70b42e2a171c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: ISA 7:10
Text: Moreover the LORD spake again unto Ahaz, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:142b8bcc-dbcf-4855-acab-07578beb777c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: ISA 7:11
Text: Ask thee a sign of the LORD thy God; ask it either in the depth, or in the height above.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87daef22-2a67-4b94-ab39-405754248e9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: ISA 7:12
Text: But Ahaz said, I will not ask, neither will I tempt the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c89ac588-7ee7-46fe-a603-ff4c036212c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: ISA 7:13
Text: And he said, Hear ye now, O house of David; Is it a small thing for you to weary men, but will ye weary my God also?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1aee9d98-7377-4281-9c48-0dbcba871827>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: ISA 7:14
Text: Therefore the Lord himself shall give you a sign; Behold, a virgin shall conceive, and bear a son, and shall call his name Immanuel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d887efda-4ae9-4794-b45c-f3f8fd308088>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: ISA 7:15
Text: Butter and honey shall he eat, that he may know to refuse the evil, and choose the good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49f80c79-35d4-436a-b523-40205c364b56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: ISA 7:16
Text: For before the child shall know to refuse the evil, and choose the good, the land that thou abhorrest shall be forsaken of both her kings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12cc3d20-14ed-4908-85c4-05604109928d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: ISA 7:17
Text: The LORD shall bring upon thee, and upon thy people, and upon thy father’s house, days that have not come, from the day that Ephraim departed from Judah; even the king of Assyria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a26830c4-7f79-4243-9ab0-6360ce74b16f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: ISA 7:18
Text: And it shall come to pass in that day, that the LORD shall hiss for the fly that is in the uttermost part of the rivers of Egypt, and for the bee that is in the land of Assyria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d820561f-641a-43a6-a26c-4e485d4edd78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: ISA 7:19
Text: And they shall come, and shall rest all of them in the desolate valleys, and in the holes of the rocks, and upon all thorns, and upon all bushes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc452396-a788-4e61-a618-bc4d0537186c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: ISA 7:20
Text: In the same day shall the Lord shave with a razor that is hired, namely, by them beyond the river, by the king of Assyria, the head, and the hair of the feet: and it shall also consume the beard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe8099ee-7dc0-4604-a31a-63f0c9cdb310>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: ISA 7:21
Text: And it shall come to pass in that day, that a man shall nourish a young cow, and two sheep;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fec51903-367e-4e64-bff1-eb16950dd981>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: ISA 7:22
Text: And it shall come to pass, for the abundance of milk that they shall give he shall eat butter: for butter and honey shall every one eat that is left in the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d529df60-e44f-45c6-a545-67a57982e1dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: ISA 7:23
Text: And it shall come to pass in that day, that every place shall be, where there were a thousand vines at a thousand silverlings, it shall even be for briers and thorns.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c5f6b82-80df-404b-b9aa-406f4e67d40b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: ISA 7:24
Text: With arrows and with bows shall men come thither; because all the land shall become briers and thorns.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/7/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d21509f7-7a3f-41ad-a2a2-2269faa7df4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: ISA 7:25
Text: And on all hills that shall be digged with the mattock, there shall not come thither the fear of briers and thorns: but it shall be for the sending forth of oxen, and for the treading of lesser cattle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/8/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:671328b3-4ab6-4f51-b0e6-62a8aaf261c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: ISA 8:1
Text: Moreover the LORD said unto me, Take thee a great roll, and write in it with a man’s pen concerning Mahershalalhashbaz.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/8/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e66da61c-485f-47b9-9a92-57b89b589e18>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: ISA 8:2
Text: And I took unto me faithful witnesses to record, Uriah the priest, and Zechariah the son of Jeberechiah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/8/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5defcf28-52a9-472f-82dd-e5f30e726135>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: ISA 8:3
Text: And I went unto the prophetess; and she conceived, and bare a son. Then said the LORD to me, Call his name Mahershalalhashbaz.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/8/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:def0d423-e31d-43ea-8e58-219f36855172>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: ISA 8:4
Text: For before the child shall have knowledge to cry, My father, and my mother, the riches of Damascus and the spoil of Samaria shall be taken away before the king of Assyria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/8/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76455a8c-bcf5-4ace-b161-085b0d5abd87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 68

Reference: ISA 8:5
Text: The LORD spake also unto me again, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/8/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:581c4878-3444-4c37-b210-0e5979f1ddcb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: ISA 8:6
Text: Forasmuch as this people refuseth the waters of Shiloah that go softly, and rejoice in Rezin and Remaliah’s son;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/8/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34c818d4-84b3-4337-8657-ac6fadd04c3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: ISA 8:7
Text: Now therefore, behold, the Lord bringeth up upon them the waters of the river, strong and many, even the king of Assyria, and all his glory: and he shall come up over all his channels, and go over all his banks:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/8/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f91e2739-995e-420e-a63c-0a350ef183ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: ISA 8:8
Text: And he shall pass through Judah; he shall overflow and go over, he shall reach even to the neck; and the stretching out of his wings shall fill the breadth of thy land, O Immanuel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/8/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18a9fa6a-c062-420d-9e32-f5be2120d851>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: ISA 8:9
Text: Associate yourselves, O ye people, and ye shall be broken in pieces; and give ear, all ye of far countries: gird yourselves, and ye shall be broken in pieces; gird yourselves, and ye shall be broken in pieces.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/8/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56506a13-7995-4b58-a156-1869f973b8ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: ISA 8:10
Text: Take counsel together, and it shall come to nought; speak the word, and it shall not stand: for God is with us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/8/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75d0fd31-37f2-4217-bd7c-36ec03014c14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: ISA 8:11
Text: For the LORD spake thus to me with a strong hand, and instructed me that I should not walk in the way of this people, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/8/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4785a9b3-de6f-4857-94b4-795950ebeaab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: ISA 8:12
Text: Say ye not, A confederacy, to all them to whom this people shall say, A confederacy; neither fear ye their fear, nor be afraid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/8/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:236bd485-9f50-4a5f-bd29-9d7fcbbd2b36>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: ISA 8:13
Text: Sanctify the LORD of hosts himself; and let him be your fear, and let him be your dread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/8/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ef93c1c-c232-431a-9e79-a50c4ab6b944>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: ISA 8:14
Text: And he shall be for a sanctuary; but for a stone of stumbling and for a rock of offence to both the houses of Israel, for a gin and for a snare to the inhabitants of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/8/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0a0d9d5-ec7e-4599-91eb-7fea8d35fa14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: ISA 8:15
Text: And many among them shall stumble, and fall, and be broken, and be snared, and be taken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/8/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4aacb2e4-66dc-4fd2-ba1a-c74d365d4bc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: ISA 8:16
Text: Bind up the testimony, seal the law among my disciples.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/8/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:befc6cb8-cf7d-4fc2-82e8-e2781fa63a3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: ISA 8:17
Text: And I will wait upon the LORD, that hideth his face from the house of Jacob, and I will look for him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/8/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e9417a7-e173-42cd-a49d-73857e9f7af2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: ISA 8:18
Text: Behold, I and the children whom the LORD hath given me are for signs and for wonders in Israel from the LORD of hosts, which dwelleth in mount Zion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/8/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c7eebfc-5d32-4f6d-bbe9-6e0309ca4b41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: ISA 8:19
Text: And when they shall say unto you, Seek unto them that have familiar spirits, and unto wizards that peep, and that mutter: should not a people seek unto their God? for the living to the dead?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/8/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d8ced57-8f4f-407f-bec0-ab5501d8c1ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: ISA 8:20
Text: To the law and to the testimony: if they speak not according to this word, it is because there is no light in them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/8/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f999ad8c-9260-4d16-aeb1-5ef85282c146>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: ISA 8:21
Text: And they shall pass through it, hardly bestead and hungry: and it shall come to pass, that when they shall be hungry, they shall fret themselves, and curse their king and their God, and look upward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/8/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:719d2e42-202a-4c0f-921a-577c367e2750>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: ISA 8:22
Text: And they shall look unto the earth; and behold trouble and darkness, dimness of anguish; and they shall be driven to darkness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/9/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:793e336c-55fa-449f-9855-7be4163a70c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 288

Reference: ISA 9:1
Text: Nevertheless the dimness shall not be such as was in her vexation, when at the first he lightly afflicted the land of Zebulun and the land of Naphtali, and afterward did more grievously afflict her by the way of the sea, beyond Jordan, in Galilee of the nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/9/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf7a61e3-43c3-41ad-b9be-fa37fdfdd529>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: ISA 9:2
Text: The people that walked in darkness have seen a great light: they that dwell in the land of the shadow of death, upon them hath the light shined.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/9/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:573ccf09-c266-4d3a-9e80-7753c8835c91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: ISA 9:3
Text: Thou hast multiplied the nation, and not increased the joy: they joy before thee according to the joy in harvest, and as men rejoice when they divide the spoil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/9/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ba84257-6066-413d-b2b4-84ee292404d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: ISA 9:4
Text: For thou hast broken the yoke of his burden, and the staff of his shoulder, the rod of his oppressor, as in the day of Midian.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/9/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:167eb7d6-3209-4a08-8293-dcddd0454ad3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: ISA 9:5
Text: For every battle of the warrior is with confused noise, and garments rolled in blood; but this shall be with burning and fuel of fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/9/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2906c44-d50c-415d-949b-bfa3e721316c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: ISA 9:6
Text: For unto us a child is born, unto us a son is given: and the government shall be upon his shoulder: and his name shall be called Wonderful, Counsellor, The mighty God, The everlasting Father, The Prince of Peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/9/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40801a9c-e7ae-42ac-9f11-3b5701c67bd1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: ISA 9:7
Text: Of the increase of his government and peace there shall be no end, upon the throne of David, and upon his kingdom, to order it, and to establish it with judgment and with justice from henceforth even for ever. The zeal of the LORD of hosts will perform this.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/9/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14616fe3-3a68-4a27-8970-64282ae29b2b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: ISA 9:8
Text: The Lord sent a word into Jacob, and it hath lighted upon Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/9/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8cb47d39-adf8-4fee-bf8a-49c8cb8ba4d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: ISA 9:9
Text: And all the people shall know, even Ephraim and the inhabitant of Samaria, that say in the pride and stoutness of heart,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/9/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:047bf2c5-c6ca-4079-a3e6-d5a922c6416f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: ISA 9:10
Text: The bricks are fallen down, but we will build with hewn stones: the sycomores are cut down, but we will change them into cedars.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/9/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d21689c-db81-4cfe-8349-9d94b5481ed3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: ISA 9:11
Text: Therefore the LORD shall set up the adversaries of Rezin against him, and join his enemies together;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/9/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:557bf407-e48b-4f4f-805c-b5d38464b517>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: ISA 9:12
Text: The Syrians before, and the Philistines behind; and they shall devour Israel with open mouth. For all this his anger is not turned away, but his hand is stretched out still.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/9/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5726123-7ced-40be-abcc-d082a6773f13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: ISA 9:13
Text: For the people turneth not unto him that smiteth them, neither do they seek the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/9/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44eb1b84-84e7-42e2-8904-fcb18eae41be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: ISA 9:14
Text: Therefore the LORD will cut off from Israel head and tail, branch and rush, in one day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/9/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8a318bb-9428-4a74-831a-50cc528c1dfc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: ISA 9:15
Text: The ancient and honourable, he is the head; and the prophet that teacheth lies, he is the tail.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/9/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b46a556-fca3-4e15-9930-236b1e0ed0df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: ISA 9:16
Text: For the leaders of this people cause them to err; and they that are led of them are destroyed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/9/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:386b186b-aadc-46e4-a5a3-5d4f317b798d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 299

Reference: ISA 9:17
Text: Therefore the LORD shall have no joy in their young men, neither shall have mercy on their fatherless and widows: for every one is an hypocrite and an evildoer, and every mouth speaketh folly. For all this his anger is not turned away, but his hand is stretched out still.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/9/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50b0cfe0-b030-41b8-b0e5-6faf9bd06934>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: ISA 9:18
Text: For wickedness burneth as the fire: it shall devour the briers and thorns, and shall kindle in the thickets of the forest, and they shall mount up like the lifting up of smoke.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/9/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44cc2b93-7101-4338-bcfa-a5fd8d632d82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: ISA 9:19
Text: Through the wrath of the LORD of hosts is the land darkened, and the people shall be as the fuel of the fire: no man shall spare his brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/9/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e150c3b-b345-4563-b3e2-98fbe4d141a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: ISA 9:20
Text: And he shall snatch on the right hand, and be hungry; and he shall eat on the left hand, and they shall not be satisfied: they shall eat every man the flesh of his own arm:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/9/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dea4b0de-9c00-4d10-b704-a0af792cea0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: ISA 9:21
Text: Manasseh, Ephraim; and Ephraim, Manasseh: and they together shall be against Judah. For all this his anger is not turned away, but his hand is stretched out still.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:996dfc54-6f47-4f88-bf5f-434087eb8e6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: ISA 10:1
Text: Woe unto them that decree unrighteous decrees, and that write grievousness which they have prescribed;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31f645dc-5ca5-42b4-b86d-af8dc49177f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: ISA 10:2
Text: To turn aside the needy from judgment, and to take away the right from the poor of my people, that widows may be their prey, and that they may rob the fatherless!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56222cc7-bc1c-467c-9dc0-44e5cd643128>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: ISA 10:3
Text: And what will ye do in the day of visitation, and in the desolation which shall come from far? to whom will ye flee for help? and where will ye leave your glory?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a3d6df3-3f7e-4ce4-9a8e-6eaf74bac0ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: ISA 10:4
Text: Without me they shall bow down under the prisoners, and they shall fall under the slain. For all this his anger is not turned away, but his hand is stretched out still.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47fe7796-fab8-475e-8595-cc0fa5e8e8fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: ISA 10:5
Text: O Assyrian, the rod of mine anger, and the staff in their hand is mine indignation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:423e9e4f-c6ef-4be5-8f0f-a71f08bc7df4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: ISA 10:6
Text: I will send him against an hypocritical nation, and against the people of my wrath will I give him a charge, to take the spoil, and to take the prey, and to tread them down like the mire of the streets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6ce2498-d11d-47da-81b4-a68e73e40afc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: ISA 10:7
Text: Howbeit he meaneth not so, neither doth his heart think so; but it is in his heart to destroy and cut off nations not a few.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03a5e148-6655-485e-96a3-06934f5f36ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: ISA 10:8
Text: For he saith, Are not my princes altogether kings?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fba1ba28-c590-4d95-aec3-a5e08cf34a43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: ISA 10:9
Text: Is not Calno as Carchemish? is not Hamath as Arpad? is not Samaria as Damascus?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d75b218-0567-400b-9982-50abfc3aa122>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: ISA 10:10
Text: As my hand hath found the kingdoms of the idols, and whose graven images did excel them of Jerusalem and of Samaria;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20b62218-b8bb-4a4b-a657-1b50377b6268>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: ISA 10:11
Text: Shall I not, as I have done unto Samaria and her idols, so do to Jerusalem and her idols?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:820964b3-6cec-4693-861e-f2e15c3408ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: ISA 10:12
Text: Wherefore it shall come to pass, that when the Lord hath performed his whole work upon mount Zion and on Jerusalem, I will punish the fruit of the stout heart of the king of Assyria, and the glory of his high looks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99acfc06-2731-4bdb-b475-16dee6fbe367>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: ISA 10:13
Text: For he saith, By the strength of my hand I have done it, and by my wisdom; for I am prudent: and I have removed the bounds of the people, and have robbed their treasures, and I have put down the inhabitants like a valiant man:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de464fd4-d876-4ec1-904b-778073d769df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: ISA 10:14
Text: And my hand hath found as a nest the riches of the people: and as one gathereth eggs that are left, have I gathered all the earth; and there was none that moved the wing, or opened the mouth, or peeped.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2571c0e-f58c-4767-be9d-3ff5cdb351b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 279

Reference: ISA 10:15
Text: Shall the axe boast itself against him that heweth therewith? or shall the saw magnify itself against him that shaketh it? as if the rod should shake itself against them that lift it up, or as if the staff should lift up itself, as if it were no wood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:788b2cd4-09a0-4403-852a-c1a156de9abb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: ISA 10:16
Text: Therefore shall the Lord, the Lord of hosts, send among his fat ones leanness; and under his glory he shall kindle a burning like the burning of a fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d0a0f9e-ac6b-4461-ba30-d219c5712c6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: ISA 10:17
Text: And the light of Israel shall be for a fire, and his Holy One for a flame: and it shall burn and devour his thorns and his briers in one day;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54e74c6b-e63e-40e7-b883-9b8837fda26d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: ISA 10:18
Text: And shall consume the glory of his forest, and of his fruitful field, both soul and body: and they shall be as when a standard-bearer fainteth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31fe02d9-c626-491e-9cb8-eaf77f384501>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: ISA 10:19
Text: And the rest of the trees of his forest shall be few, that a child may write them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1b02399-08d3-42bc-ab52-194ee269984e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: ISA 10:20
Text: And it shall come to pass in that day, that the remnant of Israel, and such as are escaped of the house of Jacob, shall no more again stay upon him that smote them; but shall stay upon the LORD, the Holy One of Israel, in truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:150863ef-50ff-429a-92d1-e59f1a58f722>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: ISA 10:21
Text: The remnant shall return, even the remnant of Jacob, unto the mighty God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89ee9a03-0b7d-4238-8a8b-aca67554cc66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: ISA 10:22
Text: For though thy people Israel be as the sand of the sea, yet a remnant of them shall return: the consumption decreed shall overflow with righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f048f067-f032-49e4-8ffa-2c67ee394154>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: ISA 10:23
Text: For the Lord GOD of hosts shall make a consumption, even determined, in the midst of all the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:241fe8be-d18d-4418-ad20-6b079631d357>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: ISA 10:24
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD of hosts, O my people that dwellest in Zion, be not afraid of the Assyrian: he shall smite thee with a rod, and shall lift up his staff against thee, after the manner of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e68c7e31-e305-4edd-a2c0-a4a2ac71bbfc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: ISA 10:25
Text: For yet a very little while, and the indignation shall cease, and mine anger in their destruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1888e88-8c22-42e7-83a9-32870f1e9966>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: ISA 10:26
Text: And the LORD of hosts shall stir up a scourge for him according to the slaughter of Midian at the rock of Oreb: and as his rod was upon the sea, so shall he lift it up after the manner of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be44cbab-66d5-41fc-88c5-1151c19646d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: ISA 10:27
Text: And it shall come to pass in that day, that his burden shall be taken away from off thy shoulder, and his yoke from off thy neck, and the yoke shall be destroyed because of the anointing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7e9325d-2405-4608-927c-e33575da4db3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: ISA 10:28
Text: He is come to Aiath, he is passed to Migron; at Michmash he hath laid up his carriages:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35c397a5-dd6b-4608-b923-05003a87a331>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: ISA 10:29
Text: They are gone over the passage: they have taken up their lodging at Geba; Ramah is afraid; Gibeah of Saul is fled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d80d0da-842b-4c2d-a87f-d5b6c25d3b37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: ISA 10:30
Text: Lift up thy voice, O daughter of Gallim: cause it to be heard unto Laish, O poor Anathoth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b89d54a-11a3-4dc2-879d-f997afb725a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: ISA 10:31
Text: Madmenah is removed; the inhabitants of Gebim gather themselves to flee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:530e6a4d-e2de-4e57-ac3e-d2d94e02321b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: ISA 10:32
Text: As yet shall he remain at Nob that day: he shall shake his hand against the mount of the daughter of Zion, the hill of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:966e9cb8-2919-48c8-b0ac-0c0c72548df5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: ISA 10:33
Text: Behold, the Lord, the LORD of hosts, shall lop the bough with terror: and the high ones of stature shall be hewn down, and the haughty shall be humbled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/10/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38200c2b-8333-4601-8a6f-c9787b66dcfb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: ISA 10:34
Text: And he shall cut down the thickets of the forest with iron, and Lebanon shall fall by a mighty one.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/11/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f20b9326-e9e9-493e-a68c-8fa2747d625b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: ISA 11:1
Text: And there shall come forth a rod out of the stem of Jesse, and a Branch shall grow out of his roots:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/11/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17310edf-cfc5-44a4-acb8-d7cdc0e47baa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: ISA 11:2
Text: And the spirit of the LORD shall rest upon him, the spirit of wisdom and understanding, the spirit of counsel and might, the spirit of knowledge and of the fear of the LORD;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/11/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22fa00e6-30f2-4b9f-8c80-75f21a83ac80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: ISA 11:3
Text: And shall make him of quick understanding in the fear of the LORD: and he shall not judge after the sight of his eyes, neither reprove after the hearing of his ears:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/11/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a885947-bd51-4b39-a45c-6ea20f64a905>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: ISA 11:4
Text: But with righteousness shall he judge the poor, and reprove with equity for the meek of the earth: and he shall smite the earth: with the rod of his mouth, and with the breath of his lips shall he slay the wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/11/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c41241c7-48fd-408a-a119-d8b7527708ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: ISA 11:5
Text: And righteousness shall be the girdle of his loins, and faithfulness the girdle of his reins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/11/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9cc0c621-d5ff-46e9-8e88-d778b717b05d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: ISA 11:6
Text: The wolf also shall dwell with the lamb, and the leopard shall lie down with the kid; and the calf and the young lion and the fatling together; and a little child shall lead them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/11/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f65da348-c004-4220-a536-c74a6676a64b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: ISA 11:7
Text: And the cow and the bear shall feed; their young ones shall lie down together: and the lion shall eat straw like the ox.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/11/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:647ecc27-3cd3-4f30-a4fc-360caa1eca9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: ISA 11:8
Text: And the sucking child shall play on the hole of the asp, and the weaned child shall put his hand on the cockatrice’ den.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/11/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d8103af-56ba-42b5-b576-42bf509ad954>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: ISA 11:9
Text: They shall not hurt nor destroy in all my holy mountain: for the earth shall be full of the knowledge of the LORD, as the waters cover the sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/11/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a97e5065-ba3a-4db1-819b-e675578dbf42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: ISA 11:10
Text: And in that day there shall be a root of Jesse, which shall stand for an ensign of the people; to it shall the Gentiles seek: and his rest shall be glorious.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/11/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85d99c11-70b8-487f-a910-547ddfc29159>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 325

Reference: ISA 11:11
Text: And it shall come to pass in that day, that the Lord shall set his hand again the second time to recover the remnant of his people, which shall be left, from Assyria, and from Egypt, and from Pathros, and from Cush, and from Elam, and from Shinar, and from Hamath, and from the islands of the sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/11/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c723637b-b6c0-468d-911c-2e8b6a0598b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: ISA 11:12
Text: And he shall set up an ensign for the nations, and shall assemble the outcasts of Israel, and gather together the dispersed of Judah from the four corners of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/11/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6c7e200-db11-47f2-8995-8ef50a47d476>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: ISA 11:13
Text: The envy also of Ephraim shall depart, and the adversaries of Judah shall be cut off: Ephraim shall not envy Judah, and Judah shall not vex Ephraim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/11/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b74c1706-6056-4e28-8811-4670b55c7f94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: ISA 11:14
Text: But they shall fly upon the shoulders of the Philistines toward the west; they shall spoil them of the east together: they shall lay their hand upon Edom and Moab; and the children of Ammon shall obey them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/11/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1112ba07-734c-49ea-9386-87806ffc1999>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: ISA 11:15
Text: And the LORD shall utterly destroy the tongue of the Egyptian sea; and with his mighty wind shall he shake his hand over the river, and shall smite it in the seven streams, and make men go over dryshod.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/11/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f64d56f-43fa-455a-a391-d35c17c38c64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: ISA 11:16
Text: And there shall be an highway for the remnant of his people, which shall be left, from Assyria; like as it was to Israel in the day that he came up out of the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/12/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80e1289d-e8c3-4fec-888d-f1eb230c704a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: ISA 12:1
Text: And in that day thou shalt say, O LORD, I will praise thee: though thou wast angry with me, thine anger is turned away, and thou comfortedst me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/12/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbfb6bea-d445-4d47-93b8-a9fa310cc049>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: ISA 12:2
Text: Behold, God is my salvation; I will trust, and not be afraid: for the LORD JEHOVAH is my strength and my song; he also is become my salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/12/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c139a455-a4ac-4f2e-9888-a082f90c1aab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: ISA 12:3
Text: Therefore with joy shall ye draw water out of the wells of salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/12/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0fe5ef83-a012-4100-aa13-c0773b5516d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: ISA 12:4
Text: And in that day shall ye say, Praise the LORD, call upon his name, declare his doings among the people, make mention that his name is exalted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/12/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e29a2872-bdce-41ad-92e4-29a6dcff3957>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: ISA 12:5
Text: Sing unto the LORD; for he hath done excellent things: this is known in all the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/12/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01949b4c-f35b-4a66-86ac-d6d56a702e9f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: ISA 12:6
Text: Cry out and shout, thou inhabitant of Zion: for great is the Holy One of Israel in the midst of thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/13/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5e7eaec-ae26-4b89-8d4a-3d936120cd29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: ISA 13:1
Text: The burden of Babylon, which Isaiah the son of Amoz did see.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/13/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6d3aacf-fdb4-4da4-9bf0-39ff22f3514c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: ISA 13:2
Text: Lift ye up a banner upon the high mountain, exalt the voice unto them, shake the hand, that they may go into the gates of the nobles.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/13/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1750736-0d60-4d6b-911e-e28e075016a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: ISA 13:3
Text: I have commanded my sanctified ones, I have also called my mighty ones for mine anger, even them that rejoice in my highness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/13/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5129f81-08da-414e-a900-b5f205923497>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: ISA 13:4
Text: The noise of a multitude in the mountains, like as of a great people; a tumultuous noise of the kingdoms of nations gathered together: the LORD of hosts mustereth the host of the battle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/13/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a611859-2ea5-4884-9fce-ce7b808bc28f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: ISA 13:5
Text: They come from a far country, from the end of heaven, even the LORD, and the weapons of his indignation, to destroy the whole land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/13/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fad93f0-02af-4711-b434-3398623b8f7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: ISA 13:6
Text: Howl ye; for the day of the LORD is at hand; it shall come as a destruction from the Almighty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/13/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:928887c8-223f-4b15-97bf-f0323b3db90b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: ISA 13:7
Text: Therefore shall all hands be faint, and every man’s heart shall melt:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/13/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0ae8d80-48e5-408c-a5f1-3479f04681a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: ISA 13:8
Text: And they shall be afraid: pangs and sorrows shall take hold of them; they shall be in pain as a woman that travaileth: they shall be amazed one at another; their faces shall be as flames.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/13/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28802db3-bd72-460e-9f46-4cd46bd41b27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: ISA 13:9
Text: Behold, the day of the LORD cometh, cruel both with wrath and fierce anger, to lay the land desolate: and he shall destroy the sinners thereof out of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/13/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e71ad01a-8f3e-4e5a-81d8-223b6829499f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: ISA 13:10
Text: For the stars of heaven and the constellations thereof shall not give their light: the sun shall be darkened in his going forth, and the moon shall not cause her light to shine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/13/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a7345e5-b0db-4be5-9a34-04dd2fd0464d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: ISA 13:11
Text: And I will punish the world for their evil, and the wicked for their iniquity; and I will cause the arrogancy of the proud to cease, and will lay low the haughtiness of the terrible.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/13/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4791b995-2ec8-4d67-ab64-4e560d8fe9ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: ISA 13:12
Text: I will make a man more precious than fine gold; even a man than the golden wedge of Ophir.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/13/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79e41445-c5b4-414e-b4ba-47290e877ef0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: ISA 13:13
Text: Therefore I will shake the heavens, and the earth shall remove out of her place, in the wrath of the LORD of hosts, and in the day of his fierce anger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/13/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea49c09f-670e-449a-9012-bf16ac77defc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: ISA 13:14
Text: And it shall be as the chased roe, and as a sheep that no man taketh up: they shall every man turn to his own people, and flee every one into his own land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/13/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b8abca4-8c4f-4209-8a1a-3eb4695e5c38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: ISA 13:15
Text: Every one that is found shall be thrust through; and every one that is joined unto them shall fall by the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/13/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bcb9c515-29c7-4718-89c7-a28eec971f19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: ISA 13:16
Text: Their children also shall be dashed to pieces before their eyes; their houses shall be spoiled, and their wives ravished.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/13/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22815098-2230-4f17-b229-dce87ce6abd0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: ISA 13:17
Text: Behold, I will stir up the Medes against them, which shall not regard silver; and as for gold, they shall not delight in it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/13/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:415c80f6-1a31-4551-8bdd-6fd8874ff39d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: ISA 13:18
Text: Their bows also shall dash the young men to pieces; and they shall have no pity on the fruit of the womb; their eyes shall not spare children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/13/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7f58b30-70fb-4100-824a-478ee882eb2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: ISA 13:19
Text: And Babylon, the glory of kingdoms, the beauty of the Chaldees’ excellency, shall be as when God overthrew Sodom and Gomorrah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/13/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f77b424-680e-4bd9-9014-f3716a03a49a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: ISA 13:20
Text: It shall never be inhabited, neither shall it be dwelt in from generation to generation: neither shall the Arabian pitch tent there; neither shall the shepherds make their fold there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/13/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11c9a6e4-c408-4b08-81c5-2fae1b192da5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: ISA 13:21
Text: But wild beasts of the desert shall lie there; and their houses shall be full of doleful creatures; and owls shall dwell there, and satyrs shall dance there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/13/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3e5be24-b203-4a4b-adb9-6b2dfb676e27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: ISA 13:22
Text: And the wild beasts of the islands shall cry in their desolate houses, and dragons in their pleasant palaces: and her time is near to come, and her days shall not be prolonged.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfc53b89-1038-447b-ac1d-a29ecde6f5c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: ISA 14:1
Text: For the LORD will have mercy on Jacob, and will yet choose Israel, and set them in their own land: and the strangers shall be joined with them, and they shall cleave to the house of Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05484516-3579-4f44-b575-023c9d5d3f94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 288

Reference: ISA 14:2
Text: And the people shall take them, and bring them to their place: and the house of Israel shall possess them in the land of the LORD for servants and handmaids: and they shall take them captives, whose captives they were; and they shall rule over their oppressors.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31f8ffb9-1a04-4861-b9cc-1c5ddfac019b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: ISA 14:3
Text: And it shall come to pass in the day that the LORD shall give thee rest from thy sorrow, and from thy fear, and from the hard bondage wherein thou wast made to serve,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebc9a342-4f98-4c21-99b8-ca8ca249ab25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: ISA 14:4
Text: That thou shalt take up this proverb against the king of Babylon, and say, How hath the oppressor ceased! the golden city ceased!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:304a3cae-ca7b-4adc-a08e-8c53420de7fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: ISA 14:5
Text: The LORD hath broken the staff of the wicked, and the sceptre of the rulers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c925e3d-c711-40b2-97a0-d992f3cb218d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: ISA 14:6
Text: He who smote the people in wrath with a continual stroke, he that ruled the nations in anger, is persecuted, and none hindereth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01be19d8-9111-49b5-bf8d-e73bb4dd227a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: ISA 14:7
Text: The whole earth is at rest, and is quiet: they break forth into singing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af647c39-0c9d-464b-b7cd-17efc18e3c7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: ISA 14:8
Text: Yea, the fir trees rejoice at thee, and the cedars of Lebanon, saying, Since thou art laid down, no feller is come up against us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b6facd0-a2ff-4a7f-ac4e-4a79224a7b16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: ISA 14:9
Text: Hell from beneath is moved for thee to meet thee at thy coming: it stirreth up the dead for thee, even all the chief ones of the earth; it hath raised up from their thrones all the kings of the nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0298edf2-4519-4d2b-8155-f3855f30895d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: ISA 14:10
Text: All they shall speak and say unto thee, Art thou also become weak as we? art thou become like unto us?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d77ee9c0-5815-416f-8d26-7db568fb28b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: ISA 14:11
Text: Thy pomp is brought down to the grave, and the noise of thy viols: the worm is spread under thee, and the worms cover thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3bea5cc-53dd-4c54-9388-d2391464d194>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: ISA 14:12
Text: How art thou fallen from heaven, O Lucifer, son of the morning! how art thou cut down to the ground, which didst weaken the nations!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d91031b4-93e2-4018-8c1c-854cae3a18c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: ISA 14:13
Text: For thou hast said in thine heart, I will ascend into heaven, I will exalt my throne above the stars of God: I will sit also upon the mount of the congregation, in the sides of the north:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a13f72d-8bab-443f-9927-4eb020062a8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: ISA 14:14
Text: I will ascend above the heights of the clouds; I will be like the most High.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5de9d24a-b82b-4de2-a7e4-b74efc3d7ba1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: ISA 14:15
Text: Yet thou shalt be brought down to hell, to the sides of the pit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d7c11aa-194f-4a67-a57d-dbb54acbfa69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: ISA 14:16
Text: They that see thee shall narrowly look upon thee, and consider thee, saying, Is this the man that made the earth to tremble, that did shake kingdoms;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c2d666e-7508-4025-b102-b060e3e6417a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: ISA 14:17
Text: That made the world as a wilderness, and destroyed the cities thereof; that opened not the house of his prisoners?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7045e40-66b8-4ff4-97ac-13d7f496bba9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: ISA 14:18
Text: All the kings of the nations, even all of them, lie in glory, every one in his own house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3b5dc14-f441-4918-bfcd-fdcda3829d4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: ISA 14:19
Text: But thou art cast out of thy grave like an abominable branch, and as the raiment of those that are slain, thrust through with a sword, that go down to the stones of the pit; as a carcase trodden under feet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1afb0b7c-9208-4e5a-9bbb-4c2ad1d5b386>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: ISA 14:20
Text: Thou shalt not be joined with them in burial, because thou hast destroyed thy land, and slain thy people: the seed of evildoers shall never be renowned.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b9a6641-0047-4442-9599-40d815141238>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: ISA 14:21
Text: Prepare slaughter for his children for the iniquity of their fathers; that they do not rise, nor possess the land, nor fill the face of the world with cities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30aed2fc-ca34-41e9-8102-fd1803b58821>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: ISA 14:22
Text: For I will rise up against them, saith the LORD of hosts, and cut off from Babylon the name, and remnant, and son, and nephew, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2eccb909-ef4b-4c95-8b33-f69774ada1f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: ISA 14:23
Text: I will also make it a possession for the bittern, and pools of water: and I will sweep it with the besom of destruction, saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4e78b88-10ee-4510-a621-c13e0ab898ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: ISA 14:24
Text: The LORD of hosts hath sworn, saying, Surely as I have thought, so shall it come to pass; and as I have purposed, so shall it stand:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edb7f968-8895-4904-80a5-9cf419fd2ab3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: ISA 14:25
Text: That I will break the Assyrian in my land, and upon my mountains tread him under foot: then shall his yoke depart from off them, and his burden depart from off their shoulders.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc8e659a-2a4a-491b-ae2b-153f2ddf9010>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: ISA 14:26
Text: This is the purpose that is purposed upon the whole earth: and this is the hand that is stretched out upon all the nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d5606cf-a610-4461-9255-cce428e42510>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: ISA 14:27
Text: For the LORD of hosts hath purposed, and who shall disannul it? and his hand is stretched out, and who shall turn it back?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5f317f2-aa73-4149-b87a-22002e32367d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: ISA 14:28
Text: In the year that king Ahaz died was this burden.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eef9a662-2a5e-4903-ad00-187d758b69f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: ISA 14:29
Text: Rejoice not thou, whole Palestina, because the rod of him that smote thee is broken: for out of the serpent’s root shall come forth a cockatrice, and his fruit shall be a fiery flying serpent.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4636fd60-232d-44ff-af6a-cc0b06659cd3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: ISA 14:30
Text: And the firstborn of the poor shall feed, and the needy shall lie down in safety: and I will kill thy root with famine, and he shall slay thy remnant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:687e336d-2556-423c-9b50-c14482989544>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: ISA 14:31
Text: Howl, O gate; cry, O city; thou, whole Palestina, art dissolved: for there shall come from the north a smoke, and none shall be alone in his appointed times.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/14/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9dd47f8c-d423-47ad-a519-dfcdcf1435df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: ISA 14:32
Text: What shall one then answer the messengers of the nation? That the LORD hath founded Zion, and the poor of his people shall trust in it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/15/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c78e1289-f180-4e7d-a3c5-cc8b7f035506>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: ISA 15:1
Text: The burden of Moab. Because in the night Ar of Moab is laid waste, and brought to silence; because in the night Kir of Moab is laid waste, and brought to silence;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/15/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:113102bb-8fd0-4ea4-bab6-397a460cc413>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: ISA 15:2
Text: He is gone up to Bajith, and to Dibon, the high places, to weep: Moab shall howl over Nebo, and over Medeba: on all their heads shall be baldness, and every beard cut off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/15/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c983409-2be9-4624-aaec-ff2b2b3142ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: ISA 15:3
Text: In their streets they shall gird themselves with sackcloth: on the tops of their houses, and in their streets, every one shall howl, weeping abundantly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/15/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df62ff3e-451a-45af-bce1-b73cd41c5c26>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: ISA 15:4
Text: And Heshbon shall cry, and Elealeh: their voice shall be heard even unto Jahaz: therefore the armed soldiers of Moab shall cry out; his life shall be grievous unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/15/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a4d29a9-3596-4ca8-8212-04143b56db2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: ISA 15:5
Text: My heart shall cry out for Moab; his fugitives shall flee unto Zoar, an heifer of three years old: for by the mounting up of Luhith with weeping shall they go it up; for in the way of Horonaim they shall raise up a cry of destruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/15/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:535ba01b-05ef-43b4-b119-83d4d4dd0f96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: ISA 15:6
Text: For the waters of Nimrim shall be desolate: for the hay is withered away, the grass faileth, there is no green thing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/15/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e71a1a6-e169-4a7c-b1c3-6c341c9f65ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: ISA 15:7
Text: Therefore the abundance they have gotten, and that which they have laid up, shall they carry away to the brook of the willows.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/15/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4b35558-9e44-4a1c-897a-53c5e5e88438>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: ISA 15:8
Text: For the cry is gone round about the borders of Moab; the howling thereof unto Eglaim, and the howling thereof unto Beerelim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/15/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b62c0944-4b78-4e73-b681-306448bedfea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: ISA 15:9
Text: For the waters of Dimon shall be full of blood: for I will bring more upon Dimon, lions upon him that escapeth of Moab, and upon the remnant of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/16/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab28cf28-a450-49c7-8781-af865bf259d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: ISA 16:1
Text: Send ye the lamb to the ruler of the land from Sela to the wilderness, unto the mount of the daughter of Zion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/16/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40c5494b-8c8f-4a48-90de-2028851c67ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: ISA 16:2
Text: For it shall be, that, as a wandering bird cast out of the nest, so the daughters of Moab shall be at the fords of Arnon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/16/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9db43777-ea20-4660-b808-a6ff971dac8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: ISA 16:3
Text: Take counsel, execute judgment; make thy shadow as the night in the midst of the noonday; hide the outcasts; bewray not him that wandereth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/16/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3d0e18c-86f5-4d78-a33f-de5cf9a72d59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: ISA 16:4
Text: Let mine outcasts dwell with thee, Moab; be thou a covert to them from the face of the spoiler: for the extortioner is at an end, the spoiler ceaseth, the oppressors are consumed out of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/16/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:baf7e3b7-742e-463f-a81b-624b7e14b2aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: ISA 16:5
Text: And in mercy shall the throne be established: and he shall sit upon it in truth in the tabernacle of David, judging, and seeking judgment, and hasting righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/16/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3a8cc03-d3b8-4e05-a47d-5a53dbdd97bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: ISA 16:6
Text: We have heard of the pride of Moab; he is very proud: even of his haughtiness, and his pride, and his wrath: but his lies shall not be so.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/16/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42c991b4-c393-495e-b718-816217dd6a5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: ISA 16:7
Text: Therefore shall Moab howl for Moab, every one shall howl: for the foundations of Kirhareseth shall ye mourn; surely they are stricken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/16/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26f57c0c-deb1-46cc-8486-e296d5ab5b9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 287

Reference: ISA 16:8
Text: For the fields of Heshbon languish, and the vine of Sibmah: the lords of the heathen have broken down the principal plants thereof, they are come even unto Jazer, they wandered through the wilderness: her branches are stretched out, they are gone over the sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/16/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a53f1447-d1ef-4178-b7d0-463d299bc497>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: ISA 16:9
Text: Therefore I will bewail with the weeping of Jazer the vine of Sibmah: I will water thee with my tears, O Heshbon, and Elealeh: for the shouting for thy summer fruits and for thy harvest is fallen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/16/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:536d8689-670f-49e6-a947-7907ef9519ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: ISA 16:10
Text: And gladness is taken away, and joy out of the plentiful field; and in the vineyards there shall be no singing, neither shall there be shouting: the treaders shall tread out no wine in their presses; I have made their vintage shouting to cease.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/16/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7890a917-922a-4b5e-a55e-0cce310ba0c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: ISA 16:11
Text: Wherefore my bowels shall sound like an harp for Moab, and mine inward parts for Kirharesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/16/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09f46802-8c35-4381-8401-92ba8a54b2ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: ISA 16:12
Text: And it shall come to pass, when it is seen that Moab is weary on the high place, that he shall come to his sanctuary to pray; but he shall not prevail.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/16/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ca9b567-493a-4171-9253-515aca62072c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: ISA 16:13
Text: This is the word that the LORD hath spoken concerning Moab since that time.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/16/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2e929f3-b8b8-4829-868a-5215f896619d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: ISA 16:14
Text: But now the LORD hath spoken, saying, Within three years, as the years of an hireling, and the glory of Moab shall be contemned, with all that great multitude; and the remnant shall be very small and feeble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/17/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:915c1858-b091-4855-b8db-f96980f2e02a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: ISA 17:1
Text: The burden of Damascus. Behold, Damascus is taken away from being a city, and it shall be a ruinous heap.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/17/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ecc9f162-79e4-40a2-bf61-028ec3403646>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: ISA 17:2
Text: The cities of Aroer are forsaken: they shall be for flocks, which shall lie down, and none shall make them afraid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/17/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14d57d57-e3eb-4fdd-ad89-dde597f8ab00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: ISA 17:3
Text: The fortress also shall cease from Ephraim, and the kingdom from Damascus, and the remnant of Syria: they shall be as the glory of the children of Israel, saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/17/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43b25b09-d61c-4924-8dd0-a9a4c60a32b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: ISA 17:4
Text: And in that day it shall come to pass, that the glory of Jacob shall be made thin, and the fatness of his flesh shall wax lean.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/17/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62046eac-8e94-4dc4-a389-1a28ffc31fc9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: ISA 17:5
Text: And it shall be as when the harvestman gathereth the corn, and reapeth the ears with his arm; and it shall be as he that gathereth ears in the valley of Rephaim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/17/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ff8db5c-6302-4b3d-9c01-a6b5fcade065>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: ISA 17:6
Text: Yet gleaning grapes shall be left in it, as the shaking of an olive tree, two or three berries in the top of the uppermost bough, four or five in the outmost fruitful branches thereof, saith the LORD God of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/17/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13c1c7c2-46ee-4ede-bfb2-c1e80a667b6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: ISA 17:7
Text: At that day shall a man look to his Maker, and his eyes shall have respect to the Holy One of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/17/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cc02542-3724-435b-bac9-2a9793b5d864>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: ISA 17:8
Text: And he shall not look to the altars, the work of his hands, neither shall respect that which his fingers have made, either the groves, or the images.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/17/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e891de37-c0fb-4ec2-86a1-6949b5fd3fcb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: ISA 17:9
Text: In that day shall his strong cities be as a forsaken bough, and an uppermost branch, which they left because of the children of Israel: and there shall be desolation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/17/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b0b7926-b31f-4a39-8e61-f08ec3174d10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: ISA 17:10
Text: Because thou hast forgotten the God of thy salvation, and hast not been mindful of the rock of thy strength, therefore shalt thou plant pleasant plants, and shalt set it with strange slips:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/17/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:217c66d2-ed12-45c9-9d9c-f0b1cac3c5cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: ISA 17:11
Text: In the day shalt thou make thy plant to grow, and in the morning shalt thou make thy seed to flourish: but the harvest shall be a heap in the day of grief and of desperate sorrow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/17/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9c4bf38-9ad1-458b-8e93-efd85f80dce9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: ISA 17:12
Text: Woe to the multitude of many people, which make a noise like the noise of the seas; and to the rushing of nations, that make a rushing like the rushing of mighty waters!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/17/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de1df3a4-e0ff-4f16-8f69-c5926bdf2fe2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: ISA 17:13
Text: The nations shall rush like the rushing of many waters: but God shall rebuke them, and they shall flee far off, and shall be chased as the chaff of the mountains before the wind, and like a rolling thing before the whirlwind.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/17/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:962b9702-7ca8-4f19-8892-26b2f847294e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: ISA 17:14
Text: And behold at eveningtide trouble; and before the morning he is not. This is the portion of them that spoil us, and the lot of them that rob us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/18/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95dfbb50-b8bb-4931-9a8d-b0e6530c1b10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: ISA 18:1
Text: Woe to the land shadowing with wings, which is beyond the rivers of Ethiopia:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/18/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:087b17cb-98b4-4e62-8033-d0f8414085e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 301

Reference: ISA 18:2
Text: That sendeth ambassadors by the sea, even in vessels of bulrushes upon the waters, saying, Go, ye swift messengers, to a nation scattered and peeled, to a people terrible from their beginning hitherto; a nation meted out and trodden down, whose land the rivers have spoiled!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/18/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c946857a-122b-4142-a76d-8bd28660d282>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: ISA 18:3
Text: All ye inhabitants of the world, and dwellers on the earth, see ye, when he lifteth up an ensign on the mountains; and when he bloweth a trumpet, hear ye.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/18/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d09eed0-bdbf-42e9-8904-de9c32df9576>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: ISA 18:4
Text: For so the LORD said unto me, I will take my rest, and I will consider in my dwelling place like a clear heat upon herbs, and like a cloud of dew in the heat of harvest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/18/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1a8209d-f34b-40a6-bd78-21bf9be97647>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: ISA 18:5
Text: For afore the harvest, when the bud is perfect, and the sour grape is ripening in the flower, he shall both cut off the sprigs with pruning hooks, and take away and cut down the branches.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/18/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe8b11a9-dc6b-4245-8ee4-1b139efafaff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: ISA 18:6
Text: They shall be left together unto the fowls of the mountains, and to the beasts of the earth: and the fowls shall summer upon them, and all the beasts of the earth shall winter upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/18/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b34fb15-49ff-4341-90b1-d24a348541a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 325

Reference: ISA 18:7
Text: In that time shall the present be brought unto the LORD of hosts of a people scattered and peeled, and from a people terrible from their beginning hitherto; a nation meted out and trodden under foot, whose land the rivers have spoiled, to the place of the name of the LORD of hosts, the mount Zion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15441527-98bf-4dbf-80fc-c0e32b4e4c55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: ISA 19:1
Text: The burden of Egypt. Behold, the LORD rideth upon a swift cloud, and shall come into Egypt: and the idols of Egypt shall be moved at his presence, and the heart of Egypt shall melt in the midst of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13065d59-a085-4428-ad0a-f0bd1fced0de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: ISA 19:2
Text: And I will set the Egyptians against the Egyptians: and they shall fight every one against his brother, and every one against his neighbour; city against city, and kingdom against kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3898a636-3f4e-4955-a834-d7afd63c9d17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: ISA 19:3
Text: And the spirit of Egypt shall fail in the midst thereof; and I will destroy the counsel thereof: and they shall seek to the idols, and to the charmers, and to them that have familiar spirits, and to the wizards.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0111778b-55a7-4af5-bb2b-0a222fe54940>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: ISA 19:4
Text: And the Egyptians will I give over into the hand of a cruel lord; and a fierce king shall rule over them, saith the Lord, the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a31ebac4-1cd0-49fc-a512-084a83dfe292>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: ISA 19:5
Text: And the waters shall fail from the sea, and the river shall be wasted and dried up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d3bbeca-2394-4288-af40-21c7468c1a26>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: ISA 19:6
Text: And they shall turn the rivers far away; and the brooks of defence shall be emptied and dried up: the reeds and flags shall wither.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91c7a3a5-bbd2-42ba-afe3-621aae292464>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: ISA 19:7
Text: The paper reeds by the brooks, by the mouth of the brooks, and every thing sown by the brooks, shall wither, be driven away, and be no more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ffa940e-d22d-4914-aa2a-044c93c8cedf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: ISA 19:8
Text: The fishers also shall mourn, and all they that cast angle into the brooks shall lament, and they that spread nets upon the waters shall languish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bfa33ba7-6966-4c2c-bfc9-efc5e1541891>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: ISA 19:9
Text: Moreover they that work in fine flax, and they that weave networks, shall be confounded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6eaf14c5-5b74-4ea2-a49f-b26c29cc76c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: ISA 19:10
Text: And they shall be broken in the purposes thereof, all that make sluices and ponds for fish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a9cda1f-1949-42fd-9e6f-ebda7bc5acad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: ISA 19:11
Text: Surely the princes of Zoan are fools, the counsel of the wise counsellors of Pharaoh is become brutish: how say ye unto Pharaoh, I am the son of the wise, the son of ancient kings?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7343221f-9047-4b3c-be70-6b066ceda35a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: ISA 19:12
Text: Where are they? where are thy wise men? and let them tell thee now, and let them know what the LORD of hosts hath purposed upon Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d0f802b-ce27-477f-8847-4d9625bc1280>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: ISA 19:13
Text: The princes of Zoan are become fools, the princes of Noph are deceived; they have also seduced Egypt, even they that are the stay of the tribes thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9cfdaf5-5cb0-415b-af17-20d7a196fd3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: ISA 19:14
Text: The LORD hath mingled a perverse spirit in the midst thereof: and they have caused Egypt to err in every work thereof, as a drunken man staggereth in his vomit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6c52026-7f1e-4a38-8302-a1b5c6b81bbb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: ISA 19:15
Text: Neither shall there be any work for Egypt, which the head or tail, branch or rush, may do.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbd2019d-9b02-4f86-ab37-ccab5701dfea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: ISA 19:16
Text: In that day shall Egypt be like unto women: and it shall be afraid and fear because of the shaking of the hand of the LORD of hosts, which he shaketh over it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c18380b-bc22-4b36-ae61-68e950a48313>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: ISA 19:17
Text: And the land of Judah shall be a terror unto Egypt, every one that maketh mention thereof shall be afraid in himself, because of the counsel of the LORD of hosts, which he hath determined against it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2812c440-9bef-4e21-92ed-4de6daa9ace6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: ISA 19:18
Text: In that day shall five cities in the land of Egypt speak the language of Canaan, and swear to the LORD of hosts; one shall be called, The city of destruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf2c2727-b0d0-4015-94fd-ba726fb1daf8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: ISA 19:19
Text: In that day shall there be an altar to the LORD in the midst of the land of Egypt, and a pillar at the border thereof to the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9e0d11f-3618-4bb2-b294-4686a9d4f18f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: ISA 19:20
Text: And it shall be for a sign and for a witness unto the LORD of hosts in the land of Egypt: for they shall cry unto the LORD because of the oppressors, and he shall send them a saviour, and a great one, and he shall deliver them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db3f98ce-4b51-4736-a8c9-02ea9ce6a746>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: ISA 19:21
Text: And the LORD shall be known to Egypt, and the Egyptians shall know the LORD in that day, and shall do sacrifice and oblation; yea, they shall vow a vow unto the LORD, and perform it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8a1611e-fded-43df-81da-01eda7fc135d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: ISA 19:22
Text: And the LORD shall smite Egypt: he shall smite and heal it: and they shall return even to the LORD, and he shall be intreated of them, and shall heal them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16140771-252b-49fc-a18c-7ed013ca333e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: ISA 19:23
Text: In that day shall there be a highway out of Egypt to Assyria, and the Assyrian shall come into Egypt, and the Egyptian into Assyria, and the Egyptians shall serve with the Assyrians.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99ba8118-ded9-4e5d-bfb6-02e7a7cf3d32>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: ISA 19:24
Text: In that day shall Israel be the third with Egypt and with Assyria, even a blessing in the midst of the land:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/19/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9953c14a-8230-442e-beea-19d760966d06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: ISA 19:25
Text: Whom the LORD of hosts shall bless, saying, Blessed be Egypt my people, and Assyria the work of my hands, and Israel mine inheritance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/20/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c86c034c-74e6-478d-9e0e-044bf31b6f10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: ISA 20:1
Text: In the year that Tartan came unto Ashdod, (when Sargon the king of Assyria sent him,) and fought against Ashdod, and took it;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/20/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67f6e366-6260-4068-ab3a-f83f926cd3b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: ISA 20:2
Text: At the same time spake the LORD by Isaiah the son of Amoz, saying, Go and loose the sackcloth from off thy loins, and put off thy shoe from thy foot. And he did so, walking naked and barefoot.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/20/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c32d3c44-6aa8-4d1f-b5c5-007d727b3209>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: ISA 20:3
Text: And the LORD said, Like as my servant Isaiah hath walked naked and barefoot three years for a sign and wonder upon Egypt and upon Ethiopia;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/20/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e35561f-800c-4709-b339-a7f1ac601f3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: ISA 20:4
Text: So shall the king of Assyria lead away the Egyptians prisoners, and the Ethiopians captives, young and old, naked and barefoot, even with their buttocks uncovered, to the shame of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/20/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d5f4431-4a86-4181-9a8d-4a6601f0f8c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: ISA 20:5
Text: And they shall be afraid and ashamed of Ethiopia their expectation, and of Egypt their glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/20/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f8d3c95-726c-4fd0-ab9c-92fac57050af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: ISA 20:6
Text: And the inhabitant of this isle shall say in that day, Behold, such is our expectation, whither we flee for help to be delivered from the king of Assyria: and how shall we escape?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/21/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef4b319f-93bd-4c79-a6a6-a56ae470dd70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: ISA 21:1
Text: The burden of the desert of the sea. As whirlwinds in the south pass through; so it cometh from the desert, from a terrible land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/21/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:564f86d7-25d8-44b2-8462-e8bd6dea3b2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: ISA 21:2
Text: A grievous vision is declared unto me; the treacherous dealer dealeth treacherously, and the spoiler spoileth. Go up, O Elam: besiege, O Media; all the sighing thereof have I made to cease.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/21/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af985154-d8ce-4b74-a72f-27d4b7865042>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: ISA 21:3
Text: Therefore are my loins filled with pain: pangs have taken hold upon me, as the pangs of a woman that travaileth: I was bowed down at the hearing of it; I was dismayed at the seeing of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/21/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2cddedb-97f3-40de-895c-291e8867b4fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: ISA 21:4
Text: My heart panted, fearfulness affrighted me: the night of my pleasure hath he turned into fear unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/21/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6253b6c3-2bef-42b4-99ee-67132dbfb218>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: ISA 21:5
Text: Prepare the table, watch in the watchtower, eat, drink: arise, ye princes, and anoint the shield.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/21/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5578f84c-682b-402e-91c3-2d540f8fdac0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: ISA 21:6
Text: For thus hath the LORD said unto me, Go, set a watchman, let him declare what he seeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/21/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93022ca9-a3b3-4e74-8bdd-7c45c0f10e5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: ISA 21:7
Text: And he saw a chariot with a couple of horsemen, a chariot of asses, and a chariot of camels; and he hearkened diligently with much heed:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/21/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ee7737a-f4c4-46fc-8b3f-064476bc9502>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: ISA 21:8
Text: And he cried, A lion: My lord, I stand continually upon the watchtower in the daytime, and I am set in my ward whole nights:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/21/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d0237a5-5e91-4161-832b-b6c2449cc251>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: ISA 21:9
Text: And, behold, here cometh a chariot of men, with a couple of horsemen. And he answered and said, Babylon is fallen, is fallen; and all the graven images of her gods he hath broken unto the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/21/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07588c12-2ea4-4ae4-9994-8a9c1d39d3ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: ISA 21:10
Text: O my threshing, and the corn of my floor: that which I have heard of the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, have I declared unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/21/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76c6ecc9-015d-4dec-b6fc-0bd5f12ac6d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: ISA 21:11
Text: The burden of Dumah. He calleth to me out of Seir, Watchman, what of the night? Watchman, what of the night?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/21/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9503d33f-1ae3-41ce-ae49-18ddd743ec25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: ISA 21:12
Text: The watchman said, The morning cometh, and also the night: if ye will enquire, enquire ye: return, come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/21/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c341ba21-62f6-4cf5-88b9-b5ac5d947bb8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: ISA 21:13
Text: The burden upon Arabia. In the forest in Arabia shall ye lodge, O ye travelling companies of Dedanim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/21/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05b5dea4-03dc-4f45-bb28-67b3847b6b12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: ISA 21:14
Text: The inhabitants of the land of Tema brought water to him that was thirsty, they prevented with their bread him that fled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/21/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:674c0d67-1dcf-4c4d-8472-5b1824159fc9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: ISA 21:15
Text: For they fled from the swords, from the drawn sword, and from the bent bow, and from the grievousness of war.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/21/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85c40cb8-ea64-43b3-8d44-c4524fac0f79>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: ISA 21:16
Text: For thus hath the LORD said unto me, Within a year, according to the years of an hireling, and all the glory of Kedar shall fail:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/21/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0231b9e7-dc49-47d2-a384-a6692dd9d9f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: ISA 21:17
Text: And the residue of the number of archers, the mighty men of the children of Kedar, shall be diminished: for the LORD God of Israel hath spoken it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:771ad556-c798-4393-9fdb-01c33a83512c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: ISA 22:1
Text: The burden of the valley of vision. What aileth thee now, that thou art wholly gone up to the housetops?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:558cc88a-37c7-412b-9798-9c9e98f07180>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: ISA 22:2
Text: Thou that art full of stirs, a tumultuous city, joyous city: thy slain men are not slain with the sword, nor dead in battle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b7e0f43-7ec0-40c2-b78b-ac819221498f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: ISA 22:3
Text: All thy rulers are fled together, they are bound by the archers: all that are found in thee are bound together, which have fled from far.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3540984a-72c7-4e3e-b2ce-1fcbada5f49e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: ISA 22:4
Text: Therefore said I, Look away from me; I will weep bitterly, labour not to comfort me, because of the spoiling of the daughter of my people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae5d6e1f-3625-4d6d-8f33-75c9d7a31ec7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: ISA 22:5
Text: For it is a day of trouble, and of treading down, and of perplexity by the Lord GOD of hosts in the valley of vision, breaking down the walls, and of crying to the mountains.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:322d5f7d-081e-4e28-b545-f88d3312134e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: ISA 22:6
Text: And Elam bare the quiver with chariots of men and horsemen, and Kir uncovered the shield.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7b6ed4b-fdc2-4388-ae38-b2a884782df0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: ISA 22:7
Text: And it shall come to pass, that thy choicest valleys shall be full of chariots, and the horsemen shall set themselves in array at the gate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bea53cb2-1a96-48b9-99e7-c2df82127032>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: ISA 22:8
Text: And he discovered the covering of Judah, and thou didst look in that day to the armour of the house of the forest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29c2a7f0-768b-4228-b63c-eb3d35c5b4c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: ISA 22:9
Text: Ye have seen also the breaches of the city of David, that they are many: and ye gathered together the waters of the lower pool.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a807c62e-1fef-4970-9fa7-9490dc87fe66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: ISA 22:10
Text: And ye have numbered the houses of Jerusalem, and the houses have ye broken down to fortify the wall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3fc3d61-e8cc-42fe-b8d7-085d902b537a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: ISA 22:11
Text: Ye made also a ditch between the two walls for the water of the old pool: but ye have not looked unto the maker thereof, neither had respect unto him that fashioned it long ago.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27e62a96-814a-449d-9239-77bdea2ca767>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: ISA 22:12
Text: And in that day did the Lord GOD of hosts call to weeping, and to mourning, and to baldness, and to girding with sackcloth:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2b20887-6e01-4ce0-b3af-fe5c447da7cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: ISA 22:13
Text: And behold joy and gladness, slaying oxen, and killing sheep, eating flesh, and drinking wine: let us eat and drink; for to morrow we shall die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b95e4b2-5091-4ad2-abf9-cebe2bb70750>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: ISA 22:14
Text: And it was revealed in mine ears by the LORD of hosts, Surely this iniquity shall not be purged from you till ye die, saith the Lord GOD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be8d375b-5f07-4dd8-acb4-2d4e6c6ace5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: ISA 22:15
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD of hosts, Go, get thee unto this treasurer, even unto Shebna, which is over the house, and say,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7654d0af-8a09-400a-bf3a-4b88b1921823>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: ISA 22:16
Text: What hast thou here? and whom hast thou here, that thou hast hewed thee out a sepulchre here, as he that heweth him out a sepulchre on high, and that graveth an habitation for himself in a rock?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90620a43-07be-4661-a8db-3a9e125916fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: ISA 22:17
Text: Behold, the LORD will carry thee away with a mighty captivity, and will surely cover thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78e24a3b-c631-49bf-b36e-125164b1edad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: ISA 22:18
Text: He will surely violently turn and toss thee like a ball into a large country: there shalt thou die, and there the chariots of thy glory shall be the shame of thy lord’s house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6781cdf-e326-4a86-9b8e-6963a4dc203d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: ISA 22:19
Text: And I will drive thee from thy station, and from thy state shall he pull thee down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b6f3725-6702-4b44-9f77-0a9ab481f23f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: ISA 22:20
Text: And it shall come to pass in that day, that I will call my servant Eliakim the son of Hilkiah:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4831db5e-59f2-4b82-b8a9-d88da1099d5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: ISA 22:21
Text: And I will clothe him with thy robe, and strengthen him with thy girdle, and I will commit thy government into his hand: and he shall be a father to the inhabitants of Jerusalem, and to the house of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8cda464a-394a-444f-a8fa-08c7ecb972c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: ISA 22:22
Text: And the key of the house of David will I lay upon his shoulder; so he shall open, and none shall shut; and he shall shut, and none shall open.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51a12257-dd26-4e38-836f-2088eb0bfe31>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: ISA 22:23
Text: And I will fasten him as a nail in a sure place; and he shall be for a glorious throne to his father’s house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f557409c-848c-4f4a-8668-e2a5b7033218>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: ISA 22:24
Text: And they shall hang upon him all the glory of his father’s house, the offspring and the issue, all vessels of small quantity, from the vessels of cups, even to all the vessels of flagons.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/22/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab44d12c-0622-4a8b-99d3-6655138d654a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: ISA 22:25
Text: In that day, saith the LORD of hosts, shall the nail that is fastened in the sure place be removed, and be cut down, and fall; and the burden that was upon it shall be cut off: for the LORD hath spoken it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/23/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c5cc89e-cc54-4ead-bee1-122cde8cb3c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: ISA 23:1
Text: The burden of Tyre. Howl, ye ships of Tarshish; for it is laid waste, so that there is no house, no entering in: from the land of Chittim it is revealed to them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/23/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d7fdabd-a299-4f34-b8fa-d07bf4733b1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: ISA 23:2
Text: Be still, ye inhabitants of the isle; thou whom the merchants of Zidon, that pass over the sea, have replenished.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/23/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f3f4c5f-f972-4414-bc62-ec5b19d6a458>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: ISA 23:3
Text: And by great waters the seed of Sihor, the harvest of the river, is her revenue; and she is a mart of nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/23/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:174b57e1-f41c-4f3f-a07a-dafd0ec0d372>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: ISA 23:4
Text: Be thou ashamed, O Zidon: for the sea hath spoken, even the strength of the sea, saying, I travail not, nor bring forth children, neither do I nourish up young men, nor bring up virgins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/23/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41116f2b-e00f-4076-9d23-3608720cbbca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: ISA 23:5
Text: As at the report concerning Egypt, so shall they be sorely pained at the report of Tyre.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/23/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c021efe8-f6b6-4933-8f24-8ad261b23a79>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: ISA 23:6
Text: Pass ye over to Tarshish; howl, ye inhabitants of the isle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/23/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82ace040-344d-478f-9424-206f4d68cd22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: ISA 23:7
Text: Is this your joyous city, whose antiquity is of ancient days? her own feet shall carry her afar off to sojourn.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/23/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65b8748d-b88b-4754-8836-78ee006da4ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: ISA 23:8
Text: Who hath taken this counsel against Tyre, the crowning city, whose merchants are princes, whose traffickers are the honourable of the earth?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/23/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71dfa718-a0bb-4379-8615-de8c70b525b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: ISA 23:9
Text: The LORD of hosts hath purposed it, to stain the pride of all glory, and to bring into contempt all the honourable of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/23/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e748e7d3-8fc4-4b30-a67b-22c22e4ee745>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: ISA 23:10
Text: Pass through thy land as a river, O daughter of Tarshish: there is no more strength.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/23/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7d00a88-c5c6-4da7-a6c4-13d5a8a6a954>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: ISA 23:11
Text: He stretched out his hand over the sea, he shook the kingdoms: the LORD hath given a commandment against the merchant city, to destroy the strong holds thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/23/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30149120-2d62-480c-b546-d25aa8435520>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: ISA 23:12
Text: And he said, Thou shalt no more rejoice, O thou oppressed virgin, daughter of Zidon: arise, pass over to Chittim; there also shalt thou have no rest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/23/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a191129-a01f-443e-b633-d9ca24fb7dcb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: ISA 23:13
Text: Behold the land of the Chaldeans; this people was not, till the Assyrian founded it for them that dwell in the wilderness: they set up the towers thereof, they raised up the palaces thereof; and he brought it to ruin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/23/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb042bf5-e772-442b-bb5d-644c80b4ace3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: ISA 23:14
Text: Howl, ye ships of Tarshish: for your strength is laid waste.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/23/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63051581-f7e6-44b5-bf09-c1791968a8ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: ISA 23:15
Text: And it shall come to pass in that day, that Tyre shall be forgotten seventy years, according to the days of one king: after the end of seventy years shall Tyre sing as an harlot.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/23/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d24978b-4548-4b42-a181-1f36212b86e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: ISA 23:16
Text: Take an harp, go about the city, thou harlot that hast been forgotten; make sweet melody, sing many songs, that thou mayest be remembered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/23/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1ebaefe-cef3-4fcb-a3dd-a2363e1b3daf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: ISA 23:17
Text: And it shall come to pass after the end of seventy years, that the LORD will visit Tyre, and she shall turn to her hire, and shall commit fornication with all the kingdoms of the world upon the face of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/23/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63590c57-7025-4e54-9dce-28b5998beb38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: ISA 23:18
Text: And her merchandise and her hire shall be holiness to the LORD: it shall not be treasured nor laid up; for her merchandise shall be for them that dwell before the LORD, to eat sufficiently, and for durable clothing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/24/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04e0c599-32c8-4360-81c2-3d13206be53b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: ISA 24:1
Text: Behold, the LORD maketh the earth empty, and maketh it waste, and turneth it upside down, and scattereth abroad the inhabitants thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/24/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7133ef67-708b-4a22-aeb3-e75f2f552d68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 308

Reference: ISA 24:2
Text: And it shall be, as with the people, so with the priest; as with the servant, so with his master; as with the maid, so with her mistress; as with the buyer, so with the seller; as with the lender, so with the borrower; as with the taker of usury, so with the giver of usury to him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/24/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3c85496-9e58-4ace-8269-3beac03c7a80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: ISA 24:3
Text: The land shall be utterly emptied, and utterly spoiled: for the LORD hath spoken this word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/24/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4f4fb72-3cdb-45e1-9385-a01a15162c00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: ISA 24:4
Text: The earth mourneth and fadeth away, the world languisheth and fadeth away, the haughty people of the earth do languish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/24/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8876e043-b73d-4958-957a-7b5538e85810>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: ISA 24:5
Text: The earth also is defiled under the inhabitants thereof; because they have transgressed the laws, changed the ordinance, broken the everlasting covenant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/24/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7779df5a-b24f-46cd-9180-c06c5107059b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: ISA 24:6
Text: Therefore hath the curse devoured the earth, and they that dwell therein are desolate: therefore the inhabitants of the earth are burned, and few men left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/24/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbf1d101-a5ee-45e3-9e8b-a7f1f9e409a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: ISA 24:7
Text: The new wine mourneth, the vine languisheth, all the merryhearted do sigh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/24/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43501836-bcc5-4fe3-a62e-57a32e6353ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: ISA 24:8
Text: The mirth of tabrets ceaseth, the noise of them that rejoice endeth, the joy of the harp ceaseth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/24/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b0117ca-c97e-4ad8-b775-c1e506cb06b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: ISA 24:9
Text: They shall not drink wine with a song; strong drink shall be bitter to them that drink it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/24/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06c8bd5c-0316-4499-84b6-dc7df56afdaf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: ISA 24:10
Text: The city of confusion is broken down: every house is shut up, that no man may come in.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/24/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa403857-67d7-4d4c-bdce-e71ee8c92a96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: ISA 24:11
Text: There is a crying for wine in the streets; all joy is darkened, the mirth of the land is gone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/24/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc4fd85d-b312-4708-9b57-e5e971530583>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: ISA 24:12
Text: In the city is left desolation, and the gate is smitten with destruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/24/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f07a511f-08be-4524-89c5-1da21315fa51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: ISA 24:13
Text: When thus it shall be in the midst of the land among the people, there shall be as the shaking of an olive tree, and as the gleaning grapes when the vintage is done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/24/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c2524a0-0358-4fec-8fc8-fa93c67f2daa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: ISA 24:14
Text: They shall lift up their voice, they shall sing for the majesty of the LORD, they shall cry aloud from the sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/24/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da76229d-a7da-4889-960e-73cd611096ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: ISA 24:15
Text: Wherefore glorify ye the LORD in the fires, even the name of the LORD God of Israel in the isles of the sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/24/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78598168-3f4b-45a3-97c5-d365a39fe76c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: ISA 24:16
Text: From the uttermost part of the earth have we heard songs, even glory to the righteous. But I said, My leanness, my leanness, woe unto me! the treacherous dealers have dealt treacherously; yea, the treacherous dealers have dealt very treacherously.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/24/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d73a4ff-b9ca-436c-9bb6-4f5118bc7a92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: ISA 24:17
Text: Fear, and the pit, and the snare, are upon thee, O inhabitant of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/24/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50165951-6b51-4347-be6c-e3a0eca4bf37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 286

Reference: ISA 24:18
Text: And it shall come to pass, that he who fleeth from the noise of the fear shall fall into the pit; and he that cometh up out of the midst of the pit shall be taken in the snare: for the windows from on high are open, and the foundations of the earth do shake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/24/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c3170f4-8294-441d-b0c3-68e8ed30816f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: ISA 24:19
Text: The earth is utterly broken down, the earth is clean dissolved, the earth is moved exceedingly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/24/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bb6b466-0602-4003-b085-9965c9b06949>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: ISA 24:20
Text: The earth shall reel to and fro like a drunkard, and shall be removed like a cottage; and the transgression thereof shall be heavy upon it; and it shall fall, and not rise again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/24/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1862bda9-a153-4fc2-9347-96eb60f24cc2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: ISA 24:21
Text: And it shall come to pass in that day, that the LORD shall punish the host of the high ones that are on high, and the kings of the earth upon the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/24/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:246790f6-f4e0-487a-b304-05553a958367>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: ISA 24:22
Text: And they shall be gathered together, as prisoners are gathered in the pit, and shall be shut up in the prison, and after many days shall they be visited.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/24/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd6ea2b6-2503-450f-b4c5-27fcb9c897e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: ISA 24:23
Text: Then the moon shall be confounded, and the sun ashamed, when the LORD of hosts shall reign in mount Zion, and in Jerusalem, and before his ancients gloriously.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/25/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:102b5a26-4bd4-4a69-a8c7-2b9744b45026>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: ISA 25:1
Text: O Lord, thou art my God; I will exalt thee, I will praise thy name; for thou hast done wonderful things; thy counsels of old are faithfulness and truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/25/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8104b29e-b0ae-40aa-8f3f-2befdc0d2584>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: ISA 25:2
Text: For thou hast made of a city an heap; of a defenced city a ruin: a palace of strangers to be no city; it shall never be built.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/25/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa8392f1-b9d2-4eb7-8920-77addfbd2c80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: ISA 25:3
Text: Therefore shall the strong people glorify thee, the city of the terrible nations shall fear thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/25/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c1aabb3-a9fa-44bc-a977-d1fc0d557c06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: ISA 25:4
Text: For thou hast been a strength to the poor, a strength to the needy in his distress, a refuge from the storm, a shadow from the heat, when the blast of the terrible ones is as a storm against the wall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/25/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf510f95-ff7b-4299-888e-4d468847f0be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: ISA 25:5
Text: Thou shalt bring down the noise of strangers, as the heat in a dry place; even the heat with the shadow of a cloud: the branch of the terrible ones shall be brought low.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/25/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91004dfd-b123-40b7-bef0-fd7b371984a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: ISA 25:6
Text: And in this mountain shall the LORD of hosts make unto all people a feast of fat things, a feast of wines on the lees, of fat things full of marrow, of wines on the lees well refined.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/25/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3a70311-2ce8-483e-94fa-7ccdf8f00902>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: ISA 25:7
Text: And he will destroy in this mountain the face of the covering cast over all people, and the vail that is spread over all nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/25/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a78ffb5-3178-4f1b-8d7f-9c6069734c77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: ISA 25:8
Text: He will swallow up death in victory; and the Lord GOD will wipe away tears from off all faces; and the rebuke of his people shall he take away from off all the earth: for the LORD hath spoken it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/25/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fdc0e70-3605-4c99-b4c7-f429b38fd337>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: ISA 25:9
Text: And it shall be said in that day, Lo, this is our God; we have waited for him, and he will save us: this is the LORD; we have waited for him, we will be glad and rejoice in his salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/25/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e39858b3-a923-4c0a-a653-770d7eeb3c8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: ISA 25:10
Text: For in this mountain shall the hand of the LORD rest, and Moab shall be trodden down under him, even as straw is trodden down for the dunghill.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/25/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75a009e9-49c3-4688-bff5-7defca3b63b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: ISA 25:11
Text: And he shall spread forth his hands in the midst of them, as he that swimmeth spreadeth forth his hands to swim: and he shall bring down their pride together with the spoils of their hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/25/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:376fdeb6-acd7-4256-85b7-26a8942d2580>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: ISA 25:12
Text: And the fortress of the high fort of thy walls shall he bring down, lay low, and bring to the ground, even to the dust.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/26/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a9c96ba-e634-4e78-ad79-68ab8eda38b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: ISA 26:1
Text: In that day shall this song be sung in the land of Judah; We have a strong city; salvation will God appoint for walls and bulwarks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/26/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d339da3-cd34-4a64-b26e-c6401f939927>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: ISA 26:2
Text: Open ye the gates, that the righteous nation which keepeth the truth may enter in.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/26/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b12243e-c1e5-428a-b8c2-308155372645>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: ISA 26:3
Text: Thou wilt keep him in perfect peace, whose mind is stayed on thee: because he trusteth in thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/26/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:435435bb-3c12-471a-81bd-baa3c44cfd31>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: ISA 26:4
Text: Trust ye in the LORD for ever: for in the LORD JEHOVAH is everlasting strength:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/26/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2024f83-fb13-4fbd-a6db-05649204fa54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: ISA 26:5
Text: For he bringeth down them that dwell on high; the lofty city, he layeth it low; he layeth it low, even to the ground; he bringeth it even to the dust.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/26/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e03e85d1-42e3-44df-b9ed-060973479a2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: ISA 26:6
Text: The foot shall tread it down, even the feet of the poor, and the steps of the needy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/26/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08a9762d-8da3-40c6-9c37-a1460ba6b638>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: ISA 26:7
Text: The way of the just is uprightness: thou, most upright, dost weigh the path of the just.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/26/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:211fb4f3-c4e8-4221-a399-49dd38092da4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: ISA 26:8
Text: Yea, in the way of thy judgments, O LORD, have we waited for thee; the desire of our soul is to thy name, and to the remembrance of thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/26/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ccd3d11-ae46-45b6-8989-1166426a0102>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: ISA 26:9
Text: With my soul have I desired thee in the night; yea, with my spirit within me will I seek thee early: for when thy judgments are in the earth, the inhabitants of the world will learn righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/26/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9df8b204-9cce-4965-97d2-cd709c4980cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: ISA 26:10
Text: Let favour be shewed to the wicked, yet will he not learn righteousness: in the land of uprightness will he deal unjustly, and will not behold the majesty of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/26/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e501b935-fb30-4037-8af7-57f6f7a44229>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: ISA 26:11
Text: LORD, when thy hand is lifted up, they will not see: but they shall see, and be ashamed for their envy at the people; yea, the fire of thine enemies shall devour them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/26/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:389889cb-b5dd-491f-adfc-eca6488bdbd8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: ISA 26:12
Text: LORD, thou wilt ordain peace for us: for thou also hast wrought all our works in us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/26/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77b731eb-0c16-4811-9b71-aa58b824b173>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: ISA 26:13
Text: O LORD our God, other lords beside thee have had dominion over us: but by thee only will we make mention of thy name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/26/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85bf2a3d-52c6-478d-b93f-d062574cb15c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: ISA 26:14
Text: They are dead, they shall not live; they are deceased, they shall not rise: therefore hast thou visited and destroyed them, and made all their memory to perish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/26/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0161e0a8-e84a-4fb9-9de9-c5a706fe5592>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: ISA 26:15
Text: Thou hast increased the nation, O LORD, thou hast increased the nation: thou art glorified: thou hadst removed it far unto all the ends of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/26/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ade6f901-393b-456c-82ba-99693fdf7164>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: ISA 26:16
Text: LORD, in trouble have they visited thee, they poured out a prayer when thy chastening was upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/26/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e5330ba-4862-4ee3-914e-84fe14be13fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: ISA 26:17
Text: Like as a woman with child, that draweth near the time of her delivery, is in pain, and crieth out in her pangs; so have we been in thy sight, O LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/26/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f44ffdb-150f-4cb6-a049-9ed64346e5f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: ISA 26:18
Text: We have been with child, we have been in pain, we have as it were brought forth wind; we have not wrought any deliverance in the earth; neither have the inhabitants of the world fallen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/26/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c0a49a1-d4a1-4091-8da7-a8f6d2a3eec9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: ISA 26:19
Text: Thy dead men shall live, together with my dead body shall they arise. Awake and sing, ye that dwell in dust: for thy dew is as the dew of herbs, and the earth shall cast out the dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/26/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c698d2a2-1337-4eb6-9616-836e714f8bfd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: ISA 26:20
Text: Come, my people, enter thou into thy chambers, and shut thy doors about thee: hide thyself as it were for a little moment, until the indignation be overpast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/26/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4078544-b03c-4050-98b5-42a4aa21781f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: ISA 26:21
Text: For, behold, the LORD cometh out of his place to punish the inhabitants of the earth for their iniquity: the earth also shall disclose her blood, and shall no more cover her slain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/27/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88d99b46-e99b-4669-90b3-0aa6afb4956a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: ISA 27:1
Text: In that day the LORD with his sore and great and strong sword shall punish leviathan the piercing serpent, even leviathan that crooked serpent; and he shall slay the dragon that is in the sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/27/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e788f46e-4d9e-4895-88eb-020bf3976c77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: ISA 27:2
Text: In that day sing ye unto her, A vineyard of red wine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/27/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c909291-755e-4436-b1e5-6e2abe58f884>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: ISA 27:3
Text: I the LORD do keep it; I will water it every moment: lest any hurt it, I will keep it night and day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/27/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b2146c8-561f-48a6-a6d3-75ac8f8610ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: ISA 27:4
Text: Fury is not in me: who would set the briers and thorns against me in battle? I would go through them, I would burn them together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/27/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4a6ddfa-54c1-44cb-8db2-3a7ec0dc3f1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: ISA 27:5
Text: Or let him take hold of my strength, that he may make peace with me; and he shall make peace with me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/27/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30baa9b6-f3c1-416d-9563-3f79906bf6e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: ISA 27:6
Text: He shall cause them that come of Jacob to take root: Israel shall blossom and bud, and fill the face of the world with fruit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/27/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf0178ed-ba9c-4459-8141-ef335de02256>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: ISA 27:7
Text: Hath he smitten him, as he smote those that smote him? or is he slain according to the slaughter of them that are slain by him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/27/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c76b017-05a6-49c2-b156-7d8b562fb70b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: ISA 27:8
Text: In measure, when it shooteth forth, thou wilt debate with it: he stayeth his rough wind in the day of the east wind.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/27/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0029c720-07d1-4993-9c32-953f83c54865>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: ISA 27:9
Text: By this therefore shall the iniquity of Jacob be purged; and this is all the fruit to take away his sin; when he maketh all the stones of the altar as chalkstones that are beaten in sunder, the groves and images shall not stand up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/27/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e54cdeb1-fce0-475e-80b5-6c1d1677cd92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: ISA 27:10
Text: Yet the defenced city shall be desolate, and the habitation forsaken, and left like a wilderness: there shall the calf feed, and there shall he lie down, and consume the branches thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/27/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d175c91b-2920-4750-b7c8-d69f41e0a8f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: ISA 27:11
Text: When the boughs thereof are withered, they shall be broken off: the women come, and set them on fire: for it is a people of no understanding: therefore he that made them will not have mercy on them, and he that formed them will shew them no favour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/27/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b189f858-a9d9-4314-881f-ab0610507919>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: ISA 27:12
Text: And it shall come to pass in that day, that the LORD shall beat off from the channel of the river unto the stream of Egypt, and ye shall be gathered one by one, O ye children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/27/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a81a3ee8-2f7a-4d1f-a75c-b1903b3902c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 274

Reference: ISA 27:13
Text: And it shall come to pass in that day, that the great trumpet shall be blown, and they shall come which were ready to perish in the land of Assyria, and the outcasts in the land of Egypt, and shall worship the LORD in the holy mount at Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18f8e73c-169e-4889-972f-df3947157d7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: ISA 28:1
Text: Woe to the crown of pride, to the drunkards of Ephraim, whose glorious beauty is a fading flower, which are on the head of the fat valleys of them that are overcome with wine!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c72ac658-dc1e-40b7-93e2-261e8c6999d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: ISA 28:2
Text: Behold, the Lord hath a mighty and strong one, which as a tempest of hail and a destroying storm, as a flood of mighty waters overflowing, shall cast down to the earth with the hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30f96d46-2c85-452d-92d5-2789b94b7607>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: ISA 28:3
Text: The crown of pride, the drunkards of Ephraim, shall be trodden under feet:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f16a7e8-3c6e-4133-a4a2-be27b1eba1db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: ISA 28:4
Text: And the glorious beauty, which is on the head of the fat valley, shall be a fading flower, and as the hasty fruit before the summer; which when he that looketh upon it seeth, while it is yet in his hand he eateth it up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c94f3f8-e534-47bd-9f67-8f5a012e0f4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: ISA 28:5
Text: In that day shall the LORD of hosts be for a crown of glory, and for a diadem of beauty, unto the residue of his people,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67aacf38-8987-44ca-aca5-a2e96b4b5487>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: ISA 28:6
Text: And for a spirit of judgment to him that sitteth in judgment, and for strength to them that turn the battle to the gate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96ec22eb-2e3e-41d2-85e8-2268188541d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 293

Reference: ISA 28:7
Text: But they also have erred through wine, and through strong drink are out of the way; the priest and the prophet have erred through strong drink, they are swallowed up of wine, they are out of the way through strong drink; they err in vision, they stumble in judgment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1426bf55-d5f2-45d6-b136-f13a574e3daa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: ISA 28:8
Text: For all tables are full of vomit and filthiness, so that there is no place clean.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea4a8d32-7736-4d3d-a687-8c2a4e6beabf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: ISA 28:9
Text: Whom shall he teach knowledge? and whom shall he make to understand doctrine? them that are weaned from the milk, and drawn from the breasts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bde3f3c4-32e9-4b56-97a0-b0eb8ee3c23c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: ISA 28:10
Text: For precept must be upon precept, precept upon precept; line upon line, line upon line; here a little, and there a little:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f447444-ebbb-46ab-9219-3d8deedb2d82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: ISA 28:11
Text: For with stammering lips and another tongue will he speak to this people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2996cf54-7db1-4c4f-9e27-68546070bd33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: ISA 28:12
Text: To whom he said, This is the rest wherewith ye may cause the weary to rest; and this is the refreshing: yet they would not hear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7ab3c8e-67ac-46d0-9518-65064610e262>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: ISA 28:13
Text: But the word of the LORD was unto them precept upon precept, precept upon precept; line upon line, line upon line; here a little, and there a little; that they might go, and fall backward, and be broken, and snared, and taken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5409a6e-7f0a-435c-884b-fa0b663ea75e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: ISA 28:14
Text: Wherefore hear the word of the LORD, ye scornful men, that rule this people which is in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3674dda-1321-4844-baa8-7bb0cc8eca32>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 273

Reference: ISA 28:15
Text: Because ye have said, We have made a covenant with death, and with hell are we at agreement; when the overflowing scourge shall pass through, it shall not come unto us: for we have made lies our refuge, and under falsehood have we hid ourselves:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb247549-8d30-473d-a2dd-f7817b823c03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: ISA 28:16
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD, Behold, I lay in Zion for a foundation a stone, a tried stone, a precious corner stone, a sure foundation: he that believeth shall not make haste.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:639ddc7c-f103-4dd0-a373-4d85ac9f2acd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: ISA 28:17
Text: Judgment also will I lay to the line, and righteousness to the plummet: and the hail shall sweep away the refuge of lies, and the waters shall overflow the hiding place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18ceccb5-7665-40c7-917c-5898c495733e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: ISA 28:18
Text: And your covenant with death shall be disannulled, and your agreement with hell shall not stand; when the overflowing scourge shall pass through, then ye shall be trodden down by it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8f6a262-c7fc-4b2d-889e-15be924403a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: ISA 28:19
Text: From the time that it goeth forth it shall take you: for morning by morning shall it pass over, by day and by night: and it shall be a vexation only to understand the report.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad8a1d6f-7122-4ba7-8ff7-d7b575798a9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: ISA 28:20
Text: For the bed is shorter than that a man can stretch himself on it: and the covering narrower than that he can wrap himself in it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebcc7a79-5b19-4ab8-80ee-c005202d1966>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: ISA 28:21
Text: For the LORD shall rise up as in mount Perazim, he shall be wroth as in the valley of Gibeon, that he may do his work, his strange work; and bring to pass his act, his strange act.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e57412b7-55ba-4251-bc54-9b6ecdf65066>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: ISA 28:22
Text: Now therefore be ye not mockers, lest your bands be made strong: for I have heard from the Lord GOD of hosts a consumption, even determined upon the whole earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ff8e857-4f22-4a90-8f65-be7c3fbfa0b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: ISA 28:23
Text: Give ye ear, and hear my voice; hearken, and hear my speech.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:826723af-daa3-43fe-b136-3122800596d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: ISA 28:24
Text: Doth the plowman plow all day to sow? doth he open and break the clods of his ground?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41597486-9716-4ae3-9084-dddbec9c4295>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: ISA 28:25
Text: When he hath made plain the face thereof, doth he not cast abroad the fitches, and scatter the cummin, and cast in the principal wheat and the appointed barley and the rie in their place?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42ff229d-49e0-4b15-8241-055210758f41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: ISA 28:26
Text: For his God doth instruct him to discretion, and doth teach him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16653c97-6939-43ef-aa15-02c9add9c128>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: ISA 28:27
Text: For the fitches are not threshed with a threshing instrument, neither is a cart wheel turned about upon the cummin; but the fitches are beaten out with a staff, and the cummin with a rod.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77bb6970-e65d-46df-bc4f-ea725a5474df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: ISA 28:28
Text: Bread corn is bruised; because he will not ever be threshing it, nor break it with the wheel of his cart, nor bruise it with his horsemen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/28/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:adc71ec5-61ca-4538-b797-b45e052c7e7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: ISA 28:29
Text: This also cometh forth from the LORD of hosts, which is wonderful in counsel, and excellent in working.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d750f087-6f5a-44b6-9e5c-1ee5c16fbcfe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: ISA 29:1
Text: Woe to Ariel, to Ariel, the city where David dwelt! add ye year to year; let them kill sacrifices.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3ff9c4f-ed3d-49a0-a7a3-30c8e122b815>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: ISA 29:2
Text: Yet I will distress Ariel, and there shall be heaviness and sorrow: and it shall be unto me as Ariel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:903eca8f-f28f-495d-9470-8f9c9329dae9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: ISA 29:3
Text: And I will camp against thee round about, and will lay siege against thee with a mount, and I will raise forts against thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bb12257-8509-405c-8581-223b1c85e9a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 266

Reference: ISA 29:4
Text: And thou shalt be brought down, and shalt speak out of the ground, and thy speech shall be low out of the dust, and thy voice shall be, as of one that hath a familiar spirit, out of the ground, and thy speech shall whisper out of the dust.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d450e51-f40c-4e68-a451-f3e2f9a9a858>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: ISA 29:5
Text: Moreover the multitude of thy strangers shall be like small dust, and the multitude of the terrible ones shall be as chaff that passeth away: yea, it shall be at an instant suddenly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a65db46-b896-4fb8-b932-e3299227b065>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: ISA 29:6
Text: Thou shalt be visited of the LORD of hosts with thunder, and with earthquake, and great noise, with storm and tempest, and the flame of devouring fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32b3a477-00e8-4b94-91f1-e2a01a701ca8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: ISA 29:7
Text: And the multitude of all the nations that fight against Ariel, even all that fight against her and her munition, and that distress her, shall be as a dream of a night vision.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b319e94-d603-48e3-a473-6ec0322508b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 346

Reference: ISA 29:8
Text: It shall even be as when an hungry man dreameth, and, behold, he eateth; but he awaketh, and his soul is empty: or as when a thirsty man dreameth, and, behold, he drinketh; but he awaketh, and, behold, he is faint, and his soul hath appetite: so shall the multitude of all the nations be, that fight against mount Zion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5517932-9bd6-4a50-a6ea-f4d5efd92b15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: ISA 29:9
Text: Stay yourselves, and wonder; cry ye out, and cry: they are drunken, but not with wine; they stagger, but not with strong drink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6da69575-6ba3-47aa-ad33-2514e6060dc8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: ISA 29:10
Text: For the LORD hath poured out upon you the spirit of deep sleep, and hath closed your eyes: the prophets and your rulers, the seers hath he covered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:763fa8d2-69d6-4fb1-a998-15be83eda16c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: ISA 29:11
Text: And the vision of all is become unto you as the words of a book that is sealed, which men deliver to one that is learned, saying, Read this, I pray thee: and he saith, I cannot; for it is sealed:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1e1bc9d-83ce-493f-b969-818f63823af9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: ISA 29:12
Text: And the book is delivered to him that is not learned, saying, Read this, I pray thee: and he saith, I am not learned.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3902cab1-d2dd-4912-93e1-2dd355585532>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: ISA 29:13
Text: Wherefore the Lord said, Forasmuch as this people draw near me with their mouth, and with their lips do honour me, but have removed their heart far from me, and their fear toward me is taught by the precept of men:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc04fd35-d73e-4f06-8d73-fb2d60ca86a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: ISA 29:14
Text: Therefore, behold, I will proceed to do a marvellous work among this people, even a marvellous work and a wonder: for the wisdom of their wise men shall perish, and the understanding of their prudent men shall be hid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e61d0c52-356f-46bb-a7db-cdd70c4b133c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: ISA 29:15
Text: Woe unto them that seek deep to hide their counsel from the LORD, and their works are in the dark, and they say, Who seeth us? and who knoweth us?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b29ddf16-e620-4f44-ab03-b0bdcd7fce34>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: ISA 29:16
Text: Surely your turning of things upside down shall be esteemed as the potter’s clay: for shall the work say of him that made it, He made me not? or shall the thing framed say of him that framed it, He had no understanding?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4654caa-d352-4f4f-a956-8822fb335854>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: ISA 29:17
Text: Is it not yet a very little while, and Lebanon shall be turned into a fruitful field, and the fruitful field shall be esteemed as a forest?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9f4175f-4ea2-49af-9a1a-640b87ac301e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: ISA 29:18
Text: And in that day shall the deaf hear the words of the book, and the eyes of the blind shall see out of obscurity, and out of darkness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a61c6bed-41e0-49b5-8b7a-d2e42a332a6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: ISA 29:19
Text: The meek also shall increase their joy in the LORD, and the poor among men shall rejoice in the Holy One of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a287ced9-97a5-4da9-b1a6-658d8924eac6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: ISA 29:20
Text: For the terrible one is brought to nought, and the scorner is consumed, and all that watch for iniquity are cut off:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d2a3a25-7511-40bf-bdea-ad178c332cf0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: ISA 29:21
Text: That make a man an offender for a word, and lay a snare for him that reproveth in the gate, and turn aside the just for a thing of nought.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3201b5da-4138-4c2a-a296-931e232bd45f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: ISA 29:22
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD, who redeemed Abraham, concerning the house of Jacob, Jacob shall not now be ashamed, neither shall his face now wax pale.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ab99221-2db9-4728-b2a6-3313d955d609>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: ISA 29:23
Text: But when he seeth his children, the work of mine hands, in the midst of him, they shall sanctify my name, and sanctify the Holy One of Jacob, and shall fear the God of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/29/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6af53447-9f3f-4ea6-8d62-50cb05711ba9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: ISA 29:24
Text: They also that erred in spirit shall come to understanding, and they that murmured shall learn doctrine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:970d3515-5aba-4f6c-84c2-53b8e309fd33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: ISA 30:1
Text: Woe to the rebellious children, saith the LORD, that take counsel, but not of me; and that cover with a covering, but not of my spirit, that they may add sin to sin:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d5558d1-9405-4e34-a5cb-1f1449e738fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: ISA 30:2
Text: That walk to go down into Egypt, and have not asked at my mouth; to strengthen themselves in the strength of Pharaoh, and to trust in the shadow of Egypt!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9db7195-c895-426a-a9cb-58037060ab18>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: ISA 30:3
Text: Therefore shall the strength of Pharaoh be your shame, and the trust in the shadow of Egypt your confusion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f432600f-564f-422d-8bf2-9d0d2ae5b385>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: ISA 30:4
Text: For his princes were at Zoan, and his ambassadors came to Hanes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:472ad77b-26f2-4995-aae2-fa5ace0d3771>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: ISA 30:5
Text: They were all ashamed of a people that could not profit them, nor be an help nor profit, but a shame, and also a reproach.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:059e335f-c78d-4f1a-8cba-79a95f5b8317>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 332

Reference: ISA 30:6
Text: The burden of the beasts of the south: into the land of trouble and anguish, from whence come the young and old lion, the viper and fiery flying serpent, they will carry their riches upon the shoulders of young asses, and their treasures upon the bunches of camels, to a people that shall not profit them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffb502f6-8f93-4e57-9b81-cf0fa21263f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: ISA 30:7
Text: For the Egyptians shall help in vain, and to no purpose: therefore have I cried concerning this, Their strength is to sit still.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7fb01dd-5231-4425-8dd8-ba45fc7381ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: ISA 30:8
Text: Now go, write it before them in a table, and note it in a book, that it may be for the time to come for ever and ever:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:095d45db-4f4b-4bd6-9cdb-9b0ce4e2aa0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: ISA 30:9
Text: That this is a rebellious people, lying children, children that will not hear the law of the LORD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a9b777f-587d-47c1-8636-7b05b9e45168>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: ISA 30:10
Text: Which say to the seers, See not; and to the prophets, Prophesy not unto us right things, speak unto us smooth things, prophesy deceits:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5250c207-e6bf-4976-be0e-2878ca96718c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: ISA 30:11
Text: Get you out of the way, turn aside out of the path, cause the Holy One of Israel to cease from before us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec406af3-63b6-46be-966f-ed6c7f190c8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: ISA 30:12
Text: Wherefore thus saith the Holy One of Israel, Because ye despise this word, and trust in oppression and perverseness, and stay thereon:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a42152c8-0ad0-4ae3-bf02-a7c744655a12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: ISA 30:13
Text: Therefore this iniquity shall be to you as a breach ready to fall, swelling out in a high wall, whose breaking cometh suddenly at an instant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fd38fa7-a61f-4098-ac4e-c019839aa527>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: ISA 30:14
Text: And he shall break it as the breaking of the potters’ vessel that is broken in pieces; he shall not spare: so that there shall not be found in the bursting of it a sherd to take fire from the hearth, or to take water withal out of the pit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:900338e5-ca8b-48a3-be50-91807c4ea636>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: ISA 30:15
Text: For thus saith the Lord GOD, the Holy One of Israel; In returning and rest shall ye be saved; in quietness and in confidence shall be your strength: and ye would not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0938dacc-ac77-40bc-8c37-58b99ce3e859>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: ISA 30:16
Text: But ye said, No; for we will flee upon horses; therefore shall ye flee: and, We will ride upon the swift; therefore shall they that pursue you be swift.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43c51ad3-8690-471f-8169-df41c1371a12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: ISA 30:17
Text: One thousand shall flee at the rebuke of one; at the rebuke of five shall ye flee: till ye be left as a beacon upon the top of a mountain, and as an ensign on an hill.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee9ecc53-9fab-48bf-b211-8db0e32f781c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: ISA 30:18
Text: And therefore will the LORD wait, that he may be gracious unto you, and therefore will he be exalted, that he may have mercy upon you: for the LORD is a God of judgment: blessed are all they that wait for him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56f0ba34-1f58-45a7-9f0a-4a1bc7ab6255>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: ISA 30:19
Text: For the people shall dwell in Zion at Jerusalem: thou shalt weep no more: he will be very gracious unto thee at the voice of thy cry; when he shall hear it, he will answer thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2961fcfd-17a0-4962-a1c0-6d879629dfd9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: ISA 30:20
Text: And though the Lord give you the bread of adversity, and the water of affliction, yet shall not thy teachers be removed into a corner any more, but thine eyes shall see thy teachers:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fc4830d-3886-4dbd-8c5e-a6be2f812c82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: ISA 30:21
Text: And thine ears shall hear a word behind thee, saying, This is the way, walk ye in it, when ye turn to the right hand, and when ye turn to the left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7014eb6d-e425-49a8-9ede-c1407379acf7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: ISA 30:22
Text: Ye shall defile also the covering of thy graven images of silver, and the ornament of thy molten images of gold: thou shalt cast them away as a menstruous cloth; thou shalt say unto it, Get thee hence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ceaceee-7d49-48cf-acb1-2996ba73a57f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: ISA 30:23
Text: Then shall he give the rain of thy seed, that thou shalt sow the ground withal; and bread of the increase of the earth, and it shall be fat and plenteous: in that day shall thy cattle feed in large pastures.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dcd5fbf3-468f-4627-9543-d3a81176d219>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: ISA 30:24
Text: The oxen likewise and the young asses that ear the ground shall eat clean provender, which hath been winnowed with the shovel and with the fan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5d9d813-4fc6-4d9a-8aad-bf3f55189553>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: ISA 30:25
Text: And there shall be upon every high mountain, and upon every high hill, rivers and streams of waters in the day of the great slaughter, when the towers fall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5666d51-d54f-439a-9f55-7deca38c87eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 266

Reference: ISA 30:26
Text: Moreover the light of the moon shall be as the light of the sun, and the light of the sun shall be sevenfold, as the light of seven days, in the day that the LORD bindeth up the breach of his people, and healeth the stroke of their wound.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9c784f3-61e1-4762-9ae9-b7106bce7eee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: ISA 30:27
Text: Behold, the name of the LORD cometh from far, burning with his anger, and the burden thereof is heavy: his lips are full of indignation, and his tongue as a devouring fire:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cff9d13f-a316-4cf3-9739-435d8dddbddd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: ISA 30:28
Text: And his breath, as an overflowing stream, shall reach to the midst of the neck, to sift the nations with the sieve of vanity: and there shall be a bridle in the jaws of the people, causing them to err.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37cb3d48-5874-4eac-8e51-9fe7028decd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: ISA 30:29
Text: Ye shall have a song, as in the night when a holy solemnity is kept; and gladness of heart, as when one goeth with a pipe to come into the mountain of the LORD, to the mighty One of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90c6025c-d277-46e7-a914-a81b94922fc2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: ISA 30:30
Text: And the LORD shall cause his glorious voice to be heard, and shall shew the lighting down of his arm, with the indignation of his anger, and with the flame of a devouring fire, with scattering, and tempest, and hailstones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69afe139-30b8-4ca1-ab71-2046178e6d41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: ISA 30:31
Text: For through the voice of the LORD shall the Assyrian be beaten down, which smote with a rod.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9271653-0906-41cd-97e8-467daab0ab1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: ISA 30:32
Text: And in every place where the grounded staff shall pass, which the LORD shall lay upon him, it shall be with tabrets and harps: and in battles of shaking will he fight with it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/30/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d14616cb-7900-411f-be59-99d9a25c101f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: ISA 30:33
Text: For Tophet is ordained of old; yea, for the king it is prepared; he hath made it deep and large: the pile thereof is fire and much wood; the breath of the LORD, like a stream of brimstone, doth kindle it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/31/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f21f477-12f3-4fb6-8d99-27fb5018c6dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: ISA 31:1
Text: Woe to them that go down to Egypt for help; and stay on horses, and trust in chariots, because they are many; and in horsemen, because they are very strong; but they look not unto the Holy One of Israel, neither seek the LORD!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/31/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7bc85e50-cf46-4052-8e73-458793f0af84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: ISA 31:2
Text: Yet he also is wise, and will bring evil, and will not call back his words: but will arise against the house of the evildoers, and against the help of them that work iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/31/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f644339d-7a89-4974-8d76-d46ff1a82653>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: ISA 31:3
Text: Now the Egyptians are men, and not God; and their horses flesh, and not spirit. When the LORD shall stretch out his hand, both he that helpeth shall fall, and he that is holpen shall fall down, and they all shall fail together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/31/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b69c92d3-d138-4720-b633-363b55ef91ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 348

Reference: ISA 31:4
Text: For thus hath the LORD spoken unto me, Like as the lion and the young lion roaring on his prey, when a multitude of shepherds is called forth against him, he will not be afraid of their voice, nor abase himself for the noise of them: so shall the LORD of hosts come down to fight for mount Zion, and for the hill thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/31/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d6c7848-c4fb-4438-bc58-6dd020bd64fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: ISA 31:5
Text: As birds flying, so will the LORD of hosts defend Jerusalem; defending also he will deliver it; and passing over he will preserve it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/31/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8bc6dce5-66b7-4dbb-b6fc-b9eb404a3a0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: ISA 31:6
Text: Turn ye unto him from whom the children of Israel have deeply revolted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/31/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14c273b1-2bd8-40d0-8560-c8f3dc67d576>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: ISA 31:7
Text: For in that day every man shall cast away his idols of silver, and his idols of gold, which your own hands have made unto you for a sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/31/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67f14d9b-15e1-4a1f-aec8-0e56130e0890>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: ISA 31:8
Text: Then shall the Assyrian fall with the sword, not of a mighty man; and the sword, not of a mean man, shall devour him: but he shall flee from the sword, and his young men shall be discomfited.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/31/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee85ace0-65dc-492a-8c12-dc65359aeb09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: ISA 31:9
Text: And he shall pass over to his strong hold for fear, and his princes shall be afraid of the ensign, saith the LORD, whose fire is in Zion, and his furnace in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/32/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:880cd4ae-fa38-48dd-9dcc-f9f9e6f5f863>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: ISA 32:1
Text: Behold, a king shall reign in righteousness, and princes shall rule in judgment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/32/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0abe7e0-e5fe-45a7-b56f-26b23ec9707c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: ISA 32:2
Text: And a man shall be as an hiding place from the wind, and a covert from the tempest; as rivers of water in a dry place, as the shadow of a great rock in a weary land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/32/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df4be588-84d8-4f0a-959b-99bc2176dca2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: ISA 32:3
Text: And the eyes of them that see shall not be dim, and the ears of them that hear shall hearken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/32/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc76e88c-9418-4363-b18f-9f7737b9ad18>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: ISA 32:4
Text: The heart also of the rash shall understand knowledge, and the tongue of the stammerers shall be ready to speak plainly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/32/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c932330-22aa-4766-b5eb-abe13cc833fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: ISA 32:5
Text: The vile person shall be no more called liberal, nor the churl said to be bountiful.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/32/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bb3d18f-95e5-42bf-ad12-620e3f4b917d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: ISA 32:6
Text: For the vile person will speak villany, and his heart will work iniquity, to practise hypocrisy, and to utter error against the LORD, to make empty the soul of the hungry, and he will cause the drink of the thirsty to fail.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/32/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be150c21-82c4-4921-aaca-aa6fca9625d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: ISA 32:7
Text: The instruments also of the churl are evil: he deviseth wicked devices to destroy the poor with lying words, even when the needy speaketh right.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/32/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a11e10f-6b88-4c7b-be86-90864a88cd4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: ISA 32:8
Text: But the liberal deviseth liberal things; and by liberal things shall he stand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/32/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71e52900-776f-4650-8c4e-e12ef01f59bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: ISA 32:9
Text: Rise up, ye women that are at ease; hear my voice, ye careless daughters; give ear unto my speech.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/32/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9cdfb6c0-468e-4a69-8e05-f2b0a8482c90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: ISA 32:10
Text: Many days and years shall ye be troubled, ye careless women: for the vintage shall fail, the gathering shall not come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/32/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0934347e-f94d-4f40-9c4f-4b8db57ed190>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: ISA 32:11
Text: Tremble, ye women that are at ease; be troubled, ye careless ones: strip you, and make you bare, and gird sackcloth upon your loins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/32/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6caa3ac3-69f2-4dc4-bc29-1c6fea7a1d46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: ISA 32:12
Text: They shall lament for the teats, for the pleasant fields, for the fruitful vine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/32/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f56dde90-64b0-41bf-a59d-92d654981c49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: ISA 32:13
Text: Upon the land of my people shall come up thorns and briers; yea, upon all the houses of joy in the joyous city:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/32/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:290b2892-7af7-43eb-95e8-d1035a953853>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: ISA 32:14
Text: Because the palaces shall be forsaken; the multitude of the city shall be left; the forts and towers shall be for dens for ever, a joy of wild asses, a pasture of flocks;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/32/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7749cb4-bec9-4cdd-a6c5-302239504b48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: ISA 32:15
Text: Until the spirit be poured upon us from on high, and the wilderness be a fruitful field, and the fruitful field be counted for a forest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/32/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e4fb073-6bc2-4ba2-af01-739f6bcb3d60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: ISA 32:16
Text: Then judgment shall dwell in the wilderness, and righteousness remain in the fruitful field.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/32/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5d5bf3a-aee3-4c02-8f7b-ad01b508bda6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: ISA 32:17
Text: And the work of righteousness shall be peace; and the effect of righteousness quietness and assurance for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/32/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22a2d8d4-bc91-447e-a54f-df141cc768c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: ISA 32:18
Text: And my people shall dwell in a peaceable habitation, and in sure dwellings, and in quiet resting places;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/32/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fef2ab7b-a2cd-42c7-af0b-12cc960f6001>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: ISA 32:19
Text: When it shall hail, coming down on the forest; and the city shall be low in a low place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/32/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:067c5368-c3c1-4d78-964f-5487e56ee545>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: ISA 32:20
Text: Blessed are ye that sow beside all waters, that send forth thither the feet of the ox and the ass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24534977-201d-4164-baff-e6907c887c33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 302

Reference: ISA 33:1
Text: Woe to thee that spoilest, and thou wast not spoiled; and dealest treacherously, and they dealt not treacherously with thee! when thou shalt cease to spoil, thou shalt be spoiled; and when thou shalt make an end to deal treacherously, they shall deal treacherously with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef03d9d1-2328-417d-a6f1-ce7b2be99e4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: ISA 33:2
Text: O LORD, be gracious unto us; we have waited for thee: be thou their arm every morning, our salvation also in the time of trouble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e30c5d46-0577-4115-8cda-18e253ee403f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: ISA 33:3
Text: At the noise of the tumult the people fled; at the lifting up of thyself the nations were scattered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:453c8fc9-a3a0-4683-a04b-05df68070ef4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: ISA 33:4
Text: And your spoil shall be gathered like the gathering of the caterpiller: as the running to and fro of locusts shall he run upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03bf20c4-82c5-43e1-bd04-f7e1edaaef71>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: ISA 33:5
Text: The LORD is exalted; for he dwelleth on high: he hath filled Zion with judgment and righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3eb9222c-fe40-48c4-812c-00a93a08b521>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: ISA 33:6
Text: And wisdom and knowledge shall be the stability of thy times, and strength of salvation: the fear of the LORD is his treasure.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9bbff30-46bb-4bab-97cd-c368ff259ab5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: ISA 33:7
Text: Behold, their valiant ones shall cry without: the ambassadors of peace shall weep bitterly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7bcab669-9ec5-42ce-a81e-167919f69b7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: ISA 33:8
Text: The highways lie waste, the wayfaring man ceaseth: he hath broken the covenant, he hath despised the cities, he regardeth no man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02b4ab97-08bc-47d1-914e-5a4a8b05c3b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: ISA 33:9
Text: The earth mourneth and languisheth: Lebanon is ashamed and hewn down: Sharon is like a wilderness; and Bashan and Carmel shake off their fruits.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2ac92e3-0523-410c-97d3-74b5524b341b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: ISA 33:10
Text: Now will I rise, saith the LORD; now will I be exalted; now will I lift up myself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d07545ff-e983-46f2-9dfa-ec23e5ed58d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: ISA 33:11
Text: Ye shall conceive chaff, ye shall bring forth stubble: your breath, as fire, shall devour you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99cf3e21-1c55-45ce-9211-99eaa905b0d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: ISA 33:12
Text: And the people shall be as the burnings of lime: as thorns cut up shall they be burned in the fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b524b481-f726-40e8-acb5-d2587ca65d24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: ISA 33:13
Text: Hear, ye that are far off, what I have done; and, ye that are near, acknowledge my might.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf98684c-fe6e-43fd-ad02-91ab5e74e5d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: ISA 33:14
Text: The sinners in Zion are afraid; fearfulness hath surprised the hypocrites. Who among us shall dwell with the devouring fire? who among us shall dwell with everlasting burnings?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:adb631df-3eb3-40d3-98c7-8a8df2259303>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: ISA 33:15
Text: He that walketh righteously, and speaketh uprightly; he that despiseth the gain of oppressions, that shaketh his hands from holding of bribes, that stoppeth his ears from hearing of blood, and shutteth his eyes from seeing evil;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64fcd54e-aa92-4f00-be79-9977dad4b7c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: ISA 33:16
Text: He shall dwell on high: his place of defence shall be the munitions of rocks: bread shall be given him; his waters shall be sure.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16495ce5-1eb6-45df-b7c9-4e00d66557dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: ISA 33:17
Text: Thine eyes shall see the king in his beauty: they shall behold the land that is very far off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a7e46f3-29ac-4283-ab8e-028eef0f50c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: ISA 33:18
Text: Thine heart shall meditate terror. Where is the scribe? where is the receiver? where is he that counted the towers?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52827634-9545-4060-9257-b67dd51daf9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: ISA 33:19
Text: Thou shalt not see a fierce people, a people of a deeper speech than thou canst perceive; of a stammering tongue, that thou canst not understand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00dea7b3-13a0-4687-966b-940d02e7e04b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: ISA 33:20
Text: Look upon Zion, the city of our solemnities: thine eyes shall see Jerusalem a quiet habitation, a tabernacle that shall not be taken down; not one of the stakes thereof shall ever be removed, neither shall any of the cords thereof be broken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bbac0880-e763-4cc6-a81b-02b4d39402f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: ISA 33:21
Text: But there the glorious LORD will be unto us a place of broad rivers and streams; wherein shall go no galley with oars, neither shall gallant ship pass thereby.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a28df819-5d30-42ad-94cb-544cad9151e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: ISA 33:22
Text: For the LORD is our judge, the LORD is our lawgiver, the LORD is our king; he will save us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36b96974-2863-4110-ade7-b8afc82be5a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: ISA 33:23
Text: Thy tacklings are loosed; they could not well strengthen their mast, they could not spread the sail: then is the prey of a great spoil divided; the lame take the prey.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/33/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff515f7b-8f25-4113-b40c-1c810276b722>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: ISA 33:24
Text: And the inhabitant shall not say, I am sick: the people that dwell therein shall be forgiven their iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/34/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55426684-5444-4eca-bac1-d017f8e1547f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: ISA 34:1
Text: Come near, ye nations, to hear; and hearken, ye people: let the earth hear, and all that is therein; the world, and all things that come forth of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/34/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8435eac-473c-45be-80c3-b0337e2701c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: ISA 34:2
Text: For the indignation of the LORD is upon all nations, and his fury upon all their armies: he hath utterly destroyed them, he hath delivered them to the slaughter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/34/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1d1ed4b-9de4-4e5d-9a3c-f3b186052979>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: ISA 34:3
Text: Their slain also shall be cast out, and their stink shall come up out of their carcases, and the mountains shall be melted with their blood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/34/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11563e59-0ed2-4617-aec0-d915dedc97c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: ISA 34:4
Text: And all the host of heaven shall be dissolved, and the heavens shall be rolled together as a scroll: and all their host shall fall down, as the leaf falleth off from the vine, and as a falling fig from the fig tree.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/34/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d649f314-b057-4d22-ae09-ff6f6a226f04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: ISA 34:5
Text: For my sword shall be bathed in heaven: behold, it shall come down upon Idumea, and upon the people of my curse, to judgment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/34/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98679eda-05d8-4197-b385-92b2d16040e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: ISA 34:6
Text: The sword of the LORD is filled with blood, it is made fat with fatness, and with the blood of lambs and goats, with the fat of the kidneys of rams: for the LORD hath a sacrifice in Bozrah, and a great slaughter in the land of Idumea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/34/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8b75d91-9735-4eec-b190-868f0cd4a06b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: ISA 34:7
Text: And the unicorns shall come down with them, and the bullocks with the bulls; and their land shall be soaked with blood, and their dust made fat with fatness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/34/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e366cfa-bb90-4566-9d8c-2d9a48c8d6d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: ISA 34:8
Text: For it is the day of the LORD’s vengeance, and the year of recompences for the controversy of Zion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/34/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f3d65a7-f02e-4dae-9316-c1ef81e28f6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: ISA 34:9
Text: And the streams thereof shall be turned into pitch, and the dust thereof into brimstone, and the land thereof shall become burning pitch.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/34/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa350064-3eff-4f0e-8253-1c7ebd7a63e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: ISA 34:10
Text: It shall not be quenched night nor day; the smoke thereof shall go up for ever: from generation to generation it shall lie waste; none shall pass through it for ever and ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/34/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e0bb0f9-53ef-4be7-a221-66642922fdf5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: ISA 34:11
Text: But the cormorant and the bittern shall possess it; the owl also and the raven shall dwell in it: and he shall stretch out upon it the line of confusion, and the stones of emptiness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/34/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39b18c6b-5491-4262-aadf-b129a0c16cb9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: ISA 34:12
Text: They shall call the nobles thereof to the kingdom, but none shall be there, and all her princes shall be nothing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/34/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f519046-e4eb-46b3-93bd-0d747d8e3cad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: ISA 34:13
Text: And thorns shall come up in her palaces, nettles and brambles in the fortresses thereof: and it shall be an habitation of dragons, and a court for owls.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/34/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a84e4677-297d-4bd6-bcff-573bd4074d50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: ISA 34:14
Text: The wild beasts of the desert shall also meet with the wild beasts of the island, and the satyr shall cry to his fellow; the screech owl also shall rest there, and find for herself a place of rest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/34/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fcb58fd-990e-4052-bb40-5719ae38605f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: ISA 34:15
Text: There shall the great owl make her nest, and lay, and hatch, and gather under her shadow: there shall the vultures also be gathered, every one with her mate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/34/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:337610b2-8571-47e2-8592-e2ff2329ca7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: ISA 34:16
Text: Seek ye out of the book of the LORD, and read: no one of these shall fail, none shall want her mate: for my mouth it hath commanded, and his spirit it hath gathered them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/34/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dedd05cd-9a38-4608-9732-4aef9a302aaf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: ISA 34:17
Text: And he hath cast the lot for them, and his hand hath divided it unto them by line: they shall possess it for ever, from generation to generation shall they dwell therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/35/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5461c688-4ece-4afb-8b28-cb3276443537>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: ISA 35:1
Text: The wilderness and the solitary place shall be glad for them; and the desert shall rejoice, and blossom as the rose.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/35/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:efe8d46c-6d3f-4e8a-bcfc-70b37cd69fb1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: ISA 35:2
Text: It shall blossom abundantly, and rejoice even with joy and singing: the glory of Lebanon shall be given unto it, the excellency of Carmel and Sharon, they shall see the glory of the LORD, and the excellency of our God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/35/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce3a927b-7f22-4447-abc3-ac97ba605d49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: ISA 35:3
Text: Strengthen ye the weak hands, and confirm the feeble knees.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/35/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5793869a-bb3f-4919-8470-75a7cd9075c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: ISA 35:4
Text: Say to them that are of a fearful heart, Be strong, fear not: behold, your God will come with vengeance, even God with a recompence; he will come and save you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/35/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c80199fa-1800-475f-9b17-999044a53baa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: ISA 35:5
Text: Then the eyes of the blind shall be opened, and the ears of the deaf shall be unstopped.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/35/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb576abd-0b04-4b5c-a5b7-4fadf12a3e86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: ISA 35:6
Text: Then shall the lame man leap as an hart, and the tongue of the dumb sing: for in the wilderness shall waters break out, and streams in the desert.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/35/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6019bbee-5134-443f-81c1-7e1dd30a18c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: ISA 35:7
Text: And the parched ground shall become a pool, and the thirsty land springs of water: in the habitation of dragons, where each lay, shall be grass with reeds and rushes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/35/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1b0c629-d4ad-4078-96f6-9d83d1f765c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: ISA 35:8
Text: And an highway shall be there, and a way, and it shall be called The way of holiness; the unclean shall not pass over it; but it shall be for those: the wayfaring men, though fools, shall not err therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/35/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:041ea839-5008-4208-a4a4-f168d83b9bbe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: ISA 35:9
Text: No lion shall be there, nor any ravenous beast shall go up thereon, it shall not be found there; but the redeemed shall walk there:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/35/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1be88e0f-34cd-4782-a302-d4ebbe1b16ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: ISA 35:10
Text: And the ransomed of the LORD shall return, and come to Zion with songs and everlasting joy upon their heads: they shall obtain joy and gladness, and sorrow and sighing shall flee away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/36/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91897884-0930-4fe6-9f4f-2c4336354379>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: ISA 36:1
Text: Now it came to pass in the fourteenth year of king Hezekiah, that Sennacherib king of Assyria came up against all the defenced cities of Judah, and took them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/36/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8da65aeb-a8b6-4b82-8a4b-259a269ef2cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: ISA 36:2
Text: And the king of Assyria sent Rabshakeh from Lachish to Jerusalem unto king Hezekiah with a great army. And he stood by the conduit of the upper pool in the highway of the fuller’s field.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/36/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53d82979-7ee4-4446-8c72-7c92e3c16ca9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: ISA 36:3
Text: Then came forth unto him Eliakim, Hilkiah’s son, which was over the house, and Shebna the scribe, and Joah, Asaph’s son, the recorder.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/36/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d55b060e-3739-4153-977d-4aa47b1dde93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: ISA 36:4
Text: And Rabshakeh said unto them, Say ye now to Hezekiah, Thus saith the great king, the king of Assyria, What confidence is this wherein thou trustest?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/36/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acaf89fa-a7f0-4ebb-b2c5-d368a218b6af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: ISA 36:5
Text: I say, sayest thou, (but they are but vain words) I have counsel and strength for war: now on whom dost thou trust, that thou rebellest against me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/36/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85fb862f-fb4d-47ff-aef0-07af786ef771>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: ISA 36:6
Text: Lo, thou trustest in the staff of this broken reed, on Egypt; whereon if a man lean, it will go into his hand, and pierce it: so is Pharaoh king of Egypt to all that trust in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/36/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61e248b8-8c2d-40e0-a584-f67f153d89b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: ISA 36:7
Text: But if thou say to me, We trust in the LORD our God: is it not he, whose high places and whose altars Hezekiah hath taken away, and said to Judah and to Jerusalem, Ye shall worship before this altar?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/36/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b962ace-e489-4b92-9c80-b3892472dbfc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: ISA 36:8
Text: Now therefore give pledges, I pray thee, to my master the king of Assyria, and I will give thee two thousand horses, if thou be able on thy part to set riders upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/36/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a58c7d99-9c9b-4055-9e4a-09dad4bd664f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: ISA 36:9
Text: How then wilt thou turn away the face of one captain of the least of my master’s servants, and put thy trust on Egypt for chariots and for horsemen?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/36/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1803875c-893c-4e5b-9b5d-16cd4f585e97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: ISA 36:10
Text: And am I now come up without the LORD against this land to destroy it? the LORD said unto me, Go up against this land, and destroy it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/36/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e90600cf-f126-44aa-bde3-a4b8deaa1f24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: ISA 36:11
Text: Then said Eliakim and Shebna and Joah unto Rabshakeh, Speak, I pray thee, unto thy servants in the Syrian language; for we understand it: and speak not to us in the Jews’ language, in the ears of the people that are on the wall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/36/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87b6d606-7bae-4dea-b206-9d884eb0cae9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: ISA 36:12
Text: But Rabshakeh said, Hath my master sent me to thy master and to thee to speak these words? hath he not sent me to the men that sit upon the wall, that they may eat their own dung, and drink their own piss with you?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/36/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51b64f1a-62e4-4055-9a21-498b94a339de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: ISA 36:13
Text: Then Rabshakeh stood, and cried with a loud voice in the Jews’ language, and said, Hear ye the words of the great king, the king of Assyria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/36/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5edf58f-2774-49d1-bced-03de2c55c3f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: ISA 36:14
Text: Thus saith the king, Let not Hezekiah deceive you: for he shall not be able to deliver you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/36/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2b45d7a-e841-451f-8897-b374558cac32>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: ISA 36:15
Text: Neither let Hezekiah make you trust in the LORD, saying, The LORD will surely deliver us: this city shall not be delivered into the hand of the king of Assyria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/36/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df73ee04-e3cd-4f7c-b083-84a815b760b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: ISA 36:16
Text: Hearken not to Hezekiah: for thus saith the king of Assyria, Make an agreement with me by a present, and come out to me: and eat ye every one of his vine, and every one of his fig tree, and drink ye every one the waters of his own cistern;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/36/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9912b78-ffb3-4441-8242-e80b12eed80e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: ISA 36:17
Text: Until I come and take you away to a land like your own land, a land of corn and wine, a land of bread and vineyards.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/36/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f4d3f4c-9114-4329-9bc1-d7ec2889a70c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: ISA 36:18
Text: Beware lest Hezekiah persuade you, saying, the LORD will deliver us. Hath any of the gods of the nations delivered his land out of the hand of the king of Assyria?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/36/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23807dce-3ba0-45be-96ab-9831b21c9de7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: ISA 36:19
Text: Where are the gods of Hamath and Arphad? where are the gods of Sepharvaim? and have they delivered Samaria out of my hand?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/36/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f1b5c70-b3d4-42b5-93c6-da08afbf2081>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: ISA 36:20
Text: Who are they among all the gods of these lands, that have delivered their land out of my hand, that the LORD should deliver Jerusalem out of my hand?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/36/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a724d0b6-7aed-4d0d-9825-340dd567551b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: ISA 36:21
Text: But they held their peace, and answered him not a word: for the king’s commandment was, saying, Answer him not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/36/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13c72ed1-9619-4a50-9434-3f6674f956d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: ISA 36:22
Text: Then came Eliakim, the son of Hilkiah, that was over the household, and Shebna the scribe, and Joah, the son of Asaph, the recorder, to Hezekiah with their clothes rent, and told him the words of Rabshakeh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4c919c4-93d7-47a8-a8fa-ab7eef27450f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: ISA 37:1
Text: And it came to pass, when king Hezekiah heard it, that he rent his clothes, and covered himself with sackcloth, and went into the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5f8a139-c521-41ff-9af0-059bcc7a59ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: ISA 37:2
Text: And he sent Eliakim, who was over the household, and Shebna the scribe, and the elders of the priests covered with sackcloth, unto Isaiah the prophet the son of Amoz.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e61ff468-356e-4bab-8c97-4afc1d336b67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: ISA 37:3
Text: And they said unto him, Thus saith Hezekiah, This day is a day of trouble, and of rebuke, and of blasphemy: for the children are come to the birth, and there is not strength to bring forth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ed72b71-e82b-41a4-9a18-52d7d03bd31e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 282

Reference: ISA 37:4
Text: It may be the LORD thy God will hear the words of Rabshakeh, whom the king of Assyria his master hath sent to reproach the living God, and will reprove the words which the LORD thy God hath heard: wherefore lift up thy prayer for the remnant that is left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fefddbc8-b9fa-408a-a1c4-6b47b5b90c56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: ISA 37:5
Text: So the servants of king Hezekiah came to Isaiah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66956fbd-9b21-4037-bd8d-b01eede8217e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: ISA 37:6
Text: And Isaiah said unto them, Thus shall ye say unto your master, Thus saith the LORD, Be not afraid of the words that thou hast heard, wherewith the servants of the king of Assyria have blasphemed me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fb12048-1048-467e-9d9e-18d684dab585>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: ISA 37:7
Text: Behold, I will send a blast upon him, and he shall hear a rumour, and return to his own land; and I will cause him to fall by the sword in his own land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85d1a196-0138-4ef1-94f0-d3098a7112e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: ISA 37:8
Text: So Rabshakeh returned, and found the king of Assyria warring against Libnah: for he had heard that he was departed from Lachish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9908e973-2ea8-45a2-adfe-1cd994eb7de8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: ISA 37:9
Text: And he heard say concerning Tirhakah king of Ethiopia, He is come forth to make war with thee. And when he heard it, he sent messengers to Hezekiah, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65583aec-ec84-41c4-89c0-514df5748416>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: ISA 37:10
Text: Thus shall ye speak to Hezekiah king of Judah, saying, Let not thy God, in whom thou trustest, deceive thee, saying, Jerusalem shall not be given into the hand of the king of Assyria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cce943ab-118c-4d1b-a8d5-5737c826c003>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: ISA 37:11
Text: Behold, thou hast heard what the kings of Assyria have done to all lands by destroying them utterly; and shalt thou be delivered?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b98d361f-d524-46cd-a6bf-e8f1a15d31e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: ISA 37:12
Text: Have the gods of the nations delivered them which my fathers have destroyed, as Gozan, and Haran, and Rezeph, and the children of Eden which were in Telassar?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c1d3a01-04ac-406a-97d3-d95b3b0de782>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: ISA 37:13
Text: Where is the king of Hamath, and the king of Arphad, and the king of the city of Sepharvaim, Hena, and Ivah?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ae08387-9265-431f-9834-0139412a20fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: ISA 37:14
Text: And Hezekiah received the letter from the hand of the messengers, and read it: and Hezekiah went up unto the house of the LORD, and spread it before the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b24a29e0-3d1d-45ad-b95d-dae8e7c9b2d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 70

Reference: ISA 37:15
Text: And Hezekiah prayed unto the LORD, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3c07cdd-453c-4a03-a492-6bf3aabb2afa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: ISA 37:16
Text: O LORD of hosts, God of Israel, that dwellest between the cherubims, thou art the God, even thou alone, of all the kingdoms of the earth: thou hast made heaven and earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0268c3fb-cfd9-4d18-bec2-4969c724f577>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: ISA 37:17
Text: Incline thine ear, O LORD, and hear; open thine eyes, O LORD, and see: and hear all the words of Sennacherib, which hath sent to reproach the living God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86e41e94-9874-476f-b16a-7e17cb36ec04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: ISA 37:18
Text: Of a truth, LORD, the kings of Assyria have laid waste all the nations, and their countries,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d02ded7-a992-4afd-90de-8065eb16b818>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: ISA 37:19
Text: And have cast their gods into the fire: for they were no gods, but the work of men’s hands, wood and stone: therefore they have destroyed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3436d89b-3e34-41dc-a201-1e51bfef8941>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: ISA 37:20
Text: Now therefore, O LORD our God, save us from his hand, that all the kingdoms of the earth may know that thou art the LORD, even thou only.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:775a27a2-6ee9-4ffa-871b-e557e837d685>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: ISA 37:21
Text: Then Isaiah the son of Amoz sent unto Hezekiah, saying, Thus saith the LORD God of Israel, Whereas thou hast prayed to me against Sennacherib king of Assyria:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1bc429eb-fef2-4836-b3d3-af39eadfc17f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: ISA 37:22
Text: This is the word which the LORD hath spoken concerning him; The virgin, the daughter of Zion, hath despised thee, and laughed thee to scorn; the daughter of Jerusalem hath shaken her head at thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3fcee20-8cf0-4360-ac73-1af2c9cc1257>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: ISA 37:23
Text: Whom hast thou reproached and blasphemed? and against whom hast thou exalted thy voice, and lifted up thine eyes on high? even against the Holy One of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f82d7d91-d88c-4413-8976-0ae805104839>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 348

Reference: ISA 37:24
Text: By thy servants hast thou reproached the Lord, and hast said, By the multitude of my chariots am I come up to the height of the mountains, to the sides of Lebanon; and I will cut down the tall cedars thereof, and the choice fir trees thereof: and I will enter into the height of his border, and the forest of his Carmel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e90d2737-a867-4c9a-bdcc-e0b116082268>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: ISA 37:25
Text: I have digged, and drunk water; and with the sole of my feet have I dried up all the rivers of the besieged places.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0aed99c7-b575-445e-8070-a02941a6a5db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: ISA 37:26
Text: Hast thou not heard long ago, how I have done it; and of ancient times, that I have formed it? now have I brought it to pass, that thou shouldest be to lay waste defenced cities into ruinous heaps.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93423185-57a0-4801-bfcf-7612f47a3ced>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: ISA 37:27
Text: Therefore their inhabitants were of small power, they were dismayed and confounded: they were as the grass of the field, and as the green herb, as the grass on the housetops, and as corn blasted before it be grown up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2b4c43e-9631-4287-bc17-e73913ab3fce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: ISA 37:28
Text: But I know thy abode, and thy going out, and thy coming in, and thy rage against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f0df196-098f-417b-86ee-eccd17337f51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: ISA 37:29
Text: Because thy rage against me, and thy tumult, is come up into mine ears, therefore will I put my hook in thy nose, and my bridle in thy lips, and I will turn thee back by the way by which thou camest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a56439c-0f6c-443b-95f3-75d472af1b1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: ISA 37:30
Text: And this shall be a sign unto thee, Ye shall eat this year such as groweth of itself; and the second year that which springeth of the same: and in the third year sow ye, and reap, and plant vineyards, and eat the fruit thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df0756bd-0a9d-4aa1-82bf-43167a48160e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: ISA 37:31
Text: And the remnant that is escaped of the house of Judah shall again take root downward, and bear fruit upward:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9f5bb0f-63bc-4f0f-b530-f52f1c0d7468>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: ISA 37:32
Text: For out of Jerusalem shall go forth a remnant, and they that escape out of mount Zion: the zeal of the LORD of hosts shall do this.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7763b072-c440-4f5c-9d19-a94d39fdf3d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: ISA 37:33
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD concerning the king of Assyria, He shall not come into this city, nor shoot an arrow there, nor come before it with shields, nor cast a bank against it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39668ac2-557f-4eed-ad9c-c2906c8b8b01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: ISA 37:34
Text: By the way that he came, by the same shall he return, and shall not come into this city, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d8df2fe-5883-4847-8dff-0dee6cb7e8a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: ISA 37:35
Text: For I will defend this city to save it for mine own sake, and for my servant David’s sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17803b2a-197e-491b-b25b-5bd1a0ed6ba0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: ISA 37:36
Text: Then the angel of the LORD went forth, and smote in the camp of the Assyrians a hundred and fourscore and five thousand: and when they arose early in the morning, behold, they were all dead corpses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b985bb0b-8ef1-4352-b2b0-f418d1092d41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: ISA 37:37
Text: So Sennacherib king of Assyria departed, and went and returned, and dwelt at Nineveh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/37/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9369d662-b3ab-43bf-9170-95944974ec17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: ISA 37:38
Text: And it came to pass, as he was worshipping in the house of Nisroch his god, that Adrammelech and Sharezer his sons smote him with the sword; and they escaped into the land of Armenia: and Esarhaddon his son reigned in his stead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/38/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5fdd1826-0617-4f2f-8d7f-7c8a33448174>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: ISA 38:1
Text: In those days was Hezekiah sick unto death. And Isaiah the prophet the son of Amoz came unto him, and said unto him, Thus saith the LORD, Set thine house in order: for thou shalt die, and not live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/38/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5c6bdf9-3a7d-41af-a64a-b4b8b87b0fb2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: ISA 38:2
Text: Then Hezekiah turned his face toward the wall, and prayed unto the LORD,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/38/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c6241fa-852c-426a-8ee5-48a0b1b3d7cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: ISA 38:3
Text: And said, Remember now, O LORD, I beseech thee, how I have walked before thee in truth and with a perfect heart, and have done that which is good in thy sight. And Hezekiah wept sore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/38/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b76dcd90-c279-4c69-9d04-b5c91d60b9ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: ISA 38:4
Text: Then came the word of the LORD to Isaiah, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/38/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3874c9e7-2947-4ab8-a508-563fce5579f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: ISA 38:5
Text: Go, and say to Hezekiah, Thus saith the LORD, the God of David thy father, I have heard thy prayer, I have seen thy tears: behold, I will add unto thy days fifteen years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/38/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:930f3725-39cb-4952-843f-dfc7a661930a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: ISA 38:6
Text: And I will deliver thee and this city out of the hand of the king of Assyria: and I will defend this city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/38/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56f3f62a-ffda-4a81-a922-c3136af17be9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: ISA 38:7
Text: And this shall be a sign unto thee from the LORD, that the LORD will do this thing that he hath spoken;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/38/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dac47ace-fcb0-43cd-8ae4-2879c875c25b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: ISA 38:8
Text: Behold, I will bring again the shadow of the degrees, which is gone down in the sun dial of Ahaz, ten degrees backward. So the sun returned ten degrees, by which degrees it was gone down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/38/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a669bcd-651d-4b73-bdf7-de5e97b1b35b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: ISA 38:9
Text: The writing of Hezekiah king of Judah, when he had been sick, and was recovered of his sickness:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/38/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7650fb89-3ad1-4caf-bf31-f0e099ffb7f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: ISA 38:10
Text: I said in the cutting off of my days, I shall go to the gates of the grave: I am deprived of the residue of my years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/38/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:402fb123-0e15-4c4a-859e-3b35a2f1fea6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: ISA 38:11
Text: I said, I shall not see the LORD, even the LORD, in the land of the living: I shall behold man no more with the inhabitants of the world.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/38/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bb6527c-2bff-4c0b-9579-e68d66d891ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: ISA 38:12
Text: Mine age is departed, and is removed from me as a shepherd’s tent: I have cut off like a weaver my life: he will cut me off with pining sickness: from day even to night wilt thou make an end of me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/38/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:308b5db3-7c06-432f-8ab0-bfdaf78cc390>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: ISA 38:13
Text: I reckoned till morning, that, as a lion, so will he break all my bones: from day even to night wilt thou make an end of me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/38/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f86640a9-a14a-4b45-b167-65fbef5001c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: ISA 38:14
Text: Like a crane or a swallow, so did I chatter: I did mourn as a dove: mine eyes fail with looking upward: O LORD, I am oppressed; undertake for me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/38/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:228b3294-0b33-48d2-9b8e-8bf1dd6d044b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: ISA 38:15
Text: What shall I say? he hath both spoken unto me, and himself hath done it: I shall go softly all my years in the bitterness of my soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/38/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e82ce6f4-665d-42db-b084-a0e7c7361e34>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: ISA 38:16
Text: O LORD, by these things men live, and in all these things is the life of my spirit: so wilt thou recover me, and make me to live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/38/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52210671-3d31-4ba0-bf34-2708728bca43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: ISA 38:17
Text: Behold, for peace I had great bitterness: but thou hast in love to my soul delivered it from the pit of corruption: for thou hast cast all my sins behind thy back.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/38/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f03aeb4-e619-495c-9d95-72ba31b5bf64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: ISA 38:18
Text: For the grave cannot praise thee, death can not celebrate thee: they that go down into the pit cannot hope for thy truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/38/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74e8349e-71a5-4cf2-be12-8775ff4c2078>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: ISA 38:19
Text: The living, the living, he shall praise thee, as I do this day: the father to the children shall make known thy truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/38/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0272c2b-e4fb-4221-abaf-54221d95ddd0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: ISA 38:20
Text: The LORD was ready to save me: therefore we will sing my songs to the stringed instruments all the days of our life in the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/38/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e3542a4-1fa6-48f3-a143-bd3774a5dffa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: ISA 38:21
Text: For Isaiah had said, Let them take a lump of figs, and lay it for a plaister upon the boil, and he shall recover.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/38/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e34b982-d782-4498-b1e1-0343ac083217>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: ISA 38:22
Text: Hezekiah also had said, What is the sign that I shall go up to the house of the LORD?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/39/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dcb19d95-60d1-4340-b0de-9612981a5a72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: ISA 39:1
Text: At that time Merodachbaladan, the son of Baladan, king of Babylon, sent letters and a present to Hezekiah: for he had heard that he had been sick, and was recovered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/39/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:437a49bd-ec5e-48ef-88f6-2658847cf7e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 338

Reference: ISA 39:2
Text: And Hezekiah was glad of them, and shewed them the house of his precious things, the silver, and the gold, and the spices, and the precious ointment, and all the house of his armour, and all that was found in his treasures: there was nothing in his house, nor in all his dominion, that Hezekiah shewed them not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/39/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63738fbf-6018-4403-b766-fe2015595160>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: ISA 39:3
Text: Then came Isaiah the prophet unto king Hezekiah, and said unto him, What said these men? and from whence came they unto thee? And Hezekiah said, They are come from a far country unto me, even from Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/39/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9bbaae1-95ef-45a7-9b16-e7a44b0601cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: ISA 39:4
Text: Then said he, What have they seen in thine house? And Hezekiah answered, All that is in mine house have they seen: there is nothing among my treasures that I have not shewed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/39/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c35a5d21-ec6a-43e5-afb2-4918ea305e09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: ISA 39:5
Text: Then said Isaiah to Hezekiah, Hear the word of the LORD of hosts:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/39/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13c412b5-8d85-4396-b123-8edc22877bb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: ISA 39:6
Text: Behold, the days come, that all that is in thine house, and that which thy fathers have laid up in store until this day, shall be carried to Babylon: nothing shall be left, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/39/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ceb9d69-f994-44d6-b8ec-4057d25bd117>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: ISA 39:7
Text: And of thy sons that shall issue from thee, which thou shalt beget, shall they take away; and they shall be eunuchs in the palace of the king of Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/39/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da027242-e472-49cb-98e2-6690ddc2c891>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: ISA 39:8
Text: Then said Hezekiah to Isaiah, Good is the word of the LORD which thou hast spoken. He said moreover, For there shall be peace and truth in my days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62e9aae8-2a88-4642-83d9-3a1bb22fd16a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: ISA 40:1
Text: Comfort ye, comfort ye my people, saith your God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f2440f7-367f-46b2-8c4f-0187cb53ee03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: ISA 40:2
Text: Speak ye comfortably to Jerusalem, and cry unto her, that her warfare is accomplished, that her iniquity is pardoned: for she hath received of the LORD’s hand double for all her sins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12cb5f7b-4140-4741-bed7-84fcc86aeb21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: ISA 40:3
Text: The voice of him that crieth in the wilderness, Prepare ye the way of the LORD, make straight in the desert a highway for our God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0be1027d-17ed-4d8d-979a-5c6db3706f61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: ISA 40:4
Text: Every valley shall be exalted, and every mountain and hill shall be made low: and the crooked shall be made straight, and the rough places plain:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e569c290-21e6-4aba-9e72-f5ba418aa5f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: ISA 40:5
Text: And the glory of the LORD shall be revealed, and all flesh shall see it together: for the mouth of the LORD hath spoken it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eadc7601-1c93-45c0-a282-eda9ccbe07c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: ISA 40:6
Text: The voice said, Cry. And he said, What shall I cry? All flesh is grass, and all the goodliness thereof is as the flower of the field:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86004fe6-81cf-4488-a2d5-73ec0a25ddd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: ISA 40:7
Text: The grass withereth, the flower fadeth: because the spirit of the LORD bloweth upon it: surely the people is grass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f67f77c-940b-48d6-b780-6bbaa50b59ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: ISA 40:8
Text: The grass withereth, the flower fadeth: but the word of our God shall stand for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4586b77f-7fa1-4db9-b07c-2cbd6500c504>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: ISA 40:9
Text: O Zion, that bringest good tidings, get thee up into the high mountain; O Jerusalem, that bringest good tidings, lift up thy voice with strength; lift it up, be not afraid; say unto the cities of Judah, Behold your God!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60159fdb-45de-4231-9d59-80b375738edb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: ISA 40:10
Text: Behold, the Lord GOD will come with strong hand, and his arm shall rule for him: behold, his reward is with him, and his work before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2a883eb-39c4-4c37-9944-18907544fbb8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: ISA 40:11
Text: He shall feed his flock like a shepherd: he shall gather the lambs with his arm, and carry them in his bosom, and shall gently lead those that are with young.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5df42380-df3e-4096-b10b-48173b3291ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: ISA 40:12
Text: Who hath measured the waters in the hollow of his hand, and meted out heaven with the span, and comprehended the dust of the earth in a measure, and weighed the mountains in scales, and the hills in a balance?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50adc79b-812a-4bc9-9729-58fdcf214378>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: ISA 40:13
Text: Who hath directed the Spirit of the LORD, or being his counsellor hath taught him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:757826d1-03a6-48c3-b54f-9b73cb7372ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: ISA 40:14
Text: With whom took he counsel, and who instructed him, and taught him in the path of judgment, and taught him knowledge, and shewed to him the way of understanding?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a0f458a-bba5-4425-a0e9-c6d604da3f08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: ISA 40:15
Text: Behold, the nations are as a drop of a bucket, and are counted as the small dust of the balance: behold, he taketh up the isles as a very little thing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9db3d42-2534-4b7d-9d3f-6055a72a9772>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: ISA 40:16
Text: And Lebanon is not sufficient to burn, nor the beasts thereof sufficient for a burnt offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc8a4bed-c0fc-4cc7-ae68-092fa9926fff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: ISA 40:17
Text: All nations before him are as nothing; and they are counted to him less than nothing, and vanity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d155ea79-12c4-4e17-91ac-9e32fdd9839d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: ISA 40:18
Text: To whom then will ye liken God? or what likeness will ye compare unto him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:017ad629-cc02-4fd3-b497-a5bb3e15c722>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: ISA 40:19
Text: The workman melteth a graven image, and the goldsmith spreadeth it over with gold, and casteth silver chains.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89c8b666-5371-4145-8bba-536a5408737e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: ISA 40:20
Text: He that is so impoverished that he hath no oblation chooseth a tree that will not rot; he seeketh unto him a cunning workman to prepare a graven image, that shall not be moved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67d3b081-a9da-4e87-8c6b-6d74f6ec9f41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: ISA 40:21
Text: Have ye not known? have ye not heard? hath it not been told you from the beginning? have ye not understood from the foundations of the earth?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:704b65b4-4913-4a60-95e0-a7693198c83c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: ISA 40:22
Text: It is he that sitteth upon the circle of the earth, and the inhabitants thereof are as grasshoppers; that stretcheth out the heavens as a curtain, and spreadeth them out as a tent to dwell in:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc47dbb6-d7da-4f6b-b521-e1b37f57f6c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: ISA 40:23
Text: That bringeth the princes to nothing; he maketh the judges of the earth as vanity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7f4efe5-f73b-4123-b42a-0c29f9024641>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: ISA 40:24
Text: Yea, they shall not be planted; yea, they shall not be sown: yea, their stock shall not take root in the earth: and he shall also blow upon them, and they shall wither, and the whirlwind shall take them away as stubble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef1c7a00-5c65-4b79-8361-8c1008674232>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: ISA 40:25
Text: To whom then will ye liken me, or shall I be equal? saith the Holy One.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee91613c-03a8-4334-b6ef-8f73b80f87d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: ISA 40:26
Text: Lift up your eyes on high, and behold who hath created these things, that bringeth out their host by number: he calleth them all by names by the greatness of his might, for that he is strong in power; not one faileth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf0e86e5-e84b-4a15-95a7-fb337f515a9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: ISA 40:27
Text: Why sayest thou, O Jacob, and speakest, O Israel, My way is hid from the LORD, and my judgment is passed over from my God?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d06ccad5-a405-48f6-acaf-a297d80f12f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: ISA 40:28
Text: Hast thou not known? hast thou not heard, that the everlasting God, the LORD, the Creator of the ends of the earth, fainteth not, neither is weary? there is no searching of his understanding.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96431823-6611-4a5e-96df-957d32674636>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: ISA 40:29
Text: He giveth power to the faint; and to them that have no might he increaseth strength.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bd12d74-78dd-4c36-8b8b-579c55884403>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: ISA 40:30
Text: Even the youths shall faint and be weary, and the young men shall utterly fall:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/40/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8906bd03-09f5-4063-93ca-bc9f58eb948d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: ISA 40:31
Text: But they that wait upon the LORD shall renew their strength; they shall mount up with wings as eagles; they shall run, and not be weary; and they shall walk, and not faint.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bfa66295-037f-4398-9aef-14fb57684040>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: ISA 41:1
Text: Keep silence before me, O islands; and let the people renew their strength: let them come near; then let them speak: let us come near together to judgment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9bac1a67-55ad-4eda-a32a-6f710346eb05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: ISA 41:2
Text: Who raised up the righteous man from the east, called him to his foot, gave the nations before him, and made him rule over kings? he gave them as the dust to his sword, and as driven stubble to his bow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7950d0b-2c8b-4a74-a0c8-a5a12ef9a385>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: ISA 41:3
Text: He pursued them, and passed safely; even by the way that he had not gone with his feet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b6beea4-a84a-4ec5-8278-78b1280ae5d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: ISA 41:4
Text: Who hath wrought and done it, calling the generations from the beginning? I the LORD, the first, and with the last; I am he.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02b6ae22-cc19-4df4-803e-1a8bfcdeb596>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: ISA 41:5
Text: The isles saw it, and feared; the ends of the earth were afraid, drew near, and came.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bbd5e697-3957-4a2f-a93d-2434ea1e3490>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: ISA 41:6
Text: They helped every one his neighbour; and every one said to his brother, Be of good courage.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f89892c-5381-4d32-aa63-d71b288b6990>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: ISA 41:7
Text: So the carpenter encouraged the goldsmith, and he that smootheth with the hammer him that smote the anvil, saying, It is ready for the sodering: and he fastened it with nails, that it should not be moved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe058b84-c78a-4e7e-b012-fa45faf64d80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: ISA 41:8
Text: But thou, Israel, art my servant, Jacob whom I have chosen, the seed of Abraham my friend.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11b9f93d-db06-4abf-86e7-f97ed3d60335>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: ISA 41:9
Text: Thou whom I have taken from the ends of the earth, and called thee from the chief men thereof, and said unto thee, Thou art my servant; I have chosen thee, and not cast thee away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27d89d5b-0806-47c5-868b-c4fbd73cf451>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: ISA 41:10
Text: Fear thou not; for I am with thee: be not dismayed; for I am thy God: I will strengthen thee; yea, I will help thee; yea, I will uphold thee with the right hand of my righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:978bd3e4-239c-4a3d-984c-0225b3633eca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: ISA 41:11
Text: Behold, all they that were incensed against thee shall be ashamed and confounded: they shall be as nothing; and they that strive with thee shall perish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a37a2481-f6f7-4d88-8b26-73180f737cfb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: ISA 41:12
Text: Thou shalt seek them, and shalt not find them, even them that contended with thee: they that war against thee shall be as nothing, and as a thing of nought.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22732ee5-3a65-4816-b7c6-8d38f2d498a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: ISA 41:13
Text: For I the LORD thy God will hold thy right hand, saying unto thee, Fear not; I will help thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36884275-8ec3-4861-b247-aecde3458493>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: ISA 41:14
Text: Fear not, thou worm Jacob, and ye men of Israel; I will help thee, saith the LORD, and thy redeemer, the Holy One of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e11edca1-281a-47d0-8817-797a103ab35f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: ISA 41:15
Text: Behold, I will make thee a new sharp threshing instrument having teeth: thou shalt thresh the mountains, and beat them small, and shalt make the hills as chaff.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2618e086-f4e1-4e7b-9973-fc8f1aee5706>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: ISA 41:16
Text: Thou shalt fan them, and the wind shall carry them away, and the whirlwind shall scatter them: and thou shalt rejoice in the LORD, and shalt glory in the Holy One of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5385fa67-7fb9-4998-b56c-98cc17dcd633>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: ISA 41:17
Text: When the poor and needy seek water, and there is none, and their tongue faileth for thirst, I the LORD will hear them, I the God of Israel will not forsake them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24640432-8cda-4aed-a123-1bb8e8492bb6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: ISA 41:18
Text: I will open rivers in high places, and fountains in the midst of the valleys: I will make the wilderness a pool of water, and the dry land springs of water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fca7d8ab-e00a-4561-a40b-b8c7086e2dc9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: ISA 41:19
Text: I will plant in the wilderness the cedar, the shittah tree, and the myrtle, and the oil tree; I will set in the desert the fir tree, and the pine, and the box tree together:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a7cdfa3-af33-4f67-a37b-d6a3ae46be6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: ISA 41:20
Text: That they may see, and know, and consider, and understand together, that the hand of the LORD hath done this, and the Holy One of Israel hath created it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1dc7e6a0-6f8f-4b6a-970e-64b2d2364c1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: ISA 41:21
Text: Produce your cause, saith the LORD; bring forth your strong reasons, saith the King of Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f6b386e-649b-4f6f-8f5f-2b380c73e09f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: ISA 41:22
Text: Let them bring them forth, and shew us what shall happen: let them shew the former things, what they be, that we may consider them, and know the latter end of them; or declare us things for to come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7d9c68f-dcac-460d-9190-f97ae1fb3ff1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: ISA 41:23
Text: Shew the things that are to come hereafter, that we may know that ye are gods: yea, do good, or do evil, that we may be dismayed, and behold it together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d412d644-8771-47af-83c7-c6270ce5249e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: ISA 41:24
Text: Behold, ye are of nothing, and your work of nought: an abomination is he that chooseth you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6f36b10-8985-4821-ba85-5a53c952ccb1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: ISA 41:25
Text: I have raised up one from the north, and he shall come: from the rising of the sun shall he call upon my name: and he shall come upon princes as upon morter, and as the potter treadeth clay.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c03a18b-90f1-491f-9295-be61577a44ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: ISA 41:26
Text: Who hath declared from the beginning, that we may know? and beforetime, that we may say, He is righteous? yea, there is none that sheweth, yea, there is none that declareth, yea, there is none that heareth your words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f48391a5-d620-4389-9430-39bed89a5566>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: ISA 41:27
Text: The first shall say to Zion, Behold, behold them: and I will give to Jerusalem one that bringeth good tidings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b12e810-a837-4d17-848f-9fd4abb29a02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: ISA 41:28
Text: For I beheld, and there was no man; even among them, and there was no counsellor, that, when I asked of them, could answer a word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/41/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b52752e8-3b04-48b8-a8d0-c46e1ed91fd0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: ISA 41:29
Text: Behold, they are all vanity; their works are nothing: their molten images are wind and confusion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c61b6404-a1a9-4487-ae65-10d0d3158823>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: ISA 42:1
Text: Behold my servant, whom I uphold; mine elect, in whom my soul delighteth; I have put my spirit upon him: he shall bring forth judgment to the Gentiles.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9352e5c7-f93a-4ea0-b540-610ad8ec6242>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: ISA 42:2
Text: He shall not cry, nor lift up, nor cause his voice to be heard in the street.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87af3900-d850-4702-aa60-00ea17362f9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: ISA 42:3
Text: A bruised reed shall he not break, and the smoking flax shall he not quench: he shall bring forth judgment unto truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc84c342-9c48-45c2-ad0d-9f4a14254d27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: ISA 42:4
Text: He shall not fail nor be discouraged, till he have set judgment in the earth: and the isles shall wait for his law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8a827c9-7771-43c1-8a02-fc259d7974f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: ISA 42:5
Text: Thus saith God the LORD, he that created the heavens, and stretched them out; he that spread forth the earth, and that which cometh out of it; he that giveth breath unto the people upon it, and spirit to them that walk therein:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5b4dd77-c860-469d-938b-2d30bfac8101>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: ISA 42:6
Text: I the LORD have called thee in righteousness, and will hold thine hand, and will keep thee, and give thee for a covenant of the people, for a light of the Gentiles;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77a23059-8583-43a6-81e0-2ecfd0466679>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: ISA 42:7
Text: To open the blind eyes, to bring out the prisoners from the prison, and them that sit in darkness out of the prison house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bf260ee-a4b3-469c-ad4d-f60971903402>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: ISA 42:8
Text: I am the LORD: that is my name: and my glory will I not give to another, neither my praise to graven images.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dcff4c8d-22d2-4732-b4d8-e60531e329be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: ISA 42:9
Text: Behold, the former things are come to pass, and new things do I declare: before they spring forth I tell you of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49a22b61-63be-4c64-9e54-89b443b27b3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: ISA 42:10
Text: Sing unto the LORD a new song, and his praise from the end of the earth, ye that go down to the sea, and all that is therein; the isles, and the inhabitants thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c68bb70-50f2-4880-82a2-4b3f259b67e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: ISA 42:11
Text: Let the wilderness and the cities thereof lift up their voice, the villages that Kedar doth inhabit: let the inhabitants of the rock sing, let them shout from the top of the mountains.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:756048c1-864c-41ed-8b00-be3a61b068b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: ISA 42:12
Text: Let them give glory unto the LORD, and declare his praise in the islands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e01328e0-f79e-45b6-a386-3bb022103c74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: ISA 42:13
Text: The LORD shall go forth as a mighty man, he shall stir up jealousy like a man of war: he shall cry, yea, roar; he shall prevail against his enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:320a7e70-51ac-42c0-b59d-50528488aae2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: ISA 42:14
Text: I have long time holden my peace; I have been still, and refrained myself: now will I cry like a travailing woman; I will destroy and devour at once.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6f611ca-3158-4396-be81-804e3fec96ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: ISA 42:15
Text: I will make waste mountains and hills, and dry up all their herbs; and I will make the rivers islands, and I will dry up the pools.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbd77a4c-32e0-4976-904a-0ae52bbddcc8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: ISA 42:16
Text: And I will bring the blind by a way that they knew not; I will lead them in paths that they have not known: I will make darkness light before them, and crooked things straight. These things will I do unto them, and not forsake them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23c0af78-b9b0-4903-a146-78417685dc47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: ISA 42:17
Text: They shall be turned back, they shall be greatly ashamed, that trust in graven images, that say to the molten images, Ye are our gods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc35b216-2315-4512-be10-ef1ecf2d434d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: ISA 42:18
Text: Hear, ye deaf; and look, ye blind, that ye may see.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dde3db15-3dec-45eb-a67d-a7262a07221e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: ISA 42:19
Text: Who is blind, but my servant? or deaf, as my messenger that I sent? who is blind as he that is perfect, and blind as the LORD’s servant?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:510c6eb2-7652-4c30-ba16-596c76e377bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: ISA 42:20
Text: Seeing many things, but thou observest not; opening the ears, but he heareth not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c0e776a-afe4-4190-90a3-baf7a924ad77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: ISA 42:21
Text: The LORD is well pleased for his righteousness’ sake; he will magnify the law, and make it honourable.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd92a124-8095-44db-968b-34da96fe6ca5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: ISA 42:22
Text: But this is a people robbed and spoiled; they are all of them snared in holes, and they are hid in prison houses: they are for a prey, and none delivereth; for a spoil, and none saith, Restore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f7d4d44-e9c3-484a-bf86-53904bdb7058>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: ISA 42:23
Text: Who among you will give ear to this? who will hearken and hear for the time to come?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d667f182-8d63-43e9-b989-87ca630830f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: ISA 42:24
Text: Who gave Jacob for a spoil, and Israel to the robbers? did not the LORD, he against whom we have sinned? for they would not walk in his ways, neither were they obedient unto his law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/42/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a21b258d-54d5-4449-968b-5f607898f2b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: ISA 42:25
Text: Therefore he hath poured upon him the fury of his anger, and the strength of battle: and it hath set him on fire round about, yet he knew not; and it burned him, yet he laid it not to heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0b74198-c8c9-4f4a-8b5c-a608fa371961>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: ISA 43:1
Text: But now thus saith the LORD that created thee, O Jacob, and he that formed thee, O Israel, Fear not: for I have redeemed thee, I have called thee by thy name; thou art mine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:817b49ae-0b8d-4498-803e-a5e32d3c0c50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: ISA 43:2
Text: When thou passest through the waters, I will be with thee; and through the rivers, they shall not overflow thee: when thou walkest through the fire, thou shalt not be burned; neither shall the flame kindle upon thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4cb4cff7-f493-4d86-a2f9-a2e49275b284>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: ISA 43:3
Text: For I am the LORD thy God, the Holy One of Israel, thy Saviour: I gave Egypt for thy ransom, Ethiopia and Seba for thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07144ea6-729c-47c5-8fc2-9206a0fc0e5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: ISA 43:4
Text: Since thou wast precious in my sight, thou hast been honourable, and I have loved thee: therefore will I give men for thee, and people for thy life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:480e4ad0-177b-4793-a276-5e3ea9009c1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: ISA 43:5
Text: Fear not: for I am with thee: I will bring thy seed from the east, and gather thee from the west;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6af37938-a63f-4809-b2d1-5a82a7a75cdd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: ISA 43:6
Text: I will say to the north, Give up; and to the south, Keep not back: bring my sons from far, and my daughters from the ends of the earth;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f023271-c979-4ac3-8376-780bc29f6892>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: ISA 43:7
Text: Even every one that is called by my name: for I have created him for my glory, I have formed him; yea, I have made him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df2493eb-c6e2-4b4a-b386-7c8e5bf2b5f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: ISA 43:8
Text: Bring forth the blind people that have eyes, and the deaf that have ears.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2b81376-be99-4cc8-a9b8-8557a0130ad9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: ISA 43:9
Text: Let all the nations be gathered together, and let the people be assembled: who among them can declare this, and shew us former things? let them bring forth their witnesses, that they may be justified: or let them hear, and say, It is truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af15945e-7558-411d-94ff-727a639a9bf3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: ISA 43:10
Text: Ye are my witnesses, saith the LORD, and my servant whom I have chosen: that ye may know and believe me, and understand that I am he: before me there was no God formed, neither shall there be after me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b0cd663-83c3-40ac-9000-36e598644959>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: ISA 43:11
Text: I, even I, am the LORD; and beside me there is no saviour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d93ee04-6085-4916-8501-9ac3cc0aef8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: ISA 43:12
Text: I have declared, and have saved, and I have shewed, when there was no strange god among you: therefore ye are my witnesses, saith the LORD, that I am God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3abccb8-4f5b-4811-8bd3-4031390d2ed7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: ISA 43:13
Text: Yea, before the day was I am he; and there is none that can deliver out of my hand: I will work, and who shall let it?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c3c55e6-b255-4a0d-bc3e-02ebe3daf13a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: ISA 43:14
Text: Thus saith the LORD, your redeemer, the Holy One of Israel; For your sake I have sent to Babylon, and have brought down all their nobles, and the Chaldeans, whose cry is in the ships.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:312e4c0f-c615-41d2-b457-65193aaf8ff8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: ISA 43:15
Text: I am the LORD, your Holy One, the creator of Israel, your King.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49a298ed-caf5-491b-8d5f-2c0946fce5b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: ISA 43:16
Text: Thus saith the LORD, which maketh a way in the sea, and a path in the mighty waters;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae0243ae-2421-4e7d-b2ae-5023818c79b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: ISA 43:17
Text: Which bringeth forth the chariot and horse, the army and the power; they shall lie down together, they shall not rise: they are extinct, they are quenched as tow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b000a27a-e058-44f6-8833-9642309c4e84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: ISA 43:18
Text: Remember ye not the former things, neither consider the things of old.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3435074d-e63d-4257-a19a-0e9d69a82366>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: ISA 43:19
Text: Behold, I will do a new thing; now it shall spring forth; shall ye not know it? I will even make a way in the wilderness, and rivers in the desert.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46be844b-c714-4ea6-bdf2-0cdc5f6c08dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: ISA 43:20
Text: The beast of the field shall honour me, the dragons and the owls: because I give waters in the wilderness, and rivers in the desert, to give drink to my people, my chosen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0d87094-5b1b-46c1-93a7-da2ad5d28312>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: ISA 43:21
Text: This people have I formed for myself; they shall shew forth my praise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f33f0cef-2552-4563-99cc-70066ce810fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: ISA 43:22
Text: But thou hast not called upon me, O Jacob; but thou hast been weary of me, O Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cdc0eab5-2f80-4d50-9559-5f55bfbe19cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: ISA 43:23
Text: Thou hast not brought me the small cattle of thy burnt offerings; neither hast thou honoured me with thy sacrifices. I have not caused thee to serve with an offering, nor wearied thee with incense.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0214049e-b6d0-40c8-9da1-e40e57cb1ab9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: ISA 43:24
Text: Thou hast bought me no sweet cane with money, neither hast thou filled me with the fat of thy sacrifices: but thou hast made me to serve with thy sins, thou hast wearied me with thine iniquities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47feabed-95b2-414b-a170-5b32fe7904c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: ISA 43:25
Text: I, even I, am he that blotteth out thy transgressions for mine own sake, and will not remember thy sins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:270a8d22-4e07-4710-92f6-7971a60b4820>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: ISA 43:26
Text: Put me in remembrance: let us plead together: declare thou, that thou mayest be justified.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d59d7141-e425-4700-b712-d97abd5b6364>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: ISA 43:27
Text: Thy first father hath sinned, and thy teachers have transgressed against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/43/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3765c97b-31e9-499f-8e7b-b1ead6cc9ec1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: ISA 43:28
Text: Therefore I have profaned the princes of the sanctuary, and have given Jacob to the curse, and Israel to reproaches.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd3626ae-c8be-4ad9-8024-6a0a432cc0c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: ISA 44:1
Text: Yet now hear, O Jacob my servant; and Israel, whom I have chosen:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8f65d76-6513-40f0-a5e3-b52c20ec3b16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: ISA 44:2
Text: Thus saith the LORD that made thee, and formed thee from the womb, which will help thee; Fear not, O Jacob, my servant; and thou, Jesurun, whom I have chosen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1353ed0c-2e93-4f5f-a0f3-cdcd6035d953>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: ISA 44:3
Text: For I will pour water upon him that is thirsty, and floods upon the dry ground: I will pour my spirit upon thy seed, and my blessing upon thine offspring:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfb6e517-0fc5-494f-8d27-ef6bf7ae9eca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: ISA 44:4
Text: And they shall spring up as among the grass, as willows by the water courses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b86df7f3-4b7a-4294-924a-b3edf5c2d159>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: ISA 44:5
Text: One shall say, I am the LORD’s; and another shall call himself by the name of Jacob; and another shall subscribe with his hand unto the LORD, and surname himself by the name of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5081c330-d328-42ac-bace-a0f832e7da6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: ISA 44:6
Text: Thus saith the LORD the King of Israel, and his redeemer the LORD of hosts; I am the first, and I am the last; and beside me there is no God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5951768a-582e-4eea-b32d-dbe4c2a5d6cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: ISA 44:7
Text: And who, as I, shall call, and shall declare it, and set it in order for me, since I appointed the ancient people? and the things that are coming, and shall come, let them shew unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70b075bd-d3ea-460a-96e1-965af85ce6d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: ISA 44:8
Text: Fear ye not, neither be afraid: have not I told thee from that time, and have declared it? ye are even my witnesses. Is there a God beside me? yea, there is no God; I know not any.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4d8be06-ad70-47ed-85cf-912b9ce244d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: ISA 44:9
Text: They that make a graven image are all of them vanity; and their delectable things shall not profit; and they are their own witnesses; they see not, nor know; that they may be ashamed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7146ac0-9dc9-4ad0-a568-a083e09717b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: ISA 44:10
Text: Who hath formed a god, or molten a graven image that is profitable for nothing?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72a296af-3887-4266-af25-364f6f94d321>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: ISA 44:11
Text: Behold, all his fellows shall be ashamed: and the workmen, they are of men: let them all be gathered together, let them stand up; yet they shall fear, and they shall be ashamed together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b76a73a1-9c21-4fd8-b91b-b1b704e9436e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: ISA 44:12
Text: The smith with the tongs both worketh in the coals, and fashioneth it with hammers, and worketh it with the strength of his arms: yea, he is hungry, and his strength faileth: he drinketh no water, and is faint.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e70e3c53-a103-46b7-8298-864e2a91c324>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: ISA 44:13
Text: The carpenter stretcheth out his rule; he marketh it out with a line; he fitteth it with planes, and he marketh it out with the compass, and maketh it after the figure of a man, according to the beauty of a man; that it may remain in the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5fa2fe87-a2cd-4d50-9a8c-7da0faf78934>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: ISA 44:14
Text: He heweth him down cedars, and taketh the cypress and the oak, which he strengtheneth for himself among the trees of the forest: he planteth an ash, and the rain doth nourish it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc2850c4-9924-46f7-97e1-3f529887df70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: ISA 44:15
Text: Then shall it be for a man to burn: for he will take thereof, and warm himself; yea, he kindleth it, and baketh bread; yea, he maketh a god, and worshippeth it; he maketh it a graven image, and falleth down thereto.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23f84a70-e82d-417d-a7d6-9827ddf99a00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: ISA 44:16
Text: He burneth part thereof in the fire; with part thereof he eateth flesh; he roasteth roast, and is satisfied: yea, he warmeth himself, and saith, Aha, I am warm, I have seen the fire:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1baa1fa1-479c-4ece-abe5-145f9b36b4dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: ISA 44:17
Text: And the residue thereof he maketh a god, even his graven image: he falleth down unto it, and worshippeth it, and prayeth unto it, and saith, Deliver me; for thou art my god.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4545dc34-0e05-4465-9264-19e1db6d9b5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: ISA 44:18
Text: They have not known nor understood: for he hath shut their eyes, that they cannot see; and their hearts, that they cannot understand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00ce2272-4988-4b64-a1b5-7955f548b4f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 337

Reference: ISA 44:19
Text: And none considereth in his heart, neither is there knowledge nor understanding to say, I have burned part of it in the fire; yea, also I have baked bread upon the coals thereof; I have roasted flesh, and eaten it: and shall I make the residue thereof an abomination? shall I fall down to the stock of a tree?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a79c2af-c002-48c6-975c-5d5165f4c07a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: ISA 44:20
Text: He feedeth on ashes: a deceived heart hath turned him aside, that he cannot deliver his soul, nor say, Is there not a lie in my right hand?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:deb23f5b-a4a3-45a7-a26c-36899c99903b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: ISA 44:21
Text: Remember these, O Jacob and Israel; for thou art my servant: I have formed thee; thou art my servant: O Israel, thou shalt not be forgotten of me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bcb68f2b-c89f-48cf-b135-8f8dc3d8d056>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: ISA 44:22
Text: I have blotted out, as a thick cloud, thy transgressions, and, as a cloud, thy sins: return unto me; for I have redeemed thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fdecab40-b6d3-4733-8c3f-63996adbff0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: ISA 44:23
Text: Sing, O ye heavens; for the LORD hath done it: shout, ye lower parts of the earth: break forth into singing, ye mountains, O forest, and every tree therein: for the LORD hath redeemed Jacob, and glorified himself in Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b2b0b1c-171e-4a87-ac55-dc49d174980e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: ISA 44:24
Text: Thus saith the LORD, thy redeemer, and he that formed thee from the womb, I am the LORD that maketh all things; that stretcheth forth the heavens alone; that spreadeth abroad the earth by myself;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:091316b2-4816-4251-9c49-32a539bc6d63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: ISA 44:25
Text: That frustrateth the tokens of the liars, and maketh diviners mad; that turneth wise men backward, and maketh their knowledge foolish;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7065ee7a-5c25-4e77-8260-64f027a75cca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: ISA 44:26
Text: That confirmeth the word of his servant, and performeth the counsel of his messengers; that saith to Jerusalem, Thou shalt be inhabited; and to the cities of Judah, Ye shall be built, and I will raise up the decayed places thereof:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d091bfe5-34f6-4493-9b54-c0a5025a2f91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: ISA 44:27
Text: That saith to the deep, Be dry, and I will dry up thy rivers:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/44/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d16e732-9df2-4b53-89c3-ad9a2d43edb6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: ISA 44:28
Text: That saith of Cyrus, He is my shepherd, and shall perform all my pleasure: even saying to Jerusalem, Thou shalt be built; and to the temple, Thy foundation shall be laid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e5f47c4-edcf-4724-8958-b4fd7d7a5ae4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: ISA 45:1
Text: Thus saith the LORD to his anointed, to Cyrus, whose right hand I have holden, to subdue nations before him; and I will loose the loins of kings, to open before him the two leaved gates; and the gates shall not be shut;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a78197f9-0ec3-43a8-aa84-30254f7fb20f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: ISA 45:2
Text: I will go before thee, and make the crooked places straight: I will break in pieces the gates of brass, and cut in sunder the bars of iron:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5fc5a59c-3ae8-4ee8-aa7a-62d2473ad34e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: ISA 45:3
Text: And I will give thee the treasures of darkness, and hidden riches of secret places, that thou mayest know that I, the LORD, which call thee by thy name, am the God of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e378758f-b9ee-44bd-a632-72e851fd8569>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: ISA 45:4
Text: For Jacob my servant’s sake, and Israel mine elect, I have even called thee by thy name: I have surnamed thee, though thou hast not known me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44954f1d-a39d-43e4-afdb-9d6d0e01e379>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: ISA 45:5
Text: I am the LORD, and there is none else, there is no God beside me: I girded thee, though thou hast not known me:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e097918-870f-424e-97b7-2efc6d477f11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: ISA 45:6
Text: That they may know from the rising of the sun, and from the west, that there is none beside me. I am the LORD, and there is none else.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cc601b9-3fb1-497a-b8a6-2b0dd2c36330>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: ISA 45:7
Text: I form the light, and create darkness: I make peace, and create evil: I the LORD do all these things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08f13f6f-d199-42c4-a3a8-169d5cf7dd66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: ISA 45:8
Text: Drop down, ye heavens, from above, and let the skies pour down righteousness: let the earth open, and let them bring forth salvation, and let righteousness spring up together; I the LORD have created it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c74e9b3a-fca9-49ed-b788-d727f74ec3ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: ISA 45:9
Text: Woe unto him that striveth with his Maker! Let the potsherd strive with the potsherds of the earth. Shall the clay say to him that fashioneth it, What makest thou? or thy work, He hath no hands?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b433e089-8afb-4b77-bc17-a4aee527988c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: ISA 45:10
Text: Woe unto him that saith unto his father, What begettest thou? or to the woman, What hast thou brought forth?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e251acf-d079-4042-b628-d6c95f35c688>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: ISA 45:11
Text: Thus saith the LORD, the Holy One of Israel, and his Maker, Ask me of things to come concerning my sons, and concerning the work of my hands command ye me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07a71a5c-4178-4354-b044-15b291ad8280>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: ISA 45:12
Text: I have made the earth, and created man upon it: I, even my hands, have stretched out the heavens, and all their host have I commanded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50fd40ce-ae84-4a27-b421-b6966d37e6d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: ISA 45:13
Text: I have raised him up in righteousness, and I will direct all his ways: he shall build my city, and he shall let go my captives, not for price nor reward, saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0241597c-8749-467e-abc4-cadba37fea35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 393

Reference: ISA 45:14
Text: Thus saith the LORD, The labour of Egypt, and merchandise of Ethiopia and of the Sabeans, men of stature, shall come over unto thee, and they shall be thine: they shall come after thee; in chains they shall come over, and they shall fall down unto thee, they shall make supplication unto thee, saying, Surely God is in thee; and there is none else, there is no God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aee1a7c4-9e11-4b57-8d4e-1ee0c6da418c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: ISA 45:15
Text: Verily thou art a God that hidest thyself, O God of Israel, the Saviour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5ca84cb-6475-4c5c-937f-0030d77c82ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: ISA 45:16
Text: They shall be ashamed, and also confounded, all of them: they shall go to confusion together that are makers of idols.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e0910f6-e10b-4c08-bbdd-63b420598838>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: ISA 45:17
Text: But Israel shall be saved in the LORD with an everlasting salvation: ye shall not be ashamed nor confounded world without end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1760a1b1-cf85-48ab-9e98-e4908973bc20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: ISA 45:18
Text: For thus saith the LORD that created the heavens; God himself that formed the earth and made it; he hath established it, he created it not in vain, he formed it to be inhabited: I am the LORD; and there is none else.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c246e7b2-2b73-4d58-b838-29b9cbdfb73c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: ISA 45:19
Text: I have not spoken in secret, in a dark place of the earth: I said not unto the seed of Jacob, Seek ye me in vain: I the LORD speak righteousness, I declare things that are right.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85adbe04-da39-43da-92f3-8532971c2b07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: ISA 45:20
Text: Assemble yourselves and come; draw near together, ye that are escaped of the nations: they have no knowledge that set up the wood of their graven image, and pray unto a god that cannot save.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42062df5-3efc-45ce-85b8-1768f2a678b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 277

Reference: ISA 45:21
Text: Tell ye, and bring them near; yea, let them take counsel together: who hath declared this from ancient time? who hath told it from that time? have not I the LORD? and there is no God else beside me; a just God and a Saviour; there is none beside me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0e7dc77-eb76-45de-a3ef-21695a4fbd10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: ISA 45:22
Text: Look unto me, and be ye saved, all the ends of the earth: for I am God, and there is none else.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:453ec5ab-ce28-453e-9b77-74a436f93d0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: ISA 45:23
Text: I have sworn by myself, the word is gone out of my mouth in righteousness, and shall not return, That unto me every knee shall bow, every tongue shall swear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ad81cb9-552d-4575-9ade-3ed2b203db5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: ISA 45:24
Text: Surely, shall one say, in the LORD have I righteousness and strength: even to him shall men come; and all that are incensed against him shall be ashamed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/45/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6990acba-150a-4a1c-ba17-d2a6cd65ff20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: ISA 45:25
Text: In the LORD shall all the seed of Israel be justified, and shall glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/46/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fb79b2e-aab2-4ff5-adfc-901a9c841688>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: ISA 46:1
Text: Bel boweth down, Nebo stoopeth, their idols were upon the beasts, and upon the cattle: your carriages were heavy loaden; they are a burden to the weary beast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/46/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1137766d-c88e-408f-8423-e97bb9801111>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: ISA 46:2
Text: They stoop, they bow down together; they could not deliver the burden, but themselves are gone into captivity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/46/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:667f4444-d1fb-429b-b6dd-247973d532b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: ISA 46:3
Text: Hearken unto me, O house of Jacob, and all the remnant of the house of Israel, which are borne by me from the belly, which are carried from the womb:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/46/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2efd428e-75de-42fe-8fdd-985f62d7e18c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: ISA 46:4
Text: And even to your old age I am he; and even to hoar hairs will I carry you: I have made, and I will bear; even I will carry, and will deliver you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/46/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03cdde4f-97ca-4c6c-983c-306807109e17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: ISA 46:5
Text: To whom will ye liken me, and make me equal, and compare me, that we may be like?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/46/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91c65efb-5a8a-4aba-93fc-f84cf231b522>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: ISA 46:6
Text: They lavish gold out of the bag, and weigh silver in the balance, and hire a goldsmith; and he maketh it a god: they fall down, yea, they worship.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/46/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd3ae40d-da06-410a-af06-ee991fc3be07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: ISA 46:7
Text: They bear him upon the shoulder, they carry him, and set him in his place, and he standeth; from his place shall he not remove: yea, one shall cry unto him, yet can he not answer, nor save him out of his trouble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/46/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7819d7a9-e91b-4f11-9b80-998c7faf2c57>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: ISA 46:8
Text: Remember this, and shew yourselves men: bring it again to mind, O ye transgressors.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/46/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f49ca677-1d81-4203-b59b-2872dbf2350e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: ISA 46:9
Text: Remember the former things of old: for I am God, and there is none else; I am God, and there is none like me,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/46/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:680d6ae4-700c-4bf5-a13d-1fffbab40858>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: ISA 46:10
Text: Declaring the end from the beginning, and from ancient times the things that are not yet done, saying, My counsel shall stand, and I will do all my pleasure:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/46/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c1523e0-6ee0-4200-9999-293105c299f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: ISA 46:11
Text: Calling a ravenous bird from the east, the man that executeth my counsel from a far country: yea, I have spoken it, I will also bring it to pass; I have purposed it, I will also do it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/46/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c91d02e-598d-4a33-9966-15c9bf908023>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: ISA 46:12
Text: Hearken unto me, ye stouthearted, that are far from righteousness:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/46/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc63de18-597e-4780-9864-a10062d3fc41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: ISA 46:13
Text: I bring near my righteousness; it shall not be far off, and my salvation shall not tarry: and I will place salvation in Zion for Israel my glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/47/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6576b779-6769-47ab-8407-6f8721f66684>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: ISA 47:1
Text: Come down, and sit in the dust, O virgin daughter of Babylon, sit on the ground: there is no throne, O daughter of the Chaldeans: for thou shalt no more be called tender and delicate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/47/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5042ef95-3565-4293-9124-cf8fd59c1d97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: ISA 47:2
Text: Take the millstones, and grind meal: uncover thy locks, make bare the leg, uncover the thigh, pass over the rivers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/47/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f68e7acb-c484-4e0c-8f2c-6e1eceaa3124>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: ISA 47:3
Text: Thy nakedness shall be uncovered, yea, thy shame shall be seen: I will take vengeance, and I will not meet thee as a man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/47/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03910dcc-c216-483e-8d9d-b5b269e37e78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: ISA 47:4
Text: As for our redeemer, the LORD of hosts is his name, the Holy One of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/47/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d22256c9-96c7-4752-a783-b9137dc1a604>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: ISA 47:5
Text: Sit thou silent, and get thee into darkness, O daughter of the Chaldeans: for thou shalt no more be called, The lady of kingdoms.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/47/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4432be7b-2a99-419d-ae43-e8cd31f8db8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: ISA 47:6
Text: I was wroth with my people, I have polluted mine inheritance, and given them into thine hand: thou didst shew them no mercy; upon the ancient hast thou very heavily laid thy yoke.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/47/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7da4ad0d-8e40-4a39-9244-e2b36ceff7c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: ISA 47:7
Text: And thou saidst, I shall be a lady for ever: so that thou didst not lay these things to thy heart, neither didst remember the latter end of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/47/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71838990-b0d6-4889-ba03-46060eb7b926>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: ISA 47:8
Text: Therefore hear now this, thou that art given to pleasures, that dwellest carelessly, that sayest in thine heart, I am, and none else beside me; I shall not sit as a widow, neither shall I know the loss of children:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/47/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42d03215-bafb-4859-b428-228ed224b5ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: ISA 47:9
Text: But these two things shall come to thee in a moment in one day, the loss of children, and widowhood: they shall come upon thee in their perfection for the multitude of thy sorceries, and for the great abundance of thine enchantments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/47/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f47c51ad-7f1b-406d-8d68-7457db86fa53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: ISA 47:10
Text: For thou hast trusted in thy wickedness: thou hast said, None seeth me. Thy wisdom and thy knowledge, it hath perverted thee; and thou hast said in thine heart, I am, and none else beside me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/47/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f540a990-8756-4fff-9ce7-52ffbda8ecb5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: ISA 47:11
Text: Therefore shall evil come upon thee; thou shalt not know from whence it riseth: and mischief shall fall upon thee; thou shalt not be able to put it off: and desolation shall come upon thee suddenly, which thou shalt not know.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/47/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a18ef82-60a2-46e3-8df0-b490481420ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: ISA 47:12
Text: Stand now with thine enchantments, and with the multitude of thy sorceries, wherein thou hast laboured from thy youth; if so be thou shalt be able to profit, if so be thou mayest prevail.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/47/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0be798eb-6c51-4dd5-be02-2f558696db6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: ISA 47:13
Text: Thou art wearied in the multitude of thy counsels. Let now the astrologers, the stargazers, the monthly prognosticators, stand up, and save thee from these things that shall come upon thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/47/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1eb11aa1-c30b-493c-9a31-713056e6b03d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: ISA 47:14
Text: Behold, they shall be as stubble; the fire shall burn them; they shall not deliver themselves from the power of the flame: there shall not be a coal to warm at, nor fire to sit before it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/47/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3efa86de-c930-4364-a19a-956b712fc05c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: ISA 47:15
Text: Thus shall they be unto thee with whom thou hast laboured, even thy merchants, from thy youth: they shall wander every one to his quarter; none shall save thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/48/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d83a9946-1691-4881-880e-5917dd6cc662>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: ISA 48:1
Text: Hear ye this, O house of Jacob, which are called by the name of Israel, and are come forth out of the waters of Judah, which swear by the name of the LORD, and make mention of the God of Israel, but not in truth, nor in righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/48/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:360805ae-fe5b-4ac0-96df-428463b4dcf1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: ISA 48:2
Text: For they call themselves of the holy city, and stay themselves upon the God of Israel; The LORD of hosts is his name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/48/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23151071-8558-441c-aa77-f3c75a3ef632>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: ISA 48:3
Text: I have declared the former things from the beginning; and they went forth out of my mouth, and I shewed them; I did them suddenly, and they came to pass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/48/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fc90577-4339-4262-be9a-d6dbb1b1eca3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: ISA 48:4
Text: Because I knew that thou art obstinate, and thy neck is an iron sinew, and thy brow brass;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/48/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f046597-bdd0-4a42-a598-6b37300a0de0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: ISA 48:5
Text: I have even from the beginning declared it to thee; before it came to pass I shewed it thee: lest thou shouldest say, Mine idol hath done them, and my graven image, and my molten image, hath commanded them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/48/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ac23b26-5d90-4704-abfe-3953539e3304>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: ISA 48:6
Text: Thou hast heard, see all this; and will not ye declare it? I have shewed thee new things from this time, even hidden things, and thou didst not know them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/48/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7d61a14-be56-4888-aae5-9fdd44636468>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: ISA 48:7
Text: They are created now, and not from the beginning; even before the day when thou heardest them not; lest thou shouldest say, Behold, I knew them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/48/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0bb1f41-34f8-4185-9ada-cdb26ef85f1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: ISA 48:8
Text: Yea, thou heardest not; yea, thou knewest not; yea, from that time that thine ear was not opened: for I knew that thou wouldest deal very treacherously, and wast called a transgressor from the womb.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/48/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c67eaeda-19a8-4de1-b485-a704751bdf24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: ISA 48:9
Text: For my name’s sake will I defer mine anger, and for my praise will I refrain for thee, that I cut thee not off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/48/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8b86883-90ac-4d06-8e59-a4c72cfa9a22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: ISA 48:10
Text: Behold, I have refined thee, but not with silver; I have chosen thee in the furnace of affliction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/48/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a0d2e17-c85f-4936-911e-e4d8abb5a50d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: ISA 48:11
Text: For mine own sake, even for mine own sake, will I do it: for how should my name be polluted? and I will not give my glory unto another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/48/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc6c697a-3187-4626-9307-210dbc18b675>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: ISA 48:12
Text: Hearken unto me, O Jacob and Israel, my called; I am he; I am the first, I also am the last.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/48/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bd0b1a4-9651-48e8-8943-10e7ee1c5a20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: ISA 48:13
Text: Mine hand also hath laid the foundation of the earth, and my right hand hath spanned the heavens: when I call unto them, they stand up together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/48/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db6df429-c799-4af0-9368-d78f619e19f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: ISA 48:14
Text: All ye, assemble yourselves, and hear; which among them hath declared these things? The LORD hath loved him: he will do his pleasure on Babylon, and his arm shall be on the Chaldeans.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/48/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86baa086-bbc1-4a64-9167-020e1e8fd3c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: ISA 48:15
Text: I, even I, have spoken; yea, I have called him: I have brought him, and he shall make his way prosperous.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/48/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03375625-c7ab-42ca-b29c-2258c2213c1e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: ISA 48:16
Text: Come ye near unto me, hear ye this; I have not spoken in secret from the beginning; from the time that it was, there am I: and now the Lord GOD, and his Spirit, hath sent me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/48/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f46eae85-259f-4e7e-9b69-bd934d973767>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: ISA 48:17
Text: Thus saith the LORD, thy Redeemer, the Holy One of Israel; I am the LORD thy God which teacheth thee to profit, which leadeth thee by the way that thou shouldest go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/48/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e0580bc-2ee8-473b-9c80-8fbf52b939fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: ISA 48:18
Text: O that thou hadst hearkened to my commandments! then had thy peace been as a river, and thy righteousness as the waves of the sea:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/48/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f8a0767-aa11-496c-8013-69f2b75c6530>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: ISA 48:19
Text: Thy seed also had been as the sand, and the offspring of thy bowels like the gravel thereof; his name should not have been cut off nor destroyed from before me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/48/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d728c613-2747-4416-bbe1-53f58a0d7d14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: ISA 48:20
Text: Go ye forth of Babylon, flee ye from the Chaldeans, with a voice of singing declare ye, tell this, utter it even to the end of the earth; say ye, The LORD hath redeemed his servant Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/48/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:714e4b3e-c313-490f-9577-a285a7f7dbd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: ISA 48:21
Text: And they thirsted not when he led them through the deserts: he caused the waters to flow out of the rock for them: he clave the rock also, and the waters gushed out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/48/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14d7920f-cbd3-4f00-a830-8a2cab45f093>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: ISA 48:22
Text: There is no peace, saith the LORD, unto the wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7ea8265-15f3-4674-8ac1-6f6b9ef3e8b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: ISA 49:1
Text: Listen, O isles, unto me; and hearken, ye people, from far; The LORD hath called me from the womb; from the bowels of my mother hath he made mention of my name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fa8daf4-c6f2-4476-9e45-04d9d74f0c08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: ISA 49:2
Text: And he hath made my mouth like a sharp sword; in the shadow of his hand hath he hid me, and made me a polished shaft; in his quiver hath he hid me;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46a31c98-dd00-4bd6-a03c-0190dfc1948a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: ISA 49:3
Text: And said unto me, Thou art my servant, O Israel, in whom I will be glorified.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52e8a9d9-d0a0-405d-9fa5-1026695d5478>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: ISA 49:4
Text: Then I said, I have laboured in vain, I have spent my strength for nought, and in vain: yet surely my judgment is with the LORD, and my work with my God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d12946e-0125-4160-82a4-1c082273ff9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: ISA 49:5
Text: And now, saith the LORD that formed me from the womb to be his servant, to bring Jacob again to him, Though Israel be not gathered, yet shall I be glorious in the eyes of the LORD, and my God shall be my strength.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f4dda41-8cc4-4c15-b0a5-777c943d2961>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 277

Reference: ISA 49:6
Text: And he said, It is a light thing that thou shouldest be my servant to raise up the tribes of Jacob, and to restore the preserved of Israel: I will also give thee for a light to the Gentiles, that thou mayest be my salvation unto the end of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:130787f3-a23a-4b54-b08d-b841dee075f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 321

Reference: ISA 49:7
Text: Thus saith the LORD, the Redeemer of Israel, and his Holy One, to him whom man despiseth, to him whom the nation abhorreth, to a servant of rulers, Kings shall see and arise, princes also shall worship, because of the LORD that is faithful, and the Holy One of Israel, and he shall choose thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01aa9be7-7605-48f7-87fc-f7bfdc2f757c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: ISA 49:8
Text: Thus saith the LORD, In an acceptable time have I heard thee, and in a day of salvation have I helped thee: and I will preserve thee, and give thee for a covenant of the people, to establish the earth, to cause to inherit the desolate heritages;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8c27396-65b9-4d7e-91dc-7dada00f4490>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: ISA 49:9
Text: That thou mayest say to the prisoners, Go forth; to them that are in darkness, Shew yourselves. They shall feed in the ways, and their pastures shall be in all high places.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95f593d9-17f0-420a-a7a7-6e6b7b97479a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: ISA 49:10
Text: They shall not hunger nor thirst; neither shall the heat nor sun smite them: for he that hath mercy on them shall lead them, even by the springs of water shall he guide them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57da8b01-7eb9-4b48-b85b-ca091d0aa7fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: ISA 49:11
Text: And I will make all my mountains a way, and my highways shall be exalted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e59a6b04-76a1-48de-94aa-d5ff42205d42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: ISA 49:12
Text: Behold, these shall come from far: and, lo, these from the north and from the west; and these from the land of Sinim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b6894da-2260-435a-90d2-9e470cf37055>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: ISA 49:13
Text: Sing, O heavens; and be joyful, O earth; and break forth into singing, O mountains: for the LORD hath comforted his people, and will have mercy upon his afflicted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:793428bd-2f82-4da0-98cc-97daa1f17f38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: ISA 49:14
Text: But Zion said, The LORD hath forsaken me, and my Lord hath forgotten me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97b732d9-3cdd-4072-a844-5caf047f50ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: ISA 49:15
Text: Can a woman forget her sucking child, that she should not have compassion on the son of her womb? yea, they may forget, yet will I not forget thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3df129ee-a6a1-4574-a4f0-66f36bb29a30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: ISA 49:16
Text: Behold, I have graven thee upon the palms of my hands; thy walls are continually before me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50c52a46-e9c6-42e6-9748-a02fb4e329c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: ISA 49:17
Text: Thy children shall make haste; thy destroyers and they that made thee waste shall go forth of thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96da2fe1-68bd-48e7-8a8d-874a45d6a894>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: ISA 49:18
Text: Lift up thine eyes round about, and behold: all these gather themselves together, and come to thee. As I live, saith the LORD, thou shalt surely clothe thee with them all, as with an ornament, and bind them on thee, as a bride doeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef98fbb4-1ca7-48da-83d7-56fc1121087b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: ISA 49:19
Text: For thy waste and thy desolate places, and the land of thy destruction, shall even now be too narrow by reason of the inhabitants, and they that swallowed thee up shall be far away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bfd9060-1e78-40ea-9856-4f58826bc3f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: ISA 49:20
Text: The children which thou shalt have, after thou hast lost the other, shall say again in thine ears, The place is too strait for me: give place to me that I may dwell.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:020aeec8-7e30-4875-987b-9b1a100ed06a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: ISA 49:21
Text: Then shalt thou say in thine heart, Who hath begotten me these, seeing I have lost my children, and am desolate, a captive, and removing to and fro? and who hath brought up these? Behold, I was left alone; these, where had they been?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4604d606-6e51-480c-bb4f-671c167e54d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: ISA 49:22
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD, Behold, I will lift up mine hand to the Gentiles, and set up my standard to the people: and they shall bring thy sons in their arms, and thy daughters shall be carried upon their shoulders.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f38b9ba-4a34-4ce0-a3f7-a26200241c10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 289

Reference: ISA 49:23
Text: And kings shall be thy nursing fathers, and their queens thy nursing mothers: they shall bow down to thee with their face toward the earth, and lick up the dust of thy feet; and thou shalt know that I am the LORD: for they shall not be ashamed that wait for me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f6008f2-a3ea-4218-baae-64379b8203f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: ISA 49:24
Text: Shall the prey be taken from the mighty, or the lawful captive delivered?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d227aaea-1d6e-4444-9774-5c2e162db0b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: ISA 49:25
Text: But thus saith the LORD, Even the captives of the mighty shall be taken away, and the prey of the terrible shall be delivered: for I will contend with him that contendeth with thee, and I will save thy children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/49/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:045b7256-0012-4624-9932-56c0c6a54ae2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: ISA 49:26
Text: And I will feed them that oppress thee with their own flesh; and they shall be drunken with their own blood, as with sweet wine: and all flesh shall know that I the LORD am thy Saviour and thy Redeemer, the mighty One of Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/50/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e631fcc-890e-44c4-922e-35216305f7e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 281

Reference: ISA 50:1
Text: Thus saith the LORD, Where is the bill of your mother’s divorcement, whom I have put away? or which of my creditors is it to whom I have sold you? Behold, for your iniquities have ye sold yourselves, and for your transgressions is your mother put away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/50/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85d796c9-09ff-4ad0-9708-be116cf082c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 333

Reference: ISA 50:2
Text: Wherefore, when I came, was there no man? when I called, was there none to answer? Is my hand shortened at all, that it cannot redeem? or have I no power to deliver? behold, at my rebuke I dry up the sea, I make the rivers a wilderness: their fish stinketh, because there is no water, and dieth for thirst.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/50/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58501a88-8f23-416b-a0a2-b9981bc81ef1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: ISA 50:3
Text: I clothe the heavens with blackness, and I make sackcloth their covering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/50/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afcfbce8-4a0f-4460-acf8-a42a98dec41c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: ISA 50:4
Text: The Lord GOD hath given me the tongue of the learned, that I should know how to speak a word in season to him that is weary: he wakeneth morning by morning, he wakeneth mine ear to hear as the learned.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/50/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97b24824-1191-484e-ae83-c0a7a194f3d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: ISA 50:5
Text: The Lord GOD hath opened mine ear, and I was not rebellious, neither turned away back.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/50/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2116463-4af3-441e-9539-0e5cd9061f87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: ISA 50:6
Text: I gave my back to the smiters, and my cheeks to them that plucked off the hair: I hid not my face from shame and spitting.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/50/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3260a07-8a7f-4e83-8485-fe24133cf5d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: ISA 50:7
Text: For the Lord GOD will help me; therefore shall I not be confounded: therefore have I set my face like a flint, and I know that I shall not be ashamed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/50/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3210da78-d9e5-4b68-a68c-c9296c8735c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: ISA 50:8
Text: He is near that justifieth me; who will contend with me? let us stand together: who is mine adversary? let him come near to me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/50/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6e4881f-38e0-47e3-9c82-8a1c35646412>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: ISA 50:9
Text: Behold, the Lord GOD will help me; who is he that shall condemn me? lo, they all shall wax old as a garment; the moth shall eat them up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/50/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fed93b5d-cb31-42ad-8639-18a7e954c0f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: ISA 50:10
Text: Who is among you that feareth the LORD, that obeyeth the voice of his servant, that walketh in darkness, and hath no light? let him trust in the name of the LORD, and stay upon his God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/50/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:596b4218-3cbb-4ccd-8648-df95e3b55cfb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: ISA 50:11
Text: Behold, all ye that kindle a fire, that compass yourselves about with sparks: walk in the light of your fire, and in the sparks that ye have kindled. This shall ye have of mine hand; ye shall lie down in sorrow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/51/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:406e5b27-b057-4578-8dee-ae6f235ee56a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: ISA 51:1
Text: Hearken to me, ye that follow after righteousness, ye that seek the LORD: look unto the rock whence ye are hewn, and to the hole of the pit whence ye are digged.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/51/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3e5dafa-c497-4407-a002-f5ed39cf7d54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: ISA 51:2
Text: Look unto Abraham your father, and unto Sarah that bare you: for I called him alone, and blessed him, and increased him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/51/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08e34cfe-78de-4624-b22a-68d7a54f9840>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: ISA 51:3
Text: For the LORD shall comfort Zion: he will comfort all her waste places; and he will make her wilderness like Eden, and her desert like the garden of the LORD; joy and gladness shall be found therein, thanksgiving, and the voice of melody.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/51/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92aad2ad-7c7f-4681-9156-cb2b62a7fef1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: ISA 51:4
Text: Hearken unto me, my people; and give ear unto me, O my nation: for a law shall proceed from me, and I will make my judgment to rest for a light of the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/51/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55e6b192-e6cf-4893-9f21-dc1894bf0fe5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: ISA 51:5
Text: My righteousness is near; my salvation is gone forth, and mine arms shall judge the people; the isles shall wait upon me, and on mine arm shall they trust.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/51/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bde4a147-7b8e-4867-a3a6-7413badc7f81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 318

Reference: ISA 51:6
Text: Lift up your eyes to the heavens, and look upon the earth beneath: for the heavens shall vanish away like smoke, and the earth shall wax old like a garment, and they that dwell therein shall die in like manner: but my salvation shall be for ever, and my righteousness shall not be abolished.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/51/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e0c88b0-7229-4694-9c23-087186fb1121>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: ISA 51:7
Text: Hearken unto me, ye that know righteousness, the people in whose heart is my law; fear ye not the reproach of men, neither be ye afraid of their revilings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/51/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd6af787-df7c-47c7-98f7-1ec589bb5643>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: ISA 51:8
Text: For the moth shall eat them up like a garment, and the worm shall eat them like wool: but my righteousness shall be for ever, and my salvation from generation to generation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/51/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:668909fa-7dd0-4e72-8310-b460c0382607>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: ISA 51:9
Text: Awake, awake, put on strength, O arm of the LORD; awake, as in the ancient days, in the generations of old. Art thou not it that hath cut Rahab, and wounded the dragon?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/51/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:796ce280-d9a4-48e8-88ff-89894bf5f2b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: ISA 51:10
Text: Art thou not it which hath dried the sea, the waters of the great deep; that hath made the depths of the sea a way for the ransomed to pass over?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/51/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff8230c5-f5d9-4818-a4e7-0995598085af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: ISA 51:11
Text: Therefore the redeemed of the LORD shall return, and come with singing unto Zion; and everlasting joy shall be upon their head: they shall obtain gladness and joy; and sorrow and mourning shall flee away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/51/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b159ecd9-b558-44fb-b9bb-3b908b367cd4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: ISA 51:12
Text: I, even I, am he that comforteth you: who art thou, that thou shouldest be afraid of a man that shall die, and of the son of man which shall be made as grass;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/51/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8047b560-b676-4f53-b6f8-2a3cf91386b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 288

Reference: ISA 51:13
Text: And forgettest the LORD thy maker, that hath stretched forth the heavens, and laid the foundations of the earth; and hast feared continually every day because of the fury of the oppressor, as if he were ready to destroy? and where is the fury of the oppressor?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/51/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d56cfd9a-fc7e-40c6-b794-59c1d93856b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: ISA 51:14
Text: The captive exile hasteneth that he may be loosed, and that he should not die in the pit, nor that his bread should fail.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/51/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e960615-7aae-4536-ba50-f442746350c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: ISA 51:15
Text: But I am the LORD thy God, that divided the sea, whose waves roared: The LORD of hosts is his name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/51/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0da8482-e308-466b-8eb7-d496e9ee4015>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: ISA 51:16
Text: And I have put my words in thy mouth, and I have covered thee in the shadow of mine hand, that I may plant the heavens, and lay the foundations of the earth, and say unto Zion, Thou art my people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/51/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d53232f9-a5a3-4a95-a64b-4b515aae2c3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: ISA 51:17
Text: Awake, awake, stand up, O Jerusalem, which hast drunk at the hand of the LORD the cup of his fury; thou hast drunken the dregs of the cup of trembling, and wrung them out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/51/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c89886d5-567d-4ea1-8a9e-adb2eab8a312>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: ISA 51:18
Text: There is none to guide her among all the sons whom she hath brought forth; neither is there any that taketh her by the hand of all the sons that she hath brought up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/51/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d60dfa0-2d1f-4eca-99d4-e9502871efc7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: ISA 51:19
Text: These two things are come unto thee; who shall be sorry for thee? desolation, and destruction, and the famine, and the sword: by whom shall I comfort thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/51/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2335d8dc-2b3e-48e7-ba14-8df873c92da0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: ISA 51:20
Text: Thy sons have fainted, they lie at the head of all the streets, as a wild bull in a net: they are full of the fury of the LORD, the rebuke of thy God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/51/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83ee4f37-1a40-4ac0-903f-c52faba1bd48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: ISA 51:21
Text: Therefore hear now this, thou afflicted, and drunken, but not with wine:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/51/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa5bc2b1-e579-4108-a7cb-68d7bed264be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: ISA 51:22
Text: Thus saith thy Lord the LORD, and thy God that pleadeth the cause of his people, Behold, I have taken out of thine hand the cup of trembling, even the dregs of the cup of my fury; thou shalt no more drink it again:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/51/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bacf63ac-f4e8-4b56-b0d8-f311fad0b77d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: ISA 51:23
Text: But I will put it into the hand of them that afflict thee; which have said to thy soul, Bow down, that we may go over: and thou hast laid thy body as the ground, and as the street, to them that went over.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/52/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53ec5992-8460-4d91-8ed6-569e2150c8b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: ISA 52:1
Text: Awake, awake; put on thy strength, O Zion; put on thy beautiful garments, O Jerusalem, the holy city: for henceforth there shall no more come into thee the uncircumcised and the unclean.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/52/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58ed9935-9854-485d-ad7f-c44f0061aafc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: ISA 52:2
Text: Shake thyself from the dust; arise, and sit down, O Jerusalem: loose thyself from the bands of thy neck, O captive daughter of Zion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/52/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64af15a4-153c-4949-be89-cc5ccd2c1867>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: ISA 52:3
Text: For thus saith the LORD, Ye have sold yourselves for nought; and ye shall be redeemed without money.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/52/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bfb8084-f6d0-43d1-aa00-c3f0a55c1a81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: ISA 52:4
Text: For thus saith the Lord GOD, My people went down aforetime into Egypt to sojourn there; and the Assyrian oppressed them without cause.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/52/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:416c2298-19e2-4417-b92d-48d3134bc829>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: ISA 52:5
Text: Now therefore, what have I here, saith the LORD, that my people is taken away for nought? they that rule over them make them to howl, saith the LORD; and my name continually every day is blasphemed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/52/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef79550c-bc96-46ee-9de7-83ff096ee37a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: ISA 52:6
Text: Therefore my people shall know my name: therefore they shall know in that day that I am he that doth speak: behold, it is I.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/52/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92ee2702-e2c8-4c7a-8a66-79064b118502>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: ISA 52:7
Text: How beautiful upon the mountains are the feet of him that bringeth good tidings, that publisheth peace; that bringeth good tidings of good, that publisheth salvation; that saith unto Zion, Thy God reigneth!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/52/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6fc8cdc3-9e91-4dfc-9597-6ad2fdd9fc42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: ISA 52:8
Text: Thy watchmen shall lift up the voice; with the voice together shall they sing: for they shall see eye to eye, when the LORD shall bring again Zion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/52/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23755dff-5b77-4d15-aa76-07b05b92387b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: ISA 52:9
Text: Break forth into joy, sing together, ye waste places of Jerusalem: for the LORD hath comforted his people, he hath redeemed Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/52/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:690bfcd8-7571-4591-b81b-0ec01be544bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: ISA 52:10
Text: The LORD hath made bare his holy arm in the eyes of all the nations; and all the ends of the earth shall see the salvation of our God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/52/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec0f97d7-7195-43f0-99d9-d8b8e2a34509>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: ISA 52:11
Text: Depart ye, depart ye, go ye out from thence, touch no unclean thing; go ye out of the midst of her; be ye clean, that bear the vessels of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/52/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c925789-ba08-4030-bae9-5dd6f3016372>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: ISA 52:12
Text: For ye shall not go out with haste, nor go by flight: for the LORD will go before you; and the God of Israel will be your rereward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/52/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5910273f-75a0-40d3-92c8-a082e422d120>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: ISA 52:13
Text: Behold, my servant shall deal prudently, he shall be exalted and extolled, and be very high.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/52/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5646efb0-b7fe-432b-8ac0-d457cc159811>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: ISA 52:14
Text: As many were astonied at thee; his visage was so marred more than any man, and his form more than the sons of men:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/52/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17e1ea7c-5309-4642-ad6b-779b16cc789a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: ISA 52:15
Text: So shall he sprinkle many nations; the kings shall shut their mouths at him: for that which had not been told them shall they see; and that which they had not heard shall they consider.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/53/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e3fdec7-a3aa-4340-b623-bd7a1506be29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: ISA 53:1
Text: Who hath believed our report? and to whom is the arm of the LORD revealed?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/53/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d63ad328-baa7-46cc-a154-7e6bda942756>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: ISA 53:2
Text: For he shall grow up before him as a tender plant, and as a root out of a dry ground: he hath no form nor comeliness; and when we shall see him, there is no beauty that we should desire him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/53/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8368ecd-d527-4ef6-9ab1-b21191d7ff74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: ISA 53:3
Text: He is despised and rejected of men; a man of sorrows, and acquainted with grief: and we hid as it were our faces from him; he was despised, and we esteemed him not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/53/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b0851e5-1df6-4c31-93d2-32cf87ad26e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: ISA 53:4
Text: Surely he hath borne our griefs, and carried our sorrows: yet we did esteem him stricken, smitten of God, and afflicted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/53/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28ec85ed-27a1-4d93-a67d-895bac19e8ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: ISA 53:5
Text: But he was wounded for our transgressions, he was bruised for our iniquities: the chastisement of our peace was upon him; and with his stripes we are healed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/53/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:744a2fb6-c907-43ce-a0f8-f552a55f5ab1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: ISA 53:6
Text: All we like sheep have gone astray; we have turned every one to his own way; and the LORD hath laid on him the iniquity of us all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/53/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89b15d20-1007-44ee-9bb7-24b410bf51e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: ISA 53:7
Text: He was oppressed, and he was afflicted, yet he opened not his mouth: he is brought as a lamb to the slaughter, and as a sheep before her shearers is dumb, so he openeth not his mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/53/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2d772a2-1476-4eb7-b641-9ae37e37b619>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: ISA 53:8
Text: He was taken from prison and from judgment: and who shall declare his generation? for he was cut off out of the land of the living: for the transgression of my people was he stricken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/53/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4c2ab9c-a6bb-451a-80e2-a29aafb78612>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: ISA 53:9
Text: And he made his grave with the wicked, and with the rich in his death; because he had done no violence, neither was any deceit in his mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/53/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5629bcf-ac9c-4caf-841b-cf8c9563d306>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: ISA 53:10
Text: Yet it pleased the LORD to bruise him; he hath put him to grief: when thou shalt make his soul an offering for sin, he shall see his seed, he shall prolong his days, and the pleasure of the LORD shall prosper in his hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/53/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:736476d0-7099-4a87-a273-4b044ac55165>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: ISA 53:11
Text: He shall see of the travail of his soul, and shall be satisfied: by his knowledge shall my righteous servant justify many; for he shall bear their iniquities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/53/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6fc3a1ba-e2fb-407e-a9ac-673e99b9ff29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 294

Reference: ISA 53:12
Text: Therefore will I divide him a portion with the great, and he shall divide the spoil with the strong; because he hath poured out his soul unto death: and he was numbered with the transgressors; and he bare the sin of many, and made intercession for the transgressors.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/54/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ef7ede1-88f4-4c3a-ae0d-6959cf42ad2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: ISA 54:1
Text: Sing, O barren, thou that didst not bear; break forth into singing, and cry aloud, thou that didst not travail with child: for more are the children of the desolate than the children of the married wife, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/54/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca40d30b-82c6-48ee-a71d-59ae00e02478>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: ISA 54:2
Text: Enlarge the place of thy tent, and let them stretch forth the curtains of thine habitations: spare not, lengthen thy cords, and strengthen thy stakes;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/54/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04cdc5d8-fe55-495b-ba6b-8b8ed4c650f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: ISA 54:3
Text: For thou shalt break forth on the right hand and on the left; and thy seed shall inherit the Gentiles, and make the desolate cities to be inhabited.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/54/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:098c36f3-79b1-4e60-bbff-afc8c28ef0ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: ISA 54:4
Text: Fear not; for thou shalt not be ashamed: neither be thou confounded; for thou shalt not be put to shame: for thou shalt forget the shame of thy youth, and shalt not remember the reproach of thy widowhood any more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/54/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3fb0d19f-8f57-4c96-996d-e8f0e256b7b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: ISA 54:5
Text: For thy Maker is thine husband; the LORD of hosts is his name; and thy Redeemer the Holy One of Israel; The God of the whole earth shall he be called.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/54/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33de0210-7ea3-40be-aa5a-39d531a0ece8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: ISA 54:6
Text: For the LORD hath called thee as a woman forsaken and grieved in spirit, and a wife of youth, when thou wast refused, saith thy God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/54/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:906e6edf-6302-4d19-ad4d-4a5ab6dc33ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: ISA 54:7
Text: For a small moment have I forsaken thee; but with great mercies will I gather thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/54/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a79ce035-a70f-44d2-a8db-a4c13732057f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: ISA 54:8
Text: In a little wrath I hid my face from thee for a moment; but with everlasting kindness will I have mercy on thee, saith the LORD thy Redeemer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/54/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2ae6872-a37c-44cc-829b-1546d071f7b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: ISA 54:9
Text: For this is as the waters of Noah unto me: for as I have sworn that the waters of Noah should no more go over the earth; so have I sworn that I would not be wroth with thee, nor rebuke thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/54/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41dab683-a6a8-49ad-9818-56b6eebd8348>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: ISA 54:10
Text: For the mountains shall depart, and the hills be removed; but my kindness shall not depart from thee, neither shall the covenant of my peace be removed, saith the LORD that hath mercy on thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/54/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92df707b-993e-4648-83b0-18e4e37b8d41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: ISA 54:11
Text: O thou afflicted, tossed with tempest, and not comforted, behold, I will lay thy stones with fair colours, and lay thy foundations with sapphires.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/54/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41282e13-5479-420d-9205-552624469510>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: ISA 54:12
Text: And I will make thy windows of agates, and thy gates of carbuncles, and all thy borders of pleasant stones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/54/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c921508a-896d-4b18-9460-d00461cb9fe0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: ISA 54:13
Text: And all thy children shall be taught of the LORD; and great shall be the peace of thy children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/54/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f11f1980-70fb-4e25-a2c8-17ca7385ba43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: ISA 54:14
Text: In righteousness shalt thou be established: thou shalt be far from oppression; for thou shalt not fear: and from terror; for it shall not come near thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/54/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e1013cf-78cd-4670-9232-712b70570062>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: ISA 54:15
Text: Behold, they shall surely gather together, but not by me: whosoever shall gather together against thee shall fall for thy sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/54/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f1dd224-d621-4785-a36f-c73af7e4f1d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: ISA 54:16
Text: Behold, I have created the smith that bloweth the coals in the fire, and that bringeth forth an instrument for his work; and I have created the waster to destroy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/54/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c61a750-032f-4d2a-a7f2-04bd182edb26>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: ISA 54:17
Text: No weapon that is formed against thee shall prosper; and every tongue that shall rise against thee in judgment thou shalt condemn. This is the heritage of the servants of the LORD, and their righteousness is of me, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/55/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26b790bf-f28b-44a5-a247-a435e343b6f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: ISA 55:1
Text: Ho, every one that thirsteth, come ye to the waters, and he that hath no money; come ye, buy, and eat; yea, come, buy wine and milk without money and without price.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/55/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b203c8a-db13-4ef9-8e3f-fea9c0b90931>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: ISA 55:2
Text: Wherefore do ye spend money for that which is not bread? and your labour for that which satisfieth not? hearken diligently unto me, and eat ye that which is good, and let your soul delight itself in fatness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/55/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1de54caa-909b-4ce5-bb96-19bbbbdd119d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: ISA 55:3
Text: Incline your ear, and come unto me: hear, and your soul shall live; and I will make an everlasting covenant with you, even the sure mercies of David.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/55/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:013d4fac-36ec-4869-b6b8-b18d8583f4ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: ISA 55:4
Text: Behold, I have given him for a witness to the people, a leader and commander to the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/55/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4853886-08e2-4829-b986-a6c53986f2bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: ISA 55:5
Text: Behold, thou shalt call a nation that thou knowest not, and nations that knew not thee shall run unto thee because of the LORD thy God, and for the Holy One of Israel; for he hath glorified thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/55/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4c5a318-fe65-4f59-a5b6-d43821893ab4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: ISA 55:6
Text: Seek ye the LORD while he may be found, call ye upon him while he is near:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/55/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea709e0a-e1e4-4cb9-9d6c-a038bc1487fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: ISA 55:7
Text: Let the wicked forsake his way, and the unrighteous man his thoughts: and let him return unto the LORD, and he will have mercy upon him; and to our God, for he will abundantly pardon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/55/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19105140-c77f-40e3-8fde-89823f0b5e56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: ISA 55:8
Text: For my thoughts are not your thoughts, neither are your ways my ways, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/55/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3390df4c-cce5-42e6-8213-29a44acf3bba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: ISA 55:9
Text: For as the heavens are higher than the earth, so are my ways higher than your ways, and my thoughts than your thoughts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/55/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92d467c6-fd5e-41a8-934f-9b9fea29ae42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: ISA 55:10
Text: For as the rain cometh down, and the snow from heaven, and returneth not thither, but watereth the earth, and maketh it bring forth and bud, that it may give seed to the sower, and bread to the eater:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/55/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cff8653a-a3aa-4035-8c71-cb5227a48c8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: ISA 55:11
Text: So shall my word be that goeth forth out of my mouth: it shall not return unto me void, but it shall accomplish that which I please, and it shall prosper in the thing whereto I sent it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/55/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72ba19c0-d9a4-49e3-bc4f-9831e9145880>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: ISA 55:12
Text: For ye shall go out with joy, and be led forth with peace: the mountains and the hills shall break forth before you into singing, and all the trees of the field shall clap their hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/55/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25796258-12b0-4d02-82bf-cbbb87659d7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: ISA 55:13
Text: Instead of the thorn shall come up the fir tree, and instead of the brier shall come up the myrtle tree: and it shall be to the LORD for a name, for an everlasting sign that shall not be cut off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/56/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a777b060-f133-4a37-a420-0d427cf1b7bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: ISA 56:1
Text: Thus saith the LORD, Keep ye judgment, and do justice: for my salvation is near to come, and my righteousness to be revealed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/56/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:508121a3-00ee-41b7-82df-5e968b2d1d7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: ISA 56:2
Text: Blessed is the man that doeth this, and the son of man that layeth hold on it; that keepeth the sabbath from polluting it, and keepeth his hand from doing any evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/56/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e64fb74d-b39b-46ca-acdb-a7ab5cb239dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: ISA 56:3
Text: Neither let the son of the stranger, that hath joined himself to the LORD, speak, saying, The LORD hath utterly separated me from his people: neither let the eunuch say, Behold, I am a dry tree.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/56/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dabe87e3-547f-411d-a95d-dfe68f2cec46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: ISA 56:4
Text: For thus saith the LORD unto the eunuchs that keep my sabbaths, and choose the things that please me, and take hold of my covenant;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/56/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d64ea6fb-0c51-4197-bf53-af2bd227994e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: ISA 56:5
Text: Even unto them will I give in mine house and within my walls a place and a name better than of sons and of daughters: I will give them an everlasting name, that shall not be cut off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/56/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22e2e624-d514-474c-a2ad-e1058608d4f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: ISA 56:6
Text: Also the sons of the stranger, that join themselves to the LORD, to serve him, and to love the name of the LORD, to be his servants, every one that keepeth the sabbath from polluting it, and taketh hold of my covenant;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/56/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bb7d934-ff27-4ef2-a673-5f157ce0c448>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: ISA 56:7
Text: Even them will I bring to my holy mountain, and make them joyful in my house of prayer: their burnt offerings and their sacrifices shall be accepted upon mine altar; for mine house shall be called an house of prayer for all people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/56/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac30cc27-a295-4989-ae24-9802f433a5f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: ISA 56:8
Text: The Lord GOD, which gathereth the outcasts of Israel saith, Yet will I gather others to him, beside those that are gathered unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/56/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65654ab0-199b-428e-8dba-2524b8093630>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: ISA 56:9
Text: All ye beasts of the field, come to devour, yea, all ye beasts in the forest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/56/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bc822de-de91-415b-aeda-e3143f6c01c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: ISA 56:10
Text: His watchmen are blind: they are all ignorant, they are all dumb dogs, they cannot bark; sleeping, lying down, loving to slumber.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/56/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db82b44a-5a34-40cc-a295-5ba9994f4363>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: ISA 56:11
Text: Yea, they are greedy dogs which can never have enough, and they are shepherds that cannot understand: they all look to their own way, every one for his gain, from his quarter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/56/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1e6231d-a879-479c-ae60-4e1d7563a1dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: ISA 56:12
Text: Come ye, say they, I will fetch wine, and we will fill ourselves with strong drink; and to morrow shall be as this day, and much more abundant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/57/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec8096c5-2619-4ea0-989a-fbe6eedf87c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: ISA 57:1
Text: The righteous perisheth, and no man layeth it to heart: and merciful men are taken away, none considering that the righteous is taken away from the evil to come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/57/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1941ffcd-fe50-4472-8241-0af51ddd88a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: ISA 57:2
Text: He shall enter into peace: they shall rest in their beds, each one walking in his uprightness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/57/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5672490-0505-4931-ba49-3e0c4c414766>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: ISA 57:3
Text: But draw near hither, ye sons of the sorceress, the seed of the adulterer and the whore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/57/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4759b414-af49-4321-be08-0bf2229f1e7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: ISA 57:4
Text: Against whom do ye sport yourselves? against whom make ye a wide mouth, and draw out the tongue? are ye not children of transgression, a seed of falsehood,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/57/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af83f928-526b-4ea8-8c52-5185b8db417d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: ISA 57:5
Text: Enflaming yourselves with idols under every green tree, slaying the children in the valleys under the clifts of the rocks?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/57/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7fd1aee-1641-499f-b9c4-f1fef8c19385>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: ISA 57:6
Text: Among the smooth stones of the stream is thy portion; they, they are thy lot: even to them hast thou poured a drink offering, thou hast offered a meat offering. Should I receive comfort in these?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/57/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d62765a-8c25-4548-bfe4-2d946ab0eb1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: ISA 57:7
Text: Upon a lofty and high mountain hast thou set thy bed: even thither wentest thou up to offer sacrifice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/57/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5f03d8d-bfc3-49e3-92d7-448bda81beed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: ISA 57:8
Text: Behind the doors also and the posts hast thou set up thy remembrance: for thou hast discovered thyself to another than me, and art gone up; thou hast enlarged thy bed, and made thee a covenant with them; thou lovedst their bed where thou sawest it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/57/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bac5c9a5-04a8-4478-bcb4-68de6990ddaf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: ISA 57:9
Text: And thou wentest to the king with ointment, and didst increase thy perfumes, and didst send thy messengers far off, and didst debase thyself even unto hell.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/57/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58266fd0-3339-4043-9b09-cc86c0c5069f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: ISA 57:10
Text: Thou art wearied in the greatness of thy way; yet saidst thou not, There is no hope: thou hast found the life of thine hand; therefore thou wast not grieved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/57/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1c0ca7a-c07c-4518-b718-de50b9ae6bb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: ISA 57:11
Text: And of whom hast thou been afraid or feared, that thou hast lied, and hast not remembered me, nor laid it to thy heart? have not I held my peace even of old, and thou fearest me not?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/57/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:360a24e0-e6cf-4619-a603-76695a893c45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: ISA 57:12
Text: I will declare thy righteousness, and thy works; for they shall not profit thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/57/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df5b6445-77b1-4072-bebb-6f4b79c74d37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: ISA 57:13
Text: When thou criest, let thy companies deliver thee; but the wind shall carry them all away; vanity shall take them: but he that putteth his trust in me shall possess the land, and shall inherit my holy mountain;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/57/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c8c3585-332a-4f9e-80a5-6ccbca5daa09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: ISA 57:14
Text: And shall say, Cast ye up, cast ye up, prepare the way, take up the stumblingblock out of the way of my people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/57/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f36adbe2-5f74-4497-b09c-5541785fd18e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: ISA 57:15
Text: For thus saith the high and lofty One that inhabiteth eternity, whose name is Holy; I dwell in the high and holy place, with him also that is of a contrite and humble spirit, to revive the spirit of the humble, and to revive the heart of the contrite ones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/57/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6774384f-b03f-471a-9e14-e341063b1023>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: ISA 57:16
Text: For I will not contend for ever, neither will I be always wroth: for the spirit should fail before me, and the souls which I have made.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/57/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:423fbfd2-9c28-4298-965c-1783b9e60a80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: ISA 57:17
Text: For the iniquity of his covetousness was I wroth, and smote him: I hid me, and was wroth, and he went on frowardly in the way of his heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/57/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1358f2bc-27d6-4171-bcd6-c4511658ce6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: ISA 57:18
Text: I have seen his ways, and will heal him: I will lead him also, and restore comforts unto him and to his mourners.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/57/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7187eded-7d73-4229-b00a-b7a5a2c91fa1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: ISA 57:19
Text: I create the fruit of the lips; Peace, peace to him that is far off, and to him that is near, saith the LORD; and I will heal him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/57/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edfbd488-04e5-4a88-8ba4-41ffa93431f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: ISA 57:20
Text: But the wicked are like the troubled sea, when it cannot rest, whose waters cast up mire and dirt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/57/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:070583d3-0ef0-4b3f-9c92-c83496d390b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: ISA 57:21
Text: There is no peace, saith my God, to the wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/58/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b93e6cc2-03eb-48b9-ae73-85b3f6ce4fc8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: ISA 58:1
Text: Cry aloud, spare not, lift up thy voice like a trumpet, and shew my people their transgression, and the house of Jacob their sins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/58/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fa6aea5-8dad-47b4-bc92-9cb39f03bfec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: ISA 58:2
Text: Yet they seek me daily, and delight to know my ways, as a nation that did righteousness, and forsook not the ordinance of their God: they ask of me the ordinances of justice; they take delight in approaching to God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/58/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1e552d3-f924-49fd-b0ce-766ce5bd67d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: ISA 58:3
Text: Wherefore have we fasted, say they, and thou seest not? wherefore have we afflicted our soul, and thou takest no knowledge? Behold, in the day of your fast ye find pleasure, and exact all your labours.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/58/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20f6fa06-6fbf-4a66-bedf-c95874b9d67b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: ISA 58:4
Text: Behold, ye fast for strife and debate, and to smite with the fist of wickedness: ye shall not fast as ye do this day, to make your voice to be heard on high.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/58/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e63c281-3e53-4ccf-b899-dbdeabcc8104>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: ISA 58:5
Text: Is it such a fast that I have chosen? a day for a man to afflict his soul? is it to bow down his head as a bulrush, and to spread sackcloth and ashes under him? wilt thou call this a fast, and an acceptable day to the LORD?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/58/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfea3fb6-09e9-42da-a9eb-c9ce61c47d44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: ISA 58:6
Text: Is not this the fast that I have chosen? to loose the bands of wickedness, to undo the heavy burdens, and to let the oppressed go free, and that ye break every yoke?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/58/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37f704de-78a1-4432-834f-4030890f26e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: ISA 58:7
Text: Is it not to deal thy bread to the hungry, and that thou bring the poor that are cast out to thy house? when thou seest the naked, that thou cover him; and that thou hide not thyself from thine own flesh?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/58/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ab2bb16-7e34-425a-b78d-babd9429004c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: ISA 58:8
Text: Then shall thy light break forth as the morning, and thine health shall spring forth speedily: and thy righteousness shall go before thee; the glory of the LORD shall be thy rereward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/58/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a980a29-24bc-4e96-ba93-0e3fcb8ec4a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: ISA 58:9
Text: Then shalt thou call, and the LORD shall answer; thou shalt cry, and he shall say, Here I am. If thou take away from the midst of thee the yoke, the putting forth of the finger, and speaking vanity;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/58/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:320b0ebf-7ca1-4c68-8f65-40b156159273>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: ISA 58:10
Text: And if thou draw out thy soul to the hungry, and satisfy the afflicted soul; then shall thy light rise in obscurity, and thy darkness be as the noon day:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/58/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09e519e0-62a1-4545-8066-a6be6e82aa97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: ISA 58:11
Text: And the LORD shall guide thee continually, and satisfy thy soul in drought, and make fat thy bones: and thou shalt be like a watered garden, and like a spring of water, whose waters fail not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/58/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:052c8db1-7308-4251-b01e-d890663959f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: ISA 58:12
Text: And they that shall be of thee shall build the old waste places: thou shalt raise up the foundations of many generations; and thou shalt be called, The repairer of the breach, The restorer of paths to dwell in.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/58/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54fd2c77-9499-450c-a9b2-30f4c214d3d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 288

Reference: ISA 58:13
Text: If thou turn away thy foot from the sabbath, from doing thy pleasure on my holy day; and call the sabbath a delight, the holy of the LORD, honourable; and shalt honour him, not doing thine own ways, nor finding thine own pleasure, nor speaking thine own words:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/58/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a90ccdd8-e90d-411a-87b0-f51dc2c7351a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: ISA 58:14
Text: Then shalt thou delight thyself in the LORD; and I will cause thee to ride upon the high places of the earth, and feed thee with the heritage of Jacob thy father: for the mouth of the LORD hath spoken it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/59/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a85c2531-254d-4508-b947-d92bd480ceae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: ISA 59:1
Text: Behold, the LORD’s hand is not shortened, that it cannot save; neither his ear heavy, that it cannot hear:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/59/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb56c2ae-823d-4af3-8a32-2a4f80ad4af8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: ISA 59:2
Text: But your iniquities have separated between you and your God, and your sins have hid his face from you, that he will not hear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/59/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df5a588b-bda4-46fb-ae32-0f992d578ac3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: ISA 59:3
Text: For your hands are defiled with blood, and your fingers with iniquity; your lips have spoken lies, your tongue hath muttered perverseness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/59/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:614b9a40-d743-44b0-a1c2-6cc90f004f52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: ISA 59:4
Text: None calleth for justice, nor any pleadeth for truth: they trust in vanity, and speak lies; they conceive mischief, and bring forth iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/59/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fc875e3-3233-468c-aabe-e439067d2d93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: ISA 59:5
Text: They hatch cockatrice’ eggs, and weave the spider’s web: he that eateth of their eggs dieth, and that which is crushed breaketh out into a viper.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/59/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0a5d852-e2b9-4a94-a04b-c0ed799ad58e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: ISA 59:6
Text: Their webs shall not become garments, neither shall they cover themselves with their works: their works are works of iniquity, and the act of violence is in their hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/59/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8f323ad-7769-4a83-b695-fc43bbdc35bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: ISA 59:7
Text: Their feet run to evil, and they make haste to shed innocent blood: their thoughts are thoughts of iniquity; wasting and destruction are in their paths.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/59/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c94d5af2-eaa1-40e9-8113-1b2c4c7e2a41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: ISA 59:8
Text: The way of peace they know not; and there is no judgment in their goings: they have made them crooked paths: whosoever goeth therein shall not know peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/59/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23fe8875-7355-423f-b753-784f3a932431>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: ISA 59:9
Text: Therefore is judgment far from us, neither doth justice overtake us: we wait for light, but behold obscurity; for brightness, but we walk in darkness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/59/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa76b6a8-93a9-4fba-858b-f3b365adc393>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: ISA 59:10
Text: We grope for the wall like the blind, and we grope as if we had no eyes: we stumble at noon day as in the night; we are in desolate places as dead men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/59/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ac61662-1a2d-4536-8028-9d3f83f2215c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: ISA 59:11
Text: We roar all like bears, and mourn sore like doves: we look for judgment, but there is none; for salvation, but it is far off from us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/59/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02d861c2-282e-4263-9007-28df31eacfd8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: ISA 59:12
Text: For our transgressions are multiplied before thee, and our sins testify against us: for our transgressions are with us; and as for our iniquities, we know them;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/59/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fcd4b4a3-ba69-4c51-9201-45bbe86d2775>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: ISA 59:13
Text: In transgressing and lying against the LORD, and departing away from our God, speaking oppression and revolt, conceiving and uttering from the heart words of falsehood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/59/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5884edd-fe95-4428-a263-4b0ef99b6c83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: ISA 59:14
Text: And judgment is turned away backward, and justice standeth afar off: for truth is fallen in the street, and equity cannot enter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/59/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03a2c905-0162-4d4b-8681-b444e92a28d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: ISA 59:15
Text: Yea, truth faileth; and he that departeth from evil maketh himself a prey: and the LORD saw it, and it displeased him that there was no judgment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/59/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:321d41a6-ea10-453d-ada1-2b5cbf7e8f7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: ISA 59:16
Text: And he saw that there was no man, and wondered that there was no intercessor: therefore his arm brought salvation unto him; and his righteousness, it sustained him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/59/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b34ce44c-8735-4365-bb83-13e0a2a176fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: ISA 59:17
Text: For he put on righteousness as a breastplate, and an helmet of salvation upon his head; and he put on the garments of vengeance for clothing, and was clad with zeal as a cloak.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/59/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:022639ad-5805-4022-8fc4-7dc6cd0c614c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: ISA 59:18
Text: According to their deeds, accordingly he will repay, fury to his adversaries, recompence to his enemies; to the islands he will repay recompence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/59/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f595f8f-f582-4969-b387-03331cf41b31>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: ISA 59:19
Text: So shall they fear the name of the LORD from the west, and his glory from the rising of the sun. When the enemy shall come in like a flood, the Spirit of the LORD shall lift up a standard against him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/59/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3173b87c-aa27-4cec-b64a-353e04c3f9ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: ISA 59:20
Text: And the Redeemer shall come to Zion, and unto them that turn from transgression in Jacob, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/59/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e12d13ee-16e0-4eb7-98bf-b43924fe3f04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 316

Reference: ISA 59:21
Text: As for me, this is my covenant with them, saith the LORD; My spirit that is upon thee, and my words which I have put in thy mouth, shall not depart out of thy mouth, nor out of the mouth of thy seed, nor out of the mouth of thy seed’s seed, saith the LORD, from henceforth and for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/60/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f447301a-c9c9-430c-9cd7-da6280bc6d30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: ISA 60:1
Text: Arise, shine; for thy light is come, and the glory of the LORD is risen upon thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/60/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11de2a75-c601-4627-bcce-71a1414abe30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: ISA 60:2
Text: For, behold, the darkness shall cover the earth, and gross darkness the people: but the LORD shall arise upon thee, and his glory shall be seen upon thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/60/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a850d4a3-6186-4290-938c-924feda59073>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: ISA 60:3
Text: And the Gentiles shall come to thy light, and kings to the brightness of thy rising.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/60/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:811facfe-d964-4d2d-b593-4933895fd2e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: ISA 60:4
Text: Lift up thine eyes round about, and see: all they gather themselves together, they come to thee: thy sons shall come from far, and thy daughters shall be nursed at thy side.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/60/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92be370d-8ede-4e9b-a2a0-328c0f223d56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: ISA 60:5
Text: Then thou shalt see, and flow together, and thine heart shall fear, and be enlarged; because the abundance of the sea shall be converted unto thee, the forces of the Gentiles shall come unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/60/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f41877d-9629-4989-9912-cebc0d8425ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: ISA 60:6
Text: The multitude of camels shall cover thee, the dromedaries of Midian and Ephah; all they from Sheba shall come: they shall bring gold and incense; and they shall shew forth the praises of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/60/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8c758e7-6ff0-496e-8822-a7ad29665258>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: ISA 60:7
Text: All the flocks of Kedar shall be gathered together unto thee, the rams of Nebaioth shall minister unto thee: they shall come up with acceptance on mine altar, and I will glorify the house of my glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/60/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f75d45c6-1b71-45aa-b831-ff3fcd700210>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: ISA 60:8
Text: Who are these that fly as a cloud, and as the doves to their windows?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/60/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57f5dd9f-734c-4c58-b076-11614969fede>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: ISA 60:9
Text: Surely the isles shall wait for me, and the ships of Tarshish first, to bring thy sons from far, their silver and their gold with them, unto the name of the LORD thy God, and to the Holy One of Israel, because he hath glorified thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/60/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aed83d82-171a-4ac7-a822-199c746ca8ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: ISA 60:10
Text: And the sons of strangers shall build up thy walls, and their kings shall minister unto thee: for in my wrath I smote thee, but in my favour have I had mercy on thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/60/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d25c686-1811-4aaf-af31-5ba00cdfe240>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: ISA 60:11
Text: Therefore thy gates shall be open continually; they shall not be shut day nor night; that men may bring unto thee the forces of the Gentiles, and that their kings may be brought.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/60/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c35db254-5004-4319-a7c6-4f6ea3d09053>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: ISA 60:12
Text: For the nation and kingdom that will not serve thee shall perish; yea, those nations shall be utterly wasted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/60/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef0b05df-bf75-4023-addd-d4e7f258fbf9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: ISA 60:13
Text: The glory of Lebanon shall come unto thee, the fir tree, the pine tree, and the box together, to beautify the place of my sanctuary; and I will make the place of my feet glorious.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/60/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37405ca9-b800-4d45-99eb-681864dddf3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: ISA 60:14
Text: The sons also of them that afflicted thee shall come bending unto thee; and all they that despised thee shall bow themselves down at the soles of thy feet; and they shall call thee; The city of the LORD, The Zion of the Holy One of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/60/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f82ebc1b-6293-4e36-929c-f9a773cb9012>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: ISA 60:15
Text: Whereas thou hast been forsaken and hated, so that no man went through thee, I will make thee an eternal excellency, a joy of many generations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/60/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ddc7000-872d-435f-819f-9663b4e7400c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: ISA 60:16
Text: Thou shalt also suck the milk of the Gentiles, and shalt suck the breast of kings: and thou shalt know that I the LORD am thy Saviour and thy Redeemer, the mighty One of Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/60/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:253a87ee-48fc-4f24-ab95-efa9e70e9936>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: ISA 60:17
Text: For brass I will bring gold, and for iron I will bring silver, and for wood brass, and for stones iron: I will also make thy officers peace, and thine exactors righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/60/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1c4874a-3eb6-49f6-9bc0-66b1364485e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: ISA 60:18
Text: Violence shall no more be heard in thy land, wasting nor destruction within thy borders; but thou shalt call thy walls Salvation, and thy gates Praise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/60/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c001b5b1-c2a5-4500-81d4-4b4759d2d0e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: ISA 60:19
Text: The sun shall be no more thy light by day; neither for brightness shall the moon give light unto thee: but the LORD shall be unto thee an everlasting light, and thy God thy glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/60/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2cd59cf-0d61-4948-a279-3bc748426949>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: ISA 60:20
Text: Thy sun shall no more go down; neither shall thy moon withdraw itself: for the LORD shall be thine everlasting light, and the days of thy mourning shall be ended.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/60/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:556869cb-a4ac-4c57-a35a-71d875533e3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: ISA 60:21
Text: Thy people also shall be all righteous: they shall inherit the land for ever, the branch of my planting, the work of my hands, that I may be glorified.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/60/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe7d2d17-79a5-4dc6-a1cf-9dac591a973f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: ISA 60:22
Text: A little one shall become a thousand, and a small one a strong nation: I the LORD will hasten it in his time.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/61/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c558d7d-fda3-4328-b5b4-f4b581a27dd2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 274

Reference: ISA 61:1
Text: The Spirit of the Lord GOD is upon me; because the LORD hath anointed me to preach good tidings unto the meek; he hath sent me to bind up the brokenhearted, to proclaim liberty to the captives, and the opening of the prison to them that are bound;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/61/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89905541-2c15-4b94-a3b7-dfc02b4868b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: ISA 61:2
Text: To proclaim the acceptable year of the LORD, and the day of vengeance of our God; to comfort all that mourn;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/61/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:239da60e-b4b0-4b94-9d64-93b99913f23c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 287

Reference: ISA 61:3
Text: To appoint unto them that mourn in Zion, to give unto them beauty for ashes, the oil of joy for mourning, the garment of praise for the spirit of heaviness; that they might be called trees of righteousness, the planting of the LORD, that he might be glorified.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/61/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16e115a4-164c-4eb9-a8e3-6ed13a782dc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: ISA 61:4
Text: And they shall build the old wastes, they shall raise up the former desolations, and they shall repair the waste cities, the desolations of many generations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/61/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4271cb80-fcd9-4d41-a3da-b95697405371>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: ISA 61:5
Text: And strangers shall stand and feed your flocks, and the sons of the alien shall be your plowmen and your vinedressers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/61/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34f3edc9-eeae-4e3e-a2f4-312019a27418>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: ISA 61:6
Text: But ye shall be named the Priests of the LORD: men shall call you the Ministers of our God: ye shall eat the riches of the Gentiles, and in their glory shall ye boast yourselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/61/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1d57ce7-f416-42bf-892a-ba4e28fde7d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: ISA 61:7
Text: For your shame ye shall have double; and for confusion they shall rejoice in their portion: therefore in their land they shall possess the double: everlasting joy shall be unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/61/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d0263e3-23a3-4f98-9145-3e4425a976d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: ISA 61:8
Text: For I the LORD love judgment, I hate robbery for burnt offering; and I will direct their work in truth, and I will make an everlasting covenant with them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/61/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:627bee05-603d-4678-b5f7-6829e204c2e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: ISA 61:9
Text: And their seed shall be known among the Gentiles, and their offspring among the people: all that see them shall acknowledge them, that they are the seed which the LORD hath blessed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/61/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ac1cbdf-1a86-438a-89be-ae12beb1a276>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 301

Reference: ISA 61:10
Text: I will greatly rejoice in the LORD, my soul shall be joyful in my God; for he hath clothed me with the garments of salvation, he hath covered me with the robe of righteousness, as a bridegroom decketh himself with ornaments, and as a bride adorneth herself with her jewels.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/61/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ed0d591-944d-41c7-a1cf-4ecf9d856451>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: ISA 61:11
Text: For as the earth bringeth forth her bud, and as the garden causeth the things that are sown in it to spring forth; so the Lord GOD will cause righteousness and praise to spring forth before all the nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/62/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a0df3c1-6994-4b1c-a8d7-4f319741f028>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: ISA 62:1
Text: For Zion’s sake will I not hold my peace, and for Jerusalem’s sake I will not rest, until the righteousness thereof go forth as brightness, and the salvation thereof as a lamp that burneth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/62/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bdf441c4-6dd4-4319-ad97-e5b4ee16201f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: ISA 62:2
Text: And the Gentiles shall see thy righteousness, and all kings thy glory: and thou shalt be called by a new name, which the mouth of the LORD shall name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/62/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31ddd7fd-d624-4ff1-a036-76e767c58739>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: ISA 62:3
Text: Thou shalt also be a crown of glory in the hand of the LORD, and a royal diadem in the hand of thy God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/62/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5bb4a82-0072-4a31-bbf6-14dd8223f7da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: ISA 62:4
Text: Thou shalt no more be termed Forsaken; neither shall thy land any more be termed Desolate: but thou shalt be called Hephzibah, and thy land Beulah: for the LORD delighteth in thee, and thy land shall be married.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/62/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:faa0871a-de7c-4966-b33d-432d1fff9f63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: ISA 62:5
Text: For as a young man marrieth a virgin, so shall thy sons marry thee: and as the bridegroom rejoiceth over the bride, so shall thy God rejoice over thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/62/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08464218-a217-4e3f-bf43-060103eb70d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: ISA 62:6
Text: I have set watchmen upon thy walls, O Jerusalem, which shall never hold their peace day nor night: ye that make mention of the LORD, keep not silence,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/62/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d353ff7d-f8b7-4ecd-ab95-043858976bdd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: ISA 62:7
Text: And give him no rest, till he establish, and till he make Jerusalem a praise in the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/62/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d04e291-791f-4141-8184-1770f69ab9a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: ISA 62:8
Text: The LORD hath sworn by his right hand, and by the arm of his strength, Surely I will no more give thy corn to be meat for thine enemies; and the sons of the stranger shall not drink thy wine, for the which thou hast laboured:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/62/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de1fe725-16ab-4c59-96d5-6287db101ef7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: ISA 62:9
Text: But they that have gathered it shall eat it, and praise the LORD; and they that have brought it together shall drink it in the courts of my holiness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/62/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0b9387c-302a-4568-bd8f-66430095f2f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: ISA 62:10
Text: Go through, go through the gates; prepare ye the way of the people; cast up, cast up the highway; gather out the stones; lift up a standard for the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/62/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e92c9798-4c9a-4564-8cf6-7a5018bf16b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: ISA 62:11
Text: Behold, the LORD hath proclaimed unto the end of the world, Say ye to the daughter of Zion, Behold, thy salvation cometh; behold, his reward is with him, and his work before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/62/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ec44453-ccd7-4c56-8623-43e54bf73c85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: ISA 62:12
Text: And they shall call them, The holy people, The redeemed of the LORD: and thou shalt be called, Sought out, A city not forsaken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/63/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70ea34e1-8169-45ad-a1a8-eaafbd1ea285>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: ISA 63:1
Text: Who is this that cometh from Edom, with dyed garments from Bozrah? this that is glorious in his apparel, travelling in the greatness of his strength? I that speak in righteousness, mighty to save.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/63/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb7ff19c-3629-4027-8a2f-d04f83e6768f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: ISA 63:2
Text: Wherefore art thou red in thine apparel, and thy garments like him that treadeth in the winefat?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/63/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56516653-34cc-44be-9a66-ed20c419ae0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: ISA 63:3
Text: I have trodden the winepress alone; and of the people there was none with me: for I will tread them in mine anger, and trample them in my fury; and their blood shall be sprinkled upon my garments, and I will stain all my raiment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/63/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7437a167-2f03-4a27-8659-3d4605e23752>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: ISA 63:4
Text: For the day of vengeance is in mine heart, and the year of my redeemed is come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/63/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b5df689-08f0-4187-a3e6-6f13cc8bc2a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: ISA 63:5
Text: And I looked, and there was none to help; and I wondered that there was none to uphold: therefore mine own arm brought salvation unto me; and my fury, it upheld me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/63/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9454804-3484-4257-b6d0-730850e7b4d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: ISA 63:6
Text: And I will tread down the people in mine anger, and make them drunk in my fury, and I will bring down their strength to the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/63/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5626ac5-e101-41cd-9cc4-dada43f8324d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 320

Reference: ISA 63:7
Text: I will mention the lovingkindnesses of the LORD, and the praises of the LORD, according to all that the LORD hath bestowed on us, and the great goodness toward the house of Israel, which he hath bestowed on them according to his mercies, and according to the multitude of his lovingkindnesses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/63/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b53b799a-d576-4d47-9a6f-67228720c7f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: ISA 63:8
Text: For he said, Surely they are my people, children that will not lie: so he was their Saviour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/63/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1117a518-9876-4cdc-b879-f2235f7b0367>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: ISA 63:9
Text: In all their affliction he was afflicted, and the angel of his presence saved them: in his love and in his pity he redeemed them; and he bare them, and carried them all the days of old.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/63/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7f60aab-fa49-4d77-ab8b-6963659cf3cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: ISA 63:10
Text: But they rebelled, and vexed his holy Spirit: therefore he was turned to be their enemy, and he fought against them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/63/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f95f5e28-215c-4426-81da-0c57d2d2fd27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: ISA 63:11
Text: Then he remembered the days of old, Moses, and his people, saying, Where is he that brought them up out of the sea with the shepherd of his flock? where is he that put his holy Spirit within him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/63/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c4a2a5d-99f9-4d76-ad1f-10e570de7170>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: ISA 63:12
Text: That led them by the right hand of Moses with his glorious arm, dividing the water before them, to make himself an everlasting name?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/63/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:452632b9-372d-40d9-899a-0238da154baf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: ISA 63:13
Text: That led them through the deep, as an horse in the wilderness, that they should not stumble?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/63/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3675105e-445f-41d8-a945-cd0268eb5705>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: ISA 63:14
Text: As a beast goeth down into the valley, the Spirit of the LORD caused him to rest: so didst thou lead thy people, to make thyself a glorious name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/63/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19a726a4-1c92-4ff9-b665-f3742f225ed8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: ISA 63:15
Text: Look down from heaven, and behold from the habitation of thy holiness and of thy glory: where is thy zeal and thy strength, the sounding of thy bowels and of thy mercies toward me? are they restrained?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/63/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1051dc7-5183-4db7-b3ec-ab3a4ac1adb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: ISA 63:16
Text: Doubtless thou art our father, though Abraham be ignorant of us, and Israel acknowledge us not: thou, O LORD, art our father, our redeemer; thy name is from everlasting.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/63/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:972257cd-97ba-4eaf-8f54-7c8e7981d09f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: ISA 63:17
Text: O LORD, why hast thou made us to err from thy ways, and hardened our heart from thy fear? Return for thy servants’ sake, the tribes of thine inheritance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/63/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:238c8d4a-c625-4fd7-8198-df9276649121>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: ISA 63:18
Text: The people of thy holiness have possessed it but a little while: our adversaries have trodden down thy sanctuary.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/63/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf46696f-7828-4666-8f3e-dc7d9a2a4a22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: ISA 63:19
Text: We are thine: thou never barest rule over them; they were not called by thy name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/64/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d0a32f5-b266-4bcd-9fd2-4b6d999ff24b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: ISA 64:1
Text: Oh that thou wouldest rend the heavens, that thou wouldest come down, that the mountains might flow down at thy presence,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/64/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:149f047a-ab88-411a-ad03-56f92beff282>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: ISA 64:2
Text: As when the melting fire burneth, the fire causeth the waters to boil, to make thy name known to thine adversaries, that the nations may tremble at thy presence!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/64/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfa5d152-8c62-44a2-ba9a-1a76531d9eef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: ISA 64:3
Text: When thou didst terrible things which we looked not for, thou camest down, the mountains flowed down at thy presence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/64/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8057b436-ed35-4f9b-9309-455da65c1a73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: ISA 64:4
Text: For since the beginning of the world men have not heard, nor perceived by the ear, neither hath the eye seen, O God, beside thee, what he hath prepared for him that waiteth for him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/64/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29ee849b-7a52-4775-8c34-58c97baefa10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: ISA 64:5
Text: Thou meetest him that rejoiceth and worketh righteousness, those that remember thee in thy ways: behold, thou art wroth; for we have sinned: in those is continuance, and we shall be saved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/64/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:509567c6-4ce8-4410-8d5c-a70ae1823a23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: ISA 64:6
Text: But we are all as an unclean thing, and all our righteousnesses are as filthy rags; and we all do fade as a leaf; and our iniquities, like the wind, have taken us away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/64/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff870837-c195-4650-8d22-746a2bd90683>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: ISA 64:7
Text: And there is none that calleth upon thy name, that stirreth up himself to take hold of thee: for thou hast hid thy face from us, and hast consumed us, because of our iniquities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/64/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eeb65c05-fa25-4555-964a-541c923f1392>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: ISA 64:8
Text: But now, O LORD, thou art our father; we are the clay, and thou our potter; and we all are the work of thy hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/64/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6cb45b0e-978b-4176-988e-077ccef46874>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: ISA 64:9
Text: Be not wroth very sore, O LORD, neither remember iniquity for ever: behold, see, we beseech thee, we are all thy people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/64/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6efab82-a661-4ab1-b2e0-ef133eea4dc5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: ISA 64:10
Text: Thy holy cities are a wilderness, Zion is a wilderness, Jerusalem a desolation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/64/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92378357-c859-4338-a84c-23b0918faff5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: ISA 64:11
Text: Our holy and our beautiful house, where our fathers praised thee, is burned up with fire: and all our pleasant things are laid waste.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/64/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8447274-1982-4e0c-a24b-b4a9e4615bdb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: ISA 64:12
Text: Wilt thou refrain thyself for these things, O LORD? wilt thou hold thy peace, and afflict us very sore?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7d5daad-d11b-4b7e-b47b-0e2f249d0be7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: ISA 65:1
Text: I am sought of them that asked not for me; I am found of them that sought me not: I said, Behold me, behold me, unto a nation that was not called by my name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14968aab-fa50-418f-bd0e-94e3114eeb73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: ISA 65:2
Text: I have spread out my hands all the day unto a rebellious people, which walketh in a way that was not good, after their own thoughts;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9617e4a-2219-416c-8185-f9ffb8ff9b47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: ISA 65:3
Text: A people that provoketh me to anger continually to my face; that sacrificeth in gardens, and burneth incense upon altars of brick;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b443145-beb4-4efd-9027-1e82021fe278>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: ISA 65:4
Text: Which remain among the graves, and lodge in the monuments, which eat swine’s flesh, and broth of abominable things is in their vessels;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88f47e55-d7be-427d-9c8a-eb317c38aca0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: ISA 65:5
Text: Which say, Stand by thyself, come not near to me; for I am holier than thou. These are a smoke in my nose, a fire that burneth all the day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb33e860-1846-48a2-b354-eb0e0885f203>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: ISA 65:6
Text: Behold, it is written before me: I will not keep silence, but will recompense, even recompense into their bosom,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9cd81754-23c1-42a3-889e-46e1f1a54200>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: ISA 65:7
Text: Your iniquities, and the iniquities of your fathers together, saith the LORD, which have burned incense upon the mountains, and blasphemed me upon the hills: therefore will I measure their former work into their bosom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07a92351-d9e7-4bd5-b005-7edc57806fb9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: ISA 65:8
Text: Thus saith the LORD, As the new wine is found in the cluster, and one saith, Destroy it not; for a blessing is in it: so will I do for my servants’ sakes, that I may not destroy them all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69560471-6249-4a32-bbae-27f8be97c45b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: ISA 65:9
Text: And I will bring forth a seed out of Jacob, and out of Judah an inheritor of my mountains: and mine elect shall inherit it, and my servants shall dwell there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8c4316d-2858-45bc-b31f-844363ae1722>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: ISA 65:10
Text: And Sharon shall be a fold of flocks, and the valley of Achor a place for the herds to lie down in, for my people that have sought me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d427bcf-69b4-4a52-9ac3-12b57a1c6033>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: ISA 65:11
Text: But ye are they that forsake the LORD, that forget my holy mountain, that prepare a table for that troop, and that furnish the drink offering unto that number.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0bd7f95-b9c7-4421-b41b-f38be5b535bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 262

Reference: ISA 65:12
Text: Therefore will I number you to the sword, and ye shall all bow down to the slaughter: because when I called, ye did not answer; when I spake, ye did not hear; but did evil before mine eyes, and did choose that wherein I delighted not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85085f3c-706e-4285-8852-ba207029e7ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: ISA 65:13
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD, Behold, my servants shall eat, but ye shall be hungry: behold, my servants shall drink, but ye shall be thirsty: behold, my servants shall rejoice, but ye shall be ashamed:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:065908ca-c392-4904-b421-03debba31b0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: ISA 65:14
Text: Behold, my servants shall sing for joy of heart, but ye shall cry for sorrow of heart, and shall howl for vexation of spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:483c1d66-07d8-437f-a6da-e86324e9d4b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: ISA 65:15
Text: And ye shall leave your name for a curse unto my chosen: for the Lord GOD shall slay thee, and call his servants by another name:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a93764dd-f56a-4ffa-99e5-c0391e0a692f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: ISA 65:16
Text: That he who blesseth himself in the earth shall bless himself in the God of truth; and he that sweareth in the earth shall swear by the God of truth; because the former troubles are forgotten, and because they are hid from mine eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c503b2f6-1882-45df-b44b-e344f637c02b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: ISA 65:17
Text: For, behold, I create new heavens and a new earth: and the former shall not be remembered, nor come into mind.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:650a3f76-8e9b-431d-b0c6-e002a26073e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: ISA 65:18
Text: But be ye glad and rejoice for ever in that which I create: for, behold, I create Jerusalem a rejoicing, and her people a joy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b36700aa-7694-488b-9c72-fe85c8f98ca5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: ISA 65:19
Text: And I will rejoice in Jerusalem, and joy in my people: and the voice of weeping shall be no more heard in her, nor the voice of crying.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a25f071b-d5d6-42d1-b2dd-52066fbf65c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: ISA 65:20
Text: There shall be no more thence an infant of days, nor an old man that hath not filled his days: for the child shall die an hundred years old; but the sinner being an hundred years old shall be accursed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1486216-95a2-4c84-9cbd-8f541f2ca1e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: ISA 65:21
Text: And they shall build houses, and inhabit them; and they shall plant vineyards, and eat the fruit of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d73a2581-2e0f-4eeb-ab62-1cb28ebd0dab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: ISA 65:22
Text: They shall not build, and another inhabit; they shall not plant, and another eat: for as the days of a tree are the days of my people, and mine elect shall long enjoy the work of their hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d360231-90d3-4583-b072-4a46964019ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: ISA 65:23
Text: They shall not labour in vain, nor bring forth for trouble; for they are the seed of the blessed of the LORD, and their offspring with them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dcc277bb-08b5-4638-badc-fdb54f75c7e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: ISA 65:24
Text: And it shall come to pass, that before they call, I will answer; and while they are yet speaking, I will hear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/65/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30ecf7e2-d8dc-41e0-9e72-1afced9768b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: ISA 65:25
Text: The wolf and the lamb shall feed together, and the lion shall eat straw like the bullock: and dust shall be the serpent’s meat. They shall not hurt nor destroy in all my holy mountain, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:475ea034-33ae-487b-bbe6-05fffe84d03f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: ISA 66:1
Text: Thus saith the LORD, The heaven is my throne, and the earth is my footstool: where is the house that ye build unto me? and where is the place of my rest?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f941ed0-fefb-4949-8c6c-73a8ec2ed367>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: ISA 66:2
Text: For all those things hath mine hand made, and all those things have been, saith the LORD: but to this man will I look, even to him that is poor and of a contrite spirit, and trembleth at my word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f56b3b2b-87a3-46e6-9c92-cce0f14c3a8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 335

Reference: ISA 66:3
Text: He that killeth an ox is as if he slew a man; he that sacrificeth a lamb, as if he cut off a dog’s neck; he that offereth an oblation, as if he offered swine’s blood; he that burneth incense, as if he blessed an idol. Yea, they have chosen their own ways, and their soul delighteth in their abominations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5a78743-db8f-449d-b1a1-c51ae083ff2d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: ISA 66:4
Text: I also will choose their delusions, and will bring their fears upon them; because when I called, none did answer; when I spake, they did not hear: but they did evil before mine eyes, and chose that in which I delighted not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78fc6aac-d72e-4424-bc85-0a65ddc0b990>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: ISA 66:5
Text: Hear the word of the LORD, ye that tremble at his word; Your brethren that hated you, that cast you out for my name’s sake, said, Let the LORD be glorified: but he shall appear to your joy, and they shall be ashamed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20799d1c-7f09-4c3b-bb1d-577ca565b44a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: ISA 66:6
Text: A voice of noise from the city, a voice from the temple, a voice of the LORD that rendereth recompence to his enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37dc286e-a5ac-4d0e-b615-9ad1e3d796b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: ISA 66:7
Text: Before she travailed, she brought forth; before her pain came, she was delivered of a man child.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee5139a6-7fd2-463a-8591-624c9cd5a9f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: ISA 66:8
Text: Who hath heard such a thing? who hath seen such things? Shall the earth be made to bring forth in one day? or shall a nation be born at once? for as soon as Zion travailed, she brought forth her children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2e5437b-1157-4cad-b809-3fa119e8bb0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: ISA 66:9
Text: Shall I bring to the birth, and not cause to bring forth? saith the LORD: shall I cause to bring forth, and shut the womb? saith thy God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0e4f8dd-12fc-45ff-8b94-fb19b4ecc760>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: ISA 66:10
Text: Rejoice ye with Jerusalem, and be glad with her, all ye that love her: rejoice for joy with her, all ye that mourn for her:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3fd1c3e-b669-40f0-a1f6-57f67bc80574>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: ISA 66:11
Text: That ye may suck, and be satisfied with the breasts of her consolations; that ye may milk out, and be delighted with the abundance of her glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68580ce0-d475-495e-a27e-cb104945ff44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: ISA 66:12
Text: For thus saith the LORD, Behold, I will extend peace to her like a river, and the glory of the Gentiles like a flowing stream: then shall ye suck, ye shall be borne upon her sides, and be dandled upon her knees.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81709f62-b9e3-43f1-b76a-294c65f5a4b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: ISA 66:13
Text: As one whom his mother comforteth, so will I comfort you; and ye shall be comforted in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9b6608f-eb84-4006-8609-bea0777217b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: ISA 66:14
Text: And when ye see this, your heart shall rejoice, and your bones shall flourish like an herb: and the hand of the LORD shall be known toward his servants, and his indignation toward his enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b404899-4548-414c-8389-bb9bf90dc5b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: ISA 66:15
Text: For, behold, the LORD will come with fire, and with his chariots like a whirlwind, to render his anger with fury, and his rebuke with flames of fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b3fd916-e084-417e-8a92-5fa1b9926aa9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: ISA 66:16
Text: For by fire and by his sword will the LORD plead with all flesh: and the slain of the LORD shall be many.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6d0e9aa-e0b1-457c-9313-a3e1465dc0f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: ISA 66:17
Text: They that sanctify themselves, and purify themselves in the gardens behind one tree in the midst, eating swine’s flesh, and the abomination, and the mouse, shall be consumed together, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ab800de-d73a-4d9f-b1e8-63fef6facba7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: ISA 66:18
Text: For I know their works and their thoughts: it shall come, that I will gather all nations and tongues; and they shall come, and see my glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:434355ea-4d46-4561-b485-67835eccfbab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 320

Reference: ISA 66:19
Text: And I will set a sign among them, and I will send those that escape of them unto the nations, to Tarshish, Pul, and Lud, that draw the bow, to Tubal, and Javan, to the isles afar off, that have not heard my fame, neither have seen my glory; and they shall declare my glory among the Gentiles.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4405eb0-9e87-4046-b885-11ac12bea4c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 337

Reference: ISA 66:20
Text: And they shall bring all your brethren for an offering unto the LORD out of all nations upon horses, and in chariots, and in litters, and upon mules, and upon swift beasts, to my holy mountain Jerusalem, saith the LORD, as the children of Israel bring an offering in a clean vessel into the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed5f8e21-619b-47df-8553-ff5aaf109855>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: ISA 66:21
Text: And I will also take of them for priests and for Levites, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80b5e993-f5df-41f8-a09a-b0f3ffc1a0e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: ISA 66:22
Text: For as the new heavens and the new earth, which I will make, shall remain before me, saith the LORD, so shall your seed and your name remain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9c4d7d8-365a-4ac1-9e2c-4f6b23469228>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: ISA 66:23
Text: And it shall come to pass, that from one new moon to another, and from one sabbath to another, shall all flesh come to worship before me, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ISA/66/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76b623dd-9dd6-49f8-8338-020ab3e1cab6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: ISA 66:24
Text: And they shall go forth, and look upon the carcases of the men that have transgressed against me: for their worm shall not die, neither shall their fire be quenched; and they shall be an abhorring unto all flesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85a2462e-6ba7-4d70-a4d9-e24b0b7f5354>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: JER 1:1
Text: The words of Jeremiah the son of Hilkiah, of the priests that were in Anathoth in the land of Benjamin:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1bc7129-a84a-4cb4-9c7e-9dc39ea1a92a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: JER 1:2
Text: To whom the word of the LORD came in the days of Josiah the son of Amon king of Judah, in the thirteenth year of his reign.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85577699-ce2c-436b-98fe-1cc520eb7ae1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: JER 1:3
Text: It came also in the days of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah, unto the end of the eleventh year of Zedekiah the son of Josiah king of Judah, unto the carrying away of Jerusalem captive in the fifth month.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd654b52-eb17-45c6-b814-a785bd94c845>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: JER 1:4
Text: Then the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ac25975-1e1d-4de8-9185-a5651a2589ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: JER 1:5
Text: Before I formed thee in the belly I knew thee; and before thou camest forth out of the womb I sanctified thee, and I ordained thee a prophet unto the nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eec56671-abc4-4d7b-a073-f188d31e0d15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: JER 1:6
Text: Then said I, Ah, Lord GOD! behold, I cannot speak: for I am a child.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3c1bff9-d58d-475a-beac-d3e75af39cd5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: JER 1:7
Text: But the LORD said unto me, Say not, I am a child: for thou shalt go to all that I shall send thee, and whatsoever I command thee thou shalt speak.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d052349-6d6c-4fbe-a84f-fc5690d17666>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: JER 1:8
Text: Be not afraid of their faces: for I am with thee to deliver thee, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c64b2d8-3fe3-4f0d-9d42-2a8484bb62bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: JER 1:9
Text: Then the LORD put forth his hand, and touched my mouth. And the LORD said unto me, Behold, I have put my words in thy mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:778d8295-1d96-4d08-9880-2fd54939832b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: JER 1:10
Text: See, I have this day set thee over the nations and over the kingdoms, to root out, and to pull down, and to destroy, and to throw down, to build, and to plant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f64ad96b-a8d7-473b-8314-ac872484e251>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: JER 1:11
Text: Moreover the word of the LORD came unto me, saying, Jeremiah, what seest thou? And I said, I see a rod of an almond tree.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b2f6027-221f-4719-9df5-fba5ee4f5533>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: JER 1:12
Text: Then said the LORD unto me, Thou hast well seen: for I will hasten my word to perform it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9fcb577-d2e7-425a-b7af-bcd8944099c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JER 1:13
Text: And the word of the LORD came unto me the second time, saying, What seest thou? And I said, I see a seething pot; and the face thereof is toward the north.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:979f278f-7dae-4b42-a178-78ff406e0d0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: JER 1:14
Text: Then the LORD said unto me, Out of the north an evil shall break forth upon all the inhabitants of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d17537ab-bcec-4677-971e-da096984ba56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 298

Reference: JER 1:15
Text: For, lo, I will call all the families of the kingdoms of the north, saith the LORD; and they shall come, and they shall set every one his throne at the entering of the gates of Jerusalem, and against all the walls thereof round about, and against all the cities of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8f0bea0-51fe-4f99-a921-61801df13bbd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: JER 1:16
Text: And I will utter my judgments against them touching all their wickedness, who have forsaken me, and have burned incense unto other gods, and worshipped the works of their own hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1510349-5217-4021-91a4-bcb93fb83526>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JER 1:17
Text: Thou therefore gird up thy loins, and arise, and speak unto them all that I command thee: be not dismayed at their faces, lest I confound thee before them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b368e80e-0a4c-49ef-891f-979a39199c28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: JER 1:18
Text: For, behold, I have made thee this day a defenced city, and an iron pillar, and brasen walls against the whole land, against the kings of Judah, against the princes thereof, against the priests thereof, and against the people of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36f46398-1426-40bc-bd74-68fe1b862a39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: JER 1:19
Text: And they shall fight against thee; but they shall not prevail against thee; for I am with thee, saith the LORD, to deliver thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a75c4580-25b5-48bf-9361-cdeff3ce2a8e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: JER 2:1
Text: Moreover the word of the LORD came to me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e58c2e6-d4c1-4013-bcd2-d1080dcbcba2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: JER 2:2
Text: Go and cry in the ears of Jerusalem, saying, Thus saith the LORD; I remember thee, the kindness of thy youth, the love of thine espousals, when thou wentest after me in the wilderness, in a land that was not sown.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aed94dbe-c7a9-43fb-a9c8-8f53b92abaee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: JER 2:3
Text: Israel was holiness unto the LORD, and the firstfruits of his increase: all that devour him shall offend; evil shall come upon them, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f779c340-fcc5-4af6-a27d-c58af4fdf801>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: JER 2:4
Text: Hear ye the word of the LORD, O house of Jacob, and all the families of the house of Israel:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67145d9b-76a1-4eab-8de9-bff30bc803dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: JER 2:5
Text: Thus saith the LORD, What iniquity have your fathers found in me, that they are gone far from me, and have walked after vanity, and are become vain?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf6f35f3-3508-4fa1-bf38-f9f280c78b05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 304

Reference: JER 2:6
Text: Neither said they, Where is the LORD that brought us up out of the land of Egypt, that led us through the wilderness, through a land of deserts and of pits, through a land of drought, and of the shadow of death, through a land that no man passed through, and where no man dwelt?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f76455f-dc3e-40a1-af53-88f22583a37f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: JER 2:7
Text: And I brought you into a plentiful country, to eat the fruit thereof and the goodness thereof; but when ye entered, ye defiled my land, and made mine heritage an abomination.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f924da4a-266d-4f4e-954c-1ff470d1c72b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: JER 2:8
Text: The priests said not, Where is the LORD? and they that handle the law knew me not: the pastors also transgressed against me, and the prophets prophesied by Baal, and walked after things that do not profit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8513501f-6449-456e-a8fd-750926f0a6ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: JER 2:9
Text: Wherefore I will yet plead with you, saith the LORD, and with your children’s children will I plead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc9081de-d5b8-4040-a0eb-e6ca46a7f700>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: JER 2:10
Text: For pass over the isles of Chittim, and see; and send unto Kedar, and consider diligently, and see if there be such a thing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7b00733-3967-4d19-aa93-43ee78daeb72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: JER 2:11
Text: Hath a nation changed their gods, which are yet no gods? but my people have changed their glory for that which doth not profit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9795386-57ef-4494-b954-16ad743ebe08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: JER 2:12
Text: Be astonished, O ye heavens, at this, and be horribly afraid, be ye very desolate, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:464484a0-9eb5-41ce-a073-e470a413bf89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: JER 2:13
Text: For my people have committed two evils; they have forsaken me the fountain of living waters, and hewed them out cisterns, broken cisterns, that can hold no water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:175f235b-307b-473b-bec5-c1b2bfb748f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: JER 2:14
Text: Is Israel a servant? is he a homeborn slave? why is he spoiled?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f1dd300-f5b4-4f0c-93a6-ade216cb3881>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: JER 2:15
Text: The young lions roared upon him, and yelled, and they made his land waste: his cities are burned without inhabitant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c0b8072-4803-4579-af84-389120046a8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: JER 2:16
Text: Also the children of Noph and Tahapanes have broken the crown of thy head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77d10601-ba04-45d9-9af5-8b434758ebac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: JER 2:17
Text: Hast thou not procured this unto thyself, in that thou hast forsaken the LORD thy God, when he led thee by the way?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb8c4f56-2333-431d-af85-4442c7321825>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: JER 2:18
Text: And now what hast thou to do in the way of Egypt, to drink the waters of Sihor? or what hast thou to do in the way of Assyria, to drink the waters of the river?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6854ac58-73df-45a0-a28f-ffe9ec893467>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: JER 2:19
Text: Thine own wickedness shall correct thee, and thy backslidings shall reprove thee: know therefore and see that it is an evil thing and bitter, that thou hast forsaken the LORD thy God, and that my fear is not in thee, saith the Lord GOD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb9c3816-a3bc-4a61-a6d3-37ceda2d4ff9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: JER 2:20
Text: For of old time I have broken thy yoke, and burst thy bands; and thou saidst, I will not transgress; when upon every high hill and under every green tree thou wanderest, playing the harlot.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae2127fa-7775-4a5c-b744-97586d1391ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: JER 2:21
Text: Yet I had planted thee a noble vine, wholly a right seed: how then art thou turned into the degenerate plant of a strange vine unto me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c09e64db-455a-4e8e-832a-c72a329ff413>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: JER 2:22
Text: For though thou wash thee with nitre, and take thee much soap, yet thine iniquity is marked before me, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01b419db-f661-4d27-ad71-cc5cf8aea724>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: JER 2:23
Text: How canst thou say, I am not polluted, I have not gone after Baalim? see thy way in the valley, know what thou hast done: thou art a swift dromedary traversing her ways;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fdcaef3a-458b-4f0a-b846-b2cd529e04c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: JER 2:24
Text: A wild ass used to the wilderness, that snuffeth up the wind at her pleasure; in her occasion who can turn her away? all they that seek her will not weary themselves; in her month they shall find her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5c1830a-e4f3-4e58-bf79-a0bac934bc68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: JER 2:25
Text: Withhold thy foot from being unshod, and thy throat from thirst: but thou saidst, There is no hope: no; for I have loved strangers, and after them will I go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75a656cf-d79f-4ce7-8673-1a3c1a22c374>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: JER 2:26
Text: As the thief is ashamed when he is found, so is the house of Israel ashamed; they, their kings, their princes, and their priests, and their prophets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a599ea17-8946-4298-b550-f020d992e534>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: JER 2:27
Text: Saying to a stock, Thou art my father; and to a stone, Thou hast brought me forth: for they have turned their back unto me, and not their face: but in the time of their trouble they will say, Arise, and save us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1c124a6-8f76-4cec-a32a-c029ff7f21bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: JER 2:28
Text: But where are thy gods that thou hast made thee? let them arise, if they can save thee in the time of thy trouble: for according to the number of thy cities are thy gods, O Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e47ba16-b614-4022-861c-9164bfc1dce8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: JER 2:29
Text: Wherefore will ye plead with me? ye all have transgressed against me, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c31d386a-7209-42bd-b26c-2cf011638da2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: JER 2:30
Text: In vain have I smitten your children; they received no correction: your own sword hath devoured your prophets, like a destroying lion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:124d1e25-ff2a-466f-a965-ca70d191612b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: JER 2:31
Text: O generation, see ye the word of the LORD. Have I been a wilderness unto Israel? a land of darkness? wherefore say my people, We are lords; we will come no more unto thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79e364f6-1020-4fae-97b1-a1104967f4a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: JER 2:32
Text: Can a maid forget her ornaments, or a bride her attire? yet my people have forgotten me days without number.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b09e37f-2cf7-4f3a-8c02-f6c4b3afe70c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: JER 2:33
Text: Why trimmest thou thy way to seek love? therefore hast thou also taught the wicked ones thy ways.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d09a7041-b40f-44a4-81df-b72d7fc189c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: JER 2:34
Text: Also in thy skirts is found the blood of the souls of the poor innocents: I have not found it by secret search, but upon all these.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98d17735-7965-4b0e-8a84-3e6b54c0c251>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: JER 2:35
Text: Yet thou sayest, Because I am innocent, surely his anger shall turn from me. Behold, I will plead with thee, because thou sayest, I have not sinned.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b39d457c-11f0-456c-9e8e-98095a40448e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: JER 2:36
Text: Why gaddest thou about so much to change thy way? thou also shalt be ashamed of Egypt, as thou wast ashamed of Assyria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/2/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78ad27c5-b88f-40b3-aa44-a8deea100708>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: JER 2:37
Text: Yea, thou shalt go forth from him, and thine hands upon thine head: for the LORD hath rejected thy confidences, and thou shalt not prosper in them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9fe4394-04cd-4264-8d10-a9a4b0fe3926>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: JER 3:1
Text: They say, If a man put away his wife, and she go from him, and become another man’s, shall he return unto her again? shall not that land be greatly polluted? but thou hast played the harlot with many lovers; yet return again to me, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9cc84b58-c18e-4c2d-824c-5d2c156f35fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: JER 3:2
Text: Lift up thine eyes unto the high places, and see where thou hast not been lien with. In the ways hast thou sat for them, as the Arabian in the wilderness; and thou hast polluted the land with thy whoredoms and with thy wickedness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d058186-0299-468d-bea6-9239eb00d6df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: JER 3:3
Text: Therefore the showers have been withholden, and there hath been no latter rain; and thou hadst a whore’s forehead, thou refusedst to be ashamed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5108f526-a9b2-49bc-b6c7-b65b9b02409d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: JER 3:4
Text: Wilt thou not from this time cry unto me, My father, thou art the guide of my youth?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4d902dc-74ba-40ec-8898-900bf60a8952>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: JER 3:5
Text: Will he reserve his anger for ever? will he keep it to the end? Behold, thou hast spoken and done evil things as thou couldest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebf4be18-9312-4b26-9998-79035efaf085>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: JER 3:6
Text: The LORD said also unto me in the days of Josiah the king, Hast thou seen that which backsliding Israel hath done? she is gone up upon every high mountain and under every green tree, and there hath played the harlot.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:654660a3-d566-42e6-8792-2f143d6abe03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: JER 3:7
Text: And I said after she had done all these things, Turn thou unto me. But she returned not. And her treacherous sister Judah saw it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9863f7c-1604-46e9-a8c5-76b1dce49ee4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: JER 3:8
Text: And I saw, when for all the causes whereby backsliding Israel committed adultery I had put her away, and given her a bill of divorce; yet her treacherous sister Judah feared not, but went and played the harlot also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:364efe05-7579-4015-a44d-09affc20896a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: JER 3:9
Text: And it came to pass through the lightness of her whoredom, that she defiled the land, and committed adultery with stones and with stocks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0fa9ca87-9971-42da-9ad5-f819b006b5ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: JER 3:10
Text: And yet for all this her treacherous sister Judah hath not turned unto me with her whole heart, but feignedly, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69236afc-3cb6-4f35-a747-7baae1f39547>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: JER 3:11
Text: And the LORD said unto me, The backsliding Israel hath justified herself more than treacherous Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8877feb-8a48-4ba2-9699-773648e81bef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: JER 3:12
Text: Go and proclaim these words toward the north, and say, Return, thou backsliding Israel, saith the LORD; and I will not cause mine anger to fall upon you: for I am merciful, saith the LORD, and I will not keep anger for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52006f11-4dff-45c2-b8bc-675e2040f6ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: JER 3:13
Text: Only acknowledge thine iniquity, that thou hast transgressed against the LORD thy God, and hast scattered thy ways to the strangers under every green tree, and ye have not obeyed my voice, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99dcff78-5513-4258-a556-a443afa54ff7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JER 3:14
Text: Turn, O backsliding children, saith the LORD; for I am married unto you: and I will take you one of a city, and two of a family, and I will bring you to Zion:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:397f588e-5355-4bd9-922f-ddc810a799bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: JER 3:15
Text: And I will give you pastors according to mine heart, which shall feed you with knowledge and understanding.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d2afceb-ff05-4f2e-9aac-15d688bc8758>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 323

Reference: JER 3:16
Text: And it shall come to pass, when ye be multiplied and increased in the land, in those days, saith the LORD, they shall say no more, The ark of the covenant of the LORD: neither shall it come to mind: neither shall they remember it; neither shall they visit it; neither shall that be done any more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8468cfd5-6d51-4206-a2ff-df1d7e59993b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: JER 3:17
Text: At that time they shall call Jerusalem the throne of the LORD; and all the nations shall be gathered unto it, to the name of the LORD, to Jerusalem: neither shall they walk any more after the imagination of their evil heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5484d58-2cf2-4e71-ad65-12d42adac891>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: JER 3:18
Text: In those days the house of Judah shall walk with the house of Israel, and they shall come together out of the land of the north to the land that I have given for an inheritance unto your fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a0cda81-6798-4cdf-8493-4a991f08ece8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: JER 3:19
Text: But I said, How shall I put thee among the children, and give thee a pleasant land, a goodly heritage of the hosts of nations? and I said, Thou shalt call me, My father; and shalt not turn away from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e517d934-3ef3-4808-be04-876299e39a7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: JER 3:20
Text: Surely as a wife treacherously departeth from her husband, so have ye dealt treacherously with me, O house of Israel, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1690ae48-6baa-40a5-ab65-3c4efa7c657c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: JER 3:21
Text: A voice was heard upon the high places, weeping and supplications of the children of Israel: for they have perverted their way, and they have forgotten the LORD their God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be2b8972-2849-4a16-b2d3-67004e956b92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: JER 3:22
Text: Return, ye backsliding children, and I will heal your backslidings. Behold, we come unto thee; for thou art the LORD our God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2525cd2-fc03-4aa8-b579-acb791842aa7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: JER 3:23
Text: Truly in vain is salvation hoped for from the hills, and from the multitude of mountains: truly in the LORD our God is the salvation of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a913035-254e-49bb-90b6-5548431f27e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: JER 3:24
Text: For shame hath devoured the labour of our fathers from our youth; their flocks and their herds, their sons and their daughters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/3/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf07893c-fe8f-43fa-942a-aded401cdf50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: JER 3:25
Text: We lie down in our shame, and our confusion covereth us: for we have sinned against the LORD our God, we and our fathers, from our youth even unto this day, and have not obeyed the voice of the LORD our God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59c04123-f14e-4b50-beac-1898cabd9af3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: JER 4:1
Text: If thou wilt return, O Israel, saith the LORD, return unto me: and if thou wilt put away thine abominations out of my sight, then shalt thou not remove.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1d6d542-3fee-4db6-af5f-442a6c44897f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JER 4:2
Text: And thou shalt swear, The LORD liveth, in truth, in judgment, and in righteousness; and the nations shall bless themselves in him, and in him shall they glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5423fbeb-fdbe-43b9-9bdc-1dfdbde3d1a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: JER 4:3
Text: For thus saith the LORD to the men of Judah and Jerusalem, Break up your fallow ground, and sow not among thorns.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50338cda-b71c-43c8-b51b-51c3aca6faf4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: JER 4:4
Text: Circumcise yourselves to the LORD, and take away the foreskins of your heart, ye men of Judah and inhabitants of Jerusalem: lest my fury come forth like fire, and burn that none can quench it, because of the evil of your doings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e5efcea-0ccc-4a9d-9086-edfa46d802f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: JER 4:5
Text: Declare ye in Judah, and publish in Jerusalem; and say, Blow ye the trumpet in the land: cry, gather together, and say, Assemble yourselves, and let us go into the defenced cities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fed0bf2f-3456-4e37-b18f-7c7897992f30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: JER 4:6
Text: Set up the standard toward Zion: retire, stay not: for I will bring evil from the north, and a great destruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfd3041f-080d-49d1-89a7-2e9ff262cbbb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: JER 4:7
Text: The lion is come up from his thicket, and the destroyer of the Gentiles is on his way; he is gone forth from his place to make thy land desolate; and thy cities shall be laid waste, without an inhabitant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aea75910-8079-4072-8b77-20c93e95e8ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: JER 4:8
Text: For this gird you with sackcloth, lament and howl: for the fierce anger of the LORD is not turned back from us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7556ec8f-8064-41fd-a535-a6ed432e4de3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: JER 4:9
Text: And it shall come to pass at that day, saith the LORD, that the heart of the king shall perish, and the heart of the princes; and the priests shall be astonished, and the prophets shall wonder.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbb1e99f-a5c4-46cf-94af-c348fe185706>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JER 4:10
Text: Then said I, Ah, Lord GOD! surely thou hast greatly deceived this people and Jerusalem, saying, Ye shall have peace; whereas the sword reacheth unto the soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10137820-323f-4ec5-90f8-66491b0f438d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: JER 4:11
Text: At that time shall it be said to this people and to Jerusalem, A dry wind of the high places in the wilderness toward the daughter of my people, not to fan, nor to cleanse,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b773b9c-2457-4021-a4f5-2d659fde0595>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: JER 4:12
Text: Even a full wind from those places shall come unto me: now also will I give sentence against them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e042817-3361-4a15-a9c3-f193c01384a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: JER 4:13
Text: Behold, he shall come up as clouds, and his chariots shall be as a whirlwind: his horses are swifter than eagles. Woe unto us! for we are spoiled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c724960-66a8-4721-a2dc-a4cad993c63a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: JER 4:14
Text: O Jerusalem, wash thine heart from wickedness, that thou mayest be saved. How long shall thy vain thoughts lodge within thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9c9659f-9da1-468d-94f6-280a5198c145>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: JER 4:15
Text: For a voice declareth from Dan, and publisheth affliction from mount Ephraim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41c3e775-aa2a-4e60-9b1f-5cbb8910e612>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: JER 4:16
Text: Make ye mention to the nations; behold, publish against Jerusalem, that watchers come from a far country, and give out their voice against the cities of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0c74d5f-ca10-443f-9c33-fcc436467750>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: JER 4:17
Text: As keepers of a field, are they against her round about; because she hath been rebellious against me, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5d0aabf-bb7a-4a43-8b69-2e972349e21e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: JER 4:18
Text: Thy way and thy doings have procured these things unto thee; this is thy wickedness, because it is bitter, because it reacheth unto thine heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed72c8c9-4e9f-4d58-be49-f80db263f027>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: JER 4:19
Text: My bowels, my bowels! I am pained at my very heart; my heart maketh a noise in me; I cannot hold my peace, because thou hast heard, O my soul, the sound of the trumpet, the alarm of war.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7630baed-9bf8-47f5-955d-0a872ba5df8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: JER 4:20
Text: Destruction upon destruction is cried; for the whole land is spoiled: suddenly are my tents spoiled, and my curtains in a moment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9eba0d6a-ed34-4b2b-b62b-ff7de7f4280f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: JER 4:21
Text: How long shall I see the standard, and hear the sound of the trumpet?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5b00138-c521-4d11-826b-f2374de9679b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: JER 4:22
Text: For my people is foolish, they have not known me; they are sottish children, and they have none understanding: they are wise to do evil, but to do good they have no knowledge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca33bedf-2f2f-4126-9608-fffe98cf45ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: JER 4:23
Text: I beheld the earth, and, lo, it was without form, and void; and the heavens, and they had no light.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5fd3280-755c-4885-b697-49a29e8287fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: JER 4:24
Text: I beheld the mountains, and, lo, they trembled, and all the hills moved lightly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69eba23e-5dca-419c-ac32-e9a94559f847>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: JER 4:25
Text: I beheld, and, lo, there was no man, and all the birds of the heavens were fled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:360e5315-24c3-4b33-a67d-66c30d60b551>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: JER 4:26
Text: I beheld, and, lo, the fruitful place was a wilderness, and all the cities thereof were broken down at the presence of the LORD, and by his fierce anger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0fb7d301-a7d4-4ece-b3b5-e74d3dbcdc9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: JER 4:27
Text: For thus hath the LORD said, The whole land shall be desolate; yet will I not make a full end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbd21b61-9a06-4038-a87a-4575b9f09bbb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: JER 4:28
Text: For this shall the earth mourn, and the heavens above be black; because I have spoken it, I have purposed it, and will not repent, neither will I turn back from it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d25c2905-4597-446c-9742-b79679f21026>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: JER 4:29
Text: The whole city shall flee for the noise of the horsemen and bowmen; they shall go into thickets, and climb up upon the rocks: every city shall be forsaken, and not a man dwell therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6996367f-8c94-46cb-8cc5-7e4f08018b99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 301

Reference: JER 4:30
Text: And when thou art spoiled, what wilt thou do? Though thou clothest thyself with crimson, though thou deckest thee with ornaments of gold, though thou rentest thy face with painting, in vain shalt thou make thyself fair; thy lovers will despise thee, they will seek thy life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/4/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc39905a-48fd-4cf4-87c3-5e7652d41fa8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 293

Reference: JER 4:31
Text: For I have heard a voice as of a woman in travail, and the anguish as of her that bringeth forth her first child, the voice of the daughter of Zion, that bewaileth herself, that spreadeth her hands, saying, Woe is me now! for my soul is wearied because of murderers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfd90332-8797-4cfe-a690-8b36f13e7efb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: JER 5:1
Text: Run ye to and fro through the streets of Jerusalem, and see now, and know, and seek in the broad places thereof, if ye can find a man, if there be any that executeth judgment, that seeketh the truth; and I will pardon it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ba4762e-5979-4207-b360-f96640f56ecb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: JER 5:2
Text: And though they say, The LORD liveth; surely they swear falsely.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79885aeb-0823-4a49-8f6d-3104a0ef1923>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 266

Reference: JER 5:3
Text: O LORD, are not thine eyes upon the truth? thou hast stricken them, but they have not grieved; thou hast consumed them, but they have refused to receive correction: they have made their faces harder than a rock; they have refused to return.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd8cf8cf-bc89-4f58-bb8e-0c94a764d100>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: JER 5:4
Text: Therefore I said, Surely these are poor; they are foolish: for they know not the way of the LORD, nor the judgment of their God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a62bd285-0dde-42d7-acd6-296917533c04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: JER 5:5
Text: I will get me unto the great men, and will speak unto them; for they have known the way of the LORD, and the judgment of their God: but these have altogether broken the yoke, and burst the bonds.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38007b54-630d-489f-a37d-d2eed705af4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 297

Reference: JER 5:6
Text: Wherefore a lion out of the forest shall slay them, and a wolf of the evenings shall spoil them, a leopard shall watch over their cities: every one that goeth out thence shall be torn in pieces: because their transgressions are many, and their backslidings are increased.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a784a906-7f8c-4128-9040-b73169636f6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: JER 5:7
Text: How shall I pardon thee for this? thy children have forsaken me, and sworn by them that are no gods: when I had fed them to the full, they then committed adultery, and assembled themselves by troops in the harlots’ houses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:777b0d96-e40e-4da8-bc6d-294aae88a716>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: JER 5:8
Text: They were as fed horses in the morning: every one neighed after his neighbour’s wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c4a6c8f-8f3b-4f6e-acbf-179cdb9cf1cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: JER 5:9
Text: Shall I not visit for these things? saith the LORD: and shall not my soul be avenged on such a nation as this?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94839477-d1ce-45f5-b538-88116212ba2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: JER 5:10
Text: Go ye up upon her walls, and destroy; but make not a full end: take away her battlements; for they are not the LORD’s.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89287fe4-08c3-4804-b716-50e1c29c6fbe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: JER 5:11
Text: For the house of Israel and the house of Judah have dealt very treacherously against me, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f27cf78a-befb-4007-873b-08d26bf32e12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: JER 5:12
Text: They have belied the LORD, and said, It is not he; neither shall evil come upon us; neither shall we see sword nor famine:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a90048df-782a-4990-b209-a741e507309a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: JER 5:13
Text: And the prophets shall become wind, and the word is not in them: thus shall it be done unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7016a845-5a9a-404e-a33b-9ac02b5838d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: JER 5:14
Text: Wherefore thus saith the LORD God of hosts, Because ye speak this word, behold, I will make my words in thy mouth fire, and this people wood, and it shall devour them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7feeaf0c-4db8-4fa7-a3f9-633d8b326c83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: JER 5:15
Text: Lo, I will bring a nation upon you from far, O house of Israel, saith the LORD: it is a mighty nation, it is an ancient nation, a nation whose language thou knowest not, neither understandest what they say.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d5f27ef-1550-4a2a-bc7a-17bd408e82f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: JER 5:16
Text: Their quiver is as an open sepulchre, they are all mighty men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fcfe26bb-8afd-4306-816d-ee4a05d6fddd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 297

Reference: JER 5:17
Text: And they shall eat up thine harvest, and thy bread, which thy sons and thy daughters should eat: they shall eat up thy flocks and thine herds: they shall eat up thy vines and thy fig trees: they shall impoverish thy fenced cities, wherein thou trustedst, with the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65efd561-346e-40e5-9ce1-d78153fd2bdb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: JER 5:18
Text: Nevertheless in those days, saith the LORD, I will not make a full end with you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d30844ad-08d1-4f85-ad4c-a1eebd01bc10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: JER 5:19
Text: And it shall come to pass, when ye shall say, Wherefore doeth the LORD our God all these things unto us? then shalt thou answer them, Like as ye have forsaken me, and served strange gods in your land, so shall ye serve strangers in a land that is not yours.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fcdb494-c634-4f0e-8088-20003261cefd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: JER 5:20
Text: Declare this in the house of Jacob, and publish it in Judah, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16d80132-c0bd-4316-812e-21a9789c88c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: JER 5:21
Text: Hear now this, O foolish people, and without understanding; which have eyes, and see not; which have ears, and hear not:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4768486-2fed-4c0e-a183-fd8a877cad52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 314

Reference: JER 5:22
Text: Fear ye not me? saith the LORD: will ye not tremble at my presence, which have placed the sand for the bound of the sea by a perpetual decree, that it cannot pass it: and though the waves thereof toss themselves, yet can they not prevail; though they roar, yet can they not pass over it?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbca6abc-9594-4475-94c0-fcbfbac61171>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: JER 5:23
Text: But this people hath a revolting and a rebellious heart; they are revolted and gone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a32a1ecf-841c-4166-8b76-0b1ed64d10e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: JER 5:24
Text: Neither say they in their heart, Let us now fear the LORD our God, that giveth rain, both the former and the latter, in his season: he reserveth unto us the appointed weeks of the harvest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:532ff8c6-e65d-4b65-82f8-79de8212dd3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: JER 5:25
Text: Your iniquities have turned away these things, and your sins have withholden good things from you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f464bea-88bd-4229-86e3-3ebd0e414bc5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: JER 5:26
Text: For among my people are found wicked men: they lay wait, as he that setteth snares; they set a trap, they catch men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4f3cccb-cbb6-4e4f-b7f0-d8f8a5e043a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: JER 5:27
Text: As a cage is full of birds, so are their houses full of deceit: therefore they are become great, and waxen rich.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98395a7a-401f-4d36-8d61-e1fe38203afb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: JER 5:28
Text: They are waxen fat, they shine: yea, they overpass the deeds of the wicked: they judge not the cause, the cause of the fatherless, yet they prosper; and the right of the needy do they not judge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df2478b2-d87a-4559-841c-ba59f3426cca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: JER 5:29
Text: Shall I not visit for these things? saith the LORD: shall not my soul be avenged on such a nation as this?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df44c4d6-9535-4e86-8880-010fd0641d64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: JER 5:30
Text: A wonderful and horrible thing is committed in the land;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/5/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:215320e2-d115-48b8-9df8-79001e106e13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: JER 5:31
Text: The prophets prophesy falsely, and the priests bear rule by their means; and my people love to have it so: and what will ye do in the end thereof?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c9ad078-18df-44e2-892d-8b578ebc0711>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: JER 6:1
Text: O ye children of Benjamin, gather yourselves to flee out of the midst of Jerusalem, and blow the trumpet in Tekoa, and set up a sign of fire in Bethhaccerem: for evil appeareth out of the north, and great destruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05fe4759-28bb-4b00-989c-c62bb560c9c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: JER 6:2
Text: I have likened the daughter of Zion to a comely and delicate woman.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b9f927c-81ac-4dbb-a238-2c2b7dee11bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: JER 6:3
Text: The shepherds with their flocks shall come unto her; they shall pitch their tents against her round about; they shall feed every one in his place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3c5ad3e-d586-4de9-a3e4-ebc0e87ec460>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: JER 6:4
Text: Prepare ye war against her; arise, and let us go up at noon. Woe unto us! for the day goeth away, for the shadows of the evening are stretched out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31ab5cf2-ef23-41f0-a006-007cd4b78960>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: JER 6:5
Text: Arise, and let us go by night, and let us destroy her palaces.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af13dbce-ba3f-4578-9528-2a6ab908e21d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: JER 6:6
Text: For thus hath the LORD of hosts said, Hew ye down trees, and cast a mount against Jerusalem: this is the city to be visited; she is wholly oppression in the midst of her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71a0f735-b235-4983-9efa-a1289770d1e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: JER 6:7
Text: As a fountain casteth out her waters, so she casteth out her wickedness: violence and spoil is heard in her; before me continually is grief and wounds.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40aa710c-804f-441e-b119-08ed7bb0b2bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: JER 6:8
Text: Be thou instructed, O Jerusalem, lest my soul depart from thee; lest I make thee desolate, a land not inhabited.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f251c70b-d32f-4d62-9de1-9405321dc2ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: JER 6:9
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts, They shall throughly glean the remnant of Israel as a vine: turn back thine hand as a grapegatherer into the baskets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b10d8a56-2fec-4c50-8b87-236cad5b6f15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: JER 6:10
Text: To whom shall I speak, and give warning, that they may hear? behold, their ear is uncircumcised, and they cannot hearken: behold, the word of the LORD is unto them a reproach; they have no delight in it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c84c292a-f557-4038-9b49-6ce9137b206b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 280

Reference: JER 6:11
Text: Therefore I am full of the fury of the LORD; I am weary with holding in: I will pour it out upon the children abroad, and upon the assembly of young men together: for even the husband with the wife shall be taken, the aged with him that is full of days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62bb7b9f-596a-4648-8d9e-e0c2491dc814>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: JER 6:12
Text: And their houses shall be turned unto others, with their fields and wives together: for I will stretch out my hand upon the inhabitants of the land, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53479b6c-8c56-40b7-95f4-4d5ce64eddd3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: JER 6:13
Text: For from the least of them even unto the greatest of them every one is given to covetousness; and from the prophet even unto the priest every one dealeth falsely.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4b8ffb2-a9b5-4754-8bca-74157c43a0a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: JER 6:14
Text: They have healed also the hurt of the daughter of my people slightly, saying, Peace, peace; when there is no peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b642cdbb-08c5-433d-8c29-fa91bb09a66f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: JER 6:15
Text: Were they ashamed when they had committed abomination? nay, they were not at all ashamed, neither could they blush: therefore they shall fall among them that fall: at the time that I visit them they shall be cast down, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d0fdcab-e02c-47cb-aecf-7d288178baab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: JER 6:16
Text: Thus saith the LORD, Stand ye in the ways, and see, and ask for the old paths, where is the good way, and walk therein, and ye shall find rest for your souls. But they said, We will not walk therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7302fdba-befa-4af6-afca-86b69d3e7863>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: JER 6:17
Text: Also I set watchmen over you, saying, Hearken to the sound of the trumpet. But they said, We will not hearken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db261b45-0ee1-4d54-8884-3338617f9787>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: JER 6:18
Text: Therefore hear, ye nations, and know, O congregation, what is among them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf7b5064-3deb-4d4b-b173-2a48b475228a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: JER 6:19
Text: Hear, O earth: behold, I will bring evil upon this people, even the fruit of their thoughts, because they have not hearkened unto my words, nor to my law, but rejected it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b81ed2e-5d4a-41c5-aaf5-6f4095fcde62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: JER 6:20
Text: To what purpose cometh there to me incense from Sheba, and the sweet cane from a far country? your burnt offerings are not acceptable, nor your sacrifices sweet unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9aa9db36-4184-4614-bf2b-53549abc2450>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: JER 6:21
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD, Behold, I will lay stumblingblocks before this people, and the fathers and the sons together shall fall upon them; the neighbour and his friend shall perish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f354d68-9855-41b4-8c82-6ffd159f69f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: JER 6:22
Text: Thus saith the LORD, Behold, a people cometh from the north country, and a great nation shall be raised from the sides of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c726859-c96e-4fb6-abd1-cb6004888644>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: JER 6:23
Text: They shall lay hold on bow and spear; they are cruel, and have no mercy; their voice roareth like the sea; and they ride upon horses, set in array as men for war against thee, O daughter of Zion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec86d60b-d3c4-4771-b605-b0f35cd689f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: JER 6:24
Text: We have heard the fame thereof: our hands wax feeble: anguish hath taken hold of us, and pain, as of a woman in travail.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36592041-61a8-429c-bb53-e6900520013b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: JER 6:25
Text: Go not forth into the field, nor walk by the way; for the sword of the enemy and fear is on every side.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:044c08ca-0c97-43c2-8220-273f5d87ed3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: JER 6:26
Text: O daughter of my people, gird thee with sackcloth, and wallow thyself in ashes: make thee mourning, as for an only son, most bitter lamentation: for the spoiler shall suddenly come upon us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bdbdbda6-df32-4b69-8305-cd664d4c9123>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: JER 6:27
Text: I have set thee for a tower and a fortress among my people, that thou mayest know and try their way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41ced15c-d3ec-4aa2-a81b-44e29f571097>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: JER 6:28
Text: They are all grievous revolters, walking with slanders: they are brass and iron; they are all corrupters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33222580-13d8-4fdd-9288-ae2c0ac0f5d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: JER 6:29
Text: The bellows are burned, the lead is consumed of the fire; the founder melteth in vain: for the wicked are not plucked away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/6/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bea2ef87-2869-4fb9-9ccc-87c89256c8da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: JER 6:30
Text: Reprobate silver shall men call them, because the LORD hath rejected them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e23e3c4-c399-413b-ab30-2e84c016b136>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: JER 7:1
Text: The word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eac372ec-fc6b-4568-82b1-8a66aeaf218a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: JER 7:2
Text: Stand in the gate of the LORD’s house, and proclaim there this word, and say, Hear the word of the LORD, all ye of Judah, that enter in at these gates to worship the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ff02e49-5276-4d62-9e7e-ea73594be4be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: JER 7:3
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, Amend your ways and your doings, and I will cause you to dwell in this place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9963aba9-d7d1-4399-bc30-5a12177f650f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: JER 7:4
Text: Trust ye not in lying words, saying, The temple of the LORD, The temple of the LORD, The temple of the LORD, are these.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4e36b26-0e0d-44fc-91c0-44236b311f05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: JER 7:5
Text: For if ye throughly amend your ways and your doings; if ye throughly execute judgment between a man and his neighbour;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6d1480b-1089-4aa7-9ddf-5c9667c2870f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: JER 7:6
Text: If ye oppress not the stranger, the fatherless, and the widow, and shed not innocent blood in this place, neither walk after other gods to your hurt:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2759a3f-f076-4448-b422-3dd4f1b0b942>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: JER 7:7
Text: Then will I cause you to dwell in this place, in the land that I gave to your fathers, for ever and ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff90ea62-0040-48db-8a1f-53fde893598d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: JER 7:8
Text: Behold, ye trust in lying words, that cannot profit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34db0974-137e-4f14-a30a-bdd0ced3afce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: JER 7:9
Text: Will ye steal, murder, and commit adultery, and swear falsely, and burn incense unto Baal, and walk after other gods whom ye know not;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47bee3a2-759f-4f8e-9617-08032b506f58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: JER 7:10
Text: And come and stand before me in this house, which is called by my name, and say, We are delivered to do all these abominations?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:851ad89a-890c-473d-94cf-1e611057a54a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: JER 7:11
Text: Is this house, which is called by my name, become a den of robbers in your eyes? Behold, even I have seen it, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f97c4c6b-3363-4fb9-b56b-cc5d1d7348a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: JER 7:12
Text: But go ye now unto my place which was in Shiloh, where I set my name at the first, and see what I did to it for the wickedness of my people Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:680a567f-09ac-4b7d-9f8a-c6ea8be58b59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: JER 7:13
Text: And now, because ye have done all these works, saith the LORD, and I spake unto you, rising up early and speaking, but ye heard not; and I called you, but ye answered not;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:800b0011-6ba5-4ffc-81a2-93b1cb8aa808>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: JER 7:14
Text: Therefore will I do unto this house, which is called by my name, wherein ye trust, and unto the place which I gave to you and to your fathers, as I have done to Shiloh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a6871d6-d7bc-4c5c-9e19-3d7742f3e808>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: JER 7:15
Text: And I will cast you out of my sight, as I have cast out all your brethren, even the whole seed of Ephraim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c102bac3-3ba9-40be-a6d4-22156b49400a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: JER 7:16
Text: Therefore pray not thou for this people, neither lift up cry nor prayer for them, neither make intercession to me: for I will not hear thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f68a1998-5f52-475f-996d-1e7235f1e800>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: JER 7:17
Text: Seest thou not what they do in the cities of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0fb2de40-e645-414b-92be-6709d92eb7db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: JER 7:18
Text: The children gather wood, and the fathers kindle the fire, and the women knead their dough, to make cakes to the queen of heaven, and to pour out drink offerings unto other gods, that they may provoke me to anger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9a267af-b582-4c4e-8c96-831519f11b7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: JER 7:19
Text: Do they provoke me to anger? saith the LORD: do they not provoke themselves to the confusion of their own faces?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fcfd2510-6a4e-4d27-a4d9-bdae8f597d86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: JER 7:20
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, mine anger and my fury shall be poured out upon this place, upon man, and upon beast, and upon the trees of the field, and upon the fruit of the ground; and it shall burn, and shall not be quenched.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eaa8304c-4f8b-420c-bb7e-d6e039a6789b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: JER 7:21
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Put your burnt offerings unto your sacrifices, and eat flesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf7c9f0e-c7bb-448b-be79-20b6d390b13f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: JER 7:22
Text: For I spake not unto your fathers, nor commanded them in the day that I brought them out of the land of Egypt, concerning burnt offerings or sacrifices:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfe1a636-ca4f-4fbf-965d-ee4f4b8cd3d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: JER 7:23
Text: But this thing commanded I them, saying, Obey my voice, and I will be your God, and ye shall be my people: and walk ye in all the ways that I have commanded you, that it may be well unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4d8b584-3f60-4294-953b-a1166cb9908c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: JER 7:24
Text: But they hearkened not, nor inclined their ear, but walked in the counsels and in the imagination of their evil heart, and went backward, and not forward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58922acb-df53-4e2b-856e-dfe99621b06c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: JER 7:25
Text: Since the day that your fathers came forth out of the land of Egypt unto this day I have even sent unto you all my servants the prophets, daily rising up early and sending them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2498d50-64f4-4481-b214-2f26a47bb9e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: JER 7:26
Text: Yet they hearkened not unto me, nor inclined their ear, but hardened their neck: they did worse than their fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51c15adf-b3a2-4d65-aeb7-f9fa8901b037>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: JER 7:27
Text: Therefore thou shalt speak all these words unto them; but they will not hearken to thee: thou shalt also call unto them; but they will not answer thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a5c3138-680f-414e-9bc1-04079b4c0383>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: JER 7:28
Text: But thou shalt say unto them, This is a nation that obeyeth not the voice of the LORD their God, nor receiveth correction: truth is perished, and is cut off from their mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4def0a2-5b93-44ab-9e49-987654bb4026>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: JER 7:29
Text: Cut off thine hair, O Jerusalem, and cast it away, and take up a lamentation on high places; for the LORD hath rejected and forsaken the generation of his wrath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9009e2e3-416d-4629-ae15-4d6e7b6f3513>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JER 7:30
Text: For the children of Judah have done evil in my sight, saith the LORD: they have set their abominations in the house which is called by my name, to pollute it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc5b70fc-8a32-4e18-b1ba-79e3aeeeb132>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: JER 7:31
Text: And they have built the high places of Tophet, which is in the valley of the son of Hinnom, to burn their sons and their daughters in the fire; which I commanded them not, neither came it into my heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea595bc4-f43d-4e6e-a745-427b569abf80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: JER 7:32
Text: Therefore, behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that it shall no more be called Tophet, nor the valley of the son of Hinnom, but the valley of slaughter: for they shall bury in Tophet, till there be no place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e0a7b14-3bb2-4ed9-b9f5-ce3d88dda8ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: JER 7:33
Text: And the carcases of this people shall be meat for the fowls of the heaven, and for the beasts of the earth; and none shall fray them away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/7/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4435199-6b5e-4478-8cb0-47af01b15eec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: JER 7:34
Text: Then will I cause to cease from the cities of Judah, and from the streets of Jerusalem, the voice of mirth, and the voice of gladness, the voice of the bridegroom, and the voice of the bride: for the land shall be desolate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/8/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d569bc0-6f9f-45f5-8ebe-085310a54527>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: JER 8:1
Text: At that time, saith the LORD, they shall bring out the bones of the kings of Judah, and the bones of his princes, and the bones of the priests, and the bones of the prophets, and the bones of the inhabitants of Jerusalem, out of their graves:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/8/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c1b2b3d-8e85-4430-bf8f-f3bce9c9fa7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 344

Reference: JER 8:2
Text: And they shall spread them before the sun, and the moon, and all the host of heaven, whom they have loved, and whom they have served, and after whom they have walked, and whom they have sought, and whom they have worshipped: they shall not be gathered, nor be buried; they shall be for dung upon the face of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/8/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3bb0d394-c420-4f2c-a54f-8421f846970d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: JER 8:3
Text: And death shall be chosen rather than life by all the residue of them that remain of this evil family, which remain in all the places whither I have driven them, saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/8/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0407530-6fc5-451c-9cba-6e76b45e3bed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: JER 8:4
Text: Moreover thou shalt say unto them, Thus saith the LORD; Shall they fall, and not arise? shall he turn away, and not return?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/8/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b649a54d-1837-488b-8ebe-15c607c98e86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: JER 8:5
Text: Why then is this people of Jerusalem slidden back by a perpetual backsliding? they hold fast deceit, they refuse to return.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/8/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:910dbb24-f2a6-46c4-96eb-7dd3c266bfc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: JER 8:6
Text: I hearkened and heard, but they spake not aright: no man repented him of his wickedness, saying, What have I done? every one turned to his course, as the horse rusheth into the battle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/8/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:727a05f9-9d50-4bb6-93c8-f0c558686fbd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: JER 8:7
Text: Yea, the stork in the heaven knoweth her appointed times; and the turtle and the crane and the swallow observe the time of their coming; but my people know not the judgment of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/8/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f29a3d0-0f76-4267-9300-c17c291b955e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: JER 8:8
Text: How do ye say, We are wise, and the law of the LORD is with us? Lo, certainly in vain made he it; the pen of the scribes is in vain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/8/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b4ca6d0-9801-45b3-9b9c-cb07f00a4a28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: JER 8:9
Text: The wise men are ashamed, they are dismayed and taken: lo, they have rejected the word of the LORD; and what wisdom is in them?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/8/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3b522da-d33f-42d5-96f4-4e0af58c3a30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 266

Reference: JER 8:10
Text: Therefore will I give their wives unto others, and their fields to them that shall inherit them: for every one from the least even unto the greatest is given to covetousness, from the prophet even unto the priest every one dealeth falsely.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/8/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3adfadef-ada3-423d-85cf-9883fd3e4bed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: JER 8:11
Text: For they have healed the hurt of the daughter of my people slightly, saying, Peace, peace; when there is no peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/8/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56f3f04b-4490-425f-ab58-0b91a3ab9a5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: JER 8:12
Text: Were they ashamed when they had committed abomination? nay, they were not at all ashamed, neither could they blush: therefore shall they fall among them that fall: in the time of their visitation they shall be cast down, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/8/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:250912fd-8d72-4aa2-8153-f69f75843df9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: JER 8:13
Text: I will surely consume them, saith the LORD: there shall be no grapes on the vine, nor figs on the fig tree, and the leaf shall fade; and the things that I have given them shall pass away from them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/8/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ad93e51-44b1-4ee2-9f69-8c4208ea6661>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 262

Reference: JER 8:14
Text: Why do we sit still? assemble yourselves, and let us enter into the defenced cities, and let us be silent there: for the LORD our God hath put us to silence, and given us water of gall to drink, because we have sinned against the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/8/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:232aef98-13f3-4d6e-b7fd-d1b383720a2b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: JER 8:15
Text: We looked for peace, but no good came; and for a time of health, and behold trouble!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/8/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d00403a6-cd73-4e87-b012-7561f19574b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: JER 8:16
Text: The snorting of his horses was heard from Dan: the whole land trembled at the sound of the neighing of his strong ones; for they are come, and have devoured the land, and all that is in it; the city, and those that dwell therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/8/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27d69c96-8152-47e1-ad26-45370e573b00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: JER 8:17
Text: For, behold, I will send serpents, cockatrices, among you, which will not be charmed, and they shall bite you, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/8/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09847227-f45d-489e-878e-c384b2bfa9c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: JER 8:18
Text: When I would comfort myself against sorrow, my heart is faint in me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/8/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9af848c7-7128-408d-b4a0-681d78bc967a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: JER 8:19
Text: Behold the voice of the cry of the daughter of my people because of them that dwell in a far country: Is not the LORD in Zion? is not her king in her? Why have they provoked me to anger with their graven images, and with strange vanities?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/8/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea62996c-48c7-4c0a-9971-ffdead5083cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: JER 8:20
Text: The harvest is past, the summer is ended, and we are not saved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/8/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df60cea8-4dc9-4237-94fe-9ba028622fdc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: JER 8:21
Text: For the hurt of the daughter of my people am I hurt; I am black; astonishment hath taken hold on me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/8/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2b3d417-90bf-4464-b835-4393c152ae46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: JER 8:22
Text: Is there no balm in Gilead; is there no physician there? why then is not the health of the daughter of my people recovered?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07f844b3-7977-47be-a5d5-c6c455b8572b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: JER 9:1
Text: Oh that my head were waters, and mine eyes a fountain of tears, that I might weep day and night for the slain of the daughter of my people!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3262df10-07a5-43c4-beec-05181e89a155>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: JER 9:2
Text: Oh that I had in the wilderness a lodging place of wayfaring men; that I might leave my people, and go from them! for they be all adulterers, an assembly of treacherous men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5b34883-95ce-40a5-a955-83f63e9246a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: JER 9:3
Text: And they bend their tongues like their bow for lies: but they are not valiant for the truth upon the earth; for they proceed from evil to evil, and they know not me, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c7dd0e6-0d6d-4a93-b43a-619604ba88b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JER 9:4
Text: Take ye heed every one of his neighbour, and trust ye not in any brother: for every brother will utterly supplant, and every neighbour will walk with slanders.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a24cad40-b0be-460f-b263-c5696bd8005f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: JER 9:5
Text: And they will deceive every one his neighbour, and will not speak the truth: they have taught their tongue to speak lies, and weary themselves to commit iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79b0d6e0-fec7-4cd2-8595-f0ad23fd0d85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: JER 9:6
Text: Thine habitation is in the midst of deceit; through deceit they refuse to know me, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f727fd99-cda1-4fe1-ae5e-2942aad1d11d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: JER 9:7
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD of hosts, Behold, I will melt them, and try them; for how shall I do for the daughter of my people?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35d31337-c330-4e6b-82a0-c679837f1a26>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: JER 9:8
Text: Their tongue is as an arrow shot out; it speaketh deceit: one speaketh peaceably to his neighbour with his mouth, but in heart he layeth his wait.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71cef59f-b4e7-418f-b56c-6c4d5f6e0576>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: JER 9:9
Text: Shall I not visit them for these things? saith the LORD: shall not my soul be avenged on such a nation as this?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e0bf531-36f5-47f4-8dbd-7328ea99448f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 317

Reference: JER 9:10
Text: For the mountains will I take up a weeping and wailing, and for the habitations of the wilderness a lamentation, because they are burned up, so that none can pass through them; neither can men hear the voice of the cattle; both the fowl of the heavens and the beast are fled; they are gone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:add8bae1-f202-4b37-ad64-d9bb36b54689>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: JER 9:11
Text: And I will make Jerusalem heaps, and a den of dragons; and I will make the cities of Judah desolate, without an inhabitant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b467c450-8c6d-4dc9-9d37-9945144408ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: JER 9:12
Text: Who is the wise man, that may understand this? and who is he to whom the mouth of the LORD hath spoken, that he may declare it, for what the land perisheth and is burned up like a wilderness, that none passeth through?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:858132ac-51a3-4b92-8435-8a68112e838d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: JER 9:13
Text: And the LORD saith, Because they have forsaken my law which I set before them, and have not obeyed my voice, neither walked therein;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e00f420f-cb49-4523-ab9d-e9f943ec3c0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: JER 9:14
Text: But have walked after the imagination of their own heart, and after Baalim, which their fathers taught them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f33348ec-9f6b-4e3d-b9a0-c46549464dc8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JER 9:15
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Behold, I will feed them, even this people, with wormwood, and give them water of gall to drink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d7fb8ca-f033-464c-8251-de5037e2ee64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: JER 9:16
Text: I will scatter them also among the heathen, whom neither they nor their fathers have known: and I will send a sword after them, till I have consumed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b4f384e-1591-4347-86fe-dcd19c0d8c89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: JER 9:17
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts, Consider ye, and call for the mourning women, that they may come; and send for cunning women, that they may come:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fffa543-22ce-44ac-897f-cc05b9c7e5c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: JER 9:18
Text: And let them make haste, and take up a wailing for us, that our eyes may run down with tears, and our eyelids gush out with waters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6154904f-dc1a-4d3d-9889-fa3abd4697f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: JER 9:19
Text: For a voice of wailing is heard out of Zion, How are we spoiled! we are greatly confounded, because we have forsaken the land, because our dwellings have cast us out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6115c072-a844-46db-a109-76b7cc76164a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: JER 9:20
Text: Yet hear the word of the LORD, O ye women, and let your ear receive the word of his mouth, and teach your daughters wailing, and every one her neighbour lamentation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:032cf624-000f-4871-bbdc-b79d53ccb883>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: JER 9:21
Text: For death is come up into our windows, and is entered into our palaces, to cut off the children from without, and the young men from the streets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b580323e-b900-4128-be55-460b094dfa6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: JER 9:22
Text: Speak, Thus saith the LORD, Even the carcases of men shall fall as dung upon the open field, and as the handful after the harvestman, and none shall gather them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bce8d601-8428-4fe9-8cc1-d5c3f822d6ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: JER 9:23
Text: Thus saith the LORD, Let not the wise man glory in his wisdom, neither let the mighty man glory in his might, let not the rich man glory in his riches:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23b38be1-364b-42f8-a30a-a3560d0f9139>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: JER 9:24
Text: But let him that glorieth glory in this, that he understandeth and knoweth me, that I am the LORD which exercise lovingkindness, judgment, and righteousness, in the earth: for in these things I delight, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa3bfae0-37d4-4422-83f9-77ef2161a77f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: JER 9:25
Text: Behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that I will punish all them which are circumcised with the uncircumcised;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/9/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35030f93-e58b-451d-aa34-139ff6d9f39f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 262

Reference: JER 9:26
Text: Egypt, and Judah, and Edom, and the children of Ammon, and Moab, and all that are in the utmost corners, that dwell in the wilderness: for all these nations are uncircumcised, and all the house of Israel are uncircumcised in the heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1ea5de7-d040-4995-8f01-c0d64bf4d88b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: JER 10:1
Text: Hear ye the word which the LORD speaketh unto you, O house of Israel:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:316e253a-34af-40a3-a7f7-f0da165d24ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: JER 10:2
Text: Thus saith the LORD, Learn not the way of the heathen, and be not dismayed at the signs of heaven; for the heathen are dismayed at them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3bd79cca-1e4c-4109-a68c-b73cd09fdbc2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: JER 10:3
Text: For the customs of the people are vain: for one cutteth a tree out of the forest, the work of the hands of the workman, with the axe.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e93ad84-6f3e-402f-93bf-1cdf01ef2dfe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: JER 10:4
Text: They deck it with silver and with gold; they fasten it with nails and with hammers, that it move not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd5d5048-c024-4130-af78-42c301766d21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: JER 10:5
Text: They are upright as the palm tree, but speak not: they must needs be borne, because they cannot go. Be not afraid of them; for they cannot do evil, neither also is it in them to do good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db43a2f6-b8cf-4b64-87d9-bc18cea7495b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: JER 10:6
Text: Forasmuch as there is none like unto thee, O LORD; thou art great, and thy name is great in might.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2dbb27aa-acac-48d1-9943-5e09279fce53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: JER 10:7
Text: Who would not fear thee, O King of nations? for to thee doth it appertain: forasmuch as among all the wise men of the nations, and in all their kingdoms, there is none like unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d77058a4-5e60-445a-b643-d28f1e4fc332>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: JER 10:8
Text: But they are altogether brutish and foolish: the stock is a doctrine of vanities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:807a325f-d013-43db-8371-a87d46dd2533>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: JER 10:9
Text: Silver spread into plates is brought from Tarshish, and gold from Uphaz, the work of the workman, and of the hands of the founder: blue and purple is their clothing: they are all the work of cunning men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3aa9da3-4cbe-4ab6-b297-91cc81438876>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: JER 10:10
Text: But the LORD is the true God, he is the living God, and an everlasting king: at his wrath the earth shall tremble, and the nations shall not be able to abide his indignation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68484814-a50d-4673-92d0-61dbeec4f2fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: JER 10:11
Text: Thus shall ye say unto them, The gods that have not made the heavens and the earth, even they shall perish from the earth, and from under these heavens.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:852c971f-96f5-42f6-aa60-395de7c45f72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: JER 10:12
Text: He hath made the earth by his power, he hath established the world by his wisdom, and hath stretched out the heavens by his discretion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a9049b6-5f32-4581-abc7-c25ed43e3e97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: JER 10:13
Text: When he uttereth his voice, there is a multitude of waters in the heavens, and he causeth the vapours to ascend from the ends of the earth; he maketh lightnings with rain, and bringeth forth the wind out of his treasures.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd4e7af8-1d60-45df-aed8-c3cf7650b297>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JER 10:14
Text: Every man is brutish in his knowledge: every founder is confounded by the graven image: for his molten image is falsehood, and there is no breath in them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f3e6bbe-7b6e-4802-847e-b07d278e3c62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: JER 10:15
Text: They are vanity, and the work of errors: in the time of their visitation they shall perish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f0054a3-84f0-4309-be4d-8d8695d141e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: JER 10:16
Text: The portion of Jacob is not like them: for he is the former of all things; and Israel is the rod of his inheritance: The LORD of hosts is his name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fcefd0af-42a2-4408-85d9-f8a196ee4261>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: JER 10:17
Text: Gather up thy wares out of the land, O inhabitant of the fortress.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2b5ed4d-e2cb-44c2-8f55-6f92c1e686b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: JER 10:18
Text: For thus saith the LORD, Behold, I will sling out the inhabitants of the land at this once, and will distress them, that they may find it so.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4518346-1aa8-40b5-a9b4-0fb30ce77e8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: JER 10:19
Text: Woe is me for my hurt! my wound is grievous; but I said, Truly this is a grief, and I must bear it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e8b10c9-49ef-48ea-8eb1-6fa01045a890>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: JER 10:20
Text: My tabernacle is spoiled, and all my cords are broken: my children are gone forth of me, and they are not: there is none to stretch forth my tent any more, and to set up my curtains.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bbd050d-a76a-4845-b458-f90beadecaea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: JER 10:21
Text: For the pastors are become brutish, and have not sought the LORD: therefore they shall not prosper, and all their flocks shall be scattered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f096138-27c7-4ad3-8491-09e0fe2a888c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: JER 10:22
Text: Behold, the noise of the bruit is come, and a great commotion out of the north country, to make the cities of Judah desolate, and a den of dragons.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ff761e9-c72c-4baa-b1f4-9a83dd01f566>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: JER 10:23
Text: O LORD, I know that the way of man is not in himself: it is not in man that walketh to direct his steps.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d3af66b-68ce-4fcd-b7df-3c698461595b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: JER 10:24
Text: O LORD, correct me, but with judgment; not in thine anger, lest thou bring me to nothing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/10/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:adf05426-b2e5-429b-a39f-2328facaab1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: JER 10:25
Text: Pour out thy fury upon the heathen that know thee not, and upon the families that call not on thy name: for they have eaten up Jacob, and devoured him, and consumed him, and have made his habitation desolate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/11/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:583be3d2-f3c5-49cd-8ae7-7da785025c11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: JER 11:1
Text: The word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/11/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a648bbf-998f-436f-87b2-a089db2351c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: JER 11:2
Text: Hear ye the words of this covenant, and speak unto the men of Judah, and to the inhabitants of Jerusalem;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/11/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8937a36-3263-4a5a-9de3-33de96900c8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: JER 11:3
Text: And say thou unto them, Thus saith the LORD God of Israel; Cursed be the man that obeyeth not the words of this covenant,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/11/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a631fa15-d12b-4c55-be83-3177e48be437>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: JER 11:4
Text: Which I commanded your fathers in the day that I brought them forth out of the land of Egypt, from the iron furnace, saying, Obey my voice, and do them, according to all which I command you: so shall ye be my people, and I will be your God:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/11/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c186acd3-cee9-4f21-a858-3f8549015334>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: JER 11:5
Text: That I may perform the oath which I have sworn unto your fathers, to give them a land flowing with milk and honey, as it is this day. Then answered I, and said, So be it, O LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/11/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:adfe7ec9-04a6-4a88-8b43-0ba0f373fefc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: JER 11:6
Text: Then the LORD said unto me, Proclaim all these words in the cities of Judah, and in the streets of Jerusalem, saying, Hear ye the words of this covenant, and do them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/11/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2851a57-570d-4696-b2a6-c3c49cea3b1e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: JER 11:7
Text: For I earnestly protested unto your fathers in the day that I brought them up out of the land of Egypt, even unto this day, rising early and protesting, saying, Obey my voice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/11/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e752034-c937-4464-9d7a-d80f0d51ffe1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: JER 11:8
Text: Yet they obeyed not, nor inclined their ear, but walked every one in the imagination of their evil heart: therefore I will bring upon them all the words of this covenant, which I commanded them to do: but they did them not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/11/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1ad52cc-3bec-4a40-aaec-832f519627ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: JER 11:9
Text: And the LORD said unto me, A conspiracy is found among the men of Judah, and among the inhabitants of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/11/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4d691a6-bd2f-4cd7-915b-7c476eb4e29d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 266

Reference: JER 11:10
Text: They are turned back to the iniquities of their forefathers, which refused to hear my words; and they went after other gods to serve them: the house of Israel and the house of Judah have broken my covenant which I made with their fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/11/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e59b0c89-bad0-4c71-b36c-ac7d2ac966eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: JER 11:11
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD, Behold, I will bring evil upon them, which they shall not be able to escape; and though they shall cry unto me, I will not hearken unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/11/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ca4b28c-fe2b-49fe-9aeb-f4f08ab2e4d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: JER 11:12
Text: Then shall the cities of Judah and inhabitants of Jerusalem go, and cry unto the gods unto whom they offer incense: but they shall not save them at all in the time of their trouble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/11/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a305a9a-4563-4ce5-8680-a8822012f717>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: JER 11:13
Text: For according to the number of thy cities were thy gods, O Judah; and according to the number of the streets of Jerusalem have ye set up altars to that shameful thing, even altars to burn incense unto Baal.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/11/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b21eac41-7ef6-4342-905d-f5f80735a9f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: JER 11:14
Text: Therefore pray not thou for this people, neither lift up a cry or prayer for them: for I will not hear them in the time that they cry unto me for their trouble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/11/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:213ffd22-2268-436c-b84a-e3c03dfaa1b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: JER 11:15
Text: What hath my beloved to do in mine house, seeing she hath wrought lewdness with many, and the holy flesh is passed from thee? when thou doest evil, then thou rejoicest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/11/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a81d5d50-3bc5-4d6d-a28c-762c0f1bf38e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: JER 11:16
Text: The LORD called thy name, A green olive tree, fair, and of goodly fruit: with the noise of a great tumult he hath kindled fire upon it, and the branches of it are broken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/11/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d0ce7a8-65d6-4ff6-925a-b3047d72bce7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: JER 11:17
Text: For the LORD of hosts, that planted thee, hath pronounced evil against thee, for the evil of the house of Israel and of the house of Judah, which they have done against themselves to provoke me to anger in offering incense unto Baal.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/11/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37da543c-b77e-4d18-81da-bce2cff432fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: JER 11:18
Text: And the LORD hath given me knowledge of it, and I know it: then thou shewedst me their doings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/11/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fd4d567-b553-41b4-98b2-a4fe718db817>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 298

Reference: JER 11:19
Text: But I was like a lamb or an ox that is brought to the slaughter; and I knew not that they had devised devices against me, saying, Let us destroy the tree with the fruit thereof, and let us cut him off from the land of the living, that his name may be no more remembered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/11/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a01e8025-0756-4be1-9ae1-be5e483a5913>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: JER 11:20
Text: But, O LORD of hosts, that judgest righteously, that triest the reins and the heart, let me see thy vengeance on them: for unto thee have I revealed my cause.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/11/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71174aef-2a6e-4221-966a-8fc2d2944c88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: JER 11:21
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD of the men of Anathoth, that seek thy life, saying, Prophesy not in the name of the LORD, that thou die not by our hand:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/11/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5f3364a-a6ec-4cb9-9be0-7bb396ec1415>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JER 11:22
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD of hosts, Behold, I will punish them: the young men shall die by the sword; their sons and their daughters shall die by famine:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/11/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ede10025-99c3-4981-8215-ed63982d570d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: JER 11:23
Text: And there shall be no remnant of them: for I will bring evil upon the men of Anathoth, even the year of their visitation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/12/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cf8aff4-b9d6-4603-b58b-0fc9cca4dd76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: JER 12:1
Text: Righteous art thou, O LORD, when I plead with thee: yet let me talk with thee of thy judgments: Wherefore doth the way of the wicked prosper? wherefore are all they happy that deal very treacherously?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/12/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9810ad75-d69d-41f1-94b6-2c85614108ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: JER 12:2
Text: Thou hast planted them, yea, they have taken root: they grow, yea, they bring forth fruit: thou art near in their mouth, and far from their reins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/12/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a4ac918-90f8-48ac-9f01-b9af05b58504>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: JER 12:3
Text: But thou, O LORD, knowest me: thou hast seen me, and tried mine heart toward thee: pull them out like sheep for the slaughter, and prepare them for the day of slaughter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/12/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c18f51bd-a745-4500-af26-0d0f96122824>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: JER 12:4
Text: How long shall the land mourn, and the herbs of every field wither, for the wickedness of them that dwell therein? the beasts are consumed, and the birds; because they said, He shall not see our last end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/12/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1873cdd-37e2-46b5-9e37-1a43314d041f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: JER 12:5
Text: If thou hast run with the footmen, and they have wearied thee, then how canst thou contend with horses? and if in the land of peace, wherein thou trustedst, they wearied thee, then how wilt thou do in the swelling of Jordan?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/12/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:040de19b-0712-4501-bcd6-8749f70346b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: JER 12:6
Text: For even thy brethren, and the house of thy father, even they have dealt treacherously with thee; yea, they have called a multitude after thee: believe them not, though they speak fair words unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/12/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7a59044-997e-44e4-aef3-558afe141b2b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: JER 12:7
Text: I have forsaken mine house, I have left mine heritage; I have given the dearly beloved of my soul into the hand of her enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/12/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64948436-a0fa-4eb3-8e12-469f795b14ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: JER 12:8
Text: Mine heritage is unto me as a lion in the forest; it crieth out against me: therefore have I hated it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/12/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bd6a217-89a3-4b76-9f69-afa2373bea71>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: JER 12:9
Text: Mine heritage is unto me as a speckled bird, the birds round about are against her; come ye, assemble all the beasts of the field, come to devour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/12/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69e67c25-b937-4419-96d6-c27846021528>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: JER 12:10
Text: Many pastors have destroyed my vineyard, they have trodden my portion under foot, they have made my pleasant portion a desolate wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/12/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d6a59e7-dc25-4555-81bc-6885e30acb6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: JER 12:11
Text: They have made it desolate, and being desolate it mourneth unto me; the whole land is made desolate, because no man layeth it to heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/12/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4246e7dc-1bd5-44c1-a688-a220bce8667b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: JER 12:12
Text: The spoilers are come upon all high places through the wilderness: for the sword of the LORD shall devour from the one end of the land even to the other end of the land: no flesh shall have peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/12/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:659e98ba-ad81-413c-9cc6-721c75c014d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: JER 12:13
Text: They have sown wheat, but shall reap thorns: they have put themselves to pain, but shall not profit: and they shall be ashamed of your revenues because of the fierce anger of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/12/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77a10ac7-0cc0-442c-a265-4921f2d3bbe0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: JER 12:14
Text: Thus saith the LORD against all mine evil neighbours, that touch the inheritance which I have caused my people Israel to inherit; Behold, I will pluck them out of their land, and pluck out the house of Judah from among them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/12/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5427017-5f81-441d-b721-d76a8dae5c08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: JER 12:15
Text: And it shall come to pass, after that I have plucked them out I will return, and have compassion on them, and will bring them again, every man to his heritage, and every man to his land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/12/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:928becca-7893-4278-bb11-6ddcb6a1d15f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: JER 12:16
Text: And it shall come to pass, if they will diligently learn the ways of my people, to swear by my name, The LORD liveth; as they taught my people to swear by Baal; then shall they be built in the midst of my people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/12/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d1369e8-f49b-485a-833f-80f83592498a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: JER 12:17
Text: But if they will not obey, I will utterly pluck up and destroy that nation, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c426b6f4-cea9-4ba1-aa14-fb44ad4561ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: JER 13:1
Text: Thus saith the LORD unto me, Go and get thee a linen girdle, and put it upon thy loins, and put it not in water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9772ff4f-50ed-423f-a959-6fc9cec0f712>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: JER 13:2
Text: So I got a girdle according to the word of the LORD, and put it on my loins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b0eaf08-cc70-440f-819c-431877bcb9c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: JER 13:3
Text: And the word of the LORD came unto me the second time, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7c9b150-332e-4e7c-8991-08ee94c6e4f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: JER 13:4
Text: Take the girdle that thou hast got, which is upon thy loins, and arise, go to Euphrates, and hide it there in a hole of the rock.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19267e87-997b-4f20-9891-aea8e1dc2133>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: JER 13:5
Text: So I went, and hid it by Euphrates, as the LORD commanded me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f96a2f50-25c5-4947-9c6c-d3351b66e893>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: JER 13:6
Text: And it came to pass after many days, that the LORD said unto me, Arise, go to Euphrates, and take the girdle from thence, which I commanded thee to hide there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb1a9e78-3427-44e8-beb6-1d2d480af047>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: JER 13:7
Text: Then I went to Euphrates, and digged, and took the girdle from the place where I had hid it: and, behold, the girdle was marred, it was profitable for nothing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e634885-c372-4d1a-ae51-6c51de129ef1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: JER 13:8
Text: Then the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2166a318-d6df-420d-a779-14542ed9ee33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: JER 13:9
Text: Thus saith the LORD, After this manner will I mar the pride of Judah, and the great pride of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac4e7dc9-3c38-433c-aec0-a4d966138249>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: JER 13:10
Text: This evil people, which refuse to hear my words, which walk in the imagination of their heart, and walk after other gods, to serve them, and to worship them, shall even be as this girdle, which is good for nothing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eaba4e04-f02b-4337-bb4c-300e37261ca7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 301

Reference: JER 13:11
Text: For as the girdle cleaveth to the loins of a man, so have I caused to cleave unto me the whole house of Israel and the whole house of Judah, saith the LORD; that they might be unto me for a people, and for a name, and for a praise, and for a glory: but they would not hear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00a4dfd3-cc65-4cc2-9cc0-5714ba92ca8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: JER 13:12
Text: Therefore thou shalt speak unto them this word; Thus saith the LORD God of Israel, Every bottle shall be filled with wine: and they shall say unto thee, Do we not certainly know that every bottle shall be filled with wine?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9f4d630-b9bd-4355-81a5-84575fbfeaf9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: JER 13:13
Text: Then shalt thou say unto them, Thus saith the LORD, Behold, I will fill all the inhabitants of this land, even the kings that sit upon David’s throne, and the priests, and the prophets, and all the inhabitants of Jerusalem, with drunkenness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8078e089-a3b5-4ac5-85dd-4690008f1105>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: JER 13:14
Text: And I will dash them one against another, even the fathers and the sons together, saith the LORD: I will not pity, nor spare, nor have mercy, but destroy them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ad3df25-9ff4-4817-944c-46bcc8aa1f14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: JER 13:15
Text: Hear ye, and give ear; be not proud: for the LORD hath spoken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92195ac6-c77a-426f-8805-051fd9b16a73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: JER 13:16
Text: Give glory to the LORD your God, before he cause darkness, and before your feet stumble upon the dark mountains, and, while ye look for light, he turn it into the shadow of death, and make it gross darkness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d43dda4a-7ef4-452e-98bf-4f496c32bae5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: JER 13:17
Text: But if ye will not hear it, my soul shall weep in secret places for your pride; and mine eye shall weep sore, and run down with tears, because the LORD’s flock is carried away captive.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:745650ce-1a9a-4f52-a908-2499ecb58e47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: JER 13:18
Text: Say unto the king and to the queen, Humble yourselves, sit down: for your principalities shall come down, even the crown of your glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0d8ce1f-71ce-4c52-a76f-b8c2158fa623>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: JER 13:19
Text: The cities of the south shall be shut up, and none shall open them: Judah shall be carried away captive all of it, it shall be wholly carried away captive.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07b12936-1086-4cc4-be0e-6a27324d0873>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: JER 13:20
Text: Lift up your eyes, and behold them that come from the north: where is the flock that was given thee, thy beautiful flock?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43a16678-3f26-4504-8e1a-870973f996a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: JER 13:21
Text: What wilt thou say when he shall punish thee? for thou hast taught them to be captains, and as chief over thee: shall not sorrows take thee, as a woman in travail?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8fad96a-e45f-485f-b56d-280bf8cb990f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: JER 13:22
Text: And if thou say in thine heart, Wherefore come these things upon me? For the greatness of thine iniquity are thy skirts discovered, and thy heels made bare.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eaad1951-2296-4bb6-a777-6e5bd8028091>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: JER 13:23
Text: Can the Ethiopian change his skin, or the leopard his spots? then may ye also do good, that are accustomed to do evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84d17ac5-0b58-4014-87af-f354eb72f7ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: JER 13:24
Text: Therefore will I scatter them as the stubble that passeth away by the wind of the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2892d72a-fb21-4582-a1e9-d4f75a12d5df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: JER 13:25
Text: This is thy lot, the portion of thy measures from me, saith the LORD; because thou hast forgotten me, and trusted in falsehood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f213178-8967-4334-8556-47a4f954e382>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: JER 13:26
Text: Therefore will I discover thy skirts upon thy face, that thy shame may appear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/13/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e81c99dc-651e-415a-9a1a-e125f0340eaf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: JER 13:27
Text: I have seen thine adulteries, and thy neighings, the lewdness of thy whoredom, and thine abominations on the hills in the fields. Woe unto thee, O Jerusalem! wilt thou not be made clean? when shall it once be?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/14/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b79e8d60-7ce2-4322-95e6-e3f9fcc3d113>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: JER 14:1
Text: The word of the LORD that came to Jeremiah concerning the dearth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/14/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3eaf947-d111-412a-a843-f2d951da150d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: JER 14:2
Text: Judah mourneth, and the gates thereof languish; they are black unto the ground; and the cry of Jerusalem is gone up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/14/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f92e1788-51b5-4657-8874-a9be27d50921>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: JER 14:3
Text: And their nobles have sent their little ones to the waters: they came to the pits, and found no water; they returned with their vessels empty; they were ashamed and confounded, and covered their heads.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/14/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a9ff94d-e41b-4b10-bb63-515a88e3c8af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: JER 14:4
Text: Because the ground is chapt, for there was no rain in the earth, the plowmen were ashamed, they covered their heads.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/14/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91eaa2ba-1858-4c53-8e87-d1a41139f736>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: JER 14:5
Text: Yea, the hind also calved in the field, and forsook it, because there was no grass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/14/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89aad3c6-e252-4b57-9d27-a7f1fc1aee70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: JER 14:6
Text: And the wild asses did stand in the high places, they snuffed up the wind like dragons; their eyes did fail, because there was no grass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/14/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e23f7052-6cfe-4f1c-a625-cf6862cdec4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: JER 14:7
Text: O LORD, though our iniquities testify against us, do thou it for thy name’s sake: for our backslidings are many; we have sinned against thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/14/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1fc1332-2548-44cc-969b-d46b6582442a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: JER 14:8
Text: O the hope of Israel, the saviour thereof in time of trouble, why shouldest thou be as a stranger in the land, and as a wayfaring man that turneth aside to tarry for a night?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/14/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f5ef43e-df76-4e8b-b6a4-95fa77c7ff32>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: JER 14:9
Text: Why shouldest thou be as a man astonied, as a mighty man that cannot save? yet thou, O LORD, art in the midst of us, and we are called by thy name; leave us not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/14/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38369ffb-3913-40b8-9486-a8ed66f49e56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: JER 14:10
Text: Thus saith the LORD unto this people, Thus have they loved to wander, they have not refrained their feet, therefore the LORD doth not accept them; he will now remember their iniquity, and visit their sins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/14/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbc8e4e9-ea8d-44e1-a61b-d9e19b231e39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: JER 14:11
Text: Then said the LORD unto me, Pray not for this people for their good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/14/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1bbf936-d5e4-49e8-b3bc-dfddbce222e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: JER 14:12
Text: When they fast, I will not hear their cry; and when they offer burnt offering and an oblation, I will not accept them: but I will consume them by the sword, and by the famine, and by the pestilence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/14/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ecf2247b-c2cf-4f63-976a-dbe38d79a346>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: JER 14:13
Text: Then said I, Ah, Lord GOD! behold, the prophets say unto them, Ye shall not see the sword, neither shall ye have famine; but I will give you assured peace in this place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/14/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ceba8342-ba03-4fb7-8b04-75505caeef98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: JER 14:14
Text: Then the LORD said unto me, The prophets prophesy lies in my name: I sent them not, neither have I commanded them, neither spake unto them: they prophesy unto you a false vision and divination, and a thing of nought, and the deceit of their heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/14/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:160c3b09-a624-472a-a7b7-c9d4978ebceb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: JER 14:15
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD concerning the prophets that prophesy in my name, and I sent them not, yet they say, Sword and famine shall not be in this land; By sword and famine shall those prophets be consumed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/14/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2854a1cb-162d-4c41-accd-15079ceb7e9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 286

Reference: JER 14:16
Text: And the people to whom they prophesy shall be cast out in the streets of Jerusalem because of the famine and the sword; and they shall have none to bury them, them, their wives, nor their sons, nor their daughters: for I will pour their wickedness upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/14/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a03336eb-959c-45a0-8df1-e7601c45c298>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: JER 14:17
Text: Therefore thou shalt say this word unto them; Let mine eyes run down with tears night and day, and let them not cease: for the virgin daughter of my people is broken with a great breach, with a very grievous blow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/14/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5969255-17c2-4d07-943f-0b41b751ea35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: JER 14:18
Text: If I go forth into the field, then behold the slain with the sword! and if I enter into the city, then behold them that are sick with famine! yea, both the prophet and the priest go about into a land that they know not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/14/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fc190a2-72a5-4107-8fe6-5a9cc36a9ed1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: JER 14:19
Text: Hast thou utterly rejected Judah? hath thy soul lothed Zion? why hast thou smitten us, and there is no healing for us? we looked for peace, and there is no good; and for the time of healing, and behold trouble!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/14/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae0b7c5a-f1d4-4b72-ac95-011e4395a610>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: JER 14:20
Text: We acknowledge, O LORD, our wickedness, and the iniquity of our fathers: for we have sinned against thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/14/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29f58677-dcb4-4dd9-95bf-9ce7e9a857b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: JER 14:21
Text: Do not abhor us, for thy name’s sake, do not disgrace the throne of thy glory: remember, break not thy covenant with us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/14/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14925c6d-a8df-4336-8ef4-dac3c5278634>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: JER 14:22
Text: Are there any among the vanities of the Gentiles that can cause rain? or can the heavens give showers? art not thou he, O LORD our God? therefore we will wait upon thee: for thou hast made all these things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/15/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4962576d-98a9-4f42-998a-f97b5141bc07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: JER 15:1
Text: Then said the LORD unto me, Though Moses and Samuel stood before me, yet my mind could not be toward this people: cast them out of my sight, and let them go forth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/15/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9b9ee40-9ead-4add-996d-96f6a4895a00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 329

Reference: JER 15:2
Text: And it shall come to pass, if they say unto thee, Whither shall we go forth? then thou shalt tell them, Thus saith the LORD; Such as are for death, to death; and such as are for the sword, to the sword; and such as are for the famine, to the famine; and such as are for the captivity, to the captivity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/15/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddf0867a-42f6-4c11-8bce-b040145ffb40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: JER 15:3
Text: And I will appoint over them four kinds, saith the LORD: the sword to slay, and the dogs to tear, and the fowls of the heaven, and the beasts of the earth, to devour and destroy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/15/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93c3104c-8e40-4c30-9d2d-86b7188fdff1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JER 15:4
Text: And I will cause them to be removed into all kingdoms of the earth, because of Manasseh the son of Hezekiah king of Judah, for that which he did in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/15/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1361bd09-de75-47ad-b214-67808eba4781>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: JER 15:5
Text: For who shall have pity upon thee, O Jerusalem? or who shall bemoan thee? or who shall go aside to ask how thou doest?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/15/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e491e546-057c-4a62-bbae-a9507c0bbe51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JER 15:6
Text: Thou hast forsaken me, saith the LORD, thou art gone backward: therefore will I stretch out my hand against thee, and destroy thee; I am weary with repenting.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/15/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3810b397-c40b-4256-a9e4-93311ce2e1b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: JER 15:7
Text: And I will fan them with a fan in the gates of the land; I will bereave them of children, I will destroy my people since they return not from their ways.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/15/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:023548a0-3be2-46cc-ad07-f8b338192f78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: JER 15:8
Text: Their widows are increased to me above the sand of the seas: I have brought upon them against the mother of the young men a spoiler at noonday: I have caused him to fall upon it suddenly, and terrors upon the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/15/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7bf9bfb6-b5e3-43b6-89ff-d8af7288fa63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: JER 15:9
Text: She that hath borne seven languisheth: she hath given up the ghost; her sun is gone down while it was yet day: she hath been ashamed and confounded: and the residue of them will I deliver to the sword before their enemies, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/15/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d48b007f-de6e-4740-880d-ee61b2d1c42a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: JER 15:10
Text: Woe is me, my mother, that thou hast borne me a man of strife and a man of contention to the whole earth! I have neither lent on usury, nor men have lent to me on usury; yet every one of them doth curse me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/15/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:464eb88f-50d2-413a-b3ab-918d2ae291be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: JER 15:11
Text: The LORD said, Verily it shall be well with thy remnant; verily I will cause the enemy to entreat thee well in the time of evil and in the time of affliction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/15/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d777168-fe1c-4a97-81a9-3425998dbb25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: JER 15:12
Text: Shall iron break the northern iron and the steel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/15/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89a81688-bc3f-40fb-b047-97c2c702aa96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: JER 15:13
Text: Thy substance and thy treasures will I give to the spoil without price, and that for all thy sins, even in all thy borders.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/15/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47b332bc-745c-45ab-9949-dde62507d180>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: JER 15:14
Text: And I will make thee to pass with thine enemies into a land which thou knowest not: for a fire is kindled in mine anger, which shall burn upon you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/15/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b1171f1-4464-45b6-a1d6-14aaaacfd9ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: JER 15:15
Text: O LORD, thou knowest: remember me, and visit me, and revenge me of my persecutors; take me not away in thy longsuffering: know that for thy sake I have suffered rebuke.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/15/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f317a2e8-8302-4513-b1bc-000185bce406>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: JER 15:16
Text: Thy words were found, and I did eat them; and thy word was unto me the joy and rejoicing of mine heart: for I am called by thy name, O LORD God of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/15/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74cddc97-7620-4d12-abe7-4f8a5786c836>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: JER 15:17
Text: I sat not in the assembly of the mockers, nor rejoiced; I sat alone because of thy hand: for thou hast filled me with indignation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/15/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:933a8061-50df-4c18-a75a-d967b5b26bbb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: JER 15:18
Text: Why is my pain perpetual, and my wound incurable, which refuseth to be healed? wilt thou be altogether unto me as a liar, and as waters that fail?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/15/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91a0f344-e213-449e-8538-3717f8db5a6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: JER 15:19
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD, If thou return, then will I bring thee again, and thou shalt stand before me: and if thou take forth the precious from the vile, thou shalt be as my mouth: let them return unto thee; but return not thou unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/15/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c1ca4f5-c12a-45d3-a57d-fd121e6666f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: JER 15:20
Text: And I will make thee unto this people a fenced brasen wall: and they shall fight against thee, but they shall not prevail against thee: for I am with thee to save thee and to deliver thee, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/15/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d52b7186-0f7e-4ff5-80b9-717400ed6178>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: JER 15:21
Text: And I will deliver thee out of the hand of the wicked, and I will redeem thee out of the hand of the terrible.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/16/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49ff17d0-3964-4f76-a3d1-fe318eb0c4d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: JER 16:1
Text: The word of the LORD came also unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/16/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc02986f-6b2e-47fa-a97d-f2b4548d0586>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: JER 16:2
Text: Thou shalt not take thee a wife, neither shalt thou have sons or daughters in this place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/16/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8494a0c8-f213-4ae7-b296-819a199d9996>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: JER 16:3
Text: For thus saith the LORD concerning the sons and concerning the daughters that are born in this place, and concerning their mothers that bare them, and concerning their fathers that begat them in this land;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/16/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f4354ff-ca24-4fb0-85df-89cb98fa3ed0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 320

Reference: JER 16:4
Text: They shall die of grievous deaths; they shall not be lamented; neither shall they be buried; but they shall be as dung upon the face of the earth: and they shall be consumed by the sword, and by famine; and their carcases shall be meat for the fowls of heaven, and for the beasts of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/16/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:858fef5f-38c7-45fe-966c-9755b1290efe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: JER 16:5
Text: For thus saith the LORD, Enter not into the house of mourning, neither go to lament nor bemoan them: for I have taken away my peace from this people, saith the LORD, even lovingkindness and mercies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/16/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab7400e7-02e9-4587-b862-4a0e16bc4fae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: JER 16:6
Text: Both the great and the small shall die in this land: they shall not be buried, neither shall men lament for them, nor cut themselves, nor make themselves bald for them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/16/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47aab953-8c66-4bbf-87e7-eaf6ec6465c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: JER 16:7
Text: Neither shall men tear themselves for them in mourning, to comfort them for the dead; neither shall men give them the cup of consolation to drink for their father or for their mother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/16/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b61c527a-4f3e-4ecb-9c11-028f8b5fdcef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: JER 16:8
Text: Thou shalt not also go into the house of feasting, to sit with them to eat and to drink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/16/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:465268cc-7837-4e92-ac0a-c03d30b1b71f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: JER 16:9
Text: For thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Behold, I will cause to cease out of this place in your eyes, and in your days, the voice of mirth, and the voice of gladness, the voice of the bridegroom, and the voice of the bride.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/16/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6fcbb30-975a-493c-9261-4103b6b4284c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 294

Reference: JER 16:10
Text: And it shall come to pass, when thou shalt shew this people all these words, and they shall say unto thee, Wherefore hath the LORD pronounced all this great evil against us? or what is our iniquity? or what is our sin that we have committed against the LORD our God?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/16/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e30ac71-578b-45ed-89cd-701da7f1ae75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: JER 16:11
Text: Then shalt thou say unto them, Because your fathers have forsaken me, saith the LORD, and have walked after other gods, and have served them, and have worshipped them, and have forsaken me, and have not kept my law;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/16/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d22d488-c995-46f0-abf4-9e20eaecda1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: JER 16:12
Text: And ye have done worse than your fathers; for, behold, ye walk every one after the imagination of his evil heart, that they may not hearken unto me:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/16/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bedc1e8f-4fce-40a7-b62b-af4c50f6834b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: JER 16:13
Text: Therefore will I cast you out of this land into a land that ye know not, neither ye nor your fathers; and there shall ye serve other gods day and night; where I will not shew you favour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/16/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5b1c74d-bca2-49dd-838a-aa9da82aef51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: JER 16:14
Text: Therefore, behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that it shall no more be said, The LORD liveth, that brought up the children of Israel out of the land of Egypt;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/16/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5567b21-443c-420b-8fc6-159e65dd3bfd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: JER 16:15
Text: But, The LORD liveth, that brought up the children of Israel from the land of the north, and from all the lands whither he had driven them: and I will bring them again into their land that I gave unto their fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/16/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:220c695e-1f31-477a-a44b-f8c76fd55a5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: JER 16:16
Text: Behold, I will send for many fishers, saith the LORD, and they shall fish them; and after will I send for many hunters, and they shall hunt them from every mountain, and from every hill, and out of the holes of the rocks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/16/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b99557d-ee3e-47a7-a69d-a3192fdda115>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: JER 16:17
Text: For mine eyes are upon all their ways: they are not hid from my face, neither is their iniquity hid from mine eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/16/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29489855-72ed-4a3d-a7c0-a91d123d81a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: JER 16:18
Text: And first I will recompense their iniquity and their sin double; because they have defiled my land, they have filled mine inheritance with the carcases of their detestable and abominable things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/16/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad57fc2a-d096-4489-bec6-079455e3de0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: JER 16:19
Text: O LORD, my strength, and my fortress, and my refuge in the day of affliction, the Gentiles shall come unto thee from the ends of the earth, and shall say, Surely our fathers have inherited lies, vanity, and things wherein there is no profit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/16/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0367a6c-72e1-466c-afd8-52bea4e23dc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: JER 16:20
Text: Shall a man make gods unto himself, and they are no gods?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/16/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9666131a-debd-413e-b56b-39736f9bb0fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: JER 16:21
Text: Therefore, behold, I will this once cause them to know, I will cause them to know mine hand and my might; and they shall know that my name is The LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6ff76fe-eccd-4994-a922-560d13767bb7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: JER 17:1
Text: The sin of Judah is written with a pen of iron, and with the point of a diamond: it is graven upon the table of their heart, and upon the horns of your altars;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7f1b195-1d9e-49c0-99d9-bfe1e35f2fd5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: JER 17:2
Text: Whilst their children remember their altars and their groves by the green trees upon the high hills.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cf56e79-913e-4cb4-859a-cd00cf4e6611>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: JER 17:3
Text: O my mountain in the field, I will give thy substance and all thy treasures to the spoil, and thy high places for sin, throughout all thy borders.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d903656-b45f-49be-811e-775bf056f084>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: JER 17:4
Text: And thou, even thyself, shalt discontinue from thine heritage that I gave thee; and I will cause thee to serve thine enemies in the land which thou knowest not: for ye have kindled a fire in mine anger, which shall burn for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd54a49f-3dc7-4ece-b442-c2acb43635ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: JER 17:5
Text: Thus saith the LORD; Cursed be the man that trusteth in man, and maketh flesh his arm, and whose heart departeth from the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f162c8d-910e-4d67-ad74-979040a1d364>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: JER 17:6
Text: For he shall be like the heath in the desert, and shall not see when good cometh; but shall inhabit the parched places in the wilderness, in a salt land and not inhabited.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43d72a61-918e-42e7-bb36-0a95f292c07b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: JER 17:7
Text: Blessed is the man that trusteth in the LORD, and whose hope the LORD is.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc29d195-6a14-4118-9da3-d2184a791622>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 277

Reference: JER 17:8
Text: For he shall be as a tree planted by the waters, and that spreadeth out her roots by the river, and shall not see when heat cometh, but her leaf shall be green; and shall not be careful in the year of drought, neither shall cease from yielding fruit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29671385-e15c-4a98-acf5-bda551e4b2cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: JER 17:9
Text: The heart is deceitful above all things, and desperately wicked: who can know it?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a758fab4-0072-4882-87ce-af79bc47ec57>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: JER 17:10
Text: I the LORD search the heart, I try the reins, even to give every man according to his ways, and according to the fruit of his doings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3efc1a0-a69e-44be-94bc-f22ee6a019ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: JER 17:11
Text: As the partridge sitteth on eggs, and hatcheth them not; so he that getteth riches, and not by right, shall leave them in the midst of his days, and at his end shall be a fool.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2f15588-2b60-42cb-832b-b55cec2415de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: JER 17:12
Text: A glorious high throne from the beginning is the place of our sanctuary.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd6ccfd2-3346-4307-ab6c-c60f5a441b17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: JER 17:13
Text: O LORD, the hope of Israel, all that forsake thee shall be ashamed, and they that depart from me shall be written in the earth, because they have forsaken the LORD, the fountain of living waters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e31ad4e9-5e5a-4b5c-8d45-42f793aa5eb0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: JER 17:14
Text: Heal me, O LORD, and I shall be healed; save me, and I shall be saved: for thou art my praise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18f5831b-1faa-493b-8dba-72dcfbcf2520>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: JER 17:15
Text: Behold, they say unto me, Where is the word of the LORD? let it come now.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e7d44cf-6da8-44ef-9e3e-762304cf4515>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: JER 17:16
Text: As for me, I have not hastened from being a pastor to follow thee: neither have I desired the woeful day; thou knowest: that which came out of my lips was right before thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28dcc94d-6966-416c-8ebe-f943c494e762>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: JER 17:17
Text: Be not a terror unto me: thou art my hope in the day of evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4de3188-3263-4fb5-87a6-d8070868b053>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: JER 17:18
Text: Let them be confounded that persecute me, but let not me be confounded: let them be dismayed, but let not me be dismayed: bring upon them the day of evil, and destroy them with double destruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31993ada-8d3f-4a69-858d-7ce01fddcbb6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: JER 17:19
Text: Thus said the LORD unto me; Go and stand in the gate of the children of the people, whereby the kings of Judah come in, and by the which they go out, and in all the gates of Jerusalem;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9649b7f7-48e1-4759-9535-75469e119e97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: JER 17:20
Text: And say unto them, Hear ye the word of the LORD, ye kings of Judah, and all Judah, and all the inhabitants of Jerusalem, that enter in by these gates:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8f0a6fb-b7fd-46d3-b12a-ee8d761ce624>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: JER 17:21
Text: Thus saith the LORD; Take heed to yourselves, and bear no burden on the sabbath day, nor bring it in by the gates of Jerusalem;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94a2d07d-2fc3-4784-b11c-55bc3510afd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: JER 17:22
Text: Neither carry forth a burden out of your houses on the sabbath day, neither do ye any work, but hallow ye the sabbath day, as I commanded your fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fae3f760-fdb5-45bc-ad65-12479fd4ccf6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: JER 17:23
Text: But they obeyed not, neither inclined their ear, but made their neck stiff, that they might not hear, nor receive instruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34c4ab70-3a11-4681-acb1-090921fa0e02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: JER 17:24
Text: And it shall come to pass, if ye diligently hearken unto me, saith the LORD, to bring in no burden through the gates of this city on the sabbath day, but hallow the sabbath day, to do no work therein;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d96734e1-d160-4d8e-bee7-9efc1bfdc23c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 278

Reference: JER 17:25
Text: Then shall there enter into the gates of this city kings and princes sitting upon the throne of David, riding in chariots and on horses, they, and their princes, the men of Judah, and the inhabitants of Jerusalem: and this city shall remain for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c36931d3-af0d-4257-a212-7bbe3a5d51ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 343

Reference: JER 17:26
Text: And they shall come from the cities of Judah, and from the places about Jerusalem, and from the land of Benjamin, and from the plain, and from the mountains, and from the south, bringing burnt offerings, and sacrifices, and meat offerings, and incense, and bringing sacrifices of praise, unto the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/17/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86edc7b8-3cab-40b9-96e4-d89d8b0f37b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 302

Reference: JER 17:27
Text: But if ye will not hearken unto me to hallow the sabbath day, and not to bear a burden, even entering in at the gates of Jerusalem on the sabbath day; then will I kindle a fire in the gates thereof, and it shall devour the palaces of Jerusalem, and it shall not be quenched.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/18/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba2383d7-fae8-4c70-b08d-693d4e2b3e28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: JER 18:1
Text: The word which came to Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/18/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f359e323-bf7c-496c-8e5f-988d62c89c67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: JER 18:2
Text: Arise, and go down to the potter’s house, and there I will cause thee to hear my words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/18/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eba8aaa2-1600-471f-b383-baf121c07da4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: JER 18:3
Text: Then I went down to the potter’s house, and, behold, he wrought a work on the wheels.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/18/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15b1c085-331e-4f32-8dbe-d677783f48c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: JER 18:4
Text: And the vessel that he made of clay was marred in the hand of the potter: so he made it again another vessel, as seemed good to the potter to make it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/18/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2555e10-a791-416a-8669-4f92d48c8bc5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 72

Reference: JER 18:5
Text: Then the word of the LORD came to me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/18/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a8e5a0c-b36a-492d-84f2-089f53cfa9da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: JER 18:6
Text: O house of Israel, cannot I do with you as this potter? saith the LORD. Behold, as the clay is in the potter’s hand, so are ye in mine hand, O house of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/18/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ecf1bf7-4449-4e94-b42a-423427f1eb11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: JER 18:7
Text: At what instant I shall speak concerning a nation, and concerning a kingdom, to pluck up, and to pull down, and to destroy it;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/18/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c874072f-0cf9-434f-aab4-c66cfe6458ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: JER 18:8
Text: If that nation, against whom I have pronounced, turn from their evil, I will repent of the evil that I thought to do unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/18/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45ffab52-9b4d-4deb-9783-918e5711207b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: JER 18:9
Text: And at what instant I shall speak concerning a nation, and concerning a kingdom, to build and to plant it;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/18/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8c4df86-486b-4c02-824b-7e07e97186ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: JER 18:10
Text: If it do evil in my sight, that it obey not my voice, then I will repent of the good, wherewith I said I would benefit them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/18/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bff7d4de-624c-4e50-b07a-d70611452f58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 292

Reference: JER 18:11
Text: Now therefore go to, speak to the men of Judah, and to the inhabitants of Jerusalem, saying, Thus saith the LORD; Behold, I frame evil against you, and devise a device against you: return ye now every one from his evil way, and make your ways and your doings good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/18/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:436b46f4-20c3-4863-aff8-de0d1b01d54a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: JER 18:12
Text: And they said, There is no hope: but we will walk after our own devices, and we will every one do the imagination of his evil heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/18/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:189e8e4b-bcf0-45fa-9d7f-0b1b28d4185c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: JER 18:13
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD; Ask ye now among the heathen, who hath heard such things: the virgin of Israel hath done a very horrible thing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/18/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cadd5e39-18e8-4c59-82f7-a4609a57e04c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: JER 18:14
Text: Will a man leave the snow of Lebanon which cometh from the rock of the field? or shall the cold flowing waters that come from another place be forsaken?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/18/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b3feafd-fda1-4462-afa4-c34ecf643aa5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: JER 18:15
Text: Because my people hath forgotten me, they have burned incense to vanity, and they have caused them to stumble in their ways from the ancient paths, to walk in paths, in a way not cast up;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/18/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbce1e82-95b2-4685-be43-4c306bfd7b43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: JER 18:16
Text: To make their land desolate, and a perpetual hissing; every one that passeth thereby shall be astonished, and wag his head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/18/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d68b989a-7bf5-4197-85c1-b790cd29cfae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: JER 18:17
Text: I will scatter them as with an east wind before the enemy; I will shew them the back, and not the face, in the day of their calamity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/18/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d64a20f9-2f06-4bf9-b08b-6ec871097aad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 286

Reference: JER 18:18
Text: Then said they, Come and let us devise devices against Jeremiah; for the law shall not perish from the priest, nor counsel from the wise, nor the word from the prophet. Come, and let us smite him with the tongue, and let us not give heed to any of his words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/18/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c489e451-2575-4066-9f60-9f795407605e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: JER 18:19
Text: Give heed to me, O LORD, and hearken to the voice of them that contend with me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/18/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1038bbc-6001-401d-b050-56ae22ce796a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: JER 18:20
Text: Shall evil be recompensed for good? for they have digged a pit for my soul. Remember that I stood before thee to speak good for them, and to turn away thy wrath from them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/18/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a611eda-de76-4aac-b628-488f7c3b3ddf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: JER 18:21
Text: Therefore deliver up their children to the famine, and pour out their blood by the force of the sword; and let their wives be bereaved of their children, and be widows; and let their men be put to death; let their young men be slain by the sword in battle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/18/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0335a6e-72d6-45df-b0a4-5be2c4ad4db9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JER 18:22
Text: Let a cry be heard from their houses, when thou shalt bring a troop suddenly upon them: for they have digged a pit to take me, and hid snares for my feet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/18/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b669ac9e-e68c-4fc0-aa48-99392026393a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: JER 18:23
Text: Yet, LORD, thou knowest all their counsel against me to slay me: forgive not their iniquity, neither blot out their sin from thy sight, but let them be overthrown before thee; deal thus with them in the time of thine anger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/19/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41bfd3ff-50aa-4960-941e-fea5e81f1382>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: JER 19:1
Text: Thus saith the LORD, Go and get a potter’s earthen bottle, and take of the ancients of the people, and of the ancients of the priests;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/19/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b7f85e4-ffc7-4608-a8b4-ab11c4cc31bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: JER 19:2
Text: And go forth unto the valley of the son of Hinnom, which is by the entry of the east gate, and proclaim there the words that I shall tell thee,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/19/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0129fa1-f0e0-4749-8a9a-040936a739be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: JER 19:3
Text: And say, Hear ye the word of the LORD, O kings of Judah, and inhabitants of Jerusalem; Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Behold, I will bring evil upon this place, the which whosoever heareth, his ears shall tingle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/19/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:078faa2f-d627-43ca-8513-3f66a59829bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: JER 19:4
Text: Because they have forsaken me, and have estranged this place, and have burned incense in it unto other gods, whom neither they nor their fathers have known, nor the kings of Judah, and have filled this place with the blood of innocents;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/19/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:338d6079-62c0-4e8b-aa5b-b490e7e17c41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: JER 19:5
Text: They have built also the high places of Baal, to burn their sons with fire for burnt offerings unto Baal, which I commanded not, nor spake it, neither came it into my mind:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/19/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddcce0d3-fe4f-4d0d-b5be-6d88b999612d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: JER 19:6
Text: Therefore, behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that this place shall no more be called Tophet, nor The valley of the son of Hinnom, but The valley of slaughter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/19/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47a15724-5887-4b25-9900-5b4857456d3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 314

Reference: JER 19:7
Text: And I will make void the counsel of Judah and Jerusalem in this place; and I will cause them to fall by the sword before their enemies, and by the hands of them that seek their lives: and their carcases will I give to be meat for the fowls of the heaven, and for the beasts of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/19/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca986538-b150-4815-bdfd-1e7052b294fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: JER 19:8
Text: And I will make this city desolate, and an hissing; every one that passeth thereby shall be astonished and hiss because of all the plagues thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/19/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:390bd0ab-e325-4919-adc4-37a4f27e658b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 273

Reference: JER 19:9
Text: And I will cause them to eat the flesh of their sons and the flesh of their daughters, and they shall eat every one the flesh of his friend in the siege and straitness, wherewith their enemies, and they that seek their lives, shall straiten them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/19/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:912e9628-006a-43f6-b72a-452ae9de8b29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: JER 19:10
Text: Then shalt thou break the bottle in the sight of the men that go with thee,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/19/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:902f8bfd-0070-408f-a72e-5f0668a52a16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: JER 19:11
Text: And shalt say unto them, Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Even so will I break this people and this city, as one breaketh a potter’s vessel, that cannot be made whole again: and they shall bury them in Tophet, till there be no place to bury.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/19/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a49b27e3-4472-4de6-a9f6-d78826af5ce4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: JER 19:12
Text: Thus will I do unto this place, saith the LORD, and to the inhabitants thereof, and even make this city as Tophet:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/19/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ff83bc4-848f-4687-9595-b8936715f8a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 285

Reference: JER 19:13
Text: And the houses of Jerusalem, and the houses of the kings of Judah, shall be defiled as the place of Tophet, because of all the houses upon whose roofs they have burned incense unto all the host of heaven, and have poured out drink offerings unto other gods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/19/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5262a81-c154-4b3e-b813-9c42d0d191fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: JER 19:14
Text: Then came Jeremiah from Tophet, whither the LORD had sent him to prophesy; and he stood in the court of the LORD’s house; and said to all the people,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/19/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ea1f52c-1066-48b4-9f6f-c33ae4cf3f8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: JER 19:15
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Behold, I will bring upon this city and upon all her towns all the evil that I have pronounced against it, because they have hardened their necks, that they might not hear my words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/20/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5104f2af-04d9-4499-8b78-33f175619811>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: JER 20:1
Text: Now Pashur the son of Immer the priest, who was also chief governor in the house of the LORD, heard that Jeremiah prophesied these things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/20/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aed10f8d-2499-49a7-8b75-9423de549c8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: JER 20:2
Text: Then Pashur smote Jeremiah the prophet, and put him in the stocks that were in the high gate of Benjamin, which was by the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/20/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e530d7b5-c454-4171-b9b5-cd85a8b8fd17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: JER 20:3
Text: And it came to pass on the morrow, that Pashur brought forth Jeremiah out of the stocks. Then said Jeremiah unto him, The LORD hath not called thy name Pashur, but Magormissabib.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/20/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b34f784b-2f90-4cd8-a6b9-50350bf4d613>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 350

Reference: JER 20:4
Text: For thus saith the LORD, Behold, I will make thee a terror to thyself, and to all thy friends: and they shall fall by the sword of their enemies, and thine eyes shall behold it: and I will give all Judah into the hand of the king of Babylon, and he shall carry them captive into Babylon, and shall slay them with the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/20/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3636ab9d-ed76-4ed7-92b8-6f40fba9984c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 301

Reference: JER 20:5
Text: Moreover I will deliver all the strength of this city, and all the labours thereof, and all the precious things thereof, and all the treasures of the kings of Judah will I give into the hand of their enemies, which shall spoil them, and take them, and carry them to Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/20/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35ff946e-7457-4a54-8866-5cbabc763014>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: JER 20:6
Text: And thou, Pashur, and all that dwell in thine house shall go into captivity: and thou shalt come to Babylon, and there thou shalt die, and shalt be buried there, thou, and all thy friends, to whom thou hast prophesied lies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/20/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bc2bd25-2a6b-42cc-aab5-0c921c72ed69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: JER 20:7
Text: O LORD, thou hast deceived me, and I was deceived; thou art stronger than I, and hast prevailed: I am in derision daily, every one mocketh me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/20/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f78aff72-1af0-4d47-b0db-2ea8d0c9cf44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: JER 20:8
Text: For since I spake, I cried out, I cried violence and spoil; because the word of the LORD was made a reproach unto me, and a derision, daily.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/20/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11a7e4c1-ec20-4f09-92aa-d0318f1a068d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: JER 20:9
Text: Then I said, I will not make mention of him, nor speak any more in his name. But his word was in mine heart as a burning fire shut up in my bones, and I was weary with forbearing, and I could not stay.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/20/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c37797a-f2cd-4a26-980f-dcdfc48f200a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: JER 20:10
Text: For I heard the defaming of many, fear on every side. Report, say they, and we will report it. All my familiars watched for my halting, saying, Peradventure he will be enticed, and we shall prevail against him, and we shall take our revenge on him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/20/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22f7ee6c-c37b-49ee-919f-326746edde7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: JER 20:11
Text: But the LORD is with me as a mighty terrible one: therefore my persecutors shall stumble, and they shall not prevail: they shall be greatly ashamed; for they shall not prosper: their everlasting confusion shall never be forgotten.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/20/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94563be9-722a-41e4-b5be-c4c7b5bd1e2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: JER 20:12
Text: But, O LORD of hosts, that triest the righteous, and seest the reins and the heart, let me see thy vengeance on them: for unto thee have I opened my cause.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/20/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2c1932f-a97a-48e0-b15b-eba19973f106>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: JER 20:13
Text: Sing unto the LORD, praise ye the LORD: for he hath delivered the soul of the poor from the hand of evildoers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/20/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe27992c-5815-4a08-ac8c-ac25c6ada35e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: JER 20:14
Text: Cursed be the day wherein I was born: let not the day wherein my mother bare me be blessed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/20/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ddd3950-f079-4f02-ab62-be7cb9d3f8fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: JER 20:15
Text: Cursed be the man who brought tidings to my father, saying, A man child is born unto thee; making him very glad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/20/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef5a124e-9472-40be-8b47-be2eb4fae8f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: JER 20:16
Text: And let that man be as the cities which the LORD overthrew, and repented not: and let him hear the cry in the morning, and the shouting at noontide;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/20/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98321854-1a86-4f9a-9e52-23004c5e1c5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: JER 20:17
Text: Because he slew me not from the womb; or that my mother might have been my grave, and her womb to be always great with me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/20/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8dbf3e7-2d4d-40d8-8e91-6edbe45123c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: JER 20:18
Text: Wherefore came I forth out of the womb to see labour and sorrow, that my days should be consumed with shame?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/21/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d0a7034-21ab-492e-9a58-ff574b8ab3e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: JER 21:1
Text: The word which came unto Jeremiah from the LORD, when king Zedekiah sent unto him Pashur the son of Melchiah, and Zephaniah the son of Maaseiah the priest, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/21/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d52ca2ba-9cb6-46b4-9b85-176d4a36e4fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: JER 21:2
Text: Enquire, I pray thee, of the LORD for us; for Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon maketh war against us; if so be that the LORD will deal with us according to all his wondrous works, that he may go up from us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/21/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43b1d0ea-85b4-4ecb-b869-9c28bf6dd996>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: JER 21:3
Text: Then said Jeremiah unto them, Thus shall ye say to Zedekiah:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/21/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0d25612-8ecc-450c-bc72-c651b084a830>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 295

Reference: JER 21:4
Text: Thus saith the LORD God of Israel; Behold, I will turn back the weapons of war that are in your hands, wherewith ye fight against the king of Babylon, and against the Chaldeans, which besiege you without the walls, and I will assemble them into the midst of this city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/21/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5b66fb2-ba03-4ded-b0fc-b3b000866a1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: JER 21:5
Text: And I myself will fight against you with an outstretched hand and with a strong arm, even in anger, and in fury, and in great wrath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/21/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8042addd-1366-4d54-b863-b011d8864140>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: JER 21:6
Text: And I will smite the inhabitants of this city, both man and beast: they shall die of a great pestilence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/21/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a5685f4-8b49-45e6-b84d-a3b3143737a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 468

Reference: JER 21:7
Text: And afterward, saith the LORD, I will deliver Zedekiah king of Judah, and his servants, and the people, and such as are left in this city from the pestilence, from the sword, and from the famine, into the hand of Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon, and into the hand of their enemies, and into the hand of those that seek their life: and he shall smite them with the edge of the sword; he shall not spare them, neither have pity, nor have mercy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/21/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bd4ff1e-7c8b-426c-89c1-1888dfa02ec0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: JER 21:8
Text: And unto this people thou shalt say, Thus saith the LORD; Behold, I set before you the way of life, and the way of death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/21/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f25b63b-bef6-44f5-8db8-884ca3ccce5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: JER 21:9
Text: He that abideth in this city shall die by the sword, and by the famine, and by the pestilence: but he that goeth out, and falleth to the Chaldeans that besiege you, he shall live, and his life shall be unto him for a prey.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/21/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb530d47-07a1-4a4a-a92a-3594c9cf2932>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: JER 21:10
Text: For I have set my face against this city for evil, and not for good, saith the LORD: it shall be given into the hand of the king of Babylon, and he shall burn it with fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/21/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9bd97e3-7a7e-4043-a801-b7a9212b7fa8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: JER 21:11
Text: And touching the house of the king of Judah, say, Hear ye the word of the LORD;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/21/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6f6a49c-d1a8-4e33-8c06-791424f80a72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 266

Reference: JER 21:12
Text: O house of David, thus saith the LORD; Execute judgment in the morning, and deliver him that is spoiled out of the hand of the oppressor, lest my fury go out like fire, and burn that none can quench it, because of the evil of your doings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/21/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:100e494e-7201-4463-a5d8-db314f42c283>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: JER 21:13
Text: Behold, I am against thee, O inhabitant of the valley, and rock of the plain, saith the LORD; which say, Who shall come down against us? or who shall enter into our habitations?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/21/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5d499d4-3112-4d24-8618-07aaa0dc4402>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: JER 21:14
Text: But I will punish you according to the fruit of your doings, saith the LORD: and I will kindle a fire in the forest thereof, and it shall devour all things round about it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed85ed01-3ed1-4f2d-8323-1e7d1996040c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: JER 22:1
Text: Thus saith the LORD; Go down to the house of the king of Judah, and speak there this word,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d9af8d3-0ce3-43a4-b99d-447077a74b1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: JER 22:2
Text: And say, Hear the word of the LORD, O king of Judah, that sittest upon the throne of David, thou, and thy servants, and thy people that enter in by these gates:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae55c65f-55ce-4ceb-a54c-d49cdf6acae2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: JER 22:3
Text: Thus saith the LORD; Execute ye judgment and righteousness, and deliver the spoiled out of the hand of the oppressor: and do no wrong, do no violence to the stranger, the fatherless, nor the widow, neither shed innocent blood in this place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2f012a5-486d-448d-a2ec-157896d2a2e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: JER 22:4
Text: For if ye do this thing indeed, then shall there enter in by the gates of this house kings sitting upon the throne of David, riding in chariots and on horses, he, and his servants, and his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85c710ff-90fa-416d-81bc-b09803d84b0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: JER 22:5
Text: But if ye will not hear these words, I swear by myself, saith the LORD, that this house shall become a desolation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c2b06df-bfd9-455c-8a47-9b2694b2f091>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: JER 22:6
Text: For thus saith the LORD unto the king’s house of Judah; Thou art Gilead unto me, and the head of Lebanon: yet surely I will make thee a wilderness, and cities which are not inhabited.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34feb6a4-d843-44ad-99a2-c42fe7ced53c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: JER 22:7
Text: And I will prepare destroyers against thee, every one with his weapons: and they shall cut down thy choice cedars, and cast them into the fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8056903-5e69-4396-b5ef-d3ff9875613a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: JER 22:8
Text: And many nations shall pass by this city, and they shall say every man to his neighbour, Wherefore hath the LORD done thus unto this great city?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3dff7d0-a9b0-4a7c-8368-46065470297d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: JER 22:9
Text: Then they shall answer, Because they have forsaken the covenant of the LORD their God, and worshipped other gods, and served them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cdbe1ece-eca2-4439-9a5f-893cfb36d8ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: JER 22:10
Text: Weep ye not for the dead, neither bemoan him: but weep sore for him that goeth away: for he shall return no more, nor see his native country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d674c80a-b467-4eee-bb33-7286bad7f5bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: JER 22:11
Text: For thus saith the LORD touching Shallum the son of Josiah king of Judah, which reigned instead of Josiah his father, which went forth out of this place; He shall not return thither any more:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ecd34173-cd9c-481d-83a2-3329119c0335>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: JER 22:12
Text: But he shall die in the place whither they have led him captive, and shall see this land no more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:572b3351-f2fe-495f-a0d6-4b1d4f72a153>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: JER 22:13
Text: Woe unto him that buildeth his house by unrighteousness, and his chambers by wrong; that useth his neighbour’s service without wages, and giveth him not for his work;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6395520e-8115-4889-9d6d-fbd50cd683fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: JER 22:14
Text: That saith, I will build me a wide house and large chambers, and cutteth him out windows; and it is cieled with cedar, and painted with vermilion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24146a49-9821-455c-bd3b-df0f77c2639a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: JER 22:15
Text: Shalt thou reign, because thou closest thyself in cedar? did not thy father eat and drink, and do judgment and justice, and then it was well with him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc5814e6-0873-4a16-9ce8-0b8db129c198>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: JER 22:16
Text: He judged the cause of the poor and needy; then it was well with him: was not this to know me? saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:162e9773-cdda-4d0b-b270-df378870995b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: JER 22:17
Text: But thine eyes and thine heart are not but for thy covetousness, and for to shed innocent blood, and for oppression, and for violence, to do it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2c093e6-40d0-46e8-84b7-88fecb2e5b04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: JER 22:18
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD concerning Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah; They shall not lament for him, saying, Ah my brother! or, Ah sister! they shall not lament for him, saying, Ah lord! or, Ah his glory!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54e02b98-e47e-42e9-b25d-db608dcfdaa5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: JER 22:19
Text: He shall be buried with the burial of an ass, drawn and cast forth beyond the gates of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e37a55a-a505-4ed0-bf82-0873a1c6d855>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: JER 22:20
Text: Go up to Lebanon, and cry; and lift up thy voice in Bashan, and cry from the passages: for all thy lovers are destroyed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9836d76-58ea-4cc9-80c4-e62ad42d11d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: JER 22:21
Text: I spake unto thee in thy prosperity; but thou saidst, I will not hear. This hath been thy manner from thy youth, that thou obeyedst not my voice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edae8d69-4c89-418c-99ed-dfd9ccde69f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: JER 22:22
Text: The wind shall eat up all thy pastors, and thy lovers shall go into captivity: surely then shalt thou be ashamed and confounded for all thy wickedness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f6e29df-74d4-4a67-b67b-c85ea42dbff4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: JER 22:23
Text: O inhabitant of Lebanon, that makest thy nest in the cedars, how gracious shalt thou be when pangs come upon thee, the pain as of a woman in travail!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0ad12d4-c849-4f60-9fb0-7cea351f670e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: JER 22:24
Text: As I live, saith the LORD, though Coniah the son of Jehoiakim king of Judah were the signet upon my right hand, yet would I pluck thee thence;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61d2573b-394f-499d-875f-38e1d83c2232>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: JER 22:25
Text: And I will give thee into the hand of them that seek thy life, and into the hand of them whose face thou fearest, even into the hand of Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon, and into the hand of the Chaldeans.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:322ff49e-0801-4591-ba6d-07d3e1b24c2b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: JER 22:26
Text: And I will cast thee out, and thy mother that bare thee, into another country, where ye were not born; and there shall ye die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e04491e1-4d23-4d4d-b2e6-aea708125359>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: JER 22:27
Text: But to the land whereunto they desire to return, thither shall they not return.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:beb5d9b3-7f37-4200-9737-8795a3637be8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: JER 22:28
Text: Is this man Coniah a despised broken idol? is he a vessel wherein is no pleasure? wherefore are they cast out, he and his seed, and are cast into a land which they know not?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e160a35-9579-477c-be05-d54f8945daa5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: JER 22:29
Text: O earth, earth, earth, hear the word of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/22/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6f6aa0f-eeef-44d1-8e57-e71d4cdf05a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: JER 22:30
Text: Thus saith the LORD, Write ye this man childless, a man that shall not prosper in his days: for no man of his seed shall prosper, sitting upon the throne of David, and ruling any more in Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d65186f-d356-4741-a31e-fcd163e18a74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: JER 23:1
Text: Woe be unto the pastors that destroy and scatter the sheep of my pasture! saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75e050f2-53e8-4cd2-b6c4-115ec0fb3abb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: JER 23:2
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD God of Israel against the pastors that feed my people; Ye have scattered my flock, and driven them away, and have not visited them: behold, I will visit upon you the evil of your doings, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9f48cd7-1a09-49c5-b0bd-af35a9b025e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: JER 23:3
Text: And I will gather the remnant of my flock out of all countries whither I have driven them, and will bring them again to their folds; and they shall be fruitful and increase.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5cdf40f9-d7ff-4ba8-b98e-0ddb3a96bd73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: JER 23:4
Text: And I will set up shepherds over them which shall feed them: and they shall fear no more, nor be dismayed, neither shall they be lacking, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12a085b1-132c-4905-9e9b-3e0cd78fad9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: JER 23:5
Text: Behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that I will raise unto David a righteous Branch, and a King shall reign and prosper, and shall execute judgment and justice in the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8bb8b5c-b14b-4afa-8133-1e6caecf8b51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: JER 23:6
Text: In his days Judah shall be saved, and Israel shall dwell safely: and this is his name whereby he shall be called, THE LORD OUR RIGHTEOUSNESS.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1a37d57-9aaa-4a87-b290-5e970ffb7e79>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: JER 23:7
Text: Therefore, behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that they shall no more say, The LORD liveth, which brought up the children of Israel out of the land of Egypt;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:204987ae-d701-43a9-96f7-590b10288c7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: JER 23:8
Text: But, The LORD liveth, which brought up and which led the seed of the house of Israel out of the north country, and from all countries whither I had driven them; and they shall dwell in their own land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05958577-f8c2-4ad6-9ea1-bc4464683104>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: JER 23:9
Text: Mine heart within me is broken because of the prophets; all my bones shake; I am like a drunken man, and like a man whom wine hath overcome, because of the LORD, and because of the words of his holiness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa5b1fd4-9bd1-454b-828e-ab7ed9738a06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: JER 23:10
Text: For the land is full of adulterers; for because of swearing the land mourneth; the pleasant places of the wilderness are dried up, and their course is evil, and their force is not right.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb630986-3468-4788-8f30-be71b9329150>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: JER 23:11
Text: For both prophet and priest are profane; yea, in my house have I found their wickedness, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a1b8f3c-76bb-4538-aff5-8eb7fd4042bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: JER 23:12
Text: Wherefore their way shall be unto them as slippery ways in the darkness: they shall be driven on, and fall therein: for I will bring evil upon them, even the year of their visitation, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc1a6b19-c1ce-4354-8260-e61abd23cb3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: JER 23:13
Text: And I have seen folly in the prophets of Samaria; they prophesied in Baal, and caused my people Israel to err.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f1f3a58-9b7e-4a0c-9a9e-cdb1dcf0b127>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 300

Reference: JER 23:14
Text: I have seen also in the prophets of Jerusalem an horrible thing: they commit adultery, and walk in lies: they strengthen also the hands of evildoers, that none doth return from his wickedness; they are all of them unto me as Sodom, and the inhabitants thereof as Gomorrah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05f738a5-efa7-41f0-b34b-4c9bfcc9c05f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: JER 23:15
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD of hosts concerning the prophets; Behold, I will feed them with wormwood, and make them drink the water of gall: for from the prophets of Jerusalem is profaneness gone forth into all the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7af9b458-f598-41f6-a867-d8b1a48438af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: JER 23:16
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts, Hearken not unto the words of the prophets that prophesy unto you: they make you vain: they speak a vision of their own heart, and not out of the mouth of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abd4bc2f-7d28-44c4-83a7-d31d00cf35aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: JER 23:17
Text: They say still unto them that despise me, The LORD hath said, Ye shall have peace; and they say unto every one that walketh after the imagination of his own heart, No evil shall come upon you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a331bc6-b59a-4c1a-b6d1-0bb30c2f7aa2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: JER 23:18
Text: For who hath stood in the counsel of the LORD, and hath perceived and heard his word? who hath marked his word, and heard it?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c967bdeb-83b8-42b6-8230-9b2cbb96fffe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: JER 23:19
Text: Behold, a whirlwind of the LORD is gone forth in fury, even a grievous whirlwind: it shall fall grievously upon the head of the wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f1d4340-4b1e-45a4-9646-7670726a0f27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: JER 23:20
Text: The anger of the LORD shall not return, until he have executed, and till he have performed the thoughts of his heart: in the latter days ye shall consider it perfectly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9df48389-8b38-4814-a439-ce038e171913>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: JER 23:21
Text: I have not sent these prophets, yet they ran: I have not spoken to them, yet they prophesied.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19b6b7bc-85e1-4727-8cb4-8ffbf775cb5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: JER 23:22
Text: But if they had stood in my counsel, and had caused my people to hear my words, then they should have turned them from their evil way, and from the evil of their doings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f85dca33-8b70-4e05-94d1-f0cccc09e419>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: JER 23:23
Text: Am I a God at hand, saith the LORD, and not a God afar off?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5da4a6c2-7cfd-4f8b-b82d-e93987277283>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: JER 23:24
Text: Can any hide himself in secret places that I shall not see him? saith the LORD. Do not I fill heaven and earth? saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eed5a780-92e1-437f-8e02-f59a1be589b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: JER 23:25
Text: I have heard what the prophets said, that prophesy lies in my name, saying, I have dreamed, I have dreamed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2725e31f-fd6b-4894-9d64-9c50728515f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: JER 23:26
Text: How long shall this be in the heart of the prophets that prophesy lies? yea, they are prophets of the deceit of their own heart;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab39862a-46b1-4393-8d4e-4d9a79591d66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: JER 23:27
Text: Which think to cause my people to forget my name by their dreams which they tell every man to his neighbour, as their fathers have forgotten my name for Baal.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e87cf844-2497-4fdd-a757-b5b6580ba81d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: JER 23:28
Text: The prophet that hath a dream, let him tell a dream; and he that hath my word, let him speak my word faithfully. What is the chaff to the wheat? saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:390ffa39-beaa-4b06-b387-2c81c3f73a53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: JER 23:29
Text: Is not my word like as a fire? saith the LORD; and like a hammer that breaketh the rock in pieces?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68d00378-9141-452f-b85c-cac35aa4980d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: JER 23:30
Text: Therefore, behold, I am against the prophets, saith the LORD, that steal my words every one from his neighbour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:701e4a9b-680c-43b9-a965-f16d6a924e80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: JER 23:31
Text: Behold, I am against the prophets, saith the LORD, that use their tongues, and say, He saith.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2567f779-e100-4981-8c73-c1580940a956>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 290

Reference: JER 23:32
Text: Behold, I am against them that prophesy false dreams, saith the LORD, and do tell them, and cause my people to err by their lies, and by their lightness; yet I sent them not, nor commanded them: therefore they shall not profit this people at all, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3be9c414-bd8e-4cca-90b9-38fd3a4369b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: JER 23:33
Text: And when this people, or the prophet, or a priest, shall ask thee, saying, What is the burden of the LORD? thou shalt then say unto them, What burden? I will even forsake you, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ae6a166-240d-46d2-b735-151acf655d33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: JER 23:34
Text: And as for the prophet, and the priest, and the people, that shall say, The burden of the LORD, I will even punish that man and his house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:470c8bbd-71c2-4678-a710-a2b95484f8d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: JER 23:35
Text: Thus shall ye say every one to his neighbour, and every one to his brother, What hath the LORD answered? and, What hath the LORD spoken?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43c99b20-5eea-423a-8a02-dd54b895d2ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: JER 23:36
Text: And the burden of the LORD shall ye mention no more: for every man’s word shall be his burden; for ye have perverted the words of the living God, of the LORD of hosts our God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3427dad-e503-4613-96ba-1c0b54f1bf40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: JER 23:37
Text: Thus shalt thou say to the prophet, What hath the LORD answered thee? and, What hath the LORD spoken?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cbade4c-7bca-4909-9c7f-3dcd3f43aba6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: JER 23:38
Text: But since ye say, The burden of the LORD; therefore thus saith the LORD; Because ye say this word, The burden of the LORD, and I have sent unto you, saying, Ye shall not say, The burden of the LORD;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee260b29-b435-4323-9b44-67bdf678eb8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: JER 23:39
Text: Therefore, behold, I, even I, will utterly forget you, and I will forsake you, and the city that I gave you and your fathers, and cast you out of my presence:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/23/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51ff775f-715b-45c6-ab55-85507e16a80d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: JER 23:40
Text: And I will bring an everlasting reproach upon you, and a perpetual shame, which shall not be forgotten.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/24/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddf9e482-81c8-4c28-97fc-4722ebe6e245>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 338

Reference: JER 24:1
Text: The LORD shewed me, and, behold, two baskets of figs were set before the temple of the LORD, after that Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon had carried away captive Jeconiah the son of Jehoiakim king of Judah, and the princes of Judah, with the carpenters and smiths, from Jerusalem, and had brought them to Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/24/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1d2a395-7c12-4659-8918-ac0b11e11e3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JER 24:2
Text: One basket had very good figs, even like the figs that are first ripe: and the other basket had very naughty figs, which could not be eaten, they were so bad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/24/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f21945bf-d5c1-400c-9f29-38a7f16ea9db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: JER 24:3
Text: Then said the LORD unto me, What seest thou, Jeremiah? And I said, Figs; the good figs, very good; and the evil, very evil, that cannot be eaten, they are so evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/24/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:566e0c0e-cac7-4a55-982a-f008588827fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: JER 24:4
Text: Again the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/24/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fcfafcd-c881-4523-89eb-9dbc487e22a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: JER 24:5
Text: Thus saith the LORD, the God of Israel; Like these good figs, so will I acknowledge them that are carried away captive of Judah, whom I have sent out of this place into the land of the Chaldeans for their good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/24/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89aa3220-85be-4fa8-95ed-3cdd37ac83fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: JER 24:6
Text: For I will set mine eyes upon them for good, and I will bring them again to this land: and I will build them, and not pull them down; and I will plant them, and not pluck them up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/24/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f0136b0-2921-442b-ba70-d28dbdf5431e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: JER 24:7
Text: And I will give them an heart to know me, that I am the LORD: and they shall be my people, and I will be their God: for they shall return unto me with their whole heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/24/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43949f09-a4dc-4684-a31d-67a119a9d91f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: JER 24:8
Text: And as the evil figs, which cannot be eaten, they are so evil; surely thus saith the LORD, So will I give Zedekiah the king of Judah, and his princes, and the residue of Jerusalem, that remain in this land, and them that dwell in the land of Egypt:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/24/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b6ad966-0ffd-4a52-a736-fa3c9a57cc7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: JER 24:9
Text: And I will deliver them to be removed into all the kingdoms of the earth for their hurt, to be a reproach and a proverb, a taunt and a curse, in all places whither I shall drive them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/24/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6116ea77-6e26-437a-b431-fbe71846c9c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JER 24:10
Text: And I will send the sword, the famine, and the pestilence, among them, till they be consumed from off the land that I gave unto them and to their fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ff5999d-c31a-4f41-92f0-47bff192a1d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: JER 25:1
Text: The word that came to Jeremiah concerning all the people of Judah in the fourth year of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah, that was the first year of Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52e228d5-8113-48bb-bd01-82377861a3ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: JER 25:2
Text: The which Jeremiah the prophet spake unto all the people of Judah, and to all the inhabitants of Jerusalem, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2aa9919b-6425-4d49-9ec1-dc61edf3ae95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: JER 25:3
Text: From the thirteenth year of Josiah the son of Amon king of Judah, even unto this day, that is the three and twentieth year, the word of the LORD hath come unto me, and I have spoken unto you, rising early and speaking; but ye have not hearkened.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c06cccb1-6bac-4597-b22b-b49fc9f2590d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: JER 25:4
Text: And the LORD hath sent unto you all his servants the prophets, rising early and sending them; but ye have not hearkened, nor inclined your ear to hear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75f0890e-b9c7-48e9-84e8-7dadf6b6b965>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: JER 25:5
Text: They said, Turn ye again now every one from his evil way, and from the evil of your doings, and dwell in the land that the LORD hath given unto you and to your fathers for ever and ever:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bbba83e7-f5ae-4c69-8327-14eecc434f72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: JER 25:6
Text: And go not after other gods to serve them, and to worship them, and provoke me not to anger with the works of your hands; and I will do you no hurt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0acb036-196c-4954-8e6d-828db787bfe9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: JER 25:7
Text: Yet ye have not hearkened unto me, saith the LORD; that ye might provoke me to anger with the works of your hands to your own hurt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7cf92bf1-58dd-4a9d-ba15-bc4363f93933>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: JER 25:8
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD of hosts; Because ye have not heard my words,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c99f524-4133-4204-ad40-27647d0ad1f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 378

Reference: JER 25:9
Text: Behold, I will send and take all the families of the north, saith the LORD, and Nebuchadrezzar the king of Babylon, my servant, and will bring them against this land, and against the inhabitants thereof, and against all these nations round about, and will utterly destroy them, and make them an astonishment, and an hissing, and perpetual desolations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d9ffdf8-620c-4ea7-ae13-307972ee30ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: JER 25:10
Text: Moreover I will take from them the voice of mirth, and the voice of gladness, the voice of the bridegroom, and the voice of the bride, the sound of the millstones, and the light of the candle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14b8d677-cd9c-4378-a9f9-3244484fbbc3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: JER 25:11
Text: And this whole land shall be a desolation, and an astonishment; and these nations shall serve the king of Babylon seventy years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f25545f2-59ed-4da8-8c1c-3cc4486bbf64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: JER 25:12
Text: And it shall come to pass, when seventy years are accomplished, that I will punish the king of Babylon, and that nation, saith the LORD, for their iniquity, and the land of the Chaldeans, and will make it perpetual desolations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71164ff6-e9b6-4897-8b52-374a732c9ed3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: JER 25:13
Text: And I will bring upon that land all my words which I have pronounced against it, even all that is written in this book, which Jeremiah hath prophesied against all the nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4966a52b-453b-4fb4-854a-7c1ae8705057>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: JER 25:14
Text: For many nations and great kings shall serve themselves of them also: and I will recompense them according to their deeds, and according to the works of their own hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f95c3400-8445-41da-952b-1e2975a9ee9f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: JER 25:15
Text: For thus saith the LORD God of Israel unto me; Take the wine cup of this fury at my hand, and cause all the nations, to whom I send thee, to drink it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff017bad-28a4-4b9b-b68f-4b8b9f753415>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: JER 25:16
Text: And they shall drink, and be moved, and be mad, because of the sword that I will send among them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e16d8cf0-65c8-4d7f-94f5-2f53cd5aca32>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: JER 25:17
Text: Then took I the cup at the LORD’s hand, and made all the nations to drink, unto whom the LORD had sent me:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44582a4e-a06f-4931-a4ac-ed4095a4afb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: JER 25:18
Text: To wit, Jerusalem, and the cities of Judah, and the kings thereof, and the princes thereof, to make them a desolation, an astonishment, an hissing, and a curse; as it is this day;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6cb5288c-aaa9-46b6-9ecb-593b1d6e7014>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: JER 25:19
Text: Pharaoh king of Egypt, and his servants, and his princes, and all his people;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb43dde8-1e02-45e1-b041-5afcd456778f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: JER 25:20
Text: And all the mingled people, and all the kings of the land of Uz, and all the kings of the land of the Philistines, and Ashkelon, and Azzah, and Ekron, and the remnant of Ashdod,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8dbfc33d-adef-40bb-befd-6f0430771033>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 70

Reference: JER 25:21
Text: Edom, and Moab, and the children of Ammon,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d964c71-6829-45a5-83d6-a5ca304d0062>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: JER 25:22
Text: And all the kings of Tyrus, and all the kings of Zidon, and the kings of the isles which are beyond the sea,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0a84eb8-12f3-4632-8ca5-a3386d995149>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: JER 25:23
Text: Dedan, and Tema, and Buz, and all that are in the utmost corners,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1fc3d7b-a808-4cb5-9733-3c5972c21253>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: JER 25:24
Text: And all the kings of Arabia, and all the kings of the mingled people that dwell in the desert,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c1be3ed-d4e8-434e-b021-ab07d79e5366>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: JER 25:25
Text: And all the kings of Zimri, and all the kings of Elam, and all the kings of the Medes,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:269fca1a-0013-49c1-a75f-8b024ace20e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: JER 25:26
Text: And all the kings of the north, far and near, one with another, and all the kingdoms of the world, which are upon the face of the earth: and the king of Sheshach shall drink after them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce7716c0-cc8f-4aa2-9b72-df100a685bf3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: JER 25:27
Text: Therefore thou shalt say unto them, Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Drink ye, and be drunken, and spue, and fall, and rise no more, because of the sword which I will send among you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73448693-4983-443d-8849-cc6e3ad2820c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: JER 25:28
Text: And it shall be, if they refuse to take the cup at thine hand to drink, then shalt thou say unto them, Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Ye shall certainly drink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b8d26f2-4707-4ae6-a5ae-b1999ec17d5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: JER 25:29
Text: For, lo, I begin to bring evil on the city which is called by my name, and should ye be utterly unpunished? Ye shall not be unpunished: for I will call for a sword upon all the inhabitants of the earth, saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed789c1c-fe90-4bea-b4b4-eeb6af78473a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 320

Reference: JER 25:30
Text: Therefore prophesy thou against them all these words, and say unto them, The LORD shall roar from on high, and utter his voice from his holy habitation; he shall mightily roar upon his habitation; he shall give a shout, as they that tread the grapes, against all the inhabitants of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55e78c3d-05e1-47f9-8d4f-96f5c1725d47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: JER 25:31
Text: A noise shall come even to the ends of the earth; for the LORD hath a controversy with the nations, he will plead with all flesh; he will give them that are wicked to the sword, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6fd9466-2793-430c-8d6d-40b374a6351a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: JER 25:32
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts, Behold, evil shall go forth from nation to nation, and a great whirlwind shall be raised up from the coasts of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cce50dfd-f71f-4e64-a13d-b1cddd12e30c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: JER 25:33
Text: And the slain of the LORD shall be at that day from one end of the earth even unto the other end of the earth: they shall not be lamented, neither gathered, nor buried; they shall be dung upon the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47752ec3-79bd-4609-9aa1-406bdc0285db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: JER 25:34
Text: Howl, ye shepherds, and cry; and wallow yourselves in the ashes, ye principal of the flock: for the days of your slaughter and of your dispersions are accomplished; and ye shall fall like a pleasant vessel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed422a77-b921-4055-85de-da0911d7a319>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: JER 25:35
Text: And the shepherds shall have no way to flee, nor the principal of the flock to escape.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33432f45-b8f6-43ed-ac98-2a44d45157fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: JER 25:36
Text: A voice of the cry of the shepherds, and an howling of the principal of the flock, shall be heard: for the LORD hath spoiled their pasture.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b24397a-964d-40ea-8404-f3ab429f2558>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: JER 25:37
Text: And the peaceable habitations are cut down because of the fierce anger of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/25/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7093111-d47a-4cc8-8586-cace1d287d27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: JER 25:38
Text: He hath forsaken his covert, as the lion: for their land is desolate because of the fierceness of the oppressor, and because of his fierce anger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c082edb-9828-48c2-8d99-f10b94c2ce08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: JER 26:1
Text: In the beginning of the reign of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah came this word from the LORD, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91632a2b-37f8-4ae7-b6e9-fbe2118f8585>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: JER 26:2
Text: Thus saith the LORD; Stand in the court of the LORD’s house, and speak unto all the cities of Judah, which come to worship in the LORD’s house, all the words that I command thee to speak unto them; diminish not a word:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:072bdd65-f22d-4793-948e-be000fa03aa3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: JER 26:3
Text: If so be they will hearken, and turn every man from his evil way, that I may repent me of the evil, which I purpose to do unto them because of the evil of their doings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b99b834-37bb-4573-adc7-cfc19cbdebfa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: JER 26:4
Text: And thou shalt say unto them, Thus saith the LORD; If ye will not hearken to me, to walk in my law, which I have set before you,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:372e2441-06a0-46a2-ad11-a2287caaf4c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: JER 26:5
Text: To hearken to the words of my servants the prophets, whom I sent unto you, both rising up early, and sending them, but ye have not hearkened;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:543812b0-07cd-47c0-bb65-043118ed0c95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: JER 26:6
Text: Then will I make this house like Shiloh, and will make this city a curse to all the nations of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:930a037f-cb7d-47f8-a318-a04591e612ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: JER 26:7
Text: So the priests and the prophets and all the people heard Jeremiah speaking these words in the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f59ad9e-b857-4b2e-bf40-8790b2a50930>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: JER 26:8
Text: Now it came to pass, when Jeremiah had made an end of speaking all that the LORD had commanded him to speak unto all the people, that the priests and the prophets and all the people took him, saying, Thou shalt surely die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d97d07b-0908-4c66-9c8e-aeae12d202cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: JER 26:9
Text: Why hast thou prophesied in the name of the LORD, saying, This house shall be like Shiloh, and this city shall be desolate without an inhabitant? And all the people were gathered against Jeremiah in the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d6385af-f651-4532-bfeb-af33e473e92d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: JER 26:10
Text: When the princes of Judah heard these things, then they came up from the king’s house unto the house of the LORD, and sat down in the entry of the new gate of the LORD’s house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f2cbcc3-d26e-4082-9f9d-f72dfa293d7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: JER 26:11
Text: Then spake the priests and the prophets unto the princes and to all the people, saying, This man is worthy to die; for he hath prophesied against this city, as ye have heard with your ears.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4a39019-3edc-4869-ac2d-ff5400e85ec5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: JER 26:12
Text: Then spake Jeremiah unto all the princes and to all the people, saying, The LORD sent me to prophesy against this house and against this city all the words that ye have heard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e260f139-a4e1-4219-8e46-62830426027b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: JER 26:13
Text: Therefore now amend your ways and your doings, and obey the voice of the LORD your God; and the LORD will repent him of the evil that he hath pronounced against you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01db06d2-bf98-48de-9778-ee5c93ff6fa8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: JER 26:14
Text: As for me, behold, I am in your hand: do with me as seemeth good and meet unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0d63269-36b8-49e2-a2e2-b38d35957696>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 273

Reference: JER 26:15
Text: But know ye for certain, that if ye put me to death, ye shall surely bring innocent blood upon yourselves, and upon this city, and upon the inhabitants thereof: for of a truth the LORD hath sent me unto you to speak all these words in your ears.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2e8d660-f414-41c5-a3b8-d88392640fd0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: JER 26:16
Text: Then said the princes and all the people unto the priests and to the prophets; This man is not worthy to die: for he hath spoken to us in the name of the LORD our God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d8f7081-a0ee-4740-b054-1f50bec97076>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: JER 26:17
Text: Then rose up certain of the elders of the land, and spake to all the assembly of the people, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f356ea4a-9702-4f56-bcf0-021a4395ed41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 305

Reference: JER 26:18
Text: Micah the Morasthite prophesied in the days of Hezekiah king of Judah, and spake to all the people of Judah, saying, Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Zion shall be plowed like a field, and Jerusalem shall become heaps, and the mountain of the house as the high places of a forest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79cd1904-e810-44fb-a5fc-41c6d50cf81b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: JER 26:19
Text: Did Hezekiah king of Judah and all Judah put him at all to death? did he not fear the LORD, and besought the LORD, and the LORD repented him of the evil which he had pronounced against them? Thus might we procure great evil against our souls.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a051f43-df21-4f6a-a2ea-298c437a78e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: JER 26:20
Text: And there was also a man that prophesied in the name of the LORD, Urijah the son of Shemaiah of Kirjathjearim, who prophesied against this city and against this land according to all the words of Jeremiah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a17e6099-0ef4-40f9-a264-459502d5c1e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: JER 26:21
Text: And when Jehoiakim the king, with all his mighty men, and all the princes, heard his words, the king sought to put him to death: but when Urijah heard it, he was afraid, and fled, and went into Egypt;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ebd83b4-1c6e-44ee-97d1-72553f7a90e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: JER 26:22
Text: And Jehoiakim the king sent men into Egypt, namely, Elnathan the son of Achbor, and certain men with him into Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91a746fb-e43c-4c85-a443-60cc875573d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: JER 26:23
Text: And they fetched forth Urijah out of Egypt, and brought him unto Jehoiakim the king; who slew him with the sword, and cast his dead body into the graves of the common people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/26/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b67c617e-4aef-4f6c-a0f3-0b173f93877f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: JER 26:24
Text: Nevertheless the hand of Ahikam the son of Shaphan was with Jeremiah, that they should not give him into the hand of the people to put him to death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/27/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:458dc597-d56a-4a5c-b9f6-22b7e2b931fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: JER 27:1
Text: In the beginning of the reign of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah came this word unto Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/27/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6192d389-f672-4ab6-a9c9-1088a21a47af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: JER 27:2
Text: Thus saith the LORD to me; Make thee bonds and yokes, and put them upon thy neck,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/27/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64c4dd64-c279-4997-a5d3-00d34a048b3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: JER 27:3
Text: And send them to the king of Edom, and to the king of Moab, and to the king of the Ammonites, and to the king of Tyrus, and to the king of Zidon, by the hand of the messengers which come to Jerusalem unto Zedekiah king of Judah;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/27/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a2b0c12-2c90-467a-b69e-24dc8bf501a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: JER 27:4
Text: And command them to say unto their masters, Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Thus shall ye say unto your masters;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/27/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:516faa3a-d7a1-40f9-acb1-0df5be791c95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: JER 27:5
Text: I have made the earth, the man and the beast that are upon the ground, by my great power and by my outstretched arm, and have given it unto whom it seemed meet unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/27/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf4cb307-adfc-43ac-bb0c-104a1eb37a4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: JER 27:6
Text: And now have I given all these lands into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon, my servant; and the beasts of the field have I given him also to serve him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/27/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ef76c87-3e7e-42dc-b38d-ad71af5d4e1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: JER 27:7
Text: And all nations shall serve him, and his son, and his son’s son, until the very time of his land come: and then many nations and great kings shall serve themselves of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/27/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d2aadf2-00e3-495b-8d66-a44cba5f7360>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 364

Reference: JER 27:8
Text: And it shall come to pass, that the nation and kingdom which will not serve the same Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon, and that will not put their neck under the yoke of the king of Babylon, that nation will I punish, saith the LORD, with the sword, and with the famine, and with the pestilence, until I have consumed them by his hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/27/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c6e50d1-05df-4927-9536-7d8e258ce465>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: JER 27:9
Text: Therefore hearken not ye to your prophets, nor to your diviners, nor to your dreamers, nor to your enchanters, nor to your sorcerers, which speak unto you, saying, Ye shall not serve the king of Babylon:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/27/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a770fcf-05f6-41e1-957c-6a8322f07c8e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: JER 27:10
Text: For they prophesy a lie unto you, to remove you far from your land; and that I should drive you out, and ye should perish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/27/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa8b8dd7-b3f8-480e-af0e-2fa8760aad88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: JER 27:11
Text: But the nations that bring their neck under the yoke of the king of Babylon, and serve him, those will I let remain still in their own land, saith the LORD; and they shall till it, and dwell therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/27/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:448d98e9-7776-4f5f-ab98-7af34a8637d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: JER 27:12
Text: I spake also to Zedekiah king of Judah according to all these words, saying, Bring your necks under the yoke of the king of Babylon, and serve him and his people, and live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/27/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82bbd5d7-5d0e-408c-8979-daf91782c8e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: JER 27:13
Text: Why will ye die, thou and thy people, by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence, as the LORD hath spoken against the nation that will not serve the king of Babylon?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/27/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7d0b1f5-a783-4d41-a706-09d7c99eff5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: JER 27:14
Text: Therefore hearken not unto the words of the prophets that speak unto you, saying, Ye shall not serve the king of Babylon: for they prophesy a lie unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/27/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4625a3f0-eaf1-42a6-8bf2-0b9ff641b5ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: JER 27:15
Text: For I have not sent them, saith the LORD, yet they prophesy a lie in my name; that I might drive you out, and that ye might perish, ye, and the prophets that prophesy unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/27/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8b1205e-8257-4084-b5de-33caa53e2fc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 307

Reference: JER 27:16
Text: Also I spake to the priests and to all this people, saying, Thus saith the LORD; Hearken not to the words of your prophets that prophesy unto you, saying, Behold, the vessels of the LORD’s house shall now shortly be brought again from Babylon: for they prophesy a lie unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/27/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2b7f8e8-4f20-4513-a454-834595f29b14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: JER 27:17
Text: Hearken not unto them; serve the king of Babylon, and live: wherefore should this city be laid waste?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/27/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63c290b8-df1c-4d09-9e8b-4362ae30521e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 281

Reference: JER 27:18
Text: But if they be prophets, and if the word of the LORD be with them, let them now make intercession to the LORD of hosts, that the vessels which are left in the house of the LORD, and in the house of the king of Judah, and at Jerusalem, go not to Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/27/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6df0e3a-b8ca-49bb-a184-f47718f76541>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: JER 27:19
Text: For thus saith the LORD of hosts concerning the pillars, and concerning the sea, and concerning the bases, and concerning the residue of the vessels that remain in this city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/27/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca06dc40-6fbc-494e-a6d3-0f2a3ee19a13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: JER 27:20
Text: Which Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon took not, when he carried away captive Jeconiah the son of Jehoiakim king of Judah from Jerusalem to Babylon, and all the nobles of Judah and Jerusalem;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/27/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a8ab2d8-90aa-40f3-b2ce-24ce7afa974c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: JER 27:21
Text: Yea, thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, concerning the vessels that remain in the house of the LORD, and in the house of the king of Judah and of Jerusalem;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/27/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:395eb836-a997-416b-b0a4-0e1254fc642c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: JER 27:22
Text: They shall be carried to Babylon, and there shall they be until the day that I visit them, saith the LORD; then will I bring them up, and restore them to this place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/28/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:144ed558-6180-484a-8d15-7dd2fede2b6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 328

Reference: JER 28:1
Text: And it came to pass the same year, in the beginning of the reign of Zedekiah king of Judah, in the fourth year, and in the fifth month, that Hananiah the son of Azur the prophet, which was of Gibeon, spake unto me in the house of the LORD, in the presence of the priests and of all the people, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/28/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ecbbb14-2a88-454a-8d16-ddfd15024c4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: JER 28:2
Text: Thus speaketh the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, saying, I have broken the yoke of the king of Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/28/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc81d553-4eba-47c4-ba9c-7165d4610bc8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: JER 28:3
Text: Within two full years will I bring again into this place all the vessels of the LORD’s house, that Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon took away from this place, and carried them to Babylon:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/28/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92a722dc-0c30-46ec-a883-93384110c8f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: JER 28:4
Text: And I will bring again to this place Jeconiah the son of Jehoiakim king of Judah, with all the captives of Judah, that went into Babylon, saith the LORD: for I will break the yoke of the king of Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/28/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d989116d-5004-47fa-bfa9-cea7a0c1b0db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: JER 28:5
Text: Then the prophet Jeremiah said unto the prophet Hananiah in the presence of the priests, and in the presence of all the people that stood in the house of the LORD,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/28/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c460049-0da8-4c4e-ac55-408bdac142b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: JER 28:6
Text: Even the prophet Jeremiah said, Amen: the LORD do so: the LORD perform thy words which thou hast prophesied, to bring again the vessels of the LORD’s house, and all that is carried away captive, from Babylon into this place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/28/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9ee2dba-a86e-4efb-9088-faf98a86a7d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: JER 28:7
Text: Nevertheless hear thou now this word that I speak in thine ears, and in the ears of all the people;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/28/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32e2d80a-80c4-4e9e-95c6-c79a43695090>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: JER 28:8
Text: The prophets that have been before me and before thee of old prophesied both against many countries, and against great kingdoms, of war, and of evil, and of pestilence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/28/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bbaa7964-20e9-4cda-b744-c1e4f1113b4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: JER 28:9
Text: The prophet which prophesieth of peace, when the word of the prophet shall come to pass, then shall the prophet be known, that the LORD hath truly sent him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/28/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d37ea43-232c-4fc5-83a3-6c0643af4fa6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: JER 28:10
Text: Then Hananiah the prophet took the yoke from off the prophet Jeremiah’s neck, and brake it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/28/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:598c3c32-65be-4784-abbe-3808fe468c77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 278

Reference: JER 28:11
Text: And Hananiah spake in the presence of all the people, saying, Thus saith the LORD; Even so will I break the yoke of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon from the neck of all nations within the space of two full years. And the prophet Jeremiah went his way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/28/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59e32419-1c47-4e57-8f2b-a97d551ce52c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: JER 28:12
Text: Then the word of the LORD came unto Jeremiah the prophet, after that Hananiah the prophet had broken the yoke from off the neck of the prophet Jeremiah, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/28/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a9de744-9033-4fa5-ba1b-dc27b4b0a4d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: JER 28:13
Text: Go and tell Hananiah, saying, Thus saith the LORD; Thou hast broken the yokes of wood; but thou shalt make for them yokes of iron.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/28/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:903b708c-9913-45fe-b38e-4006201fad2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: JER 28:14
Text: For thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; I have put a yoke of iron upon the neck of all these nations, that they may serve Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon; and they shall serve him: and I have given him the beasts of the field also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/28/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2034a8a-e495-4e7c-bf29-54a0a42280a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: JER 28:15
Text: Then said the prophet Jeremiah unto Hananiah the prophet, Hear now, Hananiah; The LORD hath not sent thee; but thou makest this people to trust in a lie.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/28/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73d697c0-f225-40cf-b3ea-b93213d4d45b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: JER 28:16
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD; Behold, I will cast thee from off the face of the earth: this year thou shalt die, because thou hast taught rebellion against the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/28/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f21bba32-dfc5-4f57-af55-b0bf32fbb6d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: JER 28:17
Text: So Hananiah the prophet died the same year in the seventh month.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bdbede3f-b405-4a11-9c66-453248bbef54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 310

Reference: JER 29:1
Text: Now these are the words of the letter that Jeremiah the prophet sent from Jerusalem unto the residue of the elders which were carried away captives, and to the priests, and to the prophets, and to all the people whom Nebuchadnezzar had carried away captive from Jerusalem to Babylon;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:111a54c1-facf-4307-866d-9d2a70188455>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: JER 29:2
Text: (After that Jeconiah the king, and the queen, and the eunuchs, the princes of Judah and Jerusalem, and the carpenters, and the smiths, were departed from Jerusalem;)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:736a7dee-d30d-4bf8-bd5e-debfe0edc7e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: JER 29:3
Text: By the hand of Elasah the son of Shaphan, and Gemariah the son of Hilkiah, (whom Zedekiah king of Judah sent unto Babylon to Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon) saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d4b33cd-f415-40a0-9240-8fbcc854649d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: JER 29:4
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, unto all that are carried away captives, whom I have caused to be carried away from Jerusalem unto Babylon;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a55cfb73-a3dd-41bd-b7e7-1aa959503815>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: JER 29:5
Text: Build ye houses, and dwell in them; and plant gardens, and eat the fruit of them;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be2be895-711f-45a9-9398-b7f70a79f182>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: JER 29:6
Text: Take ye wives, and beget sons and daughters; and take wives for your sons, and give your daughters to husbands, that they may bear sons and daughters; that ye may be increased there, and not diminished.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3361f42d-2b3e-4876-9512-74c940d7814c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: JER 29:7
Text: And seek the peace of the city whither I have caused you to be carried away captives, and pray unto the LORD for it: for in the peace thereof shall ye have peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b3237a5-15b3-46b0-9c80-0f1d080860d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: JER 29:8
Text: For thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Let not your prophets and your diviners, that be in the midst of you, deceive you, neither hearken to your dreams which ye cause to be dreamed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1ac7ff4-c8a1-4e3a-ad10-cfbe787b7813>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: JER 29:9
Text: For they prophesy falsely unto you in my name: I have not sent them, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b934141-74e7-436e-bdb7-7caec0707f21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: JER 29:10
Text: For thus saith the LORD, That after seventy years be accomplished at Babylon I will visit you, and perform my good word toward you, in causing you to return to this place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:060e8281-4922-4024-b964-a8c35fd6fe86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: JER 29:11
Text: For I know the thoughts that I think toward you, saith the LORD, thoughts of peace, and not of evil, to give you an expected end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c3b562a-5c74-4c42-a28e-bc24fafd6924>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: JER 29:12
Text: Then shall ye call upon me, and ye shall go and pray unto me, and I will hearken unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6dd9bbb6-a92f-4d47-b41d-94d5324bbf1e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: JER 29:13
Text: And ye shall seek me, and find me, when ye shall search for me with all your heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:899bcf5c-2db6-4050-8f30-744f11f1b251>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 309

Reference: JER 29:14
Text: And I will be found of you, saith the LORD: and I will turn away your captivity, and I will gather you from all the nations, and from all the places whither I have driven you, saith the LORD; and I will bring you again into the place whence I caused you to be carried away captive.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f124adb-41a5-4206-bae8-16ed5117c724>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: JER 29:15
Text: Because ye have said, The LORD hath raised us up prophets in Babylon;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:223e6b0b-f431-4301-a2c6-f8f389cea3db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: JER 29:16
Text: Know that thus saith the LORD of the king that sitteth upon the throne of David, and of all the people that dwelleth in this city, and of your brethren that are not gone forth with you into captivity;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef958221-a8c1-41fb-acea-e67fd7e4a992>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: JER 29:17
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Behold, I will send upon them the sword, the famine, and the pestilence, and will make them like vile figs, that cannot be eaten, they are so evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dea647da-800e-435f-813e-7bbd90d909cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 299

Reference: JER 29:18
Text: And I will persecute them with the sword, with the famine, and with the pestilence, and will deliver them to be removed to all the kingdoms of the earth, to be a curse, and an astonishment, and an hissing, and a reproach, among all the nations whither I have driven them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edfff5c5-1c16-4054-8fcc-91f5ac8008d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: JER 29:19
Text: Because they have not hearkened to my words, saith the LORD, which I sent unto them by my servants the prophets, rising up early and sending them; but ye would not hear, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01abe427-c613-460a-9fbf-5a8bdf88e8db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: JER 29:20
Text: Hear ye therefore the word of the LORD, all ye of the captivity, whom I have sent from Jerusalem to Babylon:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9add50f-b91f-4973-801a-471ed4692d99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 301

Reference: JER 29:21
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, of Ahab the son of Kolaiah, and of Zedekiah the son of Maaseiah, which prophesy a lie unto you in my name; Behold, I will deliver them into the hand of Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon; and he shall slay them before your eyes;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8bffe5b-c02a-4b2e-8cdf-43d30a65a380>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: JER 29:22
Text: And of them shall be taken up a curse by all the captivity of Judah which are in Babylon, saying, The LORD make thee like Zedekiah and like Ahab, whom the king of Babylon roasted in the fire;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93cef6d5-5531-472d-b9fe-db888b54546f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: JER 29:23
Text: Because they have committed villany in Israel, and have committed adultery with their neighbours’ wives, and have spoken lying words in my name, which I have not commanded them; even I know, and am a witness, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b33d0424-e4e9-4a34-9aab-72b9c717bbdc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: JER 29:24
Text: Thus shalt thou also speak to Shemaiah the Nehelamite, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:235013d5-5068-489f-baff-c79c68b0d525>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: JER 29:25
Text: Thus speaketh the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, saying, Because thou hast sent letters in thy name unto all the people that are at Jerusalem, and to Zephaniah the son of Maaseiah the priest, and to all the priests, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88df354a-d4c1-49ae-bb5f-f6a9f5e45a61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: JER 29:26
Text: The LORD hath made thee priest in the stead of Jehoiada the priest, that ye should be officers in the house of the LORD, for every man that is mad, and maketh himself a prophet, that thou shouldest put him in prison, and in the stocks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be29c787-b7bc-4b06-adac-b8a33065763f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: JER 29:27
Text: Now therefore why hast thou not reproved Jeremiah of Anathoth, which maketh himself a prophet to you?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc3faa7e-c269-4902-b7f0-4cda58f078ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: JER 29:28
Text: For therefore he sent unto us in Babylon, saying, This captivity is long: build ye houses, and dwell in them; and plant gardens, and eat the fruit of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60247929-9366-4711-beab-019c5954f57a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: JER 29:29
Text: And Zephaniah the priest read this letter in the ears of Jeremiah the prophet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a400c56-b031-477f-bc47-ebfd911c8fbe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: JER 29:30
Text: Then came the word of the LORD unto Jeremiah, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30e25ed8-d5fc-437e-aa4f-c78d13a6bcfb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: JER 29:31
Text: Send to all them of the captivity, saying, Thus saith the LORD concerning Shemaiah the Nehelamite; Because that Shemaiah hath prophesied unto you, and I sent him not, and he caused you to trust in a lie:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/29/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b10a44b1-9ec9-4ca0-9ce8-ef80ac8a2817>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 301

Reference: JER 29:32
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD; Behold, I will punish Shemaiah the Nehelamite, and his seed: he shall not have a man to dwell among this people; neither shall he behold the good that I will do for my people, saith the LORD; because he hath taught rebellion against the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37c026ca-dda6-42d7-aa51-ccf2ae79a05f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: JER 30:1
Text: The word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96f13267-32df-4d3a-956a-c8bd99af3615>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: JER 30:2
Text: Thus speaketh the LORD God of Israel, saying, Write thee all the words that I have spoken unto thee in a book.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42ad9ddb-4c2e-4ebe-ab77-b4ca917d453e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: JER 30:3
Text: For, lo, the days come, saith the LORD, that I will bring again the captivity of my people Israel and Judah, saith the LORD: and I will cause them to return to the land that I gave to their fathers, and they shall possess it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2555114a-f895-4a31-817d-4edf806eefb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: JER 30:4
Text: And these are the words that the LORD spake concerning Israel and concerning Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5fbc546b-5f00-463b-90ab-b87d03db4a20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: JER 30:5
Text: For thus saith the LORD; We have heard a voice of trembling, of fear, and not of peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:891aa352-8853-41d4-a4ab-a6ac24c0d8d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: JER 30:6
Text: Ask ye now, and see whether a man doth travail with child? wherefore do I see every man with his hands on his loins, as a woman in travail, and all faces are turned into paleness?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95e7f5d3-9a8b-44b7-93fe-0f516177feb5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: JER 30:7
Text: Alas! for that day is great, so that none is like it: it is even the time of Jacob’s trouble, but he shall be saved out of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98d5b75a-5398-4d9e-be1d-60f8a777032a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: JER 30:8
Text: For it shall come to pass in that day, saith the LORD of hosts, that I will break his yoke from off thy neck, and will burst thy bonds, and strangers shall no more serve themselves of him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4dafbc77-c148-4198-b519-8a3dd1069aa8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: JER 30:9
Text: But they shall serve the LORD their God, and David their king, whom I will raise up unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b208b07a-2d11-49b2-b1d7-d5a82ce1ea9e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 295

Reference: JER 30:10
Text: Therefore fear thou not, O my servant Jacob, saith the LORD; neither be dismayed, O Israel: for, lo, I will save thee from afar, and thy seed from the land of their captivity; and Jacob shall return, and shall be in rest, and be quiet, and none shall make him afraid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:418bf83a-a39b-40be-922f-93bab33427b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: JER 30:11
Text: For I am with thee, saith the LORD, to save thee: though I make a full end of all nations whither I have scattered thee, yet I will not make a full end of thee: but I will correct thee in measure, and will not leave thee altogether unpunished.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:310382c7-7eb8-43b1-939d-472a87ff8f23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: JER 30:12
Text: For thus saith the LORD, Thy bruise is incurable, and thy wound is grievous.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d7af4da-a21f-4a9e-9591-1803525cface>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: JER 30:13
Text: There is none to plead thy cause, that thou mayest be bound up: thou hast no healing medicines.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3049a467-c548-46b9-8783-349945190e30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: JER 30:14
Text: All thy lovers have forgotten thee; they seek thee not; for I have wounded thee with the wound of an enemy, with the chastisement of a cruel one, for the multitude of thine iniquity; because thy sins were increased.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:305ed6da-6d82-4929-9262-1d9b30c9eb90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: JER 30:15
Text: Why criest thou for thine affliction? thy sorrow is incurable for the multitude of thine iniquity: because thy sins were increased, I have done these things unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d17efd9-a661-4ac7-a1f7-82c90c337db3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: JER 30:16
Text: Therefore all they that devour thee shall be devoured; and all thine adversaries, every one of them, shall go into captivity; and they that spoil thee shall be a spoil, and all that prey upon thee will I give for a prey.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1835c5ee-f09d-4df2-97c3-1e0ef7c55d27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: JER 30:17
Text: For I will restore health unto thee, and I will heal thee of thy wounds, saith the LORD; because they called thee an Outcast, saying, This is Zion, whom no man seeketh after.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e152eff4-554a-41d0-bc64-fb3dbad90d7a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: JER 30:18
Text: Thus saith the LORD; Behold, I will bring again the captivity of Jacob’s tents, and have mercy on his dwellingplaces; and the city shall be builded upon her own heap, and the palace shall remain after the manner thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc6e5192-3e2b-4e60-a54b-d21a6027f29e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: JER 30:19
Text: And out of them shall proceed thanksgiving and the voice of them that make merry: and I will multiply them, and they shall not be few; I will also glorify them, and they shall not be small.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26975dee-46a7-42eb-a9bd-4772eab057d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: JER 30:20
Text: Their children also shall be as aforetime, and their congregation shall be established before me, and I will punish all that oppress them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77583f88-a3bf-4a42-bf17-b55e6b6d581a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: JER 30:21
Text: And their nobles shall be of themselves, and their governor shall proceed from the midst of them; and I will cause him to draw near, and he shall approach unto me: for who is this that engaged his heart to approach unto me? saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:150fc9a6-ceec-4abe-81a1-195c7a1da136>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: JER 30:22
Text: And ye shall be my people, and I will be your God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4cf4bc75-88c4-49b8-ab98-2845a86993d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: JER 30:23
Text: Behold, the whirlwind of the LORD goeth forth with fury, a continuing whirlwind: it shall fall with pain upon the head of the wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/30/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3bf1a24a-170e-47ab-9f42-ff31cb5186ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: JER 30:24
Text: The fierce anger of the LORD shall not return, until he hath done it, and until he have performed the intents of his heart: in the latter days ye shall consider it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77afc590-5e61-4e1f-8615-187c0c960d1e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: JER 31:1
Text: At the same time, saith the LORD, will I be the God of all the families of Israel, and they shall be my people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8e7d69e-837d-4e04-ab8e-d357a9661b8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: JER 31:2
Text: Thus saith the LORD, The people which were left of the sword found grace in the wilderness; even Israel, when I went to cause him to rest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa8a80ed-a22e-4ac3-96aa-403efa437505>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: JER 31:3
Text: The LORD hath appeared of old unto me, saying, Yea, I have loved thee with an everlasting love: therefore with lovingkindness have I drawn thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0829f8d-02d5-4bce-899c-de51cb8a670e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: JER 31:4
Text: Again I will build thee, and thou shalt be built, O virgin of Israel: thou shalt again be adorned with thy tabrets, and shalt go forth in the dances of them that make merry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16a288d8-ce31-48dc-af01-a24faa90930a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: JER 31:5
Text: Thou shalt yet plant vines upon the mountains of Samaria: the planters shall plant, and shall eat them as common things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0d5fc0c-f70b-41e6-952b-ca428a6ed05b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: JER 31:6
Text: For there shall be a day, that the watchmen upon the mount Ephraim shall cry, Arise ye, and let us go up to Zion unto the LORD our God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a14087d-da33-4cf2-98a3-4e34ec16dbf1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: JER 31:7
Text: For thus saith the LORD; Sing with gladness for Jacob, and shout among the chief of the nations: publish ye, praise ye, and say, O LORD, save thy people, the remnant of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b18a6b1-41a7-44ba-8403-2c535d802550>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: JER 31:8
Text: Behold, I will bring them from the north country, and gather them from the coasts of the earth, and with them the blind and the lame, the woman with child and her that travaileth with child together: a great company shall return thither.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2079dee-6e56-4ccd-9b98-814145d03e84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: JER 31:9
Text: They shall come with weeping, and with supplications will I lead them: I will cause them to walk by the rivers of waters in a straight way, wherein they shall not stumble: for I am a father to Israel, and Ephraim is my firstborn.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:557fb994-cda7-4583-b330-dafe56766076>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: JER 31:10
Text: Hear the word of the LORD, O ye nations, and declare it in the isles afar off, and say, He that scattered Israel will gather him, and keep him, as a shepherd doth his flock.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb0922c3-1c47-4d81-8a26-e4645c51dd58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: JER 31:11
Text: For the LORD hath redeemed Jacob, and ransomed him from the hand of him that was stronger than he.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dcc44338-f39b-4966-afa4-ce4cee3d619a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 312

Reference: JER 31:12
Text: Therefore they shall come and sing in the height of Zion, and shall flow together to the goodness of the LORD, for wheat, and for wine, and for oil, and for the young of the flock and of the herd: and their soul shall be as a watered garden; and they shall not sorrow any more at all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae52c513-1eba-4d4a-ada3-d7012ad0a37d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: JER 31:13
Text: Then shall the virgin rejoice in the dance, both young men and old together: for I will turn their mourning into joy, and will comfort them, and make them rejoice from their sorrow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1940ce5b-1e08-4a4f-b810-c32f80fe4376>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: JER 31:14
Text: And I will satiate the soul of the priests with fatness, and my people shall be satisfied with my goodness, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02be8538-44f7-45ed-b784-29dcb423e52f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: JER 31:15
Text: Thus saith the LORD; A voice was heard in Ramah, lamentation, and bitter weeping; Rahel weeping for her children refused to be comforted for her children, because they were not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:186fe999-e4d6-4059-bbda-c1ff14673773>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: JER 31:16
Text: Thus saith the LORD; Refrain thy voice from weeping, and thine eyes from tears: for thy work shall be rewarded, saith the LORD; and they shall come again from the land of the enemy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6a6f413-07b3-4a4e-bcff-f26b0bbc5a2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: JER 31:17
Text: And there is hope in thine end, saith the LORD, that thy children shall come again to their own border.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70a6e11b-68ba-4e39-ad51-c079f9ccc067>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: JER 31:18
Text: I have surely heard Ephraim bemoaning himself thus; Thou hast chastised me, and I was chastised, as a bullock unaccustomed to the yoke: turn thou me, and I shall be turned; for thou art the LORD my God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01f6524a-4689-405c-88b0-6aa6c8a3d945>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: JER 31:19
Text: Surely after that I was turned, I repented; and after that I was instructed, I smote upon my thigh: I was ashamed, yea, even confounded, because I did bear the reproach of my youth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b46a9476-8c7e-492d-817c-ca0deadad355>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: JER 31:20
Text: Is Ephraim my dear son? is he a pleasant child? for since I spake against him, I do earnestly remember him still: therefore my bowels are troubled for him; I will surely have mercy upon him, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88c38fed-240b-48f7-9ed2-57cda8d70430>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: JER 31:21
Text: Set thee up waymarks, make thee high heaps: set thine heart toward the highway, even the way which thou wentest: turn again, O virgin of Israel, turn again to these thy cities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:229e4733-8a70-465f-9b0b-782436ba505e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: JER 31:22
Text: How long wilt thou go about, O thou backsliding daughter? for the LORD hath created a new thing in the earth, A woman shall compass a man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:631a9110-e8d2-49aa-aa65-43cdc4fd41a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: JER 31:23
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; As yet they shall use this speech in the land of Judah and in the cities thereof, when I shall bring again their captivity; The LORD bless thee, O habitation of justice, and mountain of holiness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69ca56c0-82a3-49b4-84ca-ec309e5dd45e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: JER 31:24
Text: And there shall dwell in Judah itself, and in all the cities thereof together, husbandmen, and they that go forth with flocks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3c75c76-4153-460b-bfc3-aef97b217ac0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: JER 31:25
Text: For I have satiated the weary soul, and I have replenished every sorrowful soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ece6bf9-0aee-418b-8b2e-2043b2caecd4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: JER 31:26
Text: Upon this I awaked, and beheld; and my sleep was sweet unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1d05a99-3f98-4054-acf5-2493354c79d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: JER 31:27
Text: Behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that I will sow the house of Israel and the house of Judah with the seed of man, and with the seed of beast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88faab47-5d3d-4894-bcdb-aa00c3dc4db1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: JER 31:28
Text: And it shall come to pass, that like as I have watched over them, to pluck up, and to break down, and to throw down, and to destroy, and to afflict; so will I watch over them, to build, and to plant, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13ca97ce-5176-4736-9b4e-1f75495439c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: JER 31:29
Text: In those days they shall say no more, The fathers have eaten a sour grape, and the children’s teeth are set on edge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
