Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: JER 31:30
Text: But every one shall die for his own iniquity: every man that eateth the sour grape, his teeth shall be set on edge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a4ce276-4d11-4a67-a125-96e670c37e41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: JER 31:31
Text: Behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that I will make a new covenant with the house of Israel, and with the house of Judah:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f907618-691a-4e6c-ba4f-9a69ded587bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: JER 31:32
Text: Not according to the covenant that I made with their fathers in the day that I took them by the hand to bring them out of the land of Egypt; which my covenant they brake, although I was an husband unto them, saith the LORD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae344c61-7ade-4eae-a394-b5ad0d3790f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: JER 31:33
Text: But this shall be the covenant that I will make with the house of Israel; After those days, saith the LORD, I will put my law in their inward parts, and write it in their hearts; and will be their God, and they shall be my people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c84e0fc3-6c71-4470-af84-14e32ed98cfe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 299

Reference: JER 31:34
Text: And they shall teach no more every man his neighbour, and every man his brother, saying, Know the LORD: for they shall all know me, from the least of them unto the greatest of them, saith the LORD: for I will forgive their iniquity, and I will remember their sin no more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea171bf0-b901-423f-b177-a91e786ac365>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: JER 31:35
Text: Thus saith the LORD, which giveth the sun for a light by day, and the ordinances of the moon and of the stars for a light by night, which divideth the sea when the waves thereof roar; The LORD of hosts is his name:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:839a35c8-fa62-4e97-aaec-ea34f2e881f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: JER 31:36
Text: If those ordinances depart from before me, saith the LORD, then the seed of Israel also shall cease from being a nation before me for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae5ceaa6-c11f-4456-b2b8-67ff34ab8005>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: JER 31:37
Text: Thus saith the LORD; If heaven above can be measured, and the foundations of the earth searched out beneath, I will also cast off all the seed of Israel for all that they have done, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8fd8cc7-7846-4e5d-b59e-a07f70ea7d1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: JER 31:38
Text: Behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that the city shall be built to the LORD from the tower of Hananeel unto the gate of the corner.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f472afe1-0230-43ba-a154-9ea7461d2005>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: JER 31:39
Text: And the measuring line shall yet go forth over against it upon the hill Gareb, and shall compass about to Goath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/31/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:800c3dc6-f3bf-4c07-af10-25c104b77656>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 274

Reference: JER 31:40
Text: And the whole valley of the dead bodies, and of the ashes, and all the fields unto the brook of Kidron, unto the corner of the horse gate toward the east, shall be holy unto the LORD; it shall not be plucked up, nor thrown down any more for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83a0e9bc-5956-44a2-bfb2-631710d556ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: JER 32:1
Text: The word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD in the tenth year of Zedekiah king of Judah, which was the eighteenth year of Nebuchadrezzar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63ab2a43-5a29-454a-b930-cdbea886a7bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: JER 32:2
Text: For then the king of Babylon’s army besieged Jerusalem: and Jeremiah the prophet was shut up in the court of the prison, which was in the king of Judah’s house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ba60a60-c3ac-49aa-a6da-5aa9959972f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: JER 32:3
Text: For Zedekiah king of Judah had shut him up, saying, Wherefore dost thou prophesy, and say, Thus saith the LORD, Behold, I will give this city into the hand of the king of Babylon, and he shall take it;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bb02405-cedf-4d07-93be-bd8d8c4c32f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: JER 32:4
Text: And Zedekiah king of Judah shall not escape out of the hand of the Chaldeans, but shall surely be delivered into the hand of the king of Babylon, and shall speak with him mouth to mouth, and his eyes shall behold his eyes;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b146ad8-96f4-405b-9e46-303d4a9d292d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: JER 32:5
Text: And he shall lead Zedekiah to Babylon, and there shall he be until I visit him, saith the LORD: though ye fight with the Chaldeans, ye shall not prosper.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14ce4323-d38a-4209-99b0-2368ccb2313b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: JER 32:6
Text: And Jeremiah said, The word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59737317-6e20-4da6-bbd2-1ed749a74c86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: JER 32:7
Text: Behold, Hanameel the son of Shallum thine uncle shall come unto thee saying, Buy thee my field that is in Anathoth: for the right of redemption is thine to buy it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b881946c-5baa-4a1e-b403-c0e7ec70a485>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 369

Reference: JER 32:8
Text: So Hanameel mine uncle’s son came to me in the court of the prison according to the word of the LORD, and said unto me, Buy my field, I pray thee, that is in Anathoth, which is in the country of Benjamin: for the right of inheritance is thine, and the redemption is thine; buy it for thyself. Then I knew that this was the word of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41b6d558-3da5-4099-bc9e-a4f2239d2ccd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: JER 32:9
Text: And I bought the field of Hanameel my uncle’s son, that was in Anathoth, and weighed him the money, even seventeen shekels of silver.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e4adcfe-c486-47da-a781-5530f905763a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: JER 32:10
Text: And I subscribed the evidence, and sealed it, and took witnesses, and weighed him the money in the balances.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d857b007-02ed-4c3a-bd66-0c268235ca79>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: JER 32:11
Text: So I took the evidence of the purchase, both that which was sealed according to the law and custom, and that which was open:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86a2c82d-e9a3-40f5-84cd-281e05ed1b2d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 300

Reference: JER 32:12
Text: And I gave the evidence of the purchase unto Baruch the son of Neriah, the son of Maaseiah, in the sight of Hanameel mine uncle’s son, and in the presence of the witnesses that subscribed the book of the purchase, before all the Jews that sat in the court of the prison.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa2f8e78-0188-46b6-a0fa-ff342005a023>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 69

Reference: JER 32:13
Text: And I charged Baruch before them, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb2d6b73-d455-4fc6-bb0d-343cf50cba37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: JER 32:14
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Take these evidences, this evidence of the purchase, both which is sealed, and this evidence which is open; and put them in an earthen vessel, that they may continue many days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1ef788a-a8ff-4832-8be6-eaf1627b3989>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: JER 32:15
Text: For thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Houses and fields and vineyards shall be possessed again in this land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d991664e-65e9-4545-8f96-e0e7c6d35bb7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: JER 32:16
Text: Now when I had delivered the evidence of the purchase unto Baruch the son of Neriah, I prayed unto the LORD, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d39fa511-e181-48d6-ad15-13a0cf9c4992>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: JER 32:17
Text: Ah Lord GOD! behold, thou hast made the heaven and the earth by thy great power and stretched out arm, and there is nothing too hard for thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1e4f205-6dc1-4777-84b1-f2218b4d9973>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: JER 32:18
Text: Thou shewest lovingkindness unto thousands, and recompensest the iniquity of the fathers into the bosom of their children after them: the Great, the Mighty God, the LORD of hosts, is his name,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b665af4-1d63-4421-beb8-ba44b2c10889>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: JER 32:19
Text: Great in counsel, and mighty in work: for thine eyes are open upon all the ways of the sons of men: to give every one according to his ways, and according to the fruit of his doings:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e65e0b02-e83e-491d-a8cf-93c535f52623>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: JER 32:20
Text: Which hast set signs and wonders in the land of Egypt, even unto this day, and in Israel, and among other men; and hast made thee a name, as at this day;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fcae6b2-b62a-44ee-8e76-15bbc4563453>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: JER 32:21
Text: And hast brought forth thy people Israel out of the land of Egypt with signs, and with wonders, and with a strong hand, and with a stretched out arm, and with great terror;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a818f646-097a-4030-a5d8-7cb63d744766>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: JER 32:22
Text: And hast given them this land, which thou didst swear to their fathers to give them, a land flowing with milk and honey;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b49d89e5-94c2-42d1-b66f-1432632c6b56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: JER 32:23
Text: And they came in, and possessed it; but they obeyed not thy voice, neither walked in thy law; they have done nothing of all that thou commandedst them to do: therefore thou hast caused all this evil to come upon them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:990eeebf-c1c0-44de-abc9-7cb4fe40e4dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 298

Reference: JER 32:24
Text: Behold the mounts, they are come unto the city to take it; and the city is given into the hand of the Chaldeans, that fight against it, because of the sword, and of the famine, and of the pestilence: and what thou hast spoken is come to pass; and, behold, thou seest it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6402b98-7407-4c69-8672-69c031b1dc69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: JER 32:25
Text: And thou hast said unto me, O Lord GOD, Buy thee the field for money, and take witnesses; for the city is given into the hand of the Chaldeans.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6859da54-502a-465e-82c3-9b4be0507d69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: JER 32:26
Text: Then came the word of the LORD unto Jeremiah, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f7347d9-5bd6-4b52-a023-cb9bae59111b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: JER 32:27
Text: Behold, I am the LORD, the God of all flesh: is there any thing too hard for me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9caa8b85-3f8d-4897-accb-859221774d7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: JER 32:28
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD; Behold, I will give this city into the hand of the Chaldeans, and into the hand of Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon, and he shall take it:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b0a5700-1ac1-4add-8557-54a725d6c158>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: JER 32:29
Text: And the Chaldeans, that fight against this city, shall come and set fire on this city, and burn it with the houses, upon whose roofs they have offered incense unto Baal, and poured out drink offerings unto other gods, to provoke me to anger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc3837f1-7cd1-46c8-8ddb-fdc3426181a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: JER 32:30
Text: For the children of Israel and the children of Judah have only done evil before me from their youth: for the children of Israel have only provoked me to anger with the work of their hands, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f4d3a29-dd2f-4566-a268-e5c3f50bc674>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: JER 32:31
Text: For this city hath been to me as a provocation of mine anger and of my fury from the day that they built it even unto this day; that I should remove it from before my face,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:023b2da1-dd33-4b74-b0f2-5b2f85ea4361>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 277

Reference: JER 32:32
Text: Because of all the evil of the children of Israel and of the children of Judah, which they have done to provoke me to anger, they, their kings, their princes, their priests, and their prophets, and the men of Judah, and the inhabitants of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35f63c27-e66a-4887-9a18-0deab64c2157>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: JER 32:33
Text: And they have turned unto me the back, and not the face: though I taught them, rising up early and teaching them, yet they have not hearkened to receive instruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4445ab1-9df9-453a-a961-083166c13ebc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: JER 32:34
Text: But they set their abominations in the house, which is called by my name, to defile it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6fb42be5-7100-48c6-9115-21f4d69b1ddc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 310

Reference: JER 32:35
Text: And they built the high places of Baal, which are in the valley of the son of Hinnom, to cause their sons and their daughters to pass through the fire unto Molech; which I commanded them not, neither came it into my mind, that they should do this abomination, to cause Judah to sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0c5ae4b-804c-41cf-a156-df506d63cbc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: JER 32:36
Text: And now therefore thus saith the LORD, the God of Israel, concerning this city, whereof ye say, It shall be delivered into the hand of the king of Babylon by the sword, and by the famine, and by the pestilence;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cad19dd-0971-4185-8e6b-a14af5535749>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: JER 32:37
Text: Behold, I will gather them out of all countries, whither I have driven them in mine anger, and in my fury, and in great wrath; and I will bring them again unto this place, and I will cause them to dwell safely:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3dd49ec8-e093-4104-9551-684b12fdd377>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: JER 32:38
Text: And they shall be my people, and I will be their God:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a5c6067-927e-4ddd-af07-90951662917d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: JER 32:39
Text: And I will give them one heart, and one way, that they may fear me for ever, for the good of them, and of their children after them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:170150b8-5b58-4c7e-8c49-b84a50b9b666>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: JER 32:40
Text: And I will make an everlasting covenant with them, that I will not turn away from them, to do them good; but I will put my fear in their hearts, that they shall not depart from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32285af8-7863-4972-88ae-92d38e19ad35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: JER 32:41
Text: Yea, I will rejoice over them to do them good, and I will plant them in this land assuredly with my whole heart and with my whole soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:858d59e0-9140-41cf-b52a-1e34287d69d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: JER 32:42
Text: For thus saith the LORD; Like as I have brought all this great evil upon this people, so will I bring upon them all the good that I have promised them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75ca4e56-3eab-42eb-a5d0-367b57c00e6d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: JER 32:43
Text: And fields shall be bought in this land, whereof ye say, It is desolate without man or beast; it is given into the hand of the Chaldeans.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/32/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5571114c-58ff-4488-96c3-ff809d7e14ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 367

Reference: JER 32:44
Text: Men shall buy fields for money, and subscribe evidences, and seal them, and take witnesses in the land of Benjamin, and in the places about Jerusalem, and in the cities of Judah, and in the cities of the mountains, and in the cities of the valley, and in the cities of the south: for I will cause their captivity to return, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ccfbbcc6-3f61-4fe9-ba97-25cdf3345737>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: JER 33:1
Text: Moreover the word of the LORD came unto Jeremiah the second time, while he was yet shut up in the court of the prison, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:154a670e-de7b-4fea-bd22-647baf02b2d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: JER 33:2
Text: Thus saith the LORD the maker thereof, the LORD that formed it, to establish it; the LORD is his name;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:834a1ea9-2a99-4d56-9552-f3cb156b689b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: JER 33:3
Text: Call unto me, and I will answer thee, and shew thee great and mighty things, which thou knowest not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c9264cd-431c-40a5-999d-2a2210d2d788>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: JER 33:4
Text: For thus saith the LORD, the God of Israel, concerning the houses of this city, and concerning the houses of the kings of Judah, which are thrown down by the mounts, and by the sword;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9768a363-a392-45ff-80c6-38dceda68e79>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: JER 33:5
Text: They come to fight with the Chaldeans, but it is to fill them with the dead bodies of men, whom I have slain in mine anger and in my fury, and for all whose wickedness I have hid my face from this city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9173e396-169d-4bcb-b364-dcf33d07e3fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: JER 33:6
Text: Behold, I will bring it health and cure, and I will cure them, and will reveal unto them the abundance of peace and truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1169d715-dc94-450a-a266-291ef3aa65f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: JER 33:7
Text: And I will cause the captivity of Judah and the captivity of Israel to return, and will build them, as at the first.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b3106ed-276f-4787-95eb-18b6b25500e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: JER 33:8
Text: And I will cleanse them from all their iniquity, whereby they have sinned against me; and I will pardon all their iniquities, whereby they have sinned, and whereby they have transgressed against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2e039dd-0b23-43b1-8d5d-361e43758be4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 278

Reference: JER 33:9
Text: And it shall be to me a name of joy, a praise and an honour before all the nations of the earth, which shall hear all the good that I do unto them: and they shall fear and tremble for all the goodness and for all the prosperity that I procure unto it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21992d0f-a618-4a57-a56d-8673526258e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 289

Reference: JER 33:10
Text: Thus saith the LORD; Again there shall be heard in this place, which ye say shall be desolate without man and without beast, even in the cities of Judah, and in the streets of Jerusalem, that are desolate, without man, and without inhabitant, and without beast,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:569683c4-ae4c-4505-a935-50e5146937be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 412

Reference: JER 33:11
Text: The voice of joy, and the voice of gladness, the voice of the bridegroom, and the voice of the bride, the voice of them that shall say, Praise the LORD of hosts: for the LORD is good; for his mercy endureth for ever: and of them that shall bring the sacrifice of praise into the house of the LORD. For I will cause to return the captivity of the land, as at the first, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:196b0672-5589-471a-a58a-633be35fbbda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: JER 33:12
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Again in this place, which is desolate without man and without beast, and in all the cities thereof, shall be an habitation of shepherds causing their flocks to lie down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66212153-83dd-4ef5-82ab-2de4e59b2994>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 296

Reference: JER 33:13
Text: In the cities of the mountains, in the cities of the vale, and in the cities of the south, and in the land of Benjamin, and in the places about Jerusalem, and in the cities of Judah, shall the flocks pass again under the hands of him that telleth them, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86eda043-62f3-44d6-a697-132c4405b8b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: JER 33:14
Text: Behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that I will perform that good thing which I have promised unto the house of Israel and to the house of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b685013a-3915-4ec8-bf13-c27cac61c659>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JER 33:15
Text: In those days, and at that time, will I cause the Branch of righteousness to grow up unto David; and he shall execute judgment and righteousness in the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf5ed3c0-4895-4f78-a727-4ade4b4f2077>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: JER 33:16
Text: In those days shall Judah be saved, and Jerusalem shall dwell safely: and this is the name wherewith she shall be called, The LORD our righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d767edff-6784-4f1e-970d-3dd356ae8bfa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: JER 33:17
Text: For thus saith the LORD; David shall never want a man to sit upon the throne of the house of Israel;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:466080c2-f0d6-4c27-bf9b-5bd8d9952ec2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: JER 33:18
Text: Neither shall the priests the Levites want a man before me to offer burnt offerings, and to kindle meat offerings, and to do sacrifice continually.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b15a43e-2262-47aa-b67f-6d8f4a57d632>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: JER 33:19
Text: And the word of the LORD came unto Jeremiah, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b855971f-8e27-4772-bec8-ea1dd6152429>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: JER 33:20
Text: Thus saith the LORD; If ye can break my covenant of the day, and my covenant of the night, and that there should not be day and night in their season;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0bfeb46-5735-4461-befa-08b1ba8300af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: JER 33:21
Text: Then may also my covenant be broken with David my servant, that he should not have a son to reign upon his throne; and with the Levites the priests, my ministers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7291d91-126e-4bb4-87a2-4fd30bcbfb53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: JER 33:22
Text: As the host of heaven cannot be numbered, neither the sand of the sea measured: so will I multiply the seed of David my servant, and the Levites that minister unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbe4ed28-3ce0-4537-95a2-bddc468d65d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: JER 33:23
Text: Moreover the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9242df0b-341d-4273-9f10-f5698977bb44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: JER 33:24
Text: Considerest thou not what this people have spoken, saying, The two families which the LORD hath chosen, he hath even cast them off? thus they have despised my people, that they should be no more a nation before them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:261604bd-c2e7-4f20-9549-1007e11ce568>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: JER 33:25
Text: Thus saith the LORD; If my covenant be not with day and night, and if I have not appointed the ordinances of heaven and earth;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/33/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fad1f64-4cb7-4216-aae1-20d77c3044d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: JER 33:26
Text: Then will I cast away the seed of Jacob and David my servant, so that I will not take any of his seed to be rulers over the seed of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob: for I will cause their captivity to return, and have mercy on them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/34/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70395fc2-3876-4957-902b-e7f50bfe82f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: JER 34:1
Text: The word which came unto Jeremiah from the LORD, when Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, and all his army, and all the kingdoms of the earth of his dominion, and all the people, fought against Jerusalem, and against all the cities thereof, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/34/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:932a8704-613a-4bee-8a53-72ce010197cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: JER 34:2
Text: Thus saith the LORD, the God of Israel; Go and speak to Zedekiah king of Judah, and tell him, Thus saith the LORD; Behold, I will give this city into the hand of the king of Babylon, and he shall burn it with fire:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/34/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:067becaa-a8f7-4ff6-b5a7-b625d7eb6f13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: JER 34:3
Text: And thou shalt not escape out of his hand, but shalt surely be taken, and delivered into his hand; and thine eyes shall behold the eyes of the king of Babylon, and he shall speak with thee mouth to mouth, and thou shalt go to Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/34/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb0a44d4-613f-402b-8ebd-d00b2ccd1aa1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: JER 34:4
Text: Yet hear the word of the LORD, O Zedekiah king of Judah; Thus saith the LORD of thee, Thou shalt not die by the sword:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/34/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9df3bb99-7e6d-4d3f-8c25-16201f5ff7d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 262

Reference: JER 34:5
Text: But thou shalt die in peace: and with the burnings of thy fathers, the former kings which were before thee, so shall they burn odours for thee; and they will lament thee, saying, Ah lord! for I have pronounced the word, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/34/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a5aed32-6e86-49ef-bb30-7cf4f36c24fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: JER 34:6
Text: Then Jeremiah the prophet spake all these words unto Zedekiah king of Judah in Jerusalem,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/34/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbc22ba0-67d5-437c-ac9e-f0cc8a99d503>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: JER 34:7
Text: When the king of Babylon’s army fought against Jerusalem, and against all the cities of Judah that were left, against Lachish, and against Azekah: for these defenced cities remained of the cities of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/34/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f67555ef-585a-423e-9431-3a44e231d9a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: JER 34:8
Text: This is the word that came unto Jeremiah from the LORD, after that the king Zedekiah had made a covenant with all the people which were at Jerusalem, to proclaim liberty unto them;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/34/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e971f81f-3650-4d75-b4ec-64d9c3fe20c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: JER 34:9
Text: That every man should let his manservant, and every man his maidservant, being an Hebrew or an Hebrewess, go free; that none should serve himself of them, to wit, of a Jew his brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/34/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:988e8144-7564-45e2-a6c7-33bd010048f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 285

Reference: JER 34:10
Text: Now when all the princes, and all the people, which had entered into the covenant, heard that every one should let his manservant, and every one his maidservant, go free, that none should serve themselves of them any more, then they obeyed, and let them go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/34/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71f422c9-7d35-438a-93c0-5f9c2d2b31d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: JER 34:11
Text: But afterward they turned, and caused the servants and the handmaids, whom they had let go free, to return, and brought them into subjection for servants and for handmaids.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/34/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbd0d204-7497-4154-8bdc-5a5f37c20ff4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: JER 34:12
Text: Therefore the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/34/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e3e273d-2def-4ef5-88d2-5eb3c05ad17b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: JER 34:13
Text: Thus saith the LORD, the God of Israel; I made a covenant with your fathers in the day that I brought them forth out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of bondmen, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/34/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e485b990-bd25-419b-a112-ba5ff779d3ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 274

Reference: JER 34:14
Text: At the end of seven years let ye go every man his brother an Hebrew, which hath been sold unto thee; and when he hath served thee six years, thou shalt let him go free from thee: but your fathers hearkened not unto me, neither inclined their ear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/34/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e910072-4c37-4cfe-a57f-e1af74ad26a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: JER 34:15
Text: And ye were now turned, and had done right in my sight, in proclaiming liberty every man to his neighbour; and ye had made a covenant before me in the house which is called by my name:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/34/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55f4ffbe-2fcb-4d38-89b8-2451b9a707f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: JER 34:16
Text: But ye turned and polluted my name, and caused every man his servant, and every man his handmaid, whom ye had set at liberty at their pleasure, to return, and brought them into subjection, to be unto you for servants and for handmaids.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/34/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e260619-ce09-4358-9aad-80d9946c5a70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 347

Reference: JER 34:17
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD; Ye have not hearkened unto me, in proclaiming liberty, every one to his brother, and every man to his neighbour: behold, I proclaim a liberty for you, saith the LORD, to the sword, to the pestilence, and to the famine; and I will make you to be removed into all the kingdoms of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/34/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b169f0df-f224-4f7a-a5d1-51f571bec44e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: JER 34:18
Text: And I will give the men that have transgressed my covenant, which have not performed the words of the covenant which they had made before me, when they cut the calf in twain, and passed between the parts thereof,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/34/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2690b145-7ab3-4c8d-ac02-705cc22a830f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JER 34:19
Text: The princes of Judah, and the princes of Jerusalem, the eunuchs, and the priests, and all the people of the land, which passed between the parts of the calf;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/34/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f1b7dcd-4c8d-4751-bbeb-db5c2a9c7f3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: JER 34:20
Text: I will even give them into the hand of their enemies, and into the hand of them that seek their life: and their dead bodies shall be for meat unto the fowls of the heaven, and to the beasts of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/34/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db15dd03-f01e-4dc7-9cac-306c97956c12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: JER 34:21
Text: And Zedekiah king of Judah and his princes will I give into the hand of their enemies, and into the hand of them that seek their life, and into the hand of the king of Babylon’s army, which are gone up from you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/34/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e123baaa-cb29-43c5-835e-f19dab3c96ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: JER 34:22
Text: Behold, I will command, saith the LORD, and cause them to return to this city; and they shall fight against it, and take it, and burn it with fire: and I will make the cities of Judah a desolation without an inhabitant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/35/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59d97866-ecd7-44f1-b5e1-fcd722d6cbb0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: JER 35:1
Text: The word which came unto Jeremiah from the LORD in the days of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/35/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ebfeb50-5e8e-4d46-9b4f-3d284fe7e3c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JER 35:2
Text: Go unto the house of the Rechabites, and speak unto them, and bring them into the house of the LORD, into one of the chambers, and give them wine to drink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/35/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:add30bd4-6ea6-442c-8efe-3ca3f98fc0b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: JER 35:3
Text: Then I took Jaazaniah the son of Jeremiah, the son of Habaziniah, and his brethren, and all his sons, and the whole house of the Rechabites;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/35/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e68500d-ddc7-446f-aa16-b5e1a05eed67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: JER 35:4
Text: And I brought them into the house of the LORD, into the chamber of the sons of Hanan, the son of Igdaliah, a man of God, which was by the chamber of the princes, which was above the chamber of Maaseiah the son of Shallum, the keeper of the door:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/35/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a76d6c7b-d5ee-4d08-a4aa-bfd395cbe5b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: JER 35:5
Text: And I set before the sons of the house of the Rechabites pots full of wine, and cups, and I said unto them, Drink ye wine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/35/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6082c77-8b4f-41f4-b41b-8e9763ca8904>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: JER 35:6
Text: But they said, We will drink no wine: for Jonadab the son of Rechab our father commanded us, saying, Ye shall drink no wine, neither ye, nor your sons for ever:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/35/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed75c0bb-7da6-457e-9c5c-07be9868ba99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: JER 35:7
Text: Neither shall ye build house, nor sow seed, nor plant vineyard, nor have any: but all your days ye shall dwell in tents; that ye may live many days in the land where ye be strangers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/35/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c21e6836-b9c3-447f-8074-812f055012d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: JER 35:8
Text: Thus have we obeyed the voice of Jonadab the son of Rechab our father in all that he hath charged us, to drink no wine all our days, we, our wives, our sons, nor our daughters;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/35/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e92be5c-06aa-46cc-bb74-20e92a1afa37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: JER 35:9
Text: Nor to build houses for us to dwell in: neither have we vineyard, nor field, nor seed:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/35/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:844b1ae8-b842-41fe-bbc1-91c4994fff91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: JER 35:10
Text: But we have dwelt in tents, and have obeyed, and done according to all that Jonadab our father commanded us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/35/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfbb7e85-25cd-46a0-bc0a-d5f8fbc406c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: JER 35:11
Text: But it came to pass, when Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon came up into the land, that we said, Come, and let us go to Jerusalem for fear of the army of the Chaldeans, and for fear of the army of the Syrians: so we dwell at Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/35/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7174673-d8d9-4cb6-bca7-08a82e7f1ae9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: JER 35:12
Text: Then came the word of the LORD unto Jeremiah, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/35/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f69ac923-3dd0-4833-b7ce-8b271454052c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: JER 35:13
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Go and tell the men of Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem, Will ye not receive instruction to hearken to my words? saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/35/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:596122d4-09ca-4a19-951f-b878a15184f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 299

Reference: JER 35:14
Text: The words of Jonadab the son of Rechab, that he commanded his sons not to drink wine, are performed; for unto this day they drink none, but obey their father’s commandment: notwithstanding I have spoken unto you, rising early and speaking; but ye hearkened not unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/35/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01edce18-2fcd-462a-8b1d-0ecd52ad2446>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 370

Reference: JER 35:15
Text: I have sent also unto you all my servants the prophets, rising up early and sending them, saying, Return ye now every man from his evil way, and amend your doings, and go not after other gods to serve them, and ye shall dwell in the land which I have given to you and to your fathers: but ye have not inclined your ear, nor hearkened unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/35/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afe66e77-4332-4de6-84b3-0db0ad10b0ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: JER 35:16
Text: Because the sons of Jonadab the son of Rechab have performed the commandment of their father, which he commanded them; but this people hath not hearkened unto me:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/35/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d081156e-9c41-453c-85fe-6d92125c2fa3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 329

Reference: JER 35:17
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD God of hosts, the God of Israel; Behold, I will bring upon Judah and upon all the inhabitants of Jerusalem all the evil that I have pronounced against them: because I have spoken unto them, but they have not heard; and I have called unto them, but they have not answered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/35/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4f68b87-ae34-4ad9-a4b3-84b65b115cae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 274

Reference: JER 35:18
Text: And Jeremiah said unto the house of the Rechabites, Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Because ye have obeyed the commandment of Jonadab your father, and kept all his precepts, and done according unto all that he hath commanded you:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/35/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21b8819e-78a9-4063-922d-871228e8539e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: JER 35:19
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Jonadab the son of Rechab shall not want a man to stand before me for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80d71b38-2cde-4696-ae62-046902e34f50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: JER 36:1
Text: And it came to pass in the fourth year of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah, that this word came unto Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec1df35d-123f-4188-81c6-4d1ec67bfb77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: JER 36:2
Text: Take thee a roll of a book, and write therein all the words that I have spoken unto thee against Israel, and against Judah, and against all the nations, from the day I spake unto thee, from the days of Josiah, even unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f135aa41-13f1-4937-a7b2-392ebf87d8c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: JER 36:3
Text: It may be that the house of Judah will hear all the evil which I purpose to do unto them; that they may return every man from his evil way; that I may forgive their iniquity and their sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:492c18f0-944b-4706-9f7c-15db50216e57>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: JER 36:4
Text: Then Jeremiah called Baruch the son of Neriah: and Baruch wrote from the mouth of Jeremiah all the words of the LORD, which he had spoken unto him, upon a roll of a book.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:597fd0a5-d425-40aa-8a12-feaff49eadd4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: JER 36:5
Text: And Jeremiah commanded Baruch, saying, I am shut up; I cannot go into the house of the LORD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc9b5c1e-8b3a-494b-8156-c988d9ae1303>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: JER 36:6
Text: Therefore go thou, and read in the roll, which thou hast written from my mouth, the words of the LORD in the ears of the people in the LORD’s house upon the fasting day: and also thou shalt read them in the ears of all Judah that come out of their cities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:821216df-80f2-4029-95ca-2287dc197748>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: JER 36:7
Text: It may be they will present their supplication before the LORD, and will return every one from his evil way: for great is the anger and the fury that the LORD hath pronounced against this people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ee33a14-681c-44fe-aef4-71781de31e57>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JER 36:8
Text: And Baruch the son of Neriah did according to all that Jeremiah the prophet commanded him, reading in the book the words of the LORD in the LORD’s house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce88ff9c-fd00-44cb-a14c-987322eea79d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 279

Reference: JER 36:9
Text: And it came to pass in the fifth year of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah, in the ninth month, that they proclaimed a fast before the LORD to all the people in Jerusalem, and to all the people that came from the cities of Judah unto Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14516e1f-74a4-4d61-9397-25d1b53bbd91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 266

Reference: JER 36:10
Text: Then read Baruch in the book the words of Jeremiah in the house of the LORD, in the chamber of Gemariah the son of Shaphan the scribe, in the higher court, at the entry of the new gate of the LORD’s house, in the ears of all the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:534a6a88-7de1-4adf-82a8-65e2361d5f0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: JER 36:11
Text: When Michaiah the son of Gemariah, the son of Shaphan, had heard out of the book all the words of the LORD,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d113a36-bb7b-46f3-90f4-350e0ae8c951>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 314

Reference: JER 36:12
Text: Then he went down into the king’s house, into the scribe’s chamber: and, lo, all the princes sat there, even Elishama the scribe, and Delaiah the son of Shemaiah, and Elnathan the son of Achbor, and Gemariah the son of Shaphan, and Zedekiah the son of Hananiah, and all the princes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a85fe8a-d19e-4339-ab2f-15fb81f614b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: JER 36:13
Text: Then Michaiah declared unto them all the words that he had heard, when Baruch read the book in the ears of the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb95164a-58e4-4700-be2d-656bd53027d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 311

Reference: JER 36:14
Text: Therefore all the princes sent Jehudi the son of Nethaniah, the son of Shelemiah, the son of Cushi, unto Baruch, saying, Take in thine hand the roll wherein thou hast read in the ears of the people, and come. So Baruch the son of Neriah took the roll in his hand, and came unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:503b8371-b7c2-4791-8e1d-dbe285b30197>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: JER 36:15
Text: And they said unto him, Sit down now, and read it in our ears. So Baruch read it in their ears.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7d66a0b-01aa-4833-bd6d-38a2473fbf5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: JER 36:16
Text: Now it came to pass, when they had heard all the words, they were afraid both one and other, and said unto Baruch, We will surely tell the king of all these words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82b529b5-201e-4837-b565-1e5e6c82aaa5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: JER 36:17
Text: And they asked Baruch, saying, Tell us now, How didst thou write all these words at his mouth?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de78031e-9e16-4f6c-ab34-3d7d30a4adf7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: JER 36:18
Text: Then Baruch answered them, He pronounced all these words unto me with his mouth, and I wrote them with ink in the book.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39e983b5-62cf-4e29-abaa-e4c05b3731d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: JER 36:19
Text: Then said the princes unto Baruch, Go, hide thee, thou and Jeremiah; and let no man know where ye be.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5665990e-cb1a-46d8-b3f9-9f0ca22c06ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JER 36:20
Text: And they went in to the king into the court, but they laid up the roll in the chamber of Elishama the scribe, and told all the words in the ears of the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22f489a6-a4e5-4276-a690-d7f92c8d714f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: JER 36:21
Text: So the king sent Jehudi to fetch the roll: and he took it out of Elishama the scribe’s chamber. And Jehudi read it in the ears of the king, and in the ears of all the princes which stood beside the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e84dc6d-4db2-4d77-8468-01c920bfec84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: JER 36:22
Text: Now the king sat in the winterhouse in the ninth month: and there was a fire on the hearth burning before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5347b3f-74be-4058-9c22-59b16ca80451>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: JER 36:23
Text: And it came to pass, that when Jehudi had read three or four leaves, he cut it with the penknife, and cast it into the fire that was on the hearth, until all the roll was consumed in the fire that was on the hearth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f1834b1-ade5-40e7-b377-854404b9b197>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: JER 36:24
Text: Yet they were not afraid, nor rent their garments, neither the king, nor any of his servants that heard all these words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ca9e8ea-dbda-459f-984f-271481b30baa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: JER 36:25
Text: Nevertheless Elnathan and Delaiah and Gemariah had made intercession to the king that he would not burn the roll: but he would not hear them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c281d40-3568-41ce-ac88-c2fd69bcde14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: JER 36:26
Text: But the king commanded Jerahmeel the son of Hammelech, and Seraiah the son of Azriel, and Shelemiah the son of Abdeel, to take Baruch the scribe and Jeremiah the prophet: but the LORD hid them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d7237eb-6f84-420f-a3f8-0f5ec786a70a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: JER 36:27
Text: Then the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah, after that the king had burned the roll, and the words which Baruch wrote at the mouth of Jeremiah, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4400bd6f-12e1-479e-9d88-a4fa163016b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: JER 36:28
Text: Take thee again another roll, and write in it all the former words that were in the first roll, which Jehoiakim the king of Judah hath burned.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2083b168-3bdb-4894-82d9-d4e33b611cd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 286

Reference: JER 36:29
Text: And thou shalt say to Jehoiakim king of Judah, Thus saith the LORD; Thou hast burned this roll, saying, Why hast thou written therein, saying, The king of Babylon shall certainly come and destroy this land, and shall cause to cease from thence man and beast?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a6f7936-1e48-4266-9f32-8f7e1bd6299a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: JER 36:30
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD of Jehoiakim king of Judah; He shall have none to sit upon the throne of David: and his dead body shall be cast out in the day to the heat, and in the night to the frost.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acccf055-2178-4e4e-b206-9860fcf767a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: JER 36:31
Text: And I will punish him and his seed and his servants for their iniquity; and I will bring upon them, and upon the inhabitants of Jerusalem, and upon the men of Judah, all the evil that I have pronounced against them; but they hearkened not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/36/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f0b06ea-0774-4f06-809e-958077699a2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 294

Reference: JER 36:32
Text: Then took Jeremiah another roll, and gave it to Baruch the scribe, the son of Neriah; who wrote therein from the mouth of Jeremiah all the words of the book which Jehoiakim king of Judah had burned in the fire: and there were added besides unto them many like words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/37/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d9312a0-25ae-4cac-9193-44ff6f02e9db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: JER 37:1
Text: And king Zedekiah the son of Josiah reigned instead of Coniah the son of Jehoiakim, whom Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon made king in the land of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/37/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0219c14a-62f0-49a8-aed6-1e537fc96bd2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: JER 37:2
Text: But neither he, nor his servants, nor the people of the land, did hearken unto the words of the LORD, which he spake by the prophet Jeremiah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/37/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a14c7ee-53a3-4ab3-ac86-860d8f871b61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: JER 37:3
Text: And Zedekiah the king sent Jehucal the son of Shelemiah and Zephaniah the son of Maaseiah the priest to the prophet Jeremiah, saying, Pray now unto the LORD our God for us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/37/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6fdc68c9-29e2-497b-af08-d1c5b713ee93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: JER 37:4
Text: Now Jeremiah came in and went out among the people: for they had not put him into prison.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/37/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:250ef4ea-4839-4d72-84d2-b323a128079e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: JER 37:5
Text: Then Pharaoh’s army was come forth out of Egypt: and when the Chaldeans that besieged Jerusalem heard tidings of them, they departed from Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/37/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae1b51db-9050-42a1-8dd3-971f4d56a494>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: JER 37:6
Text: Then came the word of the LORD unto the prophet Jeremiah saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/37/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16e1fd5e-64b9-4df1-894c-350226500126>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: JER 37:7
Text: Thus saith the LORD, the God of Israel; Thus shall ye say to the king of Judah, that sent you unto me to enquire of me; Behold, Pharaoh’s army, which is come forth to help you, shall return to Egypt into their own land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/37/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ccaa9fa9-f5a7-4dca-85f9-61f06d73f9ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: JER 37:8
Text: And the Chaldeans shall come again, and fight against this city, and take it, and burn it with fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/37/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c8fe4c8-b70b-437c-aca5-927135a7bc7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: JER 37:9
Text: Thus saith the LORD; Deceive not yourselves, saying, The Chaldeans shall surely depart from us: for they shall not depart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/37/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60cca388-8362-465d-809d-1d680187e7d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: JER 37:10
Text: For though ye had smitten the whole army of the Chaldeans that fight against you, and there remained but wounded men among them, yet should they rise up every man in his tent, and burn this city with fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/37/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f6e7306-f1ea-463b-882d-7487982b091b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: JER 37:11
Text: And it came to pass, that when the army of the Chaldeans was broken up from Jerusalem for fear of Pharaoh’s army,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/37/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad6eadb5-34c7-4e7a-bb4e-cc704cacabda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: JER 37:12
Text: Then Jeremiah went forth out of Jerusalem to go into the land of Benjamin, to separate himself thence in the midst of the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/37/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9faa8adf-c403-43de-8af6-90489fba79be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: JER 37:13
Text: And when he was in the gate of Benjamin, a captain of the ward was there, whose name was Irijah, the son of Shelemiah, the son of Hananiah; and he took Jeremiah the prophet, saying, Thou fallest away to the Chaldeans.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/37/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7f6bff2-f0e3-4a1a-b35a-46e1cebbe04e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: JER 37:14
Text: Then said Jeremiah, It is false; I fall not away to the Chaldeans. But he hearkened not to him: so Irijah took Jeremiah, and brought him to the princes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/37/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:092288df-3b42-41f7-9f55-8f45573b6ceb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: JER 37:15
Text: Wherefore the princes were wroth with Jeremiah, and smote him, and put him in prison in the house of Jonathan the scribe: for they had made that the prison.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/37/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a632ca0b-d299-4e80-9021-2ee10db659d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: JER 37:16
Text: When Jeremiah was entered into the dungeon, and into the cabins, and Jeremiah had remained there many days;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/37/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f32ea10f-4706-4ea6-9611-47cab90a1023>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: JER 37:17
Text: Then Zedekiah the king sent, and took him out: and the king asked him secretly in his house, and said, Is there any word from the LORD? And Jeremiah said, There is: for, said he, thou shalt be delivered into the hand of the king of Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/37/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:030a9ede-8dc4-4b30-b9e1-a3580e83f660>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JER 37:18
Text: Moreover Jeremiah said unto king Zedekiah, What have I offended against thee, or against thy servants, or against this people, that ye have put me in prison?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/37/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c26bfa0c-a581-40da-a706-4aec02d37431>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: JER 37:19
Text: Where are now your prophets which prophesied unto you, saying, The king of Babylon shall not come against you, nor against this land?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/37/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16b77813-5312-42ef-a5ff-5a606a891a20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: JER 37:20
Text: Therefore hear now, I pray thee, O my lord the king: let my supplication, I pray thee, be accepted before thee; that thou cause me not to return to the house of Jonathan the scribe, lest I die there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/37/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abedc18e-f509-42a6-981e-2de2ca3ef2a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 300

Reference: JER 37:21
Text: Then Zedekiah the king commanded that they should commit Jeremiah into the court of the prison, and that they should give him daily a piece of bread out of the bakers’ street, until all the bread in the city were spent. Thus Jeremiah remained in the court of the prison.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a57a8605-431f-4400-971c-011a369e3eb5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: JER 38:1
Text: Then Shephatiah the son of Mattan, and Gedaliah the son of Pashur, and Jucal the son of Shelemiah, and Pashur the son of Malchiah, heard the words that Jeremiah had spoken unto all the people, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abe170e1-dc7e-4758-bbd3-7def7c554d3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: JER 38:2
Text: Thus saith the LORD, He that remaineth in this city shall die by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence: but he that goeth forth to the Chaldeans shall live; for he shall have his life for a prey, and shall live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc3a747e-cf85-4af8-9409-25fbc9512dd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: JER 38:3
Text: Thus saith the LORD, This city shall surely be given into the hand of the king of Babylon’s army, which shall take it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43a5e56b-5bdc-4ef0-93d6-432d546a489e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 325

Reference: JER 38:4
Text: Therefore the princes said unto the king, We beseech thee, let this man be put to death: for thus he weakeneth the hands of the men of war that remain in this city, and the hands of all the people, in speaking such words unto them: for this man seeketh not the welfare of this people, but the hurt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:872c028d-7f13-4ae2-8a03-7407c94275c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: JER 38:5
Text: Then Zedekiah the king said, Behold, he is in your hand: for the king is not he that can do any thing against you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd5949f7-c17e-404d-8bd6-062cffab29d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: JER 38:6
Text: Then took they Jeremiah, and cast him into the dungeon of Malchiah the son of Hammelech, that was in the court of the prison: and they let down Jeremiah with cords. And in the dungeon there was no water, but mire: so Jeremiah sunk in the mire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:558f4ea8-eb07-4d68-bcf8-313f54b45440>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: JER 38:7
Text: Now when Ebedmelech the Ethiopian, one of the eunuchs which was in the king’s house, heard that they had put Jeremiah in the dungeon; the king then sitting in the gate of Benjamin;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a973aeb0-391b-4c55-b452-9bc5242176aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: JER 38:8
Text: Ebedmelech went forth out of the king’s house, and spake to the king saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90562315-f8ec-4234-9d7d-01d73a1335de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: JER 38:9
Text: My lord the king, these men have done evil in all that they have done to Jeremiah the prophet, whom they have cast into the dungeon; and he is like to die for hunger in the place where he is: for there is no more bread in the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bac2e2e4-1e58-452f-a98b-c4b56a1c53a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: JER 38:10
Text: Then the king commanded Ebedmelech the Ethiopian, saying, Take from hence thirty men with thee, and take up Jeremiah the prophet out of the dungeon, before he die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6a56679-5302-4b90-aacf-dbaa0fe5c841>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: JER 38:11
Text: So Ebedmelech took the men with him, and went into the house of the king under the treasury, and took thence old cast clouts and old rotten rags, and let them down by cords into the dungeon to Jeremiah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8f7fc19-3866-4ecb-a718-03918bbecfff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: JER 38:12
Text: And Ebedmelech the Ethiopian said unto Jeremiah, Put now these old cast clouts and rotten rags under thine armholes under the cords. And Jeremiah did so.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b5dd7c5-a834-46f3-96dd-11b311c08f80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: JER 38:13
Text: So they drew up Jeremiah with cords, and took him up out of the dungeon: and Jeremiah remained in the court of the prison.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f36fc290-c85a-4d04-a40a-2b7a2a7cf24a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: JER 38:14
Text: Then Zedekiah the king sent, and took Jeremiah the prophet unto him into the third entry that is in the house of the LORD: and the king said unto Jeremiah, I will ask thee a thing; hide nothing from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06e2d812-db03-4141-9847-a8afbad85100>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JER 38:15
Text: Then Jeremiah said unto Zedekiah, If I declare it unto thee, wilt thou not surely put me to death? and if I give thee counsel, wilt thou not hearken unto me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08623269-8d70-4715-9412-010d94eb266f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: JER 38:16
Text: So Zedekiah the king sware secretly unto Jeremiah, saying, As the LORD liveth, that made us this soul, I will not put thee to death, neither will I give thee into the hand of these men that seek thy life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a21c173a-c021-444e-b54f-9e1e49e94d09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 298

Reference: JER 38:17
Text: Then said Jeremiah unto Zedekiah, Thus saith the LORD, the God of hosts, the God of Israel; If thou wilt assuredly go forth unto the king of Babylon’s princes, then thy soul shall live, and this city shall not be burned with fire; and thou shalt live, and thine house:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17fe8b67-faa9-4ed3-8287-efb50a7c8f41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: JER 38:18
Text: But if thou wilt not go forth to the king of Babylon’s princes, then shall this city be given into the hand of the Chaldeans, and they shall burn it with fire, and thou shalt not escape out of their hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fcb75826-0c22-4c32-8b86-5ecc429235dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: JER 38:19
Text: And Zedekiah the king said unto Jeremiah, I am afraid of the Jews that are fallen to the Chaldeans, lest they deliver me into their hand, and they mock me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abd8eba6-6591-4f8a-93e6-60ec32ba90c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: JER 38:20
Text: But Jeremiah said, They shall not deliver thee. Obey, I beseech thee, the voice of the LORD, which I speak unto thee: so it shall be well unto thee, and thy soul shall live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d99096df-3a70-4a3b-8e27-691bbcf3354e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: JER 38:21
Text: But if thou refuse to go forth, this is the word that the LORD hath shewed me:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85cede53-e1d7-4bbe-8cac-d4352ead7ab8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 310

Reference: JER 38:22
Text: And, behold, all the women that are left in the king of Judah’s house shall be brought forth to the king of Babylon’s princes, and those women shall say, Thy friends have set thee on, and have prevailed against thee: thy feet are sunk in the mire, and they are turned away back.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a35d4e9-c975-49ce-ace0-6e926a1baefd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: JER 38:23
Text: So they shall bring out all thy wives and thy children to the Chaldeans: and thou shalt not escape out of their hand, but shalt be taken by the hand of the king of Babylon: and thou shalt cause this city to be burned with fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b9d9cdf-a45c-4875-81d1-aee7fda129e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: JER 38:24
Text: Then said Zedekiah unto Jeremiah, Let no man know of these words, and thou shalt not die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2366aa54-b65b-4501-8284-07539dfa0a61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: JER 38:25
Text: But if the princes hear that I have talked with thee, and they come unto thee, and say unto thee, Declare unto us now what thou hast said unto the king, hide it not from us, and we will not put thee to death; also what the king said unto thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:963fd72e-ba00-40f5-91b0-fa9d9f6158dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: JER 38:26
Text: Then thou shalt say unto them, I presented my supplication before the king, that he would not cause me to return to Jonathan’s house, to die there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:704ce394-1b85-44b8-b57f-6702dd7a3e3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: JER 38:27
Text: Then came all the princes unto Jeremiah, and asked him: and he told them according to all these words that the king had commanded. So they left off speaking with him; for the matter was not perceived.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/38/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5763f97b-0169-489e-8004-7ddb2334a665>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: JER 38:28
Text: So Jeremiah abode in the court of the prison until the day that Jerusalem was taken: and he was there when Jerusalem was taken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/39/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:335a27ee-d14d-4776-a51c-8d3c40b8603c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JER 39:1
Text: In the ninth year of Zedekiah king of Judah, in the tenth month, came Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon and all his army against Jerusalem, and they besieged it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/39/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e54e4f27-7c51-4c79-9bbf-335cc2a03713>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: JER 39:2
Text: And in the eleventh year of Zedekiah, in the fourth month, the ninth day of the month, the city was broken up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/39/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf7f29a7-e978-459a-8bb1-21e30c4800d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: JER 39:3
Text: And all the princes of the king of Babylon came in, and sat in the middle gate, even Nergalsharezer, Samgarnebo, Sarsechim, Rabsaris, Nergalsharezer, Rabmag, with all the residue of the princes of the king of Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/39/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6851e8a6-f06c-403d-93ac-ff8b086078cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 283

Reference: JER 39:4
Text: And it came to pass, that when Zedekiah the king of Judah saw them, and all the men of war, then they fled, and went forth out of the city by night, by the way of the king’s garden, by the gate betwixt the two walls: and he went out the way of the plain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/39/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9d71d01-c1af-4b3a-975f-91b8ad823434>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: JER 39:5
Text: But the Chaldeans’ army pursued after them, and overtook Zedekiah in the plains of Jericho: and when they had taken him, they brought him up to Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon to Riblah in the land of Hamath, where he gave judgment upon him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/39/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab5ad121-62a0-4eb2-9cb4-7927cd2ac4e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: JER 39:6
Text: Then the king of Babylon slew the sons of Zedekiah in Riblah before his eyes: also the king of Babylon slew all the nobles of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/39/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de093468-829d-4723-b21a-c1191aa51e9f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: JER 39:7
Text: Moreover he put out Zedekiah’s eyes, and bound him with chains, to carry him to Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/39/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1edd8871-0223-4a63-a450-3a58941b59cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: JER 39:8
Text: And the Chaldeans burned the king’s house, and the houses of the people, with fire, and brake down the walls of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/39/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7266d0fb-75fa-4bab-8550-2db457341551>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: JER 39:9
Text: Then Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard carried away captive into Babylon the remnant of the people that remained in the city, and those that fell away, that fell to him, with the rest of the people that remained.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/39/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6f21e19-f9d0-433c-8e29-12113cf16df4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: JER 39:10
Text: But Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard left of the poor of the people, which had nothing, in the land of Judah, and gave them vineyards and fields at the same time.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/39/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15803089-c72f-436c-865d-da3f8e961b49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: JER 39:11
Text: Now Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon gave charge concerning Jeremiah to Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/39/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bdc7e37-c546-445d-8910-3d929c2d26ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: JER 39:12
Text: Take him, and look well to him, and do him no harm; but do unto him even as he shall say unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/39/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51b12480-588b-48fa-870a-c35ca1964ed6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: JER 39:13
Text: So Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard sent, and Nebushasban, Rabsaris, and Nergalsharezer, Rabmag, and all the king of Babylon’s princes;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/39/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86fb56cf-91f9-4c24-9e4e-c575562a14a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: JER 39:14
Text: Even they sent, and took Jeremiah out of the court of the prison, and committed him unto Gedaliah the son of Ahikam the son of Shaphan, that he should carry him home: so he dwelt among the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/39/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb432fc9-9c97-4e4a-9812-9c856a485f07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: JER 39:15
Text: Now the word of the LORD came unto Jeremiah, while he was shut up in the court of the prison, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/39/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c1c1228-90f4-4990-b977-d2ee9eafc8af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: JER 39:16
Text: Go and speak to Ebedmelech the Ethiopian, saying, Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Behold, I will bring my words upon this city for evil, and not for good; and they shall be accomplished in that day before thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/39/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2f9facf-02a4-43be-8c44-7d2267f31e3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: JER 39:17
Text: But I will deliver thee in that day, saith the LORD: and thou shalt not be given into the hand of the men of whom thou art afraid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/39/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58f4c7c7-7075-4880-bab5-1549efc2f181>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: JER 39:18
Text: For I will surely deliver thee, and thou shalt not fall by the sword, but thy life shall be for a prey unto thee: because thou hast put thy trust in me, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/40/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ca3395b-a0d9-4667-bf0c-5f128484d927>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 302

Reference: JER 40:1
Text: The word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD, after that Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard had let him go from Ramah, when he had taken him being bound in chains among all that were carried away captive of Jerusalem and Judah, which were carried away captive unto Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/40/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8eafa03-570d-4106-a85f-698a2177665d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: JER 40:2
Text: And the captain of the guard took Jeremiah, and said unto him, The LORD thy God hath pronounced this evil upon this place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/40/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97ec52cc-725a-4d82-922c-0e81d2944e80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: JER 40:3
Text: Now the LORD hath brought it, and done according as he hath said: because ye have sinned against the LORD, and have not obeyed his voice, therefore this thing is come upon you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/40/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8db5774-9d04-42eb-b486-b8fee7cbe2cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 375

Reference: JER 40:4
Text: And now, behold, I loose thee this day from the chains which were upon thine hand. If it seem good unto thee to come with me into Babylon, come; and I will look well unto thee: but if it seem ill unto thee to come with me into Babylon, forbear: behold, all the land is before thee: whither it seemeth good and convenient for thee to go, thither go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/40/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:977c350e-fd85-4129-82eb-ac9eddbb49c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 374

Reference: JER 40:5
Text: Now while he was not yet gone back, he said, Go back also to Gedaliah the son of Ahikam the son of Shaphan, whom the king of Babylon hath made governor over the cities of Judah, and dwell with him among the people: or go wheresoever it seemeth convenient unto thee to go. So the captain of the guard gave him victuals and a reward, and let him go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/40/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b43c16e-5d31-4952-965b-878c42c11ac0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: JER 40:6
Text: Then went Jeremiah unto Gedaliah the son of Ahikam to Mizpah; and dwelt with him among the people that were left in the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/40/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6061508b-9ea2-4bb2-ae7d-178078745c51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 347

Reference: JER 40:7
Text: Now when all the captains of the forces which were in the fields, even they and their men, heard that the king of Babylon had made Gedaliah the son of Ahikam governor in the land, and had committed unto him men, and women, and children, and of the poor of the land, of them that were not carried away captive to Babylon;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/40/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8134fe22-d930-4f1c-ab4e-a2375ef7fbad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 277

Reference: JER 40:8
Text: Then they came to Gedaliah to Mizpah, even Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, and Johanan and Jonathan the sons of Kareah, and Seraiah the son of Tanhumeth, and the sons of Ephai the Netophathite, and Jezaniah the son of a Maachathite, they and their men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/40/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42501cd6-9bce-4e4a-be5c-784e6c62cc75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: JER 40:9
Text: And Gedaliah the son of Ahikam the son of Shaphan sware unto them and to their men, saying, Fear not to serve the Chaldeans: dwell in the land, and serve the king of Babylon, and it shall be well with you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/40/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72322fae-938c-41f7-8696-958ca6ce8aff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: JER 40:10
Text: As for me, behold, I will dwell at Mizpah, to serve the Chaldeans, which will come unto us: but ye, gather ye wine, and summer fruits, and oil, and put them in your vessels, and dwell in your cities that ye have taken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/40/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fc57704-83b7-49fc-8892-a80df8ea1df0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: JER 40:11
Text: Likewise when all the Jews that were in Moab, and among the Ammonites, and in Edom, and that were in all the countries, heard that the king of Babylon had left a remnant of Judah, and that he had set over them Gedaliah the son of Ahikam the son of Shaphan;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/40/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66d9f7fb-b0be-4d42-b77a-0607477772c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: JER 40:12
Text: Even all the Jews returned out of all places whither they were driven, and came to the land of Judah, to Gedaliah, unto Mizpah, and gathered wine and summer fruits very much.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/40/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5189c0d-5bff-4bc9-a74e-014d7ece276c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: JER 40:13
Text: Moreover Johanan the son of Kareah, and all the captains of the forces that were in the fields, came to Gedaliah to Mizpah,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/40/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ec96833-191a-417e-a883-36b8dba4abdf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: JER 40:14
Text: And said unto him, Dost thou certainly know that Baalis the king of the Ammonites hath sent Ishmael the son of Nethaniah to slay thee? But Gedaliah the son of Ahikam believed them not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/40/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0839672a-7d65-4f5f-bf67-fdfa8fd2a2e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 331

Reference: JER 40:15
Text: Then Johanan the son of Kareah spake to Gedaliah in Mizpah secretly saying, Let me go, I pray thee, and I will slay Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, and no man shall know it: wherefore should he slay thee, that all the Jews which are gathered unto thee should be scattered, and the remnant in Judah perish?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/40/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4e8951e-30a9-4ec4-946a-22cd1696e8c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: JER 40:16
Text: But Gedaliah the son of Ahikam said unto Johanan the son of Kareah, Thou shalt not do this thing: for thou speakest falsely of Ishmael.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/41/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae0eb225-913f-4722-ad1e-2fcebd267b60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 291

Reference: JER 41:1
Text: Now it came to pass in the seventh month, that Ishmael the son of Nethaniah the son of Elishama, of the seed royal, and the princes of the king, even ten men with him, came unto Gedaliah the son of Ahikam to Mizpah; and there they did eat bread together in Mizpah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/41/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d625dc2-6301-479c-b6f0-a823335ef7f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: JER 41:2
Text: Then arose Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, and the ten men that were with him, and smote Gedaliah the son of Ahikam the son of Shaphan with the sword, and slew him, whom the king of Babylon had made governor over the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/41/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd04f020-ca97-4edc-a06d-db62e15c90a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: JER 41:3
Text: Ishmael also slew all the Jews that were with him, even with Gedaliah, at Mizpah, and the Chaldeans that were found there, and the men of war.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/41/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b64a0f6a-bcb0-4b3d-a877-163d6ee5897a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: JER 41:4
Text: And it came to pass the second day after he had slain Gedaliah, and no man knew it,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/41/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90e586ca-0e6d-444f-9fc8-5913b38cc14b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: JER 41:5
Text: That there came certain from Shechem, from Shiloh, and from Samaria, even fourscore men, having their beards shaven, and their clothes rent, and having cut themselves, with offerings and incense in their hand, to bring them to the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/41/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43933e68-f34b-4a6b-aeb8-40a6e92013fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: JER 41:6
Text: And Ishmael the son of Nethaniah went forth from Mizpah to meet them, weeping all along as he went: and it came to pass, as he met them, he said unto them, Come to Gedaliah the son of Ahikam.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/41/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8cd4fb6-96f0-494a-bb8d-ff878e63173e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: JER 41:7
Text: And it was so, when they came into the midst of the city, that Ishmael the son of Nethaniah slew them, and cast them into the midst of the pit, he, and the men that were with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/41/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98aff1dd-6de9-4f62-98b2-4124fd938b43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: JER 41:8
Text: But ten men were found among them that said unto Ishmael, Slay us not: for we have treasures in the field, of wheat, and of barley, and of oil, and of honey. So he forbare, and slew them not among their brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/41/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40a14690-1bfd-429a-9c87-90d8bab8650e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 274

Reference: JER 41:9
Text: Now the pit wherein Ishmael had cast all the dead bodies of the men, whom he had slain because of Gedaliah, was it which Asa the king had made for fear of Baasha king of Israel: and Ishmael the son of Nethaniah filled it with them that were slain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/41/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee4a1c63-56cc-4b4e-a5f6-f28eac6ede52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 374

Reference: JER 41:10
Text: Then Ishmael carried away captive all the residue of the people that were in Mizpah, even the king’s daughters, and all the people that remained in Mizpah, whom Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard had committed to Gedaliah the son of Ahikam: and Ishmael the son of Nethaniah carried them away captive, and departed to go over to the Ammonites.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/41/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:672122b4-e13e-40ec-8b33-026b8a38c0a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: JER 41:11
Text: But when Johanan the son of Kareah, and all the captains of the forces that were with him, heard of all the evil that Ishmael the son of Nethaniah had done,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/41/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0803c48f-8cf7-459a-a90c-493cd0009621>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: JER 41:12
Text: Then they took all the men, and went to fight with Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, and found him by the great waters that are in Gibeon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/41/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18b5e672-158b-46e6-9051-20c5cbdfd0b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: JER 41:13
Text: Now it came to pass, that when all the people which were with Ishmael saw Johanan the son of Kareah, and all the captains of the forces that were with him, then they were glad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/41/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:713f76ea-163b-4ca3-98e0-53c6ae6897d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: JER 41:14
Text: So all the people that Ishmael had carried away captive from Mizpah cast about and returned, and went unto Johanan the son of Kareah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/41/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4088c55-c17a-4fbd-ae4a-3b8779215f67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: JER 41:15
Text: But Ishmael the son of Nethaniah escaped from Johanan with eight men, and went to the Ammonites.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/41/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc85eea1-cea5-4774-95ff-b20cad5fc514>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 384

Reference: JER 41:16
Text: Then took Johanan the son of Kareah, and all the captains of the forces that were with him, all the remnant of the people whom he had recovered from Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, from Mizpah, after that he had slain Gedaliah the son of Ahikam, even mighty men of war, and the women, and the children, and the eunuchs, whom he had brought again from Gibeon:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/41/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d81e690c-d801-43dc-bbd3-d73bb8011cdb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: JER 41:17
Text: And they departed, and dwelt in the habitation of Chimham, which is by Bethlehem, to go to enter into Egypt,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/41/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6927e91-3725-40d1-9f90-6efcc35e9674>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: JER 41:18
Text: Because of the Chaldeans: for they were afraid of them, because Ishmael the son of Nethaniah had slain Gedaliah the son of Ahikam, whom the king of Babylon made governor in the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/42/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a953ebd-1aac-4a10-8430-780adf1dab63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: JER 42:1
Text: Then all the captains of the forces, and Johanan the son of Kareah, and Jezaniah the son of Hoshaiah, and all the people from the least even unto the greatest, came near,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/42/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:265b0179-deb9-4439-bd2b-b56075c3a2f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: JER 42:2
Text: And said unto Jeremiah the prophet, Let, we beseech thee, our supplication be accepted before thee, and pray for us unto the LORD thy God, even for all this remnant; (for we are left but a few of many, as thine eyes do behold us:)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/42/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e7673c8-ff4d-4c8b-9a55-ec250041c3a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: JER 42:3
Text: That the LORD thy God may shew us the way wherein we may walk, and the thing that we may do.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/42/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd463811-6901-44ae-865e-6361a0a56f19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 293

Reference: JER 42:4
Text: Then Jeremiah the prophet said unto them, I have heard you; behold, I will pray unto the LORD your God according to your words; and it shall come to pass, that whatsoever thing the LORD shall answer you, I will declare it unto you; I will keep nothing back from you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/42/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:312601b7-f902-464f-ab66-38c6bbade7c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: JER 42:5
Text: Then they said to Jeremiah, The LORD be a true and faithful witness between us, if we do not even according to all things for the which the LORD thy God shall send thee to us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/42/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cc58e9f-bc80-460a-a57e-045d537552f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: JER 42:6
Text: Whether it be good, or whether it be evil, we will obey the voice of the LORD our God, to whom we send thee; that it may be well with us, when we obey the voice of the LORD our God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/42/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ad0e749-7869-48d0-bbe7-5a079dab298e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: JER 42:7
Text: And it came to pass after ten days, that the word of the LORD came unto Jeremiah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/42/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49b3fce1-f051-4de0-b0ea-acaebc171c77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: JER 42:8
Text: Then called he Johanan the son of Kareah, and all the captains of the forces which were with him, and all the people from the least even to the greatest,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/42/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed2d80d3-bc59-42a1-b12f-4048a9b9948a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: JER 42:9
Text: And said unto them, Thus saith the LORD, the God of Israel, unto whom ye sent me to present your supplication before him;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/42/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c31b4146-4eaa-434e-aa61-978e7b00e9aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: JER 42:10
Text: If ye will still abide in this land, then will I build you, and not pull you down, and I will plant you, and not pluck you up: for I repent me of the evil that I have done unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/42/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f175ea6a-17c6-4dee-a0f8-89aef117d55f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: JER 42:11
Text: Be not afraid of the king of Babylon, of whom ye are afraid; be not afraid of him, saith the LORD: for I am with you to save you, and to deliver you from his hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/42/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a16da1cc-5cd5-4568-9f4f-9cadac36b98d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: JER 42:12
Text: And I will shew mercies unto you, that he may have mercy upon you, and cause you to return to your own land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/42/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27149dac-6e36-4210-9af4-e250d42d57fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: JER 42:13
Text: But if ye say, We will not dwell in this land, neither obey the voice of the LORD your God,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/42/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1784773-8900-4299-a9ef-70cb275b6e98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: JER 42:14
Text: Saying, No; but we will go into the land of Egypt, where we shall see no war, nor hear the sound of the trumpet, nor have hunger of bread; and there will we dwell:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/42/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd00f9fd-62a1-4b4c-9bb3-d210475e3331>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: JER 42:15
Text: And now therefore hear the word of the LORD, ye remnant of Judah; Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; If ye wholly set your faces to enter into Egypt, and go to sojourn there;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/42/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c19125e9-957c-4e57-b0cc-f88dd237007e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: JER 42:16
Text: Then it shall come to pass, that the sword, which ye feared, shall overtake you there in the land of Egypt, and the famine, whereof ye were afraid, shall follow close after you there in Egypt; and there ye shall die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/42/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a0ad0e0-fbd9-488b-bc49-ead1bf28de97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: JER 42:17
Text: So shall it be with all the men that set their faces to go into Egypt to sojourn there; they shall die by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence: and none of them shall remain or escape from the evil that I will bring upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/42/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e37cb9f-b465-4e26-8641-b2b80f6739bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 357

Reference: JER 42:18
Text: For thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; As mine anger and my fury hath been poured forth upon the inhabitants of Jerusalem; so shall my fury be poured forth upon you, when ye shall enter into Egypt: and ye shall be an execration, and an astonishment, and a curse, and a reproach; and ye shall see this place no more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/42/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a6f6ed8-302c-45e2-9f10-ebe365098876>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: JER 42:19
Text: The LORD hath said concerning you, O ye remnant of Judah; Go ye not into Egypt: know certainly that I have admonished you this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/42/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f65730c9-732e-418a-a12c-af95beec9c4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: JER 42:20
Text: For ye dissembled in your hearts, when ye sent me unto the LORD your God, saying, Pray for us unto the LORD our God; and according unto all that the LORD our God shall say, so declare unto us, and we will do it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/42/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0992223-94d9-4231-8c44-1aec189477ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: JER 42:21
Text: And now I have this day declared it to you; but ye have not obeyed the voice of the LORD your God, nor any thing for the which he hath sent me unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/42/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9214d16d-d56f-4af7-8461-58e9784fef69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: JER 42:22
Text: Now therefore know certainly that ye shall die by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence, in the place whither ye desire to go and to sojourn.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/43/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d695542d-4680-4132-a6ee-41ccf8b1a348>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: JER 43:1
Text: And it came to pass, that when Jeremiah had made an end of speaking unto all the people all the words of the LORD their God, for which the LORD their God had sent him to them, even all these words,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/43/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54f16d33-08b4-40f8-b1f2-5674d45c9ed2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: JER 43:2
Text: Then spake Azariah the son of Hoshaiah, and Johanan the son of Kareah, and all the proud men, saying unto Jeremiah, Thou speakest falsely: the LORD our God hath not sent thee to say, Go not into Egypt to sojourn there:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/43/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8751f189-be69-4d5c-8daf-bd45ce5c895e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: JER 43:3
Text: But Baruch the son of Neriah setteth thee on against us, for to deliver us into the hand of the Chaldeans, that they might put us to death, and carry us away captives into Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/43/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97a4ac17-7880-4576-8ed9-5f577bc23007>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: JER 43:4
Text: So Johanan the son of Kareah, and all the captains of the forces, and all the people, obeyed not the voice of the LORD, to dwell in the land of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/43/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cfdace3-33be-4bf3-ab66-81154ffa7c48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: JER 43:5
Text: But Johanan the son of Kareah, and all the captains of the forces, took all the remnant of Judah, that were returned from all nations, whither they had been driven, to dwell in the land of Judah;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/43/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d6ff3d2-9e0f-46c2-bd73-e8c64f059755>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: JER 43:6
Text: Even men, and women, and children, and the king’s daughters, and every person that Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard had left with Gedaliah the son of Ahikam the son of Shaphan, and Jeremiah the prophet, and Baruch the son of Neriah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/43/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a68528d-0e68-4650-b710-a2284d906d68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: JER 43:7
Text: So they came into the land of Egypt: for they obeyed not the voice of the LORD: thus came they even to Tahpanhes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/43/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:238e31a5-9c61-4737-8f92-29c08368b0f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: JER 43:8
Text: Then came the word of the LORD unto Jeremiah in Tahpanhes, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/43/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f6202f4-fe39-4a7e-b069-7376f35acd4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: JER 43:9
Text: Take great stones in thine hand, and hide them in the clay in the brickkiln, which is at the entry of Pharaoh’s house in Tahpanhes, in the sight of the men of Judah;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/43/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c210d7b-9c3a-4f18-8b59-27acc566743f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 281

Reference: JER 43:10
Text: And say unto them, Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Behold, I will send and take Nebuchadrezzar the king of Babylon, my servant, and will set his throne upon these stones that I have hid; and he shall spread his royal pavilion over them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/43/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad3355b4-e6b6-4ab4-a6ee-133762245a6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: JER 43:11
Text: And when he cometh, he shall smite the land of Egypt, and deliver such as are for death to death; and such as are for captivity to captivity; and such as are for the sword to the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/43/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87acc694-b59a-46e6-a303-bd03748dc811>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: JER 43:12
Text: And I will kindle a fire in the houses of the gods of Egypt; and he shall burn them, and carry them away captives: and he shall array himself with the land of Egypt, as a shepherd putteth on his garment; and he shall go forth from thence in peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/43/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb52bb38-9902-4b2e-81d7-53d145c0842b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: JER 43:13
Text: He shall break also the images of Bethshemesh, that is in the land of Egypt; and the houses of the gods of the Egyptians shall he burn with fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7331323-33fa-490c-b7c0-9e503d47791e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: JER 44:1
Text: The word that came to Jeremiah concerning all the Jews which dwell in the land of Egypt, which dwell at Migdol, and at Tahpanhes, and at Noph, and in the country of Pathros, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9789fa18-9027-430b-9ca9-6cf77b30fb1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: JER 44:2
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Ye have seen all the evil that I have brought upon Jerusalem, and upon all the cities of Judah; and, behold, this day they are a desolation, and no man dwelleth therein,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50013f77-6724-4ed4-a3e0-f891384ff809>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: JER 44:3
Text: Because of their wickedness which they have committed to provoke me to anger, in that they went to burn incense, and to serve other gods, whom they knew not, neither they, ye, nor your fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:798ce0be-3f12-4700-bf8e-105dd943c733>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: JER 44:4
Text: Howbeit I sent unto you all my servants the prophets, rising early and sending them, saying, Oh, do not this abominable thing that I hate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cde7dfa0-e9cf-4e82-bf96-b8f1753300dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: JER 44:5
Text: But they hearkened not, nor inclined their ear to turn from their wickedness, to burn no incense unto other gods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1612eb2d-3edd-49cb-bad3-f07d4b47cc60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: JER 44:6
Text: Wherefore my fury and mine anger was poured forth, and was kindled in the cities of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem; and they are wasted and desolate, as at this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5abe912b-00a4-449e-bd8a-ba5ef78c2191>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: JER 44:7
Text: Therefore now thus saith the LORD, the God of hosts, the God of Israel; Wherefore commit ye this great evil against your souls, to cut off from you man and woman, child and suckling, out of Judah, to leave you none to remain;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e5ebd7e-dfbe-48c3-a626-8c079d4534d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 286

Reference: JER 44:8
Text: In that ye provoke me unto wrath with the works of your hands, burning incense unto other gods in the land of Egypt, whither ye be gone to dwell, that ye might cut yourselves off, and that ye might be a curse and a reproach among all the nations of the earth?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e302cf8-9f31-4b91-b1f6-b5f055240a15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 293

Reference: JER 44:9
Text: Have ye forgotten the wickedness of your fathers, and the wickedness of the kings of Judah, and the wickedness of their wives, and your own wickedness, and the wickedness of your wives, which they have committed in the land of Judah, and in the streets of Jerusalem?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56983ac6-4bd1-4241-8b82-4455b7c4c827>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: JER 44:10
Text: They are not humbled even unto this day, neither have they feared, nor walked in my law, nor in my statutes, that I set before you and before your fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7842a6c0-2771-4287-992e-850fa0fb4343>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: JER 44:11
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Behold, I will set my face against you for evil, and to cut off all Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d12f98e-737f-44bd-abbe-aab788f76d70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 431

Reference: JER 44:12
Text: And I will take the remnant of Judah, that have set their faces to go into the land of Egypt to sojourn there, and they shall all be consumed, and fall in the land of Egypt; they shall even be consumed by the sword and by the famine: they shall die, from the least even unto the greatest, by the sword and by the famine: and they shall be an execration, and an astonishment, and a curse, and a reproach.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19125ce9-a190-4f99-8efe-b890b3e6329f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: JER 44:13
Text: For I will punish them that dwell in the land of Egypt, as I have punished Jerusalem, by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:134f7e10-7f2b-4f06-84df-6caadbe95825>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 299

Reference: JER 44:14
Text: So that none of the remnant of Judah, which are gone into the land of Egypt to sojourn there, shall escape or remain, that they should return into the land of Judah, to the which they have a desire to return to dwell there: for none shall return but such as shall escape.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3f38f31-748c-4558-8249-48f5582ce118>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: JER 44:15
Text: Then all the men which knew that their wives had burned incense unto other gods, and all the women that stood by, a great multitude, even all the people that dwelt in the land of Egypt, in Pathros, answered Jeremiah, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef2cddcc-cdb6-4003-ad65-5c3ca54139b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: JER 44:16
Text: As for the word that thou hast spoken unto us in the name of the LORD, we will not hearken unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8c25b79-b031-4921-b0f3-407016359107>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 378

Reference: JER 44:17
Text: But we will certainly do whatsoever thing goeth forth out of our own mouth, to burn incense unto the queen of heaven, and to pour out drink offerings unto her, as we have done, we, and our fathers, our kings, and our princes, in the cities of Judah, and in the streets of Jerusalem: for then had we plenty of victuals, and were well, and saw no evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a460991a-f15b-49cc-bbee-b303a0b14c09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: JER 44:18
Text: But since we left off to burn incense to the queen of heaven, and to pour out drink offerings unto her, we have wanted all things, and have been consumed by the sword and by the famine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7b8f10c-0430-43ae-9c0f-6d13ece3887f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: JER 44:19
Text: And when we burned incense to the queen of heaven, and poured out drink offerings unto her, did we make her cakes to worship her, and pour out drink offerings unto her, without our men?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:624b7369-eb33-4b1f-b21f-659828a1b1af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: JER 44:20
Text: Then Jeremiah said unto all the people, to the men, and to the women, and to all the people which had given him that answer, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0500358f-7cdd-4374-95ea-440f3ecdbcee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: JER 44:21
Text: The incense that ye burned in the cities of Judah, and in the streets of Jerusalem, ye, and your fathers, your kings, and your princes, and the people of the land, did not the LORD remember them, and came it not into his mind?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:734a6ed3-8c41-4a9c-9845-1335315ef9c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: JER 44:22
Text: So that the LORD could no longer bear, because of the evil of your doings, and because of the abominations which ye have committed; therefore is your land a desolation, and an astonishment, and a curse, without an inhabitant, as at this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fddb104c-7440-4c95-9be4-e6eac28aa250>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 273

Reference: JER 44:23
Text: Because ye have burned incense, and because ye have sinned against the LORD, and have not obeyed the voice of the LORD, nor walked in his law, nor in his statutes, nor in his testimonies; therefore this evil is happened unto you, as at this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6cb7c36b-3590-403a-a96e-e301abd1435f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: JER 44:24
Text: Moreover Jeremiah said unto all the people, and to all the women, Hear the word of the LORD, all Judah that are in the land of Egypt:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4a1624e-4962-4d54-81ef-7617b06d02d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 376

Reference: JER 44:25
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, saying; Ye and your wives have both spoken with your mouths, and fulfilled with your hand, saying, We will surely perform our vows that we have vowed, to burn incense to the queen of heaven, and to pour out drink offerings unto her: ye will surely accomplish your vows, and surely perform your vows.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d2e9b31-6437-492e-9218-56015c07136f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 289

Reference: JER 44:26
Text: Therefore hear ye the word of the LORD, all Judah that dwell in the land of Egypt; Behold, I have sworn by my great name, saith the LORD, that my name shall no more be named in the mouth of any man of Judah in all the land of Egypt, saying, The Lord GOD liveth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a64eee53-93d2-4c0f-9a0b-7e4fbc69b73f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: JER 44:27
Text: Behold, I will watch over them for evil, and not for good: and all the men of Judah that are in the land of Egypt shall be consumed by the sword and by the famine, until there be an end of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7bc28ac7-3564-4155-a1ad-00798ec347b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: JER 44:28
Text: Yet a small number that escape the sword shall return out of the land of Egypt into the land of Judah, and all the remnant of Judah, that are gone into the land of Egypt to sojourn there, shall know whose words shall stand, mine, or theirs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e4ebb56-6f6e-4903-b9c7-348729386ba3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: JER 44:29
Text: And this shall be a sign unto you, saith the LORD, that I will punish you in this place, that ye may know that my words shall surely stand against you for evil:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/44/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69f1908f-d785-46b5-8a91-64a4290cca88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 291

Reference: JER 44:30
Text: Thus saith the LORD; Behold, I will give Pharaohhophra king of Egypt into the hand of his enemies, and into the hand of them that seek his life; as I gave Zedekiah king of Judah into the hand of Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon, his enemy, and that sought his life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/45/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffd3b723-1f4b-47bf-88ac-600037b1f79a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: JER 45:1
Text: The word that Jeremiah the prophet spake unto Baruch the son of Neriah, when he had written these words in a book at the mouth of Jeremiah, in the fourth year of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/45/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad0c87cc-b52f-49e5-a5a5-10f61b1e1551>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: JER 45:2
Text: Thus saith the LORD, the God of Israel, unto thee, O Baruch:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/45/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5a1006c-7328-4d7f-8329-077c044f6c4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: JER 45:3
Text: Thou didst say, Woe is me now! for the LORD hath added grief to my sorrow; I fainted in my sighing, and I find no rest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/45/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc2bc75f-2c4d-44a9-bc72-1a624103dea9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: JER 45:4
Text: Thus shalt thou say unto him, The LORD saith thus; Behold, that which I have built will I break down, and that which I have planted I will pluck up, even this whole land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/45/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b670ebbf-c16d-4939-b2dc-c735ddaf9b1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: JER 45:5
Text: And seekest thou great things for thyself? seek them not: for, behold, I will bring evil upon all flesh, saith the LORD: but thy life will I give unto thee for a prey in all places whither thou goest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7d3c371-570d-4f9c-af1a-f79cf7e2462d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: JER 46:1
Text: The word of the LORD which came to Jeremiah the prophet against the Gentiles;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29214b51-0d63-4158-8553-547d7962f8ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: JER 46:2
Text: Against Egypt, against the army of Pharaohnecho king of Egypt, which was by the river Euphrates in Carchemish, which Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon smote in the fourth year of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah king of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:011bca5d-20c0-4a2e-a446-e2b10aa575a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: JER 46:3
Text: Order ye the buckler and shield, and draw near to battle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b38a3531-6d3e-4de1-9a2a-acabbdbc6128>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: JER 46:4
Text: Harness the horses; and get up, ye horsemen, and stand forth with your helmets; furbish the spears, and put on the brigandines.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23acdc8b-fcd2-4597-bd4d-879ce06c62bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: JER 46:5
Text: Wherefore have I seen them dismayed and turned away back? and their mighty ones are beaten down, and are fled apace, and look not back: for fear was round about, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a683ed2-fa31-49e0-8d63-c16b0b0fd39e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: JER 46:6
Text: Let not the swift flee away, nor the mighty man escape; they shall stumble, and fall toward the north by the river Euphrates.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2cbf7624-2bf0-492b-92b2-2b3044d151f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: JER 46:7
Text: Who is this that cometh up as a flood, whose waters are moved as the rivers?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45c3fc1d-306a-489d-8a1f-1b97203a2721>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: JER 46:8
Text: Egypt riseth up like a flood, and his waters are moved like the rivers; and he saith, I will go up, and will cover the earth; I will destroy the city and the inhabitants thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:745495ee-5073-47e2-a4c8-72726c9b44ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: JER 46:9
Text: Come up, ye horses; and rage, ye chariots; and let the mighty men come forth; the Ethiopians and the Libyans, that handle the shield; and the Lydians, that handle and bend the bow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38784e67-43ed-4ac4-b54d-58bb627c06bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 309

Reference: JER 46:10
Text: For this is the day of the Lord GOD of hosts, a day of vengeance, that he may avenge him of his adversaries: and the sword shall devour, and it shall be satiate and made drunk with their blood: for the Lord GOD of hosts hath a sacrifice in the north country by the river Euphrates.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:accd5195-fecd-482f-9466-9dda31a8c1f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: JER 46:11
Text: Go up into Gilead, and take balm, O virgin, the daughter of Egypt: in vain shalt thou use many medicines; for thou shalt not be cured.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ddb1d1d-1caa-4871-9406-bed69d8db5ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: JER 46:12
Text: The nations have heard of thy shame, and thy cry hath filled the land: for the mighty man hath stumbled against the mighty, and they are fallen both together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7d13d79-ba8a-4493-86bb-349b9c8e73bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: JER 46:13
Text: The word that the LORD spake to Jeremiah the prophet, how Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon should come and smite the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d09880f0-af74-48c0-ab4c-f690d286b281>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: JER 46:14
Text: Declare ye in Egypt, and publish in Migdol, and publish in Noph and in Tahpanhes: say ye, Stand fast, and prepare thee; for the sword shall devour round about thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1e58c25-4c56-43df-9e59-72c31cab6c67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: JER 46:15
Text: Why are thy valiant men swept away? they stood not, because the LORD did drive them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c90016a0-31bc-41eb-8b42-4619bc0282c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: JER 46:16
Text: He made many to fall, yea, one fell upon another: and they said, Arise, and let us go again to our own people, and to the land of our nativity, from the oppressing sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58f83630-c2df-4b59-82f8-6c0fe6a78800>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: JER 46:17
Text: They did cry there, Pharaoh king of Egypt is but a noise; he hath passed the time appointed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3dd00186-d461-4845-83bd-f741b64c9503>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: JER 46:18
Text: As I live, saith the King, whose name is the LORD of hosts, Surely as Tabor is among the mountains, and as Carmel by the sea, so shall he come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3fdb8081-ab28-452c-9d9f-746f09b1e4bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: JER 46:19
Text: O thou daughter dwelling in Egypt, furnish thyself to go into captivity: for Noph shall be waste and desolate without an inhabitant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6734f79-e7b9-494e-8588-6512871aa7c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: JER 46:20
Text: Egypt is like a very fair heifer, but destruction cometh; it cometh out of the north.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5498e559-65ef-425a-963c-309f7ce4940a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: JER 46:21
Text: Also her hired men are in the midst of her like fatted bullocks; for they also are turned back, and are fled away together: they did not stand, because the day of their calamity was come upon them, and the time of their visitation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a0d99ea-e08a-4219-af52-0ba57a3e16bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: JER 46:22
Text: The voice thereof shall go like a serpent; for they shall march with an army, and come against her with axes, as hewers of wood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8640e817-1358-4c0e-aff5-e84e86b1378c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: JER 46:23
Text: They shall cut down her forest, saith the LORD, though it cannot be searched; because they are more than the grasshoppers, and are innumerable.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1bdd83f6-6f14-400a-81ec-6819fe8e9d14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: JER 46:24
Text: The daughter of Egypt shall be confounded; she shall be delivered into the hand of the people of the north.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fe95a28-8cf6-49f1-846d-b808bc989b92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: JER 46:25
Text: The LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, saith; Behold, I will punish the multitude of No, and Pharaoh, and Egypt, with their gods, and their kings; even Pharaoh, and all them that trust in him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c34f126e-d072-49e7-97a5-ab9934235311>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: JER 46:26
Text: And I will deliver them into the hand of those that seek their lives, and into the hand of Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon, and into the hand of his servants: and afterward it shall be inhabited, as in the days of old, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f95bd062-e80f-41f5-a523-eceda8de2b44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 273

Reference: JER 46:27
Text: But fear not thou, O my servant Jacob, and be not dismayed, O Israel: for, behold, I will save thee from afar off, and thy seed from the land of their captivity; and Jacob shall return, and be in rest and at ease, and none shall make him afraid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/46/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:577699bd-77a6-4f6e-bb74-2fda431d9913>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 286

Reference: JER 46:28
Text: Fear thou not, O Jacob my servant, saith the LORD: for I am with thee; for I will make a full end of all the nations whither I have driven thee: but I will not make a full end of thee, but correct thee in measure; yet will I not leave thee wholly unpunished.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/47/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff71b73d-c05b-4ff5-b8aa-9f4933917197>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: JER 47:1
Text: The word of the LORD that came to Jeremiah the prophet against the Philistines, before that Pharaoh smote Gaza.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/47/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08178383-9595-47f6-8c0e-b1ad9c396fd3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 288

Reference: JER 47:2
Text: Thus saith the LORD; Behold, waters rise up out of the north, and shall be an overflowing flood, and shall overflow the land, and all that is therein; the city, and them that dwell therein: then the men shall cry, and all the inhabitants of the land shall howl.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/47/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:374883cf-4f67-4323-a35d-fc0e0b9cd0f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: JER 47:3
Text: At the noise of the stamping of the hoofs of his strong horses, at the rushing of his chariots, and at the rumbling of his wheels, the fathers shall not look back to their children for feebleness of hands;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/47/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:213091a6-e34e-4c3c-a700-67da467a48c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: JER 47:4
Text: Because of the day that cometh to spoil all the Philistines, and to cut off from Tyrus and Zidon every helper that remaineth: for the LORD will spoil the Philistines, the remnant of the country of Caphtor.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/47/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0c29076-0895-45b7-a26d-caf69773bdda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: JER 47:5
Text: Baldness is come upon Gaza; Ashkelon is cut off with the remnant of their valley: how long wilt thou cut thyself?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/47/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fae60412-11fa-45f5-a197-dc80c122bbd9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: JER 47:6
Text: O thou sword of the LORD, how long will it be ere thou be quiet? put up thyself into thy scabbard, rest, and be still.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/47/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0329c86c-2cc4-4482-a015-2a94d4cf618f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: JER 47:7
Text: How can it be quiet, seeing the LORD hath given it a charge against Ashkelon, and against the sea shore? there hath he appointed it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed9d72d0-2197-41d6-9b93-5b9afeef1839>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: JER 48:1
Text: Against Moab thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Woe unto Nebo! for it is spoiled: Kiriathaim is confounded and taken: Misgab is confounded and dismayed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fe4dbb4-79a2-4a7f-a08b-d346774b5f41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: JER 48:2
Text: There shall be no more praise of Moab: in Heshbon they have devised evil against it; come, and let us cut it off from being a nation. Also thou shalt be cut down, O Madmen; the sword shall pursue thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e40fa439-9c53-4e06-bfca-d4521b6a2ffc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: JER 48:3
Text: A voice of crying shall be from Horonaim, spoiling and great destruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b92c6a9-0301-4733-8090-d37ea6b1fd5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: JER 48:4
Text: Moab is destroyed; her little ones have caused a cry to be heard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e223b1d1-6dd7-44ab-b640-d08891905a20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: JER 48:5
Text: For in the going up of Luhith continual weeping shall go up; for in the going down of Horonaim the enemies have heard a cry of destruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c453767b-93b4-4d22-a8f2-d65a5c146560>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: JER 48:6
Text: Flee, save your lives, and be like the heath in the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b10f10a-6c1a-459a-ab48-5e24ca6efe14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: JER 48:7
Text: For because thou hast trusted in thy works and in thy treasures, thou shalt also be taken: and Chemosh shall go forth into captivity with his priests and his princes together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:530f705a-8bea-495a-8eb6-545f2c20e25f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JER 48:8
Text: And the spoiler shall come upon every city, and no city shall escape: the valley also shall perish, and the plain shall be destroyed, as the LORD hath spoken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6aecf630-6e9a-4f9a-a6b9-1e5723837d66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: JER 48:9
Text: Give wings unto Moab, that it may flee and get away: for the cities thereof shall be desolate, without any to dwell therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:291e6c66-f299-4970-a687-c25070bd8f23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: JER 48:10
Text: Cursed be he that doeth the work of the LORD deceitfully, and cursed be he that keepeth back his sword from blood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37e77b58-b9af-415a-bd34-ea7fc0f0d381>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: JER 48:11
Text: Moab hath been at ease from his youth, and he hath settled on his lees, and hath not been emptied from vessel to vessel, neither hath he gone into captivity: therefore his taste remained in him, and his scent is not changed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad617825-7c6b-4de9-8bc4-e69f6b23d361>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: JER 48:12
Text: Therefore, behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that I will send unto him wanderers, that shall cause him to wander, and shall empty his vessels, and break their bottles.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ee2355d-6a37-427c-87e6-766cfe7af09e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: JER 48:13
Text: And Moab shall be ashamed of Chemosh, as the house of Israel was ashamed of Bethel their confidence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e80674e7-544b-4798-add7-a9a0caf17016>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: JER 48:14
Text: How say ye, We are mighty and strong men for the war?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bb2283d-08fc-4331-99c1-86a5af4b6468>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: JER 48:15
Text: Moab is spoiled, and gone up out of her cities, and his chosen young men are gone down to the slaughter, saith the King, whose name is the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:759e460b-0031-4f1f-bb35-8fa119413fd2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: JER 48:16
Text: The calamity of Moab is near to come, and his affliction hasteth fast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0de59056-357c-42cc-81c3-90ca712fb46c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: JER 48:17
Text: All ye that are about him, bemoan him; and all ye that know his name, say, How is the strong staff broken, and the beautiful rod!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc6d242c-75e3-4bd9-9f9f-8cc7c81e5390>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: JER 48:18
Text: Thou daughter that dost inhabit Dibon, come down from thy glory, and sit in thirst; for the spoiler of Moab shall come upon thee, and he shall destroy thy strong holds.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5cc6ea64-7ce6-4798-91d9-fd968a0e5de7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: JER 48:19
Text: O inhabitant of Aroer, stand by the way, and espy; ask him that fleeth, and her that escapeth, and say, What is done?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d0d4468-fc4f-401c-8074-09c223869336>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: JER 48:20
Text: Moab is confounded; for it is broken down: howl and cry; tell ye it in Arnon, that Moab is spoiled,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86f7a459-21af-4b01-b0a5-78759165ebc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: JER 48:21
Text: And judgment is come upon the plain country; upon Holon, and upon Jahazah, and upon Mephaath,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63be3d46-5799-44c3-b640-f77d902be2f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: JER 48:22
Text: And upon Dibon, and upon Nebo, and upon Bethdiblathaim,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9cbb5042-c1f2-4fb7-8f12-c547502df80c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: JER 48:23
Text: And upon Kiriathaim, and upon Bethgamul, and upon Bethmeon,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20f2bc76-139f-4a16-a36a-7e7913ea9b06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: JER 48:24
Text: And upon Kerioth, and upon Bozrah, and upon all the cities of the land of Moab, far or near.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afc92589-8578-4f39-9e07-614f83af4233>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: JER 48:25
Text: The horn of Moab is cut off, and his arm is broken, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aaa4883f-f813-4ce2-a3b2-e55cfbcf2740>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: JER 48:26
Text: Make ye him drunken: for he magnified himself against the LORD: Moab also shall wallow in his vomit, and he also shall be in derision.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:780ef613-af1a-464a-98e6-87c8d61c578e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: JER 48:27
Text: For was not Israel a derision unto thee? was he found among thieves? for since thou spakest of him, thou skippedst for joy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9649ee34-15b7-49bd-9ffb-381f2c6d4682>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: JER 48:28
Text: O ye that dwell in Moab, leave the cities, and dwell in the rock, and be like the dove that maketh her nest in the sides of the hole’s mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:589a8274-5856-4c21-a90e-dad0fc00da2f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: JER 48:29
Text: We have heard the pride of Moab, (he is exceeding proud) his loftiness, and his arrogancy, and his pride, and the haughtiness of his heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:347c604e-b5ee-48db-808b-7e31cf978b01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: JER 48:30
Text: I know his wrath, saith the LORD; but it shall not be so; his lies shall not so effect it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8de11cc-9ad5-4ecc-98d0-0587e23f0eb8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: JER 48:31
Text: Therefore will I howl for Moab, and I will cry out for all Moab; mine heart shall mourn for the men of Kirheres.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a45b4d1a-5787-456e-af92-d261baa31b24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: JER 48:32
Text: O vine of Sibmah, I will weep for thee with the weeping of Jazer: thy plants are gone over the sea, they reach even to the sea of Jazer: the spoiler is fallen upon thy summer fruits and upon thy vintage.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e1bf9fd-6eed-420d-8814-457aa35254df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: JER 48:33
Text: And joy and gladness is taken from the plentiful field, and from the land of Moab, and I have caused wine to fail from the winepresses: none shall tread with shouting; their shouting shall be no shouting.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:788c15d8-a925-48bd-bfe3-a0a8b18f9ab7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: JER 48:34
Text: From the cry of Heshbon even unto Elealeh, and even unto Jahaz, have they uttered their voice, from Zoar even unto Horonaim, as an heifer of three years old: for the waters also of Nimrim shall be desolate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:228a5566-4d62-420e-8fec-1696abbd4adc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: JER 48:35
Text: Moreover I will cause to cease in Moab, saith the LORD, him that offereth in the high places, and him that burneth incense to his gods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad18537a-afc9-438a-b764-d55a545a2559>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: JER 48:36
Text: Therefore mine heart shall sound for Moab like pipes, and mine heart shall sound like pipes for the men of Kirheres: because the riches that he hath gotten are perished.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b1798cf-c32e-44ab-8503-fa7ff6ae594a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: JER 48:37
Text: For every head shall be bald, and every beard clipped: upon all the hands shall be cuttings, and upon the loins sackcloth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d25dfa61-944f-4b73-9b24-1fc07f0dcdf6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: JER 48:38
Text: There shall be lamentation generally upon all the housetops of Moab, and in the streets thereof: for I have broken Moab like a vessel wherein is no pleasure, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ff8ecab-99c1-4ec1-864a-b7b6d3a23ced>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: JER 48:39
Text: They shall howl, saying, How is it broken down! how hath Moab turned the back with shame! so shall Moab be a derision and a dismaying to all them about him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8310eace-b67d-40ab-b1c1-e0be6b5e2ec6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: JER 48:40
Text: For thus saith the LORD; Behold, he shall fly as an eagle, and shall spread his wings over Moab.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c656d586-aa72-48fb-b295-d2f3958f21aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: JER 48:41
Text: Kerioth is taken, and the strong holds are surprised, and the mighty men’s hearts in Moab at that day shall be as the heart of a woman in her pangs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b661c39e-cf97-4a5c-87cd-7911ca33ca9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: JER 48:42
Text: And Moab shall be destroyed from being a people, because he hath magnified himself against the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50a9edc9-dd41-478c-a815-6cc475a68b8e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: JER 48:43
Text: Fear, and the pit, and the snare, shall be upon thee, O inhabitant of Moab, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dba5adbe-1dc3-49ea-a845-a7a6d300b4be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: JER 48:44
Text: He that fleeth from the fear shall fall into the pit; and he that getteth up out of the pit shall be taken in the snare: for I will bring upon it, even upon Moab, the year of their visitation, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b92e972c-6044-4ca2-af72-8c4b5493599c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 266

Reference: JER 48:45
Text: They that fled stood under the shadow of Heshbon because of the force: but a fire shall come forth out of Heshbon, and a flame from the midst of Sihon, and shall devour the corner of Moab, and the crown of the head of the tumultuous ones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3068f702-2f85-4d82-b793-ff02f9a1c245>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: JER 48:46
Text: Woe be unto thee, O Moab! the people of Chemosh perisheth: for thy sons are taken captives, and thy daughters captives.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/48/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05a02171-557a-42cc-8fc3-4bc419a37934>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: JER 48:47
Text: Yet will I bring again the captivity of Moab in the latter days, saith the LORD. Thus far is the judgment of Moab.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a6d0626-7a4b-486e-b072-2dba92e2b5b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JER 49:1
Text: Concerning the Ammonites, thus saith the LORD; Hath Israel no sons? hath he no heir? why then doth their king inherit Gad, and his people dwell in his cities?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad7785e1-1505-458b-ad3a-378030c61bb9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 301

Reference: JER 49:2
Text: Therefore, behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that I will cause an alarm of war to be heard in Rabbah of the Ammonites; and it shall be a desolate heap, and her daughters shall be burned with fire: then shall Israel be heir unto them that were his heirs, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2eb7d82f-7703-4d5d-9652-cd98c5520c19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: JER 49:3
Text: Howl, O Heshbon, for Ai is spoiled: cry, ye daughters of Rabbah, gird you with sackcloth; lament, and run to and fro by the hedges; for their king shall go into captivity, and his priests and his princes together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6bd41fd-16ab-4d18-8154-c75e79c3b16a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: JER 49:4
Text: Wherefore gloriest thou in the valleys, thy flowing valley, O backsliding daughter? that trusted in her treasures, saying, Who shall come unto me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d161122e-b76d-4cc6-a6dd-4f6dc62c6ddb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: JER 49:5
Text: Behold, I will bring a fear upon thee, saith the Lord GOD of hosts, from all those that be about thee; and ye shall be driven out every man right forth; and none shall gather up him that wandereth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94937e75-40b3-47c4-84ac-02572c39ea42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: JER 49:6
Text: And afterward I will bring again the captivity of the children of Ammon, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:195a4eae-4342-4382-af51-2795b74164ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: JER 49:7
Text: Concerning Edom, thus saith the LORD of hosts; Is wisdom no more in Teman? is counsel perished from the prudent? is their wisdom vanished?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58e16702-deb1-44b2-a192-3cdbbe1a5469>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: JER 49:8
Text: Flee ye, turn back, dwell deep, O inhabitants of Dedan; for I will bring the calamity of Esau upon him, the time that I will visit him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e62be676-7904-4779-bd55-16ea421a72a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: JER 49:9
Text: If grapegatherers come to thee, would they not leave some gleaning grapes? if thieves by night, they will destroy till they have enough.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8409a368-e1cf-43a7-8596-d0686c8f8092>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: JER 49:10
Text: But I have made Esau bare, I have uncovered his secret places, and he shall not be able to hide himself: his seed is spoiled, and his brethren, and his neighbours, and he is not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd95c153-75c3-4202-a101-08264970aac0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: JER 49:11
Text: Leave thy fatherless children, I will preserve them alive; and let thy widows trust in me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15005f05-069d-47f0-ac85-b03e793d1392>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: JER 49:12
Text: For thus saith the LORD; Behold, they whose judgment was not to drink of the cup have assuredly drunken; and art thou he that shall altogether go unpunished? thou shalt not go unpunished, but thou shalt surely drink of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:efd87e5d-7c63-47bf-8f85-3f44eab79fa3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: JER 49:13
Text: For I have sworn by myself, saith the LORD, that Bozrah shall become a desolation, a reproach, a waste, and a curse; and all the cities thereof shall be perpetual wastes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f30d92a-2e08-476f-addd-1cc887fe5536>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JER 49:14
Text: I have heard a rumour from the LORD, and an ambassador is sent unto the heathen, saying, Gather ye together, and come against her, and rise up to the battle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53ccf023-45db-44d7-93b0-63df71c25d78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: JER 49:15
Text: For, lo, I will make thee small among the heathen, and despised among men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06a0e8c6-b80a-419f-b803-d2f170fe106d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 289

Reference: JER 49:16
Text: Thy terribleness hath deceived thee, and the pride of thine heart, O thou that dwellest in the clefts of the rock, that holdest the height of the hill: though thou shouldest make thy nest as high as the eagle, I will bring thee down from thence, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:937326af-52a7-4ec0-95be-157ebb7f5d29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: JER 49:17
Text: Also Edom shall be a desolation: every one that goeth by it shall be astonished, and shall hiss at all the plagues thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a66c9ae9-a3a2-46c9-b161-3507afe222c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JER 49:18
Text: As in the overthrow of Sodom and Gomorrah and the neighbour cities thereof, saith the LORD, no man shall abide there, neither shall a son of man dwell in it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc12da9c-9fee-4050-9f9c-1fa31da2485d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 338

Reference: JER 49:19
Text: Behold, he shall come up like a lion from the swelling of Jordan against the habitation of the strong: but I will suddenly make him run away from her: and who is a chosen man, that I may appoint over her? for who is like me? and who will appoint me the time? and who is that shepherd that will stand before me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abf6ec33-48a6-42f8-8e9f-c2127d135a61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: JER 49:20
Text: Therefore hear the counsel of the LORD, that he hath taken against Edom; and his purposes, that he hath purposed against the inhabitants of Teman: Surely the least of the flock shall draw them out: surely he shall make their habitations desolate with them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:470de1e9-8a76-4bbe-8554-7a693020d620>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: JER 49:21
Text: The earth is moved at the noise of their fall, at the cry the noise thereof was heard in the Red sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7858ec53-e712-40de-aab0-884dce151843>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: JER 49:22
Text: Behold, he shall come up and fly as the eagle, and spread his wings over Bozrah: and at that day shall the heart of the mighty men of Edom be as the heart of a woman in her pangs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6241b05c-2139-4ef8-ad50-fb9094982b8e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: JER 49:23
Text: Concerning Damascus. Hamath is confounded, and Arpad: for they have heard evil tidings: they are fainthearted; there is sorrow on the sea; it cannot be quiet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45f2c6c7-b03f-4d3c-84a6-941954fad49c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: JER 49:24
Text: Damascus is waxed feeble, and turneth herself to flee, and fear hath seized on her: anguish and sorrows have taken her, as a woman in travail.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5f0bfbc-37c2-4da6-b54c-f4ff9e556a8e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: JER 49:25
Text: How is the city of praise not left, the city of my joy!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df7eaebe-8a13-4271-9ea4-75835aced982>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: JER 49:26
Text: Therefore her young men shall fall in her streets, and all the men of war shall be cut off in that day, saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f40519a-3196-4672-b0ce-ca8284a72d70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: JER 49:27
Text: And I will kindle a fire in the wall of Damascus, and it shall consume the palaces of Benhadad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:783b0f26-eb4c-4f0c-9621-850057088b04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: JER 49:28
Text: Concerning Kedar, and concerning the kingdoms of Hazor, which Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon shall smite, thus saith the LORD; Arise ye, go up to Kedar, and spoil the men of the east.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b30370f4-8f17-4db3-9f2f-8b86e5354ac1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: JER 49:29
Text: Their tents and their flocks shall they take away: they shall take to themselves their curtains, and all their vessels, and their camels; and they shall cry unto them, Fear is on every side.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17dab076-a70c-42b3-bbe6-45266d2e72c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: JER 49:30
Text: Flee, get you far off, dwell deep, O ye inhabitants of Hazor, saith the LORD; for Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon hath taken counsel against you, and hath conceived a purpose against you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7b1030d-a5d0-43d0-8220-37e7fe7c97c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: JER 49:31
Text: Arise, get you up unto the wealthy nation, that dwelleth without care, saith the LORD, which have neither gates nor bars, which dwell alone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de8981c9-87ff-4f87-a388-85a7f8d40f65>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: JER 49:32
Text: And their camels shall be a booty, and the multitude of their cattle a spoil: and I will scatter into all winds them that are in the utmost corners; and I will bring their calamity from all sides thereof, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da6b3a8a-3451-4a47-8764-d680f448a79a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: JER 49:33
Text: And Hazor shall be a dwelling for dragons, and a desolation for ever: there shall no man abide there, nor any son of man dwell in it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c975b347-c889-4b64-ab1f-02d1a3dfb325>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: JER 49:34
Text: The word of the LORD that came to Jeremiah the prophet against Elam in the beginning of the reign of Zedekiah king of Judah, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2aa1c015-948b-4154-b401-2c01b152d330>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: JER 49:35
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Behold, I will break the bow of Elam, the chief of their might.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1f8c50c-d13e-45a0-adb9-9bc917902a08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: JER 49:36
Text: And upon Elam will I bring the four winds from the four quarters of heaven, and will scatter them toward all those winds; and there shall be no nation whither the outcasts of Elam shall not come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52815165-c0b4-497d-a577-93aaf8efee1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: JER 49:37
Text: For I will cause Elam to be dismayed before their enemies, and before them that seek their life: and I will bring evil upon them, even my fierce anger, saith the LORD; and I will send the sword after them, till I have consumed them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f05f2196-cb04-496d-b315-8f8ce3c7431e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: JER 49:38
Text: And I will set my throne in Elam, and will destroy from thence the king and the princes, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/49/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbc13a78-f425-4480-84da-7261e9378fb7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: JER 49:39
Text: But it shall come to pass in the latter days, that I will bring again the captivity of Elam, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42077461-69b6-4094-800b-e1c5bc7db5e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: JER 50:1
Text: The word that the LORD spake against Babylon and against the land of the Chaldeans by Jeremiah the prophet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50d363a4-511a-44cb-8d89-f1d4e578fc91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: JER 50:2
Text: Declare ye among the nations, and publish, and set up a standard; publish, and conceal not: say, Babylon is taken, Bel is confounded, Merodach is broken in pieces; her idols are confounded, her images are broken in pieces.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c3e6012-7bc5-4a37-95f1-7ef87e41f634>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: JER 50:3
Text: For out of the north there cometh up a nation against her, which shall make her land desolate, and none shall dwell therein: they shall remove, they shall depart, both man and beast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0794f148-82bf-4a0b-944e-9ba603cde380>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: JER 50:4
Text: In those days, and in that time, saith the LORD, the children of Israel shall come, they and the children of Judah together, going and weeping: they shall go, and seek the LORD their God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b4104b8-80a9-4525-9e4c-01bed7b5d606>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: JER 50:5
Text: They shall ask the way to Zion with their faces thitherward, saying, Come, and let us join ourselves to the LORD in a perpetual covenant that shall not be forgotten.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5aea588c-2dbd-4443-8727-fbd7ca5bf38e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: JER 50:6
Text: My people hath been lost sheep: their shepherds have caused them to go astray, they have turned them away on the mountains: they have gone from mountain to hill, they have forgotten their restingplace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48ae1216-d353-4959-aaa4-1f25f7259305>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: JER 50:7
Text: All that found them have devoured them: and their adversaries said, We offend not, because they have sinned against the LORD, the habitation of justice, even the LORD, the hope of their fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae6e4e5d-3e91-4744-9227-1048956e41c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: JER 50:8
Text: Remove out of the midst of Babylon, and go forth out of the land of the Chaldeans, and be as the he goats before the flocks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bff40587-bbdc-4b86-92ef-c08ce248b6a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 298

Reference: JER 50:9
Text: For, lo, I will raise and cause to come up against Babylon an assembly of great nations from the north country: and they shall set themselves in array against her; from thence she shall be taken: their arrows shall be as of a mighty expert man; none shall return in vain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d5b331c-d211-4cd7-9c12-031953d4914c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: JER 50:10
Text: And Chaldea shall be a spoil: all that spoil her shall be satisfied, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:469d7f16-d84c-4a29-9fb1-1af13e09d081>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: JER 50:11
Text: Because ye were glad, because ye rejoiced, O ye destroyers of mine heritage, because ye are grown fat as the heifer at grass, and bellow as bulls;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0971d3f-ed44-4765-88b8-da59c3167dc7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: JER 50:12
Text: Your mother shall be sore confounded; she that bare you shall be ashamed: behold, the hindermost of the nations shall be a wilderness, a dry land, and a desert.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5a366b5-32b6-4ba1-8835-c3881d5f898c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: JER 50:13
Text: Because of the wrath of the LORD it shall not be inhabited, but it shall be wholly desolate: every one that goeth by Babylon shall be astonished, and hiss at all her plagues.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5661eb00-2bef-4fae-b397-77ff589ff85a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: JER 50:14
Text: Put yourselves in array against Babylon round about: all ye that bend the bow, shoot at her, spare no arrows: for she hath sinned against the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9d04591-5935-4259-b9c8-0f7bb5a0fe80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: JER 50:15
Text: Shout against her round about: she hath given her hand: her foundations are fallen, her walls are thrown down: for it is the vengeance of the LORD: take vengeance upon her; as she hath done, do unto her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d551209e-120d-4e00-8096-8598bd7f0ee2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: JER 50:16
Text: Cut off the sower from Babylon, and him that handleth the sickle in the time of harvest: for fear of the oppressing sword they shall turn every one to his people, and they shall flee every one to his own land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4642c91d-99b9-4bcf-9f97-9984d84ce203>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: JER 50:17
Text: Israel is a scattered sheep; the lions have driven him away: first the king of Assyria hath devoured him; and last this Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon hath broken his bones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c923decd-ee7d-4a54-a3c6-e88a629d4043>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JER 50:18
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; Behold, I will punish the king of Babylon and his land, as I have punished the king of Assyria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff617dd9-7376-46fc-a97f-249f19006036>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: JER 50:19
Text: And I will bring Israel again to his habitation, and he shall feed on Carmel and Bashan, and his soul shall be satisfied upon mount Ephraim and Gilead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16d3fd4d-8b84-4b66-bbbe-99b6646df43a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: JER 50:20
Text: In those days, and in that time, saith the LORD, the iniquity of Israel shall be sought for, and there shall be none; and the sins of Judah, and they shall not be found: for I will pardon them whom I reserve.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d988dde3-81ed-415a-8c1e-c9b7f7788034>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: JER 50:21
Text: Go up against the land of Merathaim, even against it, and against the inhabitants of Pekod: waste and utterly destroy after them, saith the LORD, and do according to all that I have commanded thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1bf1e9b1-c092-4fc0-a97c-c5abca232ec4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: JER 50:22
Text: A sound of battle is in the land, and of great destruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31a6c5cb-00f9-4673-ac40-2b4a4a8d8a7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: JER 50:23
Text: How is the hammer of the whole earth cut asunder and broken! how is Babylon become a desolation among the nations!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9576c50-4ade-42cf-9e8a-14af436ddc91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: JER 50:24
Text: I have laid a snare for thee, and thou art also taken, O Babylon, and thou wast not aware: thou art found, and also caught, because thou hast striven against the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:483529c1-0990-4948-b442-c54031475647>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: JER 50:25
Text: The LORD hath opened his armoury, and hath brought forth the weapons of his indignation: for this is the work of the Lord GOD of hosts in the land of the Chaldeans.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:528c76ef-7341-45f3-ae5a-8d9fff32a8d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: JER 50:26
Text: Come against her from the utmost border, open her storehouses: cast her up as heaps, and destroy her utterly: let nothing of her be left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c47511f-e08d-4858-a1eb-bf62c55f631f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: JER 50:27
Text: Slay all her bullocks; let them go down to the slaughter: woe unto them! for their day is come, the time of their visitation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31195fbb-d0e9-49f1-994f-85cf2e7874a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: JER 50:28
Text: The voice of them that flee and escape out of the land of Babylon, to declare in Zion the vengeance of the LORD our God, the vengeance of his temple.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a8a34ab-c88c-4855-b09a-8d0383905866>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 312

Reference: JER 50:29
Text: Call together the archers against Babylon: all ye that bend the bow, camp against it round about; let none thereof escape: recompense her according to her work; according to all that she hath done, do unto her: for she hath been proud against the LORD, against the Holy One of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62d9b7a9-2ac3-4328-86f2-7b752265c62d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: JER 50:30
Text: Therefore shall her young men fall in the streets, and all her men of war shall be cut off in that day, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:159902ae-0bc9-455e-91c7-706906057d86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: JER 50:31
Text: Behold, I am against thee, O thou most proud, saith the Lord GOD of hosts: for thy day is come, the time that I will visit thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e29f4ad-2ad3-44ec-b799-6accc801eebb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: JER 50:32
Text: And the most proud shall stumble and fall, and none shall raise him up: and I will kindle a fire in his cities, and it shall devour all round about him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e4facb8-7121-42e1-a935-b3e4a4770beb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: JER 50:33
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts; The children of Israel and the children of Judah were oppressed together: and all that took them captives held them fast; they refused to let them go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd4bc331-0125-4fe2-be25-e2e9b9bcbf9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: JER 50:34
Text: Their Redeemer is strong; the LORD of hosts is his name: he shall throughly plead their cause, that he may give rest to the land, and disquiet the inhabitants of Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a1c8018-9d10-4b4c-a8b2-48d6a12f666e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: JER 50:35
Text: A sword is upon the Chaldeans, saith the LORD, and upon the inhabitants of Babylon, and upon her princes, and upon her wise men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24721f74-78c7-4897-b57a-9410fe385ab1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: JER 50:36
Text: A sword is upon the liars; and they shall dote: a sword is upon her mighty men; and they shall be dismayed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb261928-4f35-41b9-8b2e-5cc54f57f3d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: JER 50:37
Text: A sword is upon their horses, and upon their chariots, and upon all the mingled people that are in the midst of her; and they shall become as women: a sword is upon her treasures; and they shall be robbed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27d97aa1-0ae0-4194-9849-a57d879b4c5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: JER 50:38
Text: A drought is upon her waters; and they shall be dried up: for it is the land of graven images, and they are mad upon their idols.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fdc47c8-9fe7-487b-9bd9-c0af5a79ec20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: JER 50:39
Text: Therefore the wild beasts of the desert with the wild beasts of the islands shall dwell there, and the owls shall dwell therein: and it shall be no more inhabited for ever; neither shall it be dwelt in from generation to generation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:054d7ae4-d41f-4be0-9db6-a69d058ec739>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: JER 50:40
Text: As God overthrew Sodom and Gomorrah and the neighbour cities thereof, saith the LORD; so shall no man abide there, neither shall any son of man dwell therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db934e96-391f-4ed5-862a-ef16681c45dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: JER 50:41
Text: Behold, a people shall come from the north, and a great nation, and many kings shall be raised up from the coasts of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a61cd535-dd76-4949-82b5-26d882fd07f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: JER 50:42
Text: They shall hold the bow and the lance: they are cruel, and will not shew mercy: their voice shall roar like the sea, and they shall ride upon horses, every one put in array, like a man to the battle, against thee, O daughter of Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7064a498-0e7c-4d91-a667-5c0bad2d0cfe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: JER 50:43
Text: The king of Babylon hath heard the report of them, and his hands waxed feeble: anguish took hold of him, and pangs as of a woman in travail.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f7eb61a-0068-4b8f-937b-e0fbc29b8336>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 336

Reference: JER 50:44
Text: Behold, he shall come up like a lion from the swelling of Jordan unto the habitation of the strong: but I will make them suddenly run away from her: and who is a chosen man, that I may appoint over her? for who is like me? and who will appoint me the time? and who is that shepherd that will stand before me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fcd114f0-1ce8-441c-9a5b-e4f1c1d17c6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 290

Reference: JER 50:45
Text: Therefore hear ye the counsel of the LORD, that he hath taken against Babylon; and his purposes, that he hath purposed against the land of the Chaldeans: Surely the least of the flock shall draw them out: surely he shall make their habitation desolate with them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/50/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61cf89c1-7fd0-4014-91f4-ead1e8769467>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: JER 50:46
Text: At the noise of the taking of Babylon the earth is moved, and the cry is heard among the nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f749a717-9727-4854-b3e3-5a08fce86386>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: JER 51:1
Text: Thus saith the LORD; Behold, I will raise up against Babylon, and against them that dwell in the midst of them that rise up against me, a destroying wind;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6101f91-16b3-4081-bbaf-365f6b22ee69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: JER 51:2
Text: And will send unto Babylon fanners, that shall fan her, and shall empty her land: for in the day of trouble they shall be against her round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1bf933c-8136-48f7-92ef-d381d10bf1c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: JER 51:3
Text: Against him that bendeth let the archer bend his bow, and against him that lifteth himself up in his brigandine: and spare ye not her young men; destroy ye utterly all her host.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb1f5385-01a9-4ba1-913f-c9da7e6b9472>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: JER 51:4
Text: Thus the slain shall fall in the land of the Chaldeans, and they that are thrust through in her streets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee20e1cd-a311-4824-b5b5-1349b49dac47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: JER 51:5
Text: For Israel hath not been forsaken, nor Judah of his God, of the LORD of hosts; though their land was filled with sin against the Holy One of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:820becdb-230b-4ca9-ae92-7ab16208ed3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: JER 51:6
Text: Flee out of the midst of Babylon, and deliver every man his soul: be not cut off in her iniquity; for this is the time of the LORD’s vengeance; he will render unto her a recompence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4c95918-ac3b-40f2-b6ed-d75133f8a230>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: JER 51:7
Text: Babylon hath been a golden cup in the LORD’s hand, that made all the earth drunken: the nations have drunken of her wine; therefore the nations are mad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:419c4b01-9872-4cd9-a3fb-7e380ce51b7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: JER 51:8
Text: Babylon is suddenly fallen and destroyed: howl for her; take balm for her pain, if so be she may be healed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:945dde51-1b63-4d2e-ac56-652b97ff500a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: JER 51:9
Text: We would have healed Babylon, but she is not healed: forsake her, and let us go every one into his own country: for her judgment reacheth unto heaven, and is lifted up even to the skies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:880857ff-9a73-4c58-821a-726497533ab3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: JER 51:10
Text: The LORD hath brought forth our righteousness: come, and let us declare in Zion the work of the LORD our God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc31a8ef-a078-4b9c-a077-5044fc27e1ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: JER 51:11
Text: Make bright the arrows; gather the shields: the LORD hath raised up the spirit of the kings of the Medes: for his device is against Babylon, to destroy it; because it is the vengeance of the LORD, the vengeance of his temple.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2be6a0f8-c812-4710-b90d-7a6307ab0128>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: JER 51:12
Text: Set up the standard upon the walls of Babylon, make the watch strong, set up the watchmen, prepare the ambushes: for the LORD hath both devised and done that which he spake against the inhabitants of Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40fa7b21-9fc9-4f35-b175-7d3d41b3de1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: JER 51:13
Text: O thou that dwellest upon many waters, abundant in treasures, thine end is come, and the measure of thy covetousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d974f273-00b9-455e-8f90-6585a68aa727>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: JER 51:14
Text: The LORD of hosts hath sworn by himself, saying, Surely I will fill thee with men, as with caterpillers; and they shall lift up a shout against thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9190e64d-a2f5-4288-b4cd-9a9b1ea446a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: JER 51:15
Text: He hath made the earth by his power, he hath established the world by his wisdom, and hath stretched out the heaven by his understanding.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c303d20-43d6-4100-98e0-91cc2b0a19a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: JER 51:16
Text: When he uttereth his voice, there is a multitude of waters in the heavens; and he causeth the vapours to ascend from the ends of the earth: he maketh lightnings with rain, and bringeth forth the wind out of his treasures.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d85d218-b8e2-4ebb-8425-166567bd795d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JER 51:17
Text: Every man is brutish by his knowledge; every founder is confounded by the graven image: for his molten image is falsehood, and there is no breath in them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:579da2d7-72b3-4f79-9ab7-3cf43ebd30fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: JER 51:18
Text: They are vanity, the work of errors: in the time of their visitation they shall perish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de112c85-095d-4d45-8b79-a23e4c87aa61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: JER 51:19
Text: The portion of Jacob is not like them; for he is the former of all things: and Israel is the rod of his inheritance: the LORD of hosts is his name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51ae827a-28dd-4339-bd15-b81982a30741>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: JER 51:20
Text: Thou art my battle axe and weapons of war: for with thee will I break in pieces the nations, and with thee will I destroy kingdoms;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:287b23ee-1c8a-4361-ae52-ce33feb4b2ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: JER 51:21
Text: And with thee will I break in pieces the horse and his rider; and with thee will I break in pieces the chariot and his rider;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac9bddae-e01e-443c-983f-521e0a903076>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: JER 51:22
Text: With thee also will I break in pieces man and woman; and with thee will I break in pieces old and young; and with thee will I break in pieces the young man and the maid;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00c3c736-afd5-4a06-a04c-bdc974290e03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: JER 51:23
Text: I will also break in pieces with thee the shepherd and his flock; and with thee will I break in pieces the husbandman and his yoke of oxen; and with thee will I break in pieces captains and rulers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9b07a6d-c3ab-4d58-b791-5d1da2f2183d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: JER 51:24
Text: And I will render unto Babylon and to all the inhabitants of Chaldea all their evil that they have done in Zion in your sight, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58e8c986-9371-453d-bb0f-d4fd310ccdb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: JER 51:25
Text: Behold, I am against thee, O destroying mountain, saith the LORD, which destroyest all the earth: and I will stretch out mine hand upon thee, and roll thee down from the rocks, and will make thee a burnt mountain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ec57c53-80a5-4fdd-96dd-2b92e51ee2b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: JER 51:26
Text: And they shall not take of thee a stone for a corner, nor a stone for foundations; but thou shalt be desolate for ever, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81c8cda9-722d-4696-8392-5a0a45dcd3e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 288

Reference: JER 51:27
Text: Set ye up a standard in the land, blow the trumpet among the nations, prepare the nations against her, call together against her the kingdoms of Ararat, Minni, and Ashchenaz; appoint a captain against her; cause the horses to come up as the rough caterpillers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:efec3329-45f0-49fe-82d4-5ac7fcbabe23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: JER 51:28
Text: Prepare against her the nations with the kings of the Medes, the captains thereof, and all the rulers thereof, and all the land of his dominion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8fb1ebe-fa14-437e-ae7d-ece9d36a3be5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: JER 51:29
Text: And the land shall tremble and sorrow: for every purpose of the LORD shall be performed against Babylon, to make the land of Babylon a desolation without an inhabitant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7eb73aa-606d-44e7-bccf-3e565d7de636>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: JER 51:30
Text: The mighty men of Babylon have forborn to fight, they have remained in their holds: their might hath failed; they became as women: they have burned her dwellingplaces; her bars are broken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:652bf21e-3050-4db5-ad2b-e4981522cdba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: JER 51:31
Text: One post shall run to meet another, and one messenger to meet another, to shew the king of Babylon that his city is taken at one end,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6d3f8b4-e007-4730-a225-ab3dd1158809>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: JER 51:32
Text: And that the passages are stopped, and the reeds they have burned with fire, and the men of war are affrighted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:557f55cd-206f-4c6e-ad24-779dc9147d83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: JER 51:33
Text: For thus saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel; The daughter of Babylon is like a threshingfloor, it is time to thresh her: yet a little while, and the time of her harvest shall come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3a2f94a-5b9e-4b6f-a7a0-0ece1cde7c7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: JER 51:34
Text: Nebuchadrezzar the king of Babylon hath devoured me, he hath crushed me, he hath made me an empty vessel, he hath swallowed me up like a dragon, he hath filled his belly with my delicates, he hath cast me out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d6db9d5-7626-451c-825a-eaa917eedd14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JER 51:35
Text: The violence done to me and to my flesh be upon Babylon, shall the inhabitant of Zion say; and my blood upon the inhabitants of Chaldea, shall Jerusalem say.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2abbea0-6738-414d-9b04-8276eb6ec06b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: JER 51:36
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD; Behold, I will plead thy cause, and take vengeance for thee; and I will dry up her sea, and make her springs dry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36caac8e-9e12-4738-93ed-163b13a2037a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: JER 51:37
Text: And Babylon shall become heaps, a dwellingplace for dragons, an astonishment, and an hissing, without an inhabitant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1eddbb6-d60f-442c-bfa9-7e55862cedf9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: JER 51:38
Text: They shall roar together like lions: they shall yell as lions’ whelps.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acce79ad-0534-45eb-9541-aca076560608>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: JER 51:39
Text: In their heat I will make their feasts, and I will make them drunken, that they may rejoice, and sleep a perpetual sleep, and not wake, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a506ce9a-3879-4740-9267-98868c52f36a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: JER 51:40
Text: I will bring them down like lambs to the slaughter, like rams with he goats.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78e0f294-67ff-426e-87ce-46132c47cc7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: JER 51:41
Text: How is Sheshach taken! and how is the praise of the whole earth surprised! how is Babylon become an astonishment among the nations!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71317537-1f3b-4f9e-8838-bfcfba648e3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: JER 51:42
Text: The sea is come up upon Babylon: she is covered with the multitude of the waves thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d97a29b-4b25-49bf-b69f-b0d5df76d50c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: JER 51:43
Text: Her cities are a desolation, a dry land, and a wilderness, a land wherein no man dwelleth, neither doth any son of man pass thereby.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc176285-7ec3-47c5-b932-2a0443d8a2f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: JER 51:44
Text: And I will punish Bel in Babylon, and I will bring forth out of his mouth that which he hath swallowed up: and the nations shall not flow together any more unto him: yea, the wall of Babylon shall fall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2eef775-ed2f-4ce4-88bb-538932925b76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: JER 51:45
Text: My people, go ye out of the midst of her, and deliver ye every man his soul from the fierce anger of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dace28fc-e2f6-4f35-a327-3e9ebbd418ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: JER 51:46
Text: And lest your heart faint, and ye fear for the rumour that shall be heard in the land; a rumour shall both come one year, and after that in another year shall come a rumour, and violence in the land, ruler against ruler.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc0119d4-292e-472a-ac75-0c4e96c20bf1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: JER 51:47
Text: Therefore, behold, the days come, that I will do judgment upon the graven images of Babylon: and her whole land shall be confounded, and all her slain shall fall in the midst of her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df1711ca-dd03-47dc-b513-17c295531d9f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: JER 51:48
Text: Then the heaven and the earth, and all that is therein, shall sing for Babylon: for the spoilers shall come unto her from the north, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40d47030-ce70-43b5-bcb1-bee42b9f6c9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: JER 51:49
Text: As Babylon hath caused the slain of Israel to fall, so at Babylon shall fall the slain of all the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:951274e8-ce19-4fa9-acbf-d4e967e10bae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: JER 51:50
Text: Ye that have escaped the sword, go away, stand not still: remember the LORD afar off, and let Jerusalem come into your mind.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b380be1-70ef-4f70-bd83-aff03d6c4eaf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: JER 51:51
Text: We are confounded, because we have heard reproach: shame hath covered our faces: for strangers are come into the sanctuaries of the LORD’s house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0241ed2d-a85a-428a-adc9-0c12a97bd990>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: JER 51:52
Text: Wherefore, behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that I will do judgment upon her graven images: and through all her land the wounded shall groan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5506dd9-ebc7-4dbc-aa0e-86810a7b3f45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JER 51:53
Text: Though Babylon should mount up to heaven, and though she should fortify the height of her strength, yet from me shall spoilers come unto her, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5735a2a-872d-46fb-8560-204956e296bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: JER 51:54
Text: A sound of a cry cometh from Babylon, and great destruction from the land of the Chaldeans:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/55
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c783237-a084-4468-bd4d-c0b875d7a57b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JER 51:55
Text: Because the LORD hath spoiled Babylon, and destroyed out of her the great voice; when her waves do roar like great waters, a noise of their voice is uttered:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/56
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8305581e-b7af-4057-a87c-9e72a1fcbf70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: JER 51:56
Text: Because the spoiler is come upon her, even upon Babylon, and her mighty men are taken, every one of their bows is broken: for the LORD God of recompences shall surely requite.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/57
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99fabe9e-d62d-46f9-b7cc-740b172371b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: JER 51:57
Text: And I will make drunk her princes, and her wise men, her captains, and her rulers, and her mighty men: and they shall sleep a perpetual sleep, and not wake, saith the King, whose name is the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/58
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14daa7a0-bbe3-4a43-a8c3-079b7292f826>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: JER 51:58
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts; The broad walls of Babylon shall be utterly broken, and her high gates shall be burned with fire; and the people shall labour in vain, and the folk in the fire, and they shall be weary.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/59
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d33f0a3-5294-4b48-a27e-841a3398c39e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: JER 51:59
Text: The word which Jeremiah the prophet commanded Seraiah the son of Neriah, the son of Maaseiah, when he went with Zedekiah the king of Judah into Babylon in the fourth year of his reign. And this Seraiah was a quiet prince.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/60
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76aa007c-a546-4751-baa4-b0cb7e46570d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: JER 51:60
Text: So Jeremiah wrote in a book all the evil that should come upon Babylon, even all these words that are written against Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/61
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92a021b5-3ce9-46f0-bbd6-b3d322784e2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: JER 51:61
Text: And Jeremiah said to Seraiah, When thou comest to Babylon, and shalt see, and shalt read all these words;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/62
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d954f9c7-afdd-4526-8edf-4a4aeea348a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: JER 51:62
Text: Then shalt thou say, O LORD, thou hast spoken against this place, to cut it off, that none shall remain in it, neither man nor beast, but that it shall be desolate for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/63
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b1167d0-230b-4108-98ea-2a7c5dfe86b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: JER 51:63
Text: And it shall be, when thou hast made an end of reading this book, that thou shalt bind a stone to it, and cast it into the midst of Euphrates:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/51/64
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9cb5bf43-99ea-4397-9bfb-da8685ca358c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: JER 51:64
Text: And thou shalt say, Thus shall Babylon sink, and shall not rise from the evil that I will bring upon her: and they shall be weary. Thus far are the words of Jeremiah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:706d48a5-f5c0-4668-80f9-30c23afd9969>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: JER 52:1
Text: Zedekiah was one and twenty years old when he began to reign, and he reigned eleven years in Jerusalem. And his mother’s name was Hamutal the daughter of Jeremiah of Libnah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:495db96b-83cf-427d-bbce-cf0ffa951308>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: JER 52:2
Text: And he did that which was evil in the eyes of the LORD, according to all that Jehoiakim had done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:854ffe6d-5c0b-4da0-8e8f-bbd48bd6bff3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: JER 52:3
Text: For through the anger of the LORD it came to pass in Jerusalem and Judah, till he had cast them out from his presence, that Zedekiah rebelled against the king of Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bec1aaee-c880-4843-ac08-fa6a9ba98ef3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: JER 52:4
Text: And it came to pass in the ninth year of his reign, in the tenth month, in the tenth day of the month, that Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon came, he and all his army, against Jerusalem, and pitched against it, and built forts against it round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4531d691-5274-460c-944f-49db66191404>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: JER 52:5
Text: So the city was besieged unto the eleventh year of king Zedekiah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66cf0362-839b-4d3d-b9d4-0c3296043155>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: JER 52:6
Text: And in the fourth month, in the ninth day of the month, the famine was sore in the city, so that there was no bread for the people of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60b8d8be-72a4-4650-ade1-5499c48865ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 293

Reference: JER 52:7
Text: Then the city was broken up, and all the men of war fled, and went forth out of the city by night by the way of the gate between the two walls, which was by the king’s garden; (now the Chaldeans were by the city round about:) and they went by the way of the plain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f39e813a-70b6-43ee-8e9b-90161825540f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: JER 52:8
Text: But the army of the Chaldeans pursued after the king, and overtook Zedekiah in the plains of Jericho; and all his army was scattered from him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a5683cb-e8fd-46b7-a407-a54f762be73f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: JER 52:9
Text: Then they took the king, and carried him up unto the king of Babylon to Riblah in the land of Hamath; where he gave judgment upon him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29412e9d-0cb3-423b-9840-9d475b2085a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: JER 52:10
Text: And the king of Babylon slew the sons of Zedekiah before his eyes: he slew also all the princes of Judah in Riblah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2096fd26-644d-495b-8d62-4327689e046f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: JER 52:11
Text: Then he put out the eyes of Zedekiah; and the king of Babylon bound him in chains, and carried him to Babylon, and put him in prison till the day of his death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2584128c-ed43-4f0f-896f-cb95ee30046b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: JER 52:12
Text: Now in the fifth month, in the tenth day of the month, which was the nineteenth year of Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon, came Nebuzaradan, captain of the guard, which served the king of Babylon, into Jerusalem,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd6e15d0-e5b6-41fc-82ab-a20b5a3b4392>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: JER 52:13
Text: And burned the house of the LORD, and the king’s house; and all the houses of Jerusalem, and all the houses of the great men, burned he with fire:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fd84706-285c-412d-a778-dae0066cd3a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: JER 52:14
Text: And all the army of the Chaldeans, that were with the captain of the guard, brake down all the walls of Jerusalem round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:530135f9-7f32-4e30-b0c3-08930c3c0e72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 273

Reference: JER 52:15
Text: Then Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard carried away captive certain of the poor of the people, and the residue of the people that remained in the city, and those that fell away, that fell to the king of Babylon, and the rest of the multitude.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edefc865-4582-4ec6-8aad-65c1021e4cf5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: JER 52:16
Text: But Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard left certain of the poor of the land for vinedressers and for husbandmen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8bdbccc7-2767-4027-9492-830ae1940967>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: JER 52:17
Text: Also the pillars of brass that were in the house of the LORD, and the bases, and the brasen sea that was in the house of the LORD, the Chaldeans brake, and carried all the brass of them to Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c344b62d-4126-4083-a102-12b50c74ae11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: JER 52:18
Text: The caldrons also, and the shovels, and the snuffers, and the bowls, and the spoons, and all the vessels of brass wherewith they ministered, took they away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df0a0da2-0d55-4eb2-8ebb-d8a4a363746e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: JER 52:19
Text: And the basons, and the firepans, and the bowls, and the caldrons, and the candlesticks, and the spoons, and the cups; that which was of gold in gold, and that which was of silver in silver, took the captain of the guard away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10fbc422-c4a1-4481-88c9-ca5009b62058>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: JER 52:20
Text: The two pillars, one sea, and twelve brasen bulls that were under the bases, which king Solomon had made in the house of the LORD: the brass of all these vessels was without weight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f757faf7-12d1-495f-b776-185977ddf0e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: JER 52:21
Text: And concerning the pillars, the height of one pillar was eighteen cubits; and a fillet of twelve cubits did compass it; and the thickness thereof was four fingers: it was hollow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e9e5f4c-8ab2-4529-9457-66faf1b9d27d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: JER 52:22
Text: And a chapiter of brass was upon it; and the height of one chapiter was five cubits, with network and pomegranates upon the chapiters round about, all of brass. The second pillar also and the pomegranates were like unto these.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6325113c-c697-45d4-a444-be647ab5382e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: JER 52:23
Text: And there were ninety and six pomegranates on a side; and all the pomegranates upon the network were an hundred round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d539b438-6aff-456a-a126-fa04b0102dfb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: JER 52:24
Text: And the captain of the guard took Seraiah the chief priest, and Zephaniah the second priest, and the three keepers of the door:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff7b8f2c-df2b-4bae-9760-d79c76a97023>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 358

Reference: JER 52:25
Text: He took also out of the city an eunuch, which had the charge of the men of war; and seven men of them that were near the king’s person, which were found in the city; and the principal scribe of the host, who mustered the people of the land; and threescore men of the people of the land, that were found in the midst of the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1abd2665-8447-4a0e-ac15-777a8776edc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: JER 52:26
Text: So Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard took them, and brought them to the king of Babylon to Riblah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2ccb064-af98-41a9-83db-d3a0d8b1a190>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: JER 52:27
Text: And the king of Babylon smote them, and put them to death in Riblah in the land of Hamath. Thus Judah was carried away captive out of his own land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d45df8d-4c62-4708-9284-9d849b9c456d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: JER 52:28
Text: This is the people whom Nebuchadrezzar carried away captive: in the seventh year three thousand Jews and three and twenty:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:736493c2-f282-4247-be22-d4ecad617209>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: JER 52:29
Text: In the eighteenth year of Nebuchadrezzar he carried away captive from Jerusalem eight hundred thirty and two persons:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9eb592c-13a0-41b0-9680-3890fefbee6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: JER 52:30
Text: In the three and twentieth year of Nebuchadrezzar Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard carried away captive of the Jews seven hundred forty and five persons: all the persons were four thousand and six hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1f4294d-c581-4c37-925f-be6bcc7307bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 341

Reference: JER 52:31
Text: And it came to pass in the seven and thirtieth year of the captivity of Jehoiachin king of Judah, in the twelfth month, in the five and twentieth day of the month, that Evilmerodach king of Babylon in the first year of his reign lifted up the head of Jehoiachin king of Judah, and brought him forth out of prison.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:580d6300-a0f2-46ea-bc2d-8bc52cdcb9bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: JER 52:32
Text: And spake kindly unto him, and set his throne above the throne of the kings that were with him in Babylon,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1fa671f-23be-4ff9-8fe0-20334b2c759b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: JER 52:33
Text: And changed his prison garments: and he did continually eat bread before him all the days of his life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JER/52/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b02e5d39-4f7e-41ba-b532-d6853b48cd94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: JER 52:34
Text: And for his diet, there was a continual diet given him of the king of Babylon, every day a portion until the day of his death, all the days of his life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2068f2a-70f1-4d03-9f8e-f0e30ec65955>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: LAM 1:1
Text: How doth the city sit solitary, that was full of people! how is she become as a widow! she that was great among the nations, and princess among the provinces, how is she become tributary!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c60abf05-a21d-4584-96b1-6969133358b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: LAM 1:2
Text: She weepeth sore in the night, and her tears are on her cheeks: among all her lovers she hath none to comfort her: all her friends have dealt treacherously with her, they are become her enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74741b1e-b7d4-4995-b91a-7c404c88aaf2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: LAM 1:3
Text: Judah is gone into captivity because of affliction, and because of great servitude: she dwelleth among the heathen, she findeth no rest: all her persecutors overtook her between the straits.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:083ed0f7-7fad-4899-b7f5-cd091901dd49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: LAM 1:4
Text: The ways of Zion do mourn, because none come to the solemn feasts: all her gates are desolate: her priests sigh, her virgins are afflicted, and she is in bitterness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba266fac-9fcd-498b-b471-c3245e9b02ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: LAM 1:5
Text: Her adversaries are the chief, her enemies prosper; for the LORD hath afflicted her for the multitude of her transgressions: her children are gone into captivity before the enemy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8315f7f7-260c-47ef-a917-1c223979dce1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: LAM 1:6
Text: And from the daughter of Zion all her beauty is departed: her princes are become like harts that find no pasture, and they are gone without strength before the pursuer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed5af943-deec-44ab-88db-741a09012093>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 280

Reference: LAM 1:7
Text: Jerusalem remembered in the days of her affliction and of her miseries all her pleasant things that she had in the days of old, when her people fell into the hand of the enemy, and none did help her: the adversaries saw her, and did mock at her sabbaths.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df2cb97e-5ac8-4be9-b2ca-b0308b14bfe2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: LAM 1:8
Text: Jerusalem hath grievously sinned; therefore she is removed: all that honoured her despise her, because they have seen her nakedness: yea, she sigheth, and turneth backward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32f4a3cc-4948-4c87-8a78-1f810f8b509a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: LAM 1:9
Text: Her filthiness is in her skirts; she remembereth not her last end; therefore she came down wonderfully: she had no comforter. O LORD, behold my affliction: for the enemy hath magnified himself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a18d4d27-1415-4402-a8b0-61081b36c43f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: LAM 1:10
Text: The adversary hath spread out his hand upon all her pleasant things: for she hath seen that the heathen entered into her sanctuary, whom thou didst command that they should not enter into thy congregation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4becfdb6-8b0e-4884-a134-9c8d0de1a7c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: LAM 1:11
Text: All her people sigh, they seek bread; they have given their pleasant things for meat to relieve the soul: see, O LORD, and consider; for I am become vile.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1aac509e-e793-49d2-b83a-3086eb89f9ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: LAM 1:12
Text: Is it nothing to you, all ye that pass by? behold, and see if there be any sorrow like unto my sorrow, which is done unto me, wherewith the LORD hath afflicted me in the day of his fierce anger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68ae7c78-cb3b-4acb-b9e7-fb4846a0f382>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: LAM 1:13
Text: From above hath he sent fire into my bones, and it prevaileth against them: he hath spread a net for my feet, he hath turned me back: he hath made me desolate and faint all the day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:875e7933-aeca-4fb8-9995-83c44fbe3a5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: LAM 1:14
Text: The yoke of my transgressions is bound by his hand: they are wreathed, and come up upon my neck: he hath made my strength to fall, the LORD hath delivered me into their hands, from whom I am not able to rise up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30718b3c-706c-4ee4-9f0e-a2bb580ef5f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: LAM 1:15
Text: The LORD hath trodden under foot all my mighty men in the midst of me: he hath called an assembly against me to crush my young men: the LORD hath trodden the virgin, the daughter of Judah, as in a winepress.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:768b971d-da85-41a7-9984-42d1692c7b9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: LAM 1:16
Text: For these things I weep; mine eye, mine eye runneth down with water, because the comforter that should relieve my soul is far from me: my children are desolate, because the enemy prevailed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79432526-9e93-4bef-b87d-47a5711a81ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: LAM 1:17
Text: Zion spreadeth forth her hands, and there is none to comfort her: the LORD hath commanded concerning Jacob, that his adversaries should be round about him: Jerusalem is as a menstruous woman among them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f004a991-f222-4504-8103-16ea12e89a27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: LAM 1:18
Text: The LORD is righteous; for I have rebelled against his commandment: hear, I pray you, all people, and behold my sorrow: my virgins and my young men are gone into captivity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99fa4362-1daa-42d3-ac6d-ceafd979aa43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: LAM 1:19
Text: I called for my lovers, but they deceived me: my priests and mine elders gave up the ghost in the city, while they sought their meat to relieve their souls.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0dc8b8c9-d3aa-48fd-95ba-0800a08436b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: LAM 1:20
Text: Behold, O LORD; for I am in distress: my bowels are troubled; mine heart is turned within me; for I have grievously rebelled: abroad the sword bereaveth, at home there is as death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/1/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c69eeba-a7a8-4967-b882-7c74e7f6af48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: LAM 1:21
Text: They have heard that I sigh: there is none to comfort me: all mine enemies have heard of my trouble; they are glad that thou hast done it: thou wilt bring the day that thou hast called, and they shall be like unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/1/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fcb0efe6-1ad3-4491-b971-84a0cca342fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: LAM 1:22
Text: Let all their wickedness come before thee; and do unto them, as thou hast done unto me for all my transgressions: for my sighs are many, and my heart is faint.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24014b7a-8eea-43e6-a50f-a41c0285f47b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: LAM 2:1
Text: How hath the LORD covered the daughter of Zion with a cloud in his anger, and cast down from heaven unto the earth the beauty of Israel, and remembered not his footstool in the day of his anger!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df60978f-fa44-4dd7-abbf-4a70723e16cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 274

Reference: LAM 2:2
Text: The LORD hath swallowed up all the habitations of Jacob, and hath not pitied: he hath thrown down in his wrath the strong holds of the daughter of Judah; he hath brought them down to the ground: he hath polluted the kingdom and the princes thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ef14fd9-97ca-4693-916f-17f20789062c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: LAM 2:3
Text: He hath cut off in his fierce anger all the horn of Israel: he hath drawn back his right hand from before the enemy, and he burned against Jacob like a flaming fire, which devoureth round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29d7ac24-e19e-481e-8dd0-9f37438452ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: LAM 2:4
Text: He hath bent his bow like an enemy: he stood with his right hand as an adversary, and slew all that were pleasant to the eye in the tabernacle of the daughter of Zion: he poured out his fury like fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0cc8371-b750-4063-9330-3abc59548652>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: LAM 2:5
Text: The LORD was as an enemy: he hath swallowed up Israel, he hath swallowed up all her palaces: he hath destroyed his strong holds, and hath increased in the daughter of Judah mourning and lamentation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6aec3b6-d89c-4c14-806a-37ec153c90a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 299

Reference: LAM 2:6
Text: And he hath violently taken away his tabernacle, as if it were of a garden: he hath destroyed his places of the assembly: the LORD hath caused the solemn feasts and sabbaths to be forgotten in Zion, and hath despised in the indignation of his anger the king and the priest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a89ec26-db56-4274-9802-b37115d26fbb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: LAM 2:7
Text: The LORD hath cast off his altar, he hath abhorred his sanctuary, he hath given up into the hand of the enemy the walls of her palaces; they have made a noise in the house of the LORD, as in the day of a solemn feast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e759289-4349-45cd-9af6-38c697a31c8e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: LAM 2:8
Text: The LORD hath purposed to destroy the wall of the daughter of Zion: he hath stretched out a line, he hath not withdrawn his hand from destroying: therefore he made the rampart and the wall to lament; they languished together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d7b2edc-2f53-4498-9058-9aa38dec05cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: LAM 2:9
Text: Her gates are sunk into the ground; he hath destroyed and broken her bars: her king and her princes are among the Gentiles: the law is no more; her prophets also find no vision from the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3fa677e8-e565-4eb7-8f6d-76f0754a88ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: LAM 2:10
Text: The elders of the daughter of Zion sit upon the ground, and keep silence: they have cast up dust upon their heads; they have girded themselves with sackcloth: the virgins of Jerusalem hang down their heads to the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26c108da-84a7-428d-a6d7-6a0178621367>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: LAM 2:11
Text: Mine eyes do fail with tears, my bowels are troubled, my liver is poured upon the earth, for the destruction of the daughter of my people; because the children and the sucklings swoon in the streets of the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5509465b-2bea-40b2-bddd-9153f36acebf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: LAM 2:12
Text: They say to their mothers, Where is corn and wine? when they swooned as the wounded in the streets of the city, when their soul was poured out into their mothers’ bosom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3510fd6a-5ddd-4120-8808-f2edd941aac0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: LAM 2:13
Text: What thing shall I take to witness for thee? what thing shall I liken to thee, O daughter of Jerusalem? what shall I equal to thee, that I may comfort thee, O virgin daughter of Zion? for thy breach is great like the sea: who can heal thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6403d62-9daf-4fc6-a29e-2fe33a600ee9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: LAM 2:14
Text: Thy prophets have seen vain and foolish things for thee: and they have not discovered thine iniquity, to turn away thy captivity; but have seen for thee false burdens and causes of banishment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8fcf36c0-edf2-4332-bee9-9843f4af71a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: LAM 2:15
Text: All that pass by clap their hands at thee; they hiss and wag their head at the daughter of Jerusalem, saying, Is this the city that men call The perfection of beauty, The joy of the whole earth?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e2d5c11-3cbb-40a3-96dd-172717bf7973>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: LAM 2:16
Text: All thine enemies have opened their mouth against thee: they hiss and gnash the teeth: they say, We have swallowed her up: certainly this is the day that we looked for; we have found, we have seen it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1e04428-30b1-4429-aa0a-550a47b22de6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 282

Reference: LAM 2:17
Text: The LORD hath done that which he had devised; he hath fulfilled his word that he had commanded in the days of old: he hath thrown down, and hath not pitied: and he hath caused thine enemy to rejoice over thee, he hath set up the horn of thine adversaries.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ab4b5fc-5683-436e-95b0-681a7c3888fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: LAM 2:18
Text: Their heart cried unto the LORD, O wall of the daughter of Zion, let tears run down like a river day and night: give thyself no rest; let not the apple of thine eye cease.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05a53525-a915-48cf-aa03-cc28e8f475c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: LAM 2:19
Text: Arise, cry out in the night: in the beginning of the watches pour out thine heart like water before the face of the LORD: lift up thy hands toward him for the life of thy young children, that faint for hunger in the top of every street.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:caed6d6f-95c1-471e-9ba0-f093ca458845>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: LAM 2:20
Text: Behold, O LORD, and consider to whom thou hast done this. Shall the women eat their fruit, and children of a span long? shall the priest and the prophet be slain in the sanctuary of the Lord?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d884b51f-06f2-4f7e-b453-66cdbaac502f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: LAM 2:21
Text: The young and the old lie on the ground in the streets: my virgins and my young men are fallen by the sword; thou hast slain them in the day of thine anger; thou hast killed, and not pitied.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3ab2caa-5b12-48d8-9a21-24f6750ee2bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: LAM 2:22
Text: Thou hast called as in a solemn day my terrors round about, so that in the day of the LORD’s anger none escaped nor remained: those that I have swaddled and brought up hath mine enemy consumed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a65e662e-9635-4c49-abe0-7049064fa584>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: LAM 3:1
Text: I am the man that hath seen affliction by the rod of his wrath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:810c7702-70e1-44f8-bec6-11ffb77e1f95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: LAM 3:2
Text: He hath led me, and brought me into darkness, but not into light.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa69c387-9573-43a7-be8f-08507af27d6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: LAM 3:3
Text: Surely against me is he turned; he turneth his hand against me all the day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:faee6d25-6410-4ea4-9f82-57b3c93fa06d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: LAM 3:4
Text: My flesh and my skin hath he made old; he hath broken my bones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ae58510-f00e-4517-af68-b11a4a6adcc5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: LAM 3:5
Text: He hath builded against me, and compassed me with gall and travail.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:975031fd-29be-4fe9-b65c-3a1bab33ce80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: LAM 3:6
Text: He hath set me in dark places, as they that be dead of old.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54643ef9-c45e-4ccd-bb0f-797fcb039b8e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: LAM 3:7
Text: He hath hedged me about, that I cannot get out: he hath made my chain heavy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02210aef-61ae-4344-9bbd-0da170c9a167>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: LAM 3:8
Text: Also when I cry and shout, he shutteth out my prayer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c836590e-1e3c-41a9-9ef6-6e4efd1fe3c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: LAM 3:9
Text: He hath inclosed my ways with hewn stone, he hath made my paths crooked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b62bcfab-058e-4be1-b74d-b276da406183>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: LAM 3:10
Text: He was unto me as a bear lying in wait, and as a lion in secret places.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb046122-7bab-497f-9fcb-f8ee4e4fbc7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: LAM 3:11
Text: He hath turned aside my ways, and pulled me in pieces: he hath made me desolate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25a45f28-f83b-4bcd-ad57-7271c678ef34>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: LAM 3:12
Text: He hath bent his bow, and set me as a mark for the arrow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:302597c2-4f2e-4baf-9a88-9891d232a13d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: LAM 3:13
Text: He hath caused the arrows of his quiver to enter into my reins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:390f3525-9e5b-4b4a-9bba-f6e3b83691f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: LAM 3:14
Text: I was a derision to all my people; and their song all the day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce63a207-5656-4f06-9dc3-638348c94a6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: LAM 3:15
Text: He hath filled me with bitterness, he hath made me drunken with wormwood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58d4f08a-520b-442b-999d-5340925e9032>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: LAM 3:16
Text: He hath also broken my teeth with gravel stones, he hath covered me with ashes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6769ad56-1e47-494c-8e47-4b86b53cee11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: LAM 3:17
Text: And thou hast removed my soul far off from peace: I forgat prosperity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75316319-2b20-4956-884a-7cd4e5cb86c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: LAM 3:18
Text: And I said, My strength and my hope is perished from the LORD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7853a1c6-a0d2-4640-a223-30170cc4e63f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: LAM 3:19
Text: Remembering mine affliction and my misery, the wormwood and the gall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:055ea03c-f8f4-45a2-831a-202c1d7fe059>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: LAM 3:20
Text: My soul hath them still in remembrance, and is humbled in me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d2bd89f-eb0c-417b-80c4-8e266943b51e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: LAM 3:21
Text: This I recall to my mind, therefore have I hope.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:140199be-4aea-411e-b926-f343cc2e1a25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: LAM 3:22
Text: It is of the LORD’s mercies that we are not consumed, because his compassions fail not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e357e76e-0386-4a48-b03d-a4031f0eb442>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: LAM 3:23
Text: They are new every morning: great is thy faithfulness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bf1eeb9-e409-4ac8-ae5f-fde91d890f76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: LAM 3:24
Text: The LORD is my portion, saith my soul; therefore will I hope in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02047a62-18e1-4de7-8576-5a1571739404>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: LAM 3:25
Text: The LORD is good unto them that wait for him, to the soul that seeketh him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee01bfe6-15a2-48d5-a31d-cac7b9906a28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: LAM 3:26
Text: It is good that a man should both hope and quietly wait for the salvation of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bf808ad-ceb9-4ff7-8cde-7189bee833ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: LAM 3:27
Text: It is good for a man that he bear the yoke of his youth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8aa9a6be-50c0-40ba-a9e3-07818f021c10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: LAM 3:28
Text: He sitteth alone and keepeth silence, because he hath borne it upon him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54309042-d244-4164-8165-27a67f2bdd3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: LAM 3:29
Text: He putteth his mouth in the dust; if so be there may be hope.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c9f5198-425f-4d88-9ff9-31cd434fcc22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: LAM 3:30
Text: He giveth his cheek to him that smiteth him: he is filled full with reproach.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5a7960f-81c5-47a3-aa70-da365c27e97e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 67

Reference: LAM 3:31
Text: For the LORD will not cast off for ever:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0452130-5189-4ffe-b107-8b3467f6bd61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: LAM 3:32
Text: But though he cause grief, yet will he have compassion according to the multitude of his mercies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7992649-52ec-4079-95d3-a7a84d1487f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: LAM 3:33
Text: For he doth not afflict willingly nor grieve the children of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:151425f8-440f-4cd4-bdd8-a7282a73d9f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: LAM 3:34
Text: To crush under his feet all the prisoners of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94d6a893-86a9-40fa-a275-54ae4b2cd3f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: LAM 3:35
Text: To turn aside the right of a man before the face of the most High,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca9c474a-05ec-44fd-8272-d7284f6da3ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: LAM 3:36
Text: To subvert a man in his cause, the LORD approveth not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:401f01ba-5c05-47ee-96d6-958f28739d98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: LAM 3:37
Text: Who is he that saith, and it cometh to pass, when the Lord commandeth it not?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:825261f5-1402-4e03-95f8-6c425da48dcd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: LAM 3:38
Text: Out of the mouth of the most High proceedeth not evil and good?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89b177c9-cb2b-4ac0-bc6d-9eec54fae3d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: LAM 3:39
Text: Wherefore doth a living man complain, a man for the punishment of his sins?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:add7b2fd-525b-4764-b266-9ba89ad4bd7a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: LAM 3:40
Text: Let us search and try our ways, and turn again to the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:860b630f-688f-458a-b745-3272f45fa516>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: LAM 3:41
Text: Let us lift up our heart with our hands unto God in the heavens.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23d28d3e-5394-4a09-abed-d53b07268678>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: LAM 3:42
Text: We have transgressed and have rebelled: thou hast not pardoned.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b56c6238-2b16-47df-9c5f-f89315ec9ce0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: LAM 3:43
Text: Thou hast covered with anger, and persecuted us: thou hast slain, thou hast not pitied.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a90628fc-9116-47dd-8661-c391f96ed59e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: LAM 3:44
Text: Thou hast covered thyself with a cloud, that our prayer should not pass through.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a13c3640-5248-4366-80fb-d8564046c44c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: LAM 3:45
Text: Thou hast made us as the offscouring and refuse in the midst of the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e007dfaf-3be0-489a-a09f-798d7bc547ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: LAM 3:46
Text: All our enemies have opened their mouths against us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6434cd8f-d97f-495e-b5aa-cab76c0c51e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: LAM 3:47
Text: Fear and a snare is come upon us, desolation and destruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd1842cb-c580-4385-b628-c1827831a7ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: LAM 3:48
Text: Mine eye runneth down with rivers of water for the destruction of the daughter of my people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5e2b242-edd9-4846-878d-3ca2564f7cf1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: LAM 3:49
Text: Mine eye trickleth down, and ceaseth not, without any intermission.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90275b1e-407d-4b6e-92c6-f2bd26dd662c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: LAM 3:50
Text: Till the LORD look down, and behold from heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5ffd70e-16a5-432c-b3e6-94a578fd5297>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: LAM 3:51
Text: Mine eye affecteth mine heart because of all the daughters of my city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1629e140-8691-47e6-8b35-de57961a138d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: LAM 3:52
Text: Mine enemies chased me sore, like a bird, without cause.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:795c35fc-167c-4b01-aff6-d675ed2edf90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: LAM 3:53
Text: They have cut off my life in the dungeon, and cast a stone upon me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fba15316-d678-4436-80a9-738455e5c4b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: LAM 3:54
Text: Waters flowed over mine head; then I said, I am cut off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/55
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1882a3f6-6aef-4ed1-b50d-17e3958bca3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: LAM 3:55
Text: I called upon thy name, O LORD, out of the low dungeon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/56
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18ed8547-57da-4d28-a015-208d82e8e518>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: LAM 3:56
Text: Thou hast heard my voice: hide not thine ear at my breathing, at my cry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/57
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76a91270-8e9f-4bef-9eff-8303774c9a5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: LAM 3:57
Text: Thou drewest near in the day that I called upon thee: thou saidst, Fear not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/58
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2fb3ff9-a400-40db-826a-c2d34d242321>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: LAM 3:58
Text: O LORD, thou hast pleaded the causes of my soul; thou hast redeemed my life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/59
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d857730-2bce-4cdf-a08c-c3dcd0cf2d8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: LAM 3:59
Text: O LORD, thou hast seen my wrong: judge thou my cause.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/60
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c30efc3c-596e-40df-bfbe-06b7c7ad4d0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: LAM 3:60
Text: Thou hast seen all their vengeance and all their imaginations against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/61
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83047a33-5afe-40d0-98d2-af947aaf6090>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: LAM 3:61
Text: Thou hast heard their reproach, O LORD, and all their imaginations against me;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/62
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0eba385-4426-4d6f-a6cb-ec7ee94a2680>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: LAM 3:62
Text: The lips of those that rose up against me, and their device against me all the day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/63
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:977370ae-e4ed-4f8b-a4c4-a9a8cb94c9c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: LAM 3:63
Text: Behold their sitting down, and their rising up; I am their musick.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/64
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0a45ddd-96a1-411d-bbeb-1433114e07a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: LAM 3:64
Text: Render unto them a recompence, O LORD, according to the work of their hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/65
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2271f8a-c29c-40b1-b308-547ab20e60cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: LAM 3:65
Text: Give them sorrow of heart, thy curse unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/3/66
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8e90311-bf30-47ab-9e0c-29605263af0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: LAM 3:66
Text: Persecute and destroy them in anger from under the heavens of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39afa518-2109-4d21-80c0-804472831e7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: LAM 4:1
Text: How is the gold become dim! how is the most fine gold changed! the stones of the sanctuary are poured out in the top of every street.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7513c448-1b96-4933-b330-360aa827fd58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: LAM 4:2
Text: The precious sons of Zion, comparable to fine gold, how are they esteemed as earthen pitchers, the work of the hands of the potter!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:594c14b3-68e9-446e-bc3a-3311d41e985b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: LAM 4:3
Text: Even the sea monsters draw out the breast, they give suck to their young ones: the daughter of my people is become cruel, like the ostriches in the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b97fed9-9a53-4cbf-9ecc-4aaa82c7298c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: LAM 4:4
Text: The tongue of the sucking child cleaveth to the roof of his mouth for thirst: the young children ask bread, and no man breaketh it unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e7ccfbc-e237-4c25-9954-57459213f61c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: LAM 4:5
Text: They that did feed delicately are desolate in the streets: they that were brought up in scarlet embrace dunghills.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a57039a-ab61-42c3-a7b3-9b20c115f87f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: LAM 4:6
Text: For the punishment of the iniquity of the daughter of my people is greater than the punishment of the sin of Sodom, that was overthrown as in a moment, and no hands stayed on her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c004e2f8-0d5b-46dd-a29a-119c52f9366b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: LAM 4:7
Text: Her Nazarites were purer than snow, they were whiter than milk, they were more ruddy in body than rubies, their polishing was of sapphire:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32901167-e063-459b-98bc-e97e6593707c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: LAM 4:8
Text: Their visage is blacker than a coal; they are not known in the streets: their skin cleaveth to their bones; it is withered, it is become like a stick.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69eea2a6-9c75-430e-9c5b-b0fdd0f5c343>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: LAM 4:9
Text: They that be slain with the sword are better than they that be slain with hunger: for these pine away, stricken through for want of the fruits of the field.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4740651-ee46-4d5c-b901-277b59629209>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: LAM 4:10
Text: The hands of the pitiful women have sodden their own children: they were their meat in the destruction of the daughter of my people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e024493-0025-41b0-b0eb-bb8f59404269>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: LAM 4:11
Text: The LORD hath accomplished his fury; he hath poured out his fierce anger, and hath kindled a fire in Zion, and it hath devoured the foundations thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57588a84-4d5d-4f42-8629-371f9eaecff0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: LAM 4:12
Text: The kings of the earth, and all the inhabitants of the world, would not have believed that the adversary and the enemy should have entered into the gates of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f41de8fd-4b8b-4384-812e-bffa4ff15cb7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: LAM 4:13
Text: For the sins of her prophets, and the iniquities of her priests, that have shed the blood of the just in the midst of her,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24ec3ce9-53b7-464e-a97f-ce3993b7b768>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: LAM 4:14
Text: They have wandered as blind men in the streets, they have polluted themselves with blood, so that men could not touch their garments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e99a5a1-2c71-4609-a6ee-c566dc45e5f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: LAM 4:15
Text: They cried unto them, Depart ye; it is unclean; depart, depart, touch not: when they fled away and wandered, they said among the heathen, They shall no more sojourn there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d794c17-1bf0-4e76-8e6b-2dba9d55aa2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: LAM 4:16
Text: The anger of the LORD hath divided them; he will no more regard them: they respected not the persons of the priests, they favoured not the elders.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb3450f3-457c-447b-abb1-b755a31c23d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: LAM 4:17
Text: As for us, our eyes as yet failed for our vain help: in our watching we have watched for a nation that could not save us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/4/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e63fc19-954c-4fa3-9c66-281c7b19ab55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: LAM 4:18
Text: They hunt our steps, that we cannot go in our streets: our end is near, our days are fulfilled; for our end is come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/4/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:812c2ac6-c39c-4a1e-9fcf-62aaa46cc946>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: LAM 4:19
Text: Our persecutors are swifter than the eagles of the heaven: they pursued us upon the mountains, they laid wait for us in the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/4/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a78d2d57-f641-4ebf-be34-881f0e997284>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: LAM 4:20
Text: The breath of our nostrils, the anointed of the LORD, was taken in their pits, of whom we said, Under his shadow we shall live among the heathen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/4/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6001747b-21b9-4656-97ab-ee7d465b88fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: LAM 4:21
Text: Rejoice and be glad, O daughter of Edom, that dwellest in the land of Uz; the cup also shall pass through unto thee: thou shalt be drunken, and shalt make thyself naked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/4/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34dda342-3577-4a06-bba9-b7e7f20877e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: LAM 4:22
Text: The punishment of thine iniquity is accomplished, O daughter of Zion; he will no more carry thee away into captivity: he will visit thine iniquity, O daughter of Edom; he will discover thy sins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:733ccce6-0653-47e7-b31c-2f72bae1ae8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: LAM 5:1
Text: Remember, O LORD, what is come upon us: consider, and behold our reproach.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37526b8e-e96e-4c07-bfc2-7939b91f13ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: LAM 5:2
Text: Our inheritance is turned to strangers, our houses to aliens.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d1bb797-daee-41ae-9fa2-8e1b3200f189>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: LAM 5:3
Text: We are orphans and fatherless, our mothers are as widows.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:555ff862-3391-4034-8916-687e1feb3624>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: LAM 5:4
Text: We have drunken our water for money; our wood is sold unto us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:051e42c4-eb0c-4fc3-b68e-241d23ff2fca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: LAM 5:5
Text: Our necks are under persecution: we labour, and have no rest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08a74190-5f85-487b-a001-cf14c9b9e2c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: LAM 5:6
Text: We have given the hand to the Egyptians, and to the Assyrians, to be satisfied with bread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab69ffe7-4f22-498c-9405-9860fa5a16ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: LAM 5:7
Text: Our fathers have sinned, and are not; and we have borne their iniquities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46425abb-c555-4324-af42-eeb669aeeca4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: LAM 5:8
Text: Servants have ruled over us: there is none that doth deliver us out of their hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edae0d90-2d83-4f9d-aafa-d249a16a3521>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: LAM 5:9
Text: We gat our bread with the peril of our lives because of the sword of the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2dacebf-0793-4c0c-845b-a29fb190ab8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: LAM 5:10
Text: Our skin was black like an oven because of the terrible famine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58362ae6-0425-4afc-af8a-aaa5012652d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: LAM 5:11
Text: They ravished the women in Zion, and the maids in the cities of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c5ec315-7e64-49ba-866e-ddbf79754e41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: LAM 5:12
Text: Princes are hanged up by their hand: the faces of elders were not honoured.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1753448-8259-4ebd-ad2e-d0a537f87622>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: LAM 5:13
Text: They took the young men to grind, and the children fell under the wood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac9779b3-e8cf-419a-83a6-d9d2eed5a519>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: LAM 5:14
Text: The elders have ceased from the gate, the young men from their musick.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45ffe37f-8a61-48cd-91a5-c7ba33b5def2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: LAM 5:15
Text: The joy of our heart is ceased; our dance is turned into mourning.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06d0f013-aaf1-4a1c-aee5-f89a915f4f86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: LAM 5:16
Text: The crown is fallen from our head: woe unto us, that we have sinned!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/5/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11280b4e-da14-4d7b-8c63-7f024b09e162>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: LAM 5:17
Text: For this our heart is faint; for these things our eyes are dim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/5/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a8d7372-3464-4558-adc8-fcfd336c8955>
