Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: LAM 5:19
Text: Thou, O LORD, remainest for ever; thy throne from generation to generation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/5/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1a95b77-896d-419a-9ef5-97c08461d21b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: LAM 5:20
Text: Wherefore dost thou forget us for ever, and forsake us so long time?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/5/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c29c3cc9-151d-42d1-9a68-88eb234d88f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: LAM 5:21
Text: Turn thou us unto thee, O LORD, and we shall be turned; renew our days as of old.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LAM/5/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e91dacad-d7b8-4c8d-984e-048900c15d33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: LAM 5:22
Text: But thou hast utterly rejected us; thou art very wroth against us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5fa73fca-4ffd-4935-a251-9f48805209a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: EZK 1:1
Text: Now it came to pass in the thirtieth year, in the fourth month, in the fifth day of the month, as I was among the captives by the river of Chebar, that the heavens were opened, and I saw visions of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:157fdd9f-cc98-4634-b0de-1143e4f97cf3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: EZK 1:2
Text: In the fifth day of the month, which was the fifth year of king Jehoiachin’s captivity,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9f2a716-c5cc-4ca7-a2d9-40f6ef7eb655>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: EZK 1:3
Text: The word of the LORD came expressly unto Ezekiel the priest, the son of Buzi, in the land of the Chaldeans by the river Chebar; and the hand of the LORD was there upon him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8d2230f-2558-4ed1-b12f-9fb793e3e0f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: EZK 1:4
Text: And I looked, and, behold, a whirlwind came out of the north, a great cloud, and a fire infolding itself, and a brightness was about it, and out of the midst thereof as the colour of amber, out of the midst of the fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bffffeb5-f48d-44de-ac38-8d2747a275a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: EZK 1:5
Text: Also out of the midst thereof came the likeness of four living creatures. And this was their appearance; they had the likeness of a man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:553c4a72-25ea-4110-905f-2e55bdfaa6d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: EZK 1:6
Text: And every one had four faces, and every one had four wings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c851a422-8771-42c7-9ca1-6de413cd22b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: EZK 1:7
Text: And their feet were straight feet; and the sole of their feet was like the sole of a calf’s foot: and they sparkled like the colour of burnished brass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82c8a06c-4dea-4408-9eb4-b7e6f8cef778>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: EZK 1:8
Text: And they had the hands of a man under their wings on their four sides; and they four had their faces and their wings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:150edb3f-627a-4640-9ddb-511cd78e86e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: EZK 1:9
Text: Their wings were joined one to another; they turned not when they went; they went every one straight forward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cabe5fcd-adef-4a6e-bdfd-16ce2f2c6fc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: EZK 1:10
Text: As for the likeness of their faces, they four had the face of a man, and the face of a lion, on the right side: and they four had the face of an ox on the left side; they four also had the face of an eagle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55a7c070-6b27-4cb5-9d8d-87bc41d2611b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: EZK 1:11
Text: Thus were their faces: and their wings were stretched upward; two wings of every one were joined one to another, and two covered their bodies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09be0f85-c94f-48c5-aa3b-291ca3a28796>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: EZK 1:12
Text: And they went every one straight forward: whither the spirit was to go, they went; and they turned not when they went.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31e34623-e6d7-4940-a84a-64932c43ffad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: EZK 1:13
Text: As for the likeness of the living creatures, their appearance was like burning coals of fire, and like the appearance of lamps: it went up and down among the living creatures; and the fire was bright, and out of the fire went forth lightning.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56bd94ff-949f-429c-bf69-f39a092406f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: EZK 1:14
Text: And the living creatures ran and returned as the appearance of a flash of lightning.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1bfe4cb5-66c4-4879-a5a6-ee3c8340afdd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: EZK 1:15
Text: Now as I beheld the living creatures, behold one wheel upon the earth by the living creatures, with his four faces.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32b562d0-a94c-4668-b669-245336523dcf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: EZK 1:16
Text: The appearance of the wheels and their work was like unto the colour of a beryl: and they four had one likeness: and their appearance and their work was as it were a wheel in the middle of a wheel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51eb71df-ec3a-43c8-87ad-31f1bce22ea0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: EZK 1:17
Text: When they went, they went upon their four sides: and they turned not when they went.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:879fc4f0-9b68-4e12-99cd-5cff53f67990>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: EZK 1:18
Text: As for their rings, they were so high that they were dreadful; and their rings were full of eyes round about them four.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa13518f-ea6e-4954-a1cf-04cb533a4b72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: EZK 1:19
Text: And when the living creatures went, the wheels went by them: and when the living creatures were lifted up from the earth, the wheels were lifted up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:750ceaf9-c40f-47a5-b60c-397bd7242565>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: EZK 1:20
Text: Whithersoever the spirit was to go, they went, thither was their spirit to go; and the wheels were lifted up over against them: for the spirit of the living creature was in the wheels.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afa6ec6f-f59e-48dd-a49a-ce7be9861571>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: EZK 1:21
Text: When those went, these went; and when those stood, these stood; and when those were lifted up from the earth, the wheels were lifted up over against them: for the spirit of the living creature was in the wheels.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2209fa6-da8b-4037-822a-e0777b6dd9a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: EZK 1:22
Text: And the likeness of the firmament upon the heads of the living creature was as the colour of the terrible crystal, stretched forth over their heads above.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64599845-b0af-4a80-92c9-95575c37f241>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: EZK 1:23
Text: And under the firmament were their wings straight, the one toward the other: every one had two, which covered on this side, and every one had two, which covered on that side, their bodies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3491bbe-f89e-478d-bfe1-e7b8411cc38b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: EZK 1:24
Text: And when they went, I heard the noise of their wings, like the noise of great waters, as the voice of the Almighty, the voice of speech, as the noise of an host: when they stood, they let down their wings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff965384-fdd8-42f5-9f52-da9a5c18b21f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: EZK 1:25
Text: And there was a voice from the firmament that was over their heads, when they stood, and had let down their wings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3d9343d-786e-48fe-807a-4ceba7201312>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: EZK 1:26
Text: And above the firmament that was over their heads was the likeness of a throne, as the appearance of a sapphire stone: and upon the likeness of the throne was the likeness as the appearance of a man above upon it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8d299c5-6661-4557-a7fa-5a4ef7b9fe83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 283

Reference: EZK 1:27
Text: And I saw as the colour of amber, as the appearance of fire round about within it, from the appearance of his loins even upward, and from the appearance of his loins even downward, I saw as it were the appearance of fire, and it had brightness round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/1/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04c9fa9a-f982-453f-98f6-ff109344a7b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 294

Reference: EZK 1:28
Text: As the appearance of the bow that is in the cloud in the day of rain, so was the appearance of the brightness round about. This was the appearance of the likeness of the glory of the LORD. And when I saw it, I fell upon my face, and I heard a voice of one that spake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c4998fb-dc26-4f30-a4a9-918827f3b64c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: EZK 2:1
Text: And he said unto me, Son of man, stand upon thy feet, and I will speak unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14ab0da7-d6c0-4a65-8838-5dae6d778454>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: EZK 2:2
Text: And the spirit entered into me when he spake unto me, and set me upon my feet, that I heard him that spake unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d2bff04-110f-49c6-8f38-69bbc60afd04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: EZK 2:3
Text: And he said unto me, Son of man, I send thee to the children of Israel, to a rebellious nation that hath rebelled against me: they and their fathers have transgressed against me, even unto this very day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5a8d029-af78-4301-b20b-7efe59deaf87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: EZK 2:4
Text: For they are impudent children and stiffhearted. I do send thee unto them; and thou shalt say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3f8862c-7b6c-4a63-9787-9f86ee02bf6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: EZK 2:5
Text: And they, whether they will hear, or whether they will forbear, (for they are a rebellious house,) yet shall know that there hath been a prophet among them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d9b6ec9-81ac-4df2-9873-951fcbd87f75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 277

Reference: EZK 2:6
Text: And thou, son of man, be not afraid of them, neither be afraid of their words, though briers and thorns be with thee, and thou dost dwell among scorpions: be not afraid of their words, nor be dismayed at their looks, though they be a rebellious house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:973e7ec1-479a-4443-9fdc-7e65cdcf3924>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: EZK 2:7
Text: And thou shalt speak my words unto them, whether they will hear, or whether they will forbear: for they are most rebellious.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebd2e4a5-5420-4ba1-baf5-203be311bd24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: EZK 2:8
Text: But thou, son of man, hear what I say unto thee; Be not thou rebellious like that rebellious house: open thy mouth, and eat that I give thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d6a72f8-2e02-4e51-8741-f0edc80d43e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: EZK 2:9
Text: And when I looked, behold, an hand was sent unto me; and, lo, a roll of a book was therein;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f73247d3-1bd4-4a02-a4d7-9987561de6f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EZK 2:10
Text: And he spread it before me; and it was written within and without: and there was written therein lamentations, and mourning, and woe.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:482933d9-d5af-477f-aae6-bef2aa093667>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: EZK 3:1
Text: Moreover he said unto me, Son of man, eat that thou findest; eat this roll, and go speak unto the house of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4169884-4bdf-4e99-9f68-3c9b4acd49b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: EZK 3:2
Text: So I opened my mouth, and he caused me to eat that roll.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4271b420-6fad-4ca6-b7e9-f558f7fc3668>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: EZK 3:3
Text: And he said unto me, Son of man, cause thy belly to eat, and fill thy bowels with this roll that I give thee. Then did I eat it; and it was in my mouth as honey for sweetness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4b3f3c2-b43b-43b6-bdae-91e410793c36>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: EZK 3:4
Text: And he said unto me, Son of man, go, get thee unto the house of Israel, and speak with my words unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df0a99cc-a670-48b7-8642-28daf820ecdd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: EZK 3:5
Text: For thou art not sent to a people of a strange speech and of an hard language, but to the house of Israel;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4cc78e13-8279-477c-bf7c-5d93832b5dcf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: EZK 3:6
Text: Not to many people of a strange speech and of an hard language, whose words thou canst not understand. Surely, had I sent thee to them, they would have hearkened unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b28aa599-c29d-421e-ab48-ef44238c0d91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: EZK 3:7
Text: But the house of Israel will not hearken unto thee; for they will not hearken unto me: for all the house of Israel are impudent and hardhearted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:543d6248-e78f-4678-9ac0-729cd53df615>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: EZK 3:8
Text: Behold, I have made thy face strong against their faces, and thy forehead strong against their foreheads.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7a1b9b6-dde6-4704-9e3a-275a7148c450>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: EZK 3:9
Text: As an adamant harder than flint have I made thy forehead: fear them not, neither be dismayed at their looks, though they be a rebellious house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d425849-9e19-4628-97ac-61f3cb53f4f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: EZK 3:10
Text: Moreover he said unto me, Son of man, all my words that I shall speak unto thee receive in thine heart, and hear with thine ears.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f730f62-4538-441d-8680-19030a2f5aea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: EZK 3:11
Text: And go, get thee to them of the captivity, unto the children of thy people, and speak unto them, and tell them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; whether they will hear, or whether they will forbear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04f20daa-da78-44bc-b293-267a9e4c621f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: EZK 3:12
Text: Then the spirit took me up, and I heard behind me a voice of a great rushing, saying, Blessed be the glory of the LORD from his place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ccf6ad63-45eb-4a4a-be26-8b7c313e18e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: EZK 3:13
Text: I heard also the noise of the wings of the living creatures that touched one another, and the noise of the wheels over against them, and a noise of a great rushing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55e85afa-64fd-480b-a25d-9898e847de80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: EZK 3:14
Text: So the spirit lifted me up, and took me away, and I went in bitterness, in the heat of my spirit; but the hand of the LORD was strong upon me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35d4e467-4575-4d36-977f-3db8201893ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: EZK 3:15
Text: Then I came to them of the captivity at Telabib, that dwelt by the river of Chebar, and I sat where they sat, and remained there astonished among them seven days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81a34482-ac87-4743-829d-5347c6f89cb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: EZK 3:16
Text: And it came to pass at the end of seven days, that the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d8670df-eb60-4522-801f-743e97dba7dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EZK 3:17
Text: Son of man, I have made thee a watchman unto the house of Israel: therefore hear the word at my mouth, and give them warning from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96d8365a-1531-47a8-96d5-0701d01021dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: EZK 3:18
Text: When I say unto the wicked, Thou shalt surely die; and thou givest him not warning, nor speakest to warn the wicked from his wicked way, to save his life; the same wicked man shall die in his iniquity; but his blood will I require at thine hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:debac644-9396-41de-8b9b-ec08757667d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: EZK 3:19
Text: Yet if thou warn the wicked, and he turn not from his wickedness, nor from his wicked way, he shall die in his iniquity; but thou hast delivered thy soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3396dc3-342e-4f32-9d70-a3c4d030843d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 339

Reference: EZK 3:20
Text: Again, When a righteous man doth turn from his righteousness, and commit iniquity, and I lay a stumbling-block before him, he shall die: because thou hast not given him warning, he shall die in his sin, and his righteousness which he hath done shall not be remembered; but his blood will I require at thine hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:853833e1-ae4a-48db-8fc9-0fc312bf09ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: EZK 3:21
Text: Nevertheless if thou warn the righteous man, that the righteous sin not, and he doth not sin, he shall surely live, because he is warned; also thou hast delivered thy soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:315294ef-001f-4069-bcc9-bd50614220eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: EZK 3:22
Text: And the hand of the LORD was there upon me; and he said unto me, Arise, go forth into the plain, and I will there talk with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c04fd68-2e04-4364-9648-34f8391a913d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: EZK 3:23
Text: Then I arose, and went forth into the plain: and, behold, the glory of the LORD stood there, as the glory which I saw by the river of Chebar: and I fell on my face.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60332a42-4d75-480c-b155-00087061220f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EZK 3:24
Text: Then the spirit entered into me, and set me upon my feet, and spake with me, and said unto me, Go, shut thyself within thine house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7f4cb1a-0f14-4a33-8e4e-94be42fb0266>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: EZK 3:25
Text: But thou, O son of man, behold, they shall put bands upon thee, and shall bind thee with them, and thou shalt not go out among them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8360894-c83a-4e97-9c0f-31983c5167a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: EZK 3:26
Text: And I will make thy tongue cleave to the roof of thy mouth, that thou shalt be dumb, and shalt not be to them a reprover: for they are a rebellious house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/3/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95ebca30-8ef6-4fc0-a7da-0badd3f9f447>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: EZK 3:27
Text: But when I speak with thee, I will open thy mouth, and thou shalt say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; He that heareth, let him hear; and he that forbeareth, let him forbear: for they are a rebellious house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b937970-53e8-4c22-b3fc-4dc2c0fd5fb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: EZK 4:1
Text: Thou also, son of man, take thee a tile, and lay it before thee, and pourtray upon it the city, even Jerusalem:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4cbaea7d-cbc4-4c76-ad13-2142e4697fbf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: EZK 4:2
Text: And lay siege against it, and build a fort against it, and cast a mount against it; set the camp also against it, and set battering rams against it round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d5ee71a-598a-4f8f-b846-79e880566696>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: EZK 4:3
Text: Moreover take thou unto thee an iron pan, and set it for a wall of iron between thee and the city: and set thy face against it, and it shall be besieged, and thou shalt lay siege against it. This shall be a sign to the house of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d1af180-d0c4-4d0c-9948-dbea7fa5b10e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: EZK 4:4
Text: Lie thou also upon thy left side, and lay the iniquity of the house of Israel upon it: according to the number of the days that thou shalt lie upon it thou shalt bear their iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e334b37-4234-40e7-af55-281d51ae0d34>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: EZK 4:5
Text: For I have laid upon thee the years of their iniquity, according to the number of the days, three hundred and ninety days: so shalt thou bear the iniquity of the house of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8daf6532-ea29-4c4a-a3d8-607a8e22014d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: EZK 4:6
Text: And when thou hast accomplished them, lie again on thy right side, and thou shalt bear the iniquity of the house of Judah forty days: I have appointed thee each day for a year.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a209608c-68ab-4039-aafe-d64e58b47449>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EZK 4:7
Text: Therefore thou shalt set thy face toward the siege of Jerusalem, and thine arm shall be uncovered, and thou shalt prophesy against it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb5cd1db-de36-4cf0-8021-465dd89a12de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: EZK 4:8
Text: And, behold, I will lay bands upon thee, and thou shalt not turn thee from one side to another, till thou hast ended the days of thy siege.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8f4b2f1-64ec-4050-b866-cef022014356>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 301

Reference: EZK 4:9
Text: Take thou also unto thee wheat, and barley, and beans, and lentiles, and millet, and fitches, and put them in one vessel, and make thee bread thereof, according to the number of the days that thou shalt lie upon thy side, three hundred and ninety days shalt thou eat thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b7b4f4e-ccf2-4a41-b5db-7bbb1b56b316>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: EZK 4:10
Text: And thy meat which thou shalt eat shall be by weight, twenty shekels a day: from time to time shalt thou eat it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab723810-47d1-4a1f-93bc-1168fd0608dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: EZK 4:11
Text: Thou shalt drink also water by measure, the sixth part of an hin: from time to time shalt thou drink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ea49b81-cbf8-44dc-804d-9c84197eca01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: EZK 4:12
Text: And thou shalt eat it as barley cakes, and thou shalt bake it with dung that cometh out of man, in their sight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49234afa-df60-4be6-825c-e6c8d482b1ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: EZK 4:13
Text: And the LORD said, Even thus shall the children of Israel eat their defiled bread among the Gentiles, whither I will drive them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61bd4ade-fb74-4960-b071-76793ea7d35a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: EZK 4:14
Text: Then said I, Ah Lord GOD! behold, my soul hath not been polluted: for from my youth up even till now have I not eaten of that which dieth of itself, or is torn in pieces; neither came there abominable flesh into my mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e1e4c0c-5a1f-49b4-8c26-2aece179096c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: EZK 4:15
Text: Then he said unto me, Lo, I have given thee cow’s dung for man’s dung, and thou shalt prepare thy bread therewith.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9aa7ac71-feb6-41ed-8b18-d5a53275ae2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: EZK 4:16
Text: Moreover he said unto me, Son of man, behold, I will break the staff of bread in Jerusalem: and they shall eat bread by weight, and with care; and they shall drink water by measure, and with astonishment:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70c30d34-6266-4c14-b3a7-b4b254b10328>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: EZK 4:17
Text: That they may want bread and water, and be astonied one with another, and consume away for their iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aad82bef-808d-4ff4-9d69-398f4acdb99a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: EZK 5:1
Text: And thou, son of man, take thee a sharp knife, take thee a barber’s razor, and cause it to pass upon thine head and upon thy beard: then take thee balances to weigh, and divide the hair.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7853d8c6-484a-4608-a516-b3ba3e341d1e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 288

Reference: EZK 5:2
Text: Thou shalt burn with fire a third part in the midst of the city, when the days of the siege are fulfilled: and thou shalt take a third part, and smite about it with a knife: and a third part thou shalt scatter in the wind; and I will draw out a sword after them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05b463d7-35dc-4d35-b020-b4d7e6ea5497>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: EZK 5:3
Text: Thou shalt also take thereof a few in number, and bind them in thy skirts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbd45843-682f-4164-a78d-ec8ada8536be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: EZK 5:4
Text: Then take of them again, and cast them into the midst of the fire, and burn them in the fire; for thereof shall a fire come forth into all the house of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a954207c-4ddd-45b5-8963-afac5dc0f642>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: EZK 5:5
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; This is Jerusalem: I have set it in the midst of the nations and countries that are round about her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e94eaf4c-4342-4b1b-abf2-3fbe24b78b12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: EZK 5:6
Text: And she hath changed my judgments into wickedness more than the nations, and my statutes more than the countries that are round about her: for they have refused my judgments and my statutes, they have not walked in them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e6257d9-0277-479f-a730-71761b4f4600>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: EZK 5:7
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Because ye multiplied more than the nations that are round about you, and have not walked in my statutes, neither have kept my judgments, neither have done according to the judgments of the nations that are round about you;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37fbcb91-0c88-4d84-b724-74056f621a6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: EZK 5:8
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I, even I, am against thee, and will execute judgments in the midst of thee in the sight of the nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db761dbf-1c69-4284-b2b0-091f60e2b693>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EZK 5:9
Text: And I will do in thee that which I have not done, and whereunto I will not do any more the like, because of all thine abominations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54c9c156-9878-43bd-8a41-55775a574877>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: EZK 5:10
Text: Therefore the fathers shall eat the sons in the midst of thee, and the sons shall eat their fathers; and I will execute judgments in thee, and the whole remnant of thee will I scatter into all the winds.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06db53c2-0956-43d5-8eed-85d5ad228c50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 277

Reference: EZK 5:11
Text: Wherefore, as I live, saith the Lord GOD; Surely, because thou hast defiled my sanctuary with all thy detestable things, and with all thine abominations, therefore will I also diminish thee; neither shall mine eye spare, neither will I have any pity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91985bfa-2785-4191-9640-a6ebe3c67f4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 290

Reference: EZK 5:12
Text: A third part of thee shall die with the pestilence, and with famine shall they be consumed in the midst of thee: and a third part shall fall by the sword round about thee; and I will scatter a third part into all the winds, and I will draw out a sword after them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32ba1c08-baaf-422a-a777-30381c50bb10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: EZK 5:13
Text: Thus shall mine anger be accomplished, and I will cause my fury to rest upon them, and I will be comforted: and they shall know that I the LORD have spoken it in my zeal, when I have accomplished my fury in them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de5cc90e-25d8-4e1a-a5eb-e40cca26f107>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: EZK 5:14
Text: Moreover I will make thee waste, and a reproach among the nations that are round about thee, in the sight of all that pass by.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03c9b5b8-778f-4aba-aa7b-db50ca7e87ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: EZK 5:15
Text: So it shall be a reproach and a taunt, an instruction and an astonishment unto the nations that are round about thee, when I shall execute judgments in thee in anger and in fury and in furious rebukes. I the LORD have spoken it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:356916c0-80e5-48f3-b284-36d9112c48fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: EZK 5:16
Text: When I shall send upon them the evil arrows of famine, which shall be for their destruction, and which I will send to destroy you: and I will increase the famine upon you, and will break your staff of bread:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/5/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c12d11a-215a-40e7-9473-a12fcd970961>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: EZK 5:17
Text: So will I send upon you famine and evil beasts, and they shall bereave thee: and pestilence and blood shall pass through thee; and I will bring the sword upon thee. I the LORD have spoken it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28d45770-6018-411d-bd06-a5f2ff9b31b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 72

Reference: EZK 6:1
Text: And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d4a6c2c-8b61-45ec-b9b9-458f4da65c1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: EZK 6:2
Text: Son of man, set thy face toward the mountains of Israel, and prophesy against them,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb6ef99a-541c-4339-9ee3-b88f0a6e2841>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: EZK 6:3
Text: And say, Ye mountains of Israel, hear the word of the Lord GOD; Thus saith the Lord GOD to the mountains, and to the hills, to the rivers, and to the valleys; Behold, I, even I, will bring a sword upon you, and I will destroy your high places.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f8d7b74-5197-4271-b804-ab7b2e082c36>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: EZK 6:4
Text: And your altars shall be desolate, and your images shall be broken: and I will cast down your slain men before your idols.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14d44aa8-1490-4b76-b8cc-682ce286ee35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: EZK 6:5
Text: And I will lay the dead carcases of the children of Israel before their idols; and I will scatter your bones round about your altars.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:daa3ba78-a98f-4e8d-8452-9c56f18f56b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 283

Reference: EZK 6:6
Text: In all your dwellingplaces the cities shall be laid waste, and the high places shall be desolate; that your altars may be laid waste and made desolate, and your idols may be broken and cease, and your images may be cut down, and your works may be abolished.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b8e0e21-ec46-4e46-bf31-1c05543ed6e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: EZK 6:7
Text: And the slain shall fall in the midst of you, and ye shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:472a40fc-00ba-405d-adc2-857ddccbd899>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: EZK 6:8
Text: Yet will I leave a remnant, that ye may have some that shall escape the sword among the nations, when ye shall be scattered through the countries.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4fa5ef6-5866-4c61-bd9a-ae2afa7f68f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 362

Reference: EZK 6:9
Text: And they that escape of you shall remember me among the nations whither they shall be carried captives, because I am broken with their whorish heart, which hath departed from me, and with their eyes, which go a whoring after their idols: and they shall lothe themselves for the evils which they have committed in all their abominations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2dc1d8a3-7de3-485c-9550-34b8f7447c4f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: EZK 6:10
Text: And they shall know that I am the LORD, and that I have not said in vain that I would do this evil unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d00c3527-bf7f-4352-815b-290afc6f70cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: EZK 6:11
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; Smite with thine hand, and stamp with thy foot, and say, Alas for all the evil abominations of the house of Israel! for they shall fall by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00631d68-5730-4d8a-9ba5-083feae9ed99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: EZK 6:12
Text: He that is far off shall die of the pestilence; and he that is near shall fall by the sword; and he that remaineth and is besieged shall die by the famine: thus will I accomplish my fury upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5dde32ce-9ca6-41b4-aaa1-47b70a39dc59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 314

Reference: EZK 6:13
Text: Then shall ye know that I am the LORD, when their slain men shall be among their idols round about their altars, upon every high hill, in all the tops of the mountains, and under every green tree, and under every thick oak, the place where they did offer sweet savour to all their idols.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/6/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c492580f-59dd-4a70-8716-db2654ad6b7a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: EZK 6:14
Text: So will I stretch out my hand upon them, and make the land desolate, yea, more desolate than the wilderness toward Diblath, in all their habitations: and they shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:373b6fb9-6585-4318-92d6-823704ac386b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: EZK 7:1
Text: Moreover the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7432d11e-95a5-42bc-be35-77763a2cdae5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: EZK 7:2
Text: Also, thou son of man, thus saith the Lord GOD unto the land of Israel; An end, the end is come upon the four corners of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11fafd08-4dfe-4544-aed9-0d59d7171f7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: EZK 7:3
Text: Now is the end come upon thee, and I will send mine anger upon thee, and will judge thee according to thy ways, and will recompense upon thee all thine abominations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cf78b8e-89f1-40d4-97db-df355760a7c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: EZK 7:4
Text: And mine eye shall not spare thee, neither will I have pity: but I will recompense thy ways upon thee, and thine abominations shall be in the midst of thee: and ye shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84436afd-32b5-43fa-8179-beb9915bb611>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: EZK 7:5
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; An evil, an only evil, behold, is come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c080a170-ea65-4f28-89f7-8142f35d5b07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: EZK 7:6
Text: An end is come, the end is come: it watcheth for thee; behold, it is come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9948baab-e2bb-47ea-a522-b5c32a9b965e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: EZK 7:7
Text: The morning is come unto thee, O thou that dwellest in the land: the time is come, the day of trouble is near, and not the sounding again of the mountains.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a21714ac-7434-4b55-ad38-98268de289ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: EZK 7:8
Text: Now will I shortly pour out my fury upon thee, and accomplish mine anger upon thee: and I will judge thee according to thy ways, and will recompense thee for all thine abominations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b58a2ee5-e0e9-4a8d-9ff6-7814a2b8ac06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: EZK 7:9
Text: And mine eye shall not spare, neither will I have pity: I will recompense thee according to thy ways and thine abominations that are in the midst of thee; and ye shall know that I am the LORD that smiteth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16ef3b24-fe21-4fb7-a736-a5f4e30fc61c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: EZK 7:10
Text: Behold the day, behold, it is come: the morning is gone forth; the rod hath blossomed, pride hath budded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88ca704b-8f61-4230-8c31-dffa5f42b852>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: EZK 7:11
Text: Violence is risen up into a rod of wickedness: none of them shall remain, nor of their multitude, nor of any of theirs: neither shall there be wailing for them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbe842a1-3419-4218-8473-3c8f907dc28a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EZK 7:12
Text: The time is come, the day draweth near: let not the buyer rejoice, nor the seller mourn: for wrath is upon all the multitude thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a21cb9a2-c91e-4ce7-8ca4-7ce49abbb8d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: EZK 7:13
Text: For the seller shall not return to that which is sold, although they were yet alive: for the vision is touching the whole multitude thereof, which shall not return; neither shall any strengthen himself in the iniquity of his life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bfdd8a9f-9961-491f-aeac-6e4827872875>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EZK 7:14
Text: They have blown the trumpet, even to make all ready; but none goeth to the battle: for my wrath is upon all the multitude thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aeabe583-bccc-426c-b43d-fe7668ee9889>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: EZK 7:15
Text: The sword is without, and the pestilence and the famine within: he that is in the field shall die with the sword; and he that is in the city, famine and pestilence shall devour him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:baf7e57f-0898-41f1-8fda-a9dfca2f724c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: EZK 7:16
Text: But they that escape of them shall escape, and shall be on the mountains like doves of the valleys, all of them mourning, every one for his iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed95a29e-6fb5-44e7-b78e-99d18a16e203>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: EZK 7:17
Text: All hands shall be feeble, and all knees shall be weak as water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b2106c0-a201-4292-a158-cc096901f728>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: EZK 7:18
Text: They shall also gird themselves with sackcloth, and horror shall cover them; and shame shall be upon all faces, and baldness upon all their heads.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec1a3ba4-21fc-4384-822a-6636d4f4f8f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 318

Reference: EZK 7:19
Text: They shall cast their silver in the streets, and their gold shall be removed: their silver and their gold shall not be able to deliver them in the day of the wrath of the LORD: they shall not satisfy their souls, neither fill their bowels: because it is the stumblingblock of their iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e48dd50-d862-4dd8-9d1e-7e71381d71ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: EZK 7:20
Text: As for the beauty of his ornament, he set it in majesty: but they made the images of their abominations and of their detestable things therein: therefore have I set it far from them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38d9b9f9-0a5f-4711-a4a5-2435aa556f29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EZK 7:21
Text: And I will give it into the hands of the strangers for a prey, and to the wicked of the earth for a spoil; and they shall pollute it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d563c8b-4dfc-4898-8696-d42d558c7665>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: EZK 7:22
Text: My face will I turn also from them, and they shall pollute my secret place: for the robbers shall enter into it, and defile it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38cba129-1cd5-461c-a9fa-cbf3575d2378>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: EZK 7:23
Text: Make a chain: for the land is full of bloody crimes, and the city is full of violence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:628dcc07-5fca-44ff-a47c-b10aba585ea8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: EZK 7:24
Text: Wherefore I will bring the worst of the heathen, and they shall possess their houses: I will also make the pomp of the strong to cease; and their holy places shall be defiled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73a78412-0b1e-4898-8648-a7009304fd84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: EZK 7:25
Text: Destruction cometh; and they shall seek peace, and there shall be none.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10ec995d-dbfb-4d9b-b6df-7a818144a5e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: EZK 7:26
Text: Mischief shall come upon mischief, and rumour shall be upon rumour; then shall they seek a vision of the prophet; but the law shall perish from the priest, and counsel from the ancients.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/7/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc6fd8c1-9370-4798-aef0-d9ea6237f924>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 283

Reference: EZK 7:27
Text: The king shall mourn, and the prince shall be clothed with desolation, and the hands of the people of the land shall be troubled: I will do unto them after their way, and according to their deserts will I judge them; and they shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/8/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41f8784e-03cb-4b70-8a6f-b4beb38828e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: EZK 8:1
Text: And it came to pass in the sixth year, in the sixth month, in the fifth day of the month, as I sat in mine house, and the elders of Judah sat before me, that the hand of the Lord GOD fell there upon me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/8/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:799b7168-c80e-43bd-8248-7455dda86d01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: EZK 8:2
Text: Then I beheld, and lo a likeness as the appearance of fire: from the appearance of his loins even downward, fire; and from his loins even upward, as the appearance of brightness, as the colour of amber.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/8/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80b9bb7b-6c0c-4b70-a463-bf9ae227cff3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 347

Reference: EZK 8:3
Text: And he put forth the form of an hand, and took me by a lock of mine head; and the spirit lifted me up between the earth and the heaven, and brought me in the visions of God to Jerusalem, to the door of the inner gate that looketh toward the north; where was the seat of the image of jealousy, which provoketh to jealousy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/8/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:549173ef-4d6b-42fb-bdba-3ad2ed0b0283>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: EZK 8:4
Text: And, behold, the glory of the God of Israel was there, according to the vision that I saw in the plain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/8/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fcfd46da-b41e-42fe-9d9f-82f286fa3356>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: EZK 8:5
Text: Then said he unto me, Son of man, lift up thine eyes now the way toward the north. So I lifted up mine eyes the way toward the north, and behold northward at the gate of the altar this image of jealousy in the entry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/8/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c889e905-34aa-4968-857d-7d20c3a584be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: EZK 8:6
Text: He said furthermore unto me, Son of man, seest thou what they do? even the great abominations that the house of Israel committeth here, that I should go far off from my sanctuary? but turn thee yet again, and thou shalt see greater abominations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/8/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:307c8243-a8af-4118-9b96-501fa4e42e8e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: EZK 8:7
Text: And he brought me to the door of the court; and when I looked, behold a hole in the wall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/8/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8422b640-bd31-463e-ab33-25bd57ddea4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: EZK 8:8
Text: Then said he unto me, Son of man, dig now in the wall: and when I had digged in the wall, behold a door.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/8/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5ff3c8b-a196-4408-8de3-d6c27495c3c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: EZK 8:9
Text: And he said unto me, Go in, and behold the wicked abominations that they do here.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/8/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9adf1bfc-642a-422c-af8e-186370918aad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: EZK 8:10
Text: So I went in and saw; and behold every form of creeping things, and abominable beasts, and all the idols of the house of Israel, pourtrayed upon the wall round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/8/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5b3283a-c7bf-445f-80b0-3130d6cde5c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: EZK 8:11
Text: And there stood before them seventy men of the ancients of the house of Israel, and in the midst of them stood Jaazaniah the son of Shaphan, with every man his censer in his hand; and a thick cloud of incense went up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/8/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:146be05d-54e1-4f5b-aded-0ba5d975b1f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: EZK 8:12
Text: Then said he unto me, Son of man, hast thou seen what the ancients of the house of Israel do in the dark, every man in the chambers of his imagery? for they say, the LORD seeth us not; the LORD hath forsaken the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/8/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a9c305f-1c1f-42c4-b906-1130f5156b8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: EZK 8:13
Text: He said also unto me, Turn thee yet again, and thou shalt see greater abominations that they do.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/8/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7d0cc7c-63ad-4d2f-8080-8bcc97c2296d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: EZK 8:14
Text: Then he brought me to the door of the gate of the LORD’s house which was toward the north; and, behold, there sat women weeping for Tammuz.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/8/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2db4c8d-b372-4102-8097-574c3e8490bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: EZK 8:15
Text: Then said he unto me, Hast thou seen this, O son of man? turn thee yet again, and thou shalt see greater abominations than these.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/8/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a913be8-71f7-4fbc-acc8-952d49356e86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 331

Reference: EZK 8:16
Text: And he brought me into the inner court of the LORD’s house, and, behold, at the door of the temple of the LORD, between the porch and the altar, were about five and twenty men, with their backs toward the temple of the LORD, and their faces toward the east; and they worshipped the sun toward the east.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/8/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:597238ff-b1cb-4354-a19a-4da33eaadfa9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 314

Reference: EZK 8:17
Text: Then he said unto me, Hast thou seen this, O son of man? Is it a light thing to the house of Judah that they commit the abominations which they commit here? for they have filled the land with violence, and have returned to provoke me to anger: and, lo, they put the branch to their nose.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/8/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed9b325a-da58-41cb-a57f-31d75f8fc639>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: EZK 8:18
Text: Therefore will I also deal in fury: mine eye shall not spare, neither will I have pity: and though they cry in mine ears with a loud voice, yet will I not hear them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/9/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef256b6d-734b-4301-bed2-f78085873b60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: EZK 9:1
Text: He cried also in mine ears with a loud voice, saying, Cause them that have charge over the city to draw near, even every man with his destroying weapon in his hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/9/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d1071dc-cccc-423a-9992-92d3844a27ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 299

Reference: EZK 9:2
Text: And, behold, six men came from the way of the higher gate, which lieth toward the north, and every man a slaughter weapon in his hand; and one man among them was clothed with linen, with a writer’s inkhorn by his side: and they went in, and stood beside the brasen altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/9/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0368a8df-643f-4f0b-90e0-7fc4054dab1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: EZK 9:3
Text: And the glory of the God of Israel was gone up from the cherub, whereupon he was, to the threshold of the house. And he called to the man clothed with linen, which had the writer’s inkhorn by his side;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/9/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d186a354-df02-49b7-835d-fd1d1a7f31da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: EZK 9:4
Text: And the LORD said unto him, Go through the midst of the city, through the midst of Jerusalem, and set a mark upon the foreheads of the men that sigh and that cry for all the abominations that be done in the midst thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/9/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5c99575-7346-4cbd-9a11-83e9ad3b6ee4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: EZK 9:5
Text: And to the others he said in mine hearing, Go ye after him through the city, and smite: let not your eye spare, neither have ye pity:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/9/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94220e83-7b00-4770-afea-75ebbb52bf1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: EZK 9:6
Text: Slay utterly old and young, both maids, and little children, and women: but come not near any man upon whom is the mark; and begin at my sanctuary. Then they began at the ancient men which were before the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/9/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f69ca93-1bca-4709-8f93-37c9413fcea4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EZK 9:7
Text: And he said unto them, Defile the house, and fill the courts with the slain: go ye forth. And they went forth, and slew in the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/9/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b3e9f6d-6509-426c-a70e-b7cb91689c75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: EZK 9:8
Text: And it came to pass, while they were slaying them, and I was left, that I fell upon my face, and cried, and said, Ah Lord GOD! wilt thou destroy all the residue of Israel in thy pouring out of thy fury upon Jerusalem?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/9/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1caeecaf-6cfb-40a3-8fef-3fc755b79e92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: EZK 9:9
Text: Then said he unto me, The iniquity of the house of Israel and Judah is exceeding great, and the land is full of blood, and the city full of perverseness: for they say, The LORD hath forsaken the earth, and the LORD seeth not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/9/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22e88dac-892e-4b4f-bb91-396683048739>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: EZK 9:10
Text: And as for me also, mine eye shall not spare, neither will I have pity, but I will recompense their way upon their head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/9/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c904d01e-d1b7-4200-a289-f0476211ca2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: EZK 9:11
Text: And, behold, the man clothed with linen, which had the inkhorn by his side, reported the matter, saying, I have done as thou hast commanded me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/10/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8adf013c-7b7a-42b4-b5bc-7c39dfbd7c31>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: EZK 10:1
Text: Then I looked, and, behold, in the firmament that was above the head of the cherubims there appeared over them as it were a sapphire stone, as the appearance of the likeness of a throne.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/10/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8a11d55-868e-48a6-9733-b20c76ee5230>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: EZK 10:2
Text: And he spake unto the man clothed with linen, and said, Go in between the wheels, even under the cherub, and fill thine hand with coals of fire from between the cherubims, and scatter them over the city. And he went in in my sight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/10/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d409dacc-35a7-4e1e-a3f5-9bb0276a6a85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: EZK 10:3
Text: Now the cherubims stood on the right side of the house, when the man went in; and the cloud filled the inner court.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/10/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df5811ea-a3fb-4563-86c6-33fa0f163649>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: EZK 10:4
Text: Then the glory of the LORD went up from the cherub, and stood over the threshold of the house; and the house was filled with the cloud, and the court was full of the brightness of the LORD’s glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/10/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:efb095c7-9da6-4caf-a05c-ed047e264b07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: EZK 10:5
Text: And the sound of the cherubims’ wings was heard even to the outer court, as the voice of the Almighty God when he speaketh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/10/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0166a460-7e3b-4d1a-855b-95e34c8fcb00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: EZK 10:6
Text: And it came to pass, that when he had commanded the man clothed with linen, saying, Take fire from between the wheels, from between the cherubims; then he went in, and stood beside the wheels.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/10/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82c0bc1a-ac5f-4dcf-b675-e8b70c8bd063>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: EZK 10:7
Text: And one cherub stretched forth his hand from between the cherubims unto the fire that was between the cherubims, and took thereof, and put it into the hands of him that was clothed with linen: who took it, and went out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/10/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d7bcc8e-b2af-4f7e-bdbd-d80673693c5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: EZK 10:8
Text: And there appeared in the cherubims the form of a man’s hand under their wings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/10/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:208978c5-b64a-46a4-8193-faa5446afe34>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: EZK 10:9
Text: And when I looked, behold the four wheels by the cherubims, one wheel by one cherub, and another wheel by another cherub: and the appearance of the wheels was as the colour of a beryl stone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/10/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:faf353fb-bdfc-4d44-908d-873e5658a85a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: EZK 10:10
Text: And as for their appearances, they four had one likeness, as if a wheel had been in the midst of a wheel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/10/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d470fed-d1a4-435e-bf60-94d80568fddb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: EZK 10:11
Text: When they went, they went upon their four sides; they turned not as they went, but to the place whither the head looked they followed it; they turned not as they went.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/10/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71499455-cb98-4888-b2a7-4bc6d9c9ce60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: EZK 10:12
Text: And their whole body, and their backs, and their hands, and their wings, and the wheels, were full of eyes round about, even the wheels that they four had.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/10/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16c5135d-a28b-4b78-8fb7-70c0cb616b56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: EZK 10:13
Text: As for the wheels, it was cried unto them in my hearing, O wheel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/10/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44a711e9-5541-4f7b-bd15-0c5e6c061537>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: EZK 10:14
Text: And every one had four faces: the first face was the face of a cherub, and the second face was the face of a man, and the third the face of a lion, and the fourth the face of an eagle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/10/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20341368-4a9a-4fc8-8da4-aab20c32dc37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: EZK 10:15
Text: And the cherubims were lifted up. This is the living creature that I saw by the river of Chebar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/10/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:184cddcc-25fb-445f-b5cd-f431848b4e12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: EZK 10:16
Text: And when the cherubims went, the wheels went by them: and when the cherubims lifted up their wings to mount up from the earth, the same wheels also turned not from beside them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/10/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57b8d056-8b49-4b56-a748-724c235dca1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: EZK 10:17
Text: When they stood, these stood; and when they were lifted up, these lifted up themselves also: for the spirit of the living creature was in them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/10/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6067244-5b9d-45cd-9875-c8ce457844c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: EZK 10:18
Text: Then the glory of the LORD departed from off the threshold of the house, and stood over the cherubims.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/10/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7de768c-33ff-480a-b9ed-efe01132816f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 293

Reference: EZK 10:19
Text: And the cherubims lifted up their wings, and mounted up from the earth in my sight: when they went out, the wheels also were beside them, and every one stood at the door of the east gate of the LORD’s house; and the glory of the God of Israel was over them above.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/10/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c25b6145-1263-47de-ad13-b79cd26a801a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: EZK 10:20
Text: This is the living creature that I saw under the God of Israel by the river of Chebar; and I knew that they were the cherubims.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/10/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4357d99f-0e4d-44a4-8b11-424a4707a5c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: EZK 10:21
Text: Every one had four faces apiece, and every one four wings; and the likeness of the hands of a man was under their wings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/10/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3e765bd-5fe2-49af-b91a-cfabd7a105fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: EZK 10:22
Text: And the likeness of their faces was the same faces which I saw by the river of Chebar, their appearances and themselves: they went every one straight forward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3cc4dd8-654f-4f4e-a291-51e6bdff21e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 297

Reference: EZK 11:1
Text: Moreover the spirit lifted me up, and brought me unto the east gate of the LORD’s house, which looketh eastward: and behold at the door of the gate five and twenty men; among whom I saw Jaazaniah the son of Azur, and Pelatiah the son of Benaiah, princes of the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28d8049e-8541-49cb-87f0-77492302a891>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: EZK 11:2
Text: Then said he unto me, Son of man, these are the men that devise mischief, and give wicked counsel in this city:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9cd11d34-5483-4902-bc30-71381f7452e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: EZK 11:3
Text: Which say, It is not near; let us build houses: this city is the caldron, and we be the flesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0189efcb-02eb-46c1-b3f4-404d6d6b243e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: EZK 11:4
Text: Therefore prophesy against them, prophesy, O son of man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00337050-a482-4812-9baa-15828567f83f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: EZK 11:5
Text: And the Spirit of the LORD fell upon me, and said unto me, Speak; Thus saith the LORD; Thus have ye said, O house of Israel: for I know the things that come into your mind, every one of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99e775a9-48b2-4ae0-b4c7-375524fc3380>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: EZK 11:6
Text: Ye have multiplied your slain in this city, and ye have filled the streets thereof with the slain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b11cf6ad-5ce2-432a-a702-e3b491d7b6fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: EZK 11:7
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Your slain whom ye have laid in the midst of it, they are the flesh, and this city is the caldron: but I will bring you forth out of the midst of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfc5a603-c11c-4786-953f-2b2c451c385d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: EZK 11:8
Text: Ye have feared the sword; and I will bring a sword upon you, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aee40690-f9a1-43b1-acc4-e017dd2919f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: EZK 11:9
Text: And I will bring you out of the midst thereof, and deliver you into the hands of strangers, and will execute judgments among you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa87e48c-d55d-4d97-923f-3d556d6a890e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: EZK 11:10
Text: Ye shall fall by the sword; I will judge you in the border of Israel; and ye shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5c495fb-32c1-4153-802e-8775ffc6cb6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: EZK 11:11
Text: This city shall not be your caldron, neither shall ye be the flesh in the midst thereof; but I will judge you in the border of Israel:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:898c1286-c55c-4766-8dd5-c83db5d98a1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: EZK 11:12
Text: And ye shall know that I am the LORD: for ye have not walked in my statutes, neither executed my judgments, but have done after the manners of the heathen that are round about you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1987d09-8948-437d-a5d1-a4030f3340d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: EZK 11:13
Text: And it came to pass, when I prophesied, that Pelatiah the son of Benaiah died. Then fell I down upon my face, and cried with a loud voice, and said, Ah Lord GOD! wilt thou make a full end of the remnant of Israel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f5e678e-ff24-4d2c-b49e-237766ed021f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: EZK 11:14
Text: Again the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:469fc46c-c43e-4d87-a239-bc310ac99196>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: EZK 11:15
Text: Son of man, thy brethren, even thy brethren, the men of thy kindred, and all the house of Israel wholly, are they unto whom the inhabitants of Jerusalem have said, Get you far from the LORD: unto us is this land given in possession.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8113abef-1f68-4fbc-ba0a-d6c2c4d9a44d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: EZK 11:16
Text: Therefore say, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Although I have cast them far off among the heathen, and although I have scattered them among the countries, yet will I be to them as a little sanctuary in the countries where they shall come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b396883-8d89-4b12-af3e-76ea317e2b00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: EZK 11:17
Text: Therefore say, Thus saith the Lord GOD; I will even gather you from the people, and assemble you out of the countries where ye have been scattered, and I will give you the land of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aea00175-44e4-46de-bfdb-47a9958bd589>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: EZK 11:18
Text: And they shall come thither, and they shall take away all the detestable things thereof and all the abominations thereof from thence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c9527e2-177c-40d0-b624-e32452526a9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: EZK 11:19
Text: And I will give them one heart, and I will put a new spirit within you; and I will take the stony heart out of their flesh, and will give them an heart of flesh:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c982cf8-b365-4e4a-8d15-6de5a41a9d1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: EZK 11:20
Text: That they may walk in my statutes, and keep mine ordinances, and do them: and they shall be my people, and I will be their God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ed00305-6dbd-4719-9654-0dd71080f8ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: EZK 11:21
Text: But as for them whose heart walketh after the heart of their detestable things and their abominations, I will recompense their way upon their own heads, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e212f62b-6849-48c4-a0a8-8ba91de3496e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: EZK 11:22
Text: Then did the cherubims lift up their wings, and the wheels beside them; and the glory of the God of Israel was over them above.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c02cad4-c616-453f-984e-28c184f9b60e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: EZK 11:23
Text: And the glory of the LORD went up from the midst of the city, and stood upon the mountain which is on the east side of the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7828c35c-9d3b-47c3-befa-e3a408cc51f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: EZK 11:24
Text: Afterwards the spirit took me up, and brought me in a vision by the Spirit of God into Chaldea, to them of the captivity. So the vision that I had seen went up from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/11/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:049c0cd9-b0b5-415b-999a-bdb509687af4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: EZK 11:25
Text: Then I spake unto them of the captivity all the things that the LORD had shewed me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b5d170f-df16-454e-a123-784c89e5b1e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: EZK 12:1
Text: The word of the LORD also came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1343836f-c228-4779-9dff-8b00739b431a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: EZK 12:2
Text: Son of man, thou dwellest in the midst of a rebellious house, which have eyes to see, and see not; they have ears to hear, and hear not: for they are a rebellious house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5321be5f-1f08-4c98-bf1f-5e6e64ab2d67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: EZK 12:3
Text: Therefore, thou son of man, prepare thee stuff for removing, and remove by day in their sight; and thou shalt remove from thy place to another place in their sight: it may be they will consider, though they be a rebellious house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee6e1f3b-1f97-4a7a-a39c-31a343a589be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: EZK 12:4
Text: Then shalt thou bring forth thy stuff by day in their sight, as stuff for removing: and thou shalt go forth at even in their sight, as they that go forth into captivity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9544657-127b-4f59-8375-f06983cc913c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: EZK 12:5
Text: Dig thou through the wall in their sight, and carry out thereby.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ced7ba9-6224-450b-a8ce-fff72fe8f4ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: EZK 12:6
Text: In their sight shalt thou bear it upon thy shoulders, and carry it forth in the twilight: thou shalt cover thy face, that thou see not the ground: for I have set thee for a sign unto the house of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd363815-4ecb-4d00-80c1-c976fbae9991>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: EZK 12:7
Text: And I did so as I was commanded: I brought forth my stuff by day, as stuff for captivity, and in the even I digged through the wall with mine hand; I brought it forth in the twilight, and I bare it upon my shoulder in their sight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f1f8bac-74f9-4f61-a85e-b091283d48c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: EZK 12:8
Text: And in the morning came the word of the LORD unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9497a225-0d99-457d-8b4a-bbb307af2ed2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: EZK 12:9
Text: Son of man, hath not the house of Israel, the rebellious house, said unto thee, What doest thou?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02c4b0f6-3459-4347-9cf4-5450a62a2086>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: EZK 12:10
Text: Say thou unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; This burden concerneth the prince in Jerusalem, and all the house of Israel that are among them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a034f687-b01e-40b9-8068-36518523a000>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: EZK 12:11
Text: Say, I am your sign: like as I have done, so shall it be done unto them: they shall remove and go into captivity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7ffecd7-aa13-4c61-a16e-d839042b2cd3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: EZK 12:12
Text: And the prince that is among them shall bear upon his shoulder in the twilight, and shall go forth: they shall dig through the wall to carry out thereby: he shall cover his face, that he see not the ground with his eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e1f4319-7f7d-4a57-8f6c-98d439b95419>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: EZK 12:13
Text: My net also will I spread upon him, and he shall be taken in my snare: and I will bring him to Babylon to the land of the Chaldeans; yet shall he not see it, though he shall die there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9982e8a9-2017-464f-9988-922ec0452d61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: EZK 12:14
Text: And I will scatter toward every wind all that are about him to help him, and all his bands; and I will draw out the sword after them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7835bf33-c2b7-44f7-a602-41b0a9d81a82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: EZK 12:15
Text: And they shall know that I am the LORD, when I shall scatter them among the nations, and disperse them in the countries.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a35bc2dc-2ce8-4bf2-92f2-2d6dd16418b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: EZK 12:16
Text: But I will leave a few men of them from the sword, from the famine, and from the pestilence; that they may declare all their abominations among the heathen whither they come; and they shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0384a947-8548-43cb-a8fd-a8c5be013206>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: EZK 12:17
Text: Moreover the word of the LORD came to me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3b61ba1-5423-4fa6-9707-01a487199258>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: EZK 12:18
Text: Son of man, eat thy bread with quaking, and drink thy water with trembling and with carefulness;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6aed9b43-970a-4966-b66e-dbf1e9ea45f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 346

Reference: EZK 12:19
Text: And say unto the people of the land, Thus saith the Lord GOD of the inhabitants of Jerusalem, and of the land of Israel; They shall eat their bread with carefulness, and drink their water with astonishment, that her land may be desolate from all that is therein, because of the violence of all them that dwell therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ddb98e1-d5b0-4f8d-a592-7189859e881e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: EZK 12:20
Text: And the cities that are inhabited shall be laid waste, and the land shall be desolate; and ye shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63e782f2-8da9-4ce8-88b7-8f78e01dc89e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: EZK 12:21
Text: And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f12c774-7d6d-4eca-b02f-3de07fdbdb8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: EZK 12:22
Text: Son of man, what is that proverb that ye have in the land of Israel, saying, The days are prolonged, and every vision faileth?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ec4860d-f4bd-4a76-b0dd-a2d18caeff7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: EZK 12:23
Text: Tell them therefore, Thus saith the Lord GOD; I will make this proverb to cease, and they shall no more use it as a proverb in Israel; but say unto them, The days are at hand, and the effect of every vision.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8782e320-a2b3-4576-b0d9-58ba77f493b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: EZK 12:24
Text: For there shall be no more any vain vision nor flattering divination within the house of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:731e360d-a15c-4782-92ab-d4457163b8a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: EZK 12:25
Text: For I am the LORD: I will speak, and the word that I shall speak shall come to pass; it shall be no more prolonged: for in your days, O rebellious house, will I say the word, and will perform it, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbea29bc-8fec-4c0b-bef7-a46b81c9cafd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: EZK 12:26
Text: Again the word of the LORD came to me, saying.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:461d2dd1-8992-4a60-bc0f-a40dcb93d5c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: EZK 12:27
Text: Son of man, behold, they of the house of Israel say, The vision that he seeth is for many days to come, and he prophesieth of the times that are far off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/12/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22240377-efbe-414f-90a6-388da9a6a6e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: EZK 12:28
Text: Therefore say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; There shall none of my words be prolonged any more, but the word which I have spoken shall be done, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/13/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aed03de9-98a9-4d6a-bd12-4bccb04387f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: EZK 13:1
Text: And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/13/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da83812c-774a-4fff-9d5e-582eab07a586>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: EZK 13:2
Text: Son of man, prophesy against the prophets of Israel that prophesy, and say thou unto them that prophesy out of their own hearts, Hear ye the word of the LORD;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/13/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:563c86b6-ae96-45c2-9860-b9029b9c4ec1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: EZK 13:3
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; Woe unto the foolish prophets, that follow their own spirit, and have seen nothing!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/13/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cacf1fd-5d1b-4fb9-bd4a-456ed95742f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: EZK 13:4
Text: O Israel, thy prophets are like the foxes in the deserts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/13/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65f3d5f9-d3d9-4ae0-9085-3ec3417bfcf2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EZK 13:5
Text: Ye have not gone up into the gaps, neither made up the hedge for the house of Israel to stand in the battle in the day of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/13/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13942d1b-06eb-4499-a8ce-029e3c523235>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: EZK 13:6
Text: They have seen vanity and lying divination, saying, The LORD saith: and the LORD hath not sent them: and they have made others to hope that they would confirm the word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/13/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68de5fc2-4784-4157-936e-450b43d3b9c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: EZK 13:7
Text: Have ye not seen a vain vision, and have ye not spoken a lying divination, whereas ye say, The LORD saith it; albeit I have not spoken?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/13/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e8e6574-af6f-4ff1-a9e0-d123003c6c80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: EZK 13:8
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Because ye have spoken vanity, and seen lies, therefore, behold, I am against you, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/13/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b84f9cc2-c4d6-45a3-afa3-0785f4771d3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 315

Reference: EZK 13:9
Text: And mine hand shall be upon the prophets that see vanity, and that divine lies: they shall not be in the assembly of my people, neither shall they be written in the writing of the house of Israel, neither shall they enter into the land of Israel; and ye shall know that I am the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/13/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:351edaa6-3c7c-469a-9552-7cb054f6a79d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: EZK 13:10
Text: Because, even because they have seduced my people, saying, Peace; and there was no peace; and one built up a wall, and, lo, others daubed it with untempered morter:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/13/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bdee38e-7978-443c-8faa-35a87bda3a1e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: EZK 13:11
Text: Say unto them which daub it with untempered morter, that it shall fall: there shall be an overflowing shower; and ye, O great hailstones, shall fall; and a stormy wind shall rend it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/13/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42ecc50c-3dac-4d93-bb21-5735c54c2a8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: EZK 13:12
Text: Lo, when the wall is fallen, shall it not be said unto you, Where is the daubing wherewith ye have daubed it?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/13/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b47c52f-b198-41dc-9ad2-30d98b9aee9f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: EZK 13:13
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; I will even rend it with a stormy wind in my fury; and there shall be an overflowing shower in mine anger, and great hailstones in my fury to consume it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/13/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4e2b4b2-d44d-4519-81c6-b86c1ae1d862>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 290

Reference: EZK 13:14
Text: So will I break down the wall that ye have daubed with untempered morter, and bring it down to the ground, so that the foundation thereof shall be discovered, and it shall fall, and ye shall be consumed in the midst thereof: and ye shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/13/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cbc7fa0-cc9f-41a1-a8a2-38e730182677>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: EZK 13:15
Text: Thus will I accomplish my wrath upon the wall, and upon them that have daubed it with untempered morter, and will say unto you, The wall is no more, neither they that daubed it;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/13/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8c82f26-f335-48f6-8195-082cf12b8b8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: EZK 13:16
Text: To wit, the prophets of Israel which prophesy concerning Jerusalem, and which see visions of peace for her, and there is no peace, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/13/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22c013ca-5450-4c0c-81da-1ce8f0e17aef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: EZK 13:17
Text: Likewise, thou son of man, set thy face against the daughters of thy people, which prophesy out of their own heart; and prophesy thou against them,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/13/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b8dc1d3-f214-426a-8156-9134e2be276f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: EZK 13:18
Text: And say, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Woe to the women that sew pillows to all armholes, and make kerchiefs upon the head of every stature to hunt souls! Will ye hunt the souls of my people, and will ye save the souls alive that come unto you?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/13/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b75c48df-9a5a-44e7-8ef9-f46074bd7be3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: EZK 13:19
Text: And will ye pollute me among my people for handfuls of barley and for pieces of bread, to slay the souls that should not die, and to save the souls alive that should not live, by your lying to my people that hear your lies?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/13/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85006c96-c7e1-482f-b31c-631b042fa7f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: EZK 13:20
Text: Wherefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I am against your pillows, wherewith ye there hunt the souls to make them fly, and I will tear them from your arms, and will let the souls go, even the souls that ye hunt to make them fly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/13/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1fa0940-b4fe-4b72-8363-32211af05544>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: EZK 13:21
Text: Your kerchiefs also will I tear, and deliver my people out of your hand, and they shall be no more in your hand to be hunted; and ye shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/13/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a32119d-bec2-4742-ba0d-b32d080ff60f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: EZK 13:22
Text: Because with lies ye have made the heart of the righteous sad, whom I have not made sad; and strengthened the hands of the wicked, that he should not return from his wicked way, by promising him life:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/13/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89013d45-f26d-4e3f-a9a4-795289e3c79a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: EZK 13:23
Text: Therefore ye shall see no more vanity, nor divine divinations: for I will deliver my people out of your hand: and ye shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/14/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7dd71f14-0130-4b7f-8f33-3702a1bea841>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: EZK 14:1
Text: Then came certain of the elders of Israel unto me, and sat before me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/14/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:163141c2-cf1a-4199-b85e-4a3dd1420179>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: EZK 14:2
Text: And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/14/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1212ce5-7dee-473e-bec4-7af778597e33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: EZK 14:3
Text: Son of man, these men have set up their idols in their heart, and put the stumblingblock of their iniquity before their face: should I be enquired of at all by them?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/14/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b0827c5-327a-48ef-8747-7d96b46c80d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 341

Reference: EZK 14:4
Text: Therefore speak unto them, and say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Every man of the house of Israel that setteth up his idols in his heart, and putteth the stumblingblock of his iniquity before his face, and cometh to the prophet; I the LORD will answer him that cometh according to the multitude of his idols;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/14/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:777623c4-c7ba-4558-9fbb-337c238886fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: EZK 14:5
Text: That I may take the house of Israel in their own heart, because they are all estranged from me through their idols.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/14/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b59b3ce4-2c56-4995-adf1-28922e134853>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: EZK 14:6
Text: Therefore say unto the house of Israel, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Repent, and turn yourselves from your idols; and turn away your faces from all your abominations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/14/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a522e113-38bd-476c-9bdc-5a6565abc9c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 342

Reference: EZK 14:7
Text: For every one of the house of Israel, or of the stranger that sojourneth in Israel, which separateth himself from me, and setteth up his idols in his heart, and putteth the stumblingblock of his iniquity before his face, and cometh to a prophet to enquire of him concerning me; I the LORD will answer him by myself:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/14/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:158e5565-59c0-4031-8dc9-95599f5b2d47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: EZK 14:8
Text: And I will set my face against that man, and will make him a sign and a proverb, and I will cut him off from the midst of my people; and ye shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/14/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bbfb77f-e8a1-4186-a037-821ce0574c48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: EZK 14:9
Text: And if the prophet be deceived when he hath spoken a thing, I the LORD have deceived that prophet, and I will stretch out my hand upon him, and will destroy him from the midst of my people Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/14/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7a30e38-30f9-48fc-9ba7-d836c2ca0c02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: EZK 14:10
Text: And they shall bear the punishment of their iniquity: the punishment of the prophet shall be even as the punishment of him that seeketh unto him;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/14/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e50cfa8-1303-4b54-9757-573e34507963>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: EZK 14:11
Text: That the house of Israel may go no more astray from me, neither be polluted any more with all their transgressions; but that they may be my people, and I may be their God, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/14/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74909650-2e6f-4ed9-8056-ffaf19e21785>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: EZK 14:12
Text: The word of the LORD came again to me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/14/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa7ac0cb-7cda-4eab-bfa1-8106510201f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: EZK 14:13
Text: Son of man, when the land sinneth against me by trespassing grievously, then will I stretch out mine hand upon it, and will break the staff of the bread thereof, and will send famine upon it, and will cut off man and beast from it:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/14/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0259012b-3215-4fba-9445-8d2ef1590cc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: EZK 14:14
Text: Though these three men, Noah, Daniel, and Job, were in it, they should deliver but their own souls by their righteousness, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/14/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c96fde8-15e5-41a8-8f81-d34686b8aa2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: EZK 14:15
Text: If I cause noisome beasts to pass through the land, and they spoil it, so that it be desolate, that no man may pass through because of the beasts:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/14/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:015987af-82a2-42b0-af42-5819ca5bf504>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: EZK 14:16
Text: Though these three men were in it, as I live, saith the Lord GOD, they shall deliver neither sons nor daughters; they only shall be delivered, but the land shall be desolate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/14/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0916d99d-39a4-46fd-8853-f800f69db9e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: EZK 14:17
Text: Or if I bring a sword upon that land, and say, Sword, go through the land; so that I cut off man and beast from it:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/14/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c42ebe56-c375-43d3-94fc-af1aa4a9e27f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: EZK 14:18
Text: Though these three men were in it, as I live, saith the Lord GOD, they shall deliver neither sons nor daughters, but they only shall be delivered themselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/14/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b7affcb-03bb-4cd1-bc76-93daf2c99768>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: EZK 14:19
Text: Or if I send a pestilence into that land, and pour out my fury upon it in blood, to cut off from it man and beast:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/14/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37ec779b-6560-47d3-8a4c-fb54852ddb92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: EZK 14:20
Text: Though Noah, Daniel, and Job were in it, as I live, saith the Lord GOD, they shall deliver neither son nor daughter; they shall but deliver their own souls by their righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/14/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a696c260-ae26-4383-9b6a-3110db80ad70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: EZK 14:21
Text: For thus saith the Lord GOD; How much more when I send my four sore judgments upon Jerusalem, the sword, and the famine, and the noisome beast, and the pestilence, to cut off from it man and beast?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/14/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a645b346-b3e9-4905-891c-a6f0276d2ebe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 342

Reference: EZK 14:22
Text: Yet, behold, therein shall be left a remnant that shall be brought forth, both sons and daughters: behold, they shall come forth unto you, and ye shall see their way and their doings: and ye shall be comforted concerning the evil that I have brought upon Jerusalem, even concerning all that I have brought upon it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/14/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab7345f9-eaaa-4c2b-bbfb-d74599c72a8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: EZK 14:23
Text: And they shall comfort you, when ye see their ways and their doings: and ye shall know that I have not done without cause all that I have done in it, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/15/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4897fed-f783-425f-bfe7-919c1113c7e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: EZK 15:1
Text: And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/15/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1d2f464-c8f5-4cda-b699-ddebdd950ad7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: EZK 15:2
Text: Son of man, what is the vine tree more than any tree, or than a branch which is among the trees of the forest?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/15/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:315d7dc0-2269-4e68-84a3-3c942358a770>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: EZK 15:3
Text: Shall wood be taken thereof to do any work? or will men take a pin of it to hang any vessel thereon?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/15/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26c8441d-9acb-4282-a76f-45ee3570f094>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: EZK 15:4
Text: Behold, it is cast into the fire for fuel; the fire devoureth both the ends of it, and the midst of it is burned. Is it meet for any work?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/15/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b678e38-c869-4705-bc4c-e34f54bceb34>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: EZK 15:5
Text: Behold, when it was whole, it was meet for no work: how much less shall it be meet yet for any work, when the fire hath devoured it, and it is burned?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/15/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ab5c7f6-cbe6-4bfe-8fdb-d6e54b68485a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: EZK 15:6
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; As the vine tree among the trees of the forest, which I have given to the fire for fuel, so will I give the inhabitants of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/15/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c22cf1a2-5be3-4986-a3dc-af916dc6e102>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: EZK 15:7
Text: And I will set my face against them; they shall go out from one fire, and another fire shall devour them; and ye shall know that I am the LORD, when I set my face against them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/15/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ef8c545-2965-4218-93d8-c38a775e51b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: EZK 15:8
Text: And I will make the land desolate, because they have committed a trespass, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2603ce2c-e5ed-46f5-9591-b1fdc842630e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: EZK 16:1
Text: Again the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a258a449-2a0d-4e2c-932b-ba66b9f113aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: EZK 16:2
Text: Son of man, cause Jerusalem to know her abominations,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80ed3294-b107-473f-91d0-e5f0ad38f900>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: EZK 16:3
Text: And say, Thus saith the Lord GOD unto Jerusalem; Thy birth and thy nativity is of the land of Canaan; thy father was an Amorite, and thy mother an Hittite.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:178b3b3f-8650-4287-909b-bb56cb5898e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: EZK 16:4
Text: And as for thy nativity, in the day thou wast born thy navel was not cut, neither wast thou washed in water to supple thee; thou wast not salted at all, nor swaddled at all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0ada0b9-f2a5-4f36-9cdd-aba8ce6ee591>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: EZK 16:5
Text: None eye pitied thee, to do any of these unto thee, to have compassion upon thee; but thou wast cast out in the open field, to the lothing of thy person, in the day that thou wast born.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3545cfea-87b3-4342-82c9-11ccfba55770>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: EZK 16:6
Text: And when I passed by thee, and saw thee polluted in thine own blood, I said unto thee when thou wast in thy blood, Live; yea, I said unto thee when thou wast in thy blood, Live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfa6d425-34f8-415b-92d4-8fbedee5fcf8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: EZK 16:7
Text: I have caused thee to multiply as the bud of the field, and thou hast increased and waxen great, and thou art come to excellent ornaments: thy breasts are fashioned, and thine hair is grown, whereas thou wast naked and bare.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c90cb83e-ef7a-4128-b777-c30dba792836>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 281

Reference: EZK 16:8
Text: Now when I passed by thee, and looked upon thee, behold, thy time was the time of love; and I spread my skirt over thee, and covered thy nakedness: yea, I sware unto thee, and entered into a covenant with thee, saith the Lord GOD, and thou becamest mine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c18144d2-40c0-415e-bde3-93af9facb82f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: EZK 16:9
Text: Then washed I thee with water; yea, I throughly washed away thy blood from thee, and I anointed thee with oil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f127637-3cb1-43ac-ac08-1bcea0fd8c8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: EZK 16:10
Text: I clothed thee also with broidered work, and shod thee with badgers’ skin, and I girded thee about with fine linen, and I covered thee with silk.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5ad891a-ea1f-4147-b953-6fed6cf93346>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: EZK 16:11
Text: I decked thee also with ornaments, and I put bracelets upon thy hands, and a chain on thy neck.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b4247ff-3412-47de-8091-fd6f1e6c71d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: EZK 16:12
Text: And I put a jewel on thy forehead, and earrings in thine ears, and a beautiful crown upon thine head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b98c71fb-e3eb-4bf3-85ec-8b060ac6ad49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: EZK 16:13
Text: Thus wast thou decked with gold and silver; and thy raiment was of fine linen, and silk, and broidered work; thou didst eat fine flour, and honey, and oil: and thou wast exceeding beautiful, and thou didst prosper into a kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e94e0c8-b2e1-49f4-b171-a72f4792b25b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: EZK 16:14
Text: And thy renown went forth among the heathen for thy beauty: for it was perfect through my comeliness, which I had put upon thee, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15680099-08b9-491d-aedb-4539064ed279>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: EZK 16:15
Text: But thou didst trust in thine own beauty, and playedst the harlot because of thy renown, and pouredst out thy fornications on every one that passed by; his it was.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9390f555-1f7a-463f-a72d-a9429a586064>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: EZK 16:16
Text: And of thy garments thou didst take, and deckedst thy high places with divers colours, and playedst the harlot thereupon: the like things shall not come, neither shall it be so.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35a79bad-23ef-4f0a-8c2c-1f1aae4fa7a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: EZK 16:17
Text: Thou hast also taken thy fair jewels of my gold and of my silver, which I had given thee, and madest to thyself images of men, and didst commit whoredom with them,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22d2c2dc-4488-4917-9cdb-213ad796c8b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: EZK 16:18
Text: And tookest thy broidered garments, and coveredst them: and thou hast set mine oil and mine incense before them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7172c598-3b0b-4e02-b1d8-ddcaf111b516>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: EZK 16:19
Text: My meat also which I gave thee, fine flour, and oil, and honey, wherewith I fed thee, thou hast even set it before them for a sweet savour: and thus it was, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acf31d99-74c1-4438-bf45-a9bc52422b21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: EZK 16:20
Text: Moreover thou hast taken thy sons and thy daughters, whom thou hast borne unto me, and these hast thou sacrificed unto them to be devoured. Is this of thy whoredoms a small matter,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42126267-2904-46e9-b279-b49b7a0ef651>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: EZK 16:21
Text: That thou hast slain my children, and delivered them to cause them to pass through the fire for them?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c26488b7-63cb-412a-a663-eec9a326025d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: EZK 16:22
Text: And in all thine abominations and thy whoredoms thou hast not remembered the days of thy youth, when thou wast naked and bare, and wast polluted in thy blood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c58c4970-fcd4-42b3-a942-4646536e3a5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: EZK 16:23
Text: And it came to pass after all thy wickedness, (woe, woe unto thee! saith the LORD GOD;)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f75bf32-5001-4b2d-86d7-d5f3a369b656>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: EZK 16:24
Text: That thou hast also built unto thee an eminent place, and hast made thee an high place in every street.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d6ae47b-100b-46e4-93c6-77a12040f68d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: EZK 16:25
Text: Thou hast built thy high place at every head of the way, and hast made thy beauty to be abhorred, and hast opened thy feet to every one that passed by, and multiplied thy whoredoms.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4f81d7c-d469-4265-9bdd-f5270b232c04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: EZK 16:26
Text: Thou hast also committed fornication with the Egyptians thy neighbours, great of flesh; and hast increased thy whoredoms, to provoke me to anger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2332b0e6-19db-47c5-a3ff-92a8f04a296b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: EZK 16:27
Text: Behold, therefore I have stretched out my hand over thee, and have diminished thine ordinary food, and delivered thee unto the will of them that hate thee, the daughters of the Philistines, which are ashamed of thy lewd way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e34c43e3-4859-47d2-93be-598164a1be42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: EZK 16:28
Text: Thou hast played the whore also with the Assyrians, because thou wast unsatiable; yea, thou hast played the harlot with them, and yet couldest not be satisfied.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1867484e-f8c7-4224-ae4f-2026508c3023>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: EZK 16:29
Text: Thou hast moreover multiplied thy fornication in the land of Canaan unto Chaldea; and yet thou wast not satisfied therewith.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0d72c37-9b2b-417c-984b-8a311e16dd82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: EZK 16:30
Text: How weak is thine heart, saith the LORD GOD, seeing thou doest all these things, the work of an imperious whorish woman;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11cb8ebe-e9ab-4c25-836e-ac37dc6653af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: EZK 16:31
Text: In that thou buildest thine eminent place in the head of every way, and makest thine high place in every street; and hast not been as an harlot, in that thou scornest hire;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6a309c7-92a3-4806-8587-b08ad6e3632c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: EZK 16:32
Text: But as a wife that committeth adultery, which taketh strangers instead of her husband!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a1052f1-73b4-493e-b9da-05108671329c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: EZK 16:33
Text: They give gifts to all whores: but thou givest thy gifts to all thy lovers, and hirest them, that they may come unto thee on every side for thy whoredom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f31ff731-77a8-4faa-82b2-90fa1891b33c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: EZK 16:34
Text: And the contrary is in thee from other women in thy whoredoms, whereas none followeth thee to commit whoredoms: and in that thou givest a reward, and no reward is given unto thee, therefore thou art contrary.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb015c00-941a-48d9-8acb-6e254f2ba4cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: EZK 16:35
Text: Wherefore, O harlot, hear the word of the LORD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21ea9d83-5f15-465c-a9e9-66adbb85cbec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: EZK 16:36
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because thy filthiness was poured out, and thy nakedness discovered through thy whoredoms with thy lovers, and with all the idols of thy abominations, and by the blood of thy children, which thou didst give unto them;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:404663f7-7641-42db-8a21-253246803ce0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 312

Reference: EZK 16:37
Text: Behold, therefore I will gather all thy lovers, with whom thou hast taken pleasure, and all them that thou hast loved, with all them that thou hast hated; I will even gather them round about against thee, and will discover thy nakedness unto them, that they may see all thy nakedness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c30d950a-ab49-4c4c-976e-fe85833572b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: EZK 16:38
Text: And I will judge thee, as women that break wedlock and shed blood are judged; and I will give thee blood in fury and jealousy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12e587a0-a2c0-4a4d-92dd-c5c5c905d854>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: EZK 16:39
Text: And I will also give thee into their hand, and they shall throw down thine eminent place, and shall break down thy high places: they shall strip thee also of thy clothes, and shall take thy fair jewels, and leave thee naked and bare.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b124e0f-fd82-40d2-bd49-65731a824fad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EZK 16:40
Text: They shall also bring up a company against thee, and they shall stone thee with stones, and thrust thee through with their swords.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cc96cb5-ae25-42c9-b84d-fd50f312fc07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: EZK 16:41
Text: And they shall burn thine houses with fire, and execute judgments upon thee in the sight of many women: and I will cause thee to cease from playing the harlot, and thou also shalt give no hire any more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50f2bd39-faa5-4404-9684-894fbca220c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: EZK 16:42
Text: So will I make my fury toward thee to rest, and my jealousy shall depart from thee, and I will be quiet, and will be no more angry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ba69337-aaa8-439e-b59d-27128bc166f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 280

Reference: EZK 16:43
Text: Because thou hast not remembered the days of thy youth, but hast fretted me in all these things; behold, therefore I also will recompense thy way upon thine head, saith the Lord GOD: and thou shalt not commit this lewdness above all thine abominations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7238957f-5c89-45ab-8128-3406d5ed9c55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: EZK 16:44
Text: Behold, every one that useth proverbs shall use this proverb against thee, saying, As is the mother, so is her daughter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0a4f75d-15e3-4566-a2cb-97312e712fac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: EZK 16:45
Text: Thou art thy mother’s daughter, that lotheth her husband and her children; and thou art the sister of thy sisters, which lothed their husbands and their children: your mother was an Hittite, and your father an Amorite.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31b26f33-7d87-4878-a7f3-84a26745a332>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: EZK 16:46
Text: And thine elder sister is Samaria, she and her daughters that dwell at thy left hand: and thy younger sister, that dwelleth at thy right hand, is Sodom and her daughters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:281bb292-2666-4ef1-ad51-d3e1bd75fc82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: EZK 16:47
Text: Yet hast thou not walked after their ways, nor done after their abominations: but, as if that were a very little thing, thou wast corrupted more than they in all thy ways.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:efdd706b-99f3-459c-980a-9a8dff452be0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: EZK 16:48
Text: As I live, saith the Lord GOD, Sodom thy sister hath not done, she nor her daughters, as thou hast done, thou and thy daughters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5caa123-f9f3-4579-8cf4-d3b3845c9d5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: EZK 16:49
Text: Behold, this was the iniquity of thy sister Sodom, pride, fulness of bread, and abundance of idleness was in her and in her daughters, neither did she strengthen the hand of the poor and needy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ce04289-1ce9-4341-90f0-307f3a21886d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: EZK 16:50
Text: And they were haughty, and committed abomination before me: therefore I took them away as I saw good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c264dfb-da93-46db-aa88-33f6a4a18f8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: EZK 16:51
Text: Neither hath Samaria committed half of thy sins; but thou hast multiplied thine abominations more than they, and hast justified thy sisters in all thine abominations which thou hast done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7450625e-3279-4299-895f-8d2870f1d5d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 281

Reference: EZK 16:52
Text: Thou also, which hast judged thy sisters, bear thine own shame for thy sins that thou hast committed more abominable than they: they are more righteous than thou: yea, be thou confounded also, and bear thy shame, in that thou hast justified thy sisters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8232260-c241-4eda-8616-c2b28f4a2818>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: EZK 16:53
Text: When I shall bring again their captivity, the captivity of Sodom and her daughters, and the captivity of Samaria and her daughters, then will I bring again the captivity of thy captives in the midst of them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f0ffe73-afef-4375-8060-e56fafba0255>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EZK 16:54
Text: That thou mayest bear thine own shame, and mayest be confounded in all that thou hast done, in that thou art a comfort unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/55
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b91f1c14-59d6-4585-b84c-ca1e32d11ca4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: EZK 16:55
Text: When thy sisters, Sodom and her daughters, shall return to their former estate, and Samaria and her daughters shall return to their former estate, then thou and thy daughters shall return to your former estate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/56
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf66b59e-b3be-4b8f-be91-ddfe95086473>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: EZK 16:56
Text: For thy sister Sodom was not mentioned by thy mouth in the day of thy pride,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/57
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0865454c-3ba3-49e3-96a1-a2216626b28a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: EZK 16:57
Text: Before thy wickedness was discovered, as at the time of thy reproach of the daughters of Syria, and all that are round about her, the daughters of the Philistines, which despise thee round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/58
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed2d0e7a-4f8d-4cf6-b664-b60cfa34c7ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: EZK 16:58
Text: Thou hast borne thy lewdness and thine abominations, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/59
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60144e5a-80b6-40dc-bc33-92f89d502499>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EZK 16:59
Text: For thus saith the Lord GOD; I will even deal with thee as thou hast done, which hast despised the oath in breaking the covenant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/60
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2142d37-f3b3-406c-9394-7b58aadc3a40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EZK 16:60
Text: Nevertheless I will remember my covenant with thee in the days of thy youth, and I will establish unto thee an everlasting covenant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/61
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e3a51f7-8354-4413-a316-7e73b4f17c08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: EZK 16:61
Text: Then thou shalt remember thy ways, and be ashamed, when thou shalt receive thy sisters, thine elder and thy younger: and I will give them unto thee for daughters, but not by thy covenant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/62
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f3abc04-6621-4780-a2dd-0f78c9d3920f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: EZK 16:62
Text: And I will establish my covenant with thee; and thou shalt know that I am the LORD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/16/63
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36642e75-2fbb-46d9-b2fe-ef30b55bbdaa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: EZK 16:63
Text: That thou mayest remember, and be confounded, and never open thy mouth any more because of thy shame, when I am pacified toward thee for all that thou hast done, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6f10846-2f3d-49f0-9e79-eadb6b67ec0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: EZK 17:1
Text: And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5feb021-4751-4512-a12f-60629847aa87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: EZK 17:2
Text: Son of man, put forth a riddle, and speak a parable unto the house of Israel;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a27845b7-76d0-404b-b4c4-d240642a9bef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: EZK 17:3
Text: And say, Thus saith the Lord GOD; A great eagle with great wings, longwinged, full of feathers, which had divers colours, came unto Lebanon, and took the highest branch of the cedar:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:870c8974-99c8-4c19-84fc-ea1ec9c48146>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: EZK 17:4
Text: He cropped off the top of his young twigs, and carried it into a land of traffick; he set it in a city of merchants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e85baa70-9643-434b-be7b-e4ca876e8e58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: EZK 17:5
Text: He took also of the seed of the land, and planted it in a fruitful field; he placed it by great waters, and set it as a willow tree.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70e63737-fdd9-4a68-892b-efb64ead2136>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: EZK 17:6
Text: And it grew, and became a spreading vine of low stature, whose branches turned toward him, and the roots thereof were under him: so it became a vine, and brought forth branches, and shot forth sprigs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34930636-bea5-4917-8cd1-2ff2789dca66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: EZK 17:7
Text: There was also another great eagle with great wings and many feathers: and, behold, this vine did bend her roots toward him, and shot forth her branches toward him, that he might water it by the furrows of her plantation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0ce74bc-902e-40d8-a2be-678f1d9adf5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: EZK 17:8
Text: It was planted in a good soil by great waters, that it might bring forth branches, and that it might bear fruit, that it might be a goodly vine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa72bbf1-5fd7-450b-8865-4ddb296b9fe7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 292

Reference: EZK 17:9
Text: Say thou, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Shall it prosper? shall he not pull up the roots thereof, and cut off the fruit thereof, that it wither? it shall wither in all the leaves of her spring, even without great power or many people to pluck it up by the roots thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c24aea05-58d5-4c15-b318-13d50135f6ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: EZK 17:10
Text: Yea, behold, being planted, shall it prosper? shall it not utterly wither, when the east wind toucheth it? it shall wither in the furrows where it grew.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94b694bc-74a7-45d1-9fa2-c0f8b493da9f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: EZK 17:11
Text: Moreover the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ddeb854-3e5b-4ade-bc34-af02ac6f0e75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: EZK 17:12
Text: Say now to the rebellious house, Know ye not what these things mean? tell them, Behold, the king of Babylon is come to Jerusalem, and hath taken the king thereof, and the princes thereof, and led them with him to Babylon;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12a5e16b-8d0f-470f-9e20-ff60fc2aac74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: EZK 17:13
Text: And hath taken of the king’s seed, and made a covenant with him, and hath taken an oath of him: he hath also taken the mighty of the land:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4490f04-b91c-4738-8bf6-c9872d7c08f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: EZK 17:14
Text: That the kingdom might be base, that it might not lift itself up, but that by keeping of his covenant it might stand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71af6a1f-fec7-4e6a-bfd2-cdcb88176b0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: EZK 17:15
Text: But he rebelled against him in sending his ambassadors into Egypt, that they might give him horses and much people. Shall he prosper? shall he escape that doeth such things? or shall he break the covenant, and be delivered?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e0e5efe-00d5-44f9-a552-e6fa5579501a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: EZK 17:16
Text: As I live, saith the Lord GOD, surely in the place where the king dwelleth that made him king, whose oath he despised, and whose covenant he brake, even with him in the midst of Babylon he shall die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7baf75c6-60ed-4b38-8470-316163a631ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: EZK 17:17
Text: Neither shall Pharaoh with his mighty army and great company make for him in the war, by casting up mounts, and building forts, to cut off many persons:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9bd9841e-e567-4877-9356-368ee161e8c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: EZK 17:18
Text: Seeing he despised the oath by breaking the covenant, when, lo, he had given his hand, and hath done all these things, he shall not escape.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16caa1c9-8cd4-463e-8d30-6541bdbf4390>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: EZK 17:19
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; As I live, surely mine oath that he hath despised, and my covenant that he hath broken, even it will I recompense upon his own head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f67b34df-c55b-41e4-aa9f-d78f28b59760>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: EZK 17:20
Text: And I will spread my net upon him, and he shall be taken in my snare, and I will bring him to Babylon, and will plead with him there for his trespass that he hath trespassed against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb80eac6-e259-4279-a09f-6840a21f2823>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: EZK 17:21
Text: And all his fugitives with all his bands shall fall by the sword, and they that remain shall be scattered toward all winds: and ye shall know that I the LORD have spoken it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f731d66-1256-40f8-a3b6-884ba581458d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: EZK 17:22
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; I will also take of the highest branch of the high cedar, and will set it; I will crop off from the top of his young twigs a tender one, and will plant it upon an high mountain and eminent:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a580661d-0673-488e-b270-588005580307>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: EZK 17:23
Text: In the mountain of the height of Israel will I plant it: and it shall bring forth boughs, and bear fruit, and be a goodly cedar: and under it shall dwell all fowl of every wing; in the shadow of the branches thereof shall they dwell.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/17/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7c6dc97-250e-43f6-b61c-215e88f86346>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: EZK 17:24
Text: And all the trees of the field shall know that I the LORD have brought down the high tree, have exalted the low tree, have dried up the green tree, and have made the dry tree to flourish: I the LORD have spoken and have done it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc953604-b8ff-4909-aba4-c03a83701e49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: EZK 18:1
Text: The word of the LORD came unto me again, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ecc62045-0fcc-4c1b-b04d-8d6aaec0e8f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: EZK 18:2
Text: What mean ye, that ye use this proverb concerning the land of Israel, saying, The fathers have eaten sour grapes, and the children’s teeth are set on edge?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a997eac-8e04-40c8-848c-0abdc0770e28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: EZK 18:3
Text: As I live, saith the Lord GOD, ye shall not have occasion any more to use this proverb in Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6baad56-7336-4f7c-a564-c58d19ade93b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: EZK 18:4
Text: Behold, all souls are mine; as the soul of the father, so also the soul of the son is mine: the soul that sinneth, it shall die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bc0a133-5ce6-4ede-bd81-860b7827cb15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: EZK 18:5
Text: But if a man be just, and do that which is lawful and right,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a724efe-2c7c-41fd-a130-391d94ba7fce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: EZK 18:6
Text: And hath not eaten upon the mountains, neither hath lifted up his eyes to the idols of the house of Israel, neither hath defiled his neighbour’s wife, neither hath come near to a menstruous woman,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec9c2e2d-f032-48e0-bef0-2d947789aadf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: EZK 18:7
Text: And hath not oppressed any, but hath restored to the debtor his pledge, hath spoiled none by violence, hath given his bread to the hungry, and hath covered the naked with a garment;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f75b775e-2061-43f2-a094-f148c18b7994>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: EZK 18:8
Text: He that hath not given forth upon usury, neither hath taken any increase, that hath withdrawn his hand from iniquity, hath executed true judgment between man and man,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7a0a028-54ca-4f24-88ce-fffb9834437d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: EZK 18:9
Text: Hath walked in my statutes, and hath kept my judgments, to deal truly; he is just, he shall surely live, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2e56023-537d-4ba5-8d90-051b0556c1de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: EZK 18:10
Text: If he beget a son that is a robber, a shedder of blood, and that doeth the like to any one of these things,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a26a270a-92db-4ba9-bfcc-fef40833e075>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: EZK 18:11
Text: And that doeth not any of those duties, but even hath eaten upon the mountains, and defiled his neighbour’s wife,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70009952-2d14-49fb-bd79-3f55ea3d0e05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: EZK 18:12
Text: Hath oppressed the poor and needy, hath spoiled by violence, hath not restored the pledge, and hath lifted up his eyes to the idols, hath committed abomination,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:555baf3b-974f-4bfb-b743-3baf26d20aaf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: EZK 18:13
Text: Hath given forth upon usury, and hath taken increase: shall he then live? he shall not live: he hath done all these abominations; he shall surely die; his blood shall be upon him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc4751ae-ee60-4950-b87b-b3e560561dd1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: EZK 18:14
Text: Now, lo, if he beget a son, that seeth all his father’s sins which he hath done, and considereth, and doeth not such like,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6375faa9-0330-4e88-ab47-fab269eb21d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: EZK 18:15
Text: That hath not eaten upon the mountains, neither hath lifted up his eyes to the idols of the house of Israel, hath not defiled his neighbour’s wife,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df024356-61fa-4847-94f6-116d0943e1b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: EZK 18:16
Text: Neither hath oppressed any, hath not withholden the pledge, neither hath spoiled by violence, but hath given his bread to the hungry, and hath covered the naked with a garment,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12ea330f-831e-4896-85fe-6fb8af21d186>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: EZK 18:17
Text: That hath taken off his hand from the poor, that hath not received usury nor increase, hath executed my judgments, hath walked in my statutes; he shall not die for the iniquity of his father, he shall surely live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:968a4aa8-5712-4e13-9706-640e25e462ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: EZK 18:18
Text: As for his father, because he cruelly oppressed, spoiled his brother by violence, and did that which is not good among his people, lo, even he shall die in his iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68a4aac2-c6a4-4ebc-be41-d8028aeeab48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: EZK 18:19
Text: Yet say ye, Why? doth not the son bear the iniquity of the father? When the son hath done that which is lawful and right, and hath kept all my statutes, and hath done them, he shall surely live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf782ac1-22bd-4f73-b676-f7a0d9efd64a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: EZK 18:20
Text: The soul that sinneth, it shall die. The son shall not bear the iniquity of the father, neither shall the father bear the iniquity of the son: the righteousness of the righteous shall be upon him, and the wickedness of the wicked shall be upon him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7700fd69-b533-49d1-9c1a-1ce5a80fcc9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: EZK 18:21
Text: But if the wicked will turn from all his sins that he hath committed, and keep all my statutes, and do that which is lawful and right, he shall surely live, he shall not die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d031aa9c-c221-4a47-93c8-6dd872bcbcc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: EZK 18:22
Text: All his transgressions that he hath committed, they shall not be mentioned unto him: in his righteousness that he hath done he shall live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2dcc0f7b-2ba2-4544-bea5-3832ba879967>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EZK 18:23
Text: Have I any pleasure at all that the wicked should die? saith the Lord GOD: and not that he should return from his ways, and live?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:396f0f8c-17fc-4f09-a565-5f2e57645211>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 361

Reference: EZK 18:24
Text: But when the righteous turneth away from his righteousness, and committeth iniquity, and doeth according to all the abominations that the wicked man doeth, shall he live? All his righteousness that he hath done shall not be mentioned: in his trespass that he hath trespassed, and in his sin that he hath sinned, in them shall he die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ed93c3d-5554-4367-a415-8aa4b253c887>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: EZK 18:25
Text: Yet ye say, The way of the LORD is not equal. Hear now, O house of Israel; Is not my way equal? are not your ways unequal?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4cce6e3f-240a-40db-b32c-cf81b5abc31c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: EZK 18:26
Text: When a righteous man turneth away from his righteousness, and committeth iniquity, and dieth in them; for his iniquity that he hath done shall he die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a54a55cf-393a-4ee2-a6ce-c44aeabab2cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: EZK 18:27
Text: Again, when the wicked man turneth away from his wickedness that he hath committed, and doeth that which is lawful and right, he shall save his soul alive.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17ac45ab-f816-490a-872b-99a4a940d491>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EZK 18:28
Text: Because he considereth, and turneth away from all his transgressions that he hath committed, he shall surely live, he shall not die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ff94d3d-571e-42da-aac0-336b5d3eddc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: EZK 18:29
Text: Yet saith the house of Israel, The way of the LORD is not equal. O house of Israel, are not my ways equal? are not your ways unequal?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a1658d0-9af8-49a1-b2d2-8e987c5d6120>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: EZK 18:30
Text: Therefore I will judge you, O house of Israel, every one according to his ways, saith the Lord GOD. Repent, and turn yourselves from all your transgressions; so iniquity shall not be your ruin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:788a453c-6bd7-4bd5-afb3-1a695d0254cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: EZK 18:31
Text: Cast away from you all your transgressions, whereby ye have transgressed; and make you a new heart and a new spirit: for why will ye die, O house of Israel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/18/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edb4f364-8e78-4971-9255-0f9469500ec2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: EZK 18:32
Text: For I have no pleasure in the death of him that dieth, saith the Lord GOD: wherefore turn yourselves, and live ye.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/19/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2db7ced-00e7-4314-8e33-7f5230179031>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: EZK 19:1
Text: Moreover take thou up a lamentation for the princes of Israel,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/19/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2341e4a-7838-4f09-89a3-db03f727db8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: EZK 19:2
Text: And say, What is thy mother? A lioness: she lay down among lions, she nourished her whelps among young lions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/19/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed212342-2a87-4447-804e-ecf168818951>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: EZK 19:3
Text: And she brought up one of her whelps: it became a young lion, and it learned to catch the prey; it devoured men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/19/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf2a2b16-0ed0-4e69-a50b-ab52cf6cca59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: EZK 19:4
Text: The nations also heard of him; he was taken in their pit, and they brought him with chains unto the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/19/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38fbe3a6-92b5-41ac-9261-73ee367104f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: EZK 19:5
Text: Now when she saw that she had waited, and her hope was lost, then she took another of her whelps, and made him a young lion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/19/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f82f259f-a89f-4d7d-8433-ca941d23bb1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: EZK 19:6
Text: And he went up and down among the lions, he became a young lion, and learned to catch the prey, and devoured men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/19/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2e6125d-536a-4be7-a2d5-d0ae47b6f2f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: EZK 19:7
Text: And he knew their desolate palaces, and he laid waste their cities; and the land was desolate, and the fulness thereof, by the noise of his roaring.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/19/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb30dfc7-c61a-43cb-bd4a-9a4a4091edf7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: EZK 19:8
Text: Then the nations set against him on every side from the provinces, and spread their net over him: he was taken in their pit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/19/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6af348b9-b56b-42bb-ac3d-f9110b22d842>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: EZK 19:9
Text: And they put him in ward in chains, and brought him to the king of Babylon: they brought him into holds, that his voice should no more be heard upon the mountains of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/19/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4fccc68-1ed6-4251-8695-f3103298530a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: EZK 19:10
Text: Thy mother is like a vine in thy blood, planted by the waters: she was fruitful and full of branches by reason of many waters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/19/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04a2b2fd-7308-4507-88f1-fb478cd75ddb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: EZK 19:11
Text: And she had strong rods for the sceptres of them that bare rule, and her stature was exalted among the thick branches, and she appeared in her height with the multitude of her branches.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/19/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9147b21-67e8-41cf-9874-84a9fac15c54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: EZK 19:12
Text: But she was plucked up in fury, she was cast down to the ground, and the east wind dried up her fruit: her strong rods were broken and withered; the fire consumed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/19/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13b29300-2704-4701-b6ec-b67907ac2934>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: EZK 19:13
Text: And now she is planted in the wilderness, in a dry and thirsty ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/19/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79eb5068-27b0-41a3-8a98-094a9fbf0032>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: EZK 19:14
Text: And fire is gone out of a rod of her branches, which hath devoured her fruit, so that she hath no strong rod to be a sceptre to rule. This is a lamentation, and shall be for a lamentation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1499f8b3-649a-4ee2-868e-433545653f45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: EZK 20:1
Text: And it came to pass in the seventh year, in the fifth month, the tenth day of the month, that certain of the elders of Israel came to enquire of the LORD, and sat before me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1db153ae-2625-45ea-94b1-412fa5f22cfd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: EZK 20:2
Text: Then came the word of the LORD unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1c564b1-b17c-4f83-aa23-a1eb91797892>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: EZK 20:3
Text: Son of man, speak unto the elders of Israel, and say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Are ye come to enquire of me? As I live, saith the Lord GOD, I will not be enquired of by you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43fb97e3-8412-434d-8a0b-88cc33411bac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: EZK 20:4
Text: Wilt thou judge them, son of man, wilt thou judge them? cause them to know the abominations of their fathers:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a23e1498-e446-4e5f-8f2b-5f2f99134783>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 287

Reference: EZK 20:5
Text: And say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; In the day when I chose Israel, and lifted up mine hand unto the seed of the house of Jacob, and made myself known unto them in the land of Egypt, when I lifted up mine hand unto them, saying, I am the LORD your God;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35084c58-c12a-43ae-a2c6-59279fea535e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: EZK 20:6
Text: In the day that I lifted up mine hand unto them, to bring them forth of the land of Egypt into a land that I had espied for them, flowing with milk and honey, which is the glory of all lands:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3c0547b-08a9-488c-bc97-6f4d8faae333>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: EZK 20:7
Text: Then said I unto them, Cast ye away every man the abominations of his eyes, and defile not yourselves with the idols of Egypt: I am the LORD your God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6eb2bbd0-ca44-4d21-b742-978581f7a551>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 316

Reference: EZK 20:8
Text: But they rebelled against me, and would not hearken unto me: they did not every man cast away the abominations of their eyes, neither did they forsake the idols of Egypt: then I said, I will pour out my fury upon them, to accomplish my anger against them in the midst of the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9d4165b-6269-4513-bb68-95ecebd542c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: EZK 20:9
Text: But I wrought for my name’s sake, that it should not be polluted before the heathen, among whom they were, in whose sight I made myself known unto them, in bringing them forth out of the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02af5153-ae60-497e-955f-bcaf45239828>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: EZK 20:10
Text: Wherefore I caused them to go forth out of the land of Egypt, and brought them into the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6125383b-504c-4146-b039-38823d8687a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: EZK 20:11
Text: And I gave them my statutes, and shewed them my judgments, which if a man do, he shall even live in them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23e632ca-8b96-4155-9670-513841468368>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EZK 20:12
Text: Moreover also I gave them my sabbaths, to be a sign between me and them, that they might know that I am the LORD that sanctify them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36f5e70f-f606-49f3-8b1b-ab03427243ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 324

Reference: EZK 20:13
Text: But the house of Israel rebelled against me in the wilderness: they walked not in my statutes, and they despised my judgments, which if a man do, he shall even live in them; and my sabbaths they greatly polluted: then I said, I would pour out my fury upon them in the wilderness, to consume them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6cd3af93-2a0c-4abc-bba4-6c9c372b131b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: EZK 20:14
Text: But I wrought for my name’s sake, that it should not be polluted before the heathen, in whose sight I brought them out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f924c175-3436-4630-ba68-c9edbd4392fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: EZK 20:15
Text: Yet also I lifted up my hand unto them in the wilderness, that I would not bring them into the land which I had given them, flowing with milk and honey, which is the glory of all lands;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9340cfb0-7628-4a77-96fe-e69a0e43a79d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EZK 20:16
Text: Because they despised my judgments, and walked not in my statutes, but polluted my sabbaths: for their heart went after their idols.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0422f19e-305d-49da-9015-b9874b6066f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: EZK 20:17
Text: Nevertheless mine eye spared them from destroying them, neither did I make an end of them in the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:652272f8-a817-4ad0-baa5-cf0c07907be8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: EZK 20:18
Text: But I said unto their children in the wilderness, Walk ye not in the statutes of your fathers, neither observe their judgments, nor defile yourselves with their idols:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1afee009-b037-4489-a691-808afac529f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: EZK 20:19
Text: I am the LORD your God; walk in my statutes, and keep my judgments, and do them;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abc417a9-ee9b-4a2c-97f3-62ad8a215508>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: EZK 20:20
Text: And hallow my sabbaths; and they shall be a sign between me and you, that ye may know that I am the LORD your God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:527002b4-d7d0-42e7-bf67-52b8ea6fe8c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 325

Reference: EZK 20:21
Text: Notwithstanding the children rebelled against me: they walked not in my statutes, neither kept my judgments to do them, which if a man do, he shall even live in them; they polluted my sabbaths: then I said, I would pour out my fury upon them, to accomplish my anger against them in the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78c59eb4-d006-4989-bdd3-8ba69ea36ffa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: EZK 20:22
Text: Nevertheless I withdrew mine hand, and wrought for my name’s sake, that it should not be polluted in the sight of the heathen, in whose sight I brought them forth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9d9ce6e-b8c1-4959-b1a2-0455fe7a45bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: EZK 20:23
Text: I lifted up mine hand unto them also in the wilderness, that I would scatter them among the heathen, and disperse them through the countries;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f82eb19-df3e-44c2-b019-cde7735b4ab0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: EZK 20:24
Text: Because they had not executed my judgments, but had despised my statutes, and had polluted my sabbaths, and their eyes were after their fathers’ idols.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9642f32-9869-4469-9b2a-908f0201581b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: EZK 20:25
Text: Wherefore I gave them also statutes that were not good, and judgments whereby they should not live;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7dd76762-d3a3-4ee6-a233-b7b3b3ef201f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: EZK 20:26
Text: And I polluted them in their own gifts, in that they caused to pass through the fire all that openeth the womb, that I might make them desolate, to the end that they might know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d1f85d8-f830-4ca3-9687-6b861e30a5ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: EZK 20:27
Text: Therefore, son of man, speak unto the house of Israel, and say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Yet in this your fathers have blasphemed me, in that they have committed a trespass against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6bd3457-e608-4d39-9656-eb53e07f4abe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 368

Reference: EZK 20:28
Text: For when I had brought them into the land, for the which I lifted up mine hand to give it to them, then they saw every high hill, and all the thick trees, and they offered there their sacrifices, and there they presented the provocation of their offering: there also they made their sweet savour, and poured out there their drink offerings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58fc5345-a484-4a54-b8d5-72bfc4e999dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: EZK 20:29
Text: Then I said unto them, What is the high place whereunto ye go? And the name whereof is called Bamah unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:678706e4-6492-4c32-bf7c-bab5ec994d4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: EZK 20:30
Text: Wherefore say unto the house of Israel, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Are ye polluted after the manner of your fathers? and commit ye whoredom after their abominations?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:816e2aeb-fe6b-4d95-8093-d889fcb2a9fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 288

Reference: EZK 20:31
Text: For when ye offer your gifts, when ye make your sons to pass through the fire, ye pollute yourselves with all your idols, even unto this day: and shall I be enquired of by you, O house of Israel? As I live, saith the Lord GOD, I will not be enquired of by you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f994b1ca-ac5e-44e8-8a92-b5d6fa16cc3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: EZK 20:32
Text: And that which cometh into your mind shall not be at all, that ye say, We will be as the heathen, as the families of the countries, to serve wood and stone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1887ad3-854b-4387-8f74-949afac37e65>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: EZK 20:33
Text: As I live, saith the Lord GOD, surely with a mighty hand, and with a stretched out arm, and with fury poured out, will I rule over you:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd051cec-806d-4511-ab3d-0321271bd2a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: EZK 20:34
Text: And I will bring you out from the people, and will gather you out of the countries wherein ye are scattered, with a mighty hand, and with a stretched out arm, and with fury poured out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81a0a266-aabf-4532-b7f5-981670a6eb3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: EZK 20:35
Text: And I will bring you into the wilderness of the people, and there will I plead with you face to face.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e07838dd-65ba-467d-a323-91336673551f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: EZK 20:36
Text: Like as I pleaded with your fathers in the wilderness of the land of Egypt, so will I plead with you, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78f8b662-c394-4b89-b45e-adbda5220348>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: EZK 20:37
Text: And I will cause you to pass under the rod, and I will bring you into the bond of the covenant:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21252ea1-b8c9-4fc3-9bf4-4810baa60e40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: EZK 20:38
Text: And I will purge out from among you the rebels, and them that transgress against me: I will bring them forth out of the country where they sojourn, and they shall not enter into the land of Israel: and ye shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95ad2404-61e1-4ecf-8e57-8241f8edf6ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: EZK 20:39
Text: As for you, O house of Israel, thus saith the Lord GOD; Go ye, serve ye every one his idols, and hereafter also, if ye will not hearken unto me: but pollute ye my holy name no more with your gifts, and with your idols.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1220abac-2a82-4265-936d-7ee8e936dc4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 320

Reference: EZK 20:40
Text: For in mine holy mountain, in the mountain of the height of Israel, saith the Lord GOD, there shall all the house of Israel, all of them in the land, serve me: there will I accept them, and there will I require your offerings, and the firstfruits of your oblations, with all your holy things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e9cab92-4d76-4831-a83e-615fb84691c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: EZK 20:41
Text: I will accept you with your sweet savour, when I bring you out from the people, and gather you out of the countries wherein ye have been scattered; and I will be sanctified in you before the heathen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e084a21-9d5e-40ef-aded-df074f04549a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: EZK 20:42
Text: And ye shall know that I am the LORD, when I shall bring you into the land of Israel, into the country for the which I lifted up mine hand to give it to your fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:784fb7d6-2948-469b-ac34-4ece11de7c2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: EZK 20:43
Text: And there shall ye remember your ways, and all your doings, wherein ye have been defiled; and ye shall lothe yourselves in your own sight for all your evils that ye have committed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5875f99f-6aea-44ea-a793-b4363df22fc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: EZK 20:44
Text: And ye shall know that I am the LORD when I have wrought with you for my name’s sake, not according to your wicked ways, nor according to your corrupt doings, O ye house of Israel, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24002dc3-30c0-4b9e-b054-b517b6b858c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: EZK 20:45
Text: Moreover the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a66d8159-3714-46b2-80b4-2f7dc350180f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EZK 20:46
Text: Son of man, set thy face toward the south, and drop thy word toward the south, and prophesy against the forest of the south field;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff62e401-a55d-4848-bc11-b7aa5f6e4dec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 327

Reference: EZK 20:47
Text: And say to the forest of the south, Hear the word of the LORD; Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I will kindle a fire in thee, and it shall devour every green tree in thee, and every dry tree: the flaming flame shall not be quenched, and all faces from the south to the north shall be burned therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a8aaae4-5224-4b1f-a105-f6351f809e1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: EZK 20:48
Text: And all flesh shall see that I the LORD have kindled it: it shall not be quenched.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/20/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c98ad9df-d517-4280-96e1-c6181f25bd0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: EZK 20:49
Text: Then said I, Ah Lord GOD! they say of me, Doth he not speak parables?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8b8915e-781c-4876-b605-a7a740dc50c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: EZK 21:1
Text: And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33707542-be7d-4c20-9904-86fec0ded2cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: EZK 21:2
Text: Son of man, set thy face toward Jerusalem, and drop thy word toward the holy places, and prophesy against the land of Israel,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:623cfb71-b3cf-4616-b409-63b2bfde8cc8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: EZK 21:3
Text: And say to the land of Israel, Thus saith the LORD; Behold, I am against thee, and will draw forth my sword out of his sheath, and will cut off from thee the righteous and the wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d824c3f-edd6-47fe-b018-5d99053da232>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: EZK 21:4
Text: Seeing then that I will cut off from thee the righteous and the wicked, therefore shall my sword go forth out of his sheath against all flesh from the south to the north:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e0d2d63-d166-44c3-bf87-7c3974601030>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: EZK 21:5
Text: That all flesh may know that I the LORD have drawn forth my sword out of his sheath: it shall not return any more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16680d59-0d03-4be5-9237-9f7134aca64f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: EZK 21:6
Text: Sigh therefore, thou son of man, with the breaking of thy loins; and with bitterness sigh before their eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6dfb4f87-a4bb-4781-b64e-b4a27ef4dcd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 348

Reference: EZK 21:7
Text: And it shall be, when they say unto thee, Wherefore sighest thou? that thou shalt answer, For the tidings; because it cometh: and every heart shall melt, and all hands shall be feeble, and every spirit shall faint, and all knees shall be weak as water: behold, it cometh, and shall be brought to pass, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a7718b7-4d69-40a9-80e7-2152c844bb74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: EZK 21:8
Text: Again the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:813a5fbf-ce81-4a97-9763-eb2c2c6754ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: EZK 21:9
Text: Son of man, prophesy, and say, Thus saith the LORD; Say, A sword, a sword is sharpened, and also furbished:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:724eded8-6ddc-4d83-b668-da4dacc8e134>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: EZK 21:10
Text: It is sharpened to make a sore slaughter; it is furbished that it may glitter: should we then make mirth? it contemneth the rod of my son, as every tree.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db7f6653-761d-4891-a007-c1def1c1b275>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: EZK 21:11
Text: And he hath given it to be furbished, that it may be handled: this sword is sharpened, and it is furbished, to give it into the hand of the slayer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9e3c7bf-c41e-430b-bff6-af2a6e8a9f49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: EZK 21:12
Text: Cry and howl, son of man: for it shall be upon my people, it shall be upon all the princes of Israel: terrors by reason of the sword shall be upon my people: smite therefore upon thy thigh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dabd8e83-49a8-47fd-b88b-113a27c2f292>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: EZK 21:13
Text: Because it is a trial, and what if the sword contemn even the rod? it shall be no more, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74614927-9f9f-4a07-8c70-fd3f2eb2a252>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: EZK 21:14
Text: Thou therefore, son of man, prophesy, and smite thine hands together, and let the sword be doubled the third time, the sword of the slain: it is the sword of the great men that are slain, which entereth into their privy chambers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50ff32a2-7364-4589-ad1a-885bb0f5d38f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: EZK 21:15
Text: I have set the point of the sword against all their gates, that their heart may faint, and their ruins be multiplied: ah! it is made bright, it is wrapped up for the slaughter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6e335da-f481-4bdf-86c6-8fc35db7dc10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: EZK 21:16
Text: Go thee one way or other, either on the right hand, or on the left, whithersoever thy face is set.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:536355b2-0189-441d-a63d-ce9a94026bc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: EZK 21:17
Text: I will also smite mine hands together, and I will cause my fury to rest: I the LORD have said it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a64d73d0-2091-4737-89ee-127aaae31155>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: EZK 21:18
Text: The word of the LORD came unto me again, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb832ed5-32a6-410f-a15d-5d5ff912960e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: EZK 21:19
Text: Also, thou son of man, appoint thee two ways, that the sword of the king of Babylon may come: both twain shall come forth out of one land: and choose thou a place, choose it at the head of the way to the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d00bc897-e3f3-474c-9a03-8e06b9eb70f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: EZK 21:20
Text: Appoint a way, that the sword may come to Rabbath of the Ammonites, and to Judah in Jerusalem the defenced.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:885f8168-a78e-446e-ad34-610566f5495d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: EZK 21:21
Text: For the king of Babylon stood at the parting of the way, at the head of the two ways, to use divination: he made his arrows bright, he consulted with images, he looked in the liver.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc8a313f-1f0c-47f6-a1f8-1f4f66813ebe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: EZK 21:22
Text: At his right hand was the divination for Jerusalem, to appoint captains, to open the mouth in the slaughter, to lift up the voice with shouting, to appoint battering rams against the gates, to cast a mount, and to build a fort.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e7e3a25-7614-4f6a-9f7d-20645b47a834>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: EZK 21:23
Text: And it shall be unto them as a false divination in their sight, to them that have sworn oaths: but he will call to remembrance the iniquity, that they may be taken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00f18680-4939-4e14-abc1-26ebc7183991>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 289

Reference: EZK 21:24
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Because ye have made your iniquity to be remembered, in that your transgressions are discovered, so that in all your doings your sins do appear; because, I say, that ye are come to remembrance, ye shall be taken with the hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffd3d3a4-cc51-44ab-bb73-34ad1d93b09d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: EZK 21:25
Text: And thou, profane wicked prince of Israel, whose day is come, when iniquity shall have an end,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0be5d7e9-ee55-46e3-a82f-e26eb0c50878>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: EZK 21:26
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; Remove the diadem, and take off the crown: this shall not be the same: exalt him that is low, and abase him that is high.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c5a7293-a731-4a0c-a96d-ef186a1b1756>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: EZK 21:27
Text: I will overturn, overturn, overturn, it: and it shall be no more, until he come whose right it is; and I will give it him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a32510a-8355-4652-bfd4-9ce3077ced9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: EZK 21:28
Text: And thou, son of man, prophesy and say, Thus saith the Lord GOD concerning the Ammonites, and concerning their reproach; even say thou, The sword, the sword is drawn: for the slaughter it is furbished, to consume because of the glittering:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2655b03e-fb66-4e52-bb92-541d744cdb7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: EZK 21:29
Text: Whiles they see vanity unto thee, whiles they divine a lie unto thee, to bring thee upon the necks of them that are slain, of the wicked, whose day is come, when their iniquity shall have an end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99ac166d-6ce7-4c8e-bda2-9c0a141a605e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: EZK 21:30
Text: Shall I cause it to return into his sheath? I will judge thee in the place where thou wast created, in the land of thy nativity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:613d6b1a-f7ab-4d23-84ad-e1b648e0505c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: EZK 21:31
Text: And I will pour out mine indignation upon thee, I will blow against thee in the fire of my wrath, and deliver thee into the hand of brutish men, and skilful to destroy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/21/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0f6ac39-6ff6-4b3d-875c-2091ea6b2093>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: EZK 21:32
Text: Thou shalt be for fuel to the fire; thy blood shall be in the midst of the land; thou shalt be no more remembered: for I the LORD have spoken it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aba10f25-cb97-4ccc-b2f3-5b7baa740313>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: EZK 22:1
Text: Moreover the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:844806fc-8243-4153-9836-bdcdcbfa3e5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: EZK 22:2
Text: Now, thou son of man, wilt thou judge, wilt thou judge the bloody city? yea, thou shalt shew her all her abominations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2223dff0-c2ad-44e1-92c7-eb84f701247c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: EZK 22:3
Text: Then say thou, Thus saith the Lord GOD, The city sheddeth blood in the midst of it, that her time may come, and maketh idols against herself to defile herself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c7244e4-b2b8-4ee3-a21f-f943060749a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 311

Reference: EZK 22:4
Text: Thou art become guilty in thy blood that thou hast shed; and hast defiled thyself in thine idols which thou hast made; and thou hast caused thy days to draw near, and art come even unto thy years: therefore have I made thee a reproach unto the heathen, and a mocking to all countries.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6543b5db-0d67-405f-b19a-788f5b08fcb0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: EZK 22:5
Text: Those that be near, and those that be far from thee, shall mock thee, which art infamous and much vexed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f1f6aaa-a437-470b-8d68-ad16cb9288c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: EZK 22:6
Text: Behold, the princes of Israel, every one were in thee to their power to shed blood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53fd7383-93cf-4b10-82f7-aad886d06d02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: EZK 22:7
Text: In thee have they set light by father and mother: in the midst of thee have they dealt by oppression with the stranger: in thee have they vexed the fatherless and the widow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:caee9fcf-ab66-4057-b61f-2ce1dd245c33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: EZK 22:8
Text: Thou hast despised mine holy things, and hast profaned my sabbaths.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0dda65ab-94ea-4857-b0be-3d403b0f40ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EZK 22:9
Text: In thee are men that carry tales to shed blood: and in thee they eat upon the mountains: in the midst of thee they commit lewdness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb9e346f-feaa-40ba-8ac3-a9200755a524>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: EZK 22:10
Text: In thee have they discovered their fathers’ nakedness: in thee have they humbled her that was set apart for pollution.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:586fb726-aecc-491f-bc1a-5b708b5a104c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: EZK 22:11
Text: And one hath committed abomination with his neighbour’s wife; and another hath lewdly defiled his daughter in law; and another in thee hath humbled his sister, his father’s daughter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e802483d-15ec-49de-98dc-3414bf429dcc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: EZK 22:12
Text: In thee have they taken gifts to shed blood; thou hast taken usury and increase, and thou hast greedily gained of thy neighbours by extortion, and hast forgotten me, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de2bba41-00de-4b47-a850-f75ca581b574>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: EZK 22:13
Text: Behold, therefore I have smitten mine hand at thy dishonest gain which thou hast made, and at thy blood which hath been in the midst of thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00f89d3a-1b37-4e2c-862b-140d27b0ea49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: EZK 22:14
Text: Can thine heart endure, or can thine hands be strong, in the days that I shall deal with thee? I the LORD have spoken it, and will do it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2e709a1-16b7-4576-808c-0b20fe4aa177>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: EZK 22:15
Text: And I will scatter thee among the heathen, and disperse thee in the countries, and will consume thy filthiness out of thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68b4c22b-834c-4e86-8901-6e08b6896a04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: EZK 22:16
Text: And thou shalt take thine inheritance in thyself in the sight of the heathen, and thou shalt know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9b5a6f2-b1c4-4437-8653-e39f3c930c98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: EZK 22:17
Text: And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c3bf13d-aa0d-42ab-a4b4-f3e67f54529c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: EZK 22:18
Text: Son of man, the house of Israel is to me become dross: all they are brass, and tin, and iron, and lead, in the midst of the furnace; they are even the dross of silver.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5395570-f967-475f-980c-c418858fe4b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EZK 22:19
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Because ye are all become dross, behold, therefore I will gather you into the midst of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5ce5efe-27ed-4ed9-a8d4-9c9c6f015762>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: EZK 22:20
Text: As they gather silver, and brass, and iron, and lead, and tin, into the midst of the furnace, to blow the fire upon it, to melt it; so will I gather you in mine anger and in my fury, and I will leave you there, and melt you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ed8ebe2-1037-413e-adc2-e746a08018f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: EZK 22:21
Text: Yea, I will gather you, and blow upon you in the fire of my wrath, and ye shall be melted in the midst therof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eab3fe3a-8fc2-4477-931e-dbb37e270b6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: EZK 22:22
Text: As silver is melted in the midst of the furnace, so shall ye be melted in the midst thereof; and ye shall know that I the LORD have poured out my fury upon you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c70e83d-db35-4ff5-be2b-de0bdf0a5a0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: EZK 22:23
Text: And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d62a6fd6-eee2-4a70-8ddf-250dd2bb80ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: EZK 22:24
Text: Son of man, say unto her, Thou art the land that is not cleansed, nor rained upon in the day of indignation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc4a9bc1-6dc9-4996-918f-27e48174272f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: EZK 22:25
Text: There is a conspiracy of her prophets in the midst thereof, like a roaring lion ravening the prey; they have devoured souls; they have taken the treasure and precious things; they have made her many widows in the midst thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a3675d5-75e7-484e-baba-711baeee4205>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 298

Reference: EZK 22:26
Text: Her priests have violated my law, and have profaned mine holy things: they have put no difference between the holy and profane, neither have they shewed difference between the unclean and the clean, and have hid their eyes from my sabbaths, and I am profaned among them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a4b1aec-a68e-4cd0-9e71-9390ef5e0eef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: EZK 22:27
Text: Her princes in the midst thereof are like wolves ravening the prey, to shed blood, and to destroy souls, to get dishonest gain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1c26776-31c5-448a-9a71-c7ff825cefab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: EZK 22:28
Text: And her prophets have daubed them with untempered morter, seeing vanity, and divining lies unto them, saying, Thus saith the Lord GOD, when the LORD hath not spoken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4261c012-b045-4767-b73a-a564162e7313>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: EZK 22:29
Text: The people of the land have used oppression, and exercised robbery, and have vexed the poor and needy: yea, they have oppressed the stranger wrongfully.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d46af5a-6e06-418e-a574-256f325fdf8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: EZK 22:30
Text: And I sought for a man among them, that should make up the hedge, and stand in the gap before me for the land, that I should not destroy it: but I found none.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/22/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:478565e8-cd78-4e75-a79d-3a6edbbabcdb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: EZK 22:31
Text: Therefore have I poured out mine indignation upon them; I have consumed them with the fire of my wrath: their own way have I recompensed upon their heads, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:079b7bdb-d669-424e-92c9-ccd0396a2554>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: EZK 23:1
Text: The word of the LORD came again unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6fdc9b06-4c53-416b-94f1-708ae4d2a6e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: EZK 23:2
Text: Son of man, there were two women, the daughters of one mother:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:028e1500-3899-4140-88f2-3712548c0847>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: EZK 23:3
Text: And they committed whoredoms in Egypt; they committed whoredoms in their youth: there were their breasts pressed, and there they bruised the teats of their virginity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22a83f89-203e-47c9-8f66-6f45e802faf1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: EZK 23:4
Text: And the names of them were Aholah the elder, and Aholibah her sister: and they were mine, and they bare sons and daughters. Thus were their names; Samaria is Aholah, and Jerusalem Aholibah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c44e6670-4318-4a54-a35a-f68cd17b71c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: EZK 23:5
Text: And Aholah played the harlot when she was mine; and she doted on her lovers, on the Assyrians her neighbours,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:413eaf80-b0e3-4844-96b4-026e557255cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: EZK 23:6
Text: Which were clothed with blue, captains and rulers, all of them desirable young men, horsemen riding upon horses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2fcbe1b-e46b-45c3-b49d-79420e6743b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: EZK 23:7
Text: Thus she committed her whoredoms with them, with all them that were the chosen men of Assyria, and with all on whom she doted: with all their idols she defiled herself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74928292-ac70-40da-a9d9-1b927e0e3694>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: EZK 23:8
Text: Neither left she her whoredoms brought from Egypt: for in her youth they lay with her, and they bruised the breasts of her virginity, and poured their whoredom upon her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6b46367-9e9e-41c8-be0e-4be1a000c078>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: EZK 23:9
Text: Wherefore I have delivered her into the hand of her lovers, into the hand of the Assyrians, upon whom she doted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76f2b6c7-8d1a-47d1-a7ba-00a39c43cd5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: EZK 23:10
Text: These discovered her nakedness: they took her sons and her daughters, and slew her with the sword: and she became famous among women; for they had executed judgment upon her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfe408ca-0f95-426d-ab20-991837ecae97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: EZK 23:11
Text: And when her sister Aholibah saw this, she was more corrupt in her inordinate love than she, and in her whoredoms more than her sister in her whoredoms.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29e4e505-41cb-4cde-8cef-521ba932e899>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: EZK 23:12
Text: She doted upon the Assyrians her neighbours, captains and rulers clothed most gorgeously, horsemen riding upon horses, all of them desirable young men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79dcb0a3-088f-448b-ae18-9b7c0da2d373>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: EZK 23:13
Text: Then I saw that she was defiled, that they took both one way,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f990058-4a24-4876-b6ac-e5c3cf43bec9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: EZK 23:14
Text: And that she increased her whoredoms: for when she saw men pourtrayed upon the wall, the images of the Chaldeans pourtrayed with vermilion,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03130206-d02a-4d2c-93d6-9cefb20c9774>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: EZK 23:15
Text: Girded with girdles upon their loins, exceeding in dyed attire upon their heads, all of them princes to look to, after the manner of the Babylonians of Chaldea, the land of their nativity:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55e6b9d2-bcb5-4915-b77a-3491082854b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: EZK 23:16
Text: And as soon as she saw them with her eyes, she doted upon them, and sent messengers unto them into Chaldea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40a355af-6c1e-4045-89b3-395e3fb811b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: EZK 23:17
Text: And the Babylonians came to her into the bed of love, and they defiled her with their whoredom, and she was polluted with them, and her mind was alienated from them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed6831c6-4c22-451d-b471-7f712b50ad67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: EZK 23:18
Text: So she discovered her whoredoms, and discovered her nakedness: then my mind was alienated from her, like as my mind was alienated from her sister.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22feb425-e254-4bf5-b1bf-6489e24240eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: EZK 23:19
Text: Yet she multiplied her whoredoms, in calling to remembrance the days of her youth, wherein she had played the harlot in the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28156b6f-124b-485c-bf56-df57ce9cb5e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: EZK 23:20
Text: For she doted upon their paramours, whose flesh is as the flesh of asses, and whose issue is like the issue of horses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b2afe88-3601-4859-9e45-cc4b25f07e81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: EZK 23:21
Text: Thus thou calledst to remembrance the lewdness of thy youth, in bruising thy teats by the Egyptians for the paps of thy youth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d62791de-be08-4f6c-a67a-70587d62a5f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: EZK 23:22
Text: Therefore, O Aholibah, thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I will raise up thy lovers against thee, from whom thy mind is alienated, and I will bring them against thee on every side;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4a49120-253c-453f-aeef-701d041bd369>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: EZK 23:23
Text: The Babylonians, and all the Chaldeans, Pekod, and Shoa, and Koa, and all the Assyrians with them: all of them desirable young men, captains and rulers, great lords and renowned, all of them riding upon horses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00d170e9-1964-48b7-8ddb-ad10463051d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 292

Reference: EZK 23:24
Text: And they shall come against thee with chariots, wagons, and wheels, and with an assembly of people, which shall set against thee buckler and shield and helmet round about: and I will set judgment before them, and they shall judge thee according to their judgments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54eb9cdd-8fdd-459f-898c-a7785069b34c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 287

Reference: EZK 23:25
Text: And I will set my jealousy against thee, and they shall deal furiously with thee: they shall take away thy nose and thine ears; and thy remnant shall fall by the sword: they shall take thy sons and thy daughters; and thy residue shall be devoured by the fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d06180fd-3c8c-4acc-8036-a20679f1c38f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: EZK 23:26
Text: They shall also strip thee out of thy clothes, and take away thy fair jewels.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:586f547e-e8a0-4136-9b35-ce59701ba0e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: EZK 23:27
Text: Thus will I make thy lewdness to cease from thee, and thy whoredom brought from the land of Egypt: so that thou shalt not lift up thine eyes unto them, nor remember Egypt any more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65cbee26-277e-427d-84d9-26ecd99f8eb1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: EZK 23:28
Text: For thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I will deliver thee into the hand of them whom thou hatest, into the hand of them from whom thy mind is alienated:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46d432f8-d90e-45fe-acba-8b38a0648788>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: EZK 23:29
Text: And they shall deal with thee hatefully, and shall take away all thy labour, and shall leave thee naked and bare: and the nakedness of thy whoredoms shall be discovered, both thy lewdness and thy whoredoms.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8bdc7229-4a6a-4aa1-a0e8-2ca98bcbc4e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: EZK 23:30
Text: I will do these things unto thee, because thou hast gone a whoring after the heathen, and because thou art polluted with their idols.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eba77cb6-bd77-4e46-a8f9-d632b88e6965>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: EZK 23:31
Text: Thou hast walked in the way of thy sister; therefore will I give her cup into thine hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7bdb18a-1bac-419e-a1db-2d5bd7bbad95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: EZK 23:32
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; Thou shalt drink of thy sister’s cup deep and large: thou shalt be laughed to scorn and had in derision; it containeth much.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5033967-5575-481e-8c3e-fa7f080e1d73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EZK 23:33
Text: Thou shalt be filled with drunkenness and sorrow, with the cup of astonishment and desolation, with the cup of thy sister Samaria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1da7a165-716f-407f-8d54-87ecec341609>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: EZK 23:34
Text: Thou shalt even drink it and suck it out, and thou shalt break the sherds thereof, and pluck off thine own breasts: for I have spoken it, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b7efb51-9a0b-4599-8475-2f41c7bfbf23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: EZK 23:35
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Because thou hast forgotten me, and cast me behind thy back, therefore bear thou also thy lewdness and thy whoredoms.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73b95156-bd56-4636-bbbe-fa7a378b4902>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: EZK 23:36
Text: The LORD said moreover unto me; Son of man, wilt thou judge Aholah and Aholibah? yea, declare unto them their abominations;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62bb77b1-d2c9-4739-a632-e053d28782f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: EZK 23:37
Text: That they have committed adultery, and blood is in their hands, and with their idols have they committed adultery, and have also caused their sons, whom they bare unto me, to pass for them through the fire, to devour them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:795df6cf-8c3f-4b9c-8e5b-ce3978cdb0d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: EZK 23:38
Text: Moreover this they have done unto me: they have defiled my sanctuary in the same day, and have profaned my sabbaths.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc462053-f53b-4275-b494-c19098ac7c67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: EZK 23:39
Text: For when they had slain their children to their idols, then they came the same day into my sanctuary to profane it; and, lo, thus have they done in the midst of mine house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:795b449f-2dba-4e9f-bb99-2e7a1a02d652>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: EZK 23:40
Text: And furthermore, that ye have sent for men to come from far, unto whom a messenger was sent; and, lo, they came: for whom thou didst wash thyself, paintedst thy eyes, and deckedst thyself with ornaments,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f9180ea-56f5-4055-9db3-50c0676e362a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: EZK 23:41
Text: And satest upon a stately bed, and a table prepared before it, whereupon thou hast set mine incense and mine oil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae1624cc-a57c-4844-a765-1fe6b4b3813b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: EZK 23:42
Text: And a voice of a multitude being at ease was with her: and with the men of the common sort were brought Sabeans from the wilderness, which put bracelets upon their hands, and beautiful crowns upon their heads.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bf45f0a-8b79-421a-b1c2-f41c1e3719ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: EZK 23:43
Text: Then said I unto her that was old in adulteries, Will they now commit whoredoms with her, and she with them?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c21c977-9cf0-48af-baab-3dbfda91ec01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: EZK 23:44
Text: Yet they went in unto her, as they go in unto a woman that playeth the harlot: so went they in unto Aholah and unto Aholibah, the lewd women.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:754e8a35-3531-4628-b744-b3b53f19b3b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: EZK 23:45
Text: And the righteous men, they shall judge them after the manner of adulteresses, and after the manner of women that shed blood; because they are adulteresses, and blood is in their hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e390739-5f85-48b7-a0f6-dfdcaa28a859>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: EZK 23:46
Text: For thus saith the Lord GOD; I will bring up a company upon them, and will give them to be removed and spoiled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4471ac5-1bbc-4cd9-afeb-3ad7ae465173>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: EZK 23:47
Text: And the company shall stone them with stones, and dispatch them with their swords; they shall slay their sons and their daughters, and burn up their houses with fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:760f606e-03fa-4b42-8172-010bd28f3200>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: EZK 23:48
Text: Thus will I cause lewdness to cease out of the land, that all women may be taught not to do after your lewdness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/23/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76665090-bb5c-40bd-a426-df94e7c36d42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: EZK 23:49
Text: And they shall recompense your lewdness upon you, and ye shall bear the sins of your idols: and ye shall know that I am the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a552fdc3-0c72-4633-a7d0-b0da50f115fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: EZK 24:1
Text: Again in the ninth year, in the tenth month, in the tenth day of the month, the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21796930-953c-4b00-943f-22deb288ef1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EZK 24:2
Text: Son of man, write thee the name of the day, even of this same day: the king of Babylon set himself against Jerusalem this same day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be45d753-5282-4c03-a11b-8ba81da9bbcd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: EZK 24:3
Text: And utter a parable unto the rebellious house, and say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Set on a pot, set it on, and also pour water into it:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:168e0946-94aa-4370-a28e-ccd8113bbcb7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: EZK 24:4
Text: Gather the pieces thereof into it, even every good piece, the thigh, and the shoulder; fill it with the choice bones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e94cc54-ce05-4250-a7c1-6199e2aca079>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EZK 24:5
Text: Take the choice of the flock, and burn also the bones under it, and make it boil well, and let them seethe the bones of it therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee852148-f84f-426b-a1be-241ac39a56cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: EZK 24:6
Text: Wherefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Woe to the bloody city, to the pot whose scum is therein, and whose scum is not gone out of it! bring it out piece by piece; let no lot fall upon it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a58415b-5239-496b-b9cf-b222b60c38e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EZK 24:7
Text: For her blood is in the midst of her; she set it upon the top of a rock; she poured it not upon the ground, to cover it with dust;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fe5eef5-ad0b-4c32-8b7e-ecf29cccf38d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EZK 24:8
Text: That it might cause fury to come up to take vengeance; I have set her blood upon the top of a rock, that it should not be covered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad532b84-a446-4571-8d9a-bdc44b447da2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: EZK 24:9
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Woe to the bloody city! I will even make the pile for fire great.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8aa4ba53-12ac-415e-93f3-a89efc55b167>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: EZK 24:10
Text: Heap on wood, kindle the fire, consume the flesh, and spice it well, and let the bones be burned.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9e89924-2c5f-432f-bdab-7becea8c9e91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: EZK 24:11
Text: Then set it empty upon the coals thereof, that the brass of it may be hot, and may burn, and that the filthiness of it may be molten in it, that the scum of it may be consumed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb4f902d-f705-4d87-a5fa-c4583f46f85c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: EZK 24:12
Text: She hath wearied herself with lies, and her great scum went not forth out of her: her scum shall be in the fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a84bfcef-5f65-48f9-a83b-27b4e2966cdd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: EZK 24:13
Text: In thy filthiness is lewdness: because I have purged thee, and thou wast not purged, thou shalt not be purged from thy filthiness any more, till I have caused my fury to rest upon thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1760f84d-4416-4a5d-9e02-7d9a1767ff13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: EZK 24:14
Text: I the LORD have spoken it: it shall come to pass, and I will do it; I will not go back, neither will I spare, neither will I repent; according to thy ways, and according to thy doings, shall they judge thee, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e8ac140-f8bf-4f1d-a307-79bbdfa852be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: EZK 24:15
Text: Also the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88af5f0b-2c12-4afc-a200-92df3769a98c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: EZK 24:16
Text: Son of man, behold, I take away from thee the desire of thine eyes with a stroke: yet neither shalt thou mourn nor weep, neither shall thy tears run down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12aad4d5-c6b2-40a9-8f1e-bc8a265ccf4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: EZK 24:17
Text: Forbear to cry, make no mourning for the dead, bind the tire of thine head upon thee, and put on thy shoes upon thy feet, and cover not thy lips, and eat not the bread of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:014857bd-89b9-40bd-812c-75e86440aa82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: EZK 24:18
Text: So I spake unto the people in the morning: and at even my wife died; and I did in the morning as I was commanded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4921a192-0360-45b5-98f6-af7a76450aff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: EZK 24:19
Text: And the people said unto me, Wilt thou not tell us what these things are to us, that thou doest so?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1eb6dc13-ce21-43aa-8591-52e2f7ee74a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: EZK 24:20
Text: Then I answered them, The word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b02f3236-f9db-4ece-bfca-51269bcb1218>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 289

Reference: EZK 24:21
Text: Speak unto the house of Israel, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I will profane my sanctuary, the excellency of your strength, the desire of your eyes, and that which your soul pitieth; and your sons and your daughters whom ye have left shall fall by the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:555cf93d-caf5-40e7-815f-40785f984989>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: EZK 24:22
Text: And ye shall do as I have done: ye shall not cover your lips, nor eat the bread of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f79ea2f-7365-4f45-a3ea-f62b56424814>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: EZK 24:23
Text: And your tires shall be upon your heads, and your shoes upon your feet: ye shall not mourn nor weep; but ye shall pine away for your iniquities, and mourn one toward another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2639011f-b76e-4752-b3af-5baf87db4e46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: EZK 24:24
Text: Thus Ezekiel is unto you a sign: according to all that he hath done shall ye do: and when this cometh, ye shall know that I am the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f56450af-8e50-41bf-bb6d-7c2a56892777>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: EZK 24:25
Text: Also, thou son of man, shall it not be in the day when I take from them their strength, the joy of their glory, the desire of their eyes, and that whereupon they set their minds, their sons and their daughters,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1a97f88-2073-4c4c-a71d-ec3b19bd2f74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: EZK 24:26
Text: That he that escapeth in that day shall come unto thee, to cause thee to hear it with thine ears?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/24/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6842082-8d8f-4589-a0eb-0cd57fe5a8aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: EZK 24:27
Text: In that day shall thy mouth be opened to him which is escaped, and thou shalt speak, and be no more dumb: and thou shalt be a sign unto them; and they shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/25/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bc8c638-b4f3-49dd-9b9e-7f62f022433d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: EZK 25:1
Text: The word of the LORD came again unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/25/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57bd3131-e63b-41de-bb68-2efc0008da33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: EZK 25:2
Text: Son of man, set thy face against the Ammonites, and prophesy against them;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/25/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d164a46-ba85-4d78-8d9d-7b1bf1ee1eaa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 297

Reference: EZK 25:3
Text: And say unto the Ammonites, Hear the word of the Lord GOD; Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because thou saidst, Aha, against my sanctuary, when it was profaned; and against the land of Israel, when it was desolate; and against the house of Judah, when they went into captivity;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/25/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbe94bb4-fe8a-46ab-9b0c-0904d492749e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: EZK 25:4
Text: Behold, therefore I will deliver thee to the men of the east for a possession, and they shall set their palaces in thee, and make their dwellings in thee: they shall eat thy fruit, and they shall drink thy milk.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/25/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64f6a854-54c5-498e-b51a-74703ffa0542>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: EZK 25:5
Text: And I will make Rabbah a stable for camels, and the Ammonites a couching place for flocks: and ye shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/25/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d8cdaa2-1601-4bd3-880a-f86c7274a438>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: EZK 25:6
Text: For thus saith the Lord GOD; Because thou hast clapped thine hands, and stamped with the feet, and rejoiced in heart with all thy despite against the land of Israel;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/25/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ae364da-893d-4898-8cbd-ff6311db23b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 290

Reference: EZK 25:7
Text: Behold, therefore I will stretch out mine hand upon thee, and will deliver thee for a spoil to the heathen; and I will cut thee off from the people, and I will cause thee to perish out of the countries: I will destroy thee; and thou shalt know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/25/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1cbbf2f-bb2f-44cd-af79-10bff6d43be9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: EZK 25:8
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because that Moab and Seir do say, Behold, the house of Judah is like unto all the heathen;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/25/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8efdbc9c-5ace-4f74-a4e2-aec10e471688>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: EZK 25:9
Text: Therefore, behold, I will open the side of Moab from the cities, from his cities which are on his frontiers, the glory of the country, Bethjeshimoth, Baalmeon, and Kiriathaim,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/25/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67efa916-b0ba-4692-8f8d-1c4ed0df3295>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: EZK 25:10
Text: Unto the men of the east with the Ammonites, and will give them in possession, that the Ammonites may not be remembered among the nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/25/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fe706d3-5387-4e3a-b04d-9137228671b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: EZK 25:11
Text: And I will execute judgments upon Moab; and they shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/25/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eabdb616-19f9-41f8-8283-489a4923c41c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: EZK 25:12
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because that Edom hath dealt against the house of Judah by taking vengeance, and hath greatly offended, and revenged himself upon them;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/25/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc59c211-2ffa-45d5-822c-a2303a0962a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: EZK 25:13
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; I will also stretch out mine hand upon Edom, and will cut off man and beast from it; and I will make it desolate from Teman; and they of Dedan shall fall by the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/25/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:955c3552-068b-4188-83d9-e7ce66c7f68a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: EZK 25:14
Text: And I will lay my vengeance upon Edom by the hand of my people Israel: and they shall do in Edom according to mine anger and according to my fury; and they shall know my vengeance, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/25/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7095543-02ae-4b01-9adf-27ebdb636aee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: EZK 25:15
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because the Philistines have dealt by revenge, and have taken vengeance with a despiteful heart, to destroy it for the old hatred;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/25/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f8b21cc-fa30-4ba0-888b-ed8628f40b9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: EZK 25:16
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I will stretch out mine hand upon the Philistines, and I will cut off the Cherethims, and destroy the remnant of the sea coast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/25/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f694850-373a-4183-a163-aea313429534>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: EZK 25:17
Text: And I will execute great vengeance upon them with furious rebukes; and they shall know that I am the LORD, when I shall lay my vengeance upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/26/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88b90686-09b3-4b30-9496-e8e0679f5481>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: EZK 26:1
Text: And it came to pass in the eleventh year, in the first day of the month, that the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/26/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46283bea-5256-4e04-b4dc-935e0b7ef15c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: EZK 26:2
Text: Son of man, because that Tyrus hath said against Jerusalem, Aha, she is broken that was the gates of the people: she is turned unto me: I shall be replenished, now she is laid waste:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/26/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1df03334-d2e5-4877-a41f-dfaa28e6410a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: EZK 26:3
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I am against thee, O Tyrus, and will cause many nations to come up against thee, as the sea causeth his waves to come up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/26/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:badc90b0-7810-4d29-8ae2-4170babbfa97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: EZK 26:4
Text: And they shall destroy the walls of Tyrus, and break down her towers: I will also scrape her dust from her, and make her like the top of a rock.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/26/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c748eddb-3499-4fb1-9ad7-343523a4d4a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: EZK 26:5
Text: It shall be a place for the spreading of nets in the midst of the sea: for I have spoken it, saith the Lord GOD: and it shall become a spoil to the nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/26/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ade68a80-9b5d-449f-9ec1-1d5b578ef984>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: EZK 26:6
Text: And her daughters which are in the field shall be slain by the sword; and they shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/26/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25670c14-cb30-4d49-8479-1a34138c0a94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: EZK 26:7
Text: For thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I will bring upon Tyrus Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon, a king of kings, from the north, with horses, and with chariots, and with horsemen, and companies, and much people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/26/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:219de0dc-ff69-4ce6-ac37-19bb592963fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: EZK 26:8
Text: He shall slay with the sword thy daughters in the field: and he shall make a fort against thee, and cast a mount against thee, and lift up the buckler against thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/26/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b30fbd0a-4423-4e57-af88-29cf7c902ae9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: EZK 26:9
Text: And he shall set engines of war against thy walls, and with his axes he shall break down thy towers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/26/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60555dc5-8952-4a3b-8fc3-d885b066b785>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: EZK 26:10
Text: By reason of the abundance of his horses their dust shall cover thee: thy walls shall shake at the noise of the horsemen, and of the wheels, and of the chariots, when he shall enter into thy gates, as men enter into a city wherein is made a breach.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/26/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0dc4a2ab-eb3e-422a-9155-3b79303d9efa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: EZK 26:11
Text: With the hoofs of his horses shall he tread down all thy streets: he shall slay thy people by the sword, and thy strong garrisons shall go down to the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/26/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95953d14-ede4-4f6b-9249-e90fe99dc61e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: EZK 26:12
Text: And they shall make a spoil of thy riches, and make a prey of thy merchandise: and they shall break down thy walls, and destroy thy pleasant houses: and they shall lay thy stones and thy timber and thy dust in the midst of the water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/26/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46255678-b876-46e5-b803-ce55afe13472>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: EZK 26:13
Text: And I will cause the noise of thy songs to cease; and the sound of thy harps shall be no more heard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/26/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7ad6595-4f7c-4038-bbb8-424df6ffba9e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: EZK 26:14
Text: And I will make thee like the top of a rock: thou shalt be a place to spread nets upon; thou shalt be built no more: for I the LORD have spoken it, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/26/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24d24d0d-14cc-4aa6-8b05-7562e1844f4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: EZK 26:15
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD to Tyrus; Shall not the isles shake at the sound of thy fall, when the wounded cry, when the slaughter is made in the midst of thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/26/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a31b3ef-0741-4b99-8576-f17237ff8b13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 298

Reference: EZK 26:16
Text: Then all the princes of the sea shall come down from their thrones, and lay away their robes, and put off their broidered garments: they shall clothe themselves with trembling; they shall sit upon the ground, and shall tremble at every moment, and be astonished at thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/26/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61f71b8e-3700-429e-b7e8-123d375f21cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 280

Reference: EZK 26:17
Text: And they shall take up a lamentation for thee, and say to thee, How art thou destroyed, that wast inhabited of seafaring men, the renowned city, which wast strong in the sea, she and her inhabitants, which cause their terror to be on all that haunt it!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/26/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c919c62-6bcc-4ad6-a282-25bf3b8222ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: EZK 26:18
Text: Now shall the isles tremble in the day of thy fall; yea, the isles that are in the sea shall be troubled at thy departure.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/26/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0805fcc-e3a8-4eae-9573-79d9ccc8b44c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: EZK 26:19
Text: For thus saith the Lord GOD; When I shall make thee a desolate city, like the cities that are not inhabited; when I shall bring up the deep upon thee, and great waters shall cover thee;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/26/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1465ad10-8f3e-4f49-8169-04a9e45838fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 311

Reference: EZK 26:20
Text: When I shall bring thee down with them that descend into the pit, with the people of old time, and shall set thee in the low parts of the earth, in places desolate of old, with them that go down to the pit, that thou be not inhabited; and I shall set glory in the land of the living;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/26/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3c3f412-ac7b-459a-8644-6886abc21ff2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: EZK 26:21
Text: I will make thee a terror, and thou shalt be no more: though thou be sought for, yet shalt thou never be found again, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9c6ace4-aa1c-40bb-8763-c36d77ea1a4f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: EZK 27:1
Text: The word of the LORD came again unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c66bde41-e3ec-4467-808b-409ff80d68f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: EZK 27:2
Text: Now, thou son of man, take up a lamentation for Tyrus;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df0811ab-e832-485a-a33f-0944a6f53952>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: EZK 27:3
Text: And say unto Tyrus, O thou that art situate at the entry of the sea, which art a merchant of the people for many isles, Thus saith the Lord GOD; O Tyrus, thou hast said, I am of perfect beauty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58807cb8-dae9-4eb8-a185-66dd1a63eb80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: EZK 27:4
Text: Thy borders are in the midst of the seas, thy builders have perfected thy beauty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bccbc4cc-3a27-4500-9785-47c2834b52c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: EZK 27:5
Text: They have made all thy ship boards of fir trees of Senir: they have taken cedars from Lebanon to make masts for thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7efbaa5b-c09c-488e-86ac-9a765f6cc716>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: EZK 27:6
Text: Of the oaks of Bashan have they made thine oars; the company of the Ashurites have made thy benches of ivory, brought out of the isles of Chittim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c0d26e5-be33-45da-8708-3d71bbc532ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: EZK 27:7
Text: Fine linen with broidered work from Egypt was that which thou spreadest forth to be thy sail; blue and purple from the isles of Elishah was that which covered thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:698ffee2-e4af-48e8-9903-c9686d466b7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: EZK 27:8
Text: The inhabitants of Zidon and Arvad were thy mariners: thy wise men, O Tyrus, that were in thee, were thy pilots.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38ed346b-29a7-426d-b422-f0ca8b41af9e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: EZK 27:9
Text: The ancients of Gebal and the wise men thereof were in thee thy calkers: all the ships of the sea with their mariners were in thee to occupy thy merchandise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:039c5ad9-77f4-4a5b-9a7c-b8f82cc00725>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: EZK 27:10
Text: They of Persia and of Lud and of Phut were in thine army, thy men of war: they hanged the shield and helmet in thee; they set forth thy comeliness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c4be354-9521-4135-8ca4-3a65934ccdc0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: EZK 27:11
Text: The men of Arvad with thine army were upon thy walls round about, and the Gammadims were in thy towers: they hanged their shields upon thy walls round about; they have made thy beauty perfect.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df03151c-5767-4e15-811a-55efbc3d6600>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: EZK 27:12
Text: Tarshish was thy merchant by reason of the multitude of all kind of riches; with silver, iron, tin, and lead, they traded in thy fairs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4cebe87b-3a83-48e6-8a0c-a0660551498b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: EZK 27:13
Text: Javan, Tubal, and Meshech, they were thy merchants: they traded the persons of men and vessels of brass in thy market.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58dd06d1-f6a7-459e-b302-fb73bf89ea6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: EZK 27:14
Text: They of the house of Togarmah traded in thy fairs with horses and horsemen and mules.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2773e1e-eb84-4329-9b90-aeebb5ecac9f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: EZK 27:15
Text: The men of Dedan were thy merchants; many isles were the merchandise of thine hand: they brought thee for a present horns of ivory and ebony.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16728860-f2d6-47d5-977f-d3de0963122e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: EZK 27:16
Text: Syria was thy merchant by reason of the multitude of the wares of thy making: they occupied in thy fairs with emeralds, purple, and broidered work, and fine linen, and coral, and agate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35eaada8-82b6-4974-91cd-107a216dc266>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: EZK 27:17
Text: Judah, and the land of Israel, they were thy merchants: they traded in thy market wheat of Minnith, and Pannag, and honey, and oil, and balm.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:623ecd3b-5b68-42ba-997e-9ec3a9b22a1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: EZK 27:18
Text: Damascus was thy merchant in the multitude of the wares of thy making, for the multitude of all riches; in the wine of Helbon, and white wool.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c325b94-865b-4f9a-b74a-661923f92d6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: EZK 27:19
Text: Dan also and Javan going to and fro occupied in thy fairs: bright iron, cassia, and calamus, were in thy market.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72b4f440-56e6-4b17-9598-536d3f78e191>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: EZK 27:20
Text: Dedan was thy merchant in precious clothes for chariots.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:203fc393-5ce2-47e0-917c-a476a2e31118>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: EZK 27:21
Text: Arabia, and all the princes of Kedar, they occupied with thee in lambs, and rams, and goats: in these were they thy merchants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a2f69ce-b075-4093-9df5-6e2d9722d289>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: EZK 27:22
Text: The merchants of Sheba and Raamah, they were thy merchants: they occupied in thy fairs with chief of all spices, and with all precious stones, and gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd944a56-b4e5-4a64-a62f-cfbf614ef8d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: EZK 27:23
Text: Haran, and Canneh, and Eden, the merchants of Sheba, Asshur, and Chilmad, were thy merchants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7868495-147a-49a2-81cf-c5364f6e2eb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: EZK 27:24
Text: These were thy merchants in all sorts of things, in blue clothes, and broidered work, and in chests of rich apparel, bound with cords, and made of cedar, among thy merchandise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19958614-27da-46db-81c9-d64fd96366bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EZK 27:25
Text: The ships of Tarshish did sing of thee in thy market: and thou wast replenished, and made very glorious in the midst of the seas.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db4d98fb-f945-43c5-94bc-ab7ca699f0f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: EZK 27:26
Text: Thy rowers have brought thee into great waters: the east wind hath broken thee in the midst of the seas.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab079afa-b12f-4b82-b353-2d220fc0aef9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 310

Reference: EZK 27:27
Text: Thy riches, and thy fairs, thy merchandise, thy mariners, and thy pilots, thy calkers, and the occupiers of thy merchandise, and all thy men of war, that are in thee, and in all thy company which is in the midst of thee, shall fall into the midst of the seas in the day of thy ruin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6dc5309e-97e6-429f-8cf7-558ac44e15f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: EZK 27:28
Text: The suburbs shall shake at the sound of the cry of thy pilots.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:523d5e0e-41f7-46cd-bf59-48f75475a9d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: EZK 27:29
Text: And all that handle the oar, the mariners, and all the pilots of the sea, shall come down from their ships, they shall stand upon the land;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1237672c-ab55-4b46-867f-d5a8f9a231bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: EZK 27:30
Text: And shall cause their voice to be heard against thee, and shall cry bitterly, and shall cast up dust upon their heads, they shall wallow themselves in the ashes:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a2989ca-e316-46f4-a41f-d9a2879c646a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: EZK 27:31
Text: And they shall make themselves utterly bald for thee, and gird them with sackcloth, and they shall weep for thee with bitterness of heart and bitter wailing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f8294ac-50a2-42b3-8c50-834f11f65bc3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: EZK 27:32
Text: And in their wailing they shall take up a lamentation for thee, and lament over thee, saying, What city is like Tyrus, like the destroyed in the midst of the sea?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b359863-66d2-4d0b-a867-866dbeead842>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: EZK 27:33
Text: When thy wares went forth out of the seas, thou filledst many people; thou didst enrich the kings of the earth with the multitude of thy riches and of thy merchandise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cdcdf122-bc20-4fdd-8291-af6891bb8f66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: EZK 27:34
Text: In the time when thou shalt be broken by the seas in the depths of the waters thy merchandise and all thy company in the midst of thee shall fall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6effe854-7b50-45d6-87e8-630d5a548ee2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: EZK 27:35
Text: All the inhabitants of the isles shall be astonished at thee, and their kings shall be sore afraid, they shall be troubled in their countenance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/27/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc3773b7-430c-4667-8252-68be83f83080>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: EZK 27:36
Text: The merchants among the people shall hiss at thee; thou shalt be a terror, and never shalt be any more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2be5972-a093-4c12-abfe-c2a895d108ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: EZK 28:1
Text: The word of the LORD came again unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08878c71-227b-4e6a-a8b6-d143e9679d2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 293

Reference: EZK 28:2
Text: Son of man, say unto the prince of Tyrus, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because thine heart is lifted up, and thou hast said, I am a God, I sit in the seat of God, in the midst of the seas; yet thou art a man, and not God, though thou set thine heart as the heart of God:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d280dbb-1ea2-4ad5-a560-59d41d346d09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: EZK 28:3
Text: Behold, thou art wiser than Daniel; there is no secret that they can hide from thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bba7c82a-d53f-4a9f-92aa-69e0887eeb75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: EZK 28:4
Text: With thy wisdom and with thine understanding thou hast gotten thee riches, and hast gotten gold and silver into thy treasures:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27837f8d-80be-481e-b4e8-459451f3566c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: EZK 28:5
Text: By thy great wisdom and by thy traffick hast thou increased thy riches, and thine heart is lifted up because of thy riches:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eae7c24f-48fc-4805-b9a3-5df8f3d141f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: EZK 28:6
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Because thou hast set thine heart as the heart of God;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7add6918-48f6-4b10-bfee-1dad2eb1da21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: EZK 28:7
Text: Behold, therefore I will bring strangers upon thee, the terrible of the nations: and they shall draw their swords against the beauty of thy wisdom, and they shall defile thy brightness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4afadcc8-35f7-468e-a659-8b8e35f959d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: EZK 28:8
Text: They shall bring thee down to the pit, and thou shalt die the deaths of them that are slain in the midst of the seas.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8810a657-af91-489a-841c-fa41e198909c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: EZK 28:9
Text: Wilt thou yet say before him that slayeth thee, I am God? but thou shalt be a man, and no God, in the hand of him that slayeth thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e110ed46-6505-49ae-ad2d-ffc48dfdc6f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: EZK 28:10
Text: Thou shalt die the deaths of the uncircumcised by the hand of strangers: for I have spoken it, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2cd995e0-01ee-4961-a14a-025939d2abe1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: EZK 28:11
Text: Moreover the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:727aca2b-3097-4bcb-9d14-812f80edfc77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: EZK 28:12
Text: Son of man, take up a lamentation upon the king of Tyrus, and say unto him, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Thou sealest up the sum, full of wisdom, and perfect in beauty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7bafece0-f858-4c5b-bdc8-21d9cc313e6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 342

Reference: EZK 28:13
Text: Thou hast been in Eden the garden of God; every precious stone was thy covering, the sardius, topaz, and the diamond, the beryl, the onyx, and the jasper, the sapphire, the emerald, and the carbuncle, and gold: the workmanship of thy tabrets and of thy pipes was prepared in thee in the day that thou wast created.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69f77487-52c5-4428-a76b-ffcac62941df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: EZK 28:14
Text: Thou art the anointed cherub that covereth; and I have set thee so: thou wast upon the holy mountain of God; thou hast walked up and down in the midst of the stones of fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5cb4b30e-4dc9-422b-a79f-194fb1f0628c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: EZK 28:15
Text: Thou wast perfect in thy ways from the day that thou wast created, till iniquity was found in thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8396158-0d92-434c-8104-b3f84ab6768f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 283

Reference: EZK 28:16
Text: By the multitude of thy merchandise they have filled the midst of thee with violence, and thou hast sinned: therefore I will cast thee as profane out of the mountain of God: and I will destroy thee, O covering cherub, from the midst of the stones of fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c741802-2f07-4076-ae39-49863f1a7a3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: EZK 28:17
Text: Thine heart was lifted up because of thy beauty, thou hast corrupted thy wisdom by reason of thy brightness: I will cast thee to the ground, I will lay thee before kings, that they may behold thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfae28ee-00fe-48d1-829a-11e0fd997ea0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 303

Reference: EZK 28:18
Text: Thou hast defiled thy sanctuaries by the multitude of thine iniquities, by the iniquity of thy traffick; therefore will I bring forth a fire from the midst of thee, it shall devour thee, and I will bring thee to ashes upon the earth in the sight of all them that behold thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d336f0ce-6f7a-4ae5-bbb9-eb61349aedfc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: EZK 28:19
Text: All they that know thee among the people shall be astonished at thee: thou shalt be a terror, and never shalt thou be any more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53545d13-8259-4deb-98c5-3c15a19dbd30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: EZK 28:20
Text: Again the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2300c778-a76d-4fa4-8453-49e2c937f57a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: EZK 28:21
Text: Son of man, set thy face against Zidon, and prophesy against it,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01a23e9a-c72f-4884-abaf-200630a74263>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: EZK 28:22
Text: And say, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I am against thee, O Zidon; and I will be glorified in the midst of thee: and they shall know that I am the LORD, when I shall have executed judgments in her, and shall be sanctified in her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03dfc48a-cce1-40cb-9413-564dd6baa5f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: EZK 28:23
Text: For I will send into her pestilence, and blood into her streets; and the wounded shall be judged in the midst of her by the sword upon her on every side; and they shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4c17a2f-4388-454e-bd77-14c3d3cf0ca2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: EZK 28:24
Text: And there shall be no more a pricking brier unto the house of Israel, nor any grieving thorn of all that are round about them, that despised them; and they shall know that I am the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39da6ef0-824c-4a73-b1b5-1bf9a9aa6dc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 282

Reference: EZK 28:25
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; When I shall have gathered the house of Israel from the people among whom they are scattered, and shall be sanctified in them in the sight of the heathen, then shall they dwell in their land that I have given to my servant Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/28/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7e1c22a-04a1-494c-86b1-0c16a33ce0c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 280

Reference: EZK 28:26
Text: And they shall dwell safely therein, and shall build houses, and plant vineyards; yea, they shall dwell with confidence, when I have executed judgments upon all those that despise them round about them; and they shall know that I am the LORD their God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/29/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43adc4a6-ce18-42e4-be6e-0e20e6844023>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: EZK 29:1
Text: In the tenth year, in the tenth month, in the twelfth day of the month, the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/29/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c91df65-f16e-44b4-aa13-a199a21436b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: EZK 29:2
Text: Son of man, set thy face against Pharaoh king of Egypt, and prophesy against him, and against all Egypt:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/29/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48ebcf8d-0315-43e7-9350-8405b9b10d55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: EZK 29:3
Text: Speak, and say, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I am against thee, Pharaoh king of Egypt, the great dragon that lieth in the midst of his rivers, which hath said, My river is mine own, and I have made it for myself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/29/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2790d47d-7f83-46f3-8d61-93c0d1fc2b46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: EZK 29:4
Text: But I will put hooks in thy jaws, and I will cause the fish of thy rivers to stick unto thy scales, and I will bring thee up out of the midst of thy rivers, and all the fish of thy rivers shall stick unto thy scales.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/29/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65788260-564c-46ba-8512-434fecf54738>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 287

Reference: EZK 29:5
Text: And I will leave thee thrown into the wilderness, thee and all the fish of thy rivers: thou shalt fall upon the open fields; thou shalt not be brought together, nor gathered: I have given thee for meat to the beasts of the field and to the fowls of the heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/29/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc15f843-2f71-4603-b982-394552ef8612>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: EZK 29:6
Text: And all the inhabitants of Egypt shall know that I am the LORD, because they have been a staff of reed to the house of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/29/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:692ebef9-7380-41e4-ae2a-af169398a23b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: EZK 29:7
Text: When they took hold of thee by thy hand, thou didst break, and rend all their shoulder: and when they leaned upon thee, thou brakest, and madest all their loins to be at a stand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/29/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56d8a53c-759f-41b7-a9a4-5a2e6c801cfe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: EZK 29:8
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I will bring a sword upon thee, and cut off man and beast out of thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/29/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:903b176f-a01c-49d3-9443-3af0e75ebe8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: EZK 29:9
Text: And the land of Egypt shall be desolate and waste; and they shall know that I am the LORD: because he hath said, The river is mine, and I have made it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/29/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7ecde52-f925-4a3a-af4f-de8a0e16a84f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: EZK 29:10
Text: Behold, therefore I am against thee, and against thy rivers, and I will make the land of Egypt utterly waste and desolate, from the tower of Syene even unto the border of Ethiopia.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/29/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1559656-ff44-4c6b-acc2-df038c39ef98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: EZK 29:11
Text: No foot of man shall pass through it, nor foot of beast shall pass through it, neither shall it be inhabited forty years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/29/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ed3f62a-8a55-4788-a0d4-7f29f46b00ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 300

Reference: EZK 29:12
Text: And I will make the land of Egypt desolate in the midst of the countries that are desolate, and her cities among the cities that are laid waste shall be desolate forty years: and I will scatter the Egyptians among the nations, and will disperse them through the countries.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/29/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6dfcf556-29de-40dd-8a79-1d3ce1836616>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: EZK 29:13
Text: Yet thus saith the Lord GOD; At the end of forty years will I gather the Egyptians from the people whither they were scattered:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
