Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: EZK 29:14
Text: And I will bring again the captivity of Egypt, and will cause them to return into the land of Pathros, into the land of their habitation; and they shall be there a base kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/29/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f905408b-a035-45b0-a60b-0bfe11ec4e69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: EZK 29:15
Text: It shall be the basest of the kingdoms; neither shall it exalt itself any more above the nations: for I will diminish them, that they shall no more rule over the nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/29/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7da257e8-a849-403e-936f-264c4a8a8a4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: EZK 29:16
Text: And it shall be no more the confidence of the house of Israel, which bringeth their iniquity to remembrance, when they shall look after them: but they shall know that I am the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/29/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8543f7d8-a4c0-4a6a-9068-c5357602bd0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: EZK 29:17
Text: And it came to pass in the seven and twentieth year, in the first month, in the first day of the month, the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/29/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5501848a-0649-49eb-b829-5dffb6c431eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: EZK 29:18
Text: Son of man, Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon caused his army to serve a great service against Tyrus: every head was made bald, and every shoulder was peeled: yet had he no wages, nor his army, for Tyrus, for the service that he had served against it:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/29/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:746d11fe-205e-41b2-9225-d003895f1ab4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: EZK 29:19
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I will give the land of Egypt unto Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon; and he shall take her multitude, and take her spoil, and take her prey; and it shall be the wages for his army.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/29/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84a5bd8c-f3d1-4d03-873b-4bfcb50a727d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EZK 29:20
Text: I have given him the land of Egypt for his labour wherewith he served against it, because they wrought for me, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/29/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e070421f-cc5b-4b74-9d84-96b3939a153b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: EZK 29:21
Text: In that day will I cause the horn of the house of Israel to bud forth, and I will give thee the opening of the mouth in the midst of them; and they shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b9c8f1a-0d3d-4ad5-b3d8-5d90a478c207>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: EZK 30:1
Text: The word of the LORD came again unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c4df7e4-4757-4b39-8dd2-7478a52e31a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: EZK 30:2
Text: Son of man, prophesy and say, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Howl ye, Woe worth the day!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4954fe3c-7822-4dc0-a296-8e33746f880a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: EZK 30:3
Text: For the day is near, even the day of the LORD is near, a cloudy day; it shall be the time of the heathen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73eb4329-b029-44b5-99c2-8ba6fafeacfd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: EZK 30:4
Text: And the sword shall come upon Egypt, and great pain shall be in Ethiopia, when the slain shall fall in Egypt, and they shall take away her multitude, and her foundations shall be broken down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4d21653-bd97-40f2-8298-17ca080c56ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: EZK 30:5
Text: Ethiopia, and Libya, and Lydia, and all the mingled people, and Chub, and the men of the land that is in league, shall fall with them by the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19df785c-9c3d-4df1-abb4-527f8fde2622>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: EZK 30:6
Text: Thus saith the LORD; They also that uphold Egypt shall fall; and the pride of her power shall come down: from the tower of Syene shall they fall in it by the sword, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca5877f5-6e21-49a8-bfa4-4a1d818243e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: EZK 30:7
Text: And they shall be desolate in the midst of the countries that are desolate, and her cities shall be in the midst of the cities that are wasted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82404150-a302-4a85-91b2-afed6fe92d3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: EZK 30:8
Text: And they shall know that I am the LORD, when I have set a fire in Egypt, and when all her helpers shall be destroyed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fa3f908-e41f-4325-a628-0e1a43ff75c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: EZK 30:9
Text: In that day shall messengers go forth from me in ships to make the careless Ethiopians afraid, and great pain shall come upon them, as in the day of Egypt: for, lo, it cometh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:587df4e4-05ec-4405-9b6a-d64da27d1c9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: EZK 30:10
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; I will also make the multitude of Egypt to cease by the hand of Nebuchadrezzar king of Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8f926a9-60e4-4b9b-bee1-d740da19c427>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: EZK 30:11
Text: He and his people with him, the terrible of the nations, shall be brought to destroy the land: and they shall draw their swords against Egypt, and fill the land with the slain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d33c3f40-3585-47ff-a837-cf73e62ff806>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: EZK 30:12
Text: And I will make the rivers dry, and sell the land into the hand of the wicked: and I will make the land waste, and all that is therein, by the hand of strangers: I the LORD have spoken it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:238db3dd-8e7e-47c7-bd4a-45e47db74a4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: EZK 30:13
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; I will also destroy the idols, and I will cause their images to cease out of Noph; and there shall be no more a prince of the land of Egypt: and I will put a fear in the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb3f0a23-7244-4274-b1ae-7a8d531384cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: EZK 30:14
Text: And I will make Pathros desolate, and will set fire in Zoan, and will execute judgments in No.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa97b714-c3d0-40ba-ac1c-a2cacb8800d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: EZK 30:15
Text: And I will pour my fury upon Sin, the strength of Egypt; and I will cut off the multitude of No.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a63d4ea3-61c3-4bab-bdde-9f5dc62246d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: EZK 30:16
Text: And I will set fire in Egypt: Sin shall have great pain, and No shall be rent asunder, and Noph shall have distresses daily.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd0ae69a-70a9-4115-a261-40571eb71382>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: EZK 30:17
Text: The young men of Aven and of Pibeseth shall fall by the sword: and these cities shall go into captivity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79cc074b-6d92-4d51-8590-c2636a30e8c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: EZK 30:18
Text: At Tehaphnehes also the day shall be darkened, when I shall break there the yokes of Egypt: and the pomp of her strength shall cease in her: as for her, a cloud shall cover her, and her daughters shall go into captivity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46351b14-aed5-4554-b83a-d5cd6f624926>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: EZK 30:19
Text: Thus will I execute judgments in Egypt: and they shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a7f436c-a1cf-45fd-a27a-5c29d4cc5e28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: EZK 30:20
Text: And it came to pass in the eleventh year, in the first month, in the seventh day of the month, that the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af38370a-1907-4d37-8a4e-08e380806b04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: EZK 30:21
Text: Son of man, I have broken the arm of Pharaoh king of Egypt; and, lo, it shall not be bound up to be healed, to put a roller to bind it, to make it strong to hold the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c0ceb88-421c-4fc8-8680-617dcb1aa2b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: EZK 30:22
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I am against Pharaoh king of Egypt, and will break his arms, the strong, and that which was broken; and I will cause the sword to fall out of his hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a624a92e-af44-42dd-ab01-a075310f5f48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: EZK 30:23
Text: And I will scatter the Egyptians among the nations, and will disperse them through the countries.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b6a9fd2-d91c-4cad-beee-a1210d130524>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: EZK 30:24
Text: And I will strengthen the arms of the king of Babylon, and put my sword in his hand: but I will break Pharaoh’s arms, and he shall groan before him with the groanings of a deadly wounded man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e23e083-ebaa-45ed-8ab6-e517710a369e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 279

Reference: EZK 30:25
Text: But I will strengthen the arms of the king of Babylon, and the arms of Pharaoh shall fall down; and they shall know that I am the LORD, when I shall put my sword into the hand of the king of Babylon, and he shall stretch it out upon the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/30/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d810488-be3d-43e2-8f50-f331014e8972>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EZK 30:26
Text: And I will scatter the Egyptians among the nations, and disperse them among the countries; and they shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/31/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:366b79d6-ff82-48ed-8f79-0d17c765a668>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: EZK 31:1
Text: And it came to pass in the eleventh year, in the third month, in the first day of the month, that the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/31/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e563ddf-5bcb-4c8c-b2f8-125bc359bdd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: EZK 31:2
Text: Son of man, speak unto Pharaoh king of Egypt, and to his multitude; Whom art thou like in thy greatness?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/31/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75d88035-c185-4deb-9979-b08b089c744b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: EZK 31:3
Text: Behold, the Assyrian was a cedar in Lebanon with fair branches, and with a shadowing shroud, and of an high stature; and his top was among the thick boughs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/31/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb80abeb-7795-4ee3-8e88-e8dacd5ad399>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: EZK 31:4
Text: The waters made him great, the deep set him up on high with her rivers running round about his plants, and sent her little rivers unto all the trees of the field.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/31/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a21bf4d-4136-4a79-93af-5c3bc17fa534>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: EZK 31:5
Text: Therefore his height was exalted above all the trees of the field, and his boughs were multiplied, and his branches became long because of the multitude of waters, when he shot forth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/31/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a4865a2-a3d1-4ee2-92b8-30af38264ad5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: EZK 31:6
Text: All the fowls of heaven made their nests in his boughs, and under his branches did all the beasts of the field bring forth their young, and under his shadow dwelt all great nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/31/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae347e69-6185-4aa8-bc8d-cbf88c7eb341>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: EZK 31:7
Text: Thus was he fair in his greatness, in the length of his branches: for his root was by great waters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/31/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9bdee3da-307c-45fd-a1c1-1982dfba2703>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: EZK 31:8
Text: The cedars in the garden of God could not hide him: the fir trees were not like his boughs, and the chestnut trees were not like his branches; nor any tree in the garden of God was like unto him in his beauty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/31/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37a80679-1956-44a2-a1e6-4bd04eae0eb5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: EZK 31:9
Text: I have made him fair by the multitude of his branches: so that all the trees of Eden, that were in the garden of God, envied him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/31/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f27ab48-50b6-44b1-831f-44f7fe578506>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: EZK 31:10
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Because thou hast lifted up thyself in height, and he hath shot up his top among the thick boughs, and his heart is lifted up in his height;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/31/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a07416a-b660-47b3-b009-5d25e8931885>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: EZK 31:11
Text: I have therefore delivered him into the hand of the mighty one of the heathen; he shall surely deal with him: I have driven him out for his wickedness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/31/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64a12206-5b40-44fa-a74f-5d79660fe07b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 314

Reference: EZK 31:12
Text: And strangers, the terrible of the nations, have cut him off, and have left him: upon the mountains and in all the valleys his branches are fallen, and his boughs are broken by all the rivers of the land; and all the people of the earth are gone down from his shadow, and have left him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/31/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5606585-56db-419c-9905-55230000705c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: EZK 31:13
Text: Upon his ruin shall all the fowls of the heaven remain, and all the beasts of the field shall be upon his branches:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/31/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98f2c69b-9228-4aef-8850-647444dd1a72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 378

Reference: EZK 31:14
Text: To the end that none of all the trees by the waters exalt themselves for their height, neither shoot up their top among the thick boughs, neither their trees stand up in their height, all that drink water: for they are all delivered unto death, to the nether parts of the earth, in the midst of the children of men, with them that go down to the pit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/31/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e244b1f5-2b11-4cd8-b4b9-43e722b25bc8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 301

Reference: EZK 31:15
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; In the day when he went down to the grave I caused a mourning: I covered the deep for him, and I restrained the floods thereof, and the great waters were stayed: and I caused Lebanon to mourn for him, and all the trees of the field fainted for him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/31/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5c4f6ac-f763-4505-96eb-c520226d4379>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 281

Reference: EZK 31:16
Text: I made the nations to shake at the sound of his fall, when I cast him down to hell with them that descend into the pit: and all the trees of Eden, the choice and best of Lebanon, all that drink water, shall be comforted in the nether parts of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/31/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17213241-e770-410f-ab75-700bf33c5b61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: EZK 31:17
Text: They also went down into hell with him unto them that be slain with the sword; and they that were his arm, that dwelt under his shadow in the midst of the heathen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/31/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be61be22-f100-455b-bd5b-8c685bfbe971>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 341

Reference: EZK 31:18
Text: To whom art thou thus like in glory and in greatness among the trees of Eden? yet shalt thou be brought down with the trees of Eden unto the nether parts of the earth: thou shalt lie in the midst of the uncircumcised with them that be slain by the sword. This is Pharaoh and all his multitude, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3730a61-20d9-4240-8283-0e2a11580785>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: EZK 32:1
Text: And it came to pass in the twelfth year, in the twelfth month, in the first day of the month, that the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86173b58-e72e-45d0-a250-5e834413a3d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 292

Reference: EZK 32:2
Text: Son of man, take up a lamentation for Pharaoh king of Egypt, and say unto him, Thou art like a young lion of the nations, and thou art as a whale in the seas: and thou camest forth with thy rivers, and troubledst the waters with thy feet, and fouledst their rivers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37e2d258-3f99-444d-bccd-1725d4be1c68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: EZK 32:3
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; I will therefore spread out my net over thee with a company of many people; and they shall bring thee up in my net.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ebb27fc-9892-474d-bb78-bda8722e7c21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: EZK 32:4
Text: Then will I leave thee upon the land, I will cast thee forth upon the open field, and will cause all the fowls of the heaven to remain upon thee, and I will fill the beasts of the whole earth with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d9e37c3-3941-4972-ae11-52953b43b963>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: EZK 32:5
Text: And I will lay thy flesh upon the mountains, and fill the valleys with thy height.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1458ff6-2cf8-4ae1-8fa1-4a4df489132f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: EZK 32:6
Text: I will also water with thy blood the land wherein thou swimmest, even to the mountains; and the rivers shall be full of thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:763bf1c6-601b-4049-b7de-8b62d466c508>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: EZK 32:7
Text: And when I shall put thee out, I will cover the heaven, and make the stars thereof dark; I will cover the sun with a cloud, and the moon shall not give her light.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa6e3822-8044-4f16-a68b-863e7eaafd7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: EZK 32:8
Text: All the bright lights of heaven will I make dark over thee, and set darkness upon thy land, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf136b1d-5121-42e3-ba76-a353a867dcf7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: EZK 32:9
Text: I will also vex the hearts of many people, when I shall bring thy destruction among the nations, into the countries which thou hast not known.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:314abeda-21a4-42b1-b7c4-7c6c7a7fb2a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: EZK 32:10
Text: Yea, I will make many people amazed at thee, and their kings shall be horribly afraid for thee, when I shall brandish my sword before them; and they shall tremble at every moment, every man for his own life, in the day of thy fall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e57e0cb9-615f-4c04-b235-12d8e6f82c17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: EZK 32:11
Text: For thus saith the Lord GOD; The sword of the king of Babylon shall come upon thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e7a7514-aa81-4bcb-8c5c-c45d427a15fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: EZK 32:12
Text: By the swords of the mighty will I cause thy multitude to fall, the terrible of the nations, all of them: and they shall spoil the pomp of Egypt, and all the multitude thereof shall be destroyed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:428d51a3-fcd2-4801-91bf-ae39b3365dd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: EZK 32:13
Text: I will destroy also all the beasts thereof from beside the great waters; neither shall the foot of man trouble them any more, nor the hoofs of beasts trouble them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c462d9a0-64df-4464-a72a-877bf73dde9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: EZK 32:14
Text: Then will I make their waters deep, and cause their rivers to run like oil, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35b504ba-9617-4f6d-a156-567a8780ef6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: EZK 32:15
Text: When I shall make the land of Egypt desolate, and the country shall be destitute of that whereof it was full, when I shall smite all them that dwell therein, then shall they know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc404933-aafd-41fe-b7bf-cdc934a71e94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: EZK 32:16
Text: This is the lamentation wherewith they shall lament her: the daughters of the nations shall lament her: they shall lament for her, even for Egypt, and for all her multitude, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1a04208-2e98-45ec-a52e-a28726588382>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: EZK 32:17
Text: It came to pass also in the twelfth year, in the fifteenth day of the month, that the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4cb8a84-0238-4a00-a047-56731959e5a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: EZK 32:18
Text: Son of man, wail for the multitude of Egypt, and cast them down, even her, and the daughters of the famous nations, unto the nether parts of the earth, with them that go down into the pit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:156a919a-96f7-4e5f-a610-2b4836dbe69e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: EZK 32:19
Text: Whom dost thou pass in beauty? go down, and be thou laid with the uncircumcised.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56a5c801-520d-40cb-b1fd-ad91bbc890b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EZK 32:20
Text: They shall fall in the midst of them that are slain by the sword: she is delivered to the sword: draw her and all her multitudes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b90c32ae-7cc1-4b45-abcb-c5ac27dca812>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: EZK 32:21
Text: The strong among the mighty shall speak to him out of the midst of hell with them that help him: they are gone down, they lie uncircumcised, slain by the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34cb0d52-55bf-42ae-b8c7-77dc2f15c8b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: EZK 32:22
Text: Asshur is there and all her company: his graves are about him: all of them slain, fallen by the sword:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b076ee2-d6b1-4591-b962-4a2d546b63e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: EZK 32:23
Text: Whose graves are set in the sides of the pit, and her company is round about her grave: all of them slain, fallen by the sword, which caused terror in the land of the living.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3915be77-b95f-4537-bc1d-2deaea63f1d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 316

Reference: EZK 32:24
Text: There is Elam and all her multitude round about her grave, all of them slain, fallen by the sword, which are gone down uncircumcised into the nether parts of the earth, which caused their terror in the land of the living; yet have they borne their shame with them that go down to the pit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17b2d2e5-de8d-4010-a8d5-f7521a0e0a48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 351

Reference: EZK 32:25
Text: They have set her a bed in the midst of the slain with all her multitude: her graves are round about him: all of them uncircumcised, slain by the sword: though their terror was caused in the land of the living, yet have they borne their shame with them that go down to the pit: he is put in the midst of them that be slain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8556c69a-8ad8-4b8a-9991-c58958a7ed2f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: EZK 32:26
Text: There is Meshech, Tubal, and all her multitude: her graves are round about him: all of them uncircumcised, slain by the sword, though they caused their terror in the land of the living.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e89aa1c-23a6-442e-ab15-d46ae53d2128>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 327

Reference: EZK 32:27
Text: And they shall not lie with the mighty that are fallen of the uncircumcised, which are gone down to hell with their weapons of war: and they have laid their swords under their heads, but their iniquities shall be upon their bones, though they were the terror of the mighty in the land of the living.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f12dab6-e673-4320-ab05-9cfb9c077f54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: EZK 32:28
Text: Yea, thou shalt be broken in the midst of the uncircumcised, and shalt lie with them that are slain with the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b46f386-7a94-4388-88b8-0fff24d4386f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: EZK 32:29
Text: There is Edom, her kings, and all her princes, which with their might are laid by them that were slain by the sword: they shall lie with the uncircumcised, and with them that go down to the pit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2d2eacb-274e-4d6c-95f1-3f9b72c740ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 306

Reference: EZK 32:30
Text: There be the princes of the north, all of them, and all the Zidonians, which are gone down with the slain; with their terror they are ashamed of their might; and they lie uncircumcised with them that be slain by the sword, and bear their shame with them that go down to the pit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:673cae80-2a3e-4120-9f3b-4e2726218677>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: EZK 32:31
Text: Pharaoh shall see them, and shall be comforted over all his multitude, even Pharaoh and all his army slain by the sword, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/32/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a4f88fb-cb39-4f4b-a0fe-133cfc4ae043>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: EZK 32:32
Text: For I have caused my terror in the land of the living: and he shall be laid in the midst of the uncircumcised with them that are slain with the sword, even Pharaoh and all his multitude, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67aed0aa-0a7b-4736-9332-f522c4d483af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: EZK 33:1
Text: Again the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:daef6b00-a1c6-47b1-ba39-b1d5046dd04d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: EZK 33:2
Text: Son of man, speak to the children of thy people, and say unto them, When I bring the sword upon a land, if the people of the land take a man of their coasts, and set him for their watchman:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec869166-316c-4f31-b59d-30a1cb35f071>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: EZK 33:3
Text: If when he seeth the sword come upon the land, he blow the trumpet, and warn the people;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14fc1e1e-5930-4c84-88c0-edc4895f93e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: EZK 33:4
Text: Then whosoever heareth the sound of the trumpet, and taketh not warning; if the sword come, and take him away, his blood shall be upon his own head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a378650a-383a-4a84-9b6a-a6b254d343c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: EZK 33:5
Text: He heard the sound of the trumpet, and took not warning; his blood shall be upon him. But he that taketh warning shall deliver his soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:120c1f6c-9fc8-4b70-90e9-aa89bc56ab52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: EZK 33:6
Text: But if the watchman see the sword come, and blow not the trumpet, and the people be not warned; if the sword come, and take any person from among them, he is taken away in his iniquity; but his blood will I require at the watchman’s hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5686609e-63d0-49fe-965e-9a6e24296a27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: EZK 33:7
Text: So thou, O son of man, I have set thee a watchman unto the house of Israel; therefore thou shalt hear the word at my mouth, and warn them from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:489eafa2-bf1b-4498-9ccc-0a38da7603f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: EZK 33:8
Text: When I say unto the wicked, O wicked man, thou shalt surely die; if thou dost not speak to warn the wicked from his way, that wicked man shall die in his iniquity; but his blood will I require at thine hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:768c288c-d404-4823-97df-66a579fc518b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: EZK 33:9
Text: Nevertheless, if thou warn the wicked of his way to turn from it; if he do not turn from his way, he shall die in his iniquity; but thou hast delivered thy soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38aa5b75-6a68-49b3-bf5e-03fab03bfb24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: EZK 33:10
Text: Therefore, O thou son of man, speak unto the house of Israel; Thus ye speak, saying, If our transgressions and our sins be upon us, and we pine away in them, how should we then live?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38639572-2989-4f98-b21f-265c106b4e8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: EZK 33:11
Text: Say unto them, As I live, saith the Lord GOD, I have no pleasure in the death of the wicked; but that the wicked turn from his way and live: turn ye, turn ye from your evil ways; for why will ye die, O house of Israel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d984d6c2-9d01-4162-bb09-d570a4d49078>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 387

Reference: EZK 33:12
Text: Therefore, thou son of man, say unto the children of thy people, The righteousness of the righteous shall not deliver him in the day of his transgression: as for the wickedness of the wicked, he shall not fall thereby in the day that he turneth from his wickedness; neither shall the righteous be able to live for his righteousness in the day that he sinneth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4e74082-751c-4af6-b1ae-112540f5bd60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: EZK 33:13
Text: When I shall say to the righteous, that he shall surely live; if he trust to his own righteousness, and commit iniquity, all his righteousnesses shall not be remembered; but for his iniquity that he hath committed, he shall die for it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d3dbdcf-c274-4006-9e6c-4fcf8381304c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: EZK 33:14
Text: Again, when I say unto the wicked, Thou shalt surely die; if he turn from his sin, and do that which is lawful and right;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:957ea07c-18c3-4d69-a21d-bbe2899482e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: EZK 33:15
Text: If the wicked restore the pledge, give again that he had robbed, walk in the statutes of life, without committing iniquity; he shall surely live, he shall not die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1dfd35f-a5d3-45f1-9b2d-a0b3673f650b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: EZK 33:16
Text: None of his sins that he hath committed shall be mentioned unto him: he hath done that which is lawful and right; he shall surely live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e61e8d86-70ec-40de-94a2-346b6661b601>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: EZK 33:17
Text: Yet the children of thy people say, The way of the Lord is not equal: but as for them, their way is not equal.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94e7b7ae-5a93-4aad-a871-5147818a375b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: EZK 33:18
Text: When the righteous turneth from his righteousness, and committeth iniquity, he shall even die thereby.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a766f9b9-7747-4a50-bb46-b9791edd595f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: EZK 33:19
Text: But if the wicked turn from his wickedness, and do that which is lawful and right, he shall live thereby.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:638c77de-f1ca-4dc2-8086-34a56945d383>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: EZK 33:20
Text: Yet ye say, The way of the Lord is not equal. O ye house of Israel, I will judge you every one after his ways.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39c7670f-6b79-433e-9a1e-0210cc09bc69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: EZK 33:21
Text: And it came to pass in the twelfth year of our captivity, in the tenth month, in the fifth day of the month, that one that had escaped out of Jerusalem came unto me, saying, The city is smitten.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dcd08421-2240-4afb-af34-153403971e25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: EZK 33:22
Text: Now the hand of the LORD was upon me in the evening, afore he that was escaped came; and had opened my mouth, until he came to me in the morning; and my mouth was opened, and I was no more dumb.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4386da29-f1be-4984-a3e4-8ffc9abadded>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: EZK 33:23
Text: Then the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66261368-6d77-4d6a-a76f-063d9eec532b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: EZK 33:24
Text: Son of man, they that inhabit those wastes of the land of Israel speak, saying, Abraham was one, and he inherited the land: but we are many; the land is given us for inheritance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c66e26a7-70ee-433e-a8d8-04da2136a7ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: EZK 33:25
Text: Wherefore say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Ye eat with the blood, and lift up your eyes toward your idols, and shed blood: and shall ye possess the land?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bde39a0-bcad-41bf-accd-4255594e2418>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: EZK 33:26
Text: Ye stand upon your sword, ye work abomination, and ye defile every one his neighbour’s wife: and shall ye possess the land?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7809101a-67d5-4558-835f-7839182ea896>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 300

Reference: EZK 33:27
Text: Say thou thus unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; As I live, surely they that are in the wastes shall fall by the sword, and him that is in the open field will I give to the beasts to be devoured, and they that be in the forts and in the caves shall die of the pestilence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f3f161b-6195-4016-b755-77cf89cd6480>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: EZK 33:28
Text: For I will lay the land most desolate, and the pomp of her strength shall cease; and the mountains of Israel shall be desolate, that none shall pass through.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3382f9cb-3057-4747-b013-162e96c85f31>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: EZK 33:29
Text: Then shall they know that I am the LORD, when I have laid the land most desolate because of all their abominations which they have committed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb5998d6-46b7-4e38-9b99-cefcc5575eab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 290

Reference: EZK 33:30
Text: Also, thou son of man, the children of thy people still are talking against thee by the walls and in the doors of the houses, and speak one to another, every one to his brother, saying, Come, I pray you, and hear what is the word that cometh forth from the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:771c9842-84ee-43c5-8947-3a6fa9335474>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: EZK 33:31
Text: And they come unto thee as the people cometh, and they sit before thee as my people, and they hear thy words, but they will not do them: for with their mouth they shew much love, but their heart goeth after their covetousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f5cccb9-5222-4d9b-8c25-fdcf043a4094>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: EZK 33:32
Text: And, lo, thou art unto them as a very lovely song of one that hath a pleasant voice, and can play well on an instrument: for they hear thy words, but they do them not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/33/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4dec1a87-6c1f-41ac-b4cd-3a478254460a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: EZK 33:33
Text: And when this cometh to pass, (lo, it will come,) then shall they know that a prophet hath been among them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b792f2cb-0af9-47a4-96fe-e5f439a3e2a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: EZK 34:1
Text: And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bdc45ced-a31c-4316-9eaa-bf7be2799eda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: EZK 34:2
Text: Son of man, prophesy against the shepherds of Israel, prophesy, and say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD unto the shepherds; Woe be to the shepherds of Israel that do feed themselves! should not the shepherds feed the flocks?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c583376-cda0-4f6e-9a9c-63c9a553bc2b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: EZK 34:3
Text: Ye eat the fat, and ye clothe you with the wool, ye kill them that are fed: but ye feed not the flock.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a6a8a9d-6b8e-4742-9bad-f52f392946e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 311

Reference: EZK 34:4
Text: The diseased have ye not strengthened, neither have ye healed that which was sick, neither have ye bound up that which was broken, neither have ye brought again that which was driven away, neither have ye sought that which was lost; but with force and with cruelty have ye ruled them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26ae1925-9906-442f-92ed-8da0fbe8127a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EZK 34:5
Text: And they were scattered, because there is no shepherd: and they became meat to all the beasts of the field, when they were scattered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc727044-d89c-4402-9b9f-bdda34218a3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: EZK 34:6
Text: My sheep wandered through all the mountains, and upon every high hill: yea, my flock was scattered upon all the face of the earth, and none did search or seek after them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83987a1e-47cf-4957-abf3-6a3641076004>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: EZK 34:7
Text: Therefore, ye shepherds, hear the word of the LORD;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc6094ed-1112-4019-9232-34a12072b50b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 283

Reference: EZK 34:8
Text: As I live, saith the Lord GOD, surely because my flock became a prey, and my flock became meat to every beast of the field, because there was no shepherd, neither did my shepherds search for my flock, but the shepherds fed themselves, and fed not my flock;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa0f16aa-cbb8-4c3d-ac76-2332e506ba93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: EZK 34:9
Text: Therefore, O ye shepherds, hear the word of the LORD;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e23e203-6548-4cb7-a136-ea2b8e7599bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 315

Reference: EZK 34:10
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I am against the shepherds; and I will require my flock at their hand, and cause them to cease from feeding the flock; neither shall the shepherds feed themselves any more; for I will deliver my flock from their mouth, that they may not be meat for them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90ee7434-598a-452c-a9a2-808afb776bfd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: EZK 34:11
Text: For thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I, even I, will both search my sheep, and seek them out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09014ab4-18b0-473e-be7f-f39e6b783ffe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: EZK 34:12
Text: As a shepherd seeketh out his flock in the day that he is among his sheep that are scattered; so will I seek out my sheep, and will deliver them out of all places where they have been scattered in the cloudy and dark day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c18d1262-5358-4b77-8d9e-7e975c20d03e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: EZK 34:13
Text: And I will bring them out from the people, and gather them from the countries, and will bring them to their own land, and feed them upon the mountains of Israel by the rivers, and in all the inhabited places of the country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62313bd4-5d35-4228-9ad7-f7a8973e84b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: EZK 34:14
Text: I will feed them in a good pasture, and upon the high mountains of Israel shall their fold be: there shall they lie in a good fold, and in a fat pasture shall they feed upon the mountains of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d98458ed-7d09-4a93-9e45-907df8bfa7c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: EZK 34:15
Text: I will feed my flock, and I will cause them to lie down, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16a9cfe3-c07b-47f3-bd5d-e80426951da9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: EZK 34:16
Text: I will seek that which was lost, and bring again that which was driven away, and will bind up that which was broken, and will strengthen that which was sick: but I will destroy the fat and the strong; I will feed them with judgment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b61b2e54-66c4-48e7-bd5c-4972f4d361fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EZK 34:17
Text: And as for you, O my flock, thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I judge between cattle and cattle, between the rams and the he goats.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d785b003-0de6-4590-aeb9-bdaf3198a9bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: EZK 34:18
Text: Seemeth it a small thing unto you to have eaten up the good pasture, but ye must tread down with your feet the residue of your pastures? and to have drunk of the deep waters, but ye must foul the residue with your feet?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb7c46a1-7475-4197-b9d6-53815a817e73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EZK 34:19
Text: And as for my flock, they eat that which ye have trodden with your feet; and they drink that which ye have fouled with your feet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a135708-1d42-47d1-8e0e-6469105f6a40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: EZK 34:20
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD unto them; Behold, I, even I, will judge between the fat cattle and between the lean cattle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e73eea9b-d912-4e70-82d0-9d110f5a9ddd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EZK 34:21
Text: Because ye have thrust with side and with shoulder, and pushed all the diseased with your horns, till ye have scattered them abroad;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebb3c9c5-13fa-46ff-9e68-c84c92caac93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: EZK 34:22
Text: Therefore will I save my flock, and they shall no more be a prey; and I will judge between cattle and cattle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:585abe43-c5e3-4ed8-817b-af948dbf67cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: EZK 34:23
Text: And I will set up one shepherd over them, and he shall feed them, even my servant David; he shall feed them, and he shall be their shepherd.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67063a5a-1494-49c2-a13f-27f04021cd8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: EZK 34:24
Text: And I the LORD will be their God, and my servant David a prince among them; I the LORD have spoken it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce6ea000-11fd-43c6-871b-12ed977a7245>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: EZK 34:25
Text: And I will make with them a covenant of peace, and will cause the evil beasts to cease out of the land: and they shall dwell safely in the wilderness, and sleep in the woods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:602a4d9a-7aeb-427d-a754-f9cb3802a6a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: EZK 34:26
Text: And I will make them and the places round about my hill a blessing; and I will cause the shower to come down in his season; there shall be showers of blessing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:146b9173-25d0-4e1d-8aa2-1af8622d95fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 309

Reference: EZK 34:27
Text: And the tree of the field shall yield her fruit, and the earth shall yield her increase, and they shall be safe in their land, and shall know that I am the LORD, when I have broken the bands of their yoke, and delivered them out of the hand of those that served themselves of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac56d513-84a6-4f1a-8f37-99f7b1faa091>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: EZK 34:28
Text: And they shall no more be a prey to the heathen, neither shall the beast of the land devour them; but they shall dwell safely, and none shall make them afraid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:436f118e-804c-49aa-b0d9-561ff4261fa5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: EZK 34:29
Text: And I will raise up for them a plant of renown, and they shall be no more consumed with hunger in the land, neither bear the shame of the heathen any more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbaa966b-776b-4812-91fb-56b6790db230>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: EZK 34:30
Text: Thus shall they know that I the LORD their God am with them, and that they, even the house of Israel, are my people, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/34/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44fa4f59-1f8f-40f7-9122-c3bc5e22ec9f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: EZK 34:31
Text: And ye my flock, the flock of my pasture, are men, and I am your God, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/35/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6e69da2-5bf8-4cfb-8a2b-11db796c32b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: EZK 35:1
Text: Moreover the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/35/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1ee0851-c91d-4f31-9af8-bf77d4778b0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: EZK 35:2
Text: Son of man, set thy face against mount Seir, and prophesy against it,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/35/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afe0ab3f-0a16-49df-96f4-3190f5949978>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: EZK 35:3
Text: And say unto it, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, O mount Seir, I am against thee, and I will stretch out mine hand against thee, and I will make thee most desolate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/35/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50f96a4f-1cc4-49b3-9a6f-37f2e3fa6ba1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: EZK 35:4
Text: I will lay thy cities waste, and thou shalt be desolate, and thou shalt know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/35/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a1fc5c7-900a-4d45-a61f-8fbb2a1d0162>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: EZK 35:5
Text: Because thou hast had a perpetual hatred, and hast shed the blood of the children of Israel by the force of the sword in the time of their calamity, in the time that their iniquity had an end:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/35/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae86560e-d0c6-4dc3-bbef-aed6b1ff0938>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: EZK 35:6
Text: Therefore, as I live, saith the Lord GOD, I will prepare thee unto blood, and blood shall pursue thee: sith thou hast not hated blood, even blood shall pursue thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/35/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:373f860d-3b58-404b-8a09-22772218dd0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: EZK 35:7
Text: Thus will I make mount Seir most desolate, and cut off from it him that passeth out and him that returneth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/35/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1b9669f-1909-42ae-8ec5-d3ef189d6129>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: EZK 35:8
Text: And I will fill his mountains with his slain men: in thy hills, and in thy valleys, and in all thy rivers, shall they fall that are slain with the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/35/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85a0292a-ed8d-42b2-af60-aaa2bafccee2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: EZK 35:9
Text: I will make thee perpetual desolations, and thy cities shall not return: and ye shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/35/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8044a8e1-69e2-4066-aa23-71a49fd7e7bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EZK 35:10
Text: Because thou hast said, These two nations and these two countries shall be mine, and we will possess it; whereas the LORD was there:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/35/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43b5b323-610f-41dd-a358-aca7275226b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: EZK 35:11
Text: Therefore, as I live, saith the Lord GOD, I will even do according to thine anger, and according to thine envy which thou hast used out of thy hatred against them; and I will make myself known among them, when I have judged thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/35/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e93eb9aa-2639-4e7e-b0c3-d0e1b7fc1183>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: EZK 35:12
Text: And thou shalt know that I am the LORD, and that I have heard all thy blasphemies which thou hast spoken against the mountains of Israel, saying, They are laid desolate, they are given us to consume.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/35/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a5c926b-6e0e-488e-8077-1b8076dc9cb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: EZK 35:13
Text: Thus with your mouth ye have boasted against me, and have multiplied your words against me: I have heard them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/35/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e65b5876-6fcb-436b-89d1-eee274801d0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: EZK 35:14
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; When the whole earth rejoiceth, I will make thee desolate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/35/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7dbae1bf-7038-4919-9de2-5231175422db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: EZK 35:15
Text: As thou didst rejoice at the inheritance of the house of Israel, because it was desolate, so will I do unto thee: thou shalt be desolate, O mount Seir, and all Idumea, even all of it: and they shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c35ff380-683c-488c-afde-6105b322d643>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: EZK 36:1
Text: Also, thou son of man, prophesy unto the mountains of Israel, and say, Ye mountains of Israel, hear the word of the LORD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c050e6f-f816-40d1-8df1-5d4767e50be6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: EZK 36:2
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because the enemy hath said against you, Aha, even the ancient high places are ours in possession:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6dbfac4-1e1f-4e02-9bf7-e1b93cd83450>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 292

Reference: EZK 36:3
Text: Therefore prophesy and say, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because they have made you desolate, and swallowed you up on every side, that ye might be a possession unto the residue of the heathen, and ye are taken up in the lips of talkers, and are an infamy of the people:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00191d62-7b68-4da7-b87b-14363b5c554c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 333

Reference: EZK 36:4
Text: Therefore, ye mountains of Israel, hear the word of the Lord GOD; Thus saith the Lord GOD to the mountains, and to the hills, to the rivers, and to the valleys, to the desolate wastes, and to the cities that are forsaken, which became a prey and derision to the residue of the heathen that are round about;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65e834d4-ae1a-4bc4-9ae9-811c5062e228>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 303

Reference: EZK 36:5
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Surely in the fire of my jealousy have I spoken against the residue of the heathen, and against all Idumea, which have appointed my land into their possession with the joy of all their heart, with despiteful minds, to cast it out for a prey.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4d13c6f-a7b7-408d-adf5-4ad56808af92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 283

Reference: EZK 36:6
Text: Prophesy therefore concerning the land of Israel, and say unto the mountains, and to the hills, to the rivers, and to the valleys, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I have spoken in my jealousy and in my fury, because ye have borne the shame of the heathen:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb47c035-d823-4503-b221-2fdf87d6e3ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EZK 36:7
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; I have lifted up mine hand, Surely the heathen that are about you, they shall bear their shame.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14fab6f7-abf9-4f37-9591-98825d30d7e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: EZK 36:8
Text: But ye, O mountains of Israel, ye shall shoot forth your branches, and yield your fruit to my people of Israel; for they are at hand to come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e389b253-e8f4-45d3-9371-ae6271adef0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: EZK 36:9
Text: For, behold, I am for you, and I will turn unto you, and ye shall be tilled and sown:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fa80279-3d9f-4ccc-9be5-7b4e5e30ffd2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: EZK 36:10
Text: And I will multiply men upon you, all the house of Israel, even all of it: and the cities shall be inhabited, and the wastes shall be builded:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc899b9f-73b8-415d-bdd2-e88d2ffcbc6d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: EZK 36:11
Text: And I will multiply upon you man and beast; and they shall increase and bring fruit: and I will settle you after your old estates, and will do better unto you than at your beginnings: and ye shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae0fcd4c-804b-4fb4-b2d8-e3d8904aad0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: EZK 36:12
Text: Yea, I will cause men to walk upon you, even my people Israel; and they shall possess thee, and thou shalt be their inheritance, and thou shalt no more henceforth bereave them of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0edb07ce-1375-417e-a3eb-3aaa0986b5ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: EZK 36:13
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; Because they say unto you, Thou land devourest up men, and hast bereaved thy nations:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f375b499-1b5c-4059-980b-230e5b3cadf4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: EZK 36:14
Text: Therefore thou shalt devour men no more, neither bereave thy nations any more, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a50e059-2d48-4f71-994f-bdd8cb1d39b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: EZK 36:15
Text: Neither will I cause men to hear in thee the shame of the heathen any more, neither shalt thou bear the reproach of the people any more, neither shalt thou cause thy nations to fall any more, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf7745cd-f41b-440d-8336-3ee254feb2b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: EZK 36:16
Text: Moreover the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:017d5fef-e42f-4e8f-8a2c-2bdff7e0f39b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: EZK 36:17
Text: Son of man, when the house of Israel dwelt in their own land, they defiled it by their own way and by their doings: their way was before me as the uncleanness of a removed woman.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e76b0934-c070-41b4-b34d-39ae2bcd2fc8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: EZK 36:18
Text: Wherefore I poured my fury upon them for the blood that they had shed upon the land, and for their idols wherewith they had polluted it:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb15dc01-b465-4039-b96b-3f38fb7a89a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: EZK 36:19
Text: And I scattered them among the heathen, and they were dispersed through the countries: according to their way and according to their doings I judged them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ffe3fa8-fadf-4dce-b7df-df941f8669e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: EZK 36:20
Text: And when they entered unto the heathen, whither they went, they profaned my holy name, when they said to them, These are the people of the LORD, and are gone forth out of his land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:470d3b49-1a45-4cc9-b357-4405f55e64bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: EZK 36:21
Text: But I had pity for mine holy name, which the house of Israel had profaned among the heathen, whither they went.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:737209c5-6ab8-4626-8ccb-788db9828526>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: EZK 36:22
Text: Therefore say unto the house of Israel, thus saith the Lord GOD; I do not this for your sakes, O house of Israel, but for mine holy name’s sake, which ye have profaned among the heathen, whither ye went.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4af034b5-f783-4994-85d5-fc1ad0a42106>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: EZK 36:23
Text: And I will sanctify my great name, which was profaned among the heathen, which ye have profaned in the midst of them; and the heathen shall know that I am the LORD, saith the Lord GOD, when I shall be sanctified in you before their eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c32fdff1-7c93-44e7-80c7-25a531e916c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: EZK 36:24
Text: For I will take you from among the heathen, and gather you out of all countries, and will bring you into your own land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee88e1c5-dc16-47d3-ad3e-cd8dc8d166e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: EZK 36:25
Text: Then will I sprinkle clean water upon you, and ye shall be clean: from all your filthiness, and from all your idols, will I cleanse you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e2286e7-f6e6-45ac-8cfe-4fc3b7e3c274>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: EZK 36:26
Text: A new heart also will I give you, and a new spirit will I put within you: and I will take away the stony heart out of your flesh, and I will give you an heart of flesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86266011-4443-4029-bf18-c4f312121bea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: EZK 36:27
Text: And I will put my spirit within you, and cause you to walk in my statutes, and ye shall keep my judgments, and do them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a462fdc5-ce31-4e64-b12e-4fe560a4b650>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: EZK 36:28
Text: And ye shall dwell in the land that I gave to your fathers; and ye shall be my people, and I will be your God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc036564-d1ce-441b-ba84-1da9dc53ccc2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EZK 36:29
Text: I will also save you from all your uncleannesses: and I will call for the corn, and will increase it, and lay no famine upon you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57336370-7828-4924-89ca-6acbe5f2f90c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: EZK 36:30
Text: And I will multiply the fruit of the tree, and the increase of the field, that ye shall receive no more reproach of famine among the heathen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ec4459e-68f5-4e0d-baa8-80e25550c9a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: EZK 36:31
Text: Then shall ye remember your own evil ways, and your doings that were not good, and shall lothe yourselves in your own sight for your iniquities and for your abominations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d43a33b4-88b5-4ed7-9f6f-25304cd557c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: EZK 36:32
Text: Not for your sakes do I this, saith the Lord GOD, be it known unto you: be ashamed and confounded for your own ways, O house of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b222f05e-f709-4ec6-bf7c-cade009524f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: EZK 36:33
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; In the day that I shall have cleansed you from all your iniquities I will also cause you to dwell in the cities, and the wastes shall be builded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52b49d91-bf59-4f31-8c7c-76231a319ece>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: EZK 36:34
Text: And the desolate land shall be tilled, whereas it lay desolate in the sight of all that passed by.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0fceca8-0342-4b4a-b569-06bc9d5bc473>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: EZK 36:35
Text: And they shall say, This land that was desolate is become like the garden of Eden; and the waste and desolate and ruined cities are become fenced, and are inhabited.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f51d2106-be4d-47bb-ba22-18084389020a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: EZK 36:36
Text: Then the heathen that are left round about you shall know that I the LORD build the ruined places, and plant that that was desolate: I the LORD have spoken it, and I will do it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3089fb0f-d79e-4654-8c30-8a0636085213>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: EZK 36:37
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; I will yet for this be enquired of by the house of Israel, to do it for them; I will increase them with men like a flock.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/36/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3beebe08-1fc1-48ea-8361-b2faca0b2d92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: EZK 36:38
Text: As the holy flock, as the flock of Jerusalem in her solemn feasts; so shall the waste cities be filled with flocks of men: and they shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2adb2d63-add9-4700-ad55-06247669b3e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: EZK 37:1
Text: The hand of the LORD was upon me, and carried me out in the spirit of the LORD, and set me down in the midst of the valley which was full of bones,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8f66d95-c127-4f3b-ad65-19d1ba18131f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: EZK 37:2
Text: And caused me to pass by them round about: and, behold, there were very many in the open valley; and, lo, they were very dry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60490db3-9e33-4a7d-9334-81f73b59a29f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: EZK 37:3
Text: And he said unto me, Son of man, can these bones live? And I answered, O Lord GOD, thou knowest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5ad7fb8-f9c6-40b0-9e67-4ab576c63825>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: EZK 37:4
Text: Again he said unto me, Prophesy upon these bones, and say unto them, O ye dry bones, hear the word of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c02f0df-5c7c-4e59-be1b-d8ccb3de22ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: EZK 37:5
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD unto these bones; Behold, I will cause breath to enter into you, and ye shall live:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5359254-ac5a-44cf-80e6-17a4ec574a3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: EZK 37:6
Text: And I will lay sinews upon you, and will bring up flesh upon you, and cover you with skin, and put breath in you, and ye shall live; and ye shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bea57448-6b44-45da-98b3-d210525c795b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: EZK 37:7
Text: So I prophesied as I was commanded: and as I prophesied, there was a noise, and behold a shaking, and the bones came together, bone to his bone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca99be08-b4a4-43b0-be60-808c4a5b0f1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: EZK 37:8
Text: And when I beheld, lo, the sinews and the flesh came up upon them, and the skin covered them above: but there was no breath in them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c25501cf-08b5-4401-bc15-93039a11c3fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: EZK 37:9
Text: Then said he unto me, Prophesy unto the wind, prophesy, son of man, and say to the wind, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Come from the four winds, O breath, and breathe upon these slain, that they may live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5bbe6e7-1df1-4b86-96eb-9b684094f27c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: EZK 37:10
Text: So I prophesied as he commanded me, and the breath came into them, and they lived, and stood up upon their feet, an exceeding great army.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3506379-fecc-46d2-9967-cf3fb21e60df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: EZK 37:11
Text: Then he said unto me, Son of man, these bones are the whole house of Israel: behold, they say, Our bones are dried, and our hope is lost: we are cut off for our parts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68d8871a-df13-4ea9-bc19-93d2fdbb84c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: EZK 37:12
Text: Therefore prophesy and say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, O my people, I will open your graves, and cause you to come up out of your graves, and bring you into the land of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:415fd822-4330-4f87-b833-6b40c2f6c4b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: EZK 37:13
Text: And ye shall know that I am the LORD, when I have opened your graves, O my people, and brought you up out of your graves,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc2c1acc-671b-4f84-a8b4-1e0b38437ecb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: EZK 37:14
Text: And shall put my spirit in you, and ye shall live, and I shall place you in your own land: then shall ye know that I the LORD have spoken it, and performed it, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ca64c00-114d-42c8-8575-e760de885fd3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: EZK 37:15
Text: The word of the LORD came again unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1c8810a-c7aa-49c8-92dd-d5d23c8975b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 277

Reference: EZK 37:16
Text: Moreover, thou son of man, take thee one stick, and write upon it, For Judah, and for the children of Israel his companions: then take another stick, and write upon it, For Joseph, the stick of Ephraim and for all the house of Israel his companions:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0f03cbb-7bd0-4536-ac88-ca42cd998ed3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: EZK 37:17
Text: And join them one to another into one stick; and they shall become one in thine hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc5f2f5f-e7c7-4b24-825f-4970fe9849e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: EZK 37:18
Text: And when the children of thy people shall speak unto thee, saying, Wilt thou not shew us what thou meanest by these?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8ac41f8-e637-4db2-8f11-5ae0c98c6205>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 298

Reference: EZK 37:19
Text: Say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I will take the stick of Joseph, which is in the hand of Ephraim, and the tribes of Israel his fellows, and will put them with him, even with the stick of Judah, and make them one stick, and they shall be one in mine hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:898f0707-10ca-475c-915c-c1f14f3a0e26>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: EZK 37:20
Text: And the sticks whereon thou writest shall be in thine hand before their eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e95815e-b712-4d5d-b331-6c30376d0f58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: EZK 37:21
Text: And say unto them, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I will take the children of Israel from among the heathen, whither they be gone, and will gather them on every side, and bring them into their own land:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfa8d649-bfed-41ac-b781-68647532cfe6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: EZK 37:22
Text: And I will make them one nation in the land upon the mountains of Israel; and one king shall be king to them all: and they shall be no more two nations, neither shall they be divided into two kingdoms any more at all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30b3cc35-2b85-4c7d-b5c1-25a0f5605baf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 319

Reference: EZK 37:23
Text: Neither shall they defile themselves any more with their idols, nor with their detestable things, nor with any of their transgressions: but I will save them out of all their dwellingplaces, wherein they have sinned, and will cleanse them: so shall they be my people, and I will be their God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c67250a-550f-4cde-a606-5b55db9d0bc5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: EZK 37:24
Text: And David my servant shall be king over them; and they all shall have one shepherd: they shall also walk in my judgments, and observe my statutes, and do them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d597fa90-efc7-48d6-b27c-84c2cafb38f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 290

Reference: EZK 37:25
Text: And they shall dwell in the land that I have given unto Jacob my servant, wherein your fathers have dwelt; and they shall dwell therein, even they, and their children, and their children’s children for ever: and my servant David shall be their prince for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78c5611c-f1b9-43f2-beb6-ced6b2012b8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: EZK 37:26
Text: Moreover I will make a covenant of peace with them; it shall be an everlasting covenant with them: and I will place them, and multiply them, and will set my sanctuary in the midst of them for evermore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85d8921c-5378-49c2-a4b5-f67d87c39fdf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: EZK 37:27
Text: My tabernacle also shall be with them: yea, I will be their God, and they shall be my people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/37/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d77f0b54-50cd-4c5f-8d8e-435c1a27f6cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: EZK 37:28
Text: And the heathen shall know that I the LORD do sanctify Israel, when my sanctuary shall be in the midst of them for evermore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/38/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3b14184-8c4a-49df-b82c-1875c2b8a751>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: EZK 38:1
Text: And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/38/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db024280-7936-4b1f-8b61-3ec7b6f8501b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: EZK 38:2
Text: Son of man, set thy face against Gog, the land of Magog, the chief prince of Meshech and Tubal, and prophesy against him,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/38/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f88c75e-d442-46ef-9576-436281f17ab3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: EZK 38:3
Text: And say, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I am against thee, O Gog, the chief prince of Meshech and Tubal:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/38/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:805e0048-b03a-411d-9555-771e32a16869>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: EZK 38:4
Text: And I will turn thee back, and put hooks into thy jaws, and I will bring thee forth, and all thine army, horses and horsemen, all of them clothed with all sorts of armour, even a great company with bucklers and shields, all of them handling swords:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/38/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2e9d78a-e7b3-4fa0-844e-67a2f778f7a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: EZK 38:5
Text: Persia, Ethiopia, and Libya with them; all of them with shield and helmet:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/38/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9841a353-2d15-4163-98b0-039be5bdedb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: EZK 38:6
Text: Gomer, and all his bands; the house of Togarmah of the north quarters, and all his bands: and many people with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/38/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee9167de-a315-4e41-801f-fbb2c55dafe9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: EZK 38:7
Text: Be thou prepared, and prepare for thyself, thou, and all thy company that are assembled unto thee, and be thou a guard unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/38/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:012e4a70-27e9-42a9-8358-6cb6a92b6de4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 336

Reference: EZK 38:8
Text: After many days thou shalt be visited: in the latter years thou shalt come into the land that is brought back from the sword, and is gathered out of many people, against the mountains of Israel, which have been always waste: but it is brought forth out of the nations, and they shall dwell safely all of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/38/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78a7f704-4921-42af-83e4-78658cc198a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: EZK 38:9
Text: Thou shalt ascend and come like a storm, thou shalt be like a cloud to cover the land, thou, and all thy bands, and many people with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/38/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbc9a5a9-3398-424f-a241-d5d2e1c2800b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: EZK 38:10
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; It shall also come to pass, that at the same time shall things come into thy mind, and thou shalt think an evil thought:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/38/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a054f4fc-03c9-4e8c-82b4-7e6e66c01036>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: EZK 38:11
Text: And thou shalt say, I will go up to the land of unwalled villages; I will go to them that are at rest, that dwell safely, all of them dwelling without walls, and having neither bars nor gates,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/38/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:140b6638-ea66-47e3-968f-5380ed74430b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: EZK 38:12
Text: To take a spoil, and to take a prey; to turn thine hand upon the desolate places that are now inhabited, and upon the people that are gathered out of the nations, which have gotten cattle and goods, that dwell in the midst of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/38/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a952673-0310-4007-ae38-d31d4837059b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 294

Reference: EZK 38:13
Text: Sheba, and Dedan, and the merchants of Tarshish, with all the young lions thereof, shall say unto thee, Art thou come to take a spoil? hast thou gathered thy company to take a prey? to carry away silver and gold, to take away cattle and goods, to take a great spoil?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/38/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60f61557-5621-4240-9fd7-23c0a3f7de32>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: EZK 38:14
Text: Therefore, son of man, prophesy and say unto Gog, Thus saith the Lord GOD; In that day when my people of Israel dwelleth safely, shalt thou not know it?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/38/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b2d55cc-3a5b-45a3-a9e5-eafc38da112f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: EZK 38:15
Text: And thou shalt come from thy place out of the north parts, thou, and many people with thee, all of them riding upon horses, a great company, and a mighty army:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/38/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b2531d5-6d97-4d74-9362-d06e3e167bf3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: EZK 38:16
Text: And thou shalt come up against my people of Israel, as a cloud to cover the land; it shall be in the latter days, and I will bring thee against my land, that the heathen may know me, when I shall be sanctified in thee, O Gog, before their eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/38/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43e18ba3-6630-47ca-86bb-431552614e9e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: EZK 38:17
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; Art thou he of whom I have spoken in old time by my servants the prophets of Israel, which prophesied in those days many years that I would bring thee against them?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/38/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77011094-7127-4448-a7fc-07781b36324f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: EZK 38:18
Text: And it shall come to pass at the same time when Gog shall come against the land of Israel, saith the Lord GOD, that my fury shall come up in my face.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/38/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d3dfc0b-c3a8-4f3d-b9f3-c865989281f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: EZK 38:19
Text: For in my jealousy and in the fire of my wrath have I spoken, Surely in that day there shall be a great shaking in the land of Israel;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/38/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6b5b534-1158-4d7d-b9d5-e11caf6357a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 362

Reference: EZK 38:20
Text: So that the fishes of the sea, and the fowls of the heaven, and the beasts of the field, and all creeping things that creep upon the earth, and all the men that are upon the face of the earth, shall shake at my presence, and the mountains shall be thrown down, and the steep places shall fall, and every wall shall fall to the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/38/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c166b04-7f46-4c39-ac3d-729d57f97c79>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: EZK 38:21
Text: And I will call for a sword against him throughout all my mountains, saith the Lord GOD: every man’s sword shall be against his brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/38/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0a6bb14-0431-4b5e-b028-7f0ca1b1f9a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: EZK 38:22
Text: And I will plead against him with pestilence and with blood; and I will rain upon him, and upon his bands, and upon the many people that are with him, an overflowing rain, and great hailstones, fire, and brimstone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/38/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c70b2ce-60fb-4b35-9a3f-8522e0a24250>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: EZK 38:23
Text: Thus will I magnify myself, and sanctify myself; and I will be known in the eyes of many nations, and they shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e38fc78f-3a6c-4115-9340-97833cc8ec16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: EZK 39:1
Text: Therefore, thou son of man, prophesy against Gog, and say, Thus saith the Lord GOD; Behold, I am against thee, O Gog, the chief prince of Meshech and Tubal:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93476f00-2bf1-4987-9c0c-f5eb9908e25b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: EZK 39:2
Text: And I will turn thee back, and leave but the sixth part of thee, and will cause thee to come up from the north parts, and will bring thee upon the mountains of Israel:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73d90352-139a-4c79-9565-1ee423c885bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: EZK 39:3
Text: And I will smite thy bow out of thy left hand, and will cause thine arrows to fall out of thy right hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8e92f4c-67d1-4b63-a340-ebc792d9b72c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: EZK 39:4
Text: Thou shalt fall upon the mountains of Israel, thou, and all thy bands, and the people that is with thee: I will give thee unto the ravenous birds of every sort, and to the beasts of the field to be devoured.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f1a0dec-47dd-4a23-a9ad-431d8f639386>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: EZK 39:5
Text: Thou shalt fall upon the open field: for I have spoken it, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c5f0023-57fa-4bc1-ae45-f56c2619096a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: EZK 39:6
Text: And I will send a fire on Magog, and among them that dwell carelessly in the isles: and they shall know that I am the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0dcbbb46-0bbf-45d8-87db-cb6028cde09b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: EZK 39:7
Text: So will I make my holy name known in the midst of my people Israel; and I will not let them pollute my holy name any more: and the heathen shall know that I am the LORD, the Holy One in Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41fb45e5-e78d-4c94-a585-35b6d70452f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: EZK 39:8
Text: Behold, it is come, and it is done, saith the Lord GOD; this is the day whereof I have spoken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7489da5-d140-4323-a125-358b1389e637>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 274

Reference: EZK 39:9
Text: And they that dwell in the cities of Israel shall go forth, and shall set on fire and burn the weapons, both the shields and the bucklers, the bows and the arrows, and the handstaves, and the spears, and they shall burn them with fire seven years:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b011775f-091f-4cac-8f59-b053bc69499f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: EZK 39:10
Text: So that they shall take no wood out of the field, neither cut down any out of the forests; for they shall burn the weapons with fire: and they shall spoil those that spoiled them, and rob those that robbed them, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d4db25b-2399-4a29-bff5-82b79d8a92da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 327

Reference: EZK 39:11
Text: And it shall come to pass in that day, that I will give unto Gog a place there of graves in Israel, the valley of the passengers on the east of the sea: and it shall stop the noses of the passengers: and there shall they bury Gog and all his multitude: and they shall call it The valley of Hamongog.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3386ad58-9152-4803-9640-8d6f302bfe73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: EZK 39:12
Text: And seven months shall the house of Israel be burying of them, that they may cleanse the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b11040c3-e079-416f-a744-3ee579fa2dda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: EZK 39:13
Text: Yea, all the people of the land shall bury them; and it shall be to them a renown the day that I shall be glorified, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5394beed-7d45-460c-9046-4c8428002e5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: EZK 39:14
Text: And they shall sever out men of continual employment, passing through the land to bury with the passengers those that remain upon the face of the earth, to cleanse it: after the end of seven months shall they search.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a92ea20d-7bc1-4b34-ba8a-d35ee77e9149>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: EZK 39:15
Text: And the passengers that pass through the land, when any seeth a man’s bone, then shall he set up a sign by it, till the buriers have buried it in the valley of Hamongog.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:335235c2-1b02-4154-bf7a-16c7134d45eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: EZK 39:16
Text: And also the name of the city shall be Hamonah. Thus shall they cleanse the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07e7fb49-5b2f-424f-acd9-d9deaffad96b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 341

Reference: EZK 39:17
Text: And, thou son of man, thus saith the Lord GOD; Speak unto every feathered fowl, and to every beast of the field, Assemble yourselves, and come; gather yourselves on every side to my sacrifice that I do sacrifice for you, even a great sacrifice upon the mountains of Israel, that ye may eat flesh, and drink blood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e74c1bd1-2225-43ed-b5ee-3c393446dce9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: EZK 39:18
Text: Ye shall eat the flesh of the mighty, and drink the blood of the princes of the earth, of rams, of lambs, and of goats, of bullocks, all of them fatlings of Bashan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d16b6f6-6ee8-4c1b-9dfb-b55d3d960cd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: EZK 39:19
Text: And ye shall eat fat till ye be full, and drink blood till ye be drunken, of my sacrifice which I have sacrificed for you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c7df50b-ac68-49eb-82eb-60e7d618dfc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: EZK 39:20
Text: Thus ye shall be filled at my table with horses and chariots, with mighty men, and with all men of war, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d683e31c-58f3-4078-9a58-c06e616047b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: EZK 39:21
Text: And I will set my glory among the heathen, and all the heathen shall see my judgment that I have executed, and my hand that I have laid upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80aed587-0bb5-41e9-9725-229b8045f848>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: EZK 39:22
Text: So the house of Israel shall know that I am the LORD their God from that day and forward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:341d3475-301f-4ea0-a74b-7af9b2442a1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: EZK 39:23
Text: And the heathen shall know that the house of Israel went into captivity for their iniquity: because they trespassed against me, therefore hid I my face from them, and gave them into the hand of their enemies: so fell they all by the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:568d0b5a-4be8-45b0-b7f8-c91eef154b73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: EZK 39:24
Text: According to their uncleanness and according to their transgressions have I done unto them, and hid my face from them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ec3fdb4-0db0-4a97-8318-678a9d77afee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: EZK 39:25
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Now will I bring again the captivity of Jacob, and have mercy upon the whole house of Israel, and will be jealous for my holy name;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2df500c-ca1b-4993-92e0-4dd06c99085e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: EZK 39:26
Text: After that they have borne their shame, and all their trespasses whereby they have trespassed against me, when they dwelt safely in their land, and none made them afraid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc93da14-2d89-4e78-afc7-1458fb4cc94f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: EZK 39:27
Text: When I have brought them again from the people, and gathered them out of their enemies’ lands, and am sanctified in them in the sight of many nations;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:523c161a-c2f8-48b6-abe4-21a1d7188592>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: EZK 39:28
Text: Then shall they know that I am the LORD their God, which caused them to be led into captivity among the heathen: but I have gathered them unto their own land, and have left none of them any more there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/39/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05ffde77-5cfe-49d7-ba93-4799fa5b006f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: EZK 39:29
Text: Neither will I hide my face any more from them: for I have poured out my spirit upon the house of Israel, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/40/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e27e8e7-7a52-410a-bf2b-da131d283c27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: EZK 40:1
Text: In the five and twentieth year of our captivity, in the beginning of the year, in the tenth day of the month, in the fourteenth year after that the city was smitten, in the selfsame day the hand of the LORD was upon me, and brought me thither.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/40/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e79dc75b-fc66-4e81-8d59-b3ca5a02ebb2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: EZK 40:2
Text: In the visions of God brought he me into the land of Israel, and set me upon a very high mountain, by which was as the frame of a city on the south.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/40/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79a7da9f-57b6-4dfb-a5c6-e57293bf67c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: EZK 40:3
Text: And he brought me thither, and, behold, there was a man, whose appearance was like the appearance of brass, with a line of flax in his hand, and a measuring reed; and he stood in the gate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/40/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a27f7f5c-8291-46a7-82d5-e94315757bc8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 295

Reference: EZK 40:4
Text: And the man said unto me, Son of man, behold with thine eyes, and hear with thine ears, and set thine heart upon all that I shall shew thee; for to the intent that I might shew them unto thee art thou brought hither: declare all that thou seest to the house of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/40/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52e9a1a5-64a9-421f-8b57-f430f37251be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: EZK 40:5
Text: And behold a wall on the outside of the house round about, and in the man’s hand a measuring reed of six cubits long by the cubit and an hand breadth: so he measured the breadth of the building, one reed; and the height, one reed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/40/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bf8e511-724e-43b4-aa64-09a864406f55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: EZK 40:6
Text: Then came he unto the gate which looketh toward the east, and went up the stairs thereof, and measured the threshold of the gate, which was one reed broad; and the other threshold of the gate, which was one reed broad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/40/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4101af9-7622-44ea-b1b2-31b717279bc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: EZK 40:7
Text: And every little chamber was one reed long, and one reed broad; and between the little chambers were five cubits; and the threshold of the gate by the porch of the gate within was one reed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/40/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28f97c0b-8a14-4a87-9342-29d0403eac47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: EZK 40:8
Text: He measured also the porch of the gate within, one reed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/40/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4884e2ed-9dab-4423-90d3-a3707b70d2a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: EZK 40:9
Text: Then measured he the porch of the gate, eight cubits; and the posts thereof, two cubits; and the porch of the gate was inward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/40/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8fc0199-fb06-4d2b-bb4e-3a18f3129588>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: EZK 40:10
Text: And the little chambers of the gate eastward were three on this side, and three on that side; they three were of one measure: and the posts had one measure on this side and on that side.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/40/11
