Reference: EZK 43:1
Text: Afterward he brought me to the gate, even the gate that looketh toward the east:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9afce6a1-d148-462e-ae02-72591eb82796>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: EZK 43:2
Text: And, behold, the glory of the God of Israel came from the way of the east: and his voice was like a noise of many waters: and the earth shined with his glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30668bab-e537-485b-a4e9-6e82901ac0ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: EZK 43:3
Text: And it was according to the appearance of the vision which I saw, even according to the vision that I saw when I came to destroy the city: and the visions were like the vision that I saw by the river Chebar; and I fell upon my face.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebb7df83-9dd1-4101-868f-941ab2deb064>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: EZK 43:4
Text: And the glory of the LORD came into the house by the way of the gate whose prospect is toward the east.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:578a1ce3-b6ac-4966-b14c-890d1684e243>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: EZK 43:5
Text: So the spirit took me up, and brought me into the inner court; and, behold, the glory of the LORD filled the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72d9135d-7d80-46e3-a4cb-0e78b5615c8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: EZK 43:6
Text: And I heard him speaking unto me out of the house; and the man stood by me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42121eef-f648-4d87-96f5-c64486b178a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 357

Reference: EZK 43:7
Text: And he said unto me, Son of man, the place of my throne, and the place of the soles of my feet, where I will dwell in the midst of the children of Israel for ever, and my holy name, shall the house of Israel no more defile, neither they, nor their kings, by their whoredom, nor by the carcases of their kings in their high places.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3733c8d1-384c-442e-b022-06c735b212df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: EZK 43:8
Text: In their setting of their threshold by my thresholds, and their post by my posts, and the wall between me and them, they have even defiled my holy name by their abominations that they have committed: wherefore I have consumed them in mine anger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1257dde7-16ca-468f-aac6-a9e555a261d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EZK 43:9
Text: Now let them put away their whoredom, and the carcases of their kings, far from me, and I will dwell in the midst of them for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6fa45a3-f84a-42fa-a433-0b87cb977cc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: EZK 43:10
Text: Thou son of man, shew the house to the house of Israel, that they may be ashamed of their iniquities: and let them measure the pattern.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bca122e1-4fa7-48f4-b308-6c42378cb31c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 421

Reference: EZK 43:11
Text: And if they be ashamed of all that they have done, shew them the form of the house, and the fashion thereof, and the goings out thereof, and the comings in thereof, and all the forms thereof, and all the ordinances thereof, and all the forms thereof, and all the laws thereof: and write it in their sight, that they may keep the whole form thereof, and all the ordinances thereof, and do them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8be829bd-5a3a-45b7-a591-c5b1989d66b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: EZK 43:12
Text: This is the law of the house; Upon the top of the mountain the whole limit thereof round about shall be most holy. Behold, this is the law of the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da581cd8-04dd-40ba-8862-03222caa8117>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 307

Reference: EZK 43:13
Text: And these are the measures of the altar after the cubits: The cubit is a cubit and an hand breadth; even the bottom shall be a cubit, and the breadth a cubit, and the border thereof by the edge thereof round about shall be a span: and this shall be the higher place of the altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74094d36-bca3-4118-b3eb-0c66cf5487e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: EZK 43:14
Text: And from the bottom upon the ground even to the lower settle shall be two cubits, and the breadth one cubit; and from the lesser settle even to the greater settle shall be four cubits, and the breadth one cubit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fab65c5-b956-48da-ba93-d15d1ca0485b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: EZK 43:15
Text: So the altar shall be four cubits; and from the altar and upward shall be four horns.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:221580db-0a30-4a11-bd72-9844b86b90bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: EZK 43:16
Text: And the altar shall be twelve cubits long, twelve broad, square in the four squares thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04457a89-36e3-4e98-96d4-d458b40b3cb0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: EZK 43:17
Text: And the settle shall be fourteen cubits long and fourteen broad in the four squares thereof; and the border about it shall be half a cubit; and the bottom thereof shall be a cubit about; and his stairs shall look toward the east.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b810b359-bc2e-4ea8-b4cc-ce8ef8e66e74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: EZK 43:18
Text: And he said unto me, Son of man, thus saith the Lord GOD; These are the ordinances of the altar in the day when they shall make it, to offer burnt offerings thereon, and to sprinkle blood thereon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01f497ec-e27f-466f-b6ef-4b86aa07efbb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: EZK 43:19
Text: And thou shalt give to the priests the Levites that be of the seed of Zadok, which approach unto me, to minister unto me, saith the Lord GOD, a young bullock for a sin offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb7828ee-cac3-4b91-aacb-b5b0a7a324c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: EZK 43:20
Text: And thou shalt take of the blood thereof, and put it on the four horns of it, and on the four corners of the settle, and upon the border round about: thus shalt thou cleanse and purge it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b9f924d-d733-49c4-80d3-6d39269a45cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: EZK 43:21
Text: Thou shalt take the bullock also of the sin offering, and he shall burn it in the appointed place of the house, without the sanctuary.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb2713c5-4ed0-439b-87ff-fcc4112e7391>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: EZK 43:22
Text: And on the second day thou shalt offer a kid of the goats without blemish for a sin offering; and they shall cleanse the altar, as they did cleanse it with the bullock.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bc2e290-c546-45ee-9464-c3a2ca193a16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: EZK 43:23
Text: When thou hast made an end of cleansing it, thou shalt offer a young bullock without blemish, and a ram out of the flock without blemish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b83c4c2d-9d74-4fb9-9789-5b6378643d18>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: EZK 43:24
Text: And thou shalt offer them before the LORD, and the priests shall cast salt upon them, and they shall offer them up for a burnt offering unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9a7c6b9-3c78-47e8-96d2-88ffb8904fd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: EZK 43:25
Text: Seven days shalt thou prepare every day a goat for a sin offering: they shall also prepare a young bullock, and a ram out of the flock, without blemish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4ee5a55-0cc8-4ba7-9736-f38648dea5fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: EZK 43:26
Text: Seven days shall they purge the altar and purify it; and they shall consecrate themselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/43/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94c8e854-7e83-443d-a1c2-240406d56982>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: EZK 43:27
Text: And when these days are expired, it shall be, that upon the eighth day, and so forward, the priests shall make your burnt offerings upon the altar, and your peace offerings; and I will accept you, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff0735fd-487b-404b-a5d0-256206d40f1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: EZK 44:1
Text: Then he brought me back the way of the gate of the outward sanctuary which looketh toward the east; and it was shut.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acc176e5-5ac5-409b-b0bf-24d437f9b8fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: EZK 44:2
Text: Then said the LORD unto me; This gate shall be shut, it shall not be opened, and no man shall enter in by it; because the LORD, the God of Israel, hath entered in by it, therefore it shall be shut.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:946ce0c2-5d47-4b5e-b39c-31660accd453>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: EZK 44:3
Text: It is for the prince; the prince, he shall sit in it to eat bread before the LORD; he shall enter by the way of the porch of that gate, and shall go out by the way of the same.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffc5bd8d-8add-49ac-a2e6-d8029672c4c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: EZK 44:4
Text: Then brought he me the way of the north gate before the house: and I looked, and, behold, the glory of the LORD filled the house of the LORD: and I fell upon my face.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92f964f0-fd1c-4fca-8b39-359db8edfea9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 321

Reference: EZK 44:5
Text: And the LORD said unto me, Son of man, mark well, and behold with thine eyes, and hear with thine ears all that I say unto thee concerning all the ordinances of the house of the LORD, and all the laws thereof; and mark well the entering in of the house, with every going forth of the sanctuary.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b126ac80-c664-4fcd-aef1-b857e1f7ffea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: EZK 44:6
Text: And thou shalt say to the rebellious, even to the house of Israel, Thus saith the Lord GOD; O ye house of Israel, let it suffice you of all your abominations,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7db0d01-14d9-46ba-827c-ab76d9f0359b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 298

Reference: EZK 44:7
Text: In that ye have brought into my sanctuary strangers, uncircumcised in heart, and uncircumcised in flesh, to be in my sanctuary, to pollute it, even my house, when ye offer my bread, the fat and the blood, and they have broken my covenant because of all your abominations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:886843a2-d67f-478f-ac2c-b8a3f0d3465c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: EZK 44:8
Text: And ye have not kept the charge of mine holy things: but ye have set keepers of my charge in my sanctuary for yourselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:586011e1-ef9a-44e1-95aa-727d348bade5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: EZK 44:9
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; No stranger, uncircumcised in heart, nor uncircumcised in flesh, shall enter into my sanctuary, of any stranger that is among the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b823def8-b146-4a22-9638-50e092ff7b1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: EZK 44:10
Text: And the Levites that are gone away far from me, when Israel went astray, which went astray away from me after their idols; they shall even bear their iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:549801db-6879-478d-8f61-8f22977be835>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: EZK 44:11
Text: Yet they shall be ministers in my sanctuary, having charge at the gates of the house, and ministering to the house: they shall slay the burnt offering and the sacrifice for the people, and they shall stand before them to minister unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c09eb570-2036-4f5a-b1a6-de34a03143da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: EZK 44:12
Text: Because they ministered unto them before their idols, and caused the house of Israel to fall into iniquity; therefore have I lifted up mine hand against them, saith the Lord GOD, and they shall bear their iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c47d96d-89f7-4e36-a2d0-d6b12d05526c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: EZK 44:13
Text: And they shall not come near unto me, to do the office of a priest unto me, nor to come near to any of my holy things, in the most holy place: but they shall bear their shame, and their abominations which they have committed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f177dc2-cb1e-4bc2-ba31-155014de1f55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: EZK 44:14
Text: But I will make them keepers of the charge of the house, for all the service thereof, and for all that shall be done therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04c76b72-1580-4956-88ef-74e1f735c8f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 300

Reference: EZK 44:15
Text: But the priests the Levites, the sons of Zadok, that kept the charge of my sanctuary when the children of Israel went astray from me, they shall come near to me to minister unto me, and they shall stand before me to offer unto me the fat and the blood, saith the Lord GOD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24a09c4e-2686-40a8-b4d4-047e90625240>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: EZK 44:16
Text: They shall enter into my sanctuary, and they shall come near to my table, to minister unto me, and they shall keep my charge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ead603a-757e-4e44-93a9-038060ba8302>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: EZK 44:17
Text: And it shall come to pass, that when they enter in at the gates of the inner court, they shall be clothed with linen garments; and no wool shall come upon them, whiles they minister in the gates of the inner court, and within.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64bbc120-faec-49d7-ba80-1748262ba484>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: EZK 44:18
Text: They shall have linen bonnets upon their heads, and shall have linen breeches upon their loins; they shall not gird themselves with any thing that causeth sweat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:963ef9ff-2645-4768-94bf-9baa3a9e051b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 305

Reference: EZK 44:19
Text: And when they go forth into the utter court, even into the utter court to the people, they shall put off their garments wherein they ministered, and lay them in the holy chambers, and they shall put on other garments; and they shall not sanctify the people with their garments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9068c9ba-c0dd-478e-a4dc-b3a4ad3d7540>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: EZK 44:20
Text: Neither shall they shave their heads, nor suffer their locks to grow long; they shall only poll their heads.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d9aeceb-a20a-451c-bec8-5f59eead87c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: EZK 44:21
Text: Neither shall any priest drink wine, when they enter into the inner court.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49aadd22-5b79-4c5a-b9d9-7f85f13d4e5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: EZK 44:22
Text: Neither shall they take for their wives a widow, nor her that is put away: but they shall take maidens of the seed of the house of Israel, or a widow that had a priest before.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35953f15-5a60-475d-bd5b-3f73e6870b2d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: EZK 44:23
Text: And they shall teach my people the difference between the holy and profane, and cause them to discern between the unclean and the clean.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:464acadb-9fb6-4605-a3f7-47376e67c51e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: EZK 44:24
Text: And in controversy they shall stand in judgment; and they shall judge it according to my judgments: and they shall keep my laws and my statutes in all mine assemblies; and they shall hallow my sabbaths.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9999944-5d1c-425e-b58e-82449f60d0a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: EZK 44:25
Text: And they shall come at no dead person to defile themselves: but for father, or for mother, or for son, or for daughter, for brother, or for sister that hath had no husband, they may defile themselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c08e984-8484-43ba-9077-9622cea72307>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: EZK 44:26
Text: And after he is cleansed, they shall reckon unto him seven days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0efffd1d-be41-4930-a691-1ef324700b1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: EZK 44:27
Text: And in the day that he goeth into the sanctuary, unto the inner court, to minister in the sanctuary, he shall offer his sin offering, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:baedda7d-c443-4f2f-ac84-027bcbd95f7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: EZK 44:28
Text: And it shall be unto them for an inheritance: I am their inheritance: and ye shall give them no possession in Israel: I am their possession.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b35adc18-6e01-4c4e-9d63-12a7cac531c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: EZK 44:29
Text: They shall eat the meat offering, and the sin offering, and the trespass offering: and every dedicated thing in Israel shall be theirs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7ac8723-b1a4-4b97-a9fa-21aab74171ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 279

Reference: EZK 44:30
Text: And the first of all the firstfruits of all things, and every oblation of all, of every sort of your oblations, shall be the priest’s: ye shall also give unto the priest the first of your dough, that he may cause the blessing to rest in thine house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/44/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9191cc53-1939-4b54-b1da-78253a657dba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: EZK 44:31
Text: The priests shall not eat of any thing that is dead of itself, or torn, whether it be fowl or beast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1757312-d599-4bd1-a3fe-26f013a5bf71>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 325

Reference: EZK 45:1
Text: Moreover, when ye shall divide by lot the land for inheritance, ye shall offer an oblation unto the LORD, an holy portion of the land: the length shall be the length of five and twenty thousand reeds, and the breadth shall be ten thousand. This shall be holy in all the borders thereof round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf22e992-232a-4bc4-8603-417fa08b5bcc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: EZK 45:2
Text: Of this there shall be for the sanctuary five hundred in length, with five hundred in breadth, square round about; and fifty cubits round about for the suburbs thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26a7a9ee-d986-4313-9303-555470850e98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: EZK 45:3
Text: And of this measure shalt thou measure the length of five and twenty thousand, and the breadth of ten thousand: and in it shall be the sanctuary and the most holy place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00d89509-2f7c-4473-b9cd-88e39d0060e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: EZK 45:4
Text: The holy portion of the land shall be for the priests the ministers of the sanctuary, which shall come near to minister unto the LORD: and it shall be a place for their houses, and an holy place for the sanctuary.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc30c33f-c5bc-4422-afd1-027b5ae8b33a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: EZK 45:5
Text: And the five and twenty thousand of length, and the ten thousand of breadth shall also the Levites, the ministers of the house, have for themselves, for a possession for twenty chambers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff7f3088-de75-42ca-874f-6a8ce34ba724>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: EZK 45:6
Text: And ye shall appoint the possession of the city five thousand broad, and five and twenty thousand long, over against the oblation of the holy portion: it shall be for the whole house of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a648fd71-23f3-4388-afab-d7fa8ae1174e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 417

Reference: EZK 45:7
Text: And a portion shall be for the prince on the one side and on the other side of the oblation of the holy portion, and of the possession of the city, before the oblation of the holy portion, and before the possession of the city, from the west side westward, and from the east side eastward: and the length shall be over against one of the portions, from the west border unto the east border.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c16e241a-f1b4-4f9e-bc45-1f8d6bca9aed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: EZK 45:8
Text: In the land shall be his possession in Israel: and my princes shall no more oppress my people; and the rest of the land shall they give to the house of Israel according to their tribes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96c4e490-5d12-4544-8eea-150d539e81eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: EZK 45:9
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; Let it suffice you, O princes of Israel: remove violence and spoil, and execute judgment and justice, take away your exactions from my people, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4dbd3928-eec5-40d4-b02b-61da86859bce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: EZK 45:10
Text: Ye shall have just balances, and a just ephah, and a just bath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:445b2cfc-0bb1-4f52-9315-5517affb4636>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: EZK 45:11
Text: The ephah and the bath shall be of one measure, that the bath may contain the tenth part of an homer, and the ephah the tenth part of an homer: the measure thereof shall be after the homer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5208903b-fdd3-4f77-ad55-88e1e5e9651a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: EZK 45:12
Text: And the shekel shall be twenty gerahs: twenty shekels, five and twenty shekels, fifteen shekels, shall be your maneh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1737caf0-39ea-411a-bbd0-bac2ee13d52e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: EZK 45:13
Text: This is the oblation that ye shall offer; the sixth part of an ephah of an homer of wheat, and ye shall give the sixth part of an ephah of an homer of barley:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f64d2e6c-c4a9-4a57-aad2-54ff881e86b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: EZK 45:14
Text: Concerning the ordinance of oil, the bath of oil, ye shall offer the tenth part of a bath out of the cor, which is an homer of ten baths; for ten baths are an homer:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85419a18-bcf0-4848-81ff-a642b514100f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: EZK 45:15
Text: And one lamb out of the flock, out of two hundred, out of the fat pastures of Israel; for a meat offering, and for a burnt offering, and for peace offerings, to make reconciliation for them, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:647f0f70-9243-40cb-88ee-35d18bc487bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: EZK 45:16
Text: All the people of the land shall give this oblation for the prince in Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:755b1a47-a843-4958-a85f-c635500c5096>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 385

Reference: EZK 45:17
Text: And it shall be the prince’s part to give burnt offerings, and meat offerings, and drink offerings, in the feasts, and in the new moons, and in the sabbaths, in all solemnities of the house of Israel: he shall prepare the sin offering, and the meat offering, and the burnt offering, and the peace offerings, to make reconciliation for the house of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b943fcf8-6573-42cb-9df5-408e13fdfec9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: EZK 45:18
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; In the first month, in the first day of the month, thou shalt take a young bullock without blemish, and cleanse the sanctuary:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9dc8f3c-779f-4ecf-a5ba-efde0f35e20d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: EZK 45:19
Text: And the priest shall take of the blood of the sin offering, and put it upon the posts of the house, and upon the four corners of the settle of the altar, and upon the posts of the gate of the inner court.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c81827ca-e92c-4b42-9360-ef1836fa92a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: EZK 45:20
Text: And so thou shalt do the seventh day of the month for every one that erreth, and for him that is simple: so shall ye reconcile the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5aac44fc-a8cf-43a9-a256-bebb1692b1dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: EZK 45:21
Text: In the first month, in the fourteenth day of the month, ye shall have the passover, a feast of seven days; unleavened bread shall be eaten.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb603c86-c670-43e1-94f8-1ba12ce5e0fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: EZK 45:22
Text: And upon that day shall the prince prepare for himself and for all the people of the land a bullock for a sin offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a186dd5-74bf-4be0-a043-27f75913b115>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: EZK 45:23
Text: And seven days of the feast he shall prepare a burnt offering to the LORD, seven bullocks and seven rams without blemish daily the seven days; and a kid of the goats daily for a sin offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49949b52-6574-4d41-9de2-00117b9f9d53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: EZK 45:24
Text: And he shall prepare a meat offering of an ephah for a bullock, and an ephah for a ram, and an hin of oil for an ephah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/45/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd37f6dd-a640-4e11-856c-87776c04881f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: EZK 45:25
Text: In the seventh month, in the fifteenth day of the month, shall he do the like in the feast of the seven days, according to the sin offering, according to the burnt offering, and according to the meat offering, and according to the oil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da01dbfc-bcad-49c6-b9fb-b9462747eecb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: EZK 46:1
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; The gate of the inner court that looketh toward the east shall be shut the six working days; but on the sabbath it shall be opened, and in the day of the new moon it shall be opened.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fe0d226-4967-4148-8c92-37afa639f329>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 339

Reference: EZK 46:2
Text: And the prince shall enter by the way of the porch of that gate without, and shall stand by the post of the gate, and the priests shall prepare his burnt offering and his peace offerings, and he shall worship at the threshold of the gate: then he shall go forth; but the gate shall not be shut until the evening.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23f84302-ac7a-402a-ad62-a84485a2214c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: EZK 46:3
Text: Likewise the people of the land shall worship at the door of this gate before the LORD in the sabbaths and in the new moons.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7112eec5-c26a-4c4d-bab2-ff189bc57051>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: EZK 46:4
Text: And the burnt offering that the prince shall offer unto the LORD in the sabbath day shall be six lambs without blemish, and a ram without blemish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11cc0139-6b20-4931-8c8a-e99f8f4a6a12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: EZK 46:5
Text: And the meat offering shall be an ephah for a ram, and the meat offering for the lambs as he shall be able to give, and an hin of oil to an ephah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e52fd8f2-63df-4802-b798-0181aa2e7a67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: EZK 46:6
Text: And in the day of the new moon it shall be a young bullock without blemish, and six lambs, and a ram: they shall be without blemish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c87e251e-f05f-4730-b03d-e9bff9df793b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: EZK 46:7
Text: And he shall prepare a meat offering, an ephah for a bullock, and an ephah for a ram, and for the lambs according as his hand shall attain unto, and an hin of oil to an ephah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3347cb9-dae5-4748-8e76-9d438bca4ddd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: EZK 46:8
Text: And when the prince shall enter, he shall go in by the way of the porch of that gate, and he shall go forth by the way thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d32845b6-81b1-4ea4-a602-15599a12c6e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 404

Reference: EZK 46:9
Text: But when the people of the land shall come before the LORD in the solemn feasts, he that entereth in by the way of the north gate to worship shall go out by the way of the south gate; and he that entereth by the way of the south gate shall go forth by the way of the north gate: he shall not return by the way of the gate whereby he came in, but shall go forth over against it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5790c9aa-eea3-4bff-bbfc-268e019c2328>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: EZK 46:10
Text: And the prince in the midst of them, when they go in, shall go in; and when they go forth, shall go forth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6094fa39-bd66-41a8-bb04-4387dee79560>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: EZK 46:11
Text: And in the feasts and in the solemnities the meat offering shall be an ephah to a bullock, and an ephah to a ram, and to the lambs as he is able to give, and an hin of oil to an ephah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d261d3a-30d6-4ff8-8202-ed7e92c5b2bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 367

Reference: EZK 46:12
Text: Now when the prince shall prepare a voluntary burnt offering or peace offerings voluntarily unto the LORD, one shall then open him the gate that looketh toward the east, and he shall prepare his burnt offering and his peace offerings, as he did on the sabbath day: then he shall go forth; and after his going forth one shall shut the gate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93a99b42-6eae-4c59-9ddf-81f709c1c501>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: EZK 46:13
Text: Thou shalt daily prepare a burnt offering unto the LORD of a lamb of the first year without blemish: thou shalt prepare it every morning.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77f4df52-3438-48de-9ad9-aa5cf072753d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: EZK 46:14
Text: And thou shalt prepare a meat offering for it every morning, the sixth part of an ephah, and the third part of an hin of oil, to temper with the fine flour; a meat offering continually by a perpetual ordinance unto the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ed52fcd-614e-498c-a0a1-ff02d9631d7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: EZK 46:15
Text: Thus shall they prepare the lamb, and the meat offering, and the oil, every morning for a continual burnt offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6b6c17d-b257-4be9-b88e-2a2a18eb8192>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: EZK 46:16
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; If the prince give a gift unto any of his sons, the inheritance thereof shall be his sons’; it shall be their possession by inheritance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0c78939-08b2-4002-a92d-da950370e70e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: EZK 46:17
Text: But if he give a gift of his inheritance to one of his servants, then it shall be his to the year of liberty; after it shall return to the prince: but his inheritance shall be his sons’ for them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bcc9a95a-2dd6-468e-966d-1ee3385331d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: EZK 46:18
Text: Moreover the prince shall not take of the people’s inheritance by oppression, to thrust them out of their possession; but he shall give his sons inheritance out of his own possession: that my people be not scattered every man from his possession.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67a58259-41a7-489e-81b5-c5cc229761cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: EZK 46:19
Text: After he brought me through the entry, which was at the side of the gate, into the holy chambers of the priests, which looked toward the north: and, behold, there was a place on the two sides westward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa6a4534-92c6-47d1-bda5-907e7211253b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: EZK 46:20
Text: Then said he unto me, This is the place where the priests shall boil the trespass offering and the sin offering, where they shall bake the meat offering; that they bear them not out into the utter court, to sanctify the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ef04320-0da4-4f4d-80cd-718f7a8b4952>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: EZK 46:21
Text: Then he brought me forth into the utter court, and caused me to pass by the four corners of the court; and, behold, in every corner of the court there was a court.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5d28951-b2fd-4ee5-aa6d-f46822c3f826>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: EZK 46:22
Text: In the four corners of the court there were courts joined of forty cubits long and thirty broad: these four corners were of one measure.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66641040-962e-490f-afdb-44dc9c79ab4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: EZK 46:23
Text: And there was a row of building round about in them, round about them four, and it was made with boiling places under the rows round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/46/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ddded6a-fd05-4f64-9e32-e8141ed91e88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: EZK 46:24
Text: Then said he unto me, These are the places of them that boil, where the ministers of the house shall boil the sacrifice of the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/47/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93baa9ab-76d4-4c82-be24-c859df6a73d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 319

Reference: EZK 47:1
Text: Afterward he brought me again unto the door of the house; and, behold, waters issued out from under the threshold of the house eastward: for the forefront of the house stood toward the east, and the waters came down from under from the right side of the house, at the south side of the altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/47/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc2df29b-6580-49a8-b6a4-d0a82859489c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: EZK 47:2
Text: Then brought he me out of the way of the gate northward, and led me about the way without unto the utter gate by the way that looketh eastward; and, behold, there ran out waters on the right side.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/47/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d385255-c344-4a20-9f69-6ec361072b4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: EZK 47:3
Text: And when the man that had the line in his hand went forth eastward, he measured a thousand cubits, and he brought me through the waters; the waters were to the ankles.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/47/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3089cf38-df27-47e5-9f8f-6f40369a8d87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: EZK 47:4
Text: Again he measured a thousand, and brought me through the waters; the waters were to the knees. Again he measured a thousand, and brought me through; the waters were to the loins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/47/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:721cc79f-2859-4607-8d88-ebe93d0aacd8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: EZK 47:5
Text: Afterward he measured a thousand; and it was a river that I could not pass over: for the waters were risen, waters to swim in, a river that could not be passed over.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/47/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4572890b-d03e-4b66-bb52-a4f991aa7a79>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: EZK 47:6
Text: And he said unto me, Son of man, hast thou seen this? Then he brought me, and caused me to return to the brink of the river.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/47/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4664aea7-3c8d-4a02-97f3-70e45a9aa3e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: EZK 47:7
Text: Now when I had returned, behold, at the bank of the river were very many trees on the one side and on the other.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/47/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:665fd3b7-3404-41c4-8a94-10099860fe0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: EZK 47:8
Text: Then said he unto me, These waters issue out toward the east country, and go down into the desert, and go into the sea: which being brought forth into the sea, the waters shall be healed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/47/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5306c83-de7a-49f7-a66a-81e6056a99cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 317

Reference: EZK 47:9
Text: And it shall come to pass, that every thing that liveth, which moveth, whithersoever the rivers shall come, shall live: and there shall be a very great multitude of fish, because these waters shall come thither: for they shall be healed; and every thing shall live whither the river cometh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/47/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bceee144-5a24-43d9-88a7-22eddded83f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: EZK 47:10
Text: And it shall come to pass, that the fishers shall stand upon it from Engedi even unto Eneglaim; they shall be a place to spread forth nets; their fish shall be according to their kinds, as the fish of the great sea, exceeding many.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/47/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20714321-51c3-4b7d-a103-afe7d1e87647>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: EZK 47:11
Text: But the miry places thereof and the marishes thereof shall not be healed; they shall be given to salt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/47/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60375feb-6914-483b-9a66-4dd88795f512>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 388

Reference: EZK 47:12
Text: And by the river upon the bank thereof, on this side and on that side, shall grow all trees for meat, whose leaf shall not fade, neither shall the fruit thereof be consumed: it shall bring forth new fruit according to his months, because their waters they issued out of the sanctuary: and the fruit thereof shall be for meat, and the leaf thereof for medicine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/47/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0da42948-dfec-4e0e-a69f-65596e71da0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: EZK 47:13
Text: Thus saith the Lord GOD; This shall be the border, whereby ye shall inherit the land according to the twelve tribes of Israel: Joseph shall have two portions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/47/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1d2f320-5838-49c4-8609-8d74865cb9a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: EZK 47:14
Text: And ye shall inherit it, one as well as another: concerning the which I lifted up mine hand to give it unto your fathers: and this land shall fall unto you for inheritance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/47/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e5a7026-f201-4c3f-93de-13a0fca51583>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: EZK 47:15
Text: And this shall be the border of the land toward the north side, from the great sea, the way of Hethlon, as men go to Zedad;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/47/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52b2a068-141d-492b-89c4-a75a31b81112>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: EZK 47:16
Text: Hamath, Berothah, Sibraim, which is between the border of Damascus and the border of Hamath; Hazarhatticon, which is by the coast of Hauran.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/47/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc2fc5c1-0d51-4548-a2e6-a5ba80f63364>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: EZK 47:17
Text: And the border from the sea shall be Hazarenan, the border of Damascus, and the north northward, and the border of Hamath. And this is the north side.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/47/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9bb82d39-1832-4e1d-9dae-03b32fd7f1aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: EZK 47:18
Text: And the east side ye shall measure from Hauran, and from Damascus, and from Gilead, and from the land of Israel by Jordan, from the border unto the east sea. And this is the east side.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/47/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f5c8637-82d0-4df8-a3e1-e35810e0801a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: EZK 47:19
Text: And the south side southward, from Tamar even to the waters of strife in Kadesh, the river to the great sea. And this is the south side southward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/47/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b01b44e4-22ef-4f2e-b7c2-08da6470326c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: EZK 47:20
Text: The west side also shall be the great sea from the border, till a man come over against Hamath. This is the west side.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/47/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6952344-f6b9-4951-b26d-bf95bea7512e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: EZK 47:21
Text: So shall ye divide this land unto you according to the tribes of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/47/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:150455f4-b60a-4202-b773-b87cec6727b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 342

Reference: EZK 47:22
Text: And it shall come to pass, that ye shall divide it by lot for an inheritance unto you, and to the strangers that sojourn among you, which shall beget children among you: and they shall be unto you as born in the country among the children of Israel; they shall have inheritance with you among the tribes of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/47/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc2cbcab-eba3-46a7-8139-09705053ac37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: EZK 47:23
Text: And it shall come to pass, that in what tribe the stranger sojourneth, there shall ye give him his inheritance, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
