Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: EZK 48:26
Text: And by the border of Issachar, from the east side unto the west side, Zebulun a portion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/48/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d83d7a29-a5cb-40bc-a209-776a27b038d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: EZK 48:27
Text: And by the border of Zebulun, from the east side unto the west side, Gad a portion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/48/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df62b99a-4cdc-4e53-9a60-3da4a40d8ce9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: EZK 48:28
Text: And by the border of Gad, at the south side southward, the border shall be even from Tamar unto the waters of strife in Kadesh, and to the river toward the great sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/48/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9df8887-a597-4fdc-b525-79c28852decc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: EZK 48:29
Text: This is the land which ye shall divide by lot unto the tribes of Israel for inheritance, and these are their portions, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/48/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7a12968-1b90-4c1a-bd52-7452ec589542>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: EZK 48:30
Text: And these are the goings out of the city on the north side, four thousand and five hundred measures.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/48/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:406855dd-a835-4c34-bc59-816e8e87d63c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: EZK 48:31
Text: And the gates of the city shall be after the names of the tribes of Israel: three gates northward; one gate of Reuben, one gate of Judah, one gate of Levi.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/48/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9295a810-c192-4400-9522-6e72dd41ed63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: EZK 48:32
Text: And at the east side four thousand and five hundred: and three gates; and one gate of Joseph, one gate of Benjamin, one gate of Dan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/48/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7768492-1afa-4b15-9579-1021ba92f8c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: EZK 48:33
Text: And at the south side four thousand and five hundred measures: and three gates; one gate of Simeon, one gate of Issachar, one gate of Zebulun.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/48/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c40a7ca-8c7a-4b60-9ba4-141dd1f0c3ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: EZK 48:34
Text: At the west side four thousand and five hundred, with their three gates; one gate of Gad, one gate of Asher, one gate of Naphtali.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EZK/48/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3bac883b-6f5f-4c8e-9b6c-90ec4ecb1da9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: EZK 48:35
Text: It was round about eighteen thousand measures: and the name of the city from that day shall be, The LORD is there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3119397-69c3-4c19-ad38-9443af36ea5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: DAN 1:1
Text: In the third year of the reign of Jehoiakim king of Judah came Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon unto Jerusalem, and besieged it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8d8cf05-eddd-42d4-8576-0016898f1d9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: DAN 1:2
Text: And the Lord gave Jehoiakim king of Judah into his hand, with part of the vessels of the house of God: which he carried into the land of Shinar to the house of his god; and he brought the vessels into the treasure house of his god.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:756ea23e-6cb8-45d6-b6d8-e4e91a4aafc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: DAN 1:3
Text: And the king spake unto Ashpenaz the master of his eunuchs, that he should bring certain of the children of Israel, and of the king’s seed, and of the princes;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:797ba8fb-fe8b-4bf2-95f2-5434957f7ff0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 294

Reference: DAN 1:4
Text: Children in whom was no blemish, but well favoured, and skilful in all wisdom, and cunning in knowledge, and understanding science, and such as had ability in them to stand in the king’s palace, and whom they might teach the learning and the tongue of the Chaldeans.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6d0fa46-f5a8-472f-b8fa-d80deae7d4da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: DAN 1:5
Text: And the king appointed them a daily provision of the king’s meat, and of the wine which he drank: so nourishing them three years, that at the end thereof they might stand before the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2804e69-1bc0-4cfb-8100-9dd62ad96f51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: DAN 1:6
Text: Now among these were of the children of Judah, Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0121e615-487c-44f3-909c-1089ae8b4380>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: DAN 1:7
Text: Unto whom the prince of the eunuchs gave names: for he gave unto Daniel the name of Belteshazzar; and to Hananiah, of Shadrach; and to Mishael, of Meshach; and to Azariah, of Abednego.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6f52fdc-4b2a-44e4-8935-76371db57f42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: DAN 1:8
Text: But Daniel purposed in his heart that he would not defile himself with the portion of the king’s meat, nor with the wine which he drank: therefore he requested of the prince of the eunuchs that he might not defile himself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa684f39-10c0-4207-8878-568c63544d6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: DAN 1:9
Text: Now God had brought Daniel into favour and tender love with the prince of the eunuchs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3ab9cd6-c11b-41e3-9bd0-3857486057ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: DAN 1:10
Text: And the prince of the eunuchs said unto Daniel, I fear my lord the king, who hath appointed your meat and your drink: for why should he see your faces worse liking than the children which are of your sort? then shall ye make me endanger my head to the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:756d4a21-5ea4-4334-94e6-82bc2a045d78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: DAN 1:11
Text: Then said Daniel to Melzar, whom the prince of the eunuchs had set over Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dcab8960-2da4-4b79-9eff-2d833aab0398>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: DAN 1:12
Text: Prove thy servants, I beseech thee, ten days; and let them give us pulse to eat, and water to drink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e097fdc4-84f7-4f26-953d-7fedbb99ab55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: DAN 1:13
Text: Then let our countenances be looked upon before thee, and the countenance of the children that eat of the portion of the king’s meat: and as thou seest, deal with thy servants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c9e43f7-7bad-4797-bc38-5004a8aa013b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: DAN 1:14
Text: So he consented to them in this matter, and proved them ten days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74966045-3688-4237-908e-3612bd3d560b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: DAN 1:15
Text: And at the end of ten days their countenances appeared fairer and fatter in flesh than all the children which did eat the portion of the king’s meat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:967a7b62-e573-4e79-9ea8-bbd445b509e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: DAN 1:16
Text: Thus Melzar took away the portion of their meat, and the wine that they should drink; and gave them pulse.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b38b597a-874f-4451-83b8-9631eae498d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: DAN 1:17
Text: As for these four children, God gave them knowledge and skill in all learning and wisdom: and Daniel had understanding in all visions and dreams.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa1e72b7-b716-42ba-9164-5f87d410fa36>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: DAN 1:18
Text: Now at the end of the days that the king had said he should bring them in, then the prince of the eunuchs brought them in before Nebuchadnezzar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7678af2e-08d2-46f2-acdd-63e120927b2f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: DAN 1:19
Text: And the king communed with them; and among them all was found none like Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah: therefore stood they before the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b870d6e6-20ca-40c8-9148-1b23e64d4b33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: DAN 1:20
Text: And in all matters of wisdom and understanding, that the king enquired of them, he found them ten times better than all the magicians and astrologers that were in all his realm.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/1/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7afca30e-d640-4dac-90b0-80b8fbd4f112>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: DAN 1:21
Text: And Daniel continued even unto the first year of king Cyrus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2e14091-7066-4f94-a131-098b6cce4d70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: DAN 2:1
Text: And in the second year of the reign of Nebuchadnezzar Nebuchadnezzar dreamed dreams, wherewith his spirit was troubled, and his sleep brake from him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61b42662-56d5-4bb0-bbd7-5a69811ba16d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: DAN 2:2
Text: Then the king commanded to call the magicians, and the astrologers, and the sorcerers, and the Chaldeans, for to shew the king his dreams. So they came and stood before the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5922734-8955-4b6c-9354-19a48fcab061>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: DAN 2:3
Text: And the king said unto them, I have dreamed a dream, and my spirit was troubled to know the dream.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:103dffd5-8076-4c8b-ab5b-4a3ffb076197>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: DAN 2:4
Text: Then spake the Chaldeans to the king in Syriack, O king, live for ever: tell thy servants the dream, and we will shew the interpretation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b6843a4-995f-4703-9578-be073ffc6b64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: DAN 2:5
Text: The king answered and said to the Chaldeans, The thing is gone from me: if ye will not make known unto me the dream, with the interpretation thereof, ye shall be cut in pieces, and your houses shall be made a dunghill.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d52708e-e360-4802-84a0-94c963b5ce28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: DAN 2:6
Text: But if ye shew the dream, and the interpretation thereof, ye shall receive of me gifts and rewards and great honour: therefore shew me the dream, and the interpretation thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a2bba44-5aa0-45ba-874c-2658fac2308a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: DAN 2:7
Text: They answered again and said, Let the king tell his servants the dream, and we will shew the interpretation of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4e1ca6d-a5b6-4221-a0c9-2c645f8dfd89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: DAN 2:8
Text: The king answered and said, I know of certainty that ye would gain the time, because ye see the thing is gone from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:baee1ffd-c9fd-43d5-b4a4-47420cda6ba6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 292

Reference: DAN 2:9
Text: But if ye will not make known unto me the dream, there is but one decree for you: for ye have prepared lying and corrupt words to speak before me, till the time be changed: therefore tell me the dream, and I shall know that ye can shew me the interpretation thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d808755-aca5-4455-be1f-719ac283b32b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: DAN 2:10
Text: The Chaldeans answered before the king, and said, There is not a man upon the earth that can shew the king’s matter: therefore there is no king, lord, nor ruler, that asked such things at any magician, or astrologer, or Chaldean.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf1b9390-23f2-4bc1-959d-9c8ed04245f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: DAN 2:11
Text: And it is a rare thing that the king requireth, and there is none other that can shew it before the king, except the gods, whose dwelling is not with flesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4efa8092-f28b-41ec-bfcb-fc691bd0d126>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: DAN 2:12
Text: For this cause the king was angry and very furious, and commanded to destroy all the wise men of Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e1de017-79ec-4670-b7d2-27d835e78887>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: DAN 2:13
Text: And the decree went forth that the wise men should be slain; and they sought Daniel and his fellows to be slain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93f55688-70dd-4b75-a448-b91e94f7149d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: DAN 2:14
Text: Then Daniel answered with counsel and wisdom to Arioch the captain of the king’s guard, which was gone forth to slay the wise men of Babylon:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d031d140-9456-4db3-b070-a11a69eb6adc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: DAN 2:15
Text: He answered and said to Arioch the king’s captain, Why is the decree so hasty from the king? Then Arioch made the thing known to Daniel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9e6ce7e-515f-4965-b735-8099d2b49481>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: DAN 2:16
Text: Then Daniel went in, and desired of the king that he would give him time, and that he would shew the king the interpretation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:598260be-b168-45b4-b1f3-868a600c9a44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: DAN 2:17
Text: Then Daniel went to his house, and made the thing known to Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah, his companions:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7c3bf18-51fc-424b-bba7-26201f3352a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: DAN 2:18
Text: That they would desire mercies of the God of heaven concerning this secret; that Daniel and his fellows should not perish with the rest of the wise men of Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af4ed789-dd8c-44a7-a8b3-5ab061a30ff8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: DAN 2:19
Text: Then was the secret revealed unto Daniel in a night vision. Then Daniel blessed the God of heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e501f59-d6b8-4924-8548-8703fd734789>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: DAN 2:20
Text: Daniel answered and said, Blessed be the name of God for ever and ever: for wisdom and might are his:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f683bdd-0b76-42bd-8e08-b0ce3d00310d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: DAN 2:21
Text: And he changeth the times and the seasons: he removeth kings, and setteth up kings: he giveth wisdom unto the wise, and knowledge to them that know understanding:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:458a41b7-8cb5-4a30-99f4-968df5668362>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: DAN 2:22
Text: He revealeth the deep and secret things: he knoweth what is in the darkness, and the light dwelleth with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2a90ec1-bff1-46cb-8e4e-52e729c2c8c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: DAN 2:23
Text: I thank thee, and praise thee, O thou God of my fathers, who hast given me wisdom and might, and hast made known unto me now what we desired of thee: for thou hast now made known unto us the king’s matter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c11b6f0d-fe03-42cd-874b-8556ab0751a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: DAN 2:24
Text: Therefore Daniel went in unto Arioch, whom the king had ordained to destroy the wise men of Babylon: he went and said thus unto him; Destroy not the wise men of Babylon: bring me in before the king, and I will shew unto the king the interpretation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f31545be-1f45-41f1-8d79-339af784ffc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: DAN 2:25
Text: Then Arioch brought in Daniel before the king in haste, and said thus unto him, I have found a man of the captives of Judah, that will make known unto the king the interpretation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1416e51c-b3ab-486c-a358-e8618adeb13b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: DAN 2:26
Text: The king answered and said to Daniel, whose name was Belteshazzar, Art thou able to make known unto me the dream which I have seen, and the interpretation thereof?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dca1b04c-c924-4a2e-b8b1-7a504f296c91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: DAN 2:27
Text: Daniel answered in the presence of the king, and said, The secret which the king hath demanded cannot the wise men, the astrologers, the magicians, the soothsayers, shew unto the king;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df21cb78-1612-4b5d-ab7f-81ea32a63619>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: DAN 2:28
Text: But there is a God in heaven that revealeth secrets, and maketh known to the king Nebuchadnezzar what shall be in the latter days. Thy dream, and the visions of thy head upon thy bed, are these;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7481ef7c-5702-4abe-a361-44b848834d1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: DAN 2:29
Text: As for thee, O king, thy thoughts came into thy mind upon thy bed, what should come to pass hereafter: and he that revealeth secrets maketh known to thee what shall come to pass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86769902-38ff-44a0-8535-c2fda6234e6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: DAN 2:30
Text: But as for me, this secret is not revealed to me for any wisdom that I have more than any living, but for their sakes that shall make known the interpretation to the king, and that thou mightest know the thoughts of thy heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7bc6226-5153-4dbc-99e2-065767bbc3b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: DAN 2:31
Text: Thou, O king, sawest, and behold a great image. This great image, whose brightness was excellent, stood before thee; and the form thereof was terrible.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df9bf2b4-decd-4152-8917-405f2d2a3866>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: DAN 2:32
Text: This image’s head was of fine gold, his breast and his arms of silver, his belly and his thighs of brass,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cba7bcb0-dfd7-43ab-aeb5-f9641b101af9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: DAN 2:33
Text: His legs of iron, his feet part of iron and part of clay.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6dc6454-9b39-48a4-b0b8-1b6b2d321a0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: DAN 2:34
Text: Thou sawest till that a stone was cut out without hands, which smote the image upon his feet that were of iron and clay, and brake them to pieces.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f9f7801-2587-44a1-ad33-3cf7bc1efd84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 330

Reference: DAN 2:35
Text: Then was the iron, the clay, the brass, the silver, and the gold, broken to pieces together, and became like the chaff of the summer threshingfloors; and the wind carried them away, that no place was found for them: and the stone that smote the image became a great mountain, and filled the whole earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ff3a5c8-fb27-4a88-8ae8-03e6b30365e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: DAN 2:36
Text: This is the dream; and we will tell the interpretation thereof before the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c70f12a7-6df0-4a02-aabd-c0946b39f4aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: DAN 2:37
Text: Thou, O king, art a king of kings: for the God of heaven hath given thee a kingdom, power, and strength, and glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22f823c1-a6e2-4cd6-89bd-d8c67437db64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: DAN 2:38
Text: And wheresoever the children of men dwell, the beasts of the field and the fowls of the heaven hath he given into thine hand, and hath made thee ruler over them all. Thou art this head of gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1b510e4-ef1a-48c2-be98-fed375c85159>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: DAN 2:39
Text: And after thee shall arise another kingdom inferior to thee, and another third kingdom of brass, which shall bear rule over all the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c5148e6-27cc-403c-80b3-a4fa4813f3de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: DAN 2:40
Text: And the fourth kingdom shall be strong as iron: forasmuch as iron breaketh in pieces and subdueth all things: and as iron that breaketh all these, shall it break in pieces and bruise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe18f4f0-4084-4698-bf15-ac397a23ed82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: DAN 2:41
Text: And whereas thou sawest the feet and toes, part of potters’ clay, and part of iron, the kingdom shall be divided; but there shall be in it of the strength of the iron, forasmuch as thou sawest the iron mixed with miry clay.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c95b6a37-f8e9-4ddb-8eaf-e94ae558e9ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: DAN 2:42
Text: And as the toes of the feet were part of iron, and part of clay, so the kingdom shall be partly strong, and partly broken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:070ab93a-2b2f-4d09-8067-0c48a9d59693>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: DAN 2:43
Text: And whereas thou sawest iron mixed with miry clay, they shall mingle themselves with the seed of men: but they shall not cleave one to another, even as iron is not mixed with clay.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3578e2dc-9737-4e97-93fb-46675ac8fd0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: DAN 2:44
Text: And in the days of these kings shall the God of heaven set up a kingdom, which shall never be destroyed: and the kingdom shall not be left to other people, but it shall break in pieces and consume all these kingdoms, and it shall stand for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41a1feda-e2f8-4c6f-b906-00270046150c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 334

Reference: DAN 2:45
Text: Forasmuch as thou sawest that the stone was cut out of the mountain without hands, and that it brake in pieces the iron, the brass, the clay, the silver, and the gold; the great God hath made known to the king what shall come to pass hereafter: and the dream is certain, and the interpretation thereof sure.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:173c27e8-a5b2-4692-921b-9ad5e5c7e55c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: DAN 2:46
Text: Then the king Nebuchadnezzar fell upon his face, and worshipped Daniel, and commanded that they should offer an oblation and sweet odours unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65f103b8-6c62-42dc-9152-6a608cc871ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: DAN 2:47
Text: The king answered unto Daniel, and said, Of a truth it is, that your God is a God of gods, and a Lord of kings, and a revealer of secrets, seeing thou couldest reveal this secret.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfd8618c-a323-4656-9d2f-236a66768446>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: DAN 2:48
Text: Then the king made Daniel a great man, and gave him many great gifts, and made him ruler over the whole province of Babylon, and chief of the governors over all the wise men of Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/2/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a495ac23-7f3e-4343-8491-a1d30a1b5569>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: DAN 2:49
Text: Then Daniel requested of the king, and he set Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, over the affairs of the province of Babylon: but Daniel sat in the gate of the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c2034df-3c20-4a9c-8a06-9d9aef5e4a94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: DAN 3:1
Text: Nebuchadnezzar the king made an image of gold, whose height was threescore cubits, and the breadth thereof six cubits: he set it up in the plain of Dura, in the province of Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1728ccf7-5cd1-4f78-9f68-3bcab4bec7b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 301

Reference: DAN 3:2
Text: Then Nebuchadnezzar the king sent to gather together the princes, the governors, and the captains, the judges, the treasurers, the counsellors, the sheriffs, and all the rulers of the provinces, to come to the dedication of the image which Nebuchadnezzar the king had set up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f55d7fca-bb44-433b-ba1f-0c0b7cdd9926>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 329

Reference: DAN 3:3
Text: Then the princes, the governors, and captains, the judges, the treasurers, the counsellors, the sheriffs, and all the rulers of the provinces, were gathered together unto the dedication of the image that Nebuchadnezzar the king had set up; and they stood before the image that Nebuchadnezzar had set up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70b5efbe-a79d-420a-9d2c-1676f9723065>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: DAN 3:4
Text: Then an herald cried aloud, To you it is commanded, O people, nations, and languages,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8fbb0616-ec5b-4563-8875-5cee7d578a76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: DAN 3:5
Text: That at what time ye hear the sound of the cornet, flute, harp, sackbut, psaltery, dulcimer, and all kinds of musick, ye fall down and worship the golden image that Nebuchadnezzar the king hath set up:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03ab2f80-e69a-47aa-b9e1-7c931e7f750e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: DAN 3:6
Text: And whoso falleth not down and worshippeth shall the same hour be cast into the midst of a burning fiery furnace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbffcf7c-37d8-470d-ae78-d35920416352>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 288

Reference: DAN 3:7
Text: Therefore at that time, when all the people heard the sound of the cornet, flute, harp, sackbut, psaltery, and all kinds of musick, all the people, the nations, and the languages, fell down and worshipped the golden image that Nebuchadnezzar the king had set up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4feeab76-1c82-4dd8-87e5-51b65cb51e42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: DAN 3:8
Text: Wherefore at that time certain Chaldeans came near, and accused the Jews.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50b60810-53a8-4fd0-87e9-e5630da3e7cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: DAN 3:9
Text: They spake and said to the king Nebuchadnezzar, O king, live for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88a12e12-e237-4fa6-96c8-8f1af8261ea6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: DAN 3:10
Text: Thou, O king, hast made a decree, that every man that shall hear the sound of the cornet, flute, harp, sackbut, psaltery, and dulcimer, and all kinds of musick, shall fall down and worship the golden image:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0bd76cf-df97-4859-b1a1-aee66cdefa32>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: DAN 3:11
Text: And whoso falleth not down and worshippeth, that he should be cast into the midst of a burning fiery furnace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:787ef809-ef09-4907-9434-acecda11f0cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: DAN 3:12
Text: There are certain Jews whom thou hast set over the affairs of the province of Babylon, Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego; these men, O king, have not regarded thee: they serve not thy gods, nor worship the golden image which thou hast set up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1172c325-3e9d-4cfc-8cae-1ecbe5d606ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: DAN 3:13
Text: Then Nebuchadnezzar in his rage and fury commanded to bring Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego. Then they brought these men before the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64938da5-e596-4a47-a320-5523469816a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: DAN 3:14
Text: Nebuchadnezzar spake and said unto them, Is it true, O Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, do not ye serve my gods, nor worship the golden image which I have set up?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ca8e45d-0530-4723-bf7a-869c0e4600f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 384

Reference: DAN 3:15
Text: Now if ye be ready that at what time ye hear the sound of the cornet, flute, harp, sackbut, psaltery, and dulcimer, and all kinds of musick, ye fall down and worship the image which I have made; well: but if ye worship not, ye shall be cast the same hour into the midst of a burning fiery furnace; and who is that God that shall deliver you out of my hands?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d56c8288-a860-44c6-887c-eaba9974081d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: DAN 3:16
Text: Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, answered and said to the king, O Nebuchadnezzar, we are not careful to answer thee in this matter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e60b6935-5e84-464c-b630-6e1ef7423a77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: DAN 3:17
Text: If it be so, our God whom we serve is able to deliver us from the burning fiery furnace, and he will deliver us out of thine hand, O king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa64d419-a73f-4703-beb9-cb5c68e920d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: DAN 3:18
Text: But if not, be it known unto thee, O king, that we will not serve thy gods, nor worship the golden image which thou hast set up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:105ee500-f36e-4e7b-ae2e-38768cf7f063>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: DAN 3:19
Text: Then was Nebuchadnezzar full of fury, and the form of his visage was changed against Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego: therefore he spake, and commanded that they should heat the furnace one seven times more than it was wont to be heated.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0556f38-72b3-4547-92f9-a8ad4809843f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: DAN 3:20
Text: And he commanded the most mighty men that were in his army to bind Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, and to cast them into the burning fiery furnace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48ccc49a-0f89-4813-9012-34a2f34a97bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: DAN 3:21
Text: Then these men were bound in their coats, their hosen, and their hats, and their other garments, and were cast into the midst of the burning fiery furnace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7913f28a-131e-4a5a-b92d-ebee4bf4a475>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: DAN 3:22
Text: Therefore because the king’s commandment was urgent, and the furnace exceeding hot, the flames of the fire slew those men that took up Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebfa60d9-9acc-4c71-934a-4ab21a141743>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: DAN 3:23
Text: And these three men, Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, fell down bound into the midst of the burning fiery furnace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca382512-f6e1-4e08-90e9-3631340f28de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: DAN 3:24
Text: Then Nebuchadnezzar the king was astonied, and rose up in haste, and spake, and said unto his counsellors, Did not we cast three men bound into the midst of the fire? They answered and said unto the king, True, O king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd411636-7cb2-4180-b336-f3943f3a92f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: DAN 3:25
Text: He answered and said, Lo, I see four men loose, walking in the midst of the fire, and they have no hurt; and the form of the fourth is like the Son of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:024bbc2c-9cc3-4ebd-b68a-de2e3657251e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 291

Reference: DAN 3:26
Text: Then Nebuchadnezzar came near to the mouth of the burning fiery furnace, and spake, and said, Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, ye servants of the most high God, come forth, and come hither. Then Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, came forth of the midst of the fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c058bf7a-094f-4344-8e24-799fcea54351>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 293

Reference: DAN 3:27
Text: And the princes, governors, and captains, and the king’s counsellors, being gathered together, saw these men, upon whose bodies the fire had no power, nor was an hair of their head singed, neither were their coats changed, nor the smell of fire had passed on them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81cec159-5d26-4d1d-a859-b865ae54e608>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 322

Reference: DAN 3:28
Text: Then Nebuchadnezzar spake, and said, Blessed be the God of Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, who hath sent his angel, and delivered his servants that trusted in him, and have changed the king’s word, and yielded their bodies, that they might not serve nor worship any god, except their own God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1807da8-aad5-4607-9dc9-86772927f5ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 305

Reference: DAN 3:29
Text: Therefore I make a decree, That every people, nation, and language, which speak any thing amiss against the God of Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, shall be cut in pieces, and their houses shall be made a dunghill: because there is no other God that can deliver after this sort.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/3/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc7ddd45-c54c-4868-8bea-fd395695922d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: DAN 3:30
Text: Then the king promoted Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, in the province of Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8b040b7-b248-47f3-9231-26c414968c94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: DAN 4:1
Text: Nebuchadnezzar the king, unto all people, nations, and languages, that dwell in all the earth; Peace be multiplied unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67273d0b-c326-412b-a6fa-cc12b38d2e75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: DAN 4:2
Text: I thought it good to shew the signs and wonders that the high God hath wrought toward me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0a1db89-0dbc-4839-a05d-8a8018d040bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: DAN 4:3
Text: How great are his signs! and how mighty are his wonders! his kingdom is an everlasting kingdom, and his dominion is from generation to generation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26b98a0f-b251-44e5-a4f3-3e27b9c7becc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: DAN 4:4
Text: I Nebuchadnezzar was at rest in mine house, and flourishing in my palace:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9fa2b03-d364-4c06-b805-f66bf412296b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: DAN 4:5
Text: I saw a dream which made me afraid, and the thoughts upon my bed and the visions of my head troubled me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7010ef15-1b8c-4804-be2f-d49201fc4d66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: DAN 4:6
Text: Therefore made I a decree to bring in all the wise men of Babylon before me, that they might make known unto me the interpretation of the dream.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3d39be8-be75-4707-ab24-670cf75178e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: DAN 4:7
Text: Then came in the magicians, the astrologers, the Chaldeans, and the soothsayers: and I told the dream before them; but they did not make known unto me the interpretation thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d769e1be-e6f5-43b9-b6c9-74d1bd11b2c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: DAN 4:8
Text: But at the last Daniel came in before me, whose name was Belteshazzar, according to the name of my God, and in whom is the spirit of the holy gods: and before him I told the dream, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ba96dd0-bfe5-4d9d-80f4-2ade9395ae96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: DAN 4:9
Text: O Belteshazzar, master of the magicians, because I know that the spirit of the holy gods is in thee, and no secret troubleth thee, tell me the visions of my dream that I have seen, and the interpretation thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfcce364-28b8-44d0-b266-86b52c97aa0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: DAN 4:10
Text: Thus were the visions of mine head in my bed; I saw, and behold a tree in the midst of the earth, and the height thereof was great.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f111e7df-e65e-4f96-a5e0-a3f62adcd052>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: DAN 4:11
Text: The tree grew, and was strong, and the height thereof reached unto heaven, and the sight thereof to the end of all the earth:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2946dd9a-225f-44e7-b25c-0956bc274658>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: DAN 4:12
Text: The leaves thereof were fair, and the fruit thereof much, and in it was meat for all: the beasts of the field had shadow under it, and the fowls of the heaven dwelt in the boughs thereof, and all flesh was fed of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6228ff76-e7c4-49f3-9b80-77f9a3261eed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: DAN 4:13
Text: I saw in the visions of my head upon my bed, and, behold, a watcher and an holy one came down from heaven;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91f4d54d-76d0-42f3-bc47-529646617d45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: DAN 4:14
Text: He cried aloud, and said thus, Hew down the tree, and cut off his branches, shake off his leaves, and scatter his fruit: let the beasts get away from under it, and the fowls from his branches:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bfa9558b-7f70-4eca-89a1-abeb1e0135c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: DAN 4:15
Text: Nevertheless leave the stump of his roots in the earth, even with a band of iron and brass, in the tender grass of the field; and let it be wet with the dew of heaven, and let his portion be with the beasts in the grass of the earth:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d23db6e-74cd-48ec-8e2e-3b8f3591c911>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: DAN 4:16
Text: Let his heart be changed from man’s, and let a beast’s heart be given unto him; and let seven times pass over him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34bf0c33-3c71-4b56-b186-c988c842e5ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: DAN 4:17
Text: This matter is by the decree of the watchers, and the demand by the word of the holy ones: to the intent that the living may know that the most High ruleth in the kingdom of men, and giveth it to whomsoever he will, and setteth up over it the basest of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b8e5425-d3ae-4077-892c-5446d8c731f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 294

Reference: DAN 4:18
Text: This dream I king Nebuchadnezzar have seen. Now thou, O Belteshazzar, declare the interpretation thereof, forasmuch as all the wise men of my kingdom are not able to make known unto me the interpretation: but thou art able; for the spirit of the holy gods is in thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe300a88-1bbf-4b9f-8cfd-ef3fda08155d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 357

Reference: DAN 4:19
Text: Then Daniel, whose name was Belteshazzar, was astonied for one hour, and his thoughts troubled him. The king spake, and said, Belteshazzar, let not the dream, or the interpretation thereof, trouble thee. Belteshazzar answered and said, My lord, the dream be to them that hate thee, and the interpretation thereof to thine enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0f5cabe-473a-455e-aaa3-f7c108b92111>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: DAN 4:20
Text: The tree that thou sawest, which grew, and was strong, whose height reached unto the heaven, and the sight thereof to all the earth;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:162495d2-2972-45cb-b5f4-b875e05b3d05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: DAN 4:21
Text: Whose leaves were fair, and the fruit thereof much, and in it was meat for all; under which the beasts of the field dwelt, and upon whose branches the fowls of the heaven had their habitation:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16243ab9-d086-4476-a166-122b03896bca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: DAN 4:22
Text: It is thou, O king, that art grown and become strong: for thy greatness is grown, and reacheth unto heaven, and thy dominion to the end of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9de24fb-d8c1-48b6-a09c-52f089f6fb42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 401

Reference: DAN 4:23
Text: And whereas the king saw a watcher and an holy one coming down from heaven, and saying, Hew the tree down, and destroy it; yet leave the stump of the roots thereof in the earth, even with a band of iron and brass, in the tender grass of the field; and let it be wet with the dew of heaven, and let his portion be with the beasts of the field, till seven times pass over him;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f7d9232-f69f-4d8e-80d5-53eb09d2557b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: DAN 4:24
Text: This is the interpretation, O king, and this is the decree of the most High, which is come upon my lord the king:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81033567-b7e0-42f6-a07f-db7a9d5690cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 353

Reference: DAN 4:25
Text: That they shall drive thee from men, and thy dwelling shall be with the beasts of the field, and they shall make thee to eat grass as oxen, and they shall wet thee with the dew of heaven, and seven times shall pass over thee, till thou know that the most High ruleth in the kingdom of men, and giveth it to whomsoever he will.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f384391-b511-452c-b31e-a254950b4d74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: DAN 4:26
Text: And whereas they commanded to leave the stump of the tree roots; thy kingdom shall be sure unto thee, after that thou shalt have known that the heavens do rule.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac945809-35e1-4171-a7cb-bcfdae41a01a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: DAN 4:27
Text: Wherefore, O king, let my counsel be acceptable unto thee, and break off thy sins by righteousness, and thine iniquities by shewing mercy to the poor; if it may be a lengthening of thy tranquillity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8a5ddfc-e655-4b5d-99e8-21767da738df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 70

Reference: DAN 4:28
Text: All this came upon the king Nebuchadnezzar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86798855-c301-4b6f-9a0d-8f76d27e6cd2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: DAN 4:29
Text: At the end of twelve months he walked in the palace of the kingdom of Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0d6257d-b5cc-4c86-9993-3bc541e8db4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: DAN 4:30
Text: The king spake, and said, Is not this great Babylon, that I have built for the house of the kingdom by the might of my power, and for the honour of my majesty?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7b7a99d-296a-4225-a6a4-2d483f9bd635>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: DAN 4:31
Text: While the word was in the king’s mouth, there fell a voice from heaven, saying, O king Nebuchadnezzar, to thee it is spoken; The kingdom is departed from thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f105d3b-9a1f-4818-8437-517099339359>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 301

Reference: DAN 4:32
Text: And they shall drive thee from men, and thy dwelling shall be with the beasts of the field: they shall make thee to eat grass as oxen, and seven times shall pass over thee, until thou know that the most High ruleth in the kingdom of men, and giveth it to whomsoever he will.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:234ead49-937d-4fdc-91e8-c715d9bdc649>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: DAN 4:33
Text: The same hour was the thing fulfilled upon Nebuchadnezzar: and he was driven from men, and did eat grass as oxen, and his body was wet with the dew of heaven, till his hairs were grown like eagles’ feathers, and his nails like birds’ claws.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3fba6449-45e7-4711-aaf4-5e03ccc7f43d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 319

Reference: DAN 4:34
Text: And at the end of the days I Nebuchadnezzar lifted up mine eyes unto heaven, and mine understanding returned unto me, and I blessed the most High, and I praised and honoured him that liveth for ever, whose dominion is an everlasting dominion, and his kingdom is from generation to generation:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb8cb223-7ab8-4c69-a3bc-d1bcf3bb4b75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: DAN 4:35
Text: And all the inhabitants of the earth are reputed as nothing: and he doeth according to his will in the army of heaven, and among the inhabitants of the earth: and none can stay his hand, or say unto him, What doest thou?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec631706-1695-4df5-907a-4c24bd9fd6fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: DAN 4:36
Text: At the same time my reason returned unto me; and for the glory of my kingdom, mine honour and brightness returned unto me; and my counsellors and my lords sought unto me; and I was established in my kingdom, and excellent majesty was added unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/4/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d29772b-4f53-4247-aae5-ebd05374e9d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: DAN 4:37
Text: Now I Nebuchadnezzar praise and extol and honour the King of heaven, all whose works are truth, and his ways judgment: and those that walk in pride he is able to abase.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a7b4874-8a55-49a7-803d-68e026d96743>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: DAN 5:1
Text: Belshazzar the king made a great feast to a thousand of his lords, and drank wine before the thousand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c3fa09a-f32e-4553-a940-65dcde0323c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 281

Reference: DAN 5:2
Text: Belshazzar, whiles he tasted the wine, commanded to bring the golden and silver vessels which his father Nebuchadnezzar had taken out of the temple which was in Jerusalem; that the king, and his princes, his wives, and his concubines, might drink therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8f79004-7cf0-4cad-803d-125dd483d204>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: DAN 5:3
Text: Then they brought the golden vessels that were taken out of the temple of the house of God which was at Jerusalem; and the king, and his princes, his wives, and his concubines, drank in them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d71924eb-5e3c-4112-9d2b-7f86793e6de4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: DAN 5:4
Text: They drank wine, and praised the gods of gold, and of silver, of brass, of iron, of wood, and of stone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9bf8e5e6-766f-42a1-9a16-e5ba09b8e103>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: DAN 5:5
Text: In the same hour came forth fingers of a man’s hand, and wrote over against the candlestick upon the plaister of the wall of the king’s palace: and the king saw the part of the hand that wrote.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:534773d8-8156-4a7d-9209-4e91cc00f662>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: DAN 5:6
Text: Then the king’s countenance was changed, and his thoughts troubled him, so that the joints of his loins were loosed, and his knees smote one against another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c116154-f530-48c8-94ad-e165daa3654b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 360

Reference: DAN 5:7
Text: The king cried aloud to bring in the astrologers, the Chaldeans, and the soothsayers. And the king spake, and said to the wise men of Babylon, Whosoever shall read this writing, and shew me the interpretation thereof, shall be clothed with scarlet, and have a chain of gold about his neck, and shall be the third ruler in the kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e72daf1-5c11-4bf2-9719-09aa9f76d614>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: DAN 5:8
Text: Then came in all the king’s wise men: but they could not read the writing, nor make known to the king the interpretation thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cff501c-0578-46cd-9c9e-d2deb5fd6d4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: DAN 5:9
Text: Then was king Belshazzar greatly troubled, and his countenance was changed in him, and his lords were astonied.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1c4cbd9-c443-46f5-bb98-796a6607d155>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: DAN 5:10
Text: Now the queen by reason of the words of the king and his lords came into the banquet house: and the queen spake and said, O king, live for ever: let not thy thoughts trouble thee, nor let thy countenance be changed:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00ff6444-eb08-43fa-8777-eb9eac12b045>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 351

Reference: DAN 5:11
Text: There is a man in thy kingdom, in whom is the spirit of the holy gods; and in the days of thy father light and understanding and wisdom, like the wisdom of the gods, was found in him; whom the king Nebuchadnezzar thy father, the king, I say, thy father, made master of the magicians, astrologers, Chaldeans, and soothsayers;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e30a1d9-992b-4e36-887a-27422d3c6ee7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 303

Reference: DAN 5:12
Text: Forasmuch as an excellent spirit, and knowledge, and understanding, interpreting of dreams, and shewing of hard sentences, and dissolving of doubts, were found in the same Daniel, whom the king named Belteshazzar: now let Daniel be called, and he will shew the interpretation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e750712a-5cb9-48b6-a45b-cf3e03337d9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: DAN 5:13
Text: Then was Daniel brought in before the king. And the king spake and said unto Daniel, Art thou that Daniel, which art of the children of the captivity of Judah, whom the king my father brought out of Jewry?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d26dfa88-a24f-4f2d-9ba0-a5617b7ad869>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: DAN 5:14
Text: I have even heard of thee, that the spirit of the gods is in thee, and that light and understanding and excellent wisdom is found in thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3b05236-1ab0-4f8d-8d7f-021135959a8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: DAN 5:15
Text: And now the wise men, the astrologers, have been brought in before me, that they should read this writing, and make known unto me the interpretation thereof: but they could not shew the interpretation of the thing:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27d6b35b-e587-407c-9aa2-c19a8812b9bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 318

Reference: DAN 5:16
Text: And I have heard of thee, that thou canst make interpretations, and dissolve doubts: now if thou canst read the writing, and make known to me the interpretation thereof, thou shalt be clothed with scarlet, and have a chain of gold about thy neck, and shalt be the third ruler in the kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db11f819-00ff-4460-9882-119bd1c21fd2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: DAN 5:17
Text: Then Daniel answered and said before the king, Let thy gifts be to thyself, and give thy rewards to another; yet I will read the writing unto the king, and make known to him the interpretation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:514a2b58-68c5-43b1-bb8f-2265873d2b0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: DAN 5:18
Text: O thou king, the most high God gave Nebuchadnezzar thy father a kingdom, and majesty, and glory, and honour:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41914993-51b6-4f75-b117-26005c131179>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: DAN 5:19
Text: And for the majesty that he gave him, all people, nations, and languages, trembled and feared before him: whom he would he slew; and whom he would he kept alive; and whom he would he set up; and whom he would he put down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c5d533d-e7cd-4670-8e78-3e7d8c0315a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: DAN 5:20
Text: But when his heart was lifted up, and his mind hardened in pride, he was deposed from his kingly throne, and they took his glory from him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bdb8155-829e-4841-8328-3e321088d74d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 344

Reference: DAN 5:21
Text: And he was driven from the sons of men; and his heart was made like the beasts, and his dwelling was with the wild asses: they fed him with grass like oxen, and his body was wet with the dew of heaven; till he knew that the most high God ruled in the kingdom of men, and that he appointeth over it whomsoever he will.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:190bab0e-c883-476b-aafa-7580f7ea1f25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: DAN 5:22
Text: And thou his son, O Belshazzar, hast not humbled thine heart, though thou knewest all this;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7df664e-bbec-4902-a530-fe99afebd004>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 436

Reference: DAN 5:23
Text: But hast lifted up thyself against the Lord of heaven; and they have brought the vessels of his house before thee, and thou, and thy lords, thy wives, and thy concubines, have drunk wine in them; and thou hast praised the gods of silver, and gold, of brass, iron, wood, and stone, which see not, nor hear, nor know: and the God in whose hand thy breath is, and whose are all thy ways, hast thou not glorified:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72dd7b1d-69dd-4814-a933-4b01c30d4930>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: DAN 5:24
Text: Then was the part of the hand sent from him; and this writing was written.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb901851-1372-43b8-bd12-339e636ed382>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: DAN 5:25
Text: And this is the writing that was written, MENE, MENE, TEKEL, UPHARSIN.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ca8c31f-e37f-4f7a-9c38-0ab4fc727aa0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: DAN 5:26
Text: This is the interpretation of the thing: MENE; God hath numbered thy kingdom, and finished it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ba3d75d-1345-4210-99a2-4cc20ac4b41a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: DAN 5:27
Text: TEKEL; Thou art weighed in the balances, and art found wanting.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56fe3e0a-bbc7-43e4-9c01-ca65666a7236>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: DAN 5:28
Text: PERES; Thy kingdom is divided, and given to the Medes and Persians.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a634bdc-9b02-474d-9531-2a5209407c36>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: DAN 5:29
Text: Then commanded Belshazzar, and they clothed Daniel with scarlet, and put a chain of gold about his neck, and made a proclamation concerning him, that he should be the third ruler in the kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92701b1f-3172-4dba-b94b-2679859cc637>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: DAN 5:30
Text: In that night was Belshazzar the king of the Chaldeans slain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/5/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a48e88dc-b083-48f8-a0db-0e9478a1a876>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: DAN 5:31
Text: And Darius the Median took the kingdom, being about threescore and two years old.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:775eb722-4d36-4165-a340-13fcb31dc95b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: DAN 6:1
Text: It pleased Darius to set over the kingdom an hundred and twenty princes, which should be over the whole kingdom;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98fb5333-3063-4d66-afa3-e32b51f7c677>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: DAN 6:2
Text: And over these three presidents; of whom Daniel was first: that the princes might give accounts unto them, and the king should have no damage.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a586c03-a326-4d45-a5db-5f02a4383de2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: DAN 6:3
Text: Then this Daniel was preferred above the presidents and princes, because an excellent spirit was in him; and the king thought to set him over the whole realm.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b546930-0ea8-4044-bc7f-566c41965795>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: DAN 6:4
Text: Then the presidents and princes sought to find occasion against Daniel concerning the kingdom; but they could find none occasion nor fault; forasmuch as he was faithful, neither was there any error or fault found in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b56e11da-60be-472b-9f1f-9c2c7251eed5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: DAN 6:5
Text: Then said these men, We shall not find any occasion against this Daniel, except we find it against him concerning the law of his God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffaa96ac-589a-4c78-9e75-b525de8eb9a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: DAN 6:6
Text: Then these presidents and princes assembled together to the king, and said thus unto him, King Darius, live for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c19be95e-20a9-4d81-93f4-4db28a4cc603>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 341

Reference: DAN 6:7
Text: All the presidents of the kingdom, the governors, and the princes, the counsellors, and the captains, have consulted together to establish a royal statute, and to make a firm decree, that whosoever shall ask a petition of any God or man for thirty days, save of thee, O king, he shall be cast into the den of lions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c6bd0a3-fd2d-4782-8816-ed987522ad43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: DAN 6:8
Text: Now, O king, establish the decree, and sign the writing, that it be not changed, according to the law of the Medes and Persians, which altereth not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:813a661f-c59d-46e1-b629-afafdb5d9a00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: DAN 6:9
Text: Wherefore king Darius signed the writing and the decree.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a443cb3a-f220-4e09-9776-b1018212f3ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: DAN 6:10
Text: Now when Daniel knew that the writing was signed, he went into his house; and his windows being open in his chamber toward Jerusalem, he kneeled upon his knees three times a day, and prayed, and gave thanks before his God, as he did aforetime.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f54dc23-0bf9-44d3-abd9-5e8e1ee0cdf9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: DAN 6:11
Text: Then these men assembled, and found Daniel praying and making supplication before his God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ef9569d-ca69-4ff4-abca-435302d5db87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 389

Reference: DAN 6:12
Text: Then they came near, and spake before the king concerning the king’s decree; Hast thou not signed a decree, that every man that shall ask a petition of any God or man within thirty days, save of thee, O king, shall be cast into the den of lions? The king answered and said, The thing is true, according to the law of the Medes and Persians, which altereth not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99d83061-3309-4b54-b58f-e45174c265a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: DAN 6:13
Text: Then answered they and said before the king, That Daniel, which is of the children of the captivity of Judah, regardeth not thee, O king, nor the decree that thou hast signed, but maketh his petition three times a day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:438a53d7-4700-4c11-ab79-8ea688a3c0d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: DAN 6:14
Text: Then the king, when he heard these words, was sore displeased with himself, and set his heart on Daniel to deliver him: and he laboured till the going down of the sun to deliver him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f71fd038-97b4-4398-9a45-dcea984e2452>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: DAN 6:15
Text: Then these men assembled unto the king, and said unto the king, Know, O king, that the law of the Medes and Persians is, That no decree nor statute which the king establisheth may be changed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:536443f0-97aa-4b2e-9d28-14ca3fec1f32>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: DAN 6:16
Text: Then the king commanded, and they brought Daniel, and cast him into the den of lions. Now the king spake and said unto Daniel, Thy God whom thou servest continually, he will deliver thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9326d4b9-4649-49d6-ad3f-674737873252>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: DAN 6:17
Text: And a stone was brought, and laid upon the mouth of the den; and the king sealed it with his own signet, and with the signet of his lords; that the purpose might not be changed concerning Daniel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5485517-12aa-43f6-92fb-4fc6eda34869>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: DAN 6:18
Text: Then the king went to his palace, and passed the night fasting: neither were instruments of musick brought before him: and his sleep went from him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0141cc0a-0c6e-47aa-b7f0-20aef61e9d46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: DAN 6:19
Text: Then the king arose very early in the morning, and went in haste unto the den of lions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd5971f2-c84c-41c2-a050-770d75c947ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: DAN 6:20
Text: And when he came to the den, he cried with a lamentable voice unto Daniel: and the king spake and said to Daniel, O Daniel, servant of the living God, is thy God, whom thou servest continually, able to deliver thee from the lions?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:777355d5-c122-4fcd-a251-42cade6c0ba8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: DAN 6:21
Text: Then said Daniel unto the king, O king, live for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1216529b-578b-4489-881a-cdde3047d918>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: DAN 6:22
Text: My God hath sent his angel, and hath shut the lions’ mouths, that they have not hurt me: forasmuch as before him innocency was found in me; and also before thee, O king, have I done no hurt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0584a2b7-48de-494d-bc36-acb1204b9349>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: DAN 6:23
Text: Then was the king exceedingly glad for him, and commanded that they should take Daniel up out of the den. So Daniel was taken up out of the den, and no manner of hurt was found upon him, because he believed in his God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfdb0b3a-fa4f-461f-a83a-0880f6856a2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 303

Reference: DAN 6:24
Text: And the king commanded, and they brought those men which had accused Daniel, and they cast them into the den of lions, them, their children, and their wives; and the lions had the mastery of them, and brake all their bones in pieces or ever they came at the bottom of the den.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea2e5ceb-e7f5-445b-8b81-a98e283b6bb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: DAN 6:25
Text: Then king Darius wrote unto all people, nations, and languages, that dwell in all the earth; Peace be multiplied unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f4240ad-fc30-4606-9ddb-b385b7c1483c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: DAN 6:26
Text: I make a decree, That in every dominion of my kingdom men tremble and fear before the God of Daniel: for he is the living God, and stedfast for ever, and his kingdom that which shall not be destroyed, and his dominion shall be even unto the end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7aab7dcf-1a38-4200-9d98-70412b85a03a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: DAN 6:27
Text: He delivereth and rescueth, and he worketh signs and wonders in heaven and in earth, who hath delivered Daniel from the power of the lions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/6/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:860040cc-efcd-4081-ad29-b9207765587a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: DAN 6:28
Text: So this Daniel prospered in the reign of Darius, and in the reign of Cyrus the Persian.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73583a69-b372-41cc-960f-0ea5097c711a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: DAN 7:1
Text: In the first year of Belshazzar king of Babylon Daniel had a dream and visions of his head upon his bed: then he wrote the dream, and told the sum of the matters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8381cd57-a1c2-4e75-ac02-8a64ed5545e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: DAN 7:2
Text: Daniel spake and said, I saw in my vision by night, and, behold, the four winds of the heaven strove upon the great sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc98cfac-808a-42a5-99d5-12b6e5b54507>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: DAN 7:3
Text: And four great beasts came up from the sea, diverse one from another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee32eb2e-34dc-4c62-9877-5bc18412cc3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: DAN 7:4
Text: The first was like a lion, and had eagle’s wings: I beheld till the wings thereof were plucked, and it was lifted up from the earth, and made stand upon the feet as a man, and a man’s heart was given to it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05c85ae9-1b39-43a9-8d0a-929f91906895>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: DAN 7:5
Text: And behold another beast, a second, like to a bear, and it raised up itself on one side, and it had three ribs in the mouth of it between the teeth of it: and they said thus unto it, Arise, devour much flesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed51bd42-bd20-462c-b083-7b5ec8f8d368>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: DAN 7:6
Text: After this I beheld, and lo another, like a leopard, which had upon the back of it four wings of a fowl; the beast had also four heads; and dominion was given to it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9e269f1-3936-4abc-b72b-530431c46042>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 327

Reference: DAN 7:7
Text: After this I saw in the night visions, and behold a fourth beast, dreadful and terrible, and strong exceedingly; and it had great iron teeth: it devoured and brake in pieces, and stamped the residue with the feet of it: and it was diverse from all the beasts that were before it; and it had ten horns.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11e65424-6a7c-41f2-a967-3a82ba3e914b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 274

Reference: DAN 7:8
Text: I considered the horns, and, behold, there came up among them another little horn, before whom there were three of the first horns plucked up by the roots: and, behold, in this horn were eyes like the eyes of man, and a mouth speaking great things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34282208-049d-4b65-98c7-e444248cb6c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: DAN 7:9
Text: I beheld till the thrones were cast down, and the Ancient of days did sit, whose garment was white as snow, and the hair of his head like the pure wool: his throne was like the fiery flame, and his wheels as burning fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8ac8230-4fba-4f22-8d72-cddb49fc4b09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: DAN 7:10
Text: A fiery stream issued and came forth from before him: thousand thousands ministered unto him, and ten thousand times ten thousand stood before him: the judgment was set, and the books were opened.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afa125ef-c92a-47eb-8bae-6603017f07f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: DAN 7:11
Text: I beheld then because of the voice of the great words which the horn spake: I beheld even till the beast was slain, and his body destroyed, and given to the burning flame.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc0cab87-b7c6-45d7-b2f0-73c997bd697f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: DAN 7:12
Text: As concerning the rest of the beasts, they had their dominion taken away: yet their lives were prolonged for a season and time.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49639b94-0610-4f6c-87a8-ab48fbb6e667>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: DAN 7:13
Text: I saw in the night visions, and, behold, one like the Son of man came with the clouds of heaven, and came to the Ancient of days, and they brought him near before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa3b57a5-b631-4964-95bf-8d70b2f9a8d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: DAN 7:14
Text: And there was given him dominion, and glory, and a kingdom, that all people, nations, and languages, should serve him: his dominion is an everlasting dominion, which shall not pass away, and his kingdom that which shall not be destroyed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce00242f-e0d0-4290-a380-b8e9a29dbedd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: DAN 7:15
Text: I Daniel was grieved in my spirit in the midst of my body, and the visions of my head troubled me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81b09361-d58f-4dda-bc13-9780b2d6b360>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: DAN 7:16
Text: I came near unto one of them that stood by, and asked him the truth of all this. So he told me, and made me know the interpretation of the things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81e757ed-4325-40f3-8bf6-4b313bb14754>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: DAN 7:17
Text: These great beasts, which are four, are four kings, which shall arise out of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e54d006-0a7b-4a4a-aeca-64fe6137630f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: DAN 7:18
Text: But the saints of the most High shall take the kingdom, and possess the kingdom for ever, even for ever and ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe7a421c-028c-4b08-92ff-8fa0dd03ebc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: DAN 7:19
Text: Then I would know the truth of the fourth beast, which was diverse from all the others, exceeding dreadful, whose teeth were of iron, and his nails of brass; which devoured, brake in pieces, and stamped the residue with his feet;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:604c9bd6-721a-4e5f-a688-28db2c9e6fa4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: DAN 7:20
Text: And of the ten horns that were in his head, and of the other which came up, and before whom three fell; even of that horn that had eyes, and a mouth that spake very great things, whose look was more stout than his fellows.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abfab1d9-91f4-4b44-bb13-3a3b3ebe563c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: DAN 7:21
Text: I beheld, and the same horn made war with the saints, and prevailed against them;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c893b78-9a1a-4763-9d00-dd5e0e16d9e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: DAN 7:22
Text: Until the Ancient of days came, and judgment was given to the saints of the most High; and the time came that the saints possessed the kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d2e7875-bea1-433b-abce-0d93b5594004>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: DAN 7:23
Text: Thus he said, The fourth beast shall be the fourth kingdom upon earth, which shall be diverse from all kingdoms, and shall devour the whole earth, and shall tread it down, and break it in pieces.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e2a6c18-b4d7-4928-9f48-0927e424c5b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: DAN 7:24
Text: And the ten horns out of this kingdom are ten kings that shall arise: and another shall rise after them; and he shall be diverse from the first, and he shall subdue three kings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5737a78a-ea4f-40fb-ae87-fc16073de5f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: DAN 7:25
Text: And he shall speak great words against the most High, and shall wear out the saints of the most High, and think to change times and laws: and they shall be given into his hand until a time and times and the dividing of time.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a152a479-2434-48fc-867e-cbc9be02a5c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: DAN 7:26
Text: But the judgment shall sit, and they shall take away his dominion, to consume and to destroy it unto the end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40b6ac07-492c-4721-a291-5816abf52bdd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: DAN 7:27
Text: And the kingdom and dominion, and the greatness of the kingdom under the whole heaven, shall be given to the people of the saints of the most High, whose kingdom is an everlasting kingdom, and all dominions shall serve and obey him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/7/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f8c95d5-19e4-4fb9-8741-fbc63761b50d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: DAN 7:28
Text: Hitherto is the end of the matter. As for me Daniel, my cogitations much troubled me, and my countenance changed in me: but I kept the matter in my heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5210ef6-5915-461c-8139-8a1169bd3946>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: DAN 8:1
Text: In the third year of the reign of king Belshazzar a vision appeared unto me, even unto me Daniel, after that which appeared unto me at the first.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e73bf19b-609b-4170-aad5-57b8654a3f2d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: DAN 8:2
Text: And I saw in a vision; and it came to pass, when I saw, that I was at Shushan in the palace, which is in the province of Elam; and I saw in a vision, and I was by the river of Ulai.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b45a007-025e-4530-972b-c81b16891c50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: DAN 8:3
Text: Then I lifted up mine eyes, and saw, and, behold, there stood before the river a ram which had two horns: and the two horns were high; but one was higher than the other, and the higher came up last.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ecc688e-a012-455e-87d7-caa169edb401>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: DAN 8:4
Text: I saw the ram pushing westward, and northward, and southward; so that no beasts might stand before him, neither was there any that could deliver out of his hand; but he did according to his will, and became great.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b11df5e-7b46-4890-bb86-7ed6b3a8be93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: DAN 8:5
Text: And as I was considering, behold, an he goat came from the west on the face of the whole earth, and touched not the ground: and the goat had a notable horn between his eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad6385cf-18d2-43e6-af35-93335fcdb69b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: DAN 8:6
Text: And he came to the ram that had two horns, which I had seen standing before the river, and ran unto him in the fury of his power.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5edcbc00-b6a9-4e44-8310-1caa04b91ccc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 326

Reference: DAN 8:7
Text: And I saw him come close unto the ram, and he was moved with choler against him, and smote the ram, and brake his two horns: and there was no power in the ram to stand before him, but he cast him down to the ground, and stamped upon him: and there was none that could deliver the ram out of his hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00ff9a9c-e2b2-44ed-8492-e72e2fc0c0a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: DAN 8:8
Text: Therefore the he goat waxed very great: and when he was strong, the great horn was broken; and for it came up four notable ones toward the four winds of heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e72cef4-368c-4098-9743-0d7a68958165>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: DAN 8:9
Text: And out of one of them came forth a little horn, which waxed exceeding great, toward the south, and toward the east, and toward the pleasant land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0f974e9-9277-47a9-b59d-b57df2e18acb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: DAN 8:10
Text: And it waxed great, even to the host of heaven; and it cast down some of the host and of the stars to the ground, and stamped upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbe44d50-980f-4d28-845f-afbb813e47fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: DAN 8:11
Text: Yea, he magnified himself even to the prince of the host, and by him the daily sacrifice was taken away, and the place of the sanctuary was cast down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fbf5e1d-d1d0-4230-aab1-192df78e7cab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: DAN 8:12
Text: And an host was given him against the daily sacrifice by reason of transgression, and it cast down the truth to the ground; and it practised, and prospered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8bc1164e-7259-4135-841e-9b7ae040af9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 283

Reference: DAN 8:13
Text: Then I heard one saint speaking, and another saint said unto that certain saint which spake, How long shall be the vision concerning the daily sacrifice, and the transgression of desolation, to give both the sanctuary and the host to be trodden under foot?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d21f1c2a-720a-4077-8ad3-9606d1c7b578>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: DAN 8:14
Text: And he said unto me, Unto two thousand and three hundred days; then shall the sanctuary be cleansed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fca2730-3c8b-4627-a52e-192dc6533885>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: DAN 8:15
Text: And it came to pass, when I, even I Daniel, had seen the vision, and sought for the meaning, then, behold, there stood before me as the appearance of a man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8cb36c11-4249-4fb1-9304-679e281412be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: DAN 8:16
Text: And I heard a man’s voice between the banks of Ulai, which called, and said, Gabriel, make this man to understand the vision.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40aefd94-dd6d-457f-8653-b40b7f7a8d24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: DAN 8:17
Text: So he came near where I stood: and when he came, I was afraid, and fell upon my face: but he said unto me, Understand, O son of man: for at the time of the end shall be the vision.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6d889fd-70e6-49f7-b9fc-bdceef9b2652>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: DAN 8:18
Text: Now as he was speaking with me, I was in a deep sleep on my face toward the ground: but he touched me, and set me upright.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fadf9932-9a4d-493b-a6f0-5f3b0d9759fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: DAN 8:19
Text: And he said, Behold, I will make thee know what shall be in the last end of the indignation: for at the time appointed the end shall be.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b81cdb68-5923-4503-a5d8-233850653b1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: DAN 8:20
Text: The ram which thou sawest having two horns are the kings of Media and Persia.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af248cd6-44f7-4ba4-b166-8feca19f3bcc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: DAN 8:21
Text: And the rough goat is the king of Grecia: and the great horn that is between his eyes is the first king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c29a08cd-9e22-4141-aa12-cb38b73e0841>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: DAN 8:22
Text: Now that being broken, whereas four stood up for it, four kingdoms shall stand up out of the nation, but not in his power.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:195e38f4-9725-4f5d-baba-97ccb6b583ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: DAN 8:23
Text: And in the latter time of their kingdom, when the transgressors are come to the full, a king of fierce countenance, and understanding dark sentences, shall stand up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a019333f-5f01-4dd9-b753-73700bd0d0ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: DAN 8:24
Text: And his power shall be mighty, but not by his own power: and he shall destroy wonderfully, and shall prosper, and practise, and shall destroy the mighty and the holy people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77989ebe-bcaf-4c8b-8062-61b96d79448c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 266

Reference: DAN 8:25
Text: And through his policy also he shall cause craft to prosper in his hand; and he shall magnify himself in his heart, and by peace shall destroy many: he shall also stand up against the Prince of princes; but he shall be broken without hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f1fc4fc-62ff-4abc-9bb0-eb90d0cd58df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: DAN 8:26
Text: And the vision of the evening and the morning which was told is true: wherefore shut thou up the vision; for it shall be for many days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/8/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b135310f-d646-4752-bd25-50980978d30c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: DAN 8:27
Text: And I Daniel fainted, and was sick certain days; afterward I rose up, and did the king’s business; and I was astonished at the vision, but none understood it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:693429ca-7d25-4ac2-8a1c-59261ed29b39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: DAN 9:1
Text: In the first year of Darius the son of Ahasuerus, of the seed of the Medes, which was made king over the realm of the Chaldeans;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca534753-5c1b-441a-8759-85349865a79c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: DAN 9:2
Text: In the first year of his reign I Daniel understood by books the number of the years, whereof the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah the prophet, that he would accomplish seventy years in the desolations of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:748bafef-858d-49cc-a0f0-15440cb3ffe1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: DAN 9:3
Text: And I set my face unto the Lord God, to seek by prayer and supplications, with fasting, and sackcloth, and ashes:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd34b05d-35c1-4e46-a7d0-1404abd4eda7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: DAN 9:4
Text: And I prayed unto the LORD my God, and made my confession, and said, O Lord, the great and dreadful God, keeping the covenant and mercy to them that love him, and to them that keep his commandments;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a6af859-f416-4b45-875f-3a153490f3a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: DAN 9:5
Text: We have sinned, and have committed iniquity, and have done wickedly, and have rebelled, even by departing from thy precepts and from thy judgments:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f322be4-4c79-47c4-8ae6-5a160d23d5e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: DAN 9:6
Text: Neither have we hearkened unto thy servants the prophets, which spake in thy name to our kings, our princes, and our fathers, and to all the people of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f4ec30d-7b90-4e9c-94de-449229a7d889>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 355

Reference: DAN 9:7
Text: O LORD, righteousness belongeth unto thee, but unto us confusion of faces, as at this day; to the men of Judah, and to the inhabitants of Jerusalem, and unto all Israel, that are near, and that are far off, through all the countries whither thou hast driven them, because of their trespass that they have trespassed against thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4615326e-dc27-4226-9d91-193755daaeae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: DAN 9:8
Text: O Lord, to us belongeth confusion of face, to our kings, to our princes, and to our fathers, because we have sinned against thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f61097d4-a09c-4670-853c-0144ad93bcf6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: DAN 9:9
Text: To the Lord our God belong mercies and forgivenesses, though we have rebelled against him;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33f1ea3c-2a99-4838-882c-9cac75e6cc77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: DAN 9:10
Text: Neither have we obeyed the voice of the LORD our God, to walk in his laws, which he set before us by his servants the prophets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9128a690-6759-4421-89d2-ef195d962d45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: DAN 9:11
Text: Yea, all Israel have transgressed thy law, even by departing, that they might not obey thy voice; therefore the curse is poured upon us, and the oath that is written in the law of Moses the servant of God, because we have sinned against him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d407ac62-1d97-4105-9739-0f2c77557453>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: DAN 9:12
Text: And he hath confirmed his words, which he spake against us, and against our judges that judged us, by bringing upon us a great evil: for under the whole heaven hath not been done as hath been done upon Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d25adb0a-f254-48f4-b6d9-b57f9ab565d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: DAN 9:13
Text: As it is written in the law of Moses, all this evil is come upon us: yet made we not our prayer before the LORD our God, that we might turn from our iniquities, and understand thy truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ce2ce32-f9f1-4b4f-aa75-454de6b07253>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: DAN 9:14
Text: Therefore hath the LORD watched upon the evil, and brought it upon us: for the LORD our God is righteous in all his works which he doeth: for we obeyed not his voice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd3ffcf1-00ce-4c39-8aeb-a561f1f903e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: DAN 9:15
Text: And now, O Lord our God, that hast brought thy people forth out of the land of Egypt with a mighty hand, and hast gotten thee renown, as at this day; we have sinned, we have done wickedly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35ef50aa-f767-4c7f-baf9-7c97b6cc9d77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 308

Reference: DAN 9:16
Text: O LORD, according to all thy righteousness, I beseech thee, let thine anger and thy fury be turned away from thy city Jerusalem, thy holy mountain: because for our sins, and for the iniquities of our fathers, Jerusalem and thy people are become a reproach to all that are about us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4797829-787b-4dff-bf3f-4e3468fc8b28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: DAN 9:17
Text: Now therefore, O our God, hear the prayer of thy servant, and his supplications, and cause thy face to shine upon thy sanctuary that is desolate, for the Lord’s sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be29584f-bb87-4438-8cd1-3f5bfe2774a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: DAN 9:18
Text: O my God, incline thine ear, and hear; open thine eyes, and behold our desolations, and the city which is called by thy name: for we do not present our supplications before thee for our righteousnesses, but for thy great mercies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7424e33-c711-4c5e-8531-11445624b251>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: DAN 9:19
Text: O Lord, hear; O Lord, forgive; O Lord, hearken and do; defer not, for thine own sake, O my God: for thy city and thy people are called by thy name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f477e7eb-e3ad-422d-a0ed-4e98cc59bd1e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: DAN 9:20
Text: And whiles I was speaking, and praying, and confessing my sin and the sin of my people Israel, and presenting my supplication before the LORD my God for the holy mountain of my God;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77b804d4-e07c-4c42-bba9-5fe716eab5e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: DAN 9:21
Text: Yea, whiles I was speaking in prayer, even the man Gabriel, whom I had seen in the vision at the beginning, being caused to fly swiftly, touched me about the time of the evening oblation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4d250ac-299c-4d4d-8fee-820bdfffc21a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: DAN 9:22
Text: And he informed me, and talked with me, and said, O Daniel, I am now come forth to give thee skill and understanding.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a582b6f1-708b-4a96-b4ac-4a167477a689>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: DAN 9:23
Text: At the beginning of thy supplications the commandment came forth, and I am come to shew thee; for thou art greatly beloved: therefore understand the matter, and consider the vision.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4952b391-b575-48ab-b9fb-c27697584a68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 305

Reference: DAN 9:24
Text: Seventy weeks are determined upon thy people and upon thy holy city, to finish the transgression, and to make an end of sins, and to make reconciliation for iniquity, and to bring in everlasting righteousness, and to seal up the vision and prophecy, and to anoint the most Holy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ca92d33-f4a0-476a-a625-601955130361>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 288

Reference: DAN 9:25
Text: Know therefore and understand, that from the going forth of the commandment to restore and to build Jerusalem unto the Messiah the Prince shall be seven weeks, and threescore and two weeks: the street shall be built again, and the wall, even in troublous times.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4856382e-0cf9-4722-8176-dbe65080bf8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 294

Reference: DAN 9:26
Text: And after threescore and two weeks shall Messiah be cut off, but not for himself: and the people of the prince that shall come shall destroy the city and the sanctuary; and the end thereof shall be with a flood, and unto the end of the war desolations are determined.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/9/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a319bd1-6610-4cfa-a04b-38f908b7f3c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 322

Reference: DAN 9:27
Text: And he shall confirm the covenant with many for one week: and in the midst of the week he shall cause the sacrifice and the oblation to cease, and for the overspreading of abominations he shall make it desolate, even until the consummation, and that determined shall be poured upon the desolate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/10/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:933f16af-758b-4ed5-860e-9af49e71f47b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: DAN 10:1
Text: In the third year of Cyrus king of Persia a thing was revealed unto Daniel, whose name was called Belteshazzar; and the thing was true, but the time appointed was long: and he understood the thing, and had understanding of the vision.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/10/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4288bea9-e350-484f-a499-9dd95803e1a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: DAN 10:2
Text: In those days I Daniel was mourning three full weeks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/10/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8697b4ba-90ad-4546-8173-5713e5977b9f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: DAN 10:3
Text: I ate no pleasant bread, neither came flesh nor wine in my mouth, neither did I anoint myself at all, till three whole weeks were fulfilled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/10/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6d0264e-8da6-468a-bbc6-9b9469dd425a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: DAN 10:4
Text: And in the four and twentieth day of the first month, as I was by the side of the great river, which is Hiddekel;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/10/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea6e4413-04ee-49ba-824a-2c1c5f98e1c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: DAN 10:5
Text: Then I lifted up mine eyes, and looked, and behold a certain man clothed in linen, whose loins were girded with fine gold of Uphaz:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/10/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6aca29d0-26e5-4a90-ae87-a606e6c27651>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: DAN 10:6
Text: His body also was like the beryl, and his face as the appearance of lightning, and his eyes as lamps of fire, and his arms and his feet like in colour to polished brass, and the voice of his words like the voice of a multitude.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/10/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ea67af9-3241-4e07-902f-ff82c91efb72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: DAN 10:7
Text: And I Daniel alone saw the vision: for the men that were with me saw not the vision; but a great quaking fell upon them, so that they fled to hide themselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/10/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae50b4e8-2c80-491e-9e48-62399648b28a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: DAN 10:8
Text: Therefore I was left alone, and saw this great vision, and there remained no strength in me: for my comeliness was turned in me into corruption, and I retained no strength.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/10/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b956a259-89e8-414f-ba32-6c61bae11bf7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: DAN 10:9
Text: Yet heard I the voice of his words: and when I heard the voice of his words, then was I in a deep sleep on my face, and my face toward the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/10/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22b2a0be-5abb-46fe-bc02-f89b6fc085cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: DAN 10:10
Text: And, behold, an hand touched me, which set me upon my knees and upon the palms of my hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/10/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db63d16e-3331-43f4-b471-02ca5d54d227>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: DAN 10:11
Text: And he said unto me, O Daniel, a man greatly beloved, understand the words that I speak unto thee, and stand upright: for unto thee am I now sent. And when he had spoken this word unto me, I stood trembling.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/10/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:597276d8-6731-4ae1-9398-7baf9985a075>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: DAN 10:12
Text: Then said he unto me, Fear not, Daniel: for from the first day that thou didst set thine heart to understand, and to chasten thyself before thy God, thy words were heard, and I am come for thy words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/10/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17567146-3b55-4d1a-a4bf-70d575f7fa0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: DAN 10:13
Text: But the prince of the kingdom of Persia withstood me one and twenty days: but, lo, Michael, one of the chief princes, came to help me; and I remained there with the kings of Persia.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/10/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4161a04-3329-48b6-aa5c-409efa9e1d68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: DAN 10:14
Text: Now I am come to make thee understand what shall befall thy people in the latter days: for yet the vision is for many days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/10/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91321e25-914f-4c93-ae04-5596ce62549a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: DAN 10:15
Text: And when he had spoken such words unto me, I set my face toward the ground, and I became dumb.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/10/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:766cb6d0-a0d6-4472-a7ce-037231bc60f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: DAN 10:16
Text: And, behold, one like the similitude of the sons of men touched my lips: then I opened my mouth, and spake, and said unto him that stood before me, O my lord, by the vision my sorrows are turned upon me, and I have retained no strength.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/10/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62588d39-2578-4424-aa57-9c0a57e06cd4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: DAN 10:17
Text: For how can the servant of this my lord talk with this my lord? for as for me, straightway there remained no strength in me, neither is there breath left in me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/10/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:983f7470-aa25-4594-be16-75bdc5216d48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: DAN 10:18
Text: Then there came again and touched me one like the appearance of a man, and he strengthened me,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/10/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ee52f79-b8f2-474f-927f-f41cf2ecb3c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: DAN 10:19
Text: And said, O man greatly beloved, fear not: peace be unto thee, be strong, yea, be strong. And when he had spoken unto me, I was strengthened, and said, Let my lord speak; for thou hast strengthened me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/10/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40dce419-2bdc-4d4b-bd26-32df02794f1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: DAN 10:20
Text: Then said he, Knowest thou wherefore I come unto thee? and now will I return to fight with the prince of Persia: and when I am gone forth, lo, the prince of Grecia shall come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/10/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e17c31c-110a-4197-938a-bd22545be9bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: DAN 10:21
Text: But I will shew thee that which is noted in the scripture of truth: and there is none that holdeth with me in these things, but Michael your prince.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6778562-3b29-4a7b-9ed8-b3003c1a5bcc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: DAN 11:1
Text: Also I in the first year of Darius the Mede, even I, stood to confirm and to strengthen him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e8d4d6c-a005-4ca8-951a-f4fb7885e28a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: DAN 11:2
Text: And now will I shew thee the truth. Behold, there shall stand up yet three kings in Persia; and the fourth shall be far richer than they all: and by his strength through his riches he shall stir up all against the realm of Grecia.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a76436cf-764c-4e1e-af5d-cdc6e78b724b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: DAN 11:3
Text: And a mighty king shall stand up, that shall rule with great dominion, and do according to his will.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6df0ec74-3812-412d-914d-49819692fb90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: DAN 11:4
Text: And when he shall stand up, his kingdom shall be broken, and shall be divided toward the four winds of heaven; and not to his posterity, nor according to his dominion which he ruled: for his kingdom shall be plucked up, even for others beside those.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ad17c88-1329-4edd-b130-52e25de6d734>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: DAN 11:5
Text: And the king of the south shall be strong, and one of his princes; and he shall be strong above him, and have dominion; his dominion shall be a great dominion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e391a52-db41-4ed7-839c-1469268c25a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 390

Reference: DAN 11:6
Text: And in the end of years they shall join themselves together; for the king’s daughter of the south shall come to the king of the north to make an agreement: but she shall not retain the power of the arm; neither shall he stand, nor his arm: but she shall be given up, and they that brought her, and he that begat her, and he that strengthened her in these times.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6568ced-fc03-49f7-9867-29b96138b4c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: DAN 11:7
Text: But out of a branch of her roots shall one stand up in his estate, which shall come with an army, and shall enter into the fortress of the king of the north, and shall deal against them, and shall prevail:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c93583b-cdb4-47fe-8221-69c989d5852a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: DAN 11:8
Text: And shall also carry captives into Egypt their gods, with their princes, and with their precious vessels of silver and of gold; and he shall continue more years than the king of the north.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:475b4bec-a381-44cf-b8cc-22a1895ae4cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: DAN 11:9
Text: So the king of the south shall come into his kingdom, and shall return into his own land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60519add-f65a-4930-b4ad-6374b559d243>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: DAN 11:10
Text: But his sons shall be stirred up, and shall assemble a multitude of great forces: and one shall certainly come, and overflow, and pass through: then shall he return, and be stirred up, even to his fortress.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8052c6f4-9156-4835-9450-ca5053596fe7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: DAN 11:11
Text: And the king of the south shall be moved with choler, and shall come forth and fight with him, even with the king of the north: and he shall set forth a great multitude; but the multitude shall be given into his hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce1abc6d-b248-475b-8539-42c886bb707d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: DAN 11:12
Text: And when he hath taken away the multitude, his heart shall be lifted up; and he shall cast down many ten thousands: but he shall not be strengthened by it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18b0c4de-1393-49f3-bd8c-09641729fe8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: DAN 11:13
Text: For the king of the north shall return, and shall set forth a multitude greater than the former, and shall certainly come after certain years with a great army and with much riches.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3526e37c-1aa8-43d7-809f-27b3fd7da038>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: DAN 11:14
Text: And in those times there shall many stand up against the king of the south: also the robbers of thy people shall exalt themselves to establish the vision; but they shall fall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de220dbf-7435-481d-909f-952af0d58d11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: DAN 11:15
Text: So the king of the north shall come, and cast up a mount, and take the most fenced cities: and the arms of the south shall not withstand, neither his chosen people, neither shall there be any strength to withstand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f61e62e-43d2-45b9-b40c-6dc4394cf772>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: DAN 11:16
Text: But he that cometh against him shall do according to his own will, and none shall stand before him: and he shall stand in the glorious land, which by his hand shall be consumed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd201349-3243-4ed0-b711-c166068107e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 266

Reference: DAN 11:17
Text: He shall also set his face to enter with the strength of his whole kingdom, and upright ones with him; thus shall he do: and he shall give him the daughter of women, corrupting her: but she shall not stand on his side, neither be for him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:869f4be6-5699-41fd-b58b-61c8ca1f0a72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: DAN 11:18
Text: After this shall he turn his face unto the isles, and shall take many: but a prince for his own behalf shall cause the reproach offered by him to cease; without his own reproach he shall cause it to turn upon him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3f6cfff-fc5d-409b-9d1a-bd51a30d1448>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: DAN 11:19
Text: Then he shall turn his face toward the fort of his own land: but he shall stumble and fall, and not be found.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c92ad1e1-d09b-4ad2-9899-882b2c2dcfa4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: DAN 11:20
Text: Then shall stand up in his estate a raiser of taxes in the glory of the kingdom: but within few days he shall be destroyed, neither in anger, nor in battle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12df5195-6be3-42ca-8800-dc3a4911cc2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: DAN 11:21
Text: And in his estate shall stand up a vile person, to whom they shall not give the honour of the kingdom: but he shall come in peaceably, and obtain the kingdom by flatteries.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7563302e-6976-4bac-a5c0-030124f9f7c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: DAN 11:22
Text: And with the arms of a flood shall they be overflown from before him, and shall be broken; yea, also the prince of the covenant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0343589b-123e-4f98-9b79-93b37afc4509>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: DAN 11:23
Text: And after the league made with him he shall work deceitfully: for he shall come up, and shall become strong with a small people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9652541-4c7e-4c06-80d1-fb26017875e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 323

Reference: DAN 11:24
Text: He shall enter peaceably even upon the fattest places of the province; and he shall do that which his fathers have not done, nor his fathers’ fathers; he shall scatter among them the prey, and spoil, and riches: yea, and he shall forecast his devices against the strong holds, even for a time.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a6751d5-e575-4f72-9540-f97ef21f19e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 283

Reference: DAN 11:25
Text: And he shall stir up his power and his courage against the king of the south with a great army; and the king of the south shall be stirred up to battle with a very great and mighty army; but he shall not stand: for they shall forecast devices against him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1784d84f-094f-4cc0-aed8-ad3ba8dcb70a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: DAN 11:26
Text: Yea, they that feed of the portion of his meat shall destroy him, and his army shall overflow: and many shall fall down slain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d71d858a-20cf-4200-80b5-edd36b86beb8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: DAN 11:27
Text: And both of these kings’ hearts shall be to do mischief, and they shall speak lies at one table; but it shall not prosper: for yet the end shall be at the time appointed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83487f59-8719-46b5-95d9-3ac72a1d6ba2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: DAN 11:28
Text: Then shall he return into his land with great riches; and his heart shall be against the holy covenant; and he shall do exploits, and return to his own land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a5db83c-b81f-4c72-9472-5ee01a85bc58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: DAN 11:29
Text: At the time appointed he shall return, and come toward the south; but it shall not be as the former, or as the latter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a2da9ca-6d5d-45cd-8d4a-fcadcc84f52b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: DAN 11:30
Text: For the ships of Chittim shall come against him: therefore he shall be grieved, and return, and have indignation against the holy covenant: so shall he do; he shall even return, and have intelligence with them that forsake the holy covenant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb12088d-5676-4417-95ba-2c1b7ca67052>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: DAN 11:31
Text: And arms shall stand on his part, and they shall pollute the sanctuary of strength, and shall take away the daily sacrifice, and they shall place the abomination that maketh desolate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:753fae43-c49c-40f2-a9de-94f7098a5452>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: DAN 11:32
Text: And such as do wickedly against the covenant shall he corrupt by flatteries: but the people that do know their God shall be strong, and do exploits.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8dbbc0f4-a122-4d30-9730-e9d323815cef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: DAN 11:33
Text: And they that understand among the people shall instruct many: yet they shall fall by the sword, and by flame, by captivity, and by spoil, many days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f733238e-05df-4b1f-964e-0697d1d68096>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: DAN 11:34
Text: Now when they shall fall, they shall be holpen with a little help: but many shall cleave to them with flatteries.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38b438aa-21de-424b-9703-01b21a26bc18>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: DAN 11:35
Text: And some of them of understanding shall fall, to try them, and to purge, and to make them white, even to the time of the end: because it is yet for a time appointed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4c7d627-9bb2-4bff-a94e-ff6e04ec28b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 295

Reference: DAN 11:36
Text: And the king shall do according to his will; and he shall exalt himself, and magnify himself above every god, and shall speak marvellous things against the God of gods, and shall prosper till the indignation be accomplished: for that that is determined shall be done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c33b89ef-5083-4006-a16d-02705990ed20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: DAN 11:37
Text: Neither shall he regard the God of his fathers, nor the desire of women, nor regard any god: for he shall magnify himself above all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c774393-ef0d-4051-956f-ccfb45ac54df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: DAN 11:38
Text: But in his estate shall he honour the God of forces: and a god whom his fathers knew not shall he honour with gold, and silver, and with precious stones, and pleasant things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d6a7d46-2161-48c4-bf92-9c1666bf242c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: DAN 11:39
Text: Thus shall he do in the most strong holds with a strange god, whom he shall acknowledge and increase with glory: and he shall cause them to rule over many, and shall divide the land for gain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa757f56-3999-4541-b3fd-92367be9b932>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 290

Reference: DAN 11:40
Text: And at the time of the end shall the king of the south push at him: and the king of the north shall come against him like a whirlwind, with chariots, and with horsemen, and with many ships; and he shall enter into the countries, and shall overflow and pass over.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe6d777b-2938-49cc-9718-124d19a7588b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: DAN 11:41
Text: He shall enter also into the glorious land, and many countries shall be overthrown: but these shall escape out of his hand, even Edom, and Moab, and the chief of the children of Ammon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d7cd821-8db8-402a-8e9f-c3d451294173>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: DAN 11:42
Text: He shall stretch forth his hand also upon the countries: and the land of Egypt shall not escape.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d67e4257-afda-4b0d-bcb5-f84d49d21b76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: DAN 11:43
Text: But he shall have power over the treasures of gold and of silver, and over all the precious things of Egypt: and the Libyans and the Ethiopians shall be at his steps.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:875d0d2f-9204-4a84-86fc-141b8d8fe97c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: DAN 11:44
Text: But tidings out of the east and out of the north shall trouble him: therefore he shall go forth with great fury to destroy, and utterly to make away many.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/11/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bea71bb6-b15a-4f5e-ba23-af9f1c3fc743>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: DAN 11:45
Text: And he shall plant the tabernacles of his palace between the seas in the glorious holy mountain; yet he shall come to his end, and none shall help him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/12/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a5aab30-8aa5-4622-b928-48c82563f368>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 335

Reference: DAN 12:1
Text: And at that time shall Michael stand up, the great prince which standeth for the children of thy people: and there shall be a time of trouble, such as never was since there was a nation even to that same time: and at that time thy people shall be delivered, every one that shall be found written in the book.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/12/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebd8064b-c906-407c-a440-16426e827f1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: DAN 12:2
Text: And many of them that sleep in the dust of the earth shall awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/12/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d93401a-65a2-4d27-af99-62a1cb81cdd3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: DAN 12:3
Text: And they that be wise shall shine as the brightness of the firmament; and they that turn many to righteousness as the stars for ever and ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/12/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d28a6601-b20a-474c-8260-e12e9e5cf714>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: DAN 12:4
Text: But thou, O Daniel, shut up the words, and seal the book, even to the time of the end: many shall run to and fro, and knowledge shall be increased.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/12/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d0a9be8-6ef4-4916-9585-79034134dba3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: DAN 12:5
Text: Then I Daniel looked, and, behold, there stood other two, the one on this side of the bank of the river, and the other on that side of the bank of the river.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/12/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d229e999-d7bc-4190-95c1-50a2bf6cf808>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: DAN 12:6
Text: And one said to the man clothed in linen, which was upon the waters of the river, How long shall it be to the end of these wonders?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/12/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70eaa18d-1fce-4bc5-8a13-4f8d06375cff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 366

Reference: DAN 12:7
Text: And I heard the man clothed in linen, which was upon the waters of the river, when he held up his right hand and his left hand unto heaven, and sware by him that liveth for ever that it shall be for a time, times, and an half; and when he shall have accomplished to scatter the power of the holy people, all these things shall be finished.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/12/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41cfec51-7376-4612-ae63-c4b5906cf1fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: DAN 12:8
Text: And I heard, but I understood not: then said I, O my Lord, what shall be the end of these things?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/12/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a706950-c1f3-4e65-a6e5-c028b32cbe8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: DAN 12:9
Text: And he said, Go thy way, Daniel: for the words are closed up and sealed till the time of the end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/12/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06dcecf1-920c-470c-8433-f2b69b7f8a6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: DAN 12:10
Text: Many shall be purified, and made white, and tried; but the wicked shall do wickedly: and none of the wicked shall understand; but the wise shall understand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/12/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8afda76-9764-43fd-824e-ebada291dba4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: DAN 12:11
Text: And from the time that the daily sacrifice shall be taken away, and the abomination that maketh desolate set up, there shall be a thousand two hundred and ninety days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/12/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0859daab-a51a-440f-8498-2109b8604ac5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: DAN 12:12
Text: Blessed is he that waiteth, and cometh to the thousand three hundred and five and thirty days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/DAN/12/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:094fab7d-0232-48da-ac88-e4c01debe8d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: DAN 12:13
Text: But go thou thy way till the end be: for thou shalt rest, and stand in thy lot at the end of the days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5583359b-de37-4b6d-9447-d205cae3c7b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: HOS 1:1
Text: The word of the LORD that came unto Hosea, the son of Beeri, in the days of Uzziah, Jotham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah, kings of Judah, and in the days of Jeroboam the son of Joash, king of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf0b29ce-faa3-4a6d-82eb-12f80c19d885>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: HOS 1:2
Text: The beginning of the word of the LORD by Hosea. And the LORD said to Hosea, Go, take unto thee a wife of whoredoms and children of whoredoms: for the land hath committed great whoredom, departing from the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83255c25-0628-432d-9bf7-584541eca84b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: HOS 1:3
Text: So he went and took Gomer the daughter of Diblaim; which conceived, and bare him a son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20ce1ddf-5b35-450c-979c-bb60ff1cecd4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: HOS 1:4
Text: And the LORD said unto him, Call his name Jezreel; for yet a little while, and I will avenge the blood of Jezreel upon the house of Jehu, and will cause to cease the kingdom of the house of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5978714e-777d-4215-a56e-d0b338041a2b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: HOS 1:5
Text: And it shall come to pass at that day, that I will break the bow of Israel, in the valley of Jezreel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:207d6369-f1aa-4e49-aa14-3e9efe7081d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: HOS 1:6
Text: And she conceived again, and bare a daughter. And God said unto him, Call her name Loruhamah: for I will no more have mercy upon the house of Israel; but I will utterly take them away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc231901-33e3-4d76-9702-3fd016e2bbe1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: HOS 1:7
Text: But I will have mercy upon the house of Judah, and will save them by the LORD their God, and will not save them by bow, nor by sword, nor by battle, by horses, nor by horsemen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:375bee30-7a28-4a18-8860-a70e9bfe944c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: HOS 1:8
Text: Now when she had weaned Loruhamah, she conceived, and bare a son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b6707b5-c4cb-4805-a713-3ca89b60b030>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: HOS 1:9
Text: Then said God, Call his name Loammi: for ye are not my people, and I will not be your God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9edb899-d969-4c5c-b30a-ba9f0cb74348>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 304

Reference: HOS 1:10
Text: Yet the number of the children of Israel shall be as the sand of the sea, which cannot be measured nor numbered; and it shall come to pass, that in the place where it was said unto them, Ye are not my people, there it shall be said unto them, Ye are the sons of the living God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22afc397-eaaa-451d-81c5-d06a7d3f3a05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: HOS 1:11
Text: Then shall the children of Judah and the children of Israel be gathered together, and appoint themselves one head, and they shall come up out of the land: for great shall be the day of Jezreel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:162189c8-d9ed-4e83-9a21-258c8235941a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: HOS 2:1
Text: Say ye unto your brethren, Ammi; and to your sisters, Ruhamah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c04fd3e6-5e66-49be-a6a9-eae236b66ff1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: HOS 2:2
Text: Plead with your mother, plead: for she is not my wife, neither am I her husband: let her therefore put away her whoredoms out of her sight, and her adulteries from between her breasts;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e50ff7d-9e78-4ef9-857f-992c84097d8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: HOS 2:3
Text: Lest I strip her naked, and set her as in the day that she was born, and make her as a wilderness, and set her like a dry land, and slay her with thirst.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:667be082-7e0d-461e-bcf1-40cecbe67762>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: HOS 2:4
Text: And I will not have mercy upon her children; for they be the children of whoredoms.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0eae1778-778a-4aa3-a8bb-54afe6548a3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: HOS 2:5
Text: For their mother hath played the harlot: she that conceived them hath done shamefully: for she said, I will go after my lovers, that give me my bread and my water, my wool and my flax, mine oil and my drink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:862bd1d0-eaa9-4869-896c-5b48343b75ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: HOS 2:6
Text: Therefore, behold, I will hedge up thy way with thorns, and make a wall, that she shall not find her paths.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5be7771-327b-4187-aeda-6b6f6d81ef79>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: HOS 2:7
Text: And she shall follow after her lovers, but she shall not overtake them; and she shall seek them, but shall not find them: then shall she say, I will go and return to my first husband; for then was it better with me than now.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d572629-c27f-4b37-97ba-ce17c70c8dd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: HOS 2:8
Text: For she did not know that I gave her corn, and wine, and oil, and multiplied her silver and gold, which they prepared for Baal.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba28f28c-e852-436e-9d80-ceb4ca5539cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: HOS 2:9
Text: Therefore will I return, and take away my corn in the time thereof, and my wine in the season thereof, and will recover my wool and my flax given to cover her nakedness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b7f6009-9853-4101-b202-8a68b6c82559>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: HOS 2:10
Text: And now will I discover her lewdness in the sight of her lovers, and none shall deliver her out of mine hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27adf9c3-0394-4e30-9e9f-5ef14f7c9db7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: HOS 2:11
Text: I will also cause all her mirth to cease, her feast days, her new moons, and her sabbaths, and all her solemn feasts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:242364df-cdcb-4c46-a774-cd9d96f61c7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: HOS 2:12
Text: And I will destroy her vines and her fig trees, whereof she hath said, These are my rewards that my lovers have given me: and I will make them a forest, and the beasts of the field shall eat them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67f7ad90-f287-405a-8920-177224bb3c49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: HOS 2:13
Text: And I will visit upon her the days of Baalim, wherein she burned incense to them, and she decked herself with her earrings and her jewels, and she went after her lovers, and forgat me, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eea8d2a3-85e1-4cda-b287-1c1f86b984f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: HOS 2:14
Text: Therefore, behold, I will allure her, and bring her into the wilderness, and speak comfortably unto her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b3094c6-340d-4d81-874a-14a88d768fba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: HOS 2:15
Text: And I will give her her vineyards from thence, and the valley of Achor for a door of hope: and she shall sing there, as in the days of her youth, and as in the day when she came up out of the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e6af91c-6a88-4a55-b767-bf87a3dbed81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: HOS 2:16
Text: And it shall be at that day, saith the LORD, that thou shalt call me Ishi; and shalt call me no more Baali.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:239e72a9-4f04-4abb-a185-786e9893cd17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: HOS 2:17
Text: For I will take away the names of Baalim out of her mouth, and they shall no more be remembered by their name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b8ada94-eaa5-47f4-b760-a1fa598bec7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 288

Reference: HOS 2:18
Text: And in that day will I make a covenant for them with the beasts of the field and with the fowls of heaven, and with the creeping things of the ground: and I will break the bow and the sword and the battle out of the earth, and will make them to lie down safely.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc546070-bf97-45ae-b153-a708d651d249>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: HOS 2:19
Text: And I will betroth thee unto me for ever; yea, I will betroth thee unto me in righteousness, and in judgment, and in lovingkindness, and in mercies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b881298c-558f-4667-8e30-5d310839b357>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: HOS 2:20
Text: I will even betroth thee unto me in faithfulness: and thou shalt know the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8918303-c5ee-4ae7-a34e-a118f89f8b79>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: HOS 2:21
Text: And it shall come to pass in that day, I will hear, saith the LORD, I will hear the heavens, and they shall hear the earth;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9ac782b-b9b6-4cd5-9894-6d033d524801>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: HOS 2:22
Text: And the earth shall hear the corn, and the wine, and the oil; and they shall hear Jezreel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/2/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0507bd30-2f37-4a62-aad9-c32f26fbf69b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: HOS 2:23
Text: And I will sow her unto me in the earth; and I will have mercy upon her that had not obtained mercy; and I will say to them which were not my people, Thou art my people; and they shall say, Thou art my God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e61adf8-5c3c-4686-ac3b-d9e8c5fa2cf0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: HOS 3:1
Text: Then said the LORD unto me, Go yet, love a woman beloved of her friend, yet an adulteress, according to the love of the LORD toward the children of Israel, who look to other gods, and love flagons of wine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3e14c38-7335-4da1-8d55-4e6ef9d237f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: HOS 3:2
Text: So I bought her to me for fifteen pieces of silver, and for an homer of barley, and an half homer of barley:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc5f1c62-9918-4d71-8631-bb0dca08c875>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: HOS 3:3
Text: And I said unto her, Thou shalt abide for me many days; thou shalt not play the harlot, and thou shalt not be for another man: so will I also be for thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e956572-44bf-49a1-9c89-0d9923c7dedd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: HOS 3:4
Text: For the children of Israel shall abide many days without a king, and without a prince, and without a sacrifice, and without an image, and without an ephod, and without teraphim:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18caaea7-e409-47f8-af6a-2ba1d3e5f34a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: HOS 3:5
Text: Afterward shall the children of Israel return, and seek the LORD their God, and David their king; and shall fear the LORD and his goodness in the latter days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed878d68-1915-42a6-a240-62c4f6e31411>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: HOS 4:1
Text: Hear the word of the LORD, ye children of Israel: for the LORD hath a controversy with the inhabitants of the land, because there is no truth, nor mercy, nor knowledge of God in the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0edc7d42-6861-40ee-ac1c-0e29df40187a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: HOS 4:2
Text: By swearing, and lying, and killing, and stealing, and committing adultery, they break out, and blood toucheth blood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef19014c-0a09-4b49-8ae7-59877f9d8969>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: HOS 4:3
Text: Therefore shall the land mourn, and every one that dwelleth therein shall languish, with the beasts of the field, and with the fowls of heaven; yea, the fishes of the sea also shall be taken away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04208d98-947f-4954-b384-7b75d048f2e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: HOS 4:4
Text: Yet let no man strive, nor reprove another: for thy people are as they that strive with the priest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6fceb685-546d-486b-9d28-29ac5049a1c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: HOS 4:5
Text: Therefore shalt thou fall in the day, and the prophet also shall fall with thee in the night, and I will destroy thy mother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e8ae26e-401b-45c1-a6a5-a511b8703459>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: HOS 4:6
Text: My people are destroyed for lack of knowledge: because thou hast rejected knowledge, I will also reject thee, that thou shalt be no priest to me: seeing thou hast forgotten the law of thy God, I will also forget thy children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e59dee2-16c6-471d-9b28-d062d55e0da8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: HOS 4:7
Text: As they were increased, so they sinned against me: therefore will I change their glory into shame.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef0474d4-137f-4440-9bbe-88f5983fb192>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: HOS 4:8
Text: They eat up the sin of my people, and they set their heart on their iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02354307-262b-4f59-a5d7-6e19e1c36fe2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: HOS 4:9
Text: And there shall be, like people, like priest: and I will punish them for their ways, and reward them their doings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a40b901-a7c7-4b42-9959-b6f3d4398b81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: HOS 4:10
Text: For they shall eat, and not have enough: they shall commit whoredom, and shall not increase: because they have left off to take heed to the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b17ebfbb-5ad9-48f3-9727-a9a13f4f3eb8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: HOS 4:11
Text: Whoredom and wine and new wine take away the heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29272bf7-11b5-40d2-8d7a-bc14860fddbe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: HOS 4:12
Text: My people ask counsel at their stocks, and their staff declareth unto them: for the spirit of whoredoms hath caused them to err, and they have gone a whoring from under their God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:303aaeee-9e1c-4c3c-ade7-371a78946596>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: HOS 4:13
Text: They sacrifice upon the tops of the mountains, and burn incense upon the hills, under oaks and poplars and elms, because the shadow thereof is good: therefore your daughters shall commit whoredom, and your spouses shall commit adultery.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6fc937e-363d-423e-a263-9d36f99c7a27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: HOS 4:14
Text: I will not punish your daughters when they commit whoredom, nor your spouses when they commit adultery: for themselves are separated with whores, and they sacrifice with harlots: therefore the people that doth not understand shall fall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4961c7ee-fed4-42e2-95f1-f245a1fa9b47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: HOS 4:15
Text: Though thou, Israel, play the harlot, yet let not Judah offend; and come not ye unto Gilgal, neither go ye up to Bethaven, nor swear, The LORD liveth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fcacbbb-d572-4eff-bbec-7f1d697d50de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: HOS 4:16
Text: For Israel slideth back as a backsliding heifer: now the LORD will feed them as a lamb in a large place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2148eca-2ae7-4ac0-9723-2f8f6ada097c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 69

Reference: HOS 4:17
Text: Ephraim is joined to idols: let him alone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/4/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a57bcd94-e5e1-4852-8f44-59af11e15007>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: HOS 4:18
Text: Their drink is sour: they have committed whoredom continually: her rulers with shame do love, Give ye.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/4/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0655032-37b0-4c19-8584-d91d57cc74b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: HOS 4:19
Text: The wind hath bound her up in her wings, and they shall be ashamed because of their sacrifices.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e09e3ee-ade5-4238-a6b6-98cf70eab4d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: HOS 5:1
Text: Hear ye this, O priests; and hearken, ye house of Israel; and give ye ear, O house of the king; for judgment is toward you, because ye have been a snare on Mizpah, and a net spread upon Tabor.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:baa30d94-e437-43dc-92d3-7c24507edd29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: HOS 5:2
Text: And the revolters are profound to make slaughter, though I have been a rebuker of them all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01a2bf96-2908-40be-884c-99a0dc09b34e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: HOS 5:3
Text: I know Ephraim, and Israel is not hid from me: for now, O Ephraim, thou committest whoredom, and Israel is defiled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fa31ab9-446d-40f0-bdba-cab1095e9a8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: HOS 5:4
Text: They will not frame their doings to turn unto their God: for the spirit of whoredoms is in the midst of them, and they have not known the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e79a8da6-1cc1-4718-848a-c3ff913fd006>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: HOS 5:5
Text: And the pride of Israel doth testify to his face: therefore shall Israel and Ephraim fall in their iniquity: Judah also shall fall with them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3723c2b9-9598-4036-bf13-4230fc84d42a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: HOS 5:6
Text: They shall go with their flocks and with their herds to seek the LORD; but they shall not find him; he hath withdrawn himself from them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3b77539-9a50-426f-a4bb-eb16f2aab571>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: HOS 5:7
Text: They have dealt treacherously against the LORD: for they have begotten strange children: now shall a month devour them with their portions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c1193ab-860b-4166-b3c3-418e5e1efe12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: HOS 5:8
Text: Blow ye the cornet in Gibeah, and the trumpet in Ramah: cry aloud at Bethaven, after thee, O Benjamin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f83ff85c-d224-4712-8311-f35eb1584846>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: HOS 5:9
Text: Ephraim shall be desolate in the day of rebuke: among the tribes of Israel have I made known that which shall surely be.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:585f030f-9fe0-4189-818b-ed379f0457a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: HOS 5:10
Text: The princes of Judah were like them that remove the bound: therefore I will pour out my wrath upon them like water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf2c8bc3-aab1-47fd-9e78-5a9db6944fc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: HOS 5:11
Text: Ephraim is oppressed and broken in judgment, because he willingly walked after the commandment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be044a60-5782-4499-a64f-1adea757b22a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: HOS 5:12
Text: Therefore will I be unto Ephraim as a moth, and to the house of Judah as rottenness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f00a92a-0e86-401f-9201-bd332bfcc6eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: HOS 5:13
Text: When Ephraim saw his sickness, and Judah saw his wound, then went Ephraim to the Assyrian, and sent to king Jareb: yet could he not heal you, nor cure you of your wound.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88b05e2f-3a99-44ee-8ea2-35a80e4a780a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: HOS 5:14
Text: For I will be unto Ephraim as a lion, and as a young lion to the house of Judah: I, even I, will tear and go away; I will take away, and none shall rescue him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e76a5f9b-6a3c-414b-95bf-3b81c0924e7a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: HOS 5:15
Text: I will go and return to my place, till they acknowledge their offence, and seek my face: in their affliction they will seek me early.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af6b769c-1834-4e68-8b78-ccbf0ac64263>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: HOS 6:1
Text: Come, and let us return unto the LORD: for he hath torn, and he will heal us; he hath smitten, and he will bind us up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9cc1b3c9-880f-48c5-b225-9b94c1620480>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: HOS 6:2
Text: After two days will he revive us: in the third day he will raise us up, and we shall live in his sight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7889052a-d855-4332-91d3-648fe25e1ae9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: HOS 6:3
Text: Then shall we know, if we follow on to know the LORD: his going forth is prepared as the morning; and he shall come unto us as the rain, as the latter and former rain unto the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed988015-f995-45c4-8be9-303b103a2334>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: HOS 6:4
Text: O Ephraim, what shall I do unto thee? O Judah, what shall I do unto thee? for your goodness is as a morning cloud, and as the early dew it goeth away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55ce5201-65bf-4d4a-944f-06d09d6a6e91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: HOS 6:5
Text: Therefore have I hewed them by the prophets; I have slain them by the words of my mouth: and thy judgments are as the light that goeth forth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65798157-0375-41c6-b1de-feae9186998e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: HOS 6:6
Text: For I desired mercy, and not sacrifice; and the knowledge of God more than burnt offerings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6ad0a8f-9065-4a51-8607-bd3890ced62e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: HOS 6:7
Text: But they like men have transgressed the covenant: there have they dealt treacherously against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74e7fea1-97c9-44f3-b2ad-e227bced324b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: HOS 6:8
Text: Gilead is a city of them that work iniquity, and is polluted with blood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e03f9901-dffc-49ef-990e-878c6f49db49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: HOS 6:9
Text: And as troops of robbers wait for a man, so the company of priests murder in the way by consent: for they commit lewdness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e5db702-a194-4400-87d0-76043b9b2623>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: HOS 6:10
Text: I have seen an horrible thing in the house of Israel: there is the whoredom of Ephraim, Israel is defiled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00e4ef70-55f7-4d8f-8f43-0c5c61984793>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: HOS 6:11
Text: Also, O Judah, he hath set an harvest for thee, when I returned the captivity of my people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a1a05f7-be15-420a-9891-1a3a3945538f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: HOS 7:1
Text: When I would have healed Israel, then the iniquity of Ephraim was discovered, and the wickedness of Samaria: for they commit falsehood; and the thief cometh in, and the troop of robbers spoileth without.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37ee948e-ea81-4b1f-9c4a-0f213e944cbf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: HOS 7:2
Text: And they consider not in their hearts that I remember all their wickedness: now their own doings have beset them about; they are before my face.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7e7b6e1-96c6-4ac3-879c-959b27605362>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: HOS 7:3
Text: They make the king glad with their wickedness, and the princes with their lies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19944f1b-2d0b-48e0-b4fb-d7b86271276c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: HOS 7:4
Text: They are all adulterers, as an oven heated by the baker, who ceaseth from raising after he hath kneaded the dough, until it be leavened.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3981adc-39f1-4358-bfe2-3c029808ddd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: HOS 7:5
Text: In the day of our king the princes have made him sick with bottles of wine; he stretched out his hand with scorners.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90847c7a-90f6-4dca-998d-97ac844cac55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: HOS 7:6
Text: For they have made ready their heart like an oven, whiles they lie in wait: their baker sleepeth all the night; in the morning it burneth as a flaming fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e962fd78-3a8a-4b97-b2ed-ec2f57eba868>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: HOS 7:7
Text: They are all hot as an oven, and have devoured their judges; all their kings are fallen: there is none among them that calleth unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bed7eb83-dbe7-460a-a9f1-849e539a2333>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: HOS 7:8
Text: Ephraim, he hath mixed himself among the people; Ephraim is a cake not turned.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90ec22a5-a2ee-4948-befd-dfa785a29c66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: HOS 7:9
Text: Strangers have devoured his strength, and he knoweth it not: yea, gray hairs are here and there upon him, yet he knoweth not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5709f5b0-0c18-4fb0-bd12-6468614abec9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: HOS 7:10
Text: And the pride of Israel testifieth to his face: and they do not return to the LORD their God, nor seek him for all this.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3904cb97-6630-4695-ba9c-1fe8d875832a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: HOS 7:11
Text: Ephraim also is like a silly dove without heart: they call to Egypt, they go to Assyria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a43d2560-69d8-4b0c-950c-89397b6b2ec6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: HOS 7:12
Text: When they shall go, I will spread my net upon them; I will bring them down as the fowls of the heaven; I will chastise them, as their congregation hath heard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3e2d3a7-173f-4702-a3d0-566477158643>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: HOS 7:13
Text: Woe unto them! for they have fled from me: destruction unto them! because they have transgressed against me: though I have redeemed them, yet they have spoken lies against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/7/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8caa5c89-ae85-4e86-b9fd-97388f3dbc50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: HOS 7:14
Text: And they have not cried unto me with their heart, when they howled upon their beds: they assemble themselves for corn and wine, and they rebel against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/7/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e5e2320-eb69-4553-8310-7fc5ef7c8f13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: HOS 7:15
Text: Though I have bound and strengthened their arms, yet do they imagine mischief against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/7/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c7694d5-7ee8-4a20-8bfd-a6e0e376ad01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: HOS 7:16
Text: They return, but not to the most High: they are like a deceitful bow: their princes shall fall by the sword for the rage of their tongue: this shall be their derision in the land of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/8/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3583bfa5-9afe-4c8f-9727-5301b4b47324>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: HOS 8:1
Text: Set the trumpet to thy mouth. He shall come as an eagle against the house of the LORD, because they have transgressed my covenant, and trespassed against my law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/8/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a57d00b-137a-49ab-9c29-5285e9733fde>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: HOS 8:2
Text: Israel shall cry unto me, My God, we know thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/8/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19179f13-b883-4e35-bb0d-dfb66b78d839>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: HOS 8:3
Text: Israel hath cast off the thing that is good: the enemy shall pursue him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/8/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:603ffb36-a3c5-4f0d-a764-759f7ddbebe3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: HOS 8:4
Text: They have set up kings, but not by me: they have made princes, and I knew it not: of their silver and their gold have they made them idols, that they may be cut off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/8/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c13988a2-acb4-4e6d-926f-221238f31184>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: HOS 8:5
Text: Thy calf, O Samaria, hath cast thee off; mine anger is kindled against them: how long will it be ere they attain to innocency?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/8/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0d1cfe5-f5ae-48c1-8d30-f071d29f8d8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: HOS 8:6
Text: For from Israel was it also: the workman made it; therefore it is not God: but the calf of Samaria shall be broken in pieces.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/8/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2d78029-610d-436b-a2cb-1670bb01571b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: HOS 8:7
Text: For they have sown the wind, and they shall reap the whirlwind: it hath no stalk; the bud shall yield no meal: if so be it yield, the strangers shall swallow it up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/8/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b28732fb-e9a6-4005-864c-2df548116451>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: HOS 8:8
Text: Israel is swallowed up: now shall they be among the Gentiles as a vessel wherein is no pleasure.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/8/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b69ca1f-4c84-4f64-a823-0fb3322e6ad7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: HOS 8:9
Text: For they are gone up to Assyria, a wild ass alone by himself: Ephraim hath hired lovers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/8/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f784dfd-4822-497a-991b-377d714c1b7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: HOS 8:10
Text: Yea, though they have hired among the nations, now will I gather them, and they shall sorrow a little for the burden of the king of princes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/8/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3581af4e-8136-46ed-800c-9b12d21df0c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: HOS 8:11
Text: Because Ephraim hath made many altars to sin, altars shall be unto him to sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/8/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7a0f601-c44f-4c8a-9f9f-f8aa23dd5785>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: HOS 8:12
Text: I have written to him the great things of my law, but they were counted as a strange thing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/8/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91c1bc25-abd0-4b2d-b206-991b95841e94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: HOS 8:13
Text: They sacrifice flesh for the sacrifices of mine offerings, and eat it; but the LORD accepteth them not; now will he remember their iniquity, and visit their sins: they shall return to Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/8/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4cb9f9e0-c5d0-49ff-b46b-8b04827233b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: HOS 8:14
Text: For Israel hath forgotten his Maker, and buildeth temples; and Judah hath multiplied fenced cities: but I will send a fire upon his cities, and it shall devour the palaces thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/9/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd5d3c93-f5e1-4ee2-99b3-a666a6656e14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: HOS 9:1
Text: Rejoice not, O Israel, for joy, as other people: for thou hast gone a whoring from thy God, thou hast loved a reward upon every cornfloor.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/9/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e429d43-d731-48aa-93d2-38a33d3e1c4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: HOS 9:2
Text: The floor and the winepress shall not feed them, and the new wine shall fail in her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/9/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe31e7b4-f311-4ff0-8017-0cabad7ac655>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: HOS 9:3
Text: They shall not dwell in the LORD’s land; but Ephraim shall return to Egypt, and they shall eat unclean things in Assyria.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/9/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b4ee811-5f8c-4849-b6c2-45648ed343d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 291

Reference: HOS 9:4
Text: They shall not offer wine offerings to the LORD, neither shall they be pleasing unto him: their sacrifices shall be unto them as the bread of mourners; all that eat thereof shall be polluted: for their bread for their soul shall not come into the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/9/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8c67dea-d447-412c-8705-dc065fa2d8d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: HOS 9:5
Text: What will ye do in the solemn day, and in the day of the feast of the LORD?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/9/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5812aa94-92bd-4566-a86c-1717cbe1575f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: HOS 9:6
Text: For, lo, they are gone because of destruction: Egypt shall gather them up, Memphis shall bury them: the pleasant places for their silver, nettles shall possess them: thorns shall be in their tabernacles.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/9/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5daafdac-5c66-4ec7-9db6-1ccd9ce3cfc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: HOS 9:7
Text: The days of visitation are come, the days of recompence are come; Israel shall know it: the prophet is a fool, the spiritual man is mad, for the multitude of thine iniquity, and the great hatred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/9/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfc4e019-8b71-4966-bb1a-cf4c99dde8cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: HOS 9:8
Text: The watchman of Ephraim was with my God: but the prophet is a snare of a fowler in all his ways, and hatred in the house of his God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/9/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe1aeba0-d03d-48b5-b216-898f4af7d9fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: HOS 9:9
Text: They have deeply corrupted themselves, as in the days of Gibeah: therefore he will remember their iniquity, he will visit their sins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/9/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:816469ce-c86f-4449-a49b-041c5dbc8375>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: HOS 9:10
Text: I found Israel like grapes in the wilderness; I saw your fathers as the firstripe in the fig tree at her first time: but they went to Baalpeor, and separated themselves unto that shame; and their abominations were according as they loved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/9/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3a2953f-648b-406e-87df-3d11c7352e42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: HOS 9:11
Text: As for Ephraim, their glory shall fly away like a bird, from the birth, and from the womb, and from the conception.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/9/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80384976-f013-439b-9007-163a8b041964>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: HOS 9:12
Text: Though they bring up their children, yet will I bereave them, that there shall not be a man left: yea, woe also to them when I depart from them!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/9/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6fcb0637-745e-4457-a65b-69c7433adeb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: HOS 9:13
Text: Ephraim, as I saw Tyrus, is planted in a pleasant place: but Ephraim shall bring forth his children to the murderer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/9/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6737ecf3-ca1f-415b-8340-1d4f511c45b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: HOS 9:14
Text: Give them, O LORD: what wilt thou give? give them a miscarrying womb and dry breasts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/9/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa94ff49-0890-4acd-b79b-8e9e51672a5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: HOS 9:15
Text: All their wickedness is in Gilgal: for there I hated them: for the wickedness of their doings I will drive them out of mine house, I will love them no more: all their princes are revolters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/9/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:618466ba-d6c4-4b93-a43f-b0557bdd60f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: HOS 9:16
Text: Ephraim is smitten, their root is dried up, they shall bear no fruit: yea, though they bring forth, yet will I slay even the beloved fruit of their womb.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/9/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7df271b6-e832-4e70-b4c1-db169774caa7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: HOS 9:17
Text: My God will cast them away, because they did not hearken unto him: and they shall be wanderers among the nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/10/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35ad1000-94fa-4c4e-b0f0-e039f95eff7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: HOS 10:1
Text: Israel is an empty vine, he bringeth forth fruit unto himself: according to the multitude of his fruit he hath increased the altars; according to the goodness of his land they have made goodly images.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/10/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f3c350d-4d84-48b2-8bca-1b92bcbd3cda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: HOS 10:2
Text: Their heart is divided; now shall they be found faulty: he shall break down their altars, he shall spoil their images.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/10/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9aa0d5f0-a6a4-4382-a3bb-551ec57e14a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: HOS 10:3
Text: For now they shall say, We have no king, because we feared not the LORD; what then should a king do to us?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/10/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24e7dd20-47f5-4adc-b92b-871a3a08346d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: HOS 10:4
Text: They have spoken words, swearing falsely in making a covenant: thus judgment springeth up as hemlock in the furrows of the field.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/10/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02d39554-67ac-48cf-a40f-188334f5ef89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: HOS 10:5
Text: The inhabitants of Samaria shall fear because of the calves of Bethaven: for the people thereof shall mourn over it, and the priests thereof that rejoiced on it, for the glory thereof, because it is departed from it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/10/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5a4f60c-ef07-48ce-9b9e-b4848fcac5a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: HOS 10:6
Text: It shall be also carried unto Assyria for a present to king Jareb: Ephraim shall receive shame, and Israel shall be ashamed of his own counsel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/10/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e625c8a7-227c-42af-acaf-83b67b98a101>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: HOS 10:7
Text: As for Samaria, her king is cut off as the foam upon the water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/10/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38d7945f-b8e6-4c10-a044-21bb327e5509>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: HOS 10:8
Text: The high places also of Aven, the sin of Israel, shall be destroyed: the thorn and the thistle shall come up on their altars; and they shall say to the mountains, Cover us; and to the hills, Fall on us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/10/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3aeb2288-52b7-48fe-88a9-6da6dc991121>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: HOS 10:9
Text: O Israel, thou hast sinned from the days of Gibeah: there they stood: the battle in Gibeah against the children of iniquity did not overtake them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/10/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14ce172d-afca-499d-bd9b-2fbd5a9b4a1e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: HOS 10:10
Text: It is in my desire that I should chastise them; and the people shall be gathered against them, when they shall bind themselves in their two furrows.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/10/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:197f831b-eb95-4b76-813a-6db332106668>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: HOS 10:11
Text: And Ephraim is as an heifer that is taught, and loveth to tread out the corn; but I passed over upon her fair neck: I will make Ephraim to ride; Judah shall plow, and Jacob shall break his clods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/10/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d559ccee-6de4-445b-a5c9-85d721979546>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: HOS 10:12
Text: Sow to yourselves in righteousness, reap in mercy; break up your fallow ground: for it is time to seek the LORD, till he come and rain righteousness upon you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/10/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72ad0058-e3dd-4be2-8476-306bd6938595>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: HOS 10:13
Text: Ye have plowed wickedness, ye have reaped iniquity; ye have eaten the fruit of lies: because thou didst trust in thy way, in the multitude of thy mighty men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/10/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43f1e666-2a97-4e15-b436-d547eab0bf92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: HOS 10:14
Text: Therefore shall a tumult arise among thy people, and all thy fortresses shall be spoiled, as Shalman spoiled Betharbel in the day of battle: the mother was dashed in pieces upon her children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/10/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d419e9d-23c9-4e6f-bfba-189f1b81b877>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: HOS 10:15
Text: So shall Bethel do unto you because of your great wickedness: in a morning shall the king of Israel utterly be cut off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/11/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d11193f-7469-4111-8bc6-ab170f33f20a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: HOS 11:1
Text: When Israel was a child, then I loved him, and called my son out of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/11/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc9d3899-cadc-44f4-918c-7dfbf06484c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: HOS 11:2
Text: As they called them, so they went from them: they sacrificed unto Baalim, and burned incense to graven images.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/11/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c80794d5-9fb6-4d86-bf3d-e61ca916f23f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: HOS 11:3
Text: I taught Ephraim also to go, taking them by their arms; but they knew not that I healed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/11/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e706c565-faa6-47da-bf8f-a9c11e3735fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: HOS 11:4
Text: I drew them with cords of a man, with bands of love: and I was to them as they that take off the yoke on their jaws, and I laid meat unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/11/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d29a41ba-cd7c-4e79-90e7-be76c8851656>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: HOS 11:5
Text: He shall not return into the land of Egypt, and the Assyrian shall be his king, because they refused to return.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/11/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1961967-63d0-4ba6-9c47-fd269f2a2a6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: HOS 11:6
Text: And the sword shall abide on his cities, and shall consume his branches, and devour them, because of their own counsels.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/11/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:093e8b84-1ede-40d8-a361-719c4afc8acf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: HOS 11:7
Text: And my people are bent to backsliding from me: though they called them to the most High, none at all would exalt him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/11/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1aba6d0-18e2-4b9a-91cc-c2fff397d04a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: HOS 11:8
Text: How shall I give thee up, Ephraim? how shall I deliver thee, Israel? how shall I make thee as Admah? how shall I set thee as Zeboim? mine heart is turned within me, my repentings are kindled together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/11/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae3b2719-1afb-4cdc-b451-db9701d98cfd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: HOS 11:9
Text: I will not execute the fierceness of mine anger, I will not return to destroy Ephraim: for I am God, and not man; the Holy One in the midst of thee: and I will not enter into the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/11/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9f11d35-5257-4dd2-af7c-547038a0894c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: HOS 11:10
Text: They shall walk after the LORD: he shall roar like a lion: when he shall roar, then the children shall tremble from the west.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/11/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ce3d41a-ebf5-4715-b94a-dc4e6472b4bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: HOS 11:11
Text: They shall tremble as a bird out of Egypt, and as a dove out of the land of Assyria: and I will place them in their houses, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/11/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0bf4ee4-8ff5-4c06-9176-170d2e912d53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: HOS 11:12
Text: Ephraim compasseth me about with lies, and the house of Israel with deceit: but Judah yet ruleth with God, and is faithful with the saints.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/12/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abceb4d2-ed27-46cc-91bd-e848fa08ed66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: HOS 12:1
Text: Ephraim feedeth on wind, and followeth after the east wind: he daily increaseth lies and desolation; and they do make a covenant with the Assyrians, and oil is carried into Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/12/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:945e9425-463e-4d90-a431-889d73caeade>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: HOS 12:2
Text: The LORD hath also a controversy with Judah, and will punish Jacob according to his ways; according to his doings will he recompense him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/12/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5ecf10a-6e4a-425e-9d03-423a4aa65d7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: HOS 12:3
Text: He took his brother by the heel in the womb, and by his strength he had power with God:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/12/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9817f351-6be1-4cd4-bf87-7e584f42ffb8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: HOS 12:4
Text: Yea, he had power over the angel, and prevailed: he wept, and made supplication unto him: he found him in Bethel, and there he spake with us;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/12/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfa25803-212a-4e0d-8eae-8014d00197e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: HOS 12:5
Text: Even the LORD God of hosts; the LORD is his memorial.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/12/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0665e4c-8ca7-41ec-8f0e-905d9f2daa38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: HOS 12:6
Text: Therefore turn thou to thy God: keep mercy and judgment and wait on thy God continually.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/12/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:616f5656-c691-48af-b217-bfc088e60f8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: HOS 12:7
Text: He is a merchant, the balances of deceit are in his hand: he loveth to oppress.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/12/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aadc48a5-47b2-491a-b4d4-0e7dcae0f167>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: HOS 12:8
Text: And Ephraim said, Yet I am become rich, I have found me out substance: in all my labours they shall find none iniquity in me that were sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/12/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b973ae0e-b858-412a-9788-d0b64ce07363>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: HOS 12:9
Text: And I that am the LORD thy God from the land of Egypt will yet make thee to dwell in tabernacles, as in the days of the solemn feast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/12/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63bac26e-fa76-4807-9a8f-3c6e0a55ca54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: HOS 12:10
Text: I have also spoken by the prophets, and I have multiplied visions, and used similitudes, by the ministry of the prophets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/12/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c47b030-f309-4c69-b144-d1c8f02b7478>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: HOS 12:11
Text: Is there iniquity in Gilead? surely they are vanity: they sacrifice bullocks in Gilgal; yea, their altars are as heaps in the furrows of the fields.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/12/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3aa3df4b-2cd2-4397-975a-3d1bdfb3e012>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: HOS 12:12
Text: And Jacob fled into the country of Syria, and Israel served for a wife, and for a wife he kept sheep.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/12/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9b6373b-49a9-4aeb-af55-4394b959da58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: HOS 12:13
Text: And by a prophet the LORD brought Israel out of Egypt, and by a prophet was he preserved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/12/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6e5c7b9-6be7-4a5f-b2f3-826a4d418eca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: HOS 12:14
Text: Ephraim provoked him to anger most bitterly: therefore shall he leave his blood upon him, and his reproach shall his LORD return unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/13/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cde0baa4-71e8-49d8-9338-71f0be763561>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: HOS 13:1
Text: When Ephraim spake trembling, he exalted himself in Israel; but when he offended in Baal, he died.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/13/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec7b154e-0d17-4665-8405-45e47d3574ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: HOS 13:2
Text: And now they sin more and more, and have made them molten images of their silver, and idols according to their own understanding, all of it the work of the craftsmen: they say of them, Let the men that sacrifice kiss the calves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/13/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:351db5c3-31cd-4a8c-bece-186fa2ef7cea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: HOS 13:3
Text: Therefore they shall be as the morning cloud and as the early dew that passeth away, as the chaff that is driven with the whirlwind out of the floor, and as the smoke out of the chimney.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/13/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77e6656f-0acb-4d26-9275-90170310d62b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: HOS 13:4
Text: Yet I am the LORD thy God from the land of Egypt, and thou shalt know no god but me: for there is no saviour beside me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/13/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b25a1a4-1d1b-4738-810b-80d018aa8787>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: HOS 13:5
Text: I did know thee in the wilderness, in the land of great drought.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/13/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18f8fc30-a241-423a-aa8d-002bec77d3d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: HOS 13:6
Text: According to their pasture, so were they filled; they were filled, and their heart was exalted; therefore have they forgotten me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/13/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7eb85a8c-7831-4ce6-b583-0e7012933cb8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: HOS 13:7
Text: Therefore I will be unto them as a lion: as a leopard by the way will I observe them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/13/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5963669-ae11-448c-88a4-71d95b319b6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: HOS 13:8
Text: I will meet them as a bear that is bereaved of her whelps, and will rend the caul of their heart, and there will I devour them like a lion: the wild beast shall tear them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/13/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0fa0e2fe-6342-4bc0-965c-7553b9968fad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: HOS 13:9
Text: O Israel, thou hast destroyed thyself; but in me is thine help.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/13/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5555b6ed-f53a-4a04-9648-9a31dca43744>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: HOS 13:10
Text: I will be thy king: where is any other that may save thee in all thy cities? and thy judges of whom thou saidst, Give me a king and princes?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/13/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15f720d4-cd79-4487-b96c-4be58b638cd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: HOS 13:11
Text: I gave thee a king in mine anger, and took him away in my wrath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/13/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88844e42-3e47-4e57-a2d9-e1e37afca9f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: HOS 13:12
Text: The iniquity of Ephraim is bound up; his sin is hid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/13/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d26e9a3-51f0-4610-8149-2868699a5ac3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: HOS 13:13
Text: The sorrows of a travailing woman shall come upon him: he is an unwise son; for he should not stay long in the place of the breaking forth of children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/13/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26530cb9-f049-4d4e-9cfd-b4a6434920f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: HOS 13:14
Text: I will ransom them from the power of the grave; I will redeem them from death: O death, I will be thy plagues; O grave, I will be thy destruction: repentance shall be hid from mine eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/13/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:731c95c1-0f48-43d5-8edb-c38cbc2e9acf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: HOS 13:15
Text: Though he be fruitful among his brethren, an east wind shall come, the wind of the LORD shall come up from the wilderness, and his spring shall become dry, and his fountain shall be dried up: he shall spoil the treasure of all pleasant vessels.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/13/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4036bce-399e-4435-ac95-39ba2c058dc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: HOS 13:16
Text: Samaria shall become desolate; for she hath rebelled against her God: they shall fall by the sword: their infants shall be dashed in pieces, and their women with child shall be ripped up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/14/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dca32039-c970-4be0-8fe6-f839670b82fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: HOS 14:1
Text: O israel, return unto the LORD thy God; for thou hast fallen by thine iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/14/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e4f39e8-67b5-4825-a087-8ee44c4634ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: HOS 14:2
Text: Take with you words, and turn to the LORD: say unto him, Take away all iniquity, and receive us graciously: so will we render the calves of our lips.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/14/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ec13041-22da-44a9-8458-39b1a11f7e5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: HOS 14:3
Text: Asshur shall not save us; we will not ride upon horses: neither will we say any more to the work of our hands, Ye are our gods: for in thee the fatherless findeth mercy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/14/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01b652bc-21fc-42cc-8246-0a7168ab7e25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: HOS 14:4
Text: I will heal their backsliding, I will love them freely: for mine anger is turned away from him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/14/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb3828c1-69f1-463a-b260-5dce46a96748>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: HOS 14:5
Text: I will be as the dew unto Israel: he shall grow as the lily, and cast forth his roots as Lebanon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/14/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eac9af82-fa22-4c63-9c8d-812f07710cc5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: HOS 14:6
Text: His branches shall spread, and his beauty shall be as the olive tree, and his smell as Lebanon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/14/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8f8983b-c8dc-4e99-bf2b-b0586595e2de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: HOS 14:7
Text: They that dwell under his shadow shall return; they shall revive as the corn, and grow as the vine: the scent thereof shall be as the wine of Lebanon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/14/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59ff8f46-835d-486f-93b5-b0b67ad086bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: HOS 14:8
Text: Ephraim shall say, What have I to do any more with idols? I have heard him, and observed him: I am like a green fir tree. From me is thy fruit found.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HOS/14/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2063d8c9-8000-4f12-9332-9b09ae8d42e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: HOS 14:9
Text: Who is wise, and he shall understand these things? prudent, and he shall know them? for the ways of the LORD are right, and the just shall walk in them: but the transgressors shall fall therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72e61996-cffe-4cf1-9c90-e59a0bf96450>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: JOL 1:1
Text: The word of the LORD that came to Joel the son of Pethuel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f39f76e8-383a-42b8-9f28-d36e6efb1224>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: JOL 1:2
Text: Hear this, ye old men, and give ear, all ye inhabitants of the land. Hath this been in your days, or even in the days of your fathers?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d39d1a6-7c9a-4951-b6b0-5cae95e44250>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: JOL 1:3
Text: Tell ye your children of it, and let your children tell their children, and their children another generation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f42ede56-519f-4ca8-95ae-0755628588e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: JOL 1:4
Text: That which the palmerworm hath left hath the locust eaten; and that which the locust hath left hath the cankerworm eaten; and that which the cankerworm hath left hath the caterpiller eaten.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70bcbeed-ebdb-4ebc-8125-688413f76025>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: JOL 1:5
Text: Awake, ye drunkards, and weep; and howl, all ye drinkers of wine, because of the new wine; for it is cut off from your mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3a7c8cd-dd8b-4a4c-b085-adc36612c51a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: JOL 1:6
Text: For a nation is come up upon my land, strong, and without number, whose teeth are the teeth of a lion, and he hath the cheek teeth of a great lion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e4d4aa6-d9cd-4719-a2c7-8a1bb7e49a9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: JOL 1:7
Text: He hath laid my vine waste, and barked my fig tree: he hath made it clean bare, and cast it away; the branches thereof are made white.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f2b06f2-e747-446d-8621-2cfa45aede7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: JOL 1:8
Text: Lament like a virgin girded with sackcloth for the husband of her youth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:baca8c67-d9b4-4633-83d5-94a2ba39555f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: JOL 1:9
Text: The meat offering and the drink offering is cut off from the house of the LORD; the priests, the LORD’s ministers, mourn.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3ab6b29-e932-4fc3-817d-11fe8ac9b17a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: JOL 1:10
Text: The field is wasted, the land mourneth; for the corn is wasted: the new wine is dried up, the oil languisheth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd4f4278-6bed-48ed-9526-83c01c7f1048>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: JOL 1:11
Text: Be ye ashamed, O ye husbandmen; howl, O ye vinedressers, for the wheat and for the barley; because the harvest of the field is perished.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:839969ee-6f2c-46e3-89c6-c4a025a4895c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: JOL 1:12
Text: The vine is dried up, and the fig tree languisheth; the pomegranate tree, the palm tree also, and the apple tree, even all the trees of the field, are withered: because joy is withered away from the sons of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9791a552-5bd7-499b-9f46-647409f87239>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: JOL 1:13
Text: Gird yourselves, and lament, ye priests: howl, ye ministers of the altar: come, lie all night in sackcloth, ye ministers of my God: for the meat offering and the drink offering is withholden from the house of your God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c05275a-4113-45bf-98a0-c88e5e7b37df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: JOL 1:14
Text: Sanctify ye a fast, call a solemn assembly, gather the elders and all the inhabitants of the land into the house of the LORD your God, and cry unto the LORD,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0e8c048-5ae3-459f-97d7-8b87702c66d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: JOL 1:15
Text: Alas for the day! for the day of the LORD is at hand, and as a destruction from the Almighty shall it come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:871b087d-796c-4aae-b868-106d6c5433df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: JOL 1:16
Text: Is not the meat cut off before our eyes, yea, joy and gladness from the house of our God?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e8846d2-5afb-4bb0-978d-3b062867b287>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: JOL 1:17
Text: The seed is rotten under their clods, the garners are laid desolate, the barns are broken down; for the corn is withered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c84e24af-cf8d-4b0a-9e52-b89fd0baf5ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: JOL 1:18
Text: How do the beasts groan! the herds of cattle are perplexed, because they have no pasture; yea, the flocks of sheep are made desolate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e399a6d-52b0-43a5-a2ac-ab8c5d6f84f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: JOL 1:19
Text: O LORD, to thee will I cry: for the fire hath devoured the pastures of the wilderness, and the flame hath burned all the trees of the field.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bceda16c-3b25-479f-8842-7881113c306b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: JOL 1:20
Text: The beasts of the field cry also unto thee: for the rivers of waters are dried up, and the fire hath devoured the pastures of the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:461e8355-ed13-4d6c-9772-3dd448027364>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: JOL 2:1
Text: Blow ye the trumpet in Zion, and sound an alarm in my holy mountain: let all the inhabitants of the land tremble: for the day of the LORD cometh, for it is nigh at hand;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afd89cf0-c727-4406-851c-2163c98fab27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 282

Reference: JOL 2:2
Text: A day of darkness and of gloominess, a day of clouds and of thick darkness, as the morning spread upon the mountains: a great people and a strong; there hath not been ever the like, neither shall be any more after it, even to the years of many generations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:122ac23c-85e4-4b21-9381-775535693eba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: JOL 2:3
Text: A fire devoureth before them; and behind them a flame burneth: the land is as the garden of Eden before them, and behind them a desolate wilderness; yea, and nothing shall escape them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c328f4d-fb74-4b5c-b841-03438cfa81e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: JOL 2:4
Text: The appearance of them is as the appearance of horses; and as horsemen, so shall they run.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7ed077e-27d1-4d91-b8fd-c14cb1a056e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: JOL 2:5
Text: Like the noise of chariots on the tops of mountains shall they leap, like the noise of a flame of fire that devoureth the stubble, as a strong people set in battle array.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afb1ddeb-a725-48d2-b598-d9f55c670aea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: JOL 2:6
Text: Before their face the people shall be much pained: all faces shall gather blackness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ba5dce3-341c-4cd5-945f-d15bcf73090e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JOL 2:7
Text: They shall run like mighty men; they shall climb the wall like men of war; and they shall march every one on his ways, and they shall not break their ranks:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a56188e-128b-4b2c-a67d-c13ed3aba3d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: JOL 2:8
Text: Neither shall one thrust another; they shall walk every one in his path: and when they fall upon the sword, they shall not be wounded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52d1f298-7a20-4a19-b5e1-fdaf48dbe38d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: JOL 2:9
Text: They shall run to and fro in the city; they shall run upon the wall, they shall climb up upon the houses; they shall enter in at the windows like a thief.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0cdec19-c503-4eac-b518-52930d897ea6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: JOL 2:10
Text: The earth shall quake before them; the heavens shall tremble: the sun and the moon shall be dark, and the stars shall withdraw their shining:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c5e6cce-527f-4c23-90e2-91f6e93e6377>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: JOL 2:11
Text: And the LORD shall utter his voice before his army: for his camp is very great: for he is strong that executeth his word: for the day of the LORD is great and very terrible; and who can abide it?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d575d33-182a-4cda-a757-6368a92a183d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: JOL 2:12
Text: Therefore also now, saith the LORD, turn ye even to me with all your heart, and with fasting, and with weeping, and with mourning:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9bbea467-022b-45a9-b3c5-10a072fc29f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: JOL 2:13
Text: And rend your heart, and not your garments, and turn unto the LORD your God: for he is gracious and merciful, slow to anger, and of great kindness, and repenteth him of the evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d0e2f93-0563-448b-ba74-5307d697e20c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: JOL 2:14
Text: Who knoweth if he will return and repent, and leave a blessing behind him; even a meat offering and a drink offering unto the LORD your God?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1641bd9-3c04-4b37-9822-689ac73e70be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: JOL 2:15
Text: Blow the trumpet in Zion, sanctify a fast, call a solemn assembly:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65327dc7-f3b5-460d-b1c6-35ee2ab0d166>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: JOL 2:16
Text: Gather the people, sanctify the congregation, assemble the elders, gather the children, and those that suck the breasts: let the bridegroom go forth of his chamber, and the bride out of her closet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10b22c56-99bc-4e4d-8f92-12d3342e5ab8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 297

Reference: JOL 2:17
Text: Let the priests, the ministers of the LORD, weep between the porch and the altar, and let them say, Spare thy people, O LORD, and give not thine heritage to reproach, that the heathen should rule over them: wherefore should they say among the people, Where is their God?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83c1e407-4e7e-44d0-bdc2-b2dcec38e4f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: JOL 2:18
Text: Then will the LORD be jealous for his land, and pity his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66c2787f-a253-4d71-88b9-031125fabbeb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: JOL 2:19
Text: Yea, the LORD will answer and say unto his people, Behold, I will send you corn, and wine, and oil, and ye shall be satisfied therewith: and I will no more make you a reproach among the heathen:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:569d0244-f97c-4ec3-bea8-4997b3153df4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 308

Reference: JOL 2:20
Text: But I will remove far off from you the northern army, and will drive him into a land barren and desolate, with his face toward the east sea, and his hinder part toward the utmost sea, and his stink shall come up, and his ill savour shall come up, because he hath done great things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33f70531-be69-413e-9037-157c17e9fad1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: JOL 2:21
Text: Fear not, O land; be glad and rejoice: for the LORD will do great things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f5d91ca-378d-400e-be78-5d4d1d876dd5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: JOL 2:22
Text: Be not afraid, ye beasts of the field: for the pastures of the wilderness do spring, for the tree beareth her fruit, the fig tree and the vine do yield their strength.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f76791c9-905a-41c3-bb18-ede7f6f703a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: JOL 2:23
Text: Be glad then, ye children of Zion, and rejoice in the LORD your God: for he hath given you the former rain moderately, and he will cause to come down for you the rain, the former rain, and the latter rain in the first month.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:552274c1-68e2-4578-aa4d-eaacf3e9cdee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: JOL 2:24
Text: And the floors shall be full of wheat, and the vats shall overflow with wine and oil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:309166d2-2f83-4c0a-862c-61c8319c18ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JOL 2:25
Text: And I will restore to you the years that the locust hath eaten, the cankerworm, and the caterpiller, and the palmerworm, my great army which I sent among you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d7c7617-0ac7-46fc-8135-64fce55b2b17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: JOL 2:26
Text: And ye shall eat in plenty, and be satisfied, and praise the name of the LORD your God, that hath dealt wondrously with you: and my people shall never be ashamed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3e4986b-71f0-4508-8a7d-483a161adb9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: JOL 2:27
Text: And ye shall know that I am in the midst of Israel, and that I am the LORD your God, and none else: and my people shall never be ashamed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f1d48b4-0cbd-4420-b0e3-415ba58c3654>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: JOL 2:28
Text: And it shall come to pass afterward, that I will pour out my spirit upon all flesh; and your sons and your daughters shall prophesy, your old men shall dream dreams, your young men shall see visions:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abed7267-2593-4bb1-97f4-d2e9b0ec5c3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: JOL 2:29
Text: And also upon the servants and upon the handmaids in those days will I pour out my spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ed0dbdb-1633-4436-a790-533c1d2606cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: JOL 2:30
Text: And I will shew wonders in the heavens and in the earth, blood, and fire, and pillars of smoke.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5748a210-7fc0-49ea-b628-d5c632b52172>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: JOL 2:31
Text: The sun shall be turned into darkness, and the moon into blood, before the great and terrible day of the LORD come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/2/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5ca0845-9599-40a3-ae89-8b9b291e3ff2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: JOL 2:32
Text: And it shall come to pass, that whosoever shall call on the name of the LORD shall be delivered: for in mount Zion and in Jerusalem shall be deliverance, as the LORD hath said, and in the remnant whom the LORD shall call.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:499a4000-b146-46fb-8f4f-f728ae078ccf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: JOL 3:1
Text: For, behold, in those days, and in that time, when I shall bring again the captivity of Judah and Jerusalem,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30863672-c047-4c5b-8949-6dacd0481f94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: JOL 3:2
Text: I will also gather all nations, and will bring them down into the valley of Jehoshaphat, and will plead with them there for my people and for my heritage Israel, whom they have scattered among the nations, and parted my land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08a833e1-5bda-4d10-8d39-9fca387f9329>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: JOL 3:3
Text: And they have cast lots for my people; and have given a boy for an harlot, and sold a girl for wine, that they might drink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afbe9681-81e5-47fe-b910-370fedd89a14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: JOL 3:4
Text: Yea, and what have ye to do with me, O Tyre, and Zidon, and all the coasts of Palestine? will ye render me a recompence? and if ye recompense me, swiftly and speedily will I return your recompence upon your own head;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c7393c0-07d7-4e1a-87d4-25b3d4cca8a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: JOL 3:5
Text: Because ye have taken my silver and my gold, and have carried into your temples my goodly pleasant things:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbd8ee90-0725-406a-b7dd-90a1421ef9b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: JOL 3:6
Text: The children also of Judah and the children of Jerusalem have ye sold unto the Grecians, that ye might remove them far from their border.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1f53339-88ef-443f-96fa-ae3968acdc90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: JOL 3:7
Text: Behold, I will raise them out of the place whither ye have sold them, and will return your recompence upon your own head:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ef942b2-9cee-45b1-91b3-80a079a14fb2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: JOL 3:8
Text: And I will sell your sons and your daughters into the hand of the children of Judah, and they shall sell them to the Sabeans, to a people far off: for the LORD hath spoken it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:471b8543-f078-466e-a94e-6dc72c6bc22a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: JOL 3:9
Text: Proclaim ye this among the Gentiles; Prepare war, wake up the mighty men, let all the men of war draw near; let them come up:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c6111f3-1b29-48df-9b32-0ddb083ebdf1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: JOL 3:10
Text: Beat your plowshares into swords and your pruninghooks into spears: let the weak say, I am strong.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5888607-b9fd-4892-900c-dc103ee09e6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: JOL 3:11
Text: Assemble yourselves, and come, all ye heathen, and gather yourselves together round about: thither cause thy mighty ones to come down, O LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef3cec7d-da59-4349-83d2-6039e4aef483>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: JOL 3:12
Text: Let the heathen be wakened, and come up to the valley of Jehoshaphat: for there will I sit to judge all the heathen round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b36c3809-47e5-4aa0-b61c-b319552d9725>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: JOL 3:13
Text: Put ye in the sickle, for the harvest is ripe: come, get you down; for the press is full, the fats overflow; for their wickedness is great.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba39d51a-fa92-4ece-806e-1bdc7f05371a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: JOL 3:14
Text: Multitudes, multitudes in the valley of decision: for the day of the LORD is near in the valley of decision.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aae7098a-6bb1-414c-9c7b-6acbf8c87c0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: JOL 3:15
Text: The sun and the moon shall be darkened, and the stars shall withdraw their shining.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e61729d7-5e5e-417a-b27e-026a419140c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: JOL 3:16
Text: The LORD also shall roar out of Zion, and utter his voice from Jerusalem; and the heavens and the earth shall shake: but the LORD will be the hope of his people, and the strength of the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cedaebf9-af47-44a2-a7ff-961d2e54732d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: JOL 3:17
Text: So shall ye know that I am the LORD your God dwelling in Zion, my holy mountain: then shall Jerusalem be holy, and there shall no strangers pass through her any more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ffb90e9-c019-4817-ab84-efae12944f74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 299

Reference: JOL 3:18
Text: And it shall come to pass in that day, that the mountains shall drop down new wine, and the hills shall flow with milk, and all the rivers of Judah shall flow with waters, and a fountain shall come forth out of the house of the LORD, and shall water the valley of Shittim.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff23dabc-314b-404f-a822-996cffc588de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: JOL 3:19
Text: Egypt shall be a desolation, and Edom shall be a desolate wilderness, for the violence against the children of Judah, because they have shed innocent blood in their land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/3/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6705da4-2171-4f9f-a535-42d01ff48eac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: JOL 3:20
Text: But Judah shall dwell for ever, and Jerusalem from generation to generation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JOL/3/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a004b447-c628-4bf8-bde6-d14e3a035b63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: JOL 3:21
Text: For I will cleanse their blood that I have not cleansed: for the LORD dwelleth in Zion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2cb8638-1460-4771-8293-3e9c024e5ed3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: AMO 1:1
Text: The words of Amos, who was among the herdmen of Tekoa, which he saw concerning Israel in the days of Uzziah king of Judah, and in the days of Jeroboam the son of Joash king of Israel, two years before the earthquake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3075dd2d-554e-4898-860b-9dd44c91cc0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: AMO 1:2
Text: And he said, The LORD will roar from Zion, and utter his voice from Jerusalem; and the habitations of the shepherds shall mourn, and the top of Carmel shall wither.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a45df0f3-7f07-445e-b482-178901a44153>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: AMO 1:3
Text: Thus saith the LORD; For three transgressions of Damascus, and for four, I will not turn away the punishment thereof; because they have threshed Gilead with threshing instruments of iron:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:939da74e-5992-4387-852b-0adce13406f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: AMO 1:4
Text: But I will send a fire into the house of Hazael, which shall devour the palaces of Benhadad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f040e6a7-30f3-47c2-b659-0362ea645650>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: AMO 1:5
Text: I will break also the bar of Damascus, and cut off the inhabitant from the plain of Aven, and him that holdeth the sceptre from the house of Eden: and the people of Syria shall go into captivity unto Kir, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1e47f46-56a5-4d3c-af51-64d9b2180614>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: AMO 1:6
Text: Thus saith the LORD; For three transgressions of Gaza, and for four, I will not turn away the punishment thereof; because they carried away captive the whole captivity, to deliver them up to Edom:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ff5ee91-8d98-4389-b15b-ccbddc423082>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: AMO 1:7
Text: But I will send a fire on the wall of Gaza, which shall devour the palaces thereof:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b526fb9-49f7-4ec4-b657-e6bc00cedc89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: AMO 1:8
Text: And I will cut off the inhabitant from Ashdod, and him that holdeth the sceptre from Ashkelon, and I will turn mine hand against Ekron: and the remnant of the Philistines shall perish, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1686742-5f94-49e8-b663-e7a4d3ffa0bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: AMO 1:9
Text: Thus saith the LORD; For three transgressions of Tyrus, and for four, I will not turn away the punishment thereof; because they delivered up the whole captivity to Edom, and remembered not the brotherly covenant:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8542c890-79b7-4ab2-bff1-50db7bc0c443>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: AMO 1:10
Text: But I will send a fire on the wall of Tyrus, which shall devour the palaces thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3cb9c9c-02e7-4ef6-b36f-20da3bb56d08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 285

Reference: AMO 1:11
Text: Thus saith the LORD; For three transgressions of Edom, and for four, I will not turn away the punishment thereof; because he did pursue his brother with the sword, and did cast off all pity, and his anger did tear perpetually, and he kept his wrath for ever:


