Reference: AMO 2:6
Text: Thus saith the LORD; For three transgressions of Israel, and for four, I will not turn away the punishment thereof; because they sold the righteous for silver, and the poor for a pair of shoes;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f29d59bd-39af-47c1-8e20-32ed33911894>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: AMO 2:7
Text: That pant after the dust of the earth on the head of the poor, and turn aside the way of the meek: and a man and his father will go in unto the same maid, to profane my holy name:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67d2a21c-34c2-4d65-8cff-05d3c43d5769>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: AMO 2:8
Text: And they lay themselves down upon clothes laid to pledge by every altar, and they drink the wine of the condemned in the house of their god.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3a34fe3-c5b1-45ff-8825-b42fb823a74a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: AMO 2:9
Text: Yet destroyed I the Amorite before them, whose height was like the height of the cedars, and he was strong as the oaks; yet I destroyed his fruit from above, and his roots from beneath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ec30758-77b8-4e6c-9e4e-fe3991afebc3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: AMO 2:10
Text: Also I brought you up from the land of Egypt, and led you forty years through the wilderness, to possess the land of the Amorite.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e6077ca-4adb-4d6e-b947-7beff5c0d02a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: AMO 2:11
Text: And I raised up of your sons for prophets, and of your young men for Nazarites. Is it not even thus, O ye children of Israel? saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc346e53-3f35-465e-a23a-a4dbf0098044>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: AMO 2:12
Text: But ye gave the Nazarites wine to drink; and commanded the prophets, saying, Prophesy not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:433e361a-e4be-421b-8314-e8b270a2e676>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: AMO 2:13
Text: Behold, I am pressed under you, as a cart is pressed that is full of sheaves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c08128d8-9607-4e9c-913d-4151ee49da55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: AMO 2:14
Text: Therefore the flight shall perish from the swift, and the strong shall not strengthen his force, neither shall the mighty deliver himself:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12768a47-1393-4116-957f-41572ddf1cd9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: AMO 2:15
Text: Neither shall he stand that handleth the bow; and he that is swift of foot shall not deliver himself: neither shall he that rideth the horse deliver himself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb811c49-b246-4d23-ac00-bb800b351a9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: AMO 2:16
Text: And he that is courageous among the mighty shall flee away naked in that day, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
