Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: AMO 3:1
Text: Hear this word that the LORD hath spoken against you, O children of Israel, against the whole family which I brought up from the land of Egypt, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2b23126-320c-4e54-9a8d-01aa08dc0922>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: AMO 3:2
Text: You only have I known of all the families of the earth: therefore I will punish you for all your iniquities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f85e6739-0026-41c7-8b01-a2165035682e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 71

Reference: AMO 3:3
Text: Can two walk together, except they be agreed?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73af2194-7530-4f94-891d-8db1cc6e844c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: AMO 3:4
Text: Will a lion roar in the forest, when he hath no prey? will a young lion cry out of his den, if he have taken nothing?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f4f751e-3158-43fc-8732-8b296f23ae26>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: AMO 3:5
Text: Can a bird fall in a snare upon the earth, where no gin is for him? shall one take up a snare from the earth, and have taken nothing at all?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18108026-4f13-4616-be40-08a5604dc54d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: AMO 3:6
Text: Shall a trumpet be blown in the city, and the people not be afraid? shall there be evil in a city, and the LORD hath not done it?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:237ebe4f-f660-4348-a56d-cbacb1f12f00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: AMO 3:7
Text: Surely the Lord GOD will do nothing, but he revealeth his secret unto his servants the prophets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6139729-0b65-4263-957e-cb1abff16f3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: AMO 3:8
Text: The lion hath roared, who will not fear? the Lord GOD hath spoken, who can but prophesy?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:026f6f72-ca2a-4475-95bf-d3cfbf03b0af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: AMO 3:9
Text: Publish in the palaces at Ashdod, and in the palaces in the land of Egypt, and say, Assemble yourselves upon the mountains of Samaria, and behold the great tumults in the midst thereof, and the oppressed in the midst thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56c4d2d7-2a45-496e-bc08-452d7c35ebc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: AMO 3:10
Text: For they know not to do right, saith the LORD, who store up violence and robbery in their palaces.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe3210a1-08bf-483f-83df-3d3caa9f317b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: AMO 3:11
Text: Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; An adversary there shall be even round about the land; and he shall bring down thy strength from thee, and thy palaces shall be spoiled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06df76f2-89ac-45f9-950f-4c76ce45a18a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: AMO 3:12
Text: Thus saith the LORD; As the shepherd taketh out of the mouth of the lion two legs, or a piece of an ear; so shall the children of Israel be taken out that dwell in Samaria in the corner of a bed, and in Damascus in a couch.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6a2c140-785f-411f-a076-5da85d1ee0ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: AMO 3:13
Text: Hear ye, and testify in the house of Jacob, saith the Lord GOD, the God of hosts,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93a2f03b-3be9-47a6-9dfc-a9e5b9d7eafc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: AMO 3:14
Text: That in the day that I shall visit the transgressions of Israel upon him I will also visit the altars of Bethel: and the horns of the altar shall be cut off, and fall to the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7be3124a-b112-4e31-820c-9062e13c533b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: AMO 3:15
Text: And I will smite the winter house with the summer house; and the houses of ivory shall perish, and the great houses shall have an end, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ca0614b-2e11-4ce2-8955-22f253e6f0ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: AMO 4:1
Text: Hear this word, ye kine of Bashan, that are in the mountain of Samaria, which oppress the poor, which crush the needy, which say to their masters, Bring, and let us drink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:368e1763-8979-4d0b-ab55-2a0017f09db5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: AMO 4:2
Text: The Lord GOD hath sworn by his holiness, that, lo, the days shall come upon you, that he will take you away with hooks, and your posterity with fishhooks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ea055d2-496f-4d8f-8aa2-021e8b668225>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: AMO 4:3
Text: And ye shall go out at the breaches, every cow at that which is before her; and ye shall cast them into the palace, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74e7b56e-730b-4bf3-b2b9-f93fd2b9d70b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: AMO 4:4
Text: Come to Bethel, and transgress; at Gilgal multiply transgression; and bring your sacrifices every morning, and your tithes after three years:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:748cadb1-b02b-4d71-baed-8e14ea1227cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: AMO 4:5
Text: And offer a sacrifice of thanksgiving with leaven, and proclaim and publish the free offerings: for this liketh you, O ye children of Israel, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c95e0f5f-08c6-4b7c-a910-e8e87616dde2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: AMO 4:6
Text: And I also have given you cleanness of teeth in all your cities, and want of bread in all your places: yet have ye not returned unto me, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf0de08f-0cad-43bb-8cfa-a79a6b69e6dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 279

Reference: AMO 4:7
Text: And also I have withholden the rain from you, when there were yet three months to the harvest: and I caused it to rain upon one city, and caused it not to rain upon another city: one piece was rained upon, and the piece whereupon it rained not withered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbace231-fc49-49ca-aafd-8f147aba9f96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: AMO 4:8
Text: So two or three cities wandered unto one city, to drink water; but they were not satisfied: yet have ye not returned unto me, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8f9824b-df04-46d9-a5cc-de3847582711>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: AMO 4:9
Text: I have smitten you with blasting and mildew: when your gardens and your vineyards and your fig trees and your olive trees increased, the palmerworm devoured them: yet have ye not returned unto me, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:660b2935-1494-4a48-92b1-fe9cb4d17d3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 288

Reference: AMO 4:10
Text: I have sent among you the pestilence after the manner of Egypt: your young men have I slain with the sword, and have taken away your horses; and I have made the stink of your camps to come up unto your nostrils: yet have ye not returned unto me, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02d7ddb2-de5e-4979-b134-7d9b4b42aa0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: AMO 4:11
Text: I have overthrown some of you, as God overthrew Sodom and Gomorrah, and ye were as a firebrand plucked out of the burning: yet have ye not returned unto me, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac47c592-c52d-4f5b-8829-03d800ebfb0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: AMO 4:12
Text: Therefore thus will I do unto thee, O Israel: and because I will do this unto thee, prepare to meet thy God, O Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cdf7a8f3-ee85-4be2-9004-8b2bab7b1d8e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: AMO 4:13
Text: For, lo, he that formeth the mountains, and createth the wind, and declareth unto man what is his thought, that maketh the morning darkness, and treadeth upon the high places of the earth, The LORD, The God of hosts, is his name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:710c156c-d464-466d-8265-a8d765cbbad4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: AMO 5:1
Text: Hear ye this word which I take up against you, even a lamentation, O house of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6a182fe-d859-4899-a436-a02f0cea1373>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: AMO 5:2
Text: The virgin of Israel is fallen; she shall no more rise: she is forsaken upon her land; there is none to raise her up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca534389-2edd-4335-ae74-46dd6bc4ebaa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: AMO 5:3
Text: For thus saith the Lord GOD; The city that went out by a thousand shall leave an hundred, and that which went forth by an hundred shall leave ten, to the house of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f21ba2b2-28c6-471d-ba42-f56c43f9e29b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: AMO 5:4
Text: For thus saith the LORD unto the house of Israel, Seek ye me, and ye shall live:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1745bb25-dfb7-49a1-935d-e3d2f5f8c525>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: AMO 5:5
Text: But seek not Bethel, nor enter into Gilgal, and pass not to Beersheba: for Gilgal shall surely go into captivity, and Bethel shall come to nought.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31214150-dba3-405c-8de6-5aca8f7cb6c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: AMO 5:6
Text: Seek the LORD, and ye shall live; lest he break out like fire in the house of Joseph, and devour it, and there be none to quench it in Bethel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7baa76e3-902c-46b8-9867-0add61627fc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: AMO 5:7
Text: Ye who turn judgment to wormwood, and leave off righteousness in the earth,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4004f127-718f-450d-9230-ae43f21cf5b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: AMO 5:8
Text: Seek him that maketh the seven stars and Orion, and turneth the shadow of death into the morning, and maketh the day dark with night: that calleth for the waters of the sea, and poureth them out upon the face of the earth: The LORD is his name:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df44a789-3354-4769-b115-bfaf772d450d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: AMO 5:9
Text: That strengtheneth the spoiled against the strong, so that the spoiled shall come against the fortress.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b38c2022-6fd9-485b-a599-7d0808aaae22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: AMO 5:10
Text: They hate him that rebuketh in the gate, and they abhor him that speaketh uprightly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a1a2452-f5af-41c1-aaf8-56fd16dd47a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: AMO 5:11
Text: Forasmuch therefore as your treading is upon the poor, and ye take from him burdens of wheat: ye have built houses of hewn stone, but ye shall not dwell in them; ye have planted pleasant vineyards, but ye shall not drink wine of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e89ac6e-da77-4fb3-b848-7493043b0817>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: AMO 5:12
Text: For I know your manifold transgressions and your mighty sins: they afflict the just, they take a bribe, and they turn aside the poor in the gate from their right.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42858004-b607-4b67-bcb4-de8401dd9c02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: AMO 5:13
Text: Therefore the prudent shall keep silence in that time; for it is an evil time.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f2ae938-a31e-4157-ab2d-a493055f6438>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: AMO 5:14
Text: Seek good, and not evil, that ye may live: and so the LORD, the God of hosts, shall be with you, as ye have spoken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb2a4a47-4d12-4100-b713-c2e7b47e826b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: AMO 5:15
Text: Hate the evil, and love the good, and establish judgment in the gate: it may be that the LORD God of hosts will be gracious unto the remnant of Joseph.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c55afed2-dc3d-407b-a6bc-dea905b9aa75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: AMO 5:16
Text: Therefore the LORD, the God of hosts, the LORD, saith thus; Wailing shall be in all streets; and they shall say in all the highways, Alas! alas! and they shall call the husbandman to mourning, and such as are skilful of lamentation to wailing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af0c24a9-f5e2-4490-87cb-a6c21bd7ee42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: AMO 5:17
Text: And in all vineyards shall be wailing: for I will pass through thee, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83c4e683-fd82-405d-98b3-a20f47d9a1a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: AMO 5:18
Text: Woe unto you that desire the day of the LORD! to what end is it for you? the day of the LORD is darkness, and not light.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e81a5bad-093e-4a9e-99e5-47d26ffd47e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: AMO 5:19
Text: As if a man did flee from a lion, and a bear met him; or went into the house, and leaned his hand on the wall, and a serpent bit him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12a5db55-edf3-498f-a896-226e0abe3021>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: AMO 5:20
Text: Shall not the day of the LORD be darkness, and not light? even very dark, and no brightness in it?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2d879de-4396-42c1-864d-c34e48afe6db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: AMO 5:21
Text: I hate, I despise your feast days, and I will not smell in your solemn assemblies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9146aff0-638e-4ecf-9156-31d97f04b85d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: AMO 5:22
Text: Though ye offer me burnt offerings and your meat offerings, I will not accept them: neither will I regard the peace offerings of your fat beasts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20855896-5469-414c-973c-7a7b85061465>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: AMO 5:23
Text: Take thou away from me the noise of thy songs; for I will not hear the melody of thy viols.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44ef0695-1543-4c72-bbb2-6cc2ac63fd7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: AMO 5:24
Text: But let judgment run down as waters, and righteousness as a mighty stream.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11fa710b-2c2f-4348-bdaa-c4003ee33a28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: AMO 5:25
Text: Have ye offered unto me sacrifices and offerings in the wilderness forty years, O house of Israel?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aaa63b66-8cde-445b-bd75-04b6dfd1bd39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: AMO 5:26
Text: But ye have borne the tabernacle of your Moloch and Chiun your images, the star of your god, which ye made to yourselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/5/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78f5fbe4-95a5-4345-9ee3-4035c23fa2f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: AMO 5:27
Text: Therefore will I cause you to go into captivity beyond Damascus, saith the LORD, whose name is The God of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:114eb222-1795-41fd-977a-4c73e2c4ca4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: AMO 6:1
Text: Woe to them that are at ease in Zion, and trust in the mountain of Samaria, which are named chief of the nations, to whom the house of Israel came!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c80f4add-e60a-4165-90eb-dc3ba628fe53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: AMO 6:2
Text: Pass ye unto Calneh, and see; and from thence go ye to Hamath the great: then go down to Gath of the Philistines: be they better than these kingdoms? or their border greater than your border?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ffad3b7-8e95-4d26-87cc-44e894a9894d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: AMO 6:3
Text: Ye that put far away the evil day, and cause the seat of violence to come near;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fdce8f0d-9acf-41bc-a3f5-a3a6551056bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: AMO 6:4
Text: That lie upon beds of ivory, and stretch themselves upon their couches, and eat the lambs out of the flock, and the calves out of the midst of the stall;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71546549-1947-4e4f-9a5b-0c9d20cf305a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: AMO 6:5
Text: That chant to the sound of the viol, and invent to themselves instruments of musick, like David;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bec99a18-7198-4498-9037-01de3ed27162>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: AMO 6:6
Text: That drink wine in bowls, and anoint themselves with the chief ointments: but they are not grieved for the affliction of Joseph.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9bdd90cd-d07c-4d36-80f6-e444b4f8d06e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: AMO 6:7
Text: Therefore now shall they go captive with the first that go captive, and the banquet of them that stretched themselves shall be removed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b70a0ac-bb3a-4463-8959-21ea14ffa624>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: AMO 6:8
Text: The Lord GOD hath sworn by himself, saith the LORD the God of hosts, I abhor the excellency of Jacob, and hate his palaces: therefore will I deliver up the city with all that is therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56329824-c440-4059-a740-3dfbeae181e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: AMO 6:9
Text: And it shall come to pass, if there remain ten men in one house, that they shall die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5077ac1-d0ec-48a3-8676-fe4e5a6b4d0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 328

Reference: AMO 6:10
Text: And a man’s uncle shall take him up, and he that burneth him, to bring out the bones out of the house, and shall say unto him that is by the sides of the house, Is there yet any with thee? and he shall say, No. Then shall he say, Hold thy tongue: for we may not make mention of the name of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23441148-4882-4352-be3a-91f28d6d227a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: AMO 6:11
Text: For, behold, the LORD commandeth, and he will smite the great house with breaches, and the little house with clefts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27c8a48d-8de7-4008-8d92-babf7594a8fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: AMO 6:12
Text: Shall horses run upon the rock? will one plow there with oxen? for ye have turned judgment into gall, and the fruit of righteousness into hemlock:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5411495-f111-4c8e-8f90-0b5141c82388>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: AMO 6:13
Text: Ye which rejoice in a thing of nought, which say, Have we not taken to us horns by our own strength?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/6/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee074750-2b9c-4e7d-97cc-3a9a6d9c123b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: AMO 6:14
Text: But, behold, I will raise up against you a nation, O house of Israel, saith the LORD the God of hosts; and they shall afflict you from the entering in of Hemath unto the river of the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11fa3d01-e666-4162-92f8-7950dad6d8db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: AMO 7:1
Text: Thus hath the Lord GOD shewed unto me; and, behold, he formed grasshoppers in the beginning of the shooting up of the latter growth; and, lo, it was the latter growth after the king’s mowings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ab36d52-203f-4616-85f2-8eaf77d44c63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: AMO 7:2
Text: And it came to pass, that when they had made an end of eating the grass of the land, then I said, O Lord GOD, forgive, I beseech thee: by whom shall Jacob arise? for he is small.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c585f4f6-7c02-49cb-929d-549bd67be45e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: AMO 7:3
Text: The LORD repented for this: It shall not be, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60e30813-587a-47a6-b291-dab947e1833c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: AMO 7:4
Text: Thus hath the Lord GOD shewed unto me: and, behold, the Lord GOD called to contend by fire, and it devoured the great deep, and did eat up a part.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe8f033f-5ad2-4817-a4a1-9acbda4b834b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: AMO 7:5
Text: Then said I, O Lord GOD, cease, I beseech thee: by whom shall Jacob arise? for he is small.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9df4bb42-bc47-4163-bbb0-373977850512>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: AMO 7:6
Text: The LORD repented for this: This also shall not be, saith the Lord GOD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56d4c665-8a86-4091-b0d0-70e087201726>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: AMO 7:7
Text: Thus he shewed me: and, behold, the LORD stood upon a wall made by a plumbline, with a plumbline in his hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9035436f-614e-4530-95be-9cb29fd10140>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: AMO 7:8
Text: And the LORD said unto me, Amos, what seest thou? And I said, A plumbline. Then said the LORD, Behold, I will set a plumbline in the midst of my people Israel: I will not again pass by them any more:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86f7a3eb-2213-4f8f-858c-e0e4aeddbe7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: AMO 7:9
Text: And the high places of Isaac shall be desolate, and the sanctuaries of Israel shall be laid waste; and I will rise against the house of Jeroboam with the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a64727e6-146e-4437-bb9c-68e58eca27dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: AMO 7:10
Text: Then Amaziah the priest of Bethel sent to Jeroboam king of Israel, saying, Amos hath conspired against thee in the midst of the house of Israel: the land is not able to bear all his words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97b1ee1f-ffba-475d-b1d4-1cc4eac74fd1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: AMO 7:11
Text: For thus Amos saith, Jeroboam shall die by the sword, and Israel shall surely be led away captive out of their own land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:899b7005-ab95-42f5-8fbc-6cb6181d00ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: AMO 7:12
Text: Also Amaziah said unto Amos, O thou seer, go, flee thee away into the land of Judah, and there eat bread, and prophesy there:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac332d4f-f2a8-4d49-b4c9-69846b43ccbe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: AMO 7:13
Text: But prophesy not again any more at Bethel: for it is the king’s chapel, and it is the king’s court.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/7/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ecb1190-ff48-46f5-a23f-26ea386ff3c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: AMO 7:14
Text: Then answered Amos, and said to Amaziah, I was no prophet, neither was I a prophet’s son; but I was an herdman, and a gatherer of sycomore fruit:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/7/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0fdb5081-3097-4158-9e74-7b38dc5b27fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: AMO 7:15
Text: And the LORD took me as I followed the flock, and the LORD said unto me, Go, prophesy unto my people Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/7/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0dbeaaf3-9baf-4efa-bc52-4b12e179327a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: AMO 7:16
Text: Now therefore hear thou the word of the LORD: Thou sayest, Prophesy not against Israel, and drop not thy word against the house of Isaac.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/7/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00aeaeaa-b7a0-4e3c-814e-22af39fdbbbd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 293

Reference: AMO 7:17
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD; Thy wife shall be an harlot in the city, and thy sons and thy daughters shall fall by the sword, and thy land shall be divided by line; and thou shalt die in a polluted land: and Israel shall surely go into captivity forth of his land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/8/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abdfdf20-492e-42c3-8983-9864bdadd366>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: AMO 8:1
Text: Thus hath the Lord GOD shewed unto me: and behold a basket of summer fruit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/8/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dea3e265-787e-40ec-87e0-2b220827a3c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: AMO 8:2
Text: And he said, Amos, what seest thou? And I said, A basket of summer fruit. Then said the LORD unto me, The end is come upon my people of Israel; I will not again pass by them any more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/8/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:240abec0-f81c-4de7-9377-600d1c1e72a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: AMO 8:3
Text: And the songs of the temple shall be howlings in that day, saith the Lord GOD: there shall be many dead bodies in every place; they shall cast them forth with silence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/8/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6fc87389-0d33-4695-9a01-2be8fb3dc27e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: AMO 8:4
Text: Hear this, O ye that swallow up the needy, even to make the poor of the land to fail,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/8/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15d5251c-be09-4db7-b183-a79de1abc7a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: AMO 8:5
Text: Saying, When will the new moon be gone, that we may sell corn? and the sabbath, that we may set forth wheat, making the ephah small, and the shekel great, and falsifying the balances by deceit?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/8/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:711d534e-d433-4af8-b07d-bb1b75455969>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: AMO 8:6
Text: That we may buy the poor for silver, and the needy for a pair of shoes; yea, and sell the refuse of the wheat?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/8/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8bd4ff9-1bf9-491d-aa81-3470c3a2c665>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: AMO 8:7
Text: The LORD hath sworn by the excellency of Jacob, Surely I will never forget any of their works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/8/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:774983b7-78e7-4c8e-bb47-9f421d06787e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: AMO 8:8
Text: Shall not the land tremble for this, and every one mourn that dwelleth therein? and it shall rise up wholly as a flood; and it shall be cast out and drowned, as by the flood of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/8/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6ee9794-a338-492a-8b52-4c67b3ef5052>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: AMO 8:9
Text: And it shall come to pass in that day, saith the Lord GOD, that I will cause the sun to go down at noon, and I will darken the earth in the clear day:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/8/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:130de6bc-d3a8-402a-b5ea-ab9d9eaa7042>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: AMO 8:10
Text: And I will turn your feasts into mourning, and all your songs into lamentation; and I will bring up sackcloth upon all loins, and baldness upon every head; and I will make it as the mourning of an only son, and the end thereof as a bitter day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/8/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a049f7a6-03cf-4fe7-b194-f8eb42557c3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: AMO 8:11
Text: Behold, the days come, saith the Lord GOD, that I will send a famine in the land, not a famine of bread, nor a thirst for water, but of hearing the words of the LORD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/8/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c59c319-5c33-4e38-94f4-f21ed888e4d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: AMO 8:12
Text: And they shall wander from sea to sea, and from the north even to the east, they shall run to and fro to seek the word of the LORD, and shall not find it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/8/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62cadf8c-b4e3-4c60-b85d-9ffa48b59f02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: AMO 8:13
Text: In that day shall the fair virgins and young men faint for thirst.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/8/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c480718-7245-40cf-b169-71f2ea982208>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: AMO 8:14
Text: They that swear by the sin of Samaria, and say, Thy god, O Dan, liveth; and, The manner of Beersheba liveth; even they shall fall, and never rise up again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/9/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff1501a5-f0a6-4579-9ace-219b51e1d3e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 319

Reference: AMO 9:1
Text: I saw the LORD standing upon the altar: and he said, Smite the lintel of the door, that the posts may shake: and cut them in the head, all of them; and I will slay the last of them with the sword: he that fleeth of them shall not flee away, and he that escapeth of them shall not be delivered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/9/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91739a8f-e1bc-4f36-b6d8-aad6ff913611>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: AMO 9:2
Text: Though they dig into hell, thence shall mine hand take them; though they climb up to heaven, thence will I bring them down:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/9/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f42b795-0c65-4b04-8d52-65f6f5f088cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: AMO 9:3
Text: And though they hide themselves in the top of Carmel, I will search and take them out thence; and though they be hid from my sight in the bottom of the sea, thence will I command the serpent, and he shall bite them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/9/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbb4ca53-a200-4bcf-b355-9413b986566c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: AMO 9:4
Text: And though they go into captivity before their enemies, thence will I command the sword, and it shall slay them: and I will set mine eyes upon them for evil, and not for good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/9/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a34215d3-a1cc-4de8-befd-38651c366b41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: AMO 9:5
Text: And the Lord GOD of hosts is he that toucheth the land, and it shall melt, and all that dwell therein shall mourn: and it shall rise up wholly like a flood; and shall be drowned, as by the flood of Egypt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/9/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b725a1d-4f9d-4cc9-8701-f6125bf978bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: AMO 9:6
Text: It is he that buildeth his stories in the heaven, and hath founded his troop in the earth; he that calleth for the waters of the sea, and poureth them out upon the face of the earth: The LORD is his name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/9/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8e21826-efaf-4a6c-a518-17cec4fb637c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: AMO 9:7
Text: Are ye not as children of the Ethiopians unto me, O children of Israel? saith the LORD. Have not I brought up Israel out of the land of Egypt? and the Philistines from Caphtor, and the Syrians from Kir?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/9/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50925944-98d6-4f6d-a79c-d86e871aee97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: AMO 9:8
Text: Behold, the eyes of the Lord GOD are upon the sinful kingdom, and I will destroy it from off the face of the earth; saving that I will not utterly destroy the house of Jacob, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/9/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e924328-379b-4884-ac72-7d564bde2d7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: AMO 9:9
Text: For, lo, I will command, and I will sift the house of Israel among all nations, like as corn is sifted in a sieve, yet shall not the least grain fall upon the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/9/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b72355d-a980-4bb9-9634-9b4f8729e869>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: AMO 9:10
Text: All the sinners of my people shall die by the sword, which say, The evil shall not overtake nor prevent us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/9/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac1394f3-8370-4627-aedf-17dbf47d7656>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: AMO 9:11
Text: In that day will I raise up the tabernacle of David that is fallen, and close up the breaches thereof; and I will raise up his ruins, and I will build it as in the days of old:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/9/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a939893-d86b-4b35-ae21-d570d9520584>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: AMO 9:12
Text: That they may possess the remnant of Edom, and of all the heathen, which are called by my name, saith the LORD that doeth this.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/9/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b4c769b-9076-4db1-a6aa-5dbbd99410bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: AMO 9:13
Text: Behold, the days come, saith the LORD, that the plowman shall overtake the reaper, and the treader of grapes him that soweth seed; and the mountains shall drop sweet wine, and all the hills shall melt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/9/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:947bb8c4-5baa-45f1-a664-f5f2d536fe2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: AMO 9:14
Text: And I will bring again the captivity of my people of Israel, and they shall build the waste cities, and inhabit them; and they shall plant vineyards, and drink the wine thereof; they shall also make gardens, and eat the fruit of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/AMO/9/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8c29493-85d6-413d-9726-73fad1cd6da5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: AMO 9:15
Text: And I will plant them upon their land, and they shall no more be pulled up out of their land which I have given them, saith the LORD thy God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/OBA/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:723077a0-71ca-43c0-9b40-3cc5bfdb7988>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: OBA 1:1
Text: The vision of Obadiah. Thus saith the Lord GOD concerning Edom; We have heard a rumour from the LORD, and an ambassador is sent among the heathen, Arise ye, and let us rise up against her in battle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/OBA/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f454feda-ecdb-4223-98b1-7339551bc19a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: OBA 1:2
Text: Behold, I have made thee small among the heathen: thou art greatly despised.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/OBA/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91f1e820-26d6-4c18-bd6a-cac24ab2c1a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: OBA 1:3
Text: The pride of thine heart hath deceived thee, thou that dwellest in the clefts of the rock, whose habitation is high; that saith in his heart, Who shall bring me down to the ground?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/OBA/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19d9b650-20c2-48c5-8323-c816ebadf4f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: OBA 1:4
Text: Though thou exalt thyself as the eagle, and though thou set thy nest among the stars, thence will I bring thee down, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/OBA/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67193a5f-d84f-426a-8285-8302581b6ea4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: OBA 1:5
Text: If thieves came to thee, if robbers by night, (how art thou cut off!) would they not have stolen till they had enough? if the grapegatherers came to thee, would they not leave some grapes?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/OBA/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4cf06107-b422-4902-bd00-7cbbf3f244ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: OBA 1:6
Text: How are the things of Esau searched out! how are his hidden things sought up!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/OBA/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43b24662-47cd-4454-abca-7a3b9d4a0078>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: OBA 1:7
Text: All the men of thy confederacy have brought thee even to the border: the men that were at peace with thee have deceived thee, and prevailed against thee; they that eat thy bread have laid a wound under thee: there is none understanding in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/OBA/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cd14faf-92b9-4ab7-b5d9-35b80d0e71d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: OBA 1:8
Text: Shall I not in that day, saith the LORD, even destroy the wise men out of Edom, and understanding out of the mount of Esau?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/OBA/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:641a747d-6f09-44f1-8ff8-b8d20ca63b32>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: OBA 1:9
Text: And thy mighty men, O Teman, shall be dismayed, to the end that every one of the mount of Esau may be cut off by slaughter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/OBA/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e272f033-4656-4820-a18c-28e8b8e05a8e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: OBA 1:10
Text: For thy violence against thy brother Jacob shame shall cover thee, and thou shalt be cut off for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/OBA/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75d07d56-a870-4db6-abfa-67992d0b0fc9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: OBA 1:11
Text: In the day that thou stoodest on the other side, in the day that the strangers carried away captive his forces, and foreigners entered into his gates, and cast lots upon Jerusalem, even thou wast as one of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/OBA/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29dd60cb-02ec-40d1-ac0b-abb2a5fc0c7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 289

Reference: OBA 1:12
Text: But thou shouldest not have looked on the day of thy brother in the day that he became a stranger; neither shouldest thou have rejoiced over the children of Judah in the day of their destruction; neither shouldest thou have spoken proudly in the day of distress.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/OBA/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e985b124-ee24-4169-879e-18adee273549>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: OBA 1:13
Text: Thou shouldest not have entered into the gate of my people in the day of their calamity; yea, thou shouldest not have looked on their affliction in the day of their calamity, nor have laid hands on their substance in the day of their calamity;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/OBA/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4063223d-38bf-4196-a1dd-f5ef5ed9a2d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: OBA 1:14
Text: Neither shouldest thou have stood in the crossway, to cut off those of his that did escape; neither shouldest thou have delivered up those of his that did remain in the day of distress.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/OBA/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:412d5f92-6dff-4575-8d3c-8c1320dd53ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: OBA 1:15
Text: For the day of the LORD is near upon all the heathen: as thou hast done, it shall be done unto thee: thy reward shall return upon thine own head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/OBA/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bc1f424-c7bf-4b0c-a49c-aa5109435829>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: OBA 1:16
Text: For as ye have drunk upon my holy mountain, so shall all the heathen drink continually, yea, they shall drink, and they shall swallow down, and they shall be as though they had not been.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/OBA/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4a390bf-e288-4e31-9c48-97259f437df4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: OBA 1:17
Text: But upon mount Zion shall be deliverance, and there shall be holiness; and the house of Jacob shall possess their possessions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/OBA/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:944742bf-5230-4d67-b805-c0051408285a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: OBA 1:18
Text: And the house of Jacob shall be a fire, and the house of Joseph a flame, and the house of Esau for stubble, and they shall kindle in them, and devour them; and there shall not be any remaining of the house of Esau; for the LORD hath spoken it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/OBA/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8fe27ff2-8e21-4606-9b27-61bd4dfa574d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: OBA 1:19
Text: And they of the south shall possess the mount of Esau; and they of the plain the Philistines: and they shall possess the fields of Ephraim, and the fields of Samaria: and Benjamin shall possess Gilead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/OBA/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4db65c5-3c72-45c5-8dbd-03c32917259a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: OBA 1:20
Text: And the captivity of this host of the children of Israel shall possess that of the Canaanites, even unto Zarephath; and the captivity of Jerusalem, which is in Sepharad, shall possess the cities of the south.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/OBA/1/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73e0c590-5182-4f72-af71-94961029f8c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: OBA 1:21
Text: And saviours shall come up on mount Zion to judge the mount of Esau; and the kingdom shall be the LORD’s.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f256be5-4d09-47c1-8479-ce18039c5b5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: JON 1:1
Text: Now the word of the LORD came unto Jonah the son of Amittai, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa6ef912-3996-49c0-9fd4-abd1643b8687>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: JON 1:2
Text: Arise, go to Nineveh, that great city, and cry against it; for their wickedness is come up before me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4639bf57-6251-433a-9912-a4ea43eda255>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: JON 1:3
Text: But Jonah rose up to flee unto Tarshish from the presence of the LORD, and went down to Joppa; and he found a ship going to Tarshish: so he paid the fare thereof, and went down into it, to go with them unto Tarshish from the presence of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5e50086-34a4-4590-8b3b-6d9f9a7b9f87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: JON 1:4
Text: But the LORD sent out a great wind into the sea, and there was a mighty tempest in the sea, so that the ship was like to be broken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46f3ac87-9240-4872-b089-6c0bf107ee47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: JON 1:5
Text: Then the mariners were afraid, and cried every man unto his god, and cast forth the wares that were in the ship into the sea, to lighten it of them. But Jonah was gone down into the sides of the ship; and he lay, and was fast asleep.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12bc32f7-49a0-4071-81de-7d23359ae30c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: JON 1:6
Text: So the shipmaster came to him, and said unto him, What meanest thou, O sleeper? arise, call upon thy God, if so be that God will think upon us, that we perish not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8b86ee4-8d51-4eec-a75c-87c8adb4a88e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: JON 1:7
Text: And they said every one to his fellow, Come, and let us cast lots, that we may know for whose cause this evil is upon us. So they cast lots, and the lot fell upon Jonah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:218ad263-fa79-46ab-b3b6-064bc3b7b6dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: JON 1:8
Text: Then said they unto him, Tell us, we pray thee, for whose cause this evil is upon us; What is thine occupation? and whence comest thou? what is thy country? and of what people art thou?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8c16657-f29e-453a-a2b4-25b62a5b2e67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: JON 1:9
Text: And he said unto them, I am an Hebrew; and I fear the LORD, the God of heaven, which hath made the sea and the dry land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12338623-45bd-4a99-ae9f-aed413fb0273>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: JON 1:10
Text: Then were the men exceedingly afraid, and said unto him. Why hast thou done this? For the men knew that he fled from the presence of the LORD, because he had told them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:adcf7c96-cba1-4e7b-95a4-938100fa2bde>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: JON 1:11
Text: Then said they unto him, What shall we do unto thee, that the sea may be calm unto us? for the sea wrought, and was tempestuous.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73648802-d57f-4289-97e3-ffe2d6a56cf4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: JON 1:12
Text: And he said unto them, Take me up, and cast me forth into the sea; so shall the sea be calm unto you: for I know that for my sake this great tempest is upon you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7538ad12-9a2a-45df-a0c8-a4a86ef37647>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: JON 1:13
Text: Nevertheless the men rowed hard to bring it to the land; but they could not: for the sea wrought, and was tempestuous against them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87d3b5e3-6f61-4ec7-a2a2-fca5a04ad766>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: JON 1:14
Text: Wherefore they cried unto the LORD, and said, We beseech thee, O LORD, we beseech thee, let us not perish for this man’s life, and lay not upon us innocent blood: for thou, O LORD, hast done as it pleased thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7cef7bde-b3f5-4cf5-a3c6-94a5cfafa097>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: JON 1:15
Text: So they look up Jonah, and cast him forth into the sea: and the sea ceased from her raging.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32d79f56-8aef-48a4-bc72-8c98f2154033>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: JON 1:16
Text: Then the men feared the LORD exceedingly, and offered a sacrifice unto the LORD, and made vows.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb96b1dd-59f5-4a27-b0bc-8cc83163087a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: JON 1:17
Text: Now the LORD had prepared a great fish to swallow up Jonah. And Jonah was in the belly of the fish three days and three nights.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db33277f-48c9-4fd6-8b4a-7323110e38a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: JON 2:1
Text: Then Jonah prayed unto the LORD his God out of the fish’s belly,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6897fec7-5989-413b-b041-d099f26aedf2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: JON 2:2
Text: And said, I cried by reason of mine affliction unto the LORD, and he heard me; out of the belly of hell cried I, and thou heardest my voice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5d18c5e-99e4-487a-9340-8d138f55f828>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: JON 2:3
Text: For thou hadst cast me into the deep, in the midst of the seas; and the floods compassed me about: all thy billows and thy waves passed over me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47d14af6-977b-448a-8b5e-b17c8e5007dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: JON 2:4
Text: Then I said, I am cast out of thy sight; yet I will look again toward thy holy temple.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66355b54-a229-470a-90a0-beffb0a23d5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: JON 2:5
Text: The waters compassed me about, even to the soul: the depth closed me round about, the weeds were wrapped about my head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52bb13cf-2251-4d95-9f48-c4773ef8be83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: JON 2:6
Text: I went down to the bottoms of the mountains; the earth with her bars was about me for ever: yet hast thou brought up my life from corruption, O LORD my God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e856a291-2d09-4525-ba03-9042232e800e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: JON 2:7
Text: When my soul fainted within me I remembered the LORD: and my prayer came in unto thee, into thine holy temple.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:511b7233-ef3e-4775-9ce0-a816ae9ad6dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: JON 2:8
Text: They that observe lying vanities forsake their own mercy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:953d0e21-f745-45fe-b51b-f972b478a49e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: JON 2:9
Text: But I will sacrifice unto thee with the voice of thanksgiving; I will pay that that I have vowed. Salvation is of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:667dcf0e-92da-4ca3-9974-0b678df7d260>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: JON 2:10
Text: And the LORD spake unto the fish, and it vomited out Jonah upon the dry land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72acee48-2b55-438d-a6b3-83ebd6ee64ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: JON 3:1
Text: And the word of the LORD came unto Jonah the second time, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7142f11-43e1-4510-b204-962647eb8f6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: JON 3:2
Text: Arise, go unto Nineveh, that great city, and preach unto it the preaching that I bid thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb77c963-fa15-422a-823f-f23f48d6f3ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: JON 3:3
Text: So Jonah arose, and went unto Nineveh, according to the word of the LORD. Now Nineveh was an exceeding great city of three days’ journey.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0202158f-49d5-411a-af3c-513375d68a5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: JON 3:4
Text: And Jonah began to enter into the city a day’s journey, and he cried, and said, Yet forty days, and Nineveh shall be overthrown.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ed2112a-0f25-47cf-8eb4-c3f598004698>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: JON 3:5
Text: So the people of Nineveh believed God, and proclaimed a fast, and put on sackcloth, from the greatest of them even to the least of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e723a4c8-1d79-4c79-a032-34651ce1639f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: JON 3:6
Text: For word came unto the king of Nineveh, and he arose from his throne, and he laid his robe from him, and covered him with sackcloth, and sat in ashes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2a82126-0a3e-468d-8029-5e9b31972f73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: JON 3:7
Text: And he caused it to be proclaimed and published through Nineveh by the decree of the king and his nobles, saying, Let neither man nor beast, herd nor flock, taste any thing: let them not feed, nor drink water:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06e743bc-3dc3-4bc3-bd95-dd3ec5d79562>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: JON 3:8
Text: But let man and beast be covered with sackcloth, and cry mightily unto God: yea, let them turn every one from his evil way, and from the violence that is in their hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d38ff068-bbc3-41e8-bedd-c7d656bd358f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: JON 3:9
Text: Who can tell if God will turn and repent, and turn away from his fierce anger, that we perish not?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3908e5ac-ab23-4838-b690-e4cfeef32812>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: JON 3:10
Text: And God saw their works, that they turned from their evil way; and God repented of the evil, that he had said that he would do unto them; and he did it not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e77da217-3385-42c6-9618-26e940fc499f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: JON 4:1
Text: But it displeased Jonah exceedingly, and he was very angry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9a46f20-a83d-4d9a-a9c4-3c45d34287cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 303

Reference: JON 4:2
Text: And he prayed unto the LORD, and said, I pray thee, O LORD, was not this my saying, when I was yet in my country? Therefore I fled before unto Tarshish: for I knew that thou art a gracious God, and merciful, slow to anger, and of great kindness, and repentest thee of the evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1739c588-d77e-45d1-b5f3-0892e59de08a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: JON 4:3
Text: Therefore now, O LORD, take, I beseech thee, my life from me; for it is better for me to die than to live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e19dc31-ff0b-4a4f-b751-82f338155e0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: JON 4:4
Text: Then said the LORD, Doest thou well to be angry?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31d61b44-1e64-4869-86c9-84fc14ca2966>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: JON 4:5
Text: So Jonah went out of the city, and sat on the east side of the city, and there made him a booth, and sat under it in the shadow, till he might see what would become of the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d376a718-081f-4698-a80a-2af6fc1d002e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: JON 4:6
Text: And the LORD God prepared a gourd, and made it to come up over Jonah, that it might be a shadow over his head, to deliver him from his grief. So Jonah was exceeding glad of the gourd.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77ff6b96-97c2-49a6-85c9-77b0a03a7d56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: JON 4:7
Text: But God prepared a worm when the morning rose the next day, and it smote the gourd that it withered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5145383-c66f-4fcb-8fd9-53aba74a42fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: JON 4:8
Text: And it came to pass, when the sun did arise, that God prepared a vehement east wind; and the sun beat upon the head of Jonah, that he fainted, and wished in himself to die, and said, It is better for me to die than to live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:943efb48-5f5c-49c5-b6ca-9f9a00489212>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: JON 4:9
Text: And God said to Jonah, Doest thou well to be angry for the gourd? And he said, I do well to be angry, even unto death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f15aa8c-7804-4da6-855b-8660a1db7303>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: JON 4:10
Text: Then said the LORD, Thou hast had pity on the gourd, for the which thou hast not laboured, neither madest it grow; which came up in a night, and perished in a night:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JON/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08425594-7dd7-4709-881c-150ed73129b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: JON 4:11
Text: And should not I spare Nineveh, that great city, wherein are more than sixscore thousand persons that cannot discern between their right hand and their left hand; and also much cattle?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9856da14-09e7-44df-90f4-aa3d11e3a24f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: MIC 1:1
Text: The word of the LORD that came to Micah the Morasthite in the days of Jotham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah, kings of Judah, which he saw concerning Samaria and Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0411848c-50c0-42cf-972b-9f4455da7486>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: MIC 1:2
Text: Hear, all ye people; hearken, O earth, and all that therein is: and let the Lord GOD be witness against you, the LORD from his holy temple.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:663c1fed-e02a-43b7-9f19-ba58b6a99abf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: MIC 1:3
Text: For, behold, the LORD cometh forth out of his place, and will come down, and tread upon the high places of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6471dabd-b8e0-466e-898c-bdefebeb6b5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: MIC 1:4
Text: And the mountains shall be molten under him, and the valleys shall be cleft, as wax before the fire, and as the waters that are poured down a steep place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5391919-9225-47d4-ac59-7a6721e8d091>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: MIC 1:5
Text: For the transgression of Jacob is all this, and for the sins of the house of Israel. What is the transgression of Jacob? is it not Samaria? and what are the high places of Judah? are they not Jerusalem?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de4ec6bb-eb53-4218-9520-2b8b1888bc6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: MIC 1:6
Text: Therefore I will make Samaria as an heap of the field, and as plantings of a vineyard: and I will pour down the stones thereof into the valley, and I will discover the foundations thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f8d782a-ad05-45eb-b648-595dccbbc4f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: MIC 1:7
Text: And all the graven images thereof shall be beaten to pieces, and all the hires thereof shall be burned with the fire, and all the idols thereof will I lay desolate: for she gathered it of the hire of an harlot, and they shall return to the hire of an harlot.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43d66369-0dd3-49d6-aeac-ab682ef902a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: MIC 1:8
Text: Therefore I will wail and howl, I will go stripped and naked: I will make a wailing like the dragons, and mourning as the owls.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:138f9b7c-1efb-407c-a6d3-7c0fe1bba130>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MIC 1:9
Text: For her wound is incurable; for it is come unto Judah; he is come unto the gate of my people, even to Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a4067fe-0dab-426b-a7ac-c953f3513620>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MIC 1:10
Text: Declare ye it not at Gath, weep ye not at all: in the house of Aphrah roll thyself in the dust.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:436495bd-91bf-4fec-b2f7-2bf378c1e073>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: MIC 1:11
Text: Pass ye away, thou inhabitant of Saphir, having thy shame naked: the inhabitant of Zaanan came not forth in the mourning of Bethezel; he shall receive of you his standing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:982d6420-1b79-48e3-a509-f1832bc27c2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: MIC 1:12
Text: For the inhabitant of Maroth waited carefully for good: but evil came down from the LORD unto the gate of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:277e903a-af3f-4669-8bec-422245435be1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: MIC 1:13
Text: O thou inhabitant of Lachish, bind the chariot to the swift beast: she is the beginning of the sin to the daughter of Zion: for the transgressions of Israel were found in thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ccbacb15-21c6-49ac-bf40-f4c7ff945d4f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: MIC 1:14
Text: Therefore shalt thou give presents to Moreshethgath: the houses of Achzib shall be a lie to the kings of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b2c518c-6ba3-4ddb-af3f-7ff7131986e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: MIC 1:15
Text: Yet will I bring an heir unto thee, O inhabitant of Mareshah: he shall come unto Adullam the glory of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97d8cca7-f8a4-4372-994d-26171595c98e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: MIC 1:16
Text: Make thee bald, and poll thee for thy delicate children; enlarge thy baldness as the eagle; for they are gone into captivity from thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed756131-d3c3-417c-a1ef-150f4c3096ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: MIC 2:1
Text: Woe to them that devise iniquity, and work evil upon their beds! when the morning is light, they practise it, because it is in the power of their hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29373536-c870-41a5-b8d7-f81ec1535856>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: MIC 2:2
Text: And they covet fields, and take them by violence; and houses, and take them away: so they oppress a man and his house, even a man and his heritage.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfc103b7-9a36-44b0-b48b-c5ba19271061>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: MIC 2:3
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD; Behold, against this family do I devise an evil, from which ye shall not remove your necks; neither shall ye go haughtily: for this time is evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2525e42e-99a0-4590-83b1-86034bb975b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: MIC 2:4
Text: In that day shall one take up a parable against you, and lament with a doleful lamentation, and say, We be utterly spoiled: he hath changed the portion of my people: how hath he removed it from me! turning away he hath divided our fields.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57099127-e498-4160-9a00-596ae3b9fa97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: MIC 2:5
Text: Therefore thou shalt have none that shall cast a cord by lot in the congregation of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0447a40c-044e-4076-b2da-f9d47935dc57>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: MIC 2:6
Text: Prophesy ye not, say they to them that prophesy: they shall not prophesy to them, that they shall not take shame.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e318ea6-8643-4ef5-9d02-1b0b483a2bee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: MIC 2:7
Text: O thou that art named the house of Jacob, is the spirit of the LORD straitened? are these his doings? do not my words do good to him that walketh uprightly?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b89f7c22-b3fa-4336-acfb-30547d45bfea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: MIC 2:8
Text: Even of late my people is risen up as an enemy: ye pull off the robe with the garment from them that pass by securely as men averse from war.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50747548-ef5e-4304-a958-27e3a9e4a06f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MIC 2:9
Text: The women of my people have ye cast out from their pleasant houses; from their children have ye taken away my glory for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5919ef7-7a41-4e5c-83c1-22cd329fa82b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MIC 2:10
Text: Arise ye, and depart; for this is not your rest: because it is polluted, it shall destroy you, even with a sore destruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb8a2b48-c9ee-4b47-b0b0-7a96fdf655f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: MIC 2:11
Text: If a man walking in the spirit and falsehood do lie, saying, I will prophesy unto thee of wine and of strong drink; he shall even be the prophet of this people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7047f1d0-6ded-429f-803e-480250ece8ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: MIC 2:12
Text: I will surely assemble, O Jacob, all of thee; I will surely gather the remnant of Israel; I will put them together as the sheep of Bozrah, as the flock in the midst of their fold: they shall make great noise by reason of the multitude of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69a3c68e-0302-4aa5-9598-5df3d690259e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: MIC 2:13
Text: The breaker is come up before them: they have broken up, and have passed through the gate, and are gone out by it: and their king shall pass before them, and the LORD on the head of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42cfe94e-e4fb-4f49-b9fe-ab329564dcc2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: MIC 3:1
Text: And I said, Hear, I pray you, O heads of Jacob, and ye princes of the house of Israel; Is it not for you to know judgment?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de07f8b4-43cf-4179-a900-5e64fb01e27c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: MIC 3:2
Text: Who hate the good, and love the evil; who pluck off their skin from off them, and their flesh from off their bones;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae98fd81-8850-49e7-b845-36503ba6c564>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: MIC 3:3
Text: Who also eat the flesh of my people, and flay their skin from off them; and they break their bones, and chop them in pieces, as for the pot, and as flesh within the caldron.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d180afb2-1da9-4842-80f7-69dfa03fd542>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: MIC 3:4
Text: Then shall they cry unto the LORD, but he will not hear them: he will even hide his face from them at that time, as they have behaved themselves ill in their doings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72c43953-51f0-4331-8d30-eb0f654021c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: MIC 3:5
Text: Thus saith the LORD concerning the prophets that make my people err, that bite with their teeth, and cry, Peace; and he that putteth not into their mouths, they even prepare war against him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49c999c4-1694-4e27-83df-f514bf267def>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: MIC 3:6
Text: Therefore night shall be unto you, that ye shall not have a vision; and it shall be dark unto you, that ye shall not divine; and the sun shall go down over the prophets, and the day shall be dark over them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58ffc224-d0b7-4556-956d-7d452b9a9980>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: MIC 3:7
Text: Then shall the seers be ashamed, and the diviners confounded: yea, they shall all cover their lips; for there is no answer of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f672eab6-68eb-4f4c-88f8-36c5869aeeb1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: MIC 3:8
Text: But truly I am full of power by the spirit of the LORD, and of judgment, and of might, to declare unto Jacob his transgression, and to Israel his sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1db81205-c416-4679-bed0-b906b3428d1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: MIC 3:9
Text: Hear this, I pray you, ye heads of the house of Jacob, and princes of the house of Israel, that abhor judgment, and pervert all equity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad420df4-202c-4da3-b89c-1ade1475e4aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: MIC 3:10
Text: They build up Zion with blood, and Jerusalem with iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3680ebd1-f75f-423d-98bf-8a23806de8f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: MIC 3:11
Text: The heads thereof judge for reward, and the priests thereof teach for hire, and the prophets thereof divine for money: yet will they lean upon the LORD, and say, Is not the LORD among us? none evil can come upon us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57d8b030-5fd4-4777-92be-6c4160ccfb44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: MIC 3:12
Text: Therefore shall Zion for your sake be plowed as a field, and Jerusalem shall become heaps, and the mountain of the house as the high places of the forest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96a8df8a-49fd-4571-b64a-551f529e5fa8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: MIC 4:1
Text: But in the last days it shall come to pass, that the mountain of the house of the LORD shall be established in the top of the mountains, and it shall be exalted above the hills; and people shall flow unto it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:089eb70e-f487-4646-9597-23884555380e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 295

Reference: MIC 4:2
Text: And many nations shall come, and say, Come, and let us go up to the mountain of the LORD, and to the house of the God of Jacob; and he will teach us of his ways, and we will walk in his paths: for the law shall go forth of Zion, and the word of the LORD from Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40e349b3-d132-4e1d-a0b8-f9764cbd40a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 273

Reference: MIC 4:3
Text: And he shall judge among many people, and rebuke strong nations afar off; and they shall beat their swords into plowshares, and their spears into pruninghooks: nation shall not lift up a sword against nation, neither shall they learn war any more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7bd13b77-b948-4559-97e8-69d8edf5a261>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: MIC 4:4
Text: But they shall sit every man under his vine and under his fig tree; and none shall make them afraid: for the mouth of the LORD of hosts hath spoken it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b0ccdc5-6441-4b1a-9b35-a2ee9f0df499>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: MIC 4:5
Text: For all people will walk every one in the name of his god, and we will walk in the name of the LORD our God for ever and ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e368055-646b-4c60-845a-ee225a766919>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: MIC 4:6
Text: In that day, saith the LORD, will I assemble her that halteth, and I will gather her that is driven out, and her that I have afflicted;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13831386-63c7-4a88-898e-5c81b3e895b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: MIC 4:7
Text: And I will make her that halted a remnant, and her that was cast far off a strong nation: and the LORD shall reign over them in mount Zion from henceforth, even for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:176c0819-0434-4bea-ba97-18f4dc47f4f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: MIC 4:8
Text: And thou, O tower of the flock, the strong hold of the daughter of Zion, unto thee shall it come, even the first dominion; the kingdom shall come to the daughter of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46ceb446-2130-4e82-8d8c-70cd52bfc0d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: MIC 4:9
Text: Now why dost thou cry out aloud? is there no king in thee? is thy counsellor perished? for pangs have taken thee as a woman in travail.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89c2995a-2850-49ca-83a7-350f517d591b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 321

Reference: MIC 4:10
Text: Be in pain, and labour to bring forth, O daughter of Zion, like a woman in travail: for now shalt thou go forth out of the city, and thou shalt dwell in the field, and thou shalt go even to Babylon; there shalt thou be delivered; there the LORD shall redeem thee from the hand of thine enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d549dca8-5068-4d03-8ccf-d7edfcbde3ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: MIC 4:11
Text: Now also many nations are gathered against thee, that say, Let her be defiled, and let our eye look upon Zion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8dba0b0-974c-4b10-aad9-581ff53d281d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: MIC 4:12
Text: But they know not the thoughts of the LORD, neither understand they his counsel: for he shall gather them as the sheaves into the floor.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f501bc07-93b2-4875-8a61-ac5d77d7f233>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: MIC 4:13
Text: Arise and thresh, O daughter of Zion: for I will make thine horn iron, and I will make thy hoofs brass: and thou shalt beat in pieces many people: and I will consecrate their gain unto the LORD, and their substance unto the Lord of the whole earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc6fc825-255e-4dc8-a6b7-be2b8c26fe3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: MIC 5:1
Text: Now gather thyself in troops, O daughter of troops: he hath laid siege against us: they shall smite the judge of Israel with a rod upon the cheek.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64d75ab8-8b60-476c-a850-2b9884badaea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: MIC 5:2
Text: But thou, Bethlehem Ephratah, though thou be little among the thousands of Judah, yet out of thee shall he come forth unto me that is to be ruler in Israel; whose goings forth have been from of old, from everlasting.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed28691b-6bfd-482c-b2f4-0fb26db92d35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: MIC 5:3
Text: Therefore will he give them up, until the time that she which travaileth hath brought forth: then the remnant of his brethren shall return unto the children of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edb49c77-83c2-4e6e-bb25-54bee5d084ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: MIC 5:4
Text: And he shall stand and feed in the strength of the LORD, in the majesty of the name of the LORD his God; and they shall abide: for now shall he be great unto the ends of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1014e5d3-2706-4a58-8831-a50bf30def61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: MIC 5:5
Text: And this man shall be the peace, when the Assyrian shall come into our land: and when he shall tread in our palaces, then shall we raise against him seven shepherds, and eight principal men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b2916b7-6587-4501-ac1d-6c9f1b3d9fc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: MIC 5:6
Text: And they shall waste the land of Assyria with the sword, and the land of Nimrod in the entrances thereof: thus shall he deliver us from the Assyrian, when he cometh into our land, and when he treadeth within our borders.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fcfcbc5-aeaf-4f1c-801d-7363e2f29e1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: MIC 5:7
Text: And the remnant of Jacob shall be in the midst of many people as a dew from the LORD, as the showers upon the grass, that tarrieth not for man, nor waiteth for the sons of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f780c31-d314-4bc6-a02d-ea6b2c9c9f2b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 279

Reference: MIC 5:8
Text: And the remnant of Jacob shall be among the Gentiles in the midst of many people as a lion among the beasts of the forest, as a young lion among the flocks of sheep: who, if he go through, both treadeth down, and teareth in pieces, and none can deliver.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b20bdacd-9756-4dcd-9103-cb9ec13f1565>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: MIC 5:9
Text: Thine hand shall be lifted up upon thine adversaries, and all thine enemies shall be cut off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e411b50e-0e64-41b7-ba71-63dd04f79809>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: MIC 5:10
Text: And it shall come to pass in that day, saith the LORD, that I will cut off thy horses out of the midst of thee, and I will destroy thy chariots:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbddef3c-dbc8-44aa-b876-b1c0f51b127c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: MIC 5:11
Text: And I will cut off the cities of thy land, and throw down all thy strong holds:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c130445a-033b-4c4e-afc3-200b7277d985>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MIC 5:12
Text: And I will cut off witchcrafts out of thine hand; and thou shalt have no more soothsayers:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bae85a5c-1cff-4462-9952-1c948cf464e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: MIC 5:13
Text: Thy graven images also will I cut off, and thy standing images out of the midst of thee; and thou shalt no more worship the work of thine hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:775e5d12-0378-41da-8e75-f72bf8e4a04f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: MIC 5:14
Text: And I will pluck up thy groves out of the midst of thee: so will I destroy thy cities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a97abf5c-3564-441d-b0b0-7c28ffcf6234>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: MIC 5:15
Text: And I will execute vengeance in anger and fury upon the heathen, such as they have not heard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d4bb7d9-e0b7-4e42-98fd-96996eb44d94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: MIC 6:1
Text: Hear ye now what the LORD saith; Arise, contend thou before the mountains, and let the hills hear thy voice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:503c7f4b-a7b4-4d93-a609-515118282649>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: MIC 6:2
Text: Hear ye, O mountains, the LORD’s controversy, and ye strong foundations of the earth: for the LORD hath a controversy with his people, and he will plead with Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27c595a7-0261-45c6-9b6a-1ea1577976e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: MIC 6:3
Text: O my people, what have I done unto thee? and wherein have I wearied thee? testify against me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78f8e8c1-91bc-49f2-98de-f0a176c7ab23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: MIC 6:4
Text: For I brought thee up out of the land of Egypt, and redeemed thee out of the house of servants; and I sent before thee Moses, Aaron, and Miriam.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a232919-969b-4a15-a00f-80c8e5504cc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: MIC 6:5
Text: O my people, remember now what Balak king of Moab consulted, and what Balaam the son of Beor answered him from Shittim unto Gilgal; that ye may know the righteousness of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1176021a-0fb0-406a-892e-143f2f4ab9a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: MIC 6:6
Text: Wherewith shall I come before the LORD, and bow myself before the high God? shall I come before him with burnt offerings, with calves of a year old?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e4b32ea-9d27-41aa-86f6-a450f508eda2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: MIC 6:7
Text: Will the LORD be pleased with thousands of rams, or with ten thousands of rivers of oil? shall I give my firstborn for my transgression, the fruit of my body for the sin of my soul?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ca1c678-9a58-4c0c-a2c9-80455dd4d0fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: MIC 6:8
Text: He hath shewed thee, O man, what is good; and what doth the LORD require of thee, but to do justly, and to love mercy, and to walk humbly with thy God?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e448837-029b-49f3-8638-d5530d02404e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: MIC 6:9
Text: The LORD’s voice crieth unto the city, and the man of wisdom shall see thy name: hear ye the rod, and who hath appointed it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:605064bd-9526-4f7a-9b87-8453ed1e1a41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MIC 6:10
Text: Are there yet the treasures of wickedness in the house of the wicked, and the scant measure that is abominable?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e96bb2ed-f4c4-4831-bcd6-92625c61c9d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: MIC 6:11
Text: Shall I count them pure with the wicked balances, and with the bag of deceitful weights?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d76912c0-ccab-44b6-9f08-e04f1f77ec7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: MIC 6:12
Text: For the rich men thereof are full of violence, and the inhabitants thereof have spoken lies, and their tongue is deceitful in their mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6dcbf52-5996-4424-8db4-e5db7bbafc20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: MIC 6:13
Text: Therefore also will I make thee sick in smiting thee, in making thee desolate because of thy sins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/6/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e9d96ce-65ab-4923-9847-826e9466504f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: MIC 6:14
Text: Thou shalt eat, but not be satisfied; and thy casting down shall be in the midst of thee; and thou shalt take hold, but shalt not deliver; and that which thou deliverest will I give up to the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/6/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f5c84a9-5469-4c35-adab-467beecb6302>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: MIC 6:15
Text: Thou shalt sow, but thou shalt not reap; thou shalt tread the olives, but thou shalt not anoint thee with oil; and sweet wine, but shalt not drink wine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/6/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:efeb9625-874b-4080-a814-ec1b9ac07b12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 261

Reference: MIC 6:16
Text: For the statutes of Omri are kept, and all the works of the house of Ahab, and ye walk in their counsels; that I should make thee a desolation, and the inhabitants thereof an hissing: therefore ye shall bear the reproach of my people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:896f21bb-023d-4976-88dc-f7dfe7dfb6fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: MIC 7:1
Text: Woe is me! for I am as when they have gathered the summer fruits, as the grapegleanings of the vintage: there is no cluster to eat: my soul desired the firstripe fruit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2009fdf-dd2c-4053-8c0f-e9e324d1cc03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: MIC 7:2
Text: The good man is perished out of the earth: and there is none upright among men: they all lie in wait for blood; they hunt every man his brother with a net.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2ff2c91-625e-4459-8cc2-27b0918480ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: MIC 7:3
Text: That they may do evil with both hands earnestly, the prince asketh, and the judge asketh for a reward; and the great man, he uttereth his mischievous desire: so they wrap it up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:772ded55-fe94-4d2b-bcca-66e1c3b78e60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: MIC 7:4
Text: The best of them is as a brier: the most upright is sharper than a thorn hedge: the day of thy watchmen and thy visitation cometh; now shall be their perplexity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07e0079e-546a-4798-a36c-5e45931d606f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: MIC 7:5
Text: Trust ye not in a friend, put ye not confidence in a guide: keep the doors of thy mouth from her that lieth in thy bosom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:489d2bec-e363-4585-a045-f8523d435884>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: MIC 7:6
Text: For the son dishonoureth the father, the daughter riseth up against her mother, the daughter in law against her mother in law; a man’s enemies are the men of his own house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7cf02ef-5f95-44ee-bce5-3059498d6d17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: MIC 7:7
Text: Therefore I will look unto the LORD; I will wait for the God of my salvation: my God will hear me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc7a0df9-d422-4e2c-9971-9adda95d6002>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: MIC 7:8
Text: Rejoice not against me, O mine enemy: when I fall, I shall arise; when I sit in darkness, the LORD shall be a light unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e9d534b-9e76-454d-a6d3-097efd50ef20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: MIC 7:9
Text: I will bear the indignation of the LORD, because I have sinned against him, until he plead my cause, and execute judgment for me: he will bring me forth to the light, and I shall behold his righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02db8d97-d8c7-4366-9e27-4d1e9dd1d0c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: MIC 7:10
Text: Then she that is mine enemy shall see it, and shame shall cover her which said unto me, Where is the LORD thy God? mine eyes shall behold her: now shall she be trodden down as the mire of the streets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ea495be-2e7d-4805-9e7e-8f7620d55397>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MIC 7:11
Text: In the day that thy walls are to be built, in that day shall the decree be far removed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de838a74-e578-409b-a685-54432d8795b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: MIC 7:12
Text: In that day also he shall come even to thee from Assyria, and from the fortified cities, and from the fortress even to the river, and from sea to sea, and from mountain to mountain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00246917-3346-4620-a66f-814d921d9654>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: MIC 7:13
Text: Notwithstanding the land shall be desolate because of them that dwell therein, for the fruit of their doings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/7/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4efedf2f-ffc5-4e80-95bb-e2fc3e595c12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: MIC 7:14
Text: Feed thy people with thy rod, the flock of thine heritage, which dwell solitarily in the wood, in the midst of Carmel: let them feed in Bashan and Gilead, as in the days of old.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/7/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:391bb0c0-dcfe-4076-bbec-57746c532009>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: MIC 7:15
Text: According to the days of thy coming out of the land of Egypt will I shew unto him marvellous things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/7/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43034680-651f-4ac5-a3f8-f859dce84140>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: MIC 7:16
Text: The nations shall see and be confounded at all their might: they shall lay their hand upon their mouth, their ears shall be deaf.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/7/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8393fef-f740-42b5-81d1-daad91201f0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: MIC 7:17
Text: They shall lick the dust like a serpent, they shall move out of their holes like worms of the earth: they shall be afraid of the LORD our God, and shall fear because of thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/7/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d64057f8-c20b-422a-a5ff-97d8d1665916>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: MIC 7:18
Text: Who is a God like unto thee, that pardoneth iniquity, and passeth by the transgression of the remnant of his heritage? he retaineth not his anger for ever, because he delighteth in mercy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/7/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:478e595d-555e-4e29-b66f-a8ef85385625>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: MIC 7:19
Text: He will turn again, he will have compassion upon us; he will subdue our iniquities; and thou wilt cast all their sins into the depths of the sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MIC/7/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9a6e449-d100-42c9-8ce5-a07525a8ade1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MIC 7:20
Text: Thou wilt perform the truth to Jacob, and the mercy to Abraham, which thou hast sworn unto our fathers from the days of old.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13d24362-49b7-4549-9d08-51ec60debacc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: NAH 1:1
Text: The burden of Nineveh. The book of the vision of Nahum the Elkoshite.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d55bbbcc-8ae6-4a5c-b0c3-9702b661c247>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: NAH 1:2
Text: God is jealous, and the LORD revengeth; the LORD revengeth, and is furious; the LORD will take vengeance on his adversaries, and he reserveth wrath for his enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2dc6ac1-493f-4538-9353-4a4061b8cc63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: NAH 1:3
Text: The LORD is slow to anger, and great in power, and will not at all acquit the wicked: the LORD hath his way in the whirlwind and in the storm, and the clouds are the dust of his feet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b15961e-71ed-4d44-b5e7-b42679e643d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: NAH 1:4
Text: He rebuketh the sea, and maketh it dry, and drieth up all the rivers: Bashan languisheth, and Carmel, and the flower of Lebanon languisheth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9643fd07-60fc-4057-b816-707f08a63842>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: NAH 1:5
Text: The mountains quake at him, and the hills melt, and the earth is burned at his presence, yea, the world, and all that dwell therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fb29eb0-bec2-4079-9aa8-33f4cbdb79b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: NAH 1:6
Text: Who can stand before his indignation? and who can abide in the fierceness of his anger? his fury is poured out like fire, and the rocks are thrown down by him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1acece05-8793-4a37-8e18-60e384207770>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: NAH 1:7
Text: The LORD is good, a strong hold in the day of trouble; and he knoweth them that trust in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4749ef47-3001-40cb-b89c-706d5792d88b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: NAH 1:8
Text: But with an overrunning flood he will make an utter end of the place thereof, and darkness shall pursue his enemies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbe0f12f-b375-4156-90f3-017241d42219>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: NAH 1:9
Text: What do ye imagine against the LORD? he will make an utter end: affliction shall not rise up the second time.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5783c10-74a5-49ac-9f12-808c184e4ed6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: NAH 1:10
Text: For while they be folden together as thorns, and while they are drunken as drunkards, they shall be devoured as stubble fully dry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04fe0546-7413-48d3-bcb6-96a6e351f09d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: NAH 1:11
Text: There is one come out of thee, that imagineth evil against the LORD, a wicked counsellor.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2ad2c06-a527-43dd-a5e6-f61b81e4d2db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: NAH 1:12
Text: Thus saith the LORD; Though they be quiet, and likewise many, yet thus shall they be cut down, when he shall pass through. Though I have afflicted thee, I will afflict thee no more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1aeeb545-340d-411b-b1da-331a9c8dd52d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: NAH 1:13
Text: For now will I break his yoke from off thee, and will burst thy bonds in sunder.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13bfc272-5e7c-4965-bea9-349819ee8cd5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: NAH 1:14
Text: And the LORD hath given a commandment concerning thee, that no more of thy name be sown: out of the house of thy gods will I cut off the graven image and the molten image: I will make thy grave; for thou art vile.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ae8b941-2c2c-438c-b6e5-ec8cf0bd4ae0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: NAH 1:15
Text: Behold upon the mountains the feet of him that bringeth good tidings, that publisheth peace! O Judah, keep thy solemn feasts, perform thy vows: for the wicked shall no more pass through thee; he is utterly cut off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4d0b1d8-d5b3-4811-ba28-76faf057c1c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: NAH 2:1
Text: He that dasheth in pieces is come up before thy face: keep the munition, watch the way, make thy loins strong, fortify thy power mightily.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1f0656c-5dc4-4c98-895e-5b22dc515880>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: NAH 2:2
Text: For the LORD hath turned away the excellency of Jacob, as the excellency of Israel: for the emptiers have emptied them out, and marred their vine branches.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:650831e9-32d8-4859-b100-32edf5a38747>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: NAH 2:3
Text: The shield of his mighty men is made red, the valiant men are in scarlet: the chariots shall be with flaming torches in the day of his preparation, and the fir trees shall be terribly shaken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ece79be-a554-4231-87d5-0fed4eea07c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: NAH 2:4
Text: The chariots shall rage in the streets, they shall justle one against another in the broad ways: they shall seem like torches, they shall run like the lightnings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5651cd19-cf62-4bc0-9e3f-14726e235deb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: NAH 2:5
Text: He shall recount his worthies: they shall stumble in their walk; they shall make haste to the wall thereof, and the defence shall be prepared.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ea158bf-6d22-4cbc-b01a-57233793fe6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: NAH 2:6
Text: The gates of the rivers shall be opened, and the palace shall be dissolved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:168d3ee9-c71d-42f8-ab56-05a870446aea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: NAH 2:7
Text: And Huzzab shall be led away captive, she shall be brought up, and her maids shall lead her as with the voice of doves, tabering upon their breasts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7bd5ca5-d71c-4db0-8eb1-11197eae0a78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: NAH 2:8
Text: But Nineveh is of old like a pool of water: yet they shall flee away. Stand, stand, shall they cry; but none shall look back.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:618f62e0-3aa0-4d5a-a4c5-51c128abdd15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: NAH 2:9
Text: Take ye the spoil of silver, take the spoil of gold: for there is none end of the store and glory out of all the pleasant furniture.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de7744ab-df37-4699-bd93-33f87c1e1db4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: NAH 2:10
Text: She is empty, and void, and waste: and the heart melteth, and the knees smite together, and much pain is in all loins, and the faces of them all gather blackness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:639361ed-3d65-4574-8b63-e8eb422977e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: NAH 2:11
Text: Where is the dwelling of the lions, and the feedingplace of the young lions, where the lion, even the old lion, walked, and the lion’s whelp, and none made them afraid?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00d13702-bc0a-4975-abeb-b9daf490b97e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: NAH 2:12
Text: The lion did tear in pieces enough for his whelps, and strangled for his lionesses, and filled his holes with prey, and his dens with ravin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ff187b2-3e5b-4dab-88d6-68be0cb6da38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 265

Reference: NAH 2:13
Text: Behold, I am against thee, saith the LORD of hosts, and I will burn her chariots in the smoke, and the sword shall devour thy young lions: and I will cut off thy prey from the earth, and the voice of thy messengers shall no more be heard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93af638a-7abb-478e-ad7b-b699f9fafbaf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: NAH 3:1
Text: Woe to the bloody city! it is all full of lies and robbery; the prey departeth not;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e4cfb00-eddf-41f0-89c7-3626178172b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: NAH 3:2
Text: The noise of a whip, and the noise of the rattling of the wheels, and of the pransing horses, and of the jumping chariots.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99ac67c4-d263-4adb-ba57-a6c442f23974>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: NAH 3:3
Text: The horseman lifteth up both the bright sword and the glittering spear: and there is a multitude of slain, and a great number of carcases; and there is none end of their corpses; they stumble upon their corpses:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7eb41d9f-0790-49a2-b123-d59369fab8ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: NAH 3:4
Text: Because of the multitude of the whoredoms of the wellfavoured harlot, the mistress of witchcrafts, that selleth nations through her whoredoms, and families through her witchcrafts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b628cd3c-b28c-4add-9f29-6742660312e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: NAH 3:5
Text: Behold, I am against thee, saith the LORD of hosts; and I will discover thy skirts upon thy face, and I will shew the nations thy nakedness, and the kingdoms thy shame.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d0656d8-cfec-416f-a351-d1bfea454598>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: NAH 3:6
Text: And I will cast abominable filth upon thee, and make thee vile, and will set thee as a gazingstock.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:551e9355-10fd-436a-ab01-4da5412fedbe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: NAH 3:7
Text: And it shall come to pass, that all they that look upon thee shall flee from thee, and say, Nineveh is laid waste: who will bemoan her? whence shall I seek comforters for thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be35bfc0-3164-4062-a62c-d12e44976e38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: NAH 3:8
Text: Art thou better than populous No, that was situate among the rivers, that had the waters round about it, whose rampart was the sea, and her wall was from the sea?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8319bf84-fe60-4a39-a2f9-0dab06aa09b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: NAH 3:9
Text: Ethiopia and Egypt were her strength, and it was infinite; Put and Lubim were thy helpers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00597a0d-9aa4-4191-a099-73bf28e2dcd5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: NAH 3:10
Text: Yet was she carried away, she went into captivity: her young children also were dashed in pieces at the top of all the streets: and they cast lots for her honourable men, and all her great men were bound in chains.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68b294fd-2d89-4089-9850-10ba83201bd8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: NAH 3:11
Text: Thou also shalt be drunken: thou shalt be hid, thou also shalt seek strength because of the enemy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1cf39f3-569a-407a-a3b1-0a211c0243de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: NAH 3:12
Text: All thy strong holds shall be like fig trees with the firstripe figs: if they be shaken, they shall even fall into the mouth of the eater.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00c0eef8-1eaf-48f0-a70c-bc31e638282f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: NAH 3:13
Text: Behold, thy people in the midst of thee are women: the gates of thy land shall be set wide open unto thine enemies: the fire shall devour thy bars.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41779c00-45d1-4c69-b124-483b1447f38c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: NAH 3:14
Text: Draw thee waters for the siege, fortify thy strong holds: go into clay, and tread the morter, make strong the brickkiln.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b3a2312-7cf4-4a6b-beca-41002bd47784>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: NAH 3:15
Text: There shall the fire devour thee; the sword shall cut thee off, it shall eat thee up like the cankerworm: make thyself many as the cankerworm, make thyself many as the locusts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b81d4e9-5c0e-4b5d-b195-ce138c619c15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: NAH 3:16
Text: Thou hast multiplied thy merchants above the stars of heaven: the cankerworm spoileth, and fleeth away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83ce0f2b-1660-4702-92d9-c45a74bb5d38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: NAH 3:17
Text: Thy crowned are as the locusts, and thy captains as the great grasshoppers, which camp in the hedges in the cold day, but when the sun ariseth they flee away, and their place is not known where they are.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e97ff38-85da-4e2d-abf0-34ea4e6de581>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: NAH 3:18
Text: Thy shepherds slumber, O king of Assyria: thy nobles shall dwell in the dust: thy people is scattered upon the mountains, and no man gathereth them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/NAH/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebea08dc-0007-400d-97a8-c95672e78cd2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: NAH 3:19
Text: There is no healing of thy bruise; thy wound is grievous: all that hear the bruit of thee shall clap the hands over thee: for upon whom hath not thy wickedness passed continually?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c60c823c-5920-432c-90a4-d4b3af5a98a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 72

Reference: HAB 1:1
Text: The burden which Habakkuk the prophet did see.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1d76e2c-7068-4746-b6df-2068414658c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: HAB 1:2
Text: O LORD, how long shall I cry, and thou wilt not hear! even cry out unto thee of violence, and thou wilt not save!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32f736a1-6056-46c8-a0e5-f1eead29e4a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: HAB 1:3
Text: Why dost thou shew me iniquity, and cause me to behold grievance? for spoiling and violence are before me: and there are that raise up strife and contention.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21257d2b-18c0-4cf7-b2c5-eda1a369c5cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: HAB 1:4
Text: Therefore the law is slacked, and judgment doth never go forth: for the wicked doth compass about the righteous; therefore wrong judgment proceedeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0526751-8c53-4fde-bd8f-f03001eb6f31>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: HAB 1:5
Text: Behold ye among the heathen, and regard, and wonder marvelously: for I will work a work in your days which ye will not believe, though it be told you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b2fb86d-b0c4-4c74-9437-b657ee4e7593>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: HAB 1:6
Text: For, lo, I raise up the Chaldeans, that bitter and hasty nation, which shall march through the breadth of the land, to possess the dwellingplaces that are not theirs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55ffc6be-fd8b-40eb-8722-b968f4f6f1ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: HAB 1:7
Text: They are terrible and dreadful: their judgment and their dignity shall proceed of themselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d735e19-ebc2-4eda-b279-2771587ea194>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: HAB 1:8
Text: Their horses also are swifter than the leopards, and are more fierce than the evening wolves: and their horsemen shall spread themselves, and their horsemen shall come from far; they shall fly as the eagle that hasteth to eat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d887d51-4f3a-44fd-8542-be7e0468e8e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: HAB 1:9
Text: They shall come all for violence: their faces shall sup up as the east wind, and they shall gather the captivity as the sand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ef160c0-f49b-42c6-ac07-6d757cfb4070>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: HAB 1:10
Text: And they shall scoff at the kings, and the princes shall be a scorn unto them: they shall deride every strong hold; for they shall heap dust, and take it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71dd5e53-92d9-4d36-83e0-ffbbd9df6e27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: HAB 1:11
Text: Then shall his mind change, and he shall pass over, and offend, imputing this his power unto his god.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:097fca77-f1c9-4cb1-9de8-48d13e168b86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: HAB 1:12
Text: Art thou not from everlasting, O LORD my God, mine Holy One? we shall not die. O LORD, thou hast ordained them for judgment; and, O mighty God, thou hast established them for correction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb813f43-80eb-43ad-be64-ea7f9dd1f922>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: HAB 1:13
Text: Thou art of purer eyes than to behold evil, and canst not look on iniquity: wherefore lookest thou upon them that deal treacherously, and holdest thy tongue when the wicked devoureth the man that is more righteous than he?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c6c57de-9c12-4d54-8db9-c55b49edc277>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: HAB 1:14
Text: And makest men as the fishes of the sea, as the creeping things, that have no ruler over them?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:741f0fbf-21c7-411c-a6b2-e7da0df79117>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: HAB 1:15
Text: They take up all of them with the angle, they catch them in their net, and gather them in their drag: therefore they rejoice and are glad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12475d60-cae7-4b2c-beb0-2473693e73a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: HAB 1:16
Text: Therefore they sacrifice unto their net, and burn incense unto their drag; because by them their portion is fat, and their meat plenteous.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:187e7a2a-4ded-4d99-97a7-544c344f7af8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: HAB 1:17
Text: Shall they therefore empty their net, and not spare continually to slay the nations?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e2fc22e-96a9-4bae-8cf7-c35b37a80cdc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: HAB 2:1
Text: I will stand upon my watch, and set me upon the tower, and will watch to see what he will say unto me, and what I shall answer when I am reproved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72f39743-9eaa-4e8c-87c2-8870512ccf2b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: HAB 2:2
Text: And the LORD answered me, and said, Write the vision, and make it plain upon tables, that he may run that readeth it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00de0d4c-0b5b-46a2-8c16-b4a98124ffb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: HAB 2:3
Text: For the vision is yet for an appointed time, but at the end it shall speak, and not lie: though it tarry, wait for it; because it will surely come, it will not tarry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6abf4568-d8ef-452e-b668-3d80af3bde19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: HAB 2:4
Text: Behold, his soul which is lifted up is not upright in him: but the just shall live by his faith.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:422905b1-02c6-43ac-8842-a6f9ee124034>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: HAB 2:5
Text: Yea also, because he transgresseth by wine, he is a proud man, neither keepeth at home, who enlargeth his desire as hell, and is as death, and cannot be satisfied, but gathereth unto him all nations, and heapeth unto him all people:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:497a75ea-866f-4dd4-95ab-73026d8dc928>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: HAB 2:6
Text: Shall not all these take up a parable against him, and a taunting proverb against him, and say, Woe to him that increaseth that which is not his! how long? and to him that ladeth himself with thick clay!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa70de0d-2930-413a-a22a-7b623181fa46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: HAB 2:7
Text: Shall they not rise up suddenly that shall bite thee, and awake that shall vex thee, and thou shalt be for booties unto them?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b944d890-54a3-4ce6-af52-b1554027be80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: HAB 2:8
Text: Because thou hast spoiled many nations, all the remnant of the people shall spoil thee; because of men’s blood, and for the violence of the land, of the city, and of all that dwell therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1846a2e-e64d-44a1-adac-4955cf489a6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: HAB 2:9
Text: Woe to him that coveteth an evil covetousness to his house, that he may set his nest on high, that he may be delivered from the power of evil!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd2c8021-8ea2-4edb-b618-648a211021e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: HAB 2:10
Text: Thou hast consulted shame to thy house by cutting off many people, and hast sinned against thy soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d49ff1d9-0362-480c-ae7d-6619b11c8961>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: HAB 2:11
Text: For the stone shall cry out of the wall, and the beam out of the timber shall answer it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:856f21ec-9ba9-469c-9eb0-7b55cb9bfd5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: HAB 2:12
Text: Woe to him that buildeth a town with blood, and stablisheth a city by iniquity!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5018d613-f285-46f9-b0ff-4fb0d438c3d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: HAB 2:13
Text: Behold, is it not of the LORD of hosts that the people shall labour in the very fire, and the people shall weary themselves for very vanity?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:adb1eda5-b5e2-4a28-a87d-b95614d7213a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: HAB 2:14
Text: For the earth shall be filled with the knowledge of the glory of the LORD, as the waters cover the sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b705ce3d-2562-4ae5-b1a4-1a8e31bb6067>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: HAB 2:15
Text: Woe unto him that giveth his neighbour drink, that puttest thy bottle to him, and makest him drunken also, that thou mayest look on their nakedness!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2091dcdf-056e-4433-934b-5145ec0093aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: HAB 2:16
Text: Thou art filled with shame for glory: drink thou also, and let thy foreskin be uncovered: the cup of the LORD’s right hand shall be turned unto thee, and shameful spewing shall be on thy glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a956df09-9a24-40e5-bbb1-d6583624ab26>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: HAB 2:17
Text: For the violence of Lebanon shall cover thee, and the spoil of beasts, which made them afraid, because of men’s blood, and for the violence of the land, of the city, and of all that dwell therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4f3e8ff-56c1-4a06-8273-7ecccce691ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: HAB 2:18
Text: What profiteth the graven image that the maker thereof hath graven it; the molten image, and a teacher of lies, that the maker of his work trusteth therein, to make dumb idols?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90272926-0add-41bf-9a5c-66e8795b9788>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: HAB 2:19
Text: Woe unto him that saith to the wood, Awake; to the dumb stone, Arise, it shall teach! Behold, it is laid over with gold and silver, and there is no breath at all in the midst of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c68c3b1-6cf5-4722-aeb8-89dae650eb56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: HAB 2:20
Text: But the LORD is in his holy temple: let all the earth keep silence before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0688f08c-681d-4823-b4be-1c3bf0400975>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: HAB 3:1
Text: A prayer of Habakkuk the prophet upon Shigionoth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7157d3ee-c758-4c3c-b0e4-a46577939b44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: HAB 3:2
Text: O LORD, I have heard thy speech, and was afraid: O LORD, revive thy work in the midst of the years, in the midst of the years make known; in wrath remember mercy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7b6d13a-af30-4fed-ad05-534f4c654e53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: HAB 3:3
Text: God came from Teman, and the Holy One from mount Paran. Selah. His glory covered the heavens, and the earth was full of his praise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1fa5062-9dbe-485e-81e3-7a2542a50d5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: HAB 3:4
Text: And his brightness was as the light; he had horns coming out of his hand: and there was the hiding of his power.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8db8cbbb-fba5-4783-9ceb-8eef6f45c2aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: HAB 3:5
Text: Before him went the pestilence, and burning coals went forth at his feet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:645a81d7-5e2c-4844-b102-e373afe6a3ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: HAB 3:6
Text: He stood, and measured the earth: he beheld, and drove asunder the nations; and the everlasting mountains were scattered, the perpetual hills did bow: his ways are everlasting.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4cfa9b2-0233-4778-9ea5-e7d8086132e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: HAB 3:7
Text: I saw the tents of Cushan in affliction: and the curtains of the land of Midian did tremble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e6870f2-3566-4976-8223-e8a15a5c4df6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: HAB 3:8
Text: Was the LORD displeased against the rivers? was thine anger against the rivers? was thy wrath against the sea, that thou didst ride upon thine horses and thy chariots of salvation?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fbb1490-1cc3-4bf9-b341-9963a6d17ad7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: HAB 3:9
Text: Thy bow was made quite naked, according to the oaths of the tribes, even thy word. Selah. Thou didst cleave the earth with rivers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1bbac1f7-4b2c-4974-9fb4-b0c751107c7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: HAB 3:10
Text: The mountains saw thee, and they trembled: the overflowing of the water passed by: the deep uttered his voice, and lifted up his hands on high.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb130318-565b-41f2-8400-7e9ed20dd801>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: HAB 3:11
Text: The sun and moon stood still in their habitation: at the light of thine arrows they went, and at the shining of thy glittering spear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:685a411e-d243-4a86-aa74-af9841b32d8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: HAB 3:12
Text: Thou didst march through the land in indignation, thou didst thresh the heathen in anger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3ffe072-e977-4af1-a5c7-470c43d6986c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: HAB 3:13
Text: Thou wentest forth for the salvation of thy people, even for salvation with thine anointed; thou woundedst the head out of the house of the wicked, by discovering the foundation unto the neck. Selah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3624c37-d2da-4029-89eb-effd90655f20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: HAB 3:14
Text: Thou didst strike through with his staves the head of his villages: they came out as a whirlwind to scatter me: their rejoicing was as to devour the poor secretly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:581c45fa-9629-466e-ae58-73c0cec0f2c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: HAB 3:15
Text: Thou didst walk through the sea with thine horses, through the heap of great waters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c96a13a-44c5-4099-883e-4ce5ff5f2ee2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 263

Reference: HAB 3:16
Text: When I heard, my belly trembled; my lips quivered at the voice: rottenness entered into my bones, and I trembled in myself, that I might rest in the day of trouble: when he cometh up unto the people, he will invade them with his troops.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a06cf3c9-f68d-41b0-8a60-34f2da69fda9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: HAB 3:17
Text: Although the fig tree shall not blossom, neither shall fruit be in the vines; the labour of the olive shall fail, and the fields shall yield no meat; the flock shall be cut off from the fold, and there shall be no herd in the stalls:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5e2ae41-d61a-4487-aa40-cf83250181ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: HAB 3:18
Text: Yet I will rejoice in the LORD, I will joy in the God of my salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAB/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f6e0c73-86f2-4ba4-aca0-1d86a625c8db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: HAB 3:19
Text: The LORD God is my strength, and he will make my feet like hinds’ feet, and he will make me to walk upon mine high places. To the chief singer on my stringed instruments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59f30fb0-d5ed-4f8d-8f32-8d3ccfbc0a24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: ZEP 1:1
Text: The word of the LORD which came unto Zephaniah the son of Cushi, the son of Gedaliah, the son of Amariah, the son of Hizkiah, in the days of Josiah the son of Amon, king of Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acefb8ae-6d45-48b3-a714-6141dab361fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: ZEP 1:2
Text: I will utterly consume all things from off the land, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bdec8117-28fd-4308-9ea5-e6718eb374d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: ZEP 1:3
Text: I will consume man and beast; I will consume the fowls of the heaven, and the fishes of the sea, and the stumblingblocks with the wicked: and I will cut off man from off the land, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:232f592c-4d21-4b08-8af0-8829c68e3277>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: ZEP 1:4
Text: I will also stretch out mine hand upon Judah, and upon all the inhabitants of Jerusalem; and I will cut off the remnant of Baal from this place, and the name of the Chemarims with the priests;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4096afa-4543-410f-ae79-8eec94c85554>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: ZEP 1:5
Text: And them that worship the host of heaven upon the housetops; and them that worship and that swear by the LORD, and that swear by Malcham;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6cef74cc-12d1-4f18-8006-38efa64ed4a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: ZEP 1:6
Text: And them that are turned back from the LORD; and those that have not sought the LORD, nor enquired for him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ce13c1a-b57b-437f-b9c0-433f6804e4ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: ZEP 1:7
Text: Hold thy peace at the presence of the Lord GOD: for the day of the LORD is at hand: for the LORD hath prepared a sacrifice, he hath bid his guests.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8571541e-6a83-4686-9ef0-ecf0d7f87538>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: ZEP 1:8
Text: And it shall come to pass in the day of the LORD’s sacrifice, that I will punish the princes, and the king’s children, and all such as are clothed with strange apparel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b5d195f-d318-4831-b28c-a2b80e5a72b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: ZEP 1:9
Text: In the same day also will I punish all those that leap on the threshold, which fill their masters’ houses with violence and deceit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2dcd954-6dd7-4ee5-ba19-64a8bb53310e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: ZEP 1:10
Text: And it shall come to pass in that day, saith the LORD, that there shall be the noise of a cry from the fish gate, and an howling from the second, and a great crashing from the hills.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18d75e3b-aca7-4af7-8b4e-e63e5b4d7460>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: ZEP 1:11
Text: Howl, ye inhabitants of Maktesh, for all the merchant people are cut down; all they that bear silver are cut off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6062ec0-3e00-43ea-b64b-8377da214769>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: ZEP 1:12
Text: And it shall come to pass at that time, that I will search Jerusalem with candles, and punish the men that are settled on their lees: that say in their heart, The LORD will not do good, neither will he do evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3bf86e1f-af17-4f41-acf9-e22914c6f8b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: ZEP 1:13
Text: Therefore their goods shall become a booty, and their houses a desolation: they shall also build houses, but not inhabit them; and they shall plant vineyards, but not drink the wine thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0ff6f18-7dbb-4fb0-8acb-4eef903223b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: ZEP 1:14
Text: The great day of the LORD is near, it is near, and hasteth greatly, even the voice of the day of the LORD: the mighty man shall cry there bitterly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2123a5af-e2f9-47a9-92d9-70d536678111>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: ZEP 1:15
Text: That day is a day of wrath, a day of trouble and distress, a day of wasteness and desolation, a day of darkness and gloominess, a day of clouds and thick darkness,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91a390de-5924-4f00-942d-395ed813169e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: ZEP 1:16
Text: A day of the trumpet and alarm against the fenced cities, and against the high towers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b8aee48-7527-46f1-b72b-e50f21d86de3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: ZEP 1:17
Text: And I will bring distress upon men, that they shall walk like blind men, because they have sinned against the LORD: and their blood shall be poured out as dust, and their flesh as the dung.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91db4a1f-83da-4dbd-a9c5-f59c83fa2fa6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: ZEP 1:18
Text: Neither their silver nor their gold shall be able to deliver them in the day of the LORD’s wrath; but the whole land shall be devoured by the fire of his jealousy: for he shall make even a speedy riddance of all them that dwell in the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86ccf3b2-4d32-403d-92f0-7574c4d91f02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: ZEP 2:1
Text: Gather yourselves together, yea, gather together, O nation not desired;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:270865ce-c707-4d1c-a676-7e6ef6c1552b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: ZEP 2:2
Text: Before the decree bring forth, before the day pass as the chaff, before the fierce anger of the LORD come upon you, before the day of the LORD’s anger come upon you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78985737-5882-4876-b9cc-6efbaebedd0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: ZEP 2:3
Text: Seek ye the LORD, all ye meek of the earth, which have wrought his judgment; seek righteousness, seek meekness: it may be ye shall be hid in the day of the LORD’s anger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9b0a5ed-04e3-487e-a99f-649b1ae3137f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: ZEP 2:4
Text: For Gaza shall be forsaken, and Ashkelon a desolation: they shall drive out Ashdod at the noon day, and Ekron shall be rooted up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7386aaaf-859a-4426-bec4-afa83e3a7858>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: ZEP 2:5
Text: Woe unto the inhabitants of the sea coast, the nation of the Cherethites! the word of the LORD is against you; O Canaan, the land of the Philistines, I will even destroy thee, that there shall be no inhabitant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc0418a4-6b76-41cc-a329-c1bc4c473aad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: ZEP 2:6
Text: And the sea coast shall be dwellings and cottages for shepherds, and folds for flocks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f78ab6f-4382-4932-af23-1c7365e881c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: ZEP 2:7
Text: And the coast shall be for the remnant of the house of Judah; they shall feed thereupon: in the houses of Ashkelon shall they lie down in the evening: for the LORD their God shall visit them, and turn away their captivity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28c4a7ef-4526-47ed-ab97-d8335618e087>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: ZEP 2:8
Text: I have heard the reproach of Moab, and the revilings of the children of Ammon, whereby they have reproached my people, and magnified themselves against their border.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c366eb82-82a7-4d13-b489-e5ec02b9fbae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 324

Reference: ZEP 2:9
Text: Therefore as I live, saith the LORD of hosts, the God of Israel, Surely Moab shall be as Sodom, and the children of Ammon as Gomorrah, even the breeding of nettles, and saltpits, and a perpetual desolation: the residue of my people shall spoil them, and the remnant of my people shall possess them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a94da70b-5484-444a-ae0a-044fd3f28763>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: ZEP 2:10
Text: This shall they have for their pride, because they have reproached and magnified themselves against the people of the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0fa056bb-9ca3-46c2-a78b-e8ed765fff1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: ZEP 2:11
Text: The LORD will be terrible unto them: for he will famish all the gods of the earth; and men shall worship him, every one from his place, even all the isles of the heathen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:795fe4ee-417d-4d64-a7c8-a063a038ea71>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: ZEP 2:12
Text: Ye Ethiopians also, ye shall be slain by my sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f046ffd-19c4-4b67-ae33-cc8c3fbe7a83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: ZEP 2:13
Text: And he will stretch out his hand against the north, and destroy Assyria; and will make Nineveh a desolation, and dry like a wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7556414-5061-4646-b225-765fc9e05cf4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 294

Reference: ZEP 2:14
Text: And flocks shall lie down in the midst of her, all the beasts of the nations: both the cormorant and the bittern shall lodge in the upper lintels of it; their voice shall sing in the windows; desolation shall be in the thresholds; for he shall uncover the cedar work.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bde77a95-b1a8-4562-a167-aae5ec9ceeaf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 262

Reference: ZEP 2:15
Text: This is the rejoicing city that dwelt carelessly, that said in her heart, I am, and there is none beside me: how is she become a desolation, a place for beasts to lie down in! every one that passeth by her shall hiss, and wag his hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fb4b187-5c73-4891-b3f7-f711d2caaa3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: ZEP 3:1
Text: Woe to her that is filthy and polluted, to the oppressing city!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe5d088c-9a51-4081-80cc-2cb8a123558f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: ZEP 3:2
Text: She obeyed not the voice; she received not correction; she trusted not in the LORD; she drew not near to her God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf761db5-9ae1-4e2a-9fe3-2d767a0c0dce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: ZEP 3:3
Text: Her princes within her are roaring lions; her judges are evening wolves; they gnaw not the bones till the morrow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf544491-4a4b-49a2-bef6-5963271c9b0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: ZEP 3:4
Text: Her prophets are light and treacherous persons: her priests have polluted the sanctuary, they have done violence to the law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad6f2011-29de-44c5-a70a-e6575a362aa3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: ZEP 3:5
Text: The just LORD is in the midst thereof; he will not do iniquity: every morning doth he bring his judgment to light, he faileth not; but the unjust knoweth no shame.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c806fe7b-b400-4ffb-82aa-192df14bc7fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: ZEP 3:6
Text: I have cut off the nations: their towers are desolate; I made their streets waste, that none passeth by: their cities are destroyed, so that there is no man, that there is none inhabitant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1751dc05-ab5e-445b-8f57-aceedacc0e78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: ZEP 3:7
Text: I said, Surely thou wilt fear me, thou wilt receive instruction; so their dwelling should not be cut off, howsoever I punished them: but they rose early, and corrupted all their doings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44432232-b6f1-4036-9ec4-621f9ae884f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 319

Reference: ZEP 3:8
Text: Therefore wait ye upon me, saith the LORD, until the day that I rise up to the prey: for my determination is to gather the nations, that I may assemble the kingdoms, to pour upon them mine indignation, even all my fierce anger: for all the earth shall be devoured with the fire of my jealousy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ab2ba22-34dd-46ad-b311-b1b2552a31b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: ZEP 3:9
Text: For then will I turn to the people a pure language, that they may all call upon the name of the LORD, to serve him with one consent.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff15a0bc-ec64-4786-81b9-3534c34cb7ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: ZEP 3:10
Text: From beyond the rivers of Ethiopia my suppliants, even the daughter of my dispersed, shall bring mine offering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c30df25b-dbc6-4906-a9ab-8e42d694b4c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 273

Reference: ZEP 3:11
Text: In that day shalt thou not be ashamed for all thy doings, wherein thou hast transgressed against me: for then I will take away out of the midst of thee them that rejoice in thy pride, and thou shalt no more be haughty because of my holy mountain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a64c8051-ed40-4687-8049-fa85e1eedfd5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: ZEP 3:12
Text: I will also leave in the midst of thee an afflicted and poor people, and they shall trust in the name of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65267315-0912-4350-958b-28fcdc8be2f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: ZEP 3:13
Text: The remnant of Israel shall not do iniquity, nor speak lies; neither shall a deceitful tongue be found in their mouth: for they shall feed and lie down, and none shall make them afraid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d446aac-c43c-42a8-9a52-132ddfa5efb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: ZEP 3:14
Text: Sing, O daughter of Zion; shout, O Israel; be glad and rejoice with all the heart, O daughter of Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36343477-da7e-4f7d-8600-fa39b95472d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: ZEP 3:15
Text: The LORD hath taken away thy judgments, he hath cast out thine enemy: the king of Israel, even the LORD, is in the midst of thee: thou shalt not see evil any more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42ff1b7f-250e-40bb-8473-01d24abd783e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: ZEP 3:16
Text: In that day it shall be said to Jerusalem, Fear thou not: and to Zion, Let not thine hands be slack.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea088795-3455-49c3-867d-5888494583b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: ZEP 3:17
Text: The LORD thy God in the midst of thee is mighty; he will save, he will rejoice over thee with joy; he will rest in his love, he will joy over thee with singing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:adffda9e-6053-44ee-822f-86645050bbd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: ZEP 3:18
Text: I will gather them that are sorrowful for the solemn assembly, who are of thee, to whom the reproach of it was a burden.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fccf418-5a7b-4b24-b8f6-d7cfecab6caf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: ZEP 3:19
Text: Behold, at that time I will undo all that afflict thee: and I will save her that halteth, and gather her that was driven out; and I will get them praise and fame in every land where they have been put to shame.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEP/3/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d27ebc5-1145-493c-bccc-2602e53009db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: ZEP 3:20
Text: At that time will I bring you again, even in the time that I gather you: for I will make you a name and a praise among all people of the earth, when I turn back your captivity before your eyes, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82b58952-9703-4e20-91cc-5b86cc41d7dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 280

Reference: HAG 1:1
Text: In the second year of Darius the king, in the sixth month, in the first day of the month, came the word of the LORD by Haggai the prophet unto Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, governor of Judah, and to Joshua the son of Josedech, the high priest, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05cfe63e-ff33-4f3b-840d-476ab2fb4087>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: HAG 1:2
Text: Thus speaketh the LORD of hosts, saying, This people say, The time is not come, the time that the LORD’s house should be built.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89a790a3-ea8e-4a52-b3c6-94bf66c3a64e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: HAG 1:3
Text: Then came the word of the LORD by Haggai the prophet, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30f34159-6077-44cb-8de7-df59f5359ec8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: HAG 1:4
Text: Is it time for you, O ye, to dwell in your cieled houses, and this house lie waste?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8baf4fea-4f57-47c2-b2ee-d8f8107c6927>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: HAG 1:5
Text: Now therefore thus saith the LORD of hosts; Consider your ways.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84a2a703-a3d5-4536-92a1-c0b4bc32b46c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: HAG 1:6
Text: Ye have sown much, and bring in little; ye eat, but ye have not enough; ye drink, but ye are not filled with drink; ye clothe you, but there is none warm; and he that earneth wages earneth wages to put it into a bag with holes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b6ff550-748d-41ca-a316-064569d37ede>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: HAG 1:7
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Consider your ways.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81ce46e8-095b-4167-aab7-c7bac81c2bdc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: HAG 1:8
Text: Go up to the mountain, and bring wood, and build the house; and I will take pleasure in it, and I will be glorified, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8014209-18b9-43d7-8d30-799b6c65930c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: HAG 1:9
Text: Ye looked for much, and, lo it came to little; and when ye brought it home, I did blow upon it. Why? saith the LORD of hosts. Because of mine house that is waste, and ye run every man unto his own house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:037c81dd-b9bc-45bb-a6ef-a44121d7adbc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: HAG 1:10
Text: Therefore the heaven over you is stayed from dew, and the earth is stayed from her fruit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc31c957-7e7d-4e9c-93be-f9be9302c39c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: HAG 1:11
Text: And I called for a drought upon the land, and upon the mountains, and upon the corn, and upon the new wine, and upon the oil, and upon that which the ground bringeth forth, and upon men, and upon cattle, and upon all the labour of the hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3fa3ffb0-b23b-4d16-a6a8-a58ef71ae445>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 303

Reference: HAG 1:12
Text: Then Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, and Joshua the son of Josedech, the high priest, with all the remnant of the people, obeyed the voice of the LORD their God, and the words of Haggai the prophet, as the LORD their God had sent him, and the people did fear before the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aef3b886-d4d1-4d42-af5f-1e30aaa4b223>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: HAG 1:13
Text: Then spake Haggai the LORD’s messenger in the LORD’s message unto the people, saying, I am with you, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:255fdeb0-eb6e-4e6a-8837-d89772eccb85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 301

Reference: HAG 1:14
Text: And the LORD stirred up the spirit of Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, governor of Judah, and the spirit of Joshua the son of Josedech, the high priest, and the spirit of all the remnant of the people; and they came and did work in the house of the LORD of hosts, their God,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f6d713a-b6fb-4806-be64-712cdc235115>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: HAG 1:15
Text: In the four and twentieth day of the sixth month, in the second year of Darius the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:364c3f02-134c-4934-8e1a-9575709bdb3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: HAG 2:1
Text: In the seventh month, in the one and twentieth day of the month, came the word of the LORD by the prophet Haggai, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10b476a8-95b5-4ddb-ad43-d26472596fdc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: HAG 2:2
Text: Speak now to Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, governor of Judah, and to Joshua the son of Josedech, the high priest, and to the residue of the people, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0500dab0-dd0c-4b03-8711-490138798631>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: HAG 2:3
Text: Who is left among you that saw this house in her first glory? and how do ye see it now? is it not in your eyes in comparison of it as nothing?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:daf90cde-ab78-4dd8-828d-4a90876ec73d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: HAG 2:4
Text: Yet now be strong, O Zerubbabel, saith the LORD; and be strong, O Joshua, son of Josedech, the high priest; and be strong, all ye people of the land, saith the LORD, and work: for I am with you, saith the LORD of hosts:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ed4288a-d5d5-447c-b267-aa8cfeca6b7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: HAG 2:5
Text: According to the word that I covenanted with you when ye came out of Egypt, so my spirit remaineth among you: fear ye not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09f25a0d-3502-4ba0-a8df-d526b4bf9456>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: HAG 2:6
Text: For thus saith the LORD of hosts; Yet once, it is a little while, and I will shake the heavens, and the earth, and the sea, and the dry land;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:943980e3-3d68-43f6-abb9-4321b56ca21c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: HAG 2:7
Text: And I will shake all nations, and the desire of all nations shall come: and I will fill this house with glory, saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9152d939-4126-4202-8a4c-d22291486541>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: HAG 2:8
Text: The silver is mine, and the gold is mine, saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:058bfc0d-6c24-4190-a5e6-3ab20cf84f74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: HAG 2:9
Text: The glory of this latter house shall be greater than of the former, saith the LORD of hosts: and in this place will I give peace, saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50f22b96-ee08-4967-b427-11a3f99242f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: HAG 2:10
Text: In the four and twentieth day of the ninth month, in the second year of Darius, came the word of the LORD by Haggai the prophet, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e474e63-0f91-4203-923f-4ae2618353cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: HAG 2:11
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Ask now the priests concerning the law, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b379c127-7834-4801-bd02-810719aa2690>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: HAG 2:12
Text: If one bear holy flesh in the skirt of his garment, and with his skirt do touch bread, or pottage, or wine, or oil, or any meat, shall it be holy? And the priests answered and said, No.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5947bfe2-adba-47c2-94de-976397c62d49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: HAG 2:13
Text: Then said Haggai, If one that is unclean by a dead body touch any of these, shall it be unclean? And the priests answered and said, It shall be unclean.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d173d612-23b3-44c3-81a2-89890af5dd86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: HAG 2:14
Text: Then answered Haggai, and said, So is this people, and so is this nation before me, saith the LORD; and so is every work of their hands; and that which they offer there is unclean.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0402227d-eac2-416f-a7e0-ddd72bb5ea76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: HAG 2:15
Text: And now, I pray you, consider from this day and upward, from before a stone was laid upon a stone in the temple of the LORD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16b1d3c7-5c91-41b2-b182-92d017aaf589>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: HAG 2:16
Text: Since those days were, when one came to an heap of twenty measures, there were but ten: when one came to the pressfat for to draw out fifty vessels out of the press, there were but twenty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afacbc17-81d8-41f4-9d2b-d74142efac51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: HAG 2:17
Text: I smote you with blasting and with mildew and with hail in all the labours of your hands; yet ye turned not to me, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83748e2c-5b7b-477d-bb28-5bc7dc40ffab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: HAG 2:18
Text: Consider now from this day and upward, from the four and twentieth day of the ninth month, even from the day that the foundation of the LORD’s temple was laid, consider it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f390669e-85bb-4ce1-8b08-57a3fc655488>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: HAG 2:19
Text: Is the seed yet in the barn? yea, as yet the vine, and the fig tree, and the pomegranate, and the olive tree, hath not brought forth: from this day will I bless you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:101f6538-9cd2-4bad-9c67-a461d9415b00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: HAG 2:20
Text: And again the word of the LORD came unto Haggai in the four and twentieth day of the month, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe1898ce-44e9-4a4b-8aac-149874184ba8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: HAG 2:21
Text: Speak to Zerubbabel, governor of Judah, saying, I will shake the heavens and the earth;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53bb1cd2-4f76-4695-9bd8-6d2562821c86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 287

Reference: HAG 2:22
Text: And I will overthrow the throne of kingdoms, and I will destroy the strength of the kingdoms of the heathen; and I will overthrow the chariots, and those that ride in them; and the horses and their riders shall come down, every one by the sword of his brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HAG/2/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c90ef4bc-d8e1-4262-8f63-bba386d944b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: HAG 2:23
Text: In that day, saith the LORD of hosts, will I take thee, O Zerubbabel, my servant, the son of Shealtiel, saith the LORD, and will make thee as a signet: for I have chosen thee, saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:681c2295-0ac7-477f-a222-9be235d8a542>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: ZEC 1:1
Text: In the eighth month, in the second year of Darius, came the word of the LORD unto Zechariah, the son of Berechiah, the son of Iddo the prophet, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:915145a0-2e83-4410-924f-8f92fe073b3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: ZEC 1:2
Text: The LORD hath been sore displeased with your fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f25f68e-31fe-4534-8019-eeead3133813>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: ZEC 1:3
Text: Therefore say thou unto them, Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Turn ye unto me, saith the LORD of hosts, and I will turn unto you, saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51f2986d-0b15-4f5f-9990-c0c8c439248e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: ZEC 1:4
Text: Be ye not as your fathers, unto whom the former prophets have cried, saying, Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Turn ye now from your evil ways, and from your evil doings: but they did not hear, nor hearken unto me, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7284b861-84d8-4d8a-9073-045d7a79ed3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: ZEC 1:5
Text: Your fathers, where are they? and the prophets, do they live for ever?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b2fe23a-99ea-42f9-bc30-7bf77593beb6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 294

Reference: ZEC 1:6
Text: But my words and my statutes, which I commanded my servants the prophets, did they not take hold of your fathers? and they returned and said, Like as the LORD of hosts thought to do unto us, according to our ways, and according to our doings, so hath he dealt with us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed974b65-3f30-4501-98c1-7e81d17b6a9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: ZEC 1:7
Text: Upon the four and twentieth day of the eleventh month, which is the month Sebat, in the second year of Darius, came the word of the LORD unto Zechariah, the son of Berechiah, the son of Iddo the prophet, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4580875d-b483-4fbe-b0d5-d7e492aaa17a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: ZEC 1:8
Text: I saw by night, and behold a man riding upon a red horse, and he stood among the myrtle trees that were in the bottom; and behind him were there red horses, speckled, and white.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ae98f62-19f1-41fe-898b-d5ec8f03a70a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: ZEC 1:9
Text: Then said I, O my lord, what are these? And the angel that talked with me said unto me, I will shew thee what these be.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47eb0c9b-7fed-4d36-aa3b-3b03cd884a56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: ZEC 1:10
Text: And the man that stood among the myrtle trees answered and said, These are they whom the LORD hath sent to walk to and fro through the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dcba4ce5-a669-4fb4-89d5-36e87786dc41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: ZEC 1:11
Text: And they answered the angel of the LORD that stood among the myrtle trees, and said, We have walked to and fro through the earth, and, behold, all the earth sitteth still, and is at rest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:530f1e64-1510-4b06-9d23-c57ebe88769d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: ZEC 1:12
Text: Then the angel of the LORD answered and said, O LORD of hosts, how long wilt thou not have mercy on Jerusalem and on the cities of Judah, against which thou hast had indignation these threescore and ten years?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69367fd7-dc7d-40cd-a127-16fda2810d20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: ZEC 1:13
Text: And the LORD answered the angel that talked with me with good words and comfortable words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3c42106-1dae-44d7-bc46-227b2f691906>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: ZEC 1:14
Text: So the angel that communed with me said unto me, Cry thou, saying, Thus saith the LORD of hosts; I am jealous for Jerusalem and for Zion with a great jealousy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c4506f7-4c31-4240-8e20-dc42db34b571>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: ZEC 1:15
Text: And I am very sore displeased with the heathen that are at ease: for I was but a little displeased, and they helped forward the affliction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7fdac4b-e903-4dd5-8242-c250dce6a214>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: ZEC 1:16
Text: Therefore thus saith the LORD; I am returned to Jerusalem with mercies: my house shall be built in it, saith the LORD of hosts, and a line shall be stretched forth upon Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cdffd2a-bde2-4447-8141-146d5928bdbe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: ZEC 1:17
Text: Cry yet, saying, Thus saith the LORD of hosts; My cities through prosperity shall yet be spread abroad; and the LORD shall yet comfort Zion, and shall yet choose Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6102b7fc-9083-40c3-9b8d-f17842e065e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: ZEC 1:18
Text: Then lifted I up mine eyes, and saw, and behold four horns.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c790b761-ef24-4c27-9c90-ec201a8d04b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: ZEC 1:19
Text: And I said unto the angel that talked with me, What be these? And he answered me, These are the horns which have scattered Judah, Israel, and Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a291760a-a75d-49dc-a4a6-28d537fea0a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 66

Reference: ZEC 1:20
Text: And the LORD shewed me four carpenters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/1/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3fcc132b-a00c-4719-834f-e83a9a4f71d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 306

Reference: ZEC 1:21
Text: Then said I, What come these to do? And he spake, saying, These are the horns which have scattered Judah, so that no man did lift up his head: but these are come to fray them, to cast out the horns of the Gentiles, which lifted up their horn over the land of Judah to scatter it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb720463-3a90-4898-8353-df20728ce952>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: ZEC 2:1
Text: I lifted up mine eyes again, and looked, and behold a man with a measuring line in his hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:154daae7-8c2b-46f9-b28e-7b47bce465fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: ZEC 2:2
Text: Then said I, Whither goest thou? And he said unto me, To measure Jerusalem, to see what is the breadth thereof, and what is the length thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7797dfe2-c3de-492d-96b3-f431c72f4796>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: ZEC 2:3
Text: And, behold, the angel that talked with me went forth, and another angel went out to meet him,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:026e7ee7-2b62-4265-a7e5-802aa558fe36>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: ZEC 2:4
Text: And said unto him, Run, speak to this young man, saying, Jerusalem shall be inhabited as towns without walls for the multitude of men and cattle therein:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36772c4b-61e4-4faf-b844-bac4ee389a01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: ZEC 2:5
Text: For I, saith the LORD, will be unto her a wall of fire round about, and will be the glory in the midst of her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f23b26a7-8e08-47b9-af00-53604a79071f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: ZEC 2:6
Text: Ho, ho, come forth, and flee from the land of the north, saith the LORD: for I have spread you abroad as the four winds of the heaven, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8bbecb46-f4a7-468e-acf8-c7175432566e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: ZEC 2:7
Text: Deliver thyself, O Zion, that dwellest with the daughter of Babylon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b5c8d08-feeb-4fd9-b4c3-ba1eb0bf79e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: ZEC 2:8
Text: For thus saith the LORD of hosts; After the glory hath he sent me unto the nations which spoiled you: for he that toucheth you toucheth the apple of his eye.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31baccff-d885-4dcf-aa20-0fb011aef1cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: ZEC 2:9
Text: For, behold, I will shake mine hand upon them, and they shall be a spoil to their servants: and ye shall know that the LORD of hosts hath sent me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca14c89b-4f11-4c19-812e-96e58ea2151a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: ZEC 2:10
Text: Sing and rejoice, O daughter of Zion: for, lo, I come, and I will dwell in the midst of thee, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b692498e-f484-4fbd-a355-9d334f27efa0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: ZEC 2:11
Text: And many nations shall be joined to the LORD in that day, and shall be my people: and I will dwell in the midst of thee, and thou shalt know that the LORD of hosts hath sent me unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56ccad53-e9cf-4502-9bf8-0210a539a7d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: ZEC 2:12
Text: And the LORD shall inherit Judah his portion in the holy land, and shall choose Jerusalem again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3db8172-cd4c-4832-848c-fd52569623ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: ZEC 2:13
Text: Be silent, O all flesh, before the LORD: for he is raised up out of his holy habitation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d585672-93cc-4bc2-9237-848db4637a66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: ZEC 3:1
Text: And he shewed me Joshua the high priest standing before the angel of the LORD, and Satan standing at his right hand to resist him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f8a199f-fd59-465f-b0e7-8380768b6499>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: ZEC 3:2
Text: And the LORD said unto Satan, The LORD rebuke thee, O Satan; even the LORD that hath chosen Jerusalem rebuke thee: is not this a brand plucked out of the fire?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:474b6b10-da5e-46dd-954e-58fcd2ed6137>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: ZEC 3:3
Text: Now Joshua was clothed with filthy garments, and stood before the angel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83cb23d9-a81c-4920-aa30-52e50eb2ab38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: ZEC 3:4
Text: And he answered and spake unto those that stood before him, saying, Take away the filthy garments from him. And unto him he said, Behold, I have caused thine iniquity to pass from thee, and I will clothe thee with change of raiment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ceac215-cab9-4ecc-9144-daa7fc8ffafb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: ZEC 3:5
Text: And I said, Let them set a fair mitre upon his head. So they set a fair mitre upon his head, and clothed him with garments. And the angel of the LORD stood by.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffe99107-b8b6-4879-a842-3675c30e7650>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: ZEC 3:6
Text: And the angel of the LORD protested unto Joshua, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b870fceb-d92a-4411-8945-71cf452d3f97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: ZEC 3:7
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts; If thou wilt walk in my ways, and if thou wilt keep my charge, then thou shalt also judge my house, and shalt also keep my courts, and I will give thee places to walk among these that stand by.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:560359ec-dbad-4aa1-ba58-22fb5bf9b7d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: ZEC 3:8
Text: Hear now, O Joshua the high priest, thou, and thy fellows that sit before thee: for they are men wondered at: for, behold, I will bring forth my servant the BRANCH.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a794e02-418e-4fdf-a79a-94b487e4df22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: ZEC 3:9
Text: For behold the stone that I have laid before Joshua; upon one stone shall be seven eyes: behold, I will engrave the graving thereof, saith the LORD of hosts, and I will remove the iniquity of that land in one day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e53d9e5-ec96-47fe-97de-5cab5fb7841a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: ZEC 3:10
Text: In that day, saith the LORD of hosts, shall ye call every man his neighbour under the vine and under the fig tree.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3fb288bd-c3e1-45c6-b90e-955c5fb0d27a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: ZEC 4:1
Text: And the angel that talked with me came again, and waked me, as a man that is wakened out of his sleep.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4547884-b1b7-445f-9ea9-5bea5b57ef1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: ZEC 4:2
Text: And said unto me, What seest thou? And I said, I have looked, and behold a candlestick all of gold, with a bowl upon the top of it, and his seven lamps thereon, and seven pipes to the seven lamps, which are upon the top thereof:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27166830-915a-4e13-ac30-d44914601e6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: ZEC 4:3
Text: And two olive trees by it, one upon the right side of the bowl, and the other upon the left side thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d192564f-905a-4827-bf59-429767bf054a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: ZEC 4:4
Text: So I answered and spake to the angel that talked with me, saying, What are these, my lord?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38da86f7-ffd8-44a7-97ef-b9f33e58c695>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: ZEC 4:5
Text: Then the angel that talked with me answered and said unto me, Knowest thou not what these be? And I said, No, my lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a11cd862-0002-4e36-9be3-c8a4c65b6d4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: ZEC 4:6
Text: Then he answered and spake unto me, saying, This is the word of the LORD unto Zerubbabel, saying, Not by might, nor by power, but by my spirit, saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbdf423a-1dc0-4195-a17b-367a7e1c89f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: ZEC 4:7
Text: Who art thou, O great mountain? before Zerubbabel thou shalt become a plain: and he shall bring forth the headstone thereof with shoutings, crying, Grace, grace unto it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1816b547-1bf3-4d74-a7e5-22e9f4dc1e85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: ZEC 4:8
Text: Moreover the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce2f7658-3565-46b8-b534-ade343f07186>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: ZEC 4:9
Text: The hands of Zerubbabel have laid the foundation of this house; his hands shall also finish it; and thou shalt know that the LORD of hosts hath sent me unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:729c8b39-897c-4246-a9f7-d910a30eb692>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: ZEC 4:10
Text: For who hath despised the day of small things? for they shall rejoice, and shall see the plummet in the hand of Zerubbabel with those seven; they are the eyes of the LORD, which run to and fro through the whole earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14d4c508-5452-41d9-bbb1-d19612ac7703>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: ZEC 4:11
Text: Then answered I, and said unto him, What are these two olive trees upon the right side of the candlestick and upon the left side thereof?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ab6902f-ad20-4c59-b7ef-d8ae67ee2e56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: ZEC 4:12
Text: And I answered again, and said unto him, What be these two olive branches which through the two golden pipes empty the golden oil out of themselves?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afbc5001-1d00-4d01-8d5d-df5bec61bd1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: ZEC 4:13
Text: And he answered me and said, Knowest thou not what these be? And I said, No, my lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:297ebc53-396c-4a68-930b-f304912f06ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: ZEC 4:14
Text: Then said he, These are the two anointed ones, that stand by the LORD of the whole earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c7daf4f-4d7a-42b4-ba6a-b7a218ed0a6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: ZEC 5:1
Text: Then I turned, and lifted up mine eyes, and looked, and behold a flying roll.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24b758b4-b167-4e3d-ae3a-a3adae8d144f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: ZEC 5:2
Text: And he said unto me, What seest thou? And I answered, I see a flying roll; the length thereof is twenty cubits, and the breadth thereof ten cubits.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a51d45f-a41c-4792-9fd0-7590847068b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: ZEC 5:3
Text: Then said he unto me, This is the curse that goeth forth over the face of the whole earth: for every one that stealeth shall be cut off as on this side according to it; and every one that sweareth shall be cut off as on that side according to it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2da84da3-2a05-4cd1-82cf-e1b60577262b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 297

Reference: ZEC 5:4
Text: I will bring it forth, saith the LORD of hosts, and it shall enter into the house of the thief, and into the house of him that sweareth falsely by my name: and it shall remain in the midst of his house, and shall consume it with the timber thereof and the stones thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee827b64-38db-476d-8fb5-0552282fd3f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: ZEC 5:5
Text: Then the angel that talked with me went forth, and said unto me, Lift up now thine eyes, and see what is this that goeth forth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3103953-e0fb-481d-a454-62972de1302a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: ZEC 5:6
Text: And I said, What is it? And he said, This is an ephah that goeth forth. He said moreover, This is their resemblance through all the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1258ce2f-6ee1-4903-9226-40e722fc7dd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: ZEC 5:7
Text: And, behold, there was lifted up a talent of lead: and this is a woman that sitteth in the midst of the ephah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36265ec4-71a0-477d-afea-76368f334e88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: ZEC 5:8
Text: And he said, This is wickedness. And he cast it into the midst of the ephah; and he cast the weight of lead upon the mouth thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8138637-60df-4207-a2ad-995e3ed02327>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: ZEC 5:9
Text: Then lifted I up mine eyes, and looked, and, behold, there came out two women, and the wind was in their wings; for they had wings like the wings of a stork: and they lifted up the ephah between the earth and the heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72005dd7-25b6-411f-9683-9391efb5fd4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: ZEC 5:10
Text: Then said I to the angel that talked with me, Whither do these bear the ephah?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62d8d818-89c7-4f20-8514-0e2519f1ade7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: ZEC 5:11
Text: And he said unto me, To build it an house in the land of Shinar: and it shall be established, and set there upon her own base.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b3cac76-c2cb-48f7-886a-466275d02a7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: ZEC 6:1
Text: And I turned, and lifted up mine eyes, and looked, and, behold, there came four chariots out from between two mountains; and the mountains were mountains of brass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b172d9b-5857-44d0-ba8d-314a3b5c1d94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: ZEC 6:2
Text: In the first chariot were red horses; and in the second chariot black horses;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25119d4e-1837-447d-b85d-9a61713b9359>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: ZEC 6:3
Text: And in the third chariot white horses; and in the fourth chariot grisled and bay horses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30dd2300-f0b1-4f69-9282-2b9ea78ab78d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: ZEC 6:4
Text: Then I answered and said unto the angel that talked with me, What are these, my lord?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51049a13-d609-4629-8908-7866a8ee4d2f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: ZEC 6:5
Text: And the angel answered and said unto me, These are the four spirits of the heavens, which go forth from standing before the LORD of all the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7f6d56b-eba2-4eef-b2f1-078cbd093ca2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: ZEC 6:6
Text: The black horses which are therein go forth into the north country; and the white go forth after them; and the grisled go forth toward the south country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:764bc833-d51b-4bcf-aea8-fbfed8643e9f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: ZEC 6:7
Text: And the bay went forth, and sought to go that they might walk to and fro through the earth: and he said, Get you hence, walk to and fro through the earth. So they walked to and fro through the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f609128-605d-411b-8cd1-dcf464178c93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: ZEC 6:8
Text: Then cried he upon me, and spake unto me, saying, Behold, these that go toward the north country have quieted my spirit in the north country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:688b975a-1c5d-49aa-8963-293451e6f7ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 72

Reference: ZEC 6:9
Text: And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e0da90d-2880-457f-96e6-e65248fda733>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: ZEC 6:10
Text: Take of them of the captivity, even of Heldai, of Tobijah, and of Jedaiah, which are come from Babylon, and come thou the same day, and go into the house of Josiah the son of Zephaniah;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bc44d1c-84d6-4bb9-a296-696053e8b98a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: ZEC 6:11
Text: Then take silver and gold, and make crowns, and set them upon the head of Joshua the son of Josedech, the high priest;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e82765ab-eb47-4cff-baaa-8a1a9c7d0dc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: ZEC 6:12
Text: And speak unto him, saying, Thus speaketh the LORD of hosts, saying, Behold the man whose name is The BRANCH; and he shall grow up out of his place, and he shall build the temple of the LORD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7788dbe6-c0d5-46c3-909a-a0df275f7dce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: ZEC 6:13
Text: Even he shall build the temple of the LORD; and he shall bear the glory, and shall sit and rule upon his throne; and he shall be a priest upon his throne: and the counsel of peace shall be between them both.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/6/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fde2eec5-b169-420d-8667-299a9b80e833>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: ZEC 6:14
Text: And the crowns shall be to Helem, and to Tobijah, and to Jedaiah, and to Hen the son of Zephaniah, for a memorial in the temple of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/6/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ededd1d6-fb5a-4a54-8631-1703d40ba595>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: ZEC 6:15
Text: And they that are far off shall come and build in the temple of the LORD, and ye shall know that the LORD of hosts hath sent me unto you. And this shall come to pass, if ye will diligently obey the voice of the LORD your God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20027847-3339-47b7-8f84-34cde2ce0272>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: ZEC 7:1
Text: And it came to pass in the fourth year of king Darius, that the word of the LORD came unto Zechariah in the fourth day of the ninth month, even in Chisleu;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c68d60e2-2f96-48e5-ba26-1691732a308f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: ZEC 7:2
Text: When they had sent unto the house of God Sherezer and Regemmelech, and their men, to pray before the LORD,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c23dcfd-c91d-4981-9a02-d864a78d0eb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: ZEC 7:3
Text: And to speak unto the priests which were in the house of the LORD of hosts, and to the prophets, saying, Should I weep in the fifth month, separating myself, as I have done these so many years?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb3ec2b5-0a65-4f0b-9b1a-75cc0282c086>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: ZEC 7:4
Text: Then came the word of the LORD of hosts unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c229222e-5135-4fb3-b7ee-9801d0220888>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: ZEC 7:5
Text: Speak unto all the people of the land, and to the priests, saying, When ye fasted and mourned in the fifth and seventh month, even those seventy years, did ye at all fast unto me, even to me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6cb6d490-e43d-4cce-a073-3d6441308584>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: ZEC 7:6
Text: And when ye did eat, and when ye did drink, did not ye eat for yourselves, and drink for yourselves?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20ee94ff-3490-4fca-9c85-df170f179188>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: ZEC 7:7
Text: Should ye not hear the words which the LORD hath cried by the former prophets, when Jerusalem was inhabited and in prosperity, and the cities thereof round about her, when men inhabited the south and the plain?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76f019fd-f811-42bd-8923-60f332b6a7d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: ZEC 7:8
Text: And the word of the LORD came unto Zechariah, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74e86f8a-0019-4e37-9890-aeba6a811945>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: ZEC 7:9
Text: Thus speaketh the LORD of hosts, saying, Execute true judgment, and shew mercy and compassions every man to his brother:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f6e0ad3-1fa4-4c9b-8084-70803888b701>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: ZEC 7:10
Text: And oppress not the widow, nor the fatherless, the stranger, nor the poor; and let none of you imagine evil against his brother in your heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50c76e23-a1ee-4294-bca1-10b0593cf23e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: ZEC 7:11
Text: But they refused to hearken, and pulled away the shoulder, and stopped their ears, that they should not hear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:295da9dd-a82b-47d2-909f-c371d74648c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: ZEC 7:12
Text: Yea, they made their hearts as an adamant stone, lest they should hear the law, and the words which the LORD of hosts hath sent in his spirit by the former prophets: therefore came a great wrath from the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a4c002b-a29e-4ac7-ad07-275be79e0ae4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: ZEC 7:13
Text: Therefore it is come to pass, that as he cried, and they would not hear; so they cried, and I would not hear, saith the LORD of hosts:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/7/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50695c5b-de59-4c70-b82f-87c22b8fa4c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: ZEC 7:14
Text: But I scattered them with a whirlwind among all the nations whom they knew not. Thus the land was desolate after them, that no man passed through nor returned: for they laid the pleasant land desolate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/8/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f04be03-6a98-4d88-b6f2-b377eed48f50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: ZEC 8:1
Text: Again the word of the LORD of hosts came to me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/8/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5b0a4fa-ab0c-4195-9618-adfd82dc44d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: ZEC 8:2
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts; I was jealous for Zion with great jealousy, and I was jealous for her with great fury.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/8/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44c64d8c-f40c-4c60-9250-f147fa5ed056>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: ZEC 8:3
Text: Thus saith the LORD; I am returned unto Zion, and will dwell in the midst of Jerusalem: and Jerusalem shall be called a city of truth; and the mountain of the LORD of hosts the holy mountain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/8/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:871e6f04-1510-4028-b9e0-8604682973fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: ZEC 8:4
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts; There shall yet old men and old women dwell in the streets of Jerusalem, and every man with his staff in his hand for very age.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/8/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0cad3c9-e5db-40c1-8027-78c462ea7c62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: ZEC 8:5
Text: And the streets of the city shall be full of boys and girls playing in the streets thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/8/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1ff8e67-37c7-4439-9829-e648360ec9d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: ZEC 8:6
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts; If it be marvellous in the eyes of the remnant of this people in these days, should it also be marvellous in mine eyes? saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/8/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93a4f845-f1a4-4035-b7a2-c64980eaeb73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: ZEC 8:7
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Behold, I will save my people from the east country, and from the west country;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/8/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9487f546-7926-49be-b067-ec8953592c71>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: ZEC 8:8
Text: And I will bring them, and they shall dwell in the midst of Jerusalem: and they shall be my people, and I will be their God, in truth and in righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/8/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c295b19c-5134-49f1-b2d9-19082b7f5578>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: ZEC 8:9
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts; Let your hands be strong, ye that hear in these days these words by the mouth of the prophets, which were in the day that the foundation of the house of the LORD of hosts was laid, that the temple might be built.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/8/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:595dac19-8a67-4704-8e5b-2d2a972ef778>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: ZEC 8:10
Text: For before these days there was no hire for man, nor any hire for beast; neither was there any peace to him that went out or came in because of the affliction: for I set all men every one against his neighbour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/8/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3d04a5f-dd55-46a7-82b0-a221e0916da1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: ZEC 8:11
Text: But now I will not be unto the residue of this people as in the former days, saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/8/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96d4b461-68b9-4a8e-86a4-fd5051ec8fe9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: ZEC 8:12
Text: For the seed shall be prosperous; the vine shall give her fruit, and the ground shall give her increase, and the heavens shall give their dew; and I will cause the remnant of this people to possess all these things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/8/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c69f178-65c2-41d3-923a-dbd6b2231b22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: ZEC 8:13
Text: And it shall come to pass, that as ye were a curse among the heathen, O house of Judah, and house of Israel; so will I save you, and ye shall be a blessing: fear not, but let your hands be strong.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/8/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04f086d2-99ff-42f2-9e8b-489777e14d8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: ZEC 8:14
Text: For thus saith the LORD of hosts; As I thought to punish you, when your fathers provoked me to wrath, saith the LORD of hosts, and I repented not:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/8/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b858797-a5bc-48d2-95f1-ce90987a9a18>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: ZEC 8:15
Text: So again have I thought in these days to do well unto Jerusalem and to the house of Judah: fear ye not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/8/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b7a87b1-4c6c-4b48-8a3c-5ea3f1ff5010>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: ZEC 8:16
Text: These are the things that ye shall do; Speak ye every man the truth to his neighbour; execute the judgment of truth and peace in your gates:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/8/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64faf456-d4ee-49d7-b256-53b63cd8e163>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: ZEC 8:17
Text: And let none of you imagine evil in your hearts against his neighbour; and love no false oath: for all these are things that I hate, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/8/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84bd5b12-ac43-46c5-8e3e-d220f57d372f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: ZEC 8:18
Text: And the word of the LORD of hosts came unto me, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/8/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:413f38e7-f229-40b0-80cf-f600bc709334>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: ZEC 8:19
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts; The fast of the fourth month, and the fast of the fifth, and the fast of the seventh, and the fast of the tenth, shall be to the house of Judah joy and gladness, and cheerful feasts; therefore love the truth and peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/8/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:712696ea-02a2-4439-88b2-b2f30ba046e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: ZEC 8:20
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts; It shall yet come to pass, that there shall come people, and the inhabitants of many cities:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/8/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e2f7809-99d9-4964-83c9-a4da38b1f996>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: ZEC 8:21
Text: And the inhabitants of one city shall go to another, saying, Let us go speedily to pray before the LORD, and to seek the LORD of hosts: I will go also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/8/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5616762-788d-4b76-8f6d-e54adcb07ebe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: ZEC 8:22
Text: Yea, many people and strong nations shall come to seek the LORD of hosts in Jerusalem, and to pray before the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/8/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a785efab-6736-438f-a683-ccf0c81b4547>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: ZEC 8:23
Text: Thus saith the LORD of hosts; In those days it shall come to pass, that ten men shall take hold out of all languages of the nations, even shall take hold of the skirt of him that is a Jew, saying, We will go with you: for we have heard that God is with you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/9/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29e9910e-1cf9-47a5-b111-5b313de8fac6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: ZEC 9:1
Text: The burden of the word of the LORD in the land of Hadrach, and Damascus shall be the rest thereof: when the eyes of man, as of all the tribes of Israel, shall be toward the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/9/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02c32342-a9ea-42d2-b0bb-ca7db56fae91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: ZEC 9:2
Text: And Hamath also shall border thereby; Tyrus, and Zidon, though it be very wise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/9/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae8d1baa-3c04-4220-8c06-8a029f3a99dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: ZEC 9:3
Text: And Tyrus did build herself a strong hold, and heaped up silver as the dust, and fine gold as the mire of the streets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/9/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a852656c-07a8-4f3f-91ca-a20a4d0dee07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: ZEC 9:4
Text: Behold, the LORD will cast her out, and he will smite her power in the sea; and she shall be devoured with fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/9/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38b0f2bb-9d82-4d70-b46a-9df6106b6b5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: ZEC 9:5
Text: Ashkelon shall see it, and fear; Gaza also shall see it, and be very sorrowful, and Ekron; for her expectation shall be ashamed; and the king shall perish from Gaza, and Ashkelon shall not be inhabited.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/9/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7804d84b-610c-4a35-b2d6-d3c3527b4cc9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: ZEC 9:6
Text: And a bastard shall dwell in Ashdod, and I will cut off the pride of the Philistines.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/9/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96249d55-cdf2-4d8e-a62e-4affcf2cfe9e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: ZEC 9:7
Text: And I will take away his blood out of his mouth, and his abominations from between his teeth: but he that remaineth, even he, shall be for our God, and he shall be as a governor in Judah, and Ekron as a Jebusite.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/9/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea9bf7dd-5c53-4938-8972-caf237ab1cb6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: ZEC 9:8
Text: And I will encamp about mine house because of the army, because of him that passeth by, and because of him that returneth: and no oppressor shall pass through them any more: for now have I seen with mine eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/9/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2d7eb9b-17e6-4a7d-8d88-d4faa5d7c162>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: ZEC 9:9
Text: Rejoice greatly, O daughter of Zion; shout, O daughter of Jerusalem: behold, thy King cometh unto thee: he is just, and having salvation; lowly, and riding upon an ass, and upon a colt the foal of an ass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/9/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bb7e9f5-4248-44c8-a3c4-32e9e38f326a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 279

Reference: ZEC 9:10
Text: And I will cut off the chariot from Ephraim, and the horse from Jerusalem, and the battle bow shall be cut off: and he shall speak peace unto the heathen: and his dominion shall be from sea even to sea, and from the river even to the ends of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/9/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:823ab43b-622b-4812-b38a-a32d9d36b6ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: ZEC 9:11
Text: As for thee also, by the blood of thy covenant I have sent forth thy prisoners out of the pit wherein is no water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/9/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92c89c58-ee63-4444-90b9-6ab2513eb056>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: ZEC 9:12
Text: Turn you to the strong hold, ye prisoners of hope: even to day do I declare that I will render double unto thee;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/9/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a74a913e-23dd-4843-a828-b7637e51ef3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: ZEC 9:13
Text: When I have bent Judah for me, filled the bow with Ephraim, and raised up thy sons, O Zion, against thy sons, O Greece, and made thee as the sword of a mighty man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/9/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ecdda1d5-ef60-4d59-afeb-43610ae950db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: ZEC 9:14
Text: And the LORD shall be seen over them, and his arrow shall go forth as the lightning: and the LORD God shall blow the trumpet, and shall go with whirlwinds of the south.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/9/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74d61efc-e32d-4c98-bc7a-53a0285c660a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: ZEC 9:15
Text: The LORD of hosts shall defend them; and they shall devour, and subdue with sling stones; and they shall drink, and make a noise as through wine; and they shall be filled like bowls, and as the corners of the altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/9/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a711925c-9734-46e0-94e6-70e49b5f1e4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: ZEC 9:16
Text: And the LORD their God shall save them in that day as the flock of his people: for they shall be as the stones of a crown, lifted up as an ensign upon his land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/9/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0b30017-2afc-45f3-b3bc-d86d71518845>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: ZEC 9:17
Text: For how great is his goodness, and how great is his beauty! corn shall make the young men cheerful, and new wine the maids.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/10/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b59cc018-e18b-4f89-9e3a-d3adf4461685>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: ZEC 10:1
Text: Ask ye of the LORD rain in the time of the latter rain; so the LORD shall make bright clouds, and give them showers of rain, to every one grass in the field.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/10/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c673f5e-e028-47b3-91bd-ccdc9b84dbb1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: ZEC 10:2
Text: For the idols have spoken vanity, and the diviners have seen a lie, and have told false dreams; they comfort in vain: therefore they went their way as a flock, they were troubled, because there was no shepherd.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/10/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab91cd4b-b748-470a-80a1-eee970c0dcdb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: ZEC 10:3
Text: Mine anger was kindled against the shepherds, and I punished the goats: for the LORD of hosts hath visited his flock the house of Judah, and hath made them as his goodly horse in the battle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/10/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47059766-64d8-4f8f-a9e5-cd0744766fb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: ZEC 10:4
Text: Out of him came forth the corner, out of him the nail, out of him the battle bow, out of him every oppressor together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/10/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:172f6681-ce62-4fab-b9f1-a6ab666df420>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: ZEC 10:5
Text: And they shall be as mighty men, which tread down their enemies in the mire of the streets in the battle: and they shall fight, because the LORD is with them, and the riders on horses shall be confounded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/10/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e54ba2ed-c3a6-4a32-abed-b36a93b98273>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 278

Reference: ZEC 10:6
Text: And I will strengthen the house of Judah, and I will save the house of Joseph, and I will bring them again to place them; for I have mercy upon them: and they shall be as though I had not cast them off: for I am the LORD their God, and will hear them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/10/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddec697f-c2a4-4e80-b222-d4d9d483ca81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: ZEC 10:7
Text: And they of Ephraim shall be like a mighty man, and their heart shall rejoice as through wine: yea, their children shall see it, and be glad; their heart shall rejoice in the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/10/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52def7d9-734d-45bc-b477-cf947543ec80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: ZEC 10:8
Text: I will hiss for them, and gather them; for I have redeemed them: and they shall increase as they have increased.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/10/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad4462ea-b881-4a09-b200-3557acae809b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: ZEC 10:9
Text: And I will sow them among the people: and they shall remember me in far countries; and they shall live with their children, and turn again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/10/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c6d9ca7-903b-4cfb-b64b-f777c52bcc3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: ZEC 10:10
Text: I will bring them again also out of the land of Egypt, and gather them out of Assyria; and I will bring them into the land of Gilead and Lebanon; and place shall not be found for them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/10/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ae5f0b9-b655-4acb-8844-5bf9cc8d7955>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: ZEC 10:11
Text: And he shall pass through the sea with affliction, and shall smite the waves in the sea, and all the deeps of the river shall dry up: and the pride of Assyria shall be brought down, and the sceptre of Egypt shall depart away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/10/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c2412be-840f-4a97-ba1d-2db07744c74b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: ZEC 10:12
Text: And I will strengthen them in the LORD; and they shall walk up and down in his name, saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/11/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ed335c9-0719-4433-a448-e0643d016b81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: ZEC 11:1
Text: Open thy doors, O Lebanon, that the fire may devour thy cedars.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/11/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46e83ab1-95a7-434f-a9dd-0dbc984c588c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: ZEC 11:2
Text: Howl, fir tree; for the cedar is fallen; because the mighty are spoiled: howl, O ye oaks of Bashan; for the forest of the vintage is come down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/11/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79bb8646-7c30-42f0-82ec-9a51f5be8a23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: ZEC 11:3
Text: There is a voice of the howling of the shepherds; for their glory is spoiled: a voice of the roaring of young lions; for the pride of Jordan is spoiled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/11/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e450631-1b49-47f6-b745-7c1f69532b6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: ZEC 11:4
Text: Thus saith the LORD my God; Feed the flock of the slaughter;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/11/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7786a1da-ea40-4c3b-ac1f-913c672ba2ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: ZEC 11:5
Text: Whose possessors slay them, and hold themselves not guilty: and they that sell them say, Blessed be the LORD; for I am rich: and their own shepherds pity them not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/11/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c92fac67-d25b-4207-b2bd-80311b1bab11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: ZEC 11:6
Text: For I will no more pity the inhabitants of the land, saith the LORD: but, lo, I will deliver the men every one into his neighbour’s hand, and into the hand of his king: and they shall smite the land, and out of their hand I will not deliver them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/11/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04c927de-7803-4c3c-a373-5d7c446de448>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: ZEC 11:7
Text: And I will feed the flock of slaughter, even you, O poor of the flock. And I took unto me two staves; the one I called Beauty, and the other I called Bands; and I fed the flock.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/11/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68335f42-549f-482f-8ed1-ad267838a7ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: ZEC 11:8
Text: Three shepherds also I cut off in one month; and my soul lothed them, and their soul also abhorred me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/11/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab0a7e94-7c6e-44b2-8574-5fcf13e1c5d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: ZEC 11:9
Text: Then said I, I will not feed you: that that dieth, let it die; and that that is to be cut off, let it be cut off; and let the rest eat every one the flesh of another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/11/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbf33f01-d8bd-4efe-a6ff-478d76a80814>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: ZEC 11:10
Text: And I took my staff, even Beauty, and cut it asunder, that I might break my covenant which I had made with all the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/11/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:333c70b5-697c-4c44-902d-3d93fbcf5b20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: ZEC 11:11
Text: And it was broken in that day: and so the poor of the flock that waited upon me knew that it was the word of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/11/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be8f727c-1f8e-4c43-ba95-026a4c428834>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: ZEC 11:12
Text: And I said unto them, If ye think good, give me my price; and if not, forbear. So they weighed for my price thirty pieces of silver.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/11/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:785def90-441f-49ed-a6a8-1269fbc5b283>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: ZEC 11:13
Text: And the LORD said unto me, Cast it unto the potter: a goodly price that I was prised at of them. And I took the thirty pieces of silver, and cast them to the potter in the house of the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/11/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:583b6140-a3ef-4996-b528-bb0ec55d3e25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: ZEC 11:14
Text: Then I cut asunder mine other staff, even Bands, that I might break the brotherhood between Judah and Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/11/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:646fde14-b8d3-42e9-a65d-ff49febbf30e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: ZEC 11:15
Text: And the LORD said unto me, Take unto thee yet the instruments of a foolish shepherd.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/11/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09dc0139-8a16-4135-bd8c-c2d19bfc30b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 291

Reference: ZEC 11:16
Text: For, lo, I will raise up a shepherd in the land, which shall not visit those that be cut off, neither shall seek the young one, nor heal that that is broken, nor feed that that standeth still: but he shall eat the flesh of the fat, and tear their claws in pieces.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/11/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13f6fc31-33b0-4080-a473-0db00e0711de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: ZEC 11:17
Text: Woe to the idol shepherd that leaveth the flock! the sword shall be upon his arm, and upon his right eye: his arm shall be clean dried up, and his right eye shall be utterly darkened.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/12/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c51c3a6-2f5e-4d9c-9ea4-0585a384db9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: ZEC 12:1
Text: The burden of the word of the LORD for Israel, saith the LORD, which stretcheth forth the heavens, and layeth the foundation of the earth, and formeth the spirit of man within him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/12/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e47158ba-22a9-4a2c-ac7e-389daa95e69d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: ZEC 12:2
Text: Behold, I will make Jerusalem a cup of trembling unto all the people round about, when they shall be in the siege both against Judah and against Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/12/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1e7c3b8-2352-48ee-b092-fccc061325e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: ZEC 12:3
Text: And in that day will I make Jerusalem a burdensome stone for all people: all that burden themselves with it shall be cut in pieces, though all the people of the earth be gathered together against it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/12/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c80c49e8-2ee4-4abd-8a8a-7f4997842d51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: ZEC 12:4
Text: In that day, saith the LORD, I will smite every horse with astonishment, and his rider with madness: and I will open mine eyes upon the house of Judah, and will smite every horse of the people with blindness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/12/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c8b4ed8-c6f6-4227-b731-1294489a2bc3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: ZEC 12:5
Text: And the governors of Judah shall say in their heart, The inhabitants of Jerusalem shall be my strength in the LORD of hosts their God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/12/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:339cd781-c0e0-4117-9411-07719a7a193f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 310

Reference: ZEC 12:6
Text: In that day will I make the governors of Judah like an hearth of fire among the wood, and like a torch of fire in a sheaf; and they shall devour all the people round about, on the right hand and on the left: and Jerusalem shall be inhabited again in her own place, even in Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/12/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f68759a5-dd4a-4f5d-993d-f8d21a24a5ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: ZEC 12:7
Text: The LORD also shall save the tents of Judah first, that the glory of the house of David and the glory of the inhabitants of Jerusalem do not magnify themselves against Judah.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/12/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4882aaf4-4219-424a-bc4b-1eac79475ae2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: ZEC 12:8
Text: In that day shall the LORD defend the inhabitants of Jerusalem; and he that is feeble among them at that day shall be as David; and the house of David shall be as God, as the angel of the LORD before them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/12/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d63aebc5-f962-4506-a06e-0390c6765b19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: ZEC 12:9
Text: And it shall come to pass in that day, that I will seek to destroy all the nations that come against Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/12/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d78bc08-84f7-4ddc-a75e-27066330e122>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 349

Reference: ZEC 12:10
Text: And I will pour upon the house of David, and upon the inhabitants of Jerusalem, the spirit of grace and of supplications: and they shall look upon me whom they have pierced, and they shall mourn for him, as one mourneth for his only son, and shall be in bitterness for him, as one that is in bitterness for his firstborn.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/12/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d646318-2e44-434c-996f-49e2aa94b370>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: ZEC 12:11
Text: In that day shall there be a great mourning in Jerusalem, as the mourning of Hadadrimmon in the valley of Megiddon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/12/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf476690-dc8f-4081-ac62-c2bd69ec4154>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: ZEC 12:12
Text: And the land shall mourn, every family apart; the family of the house of David apart, and their wives apart; the family of the house of Nathan apart, and their wives apart;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/12/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0f25e2d-eeb5-4135-8981-d5c536c7d6d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: ZEC 12:13
Text: The family of the house of Levi apart, and their wives apart; the family of Shimei apart, and their wives apart;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/12/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ba23666-eb5f-4593-ad7b-9b6dd3a9dace>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: ZEC 12:14
Text: All the families that remain, every family apart, and their wives apart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/13/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8979b1a5-0f5e-47ce-9178-3abe71488c73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: ZEC 13:1
Text: In that day there shall be a fountain opened to the house of David and to the inhabitants of Jerusalem for sin and for uncleanness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/13/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4147a7ce-1c65-4160-a624-b50d15fab074>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: ZEC 13:2
Text: And it shall come to pass in that day, saith the LORD of hosts, that I will cut off the names of the idols out of the land, and they shall no more be remembered: and also I will cause the prophets and the unclean spirit to pass out of the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/13/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d386d08-02d0-47de-a23c-f4fbef28387e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 313

Reference: ZEC 13:3
Text: And it shall come to pass, that when any shall yet prophesy, then his father and his mother that begat him shall say unto him, Thou shalt not live; for thou speakest lies in the name of the LORD: and his father and his mother that begat him shall thrust him through when he prophesieth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/13/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76e29457-6576-4ea3-b40e-69416ba6bcd8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: ZEC 13:4
Text: And it shall come to pass in that day, that the prophets shall be ashamed every one of his vision, when he hath prophesied; neither shall they wear a rough garment to deceive:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/13/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80251b22-36cc-4e65-89bf-675b479dc898>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: ZEC 13:5
Text: But he shall say, I am no prophet, I am an husbandman; for man taught me to keep cattle from my youth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/13/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2abafc18-cbb9-4457-9715-c81c0e65ec0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: ZEC 13:6
Text: And one shall say unto him, What are these wounds in thine hands? Then he shall answer, Those with which I was wounded in the house of my friends.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/13/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f84882c9-a35c-45d3-9fbf-2cfaef528986>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: ZEC 13:7
Text: Awake, O sword, against my shepherd, and against the man that is my fellow, saith the LORD of hosts: smite the shepherd, and the sheep shall be scattered: and I will turn mine hand upon the little ones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/13/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36ce51de-18f3-4d26-9e05-0b414469c863>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: ZEC 13:8
Text: And it shall come to pass, that in all the land, saith the LORD, two parts therein shall be cut off and die; but the third shall be left therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/13/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1bfa2a49-e213-4ebe-b06d-ee75827951e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 274

Reference: ZEC 13:9
Text: And I will bring the third part through the fire, and will refine them as silver is refined, and will try them as gold is tried: they shall call on my name, and I will hear them: I will say, It is my people: and they shall say, The LORD is my God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/14/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c49348f2-6354-4c5a-98bd-345639757fc7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: ZEC 14:1
Text: Behold, the day of the LORD cometh, and thy spoil shall be divided in the midst of thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/14/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:842511b8-c18a-4411-9128-1cf6913c53c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 279

Reference: ZEC 14:2
Text: For I will gather all nations against Jerusalem to battle; and the city shall be taken, and the houses rifled, and the women ravished; and half of the city shall go forth into captivity, and the residue of the people shall not be cut off from the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/14/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d7323f0-3b3a-43fe-8bb3-a10ba11b1c21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: ZEC 14:3
Text: Then shall the LORD go forth, and fight against those nations, as when he fought in the day of battle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/14/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e46c48f6-4492-4444-b017-cc6ef6b01ff5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 352

Reference: ZEC 14:4
Text: And his feet shall stand in that day upon the mount of Olives, which is before Jerusalem on the east, and the mount of Olives shall cleave in the midst thereof toward the east and toward the west, and there shall be a very great valley; and half of the mountain shall remove toward the north, and half of it toward the south.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/14/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e585458-8049-4933-b5a7-74ada9afdc96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 293

Reference: ZEC 14:5
Text: And ye shall flee to the valley of the mountains; for the valley of the mountains shall reach unto Azal: yea, ye shall flee, like as ye fled from before the earthquake in the days of Uzziah king of Judah: and the LORD my God shall come, and all the saints with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/14/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d60b3be4-0972-473d-86f4-1b5e043635f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: ZEC 14:6
Text: And it shall come to pass in that day, that the light shall not be clear, nor dark:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/14/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3c0b5f0-7fd6-4644-a775-ac35b7e2813c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: ZEC 14:7
Text: But it shall be one day which shall be known to the LORD, not day, nor night: but it shall come to pass, that at evening time it shall be light.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/14/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46a3316e-8f08-4f16-8b91-2cd22a7bce30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: ZEC 14:8
Text: And it shall be in that day, that living waters shall go out from Jerusalem; half of them toward the former sea, and half of them toward the hinder sea: in summer and in winter shall it be.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/14/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea6a919e-4a05-4bf8-93dd-41728783b0fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: ZEC 14:9
Text: And the LORD shall be king over all the earth: in that day shall there be one LORD, and his name one.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/14/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:107622b8-d6dc-4018-a5e5-e79ccd4fc9fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 303

Reference: ZEC 14:10
Text: All the land shall be turned as a plain from Geba to Rimmon south of Jerusalem: and it shall be lifted up, and inhabited in her place, from Benjamin’s gate unto the place of the first gate, unto the corner gate, and from the tower of Hananeel unto the king’s winepresses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/14/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d12efdf-0c34-46c6-990e-e16dc93e1c56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: ZEC 14:11
Text: And men shall dwell in it, and there shall be no more utter destruction; but Jerusalem shall be safely inhabited.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/14/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca7f5c7a-b41e-417f-9206-66fadd9face2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 304

Reference: ZEC 14:12
Text: And this shall be the plague wherewith the LORD will smite all the people that have fought against Jerusalem; Their flesh shall consume away while they stand upon their feet, and their eyes shall consume away in their holes, and their tongue shall consume away in their mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/14/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91bf88d7-3de3-44c8-992c-177c874bf7fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: ZEC 14:13
Text: And it shall come to pass in that day, that a great tumult from the LORD shall be among them; and they shall lay hold every one on the hand of his neighbour, and his hand shall rise up against the hand of his neighbour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/14/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c21fe5f-e3d6-4881-a44a-2010ab7c6e1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: ZEC 14:14
Text: And Judah also shall fight at Jerusalem; and the wealth of all the heathen round about shall be gathered together, gold, and silver, and apparel, in great abundance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/14/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5e3c780-d870-47d5-95e5-f5dbfda3985a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: ZEC 14:15
Text: And so shall be the plague of the horse, of the mule, of the camel, and of the ass, and of all the beasts that shall be in these tents, as this plague.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/14/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a37440af-a68e-4496-a15e-44d936b006ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: ZEC 14:16
Text: And it shall come to pass, that every one that is left of all the nations which came against Jerusalem shall even go up from year to year to worship the King, the LORD of hosts, and to keep the feast of tabernacles.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/14/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fdf22774-b1ca-4786-99a4-55b5cee16c9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: ZEC 14:17
Text: And it shall be, that whoso will not come up of all the families of the earth unto Jerusalem to worship the King, the LORD of hosts, even upon them shall be no rain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/14/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59835b7d-2e54-4e96-81f0-5ea342a61c3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: ZEC 14:18
Text: And if the family of Egypt go not up, and come not, that have no rain; there shall be the plague, wherewith the LORD will smite the heathen that come not up to keep the feast of tabernacles.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/14/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3212fa3-737f-4ee8-9bd6-52c7e87fbe6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: ZEC 14:19
Text: This shall be the punishment of Egypt, and the punishment of all nations that come not up to keep the feast of tabernacles.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/14/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5e2b2d7-18a5-4ed7-8c1d-ff5f8d115bb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: ZEC 14:20
Text: In that day shall there be upon the bells of the horses, HOLINESS UNTO THE LORD; and the pots in the LORD’s house shall be like the bowls before the altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/ZEC/14/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29f56ae0-c0a3-43f8-b0b2-311f01a378da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: ZEC 14:21
Text: Yea, every pot in Jerusalem and in Judah shall be holiness unto the LORD of hosts: and all they that sacrifice shall come and take of them, and seethe therein: and in that day there shall be no more the Canaanite in the house of the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b18835a-bc60-4f10-94b1-675cff878556>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: MAL 1:1
Text: The burden of the word of the LORD to Israel by Malachi.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2cbdfab-5f9a-45dd-9cc4-856d58ec8085>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: MAL 1:2
Text: I have loved you, saith the LORD. Yet ye say, Wherein hast thou loved us? Was not Esau Jacob’s brother? saith the LORD: yet I loved Jacob,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4125972-7a1f-41f6-9855-f0189b557461>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: MAL 1:3
Text: And I hated Esau, and laid his mountains and his heritage waste for the dragons of the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e4e9ab9-a74a-4f80-b61f-263d3132c08b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 304

Reference: MAL 1:4
Text: Whereas Edom saith, We are impoverished, but we will return and build the desolate places; thus saith the LORD of hosts, They shall build, but I will throw down; and they shall call them, The border of wickedness, and, The people against whom the LORD hath indignation for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7bea5887-14a4-4ba7-86ce-51f6ef3ca2f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MAL 1:5
Text: And your eyes shall see, and ye shall say, The LORD will be magnified from the border of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f65298a2-9e82-4381-bc5f-5adc1419c05b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 278

Reference: MAL 1:6
Text: A son honoureth his father, and a servant his master: if then I be a father, where is mine honour? and if I be a master, where is my fear? saith the LORD of hosts unto you, O priests, that despise my name. And ye say, Wherein have we despised thy name?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75bdea4d-aaf0-44ed-a2b9-7258ce4fa78b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: MAL 1:7
Text: Ye offer polluted bread upon mine altar; and ye say, Wherein have we polluted thee? In that ye say, The table of the LORD is contemptible.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71320eb0-245a-4539-b8a4-f2d9413e3afa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: MAL 1:8
Text: And if ye offer the blind for sacrifice, is it not evil? and if ye offer the lame and sick, is it not evil? offer it now unto thy governor; will he be pleased with thee, or accept thy person? saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a4f5a64-730d-4e61-b8c9-afe954663e40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: MAL 1:9
Text: And now, I pray you, beseech God that he will be gracious unto us: this hath been by your means: will he regard your persons? saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4386651b-3bdd-4be4-93d3-01e0f68d2c5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: MAL 1:10
Text: Who is there even among you that would shut the doors for nought? neither do ye kindle fire on mine altar for nought. I have no pleasure in you, saith the LORD of hosts, neither will I accept an offering at your hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c870b386-c821-464c-8c9f-6ea4d644f10c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 287

Reference: MAL 1:11
Text: For from the rising of the sun even unto the going down of the same my name shall be great among the Gentiles; and in every place incense shall be offered unto my name, and a pure offering: for my name shall be great among the heathen, saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:902c1b79-5ff7-48b5-a655-697eba30186b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: MAL 1:12
Text: But ye have profaned it, in that ye say, The table of the LORD is polluted; and the fruit thereof, even his meat, is contemptible.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d93b0c61-d632-4169-a41e-039951f114bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: MAL 1:13
Text: Ye said also, Behold, what a weariness is it! and ye have snuffed at it, saith the LORD of hosts; and ye brought that which was torn, and the lame, and the sick; thus ye brought an offering: should I accept this of your hand? saith the LORD.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4689e2e0-2605-46ac-9fac-4720df208fc5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: MAL 1:14
Text: But cursed be the deceiver, which hath in his flock a male, and voweth, and sacrificeth unto the LORD a corrupt thing: for I am a great King, saith the LORD of hosts, and my name is dreadful among the heathen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18fa63d2-7624-4ac0-bc06-24341c62d271>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: MAL 2:1
Text: And now, O ye priests, this commandment is for you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8201de49-f4d3-48c3-a038-b3c3618c78a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: MAL 2:2
Text: If ye will not hear, and if ye will not lay it to heart, to give glory unto my name, saith the LORD of hosts, I will even send a curse upon you, and I will curse your blessings: yea, I have cursed them already, because ye do not lay it to heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5a3a2b6-62a2-44b1-aa14-e31dc5b03fad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: MAL 2:3
Text: Behold, I will corrupt your seed, and spread dung upon your faces, even the dung of your solemn feasts; and one shall take you away with it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b6728b4-79e4-4e0d-960f-eaa9d36d07dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: MAL 2:4
Text: And ye shall know that I have sent this commandment unto you, that my covenant might be with Levi, saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e65709ea-a9bf-4596-a30a-05d5a1d006d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: MAL 2:5
Text: My covenant was with him of life and peace; and I gave them to him for the fear wherewith he feared me, and was afraid before my name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f01ff328-29c9-40b2-9d3a-e07ced46c367>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: MAL 2:6
Text: The law of truth was in his mouth, and iniquity was not found in his lips: he walked with me in peace and equity, and did turn many away from iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41e3dda4-5e57-4382-9168-c41233daa36f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: MAL 2:7
Text: For the priest’s lips should keep knowledge, and they should seek the law at his mouth: for he is the messenger of the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b596c973-248c-487b-93ee-bff846273812>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: MAL 2:8
Text: But ye are departed out of the way; ye have caused many to stumble at the law; ye have corrupted the covenant of Levi, saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d88591c-a939-4c48-a502-27458942fc3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: MAL 2:9
Text: Therefore have I also made you contemptible and base before all the people, according as ye have not kept my ways, but have been partial in the law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc4ca235-9690-44f8-9889-b00f674c1d7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: MAL 2:10
Text: Have we not all one father? hath not one God created us? why do we deal treacherously every man against his brother, by profaning the covenant of our fathers?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:571d7a5f-2442-4795-8b73-a2332a3d5eff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: MAL 2:11
Text: Judah hath dealt treacherously, and an abomination is committed in Israel and in Jerusalem; for Judah hath profaned the holiness of the LORD which he loved, and hath married the daughter of a strange god.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72a4884e-a697-4040-ba6b-f401f5917995>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: MAL 2:12
Text: The LORD will cut off the man that doeth this, the master and the scholar, out of the tabernacles of Jacob, and him that offereth an offering unto the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3fc208f-5f80-4d87-9bb6-bf3066df09d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: MAL 2:13
Text: And this have ye done again, covering the altar of the LORD with tears, with weeping, and with crying out, insomuch that he regardeth not the offering any more, or receiveth it with good will at your hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9ceb5c6-8c04-49f9-9231-3104fb7b5d67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: MAL 2:14
Text: Yet ye say, Wherefore? Because the LORD hath been witness between thee and the wife of thy youth, against whom thou hast dealt treacherously: yet is she thy companion, and the wife of thy covenant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e3f6132-f4e8-4e1b-b4b6-dd3848c24a19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: MAL 2:15
Text: And did not he make one? Yet had he the residue of the spirit. And wherefore one? That he might seek a godly seed. Therefore take heed to your spirit, and let none deal treacherously against the wife of his youth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fdc2379d-e23e-4875-a2fc-e149c016a21f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: MAL 2:16
Text: For the LORD, the God of Israel, saith that he hateth putting away: for one covereth violence with his garment, saith the LORD of hosts: therefore take heed to your spirit, that ye deal not treacherously.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1eaa66dc-c616-4290-8ae5-c689da5d21c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: MAL 2:17
Text: Ye have wearied the LORD with your words. Yet ye say, Wherein have we wearied him? When ye say, Every one that doeth evil is good in the sight of the LORD, and he delighteth in them; or, Where is the God of judgment?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:caa3297f-9a63-43cb-aa7c-80f0d0ee05ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 266

Reference: MAL 3:1
Text: Behold, I will send my messenger, and he shall prepare the way before me: and the LORD, whom ye seek, shall suddenly come to his temple, even the messenger of the covenant, whom ye delight in: behold, he shall come, saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91602144-75cf-48fb-b5c8-f9c132b1e66d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: MAL 3:2
Text: But who may abide the day of his coming? and who shall stand when he appeareth? for he is like a refiner’s fire, and like fullers’ soap:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2dafb2b8-afe5-4ad6-9eb4-cc752a8f00a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: MAL 3:3
Text: And he shall sit as a refiner and purifier of silver: and he shall purify the sons of Levi, and purge them as gold and silver, that they may offer unto the LORD an offering in righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf0876c8-4877-47c1-a060-810929d986c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: MAL 3:4
Text: Then shall the offering of Judah and Jerusalem be pleasant unto the LORD, as in the days of old, and as in former years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2210e8b1-01b3-492a-b26b-0e4cc93ba443>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 355

Reference: MAL 3:5
Text: And I will come near to you to judgment; and I will be a swift witness against the sorcerers, and against the adulterers, and against false swearers, and against those that oppress the hireling in his wages, the widow, and the fatherless, and that turn aside the stranger from his right, and fear not me, saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:027218be-e282-405f-8f26-f8b4369e8daa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: MAL 3:6
Text: For I am the LORD, I change not; therefore ye sons of Jacob are not consumed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd156c20-a09b-4c0f-b412-38cc1df6021f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: MAL 3:7
Text: Even from the days of your fathers ye are gone away from mine ordinances, and have not kept them. Return unto me, and I will return unto you, saith the LORD of hosts. But ye said, Wherein shall we return?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:418d35f3-7f8d-46d9-9177-3c3da0dd745f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: MAL 3:8
Text: Will a man rob God? Yet ye have robbed me. But ye say, Wherein have we robbed thee? In tithes and offerings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bf3a94e-86f4-4e86-9e1e-016f6d87a4cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: MAL 3:9
Text: Ye are cursed with a curse: for ye have robbed me, even this whole nation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d1abd0f-b9d1-4d8c-b22c-58a2f1c1d2ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 287

Reference: MAL 3:10
Text: Bring ye all the tithes into the storehouse, that there may be meat in mine house, and prove me now herewith, saith the LORD of hosts, if I will not open you the windows of heaven, and pour you out a blessing, that there shall not be room enough to receive it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5274165-1fc0-4dfd-8fe6-7c6294f4baa2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: MAL 3:11
Text: And I will rebuke the devourer for your sakes, and he shall not destroy the fruits of your ground; neither shall your vine cast her fruit before the time in the field, saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:891da90f-6656-4750-842f-ace1f4b6dc70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: MAL 3:12
Text: And all nations shall call you blessed: for ye shall be a delightsome land, saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4bf5ecf-d480-4b8f-bb9d-bb3a9b27a027>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: MAL 3:13
Text: Your words have been stout against me, saith the LORD. Yet ye say, What have we spoken so much against thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57c87a45-1e36-49c5-98f1-ae6c8f0aea5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: MAL 3:14
Text: Ye have said, It is vain to serve God: and what profit is it that we have kept his ordinance, and that we have walked mournfully before the LORD of hosts?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c07a0bfb-a351-480f-a1a5-0bab66089be8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: MAL 3:15
Text: And now we call the proud happy; yea, they that work wickedness are set up; yea, they that tempt God are even delivered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ae97dd7-71ba-4adb-8ce5-4cbe053ce829>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: MAL 3:16
Text: Then they that feared the LORD spake often one to another: and the LORD hearkened, and heard it, and a book of remembrance was written before him for them that feared the LORD, and that thought upon his name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:104d9b5d-73aa-48d0-b61a-e26f1a0bcc7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: MAL 3:17
Text: And they shall be mine, saith the LORD of hosts, in that day when I make up my jewels; and I will spare them, as a man spareth his own son that serveth him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:157e5e18-73a0-42c8-8f58-bb13879c03cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: MAL 3:18
Text: Then shall ye return, and discern between the righteous and the wicked, between him that serveth God and him that serveth him not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c0de246-7a8a-4a78-8fa4-252d36f7bbe1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: MAL 4:1
Text: For, behold, the day cometh, that shall burn as an oven; and all the proud, yea, and all that do wickedly, shall be stubble: and the day that cometh shall burn them up, saith the LORD of hosts, that it shall leave them neither root nor branch.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e790a6df-7b52-4cd5-a2eb-3ad84a745486>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: MAL 4:2
Text: But unto you that fear my name shall the Sun of righteousness arise with healing in his wings; and ye shall go forth, and grow up as calves of the stall.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cceee002-8f54-42a6-ab4a-1d070127d74a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: MAL 4:3
Text: And ye shall tread down the wicked; for they shall be ashes under the soles of your feet in the day that I shall do this, saith the LORD of hosts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c299253a-3830-4095-b569-a3b11740474c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MAL 4:4
Text: Remember ye the law of Moses my servant, which I commanded unto him in Horeb for all Israel, with the statutes and judgments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5867b972-1c63-497c-a60d-a208b44382bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: MAL 4:5
Text: Behold, I will send you Elijah the prophet before the coming of the great and dreadful day of the LORD:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAL/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80586e54-a1af-41c1-aab2-e282405ba2cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: MAL 4:6
Text: And he shall turn the heart of the fathers to the children, and the heart of the children to their fathers, lest I come and smite the earth with a curse.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e3604ed-26ec-4f78-a51f-11404c0b6817>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: MAT 1:1
Text: The book of the generation of Jesus Christ, the son of David, the son of Abraham.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d925a38-9f0d-4433-ab6b-62d3a3282aea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: MAT 1:2
Text: Abraham begat Isaac; and Isaac begat Jacob; and Jacob begat Judas and his brethren;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17195067-9adf-4bac-8b34-885888dfdcc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MAT 1:3
Text: And Judas begat Phares and Zara of Thamar; and Phares begat Esrom; and Esrom begat Aram;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fdff07d1-206e-47d7-b1d8-0d40901854c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: MAT 1:4
Text: And Aram begat Aminadab; and Aminadab begat Naasson; and Naasson begat Salmon;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69ae50b4-cfd0-4a34-8ea0-bcecc3c74a4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: MAT 1:5
Text: And Salmon begat Booz of Rachab; and Booz begat Obed of Ruth; and Obed begat Jesse;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fea37be-b4b4-452b-b0ab-a138417556e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: MAT 1:6
Text: And Jesse begat David the king; and David the king begat Solomon of her that had been the wife of Urias;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ae60b66-08ae-4bd5-8ba0-deb20197c598>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: MAT 1:7
Text: And Solomon begat Roboam; and Roboam begat Abia; and Abia begat Asa;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5a7ee7e-2be1-46e3-b98e-8ff02d561dc1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: MAT 1:8
Text: And Asa begat Josaphat; and Josaphat begat Joram; and Joram begat Ozias;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2ce2489-474c-4502-97a7-dc50f367e114>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: MAT 1:9
Text: And Ozias begat Joatham; and Joatham begat Achaz; and Achaz begat Ezekias;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:726430d3-ba95-4867-8877-992c1650fef4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: MAT 1:10
Text: And Ezekias begat Manasses; and Manasses begat Amon; and Amon begat Josias;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f62426c2-3cca-4724-ad2d-ad7945565671>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: MAT 1:11
Text: And Josias begat Jechonias and his brethren, about the time they were carried away to Babylon:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ff76875-2bff-4c30-bd16-c83aeb354729>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: MAT 1:12
Text: And after they were brought to Babylon, Jechonias begat Salathiel; and Salathiel begat Zorobabel;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:434069d9-7b90-4098-8c22-21f46c03bca2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: MAT 1:13
Text: And Zorobabel begat Abiud; and Abiud begat Eliakim; and Eliakim begat Azor;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b6e71bc-7dd3-4db9-b3c1-5ff11359111e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: MAT 1:14
Text: And Azor begat Sadoc; and Sadoc begat Achim; and Achim begat Eliud;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:329e504d-0434-4ad0-b51c-118be995aca2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: MAT 1:15
Text: And Eliud begat Eleazar; and Eleazar begat Matthan; and Matthan begat Jacob;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:642bf845-7212-4e0f-94ce-3c3dd1f4e4dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: MAT 1:16
Text: And Jacob begat Joseph the husband of Mary, of whom was born Jesus, who is called Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:644a85b8-5828-4965-8ef8-272c73988f2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: MAT 1:17
Text: So all the generations from Abraham to David are fourteen generations; and from David until the carrying away into Babylon are fourteen generations; and from the carrying away into Babylon unto Christ are fourteen generations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7717ce0-1f40-4d5c-9312-2a9590a12b45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: MAT 1:18
Text: Now the birth of Jesus Christ was on this wise: When as his mother Mary was espoused to Joseph, before they came together, she was found with child of the Holy Ghost.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d02c76f-2dc9-4a17-96e3-3d24c5e068ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: MAT 1:19
Text: Then Joseph her husband, being a just man, and not willing to make her a publick example, was minded to put her away privily.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e2b4727-011a-4cb6-9974-09d116d4afd1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: MAT 1:20
Text: But while he thought on these things, behold, the angel of the LORD appeared unto him in a dream, saying, Joseph, thou son of David, fear not to take unto thee Mary thy wife: for that which is conceived in her is of the Holy Ghost.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:740a9d14-e78d-4c7f-b1bc-bf559b886ddd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: MAT 1:21
Text: And she shall bring forth a son, and thou shalt call his name JESUS: for he shall save his people from their sins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd53891a-f28a-4fa6-b07d-7afac1e90771>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: MAT 1:22
Text: Now all this was done, that it might be fulfilled which was spoken of the Lord by the prophet, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:334bb1b1-d176-49a8-82e7-b75d7faccdaa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: MAT 1:23
Text: Behold, a virgin shall be with child, and shall bring forth a son, and they shall call his name Emmanuel, which being interpreted is, God with us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2fbe0cf-2c31-49d7-84de-17f55c4ca22d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: MAT 1:24
Text: Then Joseph being raised from sleep did as the angel of the Lord had bidden him, and took unto him his wife:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/1/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57ce3ce4-d2da-40af-95c4-29934692b2be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: MAT 1:25
Text: And knew her not till she had brought forth her firstborn son: and he called his name JESUS.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b8d9a38-941d-4670-bd96-e2fa58831b4f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: MAT 2:1
Text: Now when Jesus was born in Bethlehem of Judaea in the days of Herod the king, behold, there came wise men from the east to Jerusalem,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87f16661-a237-43b7-a3cc-7d992974c4cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: MAT 2:2
Text: Saying, Where is he that is born King of the Jews? for we have seen his star in the east, and are come to worship him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0a00db8-cfef-4928-bbb3-f99d4814f02b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MAT 2:3
Text: When Herod the king had heard these things, he was troubled, and all Jerusalem with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:291d26c1-dd78-4a02-bce1-0ced6a233111>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: MAT 2:4
Text: And when he had gathered all the chief priests and scribes of the people together, he demanded of them where Christ should be born.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:496f62e5-3930-4033-81b4-d727337048d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: MAT 2:5
Text: And they said unto him, In Bethlehem of Judaea: for thus it is written by the prophet,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f346dc28-09f5-4406-9293-198b9f0c12be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: MAT 2:6
Text: And thou Bethlehem, in the land of Juda, art not the least among the princes of Juda: for out of thee shall come a Governor, that shall rule my people Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df93d7a6-f23a-4aba-96c7-13539bb05ba5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: MAT 2:7
Text: Then Herod, when he had privily called the wise men, enquired of them diligently what time the star appeared.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:027fee62-690d-4f75-b1ab-b2471067dd0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: MAT 2:8
Text: And he sent them to Bethlehem, and said, Go and search diligently for the young child; and when ye have found him, bring me word again, that I may come and worship him also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f552c9da-94bd-415f-a9e9-b1d4313450bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: MAT 2:9
Text: When they had heard the king, they departed; and, lo, the star, which they saw in the east, went before them, till it came and stood over where the young child was.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92bb5750-7c4e-4c2e-b84a-67fe8c8ea30f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: MAT 2:10
Text: When they saw the star, they rejoiced with exceeding great joy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6146bb69-cfd3-41a8-8ef3-1267749c186b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: MAT 2:11
Text: And when they were come into the house, they saw the young child with Mary his mother, and fell down, and worshipped him: and when they had opened their treasures, they presented unto him gifts; gold, and frankincense and myrrh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fc37f88-7bf0-4ac2-8efb-a415d676e430>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: MAT 2:12
Text: And being warned of God in a dream that they should not return to Herod, they departed into their own country another way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:144fa741-38d2-4a75-8b7a-8e985cbf7b1e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 289

Reference: MAT 2:13
Text: And when they were departed, behold, the angel of the Lord appeareth to Joseph in a dream, saying, Arise, and take the young child and his mother, and flee into Egypt, and be thou there until I bring thee word: for Herod will seek the young child to destroy him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9c0f5ab-6ec4-4530-8dc5-df5d6a01bb87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: MAT 2:14
Text: When he arose, he took the young child and his mother by night, and departed into Egypt:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df796c02-14a6-4cec-b157-f1799dfeba6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: MAT 2:15
Text: And was there until the death of Herod: that it might be fulfilled which was spoken of the Lord by the prophet, saying, Out of Egypt have I called my son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7793e851-becf-485a-8278-5bf1fddcf72c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 306

Reference: MAT 2:16
Text: Then Herod, when he saw that he was mocked of the wise men, was exceeding wroth, and sent forth, and slew all the children that were in Bethlehem, and in all the coasts thereof, from two years old and under, according to the time which he had diligently enquired of the wise men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:199a44b1-bd54-4f18-91ba-cda832b40370>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: MAT 2:17
Text: Then was fulfilled that which was spoken by Jeremy the prophet, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:245d0f16-f053-4a87-9023-d00ff1785a77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: MAT 2:18
Text: In Rama was there a voice heard, lamentation, and weeping, and great mourning, Rachel weeping for her children, and would not be comforted, because they are not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef6d22b6-ac8b-4860-b41b-cbaf855edf61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: MAT 2:19
Text: But when Herod was dead, behold, an angel of the Lord appeareth in a dream to Joseph in Egypt,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:479d859e-b4b0-4c4e-97f3-b1604a7c77d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: MAT 2:20
Text: Saying, Arise, and take the young child and his mother, and go into the land of Israel: for they are dead which sought the young child’s life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb618dd8-df9e-4391-9a71-10ee4107a0d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: MAT 2:21
Text: And he arose, and took the young child and his mother, and came into the land of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2642b784-f9b6-4ce0-8b13-dea6370c4b8e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: MAT 2:22
Text: But when he heard that Archelaus did reign in Judaea in the room of his father Herod, he was afraid to go thither: notwithstanding, being warned of God in a dream, he turned aside into the parts of Galilee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/2/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b012490-2dd6-40f8-9788-616f4aaef9e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: MAT 2:23
Text: And he came and dwelt in a city called Nazareth: that it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the prophets, He shall be called a Nazarene.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8a6429a-c243-4d7a-bfc4-24f159053391>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: MAT 3:1
Text: In those days came John the Baptist, preaching in the wilderness of Judaea,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae3135a8-e4f8-49b6-ac91-60c5223028a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: MAT 3:2
Text: And saying, Repent ye: for the kingdom of heaven is at hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5191703-bc84-4e18-bcf8-8fc73a057b0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: MAT 3:3
Text: For this is he that was spoken of by the prophet Esaias, saying, The voice of one crying in the wilderness, Prepare ye the way of the Lord, make his paths straight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a393bd6-45b6-4bcb-a6e9-32714678d096>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: MAT 3:4
Text: And the same John had his raiment of camel’s hair, and a leathern girdle about his loins; and his meat was locusts and wild honey.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e85d985-e698-48bd-89b2-f10de27ebd76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: MAT 3:5
Text: Then went out to him Jerusalem, and all Judaea, and all the region round about Jordan,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7a4490b-5869-4894-8e98-4515553700ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: MAT 3:6
Text: And were baptized of him in Jordan, confessing their sins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ee06531-85f5-45dc-a620-29748480b746>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: MAT 3:7
Text: But when he saw many of the Pharisees and Sadducees come to his baptism, he said unto them, O generation of vipers, who hath warned you to flee from the wrath to come?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9099f647-398a-438e-8b97-7351f39c9e92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: MAT 3:8
Text: Bring forth therefore fruits meet for repentance:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45f37413-0316-4a47-b697-448a98f783f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: MAT 3:9
Text: And think not to say within yourselves, We have Abraham to our father: for I say unto you, that God is able of these stones to raise up children unto Abraham.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:677f2d33-7803-4580-9a27-d1ac7a002847>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: MAT 3:10
Text: And now also the axe is laid unto the root of the trees: therefore every tree which bringeth not forth good fruit is hewn down, and cast into the fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f8dd237-2c45-48cf-aedb-801e2b960f66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: MAT 3:11
Text: I indeed baptize you with water unto repentance. but he that cometh after me is mightier than I, whose shoes I am not worthy to bear: he shall baptize you with the Holy Ghost, and with fire:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a83b921b-abb3-46fb-b669-1c5703e63c27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: MAT 3:12
Text: Whose fan is in his hand, and he will throughly purge his floor, and gather his wheat into the garner; but he will burn up the chaff with unquenchable fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7c3fd48-18bc-4860-90dc-036903db2059>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: MAT 3:13
Text: Then cometh Jesus from Galilee to Jordan unto John, to be baptized of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2f130ea-58f6-4da4-8769-f26c9759c471>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MAT 3:14
Text: But John forbad him, saying, I have need to be baptized of thee, and comest thou to me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:429223d8-719a-4cd7-8488-3624eff2c52b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: MAT 3:15
Text: And Jesus answering said unto him, Suffer it to be so now: for thus it becometh us to fulfil all righteousness. Then he suffered him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c48c9e0-ca7b-468e-97ea-d0616f815838>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: MAT 3:16
Text: And Jesus, when he was baptized, went up straightway out of the water: and, lo, the heavens were opened unto him, and he saw the Spirit of God descending like a dove, and lighting upon him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63045960-39ec-4e1c-b063-65a02cfd82cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: MAT 3:17
Text: And lo a voice from heaven, saying, This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a260c034-026c-4ec1-b898-8de264f2c6c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: MAT 4:1
Text: Then was Jesus led up of the spirit into the wilderness to be tempted of the devil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:176332e9-3c67-4a96-8f8e-e1e9a5c9d726>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: MAT 4:2
Text: And when he had fasted forty days and forty nights, he was afterward an hungred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4a1a870-bfb7-4c76-bd62-4240fafec283>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: MAT 4:3
Text: And when the tempter came to him, he said, If thou be the Son of God, command that these stones be made bread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b93dd0ed-eb57-4ea4-9549-32e4b8c80606>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: MAT 4:4
Text: But he answered and said, It is written, Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that proceedeth out of the mouth of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:637b9485-7635-4c4b-b5f2-889936d0b4ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: MAT 4:5
Text: Then the devil taketh him up into the holy city, and setteth him on a pinnacle of the temple,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f225b4a-d4da-4076-b0c3-84ca983b9fb9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: MAT 4:6
Text: And saith unto him, If thou be the Son of God, cast thyself down: for it is written, He shall give his angels charge concerning thee: and in their hands they shall bear thee up, lest at any time thou dash thy foot against a stone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90251963-5f6f-4dcd-9bb8-0bb02227c731>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: MAT 4:7
Text: Jesus said unto him, It is written again, Thou shalt not tempt the Lord thy God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f626aa3-f926-4886-8715-5227c8900500>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: MAT 4:8
Text: Again, the devil taketh him up into an exceeding high mountain, and sheweth him all the kingdoms of the world, and the glory of them;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d861a86a-e73f-4bd1-9fd9-08146b66e5a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: MAT 4:9
Text: And saith unto him, All these things will I give thee, if thou wilt fall down and worship me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bbe9fb6f-19e2-4ecd-aa28-45c7cd9d1edf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: MAT 4:10
Text: Then saith Jesus unto him, Get thee hence, Satan: for it is written, Thou shalt worship the Lord thy God, and him only shalt thou serve.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:369071a0-f68c-47c5-add5-0e9b9f34ab8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: MAT 4:11
Text: Then the devil leaveth him, and, behold, angels came and ministered unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ff31605-892f-4a05-9629-524e26771bf0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: MAT 4:12
Text: Now when Jesus had heard that John was cast into prison, he departed into Galilee;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7aede0d-d110-431a-a3c3-3b64b19db42d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MAT 4:13
Text: And leaving Nazareth, he came and dwelt in Capernaum, which is upon the sea coast, in the borders of Zabulon and Nephthalim:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:efb3b20d-dc5c-4c44-a771-f7da8976269e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: MAT 4:14
Text: That it might be fulfilled which was spoken by Esaias the prophet, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db6839b2-cf1f-4202-8f16-36d03654c93d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MAT 4:15
Text: The land of Zabulon, and the land of Nephthalim, by the way of the sea, beyond Jordan, Galilee of the Gentiles;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73c41ee2-6869-4706-b0bc-65b979732ef0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: MAT 4:16
Text: The people which sat in darkness saw great light; and to them which sat in the region and shadow of death light is sprung up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a99cdfc-a161-4c5b-8001-604160a0cd96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MAT 4:17
Text: From that time Jesus began to preach, and to say, Repent: for the kingdom of heaven is at hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:738f9caa-88fc-46f4-bec3-6253f63447d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: MAT 4:18
Text: And Jesus, walking by the sea of Galilee, saw two brethren, Simon called Peter, and Andrew his brother, casting a net into the sea: for they were fishers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26b8a28e-fd89-43fc-8980-c2df5f7a9a88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: MAT 4:19
Text: And he saith unto them, Follow me, and I will make you fishers of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3c72f9c-e27f-45f6-bacb-505d76cf96cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: MAT 4:20
Text: And they straightway left their nets, and followed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e64c4485-6ab3-4068-98ae-f5ab99379a2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: MAT 4:21
Text: And going on from thence, he saw other two brethren, James the son of Zebedee, and John his brother, in a ship with Zebedee their father, mending their nets; and he called them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f325e8a8-2c77-4e5f-a88c-40b409df8ff2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: MAT 4:22
Text: And they immediately left the ship and their father, and followed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77ac910e-9732-45b8-8906-878a6469abfe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: MAT 4:23
Text: And Jesus went about all Galilee, teaching in their synagogues, and preaching the gospel of the kingdom, and healing all manner of sickness and all manner of disease among the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:162df34e-cc52-44a6-a8fc-c2bfdae7fe14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: MAT 4:24
Text: And his fame went throughout all Syria: and they brought unto him all sick people that were taken with divers diseases and torments, and those which were possessed with devils, and those which were lunatick, and those that had the palsy; and he healed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/4/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0058f15b-c33b-48d9-bc01-a6c8e17ddb6d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: MAT 4:25
Text: And there followed him great multitudes of people from Galilee, and from Decapolis, and from Jerusalem, and from Judaea, and from beyond Jordan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c888e2b8-838f-4728-b9d8-9da50fa103b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: MAT 5:1
Text: And seeing the multitudes, he went up into a mountain: and when he was set, his disciples came unto him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e05fd90-fa82-45f9-ba55-c6617158ea56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: MAT 5:2
Text: And he opened his mouth, and taught them, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f991866c-dc26-4dd2-885a-62b49faaad6d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: MAT 5:3
Text: Blessed are the poor in spirit: for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:372ff6b0-404e-4f98-87e0-e489993ce70e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: MAT 5:4
Text: Blessed are they that mourn: for they shall be comforted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15ec7a9c-35a7-4e85-b927-999e968b4f06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: MAT 5:5
Text: Blessed are the meek: for they shall inherit the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:841eb857-97da-4537-a9a5-1b119c11e8dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: MAT 5:6
Text: Blessed are they which do hunger and thirst after righteousness: for they shall be filled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4171fa41-0ea8-4f75-8d13-720cd7b03ef3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: MAT 5:7
Text: Blessed are the merciful: for they shall obtain mercy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d0f2fb9-3d99-43da-97a6-f2efffa49e27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: MAT 5:8
Text: Blessed are the pure in heart: for they shall see God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c0934b2-2da0-433e-b031-1f685a650953>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: MAT 5:9
Text: Blessed are the peacemakers: for they shall be called the children of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d776df67-dbba-43c0-9259-6a5ba62adedf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: MAT 5:10
Text: Blessed are they which are persecuted for righteousness’ sake: for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4807d2a-85a0-4725-b836-6e9f1df43403>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: MAT 5:11
Text: Blessed are ye, when men shall revile you, and persecute you, and shall say all manner of evil against you falsely, for my sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b34662ae-5482-4678-99e1-7ad5fa6c2d0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: MAT 5:12
Text: Rejoice, and be exceeding glad: for great is your reward in heaven: for so persecuted they the prophets which were before you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db4fbcd5-2087-420b-b579-51b0e4bec286>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: MAT 5:13
Text: Ye are the salt of the earth: but if the salt have lost his savour, wherewith shall it be salted? it is thenceforth good for nothing, but to be cast out, and to be trodden under foot of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:878136b3-a2f3-4518-95ea-cbf209af4bf5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: MAT 5:14
Text: Ye are the light of the world. A city that is set on an hill cannot be hid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4598362-0c4c-49ab-804b-b17c624d3d43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: MAT 5:15
Text: Neither do men light a candle, and put it under a bushel, but on a candlestick; and it giveth light unto all that are in the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab1ca982-d30e-4632-8396-f70680d08101>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: MAT 5:16
Text: Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb9d21ac-0589-4fe5-88da-a8706f25a033>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: MAT 5:17
Text: Think not that I am come to destroy the law, or the prophets: I am not come to destroy, but to fulfil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33d510dc-d9e5-49ed-a679-8335123995cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: MAT 5:18
Text: For verily I say unto you, Till heaven and earth pass, one jot or one tittle shall in no wise pass from the law, till all be fulfilled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33161a62-4073-42de-b34b-f6f2b798a6c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 266

Reference: MAT 5:19
Text: Whosoever therefore shall break one of these least commandments, and shall teach men so, he shall be called the least in the kingdom of heaven: but whosoever shall do and teach them, the same shall be called great in the kingdom of heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3fa411b8-edf4-4a3d-ae4a-82a8d4944d3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: MAT 5:20
Text: For I say unto you, That except your righteousness shall exceed the righteousness of the scribes and Pharisees, ye shall in no case enter into the kingdom of heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d2e1093-86dd-437e-9c16-fbb908230835>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: MAT 5:21
Text: Ye have heard that it was said by them of old time, Thou shalt not kill; and whosoever shall kill shall be in danger of the judgment:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cca4f00a-dd08-421c-b965-0d28c73cf401>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 289

Reference: MAT 5:22
Text: But I say unto you, That whosoever is angry with his brother without a cause shall be in danger of the judgment: and whosoever shall say to his brother, Raca, shall be in danger of the council: but whosoever shall say, Thou fool, shall be in danger of hell fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd1c1624-b434-4b74-83fa-79b1e8dbef5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: MAT 5:23
Text: Therefore if thou bring thy gift to the altar, and there rememberest that thy brother hath ought against thee;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa46575f-0ff0-4144-9e72-cf92e012f310>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MAT 5:24
Text: Leave there thy gift before the altar, and go thy way; first be reconciled to thy brother, and then come and offer thy gift.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8525edbe-d36c-46fa-8b0c-db4b465cba96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: MAT 5:25
Text: Agree with thine adversary quickly, whiles thou art in the way with him; lest at any time the adversary deliver thee to the judge, and the judge deliver thee to the officer, and thou be cast into prison.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8f43f84-e6b5-4d03-bfac-17152b32917f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: MAT 5:26
Text: Verily I say unto thee, Thou shalt by no means come out thence, till thou hast paid the uttermost farthing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37b03efa-d673-49e9-8567-2bf05164a47a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: MAT 5:27
Text: Ye have heard that it was said by them of old time, Thou shalt not commit adultery:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d051f67d-5c9e-4cf1-8176-e53015d01e24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: MAT 5:28
Text: But I say unto you, That whosoever looketh on a woman to lust after her hath committed adultery with her already in his heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7b63442-ebb5-4092-b564-24bffe40a65a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: MAT 5:29
Text: And if thy right eye offend thee, pluck it out, and cast it from thee: for it is profitable for thee that one of thy members should perish, and not that thy whole body should be cast into hell.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ccc7f8ad-ea96-473f-b274-42d33867fee3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: MAT 5:30
Text: And if thy right hand offend thee, cut it off, and cast it from thee: for it is profitable for thee that one of thy members should perish, and not that thy whole body should be cast into hell.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe3c2fc4-efbe-4f31-b4d5-9c2946b2f35c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: MAT 5:31
Text: It hath been said, Whosoever shall put away his wife, let him give her a writing of divorcement:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b82731bb-c31a-4335-baf6-98274f9e11bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: MAT 5:32
Text: But I say unto you, That whosoever shall put away his wife, saving for the cause of fornication, causeth her to commit adultery: and whosoever shall marry her that is divorced committeth adultery.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57c57bcc-708d-454a-adf0-2db0c39c8d27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: MAT 5:33
Text: Again, ye have heard that it hath been said by them of old time, Thou shalt not forswear thyself, but shalt perform unto the Lord thine oaths:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b8eadfd-4b37-4627-83d2-39dffdf23c25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: MAT 5:34
Text: But I say unto you, Swear not at all; neither by heaven; for it is God’s throne:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9f0ea71-61c1-4b23-bf33-89e1e8a458b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: MAT 5:35
Text: Nor by the earth; for it is his footstool: neither by Jerusalem; for it is the city of the great King.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f259f27-0e2d-4d4e-80bb-d70eaf4c6e1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MAT 5:36
Text: Neither shalt thou swear by thy head, because thou canst not make one hair white or black.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e5c3c23-58f9-44c6-8a2e-49bdceed09a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: MAT 5:37
Text: But let your communication be, Yea, yea; Nay, nay: for whatsoever is more than these cometh of evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3acbe31e-b4f2-4f54-9e4a-c8b0888cdad3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: MAT 5:38
Text: Ye have heard that it hath been said, An eye for an eye, and a tooth for a tooth:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0389ee83-2039-4b78-9dc9-c238e33fd338>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: MAT 5:39
Text: But I say unto you, That ye resist not evil: but whosoever shall smite thee on thy right cheek, turn to him the other also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d0779f7-0177-4e86-8dce-1dd25c0e3fd8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: MAT 5:40
Text: And if any man will sue thee at the law, and take away thy coat, let him have thy cloak also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3068e74a-62b6-4951-aeed-63a4819dca6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: MAT 5:41
Text: And whosoever shall compel thee to go a mile, go with him twain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:affb0543-51e5-4ac6-ae70-5ce8813c0ad0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: MAT 5:42
Text: Give to him that asketh thee, and from him that would borrow of thee turn not thou away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51c8aa8d-19b6-4dd5-bb5d-7ce3240d90f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MAT 5:43
Text: Ye have heard that it hath been said, Thou shalt love thy neighbour, and hate thine enemy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d34d2113-81fd-4a57-97f4-758da3c5d1fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: MAT 5:44
Text: But I say unto you, Love your enemies, bless them that curse you, do good to them that hate you, and pray for them which despitefully use you, and persecute you;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d58ae844-a79c-4a9b-a389-e7067444c8d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: MAT 5:45
Text: That ye may be the children of your Father which is in heaven: for he maketh his sun to rise on the evil and on the good, and sendeth rain on the just and on the unjust.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:efbe6503-4582-40a4-a044-d3676b7aa5f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: MAT 5:46
Text: For if ye love them which love you, what reward have ye? do not even the publicans the same?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9dd0082-70ab-4c1c-968e-e1bc64a53d4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MAT 5:47
Text: And if ye salute your brethren only, what do ye more than others? do not even the publicans so?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/5/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:309c74f7-183d-4842-88c2-342aa5f9c061>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: MAT 5:48
Text: Be ye therefore perfect, even as your Father which is in heaven is perfect.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c521272c-c985-489c-a674-f76eb16b7919>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: MAT 6:1
Text: Take heed that ye do not your alms before men, to be seen of them: otherwise ye have no reward of your Father which is in heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:612fe8fb-7ccf-4601-a4b7-27c64c561aa1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: MAT 6:2
Text: Therefore when thou doest thine alms, do not sound a trumpet before thee, as the hypocrites do in the synagogues and in the streets, that they may have glory of men. Verily I say unto you, They have their reward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b498a469-e846-4d95-84e7-e7ea9013dcd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: MAT 6:3
Text: But when thou doest alms, let not thy left hand know what thy right hand doeth:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d9e7f98-beed-4718-ba79-7adaca2cbf40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: MAT 6:4
Text: That thine alms may be in secret: and thy Father which seeth in secret himself shall reward thee openly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce74b126-27b1-497b-b528-5ec2702435ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: MAT 6:5
Text: And when thou prayest, thou shalt not be as the hypocrites are: for they love to pray standing in the synagogues and in the corners of the streets, that they may be seen of men. Verily I say unto you, They have their reward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c45609fd-42aa-4542-ba62-f871f69565c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: MAT 6:6
Text: But thou, when thou prayest, enter into thy closet, and when thou hast shut thy door, pray to thy Father which is in secret; and thy Father which seeth in secret shall reward thee openly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9cce274f-cccc-4503-9871-d4916c3626dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: MAT 6:7
Text: But when ye pray, use not vain repetitions, as the heathen do: for they think that they shall be heard for their much speaking.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c925d28f-5f27-4638-b324-6a67d01a8de0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: MAT 6:8
Text: Be not ye therefore like unto them: for your Father knoweth what things ye have need of, before ye ask him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7db17e1-802d-4b55-9e6a-a1a6dc113566>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: MAT 6:9
Text: After this manner therefore pray ye: Our Father which art in heaven, Hallowed be thy name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfbc463c-16bd-43f1-8115-e8bcbd690b28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: MAT 6:10
Text: Thy kingdom come, Thy will be done in earth, as it is in heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db4c4fee-8f3e-4d2f-acb9-b9c4bf7175a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 60

Reference: MAT 6:11
Text: Give us this day our daily bread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e975779-94c3-4c65-a172-9897dc23c2f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: MAT 6:12
Text: And forgive us our debts, as we forgive our debtors.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a56e151-c38c-415a-a4e7-8a5876094613>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: MAT 6:13
Text: And lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from evil: For thine is the kingdom, and the power, and the glory, for ever. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9492c25e-acbd-4d29-a877-85362c15d328>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: MAT 6:14
Text: For if ye forgive men their trespasses, your heavenly Father will also forgive you:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26ce21a8-d155-4559-a76a-6728b6d2fae2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: MAT 6:15
Text: But if ye forgive not men their trespasses, neither will your Father forgive your trespasses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e659f06a-49fa-4049-885b-63a7d7b79df7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: MAT 6:16
Text: Moreover when ye fast, be not, as the hypocrites, of a sad countenance: for they disfigure their faces, that they may appear unto men to fast. Verily I say unto you, They have their reward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:728443ba-2230-47a9-82ff-991007f67ffb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: MAT 6:17
Text: But thou, when thou fastest, anoint thine head, and wash thy face;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e68808a9-bd39-430b-bab6-f36d4d03213b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: MAT 6:18
Text: That thou appear not unto men to fast, but unto thy Father which is in secret: and thy Father, which seeth in secret, shall reward thee openly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c113fa7-fddf-4bab-b829-41c7536812e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MAT 6:19
Text: Lay not up for yourselves treasures upon earth, where moth and rust doth corrupt, and where thieves break through and steal:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ccba1866-18d5-460a-9f2c-cdbc6b4239e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: MAT 6:20
Text: But lay up for yourselves treasures in heaven, where neither moth nor rust doth corrupt, and where thieves do not break through nor steal:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acf4c750-ebd0-4e41-a78d-9f204041a51c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: MAT 6:21
Text: For where your treasure is, there will your heart be also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1687d9b7-7b7b-4a34-bcba-8874039375f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: MAT 6:22
Text: The light of the body is the eye: if therefore thine eye be single, thy whole body shall be full of light.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9933c61c-976c-4d38-aa1f-a0279d6c56a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: MAT 6:23
Text: But if thine eye be evil, thy whole body shall be full of darkness. If therefore the light that is in thee be darkness, how great is that darkness!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5ad1aa4-e0c9-4d20-93ad-3d213184056d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: MAT 6:24
Text: No man can serve two masters: for either he will hate the one, and love the other; or else he will hold to the one, and despise the other. Ye cannot serve God and mammon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5655beae-7aa3-4bd5-aecb-905fc66609a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: MAT 6:25
Text: Therefore I say unto you, Take no thought for your life, what ye shall eat, or what ye shall drink; nor yet for your body, what ye shall put on. Is not the life more than meat, and the body than raiment?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:395bc061-192f-4ca1-a016-b43bcfa7124e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: MAT 6:26
Text: Behold the fowls of the air: for they sow not, neither do they reap, nor gather into barns; yet your heavenly Father feedeth them. Are ye not much better than they?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76277a85-9e57-449d-b867-b98d74918cce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: MAT 6:27
Text: Which of you by taking thought can add one cubit unto his stature?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c2d1f58-906b-4754-98dc-db662c4d3f44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: MAT 6:28
Text: And why take ye thought for raiment? Consider the lilies of the field, how they grow; they toil not, neither do they spin:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bf31e25-a9fd-4580-b2ab-eebe2d93dc42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: MAT 6:29
Text: And yet I say unto you, That even Solomon in all his glory was not arrayed like one of these.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5720fa1-a126-4733-8c60-5e8d29845b68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: MAT 6:30
Text: Wherefore, if God so clothe the grass of the field, which to day is, and to morrow is cast into the oven, shall he not much more clothe you, O ye of little faith?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbc9766e-d1b4-47b5-819c-1473fb1e64e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: MAT 6:31
Text: Therefore take no thought, saying, What shall we eat? or, What shall we drink? or, Wherewithal shall we be clothed?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7bf00aff-9701-44ab-8435-00a7b521571d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: MAT 6:32
Text: (For after all these things do the Gentiles seek:) for your heavenly Father knoweth that ye have need of all these things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27a70381-5595-4e90-842e-da101932ad7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: MAT 6:33
Text: But seek ye first the kingdom of God, and his righteousness; and all these things shall be added unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/6/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b611d34-0ae7-494c-a022-1c27bf87e260>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: MAT 6:34
Text: Take therefore no thought for the morrow: for the morrow shall take thought for the things of itself. Sufficient unto the day is the evil thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62e7a065-53d5-4463-a66f-8a0508732d61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 59

Reference: MAT 7:1
Text: Judge not, that ye be not judged.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8da26d0f-5e59-4761-9527-33a7e19ab33e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: MAT 7:2
Text: For with what judgment ye judge, ye shall be judged: and with what measure ye mete, it shall be measured to you again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7ab9794-45f2-4860-888b-8e8f69c6d70e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: MAT 7:3
Text: And why beholdest thou the mote that is in thy brother’s eye, but considerest not the beam that is in thine own eye?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8461b38e-b06e-4444-ae20-5a1bf536cddf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: MAT 7:4
Text: Or how wilt thou say to thy brother, Let me pull out the mote out of thine eye; and, behold, a beam is in thine own eye?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04b61adf-3f4f-4048-b1a3-68098fe77f18>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: MAT 7:5
Text: Thou hypocrite, first cast out the beam out of thine own eye; and then shalt thou see clearly to cast out the mote out of thy brother’s eye.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4940733b-1365-46d5-9861-dac34431306f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: MAT 7:6
Text: Give not that which is holy unto the dogs, neither cast ye your pearls before swine, lest they trample them under their feet, and turn again and rend you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eac538bf-7b56-4429-be86-0ca53cd9d496>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MAT 7:7
Text: Ask, and it shall be given you; seek, and ye shall find; knock, and it shall be opened unto you:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86a7ab78-6b46-4e2e-bb9c-169e6608f8f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: MAT 7:8
Text: For every one that asketh receiveth; and he that seeketh findeth; and to him that knocketh it shall be opened.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59d25f3f-e56e-49d4-a854-9e048a715e19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: MAT 7:9
Text: Or what man is there of you, whom if his son ask bread, will he give him a stone?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:153265cf-48cb-48a8-9451-5348a7b5c1fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: MAT 7:10
Text: Or if he ask a fish, will he give him a serpent?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88a71eef-e19b-4385-8baf-b2107ab0473e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: MAT 7:11
Text: If ye then, being evil, know how to give good gifts unto your children, how much more shall your Father which is in heaven give good things to them that ask him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b620ffb-1f61-4680-b213-e8390b6233f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: MAT 7:12
Text: Therefore all things whatsoever ye would that men should do to you, do ye even so to them: for this is the law and the prophets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b77b1cd-296d-45de-9c55-92bbd23138f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: MAT 7:13
Text: Enter ye in at the strait gate: for wide is the gate, and broad is the way, that leadeth to destruction, and many there be which go in thereat:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:542ec119-29e5-45f9-9642-acd5a544ead1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: MAT 7:14
Text: Because strait is the gate, and narrow is the way, which leadeth unto life, and few there be that find it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:557b836f-cbe5-45ef-bb2e-fce32337216e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: MAT 7:15
Text: Beware of false prophets, which come to you in sheep’s clothing, but inwardly they are ravening wolves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ae7b2ff-372e-4420-af88-36bc4cb5a117>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: MAT 7:16
Text: Ye shall know them by their fruits. Do men gather grapes of thorns, or figs of thistles?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f45e4b4c-786d-4ba3-a057-8b1c1a2ee784>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: MAT 7:17
Text: Even so every good tree bringeth forth good fruit; but a corrupt tree bringeth forth evil fruit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bde00f8a-72b4-4628-979f-16221fa80044>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: MAT 7:18
Text: A good tree cannot bring forth evil fruit, neither can a corrupt tree bring forth good fruit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a30fcd8d-e19e-4ea0-baf4-725a92a253d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: MAT 7:19
Text: Every tree that bringeth not forth good fruit is hewn down, and cast into the fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8eaff04-3f0a-4746-b812-4710e6b85f1e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 72

Reference: MAT 7:20
Text: Wherefore by their fruits ye shall know them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4da289da-cb7e-4134-8ce7-80e28a8aeae6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: MAT 7:21
Text: Not every one that saith unto me, Lord, Lord, shall enter into the kingdom of heaven; but he that doeth the will of my Father which is in heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23e8e645-d13b-4490-9d23-28d6c1c2f70a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: MAT 7:22
Text: Many will say to me in that day, Lord, Lord, have we not prophesied in thy name? and in thy name have cast out devils? and in thy name done many wonderful works?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ef6d7f7-5dad-4b27-9325-b28d9629d673>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: MAT 7:23
Text: And then will I profess unto them, I never knew you: depart from me, ye that work iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4640731-5b6d-4c74-bae4-1d58e595640f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: MAT 7:24
Text: Therefore whosoever heareth these sayings of mine, and doeth them, I will liken him unto a wise man, which built his house upon a rock:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d83ddd6-8f6f-4eda-9ca8-911dcd6e2ce0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: MAT 7:25
Text: And the rain descended, and the floods came, and the winds blew, and beat upon that house; and it fell not: for it was founded upon a rock.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f234b01-bb73-4114-a619-ff60fdee26d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: MAT 7:26
Text: And every one that heareth these sayings of mine, and doeth them not, shall be likened unto a foolish man, which built his house upon the sand:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70cd587a-333e-4bd9-aca2-4f67a1f500d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: MAT 7:27
Text: And the rain descended, and the floods came, and the winds blew, and beat upon that house; and it fell: and great was the fall of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:607adfb7-a06f-46f1-a050-786300254b07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: MAT 7:28
Text: And it came to pass, when Jesus had ended these sayings, the people were astonished at his doctrine:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/7/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:122b5480-e054-4cc8-a340-c23921a8a510>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: MAT 7:29
Text: For he taught them as one having authority, and not as the scribes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:518c647c-5538-4efc-aea7-3ba1eba4f5bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: MAT 8:1
Text: When he was come down from the mountain, great multitudes followed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5eb15280-4be0-41f2-8451-e35413320235>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: MAT 8:2
Text: And, behold, there came a leper and worshipped him, saying, Lord, if thou wilt, thou canst make me clean.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8da8d075-1a45-46f0-b0d4-11132ca3820e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: MAT 8:3
Text: And Jesus put forth his hand, and touched him, saying, I will; be thou clean. And immediately his leprosy was cleansed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44458648-ba49-4f81-a711-ac587718e3d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: MAT 8:4
Text: And Jesus saith unto him, See thou tell no man; but go thy way, shew thyself to the priest, and offer the gift that Moses commanded, for a testimony unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb991d1c-156b-4edd-92f1-8ae035d90f62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MAT 8:5
Text: And when Jesus was entered into Capernaum, there came unto him a centurion, beseeching him,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc99881c-b1d5-4751-926c-49913c0c03b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: MAT 8:6
Text: And saying, Lord, my servant lieth at home sick of the palsy, grievously tormented.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a53772c-e5b2-4bf1-9065-853a6b115d43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: MAT 8:7
Text: And Jesus saith unto him, I will come and heal him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e498241-1eb3-4a79-bc0f-326f570fb25a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: MAT 8:8
Text: The centurion answered and said, Lord, I am not worthy that thou shouldest come under my roof: but speak the word only, and my servant shall be healed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59e94662-ed76-4868-8226-6c558304e83f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: MAT 8:9
Text: For I am a man under authority, having soldiers under me: and I say to this man, Go, and he goeth; and to another, Come, and he cometh; and to my servant, Do this, and he doeth it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1426ef78-de78-4052-9b7d-9a8dd212c407>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: MAT 8:10
Text: When Jesus heard it, he marvelled, and said to them that followed, Verily I say unto you, I have not found so great faith, no, not in Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab097729-bc44-4c0e-8018-f2f552a5c127>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: MAT 8:11
Text: And I say unto you, That many shall come from the east and west, and shall sit down with Abraham, and Isaac, and Jacob, in the kingdom of heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07ee8e51-18aa-49d9-9d72-12e7ca88ee53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: MAT 8:12
Text: But the children of the kingdom shall be cast out into outer darkness: there shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fe86bdf-664e-4946-b04c-e54b73609dfd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: MAT 8:13
Text: And Jesus said unto the centurion, Go thy way; and as thou hast believed, so be it done unto thee. And his servant was healed in the selfsame hour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0eb95f05-7647-4408-8f3e-e9e6d73fb8b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: MAT 8:14
Text: And when Jesus was come into Peter’s house, he saw his wife’s mother laid, and sick of a fever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5028704-cb16-49b9-946e-2dd2620c6e37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: MAT 8:15
Text: And he touched her hand, and the fever left her: and she arose, and ministered unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c76f260c-f8a9-4b49-a07a-c36a412afb33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: MAT 8:16
Text: When the even was come, they brought unto him many that were possessed with devils: and he cast out the spirits with his word, and healed all that were sick:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8fc3eb5d-f4ef-465f-8e4b-0c1d63543f37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: MAT 8:17
Text: That it might be fulfilled which was spoken by Esaias the prophet, saying, Himself took our infirmities, and bare our sicknesses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a011e3d-42af-435b-98ab-71036ba98f0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: MAT 8:18
Text: Now when Jesus saw great multitudes about him, he gave commandment to depart unto the other side.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f9863cc-67cd-41de-9b49-6047f52e9b92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: MAT 8:19
Text: And a certain scribe came, and said unto him, Master, I will follow thee whithersoever thou goest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bfa0144-6fc2-4c2d-9bab-ce87d2c80d6d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: MAT 8:20
Text: And Jesus saith unto him, The foxes have holes, and the birds of the air have nests; but the Son of man hath not where to lay his head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d610043f-b47a-484d-a4b7-fe9a3c95b779>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: MAT 8:21
Text: And another of his disciples said unto him, Lord, suffer me first to go and bury my father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45e84288-2527-474b-a071-983db62d709e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: MAT 8:22
Text: But Jesus said unto him, Follow me; and let the dead bury their dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ed618d4-d05f-4f8b-9820-99c4db9678f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: MAT 8:23
Text: And when he was entered into a ship, his disciples followed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4d1a743-b9e6-456f-8e94-2f4d4cbfcd0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: MAT 8:24
Text: And, behold, there arose a great tempest in the sea, insomuch that the ship was covered with the waves: but he was asleep.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa17a195-b452-42d7-a151-eb835caf0126>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: MAT 8:25
Text: And his disciples came to him, and awoke him, saying, Lord, save us: we perish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32590f64-e508-468c-97e8-97d2b2589377>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: MAT 8:26
Text: And he saith unto them, Why are ye fearful, O ye of little faith? Then he arose, and rebuked the winds and the sea; and there was a great calm.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f62a18b-6467-4046-a894-de3b9f9f28b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: MAT 8:27
Text: But the men marvelled, saying, What manner of man is this, that even the winds and the sea obey him!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f811831a-84ed-4524-9ef4-e8d8010147db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: MAT 8:28
Text: And when he was come to the other side into the country of the Gergesenes, there met him two possessed with devils, coming out of the tombs, exceeding fierce, so that no man might pass by that way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ba05a28-b2d4-477c-a8ac-22dfd6e4aa02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: MAT 8:29
Text: And, behold, they cried out, saying, What have we to do with thee, Jesus, thou Son of God? art thou come hither to torment us before the time?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b66d1aca-a6ab-4ff3-bc36-346f40d45d16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: MAT 8:30
Text: And there was a good way off from them an herd of many swine feeding.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3de0f6b-66bd-4582-a200-d15c29ba5b4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: MAT 8:31
Text: So the devils besought him, saying, If thou cast us out, suffer us to go away into the herd of swine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9dbac572-ed71-41ac-b285-976178f5f084>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: MAT 8:32
Text: And he said unto them, Go. And when they were come out, they went into the herd of swine: and, behold, the whole herd of swine ran violently down a steep place into the sea, and perished in the waters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad844d8b-499a-4eb7-9c7c-a64b6e5d96ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: MAT 8:33
Text: And they that kept them fled, and went their ways into the city, and told every thing, and what was befallen to the possessed of the devils.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/8/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fa754b1-d044-479c-84ca-c70e309688b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: MAT 8:34
Text: And, behold, the whole city came out to meet Jesus: and when they saw him, they besought him that he would depart out of their coasts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb6237c0-a4d0-490c-b35f-c86d65ee38a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: MAT 9:1
Text: And he entered into a ship, and passed over, and came into his own city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d926a21-baf2-45b3-8e5a-227530302749>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: MAT 9:2
Text: And, behold, they brought to him a man sick of the palsy, lying on a bed: and Jesus seeing their faith said unto the sick of the palsy; Son, be of good cheer; thy sins be forgiven thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88a8f641-783b-421e-8207-b931ae16c06d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: MAT 9:3
Text: And, behold, certain of the scribes said within themselves, This man blasphemeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52a69ec0-b4d5-48f5-b5a7-3e797f1017c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: MAT 9:4
Text: And Jesus knowing their thoughts said, Wherefore think ye evil in your hearts?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd25741a-7683-4792-83f0-59aaad11eca4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: MAT 9:5
Text: For whether is easier, to say, Thy sins be forgiven thee; or to say, Arise, and walk?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5fb86c1-4e14-4bf1-bfd7-a4c7cda55df6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: MAT 9:6
Text: But that ye may know that the Son of man hath power on earth to forgive sins, (then saith he to the sick of the palsy,) Arise, take up thy bed, and go unto thine house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f40f95fa-1619-470c-8b18-bb16e8146d96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 66

Reference: MAT 9:7
Text: And he arose, and departed to his house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:109ae34f-fb6b-43d4-bc00-6065359d86d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: MAT 9:8
Text: But when the multitudes saw it, they marvelled, and glorified God, which had given such power unto men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c4d610b-487e-4b5b-b661-fe00f306e392>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: MAT 9:9
Text: And as Jesus passed forth from thence, he saw a man, named Matthew, sitting at the receipt of custom: and he saith unto him, Follow me. And he arose, and followed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9a35621-8db2-4dea-ab36-ee7640af9171>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: MAT 9:10
Text: And it came to pass, as Jesus sat at meat in the house, behold, many publicans and sinners came and sat down with him and his disciples.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09a2d20f-7b90-4875-a397-7fc6556b2315>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MAT 9:11
Text: And when the Pharisees saw it, they said unto his disciples, Why eateth your Master with publicans and sinners?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96d495e7-4496-47ca-b8f4-14528b906a39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: MAT 9:12
Text: But when Jesus heard that, he said unto them, They that be whole need not a physician, but they that are sick.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:319b8ee2-4425-4c75-b9b9-5e0137d1b0c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: MAT 9:13
Text: But go ye and learn what that meaneth, I will have mercy, and not sacrifice: for I am not come to call the righteous, but sinners to repentance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0336544-7322-4725-8d98-36f7b2f60410>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: MAT 9:14
Text: Then came to him the disciples of John, saying, Why do we and the Pharisees fast oft, but thy disciples fast not?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bebc218b-b563-40a2-b528-4f4a7395094c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: MAT 9:15
Text: And Jesus said unto them, Can the children of the bridechamber mourn, as long as the bridegroom is with them? but the days will come, when the bridegroom shall be taken from them, and then shall they fast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fe4befa-1c3a-4047-bd2e-5f24fad8b460>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: MAT 9:16
Text: No man putteth a piece of new cloth unto an old garment, for that which is put in to fill it up taketh from the garment, and the rent is made worse.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36fa98b1-ab44-45bf-9047-230bcdfb5701>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: MAT 9:17
Text: Neither do men put new wine into old bottles: else the bottles break, and the wine runneth out, and the bottles perish: but they put new wine into new bottles, and both are preserved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f705fb0c-2eb1-46df-80eb-9e7b9fb11bd9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: MAT 9:18
Text: While he spake these things unto them, behold, there came a certain ruler, and worshipped him, saying, My daughter is even now dead: but come and lay thy hand upon her, and she shall live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f375b65f-68e8-4250-b05a-f3b44e9275e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: MAT 9:19
Text: And Jesus arose, and followed him, and so did his disciples.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5e85142-0e44-47cc-bd6d-4b1f33e39c19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: MAT 9:20
Text: And, behold, a woman, which was diseased with an issue of blood twelve years, came behind him, and touched the hem of his garment:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e6d90a4-9357-4b0b-8626-f90e455080a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: MAT 9:21
Text: For she said within herself, If I may but touch his garment, I shall be whole.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6fe5d7ed-6666-4293-9f50-732a0e3966cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: MAT 9:22
Text: But Jesus turned him about, and when he saw her, he said, Daughter, be of good comfort; thy faith hath made thee whole. And the woman was made whole from that hour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3d68488-4958-4603-8622-1b7e5ef18074>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: MAT 9:23
Text: And when Jesus came into the ruler’s house, and saw the minstrels and the people making a noise,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46c33e5c-1817-48e4-ac73-7454a8c78dda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: MAT 9:24
Text: He said unto them, Give place: for the maid is not dead, but sleepeth. And they laughed him to scorn.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd4a383d-a6a7-41dc-bab2-83191bf9a105>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: MAT 9:25
Text: But when the people were put forth, he went in, and took her by the hand, and the maid arose.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29546eeb-d9af-4ddf-90f2-0e4f96c8bea9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: MAT 9:26
Text: And the fame hereof went abroad into all that land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6def84ea-769b-49e5-9a79-54781e03b795>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: MAT 9:27
Text: And when Jesus departed thence, two blind men followed him, crying, and saying, Thou son of David, have mercy on us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06201f82-1f68-4caa-9076-13c54f530c9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: MAT 9:28
Text: And when he was come into the house, the blind men came to him: and Jesus saith unto them, Believe ye that I am able to do this? They said unto him, Yea, Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21ec79d5-7673-408a-947c-024aa74833c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: MAT 9:29
Text: Then touched he their eyes, saying, According to your faith be it unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd43dea1-be14-4a51-b4ac-0b2449970c0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: MAT 9:30
Text: And their eyes were opened; and Jesus straitly charged them, saying, See that no man know it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:639a8c22-b3ef-4e9a-a811-2bee79b4d91e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: MAT 9:31
Text: But they, when they were departed, spread abroad his fame in all that country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a17d913-e5ed-4400-bc22-1dcea7d8e37b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: MAT 9:32
Text: As they went out, behold, they brought to him a dumb man possessed with a devil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:026416f6-34fa-4431-886e-07bdf4084fe5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: MAT 9:33
Text: And when the devil was cast out, the dumb spake: and the multitudes marvelled, saying, It was never so seen in Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95934184-986d-415f-93ad-adac8e3514ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: MAT 9:34
Text: But the Pharisees said, He casteth out devils through the prince of the devils.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:def03bd5-11f0-4a81-9120-28e7aecfe3a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: MAT 9:35
Text: And Jesus went about all the cities and villages, teaching in their synagogues, and preaching the gospel of the kingdom, and healing every sickness and every disease among the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2796730c-df98-490e-a777-1c5d07cb50d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: MAT 9:36
Text: But when he saw the multitudes, he was moved with compassion on them, because they fainted, and were scattered abroad, as sheep having no shepherd.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4d758cb-8b47-4a17-92f5-adc4324ebdb8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: MAT 9:37
Text: Then saith he unto his disciples, The harvest truly is plenteous, but the labourers are few;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/9/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2856dfc-277e-409f-8002-3f328b8bb71c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: MAT 9:38
Text: Pray ye therefore the Lord of the harvest, that he will send forth labourers into his harvest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e69e9dd9-4387-4776-8606-526610e972bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: MAT 10:1
Text: And when he had called unto him his twelve disciples, he gave them power against unclean spirits, to cast them out, and to heal all manner of sickness and all manner of disease.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa6d1664-6155-4602-b752-05deb9fcb7af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: MAT 10:2
Text: Now the names of the twelve apostles are these; The first, Simon, who is called Peter, and Andrew his brother; James the son of Zebedee, and John his brother;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2cc94d6e-be59-41df-a534-b024c7b77e61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: MAT 10:3
Text: Philip, and Bartholomew; Thomas, and Matthew the publican; James the son of Alphaeus, and Lebbaeus, whose surname was Thaddaeus;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acf9a808-1757-44dd-85ef-b9cd679c7465>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: MAT 10:4
Text: Simon the Canaanite, and Judas Iscariot, who also betrayed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3404166-fe3c-401b-b614-2bb57f8d679d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: MAT 10:5
Text: These twelve Jesus sent forth, and commanded them, saying, Go not into the way of the Gentiles, and into any city of the Samaritans enter ye not:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:721b9a6f-7145-4828-b165-856ff4facdfb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: MAT 10:6
Text: But go rather to the lost sheep of the house of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1c60ab6-6ff5-4baa-b12c-e3cc425bcea0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: MAT 10:7
Text: And as ye go, preach, saying, The kingdom of heaven is at hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1dd85810-6888-44c3-9e7c-c9822cf87533>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: MAT 10:8
Text: Heal the sick, cleanse the lepers, raise the dead, cast out devils: freely ye have received, freely give.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4dd5f675-28ac-4d50-a00b-5520a1cf2b8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: MAT 10:9
Text: Provide neither gold, nor silver, nor brass in your purses,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e8dc79f-9e69-47e4-aedb-cf56ac0ba383>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: MAT 10:10
Text: Nor scrip for your journey, neither two coats, neither shoes, nor yet staves: for the workman is worthy of his meat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95d8b664-6ac0-457e-89e8-20c232e3dd6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: MAT 10:11
Text: And into whatsoever city or town ye shall enter, enquire who in it is worthy; and there abide till ye go thence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aea819fd-e7f3-46e6-bdc0-b0f723cbfa1e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 70

Reference: MAT 10:12
Text: And when ye come into an house, salute it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ae578e8-d73b-4b46-b9de-607f146d75a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: MAT 10:13
Text: And if the house be worthy, let your peace come upon it: but if it be not worthy, let your peace return to you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86648bf6-1c44-4646-8bb9-38639601a620>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: MAT 10:14
Text: And whosoever shall not receive you, nor hear your words, when ye depart out of that house or city, shake off the dust of your feet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3014979-df49-4a0e-a523-9dac55a7d937>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: MAT 10:15
Text: Verily I say unto you, It shall be more tolerable for the land of Sodom and Gomorrha in the day of judgment, than for that city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb66ac4f-1bfc-4d44-bcf8-34b86b920551>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: MAT 10:16
Text: Behold, I send you forth as sheep in the midst of wolves: be ye therefore wise as serpents, and harmless as doves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c46ea8d-f17f-4b70-be23-c8e53e6639d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: MAT 10:17
Text: But beware of men: for they will deliver you up to the councils, and they will scourge you in their synagogues;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47279990-9698-48ad-832d-1be28a580fe6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MAT 10:18
Text: And ye shall be brought before governors and kings for my sake, for a testimony against them and the Gentiles.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:089573b4-1b32-4837-847a-b6207fe6688a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: MAT 10:19
Text: But when they deliver you up, take no thought how or what ye shall speak: for it shall be given you in that same hour what ye shall speak.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f411ee4-cfe4-41bc-833e-ef04e1c61e8e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: MAT 10:20
Text: For it is not ye that speak, but the Spirit of your Father which speaketh in you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38bb9500-9274-4ae2-9a81-fec41a4d7782>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: MAT 10:21
Text: And the brother shall deliver up the brother to death, and the father the child: and the children shall rise up against their parents, and cause them to be put to death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06a47d02-439c-414b-ae58-edd3aba03d03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: MAT 10:22
Text: And ye shall be hated of all men for my name’s sake: but he that endureth to the end shall be saved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28cf2281-5ca6-4162-83e0-8d008dd0040c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: MAT 10:23
Text: But when they persecute you in this city, flee ye into another: for verily I say unto you, Ye shall not have gone over the cities of Israel, till the Son of man be come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e929d708-d0fb-43c3-8855-001a60c140b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: MAT 10:24
Text: The disciple is not above his master, nor the servant above his lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84479c09-cf97-4e8b-ba1a-9ff416e015ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: MAT 10:25
Text: It is enough for the disciple that he be as his master, and the servant as his lord. If they have called the master of the house Beelzebub, how much more shall they call them of his household?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8772d530-34dd-492e-ba17-14a4df46ae59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: MAT 10:26
Text: Fear them not therefore: for there is nothing covered, that shall not be revealed; and hid, that shall not be known.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23fa34ed-f23d-4e3d-8319-027280ca2620>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: MAT 10:27
Text: What I tell you in darkness, that speak ye in light: and what ye hear in the ear, that preach ye upon the housetops.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e38c06b4-cc5d-46b3-833d-aee30460fae3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: MAT 10:28
Text: And fear not them which kill the body, but are not able to kill the soul: but rather fear him which is able to destroy both soul and body in hell.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1f97671-f159-40ab-9181-8cf9fe99f53f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: MAT 10:29
Text: Are not two sparrows sold for a farthing? and one of them shall not fall on the ground without your Father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4070ac99-f114-4768-ab22-2d8f81f5c2d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: MAT 10:30
Text: But the very hairs of your head are all numbered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:464c9500-963e-4fe0-9223-e983b6ab1a09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: MAT 10:31
Text: Fear ye not therefore, ye are of more value than many sparrows.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab5a9621-38c7-4914-89fb-3c95c8a34746>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: MAT 10:32
Text: Whosoever therefore shall confess me before men, him will I confess also before my Father which is in heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:905dc2fe-945d-4811-abd4-d40c1c53bcee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: MAT 10:33
Text: But whosoever shall deny me before men, him will I also deny before my Father which is in heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08814397-ea05-425d-97c5-cf57dcbe24d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: MAT 10:34
Text: Think not that I am come to send peace on earth: I came not to send peace, but a sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f061c210-48c7-471b-b20d-9d85f2dbe217>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: MAT 10:35
Text: For I am come to set a man at variance against his father, and the daughter against her mother, and the daughter in law against her mother in law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64c10021-859e-4f08-bbb4-7404c3a1f7c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: MAT 10:36
Text: And a man’s foes shall be they of his own household.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3dc5e3b-4d60-4407-8a63-bb5fa3c82c28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: MAT 10:37
Text: He that loveth father or mother more than me is not worthy of me: and he that loveth son or daughter more than me is not worthy of me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2411299e-c754-4ad3-ba51-4cfa1eab02d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: MAT 10:38
Text: And he that taketh not his cross, and followeth after me, is not worthy of me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4301a1ef-d0cd-4829-96ae-e92b7226238a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MAT 10:39
Text: He that findeth his life shall lose it: and he that loseth his life for my sake shall find it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aef8de15-6d89-4a4a-84cd-afe466b762c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: MAT 10:40
Text: He that receiveth you receiveth me, and he that receiveth me receiveth him that sent me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf793b04-7382-4dd4-b6ea-ede8f16c9217>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: MAT 10:41
Text: He that receiveth a prophet in the name of a prophet shall receive a prophet’s reward; and he that receiveth a righteous man in the name of a righteous man shall receive a righteous man’s reward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/10/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02312e9f-a82f-4cf0-87a8-339289f72ccb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: MAT 10:42
Text: And whosoever shall give to drink unto one of these little ones a cup of cold water only in the name of a disciple, verily I say unto you, he shall in no wise lose his reward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5727b05e-dbd5-4f59-bd03-f09d45ef4f8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: MAT 11:1
Text: And it came to pass, when Jesus had made an end of commanding his twelve disciples, he departed thence to teach and to preach in their cities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b999570-e633-45d7-84ed-deb43a8e8032>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: MAT 11:2
Text: Now when John had heard in the prison the works of Christ, he sent two of his disciples,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0b96bf5-b924-480c-b3a7-443b8405765d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: MAT 11:3
Text: And said unto him, Art thou he that should come, or do we look for another?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:810f4cd3-1352-4d3f-903b-0ff728af32a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: MAT 11:4
Text: Jesus answered and said unto them, Go and shew John again those things which ye do hear and see:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab60943c-2bb8-4d62-a9a1-a11053199ab7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: MAT 11:5
Text: The blind receive their sight, and the lame walk, the lepers are cleansed, and the deaf hear, the dead are raised up, and the poor have the gospel preached to them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:374cb372-3fc5-4e2e-8d74-1594b53c3f81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: MAT 11:6
Text: And blessed is he, whosoever shall not be offended in me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4220d8bb-450f-45ab-a2c5-01c50a1582f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: MAT 11:7
Text: And as they departed, Jesus began to say unto the multitudes concerning John, What went ye out into the wilderness to see? A reed shaken with the wind?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8fed28c-a134-4db7-9d5a-a2e60c1bbe2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MAT 11:8
Text: But what went ye out for to see? A man clothed in soft raiment? behold, they that wear soft clothing are in kings’ houses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0b741fc-55c2-40da-9e09-f692ecefbf3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: MAT 11:9
Text: But what went ye out for to see? A prophet? yea, I say unto you, and more than a prophet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f522f21c-3cf4-4743-a7a0-a8176e0fba11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: MAT 11:10
Text: For this is he, of whom it is written, Behold, I send my messenger before thy face, which shall prepare thy way before thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:167c4008-a73f-4a3f-b005-f277b08ba70e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: MAT 11:11
Text: Verily I say unto you, Among them that are born of women there hath not risen a greater than John the Baptist: notwithstanding he that is least in the kingdom of heaven is greater than he.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a14c0ea0-2932-4f28-bb73-d47571f99588>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MAT 11:12
Text: And from the days of John the Baptist until now the kingdom of heaven suffereth violence, and the violent take it by force.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3459a0e-e08c-4656-899e-d2f034d399cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: MAT 11:13
Text: For all the prophets and the law prophesied until John.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20fa2043-badf-47ed-bbff-69f1575cb0f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: MAT 11:14
Text: And if ye will receive it, this is Elias, which was for to come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1884b756-1ece-403c-9c1f-73a284fa1498>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 68

Reference: MAT 11:15
Text: He that hath ears to hear, let him hear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61b41eca-5928-40ee-8892-72fd26b7f656>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: MAT 11:16
Text: But whereunto shall I liken this generation? It is like unto children sitting in the markets, and calling unto their fellows,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afbfc0a3-f562-4268-a8b0-d11649129ec8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: MAT 11:17
Text: And saying, We have piped unto you, and ye have not danced; we have mourned unto you, and ye have not lamented.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:015423c8-15fb-44b0-a521-89e8a2960e7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: MAT 11:18
Text: For John came neither eating nor drinking, and they say, He hath a devil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52a84347-ca79-4c09-9b3e-ea7a656fd135>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: MAT 11:19
Text: The Son of man came eating and drinking, and they say, Behold a man gluttonous, and a winebibber, a friend of publicans and sinners. But wisdom is justified of her children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:132785ca-bb39-46b8-a566-7a070205913b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: MAT 11:20
Text: Then began he to upbraid the cities wherein most of his mighty works were done, because they repented not:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5f44fe1-aa47-438a-a994-e7cb3e0ae714>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: MAT 11:21
Text: Woe unto thee, Chorazin! woe unto thee, Bethsaida! for if the mighty works, which were done in you, had been done in Tyre and Sidon, they would have repented long ago in sackcloth and ashes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c85f1f73-526c-4ef3-808a-1fd96ae3847b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: MAT 11:22
Text: But I say unto you, It shall be more tolerable for Tyre and Sidon at the day of judgment, than for you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1edf24e-c328-492c-858d-250766f2220a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: MAT 11:23
Text: And thou, Capernaum, which art exalted unto heaven, shalt be brought down to hell: for if the mighty works, which have been done in thee, had been done in Sodom, it would have remained until this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f184e909-b88a-4007-a108-b2b52bfdbf37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: MAT 11:24
Text: But I say unto you, That it shall be more tolerable for the land of Sodom in the day of judgment, than for thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ec5fdb7-37fc-42e8-845e-3dfb35392330>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: MAT 11:25
Text: At that time Jesus answered and said, I thank thee, O Father, Lord of heaven and earth, because thou hast hid these things from the wise and prudent, and hast revealed them unto babes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:729befce-8fa4-4617-930b-2cade0ccf13d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: MAT 11:26
Text: Even so, Father: for so it seemed good in thy sight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c9fbd9d-1203-4b1e-ab28-1c8d1f17e562>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: MAT 11:27
Text: All things are delivered unto me of my Father: and no man knoweth the Son, but the Father; neither knoweth any man the Father, save the Son, and he to whomsoever the Son will reveal him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de65f1bc-fa44-4aea-8b1a-212d8e7729eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: MAT 11:28
Text: Come unto me, all ye that labour and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c9d3d5c-425f-47a7-93e1-79a1a04fe283>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: MAT 11:29
Text: Take my yoke upon you, and learn of me; for I am meek and lowly in heart: and ye shall find rest unto your souls.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/11/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26d6f683-19bf-4bac-9eb1-0273922d6b2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 72

Reference: MAT 11:30
Text: For my yoke is easy, and my burden is light.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d7fa264-8e1a-450f-bca8-51bf7d8121e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: MAT 12:1
Text: At that time Jesus went on the sabbath day through the corn; and his disciples were an hungred, and began to pluck the ears of corn and to eat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb448791-137e-4057-94d6-58b0508398c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: MAT 12:2
Text: But when the Pharisees saw it, they said unto him, Behold, thy disciples do that which is not lawful to do upon the sabbath day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:117cfcc1-9e4b-4a44-a472-f19b217ba874>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: MAT 12:3
Text: But he said unto them, Have ye not read what David did, when he was an hungred, and they that were with him;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afcc5c7e-a8a8-4408-84e4-1a6f3a74500f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: MAT 12:4
Text: How he entered into the house of God, and did eat the shewbread, which was not lawful for him to eat, neither for them which were with him, but only for the priests?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:259c3ffb-8f81-43e8-9c39-92be8e77b183>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: MAT 12:5
Text: Or have ye not read in the law, how that on the sabbath days the priests in the temple profane the sabbath, and are blameless?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63e6102b-3dc9-4bc3-832a-08a3d3fceb92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: MAT 12:6
Text: But I say unto you, That in this place is one greater than the temple.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f488272-c056-4d2c-a9b4-ecd2555950da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: MAT 12:7
Text: But if ye had known what this meaneth, I will have mercy, and not sacrifice, ye would not have condemned the guiltless.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:946e7176-ec58-43a7-aea6-f0e2bf17fe88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: MAT 12:8
Text: For the Son of man is Lord even of the sabbath day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4045817b-e130-40ba-8fc4-e6e3c8914524>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: MAT 12:9
Text: And when he was departed thence, he went into their synagogue:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2e65426-a09d-45c2-96b2-01a6eb58628e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: MAT 12:10
Text: And, behold, there was a man which had his hand withered. And they asked him, saying, Is it lawful to heal on the sabbath days? that they might accuse him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae95beb4-7421-4111-af4f-b77cc248b1bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: MAT 12:11
Text: And he said unto them, What man shall there be among you, that shall have one sheep, and if it fall into a pit on the sabbath day, will he not lay hold on it, and lift it out?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26927866-7f7c-411a-b8a5-4f5a2eea9683>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: MAT 12:12
Text: How much then is a man better than a sheep? Wherefore it is lawful to do well on the sabbath days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:735c6107-ca7d-42a4-b011-372dc0436f3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: MAT 12:13
Text: Then saith he to the man, Stretch forth thine hand. And he stretched it forth; and it was restored whole, like as the other.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b43f94a4-e90a-451d-a983-afc022da5375>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: MAT 12:14
Text: Then the Pharisees went out, and held a council against him, how they might destroy him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc2fd799-09be-4fc5-810c-8c5a675ff318>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: MAT 12:15
Text: But when Jesus knew it, he withdrew himself from thence: and great multitudes followed him, and he healed them all;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7f4455b-bce3-4b1b-870d-49dde6081d6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: MAT 12:16
Text: And charged them that they should not make him known:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f03f53f8-734e-4628-ac3a-62df19b79e1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: MAT 12:17
Text: That it might be fulfilled which was spoken by Esaias the prophet, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4954f1d9-c4b0-4f9b-a0ec-7467c9cfa924>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: MAT 12:18
Text: Behold my servant, whom I have chosen; my beloved, in whom my soul is well pleased: I will put my spirit upon him, and he shall shew judgment to the Gentiles.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1ea19c6-5951-4de6-a092-a688b57b9197>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: MAT 12:19
Text: He shall not strive, nor cry; neither shall any man hear his voice in the streets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3564e8ff-d99c-4aa1-9257-eba725a2142b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: MAT 12:20
Text: A bruised reed shall he not break, and smoking flax shall he not quench, till he send forth judgment unto victory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b086eadb-d106-49ac-bc28-2e61353c8059>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 69

Reference: MAT 12:21
Text: And in his name shall the Gentiles trust.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db1c06b0-fe41-49d0-9faa-58acbd1d3847>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: MAT 12:22
Text: Then was brought unto him one possessed with a devil, blind, and dumb: and he healed him, insomuch that the blind and dumb both spake and saw.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:400eec5d-8f74-4610-a827-c5b39431f0b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: MAT 12:23
Text: And all the people were amazed, and said, Is not this the son of David?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:767c96ad-55a8-47e0-91ea-246f50fae85e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: MAT 12:24
Text: But when the Pharisees heard it, they said, This fellow doth not cast out devils, but by Beelzebub the prince of the devils.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a58d189f-fc8d-40e1-8341-e92213e2ba76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: MAT 12:25
Text: And Jesus knew their thoughts, and said unto them, Every kingdom divided against itself is brought to desolation; and every city or house divided against itself shall not stand:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f825f5de-b530-4b25-9e9c-00e4448c82f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: MAT 12:26
Text: And if Satan cast out Satan, he is divided against himself; how shall then his kingdom stand?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18768e96-a742-4400-82bb-69f86930c981>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: MAT 12:27
Text: And if I by Beelzebub cast out devils, by whom do your children cast them out? therefore they shall be your judges.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1260e412-28e1-4585-8d58-d04bf6a7a5f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: MAT 12:28
Text: But if I cast out devils by the Spirit of God, then the kingdom of God is come unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4c61d80-7e64-4309-9279-5fb6089dde59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: MAT 12:29
Text: Or else how can one enter into a strong man’s house, and spoil his goods, except he first bind the strong man? and then he will spoil his house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39dc5ad5-5cca-44ee-8717-2aa3ecd89e04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: MAT 12:30
Text: He that is not with me is against me; and he that gathereth not with me scattereth abroad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c5a685d-3e19-46c6-b956-18cee4a25a5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: MAT 12:31
Text: Wherefore I say unto you, All manner of sin and blasphemy shall be forgiven unto men: but the blasphemy against the Holy Ghost shall not be forgiven unto men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acdcd7bb-7b71-46d2-a2ff-84bc61ab4d00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: MAT 12:32
Text: And whosoever speaketh a word against the Son of man, it shall be forgiven him: but whosoever speaketh against the Holy Ghost, it shall not be forgiven him, neither in this world, neither in the world to come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b80ad4fd-9157-4b58-8d38-dbbaefda3585>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: MAT 12:33
Text: Either make the tree good, and his fruit good; or else make the tree corrupt, and his fruit corrupt: for the tree is known by his fruit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46e9a9e4-8ef5-4ab0-8c37-eaf3cd297ef0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: MAT 12:34
Text: O generation of vipers, how can ye, being evil, speak good things? for out of the abundance of the heart the mouth speaketh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ede843ce-2695-4dec-b0a0-4aa30ca635f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: MAT 12:35
Text: A good man out of the good treasure of the heart bringeth forth good things: and an evil man out of the evil treasure bringeth forth evil things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58cf7e4e-5e28-46c1-a87b-e9a34daae67c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: MAT 12:36
Text: But I say unto you, That every idle word that men shall speak, they shall give account thereof in the day of judgment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ede4b749-64ac-4b31-907a-417ef3b31564>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: MAT 12:37
Text: For by thy words thou shalt be justified, and by thy words thou shalt be condemned.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66d45708-c994-4911-822b-4295e313806a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: MAT 12:38
Text: Then certain of the scribes and of the Pharisees answered, saying, Master, we would see a sign from thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d372e41-ae05-4e47-aaa0-1744448a0dec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: MAT 12:39
Text: But he answered and said unto them, An evil and adulterous generation seeketh after a sign; and there shall no sign be given to it, but the sign of the prophet Jonas:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e34341c3-6801-4ece-9f4d-8ed9afd06e60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: MAT 12:40
Text: For as Jonas was three days and three nights in the whale’s belly; so shall the Son of man be three days and three nights in the heart of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3070c5a4-fafd-4954-b394-f37dd1335337>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: MAT 12:41
Text: The men of Nineveh shall rise in judgment with this generation, and shall condemn it: because they repented at the preaching of Jonas; and, behold, a greater than Jonas is here.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72659ed9-a941-4808-9277-5463b54f9a69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: MAT 12:42
Text: The queen of the south shall rise up in the judgment with this generation, and shall condemn it: for she came from the uttermost parts of the earth to hear the wisdom of Solomon; and, behold, a greater than Solomon is here.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fde23de9-517c-4094-9696-7a1ee339c8e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: MAT 12:43
Text: When the unclean spirit is gone out of a man, he walketh through dry places, seeking rest, and findeth none.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1639e304-b631-4d29-ac16-2bc33e9c5356>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: MAT 12:44
Text: Then he saith, I will return into my house from whence I came out; and when he is come, he findeth it empty, swept, and garnished.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67844a3b-5314-4eb0-be36-49aef232442b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: MAT 12:45
Text: Then goeth he, and taketh with himself seven other spirits more wicked than himself, and they enter in and dwell there: and the last state of that man is worse than the first. Even so shall it be also unto this wicked generation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba1ce060-3d01-4c54-91db-25a1f5cac476>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: MAT 12:46
Text: While he yet talked to the people, behold, his mother and his brethren stood without, desiring to speak with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d180483-44b2-4c05-8957-18e25dd94bf2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: MAT 12:47
Text: Then one said unto him, Behold, thy mother and thy brethren stand without, desiring to speak with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f87331e-31fc-4fcb-b9ee-8a66c3f8f0fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: MAT 12:48
Text: But he answered and said unto him that told him, Who is my mother? and who are my brethren?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69497531-6e04-4095-9a3d-a46b4fb1955d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: MAT 12:49
Text: And he stretched forth his hand toward his disciples, and said, Behold my mother and my brethren!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/12/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f19a6850-9b5e-4207-b2f9-1c9ba41f2120>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: MAT 12:50
Text: For whosoever shall do the will of my Father which is in heaven, the same is my brother, and sister, and mother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e62d0931-8c85-4f8d-b819-3423f0a2eded>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: MAT 13:1
Text: The same day went Jesus out of the house, and sat by the sea side.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71ef185b-3b1b-46c7-9f1e-2d6f0b283cad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: MAT 13:2
Text: And great multitudes were gathered together unto him, so that he went into a ship, and sat; and the whole multitude stood on the shore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bcd7cc5-f623-4a19-baa5-eda02c18f3d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MAT 13:3
Text: And he spake many things unto them in parables, saying, Behold, a sower went forth to sow;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2076778-7084-4f79-a0b6-ed042869524a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: MAT 13:4
Text: And when he sowed, some seeds fell by the way side, and the fowls came and devoured them up:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b316fc8-f45e-4177-863c-5b496fde9bfa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: MAT 13:5
Text: Some fell upon stony places, where they had not much earth: and forthwith they sprung up, because they had no deepness of earth:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41af218f-be16-4e1c-bfe2-133ad6f46e57>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: MAT 13:6
Text: And when the sun was up, they were scorched; and because they had no root, they withered away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c097de0e-4e4f-42e9-8bed-8a3dbc8cf8b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: MAT 13:7
Text: And some fell among thorns; and the thorns sprung up, and choked them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b8c293e-4277-4c33-8282-a7dd7eb685da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MAT 13:8
Text: But other fell into good ground, and brought forth fruit, some an hundredfold, some sixtyfold, some thirtyfold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eda6b4df-8250-442d-9186-3c75f6c57b3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 63

Reference: MAT 13:9
Text: Who hath ears to hear, let him hear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9cbea733-7d1c-42d0-92a9-67139e972cc5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: MAT 13:10
Text: And the disciples came, and said unto him, Why speakest thou unto them in parables?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61ecd3f7-84e5-43ad-bf40-8b25fe1b70a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: MAT 13:11
Text: He answered and said unto them, Because it is given unto you to know the mysteries of the kingdom of heaven, but to them it is not given.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dca9f68b-2222-409d-aa51-458c8e14d4f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: MAT 13:12
Text: For whosoever hath, to him shall be given, and he shall have more abundance: but whosoever hath not, from him shall be taken away even that he hath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e2a4fe7-c88b-4fdb-ba3a-018d168e97e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: MAT 13:13
Text: Therefore speak I to them in parables: because they seeing see not; and hearing they hear not, neither do they understand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f1808a0-c638-4a39-80b8-94efb901c2a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: MAT 13:14
Text: And in them is fulfilled the prophecy of Esaias, which saith, By hearing ye shall hear, and shall not understand; and seeing ye shall see, and shall not perceive:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a806512-80f9-4bf2-895c-f20b9a96e429>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 302

Reference: MAT 13:15
Text: For this people’s heart is waxed gross, and their ears are dull of hearing, and their eyes they have closed; lest at any time they should see with their eyes and hear with their ears, and should understand with their heart, and should be converted, and I should heal them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5361eaf0-d274-4bd7-a150-d97d676302a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: MAT 13:16
Text: But blessed are your eyes, for they see: and your ears, for they hear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d541ea1-e74d-4ddf-aa13-d22596716724>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: MAT 13:17
Text: For verily I say unto you, That many prophets and righteous men have desired to see those things which ye see, and have not seen them; and to hear those things which ye hear, and have not heard them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f431cdd-8e92-45b4-9aca-36935e7f13b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 71

Reference: MAT 13:18
Text: Hear ye therefore the parable of the sower.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:150570dd-84d7-4c85-8ff6-53ddd9bfc792>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: MAT 13:19
Text: When any one heareth the word of the kingdom, and understandeth it not, then cometh the wicked one, and catcheth away that which was sown in his heart. This is he which received seed by the way side.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:662b520d-3fd4-4180-909b-a456c2fe6e0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: MAT 13:20
Text: But he that received the seed into stony places, the same is he that heareth the word, and anon with joy receiveth it;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:276eae70-691b-465e-be89-58906d53335e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: MAT 13:21
Text: Yet hath he not root in himself, but dureth for a while: for when tribulation or persecution ariseth because of the word, by and by he is offended.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d0bf7cf-66df-4c3e-af64-424e7abe3d82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: MAT 13:22
Text: He also that received seed among the thorns is he that heareth the word; and the care of this world, and the deceitfulness of riches, choke the word, and he becometh unfruitful.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e89874b3-e59e-43b2-9a94-d46886bf0be9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: MAT 13:23
Text: But he that received seed into the good ground is he that heareth the word, and understandeth it; which also beareth fruit, and bringeth forth, some an hundredfold, some sixty, some thirty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab0e4878-c6e6-40c1-aa21-32a570640045>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: MAT 13:24
Text: Another parable put he forth unto them, saying, The kingdom of heaven is likened unto a man which sowed good seed in his field:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7a60ad2-1457-4ee7-b90a-41f780e192f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MAT 13:25
Text: But while men slept, his enemy came and sowed tares among the wheat, and went his way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a632912b-663b-4644-bbd0-95983cc6f9ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: MAT 13:26
Text: But when the blade was sprung up, and brought forth fruit, then appeared the tares also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b6c5ac5-3d86-47f8-ab18-eecfd2ff43f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: MAT 13:27
Text: So the servants of the householder came and said unto him, Sir, didst not thou sow good seed in thy field? from whence then hath it tares?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7e18f00-c8ca-4599-b666-eaa0dd8cbccf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: MAT 13:28
Text: He said unto them, An enemy hath done this. The servants said unto him, Wilt thou then that we go and gather them up?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3061cb0c-7923-4b3a-9a95-995c925523e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MAT 13:29
Text: But he said, Nay; lest while ye gather up the tares, ye root up also the wheat with them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:420dd08c-f950-4db2-83d8-aaeeb63e6990>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: MAT 13:30
Text: Let both grow together until the harvest: and in the time of harvest I will say to the reapers, Gather ye together first the tares, and bind them in bundles to burn them: but gather the wheat into my barn.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a67c102-7986-4a7f-b392-c8db646ee13e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: MAT 13:31
Text: Another parable put he forth unto them, saying, The kingdom of heaven is like to a grain of mustard seed, which a man took, and sowed in his field:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17243170-4cf5-45ef-865b-12028c72b749>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: MAT 13:32
Text: Which indeed is the least of all seeds: but when it is grown, it is the greatest among herbs, and becometh a tree, so that the birds of the air come and lodge in the branches thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7478dd0a-2348-44e3-b0c2-defbc7122218>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: MAT 13:33
Text: Another parable spake he unto them; The kingdom of heaven is like unto leaven, which a woman took, and hid in three measures of meal, till the whole was leavened.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96e46196-25ee-43f7-9cf0-f7767e031d58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: MAT 13:34
Text: All these things spake Jesus unto the multitude in parables; and without a parable spake he not unto them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:993d1e72-4a39-4e70-a342-e4768c3e6f04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: MAT 13:35
Text: That it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the prophet, saying, I will open my mouth in parables; I will utter things which have been kept secret from the foundation of the world.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32a88379-bf41-4372-8d61-74de4e80afb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: MAT 13:36
Text: Then Jesus sent the multitude away, and went into the house: and his disciples came unto him, saying, Declare unto us the parable of the tares of the field.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2513860d-b207-42f5-905a-f06b7aa442a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: MAT 13:37
Text: He answered and said unto them, He that soweth the good seed is the Son of man;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e43a28e9-a0f5-4100-acd3-ea9864e512ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: MAT 13:38
Text: The field is the world; the good seed are the children of the kingdom; but the tares are the children of the wicked one;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64502938-1611-455a-a147-3ffceab0fb0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: MAT 13:39
Text: The enemy that sowed them is the devil; the harvest is the end of the world; and the reapers are the angels.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc5ecff6-a5fe-4102-a939-62ed55042bf0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: MAT 13:40
Text: As therefore the tares are gathered and burned in the fire; so shall it be in the end of this world.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd5386d0-852d-4562-857a-fa8a758b6b29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: MAT 13:41
Text: The Son of man shall send forth his angels, and they shall gather out of his kingdom all things that offend, and them which do iniquity;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36d3d4a5-d9a5-4d78-ae5a-ca798d03128d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MAT 13:42
Text: And shall cast them into a furnace of fire: there shall be wailing and gnashing of teeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9655b629-660c-4d03-8cfe-990e3829efcf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: MAT 13:43
Text: Then shall the righteous shine forth as the sun in the kingdom of their Father. Who hath ears to hear, let him hear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72790042-f1e3-4e1e-8413-d1e96017a0cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: MAT 13:44
Text: Again, the kingdom of heaven is like unto treasure hid in a field; the which when a man hath found, he hideth, and for joy thereof goeth and selleth all that he hath, and buyeth that field.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a765927-1935-4c81-af3a-e69bc444e068>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: MAT 13:45
Text: Again, the kingdom of heaven is like unto a merchant man, seeking goodly pearls:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b3cac61-826d-4182-b01a-5d0d557e0203>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MAT 13:46
Text: Who, when he had found one pearl of great price, went and sold all that he had, and bought it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:964224be-fc9c-4380-9cff-bac75970647d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: MAT 13:47
Text: Again, the kingdom of heaven is like unto a net, that was cast into the sea, and gathered of every kind:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:261d7951-816e-4f5d-b7df-9ab6781f9125>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: MAT 13:48
Text: Which, when it was full, they drew to shore, and sat down, and gathered the good into vessels, but cast the bad away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df4f2b91-9e9c-4b33-a3da-bea860c48ccb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MAT 13:49
Text: So shall it be at the end of the world: the angels shall come forth, and sever the wicked from among the just,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7363fb63-3733-4f90-9d01-bef163f532d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: MAT 13:50
Text: And shall cast them into the furnace of fire: there shall be wailing and gnashing of teeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52a2d7e5-b085-4bfe-8892-3b7e9a036e56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MAT 13:51
Text: Jesus saith unto them, Have ye understood all these things? They say unto him, Yea, Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:755c9eb5-2768-42f3-b621-6de418896479>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: MAT 13:52
Text: Then said he unto them, Therefore every scribe which is instructed unto the kingdom of heaven is like unto a man that is an householder, which bringeth forth out of his treasure things new and old.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a26c848-0976-4f4b-8e34-cd02baa7b75f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: MAT 13:53
Text: And it came to pass, that when Jesus had finished these parables, he departed thence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:368f92fa-62b9-4fb5-a17c-bc0bc48fd708>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: MAT 13:54
Text: And when he was come into his own country, he taught them in their synagogue, insomuch that they were astonished, and said, Whence hath this man this wisdom, and these mighty works?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/55
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4dda451a-7161-47db-9414-76398944f050>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MAT 13:55
Text: Is not this the carpenter’s son? is not his mother called Mary? and his brethren, James, and Joses, and Simon, and Judas?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/56
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f9304ee-d345-4351-b0b1-7ad4e371807f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MAT 13:56
Text: And his sisters, are they not all with us? Whence then hath this man all these things?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/57
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:faf783ac-c81a-433f-9842-989c9247554a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: MAT 13:57
Text: And they were offended in him. But Jesus said unto them, A prophet is not without honour, save in his own country, and in his own house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/13/58
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e37ebde0-2535-458f-aa9b-d944062f6e56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: MAT 13:58
Text: And he did not many mighty works there because of their unbelief.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c67e07a-67bb-43a1-b769-d8a91eb4b87c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: MAT 14:1
Text: At that time Herod the tetrarch heard of the fame of Jesus,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef02997a-4bb2-4a1b-b412-142166ed5ca1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: MAT 14:2
Text: And said unto his servants, This is John the Baptist; he is risen from the dead; and therefore mighty works do shew forth themselves in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82248949-fbf9-40da-88ba-ca69e263c94b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: MAT 14:3
Text: For Herod had laid hold on John, and bound him, and put him in prison for Herodias’ sake, his brother Philip’s wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d07738a1-6dd8-40e9-ae61-158695c91269>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: MAT 14:4
Text: For John said unto him, It is not lawful for thee to have her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1747838-afc3-4228-a8bc-2435e060c042>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: MAT 14:5
Text: And when he would have put him to death, he feared the multitude, because they counted him as a prophet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e16bf32-2baa-46a3-ade0-079231fe8cda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: MAT 14:6
Text: But when Herod’s birthday was kept, the daughter of Herodias danced before them, and pleased Herod.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b54bef2-6360-4575-8b22-f900a0daa81e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: MAT 14:7
Text: Whereupon he promised with an oath to give her whatsoever she would ask.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d9744c0-bd1f-4425-b9b5-ae1a3f6989d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: MAT 14:8
Text: And she, being before instructed of her mother, said, Give me here John Baptist’s head in a charger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef1f9565-f191-4bf2-a0da-efef5cb89177>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: MAT 14:9
Text: And the king was sorry: nevertheless for the oath’s sake, and them which sat with him at meat, he commanded it to be given her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14503235-9806-4500-b06a-5bcfe0ff0510>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: MAT 14:10
Text: And he sent, and beheaded John in the prison.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08674dc1-9e2c-4591-9626-1ddbc310cb3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: MAT 14:11
Text: And his head was brought in a charger, and given to the damsel: and she brought it to her mother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fdc4bb17-87d1-40cb-a1c3-8b4ee4faae93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: MAT 14:12
Text: And his disciples came, and took up the body, and buried it, and went and told Jesus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93d01111-85de-4df1-b45d-fbf708600556>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: MAT 14:13
Text: When Jesus heard of it, he departed thence by ship into a desert place apart: and when the people had heard thereof, they followed him on foot out of the cities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2ec63f4-702e-4730-a174-15505eb53ff9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: MAT 14:14
Text: And Jesus went forth, and saw a great multitude, and was moved with compassion toward them, and he healed their sick.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3c10a90-58b9-491c-8516-6ee2c456c7ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: MAT 14:15
Text: And when it was evening, his disciples came to him, saying, This is a desert place, and the time is now past; send the multitude away, that they may go into the villages, and buy themselves victuals.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d54fafb7-1145-4f85-ac77-5cd716cfb955>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: MAT 14:16
Text: But Jesus said unto them, They need not depart; give ye them to eat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fe1c681-ed89-4e8b-b150-5e39f7be6c1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: MAT 14:17
Text: And they say unto him, We have here but five loaves, and two fishes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d55ecd66-e73f-4e00-af9d-988ee212d85e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 61

Reference: MAT 14:18
Text: He said, Bring them hither to me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6fc914a-6a85-4179-9707-a5bc25e1affb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: MAT 14:19
Text: And he commanded the multitude to sit down on the grass, and took the five loaves, and the two fishes, and looking up to heaven, he blessed, and brake, and gave the loaves to his disciples, and the disciples to the multitude.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f4359af-7023-4921-bf6a-8337dbeeaabc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: MAT 14:20
Text: And they did all eat, and were filled: and they took up of the fragments that remained twelve baskets full.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f35ecc0-3a73-4cce-9de2-3137d8831462>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: MAT 14:21
Text: And they that had eaten were about five thousand men, beside women and children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fe4990b-51d2-490a-968c-dec9d3411595>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: MAT 14:22
Text: And straightway Jesus constrained his disciples to get into a ship, and to go before him unto the other side, while he sent the multitudes away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0038d728-53e2-4c60-a292-c3378967a920>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: MAT 14:23
Text: And when he had sent the multitudes away, he went up into a mountain apart to pray: and when the evening was come, he was there alone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17f18466-303b-4d6a-91a8-93887d2b0d13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: MAT 14:24
Text: But the ship was now in the midst of the sea, tossed with waves: for the wind was contrary.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85ddd430-4b6d-4eb1-8275-971c173c79a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: MAT 14:25
Text: And in the fourth watch of the night Jesus went unto them, walking on the sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:baa30e5d-9650-49bd-942d-4c7fd37d109b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MAT 14:26
Text: And when the disciples saw him walking on the sea, they were troubled, saying, It is a spirit; and they cried out for fear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48bfc669-70a7-4269-a5e4-fbf30a41f30b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: MAT 14:27
Text: But straightway Jesus spake unto them, saying, Be of good cheer; it is I; be not afraid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:245fa916-d68f-4e15-a94a-393f6a0c49fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MAT 14:28
Text: And Peter answered him and said, Lord, if it be thou, bid me come unto thee on the water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c854df9-3081-4d68-b682-b657f23a0b60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: MAT 14:29
Text: And he said, Come. And when Peter was come down out of the ship, he walked on the water, to go to Jesus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7007298f-57b1-4720-9e51-6fe6c09fa1b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: MAT 14:30
Text: But when he saw the wind boisterous, he was afraid; and beginning to sink, he cried, saying, Lord, save me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43329498-4853-47c9-8cdd-acfaf5c7dc61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: MAT 14:31
Text: And immediately Jesus stretched forth his hand, and caught him, and said unto him, O thou of little faith, wherefore didst thou doubt?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85c6175d-17af-47c6-8cca-029d9cf82087>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: MAT 14:32
Text: And when they were come into the ship, the wind ceased.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59c25eb1-a788-449e-ac00-3df1de32397e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: MAT 14:33
Text: Then they that were in the ship came and worshipped him, saying, Of a truth thou art the Son of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fc51c3e-5e23-4f11-9dc6-f672895f615d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: MAT 14:34
Text: And when they were gone over, they came into the land of Gennesaret.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbd3de90-684d-47a9-8e48-0353b61c9a80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: MAT 14:35
Text: And when the men of that place had knowledge of him, they sent out into all that country round about, and brought unto him all that were diseased;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/14/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5444dcb3-9f36-4e17-8e97-fde3be6df9e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: MAT 14:36
Text: And besought him that they might only touch the hem of his garment: and as many as touched were made perfectly whole.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad749bbb-8ab8-41c5-b7d2-2564830cf886>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: MAT 15:1
Text: Then came to Jesus scribes and Pharisees, which were of Jerusalem, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c2619e6-462b-46e8-a416-3acdaaff34fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MAT 15:2
Text: Why do thy disciples transgress the tradition of the elders? for they wash not their hands when they eat bread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd26cf5f-8233-4bef-b02b-833f538400f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: MAT 15:3
Text: But he answered and said unto them, Why do ye also transgress the commandment of God by your tradition?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58b05d29-48eb-4cee-9c16-31b0bb68a6a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: MAT 15:4
Text: For God commanded, saying, Honour thy father and mother: and, He that curseth father or mother, let him die the death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:224b180c-db8f-4876-a292-cc9a7f0c4b20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: MAT 15:5
Text: But ye say, Whosoever shall say to his father or his mother, It is a gift, by whatsoever thou mightest be profited by me;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2783964e-28c3-44da-85e3-32c2c0221a5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: MAT 15:6
Text: And honour not his father or his mother, he shall be free. Thus have ye made the commandment of God of none effect by your tradition.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9654b5b3-c44d-4c7a-b55d-cb480f51abcc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: MAT 15:7
Text: Ye hypocrites, well did Esaias prophesy of you, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79eb7f71-6f80-4d5d-9ae5-d7f01408d5d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: MAT 15:8
Text: This people draweth nigh unto me with their mouth, and honoureth me with their lips; but their heart is far from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1355826d-ceab-482e-8f0f-d8620008a158>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: MAT 15:9
Text: But in vain they do worship me, teaching for doctrines the commandments of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f296baf9-9835-44ce-af3e-7a54d3e5ce6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: MAT 15:10
Text: And he called the multitude, and said unto them, Hear, and understand:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2cc64a02-67a0-4a68-b2ac-a3b38dce5d72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: MAT 15:11
Text: Not that which goeth into the mouth defileth a man; but that which cometh out of the mouth, this defileth a man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75ee8d6c-5db2-4c36-ad3b-36c335bd72e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: MAT 15:12
Text: Then came his disciples, and said unto him, Knowest thou that the Pharisees were offended, after they heard this saying?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47c1d2a3-4872-4c8b-b992-7ed0427e8387>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: MAT 15:13
Text: But he answered and said, Every plant, which my heavenly Father hath not planted, shall be rooted up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca768823-cea9-4df4-9c52-47b8b0f22190>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: MAT 15:14
Text: Let them alone: they be blind leaders of the blind. And if the blind lead the blind, both shall fall into the ditch.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e05ad607-8f22-45f1-b194-a639e44e1619>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: MAT 15:15
Text: Then answered Peter and said unto him, Declare unto us this parable.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35da9ffa-9958-41ff-b1a6-eafd0f1fdd2f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: MAT 15:16
Text: And Jesus said, Are ye also yet without understanding?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62ff11b0-bfd8-4a63-acc2-027e05ad6748>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: MAT 15:17
Text: Do not ye yet understand, that whatsoever entereth in at the mouth goeth into the belly, and is cast out into the draught?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80c57253-de9a-4bcd-a374-4ab20f31ed07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: MAT 15:18
Text: But those things which proceed out of the mouth come forth from the heart; and they defile the man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da07eef9-59c0-4258-a3c6-c5850e9a2713>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: MAT 15:19
Text: For out of the heart proceed evil thoughts, murders, adulteries, fornications, thefts, false witness, blasphemies:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7b51cc4-7abb-4f7b-a071-f738565bede2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: MAT 15:20
Text: These are the things which defile a man: but to eat with unwashen hands defileth not a man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:992c8b0e-3c7a-4ff9-876b-b710ebaca7b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: MAT 15:21
Text: Then Jesus went thence, and departed into the coasts of Tyre and Sidon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8211ac3c-5a8a-423e-888a-227a4a7bdbcc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: MAT 15:22
Text: And, behold, a woman of Canaan came out of the same coasts, and cried unto him, saying, Have mercy on me, O Lord, thou son of David; my daughter is grievously vexed with a devil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:480703c7-57b9-4f40-8525-532893acbbf9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: MAT 15:23
Text: But he answered her not a word. And his disciples came and besought him, saying, Send her away; for she crieth after us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c659d7c3-1abc-4f14-8d50-b4419980df42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: MAT 15:24
Text: But he answered and said, I am not sent but unto the lost sheep of the house of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bcd9e91d-cce8-42ff-a095-b185c6158162>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: MAT 15:25
Text: Then came she and worshipped him, saying, Lord, help me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0b3d4bb-ef31-49e0-98d4-c44214524856>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: MAT 15:26
Text: But he answered and said, It is not meet to take the children’s bread, and to cast it to dogs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f30e0179-9a86-456d-bd92-e4f96c562d23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: MAT 15:27
Text: And she said, Truth, Lord: yet the dogs eat of the crumbs which fall from their masters’ table.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4cb0b42-1047-477f-99d6-6ad03b0d03e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: MAT 15:28
Text: Then Jesus answered and said unto her, O woman, great is thy faith: be it unto thee even as thou wilt. And her daughter was made whole from that very hour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31b8fb86-f792-4d41-96da-d92be7337d39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: MAT 15:29
Text: And Jesus departed from thence, and came nigh unto the sea of Galilee; and went up into a mountain, and sat down there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5184045f-f2f9-4bf0-9b1e-d92ea0a1ff75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: MAT 15:30
Text: And great multitudes came unto him, having with them those that were lame, blind, dumb, maimed, and many others, and cast them down at Jesus’ feet; and he healed them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6d46e8e-57ab-46de-8a7f-c0314223b95a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: MAT 15:31
Text: Insomuch that the multitude wondered, when they saw the dumb to speak, the maimed to be whole, the lame to walk, and the blind to see: and they glorified the God of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5bc42bb-59ab-44ef-8f41-4fb5f70c8147>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: MAT 15:32
Text: Then Jesus called his disciples unto him, and said, I have compassion on the multitude, because they continue with me now three days, and have nothing to eat: and I will not send them away fasting, lest they faint in the way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb63aace-36ab-4c6d-b1d2-1cab527e91ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: MAT 15:33
Text: And his disciples say unto him, Whence should we have so much bread in the wilderness, as to fill so great a multitude?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a011cc6-69e6-48d5-9b31-6d6aecebc6d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: MAT 15:34
Text: And Jesus saith unto them, How many loaves have ye? And they said, Seven, and a few little fishes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2c313dd-4d2e-44b9-a4f8-3cb031287f3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: MAT 15:35
Text: And he commanded the multitude to sit down on the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53008319-0638-4903-82ae-c301c48bb107>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: MAT 15:36
Text: And he took the seven loaves and the fishes, and gave thanks, and brake them, and gave to his disciples, and the disciples to the multitude.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:881cdbe2-4a1b-42c9-9cbc-936fbabc3e4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: MAT 15:37
Text: And they did all eat, and were filled: and they took up of the broken meat that was left seven baskets full.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eee0abaf-d53c-4cbe-99ef-771caf227c34>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: MAT 15:38
Text: And they that did eat were four thousand men, beside women and children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/15/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7374135b-d108-4198-8d27-5c0c43fbb40d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: MAT 15:39
Text: And he sent away the multitude, and took ship, and came into the coasts of Magdala.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e19682b-057b-4162-bcc1-e40367b56444>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: MAT 16:1
Text: The Pharisees also with the Sadducees came, and tempting desired him that he would shew them a sign from heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15350d38-ac41-4d32-afa4-887ca66fa95f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: MAT 16:2
Text: He answered and said unto them, When it is evening, ye say, It will be fair weather: for the sky is red.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1b57c5e-6126-4e4d-9001-31f093fe5d32>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: MAT 16:3
Text: And in the morning, It will be foul weather to day: for the sky is red and lowering. O ye hypocrites, ye can discern the face of the sky; but can ye not discern the signs of the times?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9952b14-63fc-4d16-b24f-80b1d5f79514>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: MAT 16:4
Text: A wicked and adulterous generation seeketh after a sign; and there shall no sign be given unto it, but the sign of the prophet Jonas. And he left them, and departed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2157f5d7-89ed-4944-98b4-92b464d94520>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: MAT 16:5
Text: And when his disciples were come to the other side, they had forgotten to take bread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56f954ed-5524-44d5-8a11-dd1ff2d5aaa2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: MAT 16:6
Text: Then Jesus said unto them, Take heed and beware of the leaven of the Pharisees and of the Sadducees.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bef63833-0d75-45b9-abec-92a275fc0e1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: MAT 16:7
Text: And they reasoned among themselves, saying, It is because we have taken no bread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b802557f-c37a-4f29-a0e3-ed56b48e3867>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: MAT 16:8
Text: Which when Jesus perceived, he said unto them, O ye of little faith, why reason ye among yourselves, because ye have brought no bread?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4393329-3539-415c-9bbe-f7dd0946b12e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: MAT 16:9
Text: Do ye not yet understand, neither remember the five loaves of the five thousand, and how many baskets ye took up?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22140a4b-b1f2-45e3-bec6-99598c5d3613>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: MAT 16:10
Text: Neither the seven loaves of the four thousand, and how many baskets ye took up?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a594c9d1-21e8-4ca4-8539-66d8b1e85cde>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: MAT 16:11
Text: How is it that ye do not understand that I spake it not to you concerning bread, that ye should beware of the leaven of the Pharisees and of the Sadducees?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dde4870d-be13-4b29-a072-37c497c8a9c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: MAT 16:12
Text: Then understood they how that he bade them not beware of the leaven of bread, but of the doctrine of the Pharisees and of the Sadducees.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16910f98-769a-4582-bf63-1d87e4ea3597>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: MAT 16:13
Text: When Jesus came into the coasts of Caesarea Philippi, he asked his disciples, saying, Whom do men say that I the Son of man am?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff7a17ab-540a-47d4-9a27-2834fa16d8c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: MAT 16:14
Text: And they said, Some say that thou art John the Baptist: some, Elias; and others, Jeremias, or one of the prophets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f7df334-6218-4c98-90f1-463cb5f43c7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: MAT 16:15
Text: He saith unto them, But whom say ye that I am?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c847e56-2257-4252-858a-68e0cedfeb6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: MAT 16:16
Text: And Simon Peter answered and said, Thou art the Christ, the Son of the living God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2287c6d7-0d72-44e6-80e4-15358b8bea5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: MAT 16:17
Text: And Jesus answered and said unto him, Blessed art thou, Simon Barjona: for flesh and blood hath not revealed it unto thee, but my Father which is in heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb94b84d-b184-48cd-a4bf-c87ddcabf82e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: MAT 16:18
Text: And I say also unto thee, That thou art Peter, and upon this rock I will build my church; and the gates of hell shall not prevail against it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb39faea-5758-47d2-85a1-98c0fed04f79>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: MAT 16:19
Text: And I will give unto thee the keys of the kingdom of heaven: and whatsoever thou shalt bind on earth shall be bound in heaven: and whatsoever thou shalt loose on earth shall be loosed in heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c20b17f-e041-450b-9b74-05cf4e2f03f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: MAT 16:20
Text: Then charged he his disciples that they should tell no man that he was Jesus the Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddb0b7db-8573-44fd-aae0-99af5c5826d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: MAT 16:21
Text: From that time forth began Jesus to shew unto his disciples, how that he must go unto Jerusalem, and suffer many things of the elders and chief priests and scribes, and be killed, and be raised again the third day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c05c48ae-9b11-46cd-9039-44f5a142d7ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: MAT 16:22
Text: Then Peter took him, and began to rebuke him, saying, Be it far from thee, Lord: this shall not be unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf2124f6-8085-4f21-8f74-6351f22baf74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: MAT 16:23
Text: But he turned, and said unto Peter, Get thee behind me, Satan: thou art an offence unto me: for thou savourest not the things that be of God, but those that be of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90fa724e-cca0-4a5d-828f-93bdd7c917ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: MAT 16:24
Text: Then said Jesus unto his disciples, If any man will come after me, let him deny himself, and take up his cross, and follow me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64a6dfef-e506-40af-9323-89bad8f14518>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: MAT 16:25
Text: For whosoever will save his life shall lose it: and whosoever will lose his life for my sake shall find it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f70a872-a40a-4d20-af33-962d1c2312d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: MAT 16:26
Text: For what is a man profited, if he shall gain the whole world, and lose his own soul? or what shall a man give in exchange for his soul?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb1042fd-39ae-464b-95d3-5efc1cb380e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: MAT 16:27
Text: For the Son of man shall come in the glory of his Father with his angels; and then he shall reward every man according to his works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/16/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c88db88-9809-41ad-a922-eaf3cc556607>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: MAT 16:28
Text: Verily I say unto you, There be some standing here, which shall not taste of death, till they see the Son of man coming in his kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a89e421-dc8d-4b58-9503-aa6863e0e206>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: MAT 17:1
Text: And after six days Jesus taketh Peter, James, and John his brother, and bringeth them up into an high mountain apart,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c1b3250-e5f4-4c7d-8472-f030e76b075c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: MAT 17:2
Text: And was transfigured before them: and his face did shine as the sun, and his raiment was white as the light.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3b58b32-f6ba-4aab-b697-3be087371610>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: MAT 17:3
Text: And, behold, there appeared unto them Moses and Elias talking with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c461d21e-e301-4030-b51a-dd776629ac3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: MAT 17:4
Text: Then answered Peter, and said unto Jesus, Lord, it is good for us to be here: if thou wilt, let us make here three tabernacles; one for thee, and one for Moses, and one for Elias.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47c11a62-ff61-4768-b4f2-ff65a590b4b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: MAT 17:5
Text: While he yet spake, behold, a bright cloud overshadowed them: and behold a voice out of the cloud, which said, This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased; hear ye him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f41b2e8d-7922-47b5-9d93-9fd21986a886>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: MAT 17:6
Text: And when the disciples heard it, they fell on their face, and were sore afraid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7dda0428-e3a3-49fb-8509-b7fcfd928691>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: MAT 17:7
Text: And Jesus came and touched them, and said, Arise, and be not afraid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48b47388-82f2-4f0a-8def-5d3ecf409249>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: MAT 17:8
Text: And when they had lifted up their eyes, they saw no man, save Jesus only.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d186c5d-5cae-428d-a710-6c26a234e867>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: MAT 17:9
Text: And as they came down from the mountain, Jesus charged them, saying, Tell the vision to no man, until the Son of man be risen again from the dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99049235-3908-41f3-a16f-f9d3b75278a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MAT 17:10
Text: And his disciples asked him, saying, Why then say the scribes that Elias must first come?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f39f256-180d-4390-a1ba-f35bc48e5fd0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: MAT 17:11
Text: And Jesus answered and said unto them, Elias truly shall first come, and restore all things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86e93529-14f1-49ce-aae4-5c5ae9bfa075>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: MAT 17:12
Text: But I say unto you, That Elias is come already, and they knew him not, but have done unto him whatsoever they listed. Likewise shall also the Son of man suffer of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76d376d6-0327-4ae6-ad14-7593e1b344b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: MAT 17:13
Text: Then the disciples understood that he spake unto them of John the Baptist.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a207aaa8-6f49-47b8-84bf-6db090ebab86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: MAT 17:14
Text: And when they were come to the multitude, there came to him a certain man, kneeling down to him, and saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0fc8e2c8-486e-42fd-9e7b-74fe4b0a65ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: MAT 17:15
Text: Lord, have mercy on my son: for he is lunatick, and sore vexed: for ofttimes he falleth into the fire, and oft into the water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:500e9dce-1992-42d6-8f65-858e22a2d499>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: MAT 17:16
Text: And I brought him to thy disciples, and they could not cure him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2e5ca29-c0c3-4eb5-9e35-cc08310e045c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: MAT 17:17
Text: Then Jesus answered and said, O faithless and perverse generation, how long shall I be with you? how long shall I suffer you? bring him hither to me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8681fae0-694d-4498-bde0-46637383bc38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: MAT 17:18
Text: And Jesus rebuked the devil; and he departed out of him: and the child was cured from that very hour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:415f5ad2-7d29-4863-8bbe-c1d085c7a517>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: MAT 17:19
Text: Then came the disciples to Jesus apart, and said, Why could not we cast him out?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:969985b1-ebc7-4c6b-b17c-baed7e35d6e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 277

Reference: MAT 17:20
Text: And Jesus said unto them, Because of your unbelief: for verily I say unto you, If ye have faith as a grain of mustard seed, ye shall say unto this mountain, Remove hence to yonder place; and it shall remove; and nothing shall be impossible unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c90f0532-a1a6-44db-88a4-771306127ff9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: MAT 17:21
Text: Howbeit this kind goeth not out but by prayer and fasting.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:577e4d3b-e649-409e-99b5-b017a200a973>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MAT 17:22
Text: And while they abode in Galilee, Jesus said unto them, The Son of man shall be betrayed into the hands of men:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d64521e7-ea09-4175-af35-0d5520f8a9ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: MAT 17:23
Text: And they shall kill him, and the third day he shall be raised again. And they were exceeding sorry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e230b477-1b88-469c-969f-6835dbd79d64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: MAT 17:24
Text: And when they were come to Capernaum, they that received tribute money came to Peter, and said, Doth not your master pay tribute?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a0d2ece-fa9c-4fe0-ba58-acfb3d88509e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: MAT 17:25
Text: He saith, Yes. And when he was come into the house, Jesus prevented him, saying, What thinkest thou, Simon? of whom do the kings of the earth take custom or tribute? of their own children, or of strangers?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd54ceae-4db6-4833-ab46-1ec89d4c9a3b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: MAT 17:26
Text: Peter saith unto him, Of strangers. Jesus saith unto him, Then are the children free.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/17/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc8c1021-cfad-4317-9968-62060e861379>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: MAT 17:27
Text: Notwithstanding, lest we should offend them, go thou to the sea, and cast an hook, and take up the fish that first cometh up; and when thou hast opened his mouth, thou shalt find a piece of money: that take, and give unto them for me and thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:582f22d8-5b10-4177-9f72-884733ec48ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: MAT 18:1
Text: At the same time came the disciples unto Jesus, saying, Who is the greatest in the kingdom of heaven?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:144f74c8-7796-4fa6-b6e5-d858303fb834>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: MAT 18:2
Text: And Jesus called a little child unto him, and set him in the midst of them,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ccf45e22-818b-48db-b938-dcc6ca60b4cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: MAT 18:3
Text: And said, Verily I say unto you, Except ye be converted, and become as little children, ye shall not enter into the kingdom of heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:897fa367-baa0-47ac-bba9-0245b3e9ed45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: MAT 18:4
Text: Whosoever therefore shall humble himself as this little child, the same is greatest in the kingdom of heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:800c1f6a-013a-4a28-8134-4f6c4bbe8c8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: MAT 18:5
Text: And whoso shall receive one such little child in my name receiveth me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f179bcdc-a4d7-4161-93db-c39c56c9eb5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: MAT 18:6
Text: But whoso shall offend one of these little ones which believe in me, it were better for him that a millstone were hanged about his neck, and that he were drowned in the depth of the sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7cda968b-78ca-4a73-b735-716b44e434b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: MAT 18:7
Text: Woe unto the world because of offences! for it must needs be that offences come; but woe to that man by whom the offence cometh!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:319c6c73-f255-4dbe-86c3-a925d8f169a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: MAT 18:8
Text: Wherefore if thy hand or thy foot offend thee, cut them off, and cast them from thee: it is better for thee to enter into life halt or maimed, rather than having two hands or two feet to be cast into everlasting fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b404ad9a-63f9-410e-ac18-1833ced69e5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: MAT 18:9
Text: And if thine eye offend thee, pluck it out, and cast it from thee: it is better for thee to enter into life with one eye, rather than having two eyes to be cast into hell fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7a609d9-f3f4-46e0-af33-c78f8c1dfea5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: MAT 18:10
Text: Take heed that ye despise not one of these little ones; for I say unto you, That in heaven their angels do always behold the face of my Father which is in heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:321b5656-49f3-4193-b919-bbeca1b053f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: MAT 18:11
Text: For the Son of man is come to save that which was lost.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94b422b5-e954-424b-a6a4-550dc0782816>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: MAT 18:12
Text: How think ye? if a man have an hundred sheep, and one of them be gone astray, doth he not leave the ninety and nine, and goeth into the mountains, and seeketh that which is gone astray?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28af3d98-833a-47b7-aed6-b131def7641f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: MAT 18:13
Text: And if so be that he find it, verily I say unto you, he rejoiceth more of that sheep, than of the ninety and nine which went not astray.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f082b9b-706d-4154-b513-67b84f24d6c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: MAT 18:14
Text: Even so it is not the will of your Father which is in heaven, that one of these little ones should perish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bdb01d27-c722-4d1f-99f4-f4993bbeb47b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: MAT 18:15
Text: Moreover if thy brother shall trespass against thee, go and tell him his fault between thee and him alone: if he shall hear thee, thou hast gained thy brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa2f4088-be6c-44cf-86b3-567b8bfd8131>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: MAT 18:16
Text: But if he will not hear thee, then take with thee one or two more, that in the mouth of two or three witnesses every word may be established.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3e4e436-26ad-40be-8b1f-dc4dc09a8c40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: MAT 18:17
Text: And if he shall neglect to hear them, tell it unto the church: but if he neglect to hear the church, let him be unto thee as an heathen man and a publican.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3a0dd22-967f-4b36-a7bf-5ff98c2801d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: MAT 18:18
Text: Verily I say unto you, Whatsoever ye shall bind on earth shall be bound in heaven: and whatsoever ye shall loose on earth shall be loosed in heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbdbe2ea-4b1e-4bd6-bfeb-6aa23bd0579e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: MAT 18:19
Text: Again I say unto you, That if two of you shall agree on earth as touching any thing that they shall ask, it shall be done for them of my Father which is in heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8357b51e-64cb-492a-b10d-90a903f58e88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MAT 18:20
Text: For where two or three are gathered together in my name, there am I in the midst of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7259d30d-46f2-44fe-9b78-f25fb2dfdccb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: MAT 18:21
Text: Then came Peter to him, and said, Lord, how oft shall my brother sin against me, and I forgive him? till seven times?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b78575d1-2560-4faa-877f-33ad9261cb86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: MAT 18:22
Text: Jesus saith unto him, I say not unto thee, Until seven times: but, Until seventy times seven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d65d16a-ab8a-435d-b9ea-a9a6f305544e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: MAT 18:23
Text: Therefore is the kingdom of heaven likened unto a certain king, which would take account of his servants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8e33845-741a-4d4b-8cff-00afebbb5fb6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: MAT 18:24
Text: And when he had begun to reckon, one was brought unto him, which owed him ten thousand talents.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b7c59b1-e82f-4a94-9613-465a440297aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: MAT 18:25
Text: But forasmuch as he had not to pay, his lord commanded him to be sold, and his wife, and children, and all that he had, and payment to be made.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d4f2721-e774-4ac6-9774-14bcb3596609>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: MAT 18:26
Text: The servant therefore fell down, and worshipped him, saying, Lord, have patience with me, and I will pay thee all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b356e859-341d-46bf-abe1-9bec05ad4cd3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: MAT 18:27
Text: Then the lord of that servant was moved with compassion, and loosed him, and forgave him the debt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbdcb623-4925-46b3-9000-d3b2f15b3b84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: MAT 18:28
Text: But the same servant went out, and found one of his fellowservants, which owed him an hundred pence: and he laid hands on him, and took him by the throat, saying, Pay me that thou owest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb74df16-9d14-41e5-a300-8d6459b2a61f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: MAT 18:29
Text: And his fellowservant fell down at his feet, and besought him, saying, Have patience with me, and I will pay thee all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42a4177e-80fb-4695-bf0a-225dcaf40a22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: MAT 18:30
Text: And he would not: but went and cast him into prison, till he should pay the debt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8962f460-9e49-476b-911f-7883bf03a2e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: MAT 18:31
Text: So when his fellowservants saw what was done, they were very sorry, and came and told unto their lord all that was done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df245c99-4342-482e-b725-dc926a193464>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: MAT 18:32
Text: Then his lord, after that he had called him, said unto him, O thou wicked servant, I forgave thee all that debt, because thou desiredst me:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5cfbe6f1-6b87-407e-8100-ca8e07f961a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: MAT 18:33
Text: Shouldest not thou also have had compassion on thy fellowservant, even as I had pity on thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20b9f9dc-99a6-4356-9278-ad348939811f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: MAT 18:34
Text: And his lord was wroth, and delivered him to the tormentors, till he should pay all that was due unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/18/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:246316b8-cad6-4ab4-a0fd-fa0b7016ae90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: MAT 18:35
Text: So likewise shall my heavenly Father do also unto you, if ye from your hearts forgive not every one his brother their trespasses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d8b0be3-c089-42a5-8653-ddb2a9bb9fad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: MAT 19:1
Text: And it came to pass, that when Jesus had finished these sayings, he departed from Galilee, and came into the coasts of Judaea beyond Jordan;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80677856-7796-4bb5-8dfe-1f8f9c3fd146>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: MAT 19:2
Text: And great multitudes followed him; and he healed them there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf5c34d9-8ebc-4fa8-be74-952f0d7f6757>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: MAT 19:3
Text: The Pharisees also came unto him, tempting him, and saying unto him, Is it lawful for a man to put away his wife for every cause?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f89f180-3117-49d0-a511-22f9a8795b46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: MAT 19:4
Text: And he answered and said unto them, Have ye not read, that he which made them at the beginning made them male and female,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9523d89f-2391-4866-b93e-f492deb6d43b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: MAT 19:5
Text: And said, For this cause shall a man leave father and mother, and shall cleave to his wife: and they twain shall be one flesh?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e87b1d10-569e-42ab-9a84-2c594d457b88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: MAT 19:6
Text: Wherefore they are no more twain, but one flesh. What therefore God hath joined together, let not man put asunder.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e71de6ab-75d7-4a36-a0c1-cc987e47cd63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: MAT 19:7
Text: They say unto him, Why did Moses then command to give a writing of divorcement, and to put her away?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45b6f65c-4aa1-41d8-b6cc-27844e66a7c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: MAT 19:8
Text: He saith unto them, Moses because of the hardness of your hearts suffered you to put away your wives: but from the beginning it was not so.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bbda074-4261-4fb6-aa18-4e0779ee0c54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: MAT 19:9
Text: And I say unto you, Whosoever shall put away his wife, except it be for fornication, and shall marry another, committeth adultery: and whoso marrieth her which is put away doth commit adultery.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7d43ae0-0257-4853-a852-4c4f472b422e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: MAT 19:10
Text: His disciples say unto him, If the case of the man be so with his wife, it is not good to marry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1106016-53e3-4920-8bc3-a9da195a6687>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MAT 19:11
Text: But he said unto them, All men cannot receive this saying, save they to whom it is given.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:699294a9-679c-4668-9f9c-cbcde6677742>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 306

Reference: MAT 19:12
Text: For there are some eunuchs, which were so born from their mother’s womb: and there are some eunuchs, which were made eunuchs of men: and there be eunuchs, which have made themselves eunuchs for the kingdom of heaven’s sake. He that is able to receive it, let him receive it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec69a211-0a9f-44bc-aa0b-97902485e7de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: MAT 19:13
Text: Then were there brought unto him little children, that he should put his hands on them, and pray: and the disciples rebuked them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9dd308a-3850-45bb-9974-b550d1c0c888>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: MAT 19:14
Text: But Jesus said, Suffer little children, and forbid them not, to come unto me: for of such is the kingdom of heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1eceeb91-3656-4001-839c-925c8ad35732>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: MAT 19:15
Text: And he laid his hands on them, and departed thence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09c5f3ad-28fc-4779-b0ac-99417de9fb4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: MAT 19:16
Text: And, behold, one came and said unto him, Good Master, what good thing shall I do, that I may have eternal life?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5564440d-4846-4d35-8b03-53b9172cbdea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: MAT 19:17
Text: And he said unto him, Why callest thou me good? there is none good but one, that is, God: but if thou wilt enter into life, keep the commandments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0dd58b1a-8a92-4463-b50e-a6a34bf6c3c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: MAT 19:18
Text: He saith unto him, Which? Jesus said, Thou shalt do no murder, Thou shalt not commit adultery, Thou shalt not steal, Thou shalt not bear false witness,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19498ece-7350-4719-9340-9517c6d1a90a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: MAT 19:19
Text: Honour thy father and thy mother: and, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad3f4f8c-b711-4f05-847e-2816d7ab9032>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: MAT 19:20
Text: The young man saith unto him, All these things have I kept from my youth up: what lack I yet?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80abac90-8e75-4c26-b113-b0ef1c5b9b5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: MAT 19:21
Text: Jesus said unto him, If thou wilt be perfect, go and sell that thou hast, and give to the poor, and thou shalt have treasure in heaven: and come and follow me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ed8d7f8-7c19-41ab-b16c-fb7acec863b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: MAT 19:22
Text: But when the young man heard that saying, he went away sorrowful: for he had great possessions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:321351d8-5bde-4d75-8ce5-c077b7773545>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: MAT 19:23
Text: Then said Jesus unto his disciples, Verily I say unto you, That a rich man shall hardly enter into the kingdom of heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8caa2c72-ca43-4cb9-873d-9b9b1257440b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: MAT 19:24
Text: And again I say unto you, It is easier for a camel to go through the eye of a needle, than for a rich man to enter into the kingdom of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fbfa7ce-f529-4117-856c-5170ef68b83f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MAT 19:25
Text: When his disciples heard it, they were exceedingly amazed, saying, Who then can be saved?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:604d4b77-29bf-4d16-b94c-cc104adb45b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: MAT 19:26
Text: But Jesus beheld them, and said unto them, With men this is impossible; but with God all things are possible.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9cd56664-a242-451f-947c-a3deea364a77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: MAT 19:27
Text: Then answered Peter and said unto him, Behold, we have forsaken all, and followed thee; what shall we have therefore?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1259ecad-7d44-4914-807a-edbaa0b9fbbd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 262

Reference: MAT 19:28
Text: And Jesus said unto them, Verily I say unto you, That ye which have followed me, in the regeneration when the Son of man shall sit in the throne of his glory, ye also shall sit upon twelve thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf61f1fe-bd39-4dba-beef-375de8814fa6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: MAT 19:29
Text: And every one that hath forsaken houses, or brethren, or sisters, or father, or mother, or wife, or children, or lands, for my name’s sake, shall receive an hundredfold, and shall inherit everlasting life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/19/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:deadd071-d5dc-4e25-9280-48004744a964>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: MAT 19:30
Text: But many that are first shall be last; and the last shall be first.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33f837ba-c660-4173-a180-0517cd658dcb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: MAT 20:1
Text: For the kingdom of heaven is like unto a man that is an householder, which went out early in the morning to hire labourers into his vineyard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51a7adf6-0525-46ab-82d3-2a3c63506407>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: MAT 20:2
Text: And when he had agreed with the labourers for a penny a day, he sent them into his vineyard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ab220d8-95c6-4c71-bcc6-99532625d015>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: MAT 20:3
Text: And he went out about the third hour, and saw others standing idle in the marketplace,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b023c68-724a-4651-b443-5b6e11ed6c5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: MAT 20:4
Text: And said unto them; Go ye also into the vineyard, and whatsoever is right I will give you. And they went their way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2458b26a-b17d-40e2-9383-2e6406217700>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: MAT 20:5
Text: Again he went out about the sixth and ninth hour, and did likewise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2743c602-e5bb-4eb2-8f2c-9628f3d48932>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: MAT 20:6
Text: And about the eleventh hour he went out, and found others standing idle, and saith unto them, Why stand ye here all the day idle?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56ddd73a-93de-4129-9f0e-5e94976e9aa2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: MAT 20:7
Text: They say unto him, Because no man hath hired us. He saith unto them, Go ye also into the vineyard; and whatsoever is right, that shall ye receive.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6dc85a2d-2478-4bf9-9ce1-7e27d9f90711>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: MAT 20:8
Text: So when even was come, the lord of the vineyard saith unto his steward, Call the labourers, and give them their hire, beginning from the last unto the first.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d9380b6-3fb3-4439-9095-a51e6a443d70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: MAT 20:9
Text: And when they came that were hired about the eleventh hour, they received every man a penny.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc509eea-b3e8-499c-a971-26acb3068224>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: MAT 20:10
Text: But when the first came, they supposed that they should have received more; and they likewise received every man a penny.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:867b3f13-2a68-4594-bd10-fbe2b4822615>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: MAT 20:11
Text: And when they had received it, they murmured against the goodman of the house,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7552bd42-535f-4ec5-9c38-6e45b385046b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: MAT 20:12
Text: Saying, These last have wrought but one hour, and thou hast made them equal unto us, which have borne the burden and heat of the day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d1b3f51-e71b-4f73-a123-f9e53d621724>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: MAT 20:13
Text: But he answered one of them, and said, Friend, I do thee no wrong: didst not thou agree with me for a penny?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f23068b-e7ed-4097-a7df-9d5daaf218f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: MAT 20:14
Text: Take that thine is, and go thy way: I will give unto this last, even as unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f6384f2-7083-42e7-87e9-aa09727ec023>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MAT 20:15
Text: Is it not lawful for me to do what I will with mine own? Is thine eye evil, because I am good?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fbccc6e-0bbd-4a68-80e4-eca4e09ccdd2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: MAT 20:16
Text: So the last shall be first, and the first last: for many be called, but few chosen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e68c81eb-ce65-4efd-92b0-6a3309bfe562>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: MAT 20:17
Text: And Jesus going up to Jerusalem took the twelve disciples apart in the way, and said unto them,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f02cee3-110f-483c-9825-22d4b1f56d13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: MAT 20:18
Text: Behold, we go up to Jerusalem; and the Son of man shall be betrayed unto the chief priests and unto the scribes, and they shall condemn him to death,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d45a2f4-f938-4e85-bae8-eea0e9c08bf0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: MAT 20:19
Text: And shall deliver him to the Gentiles to mock, and to scourge, and to crucify him: and the third day he shall rise again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a377ee5a-c978-4c82-8e3e-566bbbc1412e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: MAT 20:20
Text: Then came to him the mother of Zebedee’s children with her sons, worshipping him, and desiring a certain thing of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72b8b2f8-e704-4e43-ac1f-690072c5cdc2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: MAT 20:21
Text: And he said unto her, What wilt thou? She saith unto him, Grant that these my two sons may sit, the one on thy right hand, and the other on the left, in thy kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1d976ab-6e0d-4002-aa5c-3b9eb5d41f60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: MAT 20:22
Text: But Jesus answered and said, Ye know not what ye ask. Are ye able to drink of the cup that I shall drink of, and to be baptized with the baptism that I am baptized with? They say unto him, We are able.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:102c6904-1d72-4988-b7c1-76b8e3a35d93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: MAT 20:23
Text: And he saith unto them, Ye shall drink indeed of my cup, and be baptized with the baptism that I am baptized with: but to sit on my right hand, and on my left, is not mine to give, but it shall be given to them for whom it is prepared of my Father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bc30b14-7233-4826-b563-ebba4478fd98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: MAT 20:24
Text: And when the ten heard it, they were moved with indignation against the two brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:209c05fb-39c4-4034-9f65-f63116a472f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: MAT 20:25
Text: But Jesus called them unto him, and said, Ye know that the princes of the Gentiles exercise dominion over them, and they that are great exercise authority upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4019e647-3c8d-438c-8768-787088496efc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: MAT 20:26
Text: But it shall not be so among you: but whosoever will be great among you, let him be your minister;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a87963f7-b867-4202-b0c4-369c6bd901f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: MAT 20:27
Text: And whosoever will be chief among you, let him be your servant:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5226015-e83b-43a9-8290-8d5e05bf27f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: MAT 20:28
Text: Even as the Son of man came not to be ministered unto, but to minister, and to give his life a ransom for many.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad605231-c7c8-4f8b-9eac-65dc7bb46091>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: MAT 20:29
Text: And as they departed from Jericho, a great multitude followed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:817fcfab-87e9-456c-bfb8-e78ecec83f53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: MAT 20:30
Text: And, behold, two blind men sitting by the way side, when they heard that Jesus passed by, cried out, saying, Have mercy on us, O Lord, thou son of David.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:988a6c10-0e86-459d-b698-ce79316c2e07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: MAT 20:31
Text: And the multitude rebuked them, because they should hold their peace: but they cried the more, saying, Have mercy on us, O Lord, thou son of David.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c19e6ae-ed77-420a-8e5a-78c3a7ab9edb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: MAT 20:32
Text: And Jesus stood still, and called them, and said, What will ye that I shall do unto you?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5388b838-1f4d-4afa-8681-83e0182ac0ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: MAT 20:33
Text: They say unto him, Lord, that our eyes may be opened.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/20/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a58d550b-4843-4e55-8e71-b0d6d57d42a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: MAT 20:34
Text: So Jesus had compassion on them, and touched their eyes: and immediately their eyes received sight, and they followed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:544011d8-9f05-45e6-bb07-c8a3aba4868a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MAT 21:1
Text: And when they drew nigh unto Jerusalem, and were come to Bethphage, unto the mount of Olives, then sent Jesus two disciples,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b3585ca-5117-4a89-bb2a-b09dfb7bdea1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: MAT 21:2
Text: Saying unto them, Go into the village over against you, and straightway ye shall find an ass tied, and a colt with her: loose them, and bring them unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9fbc0a1-e8d1-4595-9572-d58c2c913416>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MAT 21:3
Text: And if any man say ought unto you, ye shall say, The Lord hath need of them; and straightway he will send them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:022e1a9b-6261-4784-8db8-ed272d7ede12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: MAT 21:4
Text: All this was done, that it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the prophet, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c31e2761-fddd-4b0d-a5b0-aba9d730994d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: MAT 21:5
Text: Tell ye the daughter of Sion, Behold, thy King cometh unto thee, meek, and sitting upon an ass, and a colt the foal of an ass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9e4ecbb-1f0e-48a1-876c-67c9217d181e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: MAT 21:6
Text: And the disciples went, and did as Jesus commanded them,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c2aab97-59e6-4d3d-aa32-761cda74607d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: MAT 21:7
Text: And brought the ass, and the colt, and put on them their clothes, and they set him thereon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e1d6ab9-2bcd-4fa2-8ba0-ca9ee844b611>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: MAT 21:8
Text: And a very great multitude spread their garments in the way; others cut down branches from the trees, and strawed them in the way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c773882b-f522-4f55-887b-e7ed64b8c29e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: MAT 21:9
Text: And the multitudes that went before, and that followed, cried, saying, Hosanna to the son of David: Blessed is he that cometh in the name of the Lord; Hosanna in the highest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b69c0f0-8161-4b57-89dd-c1f1360adfc5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: MAT 21:10
Text: And when he was come into Jerusalem, all the city was moved, saying, Who is this?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ee5809e-d300-4f27-8f0b-932deb55c921>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: MAT 21:11
Text: And the multitude said, This is Jesus the prophet of Nazareth of Galilee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b2af4b3-2fa5-4827-a2a3-20f734d62d7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: MAT 21:12
Text: And Jesus went into the temple of God, and cast out all them that sold and bought in the temple, and overthrew the tables of the moneychangers, and the seats of them that sold doves,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:599c7ea3-1f96-47a5-a154-4ebe50dc1650>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: MAT 21:13
Text: And said unto them, It is written, My house shall be called the house of prayer; but ye have made it a den of thieves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0dd59421-38fe-40a2-8740-9eb144ab9f51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: MAT 21:14
Text: And the blind and the lame came to him in the temple; and he healed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c362d63e-018d-4001-96e6-e37475ea057b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: MAT 21:15
Text: And when the chief priests and scribes saw the wonderful things that he did, and the children crying in the temple, and saying, Hosanna to the son of David; they were sore displeased,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af25b425-c07c-4bfa-a98f-423b5b7a1835>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: MAT 21:16
Text: And said unto him, Hearest thou what these say? And Jesus saith unto them, Yea; have ye never read, Out of the mouth of babes and sucklings thou hast perfected praise?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87d6649b-3f5c-4d6a-b0fa-65c72609d27a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: MAT 21:17
Text: And he left them, and went out of the city into Bethany; and he lodged there.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94299ddf-07cb-4250-9acd-0b6749438c92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: MAT 21:18
Text: Now in the morning as he returned into the city, he hungered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29318cd0-14c7-4927-aaac-fa939795044f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: MAT 21:19
Text: And when he saw a fig tree in the way, he came to it, and found nothing thereon, but leaves only, and said unto it, Let no fruit grow on thee henceforward for ever. And presently the fig tree withered away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a3447e0-9d4c-46b0-94bf-c7bb25c74cc2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MAT 21:20
Text: And when the disciples saw it, they marvelled, saying, How soon is the fig tree withered away!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3811db13-c132-4fa8-8701-932351da50b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 286

Reference: MAT 21:21
Text: Jesus answered and said unto them, Verily I say unto you, If ye have faith, and doubt not, ye shall not only do this which is done to the fig tree, but also if ye shall say unto this mountain, Be thou removed, and be thou cast into the sea; it shall be done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01e8a859-5d40-40d6-9872-2cf0b044c519>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: MAT 21:22
Text: And all things, whatsoever ye shall ask in prayer, believing, ye shall receive.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be118b7f-7cc9-47ce-8fea-7ae06fd95303>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: MAT 21:23
Text: And when he was come into the temple, the chief priests and the elders of the people came unto him as he was teaching, and said, By what authority doest thou these things? and who gave thee this authority?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5abcae3-b9f9-461d-880a-a811ab28ee5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: MAT 21:24
Text: And Jesus answered and said unto them, I also will ask you one thing, which if ye tell me, I in like wise will tell you by what authority I do these things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98ed1280-f56f-473a-9c01-94bfa77f35e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: MAT 21:25
Text: The baptism of John, whence was it? from heaven, or of men? And they reasoned with themselves, saying, If we shall say, From heaven; he will say unto us, Why did ye not then believe him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87c82f29-64f7-46bb-9bec-aef6b1f2803a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: MAT 21:26
Text: But if we shall say, Of men; we fear the people; for all hold John as a prophet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:879c717d-aa21-43f4-9917-7072a63583df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: MAT 21:27
Text: And they answered Jesus, and said, We cannot tell. And he said unto them, Neither tell I you by what authority I do these things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8698ebb-1aad-4d23-9d96-c08efed51265>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: MAT 21:28
Text: But what think ye? A certain man had two sons; and he came to the first, and said, Son, go work to day in my vineyard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b28c010f-43e2-4f74-844f-e69369d55f12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: MAT 21:29
Text: He answered and said, I will not: but afterward he repented, and went.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6774d64-3d22-43a5-bf10-888b1898a1ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: MAT 21:30
Text: And he came to the second, and said likewise. And he answered and said, I go, sir: and went not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c35c8cc2-59ff-4b16-b00f-c23a07b3c7ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: MAT 21:31
Text: Whether of them twain did the will of his father? They say unto him, The first. Jesus saith unto them, Verily I say unto you, That the publicans and the harlots go into the kingdom of God before you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:043c92f0-5d3c-4e40-a752-ae40c0f7176d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: MAT 21:32
Text: For John came unto you in the way of righteousness, and ye believed him not: but the publicans and the harlots believed him: and ye, when ye had seen it, repented not afterward, that ye might believe him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d175c48d-3d9c-4f6e-91c4-c0ada786c86f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: MAT 21:33
Text: Hear another parable: There was a certain householder, which planted a vineyard, and hedged it round about, and digged a winepress in it, and built a tower, and let it out to husbandmen, and went into a far country:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b12e001d-3628-4c6c-a0cc-77e8a9b4573f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MAT 21:34
Text: And when the time of the fruit drew near, he sent his servants to the husbandmen, that they might receive the fruits of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f1efe3e-a90a-4f1b-99ff-22bb45792d5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: MAT 21:35
Text: And the husbandmen took his servants, and beat one, and killed another, and stoned another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ff86444-d236-43c1-bae0-1537877c0d59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: MAT 21:36
Text: Again, he sent other servants more than the first: and they did unto them likewise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b6786d8-3843-4a2c-b542-16f4fd88f43d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: MAT 21:37
Text: But last of all he sent unto them his son, saying, They will reverence my son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fad1467-2569-462e-9776-8bc0a4e9d83a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: MAT 21:38
Text: But when the husbandmen saw the son, they said among themselves, This is the heir; come, let us kill him, and let us seize on his inheritance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e792460a-8432-4310-ae21-94d2e590a0c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: MAT 21:39
Text: And they caught him, and cast him out of the vineyard, and slew him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a73fc80-25ec-4a17-9858-401eb0dccced>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MAT 21:40
Text: When the lord therefore of the vineyard cometh, what will he do unto those husbandmen?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4809528b-85cb-424e-baa5-3ec24021b7e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: MAT 21:41
Text: They say unto him, He will miserably destroy those wicked men, and will let out his vineyard unto other husbandmen, which shall render him the fruits in their seasons.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff185eda-5097-40c1-b4a7-a0a785ca0090>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: MAT 21:42
Text: Jesus saith unto them, Did ye never read in the scriptures, The stone which the builders rejected, the same is become the head of the corner: this is the Lord’s doing, and it is marvellous in our eyes?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a7f82c3-a410-4911-ad7c-f831a85615f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: MAT 21:43
Text: Therefore say I unto you, The kingdom of God shall be taken from you, and given to a nation bringing forth the fruits thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f130d2f-e3c6-4614-947c-adb316975664>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: MAT 21:44
Text: And whosoever shall fall on this stone shall be broken: but on whomsoever it shall fall, it will grind him to powder.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4b1146e-67d5-48f9-88b6-4e3aec27fc84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: MAT 21:45
Text: And when the chief priests and Pharisees had heard his parables, they perceived that he spake of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/21/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e0f6885-801d-4db2-9b49-9b6adbde84bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: MAT 21:46
Text: But when they sought to lay hands on him, they feared the multitude, because they took him for a prophet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4be12d21-3b08-4e8d-9055-76ba29ebe97b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: MAT 22:1
Text: And Jesus answered and spake unto them again by parables, and said,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ca922eb-baf7-4b12-8a18-8abd8ec2ac39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: MAT 22:2
Text: The kingdom of heaven is like unto a certain king, which made a marriage for his son,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a432ac3e-0fdc-4246-8439-0016d5b52fe7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: MAT 22:3
Text: And sent forth his servants to call them that were bidden to the wedding: and they would not come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d1972a1-9052-45ed-a115-c009d48164ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: MAT 22:4
Text: Again, he sent forth other servants, saying, Tell them which are bidden, Behold, I have prepared my dinner: my oxen and my fatlings are killed, and all things are ready: come unto the marriage.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2fce55c-ecf2-478b-a72f-d0ca3acb4bbc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: MAT 22:5
Text: But they made light of it, and went their ways, one to his farm, another to his merchandise:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea74d68f-9509-4619-bd7e-9bdf1b6d50a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: MAT 22:6
Text: And the remnant took his servants, and entreated them spitefully, and slew them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:674a1e04-9e0d-4023-a194-e42ddb5f9590>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: MAT 22:7
Text: But when the king heard thereof, he was wroth: and he sent forth his armies, and destroyed those murderers, and burned up their city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:581f8974-ee7f-4c9c-aa73-25df6e66537a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: MAT 22:8
Text: Then saith he to his servants, The wedding is ready, but they which were bidden were not worthy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:495b41d6-5423-41c0-9075-0e307bc9f73e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: MAT 22:9
Text: Go ye therefore into the highways, and as many as ye shall find, bid to the marriage.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f8d59f2-5178-4d03-8756-91161c1c83c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: MAT 22:10
Text: So those servants went out into the highways, and gathered together all as many as they found, both bad and good: and the wedding was furnished with guests.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b38bc10a-1007-4349-aa46-c4d5ce73d052>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: MAT 22:11
Text: And when the king came in to see the guests, he saw there a man which had not on a wedding garment:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9173cb2-78a0-46da-97a2-5cf9044ab507>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: MAT 22:12
Text: And he saith unto him, Friend, how camest thou in hither not having a wedding garment? And he was speechless.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74626114-ac47-424a-b1a3-fe035165cd85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: MAT 22:13
Text: Then said the king to the servants, Bind him hand and foot, and take him away, and cast him into outer darkness, there shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7da7f92a-a161-4055-9663-e9112d8bbcd0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 68

Reference: MAT 22:14
Text: For many are called, but few are chosen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b861ae5a-1258-4d8e-b9b5-d9b3ed3038a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: MAT 22:15
Text: Then went the Pharisees, and took counsel how they might entangle him in his talk.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a7e07ae-0a9b-4286-a21f-c67dcbf9aae6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: MAT 22:16
Text: And they sent out unto him their disciples with the Herodians, saying, Master, we know that thou art true, and teachest the way of God in truth, neither carest thou for any man: for thou regardest not the person of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16b8695d-640c-4982-8ee5-8061039436aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: MAT 22:17
Text: Tell us therefore, What thinkest thou? Is it lawful to give tribute unto Caesar, or not?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2668f12a-5997-4cac-b5a7-d0566e72c02f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: MAT 22:18
Text: But Jesus perceived their wickedness, and said, Why tempt ye me, ye hypocrites?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34f30d13-4ae6-4cfe-b00e-365d8cdace5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: MAT 22:19
Text: Shew me the tribute money. And they brought unto him a penny.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff70d8eb-cfd4-4334-87ac-36dd69210bd1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: MAT 22:20
Text: And he saith unto them, Whose is this image and superscription?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed8a2754-d866-4e90-8d72-03ea4df1a66a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: MAT 22:21
Text: They say unto him, Caesar’s. Then saith he unto them, Render therefore unto Caesar the things which are Caesar’s; and unto God the things that are God’s.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d254672-2504-4f90-82e8-8048683cbe2f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: MAT 22:22
Text: When they had heard these words, they marvelled, and left him, and went their way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:673c3ff7-1772-45af-8444-b38aeec7e33f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: MAT 22:23
Text: The same day came to him the Sadducees, which say that there is no resurrection, and asked him,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b36cdd0-dc5a-4638-a278-24ffb3649ae5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: MAT 22:24
Text: Saying, Master, Moses said, If a man die, having no children, his brother shall marry his wife, and raise up seed unto his brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3771bb87-975a-4fbc-a704-fead2ce2d844>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: MAT 22:25
Text: Now there were with us seven brethren: and the first, when he had married a wife, deceased, and, having no issue, left his wife unto his brother:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40e59540-f617-4b76-b589-a2c9d400bab4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: MAT 22:26
Text: Likewise the second also, and the third, unto the seventh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:438db4de-f566-4f9b-a828-0656cfea45b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 64

Reference: MAT 22:27
Text: And last of all the woman died also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3837466-a008-4aa8-b9f6-f461a1bfcf8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MAT 22:28
Text: Therefore in the resurrection whose wife shall she be of the seven? for they all had her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77170887-8a65-4aaf-9f4a-d4365b8df578>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: MAT 22:29
Text: Jesus answered and said unto them, Ye do err, not knowing the scriptures, nor the power of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cab980be-1e2e-42f4-91e1-3b746ccd8ad1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MAT 22:30
Text: For in the resurrection they neither marry, nor are given in marriage, but are as the angels of God in heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0552e53d-f77e-45a4-88b6-ed4d81aacb7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: MAT 22:31
Text: But as touching the resurrection of the dead, have ye not read that which was spoken unto you by God, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d8d19c3-f694-430d-ad8c-4db9907aab4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: MAT 22:32
Text: I am the God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob? God is not the God of the dead, but of the living.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27e9f986-ed3c-4b74-a76b-8d8ebb2e8652>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: MAT 22:33
Text: And when the multitude heard this, they were astonished at his doctrine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:342122ff-8229-4894-b9db-1624fec0c63e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: MAT 22:34
Text: But when the Pharisees had heard that he had put the Sadducees to silence, they were gathered together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:380fb35c-5608-4f7e-9cb9-a781d7184207>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: MAT 22:35
Text: Then one of them, which was a lawyer, asked him a question, tempting him, and saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3f454b6-abcf-4b47-96a4-caaa711d356b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: MAT 22:36
Text: Master, which is the great commandment in the law?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c0ae040-93a9-4f95-a9b9-d0fe7024ab20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: MAT 22:37
Text: Jesus said unto him, Thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:622e031e-bf40-40a5-82c9-13ab38f099d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 68

Reference: MAT 22:38
Text: This is the first and great commandment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91be4a8c-e7ee-4208-8fe7-02c6f45ce72c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: MAT 22:39
Text: And the second is like unto it, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9cb2f411-fcb2-492b-bafb-79a39b67c0de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: MAT 22:40
Text: On these two commandments hang all the law and the prophets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c11cc3c-a97f-41dd-a10d-80db6dc00a79>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: MAT 22:41
Text: While the Pharisees were gathered together, Jesus asked them,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:595ee092-1d67-4d03-bece-240ce5828b09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MAT 22:42
Text: Saying, What think ye of Christ? whose son is he? They say unto him, The son of David.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5acec698-3db1-4e28-8b1c-feb3cb669c60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: MAT 22:43
Text: He saith unto them, How then doth David in spirit call him Lord, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa1896fa-6350-4df7-9c9c-e1eca941a784>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: MAT 22:44
Text: The LORD said unto my Lord, Sit thou on my right hand, till I make thine enemies thy footstool?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f848925-c5c7-4b7a-be47-0e189b85a4e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: MAT 22:45
Text: If David then call him Lord, how is he his son?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/22/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f4388b8-bdbe-4c3b-bb99-59336ec23223>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: MAT 22:46
Text: And no man was able to answer him a word, neither durst any man from that day forth ask him any more questions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c964f866-31db-44a3-a0a8-3d4bedbd9d28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: MAT 23:1
Text: Then spake Jesus to the multitude, and to his disciples,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:128fa2d8-30e4-465f-a473-56b2efaeafca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: MAT 23:2
Text: Saying, The scribes and the Pharisees sit in Moses’ seat:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c1e08e9-fcc8-49f8-8923-a0a1d474108b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: MAT 23:3
Text: All therefore whatsoever they bid you observe, that observe and do; but do not ye after their works: for they say, and do not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee758eb1-be6c-43f4-badc-411960d834fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: MAT 23:4
Text: For they bind heavy burdens and grievous to be borne, and lay them on men’s shoulders; but they themselves will not move them with one of their fingers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:624a0431-5022-4361-8486-2487a396d0b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: MAT 23:5
Text: But all their works they do for to be seen of men: they make broad their phylacteries, and enlarge the borders of their garments,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:304dfe01-a19b-4dea-9d87-c257dcac54f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: MAT 23:6
Text: And love the uppermost rooms at feasts, and the chief seats in the synagogues,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:788fd740-aa0d-4b1d-b6c0-62bc2d4dbf9f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: MAT 23:7
Text: And greetings in the markets, and to be called of men, Rabbi, Rabbi.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba354960-ffd7-43d1-a4e4-a784897fb2da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: MAT 23:8
Text: But be not ye called Rabbi: for one is your Master, even Christ; and all ye are brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa3daf79-8ab4-4ce8-ac35-d3ab229ff0b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MAT 23:9
Text: And call no man your father upon the earth: for one is your Father, which is in heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81194371-b59a-4add-b341-3cd29ef63272>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: MAT 23:10
Text: Neither be ye called masters: for one is your Master, even Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9a8dc79-2fbd-4214-877e-3eda4213b927>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: MAT 23:11
Text: But he that is greatest among you shall be your servant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38f6fdff-d0ee-42e0-a7e6-c5215430750a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: MAT 23:12
Text: And whosoever shall exalt himself shall be abased; and he that shall humble himself shall be exalted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:adc62f08-85d8-4219-8320-8cf13260a683>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: MAT 23:13
Text: But woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye shut up the kingdom of heaven against men: for ye neither go in yourselves, neither suffer ye them that are entering to go in.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60697328-41d1-47d1-a682-12888dca2e00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: MAT 23:14
Text: Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye devour widows’ houses, and for a pretence make long prayer: therefore ye shall receive the greater damnation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afab9ba1-e2d6-4700-93f8-bea825dc0b07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: MAT 23:15
Text: Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye compass sea and land to make one proselyte, and when he is made, ye make him twofold more the child of hell than yourselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4229d89e-efae-44d3-8e71-0cd52cee7ca2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: MAT 23:16
Text: Woe unto you, ye blind guides, which say, Whosoever shall swear by the temple, it is nothing; but whosoever shall swear by the gold of the temple, he is a debtor!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17dd9833-8aca-4a90-8b71-2a324217e853>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MAT 23:17
Text: Ye fools and blind: for whether is greater, the gold, or the temple that sanctifieth the gold?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cac875f1-0cc2-4ada-b0bb-7a959254a0c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: MAT 23:18
Text: And, Whosoever shall swear by the altar, it is nothing; but whosoever sweareth by the gift that is upon it, he is guilty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c78347b7-595d-4902-9cb6-e8279bc84b94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: MAT 23:19
Text: Ye fools and blind: for whether is greater, the gift, or the altar that sanctifieth the gift?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa9f1303-eb68-4326-8fbc-4b91731abc69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: MAT 23:20
Text: Whoso therefore shall swear by the altar, sweareth by it, and by all things thereon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ee7cbf6-e466-4705-88d9-2b2405a6e1ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MAT 23:21
Text: And whoso shall swear by the temple, sweareth by it, and by him that dwelleth therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:157352fd-6d7d-482f-a1b7-38d834ab41ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: MAT 23:22
Text: And he that shall swear by heaven, sweareth by the throne of God, and by him that sitteth thereon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0835b6a2-a7da-4211-a445-792e650af05c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 266

Reference: MAT 23:23
Text: Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye pay tithe of mint and anise and cummin, and have omitted the weightier matters of the law, judgment, mercy, and faith: these ought ye to have done, and not to leave the other undone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a9e9596-2cc7-42a1-80ad-4ebc9219e865>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: MAT 23:24
Text: Ye blind guides, which strain at a gnat, and swallow a camel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:290a594c-2022-4a3d-ab34-ee3b1aa97e21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: MAT 23:25
Text: Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye make clean the outside of the cup and of the platter, but within they are full of extortion and excess.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24f0c939-b27d-406d-a4fe-fc951adef495>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: MAT 23:26
Text: Thou blind Pharisee, cleanse first that which is within the cup and platter, that the outside of them may be clean also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2373cb4-c143-42bd-a79c-ce5b9240eb55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: MAT 23:27
Text: Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye are like unto whited sepulchres, which indeed appear beautiful outward, but are within full of dead men’s bones, and of all uncleanness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3fc12bee-26ec-4222-83ac-22c67f4fa017>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: MAT 23:28
Text: Even so ye also outwardly appear righteous unto men, but within ye are full of hypocrisy and iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de22cf6e-d473-4c4a-a761-d3e589eeb43f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: MAT 23:29
Text: Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! because ye build the tombs of the prophets, and garnish the sepulchres of the righteous,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79298e97-0ef5-4752-baff-0293542f780e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: MAT 23:30
Text: And say, If we had been in the days of our fathers, we would not have been partakers with them in the blood of the prophets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d3565a2-4a5c-4e52-927d-c58ed002fc3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: MAT 23:31
Text: Wherefore ye be witnesses unto yourselves, that ye are the children of them which killed the prophets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c521603a-6205-44f7-8ee3-a069cd57b7ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 72

Reference: MAT 23:32
Text: Fill ye up then the measure of your fathers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14ac927a-4716-48b7-8019-638e1d387398>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: MAT 23:33
Text: Ye serpents, ye generation of vipers, how can ye escape the damnation of hell?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c93d237c-1027-45f1-a9cf-8c9fec561a2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: MAT 23:34
Text: Wherefore, behold, I send unto you prophets, and wise men, and scribes: and some of them ye shall kill and crucify; and some of them shall ye scourge in your synagogues, and persecute them from city to city:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c10dd92e-06ba-4636-92b4-044fe5d97ae9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: MAT 23:35
Text: That upon you may come all the righteous blood shed upon the earth, from the blood of righteous Abel unto the blood of Zacharias son of Barachias, whom ye slew between the temple and the altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:116e25d3-2dcd-4128-83e0-65108b01801c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: MAT 23:36
Text: Verily I say unto you, All these things shall come upon this generation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8ee989d-33fb-40b8-8c93-1636b722a33e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: MAT 23:37
Text: O Jerusalem, Jerusalem, thou that killest the prophets, and stonest them which are sent unto thee, how often would I have gathered thy children together, even as a hen gathereth her chickens under her wings, and ye would not!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf310383-8f60-4901-91ba-4895d2ca95b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: MAT 23:38
Text: Behold, your house is left unto you desolate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/23/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4d3ef86-33c1-46fa-bbb3-6d7c74713765>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: MAT 23:39
Text: For I say unto you, Ye shall not see me henceforth, till ye shall say, Blessed is he that cometh in the name of the Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7676f83-057f-4d02-90c6-e892b6aab8de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MAT 24:1
Text: And Jesus went out, and departed from the temple: and his disciples came to him for to shew him the buildings of the temple.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98f40e2e-6c47-4871-842b-63ee44280335>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: MAT 24:2
Text: And Jesus said unto them, See ye not all these things? verily I say unto you, There shall not be left here one stone upon another, that shall not be thrown down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a286340c-9d2d-473f-8aef-9bea7b7afd2d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: MAT 24:3
Text: And as he sat upon the mount of Olives, the disciples came unto him privately, saying, Tell us, when shall these things be? and what shall be the sign of thy coming, and of the end of the world?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7fd44af-0a5e-44e1-9ac5-cab638d8268c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: MAT 24:4
Text: And Jesus answered and said unto them, Take heed that no man deceive you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4a1685e-c834-4594-8621-80835f4bd96e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: MAT 24:5
Text: For many shall come in my name, saying, I am Christ; and shall deceive many.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5dda1e08-9f53-4cc2-bd42-c344308f8a1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: MAT 24:6
Text: And ye shall hear of wars and rumours of wars: see that ye be not troubled: for all these things must come to pass, but the end is not yet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bbc43ce5-12e4-4c71-aafc-76b781d29420>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: MAT 24:7
Text: For nation shall rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom: and there shall be famines, and pestilences, and earthquakes, in divers places.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbfa8d6a-5e79-4d91-a6cc-526b124be933>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 66

Reference: MAT 24:8
Text: All these are the beginning of sorrows.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:676403b9-1b45-4afc-bae9-121b7ad45584>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: MAT 24:9
Text: Then shall they deliver you up to be afflicted, and shall kill you: and ye shall be hated of all nations for my name’s sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ddd3dac-fdfa-41cb-868c-7adc8b1ed544>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: MAT 24:10
Text: And then shall many be offended, and shall betray one another, and shall hate one another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2485161e-11df-4fec-8ffa-c345462be518>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: MAT 24:11
Text: And many false prophets shall rise, and shall deceive many.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e497845f-f18b-4eae-a7e1-c77d01dd44f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: MAT 24:12
Text: And because iniquity shall abound, the love of many shall wax cold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a31a4e85-d7c3-4bd2-8791-f99f90b28b1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: MAT 24:13
Text: But he that shall endure unto the end, the same shall be saved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c147efe-2761-419e-bc81-6454ceb4a870>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: MAT 24:14
Text: And this gospel of the kingdom shall be preached in all the world for a witness unto all nations; and then shall the end come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9cecad79-00d8-4144-8eb7-e67bd7bdf32a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: MAT 24:15
Text: When ye therefore shall see the abomination of desolation, spoken of by Daniel the prophet, stand in the holy place, (whoso readeth, let him understand:)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1417fad5-9df1-48f0-9061-4bb91e9a48bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: MAT 24:16
Text: Then let them which be in Judaea flee into the mountains:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:157ad26f-1341-45df-8e4f-fd5d594cbacf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: MAT 24:17
Text: Let him which is on the housetop not come down to take any thing out of his house:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aee9221c-a073-4367-9cc7-eeed0ab0cb42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: MAT 24:18
Text: Neither let him which is in the field return back to take his clothes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24d7dc92-293f-4288-8f4e-cea396b2eba4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: MAT 24:19
Text: And woe unto them that are with child, and to them that give suck in those days!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30b7bc94-d4ba-444d-9896-1ffbffb1f212>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: MAT 24:20
Text: But pray ye that your flight be not in the winter, neither on the sabbath day:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1921a62-a254-4c19-967c-381fd8e19f08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: MAT 24:21
Text: For then shall be great tribulation, such as was not since the beginning of the world to this time, no, nor ever shall be.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:744218c5-17ef-4a63-9692-1f0e3f4b8a1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: MAT 24:22
Text: And except those days should be shortened, there should no flesh be saved: but for the elect’s sake those days shall be shortened.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62ea152c-021d-42ef-ac4d-5d91ef2df4a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: MAT 24:23
Text: Then if any man shall say unto you, Lo, here is Christ, or there; believe it not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29e2151e-be97-4c10-9720-0839ff350cbb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: MAT 24:24
Text: For there shall arise false Christs, and false prophets, and shall shew great signs and wonders; insomuch that, if it were possible, they shall deceive the very elect.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89c98aa9-ad3d-48ea-89bc-5e026bd449c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 59

Reference: MAT 24:25
Text: Behold, I have told you before.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1eb420b0-40ad-449e-bfb8-22c2fcc98a10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: MAT 24:26
Text: Wherefore if they shall say unto you, Behold, he is in the desert; go not forth: behold, he is in the secret chambers; believe it not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fb96085-30f0-496b-a3de-e949258507c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MAT 24:27
Text: For as the lightning cometh out of the east, and shineth even unto the west; so shall also the coming of the Son of man be.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f4a6ba3-e998-496c-94dc-e3fcc325aa0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: MAT 24:28
Text: For wheresoever the carcase is, there will the eagles be gathered together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d21db14a-b940-4946-914d-d4d68c0396c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: MAT 24:29
Text: Immediately after the tribulation of those days shall the sun be darkened, and the moon shall not give her light, and the stars shall fall from heaven, and the powers of the heavens shall be shaken:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ccdcb5a-ae89-4896-8328-38dd308f716e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: MAT 24:30
Text: And then shall appear the sign of the Son of man in heaven: and then shall all the tribes of the earth mourn, and they shall see the Son of man coming in the clouds of heaven with power and great glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8d7540d-dda1-4999-ae10-50c39c69a6f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: MAT 24:31
Text: And he shall send his angels with a great sound of a trumpet, and they shall gather together his elect from the four winds, from one end of heaven to the other.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cea2f77-1072-4d70-9502-51ac9dfc02da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: MAT 24:32
Text: Now learn a parable of the fig tree; When his branch is yet tender, and putteth forth leaves, ye know that summer is nigh:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75dcdf2c-a8be-4c48-9070-8c9f9fb3fc1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: MAT 24:33
Text: So likewise ye, when ye shall see all these things, know that it is near, even at the doors.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5c58636-6e19-4115-9032-55800605a69a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: MAT 24:34
Text: Verily I say unto you, This generation shall not pass, till all these things be fulfilled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c696a38-db26-43b8-a5e9-8ad0e5cd6f98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: MAT 24:35
Text: Heaven and earth shall pass away, but my words shall not pass away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9c585b9-6b45-4a05-a9f3-83cb9900eef3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: MAT 24:36
Text: But of that day and hour knoweth no man, no, not the angels of heaven, but my Father only.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01987745-501a-4751-a642-183557a247b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: MAT 24:37
Text: But as the days of Noe were, so shall also the coming of the Son of man be.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0166ce4b-bd2b-4363-8c77-c82fcd116f18>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: MAT 24:38
Text: For as in the days that were before the flood they were eating and drinking, marrying and giving in marriage, until the day that Noe entered into the ark,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:885f926b-892a-4a3a-8c19-97494bc61168>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: MAT 24:39
Text: And knew not until the flood came, and took them all away; so shall also the coming of the Son of man be.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3ce67dc-0826-4c97-bc75-baa2d33a56b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: MAT 24:40
Text: Then shall two be in the field; the one shall be taken, and the other left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27d02ebe-7b12-4e09-b916-4e6dbbfba613>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: MAT 24:41
Text: Two women shall be grinding at the mill; the one shall be taken, and the other left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a45f16a-1203-4c33-9117-8842c4eb40cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: MAT 24:42
Text: Watch therefore: for ye know not what hour your Lord doth come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef22096c-3c72-4408-8685-a38132a62823>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: MAT 24:43
Text: But know this, that if the goodman of the house had known in what watch the thief would come, he would have watched, and would not have suffered his house to be broken up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98a67244-01b5-4f0e-b8cc-2b512d933015>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MAT 24:44
Text: Therefore be ye also ready: for in such an hour as ye think not the Son of man cometh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d88cbf02-de87-4e6a-9e08-e3c81672e56b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MAT 24:45
Text: Who then is a faithful and wise servant, whom his lord hath made ruler over his household, to give them meat in due season?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba703e6c-d3db-4713-87a1-8e27d149043e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: MAT 24:46
Text: Blessed is that servant, whom his lord when he cometh shall find so doing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc21e3a0-7646-4c89-aeed-52e6df83b5c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: MAT 24:47
Text: Verily I say unto you, That he shall make him ruler over all his goods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8dc9c72b-176b-420c-9a6d-f08e5dff1428>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: MAT 24:48
Text: But and if that evil servant shall say in his heart, My lord delayeth his coming;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2de5a0dd-a18a-4487-9c20-a66a7a914ab4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: MAT 24:49
Text: And shall begin to smite his fellowservants, and to eat and drink with the drunken;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17d5e711-5efe-4e05-aecf-5fc45911286b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: MAT 24:50
Text: The lord of that servant shall come in a day when he looketh not for him, and in an hour that he is not aware of,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/24/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:916602dd-b672-4c84-afdb-e6ff61ba1688>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: MAT 24:51
Text: And shall cut him asunder, and appoint him his portion with the hypocrites: there shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5550ce12-7434-42e8-9f1c-246e458efa8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MAT 25:1
Text: Then shall the kingdom of heaven be likened unto ten virgins, which took their lamps, and went forth to meet the bridegroom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a7e68f5-da1a-43ce-8569-8824b0fdc6ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: MAT 25:2
Text: And five of them were wise, and five were foolish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d26cfff8-2852-4572-83bd-bcb9063baa2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: MAT 25:3
Text: They that were foolish took their lamps, and took no oil with them:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2894b120-53b7-4d94-9390-f9b768d21f0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: MAT 25:4
Text: But the wise took oil in their vessels with their lamps.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74e3bfbb-9b04-4956-9c5d-58a44678867d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: MAT 25:5
Text: While the bridegroom tarried, they all slumbered and slept.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2dff615c-efac-4e22-8ec4-4bca03094c21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: MAT 25:6
Text: And at midnight there was a cry made, Behold, the bridegroom cometh; go ye out to meet him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0aa0d9c-c184-46c8-a505-f8d3778966eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: MAT 25:7
Text: Then all those virgins arose, and trimmed their lamps.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1fada4a-280c-4657-96e9-7f7f2412e1f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: MAT 25:8
Text: And the foolish said unto the wise, Give us of your oil; for our lamps are gone out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8a5d1cc-3805-4503-88ee-fd5cb8f74baf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: MAT 25:9
Text: But the wise answered, saying, Not so; lest there be not enough for us and you: but go ye rather to them that sell, and buy for yourselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04dc6791-0ea8-433b-ba7a-1ffbf72771bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: MAT 25:10
Text: And while they went to buy, the bridegroom came; and they that were ready went in with him to the marriage: and the door was shut.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b4f7f44-171b-40c4-8501-295675508480>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: MAT 25:11
Text: Afterward came also the other virgins, saying, Lord, Lord, open to us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:611f46fa-c2fb-4dbc-a9f1-1a5dddcf2fa2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: MAT 25:12
Text: But he answered and said, Verily I say unto you, I know you not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47694f45-aa4a-4fc5-a7d1-c77c13810546>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: MAT 25:13
Text: Watch therefore, for ye know neither the day nor the hour wherein the Son of man cometh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2056d9c-1e78-4f18-9645-f345900850b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: MAT 25:14
Text: For the kingdom of heaven is as a man travelling into a far country, who called his own servants, and delivered unto them his goods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05f51dd2-d573-47da-9d89-e29825b4d4bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: MAT 25:15
Text: And unto one he gave five talents, to another two, and to another one; to every man according to his several ability; and straightway took his journey.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:715ff2c9-68da-4715-869f-992ee6efe2d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: MAT 25:16
Text: Then he that had received the five talents went and traded with the same, and made them other five talents.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd59a33d-77e0-4af3-8165-dc6c8673deac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: MAT 25:17
Text: And likewise he that had received two, he also gained other two.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90d63c21-7f62-4fb1-b813-3eb148c079a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MAT 25:18
Text: But he that had received one went and digged in the earth, and hid his lord’s money.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09161a4a-9d6b-4aca-895d-d8a9ad77d8c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: MAT 25:19
Text: After a long time the lord of those servants cometh, and reckoneth with them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5da8e70a-1487-4241-93cc-46df9cab5b0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: MAT 25:20
Text: And so he that had received five talents came and brought other five talents, saying, Lord, thou deliveredst unto me five talents: behold, I have gained beside them five talents more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af3efe83-63cd-4283-a4b2-9e66340c5424>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: MAT 25:21
Text: His lord said unto him, Well done, thou good and faithful servant: thou hast been faithful over a few things, I will make thee ruler over many things: enter thou into the joy of thy lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:151bf40c-8de2-4bb8-a175-139c726aa579>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: MAT 25:22
Text: He also that had received two talents came and said, Lord, thou deliveredst unto me two talents: behold, I have gained two other talents beside them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d166798-9577-423b-877b-126327af0618>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: MAT 25:23
Text: His lord said unto him, Well done, good and faithful servant; thou hast been faithful over a few things, I will make thee ruler over many things: enter thou into the joy of thy lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86476d8a-3c98-47fc-a712-585a3ac3b581>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: MAT 25:24
Text: Then he which had received the one talent came and said, Lord, I knew thee that thou art an hard man, reaping where thou hast not sown, and gathering where thou hast not strawed:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1d5f003-ba3b-4123-96a5-c25c7d3811ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MAT 25:25
Text: And I was afraid, and went and hid thy talent in the earth: lo, there thou hast that is thine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f8c397a-f6c2-41ad-9d09-f8e0d81424ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: MAT 25:26
Text: His lord answered and said unto him, Thou wicked and slothful servant, thou knewest that I reap where I sowed not, and gather where I have not strawed:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8fceff9c-cba9-4d6f-9ef7-147beeb2a0fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: MAT 25:27
Text: Thou oughtest therefore to have put my money to the exchangers, and then at my coming I should have received mine own with usury.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a78f4c3-ec91-4804-ac9c-9af64e98f451>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: MAT 25:28
Text: Take therefore the talent from him, and give it unto him which hath ten talents.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2847e38c-fe5d-49bb-9a7f-af987e775fa7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: MAT 25:29
Text: For unto every one that hath shall be given, and he shall have abundance: but from him that hath not shall be taken away even that which he hath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a691f7ac-08fc-4ec9-8ffa-01b62495f989>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: MAT 25:30
Text: And cast ye the unprofitable servant into outer darkness: there shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b611aec5-7b4d-4f87-89b3-f0c0a0a99237>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: MAT 25:31
Text: When the Son of man shall come in his glory, and all the holy angels with him, then shall he sit upon the throne of his glory:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3efe2cb6-30d8-4bd2-8fd1-d447c9ec6c39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: MAT 25:32
Text: And before him shall be gathered all nations: and he shall separate them one from another, as a shepherd divideth his sheep from the goats:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eac9a3d3-ee1e-4b1a-ba78-23661140070d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: MAT 25:33
Text: And he shall set the sheep on his right hand, but the goats on the left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4345a22a-11e2-41ce-81d9-ec1bc2ddcb99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: MAT 25:34
Text: Then shall the King say unto them on his right hand, Come, ye blessed of my Father, inherit the kingdom prepared for you from the foundation of the world:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98055ccb-7c78-43b2-82c1-5ffc82609e67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: MAT 25:35
Text: For I was an hungred, and ye gave me meat: I was thirsty, and ye gave me drink: I was a stranger, and ye took me in:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73b3be41-0d63-4249-bb70-0a6eb567aaa1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MAT 25:36
Text: Naked, and ye clothed me: I was sick, and ye visited me: I was in prison, and ye came unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e19e9dc4-2ec1-4820-843b-9870ed4361cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: MAT 25:37
Text: Then shall the righteous answer him, saying, Lord, when saw we thee an hungred, and fed thee? or thirsty, and gave thee drink?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e48e519-b0a8-48f4-8cba-e4ecc49bcbac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: MAT 25:38
Text: When saw we thee a stranger, and took thee in? or naked, and clothed thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8add893-783f-4372-be93-171a30f588aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: MAT 25:39
Text: Or when saw we thee sick, or in prison, and came unto thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ceaa818-5fa1-45c4-8155-172d6c45a689>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: MAT 25:40
Text: And the King shall answer and say unto them, Verily I say unto you, Inasmuch as ye have done it unto one of the least of these my brethren, ye have done it unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:692f1fe8-9d53-424e-86ad-fe2940a85dbc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: MAT 25:41
Text: Then shall he say also unto them on the left hand, Depart from me, ye cursed, into everlasting fire, prepared for the devil and his angels:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:765f845e-ccc0-4029-beae-2f971c4d85b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: MAT 25:42
Text: For I was an hungred, and ye gave me no meat: I was thirsty, and ye gave me no drink:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8305fea2-4f75-4e33-9b4f-4b57359e1f01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: MAT 25:43
Text: I was a stranger, and ye took me not in: naked, and ye clothed me not: sick, and in prison, and ye visited me not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf0318b3-4b47-4148-b719-d0f30f627c1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: MAT 25:44
Text: Then shall they also answer him, saying, Lord, when saw we thee an hungred, or athirst, or a stranger, or naked, or sick, or in prison, and did not minister unto thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01fb48f8-f613-490b-bc26-364f7fd624d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: MAT 25:45
Text: Then shall he answer them, saying, Verily I say unto you, Inasmuch as ye did it not to one of the least of these, ye did it not to me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/25/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5ab6fae-011d-473f-a256-db700ea33946>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MAT 25:46
Text: And these shall go away into everlasting punishment: but the righteous into life eternal.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21240aca-fee1-4c63-82b9-9fe05deb1ccd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: MAT 26:1
Text: And it came to pass, when Jesus had finished all these sayings, he said unto his disciples,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b24658c7-7ec8-4960-9c92-7daad7dc30d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: MAT 26:2
Text: Ye know that after two days is the feast of the passover, and the Son of man is betrayed to be crucified.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6389f84-344a-4109-b702-8735132cee4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: MAT 26:3
Text: Then assembled together the chief priests, and the scribes, and the elders of the people, unto the palace of the high priest, who was called Caiaphas,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b7dbd1e-af37-4ac4-b52c-4edb426403a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: MAT 26:4
Text: And consulted that they might take Jesus by subtilty, and kill him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a304fe94-0df3-465b-afa8-84d6db5b11a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: MAT 26:5
Text: But they said, Not on the feast day, lest there be an uproar among the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5fc8f09a-a4e6-4df3-934f-8b17bdd21e72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: MAT 26:6
Text: Now when Jesus was in Bethany, in the house of Simon the leper,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5c65d9e-b975-4914-a468-cb286957d55f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MAT 26:7
Text: There came unto him a woman having an alabaster box of very precious ointment, and poured it on his head, as he sat at meat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21efab7a-a26a-4004-b9c9-f33cc3285a1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: MAT 26:8
Text: But when his disciples saw it, they had indignation, saying, To what purpose is this waste?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f0fc6a8-e340-43cb-a610-f369184f78ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: MAT 26:9
Text: For this ointment might have been sold for much, and given to the poor.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e81419c5-fca4-47cf-b21a-c75976a65b6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: MAT 26:10
Text: When Jesus understood it, he said unto them, Why trouble ye the woman? for she hath wrought a good work upon me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29018ede-0287-448e-9042-00d4847ceddf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: MAT 26:11
Text: For ye have the poor always with you; but me ye have not always.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76792b63-470c-4644-8cc5-91d2e6a73bf7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: MAT 26:12
Text: For in that she hath poured this ointment on my body, she did it for my burial.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32df0942-5652-49f9-a7c6-5334fc9ef1fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: MAT 26:13
Text: Verily I say unto you, Wheresoever this gospel shall be preached in the whole world, there shall also this, that this woman hath done, be told for a memorial of her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65ea5fe5-7c2c-4046-80af-f0dbabeade4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: MAT 26:14
Text: Then one of the twelve, called Judas Iscariot, went unto the chief priests,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b71ca6c-a91a-4823-ab67-5b539d908375>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: MAT 26:15
Text: And said unto them, What will ye give me, and I will deliver him unto you? And they covenanted with him for thirty pieces of silver.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ce52bef-6af4-4901-8aa0-7f6339d7bde2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: MAT 26:16
Text: And from that time he sought opportunity to betray him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a34dfc16-b448-4758-9d5b-4e03ce2c6c71>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: MAT 26:17
Text: Now the first day of the feast of unleavened bread the disciples came to Jesus, saying unto him, Where wilt thou that we prepare for thee to eat the passover?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00e7a181-ffbc-431c-9335-5ed9a6e7691d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: MAT 26:18
Text: And he said, Go into the city to such a man, and say unto him, The Master saith, My time is at hand; I will keep the passover at thy house with my disciples.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e28d870-34ed-4897-a68a-d118f02e4ab8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: MAT 26:19
Text: And the disciples did as Jesus had appointed them; and they made ready the passover.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e882108-df82-4dbe-a94e-5f8ac1d706a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: MAT 26:20
Text: Now when the even was come, he sat down with the twelve.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20f08c39-c5d7-4989-a2dc-9196c343a0f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: MAT 26:21
Text: And as they did eat, he said, Verily I say unto you, that one of you shall betray me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84206cf0-fb3d-4568-b357-d3087be35c01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MAT 26:22
Text: And they were exceeding sorrowful, and began every one of them to say unto him, Lord, is it I?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2cd0098-1983-4a3b-8fe6-5f78d828bd4f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: MAT 26:23
Text: And he answered and said, He that dippeth his hand with me in the dish, the same shall betray me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a922f89-b732-4301-be66-0874b3380579>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: MAT 26:24
Text: The Son of man goeth as it is written of him: but woe unto that man by whom the Son of man is betrayed! it had been good for that man if he had not been born.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d01d12f-e10d-4012-bb96-4a8293d60f67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: MAT 26:25
Text: Then Judas, which betrayed him, answered and said, Master, is it I? He said unto him, Thou hast said.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d684e900-0704-4dac-a717-128a3c313d84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: MAT 26:26
Text: And as they were eating, Jesus took bread, and blessed it, and brake it, and gave it to the disciples, and said, Take, eat; this is my body.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:625c703b-236d-4f87-952f-bdcab1027651>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MAT 26:27
Text: And he took the cup, and gave thanks, and gave it to them, saying, Drink ye all of it;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a70179e-5bb4-4b87-b220-209174ffec01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: MAT 26:28
Text: For this is my blood of the new testament, which is shed for many for the remission of sins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e148fe0e-5bbe-4b43-a549-57ccba617b80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: MAT 26:29
Text: But I say unto you, I will not drink henceforth of this fruit of the vine, until that day when I drink it new with you in my Father’s kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:739395da-ef67-4772-ac7f-c8d9218b51c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: MAT 26:30
Text: And when they had sung an hymn, they went out into the mount of Olives.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2b45977-e9b3-4133-9846-6d7de5e7d299>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: MAT 26:31
Text: Then saith Jesus unto them, All ye shall be offended because of me this night: for it is written, I will smite the shepherd, and the sheep of the flock shall be scattered abroad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d312526-4285-4378-8211-1e53319d90ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: MAT 26:32
Text: But after I am risen again, I will go before you into Galilee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:725e1373-f432-4e9b-bd46-bdd461d0b663>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: MAT 26:33
Text: Peter answered and said unto him, Though all men shall be offended because of thee, yet will I never be offended.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:441b4c52-8b05-468e-9c35-dde11cf2127d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MAT 26:34
Text: Jesus said unto him, Verily I say unto thee, That this night, before the cock crow, thou shalt deny me thrice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aac32220-103d-472b-a255-e4e2aec744d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: MAT 26:35
Text: Peter said unto him, Though I should die with thee, yet will I not deny thee. Likewise also said all the disciples.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37485b87-1b0a-4159-9bb2-bef0393e103a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: MAT 26:36
Text: Then cometh Jesus with them unto a place called Gethsemane, and saith unto the disciples, Sit ye here, while I go and pray yonder.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70796071-fc53-4258-aa34-65d3b465dd8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: MAT 26:37
Text: And he took with him Peter and the two sons of Zebedee, and began to be sorrowful and very heavy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43217f6a-0631-4be8-8e24-6c22fca2037b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: MAT 26:38
Text: Then saith he unto them, My soul is exceeding sorrowful, even unto death: tarry ye here, and watch with me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:252b51ee-9ad5-4034-af33-4c1db0f48306>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: MAT 26:39
Text: And he went a little farther, and fell on his face, and prayed, saying, O my Father, if it be possible, let this cup pass from me: nevertheless not as I will, but as thou wilt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19b95159-09e6-4a1b-9944-3224b0a85747>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MAT 26:40
Text: And he cometh unto the disciples, and findeth them asleep, and saith unto Peter, What, could ye not watch with me one hour?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f50abe28-cb11-4dc2-bc9c-2eb37d4d0da0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: MAT 26:41
Text: Watch and pray, that ye enter not into temptation: the spirit indeed is willing, but the flesh is weak.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eed99d30-0691-405b-9315-fc3656007b4f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: MAT 26:42
Text: He went away again the second time, and prayed, saying, O my Father, if this cup may not pass away from me, except I drink it, thy will be done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b33cf6f6-3883-4ce5-a43d-3e37ef0fc6fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: MAT 26:43
Text: And he came and found them asleep again: for their eyes were heavy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86c97eca-660b-45a4-9a01-1f13e10a0765>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: MAT 26:44
Text: And he left them, and went away again, and prayed the third time, saying the same words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6388690b-817a-44f4-b42f-60eb01cc0dca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: MAT 26:45
Text: Then cometh he to his disciples, and saith unto them, Sleep on now, and take your rest: behold, the hour is at hand, and the Son of man is betrayed into the hands of sinners.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26a170e6-f039-4386-9520-3a85fb3d2c26>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: MAT 26:46
Text: Rise, let us be going: behold, he is at hand that doth betray me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7e5455b-d035-49bc-b4ab-75e8b154e52a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: MAT 26:47
Text: And while he yet spake, lo, Judas, one of the twelve, came, and with him a great multitude with swords and staves, from the chief priests and elders of the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d0491b5-b61c-43f5-8cf6-cedc22695423>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: MAT 26:48
Text: Now he that betrayed him gave them a sign, saying, Whomsoever I shall kiss, that same is he: hold him fast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e662cd52-8bad-46fb-9bd1-689199f615ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: MAT 26:49
Text: And forthwith he came to Jesus, and said, Hail, master; and kissed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:824759aa-828b-46f0-a015-7e5d1bcc443b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: MAT 26:50
Text: And Jesus said unto him, Friend, wherefore art thou come? Then came they, and laid hands on Jesus and took him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d22644f9-1e6a-4573-8900-8fb45d53b3e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: MAT 26:51
Text: And, behold, one of them which were with Jesus stretched out his hand, and drew his sword, and struck a servant of the high priest’s, and smote off his ear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:779f4720-5084-4877-ba8e-ee6bdbc0ffb5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: MAT 26:52
Text: Then said Jesus unto him, Put up again thy sword into his place: for all they that take the sword shall perish with the sword.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2770f9f4-47e7-4b1a-8280-be9260cf3fb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: MAT 26:53
Text: Thinkest thou that I cannot now pray to my Father, and he shall presently give me more than twelve legions of angels?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66e2ad40-75aa-4347-a88a-5b81eed4e5f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: MAT 26:54
Text: But how then shall the scriptures be fulfilled, that thus it must be?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/55
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5c8de65-36d0-4f68-9460-ae03dbdfe581>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: MAT 26:55
Text: In that same hour said Jesus to the multitudes, Are ye come out as against a thief with swords and staves for to take me? I sat daily with you teaching in the temple, and ye laid no hold on me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/56
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9f87d99-460c-46cd-a02a-0b7cb6b43d6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: MAT 26:56
Text: But all this was done, that the scriptures of the prophets might be fulfilled. Then all the disciples forsook him, and fled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/57
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c28032c0-6f48-49b7-8a5a-db714ad2df4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: MAT 26:57
Text: And they that had laid hold on Jesus led him away to Caiaphas the high priest, where the scribes and the elders were assembled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/58
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f19ce64-45d7-42ca-9210-765a5bfe781b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: MAT 26:58
Text: But Peter followed him afar off unto the high priest’s palace, and went in, and sat with the servants, to see the end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/59
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2080d496-9886-43ce-b6ab-5af08f6b728a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: MAT 26:59
Text: Now the chief priests, and elders, and all the council, sought false witness against Jesus, to put him to death;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/60
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a4bf71d-5c8f-4688-a0dd-143f4e0398ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: MAT 26:60
Text: But found none: yea, though many false witnesses came, yet found they none. At the last came two false witnesses,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/61
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d74e86c-882e-4214-bcb9-cf0c6a4442dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: MAT 26:61
Text: And said, This fellow said, I am able to destroy the temple of God, and to build it in three days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/62
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61b09a4f-5176-400d-b8ba-58ab940ecfad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: MAT 26:62
Text: And the high priest arose, and said unto him, Answerest thou nothing? what is it which these witness against thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/63
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6413892-6943-4f54-ab6d-8066ee28321b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: MAT 26:63
Text: But Jesus held his peace, And the high priest answered and said unto him, I adjure thee by the living God, that thou tell us whether thou be the Christ, the Son of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/64
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82af5122-207a-4407-bc9f-51e33a227e5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: MAT 26:64
Text: Jesus saith unto him, Thou hast said: nevertheless I say unto you, Hereafter shall ye see the Son of man sitting on the right hand of power, and coming in the clouds of heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/65
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bbe791c5-62a1-4db2-a6fd-2fe9649e1ed0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: MAT 26:65
Text: Then the high priest rent his clothes, saying, He hath spoken blasphemy; what further need have we of witnesses? behold, now ye have heard his blasphemy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/66
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f265058-08d3-411c-a9a3-9aad1d8f38e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: MAT 26:66
Text: What think ye? They answered and said, He is guilty of death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/67
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eebad8c4-81ec-4d17-91dd-38397319b75b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: MAT 26:67
Text: Then did they spit in his face, and buffeted him; and others smote him with the palms of their hands,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/68
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:adafe653-4978-4659-9489-8c80a263f020>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: MAT 26:68
Text: Saying, Prophesy unto us, thou Christ, Who is he that smote thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/69
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eadf51cc-dd48-4393-86d3-1a7af0d0651d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MAT 26:69
Text: Now Peter sat without in the palace: and a damsel came unto him, saying, Thou also wast with Jesus of Galilee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/70
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:891178f8-a913-4887-9331-6df1dae8798e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: MAT 26:70
Text: But he denied before them all, saying, I know not what thou sayest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/71
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6af78a44-5846-48c2-8b16-e1b43436712e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: MAT 26:71
Text: And when he was gone out into the porch, another maid saw him, and said unto them that were there, This fellow was also with Jesus of Nazareth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/72
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aac24cef-255d-4d05-9d2d-af3e829bdf8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: MAT 26:72
Text: And again he denied with an oath, I do not know the man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/73
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6ec3917-e287-420d-ba58-9e6b24fd82fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: MAT 26:73
Text: And after a while came unto him they that stood by, and said to Peter, Surely thou also art one of them; for thy speech bewrayeth thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/74
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20cf0d5b-12e2-458a-a702-70623424895b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: MAT 26:74
Text: Then began he to curse and to swear, saying, I know not the man. And immediately the cock crew.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/26/75
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22e9d784-1f10-4a6c-8242-8a64ac8f4518>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: MAT 26:75
Text: And Peter remembered the word of Jesus, which said unto him, Before the cock crow, thou shalt deny me thrice. And he went out, and wept bitterly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0403559-e862-4c56-bdc5-75d3e326a81f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: MAT 27:1
Text: When the morning was come, all the chief priests and elders of the people took counsel against Jesus to put him to death:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2094f67-b650-4e40-aa3f-4a82151a156f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: MAT 27:2
Text: And when they had bound him, they led him away, and delivered him to Pontius Pilate the governor.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a12403b-ffe4-4603-af7b-748cac67865e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: MAT 27:3
Text: Then Judas, which had betrayed him, when he saw that he was condemned, repented himself, and brought again the thirty pieces of silver to the chief priests and elders,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5db41b1-5c68-4a37-bf09-3e7e7c9f0c30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: MAT 27:4
Text: Saying, I have sinned in that I have betrayed the innocent blood. And they said, What is that to us? see thou to that.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:793270b4-8a3f-471c-b206-1ac4ebf73783>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MAT 27:5
Text: And he cast down the pieces of silver in the temple, and departed, and went and hanged himself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1455555d-4035-4599-8796-03e147188d47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: MAT 27:6
Text: And the chief priests took the silver pieces, and said, It is not lawful for to put them into the treasury, because it is the price of blood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76c7f645-81c3-498c-ade7-32a4eb712920>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MAT 27:7
Text: And they took counsel, and bought with them the potter’s field, to bury strangers in.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b55da601-b065-4a04-816c-7a753eb277b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: MAT 27:8
Text: Wherefore that field was called, The field of blood, unto this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c6c2f15-202a-4128-801f-fc3e0564f17f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: MAT 27:9
Text: Then was fulfilled that which was spoken by Jeremy the prophet, saying, And they took the thirty pieces of silver, the price of him that was valued, whom they of the children of Israel did value;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:517e272a-7366-42bc-b4fd-e2da6145f9f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: MAT 27:10
Text: And gave them for the potter’s field, as the Lord appointed me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4327f37a-8f4c-4e54-8cf7-54078459bd47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: MAT 27:11
Text: And Jesus stood before the governor: and the governor asked him, saying, Art thou the King of the Jews? And Jesus said unto him, Thou sayest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:222e41bd-5902-4523-a7a4-b0fb3d722bd8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: MAT 27:12
Text: And when he was accused of the chief priests and elders, he answered nothing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40513acc-bb1e-41ac-bdb0-9ad1dae39bc0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MAT 27:13
Text: Then said Pilate unto him, Hearest thou not how many things they witness against thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:666a1179-b4df-467f-bc69-aa376251bbca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: MAT 27:14
Text: And he answered him to never a word; insomuch that the governor marvelled greatly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d00090eb-ef47-44fe-87f3-9d44efcef4a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: MAT 27:15
Text: Now at that feast the governor was wont to release unto the people a prisoner, whom they would.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c718c6aa-b780-4fdf-9027-2ddd650f0283>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: MAT 27:16
Text: And they had then a notable prisoner, called Barabbas.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd6fc9a6-da8f-43cf-94c7-f153a93cf670>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: MAT 27:17
Text: Therefore when they were gathered together, Pilate said unto them, Whom will ye that I release unto you? Barabbas, or Jesus which is called Christ?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a67e9f5-2ade-4a10-8f93-e564a31b2780>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: MAT 27:18
Text: For he knew that for envy they had delivered him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2dc96f78-6afa-4db6-bddb-277ed26f8b06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: MAT 27:19
Text: When he was set down on the judgment seat, his wife sent unto him, saying, Have thou nothing to do with that just man: for I have suffered many things this day in a dream because of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f26a3ef3-8fd1-4661-9d51-a64635699414>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: MAT 27:20
Text: But the chief priests and elders persuaded the multitude that they should ask Barabbas, and destroy Jesus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eeff9ad4-d6bd-4734-885d-9ecb9aa056a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: MAT 27:21
Text: The governor answered and said unto them, Whether of the twain will ye that I release unto you? They said, Barabbas.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f08f610-fb9b-42b7-8837-22b1c074fcdb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: MAT 27:22
Text: Pilate saith unto them, What shall I do then with Jesus which is called Christ? They all say unto him, Let him be crucified.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a4be698-1b13-4155-8ca4-b66547ec8b3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MAT 27:23
Text: And the governor said, Why, what evil hath he done? But they cried out the more, saying, Let him be crucified.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7fdc95a-2dd1-4c11-9ac2-3bc083104b7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: MAT 27:24
Text: When Pilate saw that he could prevail nothing, but that rather a tumult was made, he took water, and washed his hands before the multitude, saying, I am innocent of the blood of this just person: see ye to it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4ab9b83-a6ec-481e-b580-a02d4d4a5dc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: MAT 27:25
Text: Then answered all the people, and said, His blood be on us, and on our children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:978727de-1064-4320-ada1-5aae45906c19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: MAT 27:26
Text: Then released he Barabbas unto them: and when he had scourged Jesus, he delivered him to be crucified.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d5d3417-0c32-49df-9867-4cc081c3760b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: MAT 27:27
Text: Then the soldiers of the governor took Jesus into the common hall, and gathered unto him the whole band of soldiers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37c183a3-04ba-4ccd-907b-a8193bdd9ad3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: MAT 27:28
Text: And they stripped him, and put on him a scarlet robe.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c65a456e-7976-4c4d-a3ff-740aca0da351>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: MAT 27:29
Text: And when they had platted a crown of thorns, they put it upon his head, and a reed in his right hand: and they bowed the knee before him, and mocked him, saying, Hail, King of the Jews!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39d14d81-5881-41a2-9fe0-585cbd245a64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: MAT 27:30
Text: And they spit upon him, and took the reed, and smote him on the head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f128d14b-721f-4504-a24b-141ccd9d3efb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: MAT 27:31
Text: And after that they had mocked him, they took the robe off from him, and put his own raiment on him, and led him away to crucify him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f5825fb-2a9a-4dfc-b291-5e60d561cbad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: MAT 27:32
Text: And as they came out, they found a man of Cyrene, Simon by name: him they compelled to bear his cross.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67bd91d1-5f4f-4896-bfa2-38270723ec96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MAT 27:33
Text: And when they were come unto a place called Golgotha, that is to say, a place of a skull,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ddcc66a-3daa-477c-aa03-f54620056991>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: MAT 27:34
Text: They gave him vinegar to drink mingled with gall: and when he had tasted thereof, he would not drink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:405fbacf-5749-43e1-95a8-dbe4c2cbfa7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: MAT 27:35
Text: And they crucified him, and parted his garments, casting lots: that it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the prophet, They parted my garments among them, and upon my vesture did they cast lots.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbbc919a-0896-40fb-94f0-5b725731af61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 68

Reference: MAT 27:36
Text: And sitting down they watched him there;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:552633ce-eb64-41e2-aa68-df50f9154add>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: MAT 27:37
Text: And set up over his head his accusation written, THIS IS JESUS THE KING OF THE JEWS.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:badeb356-5280-4e30-b8f2-9cde9ee91f81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: MAT 27:38
Text: Then were there two thieves crucified with him, one on the right hand, and another on the left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:738e64a2-3490-4d52-a2b4-3872f8f0f939>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: MAT 27:39
Text: And they that passed by reviled him, wagging their heads,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e5338e2-0f6d-4a04-88ef-4dd708e100bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: MAT 27:40
Text: And saying, Thou that destroyest the temple, and buildest it in three days, save thyself. If thou be the Son of God, come down from the cross.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:354184e5-b14d-4e81-a184-7cc4faf69f2d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: MAT 27:41
Text: Likewise also the chief priests mocking him, with the scribes and elders, said,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd7f4384-aba4-44ce-bde3-61a3c8cf1198>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: MAT 27:42
Text: He saved others; himself he cannot save. If he be the King of Israel, let him now come down from the cross, and we will believe him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f2d5db1-241a-487f-8211-fba850af938a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: MAT 27:43
Text: He trusted in God; let him deliver him now, if he will have him: for he said, I am the Son of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:379616ac-fbbc-4fbb-9885-9d45f3443d1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: MAT 27:44
Text: The thieves also, which were crucified with him, cast the same in his teeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5ddb89f-a603-45b4-8b3d-dc6a6c6178bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: MAT 27:45
Text: Now from the sixth hour there was darkness over all the land unto the ninth hour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69a9c305-b582-4e8e-9183-c12c7630e3b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: MAT 27:46
Text: And about the ninth hour Jesus cried with a loud voice, saying, Eli, Eli, lama sabachthani? that is to say, My God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c82e2548-c618-42f2-a1a2-b6c3d18647ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MAT 27:47
Text: Some of them that stood there, when they heard that, said, This man calleth for Elias.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b892bc06-df02-4ce1-b03e-d23649c2365a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: MAT 27:48
Text: And straightway one of them ran, and took a spunge, and filled it with vinegar, and put it on a reed, and gave him to drink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95cc84d1-e3b0-4aa1-8951-13f9cd226ee4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: MAT 27:49
Text: The rest said, Let be, let us see whether Elias will come to save him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc8d9b59-1d2c-469a-8397-c978a993e03b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: MAT 27:50
Text: Jesus, when he had cried again with a loud voice, yielded up the ghost.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3a9e9a6-e8bd-442e-8e65-780d8126fb6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: MAT 27:51
Text: And, behold, the veil of the temple was rent in twain from the top to the bottom; and the earth did quake, and the rocks rent;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8df14e8-be11-475f-b6e2-ef30c46e8cc0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: MAT 27:52
Text: And the graves were opened; and many bodies of the saints which slept arose,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bd98fd3-94b0-496b-807f-07b915a8f57e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: MAT 27:53
Text: And came out of the graves after his resurrection, and went into the holy city, and appeared unto many.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85d7c87b-1bbd-4387-a4fe-e57c1172c70f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: MAT 27:54
Text: Now when the centurion, and they that were with him, watching Jesus, saw the earthquake, and those things that were done, they feared greatly, saying, Truly this was the Son of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/55
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b96c7bc-29ed-411c-b40d-b930483e4532>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: MAT 27:55
Text: And many women were there beholding afar off, which followed Jesus from Galilee, ministering unto him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/56
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c127330b-57ae-4a6d-a928-9459b234a84e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: MAT 27:56
Text: Among which was Mary Magdalene, and Mary the mother of James and Joses, and the mother of Zebedee’s children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/57
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47e0a55b-5e6e-405c-ba36-ff7a25d88f71>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: MAT 27:57
Text: When the even was come, there came a rich man of Arimathaea, named Joseph, who also himself was Jesus’ disciple:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/58
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03bad360-4e5f-4c46-8d22-d878f2faeb21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: MAT 27:58
Text: He went to Pilate, and begged the body of Jesus. Then Pilate commanded the body to be delivered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/59
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49287105-486d-4559-8c25-5d22efd61141>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: MAT 27:59
Text: And when Joseph had taken the body, he wrapped it in a clean linen cloth,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/60
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b51a42cd-6175-4b08-8d73-edc24879b95d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: MAT 27:60
Text: And laid it in his own new tomb, which he had hewn out in the rock: and he rolled a great stone to the door of the sepulchre, and departed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/61
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6685b5f-73ca-4d5c-8cd4-8387a75f287a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: MAT 27:61
Text: And there was Mary Magdalene, and the other Mary, sitting over against the sepulchre.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/62
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b851566-020f-4a6b-a603-7cb17df9304a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: MAT 27:62
Text: Now the next day, that followed the day of the preparation, the chief priests and Pharisees came together unto Pilate,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/63
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af2790aa-a7e8-41fe-9dc6-0f6a67f1e4c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: MAT 27:63
Text: Saying, Sir, we remember that that deceiver said, while he was yet alive, After three days I will rise again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/64
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06769ec0-dc29-4e38-933e-5cd478e20496>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: MAT 27:64
Text: Command therefore that the sepulchre be made sure until the third day, lest his disciples come by night, and steal him away, and say unto the people, He is risen from the dead: so the last error shall be worse than the first.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/65
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b28d6e7e-cb1f-42b9-80b3-393a49f0545d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: MAT 27:65
Text: Pilate said unto them, Ye have a watch: go your way, make it as sure as ye can.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/27/66
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7531572-d99b-4926-9184-0c3ee2c6930d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: MAT 27:66
Text: So they went, and made the sepulchre sure, sealing the stone, and setting a watch.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/28/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7720a11-8a00-4973-ba3b-5ac324737f5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: MAT 28:1
Text: In the end of the sabbath, as it began to dawn toward the first day of the week, came Mary Magdalene and the other Mary to see the sepulchre.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/28/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac6ced73-81c8-44ce-97df-7cdb79836dd3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: MAT 28:2
Text: And, behold, there was a great earthquake: for the angel of the Lord descended from heaven, and came and rolled back the stone from the door, and sat upon it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/28/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0efa7e8b-74ee-41d1-81c4-8e728ff3e8be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: MAT 28:3
Text: His countenance was like lightning, and his raiment white as snow:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/28/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:537f4ca8-6ec2-4b13-afa8-974abcafb9b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: MAT 28:4
Text: And for fear of him the keepers did shake, and became as dead men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/28/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd08dda1-0d39-48f9-b587-224e09e70e4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: MAT 28:5
Text: And the angel answered and said unto the women, Fear not ye: for I know that ye seek Jesus, which was crucified.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/28/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c5d6f73-7f82-47ea-ac6f-15c5c120f512>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: MAT 28:6
Text: He is not here: for he is risen, as he said. Come, see the place where the Lord lay.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/28/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23e7ae50-e03f-4a56-8095-4499e3a6e00f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: MAT 28:7
Text: And go quickly, and tell his disciples that he is risen from the dead; and, behold, he goeth before you into Galilee; there shall ye see him: lo, I have told you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/28/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:395b2399-0ea7-4c17-9bb2-d9de6da1af27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: MAT 28:8
Text: And they departed quickly from the sepulchre with fear and great joy; and did run to bring his disciples word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/28/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:119b3035-1e3f-4b4a-b0e9-310e043a9b59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: MAT 28:9
Text: And as they went to tell his disciples, behold, Jesus met them, saying, All hail. And they came and held him by the feet, and worshipped him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/28/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e16d6a7e-30d3-4cda-89e7-1374ba8edfe0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: MAT 28:10
Text: Then said Jesus unto them, Be not afraid: go tell my brethren that they go into Galilee, and there shall they see me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/28/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90182255-c7fc-4cc0-8cc7-1d92a6f17f4f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: MAT 28:11
Text: Now when they were going, behold, some of the watch came into the city, and shewed unto the chief priests all the things that were done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/28/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b066e838-8345-4b41-83d6-6b89806aaa73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: MAT 28:12
Text: And when they were assembled with the elders, and had taken counsel, they gave large money unto the soldiers,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/28/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a522e9c0-5dc6-41c4-bab7-977af48b05c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: MAT 28:13
Text: Saying, Say ye, His disciples came by night, and stole him away while we slept.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/28/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbc7355e-0165-4e9a-a082-b406f4c7a112>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: MAT 28:14
Text: And if this come to the governor’s ears, we will persuade him, and secure you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/28/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19383453-7bca-4c08-bbc5-5e4a85fa180e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: MAT 28:15
Text: So they took the money, and did as they were taught: and this saying is commonly reported among the Jews until this day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/28/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6f4c29b-721c-4bcc-a998-0c960d4897ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: MAT 28:16
Text: Then the eleven disciples went away into Galilee, into a mountain where Jesus had appointed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/28/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d460a763-0af7-4efb-a97c-c3140f6d8944>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: MAT 28:17
Text: And when they saw him, they worshipped him: but some doubted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/28/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d44c693d-ade4-4286-9206-df9fda4e4d6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MAT 28:18
Text: And Jesus came and spake unto them, saying, All power is given unto me in heaven and in earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/28/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:871d4231-ed82-42e5-a09f-aff13a8d8b4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: MAT 28:19
Text: Go ye therefore, and teach all nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father, and of the Son, and of the Holy Ghost:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MAT/28/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:638f8af7-325d-45e3-b46b-37ac6a4b5555>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: MAT 28:20
Text: Teaching them to observe all things whatsoever I have commanded you: and, lo, I am with you alway, even unto the end of the world. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:565f6cc7-0b87-48aa-9c35-9fde4985710d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: MRK 1:1
Text: The beginning of the gospel of Jesus Christ, the Son of God;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:576c4259-297b-4f8c-aaf1-b0fd6cc3e760>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: MRK 1:2
Text: As it is written in the prophets, Behold, I send my messenger before thy face, which shall prepare thy way before thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91663800-1de5-4ad6-a14c-dd77d4b1d7af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: MRK 1:3
Text: The voice of one crying in the wilderness, Prepare ye the way of the Lord, make his paths straight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79c822c1-b6b4-48aa-9c11-f5290de9be7a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: MRK 1:4
Text: John did baptize in the wilderness, and preach the baptism of repentance for the remission of sins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65703968-ef23-4aac-99a5-5e621f653ded>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: MRK 1:5
Text: And there went out unto him all the land of Judaea, and they of Jerusalem, and were all baptized of him in the river of Jordan, confessing their sins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:892b8520-68f9-489b-92ce-f8c28c355b43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MRK 1:6
Text: And John was clothed with camel’s hair, and with a girdle of a skin about his loins; and he did eat locusts and wild honey;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfc99418-a13d-482e-be72-0b84c6e5ea8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: MRK 1:7
Text: And preached, saying, There cometh one mightier than I after me, the latchet of whose shoes I am not worthy to stoop down and unloose.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6ec8727-a098-4599-a3b9-b316fd6577b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: MRK 1:8
Text: I indeed have baptized you with water: but he shall baptize you with the Holy Ghost.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb7dc745-52f2-4017-ac80-662e6f64bb4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MRK 1:9
Text: And it came to pass in those days, that Jesus came from Nazareth of Galilee, and was baptized of John in Jordan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06bc2747-2f49-4bec-9741-39a5cc7a3767>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: MRK 1:10
Text: And straightway coming up out of the water, he saw the heavens opened, and the Spirit like a dove descending upon him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59ca8ed3-d510-4bc8-a98d-806ceaa21ed6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MRK 1:11
Text: And there came a voice from heaven, saying, Thou art my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69e9c399-3b7f-4b10-b85a-f6bcf4023e6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: MRK 1:12
Text: And immediately the spirit driveth him into the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9868555-1672-44c8-b5c8-17e9ae61d9a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: MRK 1:13
Text: And he was there in the wilderness forty days, tempted of Satan; and was with the wild beasts; and the angels ministered unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3eb95dc0-e101-47ca-9c00-50bcff7c2a3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: MRK 1:14
Text: Now after that John was put in prison, Jesus came into Galilee, preaching the gospel of the kingdom of God,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b266ded0-1398-4437-b330-a4be9c8f8a13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: MRK 1:15
Text: And saying, The time is fulfilled, and the kingdom of God is at hand: repent ye, and believe the gospel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af515be0-dfdd-4fc7-925d-93559360c485>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: MRK 1:16
Text: Now as he walked by the sea of Galilee, he saw Simon and Andrew his brother casting a net into the sea: for they were fishers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:623750bb-d18d-402b-a142-172f2568e86a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: MRK 1:17
Text: And Jesus said unto them, Come ye after me, and I will make you to become fishers of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d732265e-668f-43c3-a118-f70a5d230c19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: MRK 1:18
Text: And straightway they forsook their nets, and followed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d29769f2-11e9-4334-8beb-092b2826a99f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: MRK 1:19
Text: And when he had gone a little farther thence, he saw James the son of Zebedee, and John his brother, who also were in the ship mending their nets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2cba8e1c-ee40-470a-a79f-bc367c99e864>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: MRK 1:20
Text: And straightway he called them: and they left their father Zebedee in the ship with the hired servants, and went after him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42621716-1ca2-4f40-8aaa-08ba2ab008e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: MRK 1:21
Text: And they went into Capernaum; and straightway on the sabbath day he entered into the synagogue, and taught.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f960c7f9-af0b-4bf9-b6f9-19e32b86cc90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MRK 1:22
Text: And they were astonished at his doctrine: for he taught them as one that had authority, and not as the scribes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b17a3dea-a108-4837-855a-ef430564846c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: MRK 1:23
Text: And there was in their synagogue a man with an unclean spirit; and he cried out,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e673f404-8e6e-44bf-ac87-cc201e383f70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: MRK 1:24
Text: Saying, Let us alone; what have we to do with thee, thou Jesus of Nazareth? art thou come to destroy us? I know thee who thou art, the Holy One of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54bf9424-dc3e-4ecf-9b31-ccdf75898a28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: MRK 1:25
Text: And Jesus rebuked him, saying, Hold thy peace, and come out of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df51fe4e-deb4-43d3-b76a-8b2172b3da8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MRK 1:26
Text: And when the unclean spirit had torn him, and cried with a loud voice, he came out of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e78039b-bac6-4c86-a8c6-c4d91abead13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: MRK 1:27
Text: And they were all amazed, insomuch that they questioned among themselves, saying, What thing is this? what new doctrine is this? for with authority commandeth he even the unclean spirits, and they do obey him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cff9e7ab-8c45-4e6b-9af1-e18d6ba519da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: MRK 1:28
Text: And immediately his fame spread abroad throughout all the region round about Galilee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f8df904-1cc6-47d4-992c-74e58f93ff7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: MRK 1:29
Text: And forthwith, when they were come out of the synagogue, they entered into the house of Simon and Andrew, with James and John.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bb2f744-889a-4c4a-98b1-7b8761558eba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: MRK 1:30
Text: But Simon’s wife’s mother lay sick of a fever, and anon they tell him of her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c62c4d5-b5c2-40b7-8518-42a230d62596>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: MRK 1:31
Text: And he came and took her by the hand, and lifted her up; and immediately the fever left her, and she ministered unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5553c355-9562-4eaf-a98b-20b6a0bcfbb2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: MRK 1:32
Text: And at even, when the sun did set, they brought unto him all that were diseased, and them that were possessed with devils.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de09b3b2-ab9e-4569-afe3-98289acdd464>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: MRK 1:33
Text: And all the city was gathered together at the door.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:405c62c3-5230-45d3-aa17-1732c562af3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: MRK 1:34
Text: And he healed many that were sick of divers diseases, and cast out many devils; and suffered not the devils to speak, because they knew him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da11c994-be9c-4e0b-9c7d-2cb94dd9cfc0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: MRK 1:35
Text: And in the morning, rising up a great while before day, he went out, and departed into a solitary place, and there prayed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09e0f502-5059-4a3b-aa7b-c1cc3494a7fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: MRK 1:36
Text: And Simon and they that were with him followed after him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:657b850a-1075-4a9f-93f4-d67aafb6e2fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: MRK 1:37
Text: And when they had found him, they said unto him, All men seek for thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8fb5e9de-d314-4c1f-8887-823436855c5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MRK 1:38
Text: And he said unto them, Let us go into the next towns, that I may preach there also: for therefore came I forth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22589ae3-909e-47c4-be12-88d357f41b87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: MRK 1:39
Text: And he preached in their synagogues throughout all Galilee, and cast out devils.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76a6de69-9b1a-40a8-8acd-14ddc0231b35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: MRK 1:40
Text: And there came a leper to him, beseeching him, and kneeling down to him, and saying unto him, If thou wilt, thou canst make me clean.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90e7badf-cb21-450c-b8c6-a6a1d81fc4b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: MRK 1:41
Text: And Jesus, moved with compassion, put forth his hand, and touched him, and saith unto him, I will; be thou clean.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef1be2cd-d8ce-4274-8917-76231d8bf62c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: MRK 1:42
Text: And as soon as he had spoken, immediately the leprosy departed from him, and he was cleansed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c1a0b28-0f12-40a3-bf6b-2dcd71de4559>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: MRK 1:43
Text: And he straitly charged him, and forthwith sent him away;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50680bad-b56a-4ee3-b9ed-348e4bfd0d16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: MRK 1:44
Text: And saith unto him, See thou say nothing to any man: but go thy way, shew thyself to the priest, and offer for thy cleansing those things which Moses commanded, for a testimony unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/1/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a858aff6-2533-467d-9fe9-20686c076ef6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: MRK 1:45
Text: But he went out, and began to publish it much, and to blaze abroad the matter, insomuch that Jesus could no more openly enter into the city, but was without in desert places: and they came to him from every quarter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9add0d2-ffc7-4382-9bca-90509fdde364>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MRK 2:1
Text: And again he entered into Capernaum after some days; and it was noised that he was in the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a71cc02-d1cf-4813-a010-7eff39ed1083>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: MRK 2:2
Text: And straightway many were gathered together, insomuch that there was no room to receive them, no, not so much as about the door: and he preached the word unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81ee2299-0ef4-44ec-8131-a02b9ce8ce4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: MRK 2:3
Text: And they come unto him, bringing one sick of the palsy, which was borne of four.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2baec418-90d6-40f2-84e1-3d39dcb82915>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: MRK 2:4
Text: And when they could not come nigh unto him for the press, they uncovered the roof where he was: and when they had broken it up, they let down the bed wherein the sick of the palsy lay.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2a76d52-9feb-4123-a271-45db5dd78896>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: MRK 2:5
Text: When Jesus saw their faith, he said unto the sick of the palsy, Son, thy sins be forgiven thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86ed29f9-a735-423e-af45-db9f61ae1297>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: MRK 2:6
Text: But there was certain of the scribes sitting there, and reasoning in their hearts,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54e451e2-0c56-42cd-be60-b638dfef56a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: MRK 2:7
Text: Why doth this man thus speak blasphemies? who can forgive sins but God only?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2de4b5c4-2369-433a-8867-acce4b9aabbc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: MRK 2:8
Text: And immediately when Jesus perceived in his spirit that they so reasoned within themselves, he said unto them, Why reason ye these things in your hearts?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9dbf7735-3c16-43e5-a261-ea070e2d980e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: MRK 2:9
Text: Whether is it easier to say to the sick of the palsy, Thy sins be forgiven thee; or to say, Arise, and take up thy bed, and walk?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f56cb272-94d8-4fbb-a60b-b7ee36fecabd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: MRK 2:10
Text: But that ye may know that the Son of man hath power on earth to forgive sins, (he saith to the sick of the palsy,)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15715799-f20b-426f-9051-4cc909fb7a7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: MRK 2:11
Text: I say unto thee, Arise, and take up thy bed, and go thy way into thine house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb9e24a5-7bb5-4eae-b119-5eae06af1af1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: MRK 2:12
Text: And immediately he arose, took up the bed, and went forth before them all; insomuch that they were all amazed, and glorified God, saying, We never saw it on this fashion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0ffa6e7-e733-4c34-92c8-b1acef4f04b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: MRK 2:13
Text: And he went forth again by the sea side; and all the multitude resorted unto him, and he taught them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23d01965-c877-4d93-801d-0fb08b794c66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: MRK 2:14
Text: And as he passed by, he saw Levi the son of Alphaeus sitting at the receipt of custom, and said unto him, Follow me. And he arose and followed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:312c769a-a67e-430e-be26-f9b1bd4215aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: MRK 2:15
Text: And it came to pass, that, as Jesus sat at meat in his house, many publicans and sinners sat also together with Jesus and his disciples: for there were many, and they followed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77c07ecc-4b04-429e-b786-450f9684913c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: MRK 2:16
Text: And when the scribes and Pharisees saw him eat with publicans and sinners, they said unto his disciples, How is it that he eateth and drinketh with publicans and sinners?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8157039-1899-4ade-b9d2-d4d721bae9c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: MRK 2:17
Text: When Jesus heard it, he saith unto them, They that are whole have no need of the physician, but they that are sick: I came not to call the righteous, but sinners to repentance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a8f84a3-dd65-469e-bfd9-c0fcbca107a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: MRK 2:18
Text: And the disciples of John and of the Pharisees used to fast: and they come and say unto him, Why do the disciples of John and of the Pharisees fast, but thy disciples fast not?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:038a809f-de24-4ec6-afcb-1ac9c506c581>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: MRK 2:19
Text: And Jesus said unto them, Can the children of the bridechamber fast, while the bridegroom is with them? as long as they have the bridegroom with them, they cannot fast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20fcafc6-1712-47d6-94e5-40643ca29033>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: MRK 2:20
Text: But the days will come, when the bridegroom shall be taken away from them, and then shall they fast in those days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5080c1f6-35c6-4352-b7de-f437e03ff14e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: MRK 2:21
Text: No man also seweth a piece of new cloth on an old garment: else the new piece that filled it up taketh away from the old, and the rent is made worse.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b94f27f4-fa15-4845-bb33-9e19d1612966>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: MRK 2:22
Text: And no man putteth new wine into old bottles: else the new wine doth burst the bottles, and the wine is spilled, and the bottles will be marred: but new wine must be put into new bottles.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6688ec12-580d-4a00-b829-021ec3ebcabf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: MRK 2:23
Text: And it came to pass, that he went through the corn fields on the sabbath day; and his disciples began, as they went, to pluck the ears of corn.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:580cad76-8467-44d5-afec-0f4231d6b4aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: MRK 2:24
Text: And the Pharisees said unto him, Behold, why do they on the sabbath day that which is not lawful?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16aa54d7-e99a-4dcd-8b81-81c7e2d7e10c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: MRK 2:25
Text: And he said unto them, Have ye never read what David did, when he had need, and was an hungred, he, and they that were with him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26ce4fc4-d9fc-4fd7-afbf-4a77c533cdc3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: MRK 2:26
Text: How he went into the house of God in the days of Abiathar the high priest, and did eat the shewbread, which is not lawful to eat but for the priests, and gave also to them which were with him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60f8a2eb-6f7d-47ab-a6e6-7764a23bb436>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: MRK 2:27
Text: And he said unto them, The sabbath was made for man, and not man for the sabbath:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/2/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c56203c-34d8-4344-841d-712e6f2de5e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: MRK 2:28
Text: Therefore the Son of man is Lord also of the sabbath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbdefa08-65a1-4f71-a09a-3bedef0d08f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: MRK 3:1
Text: And he entered again into the synagogue; and there was a man there which had a withered hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b4b2354-0181-4a4e-a5ff-735b1733e377>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: MRK 3:2
Text: And they watched him, whether he would heal him on the sabbath day; that they might accuse him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fbac8954-d3fd-4189-82a5-6a9f877d17f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: MRK 3:3
Text: And he saith unto the man which had the withered hand, Stand forth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a61e1781-c623-435c-9190-3101fc0ffec5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: MRK 3:4
Text: And he saith unto them, Is it lawful to do good on the sabbath days, or to do evil? to save life, or to kill? But they held their peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3407575a-14ce-4739-adaa-adcb01a5dd14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: MRK 3:5
Text: And when he had looked round about on them with anger, being grieved for the hardness of their hearts, he saith unto the man, Stretch forth thine hand. And he stretched it out: and his hand was restored whole as the other.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d583b086-1014-4294-99bc-b8c49aafd108>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: MRK 3:6
Text: And the Pharisees went forth, and straightway took counsel with the Herodians against him, how they might destroy him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a70a1d4-e968-4ff2-973c-279d18e2e3e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: MRK 3:7
Text: But Jesus withdrew himself with his disciples to the sea: and a great multitude from Galilee followed him, and from Judaea,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f87ca52c-ddef-4188-ada7-cbc59cbc9ed8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: MRK 3:8
Text: And from Jerusalem, and from Idumaea, and from beyond Jordan; and they about Tyre and Sidon, a great multitude, when they had heard what great things he did, came unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d21678d4-b5c8-4bd2-8f84-0d5a22eae135>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: MRK 3:9
Text: And he spake to his disciples, that a small ship should wait on him because of the multitude, lest they should throng him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fe9c645-ed47-4d10-a407-5da693cdb8e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: MRK 3:10
Text: For he had healed many; insomuch that they pressed upon him for to touch him, as many as had plagues.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0d9c70a-fed9-480b-9f9e-61d0c26af5e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: MRK 3:11
Text: And unclean spirits, when they saw him, fell down before him, and cried, saying, Thou art the Son of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:522006e3-f383-4aa9-aaec-25d9a78cf269>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: MRK 3:12
Text: And he straitly charged them that they should not make him known.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be917e56-53fa-46ce-9b0c-22166790ee58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: MRK 3:13
Text: And he goeth up into a mountain, and calleth unto him whom he would: and they came unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9a03bd4-52ff-494d-9491-1103d93d0fdb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: MRK 3:14
Text: And he ordained twelve, that they should be with him, and that he might send them forth to preach,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c11d7e30-fbf7-4911-8a49-9f2b8abda1ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: MRK 3:15
Text: And to have power to heal sicknesses, and to cast out devils:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f04422ba-7e1f-4907-aade-20ef77a2a423>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 55

Reference: MRK 3:16
Text: And Simon he surnamed Peter;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe432164-bbf0-4cef-8971-fd3548afb9d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: MRK 3:17
Text: And James the son of Zebedee, and John the brother of James; and he surnamed them Boanerges, which is, The sons of thunder:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f71b6cf-7b1e-4595-ae54-a56b6dc442a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: MRK 3:18
Text: And Andrew, and Philip, and Bartholomew, and Matthew, and Thomas, and James the son of Alphaeus, and Thaddaeus, and Simon the Canaanite,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:862647b7-a581-4941-a31a-40f8d9b4ea65>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: MRK 3:19
Text: And Judas Iscariot, which also betrayed him: and they went into an house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fc809a1-7584-4104-acf3-fb1dd95d73bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: MRK 3:20
Text: And the multitude cometh together again, so that they could not so much as eat bread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3682647e-d117-4fad-9004-9daa79c4a981>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: MRK 3:21
Text: And when his friends heard of it, they went out to lay hold on him: for they said, He is beside himself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81bb0184-0685-4567-b1ae-b204c37a3104>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: MRK 3:22
Text: And the scribes which came down from Jerusalem said, He hath Beelzebub, and by the prince of the devils casteth he out devils.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f8d5639-5d6c-4f09-950c-b62c30e8335d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MRK 3:23
Text: And he called them unto him, and said unto them in parables, How can Satan cast out Satan?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b76effda-8869-4e3a-b06a-a0c880db0c28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: MRK 3:24
Text: And if a kingdom be divided against itself, that kingdom cannot stand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b771d668-f957-4239-8648-01c03a5de3fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: MRK 3:25
Text: And if a house be divided against itself, that house cannot stand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c16a787c-0fb2-4201-9fd2-97597d153f9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MRK 3:26
Text: And if Satan rise up against himself, and be divided, he cannot stand, but hath an end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6852495-af10-491f-9d15-b269067acd64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: MRK 3:27
Text: No man can enter into a strong man’s house, and spoil his goods, except he will first bind the strong man; and then he will spoil his house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:194f3aa2-d74c-4d43-9bae-129f2687002c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: MRK 3:28
Text: Verily I say unto you, All sins shall be forgiven unto the sons of men, and blasphemies wherewith soever they shall blaspheme:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2766f60b-7538-490b-8d76-346e4630bfd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: MRK 3:29
Text: But he that shall blaspheme against the Holy Ghost hath never forgiveness, but is in danger of eternal damnation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73cafad4-2d89-4162-9d28-6e8162ff2f6d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 72

Reference: MRK 3:30
Text: Because they said, He hath an unclean spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6eeca432-3059-4556-94b7-57b59ec251eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MRK 3:31
Text: There came then his brethren and his mother, and, standing without, sent unto him, calling him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f5302f8-a4d0-41cf-96ab-c68c241262b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: MRK 3:32
Text: And the multitude sat about him, and they said unto him, Behold, thy mother and thy brethren without seek for thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a036a32d-aeb2-4a96-9ee5-ddb6aac977e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: MRK 3:33
Text: And he answered them, saying, Who is my mother, or my brethren?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7a2f52c-523a-4a9e-aff2-ff547a7644e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: MRK 3:34
Text: And he looked round about on them which sat about him, and said, Behold my mother and my brethren!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/3/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:450025f8-df78-4a00-8405-ccef80c12d55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MRK 3:35
Text: For whosoever shall do the will of God, the same is my brother, and my sister, and mother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44596bf7-1cec-40b5-9d84-73203c2ea60d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: MRK 4:1
Text: And he began again to teach by the sea side: and there was gathered unto him a great multitude, so that he entered into a ship, and sat in the sea; and the whole multitude was by the sea on the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df80ce20-6b77-40aa-a3a2-6674e4451fe2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: MRK 4:2
Text: And he taught them many things by parables, and said unto them in his doctrine,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2154d61c-8961-468f-bf03-a942e79b4fe0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: MRK 4:3
Text: Hearken; Behold, there went out a sower to sow:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60f85fb1-5ce4-48d2-bb22-0062774a46f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: MRK 4:4
Text: And it came to pass, as he sowed, some fell by the way side, and the fowls of the air came and devoured it up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3721c1f4-e308-4683-b607-99a06a915ca7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: MRK 4:5
Text: And some fell on stony ground, where it had not much earth; and immediately it sprang up, because it had no depth of earth:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca125b02-3275-4d49-a113-a7b267ef64ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: MRK 4:6
Text: But when the sun was up, it was scorched; and because it had no root, it withered away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:799610c6-6b29-4b1f-a5cc-00a6e4bb33e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MRK 4:7
Text: And some fell among thorns, and the thorns grew up, and choked it, and it yielded no fruit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a63d95a4-347f-403c-9d10-3a818145d639>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: MRK 4:8
Text: And other fell on good ground, and did yield fruit that sprang up and increased; and brought forth, some thirty, and some sixty, and some an hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7bab79fb-1a0a-4033-aff3-0c062133a154>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: MRK 4:9
Text: And he said unto them, He that hath ears to hear, let him hear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:597da979-ce27-4eb3-a8c2-ac40e5ed8663>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: MRK 4:10
Text: And when he was alone, they that were about him with the twelve asked of him the parable.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f129caff-d939-406c-a4f8-c76e6b4f787c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: MRK 4:11
Text: And he said unto them, Unto you it is given to know the mystery of the kingdom of God: but unto them that are without, all these things are done in parables:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f103d4d9-32a5-4aa6-829a-d223cbd84d33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: MRK 4:12
Text: That seeing they may see, and not perceive; and hearing they may hear, and not understand; lest at any time they should be converted, and their sins should be forgiven them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:adf6d653-fd92-4781-a03e-26ecb8d1d82c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: MRK 4:13
Text: And he said unto them, Know ye not this parable? and how then will ye know all parables?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7214faa-97cf-4656-b7b1-b64c40ab1426>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 53

Reference: MRK 4:14
Text: The sower soweth the word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce727eb3-f9d6-4c76-af84-dc6beb802535>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: MRK 4:15
Text: And these are they by the way side, where the word is sown; but when they have heard, Satan cometh immediately, and taketh away the word that was sown in their hearts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84bd505b-44ea-4208-8b0d-e4e56df4cb5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: MRK 4:16
Text: And these are they likewise which are sown on stony ground; who, when they have heard the word, immediately receive it with gladness;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dcecb7c7-c027-4898-b781-0181a6d768a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: MRK 4:17
Text: And have no root in themselves, and so endure but for a time: afterward, when affliction or persecution ariseth for the word’s sake, immediately they are offended.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3fe65c3f-e82d-4da2-b327-47822004da35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: MRK 4:18
Text: And these are they which are sown among thorns; such as hear the word,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ca0174f-e0db-4b5f-89da-41d7d650000e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: MRK 4:19
Text: And the cares of this world, and the deceitfulness of riches, and the lusts of other things entering in, choke the word, and it becometh unfruitful.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff95ba21-c9f4-402e-b29b-b3b6530572f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: MRK 4:20
Text: And these are they which are sown on good ground; such as hear the word, and receive it, and bring forth fruit, some thirtyfold, some sixty, and some an hundred.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cba24b81-8862-4fbe-9b68-2ce3323ee26d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: MRK 4:21
Text: And he said unto them, Is a candle brought to be put under a bushel, or under a bed? and not to be set on a candlestick?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3bcab66-2cbc-4e9b-9d7f-f4e8ce0910da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: MRK 4:22
Text: For there is nothing hid, which shall not be manifested; neither was any thing kept secret, but that it should come abroad.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:564a462c-3d67-4039-910b-ec51c99588ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 70

Reference: MRK 4:23
Text: If any man have ears to hear, let him hear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3901952b-37c6-427f-bbd8-1d551506ae4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: MRK 4:24
Text: And he said unto them, Take heed what ye hear: with what measure ye mete, it shall be measured to you: and unto you that hear shall more be given.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:501745e7-b6d9-46c0-bef2-da186451643f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MRK 4:25
Text: For he that hath, to him shall be given: and he that hath not, from him shall be taken even that which he hath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbb765be-a406-43be-9d3c-b4f18e3751e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: MRK 4:26
Text: And he said, So is the kingdom of God, as if a man should cast seed into the ground;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8741f874-d959-449d-b3a0-2e6a9e4ec43b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: MRK 4:27
Text: And should sleep, and rise night and day, and the seed should spring and grow up, he knoweth not how.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e97933d5-0780-4373-bf60-771971dafa60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: MRK 4:28
Text: For the earth bringeth forth fruit of herself; first the blade, then the ear, after that the full corn in the ear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f61f7723-9d3a-49b3-9982-aa62211873e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: MRK 4:29
Text: But when the fruit is brought forth, immediately he putteth in the sickle, because the harvest is come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85e21c87-bc02-4bee-8766-5c0677b05eaa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: MRK 4:30
Text: And he said, Whereunto shall we liken the kingdom of God? or with what comparison shall we compare it?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f67e7917-d904-49d6-8a62-2e7a3daa06c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: MRK 4:31
Text: It is like a grain of mustard seed, which, when it is sown in the earth, is less than all the seeds that be in the earth:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c05378f2-f907-4167-b6c6-4efa93e4705d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: MRK 4:32
Text: But when it is sown, it groweth up, and becometh greater than all herbs, and shooteth out great branches; so that the fowls of the air may lodge under the shadow of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9475395c-f1b4-4738-9508-fecabac07014>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: MRK 4:33
Text: And with many such parables spake he the word unto them, as they were able to hear it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62a4d812-ba9d-461d-9b72-c5d63f195b92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: MRK 4:34
Text: But without a parable spake he not unto them: and when they were alone, he expounded all things to his disciples.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2cd2d53a-a153-4095-94e2-da3017996657>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: MRK 4:35
Text: And the same day, when the even was come, he saith unto them, Let us pass over unto the other side.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b559b86-1ce2-48b0-87f7-d3cc9554c8a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: MRK 4:36
Text: And when they had sent away the multitude, they took him even as he was in the ship. And there were also with him other little ships.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bf20879-b8fa-4356-b8c2-66772ae0d30e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: MRK 4:37
Text: And there arose a great storm of wind, and the waves beat into the ship, so that it was now full.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb5f9f42-1e0d-4956-801b-d7519c73e466>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: MRK 4:38
Text: And he was in the hinder part of the ship, asleep on a pillow: and they awake him, and say unto him, Master, carest thou not that we perish?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:855490f7-1101-4282-aac3-b0b119d8c453>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MRK 4:39
Text: And he arose, and rebuked the wind, and said unto the sea, Peace, be still. And the wind ceased, and there was a great calm.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f70f805c-7f5e-4856-94fc-38a603f76199>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: MRK 4:40
Text: And he said unto them, Why are ye so fearful? how is it that ye have no faith?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/4/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b6d0192-ccc5-4e5d-ae20-ab27414f2d24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: MRK 4:41
Text: And they feared exceedingly, and said one to another, What manner of man is this, that even the wind and the sea obey him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c95098c-3859-4d40-ab02-e54486b31035>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: MRK 5:1
Text: And they came over unto the other side of the sea, into the country of the Gadarenes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1fe887c-4d0f-45b7-a0ef-9ca985683429>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: MRK 5:2
Text: And when he was come out of the ship, immediately there met him out of the tombs a man with an unclean spirit,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f427cf43-41b3-4057-ac69-087c1cb537bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: MRK 5:3
Text: Who had his dwelling among the tombs; and no man could bind him, no, not with chains:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6710bb27-06a4-4f19-9db2-e22666cf0cf1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: MRK 5:4
Text: Because that he had been often bound with fetters and chains, and the chains had been plucked asunder by him, and the fetters broken in pieces: neither could any man tame him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8836db59-139c-4361-95f1-1c952058368d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: MRK 5:5
Text: And always, night and day, he was in the mountains, and in the tombs, crying, and cutting himself with stones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a07e1be-2043-4ea0-a3f7-f478b3df8d21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: MRK 5:6
Text: But when he saw Jesus afar off, he ran and worshipped him,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:175491c2-fdaa-4cd7-a87d-fc5444ca414c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: MRK 5:7
Text: And cried with a loud voice, and said, What have I to do with thee, Jesus, thou Son of the most high God? I adjure thee by God, that thou torment me not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fdd5428-b2a6-4e7f-8cdf-a9e2308e79d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: MRK 5:8
Text: For he said unto him, Come out of the man, thou unclean spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c574e7c-3b35-454f-86cf-0f2ecf4349c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MRK 5:9
Text: And he asked him, What is thy name? And he answered, saying, My name is Legion: for we are many.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa14ce53-120e-47a3-9574-3265b591851e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: MRK 5:10
Text: And he besought him much that he would not send them away out of the country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7dbdc1b9-6972-4e71-b409-99d331190b64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: MRK 5:11
Text: Now there was there nigh unto the mountains a great herd of swine feeding.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7da5702c-3bc2-4390-9940-b980635899ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: MRK 5:12
Text: And all the devils besought him, saying, Send us into the swine, that we may enter into them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0eddacb1-f5e5-48c9-bc79-39679c5865bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: MRK 5:13
Text: And forthwith Jesus gave them leave. And the unclean spirits went out, and entered into the swine: and the herd ran violently down a steep place into the sea, (they were about two thousand;) and were choked in the sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08a58f5d-fcf2-4a35-b6be-63c894a2318c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: MRK 5:14
Text: And they that fed the swine fled, and told it in the city, and in the country. And they went out to see what it was that was done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a196b5d1-660f-49be-b3e9-754aa6fccad3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: MRK 5:15
Text: And they come to Jesus, and see him that was possessed with the devil, and had the legion, sitting, and clothed, and in his right mind: and they were afraid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7059c894-1588-485f-b89f-92eb806c4743>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: MRK 5:16
Text: And they that saw it told them how it befell to him that was possessed with the devil, and also concerning the swine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e93983d-9236-475a-bb90-65403f668062>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: MRK 5:17
Text: And they began to pray him to depart out of their coasts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac6a0a40-db72-4acb-9107-ae332db1cbf5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: MRK 5:18
Text: And when he was come into the ship, he that had been possessed with the devil prayed him that he might be with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa6ee555-e33c-466b-8e2f-840345a1f871>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: MRK 5:19
Text: Howbeit Jesus suffered him not, but saith unto him, Go home to thy friends, and tell them how great things the Lord hath done for thee, and hath had compassion on thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b1c8521-55cc-4410-863a-d79af6fab425>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: MRK 5:20
Text: And he departed, and began to publish in Decapolis how great things Jesus had done for him: and all men did marvel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9be44564-00ba-49a5-b285-f494ea0cc0a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: MRK 5:21
Text: And when Jesus was passed over again by ship unto the other side, much people gathered unto him: and he was nigh unto the sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ae1f7f7-c0d9-4817-9610-fd55a5f70373>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: MRK 5:22
Text: And, behold, there cometh one of the rulers of the synagogue, Jairus by name; and when he saw him, he fell at his feet,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:173f6e95-4feb-4162-b715-9d6da78b9d16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: MRK 5:23
Text: And besought him greatly, saying, My little daughter lieth at the point of death: I pray thee, come and lay thy hands on her, that she may be healed; and she shall live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3bd25f3-6d82-48bf-83cc-bbe25486d955>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: MRK 5:24
Text: And Jesus went with him; and much people followed him, and thronged him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a06ca717-a531-4ce3-9619-d41eaf4db763>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: MRK 5:25
Text: And a certain woman, which had an issue of blood twelve years,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4116e582-7d78-4fff-b2e8-7823a8460fda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: MRK 5:26
Text: And had suffered many things of many physicians, and had spent all that she had, and was nothing bettered, but rather grew worse,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16502f62-90e8-4ac4-906f-0692f2cd0e6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: MRK 5:27
Text: When she had heard of Jesus, came in the press behind, and touched his garment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6fc10a6-b22b-46e7-b51a-bb79f633dc9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: MRK 5:28
Text: For she said, If I may touch but his clothes, I shall be whole.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6195452e-d570-4e61-b02b-5a9ed58539bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: MRK 5:29
Text: And straightway the fountain of her blood was dried up; and she felt in her body that she was healed of that plague.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6077f66a-a0c1-4938-8050-a740358f742d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: MRK 5:30
Text: And Jesus, immediately knowing in himself that virtue had gone out of him, turned him about in the press, and said, Who touched my clothes?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13126e30-90ca-4e33-be69-0559b5f1d79a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: MRK 5:31
Text: And his disciples said unto him, Thou seest the multitude thronging thee, and sayest thou, Who touched me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:822d6f08-162a-466a-b67e-f39a26c39eb9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: MRK 5:32
Text: And he looked round about to see her that had done this thing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4714064-dc9f-4a16-a299-befe95443b6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: MRK 5:33
Text: But the woman fearing and trembling, knowing what was done in her, came and fell down before him, and told him all the truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93bea78c-f6e7-4444-b0a7-471e5517a899>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: MRK 5:34
Text: And he said unto her, Daughter, thy faith hath made thee whole; go in peace, and be whole of thy plague.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0428af11-88ac-4252-b6ce-69248a48919c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: MRK 5:35
Text: While he yet spake, there came from the ruler of the synagogue’s house certain which said, Thy daughter is dead: why troublest thou the Master any further?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c17e9d2c-9d97-4896-9319-fe71e9477c27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: MRK 5:36
Text: As soon as Jesus heard the word that was spoken, he saith unto the ruler of the synagogue, Be not afraid, only believe.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b331746-4a07-4389-826b-93313b16981e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: MRK 5:37
Text: And he suffered no man to follow him, save Peter, and James, and John the brother of James.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0ccd58f-162f-46dd-8cc5-f45d639a4f52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: MRK 5:38
Text: And he cometh to the house of the ruler of the synagogue, and seeth the tumult, and them that wept and wailed greatly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6390734c-5219-4d91-916c-b917af9308b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: MRK 5:39
Text: And when he was come in, he saith unto them, Why make ye this ado, and weep? the damsel is not dead, but sleepeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5cb85464-b463-44e3-9f82-8a666b6590ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: MRK 5:40
Text: And they laughed him to scorn. But when he had put them all out, he taketh the father and the mother of the damsel, and them that were with him, and entereth in where the damsel was lying.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:599f9997-eb5f-426b-866f-d00582b7d6fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: MRK 5:41
Text: And he took the damsel by the hand, and said unto her, Talitha cumi; which is, being interpreted, Damsel, I say unto thee, arise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9651e4bb-8f11-47d8-ab8b-38071b13b1a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: MRK 5:42
Text: And straightway the damsel arose, and walked; for she was of the age of twelve years. And they were astonished with a great astonishment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/5/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b3d654a-9da3-406e-86e3-3e51ad408b30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: MRK 5:43
Text: And he charged them straitly that no man should know it; and commanded that something should be given her to eat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:974e3853-4b57-4892-a469-0620b067b400>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: MRK 6:1
Text: And he went out from thence, and came into his own country; and his disciples follow him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddfaadeb-05ad-4d41-a9be-95bdb71ad34b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 285

Reference: MRK 6:2
Text: And when the sabbath day was come, he began to teach in the synagogue: and many hearing him were astonished, saying, From whence hath this man these things? and what wisdom is this which is given unto him, that even such mighty works are wrought by his hands?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d69d66a2-9d2f-403c-b6ed-0355e769a09e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: MRK 6:3
Text: Is not this the carpenter, the son of Mary, the brother of James, and Joses, and of Juda, and Simon? and are not his sisters here with us? And they were offended at him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8949cb2-894d-4ed7-950c-5cea0c2ddcaa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: MRK 6:4
Text: But Jesus said unto them, A prophet is not without honour, but in his own country, and among his own kin, and in his own house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2d6d553-532d-417a-91ea-0142b79badb7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: MRK 6:5
Text: And he could there do no mighty work, save that he laid his hands upon a few sick folk, and healed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53f0cdcc-c7c8-4f99-881d-afa1aea2d17d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MRK 6:6
Text: And he marvelled because of their unbelief. And he went round about the villages, teaching.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:010bafe0-0f11-462b-b9f0-29c9b1a96fa8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: MRK 6:7
Text: And he called unto him the twelve, and began to send them forth by two and two; and gave them power over unclean spirits;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1b1abae-5c35-4d4a-af27-3658b30dc530>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: MRK 6:8
Text: And commanded them that they should take nothing for their journey, save a staff only; no scrip, no bread, no money in their purse:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d94b273-6c3e-40c9-82df-78402918a720>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: MRK 6:9
Text: But be shod with sandals; and not put on two coats.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d30c664-f457-4f6a-92e6-75a1a62e3dd8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MRK 6:10
Text: And he said unto them, In what place soever ye enter into an house, there abide till ye depart from that place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6c2682f-6444-4eb0-aa21-c4061be3050a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 282

Reference: MRK 6:11
Text: And whosoever shall not receive you, nor hear you, when ye depart thence, shake off the dust under your feet for a testimony against them. Verily I say unto you, It shall be more tolerable for Sodom and Gomorrha in the day of judgment, than for that city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99f08080-0261-4ee7-944c-923782eac06f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: MRK 6:12
Text: And they went out, and preached that men should repent.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e89dadd-d3a8-4660-8ec8-576901530a4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MRK 6:13
Text: And they cast out many devils, and anointed with oil many that were sick, and healed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf6f5762-c143-4496-b866-babc4c22b4e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: MRK 6:14
Text: And king Herod heard of him; (for his name was spread abroad:) and he said, That John the Baptist was risen from the dead, and therefore mighty works do shew forth themselves in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82b81332-9ad4-471a-893b-dd0ef6006364>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: MRK 6:15
Text: Others said, That it is Elias. And others said, That it is a prophet, or as one of the prophets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73f0a66a-9122-4996-a44b-8427450ab54b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: MRK 6:16
Text: But when Herod heard thereof, he said, It is John, whom I beheaded: he is risen from the dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4689fad3-28b2-4e29-9150-6ee2aa9bb08c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: MRK 6:17
Text: For Herod himself had sent forth and laid hold upon John, and bound him in prison for Herodias’ sake, his brother Philip’s wife: for he had married her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4af04ec-bf73-411b-8db3-cfac275d600a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: MRK 6:18
Text: For John had said unto Herod, It is not lawful for thee to have thy brother’s wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d68e84e7-4b93-4f14-a027-679dc80444b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: MRK 6:19
Text: Therefore Herodias had a quarrel against him, and would have killed him; but she could not:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f4d6e10-7960-4502-81b9-3c143a9938d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: MRK 6:20
Text: For Herod feared John, knowing that he was a just man and an holy, and observed him; and when he heard him, he did many things, and heard him gladly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5f7758e-ffb9-40af-96d3-b4c649289bfc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: MRK 6:21
Text: And when a convenient day was come, that Herod on his birthday made a supper to his lords, high captains, and chief estates of Galilee;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d37e695c-4f51-4980-bb43-313ed0a58b2d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: MRK 6:22
Text: And when the daughter of the said Herodias came in, and danced, and pleased Herod and them that sat with him, the king said unto the damsel, Ask of me whatsoever thou wilt, and I will give it thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80dc8e99-cb0d-4afd-b063-edcf885d05df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: MRK 6:23
Text: And he sware unto her, Whatsoever thou shalt ask of me, I will give it thee, unto the half of my kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:273ff1fc-a222-420d-ad6d-0f2c24eef9d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: MRK 6:24
Text: And she went forth, and said unto her mother, What shall I ask? And she said, The head of John the Baptist.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8598d65e-8a83-4281-ad7d-676452c4ab96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: MRK 6:25
Text: And she came in straightway with haste unto the king, and asked, saying, I will that thou give me by and by in a charger the head of John the Baptist.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3fe2e13-c7c9-43e3-bc75-cac0e3c24ec1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: MRK 6:26
Text: And the king was exceeding sorry; yet for his oath’s sake, and for their sakes which sat with him, he would not reject her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d9ff3ee-9f66-4fb1-82e3-41d646aea650>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: MRK 6:27
Text: And immediately the king sent an executioner, and commanded his head to be brought: and he went and beheaded him in the prison,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7e0f46e-5fab-4e5f-a0f9-9454efb6a8b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: MRK 6:28
Text: And brought his head in a charger, and gave it to the damsel: and the damsel gave it to her mother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3ad2f27-70e6-4ab8-811f-195136542c9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: MRK 6:29
Text: And when his disciples heard of it, they came and took up his corpse, and laid it in a tomb.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7f5f388-0700-4343-97d7-a96c24fbad78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: MRK 6:30
Text: And the apostles gathered themselves together unto Jesus, and told him all things, both what they had done, and what they had taught.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf9aef74-344a-428b-842b-dbd33ea7be25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: MRK 6:31
Text: And he said unto them, Come ye yourselves apart into a desert place, and rest a while: for there were many coming and going, and they had no leisure so much as to eat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1977dde6-feb5-4ec4-ab68-2e69b491683e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: MRK 6:32
Text: And they departed into a desert place by ship privately.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11bde544-af44-4fc3-b271-9e39d07d9e7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: MRK 6:33
Text: And the people saw them departing, and many knew him, and ran afoot thither out of all cities, and outwent them, and came together unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e97a48af-b946-4e9b-9d9c-134225ac192b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: MRK 6:34
Text: And Jesus, when he came out, saw much people, and was moved with compassion toward them, because they were as sheep not having a shepherd: and he began to teach them many things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22877c2b-3acf-4159-9e2a-27f900e77636>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: MRK 6:35
Text: And when the day was now far spent, his disciples came unto him, and said, This is a desert place, and now the time is far passed:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c3ec1fd-c2d6-42ae-8d5c-44e5595fa6cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: MRK 6:36
Text: Send them away, that they may go into the country round about, and into the villages, and buy themselves bread: for they have nothing to eat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8fa5340d-3def-46ac-9019-8f42745cddf3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: MRK 6:37
Text: He answered and said unto them, Give ye them to eat. And they say unto him, Shall we go and buy two hundred pennyworth of bread, and give them to eat?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34c96bc1-a4fd-4552-9bef-f45df139af1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: MRK 6:38
Text: He saith unto them, How many loaves have ye? go and see. And when they knew, they say, Five, and two fishes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f2e716f-ea9d-4d99-941a-4fe23c563527>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: MRK 6:39
Text: And he commanded them to make all sit down by companies upon the green grass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfac90ac-e2af-4ff8-827a-f0069ede451b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: MRK 6:40
Text: And they sat down in ranks, by hundreds, and by fifties.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ffcc3ef-8470-4f5b-bcd8-1bb9ad6fafdd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: MRK 6:41
Text: And when he had taken the five loaves and the two fishes, he looked up to heaven, and blessed, and brake the loaves, and gave them to his disciples to set before them; and the two fishes divided he among them all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19d31283-4aff-4cc5-884e-3e44935681f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 65

Reference: MRK 6:42
Text: And they did all eat, and were filled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59c5bd18-9513-44c8-adf1-31e9b42d179e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: MRK 6:43
Text: And they took up twelve baskets full of the fragments, and of the fishes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1915a5c7-985e-4926-af2f-fab0f8dd5b4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: MRK 6:44
Text: And they that did eat of the loaves were about five thousand men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73a8756b-b027-41ac-ba66-bd1543f46fa4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: MRK 6:45
Text: And straightway he constrained his disciples to get into the ship, and to go to the other side before unto Bethsaida, while he sent away the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29c3e423-bd7b-4f5e-9b83-f8454eb5bcc0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: MRK 6:46
Text: And when he had sent them away, he departed into a mountain to pray.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:661d6f6b-e1c8-4397-9cc3-f4f2eae60b43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MRK 6:47
Text: And when even was come, the ship was in the midst of the sea, and he alone on the land.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c42d468b-6e00-4929-865c-44a31df4cb88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: MRK 6:48
Text: And he saw them toiling in rowing; for the wind was contrary unto them: and about the fourth watch of the night he cometh unto them, walking upon the sea, and would have passed by them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:109d9734-8688-464f-952e-fef836b8c968>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: MRK 6:49
Text: But when they saw him walking upon the sea, they supposed it had been a spirit, and cried out:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6641680e-8d03-47a9-a334-7e2d03f092e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: MRK 6:50
Text: For they all saw him, and were troubled. And immediately he talked with them, and saith unto them, Be of good cheer: it is I; be not afraid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c814d6f8-7da1-4c6f-a17b-e86f7ab4c0ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: MRK 6:51
Text: And he went up unto them into the ship; and the wind ceased: and they were sore amazed in themselves beyond measure, and wondered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4fa40e6-04f0-465d-bd4c-034da5b9f530>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: MRK 6:52
Text: For they considered not the miracle of the loaves: for their heart was hardened.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:777c9744-bdd8-4e28-984d-aaf763d80960>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: MRK 6:53
Text: And when they had passed over, they came into the land of Gennesaret, and drew to the shore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97aa6fb6-6b29-43fb-8534-acf3b6fcda60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: MRK 6:54
Text: And when they were come out of the ship, straightway they knew him,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/55
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e639d1ee-5454-42f9-855c-97e450d1fde5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: MRK 6:55
Text: And ran through that whole region round about, and began to carry about in beds those that were sick, where they heard he was.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/6/56
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b77efc7-9406-4bd2-bfc0-3afcf7c77efa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: MRK 6:56
Text: And whithersoever he entered, into villages, or cities, or country, they laid the sick in the streets, and besought him that they might touch if it were but the border of his garment: and as many as touched him were made whole.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45a133d6-2462-4a90-95f4-592c7a30a7a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: MRK 7:1
Text: Then came together unto him the Pharisees, and certain of the scribes, which came from Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95d10f44-4369-4066-84d5-64fe3aea3d47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: MRK 7:2
Text: And when they saw some of his disciples eat bread with defiled, that is to say, with unwashen, hands, they found fault.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53f56f56-5e43-47c2-bc35-72e21a1d97f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: MRK 7:3
Text: For the Pharisees, and all the Jews, except they wash their hands oft, eat not, holding the tradition of the elders.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c736308-33e7-4404-b87b-038a00abf905>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: MRK 7:4
Text: And when they come from the market, except they wash, they eat not. And many other things there be, which they have received to hold, as the washing of cups, and pots, brasen vessels, and of tables.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14ee7573-22b5-4ea4-acf0-3890c511e6c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: MRK 7:5
Text: Then the Pharisees and scribes asked him, Why walk not thy disciples according to the tradition of the elders, but eat bread with unwashen hands?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da1fddb2-84bc-45cc-aa4e-0408b565cd49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: MRK 7:6
Text: He answered and said unto them, Well hath Esaias prophesied of you hypocrites, as it is written, This people honoureth me with their lips, but their heart is far from me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58eaf8bc-734e-4a46-aec1-d6006c31e7a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: MRK 7:7
Text: Howbeit in vain do they worship me, teaching for doctrines the commandments of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e1ee3b7-3255-4958-9202-8cfc4157bfb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: MRK 7:8
Text: For laying aside the commandment of God, ye hold the tradition of men, as the washing of pots and cups: and many other such like things ye do.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b8e8c04-6e8b-4427-9869-3553234d9a9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: MRK 7:9
Text: And he said unto them, Full well ye reject the commandment of God, that ye may keep your own tradition.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ef3b013-9c13-49f1-8803-84ef3675d32f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: MRK 7:10
Text: For Moses said, Honour thy father and thy mother; and, Whoso curseth father or mother, let him die the death:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6f528cd-3b58-4555-9178-1b2819283e2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: MRK 7:11
Text: But ye say, If a man shall say to his father or mother, It is Corban, that is to say, a gift, by whatsoever thou mightest be profited by me; he shall be free.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a5fd09d-cfbf-42ae-ae4f-51a8fd2e1996>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: MRK 7:12
Text: And ye suffer him no more to do ought for his father or his mother;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:889b0484-b237-486d-8065-5805258e0d5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: MRK 7:13
Text: Making the word of God of none effect through your tradition, which ye have delivered: and many such like things do ye.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6e779e6-6b46-470a-861f-18deeb421c8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: MRK 7:14
Text: And when he had called all the people unto him, he said unto them, Hearken unto me every one of you, and understand:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be20ee39-00a0-47c2-a365-516ae8da7fed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: MRK 7:15
Text: There is nothing from without a man, that entering into him can defile him: but the things which come out of him, those are they that defile the man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c997bdd-fb08-4021-989a-470fdc88b6d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 70

Reference: MRK 7:16
Text: If any man have ears to hear, let him hear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e331f64-a5b9-465a-a03f-fc9ee4f193e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: MRK 7:17
Text: And when he was entered into the house from the people, his disciples asked him concerning the parable.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50d025de-3f81-4d75-b87e-9a42d0e901f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: MRK 7:18
Text: And he saith unto them, Are ye so without understanding also? Do ye not perceive, that whatsoever thing from without entereth into the man, it cannot defile him;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89612500-0890-49e5-9176-1eb3d2f1d592>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: MRK 7:19
Text: Because it entereth not into his heart, but into the belly, and goeth out into the draught, purging all meats?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90d3022c-3578-45e8-83d3-32ed2e05d015>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: MRK 7:20
Text: And he said, That which cometh out of the man, that defileth the man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce838360-591a-49ae-a381-6b69ee187fc3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: MRK 7:21
Text: For from within, out of the heart of men, proceed evil thoughts, adulteries, fornications, murders,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:656b9fe4-488b-4355-a4ae-42736c01207c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: MRK 7:22
Text: Thefts, covetousness, wickedness, deceit, lasciviousness, an evil eye, blasphemy, pride, foolishness:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cffc945b-62be-4a2e-a1cd-34acf7d5f2f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: MRK 7:23
Text: All these evil things come from within, and defile the man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffc5490d-dee8-41f7-834e-71136081c725>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: MRK 7:24
Text: And from thence he arose, and went into the borders of Tyre and Sidon, and entered into an house, and would have no man know it: but he could not be hid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b91a3ef3-7b3b-40c5-8bfe-5960d486eb8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: MRK 7:25
Text: For a certain woman, whose young daughter had an unclean spirit, heard of him, and came and fell at his feet:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bdfc1e9b-61e3-4a2a-9afe-b7e588114f75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: MRK 7:26
Text: The woman was a Greek, a Syrophenician by nation; and she besought him that he would cast forth the devil out of her daughter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ae1c4d5-0f23-4f54-9dfd-a6a44a65d83c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: MRK 7:27
Text: But Jesus said unto her, Let the children first be filled: for it is not meet to take the children’s bread, and to cast it unto the dogs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7668f2d7-4d67-417a-b4c4-96cee5c74566>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: MRK 7:28
Text: And she answered and said unto him, Yes, Lord: yet the dogs under the table eat of the children’s crumbs.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0cbe853-b660-41cb-ab1c-f14add317e08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: MRK 7:29
Text: And he said unto her, For this saying go thy way; the devil is gone out of thy daughter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67b701d4-12b5-4d9b-ac9e-02bed5346d3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: MRK 7:30
Text: And when she was come to her house, she found the devil gone out, and her daughter laid upon the bed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b22005f-8ede-4137-bd20-a462975f0c40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: MRK 7:31
Text: And again, departing from the coasts of Tyre and Sidon, he came unto the sea of Galilee, through the midst of the coasts of Decapolis.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4329082-4190-48e0-b2fa-7b559e8e70fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: MRK 7:32
Text: And they bring unto him one that was deaf, and had an impediment in his speech; and they beseech him to put his hand upon him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6b21f54-3ade-444f-9e86-efe93ad7fd5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: MRK 7:33
Text: And he took him aside from the multitude, and put his fingers into his ears, and he spit, and touched his tongue;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:256663fe-6239-417c-b600-c8a9319a257c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MRK 7:34
Text: And looking up to heaven, he sighed, and saith unto him, Ephphatha, that is, Be opened.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c89d616-dbea-4d91-98a9-94657fbded0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: MRK 7:35
Text: And straightway his ears were opened, and the string of his tongue was loosed, and he spake plain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99d2d0b9-5b11-444b-8eaf-724fce9c90d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: MRK 7:36
Text: And he charged them that they should tell no man: but the more he charged them, so much the more a great deal they published it;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/7/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e59ef2d5-7e11-4dc9-81f5-c0056f51c583>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: MRK 7:37
Text: And were beyond measure astonished, saying, He hath done all things well: he maketh both the deaf to hear, and the dumb to speak.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e21e62f-a16f-44f9-b909-0a2ae4f3e4b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: MRK 8:1
Text: In those days the multitude being very great, and having nothing to eat, Jesus called his disciples unto him, and saith unto them,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20465fc9-2a68-410b-b6fa-62911f0a371b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: MRK 8:2
Text: I have compassion on the multitude, because they have now been with me three days, and have nothing to eat:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af36ddcc-3689-4118-b350-04614d8ede53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: MRK 8:3
Text: And if I send them away fasting to their own houses, they will faint by the way: for divers of them came from far.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b3997cf-409d-487c-99d3-01a4b25a89f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: MRK 8:4
Text: And his disciples answered him, From whence can a man satisfy these men with bread here in the wilderness?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf90c323-8d74-4eb0-a67e-8096bb35897c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: MRK 8:5
Text: And he asked them, How many loaves have ye? And they said, Seven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fcaee7be-7263-492e-b182-fb9742074499>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: MRK 8:6
Text: And he commanded the people to sit down on the ground: and he took the seven loaves, and gave thanks, and brake, and gave to his disciples to set before them; and they did set them before the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0a5f47a-a93a-4ab2-a6a4-4933315b66fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: MRK 8:7
Text: And they had a few small fishes: and he blessed, and commanded to set them also before them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33e3c500-894c-42ec-b85d-9d8fb8ddcd09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: MRK 8:8
Text: So they did eat, and were filled: and they took up of the broken meat that was left seven baskets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76c35b0b-4837-42e3-aa65-4e9765d4c9bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: MRK 8:9
Text: And they that had eaten were about four thousand: and he sent them away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ae82ad8-5076-4c5d-b9a4-15a9100b7768>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: MRK 8:10
Text: And straightway he entered into a ship with his disciples, and came into the parts of Dalmanutha.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37efaa8a-3d3b-4b79-96b5-ca4d45c0671a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: MRK 8:11
Text: And the Pharisees came forth, and began to question with him, seeking of him a sign from heaven, tempting him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c0ea262-142c-44ab-be41-f69d1974ac32>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: MRK 8:12
Text: And he sighed deeply in his spirit, and saith, Why doth this generation seek after a sign? verily I say unto you, There shall no sign be given unto this generation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:488dce9a-8b4d-4501-877c-bfdc3f22ec07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: MRK 8:13
Text: And he left them, and entering into the ship again departed to the other side.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b08d2e7-bf1e-40d2-92a5-10cce6ffa696>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: MRK 8:14
Text: Now the disciples had forgotten to take bread, neither had they in the ship with them more than one loaf.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d962be41-593e-4c97-9322-8befad181bff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: MRK 8:15
Text: And he charged them, saying, Take heed, beware of the leaven of the Pharisees, and of the leaven of Herod.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bca7ac50-4fc5-48c3-9359-170001e4ce5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: MRK 8:16
Text: And they reasoned among themselves, saying, It is because we have no bread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f109d43-7288-42a1-ae91-2c29aaf5752b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: MRK 8:17
Text: And when Jesus knew it, he saith unto them, Why reason ye, because ye have no bread? perceive ye not yet, neither understand? have ye your heart yet hardened?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:467f3673-29e6-4bd9-9b02-9e6ebeefd2c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: MRK 8:18
Text: Having eyes, see ye not? and having ears, hear ye not? and do ye not remember?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b649bae0-71d8-4cd1-85d8-eca05ddb19de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: MRK 8:19
Text: When I brake the five loaves among five thousand, how many baskets full of fragments took ye up? They say unto him, Twelve.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2bc5592-845e-40e0-9f13-7797dc2a6f01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: MRK 8:20
Text: And when the seven among four thousand, how many baskets full of fragments took ye up? And they said, Seven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8261b866-6e98-4923-a242-f9a49fee78b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: MRK 8:21
Text: And he said unto them, How is it that ye do not understand?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a34da895-76bf-4bae-8c61-b9566ba066b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MRK 8:22
Text: And he cometh to Bethsaida; and they bring a blind man unto him, and besought him to touch him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:085a6e6f-59da-4cda-ad4c-14b4e33ed79c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: MRK 8:23
Text: And he took the blind man by the hand, and led him out of the town; and when he had spit on his eyes, and put his hands upon him, he asked him if he saw ought.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7454917-dbfe-4cf3-b755-64ffa5ae62cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: MRK 8:24
Text: And he looked up, and said, I see men as trees, walking.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4db37e12-484f-4d7c-8cf3-743e9094dd91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: MRK 8:25
Text: After that he put his hands again upon his eyes, and made him look up: and he was restored, and saw every man clearly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3f5483f-5e11-4f2e-8a25-c5f6e7ce014b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: MRK 8:26
Text: And he sent him away to his house, saying, Neither go into the town, nor tell it to any in the town.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8cda2f35-ad92-471c-a2b7-0ef7c271d50d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: MRK 8:27
Text: And Jesus went out, and his disciples, into the towns of Caesarea Philippi: and by the way he asked his disciples, saying unto them, Whom do men say that I am?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8cfe368-8937-458b-aaf1-cf38e089a944>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MRK 8:28
Text: And they answered, John the Baptist; but some say, Elias; and others, One of the prophets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32e6bb89-ff8b-424e-957f-a71ae3a9da54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MRK 8:29
Text: And he saith unto them, But whom say ye that I am? And Peter answereth and saith unto him, Thou art the Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2f5f48a-a1ea-4712-b5a6-0cfdde0e1ec2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: MRK 8:30
Text: And he charged them that they should tell no man of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65184ca9-e779-452c-9828-febdfef7b784>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: MRK 8:31
Text: And he began to teach them, that the Son of man must suffer many things, and be rejected of the elders, and of the chief priests, and scribes, and be killed, and after three days rise again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23b4a330-cd78-44f5-bab2-641da4e47933>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: MRK 8:32
Text: And he spake that saying openly. And Peter took him, and began to rebuke him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7de5325d-fa1a-4c3d-b163-334cc2ebc1f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: MRK 8:33
Text: But when he had turned about and looked on his disciples, he rebuked Peter, saying, Get thee behind me, Satan: for thou savourest not the things that be of God, but the things that be of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc30e7e5-727f-4db6-a5b2-7f3f03ae1def>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: MRK 8:34
Text: And when he had called the people unto him with his disciples also, he said unto them, Whosoever will come after me, let him deny himself, and take up his cross, and follow me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5e04543-ac6a-4e90-9c2f-047341c882bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: MRK 8:35
Text: For whosoever will save his life shall lose it; but whosoever shall lose his life for my sake and the gospel’s, the same shall save it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c6e76f6-a60f-4600-9d96-bce3540c7651>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: MRK 8:36
Text: For what shall it profit a man, if he shall gain the whole world, and lose his own soul?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3a87f4f-4860-4430-ac9c-84f6d75d7b4f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: MRK 8:37
Text: Or what shall a man give in exchange for his soul?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/8/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:adcf042b-d8b3-4408-bc70-98998e1d7666>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: MRK 8:38
Text: Whosoever therefore shall be ashamed of me and of my words in this adulterous and sinful generation; of him also shall the Son of man be ashamed, when he cometh in the glory of his Father with the holy angels.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebae2b35-3f51-4dbb-a5bf-c18d7e0574a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: MRK 9:1
Text: And he said unto them, Verily I say unto you, That there be some of them that stand here, which shall not taste of death, till they have seen the kingdom of God come with power.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3127091a-12b3-46e4-a372-19122748a5ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: MRK 9:2
Text: And after six days Jesus taketh with him Peter, and James, and John, and leadeth them up into an high mountain apart by themselves: and he was transfigured before them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46b7f9f5-eeaf-4ff8-ba54-a7f503f81b06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: MRK 9:3
Text: And his raiment became shining, exceeding white as snow; so as no fuller on earth can white them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66bb1fa3-d2de-4274-9768-05e44659ead3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: MRK 9:4
Text: And there appeared unto them Elias with Moses: and they were talking with Jesus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39a65a9d-10c7-4b96-9eb8-8d41b9e2fd22>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: MRK 9:5
Text: And Peter answered and said to Jesus, Master, it is good for us to be here: and let us make three tabernacles; one for thee, and one for Moses, and one for Elias.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ab65ff6-7b6b-45b0-87ee-856ccb2ad3ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: MRK 9:6
Text: For he wist not what to say; for they were sore afraid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e55c45b3-a90c-482b-a6f6-adf86ed353fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: MRK 9:7
Text: And there was a cloud that overshadowed them: and a voice came out of the cloud, saying, This is my beloved Son: hear him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:932d4ee3-5780-4c52-aa10-8d49033c18f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: MRK 9:8
Text: And suddenly, when they had looked round about, they saw no man any more, save Jesus only with themselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5835f549-cdc1-491b-838f-85fbe1601263>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: MRK 9:9
Text: And as they came down from the mountain, he charged them that they should tell no man what things they had seen, till the Son of man were risen from the dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffd0670a-001f-4647-a1fb-434b449503df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: MRK 9:10
Text: And they kept that saying with themselves, questioning one with another what the rising from the dead should mean.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04f7be60-7150-4945-b36f-6d057cd1390c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: MRK 9:11
Text: And they asked him, saying, Why say the scribes that Elias must first come?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ad6d4a1-3031-40d9-823a-3c87600494a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: MRK 9:12
Text: And he answered and told them, Elias verily cometh first, and restoreth all things; and how it is written of the Son of man, that he must suffer many things, and be set at nought.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49ea006f-86a8-40cb-8659-8c2ce941f172>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: MRK 9:13
Text: But I say unto you, That Elias is indeed come, and they have done unto him whatsoever they listed, as it is written of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e996679-8a01-4f58-b8c4-c16bb0f345cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: MRK 9:14
Text: And when he came to his disciples, he saw a great multitude about them, and the scribes questioning with them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2c9998a-a480-4903-9ba2-874b8da058b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: MRK 9:15
Text: And straightway all the people, when they beheld him, were greatly amazed, and running to him saluted him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d6e3099-1cfc-4d07-a6ff-7f3233a5c240>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: MRK 9:16
Text: And he asked the scribes, What question ye with them?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6342ebc-e957-47fd-b3c4-de5ed1198468>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: MRK 9:17
Text: And one of the multitude answered and said, Master, I have brought unto thee my son, which hath a dumb spirit;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39a2b6af-6174-49a6-8d71-c51e75d10998>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: MRK 9:18
Text: And wheresoever he taketh him, he teareth him: and he foameth, and gnasheth with his teeth, and pineth away: and I spake to thy disciples that they should cast him out; and they could not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe5507a2-39a6-4f58-910d-0c31a3de21a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: MRK 9:19
Text: He answereth him, and saith, O faithless generation, how long shall I be with you? how long shall I suffer you? bring him unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ac8eab7-baa0-4c20-af4b-1f0ae2893e6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: MRK 9:20
Text: And they brought him unto him: and when he saw him, straightway the spirit tare him; and he fell on the ground, and wallowed foaming.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0b956f8-e608-4425-9242-a6fc680fc9d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: MRK 9:21
Text: And he asked his father, How long is it ago since this came unto him? And he said, Of a child.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9323ae1e-2284-4ec0-a23c-2aa62f68303c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: MRK 9:22
Text: And ofttimes it hath cast him into the fire, and into the waters, to destroy him: but if thou canst do any thing, have compassion on us, and help us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:859c76e4-d852-4f75-9375-23a7a604cc35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MRK 9:23
Text: Jesus said unto him, If thou canst believe, all things are possible to him that believeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0fca7080-7044-4980-a14a-a0d6bcddb0b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: MRK 9:24
Text: And straightway the father of the child cried out, and said with tears, Lord, I believe; help thou mine unbelief.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f8fda97-20bd-496b-9f76-f8b3b0b8b0d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: MRK 9:25
Text: When Jesus saw that the people came running together, he rebuked the foul spirit, saying unto him, Thou dumb and deaf spirit, I charge thee, come out of him, and enter no more into him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49830a96-e53b-4bf7-b89f-0eb127e6e320>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: MRK 9:26
Text: And the spirit cried, and rent him sore, and came out of him: and he was as one dead; insomuch that many said, He is dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:051dfbd0-9b68-4f5b-aa2c-162e30754221>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: MRK 9:27
Text: But Jesus took him by the hand, and lifted him up; and he arose.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:231c9b1a-871c-4dcc-86c3-c41de49d6a1e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: MRK 9:28
Text: And when he was come into the house, his disciples asked him privately, Why could not we cast him out?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b60523a7-fca4-4941-875c-97859154f2ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: MRK 9:29
Text: And he said unto them, This kind can come forth by nothing, but by prayer and fasting.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0868b99-9dc3-4b3e-8218-a290c0dbd478>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: MRK 9:30
Text: And they departed thence, and passed through Galilee; and he would not that any man should know it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b902815-8cad-4aef-85c5-1f4912cd9700>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: MRK 9:31
Text: For he taught his disciples, and said unto them, The Son of man is delivered into the hands of men, and they shall kill him; and after that he is killed, he shall rise the third day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94d0a056-54c2-4888-ac5d-220a7d37ceb0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: MRK 9:32
Text: But they understood not that saying, and were afraid to ask him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:457ab8fb-b7c1-45f6-b8b0-0111fed06123>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: MRK 9:33
Text: And he came to Capernaum: and being in the house he asked them, What was it that ye disputed among yourselves by the way?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae75af5b-e0d4-4a47-a7ee-519e8d024c30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: MRK 9:34
Text: But they held their peace: for by the way they had disputed among themselves, who should be the greatest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65222217-fc0e-417f-b641-6c243089c04d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: MRK 9:35
Text: And he sat down, and called the twelve, and saith unto them, If any man desire to be first, the same shall be last of all, and servant of all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e36471e5-c38a-498a-a7bd-b25726e0b414>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: MRK 9:36
Text: And he took a child, and set him in the midst of them: and when he had taken him in his arms, he said unto them,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5176ea1e-188a-4afc-bb1b-68c3bab930c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: MRK 9:37
Text: Whosoever shall receive one of such children in my name, receiveth me: and whosoever shall receive me, receiveth not me, but him that sent me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd1d8d2b-72b5-42bd-8d40-819f7b310c69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: MRK 9:38
Text: And John answered him, saying, Master, we saw one casting out devils in thy name, and he followeth not us: and we forbad him, because he followeth not us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9a93d4a-bb91-4a3e-9331-3ed3e2df3a6d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: MRK 9:39
Text: But Jesus said, Forbid him not: for there is no man which shall do a miracle in my name, that can lightly speak evil of me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7e0a6c5-4264-423e-b77d-e266b4a6f6a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 72

Reference: MRK 9:40
Text: For he that is not against us is on our part.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4eef3589-cce5-4358-9bf4-d6b0d2be3cff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: MRK 9:41
Text: For whosoever shall give you a cup of water to drink in my name, because ye belong to Christ, verily I say unto you, he shall not lose his reward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b6b81f86-bdad-4243-9c11-1e60ed829120>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: MRK 9:42
Text: And whosoever shall offend one of these little ones that believe in me, it is better for him that a millstone were hanged about his neck, and he were cast into the sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:091bdae0-96b7-4485-b40d-3eca424d7a75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: MRK 9:43
Text: And if thy hand offend thee, cut it off: it is better for thee to enter into life maimed, than having two hands to go into hell, into the fire that never shall be quenched:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:559e7b16-7327-4e60-be91-54a139092b99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: MRK 9:44
Text: Where their worm dieth not, and the fire is not quenched.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e2eadb5-8454-4ea5-9c2d-bcae5e93cf38>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: MRK 9:45
Text: And if thy foot offend thee, cut it off: it is better for thee to enter halt into life, than having two feet to be cast into hell, into the fire that never shall be quenched:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1c92a7f-cc08-42ba-bc79-c0f6c1024bda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: MRK 9:46
Text: Where their worm dieth not, and the fire is not quenched.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:805027f5-800c-470d-8894-d356d09bf461>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: MRK 9:47
Text: And if thine eye offend thee, pluck it out: it is better for thee to enter into the kingdom of God with one eye, than having two eyes to be cast into hell fire:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c0ef258-15a6-4092-a79b-73975a9195de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: MRK 9:48
Text: Where their worm dieth not, and the fire is not quenched.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5fdf73c-a599-4907-8c6b-281ec2255b13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MRK 9:49
Text: For every one shall be salted with fire, and every sacrifice shall be salted with salt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/9/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d88621b4-bc63-4318-8763-456f488e194a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: MRK 9:50
Text: Salt is good: but if the salt have lost his saltness, wherewith will ye season it? Have salt in yourselves, and have peace one with another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06c7d868-c760-4e56-97e6-84d1ca81287a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: MRK 10:1
Text: And he arose from thence, and cometh into the coasts of Judaea by the farther side of Jordan: and the people resort unto him again; and, as he was wont, he taught them again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6ad6990-4905-494e-948e-73d19adce40f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: MRK 10:2
Text: And the Pharisees came to him, and asked him, Is it lawful for a man to put away his wife? tempting him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f12b38d9-295c-45de-a061-09d8ec8a37b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: MRK 10:3
Text: And he answered and said unto them, What did Moses command you?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f51c515f-db99-4c5a-b7ea-6474929cc5b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: MRK 10:4
Text: And they said, Moses suffered to write a bill of divorcement, and to put her away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cad77a2-e78b-424c-bbfd-e55a5be2b6a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: MRK 10:5
Text: And Jesus answered and said unto them, For the hardness of your heart he wrote you this precept.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0a559dc-ca89-4a51-9ed0-272e5ccfe03b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: MRK 10:6
Text: But from the beginning of the creation God made them male and female.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e40ee2de-7bed-4f1d-977f-9dfeb4d87094>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: MRK 10:7
Text: For this cause shall a man leave his father and mother, and cleave to his wife;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:001b97bd-3393-4ae0-a7dc-7a5284fd2bbf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: MRK 10:8
Text: And they twain shall be one flesh: so then they are no more twain, but one flesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:854ebd77-6fcb-42d8-94c5-f3790db77c77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: MRK 10:9
Text: What therefore God hath joined together, let not man put asunder.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:347dda29-44c6-4a7d-a459-a3a7bb3cb8e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: MRK 10:10
Text: And in the house his disciples asked him again of the same matter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d62983f-9560-4c0f-bb35-5e69106306a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MRK 10:11
Text: And he saith unto them, Whosoever shall put away his wife, and marry another, committeth adultery against her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:996b1c81-791b-4acb-bf48-848f14b7ebb6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MRK 10:12
Text: And if a woman shall put away her husband, and be married to another, she committeth adultery.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dee0ca47-f270-44c9-a3e6-bcc717b92a9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: MRK 10:13
Text: And they brought young children to him, that he should touch them: and his disciples rebuked those that brought them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c285c576-6d73-4468-8d9b-17e6b18a3572>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: MRK 10:14
Text: But when Jesus saw it, he was much displeased, and said unto them, Suffer the little children to come unto me, and forbid them not: for of such is the kingdom of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d295d01-5c79-4929-9e59-a3f414cb53ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: MRK 10:15
Text: Verily I say unto you, Whosoever shall not receive the kingdom of God as a little child, he shall not enter therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:249013e6-1b1f-4d1c-9184-7e5d7aca5dee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: MRK 10:16
Text: And he took them up in his arms, put his hands upon them, and blessed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ff76b4c-a0d7-449d-a746-52656ce23273>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: MRK 10:17
Text: And when he was gone forth into the way, there came one running, and kneeled to him, and asked him, Good Master, what shall I do that I may inherit eternal life?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99dad0d6-b206-4c62-8652-2e21904017e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: MRK 10:18
Text: And Jesus said unto him, Why callest thou me good? there is none good but one, that is, God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6b95022-3374-4e38-907a-2d9d5d1b46e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: MRK 10:19
Text: Thou knowest the commandments, Do not commit adultery, Do not kill, Do not steal, Do not bear false witness, Defraud not, Honour thy father and mother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c8b9d68a-a9ee-4fe7-8a4a-86666cb54556>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: MRK 10:20
Text: And he answered and said unto him, Master, all these have I observed from my youth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4f9c33f-20c7-480f-908e-095b09c20366>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: MRK 10:21
Text: Then Jesus beholding him loved him, and said unto him, One thing thou lackest: go thy way, sell whatsoever thou hast, and give to the poor, and thou shalt have treasure in heaven: and come, take up the cross, and follow me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d3573d1-54ca-454c-b8c5-472d542bdac8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: MRK 10:22
Text: And he was sad at that saying, and went away grieved: for he had great possessions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a7aa990-15bb-4d77-9603-14a681328f02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: MRK 10:23
Text: And Jesus looked round about, and saith unto his disciples, How hardly shall they that have riches enter into the kingdom of God!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b6352aa-de70-4e50-8959-f42788800267>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: MRK 10:24
Text: And the disciples were astonished at his words. But Jesus answereth again, and saith unto them, Children, how hard is it for them that trust in riches to enter into the kingdom of God!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fc99f86-9b82-4a0c-92f6-7a82cb5fe445>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: MRK 10:25
Text: It is easier for a camel to go through the eye of a needle, than for a rich man to enter into the kingdom of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7dc956f-7351-4a0e-93f0-8103035af168>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: MRK 10:26
Text: And they were astonished out of measure, saying among themselves, Who then can be saved?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db8f4e7b-5bec-4bdd-a024-8540ed834faf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: MRK 10:27
Text: And Jesus looking upon them saith, With men it is impossible, but not with God: for with God all things are possible.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:420946cb-599b-43b6-9748-bbf67fa695a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: MRK 10:28
Text: Then Peter began to say unto him, Lo, we have left all, and have followed thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6126add-0cf0-46e9-9066-5e72b7dd07ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: MRK 10:29
Text: And Jesus answered and said, Verily I say unto you, There is no man that hath left house, or brethren, or sisters, or father, or mother, or wife, or children, or lands, for my sake, and the gospel’s,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ebd028d-d27a-4c41-8f3d-a84407a5e403>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: MRK 10:30
Text: But he shall receive an hundredfold now in this time, houses, and brethren, and sisters, and mothers, and children, and lands, with persecutions; and in the world to come eternal life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:522c64a3-818d-4fc8-bea7-4e2a2a8f9f43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: MRK 10:31
Text: But many that are first shall be last; and the last first.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:553ed62f-aa14-4667-befe-53ddc3d87778>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: MRK 10:32
Text: And they were in the way going up to Jerusalem; and Jesus went before them: and they were amazed; and as they followed, they were afraid. And he took again the twelve, and began to tell them what things should happen unto him,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08e37e42-4dbb-48d8-be62-9eff09ce3615>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: MRK 10:33
Text: Saying, Behold, we go up to Jerusalem; and the Son of man shall be delivered unto the chief priests, and unto the scribes; and they shall condemn him to death, and shall deliver him to the Gentiles:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d88d46ea-2b64-4b86-b3cf-85acca9a82c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: MRK 10:34
Text: And they shall mock him, and shall scourge him, and shall spit upon him, and shall kill him: and the third day he shall rise again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b3334d0-cff5-4be2-b76f-560c4a7ccaea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: MRK 10:35
Text: And James and John, the sons of Zebedee, come unto him, saying, Master, we would that thou shouldest do for us whatsoever we shall desire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35ad8c79-3a0b-4368-9b28-91d9863ea29c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: MRK 10:36
Text: And he said unto them, What would ye that I should do for you?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7cf7d683-80fc-417b-8f33-468f78b1454f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: MRK 10:37
Text: They said unto him, Grant unto us that we may sit, one on thy right hand, and the other on thy left hand, in thy glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fcc96ea3-6519-488a-b39b-fb6882d25f80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: MRK 10:38
Text: But Jesus said unto them, Ye know not what ye ask: can ye drink of the cup that I drink of? and be baptized with the baptism that I am baptized with?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea7b8d4e-67b0-4f9e-99bc-87267e5d946b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: MRK 10:39
Text: And they said unto him, We can. And Jesus said unto them, Ye shall indeed drink of the cup that I drink of; and with the baptism that I am baptized withal shall ye be baptized:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e191e13-61ba-4036-9ec0-f8bb627f03f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MRK 10:40
Text: But to sit on my right hand and on my left hand is not mine to give; but it shall be given to them for whom it is prepared.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ee2fd08-d924-4e77-984d-8dad896423c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: MRK 10:41
Text: And when the ten heard it, they began to be much displeased with James and John.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3e2002b-c6c5-42b6-9a1d-0c37dc8a3118>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: MRK 10:42
Text: But Jesus called them to him, and saith unto them, Ye know that they which are accounted to rule over the Gentiles exercise lordship over them; and their great ones exercise authority upon them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2211fba-d590-42a6-b656-21007968a488>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: MRK 10:43
Text: But so shall it not be among you: but whosoever will be great among you, shall be your minister:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edbd4d97-f88c-406c-898d-e361c6c3d48b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: MRK 10:44
Text: And whosoever of you will be the chiefest, shall be servant of all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7233fb24-f1d6-4c81-a45b-c4ac89312968>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: MRK 10:45
Text: For even the Son of man came not to be ministered unto, but to minister, and to give his life a ransom for many.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8269fb2-3f84-4031-bf10-238ab6f9030a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: MRK 10:46
Text: And they came to Jericho: and as he went out of Jericho with his disciples and a great number of people, blind Bartimaeus, the son of Timaeus, sat by the highway side begging.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02bb2da4-7923-4d91-b3e9-cc5d390e6f7a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: MRK 10:47
Text: And when he heard that it was Jesus of Nazareth, he began to cry out, and say, Jesus, thou son of David, have mercy on me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b038bba-e350-4772-b6e2-b0e297a6ca84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: MRK 10:48
Text: And many charged him that he should hold his peace: but he cried the more a great deal, Thou son of David, have mercy on me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4fdf916-8f82-458d-b605-76bb30676dac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: MRK 10:49
Text: And Jesus stood still, and commanded him to be called. And they call the blind man, saying unto him, Be of good comfort, rise; he calleth thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2a4ee9e-d666-40e9-8dde-a4033b614102>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: MRK 10:50
Text: And he, casting away his garment, rose, and came to Jesus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7902fc4-d7bc-4f8f-926f-70c3dca03969>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: MRK 10:51
Text: And Jesus answered and said unto him, What wilt thou that I should do unto thee? The blind man said unto him, Lord, that I might receive my sight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/10/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39739943-8c6a-4832-a48a-87d6ab53cf40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: MRK 10:52
Text: And Jesus said unto him, Go thy way; thy faith hath made thee whole. And immediately he received his sight, and followed Jesus in the way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69ca7a24-3334-4ce0-8b25-57a6d866dad7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: MRK 11:1
Text: And when they came nigh to Jerusalem, unto Bethphage and Bethany, at the mount of Olives, he sendeth forth two of his disciples,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2324d55-1cd0-4e79-a132-620168a3d952>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: MRK 11:2
Text: And saith unto them, Go your way into the village over against you: and as soon as ye be entered into it, ye shall find a colt tied, whereon never man sat; loose him, and bring him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ad4176e-2f4b-44e9-ba22-362de3948cec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MRK 11:3
Text: And if any man say unto you, Why do ye this? say ye that the Lord hath need of him; and straightway he will send him hither.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7cc329f4-2329-4fa8-bc35-ec9a41e91a67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: MRK 11:4
Text: And they went their way, and found the colt tied by the door without in a place where two ways met; and they loose him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a2bb846-1352-4fdc-a560-5d5a248970a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: MRK 11:5
Text: And certain of them that stood there said unto them, What do ye, loosing the colt?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ac20167-1172-46d8-a04d-ce3d02ca206a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: MRK 11:6
Text: And they said unto them even as Jesus had commanded: and they let them go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da053071-2b4d-4349-9e34-b6fd7456e2b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: MRK 11:7
Text: And they brought the colt to Jesus, and cast their garments on him; and he sat upon him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5eb16414-bc7a-487d-b8f1-f9c2533834d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: MRK 11:8
Text: And many spread their garments in the way: and others cut down branches off the trees, and strawed them in the way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5701dfe9-0c5e-4e07-8ab7-e262c2997b74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: MRK 11:9
Text: And they that went before, and they that followed, cried, saying, Hosanna; Blessed is he that cometh in the name of the Lord:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50e3a381-7966-49ec-bdb6-d1fc9981f28c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: MRK 11:10
Text: Blessed be the kingdom of our father David, that cometh in the name of the Lord: Hosanna in the highest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:efc67960-e9c9-4872-8098-dcd8fccf79f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: MRK 11:11
Text: And Jesus entered into Jerusalem, and into the temple: and when he had looked round about upon all things, and now the eventide was come, he went out unto Bethany with the twelve.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:941d542a-ae54-4c1f-89bc-4e6984dd3db0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: MRK 11:12
Text: And on the morrow, when they were come from Bethany, he was hungry:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb2f34ac-c236-4d90-a8be-56ee5cd4b7d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: MRK 11:13
Text: And seeing a fig tree afar off having leaves, he came, if haply he might find any thing thereon: and when he came to it, he found nothing but leaves; for the time of figs was not yet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36bbabd6-5ced-48d4-a40e-199a8c59e875>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: MRK 11:14
Text: And Jesus answered and said unto it, No man eat fruit of thee hereafter for ever. And his disciples heard it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6eec1864-b899-4d3d-a877-725277bd37df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: MRK 11:15
Text: And they come to Jerusalem: and Jesus went into the temple, and began to cast out them that sold and bought in the temple, and overthrew the tables of the moneychangers, and the seats of them that sold doves;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a374219-4104-4a9c-ba32-733bdccc2012>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: MRK 11:16
Text: And would not suffer that any man should carry any vessel through the temple.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be5ff2a8-708b-403e-9782-15aeb4227d56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: MRK 11:17
Text: And he taught, saying unto them, Is it not written, My house shall be called of all nations the house of prayer? but ye have made it a den of thieves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:096204a4-c8a4-4b35-b92c-8bdf9465aca6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: MRK 11:18
Text: And the scribes and chief priests heard it, and sought how they might destroy him: for they feared him, because all the people was astonished at his doctrine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80163d83-4022-47fa-a27f-7e5c1b409094>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: MRK 11:19
Text: And when even was come, he went out of the city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e1c7840-ef7d-4fa6-99c6-265f20c2106f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: MRK 11:20
Text: And in the morning, as they passed by, they saw the fig tree dried up from the roots.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0682d8f-5546-4b9f-af2f-5b97e2f2fa58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: MRK 11:21
Text: And Peter calling to remembrance saith unto him, Master, behold, the fig tree which thou cursedst is withered away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b1ca9ee-7607-4e76-a7dc-6856a5c65388>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: MRK 11:22
Text: And Jesus answering saith unto them, Have faith in God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8bf89136-06ef-44c8-b573-d2bab1a28f61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 287

Reference: MRK 11:23
Text: For verily I say unto you, That whosoever shall say unto this mountain, Be thou removed, and be thou cast into the sea; and shall not doubt in his heart, but shall believe that those things which he saith shall come to pass; he shall have whatsoever he saith.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5372bf65-17ae-498c-906d-5fe4aa7a959e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MRK 11:24
Text: Therefore I say unto you, What things soever ye desire, when ye pray, believe that ye receive them, and ye shall have them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce8d6869-5f98-4dae-941d-fde9523de880>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: MRK 11:25
Text: And when ye stand praying, forgive, if ye have ought against any: that your Father also which is in heaven may forgive you your trespasses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7d1961a-b1ab-4521-879a-78ea7b4a11c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MRK 11:26
Text: But if ye do not forgive, neither will your Father which is in heaven forgive your trespasses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e53a1efb-6825-437d-a4e5-b9a7522d9545>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: MRK 11:27
Text: And they come again to Jerusalem: and as he was walking in the temple, there come to him the chief priests, and the scribes, and the elders,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0eeb1e4-0d96-45ce-9df7-a41218959463>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: MRK 11:28
Text: And say unto him, By what authority doest thou these things? and who gave thee this authority to do these things?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a6e8322-bc48-4f61-936d-5fac84d766e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: MRK 11:29
Text: And Jesus answered and said unto them, I will also ask of you one question, and answer me, and I will tell you by what authority I do these things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bcd3f9cc-c498-487e-8c25-90f3c7831eed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: MRK 11:30
Text: The baptism of John, was it from heaven, or of men? answer me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bbdcd846-18c6-4989-876d-aefdb7821301>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: MRK 11:31
Text: And they reasoned with themselves, saying, If we shall say, From heaven; he will say, Why then did ye not believe him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac101c13-31aa-417a-bb83-00f67afa275d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: MRK 11:32
Text: But if we shall say, Of men; they feared the people: for all men counted John, that he was a prophet indeed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/11/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20866088-4255-419c-ae08-3a9904ea6501>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: MRK 11:33
Text: And they answered and said unto Jesus, We cannot tell. And Jesus answering saith unto them, Neither do I tell you by what authority I do these things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:552a9495-5682-40f6-b132-d738cb722723>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: MRK 12:1
Text: And he began to speak unto them by parables. A certain man planted a vineyard, and set an hedge about it, and digged a place for the winefat, and built a tower, and let it out to husbandmen, and went into a far country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aed109fc-ce13-475d-8ca2-8f509737d1c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: MRK 12:2
Text: And at the season he sent to the husbandmen a servant, that he might receive from the husbandmen of the fruit of the vineyard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:471e0c52-9ea1-455b-95e8-465ea7dee1cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: MRK 12:3
Text: And they caught him, and beat him, and sent him away empty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96ffee74-2fc5-48f2-94fb-c9f53399ca82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: MRK 12:4
Text: And again he sent unto them another servant; and at him they cast stones, and wounded him in the head, and sent him away shamefully handled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df108633-f479-4b6f-9689-88a0947679d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: MRK 12:5
Text: And again he sent another; and him they killed, and many others; beating some, and killing some.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4529943-475a-45d7-a896-3152bc444187>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: MRK 12:6
Text: Having yet therefore one son, his wellbeloved, he sent him also last unto them, saying, They will reverence my son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f970c80-8494-46aa-bead-81e86225efda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: MRK 12:7
Text: But those husbandmen said among themselves, This is the heir; come, let us kill him, and the inheritance shall be ours.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40bba3fa-bd69-4c8a-9388-c2f7697d32fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: MRK 12:8
Text: And they took him, and killed him, and cast him out of the vineyard.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71d09171-b477-4022-b9f3-f5aa8f66059c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: MRK 12:9
Text: What shall therefore the lord of the vineyard do? he will come and destroy the husbandmen, and will give the vineyard unto others.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d51d833-7514-41df-9c56-57287719320d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: MRK 12:10
Text: And have ye not read this scripture; The stone which the builders rejected is become the head of the corner:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0f7a565-8dec-42ba-a91d-8a10ae31955a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: MRK 12:11
Text: This was the Lord’s doing, and it is marvellous in our eyes?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bccaec27-63d4-412c-bea3-e5271447e70b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: MRK 12:12
Text: And they sought to lay hold on him, but feared the people: for they knew that he had spoken the parable against them: and they left him, and went their way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae928e61-ea33-4425-937f-b504abc83dd0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: MRK 12:13
Text: And they send unto him certain of the Pharisees and of the Herodians, to catch him in his words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:074d433a-cb1e-4f18-bf26-fc5285d483a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: MRK 12:14
Text: And when they were come, they say unto him, Master, we know that thou art true, and carest for no man: for thou regardest not the person of men, but teachest the way of God in truth: Is it lawful to give tribute to Caesar, or not?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d02ba17f-517f-4506-a0cd-3b8b1266f8dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: MRK 12:15
Text: Shall we give, or shall we not give? But he, knowing their hypocrisy, said unto them, Why tempt ye me? bring me a penny, that I may see it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0aa90d6-535b-4f82-b6ce-b7f9eaff5bc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: MRK 12:16
Text: And they brought it. And he saith unto them, Whose is this image and superscription? And they said unto him, Caesar’s.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:492b109b-9ef8-4630-84c2-213fb1c1af85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: MRK 12:17
Text: And Jesus answering said unto them, Render to Caesar the things that are Caesar’s, and to God the things that are God’s. And they marvelled at him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b7bc88d-4b64-40c0-a115-1fcf44f06c24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: MRK 12:18
Text: Then come unto him the Sadducees, which say there is no resurrection; and they asked him, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b128688e-ed18-4d1e-a411-d11687ce37f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: MRK 12:19
Text: Master, Moses wrote unto us, If a man’s brother die, and leave his wife behind him, and leave no children, that his brother should take his wife, and raise up seed unto his brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90a13498-2b9a-478b-adfd-c4e52bee0eb1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: MRK 12:20
Text: Now there were seven brethren: and the first took a wife, and dying left no seed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b751851-71c4-4b1d-b6a3-6dc631318e28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: MRK 12:21
Text: And the second took her, and died, neither left he any seed: and the third likewise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba43d5bc-531e-40ff-b80f-d126754a18b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: MRK 12:22
Text: And the seven had her, and left no seed: last of all the woman died also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bcf54427-209e-4e7f-a0d4-199af2667fcd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: MRK 12:23
Text: In the resurrection therefore, when they shall rise, whose wife shall she be of them? for the seven had her to wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:734c3341-b336-4606-9f40-b4a4bce70dc2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: MRK 12:24
Text: And Jesus answering said unto them, Do ye not therefore err, because ye know not the scriptures, neither the power of God?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e0b858d-8119-4202-96ae-23dcfa5e9012>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: MRK 12:25
Text: For when they shall rise from the dead, they neither marry, nor are given in marriage; but are as the angels which are in heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71192e02-7b36-4961-8274-99b995190998>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: MRK 12:26
Text: And as touching the dead, that they rise: have ye not read in the book of Moses, how in the bush God spake unto him, saying, I am the God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be59f620-35a5-4198-95f0-2664f336432f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MRK 12:27
Text: He is not the God of the dead, but the God of the living: ye therefore do greatly err.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65b8a543-c06a-42ee-83c4-ab9c13f03231>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: MRK 12:28
Text: And one of the scribes came, and having heard them reasoning together, and perceiving that he had answered them well, asked him, Which is the first commandment of all?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e0a13f5-0c8d-4290-8412-b295bdc809c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: MRK 12:29
Text: And Jesus answered him, The first of all the commandments is, Hear, O Israel; The Lord our God is one Lord:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d77aec55-b237-47ca-9136-249772b248f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: MRK 12:30
Text: And thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind, and with all thy strength: this is the first commandment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8e87969-07fe-4694-817d-744b793087fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: MRK 12:31
Text: And the second is like, namely this, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself. There is none other commandment greater than these.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29141af4-18d4-45ac-8ee5-6fe8fe9c3d8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MRK 12:32
Text: And the scribe said unto him, Well, Master, thou hast said the truth: for there is one God; and there is none other but he:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6512d7cc-5645-4b0c-a988-0b85e8677c1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: MRK 12:33
Text: And to love him with all the heart, and with all the understanding, and with all the soul, and with all the strength, and to love his neighbour as himself, is more than all whole burnt offerings and sacrifices.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:357f3c3f-2674-4559-b028-0cb89543da0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: MRK 12:34
Text: And when Jesus saw that he answered discreetly, he said unto him, Thou art not far from the kingdom of God. And no man after that durst ask him any question.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ef3e90d-d7c2-440e-b662-d9f8fd757c3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: MRK 12:35
Text: And Jesus answered and said, while he taught in the temple, How say the scribes that Christ is the son of David?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65742b34-3910-4254-823c-3e819bb93634>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: MRK 12:36
Text: For David himself said by the Holy Ghost, The LORD said to my Lord, Sit thou on my right hand, till I make thine enemies thy footstool.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1ff45f3-dfee-40ca-9845-9acb6e268a8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: MRK 12:37
Text: David therefore himself calleth him Lord; and whence is he then his son? And the common people heard him gladly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3cff740-b892-4476-943b-d5c7693916c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: MRK 12:38
Text: And he said unto them in his doctrine, Beware of the scribes, which love to go in long clothing, and love salutations in the marketplaces,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10ed7bcb-f879-40c1-9c96-09c3343d1051>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: MRK 12:39
Text: And the chief seats in the synagogues, and the uppermost rooms at feasts:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d481cd7-4d30-4701-9949-ecab5c11f05d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: MRK 12:40
Text: Which devour widows’ houses, and for a pretence make long prayers: these shall receive greater damnation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10a90ee1-9df4-44a6-a8e8-f2d974eeaa2d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: MRK 12:41
Text: And Jesus sat over against the treasury, and beheld how the people cast money into the treasury: and many that were rich cast in much.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82872044-168c-417a-97d0-80c4990df728>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: MRK 12:42
Text: And there came a certain poor widow, and she threw in two mites, which make a farthing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d5e5400-47e3-4106-b538-2f7f0b6d7363>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: MRK 12:43
Text: And he called unto him his disciples, and saith unto them, Verily I say unto you, That this poor widow hath cast more in, than all they which have cast into the treasury:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/12/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4af0159-d8c7-484f-8f59-d9ff80a1a656>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: MRK 12:44
Text: For all they did cast in of their abundance; but she of her want did cast in all that she had, even all her living.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d17f4033-d356-4f2b-a7b2-3f5436eec1bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: MRK 13:1
Text: And as he went out of the temple, one of his disciples saith unto him, Master, see what manner of stones and what buildings are here!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb0bbc8d-923a-44fd-bd70-3a3d86186222>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: MRK 13:2
Text: And Jesus answering said unto him, Seest thou these great buildings? there shall not be left one stone upon another, that shall not be thrown down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6205782-ddf6-48f0-81bd-4c06e808e8d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: MRK 13:3
Text: And as he sat upon the mount of Olives over against the temple, Peter and James and John and Andrew asked him privately,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b49754ae-1513-4794-9dd6-3f35628fae69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: MRK 13:4
Text: Tell us, when shall these things be? and what shall be the sign when all these things shall be fulfilled?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b0148e1-e98d-4bc2-b4e4-d4613cf549c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: MRK 13:5
Text: And Jesus answering them began to say, Take heed lest any man deceive you:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c97a3af9-d8b6-4291-b838-fceae3a3b32c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: MRK 13:6
Text: For many shall come in my name, saying, I am Christ; and shall deceive many.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec7b3373-3f0e-483e-846b-57d8ab2bc387>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: MRK 13:7
Text: And when ye shall hear of wars and rumours of wars, be ye not troubled: for such things must needs be; but the end shall not be yet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddafea09-bad2-4988-94ee-27951ff73567>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: MRK 13:8
Text: For nation shall rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom: and there shall be earthquakes in divers places, and there shall be famines and troubles: these are the beginnings of sorrows.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7f1c5d3-fdcc-4ef0-8409-09c70fd13847>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: MRK 13:9
Text: But take heed to yourselves: for they shall deliver you up to councils; and in the synagogues ye shall be beaten: and ye shall be brought before rulers and kings for my sake, for a testimony against them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:681bbc37-8364-437b-b8d6-ccfda2080cd5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: MRK 13:10
Text: And the gospel must first be published among all nations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c68578d9-201d-438c-8cbc-8bb708a9c28c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: MRK 13:11
Text: But when they shall lead you, and deliver you up, take no thought beforehand what ye shall speak, neither do ye premeditate: but whatsoever shall be given you in that hour, that speak ye: for it is not ye that speak, but the Holy Ghost.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1433ae0e-e2fe-4ce0-aee1-f933d106c6d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: MRK 13:12
Text: Now the brother shall betray the brother to death, and the father the son; and children shall rise up against their parents, and shall cause them to be put to death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66caa8ff-93a6-427b-8299-8d1b133bb4de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: MRK 13:13
Text: And ye shall be hated of all men for my name’s sake: but he that shall endure unto the end, the same shall be saved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d717027e-47dd-446b-8c7b-dec00630d051>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: MRK 13:14
Text: But when ye shall see the abomination of desolation, spoken of by Daniel the prophet, standing where it ought not, (let him that readeth understand,) then let them that be in Judaea flee to the mountains:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7db8b124-3423-4ead-aa29-8040d4bbd3d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: MRK 13:15
Text: And let him that is on the housetop not go down into the house, neither enter therein, to take any thing out of his house:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0cc4ecd6-8d74-475f-b0aa-51a136f38658>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: MRK 13:16
Text: And let him that is in the field not turn back again for to take up his garment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc1a833a-fe7b-4c28-af77-e84141609960>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: MRK 13:17
Text: But woe to them that are with child, and to them that give suck in those days!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d45ebceb-423b-42f3-a4ae-b300defba324>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: MRK 13:18
Text: And pray ye that your flight be not in the winter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee4d5e0e-e470-4c3c-9422-4283328ff0ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: MRK 13:19
Text: For in those days shall be affliction, such as was not from the beginning of the creation which God created unto this time, neither shall be.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff08076e-b2e9-4375-bcd4-cce9f197c5f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: MRK 13:20
Text: And except that the Lord had shortened those days, no flesh should be saved: but for the elect’s sake, whom he hath chosen, he hath shortened the days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e1c51a2-5a61-4d4a-9d60-907a5da6b454>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: MRK 13:21
Text: And then if any man shall say to you, Lo, here is Christ; or, lo, he is there; believe him not:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8514a141-8e1e-4b97-bd53-ee00b7be7589>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: MRK 13:22
Text: For false Christs and false prophets shall rise, and shall shew signs and wonders, to seduce, if it were possible, even the elect.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc977ae5-5ddc-4763-a911-cd58f6c67386>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: MRK 13:23
Text: But take ye heed: behold, I have foretold you all things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b4f948a-ee1a-4c0e-934a-f99624e120a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: MRK 13:24
Text: But in those days, after that tribulation, the sun shall be darkened, and the moon shall not give her light,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a003d79e-145e-4212-ae15-40cb2d554558>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MRK 13:25
Text: And the stars of heaven shall fall, and the powers that are in heaven shall be shaken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a6a4d8b-35f7-4e0e-bef2-def7af9a0c0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: MRK 13:26
Text: And then shall they see the Son of man coming in the clouds with great power and glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:daa5acbb-695d-4e8b-b2f5-e41bb3f92943>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: MRK 13:27
Text: And then shall he send his angels, and shall gather together his elect from the four winds, from the uttermost part of the earth to the uttermost part of heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b4644bd-137b-461e-afe3-82064f02510a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: MRK 13:28
Text: Now learn a parable of the fig tree; When her branch is yet tender, and putteth forth leaves, ye know that summer is near:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1a29c80-ab35-465c-809e-a673d2fda9ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: MRK 13:29
Text: So ye in like manner, when ye shall see these things come to pass, know that it is nigh, even at the doors.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e53e09e-81cb-4106-85c2-19a23a85f616>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: MRK 13:30
Text: Verily I say unto you, that this generation shall not pass, till all these things be done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2126a0fb-ba53-44ce-843c-bf59082b93a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: MRK 13:31
Text: Heaven and earth shall pass away: but my words shall not pass away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23f0f629-0f98-4cd3-bd76-cd9f3efd1e5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: MRK 13:32
Text: But of that day and that hour knoweth no man, no, not the angels which are in heaven, neither the Son, but the Father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f24e3c24-1691-4454-8057-579c9d8aed1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: MRK 13:33
Text: Take ye heed, watch and pray: for ye know not when the time is.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62fc514e-6ef2-4148-bcef-01557b806333>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: MRK 13:34
Text: For the Son of Man is as a man taking a far journey, who left his house, and gave authority to his servants, and to every man his work, and commanded the porter to watch.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1b99772-86b3-4f2b-b08e-8d62f3895149>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: MRK 13:35
Text: Watch ye therefore: for ye know not when the master of the house cometh, at even, or at midnight, or at the cockcrowing, or in the morning:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d901bd42-d506-4093-884d-3805eda0354b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 70

Reference: MRK 13:36
Text: Lest coming suddenly he find you sleeping.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/13/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3105cba-6836-43c0-9c43-e180862cd951>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: MRK 13:37
Text: And what I say unto you I say unto all, Watch.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2a46f37-9a56-495c-a0a3-08da2086e797>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: MRK 14:1
Text: After two days was the feast of the passover, and of unleavened bread: and the chief priests and the scribes sought how they might take him by craft, and put him to death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0508a72-aa60-4197-9be4-a3ab0fbe560d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: MRK 14:2
Text: But they said, Not on the feast day, lest there be an uproar of the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2726fe0d-2410-4ab2-b691-a94bfe61af83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: MRK 14:3
Text: And being in Bethany in the house of Simon the leper, as he sat at meat, there came a woman having an alabaster box of ointment of spikenard very precious; and she brake the box, and poured it on his head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28f44d00-e2e4-41a7-a764-40bd35b29721>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: MRK 14:4
Text: And there were some that had indignation within themselves, and said, Why was this waste of the ointment made?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34f443f5-e40f-4f76-ae36-8ae249873968>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: MRK 14:5
Text: For it might have been sold for more than three hundred pence, and have been given to the poor. And they murmured against her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a34e2cb2-1cc8-4415-a1a2-a2f1d39a1174>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: MRK 14:6
Text: And Jesus said, Let her alone; why trouble ye her? she hath wrought a good work on me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fc76c06-e83c-4fa5-9e9d-bb07b3fe29eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: MRK 14:7
Text: For ye have the poor with you always, and whensoever ye will ye may do them good: but me ye have not always.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a2a52a8-282c-4200-bdfd-ef75db89bcc3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: MRK 14:8
Text: She hath done what she could: she is come aforehand to anoint my body to the burying.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32ef31dc-60f8-4b8d-9f78-bc0b9d0fe10e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: MRK 14:9
Text: Verily I say unto you, Wheresoever this gospel shall be preached throughout the whole world, this also that she hath done shall be spoken of for a memorial of her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b52e1cd-b252-4447-b886-6da5269e2199>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: MRK 14:10
Text: And Judas Iscariot, one of the twelve, went unto the chief priests, to betray him unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:204c6dd0-38c7-49e6-84ab-177be910a2aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MRK 14:11
Text: And when they heard it, they were glad, and promised to give him money. And he sought how he might conveniently betray him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bb639a9-3809-4643-ba6a-a412b83a924b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: MRK 14:12
Text: And the first day of unleavened bread, when they killed the passover, his disciples said unto him, Where wilt thou that we go and prepare that thou mayest eat the passover?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d05af5b9-3d93-486a-a4e1-909751f31597>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: MRK 14:13
Text: And he sendeth forth two of his disciples, and saith unto them, Go ye into the city, and there shall meet you a man bearing a pitcher of water: follow him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d8294db-e732-4cb0-98de-9d367cfbe2b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: MRK 14:14
Text: And wheresoever he shall go in, say ye to the goodman of the house, The Master saith, Where is the guestchamber, where I shall eat the passover with my disciples?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca1b0b80-f7f2-4e90-875b-7fc1fc8b585e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: MRK 14:15
Text: And he will shew you a large upper room furnished and prepared: there make ready for us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:210f0396-f21e-417d-8085-bc9d94c476c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MRK 14:16
Text: And his disciples went forth, and came into the city, and found as he had said unto them: and they made ready the passover.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92d81f8a-3f24-4719-883c-16c151716b97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: MRK 14:17
Text: And in the evening he cometh with the twelve.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f13d9035-807f-4f67-8d79-d92bb95c0f5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: MRK 14:18
Text: And as they sat and did eat, Jesus said, Verily I say unto you, One of you which eateth with me shall betray me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b966eff-70d6-496a-8395-dba7ff92ea39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: MRK 14:19
Text: And they began to be sorrowful, and to say unto him one by one, Is it I? and another said, Is it I?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a8549af-f46a-437d-a44c-e5b0e1f9a8da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MRK 14:20
Text: And he answered and said unto them, It is one of the twelve, that dippeth with me in the dish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ccd06095-a889-4ed6-a1ba-08be0232f7a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: MRK 14:21
Text: The Son of man indeed goeth, as it is written of him: but woe to that man by whom the Son of man is betrayed! good were it for that man if he had never been born.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf5f6df8-4f70-458e-a829-0da32d0f9377>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: MRK 14:22
Text: And as they did eat, Jesus took bread, and blessed, and brake it, and gave to them, and said, Take, eat: this is my body.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d81e54c7-49e0-4f09-9c43-372a940906a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: MRK 14:23
Text: And he took the cup, and when he had given thanks, he gave it to them: and they all drank of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b17621d-3dda-4152-963f-45b6f7a0f0d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: MRK 14:24
Text: And he said unto them, This is my blood of the new testament, which is shed for many.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89d2db8a-0421-4102-8d04-6a57de37472d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: MRK 14:25
Text: Verily I say unto you, I will drink no more of the fruit of the vine, until that day that I drink it new in the kingdom of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44906fb6-efdb-4de2-a554-5c3ce66c4e91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: MRK 14:26
Text: And when they had sung an hymn, they went out into the mount of Olives.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1da846cc-4f06-4d93-a669-d83e39507027>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: MRK 14:27
Text: And Jesus saith unto them, All ye shall be offended because of me this night: for it is written, I will smite the shepherd, and the sheep shall be scattered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0f01d12-049e-4809-ad7e-997d71a25d9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: MRK 14:28
Text: But after that I am risen, I will go before you into Galilee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9dd31a50-e545-4588-9daf-ab65b247b556>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: MRK 14:29
Text: But Peter said unto him, Although all shall be offended, yet will not I.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c9773be-9b56-4b5a-a502-6fbc9825761f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: MRK 14:30
Text: And Jesus saith unto him, Verily I say unto thee, That this day, even in this night, before the cock crow twice, thou shalt deny me thrice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6683211-5a73-4a84-a003-7d939dbb38b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MRK 14:31
Text: But he spake the more vehemently, If I should die with thee, I will not deny thee in any wise. Likewise also said they all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80dac819-2039-4542-a222-8b425e8cd6c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: MRK 14:32
Text: And they came to a place which was named Gethsemane: and he saith to his disciples, Sit ye here, while I shall pray.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed3b29f3-4b92-4aef-b407-a3b6f6930e0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: MRK 14:33
Text: And he taketh with him Peter and James and John, and began to be sore amazed, and to be very heavy;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed1d835c-5211-487c-98a1-a04d0c0d6831>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MRK 14:34
Text: And saith unto them, My soul is exceeding sorrowful unto death: tarry ye here, and watch.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f49d13d4-9719-4bc0-af64-1ce23ba8a558>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: MRK 14:35
Text: And he went forward a little, and fell on the ground, and prayed that, if it were possible, the hour might pass from him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50426b0e-df34-47b3-a20a-182966dd4ee2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: MRK 14:36
Text: And he said, Abba, Father, all things are possible unto thee; take away this cup from me: nevertheless not what I will, but what thou wilt.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac1a20d8-fced-4ee8-9da3-86dd51df3eac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: MRK 14:37
Text: And he cometh, and findeth them sleeping, and saith unto Peter, Simon, sleepest thou? couldest not thou watch one hour?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bdce8b94-9db3-4901-b209-5cb8699acb55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: MRK 14:38
Text: Watch ye and pray, lest ye enter into temptation. The spirit truly is ready, but the flesh is weak.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d94b06c-a3a1-4870-81f5-80454fc7083b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: MRK 14:39
Text: And again he went away, and prayed, and spake the same words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05c3bbac-010e-4377-9c4a-d6cb4eb92307>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: MRK 14:40
Text: And when he returned, he found them asleep again, (for their eyes were heavy,) neither wist they what to answer him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a9bdebb-6e5c-4040-b366-4af948ae58e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: MRK 14:41
Text: And he cometh the third time, and saith unto them, Sleep on now, and take your rest: it is enough, the hour is come; behold, the Son of man is betrayed into the hands of sinners.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:816c73d2-9ea4-40bf-a911-d557649af603>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: MRK 14:42
Text: Rise up, let us go; lo, he that betrayeth me is at hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9758b22-2337-458f-b3ea-b3535b34c673>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: MRK 14:43
Text: And immediately, while he yet spake, cometh Judas, one of the twelve, and with him a great multitude with swords and staves, from the chief priests and the scribes and the elders.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b140575d-7024-4dcd-907f-b135cece99b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: MRK 14:44
Text: And he that betrayed him had given them a token, saying, Whomsoever I shall kiss, that same is he; take him, and lead him away safely.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba0ab404-f8c8-4e39-9591-fdd76a470ea8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: MRK 14:45
Text: And as soon as he was come, he goeth straightway to him, and saith, Master, master; and kissed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bbe2192-d2d9-46b8-af80-6858f39777a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: MRK 14:46
Text: And they laid their hands on him, and took him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0eb34b82-dec0-4bf9-bd24-45057ac6e24a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: MRK 14:47
Text: And one of them that stood by drew a sword, and smote a servant of the high priest, and cut off his ear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65b26a96-f428-44d8-83ad-b67742705266>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: MRK 14:48
Text: And Jesus answered and said unto them, Are ye come out, as against a thief, with swords and with staves to take me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a48ff6e1-ae7d-41ab-9220-9d8be22fc6e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: MRK 14:49
Text: I was daily with you in the temple teaching, and ye took me not: but the scriptures must be fulfilled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c8f76a1-596d-44ab-96c6-7f443ab88571>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 63

Reference: MRK 14:50
Text: And they all forsook him, and fled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:467b068c-9109-4432-adf6-a1685a588c0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: MRK 14:51
Text: And there followed him a certain young man, having a linen cloth cast about his naked body; and the young men laid hold on him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8a9e660-22c3-4012-a3c5-f26a688602d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: MRK 14:52
Text: And he left the linen cloth, and fled from them naked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9f0c6d1-6585-49a7-9edd-9bdbd6721ddc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: MRK 14:53
Text: And they led Jesus away to the high priest: and with him were assembled all the chief priests and the elders and the scribes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51658b72-b042-4359-8888-2886d01282dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: MRK 14:54
Text: And Peter followed him afar off, even into the palace of the high priest: and he sat with the servants, and warmed himself at the fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/55
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e404508e-fc4c-4ec4-890a-5cc0085b75b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: MRK 14:55
Text: And the chief priests and all the council sought for witness against Jesus to put him to death; and found none.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/56
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb0e193e-22fc-4a6b-ab1a-244ee7dbc6e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: MRK 14:56
Text: For many bare false witness against him, but their witness agreed not together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/57
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e130ee33-ebd7-4732-8725-73360ddf03fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: MRK 14:57
Text: And there arose certain, and bare false witness against him, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/58
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbded49e-8207-4024-afe1-f6be066071d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: MRK 14:58
Text: We heard him say, I will destroy this temple that is made with hands, and within three days I will build another made without hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/59
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc0ad548-ca66-4acf-8f1a-6fe1e5965cec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: MRK 14:59
Text: But neither so did their witness agree together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/60
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a85920f-41fd-4887-abee-28f8e20d1c08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: MRK 14:60
Text: And the high priest stood up in the midst, and asked Jesus, saying, Answerest thou nothing? what is it which these witness against thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/61
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d7095f3-2a9e-4eda-848a-c4abf66e1a41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: MRK 14:61
Text: But he held his peace, and answered nothing. Again the high priest asked him, and said unto him, Art thou the Christ, the Son of the Blessed?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/62
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c087ec57-2f68-43fc-89b8-a42b6bc582d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: MRK 14:62
Text: And Jesus said, I am: and ye shall see the Son of man sitting on the right hand of power, and coming in the clouds of heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/63
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae43db73-18a8-4a7d-a8e6-3679ec8ef48e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: MRK 14:63
Text: Then the high priest rent his clothes, and saith, What need we any further witnesses?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/64
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f126256f-9a60-424d-a9dd-b478745ae796>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: MRK 14:64
Text: Ye have heard the blasphemy: what think ye? And they all condemned him to be guilty of death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/65
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e939fe4b-3758-415b-adf8-729eb07ee681>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: MRK 14:65
Text: And some began to spit on him, and to cover his face, and to buffet him, and to say unto him, Prophesy: and the servants did strike him with the palms of their hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/66
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b8278e8-1e7a-47b7-840e-b258d1efa1b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MRK 14:66
Text: And as Peter was beneath in the palace, there cometh one of the maids of the high priest:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/67
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a67924b-a8ec-4052-ba6c-8a27e1f584ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: MRK 14:67
Text: And when she saw Peter warming himself, she looked upon him, and said, And thou also wast with Jesus of Nazareth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/68
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd6e6132-e288-4456-813b-01d4f6f8e73c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: MRK 14:68
Text: But he denied, saying, I know not, neither understand I what thou sayest. And he went out into the porch; and the cock crew.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/69
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05b67e65-6eb6-4397-87bb-f2f003298d68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MRK 14:69
Text: And a maid saw him again, and began to say to them that stood by, This is one of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/70
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54255645-601f-4730-b842-98b367a2ee87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: MRK 14:70
Text: And he denied it again. And a little after, they that stood by said again to Peter, Surely thou art one of them: for thou art a Galilaean, and thy speech agreeth thereto.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/71
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a809f751-1851-4294-abd6-d951e936d40e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: MRK 14:71
Text: But he began to curse and to swear, saying, I know not this man of whom ye speak.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/14/72
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:313708f8-bf12-41b3-bc52-48cf5169c73f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: MRK 14:72
Text: And the second time the cock crew. And Peter called to mind the word that Jesus said unto him, Before the cock crow twice, thou shalt deny me thrice. And when he thought thereon, he wept.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b1b4568-d1c7-4d6f-8ba9-516b623ae13b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: MRK 15:1
Text: And straightway in the morning the chief priests held a consultation with the elders and scribes and the whole council, and bound Jesus, and carried him away, and delivered him to Pilate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f935ac90-fb68-439e-b188-944b47a1e612>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: MRK 15:2
Text: And Pilate asked him, Art thou the King of the Jews? And he answering said unto them, Thou sayest it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f7557b1-0030-49be-bb8d-914a96b956ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: MRK 15:3
Text: And the chief priests accused him of many things: but he answered nothing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a249648f-6ec8-46f4-8d05-c234ca5bdf95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: MRK 15:4
Text: And Pilate asked him again, saying, Answerest thou nothing? behold how many things they witness against thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c57fd073-e08e-459d-9fc1-74e01e4b9572>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: MRK 15:5
Text: But Jesus yet answered nothing; so that Pilate marvelled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b07529c-cc8e-452f-83f5-0751149302b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: MRK 15:6
Text: Now at that feast he released unto them one prisoner, whomsoever they desired.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:efdd58ae-1b45-470b-81c0-1be9847b2872>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: MRK 15:7
Text: And there was one named Barabbas, which lay bound with them that had made insurrection with him, who had committed murder in the insurrection.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b152e422-54ab-4bc9-ba9b-9569f2ef0634>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MRK 15:8
Text: And the multitude crying aloud began to desire him to do as he had ever done unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea4911ca-a71c-45e5-93c5-0d6fb1f23236>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: MRK 15:9
Text: But Pilate answered them, saying, Will ye that I release unto you the King of the Jews?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c4dc4a7-b8ff-4d95-9a04-c5b89536827f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: MRK 15:10
Text: For he knew that the chief priests had delivered him for envy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ecfb2323-4451-4cce-a938-91634ac389d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MRK 15:11
Text: But the chief priests moved the people, that he should rather release Barabbas unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83596faf-17f3-4f69-8b86-794223734915>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: MRK 15:12
Text: And Pilate answered and said again unto them, What will ye then that I shall do unto him whom ye call the King of the Jews?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:187fd96f-f4ec-45e4-9c9b-20b45b046110>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 66

Reference: MRK 15:13
Text: And they cried out again, Crucify him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f25b175d-21eb-4023-af5d-7b1d562e7392>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MRK 15:14
Text: Then Pilate said unto them, Why, what evil hath he done? And they cried out the more exceedingly, Crucify him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4683e296-126b-43ef-9290-37679272ed55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: MRK 15:15
Text: And so Pilate, willing to content the people, released Barabbas unto them, and delivered Jesus, when he had scourged him, to be crucified.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83b10323-0637-47c3-ba81-821afc38b282>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: MRK 15:16
Text: And the soldiers led him away into the hall, called Praetorium; and they call together the whole band.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc0cf0f8-99cc-4fd9-9cac-f6373a6d0210>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: MRK 15:17
Text: And they clothed him with purple, and platted a crown of thorns, and put it about his head,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4c097a6-b32b-4a0b-a0f1-f8883e25b309>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: MRK 15:18
Text: And began to salute him, Hail, King of the Jews!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b6c9854-fd55-4088-80f4-c1c493e7388b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: MRK 15:19
Text: And they smote him on the head with a reed, and did spit upon him, and bowing their knees worshipped him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2cc106ae-5476-4875-a725-df4a01e2403f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: MRK 15:20
Text: And when they had mocked him, they took off the purple from him, and put his own clothes on him, and led him out to crucify him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6de2358-6dfe-4e5f-aa28-fbccc2f25c54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: MRK 15:21
Text: And they compel one Simon a Cyrenian, who passed by, coming out of the country, the father of Alexander and Rufus, to bear his cross.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81ff5538-ec8d-4a71-9745-6ba7d54ce24a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MRK 15:22
Text: And they bring him unto the place Golgotha, which is, being interpreted, The place of a skull.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f75cc306-8d6b-457d-8150-e3fbf5ae3dd8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: MRK 15:23
Text: And they gave him to drink wine mingled with myrrh: but he received it not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d406c53-2e38-4a47-a74d-9cf0337e1395>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MRK 15:24
Text: And when they had crucified him, they parted his garments, casting lots upon them, what every man should take.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1372344a-6ca6-43e6-87c9-81376d8dfb4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: MRK 15:25
Text: And it was the third hour, and they crucified him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0c2e4ed-da5a-40ab-8c46-896ddbab0f80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: MRK 15:26
Text: And the superscription of his accusation was written over, THE KING OF THE JEWS.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82535225-698f-4c06-8762-faa1dbb0631a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: MRK 15:27
Text: And with him they crucify two thieves; the one on his right hand, and the other on his left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f9bdf79-9dfa-4d5f-a883-94432c93e5a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MRK 15:28
Text: And the scripture was fulfilled, which saith, And he was numbered with the transgressors.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ed05ad7-08f0-4f56-9091-ed1e24f00390>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: MRK 15:29
Text: And they that passed by railed on him, wagging their heads, and saying, Ah, thou that destroyest the temple, and buildest it in three days,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6300c55b-ad80-4ef2-8434-2fb65a3f4ca1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 71

Reference: MRK 15:30
Text: Save thyself, and come down from the cross.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:615f140e-6441-485c-b4a9-e3047d9b6975>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: MRK 15:31
Text: Likewise also the chief priests mocking said among themselves with the scribes, He saved others; himself he cannot save.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8eac673f-7b45-4fcb-9a58-18fb6afe9521>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: MRK 15:32
Text: Let Christ the King of Israel descend now from the cross, that we may see and believe. And they that were crucified with him reviled him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a09aa9d-5bf7-40e5-8b93-89eeafff4f97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: MRK 15:33
Text: And when the sixth hour was come, there was darkness over the whole land until the ninth hour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e39410c5-afa0-4a50-90ad-d8f06abd0463>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: MRK 15:34
Text: And at the ninth hour Jesus cried with a loud voice, saying, Eloi, Eloi, lama sabachthani? which is, being interpreted, My God, my God, why hast thou forsaken me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e99780e0-4542-4e60-b2f0-b93000b45510>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: MRK 15:35
Text: And some of them that stood by, when they heard it, said, Behold, he calleth Elias.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3fb9514-78df-4f8b-b762-ee1f4e120a26>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: MRK 15:36
Text: And one ran and filled a spunge full of vinegar, and put it on a reed, and gave him to drink, saying, Let alone; let us see whether Elias will come to take him down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9dc5c35-9d23-4f12-b484-7f5f04ca5a2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: MRK 15:37
Text: And Jesus cried with a loud voice, and gave up the ghost.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42541540-1186-4cc1-bcb9-8117840a0751>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: MRK 15:38
Text: And the veil of the temple was rent in twain from the top to the bottom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0909dc3d-8026-4a73-8ed7-7cb668c1907f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: MRK 15:39
Text: And when the centurion, which stood over against him, saw that he so cried out, and gave up the ghost, he said, Truly this man was the Son of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4354e8f3-1561-4fb0-993a-5f129aefc64a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: MRK 15:40
Text: There were also women looking on afar off: among whom was Mary Magdalene, and Mary the mother of James the less and of Joses, and Salome;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7e1027f-58ba-4d9e-b230-b9f78deeae37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: MRK 15:41
Text: (Who also, when he was in Galilee, followed him, and ministered unto him;) and many other women which came up with him unto Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9681b75c-0f6b-4431-a908-08eac51050ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: MRK 15:42
Text: And now when the even was come, because it was the preparation, that is, the day before the sabbath,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2dcced3a-5484-40bc-80a4-389b9c0c290b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: MRK 15:43
Text: Joseph of Arimathaea, an honourable counsellor, which also waited for the kingdom of God, came, and went in boldly unto Pilate, and craved the body of Jesus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36daf860-67d8-4896-8e8a-158814eba216>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: MRK 15:44
Text: And Pilate marvelled if he were already dead: and calling unto him the centurion, he asked him whether he had been any while dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c538fb2-d6ef-402f-8064-89a9d26cbafd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: MRK 15:45
Text: And when he knew it of the centurion, he gave the body to Joseph.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a51bd697-464a-4442-b60b-3634ce2aaa5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: MRK 15:46
Text: And he bought fine linen, and took him down, and wrapped him in the linen, and laid him in a sepulchre which was hewn out of a rock, and rolled a stone unto the door of the sepulchre.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/15/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c02c98d-ad3b-4609-88b1-76eb6d8c7cb8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: MRK 15:47
Text: And Mary Magdalene and Mary the mother of Joses beheld where he was laid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/16/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ce30975-6e5e-45d8-9788-7f381c45a1cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: MRK 16:1
Text: And when the sabbath was past, Mary Magdalene, and Mary the mother of James, and Salome, had bought sweet spices, that they might come and anoint him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/16/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36266492-d007-4246-be36-1af83d4fe4a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MRK 16:2
Text: And very early in the morning the first day of the week, they came unto the sepulchre at the rising of the sun.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/16/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f179b7c6-3296-46d5-af74-8637589fe010>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: MRK 16:3
Text: And they said among themselves, Who shall roll us away the stone from the door of the sepulchre?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/16/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa7314b0-1a16-496e-b4bb-b56ccfda0ba5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: MRK 16:4
Text: And when they looked, they saw that the stone was rolled away: for it was very great.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/16/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a757e666-a15f-4d3b-af50-7619e219690c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: MRK 16:5
Text: And entering into the sepulchre, they saw a young man sitting on the right side, clothed in a long white garment; and they were affrighted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/16/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ccff3f6-c143-421b-ab0f-033add8f688a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: MRK 16:6
Text: And he saith unto them, Be not affrighted: Ye seek Jesus of Nazareth, which was crucified: he is risen; he is not here: behold the place where they laid him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/16/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aaf5eae8-9f52-427a-8aa5-f1151e47d08a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: MRK 16:7
Text: But go your way, tell his disciples and Peter that he goeth before you into Galilee: there shall ye see him, as he said unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/16/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a0213e9-2310-4d5f-bdc1-ea04b4386490>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: MRK 16:8
Text: And they went out quickly, and fled from the sepulchre; for they trembled and were amazed: neither said they any thing to any man; for they were afraid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/16/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6641cb8-07a1-41d2-9b1f-f8fbd28b10b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: MRK 16:9
Text: Now when Jesus was risen early the first day of the week, he appeared first to Mary Magdalene, out of whom he had cast seven devils.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/16/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c31a85a-1d18-48a8-abaf-485ed2b207e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: MRK 16:10
Text: And she went and told them that had been with him, as they mourned and wept.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/16/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0153b9f1-812f-44de-9d03-0e91d4873e9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: MRK 16:11
Text: And they, when they had heard that he was alive, and had been seen of her, believed not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/16/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0c16fff-91f6-4065-9c87-c23e37ceba56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: MRK 16:12
Text: After that he appeared in another form unto two of them, as they walked, and went into the country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/16/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bcfc64d-47f2-4265-9082-c0c603e4118c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: MRK 16:13
Text: And they went and told it unto the residue: neither believed they them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/16/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb7bc203-03b8-429b-ab5f-689575f8e9ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: MRK 16:14
Text: Afterward he appeared unto the eleven as they sat at meat, and upbraided them with their unbelief and hardness of heart, because they believed not them which had seen him after he was risen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/16/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f269eff9-752b-4420-bda2-38cc485d16f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: MRK 16:15
Text: And he said unto them, Go ye into all the world, and preach the gospel to every creature.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/16/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:366506cc-d0d0-4270-a866-fed91d23720e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: MRK 16:16
Text: He that believeth and is baptized shall be saved; but he that believeth not shall be damned.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/16/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a06c8f4-2507-49f2-9b4f-592cb4bc9eac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: MRK 16:17
Text: And these signs shall follow them that believe; In my name shall they cast out devils; they shall speak with new tongues;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/16/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9904d78b-1295-49fb-99c8-5b39a339b61c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: MRK 16:18
Text: They shall take up serpents; and if they drink any deadly thing, it shall not hurt them; they shall lay hands on the sick, and they shall recover.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/16/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:845de873-a684-4b65-bde3-03f01547a730>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: MRK 16:19
Text: So then after the Lord had spoken unto them, he was received up into heaven, and sat on the right hand of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/MRK/16/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c66b7db4-156b-48c4-89de-cf6387d9b0b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: MRK 16:20
Text: And they went forth, and preached every where, the Lord working with them, and confirming the word with signs following. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e687f92b-3486-4323-949e-94651ce1b557>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: LUK 1:1
Text: Forasmuch as many have taken in hand to set forth in order a declaration of those things which are most surely believed among us,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7cc1dd80-5f94-4d0d-8c8a-98e2543532ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: LUK 1:2
Text: Even as they delivered them unto us, which from the beginning were eyewitnesses, and ministers of the word;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd76db69-5afa-47cd-a593-47dd1cac15ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: LUK 1:3
Text: It seemed good to me also, having had perfect understanding of all things from the very first, to write unto thee in order, most excellent Theophilus,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0713b1f7-1258-4839-9551-c58353430d70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: LUK 1:4
Text: That thou mightest know the certainty of those things, wherein thou hast been instructed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f49cc30-d28a-4225-93ee-0db5a5273531>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: LUK 1:5
Text: THERE was in the days of Herod, the king of Judaea, a certain priest named Zacharias, of the course of Abia: and his wife was of the daughters of Aaron, and her name was Elisabeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:becf36f5-a885-4010-a817-059927dd24d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: LUK 1:6
Text: And they were both righteous before God, walking in all the commandments and ordinances of the Lord blameless.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30a00f65-ce37-462c-b5f5-2c46134d0cfd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: LUK 1:7
Text: And they had no child, because that Elisabeth was barren, and they both were now well stricken in years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b0285b4-4e06-4811-8053-e8950f2f0723>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: LUK 1:8
Text: And it came to pass, that while he executed the priest’s office before God in the order of his course,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4794242-dd38-4e94-99bc-f4ab6f63e1aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: LUK 1:9
Text: According to the custom of the priest’s office, his lot was to burn incense when he went into the temple of the Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:655c947a-d2c7-4dfc-9ab4-11c2f62ae1eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: LUK 1:10
Text: And the whole multitude of the people were praying without at the time of incense.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0899beb9-f053-471e-add9-493ca201a544>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: LUK 1:11
Text: And there appeared unto him an angel of the Lord standing on the right side of the altar of incense.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1acacbce-9bbc-4292-8a3c-07db16ef7eba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: LUK 1:12
Text: And when Zacharias saw him, he was troubled, and fear fell upon him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a08a9922-f0b7-46c0-b1f1-99f9c896808e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: LUK 1:13
Text: But the angel said unto him, Fear not, Zacharias: for thy prayer is heard; and thy wife Elisabeth shall bear thee a son, and thou shalt call his name John.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fed34ea1-8f32-4541-8781-a12c06f3c484>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: LUK 1:14
Text: And thou shalt have joy and gladness; and many shall rejoice at his birth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:366affb8-7ba8-4d9d-b4d4-13407d0b6ae6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: LUK 1:15
Text: For he shall be great in the sight of the Lord, and shall drink neither wine nor strong drink; and he shall be filled with the Holy Ghost, even from his mother’s womb.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15e7e67e-67c6-4ab0-94f4-50da3c8ab0f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: LUK 1:16
Text: And many of the children of Israel shall he turn to the Lord their God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0146cdf1-549c-4b46-a911-e2dd6330d043>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: LUK 1:17
Text: And he shall go before him in the spirit and power of Elias, to turn the hearts of the fathers to the children, and the disobedient to the wisdom of the just; to make ready a people prepared for the Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c823461b-86f0-4473-bedb-c382260f82dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: LUK 1:18
Text: And Zacharias said unto the angel, Whereby shall I know this? for I am an old man, and my wife well stricken in years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:860f4f16-fed7-4ccf-9e87-94419a67e3e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: LUK 1:19
Text: And the angel answering said unto him, I am Gabriel, that stand in the presence of God; and am sent to speak unto thee, and to shew thee these glad tidings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:828df1d0-a06f-4ec5-8529-002ac07e103b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: LUK 1:20
Text: And, behold, thou shalt be dumb, and not able to speak, until the day that these things shall be performed, because thou believest not my words, which shall be fulfilled in their season.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bc5acde9-9c35-46f3-b33e-71f7844018af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: LUK 1:21
Text: And the people waited for Zacharias, and marvelled that he tarried so long in the temple.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8feadbfb-382b-44a1-9022-6c212930da6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: LUK 1:22
Text: And when he came out, he could not speak unto them: and they perceived that he had seen a vision in the temple: for he beckoned unto them, and remained speechless.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa2f504c-e060-420a-af79-fc542fc6b5fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: LUK 1:23
Text: And it came to pass, that, as soon as the days of his ministration were accomplished, he departed to his own house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77fd8468-f092-4b5a-af28-297d1bad62a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: LUK 1:24
Text: And after those days his wife Elisabeth conceived, and hid herself five months, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fde5aee0-1898-491a-b80c-5ae465a1c235>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: LUK 1:25
Text: Thus hath the Lord dealt with me in the days wherein he looked on me, to take away my reproach among men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f11118f-e909-435e-a147-4747f3999d7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: LUK 1:26
Text: And in the sixth month the angel Gabriel was sent from God unto a city of Galilee, named Nazareth,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1ee5aa7-8370-41ee-978a-ea2df276b2a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: LUK 1:27
Text: To a virgin espoused to a man whose name was Joseph, of the house of David; and the virgin’s name was Mary.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1854bf8e-16f9-491b-9622-14fd5b656922>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: LUK 1:28
Text: And the angel came in unto her, and said, Hail, thou that art highly favoured, the Lord is with thee: blessed art thou among women.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dad41c5b-e7c5-4698-82fb-b2e017dddda6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: LUK 1:29
Text: And when she saw him, she was troubled at his saying, and cast in her mind what manner of salutation this should be.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f43f70a3-c856-4292-b4bb-04a97d8e2c6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: LUK 1:30
Text: And the angel said unto her, Fear not, Mary: for thou hast found favour with God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfb2ea80-9b23-467b-9f61-980977f61dbe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: LUK 1:31
Text: And, behold, thou shalt conceive in thy womb, and bring forth a son, and shalt call his name JESUS.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44fac087-718b-41a6-8d2f-a86bdcb093fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: LUK 1:32
Text: He shall be great, and shall be called the Son of the Highest: and the Lord God shall give unto him the throne of his father David:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3e91939-5c66-419c-b04b-fc86175c2cd2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: LUK 1:33
Text: And he shall reign over the house of Jacob for ever; and of his kingdom there shall be no end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:656bba85-2a4b-4728-bca2-c9a545e344f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: LUK 1:34
Text: Then said Mary unto the angel, How shall this be, seeing I know not a man?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ec1ed03-6f63-4882-b6e2-41f33ad9da92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: LUK 1:35
Text: And the angel answered and said unto her, The Holy Ghost shall come upon thee, and the power of the Highest shall overshadow thee: therefore also that holy thing which shall be born of thee shall be called the Son of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbd9aff9-dc96-4a4b-86b2-3b5551ed7c67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: LUK 1:36
Text: And, behold, thy cousin Elisabeth, she hath also conceived a son in her old age: and this is the sixth month with her, who was called barren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3941573-7ab8-4238-9e18-c2b511270f15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 68

Reference: LUK 1:37
Text: For with God nothing shall be impossible.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb808245-f2c5-4a48-acb0-739a71beeb07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: LUK 1:38
Text: And Mary said, Behold the handmaid of the Lord; be it unto me according to thy word. And the angel departed from her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:108ce16d-633e-45a7-8b96-58bc1b309047>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: LUK 1:39
Text: And Mary arose in those days, and went into the hill country with haste, into a city of Juda;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:113da3c7-ca7b-49b5-83c5-21222c253aca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: LUK 1:40
Text: And entered into the house of Zacharias, and saluted Elisabeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b23a545-aab2-4d2a-b6ee-c717be136ef9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: LUK 1:41
Text: And it came to pass, that, when Elisabeth heard the salutation of Mary, the babe leaped in her womb; and Elisabeth was filled with the Holy Ghost:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8425eb7-7685-485d-8419-43f25dd3af86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: LUK 1:42
Text: And she spake out with a loud voice, and said, Blessed art thou among women, and blessed is the fruit of thy womb.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4838383d-1711-46ec-8f53-4f9708edc70e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: LUK 1:43
Text: And whence is this to me, that the mother of my Lord should come to me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edbdf1a5-e7ca-4488-85bd-271dce29b033>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: LUK 1:44
Text: For, lo, as soon as the voice of thy salutation sounded in mine ears, the babe leaped in my womb for joy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b1cb4b7-70a3-417e-830d-e113d71ac55a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: LUK 1:45
Text: And blessed is she that believed: for there shall be a performance of those things which were told her from the Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d19027a-5970-4cf6-bdbf-92d00067ba14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 72

Reference: LUK 1:46
Text: And Mary said, My soul doth magnify the Lord,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ae80a42-79ba-463f-a876-cc058f2ca0b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: LUK 1:47
Text: And my spirit hath rejoiced in God my Saviour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1dbdced8-df0c-4ad1-b40a-51814a5b5bef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: LUK 1:48
Text: For he hath regarded the low estate of his handmaiden: for, behold, from henceforth all generations shall call me blessed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b87045a9-c147-4f24-8903-ba94a2974c21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: LUK 1:49
Text: For he that is mighty hath done to me great things; and holy is his name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01db67e1-df0e-4f99-8403-0eb569a714f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: LUK 1:50
Text: And his mercy is on them that fear him from generation to generation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff51f2e4-3476-42a3-8361-2d4b1ea452d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: LUK 1:51
Text: He hath shewed strength with his arm; he hath scattered the proud in the imagination of their hearts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3997171d-a60a-4c7a-b9e7-b5e1c32af985>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: LUK 1:52
Text: He hath put down the mighty from their seats, and exalted them of low degree.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffb16906-c1a7-481d-bbb0-91bfb088f993>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: LUK 1:53
Text: He hath filled the hungry with good things; and the rich he hath sent empty away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:786416d7-a058-4b65-b797-7276d52f5d1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: LUK 1:54
Text: He hath holpen his servant Israel, in remembrance of his mercy;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/55
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ffebdde-2943-4189-862b-1701528b7cd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: LUK 1:55
Text: As he spake to our fathers, to Abraham, and to his seed for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/56
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20495e37-6658-453e-88cc-6461bb57b6b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: LUK 1:56
Text: And Mary abode with her about three months, and returned to her own house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/57
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fa07469-8311-4a28-8a53-bcaa9a4cfa52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: LUK 1:57
Text: Now Elisabeth’s full time came that she should be delivered; and she brought forth a son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/58
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2d8e374-9e8b-4280-ace9-195f2e02b20b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: LUK 1:58
Text: And her neighbours and her cousins heard how the Lord had shewed great mercy upon her; and they rejoiced with her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/59
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebcb53dc-b4bf-4d3e-a8eb-a9a2b1e69625>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: LUK 1:59
Text: And it came to pass, that on the eighth day they came to circumcise the child; and they called him Zacharias, after the name of his father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/60
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ec4998c-7a65-4fe6-81c6-269897bcbdbe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: LUK 1:60
Text: And his mother answered and said, Not so; but he shall be called John.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/61
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb14ed70-8166-4645-a813-3fe3eb537dce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: LUK 1:61
Text: And they said unto her, There is none of thy kindred that is called by this name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/62
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72a3e699-325b-42b9-ad7c-341cf6aedd66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: LUK 1:62
Text: And they made signs to his father, how he would have him called.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/63
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:075466a6-5548-48a2-b932-104461e18b85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: LUK 1:63
Text: And he asked for a writing table, and wrote, saying, His name is John. And they marvelled all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/64
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09acab4b-3558-420e-8539-976d4aacd7e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: LUK 1:64
Text: And his mouth was opened immediately, and his tongue loosed, and he spake, and praised God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/65
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25b74cfd-7e60-4f88-852a-971fd8ec2e48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: LUK 1:65
Text: And fear came on all that dwelt round about them: and all these sayings were noised abroad throughout all the hill country of Judaea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/66
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:096c1f67-6644-4c16-a1df-4c66046eee95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: LUK 1:66
Text: And all they that heard them laid them up in their hearts, saying, What manner of child shall this be! And the hand of the Lord was with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/67
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05144c83-554e-4240-a4ed-70a07094ab90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: LUK 1:67
Text: And his father Zacharias was filled with the Holy Ghost, and prophesied, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/68
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0c88c35-a983-4d1b-8057-a823cf5f3fa2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: LUK 1:68
Text: Blessed be the Lord God of Israel; for he hath visited and redeemed his people,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/69
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97dca438-d031-4517-ae49-a57c3a81f8cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: LUK 1:69
Text: And hath raised up an horn of salvation for us in the house of his servant David;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/70
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7457386-868a-4e82-b925-48ab1fdfbde4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: LUK 1:70
Text: As he spake by the mouth of his holy prophets, which have been since the world began:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/71
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8da50bfa-d564-4766-88d8-7f9373ea14b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: LUK 1:71
Text: That we should be saved from our enemies, and from the hand of all that hate us;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/72
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5918f4fe-324d-4129-be4e-4148436f2b32>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: LUK 1:72
Text: To perform the mercy promised to our fathers, and to remember his holy covenant;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/73
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:527c09ce-3d29-446e-b51d-eb70ef2ea245>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: LUK 1:73
Text: The oath which he sware to our father Abraham,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/74
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65142596-eca1-4787-8f55-1e4e7e96800c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: LUK 1:74
Text: That he would grant unto us, that we being delivered out of the hand of our enemies might serve him without fear,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/75
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c62c5628-153b-4f1e-81b0-7ed3afe125bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: LUK 1:75
Text: In holiness and righteousness before him, all the days of our life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/76
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7b4b053-e82b-41ff-9000-db98a8fa9ba5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: LUK 1:76
Text: And thou, child, shalt be called the prophet of the Highest: for thou shalt go before the face of the Lord to prepare his ways;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/77
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35924c04-6a8f-4dba-bbb1-431556b098a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: LUK 1:77
Text: To give knowledge of salvation unto his people by the remission of their sins,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/78
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c031dee-7838-4ff7-bb19-a1df5f511419>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: LUK 1:78
Text: Through the tender mercy of our God; whereby the dayspring from on high hath visited us,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/79
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc1c426a-e95d-44ed-880a-d1ec1bd23597>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: LUK 1:79
Text: To give light to them that sit in darkness and in the shadow of death, to guide our feet into the way of peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/1/80
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4aa02bd9-2738-40ba-8927-695c7c83784f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: LUK 1:80
Text: And the child grew, and waxed strong in spirit, and was in the deserts till the day of his shewing unto Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edc3283a-bfd2-4d31-bfd5-59d8032381e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: LUK 2:1
Text: And it came to pass in those days, that there went out a decree from Caesar Augustus that all the world should be taxed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbfe41fd-e0f9-4964-a1d3-7440caeb7ad6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: LUK 2:2
Text: (And this taxing was first made when Cyrenius was governor of Syria.)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ac8e163-9e64-42a6-9f3f-7a257a764f30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: LUK 2:3
Text: And all went to be taxed, every one into his own city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1093455-d0bb-4ac6-a621-fdc09553de6f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: LUK 2:4
Text: And Joseph also went up from Galilee, out of the city of Nazareth, into Judaea, unto the city of David, which is called Bethlehem; (because he was of the house and lineage of David:)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e00ced5-667e-4824-88d4-13bd0f23faee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: LUK 2:5
Text: To be taxed with Mary his espoused wife, being great with child.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:744668e5-3df2-4c9c-b9c8-c6bf42adfae9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: LUK 2:6
Text: And so it was, that, while they were there, the days were accomplished that she should be delivered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd1efe07-9249-452a-a4b7-01168b4e9bc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: LUK 2:7
Text: And she brought forth her firstborn son, and wrapped him in swaddling clothes, and laid him in a manger; because there was no room for them in the inn.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c810df89-a548-4bcf-a159-e09f6cfbc843>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: LUK 2:8
Text: And there were in the same country shepherds abiding in the field, keeping watch over their flock by night.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ada3ae6b-2ce0-446e-9158-757a09dd7ea7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: LUK 2:9
Text: And, lo, the angel of the Lord came upon them, and the glory of the Lord shone round about them: and they were sore afraid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a66ec82d-2d57-485c-a64c-c001998823b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: LUK 2:10
Text: And the angel said unto them, Fear not: for, behold, I bring you good tidings of great joy, which shall be to all people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
