Reference: LUK 3:1
Text: Now in the fifteenth year of the reign of Tiberius Caesar, Pontius Pilate being governor of Judaea, and Herod being tetrarch of Galilee, and his brother Philip tetrarch of Ituraea and of the region of Trachonitis, and Lysanias the tetrarch of Abilene,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50563209-77cd-4e28-bdcd-ab3a92fd8ab3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: LUK 3:2
Text: Annas and Caiaphas being the high priests, the word of God came unto John the son of Zacharias in the wilderness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8fbb7673-47f6-40eb-a5d3-0cfbb17ce880>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: LUK 3:3
Text: And he came into all the country about Jordan, preaching the baptism of repentance for the remission of sins;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40e863a6-0704-43ae-bb35-95b32802c845>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: LUK 3:4
Text: As it is written in the book of the words of Esaias the prophet, saying, The voice of one crying in the wilderness, Prepare ye the way of the Lord, make his paths straight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f037bebe-7a49-4f07-85f3-4b246e620b45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: LUK 3:5
Text: Every valley shall be filled, and every mountain and hill shall be brought low; and the crooked shall be made straight, and the rough ways shall be made smooth;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:192bbc4e-ed9c-4a15-ac51-51af0b8a2652>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 71

Reference: LUK 3:6
Text: And all flesh shall see the salvation of God.


