Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: LUK 3:7
Text: Then said he to the multitude that came forth to be baptized of him, O generation of vipers, who hath warned you to flee from the wrath to come?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c92ad35c-eacb-4d0e-b16b-b7dbd547a5e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: LUK 3:8
Text: Bring forth therefore fruits worthy of repentance, and begin not to say within yourselves, We have Abraham to our father: for I say unto you, That God is able of these stones to raise up children unto Abraham.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57a20f6c-9f13-42a7-8224-7495a6b80e81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: LUK 3:9
Text: And now also the axe is laid unto the root of the trees: every tree therefore which bringeth not forth good fruit is hewn down, and cast into the fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06913e39-8e32-4b7e-a8c3-f6108b650748>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

