Reference: LUK 4:31
Text: And came down to Capernaum, a city of Galilee, and taught them on the sabbath days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/4/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd697634-6545-46aa-9567-98494051347e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: LUK 4:32
Text: And they were astonished at his doctrine: for his word was with power.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/4/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d64d5bbf-d563-4fdc-ac08-4723d4594c5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: LUK 4:33
Text: And in the synagogue there was a man, which had a spirit of an unclean devil, and cried out with a loud voice,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/4/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de41c324-0a75-4045-bef9-0175105ba0cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: LUK 4:34
Text: Saying, Let us alone; what have we to do with thee, thou Jesus of Nazareth? art thou come to destroy us? I know thee who thou art; the Holy One of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/4/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43f39aa1-da5d-48e4-8c8c-3715a87e840b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: LUK 4:35
Text: And Jesus rebuked him, saying, Hold thy peace, and come out of him. And when the devil had thrown him in the midst, he came out of him, and hurt him not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/4/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5923124d-1851-416c-a4c4-7582e867fe25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: LUK 4:36
Text: And they were all amazed, and spake among themselves, saying, What a word is this! for with authority and power he commandeth the unclean spirits, and they come out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/4/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dcf98200-29b8-4e6f-8221-2c2d2a19db4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: LUK 4:37
Text: And the fame of him went out into every place of the country round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/4/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5fdf8429-1303-4d02-b38b-bb570212bdc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: LUK 4:38
Text: And he arose out of the synagogue, and entered into Simon’s house. And Simon’s wife’s mother was taken with a great fever; and they besought him for her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/4/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26933885-86dc-4d7e-ba0d-619cfffbe59c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: LUK 4:39
Text: And he stood over her, and rebuked the fever; and it left her: and immediately she arose and ministered unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/4/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70290353-9475-4e6c-b91a-a7977af67c4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: LUK 4:40
Text: Now when the sun was setting, all they that had any sick with divers diseases brought them unto him; and he laid his hands on every one of them, and healed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/4/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
