Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: LUK 5:1
Text: And it came to pass, that, as the people pressed upon him to hear the word of God, he stood by the lake of Gennesaret,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0cbf322e-8bf3-42b5-9fd4-19b8f2c15b5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: LUK 5:2
Text: And saw two ships standing by the lake: but the fishermen were gone out of them, and were washing their nets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52b95577-6114-49f1-bdb6-3cd75bd27927>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: LUK 5:3
Text: And he entered into one of the ships, which was Simon’s, and prayed him that he would thrust out a little from the land. And he sat down, and taught the people out of the ship.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b4966ce-611c-4451-a4fe-09e351639a8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: LUK 5:4
Text: Now when he had left speaking, he said unto Simon, Launch out into the deep, and let down your nets for a draught.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c40ebc0-d966-4e37-b657-a396718c39bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: LUK 5:5
Text: And Simon answering said unto him, Master, we have toiled all the night, and have taken nothing: nevertheless at thy word I will let down the net.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64ebc808-d5f5-4c38-8cf4-eb2fe41d1c47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: LUK 5:6
Text: And when they had this done, they inclosed a great multitude of fishes: and their net brake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf2dfc2a-ec2d-43f4-b567-483498d28796>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: LUK 5:7
Text: And they beckoned unto their partners, which were in the other ship, that they should come and help them. And they came, and filled both the ships, so that they began to sink.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64f8a8b9-9a47-48c3-b6f5-099bcdaaf9e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: LUK 5:8
Text: When Simon Peter saw it, he fell down at Jesus’ knees, saying, Depart from me; for I am a sinful man, O Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3aec82c2-71a9-49ec-8cc9-fcb32330e091>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: LUK 5:9
Text: For he was astonished, and all that were with him, at the draught of the fishes which they had taken:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:882cb1d4-1dce-4c3e-b3d4-b4eac5eac5a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: LUK 5:10
Text: And so was also James, and John, the sons of Zebedee, which were partners with Simon. And Jesus said unto Simon, Fear not; from henceforth thou shalt catch men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d7f8c73-d82b-4146-9eea-82f4fc848d25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: LUK 5:11
Text: And when they had brought their ships to land, they forsook all, and followed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99bb9bee-50a4-4bef-9323-5c53f7ea0a63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: LUK 5:12
Text: And it came to pass, when he was in a certain city, behold a man full of leprosy: who seeing Jesus fell on his face, and besought him, saying, Lord, if thou wilt, thou canst make me clean.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f12d7d64-47db-4682-9d50-4c11e4fc6840>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: LUK 5:13
Text: And he put forth his hand, and touched him, saying, I will: be thou clean. And immediately the leprosy departed from him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40b6bcc8-51d6-46ed-801e-d6005d52b015>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: LUK 5:14
Text: And he charged him to tell no man: but go, and shew thyself to the priest, and offer for thy cleansing, according as Moses commanded, for a testimony unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51e711d8-c949-48b5-9de6-0e558cdfd054>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: LUK 5:15
Text: But so much the more went there a fame abroad of him: and great multitudes came together to hear, and to be healed by him of their infirmities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b7728c5-2f07-4e13-802c-a004a641010f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: LUK 5:16
Text: And he withdrew himself into the wilderness, and prayed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed3c5c64-0bfa-4a3b-9b35-7015de1eb1af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: LUK 5:17
Text: And it came to pass on a certain day, as he was teaching, that there were Pharisees and doctors of the law sitting by, which were come out of every town of Galilee, and Judaea, and Jerusalem: and the power of the Lord was present to heal them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7dbaba86-ba13-4c1c-8914-924f1040011b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: LUK 5:18
Text: And, behold, men brought in a bed a man which was taken with a palsy: and they sought means to bring him in, and to lay him before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b27187d8-47ac-42ff-9c67-1498d06bae10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: LUK 5:19
Text: And when they could not find by what way they might bring him in because of the multitude, they went upon the housetop, and let him down through the tiling with his couch into the midst before Jesus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed8b37d3-2598-4275-beba-4a00a39487ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: LUK 5:20
Text: And when he saw their faith, he said unto him, Man, thy sins are forgiven thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8182d12f-efb8-4cd4-b9a5-244e36193d7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: LUK 5:21
Text: And the scribes and the Pharisees began to reason, saying, Who is this which speaketh blasphemies? Who can forgive sins, but God alone?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b564616-f032-4fed-a427-80dd3525b93d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: LUK 5:22
Text: But when Jesus perceived their thoughts, he answering said unto them, What reason ye in your hearts?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9652b068-9bbe-421b-ab17-4ee3a3506f49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: LUK 5:23
Text: Whether is easier, to say, Thy sins be forgiven thee; or to say, Rise up and walk?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5288a881-2173-4589-842a-1f879adaebcb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: LUK 5:24
Text: But that ye may know that the Son of man hath power upon earth to forgive sins, (he said unto the sick of the palsy,) I say unto thee, Arise, and take up thy couch, and go into thine house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8053e4b1-d13e-4e74-9168-ed1703d6268a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: LUK 5:25
Text: And immediately he rose up before them, and took up that whereon he lay, and departed to his own house, glorifying God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1dd15d75-0ac1-4159-9a8d-7f7a4e154db9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: LUK 5:26
Text: And they were all amazed, and they glorified God, and were filled with fear, saying, We have seen strange things to day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ac070ae-ebb5-4b27-a140-3e84413ba278>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: LUK 5:27
Text: And after these things he went forth, and saw a publican, named Levi, sitting at the receipt of custom: and he said unto him, Follow me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9381d80-87d0-4518-b840-2500b7b634ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 70

Reference: LUK 5:28
Text: And he left all, rose up, and followed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32830de3-7446-4d49-bdd7-14530b682876>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: LUK 5:29
Text: And Levi made him a great feast in his own house: and there was a great company of publicans and of others that sat down with them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbbf6390-2c19-4563-a081-f8976b0a08fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: LUK 5:30
Text: But their scribes and Pharisees murmured against his disciples, saying, Why do ye eat and drink with publicans and sinners?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d4ea13c-f387-48ca-9f76-d33a3105db0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: LUK 5:31
Text: And Jesus answering said unto them, They that are whole need not a physician; but they that are sick.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c220ab70-6f0a-4bb9-87cb-1bcd7d5e5e70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: LUK 5:32
Text: I came not to call the righteous, but sinners to repentance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59b21876-1d34-461a-9eae-71bbc7ba3d37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: LUK 5:33
Text: And they said unto him, Why do the disciples of John fast often, and make prayers, and likewise the disciples of the Pharisees; but thine eat and drink?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:448237fb-548d-486c-a3f1-4c3692f21fe5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: LUK 5:34
Text: And he said unto them, Can ye make the children of the bridechamber fast, while the bridegroom is with them?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:adfa663b-cab4-46dd-81fa-baf77ac06936>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: LUK 5:35
Text: But the days will come, when the bridegroom shall be taken away from them, and then shall they fast in those days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a769822e-a839-4df9-8691-55aa05c7e13b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: LUK 5:36
Text: And he spake also a parable unto them; No man putteth a piece of a new garment upon an old; if otherwise, then both the new maketh a rent, and the piece that was taken out of the new agreeth not with the old.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:991adcd1-9ad3-430f-8ac6-f0b88c3533fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: LUK 5:37
Text: And no man putteth new wine into old bottles; else the new wine will burst the bottles, and be spilled, and the bottles shall perish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08ce1a9c-ba23-4a5c-851f-5fe9f595c43a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: LUK 5:38
Text: But new wine must be put into new bottles; and both are preserved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/5/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96cd3519-c227-4394-b982-ae1c508d57c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: LUK 5:39
Text: No man also having drunk old wine straightway desireth new: for he saith, The old is better.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:528fa110-1930-40af-88ab-1f97d2850441>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: LUK 6:1
Text: And it came to pass on the second sabbath after the first, that he went through the corn fields; and his disciples plucked the ears of corn, and did eat, rubbing them in their hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3667632-2f6e-48e2-80b6-d25a94d90878>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: LUK 6:2
Text: And certain of the Pharisees said unto them, Why do ye that which is not lawful to do on the sabbath days?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8905502-f780-493f-9d3b-c08df8403b99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: LUK 6:3
Text: And Jesus answering them said, Have ye not read so much as this, what David did, when himself was an hungred, and they which were with him;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23e2f810-d3aa-4789-9395-631a48c3f3d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: LUK 6:4
Text: How he went into the house of God, and did take and eat the shewbread, and gave also to them that were with him; which it is not lawful to eat but for the priests alone?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee6e92e7-44a1-487d-a6a1-411ac4e0a5ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: LUK 6:5
Text: And he said unto them, That the Son of man is Lord also of the sabbath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24e56c14-bc0c-43f7-80f0-784011213955>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: LUK 6:6
Text: And it came to pass also on another sabbath, that he entered into the synagogue and taught: and there was a man whose right hand was withered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5140e4b3-f062-440d-bd7a-3be198c8a4d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: LUK 6:7
Text: And the scribes and Pharisees watched him, whether he would heal on the sabbath day; that they might find an accusation against him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eca355db-a385-41ce-9d58-ecd6360401e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: LUK 6:8
Text: But he knew their thoughts, and said to the man which had the withered hand, Rise up, and stand forth in the midst. And he arose and stood forth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7f5e18c-0d96-40db-ae73-e5db072aa5e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: LUK 6:9
Text: Then said Jesus unto them, I will ask you one thing; Is it lawful on the sabbath days to do good, or to do evil? to save life, or to destroy it?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8930366e-3eae-4073-b23c-470640ad6656>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: LUK 6:10
Text: And looking round about upon them all, he said unto the man, Stretch forth thy hand. And he did so: and his hand was restored whole as the other.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
