WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6362903a-97a6-4590-b846-44b9403dc159>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: LUK 6:15
Text: Matthew and Thomas, James the son of Alphaeus, and Simon called Zelotes,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82a9a0cf-6179-42cb-8776-7254c3f0823f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: LUK 6:16
Text: And Judas the brother of James, and Judas Iscariot, which also was the traitor.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a07c3e89-d493-4862-8688-7581aac5c106>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 279

Reference: LUK 6:17
Text: And he came down with them, and stood in the plain, and the company of his disciples, and a great multitude of people out of all Judaea and Jerusalem, and from the sea coast of Tyre and Sidon, which came to hear him, and to be healed of their diseases;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8772c92-e087-4d95-8bf6-6b9de6fd5f82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: LUK 6:18
Text: And they that were vexed with unclean spirits: and they were healed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:948b8778-d6ff-4476-acd3-4929d66cc742>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: LUK 6:19
Text: And the whole multitude sought to touch him: for there went virtue out of him, and healed them all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a658e67-faed-4265-8bb6-5ce5756f3b33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: LUK 6:20
Text: And he lifted up his eyes on his disciples, and said, Blessed be ye poor: for yours is the kingdom of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a24ba73-111b-4aeb-b46a-4221a5871fc3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: LUK 6:21
Text: Blessed are ye that hunger now: for ye shall be filled. Blessed are ye that weep now: for ye shall laugh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15862e17-dc8c-4378-b081-a610b1d68b85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: LUK 6:22
Text: Blessed are ye, when men shall hate you, and when they shall separate you from their company, and shall reproach you, and cast out your name as evil, for the Son of man’s sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:093f106e-3dcf-4ac2-a046-84a5655c5829>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: LUK 6:23
Text: Rejoice ye in that day, and leap for joy: for, behold, your reward is great in heaven: for in the like manner did their fathers unto the prophets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4cb41604-60b2-443d-9108-c6447dfdfb5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: LUK 6:24
Text: But woe unto you that are rich! for ye have received your consolation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1689d7f3-1e2d-46ce-a4c2-2c237d9f9a3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: LUK 6:25
Text: Woe unto you that are full! for ye shall hunger. Woe unto you that laugh now! for ye shall mourn and weep.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8601b48e-10f7-448d-a70f-d8f03c75bcd3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: LUK 6:26
Text: Woe unto you, when all men shall speak well of you! for so did their fathers to the false prophets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93825827-34ae-4ad2-a7e7-b2c549f461c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: LUK 6:27
Text: But I say unto you which hear, Love your enemies, do good to them which hate you,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed12b251-a840-42d9-be2b-8e055e44b2ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: LUK 6:28
Text: Bless them that curse you, and pray for them which despitefully use you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4519131-bef9-457d-95a6-d4f2d295edeb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: LUK 6:29
Text: And unto him that smiteth thee on the one cheek offer also the other; and him that taketh away thy cloak forbid not to take thy coat also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ddd44b8-dfc9-4bf8-9f5b-7dfe7a798ad6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: LUK 6:30
Text: Give to every man that asketh of thee; and of him that taketh away thy goods ask them not again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fb8e852-f662-417a-bd89-3e4226bf38bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: LUK 6:31
Text: And as ye would that men should do to you, do ye also to them likewise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b14292d-1f91-4ddc-9600-0ea4927d1547>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: LUK 6:32
Text: For if ye love them which love you, what thank have ye? for sinners also love those that love them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cef0bdf0-e2fc-4268-8878-8b2d0b0cee5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: LUK 6:33
Text: And if ye do good to them which do good to you, what thank have ye? for sinners also do even the same.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c218a313-aaf3-43d0-b861-998d803c52c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: LUK 6:34
Text: And if ye lend to them of whom ye hope to receive, what thank have ye? for sinners also lend to sinners, to receive as much again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7299fdb4-a44d-48aa-af37-21fd8fb3d70b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: LUK 6:35
Text: But love ye your enemies, and do good, and lend, hoping for nothing again; and your reward shall be great, and ye shall be the children of the Highest: for he is kind unto the unthankful and to the evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cfe8bb8-72c8-42c8-bffa-e12be5afa8fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: LUK 6:36
Text: Be ye therefore merciful, as your Father also is merciful.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75858188-944c-4ddb-ad2e-6674d050d727>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: LUK 6:37
Text: Judge not, and ye shall not be judged: condemn not, and ye shall not be condemned: forgive, and ye shall be forgiven:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1d3dcd6-402e-4e33-89f2-679ca3487ebb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: LUK 6:38
Text: Give, and it shall be given unto you; good measure, pressed down, and shaken together, and running over, shall men give into your bosom. For with the same measure that ye mete withal it shall be measured to you again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3027805-5a9f-41bb-9b39-30493742b4b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: LUK 6:39
Text: And he spake a parable unto them, Can the blind lead the blind? shall they not both fall into the ditch?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:948451b5-3ee9-4974-a8db-cd30c9da0110>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: LUK 6:40
Text: The disciple is not above his master: but every one that is perfect shall be as his master.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a16e7260-52d3-4240-9781-9d746baf129d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: LUK 6:41
Text: And why beholdest thou the mote that is in thy brother’s eye, but perceivest not the beam that is in thine own eye?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:392b4e93-594c-4d03-a872-13c687ea1393>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 338

Reference: LUK 6:42
Text: Either how canst thou say to thy brother, Brother, let me pull out the mote that is in thine eye, when thou thyself beholdest not the beam that is in thine own eye? Thou hypocrite, cast out first the beam out of thine own eye, and then shalt thou see clearly to pull out the mote that is in thy brother’s eye.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67e9832c-6a22-423d-853a-305e5bd3e3f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: LUK 6:43
Text: For a good tree bringeth not forth corrupt fruit; neither doth a corrupt tree bring forth good fruit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27873d65-8ea3-4671-a183-dcadc255e75f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: LUK 6:44
Text: For every tree is known by his own fruit. For of thorns men do not gather figs, nor of a bramble bush gather they grapes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:056994ad-749c-4bd9-8d90-be8533d47be9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: LUK 6:45
Text: A good man out of the good treasure of his heart bringeth forth that which is good; and an evil man out of the evil treasure of his heart bringeth forth that which is evil: for of the abundance of the heart his mouth speaketh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:657f827c-3a3b-4921-b005-66eaf27b7669>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: LUK 6:46
Text: And why call ye me, Lord, Lord, and do not the things which I say?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0323c51c-d57f-454d-8758-0472a6cfef6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: LUK 6:47
Text: Whosoever cometh to me, and heareth my sayings, and doeth them, I will shew you to whom he is like:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56e90a36-513b-4364-b4f4-d55a1e8155be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: LUK 6:48
Text: He is like a man which built an house, and digged deep, and laid the foundation on a rock: and when the flood arose, the stream beat vehemently upon that house, and could not shake it: for it was founded upon a rock.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/6/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:075286cb-ed1d-489e-81e4-9c41b0083cd0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: LUK 6:49
Text: But he that heareth, and doeth not, is like a man that without a foundation built an house upon the earth; against which the stream did beat vehemently, and immediately it fell; and the ruin of that house was great.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e65b1c35-ca36-42ba-b103-e14b8552aa07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: LUK 7:1
Text: Now when he had ended all his sayings in the audience of the people, he entered into Capernaum.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2fac96d-a3d6-4075-9282-ad272a1b5ac6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: LUK 7:2
Text: And a certain centurion’s servant, who was dear unto him, was sick, and ready to die.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a12fa16d-b879-488a-906f-85bc9e5248b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: LUK 7:3
Text: And when he heard of Jesus, he sent unto him the elders of the Jews, beseeching him that he would come and heal his servant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1751ff9b-10de-4045-a14c-82abec45f03e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: LUK 7:4
Text: And when they came to Jesus, they besought him instantly, saying, That he was worthy for whom he should do this:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a465c3c-9184-4d4f-8feb-7d5fa04c22db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: LUK 7:5
Text: For he loveth our nation, and he hath built us a synagogue.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0b5770f-a5f2-4b66-af82-1e81a9ea26fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: LUK 7:6
Text: Then Jesus went with them. And when he was now not far from the house, the centurion sent friends to him, saying unto him, Lord, trouble not thyself: for I am not worthy that thou shouldest enter under my roof:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18c47685-4377-49d7-8638-19ad2af05d84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: LUK 7:7
Text: Wherefore neither thought I myself worthy to come unto thee: but say in a word, and my servant shall be healed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a56205e8-ae36-47e7-8b77-6b2d7f3d692d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: LUK 7:8
Text: For I also am a man set under authority, having under me soldiers, and I say unto one, Go, and he goeth; and to another, Come, and he cometh; and to my servant, Do this, and he doeth it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44ceb860-06b1-4744-b722-ad269ecbf20a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: LUK 7:9
Text: When Jesus heard these things, he marvelled at him, and turned him about, and said unto the people that followed him, I say unto you, I have not found so great faith, no, not in Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a66ec6d-c09c-4328-beb3-ea9ad86eabdc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: LUK 7:10
Text: And they that were sent, returning to the house, found the servant whole that had been sick.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54bd3b3f-acc9-44be-816d-409dd3be15ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: LUK 7:11
Text: And it came to pass the day after, that he went into a city called Nain; and many of his disciples went with him, and much people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bdc80ae-5e30-4a65-9e72-e03ee6d385e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: LUK 7:12
Text: Now when he came nigh to the gate of the city, behold, there was a dead man carried out, the only son of his mother, and she was a widow: and much people of the city was with her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2ced7d3-34a1-4c22-9ef1-1fb6c8a25801>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: LUK 7:13
Text: And when the Lord saw her, he had compassion on her, and said unto her, Weep not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98ecec01-0695-4e44-8cc2-365940e9c0e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: LUK 7:14
Text: And he came and touched the bier: and they that bare him stood still. And he said, Young man, I say unto thee, Arise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75dd6f70-46f9-4a69-a493-4f6b79f46d45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: LUK 7:15
Text: And he that was dead sat up, and began to speak. And he delivered him to his mother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af158726-8b75-4415-a583-489def921a14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: LUK 7:16
Text: And there came a fear on all: and they glorified God, saying, That a great prophet is risen up among us; and, That God hath visited his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d410d769-c887-40dc-9882-4b26b408e33b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: LUK 7:17
Text: And this rumour of him went forth throughout all Judaea, and throughout all the region round about.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55503447-563e-4610-94ac-5254d1244a37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: LUK 7:18
Text: And the disciples of John shewed him of all these things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8615691-8ca7-4a84-af27-bbad65c425b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: LUK 7:19
Text: And John calling unto him two of his disciples sent them to Jesus, saying, Art thou he that should come? or look we for another?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:911e4de8-29b9-428d-8b97-0ad33812cdf6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: LUK 7:20
Text: When the men were come unto him, they said, John Baptist hath sent us unto thee, saying, Art thou he that should come? or look we for another?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed469046-3675-4d31-bbc5-84b6a8acaa29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: LUK 7:21
Text: And in that same hour he cured many of their infirmities and plagues, and of evil spirits; and unto many that were blind he gave sight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e23e5828-17e2-4119-8e6a-c15f26a768a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 262

Reference: LUK 7:22
Text: Then Jesus answering said unto them, Go your way, and tell John what things ye have seen and heard; how that the blind see, the lame walk, the lepers are cleansed, the deaf hear, the dead are raised, to the poor the gospel is preached.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35330376-e64c-4e84-8942-4ee615f339e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: LUK 7:23
Text: And blessed is he, whosoever shall not be offended in me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6495f9e8-bbe2-423c-92de-e7d3c7888966>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: LUK 7:24
Text: And when the messengers of John were departed, he began to speak unto the people concerning John, What went ye out into the wilderness for to see? A reed shaken with the wind?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9db3ea7-9fbd-4dd5-a1a0-6abda1b8f8f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: LUK 7:25
Text: But what went ye out for to see? A man clothed in soft raiment? Behold, they which are gorgeously apparelled, and live delicately, are in kings’ courts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3791008c-81cf-4a5b-b9d3-9a23d6f7d3b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: LUK 7:26
Text: But what went ye out for to see? A prophet? Yea, I say unto you, and much more than a prophet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6d7b288-ecae-48ec-a69c-c7ec31184ea0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: LUK 7:27
Text: This is he, of whom it is written, Behold, I send my messenger before thy face, which shall prepare thy way before thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:848d68be-4614-440c-a857-ca813fd6f096>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: LUK 7:28
Text: For I say unto you, Among those that are born of women there is not a greater prophet than John the Baptist: but he that is least in the kingdom of God is greater than he.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2aa9095a-dfcd-4ab2-a124-f99d1e5ae580>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: LUK 7:29
Text: And all the people that heard him, and the publicans, justified God, being baptized with the baptism of John.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f48f8534-1b72-470b-b022-7da017e0017f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: LUK 7:30
Text: But the Pharisees and lawyers rejected the counsel of God against themselves, being not baptized of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26b5aa34-5e7e-4cd4-b379-caad2ecd39e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: LUK 7:31
Text: And the Lord said, Whereunto then shall I liken the men of this generation? and to what are they like?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06b9d7fe-6754-4357-ad37-2610e09f1579>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: LUK 7:32
Text: They are like unto children sitting in the marketplace, and calling one to another, and saying, We have piped unto you, and ye have not danced; we have mourned to you, and ye have not wept.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee435376-34bf-453a-8b3a-de640602202b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: LUK 7:33
Text: For John the Baptist came neither eating bread nor drinking wine; and ye say, He hath a devil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5f24e81-e95c-4cda-a106-93d1c538dd3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: LUK 7:34
Text: The Son of man is come eating and drinking; and ye say, Behold a gluttonous man, and a winebibber, a friend of publicans and sinners!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50b48c59-c13d-45c4-8054-988938191f50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 71

Reference: LUK 7:35
Text: But wisdom is justified of all her children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:76d6f938-20e9-4052-a297-7b58df343a53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: LUK 7:36
Text: And one of the Pharisees desired him that he would eat with him. And he went into the Pharisee’s house, and sat down to meat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ac8d963-1711-4367-bcdf-d11e06682bbd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: LUK 7:37
Text: And, behold, a woman in the city, which was a sinner, when she knew that Jesus sat at meat in the Pharisee’s house, brought an alabaster box of ointment,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57283bc4-6aef-45d9-8148-fdf168b03d3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: LUK 7:38
Text: And stood at his feet behind him weeping, and began to wash his feet with tears, and did wipe them with the hairs of her head, and kissed his feet, and anointed them with the ointment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:816d60d4-07fb-475b-aeeb-6986d7bf76a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: LUK 7:39
Text: Now when the Pharisee which had bidden him saw it, he spake within himself, saying, This man, if he were a prophet, would have known who and what manner of woman this is that toucheth him: for she is a sinner.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edc9ab41-9497-46fb-a9f1-1d082ff1b74d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: LUK 7:40
Text: And Jesus answering said unto him, Simon, I have somewhat to say unto thee. And he saith, Master, say on.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd2de120-d877-4bbb-9548-162ab509f4d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: LUK 7:41
Text: There was a certain creditor which had two debtors: the one owed five hundred pence, and the other fifty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:862c4591-6cd3-4761-b67d-cbeae5b67509>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: LUK 7:42
Text: And when they had nothing to pay, he frankly forgave them both. Tell me therefore, which of them will love him most?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22a889ab-4554-4aeb-a883-65a98b36bb2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: LUK 7:43
Text: Simon answered and said, I suppose that he, to whom he forgave most. And he said unto him, Thou hast rightly judged.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c62bef2e-d180-4cde-adc8-5dd14ff6f295>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: LUK 7:44
Text: And he turned to the woman, and said unto Simon, Seest thou this woman? I entered into thine house, thou gavest me no water for my feet: but she hath washed my feet with tears, and wiped them with the hairs of her head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aaef15e5-869f-4bb2-8cfb-b96c0d50a4fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: LUK 7:45
Text: Thou gavest me no kiss: but this woman since the time I came in hath not ceased to kiss my feet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05ef3184-fd93-4f16-b3a8-2504bd98a90a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: LUK 7:46
Text: My head with oil thou didst not anoint: but this woman hath anointed my feet with ointment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46751455-b854-4140-9c69-132753d03535>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: LUK 7:47
Text: Wherefore I say unto thee, Her sins, which are many, are forgiven; for she loved much: but to whom little is forgiven, the same loveth little.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92ff7ef1-73c6-46bf-8379-ea6a92b2722f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 71

Reference: LUK 7:48
Text: And he said unto her, Thy sins are forgiven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/7/49
