WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/8/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5a892f5-d572-4811-9b75-664f4ea7b14f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: LUK 8:50
Text: But when Jesus heard it, he answered him, saying, Fear not: believe only, and she shall be made whole.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/8/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7517e136-69bc-404c-a3df-b8ebb5dd668f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: LUK 8:51
Text: And when he came into the house, he suffered no man to go in, save Peter, and James, and John, and the father and the mother of the maiden.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/8/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56f0a41b-51ef-403e-8119-9ae0d8a10699>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: LUK 8:52
Text: And all wept, and bewailed her: but he said, Weep not; she is not dead, but sleepeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/8/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4724a177-c35f-44bb-a567-0db349e72c9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: LUK 8:53
Text: And they laughed him to scorn, knowing that she was dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/8/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2543a4f-6bbe-4562-b673-c17f96ad4b60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: LUK 8:54
Text: And he put them all out, and took her by the hand, and called, saying, Maid, arise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/8/55
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:adc6f704-023a-4ef1-92cd-09543ee549c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: LUK 8:55
Text: And her spirit came again, and she arose straightway: and he commanded to give her meat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/8/56
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1df5d498-6478-4d01-82f0-adc8659e721f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: LUK 8:56
Text: And her parents were astonished: but he charged them that they should tell no man what was done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:771bb71a-b0ae-43bb-a39c-f6d37b6f7f00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: LUK 9:1
Text: Then he called his twelve disciples together, and gave them power and authority over all devils, and to cure diseases.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fcacb94a-011f-4a23-8c16-d79fa66f50fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: LUK 9:2
Text: And he sent them to preach the kingdom of God, and to heal the sick.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1df839b7-d415-4439-9c9d-95a95c7ed400>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: LUK 9:3
Text: And he said unto them, Take nothing for your journey, neither staves, nor scrip, neither bread, neither money; neither have two coats apiece.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a29400b-ca7c-4086-8354-75c90e952a24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: LUK 9:4
Text: And whatsoever house ye enter into, there abide, and thence depart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59984ca0-a971-4cfa-b7c9-37746434c992>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: LUK 9:5
Text: And whosoever will not receive you, when ye go out of that city, shake off the very dust from your feet for a testimony against them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3a36d14-deaa-4735-a286-33961e3fc797>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: LUK 9:6
Text: And they departed, and went through the towns, preaching the gospel, and healing every where.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19653c19-592b-42f0-91b1-080953685d0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: LUK 9:7
Text: Now Herod the tetrarch heard of all that was done by him: and he was perplexed, because that it was said of some, that John was risen from the dead;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd0082c0-64a7-4398-8c56-0adfa5499011>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: LUK 9:8
Text: And of some, that Elias had appeared; and of others, that one of the old prophets was risen again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c650e60-5e52-4470-a52b-74e49eafa7b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: LUK 9:9
Text: And Herod said, John have I beheaded: but who is this, of whom I hear such things? And he desired to see him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5f52d71-a553-408e-8c41-00085173cbbf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: LUK 9:10
Text: And the apostles, when they were returned, told him all that they had done. And he took them, and went aside privately into a desert place belonging to the city called Bethsaida.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:daead114-bf95-4703-9065-f86b73d5b569>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: LUK 9:11
Text: And the people, when they knew it, followed him: and he received them, and spake unto them of the kingdom of God, and healed them that had need of healing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df015b56-5ec5-482f-8816-0e1147aa181b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: LUK 9:12
Text: And when the day began to wear away, then came the twelve, and said unto him, Send the multitude away, that they may go into the towns and country round about, and lodge, and get victuals: for we are here in a desert place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:806d2593-44ea-48c7-8da9-e445a1d3c9eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: LUK 9:13
Text: But he said unto them, Give ye them to eat. And they said, We have no more but five loaves and two fishes; except we should go and buy meat for all this people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42ba04e3-227b-401f-8f80-313d210624d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: LUK 9:14
Text: For they were about five thousand men. And he said to his disciples, Make them sit down by fifties in a company.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:219a5377-51c4-4263-9495-aae8583a3045>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 71

Reference: LUK 9:15
Text: And they did so, and made them all sit down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84848220-5605-4789-8c4b-1aceaf6c0d3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: LUK 9:16
Text: Then he took the five loaves and the two fishes, and looking up to heaven, he blessed them, and brake, and gave to the disciples to set before the multitude.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fc2e01e-0dfa-421d-832c-95d94231c735>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: LUK 9:17
Text: And they did eat, and were all filled: and there was taken up of fragments that remained to them twelve baskets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38cb39fe-9784-45ab-b388-391c16ad80b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: LUK 9:18
Text: And it came to pass, as he was alone praying, his disciples were with him: and he asked them, saying, Whom say the people that I am?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d925179-1d67-4eba-beab-404fa36eb73b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: LUK 9:19
Text: They answering said, John the Baptist; but some say, Elias; and others say, that one of the old prophets is risen again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db8aeac8-5af2-4ec5-b2ba-e1472930ec65>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: LUK 9:20
Text: He said unto them, But whom say ye that I am? Peter answering said, The Christ of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e98f2760-7ebd-4421-8fc3-2e4289709f37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: LUK 9:21
Text: And he straitly charged them, and commanded them to tell no man that thing;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96719a7d-9248-4d5b-8601-457a4ba7e521>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: LUK 9:22
Text: Saying, The Son of man must suffer many things, and be rejected of the elders and chief priests and scribes, and be slain, and be raised the third day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2703f268-12a1-444e-9d12-7f9fc9d3dcf5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: LUK 9:23
Text: And he said to them all, If any man will come after me, let him deny himself, and take up his cross daily, and follow me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a447b4c-a575-40c2-ade5-858df9c3ff99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: LUK 9:24
Text: For whosoever will save his life shall lose it: but whosoever will lose his life for my sake, the same shall save it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43d0bc91-5918-4c9e-b171-1ad13882e53c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: LUK 9:25
Text: For what is a man advantaged, if he gain the whole world, and lose himself, or be cast away?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aff396b3-458c-407b-84cf-345363ffe170>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: LUK 9:26
Text: For whosoever shall be ashamed of me and of my words, of him shall the Son of man be ashamed, when he shall come in his own glory, and in his Father’s, and of the holy angels.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b271fc4d-355a-4c53-8825-1aab9453ef8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: LUK 9:27
Text: But I tell you of a truth, there be some standing here, which shall not taste of death, till they see the kingdom of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c314b2c9-85bf-433d-930d-0db672a93252>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: LUK 9:28
Text: And it came to pass about an eight days after these sayings, he took Peter and John and James, and went up into a mountain to pray.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e4fa888-283f-4ed1-99f1-89373423e5bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: LUK 9:29
Text: And as he prayed, the fashion of his countenance was altered, and his raiment was white and glistering.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e98974e-1f7b-431b-8417-a1fdc79d2d50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: LUK 9:30
Text: And, behold, there talked with him two men, which were Moses and Elias:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:886ec8dd-2001-4059-a558-fb5f2598f6f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: LUK 9:31
Text: Who appeared in glory, and spake of his decease which he should accomplish at Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ae8cbcf-98ed-47dc-911b-8d50aa6cebae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: LUK 9:32
Text: But Peter and they that were with him were heavy with sleep: and when they were awake, they saw his glory, and the two men that stood with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0022e16-d028-40e6-bb97-f690543dd2c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: LUK 9:33
Text: And it came to pass, as they departed from him, Peter said unto Jesus, Master, it is good for us to be here: and let us make three tabernacles; one for thee, and one for Moses, and one for Elias: not knowing what he said.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3780f12-3204-4ba4-b6e7-f1ac46556a4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: LUK 9:34
Text: While he thus spake, there came a cloud, and overshadowed them: and they feared as they entered into the cloud.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef071978-195e-421c-9c6d-07e719e7ee9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: LUK 9:35
Text: And there came a voice out of the cloud, saying, This is my beloved Son: hear him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c1919aa-6ae2-4bed-9876-3dc5a2ac4f60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: LUK 9:36
Text: And when the voice was past, Jesus was found alone. And they kept it close, and told no man in those days any of those things which they had seen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4fedbc3-1512-400b-8237-9bf064c56f28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: LUK 9:37
Text: And it came to pass, that on the next day, when they were come down from the hill, much people met him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:025d4060-a55f-4e16-ba30-2b2ba9cdbe86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: LUK 9:38
Text: And, behold, a man of the company cried out, saying, Master, I beseech thee, look upon my son: for he is mine only child.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f355f0f-fe86-4268-8b9d-ef64df8e23c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: LUK 9:39
Text: And, lo, a spirit taketh him, and he suddenly crieth out; and it teareth him that he foameth again, and bruising him hardly departeth from him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f4ac719-ec4d-4782-a4c5-8c6a80bd62ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: LUK 9:40
Text: And I besought thy disciples to cast him out; and they could not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:027d40dc-1dff-4900-b942-a74e6c79112e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: LUK 9:41
Text: And Jesus answering said, O faithless and perverse generation, how long shall I be with you, and suffer you? Bring thy son hither.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af8842a4-8c30-4907-97fc-3bab1272f5ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: LUK 9:42
Text: And as he was yet a coming, the devil threw him down, and tare him. And Jesus rebuked the unclean spirit, and healed the child, and delivered him again to his father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45562fc4-0443-41ee-a0df-a76704b5aed3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: LUK 9:43
Text: And they were all amazed at the mighty power of God. But while they wondered every one at all things which Jesus did, he said unto his disciples,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afc80c3f-4858-4293-a343-fc18f02c87af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: LUK 9:44
Text: Let these sayings sink down into your ears: for the Son of man shall be delivered into the hands of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7613dbf-2ef7-4619-8d21-c2450ab758e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: LUK 9:45
Text: But they understood not this saying, and it was hid from them, that they perceived it not: and they feared to ask him of that saying.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d79686b7-f9b9-4140-9c65-11e62bd7a820>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: LUK 9:46
Text: Then there arose a reasoning among them, which of them should be greatest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
