Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: LUK 9:47
Text: And Jesus, perceiving the thought of their heart, took a child, and set him by him,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41df24e3-db1a-45f6-ac47-0c7561dd15fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: LUK 9:48
Text: And said unto them, Whosoever shall receive this child in my name receiveth me: and whosoever shall receive me receiveth him that sent me: for he that is least among you all, the same shall be great.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6cfa7b27-3746-42f1-83fc-2e7bdf471634>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: LUK 9:49
Text: And John answered and said, Master, we saw one casting out devils in thy name; and we forbad him, because he followeth not with us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1d5ded4-37df-4300-983c-24b804655118>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: LUK 9:50
Text: And Jesus said unto him, Forbid him not: for he that is not against us is for us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f2c1a08-468c-4010-857b-9daabb903599>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: LUK 9:51
Text: And it came to pass, when the time was come that he should be received up, he stedfastly set his face to go to Jerusalem,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:220d17e3-da18-4c75-9972-a2d73b13e263>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: LUK 9:52
Text: And sent messengers before his face: and they went, and entered into a village of the Samaritans, to make ready for him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:952ecac4-f035-4279-b2df-6a27816aeca6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: LUK 9:53
Text: And they did not receive him, because his face was as though he would go to Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85286f1c-3c64-4a51-a1f0-64f7388ecc04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: LUK 9:54
Text: And when his disciples James and John saw this, they said, Lord, wilt thou that we command fire to come down from heaven, and consume them, even as Elias did?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/55
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66543bde-37b2-45a8-a08c-bd174d824277>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: LUK 9:55
Text: But he turned, and rebuked them, and said, Ye know not what manner of spirit ye are of.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/56
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72aa0ec6-7485-43a2-977f-55f17c73ad62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: LUK 9:56
Text: For the Son of man is not come to destroy men’s lives, but to save them. And they went to another village.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/57
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e029162-44d6-43dc-9619-dfad58edc8fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: LUK 9:57
Text: And it came to pass, that, as they went in the way, a certain man said unto him, Lord, I will follow thee whithersoever thou goest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/58
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3dbf4b93-d564-4d39-9eda-977c6f6307de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: LUK 9:58
Text: And Jesus said unto him, Foxes have holes, and birds of the air have nests; but the Son of man hath not where to lay his head.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/59
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33838a47-f430-4ed0-9fc8-32a39dd5e9f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: LUK 9:59
Text: And he said unto another, Follow me. But he said, Lord, suffer me first to go and bury my father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/60
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aeb39ca2-569a-4a37-ab6b-75439943d21a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: LUK 9:60
Text: Jesus said unto him, Let the dead bury their dead: but go thou and preach the kingdom of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/61
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3b2da2e-22d5-4b7c-b47c-2ece754327cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: LUK 9:61
Text: And another also said, Lord, I will follow thee; but let me first go bid them farewell, which are at home at my house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/9/62
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1dca099b-f630-42ff-9885-f2d52471484e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: LUK 9:62
Text: And Jesus said unto him, No man, having put his hand to the plough, and looking back, is fit for the kingdom of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3355c078-d2ad-4871-920b-cd8522dc2a01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: LUK 10:1
Text: After these things the LORD appointed other seventy also, and sent them two and two before his face into every city and place, whither he himself would come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48bcafd9-2499-4b91-b071-303f20e7d9c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: LUK 10:2
Text: Therefore said he unto them, The harvest truly is great, but the labourers are few: pray ye therefore the Lord of the harvest, that he would send forth labourers into his harvest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96637ab0-b9a0-45f3-a8d2-80be150010c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: LUK 10:3
Text: Go your ways: behold, I send you forth as lambs among wolves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17921307-33a9-4408-b8ad-3c1a7e8ef65e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: LUK 10:4
Text: Carry neither purse, nor scrip, nor shoes: and salute no man by the way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0569da55-4447-47ca-acbf-003ab571471e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: LUK 10:5
Text: And into whatsoever house ye enter, first say, Peace be to this house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65195853-a084-4738-9f01-8512d259cd56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: LUK 10:6
Text: And if the son of peace be there, your peace shall rest upon it: if not, it shall turn to you again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36dec553-b932-4313-b40b-d4dd598ac8f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: LUK 10:7
Text: And in the same house remain, eating and drinking such things as they give: for the labourer is worthy of his hire. Go not from house to house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38df85fb-7871-4d6a-bf29-85ca5db32977>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: LUK 10:8
Text: And into whatsoever city ye enter, and they receive you, eat such things as are set before you:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b505688f-1f0d-42be-a84a-cd2031e8402f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: LUK 10:9
Text: And heal the sick that are therein, and say unto them, The kingdom of God is come nigh unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:797e505c-14a5-4031-b2e2-efe6ed0b75fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: LUK 10:10
Text: But into whatsoever city ye enter, and they receive you not, go your ways out into the streets of the same, and say,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5b169d1-427b-4ca8-a5ed-47320e7bc82c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: LUK 10:11
Text: Even the very dust of your city, which cleaveth on us, we do wipe off against you: notwithstanding be ye sure of this, that the kingdom of God is come nigh unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0cf25a6a-c922-41cf-841a-8cc65f2345f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: LUK 10:12
Text: But I say unto you, that it shall be more tolerable in that day for Sodom, than for that city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfbe7bec-c8c1-4f48-bf55-a0c0883a95a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: LUK 10:13
Text: Woe unto thee, Chorazin! woe unto thee, Bethsaida! for if the mighty works had been done in Tyre and Sidon, which have been done in you, they had a great while ago repented, sitting in sackcloth and ashes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a755bba4-37c8-4164-9cad-c2995a75dd7a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: LUK 10:14
Text: But it shall be more tolerable for Tyre and Sidon at the judgment, than for you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3fc6315c-d1fe-43e7-bb27-9f793e5ec597>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: LUK 10:15
Text: And thou, Capernaum, which art exalted to heaven, shalt be thrust down to hell.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6bc97491-2d2c-4309-84eb-da64ff5fa87c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: LUK 10:16
Text: He that heareth you heareth me; and he that despiseth you despiseth me; and he that despiseth me despiseth him that sent me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c67ee65f-cc51-458b-ace4-1a1800f4a156>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: LUK 10:17
Text: And the seventy returned again with joy, saying, Lord, even the devils are subject unto us through thy name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a206403-d9bd-476d-9a7f-8097f5c2d8cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: LUK 10:18
Text: And he said unto them, I beheld Satan as lightning fall from heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c7f388a-1edc-486f-af45-29c93b82a907>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: LUK 10:19
Text: Behold, I give unto you power to tread on serpents and scorpions, and over all the power of the enemy: and nothing shall by any means hurt you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d5f4880-76cf-4b39-aece-1814e7f3c21e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: LUK 10:20
Text: Notwithstanding in this rejoice not, that the spirits are subject unto you; but rather rejoice, because your names are written in heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52f0a028-a250-49dc-a5f3-6081ef1bb319>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 273

Reference: LUK 10:21
Text: In that hour Jesus rejoiced in spirit, and said, I thank thee, O Father, Lord of heaven and earth, that thou hast hid these things from the wise and prudent, and hast revealed them unto babes: even so, Father; for so it seemed good in thy sight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ffbb8c2-2fd1-4db5-ae7c-33b93a0bb0d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: LUK 10:22
Text: All things are delivered to me of my Father: and no man knoweth who the Son is, but the Father; and who the Father is, but the Son, and he to whom the Son will reveal him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51a39caf-d555-425f-a30e-45b794650064>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: LUK 10:23
Text: And he turned him unto his disciples, and said privately, Blessed are the eyes which see the things that ye see:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:695f9a01-589c-4237-a745-cf06e56d4411>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: LUK 10:24
Text: For I tell you, that many prophets and kings have desired to see those things which ye see, and have not seen them; and to hear those things which ye hear, and have not heard them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8fe1c456-0285-42f9-8dbe-987b7e6dc12e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: LUK 10:25
Text: And, behold, a certain lawyer stood up, and tempted him, saying, Master, what shall I do to inherit eternal life?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c4a754b-c1cc-4d6b-8b05-03b5d472ba7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: LUK 10:26
Text: He said unto him, What is written in the law? how readest thou?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a105179-ef1d-4cc8-9142-9c98c7f19554>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: LUK 10:27
Text: And he answering said, Thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy strength, and with all thy mind; and thy neighbour as thyself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8addd1c3-b871-4902-a8d2-51b3fd75e039>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: LUK 10:28
Text: And he said unto him, Thou hast answered right: this do, and thou shalt live.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b3c9e8b-76b3-4763-aa72-2ab5ed5e0662>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: LUK 10:29
Text: But he, willing to justify himself, said unto Jesus, And who is my neighbour?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddd14439-d314-4d85-9043-e2247a4fdbfe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: LUK 10:30
Text: And Jesus answering said, A certain man went down from Jerusalem to Jericho, and fell among thieves, which stripped him of his raiment, and wounded him, and departed, leaving him half dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fc5ce46-d092-4886-b92b-61131211bd30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: LUK 10:31
Text: And by chance there came down a certain priest that way: and when he saw him, he passed by on the other side.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:770b4e69-434f-4c9d-a732-931c73885460>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: LUK 10:32
Text: And likewise a Levite, when he was at the place, came and looked on him, and passed by on the other side.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f47d259-80e8-4a55-a777-4f1770a52f35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: LUK 10:33
Text: But a certain Samaritan, as he journeyed, came where he was: and when he saw him, he had compassion on him,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8044840d-093e-4bc2-acd2-7eaf01b4c9fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: LUK 10:34
Text: And went to him, and bound up his wounds, pouring in oil and wine, and set him on his own beast, and brought him to an inn, and took care of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03d923ac-7efb-4d23-8fa6-e5c73f1fb208>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: LUK 10:35
Text: And on the morrow when he departed, he took out two pence, and gave them to the host, and said unto him, Take care of him; and whatsoever thou spendest more, when I come again, I will repay thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56811e4a-31f3-4f83-9e46-d5f2452564fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: LUK 10:36
Text: Which now of these three, thinkest thou, was neighbour unto him that fell among the thieves?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:256e20d8-8ca1-4ff4-bd3e-bdc3073f8a2f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: LUK 10:37
Text: And he said, He that shewed mercy on him. Then said Jesus unto him, Go, and do thou likewise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c620e7e5-b2ec-499e-b726-07e68548a8aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: LUK 10:38
Text: Now it came to pass, as they went, that he entered into a certain village: and a certain woman named Martha received him into her house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0217b1b-3678-4454-9635-1bdda9373271>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: LUK 10:39
Text: And she had a sister called Mary, which also sat at Jesus’ feet, and heard his word.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4285883f-e60a-4727-b9ae-7b370b921d3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: LUK 10:40
Text: But Martha was cumbered about much serving, and came to him, and said, Lord, dost thou not care that my sister hath left me to serve alone? bid her therefore that she help me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfd330fd-db20-46a0-9062-3551c7e8a0a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: LUK 10:41
Text: And Jesus answered and said unto her, Martha, Martha, thou art careful and troubled about many things:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/10/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3966e5c4-a064-428b-ad9c-bf445e5dc9ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: LUK 10:42
Text: But one thing is needful: and Mary hath chosen that good part, which shall not be taken away from her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c526ddf-fe27-48eb-a5f1-5fdc48c4376f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: LUK 11:1
Text: And it came to pass, that, as he was praying in a certain place, when he ceased, one of his disciples said unto him, Lord, teach us to pray, as John also taught his disciples.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5cf36c5f-8f3e-4100-ab17-4028220562fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: LUK 11:2
Text: And he said unto them, When ye pray, say, Our Father which art in heaven, Hallowed be thy name. Thy kingdom come. Thy will be done, as in heaven, so in earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f0972ff-af58-461d-bc64-f2db0fb8bfe4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 62

Reference: LUK 11:3
Text: Give us day by day our daily bread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfc55171-a4c4-4555-aad7-975b0f12491f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: LUK 11:4
Text: And forgive us our sins; for we also forgive every one that is indebted to us. And lead us not into temptation; but deliver us from evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f0b7cca-a75a-4bf7-8630-f90817e63c0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: LUK 11:5
Text: And he said unto them, Which of you shall have a friend, and shall go unto him at midnight, and say unto him, Friend, lend me three loaves;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0211c8c-ed36-4d84-bcbb-79c4032abb62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: LUK 11:6
Text: For a friend of mine in his journey is come to me, and I have nothing to set before him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f80f413-f08c-489f-a439-c55390055068>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: LUK 11:7
Text: And he from within shall answer and say, Trouble me not: the door is now shut, and my children are with me in bed; I cannot rise and give thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a79fe9d0-b0be-456e-ad73-ac0fafad78c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: LUK 11:8
Text: I say unto you, Though he will not rise and give him, because he is his friend, yet because of his importunity he will rise and give him as many as he needeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3cd622d-94cf-47db-ac66-d8b9dda78269>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: LUK 11:9
Text: And I say unto you, Ask, and it shall be given you; seek, and ye shall find; knock, and it shall be opened unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3999e500-1960-4297-ac91-f5dae33fb133>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: LUK 11:10
Text: For every one that asketh receiveth; and he that seeketh findeth; and to him that knocketh it shall be opened.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:803f6907-bb4d-426c-967c-0016c19f177f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: LUK 11:11
Text: If a son shall ask bread of any of you that is a father, will he give him a stone? or if he ask a fish, will he for a fish give him a serpent?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c8bc0ed-1405-46ef-a1e8-967ef2ce2ad1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: LUK 11:12
Text: Or if he shall ask an egg, will he offer him a scorpion?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f195fd35-b86e-4296-904c-c436d6ee8e25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: LUK 11:13
Text: If ye then, being evil, know how to give good gifts unto your children: how much more shall your heavenly Father give the Holy Spirit to them that ask him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c19c881-6d69-46cc-8642-70811c1d626c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: LUK 11:14
Text: And he was casting out a devil, and it was dumb. And it came to pass, when the devil was gone out, the dumb spake; and the people wondered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ed36f7a-e8fd-4020-9ad3-ec79afe6a30b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: LUK 11:15
Text: But some of them said, He casteth out devils through Beelzebub the chief of the devils.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3645a564-23e1-4b86-bd3e-6ff7c93cc753>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: LUK 11:16
Text: And others, tempting him, sought of him a sign from heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e41afda-a85f-4017-86a3-4348b4400c20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: LUK 11:17
Text: But he, knowing their thoughts, said unto them, Every kingdom divided against itself is brought to desolation; and a house divided against a house falleth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45e62163-28e5-48c9-8712-0741e53e6ad8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: LUK 11:18
Text: If Satan also be divided against himself, how shall his kingdom stand? because ye say that I cast out devils through Beelzebub.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e6b9ea4-76d9-4e0e-8576-da81ec59bb81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: LUK 11:19
Text: And if I by Beelzebub cast out devils, by whom do your sons cast them out? therefore shall they be your judges.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1300d3b-a084-4326-ac7f-183d508eb254>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: LUK 11:20
Text: But if I with the finger of God cast out devils, no doubt the kingdom of God is come upon you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13b92f1f-871d-430c-9263-421b1d0507d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: LUK 11:21
Text: When a strong man armed keepeth his palace, his goods are in peace:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b51e3ec3-b123-40ea-9711-54dbcf8fce25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: LUK 11:22
Text: But when a stronger than he shall come upon him, and overcome him, he taketh from him all his armour wherein he trusted, and divideth his spoils.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d8d1a21-e2cc-4d37-b25e-4dcb352985cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: LUK 11:23
Text: He that is not with me is against me: and he that gathereth not with me scattereth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a5d80e6-4dce-4352-8a52-1078ea296804>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: LUK 11:24
Text: When the unclean spirit is gone out of a man, he walketh through dry places, seeking rest; and finding none, he saith, I will return unto my house whence I came out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd0e21ce-ca4f-4b8b-83d0-afcf6e902084>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: LUK 11:25
Text: And when he cometh, he findeth it swept and garnished.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ebc1920-8bb4-4644-9269-c0773b312ded>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: LUK 11:26
Text: Then goeth he, and taketh to him seven other spirits more wicked than himself; and they enter in, and dwell there: and the last state of that man is worse than the first.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40b8ee2b-549e-4cf4-b472-fba5ea4b90b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: LUK 11:27
Text: And it came to pass, as he spake these things, a certain woman of the company lifted up her voice, and said unto him, Blessed is the womb that bare thee, and the paps which thou hast sucked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:025a167b-6265-4f86-9bd9-27ccadbf9599>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: LUK 11:28
Text: But he said, Yea rather, blessed are they that hear the word of God, and keep it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:babd0f20-e386-412b-bc07-39f688c30729>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: LUK 11:29
Text: And when the people were gathered thick together, he began to say, This is an evil generation: they seek a sign; and there shall no sign be given it, but the sign of Jonas the prophet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8aff6aca-3e85-4483-938b-d0f79f38bdf7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: LUK 11:30
Text: For as Jonas was a sign unto the Ninevites, so shall also the Son of man be to this generation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:198d9730-256d-40a1-b3a9-8595c0e5e3f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 255

Reference: LUK 11:31
Text: The queen of the south shall rise up in the judgment with the men of this generation, and condemn them: for she came from the utmost parts of the earth to hear the wisdom of Solomon; and, behold, a greater than Solomon is here.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9cc89a9-6d67-4ab4-a8c6-17a04f44c23c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: LUK 11:32
Text: The men of Nineve shall rise up in the judgment with this generation, and shall condemn it: for they repented at the preaching of Jonas; and, behold, a greater than Jonas is here.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67e59a86-b73b-435c-8ff2-43e67bed15f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: LUK 11:33
Text: No man, when he hath lighted a candle, putteth it in a secret place, neither under a bushel, but on a candlestick, that they which come in may see the light.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9ac044a-916f-44a5-a932-deda44e4ccb7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: LUK 11:34
Text: The light of the body is the eye: therefore when thine eye is single, thy whole body also is full of light; but when thine eye is evil, thy body also is full of darkness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b54ce335-2c84-4f6c-aa92-d1a7b13f26d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: LUK 11:35
Text: Take heed therefore that the light which is in thee be not darkness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85b4f646-e452-4c04-858a-4183192ec4a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: LUK 11:36
Text: If thy whole body therefore be full of light, having no part dark, the whole shall be full of light, as when the bright shining of a candle doth give thee light.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f58e19e-6ff2-4027-9c5c-76dcddfc6b50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: LUK 11:37
Text: And as he spake, a certain Pharisee besought him to dine with him: and he went in, and sat down to meat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1364bee0-313e-4302-8b40-c0e85fa5e79d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: LUK 11:38
Text: And when the Pharisee saw it, he marvelled that he had not first washed before dinner.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:932b809b-8ca4-4033-bfdf-0ddad0a4a4e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: LUK 11:39
Text: And the Lord said unto him, Now do ye Pharisees make clean the outside of the cup and the platter; but your inward part is full of ravening and wickedness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5c7c0bc-78ee-4415-97c1-e6dc5647f18b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: LUK 11:40
Text: Ye fools, did not he that made that which is without make that which is within also?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6101b87e-7c0f-4cf2-a0de-4f7ebeeb7d5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: LUK 11:41
Text: But rather give alms of such things as ye have; and, behold, all things are clean unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a75fb6ef-58c6-48cf-9ebc-c614b1b08fdb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: LUK 11:42
Text: But woe unto you, Pharisees! for ye tithe mint and rue and all manner of herbs, and pass over judgment and the love of God: these ought ye to have done, and not to leave the other undone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81a8d15b-5caa-4fc9-b4e8-975fcbd69c01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: LUK 11:43
Text: Woe unto you, Pharisees! for ye love the uppermost seats in the synagogues, and greetings in the markets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d44772d1-3bf4-49c3-bee3-bfed74e3b553>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: LUK 11:44
Text: Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye are as graves which appear not, and the men that walk over them are not aware of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d9a38b0-2191-49a9-bac6-81a85cb2341a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: LUK 11:45
Text: Then answered one of the lawyers, and said unto him, Master, thus saying thou reproachest us also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20ee0334-7601-42bf-bdfd-d7c074443cb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: LUK 11:46
Text: And he said, Woe unto you also, ye lawyers! for ye lade men with burdens grievous to be borne, and ye yourselves touch not the burdens with one of your fingers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61897cdc-7c72-47e4-bbb4-e558a39ffc7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: LUK 11:47
Text: Woe unto you! for ye build the sepulchres of the prophets, and your fathers killed them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1823a6b9-7dc9-4aa4-bc6b-3dd8efc0a076>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: LUK 11:48
Text: Truly ye bear witness that ye allow the deeds of your fathers: for they indeed killed them, and ye build their sepulchres.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35214217-ab65-4f2c-b9d3-75fdb335e045>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: LUK 11:49
Text: Therefore also said the wisdom of God, I will send them prophets and apostles, and some of them they shall slay and persecute:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5a0334f-308a-4111-bde0-35d585b90191>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: LUK 11:50
Text: That the blood of all the prophets, which was shed from the foundation of the world, may be required of this generation;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b853f22a-0064-4c6b-ad2c-c327110877f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: LUK 11:51
Text: From the blood of Abel unto the blood of Zacharias which perished between the altar and the temple: verily I say unto you, It shall be required of this generation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3fccc402-7b9a-4e3d-b223-219d2bf298ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: LUK 11:52
Text: Woe unto you, lawyers! for ye have taken away the key of knowledge: ye entered not in yourselves, and them that were entering in ye hindered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:993baded-d04e-42a5-a9e3-4aaec38ff747>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: LUK 11:53
Text: And as he said these things unto them, the scribes and the Pharisees began to urge him vehemently, and to provoke him to speak of many things:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/11/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:591e2f3b-4163-4bb3-bd10-c37897e3e841>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: LUK 11:54
Text: Laying wait for him, and seeking to catch something out of his mouth, that they might accuse him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc5ed9b5-c1b9-49ee-844c-dc205f4879dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: LUK 12:1
Text: In the mean time, when there were gathered together an innumerable multitude of people, insomuch that they trode one upon another, he began to say unto his disciples first of all, Beware ye of the leaven of the Pharisees, which is hypocrisy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56cb5fe5-3d32-4d69-9e4b-7cc30d09aed7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: LUK 12:2
Text: For there is nothing covered, that shall not be revealed; neither hid, that shall not be known.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c76be1c2-7883-415d-aa30-62401e675bf6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: LUK 12:3
Text: Therefore whatsoever ye have spoken in darkness shall be heard in the light; and that which ye have spoken in the ear in closets shall be proclaimed upon the housetops.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d92c7bf-86ac-40f4-83c6-294db7a24eb9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: LUK 12:4
Text: And I say unto you my friends, Be not afraid of them that kill the body, and after that have no more that they can do.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e75c5b34-b947-4774-ba24-80b990711018>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: LUK 12:5
Text: But I will forewarn you whom ye shall fear: Fear him, which after he hath killed hath power to cast into hell; yea, I say unto you, Fear him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e38a2dc-3bb3-4422-8944-688a02cfa483>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: LUK 12:6
Text: Are not five sparrows sold for two farthings, and not one of them is forgotten before God?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16a34d51-87f4-44bc-b75f-124365f42ad8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: LUK 12:7
Text: But even the very hairs of your head are all numbered. Fear not therefore: ye are of more value than many sparrows.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7421cd6b-c5f4-4d79-9712-6fc6653ffa14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: LUK 12:8
Text: Also I say unto you, Whosoever shall confess me before men, him shall the Son of man also confess before the angels of God:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b1db0f6-bcc8-4b6d-8df9-9ff658c6900d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: LUK 12:9
Text: But he that denieth me before men shall be denied before the angels of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31dad97f-3699-4cb8-826e-1a001598f802>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: LUK 12:10
Text: And whosoever shall speak a word against the Son of man, it shall be forgiven him: but unto him that blasphemeth against the Holy Ghost it shall not be forgiven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a1ee859-7e3c-477e-9f76-411517b3a1fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: LUK 12:11
Text: And when they bring you unto the synagogues, and unto magistrates, and powers, take ye no thought how or what thing ye shall answer, or what ye shall say:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55348425-022e-470a-bd82-026b1b4059fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: LUK 12:12
Text: For the Holy Ghost shall teach you in the same hour what ye ought to say.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e72a513-e114-471f-9ec5-c8256aaed1c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: LUK 12:13
Text: And one of the company said unto him, Master, speak to my brother, that he divide the inheritance with me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb8badc4-7a2e-4292-ada9-6eba58becff2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: LUK 12:14
Text: And he said unto him, Man, who made me a judge or a divider over you?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2a064e3-5d99-41ba-9dc8-e3fc4749524b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: LUK 12:15
Text: And he said unto them, Take heed, and beware of covetousness: for a man’s life consisteth not in the abundance of the things which he possesseth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b862dc0a-e4a7-4ad6-96d1-ab39dad32794>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: LUK 12:16
Text: And he spake a parable unto them, saying, The ground of a certain rich man brought forth plentifully:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00cc26aa-7802-4242-ad32-3eccb45711b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: LUK 12:17
Text: And he thought within himself, saying, What shall I do, because I have no room where to bestow my fruits?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b364c6ef-478a-444b-88fa-f52c93f9d701>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: LUK 12:18
Text: And he said, This will I do: I will pull down my barns, and build greater; and there will I bestow all my fruits and my goods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9587e315-283e-4400-a916-312b3f9d26a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: LUK 12:19
Text: And I will say to my soul, Soul, thou hast much goods laid up for many years; take thine ease, eat, drink, and be merry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bd72d18-360c-4195-b175-91f237f6c478>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: LUK 12:20
Text: But God said unto him, Thou fool, this night thy soul shall be required of thee: then whose shall those things be, which thou hast provided?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45f46089-14a9-4a82-b762-34f5c4e401ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: LUK 12:21
Text: So is he that layeth up treasure for himself, and is not rich toward God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b545ac76-88bc-41ea-93fe-861e7854c1a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: LUK 12:22
Text: And he said unto his disciples, Therefore I say unto you, Take no thought for your life, what ye shall eat; neither for the body, what ye shall put on.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:966c2816-999f-4901-9f40-dfc875890b92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: LUK 12:23
Text: The life is more than meat, and the body is more than raiment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37e29933-4395-4a62-bc5a-bb7ef3d31d10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: LUK 12:24
Text: Consider the ravens: for they neither sow nor reap; which neither have storehouse nor barn; and God feedeth them: how much more are ye better than the fowls?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:993f08cd-3206-4ff7-877f-e6572ffaaa7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: LUK 12:25
Text: And which of you with taking thought can add to his stature one cubit?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0bb1817-811a-42c8-83af-0ce810caf1d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: LUK 12:26
Text: If ye then be not able to do that thing which is least, why take ye thought for the rest?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40bbdf78-b097-4987-b220-15f49cd24730>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: LUK 12:27
Text: Consider the lilies how they grow: they toil not, they spin not; and yet I say unto you, that Solomon in all his glory was not arrayed like one of these.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:395049c1-fae5-4044-a2d7-d18f99ea8c16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: LUK 12:28
Text: If then God so clothe the grass, which is to day in the field, and to morrow is cast into the oven; how much more will he clothe you, O ye of little faith?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f63dbbac-8820-4235-aa9c-4a7a897a060f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: LUK 12:29
Text: And seek not ye what ye shall eat, or what ye shall drink, neither be ye of doubtful mind.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fb0c210-8231-48e3-8b48-3da568026793>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: LUK 12:30
Text: For all these things do the nations of the world seek after: and your Father knoweth that ye have need of these things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:10ce8246-5e3f-401c-b706-ed889718897b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: LUK 12:31
Text: But rather seek ye the kingdom of God; and all these things shall be added unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc5061bc-5c13-4f9d-9a6a-1b378e80224e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: LUK 12:32
Text: Fear not, little flock; for it is your Father’s good pleasure to give you the kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2acd8817-fa8e-4d25-becd-bda730b20c8e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: LUK 12:33
Text: Sell that ye have, and give alms; provide yourselves bags which wax not old, a treasure in the heavens that faileth not, where no thief approacheth, neither moth corrupteth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88a10022-4954-472f-b9bf-5f4e63206d6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: LUK 12:34
Text: For where your treasure is, there will your heart be also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5364fb54-d2e7-4e7c-a382-85f79d4f84f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: LUK 12:35
Text: Let your loins be girded about, and your lights burning;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8824e3a-5203-4dd9-972e-b2e504c1299f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: LUK 12:36
Text: And ye yourselves like unto men that wait for their lord, when he will return from the wedding; that when he cometh and knocketh, they may open unto him immediately.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83d5e367-d7c9-41a2-a05a-89239f15aca5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: LUK 12:37
Text: Blessed are those servants, whom the lord when he cometh shall find watching: verily I say unto you, that he shall gird himself, and make them to sit down to meat, and will come forth and serve them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed3f836d-955c-44b4-aae4-1d92dc97539e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: LUK 12:38
Text: And if he shall come in the second watch, or come in the third watch, and find them so, blessed are those servants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b485c17-e621-4b41-9bd3-b992c918a44b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: LUK 12:39
Text: And this know, that if the goodman of the house had known what hour the thief would come, he would have watched, and not have suffered his house to be broken through.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66109515-0474-4908-b8cb-fa42abadd66f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: LUK 12:40
Text: Be ye therefore ready also: for the Son of man cometh at an hour when ye think not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d8b7176-a8e2-49a0-964f-15d20f197488>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: LUK 12:41
Text: Then Peter said unto him, Lord, speakest thou this parable unto us, or even to all?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60ed3f47-7e99-4878-9255-5ac391e64a49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: LUK 12:42
Text: And the Lord said, Who then is that faithful and wise steward, whom his lord shall make ruler over his household, to give them their portion of meat in due season?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2d1f1d2-fe49-4fe2-aa78-a8ba32027ac2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: LUK 12:43
Text: Blessed is that servant, whom his lord when he cometh shall find so doing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7dbb04ba-aa7b-4810-ba4f-8d19de62e756>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: LUK 12:44
Text: Of a truth I say unto you, that he will make him ruler over all that he hath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5502c1f-7a7b-4e09-a27a-0c8f671048b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: LUK 12:45
Text: But and if that servant say in his heart, My lord delayeth his coming; and shall begin to beat the menservants and maidens, and to eat and drink, and to be drunken;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d0ca0fa-0318-4eba-b17a-a55e9d8a4200>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: LUK 12:46
Text: The lord of that servant will come in a day when he looketh not for him, and at an hour when he is not aware, and will cut him in sunder, and will appoint him his portion with the unbelievers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:865e56cb-91b0-43c2-89f7-7164d81390ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: LUK 12:47
Text: And that servant, which knew his lord’s will, and prepared not himself, neither did according to his will, shall be beaten with many stripes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96118ce5-7336-4573-bc55-965d7da40b3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: LUK 12:48
Text: But he that knew not, and did commit things worthy of stripes, shall be beaten with few stripes. For unto whomsoever much is given, of him shall be much required: and to whom men have committed much, of him they will ask the more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe4618d8-2c38-4dd6-afbe-a3c0e788e2dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: LUK 12:49
Text: I am come to send fire on the earth; and what will I, if it be already kindled?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65248b48-6b90-42e6-beac-e949553f5851>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: LUK 12:50
Text: But I have a baptism to be baptized with; and how am I straitened till it be accomplished!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe2940e1-fa00-4dbd-b7d0-11f49ba51d61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: LUK 12:51
Text: Suppose ye that I am come to give peace on earth? I tell you, Nay; but rather division:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c65fc16e-661c-4dbb-8a8c-64bb9ba2d562>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: LUK 12:52
Text: For from henceforth there shall be five in one house divided, three against two, and two against three.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b72d8d2d-b377-40f3-9b3f-56c4381ebbc0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: LUK 12:53
Text: The father shall be divided against the son, and the son against the father; the mother against the daughter, and the daughter against the mother; the mother in law against her daughter in law, and the daughter in law against her mother in law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f91cff8-40e5-4588-9215-c2b08afb53e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: LUK 12:54
Text: And he said also to the people, When ye see a cloud rise out of the west, straightway ye say, There cometh a shower; and so it is.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/55
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e73257b4-d5a4-4687-a879-2aed460502d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: LUK 12:55
Text: And when ye see the south wind blow, ye say, There will be heat; and it cometh to pass.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/56
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a33dac85-5be0-4cf4-84b2-bf381b9b5551>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: LUK 12:56
Text: Ye hypocrites, ye can discern the face of the sky and of the earth; but how is it that ye do not discern this time?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/57
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ed6e18b-8327-400b-a280-ee5b5e19b71a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: LUK 12:57
Text: Yea, and why even of yourselves judge ye not what is right?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/58
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ce22b0b-4458-464c-9630-a7793b225cd2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: LUK 12:58
Text: When thou goest with thine adversary to the magistrate, as thou art in the way, give diligence that thou mayest be delivered from him; lest he hale thee to the judge, and the judge deliver thee to the officer, and the officer cast thee into prison.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/12/59
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edd8b7c0-53e9-4740-9961-4e1aff62a5cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: LUK 12:59
Text: I tell thee, thou shalt not depart thence, till thou hast paid the very last mite.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/13/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ff5cca0-aaba-4eed-9e82-02b205ed3938>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: LUK 13:1
Text: There were present at that season some that told him of the Galilaeans, whose blood Pilate had mingled with their sacrifices.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/13/2
