Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: LUK 13:6
Text: He spake also this parable; A certain man had a fig tree planted in his vineyard; and he came and sought fruit thereon, and found none.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/13/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f6442f2-5cc3-4d17-9da2-d9731ca55aba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: LUK 13:7
Text: Then said he unto the dresser of his vineyard, Behold, these three years I come seeking fruit on this fig tree, and find none: cut it down; why cumbereth it the ground?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/13/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:536adfc3-e379-4d28-ae43-3b3c6573d350>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: LUK 13:8
Text: And he answering said unto him, Lord, let it alone this year also, till I shall dig about it, and dung it:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/13/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
