Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: LUK 13:23
Text: Then said one unto him, Lord, are there few that be saved? And he said unto them,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/13/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b74f7fed-6d8f-482e-98c3-5ef8c7c142a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: LUK 13:24
Text: Strive to enter in at the strait gate: for many, I say unto you, will seek to enter in, and shall not be able.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/13/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0421ec7f-34d6-4613-be23-94fe1ec0d604>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: LUK 13:25
Text: When once the master of the house is risen up, and hath shut to the door, and ye begin to stand without, and to knock at the door, saying, Lord, Lord, open unto us; and he shall answer and say unto you, I know you not whence ye are:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/13/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2029617-00c1-4d57-bd7d-93f95774677a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: LUK 13:26
Text: Then shall ye begin to say, We have eaten and drunk in thy presence, and thou hast taught in our streets.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/13/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bd95686-f181-4b0c-b7f3-fa958f1803a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: LUK 13:27
Text: But he shall say, I tell you, I know you not whence ye are; depart from me, all ye workers of iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/13/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
