Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: LUK 14:2
Text: And, behold, there was a certain man before him which had the dropsy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02e7d5b0-d113-41b2-9061-0cfe588a167f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: LUK 14:3
Text: And Jesus answering spake unto the lawyers and Pharisees, saying, Is it lawful to heal on the sabbath day?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:054a0f32-a2ee-458d-85ff-fc00528159f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: LUK 14:4
Text: And they held their peace. And he took him, and healed him, and let him go;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2caea2e-e107-4151-835c-b68692e9ab7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: LUK 14:5
Text: And answered them, saying, Which of you shall have an ass or an ox fallen into a pit, and will not straightway pull him out on the sabbath day?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02c67930-d685-49d6-9404-baf538893e0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: LUK 14:6
Text: And they could not answer him again to these things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:109e53d4-bf88-4d64-8a7c-1f3a1541ce6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: LUK 14:7
Text: And he put forth a parable to those which were bidden, when he marked how they chose out the chief rooms; saying unto them,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ac33ab2-12d1-4b48-b67b-ffd7ca32126b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: LUK 14:8
Text: When thou art bidden of any man to a wedding, sit not down in the highest room; lest a more honourable man than thou be bidden of him;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79df5fb3-1b8e-4080-8145-cec3406abc60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: LUK 14:9
Text: And he that bade thee and him come and say to thee, Give this man place; and thou begin with shame to take the lowest room.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c221b35-6c26-4c5d-8504-c84abfb2008c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: LUK 14:10
Text: But when thou art bidden, go and sit down in the lowest room; that when he that bade thee cometh, he may say unto thee, Friend, go up higher: then shalt thou have worship in the presence of them that sit at meat with thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5fdec459-d6e2-4d02-b28c-8cdb66bfc0de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: LUK 14:11
Text: For whosoever exalteth himself shall be abased; and he that humbleth himself shall be exalted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc86ca2c-64b7-4a8b-a7ca-903b77bc33cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: LUK 14:12
Text: Then said he also to him that bade him, When thou makest a dinner or a supper, call not thy friends, nor thy brethren, neither thy kinsmen, nor thy rich neighbours; lest they also bid thee again, and a recompence be made thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2eca39d-1adc-4d49-a35b-b65253de3641>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: LUK 14:13
Text: But when thou makest a feast, call the poor, the maimed, the lame, the blind:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddd298ce-5e94-49f4-984c-8cfda21c945b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: LUK 14:14
Text: And thou shalt be blessed; for they cannot recompense thee: for thou shalt be recompensed at the resurrection of the just.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0edef2d2-b1eb-4bbb-a9ec-35747e6e2129>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: LUK 14:15
Text: And when one of them that sat at meat with him heard these things, he said unto him, Blessed is he that shall eat bread in the kingdom of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0757c056-da0e-42c5-acdf-70c25dd765e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: LUK 14:16
Text: Then said he unto him, A certain man made a great supper, and bade many:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f66f8b07-c3f3-4c1e-b06a-0edf24ecbdd1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: LUK 14:17
Text: And sent his servant at supper time to say to them that were bidden, Come; for all things are now ready.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e6297ee-33a5-4b58-ae2b-10f382e924fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: LUK 14:18
Text: And they all with one consent began to make excuse. The first said unto him, I have bought a piece of ground, and I must needs go and see it: I pray thee have me excused.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f147988-3049-41a2-9e2e-391bb1ca6132>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: LUK 14:19
Text: And another said, I have bought five yoke of oxen, and I go to prove them: I pray thee have me excused.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ecc700a5-4bb7-4f8c-9e60-18f664d15a49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: LUK 14:20
Text: And another said, I have married a wife, and therefore I cannot come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0eee077-7b77-420e-aac6-894a8a52c6b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 275

Reference: LUK 14:21
Text: So that servant came, and shewed his lord these things. Then the master of the house being angry said to his servant, Go out quickly into the streets and lanes of the city, and bring in hither the poor, and the maimed, and the halt, and the blind.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:609c2017-caac-41cb-ab42-af5ffb5609bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: LUK 14:22
Text: And the servant said, Lord, it is done as thou hast commanded, and yet there is room.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:726273c5-4eb0-4458-ac26-ce06cc5a010d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: LUK 14:23
Text: And the lord said unto the servant, Go out into the highways and hedges, and compel them to come in, that my house may be filled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf0b2d7f-1072-43d7-9ae6-a1aa30c72f81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: LUK 14:24
Text: For I say unto you, That none of those men which were bidden shall taste of my supper.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3afbbb47-7b18-4790-9dee-42d96afa9a1e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: LUK 14:25
Text: And there went great multitudes with him: and he turned, and said unto them,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d620c74c-9324-414c-b2ec-72a572aa0d5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: LUK 14:26
Text: If any man come to me, and hate not his father, and mother, and wife, and children, and brethren, and sisters, yea, and his own life also, he cannot be my disciple.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd82ce94-8c46-482a-93af-ae2183367463>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: LUK 14:27
Text: And whosoever doth not bear his cross, and come after me, cannot be my disciple.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75e67c7e-62e8-471a-a024-62bf7c61591b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: LUK 14:28
Text: For which of you, intending to build a tower, sitteth not down first, and counteth the cost, whether he have sufficient to finish it?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93f49d9a-8744-4a9b-b886-0d128b742514>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: LUK 14:29
Text: Lest haply, after he hath laid the foundation, and is not able to finish it, all that behold it begin to mock him,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fb5183e-6ba8-4ebf-bbfd-4efe47567367>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: LUK 14:30
Text: Saying, This man began to build, and was not able to finish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:56f9f69c-af3d-40b0-9300-c86d5fac135e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: LUK 14:31
Text: Or what king, going to make war against another king, sitteth not down first, and consulteth whether he be able with ten thousand to meet him that cometh against him with twenty thousand?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bae794c7-9a84-487d-8b21-16ea1e4c2ddd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: LUK 14:32
Text: Or else, while the other is yet a great way off, he sendeth an ambassage, and desireth conditions of peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6fddb046-5677-4eee-becc-87711a602e86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: LUK 14:33
Text: So likewise, whosoever he be of you that forsaketh not all that he hath, he cannot be my disciple.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3046a7f2-88f1-4fcf-9d5c-eb87bc709a85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: LUK 14:34
Text: Salt is good: but if the salt have lost his savour, wherewith shall it be seasoned?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/14/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d43e6e9-80ac-4828-bc27-e73cb7bf25a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: LUK 14:35
Text: It is neither fit for the land, nor yet for the dunghill; but men cast it out. He that hath ears to hear, let him hear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32d7a835-e29a-43d9-a942-f6d76efe2398>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: LUK 15:1
Text: Then drew near unto him all the publicans and sinners for to hear him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93fda9cd-18a6-417b-b11b-d4fd1537651c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: LUK 15:2
Text: And the Pharisees and scribes murmured, saying, This man receiveth sinners, and eateth with them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbb38cc3-3529-4caa-ae3a-a276ece8cee4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 71

Reference: LUK 15:3
Text: And he spake this parable unto them, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ee82385-93fc-40aa-9064-8b2cf0e1209e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: LUK 15:4
Text: What man of you, having an hundred sheep, if he lose one of them, doth not leave the ninety and nine in the wilderness, and go after that which is lost, until he find it?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ab9ae43-a0e4-411d-b54a-443b9b0ce75f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: LUK 15:5
Text: And when he hath found it, he layeth it on his shoulders, rejoicing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38952821-8681-4f06-aa9b-68733fa069cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: LUK 15:6
Text: And when he cometh home, he calleth together his friends and neighbours, saying unto them, Rejoice with me; for I have found my sheep which was lost.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6300374-5ce8-4499-a213-af6d38eeaf43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: LUK 15:7
Text: I say unto you, that likewise joy shall be in heaven over one sinner that repenteth, more than over ninety and nine just persons, which need no repentance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c938997-d84c-4a9d-a8a6-041a4f205b40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: LUK 15:8
Text: Either what woman having ten pieces of silver, if she lose one piece, doth not light a candle, and sweep the house, and seek diligently till she find it?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3c2379d-d89c-4057-ba96-6ce350fc94c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: LUK 15:9
Text: And when she hath found it, she calleth her friends and her neighbours together, saying, Rejoice with me; for I have found the piece which I had lost.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cdd633d7-a544-4b11-a881-1be3e2808974>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: LUK 15:10
Text: Likewise, I say unto you, there is joy in the presence of the angels of God over one sinner that repenteth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:874f4f4f-bf3a-4759-80bd-36289ea96356>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 68

Reference: LUK 15:11
Text: And he said, A certain man had two sons:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bcbe65d9-503a-4b6e-a019-9ef6cd34ab42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: LUK 15:12
Text: And the younger of them said to his father, Father, give me the portion of goods that falleth to me. And he divided unto them his living.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07bbe689-facf-4adc-9b6c-d85aa7c6a618>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: LUK 15:13
Text: And not many days after the younger son gathered all together, and took his journey into a far country, and there wasted his substance with riotous living.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2081c1a1-d347-4173-9303-45fc71c4b5ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: LUK 15:14
Text: And when he had spent all, there arose a mighty famine in that land; and he began to be in want.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de32bfdb-7e79-47fc-aa7c-579364be90a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: LUK 15:15
Text: And he went and joined himself to a citizen of that country; and he sent him into his fields to feed swine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf2e7437-95fe-4d6e-ad98-7e97e43731ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: LUK 15:16
Text: And he would fain have filled his belly with the husks that the swine did eat: and no man gave unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff8dd012-0131-4512-8b47-5767a9be411c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: LUK 15:17
Text: And when he came to himself, he said, How many hired servants of my father’s have bread enough and to spare, and I perish with hunger!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6cc350cd-8a4c-4390-9445-e942436ba9bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: LUK 15:18
Text: I will arise and go to my father, and will say unto him, Father, I have sinned against heaven, and before thee,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5896214-0b53-41a4-b85d-3850d7065a84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: LUK 15:19
Text: And am no more worthy to be called thy son: make me as one of thy hired servants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8aece51b-6145-4883-9ea8-b2595773d644>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: LUK 15:20
Text: And he arose, and came to his father. But when he was yet a great way off, his father saw him, and had compassion, and ran, and fell on his neck, and kissed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:197e3234-bbc2-472b-a2c9-ced8bd09208f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: LUK 15:21
Text: And the son said unto him, Father, I have sinned against heaven, and in thy sight, and am no more worthy to be called thy son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:328b68cb-40be-431c-b223-0403700ec2aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: LUK 15:22
Text: But the father said to his servants, Bring forth the best robe, and put it on him; and put a ring on his hand, and shoes on his feet:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cbc290b-a3fa-4baf-8cd7-e1d20405dc08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: LUK 15:23
Text: And bring hither the fatted calf, and kill it; and let us eat, and be merry:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3e5405f-c113-410e-95ec-21d1cdc9045c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: LUK 15:24
Text: For this my son was dead, and is alive again; he was lost, and is found. And they began to be merry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:55854b6c-76ad-4018-9625-108d9cf034aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: LUK 15:25
Text: Now his elder son was in the field: and as he came and drew nigh to the house, he heard musick and dancing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d17379a5-1ac6-4e88-a1da-5a2f6ea067ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: LUK 15:26
Text: And he called one of the servants, and asked what these things meant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffe6c6e5-1f77-4d7d-8fb6-09d7d00055c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: LUK 15:27
Text: And he said unto him, Thy brother is come; and thy father hath killed the fatted calf, because he hath received him safe and sound.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:048b5534-afcf-483a-a70b-9ea8646c7923>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: LUK 15:28
Text: And he was angry, and would not go in: therefore came his father out, and intreated him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:919f095d-e1d4-4150-b204-fc9180ca720b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: LUK 15:29
Text: And he answering said to his father, Lo, these many years do I serve thee, neither transgressed I at any time thy commandment: and yet thou never gavest me a kid, that I might make merry with my friends:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02884b4b-0012-415c-8da8-cf3ba46c93df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: LUK 15:30
Text: But as soon as this thy son was come, which hath devoured thy living with harlots, thou hast killed for him the fatted calf.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:747159b5-6117-4d33-acd4-89dc753cd59c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: LUK 15:31
Text: And he said unto him, Son, thou art ever with me, and all that I have is thine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/15/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1789f10-dda1-42b6-a447-5c488d9b0c1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: LUK 15:32
Text: It was meet that we should make merry, and be glad: for this thy brother was dead, and is alive again; and was lost, and is found.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5d058b7-980a-478c-84d6-2a5a3005c9cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: LUK 16:1
Text: And he said also unto his disciples, There was a certain rich man, which had a steward; and the same was accused unto him that he had wasted his goods.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee3f6170-1426-4e63-9113-0139857fb9b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: LUK 16:2
Text: And he called him, and said unto him, How is it that I hear this of thee? give an account of thy stewardship; for thou mayest be no longer steward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:835bbb6a-bf49-4c9f-920a-ce00d693942b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: LUK 16:3
Text: Then the steward said within himself, What shall I do? for my lord taketh away from me the stewardship: I cannot dig; to beg I am ashamed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2f7991e-7026-4e08-b3de-426e87a7051a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: LUK 16:4
Text: I am resolved what to do, that, when I am put out of the stewardship, they may receive me into their houses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17b849b8-9674-42c7-9c15-5267466b2a04>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: LUK 16:5
Text: So he called every one of his lord’s debtors unto him, and said unto the first, How much owest thou unto my lord?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0adb0a41-5068-4b49-8afb-641b0503bc16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: LUK 16:6
Text: And he said, An hundred measures of oil. And he said unto him, Take thy bill, and sit down quickly, and write fifty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d573950-7608-4536-8b2e-ca5b2e1de5cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: LUK 16:7
Text: Then said he to another, And how much owest thou? And he said, An hundred measures of wheat. And he said unto him, Take thy bill, and write fourscore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3772a48-aafe-42fd-b5ed-2c7f98f722f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: LUK 16:8
Text: And the lord commended the unjust steward, because he had done wisely: for the children of this world are in their generation wiser than the children of light.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b681bc64-20a3-4019-8939-c7493fcf8bb8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: LUK 16:9
Text: And I say unto you, Make to yourselves friends of the mammon of unrighteousness; that, when ye fail, they may receive you into everlasting habitations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f8e1ba0-0604-4ada-9d0c-aa4e3920b2f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: LUK 16:10
Text: He that is faithful in that which is least is faithful also in much: and he that is unjust in the least is unjust also in much.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32f01eb5-7c61-4e77-9fb5-0688c1c9c5ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: LUK 16:11
Text: If therefore ye have not been faithful in the unrighteous mammon, who will commit to your trust the true riches?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f58c091a-f026-4502-81c2-0ba04e24e229>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: LUK 16:12
Text: And if ye have not been faithful in that which is another man’s, who shall give you that which is your own?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f04515b3-3e03-4b53-becd-27d51565d1ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: LUK 16:13
Text: No servant can serve two masters: for either he will hate the one, and love the other; or else he will hold to the one, and despise the other. Ye cannot serve God and mammon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6828204b-825a-4e40-b72b-86fb6717b9ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: LUK 16:14
Text: And the Pharisees also, who were covetous, heard all these things: and they derided him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0277bc6e-d0ae-4933-a4ef-7330e6682495>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: LUK 16:15
Text: And he said unto them, Ye are they which justify yourselves before men; but God knoweth your hearts: for that which is highly esteemed among men is abomination in the sight of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:668362f1-3cc0-400d-b30a-b135ffa7bf4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: LUK 16:16
Text: The law and the prophets were until John: since that time the kingdom of God is preached, and every man presseth into it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4fd6282e-7ff6-4942-86bd-fcd9d8ab9887>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: LUK 16:17
Text: And it is easier for heaven and earth to pass, than one tittle of the law to fail.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:002e8bb5-ccdb-49d2-9cb7-44e3db16494b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: LUK 16:18
Text: Whosoever putteth away his wife, and marrieth another, committeth adultery: and whosoever marrieth her that is put away from her husband committeth adultery.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90f9c838-43cb-4f6a-91a8-3de228e4ba80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: LUK 16:19
Text: There was a certain rich man, which was clothed in purple and fine linen, and fared sumptuously every day:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42aac0ff-70b4-4d44-a71d-257642f6a06d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: LUK 16:20
Text: And there was a certain beggar named Lazarus, which was laid at his gate, full of sores,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64dc337c-d94d-4a2d-9cea-0b105a5fd213>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: LUK 16:21
Text: And desiring to be fed with the crumbs which fell from the rich man’s table: moreover the dogs came and licked his sores.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9cda9c4-9a3f-4025-a1a3-210c6f8a5903>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: LUK 16:22
Text: And it came to pass, that the beggar died, and was carried by the angels into Abraham’s bosom: the rich man also died, and was buried;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9768be45-34dc-4719-bbc1-ecddea50f2ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: LUK 16:23
Text: And in hell he lift up his eyes, being in torments, and seeth Abraham afar off, and Lazarus in his bosom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a102177-a4f1-4773-bad2-1bae8d1f93d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: LUK 16:24
Text: And he cried and said, Father Abraham, have mercy on me, and send Lazarus, that he may dip the tip of his finger in water, and cool my tongue; for I am tormented in this flame.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60c4b5fb-53a2-472c-b0d3-5f1010627d76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: LUK 16:25
Text: But Abraham said, Son, remember that thou in thy lifetime receivedst thy good things, and likewise Lazarus evil things: but now he is comforted, and thou art tormented.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0205634a-d575-48c9-82ed-7de83fd27a9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: LUK 16:26
Text: And beside all this, between us and you there is a great gulf fixed: so that they which would pass from hence to you cannot; neither can they pass to us, that would come from thence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08434646-52da-44c4-9334-4a492cd955a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: LUK 16:27
Text: Then he said, I pray thee therefore, father, that thou wouldest send him to my father’s house:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:021ac51d-0ab9-4832-8a73-c84c8fc843d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: LUK 16:28
Text: For I have five brethren; that he may testify unto them, lest they also come into this place of torment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02710c44-b8c8-4f8e-9472-bdae88853f87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: LUK 16:29
Text: Abraham saith unto him, They have Moses and the prophets; let them hear them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc36aa2c-5d32-4667-b576-f2e5311b4aff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: LUK 16:30
Text: And he said, Nay, father Abraham: but if one went unto them from the dead, they will repent.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/16/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7489a46-1368-4c39-aa9a-9a509f8cbcce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: LUK 16:31
Text: And he said unto him, If they hear not Moses and the prophets, neither will they be persuaded, though one rose from the dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2232a1fb-20d7-40b1-b1d2-4303d816cfb5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: LUK 17:1
Text: Then said he unto the disciples, It is impossible but that offences will come: but woe unto him, through whom they come!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d616367e-510d-4bd2-8987-0990da20ce5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: LUK 17:2
Text: It were better for him that a millstone were hanged about his neck, and he cast into the sea, than that he should offend one of these little ones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fbe2dc7-7c95-44f2-9b3d-649dbd71e0f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: LUK 17:3
Text: Take heed to yourselves: If thy brother trespass against thee, rebuke him; and if he repent, forgive him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1bacad95-e240-4bb2-8a41-fcd50e7e9d40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: LUK 17:4
Text: And if he trespass against thee seven times in a day, and seven times in a day turn again to thee, saying, I repent; thou shalt forgive him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6af32c4-3ff1-4277-9548-ddb63aa834be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: LUK 17:5
Text: And the apostles said unto the Lord, Increase our faith.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:796dbcc1-fda5-469a-9de1-befde4014e91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: LUK 17:6
Text: And the Lord said, If ye had faith as a grain of mustard seed, ye might say unto this sycamine tree, Be thou plucked up by the root, and be thou planted in the sea; and it should obey you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5cceb8f1-9bca-45e3-bfad-9bb3958073c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: LUK 17:7
Text: But which of you, having a servant plowing or feeding cattle, will say unto him by and by, when he is come from the field, Go and sit down to meat?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3893b1a8-7a14-4670-b82a-f9adbe4f5139>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: LUK 17:8
Text: And will not rather say unto him, Make ready wherewith I may sup, and gird thyself, and serve me, till I have eaten and drunken; and afterward thou shalt eat and drink?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
