Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: LUK 17:9
Text: Doth he thank that servant because he did the things that were commanded him? I trow not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab6f907a-c365-4b63-a3ed-5d6e12210603>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: LUK 17:10
Text: So likewise ye, when ye shall have done all those things which are commanded you, say, We are unprofitable servants: we have done that which was our duty to do.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77f862ab-1559-428d-b5b1-c0ef2c4053f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: LUK 17:11
Text: And it came to pass, as he went to Jerusalem, that he passed through the midst of Samaria and Galilee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4f47995-f8f1-4c62-905e-4664d83dd97d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: LUK 17:12
Text: And as he entered into a certain village, there met him ten men that were lepers, which stood afar off:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a722b2ed-fdda-4003-80e9-1b3068199b17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: LUK 17:13
Text: And they lifted up their voices, and said, Jesus, Master, have mercy on us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5350c023-fdda-47c6-be6b-af6bc0a21e21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: LUK 17:14
Text: And when he saw them, he said unto them, Go shew yourselves unto the priests. And it came to pass, that, as they went, they were cleansed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be4818c0-52de-4c9a-a942-739ef083114c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: LUK 17:15
Text: And one of them, when he saw that he was healed, turned back, and with a loud voice glorified God,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4418cff6-957d-4280-881d-f92224deb162>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: LUK 17:16
Text: And fell down on his face at his feet, giving him thanks: and he was a Samaritan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d0be1dd-ff6d-4bce-8ed4-046bb4c61566>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: LUK 17:17
Text: And Jesus answering said, Were there not ten cleansed? but where are the nine?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28270fdc-1d89-4369-bd1e-79d4d0bacf44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: LUK 17:18
Text: There are not found that returned to give glory to God, save this stranger.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fda06d4-2a43-42d0-b845-1e8956e5288b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: LUK 17:19
Text: And he said unto him, Arise, go thy way: thy faith hath made thee whole.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17b39246-8657-44c5-8fd2-ca95f2e52d78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: LUK 17:20
Text: And when he was demanded of the Pharisees, when the kingdom of God should come, he answered them and said, The kingdom of God cometh not with observation:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa56dae2-4cf4-4e5e-a344-b34d739de509>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: LUK 17:21
Text: Neither shall they say, Lo here! or, lo there! for, behold, the kingdom of God is within you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e81669d-34d7-4f1e-84c5-8ce4199835ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: LUK 17:22
Text: And he said unto the disciples, The days will come, when ye shall desire to see one of the days of the Son of man, and ye shall not see it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fd90115-e4a9-4527-8666-1714e763bead>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: LUK 17:23
Text: And they shall say to you, See here; or, see there: go not after them, nor follow them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87db2876-9ef3-41ec-88e9-b8b906e109fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: LUK 17:24
Text: For as the lightning, that lighteneth out of the one part under heaven, shineth unto the other part under heaven; so shall also the Son of man be in his day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25175636-2cdd-4b3d-9613-b5ccb34fa7c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: LUK 17:25
Text: But first must he suffer many things, and be rejected of this generation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:213402f8-8f01-4c3c-8234-c65d862d4b9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: LUK 17:26
Text: And as it was in the days of Noe, so shall it be also in the days of the Son of man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99669ab0-c606-41c9-b98b-3312a3ec22e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: LUK 17:27
Text: They did eat, they drank, they married wives, they were given in marriage, until the day that Noe entered into the ark, and the flood came, and destroyed them all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2eb6aac-041c-45c2-80a8-72f23105815c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: LUK 17:28
Text: Likewise also as it was in the days of Lot; they did eat, they drank, they bought, they sold, they planted, they builded;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b1bb93e-51fc-4f52-b48e-ed0f062977a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: LUK 17:29
Text: But the same day that Lot went out of Sodom it rained fire and brimstone from heaven, and destroyed them all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad165ecb-dbfb-4b21-a998-482e3d58c4be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: LUK 17:30
Text: Even thus shall it be in the day when the Son of man is revealed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0849d02e-0730-42b1-a482-5759c7370335>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: LUK 17:31
Text: In that day, he which shall be upon the housetop, and his stuff in the house, let him not come down to take it away: and he that is in the field, let him likewise not return back.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75bf49c4-9bcf-4d47-8cdf-756172a3f5a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 50

Reference: LUK 17:32
Text: Remember Lot’s wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37d1f52d-744f-40f0-b2a2-bbebe22a743e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: LUK 17:33
Text: Whosoever shall seek to save his life shall lose it; and whosoever shall lose his life shall preserve it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b804309-a2c5-4955-ba67-8ef0079e2b82>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: LUK 17:34
Text: I tell you, in that night there shall be two men in one bed; the one shall be taken, and the other shall be left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57ff6ba4-fecf-484a-a1c6-975ce06f6026>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: LUK 17:35
Text: Two women shall be grinding together; the one shall be taken, and the other left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d0de184-323c-4943-bf55-d3cc7bb49e75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: LUK 17:36
Text: Two men shall be in the field; the one shall be taken, and the other left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/17/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a05d498-425a-43de-8b5a-c2865692f020>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: LUK 17:37
Text: And they answered and said unto him, Where, Lord? And he said unto them, Wheresoever the body is, thither will the eagles be gathered together.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c7a4b21-08e5-44e5-ae4d-03bd8e25799d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: LUK 18:1
Text: And he spake a parable unto them to this end, that men ought always to pray, and not to faint;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd091d0f-33d3-4b3b-a550-561555e10e85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: LUK 18:2
Text: Saying, There was in a city a judge, which feared not God, neither regarded man:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b23c2f0-e52c-44dc-9b47-17e30aeadb9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: LUK 18:3
Text: And there was a widow in that city; and she came unto him, saying, Avenge me of mine adversary.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e524fd8a-67b9-46fd-bace-115015a55d9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: LUK 18:4
Text: And he would not for a while: but afterward he said within himself, Though I fear not God, nor regard man;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5fdde05-46cc-4f17-9431-66fb13e48393>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: LUK 18:5
Text: Yet because this widow troubleth me, I will avenge her, lest by her continual coming she weary me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2363b5b-b543-46a7-9d5a-4f30e32900ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: LUK 18:6
Text: And the Lord said, Hear what the unjust judge saith.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:145010ca-fe07-40ad-a1c8-cdddeb035e03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: LUK 18:7
Text: And shall not God avenge his own elect, which cry day and night unto him, though he bear long with them?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9ecb5b3-fc2f-4e39-9123-d5e9c7e1ffba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: LUK 18:8
Text: I tell you that he will avenge them speedily. Nevertheless when the Son of man cometh, shall he find faith on the earth?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03a4d24c-02ce-4fcc-a07a-615ca0d17406>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: LUK 18:9
Text: And he spake this parable unto certain which trusted in themselves that they were righteous, and despised others:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1dd50c1-8e59-4b0f-8793-50deb61d2670>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: LUK 18:10
Text: Two men went up into the temple to pray; the one a Pharisee, and the other a publican.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3e78d74-2e2b-4a84-b414-53d3b3899667>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: LUK 18:11
Text: The Pharisee stood and prayed thus with himself, God, I thank thee, that I am not as other men are, extortioners, unjust, adulterers, or even as this publican.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6df56168-da40-4bcb-9f07-a83c6962d10b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: LUK 18:12
Text: I fast twice in the week, I give tithes of all that I possess.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9caafa26-73d9-45d7-91c4-f87a964c129b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: LUK 18:13
Text: And the publican, standing afar off, would not lift up so much as his eyes unto heaven, but smote upon his breast, saying, God be merciful to me a sinner.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:596143f0-fb4e-459f-b16f-4fea414a5230>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: LUK 18:14
Text: I tell you, this man went down to his house justified rather than the other: for every one that exalteth himself shall be abased; and he that humbleth himself shall be exalted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e1aaa24-b70b-4d7d-9168-7cb16538ef35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: LUK 18:15
Text: And they brought unto him also infants, that he would touch them: but when his disciples saw it, they rebuked them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a336c53-256d-45f6-a933-d28e3cb3de72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: LUK 18:16
Text: But Jesus called them unto him, and said, Suffer little children to come unto me, and forbid them not: for of such is the kingdom of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c95ab00-e3e5-429c-9cfd-1a03f3783198>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: LUK 18:17
Text: Verily I say unto you, Whosoever shall not receive the kingdom of God as a little child shall in no wise enter therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:887b48ba-cf14-46a7-a3f9-803834add27b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: LUK 18:18
Text: And a certain ruler asked him, saying, Good Master, what shall I do to inherit eternal life?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f0f2a41-2f13-442c-bf6f-bec3bb59e8ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: LUK 18:19
Text: And Jesus said unto him, Why callest thou me good? none is good, save one, that is, God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec7425fd-e1fe-417c-876d-a6eb41ecd1aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: LUK 18:20
Text: Thou knowest the commandments, Do not commit adultery, Do not kill, Do not steal, Do not bear false witness, Honour thy father and thy mother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b2af7f1-fb7e-4786-9c97-05a5731a5bfe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: LUK 18:21
Text: And he said, All these have I kept from my youth up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d470db80-a37b-4fec-9bfc-32146e99404b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: LUK 18:22
Text: Now when Jesus heard these things, he said unto him, Yet lackest thou one thing: sell all that thou hast, and distribute unto the poor, and thou shalt have treasure in heaven: and come, follow me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83d41c3f-fcc6-4553-aeac-c77c73bb6ff3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: LUK 18:23
Text: And when he heard this, he was very sorrowful: for he was very rich.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b226f4d9-585c-451f-86b5-a1f6ad587b97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: LUK 18:24
Text: And when Jesus saw that he was very sorrowful, he said, How hardly shall they that have riches enter into the kingdom of God!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
