Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: LUK 18:25
Text: For it is easier for a camel to go through a needle’s eye, than for a rich man to enter into the kingdom of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df045053-486d-456f-a673-d170db9fd5c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: LUK 18:26
Text: And they that heard it said, Who then can be saved?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9dd2e32d-31ec-4058-b138-02d174a8e7e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: LUK 18:27
Text: And he said, The things which are impossible with men are possible with God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa5901ce-3ae2-4784-a726-3cf79fffc971>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: LUK 18:28
Text: Then Peter said, Lo, we have left all, and followed thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45a10086-868c-4f8a-9b7e-fbeec813b355>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: LUK 18:29
Text: And he said unto them, Verily I say unto you, There is no man that hath left house, or parents, or brethren, or wife, or children, for the kingdom of God’s sake,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6af62f9f-9962-46e7-b55b-6a61645f4d92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: LUK 18:30
Text: Who shall not receive manifold more in this present time, and in the world to come life everlasting.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e72feb49-e055-4fea-8ca3-782e24140148>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: LUK 18:31
Text: Then he took unto him the twelve, and said unto them, Behold, we go up to Jerusalem, and all things that are written by the prophets concerning the Son of man shall be accomplished.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47210fbe-6b15-4160-953e-a1f915113cd1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: LUK 18:32
Text: For he shall be delivered unto the Gentiles, and shall be mocked, and spitefully entreated, and spitted on:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6127792-9a20-4fd0-87e6-d5627f792635>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: LUK 18:33
Text: And they shall scourge him, and put him to death: and the third day he shall rise again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad7a21bf-99c0-4c60-af91-fb4977d537ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: LUK 18:34
Text: And they understood none of these things: and this saying was hid from them, neither knew they the things which were spoken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8709b8b8-e414-44e8-a2cd-39336566a2b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: LUK 18:35
Text: And it came to pass, that as he was come nigh unto Jericho, a certain blind man sat by the way side begging:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0fac7900-471b-4482-a12e-f683936cbf23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: LUK 18:36
Text: And hearing the multitude pass by, he asked what it meant.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:989ffc47-efe0-49ed-9c97-ac0aa738840e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: LUK 18:37
Text: And they told him, that Jesus of Nazareth passeth by.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:613c6faa-7df6-4609-8d2c-55607fccc986>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: LUK 18:38
Text: And he cried, saying, Jesus, thou son of David, have mercy on me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64317288-cf35-4169-b8fe-857e46eae4f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: LUK 18:39
Text: And they which went before rebuked him, that he should hold his peace: but he cried so much the more, Thou son of David, have mercy on me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d52db9f1-52f3-418c-b2ed-ba01154204df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: LUK 18:40
Text: And Jesus stood, and commanded him to be brought unto him: and when he was come near, he asked him,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c79c670f-375c-4f1f-bf91-2dee717d7010>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: LUK 18:41
Text: Saying, What wilt thou that I shall do unto thee? And he said, Lord, that I may receive my sight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58278e2f-653b-4c26-803f-e3bb105b3e0a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: LUK 18:42
Text: And Jesus said unto him, Receive thy sight: thy faith hath saved thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/18/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82b3a46c-f14b-4c12-b31a-c32253271282>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: LUK 18:43
Text: And immediately he received his sight, and followed him, glorifying God: and all the people, when they saw it, gave praise unto God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:584a7bcd-9e6f-4f8c-af82-5d99eab58660>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 72

Reference: LUK 19:1
Text: And Jesus entered and passed through Jericho.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:778d13ec-6973-420b-b120-e931941f5b2f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: LUK 19:2
Text: And, behold, there was a man named Zacchaeus, which was the chief among the publicans, and he was rich.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be272139-5789-4b35-a764-90c5e6ff3715>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: LUK 19:3
Text: And he sought to see Jesus who he was; and could not for the press, because he was little of stature.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18969811-2513-464d-908d-dc1189aa3137>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: LUK 19:4
Text: And he ran before, and climbed up into a sycomore tree to see him: for he was to pass that way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b3672d9-82ad-4111-8195-61c0f913846f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: LUK 19:5
Text: And when Jesus came to the place, he looked up, and saw him, and said unto him, Zacchaeus, make haste, and come down; for to day I must abide at thy house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a88240b5-6de2-43d0-bdd6-da7dd4de6404>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: LUK 19:6
Text: And he made haste, and came down, and received him joyfully.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21d01007-d064-40e9-b80b-a05da1532eae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: LUK 19:7
Text: And when they saw it, they all murmured, saying, That he was gone to be guest with a man that is a sinner.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26a3f1d8-97d4-4167-b8af-8d2ace9ec662>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: LUK 19:8
Text: And Zacchaeus stood, and said unto the Lord: Behold, Lord, the half of my goods I give to the poor; and if I have taken any thing from any man by false accusation, I restore him fourfold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f88290d-8dc8-4648-8c21-0d30d33e495f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: LUK 19:9
Text: And Jesus said unto him, This day is salvation come to this house, forsomuch as he also is a son of Abraham.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb1e65bf-eaa4-480d-be07-66935eb63c1b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: LUK 19:10
Text: For the Son of man is come to seek and to save that which was lost.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e5f72c2-2eb7-4609-b0f0-8d44e24b8d3e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: LUK 19:11
Text: And as they heard these things, he added and spake a parable, because he was nigh to Jerusalem, and because they thought that the kingdom of God should immediately appear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4a4f223-f322-4b7d-a08e-8698b5b711a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: LUK 19:12
Text: He said therefore, A certain nobleman went into a far country to receive for himself a kingdom, and to return.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0cb130fd-696b-47c8-8a26-b9237ab4e1e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: LUK 19:13
Text: And he called his ten servants, and delivered them ten pounds, and said unto them, Occupy till I come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f3b22d6-4e2d-4022-83b0-80ec2e5b5aa1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: LUK 19:14
Text: But his citizens hated him, and sent a message after him, saying, We will not have this man to reign over us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ebf5116-409c-4903-89d8-8f70702e49eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: LUK 19:15
Text: And it came to pass, that when he was returned, having received the kingdom, then he commanded these servants to be called unto him, to whom he had given the money, that he might know how much every man had gained by trading.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:230e53e9-90c0-4ec0-aadd-eb30a8d03347>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: LUK 19:16
Text: Then came the first, saying, Lord, thy pound hath gained ten pounds.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d9db66ee-06ba-48f0-a53e-db204671596b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: LUK 19:17
Text: And he said unto him, Well, thou good servant: because thou hast been faithful in a very little, have thou authority over ten cities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a64a4c1-c55a-4a35-992b-5c6dc3d3e628>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: LUK 19:18
Text: And the second came, saying, Lord, thy pound hath gained five pounds.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3177ec6b-fed0-4f76-b4ce-ddd93a19f5ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: LUK 19:19
Text: And he said likewise to him, Be thou also over five cities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8fed75ce-06fc-4aab-bd8b-e9d0e999f0d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: LUK 19:20
Text: And another came, saying, Lord, behold, here is thy pound, which I have kept laid up in a napkin:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57807067-b627-44f3-9076-7c62510ccf07>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: LUK 19:21
Text: For I feared thee, because thou art an austere man: thou takest up that thou layedst not down, and reapest that thou didst not sow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d392886e-4f48-4f1a-ade3-5d4f8eb25bd2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: LUK 19:22
Text: And he saith unto him, Out of thine own mouth will I judge thee, thou wicked servant. Thou knewest that I was an austere man, taking up that I laid not down, and reaping that I did not sow:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b29c87dd-f034-489c-b31d-fa97f540f692>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: LUK 19:23
Text: Wherefore then gavest not thou my money into the bank, that at my coming I might have required mine own with usury?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12a2b11e-e829-4239-8f29-1c4f804c1562>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: LUK 19:24
Text: And he said unto them that stood by, Take from him the pound, and give it to him that hath ten pounds.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7d77b19-eafd-4520-a5d7-52f1eec1538e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 79

Reference: LUK 19:25
Text: (And they said unto him, Lord, he hath ten pounds.)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7bd9dec3-72bf-4f4c-81ee-c1c814b0731f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: LUK 19:26
Text: For I say unto you, That unto every one which hath shall be given; and from him that hath not, even that he hath shall be taken away from him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1af37ea-0ea5-4053-91d8-fa37b87a1d66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: LUK 19:27
Text: But those mine enemies, which would not that I should reign over them, bring hither, and slay them before me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e4c7e16-921c-45d7-9d05-119b3ce63169>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: LUK 19:28
Text: And when he had thus spoken, he went before, ascending up to Jerusalem.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:590d7cf4-289e-4e14-97ec-26dedf8a739d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: LUK 19:29
Text: And it came to pass, when he was come nigh to Bethphage and Bethany, at the mount called the mount of Olives, he sent two of his disciples,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea730b86-e645-4d1c-813b-1d6369a2db41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: LUK 19:30
Text: Saying, Go ye into the village over against you; in the which at your entering ye shall find a colt tied, whereon yet never man sat: loose him, and bring him hither.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b2868e7-0450-4085-9477-7216c196ee80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: LUK 19:31
Text: And if any man ask you, Why do ye loose him? thus shall ye say unto him, Because the Lord hath need of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e701120d-25c1-4ca4-910a-95fbdcee0e34>
