WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30fc32c3-ea4a-4b51-946d-32cc40cb860b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: LUK 19:35
Text: And they brought him to Jesus: and they cast their garments upon the colt, and they set Jesus thereon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae5375ae-d964-49f1-8e6a-d315474de59f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: LUK 19:36
Text: And as he went, they spread their clothes in the way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a62fd366-4ffc-452a-90f3-a6fbed86be53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: LUK 19:37
Text: And when he was come nigh, even now at the descent of the mount of Olives, the whole multitude of the disciples began to rejoice and praise God with a loud voice for all the mighty works that they had seen;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:321df62f-9699-46b3-9cfd-6c3a1501765d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: LUK 19:38
Text: Saying, Blessed be the King that cometh in the name of the Lord: peace in heaven, and glory in the highest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13af2191-30a3-4c79-a62d-0ad6bccc71a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: LUK 19:39
Text: And some of the Pharisees from among the multitude said unto him, Master, rebuke thy disciples.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:698b562e-3276-44b5-b19c-5f3d3176d11d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: LUK 19:40
Text: And he answered and said unto them, I tell you that, if these should hold their peace, the stones would immediately cry out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49c3f6e3-4c56-4686-935a-29d67e0e75c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: LUK 19:41
Text: And when he was come near, he beheld the city, and wept over it,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abc1c4a4-b5f0-4db3-aa39-cd3062aa899e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: LUK 19:42
Text: Saying, If thou hadst known, even thou, at least in this thy day, the things which belong unto thy peace! but now they are hid from thine eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a051301-eb10-4e08-85bd-1fc071e127eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: LUK 19:43
Text: For the days shall come upon thee, that thine enemies shall cast a trench about thee, and compass thee round, and keep thee in on every side,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e413627-8856-4fcd-aaad-b0d13db3e844>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: LUK 19:44
Text: And shall lay thee even with the ground, and thy children within thee; and they shall not leave in thee one stone upon another; because thou knewest not the time of thy visitation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d0ee13e-1bb1-4883-95f8-395b3fd9fd60>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: LUK 19:45
Text: And he went into the temple, and began to cast out them that sold therein, and them that bought;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66efcedc-8471-4ee9-85ec-6fbf48f56427>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: LUK 19:46
Text: Saying unto them, It is written, My house is the house of prayer: but ye have made it a den of thieves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84e23d29-02dc-4ea9-9648-e3c3d9123a7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: LUK 19:47
Text: And he taught daily in the temple. But the chief priests and the scribes and the chief of the people sought to destroy him,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/19/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bae3b94c-f1a8-4bb1-8cb5-a805b76d4e3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: LUK 19:48
Text: And could not find what they might do: for all the people were very attentive to hear him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b96d7f7-a868-4eed-8e81-633ef2566f06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: LUK 20:1
Text: And it came to pass, that on one of those days, as he taught the people in the temple, and preached the gospel, the chief priests and the scribes came upon him with the elders,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99b57631-16e7-4534-9479-c83886bc00d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: LUK 20:2
Text: And spake unto him, saying, Tell us, by what authority doest thou these things? or who is he that gave thee this authority?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:429c65c0-b6b2-4d5e-b3d5-f40a4290f0a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: LUK 20:3
Text: And he answered and said unto them, I will also ask you one thing; and answer me:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ee14054-1fbf-4c0d-b7f5-cdd6bda3aef0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: LUK 20:4
Text: The baptism of John, was it from heaven, or of men?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a21c1aa-6ade-44ca-8ec0-e72805d53512>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: LUK 20:5
Text: And they reasoned with themselves, saying, If we shall say, From heaven; he will say, Why then believed ye him not?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:233f09eb-e6bd-4e7c-af76-c748d5f27e9a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: LUK 20:6
Text: But and if we say, Of men; all the people will stone us: for they be persuaded that John was a prophet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8903c2a-0d94-4211-8156-295e1c624770>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: LUK 20:7
Text: And they answered, that they could not tell whence it was.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3012f49-90bf-4cbf-b036-3f42673dc542>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: LUK 20:8
Text: And Jesus said unto them, Neither tell I you by what authority I do these things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2468d623-28cc-44f5-8dd5-30315e271363>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: LUK 20:9
Text: Then began he to speak to the people this parable; A certain man planted a vineyard, and let it forth to husbandmen, and went into a far country for a long time.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18a6b912-9666-4872-9876-4128363271d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: LUK 20:10
Text: And at the season he sent a servant to the husbandmen, that they should give him of the fruit of the vineyard: but the husbandmen beat him, and sent him away empty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed36bf6e-ceb9-4d37-8d2d-bef388743cfe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: LUK 20:11
Text: And again he sent another servant: and they beat him also, and entreated him shamefully, and sent him away empty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2091753a-852a-470b-9dea-18bb7573c172>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: LUK 20:12
Text: And again he sent a third: and they wounded him also, and cast him out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:913f0236-5e1c-496b-ac9e-e878f97d7187>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: LUK 20:13
Text: Then said the lord of the vineyard, What shall I do? I will send my beloved son: it may be they will reverence him when they see him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc9edea3-a111-4830-af50-bda9d2f5659a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: LUK 20:14
Text: But when the husbandmen saw him, they reasoned among themselves, saying, This is the heir: come, let us kill him, that the inheritance may be ours.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5d677f5-085b-4051-8f82-eecb6a61b8ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: LUK 20:15
Text: So they cast him out of the vineyard, and killed him. What therefore shall the lord of the vineyard do unto them?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f43166f-f36f-4ae7-acef-061d2d935bd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: LUK 20:16
Text: He shall come and destroy these husbandmen, and shall give the vineyard to others. And when they heard it, they said, God forbid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f62686d-6967-46f3-9df6-cd1ccce64836>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: LUK 20:17
Text: And he beheld them, and said, What is this then that is written, The stone which the builders rejected, the same is become the head of the corner?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0739d360-46ca-4158-9267-923d7b6af32b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: LUK 20:18
Text: Whosoever shall fall upon that stone shall be broken; but on whomsoever it shall fall, it will grind him to powder.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a567fec-99bb-4d63-a0d2-35c626ac0a78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: LUK 20:19
Text: And the chief priests and the scribes the same hour sought to lay hands on him; and they feared the people: for they perceived that he had spoken this parable against them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:424dedc2-5244-4bf8-88e7-0250e4f5e505>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: LUK 20:20
Text: And they watched him, and sent forth spies, which should feign themselves just men, that they might take hold of his words, that so they might deliver him unto the power and authority of the governor.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69b343a2-c391-4330-b388-12808f48824c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: LUK 20:21
Text: And they asked him, saying, Master, we know that thou sayest and teachest rightly, neither acceptest thou the person of any, but teachest the way of God truly:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5fdf9711-ed7b-45d3-a488-7065355cb0cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: LUK 20:22
Text: Is it lawful for us to give tribute unto Caesar, or no?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4401b31-3697-4e67-8021-9262f9d39878>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: LUK 20:23
Text: But he perceived their craftiness, and said unto them, Why tempt ye me?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b848de90-83b1-4a77-bb52-2728c125dcf1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: LUK 20:24
Text: Shew me a penny. Whose image and superscription hath it? They answered and said, Caesar’s.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2f83d7d-4286-4310-b7b3-344e627caaa5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: LUK 20:25
Text: And he said unto them, Render therefore unto Caesar the things which be Caesar’s, and unto God the things which be God’s.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c7f28eb-4e1a-4c7d-846d-e15528fd2ced>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: LUK 20:26
Text: And they could not take hold of his words before the people: and they marvelled at his answer, and held their peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ea83680-0806-4245-8c66-2d3fb971207a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: LUK 20:27
Text: Then came to him certain of the Sadducees, which deny that there is any resurrection; and they asked him,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5a75a9f-d380-489f-bbc5-be80a6798233>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: LUK 20:28
Text: Saying, Master, Moses wrote unto us, If any man’s brother die, having a wife, and he die without children, that his brother should take his wife, and raise up seed unto his brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5fbda2cf-2653-41d6-b972-4e8c09aa6978>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: LUK 20:29
Text: There were therefore seven brethren: and the first took a wife, and died without children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3e1153a-0d13-44ff-819e-4675e92f0409>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: LUK 20:30
Text: And the second took her to wife, and he died childless.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca57454a-d614-42e5-9286-35b2e0fa997c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: LUK 20:31
Text: And the third took her; and in like manner the seven also: and they left no children, and died.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30f7d60b-431d-4b7c-bc7f-3a1d0d9af4cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 60

Reference: LUK 20:32
Text: Last of all the woman died also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29a2f0d4-5638-4f6a-b5a0-19bc172d6600>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: LUK 20:33
Text: Therefore in the resurrection whose wife of them is she? for seven had her to wife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d30f4384-280a-4961-87a1-3a97002a5fa7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: LUK 20:34
Text: And Jesus answering said unto them, The children of this world marry, and are given in marriage:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43c5949f-1e40-4acc-9bf0-67b6640a644b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: LUK 20:35
Text: But they which shall be accounted worthy to obtain that world, and the resurrection from the dead, neither marry, nor are given in marriage:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:753ab307-0a67-4c9c-85a9-d997bcd18736>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: LUK 20:36
Text: Neither can they die any more: for they are equal unto the angels; and are the children of God, being the children of the resurrection.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97c90b72-5c0b-414f-aa9a-b603dd20de95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: LUK 20:37
Text: Now that the dead are raised, even Moses shewed at the bush, when he calleth the Lord the God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc74b0e7-b8f0-4212-bf57-3d7d7c359b33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: LUK 20:38
Text: For he is not a God of the dead, but of the living: for all live unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cfb5006b-d5c8-40a7-84a9-384beb87078c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: LUK 20:39
Text: Then certain of the scribes answering said, Master, thou hast well said.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ce832c7-4cf7-41c8-9edb-8fba51fabc70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: LUK 20:40
Text: And after that they durst not ask him any question at all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
