Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: LUK 20:41
Text: And he said unto them, How say they that Christ is David’s son?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90a6f498-3a5d-402e-a0ba-699e6f56ffd9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: LUK 20:42
Text: And David himself saith in the book of Psalms, The LORD said unto my Lord, Sit thou on my right hand,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b0fc638-b839-4784-ac05-dfa2b0a670f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 68

Reference: LUK 20:43
Text: Till I make thine enemies thy footstool.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af9ee789-edb7-42f0-a895-c4057161340c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: LUK 20:44
Text: David therefore calleth him Lord, how is he then his son?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d63e4c46-30f0-4b5f-9179-7732ec66ffa7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: LUK 20:45
Text: Then in the audience of all the people he said unto his disciples,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:115ab378-865e-4fc1-b32d-d9dd138d8289>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: LUK 20:46
Text: Beware of the scribes, which desire to walk in long robes, and love greetings in the markets, and the highest seats in the synagogues, and the chief rooms at feasts;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/20/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53607cf4-8f98-4aef-9313-879ae30f921d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: LUK 20:47
Text: Which devour widows’ houses, and for a shew make long prayers: the same shall receive greater damnation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91d7e460-f720-46ee-86d2-911ed665b179>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: LUK 21:1
Text: And he looked up, and saw the rich men casting their gifts into the treasury.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00140be1-5480-4056-9e73-7143ee31b8b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: LUK 21:2
Text: And he saw also a certain poor widow casting in thither two mites.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64892b20-29df-4e15-b7da-64acd542f760>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: LUK 21:3
Text: And he said, Of a truth I say unto you, that this poor widow hath cast in more than they all:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63ba21a4-c17b-4261-a39c-6769c7851e83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: LUK 21:4
Text: For all these have of their abundance cast in unto the offerings of God: but she of her penury hath cast in all the living that she had.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6827e638-dd0f-47e1-8865-3df38c9de3ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: LUK 21:5
Text: And as some spake of the temple, how it was adorned with goodly stones and gifts, he said,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d98b8628-3bce-4257-94a7-00733be7bf8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: LUK 21:6
Text: As for these things which ye behold, the days will come, in the which there shall not be left one stone upon another, that shall not be thrown down.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3b42587-9ab3-4235-936a-bb7ccd5107a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: LUK 21:7
Text: And they asked him, saying, Master, but when shall these things be? and what sign will there be when these things shall come to pass?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8fe7181-6855-4e5d-831f-75a245f97def>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: LUK 21:8
Text: And he said, Take heed that ye be not deceived: for many shall come in my name, saying, I am Christ; and the time draweth near: go ye not therefore after them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c61aeefa-a0f7-4ecb-be40-a9e6ba058b4f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: LUK 21:9
Text: But when ye shall hear of wars and commotions, be not terrified: for these things must first come to pass; but the end is not by and by.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22fa7da9-8cb4-470d-9d63-787cacc14b3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: LUK 21:10
Text: Then said he unto them, Nation shall rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01ae8045-b93d-4f4e-a2dc-111e78b7a30e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: LUK 21:11
Text: And great earthquakes shall be in divers places, and famines, and pestilences; and fearful sights and great signs shall there be from heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dae4f27f-5c3b-4172-80f4-0cdd7d68ff47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: LUK 21:12
Text: But before all these, they shall lay their hands on you, and persecute you, delivering you up to the synagogues, and into prisons, being brought before kings and rulers for my name’s sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78e24cc2-dee7-4c27-ace0-1a02ae9d58e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 69

Reference: LUK 21:13
Text: And it shall turn to you for a testimony.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84781e3c-66e9-4ebf-9c8d-009b347be7ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: LUK 21:14
Text: Settle it therefore in your hearts, not to meditate before what ye shall answer:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3de97fe6-edb4-466e-8340-d3a71914294a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: LUK 21:15
Text: For I will give you a mouth and wisdom, which all your adversaries shall not be able to gainsay nor resist.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8195cef-a504-438c-9fa9-d716eabef955>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: LUK 21:16
Text: And ye shall be betrayed both by parents, and brethren, and kinsfolks, and friends; and some of you shall they cause to be put to death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d1eacb3-8a29-4f0e-a49d-f431551bfb2f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: LUK 21:17
Text: And ye shall be hated of all men for my name’s sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:caf1bedd-14ae-43df-a1d4-f63cba6b1a15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: LUK 21:18
Text: But there shall not an hair of your head perish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73916002-ad82-49db-877d-149a058af867>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 67

Reference: LUK 21:19
Text: In your patience possess ye your souls.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60c27b00-2464-42ba-baf2-5ad383650a39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: LUK 21:20
Text: And when ye shall see Jerusalem compassed with armies, then know that the desolation thereof is nigh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27ebbe65-edf2-4f63-88f3-f5410637cc2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: LUK 21:21
Text: Then let them which are in Judaea flee to the mountains; and let them which are in the midst of it depart out; and let not them that are in the countries enter thereinto.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3de4ab80-4cfe-45e2-adae-4bfc2f195385>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: LUK 21:22
Text: For these be the days of vengeance, that all things which are written may be fulfilled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a00e4dc8-f9d0-49cf-9b89-414ea85bd704>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: LUK 21:23
Text: But woe unto them that are with child, and to them that give suck, in those days! for there shall be great distress in the land, and wrath upon this people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35dd92d9-205a-4c71-ac16-2bf1f0e6faa3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: LUK 21:24
Text: And they shall fall by the edge of the sword, and shall be led away captive into all nations: and Jerusalem shall be trodden down of the Gentiles, until the times of the Gentiles be fulfilled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7f5be26-1660-434a-a3ce-9ac9e06a9bda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: LUK 21:25
Text: And there shall be signs in the sun, and in the moon, and in the stars; and upon the earth distress of nations, with perplexity; the sea and the waves roaring;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0043ff02-e96d-49e8-8e43-a27d49ed0169>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: LUK 21:26
Text: Men’s hearts failing them for fear, and for looking after those things which are coming on the earth: for the powers of heaven shall be shaken.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4435aead-2f03-4eba-bb18-971eaa4d3961>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: LUK 21:27
Text: And then shall they see the Son of man coming in a cloud with power and great glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:590b2b4d-b030-42ad-b0fe-d6676d85f3bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: LUK 21:28
Text: And when these things begin to come to pass, then look up, and lift up your heads; for your redemption draweth nigh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c840a44a-b6f1-41d9-ad28-f47ebf47cd86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: LUK 21:29
Text: And he spake to them a parable; Behold the fig tree, and all the trees;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8d32327-60a1-4162-8f40-494c51a4fb45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: LUK 21:30
Text: When they now shoot forth, ye see and know of your own selves that summer is now nigh at hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ff8aa07-0e76-49ce-b57b-f75a6e290c09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: LUK 21:31
Text: So likewise ye, when ye see these things come to pass, know ye that the kingdom of God is nigh at hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73cf3ce6-cba2-4e43-99e4-39c309cbebeb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: LUK 21:32
Text: Verily I say unto you, This generation shall not pass away, till all be fulfilled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3edefb82-d1b5-4040-99b1-b285eb103eb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: LUK 21:33
Text: Heaven and earth shall pass away: but my words shall not pass away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53438e06-7345-4c65-ae3c-e2ba814aeb03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: LUK 21:34
Text: And take heed to yourselves, lest at any time your hearts be overcharged with surfeiting, and drunkenness, and cares of this life, and so that day come upon you unawares.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a725d9bd-29aa-4dc6-9291-decdc8abc765>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: LUK 21:35
Text: For as a snare shall it come on all them that dwell on the face of the whole earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc104f90-7a72-463e-b1cc-25a8f55c753f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: LUK 21:36
Text: Watch ye therefore, and pray always, that ye may be accounted worthy to escape all these things that shall come to pass, and to stand before the Son of man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a75ca3d-a8b6-41ef-bd5d-fb9699c126f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: LUK 21:37
Text: And in the day time he was teaching in the temple; and at night he went out, and abode in the mount that is called the mount of Olives.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/21/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cda9d6f8-426e-4339-a534-e0d1f8531c4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: LUK 21:38
Text: And all the people came early in the morning to him in the temple, for to hear him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f95fae38-4edc-433e-a435-b1c2a2c6386f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: LUK 22:1
Text: Now the feast of unleavened bread drew nigh, which is called the Passover.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a322d29-16e6-4249-b49e-542eea5e391c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: LUK 22:2
Text: And the chief priests and scribes sought how they might kill him; for they feared the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6088ae57-928c-42ed-b3fc-49864e41162e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: LUK 22:3
Text: Then entered Satan into Judas surnamed Iscariot, being of the number of the twelve.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c22a6a19-8e70-44b8-a0b7-5c7adc2f4456>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: LUK 22:4
Text: And he went his way, and communed with the chief priests and captains, how he might betray him unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc91ed6e-8e90-46b7-bea0-f9cb6060025f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: LUK 22:5
Text: And they were glad, and covenanted to give him money.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be918f44-4a70-4bb9-9b1a-c2aeb406c5d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: LUK 22:6
Text: And he promised, and sought opportunity to betray him unto them in the absence of the multitude.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3a58933-d9b9-46dc-9426-cbb35b6447b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: LUK 22:7
Text: Then came the day of unleavened bread, when the passover must be killed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:384b6ffb-113d-4a06-b2cc-136a5594d116>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: LUK 22:8
Text: And he sent Peter and John, saying, Go and prepare us the passover, that we may eat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0549e26-96a4-4a8b-8be0-8bb575d67b63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: LUK 22:9
Text: And they said unto him, Where wilt thou that we prepare?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:210d4d3e-c190-4cd0-8d6c-7219df6ada0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: LUK 22:10
Text: And he said unto them, Behold, when ye are entered into the city, there shall a man meet you, bearing a pitcher of water; follow him into the house where he entereth in.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b06522cf-8c34-4b71-bfb6-9eef9b4a87ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: LUK 22:11
Text: And ye shall say unto the goodman of the house, The Master saith unto thee, Where is the guestchamber, where I shall eat the passover with my disciples?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26b0752c-e568-4b5d-b830-611d35a6d316>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: LUK 22:12
Text: And he shall shew you a large upper room furnished: there make ready.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ee34c2e-6d33-4dd6-b8fb-c6d7884643fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: LUK 22:13
Text: And they went, and found as he had said unto them: and they made ready the passover.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:926e0729-f90d-48d6-be12-0879e15f13f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: LUK 22:14
Text: And when the hour was come, he sat down, and the twelve apostles with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77a60fe1-fc8a-4606-986b-0069c1eb5125>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: LUK 22:15
Text: And he said unto them, With desire I have desired to eat this passover with you before I suffer:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60e84cc0-ca26-4c61-8a50-f43137ad3ace>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: LUK 22:16
Text: For I say unto you, I will not any more eat thereof, until it be fulfilled in the kingdom of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a44ef541-a387-4f0b-91cc-4a974ae3e9f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: LUK 22:17
Text: And he took the cup, and gave thanks, and said, Take this, and divide it among yourselves:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31637dfb-2907-4ebb-9b51-0df865d432d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: LUK 22:18
Text: For I say unto you, I will not drink of the fruit of the vine, until the kingdom of God shall come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26b5cead-83e2-4428-9cd1-b32748ca3877>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: LUK 22:19
Text: And he took bread, and gave thanks, and brake it, and gave unto them, saying, This is my body which is given for you: this do in remembrance of me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88ee578b-ebcb-43b8-af9f-1f4c9db4c849>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: LUK 22:20
Text: Likewise also the cup after supper, saying, This cup is the new testament in my blood, which is shed for you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24f126c7-3dc4-4271-96ee-4f0a2600fb90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: LUK 22:21
Text: But, behold, the hand of him that betrayeth me is with me on the table.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:251a3522-0746-4d0c-979d-6d6657aa8410>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: LUK 22:22
Text: And truly the Son of man goeth, as it was determined: but woe unto that man by whom he is betrayed!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe6c4bc0-a8d9-4a09-8803-d0b3c047b78c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: LUK 22:23
Text: And they began to enquire among themselves, which of them it was that should do this thing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee32e743-7d4a-4605-8d4b-7f7c018facae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: LUK 22:24
Text: And there was also a strife among them, which of them should be accounted the greatest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:057e36f2-fb84-4223-a2d1-22b63edafc03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: LUK 22:25
Text: And he said unto them, The kings of the Gentiles exercise lordship over them; and they that exercise authority upon them are called benefactors.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d4ac394-b7a6-4984-9a4e-f1941bcaeacb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: LUK 22:26
Text: But ye shall not be so: but he that is greatest among you, let him be as the younger; and he that is chief, as he that doth serve.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8742392-6c7c-493d-8a3f-23a8a2263bef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: LUK 22:27
Text: For whether is greater, he that sitteth at meat, or he that serveth? is not he that sitteth at meat? but I am among you as he that serveth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa0155df-7f53-4e10-82cf-3a8ac4015579>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: LUK 22:28
Text: Ye are they which have continued with me in my temptations.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:766e63cc-7a61-4f83-bed8-9588aed4e8aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: LUK 22:29
Text: And I appoint unto you a kingdom, as my Father hath appointed unto me;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b6a45e1-fb4f-4dd8-a820-f00d3a4ab5b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: LUK 22:30
Text: That ye may eat and drink at my table in my kingdom, and sit on thrones judging the twelve tribes of Israel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3f96351-de7f-4252-947c-fd54f3b03b4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: LUK 22:31
Text: And the Lord said, Simon, Simon, behold, Satan hath desired to have you, that he may sift you as wheat:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9ff7589-6e7c-46a6-9fe5-7a49029daeda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: LUK 22:32
Text: But I have prayed for thee, that thy faith fail not: and when thou art converted, strengthen thy brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:deed8ff2-525c-4ccf-9427-bae91ebb83f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: LUK 22:33
Text: And he said unto him, Lord, I am ready to go with thee, both into prison, and to death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60f3d906-9de4-4802-869e-c94917b7f443>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: LUK 22:34
Text: And he said, I tell thee, Peter, the cock shall not crow this day, before that thou shalt thrice deny that thou knowest me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa3df27e-5247-4d57-9712-cfb1de9a1a26>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: LUK 22:35
Text: And he said unto them, When I sent you without purse, and scrip, and shoes, lacked ye any thing? And they said, Nothing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f948fc3-3bcd-435b-a023-450961774479>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: LUK 22:36
Text: Then said he unto them, But now, he that hath a purse, let him take it, and likewise his scrip: and he that hath no sword, let him sell his garment, and buy one.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfeb57a3-6c85-4ccd-9ef0-8de4f9af26c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: LUK 22:37
Text: For I say unto you, that this that is written must yet be accomplished in me, And he was reckoned among the transgressors: for the things concerning me have an end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51ef348e-1e05-41c2-a2b3-9a97beb7427b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: LUK 22:38
Text: And they said, Lord, behold, here are two swords. And he said unto them, It is enough.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc8d785d-a5cb-4462-a0fa-606a14eb7272>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: LUK 22:39
Text: And he came out, and went, as he was wont, to the mount of Olives; and his disciples also followed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79fa2422-9a50-45f6-9307-5cde12c894db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: LUK 22:40
Text: And when he was at the place, he said unto them, Pray that ye enter not into temptation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:421ed9d8-3439-4fdf-b56f-f40bd29e6712>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: LUK 22:41
Text: And he was withdrawn from them about a stone’s cast, and kneeled down, and prayed,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3817332a-1746-4c3d-bc03-18d200cfcd73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: LUK 22:42
Text: Saying, Father, if thou be willing, remove this cup from me: nevertheless not my will, but thine, be done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ee60d2f-4ea0-40ba-8d40-7925b9293cbd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: LUK 22:43
Text: And there appeared an angel unto him from heaven, strengthening him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6537f547-3c16-4b69-8113-7b6dc60f89a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: LUK 22:44
Text: And being in an agony he prayed more earnestly: and his sweat was as it were great drops of blood falling down to the ground.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db1b2fe2-921d-449e-8a6b-43b6313e548a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: LUK 22:45
Text: And when he rose up from prayer, and was come to his disciples, he found them sleeping for sorrow,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/46
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ace1c1a-1ef8-42de-8e17-0d80b7817f4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: LUK 22:46
Text: And said unto them, Why sleep ye? rise and pray, lest ye enter into temptation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5cf09bb-00a1-4955-b05c-181c4f66373e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: LUK 22:47
Text: And while he yet spake, behold a multitude, and he that was called Judas, one of the twelve, went before them, and drew near unto Jesus to kiss him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb5a0848-f996-47d0-96e9-7f4894615ab5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: LUK 22:48
Text: But Jesus said unto him, Judas, betrayest thou the Son of man with a kiss?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4bdbcac0-37be-4a13-842e-41b20a898b13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: LUK 22:49
Text: When they which were about him saw what would follow, they said unto him, Lord, shall we smite with the sword?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3450d3d4-689a-4dc3-8148-c19b20158be0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: LUK 22:50
Text: And one of them smote the servant of the high priest, and cut off his right ear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78e9b71f-8721-4430-ad76-c010e619ac2f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: LUK 22:51
Text: And Jesus answered and said, Suffer ye thus far. And he touched his ear, and healed him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8a7466a-07f8-43c3-a3e7-1f52bb28d063>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: LUK 22:52
Text: Then Jesus said unto the chief priests, and captains of the temple, and the elders, which were come to him, Be ye come out, as against a thief, with swords and staves?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d98ff77f-7257-4911-afc8-dd4b7f227f40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: LUK 22:53
Text: When I was daily with you in the temple, ye stretched forth no hands against me: but this is your hour, and the power of darkness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5189169e-5b7c-4ec8-bc85-e206857a3579>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: LUK 22:54
Text: Then took they him, and led him, and brought him into the high priest’s house. And Peter followed afar off.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/55
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11e6b7c6-feed-46f2-b1b7-bbec7e72c756>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: LUK 22:55
Text: And when they had kindled a fire in the midst of the hall, and were set down together, Peter sat down among them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/56
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7af07348-35a6-41b6-a66f-81e999f69016>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: LUK 22:56
Text: But a certain maid beheld him as he sat by the fire, and earnestly looked upon him, and said, This man was also with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/57
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07293327-f054-4434-95a8-4949fa00b7b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: LUK 22:57
Text: And he denied him, saying, Woman, I know him not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/58
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edb33d64-bb45-4962-87f6-036ba33d7b74>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: LUK 22:58
Text: And after a little while another saw him, and said, Thou art also of them. And Peter said, Man, I am not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/59
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45d5671a-9c27-430f-95da-2159876ba1d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: LUK 22:59
Text: And about the space of one hour after another confidently affirmed, saying, Of a truth this fellow also was with him: for he is a Galilaean.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/60
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a941516e-bca1-488c-9ed0-da222b1c93f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: LUK 22:60
Text: And Peter said, Man, I know not what thou sayest. And immediately, while he yet spake, the cock crew.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/61
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fde1ec2c-cafb-4f4d-9422-d8bc46dd1197>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: LUK 22:61
Text: And the Lord turned, and looked upon Peter. And Peter remembered the word of the Lord, how he had said unto him, Before the cock crow, thou shalt deny me thrice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/62
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa525ca2-c5f6-43aa-a5e9-6129f1d6cbdc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 66

Reference: LUK 22:62
Text: And Peter went out, and wept bitterly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/63
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:317ad184-46ec-4c6f-89c5-6dceeae8231c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: LUK 22:63
Text: And the men that held Jesus mocked him, and smote him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/64
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61fc5663-950a-4f31-95e3-96575f91a855>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: LUK 22:64
Text: And when they had blindfolded him, they struck him on the face, and asked him, saying, Prophesy, who is it that smote thee?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/65
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aade621e-7431-496e-b827-ba5a1806f5f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: LUK 22:65
Text: And many other things blasphemously spake they against him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/66
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9dfa86e-03d4-4f9a-804d-4fbae0eb6587>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: LUK 22:66
Text: And as soon as it was day, the elders of the people and the chief priests and the scribes came together, and led him into their council, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/67
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:981df3a5-b290-475a-817c-f7aa771d5141>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: LUK 22:67
Text: Art thou the Christ? tell us. And he said unto them, If I tell you, ye will not believe:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/68
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5dcbb265-d7c5-44a4-b478-ace400430351>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: LUK 22:68
Text: And if I also ask you, ye will not answer me, nor let me go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/69
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73634ac8-db2a-48d9-8005-26f09edef336>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: LUK 22:69
Text: Hereafter shall the Son of man sit on the right hand of the power of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/70
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fdbece3a-0596-471f-937a-627bd7b9ce11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: LUK 22:70
Text: Then said they all, Art thou then the Son of God? And he said unto them, Ye say that I am.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/22/71
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da6e9676-893d-416e-96e4-fa0044b06195>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: LUK 22:71
Text: And they said, What need we any further witness? for we ourselves have heard of his own mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58e079f1-6f02-4ab6-b41d-26b95f4b5916>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: LUK 23:1
Text: And the whole multitude of them arose, and led him unto Pilate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5ee7ba6-6629-4556-aee8-b54d0b8769fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: LUK 23:2
Text: And they began to accuse him, saying, We found this fellow perverting the nation, and forbidding to give tribute to Caesar, saying that he himself is Christ a King.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c142613-2bfb-4a45-8a54-cff3be26ca9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: LUK 23:3
Text: And Pilate asked him, saying, Art thou the King of the Jews? And he answered him and said, Thou sayest it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e51fdf7-c8ec-48a7-9a76-38d9149655b3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: LUK 23:4
Text: Then said Pilate to the chief priests and to the people, I find no fault in this man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddd9b8fe-2e60-4eed-837e-02d663d2c9c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: LUK 23:5
Text: And they were the more fierce, saying, He stirreth up the people, teaching throughout all Jewry, beginning from Galilee to this place.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d935f98-3827-41f7-a88a-5fa89ef4d45a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: LUK 23:6
Text: When Pilate heard of Galilee, he asked whether the man were a Galilaean.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d5c2163-5064-411a-bb0c-bb1de752c4da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: LUK 23:7
Text: And as soon as he knew that he belonged unto Herod’s jurisdiction, he sent him to Herod, who himself also was at Jerusalem at that time.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6805eb4-f190-42dc-a579-44e11dc72c40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: LUK 23:8
Text: And when Herod saw Jesus, he was exceeding glad: for he was desirous to see him of a long season, because he had heard many things of him; and he hoped to have seen some miracle done by him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5ab9e09-7705-457d-8c32-c8d42d014bdf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: LUK 23:9
Text: Then he questioned with him in many words; but he answered him nothing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c205377-4a25-4797-a0a9-cb95ff7f6cd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: LUK 23:10
Text: And the chief priests and scribes stood and vehemently accused him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18667712-bbec-4402-a980-80e15ab52636>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: LUK 23:11
Text: And Herod with his men of war set him at nought, and mocked him, and arrayed him in a gorgeous robe, and sent him again to Pilate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7638d8ef-b816-41c6-b307-a87743955c27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: LUK 23:12
Text: And the same day Pilate and Herod were made friends together: for before they were at enmity between themselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c2dd489-8da0-4bf8-9af8-6807f214474e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: LUK 23:13
Text: And Pilate, when he had called together the chief priests and the rulers and the people,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6ac6a42-4b32-41e2-a0cd-4c64d6976eb1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: LUK 23:14
Text: Said unto them, Ye have brought this man unto me, as one that perverteth the people: and, behold, I, having examined him before you, have found no fault in this man touching those things whereof ye accuse him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02a739c0-1d96-406f-bda7-5958abdb923b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: LUK 23:15
Text: No, nor yet Herod: for I sent you to him; and, lo, nothing worthy of death is done unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b369d749-ccb5-46eb-8a83-96073cb0efb0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: LUK 23:16
Text: I will therefore chastise him, and release him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aa16e338-6d98-483b-a3bd-bd949470edd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: LUK 23:17
Text: (For of necessity he must release one unto them at the feast.)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e272b0b-babf-4ce7-ad50-b461fd86500b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: LUK 23:18
Text: And they cried out all at once, saying, Away with this man, and release unto us Barabbas:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7e1968c-88fd-465b-b420-1c9a3d8f0903>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: LUK 23:19
Text: (Who for a certain sedition made in the city, and for murder, was cast into prison.)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d7ea125-06e7-41dd-9e74-16482083974c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: LUK 23:20
Text: Pilate therefore, willing to release Jesus, spake again to them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94bce12e-4a50-4c19-b20a-ec10728386dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: LUK 23:21
Text: But they cried, saying, Crucify him, crucify him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ca4014f-0d24-4544-841b-8eb9fe464ec0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: LUK 23:22
Text: And he said unto them the third time, Why, what evil hath he done? I have found no cause of death in him: I will therefore chastise him, and let him go.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1341d9f-9a03-421f-98d1-1be4a74dac88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: LUK 23:23
Text: And they were instant with loud voices, requiring that he might be crucified. And the voices of them and of the chief priests prevailed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5b4761c-e76b-486b-ad97-2e27d500f78a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: LUK 23:24
Text: And Pilate gave sentence that it should be as they required.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65de05bd-aa87-4525-adef-c5589834d9ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: LUK 23:25
Text: And he released unto them him that for sedition and murder was cast into prison, whom they had desired; but he delivered Jesus to their will.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da79644e-d72e-46f8-a125-013224dacc5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: LUK 23:26
Text: And as they led him away, they laid hold upon one Simon, a Cyrenian, coming out of the country, and on him they laid the cross, that he might bear it after Jesus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f4b0e77-1f04-43a6-9b1c-ccd5501f50aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: LUK 23:27
Text: And there followed him a great company of people, and of women, which also bewailed and lamented him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96553e9d-9ace-4324-aa46-1e89e286bf41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: LUK 23:28
Text: But Jesus turning unto them said, Daughters of Jerusalem, weep not for me, but weep for yourselves, and for your children.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14a176ca-f15e-4f69-9c3b-51c7abec6b2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: LUK 23:29
Text: For, behold, the days are coming, in the which they shall say, Blessed are the barren, and the wombs that never bare, and the paps which never gave suck.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed8ca730-613c-43dc-abf2-7cbc283447a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: LUK 23:30
Text: Then shall they begin to say to the mountains, Fall on us; and to the hills, Cover us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5cbdf029-9d3b-434b-99f7-faa28eda068a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: LUK 23:31
Text: For if they do these things in a green tree, what shall be done in the dry?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:634557a7-6552-4f91-9f94-365c91841240>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: LUK 23:32
Text: And there were also two other, malefactors, led with him to be put to death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1c077e3-06e5-4cd9-9bfc-876602de7718>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: LUK 23:33
Text: And when they were come to the place, which is called Calvary, there they crucified him, and the malefactors, one on the right hand, and the other on the left.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8084085c-c76e-472c-85ef-57754c7193a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: LUK 23:34
Text: Then said Jesus, Father, forgive them; for they know not what they do. And they parted his raiment, and cast lots.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27604d49-6500-4d68-83f6-1c44c0d6938d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: LUK 23:35
Text: And the people stood beholding. And the rulers also with them derided him, saying, He saved others; let him save himself, if he be Christ, the chosen of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aca97b65-b635-4bce-bbfc-f1a589ec5738>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: LUK 23:36
Text: And the soldiers also mocked him, coming to him, and offering him vinegar,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf383799-3453-47be-903f-32ba6da40c52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: LUK 23:37
Text: And saying, If thou be the king of the Jews, save thyself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89da0f05-68f3-4b16-8fcc-ba3ddbd5ee17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: LUK 23:38
Text: And a superscription also was written over him in letters of Greek, and Latin, and Hebrew, THIS IS THE KING OF THE JEWS.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:284e22e5-48a4-4e74-8fd9-013f9f6398db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: LUK 23:39
Text: And one of the malefactors which were hanged railed on him, saying, If thou be Christ, save thyself and us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf1580c5-223b-4297-9e97-435e135a2dc5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: LUK 23:40
Text: But the other answering rebuked him, saying, Dost not thou fear God, seeing thou art in the same condemnation?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/41
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f3e9767-e6e8-4aef-ada8-71d04880e61b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: LUK 23:41
Text: And we indeed justly; for we receive the due reward of our deeds: but this man hath done nothing amiss.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/42
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ee5edbc-301b-41cf-959a-95e04214df41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: LUK 23:42
Text: And he said unto Jesus, Lord, remember me when thou comest into thy kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/43
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16cb49d1-e8e2-4b5a-abb7-fea5481767f9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: LUK 23:43
Text: And Jesus said unto him, Verily I say unto thee, To day shalt thou be with me in paradise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/44
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df604a34-8b4f-4f34-9975-fc0d931123fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: LUK 23:44
Text: And it was about the sixth hour, and there was a darkness over all the earth until the ninth hour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/45
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7543f09-9b67-4ab8-a873-4f422e3ec6b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: LUK 23:45
Text: And the sun was darkened, and the veil of the temple was rent in the midst.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/46
