Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: LUK 23:46
Text: And when Jesus had cried with a loud voice, he said, Father, into thy hands I commend my spirit: and having said thus, he gave up the ghost.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/47
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66b4cdc1-c743-4571-a93b-6491adda9265>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: LUK 23:47
Text: Now when the centurion saw what was done, he glorified God, saying, Certainly this was a righteous man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/48
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29b445c6-6a4f-42dd-a8a2-a9e1a80ac292>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: LUK 23:48
Text: And all the people that came together to that sight, beholding the things which were done, smote their breasts, and returned.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/49
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7cb52626-7063-4298-a0bf-9f68d8f1cded>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: LUK 23:49
Text: And all his acquaintance, and the women that followed him from Galilee, stood afar off, beholding these things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/50
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a4eb973-c218-4934-a64c-1410950d5384>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: LUK 23:50
Text: And, behold, there was a man named Joseph, a counsellor; and he was a good man, and a just:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/51
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b25ae34-e7c5-463f-927d-82fceef84f27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: LUK 23:51
Text: (The same had not consented to the counsel and deed of them;) he was of Arimathaea, a city of the Jews: who also himself waited for the kingdom of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/52
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80bc00fa-f246-43b5-84ea-11467267190c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: LUK 23:52
Text: This man went unto Pilate, and begged the body of Jesus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/53
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abfa2123-4d56-4460-8da7-25c8b095ee5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: LUK 23:53
Text: And he took it down, and wrapped it in linen, and laid it in a sepulchre that was hewn in stone, wherein never man before was laid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/54
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ebd9619-4ca0-4f18-8d77-7942ef7d5f50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: LUK 23:54
Text: And that day was the preparation, and the sabbath drew on.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/55
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20ec041f-ef91-4777-a41c-60b275ebf61c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: LUK 23:55
Text: And the women also, which came with him from Galilee, followed after, and beheld the sepulchre, and how his body was laid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/LUK/23/56
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
