Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: EPH 3:14
Text: For this cause I bow my knees unto the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f98bae60-6a82-495b-afab-aeff90c09393>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: EPH 3:15
Text: Of whom the whole family in heaven and earth is named,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:110f1f46-e69a-448f-9cab-b09ddadd8f0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: EPH 3:16
Text: That he would grant you, according to the riches of his glory, to be strengthened with might by his Spirit in the inner man;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47012aeb-cdcf-4d74-a75b-9cfb6ddb995c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: EPH 3:17
Text: That Christ may dwell in your hearts by faith; that ye, being rooted and grounded in love,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31bf5f4c-5952-452a-a865-65eae54ff8c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: EPH 3:18
Text: May be able to comprehend with all saints what is the breadth, and length, and depth, and height;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fce3ee76-bfe7-4d00-ac3c-e63d22ad215d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: EPH 3:19
Text: And to know the love of Christ, which passeth knowledge, that ye might be filled with all the fulness of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/3/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:249043fd-0303-4f4d-b72a-ce7680ec2388>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: EPH 3:20
Text: Now unto him that is able to do exceeding abundantly above all that we ask or think, according to the power that worketh in us,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/3/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:292e7bf1-72f7-4b5a-a2a3-58804f1f0225>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: EPH 3:21
Text: Unto him be glory in the church by Christ Jesus throughout all ages, world without end. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c068a42-c596-4b6b-a19f-8945d65e4fb9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: EPH 4:1
Text: I therefore, the prisoner of the Lord, beseech you that ye walk worthy of the vocation wherewith ye are called,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1dc5de8c-6409-48e8-9593-d5a5edc1ed6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: EPH 4:2
Text: With all lowliness and meekness, with longsuffering, forbearing one another in love;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47cc5b80-b3f6-43ef-8c6e-2138420cbc29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: EPH 4:3
Text: Endeavouring to keep the unity of the Spirit in the bond of peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5e7faa32-18cd-47b8-af9c-0fbde1dd47b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: EPH 4:4
Text: There is one body, and one Spirit, even as ye are called in one hope of your calling;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:636c2c26-ffff-4e04-8960-6359e334e960>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 59

Reference: EPH 4:5
Text: One Lord, one faith, one baptism,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be11e44f-6093-49d4-950f-42dc20c5ac87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: EPH 4:6
Text: One God and Father of all, who is above all, and through all, and in you all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae500075-1a1a-469a-aa43-cc9de3f93c81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: EPH 4:7
Text: But unto every one of us is given grace according to the measure of the gift of Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbf44dc6-b2c0-4a25-a45b-86107f432d94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: EPH 4:8
Text: Wherefore he saith, When he ascended up on high, he led captivity captive, and gave gifts unto men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f587a59-f45b-4950-a1e8-0dcc8f2bb8bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: EPH 4:9
Text: (Now that he ascended, what is it but that he also descended first into the lower parts of the earth?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2df1da09-2db1-4682-8758-40468e99628c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: EPH 4:10
Text: He that descended is the same also that ascended up far above all heavens, that he might fill all things.)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50cb49d9-7643-4943-b08b-2d9934e63f4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: EPH 4:11
Text: And he gave some, apostles; and some, prophets; and some, evangelists; and some, pastors and teachers;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ea6223e-fa95-4131-b804-9db4a9b3957d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: EPH 4:12
Text: For the perfecting of the saints, for the work of the ministry, for the edifying of the body of Christ:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f89128a2-c8de-4dc5-91a2-f64697506304>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: EPH 4:13
Text: Till we all come in the unity of the faith, and of the knowledge of the Son of God, unto a perfect man, unto the measure of the stature of the fulness of Christ:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e39afeeb-2599-4e99-b2bf-931c0f86c3f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: EPH 4:14
Text: That we henceforth be no more children, tossed to and fro, and carried about with every wind of doctrine, by the sleight of men, and cunning craftiness, whereby they lie in wait to deceive;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6248c631-98c2-468a-8ac3-aaa3768bb591>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: EPH 4:15
Text: But speaking the truth in love, may grow up into him in all things, which is the head, even Christ:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33dc3c28-1982-4e19-9622-b7a7a6bcb846>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: EPH 4:16
Text: From whom the whole body fitly joined together and compacted by that which every joint supplieth, according to the effectual working in the measure of every part, maketh increase of the body unto the edifying of itself in love.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86f4f675-abe1-4eaf-81d2-c711f41fa76d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: EPH 4:17
Text: This I say therefore, and testify in the Lord, that ye henceforth walk not as other Gentiles walk, in the vanity of their mind,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:583cdb92-fa6f-4312-9be7-9c0ad3e09164>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: EPH 4:18
Text: Having the understanding darkened, being alienated from the life of God through the ignorance that is in them, because of the blindness of their heart:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbc61812-cb6b-4005-bfbf-7cdb6a2057e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: EPH 4:19
Text: Who being past feeling have given themselves over unto lasciviousness, to work all uncleanness with greediness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2df9ea7c-dc6f-4154-b558-99f70fac4d3a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 61

Reference: EPH 4:20
Text: But ye have not so learned Christ;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:536c17ae-dd3f-415d-b4aa-38a6f261ae94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: EPH 4:21
Text: If so be that ye have heard him, and have been taught by him, as the truth is in Jesus:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e04e0525-7d0c-42e1-9d69-f68e77fd352e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: EPH 4:22
Text: That ye put off concerning the former conversation the old man, which is corrupt according to the deceitful lusts;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3d51efa-520e-48fb-a101-6b046d879052>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 69

Reference: EPH 4:23
Text: And be renewed in the spirit of your mind;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:725c394c-08e2-4c12-85ee-6d9841de8914>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: EPH 4:24
Text: And that ye put on the new man, which after God is created in righteousness and true holiness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae540377-54f2-4459-9f76-996bd20426ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: EPH 4:25
Text: Wherefore putting away lying, speak every man truth with his neighbour: for we are members one of another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93431281-601e-4497-b575-9eaac9c31185>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: EPH 4:26
Text: Be ye angry, and sin not: let not the sun go down upon your wrath:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0cb3d4c-0cfc-4bb7-8fc9-cd3a9ee5846f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 59

Reference: EPH 4:27
Text: Neither give place to the devil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66b31ed8-4c2f-4c30-b186-00c418230e8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: EPH 4:28
Text: Let him that stole steal no more: but rather let him labour, working with his hands the thing which is good, that he may have to give to him that needeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4539d96c-9fe1-4856-b6ab-33447df39822>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: EPH 4:29
Text: Let no corrupt communication proceed out of your mouth, but that which is good to the use of edifying, that it may minister grace unto the hearers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4c466f9-27e6-40c0-a11d-32c1b0c0ee23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: EPH 4:30
Text: And grieve not the holy Spirit of God, whereby ye are sealed unto the day of redemption.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:162809bb-a37e-4d28-bbd2-0bf9ef94ab05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: EPH 4:31
Text: Let all bitterness, and wrath, and anger, and clamour, and evil speaking, be put away from you, with all malice:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/4/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:421eda66-d8c7-4a67-b59c-43ff06ca5cbb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: EPH 4:32
Text: And be ye kind one to another, tenderhearted, forgiving one another, even as God for Christ’s sake hath forgiven you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f93be92-1712-4d97-a2ae-8e5f82012536>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: EPH 5:1
Text: Be ye therefore followers of God, as dear children;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4315d91a-2831-415f-b0f1-3fba659a6187>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: EPH 5:2
Text: And walk in love, as Christ also hath loved us, and hath given himself for us an offering and a sacrifice to God for a sweetsmelling savour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6e35450-cd52-42cb-b695-4c13298642cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: EPH 5:3
Text: But fornication, and all uncleanness, or covetousness, let it not be once named among you, as becometh saints;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:482439ed-5aae-472d-bdc0-6fcb83510b32>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: EPH 5:4
Text: Neither filthiness, nor foolish talking, nor jesting, which are not convenient: but rather giving of thanks.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4a7540e-f81f-4551-a734-57b8c5564680>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: EPH 5:5
Text: For this ye know, that no whoremonger, nor unclean person, nor covetous man, who is an idolater, hath any inheritance in the kingdom of Christ and of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58200042-a847-4958-875b-94f67d1c76ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: EPH 5:6
Text: Let no man deceive you with vain words: for because of these things cometh the wrath of God upon the children of disobedience.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c20c751-2833-426d-ae97-6f1542595d24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 66

Reference: EPH 5:7
Text: Be not ye therefore partakers with them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f4d933c-c41b-41a0-a66e-aee01c611f3f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: EPH 5:8
Text: For ye were sometimes darkness, but now are ye light in the Lord: walk as children of light:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c031400-604d-482d-83e3-d8c0fb483b7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: EPH 5:9
Text: (For the fruit of the Spirit is in all goodness and righteousness and truth;)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:269fb9ef-855e-4c40-85e8-6b16db1a1cf3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 68

Reference: EPH 5:10
Text: Proving what is acceptable unto the Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50123bcb-1b22-4b3d-a5e3-a1eb5d2afb72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: EPH 5:11
Text: And have no fellowship with the unfruitful works of darkness, but rather reprove them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8ed6f66-e31e-406a-89bb-616cf525131a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: EPH 5:12
Text: For it is a shame even to speak of those things which are done of them in secret.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93b4b78f-de66-4d78-8200-6e83f1172389>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: EPH 5:13
Text: But all things that are reproved are made manifest by the light: for whatsoever doth make manifest is light.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3007992d-f72f-48b7-a920-c6325bdfe7db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: EPH 5:14
Text: Wherefore he saith, Awake thou that sleepest, and arise from the dead, and Christ shall give thee light.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6ac6149-1497-472c-98e2-b57cf2f4b6c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: EPH 5:15
Text: See then that ye walk circumspectly, not as fools, but as wise,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b9be55f-3e3a-4a5e-9456-dcdcb5167a17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: EPH 5:16
Text: Redeeming the time, because the days are evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67b0947a-a1d7-48a2-a16e-f0a6cfd4a968>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: EPH 5:17
Text: Wherefore be ye not unwise, but understanding what the will of the Lord is.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:854c1b97-f470-426f-8e8a-7a10e0dabe39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: EPH 5:18
Text: And be not drunk with wine, wherein is excess; but be filled with the Spirit;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0a77878-4d04-426e-aa5a-eb6fb271e5bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: EPH 5:19
Text: Speaking to yourselves in psalms and hymns and spiritual songs, singing and making melody in your heart to the Lord;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bac34f7-5e8f-4d53-965b-e3a5b9451cbb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: EPH 5:20
Text: Giving thanks always for all things unto God and the Father in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14ddc093-9499-453d-8de4-7dad3404e538>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: EPH 5:21
Text: Submitting yourselves one to another in the fear of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9501251a-9466-4f34-a97f-eb01966af195>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: EPH 5:22
Text: Wives, submit yourselves unto your own husbands, as unto the Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb6a423b-1462-497d-a377-b9ec1cba86a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: EPH 5:23
Text: For the husband is the head of the wife, even as Christ is the head of the church: and he is the saviour of the body.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6dcafd85-d7c5-446f-9cd7-75fb29896b97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: EPH 5:24
Text: Therefore as the church is subject unto Christ, so let the wives be to their own husbands in every thing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f5197e3-84d9-48d1-864d-ba18ca88803b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: EPH 5:25
Text: Husbands, love your wives, even as Christ also loved the church, and gave himself for it;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1560007-8021-4c85-b420-004af940e45c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: EPH 5:26
Text: That he might sanctify and cleanse it with the washing of water by the word,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:919ad1c6-18e5-4acc-b6aa-43d5af868fea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: EPH 5:27
Text: That he might present it to himself a glorious church, not having spot, or wrinkle, or any such thing; but that it should be holy and without blemish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3a0e405-08d9-4552-a3d5-4384122803a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: EPH 5:28
Text: So ought men to love their wives as their own bodies. He that loveth his wife loveth himself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:567ecb28-20d4-459e-84a7-34eed06702c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: EPH 5:29
Text: For no man ever yet hated his own flesh; but nourisheth and cherisheth it, even as the Lord the church:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3f991c10-bd6f-4eff-86c8-ee59033298db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: EPH 5:30
Text: For we are members of his body, of his flesh, and of his bones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37000ef5-5c8c-4bca-b9a7-559364585cd8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: EPH 5:31
Text: For this cause shall a man leave his father and mother, and shall be joined unto his wife, and they two shall be one flesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad35bdc0-79a9-41dc-8080-a34b78398fa3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: EPH 5:32
Text: This is a great mystery: but I speak concerning Christ and the church.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/5/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2200a1a9-82da-4d23-8dc7-923636e1ae30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: EPH 5:33
Text: Nevertheless let every one of you in particular so love his wife even as himself; and the wife see that she reverence her husband.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1566f556-cb69-4523-a52f-d609d7cea68c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: EPH 6:1
Text: Children, obey your parents in the Lord: for this is right.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79cd0991-bbe0-4507-bb71-61cfe6c1db87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: EPH 6:2
Text: Honour thy father and mother; which is the first commandment with promise;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36a7b51f-1c37-491a-8b6f-57dc70d45ad1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: EPH 6:3
Text: That it may be well with thee, and thou mayest live long on the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8328019-7a19-4cb8-b421-22ee44002e5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: EPH 6:4
Text: And, ye fathers, provoke not your children to wrath: but bring them up in the nurture and admonition of the Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4621e66-4efb-4522-91b9-1d34f210d1c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: EPH 6:5
Text: Servants, be obedient to them that are your masters according to the flesh, with fear and trembling, in singleness of your heart, as unto Christ;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d62f12a5-9875-46b0-960d-347c3cdd563c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: EPH 6:6
Text: Not with eyeservice, as menpleasers; but as the servants of Christ, doing the will of God from the heart;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce08c461-d17c-4a40-b2f1-e63ccbdfa074>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: EPH 6:7
Text: With good will doing service, as to the Lord, and not to men:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd8218b6-0363-4558-b744-1929f4962cf3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: EPH 6:8
Text: Knowing that whatsoever good thing any man doeth, the same shall he receive of the Lord, whether he be bond or free.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2dee0c03-c9dd-400a-98d3-7e31ac7cb8dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: EPH 6:9
Text: And, ye masters, do the same things unto them, forbearing threatening: knowing that your Master also is in heaven; neither is there respect of persons with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22f8419f-7a57-4fdd-882a-b142a787282f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: EPH 6:10
Text: Finally, my brethren, be strong in the Lord, and in the power of his might.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ab04247-f734-4728-b2f8-3e5710b577bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: EPH 6:11
Text: Put on the whole armour of God, that ye may be able to stand against the wiles of the devil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba031e56-4afa-4120-8c9c-04b8d8c1ba59>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: EPH 6:12
Text: For we wrestle not against flesh and blood, but against principalities, against powers, against the rulers of the darkness of this world, against spiritual wickedness in high places.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5a1805a-704a-4fd5-8953-b920b739be35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: EPH 6:13
Text: Wherefore take unto you the whole armour of God, that ye may be able to withstand in the evil day, and having done all, to stand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27a629be-aee9-4404-993e-522647f16b4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: EPH 6:14
Text: Stand therefore, having your loins girt about with truth, and having on the breastplate of righteousness;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65365fed-6f2b-4703-94a8-ce7bb42b5c4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: EPH 6:15
Text: And your feet shod with the preparation of the gospel of peace;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e050b9a9-0306-4048-87b2-5a7386ea8957>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: EPH 6:16
Text: Above all, taking the shield of faith, wherewith ye shall be able to quench all the fiery darts of the wicked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:195e9aa1-7132-4322-93b0-959606b61ef8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: EPH 6:17
Text: And take the helmet of salvation, and the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of God:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d3de25b-8704-4c33-9435-2ff21d7ab925>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: EPH 6:18
Text: Praying always with all prayer and supplication in the Spirit, and watching thereunto with all perseverance and supplication for all saints;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c184e48b-7b1f-4995-a9c9-d308ac8f22f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: EPH 6:19
Text: And for me, that utterance may be given unto me, that I may open my mouth boldly, to make known the mystery of the gospel,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e75baaa-9546-4b8e-a189-523a14fec535>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: EPH 6:20
Text: For which I am an ambassador in bonds: that therein I may speak boldly, as I ought to speak.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d793072-b9c0-4af1-aff1-01e1feac615d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: EPH 6:21
Text: But that ye also may know my affairs, and how I do, Tychicus, a beloved brother and faithful minister in the Lord, shall make known to you all things:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb672349-a850-429f-a19c-e869c59f7d0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: EPH 6:22
Text: Whom I have sent unto you for the same purpose, that ye might know our affairs, and that he might comfort your hearts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14e20962-6f42-4163-956d-a695b7c9aa02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: EPH 6:23
Text: Peace be to the brethren, and love with faith, from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/EPH/6/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c20f9606-3ed1-45c0-bcc3-4a02dca9b588>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: EPH 6:24
Text: Grace be with all them that love our Lord Jesus Christ in sincerity. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97b85727-d9a9-4dcd-8817-92f1115a4173>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: PHP 1:1
Text: Paul and Timotheus, the servants of Jesus Christ, to all the saints in Christ Jesus which are at Philippi, with the bishops and deacons:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fe57eb2-265d-4f1e-8bf4-625236ad26fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PHP 1:2
Text: Grace be unto you, and peace, from God our Father, and from the Lord Jesus Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee451d66-a8ff-4767-9c40-8f7356f582c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 71

Reference: PHP 1:3
Text: I thank my God upon every remembrance of you,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5512271b-34ef-4779-9ca9-10716cd110e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PHP 1:4
Text: Always in every prayer of mine for you all making request with joy,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee2b7da0-c1b9-41e2-9996-2a38d0d522dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PHP 1:5
Text: For your fellowship in the gospel from the first day until now;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3382b736-a58f-4474-b649-ca3a278d3226>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: PHP 1:6
Text: Being confident of this very thing, that he which hath begun a good work in you will perform it until the day of Jesus Christ:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1212ca0b-5231-4b10-aaf0-aedc276aa471>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 224

Reference: PHP 1:7
Text: Even as it is meet for me to think this of you all, because I have you in my heart; inasmuch as both in my bonds, and in the defence and confirmation of the gospel, ye all are partakers of my grace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aecfa750-6c3a-46ff-a349-2dc9ba1d5082>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: PHP 1:8
Text: For God is my record, how greatly I long after you all in the bowels of Jesus Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ac2d129-2003-4e93-b986-baba7c6f3e55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: PHP 1:9
Text: And this I pray, that your love may abound yet more and more in knowledge and in all judgment;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5212f8c-d445-49eb-bd13-c695600b1fdd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: PHP 1:10
Text: That ye may approve things that are excellent; that ye may be sincere and without offence till the day of Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3680caa9-7a36-4de9-a373-9e3f4dcc272e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PHP 1:11
Text: Being filled with the fruits of righteousness, which are by Jesus Christ, unto the glory and praise of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8bbe7ca5-daa0-4e63-b590-3c06338d5caf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: PHP 1:12
Text: But I would ye should understand, brethren, that the things which happened unto me have fallen out rather unto the furtherance of the gospel;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/13
