Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: PHP 1:13
Text: So that my bonds in Christ are manifest in all the palace, and in all other places;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44886ae8-6920-4c0b-b0ac-08742cb7b36b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: PHP 1:14
Text: And many of the brethren in the Lord, waxing confident by my bonds, are much more bold to speak the word without fear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99682cc1-110b-4f82-adf3-1c7d310a5442>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PHP 1:15
Text: Some indeed preach Christ even of envy and strife; and some also of good will:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:224d5392-864d-4a05-9d30-a41337b25b10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: PHP 1:16
Text: The one preach Christ of contention, not sincerely, supposing to add affliction to my bonds:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b0824b2-41b5-4add-b156-18f535f11348>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: PHP 1:17
Text: But the other of love, knowing that I am set for the defence of the gospel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a148009a-a521-45e0-83d8-262ccdacdccb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: PHP 1:18
Text: What then? notwithstanding, every way, whether in pretence, or in truth, Christ is preached; and I therein do rejoice, yea, and will rejoice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7cd61dcc-72a8-493b-b9bd-84a4a8e32f42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: PHP 1:19
Text: For I know that this shall turn to my salvation through your prayer, and the supply of the Spirit of Jesus Christ,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c849d634-c72f-4006-ba07-6e4f0ad174d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: PHP 1:20
Text: According to my earnest expectation and my hope, that in nothing I shall be ashamed, but that with all boldness, as always, so now also Christ shall be magnified in my body, whether it be by life, or by death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1dbff580-7ada-47a4-9388-25b0fb56194f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: PHP 1:21
Text: For to me to live is Christ, and to die is gain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa99a08c-3a9f-4426-9265-afd18136ff85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: PHP 1:22
Text: But if I live in the flesh, this is the fruit of my labour: yet what I shall choose I wot not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:750de95f-7a0f-4127-8e75-024d398fd5c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PHP 1:23
Text: For I am in a strait betwixt two, having a desire to depart, and to be with Christ; which is far better:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abcc56de-e077-45ed-bad7-cbb11a9515f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PHP 1:24
Text: Nevertheless to abide in the flesh is more needful for you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1bcd5331-87dc-4652-9e6a-0ddb99390cb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: PHP 1:25
Text: And having this confidence, I know that I shall abide and continue with you all for your furtherance and joy of faith;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cabb63f-000d-4532-ae15-07cf43b7b4d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PHP 1:26
Text: That your rejoicing may be more abundant in Jesus Christ for me by my coming to you again.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eacd91e0-e6be-4e58-81b6-d433d3f726a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: PHP 1:27
Text: Only let your conversation be as it becometh the gospel of Christ: that whether I come and see you, or else be absent, I may hear of your affairs, that ye stand fast in one spirit, with one mind striving together for the faith of the gospel;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5ee1d3c-9b1b-42bd-8a4a-fb1bcf81c7ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: PHP 1:28
Text: And in nothing terrified by your adversaries: which is to them an evident token of perdition, but to you of salvation, and that of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fd1fae3-a353-4adf-928d-e5b25fc7d509>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: PHP 1:29
Text: For unto you it is given in the behalf of Christ, not only to believe on him, but also to suffer for his sake;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/1/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7e5786a-3633-4232-9cee-120b00a72bf4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PHP 1:30
Text: Having the same conflict which ye saw in me, and now hear to be in me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:878e9c97-c4ad-41a4-a708-b4a7ab5717e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: PHP 2:1
Text: If there be therefore any consolation in Christ, if any comfort of love, if any fellowship of the Spirit, if any bowels and mercies,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57c044d1-5d4e-4704-942e-9dbbe581f491>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PHP 2:2
Text: Fulfil ye my joy, that ye be likeminded, having the same love, being of one accord, of one mind.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b6b1deb-8e36-485d-94f8-75c0da62420e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: PHP 2:3
Text: Let nothing be done through strife or vainglory; but in lowliness of mind let each esteem other better than themselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52a09c5b-cc04-44e7-8d0f-2102378d121e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PHP 2:4
Text: Look not every man on his own things, but every man also on the things of others.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb74f3d8-c8e8-4280-9972-397d251ce6da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: PHP 2:5
Text: Let this mind be in you, which was also in Christ Jesus:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42c70f9a-245f-4a25-87a1-0d98c043052a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: PHP 2:6
Text: Who, being in the form of God, thought it not robbery to be equal with God:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8e95a7a-6878-4bb4-890a-4d584cbd5fab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PHP 2:7
Text: But made himself of no reputation, and took upon him the form of a servant, and was made in the likeness of men:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78a04579-d24d-4c75-852d-c2117f8b7e92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: PHP 2:8
Text: And being found in fashion as a man, he humbled himself, and became obedient unto death, even the death of the cross.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a54823f9-e1ca-4e67-bebc-f2deea98ca88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PHP 2:9
Text: Wherefore God also hath highly exalted him, and given him a name which is above every name:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b4dbf82-840b-472c-9d32-099ac4a8e524>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: PHP 2:10
Text: That at the name of Jesus every knee should bow, of things in heaven, and things in earth, and things under the earth;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82a04b45-ee1f-4828-a6b2-5b274f61f949>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: PHP 2:11
Text: And that every tongue should confess that Jesus Christ is Lord, to the glory of God the Father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38f31a7c-c1bf-4d64-b551-f3cccb41b2d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: PHP 2:12
Text: Wherefore, my beloved, as ye have always obeyed, not as in my presence only, but now much more in my absence, work out your own salvation with fear and trembling.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04ba6613-cebe-427d-880d-41d770789ad1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: PHP 2:13
Text: For it is God which worketh in you both to will and to do of his good pleasure.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33d8d2bc-60cb-4912-824c-1de81c45adf1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: PHP 2:14
Text: Do all things without murmurings and disputings:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6c92132-19c2-4131-831c-fe53d7111dec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: PHP 2:15
Text: That ye may be blameless and harmless, the sons of God, without rebuke, in the midst of a crooked and perverse nation, among whom ye shine as lights in the world;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94f7ad93-639b-4daa-bf23-fd073ce56c96>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: PHP 2:16
Text: Holding forth the word of life; that I may rejoice in the day of Christ, that I have not run in vain, neither laboured in vain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7906d4e-dc47-4ff8-8ad8-ae46402a8465>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: PHP 2:17
Text: Yea, and if I be offered upon the sacrifice and service of your faith, I joy, and rejoice with you all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa392843-c54c-4674-8ca7-8a962691774e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: PHP 2:18
Text: For the same cause also do ye joy, and rejoice with me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87500dec-9836-496f-b529-91f685a59c3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: PHP 2:19
Text: But I trust in the Lord Jesus to send Timotheus shortly unto you, that I also may be of good comfort, when I know your state.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a00582b3-45aa-49d7-9191-5f269d917c6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PHP 2:20
Text: For I have no man likeminded, who will naturally care for your state.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:312bd838-5bae-40d7-aca8-8cd80f8937d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PHP 2:21
Text: For all seek their own, not the things which are Jesus Christ’s.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0cf6aa0b-668d-4da7-9b4e-2d955e88668b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PHP 2:22
Text: But ye know the proof of him, that, as a son with the father, he hath served with me in the gospel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1b6eee2-e00e-42c0-a090-f7767260b1f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: PHP 2:23
Text: Him therefore I hope to send presently, so soon as I shall see how it will go with me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8dbdca65-a145-40a3-b254-a92c30af8c1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PHP 2:24
Text: But I trust in the Lord that I also myself shall come shortly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69f2d4a3-c02d-4dac-9c73-f9652c31a641>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: PHP 2:25
Text: Yet I supposed it necessary to send to you Epaphroditus, my brother, and companion in labour, and fellowsoldier, but your messenger, and he that ministered to my wants.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c56141a-8059-45a6-8bda-dac0f2da2b1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: PHP 2:26
Text: For he longed after you all, and was full of heaviness, because that ye had heard that he had been sick.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:486245d2-6c33-4fe6-b02f-70d70a9f071f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: PHP 2:27
Text: For indeed he was sick nigh unto death: but God had mercy on him; and not on him only, but on me also, lest I should have sorrow upon sorrow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a51ce21-e039-48bf-92a7-590a2971d468>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: PHP 2:28
Text: I sent him therefore the more carefully, that, when ye see him again, ye may rejoice, and that I may be the less sorrowful.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d5827c9-cf62-4e16-9a47-a54d0f1117ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PHP 2:29
Text: Receive him therefore in the Lord with all gladness; and hold such in reputation:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/2/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:62a3e034-5c57-446f-8e7f-a7c25b183aaf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: PHP 2:30
Text: Because for the work of Christ he was nigh unto death, not regarding his life, to supply your lack of service toward me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c90a650c-5734-41e1-971e-103830b6236b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: PHP 3:1
Text: Finally, my brethren, rejoice in the Lord. To write the same things to you, to me indeed is not grievous, but for you it is safe.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83ca3639-c11e-44b7-9d1e-831709197e85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: PHP 3:2
Text: Beware of dogs, beware of evil workers, beware of the concision.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8266227-12fe-4a16-8d0d-87e768c3e6ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: PHP 3:3
Text: For we are the circumcision, which worship God in the spirit, and rejoice in Christ Jesus, and have no confidence in the flesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6e729db-193a-497d-b792-7ee0db208a09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: PHP 3:4
Text: Though I might also have confidence in the flesh. If any other man thinketh that he hath whereof he might trust in the flesh, I more:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4988ffdb-b72b-41eb-82e2-ffca844fea75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

