Text: Concerning zeal, persecuting the church; touching the righteousness which is in the law, blameless.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98625e52-efed-4935-97ca-bd34ba3a231c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: PHP 3:7
Text: But what things were gain to me, those I counted loss for Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d17dfe3-5ffd-46fe-81e0-3ece811755e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: PHP 3:8
Text: Yea doubtless, and I count all things but loss for the excellency of the knowledge of Christ Jesus my Lord: for whom I have suffered the loss of all things, and do count them but dung, that I may win Christ,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d36c3ef1-1daa-4648-998f-c860a178784a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: PHP 3:9
Text: And be found in him, not having mine own righteousness, which is of the law, but that which is through the faith of Christ, the righteousness which is of God by faith:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e71da86-97ca-4f38-a52a-a6c0884bbe19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: PHP 3:10
Text: That I may know him, and the power of his resurrection, and the fellowship of his sufferings, being made conformable unto his death;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a28e7e33-015f-456d-b2f2-909a5daeedb4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: PHP 3:11
Text: If by any means I might attain unto the resurrection of the dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85520c97-5995-4fa3-a705-5d8b682f78dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: PHP 3:12
Text: Not as though I had already attained, either were already perfect: but I follow after, if that I may apprehend that for which also I am apprehended of Christ Jesus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ced6b387-48a7-49b4-aca2-faf69f503899>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: PHP 3:13
Text: Brethren, I count not myself to have apprehended: but this one thing I do, forgetting those things which are behind, and reaching forth unto those things which are before,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09e715e9-5678-4c5f-a60a-e18bc54c71f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PHP 3:14
Text: I press toward the mark for the prize of the high calling of God in Christ Jesus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd26dacb-65bd-4b80-b271-e4c23c00340a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: PHP 3:15
Text: Let us therefore, as many as be perfect, be thus minded: and if in any thing ye be otherwise minded, God shall reveal even this unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25cf593b-1306-482f-90c0-fb884a3803c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: PHP 3:16
Text: Nevertheless, whereto we have already attained, let us walk by the same rule, let us mind the same thing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1ca1cae2-92ee-4336-9eac-8ad6f8ec18ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: PHP 3:17
Text: Brethren, be followers together of me, and mark them which walk so as ye have us for an ensample.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a4d3b77-fc72-4dae-b0c4-a76f8e0f3d00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: PHP 3:18
Text: (For many walk, of whom I have told you often, and now tell you even weeping, that they are the enemies of the cross of Christ:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4592c9c6-1b3d-433b-9247-57e176089b13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: PHP 3:19
Text: Whose end is destruction, whose God is their belly, and whose glory is in their shame, who mind earthly things.)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/3/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2291649b-9c20-4cf8-9dfd-a7233bfd9343>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: PHP 3:20
Text: For our conversation is in heaven; from whence also we look for the Saviour, the Lord Jesus Christ:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/3/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f28f5de-d29d-4655-b3ff-68e912f4699a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: PHP 3:21
Text: Who shall change our vile body, that it may be fashioned like unto his glorious body, according to the working whereby he is able even to subdue all things unto himself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:617c7f90-972a-4544-81c5-2da95548537e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: PHP 4:1
Text: Therefore, my brethren dearly beloved and longed for, my joy and crown, so stand fast in the Lord, my dearly beloved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:293c7016-41fe-459f-b011-f70c7227b800>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PHP 4:2
Text: I beseech Euodias, and beseech Syntyche, that they be of the same mind in the Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:426577d3-827a-4097-bdcd-e8e4d2fd6488>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: PHP 4:3
Text: And I intreat thee also, true yokefellow, help those women which laboured with me in the gospel, with Clement also, and with other my fellowlabourers, whose names are in the book of life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4af82866-0044-48db-9f00-751db2afb881>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: PHP 4:4
Text: Rejoice in the Lord alway: and again I say, Rejoice.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:391f4cc9-9aa1-4fed-907a-4a7d6d89f582>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PHP 4:5
Text: Let your moderation be known unto all men. The Lord is at hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3c95a1b4-9bef-4f8c-a074-0864baff18b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: PHP 4:6
Text: Be careful for nothing; but in every thing by prayer and supplication with thanksgiving let your requests be made known unto God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b13eb380-afd5-46a0-b326-641cf672af02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: PHP 4:7
Text: And the peace of God, which passeth all understanding, shall keep your hearts and minds through Christ Jesus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46f906c9-da31-49af-86ef-5bb70228b5e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 301

Reference: PHP 4:8
Text: Finally, brethren, whatsoever things are true, whatsoever things are honest, whatsoever things are just, whatsoever things are pure, whatsoever things are lovely, whatsoever things are of good report; if there be any virtue, and if there be any praise, think on these things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d39b7ab-c53c-43a6-a833-603743f9ecb3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: PHP 4:9
Text: Those things, which ye have both learned, and received, and heard, and seen in me, do: and the God of peace shall be with you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3d98c46-291a-4d8a-9a6b-385085c0c800>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: PHP 4:10
Text: But I rejoiced in the Lord greatly, that now at the last your care of me hath flourished again; wherein ye were also careful, but ye lacked opportunity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:347c4de0-b4af-4eb5-9ff9-79c08133085c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: PHP 4:11
Text: Not that I speak in respect of want: for I have learned, in whatsoever state I am, therewith to be content.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:613d6271-6c74-42de-86b7-95b9ab30f1b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: PHP 4:12
Text: I know both how to be abased, and I know how to abound: every where and in all things I am instructed both to be full and to be hungry, both to abound and to suffer need.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d5f0504-82a6-44ae-9224-6e785d26fb37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: PHP 4:13
Text: I can do all things through Christ which strengtheneth me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f2f3d08-6400-48b4-84af-08629e4386b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: PHP 4:14
Text: Notwithstanding ye have well done, that ye did communicate with my affliction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83329773-11fb-40d1-b420-08b0a8092d87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: PHP 4:15
Text: Now ye Philippians know also, that in the beginning of the gospel, when I departed from Macedonia, no church communicated with me as concerning giving and receiving, but ye only.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14fb3bfd-d121-4d16-8b5a-645cadcad405>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: PHP 4:16
Text: For even in Thessalonica ye sent once and again unto my necessity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57904dc6-5483-46b3-ab1f-f29a21baebbe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: PHP 4:17
Text: Not because I desire a gift: but I desire fruit that may abound to your account.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/4/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:afa67d30-e42e-44c1-8b64-3355b36c760c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: PHP 4:18
Text: But I have all, and abound: I am full, having received of Epaphroditus the things which were sent from you, an odour of a sweet smell, a sacrifice acceptable, wellpleasing to God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/4/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:933966b4-7b9b-402b-a1af-48f926f5d913>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: PHP 4:19
Text: But my God shall supply all your need according to his riches in glory by Christ Jesus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/4/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2b1f98a-320b-4bec-9ab8-bf387b6ea78f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PHP 4:20
Text: Now unto God and our Father be glory for ever and ever. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/4/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4872bac0-5690-460d-94d7-7df06c71535f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PHP 4:21
Text: Salute every saint in Christ Jesus. The brethren which are with me greet you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/4/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f03d6bd-88e6-4876-861e-e91a8fe35861>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: PHP 4:22
Text: All the saints salute you, chiefly they that are of Caesar’s household.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHP/4/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bcae2195-ca04-46cb-9ff6-954f97ca3146>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: PHP 4:23
Text: The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you all. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89315282-f93c-48f0-adb5-c7518011b1d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: COL 1:1
Text: Paul, an apostle of Jesus Christ by the will of God, and Timotheus our brother,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0dafffb1-f874-495e-ab4d-9e3dfb3679a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: COL 1:2
Text: To the saints and faithful brethren in Christ which are at Colosse: Grace be unto you, and peace, from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:765dfdf3-2fba-4d36-abb0-44363c7fd092>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: COL 1:3
Text: We give thanks to God and the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, praying always for you,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ce37284-dce7-4281-8bf9-1fae5dc0a29c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: COL 1:4
Text: Since we heard of your faith in Christ Jesus, and of the love which ye have to all the saints,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44fb01e3-ed75-4ea2-af94-444939bbf0bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: COL 1:5
Text: For the hope which is laid up for you in heaven, whereof ye heard before in the word of the truth of the gospel;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e816561-9d26-4ebc-b340-7cd4ba2c6a5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: COL 1:6
Text: Which is come unto you, as it is in all the world; and bringeth forth fruit, as it doth also in you, since the day ye heard of it, and knew the grace of God in truth:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41823386-ddf0-401a-9131-75d4c50765fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: COL 1:7
Text: As ye also learned of Epaphras our dear fellowservant, who is for you a faithful minister of Christ;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:455a826c-e3b5-4fa9-9ac1-6f0ff4d62140>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: COL 1:8
Text: Who also declared unto us your love in the Spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddc4848c-b323-475e-8815-69bce2d39455>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: COL 1:9
Text: For this cause we also, since the day we heard it, do not cease to pray for you, and to desire that ye might be filled with the knowledge of his will in all wisdom and spiritual understanding;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f41ea82-6514-46a2-8756-332a4d60d3ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: COL 1:10
Text: That ye might walk worthy of the Lord unto all pleasing, being fruitful in every good work, and increasing in the knowledge of God;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20dfa698-14f5-44aa-937e-52e1be4af4ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: COL 1:11
Text: Strengthened with all might, according to his glorious power, unto all patience and longsuffering with joyfulness;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58c396ba-853b-4b27-92e5-8f6783b422de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: COL 1:12
Text: Giving thanks unto the Father, which hath made us meet to be partakers of the inheritance of the saints in light:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20beab17-2233-4843-aa89-16512bfd014f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: COL 1:13
Text: Who hath delivered us from the power of darkness, and hath translated us into the kingdom of his dear Son:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b701d3ec-8106-4da9-9f51-e622681a6975>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: COL 1:14
Text: In whom we have redemption through his blood, even the forgiveness of sins:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4606a8b8-345e-4da5-a95e-3ded907af6b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: COL 1:15
Text: Who is the image of the invisible God, the firstborn of every creature:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94ae7bce-0ac2-4f6d-92c4-feff9387fdf3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: COL 1:16
Text: For by him were all things created, that are in heaven, and that are in earth, visible and invisible, whether they be thrones, or dominions, or principalities, or powers: all things were created by him, and for him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f595f816-47a9-4ef9-96cb-f7a825bdf146>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: COL 1:17
Text: And he is before all things, and by him all things consist.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f894f29a-2845-46bf-ad7d-415d523e54da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: COL 1:18
Text: And he is the head of the body, the church: who is the beginning, the firstborn from the dead; that in all things he might have the preeminence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8c06689-5200-4bf9-bea6-aa4d31bdc3ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: COL 1:19
Text: For it pleased the Father that in him should all fulness dwell;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d0fef70-255e-4430-8e90-e5d5d978da31>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: COL 1:20
Text: And, having made peace through the blood of his cross, by him to reconcile all things unto himself; by him, I say, whether they be things in earth, or things in heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60238544-1f92-4e48-bba6-47753ecb154b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: COL 1:21
Text: And you, that were sometime alienated and enemies in your mind by wicked works, yet now hath he reconciled


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0fb8287e-6da6-4270-805c-15d17c76afcc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: COL 1:22
Text: In the body of his flesh through death, to present you holy and unblameable and unreproveable in his sight:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77d8f053-8d07-4541-a480-a463794dd0a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: COL 1:23
Text: If ye continue in the faith grounded and settled, and be not moved away from the hope of the gospel, which ye have heard, and which was preached to every creature which is under heaven; whereof I Paul am made a minister;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4760d628-16a2-4fca-b267-6cffa1baba2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: COL 1:24
Text: Who now rejoice in my sufferings for you, and fill up that which is behind of the afflictions of Christ in my flesh for his body’s sake, which is the church:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30d0f073-d3ac-4da7-b43d-8fe2616aa68e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: COL 1:25
Text: Whereof I am made a minister, according to the dispensation of God which is given to me for you, to fulfil the word of God;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:40700e99-2ca7-4742-a0b8-743b3204ecab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: COL 1:26
Text: Even the mystery which hath been hid from ages and from generations, but now is made manifest to his saints:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3f2416a-bcc6-4529-93cb-32d670c1df4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: COL 1:27
Text: To whom God would make known what is the riches of the glory of this mystery among the Gentiles; which is Christ in you, the hope of glory:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c268182b-a3d1-4cda-b85a-8f63c1b123b6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: COL 1:28
Text: Whom we preach, warning every man, and teaching every man in all wisdom; that we may present every man perfect in Christ Jesus:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/1/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd357936-e216-4132-8791-33a1b27ed8b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: COL 1:29
Text: Whereunto I also labour, striving according to his working, which worketh in me mightily.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:382ec9a3-1c7b-43ed-8abc-18df9f2901c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: COL 2:1
Text: For I would that ye knew what great conflict I have for you, and for them at Laodicea, and for as many as have not seen my face in the flesh;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:85e923a4-b7fc-412a-b1f2-76cedcfcba24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: COL 2:2
Text: That their hearts might be comforted, being knit together in love, and unto all riches of the full assurance of understanding, to the acknowledgement of the mystery of God, and of the Father, and of Christ;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65356bcc-877f-4690-a9c2-26e46a4354d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: COL 2:3
Text: In whom are hid all the treasures of wisdom and knowledge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0bac32ef-4e4c-4f63-83cb-1515b26e2140>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: COL 2:4
Text: And this I say, lest any man should beguile you with enticing words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f566775-1ad9-4ae7-ac53-60c9b0f3bcc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: COL 2:5
Text: For though I be absent in the flesh, yet am I with you in the spirit, joying and beholding your order, and the stedfastness of your faith in Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc18b88a-47f8-4f68-9def-c00aebcef308>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: COL 2:6
Text: As ye have therefore received Christ Jesus the Lord, so walk ye in him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f4943f8-de67-4fb9-90a5-4e8dfb3f0144>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: COL 2:7
Text: Rooted and built up in him, and stablished in the faith, as ye have been taught, abounding therein with thanksgiving.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42766375-bf1d-4aeb-a741-302a8e3071e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: COL 2:8
Text: Beware lest any man spoil you through philosophy and vain deceit, after the tradition of men, after the rudiments of the world, and not after Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1a4cfad4-c6db-4022-a0b5-698aa19792b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: COL 2:9
Text: For in him dwelleth all the fulness of the Godhead bodily.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04326e6e-f546-4a2d-9c1e-cf7f6f15339a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: COL 2:10
Text: And ye are complete in him, which is the head of all principality and power:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82dd9ff1-fcde-4879-89b3-1cc9699c3b72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: COL 2:11
Text: In whom also ye are circumcised with the circumcision made without hands, in putting off the body of the sins of the flesh by the circumcision of Christ:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffd300bf-4c7b-421d-b197-9c198f9359b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: COL 2:12
Text: Buried with him in baptism, wherein also ye are risen with him through the faith of the operation of God, who hath raised him from the dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68662a7f-3e96-43f8-9d17-7f06f4d23f06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: COL 2:13
Text: And you, being dead in your sins and the uncircumcision of your flesh, hath he quickened together with him, having forgiven you all trespasses;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8080efab-86b5-45a2-8f7e-c2af17500a85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: COL 2:14
Text: Blotting out the handwriting of ordinances that was against us, which was contrary to us, and took it out of the way, nailing it to his cross;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b431278-4cd0-4b7b-b331-e0154f8f703c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: COL 2:15
Text: And having spoiled principalities and powers, he made a shew of them openly, triumphing over them in it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4617a7a-6069-4a77-a179-86781a60a761>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: COL 2:16
Text: Let no man therefore judge you in meat, or in drink, or in respect of an holyday, or of the new moon, or of the sabbath days:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0342ef2-c444-4923-b213-d55d893ec8f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: COL 2:17
Text: Which are a shadow of things to come; but the body is of Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c919286-d94e-4b90-b00c-78da36c053f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: COL 2:18
Text: Let no man beguile you of your reward in a voluntary humility and worshipping of angels, intruding into those things which he hath not seen, vainly puffed up by his fleshly mind,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2244daa-6e36-4cde-a301-667a9d684058>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: COL 2:19
Text: And not holding the Head, from which all the body by joints and bands having nourishment ministered, and knit together, increaseth with the increase of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:984d06a4-3acd-44eb-92c3-034d8380d81d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: COL 2:20
Text: Wherefore if ye be dead with Christ from the rudiments of the world, why, as though living in the world, are ye subject to ordinances,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a350eae-10d0-4cee-b762-4b5a78e3ba01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 61

Reference: COL 2:21
Text: (Touch not; taste not; handle not;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9aad514d-c63f-41e3-a0c1-e5e099628a64>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: COL 2:22
Text: Which all are to perish with the using;) after the commandments and doctrines of men?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/2/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bd1bc7c-2e9b-4a02-9090-35581150cc15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: COL 2:23
Text: Which things have indeed a shew of wisdom in will worship, and humility, and neglecting of the body: not in any honour to the satisfying of the flesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c7f4879-56f4-4c84-b260-f4f7f142a9fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: COL 3:1
Text: If ye then be risen with Christ, seek those things which are above, where Christ sitteth on the right hand of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01801983-b840-4e7a-9d91-c9059a8d3e65>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: COL 3:2
Text: Set your affection on things above, not on things on the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5904660-406f-4705-9ea2-81a35662e853>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: COL 3:3
Text: For ye are dead, and your life is hid with Christ in God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22c254b6-eb5f-47e1-8f47-410f11bbd60b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: COL 3:4
Text: When Christ, who is our life, shall appear, then shall ye also appear with him in glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb5450b7-3fe4-4b7c-8f74-7d5ab76c370d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: COL 3:5
Text: Mortify therefore your members which are upon the earth; fornication, uncleanness, inordinate affection, evil concupiscence, and covetousness, which is idolatry:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:331c2730-b655-4c22-9ca1-06c4ad2fd764>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: COL 3:6
Text: For which things’ sake the wrath of God cometh on the children of disobedience:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f01d4f62-5b15-4609-8703-a56df587410f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: COL 3:7
Text: In the which ye also walked some time, when ye lived in them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c20a3fde-b361-4985-91c3-47956d047b99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: COL 3:8
Text: But now ye also put off all these; anger, wrath, malice, blasphemy, filthy communication out of your mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cddbf9fd-7a1f-47d5-bcd2-0aaf13a8e193>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: COL 3:9
Text: Lie not one to another, seeing that ye have put off the old man with his deeds;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b021b77-a19c-4cc7-a22c-38e94e92f423>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: COL 3:10
Text: And have put on the new man, which is renewed in knowledge after the image of him that created him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a902b586-c198-4039-a18c-d0f1a194ff08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: COL 3:11
Text: Where there is neither Greek nor Jew, circumcision nor uncircumcision, Barbarian, Scythian, bond nor free: but Christ is all, and in all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3147501f-6fb7-4031-8c2d-215ad7d1b348>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: COL 3:12
Text: Put on therefore, as the elect of God, holy and beloved, bowels of mercies, kindness, humbleness of mind, meekness, longsuffering;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8a16fcb-adb9-4ac6-8fbc-adc77e2315fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: COL 3:13
Text: Forbearing one another, and forgiving one another, if any man have a quarrel against any: even as Christ forgave you, so also do ye.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f71a7c52-ac76-4f6a-95ac-10ef1b416014>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: COL 3:14
Text: And above all these things put on charity, which is the bond of perfectness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14443ed1-774e-45ea-97ed-91065ccd583d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: COL 3:15
Text: And let the peace of God rule in your hearts, to the which also ye are called in one body; and be ye thankful.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f3733ad-bd80-47f6-9dd4-a0facd5fef93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: COL 3:16
Text: Let the word of Christ dwell in you richly in all wisdom; teaching and admonishing one another in psalms and hymns and spiritual songs, singing with grace in your hearts to the Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bfa58d83-a6fb-4e61-a7fd-0cb592809e95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: COL 3:17
Text: And whatsoever ye do in word or deed, do all in the name of the Lord Jesus, giving thanks to God and the Father by him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:431fc6b7-ba20-4c4e-880e-e675db7b23b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: COL 3:18
Text: Wives, submit yourselves unto your own husbands, as it is fit in the Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb7d7584-2dec-49e1-837f-ec54971e308f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: COL 3:19
Text: Husbands, love your wives, and be not bitter against them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6767ced2-1fd4-4521-acec-565cb51a352a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: COL 3:20
Text: Children, obey your parents in all things: for this is well pleasing unto the Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83c9b6fe-a7ae-4e48-9eb3-39e5de021ed4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: COL 3:21
Text: Fathers, provoke not your children to anger, lest they be discouraged.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f217eaab-59cf-4257-9c33-6bb62c7e5452>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: COL 3:22
Text: Servants, obey in all things your masters according to the flesh; not with eyeservice, as menpleasers; but in singleness of heart, fearing God;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5b500cb-cce8-4937-bc83-6b9d6550feee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: COL 3:23
Text: And whatsoever ye do, do it heartily, as to the Lord, and not unto men;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65cf8f81-feb9-43b4-9f8f-764d1bb5bf23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: COL 3:24
Text: Knowing that of the Lord ye shall receive the reward of the inheritance: for ye serve the Lord Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/3/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f48a2a09-0b0f-4683-abb9-92c980786d0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: COL 3:25
Text: But he that doeth wrong shall receive for the wrong which he hath done: and there is no respect of persons.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af503fa8-99f5-49a6-88e7-c6e1f9f704de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: COL 4:1
Text: Masters, give unto your servants that which is just and equal; knowing that ye also have a Master in heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd0ad548-895d-4b7f-8185-a8a33500ae40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: COL 4:2
Text: Continue in prayer, and watch in the same with thanksgiving;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d92b7d59-70cc-4fa0-b628-ed87ccb84f9f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: COL 4:3
Text: Withal praying also for us, that God would open unto us a door of utterance, to speak the mystery of Christ, for which I am also in bonds:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ee271cb-46e1-46b1-b691-0000259a5e67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 75

Reference: COL 4:4
Text: That I may make it manifest, as I ought to speak.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f518a7e7-1a38-4239-b386-30f8b106af0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: COL 4:5
Text: Walk in wisdom toward them that are without, redeeming the time.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de31e0e6-e4f4-4c24-ba98-2a96bc056604>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: COL 4:6
Text: Let your speech be alway with grace, seasoned with salt, that ye may know how ye ought to answer every man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e691964b-1f42-4696-8ab0-78cacf944f88>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: COL 4:7
Text: All my state shall Tychicus declare unto you, who is a beloved brother, and a faithful minister and fellowservant in the Lord:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35200290-97bd-4629-82d6-719d8e930d70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: COL 4:8
Text: Whom I have sent unto you for the same purpose, that he might know your estate, and comfort your hearts;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e786cc5-d915-434f-8d62-6dd7a1b8fafa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: COL 4:9
Text: With Onesimus, a faithful and beloved brother, who is one of you. They shall make known unto you all things which are done here.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:571e1ce0-430e-4037-93d9-4a4785ac3abe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: COL 4:10
Text: Aristarchus my fellowprisoner saluteth you, and Marcus, sister’s son to Barnabas, (touching whom ye received commandments: if he come unto you, receive him;)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0811bd0a-ca33-4a47-8563-019179716716>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: COL 4:11
Text: And Jesus, which is called Justus, who are of the circumcision. These only are my fellowworkers unto the kingdom of God, which have been a comfort unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66c70159-6a66-44c3-a3a8-c05b7dc6eb99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: COL 4:12
Text: Epaphras, who is one of you, a servant of Christ, saluteth you, always labouring fervently for you in prayers, that ye may stand perfect and complete in all the will of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:392deb83-4f24-4992-9120-9479b40677f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: COL 4:13
Text: For I bear him record, that he hath a great zeal for you, and them that are in Laodicea, and them in Hierapolis.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a596478-3461-4f3b-b2ac-148a4b172270>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: COL 4:14
Text: Luke, the beloved physician, and Demas, greet you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7271a84c-4d36-437e-bb5a-40f73635d47f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: COL 4:15
Text: Salute the brethren which are in Laodicea, and Nymphas, and the church which is in his house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e396973f-c6c2-44f6-b14f-d69504c246c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: COL 4:16
Text: And when this epistle is read among you, cause that it be read also in the church of the Laodiceans; and that ye likewise read the epistle from Laodicea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c1b686a7-692c-401a-8450-388d2e98e54e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: COL 4:17
Text: And say to Archippus, Take heed to the ministry which thou hast received in the Lord, that thou fulfil it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/COL/4/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7154490-2d2c-4f80-8077-51e57b8216b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: COL 4:18
Text: The salutation by the hand of me Paul. Remember my bonds. Grace be with you. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39fe676e-8992-4169-a342-7fca5a2bf888>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: 1TH 1:1
Text: Paul, and Silvanus, and Timotheus, unto the church of the Thessalonians which is in God the Father and in the Lord Jesus Christ: Grace be unto you, and peace, from God our Father, and the Lord Jesus Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c505cf0f-077b-410f-9202-aa10a8a8bcd9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: 1TH 1:2
Text: We give thanks to God always for you all, making mention of you in our prayers;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dce5e168-e65d-46e2-b46c-38332e74917a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: 1TH 1:3
Text: Remembering without ceasing your work of faith, and labour of love, and patience of hope in our Lord Jesus Christ, in the sight of God and our Father;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af7e25d4-974f-4351-b893-096d2f361172>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: 1TH 1:4
Text: Knowing, brethren beloved, your election of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acf44723-5688-4993-ba07-f4eba86ad57a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 1TH 1:5
Text: For our gospel came not unto you in word only, but also in power, and in the Holy Ghost, and in much assurance; as ye know what manner of men we were among you for your sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d28054d0-adb7-4ea6-8049-7d0cdf26c6b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: 1TH 1:6
Text: And ye became followers of us, and of the Lord, having received the word in much affliction, with joy of the Holy Ghost.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca1ba77a-9424-4128-8f17-393ddeac4e2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: 1TH 1:7
Text: So that ye were ensamples to all that believe in Macedonia and Achaia.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b4accaf-2207-4e93-8150-a95c1da94080>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: 1TH 1:8
Text: For from you sounded out the word of the Lord not only in Macedonia and Achaia, but also in every place your faith to God-ward is spread abroad; so that we need not to speak any thing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99b3796c-8b97-4d7b-9070-ef8134cdbe15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 1TH 1:9
Text: For they themselves shew of us what manner of entering in we had unto you, and how ye turned to God from idols to serve the living and true God;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70012d07-6e9c-4353-9041-49c3dfe74b26>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 1TH 1:10
Text: And to wait for his Son from heaven, whom he raised from the dead, even Jesus, which delivered us from the wrath to come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c7a81d3e-2245-4447-985d-1db2b633ac81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: 1TH 2:1
Text: For yourselves, brethren, know our entrance in unto you, that it was not in vain:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1721d8f-455a-4ccc-a0f8-d6508ab2f768>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: 1TH 2:2
Text: But even after that we had suffered before, and were shamefully entreated, as ye know, at Philippi, we were bold in our God to speak unto you the gospel of God with much contention.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:839bcf5e-e82f-4d53-ba69-8f2bbe6faf09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: 1TH 2:3
Text: For our exhortation was not of deceit, nor of uncleanness, nor in guile:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac6f97db-ba8b-4c0e-aab1-dc827435ccaa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: 1TH 2:4
Text: But as we were allowed of God to be put in trust with the gospel, even so we speak; not as pleasing men, but God, which trieth our hearts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e1d1fc4-5032-46df-b9b3-a722717d8ea4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 1TH 2:5
Text: For neither at any time used we flattering words, as ye know, nor a cloke of covetousness; God is witness:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f830443-10db-4583-b6ed-abf7f4376a84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: 1TH 2:6
Text: Nor of men sought we glory, neither of you, nor yet of others, when we might have been burdensome, as the apostles of Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41db5566-df81-410b-84aa-2f2362caa91b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: 1TH 2:7
Text: But we were gentle among you, even as a nurse cherisheth her children:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a780ed31-0de9-4f34-8c18-3bddb148ad8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: 1TH 2:8
Text: So being affectionately desirous of you, we were willing to have imparted unto you, not the gospel of God only, but also our own souls, because ye were dear unto us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b663552c-4c53-4fee-989e-28ca3bc78c97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: 1TH 2:9
Text: For ye remember, brethren, our labour and travail: for labouring night and day, because we would not be chargeable unto any of you, we preached unto you the gospel of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6a01003-599d-4346-8028-f68090657713>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 1TH 2:10
Text: Ye are witnesses, and God also, how holily and justly and unblameably we behaved ourselves among you that believe:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41deb558-e83f-4789-9af4-61bfc4f94009>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 1TH 2:11
Text: As ye know how we exhorted and comforted and charged every one of you, as a father doth his children,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54447df2-4334-4fbc-9bbf-093530da907e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: 1TH 2:12
Text: That ye would walk worthy of God, who hath called you unto his kingdom and glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e98383f7-9df8-4990-b909-9ea29628d608>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 271

Reference: 1TH 2:13
Text: For this cause also thank we God without ceasing, because, when ye received the word of God which ye heard of us, ye received it not as the word of men, but as it is in truth, the word of God, which effectually worketh also in you that believe.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e8831d9-19b1-428e-882a-4b79d2fc4c4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: 1TH 2:14
Text: For ye, brethren, became followers of the churches of God which in Judaea are in Christ Jesus: for ye also have suffered like things of your own countrymen, even as they have of the Jews:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dc744960-182c-480f-8c81-92aae5b970b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 1TH 2:15
Text: Who both killed the Lord Jesus, and their own prophets, and have persecuted us; and they please not God, and are contrary to all men:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5efe539a-9283-4b21-9ec7-b980e59f029b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 1TH 2:16
Text: Forbidding us to speak to the Gentiles that they might be saved, to fill up their sins alway: for the wrath is come upon them to the uttermost.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0921f2a1-1620-44c1-ac20-e6033dcf7198>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 1TH 2:17
Text: But we, brethren, being taken from you for a short time in presence, not in heart, endeavoured the more abundantly to see your face with great desire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3afb85d6-4e09-4475-88e4-edb20dbb6eeb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: 1TH 2:18
Text: Wherefore we would have come unto you, even I Paul, once and again; but Satan hindered us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abcf5527-f93e-411c-ac65-8c85c185a0a8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: 1TH 2:19
Text: For what is our hope, or joy, or crown of rejoicing? Are not even ye in the presence of our Lord Jesus Christ at his coming?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5348dbc2-4b1d-45ac-b36c-de4bc2b1b976>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 56

Reference: 1TH 2:20
Text: For ye are our glory and joy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:591eaa4b-6677-44c4-9c55-f8250cca5be9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: 1TH 3:1
Text: Wherefore when we could no longer forbear, we thought it good to be left at Athens alone;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5454d026-6424-4afd-a9a0-24a726468ced>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 1TH 3:2
Text: And sent Timotheus, our brother, and minister of God, and our fellowlabourer in the gospel of Christ, to establish you, and to comfort you concerning your faith:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd450227-ace9-44a5-9e74-9c3197aeeb08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 1TH 3:3
Text: That no man should be moved by these afflictions: for yourselves know that we are appointed thereunto.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:38665d71-2e72-41ce-8036-44353ecf8dfd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: 1TH 3:4
Text: For verily, when we were with you, we told you before that we should suffer tribulation; even as it came to pass, and ye know.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e577c5c4-7d6a-4f7f-84f3-8b79b328c61c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: 1TH 3:5
Text: For this cause, when I could no longer forbear, I sent to know your faith, lest by some means the tempter have tempted you, and our labour be in vain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3e22b55-0426-420c-93c9-e209e73acc2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: 1TH 3:6
Text: But now when Timotheus came from you unto us, and brought us good tidings of your faith and charity, and that ye have good remembrance of us always, desiring greatly to see us, as we also to see you:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d6ea05d-96d1-440f-a679-56982464805e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 1TH 3:7
Text: Therefore, brethren, we were comforted over you in all our affliction and distress by your faith:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b70ec7b-8fa0-4573-91c9-0b8835d534ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 72

Reference: 1TH 3:8
Text: For now we live, if ye stand fast in the Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a212f2d-4126-4407-b591-a7fecca0b6bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 1TH 3:9
Text: For what thanks can we render to God again for you, for all the joy wherewith we joy for your sakes before our God;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f18a2480-812a-41c8-b124-b9854f578e62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: 1TH 3:10
Text: Night and day praying exceedingly that we might see your face, and might perfect that which is lacking in your faith?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c0bb069-c86a-415e-8742-bf538dd1ff97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: 1TH 3:11
Text: Now God himself and our Father, and our Lord Jesus Christ, direct our way unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:274f3920-f995-43c3-b9de-ff0294a16dfb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 1TH 3:12
Text: And the Lord make you to increase and abound in love one toward another, and toward all men, even as we do toward you:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f86d7bb-b141-455b-a84b-0d206b78d94a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: 1TH 3:13
Text: To the end he may stablish your hearts unblameable in holiness before God, even our Father, at the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ with all his saints.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a1e8c3e-bc85-4edf-9288-90cbb71404a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: 1TH 4:1
Text: Furthermore then we beseech you, brethren, and exhort you by the Lord Jesus, that as ye have received of us how ye ought to walk and to please God, so ye would abound more and more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f87b09b0-225e-43e8-b298-463beaae2a1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: 1TH 4:2
Text: For ye know what commandments we gave you by the Lord Jesus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0682947e-d132-443f-8e80-9cf937549ff6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 1TH 4:3
Text: For this is the will of God, even your sanctification, that ye should abstain from fornication:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8ca284e-b8d9-4c40-847a-e9c2964ddae4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: 1TH 4:4
Text: That every one of you should know how to possess his vessel in sanctification and honour;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8cf7cc2-7d2b-4bc9-aad6-8dff8cdc7e9e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: 1TH 4:5
Text: Not in the lust of concupiscence, even as the Gentiles which know not God:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6eb50d82-b1ae-4007-8225-c213c6bee5ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: 1TH 4:6
Text: That no man go beyond and defraud his brother in any matter: because that the Lord is the avenger of all such, as we also have forewarned you and testified.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3223088-7046-4590-8d19-5a1d5cf2894b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: 1TH 4:7
Text: For God hath not called us unto uncleanness, but unto holiness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a30c58d-adc2-4091-8f91-b39e9ace0078>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 1TH 4:8
Text: He therefore that despiseth, despiseth not man, but God, who hath also given unto us his holy Spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:402684df-ace6-45d4-8695-464e59c12899>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 1TH 4:9
Text: But as touching brotherly love ye need not that I write unto you: for ye yourselves are taught of God to love one another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a7837b3-fd47-472f-86c1-170e96db004f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 1TH 4:10
Text: And indeed ye do it toward all the brethren which are in all Macedonia: but we beseech you, brethren, that ye increase more and more;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79ec84f7-45b9-4c1d-98ac-273efa95bc70>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 1TH 4:11
Text: And that ye study to be quiet, and to do your own business, and to work with your own hands, as we commanded you;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e423a40c-533c-4490-a1f7-7a874edd8b02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: 1TH 4:12
Text: That ye may walk honestly toward them that are without, and that ye may have lack of nothing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d60aa762-ba66-46f7-b9b2-14a94fe7008b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: 1TH 4:13
Text: But I would not have you to be ignorant, brethren, concerning them which are asleep, that ye sorrow not, even as others which have no hope.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:facbcf40-ef0b-46bc-b14e-7ad4d5f84010>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 1TH 4:14
Text: For if we believe that Jesus died and rose again, even so them also which sleep in Jesus will God bring with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:123831fb-464d-4a17-b922-533e2a1f9688>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: 1TH 4:15
Text: For this we say unto you by the word of the Lord, that we which are alive and remain unto the coming of the Lord shall not prevent them which are asleep.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91b52afd-fb62-4839-ac08-7f69bc700dd0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 1TH 4:16
Text: For the Lord himself shall descend from heaven with a shout, with the voice of the archangel, and with the trump of God: and the dead in Christ shall rise first:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e7bd326-f179-47f3-8303-9f08ed658d40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: 1TH 4:17
Text: Then we which are alive and remain shall be caught up together with them in the clouds, to meet the Lord in the air: and so shall we ever be with the Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/4/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:320103ac-afc0-4f53-902b-203f2c1f63a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: 1TH 4:18
Text: Wherefore comfort one another with these words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d794fd31-e5cb-4067-bf33-1f6631e11b91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: 1TH 5:1
Text: But of the times and the seasons, brethren, ye have no need that I write unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7fd3a29b-fff7-44e2-93b7-d92319a0d43f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: 1TH 5:2
Text: For yourselves know perfectly that the day of the Lord so cometh as a thief in the night.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ad6951fa-d3e9-4666-be1e-b7a10345e987>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 1TH 5:3
Text: For when they shall say, Peace and safety; then sudden destruction cometh upon them, as travail upon a woman with child; and they shall not escape.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3e74a86-c438-4024-b151-9a87b3f29a7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: 1TH 5:4
Text: But ye, brethren, are not in darkness, that that day should overtake you as a thief.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:541e97f7-0679-42d4-830c-bfb32d3bc0b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: 1TH 5:5
Text: Ye are all the children of light, and the children of the day: we are not of the night, nor of darkness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5357ff37-2878-4de3-8267-7bacbc38545f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: 1TH 5:6
Text: Therefore let us not sleep, as do others; but let us watch and be sober.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0686d740-9b30-4445-85f6-d9ea35d36f68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: 1TH 5:7
Text: For they that sleep sleep in the night; and they that be drunken are drunken in the night.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b39470fc-38ef-4eeb-94a3-e15f3ee66253>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 1TH 5:8
Text: But let us, who are of the day, be sober, putting on the breastplate of faith and love; and for an helmet, the hope of salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98b6a23a-83a8-435f-8235-f993b28a29f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: 1TH 5:9
Text: For God hath not appointed us to wrath, but to obtain salvation by our Lord Jesus Christ,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ff044bb-18d9-410d-b3eb-cda62bdffa54>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: 1TH 5:10
Text: Who died for us, that, whether we wake or sleep, we should live together with him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe8dcf47-3251-4738-b689-4a109740a790>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: 1TH 5:11
Text: Wherefore comfort yourselves together, and edify one another, even as also ye do.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d6abb08-6879-42c3-bc1b-8c3e856a21d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 1TH 5:12
Text: And we beseech you, brethren, to know them which labour among you, and are over you in the Lord, and admonish you;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0ba96dd3-57d7-4ac2-b453-67fefb26751b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: 1TH 5:13
Text: And to esteem them very highly in love for their work’s sake. And be at peace among yourselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e91144cc-a9a8-40e0-9fdc-177267f85f39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 1TH 5:14
Text: Now we exhort you, brethren, warn them that are unruly, comfort the feebleminded, support the weak, be patient toward all men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:264d8dd8-3eb5-4724-b69e-30f55dbe5d67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: 1TH 5:15
Text: See that none render evil for evil unto any man; but ever follow that which is good, both among yourselves, and to all men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6515990d-ed3e-4086-84ba-1616e1f8afbf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 44

Reference: 1TH 5:16
Text: Rejoice evermore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c285c61a-4f33-42b4-ab75-dbc8d283a950>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 48

Reference: 1TH 5:17
Text: Pray without ceasing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3202fe70-9af7-423a-be11-d2892a1e7305>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: 1TH 5:18
Text: In every thing give thanks: for this is the will of God in Christ Jesus concerning you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef3c5601-5ed7-46b2-a33a-3f3c70bdfb30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 49

Reference: 1TH 5:19
Text: Quench not the Spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61884db5-fea8-4f1c-af7c-2cad32178d55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 52

Reference: 1TH 5:20
Text: Despise not prophesyings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c649c04e-6253-4489-ab89-67b1c694f6b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: 1TH 5:21
Text: Prove all things; hold fast that which is good.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67838cf8-6b2a-4993-bae0-6bb4d139a307>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 63

Reference: 1TH 5:22
Text: Abstain from all appearance of evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58ed10d9-eadb-4f5b-8ae0-aee6753a1c87>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: 1TH 5:23
Text: And the very God of peace sanctify you wholly; and I pray God your whole spirit and soul and body be preserved blameless unto the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d4df755-644d-4685-adf2-fc96d2e17d83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: 1TH 5:24
Text: Faithful is he that calleth you, who also will do it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd3d3d3f-bf60-4e0f-b437-4d9af83518bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 49

Reference: 1TH 5:25
Text: Brethren, pray for us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9efa218a-be8b-440f-9f34-b6d8f5faaa28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 68

Reference: 1TH 5:26
Text: Greet all the brethren with an holy kiss.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3356ba3-4127-4398-86b3-309649f01030>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: 1TH 5:27
Text: I charge you by the Lord that this epistle be read unto all the holy brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TH/5/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11a0a9ab-6935-4acb-8a3c-ba4b25e14d71>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: 1TH 5:28
Text: The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75b624e5-837b-4bdb-919c-4ba69799c1a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: 2TH 1:1
Text: Paul, and Silvanus, and Timotheus, unto the church of the Thessalonians in God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08b9b224-8ec8-4539-9900-3dde95cb150e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: 2TH 1:2
Text: Grace unto you, and peace, from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e27b2b92-b64f-4597-a7a3-11f1da36019f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: 2TH 1:3
Text: We are bound to thank God always for you, brethren, as it is meet, because that your faith groweth exceedingly, and the charity of every one of you all toward each other aboundeth;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae79492d-de02-4f58-aa5a-7d3f26084c35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: 2TH 1:4
Text: So that we ourselves glory in you in the churches of God for your patience and faith in all your persecutions and tribulations that ye endure:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23a697dc-8779-4bea-a1bc-307b2ba66174>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: 2TH 1:5
Text: Which is a manifest token of the righteous judgment of God, that ye may be counted worthy of the kingdom of God, for which ye also suffer:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9ca7c4f-e559-494c-88d7-6f700ca9e39a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: 2TH 1:6
Text: Seeing it is a righteous thing with God to recompense tribulation to them that trouble you;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0a8693c-6697-4dde-97dc-58699dfcbd90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 2TH 1:7
Text: And to you who are troubled rest with us, when the Lord Jesus shall be revealed from heaven with his mighty angels,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db0441ef-a8cd-41e1-9bdb-a34b892ba163>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 2TH 1:8
Text: In flaming fire taking vengeance on them that know not God, and that obey not the gospel of our Lord Jesus Christ:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1c9f1ed-213a-4e0c-a537-c23c03a7be29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 2TH 1:9
Text: Who shall be punished with everlasting destruction from the presence of the Lord, and from the glory of his power;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd33fb43-9c55-4a5c-b382-85b81b4820d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 2TH 1:10
Text: When he shall come to be glorified in his saints, and to be admired in all them that believe (because our testimony among you was believed) in that day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4f3e3bf-7c26-4c97-bf9a-135adc2b17f5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: 2TH 1:11
Text: Wherefore also we pray always for you, that our God would count you worthy of this calling, and fulfil all the good pleasure of his goodness, and the work of faith with power:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f991769-3bb9-495a-8ea5-e62c7eea7575>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: 2TH 1:12
Text: That the name of our Lord Jesus Christ may be glorified in you, and ye in him, according to the grace of our God and the Lord Jesus Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f0516df-fd2d-4b04-9b96-75d4f74a3e61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 2TH 2:1
Text: Now we beseech you, brethren, by the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ, and by our gathering together unto him,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aaf66646-0e9c-4f15-be2d-7de7df8dfe90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 2TH 2:2
Text: That ye be not soon shaken in mind, or be troubled, neither by spirit, nor by word, nor by letter as from us, as that the day of Christ is at hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d29afc4a-2ee5-4f6c-b646-41ed07c43614>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: 2TH 2:3
Text: Let no man deceive you by any means: for that day shall not come, except there come a falling away first, and that man of sin be revealed, the son of perdition;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c57fd87-1c7e-4333-b5bd-3f20ae65ed46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: 2TH 2:4
Text: Who opposeth and exalteth himself above all that is called God, or that is worshipped; so that he as God sitteth in the temple of God, shewing himself that he is God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c94a8933-22e2-4b52-b39d-7aacb3c8a4e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: 2TH 2:5
Text: Remember ye not, that, when I was yet with you, I told you these things?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e368e82a-d1ef-4457-870b-77b20c6ce39d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: 2TH 2:6
Text: And now ye know what withholdeth that he might be revealed in his time.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54a70087-3ba8-4835-b5f3-49ab36c249cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 2TH 2:7
Text: For the mystery of iniquity doth already work: only he who now letteth will let, until he be taken out of the way.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6349ffb-e5eb-4069-98be-72d80391da2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: 2TH 2:8
Text: And then shall that Wicked be revealed, whom the Lord shall consume with the spirit of his mouth, and shall destroy with the brightness of his coming:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8052024-f9c4-4e38-8b02-9960662ea871>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: 2TH 2:9
Text: Even him, whose coming is after the working of Satan with all power and signs and lying wonders,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d495c25-5fe8-4755-b115-9a81bb82b664>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: 2TH 2:10
Text: And with all deceivableness of unrighteousness in them that perish; because they received not the love of the truth, that they might be saved.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6742006e-8c44-43f0-a431-52bb30a58564>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: 2TH 2:11
Text: And for this cause God shall send them strong delusion, that they should believe a lie:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0aaf0350-64b7-49a9-b8a7-a5be932784e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 2TH 2:12
Text: That they all might be damned who believed not the truth, but had pleasure in unrighteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:630199c4-0c62-4a52-b2b9-3de5f150ef55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 232

Reference: 2TH 2:13
Text: But we are bound to give thanks alway to God for you, brethren beloved of the Lord, because God hath from the beginning chosen you to salvation through sanctification of the Spirit and belief of the truth:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7ba98cfe-67d6-4f41-8439-29004ddb4f77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 2TH 2:14
Text: Whereunto he called you by our gospel, to the obtaining of the glory of our Lord Jesus Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b0eedc2-fe18-40be-9917-49e5fe713066>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: 2TH 2:15
Text: Therefore, brethren, stand fast, and hold the traditions which ye have been taught, whether by word, or our epistle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a76e9af-fced-43f7-91f6-1d6b1fea9ec8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 2TH 2:16
Text: Now our Lord Jesus Christ himself, and God, even our Father, which hath loved us, and hath given us everlasting consolation and good hope through grace,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f9250da-34f3-4c97-bbca-79e7c627df00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: 2TH 2:17
Text: Comfort your hearts, and stablish you in every good word and work.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a41e396d-c89a-4dfb-8bbd-17bf9376b36b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 2TH 3:1
Text: Finally, brethren, pray for us, that the word of the Lord may have free course, and be glorified, even as it is with you:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d215cf3a-c56a-4af8-b0aa-470fd9380220>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: 2TH 3:2
Text: And that we may be delivered from unreasonable and wicked men: for all men have not faith.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f17242f8-4d0a-480c-879c-483fdda779e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: 2TH 3:3
Text: But the Lord is faithful, who shall stablish you, and keep you from evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88fb076f-247b-4093-84ba-f7352748a7ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 2TH 3:4
Text: And we have confidence in the Lord touching you, that ye both do and will do the things which we command you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:879b2ba0-532d-4654-9322-44bcdc4ae83c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: 2TH 3:5
Text: And the Lord direct your hearts into the love of God, and into the patient waiting for Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f021adf2-9dcd-4a42-9fa8-e22ef358f023>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: 2TH 3:6
Text: Now we command you, brethren, in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, that ye withdraw yourselves from every brother that walketh disorderly, and not after the tradition which he received of us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:72a64cb1-abbb-4ddf-accf-3a84d26f809d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 2TH 3:7
Text: For yourselves know how ye ought to follow us: for we behaved not ourselves disorderly among you;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4ccf4b8-bcc1-416c-8c4e-e46b5bf4374c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: 2TH 3:8
Text: Neither did we eat any man’s bread for nought; but wrought with labour and travail night and day, that we might not be chargeable to any of you:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df944983-fd20-4dc0-a720-a9144e54af3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: 2TH 3:9
Text: Not because we have not power, but to make ourselves an ensample unto you to follow us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c16d1f02-fdf1-4eaa-93fc-0a8f3112caf1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 2TH 3:10
Text: For even when we were with you, this we commanded you, that if any would not work, neither should he eat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd907d80-46e4-4fec-beca-0f3a2b932a9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: 2TH 3:11
Text: For we hear that there are some which walk among you disorderly, working not at all, but are busybodies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b152d7fc-d6f0-4ec1-962b-cc40ae1aa6f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 2TH 3:12
Text: Now them that are such we command and exhort by our Lord Jesus Christ, that with quietness they work, and eat their own bread.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1781d54a-4e32-4c0b-b622-8e6d9bdf5ada>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 72

Reference: 2TH 3:13
Text: But ye, brethren, be not weary in well doing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6fba9826-9689-4e90-949b-b697e3da1835>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 2TH 3:14
Text: And if any man obey not our word by this epistle, note that man, and have no company with him, that he may be ashamed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12bd6ffd-b146-4933-b3a1-c9ee46cefae1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: 2TH 3:15
Text: Yet count him not as an enemy, but admonish him as a brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68902ee0-cecd-459e-b618-277a8f1dd6c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: 2TH 3:16
Text: Now the Lord of peace himself give you peace always by all means. The Lord be with you all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a07891a-ab38-4736-970c-571c55c34fde>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: 2TH 3:17
Text: The salutation of Paul with mine own hand, which is the token in every epistle: so I write.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TH/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82524f7e-3df1-4923-ab8b-01a0a9169343>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: 2TH 3:18
Text: The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you all. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b92bef9-e3a9-4e27-9117-c121a27fc867>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: 1TI 1:1
Text: Paul, an apostle of Jesus Christ by the commandment of God our Saviour, and Lord Jesus Christ, which is our hope;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3095532-77ac-4c9d-b0b6-5d18d30b17a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: 1TI 1:2
Text: Unto Timothy, my own son in the faith: Grace, mercy, and peace, from God our Father and Jesus Christ our Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1278f4f1-0c54-469b-9985-323c3e894740>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: 1TI 1:3
Text: As I besought thee to abide still at Ephesus, when I went into Macedonia, that thou mightest charge some that they teach no other doctrine,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c11b18a3-e8eb-45b8-bb2f-0ecdc38c5afb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 1TI 1:4
Text: Neither give heed to fables and endless genealogies, which minister questions, rather than godly edifying which is in faith: so do.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7d3359b-87c1-4756-978f-c3f56fca9fc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: 1TI 1:5
Text: Now the end of the commandment is charity out of a pure heart, and of a good conscience, and of faith unfeigned:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:24a29817-981f-4729-9719-320939f6ab97>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: 1TI 1:6
Text: From which some having swerved have turned aside unto vain jangling;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f56deea-fa6f-4f6a-b80a-ad3d84979cae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 1TI 1:7
Text: Desiring to be teachers of the law; understanding neither what they say, nor whereof they affirm.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8941485-2e0c-4c89-bc56-ea5e5c7aaca8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: 1TI 1:8
Text: But we know that the law is good, if a man use it lawfully;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07a5189d-75cb-4a07-b11b-b4d08c3d563d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: 1TI 1:9
Text: Knowing this, that the law is not made for a righteous man, but for the lawless and disobedient, for the ungodly and for sinners, for unholy and profane, for murderers of fathers and murderers of mothers, for manslayers,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4078c198-0583-4b20-8fa8-d7b4a836b559>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: 1TI 1:10
Text: For whoremongers, for them that defile themselves with mankind, for menstealers, for liars, for perjured persons, and if there be any other thing that is contrary to sound doctrine;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d23d773-97ca-414f-8498-99e262005e8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: 1TI 1:11
Text: According to the glorious gospel of the blessed God, which was committed to my trust.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:694d49b3-9944-4a57-8997-e56365633679>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 1TI 1:12
Text: And I thank Christ Jesus our Lord, who hath enabled me, for that he counted me faithful, putting me into the ministry;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39fd3aa5-47fa-4059-a9e1-4e0864dc2320>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: 1TI 1:13
Text: Who was before a blasphemer, and a persecutor, and injurious: but I obtained mercy, because I did it ignorantly in unbelief.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:45f549e7-9a6a-4612-9670-5719e55ee2e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 1TI 1:14
Text: And the grace of our Lord was exceeding abundant with faith and love which is in Christ Jesus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2f84a81-8caa-4db2-8e73-41820996d703>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: 1TI 1:15
Text: This is a faithful saying, and worthy of all acceptation, that Christ Jesus came into the world to save sinners; of whom I am chief.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e35be4d9-8885-4f76-b73b-a7a10692889d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: 1TI 1:16
Text: Howbeit for this cause I obtained mercy, that in me first Jesus Christ might shew forth all longsuffering, for a pattern to them which should hereafter believe on him to life everlasting.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:851ecf60-52bb-4cd0-9d74-ab8133f71943>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: 1TI 1:17
Text: Now unto the King eternal, immortal, invisible, the only wise God, be honour and glory for ever and ever. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d68e64e-1fe6-46fd-b51b-8d75962a0e7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 1TI 1:18
Text: This charge I commit unto thee, son Timothy, according to the prophecies which went before on thee, that thou by them mightest war a good warfare;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f111c96-3a7c-4267-9e43-f7c341fb5d1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: 1TI 1:19
Text: Holding faith, and a good conscience; which some having put away concerning faith have made shipwreck:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2cba360c-6f8b-48b6-9713-0446dc8f211f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: 1TI 1:20
Text: Of whom is Hymenaeus and Alexander; whom I have delivered unto Satan, that they may learn not to blaspheme.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9c2935d-623c-42c3-a402-1e4576f40fa2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 1TI 2:1
Text: I exhort therefore, that, first of all, supplications, prayers, intercessions, and giving of thanks, be made for all men;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3eff242e-af22-48d8-aaf3-d84f3189db44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 1TI 2:2
Text: For kings, and for all that are in authority; that we may lead a quiet and peaceable life in all godliness and honesty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8bd350e2-aa12-4d02-af02-ebff5bcd952a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: 1TI 2:3
Text: For this is good and acceptable in the sight of God our Saviour;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3123b46-a23f-42a3-b5fc-5e52c3b5e4dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: 1TI 2:4
Text: Who will have all men to be saved, and to come unto the knowledge of the truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f951c29-acd6-498c-9b36-9813687e9bf8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: 1TI 2:5
Text: For there is one God, and one mediator between God and men, the man Christ Jesus;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb275144-f6e0-49e2-8638-b8a60b1e36ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: 1TI 2:6
Text: Who gave himself a ransom for all, to be testified in due time.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3715b0a6-3d09-49c4-a7eb-aeebcdf61877>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: 1TI 2:7
Text: Whereunto I am ordained a preacher, and an apostle, (I speak the truth in Christ, and lie not;) a teacher of the Gentiles in faith and verity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:775ad183-f8c7-4241-9f34-3c14fc86e732>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: 1TI 2:8
Text: I will therefore that men pray every where, lifting up holy hands, without wrath and doubting.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5efa877-d3d2-4f04-802b-4208a32eedf0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 1TI 2:9
Text: In like manner also, that women adorn themselves in modest apparel, with shamefacedness and sobriety; not with broided hair, or gold, or pearls, or costly array;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c914c08-ee8b-4d8e-8755-5ee43d302e26>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: 1TI 2:10
Text: But (which becometh women professing godliness) with good works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd98c89a-f19f-4967-94ee-162b24123f9d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: 1TI 2:11
Text: Let the woman learn in silence with all subjection.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:705bf9b4-d118-4276-b149-6061ff6951d7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: 1TI 2:12
Text: But I suffer not a woman to teach, nor to usurp authority over the man, but to be in silence.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c07eac4e-b7d3-4440-be92-9c6c79962fd6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 63

Reference: 1TI 2:13
Text: For Adam was first formed, then Eve.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8469edef-a77f-4b53-a7a4-0c0200da98de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: 1TI 2:14
Text: And Adam was not deceived, but the woman being deceived was in the transgression.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:727a59f8-4aac-4d1c-9f6d-8ee615713900>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: 1TI 2:15
Text: Notwithstanding she shall be saved in childbearing, if they continue in faith and charity and holiness with sobriety.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb6142af-af56-482c-83d0-dac3c6529394>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: 1TI 3:1
Text: This is a true saying, If a man desire the office of a bishop, he desireth a good work.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab8633b0-184e-457a-98d1-57dda2a54cae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 1TI 3:2
Text: A bishop then must be blameless, the husband of one wife, vigilant, sober, of good behaviour, given to hospitality, apt to teach;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92bc143b-06b5-42fd-addf-30d4f7169c56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: 1TI 3:3
Text: Not given to wine, no striker, not greedy of filthy lucre; but patient, not a brawler, not covetous;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32ae1af7-498c-401d-9b4d-b29f3d50efb6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: 1TI 3:4
Text: One that ruleth well his own house, having his children in subjection with all gravity;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a2b17c5-9f3b-4b37-8d79-a1dd8843035c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 1TI 3:5
Text: (For if a man know not how to rule his own house, how shall he take care of the church of God?)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89116b74-0c57-4da4-a643-d45f50d53c2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: 1TI 3:6
Text: Not a novice, lest being lifted up with pride he fall into the condemnation of the devil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71540163-4c23-464e-a8a8-0ed07212d647>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: 1TI 3:7
Text: Moreover he must have a good report of them which are without; lest he fall into reproach and the snare of the devil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:913b8183-9719-460e-b934-069e047d587b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 1TI 3:8
Text: Likewise must the deacons be grave, not doubletongued, not given to much wine, not greedy of filthy lucre;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4033263e-7fd4-4990-9487-c985c3f133b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: 1TI 3:9
Text: Holding the mystery of the faith in a pure conscience.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ae2bb33-d33f-4bc2-b2c4-cb600fdbf448>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 1TI 3:10
Text: And let these also first be proved; then let them use the office of a deacon, being found blameless.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f4d76c3-a36e-4899-9240-a085405819aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: 1TI 3:11
Text: Even so must their wives be grave, not slanderers, sober, faithful in all things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:31b33564-522b-4caa-98b4-7193bf9510a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: 1TI 3:12
Text: Let the deacons be the husbands of one wife, ruling their children and their own houses well.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42757fcc-7870-4fbf-bc46-dfa63f3286f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: 1TI 3:13
Text: For they that have used the office of a deacon well purchase to themselves a good degree, and great boldness in the faith which is in Christ Jesus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3800bff-f12d-495d-9c34-61a8adbe607c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: 1TI 3:14
Text: These things write I unto thee, hoping to come unto thee shortly:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe24a12f-f8a2-4e9c-9ec4-ae0c1569db2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: 1TI 3:15
Text: But if I tarry long, that thou mayest know how thou oughtest to behave thyself in the house of God, which is the church of the living God, the pillar and ground of the truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8cd16893-a235-494e-97b0-49a7df155336>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: 1TI 3:16
Text: And without controversy great is the mystery of godliness: God was manifest in the flesh, justified in the Spirit, seen of angels, preached unto the Gentiles, believed on in the world, received up into glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ceccf40-f54f-412f-aaaf-735f4c380349>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 1TI 4:1
Text: Now the Spirit speaketh expressly, that in the latter times some shall depart from the faith, giving heed to seducing spirits, and doctrines of devils;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3faad306-aa4a-425f-b89a-87dcd7d45f16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: 1TI 4:2
Text: Speaking lies in hypocrisy; having their conscience seared with a hot iron;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28f7d098-a305-4bde-a225-fbe696a11921>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: 1TI 4:3
Text: Forbidding to marry, and commanding to abstain from meats, which God hath created to be received with thanksgiving of them which believe and know the truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef6dcec7-5343-4096-87d1-af6a12706e76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: 1TI 4:4
Text: For every creature of God is good, and nothing to be refused, if it be received with thanksgiving:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b542a20-5901-4c6e-bb76-c2aa77d29d18>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: 1TI 4:5
Text: For it is sanctified by the word of God and prayer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16440098-2d13-4191-aa31-6417dc6102b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: 1TI 4:6
Text: If thou put the brethren in remembrance of these things, thou shalt be a good minister of Jesus Christ, nourished up in the words of faith and of good doctrine, whereunto thou hast attained.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35ed67b2-9f89-413d-b56f-beb672b82281>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: 1TI 4:7
Text: But refuse profane and old wives’ fables, and exercise thyself rather unto godliness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e619911-08a2-4345-9534-4fc1ef4a76de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: 1TI 4:8
Text: For bodily exercise profiteth little: but godliness is profitable unto all things, having promise of the life that now is, and of that which is to come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73194b7a-b76b-45ca-8cf3-6ff4b9fe4fef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: 1TI 4:9
Text: This is a faithful saying and worthy of all acceptation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eeb91985-9c5d-47a1-89ac-baa1710fd068>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: 1TI 4:10
Text: For therefore we both labour and suffer reproach, because we trust in the living God, who is the Saviour of all men, specially of those that believe.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26bfccdf-8236-4064-a9c8-556bf2c30fbf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 58

Reference: 1TI 4:11
Text: These things command and teach.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c176fa56-eeba-4bf7-8ffa-5515438d9050>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 1TI 4:12
Text: Let no man despise thy youth; but be thou an example of the believers, in word, in conversation, in charity, in spirit, in faith, in purity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18168045-c12a-42dc-abe4-e106f7894f7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: 1TI 4:13
Text: Till I come, give attendance to reading, to exhortation, to doctrine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e56efed2-aba0-49b8-99ea-b1535c49b36a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: 1TI 4:14
Text: Neglect not the gift that is in thee, which was given thee by prophecy, with the laying on of the hands of the presbytery.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4fd7fc0-c5c5-4fe1-aee0-ecce82989d6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 1TI 4:15
Text: Meditate upon these things; give thyself wholly to them; that thy profiting may appear to all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd47db6d-fb5d-43e2-8df6-a94c1137fc14>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: 1TI 4:16
Text: Take heed unto thyself, and unto the doctrine; continue in them: for in doing this thou shalt both save thyself, and them that hear thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1e42a81-12d3-440a-ba53-dd000958ee05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: 1TI 5:1
Text: Rebuke not an elder, but intreat him as a father; and the younger men as brethren;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97699252-3642-464f-aaff-9aa8199ae9a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: 1TI 5:2
Text: The elder women as mothers; the younger as sisters, with all purity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bebf8fca-3ecc-46c2-a22f-f515d179dfcb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 63

Reference: 1TI 5:3
Text: Honour widows that are widows indeed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2341391-e121-433a-9a83-c53d9d760d0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: 1TI 5:4
Text: But if any widow have children or nephews, let them learn first to shew piety at home, and to requite their parents: for that is good and acceptable before God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6497043b-7be4-4c72-94b3-d8c8adcf367a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 1TI 5:5
Text: Now she that is a widow indeed, and desolate, trusteth in God, and continueth in supplications and prayers night and day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35fa94df-18a4-47c9-af91-68ed2f6338a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 83

Reference: 1TI 5:6
Text: But she that liveth in pleasure is dead while she liveth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb4e98b4-c2f9-4939-8b48-4b107aa4b716>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: 1TI 5:7
Text: And these things give in charge, that they may be blameless.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac26b4f1-81bf-422f-8899-5b66bbfa1a43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: 1TI 5:8
Text: But if any provide not for his own, and specially for those of his own house, he hath denied the faith, and is worse than an infidel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36556ec4-51a9-4a3e-a7e8-e99e94390942>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 1TI 5:9
Text: Let not a widow be taken into the number under threescore years old, having been the wife of one man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4508cc2-55dc-459a-b7aa-c4bec9f6d53f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: 1TI 5:10
Text: Well reported of for good works; if she have brought up children, if she have lodged strangers, if she have washed the saints’ feet, if she have relieved the afflicted, if she have diligently followed every good work.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b0e56d3-eb51-485c-ad61-28fc2c4644d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: 1TI 5:11
Text: But the younger widows refuse: for when they have begun to wax wanton against Christ, they will marry;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0b8a88d4-3603-4fae-9df8-b529ce516141>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: 1TI 5:12
Text: Having damnation, because they have cast off their first faith.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:962c2a46-de77-47e4-bb9a-b51c54716885>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 1TI 5:13
Text: And withal they learn to be idle, wandering about from house to house; and not only idle, but tattlers also and busybodies, speaking things which they ought not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26380b5f-fe35-4ffc-9015-eff7c97b16ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: 1TI 5:14
Text: I will therefore that the younger women marry, bear children, guide the house, give none occasion to the adversary to speak reproachfully.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eafcea25-e80f-42e1-a509-a42a09fa703d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 73

Reference: 1TI 5:15
Text: For some are already turned aside after Satan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b9e9fea-ca49-4270-9277-b625e9893cda>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: 1TI 5:16
Text: If any man or woman that believeth have widows, let them relieve them, and let not the church be charged; that it may relieve them that are widows indeed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c1ce5b6-0a5b-49fd-9fbb-d4a63971ef28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 1TI 5:17
Text: Let the elders that rule well be counted worthy of double honour, especially they who labour in the word and doctrine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:789c14fb-e9b2-433c-ab6f-c2f77bc9701c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: 1TI 5:18
Text: For the scripture saith, Thou shalt not muzzle the ox that treadeth out the corn. And, The labourer is worthy of his reward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e6286f9-b035-4d51-88ae-214446be48a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: 1TI 5:19
Text: Against an elder receive not an accusation, but before two or three witnesses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3bd6de39-368d-4ec0-ac80-272f83912a63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: 1TI 5:20
Text: Them that sin rebuke before all, that others also may fear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9bf4852c-8f91-4a36-9cbb-e21a4e48c1d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 1TI 5:21
Text: I charge thee before God, and the Lord Jesus Christ, and the elect angels, that thou observe these things without preferring one before another, doing nothing by partiality.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91abf64f-4fc0-48c9-b703-1b941ac06500>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: 1TI 5:22
Text: Lay hands suddenly on no man, neither be partaker of other men’s sins: keep thyself pure.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53512b8b-9653-4b70-be5d-0753ededd717>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: 1TI 5:23
Text: Drink no longer water, but use a little wine for thy stomach’s sake and thine often infirmities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:211795f2-760f-4f9f-8d44-952ea00057df>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 1TI 5:24
Text: Some men’s sins are open beforehand, going before to judgment; and some men they follow after.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/5/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0038687c-11c5-49ad-a675-e2afed00b8c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: 1TI 5:25
Text: Likewise also the good works of some are manifest beforehand; and they that are otherwise cannot be hid.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ae185dd-5753-4b8f-8759-3e7c3aa4dcf1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: 1TI 6:1
Text: Let as many servants as are under the yoke count their own masters worthy of all honour, that the name of God and his doctrine be not blasphemed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02039ec1-02a3-4515-97ed-289fa302fdfd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 241

Reference: 1TI 6:2
Text: And they that have believing masters, let them not despise them, because they are brethren; but rather do them service, because they are faithful and beloved, partakers of the benefit. These things teach and exhort.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe6a2fe8-ae9c-4832-a795-cf36a3f2e4e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: 1TI 6:3
Text: If any man teach otherwise, and consent not to wholesome words, even the words of our Lord Jesus Christ, and to the doctrine which is according to godliness;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e67e83d8-f6e9-484f-b7f0-4bd019513329>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 1TI 6:4
Text: He is proud, knowing nothing, but doting about questions and strifes of words, whereof cometh envy, strife, railings, evil surmisings,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81198e62-2be7-4122-acbe-4b39c532760d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 1TI 6:5
Text: Perverse disputings of men of corrupt minds, and destitute of the truth, supposing that gain is godliness: from such withdraw thyself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:987dd9de-6cfd-4a2d-ad54-23e45da4702f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 71

Reference: 1TI 6:6
Text: But godliness with contentment is great gain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c160cfee-a0e4-427d-ac8f-6b40f76be901>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: 1TI 6:7
Text: For we brought nothing into this world, and it is certain we can carry nothing out.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f8545f6-acc3-402f-8d24-32135f79783f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: 1TI 6:8
Text: And having food and raiment let us be therewith content.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4eed07ef-fdc3-4cd4-8b32-32602248adae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 1TI 6:9
Text: But they that will be rich fall into temptation and a snare, and into many foolish and hurtful lusts, which drown men in destruction and perdition.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9302ca1-3a88-42c5-b2fb-6c9487694462>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 1TI 6:10
Text: For the love of money is the root of all evil: which while some coveted after, they have erred from the faith, and pierced themselves through with many sorrows.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94ca9a1d-b8e9-4c5b-90ac-305b781aa1b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 1TI 6:11
Text: But thou, O man of God, flee these things; and follow after righteousness, godliness, faith, love, patience, meekness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d6deffce-5af4-4f97-8ec0-6f28b557317d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 1TI 6:12
Text: Fight the good fight of faith, lay hold on eternal life, whereunto thou art also called, and hast professed a good profession before many witnesses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd36999d-5ae2-49e9-bf32-5d40cf1a2d44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 1TI 6:13
Text: I give thee charge in the sight of God, who quickeneth all things, and before Christ Jesus, who before Pontius Pilate witnessed a good confession;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/6/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b287bffc-d08e-43fe-b1e0-498f4018823b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: 1TI 6:14
Text: That thou keep this commandment without spot, unrebukable, until the appearing of our Lord Jesus Christ:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/6/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:569d4875-fdb4-4901-a619-282cff10963f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 1TI 6:15
Text: Which in his times he shall shew, who is the blessed and only Potentate, the King of kings, and Lord of lords;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/6/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1959204a-3f46-43c8-8073-2ef0fdfcbe5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: 1TI 6:16
Text: Who only hath immortality, dwelling in the light which no man can approach unto; whom no man hath seen, nor can see: to whom be honour and power everlasting. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/6/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05e16875-ac1a-4714-8894-d4cb6f0e1acf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: 1TI 6:17
Text: Charge them that are rich in this world, that they be not highminded, nor trust in uncertain riches, but in the living God, who giveth us richly all things to enjoy;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/6/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4a99f90-4516-49a0-9299-dafde755e760>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 1TI 6:18
Text: That they do good, that they be rich in good works, ready to distribute, willing to communicate;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/6/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c658c4d-44ce-4865-88a6-35770ab8eb3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: 1TI 6:19
Text: Laying up in store for themselves a good foundation against the time to come, that they may lay hold on eternal life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/6/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6f63582-adf9-4709-aa86-7eb0956d994b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: 1TI 6:20
Text: O Timothy, keep that which is committed to thy trust, avoiding profane and vain babblings, and oppositions of science falsely so called:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1TI/6/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a3b783a-3ee2-4ccb-bc88-6cd84f1cc329>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: 1TI 6:21
Text: Which some professing have erred concerning the faith. Grace be with thee. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae5945cc-8d5b-4735-929a-4ffd281be5e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 2TI 1:1
Text: Paul, an apostle of Jesus Christ by the will of God, according to the promise of life which is in Christ Jesus,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c48f854d-26af-4c80-bb01-7a79650e5652>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 2TI 1:2
Text: To Timothy, my dearly beloved son: Grace, mercy, and peace, from God the Father and Christ Jesus our Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c178ff4c-9961-40aa-bbff-a4ac828be839>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 2TI 1:3
Text: I thank God, whom I serve from my forefathers with pure conscience, that without ceasing I have remembrance of thee in my prayers night and day;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3bed1cc5-fdc2-4788-a87c-601c89e282ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: 2TI 1:4
Text: Greatly desiring to see thee, being mindful of thy tears, that I may be filled with joy;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21caa380-23e2-42ed-b5e0-79a7b8eba11c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: 2TI 1:5
Text: When I call to remembrance the unfeigned faith that is in thee, which dwelt first in thy grandmother Lois, and thy mother Eunice; and I am persuaded that in thee also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9bf0823b-3af8-460d-8efe-44a0e6407498>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: 2TI 1:6
Text: Wherefore I put thee in remembrance that thou stir up the gift of God, which is in thee by the putting on of my hands.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:449226f4-18cd-4d82-a13a-5f49e9f25632>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: 2TI 1:7
Text: For God hath not given us the spirit of fear; but of power, and of love, and of a sound mind.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eeed3091-f201-4ab3-882f-8ed89678093a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: 2TI 1:8
Text: Be not thou therefore ashamed of the testimony of our Lord, nor of me his prisoner: but be thou partaker of the afflictions of the gospel according to the power of God;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65c5620b-79d9-4f4a-a554-0463b1a4835e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: 2TI 1:9
Text: Who hath saved us, and called us with an holy calling, not according to our works, but according to his own purpose and grace, which was given us in Christ Jesus before the world began,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf117d6f-ce36-499e-af34-9e8fd16dd021>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: 2TI 1:10
Text: But is now made manifest by the appearing of our Saviour Jesus Christ, who hath abolished death, and hath brought life and immortality to light through the gospel:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a7a6dd7-2599-4bf7-855b-7713946fa48a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: 2TI 1:11
Text: Whereunto I am appointed a preacher, and an apostle, and a teacher of the Gentiles.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4829262-b095-483d-a4f2-7c12ce10f087>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: 2TI 1:12
Text: For the which cause I also suffer these things: nevertheless I am not ashamed: for I know whom I have believed, and am persuaded that he is able to keep that which I have committed unto him against that day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:661fdcea-e991-43aa-8416-baf2cef9ec0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: 2TI 1:13
Text: Hold fast the form of sound words, which thou hast heard of me, in faith and love which is in Christ Jesus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51bb4c05-21e3-4bc6-8f4f-92f4101eb97b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: 2TI 1:14
Text: That good thing which was committed unto thee keep by the Holy Ghost which dwelleth in us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f430ccb1-9a95-43ce-8356-b87a6371943b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: 2TI 1:15
Text: This thou knowest, that all they which are in Asia be turned away from me; of whom are Phygellus and Hermogenes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b086e22-1d94-4579-981d-f1a7c93f55e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 2TI 1:16
Text: The Lord give mercy unto the house of Onesiphorus; for he oft refreshed me, and was not ashamed of my chain:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28556896-843e-476b-ada6-35b4aa6bb14a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: 2TI 1:17
Text: But, when he was in Rome, he sought me out very diligently, and found me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b651cf1a-feed-41d0-9941-92f8fcdb2f33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 2TI 1:18
Text: The Lord grant unto him that he may find mercy of the Lord in that day: and in how many things he ministered unto me at Ephesus, thou knowest very well.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:629f88cf-0b18-40fc-b449-f6f5c18d8018>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: 2TI 2:1
Text: Thou therefore, my son, be strong in the grace that is in Christ Jesus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de6680cb-f286-4be8-9d97-b66699105371>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 2TI 2:2
Text: And the things that thou hast heard of me among many witnesses, the same commit thou to faithful men, who shall be able to teach others also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79e2a5fa-a7b5-4e2b-a159-82e867c1675e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: 2TI 2:3
Text: Thou therefore endure hardness, as a good soldier of Jesus Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d9d27b8-b081-4ed6-a9b7-71466f06542c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 2TI 2:4
Text: No man that warreth entangleth himself with the affairs of this life; that he may please him who hath chosen him to be a soldier.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:267e3e78-65a3-4e6f-b0ec-5242ce13f4e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: 2TI 2:5
Text: And if a man also strive for masteries, yet is he not crowned, except he strive lawfully.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a47215ab-934e-4cca-90c7-a2e2e965860c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: 2TI 2:6
Text: The husbandman that laboureth must be first partaker of the fruits.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9ddd346-f7cd-4dfc-a1e3-16412f2f8a44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: 2TI 2:7
Text: Consider what I say; and the Lord give thee understanding in all things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04ebc2ba-1ec3-46c3-b4d7-2cb8cd47e34d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: 2TI 2:8
Text: Remember that Jesus Christ of the seed of David was raised from the dead according to my gospel:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b39c22f-34c6-41ef-96d4-37d5ae0a6699>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: 2TI 2:9
Text: Wherein I suffer trouble, as an evil doer, even unto bonds; but the word of God is not bound.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28507ed4-0551-486c-8d1d-bcdfe215f935>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: 2TI 2:10
Text: Therefore I endure all things for the elect’s sakes, that they may also obtain the salvation which is in Christ Jesus with eternal glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c95005d-231b-4ffa-aa4b-6809bced5bce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: 2TI 2:11
Text: It is a faithful saying: For if we be dead with him, we shall also live with him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8356fafc-d200-4d83-9fa9-f2d6df8b6129>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: 2TI 2:12
Text: If we suffer, we shall also reign with him: if we deny him, he also will deny us:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f13e83ba-25d7-4291-aa98-563a03e17fe8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: 2TI 2:13
Text: If we believe not, yet he abideth faithful: he cannot deny himself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3cbc8c0-6334-43c6-a52b-866dc57069e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: 2TI 2:14
Text: Of these things put them in remembrance, charging them before the Lord that they strive not about words to no profit, but to the subverting of the hearers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:766afd52-a247-4f9c-afc9-25618867aeb6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 2TI 2:15
Text: Study to shew thyself approved unto God, a workman that needeth not to be ashamed, rightly dividing the word of truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aba63287-0720-4ae4-a6ba-5977c2a514ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: 2TI 2:16
Text: But shun profane and vain babblings: for they will increase unto more ungodliness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f31ce9da-419d-4649-8a2c-20afe0bbaeff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: 2TI 2:17
Text: And their word will eat as doth a canker: of whom is Hymenaeus and Philetus;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a9de171-d271-4307-b3b4-de72ef460b45>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: 2TI 2:18
Text: Who concerning the truth have erred, saying that the resurrection is past already; and overthrow the faith of some.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2f3c9b6-4fa1-45b6-be94-3333de7da2d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: 2TI 2:19
Text: Nevertheless the foundation of God standeth sure, having this seal, The Lord knoweth them that are his. And, Let every one that nameth the name of Christ depart from iniquity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e28ca716-7b07-40b8-96c6-c82992274aa0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: 2TI 2:20
Text: But in a great house there are not only vessels of gold and of silver, but also of wood and of earth; and some to honour, and some to dishonour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3e182a8-750c-48c9-badb-8da279d63b35>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 2TI 2:21
Text: If a man therefore purge himself from these, he shall be a vessel unto honour, sanctified, and meet for the master’s use, and prepared unto every good work.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de94eeef-f9bc-4c4f-9cc5-2026d2c201c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: 2TI 2:22
Text: Flee also youthful lusts: but follow righteousness, faith, charity, peace, with them that call on the Lord out of a pure heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b480ec1-2f3f-4bf3-8e45-692aec9b6b62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: 2TI 2:23
Text: But foolish and unlearned questions avoid, knowing that they do gender strifes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd4f8507-4cd6-4252-9c6e-0c477a3f9dab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: 2TI 2:24
Text: And the servant of the Lord must not strive; but be gentle unto all men, apt to teach, patient,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfe77f55-efe1-4c74-b7ae-7458c7283ae1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 2TI 2:25
Text: In meekness instructing those that oppose themselves; if God peradventure will give them repentance to the acknowledging of the truth;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/2/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99300a6c-ed03-4a71-896b-82dd4fc05e16>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: 2TI 2:26
Text: And that they may recover themselves out of the snare of the devil, who are taken captive by him at his will.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9cc64151-13ef-432a-9501-99e7b2238786>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: 2TI 3:1
Text: This know also, that in the last days perilous times shall come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f35abc2-4a42-4ce8-8ea4-00a55d49abba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: 2TI 3:2
Text: For men shall be lovers of their own selves, covetous, boasters, proud, blasphemers, disobedient to parents, unthankful, unholy,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc034deb-6e4d-4de3-bc66-c3366486f74a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: 2TI 3:3
Text: Without natural affection, trucebreakers, false accusers, incontinent, fierce, despisers of those that are good,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e6ee76a-0edb-4b5e-a808-40552de236ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: 2TI 3:4
Text: Traitors, heady, highminded, lovers of pleasures more than lovers of God;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79bd7042-3a94-4d86-a4c7-d27179fc1830>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: 2TI 3:5
Text: Having a form of godliness, but denying the power thereof: from such turn away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bcfb1ffd-b9f8-4ea7-8a6f-7f7052a1a3cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: 2TI 3:6
Text: For of this sort are they which creep into houses, and lead captive silly women laden with sins, led away with divers lusts,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aac089cb-2d6c-4d71-a157-914664d17ad0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: 2TI 3:7
Text: Ever learning, and never able to come to the knowledge of the truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b575306-e9fa-496e-b95c-f00968cb0527>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 2TI 3:8
Text: Now as Jannes and Jambres withstood Moses, so do these also resist the truth: men of corrupt minds, reprobate concerning the faith.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53589e0e-0a0a-41cb-b9bb-135607f17562>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 2TI 3:9
Text: But they shall proceed no further: for their folly shall be manifest unto all men, as theirs also was.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96768d3b-622d-487c-b714-1b761301677c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: 2TI 3:10
Text: But thou hast fully known my doctrine, manner of life, purpose, faith, longsuffering, charity, patience,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:182cd63f-2b49-43bf-b4fe-52ead2bb63db>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 2TI 3:11
Text: Persecutions, afflictions, which came unto me at Antioch, at Iconium, at Lystra; what persecutions I endured: but out of them all the Lord delivered me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af581b91-fca1-4382-8d50-3a5fc6800465>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: 2TI 3:12
Text: Yea, and all that will live godly in Christ Jesus shall suffer persecution.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:770297d6-ced0-4ec9-851d-1b97a63882b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: 2TI 3:13
Text: But evil men and seducers shall wax worse and worse, deceiving, and being deceived.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5093719f-334d-413d-9017-4f49431d9bcd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 2TI 3:14
Text: But continue thou in the things which thou hast learned and hast been assured of, knowing of whom thou hast learned them;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1be5eedc-b7cd-4cb7-a598-c53631f009af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 2TI 3:15
Text: And that from a child thou hast known the holy scriptures, which are able to make thee wise unto salvation through faith which is in Christ Jesus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2062f03f-0ed2-4074-9be7-ce4178fa9d4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 2TI 3:16
Text: All scripture is given by inspiration of God, and is profitable for doctrine, for reproof, for correction, for instruction in righteousness:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b4d3bf0-868b-4a2e-9d0e-4fcfeb15609e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: 2TI 3:17
Text: That the man of God may be perfect, throughly furnished unto all good works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d88f87d7-f697-4fd1-b244-94bc22e0d407>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 2TI 4:1
Text: I charge thee therefore before God, and the Lord Jesus Christ, who shall judge the quick and the dead at his appearing and his kingdom;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a747390-a217-4f78-9c5e-e147a7feeb00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 2TI 4:2
Text: Preach the word; be instant in season, out of season; reprove, rebuke, exhort with all longsuffering and doctrine.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1afa9788-8dc7-48a4-bb0f-10b44371a652>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 2TI 4:3
Text: For the time will come when they will not endure sound doctrine; but after their own lusts shall they heap to themselves teachers, having itching ears;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6657b175-710f-402e-9cf4-237128fcf534>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: 2TI 4:4
Text: And they shall turn away their ears from the truth, and shall be turned unto fables.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42cb8716-c152-4e33-82a7-75cd7556a60b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: 2TI 4:5
Text: But watch thou in all things, endure afflictions, do the work of an evangelist, make full proof of thy ministry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ce1c7c1-fa0d-4f89-ac90-f9cdabd86cf1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: 2TI 4:6
Text: For I am now ready to be offered, and the time of my departure is at hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81b8c408-c4d4-4db7-a2e3-095b77766cf3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: 2TI 4:7
Text: I have fought a good fight, I have finished my course, I have kept the faith:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b02ce0c4-d0e7-4f97-872e-4ab97b1b0e29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: 2TI 4:8
Text: Henceforth there is laid up for me a crown of righteousness, which the Lord, the righteous judge, shall give me at that day: and not to me only, but unto all them also that love his appearing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f12ed006-acad-4d89-bcfb-26ac932b791f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 67

Reference: 2TI 4:9
Text: Do thy diligence to come shortly unto me:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b0b73c2-387d-48fe-ad3c-d8c5fde0f2c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: 2TI 4:10
Text: For Demas hath forsaken me, having loved this present world, and is departed unto Thessalonica; Crescens to Galatia, Titus unto Dalmatia.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b23cd95-9e31-4d03-b844-07a83aa98465>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: 2TI 4:11
Text: Only Luke is with me. Take Mark, and bring him with thee: for he is profitable to me for the ministry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c5236206-afe8-4f27-9c63-7ec02d456944>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 63

Reference: 2TI 4:12
Text: And Tychicus have I sent to Ephesus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54e1f9e4-c229-4148-b89b-8a281982cfeb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: 2TI 4:13
Text: The cloke that I left at Troas with Carpus, when thou comest, bring with thee, and the books, but especially the parchments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46bbfb62-42ce-43dd-9716-82051bd49425>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: 2TI 4:14
Text: Alexander the coppersmith did me much evil: the Lord reward him according to his works:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5af6b8d6-6af3-4bb8-95cd-16d71fdde784>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: 2TI 4:15
Text: Of whom be thou ware also; for he hath greatly withstood our words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41e686c7-8da7-4faf-8b60-855dedf06470>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: 2TI 4:16
Text: At my first answer no man stood with me, but all men forsook me: I pray God that it may not be laid to their charge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:035e49d8-94bc-45f1-a896-f5f8f943a651>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: 2TI 4:17
Text: Notwithstanding the Lord stood with me, and strengthened me; that by me the preaching might be fully known, and that all the Gentiles might hear: and I was delivered out of the mouth of the lion.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/4/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:409284ce-e23c-4efe-9455-353018fbc262>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: 2TI 4:18
Text: And the Lord shall deliver me from every evil work, and will preserve me unto his heavenly kingdom: to whom be glory for ever and ever. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/4/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd40c74d-707c-4af5-8b31-a0a676da9b46>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: 2TI 4:19
Text: Salute Prisca and Aquila, and the household of Onesiphorus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/4/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:248c3f61-454d-473d-bee9-48f96c94294a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: 2TI 4:20
Text: Erastus abode at Corinth: but Trophimus have I left at Miletum sick.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/4/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ad8e7e7-0c36-473b-ac9a-81c9e7c6d657>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 2TI 4:21
Text: Do thy diligence to come before winter. Eubulus greeteth thee, and Pudens, and Linus, and Claudia, and all the brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2TI/4/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:510ed4ac-26e1-474f-ae9c-b8063f6f6817>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: 2TI 4:22
Text: The Lord Jesus Christ be with thy spirit. Grace be with you. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41cc22de-41e2-4984-8b96-d919166f8397>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: TIT 1:1
Text: Paul, a servant of God, and an apostle of Jesus Christ, according to the faith of God’s elect, and the acknowledging of the truth which is after godliness;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:572fd4fd-4e21-47cf-b74e-19b97eb1731d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: TIT 1:2
Text: In hope of eternal life, which God, that cannot lie, promised before the world began;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ade61fb1-daad-455f-bbdd-88539b1429f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: TIT 1:3
Text: But hath in due times manifested his word through preaching, which is committed unto me according to the commandment of God our Saviour;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b7d66b5-72b0-4927-b6ba-be0d13544a41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: TIT 1:4
Text: To Titus, mine own son after the common faith: Grace, mercy, and peace, from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ our Saviour.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f9f1df6-3447-4f88-a1bd-338b93443e8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: TIT 1:5
Text: For this cause left I thee in Crete, that thou shouldest set in order the things that are wanting, and ordain elders in every city, as I had appointed thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91fb46fe-439b-4b91-9893-19d006bba295>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: TIT 1:6
Text: If any be blameless, the husband of one wife, having faithful children not accused of riot or unruly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:25136f5f-aa14-4e3b-a119-95cf1274d1ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: TIT 1:7
Text: For a bishop must be blameless, as the steward of God; not selfwilled, not soon angry, not given to wine, no striker, not given to filthy lucre;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8311145a-b9ea-4358-9ae7-dd8ab4a92d8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: TIT 1:8
Text: But a lover of hospitality, a lover of good men, sober, just, holy, temperate;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2c37361-17ec-4dcf-957b-52dfe9d4bf53>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: TIT 1:9
Text: Holding fast the faithful word as he hath been taught, that he may be able by sound doctrine both to exhort and to convince the gainsayers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0db2fcc-e99c-4238-9829-fd540daa8265>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: TIT 1:10
Text: For there are many unruly and vain talkers and deceivers, specially they of the circumcision:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:079834ca-7b62-4e84-a770-e695da9db8b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: TIT 1:11
Text: Whose mouths must be stopped, who subvert whole houses, teaching things which they ought not, for filthy lucre’s sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b664316-ab19-4b16-b3f6-ee82d361383d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: TIT 1:12
Text: One of themselves, even a prophet of their own, said, The Cretians are alway liars, evil beasts, slow bellies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5745990-461f-4d7f-bc7a-8d90c8fe1057>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: TIT 1:13
Text: This witness is true. Wherefore rebuke them sharply, that they may be sound in the faith;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:205e9273-2518-4b69-b144-4135b8e632eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: TIT 1:14
Text: Not giving heed to Jewish fables, and commandments of men, that turn from the truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9539d02d-7423-48e2-b6a2-cea05665a9ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: TIT 1:15
Text: Unto the pure all things are pure: but unto them that are defiled and unbelieving is nothing pure; but even their mind and conscience is defiled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d82b19f1-5fd1-4e7e-b232-ca88f7007716>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: TIT 1:16
Text: They profess that they know God; but in works they deny him, being abominable, and disobedient, and unto every good work reprobate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e198050-ee33-4910-a8ea-c75b1e5ad0a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: TIT 2:1
Text: But speak thou the things which become sound doctrine:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ebebf826-229f-4ab2-937c-d579ec971b4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: TIT 2:2
Text: That the aged men be sober, grave, temperate, sound in faith, in charity, in patience.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7deec5c-0a02-4eea-8818-d365bd2a56f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: TIT 2:3
Text: The aged women likewise, that they be in behaviour as becometh holiness, not false accusers, not given to much wine, teachers of good things;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:952f1927-cecd-4c65-a6be-21886ed96e55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: TIT 2:4
Text: That they may teach the young women to be sober, to love their husbands, to love their children,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42d9d3b7-c491-4993-818f-4b89dd2ed3e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: TIT 2:5
Text: To be discreet, chaste, keepers at home, good, obedient to their own husbands, that the word of God be not blasphemed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9e6e00b-1908-4744-b7c7-5e23975bc8f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 71

Reference: TIT 2:6
Text: Young men likewise exhort to be sober minded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc683393-b850-4d70-8b48-940a0d9d6683>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: TIT 2:7
Text: In all things shewing thyself a pattern of good works: in doctrine shewing uncorruptness, gravity, sincerity,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:116dd27e-0b0c-46e3-8ea3-d7be49c5854f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: TIT 2:8
Text: Sound speech, that cannot be condemned; that he that is of the contrary part may be ashamed, having no evil thing to say of you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b731f5e5-5f24-4e9a-a4ee-2d7ca66eb0fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: TIT 2:9
Text: Exhort servants to be obedient unto their own masters, and to please them well in all things; not answering again;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5559a28c-96a5-47c3-829e-38fa476a1421>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: TIT 2:10
Text: Not purloining, but shewing all good fidelity; that they may adorn the doctrine of God our Saviour in all things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9682e18d-40f7-421b-8343-43cdfd356f27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: TIT 2:11
Text: For the grace of God that bringeth salvation hath appeared to all men,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2543425c-80d8-4a3e-8e51-1acf6950211d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: TIT 2:12
Text: Teaching us that, denying ungodliness and worldly lusts, we should live soberly, righteously, and godly, in this present world;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4f3f16d-1be8-4953-9cbe-919f634b28a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: TIT 2:13
Text: Looking for that blessed hope, and the glorious appearing of the great God and our Saviour Jesus Christ;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6392a1e-903c-4fa2-8365-1b6be1dedffe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: TIT 2:14
Text: Who gave himself for us, that he might redeem us from all iniquity, and purify unto himself a peculiar people, zealous of good works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a07085d9-055c-4411-842b-5ddefe4e6652>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: TIT 2:15
Text: These things speak, and exhort, and rebuke with all authority. Let no man despise thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a38e5686-52f4-4e60-a0f6-ed9ab2a685e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: TIT 3:1
Text: Put them in mind to be subject to principalities and powers, to obey magistrates, to be ready to every good work,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:470ec048-a62a-45a2-b4d9-fd0ae4df0d5e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: TIT 3:2
Text: To speak evil of no man, to be no brawlers, but gentle, shewing all meekness unto all men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e9aca20-0550-45af-adef-5c49342569fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: TIT 3:3
Text: For we ourselves also were sometimes foolish, disobedient, deceived, serving divers lusts and pleasures, living in malice and envy, hateful, and hating one another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:153abf22-c676-4c2e-a05b-7d96edfcda8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: TIT 3:4
Text: But after that the kindness and love of God our Saviour toward man appeared,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7c84d0e-307b-42f0-9d7d-efe3d849f96b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: TIT 3:5
Text: Not by works of righteousness which we have done, but according to his mercy he saved us, by the washing of regeneration, and renewing of the Holy Ghost;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1d2ec9d-4aab-47cb-8015-4369707db780>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: TIT 3:6
Text: Which he shed on us abundantly through Jesus Christ our Saviour;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1f3e0df7-8a36-4841-a9dc-3a305432042c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: TIT 3:7
Text: That being justified by his grace, we should be made heirs according to the hope of eternal life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ef6764d-7790-4dc7-a576-c8feb6528230>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: TIT 3:8
Text: This is a faithful saying, and these things I will that thou affirm constantly, that they which have believed in God might be careful to maintain good works. These things are good and profitable unto men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b6c9f04-de17-4d17-a9e7-a8853b8916bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: TIT 3:9
Text: But avoid foolish questions, and genealogies, and contentions, and strivings about the law; for they are unprofitable and vain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4a57c11-df9a-47c6-9368-be5e5c0451c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: TIT 3:10
Text: A man that is an heretick after the first and second admonition reject;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:451f0153-213e-492b-98e0-feecb982239d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: TIT 3:11
Text: Knowing that he that is such is subverted, and sinneth, being condemned of himself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94a73b1c-8083-4e1d-80ee-6cdd785129ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: TIT 3:12
Text: When I shall send Artemas unto thee, or Tychicus, be diligent to come unto me to Nicopolis: for I have determined there to winter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5361976-6427-43ee-8cf9-b51985f146cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: TIT 3:13
Text: Bring Zenas the lawyer and Apollos on their journey diligently, that nothing be wanting unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ae23e24-bee3-4b29-a12e-c284c15df601>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: TIT 3:14
Text: And let ours also learn to maintain good works for necessary uses, that they be not unfruitful.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/TIT/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92254789-b074-485c-9887-5d05f2fe6928>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: TIT 3:15
Text: All that are with me salute thee. Greet them that love us in the faith. Grace be with you all. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:707c9cdf-205b-4155-aafc-c39bf84e54a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PHM 1:1
Text: Paul, a prisoner of Jesus Christ, and Timothy our brother, unto Philemon our dearly beloved, and fellowlabourer,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52e12fdb-53ae-4c55-973a-93d6a06fdee1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: PHM 1:2
Text: And to our beloved Apphia, and Archippus our fellowsoldier, and to the church in thy house:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a3ae9d0-8482-4846-b767-e8a0e2a16592>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: PHM 1:3
Text: Grace to you, and peace, from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:614ba540-90b0-4b6f-841f-78e785c831fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: PHM 1:4
Text: I thank my God, making mention of thee always in my prayers,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6f696a1c-f1fb-420a-a47e-d4084ce120e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: PHM 1:5
Text: Hearing of thy love and faith, which thou hast toward the Lord Jesus, and toward all saints;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37bb7487-489b-438c-a843-8dffae642b37>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: PHM 1:6
Text: That the communication of thy faith may become effectual by the acknowledging of every good thing which is in you in Christ Jesus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8e1c5f5-4bb2-4a0f-b1ab-061a659a108f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: PHM 1:7
Text: For we have great joy and consolation in thy love, because the bowels of the saints are refreshed by thee, brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0987a4b-0673-45c9-aade-2c96e0720b13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: PHM 1:8
Text: Wherefore, though I might be much bold in Christ to enjoin thee that which is convenient,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d68f508-1d2d-43d7-818f-67a38784c216>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: PHM 1:9
Text: Yet for love’s sake I rather beseech thee, being such an one as Paul the aged, and now also a prisoner of Jesus Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:57b5ab7b-b402-4042-976b-a9648435b26f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: PHM 1:10
Text: I beseech thee for my son Onesimus, whom I have begotten in my bonds:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:629863f3-4082-4f14-9bfa-cc784fd9b4c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: PHM 1:11
Text: Which in time past was to thee unprofitable, but now profitable to thee and to me:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ee4d28a6-c47c-44a0-80bd-799790842a4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: PHM 1:12
Text: Whom I have sent again: thou therefore receive him, that is, mine own bowels:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf15631f-8ea4-4a48-92fa-2337e9446e85>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: PHM 1:13
Text: Whom I would have retained with me, that in thy stead he might have ministered unto me in the bonds of the gospel:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0b9c344-4a77-4728-84be-138c9124b0c5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: PHM 1:14
Text: But without thy mind would I do nothing; that thy benefit should not be as it were of necessity, but willingly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75b2c11a-d19b-406d-83e6-c6dcbdd23d6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: PHM 1:15
Text: For perhaps he therefore departed for a season, that thou shouldest receive him for ever;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be732058-8891-4473-ad57-3e43521daf0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: PHM 1:16
Text: Not now as a servant, but above a servant, a brother beloved, specially to me, but how much more unto thee, both in the flesh, and in the Lord?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8d2c4330-b9b4-47d4-8a32-3617842da86e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: PHM 1:17
Text: If thou count me therefore a partner, receive him as myself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c54fe2ba-281e-401e-b74d-e9ede613d657>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: PHM 1:18
Text: If he hath wronged thee, or oweth thee ought, put that on mine account;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c34b8d83-00de-4126-93e7-410ce1ad9515>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: PHM 1:19
Text: I Paul have written it with mine own hand, I will repay it: albeit I do not say to thee how thou owest unto me even thine own self besides.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae894da0-9f6b-4542-bec5-e3f20a5931bf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: PHM 1:20
Text: Yea, brother, let me have joy of thee in the Lord: refresh my bowels in the Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:833b324e-0600-43a8-b237-227bf1bbab15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: PHM 1:21
Text: Having confidence in thy obedience I wrote unto thee, knowing that thou wilt also do more than I say.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cde483b1-b7cc-4b7c-93d6-dc6028b1d58b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: PHM 1:22
Text: But withal prepare me also a lodging: for I trust that through your prayers I shall be given unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a661f62f-e635-45a3-8b8b-ed18c79c2c5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: PHM 1:23
Text: There salute thee Epaphras, my fellowprisoner in Christ Jesus;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:450bf0ba-c445-4be9-b9fc-2e47cfbabcfb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 81

Reference: PHM 1:24
Text: Marcus, Aristarchus, Demas, Lucas, my fellowlabourers.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/PHM/1/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28ecabb4-eb03-4dfa-aade-77729f7b9559>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: PHM 1:25
Text: The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4dd4be1a-8763-425d-ade1-b791eed9a7aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: HEB 1:1
Text: God, who at sundry times and in divers manners spake in time past unto the fathers by the prophets,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94271ec1-c18b-4f7a-a4e7-edfb9658916c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: HEB 1:2
Text: Hath in these last days spoken unto us by his Son, whom he hath appointed heir of all things, by whom also he made the worlds;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3c98d5b-e453-48b9-9672-2154ff89f47f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 243

Reference: HEB 1:3
Text: Who being the brightness of his glory, and the express image of his person, and upholding all things by the word of his power, when he had by himself purged our sins, sat down on the right hand of the Majesty on high:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6697d62-c900-4888-8c5e-9616004688be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: HEB 1:4
Text: Being made so much better than the angels, as he hath by inheritance obtained a more excellent name than they.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eeeadce9-b7ff-4f52-bf06-19c3781b4af4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: HEB 1:5
Text: For unto which of the angels said he at any time, Thou art my Son, this day have I begotten thee? And again, I will be to him a Father, and he shall be to me a Son?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e5038c7a-0ea9-40ca-a9a4-a0b7d94fcf7b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: HEB 1:6
Text: And again, when he bringeth in the firstbegotten into the world, he saith, And let all the angels of God worship him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f03e4879-34e5-4f06-b87f-c0b2673f2c77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: HEB 1:7
Text: And of the angels he saith, Who maketh his angels spirits, and his ministers a flame of fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a0d6f3f-ce75-4709-bd77-986e051f6bfb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: HEB 1:8
Text: But unto the Son he saith, Thy throne, O God, is for ever and ever: a sceptre of righteousness is the sceptre of thy kingdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb7c69c7-56e6-4e92-8241-82f526bbe927>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: HEB 1:9
Text: Thou hast loved righteousness, and hated iniquity; therefore God, even thy God, hath anointed thee with the oil of gladness above thy fellows.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63a297c2-2581-47af-a124-67f12c1c571d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: HEB 1:10
Text: And, Thou, Lord, in the beginning hast laid the foundation of the earth; and the heavens are the works of thine hands:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0efd40c6-c171-489d-9d2e-82343ae57043>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: HEB 1:11
Text: They shall perish; but thou remainest; and they all shall wax old as doth a garment;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30af754f-8a7c-4ff8-b2de-3eb34079b49a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: HEB 1:12
Text: And as a vesture shalt thou fold them up, and they shall be changed: but thou art the same, and thy years shall not fail.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2ea96a35-dd2f-4e82-b4cc-44ec04058cee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: HEB 1:13
Text: But to which of the angels said he at any time, Sit on my right hand, until I make thine enemies thy footstool?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c496766-0a8c-4212-b9b0-7e94f59ec668>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: HEB 1:14
Text: Are they not all ministering spirits, sent forth to minister for them who shall be heirs of salvation?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4541388-47e3-4067-b37f-ec91cdd71a42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: HEB 2:1
Text: Therefore we ought to give the more earnest heed to the things which we have heard, lest at any time we should let them slip.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60f56d80-afda-4f9d-9d9c-3190ad8091e5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: HEB 2:2
Text: For if the word spoken by angels was stedfast, and every transgression and disobedience received a just recompence of reward;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc6c3e5b-7627-4d6b-9f63-72ca5dc3b2fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: HEB 2:3
Text: How shall we escape, if we neglect so great salvation; which at the first began to be spoken by the Lord, and was confirmed unto us by them that heard him;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:59b0bb9f-41f5-4abf-a91a-6a964466584f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: HEB 2:4
Text: God also bearing them witness, both with signs and wonders, and with divers miracles, and gifts of the Holy Ghost, according to his own will?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ff3bcae-d001-4206-8cb3-a44a5048ce27>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: HEB 2:5
Text: For unto the angels hath he not put in subjection the world to come, whereof we speak.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61a3d1bf-6025-4b0f-9ad2-e49963552d8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: HEB 2:6
Text: But one in a certain place testified, saying, What is man, that thou art mindful of him? or the son of man that thou visitest him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44fc14a3-1662-4d7a-897e-95e10a8db3a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: HEB 2:7
Text: Thou madest him a little lower than the angels; thou crownedst him with glory and honour, and didst set him over the works of thy hands:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8975827a-5998-4d6a-ba52-d781f05caf90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: HEB 2:8
Text: Thou hast put all things in subjection under his feet. For in that he put all in subjection under him, he left nothing that is not put under him. But now we see not yet all things put under him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fef44fdb-eea9-44f1-8a2c-c15ebaa38933>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: HEB 2:9
Text: But we see Jesus, who was made a little lower than the angels for the suffering of death, crowned with glory and honour; that he by the grace of God should taste death for every man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c695ae56-da36-46fe-9778-210acd4144d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: HEB 2:10
Text: For it became him, for whom are all things, and by whom are all things, in bringing many sons unto glory, to make the captain of their salvation perfect through sufferings.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc4afd53-5574-4682-9990-dccf78b0051b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: HEB 2:11
Text: For both he that sanctifieth and they who are sanctified are all of one: for which cause he is not ashamed to call them brethren,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d990228-eb67-4f01-b6dc-12f2468e8c8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: HEB 2:12
Text: Saying, I will declare thy name unto my brethren, in the midst of the church will I sing praise unto thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95fac21b-1290-4df8-951c-110a0ec0b7e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: HEB 2:13
Text: And again, I will put my trust in him. And again, Behold I and the children which God hath given me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec1e2f30-1070-41d2-ab0e-e3d072dd9d81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: HEB 2:14
Text: Forasmuch then as the children are partakers of flesh and blood, he also himself likewise took part of the same; that through death he might destroy him that had the power of death, that is, the devil;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a92c0b6c-28cb-417f-b1e4-3b65479d53a5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: HEB 2:15
Text: And deliver them who through fear of death were all their lifetime subject to bondage.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a8f800e-4a6b-4054-a3d0-c429e7a6bf4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: HEB 2:16
Text: For verily he took not on him the nature of angels; but he took on him the seed of Abraham.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39f7e07d-b5b2-4ec7-a9e0-c540b5f73008>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 233

Reference: HEB 2:17
Text: Wherefore in all things it behoved him to be made like unto his brethren, that he might be a merciful and faithful high priest in things pertaining to God, to make reconciliation for the sins of the people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bef7287-e785-413a-897e-55a86c541d1c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: HEB 2:18
Text: For in that he himself hath suffered being tempted, he is able to succour them that are tempted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37809174-1374-4915-8995-84e4d24bb670>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: HEB 3:1
Text: Wherefore, holy brethren, partakers of the heavenly calling, consider the Apostle and High Priest of our profession, Christ Jesus;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b389dba0-8f57-41a4-9ccd-a519bb4d6b91>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: HEB 3:2
Text: Who was faithful to him that appointed him, as also Moses was faithful in all his house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0e064b9-0e38-48b5-9cb2-0c80ee32c66f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: HEB 3:3
Text: For this man was counted worthy of more glory than Moses, inasmuch as he who hath builded the house hath more honour than the house.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:935613e2-5e9a-493d-8244-9cb5ceb2ee95>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: HEB 3:4
Text: For every house is builded by some man; but he that built all things is God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff5c32da-fc94-463d-8f22-457c7a9aa18f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: HEB 3:5
Text: And Moses verily was faithful in all his house, as a servant, for a testimony of those things which were to be spoken after;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2f5078a-c035-423e-840e-858b025da085>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: HEB 3:6
Text: But Christ as a son over his own house; whose house are we, if we hold fast the confidence and the rejoicing of the hope firm unto the end.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90c19e82-bbc7-410b-b847-bd2560cbcde5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: HEB 3:7
Text: Wherefore (as the Holy Ghost saith, To day if ye will hear his voice,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c902b9e-3962-413c-93f5-d08039441336>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: HEB 3:8
Text: Harden not your hearts, as in the provocation, in the day of temptation in the wilderness:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83ad9e65-4a2a-4421-b524-311393eac9fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: HEB 3:9
Text: When your fathers tempted me, proved me, and saw my works forty years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b6c5b40-ccce-4af9-b7c7-4f062c2daa55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: HEB 3:10
Text: Wherefore I was grieved with that generation, and said, They do alway err in their heart; and they have not known my ways.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50470ac0-0708-4f7a-8cc3-e211405190fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: HEB 3:11
Text: So I sware in my wrath, They shall not enter into my rest.)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46ac2d7d-d3a1-40d4-839b-86afbf4aa979>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: HEB 3:12
Text: Take heed, brethren, lest there be in any of you an evil heart of unbelief, in departing from the living God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77d7531e-4421-4a45-b88e-3921571d328c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: HEB 3:13
Text: But exhort one another daily, while it is called To day; lest any of you be hardened through the deceitfulness of sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14f05e62-7e70-4c4c-8e5c-abf8e564bf29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: HEB 3:14
Text: For we are made partakers of Christ, if we hold the beginning of our confidence stedfast unto the end;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2986c73d-b8ff-45b9-8fee-f80d78cb86a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: HEB 3:15
Text: While it is said, To day if ye will hear his voice, harden not your hearts, as in the provocation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5467f966-6e7d-4dad-a38c-8b591abecb77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: HEB 3:16
Text: For some, when they had heard, did provoke: howbeit not all that came out of Egypt by Moses.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5402ee4-eda7-4230-8710-b27bd40cc6b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: HEB 3:17
Text: But with whom was he grieved forty years? was it not with them that had sinned, whose carcases fell in the wilderness?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4982d5e-54f6-4750-9607-d0ae86a41108>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: HEB 3:18
Text: And to whom sware he that they should not enter into his rest, but to them that believed not?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75dd410d-eb1d-4bab-9126-b769bdbd9d0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: HEB 3:19
Text: So we see that they could not enter in because of unbelief.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d944da0c-a117-413c-b7d3-e19462c3bd57>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: HEB 4:1
Text: Let us therefore fear, lest, a promise being left us of entering into his rest, any of you should seem to come short of it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd38aae0-862b-4f97-80b8-b3efe998baaf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: HEB 4:2
Text: For unto us was the gospel preached, as well as unto them: but the word preached did not profit them, not being mixed with faith in them that heard it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14d120c5-0112-45ab-868f-9715fa53b5d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: HEB 4:3
Text: For we which have believed do enter into rest, as he said, As I have sworn in my wrath, if they shall enter into my rest: although the works were finished from the foundation of the world.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3038dd7c-ea38-471d-9f7e-69db1203d4a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: HEB 4:4
Text: For he spake in a certain place of the seventh day on this wise, And God did rest the seventh day from all his works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a579c3fe-d9c9-48c6-ac89-594a4b2c9d93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: HEB 4:5
Text: And in this place again, If they shall enter into my rest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1b6ddd57-64d3-4e8c-b2f1-301eeb14c2ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: HEB 4:6
Text: Seeing therefore it remaineth that some must enter therein, and they to whom it was first preached entered not in because of unbelief:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1ad18b1-2e4a-4d83-aa59-beb333b3b1eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: HEB 4:7
Text: Again, he limiteth a certain day, saying in David, To day, after so long a time; as it is said, To day if ye will hear his voice, harden not your hearts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:344619e8-3e53-4294-a9cf-f1e554800fce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: HEB 4:8
Text: For if Jesus had given them rest, then would he not afterward have spoken of another day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da848461-5959-40e9-b7a4-0a7da40ee1a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: HEB 4:9
Text: There remaineth therefore a rest to the people of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0cd10e9-8541-42b4-a5a0-d95ba0f9f193>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: HEB 4:10
Text: For he that is entered into his rest, he also hath ceased from his own works, as God did from his.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6457eeaf-a47c-48b1-af5e-b2be8c27816c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: HEB 4:11
Text: Let us labour therefore to enter into that rest, lest any man fall after the same example of unbelief.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fdeeab1-ffed-49d8-9003-5e639d5189a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: HEB 4:12
Text: For the word of God is quick, and powerful, and sharper than any twoedged sword, piercing even to the dividing asunder of soul and spirit, and of the joints and marrow, and is a discerner of the thoughts and intents of the heart.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9b66502-9fb4-4791-b9ee-367ec37ee35d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: HEB 4:13
Text: Neither is there any creature that is not manifest in his sight: but all things are naked and opened unto the eyes of him with whom we have to do.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be36979f-79bd-4295-8cbe-4869550e1676>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: HEB 4:14
Text: Seeing then that we have a great high priest, that is passed into the heavens, Jesus the Son of God, let us hold fast our profession.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d737d8de-0cd5-4abe-9c5b-1113031c0755>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: HEB 4:15
Text: For we have not an high priest which cannot be touched with the feeling of our infirmities; but was in all points tempted like as we are, yet without sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ea1f49d-1ab3-4767-b46c-aa77ee711ebd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: HEB 4:16
Text: Let us therefore come boldly unto the throne of grace, that we may obtain mercy, and find grace to help in time of need.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35d3ca52-3e31-4786-ae24-019e58a30325>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: HEB 5:1
Text: For every high priest taken from among men is ordained for men in things pertaining to God, that he may offer both gifts and sacrifices for sins:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a7590d9-57c3-487f-ab11-ab618a5838ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: HEB 5:2
Text: Who can have compassion on the ignorant, and on them that are out of the way; for that he himself also is compassed with infirmity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbfcbe8e-fddf-4662-b076-365ffd4475a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: HEB 5:3
Text: And by reason hereof he ought, as for the people, so also for himself, to offer for sins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c6e231c-b41c-4461-bdad-5e06453d92d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: HEB 5:4
Text: And no man taketh this honour unto himself, but he that is called of God, as was Aaron.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:593967e5-60af-4d9d-b667-b1fa50c49176>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: HEB 5:5
Text: So also Christ glorified not himself to be made an high priest; but he that said unto him, Thou art my Son, to day have I begotten thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b52e585d-d5ff-44a2-87b0-b72229a1d42b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: HEB 5:6
Text: As he saith also in another place, Thou art a priest for ever after the order of Melchisedec.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f79a135-e40c-49f7-adbe-260ca177835c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: HEB 5:7
Text: Who in the days of his flesh, when he had offered up prayers and supplications with strong crying and tears unto him that was able to save him from death, and was heard in that he feared;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dad65e96-18ed-4780-a660-faa459c8f863>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: HEB 5:8
Text: Though he were a Son, yet learned he obedience by the things which he suffered;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce2265d0-2f2a-43ba-8f68-99b7bbe786c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: HEB 5:9
Text: And being made perfect, he became the author of eternal salvation unto all them that obey him;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98b25f68-899c-455f-a6a7-3a3c08bd3946>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: HEB 5:10
Text: Called of God an high priest after the order of Melchisedec.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b853cdf-6781-40b8-a2cc-467b4bbb4701>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: HEB 5:11
Text: Of whom we have many things to say, and hard to be uttered, seeing ye are dull of hearing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a86c1fa-557d-4499-83aa-21190b7edd33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: HEB 5:12
Text: For when for the time ye ought to be teachers, ye have need that one teach you again which be the first principles of the oracles of God; and are become such as have need of milk, and not of strong meat.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73d371d1-0f50-4f21-86b6-639376cb6030>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: HEB 5:13
Text: For every one that useth milk is unskilful in the word of righteousness: for he is a babe.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54ac5880-1331-438f-947d-11c879af25c9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: HEB 5:14
Text: But strong meat belongeth to them that are of full age, even those who by reason of use have their senses exercised to discern both good and evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e4644a0-2a2e-4ef8-9398-8ecbb57e74ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: HEB 6:1
Text: Therefore leaving the principles of the doctrine of Christ, let us go on unto perfection; not laying again the foundation of repentance from dead works, and of faith toward God,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:30276863-b139-452f-b742-4a48f1d3016d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: HEB 6:2
Text: Of the doctrine of baptisms, and of laying on of hands, and of resurrection of the dead, and of eternal judgment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e63060cf-83a9-4b0f-8085-bdc67796954f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 61

Reference: HEB 6:3
Text: And this will we do, if God permit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/6/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8dd57184-0c1a-4b3e-8607-77173b25b175>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: HEB 6:4
Text: For it is impossible for those who were once enlightened, and have tasted of the heavenly gift, and were made partakers of the Holy Ghost,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/6/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:63a524a4-df4c-4533-a2b9-3ac69aae8bcf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: HEB 6:5
Text: And have tasted the good word of God, and the powers of the world to come,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/6/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21344af7-e7ae-4244-8adf-d52c08508a18>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: HEB 6:6
Text: If they shall fall away, to renew them again unto repentance; seeing they crucify to themselves the Son of God afresh, and put him to an open shame.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/6/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c263d487-9879-4ee4-927b-c2bf71db604e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: HEB 6:7
Text: For the earth which drinketh in the rain that cometh oft upon it, and bringeth forth herbs meet for them by whom it is dressed, receiveth blessing from God:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/6/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d709e63-2f00-47dd-8bc1-8763074da8d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: HEB 6:8
Text: But that which beareth thorns and briers is rejected, and is nigh unto cursing; whose end is to be burned.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/6/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:098fc296-ad50-4ed9-a4f0-ab76e45e0652>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: HEB 6:9
Text: But, beloved, we are persuaded better things of you, and things that accompany salvation, though we thus speak.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/6/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3cd2e0fe-a4df-469a-b510-3e7dce2bc98f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: HEB 6:10
Text: For God is not unrighteous to forget your work and labour of love, which ye have shewed toward his name, in that ye have ministered to the saints, and do minister.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/6/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0d6dfa4-b624-4809-b049-dafe2c9e5dba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: HEB 6:11
Text: And we desire that every one of you do shew the same diligence to the full assurance of hope unto the end:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/6/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:694a4fe6-cff6-4d65-ae2b-e028450400ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: HEB 6:12
Text: That ye be not slothful, but followers of them who through faith and patience inherit the promises.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/6/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08ce5678-503b-41fc-9ee1-075e6f35cf19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: HEB 6:13
Text: For when God made promise to Abraham, because he could swear by no greater, he sware by himself,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/6/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32a034a3-e63b-438d-a9f1-374c2f676642>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: HEB 6:14
Text: Saying, Surely blessing I will bless thee, and multiplying I will multiply thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/6/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0349c6a2-b1fa-44ba-8f07-1854d4cd6378>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: HEB 6:15
Text: And so, after he had patiently endured, he obtained the promise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/6/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f9e2486-1daf-44f5-8cf9-52b6ab772da6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: HEB 6:16
Text: For men verily swear by the greater: and an oath for confirmation is to them an end of all strife.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/6/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51a9043b-5326-41aa-903b-20d69b84385d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: HEB 6:17
Text: Wherein God, willing more abundantly to shew unto the heirs of promise the immutability of his counsel, confirmed it by an oath:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/6/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86e22975-a4b7-4d4b-8239-1f1ab4c7ab29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: HEB 6:18
Text: That by two immutable things, in which it was impossible for God to lie, we might have a strong consolation, who have fled for refuge to lay hold upon the hope set before us:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/6/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2d9db49-81ff-4aef-8212-6a4c67ca796f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: HEB 6:19
Text: Which hope we have as an anchor of the soul, both sure and stedfast, and which entereth into that within the veil;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/6/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d3a5e7e-3434-433c-8c85-0466e506f390>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: HEB 6:20
Text: Whither the forerunner is for us entered, even Jesus, made an high priest for ever after the order of Melchisedec.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4cdd332-6cd1-4c18-b8f3-5dfa0446dc93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: HEB 7:1
Text: For this Melchisedec, king of Salem, priest of the most high God, who met Abraham returning from the slaughter of the kings, and blessed him;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f89c631-f9ed-4349-8e93-c0612a094e40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: HEB 7:2
Text: To whom also Abraham gave a tenth part of all; first being by interpretation King of righteousness, and after that also King of Salem, which is, King of peace;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3f70ecb-2b0f-4608-9433-1bfb5b6a559e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: HEB 7:3
Text: Without father, without mother, without descent, having neither beginning of days, nor end of life; but made like unto the Son of God; abideth a priest continually.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf164c8b-81dd-493a-bbab-900770d921c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: HEB 7:4
Text: Now consider how great this man was, unto whom even the patriarch Abraham gave the tenth of the spoils.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e02ddca3-fc29-42c3-84c6-5a8ea41ca7a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 257

Reference: HEB 7:5
Text: And verily they that are of the sons of Levi, who receive the office of the priesthood, have a commandment to take tithes of the people according to the law, that is, of their brethren, though they come out of the loins of Abraham:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ab3c2c6-db98-4d92-9fca-34dc669aa0b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: HEB 7:6
Text: But he whose descent is not counted from them received tithes of Abraham, and blessed him that had the promises.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5cbefad5-757b-4394-932f-9310f731fed2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: HEB 7:7
Text: And without all contradiction the less is blessed of the better.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:379737cd-a87e-4d27-bb84-142acae16a6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: HEB 7:8
Text: And here men that die receive tithes; but there he receiveth them, of whom it is witnessed that he liveth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cca3a1d8-b8e0-43ed-b435-10166969ca63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: HEB 7:9
Text: And as I may so say, Levi also, who receiveth tithes, payed tithes in Abraham.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:caa849e4-5119-47fb-9fbf-ca56abf5a161>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: HEB 7:10
Text: For he was yet in the loins of his father, when Melchisedec met him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c814329-97ad-40e9-95b0-3c25a97eea58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: HEB 7:11
Text: If therefore perfection were by the Levitical priesthood, (for under it the people received the law,) what further need was there that another priest should rise after the order of Melchisedec, and not be called after the order of Aaron?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:15645ea2-ebba-4cf4-b5d6-c4bb92438997>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: HEB 7:12
Text: For the priesthood being changed, there is made of necessity a change also of the law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e1f7f80-24d6-4a6e-a38b-3aba257490b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: HEB 7:13
Text: For he of whom these things are spoken pertaineth to another tribe, of which no man gave attendance at the altar.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9a511335-305d-4252-8345-45eebfe97b30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: HEB 7:14
Text: For it is evident that our Lord sprang out of Juda; of which tribe Moses spake nothing concerning priesthood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be13be1c-ccb9-4416-a844-7b4a4470e233>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: HEB 7:15
Text: And it is yet far more evident: for that after the similitude of Melchisedec there ariseth another priest,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:434624cc-a749-47b1-88c0-f3d679ef4d36>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: HEB 7:16
Text: Who is made, not after the law of a carnal commandment, but after the power of an endless life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08eb166a-b3a9-4d21-bb9a-be0706dff8b9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: HEB 7:17
Text: For he testifieth, Thou art a priest for ever after the order of Melchisedec.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ea32bff-ddad-4a20-8a26-38a9ba3a0628>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: HEB 7:18
Text: For there is verily a disannulling of the commandment going before for the weakness and unprofitableness thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b50dd3fb-6d72-4154-bc69-1215c05a94b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: HEB 7:19
Text: For the law made nothing perfect, but the bringing in of a better hope did; by the which we draw nigh unto God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c12a6f9-133e-4a3a-bcf4-5116cba00bff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: HEB 7:20
Text: And inasmuch as not without an oath he was made priest:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce9d4f25-4c8f-4c70-9573-6912ed6aab61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: HEB 7:21
Text: (For those priests were made without an oath; but this with an oath by him that said unto him, The Lord sware and will not repent, Thou art a priest for ever after the order of Melchisedec:)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28965f1a-e75f-4d34-bbfa-24b0014363fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 84

Reference: HEB 7:22
Text: By so much was Jesus made a surety of a better testament.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6943f8a0-70ba-4662-ab72-3911d2eb0bf6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: HEB 7:23
Text: And they truly were many priests, because they were not suffered to continue by reason of death:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b2ef943-c629-4f50-b3f4-5e7a866be467>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: HEB 7:24
Text: But this man, because he continueth ever, hath an unchangeable priesthood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a7473bc-4450-4df3-bcba-c603ad770c86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: HEB 7:25
Text: Wherefore he is able also to save them to the uttermost that come unto God by him, seeing he ever liveth to make intercession for them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:de86eab3-e3d1-4f71-8ee0-012bfe5badbb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: HEB 7:26
Text: For such an high priest became us, who is holy, harmless, undefiled, separate from sinners, and made higher than the heavens;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01147e7c-2c8e-4790-8380-f0221ef04f58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: HEB 7:27
Text: Who needeth not daily, as those high priests, to offer up sacrifice, first for his own sins, and then for the people’s: for this he did once, when he offered up himself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/7/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b83a0aa6-28aa-424a-b448-e8a58b9271d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: HEB 7:28
Text: For the law maketh men high priests which have infirmity; but the word of the oath, which was since the law, maketh the Son, who is consecrated for evermore.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/8/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:285a393e-7e8f-42b7-89ba-e88ac52f5bba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: HEB 8:1
Text: Now of the things which we have spoken this is the sum: We have such an high priest, who is set on the right hand of the throne of the Majesty in the heavens;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/8/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a921fc99-f1f1-46d9-bba6-1648bcde25cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: HEB 8:2
Text: A minister of the sanctuary, and of the true tabernacle, which the Lord pitched, and not man.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/8/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a514b14-e5aa-4971-8b02-0400457cb727>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: HEB 8:3
Text: For every high priest is ordained to offer gifts and sacrifices: wherefore it is of necessity that this man have somewhat also to offer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/8/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80882313-ed07-43fa-b1a7-ff2adeb981e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: HEB 8:4
Text: For if he were on earth, he should not be a priest, seeing that there are priests that offer gifts according to the law:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/8/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1f43348-cd36-4363-ba0b-3351c899895c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 256

Reference: HEB 8:5
Text: Who serve unto the example and shadow of heavenly things, as Moses was admonished of God when he was about to make the tabernacle: for, See, saith he, that thou make all things according to the pattern shewed to thee in the mount.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/8/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2bb525b2-a7fd-4488-bde5-82c665588c7f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: HEB 8:6
Text: But now hath he obtained a more excellent ministry, by how much also he is the mediator of a better covenant, which was established upon better promises.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/8/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8cb51f67-fc47-4d88-9a63-94f27e67f44c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: HEB 8:7
Text: For if that first covenant had been faultless, then should no place have been sought for the second.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/8/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7650aa88-3d68-4d6d-8a33-d1b8a7e429e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: HEB 8:8
Text: For finding fault with them, he saith, Behold, the days come, saith the Lord, when I will make a new covenant with the house of Israel and with the house of Judah:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/8/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:423f333f-881f-46c1-b5d3-efcbab775965>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: HEB 8:9
Text: Not according to the covenant that I made with their fathers in the day when I took them by the hand to lead them out of the land of Egypt; because they continued not in my covenant, and I regarded them not, saith the Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/8/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41fbdf68-b9a1-4d96-8dd8-3f58a54c580b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: HEB 8:10
Text: For this is the covenant that I will make with the house of Israel after those days, saith the Lord; I will put my laws into their mind, and write them in their hearts: and I will be to them a God, and they shall be to me a people:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/8/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb9e8458-149e-4670-95dc-ffa3e73f2f06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: HEB 8:11
Text: And they shall not teach every man his neighbour, and every man his brother, saying, Know the Lord: for all shall know me, from the least to the greatest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/8/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50c28d49-5e03-4b2b-adb5-2222465dfba0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: HEB 8:12
Text: For I will be merciful to their unrighteousness, and their sins and their iniquities will I remember no more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/8/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6444eae0-af52-4d06-9061-09dedd8a39aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: HEB 8:13
Text: In that he saith, A new covenant, he hath made the first old. Now that which decayeth and waxeth old is ready to vanish away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f24f2b85-ddca-4b0a-88dc-5d7ecaf8aee9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: HEB 9:1
Text: Then verily the first covenant had also ordinances of divine service, and a worldly sanctuary.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23f09d40-8601-4708-9896-6166500d0e8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: HEB 9:2
Text: For there was a tabernacle made; the first, wherein was the candlestick, and the table, and the shewbread; which is called the sanctuary.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58bbe959-63b4-4385-97d2-115036264b4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: HEB 9:3
Text: And after the second veil, the tabernacle which is called the Holiest of all;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c94fd02a-f3cc-4c8e-9125-f57e97aafd12>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: HEB 9:4
Text: Which had the golden censer, and the ark of the covenant overlaid round about with gold, wherein was the golden pot that had manna, and Aaron’s rod that budded, and the tables of the covenant;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34ee9228-7726-4e45-b7d3-81b3de128cfe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: HEB 9:5
Text: And over it the cherubims of glory shadowing the mercyseat; of which we cannot now speak particularly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:333db2d8-c1f4-4147-aecd-ade77e1d2904>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: HEB 9:6
Text: Now when these things were thus ordained, the priests went always into the first tabernacle, accomplishing the service of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:634fe74f-8ba5-4082-9fac-987fbcfd3904>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: HEB 9:7
Text: But into the second went the high priest alone once every year, not without blood, which he offered for himself, and for the errors of the people:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5fbd7d47-f7b9-4d0a-9372-b4e53d3f3a40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: HEB 9:8
Text: The Holy Ghost this signifying, that the way into the holiest of all was not yet made manifest, while as the first tabernacle was yet standing:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c192339e-3b02-4eb0-9312-471a38c00b0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: HEB 9:9
Text: Which was a figure for the time then present, in which were offered both gifts and sacrifices, that could not make him that did the service perfect, as pertaining to the conscience;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71372d9a-872e-4d95-acbf-1bc285de0d49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: HEB 9:10
Text: Which stood only in meats and drinks, and divers washings, and carnal ordinances, imposed on them until the time of reformation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ddccf46-b409-4fb1-865b-14203f33c546>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: HEB 9:11
Text: But Christ being come an high priest of good things to come, by a greater and more perfect tabernacle, not made with hands, that is to say, not of this building;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7949495-9281-4fd5-91f9-2a5182858c4a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: HEB 9:12
Text: Neither by the blood of goats and calves, but by his own blood he entered in once into the holy place, having obtained eternal redemption for us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:29dd134f-a84d-4d01-9c55-9d77dc2cb9d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: HEB 9:13
Text: For if the blood of bulls and of goats, and the ashes of an heifer sprinkling the unclean, sanctifieth to the purifying of the flesh:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f5516c2-8ab6-4c0b-b1a6-416981f200a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: HEB 9:14
Text: How much more shall the blood of Christ, who through the eternal Spirit offered himself without spot to God, purge your conscience from dead works to serve the living God?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:53fe8f18-d7f5-41fd-a9a7-21e86ad58f9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: HEB 9:15
Text: And for this cause he is the mediator of the new testament, that by means of death, for the redemption of the transgressions that were under the first testament, they which are called might receive the promise of eternal inheritance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f09465b-0dd4-4422-a256-386e3c3dfe94>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: HEB 9:16
Text: For where a testament is, there must also of necessity be the death of the testator.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d349b7ba-c7f3-43fc-863e-3d2013335b61>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: HEB 9:17
Text: For a testament is of force after men are dead: otherwise it is of no strength at all while the testator liveth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a5ab84b-b333-4d46-a0b5-05e5bf892d9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: HEB 9:18
Text: Whereupon neither the first testament was dedicated without blood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3de55bf4-acea-4e37-96e9-8fba9e9ed6e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: HEB 9:19
Text: For when Moses had spoken every precept to all the people according to the law, he took the blood of calves and of goats, with water, and scarlet wool, and hyssop, and sprinkled both the book, and all the people,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a5a89f7c-ddcd-47d9-8c15-3f3df35c8f17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: HEB 9:20
Text: Saying, This is the blood of the testament which God hath enjoined unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52333f8f-e49e-4bcf-a4c3-a5965c63f430>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: HEB 9:21
Text: Moreover he sprinkled with blood both the tabernacle, and all the vessels of the ministry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eab3f6f0-885f-4c53-a7af-bacecdf4d6b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: HEB 9:22
Text: And almost all things are by the law purged with blood; and without shedding of blood is no remission.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87e883ed-d1b4-4ea3-9542-a3f5a71225a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: HEB 9:23
Text: It was therefore necessary that the patterns of things in the heavens should be purified with these; but the heavenly things themselves with better sacrifices than these.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f584cab6-8038-4e20-b6af-4bcf81851372>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: HEB 9:24
Text: For Christ is not entered into the holy places made with hands, which are the figures of the true; but into heaven itself, now to appear in the presence of God for us:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd6a8f24-ec57-4b73-833b-682e9c5f9593>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: HEB 9:25
Text: Nor yet that he should offer himself often, as the high priest entereth into the holy place every year with blood of others;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ad815a7-1224-45df-9266-a2eaa60f0f77>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: HEB 9:26
Text: For then must he often have suffered since the foundation of the world: but now once in the end of the world hath he appeared to put away sin by the sacrifice of himself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:072de4a6-3a96-4d60-84d0-d718c0b923cf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: HEB 9:27
Text: And as it is appointed unto men once to die, but after this the judgment:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/9/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7fd55b8-eea3-48d7-9b71-a29b4c59bc25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: HEB 9:28
Text: So Christ was once offered to bear the sins of many; and unto them that look for him shall he appear the second time without sin unto salvation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:204189cf-6587-4248-872a-3e8f3e9887af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: HEB 10:1
Text: For the law having a shadow of good things to come, and not the very image of the things, can never with those sacrifices which they offered year by year continually make the comers thereunto perfect.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5013a25f-02cb-4fa9-8e7c-97566da07923>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: HEB 10:2
Text: For then would they not have ceased to be offered? because that the worshippers once purged should have had no more conscience of sins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0949df1-7416-4ede-8096-dfc51086f01c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: HEB 10:3
Text: But in those sacrifices there is a remembrance again made of sins every year.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51de0d3a-dce3-4932-9aa8-a7a09e687884>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: HEB 10:4
Text: For it is not possible that the blood of bulls and of goats should take away sins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e0ab1f1-e388-4722-8276-cd570e98716c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: HEB 10:5
Text: Wherefore when he cometh into the world, he saith, Sacrifice and offering thou wouldest not, but a body hast thou prepared me:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3ab8ab63-da40-4539-bd69-cb353373602c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: HEB 10:6
Text: In burnt offerings and sacrifices for sin thou hast had no pleasure.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b73fe78-af80-4734-a1a5-01f2089e0e66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: HEB 10:7
Text: Then said I, Lo, I come (in the volume of the book it is written of me,) to do thy will, O God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54bbe586-3c75-4e68-a2e9-49ffbf6dd380>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: HEB 10:8
Text: Above when he said, Sacrifice and offering and burnt offerings and offering for sin thou wouldest not, neither hadst pleasure therein; which are offered by the law;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:133977e0-e4e7-4144-b9ef-b4fee2d763da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: HEB 10:9
Text: Then said he, Lo, I come to do thy will, O God. He taketh away the first, that he may establish the second.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:298a881c-81ab-4b9b-80ac-f9bfa20ac24f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: HEB 10:10
Text: By the which will we are sanctified through the offering of the body of Jesus Christ once for all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d0a1a6a-c46b-4725-8d05-faaabd80f57a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: HEB 10:11
Text: And every priest standeth daily ministering and offering oftentimes the same sacrifices, which can never take away sins:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:82bfc599-0b20-478d-ad3b-94699c412e39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: HEB 10:12
Text: But this man, after he had offered one sacrifice for sins for ever, sat down on the right hand of God;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dcad1909-0844-4833-ade2-fa90d115731c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: HEB 10:13
Text: From henceforth expecting till his enemies be made his footstool.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:21d04511-1ede-4d81-9ac1-2aa90596845c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: HEB 10:14
Text: For by one offering he hath perfected for ever them that are sanctified.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52c42227-00d5-4f38-9177-9adedc072758>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: HEB 10:15
Text: Whereof the Holy Ghost also is a witness to us: for after that he had said before,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bbc81c6e-86aa-4a3a-8e23-f96f7830999a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: HEB 10:16
Text: This is the covenant that I will make with them after those days, saith the Lord, I will put my laws into their hearts, and in their minds will I write them;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:206c963e-5cc3-4cfe-9189-47a865126d75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 82

Reference: HEB 10:17
Text: And their sins and iniquities will I remember no more.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e367b52-bd66-4730-aa83-1d0b2444b9f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: HEB 10:18
Text: Now where remission of these is, there is no more offering for sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c941d2e1-cf03-4661-813e-96fb18390784>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: HEB 10:19
Text: Having therefore, brethren, boldness to enter into the holiest by the blood of Jesus,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5f493bc-f1ad-4089-8e93-619fa5b944fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: HEB 10:20
Text: By a new and living way, which he hath consecrated for us, through the veil, that is to say, his flesh;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b4b2bd7-0653-4eb0-beea-f5d7de61dbec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: HEB 10:21
Text: And having an high priest over the house of God;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:87eca4ef-102d-4587-8643-37eddfe84744>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: HEB 10:22
Text: Let us draw near with a true heart in full assurance of faith, having our hearts sprinkled from an evil conscience, and our bodies washed with pure water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:298bd048-dad8-4ad4-bfbb-e114db24f824>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: HEB 10:23
Text: Let us hold fast the profession of our faith without wavering; (for he is faithful that promised;)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fef5e8a2-2762-4020-832e-7c64426b24c0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: HEB 10:24
Text: And let us consider one another to provoke unto love and to good works:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:470b983f-8c4d-4616-854e-9d540fdbcdb2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: HEB 10:25
Text: Not forsaking the assembling of ourselves together, as the manner of some is; but exhorting one another: and so much the more, as ye see the day approaching.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9804238e-d6fb-4dc9-bbb3-af55ffe4e921>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: HEB 10:26
Text: For if we sin wilfully after that we have received the knowledge of the truth, there remaineth no more sacrifice for sins,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e21a919d-e98c-4985-80c8-98f952a4c220>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: HEB 10:27
Text: But a certain fearful looking for of judgment and fiery indignation, which shall devour the adversaries.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ce4e712-57a8-4d7e-badc-295497b29e48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: HEB 10:28
Text: He that despised Moses’ law died without mercy under two or three witnesses:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f8a5fd4-5941-4496-8404-3cb60c9c4b62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 279

Reference: HEB 10:29
Text: Of how much sorer punishment, suppose ye, shall he be thought worthy, who hath trodden under foot the Son of God, and hath counted the blood of the covenant, wherewith he was sanctified, an unholy thing, and hath done despite unto the Spirit of grace?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f0aa9fb-898e-4eb5-a8c3-e9d007a81783>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: HEB 10:30
Text: For we know him that hath said, Vengeance belongeth unto me, I will recompense, saith the Lord. And again, The Lord shall judge his people.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2070f901-e90b-406b-be08-1988efc58d6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: HEB 10:31
Text: It is a fearful thing to fall into the hands of the living God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0cc6df00-1576-4b21-aa2e-1f9d5d032b5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: HEB 10:32
Text: But call to remembrance the former days, in which, after ye were illuminated, ye endured a great fight of afflictions;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ccb469bf-6ae5-40dd-a205-1d3893efcb9b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: HEB 10:33
Text: Partly, whilst ye were made a gazingstock both by reproaches and afflictions; and partly, whilst ye became companions of them that were so used.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1c28e3fa-9bdd-4b6f-bd71-0327b8b92111>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: HEB 10:34
Text: For ye had compassion of me in my bonds, and took joyfully the spoiling of your goods, knowing in yourselves that ye have in heaven a better and an enduring substance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dde8d52e-d6e1-4583-baa4-53ac9b09917e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: HEB 10:35
Text: Cast not away therefore your confidence, which hath great recompence of reward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5cef70a7-642e-4691-a9ce-78bd9af51b62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: HEB 10:36
Text: For ye have need of patience, that, after ye have done the will of God, ye might receive the promise.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:963e9526-321c-46cf-9be4-6513c231271c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: HEB 10:37
Text: For yet a little while, and he that shall come will come, and will not tarry.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1b123c5-d13d-47d0-9e99-14feb66ca192>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: HEB 10:38
Text: Now the just shall live by faith: but if any man draw back, my soul shall have no pleasure in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/10/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e52231ad-8a1c-409f-a6e3-39a3b7e9fdc7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: HEB 10:39
Text: But we are not of them who draw back unto perdition; but of them that believe to the saving of the soul.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ee96335-449c-42de-a35a-7d8df07859d8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: HEB 11:1
Text: Now faith is the substance of things hoped for, the evidence of things not seen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f8bed00-9fd1-45e3-adb5-e1f48e4cfb05>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 71

Reference: HEB 11:2
Text: For by it the elders obtained a good report.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06baf321-1ecf-4612-aa10-35c51a8b1025>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: HEB 11:3
Text: Through faith we understand that the worlds were framed by the word of God, so that things which are seen were not made of things which do appear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7155b10-c244-4067-a193-98b36898d9ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: HEB 11:4
Text: By faith Abel offered unto God a more excellent sacrifice than Cain, by which he obtained witness that he was righteous, God testifying of his gifts: and by it he being dead yet speaketh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:207dea6b-7963-49c5-a4d7-4938816a69eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: HEB 11:5
Text: By faith Enoch was translated that he should not see death; and was not found, because God had translated him: for before his translation he had this testimony, that he pleased God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e53d9bd-3a04-43f1-8ea1-ff25bf79598f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: HEB 11:6
Text: But without faith it is impossible to please him: for he that cometh to God must believe that he is, and that he is a rewarder of them that diligently seek him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:775e87fb-616f-4d00-ba3a-ccc52ba6d875>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: HEB 11:7
Text: By faith Noah, being warned of God of things not seen as yet, moved with fear, prepared an ark to the saving of his house; by the which he condemned the world, and became heir of the righteousness which is by faith.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96a655e2-f25f-4d6d-baaa-68eca19d7ce3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: HEB 11:8
Text: By faith Abraham, when he was called to go out into a place which he should after receive for an inheritance, obeyed; and he went out, not knowing whither he went.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3bbac4d-3a0d-4d87-b6d3-8a40f2b642da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: HEB 11:9
Text: By faith he sojourned in the land of promise, as in a strange country, dwelling in tabernacles with Isaac and Jacob, the heirs with him of the same promise:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0ab6fbb-39e2-46dc-a915-a302df107f5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: HEB 11:10
Text: For he looked for a city which hath foundations, whose builder and maker is God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ea8a362-2126-430a-94d9-524e0b626703>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: HEB 11:11
Text: Through faith also Sara herself received strength to conceive seed, and was delivered of a child when she was past age, because she judged him faithful who had promised.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35645787-19c5-4e08-9ef0-237378300bcd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: HEB 11:12
Text: Therefore sprang there even of one, and him as good as dead, so many as the stars of the sky in multitude, and as the sand which is by the sea shore innumerable.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:762f8eb4-de06-4f5b-9976-43b1590baf5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: HEB 11:13
Text: These all died in faith, not having received the promises, but having seen them afar off, and were persuaded of them, and embraced them, and confessed that they were strangers and pilgrims on the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e1f4b41-d0ed-40bc-aefc-b2bace6c84f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: HEB 11:14
Text: For they that say such things declare plainly that they seek a country.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fe5f2066-9065-4b2d-9ceb-93268a4d3d5d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: HEB 11:15
Text: And truly, if they had been mindful of that country from whence they came out, they might have had opportunity to have returned.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0fac507b-edcb-4a9a-a3b6-118c136354b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: HEB 11:16
Text: But now they desire a better country, that is, an heavenly: wherefore God is not ashamed to be called their God: for he hath prepared for them a city.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e9fc7e2-597c-423a-abe6-8ece85b96e7c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: HEB 11:17
Text: By faith Abraham, when he was tried, offered up Isaac: and he that had received the promises offered up his only begotten son,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5a45566d-a3c9-4980-90a1-7e2fd6a51e4b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: HEB 11:18
Text: Of whom it was said, That in Isaac shall thy seed be called:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:060392fe-19a0-4adf-b08c-94bf42245bf8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: HEB 11:19
Text: Accounting that God was able to raise him up, even from the dead; from whence also he received him in a figure.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8efdc6f8-8ab8-4285-99a8-3ce351b555b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: HEB 11:20
Text: By faith Isaac blessed Jacob and Esau concerning things to come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bc56be2-01b5-4b92-ba37-3d2783920ab9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: HEB 11:21
Text: By faith Jacob, when he was a dying, blessed both the sons of Joseph; and worshipped, leaning upon the top of his staff.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5927ba75-8c04-4136-95cc-a35d3e714c75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: HEB 11:22
Text: By faith Joseph, when he died, made mention of the departing of the children of Israel; and gave commandment concerning his bones.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8241046-8d2f-4919-8fd2-655b3c9c32e6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: HEB 11:23
Text: By faith Moses, when he was born, was hid three months of his parents, because they saw he was a proper child; and they were not afraid of the king’s commandment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c45fc11-2f08-43b0-810a-6ec028093e03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: HEB 11:24
Text: By faith Moses, when he was come to years, refused to be called the son of Pharaoh’s daughter;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f6bd870-978a-4785-9fdb-648baef50b5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: HEB 11:25
Text: Choosing rather to suffer affliction with the people of God, than to enjoy the pleasures of sin for a season;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cef092dd-d3d2-4f13-bee7-f60ceaad605a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: HEB 11:26
Text: Esteeming the reproach of Christ greater riches than the treasures in Egypt: for he had respect unto the recompence of the reward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9bc0b807-bb51-49ab-9f6a-b28abeb1e11b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: HEB 11:27
Text: By faith he forsook Egypt, not fearing the wrath of the king: for he endured, as seeing him who is invisible.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52e583b5-5e59-42a3-ae99-ade225419778>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: HEB 11:28
Text: Through faith he kept the passover, and the sprinkling of blood, lest he that destroyed the firstborn should touch them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e870e62e-fa17-42b6-acef-e9b282dd496c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: HEB 11:29
Text: By faith they passed through the Red sea as by dry land: which the Egyptians assaying to do were drowned.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/30
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e47a298-d749-45b1-a3aa-8ca12ce6a625>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: HEB 11:30
Text: By faith the walls of Jericho fell down, after they were compassed about seven days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/31
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e2274a60-5e11-4e33-af9d-0184bfe1ea69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: HEB 11:31
Text: By faith the harlot Rahab perished not with them that believed not, when she had received the spies with peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/32
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a1298379-5890-49af-ba48-b311910b8f39>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: HEB 11:32
Text: And what shall I more say? for the time would fail me to tell of Gedeon, and of Barak, and of Samson, and of Jephthae; of David also, and Samuel, and of the prophets:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/33
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5331de8-031b-4f4c-a05d-5a8b01e59b79>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: HEB 11:33
Text: Who through faith subdued kingdoms, wrought righteousness, obtained promises, stopped the mouths of lions.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/34
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26d63786-c99e-483f-9c74-4f1a3c345114>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: HEB 11:34
Text: Quenched the violence of fire, escaped the edge of the sword, out of weakness were made strong, waxed valiant in fight, turned to flight the armies of the aliens.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/35
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7636adcf-9d43-432e-83f0-27cd94faf0eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: HEB 11:35
Text: Women received their dead raised to life again: and others were tortured, not accepting deliverance; that they might obtain a better resurrection:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/36
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf2a154d-cb98-4978-bc6e-1b1ad13520ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: HEB 11:36
Text: And others had trial of cruel mockings and scourgings, yea, moreover of bonds and imprisonment:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/37
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35496370-2ec3-42c1-a6a9-ea6676041fa7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: HEB 11:37
Text: They were stoned, they were sawn asunder, were tempted, were slain with the sword: they wandered about in sheepskins and goatskins; being destitute, afflicted, tormented;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/38
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81a4406e-ef8c-42a9-81f7-5f2e635b734b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: HEB 11:38
Text: (Of whom the world was not worthy:) they wandered in deserts, and in mountains, and in dens and caves of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/39
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64cea9ef-38f8-4ff5-84ab-a4a474d1cb0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: HEB 11:39
Text: And these all, having obtained a good report through faith, received not the promise:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/11/40
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0a47ca3-8488-40e6-ad7e-4ba779e469bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: HEB 11:40
Text: God having provided some better thing for us, that they without us should not be made perfect.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e44bcc8f-3bca-41a0-9f62-5ef9a512a342>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: HEB 12:1
Text: Wherefore seeing we also are compassed about with so great a cloud of witnesses, let us lay aside every weight, and the sin which doth so easily beset us, and let us run with patience the race that is set before us,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:195a503b-3e0d-4892-bffe-366955bcf092>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: HEB 12:2
Text: Looking unto Jesus the author and finisher of our faith; who for the joy that was set before him endured the cross, despising the shame, and is set down at the right hand of the throne of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54cf14f4-109b-479c-8f02-06dc44cdab8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: HEB 12:3
Text: For consider him that endured such contradiction of sinners against himself, lest ye be wearied and faint in your minds.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e340c174-4880-415c-9de5-6005295ea6e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: HEB 12:4
Text: Ye have not yet resisted unto blood, striving against sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37c339e9-7480-4b47-b7ef-30148b97ca0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: HEB 12:5
Text: And ye have forgotten the exhortation which speaketh unto you as unto children, My son, despise not thou the chastening of the Lord, nor faint when thou art rebuked of him:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81494131-fd8a-44e9-a7fd-587adbd62c5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: HEB 12:6
Text: For whom the Lord loveth he chasteneth, and scourgeth every son whom he receiveth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:871781b4-486a-4a0c-9fa1-776be7d6ef28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: HEB 12:7
Text: If ye endure chastening, God dealeth with you as with sons; for what son is he whom the father chasteneth not?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54a29b43-8501-4cdf-8b81-e475dbf0669c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: HEB 12:8
Text: But if ye be without chastisement, whereof all are partakers, then are ye bastards, and not sons.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a0fbea0-869e-49ff-b3f0-975ede5a2707>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: HEB 12:9
Text: Furthermore we have had fathers of our flesh which corrected us, and we gave them reverence: shall we not much rather be in subjection unto the Father of spirits, and live?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e96ece7c-6169-43f4-9467-afa5c5156976>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: HEB 12:10
Text: For they verily for a few days chastened us after their own pleasure; but he for our profit, that we might be partakers of his holiness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b2a0488-b3e4-4d8b-858f-7eb20ad01c8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: HEB 12:11
Text: Now no chastening for the present seemeth to be joyous, but grievous: nevertheless afterward it yieldeth the peaceable fruit of righteousness unto them which are exercised thereby.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:777c0c19-c239-4f8b-a82e-6c36d80996ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: HEB 12:12
Text: Wherefore lift up the hands which hang down, and the feeble knees;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:819b946c-4dae-4b97-bdd2-83a1b370ca3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: HEB 12:13
Text: And make straight paths for your feet, lest that which is lame be turned out of the way; but let it rather be healed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:311d69fd-d10e-4d65-9f62-108208c19c2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: HEB 12:14
Text: Follow peace with all men, and holiness, without which no man shall see the Lord:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e30e6388-d266-4a1b-9ee8-1454472b2d24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: HEB 12:15
Text: Looking diligently lest any man fail of the grace of God; lest any root of bitterness springing up trouble you, and thereby many be defiled;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
