Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: HEB 12:16
Text: Lest there be any fornicator, or profane person, as Esau, who for one morsel of meat sold his birthright.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13d4ab3b-33d5-4e98-b1f6-f764cd60dec2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: HEB 12:17
Text: For ye know how that afterward, when he would have inherited the blessing, he was rejected: for he found no place of repentance, though he sought it carefully with tears.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d35fa2f0-59bc-485b-a07b-487b1e2b90fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: HEB 12:18
Text: For ye are not come unto the mount that might be touched, and that burned with fire, nor unto blackness, and darkness, and tempest,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52b7d810-7c12-4ac2-9628-950a5b2b4dbc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: HEB 12:19
Text: And the sound of a trumpet, and the voice of words; which voice they that heard intreated that the word should not be spoken to them any more:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3df1d3ec-4104-4c0f-b4ef-acdf0e4e7453>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: HEB 12:20
Text: (For they could not endure that which was commanded, And if so much as a beast touch the mountain, it shall be stoned, or thrust through with a dart:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6b2775de-269e-42e8-bdad-750d0b6cf24f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: HEB 12:21
Text: And so terrible was the sight, that Moses said, I exceedingly fear and quake:)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9cdaf3f4-4044-4fff-9b86-b12e16522af3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: HEB 12:22
Text: But ye are come unto mount Sion, and unto the city of the living God, the heavenly Jerusalem, and to an innumerable company of angels,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f48f3cea-0385-4845-b294-da50c8db96be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: HEB 12:23
Text: To the general assembly and church of the firstborn, which are written in heaven, and to God the Judge of all, and to the spirits of just men made perfect,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9a6a568-13d3-45c1-aa51-5b44a0321eef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: HEB 12:24
Text: And to Jesus the mediator of the new covenant, and to the blood of sprinkling, that speaketh better things than that of Abel.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d97b8dff-72c2-4197-8f0f-aa0845c13742>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: HEB 12:25
Text: See that ye refuse not him that speaketh. For if they escaped not who refused him that spake on earth, much more shall not we escape, if we turn away from him that speaketh from heaven:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1605b445-aad0-4c32-95e6-ed9f9e0b29a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: HEB 12:26
Text: Whose voice then shook the earth: but now he hath promised, saying, Yet once more I shake not the earth only, but also heaven.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3af82b4e-9cb1-4550-9e57-de522349db23>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: HEB 12:27
Text: And this word, Yet once more, signifieth the removing of those things that are shaken, as of things that are made, that those things which cannot be shaken may remain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3818be01-0e47-4fe5-aa13-55c06d96690a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: HEB 12:28
Text: Wherefore we receiving a kingdom which cannot be moved, let us have grace, whereby we may serve God acceptably with reverence and godly fear:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/12/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb95f4cd-48f1-4bdb-bdb7-36d2c67efedc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 60

Reference: HEB 12:29
Text: For our God is a consuming fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf8673b6-e30b-41b5-a345-4e725707d915>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 55

Reference: HEB 13:1
Text: Let brotherly love continue.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:951c04b6-4a4e-4706-8b68-f7639ccfe06c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: HEB 13:2
Text: Be not forgetful to entertain strangers: for thereby some have entertained angels unawares.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37408179-a03b-4964-8a11-729afb95d031>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: HEB 13:3
Text: Remember them that are in bonds, as bound with them; and them which suffer adversity, as being yourselves also in the body.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:405d9570-035f-428f-a9f3-b653c9294a6d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: HEB 13:4
Text: Marriage is honourable in all, and the bed undefiled: but whoremongers and adulterers God will judge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b74c661-c1ad-4d29-ab41-d941f344a73b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: HEB 13:5
Text: Let your conversation be without covetousness; and be content with such things as ye have: for he hath said, I will never leave thee, nor forsake thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73b423f8-0042-4469-b956-b68e8ba92d29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: HEB 13:6
Text: So that we may boldly say, The Lord is my helper, and I will not fear what man shall do unto me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bb0c21db-8e4d-4390-a155-ee1a99b7ebb6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: HEB 13:7
Text: Remember them which have the rule over you, who have spoken unto you the word of God: whose faith follow, considering the end of their conversation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd8a7712-f345-4137-a3be-270b7722fe08>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: HEB 13:8
Text: Jesus Christ the same yesterday, and to day, and for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed7e0775-2b41-4f37-b104-034befaab963>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: HEB 13:9
Text: Be not carried about with divers and strange doctrines. For it is a good thing that the heart be established with grace; not with meats, which have not profited them that have been occupied therein.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07d0078d-4ade-4a97-91c2-9f236dddf1f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: HEB 13:10
Text: We have an altar, whereof they have no right to eat which serve the tabernacle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e18491c3-32e7-492d-a0fa-1600aa728f15>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: HEB 13:11
Text: For the bodies of those beasts, whose blood is brought into the sanctuary by the high priest for sin, are burned without the camp.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:667d06c7-af8b-4c50-a527-e9498c920b5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: HEB 13:12
Text: Wherefore Jesus also, that he might sanctify the people with his own blood, suffered without the gate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5a1af94-1c56-4066-babd-d8678526e931>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: HEB 13:13
Text: Let us go forth therefore unto him without the camp, bearing his reproach.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75074ce0-6e02-47ac-8d25-f2791363b1b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: HEB 13:14
Text: For here have we no continuing city, but we seek one to come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91029f6f-41c8-44ee-9f86-1a5bcef0c5a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: HEB 13:15
Text: By him therefore let us offer the sacrifice of praise to God continually, that is, the fruit of our lips giving thanks to his name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ceb3c74-2116-47e2-8697-d23b9ec4e0dd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: HEB 13:16
Text: But to do good and to communicate forget not: for with such sacrifices God is well pleased.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1e335587-8188-4fd0-84ab-902d34665a1d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: HEB 13:17
Text: Obey them that have the rule over you, and submit yourselves: for they watch for your souls, as they that must give account, that they may do it with joy, and not with grief: for that is unprofitable for you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:409390fc-7629-44bf-89df-07d897efdfa4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: HEB 13:18
Text: Pray for us: for we trust we have a good conscience, in all things willing to live honestly.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:abc4f181-21cd-4035-9e70-69edc6d4b7cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: HEB 13:19
Text: But I beseech you the rather to do this, that I may be restored to you the sooner.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f198a0a6-9fd9-4d05-89fe-97817aca6658>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: HEB 13:20
Text: Now the God of peace, that brought again from the dead our Lord Jesus, that great shepherd of the sheep, through the blood of the everlasting covenant,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e9047bd1-ab0d-48ed-ba6b-8e647441a2a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: HEB 13:21
Text: Make you perfect in every good work to do his will, working in you that which is wellpleasing in his sight, through Jesus Christ; to whom be glory for ever and ever. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:95e7e95c-3f14-4653-bbf9-1c4b13409536>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: HEB 13:22
Text: And I beseech you, brethren, suffer the word of exhortation: for I have written a letter unto you in few words.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05bb0430-d5eb-49b4-b64c-90438c3b6829>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: HEB 13:23
Text: Know ye that our brother Timothy is set at liberty; with whom, if he come shortly, I will see you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db71ab4c-e5bf-414f-8b60-ffe061fad699>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: HEB 13:24
Text: Salute all them that have the rule over you, and all the saints. They of Italy salute you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/HEB/13/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c7ba316-18e6-4423-8cca-eaf45885112e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 56

Reference: HEB 13:25
Text: Grace be with you all. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:98dceb55-e153-4490-9592-4903990a9eae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: JAS 1:1
Text: James, a servant of God and of the Lord Jesus Christ, to the twelve tribes which are scattered abroad, greeting.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f555615-7fc6-4815-9b7e-78ec1f4fcc72>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 93

Reference: JAS 1:2
Text: My brethren, count it all joy when ye fall into divers temptations;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dec9574d-fb4f-46a9-bd26-4e53903e1624>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: JAS 1:3
Text: Knowing this, that the trying of your faith worketh patience.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ed42d423-8f55-49ea-a44f-0aade802983b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: JAS 1:4
Text: But let patience have her perfect work, that ye may be perfect and entire, wanting nothing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca868f2a-9d7c-45a3-8c0c-54fb26ffd2f2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: JAS 1:5
Text: If any of you lack wisdom, let him ask of God, that giveth to all men liberally, and upbraideth not; and it shall be given him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89139d4d-8743-4364-ad61-ffeeb35851ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: JAS 1:6
Text: But let him ask in faith, nothing wavering. For he that wavereth is like a wave of the sea driven with the wind and tossed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:01a3d87d-56a9-4090-a2a5-5b19a87f7ae2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: JAS 1:7
Text: For let not that man think that he shall receive any thing of the Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6ade5f7-43bf-49fd-91a7-99e78fd73c13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: JAS 1:8
Text: A double minded man is unstable in all his ways.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09e6a2b8-3ecf-45f5-a4be-856033279140>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 86

Reference: JAS 1:9
Text: Let the brother of low degree rejoice in that he is exalted:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb37f934-fe30-400f-9103-7a87f4a10aa5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: JAS 1:10
Text: But the rich, in that he is made low: because as the flower of the grass he shall pass away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92af32c1-8616-48ba-ad8a-0a174f4b547d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: JAS 1:11
Text: For the sun is no sooner risen with a burning heat, but it withereth the grass, and the flower thereof falleth, and the grace of the fashion of it perisheth: so also shall the rich man fade away in his ways.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e4bd90d9-2459-44c7-b970-e3896a6731aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: JAS 1:12
Text: Blessed is the man that endureth temptation: for when he is tried, he shall receive the crown of life, which the Lord hath promised to them that love him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d72f573-351b-4848-8e94-4d81d73d1cb9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: JAS 1:13
Text: Let no man say when he is tempted, I am tempted of God: for God cannot be tempted with evil, neither tempteth he any man:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7f7e1436-49e6-451e-a239-c1e459030230>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: JAS 1:14
Text: But every man is tempted, when he is drawn away of his own lust, and enticed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eccde527-00c5-4a3c-aefe-6524e7510190>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: JAS 1:15
Text: Then when lust hath conceived, it bringeth forth sin: and sin, when it is finished, bringeth forth death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb6747a6-243b-4e50-b24d-5929f199743e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 59

Reference: JAS 1:16
Text: Do not err, my beloved brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8aa3e79b-3efd-4072-8026-5d84e07f34ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: JAS 1:17
Text: Every good gift and every perfect gift is from above, and cometh down from the Father of lights, with whom is no variableness, neither shadow of turning.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22be2b89-629c-409d-9b0d-b53cb57ad96c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: JAS 1:18
Text: Of his own will begat he us with the word of truth, that we should be a kind of firstfruits of his creatures.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c77842f-113a-4656-90c0-d0d293bd8a7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: JAS 1:19
Text: Wherefore, my beloved brethren, let every man be swift to hear, slow to speak, slow to wrath:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:99bfa2e1-06f1-43a9-bbe2-550cc4f89a3d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: JAS 1:20
Text: For the wrath of man worketh not the righteousness of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0a1673a1-9c36-43fc-b753-a941a63d4a78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: JAS 1:21
Text: Wherefore lay apart all filthiness and superfluity of naughtiness, and receive with meekness the engrafted word, which is able to save your souls.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97476652-c8b4-4b22-982a-4c047d7dcb68>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: JAS 1:22
Text: But be ye doers of the word, and not hearers only, deceiving your own selves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4ed61eda-064c-4b1c-9abe-524258091eb6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: JAS 1:23
Text: For if any be a hearer of the word, and not a doer, he is like unto a man beholding his natural face in a glass:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d2d203c-99c4-41bb-b097-2445a8080883>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: JAS 1:24
Text: For he beholdeth himself, and goeth his way, and straightway forgetteth what manner of man he was.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f69f5de-6db4-4d3d-8e72-820387189def>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: JAS 1:25
Text: But whoso looketh into the perfect law of liberty, and continueth therein, he being not a forgetful hearer, but a doer of the work, this man shall be blessed in his deed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60e6eaa9-ebfe-4a95-aa05-905114b4a611>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: JAS 1:26
Text: If any man among you seem to be religious, and bridleth not his tongue, but deceiveth his own heart, this man’s religion is vain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/1/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3afba5b7-5d54-4866-98dc-ae3fa60eb427>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: JAS 1:27
Text: Pure religion and undefiled before God and the Father is this, To visit the fatherless and widows in their affliction, and to keep himself unspotted from the world.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f952a80-4f52-4dfa-b93c-b9ba2531971b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: JAS 2:1
Text: My brethren, have not the faith of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Lord of glory, with respect of persons.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a83f434-1bf3-47b5-9cc8-3a065932e531>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: JAS 2:2
Text: For if there come unto your assembly a man with a gold ring, in goodly apparel, and there come in also a poor man in vile raiment;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c7c8571-c7ea-42dd-a56a-21f910090660>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 203

Reference: JAS 2:3
Text: And ye have respect to him that weareth the gay clothing, and say unto him, Sit thou here in a good place; and say to the poor, Stand thou there, or sit here under my footstool:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:990c0b2a-9c36-4946-9574-b9e5ad22149b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: JAS 2:4
Text: Are ye not then partial in yourselves, and are become judges of evil thoughts?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7346daf2-f5c0-4455-9446-9120c5198ada>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: JAS 2:5
Text: Hearken, my beloved brethren, Hath not God chosen the poor of this world rich in faith, and heirs of the kingdom which he hath promised to them that love him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:097396fd-ca23-4e83-9edf-ad0b16099403>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: JAS 2:6
Text: But ye have despised the poor. Do not rich men oppress you, and draw you before the judgment seats?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c02c58bd-825e-4ff8-bd61-5df539177ab1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: JAS 2:7
Text: Do not they blaspheme that worthy name by the which ye are called?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eb65da3a-4fd4-4c8c-8ba9-adf58fd95d9f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: JAS 2:8
Text: If ye fulfil the royal law according to the scripture, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself, ye do well:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:212ad75e-8b4b-4dd8-ae1d-65b6ef883373>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: JAS 2:9
Text: But if ye have respect to persons, ye commit sin, and are convinced of the law as transgressors.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8de89463-81be-4916-875e-23d3957577b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: JAS 2:10
Text: For whosoever shall keep the whole law, and yet offend in one point, he is guilty of all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e122444e-15f4-4618-ab19-009390c8d5e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: JAS 2:11
Text: For he that said, Do not commit adultery, said also, Do not kill. Now if thou commit no adultery, yet if thou kill, thou art become a transgressor of the law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d06a97f-dac8-41a7-936b-7a876c311adc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: JAS 2:12
Text: So speak ye, and so do, as they that shall be judged by the law of liberty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5c21d2b5-bc70-4f27-82e1-c87ccbd0d3e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: JAS 2:13
Text: For he shall have judgment without mercy, that hath shewed no mercy; and mercy rejoiceth against judgment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a9e5687-9a25-4d5b-b58a-fca017f889ab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: JAS 2:14
Text: What doth it profit, my brethren, though a man say he hath faith, and have not works? can faith save him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df99861d-df67-44dd-bdb3-2be393af62f6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: JAS 2:15
Text: If a brother or sister be naked, and destitute of daily food,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:edbd9e29-2052-4837-8062-a9122cb72f2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: JAS 2:16
Text: And one of you say unto them, Depart in peace, be ye warmed and filled; notwithstanding ye give them not those things which are needful to the body; what doth it profit?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:131147f6-7586-44af-b28b-0c57d7780da7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: JAS 2:17
Text: Even so faith, if it hath not works, is dead, being alone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fd58a09-11a9-4b02-878e-b3290f7bff50>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: JAS 2:18
Text: Yea, a man may say, Thou hast faith, and I have works: shew me thy faith without thy works, and I will shew thee my faith by my works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3854798-fb77-47e4-8be4-7fce8ea50a7a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: JAS 2:19
Text: Thou believest that there is one God; thou doest well: the devils also believe, and tremble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96ca606b-af63-4b4f-a7e7-f3e538968ecd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: JAS 2:20
Text: But wilt thou know, O vain man, that faith without works is dead?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b8f52b8-c1d3-4e4c-814a-bf514c247107>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: JAS 2:21
Text: Was not Abraham our father justified by works, when he had offered Isaac his son upon the altar?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d764f7c5-1c30-419b-b3bd-88441aa47aae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: JAS 2:22
Text: Seest thou how faith wrought with his works, and by works was faith made perfect?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d62d097-a265-4cda-ba86-bccedac9f51e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: JAS 2:23
Text: And the scripture was fulfilled which saith, Abraham believed God, and it was imputed unto him for righteousness: and he was called the Friend of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c76a6db-066e-4d8f-9f54-0d68348cfd30>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: JAS 2:24
Text: Ye see then how that by works a man is justified, and not by faith only.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0369092-aa91-4609-ad32-3d7f88c7b723>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: JAS 2:25
Text: Likewise also was not Rahab the harlot justified by works, when she had received the messengers, and had sent them out another way?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/2/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:60b9a5b5-5750-43c2-aa85-c860d13ed230>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: JAS 2:26
Text: For as the body without the spirit is dead, so faith without works is dead also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:705bdcb8-3f1c-4f81-9880-904494b70665>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: JAS 3:1
Text: My brethren, be not many masters, knowing that we shall receive the greater condemnation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e907e53-e623-43e1-bf6d-1e138da4dc0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: JAS 3:2
Text: For in many things we offend all. If any man offend not in word, the same is a perfect man, and able also to bridle the whole body.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a4980152-98ee-41a5-8c41-dfbf6cecf188>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: JAS 3:3
Text: Behold, we put bits in the horses’ mouths, that they may obey us; and we turn about their whole body.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d503c8e9-c3e4-4c45-b4ae-9ce13ea62754>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: JAS 3:4
Text: Behold also the ships, which though they be so great, and are driven of fierce winds, yet are they turned about with a very small helm, whithersoever the governor listeth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7a9b7cf-1990-45cd-945e-d2076b17d04d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: JAS 3:5
Text: Even so the tongue is a little member, and boasteth great things. Behold, how great a matter a little fire kindleth!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:169357d8-c2f8-4083-8646-59e9a3363908>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: JAS 3:6
Text: And the tongue is a fire, a world of iniquity: so is the tongue among our members, that it defileth the whole body, and setteth on fire the course of nature; and it is set on fire of hell.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:36d2519d-96b2-4bb8-8012-9de26fcc1a98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: JAS 3:7
Text: For every kind of beasts, and of birds, and of serpents, and of things in the sea, is tamed, and hath been tamed of mankind:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e47970d-61cf-49ce-96bd-82132e00c63e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: JAS 3:8
Text: But the tongue can no man tame; it is an unruly evil, full of deadly poison.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bdcda3e8-aafd-4c8c-9206-9fab9eb07ec2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: JAS 3:9
Text: Therewith bless we God, even the Father; and therewith curse we men, which are made after the similitude of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eca756c6-d058-470a-8848-a082c7131bf9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: JAS 3:10
Text: Out of the same mouth proceedeth blessing and cursing. My brethren, these things ought not so to be.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f66ffb8b-adc3-4b83-8831-74fafbdb5c0b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: JAS 3:11
Text: Doth a fountain send forth at the same place sweet water and bitter?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:192d37b3-97ea-4144-b2cd-7035ac4872d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: JAS 3:12
Text: Can the fig tree, my brethren, bear olive berries? either a vine, figs? so can no fountain both yield salt water and fresh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a4a6a04-69af-487d-ab01-216af41a34c7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: JAS 3:13
Text: Who is a wise man and endued with knowledge among you? let him shew out of a good conversation his works with meekness of wisdom.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1eff7066-8367-4584-b5df-f718853579e0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: JAS 3:14
Text: But if ye have bitter envying and strife in your hearts, glory not, and lie not against the truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d27753df-335a-4169-ac16-6b1d691d6329>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: JAS 3:15
Text: This wisdom descendeth not from above, but is earthly, sensual, devilish.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9967a6e7-46ff-4ebc-98d9-c603ef1fd0d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: JAS 3:16
Text: For where envying and strife is, there is confusion and every evil work.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba10b4c2-3365-4c38-bd92-e481cbbbaca3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 199

Reference: JAS 3:17
Text: But the wisdom that is from above is first pure, then peaceable, gentle, and easy to be intreated, full of mercy and good fruits, without partiality, and without hypocrisy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03484963-e492-4438-9093-a9900cc68e00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: JAS 3:18
Text: And the fruit of righteousness is sown in peace of them that make peace.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3dc7433-6166-408f-9461-e83f3ee232bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: JAS 4:1
Text: From whence come wars and fightings among you? come they not hence, even of your lusts that war in your members?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba795182-8996-42db-b3a4-653cefeeb8ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: JAS 4:2
Text: Ye lust, and have not: ye kill, and desire to have, and cannot obtain: ye fight and war, yet ye have not, because ye ask not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bff23ebb-e9c1-45e3-a740-a9be46bbddcd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: JAS 4:3
Text: Ye ask, and receive not, because ye ask amiss, that ye may consume it upon your lusts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4461765b-e6e1-4f1a-8c74-bc9d963ccf55>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: JAS 4:4
Text: Ye adulterers and adulteresses, know ye not that the friendship of the world is enmity with God? whosoever therefore will be a friend of the world is the enemy of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67426f79-b1d5-4bce-aac1-ac17fbbe5f24>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: JAS 4:5
Text: Do ye think that the scripture saith in vain, The spirit that dwelleth in us lusteth to envy?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a28aa7b1-fd6e-451b-b73b-cbd621ca7539>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: JAS 4:6
Text: But he giveth more grace. Wherefore he saith, God resisteth the proud, but giveth grace unto the humble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea3609f3-93ed-4465-8c2e-a9985a3d8789>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: JAS 4:7
Text: Submit yourselves therefore to God. Resist the devil, and he will flee from you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7db3bfb1-5153-4726-b2bd-1de0d0b4956b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: JAS 4:8
Text: Draw nigh to God, and he will draw nigh to you. Cleanse your hands, ye sinners; and purify your hearts, ye double minded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5066add1-36b8-4f1a-bd7f-1f8f4e42decf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: JAS 4:9
Text: Be afflicted, and mourn, and weep: let your laughter be turned to mourning, and your joy to heaviness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51373b25-9cdf-4347-97ee-16904ef1c0b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: JAS 4:10
Text: Humble yourselves in the sight of the Lord, and he shall lift you up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b652a88d-bc65-4109-97de-a231dc0c6e0c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: JAS 4:11
Text: Speak not evil one of another, brethren. He that speaketh evil of his brother, and judgeth his brother, speaketh evil of the law, and judgeth the law: but if thou judge the law, thou art not a doer of the law, but a judge.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f66d3964-4228-4914-92f1-08fa89d82fcd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: JAS 4:12
Text: There is one lawgiver, who is able to save and to destroy: who art thou that judgest another?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a15e414-d9f7-42c6-8e3d-7e572ee2b052>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: JAS 4:13
Text: Go to now, ye that say, To day or to morrow we will go into such a city, and continue there a year, and buy and sell, and get gain:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:369bb60d-133d-4505-bf69-8aae9d69fd62>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: JAS 4:14
Text: Whereas ye know not what shall be on the morrow. For what is your life? It is even a vapour, that appeareth for a little time, and then vanisheth away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1fb7b1ac-8afc-4d41-a4fd-423285fd5b8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: JAS 4:15
Text: For that ye ought to say, If the Lord will, we shall live, and do this, or that.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8f96d19-15f8-40ef-80b8-81c025b1af6d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: JAS 4:16
Text: But now ye rejoice in your boastings: all such rejoicing is evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13d4f918-2493-4c9e-868b-9e37f25f5d93>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: JAS 4:17
Text: Therefore to him that knoweth to do good, and doeth it not, to him it is sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c44ecc4-fc2d-4197-a398-2c6847cb46e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: JAS 5:1
Text: Go to now, ye rich men, weep and howl for your miseries that shall come upon you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b5772a9-d016-4337-b8e5-377b5dd43a09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 85

Reference: JAS 5:2
Text: Your riches are corrupted, and your garments are motheaten.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75d2c1b0-df3b-4120-996f-caf7a063e519>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: JAS 5:3
Text: Your gold and silver is cankered; and the rust of them shall be a witness against you, and shall eat your flesh as it were fire. Ye have heaped treasure together for the last days.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e1c55924-ab23-4ec2-9526-5c276599f4b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 227

Reference: JAS 5:4
Text: Behold, the hire of the labourers who have reaped down your fields, which is of you kept back by fraud, crieth: and the cries of them which have reaped are entered into the ears of the Lord of sabaoth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fae61609-9589-447f-9161-26e997acd4ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: JAS 5:5
Text: Ye have lived in pleasure on the earth, and been wanton; ye have nourished your hearts, as in a day of slaughter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70662a70-a6ff-4712-b174-36c5b92e58d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: JAS 5:6
Text: Ye have condemned and killed the just; and he doth not resist you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16b73a07-4f53-4e90-b114-2e38e3c0e79a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: JAS 5:7
Text: Be patient therefore, brethren, unto the coming of the Lord. Behold, the husbandman waiteth for the precious fruit of the earth, and hath long patience for it, until he receive the early and latter rain.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48f4a466-d7fc-48b4-aa74-95702df9746c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: JAS 5:8
Text: Be ye also patient; stablish your hearts: for the coming of the Lord draweth nigh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d194f825-ef3c-4ddd-befa-c43a50a928d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: JAS 5:9
Text: Grudge not one against another, brethren, lest ye be condemned: behold, the judge standeth before the door.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8caba45-8d3d-4c95-89ad-5ffb0bfaefdc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: JAS 5:10
Text: Take, my brethren, the prophets, who have spoken in the name of the Lord, for an example of suffering affliction, and of patience.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e0147af-6832-4840-9514-648e32a47c56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: JAS 5:11
Text: Behold, we count them happy which endure. Ye have heard of the patience of Job, and have seen the end of the Lord; that the Lord is very pitiful, and of tender mercy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d4110070-0d1e-4b09-a3c5-2fef2c2b2ace>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: JAS 5:12
Text: But above all things, my brethren, swear not, neither by heaven, neither by the earth, neither by any other oath: but let your yea be yea; and your nay, nay; lest ye fall into condemnation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc92ddb9-6d50-4d31-92d7-0b91a10cd6c3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: JAS 5:13
Text: Is any among you afflicted? let him pray. Is any merry? let him sing psalms.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86bc365c-6745-4882-932f-65160f62e2e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: JAS 5:14
Text: Is any sick among you? let him call for the elders of the church; and let them pray over him, anointing him with oil in the name of the Lord:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18b89028-cf36-43ff-8604-cd93118b9bd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: JAS 5:15
Text: And the prayer of faith shall save the sick, and the Lord shall raise him up; and if he have committed sins, they shall be forgiven him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c5da94a-18db-4e72-b766-9b3623441cab>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: JAS 5:16
Text: Confess your faults one to another, and pray one for another, that ye may be healed. The effectual fervent prayer of a righteous man availeth much.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/5/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:70089a86-c2e3-4521-89d3-71081e6afbd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: JAS 5:17
Text: Elias was a man subject to like passions as we are, and he prayed earnestly that it might not rain: and it rained not on the earth by the space of three years and six months.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/5/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff75e31e-9074-4bdd-b219-563197a2a2be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: JAS 5:18
Text: And he prayed again, and the heaven gave rain, and the earth brought forth her fruit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/5/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3de07b50-6f9d-419c-bb08-661e97c5b742>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: JAS 5:19
Text: Brethren, if any of you do err from the truth, and one convert him;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JAS/5/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91d65a06-0853-4841-8378-cb4bf51a1c0e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: JAS 5:20
Text: Let him know, that he which converteth the sinner from the error of his way shall save a soul from death, and shall hide a multitude of sins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3402f06b-2e64-429f-89e9-10bf00623c0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 1PE 1:1
Text: Peter, an apostle of Jesus Christ, to the strangers scattered throughout Pontus, Galatia, Cappadocia, Asia, and Bithynia,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d615ca6f-b625-4755-ae67-c0b18821f6d4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: 1PE 1:2
Text: Elect according to the foreknowledge of God the Father, through sanctification of the Spirit, unto obedience and sprinkling of the blood of Jesus Christ: Grace unto you, and peace, be multiplied.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:61e96d80-ce88-460c-a84f-3d01308ae5a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: 1PE 1:3
Text: Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, which according to his abundant mercy hath begotten us again unto a lively hope by the resurrection of Jesus Christ from the dead,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0251cee5-6b36-4b31-8d90-7d841b3b0c2e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: 1PE 1:4
Text: To an inheritance incorruptible, and undefiled, and that fadeth not away, reserved in heaven for you,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0df06f50-b9ff-43b7-b46a-bf8b8c769527>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: 1PE 1:5
Text: Who are kept by the power of God through faith unto salvation ready to be revealed in the last time.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:182d8033-62a3-44ba-9e2e-62886aed9f76>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 1PE 1:6
Text: Wherein ye greatly rejoice, though now for a season, if need be, ye are in heaviness through manifold temptations:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:449b0275-d68a-4608-ab2d-100ef558bc8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: 1PE 1:7
Text: That the trial of your faith, being much more precious than of gold that perisheth, though it be tried with fire, might be found unto praise and honour and glory at the appearing of Jesus Christ:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8097d1b-fa06-4011-81ec-1998afcea22b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 1PE 1:8
Text: Whom having not seen, ye love; in whom, though now ye see him not, yet believing, ye rejoice with joy unspeakable and full of glory:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6caf531-27ab-4149-a525-5817a4a6734c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: 1PE 1:9
Text: Receiving the end of your faith, even the salvation of your souls.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67aa20a8-0d95-4777-8ed4-a81b8895d58a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: 1PE 1:10
Text: Of which salvation the prophets have enquired and searched diligently, who prophesied of the grace that should come unto you:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eed3b41c-0d57-4e37-905d-8211a733e19a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: 1PE 1:11
Text: Searching what, or what manner of time the Spirit of Christ which was in them did signify, when it testified beforehand the sufferings of Christ, and the glory that should follow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e69c000e-635c-4b00-97a8-d9869a54a6ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 288

Reference: 1PE 1:12
Text: Unto whom it was revealed, that not unto themselves, but unto us they did minister the things, which are now reported unto you by them that have preached the gospel unto you with the Holy Ghost sent down from heaven; which things the angels desire to look into.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f607253d-c4a9-40cc-b765-37a6c8f6704d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: 1PE 1:13
Text: Wherefore gird up the loins of your mind, be sober, and hope to the end for the grace that is to be brought unto you at the revelation of Jesus Christ;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7242995b-82dd-43c3-a970-4f44239eb9a7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 1PE 1:14
Text: As obedient children, not fashioning yourselves according to the former lusts in your ignorance:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e74fde4-84ce-4567-9e36-aa45ffce8532>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: 1PE 1:15
Text: But as he which hath called you is holy, so be ye holy in all manner of conversation;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbe54705-b233-4181-b11b-378349dfdd52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: 1PE 1:16
Text: Because it is written, Be ye holy; for I am holy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a362ab1b-152c-49ca-ace9-31b4b32fdce3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 1PE 1:17
Text: And if ye call on the Father, who without respect of persons judgeth according to every man’s work, pass the time of your sojourning here in fear:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8019a591-11ec-4d1c-95db-5b95acf9fc43>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 1PE 1:18
Text: Forasmuch as ye know that ye were not redeemed with corruptible things, as silver and gold, from your vain conversation received by tradition from your fathers;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2844e6b7-afb7-414e-afa3-dea4e4ff6526>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: 1PE 1:19
Text: But with the precious blood of Christ, as of a lamb without blemish and without spot:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:84a948bb-5a70-4cbd-9a49-034806e662e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: 1PE 1:20
Text: Who verily was foreordained before the foundation of the world, but was manifest in these last times for you,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73cac946-5256-4648-9977-58625e61921b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: 1PE 1:21
Text: Who by him do believe in God, that raised him up from the dead, and gave him glory; that your faith and hope might be in God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16bd32eb-5fc7-46f3-8eda-f32b081b59a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: 1PE 1:22
Text: Seeing ye have purified your souls in obeying the truth through the Spirit unto unfeigned love of the brethren, see that ye love one another with a pure heart fervently:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4dedb71-c526-4d84-83ca-463b857198d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 146

Reference: 1PE 1:23
Text: Being born again, not of corruptible seed, but of incorruptible, by the word of God, which liveth and abideth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39f99e18-7484-4b83-8276-c271753b093b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 1PE 1:24
Text: For all flesh is as grass, and all the glory of man as the flower of grass. The grass withereth, and the flower thereof falleth away:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/1/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:317fddc1-fcd8-4cc1-8e67-8c8411968f25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: 1PE 1:25
Text: But the word of the Lord endureth for ever. And this is the word which by the gospel is preached unto you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8c31e9f-91c3-42c3-be40-6217a52a656d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: 1PE 2:1
Text: Wherefore laying aside all malice, and all guile, and hypocrisies, and envies, all evil speakings,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:539fc700-6f21-4ab5-82b9-47c126046a8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: 1PE 2:2
Text: As newborn babes, desire the sincere milk of the word, that ye may grow thereby:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:621289bd-22a0-420d-b317-66a7557b817f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: 1PE 2:3
Text: If so be ye have tasted that the Lord is gracious.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d841169-ab8a-4e1c-9d69-b1b9138dbf67>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: 1PE 2:4
Text: To whom coming, as unto a living stone, disallowed indeed of men, but chosen of God, and precious,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eba5bad0-bf51-42d4-9c46-df21f8f12340>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 1PE 2:5
Text: Ye also, as lively stones, are built up a spiritual house, an holy priesthood, to offer up spiritual sacrifices, acceptable to God by Jesus Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7e33682a-4088-4581-8d5c-1c1c32e7dbc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: 1PE 2:6
Text: Wherefore also it is contained in the scripture, Behold, I lay in Sion a chief corner stone, elect, precious: and he that believeth on him shall not be confounded.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50e80084-eb29-499f-8cd9-fe43a2fce921>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: 1PE 2:7
Text: Unto you therefore which believe he is precious: but unto them which be disobedient, the stone which the builders disallowed, the same is made the head of the corner,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aebe5e42-f9a9-407a-9192-748ddea80c28>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: 1PE 2:8
Text: And a stone of stumbling, and a rock of offence, even to them which stumble at the word, being disobedient: whereunto also they were appointed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e22b2b87-d96a-497b-bbd8-bf1d9d4f121d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: 1PE 2:9
Text: But ye are a chosen generation, a royal priesthood, an holy nation, a peculiar people; that ye should shew forth the praises of him who hath called you out of darkness into his marvellous light;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c0dc787-e0d4-40d6-8274-2a65166b26c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: 1PE 2:10
Text: Which in time past were not a people, but are now the people of God: which had not obtained mercy, but now have obtained mercy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13a4c5f7-27bf-4cd5-87db-69454ce27af4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: 1PE 2:11
Text: Dearly beloved, I beseech you as strangers and pilgrims, abstain from fleshly lusts, which war against the soul;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b94412a-6576-437a-8391-ae39236d30af>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: 1PE 2:12
Text: Having your conversation honest among the Gentiles: that, whereas they speak against you as evildoers, they may by your good works, which they shall behold, glorify God in the day of visitation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ef28804f-1ca0-4433-a82f-78f7902b76cc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 1PE 2:13
Text: Submit yourselves to every ordinance of man for the Lord’s sake: whether it be to the king, as supreme;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:094a6ae9-61f2-44eb-84ec-69f452d38a6b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 1PE 2:14
Text: Or unto governors, as unto them that are sent by him for the punishment of evildoers, and for the praise of them that do well.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d46a25e2-d6f2-4784-852b-1322b1173436>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: 1PE 2:15
Text: For so is the will of God, that with well doing ye may put to silence the ignorance of foolish men:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8bb657dc-7a90-4285-98c5-38f210c77e49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: 1PE 2:16
Text: As free, and not using your liberty for a cloke of maliciousness, but as the servants of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b98dd249-14df-4fad-ae77-d5667c8f799a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: 1PE 2:17
Text: Honour all men. Love the brotherhood. Fear God. Honour the king.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0c15a444-722b-4fce-81b1-ae3912d5492a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: 1PE 2:18
Text: Servants, be subject to your masters with all fear; not only to the good and gentle, but also to the froward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6726d4d2-7fd8-4499-bfb3-24bd78a4e3b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: 1PE 2:19
Text: For this is thankworthy, if a man for conscience toward God endure grief, suffering wrongfully.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ba55187-b1e7-4d01-a474-7f230f6842e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: 1PE 2:20
Text: For what glory is it, if, when ye be buffeted for your faults, ye shall take it patiently? but if, when ye do well, and suffer for it, ye take it patiently, this is acceptable with God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04d11c6c-a22d-4be3-8b99-c4e4933ec0be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 1PE 2:21
Text: For even hereunto were ye called: because Christ also suffered for us, leaving us an example, that ye should follow his steps:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69d2f2f4-0a10-4af8-8b8f-cf95afd57823>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: 1PE 2:22
Text: Who did no sin, neither was guile found in his mouth:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8bcfb3a5-44c0-4234-9398-9f2751eb4136>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: 1PE 2:23
Text: Who, when he was reviled, reviled not again; when he suffered, he threatened not; but committed himself to him that judgeth righteously:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fccc05fd-1aa6-43c7-880e-f10c19640ef7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: 1PE 2:24
Text: Who his own self bare our sins in his own body on the tree, that we, being dead to sins, should live unto righteousness: by whose stripes ye were healed.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/2/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:08a3a28f-082a-4ee6-b995-876665cd26f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: 1PE 2:25
Text: For ye were as sheep going astray; but are now returned unto the Shepherd and Bishop of your souls.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bda6e2f2-79b9-4ca2-b4ba-ed7dc3d09dcf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 1PE 3:1
Text: Likewise, ye wives, be in subjection to your own husbands; that, if any obey not the word, they also may without the word be won by the conversation of the wives;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3f8c059-8ba8-4be8-bcc9-03ef7cd56165>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 87

Reference: 1PE 3:2
Text: While they behold your chaste conversation coupled with fear.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a9a5bc93-d9c3-4f4b-83e4-a1901385c15c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: 1PE 3:3
Text: Whose adorning let it not be that outward adorning of plaiting the hair, and of wearing of gold, or of putting on of apparel;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1380c86-b7a9-4968-9b3d-3db47b79a6ed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: 1PE 3:4
Text: But let it be the hidden man of the heart, in that which is not corruptible, even the ornament of a meek and quiet spirit, which is in the sight of God of great price.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f78d656-6121-4e00-9247-2eed0ffeb73f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: 1PE 3:5
Text: For after this manner in the old time the holy women also, who trusted in God, adorned themselves, being in subjection unto their own husbands:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3d8d9718-6269-4a95-9616-d085f8358d81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 1PE 3:6
Text: Even as Sara obeyed Abraham, calling him lord: whose daughters ye are, as long as ye do well, and are not afraid with any amazement.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f8dedc93-30cd-486a-b9fd-0e6c8366a565>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: 1PE 3:7
Text: Likewise, ye husbands, dwell with them according to knowledge, giving honour unto the wife, as unto the weaker vessel, and as being heirs together of the grace of life; that your prayers be not hindered.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f83ee15-889d-4f15-a98f-96a098f8afdb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 1PE 3:8
Text: Finally, be ye all of one mind, having compassion one of another, love as brethren, be pitiful, be courteous:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e2205b5-b86f-4282-a167-711deba7ad7d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: 1PE 3:9
Text: Not rendering evil for evil, or railing for railing: but contrariwise blessing; knowing that ye are thereunto called, that ye should inherit a blessing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:933be017-5c0a-4933-a1c9-a682b6554f4c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: 1PE 3:10
Text: For he that will love life, and see good days, let him refrain his tongue from evil, and his lips that they speak no guile:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6f30a97-7975-4001-bc19-97bdc43f8836>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: 1PE 3:11
Text: Let him eschew evil, and do good; let him seek peace, and ensue it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d87ac959-15b0-44ae-86a9-db6426f9de81>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: 1PE 3:12
Text: For the eyes of the Lord are over the righteous, and his ears are open unto their prayers: but the face of the Lord is against them that do evil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:14ae69f3-8900-47f8-bf5c-c1702688a2b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: 1PE 3:13
Text: And who is he that will harm you, if ye be followers of that which is good?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ffe93029-f55a-4604-9761-e778272e8d84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: 1PE 3:14
Text: But and if ye suffer for righteousness’ sake, happy are ye: and be not afraid of their terror, neither be troubled;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd448f92-7fcf-4739-96f0-5166d40cd461>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: 1PE 3:15
Text: But sanctify the Lord God in your hearts: and be ready always to give an answer to every man that asketh you a reason of the hope that is in you with meekness and fear:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a68a0c9e-a540-4ecb-95e8-d0b74c5b83a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: 1PE 3:16
Text: Having a good conscience; that, whereas they speak evil of you, as of evildoers, they may be ashamed that falsely accuse your good conversation in Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bcf84a79-4226-482d-bf29-8ac08f64fa09>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: 1PE 3:17
Text: For it is better, if the will of God be so, that ye suffer for well doing, than for evil doing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c96d578-94ae-446d-9abf-8d05ed77c501>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: 1PE 3:18
Text: For Christ also hath once suffered for sins, the just for the unjust, that he might bring us to God, being put to death in the flesh, but quickened by the Spirit:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5605d257-b586-435a-9f64-0676ae8a2f4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: 1PE 3:19
Text: By which also he went and preached unto the spirits in prison;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/3/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd768adc-1994-4f39-b4ce-4cd8deea0c31>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: 1PE 3:20
Text: Which sometime were disobedient, when once the longsuffering of God waited in the days of Noah, while the ark was a preparing, wherein few, that is, eight souls were saved by water.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/3/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34e3f72e-acfd-477e-a04f-1eca3d702b84>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: 1PE 3:21
Text: The like figure whereunto even baptism doth also now save us (not the putting away of the filth of the flesh, but the answer of a good conscience toward God,) by the resurrection of Jesus Christ:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/3/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f904e777-332c-4bb5-ae3b-5916b6ccee03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 147

Reference: 1PE 3:22
Text: Who is gone into heaven, and is on the right hand of God; angels and authorities and powers being made subject unto him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67f1446d-fe37-4257-a957-d1a1c4867303>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: 1PE 4:1
Text: Forasmuch then as Christ hath suffered for us in the flesh, arm yourselves likewise with the same mind: for he that hath suffered in the flesh hath ceased from sin;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d2803678-be54-4a37-ac85-33ee6afd56a1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: 1PE 4:2
Text: That he no longer should live the rest of his time in the flesh to the lusts of men, but to the will of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37803120-fd3f-48e5-916b-741f0347491e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: 1PE 4:3
Text: For the time past of our life may suffice us to have wrought the will of the Gentiles, when we walked in lasciviousness, lusts, excess of wine, revellings, banquetings, and abominable idolatries:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6cd2d532-140e-49d8-9f5a-10707c336d13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: 1PE 4:4
Text: Wherein they think it strange that ye run not with them to the same excess of riot, speaking evil of you:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bad15307-0068-40d8-81f9-175f15047d98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: 1PE 4:5
Text: Who shall give account to him that is ready to judge the quick and the dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5fac5507-2bd2-4850-9800-e9a413f3ba01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: 1PE 4:6
Text: For for this cause was the gospel preached also to them that are dead, that they might be judged according to men in the flesh, but live according to God in the spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4a4eb0cd-4d3c-4bb7-941d-e5db91a163f4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: 1PE 4:7
Text: But the end of all things is at hand: be ye therefore sober, and watch unto prayer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:94b0bf68-bc66-498a-bc05-c36447174dde>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 1PE 4:8
Text: And above all things have fervent charity among yourselves: for charity shall cover the multitude of sins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0991b83b-46b5-407c-86fb-6dc090ee8851>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: 1PE 4:9
Text: Use hospitality one to another without grudging.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:136e623c-46c3-4146-a2d4-6561c3bdad20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: 1PE 4:10
Text: As every man hath received the gift, even so minister the same one to another, as good stewards of the manifold grace of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:02b0aa3e-2faf-4c7d-918a-c8be2b769a51>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 270

Reference: 1PE 4:11
Text: If any man speak, let him speak as the oracles of God; if any man minister, let him do it as of the ability which God giveth: that God in all things may be glorified through Jesus Christ, to whom be praise and dominion for ever and ever. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c426698-b156-4812-b2f0-f54b9a0345e9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: 1PE 4:12
Text: Beloved, think it not strange concerning the fiery trial which is to try you, as though some strange thing happened unto you:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f89d448-e9f5-4866-8f0d-df234e179c9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: 1PE 4:13
Text: But rejoice, inasmuch as ye are partakers of Christ’s sufferings; that, when his glory shall be revealed, ye may be glad also with exceeding joy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:678f1449-7f31-4479-8350-9f09eb2bbddf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: 1PE 4:14
Text: If ye be reproached for the name of Christ, happy are ye; for the spirit of glory and of God resteth upon you: on their part he is evil spoken of, but on your part he is glorified.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f255de13-4291-48b7-a37a-b1abdfa85ba0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 1PE 4:15
Text: But let none of you suffer as a murderer, or as a thief, or as an evildoer, or as a busybody in other men’s matters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c190ac38-e343-4b42-978e-dc295719c884>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 1PE 4:16
Text: Yet if any man suffer as a Christian, let him not be ashamed; but let him glorify God on this behalf.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7c8775e-d83f-4544-9917-eb482230360e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 1PE 4:17
Text: For the time is come that judgment must begin at the house of God: and if it first begin at us, what shall the end be of them that obey not the gospel of God?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/4/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:937c5753-2177-4538-b164-08a13fd55f58>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: 1PE 4:18
Text: And if the righteous scarcely be saved, where shall the ungodly and the sinner appear?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/4/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1331334d-27be-4217-b530-ea738534830d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 1PE 4:19
Text: Wherefore let them that suffer according to the will of God commit the keeping of their souls to him in well doing, as unto a faithful Creator.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90c2f0d4-dd4b-417c-9db6-eb51794be4a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 1PE 5:1
Text: The elders which are among you I exhort, who am also an elder, and a witness of the sufferings of Christ, and also a partaker of the glory that shall be revealed:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a8b70c61-4814-4766-9387-1e89ae504c03>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: 1PE 5:2
Text: Feed the flock of God which is among you, taking the oversight thereof, not by constraint, but willingly; not for filthy lucre, but of a ready mind;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:423231e4-26b4-458b-a27b-d7b0acbd209f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: 1PE 5:3
Text: Neither as being lords over God’s heritage, but being ensamples to the flock.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96218141-6d7e-496e-b6d9-7695456d3544>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 1PE 5:4
Text: And when the chief Shepherd shall appear, ye shall receive a crown of glory that fadeth not away.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a3df8eb4-f960-48b0-a912-5e0aede23bb1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 215

Reference: 1PE 5:5
Text: Likewise, ye younger, submit yourselves unto the elder. Yea, all of you be subject one to another, and be clothed with humility: for God resisteth the proud, and giveth grace to the humble.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:249d9e82-6d69-47cb-b2e4-ca2f1a721c0f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: 1PE 5:6
Text: Humble yourselves therefore under the mighty hand of God, that he may exalt you in due time:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a50605f4-40a6-4f89-98c3-489b063b83f7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: 1PE 5:7
Text: Casting all your care upon him; for he careth for you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e127e64b-4df2-4380-9777-d3e03e743dec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: 1PE 5:8
Text: Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:33b1182e-5ee5-4f01-bad6-1eb5c02975a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: 1PE 5:9
Text: Whom resist stedfast in the faith, knowing that the same afflictions are accomplished in your brethren that are in the world.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13a64f0f-ef2f-4140-9fa0-182cf3bc05a6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 1PE 5:10
Text: But the God of all grace, who hath called us unto his eternal glory by Christ Jesus, after that ye have suffered a while, make you perfect, stablish, strengthen, settle you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e185216-ca12-4765-94ee-c0ae0ca3bc5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: 1PE 5:11
Text: To him be glory and dominion for ever and ever. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f0ae2ef3-5ecd-4a7d-976b-626f89d2d6a2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 1PE 5:12
Text: By Silvanus, a faithful brother unto you, as I suppose, I have written briefly, exhorting, and testifying that this is the true grace of God wherein ye stand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b458bdb1-9a3a-4734-b3c1-8d7380a894b0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: 1PE 5:13
Text: The church that is at Babylon, elected together with you, saluteth you; and so doth Marcus my son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1PE/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f9174bb0-113c-4593-abc0-a25e479795c6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: 1PE 5:14
Text: Greet ye one another with a kiss of charity. Peace be with you all that are in Christ Jesus. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af8173a6-738c-44bf-9e04-9bafbf8ef055>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: 2PE 1:1
Text: Simon Peter, a servant and an apostle of Jesus Christ, to them that have obtained like precious faith with us through the righteousness of God and our Saviour Jesus Christ:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35e028ea-0873-4ac0-806d-c26cd32da461>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: 2PE 1:2
Text: Grace and peace be multiplied unto you through the knowledge of God, and of Jesus our Lord,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a2bcf74a-21b1-4900-bd7b-19e36e74d25d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: 2PE 1:3
Text: According as his divine power hath given unto us all things that pertain unto life and godliness, through the knowledge of him that hath called us to glory and virtue:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:74868b67-853f-47d9-a4a4-86ab3a91e9e8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: 2PE 1:4
Text: Whereby are given unto us exceeding great and precious promises: that by these ye might be partakers of the divine nature, having escaped the corruption that is in the world through lust.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dfefb6eb-cbad-4c06-9328-6d6751bfb324>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: 2PE 1:5
Text: And beside this, giving all diligence, add to your faith virtue; and to virtue knowledge;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:78943ba0-2c10-4424-881f-fd94b99c7b80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: 2PE 1:6
Text: And to knowledge temperance; and to temperance patience; and to patience godliness;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c764804-49ff-41b1-a1c5-18b3fbba0e36>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: 2PE 1:7
Text: And to godliness brotherly kindness; and to brotherly kindness charity.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:242c4faa-1d72-4f24-af0f-bc84c4824abf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: 2PE 1:8
Text: For if these things be in you, and abound, they make you that ye shall neither be barren nor unfruitful in the knowledge of our Lord Jesus Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22eec5b7-5969-4b0f-9bbe-3f0975ff8242>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 150

Reference: 2PE 1:9
Text: But he that lacketh these things is blind, and cannot see afar off, and hath forgotten that he was purged from his old sins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:739d0064-094e-41e8-95c0-2630b597ed5b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: 2PE 1:10
Text: Wherefore the rather, brethren, give diligence to make your calling and election sure: for if ye do these things, ye shall never fall:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6522970b-ccc3-4573-8557-3485267f1dcf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: 2PE 1:11
Text: For so an entrance shall be ministered unto you abundantly into the everlasting kingdom of our Lord and Saviour Jesus Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c81319a8-6993-47fc-bff7-e9099d81b11a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: 2PE 1:12
Text: Wherefore I will not be negligent to put you always in remembrance of these things, though ye know them, and be established in the present truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:58f077ee-97fe-4b51-8a42-e1cae4b0645c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: 2PE 1:13
Text: Yea, I think it meet, as long as I am in this tabernacle, to stir you up by putting you in remembrance;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a26c12c4-f228-4a7e-80f3-bf7cc5d1061b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 2PE 1:14
Text: Knowing that shortly I must put off this my tabernacle, even as our Lord Jesus Christ hath shewed me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cd66e036-f898-422e-a3e8-8091617574eb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: 2PE 1:15
Text: Moreover I will endeavour that ye may be able after my decease to have these things always in remembrance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39f2df32-e940-4f34-a049-dacc0dd90508>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: 2PE 1:16
Text: For we have not followed cunningly devised fables, when we made known unto you the power and coming of our Lord Jesus Christ, but were eyewitnesses of his majesty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48e58081-4857-48e9-9d37-e7ddfad0c8b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 193

Reference: 2PE 1:17
Text: For he received from God the Father honour and glory, when there came such a voice to him from the excellent glory, This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8e77d794-38e4-4006-8c4a-8d90669d6241>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: 2PE 1:18
Text: And this voice which came from heaven we heard, when we were with him in the holy mount.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da8c53cf-80ae-4bfa-9773-f3431c47be8a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 214

Reference: 2PE 1:19
Text: We have also a more sure word of prophecy; whereunto ye do well that ye take heed, as unto a light that shineth in a dark place, until the day dawn, and the day star arise in your hearts:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4498d54-9b2e-4eca-841f-316d237abc42>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: 2PE 1:20
Text: Knowing this first, that no prophecy of the scripture is of any private interpretation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/1/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aae559c9-9429-479a-bfac-68f5209bc8bb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 2PE 1:21
Text: For the prophecy came not in old time by the will of man: but holy men of God spake as they were moved by the Holy Ghost.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:342eaf25-83ff-49dd-ace2-00f4a630569a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: 2PE 2:1
Text: But there were false prophets also among the people, even as there shall be false teachers among you, who privily shall bring in damnable heresies, even denying the Lord that bought them, and bring upon themselves swift destruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc9c1bdb-187e-4dec-8bd8-81356e27050f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: 2PE 2:2
Text: And many shall follow their pernicious ways; by reason of whom the way of truth shall be evil spoken of.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb0c8c28-f7ba-4280-8da6-8d9f9ecb47b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: 2PE 2:3
Text: And through covetousness shall they with feigned words make merchandise of you: whose judgment now of a long time lingereth not, and their damnation slumbereth not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16f362db-98c8-45a1-adac-29a48a587367>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 2PE 2:4
Text: For if God spared not the angels that sinned, but cast them down to hell, and delivered them into chains of darkness, to be reserved unto judgment;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19f758ad-0f70-4ae7-a850-c4380d9bbeff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: 2PE 2:5
Text: And spared not the old world, but saved Noah the eighth person, a preacher of righteousness, bringing in the flood upon the world of the ungodly;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fd9038c3-c391-446d-9fda-5113824770c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: 2PE 2:6
Text: And turning the cities of Sodom and Gomorrha into ashes condemned them with an overthrow, making them an ensample unto those that after should live ungodly;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:54daed5b-9a78-49c2-bc47-1d71beb74450>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: 2PE 2:7
Text: And delivered just Lot, vexed with the filthy conversation of the wicked:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:19b2eedb-e436-42fe-ae16-39e16577de41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 2PE 2:8
Text: (For that righteous man dwelling among them, in seeing and hearing, vexed his righteous soul from day to day with their unlawful deeds;)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46cfc86f-1d71-456b-8ffc-4a2b35379e7e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: 2PE 2:9
Text: The Lord knoweth how to deliver the godly out of temptations, and to reserve the unjust unto the day of judgment to be punished:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8095bec9-30be-4c8f-85d6-bbf398ee4998>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: 2PE 2:10
Text: But chiefly them that walk after the flesh in the lust of uncleanness, and despise government. Presumptuous are they, selfwilled, they are not afraid to speak evil of dignities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9727dfb6-1f93-40d9-9914-bbbe4038076a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: 2PE 2:11
Text: Whereas angels, which are greater in power and might, bring not railing accusation against them before the Lord.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c0b789ef-6e18-4356-a6a3-0b828062f5ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: 2PE 2:12
Text: But these, as natural brute beasts, made to be taken and destroyed, speak evil of the things that they understand not; and shall utterly perish in their own corruption;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:145b1da1-c9c0-4c92-b7e8-f571923daeb9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 234

Reference: 2PE 2:13
Text: And shall receive the reward of unrighteousness, as they that count it pleasure to riot in the day time. Spots they are and blemishes, sporting themselves with their own deceivings while they feast with you;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06b28165-6f3f-4bd7-9d98-6dfe69f69eed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: 2PE 2:14
Text: Having eyes full of adultery, and that cannot cease from sin; beguiling unstable souls: an heart they have exercised with covetous practices; cursed children:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b62f28f4-ffe6-4d5c-ba6b-57096054b9f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: 2PE 2:15
Text: Which have forsaken the right way, and are gone astray, following the way of Balaam the son of Bosor, who loved the wages of unrighteousness;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7bb74439-1b44-4d34-b5ba-6d3117c64aac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: 2PE 2:16
Text: But was rebuked for his iniquity: the dumb ass speaking with man’s voice forbad the madness of the prophet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e248cdde-ec99-4d8e-b7a8-aa354c2e50e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 2PE 2:17
Text: These are wells without water, clouds that are carried with a tempest; to whom the mist of darkness is reserved for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb1eed4a-a4ec-486e-a3aa-e8db061a96d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: 2PE 2:18
Text: For when they speak great swelling words of vanity, they allure through the lusts of the flesh, through much wantonness, those that were clean escaped from them who live in error.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67f44541-5e56-423e-93f7-ea8aba68365d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: 2PE 2:19
Text: While they promise them liberty, they themselves are the servants of corruption: for of whom a man is overcome, of the same is he brought in bondage.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f2e5675e-fa76-4be8-bf62-7addeca49333>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 247

Reference: 2PE 2:20
Text: For if after they have escaped the pollutions of the world through the knowledge of the Lord and Saviour Jesus Christ, they are again entangled therein, and overcome, the latter end is worse with them than the beginning.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c4209f40-9cc4-425e-99d2-1f4794213aa4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: 2PE 2:21
Text: For it had been better for them not to have known the way of righteousness, than, after they have known it, to turn from the holy commandment delivered unto them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d8240d79-9a88-4b02-a686-77705476b5c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: 2PE 2:22
Text: But it is happened unto them according to the true proverb, The dog is turned to his own vomit again; and the sow that was washed to her wallowing in the mire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c73c6d6-5d25-4ce7-92e5-d5b9bed2243e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 2PE 3:1
Text: This second epistle, beloved, I now write unto you; in both which I stir up your pure minds by way of remembrance:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8240f88a-b8d0-4e8d-9d97-8daac0910bf6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 2PE 3:2
Text: That ye may be mindful of the words which were spoken before by the holy prophets, and of the commandment of us the apostles of the Lord and Saviour:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3b92d4aa-0aeb-4608-852c-86d64b823620>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: 2PE 3:3
Text: Knowing this first, that there shall come in the last days scoffers, walking after their own lusts,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a87d2a05-37a4-446b-9736-3a6a5e3e2713>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 2PE 3:4
Text: And saying, Where is the promise of his coming? for since the fathers fell asleep, all things continue as they were from the beginning of the creation.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:34a5a27a-e807-4db4-afa4-d5be7c60d6b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: 2PE 3:5
Text: For this they willingly are ignorant of, that by the word of God the heavens were of old, and the earth standing out of the water and in the water:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e75eaabf-f928-48a2-b82d-caead003db86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: 2PE 3:6
Text: Whereby the world that then was, being overflowed with water, perished:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cbe70766-ef48-4bd0-94b3-c129a85a6ea7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: 2PE 3:7
Text: But the heavens and the earth, which are now, by the same word are kept in store, reserved unto fire against the day of judgment and perdition of ungodly men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80b42556-3986-44ee-baff-746fc64d459e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 2PE 3:8
Text: But, beloved, be not ignorant of this one thing, that one day is with the Lord as a thousand years, and a thousand years as one day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50536614-b214-4de2-b459-e2e1b38c4cc8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: 2PE 3:9
Text: The Lord is not slack concerning his promise, as some men count slackness; but is longsuffering to us-ward, not willing that any should perish, but that all should come to repentance.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e420828-bbca-4a36-8a29-c0bc651f1bca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 259

Reference: 2PE 3:10
Text: But the day of the Lord will come as a thief in the night; in the which the heavens shall pass away with a great noise, and the elements shall melt with fervent heat, the earth also and the works that are therein shall be burned up.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6dc2bb2-bc1a-411f-b622-ec52771a3ca8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: 2PE 3:11
Text: Seeing then that all these things shall be dissolved, what manner of persons ought ye to be in all holy conversation and godliness,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d80f7c4a-5e47-492e-a617-e83eb5669693>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: 2PE 3:12
Text: Looking for and hasting unto the coming of the day of God, wherein the heavens being on fire shall be dissolved, and the elements shall melt with fervent heat?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c6a68336-17c9-478a-be23-6d8c1d15f851>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: 2PE 3:13
Text: Nevertheless we, according to his promise, look for new heavens and a new earth, wherein dwelleth righteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fa01207b-3a3f-47a0-b16b-3a72f1d4b815>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 2PE 3:14
Text: Wherefore, beloved, seeing that ye look for such things, be diligent that ye may be found of him in peace, without spot, and blameless.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ac55e7d-a452-4830-b76c-ef44fb2738ea>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 2PE 3:15
Text: And account that the longsuffering of our Lord is salvation; even as our beloved brother Paul also according to the wisdom given unto him hath written unto you;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:162b1f69-df40-4f10-bf05-3d226d10ed1a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 253

Reference: 2PE 3:16
Text: As also in all his epistles, speaking in them of these things; in which are some things hard to be understood, which they that are unlearned and unstable wrest, as they do also the other scriptures, unto their own destruction.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f03b088e-84b5-46bb-99ac-e634ed57447e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: 2PE 3:17
Text: Ye therefore, beloved, seeing ye know these things before, beware lest ye also, being led away with the error of the wicked, fall from your own stedfastness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2PE/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eea02ce1-7a4a-4d11-9a49-36cbe19e5ce1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: 2PE 3:18
Text: But grow in grace, and in the knowledge of our Lord and Saviour Jesus Christ. To him be glory both now and for ever. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0bb4775-e020-4309-b914-632592c98610>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: 1JN 1:1
Text: That which was from the beginning, which we have heard, which we have seen with our eyes, which we have looked upon, and our hands have handled, of the Word of life;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea96c668-b6b0-407f-bfa6-4ed62433e2ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 1JN 1:2
Text: (For the life was manifested, and we have seen it, and bear witness, and shew unto you that eternal life, which was with the Father, and was manifested unto us;)


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:11c4ae3f-406e-47ca-b673-41e2206640fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: 1JN 1:3
Text: That which we have seen and heard declare we unto you, that ye also may have fellowship with us: and truly our fellowship is with the Father, and with his Son Jesus Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5b5c25f-5602-4b38-9c5a-6bcf88c840b7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 88

Reference: 1JN 1:4
Text: And these things write we unto you, that your joy may be full.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b52b7cb-2e43-4b41-a7b3-7bca775076d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 1JN 1:5
Text: This then is the message which we have heard of him, and declare unto you, that God is light, and in him is no darkness at all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d712d05-9542-4265-9cc7-c93336cf5b41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: 1JN 1:6
Text: If we say that we have fellowship with him, and walk in darkness, we lie, and do not the truth:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c803bc71-2354-4239-92fd-0c26cc3e3977>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: 1JN 1:7
Text: But if we walk in the light, as he is in the light, we have fellowship one with another, and the blood of Jesus Christ his Son cleanseth us from all sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c14e8b09-2c48-400a-9c48-5fcb9ffde987>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: 1JN 1:8
Text: If we say that we have no sin, we deceive ourselves, and the truth is not in us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3c5c82c-cd2a-4d8c-ae6d-602f3c7d3bc7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 1JN 1:9
Text: If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7dc9e775-d9c9-4357-ad50-23dcef2ce236>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: 1JN 1:10
Text: If we say that we have not sinned, we make him a liar, and his word is not in us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f4f3aa76-3cbc-4051-8bb1-a0df7d5541ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: 1JN 2:1
Text: My little children, these things write I unto you, that ye sin not. And if any man sin, we have an advocate with the Father, Jesus Christ the righteous:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b0ce59d7-26d6-4651-8194-d76907e61257>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: 1JN 2:2
Text: And he is the propitiation for our sins: and not for ours only, but also for the sins of the whole world.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:eac5c58d-9b1b-4302-aabf-b20e840f8d2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 94

Reference: 1JN 2:3
Text: And hereby we do know that we know him, if we keep his commandments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3c2725a-8726-4c6e-b6fb-4fec44f7c244>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: 1JN 2:4
Text: He that saith, I know him, and keepeth not his commandments, is a liar, and the truth is not in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b16a17e-7065-4478-89dd-a46195d51d21>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: 1JN 2:5
Text: But whoso keepeth his word, in him verily is the love of God perfected: hereby know we that we are in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:77907312-a968-4943-b56a-aedb88df880c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: 1JN 2:6
Text: He that saith he abideth in him ought himself also so to walk, even as he walked.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:403fe5e3-008e-4ff1-ae77-73ae6617ab8d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 1JN 2:7
Text: Brethren, I write no new commandment unto you, but an old commandment which ye had from the beginning. The old commandment is the word which ye have heard from the beginning.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:68d55587-0e05-48cf-a219-c90c495c6a11>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: 1JN 2:8
Text: Again, a new commandment I write unto you, which thing is true in him and in you: because the darkness is past, and the true light now shineth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ec19248-c4b7-4b3c-958e-c8d8d22ba949>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: 1JN 2:9
Text: He that saith he is in the light, and hateth his brother, is in darkness even until now.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e08068c-402c-4608-866c-769a2c382422>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 1JN 2:10
Text: He that loveth his brother abideth in the light, and there is none occasion of stumbling in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7588062-bd86-459a-9d6a-3eb8e4c732c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 177

Reference: 1JN 2:11
Text: But he that hateth his brother is in darkness, and walketh in darkness, and knoweth not whither he goeth, because that darkness hath blinded his eyes.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ab3e557c-2a82-484d-a254-c0378e2007e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: 1JN 2:12
Text: I write unto you, little children, because your sins are forgiven you for his name’s sake.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9302b99d-3893-41d3-994e-a2ca9d018604>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: 1JN 2:13
Text: I write unto you, fathers, because ye have known him that is from the beginning. I write unto you, young men, because ye have overcome the wicked one. I write unto you, little children, because ye have known the Father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:86ca49e6-089d-4b90-9abe-52b525992469>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 246

Reference: 1JN 2:14
Text: I have written unto you, fathers, because ye have known him that is from the beginning. I have written unto you, young men, because ye are strong, and the word of God abideth in you, and ye have overcome the wicked one.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09638e94-97d6-4cbe-8a5a-7dedab57ce90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 1JN 2:15
Text: Love not the world, neither the things that are in the world. If any man love the world, the love of the Father is not in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:536100bf-db55-43ee-9c56-314006615439>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: 1JN 2:16
Text: For all that is in the world, the lust of the flesh, and the lust of the eyes, and the pride of life, is not of the Father, but is of the world.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:272875af-6128-499d-ab4d-8ed44ae2d3d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: 1JN 2:17
Text: And the world passeth away, and the lust thereof: but he that doeth the will of God abideth for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d9bc37e-087a-49ce-bf39-738a3befdd90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: 1JN 2:18
Text: Little children, it is the last time: and as ye have heard that antichrist shall come, even now are there many antichrists; whereby we know that it is the last time.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e0b94521-97bc-4ecb-8d18-3bd0a54e7ede>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 228

Reference: 1JN 2:19
Text: They went out from us, but they were not of us; for if they had been of us, they would no doubt have continued with us: but they went out, that they might be made manifest that they were not all of us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:909af1d6-ab1a-44f9-938e-86dd7d74e126>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: 1JN 2:20
Text: But ye have an unction from the Holy One, and ye know all things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a6c460d5-4c3e-4624-be9d-3507c2ab15ac>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: 1JN 2:21
Text: I have not written unto you because ye know not the truth, but because ye know it, and that no lie is of the truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d8c1add-5770-4f98-91c4-d51bc569fe17>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 1JN 2:22
Text: Who is a liar but he that denieth that Jesus is the Christ? He is antichrist, that denieth the Father and the Son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ff1b6ae2-eedd-4925-ba14-9ad6fdfccd29>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: 1JN 2:23
Text: Whosoever denieth the Son, the same hath not the Father: he that acknowledgeth the Son hath the Father also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2c56545d-8d03-4d5e-9b84-aeb5ec07e012>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 221

Reference: 1JN 2:24
Text: Let that therefore abide in you, which ye have heard from the beginning. If that which ye have heard from the beginning shall remain in you, ye also shall continue in the Son, and in the Father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7cc74b7c-c29b-4979-9047-d59ddd660fc8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 95

Reference: 1JN 2:25
Text: And this is the promise that he hath promised us, even eternal life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4c0578d2-1ee4-4532-9737-31e166803ffb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 96

Reference: 1JN 2:26
Text: These things have I written unto you concerning them that seduce you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:71970ae0-d8a6-429d-91c6-00b490e65860>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 268

Reference: 1JN 2:27
Text: But the anointing which ye have received of him abideth in you, and ye need not that any man teach you: but as the same anointing teacheth you of all things, and is truth, and is no lie, and even as it hath taught you, ye shall abide in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:653b43ae-f9d0-46cb-9ca5-3a544b412efe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: 1JN 2:28
Text: And now, little children, abide in him; that, when he shall appear, we may have confidence, and not be ashamed before him at his coming.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/2/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:83b2d7f5-bb4c-4c60-a1f5-bff9d2f4c3bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: 1JN 2:29
Text: If ye know that he is righteous, ye know that every one that doeth righteousness is born of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d62f74ac-2b3b-451c-8f74-4cf0c30c9668>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: 1JN 3:1
Text: Behold, what manner of love the Father hath bestowed upon us, that we should be called the sons of God: therefore the world knoweth us not, because it knew him not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:26db1090-7ce1-4229-aea7-56948e20e285>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 1JN 3:2
Text: Beloved, now are we the sons of God, and it doth not yet appear what we shall be: but we know that, when he shall appear, we shall be like him; for we shall see him as he is.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf7e546d-dbc1-4343-a877-792a4c91b9b4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: 1JN 3:3
Text: And every man that hath this hope in him purifieth himself, even as he is pure.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:897a5045-a326-4aee-84c6-54ea91ae6323>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: 1JN 3:4
Text: Whosoever committeth sin transgresseth also the law: for sin is the transgression of the law.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fca93474-caf4-41df-bef7-c539dcbe3e3c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: 1JN 3:5
Text: And ye know that he was manifested to take away our sins; and in him is no sin.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8274e1f4-ddfc-4d0c-8406-e56eecbe574f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: 1JN 3:6
Text: Whosoever abideth in him sinneth not: whosoever sinneth hath not seen him, neither known him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:022e3716-8860-4158-8cb5-b25995a922fe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: 1JN 3:7
Text: Little children, let no man deceive you: he that doeth righteousness is righteous, even as he is righteous.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b266dd32-66c8-496f-a93b-9c5db634876e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: 1JN 3:8
Text: He that committeth sin is of the devil; for the devil sinneth from the beginning. For this purpose the Son of God was manifested, that he might destroy the works of the devil.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f74f402-0b62-4112-b49f-71b4e020c1da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: 1JN 3:9
Text: Whosoever is born of God doth not commit sin; for his seed remaineth in him: and he cannot sin, because he is born of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9b81df54-d719-4173-813c-c10ad9ddf7e2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: 1JN 3:10
Text: In this the children of God are manifest, and the children of the devil: whosoever doeth not righteousness is not of God, neither he that loveth not his brother.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3ad768c-5fcb-47b7-b4d8-b788db5a3a80>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: 1JN 3:11
Text: For this is the message that ye heard from the beginning, that we should love one another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46b5d667-d008-4ab4-907e-c225f15357bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 180

Reference: 1JN 3:12
Text: Not as Cain, who was of that wicked one, and slew his brother. And wherefore slew he him? Because his own works were evil, and his brother’s righteous.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4b0e30f-1304-49cf-9567-b73691dbfa69>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 74

Reference: 1JN 3:13
Text: Marvel not, my brethren, if the world hate you.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb6239de-a871-4ab6-a98c-4321e3f8a930>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: 1JN 3:14
Text: We know that we have passed from death unto life, because we love the brethren. He that loveth not his brother abideth in death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:430c1919-6788-4db5-a462-2a67bcd5d694>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: 1JN 3:15
Text: Whosoever hateth his brother is a murderer: and ye know that no murderer hath eternal life abiding in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dd3bbf80-9a37-427a-92de-4b331e344d41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: 1JN 3:16
Text: Hereby perceive we the love of God, because he laid down his life for us: and we ought to lay down our lives for the brethren.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:88bd7dae-7a6d-44b6-91a9-4b1c72396abc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: 1JN 3:17
Text: But whoso hath this world’s good, and seeth his brother have need, and shutteth up his bowels of compassion from him, how dwelleth the love of God in him?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48df9262-502a-4431-a452-f3fb1344a810>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: 1JN 3:18
Text: My little children, let us not love in word, neither in tongue; but in deed and in truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:66150c52-7303-4c89-806e-2a099c3961ec>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: 1JN 3:19
Text: And hereby we know that we are of the truth, and shall assure our hearts before him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:622e669d-ba3e-4910-ba17-8642951d5a6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: 1JN 3:20
Text: For if our heart condemn us, God is greater than our heart, and knoweth all things.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:950fe9ee-1bbb-47e7-8c59-c35df874a22a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: 1JN 3:21
Text: Beloved, if our heart condemn us not, then have we confidence toward God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9ba37f99-ad2c-485b-86d6-3f6e97edd03a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: 1JN 3:22
Text: And whatsoever we ask, we receive of him, because we keep his commandments, and do those things that are pleasing in his sight.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:04e227bf-cb4c-4e83-8b0f-cecc6856ca78>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 164

Reference: 1JN 3:23
Text: And this is his commandment, That we should believe on the name of his Son Jesus Christ, and love one another, as he gave us commandment.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/3/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:773bf6ef-39a3-4605-935c-91ed7520207f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: 1JN 3:24
Text: And he that keepeth his commandments dwelleth in him, and he in him. And hereby we know that he abideth in us, by the Spirit which he hath given us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2363d55-ecf0-42b1-803c-56347cc5eb20>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 1JN 4:1
Text: Beloved, believe not every spirit, but try the spirits whether they are of God: because many false prophets are gone out into the world.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5b7e68f3-238d-43a6-bb0c-f72a8a4997e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: 1JN 4:2
Text: Hereby know ye the Spirit of God: Every spirit that confesseth that Jesus Christ is come in the flesh is of God:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4210d95-40a5-4afc-bb88-7f8cd626aeaa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 239

Reference: 1JN 4:3
Text: And every spirit that confesseth not that Jesus Christ is come in the flesh is not of God: and this is that spirit of antichrist, whereof ye have heard that it should come; and even now already is it in the world.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d1c891d-d4ac-404f-92b5-15af3f861b6c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: 1JN 4:4
Text: Ye are of God, little children, and have overcome them: because greater is he that is in you, than he that is in the world.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5f8617b-565c-4ffe-922f-b202ef4db714>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: 1JN 4:5
Text: They are of the world: therefore speak they of the world, and the world heareth them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4dc7428a-af16-4f55-b29a-4cc318fc3f89>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: 1JN 4:6
Text: We are of God: he that knoweth God heareth us; he that is not of God heareth not us. Hereby know we the spirit of truth, and the spirit of error.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2106a944-bb37-4636-8586-9f35ff866ad4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: 1JN 4:7
Text: Beloved, let us love one another: for love is of God; and every one that loveth is born of God, and knoweth God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:927182f6-59b1-4687-bd85-2bd683ff6524>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 78

Reference: 1JN 4:8
Text: He that loveth not knoweth not God; for God is love.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e65224ce-1d90-43f8-8459-648451e1d69c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 1JN 4:9
Text: In this was manifested the love of God toward us, because that God sent his only begotten Son into the world, that we might live through him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ec2a7a94-94db-4c64-b052-679b851218cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: 1JN 4:10
Text: Herein is love, not that we loved God, but that he loved us, and sent his Son to be the propitiation for our sins.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:49915790-b0b3-4520-8564-cc35e05ed9ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 90

Reference: 1JN 4:11
Text: Beloved, if God so loved us, we ought also to love one another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/4/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:149c56b4-1be5-4461-81a3-a858f84562d1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: 1JN 4:12
Text: No man hath seen God at any time. If we love one another, God dwelleth in us, and his love is perfected in us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/4/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97bd7e31-2204-4942-8a29-b5cefdad6fb0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 117

Reference: 1JN 4:13
Text: Hereby know we that we dwell in him, and he in us, because he hath given us of his Spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/4/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce05c409-5279-43d5-9307-e6fe00b19baf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: 1JN 4:14
Text: And we have seen and do testify that the Father sent the Son to be the Saviour of the world.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/4/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:068e633a-93ad-4c63-8df2-b42d2ee91eb5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 116

Reference: 1JN 4:15
Text: Whosoever shall confess that Jesus is the Son of God, God dwelleth in him, and he in God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/4/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b9daa841-f282-41cb-8c99-78a4694df769>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 1JN 4:16
Text: And we have known and believed the love that God hath to us. God is love; and he that dwelleth in love dwelleth in God, and God in him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/4/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:46b04762-4fff-4623-ad18-59fc08fc2b8f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: 1JN 4:17
Text: Herein is our love made perfect, that we may have boldness in the day of judgment: because as he is, so are we in this world.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/4/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b100fb46-9674-4e7e-aa6b-65722f539766>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: 1JN 4:18
Text: There is no fear in love; but perfect love casteth out fear: because fear hath torment. He that feareth is not made perfect in love.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/4/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:97956829-9810-41e5-9aa1-105072817bf2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 66

Reference: 1JN 4:19
Text: We love him, because he first loved us.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/4/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:521e66cd-e2d7-4e70-956a-55778a826403>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 1JN 4:20
Text: If a man say, I love God, and hateth his brother, he is a liar: for he that loveth not his brother whom he hath seen, how can he love God whom he hath not seen?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/4/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d015134e-46e9-41dc-be8a-e96755dc7450>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: 1JN 4:21
Text: And this commandment have we from him, That he who loveth God love his brother also.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64ef96bd-d90c-4cc9-8c50-bfdc11ef3527>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: 1JN 5:1
Text: Whosoever believeth that Jesus is the Christ is born of God: and every one that loveth him that begat loveth him also that is begotten of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:80d01739-a6e2-4248-b005-59314c312e73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 120

Reference: 1JN 5:2
Text: By this we know that we love the children of God, when we love God, and keep his commandments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7bf76af8-e802-4beb-a698-e72edb0da202>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 124

Reference: 1JN 5:3
Text: For this is the love of God, that we keep his commandments: and his commandments are not grievous.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6e70c04-a2aa-4e48-8a29-4d8b45f04ec1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 144

Reference: 1JN 5:4
Text: For whatsoever is born of God overcometh the world: and this is the victory that overcometh the world, even our faith.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:af2ca2d6-2f83-4326-bd7c-44686d5debcf>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 114

Reference: 1JN 5:5
Text: Who is he that overcometh the world, but he that believeth that Jesus is the Son of God?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d89e4aae-77f3-4d0d-b633-1b2053dd5f41>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: 1JN 5:6
Text: This is he that came by water and blood, even Jesus Christ; not by water only, but by water and blood. And it is the Spirit that beareth witness, because the Spirit is truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d9f1763-125b-4c5d-8279-9fe6d707f615>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 140

Reference: 1JN 5:7
Text: For there are three that bear record in heaven, the Father, the Word, and the Holy Ghost: and these three are one.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b7155ea-9c4d-4dfa-93e2-6510eb86f4b5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: 1JN 5:8
Text: And there are three that bear witness in earth, the Spirit, and the water, and the blood: and these three agree in one.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9af2d828-0128-46ca-9130-06931928080e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 1JN 5:9
Text: If we receive the witness of men, the witness of God is greater: for this is the witness of God which he hath testified of his Son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2b16140a-8416-458a-a5a4-f985280d6cbb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: 1JN 5:10
Text: He that believeth on the Son of God hath the witness in himself: he that believeth not God hath made him a liar; because he believeth not the record that God gave of his Son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2c3b888-63b6-4f62-ac36-06f7dcb39623>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: 1JN 5:11
Text: And this is the record, that God hath given to us eternal life, and this life is in his Son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:37647ea7-4e6f-4f60-a7c6-7e767fd2c113>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: 1JN 5:12
Text: He that hath the Son hath life; and he that hath not the Son of God hath not life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:44c38e9a-160b-498e-a1ce-94eeb8c3b67f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: 1JN 5:13
Text: These things have I written unto you that believe on the name of the Son of God; that ye may know that ye have eternal life, and that ye may believe on the name of the Son of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:be0bb628-3293-41ff-8488-027b347b5702>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: 1JN 5:14
Text: And this is the confidence that we have in him, that, if we ask any thing according to his will, he heareth us:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/5/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d010cf82-affa-416d-8865-ebe3d77c9305>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: 1JN 5:15
Text: And if we know that he hear us, whatsoever we ask, we know that we have the petitions that we desired of him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/5/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac94aa64-9b84-4ee1-9198-a61fd4ed47de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 230

Reference: 1JN 5:16
Text: If any man see his brother sin a sin which is not unto death, he shall ask, and he shall give him life for them that sin not unto death. There is a sin unto death: I do not say that he shall pray for it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/5/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05141ced-914f-4768-a523-e82b61f6b5cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: 1JN 5:17
Text: All unrighteousness is sin: and there is a sin not unto death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/5/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:aefabf3c-2449-4cce-b907-4f35d0210ff1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: 1JN 5:18
Text: We know that whosoever is born of God sinneth not; but he that is begotten of God keepeth himself, and that wicked one toucheth him not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/5/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bcbb80f0-267a-47d0-9b0a-b6c68bb58811>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: 1JN 5:19
Text: And we know that we are of God, and the whole world lieth in wickedness.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/5/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d8f5136-5dc1-4ec9-958a-30a3179b4921>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 240

Reference: 1JN 5:20
Text: And we know that the Son of God is come, and hath given us an understanding, that we may know him that is true, and we are in him that is true, even in his Son Jesus Christ. This is the true God, and eternal life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/1JN/5/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:91f05127-d15d-4400-b687-e301939b7d02>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: 1JN 5:21
Text: Little children, keep yourselves from idols. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2JN/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:396a55d4-6ffc-4793-8911-13f28998141a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: 2JN 1:1
Text: The elder unto the elect lady and her children, whom I love in the truth; and not I only, but also all they that have known the truth;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2JN/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:971a9831-b42a-42e5-9d80-b72f3a967944>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 102

Reference: 2JN 1:2
Text: For the truth’s sake, which dwelleth in us, and shall be with us for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2JN/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:90a74616-66dd-459e-b9aa-3600eaf48d63>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 2JN 1:3
Text: Grace be with you, mercy, and peace, from God the Father, and from the Lord Jesus Christ, the Son of the Father, in truth and love.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2JN/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:52b6cb61-8c2d-4308-8633-782891a26e1f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 142

Reference: 2JN 1:4
Text: I rejoiced greatly that I found of thy children walking in truth, as we have received a commandment from the Father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2JN/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d7f6699-a304-4264-9c45-fb1d1a1d33e1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: 2JN 1:5
Text: And now I beseech thee, lady, not as though I wrote a new commandment unto thee, but that which we had from the beginning, that we love one another.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2JN/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e6ca59a8-d7f7-4639-9603-f84869b86da9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 170

Reference: 2JN 1:6
Text: And this is love, that we walk after his commandments. This is the commandment, That, as ye have heard from the beginning, ye should walk in it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2JN/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f484fcb-ebf0-4fa3-912d-67293503fdd4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: 2JN 1:7
Text: For many deceivers are entered into the world, who confess not that Jesus Christ is come in the flesh. This is a deceiver and an antichrist.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2JN/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9c75356c-c3ef-4301-8c96-eba1a9d7cdd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: 2JN 1:8
Text: Look to yourselves, that we lose not those things which we have wrought, but that we receive a full reward.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2JN/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3dacf382-e314-4a2d-a7e7-9b4d738af694>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 187

Reference: 2JN 1:9
Text: Whosoever transgresseth, and abideth not in the doctrine of Christ, hath not God. He that abideth in the doctrine of Christ, he hath both the Father and the Son.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2JN/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:20faedf3-7011-4732-a05a-a87ebc0a8062>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: 2JN 1:10
Text: If there come any unto you, and bring not this doctrine, receive him not into your house, neither bid him God speed:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2JN/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7f3dc0c-d6ef-472e-ad3c-31c4987bf886>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 91

Reference: 2JN 1:11
Text: For he that biddeth him God speed is partaker of his evil deeds.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2JN/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2638b549-3e76-4abc-9c55-62a9a5aa39a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: 2JN 1:12
Text: Having many things to write unto you, I would not write with paper and ink: but I trust to come unto you, and speak face to face, that our joy may be full.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/2JN/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a3f9228-1b49-4f71-a291-a12cd2476c56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: 2JN 1:13
Text: The children of thy elect sister greet thee. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/3JN/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b3459126-7c9a-430c-82c1-2c9c754030f1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: 3JN 1:1
Text: The elder unto the wellbeloved Gaius, whom I love in the truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/3JN/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6ca0f747-097b-481a-82ed-2196b5b5086e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: 3JN 1:2
Text: Beloved, I wish above all things that thou mayest prosper and be in health, even as thy soul prospereth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/3JN/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5ef11bf-8d5a-4f0e-9c05-e993823ec48e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: 3JN 1:3
Text: For I rejoiced greatly, when the brethren came and testified of the truth that is in thee, even as thou walkest in the truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/3JN/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3e902a00-f54e-4b40-9942-4be1e96e46e4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 92

Reference: 3JN 1:4
Text: I have no greater joy than to hear that my children walk in truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/3JN/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a58295a-2614-4fc3-bb28-dad0dcf24904>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: 3JN 1:5
Text: Beloved, thou doest faithfully whatsoever thou doest to the brethren, and to strangers;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/3JN/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f6a1b81-0b5d-43d2-91a1-d8224d84052d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 168

Reference: 3JN 1:6
Text: Which have borne witness of thy charity before the church: whom if thou bring forward on their journey after a godly sort, thou shalt do well:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/3JN/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4af3920f-7076-459a-a891-b6fa1877537d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: 3JN 1:7
Text: Because that for his name’s sake they went forth, taking nothing of the Gentiles.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/3JN/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:32767a19-b549-4f8f-9f20-9b79cd36a591>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 106

Reference: 3JN 1:8
Text: We therefore ought to receive such, that we might be fellowhelpers to the truth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/3JN/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1987998a-02d0-440b-a06d-b886f2737b4e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: 3JN 1:9
Text: I wrote unto the church: but Diotrephes, who loveth to have the preeminence among them, receiveth us not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/3JN/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6881db7-de0a-425a-9c7b-a44cabca566b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 272

Reference: 3JN 1:10
Text: Wherefore, if I come, I will remember his deeds which he doeth, prating against us with malicious words: and not content therewith, neither doth he himself receive the brethren, and forbiddeth them that would, and casteth them out of the church.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/3JN/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9385d0a1-471a-435a-9b35-00082ec2b22e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: 3JN 1:11
Text: Beloved, follow not that which is evil, but that which is good. He that doeth good is of God: but he that doeth evil hath not seen God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/3JN/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6a33be3-25a9-47e3-b718-64c59945ec36>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 157

Reference: 3JN 1:12
Text: Demetrius hath good report of all men, and of the truth itself: yea, and we also bear record; and ye know that our record is true.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/3JN/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a89607cf-c55c-4a17-aeb7-79b15477f99c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 103

Reference: 3JN 1:13
Text: I had many things to write, but I will not with ink and pen write unto thee:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/3JN/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e2f3cc2-fb1a-4a1f-bd2a-bef615fb24ba>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: 3JN 1:14
Text: But I trust I shall shortly see thee, and we shall speak face to face. Peace be to thee. Our friends salute thee. Greet the friends by name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d11ad7f-dce0-4882-8cc7-187c6c6b5c19>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: JUD 1:1
Text: Jude, the servant of Jesus Christ, and brother of James, to them that are sanctified by God the Father, and preserved in Jesus Christ, and called:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a3da4c9-3c1a-4dd3-ba06-9a5308be204d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 77

Reference: JUD 1:2
Text: Mercy unto you, and peace, and love, be multiplied.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:51a2dbab-39d2-40ee-ba2a-294829a38150>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: JUD 1:3
Text: Beloved, when I gave all diligence to write unto you of the common salvation, it was needful for me to write unto you, and exhort you that ye should earnestly contend for the faith which was once delivered unto the saints.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b87221e2-b7a6-4236-a7b9-6b31ccedf4d5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: JUD 1:4
Text: For there are certain men crept in unawares, who were before of old ordained to this condemnation, ungodly men, turning the grace of our God into lasciviousness, and denying the only Lord God, and our Lord Jesus Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d882f1a-9693-453d-b892-c243cb14e789>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: JUD 1:5
Text: I will therefore put you in remembrance, though ye once knew this, how that the Lord, having saved the people out of the land of Egypt, afterward destroyed them that believed not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c7e432a-2460-4743-a63b-d951d543100f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: JUD 1:6
Text: And the angels which kept not their first estate, but left their own habitation, he hath reserved in everlasting chains under darkness unto the judgment of the great day.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f3d97fed-576a-4c98-957b-78476fe93e75>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 236

Reference: JUD 1:7
Text: Even as Sodom and Gomorrha, and the cities about them in like manner, giving themselves over to fornication, and going after strange flesh, are set forth for an example, suffering the vengeance of eternal fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:225cdf84-ea1c-459b-8cd1-a77962d9cb47>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: JUD 1:8
Text: Likewise also these filthy dreamers defile the flesh, despise dominion, and speak evil of dignities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:73fff2a5-ed6e-49bf-957d-9dcda13faf99>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: JUD 1:9
Text: Yet Michael the archangel, when contending with the devil he disputed about the body of Moses, durst not bring against him a railing accusation, but said, The Lord rebuke thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d847e0d1-cb5b-42ab-a71e-3c383e450a25>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: JUD 1:10
Text: But these speak evil of those things which they know not: but what they know naturally, as brute beasts, in those things they corrupt themselves.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6e082854-82bb-4a09-bcd5-c1c9954980dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: JUD 1:11
Text: Woe unto them! for they have gone in the way of Cain, and ran greedily after the error of Balaam for reward, and perished in the gainsaying of Core.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:adf426e4-92e8-4e26-87aa-99c369f3ece2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: JUD 1:12
Text: These are spots in your feasts of charity, when they feast with you, feeding themselves without fear: clouds they are without water, carried about of winds; trees whose fruit withereth, without fruit, twice dead, plucked up by the roots;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c75ec799-7e92-473a-90e7-00e433fe15a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: JUD 1:13
Text: Raging waves of the sea, foaming out their own shame; wandering stars, to whom is reserved the blackness of darkness for ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4e97b983-3638-47a6-bd6a-6284e6479c4d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: JUD 1:14
Text: And Enoch also, the seventh from Adam, prophesied of these, saying, Behold, the Lord cometh with ten thousands of his saints,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:05c6ced0-e23f-464f-9d8e-86864dd2ebce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: JUD 1:15
Text: To execute judgment upon all, and to convince all that are ungodly among them of all their ungodly deeds which they have ungodly committed, and of all their hard speeches which ungodly sinners have spoken against him.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6a2d8c9f-ce0b-42e7-8660-7001994eced9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: JUD 1:16
Text: These are murmurers, complainers, walking after their own lusts; and their mouth speaketh great swelling words, having men’s persons in admiration because of advantage.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca36d86a-e6e7-425b-9bcc-194d0c94b382>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: JUD 1:17
Text: But, beloved, remember ye the words which were spoken before of the apostles of our Lord Jesus Christ;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d1e43ff5-36c3-4dfa-97f9-5063a38e2fbc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: JUD 1:18
Text: How that they told you there should be mockers in the last time, who should walk after their own ungodly lusts.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:925f15d4-f8ca-4414-9fa1-1a18070927b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 97

Reference: JUD 1:19
Text: These be they who separate themselves, sensual, having not the Spirit.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9f12b9e2-b01a-498c-9099-faa614148acd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: JUD 1:20
Text: But ye, beloved, building up yourselves on your most holy faith, praying in the Holy Ghost,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3799971f-41db-4f74-96d0-ec49aef6ce2a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: JUD 1:21
Text: Keep yourselves in the love of God, looking for the mercy of our Lord Jesus Christ unto eternal life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d7c712e0-33c3-4dc9-9dd4-6bf363cb62c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 76

Reference: JUD 1:22
Text: And of some have compassion, making a difference:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:27eccf27-17f5-406c-9eba-3a8000a2c8fd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: JUD 1:23
Text: And others save with fear, pulling them out of the fire; hating even the garment spotted by the flesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/JUD/1/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8851131-1999-4a50-a433-c3c6f04dae83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: JUD 1:24
Text: Now unto him that is able to keep you from falling, and to present you faultless before the presence of his glory with exceeding joy,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
