Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: JUD 1:25
Text: To the only wise God our Saviour, be glory and majesty, dominion and power, both now and ever. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/1/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5d8230cf-5054-4ec8-b3e8-a1643a1679ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: REV 1:1
Text: The Revelation of Jesus Christ, which God gave unto him, to shew unto his servants things which must shortly come to pass; and he sent and signified it by his angel unto his servant John:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/1/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1339d468-b146-4ac3-947c-2c398dbef90a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: REV 1:2
Text: Who bare record of the word of God, and of the testimony of Jesus Christ, and of all things that he saw.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/1/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93e704d5-aeb4-44c0-b488-759d58d78dd1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: REV 1:3
Text: Blessed is he that readeth, and they that hear the words of this prophecy, and keep those things which are written therein: for the time is at hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/1/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3a618bf0-e44e-4132-92d9-1bf2627b9a44>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: REV 1:4
Text: John to the seven churches which are in Asia: Grace be unto you, and peace, from him which is, and which was, and which is to come; and from the seven Spirits which are before his throne;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/1/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4760b436-21ab-4fa6-a8f8-c88146b932d0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: REV 1:5
Text: And from Jesus Christ, who is the faithful witness, and the first begotten of the dead, and the prince of the kings of the earth. Unto him that loved us, and washed us from our sins in his own blood,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/1/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e13bd28-2ffb-4498-a9f0-91b39ded79de>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: REV 1:6
Text: And hath made us kings and priests unto God and his Father; to him be glory and dominion for ever and ever. Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/1/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ca6d7007-4904-439a-93d1-439a96742362>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 190

Reference: REV 1:7
Text: Behold, he cometh with clouds; and every eye shall see him, and they also which pierced him: and all kindreds of the earth shall wail because of him. Even so, Amen.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/1/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7439658c-c2ba-4de3-b82f-38faac8a5a86>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: REV 1:8
Text: I am Alpha and Omega, the beginning and the ending, saith the Lord, which is, and which was, and which is to come, the Almighty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/1/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8c7f9a7b-64ce-4f03-85c7-3e328bcc3160>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 237

Reference: REV 1:9
Text: I John, who also am your brother, and companion in tribulation, and in the kingdom and patience of Jesus Christ, was in the isle that is called Patmos, for the word of God, and for the testimony of Jesus Christ.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/1/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c68d6bb-a00e-48c9-9cfc-143157e7c4bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 119

Reference: REV 1:10
Text: I was in the Spirit on the Lord’s day, and heard behind me a great voice, as of a trumpet,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/1/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d5b1d72b-d4f4-41df-a910-1f4387520c33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 302

Reference: REV 1:11
Text: Saying, I am Alpha and Omega, the first and the last: and, What thou seest, write in a book, and send it unto the seven churches which are in Asia; unto Ephesus, and unto Smyrna, and unto Pergamos, and unto Thyatira, and unto Sardis, and unto Philadelphia, and unto Laodicea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/1/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:085e56cd-2914-48e2-8949-5b63182d8bee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: REV 1:12
Text: And I turned to see the voice that spake with me. And being turned, I saw seven golden candlesticks;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/1/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5bbcfb2b-6421-4a89-b65e-19f40bf22350>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 186

Reference: REV 1:13
Text: And in the midst of the seven candlesticks one like unto the Son of man, clothed with a garment down to the foot, and girt about the paps with a golden girdle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/1/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b679802d-1271-4ac6-b391-ade1501ed884>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 127

Reference: REV 1:14
Text: His head and his hairs were white like wool, as white as snow; and his eyes were as a flame of fire;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/1/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5f6551a4-d986-4369-a9da-242fac03e6ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: REV 1:15
Text: And his feet like unto fine brass, as if they burned in a furnace; and his voice as the sound of many waters.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/1/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4d0ea449-8f29-4da1-ab10-3ce8a1e3527f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: REV 1:16
Text: And he had in his right hand seven stars: and out of his mouth went a sharp twoedged sword: and his countenance was as the sun shineth in his strength.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/1/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b5a3ecc8-ff39-4f61-bb2b-b90ab0715c8b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: REV 1:17
Text: And when I saw him, I fell at his feet as dead. And he laid his right hand upon me, saying unto me, Fear not; I am the first and the last:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/1/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2a3e00e0-0cfb-43d0-92eb-0ee32c7d0d92>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: REV 1:18
Text: I am he that liveth, and was dead; and, behold, I am alive for evermore, Amen; and have the keys of hell and of death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/1/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9d4cae3d-a27c-4896-9dd1-1c4fe7d3000c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: REV 1:19
Text: Write the things which thou hast seen, and the things which are, and the things which shall be hereafter;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/1/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e368f965-3ab3-4f5f-a0da-e669ac28c29f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 251

Reference: REV 1:20
Text: The mystery of the seven stars which thou sawest in my right hand, and the seven golden candlesticks. The seven stars are the angels of the seven churches: and the seven candlesticks which thou sawest are the seven churches.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8f0725be-34cd-479b-a0a1-5d3d38ae5f6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: REV 2:1
Text: Unto the angel of the church of Ephesus write; These things saith he that holdeth the seven stars in his right hand, who walketh in the midst of the seven golden candlesticks;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:48e50ea4-f397-4bf2-b0b9-a9ce70ecc8f3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: REV 2:2
Text: I know thy works, and thy labour, and thy patience, and how thou canst not bear them which are evil: and thou hast tried them which say they are apostles, and are not, and hast found them liars:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce225871-af40-4863-bb29-7a6620febb5c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 122

Reference: REV 2:3
Text: And hast borne, and hast patience, and for my name’s sake hast laboured, and hast not fainted.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ce1a3104-1d1c-4df0-87ad-ce0bfe11a0ee>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 107

Reference: REV 2:4
Text: Nevertheless I have somewhat against thee, because thou hast left thy first love.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dcbbc5e8-9e73-4bcc-81f4-0bb32f0b8fca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 218

Reference: REV 2:5
Text: Remember therefore from whence thou art fallen, and repent, and do the first works; or else I will come unto thee quickly, and will remove thy candlestick out of his place, except thou repent.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b7dc17d8-4726-47c4-8f96-14d52aeb92a4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 112

Reference: REV 2:6
Text: But this thou hast, that thou hatest the deeds of the Nicolaitanes, which I also hate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:81d5a21f-867f-4750-9f6c-ac3743e2d0b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 209

Reference: REV 2:7
Text: He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches; To him that overcometh will I give to eat of the tree of life, which is in the midst of the paradise of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:106ef8c7-7dbb-458d-ac5d-390227016901>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 148

Reference: REV 2:8
Text: And unto the angel of the church in Smyrna write; These things saith the first and the last, which was dead, and is alive;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64c06506-346c-4222-b849-5403ae7c7977>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 196

Reference: REV 2:9
Text: I know thy works, and tribulation, and poverty, (but thou art rich) and I know the blasphemy of them which say they are Jews, and are not, but are the synagogue of Satan.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3bba4c5a-7238-4417-b3e1-0b1a113379b8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 260

Reference: REV 2:10
Text: Fear none of those things which thou shalt suffer: behold, the devil shall cast some of you into prison, that ye may be tried; and ye shall have tribulation ten days: be thou faithful unto death, and I will give thee a crown of life.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3693a729-e963-44ef-92b5-32e19c204ccd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: REV 2:11
Text: He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches; He that overcometh shall not be hurt of the second death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:490dafec-f375-4e35-97a2-01bb65bc0da6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: REV 2:12
Text: And to the angel of the church in Pergamos write; These things saith he which hath the sharp sword with two edges;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dacef91a-19ec-4958-b668-51903b257171>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 266

Reference: REV 2:13
Text: I know thy works, and where thou dwellest, even where Satan’s seat is: and thou holdest fast my name, and hast not denied my faith, even in those days wherein Antipas was my faithful martyr, who was slain among you, where Satan dwelleth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a21900a5-d80e-4741-81eb-cb5bca987a98>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 264

Reference: REV 2:14
Text: But I have a few things against thee, because thou hast there them that hold the doctrine of Balaam, who taught Balac to cast a stumblingblock before the children of Israel, to eat things sacrificed unto idols, and to commit fornication.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:498f989b-1dfb-4e73-a321-5b1702c5fa2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 113

Reference: REV 2:15
Text: So hast thou also them that hold the doctrine of the Nicolaitanes, which thing I hate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fc12421f-416b-4331-9289-9c7982f90a66>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: REV 2:16
Text: Repent; or else I will come unto thee quickly, and will fight against them with the sword of my mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:659c62fd-c145-46ff-992f-5be975ffa104>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: REV 2:17
Text: He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches; To him that overcometh will I give to eat of the hidden manna, and will give him a white stone, and in the stone a new name written, which no man knoweth saving he that receiveth it.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6db1f9a0-6580-4cc0-a2c3-7e0f7af2e026>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: REV 2:18
Text: And unto the angel of the church in Thyatira write; These things saith the Son of God, who hath his eyes like unto a flame of fire, and his feet are like fine brass;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:16f4279e-b14e-4191-b6eb-518b29eaf9ad>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: REV 2:19
Text: I know thy works, and charity, and service, and faith, and thy patience, and thy works; and the last to be more than the first.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a125ccff-aeaf-4093-a83e-e9272c02f81a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 254

Reference: REV 2:20
Text: Notwithstanding I have a few things against thee, because thou sufferest that woman Jezebel, which calleth herself a prophetess, to teach and to seduce my servants to commit fornication, and to eat things sacrificed unto idols.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:820a1deb-b88e-4c71-9206-ab052b45b957>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 99

Reference: REV 2:21
Text: And I gave her space to repent of her fornication; and she repented not.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9e6f86fc-5c84-4375-b94d-82985c9632c8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: REV 2:22
Text: Behold, I will cast her into a bed, and them that commit adultery with her into great tribulation, except they repent of their deeds.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:12b85553-fad0-4e25-8e81-db444077ba40>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 213

Reference: REV 2:23
Text: And I will kill her children with death; and all the churches shall know that I am he which searcheth the reins and hearts: and I will give unto every one of you according to your works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d3573a40-60da-4b4a-a4e0-75af768deaeb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: REV 2:24
Text: But unto you I say, and unto the rest in Thyatira, as many as have not this doctrine, and which have not known the depths of Satan, as they speak; I will put upon you none other burden.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/25
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a694e9f3-8e0c-4914-a453-c1cab87c50fc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 80

Reference: REV 2:25
Text: But that which ye have already hold fast till I come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/26
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:50244968-6f96-4d41-a6d6-7d150787cf00>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 128

Reference: REV 2:26
Text: And he that overcometh, and keepeth my works unto the end, to him will I give power over the nations:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/27
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c9499761-565f-482f-b013-b62aadb06664>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: REV 2:27
Text: And he shall rule them with a rod of iron; as the vessels of a potter shall they be broken to shivers: even as I received of my Father.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/28
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d21eece5-8c42-4bad-b578-2778d3548c2c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 64

Reference: REV 2:28
Text: And I will give him the morning star.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/2/29
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cf0e4b69-47ce-4948-9d98-43063e1c939e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: REV 2:29
Text: He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/3/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3da4d89-1c7c-4a76-9faf-4c8927350d9c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: REV 3:1
Text: And unto the angel of the church in Sardis write; These things saith he that hath the seven Spirits of God, and the seven stars; I know thy works, that thou hast a name that thou livest, and art dead.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/3/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1dfffbd8-de43-4599-be46-46c53175271f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 152

Reference: REV 3:2
Text: Be watchful, and strengthen the things which remain, that are ready to die: for I have not found thy works perfect before God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/3/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7a8f3c69-5bf5-4cbf-a338-e822066e9693>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: REV 3:3
Text: Remember therefore how thou hast received and heard, and hold fast, and repent. If therefore thou shalt not watch, I will come on thee as a thief, and thou shalt not know what hour I will come upon thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/3/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b81a6ceb-7b22-47a7-a5bb-1b2feff3b7bd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 160

Reference: REV 3:4
Text: Thou hast a few names even in Sardis which have not defiled their garments; and they shall walk with me in white: for they are worthy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/3/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:23a700e3-9c58-4e25-bfb9-98c48a2dc0cb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: REV 3:5
Text: He that overcometh, the same shall be clothed in white raiment; and I will not blot out his name out of the book of life, but I will confess his name before my Father, and before his angels.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/3/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b1618ca5-496b-41c0-a9f9-7b5b54ef90c2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 100

Reference: REV 3:6
Text: He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/3/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e3fe4323-ac41-4534-bf2d-c8cf6fe0e306>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 235

Reference: REV 3:7
Text: And to the angel of the church in Philadelphia write; These things saith he that is holy, he that is true, he that hath the key of David, he that openeth, and no man shutteth; and shutteth, and no man openeth;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/3/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5b85033-9736-479a-b859-50125cec698b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: REV 3:8
Text: I know thy works: behold, I have set before thee an open door, and no man can shut it: for thou hast a little strength, and hast kept my word, and hast not denied my name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/3/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f87e7eee-491e-4ec2-b067-31f48b522784>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: REV 3:9
Text: Behold, I will make them of the synagogue of Satan, which say they are Jews, and are not, but do lie; behold, I will make them to come and worship before thy feet, and to know that I have loved thee.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/3/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1666c266-4572-4af5-a8f0-66548dcfd218>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: REV 3:10
Text: Because thou hast kept the word of my patience, I also will keep thee from the hour of temptation, which shall come upon all the world, to try them that dwell upon the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/3/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7b481c6-5e81-40fb-9800-8df19eaeabbe>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: REV 3:11
Text: Behold, I come quickly: hold that fast which thou hast, that no man take thy crown.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/3/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:026cce6c-5c72-4d34-8847-138c41e3e6ef>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 311

Reference: REV 3:12
Text: Him that overcometh will I make a pillar in the temple of my God, and he shall go no more out: and I will write upon him the name of my God, and the name of the city of my God, which is new Jerusalem, which cometh down out of heaven from my God: and I will write upon him my new name.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/3/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f6ee536f-100f-40eb-bc2b-360f00081790>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: REV 3:13
Text: He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/3/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92ab33c7-e0e7-4371-8eb0-acd97d958036>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: REV 3:14
Text: And unto the angel of the church of the Laodiceans write; These things saith the Amen, the faithful and true witness, the beginning of the creation of God;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/3/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b4a1ecf0-36cf-44c3-888e-a2def407de90>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 111

Reference: REV 3:15
Text: I know thy works, that thou art neither cold nor hot: I would thou wert cold or hot.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/3/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bd57823a-237c-40f5-92cd-092379d4a048>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: REV 3:16
Text: So then because thou art lukewarm, and neither cold nor hot, I will spue thee out of my mouth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/3/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28aab45f-f6ce-4839-9e9f-24551e722bae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 197

Reference: REV 3:17
Text: Because thou sayest, I am rich, and increased with goods, and have need of nothing; and knowest not that thou art wretched, and miserable, and poor, and blind, and naked:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/3/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6c22246c-2b30-46a8-a984-8b2dfb76d59e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 262

Reference: REV 3:18
Text: I counsel thee to buy of me gold tried in the fire, that thou mayest be rich; and white raiment, that thou mayest be clothed, and that the shame of thy nakedness do not appear; and anoint thine eyes with eyesalve, that thou mayest see.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/3/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0d47f829-9fbb-4b6b-a6b9-d9aa6036926a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: REV 3:19
Text: As many as I love, I rebuke and chasten: be zealous therefore, and repent.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/3/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7de43132-90a6-4d8b-9fed-d30a581af760>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: REV 3:20
Text: Behold, I stand at the door, and knock: if any man hear my voice, and open the door, I will come in to him, and will sup with him, and he with me.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/3/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b2e5afbe-dec0-4010-b6df-3523787315cd>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: REV 3:21
Text: To him that overcometh will I grant to sit with me in my throne, even as I also overcame, and am set down with my Father in his throne.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/3/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e772b171-3118-40ff-89e3-56af2880e1dc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 101

Reference: REV 3:22
Text: He that hath an ear, let him hear what the Spirit saith unto the churches.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/4/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:93d8756f-3eb2-4585-b464-4696915ad254>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 248

Reference: REV 4:1
Text: After this I looked, and, behold, a door was opened in heaven: and the first voice which I heard was as it were of a trumpet talking with me; which said, Come up hither, and I will shew thee things which must be hereafter.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/4/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:347a2e2f-dd38-4e33-8a61-e6eabd3ea059>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: REV 4:2
Text: And immediately I was in the spirit: and, behold, a throne was set in heaven, and one sat on the throne.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/4/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:056b4516-0882-4889-af01-e6e7c31e8874>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: REV 4:3
Text: And he that sat was to look upon like a jasper and a sardine stone: and there was a rainbow round about the throne, in sight like unto an emerald.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/4/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cdc279f3-db31-40a8-9a41-25b938e2681c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 207

Reference: REV 4:4
Text: And round about the throne were four and twenty seats: and upon the seats I saw four and twenty elders sitting, clothed in white raiment; and they had on their heads crowns of gold.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/4/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:bf770b1c-9b38-48a3-9375-75e6d67818ff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: REV 4:5
Text: And out of the throne proceeded lightnings and thunderings and voices: and there were seven lamps of fire burning before the throne, which are the seven Spirits of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/4/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ddc8e650-0b15-46a6-9e47-7f51b2fd93a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: REV 4:6
Text: And before the throne there was a sea of glass like unto crystal: and in the midst of the throne, and round about the throne, were four beasts full of eyes before and behind.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/4/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cc21043e-34bc-4b24-8f67-4d0b4163142f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: REV 4:7
Text: And the first beast was like a lion, and the second beast like a calf, and the third beast had a face as a man, and the fourth beast was like a flying eagle.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/4/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:496fded2-b1c8-4111-8738-67336abb59c4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: REV 4:8
Text: And the four beasts had each of them six wings about him; and they were full of eyes within: and they rest not day and night, saying, Holy, holy, holy, LORD God Almighty, which was, and is, and is to come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/4/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:868dbcb0-9895-465f-be76-29f5e07e6f34>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: REV 4:9
Text: And when those beasts give glory and honour and thanks to him that sat on the throne, who liveth for ever and ever,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/4/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:65789cb4-a7fe-4cbb-b88a-dc9fa6f546b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: REV 4:10
Text: The four and twenty elders fall down before him that sat on the throne, and worship him that liveth for ever and ever, and cast their crowns before the throne, saying,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/4/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c189be5c-4a42-458d-a1e4-736ba78c0cbb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 172

Reference: REV 4:11
Text: Thou art worthy, O Lord, to receive glory and honour and power: for thou hast created all things, and for thy pleasure they are and were created.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/5/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:92f4adf6-0b1d-46ca-8765-d93543199c52>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: REV 5:1
Text: And I saw in the right hand of him that sat on the throne a book written within and on the backside, sealed with seven seals.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/5/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e8725ca5-618d-424d-8d2c-d7e5ddad938a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 145

Reference: REV 5:2
Text: And I saw a strong angel proclaiming with a loud voice, Who is worthy to open the book, and to loose the seals thereof?


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/5/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5597a5ac-a885-4496-a853-89009820672a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 138

Reference: REV 5:3
Text: And no man in heaven, nor in earth, neither under the earth, was able to open the book, neither to look thereon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/5/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d0e0c117-45f6-409f-903c-d50f32175fb6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: REV 5:4
Text: And I wept much, because no man was found worthy to open and to read the book, neither to look thereon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/5/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:67ec6c70-df10-4793-932a-5cb21fdd6faa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: REV 5:5
Text: And one of the elders saith unto me, Weep not: behold, the Lion of the tribe of Juda, the Root of David, hath prevailed to open the book, and to loose the seven seals thereof.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/5/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fd82ca7-4f94-4bba-968d-21056c0f8ecc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 267

Reference: REV 5:6
Text: And I beheld, and, lo, in the midst of the throne and of the four beasts, and in the midst of the elders, stood a Lamb as it had been slain, having seven horns and seven eyes, which are the seven Spirits of God sent forth into all the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/5/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f79eb3c-df8f-4d59-9c5a-cee3988c5b57>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: REV 5:7
Text: And he came and took the book out of the right hand of him that sat upon the throne.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/5/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0fa82aec-f38a-4587-a29e-08b8cd3dbf8c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 225

Reference: REV 5:8
Text: And when he had taken the book, the four beasts and four and twenty elders fell down before the Lamb, having every one of them harps, and golden vials full of odours, which are the prayers of saints.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/5/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c54627b7-d1db-4b89-9ceb-8e28011498d9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 244

Reference: REV 5:9
Text: And they sung a new song, saying, Thou art worthy to take the book, and to open the seals thereof: for thou wast slain, and hast redeemed us to God by thy blood out of every kindred, and tongue, and people, and nation;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/5/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:39a985ad-ecab-4342-96b3-1952f5b508ca>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: REV 5:10
Text: And hast made us unto our God kings and priests: and we shall reign on the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/5/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b48fec6f-e52a-451d-825a-c5e4fb46d89b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 219

Reference: REV 5:11
Text: And I beheld, and I heard the voice of many angels round about the throne and the beasts and the elders: and the number of them was ten thousand times ten thousand, and thousands of thousands;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/5/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c74616fa-9b3e-434f-8dac-ffd72d8d029f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: REV 5:12
Text: Saying with a loud voice, Worthy is the Lamb that was slain to receive power, and riches, and wisdom, and strength, and honour, and glory, and blessing.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/5/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ea207a1a-788f-4c45-ad0f-08608f4b28a0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 297

Reference: REV 5:13
Text: And every creature which is in heaven, and on the earth, and under the earth, and such as are in the sea, and all that are in them, heard I saying, Blessing, and honour, and glory, and power, be unto him that sitteth upon the throne, and unto the Lamb for ever and ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/5/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c2cbda79-c227-44b2-91b4-5e46ac3816da>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: REV 5:14
Text: And the four beasts said, Amen. And the four and twenty elders fell down and worshipped him that liveth for ever and ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/6/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d60d1ac-9698-4b5a-9021-6a8f88be05e3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 165

Reference: REV 6:1
Text: And I saw when the Lamb opened one of the seals, and I heard, as it were the noise of thunder, one of the four beasts saying, Come and see.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/6/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:22eaee9d-6754-42da-8116-ea250c4ba234>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: REV 6:2
Text: And I saw, and behold a white horse: and he that sat on him had a bow; and a crown was given unto him: and he went forth conquering, and to conquer.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/6/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:615fbc33-b702-47d1-af04-034de70408be>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 109

Reference: REV 6:3
Text: And when he had opened the second seal, I heard the second beast say, Come and see.


WARC/1.0
