Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 143

Reference: REV 9:14
Text: Saying to the sixth angel which had the trumpet, Loose the four angels which are bound in the great river Euphrates.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/9/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c57bd29d-0482-40cf-a08e-831ac279d117>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 163

Reference: REV 9:15
Text: And the four angels were loosed, which were prepared for an hour, and a day, and a month, and a year, for to slay the third part of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/9/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7b191613-6317-4491-8cd0-a71cb631c322>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 137

Reference: REV 9:16
Text: And the number of the army of the horsemen were two hundred thousand thousand: and I heard the number of them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/9/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
