Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: REV 15:1
Text: And I saw another sign in heaven, great and marvellous, seven angels having the seven last plagues; for in them is filled up the wrath of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/15/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:47d26382-57fe-479b-b5d9-5b04d0a57ba2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 258

Reference: REV 15:2
Text: And I saw as it were a sea of glass mingled with fire: and them that had gotten the victory over the beast, and over his image, and over his mark, and over the number of his name, stand on the sea of glass, having the harps of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/15/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:953a4da7-44aa-4fae-a4eb-e1b33f03ef01>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 216

Reference: REV 15:3
Text: And they sing the song of Moses the servant of God, and the song of the Lamb, saying, Great and marvellous are thy works, Lord God Almighty; just and true are thy ways, thou King of saints.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/15/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:915aec33-0c7f-4475-82e6-cea8c842959f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 194

Reference: REV 15:4
Text: Who shall not fear thee, O Lord, and glorify thy name? for thou only art holy: for all nations shall come and worship before thee; for thy judgments are made manifest.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/15/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7874bec5-255a-4e36-a14a-4f14d76c15ce>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 132

Reference: REV 15:5
Text: And after that I looked, and, behold, the temple of the tabernacle of the testimony in heaven was opened:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/15/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:330f90b5-7dd1-4f53-b2c8-308281b5717e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: REV 15:6
Text: And the seven angels came out of the temple, having the seven plagues, clothed in pure and white linen, and having their breasts girded with golden girdles.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/15/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:89c9cdc4-3c27-4c02-8912-55f57baaf622>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 155

Reference: REV 15:7
Text: And one of the four beasts gave unto the seven angels seven golden vials full of the wrath of God, who liveth for ever and ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/15/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:914f987d-a5ae-473b-94bd-c0529519f2c1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: REV 15:8
Text: And the temple was filled with smoke from the glory of God, and from his power; and no man was able to enter into the temple, till the seven plagues of the seven angels were fulfilled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/16/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ae70ac2f-7422-4918-a751-c65186f14cf7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 171

Reference: REV 16:1
Text: And I heard a great voice out of the temple saying to the seven angels, Go your ways, and pour out the vials of the wrath of God upon the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/16/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:69cf338d-deeb-44e3-97d9-e4fdae8af664>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 217

Reference: REV 16:2
Text: And the first went, and poured out his vial upon the earth; and there fell a noisome and grievous sore upon the men which had the mark of the beast, and upon them which worshipped his image.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/16/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a7aa8c7a-fd18-4910-a250-47b454a40fb7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 162

Reference: REV 16:3
Text: And the second angel poured out his vial upon the sea; and it became as the blood of a dead man: and every living soul died in the sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/16/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d9b9f14-4c13-4a94-acdd-8c696f1f2096>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 130

Reference: REV 16:4
Text: And the third angel poured out his vial upon the rivers and fountains of waters; and they became blood.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/16/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c794cb02-e17a-40b8-91de-8f0316dc388e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 161

Reference: REV 16:5
Text: And I heard the angel of the waters say, Thou art righteous, O Lord, which art, and wast, and shalt be, because thou hast judged thus.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/16/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ac44ec58-01c3-475a-b01a-6c31cabb259b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 141

Reference: REV 16:6
Text: For they have shed the blood of saints and prophets, and thou hast given them blood to drink; for they are worthy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/16/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4cfa800a-f290-4679-9d17-4831fc1a9eed>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 134

Reference: REV 16:7
Text: And I heard another out of the altar say, Even so, Lord God Almighty, true and righteous are thy judgments.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/16/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:18f6d047-42fa-4762-8d37-91e4f274cdf6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: REV 16:8
Text: And the fourth angel poured out his vial upon the sun; and power was given unto him to scorch men with fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/16/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7d062d8a-0875-4ef7-9bc6-5ec3ee7dda0d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: REV 16:9
Text: And men were scorched with great heat, and blasphemed the name of God, which hath power over these plagues: and they repented not to give him glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/16/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2f63a358-ffd1-4c28-b44a-7aeec57fd666>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 173

Reference: REV 16:10
Text: And the fifth angel poured out his vial upon the seat of the beast; and his kingdom was full of darkness; and they gnawed their tongues for pain,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/16/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d82d288e-986b-4add-813a-699ff4866bc6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: REV 16:11
Text: And blasphemed the God of heaven because of their pains and their sores, and repented not of their deeds.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/16/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5ff65a09-cca0-49dc-bcb9-838db9cb8d73>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: REV 16:12
Text: And the sixth angel poured out his vial upon the great river Euphrates; and the water thereof was dried up, that the way of the kings of the east might be prepared.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/16/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f12c4fd2-b70f-47b9-988f-0ceed88964f0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 185

Reference: REV 16:13
Text: And I saw three unclean spirits like frogs come out of the mouth of the dragon, and out of the mouth of the beast, and out of the mouth of the false prophet.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/16/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c3203a8a-9287-4332-950c-08f21ae1ed6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 212

Reference: REV 16:14
Text: For they are the spirits of devils, working miracles, which go forth unto the kings of the earth and of the whole world, to gather them to the battle of that great day of God Almighty.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/16/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c806b4d4-ea3b-4f31-9a65-00b174b441bc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 153

Reference: REV 16:15
Text: Behold, I come as a thief. Blessed is he that watcheth, and keepeth his garments, lest he walk naked, and they see his shame.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/16/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f29b65a1-42cf-4d2d-9e1e-abda0b3c7a49>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 110

Reference: REV 16:16
Text: And he gathered them together into a place called in the Hebrew tongue Armageddon.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/16/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a0e1fb1f-67e2-4232-b877-e3a0fbaa9172>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 178

Reference: REV 16:17
Text: And the seventh angel poured out his vial into the air; and there came a great voice out of the temple of heaven, from the throne, saying, It is done.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/16/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4f12ff6d-dc19-4cdd-a7b3-d06622f8d89c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: REV 16:18
Text: And there were voices, and thunders, and lightnings; and there was a great earthquake, such as was not since men were upon the earth, so mighty an earthquake, and so great.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/16/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8ad6b2d7-80e0-42e1-a53b-f6fbb338eb10>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 231

Reference: REV 16:19
Text: And the great city was divided into three parts, and the cities of the nations fell: and great Babylon came in remembrance before God, to give unto her the cup of the wine of the fierceness of his wrath.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/16/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:13495626-99f7-4556-86af-27e75e78524d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 89

Reference: REV 16:20
Text: And every island fled away, and the mountains were not found.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/16/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e184ad37-f0d2-44a6-9d34-b38db01cf16a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: REV 16:21
Text: And there fell upon men a great hail out of heaven, every stone about the weight of a talent: and men blasphemed God because of the plague of the hail; for the plague thereof was exceeding great.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/17/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:324321d1-e4e3-4106-9f66-988df1bed108>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: REV 17:1
Text: And there came one of the seven angels which had the seven vials, and talked with me, saying unto me, Come hither; I will shew unto thee the judgment of the great whore that sitteth upon many waters:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/17/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6d5e36ab-0c7d-4820-940d-f43154dc1f71>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 175

Reference: REV 17:2
Text: With whom the kings of the earth have committed fornication, and the inhabitants of the earth have been made drunk with the wine of her fornication.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/17/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:64f391cf-c717-4e57-b3cb-dc0873509a06>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 198

Reference: REV 17:3
Text: So he carried me away in the spirit into the wilderness: and I saw a woman sit upon a scarlet coloured beast, full of names of blasphemy, having seven heads and ten horns.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/17/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4b1847a7-cbc8-402b-bce5-0747b4b7e6ae>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 223

Reference: REV 17:4
Text: And the woman was arrayed in purple and scarlet colour, and decked with gold and precious stones and pearls, having a golden cup in her hand full of abominations and filthiness of her fornication:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/17/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:931bda8b-8f31-4520-9967-4b6c8eab6153>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 149

Reference: REV 17:5
Text: And upon her forehead was a name written, MYSTERY, BABYLON THE GREAT, THE MOTHER OF HARLOTS AND ABOMINATIONS OF THE EARTH.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/17/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b92d746e-6e5e-4fa7-9f20-749df46bc753>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: REV 17:6
Text: And I saw the woman drunken with the blood of the saints, and with the blood of the martyrs of Jesus: and when I saw her, I wondered with great admiration.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/17/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f90634fc-af12-4f36-860a-6b629a86893c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 204

Reference: REV 17:7
Text: And the angel said unto me, Wherefore didst thou marvel? I will tell thee the mystery of the woman, and of the beast that carrieth her, which hath the seven heads and ten horns.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/17/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:586cd8a0-cc2e-4e5f-b08e-9f318355c907>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 328

Reference: REV 17:8
Text: The beast that thou sawest was, and is not; and shall ascend out of the bottomless pit, and go into perdition: and they that dwell on the earth shall wonder, whose names were not written in the book of life from the foundation of the world, when they behold the beast that was, and is not, and yet is.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/17/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9601ccbb-31c0-460b-89cc-c1c594131322>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 131

Reference: REV 17:9
Text: And here is the mind which hath wisdom. The seven heads are seven mountains, on which the woman sitteth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/17/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28a446bc-0203-46f3-bc82-3c5b849fc49d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 166

Reference: REV 17:10
Text: And there are seven kings: five are fallen, and one is, and the other is not yet come; and when he cometh, he must continue a short space.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/17/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:850c8750-3b60-4f92-b9fa-edc5f6d501a3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 133

Reference: REV 17:11
Text: And the beast that was, and is not, even he is the eighth, and is of the seven, and goeth into perdition.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/17/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:00e0d0dc-1e0f-4e21-807d-9b1b3a3de3f8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 169

Reference: REV 17:12
Text: And the ten horns which thou sawest are ten kings, which have received no kingdom as yet; but receive power as kings one hour with the beast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/17/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e91afd07-d057-461b-b939-5d8e1d592fd3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 104

Reference: REV 17:13
Text: These have one mind, and shall give their power and strength unto the beast.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/17/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f1b9a0d9-0f06-4da3-bbdd-b266e36fef57>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 206

Reference: REV 17:14
Text: These shall make war with the Lamb, and the Lamb shall overcome them: for he is Lord of lords, and King of kings: and they that are with him are called, and chosen, and faithful.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/17/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4824aa53-3f7f-4d42-98fd-30a62ea3cba8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: REV 17:15
Text: And he saith unto me, The waters which thou sawest, where the whore sitteth, are peoples, and multitudes, and nations, and tongues.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/17/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0e4d23b8-c73f-433b-a02c-e9f54d1d8a6a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 195

Reference: REV 17:16
Text: And the ten horns which thou sawest upon the beast, these shall hate the whore, and shall make her desolate and naked, and shall eat her flesh, and burn her with fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/17/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2fd15133-c762-4326-a274-a54e61d6d962>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 176

Reference: REV 17:17
Text: For God hath put in their hearts to fulfil his will, and to agree, and give their kingdom unto the beast, until the words of God shall be fulfilled.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/17/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d68571d-f353-45f8-b4bf-517b6f083f13>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 123

Reference: REV 17:18
Text: And the woman which thou sawest is that great city, which reigneth over the kings of the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:79512559-b868-4370-aebd-607047dc325e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: REV 18:1
Text: And after these things I saw another angel come down from heaven, having great power; and the earth was lightened with his glory.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d33c4c7-1f7d-4a6b-b56f-7df15b5d540f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 238

Reference: REV 18:2
Text: And he cried mightily with a strong voice, saying, Babylon the great is fallen, is fallen, and is become the habitation of devils, and the hold of every foul spirit, and a cage of every unclean and hateful bird.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:acba72a0-2987-43a6-80f9-30c49427f9a9>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 249

Reference: REV 18:3
Text: For all nations have drunk of the wine of the wrath of her fornication, and the kings of the earth have committed fornication with her, and the merchants of the earth are waxed rich through the abundance of her delicacies.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7c7b448b-c293-4aca-89ed-c48935f51558>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: REV 18:4
Text: And I heard another voice from heaven, saying, Come out of her, my people, that ye be not partakers of her sins, and that ye receive not of her plagues.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:9fa04d63-691d-4585-8bd0-3572456e6798>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: REV 18:5
Text: For her sins have reached unto heaven, and God hath remembered her iniquities.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e7d0f917-b65e-45c9-8f22-9f340c2df843>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 167

Reference: REV 18:6
Text: Reward her even as she rewarded you, and double unto her double according to her works: in the cup which she hath filled fill to her double.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:28667bb9-b4c2-4cf4-89e3-2e0ebb821e33>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: REV 18:7
Text: How much she hath glorified herself, and lived deliciously, so much torment and sorrow give her: for she saith in her heart, I sit a queen, and am no widow, and shall see no sorrow.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:7504affe-e7f1-42bf-9b14-cd09f7ef93fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 191

Reference: REV 18:8
Text: Therefore shall her plagues come in one day, death, and mourning, and famine; and she shall be utterly burned with fire: for strong is the Lord God who judgeth her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8a994dec-d770-463d-a33d-e41b8121720c>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 201

Reference: REV 18:9
Text: And the kings of the earth, who have committed fornication and lived deliciously with her, shall bewail her, and lament for her, when they shall see the smoke of her burning,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:770d2886-5033-4a6f-85d1-964562ad2008>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: REV 18:10
Text: Standing afar off for the fear of her torment, saying, Alas, alas that great city Babylon, that mighty city! for in one hour is thy judgment come.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:17238953-a57b-48b4-8dcb-9c0b154c1fd7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: REV 18:11
Text: And the merchants of the earth shall weep and mourn over her; for no man buyeth their merchandise any more:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:6fefacee-8011-4cc8-aee6-0a88f8dfe7e7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 287

Reference: REV 18:12
Text: The merchandise of gold, and silver, and precious stones, and of pearls, and fine linen, and purple, and silk, and scarlet, and all thyine wood, and all manner vessels of ivory, and all manner vessels of most precious wood, and of brass, and iron, and marble,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e56c0c23-9757-47fb-9c22-0ff1903cf7b1>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 211

Reference: REV 18:13
Text: And cinnamon, and odours, and ointments, and frankincense, and wine, and oil, and fine flour, and wheat, and beasts, and sheep, and horses, and chariots, and slaves, and souls of men.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3456bcfb-2d17-419f-bbf6-9a2d23e15fc4>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 202

Reference: REV 18:14
Text: And the fruits that thy soul lusted after are departed from thee, and all things which were dainty and goodly are departed from thee, and thou shalt find them no more at all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1d93a3f3-67c2-4c54-8ef4-3b8fa137ff6e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 158

Reference: REV 18:15
Text: The merchants of these things, which were made rich by her, shall stand afar off for the fear of her torment, weeping and wailing,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4af81782-d26f-4bf6-a508-bc8b477aef5f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 179

Reference: REV 18:16
Text: And saying, Alas, alas that great city, that was clothed in fine linen, and purple, and scarlet, and decked with gold, and precious stones, and pearls!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:03735407-0a88-4a8d-bde2-12b40a380467>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 188

Reference: REV 18:17
Text: For in one hour so great riches is come to nought. And every shipmaster, and all the company in ships, and sailors, and as many as trade by sea, stood afar off,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:35180290-a3da-44a3-96b2-221cdb0c7638>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 125

Reference: REV 18:18
Text: And cried when they saw the smoke of her burning, saying, What city is like unto this great city!


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:a421554f-ce0d-4c5e-9f15-e4f3b268feff>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 250

Reference: REV 18:19
Text: And they cast dust on their heads, and cried, weeping and wailing, saying, Alas, alas that great city, wherein were made rich all that had ships in the sea by reason of her costliness! for in one hour is she made desolate.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:dbf742b5-27e7-4b1a-97f5-42c6fc768262>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 126

Reference: REV 18:20
Text: Rejoice over her, thou heaven, and ye holy apostles and prophets; for God hath avenged you on her.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8cd4aa44-31a2-428b-9719-4db90cfde9d3>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 220

Reference: REV 18:21
Text: And a mighty angel took up a stone like a great millstone, and cast it into the sea, saying, Thus with violence shall that great city Babylon be thrown down, and shall be found no more at all.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/22
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:4488aba1-d7c1-4257-86c1-50be7bd9f7d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 284

Reference: REV 18:22
Text: And the voice of harpers, and musicians, and of pipers, and trumpeters, shall be heard no more at all in thee; and no craftsman, of whatsoever craft he be, shall be found any more in thee; and the sound of a millstone shall be heard no more at all in thee;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/23
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:8b3f7ebb-fb45-4efd-b53b-b69085eb3fdc>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 276

Reference: REV 18:23
Text: And the light of a candle shall shine no more at all in thee; and the voice of the bridegroom and of the bride shall be heard no more at all in thee: for thy merchants were the great men of the earth; for by thy sorceries were all nations deceived.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/18/24
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:5091cd12-ef6d-40b5-baa9-81542c4caa56>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 129

Reference: REV 18:24
Text: And in her was found the blood of prophets, and of saints, and of all that were slain upon the earth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/19/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:967c4ba7-0526-49c8-b2fc-2787e3badd48>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 183

Reference: REV 19:1
Text: And after these things I heard a great voice of much people in heaven, saying, Alleluia; Salvation, and glory, and honour, and power, unto the Lord our God:


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/19/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:ba2d6b9c-3340-4334-8230-2114b940131a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: REV 19:2
Text: For true and righteous are his judgments: for he hath judged the great whore, which did corrupt the earth with her fornication, and hath avenged the blood of his servants at her hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/19/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:43f28248-a42d-4b0c-a8eb-05bbd5150571>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 98

Reference: REV 19:3
Text: And again they said, Alleluia. And her smoke rose up for ever and ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/19/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:df5564ed-2c0c-4abf-a620-1b96ff736aeb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: REV 19:4
Text: And the four and twenty elders and the four beasts fell down and worshipped God that sat on the throne, saying, Amen; Alleluia.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/19/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:e13d72f9-9d07-40f6-bd8d-eef7db81ef83>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 151

Reference: REV 19:5
Text: And a voice came out of the throne, saying, Praise our God, all ye his servants, and ye that fear him, both small and great.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/19/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:42a4d7a3-255a-4317-8a4d-888549f28dfb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 210

Reference: REV 19:6
Text: And I heard as it were the voice of a great multitude, and as the voice of many waters, and as the voice of mighty thunderings, saying, Alleluia: for the Lord God omnipotent reigneth.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/19/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:06362259-d07a-42f1-84e3-5ac9d1e6cfe8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 154

Reference: REV 19:7
Text: Let us be glad and rejoice, and give honour to him: for the marriage of the Lamb is come, and his wife hath made herself ready.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/19/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:940a4ae0-185f-44d4-a0b6-ea3ac7253ba7>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 159

Reference: REV 19:8
Text: And to her was granted that she should be arrayed in fine linen, clean and white: for the fine linen is the righteousness of saints.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/19/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fb36ce52-6fda-4f22-8d9d-d2bf67d11610>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 184

Reference: REV 19:9
Text: And he saith unto me, Write, Blessed are they which are called unto the marriage supper of the Lamb. And he saith unto me, These are the true sayings of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/19/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:75454db6-3759-4c30-935d-5dc030d100fa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 252

Reference: REV 19:10
Text: And I fell at his feet to worship him. And he said unto me, See thou do it not: I am thy fellowservant, and of thy brethren that have the testimony of Jesus: worship God: for the testimony of Jesus is the spirit of prophecy.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/19/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2665eeb4-e459-41a5-b156-daed78259915>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 182

Reference: REV 19:11
Text: And I saw heaven opened, and behold a white horse; and he that sat upon him was called Faithful and True, and in righteousness he doth judge and make war.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/19/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7255cdd-1dd7-4eba-b0e1-a588710e3fb8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 156

Reference: REV 19:12
Text: His eyes were as a flame of fire, and on his head were many crowns; and he had a name written, that no man knew, but he himself.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/19/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:41ef38ac-cf7e-4213-ad88-bd877fca94d6>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 118

Reference: REV 19:13
Text: And he was clothed with a vesture dipped in blood: and his name is called The Word of God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/19/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c16088d6-9571-4097-ba63-2cee6c2000fb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 135

Reference: REV 19:14
Text: And the armies which were in heaven followed him upon white horses, clothed in fine linen, white and clean.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/19/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1aa30c8d-493e-436a-a0fa-633276e05969>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 229

Reference: REV 19:15
Text: And out of his mouth goeth a sharp sword, that with it he should smite the nations: and he shall rule them with a rod of iron: and he treadeth the winepress of the fierceness and wrath of Almighty God.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/19/16
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:da8b3ecb-25e2-4599-9925-2f9ea764dcb5>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 121

Reference: REV 19:16
Text: And he hath on his vesture and on his thigh a name written, KING OF KINGS, AND LORD OF LORDS.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/19/17
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d64fe1d7-a039-4c39-8fb9-9ea20447d5aa>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 226

Reference: REV 19:17
Text: And I saw an angel standing in the sun; and he cried with a loud voice, saying to all the fowls that fly in the midst of heaven, Come and gather yourselves together unto the supper of the great God;


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/19/18
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:b8f6704a-4954-499a-afb7-253006479b5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 242

Reference: REV 19:18
Text: That ye may eat the flesh of kings, and the flesh of captains, and the flesh of mighty men, and the flesh of horses, and of them that sit on them, and the flesh of all men, both free and bond, both small and great.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/19/19
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f7c543c8-179d-46d9-959a-77874474461e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 181

Reference: REV 19:19
Text: And I saw the beast, and the kings of the earth, and their armies, gathered together to make war against him that sat on the horse, and against his army.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/19/20
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:96076d61-4335-44b5-992b-b1f952ea3d5a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 293

Reference: REV 19:20
Text: And the beast was taken, and with him the false prophet that wrought miracles before him, with which he deceived them that had received the mark of the beast, and them that worshipped his image. These both were cast alive into a lake of fire burning with brimstone.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/19/21
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:0f889666-527b-43e2-a3ac-d770d183b59a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 189

Reference: REV 19:21
Text: And the remnant were slain with the sword of him that sat upon the horse, which sword proceeded out of his mouth: and all the fowls were filled with their flesh.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/20/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:1cab451f-ab5d-432b-b642-57fa498f726f>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 136

Reference: REV 20:1
Text: And I saw an angel come down from heaven, having the key of the bottomless pit and a great chain in his hand.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/20/2
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:db5d1836-ca66-4336-a4ef-451dc73eb31d>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: REV 20:2
Text: And he laid hold on the dragon, that old serpent, which is the Devil, and Satan, and bound him a thousand years,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/20/3
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:cb529744-6ab5-4f8e-adf7-aae739b4d78a>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 245

Reference: REV 20:3
Text: And cast him into the bottomless pit, and shut him up, and set a seal upon him, that he should deceive the nations no more, till the thousand years should be fulfilled: and after that he must be loosed a little season.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/20/4
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:f5b033de-3ae9-4b23-a70f-b8c5a8f8daeb>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 388

Reference: REV 20:4
Text: And I saw thrones, and they sat upon them, and judgment was given unto them: and I saw the souls of them that were beheaded for the witness of Jesus, and for the word of God, and which had not worshipped the beast, neither his image, neither had received his mark upon their foreheads, or in their hands; and they lived and reigned with Christ a thousand years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/20/5
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:09e5b3d4-e6c0-4908-8501-c43786f49302>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 139

Reference: REV 20:5
Text: But the rest of the dead lived not again until the thousand years were finished. This is the first resurrection.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/20/6
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2e85be74-ffc0-4ec8-bc2a-b3216dd0f4b2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 222

Reference: REV 20:6
Text: Blessed and holy is he that hath part in the first resurrection: on such the second death hath no power, but they shall be priests of God and of Christ, and shall reign with him a thousand years.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/20/7
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:837e3722-d4f8-4f69-b283-a278bd6d076b>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 108

Reference: REV 20:7
Text: And when the thousand years are expired, Satan shall be loosed out of his prison,


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/20/8
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:d56576eb-2a08-4181-a341-4892a70b9109>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 208

Reference: REV 20:8
Text: And shall go out to deceive the nations which are in the four quarters of the earth, Gog, and Magog, to gather them together to battle: the number of whom is as the sand of the sea.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/20/9
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:2d05d077-8c42-42c0-a4aa-bbe9d08d9fc8>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 200

Reference: REV 20:9
Text: And they went up on the breadth of the earth, and compassed the camp of the saints about, and the beloved city: and fire came down from God out of heaven, and devoured them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/20/10
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:3def8759-2f45-4532-b1e3-c7581d76771e>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 205

Reference: REV 20:10
Text: And the devil that deceived them was cast into the lake of fire and brimstone, where the beast and the false prophet are, and shall be tormented day and night for ever and ever.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/20/11
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:fac581b6-98fd-4ef9-88e0-cce74afd2980>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 174

Reference: REV 20:11
Text: And I saw a great white throne, and him that sat on it, from whose face the earth and the heaven fled away; and there was found no place for them.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/20/12
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:247dfb68-46cd-48b8-8ad0-6442eed76ba0>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 269

Reference: REV 20:12
Text: And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before God; and the books were opened: and another book was opened, which is the book of life: and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/20/13
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:07761676-6954-4cd3-9484-8e5bbd792da2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 192

Reference: REV 20:13
Text: And the sea gave up the dead which were in it; and death and hell delivered up the dead which were in them: and they were judged every man according to their works.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/20/14
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:351c4996-ee8c-4d83-be1d-63f9049525d2>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 105

Reference: REV 20:14
Text: And death and hell were cast into the lake of fire. This is the second death.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/20/15
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
WARC-Record-ID: <urn:uuid:c25d9d7b-6c15-4aa8-a9bd-0f70ee2d4324>
Content-Type: text/plain
Content-Length: 115

Reference: REV 20:15
Text: And whosoever was not found written in the book of life was cast into the lake of fire.


WARC/1.0
WARC-Type: resource
WARC-Target-URI: http://bible.org/REV/21/1
WARC-Date: 2026-05-04T00:56:34Z
